package com.darkshamanism.lotcscholar.services

@Suppress("LongMethod", "MagicNumber")
internal object StaticBooksData_ATLAS {

    private fun _ATLAS_0(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("!!Attention!!", "Tarien Arvius", "Missive to the Spellcrafter Archon IV - A Warning\nTo the Spellcrafter Archon,\nI hope this message reaches you in time. We were deceived, the Seal was a false lead, the Radiant Man, or as he is truly called, the aengul Garzardiel, had\nhis own agenda all along, and Rivel faces imminent attack and possibly annihilation.\nMost of the Spellcrafters in the task force are fully under Garzardiel’s sway, mere puppets to his will. I have broken free of his influence and escaped but in\nturn have lost both my powers from him and my skill with the Arcane. I fear how many of my decisions in the past months have been acts based not on my own judgement but on his influence!\nWhen we opened the Hall we found it littered with\nskeletal corpses: the Forgotten Dwarves were wiped out by a civil war: the ruling caste trying in desperation to give the Seal enough fuel to defeat the Ravager, and the people fighting back. It seems too that the ruling caste won the war and the death\nsimply fueled the Seal further. The city was also filled with hundreds of war constructs designed for raiding the surface for harvesting more souls: I suppose when you’ve enacted a near total genocide on your own people in the name of\nsurvival the deaths of a few hundred surface dwellers aren’t going to bother you. It seems these constructs wiped out the surviving Forgotten Dwarves.\nAs for the Seal, the machine itself is complete, but damaged: we\nsuspect the damage allowed vengeful souls to leak out and possess the constructs, wiping out the surviving dwarves. Garzardiel revealed that the goal of the Forgotten Dwarves was impossible: the Seal could never hold enough souls to\ntrap the Ravager, which begs the question, whatever does he want it for?\nOnce he had access to the Seal Garzardiel took control of the constructs and ordered the elimination of all loose ends, all who knew about the Seal.\nThat means the Spellcrafters of our company that were not fully under his sway and Rivel itself. I attempted to conceal myself, but without my arcane powers it was most difficult. The last I saw of Garzardiel was him headed to the Seal Chamber\nitself, a writhing mongoose held by the neck in his grip. After that I was forced to flee the city, and as I left I realised the direness of our situation.\nThe majority of soul harvesting constructs left for Rivel hours ago: I know not how long\nyou have to formulate a defence against their oncoming assault on the walls.\nI will find the keys and reseal this Hall. My last act will be to return the keys to their hiding places. I don’t know what Garzardiel really wanted to trap in\nthat machine, but Urguan’s Hall must never again be found.\n- Spellcrafter Tarien Arvius", ""),
        StaticBook("'The Balrog'", "Arinislia", "'The Taint'\n\n7th of The Grand Harvest, 1475\nThe day was calm and gentle. The sun was high, shining its rays down upon the Father Tree as the druids went about their day. One of the druid children suddenly runs up, gasping for breath as she appeared to have been running.\nShe looked panicked, saying that she ran into a Dread Lord summoning something in the nearby woods. Suddenly a loud shriek was heard. . All look up the natural carved stairs of the Father Tree to see the Dread Lord stand before them.\n. A ghoul standing next to him along with some followers, the Dread Lord unleashed the ghoul down upon the druids, commanded to kill them all. During this, the Dread Lord then turned and advanced up the tree,\n, telling his followers to block all that dare move up. The ghoul was quickly defeated, but not before spreading its taint on all that it bit along with ones that were near when it exploded.\nIt appeared that if something wasn’t done quickly to cleanse, they perished.\n\n       The druids now advancing further up the tree, the followers were quickly removed before advancing further up.\n. Again the druids were blocked and met with a horrible abomination. The Dread Lord cackled down at them, before unleashing a balrog upon the druids, charging down full force.\nSeveral that were in the way were easily knocked off the tree to their deaths.  The druids seemed unorganized, yet with some coordination from a few within the order, they quickly rooted the balrog and threw it off the tree.\nThe Dread Lord far gone by then yet the top of the tree tainted. The druids advance upward, circling around the taint and focused, using their healing magic to remove the corruption of the tree.\nBelow where the balrog  fell off the tree, several came from different nations and organizations and struck down the abomination where it stood.  With the Father Tree healed once more, the druids descended down and helped cleanse and heal the wounded.", ""),
        StaticBook("'The Poisoner'", "Caine Silverblade", "Investigation Report\n     The Poisoner\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-  This is the report for the investigation of a potential person of interest in the attacks on Holm by undead hordes. This person refers to themselves as 'The Poisoner', and their current\nidentity is unknown. Their compounds and poisons are believed to be used by certain members of the undead or undead sympathizers.\nInitial Investigations\n-The first sign of the POI is a sign surrounded by torches. The sign states, \"They must die.\", located in the forest east of High Rock keep.\n-The next sign are three signs located further in the forest surrounding a banner post.\n-The three signs state, \"Kill\", \"Revenge\", and \"Eliminate\".\n-The banner is a red diamond with a purple circle in the center on a black field. I removed the banner from the post to take back as evidence.\n-Written upon the banner post is the phrase,\n\"They will not see Dawn again.\"\n- East of the banner there is a tree with an X carved into it, behind said tree is the entrance to the Poisoners lair.\nInitial Investigation : The Lair\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=--The first room of the lair is 44 sq.m in the shape of an L.\n-There is a well in the SE corner of the room.\n-There is a table in the middle of the room with a single golden chalice. The chalice is\nfilled with a green liquid. \n-There are three doors leading out of the first main room.\nThey are labeled, \"The Alchemy\", \"The Deadly Storage\", and \"The Brew Dream\". \n-There is a closet in the SW corner of the room. I was unable to gain access to\nthe closet.\n- \"The Alchemy\" is 15 sq. m.\n-There are two rooms coming off of it labeled, \"The Reagent Room\" and the other is unmarked.\n-There is a cauldron in the NW corner of the room.\n-Multiple bottles hang\nfrom the walls.\n-There is a mortar\nand pestle in the NE corner of the room.\n-\"The Reagent Room\" was jammed, and thus was not able to be explored during this first investigation.\n-The Unmarked Room contains a short, decayed corpse. I assume it is the corpse of a dwarf.\n- \"The Brew Dream\" is 16 sq.m.\n-Within is stored multiple casks of alcohol.\n-Two rooms branch of from \"The Brew Dream\", \"The Diverse Storage\" and \"The Common Passage\". Neither were accesable during this investigation.\nSecond Investigation\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=--\"The Diverse Storage\" is 20 sq.m. \n- It contains four chests.\n-\"The Common Passage\" was jammed and unable to be investigated.\n-\"The Deadly Storage\" was jammed and unable to be investigated.\nThird Investigation\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=--\"The Deadly Storage\"\nis 20 sq.m.\n- Within are multiple vials of Corrosive Poison, Sickening Poison, Poison, Venom, Paralyzing Poison, and Acid Poison.\n- All other unexplored rooms were hammed and unable\nto be investigated.\nPrimary Conversation\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-- 6th of Deep Cold, 1675, I met two men on the road bearing the emblem of the poisoner upon their shields. \n- They initially wore masks, and spoke of looking for one halfling named Larry Hill.\n- After a while\nthey removed their masks, revealing their faces.\n[!]\nA drawing of Dilory Lada ((Dmercads)) takes up the page.\n[!]\nA drawing of Lytes Thadrir ((Stareless)) takes up the page.", ""),
        StaticBook("((hobbits song))", "Geedin Jayamen", "2 6 9 6 \n2 6 9\n\n2 3 4 6 4\n3 2\n4 6 7 9 8\n6 4 3\n\n2 3 4 6 4\n3 4 3 2\n4 6 7 9 8\n6 4 3 2 3 2", ""),
        StaticBook("((OOC Inquiry", "Anya Calithil", "((Hello! I would like to know if it's possible for you to craft me an unsigned golden shovel, so I may be able to design its description, name, and sign it myself! I am happy to pay for the shovel\n-LadyAmayo / Amayo#2901 on discord", ""),
        StaticBook("()Telekenisis()", "Nepir Wolfguard", ")()()()()()()()()()()(Magic guide for all those who wish to learn\n)()()()()()()()()()()(Telekinesis\n)()()()()()()()()()()(\nThis guide focuses on my own magic Telekenisis.\n\nIt is made for those who wish to learn with out a teacher And will have ways to train\n\nAlso usefull for those who do not know how to connect to the void\nLesson 1\nConnect to the void?\nYou can skip this if you are all ready able to use this.\n\nstep 1\nSit down and make sure its calm around you\nstep 2\nEmpty your mind and focus on the Emptyness\nFrom here you will start to feel the void after some time you will be able to connect with out any problems and even do it in a blink of a eye\nLesson 2\nTelekenisis\n\nYou have to learn what telekenisis is.\ntelekenisis can chance the gravity on objects \nlike on a cup or bottle\n\nthere are also things that we can not controll like water and mist as these are-\nmade up out of lots of small parts.§.\n\nOnes you understand these things you can go on and and start trying the steps on the next page\nLesson 3\n\nFirst take out a coin\ntry and move this coin over the ground or table when\n\nafter this becomes easy try flip the coin\n\nand last part try to lift it up and move it around\nlesson 4\nNow try do the same as lesson 3 but move around a cup first empty \n\nand slowly start filling it up as you train for a while untile its full from this point you can start thinking of what you want to train\nYou can train these things\n\nControll\nHow good and stead you can move objects\n\nForce\nHow mutch force you can put on a object\n\nfocus\nControlling more then one object\nThis is the end of my guide as you reached a point where you think up your own training that fits what you want to learn\n\nI hope this was of use to you and wishe you the best on your road to master telekenisis", ""),
        StaticBook("*CrumbledLetter*", "Noel Cerolith", "Every life has a story. It all begins at the start, and finishes at the end. But barely anyone knows about the middle. Its been over a year now since I have seen you, and i dont even know if this message will reach you. I left for reason that could put\nour family in danger. \n\nIm sorry for just getting up and leaving, but I hope you can forgive me... Maybe we could see each other again... In the future...\n\n Co Co", ""),
        StaticBook("-Fire Evocation-", "Garsto 'Spark' Leaf", "{-----------------}         Fire Evocation\n{-----------------}This book is about Fire evocation.\n\nThe Fire Evocationists conjure appears to be real. But it is fake. One does not have power over the elements. For an Evocationist to conjure fire from the\nvoid they have to understand the element in the real/physical world first. The easiest way of bringing Fire into the physical world would be to light a torch by using Evocation or by creating a fire which then lights a fire. As a mage becomes more\nexperienced they can eventually form balls of Fire which they could shape into objects of Fire.\n\n((The Next part of this book is OOC. Its mainly for ones who already know Magic but want to Emote it. It is OOC. Remember that...\nGarsto is focused on a spot on a hay bale in front of him.\n\nis twitching a tad with his eyes locked on the position of the hay bale. He is muttering something. \n\nA tiny faint orange flame appears on the hay bale.\nThe flame gets smaller and blows itself out.\n\nGarsto falls back into a chair in fatigue.\n\nThat was an example of a Tier 1.\n\nThe next is Tier two.\nGarsto is concentrating on an unlit torch in front of him.\n\nHis forehead is sweating and he is breathing heavily.\n\nA Spark flickers on the coal in the torch.\nThe Spark lights the coal which results in the torch being lighted.\n\nGarsto's kitchen is now lit by the torch.\n\nStumbles in Fatigue.\n\nThat was a Tier Two. Next is a Tier Four.\nGarsto is concentrating with his hand outstretched towards the cow.\n\nHe begins to breath heavily and his forehead is sweating.\n\nHe mutters something. Flames erupt from his hand spinning into a shape.\nThe Shape looks something like a small dagger. Its not clear though.\n\nOpens his eyes and mutters something sending the fiery dagger towards the cow. \n\nThat was all OOC remember.))\nIts suggest that you meditate to help your self connect to the void. This can help you improve and go through tier 1.  At Tier two the user is able to hit a target most of the time. At the end of tier two the mage will be experimenting with conjuring Fire\nballs. Its said by Tier three the mage can conjure small fire balls successfully which they can conjure as Explosive or just normal. They can also vary the temperature of their fire. \n\n((Ooc: If you dont emote Fatigue you aren't doing it right.))\nUnless you are tier five and you are conjuring a small Spark. Even if you are Tier five you can still have Fatigue depending on how big the flame. Attempting to summon white hot flames. eah, not a great idea. You would die of heat. Or lack of Mana.\nSummoning fire from a distance takes time. ((Ooc: Summoning fire ON or BENEATH someone isn't allowed.)) You cant mold flames until you start to reach the end of Tier two. Even then you can only just about mold it into a ball of fire. With difficulty.\n((Ooc: Controlling a flame that is in the Physical world and was made in the Physical world, not drawn from the void would be considered power gaming.)) You will have increased heart rate, breathing heavily and will still get sweaty at levels above tier 3\nFrom personal experiences I learnt that when pulling from the void it feels like 'tugging a rope to pull something from nothingness.'\n\nI hope this book helped you with what you were looking for about Fire Evocation.\n/Signed Garsto Leaf./\n((Ooc: If I find you use this for some description wether its for the lore of your magic application or anything else. I will make a comment on your post saying its a copy of what I wrote origionally for when I tried to apply for magic.))", ""),
