        StaticBook("146-1", "Fabius Bracchus", "Imperial Voter\nIdentification Card          \nName: Uthred Gromach\n\nYear of Birth: 1673\n\nResidency: Carolustadt\n\n146-1", ""),
        StaticBook("1668, Contract", "Horad", "DEAINN MERTZA, Let it be known by this here contract, under Codigum Articles 7, 17, 26 and 27, through the investiture of Article 19, That Horad Cain var Andest, Apostolic Baron, Holy Knight of the Canon, Prince of Seventis and Savoy\nEnfeoffs one Wilbur West with the property of Fields of Cenere, under the jurisdiction of Master Crozier, Pierre De Roth, and hereby allowed to plough and harvest the fields therein.\nHe is required to provide the Chantry with 27 bushels of grain every saint’s week. (single chest of wheat stacks)\n\n\n------------\nHerein lay signatures of the parties.\n--Horad Cain var Andest, Holy Knight of the Canon, Commander of the Blessed Chantry of the Clarion, Apostolic Baron of Judeberg, Count of Salerne, Prince of Savoy and Seventis.\n--Wilbur West.\n\n\n\n\n-*---*---*---*---*-", ""),
        StaticBook("1668, Contract-a", "Horad", "Lo, Deainn Mertza.\nBy investiture of His Lordship;\nHorad Cain var Andest, Holy Knight of The Canon, Commander of the Blessed Chantry of the Clarion, Apostolic Baron of Judeberg, Count of Salerne, Prince of Savoy and Seventis;\n-----------\nHe who holds this paper, a Man by the name of Wilbur West, has been granted the title of Yeoman of Cenere, and given the duties to manage, keep, plough and mantain the fields under the Chantry's lands. He is to provide Twenty-seven (27) ---\nbushels of wheat grain. (a single chest of stacks of wheat), every saint's week to an authority of the chantry. (Refer to Commander Horad, Warden Pierre or Captain Reeve.).\n\n\nHEREIN LAY SIGNATURES\n--Horad Cain var Andest Holy Knight of the Canon, Commander of the Blessed Chantry of the Clarion, Apostolic Baron of Judeberg, Count of Salerne, Prince of Savoy and Seventis.\n\n\n--Wilbur West, Yeoman of Cenere.", ""),
