        StaticBook("6", "Ehier", "Here's the passport you ordered\n\n500 minas in the bank account of the letter-carrier.\n\nIf i dont get my money, your fate will burn", ""),
        StaticBook("7 II III I", "Oracle", "The Theory of Magical Engineering\n\nRetold by Leyu'Maehr\n\nOracles Library\n\n20th of Snows Maiden -1443\nFirstly, you will need a suitable conduit for the Magical Imbue. Any piece of equipment should suffice, although wood lacks the endurance for a imbue. I suggest using Iron - rough, yet strong and dependable.\n(Much like dwarves, harhar!) Then, you will need to create the Magical Imbuement to be used on the empty shell (Catalyst). This is the tricky part! You will need to lay magical runes onto the Catalyst, runes that- summarise what the object's use will\nbe. For Instance, a crossbow created to pierce metal should be imbued with runes of Breaking, Unbinding, Smashing ectetera. Hopefully, this will help you create magically imbued item of your own! If you want to know more, you should consult my\nother guides on Artificing. Thanks for Reading! PS. This book has been imbued with runes of self-destruction. Ha Ha, Gotcha!", ""),
        StaticBook("8 Elements C1", "Jaya Jayamen", "8 Elements\n\n               ~by Jaya\n               Jayamen\nChapter One\n  The Adventurers \n          Guild\n\nI opened my eyes to a scene. I was in a dark room. There was a man in black clothes with a sword up against some girl’s throat in front of him.\nAcross the room from him was myself. I was clothed in light green robes.  There were also 8 pedestals in the room.  The dark clothed man spoke,\n\n“You, stay back or the girl dies.” To which the other me responded.\n“I am not afraid of you. I know your kind, dark magic, you just want the power in the temple!” to which he responded\n\n“Stay back! Or the girl dies.” To which the other me responded,\n“You won’t be able to harm her, you may have been trained in the dark, but I have been trained in the light!” At this the other me’s body started shining incredibly bright, blinding me from then scene. I then woke up with a start.\nPanting, I tried to calm myself down from the dream. I looked out of my window. It was still dark out. Sighing, I laid back down in my bed. What a dream… I thought. Then a thought clicked in my mind, today was the day I enter the Light adventurers guild.\nI lived in Revan town. A place that is a sub-city in the Light tribe’s land. The land was half city half forests. I had been feeling a bit uneasy about joining the guild, there was a test that no one was allowed to talk about.\nWell at least not about what is in the test. I wonder if it would be hard, what type of test would it be? Slowly but surely, I drifted back into sleep.\nWhen I woke up the next morning things started alright, I woke up to the smell of bacon. I slowly sat up from my bed. I got up and god dressed, equipped my sword, and headed into the kitchen.\n“Good morning Lethan.” Said my mother, placing a plate full of food on the table.\n\n“morning mom.” I replied, taking a seat. I began to dig into the meal.\n“Made you a big breakfast, I’m proud you are going to the adventurers guild.” My mom said to me as I ate. “It’s not easy being a part of the guild, from what I’ve heard from friends at least.”\nI stopped eating a moment swallowing some food and said, “I have been looking forward to it. I have been anxious about it for the last week.”\n“I’m sure you will do well.” Replied my mom. “Just do your best and I’m sure things will go well.”  To which I nodded finishing up my food.\nWhen I finished my food, I got up and got my backpack, in it I had a map of the town, a skin with water, some other things like rope, my invitation letter to the Light Adventurers Guild, and finally an old music box about half a foot large.\nThe music box was something I had found while I played in the woods years ago. I could wind the key, but it never played after I wound it. I figured it was jammed.\nI took it with me because this was the last time I would be home for a while. Adventurers guild members live at the guild.\nI turned to my mom and nodded my head. “I guess it’s time to go.” I said, “I love you mom, I’ll do my best.” To which my mom embraced me in a hug saying,\n“Be safe and come visit often.” Nodding at her after the hug, I then headed out the door to the Light Adventurer’s Guild.\nThe Light Adventurers Guild was located at a large building on the edge of a huge forest at the side of town. I walked up to the large building very nervous from the sight of the imposing building.\n. I took a moment to take in the sight and then walked into the large doorway of the building. As I walked down the large hallway I could hear odd noises coming from some of the rooms,\nwhat sounded like a lecture from others, and other types of noises from the rest of the rooms.\nMy invitation had said to go to the office at the end of the hall from the entrance to the guild. I continued walking down the hall until I got to a doorway. Cautiously I knocked on the door. A voice said,\n“Come in!” I turned the handle and went inside. As I Walked in the room I noticed myself feeling a sense of calm and peace. In the room was a desk, two chairs in front of it and one larger chair behind it,\nthere was also two large bookshelves at the back of the room. In the large chair behind the desk sat a young woman with blond hair.\n“You must be new, may I see your invitation please?” I nodded and walked to the desk taking off my backpack. I undid the latch on my bag rummaged inside it taking out a slightly crumpled invitation. I then handed it to the lady.\nThe young woman took the invitation and studied it thoroughly. After a few minutes she said, “everything checks out. Welcome to the guild Lethan.”\n\n“Thank you maim. “I replied, to which she laughed lightly.\n“please, call me Jenna.” She said. She opened a drawer in the desk and pulled out a key, a piece of paper, a map, and a ring.  She placed these items one by one on the desk.\n“the key is to your room, the map here will guild you to your classes and your way around the guild, this paper has all of your classes listed on it, finally this ring symbolizes that you are a member of the Light Adventurers Guild.\nYou will have three roommates. Kevan, Jess, and Closen. Kevan is a student from the Fire Adventurers Guild, Jess is a student from the nature guild, and Closen is a Member of our guild, the Light Adventurers guild.”\nI simply nodded taking in all the information. Jenna then said, “you have about an hour to get settled in, then you will be taking your first class, Free for all.”\nI raised a brow slightly at this, “I didn’t realize I would be taking a class so soon.” I said. “What kind of class is free for all?” to which Jenna smiled a bit and said.\n“It is a class where students show what they can do. The objective is to reach the flag in the middle of the training ground. You cannot kill or maim anyone, only light injuries are permitted. The rest will be explained at the start of the class.”\nI nodded with a slight gulp. Then I remembered something. “what about the test? I thought there was one I needed to take before joining.”\n\n“The free for all serves at a test in itself. “said Jenna.\n“I and others will be observing your skill and the other students’ skills as it goes on. As for passing or failing the test, if your abilities are not good enough, you will be put in learning classes helping you get to a basic level.\n. If you do well, you will take normal classes, if you exceed expectations, you will be put in advanced classes. Understand?”\n\n“yes.” I said, now much more nervous than when I entered.\n“better hurry to your room, and don’t be late for the class!” I nodded and exited the room.", ""),
        StaticBook("8 Elements C2", "Jaya Jayamen", "8 Elements\n\n           ~By Jaya\n            Jayamen\nChapter 2\n        Boom\n\nI started following the map to my room, Room 12, Light quarters. “I can’t believe that I was going to be in a combat class so soon. “I thought.\n“I only have a basic ability in light power, I am doomed to be in the learning classes.” \n\nI turned left and saw up ahead that two guys had another smaller guy pinned to a wall. The pinned guy said, “Hey let go, I’m warning you.”\n“or what, “said one of the guys, “you going to shoot sparks at us fire guy? “ \n\n“I might” said the pinned guy with an angered look.\n“go ahead, we’ll turn you inside out by the time you try.” Said the other guy pinning down the other. “get him!”\n\n“hey, leave him alone! “I said sternly. The two guys pinning down the other turned towards me with amused looks.\n“looks like we have a hero here.” Said one of the guys pinning the other down. “you should think be- “the guy was cut off by the pinned down guy starting to glow they turned to him and had a horrified look on their faces.\n“you can’t be doing that, that is a master level technique! You’ll blow us all up!” The pinned down guy just laughed and said, \n\n“too late!” Suddenly the pinned down guy seemed to be engulfed in flames. He turned to me and said, “Shield yourself!”.\nthe other two guys backed off, one started gathering electricity in his hand, the other was also gathering electricity in his hand.  Taking his advice, I shielded myself the best I could.\nFrom this shield I could withstand a novice level attack, but if they were right that he was using a master level technique I hoped that the distance was enough to lessen the blow of whatever was to happen.\nThe two using electricity were about to shoot it at the fire guy when the fire guy exploded with flames, sending the two electricity using guys flying against the opposing wall.\nThe flames engulfed the hallway and when the exploding flames got to me my shield instantly broke and I was forced backwards flying a few yards. I landed roughly on the ground, the air knocked out of me.\nI groaned and slowly sat up. I noticed I wasn’t burned to a crisp, that was at least good, I wasn’t burned at all though my head was still recovering from the blast.\nI looked to where the other students had been, the two electric users were knocked out cold and against the wall, the fire using guy was hurriedly making his way towards me.\nHe said “Hey there man! The names Kev, we’d better get away before a teacher comes. That was a pretty weak barrier you made. “he smiled and offered his hand.  Hesitantly I took it and hoisted myself up. Still not fully recovered I said,\n“That was some blast.” To which Kev replied,\n\n“I’ll say! I controlled the flames so it just was forceful, little to no heat from it. Come on this way, let’s get to my room!”\nKev half led half pulled me down the hallway passed the two electric users. We eventually came up to a room that had the number 12. “here it is!”\n“wait… Kev, is that short for Kevan?” \n\n“huh? “he said, “how did you know my real name?” to which I replied.\n“I just joined the school today, was told that you and two others would be my roommates.” Kev thought a moment then smiled, \n\n“Sounds great! I can’t wait to see what you can do! I hope that flimsy barrier isn’t your best!”\n!” I nodded and Kev unlocked the door and went inside as I followed. In the spacious room were four large beds each with their own drawers. There was also a large table in the middle.\nSitting at the table reading a book was a young girl with brown hair, she said, \n\n“Blowing up people on your first day Kev?” to which Kevan replied with a laugh,\n\n“yea, I guess so!” The girl just sighed and said,\n“brainless as always. Who’s with you?”\n\n“oh, this is, erm… “Kev paused for a moment then said to me, “what’s your name?”\n\n“Lethan. “I said\n“Lethan!” Kev repeated.\n\n“Well good to meet you Lethan. “said the girl in a bored tone, “I would keep away from Kev unless you like trouble.”\n\n“bah!” said Kev, “I don’t cause trouble, trouble finds me!”\nSuddenly someone behind us said, “it was him!” we turned around to see what looked like a teacher with one of the electric using guys pointing at Kev. The teacher gave Kev a stern gaze.\n“You have some explaining to do. Follow me.” Kev looked at the teacher, and said,\n\n“they provoked me, I don’t know what they would have done if I hadn’t acted up!”\n“he’s lying!” said the electric user, to which the teacher said,\n\n“enough! We will talk about this in my office, now walk!” Keven sighed and went out with the teacher, but before leaving said, “Nice meeting you Lethan, hopefully I’ll catch up- “\n“move!” said the teacher cutting him off. \n\n“alright alright…” said Kev.\n\nA few moments after they had left, I looked back at Jess, who was still studying her book,\nseemingly unaffected by what had just happened. I then took this time before the free for all to get my things unpacked and rest a bit.", ""),
        StaticBook("8th Malinor Text", "Galdin", "Grand Harvest:\n\nTranscribed by Peurith, Scribe of Malin\nIn these recent years we’ve known nothing but loss. Our father hopes that a return to tradition will remind people of better times a-...(the text is missing).  Dancing for months, great festive lamps that light up the sky as brightly as the sun, exotic\ndishes-...(more missing text).. perhaps will bring our people back together as one. At least, the is what the Forefather hopes.", ""),
