        StaticBook("A Cycle", "Katherine Liverflower", "Rain\n\nIt falls from the heavens\n\nIts descent is a constant battle to keep itself together\n\nIt falls without question of its purpose\nRacing ahead blindly against all the others\n\nIt falls for a life time\n\nReady to explode itself across the fabric of life\n\nIt falls to allow life to continue through its beauty    \n\n           Rain", ""),
        StaticBook("A Darkened Sleep", "Walter Kyroc", "The Darkened\n         Slumber\n\nA deepened rest, caused by pain.\n\nA darkened past, a tyrant in reign.\n\nA desired friend, a horrendous deed.\n\nBut not a single friend, came in time of need.\nThe best of friends, they thought they were.\n\nBut all of their past, turned into a faint blur.\n\nAnd in his life, the pain would be known.\n\nAnd cause his strife...\n...Over a throne...", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dirty Scroll", "Krim the Kobold", "[!] What appeared to be some sort of plans, or a letter, appears to be partly eaten and scribbled on with various hand prints. Perhaps something is larger to this Kobold band that meets the eye?\n\nPondering this, some words can be made out.\n\"Take ... Crossroad... Ally... Gnolls... Bridge... Soon.\" \n\nWhat did they mean by this?", ""),
        StaticBook("A drawing", "Swikerous Whitlock", "[!] A sheet of paper with a child's drawing of a hobbithole and an halfling, she'd have orange hair and a cyan white dress [!]\n\n*The signature would read Swikerous*", ""),
        StaticBook("A Final Goodbye", "Arthur Wood", "[!] You spot a sob-drenched letter.\nTo he who reads this, if ever, in my final moments, I lament in utter despair. Only three days ago did that hellspawn break into my home and ravage my daughter dead before pulling her off. My Amelia...after the death of her mother in childbirth, she\nwas the only light in my world. We were but simple folk, trying to make it in this unforgiving land. We paid the taxes month by month, and sometimes it was rough, but we always pushed through. After her mother died, she was the only light in my world, and\nnow she's gone. There is no point to keep living in this torturous life. I have the noose prepared, and my moments writing this will be my last. Goodbye, my Amelia. I hope to see you again in the afterlife, with mother...\n\n[!] The letter ends.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Jornheim trip:", "Caenir", "The clang of metal echoed on the bridge, as the Sutican guard planted his foot flat onto the chestplate of the hidious ghoul. The sun bathed them both in its warmth, the sky being as clear as the blue Sutican waters which surrounded the city in Axios. The\nheat had the young dark brown haired guard sweating buckets at a time. The ghoul showed no effects from the heat, only squeals as the guard pinned him up against the bridge's small wall with his foot. As the rays of sunlight beat down upon the guards\nit showed his light, pale face and those forrest green eyes of his. Those eyes which were now locked upon the ghoul fiercely. The ghoul himself was cloaked his face only a black shadow as it lay hidden within its hood. The bridge was a storey above the\nground, all that lay beneath it was a concrete street. As the guard brought his aurum blade down, the tip now at the ghouls throat as he lay flat on the ground. \"I'd give you your last words, but it would be a waste of good air\", the guard spitted out to\nthe ghoul in a blatant distasteful tone. No more than a second afterwards the guard had thrusted the tip of his aurum saber into the throat of the ghoul. A short time of gargling on his blood followed the ghouls last moments before he fell limp and dead.\nA triumphant smile lay on the guard's face, as he sheathed his saber back into the scabbard by his right hip. When from over his shoulder a voice called \"Tyrone! I need a moment of your time!\", the voice sounded urgent. The guard turning to his name still\nwore that smile of his as he recognised the voice greeting \"Ianryil! Good to see you friend, what is so urgent?\". Ianryil was a spook, though he was an exception. He held the rank of 'Officer' within the guards, and had the freedom to live in the Holy\nCity of Sutica. He wores dark robes, his face covered with a mask for obvious reasons. The mask was gray and lifeless only slots for his eyes and mouth was visible. Now by the guard's side, he took a few breathes, clearly having sprinted in a hurry.\n. \"It is Aerith\" he began his breathe still failing him occasionally, \"he has something to tell you\". The guard bearing his comrade's words nodded curtly as he walked past him. \"Come\" the guard beckoned to Ianryil, as the two paced most swiftly for the\ngatehouse. As the two walked eagerly together further down the bridge they came to the steps. Before them now was a high view of the city. Atop the steps they could see loads. the Clock Tower standing powerfully in the square. The quartz pillared houses,\neach with their own unique colour. The guard raising his right hand wiped the sweat from his forehead as he reached the bottom of the steps with Ianryil. The street before them was a straight path, one which like the rest was a smooth stone street. The\ngray, stoned street had some trees and bushes along its fringes. The plant life was nice it gave colour and life to the otherwise dead streets. Within seconds both of them had reached the end of the street. Taking a sharp left turn they climbed a few more\nsteps to the door of the gatehouse. Placing his key into the keyhole the guard turned and opened the door. Greeting the two as they stepped through the threshold was no other than Aerith. A dark elf, dressed casually in a dark grey robe which lay over his\nwhite clothing beneath. Aerith's pigment was slightly lighter than that of his kin. He did have high elven blood in him after all. A worried expression was etched into Aerith's gray face. The brown haired guard arched an eyebrow at his expression asking,\n\"Evening Aerith, what's so important that Ianryil had to come fetch me?\". A nervous Aerith initially fiddled with his hands before scoffing up \"It's a citizen Tyrone, they've been taken by the Frostbeards of Jornheim...\". With every word that reached\nTyrone's ears his face grew grimmer and grimmer. Though Aerith continued \"The Frostbeards refuse to let them return home and say they plan to enslave, if not kill the citizen for the smallest demeanour\". The Frostbeards were by no means a force to be\nchallenged. However, this news of dwarven ignorance and barbarity to the people in which the guard protected outraged him. Pacing through the gatehouse he came to a large wooden chest, of which he opened and pulled back the lid off. A loud exhale found\nits way through the mouth of the guard. Ianryil and Aerith stood in silence for a few seconds. The two seeing Tyrone stare into the pit of the chest, which was placed in the far left corner of the cold, dark gray room. Eventually Aerith stepped forth\nhaving given Ianryil a short glance \"what are we to do?\" he inquired. Tyrone not turning to the two for his eyes were fixed on the light brown wooden chest's content, his expression was still and cold. As his eyes flicked about in the chest for a few\nseconds more a bold smirk entered the right corner of his face. His right hand reaching into the depths of the chest was withdrawn with an iron sword held by its hilt in his grasp. The guard throwing the sword to Aerith finally replied, \"we're going to\ndeal with this... personally\". As the guard strode by the two a new flame had been lit in his eyes. Now in the square he called at the top of his lungs \"ALL GUARDS, RALLY TO THE SQUARE!\". Aerith and Ianryil stepped out of the gatehouse only to be met by\nthe guard's shout to arms. Within moments sevral guards had rallied. Ana of one was a young brown haired woman, only recently brought into the guard force. Richard being another, also a new enough guard with a stubble of brown hair. He had prvoen to be\nmost arrognat in his young age though like everyone his assisstance would be needed for this mission. Finally, Kary, the Lord Protector of Sutica came briskly into the square, looking to all the guards. \"What's going on here? That merits such a shouting\nand rally?\". The guard stepped forth dipping his head respectfully, \"I was told a citizen had been taken by the Frostbeards and is to be killed, if not sold into slavery Kary!\". Kary had always been one for a good crusade and quest. He came to the guard's\nopinion too. \"Very well Tyrone, and you wish to get back this citizen?\". The guard offered a nod of his head as nothing more needed to be said. \"I shall accompany you all then\", Kary said cooly almost as a man who couldn't wait for a good march. A smile\nnow visible on the guard's face was turned to the guards before him, \"Well what are yous waiting for? LINE UP!\". A patriotic feeling went through all the guards in the square. To stand up for Sutica always pumped the blood of these heroic guards.\nNo task was too much or too little. This was now had become a national interest. Lined up, the guards checked to ensure they had the necessary weapons for the upcoming task. When done the line of guards turned for the main gate. The guard who initiated\nthis task took his position at the front. Behind him was Kary, Aerith, Richard and Ana in that order. As the guard beckoned the five to start marching out of the city following his lead, Ianryil stuck his head of the gatehouse to say \"I'll man the gate,\nuntil yous return Tyrone!\". \"Much appreciated\" the guard replied now already making his way down the bridge. From the bridge the company made their way through the freezing snow covered land which surrounded Sutica to the north. Passing by the\nsnow-capped mountains of Ceru the company of crusaders stayed strong. The loud, howling winds blew all around them. The noise almost sounded like a cry to dissaude or unhearten the heroes, but it did not succeed. After several hours the company had come\nto the docks. A sigh of relief escaped most of the party, as Richard was first to start \"T-t-that as f-freezing, I don't know how my stubble managed to stay on!\". A light chuckle escaped Ana as she jested \"I always knew that was stuck on and you couldn't\ngrow actual hair!\". Before Richard had the time to retort the leading guard raised his right hand, \"Cease!\" he exclaimed to the group as he continued \"From here he will ferry across these treacherous waters until reach Tahn. When there, we will follow the\nmain road north which will take us to Jornheim, understood?!\". \"Yes sir!\" a united call emitted from the group, though not from Kary who whispered to the guard, \"The Frostbeards are by no means an easy push Tyrone... what is your plan?\". As\neveryone of Kary's words fell on the guard he kept his smile, he called back, in by no means a whisper, \"We will win cause we are Suticans! Who will not be seens as weak!\". A partriotic cry of \"Glory to Sutica!\" came from the party, straight after the\nguard's words. Kary couldn't help but smile at the spirit of the men who served his nation. No more words were spoken as the company all hopped aboard the ship, which had been harboured in at the docks. Shortly after a sailor came out to greet the guards,\n\"Sooticans ye' be aye? Load what ye' 'ave unto me ship 'ere and we can get goin'. The sea is suppos' to be rough tonight if you ask m'\". As the guard walked past the sailor he gave a light pat on his shoulder, \"Many thanks sir, we will need to sail for\nTahn. We do not have anything to take with us bar what we hold\". The sailor surveying the crew with a hesitant look swallowed as he went to mount the steps to the steering wheel of his ship. \"Tha's some distance from home for you lot, though it's not m'\njob to inquire\". \"I hate sailing\" a moany Richard complained as he rested his elbows on the far side of the ship looking out to the deep blue sea. The guard walking up to Aerith said \"Untie the knots which keep this shipe harboured there's\nno need to waste more time than is neceassry\". After his words Aerith nodded acknowledgingly as walked back down the plank to the harbour where he made his attempt to untie both knots, one at the front the other at the back. While the knots were being\nunfastened the guards prepared the sails for sea; as the Captain stood by the wheel. With no knots and everyone aboard the ship tooks its course into the deep blue depths of the ocean, the harbour becoming just an ever growing smaller port. Not much was\nspoken as the group sailed over the sea. Many like myself, just took in the view. It must have been a two day journey before the ship reached a harbour at Tahn. Despite some storm clouds in the distance the trip was quite pleasant with the wind in our\nback. As the party of guards departed form the ship, the guard handed the sailor a bag of minae before departing. A joyous expression crossed the features of the sailor's face as he waved to the five leaving guards; wishing them luck and fortune in their\nendeavour. As the guard took his place at the front of the line again, he called to those behind \"Retake your positions!\". In no more than a few seconds the guards were back in their five man line. Kary now behind the leading guard tapped his shoulder\nmuttering, \"Tyrone, you know the way to go still, aye?\". The guard with a nod of his head replied in a calm tone \"Of course\", shortly before raising his voice to the group \"We are taking the road North. Upon reaching the square we shall take the cart to\nJornheim, understood?\". With a united \"Understood!\" from his fellow men they began their march North. The march was not long. Even Richard managed to keep his mouth shut for the march. Bystanders whispered to the people they were with, all the while\nkeeping a suspicious type of eye contact with the Sutican guards, as they marched through the square for the Jornheim cart. The leading guard took the cart driver's hand in his given a firm shake as he greeted \"Evening sir, me and my men need to get to\nJornheim perhaps you can take us?\". A greedy smile crossed the man's face as he stared down the party of guards, \"And what would take a rally like yours to a place like that?\", the man's voice was full of condescension to the Frostbeards as he spoke. The\ngurad shook his head irritably, \"that is out business, we just need a way there.\" he hissed back as his right hand slipped into his pouch why his right hip. Retrieving a small bag of minae the guard handed it over, measly stating \"Perhaps this will rest\nyour mind friend.\". The man without question stuck the bag of minae into his cloak with an audible chuckle, \"Aye, no worries at all, come\". All the guards climbed upon the cart as it took off for Jornheim. The guard turned to his party as he stated,\n\"ready your weapons men, I will explain the plan when we arrive\". The cart tossing and turning with every stone it hit on the road finally came to a stop when the driver pulled the reign on the horses. \"Here ye are!\" he exclaimed, watching the guards", ""),
        StaticBook("A Journal", "Gantar 'The Just'", "You are the jewel to my ring. The heart of my being. The spirit to my soul. The words within the book of my life. You are the beautiful, glorious sunrise to the general sunset that is my life. When you leave, my colours turn to grey....\nAnd when you frown, a little bit of me dies. And I don't like dying. If I can, I'd like to dedicate the rest of my life trying to keep you from frowning, , and make you the happiest woman I can,\nso that I can return upon you at least a fraction of the joy you bring to me.\n**A ring would be inside some carved out papers**\n\n  Will you marry me?", ""),
        StaticBook("A Krugsmas Card", "Alfius", "[!] It's a Krugsmas Card from Alfius. There's a picture of him infront of his manor, waving and smiling.\n\n[!] There's some writing on the back.\n[!] It reads:\n\"Dear Pad and Millie,\n   Thank you both so much for bringing me so much joy here in Belvitz and for being such good friends. I got these gifts for you in hopes that they will be of use and bring you joy, however, I do warn you . . .\"\n\" . . . that I am not the best gift giver. But nonetheless, here are the gifts I got you.\"\n\"The rapier and the vest are for Padrick, he is the protector of the family and a good one at that. He's always ready to protect those close to him.\"\n\"The peeler and necklace are for Millie. The peeler will help her make exquisite meals for the family and I am positive she will look even more wonderful with the necklace.\"\n\"And for Finn I got him a tool knife, because if he's anything like . . .\"\n\". . . his father, he will want to protect and help those he cares for too.\"\n\"For Erika I got the shiniest diamonds I could find as well as a ball of yarn for her, I hope she likes the color. She's always playful and will hopefully love it.\"\n\"Like I said before, I'm not the best gift giver, but I hope these will bring you all some joy. I wish you all a very merry Krugsmas. I am so lucky to have you all.\"\n\n   - Alfius", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Morrigyn", "To whom it may be concerned,\n\nThe clinic has once again returned to a sad state. I ask for a small budget to re-renovate it to an opperational state. Beyond that, I can also seek out replacement staff and will teach people if neccesary. \nMorrigyn.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Silveress", "[!] Amongst the items\nand trinkets inside of \nthe trunk would be\nanother note with frayed edges. A deep\nblue ink would scrawl across the page with a font of all capital letters - a script that the recipient would recognize.\nMystery,\n\nI'm sorry that things had to be this way.\n\nI know that you're mad at me, but just know that I was your friend, up until you wouldn't let me be. And I still would be if it -\nwouldn't jeporadize my other relationships.\n\nYou see, in some weird, upsetting way, I'm thankful for what you've done to put me here. You've nearly singlehandedly given me friends I'll care about for years.\n... But I don't like what you've done to hurt others. This was supposed to be fun, but I realize now that it stopped being fun a really long time ago.\n\nI'm sorry that you haven't had the foresight to see where your actions would lead.\nJust know that with your banishment, I have in mind not the person you are today, but the friend that helped me dearly all those years ago.\n\nI hope that you keep in mind the vision of me of the past, before this group\nand the prospect of keeping it alive destroyed us both.\n\nI hope that you find someone like-minded enough to compliment your ideas, but smart enough to keep you out of trouble. I'm sorry that person wasn't me.\nThank you, but goodbye.\n\n• S", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Graham Milner", "Mr. Mauntel,\n\nSir, I'm volunteering myself for the diplomatic mission to Blackreach in the future in whatever capacity you might find me fitting, discluding architect. I would be happy to be considered.\n     \n       -Graham Milner", ""),
        StaticBook("A Letter", "Taren", "-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-Of all the wish I did, this is not one of them. Running away was an irrational attempt of escaping duties, problems and people. On and on...\nI really want you to forgive me, mother. I've been a terrible son and I wish I wouldn't be so\nstubborn over something so trivial like problems. I really hope that I will see you all again sometime. Take care of my sisters, please. Tell my 'father' that I'm sorry for being a horrible son, and tell everyone else that I wish them all to be well.\nLove Taren\n\n\n[!] The letter was signed with a picture. The picture had a head of a hoopoe, a poorly drawed one.\n\n\n\n\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "Rose Bell", "Dear Adrias,\nIf you're reading this, then you've been searching for something that does not belong to you.\nMy daughter isn't involved with the problems of you and I. And if I am gone by the time you come looking for this, then please spare my Rose.\nI want her to live in peace. I've spent many years insuring  that she's safe from you and others. If I am dead, I can not do so. So I beg you brother, please spare the life of my innocent Rose. She is pure and kind and does not know the many evils of\nthe world. Adrias, my heart still morns for you and your family. Mother and father think you to be dead, and our brother's and sisters want to as well. But it brakes my heart, to know the troubles of the world have blacken your heart so much, my twin.\nAfter you killed your beloved Gwendaylnn and the Dornan family, I was scared you would come after our family. Brother the value of Mina is none of equal of that, of a life. And if you read this, I hope that you have grasp this concept with my own daughter\nI fear everyday, that you will find her and I and seek for our life.  I don't have many words to say except the sweetness of mercy, I hope finds you. Nevertheless, our family isn't fond of Karlia, and thinks illy of our beautiful Rose. Such as you, we\nhave been casted out. Mother and Father, have storng ideas of how we should live, seperate of our own. Our Brother Andre and his wife Julie have been more accepting of Karlia, Rose and I, but the burdens of Mother's power in the family is great. That said\nBrother, I am willing to forgive you of all your sin. You are my brother, and I do share my heart for you. But if I am unable to do so, then I am sorry that my death came to soon.\nI ask you brother, in life and death, to please, spare my sweetest Rose.\n\nWith the purest love,\nAdrian", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter from K", "Kæthryn Ojørna", "Dear Thomas,\n By the time you are reading this letter, I have already saddled Callus and left. I have left Kjarten warmly wrapped in my home in my bed.\n If you have not noticed yet, Kuyouch is also gone. He has come with me. Thomas, I love you. ->\nBut Rivia is not for a woman like me. I have a restless soul. I mustn't become planted within a walled city. I am Nomad.\n\n    I hope you do not hate me long. Do not hunt me down or send letters.\n\n\n      Farewell,\n|\\|-|/|\n                             K", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter.", "Elizaveta vas Ruthern", "To the Brotherhood of St Karl. \n\nRecently there has been many issues regarding specific people within the Haenseti state. A list of names are as followed:\n\nWilliam Inkstone, Ranholf and Coltaine.\nFirst of all,\n\nWilliam Inkstone:\n\nWith further investigation it comes to me that he is indeed part of the Brotherhood. And yet he is a push over, whom bends to the will of those whom oppose him.\nEarlier a few saints days ago, Ranholf and another armoured friend of his - forced his arm to call me 'Goblina' - that was their only requesr as the un-named armoured fellow was strangling me.\n\nWilliam, however decided to take this further and say that my mother never wished for my birth. So instead she drank in hopes it would cause me to be stillborn. Instead that it was the cause of my crippled state and that I am a abomonation to God.\nRanholf: A known dread knight. Whom has layed hands upon children of Markev. Bullied and belittled myself for being crippled. He continues to try and cause suffering to other folk. This is not acceptable.\nColtaine: He acompanied the man named Ranholf to help aid the torment the pair with to put upon other people. Both him and Ranholf attacked an innocent man within Markev and your men stood idle.\n\nThey did nothing, simply watched this man be beated bloody.\nThe same occured to myself, I was strangled. Pinned and belittled. Upon multiple occasions, I reported it to a man named Einhart and he did nothing but be condescending. \n\nKaryssmov, stood idle. Whilst Ranholf's armoured friend strangled me.\nEihart did not react to these menaces until it broke out into a fight between a man named Jib (who began the harassment upon myself. The man threatened to kill me and push a bookshelf to crush my ribs) and Karyssmov.\nIt has gotten to the point where I am no longer willing to bite my tongue, your men are showing them selves as incapable cowards. \n\nThis matter is either dealt with, with an iron fist. Or it will be brought to the Aulic council and King Sigmar.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter.", "[Okarir'maehr] Odessa Visaj", "\"I request you to consider apologising again. Quench your pride and the lilies may blossom.\"\n\nOkarir'maehr\nOdessa Visaj", ""),
        StaticBook("a lib christmas", "Gynn Alandris", "Merry Chrimbo Liam\nyou fucking libtard\n\nlet's play it off boys\n\n\n--------------->\nNEXT PAGE\nliam bells\ndiesel smells\nhe works at subway\nhours long of easy\nwork\nmaking sammies all day\nhey\nliam bells\ndiesel smells\nlibtards are super gay\nhave fun in canada\nyour mom fuckin gay\njoy to the world\nthe government's shut down\nfinally we can build this wall\nwe've waited two long years\nfor something to bring us cheer\nand now the Don has come\nand the Dems now own the shutdown...\nlook man\n\ndonald trump deserves all his mar-a-lago trips\n\nit's hard all the pressure the libs put on him. lay off okay, he's doing his best.\nhave a merry ch-\n\nhappy holidays fuck i forgot\n\nboycott starbucks\nthis war on chrimbo has begun\n\n\nwe must fight back with donald\n\n-whumplsish", ""),
        StaticBook("A little note", "Aerilith Oakenarrow", "Dear Caara, \nwhen you read this note you have opened my gift, i wanted to give you this as a sign that i need you. You made my life infinitly better and i hope that you accept it. I worked very hard to get all these for you. Lots of love. -Signed Aerilith", ""),
        StaticBook("A Love Letter", "Lathai", "M'lady, I know you barely met me, but I wish to be more then just you're friend. Your silk tan skin smells of love that I'd like to cherish forever in my heart. I want you forever and forever until the nights grow dark. I want to know you're true feelings\nof me, so we can cherish our relationship forever.\n\nPs. Confront me first, before throwing this letter away.\n\nFrom: Lathai To: Kaia", ""),
        StaticBook("A Lover's Day.", "Kili Al-Deen", "they shine brightly in the moon lit gaze,i have traveled near and far yet seen not such beauty as this\nlike a diamond strong and proud yet pretty and pleasing to the eye.their touch is of a gentil flower on a warm sunny day,their voice is soft and\ngentil that fills the heart with a warm reassurance and a aw that makes you feel as thuo you have been touched and carryed away by a cloud,you get lost in their gaze as one gets lost in a sunset and your mood rises like the sun in the dawn. you yearn\nto be around them with and want to see their smile and happyness you feel as if its your duty to make them smile and joyfull.thy are my warm sunrise and Beautiful jem.to rise before you and make you your favorite dish and bring you roses of compasi\nhonnor and love that goes to no one but you,My dear love.\n___________________\n\n         By:Kili Al-Deen\n      (ibraheemc2000)\n\nnotes from writer:\nI made this for the enjoyment of the read and the warmth of the heart-Kili Al-Deen.", ""),
        StaticBook("A moldy journal", "Beltran", "[!]The script below is written in a shaky, but experienced hand. As you read through the journal, the letters slowly turn red as ink is replaced with blood.\n\"It grips me, this madness. It coils through my bones, the very sickness in my flesh. The holes have started to appear, symptoms of this unholy disease. I fear our time is at an end.\n\nBrother Grimsby has advised us to pray to our lord,\nso that the lord's water may sweep us away to peace, but what peace shall I know if these waters are the very root of our sickness? Even now, I ponder upon the legitimacy of our god.\"\n\n\n1570 Brother Hosei\n\"Brother Lackmin was the first to fall out of our congregation. We buried his screaming corpse in our first grave. The other's are no better. Even now, I see the rotted specks of black upon their eyelids, hint of the corruption within them.\nThe great serpent has made it's visit again. It seems to detest our diseased bodies. Though I write this entry by candlelight, I still remember it's yellow eyes.\"\n\n\n\n1570 - Brother Hosei\n\"Brother Grimsby was the last who fell, except for me. Else the hint of rot on my body, I do not seem to be sucumbing to the rot as my fellows. I call it blessed, but Grimsby named me foul. 'God's water does not wash you away to his embrace' he chortles-\nas he reanimates. I had no choice but to smash his skull open, less he does the same to me.\"\n\n\n\n\n1570 -Brother Hosei\n[!]The script below appears in a chaotic, loopy script, a noticeable difference from the previous pages.\n\n\"It is me. I am chosen. I kneel at the alter and he speaks to me. The crimson waters flow from my flesh but yet he demands more.\n'a sacrafice, a sacrafice' they whisper in my ears. My Brother's voices pester for life, but even stab after stab, slice after slice, they do not abide.\"\n\n\n\n\n1571- Brother Hosei\n[!]A picture of a snake fills the entire page, printed in crimson are the words 'It Watches, my time has come.'", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Axel Swale", "[!]\n A Letter is left in the saddle bag, it reads:\n\n This Llama is property of Axel Swale", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note", "Hearth", "No hard feelings~\n-Hearth\nPs: Enjoy the cider\nP-Ps: No more attacking please", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note to Lyeth", "Acaele", "Many greetings to you, Lyeth\n\nI am not certain that I will be remembered, though your recollection is certainly keener than most. \n\nI write to you with the quill of Acaele Lazul. I believe we last had occasion\nto speak a century or more's past.\n\nI write to you directly in part because I am uncertain of some particularities of the application process and in part because we have something of a professional\nhistory to speak of.\n\nI inquire firstly as to whether more scholars are sought to advance the library's purpose.\n\nOver the centuries as I'm sure we are both aware, the\nimmortal will find time and circumstance to don many hats and sets of robes.\n\nI find my options in the Silver City limited by years of social and political decay. In such a condition, I feel I should be able to contribute more in\nservice to the Dragur than I might be capable of in my homeland's current state. \n\nI write to ask also, should space in this academic refuge be available, whether an additional written work will be required of me.\nThere remains on the Third Floor a copy of my report on Orias, a service I rendered in good faith to your order some time past now.\n\nI have various fledgling ideas to put to paper whether this is to be done before or after a tentative\ninduction to your rank. I only ask so that, should I be able to begin sooner, I might conduct these works with the resources of the library behind me. \n\nElse, do let me know, and I shall endeavor to produce one\nbeforehand and prove what worth I may have.\n\nThank you for your time, and what support you may be able to lend in what I see as our joint quest for knowledge and collective advancement. I look forward to your\nresponse, and doubtless the graceful penmanship of a hand so well trained. \n\nAn old friend,\n\nAcaele Lazul", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note!", "Estrid", "Galanthil -\n\nI regret that we haven't had a chance to meet again! Snow was Sneothora, the woman who was supposed to be living with me. I went a year and a half living here without seeing her before she showed up out of the blue one day. We spoke very\nbriefly before I had to leave. I have not seen her in almost three years now. I hate to think what may have happened to her, but I assume it is safe to say she is not going to be returning. I live alone now, I suppose! I thank you for the gift, and I do\nhope you enjoy my gift in return. It is a bit strange to come home to find packages in my home, but I can't really complain about sweets! I wish you a wonderful day.\n\n~ Estrid Mildrathil", ""),
        StaticBook("A Note.", "Laethesia", "[!] A letter has been written here in small handwriting, the letters occasionally curled needlessly.\n\"To Cy, George paid five hundred minas to me for an expansion on his cave house, but he'd like a refund.\n\nHe hasn't built the extra room, I saw the inside myself.\n\n~Lae.\"\n\"P.S. I bought a dog! Its name is Buppy and I would die for it.\n\nP.S.S. Your dog's still great, but mine is better.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A peculiar tome", "ጕጌቻጕጋልኗጌልል ልዪልኗል", "D A G G E R S\n  \n\nI N\n\n  T   H    E\n   \n  D     A       R   K\n   \n                       H    I    G   H\n   \n\n P   R   I   N   C   E\nጕጌቻጕጋልኗጌልል ልዪልኗልዕኗሀጊርኗጊሃ ልነልቻልኗዕረጕኗክልረኗረልዕክጌኗረ ልቿኗፕክዘልዕኗጋልዕጌሁዪፕዐኗዘልዐሁኗሀጌዐኗጌ የጎልዘዐጎዘጌዐዕኗጌልጋዐጌኗጋዐልጌ ጎልቿጎዪኗክልየጎቿጌኗየጎጌቿ ጕጌቻጕጋልኗጌልል ልዪልኗልዕኗሀጊርኗጊሃ ልነልቻልኗዕረጕኗክልረኗረልዕ\nahsrfkanhfanf,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,AASDNGASNGANGJOAGNBJADBGJHABGBAOIGBUOABOUEGFBOUABGOUABDOUGBAOUBGOAUDBTUTGBAURBUBTEUBGA5Y1230759027592768027Y680923Y4U9235BUOB8VCSG9UF31BQ9URB9F9UBRIVB9Q7GF9QBEFYUIQEVRIYUQVIFHYVQIYFVBIQVB9UQ3G59781G3591GRUI1VD97G9V49U53V\nOIAHWROUAHOUHRAOUBUIOTBIBQ3BOQBUOBQTUOETBQUEOTBUQEBTUQEOBTUOQBTUOEBTUOQBOU5JNQO5NOQ5N3OUI5NUO56HUOQHOIQHIOQ3H36YQ3806YQ3805Y8Q3YQ3508YU5Q38Q35Y80Q53YQ358053QY08Q3Y53QY358YQ38Y53Q3085YQ088Y5QQ38Y580Q3Y508Q35Y8Q3508YQ5380Q35Y80Q530853Y80Q35Y08Q350835QY08\nIARNPIAHTAHRT08U3Q5NNKMAGNJKLAFGHIPAFPINAFPHIATEPIHATEBUTAEH ITEQIRBT9QUEHTR0QHET08HQT8EQYTE80HQ08THT803215828528THOUEHTAHFSIOAHFNIOAFNOAFNFAONAFOUAFNUOFEANUAOEBFAEUFBOAUEFBNAOEUFNFAEOUFNOUAENFUOABFUAOEFBAFEOUBAEFOAUEFBUOFABOAUEFBFAOUEFBUAOEFOUFEBOUAFB\nጕጌቻጕጋልኗጌልል ልዪልኗልዕኗሀጊርኗጊሃ ልነልቻልኗዕረጕኗክልረኗረልዕክጌኗረ ልቿኗፕክዘልዕኗጋልዕጌሁዪፕዐኗዘልዐሁኗሀጌዐኗጌ የጎልዘዐጎዘጌዐዕኗጌልጋዐጌኗጋዐልጌ ጎልቿጎዪኗክልየጎቿጌኗየጎጌቿ ጕጌቻጕጋልኗጌልል ልዪልኗልዕኗሀጊርኗጊሃ ልነልቻልኗዕረጕኗክልረኗረልዕክጌኗረ ልቿኗፕክዘልዕኗጋልዕጌሁዪፕዐኗዘልዐሁኗሀጌዐኗጌ የጎልዘዐጎዘጌዐዕኗጌልጋዐጌኗጋዐልጌ ጎልቿጎዪኗክልየጎቿጌኗየጎጌቿ\nH E      W  I  L   L\n\n B  E  T   R   A    Y\n\n                  S T  E  E   L\n\nW I  T  H  I  N \n           \nY    O   U   R\n            \n          T     H   R   O   A  T\nnjadgnjangdnagngadngadjngadjnbagdogadongadnognoadjnojgadnjogdanojgadnjogadnjogadnojgadnjogadnjoagdjongnjoadnjogadnojgadonjga          F   A   T   E\n            I    S\n   P E R M A N E N T\njajabgabjofbajifbiabgigijaebijgbaijhgbiahgbiadhgbgaidbagib", ""),
        StaticBook("A Prophecy", "Ceruberr Asul'Ailer", "Origins all but absolute,\nweave not past my own dispute.\n\nStrands of fate now do entwine\nboth mind and soul are my design.\n\nSafeguard not my children near,\nmine is the vessel of love and fear.\nPity not the weight of strain,\nI do this time and time again.\n\n\n\n- Thurak'Yar\n   Farseer of the Uruk.\n \n   A mysterious\n   prophecy.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Proposal", "Emanaf Delsaran", "Mr. Emanaf Delsaran\n\nA PROPOSAL FOR THE CREATION OF A MINISTER AND ASSISTANTS FOR THE OBSERVATION AND CONTROL OF THE FREE LANDS WITHIN THE DOMINIONS OF MALIN, AND THE SUPERVISION OF SETTLEMENT THEREOF\nDear Sirs -- \n\nFollowing is a proposal for the above purposes, along with a brief Treatment of the need for its adoption, written in Consideration of the recent and ongoing Incident with the Town of Arbor and further problems described below.\nFirst, a statement of the said Problems; these are, to wit:  1st. The lack of a full and detailed Survey of the Territories of the Nation -- this maintaining the Obfuscation of the Extent and Character thereof, and allowing theDevelopment thereof to be\ncontinued by foreign persons and Powers; 2nd. (following the First), the lack of any Knowledge of where the lands of the Nation ends and those of foreign Princes begin, precluding the Defense or Development of the Borders, and the Resolution of Disputes\nregarding Rights to the said Border Territories (for how can disputes be resolved if they are not known! the Foreigners may presently Impose with Impunity, as both they and the Government are ignorant of the Extent of the Boundaries); following,\nThe continuing construction of Manors, Towns, etc. on lands belonging to or claimed by the Nation, by persons or Powers who are foreign to our Land and People, and unknown to our Government, and by their meremotion these said foreign Persons or Powers are\nable to raise Barns, Storehouses, Mills, Fortifications, etc., and harvest Timber, sow Grains, and otherwise Profit by land which they have no Rights upon.\n\nThe unhappy confluence of these three said Problems enabled the\nconstruction of the Town of Arbor, from which has precipitated a certain international Incident, the circumstances of which do not require restating herein.  With this as the chief Example of the deleterious Effect of the problem, there are a number of\npetty Settlements, Manors, Towns, etc. constructed within lands of the Nation (such as their extent is known -- hence point 2, of the paragraph above), which present, if not a danger of the degree of Arbor, an Imposition on the Elvish people.\nIn light of these Concerns I propose the Government of the Nation undertake to create an Office which may resolve them (the said Concerns), by taking responsibility for undertaking, on some helpful Interval, a Full and Detailed Survey of the Territories;\nthe Delineation of the Borders thereof, and the Observation, Investigation, and Management of the said foreign Inhabitants of the Territories; and the appointment of an Elf to the Office, for its Execution, as well as such assistants as may be warrented.\nThis Officer must be empowered to Investigate the inhabitants of these various settlements, once discovered, and ensure their Loyalty to the Dominion as subjects living therein; and levy taxes against them, as the Price of protection by a\nsovereign Power (for to such they will be Entitled, as subjects); and provide for the Resolution of conflicts, if such Arise; and the discovery of hostile Persons and Powers; and to aid in their Removal.\n\nThis Proposal I humbly\nsubmit for your\nLordships’ consideration, as I find it the most expedient and Vigorous solution to the problems above stated.  I am,\n\nYour loyal Servant,\nE. Delsaran~\n\nSeventh Malin’s Welcome, 1645.\nNortheast Building Apt. 2A, Fountain Square, Caras Eldar.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Romantic Poem", "Taynuel", "<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>\n\n     A Romantic Poem\n\n    by Taynuel Faerin\n\n<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>\n<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>\n\nAzure shades of brightest hue\n\nReflecting in those eyes\n\nCascading lights of shining grace\n\nTo rival starry skies\n\n<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>\n<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>\n\nCheeks just like the finest rose\n\nTheir color soft and pure\n\nBlooming with that joyous laugh\n\nAnd smile, so demure\n\n<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>\n<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>\nPlush lips so full and radiant\n\nWith hair of fine-spun gold\n\nSkin as pale as the light of the moon\n\nA heart both brave and bold\n<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>\n<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>\n\nBeautiful beyond compare\n\nAnd fiery, and free\n\nThis gorgeous flower has a thorn\n\nUntameable as the sea\n\n<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>\n<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>\nLet none who gaze upon that face\n\nQuestion such boundless care\n\nFor no one on this mortal plain\n\nCould match a love this fair\n<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>~<>", ""),
        StaticBook("A Scouts Report", "Ithilian Enthelor", "7th of Sun's Smile 1673\n\nReport of Lord Ithilian Enthelor, leader of the Westguard Expidition  to the Yatl Wastelands.\n\nWe just arrived in the area around Poppy Hill. My soldiers have set up camp in the mountains. There has been a big increase in Vaeyl\nactivity all around the Wastelands. I am worrying they may be planning something. our first goal is to scout the terrain of Poppy Hill and then move towards the Vaeyl fort south of there. From there we will cover all of the Wastelands until we hit .......\nFirst Hope.\n\nThe mission at Poppy Hill was a great succes. we discovered a great increase in activity and alot more tents. we also came to know that they are not scared of using the Darkways now. When we followed a group of Vaeyl into the Darkways we saw\nThat it's getting worse. The Travelers have increased in even more numbers and most of the Portals seems to be working now. The darkness is growing bigger and getting more restless in there. need to watch out.\n\nThe mission to the southern fort also was a\nsucces. The amount of Vaeyl there is even bigger, same counts for golems. the terain is the same as at Poppy Hill. Mountains, snow and alot of cold weather. The terrain is no problem for my men, but the animals are. bears, wolfs, and even sometimes ...\nbandits are being a pain for our supplies here. but the morale is alright an we still got ale, so we are going forward and will not return without any information.\n\n-Lord Ithilian Enthelor, Baron of Ihirion. Commander of the Westguard Scouting Regiment.", ""),
        StaticBook("A sealed note.", "Delonna", "King Maric.\n\nIt is with great displeasure that I am unable to deliver these in person. \n\nWhile hunting the Hydra beneath the Embermoor with my Marked Men brothers, I was gravely wounded.\n\nI'm told the Clerics did -\n- their part, however will still be recovering for a long time. \n\nThus I hope this reaches you well, and that you may put it to good use.\n\nIncluded are a number of enchantment scrolls, arrows, and a basic enchanting table which I will give instructions -\n- for using.\n\nMuch of the magical energy required has already been applied, so you should be quite capable of applying the enchantments as you wish.\n\nSimply place a single single on the enchantment table, and you will be able to imbue a piece of armor -\n- with little effort.\n\nAttempting to apply more than one will result in the enchantments conflicting, negating one. \n\nAttempting to apply the enchantments to Carabarum based armor, or already enchanted armor will require an experienced enchanter.\n((Put the book in the enchantment table and shift+rightclick it while holding the item you want enchanted.))\n\nI hope these are of use to your cause.\n- Delonna.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Sealed Scroll", "Caliph Faiz Kharadeen", "Dearest David Campos or any Salvian official,\n\nI hope all is well within the nation of Salvus, may prosperity continue to reign over your lands! I bring you news over the terms of allianceship between our two humble nations.\nThe council meeting of advisors has just finished, and I write this letter fresh after the meeting. \n\nThe council unfortunately have come to the decision of declining any sort of allianceships/defensive pacts\nat this time. 9 against the idea of a defensive pact while 3 in favor. It is a unanimous decision, I am afraid. \n\nEach one has brought up convincing arguments agianst a defensive pact, such as how both our militaries are not prepared\nfor warfare, and the many disadvantages to going to war if it comes to it. We spoke long and plenty on it, and I have to agree with my advisors on this. I am no leader if I desregard what my people want. I am sorry.\n\nMay peace be with you and your people, perhaps in the future things can turn in a different direction.\n\nSigned by,\nCaliph Faiz Kharadeen", ""),
        StaticBook("A slim grimoire", "Unknown", "ＦＡＬＬＥＭ´ＲＯＣＨ\n       ＢＨＡＫＴＡＬ\n         III\n  III     I     III\n   I   I  I  I   I\n   IIIIII I IIIIII\n     I  II II  I\n     II  III  II\n      IIIIIIIII\n        IIIII\n        IIIII\n        I I I\n          `     '\n[!]\nAn odd grimoire with tattered black leather\ncover sits in your hands. By the looks of it, it probably has something to do with magic, but the entirety of the book is written in an odd language that aches the head of those who can't read it.\nHazk,\nmerin'gnu vegaati zu'nokion. \n\nRe'nokion talsh vokarl\nya'pelosr therthe'pelosr-bhaktalserthek-unkra zu'gathan.\nE\nOdurnur blothr zu'kraemsal\n\nDu\nPelosr'basular koneg\nqsuzph'dvemd\n\nDo'nekaro kuram savurr'zu bhakthal.\n\n[]  []  []  []  []  []  []\nKraemsal lerikah odurnur ubyz'fikt koneg vurrsht-chelion\nil do'jhorvastur \nsavurr'vegaati qsuzph'dvemd\n\naza uvot, do'varsku -\nO'ag'vokarl\nE\nDo'odurnur bhatti'dvemd\n\nDu\nDo'kree haurz qsuzph\nkon kreoz'bhaktal\n\n           [!]\n  Pictures have been\n  drawn alongside the\n  instruction.\n[!]\nThe first picture seems to have an odd lump of rock.\n\nIn the second one, some sort of hollow figure has been molded from the ore.\nVe\nDo'kree thur'hadan\nfhi al'kraemsal\n\n   o  -->  ö\n   O        []/\n\neg zmask, a'kyoni Kha.\n\nCul\npelosr'basular koneg'qsuzph\nZin\nDo'infinst qsuzph egodar burz'fhi yatha\n\n\n     Undere dayn!\n\nqsuzph lerikah ezg saiz undere aldunr lerikah al'kraemsal.\n    ö \n  \\[] -> ,;     ✔\n[!]\nAnother set of pictures are on the side. In the first, the figure is made to resemble a kharajyr.\n\nIn the second one, the kharajyr shrinks considerably in size.\n☬\n\n\n\n\n\n                   -1496\n                   - Z.C.", ""),
        StaticBook("a special elf", "Toe", "once upon time\n\nthere was man name adeon\n\nhe hav wite hair and very tall\n\ngood bones and strong muscals\n\ncharm smile\nhe com from band brigade\n\nbrigman say to him \"frend you ned good woman\"\n\n\"no\" adeon say \"iam not for love\"\n\n\"why not??\" frend ask\n\n\"love is for good man\" adoen say \"iam bad...\"\none day adeon meet jarsy stunton\n\na nice prety lady of oran\n\nshe hav blone hair and nice figure\n\nwide hips and tight wast\n\ngood teeth and nice hand\n\"mmMMmm\" say adoen \"helo\"\n\nnice lady blush\n\n\"excus me sir\" she say to him \"i just passin thru\"\n\n\"mmm\" he say \"lets talk\"\n\n\"ok\" say she\nshe falow him and they talk\n\nthe two hava many love nights\n\nBUT one day king of human jon horan say to him\n\n\"go kill monstars i order it\"\n\"but mlord\" say adon \"mwife is pregntn and i love her\"\n\n\"are u married?\" ask jon king horan\n\n\"no...\" adeon reply\n\n\"then go kill\" king say\n \nking is MAD\n\n!!!\non last nite befor hunting seson\n\njarzy water brake\n\n\"oh no!!\" she say \"i dont fel so good...\"\n\n\"he is coming\" adon say\n\n\"iam scared\" she say to him\n\"dont wory\" adeon say \"i believe\"\n\njarsy hold his hand\n \n\"puuuuuush!\" he say to her\n\n\"iiiii ammm!!!\" she say \"is paaainfuuull!\"\n\n\"ok\" adeon say \"breath harder\"\nafter mny hours of intense moment\n\ntwo finlly have cute babby\n\nadeon smile wit jary who is very sweaty\n\nadon kiss jarz forhead\n\n\"good job\" he say\nhapi couple very proud\n\nbut somthing is wrong...\n\n\"baby is welf!\" say jarzy \"how??\"\n\nshe is rely shock\n\n\"is ok is miracle\" adeon say \"is miracle baby we ned to take care\"\n\"he gona do gret things somday\" adon say agen\n\n\"how??\" jarz ask\n\n\"i just know ok??\" adeon say to her \"dont question\"\nmyn years later\n\ncute baby grow up witout father\n\nhe sufer many long nights alone and hunry\n\nnights cold and dark and scary somtimes\n\nbut is ok becaus he hav mny gud frends\nthey lik brothers to him\n\nvery close\n \nthey do many things togeter\n\nlik skip ropes jumpin jacks and throw rocks into water\n\nthey laugh an hav fun\n\nbut one day...\nthey all die\n\n!!!\n\nand toe is alone agen...\nhe cry few nights\n\nbut he move on\n\nhe know is what his frend would want\n\nhe look at thick clouds and smile\n\n\"i not foget frends\" toe say\ntoe go on to do adventurs\n\nhe fite mny hideos beast\n\nhe get manny money\n\nmny lady lik him\n\nbut he not hapi...\n\nhe miss mom and dad\none day he see his father face in the cloud\n\nis adeon\n\n!!!\n\"father\" toe say \"why you leave me??\"\n\n\"i did not want to\" adeon say \"but i had importrent busness...\"\n\n\"i spend mny night alone and afraid!\" toe say \"i had frends but they dead!!\"\n\"i know\" adoen say \"is hard life you hav i know this\"\n\ntoe cry abit\n\n\"dont cry\" adeon say \"is toough but you ben brave\"\ntoe cry more\n\n\"braver than any man i know\" adoen say \"i knew you specail\"\n\n\"how??\" toe say\n\ntoe sob\n\n\"i just know ok?\" adeon say\n\nadoen smile\n\"stay father\" toe say\n\n\"i wish\" adeon say \"but i mus go...\"\n\n\"go far my son\" adeon say\n\nadeon disaper\n\ntoe stop cry and smile\n\n\"i will dad\"", ""),
        StaticBook("A Stale Tale", "Nym 'Burzbuub' Eildi", "A Story of Felsen\n\n\nOnce there was a city named Felsen, capital of the Orenian Empire, home of Canonism. In this city, there lived a boy- young and innocent in God's sight. He lived in the city with his parents, who loved him very much. He was\nterribly boring. He always did what he was told and never did anything wrong. Everyone hated him. This boy's name was Faris. One day, Faris was walking through the streets, being boring and being made fun of by every boy he ever met- especially by the\nstreet urchins. However, he then did something not too boring. A street urchin walked up to him with a sharp stick seeking to murder him in cold blood. The boy was his archnemesis- the leader of the gang of urchins named Mason. Mason hated Faris, because\nhe had a loving family and good behavior. He found him to be a true scrub and the worst sort of person- worse than gutter filth. As they approached the rest of the boys began to insult Faris. Mason then remarked \"Finally gonna 'each you a lesson.\" Mason\nmoved forward, thrusting the stick towards Faris' abdomen. Faris then did the unexpected and took a step backwards, avoiding the stick. Then pulling out a small dagger from his pocket moving to stab it into Mason's jugular chord. Blood squirting from\nhis neck, the life fading from his eyes. The other boys scattering and screaming for guards. Faris, removing the blade from Mason's neck. His clothes mostly bloodied now. The guards rushed to the scene, one from behind, running the boy through with his\nshining blade, now bloody. Thus ending the perfectly intolerable boy with his perfectly loving family, and finally his perfectly unexpected murder.\n\n\nThe End.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Thesis", "Father Cedrik", "A Thesis on Charitable Evangelization, penned by Cedrik Engel, eternal servant of the Holy Father.\n\nIn nomine Patris.\n\nA man fed by another is beholden to him that provides food. Such is hardly deniable, even in the sense that a man who tends fields that\nbelong to another is beholden to him who owns the land; for land brings forth food with the labor of the tenant, and thus the tenant is fed by the landlord. This is the manner in which our world is governed. This feudal government over which our ever\nmerciful and most blessed GOD presides provides for a system that encourages loyalty and promotes a mutual understanding of responsibility. For without such a system the Holy Orenian Empire would utterly crumble upon its weak foundation, and the Church of\nthe Most High Father would be left stranded upon the harsh landscapes of this Plane. Thus, the importance of the general necessity of sustenance is realized.\n\nUpon this revelation, the Church may begin to develop a plan in which the scattered\nmasses of the Pagan world shall be brought forth into the eternal light of our Father, blessed by His Divine Providence. For from the ashes of this broken world of dismal heathens and faltering believers, the Church may yet arise anew, bearing the holy\nmight of GOD upon the mob of the proletariat, and elevate them to a higher standing, one of communion with His Divine Mercy.\n\nTherefore I beg the Church, I beseech it, to take up its Holy Standard and, in addition to the multitude of righteous\npractices it currently exercises, wield the mighty weapon of Charity, and spread His Love to all corners of this Earth, and perhaps the Pagan may begin to realize the falsity of his idolatrous gods, and turn to the liberating light of the Holy Father.\nThus I pray unto Him, that He may guide the Church with His Mighty Hand and evangelize this crippled land and the whole world may cry \"Glory!\" unto the Heavens.\n\nIn nomine Patris, Amen.\n\nDeus Magnus.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Thesis on", "Father Pierpont", "Brothers, I say unto you, have you shared the altar with believers of GOD in recent times? \n\nWhen was the last time YOU, as a proclaimed follower of GOD and keeper of the law of the Church, extended your hand to a non-believer in attempt to guide --\n- them to the Seven Skies? If the following questions left you convicted by our LORD, you are among many who see the need for spiritual revival.\n\nThink about the potential of a fully awakened church!\nWhen the Exalted received the (4) Holy Scrolls, the following of GOD was few until the three descendants of Horen brought the 'Will of The Creator' to men of many nations so that they may pass on the Regent of Heaven.\nIf it was not for the descendants of Horen preaching the gospel to lost men and women, the Church of the Canon would cease to exist and all of mankind would be damned to darkness.\nIf we are to act as the Regent of Heaven, why is it that a brother will not speak to his other brothers and warn them of the Void?\n \nIt is written that every knee shall bow when GOD reveals the entirety of the Holy Scrolls at the conclusion of our --\n- history. But there's no reason to wait for people to be converted in the end times!\n\nWe can create humble servants and devout followers of The Creator who will bring forth alms, declare for the ministry --\n-- and live a life of joy with eternal security! \n\nTo bring people closer to GOD is not only a work of priests, deacons, nuns, and monks, but something all of mankind must do.\nThough a man who has not declared for priesthood may not preach, a man through his personal testimony with The Creator can be a winner of hearts and souls to GOD by their actions and lifestyle.  It is true, you may be the only scroll someone reads.\nIt is also true that you may be the only opportunity someone has to hear about The Creator.\n\nLet yourself be read and encourage others to live a life for the LORD GOD.\n\nThe need for revival is great.\nChurches are dying.\n\nOur friends and our family are going to the Void without GOD.\n\nWhat are you going to do to stop it?\n\nCreate revival and lead people to the Almighty Creator.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Tragic Tale", "Kazimir Bazhenov", "Katala, Look.. I'm sorry for bursting out at you like that.. I'm hoping that you can forgive me... but if you can't its okay. I've forgiven you..\n\n~anonymous\n\n\n(A mark would be made to read on) >>\nI have took this book and added to it, I believe today is when I shall be killed, I can feel it in my gut, Do not feel sorrow, even if you dont I wish to tell you my final words..I Love You Kat... \n\nFarwell,\n\n-Kazimir", ""),
        StaticBook("A White Tome", "Ashanaak", "[!] The tome is bound in white leather, with only a silver diamond encircling a silver dot embossed on the front cover: the Clerical Eye. Its pages would be marblesque in color, with silver trim, and the writing a flowing font in black ink. [!]\n>>--<<=+=>>--<<\nThe Utterings of Tahariae\n>>--<<=+=>>--<<\n\n\n\nAssembled and Recorded by the Prophet Ashanaak in Vailor\n------=+=------\nThe Five Sacred Tenets of Tahariae\n------=+=------\n\nAs Recorded by the Prophet Braxis in early Anthos:\n\n\n[I] Shelter and protect thy brethren.\n[II] Cannot stray from thy faith.\n\n[III] Shall guide the lost.\n\n[IV] Shall not kill, harm, or spill the blood of the innocent.\n\n[V] Abuse of thine gift and punishment shall fall to you.\nAs Interpreted by the High Priest Heshakomeu Sohae in late Athera:\n\n\n[I] Shelter and protect thy brothers and sisters in Tahariae.\n\n[II] Do not stray in thy dedication to Tahariae.\n[III] Guide and protect the Descendants of the Four against the Impure.\n\n[IV] Do not spill the blood of the innocent.\n\n[V] Do not use Tahariae's blessing for anything other than His will.\n------=+=------\nThe Four Revelations\n------=+=------\n\nAs Recited through the Prophet Ashanaak by the Blessed Aengul of Purity, Tahariae, between the years 1436 and 1442:\n---------------\nThe Revelation of Judgment: The Apokalytiria\n---------------\n\nI am the Glory of the Rising Sun. I am the Bringer of Light. I am the Lord of Purity and the Archon of Justice. I am the Vehement Lord. I am Tahariae. Witness Me, My Chosen\nProphet. Witness Me.\n\nI, the Divine Stag, He Who Walks in Pure Light, the Great Purge, have merely watched My Servants for too long. You have Divided, and Divided you shall fall. You failed to Understand the Mission I had given you, and so you have\ndeteriorated into mere wandering healers and warriors who know only my Blessed Name. Your mockery of Faith and Piety offends Me, and so I return once more. Witness Me, Ashanaak, My Chosen Prophet. Witness Me.\n---------------\nThe Revelation of Wisdom: The Eight Woes\n---------------\n\nAnd now, my Chosen Prophet, recite My Sacred Words to thy Brothers and Sisters, or My Blessing shall be torn from their hearts for their Sins:\n[I] Woe to those that turn against Me and My Mission, for they must be cast out of thy ranks.\n[II] Woe to those who only know Me for My Blessing, and not for My Mission, and do not recognize Me and My Glory in prayer except when My power is needed.\n[III] Woe to those who refuse to heal the Innocent, to return to Pure form what has been rendered Impure.\n[IV] Woe to those who let the Impure, the Beings of Darkness and Evil, and the Descendants who bring harm to the Innocents, walk free when they cross thy path.\n[V] Woe to those who cause harm to the Innocent, for they are those you are sworn to protect.\n[VI] Woe to those who are sexually immoral, who give themselves outside of the holy bed of marriage, who dirty themselves and thus dirty the Name they represent.\n[VII] Woe to those who give themselves over to perpetual drunkenness and intoxication, for they dirty themselves and thus dirty the Name they represent. Such is only acceptable in celebrations and festivities.\n[VIII] Woe to those who steal, cheat, and utter vulgarities, who abuse the Innocent with their tongues and hands.\n---------------\nThe Revelation of Valor: The Eight Commands\n---------------\n\nAnd now, Ashanaak, I give you these Commands. Recite My Sacred Words to thy Brothers and Sisters, that you may live a Pure life:\n[I] Go forth, and spread not just my Light among the Descendants, but My Words and the Truth of My Glory.\n[II] Go forth, and become true Clerics among the Descendants: scholars, protectors, and leaders, to guide the Innocent with words, justice, and wisdom.\n[III] Go forth, and guard yourself against marriage, for service to Me demands complete and total commitment. If you do marry, do not marry those who serve Darkness and Evil, for in doing so you taint the very nature of holy matrimony.\n[IV] Go forth, and kneel before Me in maniael: private prayer, gratitude, and submission before My Glory when you awake and before you sleep.\n[V] Go forth, and kneel before Me in manaakh: prayer, worship, and submission in fellowship with your Brothers and Sisters in Me once each Elven year.\n[VI] Go forth, and respect the fallen clerics who I have sent back to you, to listen and follow what they have returned to say. And when their wisdom has been imparted, that you will have the strength and courage to send them back to My Halls.\n[VII] Go forth, and follow My Chosen Prophet, for they shall be My Light in the darkness of the world for you.\n[VIII] Go forth, and in My Blessed Name, use any means necessary to bring Purity to the Taint and Darkness that has become the world. The realm must return to how it once was, when the Four once ruled in Peace and Taint had not yet manifested. Through the\nsuffering My Mission shall bring you, remember that it is not out of Moral Good that you must do these things, but out of Necessity.\n---------------\nThe Revelation of Hope: The Anachorisi\n---------------\n\nDo all that I have commanded for you to do, and do not do all I have commanded you not to do, and you shall not perish. Nay; once suffering consume you and you leave thy mortal coil,\nI shall welcome you into My Sacred Halls, to forever be with Me in Purity, to forever be witness to My Sacred Light, forever and ever more.\n------=+=------\nThe Anamniseis\n------=+=------\n\nThe Interactions the Blessed Aengul of Purity, Tahariae, has had with His Clerics, as Recorded and Collected by the Prophet Ashanaak:\nIt was in Aegis that the Blessed Aengul of Purity, Tahariae, first came to mortalkind, but He did not reveal His blessed name. In mortal man’s wonder at His eternal and pure radiance, He was worshipped as the Creator, and only the most holy of clerics\ncould serve Him.\n\nIt was in Asulon, Aerial, the Arch-Aengul, lost the ability to grant power to Her servants, and the Aengul Gazardiael withdrew His blessing, thus why He is known as the Abandoner. Tahariae, in His infinite kindness, granted the clerics\nHis Blessing, so the holy work of healing and the purging of evil could be done still, yet He still did not reveal His blessed name, and the clerics believed their patrons to be Aerial and Gazardiael.\n\nIt was in early Anthos that He revealed Himself and\nHis Sacred Mission of Purity to the Prophet Braxis, that the bodies of Mankind be whole and protected from the forces of evil, and that taint be removed from the realm, and that the realm be returned to the Purity that existed when the Four Brothers first\nwalked the Earth.\n\nIt was in late Anthos, when the clerics were few and Setherien and the wraiths threatened the realm, that Tahariae chose four to be His champions, perfect representations of His four aspects: Judgment, Wisdom, Valor, and Hope.\nTogether, they fought the many threats to the purity of the realm.\n\nIt was in late Thales Tahariae summoned forth His clerics to investigate a portal, through which we were to enter. The Abandoner, Gazardiael, confronted Tahariae, and the two did battle\natop the mountain on which the portal was located. After the battle, and Gazardiael briefly pushed back, Tahariae manifested before the gathered clerics and their allies as a radiant white stag. He told us the portal required two keys to open, as well as\nthe Itharel of Wisdom Hosper, who had been captured by forces unknown. “O Lord, can you tell us where Hosper is?” I asked. “Nay,” He responded. “A dark force clouds My vision; I cannot see him.” So began the quest for the keys began, of which I was\nnot\ninvolved any further in.\n\nIt was in Athera that the Order of the White Lance, a union between the servants of Tahariae and Xan, Aengul of Gaurdianship and Order, was formed. Alas, it was not to last, and so began the Schism and the Conflict of Light. In\nlate Athera, Aldrik, Second Itharel of Hope, was given a vision by Tahariae commanding the Clerics and the Paladins to reunite, but such did not come to pass.\n\nIt was in Vailor that Tahariae commanded His followers to leap from high places and He would\nsave us. It was a test of faith to prepare us for His message: the realm was passing through a Great Cycle that must occur, lest the world be consumed by the Destroyer. However, in order for the Realm to be protected, four Harvesters wielding scythes must\ncut down many innocents. “For it is not out of Moral Good or Holiness that we do these things, but out of Necessity,” sayeth Tahariae unto us. So great was His insistence we trust in Him that two of us briefly lost connection to Him for not leaping\nenough, but they were forgiven, and His Blessing returned to their hearts.\n\nIt was many years later, amidst the assault of the clerics by the Being known as the Undying One, that Tahariae revealed His new commands by speaking through the cleric Ashanaak,\nchoosing him to be His next Prophet.\n\nSuch is the history of the actions of the Blessed Aengul of Purity, Tahariae, in our realm. May our actions be a testament to the Glory of Tahariae, Blessed Be His Name.\n[!] An ornate picture of a stag facing the viewer is here. Its antlers are tall and winding, and a radiant halo surrounds his head. [!]", ""),
        StaticBook("A Winter Recipe", "Commodus de Jedih", "sssssssssssssssssssDarkhaven Souse Stew\nsssssssssssssssssss\n\n\"A Winter Family Recipe\" (Aetosion).\n\nTranscribed by Comm.\n1664\nDarkhaven Souse Stew\n\nA note on the acquisition of ingredients:\n\nThe ears of the darkie should not be taken from a dead corpse, but instead from the living beast.\nOne should note not to take the whole ear, but instead just the upper half in imperial manner. The trimming of the creature's ear in this manner is in fact a humane action, helping to dull the animal's edge and render it docile.\nThis will help the poor creature better integrate into society, and serve our Emperor Godfrey more adequately. On this isle of Kalos there is want for delicate meat, and the casual waste of the dark elf's trimmed ears is a most egregious offense,-\nas when rightly prepared it is a most agreeable delicacy.\n\n-3 lbs dark elf ears, sliced into smaller pieces (kitchen scissors work best for this)\n-6 C beef broth base (yak is an acceptable substitute in Northern regions)\n\n-1 medium potato, diced\n\n-1 carrot, diced\n\n-1/4 C barley ale\n\n-1/2 Auvergnian red pepper, chopped\n-Salt and pepper to taste\n\nHeat over fire, stir until broth is a rich sanguine red, leave boiling for 10 minutes, but do not overcook the meat, else it will turn tough. Bon apétit!", ""),
        StaticBook("A Wish!", "Thane Andwise Peregrin", "I, Andwise Peregrin, wish for knowledge to a long forgotten secret.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Wizard's Wish", "Cecil", "Wishes are simply that. Wishes.\n\nHowever for the sake of holiday cheer.. That and I have been stuck in this blasted maze for over a day now..\n\nMy WISH is for the Pumpkin Crown. - Cecil, the Wizard\n\nP.S - I am lost.", ""),
        StaticBook("A.I Chapter 1", "Morgan Hallowfall", "Alchemical Index\n================ This is the Alchemical Index, inside will describe a variety of plants and potions.\n===================\nChapter One: Alchemical Reagents, their symbols, representations and usual locations.\n1. Goblin's Ivy:\nSymbol: Earth\nPotency: Weak\nRegion: Deserts, usually seen on ruins or mountains too.\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Resiliance\n-Poison\n-Death\n2. Desert Berry Bush\nSymbol: Earth\nPotency: Moderate\nRegion: In or Near Cacti\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Protection\n-Resiliance\n\n\n(This is for the Stem)\n3. Starved Coyote Tick\nSymbol: Earth\nPotency: Strong\nRegion: Corpses of Dead animals in Deserts\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Protection\n-Resiliance\n-Connection\n4. Desert Berry Bush\nSymbol: Fire\nPotency: Weak\nRegion: Same as previous\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Empowerment\n-Overwhelming\n\n(These are the berries)\n5. Blood Lotus\nSymbol: Fire\nPotency: Moderate\nRegion: Cave Entrances, Deserts\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Hope\n-Courage\n6. Drake's Tail.\nSymbol: Fire\nPotency: Strong\nRegion: In Deserts near Oasises\n\nRepresentations:\n-Heat\n-Destruction\n-Chaos\n7. Zawabate\nSymbol: Water\nPotency: Moderate\nRegion: Within Oasises, Deserts\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Life\n-Calmness\n-Rebirth\n8. Elrow Berries\nSymbol: Fire\nPotency: Moderate\nRegion: Bushes in Cold regions\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Rage\n-Anger\n-Burning\n9. Frost Vine\nSymbol: Water\nPotency: Moderate\nRegion: Shaded areas in cold climates\n\nRepresentations: \n\n-Life\n-Calmness\n-Ice\n10. Athin\nSymbol: Water\nPotency: Strong\nRegion: Under the ice of frozen lakes and rivers\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Freezing\n-Ice\n-Life\n-Balance\n11. Elf's Hair Vine\nSymbol: Air\nPotency: Strong\nRegion: Covered from the wind, top of cold mountains\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Travel\n-Gracefulness\n-Speed\n-Flight\n12. Alabaster Leaf\nSymbol: Earth\nPotency: Moderate\nRegion: Fallen Trees In forests\n\nRepresentations:\n\n- Immobility\n-Perserverance\n13. Tippen's Root\nSymbol: Earth\nPotency: Moderate\nRegion: Dead plants and animals in forests\n\nRepresentations:\n-Life\n-Regrowth\n-Endurance\n-Strength\n-Resiliance\n14. Flametounge's Root\nSymbol: Fire\nPotency: Moderate\nRegion: Forest hillsides and burnt forests\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Heat\n-Anger\n-Destruction\n15. Crimson Vase\nSymbol: Fire\nPotency: Strong\nRegion: At the base of young trees in Forests\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Heat\n-Warmth\n-Love\n-Compassion\n-Passion\n16. Blissfoil\nSymbol: Water\nPotency: Weak\nRegion: Under birch trees in forests\n\nRepresentation:\n\n-Calmness\n17. Serpent's Stalk\nSymbol: Water\nPotency: Moderate\nRegion: Near water in forests\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Life\n-Rebirth\n-Calmness\n-Fluity\n18. Crouching Feather\nSymbol: Air\nPotency: Strong\nRegion: Under big bushes and shrubs in forests and plains\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Speed\n-Travel\n-Gracefulness\n19. Saffvil\nSymbol: Earth\nPotency: Moderate\nRegion: Dead bodies or some plant decomposing plant matter in swamps\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Resiliance\n-Endurance\n-Death\n20. Dwarf's Pumpkin\nSymbol: Fire\nPotency: Moderate\nRegion: Next to muddy water in Swamps\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Rage\n-Envy\n-Bitterness\n-Power\n-Strength\n21. Mandragora\nSymbol: Water\nPotency: Moderate\nRegion: Underwater in swamps\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Life\n-Rejuvination\n-Rebirth\n-Regrowth\n23. Jailer's Moss\nSymbol: Air\nPotency: Weak\nRegion: Caves in Swamps, Inside or next to streams of water\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Travel\n-Movement\n24. Swamp's Blossom\nSymbol: Air\nPotency: Moderate\nRegion: Branches of Swamp Trees\n\nRepresentations:\n\n-Quickness\n-Speed\n-Travel\n===================\nThis concludes the first part of the book collection, for further information about alchemical concoctions, please seek the other parts of the collection or alternatively other books relevant to your research!\n===================", ""),
        StaticBook("A.R Agreement", "Raell Annungilben", "Agreement of Agriculture between Crosswinds Trading Company and Alorii Raell'onn\n\nTerms:\n1. Crosswinds Trading Company will purchase Mr Raell'onn's produce at a fair price in accordance with inflation.\n2. Mr Raell'onn will tend to the fields of Crosswinds Trading Company and help cultivate its livestock. Mr Raell'onn will not sell these goods but will be prodvided with a room, free of charge and tools, free of charge.\n\n3. Mr Raell'onn will not sell his produce from his farm or the guild to anyone without Raell Annungilbon's consent or a trade charter giving Mr Raell'onn the right to do so.\n\n4. Crosswind's Trading Company will help Mr Raell'onn with any outside threat,\nexcluding allegiance to war.\n\n5. Crosswinds Trading Company and Mr Raell'onn's farm are in a partnership. The farm cannot be sold without guild charter. To suceed from this partnership Mr Raell'onn will speak to the leader of Crosswinds Trading\nCompany personally, with a fine of 50 mina.\n\n6. Crosswinds Trading Comapany reserves the right to declare this agreement of agriculture null and void if:\n-Mr Raell'onn sells his stock to any other than Crosswinds Trading Company and their\nconstituents\n\n-Mr Raell'onn dies.\n\n-Mr Raell'onn sides with a faction Crosswinds Trading Company deems and enemy\n\n-Mr Raell'onn is deemed unfit for partnership, be it health, wealth or\nor otherwise.\n\nSigned, formally,\n\nRaell Annungilben,\n\nMaster of Crosswinds Trading Company\n\nAlorii Raell'onn", ""),
        StaticBook("Abomination, 7ft", "Pius", "Issued and confirmed by his Imperial Majesty, Godfrey I of House Horen, by the grace of the Creator, Emperor of Oren, King of Renatus and Seventis, Defender of the Faith, Protector of the Realm, Regent Eternal of the Kingdom of Heaven, Duke of Ardania,\nCrown Lands, Marna, Balamena, Count of Saltridge, Alnfayat, Alzlam, Alardy, Hrq Rmal, Garath, and Gwent, and Most Holy Emperor of the Land\n-------------------Blessings upon thee Patriots of Oren,\n\nIt has come to our attention that abominations have\nbeen walking our streets, these creatures are an afront to GOD. I have been told of sightings of a seven foot human walking around the streets. That can only occur through Daemonic possession. Furthermore, there have been sightings of diabolically strong\nhumans reaching the strength of giants. Lastly, there have been sightings of humans that can outrun a horse and can jump as high as fifteen feet, and can be so agile that you can never catch or see him properly.\n\nAll of these people must be captured as\nthey are abominations of evil demonically mutated beings. A priest must oversee their termination as he needs to be there so that he can release the original spirit that was in place before the demon caused the suffering.\n\nToov is exempt of such.", ""),
        StaticBook("Absolution&Life", "Guyden Aureon", "~*~The Emerald~*~\n            Way\n\nScribed by the Willow Druid.\n\nCreated by the Hurricane Druid.\n\n\n  Rites of Absolution\n & The Circle of Life\nRites of Absolution\n\nNature has no moral compass, as was made clear earlier. We serve as the path of morality, we serve as the patrons of right and wrong. The aspects have left us with a great freedom, in this sense, by leaving\nus to decide for ourselves what is right from wrong, and thus is the task of the Naelurir, to bring good and evil into nature. It is our divine duty to bring the followers of Aspectism into the light of goodness, to bring them\nback to a holier path, that they may also see the great green forests above, and find peace past their life's end.\n\nWhen you leave on pilgrimage, on any journey, what do you take with you? Do you bring all of your belongings,\nall of your prized possessions and papers? Do you wheel your house behind you on a wagon? You do not, no. You take only what you need for the journey, you take only what is necessary. As with any journey, we cannot march\nthrough our lives carrying unnecessary weight, and we cannot be burdened with the weight of our wrongdoings and transgressions. No, we must march on with a clear conscience, all of us, both priest and devout.\nBut we are imperfect beings, no? We commit many wrongdoings in our lives, and we trespass against our neighbors. We lie, we cheat, we stain the earth with each other's blood and leave others defenseless against the crows that\nseek to feed upon mali. But all is not lost in this, no, there is hope for absolution. We need not carry our transgressions wheresoever we walk, but we cannot forget them. Instead, we must ask the mother and father for\nforgiveness, to cleanse us of our sins, however black they may be. By their righteous power, we must seek penance to lessen the load of life upon our backs.\n\nIn my dreams, I have seen a ritual, a rite so powerful as to wash us\nclean of our transgressions and push us into a brighter future. I was sent this vision from on high, to give to you, my fellow mali, that we may all bathe in clean waters, that we may journey forward beyond this life with only\nwhat is necessary. I invite all to partake in this Rite of Absolution.\n\nThose touched by the aspects, those with the gifts, your priesthood. They must lead you on through this rite. They have been opened to the world by the\naspects, they are closest to them. Go to them when you have trespassed against others, when you have committed these transgressions against your faith and people. You will speak your sins to them, all of them. Conceal nothing\nwithin you, for the aspects will see all. To go to your priesthood speaks goodness within you, it speaks a wish to return to the green light of the aspects. You must seek out penance, a priest will not find you. The green\nlight will not find its way into you if you will not seek it out. If you cannot recognize your own wrongdoings, you cannot find the light. Search always within yourself for these, and you will find the way back to the green\nfaith.\n\nBring with you a sacrifice. A true sacrifice from you to the aspects. Penance cannot be given without great self-sacrifice, for there must be a balance. Fret not on your sacrifice, to be cleansed of guilt is a\ngift of itself. Burn it in the brazier that you may send it up to the aspects above. Only then will they look upon you, through the priest, only then can you be given true penance. Repeat this sacred prayer with your priest,\nsend it up on high;\n\nIn Elven:\n\"O' Haelun, O' Maln\nKae sul sioln uhiere, ay'khelan ito kae'leh narnsae,\navern'ehya ito kae'leh.\nnae ormartillun kae illerih, ay'kae elnarnsae'taynei uhiere, karin'ento.\nkae'leh anniln ito iyl, ay'iyl karinah karinan'ehya orento, karin'ento.\"\n\nIn Common Tongue:\n\"O' Mother, O' Father\nI seek light alone, for my path is full of darkness,\nand I wander without purpose.\nMay you grant me forgiveness, for I seek the emerald path.\nIt will be my guide, for this sunrise and all those ahead.\"\n\nAfter such, the priest will bid you a task, a task meant to atone for your transgressions. While\nthe aspects may have given you peace, you must put the world at peace, your people at peace. Only then can you be fully returned to the side of light. After, bathe yourself in clean waters, feel your sins fall away, and the\nburdens lifted from your shoulders. This is the path to peace that I have seen in my heart and in my mind. Let you follow it closely.\nThe Circle of Life\n\nWe live in a cycle of life and death, do we not? The birds and trees die out, but there is ever a forest standing, no? Songbirds fill the air, do they not? We are ever surrounded by life, yet death lurks\nand strikes here and there. No matter how oft or how heavy death's strikes may be, life ever moves on. I suppose what I'm trying to say is life finds a way no matter what you may put in it's path. Nations rise and fall,\npeoples die out, forests are burned to the ground. But life goes on, and so it goes.\n\nWe must keep this in our hearts and in our minds wherever we would walk, we must remember this circle. This is why priests\nhave taken to signing a circle over their heart, for they know it to be the truest way of the world. Things go on and on, life spirals and they are a part of the circle of life. It surrounds them, this steadfast balance. To\nkeep it with them always, they mark it on their own body, they circle their hearts before meals, during trying times as a reminder of the circle that goes round and round.\n\nIt is also for this reason that many a good\naspectist will tattoo the very circle of life onto their body somewhere, to show the world what they've dedicated their souls to protecting. To imprint their very duty onto their bodies, no matter how big or small, shows great\ndedication, and our people may look to it as a symbol of spiritual wellness, the symbol of a guide for days to come. This I call the symbol of our priesthood, of the Naelurir. Show the world who you are, lliran. Never forget\nit, for the aspects will not.\n\nShow this symbol wherever you can lliran, mark it as a prayer to the aspects above, that the cycle be maintained. Do it before meals, before hunts, when your family is sick, when great\nchange occurs in your life. Carry it with you as a shield, and the aspects light will guide your way. Mark is even on your body. The world will see your good example and follow you into the light of goodness. Teach it unto\nothers, spread the good word.\n-----\nBlessed be unto the Aspects. Blessed be.", ""),
        StaticBook("Abstract", "[Sohaer] Kalenz", "The Valleian'Acal of Larihei and the effects on the physical body.\n\nLomanih et al.; Malin's Welcome 198\n\nIn this paper we will attepmt to categorize, without searching for too through an explanation, the effects of enchanted\ngold-infused pools. We will begin with the physical alterations and come to accept that continued exposure to the pools will only lighten one's skin and hair tones while potentially increasing a subject's height. We see that neither of these effects are\nharmful to the physical body.\n\nWe will also conclude that these pools bolster an Elf's magical prowess and their natural talent to channel the Tanya that flows through our earth. We will illustrate why this increased acuity only has\npositive effects, and the suggestion of hallucinations or a clouding of judgement is beyond preposterous.\n\nFInally we shall discuss the benefits of bathing in the pools and encourage all of Malin's pure children to do the same.\nThis shall be done by introducing a concept known as the maehr'sae hiylun'ehya, which will be the driving philosophy behind our arguments.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adam", "Beelzebub", "There once was a boy, he was named Adam.\n\nAdam loved to sit on his chair.\n\nAdam's mother warned him.\n\n\"Stop! The more you sloth upon that chair, the more you shall become but a potato!\"\nAdam said \"No!\" and continued to sit upon his chair.\n\nHe cried and cried, and whined and whined. He would not move.\n\nAdam loved to sit on his chair.\n\n\"Why should I move?,\" Adam asked.\nAdam grew fatter and fatter.\n\nHe began to bald.\n\nAdam grew larger.\n\nHe sat upon his chair and all night.\nAdam's mother warned him once again.\n\n\"You shall become a chair-potato, Adam!\"\n\n\"That is what happens to boys who idle upon chairs!\"\n\nHe did not move.\nAdam grew spotty.\n\nHe became very pudgy.\n\nHe slumped to the side and released a large sigh.\n\nHe was a big chair-potato.\nAdam's mother found him upon the chair.\n\n\"Now, he is more useful!\"\n\nAdam's mother brought him into the kitchen, and he was cooked.\n\nAnd his family feasted for many days!", ""),
        StaticBook("Adam's Bravery", "Vannessa Longridge", "Chapter 1:The Sighting\n\nThey stood proudly atop the hill, the wind raging around them, their hair fighting against the tide. Swords in their sheathes, bows on their backs and arrows in their quiver, they made their way down, the 2 brothers.\n\"Are you sure that is where he lives?\"Asked Ibraheem. Adam merely nodded. They made their way to the base of Marbrand and started scaling the walls. \n\nChapter 2: Jory\nHis face was weathered, sculpted out of pure hate.\nHe stole and murdered for joy. The 2 brothers were here for just that. Steal back what was rightfully theirs, their father's sword. They creeped into Jory's bedroom skilfully when Ibraheem stepped on a loose plank. CREAK. Swift as an arrow, Jory swung his\nsword towards Ibraheem, but Adam skillfully parried the sword, bringing his dagger down on Jory's chest. In one swift movement, Adam had saved his brother's life and ended the cruel lord's life. They exited with the sword in their hand and proud of\ntheir deeds.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adunian Brothers", "Davin Lodmund", "How to vex a High Elf\nFor\nMy Adunian Brothers\nand cultures. Heaven forbid you hail from 'impurity' such as being a half elf or Adunian. Such is seen as a grand faux par, as it reminds them how they themselves were impure as to mingle with Harrenites. As of such they often tend to haul\nthemselves up in their cities, denying access to all those whom don't hail from their mighty ancestory. On the other hand, when these timid and commonly, rude creatures scurry from their lairs they are often condesending and\nnot of their kin.\nThis, my friends, is why I have personally taken it upon myself in to muse possible ways to disarm, vex and scare off this beast.\nMethod 1:\nBe from a mixed heritage, Adunian or half elf. Either will surfice.\nThe mere concept of love across races is dead with the high elf, so be spawned from such love is the ultimate vexation as proof that love conquer's order.\nHowever, be wary of mix-ed one. For a high elf may turn hostile. If that is the case be sure to play the racism card. If this fails, arm yourself and be sure to attack before the beast can charge a magical attack!\nMethod 2:\nIf they commit any actions, mutter 'Typical high elf'. Simple as that, it boils their blood good and proper.\nMethod 3:\nRemind them of how their past kin have been manipulative, crooked and evil to all whom are not their own. To remind them of their past brings them great tragedy. They may become snide however and claim that it was true and proper. If this\nis the case, be sure to verbally put them down and destroy their argument.\nMethod 4:\nDistribute this guide.\nMethod 5:\nA good old punch.", ""),
        StaticBook("Advancement I", "Marcus", "=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=\n\nMilitary Mandate of the Lord Marshal of the Apostolic Kingdom of Marna\n\n\nRank Advancements for the 1647th Year of Creation\n=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=\nOn this day, the 7th of the Grand Harvest, the following individuals shall recieve this document to recognize an advancement in rank or other commission.\n\nOskar Deitmar von Reichsmensch\n=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=Following his undertaking of an oath of obedience to His Majesty, Frederick Pius, the citizen\n\nOskar Deitmar von Reischsmensch\n\nshall be instated as Brigadier of His Majesty's Marnan Free Company\n=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=\nAnd, hence, Brigadier von Reichsmensch shall be granted the powers and responsibilities established with the said commission.\n\nValidated on the 7th Day of the Grand Harvest, on the 1647th Year of Creation\n=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=\n\nFrederick Pius of Marna, Apostolic King of Marna, Rhodesia, and Waldenia, Duke of Senntisten and Defender of Rhodesia and the Faith, Brother of Saint Lucien\n\nMarcus Arminius Rovin, Lord Marshal, O.S.L.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adventuring", "Azureth", "The life of an adventurer is difficult and dangerous. The first bit of advice here is to reconsider your choice; if you've picked up this book, you no doubt plan to at least dabble in adventuring. Know that you'll face perils both mundane and magical.\nA road is long and hot, and a sword is sharp. But if you still wish to become an adventurer, these are the components of the profession.\nI. Party Composition. Throughout this book I'll detail a few types of adventurers. Adventuring parties require a variety of cooperating members to thrive. When recruiting, try to find people that get along; infighting is a common cause for party death.\nII. Preliminaries. The first step to an adventure is finding an adventure. Towns contain message boards with potential quests on them, and people often have jobs they need done. Nobles hire spies. Kings hate bandits. High risk leads to high reward.\nIII. Travel. The best adventurers know that the journey is the most important phase of a quest. Hunger and fatigue are often underestimated. If you go to slay a monster, you want to be in prime condition when you arrive, so remember to bring plenty of\nfood, drink, comfortable bedding, and medical equipment. Navigation is also a trouble during travel. Bring a map and compass when you wander off the trail, but stick to roads when possible; beasts exist in the wilds. The class of Rangers are experts of\nnavigation, foraging, and often stealth, and typically know much about practical things. You want a good Ranger on your team for their usefulness.\nIV. Delving. Delving is entering palaces and dungeons with locks and traps. When exploring ancient ruins, always keep an eye out for seams, pressure plates, and wires, and heed every sound. Rogues know their way around mechanical contraptions, so they're\nbest for delving, and are the most stealthy class. If you plan on delving at all during an adventure, bring a Rogue.\nV. Combat. Some adventurers seek combat, while some hide from it. Unfortunately, it's around every corner. Monsters lurk in the dark, and bandits too. A good adventurer knows about all sorts of creatures and carries their weaknesses. Fighters are the most\ncommon class for combat; they simply know how to fight. Hunters are versed in monster lore and specialize in dealing with them. Tongues defuse situations before they become combat.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aengul&Daemon", "Eques Erwin Gerold", "The Aenguls are great race, just like Daemons, they are an ancient race with great power. Aenguls are a type of AenguDaemons. Not many Aenguls are known, only a few people have direct connections with the mortals. Only those that have truly shown\nthemselves to the mortals with their powers are true known Aenguls, though there are legends of many more! \n\n\n\n\nNEXT PAGE: DAEMON\nLike Aenguls, Daemons are an ancient race with GREAT power,but they normally do not use it. Daemons are part of Aengudaemons. Daemons RARELY walk in the mortal worlds, usually choosing to appear to a mortal. There are not many Daemons that have presented\nthemselves to mortals.\n\n\nNEXT PAGE: LIST OF AENGULS AND DAEMONS\nAeriel, Care Taker of Souls, and Aengul of peace and love, Patron of the Ascended. Tahariae Aengul of Purity, patron of clerics. Yeu Rthuly, Aengul of Contentment and Compassion. Xan, Aengul of Order and Guardship, Patron of the Brotherhood Golden Lion.\nList of Daemons.\nDragur, the daemon of knowledge, and creator of Dragaars and dragons, powerful god-like beings that seek to collect wisdom and information. Iblees,the corrupted, Iblees was the Daemon that wished to conquer Aegis and was defeated. He now\nhas risen once again, due to the races own curiosity of an ancient ruin in which he was being impriosoned, and threatens the races life in Athere. Metztli, the Daemon of Moon, and creator of the Kharajyr. Apohet,the Daemon of faith and ambition,and\ncreator of the Spiritual Plane that eventually was divided into the Elemental.Ancestral, and Immortal planes. Tayl, the Daemon Of Companionship, who would take the lives of the wicked, the good and everything in between if it meant rallying mortals\ntogether.\nI believe the Aenguls serve the Light, as the Daemon would do the complete opposite....\n\n\n\n\n    Written by Erwin", ""),
        StaticBook("Aeromancy", "Great Ser Arhadir Owl", "Aeromancy\n\nBy Master Of Air Ser Arhadir Owl\nDate 23rd of The Amber Cold, 1474\n\nChapter 1: How to use Air Evocation\nChapter 2: Extra Information\nChapter 3: Spells\nChapter 1:\n\n1. The first step you should take to learning Aeromancy is by observing the wind itself in action, but to do this in a windy area where you can see what the wind does to nature.\n2. The next step is to learn how to clear your mind and focus just on the void.\n3. After these first two steps you must learn to pull from the void, you do this by clearing your mind and focusing on the void and by thing about the wind itself which you have been studying.\n4. Slowly you will be able to bring small amounts of Air from the void into the world. During this stage you will find that your body is weaken and you may faint a few times trying to hold a connect to the void or by trying hard spells.\n5. Once you learnt how to pull Air from the void you can start using it practically. one of the first spells you can learn is Force push which is a basic burst of Air, this can be used to blow out torches and maybe even push people back a bit.\n6. From here it is up to you to develop Aeromancy better to learn new and intresting spells.\nChapter 2:\n\nQuestion that people have about Aeromancery's and what they can do with Aeromancy.\n-Aeromancer’s cannot control Air in the natural world only control and summon Air which they have summoned from the void.\n-Aeromancer’s cannot fly because the cannot hold a stable connection to the void while moving that fast.\n\n-Aeromancer’s do not have the ability to change the weather.\nChapter 3:\n\nBasic:\n-Force Push: The most basic of all the spells this essentially allows of an Aeromancer to push a target away or knock them over.\n-Air Ball: Another basic spell which allows for the Aeromancer to summon a ball of Air which can be fired at targets at different speeds.\nAdept:\n\n-Tornado: This is a much more defence spell which allows the Aeromancer to summon a tornado around a person or the Aeromancer him or her self,-\n- this tornado can protect from distance attacks (Best against other elemental magic attacks) or weak melee attacks.\n-Air Jump: An Aeromancer can fire a blast of air underneath him or her self which can then propel the Aeromancer up a few meters.\n-Air Burst: This spell fires a blast of air out from all around the Aeromancer which can be powerful enough to knock over many targets all out the Aeromancer.\n-Air Stream: This spell is when an Aeromancer fires a constant stream of Air which can push objects or people back, even knocking them over or stopping them from moving.\nAdvanced:\n\n-Air Leap: The same as an Air Jump but allows you to jump much higher with much more precision.\n-Speed Run: While the idea of this speed seems easy it requires a lot of concentration for a mage to be moving at a speed and be usings his or her magic, this spell allows for the Aeromancer to run slightly faster than normal.\n-Air Bolt: This is a sudden and extremely power blast of air which which can be fire long distances. When this bolt hits it can knock a person out cold or even break bones.\n\nThis concludes the Tome.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aewion", "Aewion", "Emanaf Delsaran, Lord Architect.\n\nTO ALL AMONG WHOM THIS MAY COME, GREETING:\n\nKNOW YE That having special trust in the Honesty, Prudence, and Abilities of Halerir Aewion, Virarim, I do appoint and constitute\nhim Master of Stores in my Department, and charge to him (and the further holders of that Office, under me and my successors) the maintenance and security of all supplies, materials, and sundry Stores which are within my said Department, and further\ndirect to his charge responsibility for acquisition of all materials as may from time to time be required in construction; and I further order that, while in the proper execution of this office the said Aewion shall execute by proxy and for the time\nthe power of my office, as it touches upon supplies and building materials; and that for so doing, this shall be his warrant.\n\nDone 8th The Amber Cold in the year 1653 of Aegis.\n\nThe Lord Architect:\nE. Delsaran~\n[L.S.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Aila's Shit", "Kairn Ithelanen", "The Ascended are the chosen of the Arch-Aengul, Aeriel. Her agents within the realm are chosen to uphold her virtues and combat threats to the Descendants. This book shall name and detail the Ascended in order to aid in any future dealings with them.\nName: Heial, the Master Sage.\n\nIt is claimed he appears to be of Mali'aheral descent beneath his armor, though I've yet to confirm this. Husband to Elvira.\nResidence:\n\nAbilities:\nName: Belestram, Prince of the Dominion.\n\nLooks to be of Mali'ahereal descent, prior to his ascension. The Prince stands at six feet, seven inches, and has glowing silver eyes. His skin is fair, hair golden in color.\nResidence: Dominion\n\nAbilities:\nName: Ravondir, the Red Sage.\nResidence:\n\nAbilities:\nName: Elvira\nResidence: \n\nAbilities:\nName: Nin\nResidence:\n\nAbilities:\nName: Blundermore\nResidence:\n\nAbilities:\nName: Freya\nResidence:\n\nAbilities:\nName: Warden Dwalin Irongut.\n\nThe dwarf stands at five feet tall and carries an orange gaze. He is fit, usually seen in plate armor and a dark cloak. His hair is a brown color, though it was lighter before his ascension.\nResidence:\n\nAbilities:\nName: Harlan, the Steward.\n\nMay or may not be ascended, though he works with them. Stands at 6'1, with short white hair and white eyes. His skin is fair and he appears to be in above average physical shape. Is a doctor, apparently.\nResidence: Dominion\n\nAbilities:", ""),
        StaticBook("Ailis Gallic Bio", "Ewlin Hae'vaul", "A biography on Ailis Gallic, the Highlander of Daeland.\nAilis Gallic was born outside of Santegia, on the year of 1641. She is the daughter of a man named Eignach and a woman named Briana, though she lived her life mostly with her cousin Gwion\nGallic, the current King of Daeland. She owns a cat named Scrabbles, who spends most of their days sleeping, but the animal still has a very strong bond with it's owner Ailis.\nShe is currently jobless, but has two hobbies that seem to be usual among\nhumans, which is drinking and sewing, and seems to be very talented at such, since she needs to fix her dresses oftenly. \nShe has multiple scars, but the biggest one is found on her leg, when she accidently shot her self with an arrow. Why? I don't know.\nAilis is currently single, and is very shy towards that type of situation to the point where she does not specify her sexuality, which means it is unknown to the public.\nShe stands at about 5'3\" and posesses freckles on her cheeks. Her hair is red and\nwell treated. She is obviously an Highlander, or so, it's what she says to be, but it's unsure due to her Gallic descendence, which according to her, is irregular.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aimless scribble", "Hearth", "You who look but are blind to see, st-e `to\nthe abyss there i5 only me the ab-----\n\nDo MOl vRuzT Xqnd3r", ""),
        StaticBook("Air Evocation", "Ayche Raven'kor", "Air Evocation\nThis book was created by Master Air Evocatonist Alatar of the Mage Academy\n\nRecopied By\nAyche\nTable of Conents\n\nChapter 1: The Void\n\nChapter 2: All About Wind\n\nChapter 3: Summoning\n\nChapter 4: Basic Spells\nChapter 1: \nAccording to legend and study, the void is an infinite plane of potential thought and energy surrounded by absolute darkness. Since complete darkness is rather hard to imagine, think about a blank canvas.\nHypothetically, anything can be drawn out of the void if it does not contradict nature. The first steps of becoming a mage is learning to understand the void and it's 'blank' \nconcept. Meditation is the most efficient and common way, as I have found.\nLearn how to blanket yourself in a blank state of mind and prepare to paint your canvas.\nChapter 2:\nWind and air are essences to all life around the realm of existance. You breathe it into your very self.\nWith the art of air evoction, you manipulate it. Wind is unpredictable and one\nof the best studied branches of arcane magics, You must experience the element in it's true form before you can even think about summoning it.\nIn order to achieve this, I suggest moving to a  region of high altitude and feel the wind rush over your very body. Experience how pressure seeps through the cracks of all substance. Taste it, feel it, smell it.\nAnother useful experiment is placing something in the air that can float. Watch how the wind carries the item and gently cradles it back down to the earth or carries it away.\nChapter 3:\nAfter you have learned all there is to know about your element, and your meditation is firm; you may begin your attempts in summoning your element from the void. Firstly, you must find a place of peace.\nNext, use your blank canvas to imagine air, allow the thought to fill you and the energy of yourself to course through your very blood. Through combining all of this. A small amount of wind may be conjured.\nWarning: You may pass out a few times upon first connection.\nChapter 4: After you have mastered basic connection, you can move onto some of the key spells in an air evocationist's arsenal.\nThe first and most obvious, is the force push. Essentially, a novice air evocationist musters all of his strength for one large and forceful push at the enemy.\nSecondly, and slightly more defensive, is the protective tornado.\n\nA skilled air evocationist can create a spiraling current of wind that could potentially keep most objects out of your sphere. That concludes this tome.", ""),
        StaticBook("Al-Deen's Will", "Umar Al-Deen", "Umar Al-Deen's &\nKili Al-Deen's\nwill\n-------------------everything goes to Khalid ibn Mahmoud & \nAshur Ibn Mahmoud\nnothing that is ours will be given away or sold!\n\na copy of each of kili's books go to\nYusuf Al-Nabeel,\nSaalih Al-Nabeel.\n\nour land will go to khalid and ashur\n\nEVERYTHING GOES TO KHALID AND ASHUR!\n\nif Umar Al-Deen or\n Kili Al-Deen bodie could not be buried for some unknown reason please build\nUmar Al-Deen and \nKili Al-Deen an empty grave till the body can be place in the coffin and return to the grave\n\n\nsigned by\nUmar Al-deen\nand\nKili Al-Deen", ""),
        StaticBook("Al-Nur Menu!", "Amin Al-Sham", "Al-Nur Spring Bakery & Inn\n-------------------           Menu\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-Owner: Amin Al-Sham\nLocation: Al-Khaleed, Haria, Isle Of Asul.\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-Baked Goods 2-5 Pg\nMeals 6-9 Pg\nDrinks 10-11 Pg\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-\nBaked Goods\n-------------------Bread 0.5 Minas\nbaguette 1 Minas each\nCroissant 1 Minas each\nPancake .5 Minas each\nToast .2 Minas each\nCaramel Bread .5 Minas each\nHoney Bread .5 Minas each\nChocolate Pancake 1 Minas each\nCream Pancake 1 Minas each\nButter pancake 1 Minas each\nMaple Pancake 1 Minas each\nHoney Pancake 1 Minas each\nCake 15 Minas each\nCheese Cake is 15 Minas\nChocolate Cake 20 Minas\nSweet Cake 20 Minas\nPumpkin pie 15 Minas\nChocolate Pie 15 Minas\nCream Pie 15 Minas\nMushroom Pie 15 Minas\nCannoli 15 Minas\nPlain Cookie .5 Minas\nButter Biscuits .5 Minas\nChocolate Cookie .5 Minas\nTriple Chocolate Cookie 1 Minas\nBrownie .5 Minas\nCaramel Cookie .5 Minas\nMa'amouls 1 Minas\nFortune Cookie 1 Minas\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-\n\n\n\n------------------>\n-------------------          Meals\n-------------------Sandwich 1 Minas\nPotato Chowder 1 Minas\nMashed Potatoes and cheese is 3 Minas\nMushroom Stew 1 Minas\nPumpkin Soup 1 Minas\nFondue 1 Minas\nChicken Soup 1 Minas\nMutton Soup 1 Minas\nRabbit soup 1 Minas\nVegetable Soup 1 Minas\nBeef Soup 1 Minas\nChicken Stew 2 Minas\nBeef Stew 2 Minas\nMutton Stew 2 Minas\nRabbit Stew 2 Minas\nChicken Noodle Soup 2 Minas\nMutton Noodle Soup 2 Minas\nRabbit Noodle Soup 2 Minas\nVegetable Noodle Soup 2 Minas\nBeef Noodle Soup 2 Minas\nCooked Chicken 1 Minas\nFried Chicken 2 Minas\nStuffed Chicken 3 Minas\nSteak 1 Minas\nPrime ribs (beef) 2 Minas\nMeatloaf 3 Minas\nCooked Rabbit 1 Minas\nRabbit Fricassee 2 minas\nMaple Rabbit 3 Minas\nCooked Mutton 1 Minas\nLamb Chops 3 Minas\nBurger 2 Minas\nBaked Potato 2 Minas\nChips 1 Minas\nStuffed potatos 2 Minas\nSteam Carrots 1 Minas\nCheese Omelet 1 Minas\nMushroom Omelet 1 Minas\n---