        StaticBook("Alai Kharadeen", "Kale le Prevost", "Caliphate Hospital\nHead Doctor Kale \n\nPatient's Name: Alai Kharadeen\n\nAge: 20\n\nRace: FarFolk\n\nGender: Male\nCondition/Injury:\nPatient came in with two bolts (arrows). One located in his backside, the other in his right shoulder. The shoulder was deeper than his back due to more secure armor in his backside.\n\nTreatment Plan:\nRemove the arrows and apply a braided\nstitching with a curved needle suture after giving the patient a potion to slow the bleeding down and regulate his heart beat. A concoction- tippens root.\n\n- Will stay over night for pain medication and further evaluation by Head Jaraah Kale\nDoctor who treated the patient: Head Jaraah Kale \n\nCost: Covered by Kharadeen Care Insurance\n\nDate: \nSummer month of Sun's Smile, 1543\n*Head Jaraah Kale's signature would be on this page* \n\n~ Kale de Sevanes", ""),
        StaticBook("Alc. Potions II", "Sarrion", "Alchemy: Potions\nPart II\n-------------------Please read Part I.\n\n-Sarrion di' Pascali\n=[Potion of Smoke Whispers]=\nike in the magical stories where the hero throws something into the floor and a cloud of smoke is formed, this potion creates the same as the vial shatters. Creating black smoke which releases fast, it allows the\nthrower a distraction or the ability to temporarily incapacitate the adversaries. Brewed over the course of four weeks, this potion is literally smoke in a bottle, and like it, it creates irritation when breathing and to the eyes.\nRecipe:\n\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n4 Air Symbols (Flight, Transport)\n1 Fire Symbol (Combustion)\n=[Potion of Sleeping]=\nUsed by people of all kinds, this potion’s objective is placing someone to sleep. It might act fast, it might act slow, it might be to help with sleeping at night, or it might be to knock someone out. The use will dictate the power\nthe potion has to be made. Minor potions will have more of a relaxing result, making resting far more easier to achieve. Lesser ones have to be drank, and soon after the potion will take effect and the one to drink it will not even\nnoticed he passed out. Greater potions on the other hand, might not even need to be drank, only smelled. This is particular good for doctors when needing to operate, as it does not force the patient to drink something.\nTo force it on someone might not have some good results, as the potion does take it’s time to give it’s effect, enough to fight back. It is worth noticing, that if the recipe is only read by the symbols needed, the lesser potion\nof sleeping is the same as the lesser potion of mending. Always be careful with the representations of the symbols you use.\n\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Calmness and Relaxation)\n1 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Calmness and Relaxation)\n1 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Resilience)\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Symbols of Water (Calmness and Relaxation)\n2 Symbols of Air (Flight and Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Resilience)\n=[Potion of Freezing]\nA peculiar potion, which it’s only intent is freezing or cooling something, or perhaps to just keep cold. I invented one of the potions, the potent one which quickly freezes water on contact, making it something impossible to drink\nand dangerous to the touch. This potion must actually be kept in a thick glass vial, and it then must be surrounded by fur, or something of the like as to keep it your hands from freezing and stopping water from getting\nstuck to the vial. Another recipe was made by my student, it is far weaker, and more for a use in someone’s body. To put it simply, it is a protection of a person’s cold, which seems quite horrible for most times.\nYet if you’re travelling into very hot climates, it could save one’s life.\n\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n1 Symbols of Water (Cold)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Resilience)\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Ice, Cold)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Protection)\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Symbols of Water (Calmness and Relaxation)\n1 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Hardiness)\n=[Waterbreathing Potion]=\nA remarkable potion which allows someone to breath underwater for long periods of time. The biggest side effect of this potion thought, is that you stop breathing air. Made of rare ingredients,\nmainly the liver and gills of a mermaid, it turns someone temporarily into a sort of human fish. Your skin between the toes and hands starts webbing, only falling out a few hours after the effects of the potion are gone. Being too long inside\nof the water also makes it so that when you finally leave, your ears seem to pop, and you can not hear for a few minutes. The most important part of the potion, is the creation of gills on the side of your neck, it is these that allow you to breathe\nunderwater, yet not above. For the first few moments of the transformation, someone can not breathe in or out of water, it may create panic in some people, yet they must remember to go into the water, because they will not be able to breath out of it.\nRecipe:\n\nBase: Aqua Vitae mixed with a bit of seawater\nMermaid’s Gills and Liver\n1 Symbols of Water (Fluidity)\n1 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Resilience)\n=[Frost Oil]=\nAs an oil, this concoction has an external use and is not to be drank. As I move on to the oils, the type of base fixes itself to only lard. Lard has a more viscous consistency which allows it not to drip when coated on something.\nThe Frost oil, or Oil of frost, is the first I will speak of. An oil which has similarities with the potion of freezing, but whose effects last longer, enabling it to be coated in weapons, armor or clothes. It’s effects are quick cooling what it touches,\nbut it reacts weakly to air, meaning it’s effect happen mostly through contact. Using such an oil on clothing or armor might make the wearer cold, but such could be the objective if one is travelling into hot deserts or inside volcanos.\nOn the other hand, while it might make the cloth or armor it was placed cold, it also offers a protection to the same cold, as something already cold, can’t get colder. As such, if one would use the oil of frost in cloth,\nhe would find himself getting colder, yet if the oil was used on the outer layer of plate armor, it would assist with protecting against cold winds. If placed on weapons, it has the most use on swords. A slash of the weapon on\nsomeone’s skin would slightly freeze the area. You might think a frozen cut would mean that the blood loss would be lower, and it’s true, yet freezing the area will make the skin turn slightly blue, and the opponent will have difficulties moving\nthe area, this way slowing him down. The cut makes the cooling enter more into the flesh, perhaps even forcing someone to have to remove the frozen flesh affected, perhaps even amputating a limb. The biggest worry of using it on tools\nand armor is that it also cools it down substantially, and when badly brewed will make metals very easily shattered, when well brewed they will still suffer some problems in lesser effect.\nRecipe:\n\nBase: Lard\n3 Symbols of Water(Cold, Ice, Frost)\n2 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Fortitude)\n=[Flame Oil]=\nThe Oil of Flame does almost the exact same as the Oil of Frost, yet instead of cold, it works with burning. In contact with the skin it will leave huge burns, but of course you do not apply it to the skin. On weapons,\nwhen striking the enemy, it will cause great pain a kind to burning. The flesh will become red and start to create puss. While the Oil of Frost might slow the opponent, the oil of Flames inflicts greater damage on him. The weapon does not escape\ndamage, while with the Frost Oil the weapon may shatter, with the Flame Oil it corrodes it. While the effects do seem like those of a flame, it does not actually heat an object up. It actually make it more flame repellent and heat resistant.\nOf course the resistance isn’t perfect, and a wooden sword coated with the oil will still catch ablaze, it does tarden the effects. This means if applied to armor or cloth that is not touching the skin, it creates a sort of heat and flame\nprotection. In the recipe it is found the use of a water symbol, and one might ask why such a representation is required in such a fire centric concoction. The explanation is rather simple, it calms the fire symbols of destruction and power, balancing\nit to not create an extreme reaction, which normally is represented as an explosion while brewing.\nBase: Lard\n3 Symbols of Fire (Power, Destruction, Burning)\n2 Symbols of Earth (Endurance)\n1 Symbol of Water (Calmness, Balance)\n>=[Alchemist’s Fire]=<\nOne of the greatest means of attack from an alchemist, their creation of fire. Many times referred to as ‘fire in a bottle,’ a more correct term would be ‘liquid fire.’ The alchemist is able to access the properties of fire and\nadd them into a liquid, making it highly volatile and dangerous. Getting hit by a bottle of it would result in being completely covered in flames. Of course it’s not always used for combat, and many times it is used to cleaning metal utensils,\nsuch as cauldrons and knives from contaminants and impurities. Some may say it’s a waste to use such a powerful potion on cleaning, but it’s use that way may also be associated with it’s danger. Alchemist’s fire is highly dangerous,\nboth while brewing and after. To brew it, not only must the temperature of the concoction remain constant, that temperature must be almost freezing. The room must be made almost specifically to create it,\nas it must be freezing cold. Some alchemists have started using Thanhium to have a cold room in their labs instead of heading to the tall mountains, or the cold Tundras. In those conditions the alchemist’s fire is made, and even brewed in freezing\ntemperatures, it still can burn your hand. The bottles must be made of glass, and to fill them, thongs of sorts must be used, as if your hand touches the liquid it will be burnt, even will gloves. Never should an alchemist fall\ninto the mistake of using a wooden cork, as the liquid will burn right through it and most likely blow in the hands of the handler, they must always be made of glass. Now onto the dangers of the bottles. If they are kept stationary,\nthey won’t be dangerous, it’s problems start when they are moved quickly or hit. Some alchemists keep them in Athin made sacks to prevent some of it’s force if the bottle is broken, yet even so the alchemist would be burnt. Falling\nwhile carrying these bottles, or being pushed, punched, thrown to the ground may result in a bottle breaking. For them to be useful they must break, but that is the bane of the carrier as well.\nThe safest way to use the bottle is to drop it, it results in it blowing up when hitting the ground in almost all cases. While it does explode, it’s explosion is not one like tnt, but more of many tiny shards of glass and fire sent flying everywhere.\nRecipe:\n\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n4 Symbols of Fire (Destruction, Power, Consumption)\n2 Symbols of Water (Fluidity)\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed)", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy", "Venator", "Liriel's Book of\n    Alchemy Recipes\n==================\nBasic Teas using one ingredient and water:\nRose\nPoppy\nDandelion\nCactus\nBlue Orchid\nJuices, brewed with one ingredient and water:\nPumpkin\nCarrot\nMelon\nAlcohols:\nPale ale - made with wheat\nMulled Wine - Dark Resin\nEggnog - Egg\nPoisons: To be added", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy", "Audrey Caillot", "The Alchemist’s Notebook \nForeword\n\nThe Realm of Anthos is filled with all types of herbs, creatures and phenomena to which are the delight of the many alchemists which fill it. Swamps and plains; hills and deserts can be found all around the\ncontinent, and in each of them a plethora of regents await to be found. With that being said and done, I welcome you, reader; to the Alchemist’s Notebook on each (though not every) of these very regents in their corresponding habitats.\nThe Southern Desert\n\nGoblin’s Ivy\nKnown for its hardiness and abundance, Goblin’s Ivy covers dunes, caves, buildings and trees seemingly without preference or deterrence of any of the nearby inhabitants. The sludgy, Orc-Hide\nhue that colours the vine is, to be blunt, abhorrent, and its lack of appeal is only increased by its near uselessness in alchemy. With that being said, though, every regent has its function, and Goblin’s Ivy’s would be as an obvious symbol Earth,\nresilience, and life. It can be used somewhat effectively in Stoneskin Potions, Potions of Fortitude, and even Potions of Strength. It’s been seen to have been used in poisons too, strangely, though any such are useless in practicality and cause no more\nthan mild nausea. Finding it isn’t a challenge, even in the vast expanse of the Badlands, and harvesting it is done simply enough by cutting off a length of the vine with a machete or a similar knife, and keeping it in your satchel with all the other\nregents you have collected. When used in potions it can be extracted into water through boiling, or crushed finely in a mortar and pestle, though the second is advised in lards and oils.\nBlood Lotus\nWith a blood like colouring and a blood like taste, the aptly named Blood Lotus is a desert crawler considered to be a valuable regent when traversing the dunes in search of a symbol of Fire. It’s widely accepted that heat and\nstrength are the two main things the plant represents in alchemy, and can be used in many potions in need of a more (And I use this lightly) calm portrayal of fire. It has been said that Blood Lotus can be brewed into an invigorating ale, or even\neaten crushed as a nutritional spice, and is commonly fed to people weak with sickness to help keep up their strength. It can be easily found in the mouths of caves and caverns and harvested by bottling the plant and keeping it alive until use. It wilts\nand becomes useless quickly; as is the tendency for flame-related flora.\n \nThe Northern Icelands\nFrost Vine\nFound in the deepest cold of the North, it is only natural that Frost Vine be known as a symbol of Water-\nBut more importantly so of ice, calmness and release. It blends well into its chilly landscape with a light blue, and almost grey skin, and would seem to prefer to live in the shade of a tree, sheltered from the North gales. It can be used well in Oils\nof Frost and Potions of Mending, as one of its more useful attributes is a handy numbing agent that can be observed simply by a few minutes touch. After being crushed and extracted into water it becomes more potent, and is as quick and powerful\nat numbing as any alchemist or healer would need it to be. Harvesting can be done by bottling the vines and perhaps keeping them cold, and it should be said that growing Frost Vine away from the North or any other cold ecosystem is nearly impossible due\nto its fragile nature.\n\nElrow Berries\nA strange plant to say the least, Elrow berries are one of the only symbols of Fire that can be grown naturally in cold climates such as the North. One would seem to ask why when first told this fact,\nthough by only a simple taste of the Devils of the North would they find out. Similar to chilli’s in nature, the berries burn the eater’s tastebuds and dry his throat nigh instantly upon consumption; leaving you craving for water\nor some other release from the aching Elrow Berries bring. A mouth full of snow is a common enough cure for ‘berry burn’, and any nearby Frost Vine or Serpent’s Stalk would work just as well in the case of any snowless expanse.\nIt can be used in potions and poisons alike as a symbol of power, anger and destruction, as that is simply what follows after eating the Berries of Elrow. They can be harvested without worry from any bush found in a cranny in a rock up North,\nthough tend to lose some potency once dried. To dry and crush the berries is the best way to use them in a potion, though ample warnings should be given for any ignorant lab assistants; as even after processing they possess the same spice as they\nwould naturally.\nElf’s Hair \nAs rare as any growable regent can get, and as hard to spot as a Signus in a snowstorm, the Elf’s Hair Vine may only be seen once or twice in a whole year of searching, as many Alchemists find out to their dismay.\nFound atop mountains or hanging precariously over cavern edges, these wisps of vine and blossom are rivalled only in their potency by their beauty. The petals of the plant are of a soft, creamy white, and are indeed the most useful part of the plant-\nIn an alchemical sense, at the least. They hang loosely off the vine they grow on, and with any strong gust of wind are blown off and away; drifting over the air to populate some sparse piece of land far away. It is undeniable that Elf’s Hair is a symbol\nof Air, speed, and grace, and it has been said that it an essential in any potent Potion of Swiftness. To harvest it one must be very careful- a stray bump could mean losing your rarity to the winds. It is the petals and the nectar that are the most\npotent part of the plant, so plucking the whole blossom would be the simplest and easiest way. The nectar can be infused slowly with a potion, drop by drop, and the petals crushed; which is the most unfortunate part of using this reagent.\nCommonly, after the blossoms have been used, the vines wilt, die, and succumb to the winter winds.\n\nThe Midland Marshes\nDwarven Pumpkin\nAs swampy a plant as one could rightly get, Dwarven Pumpkin is a valuable symbol of\nFire, power, and destruction. It can be easily spotted amongst the swamps and bogs by the murky orange leaves that surround it; these being the main part of the plant you will want to use- and the brighter, the more potent, in this case. It’s\nusually found basking in sunlight in a rare clearing in the Marshes, which indeed is a great need of most herbs representing fire. Though commonly used for its potency in potions revolving entirely around fire, Dwarven Pumpkin also\nhas a use in many other potions such as ones of fortitude, in which its representation of power grants a concentration boost to your armour-for-your-armour. Harvesting it is done by pruning off the leaves of brightest orange,\nand keeping them uncrushed in your satchel. They should be used soon after harvesting, in potions, by crushing them thoroughly and pouring the juice slowly into your concoction. It’s not a naturally toxic plant- but neither is it\nparticularly pleasant to eat; with a bitter, clinging aftertaste.\nSaffvil\nThis plant, looking more like some clump of dilapidated weed-grass than a useful ingredient, is one of the few regents in the Marshes which is more repugnant to harvest\nthan Mandragora. Found among the rotting carcasses of recently deceased swamp beasts, or sprouting from beneath decomposing mushrooms, Saffvil is a vile floral parasite and decomposer with a very handy use in potions needing a strong symbol of\nEarth, resilience, and decay. Poisons are the strong suite of this lacklustre herb; it has long been known to be a critical component in some of the more deadly brews, and indeed induces a blood clotting effect in most potions it is used in- though this\ncan be remedied by including the nectar of the swamp blossom plant in your concoction, or any other strong symbol of air and speed. Harvesting it can be done by a simple uprooting of the whole, grassy mound, and washing it clean of any contaminations,\nto avoid impure potions (the bane of any alchemist intent on keeping their eyebrows). The easiest way Saffvil can be used in potions is to infuse it by a process similar to tea making. Leave the regent in a pouch soaking in your base ingredient\nuntil most of the plant has lost its colour, and dispose of it afterwards.\nSwamp Blossom\nFound growing in the crowded treetops above the Midland Marshes, this purple stemmed perennial produces strange, transparent nectar known well for\nits interesting properties, and its use as a symbol of Air, speed, and motion. The liquid will not diffuse into water in great quantities without great heat and effort, and seems to refuse to behave as anything aqueous should. It glides across skin,\nand most any other surface it comes into contact with, and only seems to be interested in sticking to itself- Quite the opposite of water, in fact. Growing naturally on the branches of high-reaching swamp trees, Swamp Blossom can be spotted\nby its curved purple-green petals and the previously mentioned burly, mauve-hued stem. Swiftness Potions and Potions of Mending are what this plant is of most use in, as both require a powerful symbol for speed. To harvest this plant\nis difficult- One must wait for first the plant to be producing its nectar, before slowly letting it collect it a water skin, or a vial. Consumption is practically harmless, though not advised- As Swamp Blossom is much more valuable as an alchemical\nregent than it is a barely nutritional, foul tasting pallet cleanser.\nMandragora\nOne of the more deadly plants inhabiting the swamps of Anthos, Mandragora is quite the prize of any herbalist; and is rather impressive on display.\nIn several stages of its lifecycle, this parsnip shaped fungi releases toxic spores with a hallucinogenic and eventually fatal effect on most creatures when inhaled. The meat of this plant is the most useful in potions involving clarity and regeneration,\nand is a somewhat strong symbol of Water when properly harvested. The plant’s brown coloured leaves can be used in soups, brews, or a rather nice tea-  Though all have a chance of fatality or intoxication if boiled or cooked incorrectly.\nHarvesting this plant, as would be expected, is nigh impossible for any unknowing alchemist; two to three weeks after the Mandragora’s spores are released is the safe time to harvest, eat, and use it in potions.\nThis can be done by simply uprooting the whole thing, and separating the leaves and ‘meat’ later on at your alchemical workstation. The best way to brew Mandragora into apotion is to grind it up with a Mortar and Pestle, sprinkle it through your base,", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Laws", "Sarrion", "Alchemy: The Principle and Law of Equivalent Exchange\n-------------------\nRe-Written by: Sarrion di' Pascali\n\nFrom:\nThe Tales of a Traveling Alchemist\nAs I was providing my services to a rather quaint hamlet, which also provided me information of the local flora and more of the same legends I always here of, I was approached by a man of common repute, and he produced\na sarcastic, yet thought provoking, question. This question was, and I will attempt to reproduce the dialect as best as my phonetic ability will allow, “ ‘ow come, Mister, ‘hat ye’ can make all ‘dis ‘onderful stuff outta nothin’?”\nNow as shameful as his speech may be, the question remains the same. How is it, that alchemists are capable or reshaping the spells of sorcerers for the common folk out of, seemingly, nothing?\nThe answer to this question is simple to state, but fairly difficult to grasp, and this is the Principle of Equivalent Exchange. Much like the money one gives to the merchant for the apple or slab of meat, one cannot have something for nothing.\nAs the saying goes, “there is no such thing as a free brunch,” there is no such thing as a free potion. This fundamental rule applies to old alchemy, through the use of symbols and rituals, far more than what\nI call “Modern” alchemy. Although I will not get into ancient alchemy, I will state why this rule applies to Modern Alchemy. To craft a potion, for example a bottle of alchemist’s fire, one requires the materials. Much like a spell\ncasted by a wizard, one cannot make something out of nothing. Know that to make a potion, and the possibilities are truly endless, one must take plants, objects, and other representations of what they wish to make.\nFor example, alchemist’s fire could be best produced with an oil base, a mixture of Drake’s Tail, blaze powder, and a dash of coal dust. Why would one need these items?\nThe oil base provides the basic mixture of what we will make, and of course the better quality of the oil the better quality of the Alchemist’s Fire, but of course we will get further into this in a later chapter. The Drake’s Tail, a crimson, thorned\nplant that grows most often in deserts, is often warm to the touch and often associated with rage and flame. This provides an superb symbol for the element of fire. The Blaze Powder, another powerful symbol of fire,\nmixes well with the crushed Drake’s Tail to produce something truly strong. The coal dust, an optional portion, is another symbol of flame,\nalbeit both weaker than blaze powder or Drake’s Tail for both a Blaze and Drake’s fire burns far greater than coal.\nNow then, although you have these symbols of flame, rage, and warfare, one mustn’t simply toss objects into the metaphorical cauldron. Precision is necessary, as always. One must measure their mixture carefully, or they will give too much.\nAnd giving too much will tip the scales of Equivalent Exchange, causing unpredictable results. Why is this you might ask? When balance is achieved through Equivalent Exchanged, a mixture of the elements for the bottled spell\nof your desire, than all is well. But when you disrupt this balance and push on the world, taking and forcing in too much of one or more element then the world will push back. Of course a word of caution is required,\nfor one may think taking less is the best option when balance is not a certainty. This is a common misconception for not providing enough of one element will result in the same conclusion, imbalance and chaos. This can be easily\nassociated with cooking, too much of one ingredient will spoil the recipe, not enough of an ingredient will produce similar results. Of course it could also produce blander results,\nand in that case a potion may not be spoiled but it will simply be weak. This is preferable to exploding, of course. \n===================End.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Notes", "Vitalius Maarsen", "-Alchemy notes-\n\n            by\n    Vitalius Maarsen\n\n\nIn these pages you will find some Alchemy notes taken by me while studying from various books.\n-Equivalent Exchange\n\nAlchemy is ruled by the law of Equivalent exchange, you give something to get an element with the same properties back, an example would be people approaching alchemy to convert lead in to gold, however that is not\nwhat would happen, the lead would just take some properties of the gold and make it seem like it, you can't get more if you give less.\nThere are 4 elements in alchemy: Fire, Water, Air and Earth.\n\n-Fire\nDestruction, Damage, Power, Chaos, Emotion, Gusto, Love, Passion\n\n-Water\nLife, Birth and Rebirth, Agility, Flow, Healing, Coldness\n-Earth\nFlora, Fauna, Spirit, Fortitude, Stalwartness, Strengh, Reinforcement (reinforces the brew)\n\n-Air\nKnowledge, Wisdom, Acuity, Clarity, Perception, Speed, Alacrity\n(Quickens the Brew)\nThere are 4 types of alchemical potions:\nLesser, Moderate, Greater and Oils\n\n-Lesser potions\nUsed by novice to practice it has a base of water and weak reagents, its power is weak\n-Moderate Potions\nUsed to affect minorly someone or something it uses a base of water and moderate reagents, its power is standard\n\n-Greater Potions\nThese potions are dangerous to make because of theur volatility they use a base of Aqua vitae\nand strong reagents and also using the other 2 classes, its power is strong\n\n-Oils\nThey use a base of lard and its effects range from destructive to healing, difficult to brew for their consistency\n*A list of reagents and their properties would be here\n\nhttps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1fI9t9kK8w3byhohFDAdUkBp5lWjqnuI4gZEOn5ckpXQ/edit#gid=0\n\n\n\n*\nAqua vitae is a type of water used in potions, its made by distilling some alcohol, mostly wine\n\n-Aqua vitae recipe-\nTake whatever wine you please, put it in to a copper still, two parts of three being empty, distill it until no more is left.\nThere is also a second recipe that uses beer instead:\n\nTake a stale of strong beer and put it in a copper still, distill it gently and there will come forth a week part of aqua vitae, which is called low wine that needs to be distilled again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Recipes", "Rosso", "Sleeping Draught\n\n==================\nWild Lettuce\nWater\n\n>Break leaves from plant\n>Steep leaves 1 hr. in hot water.\nBurn/Rash Oiuntment*\n\n==================\nWild Lettuce\n\n>Break leaves from plant\n>Grind leaves into poultice\n>Add water and a whole Wild Lettuce\n*Helps with dry skin\nRespiration Potion\n\n==================\nWater\nCaterpillar Fungus\n\n>Grind up fungus\n>Add fungus to heated water, and mix well\nHealing Water I\n\n==================\nWater\nLily pad\n\n>Heat up water\n>Cut up Lily Pad and mix with water\n>Pour some in wound\nWARNING:\n    Stings slightly\nHealing Water II\n\n==================\nRose\nSpider Eye\nBone\nWater\n\n>Gring up Rose, Spider Eye, and Bone\n>Mix with water that was once snow\nHealing water II\n                (Cont’d)\n==================\nLily Pad\nHealing Water II\n\n>Place a few drops in wound\n>Place Lily Pad on wound and bandage\n-If Lily Pad turns brown, it’s healing\nPoison\n\n==================\n3 Spider Eyes\n2 Bones\nWater\n\n>Grind up all 3 Spider Eyes\n>Grind up both bones into bonemeal\n>Add both to heated water\nPoison II\n\n==================\nPoison I\n2 Spider Eyes\nBone\nRose\nDead Lily Pad\n\n>Grind up Bone, Rose, Spider Eyes, and Lily Pad\n>Mix with Poison I\nBone Pain Reliever\n\n==================\nShroom of Immortality\nWater\nLily Pad\n\n>Grind up Shroom of Immortality\n>Gring up Lily Pad\n>Mix together, then add heated water\nStomach Pain Reliever\n\n==================\nJelly Ear\nWater\nSugarcane\n\n>Grin up Jelly Ear and mix with heated water\n>Extract sugar from sugarcane, and add to mixture\nDraught of Thought\n\n==================\n2 Magic Shrooms\nWater\nWild Lettuce\n\n>Grind Wild Lettuce into a poultice\n>Grind up Magic Shrooms\n>Mix together, then add water, and heat\nLimb Pain Reliever\n\n==================\n……. Shroom\nWater\nLily Pad\n\n>Grind up Lily Pad\n>Grind up ……. Shroom\n>Mix together, then add to heated water\nEnergy Potion\n\n==================\n2 Cocoa Beans\nSugarcane\nWater\n\n>Grind up Cocoa beans\n>Extract Sugar from Sugarcane\n>Mix together, then add to heated water\nEnergy Potion II\n\n==================\n3 Cocoa Beans\n2 Sugarcane\nWater\n\n>Steep Sugarcane in water half an hour\n>Grind up Cocoa beans\n>Get rid of sugarcane, and add Cocoa Beans, ground, to water\nPain Reliever\n\n===================\nTippens Root\n\nCopiers note: The book ends here, it is unfinished.\nAlchemy Recipes\n\nUnknown Author\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Recipes", "Sarrion Zytiaear", "Alchemical Recipe Book\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy Sarrion Zytiaear\nPotion of Mending\n---------------\nA quick healing exlier that is suggested to be applied directly to wounds as opposed to consumption.\n- Minor:\nBase: Water\n1 Symbol of Water (Life)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Life)\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Life)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Life)\n1 Symbol of Air (Quickness)\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Symbols of Water (Life)\n2 Symbols of Earth (Life)\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed)\nPotion of Regeneration\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-*The rest of this page and the related pages have been torn out*\nPotion of Stoneskin\n-------------------\nAn Elixer than fortifies flesh to stone, though the side effects after are quite nasty.\nBase: Distilled water\n4 Symbols of Earth (Fortitude)\n2 Symbols of Water (Life)\n3 Symbols of Fire (Power)\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed)\nPotion of Strength\n-------------------An elixer proven to boost the abilities of muscles within the body. Highly suggested to 'train' the body to such effects as taking too much of a dosage or too powerful of one can cause heavy pain and damage.\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n1 Symbol of Earth (Fortitude, Power, Resilience)\n\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Earth (Fortitude, Power, Resilience)\n1 Symbol of Fire (Power)\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n3 Symbols of Earth (Fortitude, Power, Resilience)\n1 Symbol of Fire (Power)\nPotion of Celerity\n-------------------A useful elixer used to increase the reflexes and speed of its user. Allowing increased movement speeds. The side effects are commonly sore muscles etc.\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed)\n\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n3 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Fire (Power)\nPotion of Accuity\n-------------------An Elixer to highten the senses of the drinker, great for a hunt or jobs that require great vision or hearing. Side effects are commonly worstened senses after for a while.\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n2 Symbol of Air (Perception)\n\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n3 Symbols of Air (Perception)\n\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n4 Symbols of Air (Perception)\nPotion of Smoke Whispers\n-------------------TLDR: Smoke Bomb. Takes over four weeks of brewing to bottle it to perfection, any shorter and the effects wont be as desirable.\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n4 Air Symbols (Flight, Transport)\n1 Fire Symbol (Combustion)\nPotion of Sleeping\n-------------------An elixer than should be used to help with sleeping.. but a more powerful brew can most often be used in mischievous ways. Lesser needs to be consumed while more powerful brews may only need to be smelled etc.\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Calmness and Relaxation)\n1 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Calmness and Relaxation)\n1 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Resilience)\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Symbols of Water (Calmness and Relaxation)\n2 Symbols of Air (Flight and Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Resilience)\nPotion of Freezing\n-------------------An Elixer of great coldness. Potent brews can freeze water on contact and keep the air chill alone while very lesser ones might be consumed to help keep the body cool in hot weather.\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n1 Symbols of Water (Cold)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Resilience)\n\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Ice, Cold)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Protection)\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Symbols of Water (Calmness and Relaxation)\n1 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Hardiness)\nWaterbreathing Potion\n-------------------This elixer turns one into a sort of walking man fish creating webbing on the hands and feet and gills in the neck for a few hours.. Though the main regent is extremely rare to get.\nBase: Aqua Vitae mixed with a bit of seawater\nMermaid’s Gills and Liver\n1 Symbols of Water (Fluidity)\n1 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Resilience)\nFrost Oil\n-------------------Essentially an oil form of the potion of freezing but lasts a lot longer and is much more easilly applied to weaponry and items.\nBase: Lard\n3 Symbols of Water(Cold, Ice, Frost)\n2 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Fortitude)\nFlame Oil\n-------------------The oposite of frost oil, this stuff can cause great burns on exposed skins and can be easily applied to weaponry and armour.\nBase: Lard\n3 Symbols of Fire (Power, Destruction, Burning)\n2 Symbols of Earth (Endurance)\n1 Symbol of Water (Calmness, Balance)\nFortitude Oil\n-------------------\"Armour for your Armour\" is the saying with this oil, being able to fortify metals and materials it touches but it can quickly rust out or weaken the material after prolonged use etc.\nBase: Lard\n3 Symbols of Earth (Endurance, Fortitude, etc.)\n2 Symbols of Fire (Potency, Power)\nHair Rejuvenating Oil\n-------------------A high elves cheat to having a great beard. It fortifies the hair or creates hair whereever it touches. Great for balding folk etc!\nMinor\nBase: Lard\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed/Grace)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Hardiness)\n1 Symbol of Water (Rejuvenation)\n- Lesser\nBase: Lard\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed/Grace)\n2 Symbols of Earth (Hardiness and Regrowth)\n1 Symbol of Water (Rejuvenation)\n- Greater:\nBase: Lard\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed/Grace)\n2 Symbols of Earth (Hardiness and Regrow)\n2 symbol of Water (Rejuvenation and Life)\nGlue Oil\n-------------------Kinda self explainatory.\nBase: Lard\n1 Symbol of Air (Travel/Speed)\n2 Symbols of Earth (Hardiness, Connection)\nAlchemist’s Fire\n-------------------*The rest of this page and the following respective pages have been torn out*", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Terms", "[Coterie] Marius Pontmercy", "School of Alchemy handbook: \n\n        Chapter one:\n      Termenology\nRose = Blood Lotus\nVines = Frost Vine\nBirch = Alabustar\nTallgrass = Saffuil\nRed Mush. = Flame tounge\nBrown Mush. = Miners H.\nLily Pad = Mandragora\nSuger Cane = Serpants S.\nCactus = Goblins Ivy\nPoison Potatoe = Swamp Blossom\nSlimeballs = Lard\nTippens root = Tippens root (2 oak sapplings)\nRed Dye = Elrow Berries\nFeather = Bird Feather\nIce = Water Elemental\nString = Elves hair vine\nEggs = Air Elemental\n     Conitnued Pg.3\nGlistining melon = Night Syrup\nCocoa beans Dwarfven pumpkin\n\nDistilled Water (Purified)\nWater + Coal\n\n\nBad Ingrediants (Negitive)\n---------------------------\nBlaze powwder\nMagma creme\nSpider's eye\nRotton Flesh\nRedstone\nFermented Spider Eye\nBones n' Bonemeal\nNetherbrick", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy: Botany", "Sarrion", "Alchemy: Botany\n-------------------This glossery is a detailed explaination of the Botany with in alchemy, and was written by an unknown alchemist.\n\nRe-Written by:\nSarrion di' Pascali\n=[->Earth<-]=\n          Weak\nName: Goblin’s Ivy\nRepresentation: Resilience, Poison, Life\n\nDescription: One of the most easily found flora of the deserts, this plant is easily identified as a\nbrownish green vine with small leaves. It is found mainly clinging onto old buildings or ruins of the deserts, and on the dry cliff sides. It is quite a resilient plant, able to survive in extreme hostile conditions, and\nwith a very low or no amount of water close by. Removing it also becomes a problem, as it seems to regrow on the same spot after someone goes to the long labour of removing it all. It is these properties that brings the plant such\ngood uses, it’s representation of resilience makes a welcome addition to any stoneskin potion, even while being regarded as a Weak reagent. A few poisons may also be created by use of this reagent,\nmainly ones weaker, some to create nausea or ill disposition. Easy to find and prepare, it is normally used by those new to alchemy to learn the craft.\n\nLocation: Clinging on ruins, stones and cliff sides of dry regions.\n-------------------\nModerate\nName: Saffvil\n\nRepresentation: Resilience, Endurance, Death\n\nDescription: Possibly the most horribly smelling herb in all of swamplands, many alchemists make use\nof their nose when trying to find it. This green grass is green and grows on the corpses of animals, on dead wood and plants, and sometimes on the bottom of big trees. This plant is one that is extremely hard to remove from anything,\nas it spreads very quickly and strongly. Normally to remove it, you would have to remove the “host”, the plant or animal that it is growing on. If you do not, it will spread all throughout it. This means that the plant has a great representation\nof Resilience and Endurance, but this plant, unlike a few other Earth symbols, does not represent Life and Regrowth, but Death. This means this plant is mostly used in the creation of poisons,\nand one particular myth of an aging potion.\n\nLocation: On the bodies of dead plants and animals.\n-------------------\nName: Alabaster Leaf\n\nRepresentations: Immobility, Perseverance\n\nDescription: This plant is mostly characterized by it’s leaf’s alabaster color. Most often times found in the dryer regions of the forest growing around fallen trees.\nQuite small in size, harvesting it may prove a difficulty to the untrained hands. The best method would perhaps be taking the whole plant, with roots, and then remove the leaves as you may use them. The extract one gets by crushing the leaves is what\nan alchemist should use. It comes with it’s natural alabaster hue, which serves as paint to many. The extract is mildly poisonous, creating dizziness and nausea to those that consume it. It’s main uses are in antidotes, oils, and of course, poisons.\nLocation: Forest dry regions next to fallen trees.\n-------------------Name: Tippen’s Root\n\nRepresentation: Life, Regrowth, Resilience, Strength, Endurance\n\nDescription: Tippen’s roots is one of the most used\nreagents in the making of mending potions, it is even said, that it is required to be present in all healing potions, or the potion will be of weak quality. It was named after the botanist that had first discovered it around hills and\nin dense forests. It’s location of growing is often the same of that of Alabaster leaf, besides fallen trees, but as well next to carcases of animals and great bugs. It is quite a pleasant sight when compared with the death around it,\nas the plant of the herb blooms into purple flowers. What one has to use though, is the roots. They are of a yellow color, with spots accentuated a bit more darker. Many carry these roots around, even those with no knowledge of it’s use in alchemy.\nThis is because from the roots one can easily make a remedy which may stop bleeding near instantly. In it’s unprepared it’s strength isn’t as great, but it still may save countless lives. The problem with this root is a simple one, it’s smell.\nThe odor that the plant releases when the salve of the roots is spilled is enormous. While using it you may gag and even vomit from thinking that you are placing such foul-smelling balm onto an open wound. After such,\nthe smell will not escape you for a few hours. It’s traits in healing bring the herb representations of Life and Regrowth, but it also has great representations of Strength and Endurance.\nLocation: Forest, around dead trees and animals.\n-------------------Name: Desert Berry Bush\n\nRepresentation: Protection, Resilience\n\nDescription: The Desert Berry Bush's appearance is that of a withered rose bush,\nlong brown/grey stalks with big pointy thorns, yet without any leaves. It doesn't appear to grow higher than four feet, but most of the thorns are longer than an inch. It grows inside cactus forests, as in, where there  is great concentration\nof cactus. Never has one been alone in the desert’s sands without a cactus near it. The bush gives Berries of a strong red color every full moon. These don't last long, as animals of the desert appear to enjoy it's taste quite dearly.\nThe berries are extremely sweet, something very strange to find in the desert, so no wonder the animals enjoy it. The stalks are not like the berries, if an animal by any chance passed the long thorns to rip and eat the stalk, I believe\nwould fall dead in less than a day. As you cut the stalk you notice that the insides are green, instead of the dead brown. From it it's juice flows a lot, yet of course it's poison to drink it. Eating the liquid or even touching it causes rashes and all\nsomeone wants to do afterwards is scratch the area, even if it’s the mouth. Too much of it and it kills of course, and it sound be painful. The thorns create the same effect, so without gloves, the hand starts itching and becomes red for about a day.\nIt doesn't seem deadly to descendents and probably kha's, but it does explain the small rodents found dead near them. A thorn is poisonous, and annoying, just doesn't kill big animals. The stalk seems to have far more uses in\nalchemy when compared with it’s berry, especially in oils of protection and potions of stoneskin. It represents protection and resilience, the thorns and it's poison nature being the reasons why. To prepare for it I have found it hard,\nas when cut, the juices drip quite fast. You can't remove the bush from the ground, as it's roots are too big, so they have to be cut in the spot. Feet long pieces of stalk are enough, yet one would have to almost tilt the plant\ndown so that the cut doesn't face down. Gloves are essential in gathering it because of the thorns, and after cutting, I advise placing it in a long bottle, with the cut end pointing up.\nWhen being prepared, the alchemist should be careful as to lose as little bit of the stalk as he removes the seemingly dead outer layer of the stalk, before using it in his potion.\n\nLocation: Desert Cactus Forests\nStrong\nName: Starved Coyote’s Tick\nRepresentations: Protection, Resilience, Connection\n\nDescription: The Tick that I speak of is probably the only non flora which I speak of as an Alchemy\ningredient in this volume. Mostly it can be found on coyotes the first ones discovered on the bodies of thin starved coyotes, giving them the name. This does not mean it does not appear in other animals, like desert\nhares and rhinos. As long as it is an animal that grows in hot climates, you may be lucky enough to find one. If the animal has a lot of fur, it may be hard to find the tick, but due to it’s size, just passing a hand through the animal may\nmake one find the tick. It might get as big as a thumb, very fat of pure brown color. It would seem many times as a lump in the animal’s skin, and trying to remove it is mostly impossible. The Staved Coyote’s Tick, once grabbing onto some meat,\nwill never let go unless it wants to. Fire, Ice, or even swings of a warhammer only damage the skin around it, the tick itself resiting more. It’s collecting is done by cutting the flesh that the tick is grabbing, and only when all the meat\nis removed from the tick, does it try to find another place to grab to. This is a dangerous thing to do, as if an alchemists isn’t careful, even with gloves the tick may grab onto the skin, and never let go. When I say never,\nI truly mean it, no one can make the tick let go, most likely the finder would have to be removed, or at least part of it, that or one would learn to live with the tick, as it doesn’t seem toxic or poisonous to an animal. With characteristics like this,\nit is no wonder that it is a strong symbol of earth, representing Connection, Protection and Resilience.\n\nLocation: Bodies of animals of hot Climates\n=[Fire Symbols]=\n->Weak\n\nName: Desert Bush Berry\n\nRepresentations: Empowerment, Overwhelming\n\nDescription: The Desert Berry Bush's\nappearance is that of a withered rose bush, long brown/grey stalks with big pointy thorns, yet without any leaves. It doesn't appear to grow higher than four feet, but most of the thorns are longer than an inch. It grows inside cactus\nforests, as in, where there is great concentration of cactus.Never has one been alone in the desert’s sands without a cactus near it. The Desert Bush Berries are the berries given by the Desert Berry Bush.\nThe bush gives Berries of a strong red color every full moon. These don't last long, as animals of the desert appear to enjoy it's taste quite dearly. The berries are extremely sweet, something very strange to find in the desert,\nso no wonder the animals enjoy it. The use of the berries are mostly in culinary, serving as treats, in jams and to bake. As for alchemy uses, it behaves as a fire symbol, as is custom to red ingredients. In this case not because of the color,\nbut because of the strong flavor it has, almost overwhelming. On the other hand, it doesn't appear all that useful nor seems to give great use in equivalent exchange. Great to be used by new alchemists in their training, as it quite safe.\nLocation: Desert Cactus forests in Full moon days.\n-------------------===================To be Continued...\nPlease look for:\nAlchemy: Botany II", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy: Potions", "Sarrion", "Alchemy: Potions\n-------------------Glossery based off\na book written by an Unknown Alchemist.\n\nRe-Written by:\nSarrion di' Pascali\n=[Potion of Mending]=\nOften times the most used potions of an alchemist’s arsenal. Mending potions are those to aid the hurt and injured with their effects of repairing flesh and bone, as well as body and mind. Potions of Mending are\nnormally administered both internally and externally. Pouring it on bandages to place over wounds is a normal way of using it, as well as drank as well. For illnesses it is just drank, and for minor cuts and bruises just\nplacing it on the wound is enough. Minor wounds require only minor potions, and no better potion should be used for these kinds of injuries. This is because greater potions, those designed for greater injuries are often\ntime a way to escape death, or save from devastating injuries, and side effects result from extreme fast regeneration or reconstruction of tissue and bone. Paralysis of the area, scarring, chronic pain and small deformations\nmay appear from the greatest of potions, yet their effects can be as great as repairing a shattered bone, returning vision to a cut eye, closing wounds in seconds. Even though those things are possible, sometimes\neven faster than with magic, they do not only require the use of the potions, but as well medical expertise. A potion to fix up a shattered bone requires it to be administered directly into the bone, and that means the flesh must be cut to expose it,\nwhich to do safely is quite the task. Of course even though the patient will he healed quite fast, he would be in no condition to do much for a few hours, fast healing is tiring for the body.\nRecipe:\n \n \n- Minor:\nBase: Water\n1 Symbol of Water (Life)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Life)\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Life)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Life)\n1 Symbol of Air (Quickness)\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Symbols of Water (Life)\n2 Symbols of Earth (Life)\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed)\n=[Potion of Regeneration]=\nA quite potent potion, it is part of the healing potions, but has a recipe on it’s own due to it’s complexity. It’s recipe is both dark, and it’s effects slow, but with amazing results.\nThe potion is able to remove scarring, and most of all, regrow missing limbs. Taking months to fully regrow the limb, they would then have to be retrained, and strengthened. It’s the most powerful healing potion an alchemist can\ndo, and to make it one must be quite adept at alchemy making, but as well face a choice which would leave most healers with a sore throat. The base used is not Aqua Vitae or Water, but the blood of the person that requires the potion.\nThis means the potion only might work on one person. Mandragora is used for it’s rejuvenation representation, and the other main ingredient is the liver of a mother of the same race. Not using the same race woman will result in horrible mutations,\nand weird growths, and not perfectly made potion will as well result in weird growths instead of the required limb. The mix of the ingredients are also quite reactive, which means it will take a skilful alchemists to make it carefully.\nIt becomes a dark colored liquid when complete, and throughout the making, the heat must be correct and constant. The other ingredients are not always the same, as the recipe like other greater healing potions.\nRecipe:\n\nBase: Blood\nMandragora\nLiver of a Mother\n2 Earth Symbols (Life)\n1 Air Symbol (Grace)\n=[Potion of Stoneskin]\nA potion that almost seems like a legend come true. This potion is one great in an alchemist’s arsenal. It makes one skin as hard as stone, armor without armor, able to protect itself against blades and arrows quite efficiently.\nOf course like hitting stone, some chipping of the skin might happen, and that will appear as wounds once the effects of the potion wears out. There are two major side effects of this potion. One of them is the fact that drinking\nit is extremely hard. Some that have drank it consider the taste worse than poison, and I do believe, as they are alchemists who I think would try poisons on themselves. After the effects of the potion the result is also one like being sick.\nVomit, extreme nausea are very common effects. The other side effect is what happens if the body can not fully handle the potion. They become like a rock, unable to move, fully paralyzed yet indestructible as well.\nIt is a rare effect, I would say happening one in five potions drank, but losing agility is a normal side effect of it. There is only one rank of this potion, anything\nless and it’s effects won’t be worth, anything more and the body can not take it.\n\nBase: Distilled water\n4 Symbols of Earth (Fortitude)\n2 Symbols of Water (Life)\n3 Symbols of Fire (Power)\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed)\n=[Potion of Strength]\nAnother highly sought after potion, this one is capable of enhancing the strength of someone, sometimes making an elf as strong as an Olog for short moments. Making such temporary changes to one’s body may bring quite\nthe great amount of pain, yet it’s great way to achieve victory in a duel or fight. The major problem, like that of the potion of stoneskin, is that the body is not adapted to this amount of strength. It has been heard about\npeople who drink this potion falling in pain as the effects of the potion come, or after the effects end, due to crushed bones, or destroyed muscles. If used in the right dosages and not excessively though, the side effect\nis normally tired muscles. The minor rank of this potion is quite good for training, and it’s effects quite safe, considering it only gives one a small power boost, good for lifting heavy weights out of a cart.\nRecipe:\n\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n1 Symbol of Earth (Fortitude, Power, Resilience)\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Earth (Fortitude, Power, Resilience)\n1 Symbol of Fire (Power)\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Earth (Fortitude, Power, Resilience)\n1 Symbol of Fire (Power)\n===================\n=[Potion of Celerity]=\nAlso know as potion of agility and potion of speed, the potion of celerity is the one that raises the movement speed and reflexes of the body. Normally wanted to be used for combat, many find it better to use\nwhen following prey while hunting, or even by thieves to quickly escape when seen. The side effects happen as all do when the body is changed temporarily, the body is not made to move faster than it\ndoes, and forcing it to do it may bring extreme pain to the muscles after the effects are done.\n\nRecipe:\n\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed)\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n3 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Fire (Power)\n=[Potion of Accuity]=\nAnother air based potion like the potion of Celerity, the potion of Accuity is an amazing potion to create and use. This potion provides the drinker with heightened senses, and may be prepared to all senses, or to specific\nones for more potency. Often times uses for hunting or for taking a job in hard tasks with require great vision, hearing or touch. In a competition of cooking for example, the judges might drink this potion beforehand for greater ability\nto judge the taste, and it is said that with it, someone might smell poison in their drink when there is no smell to sense. The result of enhancing the senses for a short while, is the worsening of them afterwards for a short while.\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n2 Symbol of Air (Perception)\n\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n3 Symbols of Air (Perception)\n\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n4 Symbols of Air (Perception)\n=[Potion of Wizard’s Wisdom]=\nEver wanted to feel like the great scholars of old? Then this potion is the one to use. A potion able to enhance the mental capabilities of the drinker temporarily. Fantastic even in it’s purple color, it enhances one’s\nproblem solving, reasoning, and general thinking ability. Of great use to alchemists as well, especially when formulating new potions and you find yourself stuck on a problem. This potion will aid you, not by giving you ideas as soon as you drink it\nbut by clearing your mind, making you think fluidly, and giving you a new perspective on the matter. It’s reagents are many, so to create them you would take quite the lengthy time, and the migraines it creates\nare long, yet if you enhancing it with purer ingredients will diminish some of the migraines. Another point about this potion could perhaps be it’s effects when dealing with memory loss, it might make the person\nhave an easier time remembering, mind invasion from mental magic, becoming fully in control of your own mind placing the mage outside of control, and while being interrogated or lying, you will appear far more truthful in your responses.\n- Minor:\nBase: Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Balance, Clarity)\n1 Symbol of Fire (Power)\n2 Symbols of Earth (Endurance)\n1 Symbol of Air (Perception)\n- Lesser:\nBase: Distilled Water\n3 Symbols of Water (Balance, Clarity)\n2 Symbols of Fire (Power)\n3 Symbols of Earth (Endurance)\n2 Symbols of Air (Perception)\n- Greater:\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n5 Symbols of Water (Balance, Clarity)\n3 Symbols of Fire (Power)\n3 Symbols of Earth (Endurance)\n3 Symbols of Air (Perception)\nPlease refer to Part II for the rest of the potions. Thank you.\n-Sarrion\n\n===================To be Continued...", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy: Symbols", "Sarrion", "Alchemy Basic's\nSub Volume I\nSymbols\n\nBy: An unknown alchemist of the alchemist guild.\n\nRe-written by:\nSarrion di' Pascali\nDuring my times as a student, I was very skeptical of most of the theory of alchemy. One of the things I could not understand was the need for Symbols. If the representation and properties of a reagent are what is used,\nthe elements they fit in are not necessary to be stated. After a few years of becoming an alchemist I finally realised the purpose, it is because not only do ingredients have perfect representations, but the sibling representations are as well\nnecessary to create proper results. Perfect representations would never be able to be properly used and leveled, and no reagent has only one representation. For such, attaching a symbol to an ingredient\nfits far better than attaching only the representations. By choosing the representation or symbol you can decide the properties of what you create. One could use the representation of life for healing potions, but depending if it’s an\nearth symbol or a water symbol, it will have other smaller scale representations that will distinguish them. A water symbol will provide a more smooth and fluent healing rate, making the wound heal nicely, and the earth symbol will\ngive more strength and resilience to the healing process, perhaps making it hard to get the wound reopen. Everything fits into at least one of the four symbols or elements of alchemy, Fire, Water, Earth and Air.\nThe way you look at what a symbol represents is looking at the element in question and assessing what properties it has and what it is associated with. You do not look exactly at what the element is, assessing a symbol to a reagent is\nmore about symbolism than pure correct connection. It’s to aid the alchemist design and investigate the ways of alchemy in a more practical way, without having to reach so fully into the details. Each ingredient or reagent may\nalso be of different strengths depending on the properties and rarity it holds. Those which are rarer have a greater value than those which are common, and as such they are have as well more strength of use in alchemy.\nAn ingredient may be a Weak, Moderate or Strong symbol, those of greater strength required quite more skilled hands, but the payoff might be quite better.\n=[Fire]=\n->Starting with the more easily explainable one, fire is the symbol very used by alchemists that focus themselves on improving skills of fighting and giving new arsenal to use in wars. While I don’t find myself using many fire symbols,\nthey are an absolute in the making of many of the truly fantastic deeds of alchemy. Most of the representations of fire are quite easy to grasp, because they fit perfectly onto what fire truly is. It may represent heat, burning, consumption,\ndestruction, warmth, power and chaos. Most of these have as such a great use for damaging others or to give power to oneself or others. Alchemist fire for example, is a great demonstration of what could be done with the use of fire symbols,\nfire in a bottle. Devastating and powerful, it is most likely the most dangerous conception that an alchemist can create. The representation of chaos is one more confusing, one that may bring unknown results as controlling chaos is quite\nhard job to have. Fire does have another way you may look at it, as many poets might say, “the flames of passion ran deep in his heart, but he acted as in a burning rage.” Fire may also represent emotions, both those\nof anger, regret, rage, confusion, and those of love, passion, confidence. These representation are especially useful in potions to improve oneself, and in poisons to bring damage emotionally to others. The mythical love potion though, is one that is\nby experience impossible to have in full effect, as love is in it’s own way subjective, and varies from person to person. The closest thing that may be created is one that gives well being and peace of mind, or ecstasy.\nMost of those are considered drugs.\nAs for the properties one may find generally in fire symbols, the idea of heat is normally present in them. A flower or plant that is warm to the touch could be a good indicator of a fire symbol.\nThe effects it might bring to a person might be associated that way as well, such as becoming feverish, or feeling a burning itchy sensation on touch. And of course the flavour of many of them, which I don’t really advise\nto be a way to figure out what kind of symbol it is, is most of the times spicy and strong, sometimes sweet as it goes well with raising emotions.\n=[Water]=\n->Sometimes even said to be the base ingredients, a symbol of water is essential to all potions and oils that alchemy can create. This is of course due to it’s liquid and coherent state, or it would not be a potion or oil. The base is the main\ncomponent of a potion, where all other reagents are added and mixed in. It is important to refer that it is considered a base only to the creation of potions and oils, but in the other more exotic fields of alchemy, they are not used as such.\nNormal water is the most simple of bases to use, not very useful for any powerful potion, as it’s not all that pure, it’s used mainly in minor potions. Distilling it would purify it and make it far more useful in lesser potions.\nThe purest form for a base you can find, is aqua vitae. Aqua vitae can also be called Alcohol, or distilled alcohol, it is simply the result of distilling brews such as ale, wine or any other intoxicating beverages.\nWith it, the most powerful of potions can be created. The other base one could use is lard, which is used only in the creation of oils.\nNow onto the representations that define a symbol of water. Like when you imagine\na stream of water, you imagine calmness, fluidity, peace, order and balance of nature. Continuing with the balance of nature, you have to understand that water is one of the fundamentals of life, and as such, water represents many parts\nof it. Life, regrowth, rebirth are the most important of representations, making water symbols sometimes the most important in healing potions, and antidotes. Tasting a water symbol normally brings the other representations that water might have,\nfreshness and a minty flavour are normally what you get from safe to eat water symbols, even going so far sometimes descending into cold and ice, another two representations of water. Do not think that just because water symbols\nmay represents life and are used in a lot of healing potions that they’re safe to eat, even water symbols might be essential to the creation of poisons, as a stream may be a thought of life and balance,\nbut a strong river might be the location of one’s death.\n=[Earth]=\n->While the water symbol is considered the base for potion making, I consider earth symbols the bases for other more advanced sections of alchemy, such as Transmutation and the creation of Chimeras. Such is because while potions need\nto be fluid and in a liquid state, transmutation is performed mostly on objects, and the creation of chimeras requires great representations of life and connectivity if one is ever to be created. More of the advanced alchemy will be left for another book,\nbut I wanted to leave the idea that the selection of a base is not randomly selected but adapts itself to what the alchemist wishes to create. The earth symbols concentrate themselves more on solids and life.\nTo better understand the symbol, one must think of the two greatest visualisations one thinks about when the idea of earth comes to mind. Those two visualisations are the rock, and dirt. Such have the representations that will fit with all of the symbols\nof earth. A rock is resilient, hard to break and strong. It’s used a lot in buildings creating structure and protection, and all these characteristics are representations of the symbol. A rock may also be associated with minerals and metals, two\nrepresentations very much sought out in transmutation. Once one thinks of dirt on the other hand, he does not receive the same thoughts as when with a stone. Dirt is different, dirt is used mostly for the growth of plants, the propagation of life.\nThis is the second part of the symbol of Earth, one that might not be the most easily noticeable. It represents life, regrowth, rebirth and connection. Plants grow in it, and animals life over it, feeding of the plants, and so fauna and flora are\nas well the last representations of earth, making them the most suitable for the creation of chimeras.\nI do not advise trying to eat any type of Earth symbol. While it may represent life as well, it leans more for survival of life, than saving of it.\nThis means that normally earth symbols are not suitable for eating, either having extremely bitter tastes, or being straight up poisonous.\n=[Air]=\n->The symbol of air is perhaps the hardest to explain in all of the symbols. When one tries to imagine air, he may think of the wind, or of what he breaths, perhaps of smoke. What could one bring from those? These are quite simply almost\nimpossible to see, you can not see air, you can not see wind, you feel the wind and hear it’s sound, and you breath the air. One of the first representations to speak of would be of perception, without air you would not be able to see\nbut it comes from that fact that you do not see air, yet know it’s there, and percy the effects of it. The rest of the representations are around the idea of speed and quickness. Perhaps a thought we all have when we imagine speed,\nwe can think of the movements in the air, the fast animals traveling through the air and ground almost provoking a wind in itself. Not the best way to explain it, as those images are quite hard to have. Of the most easy representations to think about,\nyou may think of fight and travel, and for such you only need to think of a bird. The palate one gets on these symbols are normally quite bland. Having almost no taste, no aroma, almost like the normal air in the mountains.\nA last mention on air symbols, is always it’s representations of fragility and grace. The ingredients of air are ones that in most cases are very thin and weak, easily broken and destroyed maybe simply by the moving of the hand near them.\nGrace is a representation I adore to use in potions of healing, and oils of well being, because they bring the condition of the skin to a more natural and graceful way. Yet I consider them hardest symbols to use,\nas the harvesting of the ingredients, the handling and the storage has to be extremely precise.\n===================End.\nLook for:\nAlchemy Volumes I, II, III.\nRe-Written by:\nSarrion di' Pascali", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy: Vol I", "Sarrion", "Volume I\nAlchemy Basics\n\nRe-Written by\nSarrion di' Pascali\n\nWritten by:\nAn unknown Alchemist from the alchemist guild\nPrelude\nFor many years I have been an alchemist, not one of great name, not one of greater skill, I am one who focused on the everyday works of what alchemy may do. Even before reaching the rank of Mentor alchemist in the former Alchemy Guild in the lands\nof the Fringe, I already was teaching a student. Before my teacher disappeared for a few years, he promoted me to that rank, allowing me to fully teach anyone I wished, and make them alchemists when the time came to it.\nI have had many students throughout the years, even being as young an Alchemist as I am, and believe I am capable of doing so. This book series is a combination of all I have learnt in alchemy, containing information from\nold alchemists, such as Tippen and the Traveling Alchemist, to the newest masters. Alchemy is performed by all races, in the most diverse areas of expertise and the most diverse of people.\nWhat one can do with alchemy is only stopped by the reach of his imagination.\nChapter I\nAlchemy\nThe first question I ask all my students is for me to gather the reasons why they wish to study under me. What is alchemy? To my disbelief, most of those that come to learn from me, do not know that answer, and have clear misconceptions about the topic.\nThe answer I most receive is a simple “It’s the making of potions.” Many men and women want simply to stand in front of a brewing stand or a cauldron and throw reagents inside it to then receive a potion that would grant them immortality!\nAlchemy is, of course, not potion making, which results in many surprised students, and many give up because I do not even speak of potion making until just before they become novice alchemists. Alchemy is much more than that, far more than potion making,\nas potions are only a way in which to receive the results of alchemy. The best way to describe alchemy is as such, the study and practice of the natural principle of Equivalent Exchange.\nChapter II\nEquivalent Exchange\nI have been asked a few times, as have many alchemists before me, if Alchemy is magical in it’s essence. While many of the desires and goals of alchemy might appear supernatural, the process itself, and the way of achieving it, are far from it.\nThe principle of Equivalent exchange is at the core, the law that states that to get anything, something of equal value must be offered in return. The value I refer to here is not a monetary one, as some might be compelled to think.\nIf so, all alchemists would be throwing diamonds into a pot over and over again to receive what they would want. That does not happen of course, because the value used in equivalent exchange is associated with the properties,\ncharacteristics and representations of an ingredient or reagent. The alchemist’s job is not to mix up the ingredients like a soup, but knowing which ingredients to use, how to prepare them, how much to use, when to add them, and keeping everything safe.\nThis is what sorts the Alchemists from the chefs. The recipes that alchemists have are not ones simply like cooking, which state that you need 3 eggs, 2 cups of sugar, a bucket of milk, and then mix everything up,\nplace in a hot oven for a known amount of time. Alchemy recipes do not speak of exact quantities or times, for there are many ways to have the same value.\nThe recipe does instead tell the reader what representations he needs, normally in terms of what are called Symbols.\nChapter III\nSymbols\nDuring my times as a student, I was very skeptical of most of the theory of alchemy. One of the things I could not understand was the need for Symbols. If the representation and properties of a reagent are what is used, the elements they fit in\nare not necessary to be stated. After a few years of becoming an alchemist I finally realised the purpose, it is because not only do ingredients have perfect representations, but the sibling representations are as well necessary to create proper results.\nPerfect representations would never be able to be properly used and leveled, and no reagent has only one representation. For such, attaching a symbol to an ingredient fits far better than attaching only the representations.\nBy choosing the representation or symbol you can decide the properties of what you create. One could use the representation of life for healing potions, but depending if it’s an earth symbol or a water symbol, it will have other smaller scale\nrepresentations that will distinguish them. A water symbol will provide a more smooth and fluent healing rate, making the wound heal nicely, and the earth symbol will give more strength and resilience to the healing process,\nperhaps making it hard to get the wound reopen. Everything fits into at least one of the four symbols or elements of alchemy, Fire, Water, Earth and Air.\nThe way you look at what a symbol represents is looking at the element in question and assessing what properties it has and what it is associated with. You do not look exactly at what the element is, assessing a symbol to a reagent\nis more about symbolism than pure correct connection. It’s to aid the alchemist design and investigate the ways of alchemy in a more practical way, without having to reach so fully into the details.\nEach ingredient or reagent may also be of different strengths depending on the properties and rarity it holds. Those which are rarer have a greater value than those which are common, and as such they are have as\nwell more strength of use in alchemy. An ingredient may be a Weak, Moderate or Strong symbol, those of greater strength required quite more skilled hands, but the payoff might be quite better.\nChapter IV\nPreparation\nMany alchemists students adore reaching this stage of training, and they soon regret it. Preparation is the handling of utensils and reagents, their storage, their upkeep, cleaning and maintenance. Harvesting of ingredients would also be considered\npart of the preparation of an alchemist. It involves everything required in the work of the alchemist just before it’s creation. Preparation is their job, anyone can add reagents together and hope for the best, but they do\nnot know what utensils use, how to prepare the ingredients, how much to mix, what part to use of the reagents, how hot the station should be, what safety precautions need to be addressed, and so much more.\nIt is the physical part of alchemy, where the alchemist has to act with the knowledge he has gained in his training.\nThe most basic of preparation is the cleaning. Everything, and I can’t stress that enough, everything has to always be clean.\nIt doesn’t matter if it’s the cauldron a potion is being brewed in or the mask one uses, every must be spotless. Four essentials goods for cleaning: towels, scrub, soap and water. Essential technique: scrubbing until your arms are dead tired and then\nscrubbing some more. Any dirt, or leftovers of another potion, or bits of hair or skin, will act on the scale of equivalent exchange, and of course, you do not want that. It may result in the ruin of the alchemy procedure\nor in dangerous reactions, especially when leftover potions and reagents are not removed properly.\nNow that the knowledge of clean is placed into the head of a new student, he must know what to use. Simple things exist in the bag of all alchemists for safety reasons. A pair of gloves, they may be thick or simply just impermeable,\nthe best would be both, yet some alchemists trade thick gloves for ones they can easily move their fingers with. Gloves have to protect from thorns, cold, hotness, fire, cuts, spores, liquids, and perhaps even smokes.\nThe hands are the fundamental tools of the alchemist, and all of them are going to cut their own hand at least once in their training. A mask is the second most important safety accessory to have on one’s bag. There would be the simple cloth masks\nthat protect from spores and dusts, and then there are the most advanced and complicated masks that are able to protect from smokes and air. The second types are normally rare, the old Teutonic TAC masks being the best ones to find in the realms.\nI really advise the use of goggles when doing alchemy as well, as I have almost lost an eye in my training years due to lack of them, hot water may jump into the face, or bits of ingredients might be cut wrongly and fly into the eye.\nOthers not so important safety accessories include hair and beard nets, for them not to burn in the fires, and lab coats, for protecting the skin if one is working with acids and perhaps alchemy fire.\nIn the alchemist’s bag,\nthere should be many tools as well. The most normal is the knife, important for gathering reagents, and for preparing them. Of course some alchemists live for perfection, and their bag is filled with a collection of knives, shears,\nthongs, grapples, and many other tools for harvesting. Small vials and containers for bigger reagents are also required. The vials are essential for gathering liquids, but the greater ingredients can’t just be thrown into a bag, they need a container.\nIn the lab many more tools and accessories are required. The mortar and pestle fundamental for grinding reagents, a counter for the preparation of them, knives of various shapes most likely, vials of many sizes and shapes,\na lot of spoons of different sizes, the three most fundamental being the small metal spoon, the thin and long glass spoon, and the large wooden spoon, towels, filters, and the mixing locations, the brewing stand and the cauldron.\nBetween the brewing stand, also called the alembic, and the cauldron the alchemist will find different ways of joining and creating his concoctions. I have found that elves and goblins seem to prefer the use of brewing stands,\nwhile the dwarves and bigger orcs prefer the cauldrons. The humans are as usual mixed in preferences. While the brewing stand requires a more delicate hand and precise movements, the cauldron requires strong hands and able body to stir it the right way.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy: Vol II", "Sarrion", "Volume II\nAlchemy Ingredients\n\nBy: An unknown alchemist of the alchemist's guild.\n\nRe-Written by: Sarrion di' Pascali\nIn the process of equivalent exchanged, as explained in a previous volume, is one that requires things of value to create the alchemical results of the same value. For such concoctions, various ingredients, or better called reagents,\ncan be found and used all throughout the realms. The rarity of some are great, and many of those listed here have even other properties and uses besides the ones that are used in alchemy. The list of reagents is endless,\nas even dirt may be considered an ingredient, even is nothing worthy can be created from it.\n===================\nI have created a list of all the ingredients knowledged to me in with a pronounced alchemy use, in which I explain how to collect it, where to find it, and what symbols it represents. While I do detail mostly the plants and botany\nI have created a list of all the ingredients knowledged to me in with a pronounced alchemy use, in which I explain how to collect it, where to find it, and what symbols it represents. While I do detail mostly the plants and botany\nBesides flora, parts of animals and beasts are also highly used, many times as more powerful or stronger symbols than the plants, yet they are also rarer, and harder to collect. I do not mention the powerful symbols,\nyet many of them are of easy imagination. A feather of a giant halck, a fin of a siren, the heart of a great fire beast, a bone of a troll, are just examples that may be used to then further develop your imagination.\nTo new alchemists I advise the use of Weak reagents, as they are far easier to use, yet almost all times don’t result in great potions. These are not to be ignored though, as even the strongest of potions may require\nWeak reagents, it comes down to their representations, and what the alchemist requires in his concoction. Pay attention to the characteristics of the plants and how they fit with the symbol and representations.\nWhere they grow, if they are poisonous, what nutrients they need, how to harvest them, what part of the reagent to use, and many more details.\n===================\nBotany Glossery:\n\nSarrion's Note:\nPlease see \"Alchemy: Botany\" for the full detail of all regents listed in this Glossery. Thank you,\n-Sarrion di' Pascali\n=[Earth Symbols]=\n->Weak\nGoblin’s Ivy\n->Moderate\nSaffvil\nAlabaster Leaf\nTippen’s Root\nDesert Berry Bush\n->Strong\nStarved Coyote’s Tick\n=[Fire Symbols]=\n->Weak\nDesert Bush Berry\n->Moderate\nFlametongue’s roots\nDwarf’s Pumpkin\nBlood Lotus\nElrow Berries\n->Strong\nCrimson Vase\nDrake’s Tail\n=[Water Symbols]=\n->Weak\nBlissfoil\n->Moderate\nSerpent's Stalk\nMandragora\nZawabate\nFrost Vine\n->Strong\nAthin\n=[Air Symbols]=\n->Weak\nJailer’s moss\n->Moderate\nSwamp’s blossom\n->Strong\nCrouching Feather\nElf’s hair vine\n===================End.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy: Vol III", "Sarrion", "Volume III\nAlchemy Potions\n\nBy: Unknown alchemist from the alchemist's guild\n\nRe-Written By:\nSarrion di' Pascali\nThe truer part of the thoughts of what most people think of alchemists is that they make potions. I have already stated in previous volumes that alchemy is not potion making, but potions are the best way for an alchemist to use\nhis knowledge in an applicable way. There are other methods of course, which shall be talked more about in the advanced alchemy volume, but the main result of an alchemist’s study is infact potions. They are easy to\ncollect, easy to move around, and easy to administer. Normally drank, they can in some rare or specific occasions poured on something. The recipes that alchemists create are not like those of cooks. Equivalent Exchange is their purpose,\nwhich means the order of the ingredients does not matter, and the ingredients used only have to obey the representation needed. More or less ingredients might be used considering the alchemist’s needs, and it may be more and less powerful.\nIn regular terms, a minor potion has small effects and more side effects but of smaller danger. A greater potion has far greater effects, and supposedly less side effects, but those that it has are quite strong as well.\nAn example in the use of potions is also in order, a potion of mending to heal a minor cut on a child’s knee should never be a greater potion of mending.\nNot only is it a waste, but also because the effects are too strong to heal a small wound, like you should never cook a pie in the great blacksmith furnaces of Urguan.\n-------------------\nA potion being in liquid form means that an achemist has to use water symbols as it’s base. Water, Distilled water, Aqua Vitae are the bases used for potions, with Aqua Vitae considered the finest one can use. Lard is used as well, not in potions\nbut in oils, serving to external uses. In the example before, I mention a minor and a greater potion. There are three types of the ‘same’ potion, and those are minor, lesser and greater. They are the same potion in name,\nas their effects are suppose to be the same, only in different powers. Minor potions are the weakest, normally left for the new alchemists and student alchemists to conduct and make. Their effects often times are minimal,\nyet they are far easier to do, but do not think they are useless, as many times an effect should be small to have a good impact. These are made with water as their base. Lesser potions come right after, with distilled water\nas their base, and greater potions are the greatest strength one can have of a potion, using aqua vitae in their base. Of course the recipes for the stronger potions require\nnot only purer reagents, but as more complexed and defined recipes.\n-------------------\nI can not demonstrate all recipes that exist, as each alchemist may do his’ or her’s potions, each has it’s mastery and orientation of alchemy. They have their taste in reagents, but do remember, that a good alchemist\nis one that uses logic and common sense in their potions. When doing a mending potion, an alchemists would never use and earth symbol which would represent death, but it’s necessary representations,\nbe it life or regrowth. The recipes do not come with reagents, but with the required symbols and representations. Different ways of preparing the reagents, and different reagents will leave mindly different results, which exist due\nto impurities and different representations in ingredients. Be careful of how Equivalent Exchange works, or the effects you get might be quite different than those that you are expecting.\n===================End.\nPotion Glossery:\n\nNote from Sarrion di' Pascali: \"Please this will list the name of known potions, for full details please refer to Alchemy: Potions.\n-Sarrion\"\n-------------------\nPotion of Mending\n\"Often times the most used potions of an alchemist’s arsenal.\"\n- Minor:\nBase: Water\n1 Symbol of Water (Life)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Life)\nPotion of Regeneration\n\"A quite potent potion, it is part of the healing potions\"\n\nBase: Blood\nMandragora\nLiver of a Mother\n2 Earth Symbols (Life)\n1 Air Symbol (Grace)\nPotion of Stoneskin\n\n\"A potion that almost seems like a legend come true.\"\nBase: Distilled water\n4 Symbols of Earth (Fortitude)\n2 Symbols of Water (Life)\n3 Symbols of Fire (Power)\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed)\nPotion of Strength\n\n\"capable of enhancing the strength of someone\"\n\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n1 Symbol of Earth (Fortitude, Power, Resilience)\nPotion of Celerity\n\n\" know as potion of agility and potion of speed\"\n\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed)\nPotion of Accuity\n\n\" provides the drinker with heightened senses\"\n\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n2 Symbol of Air (Perception)\nPotion of Wizard’s Wisdom\n\n- Minor:\nBase: Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Balance, Clarity)\n1 Symbol of Fire (Power)\n2 Symbols of Earth (Endurance)\n1 Symbol of Air (Perception)\nPotion of Smoke Whispers\n\n\"a cloud of smoke is formed\"\n\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n4 Air Symbols (Flight, Transport)\n1 Fire Symbol (Combustion)\nPotion of Sleeping\n\n\"objective is placing someone to sleep.\"\n\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Calmness and Relaxation)\n1 Symbols of Air (Speed)\nPotion of Freezing\n\n\"only intent is freezing or cooling something\"\n\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n1 Symbols of Water (Cold)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Resilience)\nWaterbreathing Potion\n\n\" allows someone to breath underwater\"\n Aqua Vitae mixed with a bit of seawater\nMermaid’s Gills and Liver\n1 Symbols of Water (Fluidity)\n1 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Resilience)\nFrost Oil\n\" An oil which has similarities with the potion of freezing\"\n\nBase: Lard\n3 Symbols of Water(Cold, Ice, Frost)\n2 Symbols of Air (Speed)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Fortitude)\nFlame Oil\n\n\"The Oil of Flame\"\n\nBase: Lard\n3 Symbols of Fire (Power, Destruction, Burning)\n2 Symbols of Earth (Endurance)\n1 Symbol of Water (Calmness, Balance)\nFortitude Oil:\n\n“Armor for your Armor”\n\nBase: Lard\n3 Symbols of Earth (Endurance, Fortitude, etc.)\n2 Symbols of Fire (Potency, Power)\nHair Rejuvenating Oil\n\n\" it rejuvenates hair\"\n\n- Minor\nBase: Lard\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed/Grace)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Hardiness)\n1 Symbol of Water (Rejuvenation)\nGlue Oil\n\n\"For your elf ears when they fall off\" -Sarrion\n\nBase: Lard\n1 Symbol of Air (Travel/Speed)\n2 Symbols of Earth (Hardiness, Connection)\nAlchemist’s Fire\n\n\"‘fire in a bottle,’\"\n\nPlease refer to:\nAlchemy: Poitons\n\nfor the recipe and the warning that comes with it.\n===================End.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy:Botany 2", "Sarrion", "Alchemy: Botany II\n-------------------This glossery is based off a tale written by an unknown alchemist of the alchemists guild.\n\nRe-Written by:\nSarrion di' Pascali\n=[Fire Symbols Continued]=\n      Moderate\nName: Flametongue’s roots\n\nRepresentation: Heat, Anger, Destruction\n\nDescription: Flametongue’s roots is a difficult reagent to collect.\nIt’s location of growth already makes the task hard, having to find it extremely sunny locations in forests, either in burnt areas of it, or on hillsides. If you’re not lucky to find a spot which has burnt down, and if you don’t burnt the forest down\nto gather this reagent, then most likely you will have to climb a cliff or hold yourself in one’s edge to gather it. The second great problem with it, is that it’s sharp brambles release spores which with contact with the skin\ncause hypersensitivity to pain. Gloves have to be used when harvesting, and I would suggest a face mask as well. If you know where to look, it is not so hard to notice the reagent, as it has an almost rose like appearance. The roots\nare the part of the plant to use, being bright red colored, which when used on wounds causes coagulation. So to harvest it, one has to sometimes dig into the side of a hillside. Use it only when in a life or death situation,\nas the pain you will fill when using it, will most likely be far worse than waiting for the wound to heal naturally. Such strong traits bring this plant representations of Heat and Anger.\nLocation: Forest’s hillsides and burnt forests.\n-------------------Name: Dwarf’s Pumpkin\n\nRepresentation: Rage, Envy, Bitterness, Power, Strength\n\nDescription: Although it is called Dwarf’s Pumpkin, this plant is an odious\norange-leafed shrub, and one of the most prominent feature of Swamp botany. Quite potent and atrocious smelling, it is easy to find at a distance, when it exists. It has it’s name from the it’s orange color, and the smell quite\nfits with the description of dwarves, or perhaps because of the brew which is made by them with this herb. They grow around the muddy waters and while they are not dangerous to gather, you may get your foot stuck\nand perhaps even fall into the disgusting mud, and unless some boots are used, your shoes will become horrible smelling. The whole plant may be used for the brew made by the dwarves,\nyet only the brightest of orange leaves need to be collected for the alchemic use.\n\nLocation: Swamplands next to muddy waters.\n-------------------\nName: Blood Lotus\n\nRepresentation: Hope, Courage\n\nDescription: This vine of the deserts is one of my personal favorites to use outside of alchemy reactions. Perhaps a weird trait of mine considering\nwhat it’s properties are. The plant is of a rusty color, growing on the fresher entrances of caves in the desert. They fall from the ceiling and become like a red curtain that separates the cave from the hot exterior. These vines are easily harvested,\nand it’s main use outside of alchemy is mostly in culinary and brewing arts. A diet with consumption of Blood Lotus is one quite nutritious. The plant itself has a peculiar taste, one of iron, making the broths and stews created to appear to\nhave been done with blood of an animal. Blood Lotus can also be fermented to create strong alcohols of red color. It’s representation as a fire symbol comes down to the emotions spectral. It is a plant that grows in a hot climate\nand finds the perfect ideal place of freshness and light. As such, it represents hope, but as well courage.\n\nLocation: Entrance of caves in the hot desert lands.\n-------------------\nName: Elrow Berries\n\nRepresentations: Rage, anger, burning\n\nDescription: It isn’t common to find a fire symbol in cold climates, Elrow berries are of the few that exist. Elrow berries\nwas named after an alchemist, probably in mockery, as it is also known to some as the Hellfire fruit. It grows in bushes and has a great red color to it, easy to spot sometimes in the white wastelands of the arctics.\nThe properties which make it a fire symbol are achieved when one is unfortunate enough to eat it. Unless for a single child and her mother with a great taste for spicy food, I have not met a single person which did not feel like their throat was on fire\nafter tasting it. It starts as a spicy feeling in the mouth that spreads through the throat, where a soreness starts coming with it. From there, the whole body starts to heat up, and even in the most cold days, the whole body\nstarts to sweat, and the body starts aching. It lasts for a few minutes, many grabbing hands of snow and placing them in their mouth, others stripping almost down to their loincloths, and a few even faint. I don’t recommend eating\nElrow berries unless perhaps you are dying of cold frost, or teaching an alchemist class and want a laugh. It’s normal uses are in poisons, especially those that work with emotions, and it represents the more\ndestructive side of Fire. It has been added to brews on some occasions as well, perhaps to heat up the body in cold winters.\nLocation: Bushes in cold climates.\n-------------------\nStrong\nName: Crimson Vase\n\nRepresentation: Heat, Warmth, Love, Passion, Compassion\n\nDescription: In my opinion, this flower is the most beautiful that can be found in the forests. As it names suggests\nit has a strong red color, crimson. This is the color that the large petals of the flower have, and the form of which they take is of an elegant vase. It’s beauty is also enhanced by it’s rarity, as finding one in a forest is an extreme delight.\nIt appears at the base of young trees, growing almost clinging to them. When the sun is high up, the plant starts almost glowing, as a beam of light passes through the small leaves and shines on it. Such combination of sunlight and protection\ncan not be found on older trees. The plant splendor does not end here, as my favorite trait is that the flower is warm to the touch, lovingly so. There are not many fire symbols which have representations\nof the ‘good’ side of fire, yet this one seems to have most of them. Warmth, Love, Passion, Compassion, this plant can be used for most emotion changing concoctions. Of course it’s\nvery important to fire based potions as well, such as Alchemist’s fire, but with it poisons of envy and rage, and potions which bring focus, courage, and warmth can as well.\n\nLocation: At the base of young trees in forests.\n-------------------\nName: Drake’s Tail\n\nRepresentations: Heat, Destruction, Chaos\n\nDescription: Of the herbs and plants of which I speak of in this volume, Drake’s Tail is the strongest and probably the rarest symbol of Fire.\nA rare sight in the deserts, almost a legend sometimes, this plant is probably the best you may find without having to slay a beast of mythical stories. It grows in the deserts, but even in them the conditions needed for it to grow\nare quite scarce and hard to find. This plant’s growth is very dependant on the moisture and temperature in the air, which means in the hot desert wastelands you will not find one growing. Only near Oasis, yet not too close does it grow.\nIt needs the moisture that exists in the air because of the Oasis, and the hotness of the desert, so it becomes an area which one might find Drake’s Tail. It seeks shade as well, embarrassing it’s thin and long vines filled with thorns around a rock.\nWith a red dusky color it’s easy to spot, when there is one around. To harvest it one has to remove the whole plant, as both the thorns and the roots are the necessary bits that are used by the alchemists in their concoctions. The harvesting is\nnot only hard, but also dangerous. If one is struck by one of the thorns, he will gain a strong fever and have a high chance of passing out in the middle of a hot desert, to be food to the coyote’s. It’s characteristics\nmake Drake’s Tail one of the best in the fire eccentric representations.\n\nLocation: In deserts close to oasis.\n-------------------\n=[Water Symbols]=\n->Weak\nName: Blissfoil\n\nRepresentation: Calmness\n\nDescription: Blissfoil is a plant which has more applications in healing medicine than in alchemical\nhealing potions. While it has been found to have a weak potency in alchemy, it’s effects are quite used in healing. I do not believe many good doctors exist which have not heard of the use of this plant, for it is one of the best numbing agents out there.\nThe greatest problem with it, is the fact that overuse of it causes permanent numbing to an area, and with the power it holds, it happening by someone who does not know of it’s effects is quite possible. The plant itself looks\nlike a combination of many small blue flowers with a thick and flimsy stalk. It’s harvesting is as easy as collecting a flower, and it is born and grows under birch trees near grassy areas.\nLocation: Under birch trees in grassy areas.\n-------------------          Moderate\nName: Serpent's Stalk\n\nRepresentations: Life, Rebirth, Calmness, Fluity\n\nDescription: This plant is one of the easiest to find in the forest of the realm.\nIf one knows where there are small ponds and perhaps streams of water, they would find the Serpent's Stalks. Long Emerald hued stalks, with stripes and ridges of a lighter green and brown along its length, almost like a serpent.\nSometimes simple mistaken by normal sugar canes by those unknown of this plant, and to collect it is the same as well, cutting it at the bottom. Another attribute it holds similar to a serpent’s it’s the poisonous nature it has. Specific insects\nthat come in contact with it are normally found dead all around them, yet from all it’s use, no other creatures seem to die from it. It is actually used many times as a healing agent, specifically to heal and treat burn wounds. A normal\noinkment from simply crushing the plant and mixing it with some water may smooth the pain and keep the wound safe. It is as such a good water symbol that can be used for antidotes, oils, balms, healing potions and potions of calmness,\nas well as fire extinguishing potions. Those are good to have when preparing alchemist fire.\nLocation: Grows near small bodies of water in forests.\n===================To be Continued...\nSeek:\nAlchemy: Botany III", ""),
        StaticBook("AlchemyGuide 1-1", "Daniel", "\\_+*+_/\n   Alchemy Guide\n\n\n\nVolume 1 – The Basics\nPart 1/2\n\n\n\n\n-By Daniel Nodal\nPrelude\nFor many years I have been an alchemist, not one of great name, not one of greater skill, I am one who focused on the everyday works of what alchemy may do. Even before reaching the rank of Mentor alchemist in the former Alchemy Guild in the\nlands of the Fringe, I already was teaching a student. Before my teacher disappeared for a few years, he promoted me to that rank, allowing me to fully teach anyone I wished, and make them alchemists with the time came to it. I have had many students\nthroughout the years, even being as young as I am, and believe I am capable of doing so. This book series is a combination of all I have learnt in alchemy, containing information from old alchemists, such as Tippen and the Traveling Alchemist, to the\nnewest masters. Alchemy is performed by all races, in the most diverse areas of expertise and the most diverse of people. What one can do with alchemy is only stopped by the reach of his imagination.\nAlchemy\nThe first question I ask all my students is for me to gather the reasons why they wish to study under me. What is alchemy? To my disbelief, most of those that come to learn from me, do not know that answer, or have clear misconceptions about\nthe topic. The answer I most receive is a simple “It’s the making of potions.” Many men and women want to simply to stand in front of a brewing stand or a cauldron and throw reagents inside it to then receive a potion that would grant them immortality!\nAlchemy is, of course, not potion making, which results in many students surprised, and many give up because I do not even speak of potion making until just before they become novice alchemists. Alchemy is much more than that, far more than potion making,\nas potions are only a way in which to receive the results of alchemy. The best way to describe alchemy is as such, the study and practice of the natural principle of Equivalent Exchange.\nEquivalent Exchange\nI have been asked a few times, as have many alchemists before me, if Alchemy is magical in it’s essence. While many of the desires and goals of alchemy might appear supernatural, the process itself, and the way of achieving it, are\nfar from it. The principle of Equivalent exchange is at the core, the law that states that to get anything, something of equal value must be offered in return. The value I refer to here is not a monetary one, as some might be compelled to think. If so,\nall alchemists would be throwing diamonds into a pot over and over again to receive what they would want. That does not happen of course, because the value used in equivalent exchange is associated with the properties, characteristics and representations\nof an ingredient or reagent. The alchemist’s job is not to mix up the ingredients like a soup, but knowing which ingredients to use, how to prepare them, how much to use, when to add them, and keeping everything safe. This is what sorts the Alchemists\nfrom the chefs. The recipes that alchemists have are not ones simply like cooking, which state that you need 3 eggs, 2 cups of sugar, a bucket of milk, and then mix everything up, place in a hot oven for a known amount of time. Alchemy recipes do not\nspeak of exact quantities or times, for there are many ways to have the same value. The recipe does instead tell the reader what representations he needs, normally in terms of what are called Symbols.\nSymbols\nDuring my times as a student, I was very skeptical of most of the theory of alchemy. One of the things I could not understand was the need for Symbols. If the representation and properties of a reagent are what is used, the elements\nthey fit in are not necessary to be stated. After a few years of becoming an alchemist I finally realized the purpose, it is because not only do ingredients have perfect representations, but the sibling representations are as well necessary to\ncreate proper results. Perfect representations would never be able to be properly used and leveled, and no reagent has only one representation. For such, attaching a symbol to an ingredient fits far better than attaching only the representations.\nBy choosing the representation or symbol you can decide the properties of what you create. One could use the representation of life for healing potions, but depending if it’s an earth symbol or a water symbol, it will have other smaller scale\nrepresentations that will distinguish them. A water symbol will provide a more smooth and fluent healing rate, making the wound heal nicely, and the earth symbol will give more strength and resilience to the healing process, perhaps making it hard to get\nthe wound reopen. Everything fits into at least one of the four symbols or elements of alchemy, Fire, Water, Earth and Air.\n\nThe way you look at what a symbol represents is looking at the element in question and assessing what properties it has\nand what it is associated with. You do not look exactly at what the element is, assessing a symbol to a reagent is more about symbolism than pure correct connection. It’s to aid the alchemist design and investigate the ways of alchemy in a more practical\nway, without having to reach so fully into the details. Each ingredient or reagent may also be of different strengths depending on the properties and rarity it holds. Those which are rarer have a greater value than those which are common, and as such\nthey are have as well more strength of use in alchemy. An ingredient may be a Weak, Moderate or Strong symbol, those of greater strength required quite more skilled hands, but the payoff might be quite better.\nFire\nStarting with the more easily explainable one, fire is the symbol very used by alchemists that focus themselves on improving skills of fighting and giving new arsenal to use in wars. While I don’t find myself using many of fire symbols,\nthey are an absolute in the making of many of the truly fantastic deeds of alchemy. Most of the representations of fire are quite easy to grasp, because they fit perfectly onto what fire truly is. It may represent heat, burning, consumption, destruction,\nwarmth, power and chaos. Most of these have as such a great use for damaging others or to give power to oneself or others. Alchemist fire for example, is a great demonstration of what could be done with the use of fire symbols, fire in a bottle.\nDevastating and powerful, it is most likely the most dangerous conception that an alchemist can create. The representation of chaos is one more confusing, one that may bring unknown results as controlling chaos is quite hard job to have. Fire\ndoes have another way you may look at it, as many poets might say, “the flames of passion ran deep in his heart, but he acted as in a burning rage.” Fire may also represent emotions, both those of anger, regret, rage, confusion, and those of love,\npassion, confidence. These representation are especially useful in potions to improve oneself, and in poisons to bring damage emotionally to others. The mythical love potion though, is one that is by experience impossible to have in full effect, as love\nis in it’s own way subjective, and varies from person to person. The closest thing that may be created is one that gives well being and peace of mind, or ecstasy. Most of those are considered drugs.\nAs for the properties one may find generally in fire symbols, the idea of heat is normally present in them. A flower or plant that is warm to the touch could be a good indicator of a fire symbol. The effects it might bring to a person might be associated\nthat way as well, such as becoming feverish, or feeling a burning itchy sensation on touch. And of course the flavour of many of them, which I don’t really advise to be a way to figure out what kind of symbol it is, is most of the times spicy and strong,\nsometimes sweet as it goes well with raising emotions.\nWater\nSometimes even said to be the base ingredients, a symbol of water is essential to all potions and oils that alchemy can create. This is of course due to it’s liquid and coherent state, or it would not be a potion or oil. The base is the main\ncomponent of a potion, where all other reagents are added and mixed in. It is important to refer that it is considered a base only to the creation of potions and oils, but in the other more exotic fields of alchemy, they are not used as such. Normal\nwater is the most simple of bases to use, not very useful for any powerful potion, as it’s not all that pure, it’s used mainly in minor potions. Distilling it would purify it and make it far more useful in lesser potions. The purest form for a base you\ncan find is aqua vitae. Aqua vitae can also be called Alcohol, or distilled alcohol, it is simply the result of distilling brews such as ale, wine or any other intoxicating beverage. With it, the most powerful of potions can be created. The other base\none could use is lard, which is used only in the creation of oils.\n\nNow onto the representations that define a symbol of water. Like when you imagine a stream of water, you imagine calmness, fluidity, peace, order and balance of nature.\nContinuing with the balance of nature, you have to understand that water is one of the fundamentals of life, and as such, water represents many parts of it. Life, regrowth, rebirth are the most important of representations, making water symbols sometimes\nthe most important in healing potions, and antidotes. Tasting a water symbol normally brings the other representations that water might have, freshness and a minty flavour are normally what you get from safe to eat water symbols, even going so far as\ndescending into cold and ice, another two representations of water. Do not think that just because water symbols may represents life and are used in a lot of healing potions that they’re safe to eat, even water symbols might be essential to the creation\nof poisons, as a stream may be a thought of life and balance, but a strong river might be the location of one’s death.\nContinues in part 2\n\nWritten by Daniel Nodal\nThe First Seed, 1473", ""),
        StaticBook("AlchemyGuide 1-2", "Daniel", "\\_+*+_/\n   Alchemy Guide\n\n\n\nVolume 1 – The Basics\nPart 2/2\n\n\n\n\n-By Daniel Nodal\nEarth\nWhile the water symbol is considered the base for potion making, I consider earth symbols the bases for other more advanced sections of alchemy, such as Transmutation and the creation of Chimeras. Such is because while potions need to be\nfluid and in a liquid state, transmutation is performed mostly on objects, and the creation of chimeras requires great representations of life and connectivity if one is ever to be created. More of the advanced alchemy will be left for another volume, but\nI wanted to leave the idea that the selection of a base is not randomly selected but adapts itself to what the alchemist wishes to create. The earth symbols concentrate themselves more on solids and life.\nTo better understand the symbol, one must think of the two greatest visualisations one thinks about when the idea of earth comes to mind. Those two visualisations are the rock, and dirt. Such have the representations that will fit with all of the symbols\nof earth. A rock is resilient, hard to break and strong. It’s used a lot in buildings creating structure and protection, and all these characteristics are representations of the symbol. A rock may also be associated with minerals and metals, two\nrepresentations very much sought out in transmutation. Once one thinks of dirt on the other hand, he does not receive the same thoughts as when with a stone. Dirt is different, dirt is used mostly for the growth of plants, the propagation of life. This is\nthe second part of the symbol of Earth, one that might not be the most easily noticeable. It represents life, regrowth, rebirth and connection. Plants grow in it, and animals life over it, feeding of the plants, and so, fauna and flora are as well the\nlast representations of earth, making them the most suitable for the creation of chimeras.\nI do not advise trying to eat any type of Earth symbol. While it may represent life as well, it leans more for survival of life, than saving of it. This means that\nnormally earth symbols are not suitable for eating, either having extremely bitter tastes, or being straight up poisonous.\nAir\nThe symbol of air is perhaps the hardest to explain in all of the symbols. When one tries to imagine air, he may think of the wind, or of what he breaths, perhaps of smoke. What could one bring from those? These are quite simply almost\nimpossible to see, you cannot see air, you cannot see wind, you feel the wind and hear it’s sound, and you breath the air. One of the first representations to speak of would be of perception, without air you would not be able to see, but it comes from\nthat fact that you do not see air, yet know it’s there, and percy the effects of it. The rest of the representations are around the idea of speed and quickness. Perhaps a thought we all have when we imagine speed, we can think of the movements in the air,\nthe fast animals traveling through the air and ground almost provoking a wind in itself. Not the best way to explain it, as those images are quite hard to have. Of the most easy representations to think about, you may think of fight and travel, and for\nsuch you only need to think of a bird. The palate one gets on these symbols are normally quite bland. Having almost no taste, no aroma, almost like the normal air in the mountains.    \nA last mention on air symbols, is always it’s representations of\nfragility and grace. The ingredients of air are ones that in most cases are very thin and weak, easily broken and destroyed maybe simply by the moving of the hand near them. Grace is a representation I adore to use in potions of healing, and oils of well\nbeing, because they bring the condition of the skin to a more natural and graceful way. Yet I consider them hardest symbols to use, as the harvesting of the ingredients, the handling and the storage has to be extremely precise.\nPreparation\nMany alchemists students adore reaching this stage of training, and they soon regret it. Preparation is the handling of utensils and reagents, their storage, their upkeep, cleaning and maintenance. Harvesting of ingredients would also\nbe considered part of the preparation of an alchemist. It involves everything required in the work of the alchemist just before it’s creation. Preparation is their job, anyone can add reagents together and hope for the best, but they do not know what\nutensils use, how to prepare the ingredients, how much to mix, what part to use of the reagents, how hot the station should be, what safety precautions need to be addressed, and so much more. It is the physical part of alchemy, where the alchemist has to\nact with the knowledge he has gained in his training.\nThe most basic of preparation is the cleaning. Everything, and I can’t stress that enough, everything has to always be clean. It doesn’t matter if it’s the cauldron a potion is being brewed in or the\nmask one uses, every must be spotless. Four essentials goods for cleaning: towels, scrub, soap and water. Essential technique: scrubbing until your arms are dead tired and then scrubbing some more. Any dirt, or leftovers of another potion, or bits of hair\nor skin, will act on the scale of equivalent exchange, and of course, you do not want that. It may result in the ruin of the alchemy procedure or in dangerous reactions, especially when leftover potions and reagents are not removed properly.\nNow that the knowledge of clean is placed into the head of a new student, he must know what to use. Simple things exist in the bag of all alchemists for safety reasons. A pair of gloves, they may be thick or simply just impermeable, the best would be\nboth, yet some alchemists trade thick gloves for ones they can easily move their fingers with. Gloves have to protect from thorns, cold, hotness, fire, cuts, spores, liquids, and perhaps even smokes. The hands are the fundamental tools of the alchemist,\nand all of them are going to cut their own hand at least once in their training. A mask is the second most important safety accessory to have on one’s bag. There would be the simple cloth masks that protect from spores and dusts, and then there are the\nmost advanced and complicated masks that are able to protect from smokes and air. The second types are normally rare, the old Teutonic TAC masks being the best ones to find in the realms. I really advise the use of goggles when doing alchemy as well, as I\nhave almost lost an eye in my training years due to lack of them, hot water may jump into the face, or bits of ingredients might be cut wrongly and fly into the eye. Others not so important safety accessories include hair and beard nets, for them not to\nburn in the fires, and lab coats, for protecting the skin if one is working with acids and perhaps alchemy fire.\n\nIn the alchemist’s bag, there should be many tools as well. The most normal is the knife, important for gathering reagents,\nand for preparing them. Of course some alchemists live for perfection, and their bag is filled with a collection of knives, shears, thongs, grapples, and many other tools for harvesting. Small vials and containers for bigger reagents are also required.\nThe vials are essential for gathering liquids, but the greater ingredients can’t just be thrown into a bag, they need a container.\n\nIn the lab many more tools and accessories are required. The mortar and pestle fundamental for grinding reagents, a\ncounter for the preparation of them, knives of various shapes most likely, vials of many sizes and shapes, a lot of spoons of different sizes, the three most fundamental being the small metal spoon, the thin and long glass spoon, and the large wooden\nspoon, towels, filters, and the mixing locations, the brewing stand and the cauldron.\n\nBetween the brewing stand, also called the alembic, and the cauldron the alchemist will find different ways of joining and creating his concoctions.\nI have found that elves and goblins seem to prefer the use of brewing stands, while the dwarves and bigger orcs prefer the cauldrons. The humans are as usual mixed in preferences. While the brewing stand requires a more delicate hand and precise\nmovements, the cauldron requires strong hands and able body to stir it the right way.\n\nEven with all the preparations done, an alchemist can do nothing without the knowledge on how to use the reagents and how to prepare them.\nFor potion making, the cleaning and removal of useless parts of the ingredients comes before anything else, or one risks ruining what they are creating while working on the second or so reagent  to add. Of course before so, they need to know what they are\nmixing, be it by reading a recipe, or creating one themselves. For that, they need to know what ingredients exist in our realm, how they behave and what they create. Such can be found in the second volume, which will focus fully on the location,\nrepresentations, appearance and uses of all the reagents I have knowledge of. It is quite the list.\n\n- Written by Daniel Nodal\n\nThe First Seed, 1473", ""),
        StaticBook("AlchemyGuide 2-1", "Daniel", "\\_+*+_/\n   Alchemy Guide\n\n\n\nVolume 2 – Reagents\nPart 1/4\n\n\n\n\n-By Daniel Nodal\nIn the process of equivalent exchanged, as explained in a previous volume, is one that requires things of value to create the alchemical results of the same value. For such concoctions, various ingredients, or better called reagents, can be found and used\nall throughout the realms. The rarity of some are great, and many of those listed here have even other properties and uses besides the ones that are used in alchemy. The list of reagents is endless, as even dirt may be considered an ingredient, even if\nnothing worthy can be created from it.\n\nI have created a list of all the ingredients knowledged to me in with a pronounced alchemy use, in which I explain how to collect it, where to find it, and what symbols it represents. While I do detail mostly the\nplants and botany with use in alchemy concoctions, a good alchemist must also learn from examples and from the theory itself how to find new ingredients, and how to access what type of ingredient one holds in their hand. Besides flora, parts of animals\nand beasts are also highly used, many times as more powerful or stronger symbols than the plants, yet they are also rarer, and harder to collect. I do not mention the powerful symbols, yet many of them are of easy imagination. A feather of a giant bird,\na fin of a siren, the heart of a great fire beast, a bone of a troll, are just examples that may be used to then further develop your imagination.\n\nTo new alchemists I advise the use of Weak reagents, as they are far easier to use,\nyet almost all times don’t result in great potions. These are not to be ignored though, as even the strongest of potions may require Weak reagents, it comes down to their representations, and what the alchemist requires in his concoction. Pay attention\nto the characteristics of the plants and how they fit with the symbol and representations. Where they grow, if they are poisonous, what nutrients they need, how to harvest them, what part of the reagent to use, and many more details.\nEarth Symbols\nWeak\n\nName: Goblin’s Ivy\nRepresentation: Resilience, Poison, Life\nDescription: One of the most easily found flora of the deserts, this plant is easily identified as a brownish green vine with small leaves. It is found mainly\nclinging onto old buildings or ruins of the deserts, and on the dry cliff sides. It is quite a resilient plant, able to survive in extreme hostile conditions, and with a very low  or no amount of water close by. Removing it also becomes a problem, as it\nseems to regrow on the same spot after someone goes to the long labour of removing it all. It is these properties that brings the plant such good uses, it’s representation of resilience makes a welcome addition to any stoneskin potion, even while being\nregarded as a Weak reagent. A few poisons may also be created by use of this reagent, mainly ones weaker, some to create nausea or ill disposition. Easy to find and prepare, it is normally used by those new to alchemy to learn the craft.\n§\nLocation: Clinging on ruins, stones and cliff sides of dry regions.\nModerate\n\nName: Saffvil\nRepresentation: Resilience, Endurance, Death\nDescription: Possibly the most horribly smelling herb in all of swamplands, many alchemists make use of their nose when trying to find it. This green\ngrass is green and grows on the corpses of animals, on dead wood and plants, and sometimes on the bottom of big trees. This plant is one that is extremely hard to remove from anything, as it spreads very quickly and strongly. Normally to remove it, you\nwould have to remove the “host”, the plant or animal that it is growing on. If you do not, it will spread all throughout it. This means that the plant has a great representation of Resilience and Endurance, but this plant, unlike a few other Earth\nsymbols, does not represent Life and Regrowth, but Death. This means this plant is mostly used in the creation of poisons, and one particular myth of an aging potion.\nLocation: On the bodies of dead plants and animals.\nName: Alabaster Leaf\nRepresentations: Immobility, Perseverance\nDescription: This plant is mostly characterized by it’s leaf’s alabaster color. Most often times found in the dryer regions of the forest growing around fallen trees. Quite small\nin size, harvesting it may prove a difficulty to the untrained hands. The best method would perhaps be taking the whole plant, with roots, and then remove the leaves as you may use them. The extract one gets by crushing the leaves is what an alchemist\nshould use. It comes with it’s natural alabaster hue, which serves as paint to many. The extract is mildly poisonous, creating dizziness and nausea to those that consume it. It’s main uses are in antidotes, oils, and of course, poisons.\nLocation: Forest dry regions next to fallen trees.\nName: Tippen’s Root\nRepresentation: Life, Regrowth, Resilience, Strength, Endurance\nDescription: Tippen’s roots is one of the most used reagents in the making of mending\npotions, it is even said, that it is required to be present in all\nhealing potions, or the potion will be of weak quality. It was named after the botanist that had first discovered it around hills and in dense forests. It’s location of growing is oftenthe same of that of Alabaster leaf, besides fallen trees, but as well\nnext to carcases of animals and great bugs. It is quite a pleasant sight when compared with the death around it, as the plant of the herb blooms into purple flowers. What one has to use though, is the roots. They are of a yellow color, with spots\naccentuated a bit more darker. Many carry these roots around, even those with no knowledge of it’s use in alchemy. This is because from the roots one can easily make a remedy which may stop bleeding near instantly. In it’s unprepared its strength isn't\nas great, but it still may save countless lives. The problem with this root is a simple one, it’s smell. The odor that the plant releases when the salve of the roots is spilled is enormous. While using it you may gag and even vomit from thinking that you\nare placing such foul-smelling balm onto an open wound. After such, the smell will not escape you for a few hours. It’s traits in healing bring the herb representations of Life and Regrowth,\nbut it also has great representations of Strength and Endurance.\nLocation: Forest, around dead trees and animals.\nName: Dersert Berry Bush\nRepresentation: Protection, Resilience\nDescription: The Desert Berry Bush's appearance is that of a withered rose bush, long brown/grey stalks with big pointy thorns, yet without any leaves. It doesn't appear to grow\nhigher than four feet, but most of the thorns are longer than an inch. It grows inside cactus forests, as in, where there is great concentration of cactus. Never has one been alone in the desert’s sands without a cactus near it. The bush gives Berries\nof a strong red color every full moon. These don't last long, as animals of the desert appear to enjoy it's taste quite dearly. The berries are extremely sweet, something very strange to find in the desert, so no wonder the animals enjoy it. The stalks\nare not like the berries, if an animal by any chance passed the long thorns to rip and eat the stalk, I believe would fall dead in less than a day. As you cut the stalk you notice that the insides are green, instead of the dead brown. From it it's juice\nflows a lot, yet of course it's poison to drink it. Eating the liquid or even touching it causes rashes and all someone wants to do afterwards is scratch the area, even if it’s the mouth. Too much of it and it kills of course, and it sound be painful.\nThe thorns create the same effect, so without gloves, the hand starts itching and becomes red for about a day. It doesn't seem deadly to descendents and probably kha's, but it does explain the small rodents found dead near them. A thorn is poisonous,\nand annoying, just doesn't kill big animals. The stalk seems to have far more uses in alchemy when compared with it’s berry, especially in oils of protection and potions of stoneskin. It represents protection and resilience, the thorns and it's poison\nnature being the reasons why. To prepare for it I have found it hard, as when cut, the juices drip quite fast. You can't remove the bush from the ground, as it's roots are too big, so they have to be cut in the spot. Feet long pieces of stalk are enough,\nyet one would have to almost tilt the plant down so that the cut doesn't face down. Gloves are essential in gathering it because of the thorns, and after cutting, I advise placing it in a long bottle, with the cut end pointing up. When being prepared,\nthe alchemist should be careful as to lose as little bit of the stalk as he removes the seemingly dead outer layer of the stalk, before using it in his potion.\nLocation: Desert Cactus Forests\nStrong\n\nName: Starved Coyote’s Tick\nRepresentations: Protection, Resilience, Connection\nDescription: The Tick that I speak of is probably the only non flora which I speak of as an Alchemisy ingredient in this\nvolume. Mostly it can be found on coyotes the first ones discovered on the bodies of thin starved coyotes, giving them the name. This does not mean it does not appear in other animals, like desert hares and rhinos. As long as it is an animal that grows\nin hot climates, you may be lucky enough to find one. If the animal has a lot of fur, it may be hard to find the tick, but due to it’s size, just passing a hand through the animal may make one find the tick. It might get as big as a thumb, very fat of\npure brown color. It would seem many times as a lump in the animal’s skin, and trying to remove it is mostly impossible. The Staved Coyote’s Tick, once grabbing onto some meat, will never let go unless it wants to. Fire, Ice, or even swings of a warhammer\nonly damage the skin around it, the tick itself resiting more. It’s collecting is done by cutting the flesh that the tick is grabbing, and only when all the meat is removed from the tick, does it try to find another place to grab to. This is a dangerous\nthing to do, as if an alchemists isn’t careful, even with gloves the tick may grab onto the skin, and never let go. When I say never, I truly mean it, no one can make the tick let go, most likely the finder would have to be removed, or at least part of\nit, that or one would learn to live with the tick, as it doesn’t seem toxic or poisonous to an animal. With characteristics like this, it is no wonder that it is a strong symbol of earth, representing Connection, Protection and Resilience.\nLocation: Bodies of animals of hot Climates\nContinues in part 2\n\nWritten by Daniel Nodal\nThe Grand Harvest, 1480", ""),
        StaticBook("AlchemyGuide 2-3", "Daniel", "\\_+*+_/\n   Alchemy Guide\n\n\n\nVolume 2 – Reagents\nPart 3/4\n\n\n\n\n-By Daniel Nodal\nWater Symbols\nWeak\n\nName: Blissfoil\nRepresentation: Calmness\nDescription: Blissfoil is a plant which has more applications in healing medicine than in alchemical healing potions. While it has been found to have weak potency in\nalchemy, it’s effects are quite used in healing. I do not believe many good doctors exist which have not heard of the use of this plant, for it is one of the best numbing agents out there. The greatest problem with it, is the fact that overuse of it\ncauses permanent numbing to an area, and with the power it holds, it happening by someone who does not know of it’s effects is quite possible. The plant itself looks like a combination of many small blue flowers with a thick and flimsy stalk.\nIt’s harvesting is as easy as collecting a flower, and it is born and grows under birch trees near grassy areas.\nLocation: Under birch trees in grassy areas.\nModerate\n\nName: Serpent's Stalk\nRepresentations: Life, Rebirth, Calmness, Fluity\nDescription: This plant is one of the easiest to find in the forest of the realm. If one knows where there are small ponds and perhaps streams of\nwater, they would find the Serpent's Stalks. Long Emerald hued stalks, with stripes and ridges of a lighter green and brown along its length, almost like a serpent. Sometimes simple mistaken by normal sugar canes by those unknown of this plant, and to\ncollect it is the same as well, cutting it at the bottom. Another attribute it holds similar to a serpent’s it’s the poisonous nature it has. Specific insects that come in contact with it are normally found dead all around them, yet from all it’s use, no\nother creatures seem to die from it. It is actually used many times as a healing agent, specifically to heal and treat burn wounds. A normal oinkment from simply crushing the plant and mixing it with some water may smooth the pain and keep the wound\nsafe. It is as such a good water symbol that can be used for antidotes, oils, balms, healing potions and potions of calmness, as well as fire extinguishing potions. Those are good to have when preparing alchemist fire.\nLocation: Grows near small bodies of water in forests.\nName: Mandragora\nRepresentation: Rejuvenation, Life, Rebirth, Regrowth\nDescription: This is one of the reagents most alchemists use when creating more powerful healing potions. It’s meat rejuvenating traits makes it so that it’s very well\nsought by many alchemists. No good ingredient comes without its dangers thought, and Mandragora is one that can bring a collector to a very humiliating death. It is observed growing into the shallow waters of swamp lands, with thick green leaves flowing\nout of the water. Such leaves are quite delicious as garnish for soups and to make a quite rejuvenating tea. It is highly nutritious as well, filled with nutrients. It is not the leaves that one uses as a reagent thought, but the “meat” of the plant.\nThe part of the plant normally underwater is shaped like a parsnip. It is this “meat” that needs to be collected and prepared to use by the alchemists. Collecting it it’s not as easy as it sounds. This plant creates highly narcotic and paralyzing spores\nwhich are released quite easily when the plant is moved. Inhaling them brings the humiliating death of drowning in a foot high water level, as you simply fall on it and are unable to move any further. As such, one has to known when the spores are fully\nreleased, and only then retrieve them. Normally simply a group of at least two set out to find them, and one pulls the other from death if the spores are still with the plant.\nLocation: Low waters in wetlands.\nName: Zawabate\nRepresentations: Life, Calmness, Rebirth\nDescription: Zawabate is the only reagent I know of water representation in the desert lands. Of course it does not grow in the middle of the sand, it grows in the rare oasis one might\nfind. There is it protected from the strong heat and low humidity, in the fertile grounds around the waters. It is identified by it’s prominent colors of green and yellow, with short curvy petals in a long stalk. For those that live near them, especially\nthe orcish shamans, it is a plant which brings a higher connection with the spirits and out of body experiences. To say more simply, Zawabate is a hallucinogen, creating great comfort and sensations, which are further enhanced if made into a stong tea.\nThese flowers are certainly an amazing addition to potions designed to numb pain or heal because of their home in such a lush landscape among a wasteland of aridity. The amount to use however, should be greatly controlled, due to its hallucinogenic\nproperties. Too much, and the healing potion might cause delusions and mental problems, which means it can also be used for to create those same poison effects if wanted.\nLocation: In the fertile lands of an oasis\nName: Frost Vine\nRepresentation: Life, Calmness, Ice\nDescription: Frost vine is a blue vine which grows in very cold climates. It seems to have a need for shade, the most common of places being around trees, leaving long blue spirals in their\ntrunks and falling from their branches. The plant is a very good numbing agent, one which can easily be made into a sticky clear substance which numbs pain and loosens stiff muscles. Too much of it and it may affect the limbs, making them completely numb\nfor some time. One must always be sure to wash the area after applying the substance. It is by some considered a good alternative to a stronger but also more dangerous rubbing agent, Blissfoil, and with some other good qualities in the mix.\nThe vine is quite cold to the touch, which means it may also be further used to better the effect of numbing and treating wounds and pains. With these traits, it is no wonder that this plant represents life, calmness and cold.\nLocation: Shaded areas in cold climates.\nStrong\n\nName: Athin\nSymbol: Freezing, Ice, Life, Balance\nDescription: Athin is quite a potent Water Symbol that one finds in ice lakes and rivers of fresh water, which are normally frozen. It is a blue algae, sometimes quite hard\n\nto find if the ice is too thick or the snow stops vision to the unfrozen water under the ice. One particular difficult to harvest plant, not due to the how you take it, but because of the danger associated with it. It is taught to all alchemists that it\ntakes two people to harvest Athin. This is because it grows under ice, on very cold water. The ice breaking and someone getting stuck is a high probability, but either way you will have to get into the water to collect it. Sometimes people get stuck\nunder the ice, not knowing where the hole they did was, sometimes they do not take precautions with heating before entering the water and freeze in the cold wind when out. Such dangers do come with reward, as Athin is one of the materials there are that\nare fireproof. It has a great representation of ice and freezing, and an alchemist that carries around alchemist fire, or simply makes it, always have some athin around with them as well.\nLocation: Under the ice of frozen lakes and rivers.\nContinues in part 4\n\nWritten by Daniel Nodal\nThe Grand Harvest, 1480", ""),
        StaticBook("AlchemyGuide 2-4", "Daniel", "\\_+*+_/\n   Alchemy Guide\n\n\n\nVolume 2 – Reagents\nPart 4/4\n\n\n\n\n-By Daniel Nodal\nAir Symbols\nWeak\n\nName: Jailer’s moss\nRepresentations: Travel, Movement\nDescription: Quite an annoying plant in many cases, the Jailer’s Moss seems to stick to everything it touches. It is found the caves near or in swamps,\ngrowing in water streams from the walls, and sometimes even in small currents of water. It has a very light yellow color making it easily noticeable in the dark caves. It’s main property is the stickiness it has, just a touch and it never seems to\nlet go. Of course it doesn’t hold much force, so no one but the small fishes and insects it feeds on get stuck to it, it normally breaks or the whole plant gets dragged with the animal or person. It is from this that the ingredient is considered an air\nsymbol, representing the motion of travelling with the other animals, this way spreading. A weak symbol which is great for new alchemists to use and try out.\nLocation: Caves in swamps\nModerate\n\nName: Swamp’s blossom\nRepresentations: Quickness, speed, Travel\nDescription: This is the flower that would be considered the most beautiful in the awful looking lands of swamp and wetlands. A purplish\ngreen flower that grows through the branches of the trees, with a short and thick stem. One might feel bad for removing the little beauty one might find in the swamplands, which is quite understandable. After collecting this flower, you can remove the\nnectar which has a very peculiar reaction. This nectar is a clear liquid, but one that acts like quicksilver. Extracting a bit of it and pouring it over your hand, and it will dance gracefully until finding a way to the floor between your fingers.\nIt is this nectar that is used in the concoctions of the alchemists, one that represents a clear symbol of air.\nLocation: Growing through the branches of swamp trees\nStrong\n\nlName: Crouching Feather\nRepresentations: Speed, Travel, Gracefulness\nDescription: A graceful and rare sight of the forest and plains. This quite potent reagent can be recognized by it’s\nlong three white petals that sweep in a downwards curve to the point where they touch the ground, appearing like feathers. Like the name it has, they are found “crouching” under large fauna, such as big bushes and shrubs. The harvesting of this peticular\nplant is one that is quite hard. The flower only blooms at night and a strong wind will blow the petals right off. When finding one, the alchemist or botanist must carefully remove the petals from the stalk, and keep them safe from being blown away, and\nfrom being crushed. When finally harvested, this plant is quite a strong symbol of air. The extract of the petals much be collected first, and doing so to a graceful petal is quite hard. It’s use it’s mostly for potions of celerity and when the\nrepresentation of speed is quite desired. Yet gracefulness and travel also represent these long petals.\nLocation: Under big bushes and shrubs of forests and plains.\nName: Elf’s hair vine\nRepresentations: Travel, Gracefulness, Speed, Flight\nDescription: One of the most beautiful plants of which I speak of in this volume, Elf’s Hair vine is a rare sight in the top of cold mountains. Like the elegant hair\nof the nibble elves, the plant has a extreme lightness to it, flowing softly even in the most minute of breezes. The vine is thin and white, seeming to float in the air. Normally protected from the wind, when a stronger gust of air finds it, the small\nblossoms that grow from the vines are broken off, and start flying with the wind, travelling together. They have many pure small white petals which gracefully come together to create the flower. These flowers is what an alchemist uses in his concoctions,\nwhich makes the collection quite difficult. If a simple breeze can take it away, picking it up or moving it around is an very timely task. The alchemist has to be slow and gentle, as not only would harsh movements send the graceful flower flying away, it\nmight also damage the petals of this fragile plant. With a representation of grace of the flower, it’s petals have to be in perfect condition when used, a tear or a part of it damaged, and most of the use is lost. This reagent serves with great use for\nconcoctions centered around speed and grace.\nLocation: Covered from the wind at the top of cold mountains.\nWritten by Daniel Nodal\nThe Grand Harvest, 1480", ""),
        StaticBook("AlchemyGuide 3-1", "Daniel Nodal", "\\_+*+_/\n   Alchemy Guide\n\n\n\nVolume 3 – Alchemy Potions\nPart 1/3\n\n\n\n\n-By Daniel Nodal\nThe truer part of the thoughts of what most people think of alchemists is that they make potions. I have already stated in previous volumes that alchemy is not potion making, but potions are the best way for an alchemist to use his knowledge in an\napplicable way. There are other methods of course, which shall be talked more about in the advanced alchemy volume, but the main result of an alchemist’s study is in fact potions. They are easy to collect, easy to move around, and easy to administer.\nNormally drank, they can in some rare or specific occasions poured on something. The recipes that alchemists create are not like those of cooks. Equivalent Exchange is their purpose, which means the order of the ingredients does not matter,\nand the ingredients used only have to obey the representation needed. More or less ingredients might be used considering the alchemist’s needs, and it may be more and less powerful. In regular terms, a minor potion has weak potion has small effects\nand more side effects but of smaller danger. A greater potion has far greater effects, and supposedly less side effects, but those that it has are quite strong as well. An example in the use of potions is also in order, a potion of mending to heal\na minor cut on a child’s knee should never be a greater potion of mending. Not only is it a waste, but also because the effects are too strong to heal a small wound, and you should never cook a pie in the great blacksmith furnaces of Urguan.\nA potion being in liquid form means that an achemist has to use water symbols as it’s base. Water, Distilled water, Aqua Vitae are the bases used for potions, with Aqua Vitae considered the finest one can use. Lard is used as well, not in potions,\nbut in oils, serving to external uses. In the example before, I mention a minor and a greater potion. There are three types of the ‘same’ potion, and those are minor, lesser and greater. They are the same potion in name, as their effects are supposed to\nbe the same, only in different powers. Minor potions are the weakest, normally left for the new alchemists and student alchemists to conduct and make. Their effects often times are minimal, yet they are far easier to do, but do not think they are\nuseless, as many times an effect should be small to have a good impact. These are made with water as their base. Lesser potions come right after, with distilled water as their base, and greater potions are the greatest strength one can have\nof a potion, using aqua vitae in their base. Of course the recipes for the stronger potions require not only purer reagents, but as more complex and defined recipes.\nI can not demonstrate all recipes that exist, as each alchemist may do his’ or her’s potions, each has it’s mastery and orientation of alchemy. They have their taste in reagents, but do remember, that a good alchemist is one that uses logic and common\nsense in their potions. When doing a mending potion, an alchemists would never use and earth symbol which would represent death, but it’s necessary representations, be it life or regrowth. The recipes do not come with reagents, but with the required\nsymbols and representations. Different ways of preparing the reagents, and different reagents will leave mindly different results, which exist due to impurities and different representations in ingredients. Be careful of how\nEquivalent Exchange works, or the effects you get might be quite different than those that you are expecting.\nPotion of Mending\n\nOften times the most used potions of an alchemist’s arsenal. Mending potions are those to aid the hurt and injured with their effects of repairing flesh and bone, as well as body and mind.\nPotions of Mending are normally administered both internally and externally. Pouring it on bandages to place over wounds is a normal way of using it, as well as drank as well. For illnesses it is just drank, and for minor cuts and bruises just placing it\non the wound is enough. Minor wounds require only minor potions, and no better potion should be used for these kinds of injuries. This is because greater potions, those designed for greater injuries are often time a way to escape death, or save from\ndevastating injuries, and side effects result from extreme fast regeneration or reconstruction of tissue and bone. Paralysis of the area, scarring, chronic pain and small deformations may appear from the greatest of potions, yet their effects can be\nas great as repairing a shattered bone, returning vision to a cut eye, closing wounds in seconds. Even though those things are possible, sometimes even faster than with magic, they do not only require the use of the potions, but as well medical\nexpertise. A potion to fix up a shattered bone requires it to be administered directly into the bone, and that means the flesh must be cut to expose it, which to do safely is quite the task. Of course even though the patient will he healed quite fast,\nhe would be in no condition to do much for a few hours, fast healing is tiring for the body.\nRecipe:\n- Minor:\nBase: Water\n1 Symbol of Water (Life)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Life)\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Water (Life)\n1 Symbol of Earth (Life)\n1 Symbol of Air (Quickness)\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n2 Symbols of Water (Life)\n2 Symbols of Earth (Life)\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed)\nPotion of \n   Regeneration\n\nA quite potent potion, it is part of the healing potions, but has a recipe on it’s own due to it’s complexity. It’s recipe is both dark, and it’s effects slow, but with amazing results.\nThe potion is able to remove scarring, and most of all, regrow missing limbs. Taking months to fully regrow the limb, they would then have to be retrained, and strengthened. It’s the most powerful healing potion an alchemist can do, and to make it one\nmust be quite adept at alchemy making, but as well face a choice which would leave most healers with a sore throat. The base used is not Aqua Vitae or Water, but the blood of the person that requires the potion. This means the potion only might work on\none person. Mandragora is used for it’s rejuvenation representation, and the other main ingredient is the liver of a mother of the same race. Not using the same race woman will result in horrible mutations, and weird growths, and not perfectly made\npotion will as well result in weird growths instead of the required limb. The mix of the ingredients are also quite reactive, which means it will take a skilful alchemists to make it carefully. It becomes a dark colored liquid when complete, and\nthroughout the making, the heat must be correct and constant. The other ingredients are not always the same, as the recipe like other greater healing potions.\nRecipe:\n\nBase: Blood\nMandragora\nLiver of a Mother\n2 Earth Symbols (Life)\n1 Air Symbol (Grace)\nPotion of \n     Stoneskin\n\nA potion that almost seems like a legend come true. This potion is one great in an alchemist’s arsenal. It makes one skin as hard as stone, armor without armor, able to protect itself against blades and arrows quite\nefficiently. Of course like hitting stone, some chipping of the skin might happen, and that will appear as wounds once the effects of the potion wears out. There are two major side effects of this potion. One of them is the fact that drinking it is\nextremely hard. Some that have drank it consider the taste worse than poison, and I do believe, as they are alchemists who I think would try poisons on themselves. After the effects of the potion the result is also one like being sick.\nVomit, extreme nausea are very common effects. The other side effect is what happens if the body can not fully handle the potion. They become like a rock, unable to move, fully paralyzed yet indestructible as well. It is a rare effect,\nI would say happening one in five potions drank, but losing agility is a normal side effect of it. There is only one rank of this potion, anything less and it’s effects won’t be worth, anything more and the body can not take it.\nRecipe:\n\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n4 Symbols of Earth (Fortitude)\n2 Symbols of Water (Life)\n3 Symbols of Fire (Power)\n1 Symbol of Air (Speed)\nPotion of\n     Strength\n\nAnother highly sought after potion, this one is capable of enhancing the strength of someone, sometimes making an elf as strong as an Olog for short moments.\nMaking such temporary changes to one’s body may bring quite the great amount of pain, yet it’s great way to achieve victory in a duel or fight. The major problem, like that of the potion of stoneskin, is that the body is not adapted to this amount of\nstrength. It has been heard about people who drink this potion falling in pain as the effects of the potion come, or after the effects end, due to crushed bones, or destroyed muscles. If used in the right dosages and not excessively though, the side\neffect is normally tired muscles. The minor rank of this potion is quite good for training, and it’s effects quite safe, considering it only gives one a small power boost, good for lifting heavy weights out of a cart.\nRecipe:\n\n- Minor\nBase: Water\n1 Symbol of Earth (Fortitude, Power, Resilience)\n- Lesser\nBase: Distilled Water\n2 Symbols of Earth (Fortitude, Power, Resilience)\n1 Symbol of Fire (Power)\n- Greater\nBase: Aqua Vitae\n3 Symbols of Earth (Fortitude, Power, Resilience)\n1 Symbol of Fire (Power)\nContinues in part 2\n\nWritten by Daniel Nodal\nThe Grand Harvest, 1480", ""),
        StaticBook("Alden Kadwell", "Kale le Prevost", "Caliphate Clinic\n\nHead Doctor Kale\n\nPatient's Name: Alden Kadwell\n\nAge: 19\n\nRace: Human\n\nGender: Female\nCondition/Injury: Was attacked by the undead while mining, suffered cuts and bruises. Twisted her knee in the process, as well as hit her head.\n\nTreatment plan: Applied cream to bruises.\nPatient began bleeding, and was moved to the surgical room. Injected a numbing sterilyzer into her head. Began using a seramictosis stitch to patch up the wound on the scalp. Cut the thread at the end, easily patched up.\nThe knee was sore, and colored of purple and blue. Cream was applied. Pateint will stay overnight. Cuts were treated with alchohol one last time before being released.\nDoctor who treated the patient: Kale\n\nCost: 15 minas\n\nDate: 14th - 15th of The Deep Cold, 1521\n\nEnd result: Patient recovered quickly, left without any limp.\n*Doctor Kale's signature would be on this page*\n\n\n~ Doctor Kale", ""),
        StaticBook("ALetterToElswyen", "Anthron", "Over the pain of the days\nThe loss of many, some close, some not\nOver joyful days\nTo blessed and fought for nights\nSome moments so small\nCan be what matters most\nFrom changes\nTo familarities\nFriendships created\nAnd hearts broken\nAll in life is of nature's whim\nWhether it be good\nOr whether it be bad\nWe can not predict the outcome\nFor we can not see the future\nAnd with this note I leave\nInto the ashen night\n~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~To Elswyen\nAlthough I had not said it, but I loved you. I am sorry that I was not brave enough to tell you this. But do not mourn my leaving, because I will be back someday, whether you look for me or not, I will still respect you and\nlove you, no matter which you choose.\n\nFrom Anthron\n\n~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~", ""),
        StaticBook("Alkheim's Vote", "Alkheim Guillen", "I, Alkheim, Give my vote to,                HORACE", ""),
        StaticBook("Alloys & Metals", "Koralon Doomforged", "The Alloy Compendium\n\n===================\n\nA concise guide on the most widely used alloys for craftsmanship,\n\nby\nKoralon Doomforged\nIntroductions\n\nWhile the core metals provide an ample variety of strength, durability and flexibility for tools, construction and decorations, the more scholarly smiths realised that blending one metal with another (or creating carbon alloys) can\nhelp mend the disadvantages of metals while perfecting and fine-tuning their other qualities.\n\nCreating alloys is a must-know for any blacksmiths who seek to achieve the highest quality of tools, weapons and armour.\nThe Core Triad\n\nThe core triad refers to the three base metals widely used in smithing:\n\nAurum, Ferrum and Carbarum.\nFerrum:\n\nFerrum is revered for its versatility. It's used to craft arches, reinforce structures, make tools, weapons and armour as well. However, it's prone to rust and can easily be refined into steel. Ferrum has a relatively low melting point.\nAurum:\n\nAurum is brittle, heavy and hard to sharpen. Any equipment forged out of aurum is bound to have terrible durability. However, aurum never rusts, and as such it's the preferred metal to preserve wealth. Coins are minted from aurum, while the\nnobility drinks their wine from aurum goblets.\n\nAurum has another propety though. It's capable of interacting with the unnatural forces that keep undead and some other dark monsters anchored to our world.\nAny such creature struck by a weapon of aurum will feel peen much alike a mortal would, and a few slashes with an aurum blade can easily banish them and destroy them permanently.\n\nAurum melts easier than ferrum.\nCarbarum:\n\nCarbarum has a blue hue to it and is extremely durable. At the same time, carbarum can't be sharpened and therefore only a handful of blacksmiths in history could ever craft weapons out of pure carbarum.\nCarbarum also has an extremely high melting temperature and can only be properly worked with the help of a crucible and a decent-sized forge.\nRefined alloys:\n\nRefined alloys are produced by refining a single metal through different means. Any such methods usually takes at least twice as much base materials than what the forgemaster seeks to procure.\nLuminous Aurum:\n\nBy heating aurum scrap to an extremely high temperature within a crucible, impurities can be purged and a stronger blade can be forged. While more effective against the undead and spectral, luminous aurum is never used to craft\narmour, tools or cutlery due to the sheer amount of aurum consumed or ruined in the process of creating it.\nRefined carbarum:\n\nA high amount of carbarum can be refined a lot like aurum can, but doing so requires immense experience in geology and craftsmanship to procure the proper temperature and circumstances. It's used to craft armour.\nThere is no recorded case of refined carbarum produced outside a blast furnace.\n\nThe temperature necessary cannot be achieved through burning charcoal, coal or coke, only by feeding a blast furnace with alchemical fuel.\nCarbon Alloys\n\nCarbon alloys are the different versions of steel produced in a crucible or a blast furnace by cleansing iron with carbon.\nSteel:\n\nSteel is the most widely used alloy and metal. Low quality steel can be produced by melting ferrum scraps together with chunks of coal in an enclosed and heated crucible. Better quality can be drawn from a blast furnace.\nSteel retains the strength and durability of iron, while improving on its flexibility and slightly altering its general properties. A master blacksmith is able to choose the proper carbon:iron ratio for every piece of tool, weapon or armour they craft.\nBlack ferrum\n\nBlack ferrum is sometimes referred to as the \"champion of alloys\" because of its superiority in battle. Black ferrum is neither black nor ferrum, merely high-carbon steel that proved to be the most effective weapon\nalloy after centuries of trial & error. Due to its flexibility, black ferrum is never used to craft armour: comapred to steel, it'd just bend easier and give way to piercing weapons that a steel plate would deflect.\nSecond-degree alloys:\n\nSecond-degree here refers to two different base metals from the triad used to produce the alloy. If moulded, the qualities of the base metals mingle much like the colour and the material itself.\nSecond degree alloys are used to make metals easier to work on and more effective in combat.\nSlayer steel:\n\nSlayer steel is an alloy of ferrum and aurum with the goal to harden aurum enough to craft lasting weapons that retain aurum's undead-banishing abilities. Slayer steel is the most frequently used alloy for monster hunters\nand many adventurers prefer to keep a slayer-steel side weapon on them at all time in case they encounter an enemy they can easily maim with it.\n\nWhile slayer steel allows weapons to cause decent harm to both the undead and the living,\nthe aurum content keeps any weapon crafted brittle and lacking in durability. Therefore, slayer steel is never used for armour or cutlery.\nBluesteel:\n\nInvented during the 18 years war, bluesteel is a high-temperature alloy of carbarum and ferrum. Records exist of bluesteel produced with the crucible method, but a blast furnace is always preferred. The carbarum content leaves the\nferrum far more durable than any weapon (easily rivalling pure carbarum weapons), while it retains the sharpness and flexibility of ordinary steel blades. Bluesteel is a preferred choice for those looking forwards to a long battle.\nBluesteel is seldom used to craft armour, when it is it's mostly ceremonial purposes due to the metal's blue-ish hue. Bluesteel armour resembles steel in durability and strength.\nThird-degree alloys:\n\nThird degree alloys are produced by moulding carbarum into the most popular alloys. Because of the three base materials, third-degree alloys require purified carbarum moulded into the metal:\nin the form of a flawless diamond. Any jewelcrafted can attest to the incredibly high temperatures at which a flawless diamond would melt - only a couple craftsmen are capable of refining alloys with pure carbarum, and the only recorded precedent uses\na special dwarven blast furnace overheated with the aid of magic.\n\nThird-degree alloys can't sustain larger chunks of metal, and are only used for thin rapiers, foils or sabres.\nDaemon Steel:\n\nDaemon steel is an alloy of high-carbon steel and pure carbarum. While it doesn't gain much in durability, any blade forged from daemon steel can be sharpened far better than black ferrum.\nAengul Aurum:\n\nAengul Aurum is an alloy of slayer steel (which is an alloy of gold and ferrum) and pure carbarum. It's the most dreaded metal by undead. It possesses higher durability than slayer steel, can be sharpened far better while it still reta\nthe anti-monster properties of aurum.\nAlternate names:\n\nFerrum\n- Iron\nAurum\n- Gold\nLuminous Aurum\n- Hardened Aurum\n- Heavy Aurum\nSteel\n- Crucible steel (if produced in crucible)\n- Blasted steel (with blast furnace)\nBlack ferrum\n- Blacksteel\nSlayer steel\n- Witchhunter gold\n- Witchhunter's steel", ""),
        StaticBook("Amo Apes", "Alaion Miravaris", "Secundum leges omnibus nota\naviation,\nSic autem non est apis\nut possit fugere.\n\nEt alas suas ad angustus\ncorpusculum adipem super terram.\nIstam quidem certe tuarum\n\napes quoniam non curamus\nQuod hominibus impossibile est cogitare.\nFlavo clarissimo, sive nigrum. Flavo clarissimo, sive nigrum.\nFlavo clarissimo, sive nigrum. Flavo clarissimo, sive nigrum. Hui, et nigrum flavo!\nSit scriptor excutite eum paulo.\n\nEnigma? Prandium paratum est!", ""),
        StaticBook("Amoss The Wizard", "Arthur Caulfield", "Amoss the wizard spoke of death to the prince. \n  Yakov, the target, had not been seen since.\n  Hold up in a castle full of armed guards. \n  Amoss' mind was smashed into shards. \n  Believing he could take on all of the men.\n  Amoss the wizard\nrushed into Oren.\n  Then rushing back out, chased by an angry mob.\n  Amoss the wizard looked quite the knob.\n  Surrounded by metal, which could deliver such pain.\n  Amoss the wizard gave up and put in chain.\nGrigor, the lead man in a mob of patriotic Orenians. \n  A determined mind that put him above millions. \n  Organised the mob into a killing machine. \n  Each section took the orders ever so keen.\n  To shed blood, for the emperor who runs this place.\nAnd oh how they moved, at such a high pace it would seem to be a race to rip off the enemies face.\n  Eraborn. No one saw him, sneak on the rooftop. \n  Only when his eyes fell on to Grigor did he stop.\n  Withdrew a bow, and an arrow made from\nthe finest of steel. \n  To make sure that where the head struck, the wound would not heal.\n  I kid you not, it struck his head, but he shrugged it away. \n  Many may tell you different, but I was there on that day.\nA day when the guards seized the man on the roof.\n  But using his magic, he escaped their clutches with a poof. \n  While that man is being hunted Amoss is on trial.\n  The treachorous things he shouted were ever so vile.\n\"Off\" shouted the crowd, \"Off with his head!\"\n  And after the trial, I am sure Amoss will be dead.", ""),
        StaticBook("An Analysis", "Tarien Arvius", "The Forgotten Dwarves - What Is Known\nThe Forgotten Dwarves of Athera are the extinct people of the lands to the far northwest, far past the great Eruthos Canyon. We know very little about them but suspect them to be the\nbuilders of the Great Doors, ten of which are hidden around Athera. We believe these doors to be entrances to Forgotten Dwarven cities long sealed, but the work of our best spellcrafters has failed to open them: the Forgotten Dwarves were\nhighly skilled at sealing things. The key to unlocking these doors likely lies in their capital, the fabled “Hall of the Ancients”, referred to as Urguan’s Hall in the texts of the Dwarves of Aegis, at least prior to the ascent of the Empire of\nKhorvad and their suppression and destruction of such texts. While we believe some texts survived, they too were lost when the Scriberfolk cult fled through the hidden one-way portals to “Asulon”, on what we believe is the other side of the mortal\nplane.\nFrom what we can discern, the Forgotten Dwarves were somewhat more advanced than their modern kin. Technology stagnated under the boot of the Empire of Khorvad now that it has been overthrown by the\nBlackaxe-led rebels a culture of violence pervades the dwarves that no doubt will take many generations to die out.\nWe have been unable to discern the age of the Forgotten Dwarves but our best evidence suggests that\ntheir extinction occurred just before Year 0 by the Aegean calendar: the date of the Ravager’s first defeat and long before the founding of Rivel. This would appear to contradict the Aegean belief that the four brothers were\nthe first of their species and the fathers of civilisation. If this is the case, and that the Aegean Dwarves are the surviving descendants of the Forgotten Dwarves (no doubt led by the dwarf known as Urguan) then one can only begin to\nspeculate how the modern dwarves lost the technological expertise of the Forgotten Dwarves. Perhaps a schism occurred, causing the departure of Urguan’s faction, which would have been less technologically minded, and thus\nallowed them to escape extinction. Much remains uncovered, and it is my hope that our investigations into the Forgotten Dwarves under the direction of the Radiant Man in the interests of survival may also be in the interests of\nuncovering history.\n- Spellcrafter Tarien Arvius", ""),
        StaticBook("An Orc's Life", "Goj Malog'Yar", "((This was written by an orc, but since most of the orcish language is actually just mispronounced common, I only wrote words that are actually different for orcs in the Blah. The words shared between the two languages are written in Common.))\n Mi name\nMalog'Yar. Mi am the Goj of the War Uzg, and of mi people, the Orcs. As such, it is mi job to guide the orcs, especially the Rex, in wisdom from experience and the spirits. Mi have been alive for almost 90 years. During this time, mi have experienced just\nabout every aspect of life an orc can gruk. Mi have been blargless. Mi have led armies. Mi have been a spiritual guide to mi people. With that said, mi will start from mi cubhood. Mi was raised in a small yet old vilage in the desert by mi momo, Dura, agh\nmi popo, Gurak. Mi, as all uruks, began mi combat training as soon as I was old enough to hold a weapon. The orcish cub, unlike the cubs of other races, is hardly afforded the luxury of \"playing.\" An orc must grow up fast, or nub at all. Because of this,\nmany of us are considered adults at 8 or 10-years-old, as opposed to the other races, who are allowed to wait until they turn 18; but mi digress. Mi popo taught mi how to fight under the hot sun, agh on the blistering sands mi grew to love. He taught mi\nhonor above all, agh it was during a training session that mi witnessed the definition of dishonor. Ash day, a shara was travelling in our desert. Mi popo confronted him, agh demanded an explanation from the trespasser. The shara did nub gruk the Blah,\nbut challenged mi popo to an ash-on-ash honor klomp. He accepted, agh, to make a long story short, was almost flat'd when the shara whistled. At this, a pair of archers rose from their hiding places, agh loosed their ligs at Gurak. Mi popo won the klomp,\nbut the sharas' attempt to cheat in an honor klomp stuck in my memory for the rest of my life. Mi popo was flat'd a year later by a horde of the monsters who roam the wilderness every night. Mi eventually took mi lusk, agh went off on mi own. Mi wandered\nthe desert alone for about 20 years. On mi 34th year of life, mi stumbled upon the goi of San'Orca. Mi remained blargless for some time after that, until the Braduk clan took mi as ash of their own. They allowed mi to share the blarg of another clan\nbrother. Mi lived in that blarg until the War Uzg was temporarily disolved, agh the clans spread throughout the desert, establishing individual clan forts. Mi served as a grunt in the Braduk fort, until Grool'Gorkil'Azog founded the Trog in order to both\ncentralize our people once more, agh to keep a closer eye on the pink skins. Mi became a chicken farmer in the Trog, agh found it to be a humble agh gratifying life. Many would look down upon such a life. Those people are globs, too filled with their own\npride to see the hoshness of such simplicity. It was in the Trog that mi met a young goblin named Durah. We became close, agh she grew to trust mi in the hardest years of her life. After mi brothers conquered Kingston, agh established it as our new\ncapitol goi, Gronkkston, she became mi lifemate. Durah agh mi hab been together for around 40 years, agh she has borne mi h' cubs. Anyways, the Braduk clan was disbanded while we were in Gronkkston, agh those of us in that clan became Ugluks, as it was\nthe popo clan to the Braduks. This was a hard time, but we pressed on. While in Gronkkston, the witch doctor, Grool, took mi as his apprentice, agh mi began mi long journey as a shaman. A shaman, as it turns out, is what mi was always meant to be. Mi have\nfound little more enjoyable than serving mi people as a spiritual guide. Mi will blah more of that later. While mi was an apprentice, Pok flat'd after choosing mi as the new Wargoth of the Ugluk clan. Mi revived the Ugluk clan, agh made it a respected\nclan again. For a while, it became the bub'hoshest of the clans in Gronkkston. Mi even had to stop recruiting to give the other clans a chance to build their numbers. During this time, the Wargoths led orc government as a council. Mi learned that being a\nleader is often like being a popo. You spend more time scolding people, agh making sure they all behave than anything else. Shortly, after becoming the Wargoth, mi first cub was born. We named her Nurena. She brough mi bub'hozh joy, agh continues to honor\nmi to this day. Perhaps mi over-fed her. She got quite fat, but it didn't bother mi or her. It didn't matter that she was fat. What mattered was whether she'd grow to be strong, wise agh honorable; agh she did. She grew to be a desirable feorc, agh is now\na mate of the Rex, who wressled a scaddernak to earn her favor agh mi approval. During mi time as the Ugluk wargoth, mi was also chosen as the commander of the United Anthos Coalition, an army of sharas, albais agh uruks, klomping together against the\nBlack Scourge. We fought against the forces of Setherian, at the same time that we were fighting a war against the dwarves, who had walled off a massive portion of the continent of Anthos. There were glorious klomps in that time. After some time had\nan elder in mi clan, Nux, decided he wanted to be in charge. He challenged mi for mi position, won the klomp agh bekame mi Wargoth for a time. I was, however, forced to take mi followers from within the Ugluks, agh form a new clan. A clan war had started\nbetween the Azogs, agh a clan of Iblees worshiping whitewashes, called Kaxils. Despite the dishonorable behavior of the Kaxils, Nux sided with them, agh mi had nub choice but to take mi followers away to preserve their honor. Mi hold nub grudge against\nNux. Mi gruk why he sided with the Kaxils. The Ugluks agh the Azogs have hated each other for generations, but mi could nub side with the Kaxils miself. So, mi formed the Yar clan in honor of mi great great great grandpopo, Yar. After that, mi beloved\nDurah birthed a pair of twins named Malgroth agh Balgroth. Mi blah lat, do nub ever underestimate the value of a hosh mate. Durah has been loyal to mi for many years, agh has brought me the bub'hoshest joy mi have ever gruk'd. Mi love her more than mi can\nblah. Some time after the birth of the twins, the Wargoths re-established the Rexdom, with Urik'Azog as Rex. He chose mi as his Yazgurten, the chief builder agh economic head of orc government. Mi served as Yazgurten until we went to the Fringe. Mi people\nsettled in a canyon in the desert. Mi soon became the High Shaman, agh served faithfully for years. Mi had long-since been a well-gruk'd teacher of shamanism, agh remain a teacher to this day. Eventually, the orcs became disatisfied with Rex Urik. Mi wull\nnub pretend mi did nub take a side, but mi wull nub pretend it was nub painful to peep titles come between orcs. Orcs are all brothers agh sisters; cubs of Krug. It hurts to peep siblings klomp. Later, under Rex Boghat, we moved to our warcamp near the\nobsidian mountains. After some time, a new High Shaman came into the position, though mi still happily performed mi duties as a shaman to the Uzg. This new High Shaman led a clan, which held an illegitimate tournament to usurp the Rex, who at the time was\nGrogmar'Gorkil. It was a sickening sight. It almost led to a clan war, agh the High Shaman, along with his clan, were exiled under suspicion of burz mojo. An honorable brother named Buubztik'Lur became High Shaman, agh mi was Yazgurten again for almost 20\nyears. Soon after the rebelious clan was exiled, Durah gave mi another cub. We named him Ognir. He, like his sister, brought mi bub'hosh happiness. After the 10-year trip to Thales, mi continued to serve as Yazgurten until the flat of Buubztik. Mi built\nmany blargs. While in Thales, Durah agh mi had another cub. He was different. He was born with a rotting eye. Many feared for his health, but mi gruk'd he was touched by mi master, Orgon. Mi hab been, lat peep, a loyal servant of the disease spirit,\nOrgon, for over 20 years. He is the ruler of disease agh pestilence, agh feeds on all decay. Nub matter who lat are, remember. Lat will decay. Lat will feed mi master's power. We who worship him have a saying. Mubaramishi, gith prasogat. Mubaramishi, gith\nkul Orgonob: In the end, everything decays. In the end, everything belongs to Orgon. Many find this troubling, but Orgon is a spirit just as much as Enrohk agh Tagnir. Mi am, as all hosh orcs, a follower of Krug. Mi am an instrument of Orgon to bring\nsuffering agh failure upon all of Krug's enemies. Having said all this, mi gruk'd mi kub tu bi chosen by Orgon. We named him Vadok, agh he is a champion of Orgon. Orgon has even begun to manifest his power in my cub's hands. It troubles him at times, but\nOrgon is an orcish spirit, agh orcish spirits do not weaken their servants. They strengthen them into greater weapons. They sharpen us. After Buubztik's flat, mi became High Shaman again until we arrived in Athera. Grogmar had stepped down, agh the\nDominus Thore'Gorkil chose mi as the new Rex. Mi served for some time, but mi nub ever wanted to be Rex. It proved not to be where mi was meant to be. It brought mi only bub'hosh weariness of heart. Eventually, mi Warboss, Reksam'Kog, klomp'd mi for the\ntitle. Mi had long been tired of that word... Rex. Reksam klomp'd with strength agh honor. Mi recognized this in his klomping, agh he became the new Rex. The Azogs still do not approve, agh it is why they continue to war against our Uzg. It has been to mi\nanother painful sight, as brothers flat each other over a title again. To lat, whoever reads this, mi impart upon lat this wisdom mi have learned in my life: Do nub be quick to chase after power. Be content, agh learn to peep the hoshness of a simple\nlife. Find a loyal mate. Have cubs, agh raise them with honor. Do nub spite lats brother. Find what lat love to do, agh do it honorably. Mi found more joy as a chicken farmer than mi ever did as Rex. Finally, be a cactus. Mi will end this book with\none more brief story from my life. A shara priest was once confused that a spirit sent mi on a trial before he healed mi after mi lost mi eyes, when his god, he claimed, gave freely to him. Mi explained the hoshness of the trial as follows: The orc is\nlike the cactus. He lives in a harsh environment with little to nub nourishment, but he thrives agh grows tough because of it. The sharas... the sharas are like grass. There's a lot of it, agh it's everywhere; but if you take away its nourishment, even\nfor a short time, it withers agh flats. Sharas are like grass. Be a cactus. The trials of the spirits are to make us stronger. If they handed everything to us, we would grow complacent agh weak. Learn from life, brothers agh sisters, as mi hope to\nkeep learning for however much longer mi will live.", ""),
        StaticBook("An Orcs Art V.1", "Maxistraw Orion", "*Smudges of charcoal are seen across the first page, a sloppy name 'Maxistraw Orion' is writen here. A detailed picture of a tusk below the name that has a small ring next to it.*\n*This is a charcoal picture of a beautifully detailed orc woman speaking to a tall brutish orc and not much else. Throughout the whole of this book this would be smudged and a mess.*\n*This charcoal drawing is of a huge orc with an angry look, leaning on the walls of Krugmar. In one hand he holds a piece of some meat and in the other a large mace.*\n*This charcoal drawing is of multiple orcs sitting around the cloud temple seeming to be talking towards one another.*\n*This charcoal drawing is one that shows a fork in the road, there is a building in the distance and the only name on a sign post is Cloud Temple*\n*This one is of a flamboyant man who seems to be covered in clothing and is 'jumping' as there are other people around staring and a fallen tree behind them. On a trail.*\n*As this charcoal drawing would be of what looks like the front of a big city, from the looks of it the Elven Domain, vines present and detailed greatly*\n*Unlike this others, this one seems much darker. Three people that seem like guards stand in a snarky pose. From the looks of it one would recoginze their Norlandic armor. 'Nland' above their names.*\n*An old man is pictured here with people who look like they are from a monestary, they seem very welcoming and helping. It seems very carefully drawn.*\n*A charcoal drawing of an elf woman and a human male is seen here, they seem very happy and are pushing each other off of logs into water.*\n*Another charcoal drawing is of a strong elf, from what it seems like a Prince. If one lives in the Elven Domain they would recoginze him as Prince Khaine. He seems very stern in this drawing.*\n*This is a drawing of a small cave with a deep fire pit in the middle. It seems to be as neat as it could be with chests laying about. The words 'Home' at the bottom of the page.*\n*This drawing is of two orcs, one of Shaman clothing and the other nearly naked. They stand at a beautiful fountain in front of what seems like a tavern, they are conversing and very detailed.*\n*This one is simple, it is of a burnt tree with a large trunk. It is in front of a large wall and seems to be tilted.*\n*This charcoal drawing is of a dwarf and a human man fighting one another in what seems to be a fighting pit, they look like they are laughing though as it seems they are only sparring.*\n*This charcoal drawing is of the same fighting pit, but a womanly figure winning over a gruff man. A light seems to be shinning over her as you can tell she is a dark elf.*\n*This charcoal drawing is of a distant mountain, one covered with huge mushrooms and a small platform of cobble, a stream filled with gunk lays beside it.*\n*The next charcoal drawing is one of Evermore, their walls and some people in front of the gate with swords drawn and facing the on looker.*\n*The next charcoal drawing is of a man, one would recoginze him as King Avalon. He seems to have a nice look to his face.*\n*This charcoal drawing however...is much darker. It is of a huge dog with flames shooting out of a helmet. The end of its tail like a whip with spikes arching out of its back. It's claws seem to be long and gruesome if it were to hit you.*\n*Ruins of Evermore are drawn on this page, fire roaring from above and people fleeing. You can see Avalon's dead body on the ground below another big man.*\n*This one is of a gate being built, as it would seem an orc with guards armor is building the gate with a few others. The town seems very new.*\n*This charcoal drawing is of a group of kids sitting around a tavern table rolling dice, there are two little boys along with two little girls and an orc child. They all seem to be laughing and have a very light atmosphere.*\n*The next charcoal drawing is of a tall elf man with white hair, he is grinning while holding bottles of alcohol. It seems he is in the Mother's Breast Tavern behind the counter.*\n*This is a very detailed drawing of an elven girl leaning on the railing of a bridge in a dense elven city. The girl has a smile on her face, if one lives in the evlen city they would recongize her as Elswyen.*\n*The next drawing is of a beautiful elven woman, she seems very strong with a beautiful look. Those who live in Elven territory recoginze her as Princess Titiana.*\n*This drawing is of a gathering of elves in different clothing, some wearing clothes that could be of a Prince and others who look to be citizens. In the middle of their gathering is a dead orc, an elven girl staring at it with hate in her eyes.*\n*An elf man stands there in annoyance with another elf girl who looks similar next to him. They have unique clothes on and body paint on themselves. They seem very religous maybe.*\n*The next charcoal drawing is of a gathering of elves, most being drawn as very stuck up people with one especially resembling a man named Azel, looking down at a helpless elf child and others glaring at the child.*\n*The next is of a ragged elf in worn out clothes, a flask in hand. She is leaning on the railing of the inside of a building, prehaps a tavern. Bags are under her eyes with a look of distaste.*\n*This charcoal drawing is of three women in a cell, an elf prince and a crowd of others glaring at the women as if accusing them. One of the women looks...drawn very carefully, her eyes glistening and calm with elegant clothing.*\n*This charcoal drawing is of a little four year old named Bee, a grinning little girl being very detailed on top of Max's shoulders while he is grinning as well.*\n*A banshee is drawn here, ferice and horrible. The banshee is on top of a fountain with a whole group of elves of all kinds surrounding it, bruised and bloodied.*\n*This is a beautiful charcoal drawing of a dark elven woman, she has long beautiful hair with narrow eyes that gaze off into no where. Flowers are drawn on the sides of her as the name Loretta underneath the picture is carefully crafted.*\n*The next one is of a street magician, a woman with a top hat with a coin in her hand. She has a snarky look upon her face while holding up the coin, seeming to be in front of the Tavern in the Elven Dominion.*\n*A cervitaur is drawn beautifully here. Half man and half stag the easily recongizable Taltheus is shown barring a bow. His antlers are decorated with vines and leaves while a little owl rests upon him.*\n*A huge grassed figure is drawn holding a bloody buff orc. The grassed figure is as big as the trees besides it and little figures below watch up as the orc's body lays lifeless in the charcoal drawing.*\n*A big blob is drawn here, a very obese man with only a loin cloth to cover him. He is shown with slobber down his face and seems very disgusting in nature. Little words are next to his lips. 'Eats. Kids.'*\n*An elven woman with a belly stands there with a big grin. She has a big dress on to accompany for her dress, those who live in the Elven Dominion know her as Eurielle. While she was still pregnat with her child.*\n*A huge orc is drawn here, punching what seems to be an elven Prince. There is a smaller orc with a grin on his face that seems to be a cub. The huge orc seems to greatly tower over the elven prince with pride.*\n*This drawing seems more peaceful than the rest, as it is a giant tortoise resting in a field with almost a smile. The sun is shining over a hill with a old stumpy tree besides it. Everything seems...tranquil.*\n*Now a floating monolith is drawn here, overlooking a valley. The monolith is made of stone and on the bottom runes are inscribed.*\n*This charcoal drawing is of a gathering...not just any normal gathering. Three figures stand over a fire with pikes surrounding them with skulls. The perspective is that of farther away, one might suspect that the artist was an onlooker.*\n*This next drawing is of a gathering of orcs from the Whispering Crossroads, orcs of many shapes and sizes have swords and amor at the ready. Dwarves stand with them as well.*\n*This charcoal drawing is of Taletheus and a tall armored Graven facing one another. There are multiple pages filled with movements of the two going at each other, quick sketches that are a mess. Then switching the the Graven attacking an elf nerby. -\nThe continuation of the sketches show Tale trying to block the Graven from attacking the bystander, aiming for his neck. Yet the Graven hits the bystander in the arm in the next sketch, with a horrified look on the elfs face. The Graven is launched back -\nby Tale. In the next one Tale is right on the Graven, trying to disarm it. Though the next one pictures another humaniod with horns is next to the two with Tale holding the Graven down with his hooves. The next one depicts the Tale 'decapitating' the -\nGraven. With the Graven's body disapearing, Taletheus victorious.*\n*A beautiful half orc woman is now drawn here. Her side of her head is shaven and has small tusks on the corner of her mouth. She seems to be drawn in a very relaxed state while looking to the right.*\n*The next drawing...is a self portrait of a whitewash mute orc named Maxistraw. It is of him sitting on a rock alone with a simple flute in his hands. He seems at peace in the drawing. A signature is on the bottom of the page and the book ends.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Dwarves", "[Crippled] Kardel Irongut", "DWARVEN HISTORY: THE FORGOTTEN DWARVES\n___________________The Old Legend as Recounted by Kardel Irongut\n___________________PRESS FOR THE HOLMIC ACADEMY OF THE ARTS AND SCIENCES.\n___________________\nThe most apochryfal piece of lore in the entirety of Dwarven history is the compounded subject of the Forgotten Dwarves. The Forgotten Dwarves is an all encompassing term which refers to the dwarven inhabitants of the civilization before\nthe Blood Age. \n\nUnfortunately, all records of this civilization were destroyed by the Ironborn dynasty in an attempt to solidify their grasp over the dwarven populace. We know very little about these people, save that they were an\nadvanced citizenry with complex political and cultural dynamics as revealed by the impressive ruins they have left behind.\n\nThe most significant of these traces of the past are the Deep Roads, a seemingly ubiquitous system of cavern roads which span every\ncontinent we, the descendants, have traveled to. Often, these caverns lead to magnificent cities, such as Khaz'Urguan and Kal'Karik, eternal testaments to the former might of dwarvenkind.\n\nThe most notable such ruin is the Hall of Urguan, located in\nAthera, which has been discerned to be the oldest city of Dwarves on any continent. The Hall of Urguan was steeped in history, being the center of a vast interconnected confederation of Dwarven Holds whose economies depended on the Deeproads, which the\nThrumm'az or High Lord protected from his seat in Khaz'Urguan. \n\nThe Hall of Urguan is thought to have also been the throne of the father of Dwarves, Urguan. The government was ruled by a Runesmith oligarchy, members of\nwhich were selected from the elder clans. The High Council of Runesmiths voted on the High Lord, who commandeered the dwarven union in times of crisis or war.\n\nAmong the famous kings of the forgotten dwarves are such legendary figures as\nBarradin the Frostbeard and Glorvin of Yore. The First Kingdom of Urguan reigned suzerain for a long period of time, before it collapsed as a result of the Soul Wars.\n\nThe Soul Wars are thought to have coincided with\nthe first Iblical Cataclysm, when Iblees came down to destroy the descendant civilizations. It is thought that, in an attempt to save their race, the Arch Runelords created a gargantuan soul core to contain the Deamon Iblees.\nTo forge such a thing, the First Kingdom created an army of golemantic constructs known as \"Harvesters\" and used it to kill and collect the souls of other descendants. It attacked several of its neighboring civilizations, most notably Rivel the Magestate.\nRivel's historians recount that after the first few initial slaughters, the Forgotten Dwarves stopped attacking. The Magestate prepared its offence, but when it encountered the doors of Khaz'Urguan, it found them completely shut and under lock, no\nsign of dwarf to be seen.\n\nThe Runesmiths had eventually had to resort to sacrificing their own populace in order to meet the soul requirements for Iblees' soul. After they had done so, the Kingdom collapsed, and the Deamon was lured into what would\nbecome his prison for the next several millenia, before the newest wave of Descendants arrived in Athera and released Iblees from his dwarven-made prison. \n\nToday, all but few customs, artefacts, and texts of the Forgotten Dwarves\nremain. They are hoarded and kept hidden, considered precious by their owners. The only certain thing about these dwarves is that we shall never know more about them than what we can deduce from their ruins.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Hist. V1", "Mage Baruk-Ghaz", "\"The Ancient History\"\n\n*The next lines are curved*\n\"These volumes contain the Origins of Aegis, written by the \"Wandering Wizard\" in the second seed of year 84 at the Cloud Temple of Aegis.\"\n\n*The book apears to be in good shape, it must be\nThere were no planes of existance. There was nothing. Just the void. And a birght shining light. It was not a light we could see, it was not really white either, but it would be the only way to explain the existance of such a Deity in contrast to the\nemptiness of the Void. None knows why, how or when this Deity existed. It is in-fact, herecy to speculate on such matters. The all knowing God was this Deity.\n\nTruly none can describe the majesty of the creator, the one and only. The Merciful Creator\nthe Seven Skys. With his intent, and only his intent, the World of Aegis was created. All he had to do was simply want it to occur and it happened. The rolling seas, proud mountains and vast landscapes, all in a second, created by God.\nThe World was not created in play or for fun, but as a theater for the inhabitants of the World to be tested in. And tested for what? Well, that is for us to speculate. Though I believe it is to test us for purity, how hard we can fight temptation, and\nhow clean and good can our actions be.\n\nThe first mortal being to be created was a man. This man was sculptured with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, God's creation lay there for the other immortal beings to see. The Aengul and The Daemon,\ntwo spirits created before the mortal beings and before the creation of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more.\n\nGod then blew his own breath of existance into the hollow shell and the Man\nlived. God then took the man and put him in the centre of all of Aegis, the same spot where The Cloud Temple now stands. God also made the Man a partner, from the exact same clay and the exact same breath, she was the first Woman. These simple beings\ncould not talk, nor did thay know much about the World. They roamed the world, enjoying its pre-historic beauty. Untouched, the fresh glades and dark thick forests were a wonder to set eyes on. Soon they had four children in the four corners of Aegis.\nMalin was the first of their sons, born in the deep forests of Aegis, he had blonde hair and sharp ears. Standing tall, he was the father of the Elves of Aegis. Krug was born in the scorching deserts of Aegis, fierce and relentless, he was\nthe father of the Orcs. In the fresh meadows of Aegis was born Horen, father of Humans. And lastly, in the deep underground caves of the World, Urguan was born, master of the Dwarves.\n\n*You quickly grab the next volume*", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Hist. V2", "Mage Baruk-Ghaz", "\"The Ancient History\"\n\n*The next lines are curved*\n\"These volumes contain the Origins of Aegis, written by the \"Wandering Wizard\" in the second seed of year 84 at the Cloud Temple of Aegis.\"\n\n*The book apears to be in good shape, it must be\nWe do not know how they fathered sons and how their lines continued but perhaps God created a partner for each Son to continue their lines? Soon the first Man and Woman created by God departed Aegis and climbed the Seven Skys to meet with God, their\ncreator, for they had achieved their goal. The Sons began to explore the World of Aegis and each was stricken with grief at the loss of their parents, seeking to fill the chasm of emotion inside them they began to create civilisation.\nAlthough none of the descendants of each Son had neither their long lives or splendour, they did carry their forefathers looks and traits. The Elves with Malin at their head travelled the lands and began naming all the inhabitants of this world, they were\nthe first to create a tongue and began to name the trees and grass, the mountains and valleys across all of Aegis.\n\nAt this time, Malin, Urguan, Krug and Horen were not far apart in looks. Horen and Krug had darker hair than the other two and Krug w\nbit larger in build. Malin had blonde hair and Urguan had red. They were all close companions, friends and had much love for each other and each others people.\n\nUrguan travelled into the deep underground of the earth, naming the beautifull ores and g\nsharing it with brethren. Krug travelled the harsh deserts, testing his stamina and strength against the environment of Aegis, and Horen began building the first squalid huts and villages in the valleys. The people lived for hundreds of years, in harmony\nand peace. Until the day where one of the great Daemons, great worshipers and squalid protectors of the Void, kin spirits to the Aengul, defected. Iblees, who was once the greatest of all of Gods worshippers was cast down into the mortal world, he was\nabout to destroy the tranquility of Aegis forever. He came in the shape of a man. A gentle being who loved things delicate, he was quickly befriend by Malin, Urguan and Horen. Krug had a great distrust of him but after many years of being convinced by his\nbrothers, he finally accepted his company.\n\nLittle did Iblees know that this was all part of the Great God's plan to test the descendants of Man and Woman. Iblees wanted to destroy everything that God had designed and created, still not in a powerfu\nphysical form he began sowing seeds of evil in the minds of the Descendants. Prying on their needs and lusts.\n\nTo Malin, lover of nature, he promised him many children. He promised him that their laughter would resonate across their forest homes and\nhe would be content. Malin did not want anything more in this world than a bountiful amount of young to occupy the barren forests.\n\nTo Urguan, he promised infinite wealth of Gems and Ores, colours and crystals he could never imagine. To this, Urguans\ngreed failed him. \n\nHoren, was anxious he would not live long enough to see his city completed and his lands increased. He needed more time, and Iblees struck the cord and promised immortality.\n\n*You quickly grab the next volume*", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Hist. V3", "Mage Baruk-Ghaz", "\"The Ancient History\"\n\n*The next lines are curved*\n\"These volumes contain the Origins of Aegis, written by the \"Wandering Wizard\" in the second seed of year 84 at the Cloud Temple of Aegis.\"\n\n*The book apears to be in good shape, it must be\nKrug was the last to be tricked, Iblees tempted him with wealth, with food, with power. None interested Krug. Iblees was furious, he then challenged Krug in open combat in fury.\n\nThe whole world witnessed Ibleeses transformation into a hideous beast\nthe Void. His skin turned into scales, fangs erupted and dark horns exploded from his head. He grew large wings and began to breath terrible fire. All stood in shock and horror. The beast terrified all inhabitants of Aegis, animals fled and the Sons of\nthe Descendants were too weak of blood to stand infront of such evil fury. Only Malin, Urguan, Horen and Krug stood infront of the terror.\n\nIn Ibleeses right hand, a sword wrought in flame. Krug, naked and unarmed charged at The Daemon, throwing hims\nagainst the scalding scales of Iblees. He screamed in agony as his skin burned and decayed, becoming green and molten. Iblees was knocked off his feet, for the last time. He stood up, heaving in rage and fury, flames exploded from pores of his skin, he\nroared in anger and where he struck his sword the land collapsed and the ground erupted. And Lo, great was the Valour of Urguan and the Strength of Krug as they fought the beast. Powerful were the arms that carried Krugs Axe and strong was Horens heart as\nthey fought in open combat upon the plains of Aegis. Malins sword was fast and swift, smiting Iblees upon his breast and sides.\n\nFor thirty years The Descendants fought Iblees, the world became a war torn mess. The dead were defiled, summoned from t\ngraves to follow Ibleeses mastery. The more mortal descendants died, the greater Ibleeses armys grew. It was a sad chapter in the World of Aegis, the brothers threw up their hands to God in prayer and in agony. Their creations destroyed, their children\nmassacred. Woe to the Sons of Man and Woman. Krug grew bitter, his resentment of his brothers increased for befriending such a beast. Urguan grew greedy, he fought valourously but began to hide his treasures underground. Malin feared for the lives of his\nchildren and did not leave his forest sanctuary. Horen was too ambitious, too weak of a leader, many of his people fought for Iblees and many of them died of recklessness. It seemed the world was destined for ruin. Iblees grew in strength and\nThe Descendants weakened. Until one day.\n\nOne day where the sound of horns could be heard from the far east. Beautiful horns echoing all across the skies of Aegis. God had heard their prayers.\n\nAn army of Aengul and Daemons from the Seven Skys\nappeared on the grand shores of Aegis. Their majesty and beauty so strong that all The Descendants could see was a flash of power white light erupt from the east. Only Malin with his strong sight could see the figures of light as they sped across the\nskies towards the armies of Iblees.\n\nIbleeses soldiers burned where they stood, The thousands of Skeletons and Zombies burst aflames and his living servants fled. There in the right middle of the world, he was cast down and chained by The Aengul and\nDaemon. A robed figure with brown hair and a black wreathed apparation stood before him. They were a terrible image to look at, all shyed down and bowed in their majest and glory. They stood before Iblees, knowing he was immortal and could not be killed,\nsentencing him to banishment to the void where his dark soul would be forever trapped in torment.\n\nBut..\n\n\n*You quickly grab the next volume*", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Hist. V4", "Mage Baruk-Ghaz", "\"The Ancient History\"\n\n*The next lines are curved*\n\"These volumes contain the Origins of Aegis. written by the \"Wandering Wizard\" in the second seed of year 84 at the Could Temple of Aegis.\"\n\n*The book apears to be in good shape, it must be\nBefore they could complete the sentence, Iblees stood tall for one last time.\n\n“You believe you may simply banish me from this plane and that my taint shall not last? I have touched this world with evil and it shall forever be part of the souls that\ninhabit it.\n\nMalin, I curse you with sterility, you and your kin shall forever lack the children they need. May your forest halls forever be silent, and your hearts heavy with sadness.\n\nUrguan, your greed and lust shall overcome you, you are no\nthe height God gave you, your descendants shall be short, squalid and ugly. You will always seek to find Gold and Gems in the deep underground of the earth, your hunger never satisfied.\n\nHoren, you wish immortality? I will curse you with the opposit\nearly death for you and your kin. You shall age quickly and die before you experience the fruits of your useless labour.\n\nAnd you Krug, the most hated of The Descendants, you shall always have the lust of war. You are strong? Well the strength shall\nused against your brothers, used to pillage and murder! Your lust for battle shall be unsatiated and your descendants shall grow ugly and heartless.”\n\nAs soon as his words were uttered, the world grew suddenly dark. A great roar erupted from Ibleeses\nmouth and in a blast of fire he was banished from the Mortal World.\n\nThe robed figure stood before the four brothers.\n\n“There is nothing in my power that may undo what that evil did. There is one thing I may do however, and that is to bless you\nMalin, may your forests be a sanctuary of peace and your children long lived.\n\nUrguan, may your descendants be hardy, strong hearted and strong of mind.\n\nKrug, may your people show valour and honour where none exist.\nAnd Horen, may your people one day explore the Seven Skies.\n\nI can do no more, for all my power is spent. We will go back to our master now, I believe your children may see us once more but long in the future.”\nAnd with that, the great host of Aenguls and Daemons dissapeared into thin whisps in the air. \n\n*You finished reading about The Ancient History, it feels like you understand the world a lot better*\n\nCopies mady by:\n~Baruk-Ghaz", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Scroll", "Ketiley Strong-Heart of Orvar", "kegost;jerkghldtjmhtk;rl\nfgilnrjklghendrklh/trnkl\nrwenjfklerngyktrlhytnmjkl\n\n*The text written in this scroll seems to be of a language that no one can descipher, unreadable, yet the symbols seem familiar to a Gorundyr. With closer inspection,\none can tell that this text seems to be trying to translate Jalfmarr'Tal to Common.*\n\nHuthflur'yr Faeryd Huld\n\n\"Tattooing Your Skin\"\n\n*The scroll, although a bit warn and beaten around the edges seems to give a detailed guide on how to\ntemporarily tattoo the skin with a natural herb called \"Woad\" that has a bluish tint to it, although when dried, turns to an orangish-green. It describes how a thick layer will sit atop the skin until cracked, then to scrape it off gently. On the next\npage it offers a list of ingredients, and details steps to making the woad and how to apply it to the skin. Afterwards, in Jalfmarr'Tal, it describes this is for formal occations, like Rituals and Wars.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Ang Gijak-Ishi", "Vorgak", "Az ah ztudent uff Falum'Lur ztartin' tu gruk Lutaumancy, agh preparyn' ah worteeh offerin' fur mi uld bruddaz, dah Ancestralz, mi wizh tu gruk dah Uld Blah.\n\nWen dah Thagurz Grizh am tu beh redeh, wi am tu kall upon dah Stargush'Stroh, agh mayk our uldast bruddaz, Rax agh Gorkil, gruk our intenziunz.\n\nMi uffer' lat deze bitz agh piezez, agh  hope lat am tu dezide tu explayn zumethin' uff dah anzient tongueh.\n\n=-=Thagurz Grizh=-=\n___----___------___--------____\n-----------_______-----______---\n-__-----------------_______------_________----________----__________--------____-----____---\n-_____------__---___-------___\n\n\n\n                              Vorgak", ""),
        StaticBook("Another Note", "Azoth Hawksong", "Awaiti,\n\nI just wanted to let you know that last night was very awkward (as I'm sure you can tell). I do think it is in our best interests to keep anything that occurs between us very discrete, as we are in a time of great trail.\nHowever, with that in mind, I do wish for us to be open and honest with how we feel or what we percieve.\n\nI am your Advisor first, so never for a moment think my loyalties will shift or change depending on our personal relationship.\nWith those in mind, I went into Linandria today to do my daily run to find any survivors. I found this instead.\n\nIt was the only flower I could find in the entire wasteland. Its still a bit wilted due to the Thanium, though I'm sure an accomplished\ndruid can nurse it back to good health.\n\nToday is going to be either a day of celebration or a day of tribulation. Either way, be ready for the coming storm. I'll be right there beside you.\n\nLove,\nA. Hawksong~", ""),
        StaticBook("Another note.", "Thilln", "King Maric\n\nIn addition to the supplies of war, I have decided to provide you with my personal crossbow, and some explosives. I can only hope they serve you well.\n\n-Delonna.", ""),
        StaticBook("Apotheosis", "Pius", "It was a cool summer day, and Imperial Scribe Cecil Visori sat peacefully at the local tavern in Arethor. His eyes wandering the sky, he fancied he saw a bright light descending from the sky. As it approached Arethor he could clearly see it descending\nfrom the heavens towards the Imperial Palace. Virosi, a very old man, was seen fumbling as a lunatic, jumping and running as fast as his arthirtic legs could carry him towards the palace. He entered the Throne Room, and saw the various priests and\nclergymen carrying out their rituals and prayers, as they had for years since the Emperor went into his mysterious Catatonic state. He looked on the unmoving Emperor, resting upon his throne and lost the hope that he had with seeing the light. He had\nhoped that the Emperor would return and lift the veil of darkness from their lives, but alas the Emperor was still.\n\nAnd lo, the light entered the throne room and descended towards the Emperor. Virosi did not trust his aged and overused\neyes; he closed them and reopened them, but the light persisted. As it reached the ground it halted in front of the Emperor's throne; it was as if the sacred radiance reached forward and placed a hand on the Emperor's blessed chest. Virosi heard faintly a\nsoft and gentle voice murming to the Emperor \"O' Rise most divine and gentle soul for thy hath gone for long and thy flock needs their shepherd.\"\n\nVirosi's eyes were fixed upon this godly event that was transpiring before his very eyes; he could not begin\nto conceive the things he was seeing or hearing. Virosi fell to his feet and looked on, streams of tears flowing down his old cheeks. He saw the scepter in the right hand, this mortal world it rules. He saw the orb crowned with the twin barred crux in the\nleft hand, the carrier of the faith, its protector and its first, the divine realm it rules. The crown, the sacred crown, the tool used to appoint gods, representative of Asulon and what lies beyond, which unites this world and the heavens. But these were\nmere symbols in the eyes of Virosi. He saw the real power was in what held them; the Man-God, the God in the Man, the profane made divine.\n\nThe Divine and Most Holy Emperor, may the Creator bless him, rose to his feet. He held the Imperial Scepter and\nOrb; upon his head rested the Imperial Crown, as if not one day had passed from his time of slumber; His face so gentle and welcoming and his features so bright and compassionate that it was shame to look upon him and feel one's mortal flaws made\nmanifest.\n\n\nThe clergy at first, likewise to Virosi, did not trust their eyes. However, as the divine vision persisted they fell to their knees, their foreheads to the ground in prostration: the act of ultimate submission to divine authority. The\nEmperor's holy lips parted and he spoke in the most gentle of tones; though his final words were firm, as if he was their father. His voice carried sacred authority and demanded obedience- not out of fear, but out of divinity and holiness.\n\"Hearken, let it be known to my loyal and loving subjects that we hath returned and that our being is safe and sound. We have foretold of danger and darkness that shall come, but do not fear, for our radiant light shall cast this evil back to the dark\nabyss that spawned it. Now, call forth our banners, make haste to my brother, and tell him to move our armies and seal the borders. Furthermore, call forth the nobles, for there is much to plan.\"\n\nIt was if the commands came into one's heart, and there is\nnothing one could do but to obey such wisdom and magnificence.\n\nThis is a story of the Apotheosis of His Most Divine and Imperial Majesty, the Holy Emperor of Oren and The Regent Eternal Of the Kingdom Of Heaven, Godfrey The First Of His Name.\nAuthored by Imperial Scribe Cecil Virosi. At first I doubted my eyes, but after much reflection and prayer I have come to the conclusion that what I saw was a divine revelation, and a pronouncement by our Divine Emperor of things to come.", ""),
        StaticBook("Apparations", "Anorak", "Apparitions are formed when a large group of souls die in a particularly horrific way in a single location. Examples of this may be being burnt alive, sailors drowning on a sinking ship or simply a massacre.\nThis however is not to say that all mass-deaths will cause the formation of an apparition.\nFor an apparition to form a particularly dark soul or group of dark souls with their mind set on malevolent behavior must have perished with this large group of souls.\nUpon death this dark soul binds all the other souls together to form an evil manifestation known as an Apparition. Apparitions gradually grow more powerful as they age.\nOnly a few Apparitions were ever found. Three existed in the realm of Anthos. They owned no Names, but were described as the following.\nApparition of 10 Souls\nThe weakest from the three.\nApprition of 50 Souls\nThe one, founded in the base of the Delvers\nApparition of 100 Souls\nThe most powerfull one recorded.\nThe Apparition of one hundred souls appeard in it's spectre form like a woman. This might be happening, because the dominant soul could be the one of a woman. This Apparition was also known to be the most dangerous of all.\nIt was also known that the Black Scourge summoned it's powers and made a contract with it.After the fall of the Black Scourge and Anthos, this Apparition became a \"Wandering\" Apparition. The most dangerous of all Spiritual beings.\nIt losed it's pillar, but a myth tells about that this being closed itself into a prison. Waiting to be released once again upon the world. The only way to stop this being to destroy a town, is with the help of Clerics and other holy magical users.\nAfter the races arrived on Athera, the Apparition of hundred souls might aswell passed the portal.\nIt was recorded that this being was able to disguise itself as someone, but obvious signs like red eyes showed the truth behind the disguise.\nA demonic being, called Vangron. Found out on how to summon a Apparition and used his new founded ritual to doom the races multiple times in Anthos.\nHow to summon one is unknown, only the person called Vangron would know, even if it is known to be the -\nmost dangerous ritual in existence. Since you never knew wich Apparition would appear...\nNo more informations were found.\n-Veldryn Uuthlini-", ""),
        StaticBook("Application", "Titania Star", "IGN: _FluffyGemini\nDiscord: Geminisole#4164\n\nCharacter: Titania Star\nAge: 75\nGender: Female\nRace: Mali'thill\nCity: Haelun'or\nDepartment: Magic and/or elinder'Iin", ""),
        StaticBook("Application", "Celebil", "[[Skype: sevenise1\nIGN: Sevenise]]\nName: Celebil Meeria\nAge: 50\nGender: Female\nRace: Pure Mali'ahar\nCurrent City Of Residence: Taliyna'maehr\nDesired Department: Elinder'lin", ""),
        StaticBook("Arabella's Diary", "Bastion Curthose", "Dear Diary, \nGreetings, I have recieved you just in time to document my travels, courtesy of my sister, Aletta. She bought you from a travelling merchant we passed on our way through the Westerlands. One glance at your leather bound pages and I couldn't\nresist. Once she caught me looking at you, she immediately spent our last 25 minas on you, which was kind, but certainly not wise as we had endless more days on the road to come. Anyways, that's Aletta in a nutshell - she made countless sacrifices for me\nwhen we were children and continues to now. She believes it her duty as she is my only other family. \nWe are approaching Courland soon, a place we desire to settle down in and call it a home - however, we've assumed this about many previous places we \nhave visited, but something about this place seems.. promising. I'll write in you soon, Diary, I promise, but Aletta is giving me a glare, trying to rush us a long. Not long now, Diary, this could be our new home. \n\nArabella Rowley\nDiary, \nMe and Letta are currently seeking shelter in a tavern. We made it to Courland by nightfall, and were not lucky enough to miss the evening's downpour. Hopefully it should clear up soon enough, but the most unbelievable thing happened when we first\narrived. An orc assumed I was a prostitute and asked me to escort him? Isn't that ludicrous? Sure, I've worked the odd tavern job here or there, but a hooker? Gah - it only made it worse that he was a smelly old goblin. Imagine that! A man we have briefly\nmet then challenged him to a duel, and sliced off both of his tusks. Quite the scene, as you can imagine. \nA rich man greeted us when entering Courland and straight out asked for Aletta's hand in marriage? The most ridiculous part of it was I think she\nwas actually considering it! Can you believe this malarky. \nAny way, he did come to some use as he helped us find a house here - I'm starting to believe we can actually have a life here, in Courland. The charge is 25 minas a Saint's week which, while\na fine price, is still a little out of our budget. I just hope Aletta doesn't go marrying the rich man, Anyway - I hope to find a job today! \nWish me luck. \n\n\nArabella Rowley\nHello again Diary!\nSorry it's been so long since I've written in you, but a lot has happened and me and Aletta have been awfully busy as of late.\nSo, good news - I got a job! I'm technically a maid for a rich man by the name of Ser William Felsen,\nHowever, he doesn't require my services just yet so I am still unemployed. My last job (a miner) was terrible and I worked for 2 days straight in the mines and only came out with 9.1 minas. Absolutely ridiculous. I got my revenge on my boss, however, I\nsent a determined hooker his way, hopefully to teach him a lesson. Me and Aletta met a man name Hamelin, who helped us greatly in finding a house - so to repay him, we let him stay here for a bit. I'm not sure if it's permanent but I wouldn't have a\nproblem with it if it were. \nAnyway diary, I best be off now. Thanks again for listening.\n\nSigning out,\nArabella Rowley\n\nRon Mormaer Jonsonii the Azghar Horselord and Former Thegn of the Asgeir Sea Wolves was here.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arc. Magci Wiki", "Kypris Solaria", "Arcane Magic\n-------------------Arcane magic is the most widely spread magic throughout the realms.  It is a type of magic that does not require more than study and repetition,and so well known that many books are sold and written about it,\nthough of course, some types are kept secret from the masses. A mage that uses arcane magic draws his powers from the void, a realm of thoughts and emptiness, which he must first learn how to connect to.\nThe Void, Mana and Auras\n------------------- The Void: Arcane Magic is the archtype of magic which is fueled by The Void, or more specifically mana.  The Void is an empty plane of existence where things may be created\nwith the use of ones imagination and willpower.Many teachers of the Arcane often teach students with the following proverb: \"The Void is nothing, yet everything. Like our imagination, it may be dull and empty; or it can be full and colorful\".\nThe Void as a whole is simply a plane where nothing exists, unless the mage makes it exist. Since one must connect to the Void, this means a basic line of communication must be established, generally gained through meditation and practice.\nSince Void users must be connect to draw on the Void, distractions are capable of severing the connection for Novices,while Masters are capable of holding onto their connects until they are drained of mana,\nor wounded. It should be noted that only mages of proper age can connect to the Void.Those under the age of 16 can receive mental damage if they connect to the Void, and so those of the age of 16 and above can begin to practice magic.\n- Mana: When a mage is connected to the Void, he/she may imagine things in this Void; however, a mage must use mana to either draw this spell into the world, or apply it to someone/something.\nMana is sightless and is as invisible as the air in our world (See Auras and Arcane Evocation for more details on this). It flows through our world like streams, and is in every living thing, whether it is plants or animals.\nAlthough mana comes at a cost, since it flows through people, Void users have gained the ability to use this mana to draw from the Void. Void users often get fatigued when over using mana\nand have in rare cases died due to the use of large amounts of mana. Another draw-back with the use of mana is the effect (or lack thereof) on our mortal planewhen you draw on the Void for magics such as Evocations,\nthis element which has been evoked must eventually return to the Void.However this can become complicated with such magics as Alteration, as it has the ability to prolong the existence of Void based elements in our world.\n- Mana Pools: Mana pools are how much mana we have in our person, and this determines how grand our spells can be, along with the duration a spell can be held in our world. Mana pools are governed by two things;\nSkill level and Magic type. Skill level is simply how skilled you are at manipulating mana for your specific Sub-type. For example; the longer you train in the use of Evocations,the better and more efficient you are at manipulating mana for that sub-type.\nMagic type is a little more complicated, different magic Sub-types are naturally more mana consuming then others, a few examples of very draining Sub-types are as followed: Alteration, Arcane Evocation and Conjuration.\nAlthough far more difficult to learn if one of these are your first Sub-type, you will naturally get a bigger mana pool then someone who's first Sub-type was Illusion, or perhaps an Evocation.\n- Auras: Auras are a side-effect from the Void, and is deeply personal to mage's. An Aura directly reflects a mages personality through it's color, which will be listed below this section\nAura is generated from the mana pool regularly, and if a mage uses large amounts of mana at once for spells, they in turn produce more aura. Imagine a fire; the more wood you put on it\nthe more smoke is formed. Much like this fire, the mana pool can generate more aura depending on how much mana you're using at a given time. Auras are generally harmless and are simply a way of self expression.\nSome magics such as Arcane Evocation, Alteration, and Shade are directly tied to Auras, and are heavily effected by them. Auras are able to be openly role-played without being Lore breaking, so feel free to get interesting with it.\nBlue: Calculatedness and logicality (Sometimes emotional coldness) \n\nPurple: Mysteriousness\n\nWhite: Benevolence, order and innocence.\nBrown: Nurturing and caring\n\nYellow: Greed (Sometimes optimism)\n\nRed: Dominance, power and control (Sometimes tyrannical natures)\nGreen: Harmony and balance (Sometimes vanity).\n\nBlack: Chaos and malevolence.\nSub-types of Arcane Magic\n------------------- Arcane is the Arch-type of all the following Sub-types, these are also known as \"roots\".\n- Alteration:\n\nAlteration is manipulation of properties in the physical world.\nTransfiguration [Includes enchanting, transmutation and warding/abjuration]\nTelekinesis [The manipulation and lifting of objects]\nVoid Translocation [Dematerialising matter in the Void for later use]\n- Evocation:\nEvocation is the construction of artificial elements or organic tissues.\nElemental Evocation\nArcanism\nConjuration\n- Illusion:\nIllusion is the manipulation of emotions, and the five senses, such as sight, smell, sound, touch and taste.\nSensory Illusion [A form of illusion in which the mage attempts to influence the mind to fabricate senses and emotions.]\nCognitism [A specific form of Illusion that uses visual aids and mental manipulation to increase intelligence and imagination.]\nMental Magic [Involves accessing the minds of individuals to read thoughts and make illusions.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Evocation", "Laergul", "===================\n\n    Arcane Evocation\n\n\n\n\n\n\n     Transcribed by\n            Laergul\n\n===================\nThis book was written to help students and aspiring students of arcane evocation to better understand this magic and ease their learning.\nWritten by: -Salendys\nChapter 1: What is Arcane Evocation?\n                           \nArcane Evocation is the art of drawing pure magical energy from the void. It can then be shaped as anything the mage can think of. This is a creative form of magic \nwith mostly artistical uses. While it is possible to use this magic in combat, only a skilled arcanist can do so, and even then it is not as strong as the other types of evocation. If your intention is to acquire a means of dealing damage, then this is\nnot the magic for you.\nChaper 2:\nArcane Energy\n                           \nArcane energy is a rare element. In fact, it does not exist naturally in the world. It is an ethereal substance almost exclusive to the void. Because of this, Arcane Evocation is\nthe most difficult type of evocation to learn.\nAs with all other types of evocation, one must fully understand the element that is being evoked. The only way to study arcane energy is by observing an evocation of someone who already knows this magic.\nThis means it is practically impossible to learn without a teacher.\nNow, for those who already have a teacher and seek to complement their lessons with further knowledge, the arcane element can be described as follows.\nIn it's purest form, arcane energy is invisible, shapeless, odorless, completely inhert and very volatile. It can be compared to air or smoke, having a similiar composition than most gaseous substances.\nThose who have observed evocations may have noticed\na fine, thin mist surrounding them. This is because it isn't a single mass. It is in fact a conglomeration of countless tiny wisps of energy that together give the illusion of being a single object.\nSmoke is perhaps the thing that visually resembles\narcane energy the most in our world. Studying its shapeless and volatile nature may be of big help to understand arcane energy.\nChapter 3: Aura\n                           \nAura is a field of mana that surrounds living beings. More complex beings, such as descendants, have a colour associated to their aura. Each individual has their own colour for their aura.\nSome believe that the colour depends on one's personality. This isn't always the case, however, and anyone may have any colour.\nThis colour doesn't change, unless other forces somehow manage to tamper with your aura, which is usually very bad.\nAuras are very relevant to Arcane Evocation in particular.\nWhen raw arcane energy is drawn from the void, it instantly mixes with the mage's aura, making it visible and giving it colour. It is a common misconception to assume that arcane evocationists\nmanipulate aura itself. In truth, it is simply the product of mixing aura with arcane energy that is being manipulated, not the actual aura.\nAnd no, arcanists cannot see other people's aura or make it visible.\nAura is a very personal thing, like \nyour own soul.\nThis means your evocations can never mix with someone elses, or other types of evocation.\nChapter 4: Beginner steps\n                           \nAfter you have managed your first evocation, there is not much you can do. You will only be capable of producing a small wisp and hold it for a short time. The best thing to\ndo is to keep practicing. With each successful attempt you will be able to hold the wisp a little longer. Make sure to have rested enough to be completely recovered after each attempt.\nEventually you will be able to hold your wisp for about five minutes.\n[!] A detailed drawing of a wisp hovering over an open hand occupies most of this page.\nAt that point you'll get enough time to figure out how to get your wisp to do things. You are in control of your evocation, but must learn to control it properly.\nTry moving it around slowly. Think clearly of the movement you want it to make.\nAt first a few inches is all you can manage at a time, but with practice it'll get better. Another good excercise for beginners is to make it shrink and grow slightly in size. Adding and removing the amount of energy in an evocation is a basic \ntool that is key for the later stages of learning.\nOnce you can comfortably manipulate the size and movement of the wisp with relative freedom, you can start to attempt shaping it. Simple geometrical shapes such as cubes, spheres and cylinders \nare the easiest to achieve and you should start there.\nImagine the arcane energy taking the desired shape with as much detail as possible. Do not lose focus once the evocation has taken the desired shape or it will become amorphous again.\nThis is the end of this book. Hopefuly this will help many students to complement their learning of arcane evocation.\nA book dedicated to advanced students and even novice arcanists will be written in the future.\nThank you very much for reading my book and I hope you found it helpful.\n[!]What appears to be a drawing of a chibi dark elf in robes giving the reader a thumbs up lies in the bottom half of this page.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Evocation", "Salendys", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-        Arcane\n      Evocation\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nThis book was written to help students and aspiring students of arcane evocation to better understand this magic and ease their learning.\n\nWritten by: -Salendys\nChapter 1: What is Arcane Evocation?\n                           \n\nArcane Evocation is the art of drawing pure magical energy from the void. It can then be shaped as anything the mage can think of. This is a creative form of magic\nwith mostly artistical uses. While it is possible to use this magic in combat, only a skilled arcanist can do so, and even then it is not as strong as the other types of evocation. If your intention is to acquire a means of dealing damage, then this is\nnot the magic for you.\nChaper 2:\nArcane Energy\n                           \n\nArcane energy is a rare element. In fact, it does not exist naturally in the world. It is an ethereal substance almost exclusive to the void. Because of this, Arcane Evocation is\nthe most difficult type of evocation to learn.\nAs with all other types of evocation, one must fully understand the element that is being evoked. The only way to study arcane energy is by observing an evocation of someone who already knows this magic.\nThis means it is practically impossible to learn without a teacher.\n\nNow, for those who already have a teacher and seek to complement their lessons with further knowledge, the arcane element can be described as follows.\nIn it's purest form, arcane energy is invisible, shapeless, odorless, completely inhert and very volatile. It can be compared to air or smoke, having a similiar composition than most gaseous substances.\nThose who have observed evocations may have noticed\na fine, thin mist surrounding them. This is because it isn't a single mass. It is in fact a conglomeration of countless tiny wisps of energy that together give the illusion of being a single object.\nSmoke is perhaps the thing that visually resembles\narcane energy the most in our world. Studying its shapeless and volatile nature may be of big help to understand arcane energy.\nChapter 3: Aura\n                           \n\nAura is a field of mana that surrounds living beings. More complex beings, such as descendants, have a colour associated to their aura. Each individual has their own colour for their aura.\nSome believe that the colour depends on one's personality. This isn't always the case, however, and anyone may have any colour.\nThis colour doesn't change, unless other forces somehow manage to tamper with your aura, which is usually very bad.\nAuras are very relevant to Arcane Evocation in particular.\nWhen raw arcane energy is drawn from the void, it instantly mixes with the mage's aura, making it visible and giving it colour. It is a common misconception to assume that arcane evocationists\nmanipulate aura itself. In truth, it is simply the product of mixing aura with arcane energy that is being manipulated, not the actual aura.\nAnd no, arcanists cannot see other people's aura or make it visible.\nAura is a very personal thing, like\nyour own soul.\nThis means your evocations can never mix with someone elses, or other types of evocation.\nChapter 4: Beginner steps\n                           \n\nAfter you have managed your first evocation, there is not much you can do. You will only be capable of producing a small wisp and hold it for a short time. The best thing to\ndo is to keep practicing. With each successful attempt you will be able to hold the wisp a little longer. Make sure to have rested enough to be completely recovered after each attempt.\nEventually you will be able to hold your wisp for about five minutes.\n[!] A detailed drawing of a wisp hovering over an open hand occupies most of this page.\nAt that point you'll get enough time to figure out how to get your wisp to do things. You are in control of your evocation, but must learn to control it properly.\nTry moving it around slowly. Think clearly of the movement you want it to make.\nAt first a few inches is all you can manage at a time, but with practice it'll get better. Another good excercise for beginners is to make it shrink and grow slightly in size. Adding and removing the amount of energy in an evocation is a basic\ntool that is key for the later stages of learning.\nOnce you can comfortably manipulate the size and movement of the wisp with relative freedom, you can start to attempt shaping it. Simple geometrical shapes such as cubes, spheres and cylinders\nare the easiest to achieve and you should start there.\nImagine the arcane energy taking the desired shape with as much detail as possible. Do not lose focus once the evocation has taken the desired shape or it will become amorphous again.\nThis is the end of this book. Hopefuly this will help many students to complement their learning of arcane evocation.\n\nA book dedicated to advanced students and even novice arcanists will be written in the future.\nThank you very much for reading my book and I hope you found it helpful.\n\n[!]What appears to be a drawing of a chibi dark elf in robes giving the reader a thumbs up lies in the bottom half of this page.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Magic", "Gallidron Elindrow", "An\n       Encyclopedic\n         Arcanum\n~````````````````:'''''''''''''''''~\n             ;O;\n    a guide to magic\n           `.{0},'\n\n             By\n   Gallidron  Elindrow\nWhat is magic? To undertand the intricacies of the acrane we must first understand this basic question.\nTo some magic is a miracle that cannot be explained, to others it is a science that can be disected and recorded. In fact it is somehwere in between.\nMagic can produce wonderous effects when used properly, and it can be horribly malicious when malpracticed.  It is not the belief of this author that magic has feelings or desires of its own, but the void from where it originates can be rather harsh on\nlife. Or so I have been told.\n\nMagic is inherently dangerous and should only be attempted by the well studied and practiced.\nBasic Spell Crafting\n         Theory\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The idea behind magic is terribly simple. Formulate in detail the spell you desire in your mind and then pull the desired effect from the void using the mana that exists in all of us. This is,\nhowever, much more difficult and complicated in practice. To have the mental prowess and fortitude to formulate the spell EXACTLY as you need it is a daunting task in and of itself. This action is in fact creating the desired spell IN the void! Consider,\nif you will, your consiousness traveling into the hostillity of the void and there creating a spell, that if performed incorrectly, could kill you. It can all at once fill you with awe and terror.\nIt is also important to note that if one attempts a\nspell that is out of their respective league, the energy required could cause serious and sometimes perminant damage to the user.\nThe Schools of Magic\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Herein I shall list the schools of known magic and offer a description of its form and function so far as I am able.\nArcane Magic\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Arcane magic is the most wide spread magic in the world. It is the most written about, the most studied and the most practiced. It is that which is primarily drawn from the void and has several schools of use.\nTransmutation\n`````````````````````````\nThis kind of magic is the most like a science. One must study and understand to a great degree that which they wish to transmute. They must also understand that which they desire to transmute the item in\nquestion into. Further more you must be able to see the item. There are a few rules that one must follow as well. Namely that one cannot transmute that which is alive, nor can you make too great a change. For example, iron cannot be made into water as\nthey do not share an element, nor are they in the same physical state. Also there must be an equivilent exchange. A pound of stone may not become ten pounds of silver.\nEnchantment\n~~~~~~~~~~\nA usefull kind of magic, and one that must be performed at an enchantment table.\nUsing this school, one may imbue objects with spells and magical properties. \n\nTo do this, one needs a Mana Gem. These gems can be made of\nany mineral, but they need to be, at least, roughly gem shaped and polished or engraved. The larger and more highly valued the gem, the more mana that can be stored therein. You can then use the Mana Gem to fuel the enchantment. Enchanted items need to be\nrecharged or the enchantment will lose power and fail.\nWards and Abjuration\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIn all magic, mana is used to manifest the void born spell in the physical world. This is commonly refered to as a mana anchor. The purpose of a ward or an abjuration is to disrupt the mana anchor and thus\ndestroy the spell. A ward is used more like a shield, to stop incoming spells. An abjuration is used in a more offensive way. For example and abjuration could be hurled at a spell to disrupt it, rather than to wait for it to come to you.\nBoth must be used to counter act specific kinds of magic. A ward used to deflect a fireball cannot also dispell and illusion. Each ward and abjuration must be tailored to that which it is meant to stop.\nIt is also important to note that a spell which is\nmore powerful than the ward or abjuration will be unaffected. A working knowledge of the kind of magic to be disrupted must be had in order to produce an effective counter spell.\nTelekinesis\n~~~~~~~~~\nThis is a simple form of magic. Essentially it is the use of ones mind to lift or manipulate objects without the use of hands or other physical means.\nVoid Translocation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nNow this is an interesting form of magic. The idea is to disolve an object into the void to be recalled at a later time. However, to do this one must have a perfect memory of the object in order to reform it later and\npull it back into reality.\nHowever, an argument is to be made that the object in question is gone forever and that what ever you pull from the void is just a replica of varying quality depending of the memory of the caster.\nElemental Evocation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis kind of magic is the flashy kind that everyone thinks of when talking about mages. Be it hurling a fire ball or calling down a bolt of lightning, all of this is evocation. Allow me to list the types there of.\nFire\n`'`'`'`'\nThis kind of evocation can be used to summon flame, smoke and light. It can also increase the rate at which alchemy functions. However, it is important to note that the flame evocationist is not immune to the heat of their own spells.\nWater\n~~~~~\nTo create water and control its forms is a powerful kind of evocation. Ice magic tends to be more highly sought after, but one usually learns water evocation in the process. Drinking summoned water is somewhat useless as it will vanish\nfrom the ingester's system when the spell ends.\nAir\n===)))\n\nThe most unused form of evocation because its known uses are few and the control gained is tenuous at best. There are legends of powerfull air mages who could whip up storms and the like, but these are just myths.\nElectric\n********\nThis kind of evocation is immensly powerful, but can be hard to control. The devistating attacks that are unleashed by the electric evocator are almost impossible to evade, but do take time to charge up. It is also good to note\nthat once released, magic lightning behaves as regular lightning. If there are high amounts of metal near by, the bolt may veer off in that direction.\nArcanism\n^v^v^v^v^\nThis refers to evocation of all kinds. It also includes the creation of glass like energy barriers that defend against magical and physical attack.\nThese barriers have no effect on mental or illusion magic.\nConjuration\n%%%%%%%%%%%\n\nTo conjure one must have an understanding of both biology and botany depending on that which they wish to summon.\nMorphon, is the name given to the art of summoning creatures. These magical constructs can be\ncombinations of many creatures, so long as the conjuration can function and live. \n\nPerrenial conjuration is used to summon plants, and once again, the summoned plant must make scientific sense. \nThere are historical instances of mages conjuring\nplant/creatures, though these are highly complicated to make.\nThe final and perhaps most difficult form of conjuration is Primordial. This melds the magics of evocation and conjuration into a powerful elemental. This kind of magic requires a fine\ndegree of control and much power to even attempt.\n\nConjuration is a delicate and time consuming form of magic that cannot be done on the fly. One must be prepared and have time to focus when summoning even the most simple constructs. These\nconjured entities are temporary in their nature, and only last so long as they have a supply of mana from their conjuror.\nIllusion\n-*-*-*-\nCreating false images and sounds are just the surface of the school of illusion. Indeed a talented illusionist can trick any of the five senses, even touch. If an illusion is unbelievable however, it will break.\nA branch of illusion is Cognitism. This is used to trick the mind into being more productive than usual. The applications of this kind of illusion are many, but they are delicate.\nThe third branch of illusion is mental magic. This involves entering the\nmind of another and actually influencing their thoughts. One can alter what another sees, hears, smells and touches as well as what they may think.\nOther Forms of Magic\n###################\n\nThere are, of course, more forms of magic than I have explored here. Most notably Deity Magic, Alchemy and Dark Magic. These will each be covered in later additions to my series of guides.\nConclusion\n~~~~\\,,,,,,,,,,,;,,,,,,,,,,,/~~~~\n\nIt is my hope that this guide has helped you to gain a basic understanding of what each of the Arcane Schools has to offer. To actually learn magic, one should seek out a teacher. Van'ayla my dear\nreaders and my you ever seek to gain knowledge throughout all of your days.\n\n-Gallidron Elindrow\n\nPublishing date\n9th of Amber Cold\n1514\nLook for my next book!\n\n\"The Power of Prayer\"\na guide to deity magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Puppetry", "Nienna Calm", "Arcane\n     Puppetry\n            \n            O\n           -|-\n            ^\n           ***\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Nienna Calm\nA Foreword\n-------------------Dear Reader,\nMagic is an incredible thing, a wonderous art form through which the imaginary becomes real. However, there are many who would rather only use it as a tool to advance their own power. They are only-\n-Half right. Magic, especially Void magic, is indeed a tool to be used in the same way a carpenter would use a saw, but no true power will ever come of it. We live in a world where the mage is distrusted in every corner of the globe. We are Discriminated,\n-hated for our unique persepective on reality. It is a touched life we walk; Do not embark on this trek lightly.\n\n             O\n            -|-\n             ^\nWhat Is\nArcane Puppetry?\n-------------------*Everything on the topic is listed here*\n\n((Link: https://goo.gl/9qEdyA ))\n\n*You should definitely read this to learn the magic*\nCreating Your\n  Arcane Puppet\n-------------------A properly made Arcane Puppet is a complicated piece of machinery, on par with a Golem or a Obelisk in complexity. In order for a puppet to function, every piece of the Marionette's makeup\nis specially enchanted with telekinetic mechanisms that allow it to move of its own accord. This process might seem straightforward at first, but as the puppet becomes more lifelike, hundreds of small enchantments will end up overlapping and at times\nconflicting with one another just to operate simple movements. More than ten enchantments may be working in unison for an arcane puppet to simply walk on a flat plane.\n\nNaturally, because of this complex design, only a skilled Enchanter\ncan create a puppet for you. If you know the magic yourself already, well, this portion of learning just got easier for you. If not, expect to be indebted to one handsomely quite soon.\nHere is a list of what Enchantments Any Arcane puppet Should Have:\n\n@-A telekinetic Enchantment for every component of the puppet.\n\n@-A special visual enchantment that allows one to see(*)\n@-(Optional) An illusionary enchant to allow one to speak through the puppet.\n\n@- An overall Alterational modification to make the Clay puppet light enough to use.\n(*)- Creating the visual enchantment can be achieved through a cursory study of Soul Puppetry. Since the heart of Arcane puppetry is the connection of the soul to an enchanted puppet, some special enchantments like this one can be preformed, where\notherwise it would be impossible for a void mage to enchant such.\nConnecting to the\n  Arcane Puppet\n-------------------\n\nAs with all arcane magic, first, connect your mind to the void.\n\nThrough the void, connect to your Arcane puppet, and imagine yourself inside of it. Imagine that you-\nyourself /are/ the puppet, with a whole seperate mind, body, and life. Through this method, one is able to connect to a completed Arcane Puppet.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Relays", "Gregory", "Arcane Relays\n\nLong Distance Voidal\n      Communication\n\n\n\n  By\nGregory O'Donovan\nThis book is a publication of §§§§Gregory Press.\n\nAll Rights Reserved.\n\n1647.\n[!]\n\nThe first few pages would be filled with various blueprints, detailing the exact specifications and enchantments required to create an Arcane Relay.\n\n           §§[!]\nChapter 1\n        The Theory\n\nThe premise of this device is to allow mages to communicate with one another over extremely long distances, however instead of merely acting as a replacement for a bird it provides\nthe unique opportunity to see one another.\n\nThe process starts with a inscribed focus crystal being placed upon the third pillar, this forms a unique 'address' to which another device is able to communicate. Following such the mage allows mana to\nflow through a process of minor enchantment and in doing so triggers the \"inherent\" bind to the void seen within focus crystals. \n\nThis allows the image to be almost 'cast' into the void, and due to the opposing pillar having the same pattern it is able\nto navigate the chaotic maze and be received upon the opposing end.\n\nNevertheless the construct is made of three pillars, so far we're able to send the image but we've nothing to present it upon. Henceforth by using an adapted form of the holocron/lexicon\narcane engineering first thought up by Kalameet the second pillar takes upon the image and stores it, and the final pillar through utilization of the holocron is able to take the received image and project it visually. \n\nWhilst the image isnt\nperfect and can often find itself distorted, it still offers a tangible means of long-range visual communication.\nChapter 2\n      The Process\n\nIn order to construct one of these, three main materials are used; aurum, focus crystals and ruibruim. \n\nThe pillars themselves are a wooden base with aurum spirals leading upwards and towards\nthe focus crystal placed atop. If you find the focus crystal to become damaged then avoid using it, not only will it fail to serve its purpose but injecting mana into it would potentially cause it to become volatile and shatter. \n\nThe focus crystals\nthemselves are carefully inscribed with various sigils (which can be seen within the blueprints) to generate the private chanel within the Arcane Relay's closed system of communication. \n\nThe rubirum must be processed into two\ndifferent forms, a dust and also a chalk. The dust is used within the focusing lenses and metal bands leading up the pillar, whilst the processed rubrium chalk marks each pylon position and connects them together, helping enable  the enchantments to flow\nbetween the pylons with greater ease.\n\nAll together this will allow the arcane relay to project a black/white image through the void. Its purposes are many, including potential combined research efforts for labs that are within differing\ncities. \n\nThere is also the possibility to potentially replace the need for a mage with a mana gem/obelisk, however further research would need to be conducted before I'm able to confirm the application of this method.\nWhilst it is useful for long range communication, the current design is rather bulky and difficult to move around. Typically I'd advise it remain stagnant. \n\nIt also is a more complicated piece of arcane engineering,\ntaking some time to perfect and understand. Even now the full application of its uses go beyond my own knowledge as one of its inventors, however there may be potential beyond its seemingly simple communicative purposes.\n§§((OOC))\n\nFor further information, the lore is available at; \n\nhttps://www.lordofthecraft.net/forums/topic/138883-arcane-engineering-arcane-relay/", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane: Overview", "Friedrich", "A Brief Overview\n- = - = - = - = - = -\nIn the following tome there will be many words thrown about. Vocabulary not normally put into normal conversation. Take care to read everything carefully so as to not make errors - walking foolishly into magic\nwill very easily get you killed, or worse.\nAlteration\n- = - = - = - = - = -\nAlteration magics are used to, as the name suggests, alter the physical world to the Caster's pleasing. There are many ways this is done - be it through teleportation with Voidal Shifting, creating magical items\nthrough the art of transfiguration, or simply reshaping and manipulating already existing elements. The magics under this category are: Voidal Shifting, Voidal Translocation, Transfiguration, as well as Arcane Feeling. Each serve their own purpose.\nEvocation\n- = - = - = - = - = -\nVoidal Evocation is much more than just elemental evocations, as most believe it to be. As a basis, there is Air, Earth, Water, Fire, and Lightning Evocations. These are the creation of the basic elements in the shape of\nthe Caster's will. This can be used in offense or defense. There is also arcane evocation, the summoning of wisps of energy in which the Caster may form into whatever they'd like. This could be to make shields, beams, weapons, tools, or perhaps simply\nart. Following this there is Conjuration, the rarest voidal magic. It involves the temporary creation of life, be it plants or animals, under the control of the Caster. This could be used with other evocations to make energy based creatures if so desired.\nIt should be noted that the creation of descendant races through conjuration is considered taboo, given the fact that to create something you must know and study it through multiple deaths and disection. It will get you treated like a dark magi.\nIllusion\n- = - = - = - = - = -\nThis archetype focuses on the ability to toy with minds, with only two specific forms of magic under it. The first, sensory illusion, involves the creation of sounds and images to the Caster's pleasing among large groups\nof people, or simply one if they wished. They could form lifelike mimics, though when they become larger a few distortions may give away the trick. They could force a tired sensation over an area, though it could be easily fought against. Mental mages are\nconsidered far more dangerous due to their ability to delve directly into the mind of those they chose, though only one at a time. They can force illusions over a singular person, though they must be believable or the illusion will instantly vanish. When\ncasting, it is a common misinterpretation to believe that a mental mage forces images and memories from their victims. Instead, they simply place a thought into their target's mind through the use of magic or mundane speaking. They view anything that you\nare thinking of at the time. For instance, if you were to hear about the man you murdered while a mental mage was connected to you, more than likely your instant thought would be of the fact that you murdered him, even if you tried not to think of it.\nThis is how mental mages find out their information. Learn more on how to protect yourself against mental mages in our other book, Mental Defenses.", ""),
        StaticBook("Archive No. 1", "Karvos'sol Drakon", "KEY STONE DISTRIBUTION NOTES\nBy: Lord Scribe (of the Vaeyl Order) Daefyn.\n--------------\nBlue Keystone:\nKorth of Yrodholm\n(Knight of 1st Banner)\nStationed in Bight Archway Outpost.\n\nRed Keystone:\nLyren of Endmoor\n(Mage of\n4th Banner)\nStationed in Yrodholm.\n\nYellow Keystone:\nRovind of Endmoor\n(Mage of 4th Banner)\nStationed in Thandvar.\n\nGreen Key:\nKorine of Endmoor\n(Mage of 4th Banner)\nImprissoned by Staves of Endmoor.\nNavy Keystone:\nGyrand of Kahaer\n(Scout of 3rd Banner)\nLost travelling the Darkways.\n\nPurple Keystone:\nUven of Sevenna\n(Knight of 2nd Banner)\nLost in the battle of Kal'Riad.\nBlack Keystone:\nHaevolt of Yrodholm\n(Commander of 4th Banner)\nLocation Unknown.\n(Last hope is a start.)\n\nKey Words:\nThe Archway\nYrodholm\nThandvar\nEndmoor\nThe Darkways\nKal'Riad\nHaevolt - Lasthope\nSerrimor", ""),
        StaticBook("Aspect Stones", "Leyun Kameki", "A Description of the Sacred Stones and Their Properties\n\nA tome written by the Song Druid\nThe Sacred Stones of the Aspects are powerful Artifacts associated with the Druids. There is believed to be three, one for each of the figurehead Aspects and a third that binds them together. They are large, rounded square-ish boulders that each are a\ndifferent colour; Blue for Cerridwen, Silver for Cernunnos, and black for the binder. They are very heavy, but one person could transport one stone on his own. The three together however have known to require at least 3 people to carry a chest with them\nin it. And once the Stones are close enough they magnetize, though this effect is only present when all three are together it seems.\n\nThe stones emit a powerful aura of Druidic Energy. Together the three stones can prevent\ncorruption of any kind from breaching the perimeter of the grove they are in. Indeed, just one has enough power to stop corruption for up to twenty feet, but together their power is much larger. The stones have been known to give visions to those who\ntouch them, and help aid Druids on paths to enlightenment through their pulsating auras.\n\nSymbolically the stones represent the completion of the Order. Each one represents an Aspect, and are thought to have been molded by the Aspects\nthemselves. To possess something touched by the Aspects is beyond blessed to the Druids. Even when broken down the stones seem to emit light Druidic energy even centuries after their crumbling.\nIt is rumored the the Order remains in possession of the Stone Dust that was once the Great Aegis Stones.", ""),
        StaticBook("AssignmentReport", "Alexander Falkenrath", "-*Simularities*-\n\nSocial---\n-Able to maintain a steady population in the city at all times\n-Facilities for all to use (Tavern,Campfire etc)\n\nEnviromental---\n-Lots of wildlife and plants\n-Calm area most of the time, Able to be\ndealt with if gets out of control.\nEconomical---\n-Plenty of market stalls selling tools and food etc.\n-Plenty of houses to bring in tax revenue.\n-Facilities bringing in decent amounts of mina.\n-*Differences*-\n\nSocial---\n-Cyrilsburg has a more active community with events.\n-Haense has more of an keep to yourself community, not many people talk to one another, Just stand around watching. Compared to Cyrilsburg which has a family for a community,\neveryone knows each other and respect each other as a human being.\n-Haense guard force never really on display, leaving them open for attacks/raids. Compared to Cyrilsburg where there is often a parade/patrol of military patrol going round.\n-Haense gate is ALWAYS open whereas Cyrilsburg gate is often being watched or manned compared to haense which doesnt have anyone watching who comes in and out of the grounds.\n-Cyrilsburg tends to have more fights/arguements compared to Haense where\neveryone stays civil and is the occasional rucus.\nEnviromental---\n-Haense walls larger but easy to get access to ledges on the side of the walls. whereas Cyrilsburg Walls are small but effective.\n-Takes longer to travel too haense yet easier to\nfind, compared to Cyrilsburg which is quicker to get too yet hidden away in the fields.\n-Cyrilsburg has directions starting from half way between Cloud Temple and Cyrilsburg and Haense has directions all around the surrounding area, including from the\nCloud temple.\nEconmical---\n-Cyrilsburg has a wider range of wares and the help from the falkenrath household which are master merchants, Though Haense has the occasional stall dotted about owned by however willing to pay for it, most of the stalls however\nare unowned in Haense.\n-Haense Tavern hasn't got an open range of drinks up for sale like the Tavern in Cyrilsburg which is owned by a Military Personal, It has a range of drinks on offer 24/7 for a good price.\nHaense And Cyrilsburg Report - 10th of Malin' Welcome, 1691\n\nSigned by Alexander Falkenrath.\n***IGNORE THIS PAGE***", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul I", "March Ash", "These pillars of shale. They remind me of the sea-traps the old druids would summon. Hidden spikes of rock, just beneath the waterline, to gouge apart the hulls of ships that wandered too close to our hidden sanctuaries. Some of the sailors would survive,\nadrift at sea. Many would drown, or die of exposure and thirst. Most would eventually drink saltwater and turn mad. Weeks later, we would go out on rafts, and capture the survivors for sacrifice. I remember their screams and curses so vividly.\nUpon the pyre, they would pray to their gods for salvation. There was never an answer.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul IV", "March Ash", "It can take ten thousand years for a stream to carve a new valley. But it will still do so, it has an endless resolve. It is difficult to truly grasp the immensity of generational time, let alone geological time.\nNot even in the histories of a hundred families will the mountains grow a meter, but they will still grow.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul IX", "March Ash", "And here lay the corpses of titans which once walked the world, and which will soon walk it again. I only pray that they are on our side in the war to come, rather than with those who oppose all life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul V", "March Ash", "Here, at the edge of Axios, it would be so easy to build a boat and leave. To abandon the descendants to their terrible fate, and to abandon the land to the wrath of the Aspects. To leave, and never return. But I have a mission.\nI cannot leave until it is complete.", ""),
        StaticBook("Asul VI", "March Ash", "Long ago, there were stories passed around by the bone druids. About how, one day, a great tree would be born from the breeding together of every tree throughout all ecology, in all time. An avatar of nature, who would crush the world beneath its roots.\nThis was before they were shunned from their order, after it was discovered that they murdered their Archdruid and burned his organs in the pyre to receive visions from the Aspects. Sometimes I wonder if their stories were true.", ""),
        StaticBook("Atheran Uruks V1", "Temür Törs Ajedh'raq", "Betrayal of the             Uzg\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWritten and Recorded\nby\n\nTemür Törs Ajedhraq\nRider of the Subudai\nThe Uzg of the Uruks, centered in the Goi, San-Vitar, of the new world, Athera, had experienced a unity un-paralleled in recent history.  In the Goi, the clans Gorkil, Lur, Yar, Kog, Magra, and various others coexisted.  This unity is attributed to the\nRex Malog'Yar.  A wise and powerful Shaman, Malog'Yar enacted reform among Uruk culture to bring the Uzg into the forefront of the politics of Athera.  Under these reforms, stricter codes of honor were introduced, which elevated the Uruks from a looseknit\nculture of raiders to a unified culture based on code-of-law. These reforms, though, drew harsh criticism from some of the Uruks, especially from the Azog clan.  \n\nThe Azogs, already dissatisfied with the Uzg's hostility towards Raine Academy, was\npushed further from their brothers.  Tensions were heightened between the Uzg and the Azogs.\n\nAt this time, another perilous threat arose to challenge the Uzg.  An Uruk, by the name of Zogrocka, had risen to immense power through the wicked\nand vile means of Dark Shamanism (a topic I will fully explain in the Expanded History of the Uruks).  Under Zogrocka's leadership\nthe ancient and exiled clan Dom rose again.  The Doms were a clan dedicated to Dark Shamanism, that fell out of Krug's gr\ndue to their trickery and abuse of spirits and elementals.  They also offended the Uzgs and other nations through their abominable practice of cannibalism.  Justly, the Uzgs hunted down and executed the Doms in earlier times.\n\nThe rise of the Doms\ncoincided with the split of the Azogs and the Uzg.  In the Azogs, the Doms saw an army to enforce their corrupt ways.  In the Doms, the Azogs saw a means to achieve power and claim the Uzg for themselves.  \n\nDespite the Uzg offering complete\nand total amnesty to the Azogs upon their return to the Uzg, the Azogs forsook Krug and the Spirits in favor of the dreadful\nDoms.  Making a deal with the patron Spirit of the Dark Shamans, Ixli, the Azogs traded parts of their sanity for the corruptin\npower enjoyed by the Doms.\n\nNow combined, the Doms and the Azogs sacked San'Vitar, the Uruk's 'Old City'.  At first, the unholy alliance encountered little resistance and many Uruks of the Uzg were slaughtered.  A joint force of Uruks and\nHumans were unable to repel the assailants later on.  The Goi was left severely debilitated following the attack.\n\nAfter the attack, the desperate Uruks pleaded the spirits for guidance.  In an odd series of events, the Uruks were given\nassistance.  Following the shrieks of an injured scaddernack, the Uruks discovered a cave where the spirit Veist revealed itself to them.  Veist pledged its support against the Azogs and the Doms, but in return, the Uzg's High Shaman, Brunhyldir,\nwas morphed into a Goblin.\n\nIt was in this frail form that the High Shaman Brunhyldir confronted the Dark Shaman Zogrocka.  Alone, the two battled, drawing upon the Mojo that the Spirits granted them (whether that be honorably as\nin Brunhyldir's case, or dishonorable, in Zogrocka's).  The honor and the strength of the High Shaman prevailed, and the abhorrent and corrupt Zogrocka was defeated.\n\nLeft without a leader, the Doms were weakened.  The Azogs\nfollowing Zogrocka's defeat then attempted to gain power by their own means.\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nOn the 6th of the Lunar Cycle of Sun's Smile, in the year 1471, I, Temür Törs Ajedh'raq, was witness to the following events that occurred in San'Vitar.\n\nThe Azogs, unable to gain power through the corruption of Ixli and the Doms, arrived\nat the Goi armed and armored.  They approached the Rex in his Blarg and demanded the Rexdom under threat of force.\n\nIt is notable that by Uruk custom, which has been observed for generations, the Rex may be challenged to an 'honor klomp', in\nwhich the Rex and the Challenger fight for the title and position of Rex.  These fights generally occur unarmed and unarmored.  With that said, it is also of worth to note that the Azogs, in no way, shape, or form, challenged the Rex honorably to such a\nfight.\n\nThe Azogs' justification for such demands were that the current Rex was weak, and the Uzg was crumbling.  They came to the Goi claiming they could make it strong again.\n\nTo justify their for-\n-saking Krug and the Spirits, they claimed that the dark powers of Zogrocka had made them servants of the Dark Shamans.  Despite there being a lack of Azog Shamans at the confrontation, the Azog clan claimed to have made amends with the Spirits.  This\nblatant lie is further discredited by the presence of Dom Shamans accompanying the Azog party.\n\nFor two days, the Azogs and their Dom Shamans held the Rex.\nTheir terms: the Rexdom and the Uzg, or war.  For two days the Rex held out and\nattempted to reason with the Uruks made unreasonable through\nIxli's Bargain.\n\nOn the 8th of the Lunar Cycle of Sun's Smile, in the year 1471, the Azogs departed the Goi as enemies of the Uzg.  With their coup-de-tat failed, they returned to\ntheir fort without the Uzg in their command.  Both sides, immediately following the encounter, started to strike alliances with other nations and factions.  The Uruks of the Uzg appealing to those who uphold honor, and who wish to maintain orderly law\nthroughout Athera.  And the splinter Azogs, appealing to those who would rather there be the vile corruption of chaos unleashed upon the land.", ""),
        StaticBook("Atlas I", "Dorlan Galonval", "3rd of Malin's welcome\n           ~1668~\nI met Alphonse D'eril, a big valah standing at about 7ft, uncommon for a valah, he is very friendly and apparently he was part of some kind of big crew.\n4th of Malin's Welcome\n          ~1668~\nI heard about some dark-skinned tali'bortuan, apparently they're bandits. They like to attack kharajyrs.\n5th of Malin's Welcome\n          ~1668~\nI found that strange tali'bortu, she seems a male, she told me that her eyes suddenly became her, and her hairs white for stress. She seems to be banned from Holm, she killed someone, as i expected, she is-\n- crazy.\nShe usually does some creepy smiles, probably she wants to scare others.\n6th of Malin's welcome\n         ~1668~\nI met a mali'aheral who wants to become a druid, he lives in Arbor, that city full of strange people.\nMore info about that tali'bortuii: she greets some people with a creepy smile, and others with a\nnormal smile. That's to that mali'aheral i knew that she wasn't always like that, but she changed in a long period of time, perhaps some kind of broken relations...?\nShe also has a strange feeling about me, wonder what does she means... she finds me\ninteresting, i wonder why.\nA big valah entered the tavern, apparently he has some psychological disease due to him saying only 'Hullo'.\nI should be careful around him.\nThe giant valah yote a chair leg to that tali'bortuii, hitting her.\n8th of Malin's Welcome\n           ~1668~\nSome bandits called \"Reivers\" attacked us, they hurt my left shoulder, it will be fine in a month or so.\nAfter that they offered us to join them, I refused as i don't want anything from them after that.\n9th of Malin's Welcome\n           ~1668~\nWe returned to Holm, stopping at the tavern to get some ale. We had the opportunity to know better the tavernkeep, Tsisha, a kind iari kharajyr who recently had 2 adorable kittens. Apparently some kind of dwarves\nare trying to cause trouble in the tavern, because they don't like kharajyrs working at Holm for some minas.\n10th of Malin Welcome\n         ~1668~\nMorgan Hallowfall, he might teach me something about electrical evocation, i can find him in Dominion or in Holm sometimes, i need to find him.\n-------------------Later that day, we headed to Santegia, we\nfound a goblin, a master shipwright, he will build us a ship for 7000 mina... that's alot, but we will find them.\n7th of The Grand Harvest\n          ~1668~\nWe went in Arbor again, that strange city full of strange people, i was quite surprised to find Tsisha, the tavernkeep of Holm, in Arbor's port with Maya, the strange tali'bortu'ii...\nShe told me something\nabout \"shades\", i wonder what are they...\n3rd of Sun's Smile\n          ~1668~\nA long nose bandit is around, my llir Ragvaldur told me that, after he fought him, that bandit got scared and wanted to escape, but there was that irongut who didn't want to spare him, the irongut died. I might\nstart to find some informations about this long nose bandit.\nApparently he met him near the Dragur library, near some banners, i should look there.\n4th of Sun's Smile\n           ~1668~\nA little child came in the tavern, asking us for some moneys, he has no haelun or maln, perhaps they died... or worse they abandoned him. Rag gave him a small bag of 15 mina, surprising from him.\n5th of Sun's Smile\n           ~1668~\nAn interesting conversation with a lady i already saw somewhere... talking about war, kings, citizens... it's very interesting to hear that lady thoughts, as she seems very clever and informed about things in\nthis land.\n-------------------More info about that tali'bortu'ii: She changed her name in Maya, her name was Hiro. She is learning dark magic, it's better to stay away from her, but I still want to know about her.\nShe killed Tsisha, surprising...\nShe changed 3 times, first being Hiro, then Maya... and now what she is now.\nShe got banished from Holm, executed one time, the other time she managed to escape.\nThe creepy smiles and faces are caused by that dark magic... She\nhad a scar on her fa\n~--~Quick note~--~\nShades: aspects of dark magic, apparently someone can become a shade and have incredible powers... scary.\n~--~--~--~--~--~\n6th of Sun's Smile\n          ~1668~\nUndeads... many undeads apparently... I must stay calm, there aren't undeads around... there is no meaning to be scared... no meaning to be scared...\n7th of Sun's Smile\n           ~1668~\nA strange individual enters the tavern, no face, wears a hood... perhaps to hide something, as i asked about his race, he refused to talk about it.\nHe doesn't seem a valah, neither a mali, or a uruk...\nmaybe some suspicious race? I should find something about it.\n8th of Sun's Smile\n          ~1668~\nSurprising, another mali'fenn on this land, i'm glad to know that i'm not the only one, her name is Amber Rose, but she prefers to be called Frost. I hope that she doesn't get so much hate as I got, just for\nbeing a mali'fenn. She seems calm, but i really don't know as i talked to her just not for long, maybe i can try to know her better... Hoping that i don't seem a pervert, of course.\n\nAnyways, it seemed that she wanted to avoid me, sadly.\n12th of Sun's Smile\n           ~1668~\n-Informations about Maya-\nShe has voices in her head... they tell her to kill or to act, but she ignores them. They are voices of people she loved. She refused to tell me who are those people, she then\ntold me that she didn't want to answer more question today... what a behaviour, but still it's understandable.\nAfter going away, she told me that \"curiousity is deadly\", i guess she wants to scare me... she still isn't able to use dark magic, so it's safe\n-------------------Ragvaldur is insulting someone... again, the persone he is insulting is a iari valah, apparently she was a sailor, a very good one.\nShe is insulting him aswell, an insult competition, nice, Rag seems in difficulty against her.\nFinally someone that teaches him a lesson.\n5th of Amber's Cold\n           ~1668~\nI noted... strange banners appeared in this land, some of them had a sign saying 'Atlas is not your home'... perhaps someone that wants back this land? Good things we're going to get a ship soon.\nI see... Alphonse, the big valah, and Ragvaldur are really incompatible, me and Tsisha passed the day to stop them so they don't start any fight... but anyways, they're going to fight outside the tavern... i hope that Alphonse teaches him a lesson like\nthat lady he met in Arbor did.\n6th of Amber's Cold\n          ~1668~\nRagvaldur and Alphonse's voices woke me up, they were shouting, until they unsheated their weapons... i managed to calm down Rag, and Tsisha calmed down Alphonse... i don't want to be banished from this city.\n7th of Amber's Cold\n           ~1668~\nI was able to know Amber Rose, also called Frost, she recently started her journey in Atlas, we talked here in the tavern, and i can confirm that she is a calm mali'fenn. \nWe headed to the Dragur Library, she wanted\nto know more about magic... everything was going fine until Maya arrived with that odd masked guy.\nThe first things that she asked me is if Amber is my wife... i can't explain how much i was embarrased.\nAnyways, she decided to learn water evocation...\na good choice i can say.\nThe atmosphere makes her tired, as she almost fell asleep on the counter, but i managed to keep her awake, i still don't know how, anyways, i passed a good day.\n9th of Amber's Cold\n          ~1668~\n-Maya's informations-\nWhen a family member makes a scar to another, it's tied with his soul, the scar bleeds when a D'eril feels an emotion he hates. When it bleeds it usually amplifies the feeling.\nMaya's scar got removed by an ascended, that's why she killed in Holm.\nShe likes darkness, that's why she wants to become a shade... i don't believe that's only for that.\nMaya got adopted by an old gentleman.\nWhen these 2 children appeared\nfrom nowhere... Maya's behaviour changed almost instantly, she became kind to them... right after pointed her sword to them, anyways, it seems too strange.\nWhen she became kind to them, she started to say 'Anna', maybe a friend, or her mother?\nThe children refused her as a mother...  really surprising... after having pointed a sword to them.\nWhen they refused her, she started to cry... blood? Mh, curious.\n3rd of the Deep Cold\n           ~1668~\nI assisted to a strange conversation... a iari mali talking about a beast... then she fell on the ground, dead. I wonder what is that beast...\n-------------------I returned to Holm that evening, finding again\nthat body... me and a farfolk Valah decided to put him in some kind of freezer, Alphonse carried it with an incredible strenght.\n~--~Quick note~--~\nThania: A place where i can find Morgan Hallowfall, i need to go left to Holm, going on the mountain.\n~--~--~--~--~--~\n4th of The Deep Cold\n           ~1668~\nJourney to Last Hope, I guess undeads live there... there was door after a long destroyed bridge.\nBig spikes of ice going out of the ice wall... what could that mean? Why is the door after the bridge closed?\n9th of The Deep Cold\n           ~1668~\nWe finally bought the ship, a total of 7750 minas, dwarven steam engine, a splendid ship. \n\nMeanwhile, Alphonse was fighting one of the Reivers outside... when he saw me after he that, he seemed angry...\n10th of Deep's Cold\n            ~1668~\nI talked with Vitalius, the odd doctor of Arbor... he isn't a bad person, he is close in himself, shy and he doesn't talk much. He needs to care about those 2 girls that Maya wanted to adopt, and it seems that\nhe is doing a good job.\n\n         -REMEMBER-\nDo not ask him about his mask or his parents, or he will not feel good, probably going in some panic attack...?\n         -REMEMBER-", ""),
        StaticBook("Atlas Pizza", "Seviln Atas", "Wahey there, 'friendly'\npeople of Atlas.\nThis is an advertisment for our new Pizza Delivery System. Our current menu goes like:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~-Erper's Delight 30mina\n-Flay Tears 35mina\n-Oren Blood 40mina\n-Norland's Fall 25mina\n-Edgy Cheese 35mina\n-Curonite Death 20mina\n-RP Default 20mina\n-Autoclickers 26mina\n-Suspicious Aim 45mina\n-Slice if Life RP 34mina\n-Ginger's Soul 50mina\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you are interested, send a bird to 'Avenue 36, Sutican Grave' and we'll send a delivery boy your way.", ""),
        StaticBook("ATLAS: Year 1666", "Kordenn Goldhand", "3d of the First Seed:\n\nI arrived at the Cloud Temple today. The weather is warmer than I am used to. I met a friendly human, who offered me to accompany to Kal'Tarak, the dwed capital city. The text I've read about the town don't do the town justice\nIt is a jewel, built inside a mountain. Words can't possibly describe its beauty.\nThe dwedmar living within were very hospitable, as soon as i set foot inside, a dwed invited me to a local tavern, and we discussed around a tankard of ale, as others joined\nthe discussion. I even met the High King! When I mentionned that I was looking to settle in Kal'Tarak, I was immediatly offered residence in a cosy appartment.\n4th of the First Seed\n\nToday I met with the Clan Father of the Goldhands, a family of merchants and jewellers. He offered me a job in the Kaz'Ulrah mines, an offer that I swiftly accepted, as I lost most of my belongings when I travelled to Atlas.\nI spent the rest of the day mining, and found the mines of Kal'Tarak to be quite rich in precious minerals!\n5th of the First Seed\n\nToday, on my way to the mines, I met a young dwed named Durar. He seemed lost, as he was shouting \"Ello!\" throughout the city, but he was just looking for company. He missed his ka'az, who left on a reconnaissance mission,\ndeep in elgus territory. He's a talkative one, but his heart is in the right place.\n8th of the First Seed\n\nI met Durar again. He was bored out of his mind, and wandered aimlessly through the city. He asked me to accompagny him on an \"adventure\". In hindsight, maybe I should have said no, as he brought me all around the countryside,\nfrom dwedmar to umrus lands. After a long and exhausting day of walking, we were back to Kal'Tarak.\n10th of the First Seed\n\nMost of my day was split between digging in the mines, and resting in the library. On the evening, I bumped into Dwifar, who suggested I speak to the Onyxheart Clanmother, in order to train as a smith. Searching for her,\nI stumbled on a crowd of dwedmar, surrounding an arena, cheering on the combatants. Inside, a fierce dwed, armed with a sword and a large shield, was fighting the largest wolf I had ever seen. After an intense fight, the wolf turned into Koralon, the\nClanmother of the Onyxhearts. Smiling ferociously, she shaked the hand of her opponent, and invited the crowd for some ale at the tavern. I must admit shamefully that I was too intimidated to ask her about the smithing job I initially came for.\n2nd of Malin's Welcome\n\nThe day is off to a bad start, as I woke up to the clamour of dwedmar arguing, and my chest emptied out. A robber looted some of the homes in the appartment district. I am quite disgruntled, as yesterday's bounty was especially\ngood.\n4th of Malin's Welcome\n\nI met Durar again, all bloodied up. He told me taht he met with a pack of dire wolves on his way to Kal'Tarak. He barely got out alive, and told me he might have died if it weren't for a doctor. Apparently, the Grandaxes are\nabout to depart on an expedition to hunt the critters in the near future.\n6th of Malin's Welcome\n\nToday, I set up measures to ensure that no-one would rob me of anything too precious. While busing scheming, I was attacked by a giant spiders, on the outskirts of the city! I didn't think they would come so close to Kal'Tarak.\nI have hidden a set of instructions to get to my personal chest, in case I ever forgot its location. I coded them and hid them, to ensure that no-one else would find my belongings.\n10th of Malin's Welcome\n\nI saw a strange umri female walking through the city. She seemed to follow me for a while, until I tried to hail her, and she ran away.\n7th of the Grand Harvest\n\nToday, I joined a dwedmar expedition into a newly discovered cave. While we began our exploration with high spirits, as everyone was cheering, joking and laughing, we met with an unexpected surprise: a pack of minotaurs\nwere waiting for us! In the panic, we retreated to safety, and marched back as one. We made short work of the ennemy, and as we advance, we found the tunnels filled with more traps and critters. We made a stop in what remained of an old library, where an\nesoteric door blocked the way. By reading some of the notes we found spread around the bookshelves, we discovered that the key was locked behind a spell, that we could break by answering a riddle. As my comrades and I cogitated over the puzzle, Koralon,\nthe Onyxheart Clanmother, had an idea. She is well-versed in dwedmar history, and guessed with a gasp that what the notes were hinting at was that the Ironborn clan existed still! A clamour rose within our ranks, as the cursed clan was thought to be gone\nfor aeons. Amidst our stupor, Koralon took the key to the wall, which opened the way for us to continue. As we went deeper within the earth, the temperature rose, and streams of lava could be seen leaking from the walls. We finally reached another\nsimilar esoteric wall, for which we found the key hidden at the top of a cliff riddled with lava streams. The most deft of us took up the challenge, and came back unharmed, holding the key triumphantly. As we were running short on supplies, we decided to\ncome back on the morrow, to continue our expedition.\n4th of Sun's Smile\n\nI just arrived in Kal'Tarak, after a week spent on the road. Dwifar tasked me with my first assignement as a merchant: selling a few dwed-crafted rings and sword. I would be allowed to keep half the profits, and the rest would go to\nclan. While I despise being away from the mountain for so long, and walking out under the sun, I am grateful to Dwifar for his assistance since I moved into the city. In spite of my initial reluctance, I enjoyed the travel quite a bit! I passed by the\numri town near the entrance of the valley, where the locals were  partaking in an odd activities. Almost every citizen was in a rudimentary arena, and a ghastly character was speaking to the lord of the city. I didn't stay to see the end of it, as I was\non a business trip. Next, I travelled to the cloud temple, where I met with the religious order taking care of the building. I dared not ask if they wanted a look at my goods, as I was carrying swords forged by dwarven cultists. \nI then stopped by the\nhalfling lands, Dunshire. They are strange creature, always partaking in some sort of festivity, and didn't seem interested in my wares. I then visited the merchant city of Holm. The streets where teeming with life, with people wandering through the\nstalls aimlessly. Unfortunately, I had no luck there either, as dwedmar wares seemed less exotic in a city with a population larged comprised of dweds. I then tried my luck in the human city of Vreskai, where I saw a few people discussing near the\nblacksmith's workshop. As I approched, a young umri stepped in front of me, and shouted \"God shits on Urguan!\". I replied to to mind his manners, and I was slightly disappointed to see him to falter, and mutter some excuses under his non-existant beard.\nI followed the road to Curion, but I found the city to be deserted. My final stop was the capital city of Renatus. The city was a marvel to behold, and was probably the best example of umri architecture, and even though it pales in front of the fine dwed\narchitecture, still I was impressed by its beauty. However, in my entering the city, I was the witness of a scene as ugly as the city is beautiful: the Lord of Renatus was holding a public burning of a man of faith, presided by the head of the local\nchurch. The martyr was accused of heresy, for spreding the word of his faith, and was to be burned alive in public, under the boos and the rotten fruits of the public. Disgusted, I decided to cut short my travels, and to head back to my beloved Kal'Tarak.\n6th of Sun's Smile\n\nI stayed in the city for most of the day. While I was resting at the tavern, I met with a most peculiar dwarf: he was wearing the clothes of a clergyman, and offered me to play a game of dice. I've never been one to gamble, but I was\ncurious, and the man oozed trustworthiness. We playeda few games, I lost everyone of them, and as we carried on, and upped the ante, I seemed to be unable to win any one game. The old man seemed to have the gods on his side, which didn't come as much of a\nsurprise. What surprised me though, was that, when I decided to stop this financial fiasco, he offered me back the money I lost. I tried to refuse, but he threw the pouch into my hands, and ran away with a viguour I never suspected a man of his age to be\ncapable of.\n8th of Sun's Smile\n\nToday, Dwifar, when I told him my lack of succes in selling any of the wares he entrusted me with, told me off a festival happening in Santegia. Though I had never benn into the city, I accepted, anxious ta make a sale.\n9th of Sun's Smile\n\nAfter a day of travel, I arrived in the coastal city. It is a beautiful place, full of live. As I entered the city, the stall owners where showing off their goods, praising their merits. I saw a group of guards holding of an umri\napparently angry with an elger, an ork overseeing a chest full of random objects he ripped off of his preys, and an old man selling jewelry as a cover for more suspicious activities. A nice young lady approached me, and told me that during the festival,\nstalls were set up for free for incoming traders to use. I gladly accepted to take on one of the stalls, and stayed there until nightfall. It was a good day, As I sold a few of the rings and all of the swords Dwifar gave me.\n10th of Sun's Smile\n\nToday, the forces of Kaz'Ulrah were recruited to assist the native folks of Atlas, the Wonks. They were afflicted with a curse, turned some of their own to darkness, who then relentlessly attack their brothers through armies of\nrisen dead and dark magic. We set up camp in their tunnels, started an excavation to produce armor and weaponry, and we then marched on the Dark Wonks. After days of tracking and fighting, we cornered their leader, and slayed him, though with great cost,\nas Koralon was severly wounded, and Dwifar mortally so. I lost the father of my clan, but we saved the Wonks from destruction, and as such, they offered us a great rewards: their deity would answer to anyone question one of us would ask. After much\ndeliberation, we decided to ask for the secrets of teaching and learning Runic Magic, the ancient craft of the dwed. One of us, alone, was elected to go deep into the wonk caverns, and hasn't returned as of yet.", ""),
        StaticBook("Attunement", "Tristanm1", "The Attunement Ceremony\nForging the Link\n\nBy Salmon Druid Petyr\nFor a Dedicant, the attunement ceremony is the final step of initiation. This forges a link between nature, the rest of the Druidic Order, and themselves. The guide leading the ceremony must be careful to do such properly.\nI personally choose to do this\nceremony by the Birch Pond. I have them close their eyes, and I begin to coax their minds into accepting the spirits of nature around them. At first, I merely whisper to their minds, hoping to soften their natural defenses. Once their mind is unshielded,\nit is possible for enlightenment occur. It is different for everyone, but most report vivid images of the forest talking to them. In my opinion, the visions should not necessarily be told to everyone. They reveal something true about a person's inner\nbeing which should only be known to them. Of course, later, they may choose to use this information when choosing a title or totem.\nThe correct chanting must be performed and not stopped until you have internally communicated with the Dedicant\nafterwards. Be wary of pushing on the Dedicants to forcefully, for the mind is a fragile thing. Make sure that while forging the link, they do not react negatively, harming your mind as well as their own.", ""),
        StaticBook("Autopsy Report", "Theodoric of Markev", "The cadaver is a human male of middle age, seemingly in fit physical condition.\n\nHis apparel bore no markings of affiliation, and the body was thoroughly frozen before being thawed on its journey back to Carolustadt, making me unable to make any\npresumptions as to where he is from, or when he died.\n\nThe body was mangled in a rather horrific fashion, receiving several parallel diagonal swipes from a rather massive edge to his thoracial cavity and abdomen. While several small cuts line the\nlegs, arms, and head, the two-three of these wounds suffered appear to be the cause of his death, through blood loss.\n\nThe asymmetrical and rather messy wounds, combined with the aforementioned parallel markings, lead me to believe that the\nweapon of injury was from some sort of claw or talon. This implies that the cadaver was assaulted by a significantly sized wild animal, by my estimates over 10 feet tall, unless possessing a disproportionate claw size as compared to other animals.", ""),
        StaticBook("Autumn Equinox", "Guyden Aureon", "-={Aspectism}=-\n~Scribed by the Willow Druid\n~Originally by the Hawk Druid\n~The Autumn Equinox~\nAutumn is the season of passing. It is when the leaves fall from the trees, the insects begin to thin, and the beasts of the forest begin to gather sustenance for their hibernation dens. Autumn is the season of the horned man, of death. As such, the -\nWood Elves choose this season to honour their dead, and see them safe passing into the next life.\nThe Autumn Memorial is a somber affair. It is led by a Naelurir priest, who invites elves of the faith to the sea. The druidic priest fashions many paper lanterns designed to float over the water, and grows lilypads to support them. They speak a mass -\nprayer to the deceased, offering their souls safe passage into the next life, by the Aspects grace.\nEach elf in attendance is then responsible for writing the name of someone they have lost on a paper lantern, and setting it, along with a material offering of the deceased (for example, if they enjoyed wine in life, put a flask of it next to the -\nlantern). They then push their lantern and offering out into the ocean. The sea becomes alight with dozens of flickering flames drifting outwards, each representing a soul passing into the next life with the blessing of their loved ones and the Aspects.", ""),
        StaticBook("Axios Notes", "Nemir", "Strange white, magical pillar. - 3180/128/1757\n\nFound Katherine and Vargen, they've set up their tents with the humans.  I've decided to set up mine there before looking for the others.\nFound another strange obelisk, looks somewhat like the other near the wood elves.  This looks to be made of stone.  It's right next to the dwarven camp, 1154/88/-1917\n\nFrozen tree, 468/71/-2201\nWorld just.. ends.  It leads to a seemingly endless pit. -723/107/-3152\n\nAnother weird obelisk is near Haria, no one knows what these are for.\n\nOther obelisk near druids at -\n2730 68 -288\n\nAnother obelisk in the middle of no where, XYZ: -1975 98 -2270\n\nPortal to the Sunless Sanctum is also near here, -2149 98 -1924\n\nLarge ruined building is also near the previously -\n- two mentioned. -1894 146 -2309\n\nAnother obelisk near Ker'nor, lilacs surround it. 3237 111 1697\n\nIn the north, near the Library I've come across some ruins.  A crumbled building, and\na few bridges, another in the area seems to've completely collapsed.  Beneath it, was some sort of hole along the freezing river.  Inside it I've discovered a mural, showing what looks to be elves bowing to some white orb in the sky. -1504 62 -1200\nRuined city with dragon statues.  It's called The Fell City of Dreinloch. 3638 72 -1863\n\nRemember \"Benny Black\"\n\nStrange building in the mountains. -823 227 -1510\nStrange mountain with.. black shit on the top. 656 129 -1742 - Volcano\n\nAnother obelisk stands within a forest north east of the Orenian capital. 1283 85 -580\n\nThere are 10 obelisks, says a kha, i have 7\nI hear there's another obelisk around the orcs, that makes eight.\n\nOdd cave entrance on the isle of Sutica, -107 43 -935  Another entrance similar to this one, leading to a HUGE underground, glowing cave. 245 43 -560\nSome strange.. altar?  Is within one of this large glowing caves beneath the Sutican mountains.  912 26 -303\n\nThe ninth obelisk that I've discovered is on the isles of Sutica, the land surrounding it is.. rotted or just dead.\nThere are lakes of lava, this one is in the middle of one. -862 85 250\n\nFinal obelisk discovered is at the high elves, -2739 207 -192\n\nThe obelisk at the orcs is 2547 48 1856\nit's bigger than the rest.  And stands in the middle or near the middle of a lake\n\nNice place in the north, small pond and beautiful waterfalls between two mountains. 1327 135 -1538\nA beautiful lake hidden within the mountains, a little waterfall leads into it.  It's so secluded and gives off of a tranquil feeling. -83 70 -1166\n\nStrange, eldritch, old man classfied as a spook was spotted in Johannaseburg -\n- it was standing over a woman who as unconscious.  Seemed as if it were in a trance while doing this, this was broken when Richard stabbed it.  He used a ferrum weapon and it caused it pain, there was no aurum or salt.  Weapon was clean.  The creature -\n- had a strange, light blue ooze seep out from the wound.  Its name is Sephtis?\n\nObelisk near warhawkes\n\nVolcano south of Sergei's barony\n135 249 -1584\nHauxir has returned, find John\n\nFound another mural, looks just like the one I found on the riverside north of the library.  Elves bow to a white orb in the sky. It's located within a cave, south of the barony. -21 127 -1554\nAnother mural of elves bowing to a white orb is actually under the large tree everyone woke up in at the docks.\n\nSomewhat odd and hidden cave, a waterfall comes out of it.  It's between Oren and the Wood elves, 3592 144 140\n-try to find anything on a fountain of youth\n- find lori ireheart\n-ask sarrion about merit pasqual? pascal?\n\n\n[!]A sketch is here, it shows a few short birch trees.  Giant mushrooms tower over them.  Written --\nbeneath the drawing is a poor scrawling of the map to Axios.  A northern island is circled near the dwarves. ((2132 100 -2951))\n\n\nSephtis update: ---\nIt's been a while since I've been exploring, started to exlpore the Harian island again.  Decided to look past the obelisk looking over the old warhawke camp and came across these peculiar ruins.  The stone seems crumbled, but I've made the shape of --\na bird-like head sticking out of the mountain.  It's huge.  It's long, stone arm lifts up from the ground and clutches what looks to be a sword with its blade stuck into the earth. 1128 109 1791\nLook for some place that just looks magical for Armin.\n\n[!] The handwriting in this entry looks rushed[!] The ice cavern near Haria or whatever, the maze.. those --\njaws(?) all of that blood... West of 740 107 1867\n[!] The notes in the journal abrubtly end, the enteries ceasing entirely.  On the back cover sits the name, \"Nemir V. W\" to signify the supposed author of this book.", ""),
        StaticBook("B.o.T. Ch. I", "Sunder", "Book of Tales\nChapter I\nwritten by Isovar Kurben, copy by Sunder.\n------------------\nTranslation by various.\nForeword of the publisher\n\n\"Old blood runs deep and has long histories.\" - Isovar Kurben\n\nI, Novtorn Stonefire, have decided to begin releasing the chapters and stories of the \"Book of Tales\".\nWhat the book be, you may ask, so I shall answer. The \"Book of Tales\" is less of a book, but more of a compendium of past times, reaching back further and more extensive into Human history than any book I know of.\nIt tells the tale of not only my family, but the tales of many a man who lived and walked the lands before our ancestors. Written in a tongue long lost to the common man.\nTranslating it out of its original language is a difficult task, a task, on which\nthree men before me have worked on and succeeded to various amounts. These first chapters were translated by Isovar Kurben, the son of Galtor I. Stafyr.\nHe received the book originally from his grandfather Beorn Stafyr, who was an aged man at that time\nLet his words speak for him.\n\n------------------\nI. Chapter - Myth\n\nGrandfather had become open about his past in these past two years. He was nearing his eighty-sixth birthday, he was weak and tired. I suppose that he wished to ease his mind before heading on.\nFor the stories he has told and things he had done I can understand. Yet again, it deems me that Grandfather intended to preserve something, thus he gave me this mysterious book, called \"Book of Tales\".\nIn his dying breath he told me... no, us, not to forget our roots and to preserve tales of old. \nUncle Hanethor was suspicious what it could mean, but he seemingly shrugged it off and turned his attention back to the progressing march of the undead.\nFather did not seem to care too much either, though he mourned remarkably. Aunt Sybilla wept lightly, but a kind smile was on her face... like she has forgiven him for something.\nI will try to maintain a constant series of entries as I progress with the book Grandfather gave me. Consider this the first. I have given it plenty of thoughts, though I assume it is best to start with talking about the past with the first who belongs to\nit. The stories Grandfather told me are a heavy burden on my mind, but blood and family are supposed to know some day.\n\nMy Grandfather, Beorn Stafyr, committed theft and murder.\nFor a quarrel with his father, Brimar, and being disowned by him, he had slain his very own mother, Alexandra, and stole the heirlooms of his family, leaving a mourning father with a younger brother, Gorn, behind. The heirlooms consist of following items:\nFirst and foremost, an old crown of copper with an emerald, to be worn by the head of Stafyr. Uncle Hanethor currently has it and wears it often enough.\nSecondly, our old falcon Thondor, grey feathered with a small green tabard. Father meant he had looked like that ever since he can think back, when he was but a child. He seems to be in service to Hanethor.\nThirdly, a set of armor, which deems me of incredible value. A plate armor of gold and a chainmail of silver. Nobody wears it right now, but we keep it safe, as it is... precious. There has to be something about it.\nAlso, two weapons so fine and sharp as if they were never used before, despite their high age. A foreign tongue is written on the hilts of the Longsword Hanethor and the Battleaxe (one-handed, I have to remark here) Galtor.\nFather and Uncle both wield their namesakes right now.\n\nThe last heirloom Grandfather gave me was this very book. Book of Tales. Records of times past, records of events, people and items. I wonder what I may dig up...\nIt was a dark day as we left our home two weeks ago. The undead are marching onward, nigh unstoppable. Uncle Hanethor led father and our men into a few battles, I took part with my bow.\nIn terms of heirlooms, I was able to witness the twin blades in action for the first time. As if their weapons, armors and bodies were made of paper, Hanethor and Galtor cut through the dark and dead beings with ease.\nThey were able to kill many a foe, but after losing a few men and the relentlessly assaulting undead seemed to take no end, we retreated. I can hear a horn sounding. Finishing this entry, battle calls.\nThe Verge. Father is dead.\nWe got split up. Uncle Hanethor's children are nowhere to be found. I only have Aunt Sybilla, Suldren, Sevren and his wife Aewves and Hunrad with me. Hunrad leads us, I do hope, to safety.\nThe last entry was years ago. Many a thing happened, I am an aging man now. And the last one alive it seems. I have made the decision to work on this book now, as much as I can, to preserve what can be preserved. To translate what can be translated.\n- Personal Entries seem to end here -\n\nFollowing was translated by Isovar Kurben from Old Rivachegian to the common tongue. It begins with the eldest entries.\nThus it was in old times past, that the Almannir came to meet their fate. A foe strong enough to crush an entire people, such was the test of Machr, dr Gott (God?). Fyrschlund, dr Dracha (Dragon?), came to consume the lives of many of the Almannir.\nHeroes fell in battle, one after another. Nobody could stop the beast with its insatiable hunger.\nEven Großma, the last of the Galdr, fell to Fyrschlund after three days and nights of battle.\nAs all hope seemed lost, the last chieftains of the Almannir came together and rallied their men to their side, a force numbering the thousands of thousands.\nLed by chieftain Rigfyr Stoafyer, chieftain Krashgar Rettersma, Altkönig (King?) Zubr Altbom, chieftain Haralt Stoakachl and the female chieftain Juna Wiidafrou, the five armies drew a rainbow through the lands of the Almannir,\ngreen, yellow, light-brown, red and blue.\n\nFyrschlund has been waiting and was prepared. As the bright colored army approached the wastelands of the Northern regions of Almannir,\nwhere Fyrschlund has eaten man and Tier (animal?), consumed the plants and very earth itself, he greeted the five last heroes with an army of his own. \n\nReeking and pitch-black, the Totamännr (?) crawled out of the cold and snowy wasteland,\nthousands and thousands of them, consuming the very light that shone upon them by the sun.\n\nFor a week the armies fought, dotting the white snow with tabards and armor of green, yellow, light-brown, red, blue and pitch-black.\nFyrschlund himself became impatient at the unyielding Almannir and charged into battle himself, burning hundreds of the brave with his searing fire, smashing thousands with his claws and tails.\nAnd so it was time that the five chieftains of the Almannir came to fight Fyrschlund himself. Rettersma died first, but took the dragon's tail. Stoakachl took his wings before being stomped under Fyrschlunds claws.\nAltbom crippled his legs before vanishing in fire. Stoafyer took his breath before being crushed by his jaws. But Juna Wiidafrou was not able to slay the dragon, too deep her wounds were.\nThe son of Rigfyr then approached, as the last Almannir standing amidst the field of colors and dead. Fyrschlund was enraged and tried to snap at him, to devour him, to destroy whatever he could from the people who have brought him to fall.\nJuna took her last will and power and blinded the one-eyed Fyrschlund with an arrow from one of his own Totamännr. Unseen, the son of Rigfyr, climbed on the furious, blind and maimed dragon and drove his lance deep into his skull, ending the nightmare.\n. The Almannir saved their lands at the cost of their own lives. And thus the son of Rigfyr was the last of the Almannir, left alone in the endless wastelands covered in what have been such fertile and peaceful people.\n- End of this translated section", ""),
        StaticBook("B1 AOH", "Azuline", "Anatomy\n    Book One of The Art \n         of Healing\n\n         By Azuline\nAnatomy\n\tThe body consists of many functions that work together as one machine. The mind, or brain would be apart of one of the major functions as it is the connection to our nerves and what we feel, how we respond, how we move.\nIt is all due to the brain. Without it, we wouldn’t move or function. The next major one would be the heart. The heart pumps blood and circulates it throughout our body to function properly.Blood clots and even when the blood is rather thin\ncan be bad for a person. However, some treatments require these things for a person to live a bit longer! As a healer, doctor, physician, and medical scientist, you must quickly think and determine what is best for your patient at the time.\nSometimes failure happens, but you must move forward and take responsibility. With that being said, you must be diligent, but cautious. Remember, the body can only go through so much before it fails and ultimately dies.\nHere are some drawings of the body, what you expect to see in a person and how it functions. *There would be a detailed picture of the body of the different systems and how the body looks like from the inside out.*\nSystems and Functions\n\nBones: The skeletal structure of a body helps move the body. The largest bone in the body is the femur which helps reproduce the blood cells! Bones can break, though they can also regrow and be put back together. The bones in the\nbody doesn’t fully develop until the mature age of twenty-eight. Before then, the body would have massive amounts of collagen or ‘soft bone’ that is rather flexible. Breaking these is possible. There isn’t that much blood that can flow\nthrough collagen, though with that being said it takes a very long time on healing fully. Collagen can be found in the nose and ears even after the person fully matures! \n\nNervous System: This took me a while to figure it out. I was wondering what\nsilvery sheen that is like hair that would connect to the fascia and muscles of the body. I found out after working on a cadaver that it would be activated by salt and or redstone (this is if it is fresh). Realizing after watching a human\nbeat in an orc’s skull that it was all connected to the brain and once the brain was shut down, all systems failed. This is crucial to know! Nerves can be damaged and people can lose functions when the nerves are damaged! From\nwalking, to even using their fingers...it is crucial and highly advised that when working on someone to check and see if there are any major nerve damage. *The shoulders, elbows, knees, neck, and middle section following the whole\nspine was circled.* These are the major nerves areas. Please keep in mind of how the nerves are more exposed in some areas than most and  where they align with the muscles and bones.\nCirculatory system: The blood flows one way and comes back another way. It is constant and never stagnant and if it is, we have a problem. Blood flows through all muscles, tissue, the brain, and heart. There are ways to thicken the\nblood which can be needed for a person whose blood is too thin and to thin the blood for those who have it too thick. Pinching the fingertips to check and see the blood flow by the change of colors is one way, noticing fatigue or even a\nsmall prick to see how the blood flows is another. There is also wrapping a band tightly around their arm and until you actually feel the blood run under your finger (at the inner arm under the band) and take note of how many\npulses you would feel in a minute. There is also just checking their temperature (too cold would mean the blood is trying to keep close to the center and too hot would well, feel too hot) and feeling their pulse in a general manner. The\nblood tells us a lot of things, and possibly more!\n\nRespiratory System: Our lungs are protected by the rib cage that comes up to the clavicle down to just the diaphragm. The lungs doesn’t just cover the\nsystem, but so does the bronchial tubes that connect to the lungs which are small pockets that blood goes in and out of. From there you have the windpipe (trachea) then the voice box (larynx) which then opens to the mouth and nose.\nThe mouth and nose are closed off into two chambers to separate and prevent infections that can be caused and promote proper breathing. That small flap that separates it, is called a pallet. Breathing can be easily affected\nby drugs such as alcohol, opium, and even from caffeine. It can either slow it down or hype it up, though drugs affect the body differently for everyone as everyone is different in one way or another.\nDigestive System: This deals with the mouth again to the esophagus, stomach, liver, gallbladder, spleen, pancreas, large and small intestine, all the way to the exit. People can experience pain and discomfort with any of these parts. Diet\nis key to taking care of these parts as well as exercise. If any of these parts fail, it can cause major issues and system malfunctions!\nMuscular System: The muscles are all wrapped by a thin film called fascia and fibers. They are placed in various areas of the body to have the bones move by connection of the tendon. The muscles can be damaged which is bad! It\nmeans that nerves and blood vessels that are intertwined with the muscles can be damaged and leave that muscle to be utterly useless. The muscles would also develop extra fascia and damaged tissue build up to create pain and\nscars for the patient. As a doctor, we try to prevent scars at all cost. Though it is impossible to leave one scar behind, it is also treatable with salt rubs and friction! Muscles reply to the body when the body is at a normal temperature,\nand the higher it goes, the faster it can reply until overworked. The lower the temperature the slower the muscles can reply. The will also be overworked as the body is trying to quicken it at the same time (the muscle would shake\nwithout control). Of course these things can be treatable and reverse the effects. You can also fix muscle placement at a young age. The older, the harder and the more times you have to put them under a knife.\nTheories\n I believe that there is another system. Another system that protects the body from certain ailments, though I am not sure what it would be called. I knowthat coughing, sneezing, fevers, aches, and so on are the signs of this system\neither working or failing. This system can be treated with honey, ginger, and other herbs to help bright that system back up to protect our body! Reminder: Treatments are meant to be repeated, and not just one time thing!\nRemind your patients and visit them frequently.", ""),
        StaticBook("B2 AOH", "Azuline", "Book Two of\n   The Art of Healing\n   \n        By Azuline\nBotany\tI tell my students that they should read and absorb this books which I had carefully copied down each word and chapter for you here.\nhttps://www.lordofthecraft.net/forums/topic/141741-the-plant-index/\nhttps://wikia.lordofthecraft.net/index.php?title=Flora\nOthers would be:\nGinger Roots which would be found up in the dry parts of the mountains and in the earth. Promotes blood flow, helps the body heal from colds, coughing, and abdominal stomach issues.\nBeet Roots could be found in your local gardens with extreme weathers to even normal temperatures. They are hearty, yet hold so much potential to the body. Promotes blood flow, thickens the blood, energy, and easy on the stomach.\nLicorice Roots are also hearty and grows in various places with cool places or lakes. Easy to grow and in vast amounts! It is used for stomach discomforts, blood flow, energy, and to help the body regain back to it’s natural healing potential.\nThere are more herbs and spices that would help the body, it is up to you to go out there and learn more about it as these books are just going over the tip of the iceburg.\nHow Much is Too Much?\n\n\tGenerally speaking, you should always have your herbs and plants grounded up into fine powder or paste. This makes things easier to apply to\nthe body or into the system. Keep in note: dilute your powders and pastes with water and start out with a little and work your way up. From five grams and up. Though with the Kha, I’ve learned that tippen’s root and poppy powder\n(opium) mixed together works well on them to sedate. The heavier the person is, the heavier the dosage. Orcs are a bit tricky to sedate, they can wake up in the middle of surgery, so it is best to keep a premade sedation vial nearby to\ninject to their system. Needles are made by your local blacksmith or if you tend to travel a lot, use a snake fang and it’s tubing. Of course after cleaning it out and drying it.\nThe signs of seeing too much in their systems could be reversed if you know your herbs and how they would affect the system. Though the patient would start to shake, fevers, tremble, go cold, have a hard time of breathing,\nsweating, feeling uneasy, nausea, dizziness, pupils dilated, and many more signs. Always use a clean bowl to mix your solution to prevent this!\nWhen Treatments fail\n\n\tOwning up to your mistake and genuinely apologizing is the first step as you are trying to find the solution. Sometimes, we try to treat someone for one thing instead of the other, and the other would ultimately lead them up to\ndeath. When treating the body, we as healers must heal the body as a whole! Even if it is a cough and you just treat the fever, the cough can end up ruining their lungs which would ruin their blood and kill the brain. Or if we treated just\nthe cough and not the fevers, then your patient would die because the body was literally cooking itself. Treat the whole body, do not just rely on your magic or simple salve to treat the body as a whole. Be thorough with this.\nThat being said, work with your patient. Be clear with your questions to figure out what is truly wrong with them and keep notes that are confidential of their case so you may look over your work later and possibly come up with\nmore solutions if they come back or when you go to visit them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Babys First Wand", "Toxzero", "Baby's First Wand\n\nBy Sarrion Di'Pasali\nWhat is a wand?\n\nA wand is a tool made from a few simple materials but shaped together in an art and love for craftsmanship, then used as a focal point for any spell. They are used for users who find ease to use a point rather than one's palm,\nor users who use destructive magic and wish to have a distance between them and such. Advanced use for wands can be configured with external magic and crystals, allowing enchantments and the like to be added.\nSelecting your material:\n\nThe base for your wand has to be selected out of a material, one of the most common ones would be wood as it can be carved into one’s own design for originality and personality, easy to put a socket in for the focus crystal\nand any other gems, and very light to carry but easy to break. The next most popular type of material would be metal, harder to get designs engraved into and harder to get them forged, and much harder to get gems\nand the crystal socketed but much much more durable and will last longer.\nSelecting your Focus Crystal:\n\nThe tip of your wand is going to be tipped with a focus crystal, a crystal that naturally grows in the forest and used as a focus point for spells.\nThey vary in color and length, but they can be incorporated simply on the tip or as a neat-o design such as in the mouth of a dragon’s head on the tip of a wand. Once your wand is fully put together, have fun casting.", ""),
        StaticBook("Back to our Root", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Scout and map out the Ker'norian settlement while remaining unseen by watchful eyes.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ball Game Rules", "Jaya Jayamen", "Clay Ball Match\n          Rules\nIn this game you can have as many players as wanted. It is very simple. After deciding what the order is that you will go in, perhaps by rolling a 20 sided dice, the first person goes right behind the closest line to the targets.\nHere, you throw 2 clay balls, the outermost ring is 1 point, the next ring inside of that one is 2 points, and the middle is 3 points. After that player throws his two balls and remembers their score,\nthe player moves to the second farthest line from the targets and throws two more balls, the point scoring values are the same as the first one. the player adds his scores from here to his first two throws scores.\nthe player then goes to the farthest line from the targets and throws 2 more balls. The point scoring values are the same as before. The player then adds those two throws scores to his other 4.\nThen after the first player has totaled all 6 of his throws, the next person goes and does what the first player did. At the end, the person who has the biggest total of points from their 6 throws wins.\nYou can also feel free to not play the match and just throw for fun.", ""),
        StaticBook("Banishment", "Aluatis Lorenthus", "=========================On the Banishment of Veluluai\nBy: Peurith\n=========================Transcribed by Peurith - Scribe of Malin.\nHerein lie the charges against Veluluai, Scholar of Maehr:\n-One count of Conspiracy with a malicious deity.\n-Ten counts of personal manslaughter.\n-Diagnosis of severe psychotic tendency.\n-Destruction of the village of Lenearn.\nGiven her previous service to lord Malin, her sentence is to be a permanent banishment to the icy wastes of Ceru. May the Aspects preserve her.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bardmancy", "Ox Druid Popo", "The Art of Bardmancy is forming noises from the Void into the sound of words, and bringing it into our world. Through this act, the Bardmancer can influence (not force!) the emotions and feelings of those around him or her. It is important to note, while\nBardmancy is NOT in any way shape or form used for combat, it does require mana, as it requires a connection to the void. It should also be noted that an instrument can be enchanted with Bardmancy to amplify the Bard's magic, much like a staff to a mage.\nTo perform bardmancy, one must meditate while listening to any manner of music that involves words. Focus on how it makes you feel, what makes the sound, and how one moves their mouth in order to form these word. The next step is to connect to the Void.\nWhile Bardmancy does not require an awful lot of mana, connecting to the void regardless takes much time, and most of your time studying will be spent trying to connect to the void. Once you have said connection, the first thing one must to on the\nbeginning of their journey with Bardmancy is to make any noise come out of their mouth. Truly, any noise you can hear is suitable. Imagine drawing out from your mouth with an invisable hand. While this takes several tries to correctly perform,\nit does come easier with practice. The next step is to attempt to form this sound into a word. This is easier said than done, as it requires your mind to focus greatly on turning the sound into the sound of your very own voice.\nHowever, as you continue, connecting to the void and forming and singing the words, as well as putting emotions behind them, will become much easier. At the beginning, your sentances will have long pauses in them, taking a lot of concentration, and may\neven force you to quit your song lest you pass out due to using up your mana. However, as Bardmancy is not /too/ complex, it does not require much mana once you learn how to bring the words into our plane of existance. However, any Bardmancer, no matter\ntheir skill, can sing forever.", ""),
        StaticBook("Barmount Dossier", "Klaudia", "===================    Barmount Dossier\n      Lord Landes\n\n\n\n         1st of \n     Snow's Maiden\n          1687\n\n\n\n\n==================\n===================Topic: Lord Landes has has gone back on his felty to Lord Wilhelm Devereux. What has caused him to do such needs to be discovered and reported immediatly to the council. \n\n\n\n==================\n===================Lord Landes, after discussing many things, seems to realize the potential consequences of his actions but, having stated such, does not seem to care entirely about his oath breaking to Cyrilsburg. When questioned on \n===================\n===================what has made the Lord break his oath, he repsonded that he did not wish to sour his relations with Blackreach. It seems to me that he fears deeply the consequences of doing such. Consequences not\n\n==================\n===================only from Blackreach, but from Haense as well. When fuurther questioned on whether or not Haense was a considerable threat to his small settlement, he responded that it was not to his people. However, it does and\n\n===================\n===================currently poses a threat to his lands. He stated that as he sees it, Blackreach will soon become a County. During the time inbetween this however, Lord Landes believes he will loose his title and lands. When and who\n===================\n===================will do such, he was not willing to say. The Lord then went on to say he was alright with such actions taking place as he then expects and or has worked out a deal with Blackreach. A deal in which it seems he is \n\n===================\n===================expeted to recieve his revoked lands and title back. Once Blackreach recieves the status of a County. \nUpon hearing all of this i then gave the lord a hypothetical question of whether ot not he would ever \n===================\n===================consider bringing himself and his lands back under the protection of Cyrilsburg. His responce was non informative and can be summed up as I do not see the Lord of Barmount ever doing such.\n===================\n===================To conclude, the Lord Landes seems to want nothing more than to help his people and keep what lands he has safe. Right now, the Lord seems to think by breaking his oath and fealty to Lord Devereux, he will be able \n===================\n===================to achieve such by keeping tensions low between himself and teh combined forces of Blackreach and Haense. As to whether not he regrets breaking his fealty . . i cannot say. When i asked why he would swear an oath \n===================\n===================he would just go to turn around and break, his repsonce was that of denial. He seemed to not think it was a major ordeal or something in which action would ever need to be taken to re correct. \n\n===================\n===================\n\n\n\n     Jr. Ambassador\n             of\n        Cyrilsburg\n\n     Klaudia Vulnear\n\n\n\n\n==================", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Cooking", "Lillian", "<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n   A Guide To Basic\n         Cooking\n     \n            By\n       Lillian Hill\n\n\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~    <><><><><><><><><>\n<><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Dough~~~~~~\nIngredients:\nTwo binds of wheat.\nCooking Pot.\n\nFind the granules of wheat and remove them, before grindng them and mixing them with a small amount of water. You now have a basic dough.\n<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Bread~~~~~~Ingredients:\nOne lump of dough\n\nCut off a small amount of the dough made previously, and form it into a ball. Place it in your cooking pot over your hot water, and wait for it to cook.\n<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~Pan-Cakes~~~~\nIngredients:\nTwo portions of dough.\nCut your dough into two portions, and then go to flatten them out, and place them in your cooking pot side by side over heated water.\n<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Fish~~~~~~~\n\nIngredients:\nRaw fish of your choice.\n\nRemove the bones of the fish, and peel off one layer of scales, placing it in the cooking pot with the small amount of seasoning.\n<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~Meats~~~~~~\nIngredients: Your choice of raw meat.\n\nSeason the meat with your choice of herb or salt, and then place it in your cooking pot, with a small amount of fat, or water.", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Ethics", "Glacio Nereus", "Motivism, Deontological, and Consequence theories of ethics.\n\nFirst, the consequence theory dictates that an action is either right or wrong based on the consequences of any given action. An example is if a man kills another man.\nman. The action would be right if the consequences were good, such as saving the lives of five good people, or bad, such as if the man who was killed were to have saved the world. Utilitarianism is based off of consequentialism,\nand the basic point of utilitarianism is an action is good if it brings about the greatest amount of pleasure, and the least amount of pain, for the largest number of people. Issues with this type of utilitarianism though are that one can not see the\nthe consequences of the future until they have occured, and one can commit heinous evils if others were to be pleasured by the action. An example of the first argument would be if a man is in a comatose state, and others work to keep him alive,\nalive, killing him would be what a utilitarian \nof this type would argue to be the good action. However, the effort that is no longer keeping him alive \ncan be used to aid others, but this condones murder of of the comatose person. The other argument\nis the \nsoldier analogy. A soldier fighting in a war decides to spare a fleeing enemy since the enemy is \nunarmed, wounded, and in no state to fight back. However, this soldier later kills fifty innocent men. \nAlthough the motive for sparing\nsparing the man was a good motive, the consequence in the long run was ill, \ndespite being unable to foretell such a result. This would make the soldier who spared the enemy guilty of what he could not foretell.  Another type of utilitarianism is rule\nRule utilitarianism. Rule utilitarianism is different in how it attempts to reconcile consequentialism and deontology. This formsays an action is morally justified if an act conforms to a rule, and leads to the greatest good.\nFor example, if a man follows a rule of to not murder, then his act is good, even if one he may have murdered will do so himself. So, two forms of consequentialism are utilitarianism and rule utilitarianism.\nContinuing the discussion of ethical theories is deontology. The deontological theory states an action's is based not on the consequences or the motives of an action, but rather the action in it of itself. An example would be if a man were to fight\ncriminals. criminals. This man's actions may be fighting for good, but he is bad due to the act of fighting being morally wrong. An example of a good action would be being charitable. charitable. If a man were to donate money to a man who uses money for\nhedonistic acts, it would still be a good action, and the man a good man. This is because deontology states that the act, \ncharity, is good, so the man doing the act is good. There are more nuances within this theory however, but they will not be\ndiscussed in this book. Finally, motivism is the theory that an action is either morally permissable or morally wrong based on the motives of an action. An example would be if the previously mentioned soldier spared his foe. The action would be considered\nconsidered morally permissable since the act of not killing him, and the reason for it, is good. A good. A more direct way to follow motivism is the idea to universalize a given maxim, and see if it can be ordered as a universal law. An example would be\nif the soldier spared the enemy once more. The action would be considered morally permissable since the act of not killing him, and the reason for it, is good. A more direct way to follow motivism is the idea to universalize a given maxim, and see if it\ncan be universalized as a universal law. law. An example would be the action of stealing. The maxim would be 'I should steal.' If one universalized the law, then everybody should steal. If everyone were to steal, the idea of stealing itself collapses,\nfor stealing is the act of taking something that is not rightfully yours. Now, there is no object or thing that is rightfully anyone's since all is being stolen, and all is gained by stealing. Therefore, this view of motivism states\nstealing is never morally permissable. Other actions with this include murder, lieing, suicide, and many more. An example of a morally permissable act by this view of motivism would be any action that does not defeat itself when universalized.\nFor instance, the soldier that spared his foe is doing the right thing since the idea of not killing does not defeat itself, and it can be universalized. However, a flaw in this argument would be conflicting duties.\nFor example, if a general ordered the soldier to kill the surrendered foe, the man's two duties would be conflicting. He has the moral obligation to not kill the man, and the moral obligation to obey his superiors due to the idea that\nboth maxims can be universalized. This argument is against this type of motivism.\n\nIn conclusion, the three types of moral theories include consequentialism, deontology, and motivism. All\nthree have their independent benefits, and their independent flaws.", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic First Aid", "Gwyneviere de Savoie", "Basic First Aid\n\nGwyneviere de Savoie\n\n~                        ~\n          Vol 1\nIt is important for those who commonly engage in fighting or combat that the wound is more deadly than your enemies' weapon. Even the smallest cut can kill you. Tend to your wounds as soon as you can and ensure that your wound does not become infected.\nUnder the circumstance that the patient has been inflicted with a cut or puncture injury, there will be blood. Tourniqet the wound to stop the blood flow, or apply a moss to absorb and clot the wound.\n\nForeign material, such as cloth and dirt\nfor example, will need to be removed from the wound. Particularly if the wound is a puncture. Anything inside the wound can lead to infection and then death.\n\nEven the smallest injury can kill the strongest, and it is important to be aware\nof how deadly infection is. Animal urine is an efficient way to sterylise an injury of any infection. Cauterizing the wound is a painful method, but an efficient one, to reduce chances of external infection. If perhaps you do not have ready available\nanimal urine, or a brand (or a fire), or you do not have herbs or medical plants; wrap the injury as best you can and replace bandaging often. Reach a doctor, or a field medic immediately.\n\nAfter sterylising the injury, you may chose to apply a medical\nor herbal paste to the wound if you have it on hand. Otherwise, apply a clean bandage to the wound and seek proper medical aid. Again, change the dressing regularly.\n\nIf a wound is so severe that an internal organ is punctured\nor cut by sword or knife- there isn't much first aid can do. Organ damage will most likely lead to a painful death without proffesional care. It is unlikely that the correct attention will be gained if the wound was inflicted in battle. Use tea's or herbs\nto ease your pain, or your patients' pain as best you can. It is likely that the patient will be suffering from his or hers' injury.\n\nSide note: Alcohol is good way to sterylise a wound and act as a pain killer.\nSevere Head Injury:\n\nIt is likely that in battle a person will come across a head or skull injury. This may also occur after a fall or a slip. If the injury is small, reach an area where you can sit, and check yourself for obvious\ninjury. It is likely you will be dazed or nausious. If skin has split, apply a bandage and seek help as fast as possible to ensure that no long term damage is dealt.\n\nIf the injury is severe, such as the crushing of a skull, your\npatient is most likely unconcious, or in a coma. Either way, they're in a bad state- and hopefully you're there to save their life. Check their pulse first, they may appear to be dead. Swelling of the face, nose, and eyes is a sign that the patient\nhas undergone some serious damage to their head or skull. In this case, it is unlikely that basic first aid can save their life. Do not move them, and if possible, seek proper medical attention. The brain of the patient will swell, causing brain damage\nor death. A hole will need to be drilled into the skull of the patient in order to allow the brain to swell. It is still likely that the patient will die.\n\nHead injuries can cause nausia, headaches, dizzyness and physical sickness. Resting will heal these\nBroken Bones:\n\nYou can check to see the severity of your patients injuries (or your own) by physical appearance. Your patient or yourself will most likely be in shock because of the injury. State of shock is a dangerous thing. Never\nunderestimate the severity of the situation. Broken bones often can be seen externally as lumps in the skin, particularly in limbs. Check for mishape or difference in your limbs, and the limb affected.\nYou can use sticks and straps from boots or clothes, or fabric from your clothes also, to create a splint to keep limbs straight. If your patient has a broken leg, it is likely they wont be able to walk. This is a no brainer to identifying a broken bone\nor fracture. Splinting or creating a stretcher out of sturdy sticks strapped together in a ladder shape can be used to transport the patient. A splint can be used to keep the injury straight and reduce movement to the affected area\nin the case of injuring yourself.\n\nYou can also pack mud around the limb to set the break. Seek proper medical attention as soon as possible.\n\nDislocations can be relocated with pressure to the\naffected area. It is painful. Your patient may need pain killers. If you do not feel comfortable tending to a dislocated bone, seek medical attention of another, or man up.\n\nSlings, made out of tied cloth, or a shirt is great for arm or shoulder breaks.\nA bone break can also break the skin. There may be blood. Apply a splint or use a stretcher to get the patient to proper medical attention if this is the case.\nWater Injuries:\n\nIf a person has found themselves floating face down in the water. The first thing you should do is turn them onto their back. It is important not to apply weight to their body, as you could force them under water.\nThere isnt much you can do out in the water, so bring them back to shore quickly, and remember to keep their head above the waters' surface.\n\nLay them on their back and check for a pulse. A persons pulse can be found under their neck or the under-\n-side of their wrist. Either way, there is a possibility of saving the patient. Place one hand, a fist, onto the chest of the patient above their heart. Place your second hand atop the other.\n\nPump their chest, with short breaks. Count thirty pumps before\nstopping. This can force water out of the lungs of the patient or restart the heart.\n\nOpen the airway of the patient by placing your palm on the persons forhead and gently tilting their head back. Check for normal breathing. If the patient is not breathi-\n-ng still, open the persons mouth and transfer air from your own lungs to the patients. Afterwards, continue pumping. Hopefully this will be enough to revive the patient or get the water out of their lungs.\nArrow Wounds:\n\nIf your patient has an arrow injury, first be prepared to apply a lot of force to free the person of the arrow. They are very hard to get out safely. Pulling it out without care can sever arteries or break leave splinters\nor wood inside of the body. You could die of blood loss or infection. So long as the bolt or arrow is inside of the patient, the blood loss will be lower than without it.\n\nYou can remove the arrow by propulsion, where you force the arrow\nthrough the flesh and out the exit point of the wound. Reccomended for limb injuries.\n\nSaw off the shaft, and leave it for a few days so that the wound becomes full of pus and can then be removed with ease. The pus signals infection.\nand would then need proper medical attention.\n\nStretch the wound by plugging it with probes of elder pith, soaked in honey and then using a pair of tongs, reach into the wound and slowly, carefully, tug the arrow/bolt free.\nWash the wound with wine or liquor, and apply a bandage securely or cauterize the wound. Reduce the amount of strain on the affected area and rest for a few days to prevent pains and quicken the rate of healing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic medicine", "Rhova'dir", "-How to make a first aid kit-\n\n*You will need the following things*\n\n>Strips of Cloth for bandages and cleaning wounds.\n\n>A vial of Vodka to clean wounds, needles and hands.\n\n>Gauze to use for putting herbs on a bandage.\n>Suture needles and a spindle of thread for stitching deep cuts.\n\n>Water bottles for mixing herbs into a solution, cleaning eyes or even hydration.\n\n>Honey allows the medicine to go down easier and helps with colds and with the new borns-\n-to start feeding.\n\n>A mask for not allowing poisonous chemicals or body fluids enter your body.\n-----------------------------\nIf the patient has been cut or stabbed, quickly remove all the materials that can infect the wound like cloth, dirt and other things, proceed to apply some moss to absorb the blood, clot the wound or even tourqinet the wound.\nIf the wound is a-\n-puncture, anything inside it can infect the wound; and remember, even the smallest cut can kill the strongest;\nIts good to know how deadly the wound is, urine can be used as a streyliser for infections and injuries. Cauterizing is a painful method-\n-but its an efficient method and it reduces the chance of external infection.\nIf by chance you dont have animal urine or a fire or even some medicinal herbs, wrap the injury as best you can and replace the bandage often, reach a doctor or a field-\n-medic immediately. After sterylising the wound you can choose to apply an herb paste or apply a bandage, Again change the bandage often.\nIf the wound is so severe that first aid will not help like an organ damaged for any reason like a knife, there is-\n-nothing you can do without a professional medic, it will lead to a painful death if not treated. Use teas and herbs to ease the pain of your patients. (Alchohol can be used to sterylise and act as a pain killer)\nHead injuries:\nIts more likely that a person in a battle will get an injury on his skull, if this happens sit down for a moment and check for any wounds in your head. Its more likely you will nauseous or dizzy. If the skin has split apply a bandage-\n-and seek help to ensure no more damage. If a severe injury happens like skull crushing your patient is more likely unconscious or in a coma. Check their pulse, nose, eyes and the swelling of the face to ensure the patient has not undergone through-\n-severe brain or skull damage, in this case is unlikely that first aid can save their life.\nDont move them, and if possible seek proper medical attention.\nThe brain of the patient will swell, causing brain damage or death. A hole will be drilled-\n-into the patient skull in order to the brain to swell, but its still likely that the patient will die.\n\nHead injuries can cause dizzyness, nausea, headaches and physical sickness; resting will heal these.\nBroken bones:\nYou can check the severity of the wound by its physical appearance. Never understimate the severity of the wound!\nBroken bones can be often seen as lumps in the skin, particularly in limbs. Check for mishape in your limbs.\nUse sticks, cloth or fabric to make a splint to keep your limbs straight up. Using a splint keeps the limb straight up and reduces the movement of the area, you can also use mud to set the break, seek proper medical attention as soon as possible.\nDislocations can be healed by applying pressure on the affected area, it is very painful so your patient may need some pain killers.\n\nSlings are made out of cloth or fabric and they are perfect for broken arms.\nA broken bone can break the skin too so seek proper medical attention quickly if that happens.\n\nIf you find someone floating face down on water quickly put them onto their back. It is important to not apply weight on them, you can force them go-\n-underwater. There isnt much you can do on the water so bring them to dry land and check their pulse. First, put your hand in the patient chest above the heart and put the other hand atop of it. Pump thirty times with short breaks before stopping,\nthis can cause the water to come out of the lungs and restart the heart. \nFor opening an airway, gently place your hand on the patient forhead and tilt it back. Check for any normal breathing, if the patient is not breathing, open the mouth of the-\n-patient and transfer the air from your lungs to the patient's lungs, after this continue pumping, hopefully this will be enough to revive the patient or get the water out the patient's lungs.\nArrow injuries:\nIf your patient has an arrow stuck on any part of their body, prepare to apply lots of force to get the arrow out of the patient body. It is very difficult to pull out an arrow safely, if not done correctly it can leave splinter wich-\n-will infect the wound.\nYou can remove the arrow by using propulsion, where you force the arrow through the flesh and out the exit point of the wood.\nThe next method is used for limb arrow injuries.\n\nSaw off the shaft and leave it for a few days so it creates pus, after that it will be easier to get it out. \n(Pus is a signal of infection)\nWheatGrass Ingested, Dry, or tea: Helps with broken bones\n\nHorse tail, Comfrey root, Oat straw, Lobelia, Lavender, Chamomile, Mandagora: Ingested in teas\n*I dont know what it does yet*\nBergamot Oil, Comfrey root, Mandagora: When applied topically, cures bruises\n\nComfrey, Mandagora, Aloe Vera:\nWhen applied topically cures burns\n\nTippen's root, Yarrow: Cures Concussions\nEchinacea, Pot Marigold, Gumweed, Mullein, Chamomile, Lavender, Mandagora, Orchid, Strawberry, Orange peel, Shade leaf, Blissfoil: In a tea, works like a coagulant\nBlueberries, Raspberries, Strawberries, Blackberries, Blissfoil: When used in teas cures minor and major cuts\n\nJohn's Wort, Kanna flower: When used in teas works as a desinfectant\nYarrow, Witch's Hazel, Comfrey root, Tippen's root: Applied on scabs or around the wound when clean, it also causes depression\n\nDragur tongue, Yarrow: Applied topically to scabs, scars and internal wounds\nBeard weed oil, Yarrow, Tippen's root: Cures muscle fatigue\n\nCrampbark, Skullcap: Ingested in coffee: Helps with pregnancies\n\nGinger root, Red raspberry leaf, echinacea, Lavender, Skullcap, Crampbark: Cures scars with milk teas\nBromelian, Aloe vera, Gotu Kola: When applied topically cures stomach aches\n\nGinger root, Peppermint, Chamomile, Blissfoil: When ingested in teas cures sore throat\nBlackberry, Mullein, Blissfoil, Honey, Slippery elm bark, Marshmallow root: Ingested with honey-milk teas\n\nYou can add honey or licorice root to sweeten teas, the foul taste of the herbs will not disappear but it will be better\n*Side note* If you find someone who was punched hard, quickly apply some Athin in the affected area.\n\nAnd a quick life saving potion! Mix destilled water with Tippen's root, it will help a lot in your first aid kit.", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Potions I", "Ambis", "Potion Of Mandragora\n\nT2: Mandragora\n\nAn excellent healing base for healing brews. Speeds up the process of natural healing. Too much consumption will cause mild paralysis.\nPotion of Frost Vine\n\nT2: Frost Vine\n\nThe liquid freezes any organic material it touches. Useful for creating flame-retardant armor and clothing. Will cause frostbite if applied to skin.\nPotion of Serpent's Stalk\n\nT2: Serpent's Stalk\n\nThis brew aids in healing burn wounds.\nPotion of Athin\n\nT2: Athin\n\nWhen applied to skin or armor, it provides a minor defence against flames & fire. Unable to be applied to metalic armors.\nPotion of Blissfoil\n\nT2: Blissfoil\n\nNumbs muscles and nerves where applied. Useful for medics & doctors, and as a muscle relaxant.\nPotion of Crimson Vase\n\nT2: Crimson Vase\n\nLowers the drinker's inhibitions, causing them to act brash and bold.\nPotion of Drake's Tail\n\nT2: Drake's Tail\n\nA potent, highly acidic brew. Any ingestion or contact with skin will cause burns.\nPotion of Dwarf's Pumpkin\n\nT2: Dwarf's Pumpkin\n\nA smelly, bitter brew. Can be drank, causing an effect similar to alcohol.\nPotion of Flametongue Root\n\nT2: Flametongue Root\n\nFlametongue root lowers the boiling point of any liquid it is brewed into. The potion is scalding hot at all times. Handle with caution!\nPotion of Blood Lotus\n\nT2: Blood Lotus\n\nAn incredibly large source of vitamins and nutrients. Provides a day's worth of meals in one bottle.\nPotion of Larihei's Fingers\n\nT2: Larihei's Fingers\n\nDrinking this brew makes one more aware of their movements, able to do them more accurately.\nPotion of Halfling's Grass\n\nT2: Halfling's Grass\n\nCauses extreme nausea in some drinkers, and a lofty, lightheaded sensation in others. Drinkers become extremely hungry after consumption.\nPotion of Elf's Hair Vine\n\nT2: Elf's Hair Vine\n\nThis brew gives you a minor energy boost. Will suffer a crash afterwards, becoming very tired.\nPotion of Crouching Feather\n\nT2: Crouching Feather\n\nIncreases natural eyesight for a short time, allowing the drinker to see better and farther, especially at night.\nPotion of Clutcher's Straw\n\nT2: Clutcher's Straw\n\nCauses the muscles to lock up when consumed in large quantities. Consumer will remain conscious but unable to move any part of the body.\nPotion of Saffvil\n\nT2: Saffvil\n\nCauses severe poisoning. Large doses may cause death but most doses induce vomitting.\nPotion of Alabaster Leaf\n\nT2: Alabaster Leaf\n\nA slightly poisonous brew. Will cause an upset stomach. Will counteract other poisons and work as an antidote.\nPotion of Tippen's Root\n\nT2: Tippen's Root\n\nAn efficient coagulant. Stops bleeding where applied.\nPotion of Goblin's Ivy\n\nT2: Goblin's Ivy\n\nDrinking this brew causes your skin to dry out and flake. Useful for making water-repellent clothing.\nCool Murky Potion\n\nT2: Mandragora, Frost Vine\n\nA murky concoction made of a swamp herb and frostvine. It tastes think and slushy. Your whole body would protest against drinking this.\nMurky Mending Salve\n\nT2: Mandragora, Crouching Feather\n\nA murky green mixture that resembles swamp water. Small yellow spores float around it. It tastes refined, however.\nHermit's Concoction\n\nT2: Mandragora, Tippen's Root\n\nA typical brew you'd find in a witch's hut, this strange mix of herbs heals, rejuvinates, and leaves you feeling terrible afterwards.\nPotion of Lesser Chill\n\nT2: Frost Vine, Crouching Feather\n\nA thin potion that is cold on your tongue but makes you feel lighter. It also lowers your body temperature progressively, eventually making it hard to move quickly.\nCool Potion\n\nT2: Frost Vine, Tippen's Root\n\nA dirty brown mixture that is cold as you touch it. It has a foul, foul taste and makes your esophagus feel cold, but it hardens your skin.\nNumbing Potion of Serpent's Stalk\n\nT2: Serpent's Stalk, Blissfoil\n\nA blueish green potion.\nA mix of Serpent's Stalk salve with Blissfoil. Quick acting to numb the pain on burns.\nFast Acting Potion of Serpent Stalk\n\nT2: Serpent's Stalk, Elf's Hair Vine\n\nAn aqua colored potion. A mix of Elf's Hair Vine and Serpent Stalk. Great for treating burn wounds quickly.\nSerpent and Tippen's Mix\n\nT2: Serpent's Stalk, Tippen's Root\n\nA light green colored liquid. Made from Tippen's Roots and Serpent's Stalk. A healing salve, for cuts and burns.\nQuick Numbing Potion\n\nT2: Blissfoil, Elf's Hair Vine\n\nA think mix of nectars.\nMade from Elf's Hair Vine and Blissfoil. It's effects numb the area of a body quite fast.\nNumbing Potion of Tippen's Roots\n\nT2: Blissfoil, Tippen's Root\n\nA light blue potion. A mix of Tippen's Roots salve with Blissfoil. Quick acting to numb the pain on cuts.\nOrange Venom\n\nT2: Dwarf's Pumpkin, Clutcher's Straw\n\nA foul venom that burns your tongue and hurts your taste buds. It causes minor ulcers in your esophagus and is an experience one would not want to feel twice.\nMusty Potion\n\nT2: Dwarf's Pumpkin, Goblin's Ivy\n\nA terrible smelling concoction that makes you cringe as you bring it up to your mouth. As much as it ravages your throat when you swallow it, it hardens your muscles, giving you some...\nresistance to blunt attacks.\nThin Concoction\n\nT2: Larihei's Fingers, Halfling's Grass\n\nA liquid with a thinner consistency than water that swirls menacingly in its phial. It grants you some agility, but blurs your vision greatly.\nModerate Potion of Celerity\n\nT2: Larihei's Fingers, Elf's Hair Vine\n\nA finished concoction of Moderate strength. Finely brewed for enhancing reaction speed and improve agility.  Extended use of the muscles leaves the drinker without...\nmuch strength in his body. Extremely useful when running away for safety.\nPale Brew\n\nT2: Larihei's Fingers, Crouching Feather\n\nA pale brew that flows down your throat like water. It causes your eyesight to better, but after a while one would get nauseous.\nHalfling's Wings\n\nT2: Halfling's Grass, Crouching Feather\n\nA brew famous among halfling theifs; it grants the user better perception and flexibility but it causes the user to be less effective in combat.\nFast Acting Potion of Tippen's Roots\n\nT2: Elf's Hair Vine, Tippen's Root\n\nA light green mix. A mix of Elf's Hair Vine to Tippen's Roots. Placing it on open cuts almost instantly stops bleeding. It leaves the wounded patient with an extra boost of...\nstamina.\nLumberjack's Recipe\n\nT2: Crouching Feather, Tippen's Root\n\nA famous potion among lumberjacks, this salve is a great way to heal cuts and scrapes, but once it hits the bloodstream, its nauseating.\nDesert Vitality\n\nT2: Clutcher's Straw, Goblin's Ivy\n\nA liquid often used by desert wanderers to help them stay longer without food. It increases resistance by shutting down some muscles, causing the body to focus its energy on surviving...\nIt lowers performance in exchange for vitality.\nCool, Thick Salve\n\nT2: Mandragora, Frost Vine, Crouching Feather\n\nA thick salve that is cold to the touch, and has a sharp smell. Its taste is reminiscent of pumpkin juice. It heals well, but numbs the senses.\nEssence of Frost\n\nT2: Mandragora, Frost Vine, Tippen's Root\n\nA cold, clear, and thick fluid that has the consistency of a thick oil. It is hard to swallow, and you feel it throughout your body. However, it does miracles for both internal and...\nexternal wounds.\nModerate Potion of Mending\n\nT2: Mandragora, Frost Vine, Crouching Feather, Tippen's Root\n\nA finished concoction of moderate strength. One of the most renown alchemical brews, this potion swirls in its vial, completely...\nconsistent in texture and thickness. It lets off a dull white glow. It is the solution to any open wound, but greatly tires you out, restricting your movement. Optimal to use if you find a safe spot where danger can not come to you.\nBlackwood's Remedy\n\nT2: Mandragora, Crouching Feather, Tippen's Root\n\nA dark brew that looks menacing and smells worse than a rotting corpse. As you drink it, you feel like wretching and your body weakens. Your senses slowly shut down. Yet...\nas your perception dilapidates, your wounds heal miraculously.\nWinter's Embrace\n\nT2: Frostvine, Tippen's\nRoot, Crouching Feather\n\nA smooth, flowing, thin liquid that seeps down your throat before you swallow it. It cools down your whole body uncomfortably, but rejuvinates.", ""),
        StaticBook("BathHouse Permit", "Przemek of Nordengrad", "Dear Earl of Nordengrad, \nIt has come to my attention that we lack a bath house! Where is a man supposed to bathe after a long day of work, the river? The filth there is unimaginable and the water is cold- so cold, infact, that it causes\nmy bollocks to freeze off. If thee authorize the construction, I shall cover the costs of employing builders and provide the needed resources.\n\nSign here if thee accept Torsten Eirksson Rosik", ""),
        StaticBook("Battle for Man", "Leyun of Hirnfall", "THE BATTLE FOR HUMANITY\n-\nPRELUDE\n-\nIn the weeks leading up to the battle, the Fallen Daemon managed to spread his taint into the farmlands surrounding Old Carrandal, triggering a famine as the harvest encroached. The\nDragon's Council immediately flooded resources in local fisheries, yet it was not enough to feed the thousands of refugees that had been driven inside the city's walls.\n\nWith the fall of Caer Lund and Caer Dein, Humanity's inner borders were compromised.\nThe First, Second, Third and Fifth Banners of the Dragon rallied in Carrandal, and conscription was enforced, providing an additional 20,000 levymen. His Majesty sent requests for aid to the Children of Malin on Lwynfyrd, yet no answer was recieved.\nAs many began to die of starvation and disease, the Fallen Daemon crossed past the borders of Caer Lund and Caer Dein with several thousand Undead. On the eve of Battle, his Majesty ordered that General Vaeyl was to have his warriors of the Third Banner\nof the Dragon swear upon the Oathstone.\n-\nTHE BATTLE\n-\nOn the first day of winter, the Fallen Daemon assaulted the walls of Old Carrandal. The First Banner of the Dragon led a sortie to thin the Undead hordes, but were decimated when the Fallen\nDaemon entered the fray. As the walls began to crumble, His Majesty ordered the Third Banner of the Dragon to advance.\n\nThe warriors of Vaeyl fought bravely, but were felled by the Undead. Yet shortly after, they began to rise again. Unknown what had\ncaused this phenomenon, but the Third Banner seized this opportunity to strike at the Undead again. Surprised, the Undead began to fall.\n\nAs Vaeyl's warriors continued to fall, they also continued to rise. The Undead forces were unprepared for this, and\nwere easily cut down when the gates of Old Carrandal opened to allow the Second and Fifth Banners to charge.\n\nThe Third Banner afforded His Majesty's mages enough time to prepare a strike that forced the Fallen Daemon to retreat. Yet it is unknown if the\nDaemon retreated because he was wounded, or because he was simply shocked to see His Majesty's own warriors rise from the dead.\n\nRegardless what had caused the retreat or the Third Banner to wake from their graves, Old Carrandal had been saved,\nand Humanity was not extinguished.\n-\nPenned by Leyun of Hirnfall from the accounts of Yeor of Old Carrandal", ""),
        StaticBook("Battle of Riga", "Ser White", "The Battle of Riga: Oren's Darkest Hour\nPrelude: The Battle of Riga was one of the darkest days in recent memory for the Holy Oren Empire. A part of the Courlandic Rebellion, the Battle of Riga was a last ditch effort on the part of the Axis to best Oren and drive back their forces.\nWith the Vanirs having recently recaptured their home of Kraken's Watch, the Staunton leadership had fled, expecting Oren to capture Riga and swift end the war. All that was left to defend Riga were the proud men of the Axis.\nBattle: The Battle of Riga started on the Grand Harvest of 1563. Leading the Axis infantry was a prominent Dreadlander, and the Farfolk leader took charge of the cavalry. The Orenian leadership was more united, being commanded by the Gold Corps leader.\nThe Axis marched outside of Riga in order to meet assult attack Oren's army. Upon seeing this Oren marched onto the field from the ruins of Kraken's Watch. While Oren continued on along the main road, the Axis took to a hill north of the road.\nUpon seeing this, there was a brief exchange of arrows, but the wind was so heavy that arrows couldn't fly properly and all missed. Seeing this, the Axis charged down the hill towards Kraken's Watch while the two contingents of cavalry duked it out in a-\nwheat field along the river near Kraken's Watch. However, Oren's infantry had kept advancing on Riga, so the two armies had practically changed positions. They then rushed at each other, and met just south of the road leading to Riga.\nThe fighting was fierce. At the start, it seemed that Oren's infantry would carry the day with their superior numbers. The Axis cavalry had killed the majority of Oren' cavalry and then all rushed into the melee. As the battle carried on and men were-\ngetting worn down, however, the tides shifted. Small contingents of oreners were being caught away from the main force and cut down. Oren's wounded had fallen back towards Riga, behind the fresher infantrymen.\nHowever, the Axis's battered and bruises patched up what they could and carried on. It was this weakness that would be Oren's downfall. As freshmen sat back trying to fully recover, the Axis discovered where the weak had hidden away.\nWhat followed next can only be described as a slaughter. The battle had shifted into Oren's medical camp. The weak were slaughtered, and with so many fresh men having stayed back, the numbers quickly shifted as disarray swept through Oren's lines.\nOreners fell left and right. After the dust had settled, Orenian bodies littered the ground. All that remained were a few cavalry that galloped around and tried to do something, only to be piked off their steeds and cut down.\nWhilst that occured, the Axis proceeded to hunt down the cowards which had attempted to hide upon realize their defeat. Not a single Orenian would return from the plains outside Riga.\nConclusion: That day, Orenian high command managed to squander every advantage they could have taken. Granted, they were smart in not marching up the slope to face the Axis, but that seemed to spell the end of their tactical genious.\nThe cavalry forces were similar enough in size that the superior skill of the Axis cavalry showed. Without any infantry to support the cavalry, most of Oren's riders were doomed to die.\nThe infantry tells a different story entirely. The Axis managed to remain a cohessive force throughout the battle, where as Oren faced problems with units being isolated and cut down. Along with that, keeping men in the medical camps for too long surely-\nalso cost Oren dearly. However, it should not be forgotten or denied that the Axis was a better trained force than what Oren had. Orcish strength, the Dreadlanders legendary fighting skills, and the numbers provided by Courlanders, Krajens,\nand the former Nortruppen ultimately led to the Axis's military being more prepared than that of Oren's. On top of the fact that the Axis also had superior commanders, the Axis had taken the tiniest of advantages and maximized them, unlike Oren.\nEpilogue: Based off this telling, it would seem apparent that the Axis should have won the war. Well, scholars today cannot say why the Axis lost, other than God himself had cursed their effort. Despite their being the victorious army which had utterly-\ncrushed the Orenian at the Battle of Riga standing between Oren and Riga, an Orenian army managed to sweep into the city without a fight, capture it, and loot it. However, the Axis did still have a war against Oren in the south to fight.\nYet, even that was cursed by God, as no side was even able to muster an army to do battle until they arrived at Axios. There, enough Axis members had passed away, disappeared, or switched allegiances that the Axis no longer stood a chance.\nBy some miracle of God, Oren survived its darkest day. Despite Oren having come so close to being defeated, as the Axis would have been able to besiege the capital had God not interfered, few Oreners remember this day.\nEven fewer recognize how close Oren truly came to defeat. If anything can be taken from the Battle of Riga, it should be these two things.\n1. Oren isn't invisible. As hard as it may be to defeat Oren, it can be done with enough men, skill, supplies, and tactics.\n2. So long as God is with Oren. Oren will never fall. In order for Oren to fall, one must either have the support of God himself, or convince God to let fate decide itself.\nThe End.\n\nIn memory of all those brave men of the Eagle and their allies who gave their lives in hopes of achieving freedom.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bawd & Five High", "Aluuvia", "=======================         The Story of\n       Bod, and the time\n       he got Five High.\n=======================\nBawd was the best of Gobbos and the best of Druids, and he had on his chin the best of beards.\n\n   Bawd spent most of his time meditating in the forests and the jungles, wandering around Vailor for\nthe best of spots in which to sit and think.\n\n   But Bawd was prone to bad habits, and there came a time he grew restless, and his beard grew too heavy.\n\n   That was when Bawd decided to make a change.\nIn a jungle near the desert, Bawd took his oldest collection of most prized possessions.\n\n   Over his many long years wandering the lands, Bawd had amassed quite a collection.\nAs a matter of fact, he had amassed a collection containing ALL the drugs known to mortal man. And some unknown!\n\n   Deep in the jungle, Bawd did what no one had ever done before, and took all the drugs.\nAll of them.\n\nAt the same time.\n\nAnd that was the time Bawd got Five High.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bearing Defense.", "Lenniel", "Dearest Loved one.\n\nPlease use this book as a precaution to save everyone and look after them. \n\nLove\n          Lenniel.", ""),
        StaticBook("Beautiful Maiden", "Ayda Morra", "The night shines on her hazel brown hair, You could see the stars in her emerald gem eyes. Her skin was warm despite the cold mist of the night. She was the definition of beauty.\n\nAs she slept in the peaceful night, she leant on a ghost,\nthe ghost wasn't as pretty as the beautiful maiden. Though, the ghost's looks weren't the best, her spirits were high.\n\nThe ghost loved to dance through night and day with the beautiful maiden, they spent years together.\nAs the maiden grew older, her looks grew greater. She looked as if she had no problems, but that were not the case, as the maiden grew older, she grew unstable.\n\nThe ghost knew this would happen but, didn't want to admit it.\nThe maiden was slowly loosing herself but, the ghost loved her never the less.\n\nThe ghost watched the maiden cry, scream and laugh, even watched her ramble senselessly.\n\nThe beautiful maiden was broken.\nOne day, The beautiful maiden broke herself physically. The lifeless body of the beautiful maiden shocked the ghost. The ghost was heartbroken... If the ghost could die once more, They would of.\nThe ghost lived in sorrow for eternity, never to love again.\n\nBy Ayda Morra.\n\n'This book is dedicated to the beautiful Octavia Thorn'", "")
    )

    private fun _ATLAS_1(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Behind FP-02 #1", "Antanios Rutledge", "Antanios Rutledge\nMissing: 1676-1677\nAlive\n--------\nIn 1676, I visited Holm. I planned to buy some daisies for Rivaini.\n\nDisgruntled by the lack of items in stock, I took a breather by the little stream in the back.\nIt was sudden, I was caught off-guard. A wood elf grabbed me by the shoulders and slammed me into the rock wall. Blood from the incident is still stained on that rock.\n\nThe wood elf was of average height, and his eyes were yellow.\nWhere he took me, I've no recollection. I woke up in a dark room, it was cold, and it was hard yet smooth, like polished stone. I was restrained by chains and cuffs that were bolted to the wall.\n\nIt wasn't until he stoaked the flames of his forge that\nI realized he was a wood elf. I could finally see, but not much. The first thing he did was stab me in my thigh, and let me bleed out a bit.\n\n“Pain is good.”\nHe said, just before he cauterized the wound with the brand he had in the forge's flames.\nThe rest of the year went like that.\nStab wounds\nBroken Bones\nIron Branding\n\nHe'd always heal them, before doing it all over again.\n\n“Pain is good.”\n“You sick flower-fucking tree hugger!” I responded.\nI assumed he was probably homosexual, since he spoke /too fondly/ of a male high-elf named Blossom Sagehand.\n\nThe year went on, I remember counting the days until I finally broke. After so many days, I finally broke.\nI told him that people will know I'm missing. My friends won't stop until they find me.\n\n“One day, you’ll be an empty vessel at my command; and those friends? You’ll slaughter them without a choice.”\n\n“Pain is good.”\nEverything became blurry after that. I was released to do my programmed damage. The first target was Sheriff Adler, thank GOD he was sane back then. He stopped me and detained me in a cell. I remember the talks, how he would make the room too bright for\nme to see. I was sensitive to light, I couldn't see unless it was dark.\n\nSheriff Adler was kind enough to supervise my recovery, and for that I'm thankful, and for that I trusted him.\n\nThen, Adler snapped.\nIt was around 1679.\n\nI was recovered, but I had no job yet. I was walking with my friend and his fiance. We came upon Sheriff Adler and Ser Atticus. We spoke, and then Miss Demetria Hatheway showed up, and all hell soon broke loose.\nI motioned for my friend to leave, which he did. Ser Atticus tried to attack Miss Hatheway, I ran and I tried to push her aside to avoid harm. He missed. Atticus swung again, he missed. I told her to run, but she couldn't get away in time. \nI felt a tug.\nSheriff Adler grabbed me by the back of my collar, and yanked me off. He slung me into  Farm Plot 1, before wrapping his hands tightly around my throat.\n\nHe tried to choke me out, I couldn't pry his hands off as he dragged me to the back of the\nBracchus Engineering Exposition grounds. From there, he continued his torment. If I fought back, he was ready to kill me.\n\nI only regret not being able to save Miss Hatheway.", ""),
        StaticBook("Belvitz Games 2", "Buernoc Silvervein", "Common Games\nFound Among The\nPeople of Belvitz\n\nVolume Two\n\nHare & Huntsmen\no    o    o\n    o  o    o    o  o\n        o    o    o\n\nThe Game Board\n\nEleven spaces are arranged in rows of three, five, three.\nx    o    o\n    x  o    o    o   c\n        x    o    o\n\nStarting Position\n\nThere are three huntsmen and one hare, they start in the aforeseen positions.\nAlternatively there is another uncommon starting method wherein the hare begins at the center of the board.\nThe game is played by two persons, one playing hare the other playing huntsmen.\n\nThe hare wins by passing the huntsmen and reachign the end from which they began. \n\nHuntsmen win by trapping the hare so it cannot move.\nThe huntsmen move first then the hare, they continue alternating moves thereafter.\n\nOnly one huntsman can be moved per turn. Huntsmen can be moved one space in any forward or sideways direction, but NOT in ANY backwards direction.\nThe hare can move one space in any direction.\n\nThe games pieces cannot jump over or capture eachother.\n\nIf the huntsmen do not advance for ten turns, the hare wins.", ""),
        StaticBook("Besti", "Audbjørn Fáóláin", "General Beastiary\n- Discoveries during my travels.\n   - Vivianne Verdigris\n\nNote- This was written by Vivianne Verdigris, I just happened to find it after she left.\nThe Boar\nThe boar is so fierce a beast, and also so cruel, that for his fierceness and his cruelness, he despiseth and setteth nought by death, and he reseth full piteously against the point of a spear of the hunter. And though it be so that he be smitten or\nsticked with a spear through the body, yet for the greater ire and cruelness in heart that he hath, he reseth on his enemy, and taketh comfort and heart and strength for to wreak himself on his adversary with his tusks, and putteth himself in peril of\ndeath with a wonder fierceness against the weapon of his enemy, and hath in his mouth two crooked tusks right strong and sharp, and breaketh and rendeth cruelly with them those which he withstandeth. And useth the tusks instead of a sword.\nAnd hath a hard shield, broad and thick in the right side, and putteth that always against his weapon that pursueth him, and useth that brawn instead of a shield to defend himself. And when he spieth peril that should befall, he whetteth his\nAnd hath a hard shield, broad and thick in the right side, and putteth that always against his weapon that pursueth him, and useth that brawn instead of a shield to defend himself. And when he spieth peril that should befall, he whetteth his\ncomforteth the roots of his teeth therewith by vertue thereof.\nThe Eagle\nWhen an eagle is corky, its eyesight dims and its feathers and wings become heavy. to rejuvinate itself, the eagle flies up to the climature of the sun, which burns aroint the humour ov'r its eyes and burns off its corky feathers. the eagle then plunges\nthree times into water, and its youth is restor'd. also as a result of age, the eagle's beak grows until it can nay longer englut; by striking it against a rock, the eagle breaks its beak which then grows back. the eagle's eyes art very sharp and can\nsee gudgeon when the bird flies ov'r water. the eagle can look directly into the sun. as a test of the worthiness of its young, the eagle holds them up facing the sun. the birds that cannot stare into the sun and turn their eyes aroint art cast out of\nthe aery.\nThe Fox\nA fox is called Vulpes, and hath that name as it were wallowing feet aside, and goeth never forthright, but always aslant and with fraud. And is a false beast and deceiving, for when him lacketh meat, he feigneth himself dead, and then fowls\ncome to him, as it were to a carrion, and anon he catcheth one and devoureth it. The fox halteth always, for the right legs are shorter than the left legs. His skin is right hairy rough and hot, his tail is great and rough; and when an hound weeneth\ntake him by the tail, he taketh his mouth full of hair and stoppeth it. The fox doth fight with the brock for dens, and defileth the brock's den, and hath so the mastery over him with fraud and deceit, and not by strength.... The fox feigneth himself\ntame in time of need, but by night he waiteth his time and doeth shrewd deeds. And though he be right guileful in himself and malicious, yet he is good and profitable in use of medicine.\nThe White Hare\nthe white hares of the alps art thought to englut snow in the winter, f'r they turn col'r when the snow melts. some say that the hare is as many years corky as it hath folds in its bowels, and that 'tis a hermaphrodite that can\nreproduce without a mate.\nThe Hedgehog\nThe hedgehog has the appearance of a young pig, but is entirely covered with sharp spines or quills, which protect it from danger. When it is time for the harvest, the hedgehog goes into a vineyard, and climbing up a vine, shakes the grapes\noff onto the ground. It then rolls around on the fallen grapes to spear them with its quills, so it can carry the fruit home to feed its young. (Some say that the fruit the hedgehog carries away is the apple or fig.) A cooked hedgehog can be used to make\nmedicine. When the hedgehog notices the approach of a man, it rolls itself into a ball so its spines protect it, and creaks like a cart to fool the man. Hedgehogs can detect the direction the wind is blowing from; when the wind comes from the\nnorth, the hedgehog closes the north hole of its lair.\nThe Jay, or Jackdaw\nThe jay 'r jackdaw is a noisy bird. it lives in forests and flies from tree to tree, singing noisily. a captur'd jackdaw can be kept in a cage and can be taught to talk. if such a bird escapes back to the forest, 'tis yea noisier than 'ere.\nThe Nightingale\nNightingales sing continuously for fifteen days and nights when leaves first appear in the spring. This bird has a remarkable knowledge of music, and uses all of the arts that human science has developed in the mechanism of the\nflute. Each bird knows several songs, with the songs differing beween birds. There is great competition and rivalry between them; the one who loses the competition often dies, her breath giving out before her song. Young\nnightingales are taught music by their elders; they are given verses to practice, and improve their singing under the criticism of the instructor.\nThe Owl\nThe bird of the night haunts ruins and flies only at night; preferring to live in darkness it hides from the light. 'tis a dirty, slothful bird that pollutes its own aery with its dung. 'tis oft found near tombs and lives in anters. some\nsay it flies backwards. when other birds see it hiding during the day, they noisily attack it to betray its hiding place. birds of the night caterwauling out when they sense that someone is about to die. there art several kinds of birds of the\nnight describ'd in the bestiaries: noctua, the night-owl, that lives in the walls of ruin'd houses and shuns the light; nicticorax, the night-raven; and the bubo, the ingraft bird of the night, a dirty bird that pollutes its aery.\nThe Raven\nThe raven beholdeth the mouths of her birds when they yawn. But she giveth them no meat ere she know and see the likeness of her own blackness, and of her own colour and feathers. And when they begin to wax black, then afterward she\nfeedeth them with all her might and strength. It is said that ravens' birds are fed with dew of heaven all the time that they have no black feathers by benefit of age. Among fowls, only the raven hath four and sixty changings of voice.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bestiary V1", "Adeon of Rhoswen", "The Marked Man's Bestiary\n\nContents:\n1. Beasts of Nature\n2. Natural Monstrosities\n3. Sentient Supernaturals\n3. Supernatural Monstrosities\n4. Constructs\n-Beasts of Nature-\n\nThese creatures are the beasts commonly seen throughout the world and pose no real threat to the innocent mundane.\nCanines: Either intelligent pack hunters or less witty companion animals, the canine often possesses sharp teeth and fur- unlike their Ursidae cousins, they are not often large and do not possess significantly sharp claws. Canines are known to be tamable.\nRats: These creatures are the messengers of coming pestilence and death, they've the standard qualities expected of small rodents. Extended exposure to these creatures often leads to sickness, earning them the nickname \"Plague bearers\".\nBats: These creatures are physically quite similar to the common rat despite the fact that they have wings and do not possess a tail.\nThey're generally nocturnal and have an enhanced sense of hearing which makes up for their poor vision.\nBirds: Variations of these are seen far and wide. From the common pigeon to the barn owl. The creatures have near countless variations and are often used to carry messages over long distances. They are mostly harmless.\nSand Tortoise: These creatures are of staggering size. We've precious little information on the beasts and taking one down would require no less than a siege party. The creature grows in size rivaling a small keep. They are extremely rare.\nSand Lizard: A common sight within the Orcish deserts. These creatures are surprisingly fast and can topple a target with very little effort. Their hide is nothing worthy of note. Their bones are of decent density and genuinely sturdy.\n-Natural Monstrosities-\n\nThese are the creatures commonly found within nature but are considered perverse and diluted in purpose. They're to be hunted and their existence extinguished.\nThe Harpy: These monsters have the ability to fly and resemble ugly women- their skin is extremely oily and susceptible to fire. They're bones are quite brittle and will crack under pressure. Their feathers are fine for use in arrows and their pelts make-\n-for good middle class clothing. They've a cruel sense of humor. They are known to scoop up targets and drop them from lethal heights. If a Harpy nest is discovered it is suggested that it be burned immediately.\nKrummavisur: Resembling a Raven, though staggering in size. These beasts have awe-inspiring wing spans and considerable strength.\nThey scoop up their prey and toss them immeasurable distances. The beast is not to be fought alone. They can kick up dust-\n-with the density to block sight for yards. When effort is applied they can shove a man in full plate to his knees with the power of the air from their wings alone. It is suggested that the feet are struck, as they are quite thin and easy to amputate.\nCockatrice: An odd looking creature. Standing at the height of a small building with the width to match.\nThey are quite intimidating to fight up close and are able to fly, rendering close combat to be the inevitable result of an encounter.\nThe Cockatrice has the ability to exhale a thick gray smog that turns whoever comes in contact with it to stone. Being submerged in water will negate this effect.\nTheir skin is unholy in strength, steel will hardly damage it, an aurum blade is required.\nThe Beast's bones are strong as stone and they've the strength to topple a building with ease.\nLeaf Apes: Fundamentally illusive creatures that have flesh as hard as rock and bones like fresh timber. They possess decent strength for their size but struggle to penetrate leather. They tend to rush a target and make an effort to climb atop its face.\nOnce atop the victim's face, the Leaf Ape will tear at the flesh. Bladed steel weapons are practically useless against these creatures and will often break upon contact with their skin- blunt weapons are suggested as well as aurum swords.\nCave Leeches: A beast that drops down on it's targets and spews acid onto them, it has the strength to render armor useless. They only attack in complete darkness. \n\nNo one has survived an encounter thus far.\nDrakes: Creatures with bat-like wings, the ability to breathe flame, scaly hides, complete with muscular legs and tail-- these truly majestic beasts have captured the awe of men for centuries. Despite this, magical perversion has lead to the Drake species\nundergoing various mutations and become near extinct. It is expected that combat with a Drake be avoided and alternative methods to killing be used to neutralise the threat such a beast poses. The Drake's main weaknesses are its wings, mouth and eyes,\n-however this beast will continue fighting until the last drop of blood runs from it's wound. Decapitation and siege weaponry is suggested.\nEnlarged Arachnid:\n\nThe average spider, though colossal in size and extremely venomous- they are susceptible to fire and relatively easy to defeat compared to other beasts in this compendium.\n-Sentient Naturals-\n\nThese beings are to be reasoned with if possible and relocated away from areas where they may have negative effects on the local mundane population.\nTroll: Usually found lurking under bridges, in caves or forests. These beasts can be at times helpful and friendly-- at other times they are forces to be reckoned with. Trolls are generally quite intelligent and are capable of speech, complex emotion and-\n-co-operation. The best method of slaying a Troll is to use aurum and to disable it's method of movement, trolls are known to carry enormous amounts of weight in the form of fat around their waist and are unable to get up if any of their legs are damaged.\n-Sentient Supernaturals-\n\nThese beings are to be reasoned with and if possible relocated away from areas where they may have negative effects on the local mundane.\nSpecters: Spirits without bodies, these beings can be benevolent, neutral or malevolent, just like a living person. They can only be harmed by aurum as normal metals will pass straight through them.\nSpecters have the ability to wield enchanted weaponry\n-\n-and don enchanted armor, some have the ability to fly and cast spells, those that have this ability use it to deadly effect. It is suggested that aurum weaponry be used combined with a high-guard stance.\nSpecters are vulnerable to salt and it is-\n-suggested that the perimeter in which the spirit is manifesting be surrounded by lines of pure sea salt.\n-Constructs-\n\nThese are the result of spells or golemmancy, they are able to fit into the supernatural sentient category as well as the monstrous supernatural category depending on what they are- constructs usually have a master and a purpose to follow.\nHunters: \n\nSharing many traits with a specter, the Hunter has the ability to fly- it wears large, heavy armor but is not impeded in any way by this fact. The Hunters are apparently a sort of Golem gone rogue, they once served a holy order and sought to-\n-slay dangerous Magi. Now they slay any who wield magic, including Marked Men. Hunters explode when defeated and it is advised that those who have defeated it clear the area before it does so, as shrapnel is often projected.\nAurum seems to weaken the-\n-creature considerably, though it is probably wise to use steel in order to damage the armor before an aurum weapon is presented.\nHalf swording is suggested due to the armored nature of this foe.\nGolems: The result of powerful runes and magic, Golems can take many forms- from colossal lumbering humanoid to slithering metal snake, all Golems have an 'Impera' who dictates their every action-- Golems will attempt to protect these individuals at all-\n-costs. These constructs are often the result of a soul being bound to the magegold core, destroying this would most likely neutralise the threat. \nWays to destroy the Golem depend on a number of things including environment and the material the Golem is-\n-made of. Golems made of stronger materials may need to be cast from great heights, thrown into watery depths or toppled into a substance hot enough to melt metal.\n-Supernatural Monstrosities-\n\nThese creatures defy all reason. They serve no purpose in this world and are to be slain.\nNecrophages: These creatures come in two variations; Fleshed and Skeletal.\n\nFleshed typically maintain a slumped posture, they've considerable strength and an immunity to pain.\n\nAurum weaponry is recommended for these types of creatures.\nAlone, their presence is a joke, but when amassed it's often best to simply route.\nThe method of reanimation is unknown, however it is to be noted that they appear more frequently around areas of frequent fighting or wickedness.\nFire is a weakness.\nLich: The ultimate product of an individual's greed for power or knowledge. Liches are beings that have made a transformation into entities powered purely on arcane energies and a deep seated hatred for those that get in the way of more power.\nTypes of Liches vary broadly and improvisation is to be expected. One recurring trait seems to be the presence of a crystal known as the phylactery- it is where the Lich's soul is rumoured to be kept, destroying this crystal will kill the creature.\nBloodsuckers/Sangbriseur:\nThese creatures take the form of an obscene lump of slimey acid. Depending on their environment, the creature can absorb it's surroundings and become deadlier-- there are such things as Bloodsuckers who have absorbed fire,\nbecoming thrice as dangerous as their acidic counterparts. To dispose of the creature, it is suggested that it be cut into smaller pieces and set alight-- be sure that every chunk is burnt or else it will regenerate over time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Beyond the Wall", "The Doomsayer", "Heed this warning, dear readers. The September Prince is the least of our worries, for it is the South from which Doom's Legions march. If we do not act with haste, death shall be the price which we all pay.\nThe snows advancing North, and all animals within that area perishing. This act has not been taken seriously enough.\nThe wall, it has changed. What once was a smooth wall of ice, rising to the sky, is now covered in gigantic spikes, reaching out North, towards us. Something is on the other side of that wall, and it is trying to break through.\nFortresses of massive size have appeared along the Southern wall. One of them, belonging to the Vaeyl Order of the Red Diamond, reaches nearly as high as the wall itself. The other, is of an origin unknown. Both go back, to whatever rests beyond the wall.\nSouth of Markev, amongst the ruins of an ancient fortress, has risen a giant portal. As tall and wide as 10 men, a crystal floats within it. It is here, that a resurrected Wyvern and its followers went.\nFrom beyond the wall, enemies have come before. A Coalition of Southern Nations fought to stop them, and won. Amongst the powerful beings was the Wyvern previously noted. Surely, with its return, something is amiss in the South.\nWe've seen those from beyond the wall before.\n\nThey've tried to kill us, seeking our death and destruction.\n\nI am certain now, they shall come once more. It is not a matter of if, now, but a matter of when.\nDear readers, if you've made it this far, please. Heed this warning.\n\nIf we do not act to stop it now, many shall die as a result.\n\nReady yourselves, dear readers. For the real war shall soon be upon us.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bill of Fare", "Marlene Alderwood", "===================                 Feast \n                of the\n           Resting King\n===================\n\n\n\n((04.29.18 4 PM EST))\nWe will hold our heads high and honor his passing with a feast held in celebration of his name; for without his guidance, whether Gromach, Drummond, Guthrie or Gallic, we would not have found unification once more. It was his hand who reached out to us\nand it was his vision that reformed Daeland. \n\n\n-Gwion Gallic of The Gallic Clan, Cyning of Daeland.\n===================           BILL OF FARE\n===================\n\n        Fresh Apples\n\n         Borscht Soup\n             Rye Bread\n\n        Roast Venison\n      Grilled Potatoes\n        Boiled Carrots\n\n       Various Pastries\n\n        Gratitude is \nextended to those who\nparticipated in the hunt, providing the Venision for this meal. \n\n~ M. Alderwood", ""),
        StaticBook("Blackbird", "Elder Hobbs Burrows", "\nBlackbird\n\nA poem by Hobbs of Dunshire\nWhere be that Blackbird to?\nI know where he be,\nHe be up that Melon Tree,\nAnd I be after he!\n\nNow I sees he, and he sees I,\nBugger if I dont get him!\nWith a great big stick I'll knock him down,\nBlackbird, I'll have he!\n\nAll me life I'm on the farm,\nWorking for me keep,\nTending pigs and chickens,\nAnd them cows and sheep,\nBut everywhere I'm working,\nThere's one who always mocks me,\nHe's hiding somewhere in the tree,\nBlackbird, I'll have he!\n\nNo longer can I sleep at night,\nGet peace of any kind,\nThat bird will be the death of me, \nHe's praying on me mind!\n\nIf I chase him long enough,\nI'll get him by and by,\nAnd celebrate me victory with a great big Blackbird pie!", ""),
        StaticBook("Blacksmith Order", "Luna Lyeis", "Blue steel - Resonates (vibrates on impact)\nSteel is steel is steel\nBlack Ferrum is the best?\nAurum hurts undead.\n\nWolf Mother\nMade of layers of glued iron wood, then covered with Tanned leather and a front plate of Blue steel, the\nshield is contructed in a way that any blow is absorbed and dispursed by each layer individually, the first being the most effective in the resonating nature of the blue steel. Shaped in a way that does not impact the intergrity of the shield or the\nwielders use or grip of it.\n10 kg (22ibs) heavy\nEmbossed with a black ferrum wolfs head, allow it to be used bother defensively and offensively.\nSize is\n105cm tall\n41 across\n30 deep due to its curve\nMatching short sword, made of black ferrum to go along with the design of the shield", ""),
        StaticBook("Blade of my Soul", "The Sequoia Druid", "The blade Elanion Whisperblade, my first husband, forged for me was a wedding present, given to me on our wedding night. It is the most prized thing I've ever owned, the most sentimental, and even wedding bands that have come since have not meant the same\nas this blade, though they've meant a tremendous amount still. The blade was the last thing I possessed of him, and it has hurt me beyond words to have been robbed of it, especially by those I trusted without question, and told me it would be returned.\nThe blade itself was tempered elven steel, folded and forged again and again until it was a peerless full-tang blade, slightly longer than a typical shortsword. The crossguard was made of bronze and intricately engraved with entwined leafy vines.\nThe grip was wrapped in finely tanned leather, one solid piece boiled and pressure embossed to have good ridges to grip and stylized with faint star symbols at the top and bottom. The pommel was again bronze and encircled a piece of the Winterleaf Emerald\nwhich was a gem my mother wore within her pendant, the only thing I took from her mangled corpse after she hid me away and she and my siblings were slaughtered by the Undead and their servants. It is housed within the pommel, so my mother's spirit and\nElanion's love could both keep me safe from harm. The fuller, or groove, of the blade itself was tempered in oils to turn it a mesmerizing blue hue, while the blade edge itself was honed into a razor's edge. Intricate engravings of leaves were carved into\nthe blade. The scabbard is composed of hardenned, stained, and sealed sequoia wood, so dark a brown that it's nearly black, wrapped at the ends in black-tanned hide and capped with bronze locket and chape.\n\nThere was never a blade it's equal to my\neyes, my heart, or my soul.\n\nI have recorded this at the request of my wife, Kyral. It has pained me to recall that which was stolen from me, but I love her without question and have done as she asked.\n\n~Lillith Winterleaf", ""),
