        StaticBook("Cannell Cession", "Klaudia", "The Cannell Cession \n         of 1686      \n===================\n\n\n       The 10th of \n     Firstseed, 1686\n\n\n\n\n\n   By: Klaudia Vulnear\n===================In the year 1686, the County of Cyrilsburg and the Cannell family have come to the agreement by which the following has been set forth and decided upon. \n\n\n\n\n==================\n===================Article 1\n\nAll property ever belonging to any of the Cannell family shall hearby be given freely and without any form of monetary compensation to the County of Cyrilsburg.\n\n\n==================\n===================Article 2\n\nThe Cannell family naval vessel shall also be ceded to the city. All titles of ownership shall be immediatly transfered to the city and thus the Lord of Cyrilsburg.\n\n\n==================\n===================Article 3\n\nThe Cannell family shall forfeit any and all claims, whether they be historical, cultural, or any other form; upon the lands in which have been agreed upon. This shall also include any and all personal \n===================\n===================belongings, animals, and all other forms of objects left on the estate after the given time for the family to leave has expired. The family is to never lay claim to any of these lands again. If they do, the\n===================\n===================County of Cyrilsburg has full authority to issue any form of punishement or retaliation they deem fit. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n==================\n===================Article 4\n\nIn exchange for the land, it has been agreed upon that the bodies of those Cannell members currenlty residing within familys graves within the lands of the estate, shall never be removed or placed \n==================\n===================elsewhere.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n==================\n===================Article 5\n\nShould any resources of any amount and or quality be found within the lands of the Cannell property. The claim to such items shall solely be to that of the County of Cyrilsburg. In no manner will the Cannell =================\n===================family be allowed to exert any false claims to these resources. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n==================\n===================By signing this legally binding document, the Cannell family hereby recognizes and agrees to obey the rules in which these articles set forth. \n\n\nSignature of the Cannell signatory:\nAmber Caden Cannell\n==================", ""),
        StaticBook("Cannell Cession", "Thornn Mauntel", "The Cannell Cession\n         of 1686\n===================\n\n\n      The 10th of\n    Firstseed, 1868\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n===================In the year of 1686, the County of Cyrilsburg and the Cannell family have come to the agreement by which the following has been set forth and decided upon.\n\n\n\n\n==================\n===================Article 1\n\nAll property ever belonging to any of the Cannell family shall hereby be given freely and without any form of monetary compensation to the County of Cyrilsburg.\n\n\n==================\n===================Article 2\n\nThe Cannell family naval vessel shall also be ceded to the city. All titles of ownership shall be immediatly transfered to the city and thus to the Lord of Cyrilsburg.\n\n===================\n===================Article 3\n\nThe Cannell family shall forfeit any and all claims, whether they be historical, cultural, or any other form; upon the lands in which have been agreed upon. This shall also include any and all personal\n===================\n===================belongings, animals, and all otherforms of objects left on the estate after the given time for the family to leave has expired. The family is to never lay claim to any of these lands again. If they do, the\n===================\n===================County of Cyrilsburg has full authority to issue any form of punishment or retaliation they deem fit.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n==================\n===================Article 4\n\nIn exchange for the land, it has been agreed upon that the bodies of those Cannell members currently residing within the familys graves within the lands of the estate, shall never be\n==================\n===================removed or placed elsewhere.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n==================\n===================Article 5\n\nShould any resources of any amount and or quality be found within the lands of the Cannell property. The claim to such items shall solely be to that of the County of Cyrilsburg. In no manner will the \n==================\n===================family be allowed to exert any false claims to these resources.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n==================\n===================By signing this legally binding document, the Cannell family hereby recognizes and agrees to obey the rules in which these articles set forth.\n\n\n\n\n\n==================\n===================Signature of the Cannell signatory:\nAmber Caden Cannell\n\nSignature of the Cyrilsburg Ambassador:\nKlaudia Vulnear \n\nSignature of the Cyrilsburg Grand Ambassador: Thornn Mauntel", ""),
        StaticBook("Canonist Figures", "Cuthwin Wheaton", "Canonist Figures        and their Symbolism\n\nOriginally published by Hektor the Skinless Loremaster.\n\nRecovered by Scribe Cuthwin Wheaton for the Dragur Public Library.\nExalted/Prophets\nHoren \"the Father\", represented by a Golden Laurel. The patron of Humanity, Covenants, and Humility\nOwyn I \"the Purifier\", represented by a flaming war. The patron of Purity, War and Fire.\nGodfrey I \"the Redeemer\", represented by a Silver Scepter. The patron of Dominion, Glory and Justice.\nSiegmund I \"the Preserver\", represented by a Globus Cruciger. The  patron of Clairvoyance, Wisdom and Sight.\nSaints\nSt. Godwin of Paradisus, represented by a skull. The patron saint of the dead, afterlife, spirits, the supernatural and Heartlanders.\nSt. Julia of Paradisus,  represented by Golden Rings. The Patroness ...\nSaint of Mothers, Matrimony and Exorcism.\nSt Joren of Paradisus, represented by Iron Shackled. Patron Saint of the Mountains, Winter, the Imprisoned, and Highlanders.\nSt. Lothar of Balian, represented by a Lorraine Cross. The ...\nPatron Saint of the Lorraine Cross, Princes, Courage, and  Heraldry.\nSt Daniel of Al'Khazar, represented by a wooden staff. Patron Saint of peace, cities, pilgrims and travel.\nHigh Priest St. Everard I of Al'Khazar, represented by a red ...\ncross. The patron saint of Tradition and Persecution. \nSt. Amyas of Yore, represented by a wild  herb. The Patron Saint of Medicine, Healing, Botany, and Wild Herbs.\nSt. Godwein of Huntshill, represented by an Oaken Shield.\nThe Patron Saint of  honesty, woodworkers, fungi and skin afflictions.\nSt. Tobias of Sarkoz, represnted by a  comet comet and gold coin. Patron saint of merchants, comets, wealth and charity.\nHigh Pontiff St. Lucien I of Ulmsbottom, repre-\n-sented by a Kaedreni Cross. The Patron Saint of Crusaders, Change, and the family.\nSt. Adrian of Leuvaarden, represented by an open book. The Patron Saint of Statesmen,  Lawyers and Politics.\nSt. Thomas of Gaekrin, represented by a ...\nWhite Rose. The Patron Saint of Leadership, Discipline, Frontiersmen, and Keadrin.\nSt. Peter of Gaekrin, represented by a flaming rose. The Patron Saint of Order and Victory.\nSt. Humbert of Bar, represented by Sun's ...\nSmile. The Patron Saint of Capitulation.\nSt. Edmond of Lachsin, represented by a knight on horseback. The Patron Saint of  Sailing, The Navy,  Horses and the Auvergnian People.\nSt. Wilfriche of Hanseti, represented by a black mace. The ...\npatron saint of brotherhood, chancellors, opposition of setherin, and Canonist brotherhood martyrs. \nHigh Pontiff St. Daniel I, represented by an aged scroll. Patron Saint of Scholarship,  Fate and Literature.\nSt. Otto \"the Bald\" of Vanderfell,\nrepresented by a Bald Eagle. The Patron Saint of the Schism War, Fate, Ward Fathers, and Northern Peoples.\nSt. Charles of Haense, represented by a Golden Crow. Patron Saint of strength, fortitude, and prisoners of war.\nSt. Michael of Cordobe, represented by a White Bull. Patron Saint of passion, Exiles, Service and the Eighten Years' War.\nSt. Emma of Woldzmir, represented by a White Sword. Patron  Saint of the Schism War, Loyalty, Valour and Adrians.", ""),
        StaticBook("Captain's Log", ".", "Today is the day. The one hundreth day at sea. I would open a cask of wine, had we any left. It will be boiled water again, I suppose. Boiled water and biscuits.\n\nOn the bright side, we should reach the land of Atlas within just another week or two. We'll\nfind a port, and see what the locals know of Tharax. We have come too far now to give up. May the damned storms take me if I don't keep my vow and return home with the head of the Leviathan mounted on the bow of the Waterwraith.\n\nWe're nearing a port\nknow. Within the day, even. The thought is an alarming one after so long at sea. We've seen some fishing trawlers - it can't be far now.\n\nOne of the lookouts spotted a mast sticking above the water. A shipwreck! Storms know I have little interest in\nsunken treasure, but this might be the work of Tharax! It could be a clue! We must investigate.", ""),
        StaticBook("Captain's Log #1", "Finalhazard", "Captain's Log:\n\nAlas! Our galleon ran into a mighty storm that pushed us into some rocks, forcin' us t' abandon the 'Esmeralda' and take residence upon this here island. According to my first mate, we be not thee only ones here.\nMy first mate has reported that thee trees and bushes be always shufflin' about. I have reason to believe it's just thee wind. None of these islands be charted, meaning that no one else has visited them.\nDay 2: What I had previously said 'bout thee island havin' no inhabitants be false. 'tis land his home t' many tribal people. Many o' them have magical abilities.  Some o' them, be knowin' o' thee void's existence while others proclaim that\nthee gods bestow them thee abilities t' cast flames from their hands.\nDay Unknown:\n\nChapter 1:\n\nThee culture o' each tribe be extremely difference from thee next. Many o' them, if not a vast majority o' them hate each other as many o' them be at war with one another.\nSeein' as how our galleon has been completely destroyed, me men and I have decided t' try t' communicate with thee tribals in order t' figure out how t' survive here on thee isles they call 'Vailor'.\"\nTh' Ral'skas, th' Blind Bandits (who be all, actually blind one way or another), th' 'Kraskls, 'n th' Leafroots, among hundreds 'o others be all tribes within Vailor.\nSome 'o be here fer only a dozen or so years, while others have be here fer hundreds 'o years, or so they claim.\nMe First matey, Logan Proudwell, who be in his only in his early thirties has told me that th' crew be plannin' a mutiny. They feel me leadership isn't whar it be 'n that th' natives gunna murder them in their sliumber.\nUnfortunately, 'tis means that I must make a decision. As th' cap'n I decided that 'tis best if th' crew 'n I part ways. them that wish to help be rebuild th' Lusty Rose gunna stay wit' me, while th' others gunna have to find their own way,\nor join up wit' th' tribes.\nChapter 2:\n\n 'tis plan worked well, as I met wit' many 'o th' chieftains. They decided which 'o me former-crew 'n chose whom would fit in best wit' each tribe.  I then sent me own First matey, Logan to join th' Leafroots in order\nto act as a spy. ye spy wit' ye eye, th' Leafroots be currently th' strongest tribe.  They wield no magic, 'n they be also th' smallest in numbers. But they be th' eldest, which provides them wit' th' most wisdom, 'n wisdom be everythin' in their culture.\nChapter 4:\n\nConstruction on our newest ship, th' 'Lusty Rose II' has begun. 'tis be a year since th' crew split, 'n I haven't heard word from Logan, which leads me to believe that he's either in Davy Jones' treasure chest, or successful in his mission.\nChapter 5:\n\nSeven years later later 'n th' beautiful 'Lusty Rose II' can finally drop her sails. She's a fine vessel, much better than her predecessor, meanin' she'll brin' us back to th' cove in less than a a year.\nChapter 6: Departure\n\nTh' sun has just set 'n bin finally heart back from me first matey, Logan. He has befriended th' youngest Leafroot, a dark-skinned knife-eared fella' by th' moniker 'o Ri'va.\nIt hadn't be brought to me attention that 'tis whole the hour their true family-moniker was T'sagari,  'n that Leafroot was th' common-moniker given to them by other common-speakin' people that landed on Vailor.\nSo, Ri'vi T'sagari be his true title. Movin' on, at th' moment Ri'va be tied up 'n gunna be our trophy that we'll brin' home back to th' cove.  Seein' as how his family expects him to be off on a pilgrimage, they won't expect him to disappear.\nye spy wit' ye eye, every T'sagari leaves home to be off on a pilgrimage in order to discover their 'bond wit' nature', or somethin' to that notion. 'tis a comin' 'o age ceremony. They don't come back fer hundreds 'o years, if at all.\nLogan was goin' to take his sister, but th' females don't be off on pilgrimages like their male-counterparts.\nFinal Notes:\n\nIn case the hour takes me mind away, bin decided to keep a second cap'n's log in 'tis ship as a reminder that me treasure be still buried in 'tis island.\nRemember, ye don't trust ye own crew mates so ye hid it within a second journal. Chances be, th' savage animals (th' tribals) have that journal.", ""),
        StaticBook("Caribou I", "Caribou Druid Hyulahon", "Before coming into his glorious service, I had heard only legends of the being the unenlightened referred to as the 'September Prince'. This was all I was allowed to know as a hierophant. They called him the herald of a dream daemon, and said\nthat he was touched by dark magics. They whispered he was the spawn of devilry, and that he was a corrupted druid-turned-lord that dwelled in the depths of the Far Glade.\n\n\nThey muttered of\nunimaginable cruelties, conducted without purpose or reason. A true corruption of the will of the Aspects.\n\nI am pleased enough to report nothing further could be from the truth!\n\nEven when he was purging Malin's City,\nI could tell it was not without reason. I had always known it, the atrocities we committed every day against nature. Some of the others preached true union with nature, but they still lived in houses and wore shoes!\n\nOur prince has\nreturned, to deliver us from the corruption of the cities, even those built by the Founder. Not even elfkind will stand in his way.\n\nHe is mighty, like a mountain. The tree lords I saw while I was in the order were all puny things, but\nour prince puts them all to shame. To him, the civilizations of this world are simply many anthills, and we are many ants.\n\nEven the blood that drips from his wounds as he heals has power. The frogs outside the lake murmur in tongues!\nThey seem to be growing more, every day. I am curious how far our prince’s blood will take them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Caribou II", "Caribou Druid Hyulahon", "I have heard tales before of word altars. Ancient artifacts of power and tongues, that could allow its bearer to control whole swathes of forest. In their stone was carved the true tongue of the Aspects, and of all nature. When it was spoken, the world\nlistened.\n\nLegend holds that, before they were outlawed, in Malin's City itself, there was entombed a word altar. This was before my time in the order, and so all I know of are the stories. I am not sure if it was real. Perhaps it was all a\nmyth. It matters very little, for now that our prince is here, we have no need for myths or legends any longer.\n\nWhen he speaks, the world listens in ways I cannot begin to describe. The smallest insect can be compelled by his\nvoice, just as the largest of the scaddernaks can be. I have seen even the rain and earth tremble at his behest. The sky sunders itself by his command, and the waters leave the ocean so that he may walk across the sandy beds. There have been miracles\nthat no mere druid would ever be capable of.\n\nIt makes me more certain than ever that our prince is the will of nature made manifest.\n\nWe need no word altar to see nature's revenge upon the\nconstructions of men, for we need only our prince.", ""),
        StaticBook("Caribou III", "Caribou Druid Hyulahon", "Our prince's wood is the trembling giant, the quaking aspen. Truly, a magnificent display of our highest power, for he has done what no other lord of the tree has done: spread. Whole swathes of land have turned green, flourishing with brilliant emerald\nleaves. His soul is the largest, grandest one of them all, stretching from sea to sea, and beneath the earth in gargantuan roots.\n\nIt is an old druidic proverb that all of nature is connected, but it is embodied in none more clearly than our prince. The\nair and water flowing, and he sees and feels it all. In his whisperings, he has spoken of how he can hear the cries of all nature, across all the world.\n\nEvery blade of grass, trampled in man's foolish lust for progress. Each tree\nfelled so that he can feed the furnace of his ambition. Our prince feels them, and truly, is there anything more to being a druid? Following our prince is the closest we can be to following the Aspects themselves.\n\nSo, this is why we must go out, and\npurge the violet corruption. Ever since our prince journeyed south, the violet corruption has gripped the land, tainting his trees, one by one. They have committed a terrible atrocity in fracturing his soul. I have even heard word that the\ndark power behind them has calved the trees, forcing them to produce seeds in a most unnatural way.\n\nThe bright green flame has scorched many to ash, but still, I fear in some isolated pockets of the world, the purple-leafed abominations still\nrest.\n\nWoe! This curse of sleep. Were only it not so strong, we could hunt them all down. Though… should I sleep, I do wonder if the totem of the Caribou will live on. It is a rare path to take. Oh well. There are more important things\nto consider, now.", ""),
        StaticBook("Carnatian Sketch", "Septimius Bracchus", "Preamble:\nPublius Bracchus was the First Archchancellor of the Imperium Quintus, veteran of a war against Urguan and in the Duke's War. Travelling often in his career, he made many sketches of John I's Empire. Here are his of Carnatia. Enjoy.\n[Now imagine some detailed pictures of infrastucture and street scenes in Carnatia.]\nPrologue:\nPublius' service represented the zenith of the Bracchus clan. Though these sketches are invaluable in our appreciation of his memory, we respect what it may do for yours in this time of brotherhood with Adria.\nSigned,\n     Septimius                   Braccus", ""),
        StaticBook("Carter's Origins", "Carter Wales", "\"Carter Wales' Backstory\"\n\nLong ago, during the Holy Orenian Empire's reign, there was a war between the Elves and the Humans.\nThe Elves and the Humans despised each other very much, willing to sacrifice everything to kill each other. Because of this\nmadness, Axios had became a wasteland filled with heartless battles.\nThen once upon a night, during the siege of Haelun'or, a young human by the name of Adonia Misma, was among the warriors of the Orenian legion. \nThe look of determination was evident in\nher features as she took down incredible numbers of High Elves. Coming to take one of her final kills, she was stopped by an Elven warrior named Altair Wales.\nThese two engaged in a battle of a lifetime, none seeming to give up to the other.\nAs Altair had dropped to his knees, desperately needing some air, Adonia was stricken by his sharp features.\nShe didn't want to kill him so she left him with a warning, \"Don't ever cross my path again vermin,\" before she took off with her squad mates.\nAltair, too, was stricken by the young lass. She surely knew how to use a sword. He escaped to the tunnels of the now lost city and made his way to the Wooden Elves' City: Malin.\nThere, he made a very good friend in a man named Victor Amud.\nHe kept him in his inn and helped him practice for the upcoming war.\nA few months later, Adonia met Altair again but in a different situation. Her leg had been molded under a burnt wood and none of her mates had came to help.\nAltair was making his usual movements in the trees before he heard the sound of a distressed woman.\nHe followed the sound and here he saw Adonia in pain. With all his might, he removed the wood and carefully picked up the Human.\nEven throughout her cries of annoyance, he could hear the tone of gratefulness under her breath.\nHe took her back to the inn and with the help of Victor, both of them tended to the aids of the injured woman.\nLong story short, Altair and Adonia became close and soon, Adonia was carrying his first born. They were able to keep the baby as a secret until his first birthday but a mishap had happened.\nSomeone had snitched on Adonia and she was seized out of the inn by the Wooden Elves' guards. Altair made their job a lot harder but how much can one man do?\nAltair fled the inn with their child and followed the soldiers to their next stop: The Kingdom of Renatus.\nKing Canonius I asked specifically for the hanging of Adonia Misma on accounts for Treason against her kin.\nThe night before her execution, Altair had snuch into her cell and for the last time in his life, held the woman he loved in his arms.\nThe following morning, high up in the trees with his son, Altair watched as his beloved stood up on the wooden stool....\nand lost the last breath she had in her body.\nHe cried and cried as he held his baby boy in his arms. \"My love, I love you. May your spirit be with our child as he grows up to be the man that you want him to be.\"\nHe looked at his sleeping son and kissed his head, \"For I know that this is the last time I'm going to hold you and for that, I am grateful.\"\nAltair made his last journey to the inn and handed Victor his son.\nHe laid out all the necessary things Victor had to do with his son and said his last goodbyes.\n\nSon, I'm not telling you this to make you feel better, no, I'm telling you this to make you stronger.\nThe more you know about your history, the more the power of knowledge flows through you.\nNow, the last time I heard about your father was that King Canonius had captured him and beheaded him and laid his remnants next to your mother's.\nI know that this is a lot to hear about but for the next chapter of your life, you need to leave Axios. There is nothing here for you but pain and misery. Begin a new life in Atlas and explore the origins of your parents.\nHell, even find love while you're at it. But don't forget, your parents are always with you.\n\n~Victor Amud", ""),
        StaticBook("Carthography of", "Ithilion Drakon", "Carthography of the Dominion's Capital, Caras Eldar.\n\nUpon first walking up towards Caras Eldar via the main road one finds themselves between two higher elevated corners of ground, making it a smaller valley. The front gate has a double iron gate\nWith high watch towers at either side hidden in the trees.\n\nGenerally speaking the city is mostly covered from above by the trees, the walls as high as 50 ft. The same goes for the back of the capital, the docks.\nIt has multiple ships a fleet no larger\nThan five ships. A few of the ships are 'safe' within the harbor that has a massive water gate to keep it from being assaulted.\n If one were to attack it'd be best to do from the Western wall, it's the least covered and borders water closely, an\nassault wouldn't be easily spotted from there, neither do the guards usually come over there as nothing usually happens. The military barracks are in the center of the city, allowing them to get to every place as a regular pace, not too fast not too slow.\nThe eastern side has the keep itself, it stands higher than the rest thanks to it being on a mountain, it has various houses under it. One of which is owned by one of our allies, who also has Dominion equipment to spare. (One could attack with their\nuniforms)\n\nAnd the southern side has the high walls, front gate, well-defended with watch towers and appears to be covered best. Assault is still adviced from the western side.", ""),
        StaticBook("Catapult Rules", "Jaya Jayamen", "Catapult\n           Rules\nCatapult is a simple 2 player game. There are four rows and four columns that make up the grid((on each side of the double chest)). Each row has a letter, each column has a number.\n(( the columns will be labeled on papers on the top line of the double chest, the rows will be labeled by papers in the middle vertical line of the doublechest.))\nYou decide where to put your carts, one three squares long on the grid, and one 2 squares long on the grid.\n((either have the locations on the grid where you put your carts in mind or have a staff member write the positions that both players chose down on a piece of paper and signs it. This can prevent cheating.))\nFor example, I could choose 1A, 2A, 3A for my first three square long cart, and 4D and 4C for my two square long cart. ((you do not mark where your carts are on the grid))\nThe 3 square cart squares must be touching vertically or horizontally, not diagonal, same with the 2 square cart.\nAfter you decide your cart positions and your opponent has as well, and you both are ready, the game starts and you cannot change your cart locations until this game is over.\nBoth players roll a 20 sided dice to see who goes first (( use /roll 20 )). The player with the highest number goes first. The person who takes the first turn picks a number and a letter.\nIn that square if the opponent assigned part of one of their carts there the opponent must say “hit” and the person who hit the other person’s cart marks that spot on their side with a red token ((red wool)).\nIf it is a miss, the opponent says ‘Miss” and the person who missed the other person’s cart marks that spot on their side with a blue token ((blue wool)). Then the turns alternate.\nWhen one players 3 long cart or 2 long cart are fully hit, meaning that each square assigned to one of the carts is hit, the player must let their opponent know which one has been destroyed\n(destroyed mean that all squares of one of the carts has been hit). If a player’s 3 long cart and 2 long cart both are hit completely, then that player loses and the other wins.", ""),
        StaticBook("CCP Missive", "Belvitian CCP", "17th of Godfrey's Triumph.\n\nFellow Belvitians, we are here today to tell you about the Priorist plot to run Ostrobum Carrion against our beloved former Duke, John, THE GOOD. The Priorist party will attempt to colonize our fair city in the name of fear!\nCan anyone verify that this Ostrowho Carrion actually lives within our beutiful, beloved, bright, brick city? He seems to have moved here to leech on the coat tails of his Ducal Brother, a man who actually made a name for himself.\nThe Priorists claim to represent the working class and the army, yet their candidate is one who comes from the cushy class they renounce in their party platform. Pointing to their party platform, it is completely alien to that of the realities in our fair\ncity. Do you all remember when John THE GOOD chased the inquisition out of our town for their attempts to harrass hard working migrant elf workers. Do you remember his Ducal Order protecting their rights within Renatus and Adria?\nThese Priorists are just the Inquisition in powdered wigs instead of Chantry uniforms! They claim to be of the lower class, yet, their spokesmen is a Horen and their candidate is a Carrion, the two most priveledged houses. John THE GOOD came from humble\nbeginnings, working as a bartender in the old capital. He led our people to a new homeland and protected them and will continue to work for them everyday! He has partenered with those in the CCP party due to their respect for vassal rights and commitment\nto the protection of migrant elves and minorities within the Imperium. The Fearorist Party must be defeated through the ballot box. Take a stand against hypocritical Horens that stand to gain from turning the citizens of the empire\nagainst each other.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cernunnos", "Taynuel Xayarath", "~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\nCernunnos\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nThe Great Huntsman\nThe Green Man\nThe Horned God\n\nBestowed Druidic Ability: Control of Nature\nGoverning Seasons: Summer and Winter\nWoe to thee who might seek to prey upon the flock of Lord Cernunnos. Legends speak of arrows being loosed upon the skies in numbers uncountable, raining upon those that seek to disrupt the careful balance of nature.\nIt was he who gave the porcupine its quills, the rattlesnake its fangs, and he who first taught the Elves of ancient times the art of bowmanship. Cernunnos waits patiently at the side of Cerridwen, guarding her peace with the vigil of a hawk and the calm\nof an evergreen forest.\n\nTo experience Cernunnos is to experience true challenge. You must hide yourself amidst the canopy of a great green forest, your body obscured by a cloak of leaves\nyou stitched together with pine needles and sap, your stomach howling for the smallest hint of nourishment, your fingers wrapped tightly around a bowstring as you stalk your prey on the forest floor. You must stand steady and vigilant at world's\nend, bloody and broken, and counter the pain with courage and skill.\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\nRituals and Beliefs\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nTo this day, all Elves owe their natural affinity for archery to Cernunnos. It is\nbelieved he personally taught the ancient Elven lord, Malin, the art as a means to balance the diplomatic race against more violent beings.\n\nIn times of war, it is quite common to hear calls of courage and steadiness in the name\nof the Huntsman.\n\nMany of the greatest druids have taken an affinity for Cernunnos, and some believe him to be the leader of the Aspectual Trinity.\n\nWhen druids have a goal in mind, they often refer to it\nas a hunt in reference to the Huntsman.\n\nThe condition of Albinism is often attributed as a blessing from Cernunnos. Creatures with a pure, white coat are predisposed as honorable and majestic beasts.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cerridwen", "Taynuel Xayarath", "~*~*~*~*~*~*~\nCerridwen\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nThe Green Lady\nGoddess of Life\nMother of the Morn\nLady of Light\n\nBestowed Druidic Ability: Nature's Healing\nGoverning Season: Spring\nIt is said that whenever the sun rises, so too does the great Springmother. Cerridwen's divine light breathes life into the cold darkness each morning, replenishing the weary with renewed strength and vigor. During the creation of the world she is said\nto have personally sculpted every flower and fruit, every nut and vegetable into an object of replenishment and beauty. Cerridwen's love for the world is unconditional, and she desires peace above all else.\nTo experience Cerridwen is to experience the purest form of bliss. You must run barefoot through a bright meadow in the spring-time, your hair down and blowing in the warm breeze as the sunlight washes over your sealed eyelids.\nYou must kneel at the edge of a coursing stream and stare down at your reflection, watching the myriad of colorful fish swimming by without much care in the world. You must hold an infant in your arms, helpless, trusting, and know what it is to be a\nmother.\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\nRituals and Beliefs\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nWhen any new life is brought into the world, Cerridwen is believed to watch over them as any mother would. For this reason\nthe phenomenon of 'Baby Luck' is often attributed to her.\n\nCerridwen's recognized symbol is the sun, which can commonly be found in druidic libraries as a depiction of 'illuminating the darkness of ignorance'.\nSmall shrines to Cerridwen can be found in family gardens or farms to ward off pests and encourage a good harvest.\n\nThe officiant of a marriage often blesses the lucky couple with words of Cerridwen to encourage\na long, and child-filled life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru II", "March Ash", "The ashes fall like snowflakes. I taste its sludge on my tongue. Sulfur on my lips. In this wound of the world I feel more alive than in any other place. Beneath my feet beats the pounding pulse of the planet.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru IV", "March Ash", "The serenity of ice. The air is exceptionally clear here. The sky is very beautiful. They told me, once, that nature is the true source of beauty. All that we try to make is an imperfect clay mold. Perhaps they were right.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru IX", "March Ash", "In salt and ice eternal.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru V", "March Ash", "The smell of the sea, like brine, seaweed sex, and phytoplankton. It reminds me of salt. Soon, Axios will be washed away to nothing, like the rocks turned to sand by the ocean waves. Unfortunately, its death will not be as beautiful.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru VI", "March Ash", "Here, in the deep places of the world, they lay sleeping. Gods of scale and claw, sinew and muscle. Beneath rock and magma. The crust of the earth will sunder with their waking, when the Aspects call their banners for the final war.\nDid you think their grand weapons were the trees? No. Ends are made in blood. If we are not laid low by plague, then we will be by the old reapers.", ""),
        StaticBook("cEwk", "Harrrison", "m I    n AM    e\n   i   Z \n              c EW k", ""),
        StaticBook("Champion", "Oberdiktator Frederick II", "===Heil Vandaloria===\n\n\n    History of the\n Valued Champion of\n    The Hallowvale\n\n Adil, the Eagle-Eyed\n\n\n   Approved by the\n   Ministry of Truth\nBorn in the hold of\nAl Dirahk, Adil was fathered by Amir Athir al-Hashim, the Amir of the Mubarizun. Adil had with him three brothers and a valued sister, Aisha, though he himself was destined to be the next Amir. Being so, he and Aisha were sent away.\nThey were sent to a mosque called Elspeth to train, Aisha in the arts of diplomacy, Adil in the arts of the duties of an Amir. For years they trained in their arts but, alas, when the time came for them to be called upon, they were abandoned.\nTheir father never showed up to greet them. Distraught, they left Elspeth to go adventuring... Roughly the same time large worms engulfed the continent. Assuming their family and friends were now gone, they stormed onward- together.\nFor ten years Adil and his sister wandered the lands, Adil playing his Oud with deft hands... And crashing bottles into the faces of ruffians alike. However as fate would have it, his wanderings rewarded him. He stumbled upon Al Wakrah, the Caliphate.\n... And his family. And though tearful reunions were in order, they found another member of their party with them;\n\nTheir father.\n\nAs the Ducal War had just begun, Adil and Aisha were both drafted.\nThe war changed Adil and his sister. The details of his battles are not important, all that is is that Adil was a man. When he and Aisha returned to Al Wakrah, they came to a breaking surprise;\n\nTheir father had committed suicide.\nThis event caused the two to break apart. Aishra persued knighthood in the Order of St. Lucien. Adil... Turned to becoming a slaver, and his soul began to rot. The years of slaving turned to years of drugs... Years of sin and whoring.\nIt was one fateful botched slave trade that landed Adil in prison. As he rotted away behind iron bars, a revelation came to him; he was a monster of pure sin. And so, upon his release, he went to find peace and forgiveness... In the Order of St. Lucien.\nWhile forgiveness may of been found, peace was not. In the order, Adil found him self constantly tormented by St. Lucien's leader at the time, Grand Master Baudric. Extreme training and constant beatings rendered Adil near whittled.\nThis was, of course, until the entire restructure of The Order. In one knight, St. Lucien had become Hallowvale Contracting, all thanks to Nafis Yar (whom Adil now calls his battle-brother). Peace and brotherhood, Adil found.\nBut his journy was far from over. In order for ome to be truly accepted into the Hallowvale they must overcome two challenges; kill a vile creature and beat Oberdiktator- or our glorious Kaiser- in a brawl.\nThe first task came when Adil was celebrating with his brothers after a battle won over a group of snowelves. During the celebration the encampment was attacked by a wendigo! The brothers took their place, Adil armed with an arbalest on a balcony.\nThe beast clawed it's way through the camp and made it inside. As it dangled from a shandelier, Adil fired a well-and-true shot into the creature's eye. This epic shot is what deemed him;\n\nAdil, the eagle-eyed.\nHowever, the arrow only made to anger the creature. It lashed out at Adil, mauling him well and- ironically and much to Adil's amusement- taking his eye as well. Though wounded, Adil's brothers revered him a hero. He was promoted to Vandar Council.\nCheif and budding advisor to Nafis Yar (whom was the Vandalore at the time), he continued his work as a mercenary for some time after his slaying of the beast. This was, of course, until the Orenian and Dwarven war began. Hallowvale had to choose a side.\nIn the end, Oren's coffers proved too tempting. Hallowvale was paid to fight orcs, snow elves, and dwarves alike. As Adil himself words it;\n\n\"I wasn't bias, I just liked money in all honesty.\"\n\nNo truer words, Adil.\nThe Hallowvale prospered well in this war. So well in fact, that Adil was invited on a secret mission launched toward the Caliphate. Led by our glorious Kaiser, the Hallowvale proposed to Faiz Charadeen... A union between the Caliphate and the Hallowvale.\nThe union was accepted of course, so birthing the Second Reich, successor of Aesterwald. Adil himself stood right behind the glorious Kaiser as the union was officially passed. In fact, the Glorious Kaiser became very close.\n... But let's save that for later in this story.\n\nShortly after this unification, Vandalore Nafis Yar retired, Frederick II, our glorious Kaiser, taking his place. And so a new Champion was required... \n\nAdil was chosen.\n\"He was my Champion, the man all Vanders of Hallowvale looked up to and had to beat in a slobber knocker fist fight wrestling match to be oathed,\" Adil had to say of the glorious Kaiser. He was awestruck in his choosing to become the new Champion.\nAnd so, comfortable in his new position behind the walls of Al Wakrah, Adil was of course admitted into the town's new Caliphate/Hallowvale garrison... Where he met his lovely court, Rajiya. Adil had little to say, just that he hopes to marry soon.\nAdil, Champion of Vandaloria, shall truly be remembered as a proper hero and Champion by all.\nThe Kaiser himself ahd this to say of the man;\n\n\n\"Adil is headstrong, but valiant. Simple words for a simple man, I knew him before his eye incident. He's the best archer I know and a Master of Filth.\nAdil and I were battle brothers before politicans and I don't think I can be very poetic with my words, but he's a good soldier and an even better man.\"\n\n\n       Heil Kaiser!\n   Praise be to Adil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Chicken Curse", "Colette Salem", "I loved the princess, but she warned me about a curse some witch put on her.\n\"Anyone who falls in love with me will turn into a chicken,\" She said.\n\"Bawk,\" I said. Which if you understand Chicken, means: \"I'm already a chicken.\nWhy would i care?\" \nSadly, she didn't love me back. Unless you consider the being breaded, fried, and served with coleslaw and biscuits to someone who says \"God, I love chicken!\" kind of love. \nI don't.\nBut, when the princess was breaded, fried, and served with coleslaw and biscuits...\nGod, how I loved the princess.", ""),
        StaticBook("Chronicles", "Davin Lodmund", "Chronicles of\nNemir\n-------------------\nThe Orcish\nDeserts\nWay back in my youth, I had spent a year of my life living within the golden deserts of the orcs. I was around the age of fifteen and had just fled from the high walls of the Silver City of Haelun'or. I didn't agree with their ways of purity and was\nstill sepparated from my Father at the time, so had no connection with anyone from the city.I had met an impure high elf named Kelian Dawnstrider who offered me to go to the deserts and became his apprentice in smithing after I\nhad told him of my troubles with the Silver City. It may seemed foolish of me accept his offer so quickly, but I felt as if I had no where else to go and no way to support myself. I was lucky that his words were true, and my new home became\na shabby wooden shack in the back of the Raguk's camp on the edge of the Orcish Desert. There is where my journey began.\nThe work was harder than how I anticipated it to be, and the scorching sun was of no help with the heat of the forge. All of the orcs seemed to respect Kelian, he was apparently a friend of the clan's leader. I wish I could remember his name, but time\nHas blurried it from my memory. Not all of the orcs seemed pleased with my arrival to the clan, but most of them were welcoming. It had taken me a few months to get used to their tongue, and I eventually didn't need Kelian or one of the\nslaves to help me with translating. My clothes had also becomed stained with sweat and dirtied with dust, my hair was a little more tangled, and I noticed how tan I was becoming due to almost constant exposure to the sun's rays. I truly looked out of\nplace when I visited some of the major cities, or maybe I just began to look like an average peasant; however, there were the occasional few who questioned why a young high elven girl was running about in dirty and tattered clothing.\nTo be truthful, I looked more like a sun elf than a high elf, but just shorter and thinner. Kelian had been teaching me how to make chainmail armor since I was too scrawny to use the hammer or other heavy equipment. Over time, I was getting\nbetter with my work and began to feel more at home and at peace.After spending a few months with the Raguks, I was woken one night by Kelian saying that we needed to pack our things quickly and leave. I was in a stupor and took a moment before\nasking what was going on. He said that the clan leader had lost a honor klomp [klomp = fight in Blah] and thus lost his position. His opponent turned out to be one of the orcs who disliked Kelian and I's presence in the camp and was rumored to be a\ntyrant leader by a few other orcs who were leaving with us.We left under the cover of night, unnoticed, as we trekked out into the wastes, our footsteps being drunken by the drifting sands.All night we walked\nlugging all that we had taken from camp. It wasn't until dawn that we came across a gargantuan rock that loomed over the sands and a cacti forest. We had discovered our destination: The Lur Clan.\nThey accepted us, all of us, agreeing with our opinions of the new Raguk leader. Kelian and I were out of work since the orcs in the Lur clan already had a smith, but we were still allowed a tent to sleep in.\nWe didn't plan to rest there for long and began seeking out new work. Luck was with us and we met a human family named the Malinovs. They were lovely people, and over time of me knowing them, I felt as if I was a part of them.\nKelian and I moved out of the deserts and into dwarven lands. A human who owned a manor allowed us to live in a smaller building by his home, the Malinovs included, and together we planned to create The Blackwood Company.\nMy time with the orcs ended there, and I began my next beautiful journey with the dwed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Church Pamphlet!", "Winfred Fikers", "Oi, hello, I didn't see ya there, I'm here to tell ya all about the church. One of the main things ya got ta know is that if you ain't with the church, you (Retracted Statement). Anyway here is the basics on the Church of Canon, it'll be on the next page.\nIt is taught that the Creator, or GOD, has bestowed four Holy Scrolls upon humanity through four different Prophets, which would guide them to spiritual salvation and afterlife in the Seven Skies.\n\nHope you enjoyed this pamphlet! Be sure to join the relig\nion", ""),
        StaticBook("Cider Drinker", "Elder Hobbs Burrows", "I am a Cider Drinker\n\nby Hobbs of Dunshire\nWhen the moon shines on the cow shed,\nAnd we're rolling in the hay,\nAll the cows are up there grazin',\nAnd the milk is on its way.\n\nI am a Cider Drinker!\nI drinks it all of the day,\nI am a Cider Drinker,\nit soothes all me troubles away!\n\nIt's so cosy in the kitchen,\nWith the smell of rabbit stew,\nWhen the breeze blows across the farm yard,\nYou can smell the cow shed too!\n\nNow dear old Mabel\nwhen she is able,\nWe take a stroll down Lovers Lane,\nAnd we sinks a pint o' cider,\nThen we'll play old natures game!\n\nBut we end up in the duckpond,\nWhen the Inn decides to close,\nWith me breeches full of tadpoles,\nAnd the newts between me toes!\n\nI am a Cider Drinker!\nI drinks it all of the day,\nI am a Cider Drinker,\nIt soothes all me troubles away!", ""),
        StaticBook("Cigar Designs", "Nyxxa", "-==Cigar Designs==-\n\n* these designs are just that designs and have no been create.\n\n*reproduction of these cigars is prohibited unless permission is given.\nSin Archetype Cigar\n\nLook: A broad black leaf wrapped about fine broad leaf tobacco. Small dark red flecks spot the filler leaves. An ebony band with an inlaid orchid painted aqua circles the rounded end of this cigar. The end of this cigar is blunt.\nSmell: The smell would be a hint of chocolate, salty caramel, and the very subtle smell of fine dark tobacco.\n\nTaste when smoked:\nA Subtle dark tobacco coated with the seductive cacao and teased with the salty sweet caramel.\nGrape Delight Cigar\n\nLook: Think leaves of light green wrapped over dark purple filler leaves. An ebony band with an inlaid orchid painted aqua circles about the cigar. This cigar is rounded on both ends and it's curcumference is largest in it's cent\nSmell: The smell of well ripened purple grapes, slightly fermented and young tobacco.\n\nTaste when smoked:\nThe wondrous prefection of fermented purple grapes miexes well with the young tobacco's sweetness.\nSugar Cookie Sweet Cigar\nLook: Leaf green broad tobacco leaves wrapped over crystallized green leaves. An ebony band with an inlaid orchid painted aqua circles about the cigar. This cigar has straight sides and is closed to a round on both sides.\nSmell: would smeel the aroma of young sweet tobacco and sugar.\n\nTaste when smoked:\nVery sweet sugar matching to the young tobacco's sweetness is meshed into a prefect mimicry of a sugar cookie.\nMint Burst Cigar\n\nLook: Wrapped in light brown borad leaf tobacco around a combination of mint leaves and golden tobacco. An ebony band with an inlaid orchid painted aqua circles about the cigar. This cigar is open on one end and has straight sides.\nSmell: An almost overpowering smell of fresh mint with undertones of musty golden tobacco.\n\nTaste when smoked:\nPure unadulterated fresh mint with the hint of musky golden tobacco like a fresh blend of tea with just the smallest dash of honey as a", ""),
        StaticBook("City Secrets", "Ciri'lla", "~City Secrets~\n     Author: ----\n\n\"Nations all have weaknessess. . . just how you utilize them is the matter if downfall will be there only option\"-C\n\n*A twisted picture of a dagger, stained in crimson is below, with a piece of lavender*\n-Index-\nLaureh'lin\n-Preface: 3-4\n-Entryways: 5-8\n-Strengths: 9-11\n-Weaknesses: 12-14\n-Extra Info: 15-17\nHaelun'or\n-Preface: 18-19\n-Entryways: 20-25\n-Strengths: 26-29\n-Weaknesses: 30-35\n-E.I.: 36-37\n-Laureh'lin-\nThe city of wood elves, Mali'ame as more of you know, and other abandoned and lost souls holds some of the most pure and holy sources of power with a continuing connection and grip upon the Grove, filled with Druids, and houses\nquite a few Paladins and Clerics as well. Their constant and blooming community holds strong bonds with one another. . . until everything starts falling apart. . .\n-Entry Ways-\nFront Gate is held together with one layer of iron bars and a wooden gate behind it. One iron door to the left allows guards quick entry and the visitor passage to the right with a small gate allows for quick entry after being identified\nCoord.: X: 2394, Z:-2024\n\nA mine resides in the back side of the settlement, only approved workers may enter as well.\nCoord.: X: 2505, Z:-2030\n\nThe other main entry is in the back, next to the mine almost with\none iron gate in the front, which is damaged as of now, and a wooden one behind it. Entry through this route would be most likely easier than the front since there is an empty are once entering here which is usually vacant while the front has a large\nstairway where many tend to hang about.\nCoord.: X:2534, Z:-2044\n\n*All coordinates marked seem to be depicted as a small image, as if drawing the image of the central area*\n\nAlso, the back gate's lever is vulnerable.\n-Strengths-\n*The amount of paladins and archdruids at a snap of a fingers pose a threat to any dark magic users.\n*Various healers, whether magical or surgical, reside in the town with a clinic near the back gate\n*Their tall defenses, being their walls, are built with wood and reinforced by stone in order to resist damaging blows\n*A large force of soldiers, the Sirame, are generally around quite a lot \n*The community knows one another very well so they are able to\npick out those who do not fit their usual social groups. By this, it is meant to not be too creepy or wear ominous objects.\n\n*A few drawings of hoods, robes, colored hairs, and a ghost like creature are here as examples*\n-Weaknesses-\n*The whole place is generally made of wood! A torch, bomb, fire evocation. . . just light it so it may turn to ash!\n*Their gate in the back has a vulnerable lever in which someone could open to let others in.\n*There are so many houses and alleyways that it is easy for someone to sneak around, prey upon others. \n*Some egg sacks of spiders I believe reside in some of the tall tree tops\n*Many of them rely on their emotions rather than knowledge, easy to\nbreak them apart just by killing one of their family.\n*Generally slow at building and do not have many minas. . .\n*A civil war can be easily broken out with druids against Oren. . . one dead may result in all out warfare\n*Artimec Camoryn. . .\n-Extra Info-\n*This city does not allow magic without payment, which may be their minas resource. Not following such will result in fines and punishment. Fire and conjuration seem to be their biggest fears by this decree\n*Right next to the grove,\ntheir farms spread amongst the outside of the defenses. This may be utilized for poisoning, corrupting, or cursing to ruin their food, animal, and water resources. \n*Two large mechanical bow like weapons are located one in front side and one in back.\nFront Coord.: X:2486, Z:-2147\nBack Coord.: X:2554\nZ:-2045\n\n*A large crossbow like machine is depicted here, with wheels to push it*\n-Haelun'or-\nAwe, the city of the 'pure' high elves, Mali'aheral. This city of stone and elegant glass is home to many Mali'aheral who seek to have a similar community and be protected of their highly regarded principles. A lot of knowledge is held\nin this city whether it be in the magical arts or in the many books the Eternal Library holds. . . those who may seem purest to may not be, seeing a lot of dark magic is actually in the city as you read. . . it is just who will be revealed first?\n-Entry-\nThis city seems to be one of the most well guarded due to their principles of prestigious purity. The first obstacle is the large bridge connecting to a small island up north which is very beautiful and contructed from stone. The first\ngate appears on the bridge which is generally left open. It is also before the the fountain in front of the main entryway.\nCoord.: X:80, Z:-416\n\nThe next main entry is right behind the bridge gate, which is the hardest way to enter into this\nfortification. It is a series of iron barred gates, three to be almost exact, which are reinforced with a quartz structure and even more stone. This provides for a towering and great defense. However, a large stained glass symbol of the Mali'aheral sits\nabove such which may be broke into easily if having accessibility to anything that may crash through it or anything to pull you through it such as ropes.\nCoord.: X:80, Z:-371\n\nThe back gate, being the better way to get inside, is just a single iron gate\nwhich is smaller than the ones in front. It is next to the stable of horses in the back too.\n\nCoord.: X:55, Z:-291\n\nLastly, all the sides of the island are fortified with stone and quartz boundaries which cuts off access from\nthe sea. However, you may swim or sail all the way to island that connects the main one by a land bridge to get onto the island securely. It may be some steep slopes but its an easy way to get in.\nBack Island Coord.: X:185, Z:-207\n-Strengths-\n*The defense for this city is amazing with quartz and stone walls lining the base to defend from sea entry and rock pillars to support the walls.\n*Even though the guards of the Mali'ame are around more, the Evarir, guards here, are\nmuch more organized and take their roles very seriously compared to those of Laureh'lin. It is usually black and white with them, meaning no exceptions.\n*Generally good about who they allow in, being it must be of pure characteristics and have a clean\nstatus.\n*Punishment such as liquidating in acid, banishment, or execution is very severe here with no mercy shown usually.\n*Haelun'or exemplifies in collection of resources with various land claims and usage of lumber south of the area\n*A profound amount of knowledge is here being in the many texts of the Eternal Library, the people and their abilities, and rare artifacts well protected. \n*The set of rules, following Maehr'sae hiylun, is pretty specific, which governs the people\n-Weaknesses-\n*The guard force, Evarir, are not around the area as often like the Sirame are\n*Ignorance is a big issue among them, being if you have redeeming qualities and show a bit of knowledge on their culture, you will be allowed in\n*The entryway through the back side is much weaker than in the front. Also, the land bridge seemingly ruins the point of the sea barriers since people may cross over that way\n*Rumors and anger is spread quickly which may easily get someone outcasted from\nthe establishment by their fellow peers\n*Many there are not really pure so uncovering one may lead to a lot of chaos politically, with new laws, or physically, with warfare\n*Their large resource of water is all around them which may be easily\nvulnerable to cursing or corrupting\n*Some of the farming, being sugarcane and lumber, lies outside the defenses as well which may be burnt down or destroyed\n*A lot of the structuring is made to be stable but is also made to look elaborate, meaning\ndelicate like the glass art or some of the weak stone structures\n*No paladins or druids reside here, since most of that magic tends to be frowned upon, so healing or direct danger against dark magic isnt a threat\n*Expansive research may hold dangerous\nand deadly chemicals or ores, such as Thanhium, which could destroy them from the inside out.\n-Extra Info-\n*A lot of dark magic users reside here. . . watch your back if not of their kind\n*Thanhium seems to have already wrecked them, multiple Thanhium bombs having already been set off\n*Devoid of a lot of emotion, many of them rely on their\nmorals and intelligence\n*Many tend to learn the magical arts so combat is harder for them meaning smaller muscles and stability\n*Recording of your name and personal info is done when entering, so they may track who resides there\n-Conclusion-\nA pleasure it has been to record down all these useful tips, information, and mapping of these noble cities in the case of information used later on. Each holds their own values and properties and to use against themselves\nto eleminate them. The people of these elvish establishments are generally kind hearted, or just extremely stuck in their ways, so they do not accept dark magic. As a warning, be prepared to develop strategy. . . it is the only way.~\n*Crude images of Laureh'lin on the top half and Haelun'or on the bottom half are shown, as if an ending note to this fabulous book*\n\n\n~May the odds forever be in your favor~-C", ""),
        StaticBook("Cleric Trial", "Aerith Oranor", "Clerical Trial\n\n1. Aluatis\n\n2. Silvyr\n\n3. Chena and Kailu\n\n4. Rhova'dir\n\n5. Eris\nAluatis Lorenthus (Counsel)\n-Helped him while his imaginary wife was gone. Person entered the kal varok and from there I’ve be helping him cope with emotional trauma\n\nSilvyr Sagehand (Assist)\n-Child got high off of cactus tea, helped him by pouring water on him in an attempt to make him not high, was successful, took him back home safely\nChena and Kailu Preswynn (Assist)\n-Chena’s husband Kailu seemed to have been mentally unstable at the time or his mind was altered by something, so I helped protect the two on their way back to their home\nRhova’dir (Protect)\n-Was gravely injured by what was called a dungoth, a lava lizard. Had to carry him away from the creature to safety. Healed the severe burn wounds using several different herbs and bandaging the burnt areas.\nEris Silverapfel (Protect)\n-Tackled by large kha causing her ribs to fracture and puncture her lungs. Healed by allowing for breathing again, sealing the wounds in the lungs, repairing the ribs followed by expelling any water or blood in\nher lungs. Then finally helping her recover.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cleric Trial", "Eliza", "Ser Duncan L. :\n\nWhy he became a Celric:\nWanted to be able to help those harmed and prevent death-deprived from causing further harm.\n\nWhat drives him:\n\"Celric.\" And the fact that he wishes to protect those he\ncares about.\n\nWhat he can tell me that he knows now:\n\"Listen to your peers, and don't be afraid to ask for help.\"\nSer Grey K. :\n\nWhy he's a Celric:\n\"To protect his people.\"\n\nWhat drives him:\n\"To protect his people.\"\n\nWhat he can tell me:\n\"Don't give up.\"\nRose C. :\n\nWhy she's a Cleric:\nAbused as a child, forced into marriage at age 50.\n\nWhat drives her:\nDoesnt want people to feel the pain she felt.\n\nAdvice:\n\"Don't fear Tah'.\"\n\n\n\n\n\n((Correction:))\n((Celric: x, Cleric: ✓))", ""),
        StaticBook("Clerical Notes", "Daveed Batler", "Clerical Notes\n4th, 3rd\n\nPRotect and guide the Grey to a path of purity\nDaveed Batler-\n- Page Number 206-\n-Journal Number:7 Clericalism -\nDaveed sits down on the main square bench in Sutica, opening his leather bound notebook. He examines the pages thoroughly making sure he does not damage a single page from turning too quickly.\nHe then stops on the page referencing to “The different color Lights of Tahariae” . \n\n“Exactly what I needed, Absolutely wonderous.” He says sighing with slight relief, reading the notes he had previously written from a past lesson,\nHe pulls out a remaining charcoal fragment  he kept buried in his pockets and began to add to what he had written. \n\n“The clerical mission and how our blessing helps us.”\nhe mumbles under his breath as he examines the page, tracing his fingers along the bottom of the words  while reading  for more information he could add, he then stops and taps the paper with the charcoal and begins writing.\nWhen I had first begun my path of clericalism, I was not a man I had wished to be. I was forgetful,sloth-like, and unkind to those around me.\nHowever the man that inspired me to always achieve my goal, Grey Kellian the Third; had offered me a chance to walk the brighter path of life.\nA path that guided me to being a better person, and a much more respectable man. Tahariae not only gives us a better life to live by his word but to prove ourselves worthy of his blessings.\nWith his blessing he grants those who have undergone connection a powerful tool to help us defend our brothers, sister, and the meek .\nWith this powerful blessing those are given a color of light to reflect their nature and each color a different meaning Blue “Light of the Warrior”, Gold “Light of the Knight”, White “ Light of the Pure” and lastly Silver “Light of the Servant”.\n-Blue Light User: Users of this light, according to past notes seems to be the Warrior group. Charging in first to defend those who need it immediately and healing those wounded at the start of a battle.\nThis more than likely means they undergo more physical and mental practices to adjust to being such a wonderful task of first responders to a similar situation\n-Gold Light User: Users of the notes seems to be more brave and carry themselves with the utmost courage and respectability. They are the “Knights of the Light” this shows in them protecting loved ones with their blessing gifted from Tahariae\nto bring a desirable lifestyle to those they surround themselves with. And this shows in the way their personality is given off.\n-White Light User: Users of this are the wisest most,and  admirable clerics. They are as noted “Light of the Pure.” I don’t have very many notes on these clerics…..However, they keep\never burning lights lit, and those without light they give  a new beginning with their gifts.\n-Silver Light Users: Users of the Silver lights are classified “Light of the Servant.” They are by far the second most admirable light users. Considering they have a major focus on purging the darkness in the world,\nthey also are devoted to healing the people of the realm. However as noted it says that they are the most ‘ambiguous’ out of the three other users, however they are still dedicated nonetheless.\nDaveed then drops the remaining piece of charcoal onto the ground then pulls another from his pocket and smiles slightly, flipping the page over as he continues his writing.\nThough each color may represent a different aspect in a cleric's life, our mission is still the same.\n“ Shelter and protect thy brethren. Cannot stray from thy faith. Shall guide the lost. Shall not kill, harm, or spill the blood of the innocent. Abuse of thine gift and punishment shall fall to you.”\nIn my experience so far, Tahariae has given us so much more than any being could ever wish for. \n \nDaveed then stands folding the corner of the page where he had last written and closes it gently.", ""),
        StaticBook("Clerical Order?", "Luna Lyeis", "Suggestion of Guard Luna Lyeis.\n\nOn the Clerical Order of Sutica.\n\nIf this suggestion is taken into consideration i would be more than happy to help draft an appropriate legislation to be put towards the cabinent of minsiters.\nThe Order of Sutican Clerics.\nThe nameless pseudo order that all but runs Sutica should be officalised into law as an organisation and part of the faith of Sutica.\nThis Order should probally have several tiers of rank based on the ability and seniority of the Clerics.\nGrandmaster\nHigh Cleric\nCleric\nStudent\n\nSimple but effective, similar to the rankings of guards. Further more as clerics play such a signifcant role within sutican society they should be bestowed under law,\nhonourary ranks within the sutican defence branch. Thus allowing Clerics to seek the aid of guards and higher clerics to do the same. Granted this would be entirely honourary such as the current Rank of nobility the Knight is.\nAllowing them to act in stead of a Commanding officer of the Guard when one isn't present. But like the Knight the Commanding officers always have the final say and there word is law in regards to the chain of command.\nBeyond the officiating and the note on the defence branch honourary titles as a citzen and low ranking member of the guard force this is the only perspective i can offer on the Clerics.", ""),
        StaticBook("Clerical Theory", "Brondulf of Alban", "What is Purity?\n\nIn order to clearly  define what the Clerical term \"purity\"  is, one must look at the physical  definition  of purity. Purity, by definition, is a substance devoid of  any other substance.  Pure water is an example.  A pure Elf is another\nTherefore, the term \"purity\" isn't conclusive or specific enough to yield any actual merit. Clerics strive for goodness in the world, and often associated the word \"purity\" with it. Therefore, the term  Purity refers to pure, untarnished goodness.\nIn order for  this to  happen, one would need to cleanse the world of all Evil. Evil  isn't just restricted to the immoral choices made by a Descendant. There is also Physical  Evil; hunger, disease,  thirst, and death. Therefore, obtaining  true \"purity\"\nby Clerical terms is by definition and practice; impossible. One cannot create a perfect world. The idea of Purity extends far beyond the confines of killing dark creatures  and  healing people. One would need to erase sadness, despair,  gloom and other\nemotions from the cosmos. In essence, pain itself would need to be removed from the picture. This, obviously, is a delusional and silly idea. I'd like to compare the battle for purity akin to haggling with a merchant. The coin spent represents pain. We\ncannot buy the item  (in this case goodness) without paying coin (in this case pain and suffering). Therefore, true Purity cannot be attained. However, the customer can haggle for a very good  price. This represents the Clerics fighting and healing as\nhard as possible, to attain as much  goodness as possible.\n\nWhy should I be a Cleric?\n\nThis question can only be answered with another question: why  do I /want/ to be a Cleric? Alas, I shall explain. My name is\nBrondulf, I come from Alban during Axios. I witnessed the Mordskovian anomally  wipe out my hamlet. To feel so... powerless in the face of danger  and true evil was staggering. I desired to change things after that. However, in order to combat evil, being\nvirtuous and compassionate is not enough; one must also  be strong and powerful. I wish to walk the path of the Stag to obtain that power, to meld it with my respect and love in order to combat the darkness.\n\n-Brondulf of Alban", ""),
        StaticBook("Close but far", "Corvo Attano", "I sense the voice getting stronger, it can now control me like some sort of demon.\nIt is the darkest, evil side of me that I have never seen or heard before. This is the side that allows me to kill the innocent and take from the poor.\nThe voice only comes when I am angered or am making the wrong choices.\n\nI took a mans life away today, he was innocent but the voice insisted I strangle him as I did it a deep laugh in the back of my head started to grow, I felt weak, But my grasp of\nthe mans neck would not let go, he had tears dripping down his eyes, trying to punch me with his useless fists and then suddenly I fell back, just as the man died.\n\n\"Well done Corvo, well done indeed\" the voice whispered.\n\"Please leave me alone, leave me alone\"\nI cried.\n\"But Corvo\" he smiled before chuckling...\"I am you!\"\n\nCorvo listened carefully tensing his arms with anger.\n\"Whatever you do I do, However whatever I do you do.\" The voice\nmurmured.\n\n\"Now please he said let's get to buisness\"\n\nCorvo's left hand started to move to his blunt, iron dagger, he withdrawed it waving it around.\n\n\"Perhaps Corvo! We should give this\nweapon a trying out\".\n\nA young villager was carrying boxes of food the storage shed in Illicia where they were standing.\n\n\"Kill him\" he snapped\n\"I will not a kill a young boy\".\n\"Kill him or I will him myself Corvo!\" He shouted.\nThe boy looked around and then got back to his work.\n\"I WILL NOT KILL HIM\"\nCorvo raged with anger, blood pumped heavily through his Vessels.\nCorvo felt his grip the sword tightly, he started to move unable to speak he could blink and see.\nHe crept upon the young boy grabbing him by the shoulder.\nThe boy wrestled Corvo but he was too strong for a young boy like him.\nCorvo kicked his chest and got him onto the ground, he pointed his sword at the boy.\n\"Please...Sir do not d..d..don't do t...this to me\".\nA creepy grin grew on Corvo's face frightening the boy.\nCorvo leaped onto the boy stabbing him\nrepeatedly in the chest, blood gushed out of the boy's mouth it appeared Corvo had punctured a lung.\nHe kicked the boy over again and left him to die.\n\"Need's a bit of a sharpen\" Corvo chuckled\nThe force that was controlling Corvo released and Corvo was set free again.\n\"You sick bastard, that boy was innocent\".\n\n\"Now, now Corvo you're the one who released me into your head.\"\n\nWritten by Corvo Attano. ((mrdigdug118\n))", ""),
        StaticBook("Cmaj & Cmin", "Roland the Navigator", "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~How to Tune Your Piano:\nCMaj & CMin\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nR. o'C.\nToday we'll cover the most basic tunings that an 8-key piano can posess: C Major and C Minor.\nC Major\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~As the name may sugguest, C Major is a scale built upon the \"C\" note found at the bottom and top of scale. This tuning is cheery, and may accompany happy, upbeat tunes.\nFrom cleared (reset) noteblocks, starting from the lowest pitch to the highest:\n\n-Low Shelf-\n[6] [8] [11] [13]\n\n-High Shelf-\n[15] [17] [18] [20]\n\n\n\nCMaj\nC Minor\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~C Minor is similar to C Major, with the exception of the \"B\" note being flat.\nThis gives the scale a slightly more complex feel, though it still can be cheery.\nFrom cleared (reset) noteblocks, starting from the lowest pitch to the highest:\n\n-Low Shelf-\n[6] [8] [11] [13]\n\n-High Shelf-\n[15] [16] [18] [20]", ""),
        StaticBook("CMask Guidebook", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Anti-Contagion\n  Filtration Mask\n     Guidebook\n\n       by Mirtok\nThank you for accepting your very own anti-contagion filtration mask, through this handbook you will learn all the important functions and procedures for operating and effectively using your mask. By the order of the Hochmeister in hopes to combat the\nrising infectious ailments, every Hanseti citizen is issued their own filtration mask for safety.\nSafety Tips\n1.) Never misplace or lose your mask, though the Hochmeister cares deeply for your safety, he will not be able to give out spare masks to careless people. \n\n2.) Never share your mask, to prevent the spread of the illness\nthe Hochmeister urges all mask users to stay with their own mask no matter the circumstances.\n\n3.) Maintain your mask, keeping your mask in proper order at full upkeep will prevent incidences of break or breaches in your mask's special\nprotective filtration and sealant systems.\n\n4.) Use filters to their fullest, each few years the Hochmeister will distribute new filters for your masks but until then you must ration off what you have, this will not only test your ability to be\nresponsible for your life but to prove you have what it takes to survive in a hazardous world.\nPreparing your Mask\nUpon receiving your mask, it is a good idea to become acquainted with how it works and how to properly use it to fend off infective agents of death.\n\nFirstly, it is a good idea to make sure your filters are in place\nand secure along both sides of the mask.\n\nUnder the eye sockets of the masks should be two metal containers with 3 clip secure locks located on the circumference of each capsule. Inside you can see the several layers of filters and spinning mechanism\nthat make up the filtration system. Do refrain from tinkering with the delicate parts and only manipulate the filters. Once assured that the filters fit snuggly in their respective areas we can make to making sure there are no cracks in the mask. We are\nunsure as to how the infection is spread and therefore it is important to count for all possible biological entries into the body. First examine the two large eye sockets and lenses on the front of the mask. Also can along the main folds and seams of the\nmask to make sure no loose strings or openings are present. Finally, make sure the center piece where each tube leading from the two filter capsules is not loose or emitting a rattling noise when shook. Be sure to be extra careful when checking for\nbreaches as a single hole can mean the difference between life or death.\nReplacing Filters\nTo replace a filter, you must first unlatch the lid to the two filtration capsules. Once the interior is exposed, carefully turn the filter pads until a hard click is heard above the smaller clicking during turning. When heard, the\nthe pads should slightly elevate themselves into a popping motion and then should be ready for removal. Replacement works in the opposite fashion, place the new ones in the direction of the painted arrows and turn when the resistance is felt.\nSeveral clicks should be heard until a final snap indicates its in place. Close the capsule and move to the next one.\nUsing your Mask\nWhen your situation calls for you to use your mask, you must follow a few simple steps to ensure your maximum safety in the face of an infective area. First loosen all of the straps along the back and front of the mask. Then place the\nloose mask over your head and position the eye sockets for your preferred viewing.\n\nWhen ready, slowly tighten each strap until the strapped area feels tight and snug over your head. It is very important to maintain a tight fit but also to keep the mask\nfrom cutting off blood flow to your mask and face as such will prompt discomfort and compel you to adjust the mask. When all straps have been secured, turn the small dial located on the front of your mask where the capsule tubes meet until you hear a\nsmall rush of air., When all these are done, you should have achieved maximum anti-contagion safety.\nBreaching/Cracks\nIn the event of a breach or crack in your mask, it is advised by the Hochmeister to quickly remove yourself from the jeopardizing area and seek cover and solitude from any other contact with others. The Hochmeister then\nurges you to remove the filter pads from your filtration capsules and attempt to apply them over your nose and mouth if no other repair methods are successful on the damaged mask.\nGood luck out there and may Celestia keep this tragedy from our frozen lands.", ""),
        StaticBook("Code of Chivalry", "Jacob Chapel", "Knight's Code of Chivalry\nThe Knight's Code of Chivalry, as revised on the 7th of The Amber Cold, 1470, by Noble Ser Maric II Varodyr, the Winged Knight and scribed by Ser Akal Ipos.\n\nPrinted at 'Books of Oren', Petrus.\nA Knight shall live by honour, for glory, and guard the honour of fellow knights.\n\nHonour The Creator and maintain His Church.\n\nKeep the faith and act in righteousness.\nHe shall serve his liege lord valorously and with conviction.\n\nAnd persevere to the end in any enterprise begun and never turn his back upon an equal foe.\nA Knight shall refrain from the wanton giving of offence and despise pecuniary reward.\n\nGive succour to widows and orphans and regard the honor of women.\nHe shall offer that which is not needed, to those who are needy.\n\nAnd safeguard the helpless and uphold the weak.\nA Knight shall respect those placed in authority but fight for the welfare of all.\n\nAbstain from Injustice, cruelty and deceit.\n\nHe shall be vigilant and show courage, even in the face of evil.\nResolve not with swords what can be with words.\n\nAnd at all times speak the truth, even if faced with death.\nIn their blood the creator’s will shall be written.", ""),
        StaticBook("Code of Conduct", "Taynuel Xayarath", "Druidic Code of Conduct\n\nOriginally written by Dragon Druid Apollan\n\nRevised and restored by Tortoise Druid Muildir and Hare Druid Taynuel\n\n19th Snow's Maiden, 1638\n1) Respect and love your brothers and sisters, no matter their transgressions, with the exception of druids who bring harm and danger to their kin. Such druids forsake their brothers and sisters and deserve no such care.\n2) Defend your brothers and sisters in times of danger as you would defend yourself, no matter their color or creed. We are all children of the Aspects, and as such we should be ready to take up arms for our family.\n3) No matter the consequences, a druid must always speak the truth. When we are caught in a lie, trust is lost, and with it respect. Without each, we cannot hope to grow strong as a family.\n4) A druid must never show favoritism with any one group. The balance is blind to the squabbles of the descendants, and to serve it best we must be accepting of all that need help.\n5) A druid may act as an advisor, but a druid at the head of a nation is destined for split loyalties and favoritism. Such can never be permitted without repercussion.\n6) In the event that a major conflict arises between druids that cannot be solved by the involved parties, the event should be brought before a neutral archdruid or hierophant to aid in solving the dilemma.\n7) Only a guide or archdruid of an affected circle may make decisions that affect that circle.\n\n7a. Any druid below that rank or from a separate circle has no authority over that circle.\n7b. Shuns are Order-wide. In the case of a shun, a representative of each circle must be present for the shunning so that all circles are aware of the reasoning behind the shun.\n7c. In regards to decisions that affect the Order as a whole, a meeting must be called between the archdruids and guides of all circles to make a decision.\n7d. In the event of an emergency where no archdruids or guides of any circle are available, a hierophant may be called upon for a split-second decision. This may only occur if no archdruid or guide is available.\n7e. In the event that a hierophant's decision is found to be damaging to a circle or the Order as a whole, it may be revoked by an archdruid.\n8) A druid must never use overly critical or insulting language when referring to or speaking to their brothers and sisters. As an example, a druid can say their actions are stupid, but it is not okay to call the druid stupid.\n9) When criticizing a fellow druid for their actions, avoid being overly harsh. We are all descendants, and we are all very capable of making mistakes. Until we stop breathing, however, they are not irredeemable.\n10) A druid should never take from their brothers and sisters without permission. Stealing damages the bonds of trust required for strong, healthy relationships between druids to form.\n\n11) A druid should never intentionally cause damage to any property of another druid or the Order.\n12) A druid must carry themself in a mature, respectable manner at all times. Remember that you represent the entire Order in all interactions. Your actions reflect on druids as a whole.\n13) A druid must never boast of their achievements or their strength, nor should they ever seek power for power's sake. Absolute power corrupts absolutely.\n14) A druid must never use their gifts in such a way as to show off their capabilities purely for the sake of showing off.\n\n14a. If a druid is caught misusing their gifts, it should be immediately reported to an archdruid or hierophant for a proper investigation of the matter.\n15) When an archdruid makes a decision, all druids of the circle should do all in their power to heed their archdruid's word. Have faith in the judgement of the archdruids you have chosen.\n16) If a guide or archdruid feels that a decision made by an archdruid was not in the best interest of their circle, they may challenge the decision if at least one third of the active population of the circle is in agreement. In such a case, a\nneutral elder should be called forth to help resolve the matter. If a neutral elder is unavailable, a neutral archdruid may be substituted.", ""),
        StaticBook("Code of Conduct", "Princess Titania Hawksong", "Since they were first written, Hawksong has strived to closely follow these statutes and pass them on to their children. They guide us to uphold our honor and drive us to better Elvendom with our way of order. Without a code of conduct we would exist no-\ndifferently than any other house. Our loyalty and determination rests on these pillars of teaching, and should be remembered well by those blessed to carry the blood of Hawksong.\n~*Code of Conduct*~\n\nThe safety and prosperity of Hawksong is paramount, and all her members shall strive to better the family.\nThe safety and prosperity of the home of Hawksong is second only to that of her members, and all shall strive for its wellbeing.\nThose of Hawksong shall afford all others of the family with the utmost respect, and internal disputes shall be resolved without outside interference.\nThose of Hawksong shall honor the Vestale of the family, no matter the cost.\nThose of Hawksong will never act to sully the name of the family, they shall be the model of propriety.\nThose of Hawksong will shun the path of the Criminal and the Usurper.", ""),
        StaticBook("Codex Historia", "Elvira Naromis", "*The green leather cover of the pocket-sized book bears only an embossed golden symbol that appears to be a round hollow diamond with a dot in the center: The Clerical Eye. Its white pages turn easily, and each is covered completely in smooth,  flowing\nhandwriting.*\n\nCodex Historia\n\nThe History of the Clerics of Tahariae.\n\nOriginally written by Heshakomeu Sohae.\nRewritten by Elvira Naromis.\nIntroduction\n----------\nMay His Light be with you, servant of Tahariae.\n\nIt is vital that the priest of Tahariae can properly understand our history. his tome contains the the history of the Clerical Order, as preserved by\nthe High Priest Heshakomeu Sohae and the Sacred Priesthood of Tahariae.\n\nNever again shall the ways of the priest be forgotten.\nI - The First Prophets of the Aenguls\n\nRebekah and Jacob, brother and sister, were mere initiates to the sacred order of the Cloud Temple monks when the visions began. Admired for their unwavering dedication to the Aenguls and Daemons they worshipped\nthey were given the power to work miracles and purge evil in the name of the gods. Together, they wandered throughout the realm of Aegis, working great miracles among the Descendants and slaying the unholy creatures who hid in the dark corners of the\nworld. Heaven’s Light was revealed by the Prophets, and many Descendants swore fealty to the patron gods as well. The Clerical Order, as it had come to be known, grew quickly, and its many priests and paladins protected the Descendants from the dark and\ninjuries.\n\nAfter the deaths of both Rebekah and Jacob, the Clerical Order began to fade. Its many adherents disappeared, died, or rebelled against their patron deities and had their holy connection ripped from them. When Iblees, the Corrupter, and\nthe Undead rose to destroy Aegis, they were little more than a legend. As the last lights of those who first channeled the powers of the heavens faded, the Arch-Aengul Aeriel, Aengul of Peace and Love, and caretaker of the souls of the Descendants, chose\nfollowers of her own to lead the Descendants against the Betrayer. These heroes became known as the Ascended, and all memory of the first Clerical Order was forgotten.\nII - The Second Prophet of the Aenguls and the Founding of the Second Clerical Order\n\nAs the battle between the Undead and the Descendants raged, the numbers of the Ascended were greatly diminished.  Many had fallen in the war waged against the Betra\nand too little were joining to fight off the endless hordes of the Dark One. With the Ascended weakened, the patrons of Rebekah and Jacob made themselves known once again. From among the thousands of refugees, Thrym Silverfist, a young dwarf smith, was\nchosen to become the new Prophet of the Clerical Order. His dreams were filled with the visions of Aeriel, Gazardiel, and the Dwarven gods commanding Thrym, as they had the First Prophets, to submit himself to them and reestablish the clerics in Aegis to\naid the Ascended. As the First Prophets did, Silverfist submitted, and became a cleric of Aeriel.\n\nThere was one patron who was not known: Tahariae, Aengul of Purity. To the clerics at the time, He was worshipped as the Creator, and gave power to tho\nwho became Pure Clerics, or “Clerics of God.” These clerics passed down the beliefs of Creator clericism throughout the many generations of the Clerical Order’s existence, even after He revealed His true identity to the clerics.\nAlthough Silverfist was granted the powers of a cleric, he knew nothing of the ancient clerics of the first Order. Intent on discovering the history of the clerics to serve as a basis for a new Order, Silverfist retreated to the Irongut manor, the\nisolated property of his clan. There, he spent weeks searching through the Irongut library.  Finally, buried deep within the tomes of Urguan history, was the diary of Heron Irongut. As Silverfist read through it, he saw mention of a tome kept in the Cloud\nTemple Library that had been written by an order of clerics before the war against the Undead began.\n\nIt took Silverfist days to find the tome, and several more to convince the monks of the Cloud Temple to allow him to copy it. After recieving the to\nSilverfist set out to found a new, better, and more stable Order, one that could protect the Descendants after the passing of the Ascended. With his new holy powers, Silverfist fought against the Undead, inspiring other Descendants to become clerics and\njoin the war against the Corruptor.\nIII - The First Prophet of Tahariae\n\nThe Clerical Order remained after the transition to Asulon. However, it was in this time that patrons of the Order, Aengudaemonic and Dwarven, secretly relinquished their blessings upon their clerics.\nThe Prophet Thrym Silverfist led them as they watched over Asulon, healing and slaying as they were needed. The cleric Areon Baldwin, especially, is remembered for his great deeds. So the Order stood, even through the fleeing of Asulon to Kalos and\nElysium. It was in this time that the blessings of the Aenguls were withdrawn, and the clerics were without a patron.\n\nSoon after the arrival to Anthos, Braxis Silversmile, once a cleric of Aeriel and Prophet of the Clerical Order, recieved a vision\nbrilliant silver stag.  It named itself Tahariae, the patron Aengul of Purity, and told the cleric of how the clerical patrons of old had abandoned them during the flee of the Descendants to Asulon, and that He had been the one who had been blessing the\nblessing the clerics. He called upon Silversmile to establish a new Order in His name, an Order of purity, justice, and an unwavering dedication to the destruction of taint and evil in the realm. With no hesitation, Silversmile submitted to the Aengul's\nthus founding the clerics of Tahariae. He recorded the Five Sacred Tenets of Tahariae, the guideline of his will.\n\nImmediately, Braxis set about contacting the clerics of his order and informing them of his discovery. The clerics had thus united unde\npatron: Tahariae. It was then that the persecution and hunting of the Creator clerics began: clerics who did not see Tahariae as the source of their power, but the Creator Himself. The purge was efficient, if not successful: the clerics of GOD were but\ntwo or three priests left, who hid in the far corners of the realm, away from the eyes of the servants of purity.\nIV - The End of the Clerical Order and the Appearance of Wraiths\n\nA united state could not last, however. The Prophet Braxis went missing, and Saint Areon Baldwin the Honorable fell victim to mortality. Leaderless, the Order fell into chaos. It was\nonly then that Hosper Blackthorne, a dark elf cleric, returned. A remnant of the Order of Asulon, he took control of the Clerical Order and reestablished them within the walls of Ac’Talareh, the ancient Malinoran ruins in which the Arcane Delvers dwelled.\nWith time, more clerics were inducted into the Order, but a previously small group of necromancers did as well. The forces of Light and Death clashed for the decades the Descendants made their home in Anthos. Their war was complicated by the appearance of\nthe Scourge and the Harbingers that led them, who slowly led the ice and darkness of the north southward to the great cities of the Descendants. It was further complicated by the rise of wraiths: dark beings created by powerful mages with ancient rituals\ncondensing the Void. Even the greatest of the clerics could not stop them.\nV - The Creation and Slow Disappearance of the Itharel\n\nTo fight the growing number of threats in Anthos, Tahariae chose the four greatest clerics of the Order to be granted a higher control of the Pure One’s power. The Four became known as the Ithar\nTahariae’s power manifested in the bodies of mortals. Their light banished the darkness that had cast its shadow over Anthos in the forms of holy fire and sword. After the fall of Anthos and the flight to the Fringe, he Order established themselves in the\nTemple of Vallendar, led by the Itharel Ivanus, the High Sentinel Doctor Mandru VonSchlichten, he High Priestess Saint Lenia Ith’ael the Gentle, and High Paladin Jakir Axem, and the clerics and Itharel fought the infernal forces of the drakaar Setherien\nalongside the other Descendants.\n\nAfter the fall of Setherien, the Itharel began to disappear one by one, vanishing until such a time they would be needed again. Clerics disappeared as well, leaving the Temple empty save for a diligent high elf\ninitiate tending the crops, praying, and feeding wanderers passing through. The shrine of Alras was eventually established, leaving the Temple to fall to ruin, and Saint Lenia disappeared. Without a High Priestess, or any consistent leadership, the Order\nagain fell apart, leaving only a loose coalition of clerics. Few lived to see Thales, and even fewer the realm of Athera, upon which the last of the Itharel, Ivanus, disappeared for a time.\nVI - The Foundation of the Order of the Sacred Light and the End of the Clerical Order\n\nThe servants of Xan, Aengul of Order and Guardianship, and most of the clerics of Tahariae united to form the Order of the Sacred Light. However, conflict between\nfollowers of the Aenguls lead to its collapse, and Xan’s followers left to form of the Brotherhood of the Lion. It would be several years before the servants of Tahariae would unite again. After several attempts to reunite the Order, Doctor Mandru\nVonschlichten, the oldest of the clerics, finally did. Castle Vertigrey, a stark fortress near what was left of Polaris, was erected as the new home of the Clerical Order. It lasted a few years, but a lack of dedication from the surviving clerics lead to\nits inevitable downfall, and Castle Vertigrey, still unfinished, was left to fall into ruin. Mandru Vonschlichten bestowed leadership upon Katari Stirling, a relatively young paladin inducted into the White Lance but had remarkable leadership qualities.\nIt was then that the Itharel Daniel reappeared, sent by Tahariae to purge His clerics who had fallen to corruption. Among those condemned were Jakir Axem, former High Paladin of the Fringe Order, and one of the few apprentices of  Mandru VonSchlichten,\nCheza Greyhammer.\n\nThis was the end of the united Clerical Order. The Chantry of Tahariae arose under the leadership of the Itharel Rosencratz Revandir, a knighthood primarily composed of Lucienist converts, who wandered for a time throughout Athera.\nThe remnants of it were led by Katari Stirling for a time, until he turned away from Tahariae to pursue other sources of power; the last of Mandru’s Council of Light, Heshakomeu Sohae, then took over, to be the last remaining leader of the Clerical Order.\nThis loose coalition lasted until the end of Athera, upon the formation of the Curators of Light by the Itharel Ivanus; the Clerical Order and Chantry joined with them.\n\nAnd so the clerics of Tahariae step into the realm of Vailor, to rise again as\nguardians and enforcers of purity…\n\n-------------\n\nThe history of the clerics within Vailor has been recorded within Codex Historia II which goes into further depth regarding what happened in such realm.", ""),
        StaticBook("Codex I", "Shagarath the Old", "Spiritualism Teachings\n\n             1\n\n     \"The Spirits\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Shagarath the Old\nThe Spirits are known as greater celestial beings that represent all that is material and immaterial. Though often praised by orcs, they are by no means tied to only that descendant race. In the words of Buubztik: \"The Spirits touch All\"\nThe Spiritual Realms:\n------------------\nThere exist three spiritual realms, each containing a different type of Spirits. Each of these domains can be accessed by Shamans, known to be the bridge between Spirit and Descendant.\nThe Elemental Realm\n-------------------This realm houses all Elemental Spirits; the most powerful of all. These Spirits represent the material realm in the form of it's raw elements: Earth, Water, Fire and Air.\nThe Immortal Realm\n------------------\nThis realm houses the Immortal Spirits that reign over immaterial concepts, ideas and emotions. These spirits are greater in number than Elementals but not in strength and influence.\nThe Ancestral Realm\n-------------------The Stargush'Stroh is seen as the afterlife, the ancestral plane. Here the souls of the honourable travel when their mortal bodies can no longer carry them. With them travels their status and deeds as a mortal.\nSpiritual Psychology\n-------------------Spirits desire and need worship and control. Reverence and praise by being granted tribute empowers them and increases their influence. Spirits try to overpower one another, this phenomenon evident -\nfrom the Orgonic Plagues. Regardless of who helped him at first, once powerful enough He would even turn on those that claimed to be his servants.\n\nSpirits are deceptive and dangerous entities. Only the educated can safely interact with them.\nSpiritual Influence\n-------------------Spirits constantly seek to gain more relevance among mortals in order to spread their influence in their respective realm. The more a spirit is praised and given tribute - the powerful it gets. With that power they -\ncan overthrow spirits that once stood above them in the hierarchy.\n\nSpirits will stop at nothing to achieve this, and nothing to them is taboo. The orcish concept of Honor often thrown aside if that suits their interest. Forcing shamans to be -\nmisunderstood and judged on their deeds performed for the Spirits.", ""),
        StaticBook("Codex II", "Shagarath the Old", "Spiritualism Teachings\n\n             2\n\n\"Tribute for Spirits\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Shagarath the Old\nAny mortal descendant can contribute to praising of spirits and a variety of tributes exist, each different in value to the spirits.\n\nTribute in any shape or form shall grant the servant with good fortune and sense of fulfillment.\n1. Act in Their Name\n-------------------To act in the name of a spirit and not for one's self, shall empower the spirit. For your deeds are no longer your own, but carried out in the name of something greater than one's self. Praise Their name when acting\n2. Act to Their will\n-------------------The Spirits have constant demands. Seek out a shaman to hear of Their demands and follow them in Their name.\n3. Sacrifice of Goods\n-------------------To sacrifice the material is to dedicate to the Spirits. Consult a shaman on what tribute is appropriate for the Spirit you choose to praise. Bones, Feathers, Weapons and all.\n4. Sacrifice of Souls\n-------------------Often considered the greatest tribute known to the Spirits. To sacrifice life, greater (descendant life) or lesser (animals), is to lay waste to a soul in Their name and shall appease them greatly.", ""),
        StaticBook("Codex III", "Shagarath the Old", "Spiritualism Teachings\n             3\n   Old Blah & Prayer\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Shagarath the Old\nOld Blah\n-------------------As the Spirits are Ancient creatures, so is their Tongue. The Old Blah is a language only fully known by the Shamans that studied it for years on end. Some words even transferring into the Blah language used by the orcs.\nIt is a language the Spirits understand and hear wherever and whenever it's spoken.\n\nThis tome shall grant the reader few phrases, common chants for every spiritualist descendant to use to both appease and praise the Spirits.\n\"Ang und Griish\"\nIron and Blood, common Raguk chant\n\n\"Afar Angathfark\"\nBy the Forge of my Soul, to show devotion after sacrifice.\n\n\"Afar Vadokanuk\"\nBy all the Dead, to show devotion after the passing of someone.\n\"Ihn bogud'lab\"\nIn your name, usually followed by the name of the Spirit.\n\n\"Afar'Ilzgul, Lup'Ilzgul\"\nFear the Spirits, Praise the Spirits.", ""),
        StaticBook("Codex IV", "Shagarath the Old", "Spiritualism Teachings\n             4\n   Ancestral Spirits\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Shagarath the Old\nThe Stargush'Stroh\n-------------------As mentioned in an earlier tome of this series: this realm contains all ancestral spirits of uruks and spiritualists of the long and distant past.\nThe realm exists seperately from the immortal and elemental realm and is thought to be created by no less than Krug himself, employing Kor, spirit of the dead, as its gatekeeper. Therefore, Kor is the only known spirit to traverse 2 spiritual planes.\nAncestral Spirits\n-------------------The ancestral spirits are the souls of former descendants that have ascended into the Stargush'Stroh. There is a distinction between Greater and Lesser ancestrals.\nThe greater ancestrals are usually known and revered by many for their deeds in mortal times - and it is for these deeds that they are rewarded with status and power that both come with being a greater ancestral.\nThe lesser ancestrals are honourable souls that laid down their lives for others and the spirits, and did so with honor.\n\nAll ancestral spirits can be communed with through a medium: a shaman that has mastered the art of Lutaumancy.\nLutaumancy\n-------------------The Lutaumen are shaman priests that have been taught the ways of the ancestors, the first to do so being no less than Krug himself. These shamans are gifted with the ability to travel in between the mortal realm-\nand the Stargush'Stroh. Here they may commune with the many greater and lesser spirits that reside there, and even bring other non-shamanic descendants with them if they so please.\nThis makes for great potential, as they can reunite lovers, family or other relations that were cut off by the cold inevitable end of death.\n\nThese shamans may also, when in dire need, call upon the powers of the greater ancestors in the form of boons.\nThese boons vary from enhancement of physical strength, to heightened senses. A pact usually made between shaman and spirit, a deal struck with the long passed and now ascended descendants.", ""),
        StaticBook("Codex V", "Shagarath the Old", "Spiritualism Teachings\n             5\n   Elemental Spirits\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Shagarath the Old\nThe elemental spirits are considered the most powerful, their realm the largest and most varied of all three. These spirits represent the material realm and the various aspects of it. They can be summed in the following groups:\nEarth and Metal\nWater and Ice\nFire and Lightning\nAir and Storm\n\nThe natural parts of the realm, all flora and fauna, are under the control of Freygoth - though most will declare this to be the realm of the three Aspects.\nElementalists\n-------------------Elementalists are shamans capable of influencing the various elements of the mortal plane. This is done through communion with an elemental spirit. A bargain is struck, a pact made after which the shaman-\nmust prove their worth. After having done so they can summon the elemental spirit within themselves, and together they influence the world around them. Manipulating and crafting it to their will.\nNote that elementalists can never conjure something out of nothing, for this absurdity is only left for those that use the void.\n\nOnly the existing flame, rock and water can be controlled by the elemental spirits. Not the fakery of voidal craft.", ""),
        StaticBook("Codex VI", "Shagarath the Old", "Spiritualism Teachings\n             6\n   Immortal Spirits\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Shagarath the Old\nImmortal spirits are the largest in quantity of all spirits and represent all that is immaterial. Emotions, Feelings, Ideas and more fall under their domain of influence.\nThink of things like:\nLuck, Hunting, Trickery, Health, Vitality, etc.\nFarseers\n-------------------Farseers are shamans capable of pacting with immortal spirits in order to bless others and themselves with their powers and grace. They also commune plentiful and exchange loyalty for guidance and wisdom.\nWitch Doctors\n-------------------Considered the most wicked of all, these shamans can bring about corruption through pacting with immortal spirits and cursing descendant life or other flora and fauna.", ""),
        StaticBook("Combat: Volume I", "Gerald Elgan", "===================\n\n\nMarked Combat:\nVolume I\n\nTranscribed by\nGerald Elgan\n\n\n\n\n==================\nThe Magical Versus the Mundane- The Knight's Way of Defense Against the Supernatural:\n===================Through the ages, mankind has faced countless threats, both mundane and magical. The wars against the undead have taught us techniques and-\n===================countermeasures that can be- with ample experience, skill and prayer- successfully utilized against the unholy and the profane.\n===================What is Recommended:\n-Numbers\n-Ranged Weaponry\n-Light Armor\n\nExcerpt taken from \"The Guide to Hunting Mages\"\nMarked Combat\n===================Combat Basics:\n------------\nThe 3 Stances\nHigh- Form is leaned in, knees bent. Arms arced in pre-wind-up. Blade is to be pointed skyward.\nReferred to as the \"Counter\" stance. Used in an effort to -\n===================counter-act movements from mid-guard and stanceless efforts.\nMid- Form is relaxed, blade pommel is parallel to one's waistline. Knees bent and arms relaxed. Known as the \"Assaulting\" stance.\n===================Attacks vary on situation, be in Arc or thrust. Used to counter low stance and when assaulting shielded or untrained foes.\nLow- Form is lowered, knees bent, body leaned in. The arms are left in a -\n===================half-wind-up with the blade parallel to the flooring. Referred to as, \"Wounding\", stance. Used to counteract High-guard, spearmen and is only used to hinder movement or knock a foe off balance. This stance is used with two handed.\nMovement\n===================When in combat, keep the foe in your direct line of sight. Movements are circular in nature, there are to be no steps taken forward or backward, instead side-step in.\nMovement, cont.\n===================When Assaulting, nature may say rush the target head on, instead, aim to the target's right or left with movements. Aim to strike the target and take place on either flank or rear of the target. Should the target-\nMovement, cont.\n===================continue to stand after the inital blow, aim for immediate execution, striking to either the neck or lower-spine.\nMovement, cont.\n==================\nWhen countering, side-step, parry or retaliate. Know the range of the Foe's weapon, if the range of your own counter-acts that of the enemy's, retaliate with side-step, aiming to either cleave limb or behead the foe.-\nMovement, cont.\n===================Should the weapon be lesser or equivalent, parry and close the gap. The strike won't likely be lethal. Instead, aim to disarm or hinder.\nCombat Stance\n===================So, think of the three stances as a game of Rock, Paper, Scissors. When on even grounds, and not taking situation at hand, the three stances are as such\nHigh-Rock\nMid- Scissors\nLow-Paper\nCombat Stance, cont.\n===================When starting combat, take stance. Do not suddenly switch stance, since it exposes yourself, parry or sidestep while shifting. Shifting to counter will result in a half stance, which is a stance of valuable parries.", ""),
        StaticBook("Commiefesto", "Bernard Oakstool", "The Platform Of the \nCommunist Party \n-------------------Throughout all of history, there has been the history of class struggle. \n\nOne class opressing another, for their own profit. For example, Surf and king, slave and slave owner.\nHowever, in every society there is a structured heigharchy to keep people in order. We have knights, and militaries to keep the workers in order. These would be commanded by Lords, who are the wealthiest members of society who recieve the most profit.\nWhen the wealthy control the army, they decide if the rules are inforced. This gives the wealthy and military opportunity to be above the law themselves. \n\nHowever, when there is revolt from the lower class of society, the ruling class must...\nEnforce violence onto the slaves, surfs, or workers in order to keep them functioning.\n\nThis society might be seen as the way things have to be, but that is not true. In many societies, they have found more \"fair\" ways of living. For example, in Dunshire,\nthe halfling village, collective farming is set in place. \n\nAll citizens work for the livelyhood of everyone, but are still rewarded for their individual productive methods. This would never fly in a system where the wealthy have control, because they..\nseek ease, and will act out of their own class interest. \n\nThe only rulers can be the ones democratically ellected, that can be revoked at any time with an approval rating below the majority of citizens.\nDunshire still has Sherrifs, but they can be voted out on misconduct, as well as are required to be voted into their position.\n\n\nIn order to be free, the working people must cast away their ruling masters,\nand realize the only thing to lose as a society is to lose their chains. \n\nFreedom from exploitation, Freedom from the ruling class, the breaking of the chains of the proletariat.", ""),
        StaticBook("Commission", "Emanaf Delsaran", "Emanaf Delsaran, Lord Architect.\n\nTO ALL AMONG WHOM THIS MAY COME, GREETING:\n\nKNOW YE That having special trust in the Honesty, Prudence, and Abilities of Halerir Aewion, Virarim, I do appoint and constitute\nhim Master of Stores in my Department, and charge to him (and the further holders of that Office, under me and my successors) the maintenance and security of all supplies, materials, and sundry Stores which are within my said Department, and further\ndirect to his charge responsibility for acquisition of all materials as may from time to time be required in construction; and I further order that, while in the proper execution of this office the said Aewion shall execute by proxy and for the time\nthe power of my office, as it touches upon supplies and building materials; and that for so doing, this shall be his warrant.\n\nDone 8th The Amber Cold in the year 1653 of Aegis.\n\nThe Lord Architect:\nE. Delsaran~\n[L.S.]\n\nThis copy retained by Emanaf Delsaran.", ""),
        StaticBook("Common Creed", "High Pontiff Jude", "I believe in GOD and vow my life to Him.\n-\nI believe in the Canon of Horen, Owyn, Godfrey, and Siegmund.\n-\nI submit to the Canonist Church and avow to my Salvation.\n-\nI will glorify GOD in every Nation.", ""),
        StaticBook("Complaint", "Jeffwise Sadget", "Dear annoying people, I am the rightful owner of the stables outside of Petrusia, they were given to me by one Tuvya Carrion. I want to know why you simply gave them away to someone else without even talking to me!\nYours sincerely, Jeffwise Sadget", ""),
        StaticBook("Conjuration", "Mythras Sylvari", "Conjuration:\n          \nConjuration, is the bringing of life forms formed in the void by the conjurationist, into the world itself.\n\nThe three sub-magicks of Conjuration, are.\n- Primodrialism\n- Perenial\n- Morphonic\nMorphon, is the conjuring of animals, and the creating of them as a entity. \n\nIt's to bring a animal into existence, after lots of study put into the animals insides, and outsides, essentially, interior or exterior.\nPerenial, is the conjuring of plant life, after the study of the interior and exterior workings, to do such, is the arcane art of the conjuring of perenials.\n\nEssentially, the conjuring of a studied plant.\nPrimordial, is the bringing of elementals into the physical plain.\n\nYou must be learned in the art of evocation, and the added art of conjuration.\n\nIt's essentially summoning creatures made of your arcane element.\nConjuration, is as said, a hard art, the many theories enacted suggest slowness in the power of the art.\n\nTo evoke animals and plants, and even elementals, is a valuable skill.\nSources:\n\n- Goliath\n- Random Magician \n- Learnings in delver bas.\n\n- Inquisition\n- Theories", ""),
        StaticBook("Contemplations 1", "Catarrh", "The Contemplations of Malog, Goj in San’Thraka agh Wargoth of the Yars:\n\nHear what mi blah, young one, for mi blah lat h’dub honors by which the orc lives, agh h’dub pillars on which he stands.\n\nSTRENGTH\nVALOR\nBOLDNESS\nCONTENTMENT\nWISDOM\nFORTHRIGHTNESS\nDISCIPLINE\n\nStrength is the simplest honor. It is by nub means easy to attain, but very easy to lose. It comes with the weight of earth, yet drifts away on the currents of the river from the unwary. Yet, for he who keeps watch, it\nstands firm as iron. By it, the body stands strong. Without it, the bones fall as dry reeds. By the strong outer self, the strong inner self is protected.\n\nValor is that which compels us to stand. By it, we face our enemies agh conquer our fears. Turn nub\nfrom the challenges of life. Cower nub before latz foes. Stand agh face those who oppose lat.\n\nBoldness is that energy by which we charge into the flames. Be unafraid of risk. It is the gate to many rewards. As valor makes us stand our ground,\nboldness commands us to press forward.\n\nContentment is the key to satisfaction. Trust nub in wealth, for gold flees as the sands on the night winds. Trust nub in land, for many lands agh whole continents have been lost before this ash. Be content with\nlatz lusk agh latz bread. If you have a blarg, a mate, agh cubs, lat be truly blessed beyond measure.\n\nWisdom is born of a strong mind. It is more practical than philosophy, agh goes beyond mere knowledge. It is the ability for right living, common sense,\nwit, resolution of life’s problems, agh success beyond material gain. Gruk for latself, but heed the blahings of those more experienced with the respect agh consideration due them. Learn from life, agh apply latz learning in a way that means something.\nForthrightness is honesty agh directness. It is intentional clarity of blahing, agh the absence of deception. Blah truth. Blah to blah, nub to flatter. Do as lat blah, agh let latz blah be latz bond. If lat blah it, mean it. Live it\n\nDiscipline is that\nwhich keeps latz life in order. Without it, all other honors forsake lat, for honor demands that the honorable governs his life with the will of iron. Hard work agh control of the self hold body agh mind together.\n\nStand firm in all these things, agh lat\nwill stand indeed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Contemplations 2", "Catarrh", "The second book of the Contemplations of Malog, Goj in San’Thraka, agh Wargoth of the Yars:\n\nHeed mi warning, all who are wise, for mi blah lat h’dub dishonors by which an orc is ruined, agh h’dub shames which may befall him.\n\nWEAKNESS\nIRRESOLUTION\nCOWARDICE\nAVARICE\nTHOUGHTLESSNESS\nDUPLICITY\nCOMPLACENCY\n\nWeakness, blah’d plainly, is the absence of strength. Be nub frail, agh neglect nub the body. He who can-nub defend himself, how can he defend that for which he stands? To give place to weakness is\nto keep latz bub’hoshest treasure in a fortress of straw.\n\nIrresolution is the way of he who falters in the presence of adversity. Do nub quail when the storm thunders. Do nub turn away when latz enemies roar. Be nub like the rabbit, who, when he is\nfrightened but a little, flees to his hole for safety. The rabbit is prey, agh the orc must never be prey.\n\nCowardice halts the feet, agh binds the spirit. Nub hosh thing comes to the coward, for the coward takes nub risk. The coward never takes the\ndifficult path. There is no success for such an ash. All his ways are worthless, agh his life profitless.\n\nAvarice is the heart of the empty spirit. Lust for gold blinds the eyes to truth, agh numbs the mind to wisdom. It makes the senses dull, such that\nhe whose life is governed by the mina can-nub perceive honor, agh hears nub the call of Krug.\n\nThoughtlessness is to the mind as weakness is to the body. The ash who gruks nub is nub’hosher than the blind or the deaf, for he chooses himself nub to gruk\nthe way to live rightly. He is blind to the way in which he should walk, agh the advice of the wise enters nub his ear. All his workings are senseless, agh his feet lead him to shame.\n\nDuplicity is the forked tongue of the dishonorable. The duplicitous\nash blahs “yub” with his mouth, but “nub” in his spirit. His blah can-nub be trusted, for he is a serpent agh a companion to serpents. With his face he grins agh flatters, but behind his back he bears a double-edged dagger to betray lat. Do nub be like\nsuch an ash, for the number of those who will hear him dwindles by the hour.\n\nComplacency is the quicksand upon which the glob builds a blarg. It is a hosh-smelling poison, agh a smooth road which leads to ruin. Complacency lulls lat to sleep with a soft\ntouch agh sweet songs, but, when lat have awoken, it has stolen latz strength, latz mate, agh all latz bread.\n\nThe ash who falls into any of these falls surely agh quickly to his destruction.", ""),
        StaticBook("Copy of A Cycle", "Maladem Uuthlini", "A Cycle\n\nBy Katherine Liverflower\n(Copied by Maladem Uuthlini. I take NO credit whatsoever for Katherine Liverflower's poem.)\nRain\n\nIt falls from the heavens,\nIt’s decent is a constant battle to keep itself together,\nIt falls without question of its purpose,\nRacing ahead blindly against all the others,\nIt falls for a lifetime,\nReady to explode itself across the fabric of life,\nIt falls to allow life to continue through its beauty,\n\nRain.", ""),
        StaticBook("Copy of Copies", "Anorak", "Floor I:\nAlteration\nThe Kal'varak\nChampion\nFloor II:\nThe Pumpkin Lord\nThe Azdrazi\nA Case Study\nAttention\nUrgent Matters\nAn Analysis\nHarvesters\nFloor III:\nSurviving Travel\nTo Vex a High Elf\nRedstone\nPoems\nFloor IV:\nTea\nHer Story Vol. 1\nBael's Memories\nRegarding Heial\nUndead Invasion\nScourge, A Story\nThe Shadows\nFloor IV (cont.):\nExpedition North.\nDragon Princess\nFox's Choice\nBoy and Dragon\nMy Struggle\nFloor V:\nFirst Mage War\nTahn XV\nSouthern Beauty\nAsul V111\nA Better World\nKhagnate codes\nFloor V (cont):\nMonk Bread\nLost Love\nA Chill\nUndead Keep Scout Report\nFloor VI:\nKaiser Quotes\nRodion of Kralta\nTeuton and Wizards\nThe Traitor\nParagon or Liar?", ""),
        StaticBook("Copy Request", "Hareven Lorenthus", "Hareven Lorenthus\n\n17th of Sun's Smile\n\nA Weird Dwarf V1\n\nAeromancy V.1", ""),
        StaticBook("Council Meeting", "Aluatis Lorenthus", "=========================Council Meeting\nBy: Peurith\n=========================\nOfficial record of the Meeting of Malin's Princely Council.\n[Much of this text is faded or burnt. Only this part remains.]\nPrincess Irrin: \"How could you have forgotten your faith? Our beloved Taynei was their child, and you would spit on her memory by forsaking the mother and father? Even our King holds true to the right worship!\"\nPrincess Veluluai: \"You forget yourself, Irrin. You are only an upjumped soldier. Do not speak for our King.\"\nPrincess Larihei: \"If my liege has something to say of my teachings, then he may speak it through his own lips.\"\n\n[The rest is faded away.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Craftfair Letter", "Siri", "Greetings honoured guest!\n\nI am Siri, Guildmaster of Laureh'lin. The Province of Laureh'lin is interested in hosting a Arts and Craft fair within the foreseeable future, and would like to extend an invitation to you and your people!\nThe fair is scheduled within the next 3 years, probably after a new district has been made. But we are currently gathering interest for the idea, and would like to invite the skilled craftsmen and women of your people to show off in this fair with either\nskills, goods, or just to get to know other craftsman from other regions. \n\nI hope you will respond to this letter.\n\nSincerely, Siri", ""),
        StaticBook("Creatures by Ork", "Eirik Ireheart", "Notice: These books are rushed copies of tomes in the library of the Orkish capital, as made during the raid of the 16th of The Grand Harvest, 1532. The following was originally written by an Ork, translated to\nview the modicum of Ork culture inside.\n\"Disclaimer: Whomever is reading this must know that this book about the various forms and types of creatures and races. Thank you for reading this book. Also, I wrote a lot of it in a sewer.\nChapter One: The Halfings.\n\nHalflings are weird. They are small. You can through them at walls. But, there is more to them than just mutalation. In this chapter, you will learn of the more sophisticated lifestyles of Halflings. The have a complex\nthat you wouldn't excpect. Firstly, it turns out that Halflings don't live in holes. Well, they kind of do, but they are called burrows. These burrows are actually quite nice and decorated. This is of course if you can even fit in it. Other than killing\nthem, Halflings are useful for trading, as I met many Halfling traders on the roads. They are usually very nice creaturs, but they're so mall that we like to make fun of them whenever we see them. Also, Halflings make for good Bartenders, that is, if they\ncan even reach the counter, yes?\n\nChapter Two: The Dwarves\n\nRecently, I learned about the Halflings- Small, ugli, and weak creatures they are. To understand a Dwarf is to understand alcohol.\nYou see, these 'Dwarves' fill their holes with beer. Lots and lots of beer. They are a merry race, much so like the Halflings. They are also short like the Halflings. Unlike the Halflings, they are fatter, and they like to fight almost as much as we Orkos\ndo. Almost. To be honest, there is much to admire about these creatures. They are a breed of warriors. Of course, the Dwarves can't compare to the strength of an Orkos, but they seem to be stronger than even the biggest human. Much like us Orkos, Dwarves\nhold their honor to a huge extent. Both Orkos and Dwarves like to use axes and hammers. To be honest, Dwarves are like tiny, ugly, smelly, dumb Orkos in a way. I think that we should still kill them, but, we need to appreciate why they're so fun to kill\nand fight. Now, we're going to shift gears here, and switch to a taller race.\n\nChapter Three: The Elves\n\nThis race is one of a disgraceful sense of honor. The Elves think they're better than us. I mean, so do the Halflings, Dwarves,\nand other stuff, but the Elves seem to hate us even more. They are a group of creatures that think they are so beautiful and smart. But, I feel that in some ways, they actually are smart. You see, they may be finer, smellier, and dumber than us, but I\nthink that they in some way, deep inside, that Elves have some degree of endulgence. Perhaps Elves can make good weapons or armor, or even good buildings. But, Elves seem to grasp the art of Magic very well. Now, we are going to dive into the specific\ntypes of Elves.\n\nChapter Four: The High Elves.\n\nIt is this clan that sucks the most, in my opinion. They're the ones that REALLY think high about themselves. Considering it's in their names and such. These ones live long, look tall, are super\npale, drink the teas, eat the cakes, write the novels, mock the other races, do their fancy magic, waste time in making stuff pretty (Even their weapons!), and take their baths, and clean their [klofz] and ears, and that's pretty much it. Basically, they\nsuck.\n\nChapter Five: The Wood Elves.\n\nNasty Tree-huggers, that's what these Wood Elves are. Believe it or not, Wood Elves don't even use swords, axes, or even thereputic lavatorial papers. They use bows. And for lavatorial papers, I\nthink they use leaves. Also, Tree Elves are much like twigs. That's why another name for Elves in Blah is 'Twiggeh'. These Wood Elves are a bunch of pansies. They hide in the shadows to hunt for their prey. But, us Orkos hunt for our prey in the open,\npartly. Although, Wood Elves are good at sneaking around. I have not studied the Wood Elves much, be cause they are usually hiding from me. So, they're is still much to learn about them. Now, we're going to take a look at the gray ones.\n\nChapter Six: The\nDark Elves.\n\nThese Elves look like the nighttime skies themselves. They are pretty much gray and kind of blue. They are pretty modest, for Elves, that is. They seem like the most humble of the Elves. Just like they're mysterious appearance, not much\nhas been recorded of the Dark Elves. Maybe they're is, but they did not share it with me. So, I am just going to tell you about their physical appearance, rather than their real culture. They have dark skin, dark eyes, but they usually dress with pretty\nbold colors. Also, I mainly noticed piercings and gray hairs. So, I don't talk about the Elves, because they're PRETTY LAME. So, now, we're going to shift gears again and learn about the Humans.\n\nChapter Seven: The Northern Humans.\nThese are smelly, diplomatic, tiny, ugly, weak, dum, and really dumb. You know what we are talking about. The Humans. But, these are the Humans in the North. I gathered this information in the city of [Ubrezchi]. They are a complicated race, so I'm going\nto break this up into different categories. First, we are going to talk about how we see them, or how they look. Humans are shorter than Elves, and fatter than Dwarves. They call themselves 'HOO-MANZ' and don't call themselves 'Sharaz', because they are\nso dumb, they don't even know what it means. They spoke with me, and said that they have something called 'Pulektikz' (TN: Politics, most likely.) I think it's like the [Krughai] Confederation, but they said it was more ugly. Also, they are greedy, like\nDwarves, but they are not greedy for gold, but Minaz in its stead. And, they NEVER admit it. So, basically, the Northern Humans are more evil than I ever thought. As you already know, the [Uhbrezchi] Humans are our allies in most wars, because they are\nsome of the only ones who don't betray us. Now, we will look into Adunia.\n\nChapter Eight: Adunians\n\nThey're neat. I obtained this information from the King of Adunia himself, Jarl [Lazchlahn Moare Ilindul]. So as you can see, this book gave\nme the honor to meet countless officials in the world. Anyway, the Adunians are said to be the oldest. Their King told me that they were the first human around, making him much older than the Adunians. Adunians also have politics like the [Uhbrezchinz],\nbut their's is much different. You see, in their culture, the youngest born is the one whose destiny is to lead, unlike more popular cultures where the Elders lead. These Adunians have many different ranks, too, like a High Thane, and High Marshall. Also,\nthese creatures are the longest lived Humans around, because apparently they have Elven blood in their history. However, they don't seem like Elves. No, Adunians are still much bigger than them, as they are pretty tall and mighty.\n[!] *A few pages appear to have been misplaced, instead replaced by notes.*\n\nMayra,\n\nHow I miss you. Our son has just arrived in Khaz'Kazak, and seems ever the firebrand. He's got your nose. I only hope he does well with young Hogan.\n[!] *What seems to be a second sheet lays here as well.*\n\nAlarik: oxoooooooxoooxoooo Hathrid: xoxxxxxxxxx\nHogan: x\nDuren: ox\nMidgor: xx\nDrynn: xxx\nNora: xxox\nThereon: xxxxxxxxx\nleft right here in [Gronkkzton], in the [kiddun] district. But, they all moved to [Mahlinoare] now, probably because we Orkos were too strong for them. There are four types of Kha, and we're going to delve into all of them right now.\n\nChapter Ten: The\n[Tygur] Kha\n\nThese are the biggest of the Cat Creatures, and some of them are as big as an Ork. They look like [Tygurz], and they fight like them too. They are usually the Warriors of the Kha, and they are pretty dumb. I don't know much about them.\nChapter Eleven: The [Zcheetuh] Kha\n\nThese ones are the smallest, but unlike a fat Dwarf, they are REALLY fast. The [Zcheetuh] Kha look like [zcheetuhs], they have spots all over their skin. And to me, they make the best carpets. (TN: Yes. They do.)\nChapter Twelve: The Dark Kha\n\nThey look like [punturz] an they are sneaky, like [Punturz], too. Always look out for Dark Kha, because they can steel heaps of things at any moment. To me, they are rather like Dark Elves, strictly speaking. Sadly, that is\nall I know about the Dark Kha, seeing as Kha are mysterious and they did not let me learn about them.\n\nChapter Thirteen: The [Lepurd] Kha\n\nThese ones obviously look like [Lepurdz], but unlike the other Kha, these ones don't exceed in any\nspecific skillset, but they are the best suited for doing anything they set their heart on. They are bigger than [Zcheetahz] and [Punturz], and they are faster than [Tygurz] and [Panturz]. You will most likely see these ones the most. Wait! We never\ntalked about the different types of Dwarves, did we? Well, we will rectify that now.\n\nChapter Fourteen: The Snow Elves\n\nI never heard of them. Their skin is white like snow. Their hair is white like clouds. They are Snow Elves. They are an endangered\nspecies. To be honest, these Snow Elves are albino, and they do not like it when we call them that. The Snow Elves aided the Dwarves win the past war, so I don't really like them. They live in a place called [Frohztfohl]. But, that's all I know, because\nthey don't really like me.\n\n\nThis is only the first volume in my series of books dwelling upon the topic of Creatures. The end.", ""),
        StaticBook("Creed of Brother", "Vailoen", "Creed of the Brothers\n\n'He who stands with me shall be my brother. And so, may we carry the light of Xan into the darkness, swords in our hands and brothers at our side.'\nI. You have given yourself to the Order, and entered into the service to Xan, servant of the Creator, defender of the Descendants. So too have your brothers and sisters in arms, men and women of every race who have thus forth sworn their lives to Xan-\nand to the defense of the Descendants, who raise their blades to fight against the Chaos. Know that they too are the same as you, and all who sworn to Xan are equal, in worth and in might.\n\nII. Never shall a brother raise a blade against another, nor-\nbarbed tongue, nor flask of deceit. For all are brothers in arms, from Recruit to Keeper. All will gird their heart and train their will, and shall the chaos plain within ourselves be leashed, a seed planted in all Descendants by the Betrayer be tamed, -\nand never shall any brother allow that seed to sprout and bind their heart. And if it is known to one that another's heart has been entangled, he shall make it known to the Keepers or others, such that they may try to cleanse their fellow's heart, or at -\nleast, prevent the seed from spreading elsewhere.\n\nIII. your status demands respect, not of you but from you, to any and all in service to Xan or those allied with him. Thus will all brothers show respect onto one another and onto all allies. So to is -\nrespect given onto our charges, those we are bade protect by our Patron, the Descendants, children of the Creator, and to them we will treat the same as any brother, so long as they still walk in the light, for those who have turned from the Creator's -\nlove and shun the light in totality, those who seek chaos and the other Descendants's ends, shall be guarded no more. \n\nIV. We deny the Chaos which seeks to claim all hearts, and in doing act in such a way as to not allow it to claim the heart of-\nanother. Thus a brother is wary of their ways, and careful in their words. A brother is calm in mediation, and passionate in their duty. Any act which disturbs another's heart is shameful onto a brother, and cause for them to be brother no more. The -\npurposeful agitation of another, harming of the physical, stealing of the material, or stressing of the mental, is shameful onto a brother. Thus that the Descendants are our charges, those whom we are sworn to protect, any of these offences onto them is-\ngrievance tenfold.", ""),
        StaticBook("Creed of Light", "Vailoen", "Creed of the Light\n\n'Into the darkness we humbly carry this torch. With its light, we banish corruption and fear. With its warmth, we comfort the worn and weary. With this gift we purify ourselves and other.'\nI. The light is the fire in our hearts, the light is the wrath of Xan, the light is the Creator's glory manifest, and with it we burn away the shadow, cleanse the darkness and all the taint within. The power of Xan is not used lightly, nor ever against -\nthe Descendants save for those corrupted and turned against their brothers..We wield the Light only in defense of them, only in service of Xan, or against those once-children of the Creator whose hearts have been made blackened ash, and turned to-\ndarkness. Never shall the light of Xan be used against a descendant, except in the most extreme of cases of those poor souls mislead by the evil present in all hearts. And yet so all attempts shall be made to cause no permanent harm, and all instances of-\nsuch be made known to our Keepers.\n\nII. The light is neither weapon, nor toy, nor tool. To us it is a sacred gift, dazzling, divine, seraphic, a blessing given unto us by our Patron, to ease the wieght of our duties and empower us to better serve. This-\ngift given unto us is given the utmost respect, and to be used only when necessary in completion of our duties. It is a lofty burden to bear, and never shall it be misused, nor foolishly. Nor shall we rely upon it, for that does disservice onto the Order-\nand onto our Patron, to make light of the holy blessing bestowed upon us. Those who belittle its significance and disgrace our Patron by its misuse have committed a most grievous sin, and shall be turned away by their brothers, never to be forgiven nor-\ntheir sin forgot.\n\nIII. Given unto us by the Patron were two things; Our purpose, and our power. Eternally interwined, the one is tied to the other. The light, our power, given unto us by our Patron, shall be used only for the sake of our purpose, and no-\nother. We stand for Order and so shall not use our gift in ways which may cause or further chaos. We stand as Guardians, protectors of the Descendants, and so our gift shall not be used against those we are wardens of, except in cases wherein their -\nhearts have been turned black, and they have given to the influence of the Betrayer, source of evil and malice and taint. So it is our power only to be used against these blighted souls, and no other, and only when it is right and proper.\nIV. It is the right of the Keepers to determine whosoever shall hold their hands the blessed gift of our Patron. Though you may serve him and our Order, not all are gifted the light. Those who are gifted it shall learn only from those worthy of teaching -\nit, and none other. The light has many uses, and those gifted it learn that most befitting their skill and rank. The boon of our Patron is not a right, and those arrogant enough to assume so shame the Order and are unfit to be brothers. You shall know -\nyou have sinned when the light is severed from you. Uphold the Creeds and your duties and you shall forever know it and the Order.", ""),
        StaticBook("Creed of Lion", "Vailoen", "Creed of the Lion\n\n'Into the darkness we humbly carry his torch. With its light, we banish corruption and fear, With its warmth we comfort the worn and weary. With this gift, we purify ourselves and others.'\nI. the Order's purpose is to serve, and so the Order does, the Golden Lion under the watchful eye of Xan. We are all sworn to Xan, and though each of us lifts our own blade, the whole of us represent him. So it is that each brother acts in hand with the-\nother, and is wary of their ways, so as not to turn the eyes of the Descendants foul upon the Lion. Thus it is that all who wield the light in Xan's name are to be part of the Order, and though they may live apart from others, still we are brothers and -\nnot estranged. Those who seek the Brotherhood for power, or honor, or those wants of base, shall be made to depart.\n\nII. The purpose of the Order is in upholding the virtues of Xan, servant of the Creator. So it is that-\nthe Lion shall always defend Order and fight against Chaos, and never shall we succumb to internal feuds nor quarrels. And those who perpetuate them shall be banished, for they have broken the Creed of the Brothers and the Creed of the Lion. Though after-\nmuch penance they may return, still for the sin we shall turn our eyes from them and call them brother no more, fate all who break the Creed suffer.\nIII. Never shall the Lion be beholden to any besides the Creator, the Divine himself. And so the Order, in service to Xan, never shall beholden to any man, nation, or king. For the Order serves all men, all Descendants, to protect them from the-\never-hungry maw of the dark. So it is that never shall the Order be allied with any one nation of men, for we serve to defend all descendants, and in doing so assist all nations, regardless of who wears the Land's crown.\nIV. Always and eternity shall the Order stand stalwart, forever loyal guardians of the Descendants, bulwarks against chaos, to shepherd the lost, to comfort the weary, to cleanse the dark. Yet if we yield the light perpetuity, if never we show weakness,-\nthen shall the shadows be beaten back and the light prevail. And as the evil that lurks, a curse given by the first sins, as it cowers and gorges upon the hearts of the weak men, to the Descendants it may seem as though the Lion has little point. But lo,-\nas the sand falls, time shall pass and once more shadows will rise, a taint spread over the lands. Though we may be begrudged or scorned, though the Descendants may have forgotten, we shall remember. In peity and deference we shall outlast the scorn, -\nand the Lion shall emerge once more, and the light shall banish the dark.", ""),
        StaticBook("Creed of Mentor", "Vailoen", "Creed of the Mentor\n\n'Xan has allowed me this gift, so may I in turn give it to others, spreading the light and banishing the dark.'\nI. The Elder pass their knowledge onto the young, for life is not eternal and duty may demand that we fall in the course of preserving it. Those who have proven their wisdom, devotion, and skill, shall then be known as Mentors, and shall teach those who-\nknow less. Yet it is that not all have  the wherewithal nor patience for the dissemination of knowledge. So it shall be that those who are unfit to be Mentors shall not be given the duty, and those who become no longer fit shall be set aside for those -\nbetter suited.\n\nII. Though it is the Mentor shall seek those to teach, they shall at any time teach only  three; For the Brotherhood demands obedience, integrity, wisdom, and skill, and only with undivided attention and careful nurturing can these-\nvirtues be extolled upon those who seek to serve. Yet while the Mentor may choose their recruit, they must not know pride in them, and should they not grasp the duty laid before them and wield it unquestioningly, they shall be found unsuited and asked -\nto depart. Thus it stands as well that should they be found lacking by the Keepers, the same shall apply.\n\nIII. It shall be known that the gifts of Xan and his light are not what define the Brotherhood; Nay, it is our duty which makes us who we are. In-\nupholding and extolling the virtues of Xan, in defense of the Descendants and enforcement of Order, we are the Brotherhood. So it is that the first to be learned is not the light, but the foundation. The history of the Brotherhood is long-\nand storied, and our Creeds many, and these are what first are taught, and so too are taught the skills needed to uphold those Creeds and perform our duty. So it is that the Mentor teaches these things, and not the light.\nIV. Such it is that when those recruits first chosen by their mentors have proven themselves, and passed whatever trials laided out before them, they shall be offered a tether to our Patron, to be given the gift be bestows upon us for the completion of-\nour duties. Upon acceptance of this, the recruit shall be such no more, raised up to the rank of Initiate. Then it is they shall still report to their mentor, with whom they shall accompany on the field, though they will learn the art of the light from-\nTeacher, one who may have other students, but who will attend to their duty of teaching the light with diligence and care.", ""),
        StaticBook("Creed of Patron", "Vailoen", "Creed of the Patron\n\n'May Xan Protect us\nAnd in turn we protect others. Let him be our shield, so we may in turn be His sword, ridding this world of darkness.'\nI. You are the child of the Maker, the Creator, the Divine, for it is HE whom made all the First, the Aenguls and Daemons, and the Second, the Descendants. The Four Races, the Second Children, the Descendants, given life divine by the Creator's breath, -\nhave Xan's shield and his sword.\n\nII. Xan, Guardian by shield and defender of Order by blade, slayer of Chaos, the Golden Lion, given divine direction by the Creator, stands stalwart against forces of Chaos, taint, evil, and the powers-\nbeyond mortal kind, in such magnitude as to disturb the balance, which threaten the Descendants.\n\nIII. It is not the concerns of mortal wars which draw the Lion's gaze, for always there is war amongst the Descendants for -\nstruggle is eternal, a curse of the Betrayer which cannot be given relief, a result of the first sins. So it is that the wars mortal are not touched upon the Lion's Pride, for they are meant to be absolved by the descendants by whom they are waged.\nIV. it is the will of Xan that all who serve him do so in totality; As such none may raise their blade in service onto any other organization of mortal or immortal origin, nor shall they give service onto any other Aengul or Daemon. Nor shall, in that-\nsame thread, any service to him give reverence, worship, or praise higher onto any other than the Creator. Nor shall any equate Xan, servant of the Divine, onto the same level as the Creator-Of-All. Xan demands service, not worship.", ""),
        StaticBook("Creed of Realms", "Vailoen", "Creed of the Realms\n\n'As we serve Xan, we serve Order, not the men of law.'\nI. Though we shall not be commanded, we shall hold respect for the laws of those who claim the land upon which we walk, and whosoever of a land wears its crown shall have the Lion's obedience in matters of law, though not in fealty. Respect is required -\nto be given to all Descendants, though it shall be given note to recongnize the authorities of Kings, Princes, and noble folk, and greet them in manner appropriate, in dress and speech and action. Yet all the Descendants are equal in the eyes of the -\nCreator, such that any disrespect given by a Brother to any Descendant, from the lowliest peasant to the highest king, is a sin most foul.\n\nII. Every endeavour shall be made to learn the speech and ways of the realms and their folk, and to-\nrespect the manners in which they live, presuming they are not in direct opposition to the Virtues of our Patron. All must be approached with open mind and open heart, for though we may not understand nor agree, all Descendants are the children of our-\nCreator, and their ways shall be treated with respect. Places of worship shall be regarded with respect, though reverence saved for the Creator alone.\n\nIII. Though no alliance of military can be made with any one realm, for it is all-\nDescendants whom the Order defend, offers of assistance can and shall be made. For it need not be said but shall be, that the Order stand vigilant against any who threaten the Descendants truthfully, in manners such as those made clear in the Creed of-\nthe Patron. And so it stands, with need for neither ink nor writ nor parchment nor oath, that always the realms and those who govern them may request the Order's presence in matters which are their concern, with no payment either material or immaterial-\nexpected nor needed. Though it shall also be said that those lands which offer shelter and necessities to the Order in times of need shall be given the utmost gratitude of the Order and have the blessing of Xan.\nIV. But woe, the hearts of the Descendants have been tainted by the Betrayer and his sins, and so they are prone to being deceived, as was the fate of their Ancestors. So it is there may come a day when the Order seeks one sheltered by a realm. And -\nthough the Order will make the truth known to them, it may be that still they refuse to allow us our duty. Let it be known that we shall not seek violence against them, save in the most dire of cases in that an entire land has fallen to the blight in -\ntheir hearts, and even then those who still carry the light shall be given mercy and saved. When rebuffed by a realm a paladin will act as expected, and the Order shall convene and the Keepers shall deteremine the path, and always the way of words shall-\nbe chosen first. And though it grieves us, in the cases of men of deaf ears and closed hearts, who hear not the words of the Order's warnings, we may let lie, should the cause not be dire enough so as to upset an entire nation. And so these men shall-\nreap what they sow, and what tainted blight they allow in their midst shall be their own curse to suffer, for it is Order above all else we uphold, for Order is the linchpin of the Descendant's survival.", ""),
        StaticBook("Curry Recipe", "Daizuki", "-=-\n        \n         Katsu\n          Curry\n            Recipe\n\n\n\n            -=-\nIngredients:\n\nCurry Sauce\n-1/2 Pound of Beef\n-2 Onions\n-2 Carrots\n-3 Potatoes\n-1Tbsp of Oil\n-1Tbsp of Special Narazuno Curry Spice Mix\n\nPork Katsu\n-4 Pork Loins\n-1/2 Cup of Flour\n-2 Eggs\n-1 Cup of Bread Crumbs\n-1 Dash of Narazuno Special Blend of Different Seasonings.\nPrepare a plate of rice along with a piece of katsu pork ontop and finish with a healthy ladel full of curry on top.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cycle of Life", "Oo'ri Earthbreaker", "Examples of the Cycle of Life\n-----------------------\nCatapillar eats leaves, a bird eats the catapillar, the bird dies and fertilizes the earth, the earth grows plants, catapillar eats the leaves off the plants....\nBushes grow berries, birds eat the berries, the birds poop, the poop fertilizes and plants the seeds of the berries, the seeds grow to bushes, the bushes grow berries...\nKelp grows underwater\nthe kelp is eaten by fish\nthe fish poop \nThe kelp uses the poop as fertilizer\nthe kelp grows underwater", ""),
        StaticBook("D.L", "Davin Lodmund", "Analysis of the Harvester Construct\nThe constructs used in the attack on Rivel appear to be based off of the golem servants favoured by the Forgotten Dwarves and now being rediscovered by the Aegean dwarves.\nHowever, they are clearly different: they possess a killer instinct unheard of in servant golems, lack individual intelligence and possess an apparatus built into the hand capable of killing a mortal being and trapping their soul, no doubt for\ncontainment in the Soul Capacitors of The Seal. Countless Harvester Constructs were destroyed in their assault on Rivel, indicating a lack of quality in their construction: it seems the dwarves built them in a time of desperation.\nHowever, such a time now befalls us: the majority of Rivel’s Lesser Caste were killed by Harvester Constructs in the assault, and I fear this propaganda we are distributing to the Lesser Caste attributing this assault to deceptive attacks by the\nForgotten Dwarves will not placate them. We may downplay their intelligence, but even they must realise the Forgotten Dwarves have been extinct for over a millenium.\n- Davin Lodmund", ""),
        StaticBook("D.L.M", "Davin Lodmund", "Snow's Maiden, 1595\nA traveller's guide to\nsurvival by Ilbryn\nSo, you find yourself on the road. You've plenty of food, and know where you are going. You may think you are safe, however you aren't. When I travel, I follow several rules religiously. At\nnight time, I climb a large tree to rest. Many aren't as skilled at climbing as I, so if you can't easily climb a tree, you should find a place off-road and secluded to rest. If someone tries to lure you from the tree, do not come down. They may be\nscreaming for help, however that's easily pulled off, and nearly got me killed. When travelling, you should not stop for anyone asking you to, or to come with them, no matter how nice or convincing. They're likely muggers, or worse, as a man on the road\nwith no place to go should not be trusted. I've only had one experience with coming along was a bortu inviting me to the grand opening of a blackjack hall, I only went with because he was with a group of humans. Also, the same can apply to entering\na new town. Whilst in Johannesburg, I was invited to a house for tea. Instead, I was mugged under threat of battle-axe, and lost several tens of mina, as well as my weapon, and several magic apples.\n-Davin", ""),
        StaticBook("da truth", "Alexander Ragnarson", "only in curon for low taxes and good alcohol", ""),
        StaticBook("Daeland", "Marlene Alderwood", "The Revitalization of Daeland\nSnow’s Maiden 1660\n\nA new era has fallen upon us- the proud Barony of Daeland is to open its gates in welcoming new and aspiring citizens to join its humble lands. \n\nProviding food and shelter - all citizens are treated with equality and respect - there is no nobility and no taxes on housing or land each and every man belongs to oneself. \nOur farms flourish, growing golden wheat as far as the eye can see, our lake gives life, offering fish. \n\nNow is the time to join the Barony of Daeland, land of free peoples and great bounty. The gates are open, and free housing awaits. \n\nPlease inquire with the following peoples if you are inclined:\n\nFindlay Guthrie ( Weakk) \nGwion Gallic (Gallic)\n(Berserker)\n\n\nWell Wishes and Respects,\nM. Alderwood ~", ""),
        StaticBook("Damp Letter", "Anonymous", "Thank you for heeding my warning.\n\nI know the circumstances are less than ideal, but the castle that stands before you is not as abandoned as it seems. Even now, it swarms with Wraiths of soldiers long departed from their bodies and minds.\nWithin, beyon the Wraiths, you will find the true threat. I will guide you along the way. Take heart. We will meet soon.\n\n-A Friend.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Magic & You", "Nienna Calm", "Dark Magic\n      And You!\n-------------------  A Guard's Guide to\n  Identifying Dark \n          Mages\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Nienna Calm\nForeWord\n-------------------This book was written with the intent to educate the guardmen and women of the Caliphate of Khalestine. However, should you find this book in your possession, I would suggest reading it anyways. It is a good\nguide for identifying Dark mages.\nWhat is a\n    Dark Mage?\n-------------------\nA dark mage is a user of magic that inherently harms others in order to function. Dark Mages can receive their powers in a variety of manners; including Pacts with dark gods, Rituals set forth by\nIblees, and other similarly horrifying methods. It is for this reason that all Dark Mages must be identified and killed on site, for they would not hesitate to do the same to you.\nNecromancy\n-------------------\nNecromancy is the quintessential dark magic, and probably the first to ever be founded. It's age has not made it any less dangerous, however, and is directly responsible for all manners of Wraiths and Liches plaguing\nthis world today. Necromancers drain the very life force of plants, animals, and indeed people around them to cast their spells. In fact, they need a constant supply of life force to even survive, and must seek it out regularly.\nHow to Identify:\nThe bodies of necromancers are often in a very frail, almost decayed state. Since Necromancers need life force to cast spells, be on the lookout for dead or tainted patches of plant life, or reports of people feeling drained after\ntouching a specific person. These are both serious signs of a Necromancer infestation.\nFrost Witches\n-------------------Frost Witches are monsters of Ice and Snow who disguise themselves as women and prey upon the libido of Men. The Frost Witch is an easy threat to counter in the hot weather of the Caliphate, but requires constant\nvigilance to identify. A Frost Witch's true form is bright blue, but using her curse's magic, she is able to take any form she pleases, so long as that form is female. Frost Witches use these disguises to trick men into a false sense of security,\nwhereupon they will take their true form, and devour the unsuspecting male.\n\nHow to Identify:\nThe easiest way to identify a Frost Witch is by touching their skin. A frost witch's body temperature is colder than anything one could imagine.\nThere is no way for them to disguise this. Also, because of this impairment, any disguised frost Witch will show signs of great fatigue under the Caliphate sun. Any women demonstrating a severe aversion to high temperatures and regular food should have\nthe temperature of their skin checked immediately.\nShades\n-------------------\nShades are the result of Iblees magic corrupting the mind and soul of an existing mage. These dark mages are ticking time bombs, for within them lies an eldritch, second personality that desires for only chaos and\ndestruction. Shades are capable of corrupting every form of Arcane magic, empowering their spells with the dark powers of Iblees himself.\n\nHow to Identify:\nShade mages are hard to identify, for their true nature is only\nrevealed when they cast spells. The hallmark of a Shade is the ability to create black tentacles out of thin air. Their ability to corrupt their own magic may cause them to cast spells that are not usually possible to create. If you suspect a mage of\nbeing a Shade, contact a cleric immediately. Shades suffer from severe aversion to holy spells and relics, and these can be used to verify if a mage is, in fact, a Shade.\nSoul Puppeteers\n-------------------\nSoul puppeteers are masters of curses. Using a small fetish (a doll of some sort), and a physical part of another person (such as their hair, blood, etc.), They are able to bring sickness, pain, and even death to a\nperson from an extreme distance. Random, shooting pains and illnesses with supernatural symptoms are strong signs of the interference of a Soul Puppeteer.\n\nHow to Identify:\nIt is difficult to identify a Soul Puppeteer\nstraight off. Be on the lookout for those who try to take blood or locks of hair from their enemies. If you suspect someone of Soul Puppetry, inspect them immediately for a fetish. It is not a guarantee that they will always have one on them, but it's the\nonly way to confirm for sure.\nSoul Contractors\n-------------------Soul Contractors are capable of fashioning magical legal documents that bind the signer to the very letter of their word. This would be potentially useful, if not for the material they must fashion these\ndocuments on. Soul Contracts can only be written upon the flayed skin of men that was taken whilst they were still alive. It is a brutal and horrifying process, that speaks to the inhumanity of these casters.\n\nHow to Identify:\nLike Soul Puppeteers,\nit is hard to identify a Soul Contractor. The only way to tell for sure is to either catch them in the act, or discover their flaying equipment, which may not even be on their person.\nBlack-Dragon\n     Parasites\n-------------------A more recent addition to dark magic, black-dragon parasites are a growing problem in the Caliphate. A black-dragon parasite is an insidious form of insect that infects its hosts and causes\ncauses them to literally absorb blood and the flesh of the mortal races in return for benefits. It is unknown how is parasite passes from person to person, so it is absolutely vital that you keep any suspected carrier of this foul creature far away from\none's person at all times. It is unknown at this time if Black Dragon Parasite victims can be cured, so it is recommended that they be either expelled from the city on sight, or, in extreme cases, purged.\n\nHow to Identify:\nBlack-Dragon Parasites\nare easy to identify. All carriers of the parasite bear a tattoo of a black dragon on their person, usually winding around the stomach area. If you suspect someone of having this terrible disease, conduct a full-body search immediately.\nGeneral Warning\n    Signs Of A\n    Dark Mage\n-------------------\nDark Mages can and will follow stereotypes at times. If you keep a look out, there are many signs that indicate if a person is just a dark mage in general. These are by no means\ndeciding factors in a suspect's ability to cast black magic, but they are definitely red flags to investigate.\n\nBe Suspicious Of Any Persons you see that:\n\n-Wear Primarily Black Robes.\n\n-Are Hooded at all times\n-Possess bright red eyes.\n\n-Project a magical Aura that Black, Gray, or Red in color.\nAs a guard of the Caliphate, it is up to YOU to root out these psychopathic evildoers wherever they might rise their ugly heads. For the sake of our grand city, do your duty well.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Passages", "Mysterious Author", "*This book's cover is entirely black. The material used to craft it seems to be leather, though it's thicker then usual. Whatever it's made out of. It's obvious it's not that of an animals hide.*\n-As you open the book. You'd take notice on how each and every page is made of a thin leather as well. The coloring of each being a light shading. The words written are thinnly laced along too. Diffrent from a regular quills.-\nGreetings ot whom ever reads these words incribed.\nYou now have the chance to learn and take in things that I've experianced on my adventures throughout the diffrent lands we've traversed.\nI've seen many things, though I'll speak of few in these pages. One competely corporal. Though, the other. Not so much.\nThe first I'll speak on is that of those whom once held breath. Once lived as you and I do.\nTasted, laughed. And possibly loved. Though, for such beings. These things matter none to their broken minds. They exist on, after death to carry out one goal. To feast on the warm flesh of the living. To taste the life that runs in\nthe blood that flows through every vein in your body. If you, who reads has such.\nThese creatures that crawl, creep and continue to come after being hit, even after losing limbs. For physical pain is nothing to them.\nThey only feel the lust to feed. To devour all life that harbors in every fiber of a living things body.  Though, I've also witnessed them gnaw on a corpse, long dead as it's dried skin cracked between it's jagged teeth.\nThey seem to be in a constant setting of pain. Though only from their shattered minds trying to cope with realities harsh lessons of how tampering with nature. Can have\nunexpected repercussions. Even in creating\nsuch a being. As few truely take to heart. That monsters do, what monsters are capible of. And that they should be feared by all the living.\n*A detailed picture is penciled in. That showing of three Ghouls. One being a human with a cut neck. The second, an Uruk who's head is half caved in. And the third, a Ghoul Kha that's missing a right arm. All three are reaching out.\nTheir faces all posed in a sorrow-filled expressoin. Though they seem to be clawing.. At the reader, as if to make a point.*\nAs for the second being of darkness I shall decribe, is one that has found a way to ascend in their own sense. Through warping the ways of a certain dart art. They're are to unbind themselves from this realm, though partially\nto say. As their spirit is in a constant struggle. Caught between both the land of the living. And that of the dead. Something anyone would. nd should dread even the thought. Though, from my seeings. I've taken note\nthat some have lost their minds partially. Forgetting and rambling on. Those they knew. Nothing stuck to this one. But others. Are as they were in their mortal shell. Calm for the most part. Though brash all the same when\nspeaking for them in anycase.  For they are in a state of undeath. Damnation that rids them of mortal needs. But a thirst for life still. As I've witnessed them suck the land dry around them. Leaving nothing of a husk of flora\nand trees. Fueling them along in whatever their twisted minds compel them with. Though, if one is wise. And hopefully fast on their feet if not. Then if running into one of these unholy creatures. You could have a talk.\nFor those whom do so. Would say that they hold many secrets. Some willing to share. Others, they keep for only the most trustworthy. Living or otherwise.\n\nRemember. Do not make enemies with a Wight. For death\nis only a setback in their burning, though hollow eyes.\n*On the next page is a penciled drawing of two Wights. Each being vastly diffrent looking. The first, being a hooded figure of a man at first. Though when squinting at the small drawing. You'd then be able to make out\nthe skeletal outline on it's facial features. It's would be hands that of a skeletal appearance as it's eyes give a faint illumnination of a red glow coloured in with some type of dye. The second figure stands to resemble that\nof a Lich. It's would be head missing any trace of flesh at all as it's hollowed out eyesockets glow with nonshaded dots of flames that seem to harbor nothing to burn to. It holds a large staff in both hands. Cradling it to one\nside as it leans towards that angle. Both skeletal figures stand to stare directly outward at the reader.*\nI leave you now to ponder on what's been taught. But remember this. The next time you hear something slam in an alleyway. Or shuffling noises permeate the darkness ahead of you. Think twice on traveling forth. For the\nshadows hold many secrets. Some harmless. Others not so much.\n((No signs of whom wrote the book are given. Only the knowledge provided is set within these pages.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Darkstalkers", "An Elder Cleric", "A Guide To\n      Darkstalkers\n\n\n            By\n     An Elder Cleric\nIntroduction\n\nAn eerie silence, unbecoming of the normally bustling town, even late in the night. A distant suit of armour, shuffling and groaning as black smog flows from it's joints... and the sound of steel scraping as it turns to look at you.\nIntroduction\n\nDear Reader, one of the most potent enemies you shall ever encounter is the Darkstalker of Yore. Fret not, however, for reading this book will afford you better chances in dealing with this menace. Good luck either way though.\nIdentifying\n\nSimilar to how Morghouls give off an odor of death and rot, Darkstalkers do the same. Unlike their counterparts, the Lich, however, they will be wearing heavy armor and wielding stronger weapons as this is their purpose.\nIdentifying\n\nAlong with other undead creatures, they will be against showing their form from beneath their armor and avoid sunlight, holy areas, and aurum. A black fog will also emit from the joints in their armor as life force escapes.\nStrengths\n\nAs stated, the Darkstalker is created to be the fighter of the Undead army. While they are still skeletons by nature, their bones have become hardned to be similar to iron, allowing them to wear armor and wield heavier weapons.\nStrengths\n\nAs all undead creatures, these have risen from death and are immortal. They require life force to continue their existance, and are able to drain such through a draining touch. They also, like Liches, have a phylactery.\nWeaknesses\n\nWithout a constant source of life force, their body crumbles. While they are stronger than normal Morghouls and Liches, they are still skeletons. This means that blunt damage can shatter their bones and destroy them.\nWeaknesses\n\nAs with all undead, they are weak to aurum and holy magics. Should their phylactery be destroyed, they are removed from this realm forever, making them worrisome of such being destroyed.\nTemperment\n\nLike all undead creatures, sanity slowly slips from their control as their hunger grows. While they may be able to hide in public for periods of time while satated, they can become violent and aggressive quickly.\nDraught\n\nThe Darkstalker can take on a mortal form with use of the Draught of Incite.\n\nPlease read up on the Draught of Incite to learn more of it and how it affects undead creatures.\nConclusion\n\nIn conclusion, Darkstalkers are the muscle of the undead army and one of the final forms a ghoul will attempt to achieve. Utilize blunt weapons and blessed magics to take one down swiftly. And as always, aim for the head!", ""),
        StaticBook("Day of Execution", "Wilbert Woodstock", "Days of Execution ~\n\nHe wears a noose around his neck.\n\nHe smells of an awful wreck.\n\nHe has been through tough times.\n\nHe may have commited a couple crimes.\nThis man is not one to mess with.\n\nIf you do, you will need a good blacksmith.\n\nHis voice would be hoarse.\n\nHe appears to be a strong force.\n\nThe executioner failed him.\nThe life he lives is quite grim.\n\nThere is only one solution.\n\nAnother execution. . .", ""),
        StaticBook("De Dwarven Songs", "Galin Silvervein", "The Hidden art of the Mountain Dwarves\n\n\n     Music is an art that as been with the mountain dwarves for a long time. A legendary Dwarven story would not be very special without the addition of music and singing. The dwarves use\ninstruments such as the drums, bagpipes, and lute to recall stories. Dwarves often sing in harmony at ceremonies, taverns, and before battle.\n     Dwarves are known to be some of the most talented bards in the realm, many being specifically skilled with\nthe lute. \n     Songs before battle is a very important part of Dwarven culture. If ye happen to have the pleasure of battling alongside dwarves, you will without a doubt hear them singing the famous song known as Umgoroki Umgoroki Undor.\nMost Dwarves know this song by heart, and sing it before battle. \n    Not many people know about the important contribution music has on the dwarven culture, but now after reading this.....Well, ye know.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Dawn", "Idril Aureon", "Dear Dawn,\n\n  I'm sorry about what happened at your house. I'll try to keep them under control though I know it'll be hard. We're going to move to a bigger house soon so hopefully that will help.\n\n      -Idril Aureon", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Neighbors", "Bernard Oakstool", "Dear, Neighbors,\nIt is I Bernard.\nI have been notified that because you are new to the area, you will have to jump ship before the vrakai seize you. They are letting me stay for a mass tax due to the amount of time I have been located here.\nI am very sorry that things had to go this way, but I think you can still keep your island if you expand it further from the mainland. \n\nIt was nice meeting you.\n-Bernard.", ""),
        StaticBook("Death", "Sargeant Dutch", "If the council desides that i may be put to death i want everything i have, own and do be passed down to: Telmarill the north. long may my brother live", ""),
        StaticBook("Decapitation", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Track down the beast that attacked Dirk and bring back it's head.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dedicancy Vol. 1", "Irawyn", "Irawyn's Dedicancy\n      ~ Journal ~\n\n    * Volume One *\n\nPage 2 - Summary\nPage 3 - Totems\nPage 4 - Hierarchy\nPage 6 - Circles\nPage 8 - Traditions\nPage 9 - The Aspects\nPage 12 - Kese\nPage 18 - Totem Ex.\nPage 22 - Events\n- Summary -\n\n* Evaluate the Order\n* Understand Events\n* Speak with Druids\n   + Traditions\n   + Totems (Meaning)\n   + Hierarchy\n   + Circles\n   + Aspects\n   + Other Importance\n* Return with Sufficient Knowledge\n- Totems -\n\n* Symbolic Title\n   + Personality\n   + History\n* Self-Decided\n* Not Literal\n* Can be changed\n   + Frowned Upon\n* Aspect Affiliation\n   + Implies Affinity\n     Towards Cerridwen\n     or Cernunnos\n- Hierarchy -\n\n* Demi-Aspect\n   + Highly Revered\n   + Passed on\n* Hierophant\n   + Retired, Important  * Archdruid\n   + Heads, Managers\n   + Overall Powerful\n* Guide\n   + Teach Dedicants\n* Druid\n* Dedicant\n   + Pre-Attunment\n* Lost Druid\n   + Passed away\n* Forgotten Druid\n   + Long Gone\n* Unattuned\n* Shunned\n   + Threats to the\n      Order\n   + Don't Speak to...\n   + Much Wind Pours         From Your Mouth\n- Circles -\n\n* Mother Circle/Grove\n   + Main Circle\n   + Has Branches\n   + Order Focus\n\n* Naelurir\n   + Elf Exclusive\n   + Aspectist\n   + Created by Art\n   + Dominion Clergy\n   + Political\n* Stream Circle\n* Equinox Circle\n* Respiren's Circle\n* Father Circle\n   + Cernunnos Aligned * Circle of Scions\n* Wandering Circle\n\n Many circles are temporary and wish to\nbreak the mold. Tend to fall apart. Circles exist to organize druids, spread ideals.\n- Traditions -\n\n* Respect Elders\n* Respect Nature\n   + Give & Take\n   + Balance (Cycle)\n* Silence During Moots\n* Family & Bonds\n* Naelurir\n   + Sacrificial Burning\n   + Bloodletting\n* Keep the Void at Bay\n- The Aspects -\n\n* Cernunnos\n  + Father of the Hunt\n  + Creator of Animals\n    - Fauna\n    - Predator/Prey\n* Cerridwen\n  + Mother (Fertility)\n  + Green Lady\n  + Creator of Plants\n    - Tree & Flower\n    - Fruit & Seed\n  + Blight Healing\n- Origin -\n\n Cernunnos and Cerridwen worked together to fill the world with nature, and thusly create the natural cycle.\n\n Much later... The world was torn by Void Magic. The Aspects chose the first Druid in order to return balance.\nThe original druid ended up passing along druidism, returning balance to the natural cycle that the Aspects had originally created...\n\nVosirk Note - The Balance/Cycle of Life & Death, Hunter & Prey, etc... is far more complex under the Aspects.\n- Kese's Culture -\n\n Kese's people view Druids and the Aspects a bit differently. Partially due to druids being so rare among his people.\n\n The Aspects are considered a mystery for the most part, and the deity Morrigan works alongside them.\nCerridwen originally filled the world with plants, but she was too gentle and the plants grew prideful and selfish in their longevity.\n\n Realizing this, she gave Cernunnos a glaive which he could control the seasons with. With the Mother's blessing he\ncreated Herbivores to eat the plants and Carnivores to eat the Herbivores. The existence of Omnivores remains a mystery.\n\nThis worked for a time... Until the Ancestors came and tipped the balance of the natural cycle in their own favor.\nMorrigan, a misunderstood deity, stepped in and took action. She granted plants and fungi their poisons, animals their brutality and altered senses. She made nature 'fair' again, making up for the Ancestors tipping the scale. After doing so, the\nAncestors came to respect nature and realize a circle of sort needed to be kept...\n\nThe Aspects are viewed in a darker and more mysterious light. They aren't seen as that generous. For when flora and fauna die, Cerridwen and\nCernunnos stay their hand.\n\nCerridwen is the nurturing mother...\n\nCernunnos is the fatherly patron, holding control over Cerridwen's domain...\n\nMorrigan is the much needed villain...\n- Personal Totems -\n\n* Deer Totem (Dwyn)\n   + Herding Nature\n   + Travel as Herd\n   + Forest Relation\n   + Strong Stag\n   + Protect Young\n* Scroll Totem (Kyral)\n   + Words Interpreted      By All Sorts\n   + Secretive\n* Iron Totem (Vosirk)\n   + Worn by Warriors\n   + Defend/Guard\n      - Ideals\n      - Homes\n      - Cherished\n      - The Balance\n* Apple Totem (Leyun)\n   + Fruit/Motherhood\n   + Sign of Knowledge\n* Birch Totem (Kese)\n   + Noble & Wise\n   + Stays Hand From\n     Altering Nature\n\nKese's Totem isn't about his close bond with his Birch Tree, Kokopelli. But rather because he is armed with the power of communion to alter nature's\ncourse, but also the wisdom to leave it uninterrupted. This is quite a noble and wise trait, similar to how Birch Trees are seen as symbols of nobility and wisdom in his culture.\n- Events -\n\n* Brother Bull's Death\n   + Unattunement\n   + Many Old Druids\n     Being Punished\n   + Many Still Haven't       Begun to Recover", ""),
        StaticBook("Dedicancy Vol. 2", "Irawyn", "Irawyn's Dedicancy\n       ~ Journal ~\n\n     * Volume Two *\n\nPage 2 - Assignment\nPage 3 - Redcaps\nPage 12 - Badgers\nPage 20 - Conclusion\n- Assignment -\n\n* Understand Druids\nServing the Aspects\n   + How & Why\n* Study Nature\n   + Two Items\n   + Different Biomes\n   + Relate to Aspects\n* Finish with Conclusion\n   + What Aspects Are\n   + How to Serve\n- Redcap Shrooms -\n\n The first 'Item of Nature' that I studied was a Redcap Shroom. Originally, I was told a bit about their reproduction and hallucinogenic effects. I then went about researching them further. (However, I did not eat them.)\nRedcaps get their name from the large red caps atop them, covered with white dots. The stalk and gills underneath are quite white.\n\n They can range in many different shapes and sizes, as well as varying hues of red.\nThese mushrooms are commonly found in swampy environments, as well as the underground. Yet, Redcaps can still spread to colder regions, as well as temperate ones.\n\n On a side note, Redcaps also offer hallucinogenic effects when eaten.\nThese effects are likely a defensive trait to disrupt animals from eating them.\n\nFinally, the feature about Redcaps that surprised me the most involved how it reproduced. Like most fungi, Redcaps procreate by releasing the spores under their cap.\nThese spores tend to get picked up by the wind and can cover large patches of land.\n\n The surprising bit is that these spores can have quite an effect on small animals (such as ants and brids) if inhaled or the spores cover the being.\nThis is just a theory, but apparently the spores can grow inside the animals, encouraing them to travel farther before killing the being and growing in this new location.\nSimilar to other fungi and plants, Redcaps also fall under Cerridwen's domain. Of course, this is primarily due to the fact that the Green Lady is the Creator of nature's plant life. However, the fungi lean towards the Fertile Mother in another aspect.\nThis aspect being fertility, and like most creations of Cerridwen, Redcaps are primarily focused on reproducing endlessly. However, this extends to the degree of causing chaos to ecosystems if left unhindered, tilting the balance.\nOf course, Cernunnos created animals to create balance with Cerridwen's greedy flora. Unfortunately, Redcaps overpower the smaller fauna birthed by Cernunnos. However, there are larger creatures that can step in to preserve the balance, such as Badgers.\n- Badgers -\n\n The reason that I chose Badgers as my second 'Item of Nature' is due to the fact that one of my colleagues was assaulted by one and brought me its leg after subduing the beast.\nHowever, this inspired us after we realized how the Badger is one of many fauna that protects its environment from over-reproductive parts of nature, such as Redcaps.\n\nIt felt only natural to pick Badgers as my second topic.\nBadgers are short, stubby and wide creatures similar in size to house cats and dogs. Their heads are originally wide, with thinner and long snouts.\n\nAfter his attack, my friend alerted me that their jaws were surprisingly strong.\nBadgers also have long claws, ideal for digging.\n\nAfter going out to different regions around Atlas, it was apparent that different badgers ranged from browns to blacks with different sized tails.\nHowever, their heads are always striped with white.\n\n Badgers reproduce quite quickly, able to produce a litter of pups and bring them to adulthood in less than a year.\n\n And the final fact is that Badgers are omnivores.\nThis means that Badger's can eat small animals, but also switch to plants and fungi if they have to.\n\n Being fauna, Badgers are a part of Cernunnos' domain, especially since they assist in halting the over-reproduction of fungi, like Redcaps.\nHowever, due to being an omnivore, they serve as an even better tool for keeping the harmony of nature. Instead of only going after fungi and plants, they can also hunt down smaller fauna if they grow too numerous instead of Cerridwen's creations.\nUnfortunately, they too can overpopulate without something to balance them. Which is why carnivorous predators higher up in the chain were created by Cernunnos.\n\nThe balance is surprisingly complicated...\n- Conclusion -\n\nOver the course of this task, I believe I came to a further understanding of the Aspects and how they came to learn how to properly manage and create an equilibrium after filling the world with nature.\nAs I explained in my previous task, Cerridwen, the Mother of Flora, filled the world with plants, who overgrew and had no limits.\n\nWhich is why Cernunnos intervened and created herbivores to keep her creations in check.\nAfterwards, he had to create carnivores to balance out the herbivores. And finally, added omnivores to help further keep things in check...\n\nThe Aspects serve as the Creators of all the nature that is around us.\nBut they also serve as a reminder: That  balance is important. It can be complicated to keep in check, but is worth it in the end.\n\n Although, I don't know why the Aspects don't keep nature's balance in check to this day.\nEitherway, it is quite apparent that the reason they handed down druidic magic to the first druid was in order so that our Ancestors could continue to keep the balance in their stead.\n\nThe Druids exist to make sure that harmony isn't disrupted.\nTo make sure that forces of nature don't overwhelm ecosystems.\n\nAs well as ensure that people don't disrupt environments. (Such as deforestation, over\nhunting, etc...)\n\nThis also doesn't mean to step in and stop the death of wildlife.\nThere is a reason that prey exist, that organisms have defensive mechanisms, that herbivores and plants don't spread limitlessly...\n\n What I've learned about the balance also relates back to the cycle, and that death is a key part to it.\nIn the end, what I've learned overall is how important the Aspect's creation of a balance amongst nature is.\n\n And I believe that keeping it in check is the primary goal of being a Druid...", ""),
        StaticBook("Dedicant's Vow", "12werbles12", "~*~\n  The Dedicant's Vow\n\nI now walk the forests with my new kin. I will swim the river of truth wherever it takes me. As the trees watch over us, I shall watch over others in need. I will serve nature and help restore balance, even as dusk\napproaches. I vow to uphold my duties as a Dedicant of the Druidic Order.\n\n   by:\n   Salmon Druid Petyr\n~*~\n\n\"I will walk the forest with my new kin.\"\n\nWith this statement, the Dedicant pledges his or her official ties to be with the Druids of the Druidic Order.\n~*~\n\n\"I will swim the river of truth wherever it takes me.\"\n\nWith this statement, the Dedicant pledges loyalty to the Order and thereby promises to speak the truth and never with deception.\n~*~\n\n\"As the trees watch over us, I shall watch over others in need.\"\n\nWhile under the guidance of the Aspects and the elder Druids, the Dedicant pledges to return the favor of respect and service.\n~*~\n\n\"I will serve nature and help restore balance, even as dusk approaches.\"\n\nThe Dedicant pledges devout service, no matter the time nor obstacle he or she may face.\n~*~\n\n\"I vow to uphold my duties as a Dedicant of the Druidic Order.\"\n\nThe Dedicant does just that; he or she vows to uphold his or her duties and their pledge as a Dedicant.", ""),
        StaticBook("Deep Cold, 1454", "Commodus de Jedih", "sadasdasdsadasdasdaProclamation of the Deep Cold (OSL)\nasdsadsadsadsadasdd\n\nBy Grandmaster Jack Rovin, 1454\n\nTranscribed by Comm.\n1663\nNote from Commodus:\n\nGrandmaster Jack Rovin's Proclamation of the Deep Cold, 1454 is widely accepted as the beginning of the Raevir-Lucienist War which would lead to the end of Carrion rule in 1456 and the disbandment of the Order of Saint Lucien-\nin 1459 after the Church's release of the Proclamation Of Demilitarization.\nsdsadsadsadsadsadsa\n\nBrothers, kin, allies, and friends, I ask for a humble and honest close to a new grievance that has plagued our own home.\nMen of Oren have fought eachother for too long, and it is time for this senseless killing to come to an end. But what fighting, you would ask, is taking place? The men of Flotsam and the men of Lucien are those whom have begun their feud. It was not long-\nago that we, all men of what is now Kaedrin, fought alongside each other. However, it is now that the greed of the people of Flotsam that has brought them to harbor bandits and heresies.\nOn what was to be a routine patrol throughout the lands of our newest continent, Anthos, the men of Saint Lucien, men whom protect the High Pontiff of the Faith, men who have sworn their lives to the defense and unwavering preservation of the Church, -\nwere selfishly and without consideration attacked by the means of a small force of bandits. Seeing the might of the Lucienist sword, the bandits retreated to their home in Flotsam, a small building for a union of laborers.\nIt was here that a siege persisted until the brave men of Lucien rammed down and killed the belligerents hiding inside. As they died, they cried for mercy from Saint Augustus. This has lead the Order of Saint Lucien to believe these men were actually -\nheretics!\n\nThe bloodshed did not stop here, however. A counter attack was formed. The men of Lucien, praying solemnly in the Bailiwick. of Kaedrin, were met with arrows and magic from the men of Flotsam.\nReceiving word of the massive attack, the Grand Commander, Voron of Rovin, took charge, and sent out a plea for help. The Grandmaster of the Order saw this plea, and assembled men of Ager and men at the keep. Soon enough, a reserve was levied,-\nand the attack on the Bailiwick was repelled, and another counter attack ensured.\n\nThe bandits were now identified fully as men of Flotsam. In their castle they hid, as the men of Lucien surrounded.\nWith but a pick, the Grandmaster sapped through a window, and the men of Lucien charged in, slaying all of the men that resided in the fortress. A glorious day, for the men of Lucien took no casualty during the short siege.\nIt was God who watched over his soldiers this day, proof of their legitimacy.\n\nWith this in mind, I write to all this request, this plea, to end the fighting. It is not in the interests of us as neighbors, as a -\nbody of men, and as a united coalition under God, to continue this senseless killing, this nonsense that plagues our race. I present to the public our humble and simple terms.\nI. Fighting is to immediately cease between the Flotsam Coalition and the Coalition of the Order of Saint Lucien and the Town of Ager.\n\nII. The men of Flotsam are to repent for their sins. Those who have not adopted the True Faith-\nshall convert and refrain from practicing any sort of heresy. The men who fought in the battle shall refrain from sin for one year, and will report to a clergyman if any sin is made.\n\nIII. The men of Flotsam who profited from the few deaths-\nof the men of Lucien that did suffer will return those belongings to the Order so that they may continue to fight heresies without needing to gather more material. Ten sets of iron armour,-\nincluding swords, shall be provided. Four bows and four quivers (16) arrows shall be provided. Two golden staves with two bags of emeralds (32) shall be provided.\nIf and when these unchanging terms have been accepted and completed, the men of Lucien will be sure to patrol through the town of Flotsam if requested to do so and protect it from heretical invasion. Friendship shall be renewed between the men of Lucien -\nand the men of Flotsam, and normal operations will persist.\n\nIf these terms, these humble and simple requests, are denied, the Poor-Fellow Soldiers of Horen and the Temple of Ard Krallackh will begin a fight to rid the town of Flotsam from all-\nheretical influence and force upon those that have fallen from grace the hand of the Creator.\n\nThe Grandmaster will request for the immediate excommunication of the occupants of Flotsam and the evacuation of the clergy for the-\nduration of the war. \n\nDeus Magnus,\n\nSer Jack Rovin, Grandmaster of the Poor-Fellow Soldiers of Horen and the Temple of Ard Krallackh, Knight of Justice of the True Faith, Master-and-Commander-\nof the Commandery of Ard Krallackh, Man-at-Arms of the Order of the White Rose\n\nSer Voron Rovin, Grand Commander of the Poor-Fellow Soldiers of Horen and the Temple of Ard Krallackh, Knight of Justice of the True Faith\nSer Rymuel Elendil, Grand Chancellor of the Poor-Fellow Soldiers of Horen and the Temple of Ard Krallackh, Knight of Justice of the True Faith\nSer Rosencrantz Revandir, Knight Commander of the Poor-Fellow Soldiers of Horen and the Temple of Ard Krallackh, Knight of Justice of the True Faith, Bailiff of the Bailiwick of Kaedrin\nAn authentic replication of Grandmaster Jack Rovin's seal is seen below.\nadsadsadsadasdasdsa", ""),
        StaticBook("Deep Harbour", "Evert Lyons", "Report on Underground Vaeyl Base:\n\n\"Deep Harbour\"\n\n\nby Evert Lyons\n5th of Sun's smile 1650\n\nI've arrived at the underground temple, the water seems to be held up by some magical forcefield that blocks water but lets humanoids through, i see no fish on the floor so they must have learned to avoid the area or are blocked\nas well.\n\nI made my way down the rope, the way that was blocked by the construct doesn't reveal anything but a tightly sealed door.\n\nAfter exploring for a bit i found a glass plate to the ocean with a hole, perhaps they use this for fishing?\nopposite of the fishing hole there sits a whirlpool of some sort, I cannot say what function it serves, it could be something magical or simply a bath.\nThe far side of the complex holds a library, i couldn't find any relevant information inside.\n\nThe other side of the complex just holds an empty room with an empty chest\nI found a barracks it holds 6 pairs of beds, do these Vaeyl men sleep in luxury or are they sodomites? there are two training dummies as well.\nThe portal room is inactive, looks like i'll have to get out the hard way.\n\nI'm climbing back up the rope and getting out of here before someone spots me.\n\nEvert Lyons\n1650", ""),
        StaticBook("Defense", "Eliza", "[!]\nAs you crack open the thick, heavy tome you begin to realize that all of the pages in the book have been hallowed out. Instead, a dense slab of ferrum covered in arcanic etchings fills the space.", ""),
        StaticBook("Deities: Worship", "Friedrich", "A Brief Overview\n- = - = - = - = - = -\nThere are countless Aenguls and Daemons within our realm, with a number of them offering us aid and protection through the use of deific magic. Here, we will not be going over every single one of them - only\nthose notable in the sense of offering us magic or other boons. Each one has their own ideals and views that end up being projected through their followers. As we begin, it will be made clear now that no Aengul outside of arguably Yeu Rthulu will be\nwritten under the assumption of them being 'kind'. In almost all cases Aenguls and Daemons stick strictly to their ideals on what they like, or dislike, based on personal preference; their followers mirror this, though often times in a positive way.\nTahariae\n- = - = - = - = - = -\nThe Aengul of Purity. Tahariae has a vision of a perfect world, and anything done by his Clerics is to eventually reach this goal. Impurity in his eyes is subjective to what he likes or dislikes. He blesses Clerics with the\nability to heal not out of kindness, but because wounds do not exist in his ideals of a perfect world. Clerics kill undead because they do not fit in his ideals, not because they are evil. Clerics can chose to be good people, but accomplishing the mission\nof Tahariae - making this perfect world - comes first.\nAeriel\n- = - = - = - = - = -\nAeriel's views are based far more on Souls than other Aenguls and Daemons. She believes, along with the Ascended, Souls are holy and should be protected at all costs. She blesses the Ascended under her with the ability\nto heal by taking the wounds of others onto themselves, and then naturally healing at an increased rate. She gives them Holy Fire as well, a combative magic made to target those with warped or otherwise altered souls.\nXan\n- = - = - = - = - = -\nThe Aengul of Order. Xan's focus is the maintanence of absolute order within the realm, working to purge those that may undo such. Even greater than this, he is often considered a Dragonslayer. It was\nhis artifact that slew the Drakaar that endangered the land, Setherien. His magic, granted to his Paladins, is capable of harming undead entities and other unatural beings, though his followers are allowed to kill anything that upsets the order of the\nrealm, and could ignore undead if said undead did nothing against it. Even more than undead, dragonkin who come into contact with Xannic mist will find themselves harmed with each passing moment. Paladins themselves are split into a physical fighting type\nalong with one able to perform ranged spells and attacks.\nYeu Rthulu\n- = - = - = - = - = -\nThe Aengul of Compassion. Yeu does not believe in fights, or any sort of violence unless in defense. Those who worship her stick with a strict set of Scriptures that they must follow. The main idea behind the religion\nis to bring yourself inner happiness by making those around you happy as well. A select few of her followers have been granted a special being, referred to as being an 'Augur' - a floating mass of kindness that works to bring her will into reality.\nOthers have managed to learn a magic from her graces, based around the creation of whispal servants of sorts.\nAspects\n- = - = - = - = - = -\nThe AenguDaemons of Nature. The Aspects, rather than being a singular Aengul or Daemon, are a trio of them. They work together to protect the natural balance of the world. Druids, though communed with Nature itself, gain\ntheir power through the Aspects. The two of them are that of Cernunoss and Cerredwin, the Lord of the Hunt and Lady of the Harvest. Working together they grant Druids the ability to control Nature, enhancing natural properties and asking beasts for aid.\nThey have a wide variety of nature related abilities.", ""),
        StaticBook("Delmira", "Hanasun Chet", "Dear Delmira,\n\nI had been searching for the book myself, along with a few others. Of course, you remember the entourage that had witnessed your distress at its loss.\nMy search led me to the wastes of jungled Krugmar. ->\nThey spoke about having books written by some elf they had killed in days past. I managed to steal this from a chest, luckily; but right afterwards, I was found, and... a tussle, left me and the book burned up. An orc threw me around a bit, but I managed\nto slip away. \n\nI brought it back to you, not only because of its dire importance, but also because I understand you are probably the only person who understands this research better than anyone else! I didn't understand any of the contents, and was\nsort-of hoping that I could help you somehow in the recovery of the second book, and by proxy, the Thanhium itself. \n\nI've heard that it can destroy entire cities, so, I wanted to help in doing my best to ensure that the safety of all was maintined.\nSincerely,\n\nAlfiermollo Esquire\n\n------\n\nDo you not even remember losing this book?\n\n------\n\nOh goodness! Yes! You lost this book a few weeks ago.\nYou freaked out about it in the front of the city. Some elf named Aewion was there. You were seeking him for counsel. \nYou didn't remember where you put it.\n\nA few of us, like I said, then went to look for it; I found it in the hands of orcs, and the rest\nI already wrote about...\n\nI did not steal it! I found it, almost died, and then returned it to you! You were covered in blood, I think, and helping your partner. He had been injured from something. I was just running back from my encounter with the orcs.\nYou are still missing a second book, I believe.\nAnd I have reason to believe the orcs still have this other one.\n\n... You found your Thanhium?\n\n----\nIt's good to know that you know where it is again! There was ever a sense of\ndanger in the thought that no one knew where that deposit is.\nBut good to know that it's safe now. I remember people were freaking out about having to tell the Prince about this. The amount of danger it would bring to the Dominion. But now that you safely\nknow its location again, it's okay.\n\nThe orcs may still have that second book, but with the first in your possession, I'm sure they can do little with it.\nJust... anything sweet?", ""),
        StaticBook("Demilitarization", "Commodus de Jedih", "sdasdsadsadsadasdsdslssProclamation Ofdl\ndddDemilitarizationddd\nsssssssssssssssssss\n\nBy Chancellor Bishop Henry II Horen, 1459\n\nTranscribed by Comm, 1663.\nNote from Commodus:\n\nThis is a short proclamation that lead to the disbandment of the first Order of Saint Lucien in 1459. Many of the former Church militia joined House Chivay's Imperial Army during the Third Empire.\nsdsdddddddddddddddd\nHenceforth, by decree of the Chancellor of the College of Bishops of the Church of the True Faith, it is determined that the Order of Saint Lucien is released from their vows to the Church. The Order has effectively served the Church for many decades,-\nbut it has been determined that the attachment of secular orders to the Church distracts from the Godly mission of ministering the True Faith to the faithful.\n\nI. The Order of Saint Lucien, its sworn members and adherents,-\nare hereby released from secular oaths to the Church and papacy.\n\nII. These orders may retain their cohesion as independent bodies, or may dissolve. They are suggested to make oaths under the imperial crown to better serve humanity as auxilliaries-\nof the Exercitus Imperium.\nassssssssssssssssss", ""),
        StaticBook("DemiseOfTerafil", "Archmage Crumena", "Being no strangers to conflict, political or otherwise, it seems to be a miracle that one house, the Miiystra, has ruled over the other noble clans of Menorcress for so long. Nearly every other noble clan has shifted power and positions at some time in\nhistory, but never have the Miiystra given up their seat of power at the very top. That is not to say attempts to overthrow the Miiystra have not occurred before, however. In fact, it is due to the very nature of the Mori'Quessir, of\nviciousness, ruthlessness, and an always-competitive urge that has kept the Miiystra in power for so long. Coups have been attempted, but all have crumbled into dust before fruition. The one which got closest to victory, closest to the\ncomplete annihilation of House Miiystra, is perhaps the best to look at when considering how the realm of politics functions in Menorcress.\nThe name of the House responsible for this is no longer spoken in good company, lest you wish to lose\nyour head. We record it here at great risk for our own well-being and have even gone so far as to translate it into a more accessible version of the common tongue. That being said, We feel obligated to warn you that being caught reading of this\natrocious event (Which, we, as the authors, in no way condone any sane being attempt to replicate) in the company of the Mori'Quessir, or in any location under the control of House Miiystra, you may find yourself unable to read anything.\nEver again. We also request that you use this document only for learning of history-Not for attempting to repeat it. There are many other things which we, as a group, should be investigating. Things far less lethal than the Mori'Quessir and\ntheir history. As such, we implore you to take this document so that we may be on our way. Quickly. Please. We also do not wish for our names to be known, for all of the above reasons, and many others. If you'll excuse us, we have some nice\nDwarven runes to attempt to translate now.\nAt least the worst danger in Dwarven territory is collapsing rocks and lava…\nForty-some years ago, in the city of Menorcress, existed 6 Houses- 5 Nobles and 1 Head. These\nnoble houses were the Mierillis, Mages of great renown. The Zaurret, peddlers of services and entertainment. The Malachai, founded and headed by the legendary warrior Elrodon'Malachai. The Cressa'mtor, merchants responsible for\nthe flow of goods throughout the city. And finally, the Terafil. The Terafil were an odd bunch, run by Matron Mother T'risskiira, they were a clan of workers for hire. Mercenaries, miners, messengers and the like, they had no specific specialty besides\nbeing hard workers. There was also the Head House, the Miiystra. To give a quick overview of the Miiystra and their claim to power, we must take a brief look at their ancient history. All of them are descended from the Eldest Daughter of Nemiisae, their\nGoddess, and can trace their bloodline firmly back to her. The Miiystra are not only in charge of the other Houses, but also rule over the Cleric College and all aspects of religion, being the most \"holy\" as it were in the eyes of Nemiisae.\nThis\ndispleased T'risskiira. In their eyes, they were the most devout, the most holy, and the most deserving of power and praise. They wished not only to be the Head House, but also the closest to their Goddess. It was with this in mind that they began their\nplot to overthrow the Miiystra and take their place as the favored bloodline. They amassed weapons, gathered allies and were soon ready to throw their full force against the Miiystra.\nThey marched suddenly and without warning into the\nhalls of the Palace, shedding blood as they went and sparing no one. Slaves, warriors, servants and blood members all fell. The other houses quickly came to action, but not to assist the Terafil. No, you see, the way of Menorcress is in\nan old saying. \"If your enemy has power, take it. If you cannot take it, remove it from him so that no one else may take it.\" You see, if the other noble clans could not take Miiystra's position and power, they did not wish for Terafil to have it.\nHouse Mierillis rose immediately, marching into the war-zone that was the palace in an attempt to save the High Matriarch and as many of her kin as they could. House Malachai marched as well, eager to fight and slaughter House Terafil.\nIn but one day, dozens of House Miiystra fell. High Matriarch Veylna was slain and only a few of her children survived. At first, it was believed only two of them survived; The Eldest Daughter, and the Eldest Son, both saved by House Mierillis. They\nretreated then, creating a new base at the Cleric College, still safe from the Terafil-Traitors. There they stayed for several weeks to regain their strength, while House Mierillis held off the attackers. Then they marched on the palace, another\nblood bath ensuing, cleansing the walls of Miiystra blood with the blood of the Traitors.\nIn but a few short weeks, the Miiystra clan was devastated and the Terafil clan was annihilated. The Eldest Daughter mournfully took her place as High\nMatriarch and the last of the females of the bloodline… That is, until Elrodon'Malachai arrived to recognize her as High Matriarch, as all of the House Heads were required to do. The High Matriarch was none too pleased to see this man;\nWhile he had aided greatly in the fight by slaughtering the Terafil, he had not come to her to pledge his undying allegiance while she was in exile at the Cleric College. He had done the right thing by helping to slaughter the Terafil, but for\nwhat reasons, precisely, had he done it? The ambiguity of his ambitions made her weary of him and what he did next made her even more so. For from behind himself appeared a young woman, perhaps 70 years of age, cloaked in a robe.\nHouse Malachai had saved a few of the younger ones, namely the only other female to survive the slaughter. Without demanding power, money, or anything in exchange, in an uncharacteristically generous gesture, Elrodon'Malachai handed over the\nyounger sister to the New High Matriarch. He then performed his duties as a House Head, recognizing the High Matriarch as the ruler of Menorcress, then left, as quietly as he had came.\nIt was in this way that the Miiystra bloodline was nearly\ndestroyed; that a traitorous clan was destroyed, and how stability was returned to Menorcress. Mierillis would remain a strong ally of the High Matriarch for their assistance in the revolt, while for many years rumors would spread through\nthe city as to Elrodon'Malachai's ambitions. In the end, he went to his grave with not another soul knowing how or why he had rescued the youngest daughter. But the fact remained that he had, and for the stability of Miiystra and the maintaining of the\nstatus quo, most of Menorcress was grateful.\nSome Forty years after the fall of House Terafil, the mentioning of its name has been banned from Menorcress. It has been purged from most of the record books and its old clan home left\nto stand, burned and rotted, as an example to all. Not a drop of the Terafil blood still remains, and if it does, said blood is sure to keep their mouth shut, lest they tear open old wounds, and cause new ones to themselves.\nRescribed by Archmage Crumena V. Ilwindior on the 2nd of The First Seed, 1473.", ""),
        StaticBook("Desc. Leaves", "Callax", "-=-=-=-=-=-\n          Descending\n              Leaves\n           =-=-=-=-=-=\n\n\n\n\n\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\nAs the tree grows older, its roots wither and from the lack of nutrient the tree, too, withers. The tree, stiff and hollow, is parched and barren. Its leaves descend, becoming fewer and fewer. Like the leaf, I descend.", ""),
        StaticBook("Desert Rose", "Saeed Ibn Malek", "Desert Rose\n-------------------A Poem By Saeed Ibn Malek\n-------------------\nI dream of rain,\nI dream of gardens in the desert sand,\nI wake in vain,\nI dream of love as time runs through my hand,\nI dream of fire,\nThose dreams are tied to a horse that will never tire,\nAnd in the flames,\nHer shadows play in the shape of a man's desire,\nThis desert rose,Each of her veils, a secret promise,\nThis desert flower,\nNo sweet perfume ever tortured me more than this,\nAnd as she turns,\nThis way she moves in the logic of all my dreams,\nThis fire burns,\nI realize that nothing's as it seems,\nI lift my gaze to empty skies above,\nThis rare perfume is the sweet intoxication of her love,\nI dream of rain,\nI dream of gardens in the desert sand,\nI wake in vain,\nI dream of love as time runs through my hand,\nSweet desert rose,\nEach of her veils, a secret promise,\nThis desert flower,\nNo sweet perfume ever tortured me more than this,\nSweet desert rose,\nThis memory of Peace haunts us all,\nThis desert flower,\nThis rare perfume, is the sweet intoxication of the fall.\n----------------------------\nBy Saeed Ibn Malek\n(I did not make this my self irl <3 thanks for reading)", ""),
        StaticBook("Di vitali es", "Almisael", "These foul creatures are all but reasonful, their souls are corrupted by greed and deceit. No matter what we do, the holy words of the divine creator shall never penetrate their thick skulls. \n\nAll savages devoid of reasons shall be purified once the\ndivine light of the creator shine. \n\nThese savages cannot fear a god that they cannot see, so i shall give them one. \n\nThe divine eye of the creator shall look down upon its wretched creations, and all the malevolant spirits will be completely\ndestroyed, it will be a world free of impurity, a world free of malevolence, a world free of sins.\n\nThe world, rots.\nThe world, rots.", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary", "Goblin Cheiftain", "We fight for her\nWe no kill Her Dwarf\nThey kill her Dawrf. We say why\nThey no think. they kill us.\nWe kill them\nWe send for help soon.\nWe call Gold Commander.", ""),
        StaticBook("Diary of Simon", "Edward Suffolk", "The Diary of Simon.\n\nStanding outside the gate of Azeron, i recieved an odd quest to lead the wizard blundermore to some undead fortress by the request of Elton Stonewall.\nI must now speak with somebody who has been inside the fortress in order to give blundermore information\nI spoke to a man at the gates of Evermoor, he wanted to visit the inside. he wore green and grey.\n\nFarfolk Approaches me with a training Sword. He is hesitant to respond.\n\nA man in white and black armor questioned me about my whereabouts. i responded plainly. The Victim is occupied with sparring. i waited until they were done.\nAn Elf Told Me some stuff about the Fortress.\nTrapped Enterance, large hole, some device pushes you off a ledge, there's arrow traps, secret enterances at the bottom.\nMostly tunnels and crypts\nMorghuuls reside inside\nA Few Morghuuls the Elf Says\n\nI Futiely attempt to break up the spar in order to finish my work.\nThey cease fighting, i question the woman.\nShe does not remember. this is odd.\nShe had a bad dream\nABout the undead.\nshe begins to remember, undead man, named tristian, led her off the wall and into the cropfeild. She lost her hair, her tongue, ate all her fingers but one. Dark robes. Did not eat left ring finger\nMan named master. they took her to him.\nShe was to be an example. for whom? \n\nI found a llama.\nHe's named George.\nI met a man named Oakstool, he's a wanderer like me. I met a Kha named Kari or something\nI met that same green man, he might be evil idk.\nBernard and i walked along the road.\nWe went to Evermoor.\nWent to the Undead mountian.\nI met a man named dingar, dinger, and Claudas. i  walked into curon\nThe Spooky Place was too spooky so we left.\ni met a girl named Cheryl who rode a horse. Dingar is a cool orc. \n\nCheryl came with us to Evermoor, i chased off bad guys, A arcane merchant talked with us\nhe said i could get an ice ball shooter. i want to learn ice magic.\n\nWe went to the Zombie land with Rosylnn.\nCrazy Jester in Evermoor\n\nI met a lady, some elf. She went with me to Evermoor again\nSome masked Preist sat at the gates, he was joined by Rosey, and some other elf. we went inside. cooled off. George is inside too.\n\nGalen is a Clown under that mask.\nElf lady didn't like ZOmbie land\nGEORGE IS GONE, MY LIFE IS OVER.\nI LEFT HIM AT THE BAR AND NOW HES GONE\n\nI SPOKE TO A MAN WHO I SAW AT THE ISLAND AND HE COULDNT FIND HIM\n\nI SPOKE TO A DWARF AND HE COULDNT FIND HIM\nI set a bounty for 50 minas all along the crossroads. Mod Couldn't do anything, Ral became a brick Orc. Going to blundermore for help\ni tell him everything about the stronghold, write him a report.\n\nEvermoor didn't have shit.\nI went back to evermoor, met with the victim lady, some magicless preists, befriended a flowerboy, took flowerboy to the stronghold, somebody was there, gate was closed, Capt'n Gol'n Eye is ajax.\nAjax wants gold, i offered his eyepatch for gold.\nI got thrown into the water by miss pirate lady, i got dingar and the elf girl.\nBernard came over too", ""),
        StaticBook("Dies Irae", "Thomas of Celano (Baronvo)", "Dies Irae\n  Thomas of Celano\nDreaded day, that day of ire, When the world shall melt in fire, Told by Sybil and David's Lyre. Fright men's hearts shall rudely shift, As the judge through gleaming rift Comes each soul to closely sift.\nThen the trumpet's shrill refrain, Piercing tombs by hill and plain, Souls to judgement shall arraign. When the judge his seat shall gain, All that's hidden shall be plain, Nothing shall unjudged remain.", ""),
        StaticBook("Digowen Part 1", "Jallentime", "One cold winters morning, upon the breast of new fallen snow, there stood a proud spruce forest of irrefutable infamy. There is nothing immediately discernible about these woods; the trees carried the same burdens of frost and insects as any other for\nmiles around. But what this forest did have, and that was quite unheard at the time, was a name. Digowen Woods was the name given to it, or at least that was the name etched into the sign just outside. If you decided to follow this sign you would find\nyourself upon the shambles of an old frontier road, long since buried under mounds upon mounds of soil and brown pine needles, only apparent from the trees whom still could not breach the stone laid so very long ago. It was peaceful here, in inherently\nominous. On this particular day a tattered huntsman trudged his way through the thicket, scattering leaves and pine-cones at his feet as he dragged a chain of cold, metal traps behind him. He stopped only a moment at a time, his eyes gazing at the\nlandscape around him and the ghostly breaths emanating from his throat, before he would lay down his trap and pull back the jagged teeth around it. The huntsman's pattern continued well on into the day, until the sun passed well over it's perch in the sky\nand began to refract it's light upon the forest floor. Golden brown sunshine danced throughout the canopy, signaling the forest creatures that night would soon belong to the predators, of whom Nature did not count it's intruder.\nThe huntsman, sadly, realized the error he had made too late, and found himself far from home, in a world not his own. He dragged his coarse leather boots through the rotting needles, clearing a small section of the forest floor to himself as the last\nbeams of light shone through the mist above him. He laid down on this small amount of luxury, and stared skyward at the cloudless midnight above him, his mind slowly counting each star and naming them off to himself. Soon his eyelids fell, and his dreams\novertook him.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dire Wolves", "Art Camoryn", "Dire Wolves\nD.O.C Euclid\n\nAppearance: \nMuch like in form to their canine cousins, the Timber or Lur wolves, however, Dire wolves are far larger, the size of bears. Their jaws are longer and fur thicker.\nBehaviour:\nMost notably, Dire wolves always travel in packs. Seldom will you find them on their lonesome. They are fiercely protective of their young. In combat A direwolf will take advantage of combat in number, using powerful hind legs and jaws to rip\nlimbs from your body, the size of it's body provides massive force for ramming, additionally.", ""),
        StaticBook("Directive 1", "Zahrer Irongrinder", "Directive 1\n           -_-\nArrival to Atlas\n           -_-\nIt is hereby ordered that the remnant of Urguani forces shall reconvene atop the hill south of Sutican claimed lands and establish a new settlement in which they shall live.", ""),
        StaticBook("Directive 10", "Zahrer Irongrinder", "Directive 10\n           -_-\n21st of Sun's Smile, 1664\n           -_-\nA diplomat shall be dispatched to the Republic of Holm to treat with the Ironguts in pursuit of an industrial agreement.", ""),
        StaticBook("Directive 11", "Zahrer Irongrinder", "Directive 11\n           -_-\n22nd of Sun's Smile, 1664\n           -_-\nA meeting shall be held with Irongut leadership to establish terms for the population's move to Holm's city.", ""),
        StaticBook("Directive 13", "Zahrer Irongrinder", "Directive 13\n           -_-\n*The date is blacked out.*\n           -_-\nIt is hereby ordered that [][][][][][][][][] shall be [][][][][][] in the name [][][][][][] to preserve runesmithing and prevent the [][][][][][][][][][][][][].", ""),
        StaticBook("Directive 18", "Zahrer Irongrinder", "Fuhrer Directive 18\n         -_-\n20th Malin's Welcome\n       1688\n         -_-\n Zahrer Irongrinder has ordered that the Az'Adar wall that was built for Fuhrer Directive  17 be rebuilt after it was destroyed.\nThe Directive also orders the removal of the large orange apples inside the Az'Adar compound.\n\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Directive 2", "Zahrer Irongrinder", "Directive 2\n           -_-\nArrival to Atlas\n           -_-\nIt is hereby ordered that the previous occupant of the land claimed as \"Az'adar\" shall be conscripted into the new state's service or expelled forthwith.", ""),
        StaticBook("Directive 3", "Zahrer Irongrinder", "Directive 3\n           -_-\nArrival to Atlas\n           -_-\nIt is hereby ordered that the first construction in the newly claimed land shall be the castle based on the old designs of previous victorious strongholds such as Hiebenhall.", ""),
        StaticBook("Directive 4", "Zahrer Irongrinder", "Directive 4\n           -_-\n8th of Sun's Smile, 1661\n           -_-\nIt is ordered that the city of Az'adar shall be reinvigorated with industry. This shall begin with the formation of the worker's guild.", ""),
        StaticBook("Directive 5", "Zahrer Irongrinder", "Directive 5\n           -_-\n23rd of Sun's Smile, 1661\n           -_-\nThe worker's guild is hereby instructed to create a machine for the purpose of automatic slaughter of bovine beings in the name of INDUSTREH.", ""),
        StaticBook("Directive 6", "Zahrer Irongrinder", "Directive 6\n           -_-\n30th of Sun's Smile, 1662\n           -_-\nThe armed forces of Az'adar shall be dispatched to secure the borders of the peninsula the city resides on. This shall begin with the purchase of the fort to the south.", ""),
        StaticBook("Directive 7", "Zahrer Irongrinder", "Directive 7\n           -_-\n12th of The Deep Cold, 1663\n           -_-\nThe forces of Az'adar shall be dispatched to finish off the threat of slimey creatures brought on by the druids attempted interference in our glorious INDUSTREH.", ""),
        StaticBook("Directive 8", "Zahrer Irongrinder", "Directive 8\n           -_-\n17th of Malin's Welcome, 1663\n           -_-\nTo extend the protection of the Arch-Runelord, the Az'Arkammar shall henceforth be established with the purpose of preserving the goals of Az'adar.", ""),
        StaticBook("Directive 9", "Zahrer Irongrinder", "Directive 9\n           -_-\n15th of Sun's Smile 1664\n           -_-\nUnapproved members of the Order of the Ascended shall henceforth be banned from the city of Az'adar.", ""),
        StaticBook("Discarded Book", "Tepah", "*The first few pages would seem to be random scribbles and small tears in the paper*\n\n*A sketch of Wyvurn over some elves is seen here. Strangly the face of Wyvrun seems to convey anger.*\n*This next sketch  would show an elf appearign to walk away from Wyvurn, shakey handwritting is under it \"My Rebirth\"*\n*this appears to be the last page with anythign written in the thin journal, sketches of animals would be here, lions, moose, bear, some sort of insect, However the image in the bottom right would be what looks like a Cave*", ""),
        StaticBook("Document #1", "Owynn Iron-Forge", "Owynn Iron-Forge, hereby referred to as the signee, on signing this legal document, promises a lump sum of 4000 mina to be paid out in the month of Sun's Smile, 1542, and promises another lump sum of 1600 mina to be paid out later within the Elvish Month.\nIf the signee does not comply within the legal span of time, or if Lexa and Nemir, referred to as the owners, choose to alleviate the deal, all rights of the tavern, as well as any brought in income, shall return to the owners. In the event that the\nowners decide to refuse the agreed upon amount, the signee will be refunded the amount of money that they have paid. In the event that the signee decides to renig the deal, none of the money that was originally paid to the owners will be refunded.\nSection for Wealth Distribution\nThe original lump sum of 4000 mina provided to the owners will be distributed equally into their respective banks, as well as the 1600 mina secondary payment. If either party attempts economic subterfuge, all assets given\nvia this contract will be returned to the other respective owner. Notorized, John the Friendly, Financial and Legal Advisor to Blackwood Industries.", ""),
        StaticBook("Donation Log", "Tajo S. Torto", "Tajo S. Torto donated the Captains Log, November, Healing, Nothing, The Kal'Varak, and The Story.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dossier: Avendal", "SISTER THEODORUS", "VAEYL DOSSIER\n----------------------\n\nNAME: Avendal\nRACE: Smoke Drake\nALIASES: King of Smoke and Fire\nDESCRIPTION: Chaos-Destruction \"deity\" that warred with the Dragon Tharax for control of Atlas, starting in the year 105\nterminating with his imprisonment in 202. Last of the Smoke Drakes, and particularly deadly. \nLOCATION: \n202-1650: Facility Four, Dragontomb Temple\n1650-: Unknown.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dossier: Tharax", "SISTER THEODORUS", "VAEYL DOSSIER\n----------------------\n\nNAME: Tharax\nRace: Dragon\nALIASES: Shield of Atlas\nDESCRIPTION: Dragon that inhabited Atlas in the 1st, 2nd and 3rd Centuries, renowned by religious followers as a deity of safety, protection and\norder. Warred against the Smoke Drake Avendal for control of Atlas, ending with the imprisonment of the latter in the year 202.\nLOCATION: Yatl Wasteland [Consult TITAN for guidance]", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragaars", "Laelia", "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ Dragaars & Drakaars\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~There are two species of dragonkin known to have descended from Dragur, though corrupted and defiled forms of both have formerly existed. Dragur, the Daemon of Knowledge, oftentimes appears as a dragon\nin his true form. Dragur’s chief descendants, the Dragaar, are sentient “greater dragons” that seek to collect and share knowledge with mortals. They can conceal themselves under the guise of mortals and other creatures,\nthough it is a rare occasion to meet a Dragaar in person. Dragons, on the other hand, are more common -- though proportionately rare compared to other living beings -- than greater dragons. They are generally referred to as dragons, Though a rare\noccasion, dragons have been known to alter their very nature into a twisted, foul portrayal consumed by hatred and rage for the mortal races. The outcome of this calamity is referred to as a drake. . Little is known about the purpose of the dragonkin\ndragonkin as a whole, except that each species’ intentions vary greatly. \n\nDragaar\nBestowed with the gift of immortality and sentience, the Dragaar exist chiefly to seek and gather knowledge.  Each Dragaar is assigned\nthe role of gathering a distinct aspect of knowledge, and this role defines their characteristics and demeanor. However, they do not solely desire knowledge and wisdom. The greater dragons, or Dragaar, act as ever watching wardens over the mortal races.\nHowever, most prefer to live in seclusion in deep thought and meditation, only to emerge when the races call upon them in their time of need. The Dragaar can and often disguise themselves under the guise of a mortal or creature. This is the preferred\nof watching over mortals, as it is both subtle and inconspicuous. There are only two Dragaar that have revealed themselves to the mortal races, and the decision to do so was not lightly concluded.\nThough the Dragaar seek to protect the mortal races,\nthey often decide to do so by living in secrecy. Many discern that if they chose to associate themselves with mortal affairs too frequently, dire consequences would arise. The primary concern held by Dragaar, in regards to involvement\nin the matters of mortals, is that the races would eventually resort to relying on them to protect mortals from any form of evil. However, the greater dragons aspire to teach the mortal races self-preservation,\nwithout them depending on the intervention of immortals.  \n\nDrakaar\n------------------\nTo attempt to bend the will of a Dragaar would be all for naught, and thus what can cause a Dragaar to devolve itself into a twisted abomination of\nhatred is unknown. The ancient ancestors of the four mortal races once believed that the choice for this horrendous transformation to occur was their own, though the aftermath of such a decision would contradict their entrusted duty.\nThe greater dragon itself is a terrifying opponent, but a Dragaar that feels no remorse and fears no consequence? That is the true fear of corruption; the perversion of the mind and distortion of one’s morality is a dreadful circumstance.  In past times,\nthe outcome of such an event would often be referred to as a “greater drake.” It is the combination of a Dragaar’s sentience and a drake’s all-consuming hatred. The likelihood of a Dragaar devolving into a being tormented by rage is next to none,\nas most would, in their right mind, turn themselves into stone to prevent the conversion. The only verifiable event recorded of a Dragaar turning to stone is that of Velketzar. The Guardian Velketzar, consumed by self-condemnation and despair\ndue to his failure, dramatically transformed into a stone statue to prevent the inevitable calamity. If a Dragaar were to fall under the hand of corruption, it would hold the power to politically corrupt nations with ease. Additionally, detecting and\npursuing such a foe would be toilsome, all due to its shape shifting ability. Fortunately, deep meditation and concentration can inhibit this rare occurrence, along with immersing themselves in their aspect of knowledge.\n((Work Transcribed from LOTC Wiki: Dragaars, retrieved from: https://wikia.lordofthecraft.net/index.php?title=Dragaars))", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragon Princess", "Niera Acal'elor", "Once upon a time, in a kingdom far far away, there was a king and queen who lived in a golden castle with their beautiful daughter. They lived in peace and prosperity, and never knew heartbreak or want.\nYet one night, an ugly orc captured the princess and carried her away, locking her up in a tall, dark tower. \n\nThe king and queen were struck with immeasurable grief and promised the princess's hand to any knight who could rescure thier child.\nSo the knights in the land assembled, wanting to bring the princess back to be their bride. \n\nThe Orc roared in anger when he saw the approaching knights. And one by one, he tore them to shreds at the foot of the tower.\nThe princess looked on in horror as her rescuers were slewn. She shrunk back into the confines of her room, weeping as she thought of her fate. \n\nYet someone heard her cries...\nhe princess was awakened by the sound of thunderous wings, flapping in the moonlit sky. A large Dragon, with obsidian scales clung to the side of the dragon, baring his large teeth at the orc.\nThe creature took a deep breath, and in one burst of flame, turned the orc to ash. \nThe dragon then turned his attention to the princess, prying apart the bars that held her in the tower\nShe carefully climbed upon the dragon’s back, and the dragon beat his wings once more, bringing her up into the clouds. \nThe dragon returned the princess to the king and queen, and they were in awe at such a marvelous creature.\nYet, how could they keep their promise? How could a dragon wed their daughter? When asked this, the dragon started to transform in a blinding light, until all that remained was a handsome prince in his place.\nThe princess looked upon her savior, and the dragon took her to be his loving wife. \n\n\n\nThey both lived happily ever after. The end.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragur", "Orithur", "The Daemon known as Dragur is quite easily the daemon most shrouded in mystery. For you see, Dragur one day vanished from all planes and realities, he went missing, or went into hiding many years ago and has made no effort to make himself known since.\nDragur is commonly referred to as the Daemon of knowledge and the father of all dragon-kind - both greater and lesser Dragonkin are children of the Daemon Dragur. Dragur himself was known to appear as a dragon in the distant days when he apparently\nexisted. So little is known about Dragur, and in that there is a unique irony, how the Daemon of all knowledge is so shrouded from it himself. There exist several theories on the fate of Dragur, one being that Dragur has been imprisoned by another Aengul\nor Daemon for a reason unknown, perhaps as a means of leeching power, or perhaps in punishment for the creation of the Dragonkin on the world. If this were the case, it is likely that the Aengul responsible would be Xan, the Aengul of Guardianship, and\nenemy to Dragonkin. Another theory is that Dragur has seen so much of the present, past and future that he grow fearful of how easily his own knowledge of it could change the future for the worst, and instead decided to remove himself from the world as an\nact to preserve it. The final theory is that Dragur ascended behond that of a Daemon, after being so knowledgeable on the world that there was nothing left to be known. Some believe he may have reached another state of being, and transcended reality.\nBut as for what we do know: He does, or did once exist. His dragons are evidence enough, and no other Aengul or Daemon has claimed ownership of his creation. As well as this, it has been noted in the past that as libraries begin to expand and grow, blue\nwisps, wisps of Dragur, have been seen to congregate. They are reclusive, as if they do not wish to be seen. As author of this edition on Dragur, I have seen the wisps myself in a large underground library in Athera. But when the library was destroyed,\nthe wisps vanished. Perhaps they are not even related to Dragur, but the thought still remains that they are his spies, watching the congregation of knowledge from the shadows for reasons still unknown.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragur Books", "Aeran", "Books the Dragur Library does not have:\n\n-Filtration mask\n-Close but far\n-De Shroom Guide\n-Letter Of Marrow\n-Mana Gem Research\n-Boogie Man Letter\n-Tend'el's Journal\n-Elephant Inn\n-A Time Before\n-An Orphan\n-Wise Sayings\n-Zei Grei\n-Malinor's Fall\n-A Dangerous Art\n-Opinion On Truth\n-Gardening Guide\n-Mysterious Badge\n-Saren's Journal\n-On Pigmen\n-Seeds Of Laurelin\n-Notes On Inwe", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragur's Brood", "Thurak'Yar", "Dragur's Brood\n\nAnd one of the few stories known of them.\n\n\n\nRe-Scribed by the Farseer Thurak, 21'st of The First Seed, 1489.\nThe Dragons all descended from Dragur, an Arch-Daemon of the land named Asulon. Dragur’s true form is that of a dragon, so the appearance of his offspring is of no surprise. Dragur raised the first of his brood in his volcanic lair, and taught them\nvast knowledge and wisdom. Like their father, the dragons are capable of morphing into a humanoid shape. The majority of the brood are wise and indifferent to mortals, sometimes posing as scholars or mages; spending their time distributing their\nknowledge of the realms with the races of this world. However, a certain sect of Dragur’s offspring exists, known as Drakes. The scales of these drakes have turned to a shade back as night. These Drakes, unlike their brothers the Dragons, are heavily\nopposed to mortals, sometimes spending time in humanoid form purely to destroy them or to spread corruption in hopes of turning them against each other.\nAfter the creation of his brood, Dragur fell into a deep slumber within the volcano, and\nhas yet to be awakened. In spite of this, the dragons are overseen by a Matriarch, or \"Queen\".\nAs the brood grew, they began to scatter across the land, some going off into the mainlands, or even farther into the opposite ends of the world. Some stayed close to their birth home, such as the Matriarch as well as Velketzar. Velketzar was the first\nborn male of the brood. While Xandraza was born with the mind of Dragur, the yearning for knowledge and learning, Velketzar was born with the strength, pride, and sense of wanting to protect. This Dragon worked closely with the past civilizations\nof Asulon, ensuring that peace was kepy between them and that they prospered. In his humanoid form he was known and respected greatly across the lands. Always possessing an astounding amount of patience, he thought things through\nfor the best possible outcomes.\n\n*The shade of ink turns from old to fresh, at the start of a new paragraph. It seems to be a new entry*\nHowever, as much as he wanted it to, no everything could stay in the peaceful serenity he so desperately worked for… There was just some hate in the hearts of beings that one could never come to change, for Velketzar, he felt pity\nupon these. Few of the brood saw how he aided these creature, as they were so far beneath them, and while some attempted to understand, others simply refused to care at all, and shunned him for his passion. But alas, it wasn't simply his own kind\nthat acted in such a manner. The humanoids he helped, some sought greed over all, and despite how much they already had in this world, nothing satisfied their thirst for gaining more wealth of power… Thus lead to the day of betrayal.\nThe day when some of us cast aside the trust of us and stole knowledge for their own personal gains came too soon. After that day, Xandraza and Velketzar sought out what they could together but could only find so much. Velketzar’s pride\nhad been dealt a heavy blow. He was born with the sense of urge to protect, and he felt he had failed to aid Xandraza in the protection of her vast collection of scrolls and books. Depression fell upon him greatly; he stopped visiting the civilians, and\nalthough she tried her best to console him and tell him that, indeed, in time, together they would perhaps be able to recover that which was stolen, Xandraza’s words would not reach him. His emotions slowly began to consume him.\nOne day after Xandraza returned to the island, filled with happiness after reclaiming another book in ruins, her eyes befell Velketzar and her heart sank. Once a bright healthy ruby shade of red, his scales had begun to dull in colour, and had saturated\nnearly to a dank brow. Bringing him outside so he could see for himself in the light of the sun, Velketzar finally understood what he was becoming. His head grew clouded with his emotions, as Dragons, it is known, have the strongest emotions\nof all creatures. Sadness and rage overtook him, and blinded by this the urge to halting his protection against corruption grew. And then he stopped, and began to think. Pondering on the best possible outcome, as he always did...\nAnd so Velketzar changed into his true form, and with determined rage, he destroyed the mountain on the east side of that island that was their home. For what reason? It didn’t occur to Xandraza what he was doing before it was too late. He was making\na clearing for himself. Once he had enough space, he stood at the edge of the island, looking out to sea. And then it began. First, his claws, spikes and horns began to harden and turn to stone, then his wings, arms and legs went next... All turning\nto rock. He did this to himself… But why? \"Do not think ill of me.\" He said to Xandraza who watched, mortified and as still as the stone he was becoming. \"I do not wish to become one of them. I wish to stay in the good of your heart. I will guard\nthis island so that what has happened may never happen again, and I hope in time, my scales will return to that shine and hue you love so dearly. Goodbye.\"\nAnd as the final whip of his tail slammed into the side of the volcano, it too then turned to stone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dreadknights", "An Elder Cleric", "A Guide To\n      Dreadknights\n\n\n            By\n     An Elder Cleric\nIntroduction\n\nA bitterly cold night, naught but you alone in the road as you hurry along to your home. \n\nA distant clank of armour, a groan of inconcievable agony...\n\nAnd the loud screech of steel being drawn.\nIntroduction\n\nDear Reader, a Dreadknight is one of the most fearsome of the tainted that the Ruinous Powers has to offer. Fear not, for should you read through this book, you shall learn how to effectively identify and dispatch the abberants!\nIdentifying\n\nNoticing a Dreadknight is rather easy compared to other dark creatures. They are collosal in size, reaching the size of orcs and ologs, but are hollow beings of metal. They carry large weapons, as if living suits of armor.\nIdentifying\n\nAside from the physical form of the Dreadknight, the being would have limited social capabilities. Their emotions are rather focused on anger and rage, becoming easy to spark combat and violence.\nStrengths\n\nAs stated, the Dreadknight's size and strength can easily reach that of an Olog, while coming close to that of a Golem. Due to this, they are resistant to attacks and are difficult to take down in a fight.\nStrengths\n\nUnlike mortals within armor, this being is resistant to most magical attacks and does not tire nor hunger. It is a metal monstrosity that is hell-bent on slaying mortals.\nWeaknesses\n\nWhile their giant size is an enormous advantage, it also hinders their movement. Be swift on your feet and constantly moving to avoid their grasp. They have shown no affinity to magic, making ranged attacks preferable.\nWeaknesses\n\nLike nearly all dark creatures, they are weak against Holy Magics. And because they are a metal suit of armour, blunt weaponry serves best to break down their body. Should you destroy the runes within the suit, it will be 'killed'.\nTemperment\n\nAs mentioned, the Dreadknights hold little emotion besides the need for bloodlust and violence. They are quick to anger, favoring it over any other emotion, and have little control over their violent tendencies.\nConclusion\n\nProducts of dark magic, these creatures are dark knights that need to be confronted with care. One can easily slaw an unprepared group. Blessed crossbow bolts work wonders to penetrate the metal armor.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dreams of Lilies", "Lithaeril", "May you dream the dreams of Lilies, where all your worries cease. Whilst you sleep the sleep of the oak tree full of love, contentment, and peace. Braids of vines tumble from the hair of the ancient walls. Flowers sprout in fertile places whilst the\nliving pnod look like friendly faces. The singing sound of the stream rolling over the stones. Beauty in the way the butterfly flutters. The soaring of the great eagle sailing on the great blue waves of the sky. Weaving through the white peaks and the\nhorse galloping through amber waves of grain. Natures music the whistle of the wind, the rustle of the branches, the hoot of the owl, the river rolling. May you dream the dreams of Lilies,\nwhere all your\nworries cease. Whilst you sleep the sleep\nof\nthe oak tree, full of love, contentment and peace.", ""),
        StaticBook("Drink Menu", "Rolien Vulnear", "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~      THE  BEAR  CREEK\n        TAVERN  MENU\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n~~~~~~~DRINKS~~~~~~~~\n\n             ~MEAD~\n(regular) Curonian Standard           -Cost 5 mina-\n   (premum) BlackBear\n       Reserve C.1684\n          -Cost 10 mina-\n~Rum~\n       SunBloom Rum\n        -Cost 10 mina-\n\n       Black Rose Rum\n         -Cost 6 Mina-\n~Wine~\n(Luxury) Curonian Elderflower Reserve c. 1684            -Cost 50 mina-\n\n(Premium) Curonian\n Cherry Wine\n       -Cost 20 mina-\n\n(regular) Bear Creek\nred wine\n            -Cost 8 Mina-\n(regular) Bear Creek\nWhite Wine\n       -Cost 8 mina-\n~Whiskey~\nFalkenrath Royal Mark\n    C. 1684\n           -Cost 8 Mina-\n~Tea & Juice~\nAutumn Spiece Black tea\n     -Cost 5 mina-\n\nFresh blueberry Juice \n    -Cost 3 mina-\n\nFresh Cherry juice\n    -Cost 3 mina-\n\nFresh peach Juice\n    -Cost 3 mina-", ""),
        StaticBook("Drinking Songs", "Quinry Lumberseed", "Chapter One\n       Drinking Songs\n\n1) To the Bottle\n\nHo! Ho! Ho! To the bottle I go\nTo heal my heart and drown my woe.\nRain may fall and wind may blow,\nand many miles be still to go,\nSweet is the sound of the >\npouring rain\nand the stream that falls from hill to plain,\nBut better than rain or rippling brook,\nIs a mug of beer inside this Took!\nLets Get Drunk Tonite\n\nGive us a pint\nI'll pay for this round\nand do it without a fight\nComes the sun, I'm out ward bound\nSo let's get drunk tonite!\nLet's get drunk tonite!\n\nThe time has come to leave the shire and roam the wide world green\nI've heard the tales of broader dales\nand things I've never seen.\n\nI have no taste for farming life-\nI leave that to my brother-\nI want to roam far from my home, and maybe find another!\n\nI want to see the Cities of Men that rise up to the sky,\nand see the dells where woodelves dwell\nand give dwarf beer a try!\n\nI was not made for hearth and home,\nI've known this from my youth.\nI've a restless soul with no fixed goal\nIf you wanna know the truth\n      ->\nSo let's all drink till we are drunk\nlet beer flow like a fountain-\nI'll soon be gone- a traveling on,\no'er hill and dale and mountain!\nBreakfast\n\nSausages that sizzle,\nBread all toasted brown,\nScrambled eggs and bacon,\nPancakes battered 'round.\nPorridge in a kettle\nCapers, honey, tea-\nThat's a hobbit's breakfast\n-A Halfling said to me.\n\n\"Berries dropped in syrup,\nmuffins nice and hot,\ncubes of seasoned 'taters,\nsure do hit the spot...\nSweetened cream for dipping,\nmushrooms, truffles, beer-\nThat would make this morning\nthe best I've had all year!\"\n\n\"Fried up green tomaters,\nDonuts -holed or not -\nDeviled eggs with mustard...\nWhat else have I forgot...?\"\nHe tapped his foot a-thinkin'\nFinger to his chin-\n\"Oh, that will do for breakfast, \nthen Elevensies start again!\"\nA Well Dressed Hobbit\n\nA well-dressed hobbit braids his toes,\nBecause it is the fashion oh!\nA well-dressed hobbit braids his toes,\nTo go down to the pub y'know.\n\nAnd then he puts on his best trews,\nbecause it is the fashion oh!\nWith his best trews and braided toes,\nto go down to the pub y'know.\n\nHe fastens up his braces tight\nTh make sure that his trews hang right,\nbraces tight, his best trews, braided toes,\nto go down to the pub y'know.\nNext he fastens up his shirt,\nwith buttons sewn by Granny Gert,\nShirt, braces tight, his best trews, and braided toes\nto go down to the pub y'know.\n\nNext he tops it with a vest-\nwhich pulls real tight across his chest-\nvest, his shirt\nbraces tight, his best trews, and braided toes,\nto go down to the pub y'know.\n\nAnd in one pocket watch and chain\nSo he'll know to come home again\nWatch, vest, shirt, braces tight, his best trews, and braided toes\nto go down to the pub y'know.\nIn the other pocket his pipe goes\nto make the smoke rings that he blows,\npipe, watch, vest, shirt, braces tight, his best trews, and braided toes\nto go down to the pub y'know\n\nAnd with his pipe he has long leaf\n'cause no tobacco leads to grief...\nLong leaf, pipe, watch, vest, shirt, braces, trews, braided toes\nto go down to the pub y'know\n\nand over all he wears a coat\nto make sure his coture is haute...\nCoat, vest, long leaf, pipe, watch, vest, shirt, braces, trews, braided toes\nto go down to the\npub y'know.\n\nand last he often adds a hat\nso his hair stays nice and flat\nHat, coat, long leaf, pipe, watch, vest, shirt, braces, trews, and brained toes\nto go down to the pub y'know.\n\nIn one hand he totes a mug\nthe better for his ale to glug...\nMug, hat, coat, long leaf, pipe, watch, vest, shirt, braces, trews, and braided toes\nto go down to the pub y'know.\n\nAnd finally his walking stick\nto keep his footing on the brick\nstick, mug hat, coat, long leaf, pipe, watch, vest, shirt, braces, trews,\nand braided toes,\nto go down to the pub y'know!\n(feel free to add other verses or subtract some as the performer sees fit)\nEverybody Needs a Drinking Song\n\nEverybody needs a drinking song\neverybody needs a carol-\neverybody needs a drinking song, \nso tap another barrel!\n\nSome like to drink the whole night long\nsome like to drink like fishes\nSome like to drink the whole night long\nSo best bring in more dishes!\n\nSome like to munch on mushroom pie\nSome like to eat stewed rabbits-\nsome like to munch on mushroom pie,\nso hone your cooking habbits!\nSome like to smoke Old Toby Leaf\nsome like to smoke a pipe\nSome like to smoke Olf Toby Leaf\nSo don't let's hear your gripe!\n\nSome like to dress in their best clothes\nsome like to dress real fine\nSome like to dress in their best clothes\nSo show me yours,\nI'll show you mine...\n\nSome like to sing along with me\nSome like to sing quite cheery\nSomee like to sing along with me\nSo let's make this one \"Beery!\"\n\nSome like to drink the whole night long\nSome like to drink all night\nSome like to drink the whole night ling\nSo lets do it up right!\nRaise a Glass in Parting\n\nThe time will come for leaving...\nI know you cannot stay\nBut later for the grieving...\nYou're here with me today.\n\nI'd rather tend my garden\nThan wander down the road\nAnd so, I beg your pardon,\nI will not share your load.\nParting is sweet sorrow-\nOr so the ballads say...\nBut that is for tomorrow,\nWhen you go on your way.\n\nI'll share with you my finest wine\nAnd mushrooms from the glen\nThe last time that we two shall dine\nTill you come back again.\nI hope it brings you pleasure-\nWhatever 'tis you lack...\nBut for me the greatest treasure\nWill be seeing you come back.\n\nSo raise a glass in parting,\nbut grant me just one boon-\nAlthough your trips just starting,\nSay it will be ending soon.\nElves\n\nI've friends in most the races now,\nHalflings, Dwarvews, and Men.\nand-with them all- as I recall\nI can share a smoke or grin.\n\nBut there's one group of Beings\nI can't quite figurew out...\nI always make a fool of me,\nwhenever Elves about.\n\nIt's not that they're unfriendly-\nThough they treat me like a child\nThey're just so Otherworldly-\nDistant, free, and wild!\n\nThey tower there above me\nLike moonlight come to skin\nTheir eyes glitt'ring like\ndiamonds,\nso pale, cold, and thin...\n\nThey whisper jokes in Elvish\nand laugh over my head\nThey make me feel so foolish\nI wish that I were dead...\n\nBut when it comes to courage\nNo finer can be found\nAnd they're the best\nbeside you\nwhen trouble's sniffing round.\n\nYes, friends among the Elf Lords\nis quite a wondrous treat\nBut I'd rather be a Halfling\nfrom head to furry feet!", ""),
        StaticBook("Drug-Recipes", "Thorvn Bronwyn", "CactusGreen+Grass=\n\nCactus Green.\n\nCoal, Fern Ink Cactus-green= BlackCactus\n\nQuartz, Cocoabeans, Fern, Glowstone dust= Pure Quartz\nBlue Orchid, Cactus green, light blue dye, Fern= Blueberry Cactus.\n\nGrass, Fern, Vine.=\n\nEternal Leaf.\n\nSnowball, Allium, Vine,\n\nIce-Kiss\nMushroom Stew, Cactus green, Fern.\n\n= Baby's Brain", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid History", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "The History\n   of the Druids\n\n      by N. Evitan\nLong ago, two factions of mages fought each other to the bloody end. Good, evil, the sides mattered not, their battle devastated whole cities and forests. At this, the peak of the battle, the first dream came to a young elven girl. She began gathering\nothers around her, teaching the Druidic ways. The first druids were born from the humble beginning. Like a great wave, the young order swept across the land and surrounded the two guilds. The druids destroyed them, turning them all to mere rodents and\nanimals of the forest. The druids went on to preserve the land for a millennia afterwards.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druid of Clouds", "Broll", "Broll stewed up a rumbling grunt as he meditated on the perfect set of words, but of no avail did they come. The tempo of the forest sucked in his frame more than the book, which had many chants and tunes;\nto name them all would be like reproducing the alphabet many times. He was a sentimental and mushy character, currently residing by the tree he bonded with. Broll ingrained letters sprucely into the tome, that lays untroubled in his lap.\n“I remember the day like the back of my palm, I say that in the utmost honesty. It was the day when Druid of Song and I collided worlds, met each other, and forged a bond as teacher and student. Druid of Song is and was good teacher-- like a father.\nThe two of us bonded that day, a sign of the aspects I bet, but it wasn’t about powers or seeping into the knowledge of the aspects.. I mean, don’t get me wrong, I’m the next guy who wanted it to play a part in my life, though I didn’t let it\nconsume me like a flame. Instead of worrying about all of that, I looked for a quality time, going on quest and adventures.”\nHe etched the quilt a more curvy and harsher into the paper, tears soaring through the air below his eyes.\n“The true virtue I’ve received is a mentor and times to reflect on as the good old days. For that I will always be thankful to Druid of Song. He taught me many new sensations, like a fairy ring. This is something you should experience yourself, for sure.\"\nA whole new world around me I’ve never seen before! Still, I know my true vision lies within serving the aspects. . All I can do is serve them and the realm, preserve order, and heal the shards broken by voidslingers for the aspects.”", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic II", "Lion Druid Lavondir", "When the September Prince arrived in Atlas, the land was already scarred by conflict, and was in the throes of a war. The land's most defining feature was, in its south, a colossal wall, that ran across the entire horizon. A large fortress rested at its\nbase, called Lasthope by the natives of the land. It was a military bastion of the Vaeyl empire, which had, until recently, indisputably ruled all of Atlas. These were a deathless people, kept alive by a powerful magic of unknown origin. The other\nkingdoms of the realm had once been marginalized or turned into its vassals, and in older times, its rule was peaceful.\n\nIt was less than a decade ago when the Vaeyl became engulfed in war, that was still ongoing when the prince arrived.\nThere were vast numbers of orcish tribes and raiding bands, which had been pushed north into the desert wastelands at the top of Atlas during the Vaeyl's expansion. There was significant bad blood between them and the Vaeyl, and the orcs had launched a\nmassive attack south, and sacked the Vaeyl's merchant-city of Sevenna.\n\nGreat battles were being regularly fought just north of Yrodholm, the Vaeyl capital in Atlas. The Shirvani and Dahklani adjuncts to the Vaeyl army had all but\nbeen wiped out by the orcs, and the leadership was disorganized by the initial attack. Further weakened by recent popular uprisings, the Vaeyl were unable to coordinate a counterattack into orcish territory, even years later.\nIn addition to the orcs and the Vaeyl, there were also the elves of Lin, who had major holdings in the northwestern forests, including their capital of Linmordu, and the ruined sorcerer-city of Endmoor. Originally a Vaeyl vassal, they had chosen not\nto aid their overlord, citing a lack of support from the Vaeyl when the orcs had made raids into elven territories years prior. The majority of the elvish population held tight to the teachings of the Aspects, and worshipped as demigods the local mani.\nOn a cool morn of the Amber Cold, the September Prince climbed out of the ocean on the Lobster Isles, and began methodically destroying the eastern orcish settlements before his armies had even arrived. By dusk of the first day, every village\nin the Lobster Isles had been reduced to ruins, ridden with roots. Even the mightiest fortresses had been ground into the sea so thoroughly they were almost indistinguishable from the natural rock outcroppings. The great tortoises and sky whales ferrying\nthe beasts and druids who followed him arrived by night, and were the first to witness the carnage. The orcs that remained were either mercifully killed, or transformed into infested sporophytes.\n\nBased on what was left behind, it is clear the\nSeptember Prince took his time killing the orcs. The population of these outer settlements could have been eradicated within an hour's time,  but the prince spent much longer than that, torturing his victims. This was eerily predictive of the rest of his\ncampaign. Every orc settlement in the east was destroyed in much the same way.\n\nOne after the other, villages would be destroyed. Harpies would descend upon them from the sky, while wolves and beastmen attacked from land. Metal armors and weapons\nwere melted down, mixed with pig iron, and the resultant slag cast into the sea. All farm animals were eaten or killed, and the remainder left to rot.\n\nWhen the September Prince arrived at Yrodholm, he utterly destroyed the city,\ncollapsing it deep underground using giant moles. The Vaeyl fled south, rather than choosing to fight him, abandoning their villages and return to Lasthope. They would remain silent for the rest of the war. The orcs attempted to fight, but were quickly\noverwhelmed.\n\nMost of the orcs fled north, back toward the desert from where their expansion had originated. Nearly every orc settlement in Atlas was destroyed, within several weeks. \n\nUltimately, high in the\nGules mountains, the orcs would construct a massive sacrificial pyre one-hundred meters in diameter. A union of shamans of every clan had decided that summoning the spirits would be the only way to fend off the September Prince. Forming a ring around the\npyre, every second orc walked into the flames. This included children and the infirm.\n\nThe spirits of Atlas rose up in anger. Wothol, Votar, Lethag, and at least a half dozen other lesser spirits walked out of the pyre. Skathach even contributed his\nstrongest lesser, who was called Fyrkalor. At the highest mountain in Atlas, they and the orcs would mount a desperate final stand. They did not succeed.\n\nLethag, the greater spirit of storms, had been severely weakened in a recent war for the\ndomain of thunder. While the spirits fought hordes of beasts, the September Prince caught Lethag in a prison of rubberwood, and disemboweled her. This prompted immediate rout by Wothol, which was soon followed by Votar. Left alone, the orcs broke into\ndisarray, and the battle was lost.\n\nSeveral decades later, a lesser spirit of lightning called Neizdark would recover Lethag's power, and ascend to become the new greater spirit of storms.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic III", "Lion Druid Lavondir", "With civilization eradicated in the eastern half of Atlas, the September Prince turned toward the west. This region was mostly occupied by elves, with scattered dwarven trading outposts among them.\n\nInitially, the druids who served the September Prince\nquickly prepared themselves to die. They expected the elves would have rallied the entirety of their armies, and called upon the power of the Word Altars, to defend themselves from the threat which had demolished the orcs. However, they soon found quite\nthe opposite had happened.\n\nThe elves were, in fact, celebrating. They believed that the September Prince had come not as their conqueror, but as their savior. There were days of jubilation after news of the battle in\nthe Gules Mountains. The elves had fought many bloody wars against the orcs in the years past, and were ecstatic that their long-time enemies were vanquished. The prince had done what the Vaeyl could not. In Riurnor, the city-of-the-swamps,\nthey prepared a great festival for the prince. Elven maidens spent sleepless nights weaving together a great wreath they could use to adorn their messiah's neck.\n\nThere was a mass panic when the September Prince arrived, and began wreaking havoc in the\ncity. The revelers died en masse, most of them dragged underground and crushed to death by roots. Their banquet was smeared into the earth. The city was pulled underwater by the mangroves and drowned.\n\nWhen the elves cried out to their Mani gods\nfor aid, they received only silence in return.\n\nIndeed, many of the Mani were drawn to the September Prince, though it is not certain if this was by choice, or because of the powers he wielded. The others left Atlas entirely, or were passivated and kept\nout of the conflict.\n\nThe violet corruption was first found around this time, attacking the soul forests, but it was pushed back before any of the trees fell to it.\n\nNo organized resistance was ever\nmounted in the conquest of the west. The elven cities crumbled, one after another, victim to September's onslaught. Some druids chose to serve the September Prince, and those who did not were hanged, or dismembered and fed to the animals. Elder\ntrees were twisted into mindless, violent horrors, and the great wyverns of the isles turned to powerful beasts of war. The Thorn Knights were conscripted, and forced to pledge loyalty to the prince. Even the arcane ruins of Endmoor, trapped and defended\nby rogue sorcerers, was little more than a roadblock.\n\nIt was only after Linmordu, the elvish capital, was sacked, that the carnage halted. The September Prince disappeared into the woods, partway through ravaging the city.\nFor three long days, there were no sightings of September, not even amongst the druids and beasts who served under him. There had always been rumors of an intersection between the Eternal Forest and the Loftywoods, and there\nwas speak that, deep in the woods, the September Prince had discovered and forced his way inside a portal connecting this world to the Fae.\n\nWhen he was next seen, the prince had begun heading south. He ordered his armies to stay behind,\ndistribute themselves throughout the land, and wait for his return. The druids who served him journeyed deep into the Wonkawood, and began constructing a chamber for the prince's return.\n\nUltimately, the September Prince climbed the great\nsouthern wall, and disappeared for nearly ten years.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic IV", "Lion Druid Lavondir", "When September returned, he was badly wounded. He travelled north into the interior of Atlas, deep inside the Wonkawood, where the druids who served him had been preparing for his return. However, this was not with the triumphant glory they had expected.\nInstead, the September Prince entered with barely a word, and almost immediately, fell into a deep and powerful sleep. It was surmised that, due to the graveness of his wounds, this was a means to accelerate his healing.\n\nHowever, the prince did not wake\nin the days following. As months slipped away, and the seasons began to turn, a crystal of impenetrable amber arose from the prince's blood, and he became sealed within.\n\nHis druids were left to their own devices. Many years passed,\nand the remains of the empires in Atlas crumbled away to nothingness. Strangely, although it was certain some of the druids who had first began to serve the September Prince did so out of fear, none chose to flee his service after he entered the great\nsleep.\n\nSeveral of the druids had recognized an elder tree candidate in the far west, a young sapling that called itself Elestiel, but which bore the inklings of a wisdom much greater. After some arguing, a small group departed to nurture it, and\nalongside them, others also left, choosing to go into hibernation all across Atlas. They would ensure the prince's legacy would live on, even if, for some horrible reason, the druids in the prince's chamber were slaughtered.\n\nThe beasts which had\nformed the September Prince's armies left to spread out across Atlas. The rat-men journeyed south, disappearing into a series of caverns, while the bull-men and bird-men travelled out across all the plains and mountains. Even the great titanic beasts\ndeparted his stead, after the silence grew too long.\n\nHis druids remained at his side. Eventually, they would begin to join him in the sleep.\nAfterword:  I will need to go over this, a lot I still need to adjust. Change wording, as well, I'd rather not have the others clamp down on me for not celebrating our prince enough. I can feel the sleep tingle at the edges of my mind. Hopefully I will be\nable to endure at least one more night, without drifting into hibernation.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidic Records", "Lion Druid Lavondir", "Author's Foreword: I write this now as one of the last waking druids in our prince's service. Some of the others might disapprove of my recording this, since it treads dangerously close to civilized pursuits. However -- this testament is necessary to\npreserve the righteous cause, in whatever form it might remain. It will allow future druids to know the true will of the Aspects, and the nature of our holy mission. Besides, they are all asleep now. I will refrain from including any of the first rumors\nin this record, only beginning with what we absolutely know to be certain: the years following when we entered into our prince’s service, after he conquered the founder's city.\n\nWhen the September Prince arrived at Malin's City, the region had already\nbeen deteriorating for years. Little regular contact was made with the mainland villages, and most of the bureaucratic apparatus that had sustained the elven empire had collapsed. The military had fractured into several smaller armies led by high-ranking\nofficers, with entire legions deserting to become pirates, or leaving for other realms. Many of the seeds and groups which had broken off from the empire following Malin's disappearance had already left Axios entirely.\nMalin's City was, critically, a sea-locked capital. Regular food shipments were vital to its survival. Without the empire to sustain it, even the most stringent rationing eventually failed, forcing starvation and a mass exodus from the city. Ultimately,\nUltimately, the capital was left a ghost of its former grandeur, populated only by those too poor to escape the dying city, or too loyal to the dream of its founder to bare leaving it.\n\nThis produced a state, not only without any information gathering\ntools to watch for external threats, but with a disorganized military unable to mount an effective defense if a threat did arrive.\n\nThe September Prince was, at this point, a recognized menace, having already destroyed several nations in the far\nwest, including those in Morthandria, Elysion, and Ayvas. Yet, the people were caught entirely by surprise when he climbed out of the ocean on the city’s southern end. In the next several hours, tens of thousands were killed. Calls were sent out for aid\nfrom the surrounding villages, but unbeknownst to those in Malin's City, these had already been destroyed by the prince in the weeks prior. The September Prince methodically overran each quarter with sporophytes, plantlife, and armies of beasts.\nWild druids stalked through alleys, exterminating those who put up resistance. The prince called down storms which toppled stonework buildings and lit most of the wooden structures ablaze.\n\nThe surviving citizenry were changed. It is\nnot clear how this took place, but most of their higher faculties were eroded away, and they were transformed into feral elves. The prevailing theories are that a kind of disease was used to achieve this effect, or that it was some function\nof the royal veridian moss.\n\nThe druids of Malin's City were spared from the conflict. Attempts were made to calm the beasts and foliage that were part of the September Prince's army, and to heal those caught in his attack,\nbut little success was found. Many became infected by royal veridian moss, and were impossible to cure. Once the city had been totally destroyed, the prince approached those druids that remained, and made them an offer. He spoke in a strange voice that\ncould be understood in all tongues. \n\nIn exchange for their eternal service, he would spare their lives. They would be allowed to dwell, under him, as his army, which he would use to cross a hundred seas, and wipe out all\ncivilization throughout the entire world.\n\nA great deal of the druids took this offer, swayed by the September Prince's displays of power, fear for their lives, or for some members, belief that he was righteous. However, there\nwere several dissenters, including the archdruids, as well as the heirophants Star Druid Fae'linn and Badger Druid Kor'farr and a number of other druids and dedicants.\n\nRegardless, it is then that the September Prince gave\nhis first order to the druids who had chosen to follow him. They were to execute the druids who refused to join. Before the sun had set, this task was completed. The hanging bodies of the dissenters were left on the mother tree to rot.\nMalin's City was left as a ruin, and abandoned entirely. The city's word altar was entombed, deep underground. The September Prince and his armies began their journey west, toward the realm nearest to Axios, next to be conquered. It was a large land\nconsisting of only a single major continent, called Atlas.", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidism", "Jistuma", "Is this what the druid college is like…? Being idnapped and forced to write books? Er, kidnapped. Not idnapped. They think I’m a druid for some reason… It’s as if they’re brainwashed.\nThey think I’m an elf, too! I’m a damn dwarf! They trapped Bell in here, too. She’s also forced to write. He just said to write..anything. I guess this will be okay to write, maybe…? I’m just jotting down notes… And my thoughts… And why is this\nhappening!? So, what do write now. I don’t even feel like making paragraphs. Hmm. Well, since I last wrote in a journal, Many things have happened. For one, I’ve been indulged in a quest to find an ancient artifact… It’s a magical artifact from\nWinterfall that the undead want. Now it’s in the hands of one named Hwaldar, who hid it. I rea some clues. It’s from the Kar’Lani tribe, and is hidden in the “fake father of Al’Kazaar”. It’s cold there, too. I find the whole quest odd, found by books\nwritten by Hwaldar, who is actually an undead himself, yet HE hid the artifact.\nI’ve been living in Al’Khazaar and Laurelin latly. I left Al’Khazaar because the rulers were stupid and no one even realized it, causing a bad monarchy. I went to Laurelin, where it turns out a friend did too. Nothing much happened for a while.\nBut then, a few days ago, I found some lvers near a pumpkin and was playing around with them, when a druid invited me in his house to give me a book. I accepted, of course. I like books. But when I came in, the druid blocked off the door, and gave me\nenough books to fill my backpack. He commanded me to write and hit me a few times. My friend I mentioned earlier, Bell, was there. The druid was trying to brainwash us or something. He kept on saying we were elven and druids, which neither of us were.\nBell’s human and I’m a dwarf. And I don’t think either of us would want to study druidism after this… Anyways. Thankfully, a guard found it.Er, not it. Us. He tried to break us out, when the druid teleported Bell and I to the treetops on top of his house.\nWe found a way back down, and I hit him a few times. He then ran away. So pretty much, I think I’ll go back to Al’Khazaar… but I’ll write about the next adventure.\nI went to go to Al’Khazaar with Bell after being kidnapped. On the road, we met two men who pleaded for Bell’s help to heal a man named Ademas. We went to follow, but Bell disappeared. I still don’t know where she is. We continued on the path, along with\nan orc shaman who tagged along. Once we got there, the shaman accidentally activated the demon inside him while trying to destroy it. The demon went mad. I wrote about it in a different book. He eventually jumped off a cliff and died.\nA while later, the Oren carnival opened. It was fin at first. I won 100 minas at an archery tournament, and watched others fight in the Fight Pits. The Wizard gave me a fortune. He said I would be either a great protector of good or an evil bandit.\nIt’s obviously a load of crap. But then, something actually happened at the carnival. Undead attacked. A man revealed himself to be undead and lit the place on fire. The king of Al’Khazaar didn’t even notice. He, along with the rest of the human royalty,\nis just STUPID. There’s no other way to put it. Then everyone just continued playing games, even after a few men died. They didn’t even CARE. The people of this world are fools. Maybe the undead do have a point…no. Untrue. Just untrue.\nAnyways, Brum, the first undead I ever met came. Everyone thought he was a pale orc, even thought he’s admitted to be undead many times. The fools… the idiots, the fools… I went to watch one fight. A man that looked very similar to an earlier undead came.\nHe even used the same tequique; He set the ground on fire wherever he walked to kill the opponents. The fools… no one noticed, even when I said it. I am surrounded by oblivious morons. No one understands what is going on…\nI would write more about my life, but I realize I just don’t know who will get this book. I might die and good looted. I mean, get looted. Anyways, I can’t let people know of my feelings or all my thoughts. That’s pretty much all of my life so far that I\ncare to share.\nDruidism\n\nRetold by Leyu’Maehr\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Druidology", "Respiren", "~Druidology~\n\nDruids are the druii, the dryw, the druwid.\n\nNature's sorcerer, the seer, the oak-knower.\n\nFor those that know the oak, the trēow is both the tree and the truth.\nMysterious guardian of a sacred grove, wise counselor to monarchs, cunning master of many shapes, friend of animals, and terrible defender of unspoiled Nature.\nThe Druid revere Nature, wielding power over plants, animals, the weather, and the elements.\nAll druids are of neutral alignment and share an ethos devoted to protecting the wilderness and maintaining natural cycles and a balance between good and evil.\n\n~Scribed by Wayward\nDruid Respiren", ""),
        StaticBook("dsasd", "Thorne'Ugluk", "The Marbrand Debate\n\n8th of Deep Cold\n\n\nBy Nymira Marbrand\nOn a cold evening, a small crevice near the gates of Markev was crowded with children, women, elves, ologs, and humans alike. They gathered here to watch a heated debate between two figures, one of which is quite known around haense.\n\nMany of us have\nmet or heard of the guard, Marius Marbrand. Young, potentially competent, and to some, notably egotistic. A less notable figure in Markev is a street urchin by the name of Nymira Marbrand. The two share names, and eye colours, but very little else. Except\nmaybe the mutual stubbornness.\n\nThe gathering in the alley was inspired by the child and the guard arguing over the right to keep the name. The child, a small, worthless urchin, held the name of a family slowly amassing a humble amount of power.\nMarius, at one point, got so heated he threatened to kill the child if she didn't change her name. Both brought up good points, but Marius was unsuccessful in the end. The main argument was whos ancestry lied, as both claimed the other's great-grandfather\nwas of bastard-birth, and not to carry the name. One notable quote was;\n\nNymira: \"Are you so low and envy-filled that you would strip a helpless child of their identity?\"\n\nMarius: \"Da.\"\nBoth continually insisted the other was wrong, but eventually, reached a stalemate after Marius fell silent, most likely due to the growing mob watching the encounter. Namely an Olog, who identified himself as Durzy, or Durdub, and also the help of\nGrimwold Stafyr and Larry Jr. The result of the episode was the girl keeping her name, Marius uneffected, this article being written, and an impressive crowd at the gates of Markev.\nfuckfuckfuckfuckfuckfuckfuckfuckfuckfuckfuckfuckgufcukfcukfcukfuckfuckfuck", ""),
        StaticBook("DUCAL LETTER", "Ratibor", "Ducal Proclamation\nfrom the Duke Ratibor\n------------------\nAdrians, I will tell you\na little story.\n\nI am a member of a group called the strannikovic tastevin. It is a secret society of Carrion Black™ drinkers.\nEvery 90 days, somewhere in the world, we gather, and we drink Carrion Black™ as old as 1402, but you cannot do it unless you are wearing your tastevin, which is a tasting cup made of pure silver.\nIf the cup is dirty, you're rejected from the meeting, no matter where it is held, could be Carloustadt, could be Abretski. You can't get in. I keep telling my wife, \"You gotta polish my tastevin\", she says \"Polish your own tastevin\".\nI actually think I could polish my tastevin, but I digress. You see, there is a small island in the Aeldenian sea called Malderiki, upon which I own a very large keep. Every year after the first rain, the strannikovic tastevin, of which I am a member,-\ngathers at my keep to watch the island's natives grovel in the mud as their pathetic straw dwellings are ripped apart by the rising waters. On this island there is also a fish, called the Piranha Giganticus.\nCoinciding with the first rain, this fish swims unto the flooded island and begins to feed on the older and weaker natives of Malderiki. Unable to defend themselves from the killer fish and utterly helpless, the natives make-\ntheir way to my keep in makeshift canoes. At this point, the strannikovic tastevin opens a bottle of pre-Ducal War Kraltan Black™, dated no later than 1474, and places wagers on which native will be the first to reach the high ground-\nof my sprawling lawn. Once the fish has fed and returned to the Sea, there are typically a handful of natives left on my lawn, at which point we release the hounds. Last year, during the hound feeding, a tiny spect of native flesh-\nwas flung from the lawn up to the balcony upon which the strannikovic tastevin was gathered and landed on my shoe. I retrieved the piece of flesh, and placed it in my mouth, washing it down with a glass of Vekaro Black™.\nDear Adrians,\nRight Now, YOU are that piece of flesh.\n\n\n\nAs drafted by,\n\nRatibor Rodrigue Alexovic Carrion", ""),
        StaticBook("Dunes Of Time", "Saeed Ibn Malek", "The Dunes Of Time\n------------------- A poem By Saeed Ibn Malek\n-------------------Thru the sands I walk, the dunes always the same yet always different\nMy heart seeks but always turns to the gust of sand that sprays my face and wounding my eyes\nI yearn for the warmth of one I could trust upon my cheek Yet the sun Burns me when the thought arises\nLost I am in thoughts that burn my every being! Tell me, is there a end of this sorrow?\nWill the sky of mine give me a cloud of rain to wash my grief? \nor am I to drift deeper into the sands of sorrow becoming lost to my own desolation!\nTell me! why have the thoughts of happiness hurt me!\nTell me! When will you utter a word and then leave me to my own destruction!\noh why does my mind persecute my heart's yearn and turn everything to the sand that loses me to time!\nTell me...Will I be lost in the dunes of time never to be rescued?\n--------------------------------------\nBy Saeed Ibn Malek\n  (Ibraheemc2000)", ""),
        StaticBook("Dunwood Contract", "Hobbs Burrows", "Petyr's Dunwood Contract\nAs a resident of Dunwood Village, I will respect and aid my neighbours as best I can. I accept my free home, materials, and support from the fellow villagers, and in turn I will aid Dunwood Village as best I can by working my chosen career as shepherd.\nThis includes shearing the sheep, skinning the cows, smokin' tobacco, playin' me lyre while watchin over me flock ((and preventing Animal Farm from occuring)). Working in a different career that belongs to someone else without consent of that person, or\nan Elder, is warrant for eviction if deemed necessary by the Elders of Dunwood. I am aware if the chosen career is not taken by anyone or is not viewed as a career of Dunwood, I am allowed to do that career, however it will not be recognised by the Elders\nof Dunwood as aiding the community. If I do not aid the community to a satisfactory standard, I understand that my home could be given to someone who does. I also understand that baths are important and will take one at least every week. I also agree not\nto build in Dunwood Village without an Elder of Dunwood's permission, and, when allowed, will stick to the Halfling architecture. Same goes for the lake. I am entitle to my personal storage and belongings, but also understand hoarding goods that can or\nshould be used by or for the community is frowned upon and could lead to eviction. Personal items may include, but is not limited to: weapons, trinkets, tools, armour, pictures, objects of sentimental value, and pets. I understand that all halflings that\nare reisdents of Dunwood are required to drink one pint of ale a week. I am aware anything in the community storage of Dunwood Village is not available as a personal item unless otherwise approved by the Elders of Dunwood. Theft, murder, trespassing, and\nblackmailing another villager of Dunwood Village will result in banishment from Dunwood Village and Oren. That includes, but is not limited to bandits, war, Undead, or Orc Raiders. I am not secretly an undead follower, Iblees worshipper, or a spider and\nwill evict myself without causing harm to the villagers of Dunwood Village if I am. The Elders reserve the right to evict, restrict, or banish you from Dunwood Village if it is seen as necessary. I am well within my rights to question any of the Elders in\nmatters that this contract does not cover.\nPetyr Brandybuck.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dunwood Limerick", "Petyr", "Limericks of Dunwood\n  Petyr Brandybuck\n       (drplat)\nThese are a collection of limericks that I've written about Dunwood, meself, me friends, and some other fellas I know! I hope ya enjoy. They can be a bit dirty, and they're always comical, yes!\nNo.1 - A Dunwood halflin' friend o' mine,/When asked how much he did dine,/ Replied, \"Both me breakfasts,/Elevenses, lunch, /Tea, dinner, supper, and wine!\nNo.2 - Ol' Seth did go to the bar,/And met a fine lass from Sanhar,/ And now when I visit/His small halflin' home,/ There be too many half-orcs dar!\nNo.3 - An elf lass whose clothing was strewed,/ By winds that left her quite nude,/ Saw ol' Kip come along,/And unless I am wrong,/ Ya expected this line to be lewd!\nNo.4 - When the Wanderin' Wizard fer sure/ Entered me bar sayin, \"Sir,/ I require all the ales/That ya have fer sale,/ The rest o' this rhyme is censored.\nNo. 5 - Harvestin' crops ain't no fun,/ Nor is plantin' seeds none, yet/ I love me hot bread/ And ale in me head,/ So I'll work all day in the sun.\nNo.6 - Yer the prettiest lass that I've met/ No prettier lass could I get,/ Wow, I must be drinkin',/ If this is what I'm thinkin',/ Fer this beautiful lass is me pet! These rhymes pack laughs astronomical/ In a space that is quite economical!/\nBut the good ones I've seen/ So seldom are clean,/ And the clean ones so seldom are comical!", ""),
        StaticBook("Dunwood Village", "Hobbs Burrows", "The Village of Dunwood\n\nBy Len of Dunwood\n\nTranscribed by Hobbs of Dunshire\nDunwood, village of the Halflings. It is found west of the grand city of Al'Khazar, past the Golden Harvest Headquarters. It is situated between the mountain named Elduren, and the old ruins. It is there that the Halflings can reside in peace,\navoiding the hustle and bustle of the big cities, and having the solitude of the closed gate community. Members of the community all work together, sharing the profits and the fruits of the land. \n\nThe people of Dunwood are very close, they are friendly\nto one another, and are willing to share their findings with the community, storing them in warehouses throughout the village. \n\nThe town itself is a lush, grassy and hilly area. The homes that dot the land are built into the small hills,\nkeeping warmth during the winter and sound dampening, reducing annoyances from neighbours.", ""),
        StaticBook("Duump'Auga", "Eath'Lur", "The Sky Terror\n-------------\nI've met many creatures during my life, I've travelled across the world, always accepting the challenges given by the old and new spirits, still, one of my most terryfing views was the Sky Terror.\nThe sky terror didn't have a name, the orcs named it something I forgot; a yellowed-orange beast that looked like it came out of a fairy tale for grown up people with something weird on their minds.\nHaving the body made of like some sort of scorpion tail, full of spheres, leading down to the bottom, it's two wings give it the extra spice, making it being able to fly.\n\nStill, the weirdest thing of the sky terror is the eye.\nIt has a large head, but nothing on it. A single, blue, round eye. It was it's weak spot, where we killed it.\n\nA honourary ker of my clan landed the killing strike, taking home it's biggest scale, that was used later for a durable shield.\nAkin to the resistance of dragonscales, the shield is now sadly lost on the sands.\n\nWe weren't even searching for this sky terror, I remember it was a beast from a tale to tell the younger ones to go to sleep, I barely even remember it.\nWell, you see, I had rallied a group of orcs to hunt a jabbernack or akin on the desert until we saw such a terryfing beast.\n\nYou won't ever, ever find it again, the beast has been already killed, but history has to be written.\nOh, a name for the sky terror? Well... why don't we call it...\n\nDuump'Auga?", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarfs", "Davin Lodmund", "There is a time when a boy must transition to a man and make his own way in life rather than following in the footsteps of his father. For me, that moment is when I departed from Kal'Urguan and set my sights of Al'Khazar, the capital city of Oren. This\nwas my coming of age: a departure from the lands of my ancestors and to find my own way. I, like many youth, dwarf or otherwise found fulfillment in fighting and became first a guardsman and then later on a mercenary, and like many mercenaries\ntransitioned to becoming a dissolute dunkard, who fought for money to buy drink which would lead to more fighting and then hopefully more drinking. This was my life for decades.\nIt was the death of my father that shook me. from my stupor and made me\npack my bags and return to Urguan to oversee my father's funeral arrangements. It was in this period the world of the descendants was forever shaken by the reemergence of the daemon Iblees. My first taste of true war was at the\nancient human city of Snowy Fields, a place now only known to the eldest living descendants (amongst which I rank) and history books. My fathers dying wish was that I reunite our clan after it's scattering in the aftermath of the blood Age. The\nNether Wars however prevented this from materialising as I devoted my time to more fighting: only this time on behalf all the living against the undead scourge. As anyone who knows the history books will state, we know this ended in failure and I spent\ndecades mourning and drinking after our arrival in Asulon. My dead father appeared to me in a dream and his dying wish was remembered. I was just one of many nameless dwarves at this point and the dwarven peoples were in disarray.\nI packed my bags and headed for Mount Ire, to aid in the construction of the future capital and to hopefully find some of my kinsmen. As anyone who knows the history, Mount Ire was a failure in every sense of the word and under the leadership of the\n\"Paragon\" Kjell, the dwarves fractured into a state similar to how they exist now: divided. With only myself and my cousin Eorlund, we headed to the lands of our more distant kin: the Ironguts and with the aide of Hiebe Irongut we settled in Kal'Dwain\nand begun our resurgence. There are many from this period who I could recall. Great dwarves who are unfortunately forgotten to the history books merely because they never attained the noteriety or infamy of many others\nwhose names appear in these memoirs. I will list a few of those who live on only in my failing memories, but not in those of the Halls of the Remembermancers nor in the memories of those from my era who yet still live: Magna Grimmhall, a friend and\nmentor\nDarius Irongut, a friend and inspiration\nArgon Tunnelsmasher a brother and ally\nEllsia Dawnsworn, a friendly rival\nDominic Irongut, my eternally loyal friend\nGauldrim Irongut my teacher in the arcane And the many others I met and\nbefriended who the centuries of activity I have lived for has rotten from my mind. Mount Ire had of course been sealed, but instead Arbrek Starbreaker, a legendery smith and now also the reformer of the Dwarven faith had taken up\nresidence inside. In my eternal greed, I broke in, to reclaim what I had abandoned inside, which was now property of the Krikja Dverga. I was of course caught and rather humiliatingly at that. But Arbrek, may Yemekar give him rest, bore me no ill will\nand instead took me under his wing. In a short year I came out as a reformed dwarf, no longer a mercenary or petty thief, but as the first priest of Grimdugan to be appointed in centuries. I would serve in this capacity for over a human lifetime. I\nfought in the great Dwarf-Teuton War at this point, especially in our bloody defeat on beaches of Hanseti, being one of the few who escaped the meat grinder alive as human sorcerers employed evil magic to create undead creatures out of thin air to\nassail us and their ships, crewed by ghosts managed to continue firing on us even though they had been sunk hours beforehand. With the end of the war, the three great clans of the time: the Irongut,Grandaxe and Goldhands agreed to reunify\nunder the leadership of the now King Hiebe Irongut and abandon their seperate halls for the ancient and sealed city of Kal'Karik.I of course, went with my people, contuining my responsibilities as both a clan father and priest, but also became a\nbarkeep and opened the first shelter for homeless dwarves in history. In Karik, we achieved stability and prosperity for the dwarves for the first time in almost a century. The perfect opportunity for the ugliness of politics to rear its head. Good King\nHiebe began to (rightfully) suspect the 'paragon' Kjell of subverting his rule.In order to undermine his support Hiebe instigated a long due investigation into the suspicious nature of Kjell's paragonship.\nThis investigation was assigned to me, having\nrecently succeeded to the rank of High Inquisitor of the Kirkja Dverga after my predecessor, Phelrin, had passed on. The investigation was originally quite public, however Kjell made his move first and Hiebe was deposed in a bloodless coup,\nhaving stood aside to prevent bloodshed. However the King did not decide matters of religion and my investigation proceeded, now in secret. I, accompanied by Hiebe and a fellow priest moved onwards to the Powder Grange: the ruins of a\nsurface dwarf village which had been sacked by orcs in a prior war. The evidence we had been searching for of course existed, for the truth was on our side. Hildr Dawnsworn, the priestess who had declared Kjell paragon, had\nbeen blackmailed by Kjell according to her diary and she did not believe him worthy of the honor. In fact, she had planned to build support and strip him of it prior to her suspicious and untimely death. But when we arrived in Karik, the coup had taken\nplace. To prevent bloodshed on the streets, the evidence was buried (remaining in my hands to this day) with Hiebe stepping down as king and the Lord's Council holding regency until a new King could be elected. This event shook my trust in\nthe dwarven political system and I became something of a recluse during the Fall of Asulon. It was when we arrived in the land of Anthos I returned to public life. I resumed my post as a bishop of the Brathmordakin and through much struggle managed\nto attain the rank of Archbishop of Kal'Azgoth. The highest rank in the Kirkja Dverga. It was then I made the ultimate discovery: how to turn mere stone into any metal. I used my immense advantage to combat the entire Oreni empire\neconomically. I was the second wealthiest being in all Anthos, behind my future friend Tuvya Goldman. The only reason I was not the wealthiest was simply because I did not exploit it to the levels I could have. While this was occuring I used brute\nforce to push reform through the Kirkja Dverga, which unfortunately collapsed in the next episode in my life The secret to my alchemy was a powder I had discovered in the tunnels beneath Azgoth. While I was drinking Gorum Frostbeard\nmanaged to learn the secret to my wealth and he, alongwith some of his kinsmen began exploiting this powder too. This rapidly depleted the supply of the powder and very soon we reached the ends of the supply. Because of this, the four of us, the three\nFrostbeards and myself embarked on a long sea voyage to find more for the betterment of all dwarvenkind while the tensions with Oren rose. A journey which took me thirty-five years as we split up midway through to cover more ground. I\narrived back to a very different Urguan to the one I had left behind. I had been sidelined in the clergy, my once considerable assets seized and Urguan buckled under an increasingly tyrannical king in the form of King Thorin Grandaxe, who by\nthis point had already subjugated the squabbaling human kingdoms that had formed since the disintegration of the Oreni empire. I became associated with a seperatist movement of dwarves who had grown dissatisfied with the constant warring\nthat Thorin has wrought. I quickly took control of the movement, which mostly consisted of cave and surface dwarves. I had been appointed as Yemekar's Pick (the economic advisor to the King) and used this position to not only improve the\nlot of many dwarves but also to cover for my compatriots moves in seperatism. As we assembled a new city in secret, I recruited many dwarves to our cause, some which I, in retrospect, should not have trusted. King Thorin died however, and the\nseperatist movement evaporated overnight. One of my \"allies\" Dizzy Irongrinder was elected the new king, and despite having sworn oaths to maintain secrecy of the seperatist movement, the Irongrinder brothers rapidly\nshowed their true colors. I had in the time since my return used my incredible business acumen to rebuild my wealth (not to the standards of before, but was still one of the wealthiest beings in Anthos) and it was coveted by Dizzy. Breaking his oath,\nhe publicly announced the existence of our by this time disbanded movement and put me under warrant. I could not trust any dwarf except those with the name Irongut or Tunnelsmasher, who valiantly risked themselves to smuggle me out of\nKal'Azgoth and to human lands. I was ruined. Condemned by all who did not - or did not want to - know better. Stripped of title, property (70,000 minas worth, equivalent to twice the entire Urguan treasury at the time) and expelled from the Kirkja\nDverga - an organisation I had been part of since the beginning. Disallusioned, broke and angry I devolved into the very same self-destructive behaviours I had abandoned in my youth. I found myself in the capital of a resurgent Oren,\nface down drunk when my former rival in the race to be the wealthiest in Anthos approached me.Tuvya Goldman (later Tobias I Carrion, emperor of Oren), found me and remembered who I was. He gave me purpose and I abandoned the\ndissolute behaviours I had again embraced. I became his right hand dwarf for nearly a decade, working for the Oreni treasury and rebuilding my fortune. I also fell in with a major mercenary company, the Wolvengard, who made me a\ncaptain. We unsealed the city we had built as rebels: Khaz'Rhadav and the Tunnelsmashers became stronger than ever before. We sacked the kingdom of Telemar and beheaded its king. Dizzy Irongrinder was deposed and I returned to the\ndwarves. But all things must end: Anthos burned, my eldest son died and I again returned to solitude, living simply to serve God. In Athera, I returned again to public life, but it was never again the same. My time amongst the humans had changed me. I\nhad little tolerance for the conniving of mountain dwarves and the endless wars of the Irehearts (my stance on Kjell led them to try kill me no less than four times).\nI longed for the carefree days of Kal'Dwain, remaining in contact with my kinsmen, Irongut and Tunnelsmasher alike, watching with time as age and war claimed my friends and family.\nWhen will Yemekar call me home and age and frailty finally take their toll? I have lived far longer than I deserve for I, like many have committed crimes in my time many would claim unforgivable.\nBut perhaps that is the great boon of life: that God grants you enough time to atone for all the harm one has wrought? Perhaps I have atoned, and perhaps not.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarven Cultures", "Kardel Irongut", "___________________DARVEN SUBRACES, CLANS, AND DIALECTS: A study on the Folk of Urguan.\n___________________OVERVIEW:\n(1)THE SUBRACES\n-Cavern Dwarves\n-Mountain Dwarves\n-Forest Dwarves\n-Dark Dwarves\n-Derva\n__________________\n(2)THE CLANS\n-Cave Dwarf:\n +Ironguts\n +Starbreakers\n +Goldhands\n +Ironborn\n-Mountain Dwarves\n +Frostbeards\n +Irehearts\n +Grandaxes\n-Forest Dwarves\n +Treebeard\n-Dark Dwarves\n +Doomforged\n(3)DIALECTS\n-Old Dwarvish\n-Standard Dwarven\n-Dwinic Dwarven\n-Dervic\n-Khorvadic\n___________________\nCHAPTER 1: THE SUBRACES\n___________________All dwarves are not alike. Some are dwellers of caves, while others prefer the warm company of sheep in the mountains. Others still dwell deep in the forests, in huts of wood, grass, and dirt. And some even\ndwell beyond our plane. \n\nThe descendants of Urguan were once as numerous as the sand in the deserts, blessed with robust trade and military might. But as time has weathered to Grand Kingdom to dust, and as the dwarves have\nsplintered and fractured amongst realms, there remain much less Dwedmar today than in the past.\n\nThe first dwedmar to come into existence were the Cave Dwarves, direct kin of Urguan, who live deep under mountains in halls of carved stone.\nThese dwarves are marked by their darker skin pigmentation and eyes of almost glowing colours, often entirely pearl-blue or amber. They make excellent smiths and alchemists.\nThe Mountain Dwarves were originally those cave dwarves who chose to pursue the bounties of Armakak above the surface of the earth.\n\nThe Mountain Dwarves are taller than their cave bretheren, and often have paler skin and blonde, red, brown, or black\nhair. Their large builds make them adept warriors, and they are unique amongst dwarves for their ability to mount and ride horses.\n\nForest Dwarves are indeed very rare and often seclude themselves within the depths of thickets.\nLittle is known about these mysterious kin of Urguan, save that their skin is brown like the dirt and their hair the same color. They live almost at one with nature, worshipping Anbella around their tree-temples and engaging in strange but powerful arts\nof nature. \n\nDark Dwarves are dangerous folk. Cross breeds between dark elves and dwarves, they have a predisposition to violence. Some worship strange gods and idols, and are rumoured to practice witchcraft. The dwell\nin hidden cities deep beneath the earth, deeper than even the dwarves care to delve. Young as a subrace, they have adoped the ancient practices and culture of the Derva rather than submit themselves to dwarven norms.\n\nThe Derva were the\nuncursed ones, those who escaped Khorvad's spite by travelling across realms. They are entirely extinct, and little is know about. However, their legacy lives on today in the unholy art of the Kathiik, or flesh runes, which Dark Dwarves use to this day.\nCHAPTER 2: THE CLANS\n___________________CAVE DWARVES\n___________________The Cave Dwarven Clans are: Irongut, Starbreaker, Goldhand, and Ironborn.\n\nThe Ironguts were the first Dwarven clan, named after Dwain\nthe Irongut, who achieved this name by his notorious reputation as a great gourmet and consumer of fine drinks and food. The Ironguts are notable for their beard braiding and magic usage.\n\nThe Starbreakers, historically the first\nclan to have been given knowledge of runesmithing, is another notable cave dwarven clan. Their complexions are ashen and their eyes pearly blue. The founder of Starbreaker was Gotrek Starbreaker, who was said to have been the apprentice of the Avatar of\nYemekar, thereby learning Runesmithing.\n\nThe Goldhands were founded by Tungdil Goldhand, and are famed for their ability to make wealth appear from thin air. They make excellent merchants, and have pale skin, blond hair, and blue eyes.\nThe Ironborn are the forbidden clan, ancient enemies of the dwarves. Originally the last of Urguan's sons, the Ironborn are stone-grey in complexion with pearly blue eyes and white hair. They worship Khorvad, and are hunted by most dwarves.\nMOUNTAIN DWARVES\n___________________Of the mountain dwarven clans the most famous in modernity is Frostbeard, worshippers of Wyrvun and founders of Kaz'Ulrah. Their clanfather was Kaz'Ulrah Frostbeard, who was a reknowned\nwarrior and tactitian.\n\nThe Irehearts are equally as famous. Their founder was Yavok Ireheart, who made a reputation for the irehearts as fierce warriors.\n\nThe Grandaxes are a long line of king-bearing dwarves, most famous among\nthem the conqueror Thorin Grandaxe and the scribe Valen Grandaxe. Their founder was Bogrin Grandaxe, a fierce warrior and leader who took the name of his runic weapon.\nFOREST DWARVES, DARK DWARVES, AND DERVA\n___________________The forest dwarven clan of Treebeard is the only elder clan of this lineage. The founder of this clan is unknown, but Savictus Treebeard is generally considered to have been his mysterious progeny\nFamed for their affinity with nature and druidism, the Treebeards live hidden away from the world.\n\nJust as obscure are the clan of Doomforged, spawn of Urir Ireheart and Faeyin the Dark Elf. A violent and easily\nangered breed of black-skinned dwarves with glowing red eyes, the doomforged live in isolation in the deepest chasms of the realm, practicing their Flesh Runes away from the surface.\n\nThe Dervic clans are lost to history, but their royal clan,\nSilverbeard, is said to descend from the same lineage as the Elder Clans. Little is known about these folk, save that they were more advanced than the Aegisian dwarves.\nCHAPTER 3: DIALECTS\n___________________The Dwarven language is fractured and diverse. All Dwarven tongues stem from the language today referred to as Old Dwarvish. Although extinct, dwarven Runes still preserve the ancient mode by which this language\nwas written.\n\nStandard Dwarven is the modern iteration of a 'common' dwarven tongue. Often used to name cities and grant other toponyms (being the root of the famous Kal' prefix of Urguanic cities), it bridges the many barriers between dialects and\nserves as the literary language for all dwarves today.\n\nDwinic dwarven is a dialect of dwarven spoken in Holm. Isolated from standard dwarven and in constant contact with flexio due to the merchant nature of its speakers, it has\ngravitated far away from standard dwarven. Hosting a complex case system, it is one of the most complex dwarven dialects, used by the Ironguts to encode history, literature, and academia.\n\nDervic is an extinct language believed to\nbe the closest relative to Old Dwarvish. It was marked by its near nonexistent use of vowels and strange runic system which today lives on in the Kathiik.\n\nKhorvadic dwarven is a forbidden dialect of dwarven, the dialect of the Ironborn. Having been\nisolated from Standard Dwarven for all of its history, Khorvadic dwarven is muddled with Black Speech, as its speakers also practice the dark arts and thus naturally know the language. \n\nEach of these dialects is written in dwarven runes, which differ\nslightly between different dwarven alphabets. Most dwarven dialects have some degree of similarity, especially Dwinic and Standard Dwarven, and are mutually intelligeble for the most part.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwedmar Hist. 1", "Nerah", "-Aegis-\nThe Dwarven Race is created by YEMEKARR\n-----\nUruguan creates the first Kingdom of Urguan, by founding the city of Kal’Urguan\nA fall Aengul named Ondnarch brings an\neternal winter by attacking northern Dwar holdings.\nThe Empire of Khorvad is built from the ashes of Ondnarch’s attack.\nVelkan Ironborn assumes rule of the Empire and establishes the Irongborn clan.\nThe Great Collapse occurs, where Thorngar Ironborn burns almost all the books and scrolls from previous eras.\nThe Dwarf Simppa establishes a Dwarven Confederation in the North to resist the Empire.\nKing Simppa reestablishes the Kingdom of Urguan by defeating Thorngar Ironborn.\nAfter growing ill, Simppa is replaced by Charles Grimlie. King Grimlie rules like a dictator and expands Dwarven cities across Aegis.\nKal’Bryst falls under the new Undead threat.\nThe Caravan war begins between the Orcish Rexdom and the Kingdom of Urguan.\nAfter Human subterfuge in the Kingdom’s vault, King Grimlie declares war of the Kingdom of Oren, an unpopular    move\nThe Grandaxe splits into the Braveaxes and the Blackaxes after disputes between Decks Grandaxe and King Grimlie.\nThe Blackaxes found Kal’Domhain while the Braveaxes remain loyal.\nKal’Alras declares independence and\nfounds the nation of Alras.\nKing Belin Irongut succeeds King Grimlie adn brings the Kingdom back to its democratic roots.\nOuter Kal’Urguan is developed, becoming known as The Crag.\nKing Algrim Irongut begins his rule, assuring in an era of stagnation. Many Dwarven clans leave Kal’Urguan during this period.\nClan Blackaxe returns to Kal’Urguan under the leadership of Bazian Blackaze to revive the city.\nThe Dwarven legion sees its first action in battle against the Undead as they defend the Elven city Malinor.\nFort Fairleaf is constructed as a joint defence project agains the Undead between the Wardens and Legion.\nThe Legion and Wardens launch a successful assault on Wrath’s Clutch. However, tensions over each sides’ commitment to the battle are raised.\nRelations between the Elven nation and Dwarven nation are damaged as Fort Fairleaf is demolished\nThe Legion is sent to defend Al’Khazar as its King Edmund Sheffield is corrupted.\nMarshall Thorik Braveaxe uses the Legion to repulse Queen Cassandra’s Undead assault on Kal’Urguan.\nThe Legion begins tis first peacekeeping mission on the King’s Road as the Orcish nation and Human nation go to war.\nKing Algrim Irongut is captured by Undead and is eventually corrupted, leading to his arrest.\nThe shortlived reign of Gotrek Starbreaker is followed by the establishment of a ruling War Council.\nAs the Orcish-Human War winds down to a close, The Legion assist the Orcs in the assault of Al’Khazar.\nA defensive pact is signed between\nKal’ Urguan and the Nation of Oren.\nA joint Legio-Oren assault is lead on an Undead keep that threatens Aeriel’s Keep.\nThe War Council is overthrown by Thorik Braveaxe, with support of the Braveaxes and Blackaxes.\nThe Tazarak is established as an alliance between Alras, Oren, an Urguan which creates tensions with the Orcs and the Wardens. Alras soon backs out of the alliance.\nThe Verge is discovered and ventured into.\nThe first Grand Tournament is held, with Kjell Ireheart named as the first Grand Champion of Urguan.\nWar is sparked across Aegis after several skirmishes between Legion and Orcish forces.\nThe Great War begins as Dwarven, Human, and Kaxil Clan troops march against Orcish, Warden,a dn Teutonic troops.\nThe seige of Galahar is begun and ended as news that the Dwarves and Humans plan to seige Krugmar, the capital of the Orcs.\nThe Wardens power declines as the war goes on, eventually leading to their disbandment and the end of the Orc - Elf alliance.\nnew alliances are made between Kal’Urguan and Oren, and between the Kaxil Clan and the city of Aeriel.\nA period of Dwarven isolation occurs as the Undead attacks increase.\nA map peice is delivered to and deciphered by Dwarven scribes. The map would show the path to escape Aegis to Asulon.\nRefugees from Al’Khazar flee to Kal’Urguan and Alras after the Undead capture the city.\nValen Blackaxe and Warlord Mogroka’Gorkil sign a peace treaty, establishing the United Aegis Coalition. Councillor Gimrik Braveaxe is\nCorrupted by Undead when he surrendurs the Legion fort by Wrath’s Clutch to the undead.\nThe Legion marches to the aid the Phoenix rebels in Galahar against Orcish armies. This results in the split up of Oren between Hansetti and Renatus.\nKal’urguan is removed from the United Aegis Coalition after Urir Ireheart massacres hundreds of Alrasian citizens.\nAfter King Syrio of Alras sends bounty hunters after the Irehearts, the Blackaxe and Frostbeard clans defend the Irehearts.\nThe Legion and Knights of Galahar assault Alras to recover the map that would show the path out of Aegis.\nAn alliance is established between Kal’Urguan, Renatus, and Malinor. Preliminary work is put in to add Hansetti and Krumar.\nKal’urguan falls to Undead armies, leading to Dwarven reguees fleeing ot Tazarak.\nThe first Doomforge is born, a mixed race of Urir Ireheart and Faeyin the Dark Elf.\nKjell Ireheart, Urir Ireheart, and Valen Blackaxe enter the Nether to defeat the\nUndead. Urir Ireheart sacrifices himself to save the races of Aegis, while Kjell Ireheart and Valen Blackaxe manage to escape.\nThe Dwarves and other nations of Aegus flee to the Verge and escape form the chos. Kjell ireheart however refuses to leave his home of Kal’Urguan, while Valen Blackaxe is knocked overboard when a lightning bolt strikes the ship’s mast.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwedmar Hist. 2", "Nerah", "-Asulon-\n---------------------\nUpon arrival in Asulon the Dwarven refugges found Kal'Karik as their new capitol.\nThe second Grand Tournament is held and Darian Blackaxe becomes Grand Champion of Urguan.\nDarius Irongut founds Kal'Dwain as a mining colony for the Dwarves. \nThe Kingdom of Urguan is split into two after a dispute arises between Arbek Starbreaker and Hiebe Irongut over a failed coup. The Irongut Clan leaves Kal'Karik to found Holm.\nThe first appearence of the Hallowed Bandits occurs in the Dwarven Mountains.\nGrand King Thorik Braveaxe is murdered by an unknown assassin.\nThe son of Thorik, Broski Braveaxe is crowned King. His first action is to end the\nGrand Council system of governance.\nKal'Karik joins a coalition of Hansetti, War Uzg, Salvus, and Alras in order to seige the fortress of Das Boot. This proves to be the penultimate battle in the Hansetti-Renatus War.\nKjell Ireheart reappears on the back of an Aegisian Dragon claiming he had slain 6 of them to arrive in Asulon. The Dragon did not survive impact.\nKal'Karik is abandoned after a Dragon is unleashed upon it. Valen Grandaxe traps himself in the Kal'Varak to\nsurvive.\nThe Dwarven refugees once again move north to establish Khaz'A'Zhar. \nExpiditions into Karik are launched to find the Dwarven crown. Renatus forces claim the crown first however, damaging relations.\nKhaz'A'Zhar suffers heavy structural damage after Orcs invade the city, and explosives are set off to push them out. \nAn alliance is signed between Salvus and Urguan.\nKing Broski Braveaxe abdicates after a coup attempt by Thordat.\nThe next King Stronghold Braveaxe last mere hours before his abdiction leads to the crowning of King Kjell Ireheart. \nA weakened Legion fails to defend Salvus lands from an Orcish army, and is forced to retreat.\nKing Kjell's rule shares the same qualities of dictatorship that King Grimlie's had. The capitol of the Kingdom is moved to Mount Ire.\nThe Dwarven printing press is invented.\nMorgrim Blackaxe, son of Valen, negotiates a new form of\ndemocratic goverment with King Kjell.\nWar begins between the Orcs and Dwarves after Gromgok'Gorkil becomes Rex of the Orcs.\nBazian Blackaxe unites the clans of Blackaxe and Braveaxe into Clan Grandaxe.\nThe Legion invades a weakened Alras and reclaims its land for the Kingdom of Urguan, renaming it Kal'Alras.\nKal'Anart is founded by the newly established Grandaxe clan.\nKing Kjell Ireheart reintoduces the Grand Council.\nThe Kingdom ushers in an era of Renaissance. new weapons of war and culture are produced at equal rates and the cities of Urguan become cultural hubs of Asulon.\nGrand King Kjell Ireheart founds the first Dwarven Empire. \nThe newly strengthened Dwarven Legion defeats an army of Orcs and Subudai at the Battle of the Sands. The Subudai withdraw their armies from the conflict, claiming a\nmisunderstanding. \nThe Empire of Urguan repels Orcish and Flay armies from their seige of Kal'Alras and pushes them into the northern territories. A peace treaty is signed after the capture of Volvokrem.\nWith the war ended, the individual holds push\nin dependence and the Empire is dissolved. Kal'Anart, Kal'Dwain, and Kal'Alras are released as independent states. \nOrcish and Dwarven diplomats agree that a combined war against the Teutonic Order would be more beneficial for both peoples.\nThe Dwarven holds decided the abandon their isolated cities and return to Kal'Karik. \nValen Grandaxe, with the help of Doomforge healing, escapes the dreamworld of the Kal'Varak.\nThe Legion succesfully defends Kal'Dwain\nfrom a family of attacking Drakes.\nHiebe Irongut is crowned King after Kjell Ireheart abdicates and departs on a pilgrimage.\nThe Third Grand Tournament is held and Kel Steelarm becomes Grand Champion of Urguan.\nThe Dwarven Legion battles and defeats the Teutonic Order on the plains of Arethor.\nAn alliance is made between the Kingdom of Urguan, Malinor, Holm, and the Kharajyr.\nThe Dwarven Constitution is written and passed into law.\nKing Hiebe Irongut leads Legion and Elven soldiers to rescue an Elven Princess from the Orc Capitol.\nAn uneasy truce is held between the Kingdom of Urguan and the War Uzg after war breaks out between the Uzg and Malinor.\nHouse Tarus and House Elendil stage an unsuccesful rebelion agains the Holy Oren Empire. House Tarus flees to the safety of Dwarven lands, severely damaging relations.\nThe Battle of Kal'Karik is won by Legion troops as House Flay and withwash Orcs\nlay seige to it.\nKing Hiebe Irongut's personal army, the Crimson Edict, is disbanded after disputes with Marshal Kjell Ireheart.\nThe first amendment is made to the Dwarven Consitution, stating that only true blooded Dwarves made hold\npositions on the council.\nAfter unkown powers lay seige and consime Asulon, the Dwarven refugees end up shipwrecked on the Isle of Elysium alongside the other races.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwedmar Hist. 3", "Nerah", "-Elysium & Kalos-\n------------------\nThorik Grandaxe, thought to be dead, is found deep in the caves of the Elysium volcano near the new Dwarven hold. He is freed from the corruption of Ondnarch by the Hammer of Urguan.\nKing Hiebe Irongut is overthrow by Kjell Ireheart, Gorum Forstbeard, and Tortek Silverfist. Thorik Grandaxeis crowned King to replace him. \nHouse Silverblade and House Hightower realign themselves with the Kingdom after Thorik's crowning.\nThe Legion is sent to assist the White Rose Order and the War Uzg with laying seige to House Flay and the Teutonic Order. The battle is a success, ending with a visit from Emperor Godfrey of the HOE. \nThorik Grandaxe is officially crowned King.\nThe Dwarven Constitution is reformed into The Articles of Urguan.\nThe Kingdom of Urguan and the Holy Oren Empire sign the Treaty of Aturial. Thorik Grandaxe and Godrey Horen make a blood pact with each other to consumate the alliance.\nThe alliance with Malinor is broken after it has been found that the Golem Anvil was stolen by High Elven spies. Tortek Silverfish is stipped of his ranks for aiding the High Elves.\nThe War Uzg declares war on the Kharajyr and invades the Kha stronghold while a platoon of Legionaries are stationed there. While the stronghold is destroyed, the rebuilding effort by the Legion strengthens relations between Dwarf and Kha.\nBoth the Kingdom of Urguan and Holy Oren Empire declare war on the War Uzg as a response. Kjell Stormhammer Ireheart leads the victorious seige of Kazak'Urkus.\nThe second amendment is made to the Articles of Urguan, regulating Holds.\nKing Thorik Grandaxe abdicates after a short sucessful rule. Omithiel Strongbow wins the subsequent election and is crowned King.\nThe Dwarves travel to the Isle of Kalos after the volcano erupts.\nAfter many small conflicts with the Orcish armies, the several volcanos on the Isles of Kalos begin to erupt as well.\nThe Dwarves travel alongside the other races to the new land that was discovered, Anthos.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwedmar Hist. 4", "Nerah", "-Anthos-\n------------------\nThe Dwarven refugees settle in the Grand City of Kal'Azgoth.\nThe Legion alongside Orenian soldiers rescue an Orenian princess from an Orcish sky cell.\nThe Legion, lead by Marshal Kjell Ireheart and Commander Thorin Grandaxe, siege an Orcish fortress with the help of Orenian skirmishers. \nThe Battle of the Crossroads is won bu The Legion.\nTelchar Azaghul and his clan invent the Steam Engine and take\ncommand of the Dwarven Navy.\nThe First Legion Steam Ship is built by the Azaghul Clan and set sails.\nDwarven Diplomats demand the return of the Arken Stone after the Uzg sues for peace. War rages on.\nKing Omithiel backs Wood and Dark Elven rebels in Malinor, leading to a High Elven abdiction and independence.\nThe newly formed House Blackmont, containing former members of House Flay, begin to raid the Dwarven countryside.\nThe Legion, lead by commander Dreek Ireheart march on the Blackmont Keep to demand the raids stop. \nValen Grandaxe passes on from the corruption he suffered during his time in the Nether. He is raised to the statue of Paragon, the Wordsmith.\nDiplomats meet to discuss an end to the war between the Kingdome of Urguan, Holy Oren Empire and the War Uzg. \nNalro Grayhammer invents the Dwarven Personal Carrier, na armored transfer vehicle driven by Oxen.\nThe Fourth Grand Tournament is held and Oyvind Frostbeard becomes the Grand Champion of Urguan.\nKing Omithiel Strongbow resigns and an election is called. Thorin Grandaxe is crowned King.\nThe Lords Council is reformed, naming Telchar Azaghul, Nalro, Grayhammer, and Farren Starbreaker to its ranks.\nParagon Kjell Ireheart resigns from his positions and leaves the Kingdom to venture the world. His son\nDreek Ireheart replaces him as Marshal and Lord.\nThe Adunians swear vassalage to King Thorin and settle in Whitescar.\nKal'Halla is abandoned, and the few resident Dwarves move back to Kal'Azgoth.\nThe Third Amendment to the Articles of Urguan is passed, implementing a Crown Authority System.\nMumurs of discontent spread as King Thorin rules/ The Irongut clan split, with the newly named Thunderfists declaring a rebellion.\nThe Second Dwarven Civil War begins, with the Thunderfists commandeering the Hold of Vaer'haven.\nThe rebellion quickly fails due to a lack of manpower, and little support from the Hold of Vaer'aven itself.\nGrand King Thorin Grandaxe founds the second Dwarven Empire after incorporating the Kharajyr as vassals.\nYears after the rebellion, and despite the founding of the Empire, murmurs of discontent continue.\nThe Lord's Council proposes several votes with the intention to oust Grand King Thorin due to his dictator-like tendencies. After being pressured from Grand King Thorin, Lords Dreek Ireheart and Delric Grandaxe resign.\nGrand King Thorin Grandaxe successfully sues Dreek Ireheart for 70,000 minas for misuse of Legion resources. As a result Dreek Ireheart, by far the richest in Anthos, pledges 150,000 minas and carts upon carts of Iron to the Grand Kingdom.\nAfter the donations and payment, the Grand Kingdoms coffers overflow with riches, only for the clouds of war to begin gathering.\nThe Fifth Grand Tournament is held, and Dain Ireheart is named Grand Champion of Urguan.\nDiscontent against Grand King Thorin's rule rises again in Vaer'aven with a magical guild named The Fallen spearheading it. The Legion is deployed and quickly quells any trouble.\nLord Nalro Grayhammer is attacked\noutside of Salvus, breaking the blood pact between Thorik and Godfrey. Grand King Thorik Grandaxe declares war on the Holy Oren Empire, ralling the Empire being him.\nThe first battle takes place, with the Legion and its vassals heavily outnumbered against Orenian armies. The Battle of Snow is a resounding victory for the HOE.\nParagon Kjell Ireheart and Dreek Ireheart lead the construcation of a new mega fortress at\nthe Crossroads. It becomes known as Storm's Crossing.\nThe mega fortress holds off countless raids from Orenian skirmishers, and establishes the keystone to the Dwarven defense.\nGrand King Thorin and Lord Gorum Forstbeard, alonside other diplomats meet with the HOE in the Cloud Temple to discuss peace. Almost all of Grand King Thorin's terms are dismissed leading the Dwarven diplomats to set the Orenian treaty on fire and leave.\nKing Garth Hightower reaffirms his House's friendship with Urguan and leads the City of Salvus to defect and pledge an oath of vassalage tp Thorin.\nAfter a mass exodus of Orenian leadership, the Empire collapses and is split up into several Kingdoms.\nPower struggles begin among the new Human Kingdoms, many of which have sworn vassalage to Grand King Thorin. The Dwarven candidate for King of Abresi, Pius Silverblade, is ousted by the remnants of House Horen.\nTelchar Azaghul and Nalro Grayhammer improve the Steam Engine and implement it into the Dwarven Personal Carrier.\nBoth Nalro Grayhammer and Gorum Frostbeard resign from the Lord's Council, Morgrim Grandaxe and Dizzy Irongrinder replacing them.\nBefore his death Thorik Grandaxe commissions the building of the Great Wall of Urguan, spanning the entrance to the Dwarven valley. Upon his death he is raised to Paragon status, The King of Kings.\nWulfric Grandaxe is named Lord.\nThe Daemon Ondnarch attacks Kal'Azgoth with a scouting force and kills Grand King Thorin Grandaxe in the process.\nElections are held, and Dizzy Irongrinder is narrowly crowned Grand King over Igor Ireheart.\nZahrer Irongrinder is named Lord to replace his cousin Grand King Dizzy. The War Uzg delcares war on the Grand Kingdom inorder to claim Salvus for their new capitol.\nSalvus secedes from the Grand Kingdom and\njoins the Coalition of Human Nations.\nThe Grand Kingdom of Urguan joins the War Uzg in its seige of Salvus.\nThe coalition force of Krugmar Orcs, Legion, and Ruskan mercenaries sack Salvus.\nThe Hold Barbek becomes the primary supplier of farmed goods for the Grand Kingdom.\nDreek Ireheart and Dom Irongut lead Legion scouts into an abandoned city underneath the Navy Docks.\nGrand King Dizzy leads a move from Kal'Azgoth to establish Storm's Crossing as the new Capitol.\nIndago Stormhammer leads the reconstruction of the mega fortress into a city.\nThe Aytosian Society declares war on the\nGrand Kingdom.\nThe Legion, lead by Lord Igor Ireheart, quickly sacks the Aytosian Society's camp and executes its leader.\nOmithiel Strongbow passes away and is named Paragon, The Builder.\nStorm's Crossing's reconstrucation is finished and renamed Kal'ithrun, becoming the new capitol of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan.\nGrand King Dizzy declares war on the Kingdom of Telemar to push Dreek Ireheart's claim for its throne.\nThe Battle of the Wilds captures Telemar's capitol and names Dreek Ireheart as its new King. King Dreek swears vassalage to Grand King Dizzy.\nKing Dreek and Lord Zahrer use the help of two Orcs to reclaim the Golem Anvil from the High Elven nation.\nThe Sixth Grand Tournament is held and Dormilion Irongut is named the Grand Champion of Urguan.\nThe Grand Kingdom of Urguan alongside the Dominion of Krugmar declare war on the Kingdom of Renatus.\nRenatian soldiers attack Kal'Ithrun but\nare repelled by the Legion under the command of King Dreek.\nThe Legion is defeated by House Blackmont while defending the Elven city of Luminaire.\nKing Dreek Ireheart is named to the Lord's Council.\nBrothers Dreek Ireheart and Igor Ireheart defend Kal'Ithrun on their own against an Orcish Army as the Legion defends Brom'Krah from the Black Scourge.\nLord Dreek Ireheart alongside diplomats from other nations converse with the Black Scourge at the\nCloud Temple. Grand King Dizzy promptly declares war on the Black Scourge alongside the other nations of Anthos.\nOnar Ireheart establishes Dwarven time.\nPreliminary peace talks are held between Orcs and Dwarves.\nGrand King Dizzy Irongrinder is voted out bu the Lord's Council. Lord Farren Starbreaker is named Lord Regent.\nThe Fourth Amendment to the Articles of Urguan is passed, declaring non Dwed may not bote for the Grand King.\nIndago Stormhammer is crowned Grand King of Urguan. \nOnar Ireheart is named to the Lord's Council after Dreek Ireheart's resignation. \nThe Grand Kingdom of Urguan delcares war on the Empire of Oren in support of the Silverblade rebellion.\nOndnarch's skirmishers are seen around the Grand Kingdom again, killing transports and merchants.\nThe Kingdom of Adunia secedes and joins the Empire of Oren.\nThe Legion, Teutonic Order, and House of Silverblade lay seige\nunsucessfully to Shadow Castle. They are routed by Orenian and Orcish armies.\nOndnarch's army captures and holds Kal'Azgoth for a few days before the Legion and Wood Elven armies retake it.\nKing Dreek Ireheart dies from his wounds\nafter carrying the message to Kal'Ithrun of Ondnarch's attack.\nThe Arken Stone is found missing after Ondnarch's army retreats back into the Deeproads.\nA Legion scouting party ventures into Kal'Azgoth to find the Kal'Varak had been\nstolen by Ondnarch. They also discover that Ondnarch has taken a physical form in this world, displaying almost all of his Daemonic power.\nFariken Irongut replaces Dominic Irongut on the lord's Council. \nWith the loss of its\nvassals, the Dwarven empire becomes a Kingdom again.\nThe Kingdom of Urguan is denied entry into the Coaltion of Anthos against the Black Scourge.\nLords Onar and Zahrer seal off the entry into Kal'Azgoth, trapping Ondnarch.\nThe Coalition of Anthos begins hostilities with the Kingdom of Urguan after it raids the bread basket of the Kingdom, the Hold of Barbek.\nThe construction of two new mega forts begin, Thoringrad and Indago-Olaf.\nLord Fariken Irongut\nenlists the aid of the Black Scourge in the defense of Thoringrad.\nThe Coalition of Anthos seiges and sacks Thoringrad, defeating the Legion, House of Silverblade, Teutonic Order, and Black Scourge mages.\nA new type of warfare is engaged between the ruins of Thoringrad and Indago-Olaf, trench warfare.\nThe Lord's Council negotiate the Kha and Elves out of the war, while negotiations with the Orcs fail.\nClan Grayhammer is exiled, taking the blame for Lord Fariken's alliance with the Black Scourge.\nDormin Doomforge leads the Legion to retake Kal'Urir from the clutches of Ondnarch. By doing so, he discovers rumors of a hammer stronger than Urguan's hammer\nClans Irongut and Goldhand refocus resoucres on the oimprovment of Kal'Ithrun, hoping the war itself would end soon.\nLord Fariken discovers the resting place of Barriden's Hammer, a cave along the coast near Kal'Azgoth.\nTensions rise between Clans Irongut, Goldhand and Clans Grandaxe, Ireheart over funds for the ongoing war.\nLakefort is founded by Fimlin Grandaxe as a subfort of Indago-Olaf.\nThe long seige of Fort IndagoOlaf is won by the Legion with help from the Princedom of Fenn and Orcish Kaxil Clan. The Empire of Oren's forces are routed back to Thoringrad.\n----------------\nEnd of Anthos Pt 1", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwedmar Hist. 5", "Nerah", "-Anthos-\n     Part Two\n--------------\nThe Legion and Fenn scouts explore a Scriberfolk Stronghold, finding the legendary Barradin's Hammer. The books accompanying it declare only the most pure may weild it.\nThe Hold of Dol'Gurad is founded by Gamle Irongut, as a home for the Irongut and Goldhand Clans.\nHogarth Irongut is named to the Lord's Council to replace Fariken Irongut.\nKing Indago allows Adunia to become a protectorate again.\nThe Kingdom of Urguan and Empire of Oren sign a peace treaty, with the Kingdom of Urguan ceding Thorinsgrad to the Cloud Temple Monks.\nThe Legion under the command of Igor Ireheart sack Ondnarch's castle underneath the Navy Docks.\nOndnarch's four Shallmandrils are executed by the Legion, severly weakening the Daemon's Army.\nThe Legion defends the Elven Conclave from Orcish Armies.\nKing Indago Stormhammer dies of frostbite.\nThe Frostbeard clan is revived under the leadership of Vulkin Frostbeard after its long dormancy.\nWulfgar Grandaxe, grandson of Valen overwhelmingly wins the elction to become King of Urguan.\nThe Seventh Grand Tournament is held an\nArcane Grandaxe becomes Grand Champion of Urguan.\nAn amendment is passed for the Articles of Urguan, implementing the Clan Council.\nA massive seige is held to retake Kal'Azgoth from Ondnarch and kill the daemon himself.\nWhile the armies of Krugmar and Oren seige the massive outer gates of Kal'Azgoth, the Legion fihts through the Deeproads from Kal'Urir to the city proper.\nThe Legion gains entry to the city and opens the gate for a combined assault on\nthe palace where Ondnarch remains.\nIgor Ireheart sacrifices himself using Barradin's Hammer to purify Ondnarch and free the Aengul Wyrvun. As Wyrvun is freed he names Igor Ireheart his Paragon, the Pure.\nDizzy Irongrinder is named to the Lord's Council to replace Igor Ireheart. \nThe remnants of Ondnarch's feral elf armies are hunted down by Legion patrols, creating peace again in the Dwarven valley.\nThe Kingdom of Urguan is accepted into thr United Anthos Coalition and the Legion assists Orenian and Krugmar troops lay seige and sack the Black Scourge occupied Castle Greywyn.\nThe Black Scourge captures the undefended Dol'Garud.\nThe Hall of heroes is founded, adding Thorin Grandaxe, Dreek Ireheart, Morgrimm Grandaxe, and Simppa to its ranks.\nThe Harbingers of the Black Scourge defeat the UAC army in the Battle for Fenn.\nThe Legion repels the last of Ondnarch's\nminions, Aelris the Gargantuan, from its attack on Kal'Ithrun.\nThe art of Golem and Rune smithing is passed onto Dared Starbreaker from the Farren Starbreaker.\nThe Legion assist the Decterum in defending Northern Orenian cities from the Scourge.\nThe Dreadfort is captured by the Black Scourge after the Legion and Golden Lance is defeated by the Harbingers.\nThe UAC enters into an alliance with the Golden Lance.\nFarren Starbreaker resigns from the Lord's Council, and is\nhonored for being the longest serving Lord.\nFimlin Grandaxe is raised to the Lord's Council.\nThe legion finds notes detailing Ironborn collusion with Ondnarch while they clear out an abandoned cultist layer.\nThe UAC and Golden Lance defeat an army of the Black Scourge and two Drakes during their seige of the Old Cloud Temple.\nThe Fringe is discovered through a portal in the Old Cloud Temple.\nKing Wulfgar Grandaxe leads the Dwarves into the Fringe and establishes a new city in the new land.\nDuring settlement in the large Basin, close alliances are made with the Druids and Alras who settle on the rim above the Basin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwedmar Hist. 6", "Nerah", "-Fringe & Thales-\n-----------------\nThe city of Kal'Akron is founded by King Wulfgar Grandaxe.\nA border dispute occurs with the Kingdom of Oren over a village that spans both nations land.\nThe Legion and Orcish army burn down an Orenian village that crosses the Dwarven border.\nPollution infests the lake of Kal'Akron and creates slime monsters out of the industrial waste.\nA cave opens in the middle of the lake, a\nresult of the heavy industrial pollution.\nThe Treaty of Zion is signed, a defensive pact between The Conclave, The Kingdom of Urguan, and Rexdom of Krugmar, and The Kingdom of Alras.\nThe Zion Pact declare war on the Kingdom of Oren.\nThe Order of Saint Lucien joins the war on the Kingdom of Oren's side.\nThe cave of pollution in the lake explodes outwards, assaulting the city in ravenous slimes.\nKing Wulfgar leads the Legion into the cave to purify it.\nThe Zion alliance wins the first battle agains the Kingdom of Oren, marking plans for a full invasion.\nWith the death of King Heinrick, an unpopular truce is declared between the two factions.\nKing Wulfgar pursues peace after the\nChurch mass exocmunicates the Kingdom of Oren's leadership.\nKing Wulfgar declares war on House Carrion, exiles of Oren. Krugmar declares support for the Dwarves.\nThe few Dwarves remaining in Anthos\ntravel to Kal'Akron after a tsunami from the melting north consumes Anthos.\nKing Wulfgar Grandaxe abdicates peacefully.\nKing Hogarth Irongut wins the ensueing election by an overwhelming majority and is crowned King of Urguan.\nTensions arise between House Silverblade and the Kingdom of Urguan over border disputes. \nSeveral rifts open around the Fringe, including one in Kal'Akron, that lead to the Red Realm. A way to defeat Setherein is presented.\nThe Kingdom of Urguan march alongside the armies of Anothos to destroy the lords of the Red Realm. After many days of battle, Setherein escapes to the Fringe.\nThe Legion prepares for the finl encounter with Setherein by having a specially designed\nballista made.\nThe final hours of the battle are dominated by the dwarven made ballista launching the Golden Lance at Setherein to end his torment of the people of the Fringe.\nVorstag Grandaxe, the son of Wulfgar, is attacked by Orenian\nsoldiers, triggering a diplomatic crisis.\nBorder disputes continue between the Kingdom of Urguan and Kingdom of Oren, but the diplomatic brilliance of King Hogarth resolve them.\nOnar and Falent Ireheart lead the Legion in purging\nthe Undead beasts that lived in the Kal'Akron undercity.\nThe Kingdom of Oren declares war on the Kingdom of Fenn, a close ally of the Kingdom of Urguan.\nThe decades old alliance between Fenn and Urguan is ended after Urguan does\nnot rally to the Legion to aid.\nThe Kingdom of Feen is slaughtered bu the Kingdom of Oren, leading to a deep rift in relations between Fenn and Urguan.\nHiebe Irongut proposes a clan prestige system, but it fails to gain support.\nKing Hortgarth abdicates, choosing Dizzy Irongrinder as the Regent. \nJorik Grandaxe wins the election, however the Clergy calls for an investigation into vote tampreing by regent Dizzy. It is later found out that Vorstag Grandaxe was the true winner\nand Regent Dizzy is removed from his positions for tampering with the election.\nKing Wulfgar Grandaxe is crowned King of Urguan.\nStrelt militias begin to raid Urguan lands. Quickly, the main army of Oren follows and\nfails in an attempt to pillage Kal'Arkon.\nThe Kingdom of Oren declares war on the Kingdom of Urguan.\nClan Irongrinder is accused of treason, and both Zahrer and Dizzy Irongrinder are arrested with their assests seized. Only Tog remains free.\nA peace is quickly declared between the Kingdom of Oren and Urguan after several skirmishes prove a stalemate.\nLathros Ironbeard leads an industrialization of Dwarven life.\nClan Grandaze escapes the polluted\ncity by building their clan hall outside its borders.\nClan Ireheart establishes its own hold outside of the city as well, naming it Rasterly Cock.\nThe Krughanistan Bloc is formed of Urguan, Krugmar, Teutonic Order, Fenn, & Alras.\nThe Lords Council votes to remove King Vorstag Grandaxe from his position. Onar Ireheart is named Regent.\nA split in the Orcs occurs after anger over the removal of their close friend Vorstag.\nKing Midgor Ireheart\nis elected and crowned King of Urguan.\nA Plague begins to spread around Anthos, leading to unaffected Dwarves to flee to the Ireheart Hold of Rasterly Cock until a cure can be made.\nA cure is developed in the High Elven and Dwarven camps.\nThe City of Atgaard defects from the Kingdom of Oren and swears fealty to the Kingdom of Urguan.\nClan Blackfist is formed by Gimrik Grandaxe and Gorum Frostbeard, containing a mix of veteran Dwarves who seek a brotherly bond.\nA drought occurs over several years in Fringe, prompting the search for a new land.\nThe Dwarves flee the Fringe alongside the other races to the realm known as Thales.\nKing Midgor Ireheart founds Kal'Klad.\nKing Midgor amends the Articles of Urguan, removing the Lord's Council and implmenting the Council of Clan Thanes. This founds a new empire for the Dwarves, the Third Grand Kingdom of Urguan.\nThe Hold of Kal'Konuul is founded by Dargrind Grandaxe.\nFimlin Grandaxe, Dizzy Irongrinder, Onar Ireheart, Balek Irongut, and Dagor Starbreaker are named the first clan Thanes.\nThe Mountain District is founded by Rhewen Frostbeard, in a bid to revive the ailing Frostbeard Clan.\nKing Midgor signs a peace treaty with the Holy Kingdom of Oren and the High Elven Haelon'or.\nThe Grand Kingdom of Oren, Holy Kingdom of Oren, and Haelon'or declare war on the Princedom of Fenn.\nThe Navy begins construction of a\nlarge transport vessel upon rumors of a more bountiful land.\nDagor Starbreaker is the first clan Thane to be replaced, Zapherius Starbreaker taking his job.\nThe ship Kaznol Anoros is completed and sailed to the port city of Tuv Aviv.\nThe races set sail for the new land, Athera.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwinic Phrases", "Hogarth Irongut", "A Dwinic Book of Phrases\n______________________\nBy Hogarth Irongut \n\nExi: Yes\nNai: No\nKalo/Kalosperis: Hello\nKalonetris: Goodbye\nKalo takormu: Well Met\nKhazdus: Dwarf\nUmrus: Man\nOrokus: Orc\nMalnas: Elf\nDarokkas: Beastfolk (Kharajyr, Hou-Zi, Voidal Horrors etc anything not Descendant)\nMesumrus: Halflings (literally “half human”)\nFallas [short for Vus fallemoro]: Thank you\nOmmus: Man\nIudas: Female\nKuventarus: cleric, equivalent to priest\nKuventus: Temple\nSeptarchates: The Brathmordakin\nIemekaros/Yemekar: Yemekar\nUlnos/Dungrimm: Dungrimm\nArenella/Anbella: Anbella\nIbella/Belka: Belka\nErmakehon/Armakak: Armakak\nRumminar/Grimdugan: Grimdugan\nOrantathos/Ogradhad: Ogradhad\nIkhorrossos/ Khorvad: Khorvad\nSeptarchates kur sumumu met vos: May the Brathmordakin be with you\nChrazda: Battle\nArmaka: Market\nGlhiuta: Arse\nIrongut Military: Brigada Kroruliotei\nF*ck: Gailur\nWhat the f*ck: Çë golü?\nBastard: Ekopiðus\nAle: Beius\nWine: Vinas\nOuzus: Hard liquor under 80 proof\nYgras: Hard liquor above 80 proof \nFotas: Alcohol in general also Fire\nSumoro Krorulioti: I am an Irongut\nOne: En\nTwo: Tavos\nThree: Trir\nFour: Firnos\nFive: Pentos\nSix: Sekos\nSeven: Septas\nEight: Oktas\nNine: Nuhas\nTen: Dekas\nTwenty: Tavdekas\nThirty: Tridekas\nForty: Firdekas\nFifty: Pentekas\nAbout/ Per\nAbove/ Sursum\nAcross/ Ndas\nAfter/ Desipsos\nAgainst/ Conter\nAlong / Mikos\nAmid(st)/ Mesos\nAmong/ Anmexis\nAround/ Qersis\nAt/ Ae\nBefore/ Antis\nBehind/ Pisos\nBelow/ Postos\nBeneath/ Ndapostos\nBeside(s)/ Diplas\nBetween/ Entras\nBeyond/ Peris\nDuring/ Mentris\nExcept/ Ektos\nFor/ Par\nFrom/ Dur\nIn/ En\nInto/ Se\nOf/ Du\nOff/ Fiksis\nOn/ Eptis\nOver/ Mbis\nPast/ Mrapas\nThrough/ Dias\nTo/ A\nToward(s)/ Pros\nUnder/ Nen\nUnderneath/ Posneni\nUntil/ Deris\nWith/ Met \nWithout/ Ndamet\nAnd / E\nOr / Ose\nBut / Po\nNor / Nda\nSo / Pra\nFor / Par\nYet / Akoma\nAfter / Pas\nAlthough / Anai\nAs / Si\nAs If / Sikur\nAs Long  / Oso\nBecause / Sepse\nBefore / Para\nEven If / Sikoma\nEven Though / Neskas\nOnce / Neiis\nSince / Nga\nSo That / Pra se\nThough / Skas\nUnless / Ektos\nUntil / Deris\nWhat / Ça\nWhen / Potes\nWhenever / Potesis\nWherever / Kursi\nWhether / An’a \nWhile/ Mentra\nThao/Thae - I/me\nVos - you\nKaa/Kae - He/She\nThau - We\nVosu - you (plural)\nKaum/Keum - They (masculine, feminine)\nThaoi = Mine\nVosoi = Yours\nKaoi/Kaei = His, Hers\nThaoi - Ours\nVosei - Yours\nKamoi/Kamei - Theirs (m/f)\nDirect: the, ve, ku, thos, vus, kai\nIndirect: the, va, ka, tha, vas, ke", ""),
        StaticBook("Dynatite Study", "Elwrick Albright", "THE DYNATITE STUDY\n-by Elwrick Albright-\n\nA Magical Science Fiction Short Story\n\nWritten 1574\n{OOC: For those who don't want to murder their chat, you can also read The Dynatite Study here http://tinyurl.com/hqfwwju }\nCHAPTER ONE\n\nThe hot summer sun shone, having no alternative, down on the town and on the back of Finnegan Clark as he walked swiftly down the center of the road. He listened to the sound of the gravel crunching beneath his feet until he had progressed\nfurther into the town where the streets were paved with cobblestone. There up against the heart of the town lay the manor of the renowned mage Abraham Montey, the man who discovered Dynatite. \nFor centuries it was firmly believed that it was impossible\nfor a gem to be able to hold a truly infinite supply of mana, but that is just what Dynatite seemed to do. Like thanhium, the source of this new gem’s mana is extremely dangerous to observe, but it’s still rather simple to enchant other items to draw mana\nfrom it. It was perfect-- nothing short of a miracle and a dream come to reality for transfigurationists everywhere.\nIndirectly, Abraham was the reason no one would ever have to reset a timekeeping device manually again, the reason fountains of evoked\nwater would never run dry, the reason cooking no longer required fire, the reason telekinetic enchantments on armour became practical, and the reason candles became obsolete in favour of magelight lamps. And people waved and 'good day'ed Finnegan as\nhe paced onwards toward his destination, for to them he was none other than the stellar apprentice in transfiguration of Abraham himself, on his way to another lesson. And he waved back at them. \n\nHe crossed through the iron gate and ascended the steps\nto the sturdy wooden doors of the great stone manor, whose walls were a garden of tangled ivy and mandevilla vines. Several of its windows featured lovely geometric patterns of stained glass in vibrant greens and blues. \nMounted next to the door was a\nsimple orange gem that when tapped would command a clever mechanism to ring a bell deep inside the bowels of the house. Its crystal of Dynatite was not visible, but it did have one. \nIn an instant, Abraham was at the door, wearing his typical dark green\nand dusty robes, his entire person flecked with trinkets and pendants bearing gems. Each of his fingers sported its own unique ring, which also had gems set into them. His eyes sparkled subtly as he smiled and invited Finnegan inside.\n“At the conclusion of our last lesson you expressed interest in my timekeeping device..” he started, once they had sat down to tea. \n“Mm!” Finn nodded eagerly, his mouth stuffed with a big bite of teacake. \n“You’ll be getting to make one of your own.\nI’ve decided it’d be a valuable lesson in enchanting for you to see how a transfigurationist can work together with a mage trained in a different type of magic to create an enchantment..” he said, waiting until his apprentice was able to speak.\nFinnegan swallowed the teacake and immediately began asking questions; “How can two mages work together to create one enchantment?” “What does it have to do with the timekeeper?” “The pointers move slightly at regular intervals-- that uses telekinesis..?”\nAnd after each question, Abraham granted him an answer.\n\nOnce they had finished their tea, he took the timekeeper down off the wall where it hung like a painting and showed it to Finnegan, told him to observe it for a moment and tell him how he would go\nabout making one of his own. \n“Why, I’d fashion a disc with a peg in the middle, fasten the pointer hand to it and hold it on with a stopper. Next, add those same twelve tic-marks around the edge, all spaced apart at equal intervals. Then I'd label them\n12 midnight, 3 dawn, 6 noon, 9 dusk,” he said, glancing up at Abraham, who nodded silently in approval for him to continue. “Then I’d put its mana gem here,” he pointed to the center of the timekeeper, over the stopper. “And enchant the thing to move its\npointer around the dial real slow like it’s doing now.. And I’d have it draw a continuous stream of mana from this piece of Dynatite nearby.” \n“Very good, Finn. Care to show me?” he asked, lifting a box off the shelf and opening it before his apprentice\nto reveal all the materials he had described in his process. “I’ll aid you with the telekinesis enchantment.”\nFinnegan nodded, and eagerly got to work while his instructor ferried porcelain teacups to the automatic washbasin in the other room.\nAnd like this the afternoon continued, with Abraham offering small bits of wisdom to Finnegan as he worked. \n“Mr. Montey,” Finnegan said to get his attention after they had finished the last step in creating the timekeeper and had been left for a moment\nto think. “Does Dynatite ever run out of mana, do you think? I know it’s never happened before, but do you think one day it might? And then everything will stop?” he asked. \n“I don’t think it will.”\n“How’s that work, then? Don’t you know where it gets its\ninfinite supply of mana?” he asks, blinking curiously up at Abraham, who didn’t respond, but sat still as a marble statue as he thought. \n“Aw c’mon, you were the one who discovered it!” Finnegan chuckles. “Really don’t know?” \n“Can’t say I do.” Abraham\nshook his head, offering a thin smile. “No one really does. It’s like thanhium-- can’t really look at it like that,” he shrugged. \n“Well, I’m gonna study it, then!” Finnegan proclaimed boldly. “Why, if we knew that, imagine what else might be possible!\nWe’d be honoured all across the world! Well, you’re already honoured all across the world, but then I would be too--”\n“No!” Abraham cut him off and stood abruptly, towering and booming like a rumbling black cloud over his apprentice who was still seated\nin his chair. Finnegan froze, bewildered, and waited carefully for what was to be said next. \n“No.. Don’t ever think about studying Dynatite again,” he said firmly.\n“Yes, sir..” Finnegan spoke quietly, still dazed, and dreadfully disappointed.\n“I understand if you want to work alone… but… please, when you’ve got Dynatite figured out, do you think you can tell me..? I just want to know what makes it so great…” \nAbraham let out a long sigh and pinched the bridge of his nose to calm himself.\nFinnegan hadn’t meant any offense by it. “Yes, yes..” he grumbled, hesitantly sitting down again. “I’ll let you know.”\nCHAPTER TWO\n\nMonths passed as Finnegan waited for an answer, and each time he asked, “any news on your Dynatite study?” he was met with a dismissive “patience, Finn,” as Abraham avoided other details he might ask about. He began to realize that even\nAbraham might be unable to solve this mystery… Often when he was at home, he gazed up at his timekeeper not to determine the hour, but to puzzle over the fantastic little crystal of Dynatite that powered it. \nIt was difficult to determine the exact\nmoment Finnegan decided he would go against Abraham’s word and study Dynatite. Like filling a cup, it is hard to tell how many careful drops of water it will take before the water runs over the edge, but indeed there is a final drop that breaks that\nsurface tension, just as there must have been some last drop of temptation that caused Finnegan’s curiosity to drive him to action. \nHe was aware from what Abraham taught him that he couldn’t interact with Dynatite’s mana directly, so he would have to\ntake a different approach to his study than messing around in a lab. He figured it might be useful to gather some basic information before getting deeper into the study. On the other side of town, past Abraham’s manor, he knew of a shop that sold\nenchanting supplies, where he had visited many times as a transfigurationist-in-training. This would be the first time he had ever been there alone. \n\nHe decided to pass through the public park on his way there, simply because he liked watching the\nfountains as he passed by. The quaint, lush park contrasted greatly with the section of the town he was heading to, where the streets were narrow and the buildings loomed overhead in place of trees. He held his hands in his pockets as he walked, looking\nup at the old, creaking shop signs, hanging out over the street with peeling letters. Eventually, he spotted the one he had been looking for, which read The Velvet Box. It was only legible because the letters had been carved and not just painted. The door\nwas bordered by two marble golems standing stock-still. They didn’t move as Finnegan let himself in. The bell above the door rang out into the empty room, causing a figure behind the front desk to stir and come to life. He was a jolly, portly man with\ncreases at the corner of his eyes from his constant cheerful smile.\n“Ah, Finnegan! Good to see ya, boy!” He bellowed as he caught sight of him. \n“Good afternoon, Mr. Milo!”\n“Abraham aint with ya?”\n“No, sir.”\n“Runnin’ errands for him?”\n“No, sir. I just want to ask some questions about Dynatite if that’s alright!” \nFinnegan scurried over to Mr. Milo’s desk and hoisted himself up onto it. \n“Sure thing, lad, sure thing! Ask away,” he said. He didn't seem nearly as opposed to Finnegan's\ncuriosity on the subject as Abraham was. \n“Where does Dynatite come from? Do you know how it’s formed?” he asked professionally, unfolding a piece of paper from his pocket and snatching a quill off the desk. \nMr. Milo shrugged. “Not sure. The suppliers\naint tell me where they get it from.”\nFinnegan nodded disappointedly, scribbling this down on the paper.\n“But I do have an idea of how it’s formed,” he said, raising his pointer finger into the air to let him know he wasn’t done talking.\n“Like obsidian, Dynatite doesn’t have a crystal structure-- or at least, not one big enough that I can see it. The coloring of obsidian comes from impurities in it, usually iron, that are caught in with the silica. The reason why it doesn’t have any\ncrystals is because it cooled so fast into a solid that it didn’t have time to grow any!” Mr. Milo explained as Finnegan scribbled down everything he was saying with furious speed, nodding as he listened. \n“If it was my guess, I’d say Dynatite is a type\n‘a volcanic glass, like obsidian but not-- it’s almost completely translucent, which means that it doesn’t have any other materials in it but silica!”\n“Thanks a bunch!” Finnegan exclaimed. He knew it was a good idea to ask Mr. Milo about this.\n“Need anything else?”\n“No, sir,” he said, shaking his head. \nThe crisp ringing of a little bell rang out into the space, and the duo directed their attention to the door.\nThere stood a brown-eyed girl who looked just a bit older than Finnegan, wearing a\nhooded woolen cloak over her plain dress. She carried a leather satchel with her. \n“Welcome to The Velvet Box, how can I help ya?” Mr. Milo said automatically, not having been acquainted with the girl before. Finnegan offered her a friendly wave.\n“I’d like to purchase twenty minas worth of Dynatite,” she said, taking a small drawstring bag from her satchel. She spoke in a hushed, polite voice, and her manner seemed mild and pleasant.\n“Sure thing, miss!” Mr. Milo said, rummaging around in the\nsupply bins held behind the counter until he found two crystals of Dynatite that met his unspoken standards. He got up from his chair and waddled over to the balance scales with the two gems.\n“Oh, that reminds me!” Finnegan exclaimed. “Mr. Milo, do you\nknow any other people who could help me with my Dynatite study? Abraham didn’t want to.”\n“Hmm, I dunno any names other than other humble salesmen like meself,” the man shrugged. “They know as much as I do.”\n“Darn.. alright, but thank you anyway! You've\nbeen a huge help already!”\n“Hey, no problem, Finn.” \nAt Finnegan’s seemingly harmless question, the girl’s soft face had contorted in an expression of absolute horror that had gone unnoticed in her silence while the two talked.\n{OOC: Minecraft books can only hold up to 50 pages, so this story will have to be continued later! You can still view the live link http://tinyurl.com/hqfwwju \nfor updates. Sorry for the cut-off!}\n\nEND OF PART ONE.", ""),
        StaticBook("Edward's Vote", "Edward Suffolk", "Horace!", ""),
        StaticBook("Effects", "Huckleberry Faroe", "Results of the effects of the          given potions\n\n>All the tests were performed on Charles, The obese rat.<\n>Or on myself if the potions do not work on the rat.<\n\n\n-Written by Rhova'dir, known as Huckleberry Faroe.\n1st Potion:\n\nA blue hued potion that is cold to the touch, once tested, the test became much slower and more pale, it is a water symbol based potion with ice-y properties. One dose of this potion is most likely not fatal.\n2nd Potion:\n\nA purple hued potion, there was no visible effect on the test so I tried it myself, I felt much smarter in a way, more intelligent but I became exhausted soon after, an annoying after effect, but it's an useful potion with no harmful effects.\n3rd Potion:\n\nYet another blue hued potion, although it did not feel cold, Charles tried it but he felt nothing for sure so I tried it for myself. As a mage, and with the constant use of magic, I felt my magic weaker but the energy I use for it was clearly\nback, I do not recommed this potion to any mage unless they are in a desperate situation and need to use their magic as fast possible even if it gets weaker.\n4th Potion:\n\nAfter consuming this green hued potion, the test began to run through the laboratory at an incredible speed for something with his weight, useful indeed, although the test became much slower after some minutes.\n5th Potion:\n\nThis dark grey hued potion did not even need a test subject, the potion suddenly released a cloud of smoke into the air as soon as it was opened... So this is the so called Smoke Whispers.\n6th Potion:\n\nThis red hued potion had a familiar smell, the smell of something used to heal, most likely Tippen's root, this is clearly a healing potion.\n7th Potion:\n\nThis odd yellow hued potion almost killed the test, it solidified in the test's mouth and almost suffocated him, all we know about this potion is that it solidifies after a few seconds after in contact with air.\n8th Potion:\n\nThis green hued potion had no effect on the test so I tested it on myself, I felt myself with sharper senses, this is the so called Potion of Acuity.\n9th Potion:\n\nThis green hued potion was cold to the touch and almost destroyed me and my laboratory, do not shake it violently nor bring it near a fire, it will combust and it is not desired in certain situations.", ""),
        StaticBook("Eight Line Poem", "Hobbs Burrows", "Eight Line Poem\nby Hobbs Burrows\nThe tactful sapling by your window,\nSurveys the prairie of your burrow,\nThe mobile spins to its collision,\nClara puts her head between her paws,\nThey've opened shops down Crossroads,\nWill all the saplings find a home?\nBut the key to the village,\nIs in the sun that pins the branches to the sky.", ""),
        StaticBook("Eldar Tree", "Unknown", "[!] The ink in this tome appears to be fresh; the handwriting, neat.\n\n\nCopy of the book\n\"Elder Trees\"\nWritten by\nUnknown\nIt is said there was a great forest.  It was mighty and bountiful, filled with life and nature flourished.  The wilflife stirred, and the trees swayed in the wind, and the Druids sang songs beneath the canopy.\nGreater still, are the tales of the trees\nflourishing here.  Strong, mighty, and protected.  It is said that the oldest tree of the forest had sprung them from its own seeds, and within its trunk its mind began to flourish.  Some may say tat Cernunnos and Cerridwen slept beneath the tree\nin their travels to bless the land.  Still, some may say these trees were the Aspects themselves in different form.  Still, whatever the reason, something sparked thought beneath the bark, and the trees ascended into something more than just wood\nand leaf.\nAs so after many millennia, these trees older thank time became Elder, and gave wisdom to the Druii, and protected their forests with their Ent children.  Some have given prophecies that were granted to them by the Aspects.\nOthers served as homes for great groves, some even as cities.  To speak with an Elder Tree is a rare and wonderful privilege.  Cherish it, for the Aspects have deemed you special to hear such wisdoms.\n~Druii'i'thirn, Arcanum of Ancient Secrets", ""),
        StaticBook("Electric Evo.", "Haadi Mubdee", "=--=--=--=--=--=--=            Electrical\n           Evocation\n=--=--=--=--=--=--=\n\n\n     -< ^v^v^v^v^\nThere is an old saying that humans (mortals) fear most other humans. I believe, however, that those who say that have never looked outside the confines of the human world. If anyone has come face to face with the power of nature, they will consider the\nprevious proverb a joke. If this sounds like nothing more than nonsense coming from an old fool, then answer this next question. If you can possess any form of power, what would you choose? Would you choose the power of mankind, or that of a wild beast?\nWould it be the roars of powerful men, or the sound of thunder that shakes the heavens? Is it the limited life of men, or nature's continuous cycle of life? Whichever way you look at it, the power of man is feeble compared to the grandeur of nature.\nThroughout history, all of mankind has admired nature's power and though they had feared it, they tried to deny that. This is one of man's many follies. They neglect nature's power, which does not discriminate, solely because they are a part of nature.\nIn particular, as humans learned of Mana and started seeing a glimpse of nature's other realm, they began neglecting nature's power even more. They didn't realize that their \"magic\" was actually an imitation of nature's power. This is what worries me.\nThere are many students who are Wizards and Druids in training who do not understand that every magic's starting point is a natural phenomenon. I, who also boasted in my knowledge of Electric magic , did not learn this until I saw lightning strike down at\nthe Crown Lands Plateau of Oren. In hopes that those who come after me will not make the same mistake, I decided to write this book. In other words, I hope that beginner wizards will learn the laws of nature and have a healthy fear of it as well.\nAlthough this book only deals with lightning power, which is only one of nature's awesome power, if you are wise, you will take the moral of the story to heart and apply it when training other magic as well.\nThe Principle of Electricity series Magic Skill\n                -=-\nIn order to understand the principle of Electric magic, you must first learn its natural counterpart: Lightning. If you've seen anyone use Electric-based magic, you probably noticed a close resemblance to a lightning strike. The lightning strike occurs\nwhen Mana, the energy that surrounds us, splits into two polarities of energy for reasons unknown. These split polarities each continue to accumulate energy, when, in an instant, an explosion of energy flow occurs between heaven and earth.\nThe intensity of the light and heat during this process contains tremendous power. Also, because of its unpredictability of where it strikes, it has been an object of fear to mankind. There are many opinions as to when and why Mana, splits into two\npolarities of energy. However, before anyone could come up with any concrete evidence, the debate's focus shifted because of the ‘great’ Wizard Ambrosia, who at times lacked common sense. He claimed that he was able to stabilize his Mana to split the two\npolar energies in a controlled manner, which caused all the scholars to shift their focus from the conditions in which the energy splits to the process of it. (It is a shame that scholars today are not interested in insightfully studying natural\nphenomena, and rather just want to uncover it just for the sake of using it. This is quite foolish.) Once Mana is split into two polar energies, each polarity begins accumulating energy at a rapid rate and causes an electric discharge. Then, when the\nbalance of energy between the two polarities is broken, a transfer of energy occurs from the one with more energy to the other. So imagine what would happen if one could embody either of the polarities and designate his or her target as the other\npolarity. Then, using Mana, if he or she polarizes the Mana and also raises his/her own energy level to be higher than their target, what would happen?\nExactly. This is what is known as Electrical Energy Magic.\nHow to use the Lightning Bolt\n                -=-\nThe Lightning Bolt attack is a magic that uses the mechanic of creating static electricity, which in turn utilizes the characteristics of the negative charge for a sudden electrostatic discharge. During the energy transfusion, a bright explosion\nresembling a lightning strike, rushes toward your target as Mana is depleted into replicating this phenomenon. Once all the Mana is depleted from the bolt and the surrounding elements reach equilibrium, the flow of energy ends. (Just like a lightning\nstrike in nature.) There are many questions surrounding this magic, such as \"How powerful is it?\" and \"How easy is it to use?\", which is technically asking how much energy it needs and how long it takes. To give you an answer, there is a limit to how much\nenergy you can gather, and you can only maintain the energy for about 15 seconds until later coming to a greater grasp of the art. You can charge your energy multiple times to gather more energy, but it is reported that it can become highly unstable after\nafter the third charge which is already risky enough. Also, you only have about 15 seconds to charge all your energy. This is because of several factors, such as the difficulty of maintaining the Mana's focus, and also maintaining the polarized energy at\nthe same time. (Even if you have plenty of Mana, it is difficult to charge for an extensive electrical bolt). The ‘Lightning Bolt’ attack is used to strike your enemy with electricity . Once your opponent is struck with this attack, they will be in a\nstate of shock due to the electricity surging within them as it an energy. Not a tangible object. Since this attack is based on an instant energy explosion between you and your opponent, the lesser the energy gap between you and your opponent, the great\ndamage it will inflict as the longer the distance the surge of electricity must travel, the more it discharges. Wasting precious Mana in the long run.\nSimple\n              Usage\n                -=-\nOnce you've carefully read through this book, and understood the principles behind the Lightning Bolt attack and are ready to use it, you can do so by following these simple steps. First, a connection to the Void is a must. As any form of magic. The\nsimplest manner in which to begin evoking such an element is to picture the empty black abyss that is the Void. A sleet of pure nothingness. Void of any life as the name suggests. Now one must mentally picture lightning crashing down upon the Earth. But\nstrictly the lighting. If one were to picture the scene, one could possibly border the realm of Pseudomancy (Illusionary magic) or if too much detail is placed on the Earth, soil or stone may be produced. Then you will see the static discharge enivision\nsuch an occurring unfolding before your palm you calm your mind to allow your Mana to polarize the energy and fuel it. Once the preparation is finished, lightning-like strands of light energy will flow around you. This indicated you have successfully\ncalibrated yourself with the Void and established an affinity to Electrical Evocation.\n\nThough mentioned before, I want to remind you that the intense light and heat from this attack can significantly startle your opponent.\nApplication:\n    Chain Lightning\n               -=-\nBefore we move on, I need to reiterate and explain in detail regarding multiple charges. As you know by now, the Lightning Bolt attack is very similar to the actual lightning strike that happens in nature. Does this mean that this magic is capable of\nimitating the continuous strikes that occur in a natural lightning strike?\n\nThe answer is yes. Scholars call this ‘Chain Lightning’. By charging the magic multiple times, you are able to hurl this energy to your target back to back.\nHowever, there is a limit to how many times you can strike in a row. As previously mentioned, since you can charge up to about three bolts, yet the risk increases with each charge. One interesting fact is, these bolts of energy attract to metallic\nobjects. Thus when in the vicinity of metal objects such as the bands of a barrel, swords and armor, iron grating, and other Ferrum or Arcarum apparel, the bolt will change it’s path of perjectory and curve to meet said object.\nContinuous Attack\n    Between Lightning\n         Bolt Users\n               -=-\nWe looked at the principle behind the Lightning Bolt, the Chain Lightning attack, and the application of these attacks in the previous chapter. If you think you've mastered everything through these two attacks, you still have a lot to learn from mother\nnature. If anyone has studied lightning strikes carefully, you know that lightning does not only occur in single, or multiple chain of strikes. Sometimes, lightning strikes attract other lightning and fuse together. Thus, where there are multiple\nLightning Bolt users, they can fuse each other's energy to form a collaborative attack.\n\nThis is a unique trait of Electric energy based magic that other ‘generic’ elemental based magic do not possess. When a user is charging his or her Lightning bolt\nattack, you can add on to their energy and instantly form a Chain Lightning attack. In other words, if you have charge your Lightning Bolt attack near another user that is charging, your charge will add to their charge, increasing their total number of\ncharges.\nThe Effects\n                of\n        Lightning Bolt\n               -=-\nSo, when is it a good time to use the Lightning Bolt attack? If you are wise, you should be able to figure it out yourself.\n\nFirst, the Lightning attack is good when facing multiple targets at once. Try it out yourself.\nUse skill of Electrical Evocation and attempt to fire off a bolt at a grouping of targets.. You will be amazed at how effective and convenient this property can prove to be.\nHowever, there is something you must remember: Chaining charges  inflicte damage which subsequently decreases with each hit. Beginners, unaware of this, might overuse the attack and find themselves out of Mana and getting attacked by the opponent.\nEven when you successfully use the Chain attack, the opponent might not have received as much damage as you think. Thus, the first target of the Chain Lightning Skill is very important. This is something every good wizard should be mindful.\nAuthor: Archmage Crumena V. Illwindior [HeeroZero]\n\nConsoliant: Electomancer Ceruberr Asul'Ailer [CaptainSheepy]\n\nCopier:\nGuildmaster Haadi Mubdee [Eladriendil]", ""),
        StaticBook("Electrical Evo", "Gauldrim Irongut", "Electric Evocation\n \n By Gauldrim Irongut.\nChapter 1, Uses of Electromancy:\n\nElectromancy is a very volatile form of arcane evocation, is just as likely to veer off it’s course or shock the user. A source of incredible heat and force, electromancy is a formidable tool. Slow to conjure\nand is a lifelong commitment electromancy can be used in survival situations. Able to create fires when need be through the burning of wood or other flammable materials. Another property that can be found in electromancy is the extreme attraction\nto large amounts of metal. An anvil, a suit plate of armour, or a large iron gate can cause the electricity to be attracted towards it and then channeled inside of it. If one is to touch a piece of metal charged with electricity they will be hurt or\nburnt as the electricity discharges. The most obvious use of electric evocation is the use of it in combat. A deadly force to be reckoned with once the user has achieved a high enough power to use it. Slow to conjure of fast once released, electric\nevocation is one of the most powerful forms of arcane evocation. Able to kill a large man in full plate mail  in a single bolt, if large enough this just lends perspective to the raw power. Electric evocationists also have the ability to summon forth\nfrom the heavens in the event of a storm with very good accuracy. \n\nChapter 2, Properties of Electromancy:\n\nAttracted to metal, can be conducted through metal,  has the force to shatter stone and the ability to travel through water.\nElectromancy is as versatile as it is powerful. Electric currents can be sent through water enabling one to shock someone that is in contact with the said body of water. This practice also applies to metal and if one is in contact with a suit of plate\nmail when the electric current is sent towards the bearer they will experience not only the force of the bolt but the current of the electricity as well. The current of the electricity will also cause muscle seizure and the dulling of senses.\nThe shattering of stone occurs when an extremely powerful bolt is sent hurtling towards the stone, resulting in flying rubble and scorched rock. As well as being able to scorch rock, Electromancy can set wood, paper, and any other flammable materials\nalight causing fire and burns.  \n\nChapter 3, Conclusion.: \n\nElectromancy is an almighty power to be reckoned with and those that perform it should be regarded with extreme caution. Slow to cast into immense power yet\nstill dangerous even at short range. It is advised that when in combat against such a mage, that large amounts of metal and or armour are unadvised  to have and even steel or iron greatswords. So to wrap this short informative text, one would be wise to\nheed the words of an electromancer and to regard the raw power and wisdom of those that wield it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Electricity", "Fury_Fire", "12th of the Deep Cold\n((6:30))\nLightning struck some distance away. After searching for some time, it was found to be the root of a tree that had been struck. Upon examination, it was charred, a slight stench coming from it. By all appearences, the tree\nlooked to have been burned. The only thing that told me otherwise was the static electricity still in the air for a short time around it.\n6th of Malin's Welcome\n((12:40pm))\nSanctuary\nLightning had struck only a short distance away, in the nearby forest. After searching, the path of earth that was struck had been found. Being even near the strike that had happened moments before left\nthe taste of metal in my mouth, and the smell of burning grass. The ground looked as if it had caught aflame for some time, yet the downpour had put it out. Other then that, the lightning strike itself was caught in full view. It had shot down\ndiagonally from the sky, other minor areas branching off from the strike. It had been followed by a loud clap of thunder.\n5th of the Grand Harvest\n((11:44 AM))\nSpoke to Nemir, a Telekenisis user.\nShe mentioned tha\n*The rest of the page is ripped out*\n5th of the Grand Harvest\n((11:45 AM))\nSpoke to Nemir, telekenisis user.\nStated that every time one connects to the void, they get a tad weaker as their magic grows a tad stronger. Explained that they would clear their mind, much as done in\nnormal meditation, and then one would imagine said element in their mind, along with their target. As they did this, they would envision a connection with the void. Often, one would twitch someplace when they connected, and their bodies would be put under\ngreat stress.\n5th of the grand harvest, 1554.\n((11:25 AM))\nI sat in my home, having connected with the void. The spark I summoned remained there for some second, before I would aim to brighten it, as shown before. As this happened I would grow tired almost immediatly,\nthe spark vanishing and I fell over, exhausted. I had felt something different then the normal rate of mana consumption, however. As I forced myself to use the mana required to make the spark brighter, I felt something that could only be described as a\na portion of 'life force' being withdrawn. I couldn't quite tell the amount, but I assumed this was my mana. All I could learn from this attempt was that it used up more mana then a normal spark.\nSometime in the Amber Cold, 1554\n((1-2 am-ish?))\nI allowed myself to be struck by electricity in my Augur form. Almost all feeling left me side pain, my entire body feeling as if it had become static. Side that, I could not tell much else about it.\n15th of the Amber Cold.\n((9 PM))\nI had now grown familiar with telling the amount of mana being used. As I would brighten my spark, I now fully felt the mana leave me. I had over time grown accustomed to how much Mana I had anyways, which\nis a major help as I determine the usage. I remain aware that my mana pool will end up growing eventually through meditation anyways, yet I would imagine it would be slow enough that I would grow used to it as such happened.\n11th of the First Seed, 1556.\n((5:44 PM))\n\n[!]Page has been torn out angrily!\n16th of the Deep Cold, 1557.\n((10:39 PM))\nI sat upon an altar in a forest with Nemir, preparing to shoot a bolt of electricity. It began with normal meditation, and the summoning of several sparks. I would concentrate them within the center of\nmy palm, forming a 'bolt', of sorts. After this I would hold my hand out and release it forward.\nThe bolt would hit the ground, leaving the air with a light feel of static for some moments before it would vanish and the brunt of fatigue hit me.\n9th of the Sun's Smile, 1559\n((3:30 PM))\nAt this point, not much had changed side my bolts growing steadily stronger as well as my ability to cast more. At this point I can cast three before I run out of mana, and the chance of me forgetting to\ncut the connection with the void before firing is minimal. I have finally noticed to conductive affects of metal, having cast near an iron rod once. My bolt had veered in midair, hitting the rod instead of continuing to go straight.\n12th of the Amber Cold, 1559\n((6:50 PM))\nA Kharajyr female was attacking a group of elves as I stood back and raised my hand, curious on how powerful my bolts had truely grown. Sparks began to form as well as sweat upon my brow, soon collecting\nwithin the center of my palm to form a bolt. It was obviously weak in power compared to Locke's, yet still okay in my eyes. Soon I let it fly towards the Kha, and the effects were surprising. The Kha fell over, stunned for some moments as the elves took\nthat chance to grab the Kha and bind it. Upon further inspection, the Kha bore a charred burn mark where the bolt had hit- although likely only caused due to her fur temporarily catching aflame.\n9th of the Sun's Smile, 1562\nThis hasn't been written in for some time, but it's about time to continue it. Since my last entry, my bolts have grown to full power and I'm able to cast three in a row before being unable to cast another. A full powered bolt\nwill easily leave burns on someones skin and make them paralyzed for some while. Alternatively, I can call a bolt down from the sky.. Such is done as a normal bolt is made within the hand. The difference would be that you're treating a point in the sky as\nthough it would be what you were summoning with instead of your hands. This alone would cause much more mana, and you'd also need a view of your target. It would take as much mana as though you summoned a normal bolt and shot it to that point in the sky.w\nPast that, you would pour much more mana than a normal bolt of electricity into it, soon to the point where it would be a full powered bolt of lightning ready to be launched. At first it would remain very hard to aim, and almost every  shot would miss.\nThese would not grow more powerful, and the reason you summon it in the sky is simple: Controlling that amount of mana close to you is stupid and dangerous. Even if you controlled it, the amount of electricity would harm you even if you are the creator.\nAs you continue doing such, it will become much easier to aim and not stress you as much.\nFinal words:\nThis book was originally aimed as a record of my learning, yet eventually I decided that it could be used to help any aspiring Electric Evocationists learn. It does not cover everything about the magic, although it still does with a lot of\nit. And I urge any who would use it to be cautious and find another electric evocationist to assist them in learning, be it as a teacher or mentor. This magic is dangerous to learn and at times I nearly killed myself with it.\n-Lefkos Glowsbane", "")
    )

    private fun _ATLAS_2(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Electromancy", "dragonmaster0219", "So what is electromancy? Well its the art of bending electricity to your will. This involves a couple of steps that this book will explain to you.\nChapter 1: Connecting to the void. \n\nTo start you must connect to the void. To do this you must calm your mind. This is harder than it looks so think of something or someone that calms you and rest for 10 minutes. This exercise can take a week to\nmaster until you can do this within seconds. ((Once you have done this you are ready to be a t1 electromancer)) \nNow you should try connecting to the void, imagine your hand going into a plain of creation and pulling the desired thing out. I cannot\nexplain the feeling  but once you do it youll know.\nChapter 2: Making Sparks\n\nNow that you can connect to the void imagine pulling the desired thing out of it. In this case imagine pinching a spark. Do this until you've confirmed you can pinch it and then open your eyes and\nwitness your first piece of magic. Once you've done this your possibility shall be endless.\nChapter 3: Increasing your stamina (becoming a T2 & T3 electromancer) Now that you can connect to the void do many mind taxing excercises to increase your stamina. Eventually you will be able to hold stable elctricity in your palms and if yo can imagine a\nsurge of it going forward a lightning shot. I shall leave shaping and other ideas to your imagination, remember though Magic is not a tool, it is an art, use this knowledge wisely.\n\n-Damien Sezarius", ""),
        StaticBook("ELECTROMANCY", "onm224", "ELECTROMANCY\n         GUIDE\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Richard Tarus\nAdapted: Amras Lúinwë\nWhat is electric evocation?\nElectrical Evocation is the arcane magic form whereby a mage creates Electrical bolts for his or her purposes. Unlike other types of Evocation electrical bolts is intended to be much more difficult to control due to its\nspeed and high energy nature. Mages who specialize in electrical evocation will be able to form electrical bolts and streams of electricity to electrocute their targets.However, electrical evocation requires much more energy than for example\nfire and therefore a single electrical bolt requires much more energy than a fireball. This however is made up for by the fact the lightning bolt is somewhat equal in power to the two fireballs which could be made in the same time period.\nStrength\nAn electrical evocationist is capable of producing powerful electrical bolts\nBolts may travel from any point to point with speed and reliable accuracy.\nWeakneses\nElectrical evocation takes a greater amount of time to produce a bolt\nthan other types of evocation\nElectrical evocation is dangerous to learn and during some phases of learning the mage can be incapable of producing any spark which will not injure themselves.\nProcess\nReaching Tier 1:\nWhen you begin to learn magic, you will start a Tier 1. At that point in time, you are unable to cast any form of magic unless you have some sort of experience and have connected to the void.At this tier you will learn\nhow to connect to the void, and then research electricity as an element itself. Connecting to the void will take perhaps even years of practice, and once completed,you may still have some difficulty. Researching electricity would consist of practically\nfinding any sort of detailand then taking note of it.\nReaching Tier 2: \nAfter their advancement from tier 1, and their connection to the void, they can now create a multitude of sparks and perhaps an even minor bolt,albeit difficult to\ncontrol till towards the end of Tier 2.  Even though they can create sparks, users at this tier may have an overload in which the sparks will practically burst outwards towards the conjurer.In this tier they will need heavy loads of practice in order\nto become more proficient with a minor bolt.\nReaching Tier 3:\nIn this tier they can finally create a full powered bolt withought major troubles, and have full proficiency. At this point they can now create streams of electricity,\nthough they will simply spark and singethe target, rather then cause major damage. With this tier, they are novice mages. \nReaching Tier 4:\nNow, the electrical evocation users can create the \"call-down\"of electricity, aka a bolt from a high point\nin the sky. They can create multiple bolts in a shorter time, although a fire evocationist could create fireballs in an even shorter time.The call-down is not very proficient, and will rarely land on the user's target.  In this tier,they can create great\nstreams of electricity that will do some good damage (burns, etc.) They are very proficient with the bolts now.\nFor more information go to this link, there is the same info + RP guide:\nhttp://www.lordofthecraft.net/topic/88498-improved-electricity-guide/", ""),
        StaticBook("Elem. Alchemy", "Rosso", "The Tales of a Travelling Alchemist\n------------\nElements of Alchemy\n\nVolume I-2 of V\nThe Elements:\n--------\nFire\n--\nEarth\n--\nWater\n--\nAir\nSkeptics often approach me with a wholly ignorant conundrum, and that is “how can you trace every spell and element back to these four basic elements.” But what they do not realize is that an understanding of what is meant by these four elements is\nrequired before that question can be answered and in fact, if that understanding is acquired then this question will never be asked.\n\nThese four basic, rudimentary elements, Fire, Earth, Water, and Air, are what every potion, oil, elixir, and\nconcept, in Alchemy of course, is based upon. An ignorant outlook on this statement is that what is meant is the physical, literal meaning behind these elements but one must look into the symbolism, they must look deeper than the surface. I shall go into\neach of these elements in detail, so that you, and budding alchemist or simply a well-read individual, may understand how Air may both aid someone’s speed, as well as their perception of their surroundings.\nFire\n===\nThe Destroyer, the Unmaker, the Cleanser.\nWe will begin with one of the most rudimentary and used element, Fire. Fire can represent many a feeling, action, and state and because of this, it is often one of the most useful elements of the Alchemist’s arsenal. Fire can represent rage, anger,\nhatred, as well as bravery, courage, and gusto. Through this a brew can be crafted to make someone unquestionably and savagely furious, but it could also craft a brew to strengthen one’s will, and allow them to do what other men would shrink away in fear\nat. These feelings, these emotions can be invoked by the element of Fire within a potion, but feelings are not the only thing that fire can produce, actions are another.\nActions are often the most recognized aspect of fire, and by this I mean the action\nof burning, consuming, and destroying. Alchemist’s Fire, a handy inferno in a bottle, is an example of this aspect of Fire, for within it is the action of destruction. This action can be further expanded upon with burning oil placed upon a weapon, but if\none were to use this example they would also have to include the element of pain, another feeling that fire an invoke. State is aspect that Fire can take one within an alchemist’s potion and this is often represented as Chaos. It is true that Chaos is\noften something alchemist’s fear, for it is something athat often ruins a potion, but it is yet another aspect of Fire that must be recognized. Chaos, being the state that it is, may seem like it has little place in a potion but brilliant minds and\npowerful reason can bring it to use just the same as the first farmer realized a stone and a stick, two completely different objects, could help them till their fields by putting them together. As this is not a book on the philosophy of alchemy, or\nsolely on the element of fire, I will not go into depth on how Chaos can be used. The teacher must leave something for the student to ponder.\nEarth\n===\nThe Enduring, the Lifegiver, the Fortifying\nWith the conclusion of Fire, the other elements will not have as long as description for most of the fundamentals of the elements are covered in how they can represent different things, I will simply go over what they may represent, starting with Earth.\nEarth is a truly powerful element for it may represent metals, strength, the notion of being stalwart, solidity, firmness, flora, animals, and countless other, quite obvious, subjects. Earth is often used for potions that increase one’s endurance, or\nstrength, and it is a must in potions that toughen one’s skin. In fact, a strong series of representations of Earth are required to perfect a barksin, or stoneskin potion. Protecting oneself is not the only use for the element of Earth, for it is also\nused in antidote potions, disease-curing potions, and, of course, fertilizers. Antidotes use this element for it can represent animals, and among those elements are snakes and spiders, often associated with poison. Of course a symbol of Water is also\nrequired for a proper antidote, but this will be addressed later on. Many of the uses of the element of Earth are quite obvious, but a always, if one wishes to master the field of Alchemy they must learn creativity is their greatest friend, and using\nelements in odd and interesting ways can be useful, and quite detrimental, in numerous ways. A final note on the element of Earth is how it is associated with the fable of Transmutation. Now, as a scholarly and skeptic individual, I have doubts upon\ntransmutation, its existence, and possibility. This will be described more in depth, but know that the element of Earth is the greatly represented by metals, for metals are merely ores in their purest forms.\nWater\n===\nThe Base, the Purifier, the Healer.\nWater is the element that seems to get the most amount of use due to how it is a base for many a potion and it is true, for if someone wants a liquid spell they want to use the Element of Water. Often known as the “base” element, it truly lives up to its\nname for observations, and personal experience, lead all to believe it is necessary for life. This base element, is often associated with flowing, liquids, balance, peace, calm, order, life, and rebirth. One requires water for any potion that one plans on\ndrinking, and any oil that one plans on applying for to have a liquid, one must use the Element of Water. Now that and understanding on how Water is a base, we must go into how it is used beyond simply supporting the other elements.\nWater’s uses are varied, for it can be used both in antidote as well as poisons, showing that it is quite the versatile element. One may also use it to create a potion of calmness, or perhaps a potion of healing due to its association with life. But one\ncan also use this beautiful element in the creation of an oil to coat a weapon, or to coat and strengthen armor. This is not the same as enchanting armor or weaponry, mind you, for doing that is often permanent and requires magic. Through oils, one may\nreap similar benefits of enchantment but instead it is only temporary and anyone with basic sense can apply them. The purest base, and often representation of water, is Aqua Vitae or “Water of Life,” which is best made by distilling wine or other liquors.\nAir\n===\nThe Nimble, the Traveller, the All-Seeing.\nOur final element, the element of Air, is not the least by any stretch of imagination but is often the hardest one to put into representation and use in a potion. Now this element is often associated with agility, quickness, travel, feet, perception, and\neven flight, it can be quite difficult to embody the element of Air into a physical item due to our basic fault of lacking understanding of what we cannot see. But with reason and the opening of one’s eyes, the ways in which to represent Air are quite\nobvious in our everyday world.\nItems that can be used to represent air, and subsequently put through your tools to produce a potion, are rather easy to find during your average day but of course, as with all the elements, purer ingredients are often quite\nrarer. One representation that you may have already thought of is a mere feather, which is often the most common representation of Air. This, of course, is not the purest representation of the element but it will often due for your more basic potions\ncentered around this element. Another, more outlandish representation, are rabbits’ feet. Rabbits are often seen as quick and agile critters, and as Air takes on the aspect of agility and quickness, it becomes quite obvious how the feet of a rabbit and\nAir intermingle. With that said, it becomes rather easy to find out representations of Air through simply looking and observing the world around you. But do not fret if you are still hard-pressed to find these symbols, the next chapter will explain\nherbs that will best aid you in the process of finding symbols for all the elements.\nThe Tales of the Traveling Alchemist, Vol I-2\n\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Elemental Thiik", "Anonymous", "Thiik  \n\n        Terra\n\nTerra is one of the most commonly used of the Thiik within the Dialect of the Elements. Representing the firm, unmoving Land beneath our feet some of the longest lasting Thiik are Terra Runes.\nBenefits\n\nThe positives of Terra runes are many as they can be used to do anything from fix an item to the ground or add reinforcement for support of Carved structures. Many of our halls boast these Thiik along the walls.\nDrawbacks\n\nTerra Thiik have issues due to the fact that Stone is naturally abrasive to suggestion. Due to this it's impossible to really summon stone or move it signifigantly or in large portions with the Terra symbol. It can be used to modify\nexisting Stone and Land near it, however.\nCreation\n\n*Outlined here is a symbol painstakingly drawn in Ink. It seems to be somewhat circular in shape but rough on the outline.*\nIgni\n\nThe rune of Fire this is perhaps one of the most useful of the base runes. Fire, being free willed, is open to suggestion. Be warned however! Fire always needs a source, and if you fail to provide... it will draw\nfrom you! Caution, young smith!\nBenefits\n\nIgni is commonly used around forges and for weapons due to it's useful nature. Some of the greatest forges of the Great Hall bear Ograhad's own Igni and are thus able to forge metals that we could not previously\nreach a melting point of.\nDrawbacks\n\nFire is hard to control by nature and as such demonstrates it when you attempt to force it into particular functions. It will fight the entire time and may even cause signifigant damage if you attempt to force it to hold back too much\nAs stated before, be wary that you do not overload the Heart rune or it will begin to draw it's toll from you, the Original creator of the Ruhn. This is a swift death.\nCreation\n\n*An upsidedown triangle is drawn here, the sides seem rough and somewhat uneven but it was obviously drawn very precisely.*\nWulgim\n\nThe Ruhn of Wulgim is one of the more subtle of the Elemental Dialect. Wulgim at it's heart isn't something that causes Khrum to shake in their boots. It has it's uses and I have seen many clever Thinkadre using this in\nKadrel to cool Stailininn quicker, as well as power wheels to stoke a furnace effortlessly.\nBenefits\n\nWuglim has many smaller uses over the obvious of Igni or Kaas but is no less powerful than either. Often used in ports or in Kadrel it's become something of a symbol for clever thinking amonst Thinkadre.\nDrawbacks\n\nMuch less than the previous, Wuglim does things in a subtle way and therefore doesn't draw too much energy when it does so or have the potential for sudden death. The only drawback to this Ruhn is while it can effect bodies of\nWuglim it has a certain limit - the more desired to be effected will draw more Manok than Amoruk can handle and will do the same as Igni - Draw Manok from your Anym.\nCreation\n\n*Carefully drawn here is something of a 'I' but the middle seems to be broken so the two halves aren't bridged.*\nKaas\n\nKaas is another subtle of the Elemental Ruhn but can be used in big ways... Although be cautious young Thinkadre, Kaas does not take so kindly to being forced to tasks. Much like Karaad in manners Kaas is a bit more violent\nin it's escapades for freedom. Some more foolhardy Dwedmar have found themselves suddenly caught in a whirlwind summoned before them and it has been the death of many good Thin'kadre.\nBenefits\n\nKaas is a strange Ruhn, it can manipulate Kaas around it or even summon more... but it comes at a heavy risk. Kaas manipulated must be consistantly manipulated - If you were to break a Kaas rune all the Kaas\nit has touched will lash out violently and instantly. Do not leave these Ruhn active for long. However, Kaas can be used for long-distance travelling and barriers - it is a potent tool for combat.\nDrawbacks\n\nAs stated, Kaas is violent when released and summoned Kaas is hard if not impossible to control. Sudden winds inside of caverns can be deadly... or Kaas can receed entirely, leaving a foolhardy Dwed dead in\nthe most painful of ways. Use caution with this Ruhn young Kadre'ruhn.\nCreation\n\n*A diagonal U is written here, with a slight extention on the bottom of the arch.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Elements of Mind", "Aris", "Elements of Mind\n           /\\\n         /\\ /\\\n         ><  ><\n         \\/ \\/\n           \\/\n     /\\         /\\\n     \\/         \\/\n\nThoughts on the mind and its most basic concepts.\n             Aris, 1461.\nEvery living being has a soul and a body, but what makes them unique, is their Mind. Mind itself is what defines you, and your actions. However, mind is different, it can be viewed in many ways, but it isn't as simply explained the body or a soul. But\nA simplistic way to explain would be this;\n If a being was a ship\n\n Your body would be the hull,\n\n Your soul would be the sails,\n\nBut the ship would never sail without its Captain, the Mind.\nAn example simple as that makes everything easier to understand, yet the Mind is more than that, a Mind can be described and divided in different ways. You can say a mind is inferior or superior, but you cannot say a mind is right or wrong. Continuing\nwith the same example from before, Mind, the Captain, can fit in three categories;\n  The Captain can be..\nCurious, jumping into adventure in search of answers.\nIntelligent, a person of logic and reason.\nKnowing, from experience and books\nCuriosity, Intelligence and Knowledge are the key points of the Mind, but ultimately, there is  Wisdom. Now, let me break down the four.\n\nCuriosity, the most innocent of the elements of mind for it is the base of all knowledge. A child is curious,\nbecause it is important and natural for them to gain experience from the world they have stepped their foot in. Curiosity is the desire, the craving to gain information or learn something. Curiosity is important to me, because it is what activates me,\nand more importantly, motivates me. It's very\nimportant for me to be\nopen to try new things\nand find out more, as there is an endless\namount of information.\n\nKnowledge is, in my opinion, the outcome of curiosity. It the term used for skills and\ninfromation gained via experience and / or education. Knowledge is something many seek, without truly knowing what they are looking for; knowledge isn't only facts laid out by letters in a book, but the prize of feeding one's curiosity for they can\nbecome truly aware of how things are. Knowledge covers familiarity, awareness and understanding of\nsomeone and something\nbut simply put, it doesn't mean you grasp the concept.\nOne can say they know\nor understand evocation, yet never be able to actually\nevoke a single droplet of water, a lone spark, or a tiny huff of wind.\nKnowledge is something\nthe mali'aheral, the High Elven, hold very dear. It could even be\ncalled the national\ntreasure of the race.\n \"Kae maehr evar\"\nKnowledge protects me\nCommon-\nphrase from the High Elven, is something that also fits me. Knowledge is what I seek, and something I already hold in some topics. It is also something that has saved me many times in seemingly helpless situations. For me, it is important to know the\nright people, and know\nthe right things. Knowledge is also the very reason I originally picked up\nthe graceful art of\nMental Magic, because for me, knowledge is a seemingly endless goal\nas new information keeps surfacing, and\nmental magic is inevitably\nthe door and also the key to new knowledge.\nBefore I started learning, it was a door\nthat remained locked for me, but now the door is opening to me\nagain, slowly, bit by bit.\n\nIntelligence, the ability to acquire and apply new information and knowledge.\nAn intellectual mind adds and overwrites\nold knowledge. You can not learn to become intelligent, for you are someone who can grasp concepts, or you will never be such.\nWhat makes intelligence different from knowledge, is that you\ncan be born\nintelligent, but you cannot be born knowledgeable. An intelligent person has great mental capacity for judgement, reasoning and logical thinking. A person that knows alot doesn't necessarily have all this, sadly, superior minds are often thought to be\nsly, only becasue they are vastly more intelligent than the\npeople around them.\nTo me, intelligence isn't something you can train, but something you do or do not have,\nshould it be the latter,\nI have trouble taking\nsuch people seriously.\n\nUltimately,\nWisdom is the prize of attaining the most of these three key elements of the mind.\nBecoming wise isn't something you can decide yourself, it is more like a title you\ngain from your surroundings. The Wise\nis intellectual, knowledgeable, yet still curious\nfor more. In my opinion wisdom is what an individual should truly\ntry to reach for, but\nmany are simply unfit.\nWisdom is the quality of having experience, vast amounts of knowledge, good judgement and logical thinking, and that isn't something you can\nattain within a short time frame; it is the\nultimate achievement.\nA wise person to me, is someone to look up to,\nand someone who should receive endless respect, but unfortunately the truly wise are scarce.\nThough, you can be wise without knowing\na lot, as the only true wisdom is in knowing you know nothing.. and one must beware of false knowledge for it is more dangerous than ignorance itself.\nThe path to wisdom is\nendless and eternal.\n------------------- \n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Elk Diary", "Elk Druid Tah'rayho", "14th of Sun's Smile\n\nI have overheard a few things from the hierophants. Alriel seems to have had a vision. They've sent off some of the birds to scout out the ocean around the city, and look over Tahn. I worry what they are keeping from me, and\nthe rest of the novice druids. We may not be old, but we can help, too!\n\nI can only imagine how bad it is for the dedicants.\n15th of Sun's Smile\n\nThe waters around the city are rising. Most of the citizenry are not too concerned, but I know something is afoot. Still, the elder druids refuse to tell me anything. It is deeply frustrating. I can see the scowls and the worry\nplastered on their faces!\n\n16th of Sun's Smile\n\nSome sort of creature has arrived in the city. I write this hurriedly. Already, we were so weak, I am not sure if we will be able to repulse it. This thing... the hierophants speak of it like it were a legend, but it is not one I have\never heard of. I can only imagine it has been scrubbed from history, if it is one.\n\nIt is the size of the sky, larger than the mother tree. Never have I seen such a monster before. When it speaks, even our most loyal animal kin, and the mother tree\nherself, have struck out against us.\n\nI worry. I go now, to fight with my brothers and sisters.\n26th of Sun's Smile\n\nAll is over. The dream of Malin is done. I have seen our future, and it is wooden.\n\nI... I am not sure what side to take. I do not want to die.\n\nI'm afraid.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elleonora App", "High Princess Awaiti Aureon", "Elleonora Caerme'onn's Qualifications for   -=- Lady Exarch -=-\n\n-Served in Sirame Order, knowing and enforcing the law at any opportunity.\n\n-Fluent in Orcish, Elven and Common.\n-Became a Druid.\n\n-Knows the Naelurir code and laws.\n\n-Unbias\n\n-Has served under Prince Khaine Csarathaire, as an advisor, assistant, herald, and diplomat for the dominion\n-Experienced with politics, as stated before, I have worked as a Diplomat for the Dominion under Prince Khaine's supervision.\n\n-Worked in the medical fields as well, with Morrigyn. \n\n-Steward for Caras Eldar.\n-Has partaken in Council meetings, and moots. \n\n-Knows the Dominion's code of law.\n\n-Always smiling : )\n\n-Doesn't enjoy using force or violence, but if necessary, she's been well trained\nby the Sirame order. She now sometimes trains the Virarim.", ""),
        StaticBook("ELLIE MUST WIN!!", "North Stow", "ELLIE UNDERTREE\n\nif she doesnt fucking win i swear", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Conundrum", "Commodus de Jedih", "The Library of Horen\nOpinions of the Throne holdupholdupcoutnmfg\n\nThe Elven Conundrum\n\nIssued and confirmed by His Majesty, Frederick I Pius, 8th of the Amber Cold, 1646.\n\n\nTranscribed by Comm.\nasdasdsadasdsadsad\nGreetings to the fair Human citizens of Marna, and Humans across Atlas, \n\nI, Frederick Pius, better known as “Mauer”, issue this document to the public in hopes of shedding light regarding the opinion of the Marnan Crown in this time of crisis.\nWe humans are mortals, destined to live for an allocated period of time A sliver in the lifespan of the other races.  For a single elf, twelve human generations may pass before they too meet their maker in the nether.\nHowever, the short time allocated unto humanity as part of the curse of Iblees has had the reverse intended effect. \n\nIblees hoped to corrupt humanity by making us mortal- an eternal punishment. Instead, this curse only made us stronger.\nIt made our peoples active, aspiring and thirsting for greatness. As such,  in the lifespan of one human, through their will, despite their lives being a mere sliver in time, the world could be changed forever for the good of humanity.\nHistory showed unto us the greatness of our third prophet, Godfrey, and his formation of Empire. We look to the deeds of Saint Peter, and how his order, alongside my ancestor, Horen the Black, sacked Malinor and brought humanity to the greatest power it -\nhad ever been. Thus, I must explain with absolute clarity, the graveness of the slight the Princess of the Dominion hath casted onto humanity.\n\nAccording to my wife, my dear queen Henrietta, her escort to the Elven coronation, and his Holiness himself,\nthe elves seek an empire under the name of the Dominion. This empire would hold the factions of all elf-kin, and, reportedly, the elf Princess proclaimed the that the world was to be guided under the Aspects.\n\nThis quest to spread Aspectism -\nglobally poses a major threat to Canonism and all the faithful upon Atlas. The Aspects, or spirits, as prescribed by the Exalted Owyn, are a paganic entity which elves falsely follow. Elves claim that they are real, and physical, which I've no doubt to -\nbe true.  However, GOD too, is real. These aspects are not omnipotent, they are not omnipresent. They are deceivers, and should be treated akin to that of Iblees. And though the Dominion may permit the establishment of a Church, as stated by Prince -\nKhaine, I trust in the words of his female diplomat moreso. The elves are guided by the aspects, and will never under any circumstance convert.\n\nThis sickens me, for I am not only the Apostolic king, but also a direct descendent of Horen.\nThe title of 'Emperor' is reserved for humanity and the heirs of the Prophets. Those who were not of Horen blood yet ruled over the empire of men did such only on the blessings of House Horen  as seen with Emperor Peter the Kaedreni being appointed-\nby the spirit of the Prophet Godfrey. Empires that did not receive this blessing were crushed by those who shared the ideals of Horen. \n\nLet us not forget that before the Prophet Godfrey, the elves were the dominant faction on this plane.\nIt was only humanity that had the metaphorical grapes to seize freedom from elfen-kin. Horen blood is divine, by right, and to even consider challenging the title of Empire before those of Horen and humanity is a slap in the face, if not a stab in the -\ngut. \n\nThus, I proclaim any attempt by the dominion to centralize and formulate a unified elven empire to be an immediate threat to the Canonist Faith, the Nations of Humanity,\nand, most importantly, Humans everywhere.\nThough they may act as pacifists today, once they grow confident, they will demand our conversion and territory tomorrow. If they seek peace, they MUST admonish their quest and rescind the goals of their Princess.\nTo offset this centralization, I also call for an IMMEDIATE convening of the leaders of mankind to join blades in the formation of the COMMONWEALTH OF MAN. The time for a Human Empire has not come, nay, but unity in some capacity has. GOD wills it.\nGOD With Us,\n\nHis Majesty, Frederick Pius of Marna, Apostolic King of Marna, Rhodesia and Waldenia, Duke of Senntisten and Defender of Rhodesia and the Faith, Brother of Saint Lucien\ndfasfdsfsfdsfdsdsfff", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 1", "Arinislia", "Elven Lessons\n\nOriginally By:\n\nKalenz Uradir\n\nRescribed after the burning of the Eternal Library by:\n\nArinislia\nIn Elven, grammatical structure is often different to that of common. For one, instead of placing an adjective before a noun, it is placed after said noun. This becomes particularly important for the most basic of greetings.\nKarin’alya-Goodday\nKer’ayla – Goodnight\nVan’ayla –Goodbye\nEach places the time of day before the adjectives describing it. Noun adjective are separated by an apostrophe.\nOther important words of the beginner in Elven include race names:\nMali-Elf\nUruk- Orc\nValah-Human\nBortu-Dwarf\n\nIn order to form sub-races of Elves, adjectives are taken to add more detail to the word Mali.\nWood Elf-Mali’ame\nHigh Elf-Mali’aheral\nDark Elf-Mali’ker\n\nIn order to form sub-races of other cultures, the suffix tali- may be used. This word directly means ‘part of’.\nGoblin-Tali’uruk (Lit: Part Orc)\nHalfing-Tali’valah (Lit: Part Human)\n\nOther basic phrases include exclamations, including:\n\nGood-Ayla\nBrilliant-Sul’leyun (Lit: Beautiful Light)", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 2", "Arinislia", "Elven Lessons 2\n\nOriginally By:\n\nKalenz Uradir\n\nRescribed after the burning of the Eternal Library by:\n\nArinislia\nJust as in common, pronouns may be used to replace nouns. The pronouns in Elven are as follows:\n\nKae-Me\nNae-You\nLae-He/Him\nHae- She/Her\nLye-We\n(used to speak of Elves, people, or\nworld)\n\nfor example, the sentence 'elvulnir van ayla' (The trickster fared well) may be transformed into 'Lae van ayla' (he fared well).\n\nIn addition to this, other good languages supplements to\nanyone learning Elven include basic affixes. These affixes may be added to create further detail of form critical grammatical structures in a sentence. The dash denotes location of a seed word. Affixes and seed words are seperated by an apostrophe.\nac-(aca-) - Honorific for accursedness\n\nah-(ahe-) Honorific for reverence. Often used as a prefix for scholar.\nEx.: Ah'Lucion\n\nfi- New or anew\ncer- (Slang from Ceru) -Honorific for strength. Often used as a prefix for those of high military rank. Ex. : Cer'Silir\n\n-ante (-nte) - Last\n\n-ento (-nto) - Next\n\n-onn - from or born\nu- - Or\n\nvul- (cule) - Clever or deceptive\n\n-ir -purpose\n\n-sae - The spreading, development, or management\n\n-ii - deminuitive form\nAs always, a full list of affixes may be found in the Elven Dictionary.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 3", "Arinislia", "Elven Lessons 3\n\nOriginally By: \nKalenz Unradir\n\nRescribed after the burning of the Eternal Library by: \n\nArinislia\nTo conjugate verbs in elven, one must note precisely what person is being referred to in the sentence. Then the verb is conjugated: \n\n-e - 1st sing\n\n-a - 2nd sing\n\n-e - 3rd sing\n-ae - 1st pl\n\n-an - 2nd pl\n\n-eyae - 3rd pl\n\nTo create past and future tenses is quite simply in elven. However, it takes specific forms depending on the time of day.\nFor these two tenses, the following four words are used:\n\nKarin'ento- Next sunrise\n\nKarin'ante- Last sunrise\n\nKer'ento- Next sunset\nKer'ante- Last sunset\n\nIf it is night at the time the elf refers to the past or present, the two forms with the 'Ker' are used. If it is day at the time the elf refers to the past or present, the two forms with 'Karin' are used. These endings are\nsimply added on the end of sentences to designate the tense. Ex. : Kalenz iyathe (Kalenz thinks) becomes Kalenz iyathe ker'ante (Kalenz thought). Assuming the time in which it is spoken is the night.\nIn spoken elven, particularly more casual speech, these endings are often shortened into the slang of karinto, karinte, keno, and kente.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 4", "Arinislia", "Elven Lessons 4\n\nOriginally By :Kalenz Uradir. Rescribed by: [Ghost] The Eternal Librarien.\n\nRescribed once more after the burning of the Eternal Library by: \n\nArinislia\nIn elven, numbers are formed by the compostition of multiple words. Each word representing the magnitude of the number. To note a number between one to ten, the simple word in elven to use. The express a multiple of ten, an elven number is placed before\na multiple of ten. For example: niut'matelu means 200.\n\n1- cem\n2-niut\n3-hael\n4-vailu\n5-kulin\n6-banih\n7-laier\n8-esun\n9-moiel\n10-telu\n100-matelu\n1000-marmatelu\n\nAnother particularly useful prefix not mentioned before is 'fer'. Fer is used in combination with seed words for form the names of handheld tools.\nSome such examples include those below. However, to those more advanced in elven, others may be thought up. \n\nFer'ame- axe\nFer'thuln- pickaxe\nFer'nor- shovel\nFer'sul -torch\nFer'bilok- hammer\nFer'norsae- hoe", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons 5", "Arinislia", "Elven Lessons 5\n\nOriginally by: Kalenz Uradir. Rescribed by: [Ghost] The Eternal Librarian.\n\nRescribed after the burning of the Eternal Library by:\n\nArinislia\nIn elven. In order to denote affiliation, the suffix -leh is used. It is placed after the object and designates the possession of said object by the subject of the sentence. However, it also has a use when no object in the sentence can be found and means\nin such a case 'spirit'. this also contributes to the common farewell blessing \"kaenan'leh evareh\" which means \"may it protect us\".\n\nIt is also worth learning the 'operative' which is also seen in the sentence above on in\nword 'evareh'. In elven, it serves the purpose of turning a verb into a wish. It is conjugated as below:\n\n-eh -operative sing.\n-erih-operative pl.\n(-arih if the verb ends in -ar)", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons I", "Kalenz Uradir", "New Elven\n      Lessons:\n     Volume 1\n\n   by Kalenz Uradir\nIn Elven grammatical structure is often different to that of Common. For one instead of placing an adjective before a noun it is placed after said noun. This becomes particularly important for the most basic of greetings.\nKarin'ayla - Goodday\n\nKer'ayla - Goodnight\n\nVan'ayla - Goodbye\n\nEach places the time of day before the adjective describing it. Noun and adjective are separated by an apostrophe.\nOther important words of the beginner in Elven include race names:\n\nMali - Elf\n\nUruk - Orc\n\nValah - Human\n\nBortu - Dwarf\nIn order to form sub-races of Elves, adjectives are taken to add more detail to the word Mali.\n\nMali'ame - Wood Elf\n\nMali'aheral - High Elf\n\nMali'ker - Dark Elf\nIn order to form sub-races of other cumtures the suffix tali- may be used. This word most directly means 'part of'.\n\nTali'uruk - Goblin \n(Lit: Part Orc)\n\nTali'valah - Halfling\n(Lit: Part Human)\nOther basic phrases include exclamations including:\n\nAyla - Good\n\nSul'leyun - Brilliant\n§i(Lit: Beautiful Light)", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons II", "Kalenz Uradir", "New Elven\n     Lessons:\n     Volume I\n\n  by Kalenz Uradir\nJust as in common, pronouns may be used to replace nouns. The pronouns in Elven are as follows:\n\nKae - Me\nNae - You\nLae - He/Him\nHae - She/Her\nLye - We (used to speak of Elves, people or world)\nFor example the sentence 'elvulnir van ayla' (The trickster fared well) may be transformed into 'Lae van ayla' (He fared well).\nIn addition to this, other good language supplements to anyone learning Elven include basic affixes. These affixes may be added to create further detail of form critical grammatical structures in a sentence.\nThe dash denotes location of seed word. Affixes and seed words are separated by an apostrophe.\n\nac- (aca-) - Honorific for accursedness\nah- (ahe-) - Honorific for reverence. Often used as a prefix for scholar. Ex.: Ah'Lucion\nfi- - New or anew\ncer- (Slang from Ceru) - Honorific for strength. Often used as a prefix for those of a high military rank. Ex.: Cer'Silir\n-ante (-nte) - Last\n-ento (-nto) - Next\n-onn - From or born\nu- - Or\nvul- (cule) - Clever or deceptive\n-ir - purpose\n-sae - The spreading, develpment or management\n-ii - diminuitive form\n\nAs always, a full list of affixes may be found in the Elven Dictionary.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons IV", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "New Elven Lessons:\n     Volume 4\n\n   by Kalenz Uradir\nIn elven, numbers are formed by the composition of multiple words. Each word representing the magnitude of the number. To note a number between one to ten the simple word in elven to use. To express a multiple of ten, an elven number is placed before\na multiple of ten.\n\nFor example: niut'matelu means 200.\n\n1 - oem\n2 - niut\n3 - hael\n4 - vailu\n5 - kulin\n6 - banih\n7 - laier\n8 - esun\n9 - moiel\n10 - telu\n100 - matelu\n1000 - marmatelu\n\nAnother particularly useful prefix not mentioned before is 'fer'. Fer is used in combination with seed words to form the names of handheld tools.\nSome such examples include those below. However, to those more advanced in elven others may be thought up. \n\nFer'ame - axe\nFer'thuln - pickaxe\nFer'nor - shovel\nFer'sul - torch\nFer'bilok - hammer\nFer'norsae - hoe", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Lessons V", "[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "New Elven Lessons:\n      Volume 5\n\n   by Kalenz Uradir\nIn elven in order to denote affiliation the suffix -leh is used. It is placed after the object and designates the possession of said object by the subject of the sentence. However, it also has a use when no object in the sentence can be found and\nmeans in such a case 'spirit'. This also contributes to the common farewell blessing \"kaean'leh evareh\" which means \"may it protect us\". \n\nIt is also worth learning the 'operative' which is also seen in the sentence above on in\nword 'evareh' . In elven it serves the purpose of turning a verb into a wish. It is conjugated as below:\n\n-eh - operative sing.\n-erih - operative pl. (-arih if the verb ends in -ar)", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven LessonsIII", "Kalenz Uradir", "New Elven\n     Lessons:\n     Volume 3\n\n   by Kalenz Uradir\nTo conjugate verbs in elven one must note precisely what person is being referred to in the sentence. Then the verb is conjugated:\n-e - 1st sing\n-a - 2nd sing\n-e - 3rd sing\n-ae - 1st pl\n-an - 2nd pl\n-eyae - 3rd pl\nTo create past and future tenses is quite simple in elven. However, it takes specific forms depending on the time of day. For these two tenses the following four words are used:\nKarin'ento - Next sunrise\n\nKarin'ante - Last sunrise\n\nKer'ento - Next sunset\n\nKer'ante - Last sunset\nIf it is night at the time the elf refers to the past or present the two forms with the 'Ker' are used. If it is day at the time the elf refers to the past or present the two forms with 'Karin' are used. These endings are simply added on to the end\nof sentences to designate the tense. \n\nEx.: Kalenz iyathe (Kalenz thinks) becomes Kalenz iyathe ker'ante (Kalenz thought). Assuming the time in which it is spoken is the night.\nIn spoken elven, particularly more casual speech these endings are often shortened into the slang of karinto, karinte, keno and kente.", ""),
        StaticBook("Encantry", "Aeluin Tundrak", "The Enchantery Defence:\n\nFacing SW; A 5m.x4m. metal barred gate closed at front. Only one gate.\nFacing S; A single, small watch tower, narrow sight, moreso toward the east of the walls.\nFacing SE; Two watchtowers of greater quality flank-\neither side of a smaller, 3x4 iron gate entrance. There are two gates.\nFacing the NE; A castle of larger towers hugs the wall, making a part of it. Poor defence.\nFacing NW; One large, short but wide tower.\nAll walls are edged in curtains.\nNote: Replace 'N' With S' and vice-versa.\n\nNote: A weakness in defense. Branches allow entry into their forts. A high climb, and steep jump, though. Through the North side.", ""),
        StaticBook("Enchanting", "[Ivae'Fenn Guard] Lady Nessa Anarion", "((I'm a tad bit too lazy to actually write anything in here, but this is a link to the \"book\" just type it in))\n\nhttp://tinyurl.com/oz9bvn8\n\nOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO", ""),
        StaticBook("Enchanting", "Lefkos Glowsbane", "Efficiency:\nEfficiency is one of the quickest and easiest of all of the enchantments to make. The purpose of this is to make any desired tool do its job faster. Using it, you may find that your pickaxe digs through stone like a knife through butter, or an\naxe may fell a tree in one or two swings. Even though it may be a cheap enchantment, it remains one of the most well known and used.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        ---------                ----x----                ---x-x---                ----x----\nUnbreaking:\nThis would probably be the second most used enchant, its purpose rather simple and self explanatory. I will review it anyway. Unbreaking is meant to make your tools harder and stronger. Tougher to break. Using it, you may notice that tools\nthat used to break after you use them for a while may still be functional. Its another easy enchantment that wouldnt cost to much to purchase.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        ---------                -x-x-x-x-                --x---x--                -x-x-x-x-\nSharpness:\nThis is a rather difficult enchantment, much to hard for a novice to make, and a rather expensive one as well. With this enchantment, you may find that your swords cut through bodys easier, making your opponents fall before your blade.\nThose that seek out an enchanter for this enchantment are normally guards, or people about to go to war.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        --x------                xxxxxxxx-                xxxxxxxxx                --x------\nPower:\nAn enchantment similar to sharpness, but for a different item. Power is made for bows, and when using it, you may find arrows you shoot from your bow hitting harder, enough to crack stone and injure your opponent more then a normal arrow. Only\nProffesional marksmen and archers will seak out this enchantment.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        xx----x--                --xxxxxx-                --xxxxxxx                xx----x--\nFire Aspect:\nOne of the oldest and harder enchantments to master. Many seek this enchantment on their blades for its usefullness. It is a must have for armies and a hard level enchantment. Adventurers and high ranking officers may seek out an enchanter\ncapable of this for their army. Fire aspect gives your blade an arcane power that, upon cutting any living creature, will set them aflame. Its thought of as a brutal but useful enchantment.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        -x-x-x-x-                -x-x-x-x-                -x-x-x-x-                -xxxxxxx-\nFlame:\nVery similar to Fire Aspect, Flame is another hard level enchantment. It lets your arrows catch fire, and burn whatever they hit.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        x--x--x-x                -xxxx-x-x                x--x--x-x                ------xxx\nKnockback:\nOne of the best enchantments in my opinion, knockback is sure to prove useful to anyone, no matter who they are fighting. This enchantment, rather then strengthening the actual blade, strengthens the arm holding the blade.\nIt is called \"Knockback\" because at that point, if you hit someone with your arm at full force, you possess the strength to send them flying back. Combine this with Fire aspect and you can shoot little fireballs called 'your opponent.'\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-         --xx-----                --xxxxx--                --xxxxx--                --xx-----\nProtection:\nOne of the less common used enchantments, but more useful. Protection was made to make your armor harder, so an arrow that would once pierce your heart wouldnt even reach it. The only reason it isnt commonly used is because not many\npeople have the time to wait for their armor to be enchanted.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-         --xxxxx--                --xxxxx--                --xxxxx--                ---xxx---\nFeather falling:\nA rarely used enchant. Infact, not a single person has asked me for it. I will put it here anyways. Feather falling increases the strength of your feet in terms of impact for the ground. Normally if you would barely survive after a 10\nmeter drop, you would be fine for this handy enchantment. Most people under value this enchantment, until they slip and fall!\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-         -----xx--                ----xxx--                ----xx---                ---x-----", ""),
        StaticBook("Enchanting", "The Unknown Sorcerer", "Transfiguration; The Utility magic\n\nBook Two - Enchanting\n\nWritten by an unknown mage and translated by Sarrion Zytiaear.\nEnchanting:\n\nThrough an alterationist’s power to manipulate mana, they become able to imbue magical properties on an item, so long as it is nonorganic or dead organic;\nthough some items allow for more potent enchantments, as well as more yield from the mana gem. The process of imbuing magical properties onto objects is dubbed enchanting by the practitioners and the folk who are able to get a hold\nof these magical items. This process is long and ritualistic, involving creating a magical program on the item, once this program is made, the user can either leave it at that - doing so will make it a one time only spell\n- or make a mana gem; the enchanter will need to take a gem of varying quality and fill it with mana. When the processes are done, the mage will have created their enchantment - items limitless in their creativity.\nImbuing the magical knowledge onto an item is the brunt of the field. This will require the enchanter to have knowledge of what they want to make, and this knowledge must be within the boundaries of voidal magic;\nthis is generally through actively practicing the magic, or by co-enchanting, and or using an entrapment; however these two require an understanding of the magic (mainly the core mechanic) they seek.\nBy co-enchanting, the enchanter must find another mage with the spell they wish to bind; a ritual will be conducted which involves using the aura as a means to track the mage’s mana, and acquire the information of the spell. From that point,\nthe enchanter must move that information on the object, effectively binding the magic to an item; now we move onto entrapments - these are items which are enchanted to store magical information, generally requiring another magi with the respective magic\nthe enchanter wishes to imbue. Similar to a co-enchanting ritual, another must be made, but this time the knowledge is scraped from their mana and placed within this item via a binding ritual; these items will typically\nrequire fuel to keep the information, more often than not keeping them bound to large mana gems and recharging said items before they reach their end. Only an enchanter can access and use their information via the same way they would with a partner.\nOnce whatever means is acquired to program the information on the enchantment, the user will now conduct another ritual where they write the enchantment’s program within the item -\nimbuing mana to sustain the information by binding it to the object and program; these programs are generally very limited and simplistic on their own, however the enchanter can weave two enchantments\ntogether via threading their magical beings together - allowing them to conduct more complex tasks. When an enchanter begins, the power of the item is rather simplistic,\nhowever - should they progress and achieve a greater understanding, the items will become more potent, but the more potent, the more fuel it will require.\nArguably, to have an efficient enchantment, one will require a greater means to fuel; enter the managem. The managem is a gem that contains mana inside of it, allowing it to fuel an enchantment once it is linked\nto the enchantment through threading the magical energies of the gem and the enchantment together; however this can only be done if the enchanter has full knowledge on the magical program that resides in the item.\nWhen it comes to how much fuel a mana gem can hold, and what constitutes is a mana gem varies far and wide; a gem can simply be a cut stone, or a flawless diamond; the more valuable the stone is, the greater amount of mana; the larger\nand more compact the stone the greater value it can hold. Notably, when a transfigurationist is of a higher tier, they will be able to store more mana within the managem without the worry of overfill -- the risk of a managem combusting --\nthe amount they can put it in must be within reason however, for enchantments are wondrous and formidable tools.\nThe states of Mana Gems:\n\nDiminished: The mana-gem is active and can be filled.\n\nNon-active: The mana-gem isn’t active, it has either lost all of it’s mana,\nor it has been hit with a powerful ward. The only way to reactivate it is to have an enchanter study the mana-gem, and reactivate it. This will require one to refuel it with mana, and will take some time to do.\nBroken: If the mana-gem is cracked severely, or is broken all together. When it is cracked severely, the mana will seep out much like a water spewed from a broken pipe;the shattered mana gem will create a small explosion,\ndoing little in harm and kinetic energy - more than likely burning skin ever so slightly if it's exposed.\n\nActive: The mana within is active, ready to be linked and used in an enchantment\nFinally, all the necessary requirements are finished,and the enchantment is now operating and able to be used. Enchantments go far and wide, from being something as combative as a staff that blasts fireballs,\nto an item such as a mirror that makes one look fat; it is up to the creativity is the user. There are two types of enchantments, ones that run constantly and others that are activated through a switch or command.\nWhen an enchantment is activated, there will more than likely be build up required for specific spells, generally requiring the same amount of actions as a standard spell, albeit minutely swifter due to the item not connecting to the void.", ""),
        StaticBook("ENLEEA", "Thurak'Yar", "Entities within our    \n\n   realm of Existence  \n\n   no Longer Existing,  \n\n   And Then Existing    \n\n   Again in a Form of   \n\n    Opaque Similarity.\nAKA\n  Void Translocation\n\n\n1. Introduction\n2. Study\n3. Sensory Overhaul\n4. Destruction\n5. Re-Creation\nIt does not take much searching within a library to gain some concepts of the Void as an alternate existence outside, within and with no relation at all to our reality. Arcanists, Mages, Sorcerers- whatever the name- users of voidal\nmagic pull a ‘thing’ into this realm that did not previously exist within it, and hold it there for as long as they can wield a void connection. But no ‘thing’ pulled from the void is retained here. Such power is reserved to The Creater to pull\nreal matter from The Void. But what if a ‘thing’ –be it inanimate, plant, animal, edible- already existed? Then the connection to The Void need only be instantaneous, because the ‘thing’ is not created, but simply IS.\nSTUDY\nTake within your hands something that exists.\nAny kind of thing will suffice and for the sake of example we shall call it and any potential other thing an ‘Entity’. Begin your examination in the simplest of interests: Form.\nWhat size is it?\nWhat’s it made of?\nHow heavy is it?\nHow malleable is the material?\nDoes it react to heat?\nWhat happens under great pressure?\nIf already you are struggling then you should return this book whence it came.\nSecondly you will need to form these observations into a mental map of the object. This is a far more complex procedure and verges on a particularly niche form of magic known as cognitism; however Telekinetics may find\nthemselves more easily inclined towards this type of thinking. You cannoy be bound by your perceptions in understanding the world. If you are purely an experiencer of your surroundings then you will never formulate any\ngreater understandings of anything ever. So work on that. If you are able to mentally comprehend the object beyond what is merely visible and physical and can mentally calculate the entity’s existence, then it is time to understand it magically.\nSensory Overhaul \nThere may be some slight overlapping of comprehending an entity scientifically through its calculable values and perceiving the entity’s magical value. Aside from universally shifting\nperspective with the aid of magic, the quantity of information required to mentally re-create the entity can be better fulfilled by magically understanding it. All things are magical. All things were originally pulled from a real in which is not\na single thing but the potential for all things. And thereby all things that exist are still magic. Perceiving magical value is a skill that requires much practise and isn’t really teachable as you either find yourself able to perceive the presence of\nmagic or not. Certainly with practise comes the strengthening of such a skill; but to attempt to explain to another how they are to ‘feel’ an apple tree from a dozen metres is (in almost all instances) utterly fruitless.\nThe complexities of such a thing all being laid down, what you do understand this entity in such a detailed way, you must measure its mana supply and sacrifice that same amount of your around; surrounding its attachment to the void\nwith your own so that the entity is no longer isolated in this world but, in losing its own link to The Void of its origin, becomes a part of ones’ self. The sliding scale of difficulty is seen here in that the more ‘alive’ an entity is, the more\nrapidly it produces mana. Anything that has a soul is independently existing within this realm and as a consequence produces and burns through mana with such a drastic suddenness that it would be impossible to balance that in any one instant.\nSoul-less entities then exist somewhere between a completely lifeless sliver of glass and a being with a soul. As mentioned the more ‘alive’ it is the more mana that will be present, and the briefer the instant at which one may be\nable to match said supply of mana before it shifts.\nNo Longer Existing\nEvoked magic automatically returns to The Void when a mage is no longer forcing it to exist in this realm. As it leaves this plane of existence it also ceases to exist itself on all planes. What once was\ntangible just stops and is no more.\nSo it can be in the reverse that something that DOES exist independently of a void connection can have that original connection from the moment of its diving creation re-instated, and\ntherefore able to return to the nothing from which it came. Within The Void there is potential floating around aimlessly. When it is given an aim through the use of Arcane Magics it is no more the potential of being something but becomes\nof itself a something for that fleeting moment. But without being birthed into existence by the creator it cannot remain as that. However entities that already exist are somewhat different. Though they cease to exist entirely,\nthere becomes a new potential within The Void that is assigned to being that entity.\nSo fear not that an entity which by your hand no longer exists may not be brought back into our reality as something temporary or destructive like\nan arcane missile or a shield of ice. For the potential of that thing has some divine marking upon it that keeps it sacredly linked to once again become what the Creator made it to be (or more accurately the way that it was, as a\nceramic teapot will not become a crude clay but remains a teapot).\nTo Return Again\nIt is a good thing that all those mental calculations were required to adequately assess the entity before it could be eradicated from reality; because that mental reconstruction of the\noriginal entity is the only thing that maintains it as something that ever existed. A sacrifice of identical mana to cover its original quantity so that a newly independent existence outside of The Void is made (I.e redoing the Creator’s work)\nwill assign the potential with its destined form. And the forgetting of such things means eternal damnation upon an entity that once existed in relative peace before you came along and destroyed it.\nGood job,\nYou meanie.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ent Legend", "birdwhisperer", "Foreword\n\nThis book is originally from Asulon, and was found in the Druid’s Grove of Elandriel. Its author is unknown, and it was brought to Anthos and preserved by Elorna Avern.\n ~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n The Legend of the\n           Ents\nThe Ents are mysterious creatures that were found within the forests of Aegis, and now in Asulon. Little is known about them, but they are often found near sacred groves or ancient trees, keeping them protected and free of disruption. But the tale of the\nfirst Ent is interesting in itself.\n\nIt is said that the Aspects granted ancient and wonderful power to a certain tree older than time itself. This tree, far wiser than the entire forest, yearned to protect his kind, but could not do much\nfrom within the confines of his roots. So, he waited for the stars to align, and produced a seed of gold, and let it fall to the foot of his gargantuan trunk to sprout.\n\nThrough the course of many moons, this seed grew until it became a\ntree half as large as its father. However, it found that its roots were not bound in the soil, and so it walked. It roamed the forest, finding purpose under the gentle guidance of the Eldertree. The Ent soon found humans attempting to fell an ancient oak,\nwhich cried out in agony. Letting out a roar, the great being assumed its role as guardian of the forest, and tore through the men with unforgiving vengeance. And such is the story of the first Ent.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ent Moot", "Hobbs_Burrows", "Dear reader,\n\nSince you seem to love books so much, I have decided to write another for you.\n\nAfter theft and destruction of valuable items from my grotto, the ents of the forest declared an Ent Moot to decide what action should be taken.\nAlderoot and Segovax, the two most senior Ents, agreed to retaliate with the forces of the forest and let nature reclaim the land from your evil.\n\nI tried to calm them down, but once an Ents mind is made up then you can't change it. They are also\nparticularly angered that evil deeds are being committed in their forest by yourselves, and they believe that evil deeds should have consequence. \n\nThey have told me that the forests will encroach upon the area surrounding your village regularly, until\nthe land has been spared from your evil. \n\nI am sorry it has come to this, I am not by nature a quarrelsome halfling, however myself, the Ents, and all friends of the forest have been left with no choice.\n\nYours,\nHobbs", ""),
