visible and physical and can mentally calculate the entity's existence, then it is time to understand it magically.\nSensory Overhaul\nThere may be some slight overlapping of comprehending an entity scientifically through its calculatable values and perceiving the entity's magical value. Aside from universally shifting perspective with the aid of magic, the quantity\nof information required to mentally re-create the entity can be better fulfilled by magically understanding it. All things are magical. All things were originally pulled from a realm in which is not a single thing but the potential for all things. And\nthereby all things that exisst are still magic. Perceiving magical value is a skill that requires much practice and isn't really teachable as you either find yourself able to perceive the presence of magic or not. Certainly with practice comes the\nstrengthening of such a skill; but to attempt to explain to another how they are to 'feel' a rosebush from a dozen metres is (in almost all instances) utterly fruitless.\nThe complexities of such a thing all being laid down, when you do understand this entity in such a detailed way, you must measure its mana supply and sacrifice that same amount of your around; surrounding its attachment to the void with your own so\nthat the entity is no longer isolated in this world but, in losing its own link to The Void of its origin, becomes a part of ones' self. The sliding scale of difficulty is seen here in that the more 'alive' an entity is, the more rapidly it produces mana.\nAnything that has a soul is independantly existing within this realm and as a consequence produces and burns through mana with such drastic suddenness that it would be impossible to balance that in any one instant. Soul-less entities then exist\nsomewhere between a completely lifeless sliver of glass and a being with a soul. As mentioned the more 'alive' it is the more mana that will be present, and the briefer the instant at which one may be able to match said supply of mana before it shifts.\nNo Longer Existing\nEvoked magic automatically returns to The Void when a mage is no longer forcing it to exist in this realm. As it leaves this plane of existance it also ceases to exist itself on all planes. What once was tangible just stops and is\nno more.\nSo it can be in the reverse that something that DOES exist independantly of a void connection can have that original connection from the moment of its divine creation re-instated, and therefore able to return to the nothing from which it came.\nWithin The Void there is potential floating around aimlessly. When it is given an aim through the use of Arcane Magics it is no more the potential of being something but becomes of itself a something for that fleeting moment. But without being birthed\ninto existence by the creator it cannot remain as that. However entities that already exist are somewhat different. Though they cease to exist entirely, there becomes a new potential within The Void that is assigned to being that entity.\nSo fear not that an entity which by your hand no longer exists may not be brought back into our reality as something temporary or destructive like an arcane missile or a shield of ice. For the potential of that thing has some divine marking upon it that\nkeeps it sacredly linked to once again become what The Creator made it to be (or more accurately the way that it was, as a ceramic teapot will not become crude clay but remains a teapot).\nTo Return Again\nIt is a good thing that all those mental calculations were required to adequately assess the entity before it could be eradicated from reality; because that mental reconstruction of the original entity is the only thing that\nmaintains it as something that ever existed. A sacrifice of identical mana to cover its original quantity so that a newly independant existence outside of The Void is made (i.e redoing Creator's work) will assign the potential with its destined form.\nAnd the forgetting of such things means eternal damnation upon an entity that once existed in relative peace before you came along and destroyed it.\n\nGood job, you meanie.", ""),
        StaticBook("Entry #2", "Cyrene", "15th of The Grand Harvest, 1693.\n\nI lost my home. I'm no longer leading sutica, nor am I a part of it. I let my fit of rage get the best of me, and I got people hurt because of it.  I attacked my own heir after stepping down-- her wife, too. Then I ran.\nAfter a few days of wandering the south, I read through my first journal entry before I recalled Karyssmov's existence. He was in the same situation I'm in. A leader run out of their own city, left with no home or family to turn to. Now, he was the one\nwho I had to turn to. So I did.\n\nHe found me far outside of Sutica  in a tree well, where he healed my wounds and spoke with me about my situation. Part of me no longer feared him or felt distaste, but trust and the feeling of empathy. I was in the same\nsituation he was in all those years ago, and he knew this. We both did. He took advantage of this.", ""),
        StaticBook("Entry 1", "Princess Cyrene", "10th of the Grand Harvest, 1682.\n\nThe square is empty today. It's been empty for the last few days, really. I'm unsure if it's just beginning to be that time again, or if it's only temporary. I'm worried, in any case. We've made enemies, despite my effort\nto remain the nation of neutrality. The Empire has attempted to take over our land, along with Gladewynn. I fear that after their war against the Coalition is done, they will return to us and continue their conquest of Atlas and any nation that isn't\ntheir own.\n\nThey want Sutica alive. Under them. Well, they used to. Now, they want to wipe out our citizenry and leaders and start anew. I'm not sure if it's worth it to keep fighting for it anymore. I tried, and I failed. I failed as a leader.\nWord says that Karyssmov is a known Naztherak user. He makes demons. They say he now leads a faction called Arberrang. Once a powerful holy leader, turned dark. I heard that he holds ill-will towards me when I first started leading Sutica, so I found him\nin Haense and spoke with him. This was before I knew what magics he was using. We left off on good terms, and I haven't seen him since. I wonder what he's up to.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ethros Goodbye", "Gray Kellian III", "My Dearest Elinor and Gray. I know I havent spoken to either of you in a long time.. \n\nBut I have some regrets on my mind I wish to expell, before my unavoidable death sometime in the future.\nFirstly, To My First, and only son Gray, I have so much I wanted to tell you, So much I wanted to do with you, Stuff a Father and son should have done together.\n\nBut with the death of your mother. Our lives were thrown into an unavoidable chaos.\nAnd that is where my first Regret Lies. As a man who as you know, lived with the rule of \"Live your life, without Regrets.\" This is hard to speak about.. but I know you will understand.\nI wish before you ran away, Before I couldent find you, Before I went mad.. I wish I could of been there for you. to help you through the pain in your heart, to help you ease the suffering of loseing a loved one,\nBut, I couldent. I failed as a father. In more ways than one *some tear marks can be seen present in the page* I always wanted to have a family, You and your sisters were the Greatest thing to happen to me. But I failed. and I am sorry.\nSecondly, I wanted to say just how proud I am of you. I know I do not have the right because I wasent there for you growing up. But I met some of your friends. Karyssmov is a good man, And I hope you continue your friendship tell the end of times.\n*more tear marks,* I also got to see You aswell one more Elinor. And to you, I have more regrets than anyone. I always wanted to see you grow up, to see you become the brilliant young woman you are now. *tears* I know your mother never told you who your\nreal father was. But I am able to tell you.\n\n*many scribbles can be seen as if he wrote something, before scratching it out, over, and over, and over again*\n*Blank page*\nIts me.\nI know it seems farfetched.. but it is true. After your mothers partner died, and After my wife died. We both were stricken with Greif, After I fled the city, your mother moved to Haria.. On one fateful night I went to meet her. And from that visit, You\nwere created. My Daughter. Your Mother was never able to remember, we both were highly intoxicated.. But when She found out she was having a baby, I knew it was mine. and this is my greatest Regret. I never told her nor you.\nBut I couldent.. I didn't have the courage, So I Just watched over you, poseing as your uncle, I came to see you everyday, I loved you.\n\nAnd thats when Your mother made Lilliana and Ed your godparents.\nI knew if anything ever happened you would go with them I fought with your mother to reconcider, to let you go with me instead of them. but after she died, Lilliana swept in and took you away before I had the chance to take you back, to be your father.\nAnd I was greif ridden, I lost yet another child. First Gray when he ran away. Then Leona the same way. And then you.. Taken away by people I trusted. taken by people who were not your blood. all because I didnt have the courage to speak up.\nAnd it drove my madness further. Until I broke, So please. Tell Archrim I am sorry for that day, And Tell Princess Lilyana I am sorry I betrayed her and left her side for madness. And most of all, I am sorry to you Elinor\nSo Please.. Forgive me,  *Tear marks*\n\nI am so sorry... I am a horrible father,  But I hope *Tear marks* If you can forgive me, you both can live on happily.. knowing you are close family than you thought\nLove,\n\n   Your Loving Father\n     Ethro Kellian II\n\n\n  Please remember me\nwithout hate. but with Love my children,\n\nThis is Goodbye", ""),
        StaticBook("Eulogy", "Aluatis Lorenthus", "=========================Eulogy to Taynei'Hiylu\nBy: Peurith\n=========================\nTranscribed by Peurith - Scribe of Malin.\nThe loss of the green one was hard for the King. He spent two years following in his chambers, murmuring of the deep earth. [Some of the text is too faded to read.] -ply in mourning.\nOur Dragon is not dead, but the truth-... [The rest of the text is worn away to time.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Evocation Basics", "Gerald Elgan", "===================\n                                                                                                  The Basics\n             Of                       Evocation\n\nTranscribed by\nGerald Elgan\n\n\n==================\nIn order for sorcerers to put into use their craft, they must have a deep attunement with and knowledge of their element. A caster must know that fire begins with friction and the many stones that make up the earth. A common rule of thumb is:\n\"If the Sorcerer does not know how something functions, he cannot make it work himself\" This simply dictates that a mage MUST know how water flows and how wind gusts, just as much as they must know how fire feels to touch. Due to this, sorcerers often\nspend a great deal of time in study, on a deep spiritual level, of their respective element(s). Despite this rigorous training, their spells may still deal them harm, just as much as it may harm their opponent.\nEvocation is often quite physically and mentally taxing on the Sorcerer- as it takes a great deal of mana to cast. The large the object one wishes to bring forth, the more mana is required of him to cast it. And just as any other magical branch of the\nArcane tree, the mage must be capable of envisioning where he is casting his spell, and at what - that he must first visualize the spell itself, in his own mind, in order to bring forth its full fury. Therefore, a mage cannot simply conjure a fireball\nbehind a wall, nor can he cause a wave of water to appear in an area so distant- so beyond the caster's field of vision. Due to this law, Sorcerers are limited in some regard- hindered by the reaches of their sight. Despite the seemingly passive nature\nthat any one mage may seem to possess, they however remain filthy abominations- dangerous and unholy grotesqueries- who must be taught that such profane powers can bring no good, and must be wholly forgotten, for the sake of every man, woman, and child-\nfor all who walk upon God's blessed earth.\n==================", ""),
        StaticBook("Evocation: Basic", "SerahLove", "In order for Sorcerers to put into use their craft, they must have a deep attunement with and knowledge of their element. A caster must know that fire begins with friction and the many stones that make up the earth. A common rule of thumb is:\n\"If the Sorcerer does not know how something functions, he cannot make it work himself.\" This simply dictates that a mage MUST know how water flows and how wind gusts, just as much as he must know how fire feels to the touch. Due to this, sorcerers often\nspend a great deal of time in study, on a deep spiritual level, of their respective element(s). Despite this rigorous training, their spells may still deal them harm, just as much as it may harm their opponent.\n\nEvocation is often quite physically and\nmentally taxing on the Sorcerer- as it takes a great deal of mana to cast. The larger the object one wishes to bring forth, the more mana is required of him to cast the spell. And just as any other magical branch of the arcane tree, the mage must be\ncapable of envisioning where he is casting, and at what- that he must first visualize the spell itself, in his own mind, in order to bring forth its full fury. Therefore, a mage cannot simply conjure a fireball behind a wall, nor can he cause a wave of\nwater to appear in an area so distant- so beyond the caster's field of vision. Due to this law, Sorcerers are limited in some regard- hindered by the reaches of their sight.\n\nDespite the seemingly passive nature that any one mage may seem to possess, they\nhowever remain filthy adominations- dangerous and unholy grotesqueries- who must be promptly taught that such profane powers can bring no good, and must be wholly forgotten, for the sake of every man, woman, and child- for all who walk upon God's blessed\nearth.\n\n\n    The Basics of Evocation\n\n\n\n\n\n              - Arthur Versluis\n\n   Revisions by E.S. and A.F.", ""),
        StaticBook("Execution Notes", "Frederick Kelly", "The Vinter's house - partial stone, partial wood. Inside's probably wooden too. A few firestarts can smoke him out. Back door and front door. Windows, but not too opportune for escape. Forced exit. Men stationed for both ends, easy killing.\nNeed to pay mind to the god damned town by the Vinter. Proximity's too narrow, feels like he raised the manor up near it for security. Job needs to be a quick bang-up. No imperfections.\n14th, S.M., 1697\nThe Blacksmiths' smithy. Two doors at the front, one around the back. Klara will need to be killed first, then Vincent and Raymond. Together (?). Heard rumors of their family, take them to a place of death on the preconception of heading back to the lands\nLeopold de Anjou, they await the wine, they shall die upon retrieving it. A bolt to the head at the smithy, or strangulation. Whatever truly comes first.\nClaus De Anjou. Must die before all the others, discipline must be made in a measure to seem compliant and not make the others aware of what happens.\n\n§", ""),
        StaticBook("Explosive Bolts", "Head Quartermaster", "Instructions for proper use of explosive ballista bolts:\n\nStep 1 – Preparing the bolt: Remove ONLY as many explosive belts as bolts you intend to prepare. Belts are NEVER to be left lying around. Wrap the belts around the bolts\nin the carved out section just behind the bolt’s head. BE SURE THE FUSE AND AUGERED FUSE HOLE LINE UP. Stick the fuse into the hole to where there is a decent bit left on the other side of the hole.\nThe hole will protect the fuse while it burns in flight and after impact. \n\nStep 2: To loose a bolt, crank back the ballista and lift the bolt put the bolt into the firing notch in the center of the ballista. Make sure the ballista’s rope is\nagainst the back of the bolt. Set your target, and just before loosing, fire the fuse. If done correctly, then the bolt will soar to the target, hit, then explode, causing catastrophic damage to a ship and its crew.\nPrecautions:\n\nFire or lighting implements are to be kept FAR from the belts while preparing ammunition. Any spark or fire can ignite the belts causing extensive damage.\n\nWater or drink should never be be left around\naround the bolts. If they get wet, they will be useless, and these things are expensive and hard to get.", ""),
        StaticBook("Eye Transplant", "Laurinia", "12th of The Amber Cold 1479\n\nI was walking down the stone road when i was approached by a man in long dark robes. He said he had watched me care for my blind partner Sarai and asked if i was interested in learning how to heal people.\nOf course i agree'd with him and so now i am in his office learning how to recconect nerves. Specifically i am learning to recconect nerves in the eyes.\nMy teacher constantly has his hood up not once yet have i seen his face. However i presume he is an\nelf as we practice on nature, animals, and he has two small points in his hood.\n\n11th Malins Welcome\n We've been going over simple things for a few days now... I can now confidently heal nerve endings back into a working condition.. All we need n\npair of eyes for Sarai, its just finding a volunteer\n\n7th First Seed 1480\nLast night we attacked our target.. A middle aged women in which we stole the eyes of... Eyes which will now haunt me for the rest of my life.. .The vibrant blue colour of\nstick with me and haunts me at night but they are soon to be my wifes. I guess over time ill adjust to them.\n\n13th First seed\nSarai can see it was a success", ""),
        StaticBook("Fables Vol. I", "Mhel Underson", "The Farmer and the Snake\n\nOne winter a Farmer found a snake, stiff and frozen from the cold, the farmer pitied the creature, taking it up into an embrace, the warmth quickly reviving the snake, it then acts upon its instincts and bites its benefactor.\ndealing the Farmer a mortal wound \"Oh\" cried the farmer with his final breaths \"I am rightly served for pitying a scoundrel\"\nThe Eagle and the Arrow\n\nAn Eagle was soaring through the air when suddenly it heard the whizz of an Arrow, and felt itself wounded.\nSlowly it fluttered down to the earth, with its life-blood pouring out of it.\nLooking down upon the Arrow with which it had been pierced, it found that the shaft of the arrow had been feathered with one of its own plumes.\n\"Alas!\" it cried, as it died: \"We often give our enemies the means of our own destruction.\"\nThe Fisherman and the Little Fish\n\nA Fisherman who lived on the produce of his nets, one day caught a single small fish as the result of his day's labor.\nThe fish, panting convulsively, thus entreated for his life: \"O Sir, what good can I be to you, and -\nhow little I am worth! I am not yet come to my full size. Pray spare my life, and put me back into the sea. I shall soon become a large fish, fit for the tables of the rich; and then you can catch me again, and make a handsome profit of me.\"\nThe Fisherman replied: \"I should be a very simple fellow, if I were to forego my certain gain for an uncertain profit.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Face in the Tree", "Elder Hobbs Burrows", "The sight you see before you might not seem shocking, but what if I told you this tree was once a man? \n\nYes, this man's name was Ioughu. He was passing through my grotto when he knocked on my door and asked if he could use the lake to fish. I left to\ntend to my mushrooms, and when I went outside to ask if he wanted a cup of tea I found this tree with the expression of Ioughu's face in the bark. \n\nI had felt some strange disturbances in this forest, and this has confirmed my worst fears. I feel that\nblack magic is at work here in these woods, and has finally reached this grotto. I wonder if nearby there is an evil wizard whose evil machinations are spilling over into the world of the good and fair. \n\nSo I warn you, traveller, keep your eyes peeled.\nIf you need reminding, just look at poor Ioughu!", ""),
        StaticBook("Fae Comp. I", "Seer Barley", "-- Book of the Fae\nby Seer Barley\n\nVol. I: Greater Fae\n\n*A sketch of a little fairy guy dons the first page.*\nThe Fae:\nJust beneath the status of the divine above, are the divine among us; The fairies, people of the Fae.\n\nThe Gallic Clan revere them as not only sacred symbols of the wild, but as objects of power in their rites of witchcraft.\nPacts with the fae are highly sought after, ranging from simply friendship with some, to stealing the power of others.\n\nIn times of late, due in no small part to the influence of the church, these ways are hardly known and not widespread among the Clan.\nChapter 1:\n- Greater Fae\n\n*A graceful woman holds her arms wide, exhuding a regal aura, as if some alien queen.*\nGreater Fae:\nBeings of unknown power who dwell within the Fae, to respected as divine beings themselves, capable of granting great boons to the most clever of seers, and curses to the unwise clansmen.\n- Wood Wose\nLittle is known of the Wood Wose, rumored to be the ancestors of Druids. They are seen as demigods amongst the realms, similar to a spirit, however bound to the fae rather than the mortal realm.\nTheir powers are unknowable and varied, and their gifts seldom seen, as they are said to traverse the realms in the shape of an unassuming beast, to watch over their progeny and old friends, at times serving as omens or messengers from beyond the veil.\nPact: To unlock the blessing of the ancestral Wood Wose, they must be discerned from their guise of an unassuming beast, and followed into their realm by some means of planar travel.\n\nThus, they are considered out-of-reach.\n- Draoichota / Leprechaun\nThe Draoichota and Leprechaun are mysterious beings indeed, said to hold the power to grant wishes and more.\nPerhaps they are powerful sorcerers of the Imp-Folk who have ascended to a state of nigh-divinity, or perhaps they are avatars of the Aspects’ children, as the Mani are.\nThey have been seen to bear powerful fae magic, and oftentimes come to our realm with purpose. In the past, they have been seen asking for favors in exchange for their magic.\nThe most recent written account tells of a Draoichota who attempted to persuade drunkards to steal an artifact from the hoard of Dragur, a fae blade that could poison any soul.\nDraoichota and Leprechaun are two titles of a similar fairie, with Draoichota, as its name implies, being considered an ill omen, and a Leprechaun being a symbol of great fortune and generosity.\nTo discern them from eachother is a great trial, as a Draoichota will feign as benign and offer just the same as a Leprechaun will.\nThe difference is often seen in the viciously clever wordplay of their requests, or when the guise is lifted and the Draoichota’s malice is suddenly revealed. It is said that neither can lie, so take great heed of the meaning of their words.\nDraoichota pact: To trick a Draoichota is a nigh-impossible venture, but it is said that they could somehow be fooled into using their powers on one’s behalf. Beware, however; They may not appreciate your wiles.\nLeprechaun pact: Unlike the Draoichota, it's said that Leprechauns are true to their word; If you serve them, they will grant you gifts. They are also said to be summoned after summer rains, and giving them gifts of gold may incline them to repay you.\n- Zhuanth\nA frightening, mysterious creature, believed to be the blessed children of Morrigan herself, who she trusts to weave the strands of fate that guide each soul until their eventual demise.\nThey are the sentient weavers that grasp each fairie’s soul when their time has finally come.\n\nThey are believed to have all manner of powers, from the ability to predict what is to come, to delaying one’s demise.\nLittle is truly known about them, as to mortals they do not often appear.\n\n*A sketch here depicts an ominous spider.*\nZhuanth pact: It is said that the Zhuanth are bound by a strange code to not interact with the living until the moments they perish, so to seek one would be harrowing indeed. One is said to be given an opportunity to barter with them with their last gasp.\nAppendix:\nVolumes in series --\nVol I: Greater Fae\nVol II: Fae Peoples\nVol III: Fae Creatures\nVol IV: Lesser Fae\nList of Fae --\nBogeyman: Vol III\nDraoichota: Vol I\nDryad: Vol II\nEnt: Vol III\nGremlin: Vol IV\nHarpies: Vol IV\nImps: Vol II\nKelpie: Vol III\nLeprechaun: Vol I\nMinotaur: Vol II\nSatyr: Vol II\nSelkie: Vol III\nSpriggan: Vol IV\nSprite: Vol IV\nSylvan: Vol II\nTreelord: Vol II\nUnicorn: Vol III\nVodnik: Vol IV\nWood Wose: Vol I\nZhuanth: Vol I", ""),
        StaticBook("Faith: Lucienism", "Pius", "Lucienism is a reform-oriented branch of the Orenic faith that identifies with the theology and teachings of High Pontiff Lucien I (Welyn Ashford). The High Pontiff Lucien's beliefs form the basis of the sect which seeks to adhere to reformed practises\nand ecclesiastical learnings of the Orenic church.\n\nLucienism follows five basic principles of belief (not necessarily of varying importance) somewhat distinct from the un-standardized and varying Orenic Theology.\n1) Belief.\nA follower must put his faith wholly in the Creator as the sole true God and by extention the High Pontiff. Contrary beliefs to the principles of lucienism must be removed like a malignant tumour - for surely if such a tumour was left to grow\nthe results would be most unfortunate. Lucienists are fervent in their beliefs and are often hard to convince and convert. Their primary tool for conversion is intellectualism and zealous missionary effort, but they have been known to use the sword if\nabsolutely necessary.\n\n2) Worship.\nThe one true God, Creator of the universe and of man, must be worshipped according to the clergy's set guidelines and methods. This includes attending holy sermons whenever possible (At least once an elven week) and\nprayer.\n\n3) Papal Authority and Infallibity.\nThe high Pontiff is the anointed of God and thus superior to all others living or dead*. As God's prophet on Anthos, he is infallible in every possible way and incapable of wrongdoing or ill acts. His authority\nis ever-reaching and binding to all who follow the Orenic faith and his will cannot be denied by any.\n\n4) The sanctity of marriage and appropriate gender laws.\nThe sanctity of marriage must never be disturbed. Violations of the sanctity of\nmarriage must never be disturbed. Violations of the sanctity of marriage can include but are not limited to:\n\n-Sexual or other carnal relations outside of marriage. (Offspring of these unions may also be considered violations.)\n-Sexual or other carnal relations with a nonhuman of the lowest degree such as a dark elf or orc.\n-Sexual or other carnal relations with a member of the same gender.\n-Adultery, impropriety and disloyalty to one's spouse.\n-Carnal thoughts such as the\ncoveting of another man's wife.\n\nWomen cannot hold clergy or chivalric titles or inherit landed titles unless no male alternative is avaible. Males, unless proved infirm and unable to inherit accordingly, always come first in the line of succession.\n5) Veneration of the Saints.\nIt is believed that those consecrated as saints are holy and exalted and as thus should be revered and spoken of in a light of praise and adoration. While they are of course second and inferior to God and his chosen, the High\nPontiff, each saint and their aspect can teach a valuble lesson about the ways of the world and theology in general.\n___________________\n\nThe theological concept also believes in sermons, prayers and masses being said in the vernacular. Violent heretics,\ngeneral nonbelievers, and sodomites must be punished accordingly for their most grievous crimes but also must be offered a single chance of recanting and pardon prior to their executions.\n\nThe violation of these five pillars or 'rules' is punished\naccording to the offense and for the judgement of the presiding clergyman, however the reformation preaches forgiveness for one's sins as long as they are not repeated.\n\nOther beliefs and doctrines of Lucienism include:\nThe Sinfulness of Idolatry: Idolatry is a sin and is absolutely heretical, promoting pagan ideologies. God is the only deity worthy of worship and the only deity - the worship of saints or their idols is strictly forbidden. It should be noted that this\ntakes primacy over pillar five - while saints can be venerated, anything bordering on idolatry is a grave sin.\n\nSacrilege: Sacrilege is a sin beyond no other sin and almost literally deadens the offender's soul. They are damned to burn in the fires of the\nstages of the nether. Sacrilege is when one harms a holy individual, clergymen or harms something of holy value - house of worship or a holy symbol.\n\nPapal Investiture: It is taught that only the High Pontiff has the right to allocate Bishops and\nArch-Bishops to their respective dioceses and archdioceses within the Holy Oren Empire. No secular titleholder can do this, no matter their rank.\n\nLay Preaching: While Lucienist clergy does definitely exist, it is taught that the word of the faith can be\nspread and preached by any, ordained or not. It is expected of all followers of the faith to spread it to any non-believers in order to enlighten them to the true religion.\n\nCrusades: The High Pontiff has the authority to call a crusade against a certain\nnation or organization. A crusade is essentially a holy war that anybody can partake in - it is said that those who volunteer to participate in a crusade have all their previous sins forgiven and will be rewarded with a just afterlife.\nThe Family of God: All who believe in the holy Lucienist faith are part of the family of God and the High Pontiff. The High Pontiff and the clergy is like a loving and guiding father to the children who are the believers, and they should be treated as\none.\n\nExcommunications: The High Pontiff has the authority to excommunicate any member of the Orenic faith. This excommunication can be overturned by none but himself. An excommunication is the severing of a believer from the church and\nso the religion, dubbing them an apostate. Any excommunicated individual is not awarded the same legal rights as others in Oren and it is forbidden within the Lucienist religion to shelter, give aid or assistance knowingly to an excommunicated individual.\nThe Succession of the Church: As the current High Pontiff, Lucien I, has total authority and papal infallibility as God's voice on earth, it is him who shall be choosing a successor and only a successor chosen by him will be recognized by followers of\nLucienism.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall of KalAgnar", "Nerah", "The Battle Of\n         Kal'Agnar\n   by Fimlin Grandaxe\nA lone figure stood above the ranks, atop a balcony that loomed over all who were below. The armies of Urguan, Krug, Horen, and Malin scrambled about the main hall hurting to their posts.\nwarhorns blew from the south, signaling an invasion coming from the Shroom District. A deep, commanding voice emitted from the figure atop the balcony, ordering the soldiers into position, and warhorns from Kal'Agnar sounded in response.\nPlans had been leaked, screams and cries were heard as the flanking force was slaughtered, disobeying the orders to pull back. The Inner City of Kal'Agnar was all that was left to hold against the onslaught of the undead horde.\nMonsters poured past the main gate only to be quickly shot down by the many archers stationed above, was this all they had to offer? No it was not, for the Grand King had suspected that the horde would come from a more obsolete location.\nHaving suspected it being from a back entrance it was sealed up, as was every open window, except one. Though the window looking out from the mountain had a way of self-sealing, it was no match for the explosives set by the undead horde.\nWith a loud BANG and a crash the window was blasted open, in suit followed an unstoppable horde of Khorvadic minions, instanty taking over the King's Quarters.\nIn vain the armies fought to keep them from pushing further, for they had control of the doors and gates within the quarters. A flank force was sent through a secret passage into one of the King's Guard rooms, and they charged out in a whirl of fury.\nIt was not enough however and the flank force was suppressed and routed, and ever so slowly the armies were pushed back.\nIt was here, where the ultimate downfall became of The sons of Urguan. As they slowly backed away from the plague and monsters that the cultists spat out they had split apart.\nPart of the defending force went down the stairs towards the throne room, while the rest split up in the upper and lower battlements. The undead, by now had taken over the Hall of Kings, and with no passages from\neach side of the battlement to another, the army grew weaker. The division between them had not allowed a proper charge, and they could only move out for a few minutes before being forced to retreat.\nDefeat became evident, one battlement by another they each fell, one, by one. Suddenly a group of five soldiers, accompanied by the Grand King Fimlin Grandaxe and the Anniliar of Laureh'lin Phaedrus, found themselves cornered.\nHowever after searching for whatever exit there could possibly be it was found that in the back half of the battlement was a passageway to the other side. Quickly the group charged for the other side of the battlements and slew all resistance within.\nThis victory did not last long, the cultists above siezed the oppurtunity and blasted spells at those below, scattering them and forcing their retreat.\nThe Sons of Urguan had failed to hold their city against the onslaught of Khorvad, and the Ironborn clan.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall of the Mori", "Thurak", "When the murders and attacks on the city occurred, many speculations arose within the city itself of whom was to blame and who should be slaughtered for such acts against their kind – many claimed it was the work of the surfacers,\nothers believed that such things were only possible by those living within the city.\nIt was declared and enforced that all living Mori were to return to the bosom of Nemiisae and remain within the sanctum of Menocress; behind these stragglers\nto return the horror unfolded, each path and passage that journeyed through only hours before could be heard crumbling under the weight of explosives. The people were brought each in turn to the Temple of the Mother to be cleansed of their\ntaint, the sickness of the surface that had infested them. The final act of the Valsharess and her Yathrins before the war broke out.\nMany that had broken loose from such rigid traditions fought against this cleansing and became\nquickly enraged, spitting in the faces of the priestess’ whom dared demand their obedience and silence. It was not long before two factions emerged; the devout and the rebels. Beneath the surface of the world, sealed off from the blinding\ndamnation of the sun’s light, the Caverns of Menocress’ streets were littered with crude barricades, strewn with the deceased and wounded – The once marvelled city now rots with death and destruction… crumbling under the civil war. Bathed in the Life\nBlood of their kith and kin, the rebellion breached the Yathrins’ sacred enclave; banners raised in revolt, their armour and bodies marked by their treason. Once considered mere common rabble; these denizens now slaughter blessed noble\nborn and their ilk standing guard at the doors of the Temple. From behind the sealed doors both rothe and Mori alike stand in the un-ease union against the threat of tait to its own city – this seeded by those\nturned to the hubris of their Ilharn Zanunder.\n\n~Rescribed by the Farseer Thurak’Braduk, 14th of the First Seed 1484.", ""),
        StaticBook("FALUM", "Wargoth Falum'Lur", "Falum of Clan Lur\n          Vol. I\nThis story details the origin of Falum the Orc and follows his journey through his life. Through the story, there are many obstacles, challenges, and battles Falum must endure and allows one to understand his experience of those trials.\nCHAPTER ONE: THE DEPARTURE OF VAILOR\n\nDuring these times, Falum was nothing but a Cub and entered the Realm knowing nothing other than what his family had taught him. After his father had risked his life to save the Realm he ultimately cast it into\ndestruction all the same causing the Descendents of Vailor to abandon the Realm and sail towards Axios. After experience the sights through the Spirit Realm, the Descendents landed upon Vailor and had to rebuild everything from nothing. The Orcs sailed\naround the New Realm and landed upon the Jungles of Asul figuring it might be a better environment to settle in. Falum worked hard even as a Cub aspiring to one day be like his father, Dominus Vorgo’Yar.\nCHAPTER TWO: THE RISE TO REXDOM\n\nFor a time, Falum had followed his father learning the ways of the Hunt and using it as a time of concentration aside from the work that was asked of him from the nation. Upon finally returning to the War Uzg it was\nrevealed that the political state of the Orcs was in chaos after the death of Rex Kharak’Raguk. The Rightful Dominus, Vorgo’Yar returned with his cub only to find out that Kulgarok’Lak had taken his place as Rex but was quickly defeated by Malgunuz’Raguk.\nRex Malgunuz fell into a civil war between the Nation and a native Clan of Orcs called the Rams. Dominus Vorgo’Yar eventually sided with Rex Malgunuz as Orenia began marching onto their lands after wiping whatever was left of the Dreadlands.\nCHAPTER THREE: THE DEATH OF REX VORGO’YAR\n\nWhile Rex Malgunuz attempted to deal with the Civil War between the Nation and the marching of Orenia, he mysteriously disappeared leaving the peril upon his Dominus and soon Rex.\nThe few Orcs that resided in San’Kharak prepared what they could for the War to come knowing they were at great odds with the Elves assisting Orenia in the march. As they crossed onto Orcish territory incited the Battle of the Bloody Bridge\nwhere 20 Orcs battled against 150 Orenian and Elven warriors. The skirmish was lost and Oren marched upon San’Kharak preparing their siege weapons to destroy the walls. Rex Vorgo’Yar knew the land was doomed with very few supplies and sent most of the\nOrcs including his cub, Falum, to continue life elsewhere, while the Rex, the Dominus, and an Honorary held what was left of San’Kharak and succumbed to the blades of Humans and Elves.", ""),
        StaticBook("Falum'Lur VOL 3", "Wargoth Falum'Lur", "Falum of Clan Lur\n         Vol. III\nThis story details the origin of Falum the Orc and follows his journey through his life. Through the story, there are many obstacles, challenges, and battles Falum must endure and allows one to understand his experience of those trials.\nCHAPTER SEVEN: THE WARGOTH MASSACRE\n\nAs the Coalition claimed victory after victory many rejoiced in the turning of the tides. Falum attended many feasts that Drokon held in honor to whatever he wished to honor that day. Falum was honored\nto service Drokon as Targoth and helped run the thriving nation until one fateful day during a hunt against the Dungoth, Rex Drokon was fatally injured. He only survived due to Kulgarok saving him with his magic and was deemed not a whitewash,\nbut whispered things into Drokon’s ears and influenced him with the same magic. Falum walked around the newly constructed San’Torr with pride until Wargoth Lukra’Braduk met him in the sands.\nLukra spoke ill things happening in the Rex Palace that seemed all too familiar to Dark Shamanism and informed Falum that Rex Drokon and Kulgarok killed one of the other Wargoths for showing too much pride but was taken as a challenge by the Rex.\nWith this in mind, Falum returned to the early constructed Lur Den and thought upon it. After several days pass, he emerged from the Lur Den and entered the Rex Palace only to find noone around. As he walked past the Throne of the Rex, he noticed\na familiar face yet all his Spirit could feel was pity as he observed the heads of the Wargoth’s including Lukra’Braduk.\nCHAPTER EIGHT: THE DEATH OF REX DROKON’UGLUK\n\nWhile Falum never spoke of the things seen that day he continued his service to Drokon with suspicion of Kulgarok manipulating him, but made sure to keep his distance as to not end up like the others.\nWith new Wargoths to be searched for the growing War Nation became crippled until others could take their place though it only seemed it was not enough. After the few feasts and tournaments that was held Drokon vanished and no Keshig, Orc, Goblin, or Olog\ncould find him. After years of searching, Rex Drokon’s corpse was found scorched and clawed within the Dungoth lair. After witnessing the turmoil that was caused Falum begun searching for a means to make his reality more sensible so he turned towards the\nSpirits as his Father once had, left his Wargoth title behind, and set upon a nomadic journey as a servant of Ghorza the Spirit of Travel, Movement, and Fortune.\nCHAPTER NINE: SPIRIT WALKING\n\nBefore Drokon’s death, Falum met a Half Orc wandering around the Rex Palace by the name of Elphaba’Gorkil. In their discussions, Falum came to know Elphaba as his Father’s Shaman mentor as well as\nknowing Kulgarok’s misdeeds with Drokon. When it seemed the conflict would not cease Falum decided to ask Elphaba to help him train in the ways of the Shamanic Arts. Through intense training and meditation, Falum eventually became capable of speaking with\nSpirits of the Elemental Realm and bonded with a Spirit of Fire and Storm. When the Spirit of Storm demanded Falum’s trial to begin he was smited with a great bolt of lightning that ultimately killed him until Elphaba’s distress brought him back to life\nbeing reborn and renamed as, Falum, by the Spirit.", ""),
        StaticBook("Falum'Lur VOL II", "Wargoth Falum'Lur", "Falum of Clan Lur\n          Vol. II\nThis story details the origin of Falum the Orc and follows his journey through his life. Through the story, there are many obstacles, challenges, and battles Falum must endure and allows one to understand his experience of those trials.\nCHAPTER FOUR: THE REFUGEES OF AZAGHOL\n\nAfter the Siege of San’Kharak and the death of his father Vorgo’Yar, the remaining Orcs sailed across the seas to the Urguanic desert and began constructing a refugee camp\nas was provided by Grand King Torvin Grandaxe. Falum in his 20’s  humbly served as Targoth of the Orcish people and helped construct the walls and buildings although many of the Dwarves had referred to him as the Rex. Even though they pursued\na new life it was all too sudden that The Dominion of Malin had found the Orcish settlement and relayed the message to their protectorate, Orenia. As time passed by, Falum and other Wargoths had to attend the many hostile negotiations that were had\nbetween Urguan and Orenia. While Urguan kept Oren at bay, an internal controversy arose among the remaining Orcish people.\nCHAPTER FIVE: THE REXDOM OF DROKON’UGLUK\n\nWhile Oren and the Dominion once again aggressed on the Orcish people the Orc named Kulgarok sought to once again deem himself as the Rex of the lands. A council of the Wargoths was called to dispute the\nmatter where most were not in support of it and one Orc especially took a stand against it. Drokon’Ugluk faced Kulgarok’Lak and demanded they meet in combat to bring a solution to the matter. They broke into action and Drokon’Ugluk came out victorious\nand claimed the Rexdom with support of the other Wargoths. Falum eventually got inducted into Clan Lur by Eath’Lur as he was apart of the bloodline and also became Targoth serving Rex Drokon’Ugluk, but after Kulgarok’s defeat he chose to bring his\nallegiance under the Emporer of Orenia acting as his Court Mage.\nCHAPTER SIX: THE AXIONITE COALITION", ""),
        StaticBook("Famine of Winter", "Commodus de Jedih", "wsfdefelfkmfsfdsfdsfdFamine of Winter, Brought by Manlets\nsdasdasdasdsadsaddsAn Informative Pamphlet on The Opportunistic Harold Winter IV and His Bastard Cohorts.\n\nby Nafis Yar, 1542\n\nTranscribed by Comm. 1663\n“A great read while dropping a load in the privy. I cannot recommend this pamphlet highly enough.” - Nafis Yar\nsadsadasdasdasdasaa\n\nDear readers, we are at war. And I’m not writing about the Orenian-Vanderguanese War.\nI’m talking about a war with higher stakes than that war, the Zionist War, and the Ducal War combined and then divided by three.\n\nAnd the battleground is the Vander Ideology.\n3On Harold Winter IVh\n\nJust a couple of years ago, no one in the Reich save for the rumored-to be-immortal Faiz Kharadeen had ever heard the name Winter. And as of the 9th of the Amber Cold, 1942, Harold Winter IV is now the Arch-Duke of -\nVandoria suckling from the teet of a hairy half-man named Rhewen. \n\nAnd they call it Vanderguan! With that comes the spoiling of the fruits of Vander efforts to breathe life into the decrepit Khalestine.\nAnd my Uncle Siris is rolling in his grave side by side with his camel, may he rest in peace.\n\n“Imagine,” the Vanderguanese croon, “there’s no oppression. It isn’t hard, it’s true. Nothing to fight or kill for, and no Oren, too.”\nYou may find their side appealing because it rhymes. But so does this: “Hogarth Irongut is ‘witty-witty’. Get him away from the kiddie-kiddies.” And that rhymes four times, good reader. So now you know who is better. (Me).\nAll cruel jokes aside, this Harold IV has dubbed himself the leader of the Vander people, and then makes a half-man the leader of the Vander people. Neither of which were Vanders in the first place! Such bastardization. While I received the news of this -\nnew Vanderguan yesterday during my morning coffee - note, I myself a Vander - Qali, was in a prison camp after the failed siege of Khro’Nogaak where the half-men cut off my hand and forced me to listen to slantie shanties of industry so I’m a bit late on-\nthis news - I accidently spilled the contents of my #1 Dad mug onto my lap. Not only did I doze off a few times later that evening teaching my daughter how to read, it also hurt to piss.\n\nWe’ll give Harold IV the benefit of the doubt though.\nMaybe he’s trying to do something grand that I’m just unable to notice.\n\n“In an effort to conserve the freedom of all races, we join forces to fight the tyranny sweeping across Vailor” - The Unification Act of The Amber Cold, 1542, Paragraph Two.\nOut of context, one of liberal values may applaud the goals set forth by Harold IV. It appears genuine and good natured. However, one should look to the actions of Harold IV to understand what he means by “conserving the freedom.”\n“The two sovereign nations known as The Grand Kingdom of Urguan and the Konigsreich of Vandoria shall hereby be amalgamated as The Grand Empire of Vanderguan under Grand Emperor Rhewen Frostbeard, Arch-Duke of Urguan,-\nand Grand Chancellor Harold Winter IV, Arch-Duke of Vandoria” - The Unification Act of The Amber Cold, 1542, Paragraph One.\n\nIn order to conserve freedom, Harold IV gives up freedom.\nDear reader, all because Harold IV didn’t put much thought into his choice of actions doesn’t mean YOU shouldn’t! Vandoria was never officially involved in this war and could have lived out its time in isolation, focused on its people.\nHowever, those left in power have painted Oren as the boogieman and went as far as to plot against and attack allies of the previous Hallowvale regime from Oren which jeopardized and ultimately ruined relations with long-time allies.\nHarold IV and Faiz Kharadeen had the audacity to bend the knee to one half their size called the Grand Emperor not because they seek freedom from Oren, but because they have a long standing pact with the manlets. They are literally race traitors and have-\nprovoked a war that did not need to happen. \n\nWho puts these hard-headed one minded people in charge? (The answer is not me!)\n\nNow, one might put the blame on Frederick II for “abandoning” Vandoria.\nHallowvale men and women were branded as traitors and burned at the stake - the same stake the Vanderguanese fear. However it is Faiz Kharadeen and his vassals who have undermined Frederick’s rule and pushed him out of power for the former's own-\nselfish desires. And to put Harold IV who has done nothing for the nation in power is absurd. AND THEY STILL CALL IT VANDORIA. There is nothing Vander about Vandoria anymore. Degenerate immigrants were allowed to seep back into the realm and have -\ncolonized Al-Wakrah as an invading force and I'm pretty fucking sure most of them are illegals. (Of the cultist sort). The only standing, active force was witch-hunted. \n\nAnd from here on it, Vanderguan will be referred to as Caliguan.\nThere be no more Vanders there. And even this is a stretch because there are no more Qalasheen save for the Kharadeen left in Al-Wakhrah. The rest packed up when I should have as well.\nssadasdasdsadasdasdA Call To The Citizens of Caliguan\nsadsadasdasdsadasda\n\nNobles, farmers, camel merchants. Your liege lord Harold IV and Faiz Kharadeen have dragged you into a war that no one in Vandoria had business in unless they-\nwere doing mercenary work. Your liege lords have put the well being of half-men before yours and they will lead you to destruction.\n\nUnless you get your independence!\n\nCast aside Caliguan's bindings and live-\nfor yourselves. And if you play your cards right, you’ll live for many decades to come.\n\nReal Vanders and Qalasheen, ride with me. Our White Flame burns brightly.\n\nPray for an end to Winter.\nasdsadasdsadasdsadaDeclaration of Qalasheen Spring\nasdasdasdasdasdasad\n\nThe weak deserve to die so that the strong may flourish. - Vander Code\n\nsadsadasdsadsaasasa\n\nTranscribed by Comm.\nNOTE FROM COMM.\n\n- The mentioned Orenian-Vanderguanese war is now referred to as the Eighteen Years' War (High Imperial: Bellum Duodeviginti Annorum) that took place 1529-1547.", ""),
        StaticBook("Farewell", "CanadianFlag", "To the following people:\n\nLuke\nCharles\nKebab\nThunder\nKiddo\nThank you for all the great memories created on LoTC. Despite the hiatuses you've all taken, I've never forgot a single one of you. Im sure when I move to Toronto for University, I'll continue to rememeber the guys who I would game with throughout my high\nschool life. Thanks for everything. Keep in touch, and best of luck in all your future endeavors.\n\n\n-SimbaTheFatDog AKA\n_CanadianFlag_\n\n\n\nAlso\nS\nU\nC                 B\nK                 I\n                  T\nM                 C\nY                 H\n                  E\nA                 S\nS\nS", ""),
        StaticBook("Farming Contract", "Psycho The Boneless", "Farming Contract\n\nPsycho will pay\nx64 Iron Ingots\nFor every\nx6 Stacks of Wheat\n\nYou may use the farms of Kal'Tarak ONLY if you replant. If you are caught not replanting, pay is deducted and you will be fined.\n-Powered By Psycho-\nDisclaimer:\n\nYOU WILL ONLY BE PAID IF YOU RETURN THIS CONTRACT WITH THE FARMED WHEAT. TAMPERING WITH THIS CONTRACT WILL RESULT IN BEING HUNTED BY PSYCHO THE BONELESS.", ""),
        StaticBook("Father's Mark", "Guyden Aureon", "~*~The Father's~*~\n          Mark\n\nScribed by the Willow Druid.\n\nCreated by the Hawk Druid.\nWear upon your skin the mark of the Father if ye be one who stains the soil with blood. If ye be one who lives by the bow, and fights for his kin.\n\nThe father's mark is a tattoo, much like the ilmyumier indicating the Seed one belongs to. The father's\nmark, however, holds no tribal affiliations. It is for any and all of the Aspectist rite who consider themselves warriors and hunters.\n\nThe father's mark is crimson, like blood. It may either curve like a blade, or bare the jagged outcroppings of\nthe stag's horns, the sacred symbol of the huntslord Cernunnos. The mark must be worn upon the face, or upon the hand that does the killing. To wear the mark of the Father is to honour the lord of the hunt. To display your allegiance to your people and\nyour people's faith by designating yourself as both a worshipper of the old Aspectist rite, and a warrior.\nThe Father's Essence\n\nIf ye be a warrior of the old rite, carry upon you a flask containing the blood of a fully grown stag. Drink but a sip before all instances where blood must be spilled, and let the Horned Man bless you with his sacred essense.\nThe father’s essense is a vial of blood that is to be carried upon the person of an Aspectist warrior at all times. The blood of the stag is the symbolic manifestation of the spirit and faith within our hearts, and when consumed, imbues us with the\nblessing of the Father, and instills bravery in our hearts when we face the prospect of death in the line of protecting our faith and kin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fears for Task", "Ser Duncan Lefay", "List of fears, from least to greatest.\n\n\n1. Not big on spiders. Especially big spiders. Kill them all.\n\n2. Mild fear of necromorphs. Had a bad run in with one in Mordskov a while back.\n3. Fear of losing control of situations. Main reason that he doesn't enjoy drinking.\n\n4. Fear of loss. Has had it happen in many different ways, be it death, being left, etc.\n\n5. Fear of not being good enough. Can feel quite insecure at times.", ""),
        StaticBook("Felix's Journal", "Felix", "[!] The entries in the journal are messily scribed.\n\nI finally found someone that needed help today. Her name is Saetur and she has orange hair and a drug addiction.\n\nSaetur asked me to go into the mine to find her some quartz. Easy enough!\nThe second time didn't go so well, but it counts! A weird Demon-Creature diguised as a plant lady called Glineth rolled into town... We all fought and apprehended her.\n\nSuticans: 1\nVillains: 0\nThird time! Final part of the task. Turns out Richard's the kind of guy that is never NOT in trouble. I helped a Dominion soldier detain him for suspected Chimera creation, as well as multiple accounts of assault.\n\nThe guy needs to fix his life.", ""),
