        StaticBook("Fetish's Stash", "Cooper", "Hey!  You found my stash!  Take it if you want, unless you are a bad person.  I don't like bad people, they are mean and stuff.  \n-Fetish", ""),
        StaticBook("Feudalism", "Bernard Oakstool", "Feudalism, a Failure.\n-------------------\nMany of us, live in a feudal society. This is because, kings, churches and royal families take control of an area, and then force working people to pay tax to live there, and threaten those that protest.\nThis..\nfeels like something required for our society. The concept of land ownership. Ofcourse, If I said that a house didn't require ownership, that would be a stretch. The Ownership should be the family living in it, not a king who has claimed it. A house..\ndoesn't produce anything, and the king owning the house does not impact anything but simply give the king more money, while pulling the mina out of the working family.\n\nThis is why, the person who lives and works on property should have the right to it,..\nbut not the property and land other workers require to sustain themselves.\n\nThis is why, private property must be abolished. To help the working peoples of the world. No handouts for the oppressive rulers.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fi'hiiran'tanya", "Toodles", "Fi'hiiran'tanya\nOriginally written by\nValia'laure Faeifeth\n\nTranscribed for the Library of Dragur by\nRevion M. Tathron\n\nThe following is a transcript of a book found in the ruins of a house in Celein.\nThe Smile of Larihei Heals the Mind Like Milk Heals the Body.\nThe Lifting- Sacrifice\nThe Ritual of the Lifting is different from that of Untempered Fi, for it is the stringent conditions which make for the true, Tempered Fi's creation.\nThe ritual of the Elibar'acal follows, and yet it is sufficient but not necessary to create a Tempered soul.\nThe sacrifice is tied to the Altar, imbued with the magic of Fi. The room is lit only by the light of a Fi' orb in a specially made lamp.\nGold dust is scattered upon the sacrifice as the following is read. Each in attendance may bless themselves as they so desire.\n<Transcriber's note:\n\nBoth the Elvish and common versions of the Ritual have been removed, to deter those who seek to practice this vile art.>\n<Basically, it detailed how the Golden Owl is saving everyone from monsters. It wasn't worth reading, believe me.>\n\nMilk is passed between those in attendance in a Silver Chalice. It is drunk by each in turn, symbolising they are worthy of the Milk of Larihei, and therefore her smile.\nYour body unfit for the milk, Your mind unfit for the smile of Larihei, \nYour very essence forfeit.\nThe Milk is refused to the sacrifice, symbolising they are unworthy of it. A blade imbued with Fi' energy (read: Fi'chant, just as the altar is)\nis used to cut the sacrifice's throat and as this is done droplets of blue will pool on the blade's tip.\nBlood is collected in a clay pot. The droplets will spin and form a blue light which will become stable (PK)\nor will explode in a flash of light (no PK, soul escapes). It is required an orb be present to power both the altar and the blade.\nFi'hiiran'seth\nThis subtype of the magic focuses on the negation of Arcane Magic. Whether Evocation, Conjuration, Illusion, Runes, or Alteration, if can either send a forming spell back to the void or eat away at a created spell.\nThe magic will also steal the aura needed for Shade magic, but has no affect on existing tendrils.\nFi'hiiran'acaele\nThe second subtype of the magic can stop all Deity Magic. (For example: Clerical, Druidism, Shamanism, Monk, Muun'Trivazja, and Ascended). Unlike its brother subtype, which funnels mana away into the void,\nFi'hiiran'acaele disrupts a connection, interfering with someone's ability to connect with their chosen deity. This can be small, when they cast a spell, or large, severing a connection for a time.\nStrangely, neither Fi'hiiran'acaele or Fi'hiiran'seth affect Necromancy.\nThe mage must be a first-time magic user, never having connected to anything, Deity, Void, or otherwise.\nThe mage must be of good condition. Fi'hiiran'tanya corrupts the body twice as much as a normal magic, and the mage's increased metabolism may wither them away without proper care.\nThe mage must perform the Ritual.\nThis Ritual, developed by the Elibar'acals, is the source of the mage's power. They much find a sacrifice (a character willing to be permanently killed) that they know well, and kill them on the altar.\nIt is in this moment, when the soul is leaving, that the mage will connect to the Void for the first time. The soul will be returning to The Cloud Temple,\nand the mage will grab it, trapping it in a state of Limbo. A state of half-death, forever caught in the mage's grasp. The soul will become a tool,\nand will eventually forget its old self, becoming more and more compliant. There is a small chance, in the beginning years, that the soul will attempt to wrest control, though no soul has ever gained full control.\nPhysical and mental strain\nLoss of weight and muscle mass\nIncredibly realistic lucid dreams and nightmares, leading to a confusion on what is real and what is imagined.\nEnchanted areas will leave a Fi'hiiran'tanya user fatigued if they stay in there for too long a time period.\nProblems with breathing, blood loss, internal bleeding, and the rate at which wounds heal.", ""),
        StaticBook("Field Herbs", "Andriel Elré Z'lorn", "In the field there are many ways to treat the wounded. From burns to cuts to scrapes to arrow wounds, there can be many different things that may need to be cared for. Here is a guide on Medical Uses of different Herbs during everyday life.\nBlissfoil:\nBlissfoil can be very useful for minor injuries or ailments. It can relieve pain and itchyness at the slightest of touch. The oil around it's stalks and petals can be used medically to relieve these symptoms.\nTippen's Root:\nThis herb is great for stopping the bleeding of a large wound once made into a Salve/Balm. This root is known for having an unpleasent smell, however, the medical uses outweight such factors.\nFlameTounge Root:\nThis Root is not to be used lightly, and is only to be used if out of Tippen's Root. It gives off an intense heat that can be used to seal and stop blood flow. NOTE: Make sure to wear gloves when handling this Root.\nSerpent's Stalk:\nThis herb is generally dangerous for consumption as a plant, however, once one crushes the upper stalk and mix it with water, it can be used to treat burns and minor pain.\nFrost Vine:\nIt is wise to crush this herb and mix it with water. This will produce a substance, somewhat sticky, which can be used to numb areas from pain.\nAqua Nymph:\nWARNING: Only use in extreme cases.\nThis plant can cause closing of the airway if taken orally. However, if one were to receive\na terrible burn. To use the plant correctly, boil the plant (Gently) in some water, strain the plant from the water\nAqua Nymph Cont.:\nand use the remaining oil on the affected skin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire Evocation", "Anorak", "You know, there's more to fire evocation than just fireballs, right? I didn't know that for the longest time. I was self-taught, you see. Eventually-\nI learned that you can manipulate the evoked fire into whatever form you seek. If you wanted to split up an single fireball into four small, fist-sized fireballs that seperate to your sides, then you can do that\nwith minimal effect to your mana usage. You can also create concussive fireballs if you spend enough time on it. This will usually drain the most experienced fire evocationists' mana quite extensively\n- to the point of exhaustion at least. At beginner level, it's a risky thing to attempt as it-\ncould very well exhaust you to the point of death. One thing that you can also attempt as a pyromancer is to focus in on a specific object, and eventually have it burst into flames.\nPer beginning your studies, it'd likely merely just get very warm and- the like. On a closing note, fire evocation is a very unique form and can be used to do nearly anything that you can imagine - within limits, of course.\nPlease keep in mind, as a disclaimer I state that if you're not experienced enough in the art, do- not attempt any of the bigger spells that require a lot of mana. You have been warned. Copy of the book \"Fire Evocation\" by Solirynir Ilmoriel", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire Evocation", "Sarrion Zytiaear", "-=Fire Evocation=-\n\nBy Sarrion Zytiaear\nLong ago, the descendants discovered the element of fire. The main characteristics of this element were to produce light and warmth, while also offering protection and strength.\nFor ages they wished to utilize these attributes, often dreaming of using the pure essence of flame to fend off their foes. The very first mages were determined to grasp such a power as their own.\nWhile it’s unclear what the first magic may have been in the early world, many scholars believe that Pyromancy was one of the first of the elemental magics; fire being one of the simplest elements to study.\nEarly scholars sought to control the flame, and learned that one could conjure their own flames from the void. This finding conceived what was to be the beginning of modern Fire Evocation.\nFire Evocation is the art of conjuring elemental flames from the void to be controlled at the will of its caster. The basic limitations being  one's mana and basic casting principles on a weaponized magic which can be wielded to the casters imagination.\nThe first flames conjured from the void were crude and simple, not easily controlled. Over time mages had learned to manipulate the flames, using their imagination\nto cast spells in different ways rather than the ability to launch a fireball through the air.\nAfter years of experience and adaptation, mages eventually became able to alter the intensity of the heat in their flames, as well as create blue flame.\nWhile there is great flexibility with elemental evocation, typically, there are set limits. One particular mage was daring enough to attempt heating their flames to white hot, ultimately leading to their untimely death.\nAny who tried to do the same were brought to their inevitable demise. This served as a lesson to other mages that there were  boundaries that simply could not be crossed, at the cost of their life.\n-=- Modern Day -=-\n\nGradually, the art was developed into more unique uses than merely lighting their foes ablaze with a well placed fireball.\nWith different techniques being formulated, came the existence of  “Heat Evocation”. This permits the caster to kindle the heat of their element rather than only the flames themselves.\nAnother noteworthy feat of pyromancers was the revelation of  “Smoke Evocation\". As the name suggests, this brings forth the smoke of a Fire that may be used for self defense purposes without severely harming the other party.\nWhile the smoke may blind or hinder the target, it could not burn and cause them any long-term complications. Even if Fire Evocation may be one of the “simplest” magics to grasp due to the straightforward\nnature of the element, anyone can gain a variety of interesting skills with enough patience and aptitude. All thing considered, one must always remember they are playing with fire.\nToday's Fire Evocationists join the ranks with many mages and scholars in the voidal arts, Fire Evocation often being suggested  to new mages as a beginners magic for its simplicity and\nvarious uses. The most heavily utilized capabilities for those that wield this evocation,  are for those who enjoy a combative approach. There are multiple ways to use a weaponized flame: The simple fireball where one would brandish a ball of flame\nand toss it at their foe, Conjuring embers to collect at a location which expand rapidly into a fiery explosion(Not concussive), or simply using embers to light a fire. One needs to understand that voidal flames\nare dangerous and can ignite real flames upon the mortal realm, leaving behind a trail of destruction whether it be accidentally or purposely.\nOne of the more emphasized lessons a teacher could push onto their apprentice, would be to exercise caution with such flame. \n-=- The Properties of Conjured Fire -=-\n\nFlames conjured by the void are just as volatile as real flames, but their temperature can become considerably warmer and the physical form more controllable.\nThere are three different colors of flame, each with their own category of temperature. The greater amount of heat one brings to their flame, the more mana they burn in the process.\nIn order from coolest to the hottest are orange flames, blue flames, and white flame. Orange flames are simple fire, the easiest to conjure from the void.\nBlue flames, being more difficult to conjure and even hotter than lava, should be cast such with extreme caution. It’s to be noted that blue flames should only be attempted by well practiced pyromancers.\nFinally, white flames are thought to be never achieved; for every attempt has ended in death. These flames drain the casters mana very rapidly before fully formed, and if one was to manage to cast a white flame it would be too hot to handle.\nThe heat exposure will surely kill them and those in close range. Voidal flames can influence the world around them and thus can light other flammable materials ablaze, or heat metal / stone, so forth.\nThese flames mimic the properties of real fire, so it has all the weaknesses of such. Flames will always require air and space to thrive. Sand or water will suffocate and extinguish them.\nTHE END\n\nAuthors note:\nPlease understand that all voidal magic should be learned with caution and respect. This is a powerful art that many fear and hate for good reason.\n-Sarrion Zytiaear", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire Evocation", "Evelangéline", "About Fire Evocation:\n\n-Fire Evocation, one of the six evocation arts is the utilization of fire by the evocationists. Although Fire Evocation is not very hard to learn, it is one that must be practised a lot about, because of its destructive behavio\nBasic Understanding:\n\n- Fire evocation, as the other types of evocation arts, is powered by the void. The evocationist who has a connection to the void calls forth the fire from the void. One aspect that is not known by many is that the fire formed i\nnot real on this plane of existance. A thing that I tell to my students, \"The fire is fake, only the effects of the fire are real.\" is an accurate statement, considering this.\n\n-The origins of the art are unknown, although It is one of the oldest art\nProgress of A Fire Evocationist Student:\n\n- Fire evocation is easy to learn, yet hard to master. So, a Fire Evocationist needs to take their time and have stable observations and practises to use their potential to a maxiumum.\n- During the first five elven days, the student needs to form a stable connection to the void, through meditating. While meditating can be done in any position, it can also be done for flexible amounts of time. For example, while many evocationists -\nchoose to meditate for at least half an hour once. I meditated for five minutes six times a day. The important thing is efficiency, and focus. The student needs to clear their mind in order to form their first connections to the void.\n\n- After the ev\n-tionist forms a stable connection to the void, they work on conjuring low-powered flames, propably shards of embers. During this period, the evocationist must be observing how fire burns, how it spreads, and how it affects the substance it burns on.\n- After an elven week, the evocationist will get started with conjuring small flames, not exceeding the size of a regular candle's fire. During the beginning of this period the evocationist will be greatly fatigued, propably not being able to hold the -\nfire for long. The time of the evocation will increase from ten seconds to a few minutes if done correctly. The evocationist should focus on increasing the size of the flames and lenghten the duration of how long they can hold the flame.\n- After this period, the evocationist will be able to evoke bigger flames, propably not exceeding the size of an elven fist, after the two elven weeks of the period.\n\n- Next period, the evocationist will focus on shaping their flames as spheres.\nTo be able to throw fiery balls of fire at objects. The evocationist will fail to throw a ball of fire successfully the first five elven days, then will be fatigued after one small ball of fire. During the ends of this phase, the evocationist will increa-\n-se the size and range of their fire spheres, the phase lasting for nearly two more elven weeks, exactly one elven month after the evocationist had first started to learn.\n\n- From the start of the next phase, the fire evocationist will-\nbe having covered most of the parts to be known, moving to a period of practise. The evocationist will be able to evocate walls of fire and flames that are distanced from the evocationist. However, as the distance of the fire increases from the evocation-\n-ist, so does the difficulty and mana requirement. The evocationist at this point would be able to form multiple fire spheres before being fatigued, not exceeding an amount of three. While the wall of fire can be maintained for an average of thirty-\nseconds. After this period, is the mastering period.\n\n- A master of fire evocation has learned how to effectively and efficiently use their mana to cast larger flames, calling fires to this realm of existance quicker. Gaining the ability to-\nevoke large areas of vigorous, reactive fire; fire novas. Bear in mind that an evocationist should never try to evoke more than their training has given to them.\nMore Things to Know:\n\n- Although fire may be engrossing and exciting, it also is very dangerous. More than the other arts actually, at least in my point of view. You cannot, simply cannot manipulate the fire you have summoned, meaning that-\nif a fire evocationist accidentally set an object on fire, they cannot extinguish it. So try to remain calm, and don't cause accidents.\n\n- To further explain the lack of fire manipulation, I'll go into slightly more detail. A fire evocationist cannot\nutilize already existing fire. They can only summon flames from the void into this realm of existance. Once they summon the flames and use them, they are out of control. As I say to my students: The fire is alive, it has a mind of its own. You cannot -\nforce it to do anything. You can only convince it.\n\n-Lastly, an evocationist of any type shouldn't ever push their limits too hard, to exceed their level. If an evocationist proceeds to cast magic for too long-\nthey will get extremely fatigued, then maybe even lose their life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire Notes", "Epsilon Hallowfall", "Upon first sitting near fire, unsurprisingly, it was warm. I stuck my golem arm in it, then touched it. Unsurprisingly yet again, I got burnt. After observing fire for a long time, I noticed the free-will it had. It flows freely and crackles in multiple\ndirections around the general area. However, I've also found out how fast fire really can spread. The books don't exaggerate it: Fire spreads VERY easily if you give it the chance, and depending on the material. I've performed ways to put out a fire.\nThese methods include, smothering and pouring water on the fire. Although watering IS more effective, smothering also a valid option depending on the size of the flame and density.", ""),
        StaticBook("First Aid Manual", "Camille", "First Aid:\n\nShock and symptoms: Page 2 --> 7\n\nWounds: Page 8 --> 15\n\nBroken bones: Page 16 --> 22\n\nRescucitation: Page 23 --> 26\n\nPulse + Stitching: 27+\nFirst off, we'll be starting with the term \"shock\", and its definition. This usually happens to people who are wounded from combat, and from serious injuries. When a person is in shock, their pulse becomes rapid, along with their breath. Their skin turns\npale and clammy, and the victim might also feel nauseatic. Their pupils can also look enlarged, and obviously, the victims in shock are always fatigued and weak.\nTheir mental behaviour also changes, such as anxiousness or agitation.\nHow to deal with a person who's in shock?\nWell, for a starter, you'll have to elevate their legs and feet slightly to get the blood properly flowing while laying them down, and don't move them unless *absolutely* necessary.\nLoosen the clothing of the patient, and cover them with a blanket if you can to prevent chilling.\nDo not let them eat or drink anything.\nIf the person is vomiting or bleeding from the mouth, turn them to the side to prevent choking, unless you suspect\na spinal injury.\nIf a person is bleeding, then hold pressure over the bleeding area using towels or sheets. Clean and/or sterilized ones are recommended, but if absolutely necessary, use any towels or sheets you can to prevent them from dying.\nIf the patient is showing no signs of life, then we'll be talking about one of the rescucitation techniques to bring back the signs of life into their body. (Refer to page 23)\nIs the patient cut? Are they bleeding from the outside?\n\nFirst off, you'll have to clean the area from blood using sheets or cloth to examine the wound. Don't commit any mistake here, because their life will be in your hands.\nPressing against their wound with cloth to prevent more blood from spilling is the best choice until help comes. Do not, I repeat, Do *not*, urinate in a wound. Urine is the worst thing that can be put with blood, and that will result in an infection and\ndeath. No one wants urine in blood. After putting pressure on the wound, check if the blood is still spilling a lot. If not, then keep putting pressure against the wound until help arrives. If it's still bleeding a lot, then this is where you'll have to\napply a tourniquet. Tourniquets are usually the last resort to wounds because they can reduce or cut off blood supply to a whole limb, which can cause damage if left for too long. To make your own tourniquet, you'll need a belt and strap it hard around\nthe limb right above the wound, not -around- the wond, but above. You'll have to strap it hard and tight, but not too much. If you don't have a belt, then an improvised tourniquet from sheets or ripped clothing works. You'll have to wrap it around a limb\nabove the wound and tie it hard. Once that's done, the blood should be spilling out in a really small quantity. Try to not let the tourniquet on for long unless absolute necessary, because that can cause tissue damage.\nIf the patient has a large open wound, then you might need to close it via stitching. This is like stitching your ripped clothes, but instead of clothes, you'll have flesh to stitch and and close. Make sure all of your equipment is clean, and that your\nhands have been cleaned beforehand.\nPouring clean water on the wound before doing your improvised surgery is extremely important, and clear the wound from any dirt and things that aren't part of their body before stitching the wound shut.\nDoes your patient have broken bones? Well now, it all depends on what bones have been broken. Leg and arm bones? Then you'll have to make sure their bones aren't moving around too much, usually done by making them avoid moving and wrapping your improvised\nsplint around their limb. The easiest way to make your own splint, you'll need a long and hard object, usually a stick or tree branch, or even your own weapon, and something to tie it around the patient's limb with, usually cloth. Once that's done and\nit's tied properly, it should work as an improvised splint until help arrives.\nNow, the bigger problem is when their ribs are broken, because this can cause puncturing of the lungs.\nIs your victim suffering on the floor with a broken rib while making\nchoking sounds and even spitting blood, and you don't know what to do? Well, for this one, you'll have to save their lives by stabbing them. It has to be done carefully, though. You'll need a needle which is hollow from the inside, connected to a tube.\nOnce you have that, you'll have to stab the patient between the ribs into the lungs so the blood can spill out instead of making the patient choke, which will save their lives until help comes. If you don't have a needle and tube though, then you'll just\nneed a knife for that, but it isn't as great as the last tools. For this one, you'll have to stab the patient too, but you need something to keep the hole open for the blood to spill out. Though if you have nothing else, then the knife might save their\nlife if you're lucky, even if not so great.\nNow, on to the rescucitation technique. If the patient doesn't show any signs of life, such as no pulse, no breathing, or no heart beat, then you'll have to use your last bit of knowledge in hopes of saving their lives. For this once, you'll have to place\nyour palm on their chest, with your other hand above the one on the chest, and then start pushing, then letting go. Repeat the same thing every couple seconds to imitate their breathing, and you might also need to kneel down next to them, pinch their nose\nand force air through their mouth from your own mouth. Once done, go back to the pushing and releasing part of it until the patient either comes back to life or doesn't after quite some time. Don't be worried if you'll break their ribs though, because\nthat can happen, but having broken ribs is a lot better than losing one's life.\nNow, after all of this, you may ask: 'How do I check someone's pulse? How do I stitch someone's wounds?\n\nTo check someone's pulse is simple; all you have to do is press two of your fingers on the thumb side of your wrist. Now, since we're talking about\nthe pulse, let's head onto the heart activity. To check how many beats per elven minute there are, you'll have to check their pulse for fifteen elven seconds and then multiply it all by four. If it's between 60 and 100, then they're safe.\nNow, for the stitching part. First off, like always, you'll have to sterilize everything and make sure everything is clean. After that, it's recommended to irrigate the wound with boiled water. After that, poke a hole into the side of the skin, then drag\nit out from the other side of the skin, basically forcing the wound to close. The sutures have to be close to each other and from the skin edges, but not too close; the skin shouldn't pucker.\nHead Injuries: Page 32 ---> Page 35\nAnd now, finally, we'll be talking about head injuries, or head trauma.\nThose are caused when someone has been hit in the head, usually with a blunt weapon. They can range from minor injuries to severe and even deadly ones.\nFirst off, you'll have to check the pupils of the patient. Try waving a torch above their eyes, and see if their eyes respond to the light change. If not, then they're most possibly braindead. And if they are, there's no way to bring their brain back to\nlife. Though, for less severe conditions, the patient will feel dizzy, blurry vision, and will start switching from conscious to unconscious from time to time, and fluids might be leaking from either where they were hit at and/or their nose or ears.\nWhen this happens, you'll have to stop the person from moving, put pressure against their wounds to prevent them from getting in a worse condition until help arrives.\nIn any case, this should be about it. Please note that this handbook is for first aid only, which only informs you on what to do until help arrives. Professional help.\nIf you liked this book, or if you have any questions or would even like me to write\nabout a certain topic, you can send a bird to Camille Haley (iDiogen) and I will make sure to read what you have to say!", ""),
        StaticBook("First Mage War", "Elindor", "The  First  War \n      Of   Mages   \n\n Inscribed By Elindor\n\n\n ijfeaslkklmfdslkmdall\n\n\n      Chapter I\n    Magic's Genesis\nIn an age before history Aenguls and Daemons walked upon the face of the earth amongst mortals. The four fathers of all nations lived in reverence of their similarities as brothers, for to them the celestial beings were removed in near every aspect.\nThe first children of Malin, Horen, Krug and Urguan were bringing forth a new generation that reflected the talents and aspects of their forefathers. Compared to the Aenguls and Daemons, the mortals had no power at all. But united they were a force upon\nthe face of the earth, and the descendants set about establishing for themselves townships, and eventually kingdoms. To most of the deities the activites of the mortal beasts was whimsical and entertaining, but some saw the shift in power that had already\nbegun. The mortals were new to the world, yet they quickly learned and adapted to use resources to their advantage. No daemon had need to cut down a tree, yet forests were now being flattened, and the goodness of the earth ripped up and melted.\nChapter II\n   The Earliest Days\n         Of Magic\nMagic has always been in all things. By virtue of having been created from the void, every element of the universe is within itself capable of magic, however mundane. To each newly born mortal is handed a soul to posess the vessel of flesh. Suddenly the\nbeing of the seven skies were no longer separated from the other creations. To a babe newly born is bestowed a soul. With it, the potential for greatness: independant thought, power over the elements of the created world, the choice of one's destiny, and\nmost influential of all... magic. Not just regular magic like that found in a tree or a bird, but access to the limitless expanse of void. There had barely been three generations born from the fathers before the shift in power was clear to those watching.\nNot all descendants presented this danger. Some pursued knowledge and understanding, overtime making way for wisdom. And these gifted mortals conversed with the Aenguls about the nature of existence. The celestial beings were able to learn\nsome things that their immortal forms had no need to consider. And so between them a handful of Aenguls and mortals formed a wise counsel and watched as the children of mortality spread themselves across the earth in search of kingdoms and power.\nChapter III\n       Temptations\n       In Shadows\nZalam was a mortal with an insatiable hunger for magic. His thirst for greater sources of arcane energy lead him to consort with an Aengul known as Iblees. The two delved deeper into the possibilities of dark magic, and as they did so sought seclusion.\nThe counsel of wise mortals and aenguls grew concerned that these two rejected all who queried their actions. The ever heightening need for privacy was most concerning for the deities, for selfishness and jealousy were mortal attributes.\nA handful of mortals grabbed hold of Zalam one afternoon and made demands that he share what his consorting with Iblees was purposed for. His response was one without words but with a very clear message. Those who had grabbed hold of him found their skin\ngrowing brittle, their muscles weakening, and their energy quickly exhausted. The other two received dark tendrils piercing through their shoulders. Zalam made quick work of silencing the questioners and, by sunset that day, had brought three lifeless\nbodies back to Iblees. The survivor of that short magical skirmish reported back to the counsel, sparking immediate action. Confrontation was not enough. These two would have to cease their activities if they so quickly corrupted the minds of men.\nBut the world had not witnessed dark magic before. They knew not the pull that power had over mortals. In so short a time Iblees had gained followers whose loyalties would stretch even beyond their final breath. This was no longer a matter of a rogue mage\nand a fallen aengul. Now standing opposed to the wise counsel was the beginnings of an army.\nChapter IV\n  Inevitable Warfare\nIblees was still new to battles, but his tactis were wise enough to send first the mortal minions whose will's were bent to unquestionable loyalty at his promises. With sword, spear, and bow the lines of humans rushed towards the collected magi. Steel had\nyet to taste the bitter sting of magic upon its surface, and moral lives paid the price for this lesson. Soon not a soul stood to brandish a weapon against the counsel. Zalam moved in next accompanied by a horde of reanimated corpses. These proved less\nvulnerable to magic, and the tides of battle turned against the magi. The aenguls could dispel of the tainted walking corpses, but more would continue to rise. Zalam struck down an aengul whose name has forever been lost. The other aenguls of the counsel\nfled from the battle, realising that their immortality had its limits. All except for the Wandering Wizard, who rallied the magi. With him keeping Iblees' zombies at bay the magi trapped Zalam in an arcane cage. Furiously he blasted at the cage using\nevery form of magic he had learned. In desperation he screamed out for Iblees to rescue him. But no answer came. He grappled at his cage and poured all his power into breaking it. But the walls remained in tact, and the mortal's body was left drained of\nall energy in the shell of a now wearied old man. His weakened muscles could barely keep him standing, and his brittle bones shattered with every movement. About his neck was fastened a charm that seeped any mana his body could create, magically crippling\nhim so that his mind remained alert behind the broken body of a ruined mortal man.\nChapter V\n        Epilogue\nThe cunning of Iblees was beyond the might of the Wandering Wizard. Though in their magic neither could surmount the other, Iblees was without honour, willing to grasp any opportunity for advantage. The mortal magi rejoined their friend to find the\ntwo interlocked in a furious struggle. Now Iblees saw his opportunity. Lightning rained from the heavens atop the onlooking mortals. Their tragic last screams distracted the Wandering Wizard who sped to their bodies that he might save them.\nElectricity shot from Iblees' fingertip in a concentrated beam. The Wizard's being was struck through the heart. Instantly he seized up in agony. To his side appeared the shoulder of the Arcane Mage, the last survivor of the mortal mages of the counsel.\nHe aided the Wandering Wizard to rise and protected him as another rain of lightning fell from above. The Wizard drew from his pocket a common clear crystal and held it up towards Iblees. An effervescent light shone from its sides engulfing the field of\nbattle in an impenetrable brightness. When the light had dispersed Iblees stood dazed. In his present form he could no longer see. He waited for the affect to wear off but the blindness continued. Enraged he threw fire, ripped the ground assunder,\nand tainted every living thing within miles. But the Wandering Wizard and Arcane Mage remained standing in opposition. He grew all the more furious and brought forth unspeakable horrors, the names of which should never be uttered. But they were likewise\nto no affect. The Wizard and Mage opposed him yet. In a mighty sulk Iblees exploded in a raging fireball and dissappeared from the realm of mortals.\nThe wandering Wizard's power never fully returned from that day, but the Arcane Mage grew wiser still. Knowing that Iblees would appear again, he reasoned with the Four Fathers that they give him no scrap of power. But time would tell if the discernment\nof mortals could resist Iblees' deception. And what became of Zalam? His frail remains was doomes to die the death of mortals. Though whether he did pass on to the Seven Skies has never been confirmed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fnd. Alchemy 3.2", "Kardel Irongut", "___________________ALCHEMICAL FUNDAMENTALS: An overview for the aspirant alchemist.\n___________________Penned By: Professor Doctor Kardel Heronsson Irongut,\nAlch.D, Arcn.D, M.D\n___________________PART 3: ELEMENTARY HERBOLOGY CONT'D\n___________________CHAPTER 3: EARTH HERBOLOGY\n___________________Overview: Tippen's Root, Goblin's Ivy, Alabaster Leaf, Miner's Pick\n___________________\nTIPPEN’S ROOT: MODERATE SYMBOL OF EARTH\n\n _ _\n         (_\\_)\n        (__<_{}\n         (_/_)\n        |\\ |\n         \\\\| /|\n          \\|//\n           |/\n      ,.,.,|.,.,.\nLOCATION: Usually by collapsed trees or truncated stumps in the forest, growing near the roots. Hidden under about a fistful of soil. ((Roll of 14/20 or above)).\nAPPEARANCE: This fleshy, black-and-yellow speckled root ensconces itself under topsoil. It’s location is marked by small clusters of purple flowers which grow directly above it.\nCULTIVATION/PREPARATION: The power of this reagent is concentrated in the speckled root, so simply uproot this herb as it proves quite tough, and is not prone to damage.\nKnown by healers far and wide, Tippen’s root exemplifies earth’s spirit, life, flora, and fauna symbologies very well. It makes a great ingredient in any mending potion, and can be used for salves to heal wounds.\nGOBLIN’S IVY: WEAK SYMBOL OF EARTH\n\n _ _\n         (_\\_)\n        (__<_{}\n         (_/_)\n        |\\ |\n         \\\\| /|\n          \\|//\n           |/\n      ,.,.,|.,.,.\nLOCATION: In dry places, ranging from steppes to deserts. If rain falls less than once a month, Goblin’s Ivy is sure to grow. ((Roll of 9/20 or Above))\nAPPEARANCE: A thin tan-colored vine easily mistaken for something dead. It bears a pungent odour akin to that of fecal matter, and is very common.\nCULTIVATION/PREPARATION: Simply tear this disgusting herb from its perch, often around other plants, and wrap it in a moist towel to dull the stench.\nGoblin’s Ivy is very common and, aside from representing toughness only weakly, \nis a versatile “last-resort” when searching for an earth reagent. It can be used to minorly increase the prolongation of a potion’s effects.\nALABASTER LEAF: MODERATE SYMBOL OF EARTH\n\n _ _\n         (_\\_)\n        (__<_{}\n         (_/_)\n        |\\ |\n         \\\\| /|\n          \\|//\n           |/\n      ,.,.,|.,.,.\nLOCATION: Near the roots of tall, mature trees deep within forests. ((Roll of 14/20 or above)).\nAPPEARANCE: A pale, alabaster coloured leaf with large, bulbous trichomes that segment the entirety of its body. Can be used as a mild poison sure to induce vomit, and is very resilient and tough to tear.\nCULTIVATION/PREPARATION: This earth symbol is relatively easy to cultivate, being very tough and difficult to tear. If consumed, it can cause nausea and vomiting, but is rendered safe when boiled.\nAlabaster Leaf represent earth's toughness, stalwartness, resiliency, and strength aspects very well. It is archetypal in potions of strength, and can be used to greatly increase the potency of any brew.\nMINER’S PICK: STRONG SYMBOL OF EARTH\n\n _ _\n         (_\\_)\n        (__<_{}\n         (_/_)\n        |\\ |\n         \\\\| /|\n          \\|//\n           |/\n      ,.,.,|.,.,.\nLOCATION: Deep within abandoned mineshafts or caves, often growing through large boulders. ((Roll of 17/20 or above)).\nAPPEARANCE: A tough, ivy-plant with grey bark prone to growing through strong rock, the tips of its roots spiralled in a fashion reminiscent of a drill.\nCULTIVATION/PREPARATION: This incredibly rare reagent is notoriously difficult to harvest. It is recommended to bring a pickaxe (or several) along to sever the incredibly hard roots of this herb.\nDwarf’s Pick was discovered by Gauldrin Irongut in Anthos, and is one of the few strong earth herbal reagents. When boiled strongly, it makes a perfectly versatile earth reagent which is a staple in Stoneskin potions.\n___________________CHAPTER 4: AIR HERBOLOGY\n___________________Overview: Crouching Feather, Swamp Blossom, Elf's Hair Vine\n___________________\nCROUCHING FEATHER: STRONG SYMBOL OF AIR\n\n _ _\n         (_\\_)\n        (__<_{}\n         (_/_)\n        |\\ |\n         \\\\| /|\n          \\|//\n           |/\n      ,.,.,|.,.,.\nLOCATION: Hidden in bushes deep within deciduous forests, often growing close to the forest floor below thick brush. ((Roll of 17/20 or above))\nAPPEARANCE: A cluster of feather like white-yellowish leaves which are very light and fragile.\nCULTIVATION/PREPARATION: When dealing with this herb, be careful not to crush its delicate leaves as that is where its symbolic properties are the most concentrated. It is recommended to use thin scissors for this herb.\nCrouching feather is a versatile air reagent which symbolizes all of air’s inherent properties. It is best used in potions of wizard’s wisdom, due to its particular potency.\nSWAMP BLOSSOM: MODERATE SYMBOL OF AIR\n\n _ _\n         (_\\_)\n        (__<_{}\n         (_/_)\n        |\\ |\n         \\\\| /|\n          \\|//\n           |/\n      ,.,.,|.,.,.\nLOCATION: Atop tall trees in Swamps. ((Roll of 14/20 or above)).\nAPPEARANCE: Notable due to its large petals of several colours, usually streaks of blue, purple, yellow, and white. Large sac filled with liquid at the base of the pistils.\nCULTIVATION/PREPARATION: Be careful when cultivating this plant as it is quite dangerous: many an alchemist have broken limbs by falling off the canopies that this herb favours.\nSwamp Blossom best exemplifies acuity, celerity, and speed. It’s symbolic potential is contained within the sac at its center, which houses a light liquid that moves through the fingers like quicksilver.\nELF’S HAIR VINE: STRONG SYMBOL OF AIR \n _ _\n         (_\\_)\n        (__<_{}\n         (_/_)\n        |\\ |\n         \\\\| /|\n          \\|//\n           |/\n      ,.,.,|.,.,.\nLOCATION: On the edges of high cliffs. ((Roll of 17/20 or Above)).\nAPPEARANCE: Long, wispy, and pale, almost like locks of blonde hair. Nearly transparent in the sunlight, and very light in the hand.\nCULTIVATION/PREPARATION: Take care not to fall off a precipice when cultivating this reagent. Carefully pull up its long, wispy leaves towards you, making sure not to crush them.\nElf’s Hair Vine is particularly good at exemplifying Air’s more abstract potentials: namely, wisdom, intelligence, and clarity. It is a staple in any brew of Wizard’s Wisdom.\nA NOTE ON THE AUTHOR:\n\tProfessor-Doctor Kardel Heronsson Irongut, an alchemist of prestige and great renown, is famed for his contributions to the Alchemy community.\nMost famed for standardizing the recipe for Alchemist’s Fire and creating the recipe for the Potion of Regeneration, Doctor Irongut holds several diplomas and certifications in all types of alchemy and currently teaches at the Academy of Holm.", ""),
        StaticBook("For Luna", "Ethel Rose", "For Luna\n\n\nFrom your loving wife\n       Ethel Rose\nLuna,\nBefore I met you I felt like I was stuck in eternal darkness. Like I was somehow being punished for all the wrongs that I had done in this world. Until you came and made yourself my light shining in the darkness. I would have been consumed if it\nweren't for you. When I had first met you in the Dragur Library I could have never guessed of the events coming after. We've come so far. We have beautiful children, and a roof over our heads. I couldn't have asked for anything else. Nor could I have\npossibly made it any better. Believe me when I say that I love you more than I have ever loved anyone else. You've given me so much and I'd give the world for you. I was so scared when you were forced into labor. Even though everything turned out alright\nfor both you and Elinor I still feared that you wouldn't make it. I hope to spend the rest of my life with you my love. With you and all of our beautiful children. Even if we do spoil them too much.\n From, your loving wife Ethel Rose.\n[!] On this page would be a expertly drawn portrait of the entire family. Even Luna's owls and Ethel's Karin being drawn on the page.", ""),
        StaticBook("For Q", "Nikoru Shuroda", "Dear Q,\n\nYou know how I told you that you sleep horribly unless your snuggling someone with a comforting sense about them?\nWell, I'd figure I'd get you this plushie to help you sleep better when no ones near.\nI hope you like it. It's not much but it's all I could find...\n\nWhile we're here, I also wanted to tell you...thank you. Ye'know, for everything.  I'd think If it wasn't for you folks...I'd probably be dead.\nI've also been thinking...\nIt was Mika who brought me to you guys wasn't it?\n\nI don't think I can ever forgive him...or forget what he's done, not only to me but countless others.\nI've been planning to do research..on magical items...\nMaybe I can find something about his scythe...\n\n\nBut that's other business stuff.\nFrom this day forward I wish you and Tamara the best of wishes\nAfterall it's not everyday a lady finds a rare catch.\n\n~Nikky.\n\nP.S\nNo this isn't a goodbye letter. So don't take it as one.\n\nI'd just figured i'd tell multiple things in the same letter.", ""),
        StaticBook("For The King", "Ravondir", "Please remove my Oslyan flag from your wall.\n\nYour Dearest,\nJekre 'Shinluk", ""),
        StaticBook("For you.", "Ser Ajax Ironwood II", "To the woman who stole my heart.\nPerhaps you broke the law, or perhaps I let you take it. I am missing my heart, and I do not want it back. You can keep it, really, because it suits you well.\nYou've stolen the heart of a warrior, a knight, and a man. You have his strength, his loyalty and his love. You truely are special to a man who thinks like this.\nPerhaps, one day, you will fully understand the meaning of this little note, or maybe it will be too late; fate will be the teller of this tale, fair lady, and friend.", ""),
        StaticBook("Forbidden Tome", "Druid", "*A dusty, unlabeled tome. It bears more weight than most.*\n\nhttp://tinyurl.com/jlh46vp\n\n(mirror, just in case)\n\nhttp://bit.ly/2fdrcv3", ""),
        StaticBook("Forest of Cieli", "Jaya Jayamen", "==-==-====()=\n===,---,==-==-=\n,--'===='-,=====\n========='-,,,_-'\n====_==;;;==../ \\=\n==_/ \\=;;=,_/___\\\n=/ \\__\\=./ \\___\\\n/___\\_\\/___\\U=\n/___\\==/___\\==\n==U=;;==.==U===;;", ""),
        StaticBook("Forest Poem", "Daisy Applefoot", "Praise be the Dunshire woods, o' so glorious and green.\nFor without them, we'd be no goods, and all the much too lean.\nYet in spite of this, the trees are cut, and the apples be running low.\nSo I guess its time to drink our last, for our death\nbe slow", ""),
        StaticBook("Forgetten Dwarf", "Davin Lodmund", "The Forgotten Dwarves - What Is Known\nThe Forgotten Dwarves of Athera are the extinct people of the lands to the far northwest, far past the great Eruthos Canyon. We know very little about them but suspect them to be the\nbuilders of the Great Doors, ten of which are hidden around Athera. We believe these doors to be entrances to Forgotten Dwarven cities long sealed, but the work of our best spellcrafters has failed to open them: the Forgotten Dwarves were\nhighly skilled at sealing things. The key to unlocking these doors likely lies in their capital, the fabled “Hall of the Ancients”, referred to as Urguan’s Hall in the texts of the Dwarves of Aegis, at least prior to the ascent of the Empire of\nKhorvad and their suppression and destruction of such texts. While we believe some texts survived, they too were lost when the Scriberfolk cult fled through the hidden one-way portals to “Asulon”, on what we believe is the other side of the mortal plane.\nFrom what we can discern, the Forgotten Dwarves were somewhat more advanced than their modern kin. Technology stagnated under the boot of the Empire of Khorvad now that it has been overthrown by the\nBlackaxe-led rebels a culture of violence pervades the dwarves that no doubt will take many generations to die out.\nWe have been unable to discern the age of the Forgotten Dwarves but our best evidence suggests that\ntheir extinction occurred just before Year 0 by the Aegean calendar: the date of the Ravager’s first defeat and long before the founding of Rivel. This would appear to contradict the Aegean belief that the four brothers were\nthe first of their species and the fathers of civilisation. If this is the case, and that the Aegean Dwarves are the surviving descendants of the Forgotten Dwarves (no doubt led by the dwarf known as Urguan) then one can only begin to\nspeculate how the modern dwarves lost the technological expertise of the Forgotten Dwarves. Perhaps a schism occurred, causing the departure of Urguan’s faction, which would have been less technologically minded, and thus\nallowed them to escape extinction. Much remains uncovered, and it is my hope that our investigations into the Forgotten Dwarves under the direction of the Radiant Man in the interests of survival may also be in the interests of\nuncovering history.\n- Spellcrafter Tarien Arvius", ""),
        StaticBook("Fork Illusion", "Jaya Jayamen", "/\\\n       /\\ \\ \\\n   /\\ \\ \\ \\ \\\n   \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\\n    \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\\n     \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\\n      \\ \\ \\ \\ \\ \\\n       \\ \\ \\/  \\ \\\n        \\ \\/   / /\n         \\      \\ \\\n          \\  /\\ \\ \\ \n           \\/ /\\/_/\n            \\/", ""),
        StaticBook("Formal Request", "Arend Wick", "~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Herein lies a formal request from the Lord Marshal Rhys var Ruthern, on behalf of the Hansetian Republican Army, and the New Hansetian Homefront Army for resources and space for weapons development.\nWe formally request the following items:\n\n10x Training Batons\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~300 Mina for materials testing\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~A laboratory for materials testing (if possible)\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~As much Carrion Black as can be supplied.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nSigned,\nCommander Arend Wick, of the line of Wick, of the Lineage of Wick, Grand Wick of the ancestry of Wick, before Horen, there was Wick, true heirs to the Embermoore, kings of Vandoria and the Westerlands and Wick uh, Land,\nvanguard of the Wick Wood, true Hansetian patriot, veteran of the Renatian Aggression, Commander of the Hansetian Republican Army\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~", ""),
        StaticBook("Fort Lodmund", "Virkian Agnew", "Henry Lodmund.\nHead of House Lodmund.\n\nDeed of the Fort Southeast of Pembroke's walls.\n\nFort Lodmund.\nNo Taxes or Tariffs.\nMilitary settlement.\nEmployed by House Lodmund and vassals.", ""),
        StaticBook("FP-01.1 - Jak", "Adler", "5th of The Deep Cold, 1680\n\nJakhatir Irongut has finished his punishment for the murder of Virre Vitreous. He is not to receive any further punishment for this crime. \n\n- Adler\nSheriff of Adria", ""),
        StaticBook("FP-02: Antanios", "Adler", "Antanios Rutledge\nHuman\nAttempted Murder\nAlive\n1681\n---------------\nDescription\n\nBlack & grey, hooded robes - concealing his visage. Pale skin, tormented visage.\nWhilst enjoying a nice pint of ale in the tavern, accompanied by multiple other residents, I heard a strange sound outside.\n\nUpon investigation, an individual in dark robes - concealing his visage with a hood - was stood with his blade unsheathed ...\ndragging it across the gravel path.\n\nAfter a short attempt to speak to the individual, requesting that he sheathed his sword, he charged at myself. I was prepared for such, sword unsheathed, and was able to successfully parry the attack ...\nThe man then attempted to kick me in the stomach, which failed as a result of my armour; simply causing me to stumble back slightly. I recovered fast from this, and was able to land a successful slash, directed at the individual's hand that ...\nhe held the sword in. \n\nAfter such; he was tackled to the ground, and was revealed to be Antanios Rutledge; a guardsman that had gone missing around a year ago - prior to my rise to my position.\n\nHis wounds were treated, and was ...\nlocked in the cells below the Belvitz Guard compound.\n\nAntanios continued to show signs of feral behaviour; attempting to conceal his visage, specifically his eyes. To combat this, his room was stripped of such that would aid him, and was kept in ...\nlight conditions throughout the duration of his arrest.\n\nEventually after a week or so; the man was allowed a visit from friends/family. Three individuals visited him; his partner, Rivaini, and two friends - Axel Swale & Nathan.\nThroughout this; they attempted to have him released, however he was still believed to be feral, and a danger to society.\n\n[!] A side-notation is marked in brackets to the side of the previous paragraph:\n\"To be honest, the only reason that I did not ...\nexecute Antanios on the spot was because of his service within the Order of St Emma, and the role that he played within the removal of the traitorous Vladan Valic.\".\n\nEventually after many weeks of keeping him close - and a scuffle or two..\n- Antanios was released.\n\nThough, despite this, I will keep a close eye on the man; as he still acts suspiciously, and I believe that there could be deeper issues that may return in the future if triggered.\nWitnesses\n\nSeth, Human\nAmphion Enthelor, Human\nEve, Human\nEdwar' 'Fang', Human\nRivani, Farfolk\nAxel Swale, Human\nNathan, Human\n---------------\n      CONTINUED ->\nThis individual has completed their punishment for their crimes, and is not to be stopped by the Belvitz Guard for anything related to said crime. If there are any concerns, please contact myself.\n\n- Adler, Sheriff of Adria\n1681", ""),
        StaticBook("Friend or Foe?", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Gather some intel on a dreadlander from the Dunamis Fort outside our walls.", ""),
        StaticBook("Friendly Greetin", "Violet Evergreen", "Hello! \nMy name is Violet. I'm a new neighbor in the area. I brought you cookies!\nHope to meet you soon\n\nSincerely\nV.E", ""),
        StaticBook("Friends", "Isabella Jameson", "Bunny rabbit lived in the forest. He had many friends. He was proud of his friends. One day Bunny rabbit heard the loud barking of wild dogs. He was very scared. He decided to ask for help.  He quickly went to his friend deer.\nHe said, “Dear friend, some wild dogs are chasing me. Can you chase them away with your sharp antlers?” he deer said, “That is right, I can. But now I am busy. Why don’t you ask bear for help?” Bunny rabbit ran to the bear.\n“My dear friend, you are very strong. Please help me. Some wild dogs are after me. Please chase them away,” he requested to the bear. The bear replied, “I am sorry. I am hungry and tired. I need to find some food. Please ask the monkey for help.”\nPoor Bunny went to the monkey, the elephant, the goat and all his other friends. Bunny felt sad that nobody was ready to help him. He understood that he had to think of a way out by himself. He hid under a bush. He lay very still.\nThe wild dogs did not find the bunny. They went chasing other animals. Bunny rabbit learnt that he had to learn to survive by himself, not depending on his unhelpful friends.", ""),
        StaticBook("From Aesil", "Chief Naval Officer Aesilnoth", "[!] This note has been carefully written in elegant handwriting.\n\n\"Dear Nami,\nI'm so glad you felt the same as I did. I was very nervous to tell you, but I felt I needed to. You make me feel so happy and I'm so glad I got to meet you. You've-\nmade me feel like it was worth living again after both of my parents passing. I wish to spend my entire life with you if you would allow it.\n\nWith love,\nAesil\" \n[!]As you open this page a single red rose would be enclosed inside.", ""),
        StaticBook("From Hobbs", "Hobbs Burrows", "A Slip of Sheepskin Parchment\n\nDear Mrs Applefoot, \n\nI have not known you long, nor you me, and so there are some things you do not know about me. Despite being a burrower by trade, a skill passed down through generations of Burrows before\nme, I am a historian in my free time. For a while I have been investigating, tracking down, transcribing, and protecting old Halfling texts. I find that the preservation of our folk's way of life in more dire straits than ever. \n\nThat is why I have\nentrusted you with these texts. They are of the Halflings who came long before us, but will endure on paper long after we are gone from this world.\n\nI do not know what you will do with them, I only trust that they will be kept in good hands.\nIf we do not have a library, perhaps the Druids can be trusted with them as they are known for their preservation of knowledge, particularly the works of Petyr (of which there are many). You may wish to keep them for personal use and study, however, it is\nentirely up to you.\n\nHowever, my bones are old and my burrowing days are behind me. Even my eyes are starting to go, which makes reading and writing these texts even more difficult. \n\nPlease know that even when I seem absent,\nthe mists rising off of Dunshire Lake on an early morning still stirs my soul like nothing else does. \n\nFor many years, I have planned to write the second volume of A History of Halflings. The first volume of which Petyr wrote, which ended as\nwe folk left Aegis and sailed to Asulon. I never thought I could do it justice, but I have endeavoured to finish the task nonetheless. It would be good to have our entire histories documented, as you have knowledge that I do not. \n\nI leave content in the\nknowledge that there are still people good of heart in the world. That there are, and always will be, those who tinker, who farm, drink, laugh, sing, bake, fish, burrow, and share with a friend. If there is one thing this old Halfling has learned, it is\nthat the world needs us.\n\nFinally, I enclose a drawing of the townsfolk of Branborough and their children all stood under the party tent on the Tookwater River. Petyr, Faldo, Tibb, Lobo and all the rest have left their\nsignatures below it. I hope this trinket of days gone by will ease the pain of my leaving.\n\nSincerely,\nHobbs Burrows of Dunshire Village.", ""),
        StaticBook("Frost Witches", "Gallidron Elindrow", "An\n       Encounter\n           With\n      Frost Witches\n/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\/\\\n\n            By\n   Gallidron Elindrow\nI first learned of the dreaded creatures known as Frost Witches from one of the tomes of the grand libraries of old Haelun'or. I remember the fear that gripped me as a child when I learned of their macabre ways. Though as an adult of more mature\nconstitution and greater understanding, I revisted the subject of \"monsters\" and relearned the available details of the Frost Witch.\nThay are exclusivly women, so far as any adventurer who's survived an encounter with them can tell. They are grotesque and\nunnatural to look upon. Grey skinned and with eyes like ice they appear in their true form. But it is not so easy to spot them, for Ice Witches are masters of disguise and employ illusion to hide their nature. In fact, as the story goes, they will adopt\nthe guise of a young woman and sit and cry in the midst of a snowy glade to lure in unsuspecting men. The clever frost witch will attract the unwitting male and take him to the rest of her coven. There to be devoured by these fiends. They are, without\nexception, powerful magic users, though the older ones are the more dangerous and adept. In fact, every frost witch draws her power from a \"Witch Mother\" who is the head of her particular coven. Like unto a queen bee she will build her nest and gather\n\\    \"   `  I  '   \"     /\n  \\   \"   ` I '  \"     /\n    \\  O  {X}  O   /\n    /\\ , O II O ,  /\\ \n^ / % \\  ! I !   / % \\ ^\nl/ ``~'' \\  %  / ``~'' \\l\n\\ * X *  \\  /  * X * /\n  \\ i i,.,{   x   },.,i i /\n    \\     /  \\     /\n      \\ / `  ' \\  /\n            %\nG1\nworkers who rely upon her, and she them to some extent. When another frost witch is of sufficient power and experience she may set out to create her own coven. They begin by searching for women who are depressed or sadened. The frost witch will then mark\nwoman with a curse that will appear as little more than a bruise upon the back of the woman's neck. If the marked female succombs to her sadness and grief, she will become a frost witch herself. Thus do their numbers swell. It is reportedly a favorite\ntactic of the frost witches to eat a married man and then mark his grieving widow. Thus they gain both a meal and a potential coven member. The woman who is marked may not become a frost witch \"if her faith is strong and she resist her sadness to seek\nafter joy\", as the old tomes say. Though it should be noted that there is no known way to remove the curse once it is applied. The woman in question will most likely live with the mark for the rest of her days.\nIn order to destroy a frost witch coven one must destroy the witch mother. In some cases this alone is enough to cause the coven to whither and die over time. In other cases, however, another witch may be of sufficient strength to rise up and assume the\nrole of witch mother and the coven can limp on. If one is a \"monster hunter\" of sorts, then you will likely want to exterminate as many of the witches as possible to reduce the chances of this occuring.\nIt is important to note that frost witches are not rabid animals. They are clever and capable of reasoning. It is possible to treat with them, but the humor of the witch can change quickly and every moment you stand in their pressence you are in grave\ndanger. In truth they are fickle and there is no telling what a frost witch might do, should you seek to speak with them. It is said, however, that if one finds a frost witch in disguise and calls them out, the frost witch is bound by her curse to offer\nthe clever mortal one favor. But this is only rumor and would prove dangerous to study.\nA great deal of the knowledge I possess has come from the reading of books. But I have done some field research as well. The following pages will detail my, albeit brief, encounter with the frost witches.\nI was told of a coven of frost witches to be found far in the north, by a man of the nation of Salvas. His name was Archrim Elmoran and he had encoutered these witches himself. How the man survived I do not know, for it seems that the witches were intent\non eating him. I told me that there was an ancient ruin that the witches called home, upon a lonely and frozen peak. The coordinates were as follows.\n{X 153, Y -3762}\n\nI, being curious, set out to see this for myself. I traveled far into the north from\nmy home in the warm waters of New Haelun'or and traversed the mountains of the north.\n\nThere, I found a most curious set of ruins which seemed to at one point have been a church or temple of some sort. They were in a valley to the south of the\nreported witches lair. It is there that I found the symbols marked G1 (glyph 1) which you saw earlier in this book.  What ever ancient civilization left these ruins, I would be most interested to learn more about them. Whilst searching about I had the\ngood fortune to happen upon another Mali'aheral, a High Elf woman named Allona. After ensuring that she was not one of the dreaded frost witches I asked what she was doing in those parts. Apparently she was a mage and had sought solitude to meditate and\nincrease her skills. The ruins that we were in had provided such solitude until I had interrupted it. She warned me that the frost witches where still about, though further up the mountain range, and she advised me against going to investigate the area.\nWe spoke for a while longer before she showed me a cavern that she had discovered just north of the ruins. It held an ancient library of sorts and had evidently been of some importance to whatever people had left it behind. The books were too ruined to\nread, but the very exsistance of such a place is highly facinating. However, I digress.\n\nAfter parting ways I decided to go on and look in on the frost witches. It was not my intention to actually interact with them or get close enough to do so.\nWhen I approached their lonely peak an icey wind blew past me and seemed to steal the very warmth of my blood away. An ancient and imposing structure sat atop the peak and looked for all the world to be abandoned. Using some wit and no small amount of\ndexterity I climbed the peak, agianst my better judgment and explored the old fortress.\n\nIt was empty as I suspected, though the air was somehow even colder within. After looking around a bit I thought I saw foot prints in the snow, or at the very least\nimpressions of where something had been. They were by an alcove under the main floor of the ruin. As I approached I heard something moving on the other side of the alcove and quickly hid. A wall moved out and one of the menacing creatures emerged\ncautiosly from the hole. The frost witch looked about as though she knew I was there and crept forward. For all the world I thought I was doomed. Doomed for my curiosity and for my foolish assumption that the keep was empty. Only then did I realize. They\ndid not live in the delapidated structure atop the mountain, they lived beneith it. A man from Salvas had told me that those mountains were full of caverns and tunnels.\n\nThe witch moved forward and I could have sworn she could smell me. Then, just before\nshe reached my hiding place, she turned and went up the stairs to the main floor. I took no more chances and I ran for my life. I was out of the keep and down the mountain as quickly as gravity and semi-safe desent would permit.\nIn closing. Frost Witches are a dangerous facination and one should not seek them lightly. They are still there, so far as I know, lurking in the tunnels beneath that frozen mountian. \nI hope this book has been interesting at least and helpful at best.\nI hope that you remember what you have read should you ever have....\n\nAn encounter with Frost Witches.\nPublishing date\n18th of Deep cold, 1516\n\nby Gallidron Elindrow\n\nDedicated to Archrim Elmoran, the human who risked life and limb to discover the hold of the Frost Witches and told me about it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Frost Witches", "An Elder Cleric", "A Guide To\n     Frost Witches\n\n\n            by\n     An Elder Cleric\nIntroduction\n\nA feeling of dire cold creeping into the air, a dainty laugh on the wind akin to tinkling crystal...\n\nAnd long rows of sharp, ravenous teeth...facilitating an undying hunger for the flesh of men.\nIntroduction\n\nThat, dear reader, was my first introduction with the Fjaurriuga, more locally known as the 'Frost Witches', of which this book is about. Within, you will learn how to identify and more easily combat the frost-ridden witches.\nHow to Identify\n\nFrost witches are masters of illusion, making it difficult to identify them. This is touched upon later in further depth. However, their true form is an icy blue and their skin is constantly cold. They hold a distaste for heat.\nWeaknesses\n\nAs stated, Frost Witches cannot stand the heat for very long, as their bodies are a version of corrupted ice. Because of their physiology, attacks to their body crack and shatter instead of cut or maim.\nWeaknesses\n\nFrost Witches, like other dark creatures, are weak to Holy magics. \n\nThese beings also have a hunger for flesh that will drive them to feast on males that if not fed, destroys them in time.\nStrengths\n\nThe Frost Witches are masters of illusion magic, allowing them to transform their image into that of other descendants to hide their true form. They do not gain the attributes, such as strength, of these forms.\nStrengths\n\nHowever, they also gain immortality and a body 'frozen in time' of their true form. They are immune to cold and become powerful mages of ice and snow, becoming twice as strong as a water or ice voidal mage.\nPowers\n\nAs stated, they are twice as strong and efficent with Ice and Snow magic. They also grow sharpened teeth in their true form, allowing them to rip and tear flesh. Some even grow claws to eviscerate their victims.\nTemperment\n\nFrost Witches are born from women that feel lonely and rejected by love, forcing their curse to feast on the flesh of males. They'll generally be in the company of other women, excluding that of their male prey.\nTemperment\n\nThey are able to control themselves to blend into society, however they are controlled by their hunger. If they go too long without feasting, they will expose themselves.\nConclusion\n\nFrost Witches are beings that are cursed women that have succumbed to the sadness and grief within their hearts. If you suspect a woman of being such, bring them near an open flame. But be prepared for combat all the same!", ""),
        StaticBook("Frostbeard Clan", "Hamlin Frostbeard", "Frostbeard Clan\n--===============--\nThe Frostbeard clan is an elder sometimes called Azwytrumm in dwarven founded by Kaz'Ulrah son of Urguan mostly know for standing against Urguan many times and returning finally left Urguan for the final time and\ncreated its own great dwarven kingdom of Kaz'Ulrah.\n\nTo know of what dwarf belongs to this clan is rather easy as all dwarfs of this clan has there icy blue eyes and blue war paint most of the dwarfs also have a bear pelt\nover there shoulder which they obtain through trials. \n\nThe Colours of the clan are blue and white which they show in there clothing style and always wear there bear pelts to show all that they have gained honor through the clan trials.\nLife of a Frostbeard is rather harsh as being a large clan of them who are battle born and ready for a fight strength a key thing along with Loyalty and Honor being above it for there Loyalty to there clan father and each other can never be broken as long\nas there honor can hold them. As all dwarfs drinking and mining and a brawls are mostly seen when you see a Frostbeard for they care not of holding back.\n\nReligion in the Frostbeards are the Brathmordakin like all dwarfs but\nsome also worships Wyrvun along with the Brathmordakin but they pray to Wyrvun in times of battle for Wyrvun aengul of cold and righteousness.\nLaws of the Frostbeards\n--===============--Do Not Cause Harm to a Fellow Frostbeard\n\nDo Not steal from a fellow Frostbeard\n\nDo not badmouth a fellow Frostbeard\n\nAlways back up a fellow Frostbeard\nListen to your Elders and the Clan Father\n\nThe Clan Father's word is final\n\nIn case of the Clan Father becoming Grand King, he must pass on the title of Clan Father to another Frostbeard\nLoyalty to the Clan Father is a must\n\nSurrendering in battlle is not an option", ""),
