h\n13/5/2018\nEEST\n19:33-20:33\n1 hour\n\nNothing happened.(RECORDED)\nSamuel Lythian\n5/14/2018\nCST\nTime In: 4:37 PM\nTime Out: 5:37 PM\n\nNothing Happened.(RECORDED)\nEvan Lythian\n5/14/2018\nCST\nTime In:5:50\nTime Out:7:50\nNotes:I had my heart broken, yelled at a halfling, fell from the gate house, and got really sad...(RECORDED)\nSamuel Lythian\n5/16/2018\nCST\nTime In: 7:53 PM\nTime Out: 8:25 PM\n\nNothing Happened.(rECORDED)\nMarrow Scaevolus\n5/17/2018\nEST\nTime In: 7:05pm\nTime Out: 8:10pm\nTotal Time: 1 hour\n\nNothing Happened(RECORDED)\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n18/5/2018\nEEST\n10:20-11:20\n1 hour\n\nNothing happened.(RECORDED)\nOmega\n18/5/18\nGTM1\n22-23\n1 hour\n\nSome persons enter and some persong go out.(RECORDED)\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n18.5.2018-19.5.2018\nEEST\n23:01-00:01\n1 hour\n\nNothing happened.(RECORDED)\nMarrow Scaevolus\n5/18/2018\nEST\nTime In: 8:59\nTime Out: 11:53pm\nTotal Time: 2 hours\n\nA bunch of bragging idiots got killed by the guard.\n(RECORDED)\nCelia SwiftGale\n2018/05/18\nCST\nTime in 2300\nTime out 0000\n1 Hour\n(RECORDED)\nRhillen\n2018/5/19\nCEST\ntime in : 10:00\ntime out : 13:00\n3 hours\n(RECORDED)\nNilth Mustang\n2018/5/19\nEEST\nTime in: 3:50 pm\nTime out 4:10 pm\n\nnothing happened\n(RECORDED)\nNorton Brown\n19/5/2018\nGMT+2\n19.42\n20.42\n\nNothing special, some construction going on.\n(RECORDED)\nThrak Opalmane\n05/19/2018\nCST\n2:27 PM\n2:52 PM\n25 minutes\n\nNothing of interest happened.\n(RECORDED)\nOdeboy\n19/5/2018\nGMT+2\n22.33\n23.33\n\nNothing happened. \n(RECORDED)\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n19/5/2018-20/5/2018\nEEST\n22:20-0:20\n2 hours\n\n\nA couple red alerts, nothing much else.\n(RECORDED)\nAthonir Silva\n19/5/18-20/5/18\nGmt +2\n23.30-00.30\n1 hour\n\nalittle bit of traffic to the end of the shift a lot of people came through the gate had to check all....\n(RECORDED)\nCelia SwiftGale\n2018/05/19\n1700-1800\nCST\n\nNothing special to report\n(RECORDED)\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n20/5/2018\nEEST\n00:29-2:29\n2 hours\n\n'Twas pretty peaceful at the gate, but in the city some elf disturbed the peace.\n(RECORDED)\nMeryn Oakheart\n20/5/2018\nGMT\n17:20-18:20\n1 Hour\n\nNothing important happened.\n(RECORDED)\nNilth Mustang\n2018/05/20\n8:30 pm - 9:00 pm\n(RECORDED)\nThrak Opalmane\n05/20/2018\nCST\n2:18 PM\n2:52 PM\n34 minutes\n(RECORDED)\nRhillen\n05/20/2018\nCEST\n12:00 - 19:00\n9 hours\n(RECORDED)\nCelia Swift\n2018/05/21\nCST\n1500-1600\nRequesting former guardss be relieved of gate keys, and that gate keys be limited to guards only\n(RECORDED)\nAthonir Silva\n22/5/18\nGmt +2\n18.30-20.20\n1 hour 50 mins\n\nnothing special\n(RECORDED)\nMeyn Oakheart\n22/05/2018\n18:30\n19:30\n1 Hour\n\nNothing much to report.\n(RECORDED)\nGaroll Earl\n22/05/18\nGMT\n5:47\n8:47\n3 hours...\n\nNothing, besides the realisation that I need to get a social life of some sort.\n(RECORDED)\nSamuel Lythian\n5/22/2018\nCST\n1:15 AM\n2:00 AM\n\nNothing happened.\n(RECORDED)\nAthonir Silva\n5/23/18\nGmt +2\n18.35-19.45\n1 hour 10 mins\n\nhad some traffic and arguing nothing special tho\n(RECORDED)\nMeryn Oakheart\n23/5/2018\n17:00\n18:00\n1 Hour\n\nNothing but some arguing, kept it under control.\n(RECORDED)\nAthonir Silva\n25/5/18\n19.40-20.40\nAnd\n21.20-22.20\n2 hours\n\npreparing for a possible raid coming\n\n(RECORDED)\nSamuel Lythian\n5/25/2018\n1:24 PM\n1:54 PM\n30 mins.\n\n(RECORDED)\nErwin Gerold\n5/26/2018\n\n2:16PM\n3:16PM\n1 Hour\nAnother ordinary day.\n(RECORDED)", ""),
        StaticBook("GATE DUTY BOOK 4", "Dimlin Irongut", "Gate House Log Book\nRecord In Format Of:\n\n[Name]\n[Date]\n[TimeZone]\n[Time In]\n[Time Out]\n[Total Time]\nSamuel Lythian\n5/25/2018\nCST\n4:10 PM\n4:35 PM\n\nNothing Happened\n(RECORDED\nSamuel Lythian\n5/25/2018\nCST\n1:40 PM (Right after raid)\n2:10 PM\n\nRecovered from Raid. (Writing this retroactively as the old book was full.)\n(RECORDED)\nNorton Brown\n25/5/2018\nGMT+2\n23.45\n0.45\n\nNothing happened.(rECORDED\nAthonir Silva\n26/5/18\nGMT+2\n00.00-01.00\n1 hour\n\nso TIRED....(RECORDED)\nErwin Gerold\n26/5/2018\nGMT+8\n6:44PM\n1:30AM\n7 Hours\n\nNothing happened (RECORDED)\nMarrow Scaevolus\n5/26/2018\nEST\n10:40pm\n12:08am\n1 hour 30 minutes\n\nSome boy prince of renatus and too many dwarves showed up. Evan and I discussed romance.(RECORDED)\nErwin Gerold\n5/26/2017\nGMT+8\n8:44PM\n9:44PM\n1 Hour\nNothing.(RECORDED)\nGaroll Earl\n27/5/18\n14:23 \n16:27\n2 hours (and a bit which was eh)\n\nWell, some child tried to mug me, which didn't go too well for her, but she won't be here again, luckily.(RECORDED)\nGaroll Earl\n28/5/18\n11:58\n14:05\n2 hours\n\nEmpty... Peaceful, but empty.(RECORDED)\n(Forgot to Log)\nEvan Lythian\n5/23/18\ntime in:5:50\ntime out:7:50\nCST\nNotes:Yelled at some halfling to scram(RECORDED)\n(Forgot to Log)\nEvan Lythian\n5/24/18\nTime in:4:40PM\nTime out:6:40PM\nCST\nNotes:Nothing(RECORDED)\n(Forgot to log)\nEvan Lythian\n5/25/2018\nTime In:6:00PM\nTime Out:8:00PM\nCST\nNotes:nothing of interest, some drunks yelled at me.(RECORDED)\n(Forgot to log)\nEvan Lythian\n5/26/2018\nTime in:10:00PM\nTime out:12:00AM\nCST\nYelled at orcs.(RECORDED)\n(Forgot to Log)\nEvan Lythian\n5/27/2018\nTime in: 2:00 AM\nTime out: 4:00AM\nCST\n\nEerily quiet, think the gate house may be haunted... just incase I lined it with salt.(RECORDED)\nEvan Lythian\n5/28/2018\nTime in:1:30PM\nTime out:3:30 PM\nCST(RECORDED)\nHenrik Stoneblood\n30/05/18\nGMT\nTime In: 21:18\nTime Out:21:53\nTotal Time: 35 mins(RECORDED)\nMarrow Scaevolus\n30/5/15\nEST\nTime in: 6:10pm\nTime out: 6:53pm\nTotal TIme: 43 minutes(RECORDED)\nEvan Katke(Formally Lythian)\n5/30/18\nCST\nTime in:7:20\nTime out:9:20(RECORDED)\nNorton Brown\n5/6/2018\nGMT+2\n22:55\n23:55\n\nNothing happened.\n(rECORDED)\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n5/6/2018-6/6/2018\nEEST\n22:58-00:58\n2 hours\n\nSomeone came to harrass me and Norton. It pretty quickly escalated in a fight between him and Norton.(RECORDED)\nEvan Katke\n5/6/2018\nTime in:10:00PM CST\nTime out:12:00AM CST\nCST\nNothing happened(rECORDED)\nEvan Katke\n6/6/2018\nTime in:12:00AM\nTime out:2:00AM\nCST\nNothing happened(RECORDED)\nMarrow Scaevolus\n6/9/2018\nTime in: 6:36pm\nTime out: 7:36pm\nEST\n\nPeople complained. I am now depressed.(RECORDED)\nEvan Lythian\n6/10/2018\nTime in:12:30PM\nTime out:2:30PM\nCST(RECORDED)\nGaroll Earl\n10/6/18\n8:00\n10:00\nGMT\n\nNothing.\n\nRECORDED\nWulf \n10/6/18\n8:00\n10:00\nGMT\n\nNone.\n\nRECORDED\nNorton Brown\n10/6/18\n8:00\n10:00\nGMT\n\nN/A\n\nRECORDED\nMarrow Scaevolus\n6/10/2018\nTime in: 7:03pm\nTime out: 8:05pm\nEST\n\nA rather witty elf came in and I wasted a night of my life that I will never get back. Cheers.\n\nRECORDED\nMarrow Scaevolus\n6/11/2018\nTime in: 7:10pm\nTime out: 8:08pm\nEST\n\nNothing happened.\n\nRECORDED\nErwin Gerold\n6/12/2\n11:35AM\n3:20PM\nGMT+8\n\nNothing\n\nRECORDED\nMarrow Scaevolus\n6/12/2018\nTime in: 6:23pm\nTime out: 7:00pm\nEST\n\nNothing\n\nRECORDED\nEvan and Hyperion\nTime in:4:10 PM\nTime out: 5:10 PM\nCST\n\nRECORDED\nMarrow Scaevolus\n6/14/2018\nTime in: 7:15pm\nTime out: 8:10pm\nEST\n\nLiterally nothing happened. It was quiet... too quiet... Foreboding to say the least... Spooky... Drama...\nRECORDED\nKazrin Starbreaker\n6-14-18\n8:30 to 9:30\nhst \n(est)\n2:30 to 3:30\nNothing out of the ordinary  just quiet\n\nRECORDED\nKazrin Starbreaker\n6/15/18\n2:00 pm to 3:00 pm\nAn orc and olog brothers come in to the academy lookin for learning. Caused a bit of fright for Eris and a halflin. Jakhatir beleives that the Adel told him the orcs called the Ironguts a bunch of\ncoward and confronted the two.\nAdel (who was there in the academy) denied it and took side with the orcs. The orcs were offended and tensions arose. Thankfully no fighting just insults yelled at each other while the orcs and Adel left Holm.\nRECORDED\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n17/6/2018\n18:30-20:30\nEEST\n\nNothing much happened.\n\nRECORDED\nGaroll Earl\n22:00 - 02:00\nGMT\n\nNothing major... Quite lame to be honest. Blogus was sighted- but he left at the sight of me, Chet was with him.\n\nRECORDED\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n18/6/2018\n3:23-5:23\nEEST\n\nNothing happened.\n\nRECORDED\nNorton Brown\n18/6/2018\nGMT+2\n16.00\n17.00\n1 hour\n\nNothing special.\n\nRECORDED\nErwin\n19/6/2018\n1:38 AM\n2:38 AM\n1 HOUR\nNothing\n\nRECORDED\nElgeron Lumberwind\n18/6/2018\nGMT+2\n21:35PM - 23:35PM\n2h\n\nNothing unusual happened.\n\nRECORDED\nKazrin Starbreaker\n6-18-18\n3:12 to 4:12\nnothin out of the ordinary\n\nRECORDED\nNorton Brown\n19/6/2018\nGMT+2\n21.10\n23.10\n1h\n\nNothing special.\n\nRECORDED\nElgeron Lumberwind\n20/6/2018\nGMT+2\n0:45AM\n1:45AM\n1h\n\nNothing special.\n\nRECORDED\nElgeron Lumberwind\n20/6/2018\nGMT+2\n7:15AM\n8:15AM\n1h\n\nNothing special.\n\nRECORDED\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n20/6/2018\nEEST\n8:09-9:15\n2 hours and 6 minutes\n\nNothing interesting happened.\n\nRECORDED\nGaroll Earl\n15:05\n17:05\n2 hour\ngmt\n\nEhhh... Nothing too different,\n\nRECORDED\nNorton Brown\n20/6/2018\nGMT+2\n20.38\n21.38\n1h\n\nNothing special.", ""),
        StaticBook("Gate Instruction", "Svardin Grandaxe", "1). Close Gate behind them, lock them in.\n\n2). Ask for Name, Race, Reason for Visiting.\n\n3). Search them ((With /search [username] )) If they have any weapons, ask for them to be thrown into the donation hole. Inform them that their weapons are not -\nguaranteed to return. (( Just incase the guard logs off and cannot return them. Don't steal.))\n\n4). Once they have given you the weapons, open the second gate. Then, close the second gate behind them and open the first gate.", ""),
        StaticBook("GATEHOUSE BOOK 5", "Brigadier General Dimlin Irongut", "Gate House Log Book:\nRecord In Format Below:\n\nJakhatir Irongut \n02/Jul/2018\nGMT+0 17:14 To 18:00\n\nNothing happend\nKazrin Starbreaker\n6-20-18\n(EST) 3:37 to 4:45\n\nLittle kid named cut caught him secretly eating some cake his name is Cut or so he call himself. Maybe keep an eye on the lad looks 12 or 13 by the looks of it. Said his parents is off somewhere.\nWigmar\n6-20-18\n(GMT +2) 20.04 to 21.06\nTotal time: 1 hour\n\nSome old folk entered city, asking things. Nothing else.\n\n\nRECORDED\nNorton Brown\n21/6/2018\nGMT+2\n13.50\n15.50\n1h\n\nNothing special.\n\nREORDED\nElgeron Lumberwind\n21/6/2019\nGMT+2\n13:50-15:50\n2h\n\nNothing unusual\n\nRECORDED\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n21/6/2018\nEEST\n14:16-16:16\n2 hours\n\nNothing happened\n\nRECORDED\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n22/6/2018\nEEST\n16:10-17:10\n1 hour\n\nNothing interesting happened\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n22/6/2018\nEEST\n18:23-19:23\n1 hour\n\nNothing interesting happened.\n\nRECORDED\nMarrow Scaevolus\n6/22/2018\nTime in: 5:35pm\nTime out: 7:58pm\nEST\n\nEpsi and Garoll still have yet to make up.\n\nRECORDED\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n23/6/2018\nEEST\n14:54-15:54\n1 hour\n\nNothing interesting happened \n\nreorded\nElgeron Lumberwind\n23/6/2018\nGMT+2\n14:45-16:45\n2h\n\nNothing special.\n\nrecorded\nNilth Mustang\n23/6/2018\nEST\n6:33 PM - 9:16 PM\n\n\nI actually did my job for once.\n\nRecorded\nAlehan\n24/06/2018\nGMT+1\n9:56 AM- 10:56 AM\n1 hour\n\nNothing special\n\nRECORDED\nMaximus Meridio\n24/06/2018\nGMT+1\n9:56 AM - 10:56 AM\n\nRECORDED\nAlehan\n25/06/2018\nGMT+1\n2:51 PM-3:51 PM\n1 hour\nNothing special\n\nRECORDED~\nMaximus Meridio\n25/06/2018\nGMT+1\n2:51 PM - 3:51 PM\n1h\nNothing - I meet Sahar the Matrona! <3\n\nOh my. RECORDED\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n25/6/2018\nEEST\n22:33-23:45\n1 hour and 52 minutes\n\nAn ork tried to kidnap a woman, I intervened and the woman managed to run away. I received no serious injuries, but the ork managed to run away.\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n26/6/2018\n6:38-7:38\n1 hour\n\nNothing interesting happened.\n\nRECORDED\n\nRECORDED\nMaximus Meridio\n26/06/2018\nGMT+1\n17:30 - 18:30\nAll good\n\nRECORDED\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n26/6/2018\nEEST\n21:46-22:46\n1 hour\n\nNothing interesting happened\n\nRECORDED\nSamuel Lythian\n6/26/2018\nCST\n9:20-10:20 PM\n1 hour\n\nNothing happened, and I did my job. Don't yell at me please.\n\nRecorded?\nMaximus Meridio\n27/06/2018\nGMT+1\n18:11 - 19:11\nAxel Ireheart, the Tal Azmar refuge is back between us\n\nRecorded\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n28/6/2018\nEEST\n7:53-9:53\n2 hours\n\nNothing interesting happened.\n\nRECORDED\nAlehan\n28/06/2018\nGMT+1\n10:50 AM-11:50 AM\nNothing\n\nRecorded\nMaximus Meridio\n28/06/2018\nGMT+1\n10:50 AM -11:50 AM\nNothing\n\nRecorded\nAthonir Silva\n28/6/18\nGmt+2\n20.30-21.30\n\njust people coming in and out of holm\n\nRecorded\nNilth Mustang\n28/6/18\nEst\n8:43 PM- 9:40 \n\nRecorded\nAlehan\n29/06/2018\nGMT+1\n10:30 AM-11:30 AM\nnothing\n\nRecorded\nMaximus Meridio\n29/06/2018\nGMT+1\n10:30 AM - 11:30 AM\nnothing\n\nRecordedw\nAthonir Silva\n29/6/18\nGmt+2\n14.00-16.00\n2 hours\n\nAbsoultely Nothing\n\nRecorded\nEvan Katke\n6/30/2018\nTime in:5:20\nTime out:7:20\nCST\n\nRecorded\nHyperion\n7/1\nEST\n4:30\n5:30\n\nRecorded\nEvan Katke\n7/2/2018\n12:30 PM\n2:30 PM\nCST\n\nRecorded\nOmega\nDay 2/7/2018\n19:45 GTM1\n20:45 GTM1\n\nRecorded\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n2/7/2018\nEEST\n22:35-00:02\n1 hour and 27 minutes\n\nNothing much happened until Dimlin went crazy and I went to check what was the situation.\nRECORDED\nNorton Brown\n2/7/2018\nGMT+2\n22:45\n23:45\n1 hour\n\nNothing special.\n(RECORDED)\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n3/7/2018\nEEST\n20:08-21:38\n1 hour and 30 minutes\n\nNothing interesting happened.\nRECORDED\nEvan Katke\n7/6/2018\nTime in:2:47PM\nTime out:\nCST\nRECORDED\nElgeron Lumberwind\n6-7/Jul/2018\n23:45-0:45\nGMT+2\n1h\n\nNothing happened.\nRECORDED\nMarrow Scaevolus\n7/7/2018\nTime in: 10:45pm\nTime out: 12:03am\nEST\n\nTsisha doesnt like potatoes. Evan flirts with spooks. My end is nigh.\nRECORDED\nAthonir Silva\n7/7/18\n17.00-18.00\nGmt +2\n\nnothing special\nRECORDED\nWulf Edvin Kalbfleisch\n9/7/2018\nEEST\n1:30-2:30\n1 hour\n\nNothing interesting happened.\nRECORDED\nOmega\n10/7/2018\nGTM1\n20:15-20:30\n15min\n\nSome people enter some people go out.\nRECORDED\nEvan Katke\n7/9/2018\nTime in:11:00PM\nTime out:1:00AM\nCST\nnothin' dem bitches be\ncleaaar\nRECORDED\nEvan Katke\n7/10/2018\nTime in:4:00PM\nTime out:6:00PM\nMarrow Scaevolus\n7/13/2018\nTime in: 7:21pm\nTIme out: 8:05pm\nEST\n\nstuff\nRECORDED\nAthonir Silva\n14/7/18\n3.25-4.25\nGmt+2\n\nA lot of traffic\nRECORDED\nMarrow Scaevolus\n7/14/2018\nTime in: 8:19pm\nTime out: 9:24pm\nEST\n\nPeople need to get their papers in order, those daschunds. I mean, come on, people. What's so hard about buying stuff!?\nRECORDED\nEvan Katke\n7/15/2018\nTime in:9:00 PM\nTime out:11:00 PM\nCST\nRECORDED\nEvan Katke\n7/17/2018\nTime in:7:00AM\nTime Out:9:00AM\nCST\nBoring, told a reiver to run home, nothing eventful\nRECORDED", ""),
        StaticBook("Gathering Herbs", "Katherine Fisher", "===================\n\n       The Art of\n    Gathering Herbs\n\n\n\n       Written by\n      Liriel Fisher\n   \n\n\n\n==================\nForeword:\nThis book was written by myself, and the research done by my close friend and alchemic colleague Nemir. As we consider ourselves budding and self-taught alchemists, we have spent many, many hours in libraries and pouring over every tome\nrelating to the profession that we could get our hands on. Through our experimentation and unwavering dedication to the art of alchemy, we have found ourselves in need of a comprehensive collection of knowledge on just where to find the herbs we depend on\nThus, The Art of Gathering Herbs was born. I hope you find it’s contents helpful.\nChapter 1-1: Introduction to Gathering\n-------------------Herbs are the most vital and important part of an alchemist’s professional life. They provide the basic necessary ingredients involved in all proper potions, and thus, must either be purchased\nor procured on your own. Purchasing dozens of herbs can be not only expensive, but extremely time consuming as you seek out sellers or wait for that one vital herb to show up in auction. Herbs can be found through various professions other than alchemy\nitself, such as lumberjacking, farming, and fishing. Herbs can also be obtained through treasure caskets retrieved from gathering. However, the best way for an alchemist to retrieve their own herbs while continuing to advance in the skill is to gather\nthem on their own with a pair of handy alchemists shears.  These special shears can be obtained from an adequate blacksmith at minimum.  They are made from two gold ingots, and two sticks. In my experience, I would recommend obtaining a large amount\nof these tools if you are unskilled as they will break quite easily in inexperienced hands. Personally, I carried ten pairs of these on my person when out searching for herbs as a fairly skilled alchemist. My more experienced companion, Nemir,\nwas able to obtain many more herbs than I was, but finding an herb can be very enlightening when you discover it with a pair of alchemists shears.  I would not recommend using this method of obtaining herbs until you are at least fair in skill, as even at\nthat level of knowledge you will not be very successful.\nChapter 1-2: Regions\n-------------------Now, finding the various herbs has been a rigorous and lengthy process. Nemir and I have narrowed the various types of regions into four types:\nHot, cold, wet, and dry.\nYou can group various types of biomes into one category, such as taiga, ice Plains, and extreme Hills, which are all cold, etcetera.\nDry would be plains and forests, hot is desert and mesa, and wet is jungle and swamps.\nChapter 2: Herbs and Where to Find Them\n-------------------Water Symbols\nMandragora: One of the most basic herbs in alchemy is mandragora. These rooty plants can be found in wet biomes, typically swamps, within ponds. They are usually found clinging to other aquatic plant life, such as lily pads and algaes.\nSerpernt's Stalk: A staple in any alchemist or healer's stash, Serpent's Stalk is often found alongside ponds and rivers in dry climates. In my search for the herb, I commonly found this snakeish plant growing up the stalks of sugar cane near water.\nFrost Vine: This interesting blue vine can be found snaking up the trunks of trees and rock walls of cold regions. The vines are often clearly visible and easy to find.\nBlissfoil: This healer's friend can be easily spotted in fields and forests in dry regions by their brilliant blue hued flowers. Though the stalk of the plant is the useful part, the flower petals are what will help you find them easily.\nAthin: An intriguing, blue colored algae, Athin is commonly found in cold regions, growing remarkably among icy waters. Though it can be a bit hard to spot in the bleak landscape, finding an iced over pond will surely yield this herb.\nFire Symbols:\nCrimson Vase: Found most commonly in dry regions, this interesting flower can be found in grassy fields and spotted by its - you guessed it - crimson colored petals.\nDrake's Tail: This herb is truly remarkable in my opinion. It grows where few other plants can, in the hot desert heat, perched among the pale yellow sandstone rocks. Wearing leather gloves when harvesting this is highly advised.\nDwarf's Pumpkin: One might think it's bright orange petals which give it it's name would be an excellent indicator of this herb's presence, but surprisingly, I had the best luck finding this peculiar plant by rummaging through the short grasses of swamps.\nBlood Lotus: Another remarkably persistent plant, this deep red herb can be found in hot regions snaking it's way up sandstone cliffs, and winding it's way through the sands.\nFlametongue Root: Like Drake's Tail, caution is advised when harvesting this volatile herb. As the name suggests, this root grows in the ground amongst the grasses of dry regions.\nAir Symbols:\nLarihei's Fingers: This particular plant grows in cold regions among the long grasses and ferns of the forest. Not much is known about this herb, but it is always advisable to have a few of each herb on hand.\nElf's Hair Vine: Finding this herb will lead you on a trek up a mountain to find the cold, snow topped peaks where this beautiful flowered vine grows. A hardy plant, this flower can be seen peaking out through snowy cliffs.\nCrouching Feather: This beautiful plant is named for its feather like white petals, and can most commonly be found among the tall grasses of dry regions. Though not as rare as some may believe, this herb requires patience to gather.\nHalfling's Grass: This plant is named for its common use by the Halfling race as a smoking herb. Typically it is found in dry climates throughout plains and forests alike. Search for this plant in tall grasses.\nEarth Symbols:\nSaffvil: This grassy plant is found in wet biomes predominantly, and can be found by searching through the short grasses that grow close to the soil.\nTippen's Root: An extremely common place, but also very useful plant, this root is widely used by both alchemist and healer. This plant is found in the grassy plains and forests of dry biomes.\nAlabaster Leaf: This small green leafy herb can be found snaking it's way through the branches and hiding amongst the leaves of a host tree. They attach themselves to all types of trees in dry regions.\nClutcher's Straw: A dry, brittle plant that can be found growing in hot regions. Search for this herb in low-lying shrubberies.\nMetzli's Tangle: A controversially named herb, this plant can be found snaking it's way up jungle trees in wet biomes.\nGoblin's Ivy: As it's name suggests, this herb can be found growing in hot, desert climates that Uruk's prefer. It is most commonly found on stone surfaces, but it can also be found growing up cactus plants.", ""),
        StaticBook("GB Rhodesia I", "Commodus de Jedih", "dddddddddddddddddddddFirst Golden Bulldd\nddOf Rhodesia, 1643j\nfffffffffffffffffffffff\n\nFrom His Holiness, Clement III\n\nTranscribed by Comm.\n1663\nFIRST GOLDEN BULL OF RHODESIA\n\n11th of Sun’s Smile, 1643\n\nHis Holiness CLEMENT III, High Pontiff of the Church of the Canon, Archbishop of Jorenus, Lotharum, Rhodesia, Aleksandria,-\nVisigia and Erochland, Prince-Bishop of St. Thomas, Savoy, Mont St. Humbert, Johannesburg, Esheveurd, Luciensport, Huss, and Dibley, Abbot of Laureh’lin, and Hariam, Bishop of Godfreo, Versace, Mardon,-\nand Carace, Successor of the High Priesthood of the Church, Supreme Pontiff of the Church of True Faith, Keeper of the Canon, Missionary to Aeldin, High Servant to the Exalted's Testaments, Humble Servant of the Faithful and Vicar of God does decree…\nTABLE OF CONTENTS\n\nSECTION I -DIOCESAN RECONSTRUCTION\n\nSECTION II - ECCLESIASTICAL APPOINTMENTS\n\nSECTION III - SYNOD APPOINTMENTS\nSECTION IV - CANONIZATION\n\nSECTION V - HOLY KNIGHTHOOD\nddddddddddddddddddd\n\nSECTION I - DIOCESAN RECONSTRUCTION\n\nWith the healing of the Mother Church and its dissident child, a flood-\nof new clergymen have come into the ranks of God and taken His robes.\n\nTHE ARCHDIOCESE OF RHODESIA - Encompassing Marna and the Apostolic Kingdom Demesne under its jurisdiction: Administered by HIS EXCELLENCY, NOVATIAN BESEL\nTHE DIOCESE OF SENNTISTEN- Encompassing the Capital city of Senntisten and the surrounding lands. Administered by HIS GRACE, DIMMESDALE\n\nTHE ARCHDIOCESE OF JORENUS - Encompassing the  Kingdom of Hanseti-Ruska, -\nand its respective lands. Administered by HIS EXCELLENCY, ELPHIAS OF METZ\n\nTHE ARCHDIOCESE OF ALEKSANDRIA - Encompassing the Kingdom of Santegia, Presa de Madera and all settlements on that land. Administered by-\nHIS EXCELLENCY, BERNARD SOLOMON\n\nTHE ARCHDIOCESE OF RENATUM- Encompassing the Kingdom of Renatus and the holdings it defends. Administered by HIS EXCELLENCY, NATHANAEL OF AESTON\nSECTION II - ECCLESIASTICAL APPOINTMENTS\n\nAs the Church restructures, new appointments to its governance are necessary. To handle day-to-day affairs, miniscule issues, and such there are several new-\nCuria posts which are appointed.\n\nVICE-CHANCELLOR - HIS EXCELLENCY, BERNARD SOLOMON\n\nPONTIFICAL TREASURER- In charge of all finances that pass through Holy Mother Church, -\nentrusted to collect donations and fund Pontifical ventures- VACANT.\n\nGRANDMASTER OF THE ORDER OF SAINT LUCIEN- The commander of the Faith Militia branch of the sacred guard, tasked in -\ndefending the Church and enforcing her laws, is granted to HOLY SER RAKIM YAR, and shall be overseen by CLEMENT III.\n\nCURATOR OF THE ADAMANTINE CATHEDRAL- The caretaker of the Adamantine-\nCathedral located in Marna is granted to HIS EXCELLENCY, NOVATIAN BESEL  \n\nSECTION III - SYNOD APPOINTMENTS AND REFORM\n\nThe Synod shall receive the following appointments. It is the intention of the Pontificate-\nto restore the Pentarchy to consolidate the shepherds of the Church with their respective regions and to reconfigure the Synod in accordance to the current state of the Church.\nPENTARCH OF THE CANON; HIS EXCELLENCY, BERNARD SOLOMON\n\nPENTARCH OF THE CANON; HIS EXCELLENCY, ELPHIAS OF METZ\n\nPENTARCH OF THE CANON; HIS EXCELLENCY, NOVATIAN BESEL\nPENTARCH OF THE CANON; HIS EXCELLENCY, NATHANAEL OF AESTON\n\nPENTARCH OF THE CANON; HIS GRACE, ROBERT ROVIN\n\nThe Pentarchy is commissioned with the governance of -\nthe Church through the will of HIS HOLINESS, CLEMENT III\n\nSECTION IV - CANONIZATIONS\n\nWe the Pontificate, by our Apostolic Authority does grant approbation for the following-\nsanctifications to the communion of saints and beatified for their extraordinary models of piety and glory to the Church of the Canon:\n\n1. Henry Otto of Alban shall be styled as Saint Henry Otto of Alban. A champion of the commoners,-\na man with unquestionable piety in promoting faith in the Barbanov family and in the Hanseti Royal Army, he shall be known as the Patron Saint of Commoners, Justice, and Fatherhood.\nSECTION V - HOLY KNIGHTHOOD\n\nWe the Pontificate, by our Apostolic Authority call upon all Holy Knights that adorn the style of Holy Ser, Holy Knight, and any other style associated with-\nthe Office to come to the Adamantine Cathedral in Marna to swear loyalty to HIS HOLINESS CLEMENT III, and to register yourself to the new Pontificate.\n\nFide et Ordo", ""),
        StaticBook("GB Rhodesia II", "Commodus de Jedih", "sssssssssssssssssssSecond Golden Bull of\ndddRhodesia, 1650ddd\nddddddddddddddddddd\n\nFrom His Holiness,\nJude I\n\nTranscribed by Comm, 1663\nSECUNDI TAURUM AUREUS SANCTUS RHODESINSIS\n\nSECOND GOLDEN BULL OF RHODESIA\n\nThe 15th of Snow’s Maiden, 1650\nHis Holiness JUDE I, High Pontiff of the Church of the Canon, Metropolitan of Rhodesia and the Crownlands, Archbishop of Jorenus, Lotharum, Aleksandria, Phillipus, Enochas, Visigia and Erochland, Prince-Bishop of St. Thomas, Savoy, Mont St. Humbert,-\nHolofernes, Johannesburg, Esheveurd, Luciensport, Huss, and Dibley, Prince-Abbot of Laureh’lin and Hariam, Abbot of Annsden, Bishop of Godfreo, Fernandus, the Westerweald, Versace, Mardon, Metz, and Carace, Successor of the High Priesthood of the Church,-\nSupreme Pontiff of the Church of True Faith, Keeper of the Canon, Missionary to Aeldin and Svatum, High Servant to the Exalted's Testaments, Humble Servant of the Faithful and Vicar of GOD doth decree…\nTABLE OF CONTENTS\n\nSECTION I -DIOCESAN RECONSTRUCTION\nSECTION II - CURIAL APPOINTMENTS\nSECTION III - SYNOD APPOINTMENTS\nSECTION IV - SLAVERY\nSECTION V - HOLY KNIGHTHOOD\nSECTION VI - CANONIZATION\nSECTION VII -  HIGH MASS OF ST. CLEMENT\nSECTION VIII -  RHODESIAN CATECHISM SECTION IX -  MAGIC\nSECTION X - MAGISTRATE OF HERMETICS\nSECTION XI - PLENA OPERATIO\nSECTION XII - THE HUMBERTINE ORDER\nsssssssssssssssssss\n\nSECTION I - DIOCESAN RECONSTRUCTION\n\nReorganization and order highlight the first goals of His Holiness. In fulfillment of these goals, consolidation must commence-\nin order to join together those territories which have been neglected.\n\nTHE METROPOLITANATE OF RHODESIA - Encompassing Marna and the Apostolic Kingdom Demesne under its jurisdiction: Administered by HIS HOLINESS, JUDE I\n-HIS EXCELLENCY, HERMAN OF VALAAM, presiding vicar of Rhodesia.\n\nTHE ARCHDIOCESE OF JORENUS - Encompassing the  Kingdom of Hanseti-Ruska, and its respective lands. Administered by HIS EXCELLENCY,-\nYURII OF HAENSE\n\n-THE REVEREND, BERDISLEYEV, presiding vicar of Jorenus.\n\nTHE CURATE OF CURON underneath Jorenus - Encompassing the Duchy of Curon, and its respective lands.-\nAdministered by THE RIGHT REVEREND, ARTHUR DIMMESDALE\n\nTHE CURATE OF SANTEGIA-NORLAND underneath Rhodesia - Encompassing the  Kingdom of Santegia, the entity of Norland, and their respective lands. Administered by THE REVEREND, THOMAS OF ALBAN\nTHE CURATE OF VILLAVIA  underneath Jorenus - Encompassing the entity of Belvitz, the Gottlesfont Priory, and the settlements along the crossroads. Administered by HIS EXCELLENCY, YURII OF HAENSE\nSECTION II - CURIAL APPOINTMENTS\n\nAs the Church restructures, new appointments to its governance are necessary. To handle day-to-day affairs, miniscule issues, and such there are several new Curia posts which are appointed.\nVICE-CHANCELLOR - HIS EXCELLENCY, HERMAN OF VALAAM\nPATRON OF THE HOLY ORDER OF SAINT LUCIEN - GRAND PRIOR, ROBERT ROVIN \nDEAN OF THE APOSTOLIC TRIBUNAL - HIS EXCELLENCY, YURII OF HAENSE\nHEGUMEN OF ALL MONASTICS  - THE RIGHT REVEREND, ARTHUR DIMMESDALE\nDEAN OF HERMETICS  - THE REVEREND, BERDISLEYEV\n\nSECTION III - SYNOD APPOINTMENTS AND REFORM\nThe Synod shall receive the following appointments. It is the intention of the Pontificate to restore the Triarchy to consolidate the shepherds of the Church with their respective regions and to reconfigure the Synod in-\naccordance to the current state of the Church.\n\nTRIARCH OF THE CANON; HIS EXCELLENCY, YURRI OF HAENSE\n\nTRIARCH OF THE CANON; HIS EXCELLENCY, HERMAN OF VALAAM\nTRIARCH OF THE CANON; HIS EXCELLENCY, ROBERT ROVIN\n\nThe Triarchy is commissioned with the governance of the Church through the will of HIS HOLINESS, JUDE I\nSECTION IV - SLAVERY\nWe the Pontificate and the Holy Magisterium, deem that any man who takes a person: who professes the faith in almighty GOD and truthful allegiance to the Mother Church, as a slave shall be excommunicated latae sentential.\nFurthermore, We, the Pontificate, forbid and prohibit any member of the The Poor-fellows of Horen and Saint Lucien and the Adamantine Cathedral from participating in the slave trade as it is in the domain of secular authorities and thusly is considered -\nprofane. \n\nSECTION V - HOLY KNIGHTHOOD\n\nWe the Pontificate, by our Apostolic Authority call upon all Holy Knights that adorn the style of Holy Ser, Holy Knight, and any other style associated with the-\nOffice to come to the Adamantine Cathedral in Marna to swear loyalty to HIS HOLINESS JUDE I, and to register yourself to the new Pontificate.\n\nSECTION VI - CANONIZATION\nWe, the Synod and Vicar of GOD, allow and permit any cult to the person of Nafis Yar. A resolute man of GOD and friend of the Church. Baptized by His Holiness Lucien III, he led the Qali Spring against the conglomerate of Vanderguan,-\ndissolving the heathenous Caliphate and declaring Vandoria a Canonist State.﻿ Due to his aid in spreading GOD’s word, and ra﻿ising his family within the Canonist Faith, Nafis Yar is to be regarded as a Blessed of the Church.\nFurthermore, We allow and permit the cult of Catherine Francesce Horen for her piety. During her life, Catherine, took a vow not to lie, carried a life of humility and blessed virginity as well as her aid to the poor, this shows her incredible devotion -\nto GOD and His Church. With her pious way of living it is clear to Us that she is within the Skies, forever praising GOD along side the other righteous and she shall be called a Blessed of the Church.\n\nSECTION VII - HIGH MASS OF ST. CLEMENT\nIn order to bring about liturgical uniformity in the Holy Canonist Church, We the Pontificate and Synod, by our Apostolic Authority do declare the High Mass of Saint Clement to be the supreme liturgical Missile of the Holy Canonist Church.\nLet all everywhere adopt and observe this translation of the High Mass of Saint Clement,﻿ and let Masses not be sung or read according to any other formula than that of this Missal published by Us. This ordinance applies henceforth, now, and forever, -\nthroughout all the provinces of the Canonist world, to all. \n\nTherefore, no one whosoever is permitted to alter this Missile in any way. Would anyone, however, presume to commit such and act, he should know that he will incur the wrath of Almighty GOD -\nand of the High Priests Evaristus and Clement daming them to perdition through eternal fire and everlasting pain.\n\nSECTION VIII -  RHODESIAN CATECHISM \n\nWe, the Synod of His Holy Church, and His Vicar, Jude I, do proclaim with-\ngreat joy that a great Catechism shall be written. Within it there shall be all pertaining to the Church, from Dogma to Church function & canon law. Fret not, children of GOD, for the age of inactivity and passiveness is over.\nSECTION XI -  MAGIC\n\nWe, the Synod of His Holy Church, and through the word of the Vicar of GOD, do urge the faithful of all lands, to read carefully, and with clear capacities, Our word of warning. For the souls of the faithful are at risk, through-\nthe practice and use of magical abilities.\n\nMagic, in the most simple of terms, is granted to those who wish to wield such power by beings who seek to make themselves to be like GOD. Thus the Holy and Forever Exalted-\nProphet of GOD, Owyn, peace be upon him, admonished the magis for their lust for power and ambition. \n\n“And to ye magicians I admonish: GOD is incomprehensible. He cannot be divided nor made again and his mysteries are the holy mysteries,-\nand no art is alike to his power.\" -Owyn 7:7\n\nWe, therefore, must admonish the Magi for the use of their power for their own ambitions besides the glorification of GOD. And we must also admonish the Magi to forgo any magic granted by a lesser-\n‘deity' or any power of dark, dubious, or of saulite intentions.\n\nWe do however, allow and permit to any Canonist to learn and practice the esoteric art of evocation, as previously allowed within the Third Golden Bull of Johannesburg:\n“Evocation...Unlike magics achieved through grants from a higher power or deity, Evocation. . . such a fire, and earth are not considered heresies against GOD, for they are achieved through the manipulation of the world’s energy.\nThese magics are in no way against GOD, for they are not involved in the placement of another above GOD but simply the use of GOD’s creations in the world to grant themselves unnatural powers and abilities.” - Third Golden Bull of Johannesburg\nWe find this magic to be acceptable for the reasons declared upon the Third Golden Bull of Johannesburg.\n\nHowever, We, the Holy Magisterium, do understand the worry of our conservative children of GOD. Magi can not, and will not be tolerated if they are-\nto run rampant and lawlessly. Thusly, We, with full apostolic authority, set up the Magistrate of Hermetics under the Dean of Hermetics. This Magistrate is under the further scrutiny of Archbishop Yurii as he is the Dean of the Apostolic Tribunal.\nSECTION X - MAGISTRATE OF HERMETICS\n\nWe, the Synod of His Holy Church, and through the word of the Vicar of GOD, do see the necessity of the forms of magic practiced within humanity, with the position of Court Magician-\nbeing upheld throughout most Kingdoms, and notable advisors bearing knowledge of these techniques. \n\nIt is her﻿eby, through Synodal decree, that the Magistrate of Hermetics be established to oversee the training, licensing, and general\nconformity of GOD's faithful, throughout the realms of humanity who partake in such practices. This Magistrate, through the appointment by His Holiness, the Vicar of GOD, shall be overseen and cared for by the Dean of Hermetics who shall be tasked with -\nthe licensing of all Magi within the Canonist world.\n\nSECTION XI - PLENA OPERATIO\n\nFrom now forward, every clergy member is required to keep a journal of how they have spread the word of GOD that Saint’s Week.\nSECTION XII - THE HUMBERTINE ORDER\n\nWe, the Synod of His Holy Church, and through the word of the Vicar of GOD, do acknowledge the necessity for the Humbertine Order of Friars to reemerge on the land of Atlas. It is by this decree that the-\nHigh Pontiff and the Most Holy Synod of the Canonist Church do proclaim BROTHER HILARIUS to the role of Superior General. The Order shall take up residence within the Adamantine Cathedral and shall serve GOD and His Church in missionary duties.\n☩ IN NOMINE PATRIS, et Horenus, et Exaltus Honorem. Amen.\n\nREJOICE! GOD’S FAITHFUL TOIL NO LONGER.\n\nSunt etiamnum fidelium.\n\nDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDD", ""),
        StaticBook("GemDevice Report", "Pereus Frostbeard", "Throwable Magical\nParticle Ejector\n          -Report-\n\nThe Item in question is a throwable device that aids in the subversion and harm of any hostiles at a distance, in battle.\n\n*a rough sketch of the device is drawn here*\nIt comes in the shape of a palm sized blue gem, surrounded by a silver band. When the word \"Purtity\" is uttered by the user small arcane balls form around it, then it can be thrown, after a few moments the arcane balls shoot out in all directions\nand from the experiments done with the object, they are able to penetrate through clothing and flesh easily, but they're not able to pass through armor, therefore they would work best against lightly armored targets or unarmored ones.", ""),
        StaticBook("Gemstones", "Anwyn Izalith", "~*Gemstones*~\n\n     A copy written by:\n        Anwyn Izalith\n\n                ~*~\n\nThis book has been created in order to spread the cultural significance of gemstones.\n\n-Written in 1542\n-Ruby\nIt gives people increased wisdom. It is particulary useful for rash.\n\n-Emerald\nIncreases the fertility of a person, both during conception and bearing.\n-Diamond\nThe most powerful of all gems. It amplifies all other traits.\n\n-Amethyst\nCalms the nerves. Useful for study or meditation.\n\n-Sugilite\nThe healer's stone. It is used in healing arts, both magic and item.\n-Carnelian\nImproves analytical skills.\n\n-Garnet\nThe bloodstone. It is used to draw toxics from the body and aid in blood clot.\n\n-Onyx\nUsed to obtain enlightenment.\n-Hematite\nReduces stress.\n\n-Sapphire\nEnvokes peace and happiness.\n\n-Topaz\nIncreases both metal and physically stamina.\n-Tiger's eye\nDestroys anxiety. It promotes non-reckless courage.\n\n-Peridot\nUsed for growth.\n\n-Pearl\nUsed in chakra. Improves the connection with both mind and body.\n-Soladite\nAdsorbs negative thoughts from both the wearer and those around them. This negates the thoughts.", ""),
        StaticBook("Gen. Alch. Salve", "Karyssmov 'Wick' Faroe", "Directions for Karyssmovian Salve\n\nIngredients:\nTippens Root\nBlissfoil\nFrostvine\nPure grain Alcohol\n(Medical that is)\n\nDo not put too much of any material, lest an overdose can occur.\nGenerally, all of the materials should be kept at a completely even ratio as to ensure maximum safety.\n\nMash all of the above ingredients in a mortar and pestle, take the fine dust within and pour into a container with the alcohol. Size accordingly.......\nAfterwards, swirl until a fine paste is made. Keep the alcohol content low as to stop it from being watery, you do not want a watery salve. That will simply slop off.\n\nApply liberally to wound, allow it to soak in.", ""),
        StaticBook("Get Rich Quick", "Ogdan Goldhand", "Get Rich Quick\n\n   The First Steps\n\n\n\n\n           by:\n\n Ogdan Goldhand,        The First Grand\nMerchant of Kaz'Ulrah\nWhat is Mina?\n\nMina is the currency we use to value our products. Most use it everyday. On food, weapons, and whatever it is that gets them through their day. It is our currency and a staple of society.\nHow do I obtain Mina?\n\nThere are many ways to obtain mina in Atlas. How you choose to is up to you. This part of the mina making process is tough. You have to start from nothing and somehow make something. But first, lets look at our\nskills. Are we a chef? How about a miner? No? Well we need to find one gathering profession we can use to start our mina making process. \n\nFor this example I will be a lumberjack. So we chop trees day and night until we have a stock of them.\nIt is good to have variety. So we cut oak and spruce. But we also cut acacia and birch trees. This expands our inventory. This is important because customers like choices, the more the merrier.\n\nNow- we have our wood but no idea\nwhere or how much to sell for, or perhaps even how to go about it! As for now, without a shop you will have to shout atop city steps, outside of markets, approach people. People sometimes don't even know they need your product until you show them why.\nResearch\n\nAlong your travels take note of the shops. Keep a book if you must. See where prices are high and where they are low. Find out what stays in stock and what does not. Remember the locations and always, always check stores.\nUpon doing this you get an idea for how much each item costs. This is very valuable information. Perhaps the most valuable thing a merchant owns is his knowledge of prices. This is how he knows if he gets a good deal or a bad one. This determines\nthe price of the lumber we just cut. With this knowledge we now know our logs are about 1 mina each, perhaps cheaper. \n\nIf sold as bundles (64) the price could drop from to an even 50 minas. This is called a deal. You cut some off the original price,\nbut only if they buy in large amounts, are your friend, or are trying to do it as a kind gesture.\n\n\n\nLookout for Volume #2\nof GRQ. \n\nMore tips, better tricks, find it before the competition!\nOOC NOTE:\n\nI almost didn't include this because it breaks the style of the book. However, voting everyday is essential if your 'get rich quick' scheme'.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ghashn Baltbrodh", "Travista", "The Lak Mindset\n\n\n      Praise Laklul\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n*The book would be\nwritten in Blah*\n1. Laklul First\n\nYou must act to further Laklul's influence. When you fight, do so in Laklul's name, when you triumph over you foe, do so in Laklul's name; lead your life in Laklul's name. Currently, Laklul is in battle with his\ntyrannical master, Freygoth, spirit of nature, in the immortal plane. This means that you must hinder the influence of Freygoth and those who follow him be they spiritual or mortal. Druids, although they worship nature and not Freygoth directly, are a\nquintessential example of our mortal foes. Drive them from their homes, burn their lives yet spare the ones who dedicate themselves to spirits loyal to Laklul such as swamp and jungle druids. Additionally, destroy all shrines dedicated to Freygoth and\nreplace them with ones in Laklul's esteemed honour for such is the will of Laklul. Aside from Freygoth, his followers and other dishonourable spirits such as Tukki and Ixli, you should praise them for they too are great and worthy, Krug especially.\n2. Orkish Supremacy \n\nThe Ork is the only race which has worshiped the astute \nspirits; the ork is the only race which can defy all others mentally and physically. Although humility is acceptable while treading on ill, foreign lands do no\nsuch thing when they dare to take on the privilege of treading our lands. Especially the swamplands which Laklul deems his home; they must be free of foreign filth unless they pay grand spiritual reparations.\nIn addition, do not lay amongst foreigners or\nallow them to lay among you for their weakness shall diffuse into you. A strong people who can serve the spirits must have the slaves squabble far from equal. All clans which are weak in terms of the individual have issues with this just command.\n3. Strive Selfwards\n\nThe most useful servant is the most skilled one. As a servant to Laklul and most spirits we must view the world with such a lense. The two main aspects of a mortal, the mind and body, must be toiled and trialed consistently into\nimprovement. One cannot forsake one in the name of another; a Lak must be as formidable with wit as he is in the fields of war. Every Lak must be bulked to their limit, every Lak must be trained in craft and  weapon to their limit; every Lak must be\nat their peaked for this is the best way to serve Laklul. This is the will of Laklul.\n4. Lakkish Loyalty\n\nAll Laks are to be utterly devoted to the clan; to the Swampgoth. As the Swampgoth and the clan in extension act on behalf of the mighty and rightous Laklul any severing of dedication severs Laklul's positive view. It likewise\ndictates the spirits to view you with an unfavourable lense due to forsaking the oath you took before the spirits which was sealed in the blood of your initial trial. Furthermore, do not fear death if it's in the name of Laklul. Welcome it. The greatest\nof Krug's kin transcend to the ancestral plane to live gloriously as Krug does himself. If the enemy takes you captive hold sensitive details to death; if the enemy drive forth, unless the spirit of hope himself would proclaim it suicidal, fight.\nConclusive Notes:\n\n-Avoid degeneracy\n\n-Respect swampland\n\n-Respect ALL spirits bar the ones detailed previously\nPunishments:\n\nFirst Offense:\n\nThe offender is beaten\n\nSecond Offense:\n\nThe offender is beaten, a finger taken\n\nAnymore results in death", ""),
        StaticBook("Ghosts", "Ser Duncan Lefay", "A Guide To\n         Ghosts\nIntro\n\nA dark forest at night, a distinct feeling of being alone...\n\nSlowly, hairs begin to stand up on the back of your neck, a tinkling laugh heard in the distance...\n\nAnd then, the dread...\nIntro\n\nGhosts are fickle things. Many are their kinds, and many are their temperments. There are some who are content with their position in our world, and others who rage against the machine for the atrocities commited unto them...\nIdentifying\n\n There are three \"phases\" of ghosts. They start out as what's known as a haunt. They are typically black and white, with blank white eyes. Haunts will not know they are dead at first, and they'll keep their normal living routine.\nIdentifying\n\n Next, you have Revenants. These look almost the same as Haunts, however they have pupils and irises. They become this once they realize they are dead. It is at this stage that they begin to receive powers we'd associate with ghosts.\nIdentifying\n\n Lastly, we have the Poltergeist/Spectre. A Poltergeist is formed when a Revenant doesn't take their death very well, being fueled by anger and hatred. They are commonly red, ashy, have completely black eyes, or all of the above.\nIdentifying\n\nSpectres are at the complete opposite end of the spectrum, gracefully accepting their predicament. They are characterized by being mainly harmless and a glowing shade of blue.\nStrengths\n\n To start, ghosts cannot die (Obviously). They continue to grow in strength the longer they are a ghost. Their powers can range from putting out torches, to telekinesis. From levitation, to transforming their appearence.\nWeaknesses\n\nAs stated before Ghosts cannot die. However, they can be exorcized by a shaman or cleric, which allows them to move on to the after life that they deserve. One can drive them away provided they have magegold or bright light.\nTemperment\n\n As with people, the temperment and behaviour varies from ghost to ghost, some being docile, and others being completely antagonistic. Now, usually Haunts and Spectres are much more peaceful.\nTemperment\n \n When you get to the Revenants, it's about fifty-fifty. They can be docile and friendly, or they can be antagonistic and mischevious. As for poltergeists, they are always out to terrify you, and even sometimes kill you.\nTemperment\n\n However, cases of death are exceedingly rare. Ghosts usually stick to one place or person to haunt. Ghosts also exude a depressing aura. Spending too much time around a ghost can lead to suicidal thoughts, depression,\nTemperment\n\n and even itchyness and coldness. Sometimes, ghosts are even known to give a person extremly bad luck. When they are haunting a place or person, it's usually because they had ties to those things while living.\nConclusion\n\n In conclusion, Ghosts are the spirits of the deceased that have come back to walk this earth. Now you have a basic grasp of Ghosts and how to handle them in the event that you run into one.\n\nGood luck!", ""),
        StaticBook("Ghoul In Sutica", "Alex H. Aureon", "Ghoul Attack In Sutica\n\nBy Alex H. Aureon\n\"It was a regular, as I was visiting Sutica. I was minding my own business, then I saw a creature come towards, and I wasn't sure what it was. I wasn't aware that it was a ghoul at the time, and this happened around the time before I became a cleric. The\nghoul approached me, and it kept yelling out 'FOOD', and I wanted to be nice and give the creature some food. I handed it some bread, but it immeadiately threw it to the ground, and ran towards me and attempting to eat my leg. I kicked the ghoul back, but\nit just stumbled back. I unsheath my tomahawk, ready in hand for another attack. The ghoul ran at me once more, this time, I sent my tomahawk flying into his head. This tomahawk hitting his head, and sending him flying, but along with the tomahawk. I\nwalked over to the ghoul that laid on the floor. I placed a foot on the ghoul, attempting to yank the tomahawk out of its head. Suddenly, the ghoul grabbed my foot, after pulling out the tomahawk, I attempt to shake off the ghoul and step back. The ghoul\nstands and lunges itself on me, crushing my legs, and causing us to fall backwards as I hit my head against the pavement. I was unconscious, helpless on the floor. I quickly regained consciousness, and attempted to use my tomahawk to hit the ghoul in the\nhead once more, getting it stuck in it once more. The ghoul then went down to take a bite out of my chest. While, the citizens of Sutica were watching, all scared to fight the ghoul. I attempted to punch again, the ghoul biting at my arm, and I punch once\nmore, and the ghoul biting again as well. Leaving me laying on the ground in pain, making it hard for me to move. A Kha, Aife, tried to help me by pouncing on the ghoul, but the ghoul easily tossing her to the side. But indeed, it helped, buying time for\na guard to come over and strike at the ghoul's neck, causing it to die. The lifeless body falling to the side of me, as I took deep, heavy breathes. I was given medical attention to keep me alive for the time beings, and treated by clerics to help me get\nbetter. But this day forward, I remebered to always carry a gold sword with me to fight against dark beings. This day taught me a lot, and is another thing to add to my list of adventures.\"\n\n~Alex H. Aureon\n\n15th of The Grand Harvest, 1583", ""),
        StaticBook("Glory", "Baldin Frostbeard", "The Glore of tha Dweeds\nAh sen battle mane temes...New ah lek at ma body scared frem all ef them and ask ma self... Whay do I fight? Whay do I endanger ma life? Is it fer ma race nay...ma kingdem? nay... We dweeds faight fer tha glory...Fer a glory that well make othes remamber\nour deeds.\nAhm net sayen thet we most net protect tha our great Urguan...Am jest sayin thet we ar glorious as a race an we mest remember thet when we charge ento battle...We dweeds most net fear death,,, fer death in tha battle field gives us glore.\nWen we have died tha onle theng ye hav left es yer glore... For Urguan...\nWe fight with Honor...\nAnd for glory...\nWe dent fear our enemies...", ""),
        StaticBook("Golden Pools", "Aluatis Lorenthus", "=========================Banning of the Golden Pools\nBy: Peurith\n=========================Transcribed by Peurith - Scribe of Malin.\n[Only this passage remains legible.]\nThey are turning pale like corpses! They may as well be coming back with fins for arms and gills for ears! It is not right what they are doing. Such flagrant disrespect for our forefather, our gods. Until we know the full extent of these pools of gold,\nKing Malin has issued an indefinite ban on their use.\nIt is unknown how Princess Larihei will react. May Malin guide us in the dark hours to come.\n        -Irrin Sirame", ""),
        StaticBook("Gorundyr History", "Ketiley Strong-Heart", "*It is clear to see that this was written in fine onyx ink and has eloquent, fluid, and graceful letters.*\n\n\n      Gorundyr History\n\n          Written By:\n\n        Ketiley of Orvar\nHistory:\nThe Gorundyr originate from the Savaar, the self-given name for their ancient homeland located in the northern reaches of Anthos. For the Gorundyr, the belief in their gods is a large part of their identity as a people. It is believed that should\none gain the favour of the gods, they will be granted immortality and a place in the heavens.\n\nFrom the early days of their tribes, the Gorundyr have thrived in the harsh, frozen mountains of the north. Habitable land was scarce, however, the hardened\nGorundyr began to look toward each other to solve their problems. Wars raged for centuries over food, land, and other natural resources. That is, until one man put an end to the squabbling. Known as Barid The Reaver, he was a memer of the petty Clan\nOrvar. Barid led his people to victory and united the clans of the Gorundyr for the first time in history. He is credited as being the first High King, and to this day is the only man to have held that title.\n\nTheir prosparity would not last, however, for\ncreatures of evil had begun to awaken around them. It is said that demons with blackened skin rose from their frozen graves and began to terrorize the Gorundyr. A plague started to spread among the various clans with a ferocity never seen before.\nBetween beast and disease, the Gorundyr began to slowly fade away. Then, as the earth began to shake and the land began to sunder, they looked to the skies for answers.  It seemed, however, that the gods had abandoned them. What survivers were left agreed\nto flee to the southern lands in an attempt to save themselves from destruction.\n\nWhat they hoped to be a relief from their torments was met with disappointment. The land was covered in desolation far and wide. Other beings were fleeing as well, people\nwith odd appearances and strange clothing that the Gorundyr did not recognize. Weary of their situation, the Gorundyr marched southwards still, hoping to find the answers they desired. It was only when they came upon a large Temple that the events of late\nseemed clearer to them. Large armies from many different peoples had gathered here to fight the creatures from the north, what the Gorundyr had now learned to be called the “Scourge”. It seemed that their isolation had kept them in an ignorance about the\nworld around them. There was little time to ponder, however, as the armies of the Scourge descended upon the great host. The Gorundyr consolidated into one great Warband joined the others whom fought for survival against this seemingly impossible foe.\nJust as it seemed as if the armies of the mortal men would triumph, the land around them shuddered in warning. A large tidal wave appeared in the distance, raging towards both Scourge and mortal man. Many of the surviving Gorundyr sent quiet prayers to\nthe gods, unsure if this was to be their aid or damnation. They turned and followed the other survivors as they fled to towards a massive gateway. Upon entry, they found themselves in a strange new world just as the door of the arch slammed shut behind\nthem. The few survivors of the Gorundyr knelt from exhaustion and began to laugh together. The gods had given them a fierce battle to prove their worth, and they had passed. Standing tall, they gazed out unto the land before them, vowing to make the most\nof their new life.\n\nBrief history of Beliefs:\nThe Gorundyr believe in a vast array of deities said to number in the hundreds. There are, however, nine main deities that play a large part in the lives of men. When Gorund created existance, he showed his\nchildren his vision of the earth and life upon it. With no words to describe what they saw, they descended to the earth and began to work his image into reality...\nThe gods were not perfect, however. Shortly after creation, evil dug it's claws into\nMaratsu, Master of the Sky, shattering his mind. He spread his wings of midnight and drowned out sun and sky. It is here that a fierce battle raged as Gorund fought a war for existence itself. Maratsu was powerful, but proved no match for the power of\nGorund and his children. Since his body could not be destroyed, his wings were broken and he was banished to the earth. It was here where he would be imprisoned beneath the Heart Tree, a structure created by Lagara to connect nature and the cosmos.\nBound by the roots of the Heart Tree, the priests of the Gorundyr believe that Maratsu will one day break free of his bonds and bring about the end-times.\n\nBurials and Afterlife:\nDeath is far from final in the thoughts of the Gorundyr. Burial practices\nconsist of burying food, weapons, and ornaments with the dead. It is believed that while the mortal form will stay behind, the souls and their possessions will be gathered by Ankou and brought to the Blessed Isle where they may dine and slumber with\nGorund. Only those whom are seen as worthy in the eyes of the gods would be ascended to the heavens and granted immortality. Those whom are deemed unworthy in the eyes of the gods will be forgotten, their mortal being their last step in existance.\nThe Gorundyr bury their dead in large burial mounds, dozens of bodies often occupying a single one. The more powerful clans or lords have larger areas dedicated in their memory, with more belongings to portray their wealth and strength.\nCremation is not practised by the Gorundyr, and is in fact feared by all. It is believed that the burning of ones body will also destroy the soul, preventing their ascension to the heavens. It is common, then, to burn those who have dishonoured the gods,\nsuch as heretics or traitors.\n\nMilitary:\nMoulded by war and conflict within, the Gorundyr are an extremely war-bound and violent people. Historically, the Gorundyr come from harsh and unforgiving land, and as their people grew, so did the need for more\nresources and food. Since the beginning of time, war has been a constant, shaping the most able-bodied of them into tools of war.\nGorundyr Warbands:\nWarbands are the main military structure for the Gorundyr. While these bands are usually formed by individual clans, there have been many instances where warriors will flock to one individual seeking riches and glory, if they have the\nrenown and respect to lead. Operating on a system of equality, the warriors within must respect and honour those whom they fight with on the field of battle. As such, those who fight within a warband form a bond of brotherhood, willing to fight and die\nwith the brother or sister beside them. Those who prove dishonourable or untrustworthy are banished from fighting with the others, as no man will fight shoulder-to-shoulder with someone he does not trust. Anyone who has come of age and undergone the\nsacred rites in the eyes of the gods is able to join a warband, in the hopes of proving themselves. It is then up to them to win not only the favour of their brethren, but that of the gods as well.\nMasters of the seas, the Gorundyr have created\nlightweight vessels that can travel at great speeds. These longboats are their main tool in war and are essential for the mobility of their armies. The Longboats allow for travel beyond their lands, and are largely undetectable.\nThis gives the Gorundyr the advantage of stealth in their raids.\n\nWeapons and Armours:\nThe Gorundyr are masters of speed and agility, the bulk of their armies being that of light infantry. One-handed axes, swords, and shields, are stable weapons in a\nwarband and have been mastered over the centuries of their use. Battle-axes are also popular among many warriors and nothing is more fearsome than a Gorundyr reaver cleaving through the battlefield. Archers often make up a small part of a warband soldier,\nfiring from behind the safety of a shield wall and acting as support troops.\nFor defense, warriors of the Gorundyr are clad in studded-leather and chainmail. Rarely will you see one wear a breastplate and their smiths are not skilled enough for full-plate\narmour.\n\nShield Maidens:\nWhile the Gorundyr are a largely male dominated society, at least on the battlefield, there are exceptions. Many women spend their lives training for combat and are even opening welcome within the warbands.\nCalled Shield-Maidens, these women are considered as equal as the others they fight with. Shield-Maidens are highly sought after as brides, though most do not marry and instead dedicate their lives to fighting in honour of the gods.\nChampions of the Gods:\nIn old Gorundyr legends there is mention of great warriors who not only attracted the eyes of the gods, but their blessings. These men and women were said to have been granted divine gifts and are usually considered demi-gods\nthemselves. Only one champion can exist per god at any given time and requires full dedication to said deity.\nAppearance:\nWhile many of the Gorundyr were diverse in their appearances, the near extinction of their people removed many traits from the gene pool. Still, most Gorundyr can be credited as being very tall and large compared to other humans.\nAveraging a height of six feet five inches, Gorundyr warriors are some of the fiercest sights on the battlefield. The most common eye-colours would be brown, green, and grey. Some Gorundyr are known for their dark red or maroon eyes, a trait that is\nlinked to the gods, specifically Ankou. It is easy to identify a Gorundyr by not only their size, but their pale skin and long dark hair. Braided hair is very common among both men and women.", ""),
        StaticBook("Grand Kingdom", "Kardel Irongut", "DWARVEN HISTORY:\nTHE GRAND KINGDOM OF URGUAN\n___________________An overview as recounted by Kardel Irongut\n___________________PRESS FOR THE HOLMIC ACADEMY OF THE ARTS AND SCIENCES\n___________________\nThe history of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan is long as unpredictable: it spans over two centuries of political intrigue, civil strife, civilizational advancement, and almost unceasing war. Indeed, the Grand Kingdom of Urguan represents the dwarven military\nmachine at its finest, as its very foundations were in the War Council of King Gotrek Firemane \"the Absent.\"\n\nThe Second Kingdom of Urguan was a time of reformation. Founded by Simppa, each successive king from him deteriorated the Kingdom's\nstatus and power. When Gotrek Firemane took the throne and proved himself a docile and inept leader, he appointed a War Council to rule the military matters of his kingdom is his stead. Hoping this would lead to more popularity, Gotrek had put into place\nhis own overthrowal.\n\nThorik Grandaxe, today remembered as a paragon for his founding of the kingdom, was an apt and famous general much loved by the Dwarven people of the Kingdom of Urguan. In a carefully organized coup, he overthrew\nGotrek and seized power for himself. Renaming the kingdom into the Grand Kingdom of Urguan, Thorik aimed to establish a new era of prominence for the dwarves. He was succesful at this, as the Grand Kingdom of Urguan won many wars in the years to come.\nEarly in its existence, the Grand Kingdom's unruly size proved detrimental to its existence. It fragmented almost immediately after its first formation upon the mysterious dissapearance of Grand King Thorik. After a while, it was once again\nrekindled by Thorik himself, who returned from what he claimed to be a posession by Ondnarch and assumed the old throne.\n\nThe Second Grand Kingdom of Urguan was the most powerful iteration of this dwarven state. Several dwarven holds, having\nrealized that independence meant slow political and economic suffocation for their estates, subordinated themselves under this new line of democratically elected Grand Kings. Those which did not, like Vaerhaven, were subjugated with destructive\nstrength by the Grand Kings of Urguan.\n\nThe beginning of the Second Grand Kingdom of Urguan marks the Dwarven Golden Age, and the reigns of its first three Grand Kings constitue the now legendarized epoch of dwarven history known as the Era of Paragons.\nThis Era is so named because each successive king from the founding of the second Grand Kingdom for three tenures was to be remembered by history as a Paragon of the Brathmordakin.\n\nAfter Thorik, Omithiel Strongbrow, a famed architect and ingenious\ntactician and noble was elected to the Obsidian Throne. Grand King Omithiel, later remembered as Paragon Omithiel \"the Builder\" constructed several large cities as testament to the glory of dwarves. Most notable of these cities was Kal'Azgoth, the city of\ntreasure.\n\nOmithiel reorganized the guilds, revived dwarven linguistic traditions, re-emphasized ancient dwarven history, and won several large wars. The most notable of these wars were the Third and shorter Fourth Orcish Wars. Grand King Omithiel\nbrought a golden age of prosperity for Urguan, but his reign was ended when he died of old age.\n\nOmithiel was succeeded by the legendary Grand King and Paragon Thorin Grandaxe, \"the Conqueror.\" Thorin's reign started with a period of rapid\nconsolidation. Unruly dwarven Jarls and Lords were quickly subjugated under Thorin, and every last city ruled by dwarves paid tribute to him. \n\nThorin then began a campaign of military expansion. He quadrupled the Legion in size, and placed at its head a\nseries of qualified Grand Marshalls who were clever tactitians. With the army reforged and his holdings secured, Thorin then turned his eyes northward, to the non-dwarven realms of Anthos.\n\nThorin's legendary conquest of Anthos remains the single\ngreatest feat of military expansion in all of history. Not even the Empire of Oren could achieve his level of domination. Thorin conquered the entire continent, his army millions strong and his rule absolute. He dismantled the Holy Orenian Empire and\nforced the human kings to bow to him. Famously, when asked to enter a peace treaty with the northern human kingdoms after the dismantling of Oren, Thorin showed up as if to sign the treaty and burned it before the assembly at the cloud temple.\nThorin's death came unexpectedly and at the peak of his conquests. Disfigured by the deamon Ondnarch, Thorin passed away and declared his vassals liberated from his rule, profecising that no other dwarven ruler would ever be able to achieve his glory.\nHis prophecy has proven true, as since then the Dwarves have never neared the glory of the Grand Kingdom under Thorin.\n\nAfter the Era of Paragons, the Grand Kingdom quickly fell into stagnation at the hands of innumerably incompetent Grand Kings. The most\nfamed of such incompetents are Dizzy Irongrider \"The Delver King,\" Indago Stormhammer \"The Banquet King,\" Zahrer Irongrider \"The Elf Lover,\" and Uldar Irongut \"The Treasonous.\" \n\nDespite experiencing a period of growth during its\nexistence in the Fringe, the Grand Kingdom slowly buckled under the weight of ineffective leadership and an increasingly unmotivated populace. The Eighteen Years war with Oren on Vailor proved nearly fatal to the Grand Kingdom. Led into war by Midgor\nIreheart, a descendant of Kjell Ireheart, the Grand Kingdom lost half of its Vailorian territory and was only saved from annihliation by Grand King Rhewen Frostbeard.\n\nRhewen Frostbeard briefly declared an Urguanian Empire, but this venture dismantled\nwhen Vandoria, the second Archduchy of the Empire, fell to the Oreners from internal pressure. \n\nA new iteration of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan was reformed by Grand King Kardel Irongut, \"the Reformer.\" Left with a disfunctional economy and ruined\ninfrastructure, Kardel Irongut reformed the Grand Kingdom into an autocratic rather than Oligarchic state. He pursued peace with Oren and focused on architecture and culture. Kardel's rule marks the beginning of the Silver Age of the Dwarves, which saw a\nbrief albeit significant resurgence in dwarven power.\n\nThe apex of the Silver Age of Urguan was the rule of Grand King Algoda Frostbeard \"the Fist.\" Algoda saw a quickly stagnating Grand Kingdom, allied hopelessly with Oren, and turned the\nGrand Kingdom around, doubling the military and re-instating strong governance. He rebelled against Oren's nearly global hegemony and lead several attacks alongside the Axios Coalition to destroy the Empire. Algoda was captured in legendary fashion and\nexecuted in Oren while visiting a friend unofficially: his last words were \"This changes nothing,\" refering to the inevitable victory of the Axionite Coalition.\n\nThe Axionite Coalition went on to completely crush the Orenian Empire, and the Grand Kingdom\nof Urguan fast approached its twilight years. Grand King Bastion Ireheart \"the Stable.\" Bastion lead the Grand Kingdom into a final age of prosperity before its collapse, maintaining the existing system and strengthening the dwarves for a time. However,\nthe stagnation of the Kingdom soon caught up to him, and he committed suicide, leaving the Kingdom to ruin.\n\nTotal destruction came when the kings after Bastion, namely Zahrer Irongrider, who attempted to reform the Kingdom into an absolute\nmonarchy and adopted the royal name \"Silverbeard,\" allied itself with Oren and was utterly crushed in the War of the Beards by the Frostbeard lead Kingdom of Kaz'Ulrah. Fili Grandaxe's surrender to Kaz'Ulrah has been legendarized as the epitome of the\nGrand Kingdom's state of being: a former giant on its knees, drawing its final breaths. The life of the Grand Kingdom was ended when Kerwyr Frostbeard declared himself High King of Kaz'Ulrah and successor of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan, marking the\nbeginning of the Third Age of the dwarves.\n\nThe Grand Kingdom of Urguan was succeeded by several dwarven factions, the most significant being the Kingdom of Kaz'Ulrah and the Consulate of Holm. The Temple of Az'Adar is also considered a minor splinter of\nthe once Grand kingdom. Among dwarves today, the Grand Kingdom is remembered with mixed feelings. It has been mythologicized as an establishment testafying to Dwarven strength, but also as a warning against oligarchy and stagnation.", ""),
        StaticBook("Great Sun", "Man Praisesunius", "\n   \"Mermaids are\n    affronts to the\n    son. Sun.\"\n\n       -Quinn\n\n\n   14th of the\n   First Seed\n   1647\nHAVE you ever wondered why our nipples are darker? \n\n    Have you ever thought about it, future acolyte? Once you finish reading this, you'll finally be a fully fledged SUN acolyte.\nThe sun is great and we need to praise it. If there is no sun, there are no wood elf chicks to harrass in the fae ring since they would be so pale that they would get downgraded to high elves. I mean, who doesn't likes a wood elf in the fae ring?\nThe high elves are the evil scum of this world because the sun never touches their skin, their dirt makes a such great layer of scum that it blocks the sunlight, but they hide it with their weird bunny hat magic.\n\nAnd this is why we need to kill them.\nThe dark elves are the best. All they do is to stay in a cave but they maintain the properties they gained with the sun. Their ancestral stood naked in the sun for so long that the sun in their hearts grew and their nipples are even darker.\nIn our sun, correct and true faith, the dark elves are the only kind of elves that can grow nipple hair to the point that they can make braids with it. Each braid appeals greatly to the sun god.\n\nThe sun god himself has nipple hair braids.\nNow, let us all take a moment to praise the sun\npraise the sun\npraise the sun\npraise the sun\nNow, go outside and extend your arms, praising the sun.", ""),
        StaticBook("Greetings.", "George Gaia", "Hello. You may call me Mentor. There is something called \"The First Assassins Brotherhood.\" While we're still small we try and recruit only trusted people. My actual name is George Gaia, the previous owner of this house. The same person that made this\nhidden basement. I wish to get to know you. Once I find out who'se the next house owner I will make sure to \"keep an eye on you.\" I am a male and for the most time you will see me wearing a grey coat. If you find this and notice me\nI suggest that you say hello, and we can talk about this oppurtunity.", ""),
        StaticBook("gressy is a hobo", "Cato", "gressy is a ugly hobo", ""),
        StaticBook("GRQ: Vol. 2", "Ogdan Goldhand", "Get Rich Quick\n\n      Volume 2\n         \n         Shops\n\n\n\n         by:\n\n Ogdan Goldhand\nFirst Grand Merchant\n    of Kaz'Ulrah\nWhat is a shop?\n\nA shop is a place you conduct business and exchange goods for minas. They can be very convenient for you and the buyer. Would you rather shout across a city or walk down to your local stall and buy your food?\nHow do I obtain a  shop?\n\nA shop can be built if you have permission, it can be bought in prime locations, or even given to if you ask the right person. You must often contact a local steward.\nWhat do I do with \nmy shop now?\n\nYou've done it you've got your shop. Now you need to ask yourself three questions. These will determine what you sell, what you buy, and more importantly give you an idea on how to price them.\nWhat do I have an abundance of?\n\nWhat do the shops here not have in stock?\n\nHave I heard recently of someone buying something I can obtain?\nOnce you have your answer to those three questions you can start putting items up for sale in your shops. You should have a good idea on pricing from your research. If you read and followed Volume #1 that is. If you didn't gather information for an\nitem you want to price. Guess, ask, or simply try to sell it and have them make an offer on the item.\nHow will my shop \nmake me money?\n\nYou must keep your shop in stock at all times. This means you must either have a way to obtain the goods or a person who works for you obtain them for you. Better yet, your shop can buy items. That means\nthat anyone that buys from your shop, can also sell to your shop. This is free labor.\n\nYou sell an Iron ingot for 5 minas, but you can also buy it for 2. You can make 3 minas per ingot. This applys to every item. If you sell it, buy it but for lower.\nDONT FORGET to put a cap on how much you can buy. Sometimes you cant afford 10000 iron so putting a cap of 100 or 200 limits someone from sucking all your minas dry in one swoop while still keeping up your stock.\nLocation\n\nIs your shop along a road? It's a good idea to sell food there. \n\nIs your shop in a city full of wood furniture/style? Stock that wood.\n\nIs your shop the only  one stocking iron?\nsell it for higher and keep it in stock!\n\nThe key to shops is knowing what, where, and how much. \n\n\n\nLookout for Volume #3\nof GRQ. \n\n- Ogdan Goldhand", ""),
        StaticBook("Guard Report", "Luna Lyeis", "Visitors:\nClaire\nRina\nAdelle\nAedwin * visited twice\nLockezi* incident\nAster\nBolagin Eisenhorn\nAiden Druid \nElenora\nGronhiik\nDiligence culligan\nElinor* Incident\nLyra\nShan Wu Chen\nDamien\nSarrion\nMark Lander\nIadiel\nToren\nCarolina\nGalvin\nOri\nAmara\nSylva\nDivayth\nDwyn\nDesimir\nVaren'thal\nSkylar\nAllian Mendrand\nShopping:\nLotte Baptiste\nKlaus\nEvelyn of clan Eledil\nCharles the bald\nJeremiah Longhorn* Incident\nMorug\nJarvis\nRandal Eisenhorn\nKivek\nGarrond Frostbeard\nLevithor Eisenhorn\nFinmour Eisenhorn\nElorth the Darlog* searching for a suitor\nAlfred\nBolagin Eisenhorn\nResidents:\nKalius Lyeis\nRichard\nElvira\nIncidents:\n*Lockenzi tresspassed in the guard house, and the ramparts of the gate.\n*Elinor and Lockenzi returned to the ramparts after being warned and removed. were warned and removed again\n*Elinor and Lockenzi poisioned Tea and made on duty guard drink\nIt was tainted with a sleeping draught. They then tried to break into the guard house. Once Guard on duty woke up again, chased them out of the city with sword in hand.\n*Rumours of Dawrves attacking Sutican citizens, Charles the bald identified them as,\nthe Eisenhorn clan.\nUpon investigations suspects had fled.\n*Spook that slipped through the gates set of a ward within the tavern, causing a massive conflict leading to several clerics and paladins getting involved to take down the target.\nCasulties unknown.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guard Report #10", "Luna Lyeis", "Zrarly\nBanished person\nBroke into the gate house\nimpersonated a guard\nStole everything from the gate house.\nAssualted a Guard.\n\nAnd Officer Vilta allowed them to leave freely, along with his companion Wargoth.\nIs this what the guards have turned into in but 1 elven day after the departure of the captain. The barracks entrace was demolished, making it almost impossible to imprision those that break the law.\nAll my reports were stolen from the gate house\nalong with anything else that would have been within the chests. luckily i make them in atleast triplicate.\n\nThe gatehouse needs to be overhauled in the matter of sercruity, new guards need to be given keeps and the locks must be change each time a guard\nleave the service.\nFurther more the law should be upheld no matter what. What Vilta did today in spite of all the charges piled up agaisnt wargoth was simply appaling, this wargoth person was given a free ride on all charges. This is the second time an\narrest of mine has blatantly been ignored. \nIs this the king of future in the policing and protecting of Sutica i have to look forward to in the days ahead. If so, they will be dark indeed without the guiding light of our former Captain.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guard Report #11", "Luna Lyeis", "Zrarly entered the city multiple times and on each occasion myself and cyrene escorted them. The guardforce needs to be expanded so a regular watch can be maintained upon the gate.\nFurthermore we were called out to the halfling village on rumours of two orcs taking the village hostage and forcing them to construct a shrine.\nWhen we arrived the orcs were gone, and the halflings insisted that we leave and not dismantle the shrine.\nsaying they'd rather it remain standing and avoid any retaliation if they were to destory it.\nThis being settled we agreed and left them to their peace.\nA dragon flew over the city multiple times, as to why and where it came from those facts are unknown. Several men are manning the tower balista to try and shoot it down upon its next pass if possible.\nSeveral bolts where fired but none hit to my knowing", ""),
        StaticBook("Guard Report #12", "Luna Lyeis", "Kary promoted me to the rank of Guard, and paid me my salary.\n\nKary assigned me a recruit to spar with and oversee. After some back and forth i inquired if kary had seen what he had wished.\nMy assessment of the recruit is he is fine in a scruff, although his tactics are a bit underhanded. He might have had military training at some point or another, although his rogueish element seems to be at the forefront. While i wouldn't find this\nindividual as a military officer or solider as a guard he should be a fine fit. While my personal prefrence of straight up combat is all very well and good i am woman enough to admit any plans or sense of honour doesn't last the first moments of engagment\nwith the enemy.\nI took the new recruit back to the lord protector to get his set of keys and set him up with his guard uniformed armour.\n\nFurther training and spars with this recruit should prove interesting now i know what to expect\nif we were to ever come to blows again. Further note, i should get a blacksmith to adjust some of my armour as when i did a combat roll i think i may have bruised my rib, not that i showed it during the fight but it was part of the reason i asked to end\nthe fight.\nWhile plate armour is far more versatile and manuverable than many would have you believe it can still be unwieldy at times.\n\nEven with hours, upon hours of training in various conditions of how to use it to the best of its ability.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guard Report #13", "Luna Lyeis", "Indra\nJacob Boom - sword and knives.\nDael'ran - Ascended cyrenes brother?\nElvira - resident\nTam'naeuth terin - cleric, no weapons but is going to leave with some?\nhare druid taynuel - resident? lives in druid grove doesn't own land.\nare they counted as a resident?\nCharles the bald - dwarf regular visitor.\nDamien - dagger\nbobby the dwarf - an axe.\nAeran\n^The dwarf and Aeran think its funny to pretend to be hurt by the ward.\nGuyden Aureon - three blades and a rope.\nMakashima - Glaive\nfinally spoke his own name at the gate checkpoint. AKA job 'williams'\nyazarek doomforge - resident.\nZa'kabar\nEliza - not a resident\nWanted citizens door\naccess for some reason, since she doesn't go anywhere else.\nPheobe - armoured blonde woman, large sword on back\nJuldra arrived saying she needed to hide? and asked if anything strange has happened recently. she came to escape fire in than\nCourt mage was in the gate house holding up residents. specifcally claire and aryn skelt\nHe caused quiet a stir, but i believe that he is a court mage as with the changing of the locks he had access to the gate house. and the other guards seemed to be\nfine with him. to avoid any undue restlessness with the residents i took over and let claire in before further words were exchanged in heat.\nI have an odd feeling that makashima has a thing for me, his mood shifted rather dramatically when i showed him my wedding ring.\nHe seemed to have taken a keen interest in my husband suddenly, its a bit disconcerting if i'm totally honest.\nThe only reason i'm writing this in a report is due to his interest in me since the incident in the gate house, and the criminal behaviour he has shown in the past.\nSo for the sake of record i am putting my thoughts and theorys onto paper incase anything\ncomes of my concerns.\nSo Makashima gave me, some weapons, a unique looking spear and a aurum blade.\nSerinath - sword and bow.\nCecilia - druid\nAscal managed to get up on the top of the  gate, Vilta speaks highly of him and he's respected in sutica so i let it slide.\nHe showed me the progress on the enchanting of my blade, he says it should be done soon which will be good.\nFrostbeards were attacking people on Sutican roads. Specificly they attacked one of the Doomforge clan that have taken up residents in Sutica, 3 frostbeard ambushing him.\nDormin and Dural Doomforge were attacked.\nDoomforge live in clock district house 2.\nUngo bundo was there when the attack happened, seemingly on the side of the frost beards.\none was of the strongbrow clan.\nThey were dwarves of Kal'ulrah kaz'ulrah?", ""),
        StaticBook("Guard Report #15", "Luna Lyeis", "The elf from the other night showed up in town. he had no memory of the events of the prior night and his count of murder upon officer Viltaren. with the aid of a pleb we killed him, although i would of prefered to arrest and put them through the\nprocess of banishment so as to not have them continually visiting Sutica with no memory of why they seem to wake up at the monks temple every so often.\nAfter the death of the elf how ever viltaren went a little overboard and in no uncertain terms\nkilled the man that aided us in striking down her own murderer. While Viltaren had some semblence of legallity backing her actions i can't say i agree with them. yes the man in question intervened in guard affairs, insulted the guard, sutica and a guard\nofficer and refused direct order from a guard officer to leave. He did aid us in enacting some semblence of justice, but a common problem is the guards never having the support of the citzens during times of conflict.\nand the one time we have someones undivided support, he is executed for his trouble, i agree he could of obeyed Viltarens orders but after what he helped us with, i can understand the stance he took.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guard Report #16", "Luna Lyeis", "Cahir - visiting\nSkale Avern - Aila's father\nkayah sul'onn - visiting the library\nfrostbeard dwarf - no weapons - beodrik\nAtlas - Tavern\nsylvis - visiting\nElvira\nNerrin - Visiting\njeremiah longhorn - visiting\nvyrtra\nThe elf guilty of viltarens murder returned, i refused him entry to the city, while this goes against the kill order i thought it best give them a chance to know what they did, and why they are not welcome in the city anymore. furthermore an offical\nbanishment should be announced. and as a after note, i have told the elf to send a bird to the lord protector to speak on his 'case'\nhe came back to the gate under order of the lord protector to meet with him.\nSiaw - visiting- longsword and dirk\nVytharion - visiting - steel blade\nnerrin - visiting - steel halbard", ""),
        StaticBook("Guard Report #2", "Luna Lyeis", "Eisenhorn icndient.\nKivek Tora of the Eisenhorn dwarf clan turned himself in as on of the suspects in the attack of a sutican citizen the previous day. Refer to previous report for inital investigation.\nKivek confessed the clan came to the city searching\nto behead a sutican citizen on the behest of the longhorn clan.\nThe citizen that was attacked luckily survived and escaped the assualt the individual in question name was Richard.\nthe Eisenhorns still wish this individual to be killed simply for escaping.\nCaptain Archrim has forstalled Kiveks punishment in lue of him cooperating to act as an informant if the Eisenhorn clan was ever to return to Sutica. Correspondence is to be had via message through a Raven.\nTask with finding the identity of a hooded individual the suspect constantly refused orders of the Guard force.\nAsking for assitance from fellow guards, none heeded my call causing me concern in the worth of my fellow guardsman.\nTaking the task on by myself, i continued to acost the individual in question they contiually refused orders to remove the hood, stating that they were a citizen, when asked to confirm this they offered no proof.\nMoving to arrest the individual and force\nthem from the city or to a jail cell they removed their hood and robes revealing many blackened bandages covering the 'womans' body. \nMaking pursuit of the bandaged person they fled and leapt from the sutican walls diving into the lake below.\nRecomendation - All guards go through mandatory team work training...\nThe hooded and robed figure covered in bandages sought out for further questioning and detainment.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guard Report #3", "Luna Lyeis", "Visitors:\nRevian\nAeran - Coup man, visiting Taynuel the druid\nElinor - Allowed to enter after apologiesing for the previous days antics\nGobbo the Goblin\nThurak'yar\nUnknown child - let in, seemed lost and shy.\nLyanna Faisehn\nGuyden Aureon\nAvery - Holy kid?\nDimmesdale-preacher\nMarlon Day\nAngelica Silversteed\nLilly* Incident\nJohn Williams* suspect\nJob Williams* incidet\n(Also known as, Wuming the nameless and Maka Job)\nAelthir* suspect\nSulien* suspect\nKren* suspe\nResidents:\nLeyunia\nRichard\nIncidents:\nArmoured Party Visitig - Group of three armoured individuals arrived at the same time, they were short tempered. names were Aelthir, Sulien and Kren. I belive one of them to be a elven prince i met previously. unsure on accuracy of my assumptio\nClerics - Found a cleric by the name of gray? working the gates. he was causing a scene and antagonizing visitors more than guards. relived him and sent him on his way.\nLockenzi apologies for the previous days antics, and has stated that he's interested in joining the Sutican guard. I suggested he find Captain Archrim.\nHe seems like a good kid? when hes not tormenting you atleast.\nAnd elven kid? his age is 40 somthing,\nbut he acts as a teen, curious at the difference in some people and races.\nJob Williams Incident.\nhe snuck into the gate house, through apprently an open door, as to who opened it i am unsure as i had not yet left the gate house. with the assitance of Captain Archrim we interrogate him brieefly.\nHe seems to go by alot of names, i am unsure if any are actually real.\nJob\nJob Williams\nWuming the nameless\nMaka Job\nHe somehow eneded up outside, and when he was delayed with entry he force himself into the first gate\nWith bow drawn i halted his attempt at the second gate, in lifting the first gate he reinjured a previous wound, almost bleeding out between gates.\nLilly offered medical aid but i refused entry to the city, until he handed over his glaive weapon. It will\nbe returned to him once he has been healed and departs the city. Both the 'Williams' brothers are suspect to me, somthing seems off about both of them, mainly Job, or WUming, or maka job.\nLilly seems to know job in some way, perhaps further inqury\nis needed.\nMaka job broke into the guard house, with keys! and stole his glavie back, when i attempted to arrest him he attacked me.\nLockezi went for help, when they arrived and started to beat the gate house door down to help Job fled.\nDecription of Job\nChain/Plate armour mix,\nGreen tabardlike clothing.\nCarried a 7ft tall glaive\nBlack hair\nBrown eyes\nLockenzi, Rav and Thurnak all came to aid me during the attack.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guard Report #4", "Luna Lyeis", "Residents:\nClaire\nAhryn Skelt\nEurielle\nVisitors:\nAvery - Lucienist Order\nDimmesdale - Preacher\nLocke\nJohnathen Hartrot IV*\nPaya\nJohnathen Hartrot IV was asked to remove his helmet and  revlead a badly disfigured face covered in burns.\nLater as i was posting wanted posters, Johnathen pulled out a very large grey cape and withdrew the head of Job Williams. The head was placed in the\nguard barracks in a sack. He advised me that the monks will have likely worked there magic on the wanted person.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guard Report #5", "Luna Lyeis", "Visiting:\nFae\nPaxton Calum\nNaevys\nPrince Aelthos Tundrak\nFather Dimmesdale\nNaevys again\nThe Ram Druid\nIlondr\nThe city was besieged by a hot of spiders and undead lead by a drak druid. Many Suticans rallied in the defence of the federation ending in vicotry, aided by the minions of the druid seemingly turning on the dark power.\nOne man that helped with the defence of the city wearing ivory armour triggered the ward on departing the city. He was locked in between gates with several citizens so to avoid collateral damage the spook was let depart unmolestered.\nOfficer Viltaren informed me that the banished indivdual Ianril is someone of great power and should not be engaged in combat single handedly or without great assitance. When dealing with Ianril try to talk him out peacefully before even considering force\nHartrot the man whom was to be given the reward for brining the head of Job Williams to the Sutican guard on account of the wanted notice was indentified as a darkstalker spook by Cleric Aila. A short melee ensued as together we pushed him back into the\ncorner causing him to throw himself from the wall to escape.\nChasing the spook across the lake the ascended Haila entered into a coversation with the spook in an attempt to negotiate with it.\nwhen this failed Aila resumed her celrical duties and struck\nat the darkstalker. soon after the spook injured aila causing her to collapse to the ground. The spook took the time to flee thus allowing us to get Aila to safety and return her to the city for healing by Haila.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guard Report #6", "Luna Lyeis", "Visiting:\nAluatis Lorentus\nRam Druid\nAlric Dusten\nBobby Stormfist - never heard of the clan.\nClaire\nLockezi\nAlric Dusten and Dog\ngaroll\n3 others - forgot names before report\nOld human came by the gate house inquring about work. I've directed him to speak to either a steward or minister. Specific recomendaitons were the Clerics Gray, kary and Aerith.\nDue to his more senior looking years I do not foresee a future in the Watch.\nLong shift standing watch in the tavern for lady Aila as requested by Captain Archrim personally. The watch was uneventful the only thing of note being that my husband Kalius Lyeis met with Aila's clerical teacher to talk about the path of a cleric.\nFour individuals arrived at the same time, one i assumed was garoll although they were acting most percurliar. They didnt seem to remember who i was despite being friends. The others were let in, and Garoll left going for a stroll. Not sure if they return\ned.\nMore visitors:\nGorg\nAeran\nEurielle - responsible for unknown child.\nUnknown Child - Toren possible father.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guard Report #7", "Luna Lyeis", "A Litch spook thing entered the tavern, aila and those down in the knights lounge begun attacking the creatures. the individual known as Atturi playfully sparked one fo his friends. While during this rather intense bout it was not the best idea.\nthe reaciton of several individuals afterwards was completely uncalled for. Vani'ra(?) held atturi at sword point, i put a stop to that thinking it was the end of it and seeing the clerics handleing the spook with deadly effectiveness.\nThey all then swarmed atturi for no reason, tieing him up dragging him kicking and screaming out into the town square. Once again i stepped in shackling him and claiming the incident under a guards umbrella of authrority to avoid the mob\nburning Atturi at the stake. This is when the so called Knight Cleric Gray stepped in and blatantly ignored my role as a guard, throwing the innocent man off the Sutica bridge with no cause. This is a blatant abuse of power and while he did avoid the burn\ning at the stake, the man was still shackled when thrown into the lake. The mob and gray then watched as he tried to swim, taunting him all the while. While i respect Grays role as a minister of Sutica i completely disagree with the course of action he\ntook especailly seeing as he had no business becoming involved in the incident he WAS NOT PRESENT FOR.\nI would ask again that Clerics either be given a rank within the guard so as to allow a proper chain of command. Or that they stay out of guard business", ""),
        StaticBook("Guard Report #8", "Luna Lyeis", "Spook raid repelled.\nMany injured.\n\nExpedition to kill the dark druid known as willow undertaken.\n\nWidow slain, but.. at a great cost.\n\nCaptain Archrim... is gone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guardian Creed", "Vailoen", "Creed of the Guardian\n\n'And so, may we carry the light of Xan into the darkness, swords in our hands and brothers at our side. One unbreakable shield against the coming darkness. One last blade, forged in defiance of fate.'\nI. We are the shield that guards the Descendants. We are the blade which cuts through the Chaos. We are the enforcers of Order. We are the light in the dark. Never shall we surrender when the shadows advance. Never shall we let our blades leave our-\nhands, 'till death finds us. Though we may fall in the course of our duty, it is fate we accept. Though we may find no thanks for our work, we ask none, for duty does not demand it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guidance", "'Johnny Dragon'", "The Darkness falls over us all, yet those who grasp immortality fall upon the same routine. Those who wish for power, focus on the same things. You have been granted a gift, yet this gift is something that must be earned. Hunt, hide, you shall be\nbrought into the forefront and tested. The Monks will not save you, if you fall by mortal means, then you shall be removed from this world.\nHunt the others, once this is done. You will be approached, you will learn then. But for now, you are a lost\nanimal. That is what you are without guidance, an animal.\n\nDo not let instinct, destroy you. Hide, fight or heal. Whatever you truthfully wish for, you shall have it. If, you survive against the others.\n\n\n- Johnny Dragon.", ""),
        StaticBook("GUIDE LINES", "Wargoth Falum'Lur", "Guidelines of the Fire\n   Elemental Shrine\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nIn order to determine the Tier of the shrine it must be skirmished upon. Only until then will the Tier be affected by the victor otherwise it remains stagnant.\nTier 1 - Small Fire, burning of brush and grass.\n\nTier 2 - Medium Fire, burning of some trees and wheat fields\n\nTier 3 - Large Fire, the spread grows uncontainable and must be fought against otherwise leaving a burned remains.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Athera", "Azoth Hawksong", "The\nTraveler's\nGuide\nTo\nAthera\nThe Cloud Peninsula\nIn every land to which the Descendants have travelled there has been a Cloud Temple.Either the secretive Cloud Order that looks after the Descendant Races is either always one step ahead of the mortal races or the\nworld truly is littered with empty sandstone monasteries waiting for mortal monks to move in. As is the case with all of the Cloud Temples, violence is both forbidden by law and magically prohibited within the sanctuary’s bounds.\nThe Abyss\nA pit of unfathomable depth and size, the Abyss is clearly no natural phenomenon. The fabric of the world itself seems torn there, with magical energies defying the laws of nature. At the edge of the Abyss islands\nfloat on nothing and water forever plunges into the depths without ever filling the Abyss or draining the seas. The Abyss seems impossible, yet there it is, its yawning depths visible to all who travel too far to the west.\nThe Shards\nThese colossal burned spikes of land jut out over the Great Abyss towards the west of Athera. Nothing grows upon these jagged fragments of whatever was there before the Abyss was formed. Most Atheran historians believe the shards to be\nthe result of a cataclysm involving magics beyond the capabilities of mortal magi, although so far no indication has been found of how old the Shards, and by extension the Abyss, are.\nAbove the shards, upon a floating isle lies what looks like an abandoned city, but it floats too high to be reached by explorers.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Earth.", "Dael", "乇卂尺ㄒ卄 \n乇ᐯㄖ匚卂ㄒ丨ㄖ几\n\nEarth evocation is the art of evoking earth from the void. To first do this one must learn how to connect to the void which firstly starts off with clearing ones mind of everything, this is often quite hard to do your very first time.\nI reccomend you go to a very quiet place and relax for awhile, get accustomed to the place and then begin to clear your mind of everything there is to think about, rather it be your emotions, or an itch you may have. Eventually you will be able to do so.\n▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅\nNextly is summoning the earth, once you've connected to the void you'll need to disconenct and go out and find a rock of some sort, i reccomend quartz sand for your first element. From here you need to inspect the element.\n▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅\n▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅\nTo inspect the element you need to know everything about it, the feel, the taste, the way it breaks, the forms it can take, the heat resistance, the way its made underground or in caves, the look of it, the smell of it.\n▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅\n▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅\nOnce you have gathered everything you can about the element, you must connect to the void again and feed the information you've learned about the material to the void. Focus soley upon summoning\n▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅\n▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅\nYou might be able to summon only a single grain of sand at first, but its a start. The more and more you do it the better it will become over time, but if you do not practice you cannot summon more and more. Eventually pebbles.\n▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅\n▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅\nI reccomend studying many elements, one of which is Magnetus, a magnetic metal-like material. This is good for countering any metal wielding people, armor, swords, arrows, spears etc. Aside from that explore other arcane arts.\n▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅▅\nWritten by Dael'ran in 1669.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Gukdan", "Gukdan'Raguk", "Part Azh:\n\n- Du nub bi racizt\n- Du nub uze burz mojo\n- Du nub blah zhit abowt zpiridz\n- Du nub blah zhit abowt zmiffin'\n- Du nub blah zhit abowt Raguk\n- Du nub blah zhit abowt Gukdan's friendz.\nBazik Blah tu gruk:\n\nBlah = Talk, Speak, etc\nGruk = Know, Learn\nLat = You\nMi = I, Me\nZpirid = Spirits\nBubhozh = Great\nHozh = Good\nNubhozh = Bad, No good\nZkah = Fuck\nPeep = See, Look, etc\nGukdan'z favrit Zpirids:\n\nGentharuz - Zpirid ub zmiffin' ahn dah forge. (Nub blah zhit.)\n\nGazgiazh - Zpirid ub Bluud agh Bone. Impurtant fur Bluudzmiffs lyke Gukdan\n\nLeyd - Zpirid ub Raguk agh ztrength\nFur Zmiffs Onlee:\n\nDu nub blah zhit abowt Gukdan's creatiunz.\n\nLet Gukdan peep lat wurk.\n\nTu learn frum Gukdan (As lat wuld) lat muzt bi hozh friendz agh kapable.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Sorcery", "Laergul", "===================\n\n             Guide to\n            Sorcerty\n\n\n       Transcribed by\n             Laergul\n\n          By Ambros_\n\n\n===================\nCHAPTER 1\nWhat is Arcane Magic?\nAll magic uses the smae power source, although what varies from magical user to magical is dependent on how the user goes about manipulating his/her powers. Arcane magic is often\nconsidered to be a more modern version of magic compared to the ancient druids ot the gifted Ascended or Undead, although none the less Arcane magic can be considered to be the most complex of magical manipulation.\nCHAPTER 2\nHow To Manipulate Arcane Magic\nArcane magic can be manipulated in a number of ways, although most scholars believe the best way to go about doing this is creating an image in your mind of what you want the final effect\neffect of your spell to be. Some scholars believe that the best way to use the most powerful form of magic is through emotion Of course this is quite wrong and this form of magic is hard to control and should never be done. Many mages claim  that their\npowers are akin to keys (necessary to unlcok the final effect of a spell) another, new theory has begun to gain ground among younger mages.  These energetic mages assert that components aren't keys, but rather locks, suggesting\nthat even the most learned of arcanists don't fully control their own powers, and that components are necessary intruments to keep the spells in check. Whether these locks were placed by the deities themselves or are simply such an old conention that\nno one today questions their utility is anyone's guess.\nCHAPTER 3\nDiffrent Types Of Magic\nMages are mostly a combat and \"trick\" type magic.  Rarely do they have access to many of the necromany and healing magic that the Undead, Ascended, or druids might have.  Although they can often\nachieve a number of other magical feats that the other ,agical orders can not.  Since arcane magic is a magic of the mind its power is based off of your intelligence then most often than not you will see a mage locking a door with a spell, shooting fire\nfrom his staff, or moving blocks of stone about.  This is due to the fact that arcane magic is not a spiritual form of magic so any so any form of \"spiritual\" type attributes about it are gone.  A healer mage is a very rare sight as well, healing magic is\na form of \"spiritual\" magic helping the mind cleanse and wash away pain and injury. Now of course you might see an unorthodox way of healing from a mage such as sealing a wound with fire or easing pain with a numbing spell. Whatever the case is\narcane magic is a magic of the mind.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Sorcery", "Ambros", "A Guide to Sorcery\n\n\n      By Ambros\nIn this book you will find a very simple guide on being a proper mage, this would include  your supplies you need as well as the proper training you need to become a decent mage.\nWhat is Arcane Magic?\nAll magic uses the same power source, although what varies from magical user to magical is dependent on how the user goes about manipulating his/her powers. Arcane magic is often considered to be a more modern version\nof magic compared to the ancient druids ot the gifted Ascended or Undead, although none the less Arcane magic can be considered to be the most complex of magical manipulation.\nHow To Manipulate Arcane Magic.\nArcane magic can be manipulated in a number of ways, although most scholars believe the best way to go about doing this is creating an image in your mind of what you want the final effect of your spell to be.\nSome scholars believe that the best way to use the most powerful form of magic is through emotion Of course this is quite wrong and this form of magic is hard to control and should never be done. Many mages claim that their powers are akin\nto keys-necessary to unlock the final effect of a spell-another, new theory has begun to gain ground among younger mages.  These energetic mages assert that components aren't keys, but rather locks, suggesting that even the most learned of\narcanists don't fully control their own powers, and that components are necessary intruments to keep the spells in check. Whether these locks were placed by the deities themselves or are simply such an old conention that\nno one today questions their utility is anyone's guess.\nDiffrent Types Of Magic\nMages are mostly a combat and \"trick\" type magic.  Rarely do they have access to many of the necromany and healing magic that the Undead, Ascended, or druids might have.\nAlthough they can often achieve a number of other magical feats that the other magical orders can not.  Since arcane magic is a magic of the mind its power is based off of your intelligence then more often than not you will see a mage locking a door with\na spell, shooting fire from his staff, or moving blocks of stone about.  This is due to the fact that arcane magic is not a spiritual form of magic so any form of \"spiritual\" attributes about it are gone.\nA healer mage is a very rare sight as well, healing magic is a form of \"spiritual\" magic helping the mind cleanse and wash away pain and injury. Now of course you might see an unorthodox way of healing from a mage such as sealing a wound with fire\nor easing pain with a numbing spell.  Whatever the case is arcane magic is a magic of the mind.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide: Alchemy", "The Scribe", "Fund. Alchemy\nby Unknown\nThe Tales of a Travelling Alchemist\nRewritten by: The Scribe\nForeword:\nI have heard many a man ask why one such as myself, would take such an interest and dedication in the art of alchemy when there are readymade spells that could do just the same, if not better, a job than an apothecary’s potion.\nMy response to this statement is rather simple whereas one must have a certain gift for spell-slinging, rune-craft, and spirit-speaking, one mustn’t need these frivolous commodities to use a balm to menda wound, shroud themselves in a\nnigh-invisible cloak with the swig from a bitter bottle, or set someone ablaze with bottle flame. Alchemy is not merely reproducing a wizard’s spell, but it is shaping the spell in a way for common man’s use. While magic still has its place in our world,\nAlchemy allows those without the gift to reap the same benefits as any mage might.\n\nChapter 1: The Fundamentals of Alchemy\n\nThe Principle and Law of Equivalent Exchange:\nAs I was providing my services to a rather quaint hamlet, which also provided me information of the local flora and more of the same legends I always hear of, I was approached by a man of common repute, and he produced a sarcastic,\nyet thought provoking, question. This question was, and I will attempt to reproduce the dialect as best as my phonetic ability will allow, “‘ow come, Mister, ‘hat ye’ can make all ‘dis ‘onderful stuff outta nothin’?” Now as shameful as his speech may be,\nthe question remains the same. How is it, that alchemists are capable or reshaping spells of sorcerers for the common folk out of nothing? The answer to this question is simple to state, but fairly difficult to grasp, and this is the\nPrinciple of Equivalent Exchange. Much like the money one gives to the merchant for the apple or slab of meat, one cannot have something for nothing. As the saying goes, “there is no such thing as a free brunch,” there is no such thing as a free potion.\nThis fundamental rule applies to old alchemy, through the use of symbols and rituals, far more than what I call “Modern alchemy. Although I will not get into ancient alchemy, I will state why this rule applies to Modern Alchemy. To craft a potion, for\nexample, a bottle of alchemist’s fire, one requires the materials. Much like a spell casted by a wizard, one cannot make something out of nothing. Know that to make a potion, and the possibilities are truly endless, one must take plants,\nobjects, and other representations of what they wish to make. For example, alchemist’s fire could be best produced with an - -, a mixture of - -, - -, and a dash of - -. Why would one need these items?\nThe - - provides the basic mixture of what we will make, and of course the better quality of the - - the better quality of the Alchemist’s Fire, but of course we will get further into this in a later chapter. The - -, a - - plant that grows\nmost often in deserts, is often - - and often associated with - -. This provides an superb symbol for the element of - -. The - -, another powerful symbol of  - -, mixes well with the crushed - - to produce something truly strong.\nThe - -, an optional portion, is another symbol of - -, albeit both weaker than blaze - - for both a - - fire burns far greater than - -. Now then, although you have these symbols of flame, rage, and warfare, one mustn’t simply\ntoss objects into the metaphorical cauldron. Precision is necessary, as always. One must measure their mixture carefully, or they will give too much. And giving too much will tip the scales of Equivalent Exchange, causing unpredictable results.\nWhy is this you might ask? When balance is achieved through Equivalent Exchanged, a mixture of the elements for the bottled spell of your desire, then all is well. But when you disrupt this balance and push on the world,\ntaking and forcing in too much of one or more element then the world will push back. Of course a word of caution is required, for one may think taking less is the best option when balance is not a certainty. This is a common misconception for not\nproviding enough of one element will result in the same conclusion, imbalance and chaos. This can be easily associated with cooking, too much of one ingredient will spoil the recipe, not enough of an ingredient will produce\nsimilar results. Of course it could also produce blander results, and in that case a potion may not be spoiled but it will simply be weak. This is preferable to exploding, of course.\nPreparation and You: \nNovice Alchemists often question me, what advice would provide the budding alchemist, what sip of wisdom could you provide one who desires to tap your fountain of knowledge? The answer to this is rather simple\npreparation is key to any potion. What is meant by this is that to mix a potion that you would have not mixed before, or do not mix often, you must have all the facts and supplies before you begin. This is best provided in a short list of required\nprocedures if one wishes to keep their eyebrows, fingers and life.\n\n1. Have all the Facts\n2. Know the Recipe\n3. Clean and check all your instruments are working order\n4. Ensure you have plenty of whatever ingredients you are using\n5. Keep and Calm Disposition\nEven having the recipe is not enough to craft a potion, but knowledge of its origins, ingredients, and uses are crucial. Although budding alchemists often overlook this step, it may save your life one day.\nThe Tales of a the Travelling Alchemist, Vol 1\n\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n\nRecopied by The Scribe\nCloud Temple", ""),
        StaticBook("Guild Letter", "Delvin Vulso", "*A letter would appear to be in you're box, once you open it, it seemed to be a written application* \"Hello! I noticed that there was a magic guild here, I decided why not join! Or at least try to.. Anywho, I wish to join you're guild! I have taken\ninterest in Fire evocation, and decided to learn it. I did! Now I know Fire evocation.. By joining the guild I wish to learn more about other magics? and maybe trying to teach some? if that is a thing in this guild.. I haven't found any use of me anywhere\nSo hopefully joining this guild will help me even further!\n~With utmost respect, Delvin Vulso.\n((I am available when Ever im on, usually 3 pm gmt +4))", ""),
        StaticBook("Haense Dossier", "Klaudia", "===================  Haense Royal Council      Meeting Dossier\n\n\n\n         15th of \n       First Seed\n          1689\n\n\n\n\n==================\n===================Objective: The princess of Haense was killied within the Curonic lands. I am to head to Haense and seek council with the Haenseti nobility and speak to them concerning the events that led to the killing and what their\n===================responce will be.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n==================\n===================After gaining access to the Kempost in Haense, i was quickly met with an audience with Queen Elizaveta. After expressing the council, and all of Cyrilsburgs deepest sorrow to the loss of the princess, the topic shifted\n=================\n===================to that of who was behind the murder. While the Queen said the Imperial Courts were accusing some bandit groups, she also said that a man she seemed to trust, Seigmund Corbish had his own lead on the matter.\n==================\n===================Corbish stated that a group known as the Blackshirt Priorists, were the ones responcible for the attacks. However, he then went on to change such statements, by saying that a man by the name of Donald Dabber was\n===================\n===================the one who ran into the city carrying the decapitated head of the princess, and shouting at the Haenseti guards to follow him if they so wished for it back. When asked further about this man all that was said \n===================\n===================was that he is supposedly a Horen. Moving on from that point, i went on to question the whereabouts of the King and his current condition. The Queen and several of her guards all gave word that he was safe and ===================\n===================secure. Expressing min and the councils happiness to hear such, i then went on to find out how the Queen and her people planned to respond the abhorent act. While little was said by her majesty, she expressed that the \n=================\n===================situation was being looked over and handled now by the Imperial courts. Having nothing more to look into, i once again expressed our County's deepest sorrows and well wishes to her her and the Haenseti people during their time\n===================of mourning. In return i was offered words in which were, i think not meant in malice, but in caution and perhaps even warning. They were that we, and specificlly I, needed to inform the Count that we need keep closer\n\n=================\n===================eye on our walls and boundaries. The Queen seemed adamant that I heed those words and make sure the Count recieved them. From that point I took my leave of the Kempost, ushered out by the Queen and her guard, and took\n==================\n===================off for my return trip to Cyrilsburg. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n==================\n===================\n\n\n          Madame\n   Grand Ambassador\n     Klaudia Vulnear\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n==================", ""),
        StaticBook("Haenseti Kingdom", "Elizaveta vas Ruthern", "-=The Structure of          The Haensetian\n         State =-\n\n\n   Inked by Elizavets        vas Ruthern, upon\n    the 14th of The\n    Grand Harvest \n          1676\nFormation\n\nThe victory of the Carnation League, lead to the unification of all Northern people under one banner. \n\nLord Peter Barbanov shortly rose as Duke of Carnatia shortly after the victory of the Riga War.\nThe Duke commenced many reformations, eventually forming the Duchy of Haense. \n\nAfter the Hetmanate's defeat in the Krajian Rebellion, Raevir member whom fleed the war, sought refuge behind the Duchie's walls.\nDuke Peter Barbanov, offered the men and women comfortable abodes and plenty food to fill their stomachs. \n\nDue to the mass population of the Duchy, Lord Peter Barbanov requested the royal title from Emperor John III.\nDespite the political pressures from his southern, nobility - Emperor John III granted Duke Peter Barbanov title of King. Of Both Haenseti and Ruska.\nThe Regency Council\n\nThe council was established in 1668 after the death of Franz Barbanov. It's formation was brought forth due to the late King's son, being too young of age to rule. \n\nThe council was overseen and lead by Lord Chancellor\nMatthew Colborn.\n\nThe council head and its members, prevailed through the distress of losing their king to the Renatian forces. Thus saw the kingdom, to prosperity until the crowned prince was of age. \n\nIt was later disbanded\nin 1669, upon the coronation of the crowned prince - Sigmar I.\nThe Aulic Council\n\nThe Aulic Council is a form of privy council that is personally assembled by the ruling monarch of the Kingdom of Haense and active during the reign of a sovereign.\n\nUnlike the more modern councils of the south that are seen today.\nThe Kingdom of Haense retains its traditional privy council that is tailored by the ruling sovereign.\n\n While the overall positions of the council can change overtime, the typical privy council consists of the Lord Chancellor,\n, head minister of both the kingdom and the council itself, the Lord Treasurer, minister of the treasury and wealth of the kingdom, the Lord Constable, the chief lawyer and judge, and the Lord Steward or Chamberlain, head of the household.\nThe Privy Council acts as the monarch's first advisers on matters of both the internal and external affairs, and it was normal to see the monarch consult the council before declaring a course of action.\nThe Small Council\n\nEstablished in 1669, the Small Council is an assembly comprising both elected and royally-selected officials that is primarily responsible for the municipal government of the city of Markev.\nThough not the Aulic council, the small council are a lesser council. But by no means less important, those electic or royally selected are entrusted with the responsibilities more closely knitted to the citizens of Markev.\nHaenseti Military\n\nThe military structure of Haense was originally structured around to fit the - style of the Holy Orenian Empire. \n\nHowever, following the deep cold uprising and the weak state that it left the Empire in.\nThe Kingdom Of Haense abandoned the structure of the imperial army and fell back to its more traditional structure of a levy. \n\n After the reformation of the Kingdom following the Greyspine Rebellion, it was again decided that\na centralized Royal Army would allow for greater organization and distribution of resources. The current Royal Army consists of a centralized force, made up by the various companies and levies of the many fiefs of the realm.\nThe army is headed by the King, with an appointed Great Crown Hetman maintaining full-time command of the Army.\nSuccession\n\nThe Kingdom of Haense follows a strict primogeniture succession, similar to that of the Holy Orenian Empire, in that only males and sons of females may inherit. The son of the current King would be next in line to the throne.\nShould the firstborn bear no sons, then the secondborn's sons shall inherit. If there are no males left in the dynasty, then the sons of females would inherit. However, females may not inherit the crown.\nThe succession of the Royal Throne is constricted to the House of Barbanov from the figure King Peter I, whom derives his line from Emperor Alexander I, son of Emperor Tobias I, and therefore the direct line of the Prophet Sigismund.", ""),
        StaticBook("Halfling Poetry", "Hobbs Burrows", "The Halfling Book of Poetry\n\nAn Anthology by Hobbs Burrows\nIt is said that a Brandybuck lad\nIs never found sulking or sad\nFor the summers of the Vale\nare hot and full of ale\nSo the lasses go scantily clad!\n\nBy Petyr Brandybuck\nThe fields of the Vale are of gold\nAnd the folk are equally bold\nBut kiss a she-Hobbit\nAnd if she don't stop it\nYou can't say you weren't warned and/or told!\n\nBy Qaton Dribbledew\nThe tall ones are a rather odd type\nPicking wheat before it is ripe\nAnd they love to fight wars\nAnd loot all the stores\nAnd they're always looking to gripe!\n\nBy Petyr Brandybuck\nThere once was a halfling so small,\nHe seemed to be nothing at all\n'There's more than you guess,\nAbout this one I 'fess'\nSaid the wizard, 'I'll here make my call'\n\nBy Faldo Featherfoot\nBig orcs in dark woods are scary\nBut not if your feet are quite hairy\nJust lob a few stones\nTo break a few bones\nThose big orcs better be wary\n\nBy Tibb Fairfield\nThere once was a Halfling named Frerry\nWho lived in the Vale near the ferry\nHe danced with Pippin\nAt the Drunken Sheep Inn\nOn the table yet never got weary\n\nBy Faldo Featherfoot\nFifteen birds on five fir trees\nTheir feathers were fanned in a fiery breeze\nBut funny little birds they had no wings!\nO what shall we do with the funny little things?\nRoast them alive or stew them in a pot\nFry them boil them and eat them hot?\nBy Len\nA Dunwood halfling friend of mine\nWhen asked how much he did dine\nReplied 'both me breakfasts,\nElevenses, lunch,\nTea, dinner, supper, and wine!\n\nBy Petyr Brandybuck\nOld Seth did go to the bar\nAnd met a fine lass from Sanhar\nAnd now when I visit\nHis small halfling home\nThere be too many half-orcs thar!\n\nBy Petyr Brandybuck\nAn elf lass whose clothing was strewed\nBy winds that left her quite nude\nSaw old Kip come along\nAnd unless I am wrong\nYou expected this line to be lewd!\n\nBy Petyr Brandybuck\nWhen the Wandering Wizard for sure\nEntered me bar saying 'Sir,\nI require all the ales\nThat ye have for sale\nThe rest o' this rhyme is censored\n\nBy Petyr Brandybuck\nHarvesting crops ain't no fun\nNor is planting seeds none, yet\nI love me hot bread\nAnd ale in me head\nSo I'll work all day in the sun\n\nBy Petyr Brandybuck\nYer the prettiest lass that I've met\nNo prettier lass I could get\nWow, I must be drinkin'\nIf this is what I'm thinkin'\nFor this beautiful lass is me pet!\n\nBy Petyr Brandybuck\nThese rhymes pack laughs astronomical\nIn a space that is quite economical!\nBut the good ones I've seen\nSo seldom are clean\nAnd the clean ones are so seldom comical!\n\nBy Petyr Brandybuck", ""),
        StaticBook("Halfling Sayings", "Hobbs Burrows", "The Book of Halfling Proverbs\n\nAuthors unknown\n'Hill' is a hasty word for a thing that has stood since the world was shaped.\n\nAs the garden grows, so does the gardener. \n\nIf you have a garden and a library, you have everything you need.\n\nCultivation to the mind is as necessary as\nfood to the body.\n\nGardens are not made by sitting in the shade.\n\nIf you tickle the earth with a hoe, she laughs with a harvest.\n\nWalking from your front door is a dangerous business.\nIf more of us valued food and cheer and song above hoarded gold, the world would be a merrier place.\n\nShare pipes, as good friends must at a pinch.\n\nAdventures make you late for dinner.\nA burrow means comfort.\n\nMinas cannot buy you happiness.\n\nHome is where you hang your shovel. \n\nSpeak softly, and carry a big shovel.", ""),
        StaticBook("Halsworthy", "Arthur Goodwinn", "THE CONSTITUTION\n          -of-\n      HALSWORHTY\n\n            &\n \n      THE LAWS OF\n        THE CITY\n\n\n\n\n         MDCLIII\n(Type the url into your browser to view the Google Document)\n\nhttps://tinyurl.com/Halsworthy", ""),
        StaticBook("Hanging Tree", "Ayda Morra", "The Hanging Tree,\nMen with honour fight till the end, never giving up, not even in death. The rope around their necks are just small obstacles in what they stood for. They had wished to be left where they were to show that they never gave up.\nBut, their final wish was for naught when a man of tall stachure slashed their bodies to the floor and burnt them and the tree that once stood tall. \n\nMay those honourable spirits curse his name for the disrespectful actions, burning what they stood for.", ""),
        StaticBook("hanky panky", "Bjark Warghearth", "Visit me in Fi'Ceru at the back of the town.\n\n§sso we can do hanky panky", ""),
        StaticBook("Harbingers", "Veldryn Uuthlini", "These elusive creatures were quite certainly some of the most dangerous things in Anthos, a part of the Black Scourge, the beings were of a kind to glass cannons in combat, able to rend dark rifts into mortal ground to draw out the overly corrupted,\nand zealotus servants of Setherien. Along with this, these beings had been bestowed with the ability to disguise their semi-flud forms with a special form of light illusion, and unforgettably, Setherien's Boon; -\nholding within it the ability to create freezing corruptive smog from the very air about them, and condense it into frigid black flames, most would agree that these are much more dangerous than your everyday mage.\nThey were beings seeming to be made of Black smoke, only able to interract with the mortal world through their armor and robes. The standard ways of defeating a creature did not appear to work on them,\nthought holy magic seems to affect them, attacking them with normal weapons at most seemed to send them back to the North in their smoke way.\nThe title of 'Harbinger' was also a senior rank in the Destruction Cult of the Undead. Whether there is a link between the servants of Setherien and the servants of Iblees remains to be seen.\nWith Setherien defeated all the Harbingers seem to have disapeared. If they are trully gone,or are simply hiding with their master defeated is still to be seen. Some of the former known Harbingers are stated at the next pages.\nThe leader of the Harbingers, only under rule of Setherien himself. His armor was of a firery orange.\n-Vak'Thuul\nKnown Harbingers of the first age, they carried blue armor.\n\n-Nihil\n-Shae'Tan\n-Dumamis\n-Daink\n-Mortum'Vherzix\n-Khrell’os\n-Kav'Zoras\n-Orithur\nFallen mortals to the will of Setherien, they were chosen to be granted the power of their master. They carried red armor.\n-Orakana\n-Eudihr\n-Absolution\n-Xort\n-Oblitus\n-Skelvyas\n-Kaernk", ""),
        StaticBook("HarbTale Vol.II", "Orithur", "A Harbinger's Tale\n\nVolume II\n-------------------\n\nWe went under many names. Harbingers, Dark Leuitenants, Hiishtgul, but no matter what we were called, our reputation for hideous destruction,\nmutilation and fear\nwas known universally. Our first major target was the Druidic Grove of Anthos, were the Nine Harbingers gathered with the corrupted footsoldiers to slay the peaceful tree-folk. Needless to say, it was a slaughter. And we loved every moment\nof it. The acts of evil we performed were bliss to us.\n\nWe resided in Setherien's distant corrupted lands where I, the keeper of his knowledge and his library, constructed a mighty spire where it might be stored. Despite my corruption\nit seems my love for books remained untouched. It was here that I endlessly studied the races, and even the Order of the Golden Lance. Those seeds of doubt within my ashen mind grew small sprouts upon discovering so much about the world we sought to\nvanquish. Nothing made sense to me, and I at first voiced my concerns to my brothers. They spoke of treachery and it was then I saw that I was the only one, the only one to not be entirely mindless to the whim of Setherien.\n\nMany moons passed,\nand many more acts of slaughter proceeded. Continually villages and cities fell, more and more innocent victims of the Drakaar would fall, their bodies rising as twisted, distorted versions of their previous selves.\n\nI initially watched with a sense\nglee, but this glee faded as those seeds of doubt stretched into long vines, and the realisation of what was occuring continued to gradually dawn upon me.\n\nI decided action needed to be done, and I summoned my library spire to the\nfallen elven capital where I had told Setherien I'd be expanding the library's knowledge. Although a Drakaar, Setherien's lust for knowledge as all dragons do lust for was also untouched, and he willingly accepted my quest. In truth, I had wanted\nto contact the elves in a nearby settlement, as often adventurers would venture to my corrupted spire, where I would speak and discuss things endlessly with them. Needless to say I was threatened and often attacked, but despite this, I continued to learn.\nAs my painful release from Setherien's corrupted began to reach its close, I was attacked. The elves only saw that I was a Harbinger, the creature that had destroyed their home and loved ones, so I do not blame them for felling my spire.\nSetherien however, did begin to see what was becomming of me. I sensed his eyes watching me always, his distrust of me would be my undoing and I knew this. So I escaped. I latched my lifeforce to one of his Bloodshards and fled from Anthos. Alone.", ""),
        StaticBook("HarbTale Vol.III", "Orithur", "A Harbinger's Tale\n\nVolume III\n-------------------\n\nWith the eventual defeat of Setherien through the relic that was the Golden Lance, the remaining uncorrupted brothers and sisters of my old Order grouped with\nthe races to cease the evil once and for all. The Drakaar fell, and as did most of the Harbingers. To my understanding, in the final days of Setherien several Harbingers also latched themselves onto a Bloodshard and followed the races to Athera much like\nmyself, his unruly hold upon us gone.\n\nThe true sadness lies in the fallen Harbingers that never managed to escape his hold, they died proudly by his side. But then again, those that escaped are forced to remember... And we remember everything.\nWithin Athera, we disperssed and went into hiding. Although no longer a threat and no longer under the influence of Setherien, the races did not forget what we did to them. We are shunned wherever we go, and for good reason. It is safe to say I would\ndo the same. It was unlikely that we would ever be forgiven, even if we were not to blame.\n\nA few Harbingers killed themselves, unable to cope with what they had done and how the world treated them, I however, sought to repay the world, and\ngathered several of my remaining brothers. Together we pledged to give back to the world, and thus we ventured to what remained of the Order of the Golden Lance. However, we were mostly shunned upon arrival. To see our own brothers and sisters shun us,\nthis affected us greatly. And what was more, the threat of Iblees and the Undead had reared its ugly head, and the Order was consumed with hatred. In exchange for rejoining, they asked us to bring them the heads of the Undead.\nFor this reason, we did not accept their offer. We were dissapointed with what was once our life. The Order I knew would not trial by blood, the Order I knew were family. This was my family no longer.\n\nWe seperated once more, which is when I\nwas discovered by a\nhooded stranger named 'Aedrex'. The man took me in and told me of his quest to serve Dragur, collecting and storing knowledge. This being my one interest, enticed me. I accepted his offer to join him, and to this day live in hiding\nhis librarian. Everyday I see new people turn towards me not as an enemy, but as a friend. I can only hope to rebuild the person I once was in their eyes.\n\n-Orithur of the Nine", ""),
        StaticBook("Harlan", "Veldryn", "My lovable Harlan.\n\nEven when we are far away from each other or when time itself stops us from seeing each other..\n\nI will always be with you, I will always choose you, because I love you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Harvesters", "Falyen Darylus", "Analysis of the Harvester Construct\nThe constructs used in the attack on Rivel appear to be based off of the golem servants favoured by the Forgotten Dwarves and now being rediscovered by the Aegean dwarves.\nHowever, they are clearly different: they possess a killer instinct unheard of in servant golems, lack individual intelligence and possess an apparatus built into the hand capable of killing a mortal being and trapping their soul, no doubt for\ncontainment in the Soul Capacitors of The Seal. Countless Harvester Constructs were destroyed in their assault on Rivel, indicating a lack of quality in their construction: it seems the dwarves built them in a time of desperation.\nHowever, such a time now befalls us: the majority of Rivel’s Lesser Caste were killed by Harvester Constructs in the assault, and I fear this propaganda we are distributing to the Lesser Caste attributing this assault to deceptive attacks by the\nForgotten Dwarves will not placate them. We may downplay their intelligence, but even they must realise the Forgotten Dwarves have been extinct for over a millenium.\n- Senior Researcher Falyen Darylus", ""),
        StaticBook("Hasteful Notes", "Karvos'sol Drakon", "As I scribble down these notes, the beast I speak of here stands before the Ivae'Fenn within the Grand Hall of the Citadel palace. It stands around ten feet tall, a beast of four hooved legs and two arms from the front of its torso. From what the Odd-\nWanderer speaks of, the beast only exists to consume souls. It is a creature of the forest, dropping seeds and trees of birch growing instantly from the point of contact. It shoves its hands down to the stomachs of those it claims, and begins to turn-\nthem into trees. They are in agony. Their souls are taken when they are fully absorbed into the tree planted. They themselves are only covered in a layer of bark before hand, before being attached to the planted tree. The Odd Wandered claims that the-\nSeptember Prince is what it claims to have caused the disruption up north, which awoken the beast. He claims the beast wants to save our souls from the Prince.. \n*A roughly sketched picture of the beast covered the entirety of the next page.*\nPicture:\nhttps://66.media.tumblr.com/f32aceea941acb7bbf48dbf80271192b/tumblr_p4c4i53fEc1qfu9ibo1_500.gif\nIt warns us of our isolation, and insists we must make allies to avoid the fate foretold. -------------------\nIt turns out, it was all an illusion after all, as I had initially suspected. Either way, this is a warning that must not be ignored.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hawks Need You", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Attempt to recruit one person into the warhawkes and bring them to Rei or Ray for a trial.", ""),
        StaticBook("HE Report", "Aeluin Tundrak", "The High Elven Report\n\nCity of Okarn'thilln, Nation of the Mali'Aheral. \n\nThe City of Okarn'thilln is a island, the entrance being a magical bridge that goes directly into the city's Square. Walls of the city protect it from outside dangers, however caves\ncan be seen under Okarn'thilln, using siege ladders in a siege and climbing into these caves may lead to another entry point it is unknown to me as the caves aren't exposed in the insides much. In the square there is two streets, a gate in the middle of\nthe bridge on the east side. The North side being a bar. The South side being a economey center.\n\nIt seems the Mali'Aheral have no direct leader, they are lead by the Silver Council. Silver Council are abandoning the city from the threat\nof the September Prince.  All citizens are evacuating except a few. The citizens are Evacuating to Nordengrad.", ""),
        StaticBook("Healer Creed", "Vailoen", "Creed of the Healer\n\n'Through the salvation of others, we save ourselves. Deliver the salve and bring comfort to those in pain.'\nI. It is the will of xan that those bequeathed with the wherewithal to offer remedy unto others do so without discrimination, but pay heed to the protests of the less fortunate. Hold dear the sympathy and knowledge for and of the lesions of adversity; -\nfor those who would fathom them might soothe them more completely. In compassion one must understand the perturbation of the wounded and junction permitting seek out auxiliary alternatives; know well the con temporary ministrations of care-\nas you are an agent of mercy. The facility of unwavering conviction is required by those who would seek to ease the suffering of their brother, offer no wanton discomfort unto the innocent who seeks your aid; regardless of offense unto you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Healing Guide", "Alder", "~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n       Basic Healing\n\n\n~=~ A guilde to herbal & mundane healing ~=~\n\nWritten by: Monk Alder\n\n\n\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\nHello there,\n\nMy name is Alder. I have written this guide to teach those who are not familiar with healing at all, & those who have basic knowledge of the practice. I will include sections for a few healing topics that apply to a catholic standard.\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nCuts & Scrapes: \n\nTo begin make sure that all items are devoid of contaminants such as dirt, mud, dust, and any other biotic or abiotic material that is not apart of the item. \n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nWhat you will need:\n\n* Alcohol\n* Blissfoil\n* Tippens Root\n* Mandragora\n* Cloth\n* Gloves\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nWhere to find / Properties: \n\nAlcohol: Found in any bar or tavern. Antiseptic.\n\nBlissfoil: Found in grass lands. numbing agent. (Use gloves when harvesting. If to much is applied expect permanent numbness.)\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nTippens Root: Found in dense forests. Wrinkled with dark yellow spots. Stops bleeding at an extreemly fast rate.\n\nMandragora: Found in swamps & wetlands. Can be ground up to produce a skin healing goo. (Warning wear a mask\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~ \n\nwhen harvesting this plant. Toxic spores.)\n\nCloth: Found in local shops. used to cover wounds.\n\nGloves: Found in local shops. Protect hands.\n\n\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nProcedure: \n\n1) Take a cloth and soak it in alcohol. then clean off the wound.\n\n2) Get a bowl and crush up your Blissfoil applying a small amount to the wound.\n\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n3) Do the same with the Tippens Root, & then Mandragora.\n\n4) Apply a piece of cloth over the wound, the injury should now heal with haste. \n\n\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nBurns\n\nWhat you will need:\n\n* Water\n* Athin \n* Cloth\n\nNote: Athin is a blue algae found in cold bodys of water. used to heal burns.\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nProcedure:\n\n1) Soak your cloth in cold water and lightly rub the burn cleaning it off.\n\n2) Apply Mandragora to the wound to begin the healing of tissue.\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n \n3) Crush up the Athin in a bowl and apply a paste of your choice to form a lotion. \n\n4) Apply it to the wound, expect fast results and a soothing cooling sensation.\n\n5) Apply cloth over the wound.\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nFor any other injury that may be life threatening seek a Monk at the Cloud Temple.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~", ""),
        StaticBook("Healing Potions", "ilikefooddude", "Healing Potion\nA Basic Alchemy Guide\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Ingredients Needed:\n\nThree Bottles of clean water\nOne reed of the Serpent's Stalk plant\nOne large sample of Tippin's Root\nMethod\n\n1. Finely chop the Serpent's Stalk and add into the three bottles of water; stirring and infusing until the liquid turns a sickly green colour.\n\n2. Crush the Tippin's Root in a Mortar and Pestle and add to the\nLiquid, which should turn a brown or greyish colour when mixed.\n\n3. Commence to boil the potion in a brewing stand for about an hour, or until it takes on something like a rocky texture.\n\n4. Filter out the\nChunks of Serpent's Stalk and Tippin's Root with a clean cloth, and transfer the potion (Which now should be brighter and clearer than before, with shifting textures of crumbling grey) to another bottle.\nForenote\nDo not drink this potion. Apply directly to wounds with a cloth and bandage quickly. Injuries such as cuts and bruises will heal in a matter of hours, though broken bones will still take a week or two to heal. Consumption will cause nausia,\nChoking, and, sometimes death.", ""),
        StaticBook("Healthy Handbook", "Olivier Galba", "Healthy Handbook\n\nYour friendly and comprehensive guide for elementary first aid, written by the travelling physician Olivier Galba. Might save a life, or at least faff one up a few notches less.\nTable of Contents:\n\nChapter 1: Don't be silly, wrap up Billy!\nChapter 2: To drink or not to drink...\nChapter 3: Herbs useful beyond smoking!\nChapter 4: Suturing and you!\nChapter 5: Sticks and stones may break my bones...\nChapter 1: \n\nUh oh! Clumsy ol' Billy just tripped over a rake! Looks like he got out with only a minor cut, but it's going to bleed him dry! What do you do?\n\nThis is where bandages save the day.\nBandaging a wound is the most common form of first aid, and despite its simplicity is also the most important. You might die in days from a bad infection, but you'll die in hours from a profusely bleeding wound left untreated.\nBe sure to wrap any open abrasions with a fresh linen, preferably applying a topical ointment or salve. If unavailable, alcohol (such as vodka or moonshine) is also effective.\nChapter 2:\n\nAs tempting as it might be to down that bottle of moonshine, one might instead consider its effectiveness as a disinfectant. In my travels, I find strong alcohols like vodka and moonshine far superior to cleaning wounds than boiled water.\nIf a wound is bandaged but not cleaned up, you run the risk of a festering wound within a days time. Festering wounds are much harder to treat, and can prove far more fatal, so avoid them at all costs by setting aside that shot you saved for later!\nChapter 3: \n\nThough cactus green might seem to cure all of lifes ailments, there are many herbs throughout the realms which can be used outside the hookah lounge for medicinal purposes. Here we will cover the most elementary.\nAcross almost every respectable clinic and infirmary, you'll find a pretty blue flower known as blissfoil. This flower is the cornerstone of modern medicine, used as a strong anesthetic and pain reliever. Careless doses, however, can cause paralysis.\nTippen's root is another contender for the most popular healing herb. Though foul smelling, this pretty flower possesses strong healing properties, capable of stopping even a profusely bleeding wound in seconds. Always keep one handy!\nAnother common herb is frostvine, found in cold climates. It can be considered a safer alternative to blissfoil, being cold to the touch and therefore great for numbing pain, with the uncanny ability to loosen stiff muscles. Never hurts to carry around.\nChapter 4:\n\nThough tippen's root and bandages are great at plugging wounds, these resources may not always be on hand, or in large enough quantities to clot a deep gash. This is when suturing is important.\nSuturing is the delicate art of closing a wound via thread and needle, preferably after disinfecting the wound. It is reserved for deep gashes that won't otherwise stop bleeding, or heal. This is best learned through practice, not reading a fancy book.\nChapter 5:\n\nBroken bones are another tricky concept better left to its own book or apprenticeship, but a few general rules exist: if possible, 'pop' the bone back into place, splinting it with something stiff and strong.\nEnsure the patient sees a proper professional, or is at least treated with a strong elixir. Broken bones, especially compound fractures, can cause permanent disability. In these cases, amputation is often wise to avoid the limb from becoming gangrenous.\nNow go forth, and try valiantly not to rip your next bandage, down that last shot of precious vodka, smoke the clinic's frostvine, bend your suturing needle, or let that broken limb set at an awkward angle! Just don't blame me if you screw up.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hearth Mother", "Cyler Cottonwood", "Anbella, Hearth Mother\n=======================Anbella is the wife of Yemekar. Just as dwarven souls are forged on Yemekar's Ruhn-Anvil, they are ever warmed and nurtured by the loving embrace of the Hearth Mother.Tend to hearth, home,and land, drawing\nstrength and safety from truth, tradition and the rule of law. Join with friends, kin and clan in common purpose. Do not succumb to the misery of greed or the evils of strife, but always bring hope. health and cheer to those in need.\nOnce an oath is made, Anbella watches over its keeping - to break it is to wound her sorely. Children must be cherished and guarded well from harm, for they are the future of all dwarvenkind.", ""),
        StaticBook("Heaven's Womb", "Almisael", "From what i have gathered, the vaeyls were appointed to the protection of Atlas by Horen himself over 1000 years ago. \n\nI snuck inside their fortress and i saw a giant dragon skull frozen into the wall against their throne.\nThis is the dragon that they killed when they fought the Aengul all those hundreds of years ago. The Nature of the Vaeyls is confusing, they are spooks yet most of them look perfectly human\nThey were told to protect the descendents yet they are hostile towards us, if that does not mean us, then who?\n\nThe Prophecy that SHE bestowed upon us describes ice shattered and a figure standing above it whilst deathless men besoothe beneath.\nAtlas has a very rich history, more than any other continents, the things that happen are shocking. A few months ago, a black rock fell from the heavens and crashed into the northern shores of the continent. This is the first time i have seen this happen.\nWhen the earth's blood rushed towards the heaven's womb. It creates a bad omen. Needless to say that i have not yet seen this happen.\n\nSHE has perished right after bestowing the prophecy upon the wonks. Or so they say...\nThe truth is that no one in that cave has conserved any evidence of her existence. So for all we know this chief of theirs could be lying.\n\nMaybe he is testing us. I for one do not want this to end.\nThe prophet spoke: Grant me the mercy of the land, grand me the joy of the heavens, release us from our yoke of iron, thus shall our souls be saved. Forever and ever, forever and ever.\nSouls are trapped in their yokes. Mother, Mother, Mother\nMother\nMarie", ""),
        StaticBook("Heil Vandaloria", "Davin Lodmund", "===Heil Vandaloria===\nHistory of the\nValued Champion of\nThe Hallowvale\nAdil, the Eagle-Eyed\nApproved by the\nMinistry of Truth\nBorn in the hold of Al Dirahk, Adil was fathered by Amir Athir al-Hashim, the Amir of the Mubarizun. Adil had with him three brothers and a valued sister, Aisha, though he himself was destined to be the next Amir. Being so, he and Aisha were\nsent away.They were sent to a mosque called Elspeth to train, Aisha in the arts of diplomacy, Adil in the arts of the duties of an Amir. For years they trained in their arts but, alas, when the time came for them to be called upon, they were abandoned.\nTheir father never showed up to greet them. Distraught, they left Elspeth to go adventuring... Roughly the same time large worms engulfed the continent. Assuming their family and friends were now gone, they stormed onward- together.\nFor ten years Adil and his sister wandered the lands, Adil playing his Oud with deft hands... And crashing bottles into the faces of ruffians alike. However as fate would have it, his wanderings rewarded him. He stumbled upon Al Wakrah, the\n... And his family. And though tearful reunions were in order, they found another member of their party with them;\nTheir father.\nAs the Ducal War had just begun, Adil and Aisha were both drafted.\nThe war changed Adil and his sister. The details of his battles are not important, all that is is that Adil was a man. When he and Aisha returned to Al Wakrah, they came to a breaking surprise;\nTheir father had committed suicide.\nThis event caused the two to break apart. Aishra persued knighthood in the Order of St. Lucien. Adil... Turned to becoming a slaver, and his soul began to rot. The years of slaving turned to years of drugs... Years of sin and whoring.\nIt was one fateful botched slave trade that landed Adil in prison. As he rotted away behind iron bars, a revelation came to him; he was a monster of pure sin. And so, upon his release, he went to find peace and forgiveness... In the Order of St.Lucien\nWhile forgiveness may of been found, peace was not. In the order, Adil found him self constantly tormented by St. Lucien's leader at the time, Grand Master Baudric. Extreme training and constant beatings rendered Adil near whittled.\nThis was, of course, until the entire restructure of The Order. In one knight, St. Lucien had become Hallowvale Contracting, all thanks to Nafis Yar (whom Adil now calls his battle-brother). Peace and brotherhood, Adil found.\nBut his journy was far from over. In order for ome to be truly accepted into the Hallowvale they must overcome two challenges; kill a vile creature and beat Oberdiktator- or our glorious Kaiser- in a brawl.\nThe first task came when Adil was celebrating with his brothers after a battle won over a group of snowelves. During the celebration the encampment was attacked by a wendigo! The brothers took their place, Adil armed\nwith an arbalest on a balcony.\nThe beast clawed it's way through the camp and made it inside. As it dangled from a shandelier, Adil fired a well-and-true shot into the creature's eye. This epic shot is what deemed him;\nAdil, the eagle-eyed.\nHowever, the arrow only made to anger the creature. It lashed out at Adil, mauling him well and- ironically and much to Adil's amusement- taking his eye as well. Though wounded, Adil's brothers revered him a hero. He was promoted to Vandar Council.\nCheif and budding advisor to Nafis Yar (whom was the Vandalore at the time), he continued his work as a mercenary for some time after his slaying of the beast. This was, of course, until the Orenian and Dwarven war began. Hallowvale had to choose a\nIn the end, Oren's coffers proved too tempting. Hallowvale was paid to fight orcs, snow elves, and dwarves alike. As Adil himself words it;\n\"I wasn't bias, I just liked money in all honesty.\"\nNo truer words, Adil.\nThe Hallowvale prospered well in this war. So well in fact, that Adil was invited on a secret mission launched toward the Caliphate. Led by our glorious Kaiser, the Hallowvale proposed to Faiz Charadeen... A union between the Caliphate and the\nHallowvale.The union was accepted of course, so birthing the Second Reich, successor of Aesterwald. Adil himself stood right behind the glorious Kaiser as the union was officially passed. In fact, the Glorious Kaiser became very-close\n... But let's save that for later in this story.\nShortly after this unification, Vandalore Nafis Yar retired, Frederick II, our glorious Kaiser, taking his place. And so a new Champion was required...\nAdil was chosen.\n\"He was my Champion, the man all Vanders of Hallowvale looked up to and had to beat in a slobber knocker fist fight wrestling match to be oathed,\" Adil had to say of the glorious Kaiser. He was awestruck in his choosing to become the new Champion.\nAnd so, comfortable in his new position behind the walls of Al Wakrah, Adil was of course admitted into the town's new Caliphate/Hallowvale garrison... Where he met his lovely court, Rajiya. Adil had little to say, just that he hopes to marry soon.\nAdil, Champion of Vandaloria, shall truly be remembered as a proper hero and Champion by all.\nThe Kaiser himself ahd this to say of the man;\n\"Adil is headstrong, but valiant. Simple words for a simple man, I knew him before his eye incident. He's the best archer I know and a Master of Filth.\nAdil and I were battle brothers before politicans and I don't think I can be very poetic with my words, but he's a good soldier and an even better man.\"\nHeil Kaiser!\nPraise be to Adil.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hello", "Lirro Dockingrock", "Hello", ""),
        StaticBook("Helmet Permit", "Fëanor Sylvaeri", "The individual John Kowacz is as of this document granted permission to bear a helmet within the walls of Caras Eldar.\n\nSigned,\nＦｅａｎｏｒ Ｓｙｌｖａｅｒｉ\nSigned On,\n１２ｔｈ ｏｆ Ｍａｌｉｎ＇ｓ Ｗｅｌｃｏｍｅ， １６８６", ""),
        StaticBook("Helpful Hand", "Daveed Batler", "Daveed Batler Assistive Journal\nPerson One: Gray Kellian \n\nHelped by giving him my personal book.\nPerson 2 : Dymase \nGave him a bag of sugar to make cookies for his grandmother\nPerson 3:\nMoohissa Gave him a bag of sugar to bake a cake for a friend\nPerson 4: Duke\nSwept,Waxed,andMopped the boat...tiring\nPerson 5 : Guards\nHelped guard with the removale of an intruder.", ""),
        StaticBook("Helping PeopleV1", "Gray Kellian III", "My first person I helped was a girl named Elise. She was blind and looking to return her sight. So I brought her to Lily and Andriel to give her the gift of a lifetime\n(ZoruaSama)\nThe second person I helped was Alem to give a law test to Thain, which she passed yay!\n\n(seventhCircle)\nThe Third person I helped was a strange man on a horse who was looking to buy carrots. so I gatherd my hoes and went to the farm with him to get him carrots,\n\nHe then tried to recruit me for Oren army.\n(no clue, Dexxsomething)\nThe forth was when I was walking to Oren. there was a lad looking for food, and I gave him the rest of mine to help him. He thanked me and blessed me before eating his meal happily\n(Mcthornz)\nThe last was a man looking to reunite with old friends, I knew whom he was looking for and allowed him to use my parrot Blue to reconnect with his old friends\n(tidemanno)", ""),
        StaticBook("Her Moonlit Eyes", "Kili Al-Deen", "In moon Lit Gaze I saw Her Eyes,in which made my heart fill with crys, if i would fall for you it would be my demise!\nbut can I live my life with out your eyes?\nin the nights i Lie adrift in thoughts of your silky hair,and in the days i have the\nstrangth to kill a bear! and when I see you my heart races like a hare. Yet I wish you can see me amongst the croud,I shall say hi,I shall not now,days go by i see her smile, if i say hi its like a mile! oh such agony if a day goes by it will feel like\napart of me will die.\nAlas Alas it canot be more i will do it tonight!\nwhere i saw her and her eyes i will walk that mile and spare the bear for this night! the moon lit glaze fills her eyes by the tree she stands on that night i make my walk up\nslowly feeling more and more alive,what will i say what will i do for years now and i have not thought it thruo. i stand with her face to face struck by her dazziling eyes and beautiful silky hair until she made a warm smile like none ive ever seen on her\nface,and to my amaze,\nher cheeks looked ablazed.she came closer,i didnt know what do to.then i told her\"I Love You.\"with a second of silence she smiles and turns around.I walk back home in the moon light with my head down until i hear a sound\nso I turn around as i hear a gentil voice say \"I Love you too.\"\n\n\n        By:Kili Al-Deen\n       (ibraheemc2000)\n-------------------\nI made this because I was bord,i hope you injoy it and one day say it to your love i also planed this\nto be a poem but toward the end of it i couldnt find ways i could make it rhyme Hehe.\n___________________", ""),
        StaticBook("Her Story Vol. 1", "Nemir", "Chronicles of\n           Nemir\n-------------------\n\n        The Orcish\n          Deserts\nWay back in my youth, I had spent a year of my life living within the golden deserts of the orcs.  I was around the age of fifteen and had just fled from the high walls of the Silver City of Haelun'or.  I didn't agree with their ways of purity and was\nstill sepparated from my Father at the time, so had no connection with anyone from the city.\n\nI had met an impure high elf named Kelian Dawnstrider who offered me to go to the deserts and became his apprentice in smithing after I\nhad told him of my troubles with the Silver City.\n\nIt may seemed foolish of me accept his offer so quickly, but I felt as if I had no where else to go and no way to support myself.  I was lucky that his words were true, and my new home became\na shabby wooden shack in the back of the Raguk's camp on the edge of the Orcish Desert.  There is where my journey began.\nThe work was harder than how I anticipated it to be, and the scorching sun was of no help with the heat of the forge.  All of the orcs seemed to respect Kelian, he was apparently a friend of the clan's leader.  I wish I could remember his name, but time\nhas blurred it from my memory.\n\nNot all of the orcs seemed pleased with my arrival to the clan, but most of them were welcoming.  It had taken me a few months to get used to their tongue, and I eventually didn't need Kelian or one of the\nslaves to help me with translating.  My clothes had also becomed stained with sweat and dirtied with dust, my hair was a little more tangled, and I noticed how tan I was becoming due to almost constant exposure to the sun's rays.  I truly looked out of\nplace when I visited some of the major cities, or maybe I just began to look like an average peasant; however, there were the occasional few who questioned why a young high elven girl was running about in dirty and tattered clothing.\nTo be truthful, I looked more like a sun elf than a high elf, but just shorter and thinner.\n\nKelian had been teaching me how to make chainmail armor since I was too scrawny to use the hammer or other heavy equipment.  Over time, I was getting\nbetter with my work and began to feel more at home and at peace.\n\nAfter spending a few months with the Raguks, I was woken one night by Kelian saying that we needed to pack our things quickly and leave.  I was in a stupor and took a moment before\nasking what was going on.  He said that the clan leader had lost a honor klomp [klomp = fight in Blah] and thus lost his position.  His opponent turned out to be one of the orcs who disliked Kelian and I's presence in the camp and was rumored to be a\ntyrant leader by a few other orcs who were leaving with us.\n\nWe left under the cover of night, unnoticed, as we trekked out into the wastes, our footsteps being drunken by the drifting sands.  All night we walked, lugging all that we had taken from t\ncamp.  It wasn't until dawn that we came across a gargantuan rock that loomed over the sands and a cacti forest.  We had discovered our destination: The Lur Clan.\n\nThey accepted us, all of us, agreeing with our opinions of the new Raguk leader.\nKelian and I were out of work since the orcs in the Lur clan already had a smith, but we were still allowed a tent to sleep in.  We didn't plan to rest there for long and began seeking out new work.\nLuck was with us and we met a human family named the Malinovs.  They were lovely people, and over time of me knowing them, I felt as if I was a part of them.\n\nKelian and I moved out of the deserts and into dwarven lands.  A human who owned a manor\nallowed us to live in a smaller building by his home, the Malinovs included, and together we planned to  create The Blackwood Company.\n\nMy time with the orcs ended there, and I began my next beautiful journey with the dwed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Herb. Notes #1", "Emma Ludovar", "Blissfoil:\nBlissfoil can be very useful for minor injuries or ailments. It can relieve pain or itchy sensations at the slightest touch. The oil around it's stalk and petals can be used medically to relieve these sensations.\n\nTippen's Root:\nThis herb is great for stopping the bleeding of a large wound once made into a salve or balm. This root is known for having an unpleasant smell. However, the medical uses outweigh such factors.\nFlameTongue Root:\nThis root is not to be used lightly, and is only to be used if out of Tippen's Root. It gives off an intense heat that can be used to seal and stop blood flow.\nNOTE: Make sure to wear gloves when handling this root.\nSerpent's Stalk:\nThis herb is generally dangerous for consumption as a plant. However, once one crushes the upper stalk and mixes it with water, it can be used to treat burns and minor pain.\nFrost Vine:\nIt is wise to crush this herb and mix it with water. This will produce a substance, somewhat sticky, which can be used to numb areas which are giving a person pain.\nAqua Nymph:\nWARNING: Only use in extreme cases!\n\nThis plant can cause the closing of the airway if taken via the mouth. This is useful however with severe burns.\n\nTo use this plant correctly, boil the plant (gently) in some\nwater, strain the plant from the water, leaving behind an oil. Use this remaining oil on the affected skin.\n*USEFUL TOOL*\nAlchemist's Shears:\nThese special shears can be obtained from an adequate blacksmith at minimum. They're made from two gold ingots, and two sticks of freshly-cut wood.\nThese shears make the collections of herbs much easier.", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbology Notes", "Vitalius Maarsen", "-Herbology Notes-   \n\n            by\n    Vitalius Maarsen\n\n\nIn these pages you will find some notes taken   from various books\n   and learnt from\n      experience\n-Peppermint\n\nAn herb that can assist in Colds, Coughs, Inflamation, Nausea and morning Sickness that can be either drank in tea or used to produce oil.\n-Peppermint Tea\n\nBoil some water in a pot, once boiling put a teabag full of mint leaves inside the water, leaving it to rest for a few minutes, after that remove the teabag and add honey or sugar as you please.\n-Peppermint Oil\n\nAfter cleaning, chopping and drying the peppermint leaves, put them inside a jar filled with olive oil, seal it and leave it to dry outside for 1 month, once done throw the leaves out and store the oil in some vials.\n-Mint\n\nA herb that can assist with any kind of Headache, Nausea, Digestion, Coughs, Depression and Oral care that can be either drank in tea as making oil out of it is just not worth it.\n-Mint Tea\n\nAfter drying the leaves and putting them in a teabag, boil some water, once the water is boiling put the teabag inside and let it rest for a few minutes, once done add sugar or honey as you please.\n-Rosemary\n\nThis herb does have some quite useful properties, as it can help in healing wounds or bruises.\n-Rosemary Oil\n\nAfter cleaning, chopping and drying the rosemary leaves, put them inside a jar filled with olive oil, seal it and leave it to dry outside for 1 month, once done throw the leaves out and store the oil in some vials.\n-Types of Tea-\n\nChamomile: Helps with sleep.\nRose Hip: Helps with complexion, adrenaline and the imune system.\nLavander: Helps with respiratory issues, cough, asthma, and body temperature during fevers.\nHibiscus Flower: Helps with hypertension and blood pressure.\nMilk Thistle: Helps with cleaning livers and improve their function.\nDendelion: Helps with Arthristis, liver funtion, fluid retention.\nHawthorn: Helps with blood circulation and reduces stress.\nCinnamon: Enhances body strenth, fights viruses and effective with honey.\nRed Clover: Helps with stress, sleep problems, strenght and improves memory.\nNettle: Helps with high blood pressure, rheumatism, arthritis, immune system, coughs and colds.\n-Nursing Herbs-\n\n*Blood Production & Paleness:\n Wheatgrass ingested dry or in teas\n\n*Broken Bones\n Horsetail\n Confrey root\n Oat Straw\n Lobelia\n Lavander\n Chamomile\nMandragora\n-Above is ingested in teas\n Mandragora\n Comfrey root\n Bergamot Oil\n-Above is applied\n\n*Burns \n Mandragora\n Athin \n Aloe Vera\n-Above is applied\n*Colds & Common Illness\n Echinacea\n Pot Marigold\n Gumweed\n Mullein\n Chamomile\n Lavander\n Mandragora\n Orchid\n Strawberry\n Orange Peel\nShade leaf\n Blissfoil\n-Above is ingested in teas\n\n*Minor and Major Cuts\n Yarrow\n Blissfoil\n Witch's Hazel\n Comfrey\n Tippen's Root\n-Above is applied\n*Cagulations\n Blueberries\n Raspberries\n Strawberries\n Blackberries\n Blissfoil\n-Above is ingested in teas", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbs 1", "Leyun Kameki", "A Druid's Book of Herbs\nVolume 1\n\nHerbs from Solstice Druid Callax\n\nScribed with additions by Apple Druid Leyun Kameki\nLeyun's Forward\nWhen I learned to use the gifts of nature to heal, Callax gave me his list of herbs. It is time to write this information down in a form that can be widely shared. Hopefully it'll be of use to anyone who heals using herbs.\nAthin\nAn herb with a blue visage. It grows at the bottom of almost frozen lakes.\nEffects: Athin works as a cooling balm, making an excellent lotion. It also can cause blue hued skin.\nOverdose: Mild Frostbite\nAlchemical Properties:\nAthin is a strong water symbol, good for use in colder potions.\nNotes: Generally requires at least two people to harvest due to freezing conditions.\nAlabaster Leaf\nAn herb of Alabaster hue. It grows in drier areas in forests, typcally near fallen trees.\nEffects: As a mild poison, Alabaster Leaf causes dizziness and nausea.\nOverdose: Extreme fatigue.\nAlchemical Properties: Alabaster Leaf is a moderate earth symbol.\nNotes: Often used as a dye/paint. Harvest by carefully cutting the leaves.\nAqua Nymph\nA small chain of fragile blue baubbles that grow underwater. It is often mistaken for frog or toad spawn.\nEffects: Severe hallucinations when ingested as an herb. Powerful burn remedy when boiled. Causes the throat to close up when\ningested in oil form.\nOverdose: Stronger Effects\nAlchemical Properties: Aqua Nymph is a strong water symbol.\nNotes: Aqua Nymph is extremely delicate and must not be touched by hands. A correct way to harvest the herb is to take the thin layer\nof sediment that it grows in and the whole plant, scooping it into a jar so that it doesn't touch the edges and it's roots remain intact. If done any other way, it will likely ruin the plant.\n\nThe plant can be made into a powerful burn remedy by pouring\nthe whole plant into into a cauldron and small pot. When boiled, the plant's buds will release a liquid that will make a thick oil that can be easily spread over burns.\nBeard Weed\nA shaggy green moss that grows hanging from rare trees in caves. A rare herb, but grows in plentiful groups.\nEffects: With water and blissfoil, it can aid in the healing of internal organ damage and ease pain. Beard weed famously\ncauses significant hair growth. Can be poisonous if not prepared properly.\nWhen toxic, it can cause bloating, nausea, diarrhea, internal bleeding, and even death.\nOverdose: Stiffness. Possible hairgrowth across the entire body, creating a\nbeast-like appearance. Alchemical Properties:\nBeard Weed is a moderate earth symbol. It works well in hair tonics.\nBlissfoil\nAn oily blue flower that grows in clumps under birch trees.\nEffects: Numbness where the oil is applied. It has been known to cause headaches.\nOverdose: Permanent loss of touch in the affected area.\nNotes: Oils are found near the petals and stalk.\nBread Mold\nA blue or green mold that grows on bread, cheese, and other food items.\nEffects: This particular mold only affects some individuals negatively. In these individuals, exposure can cause a rash or the throat to close up. The mold\nhas disease fighting properties that can be brought out by a skilled druid.\nOverdose: Too much can caue confusion, odd behavior, a severe rash, reduced urination, or seizures.\nNotes: A druid is required to bring out the disease fighting\nproperties, and care must be taken to reduce the effect of other types of mold growing with it.\nBlood Lotus\nA rust colored herb, found growing near entrances to caves in hot climates.\nEffects: Extremely nutritious, but extended use can turn the skin orange.\nOverdose: Kidney stones.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate Fire Symbol\nNotes: Can be made into a strong, deep red alcohol.\nCrimson Vase\nA vase shaped plant with deep red petals that is commonly found in places with a mild amount of light. The herb grows on trees parasitically.\nEffects: Slight burning sensation if it's liquid is spilt. It'll cause rashes.\nOverdose: Will burn even more.\nAlchemical Properties: Crimson Vase is a strong fire symbol, typically used in love, rage, and envy potions, as well as Alchemist Fire.\nNotes: The petals are warm to the touch.\nCrouching Feather\nAn herb with three white, drooping petals. It only blooms at night under large bushes.\nEffects: Calming and clears the mind. Can cause light-headedness. With proper druidic preparation, it can be used as a sedative.\nOverdose: Coma\nAlchemical Properties: Strong air symbol. It is typically used in clarity potions.\nNotes: Crouching Feather is highly fragile. Wind can damage the plant.\nDiddyfunkle\nA bright, purple flowered herb that tends to grow in jungles and plains.\nEffects: The purple stems cause extremely itchy rashes. The center ball's jucies can be used as a sedative or to clear the mind. Can cause unconciousness\nor death if not prepared correctly.\nOverdose: Death\nNotes: Tiny amounts can be a delicacy.\nDraugr Tongue\nAn aloe like, orange flowered plant that grows in grassy plains.\nEffects: The liquid in the plant makes for a good disinfectant, but stings.\nNotes: The stem is not useful.\nDwarf's Pumpkin\nA stinky, orange leafed shrub that grows by water, usually in swamps.\nEffects: Burning taste similar to ginger.\nOverdose: Burns!\nAlchemical Properties: Strong fire symbol, commonly used in Alchemist Fire.\nNotes: Easy to pick. Smells bad. It's named for it's use in dwarven brews. The brightest leaves are the most potent.\nElf's Hair Vine\nAn white blossomed herb with an icy white visage. It grows on high cliffs in frozen lands.\nEffects: It has a calming effect and can result in more fluid movements, but may cause someone to move too fast, in which case physical\nexhaustion could be an issue.\nOverdose: Rapid heart beat, burst blood vessels ad the like.\nAlchemical Properties: Strong air symbol. It's used in grace and speed potions.\nNotes: The vine is extremely fragile, and the petals contain nectar.\nFlame Tongue Root\nA bright rust colored root with a rose-like flower. It can be found in heavily forested areas, burnt out forests, and areas with a lot of sun and water.\nEffects: The root can be used as a coagulant, though it can burn.\nBe warned that the spores can cause sensitivity to touch.\nOverdose: Too much blood cloting, strokes, etc.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate fire symbol\nNotes: Fairly hot to the touch. Watch out for those spores.\nFrost Vine\nA small, brittle blue vine that grows in frosty areas, usually on trees.\nEffects: Soothes pain and and numbs/relaxes muscles where applied. Full numbness of limbs can occur on prolonged exposure.\nOverdose: Frostbite\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate water symbol.\nGoblin's Ivy\nA short brown or green vine that can be found clinging to buildings and rocks.\nEffects: Scentless, mild, nausea inducing poison that can also cause mild dehydration.\nOverdose: More nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea.\nAlchemical Properties: Weak to moderate earth symbol commonly used in resilience potions.\nNotes: Goblin's Ivy can survive in nearly moistureless areas.\nGrobsnopper\nA pink or yellow buld-like flower that grows on trees, typically found in moist forests.\nEffects: Potent healing effects. \"Soaks up\" disease.\nOverdose: Stomach aches.\nHabgobsnit\nA tall, pale-shaded grass that grows in forests and plains.\nEffects: Juices good for numbing. It can provide a sense of clarity... or just get you high.\nOverdose: Paralysis\nKing's Ivy\nAn ivy with golden flowers and a dark green stalk that grows on rocks, tree trunks, and old ruins.\nEffects: Can be taken as a stimulent, but can cause agitation.\nOverdose: Heart attacks, and in general too much energy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbs 2", "Leyun Kameki", "A Druid's Book of Herbs\nVolume 2\n\nHerbs from Solstice Druid Callax\n\nScribed with additions by Apple Druid Leyun\nMalin's Heart\nA white flower that grows in plains and forests.\nEffects: Chewing numbs the whole body for a few minutes.\nOverdose: Prolonged numbness.\nNotes: A bit harder to find than blissfoil.\nMandragora\nA parsnip shaped herb that grows in swamps and wetlands.\nEffects: Revitalization and regenerative properties make the plant valuable, but the spores it releases in season cause hallucinations.\nOverdose: Can cause growths. The hallucinogenic spores often cause choking and can be fatal.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate water symbol, often used in healing potions.\nNotes: Harvest 2 weeks after maturity to avoid spores.\nNight Sap\nA golden sap that drips from deformed oak trees.\nEffects: Causes a sense of calm, safety, and happiness, along with tiredness. It usually makes for about 5 hours of sleep. After waking, though, it brings splitting headaches\nand paralysis for as much time as the sleep.\nOverdose: Longer lasting effects.\nNotes: Highly addictive.\nSaffvil\nA sickly green grass that grows in swamps near dead things.\nEffects: Nausea and blood clotting\nOverdose: Death\nAlchemical Properties:\nModerate fire symbol.\nSagedust\nPollen from the Alabaster plant.\nEffects: Increased metabolism and speed, along with heightened senses and a rapid heart rate.\nOverdose: Possible heart attack.\nNotes: Incredibly difficult to harvest.\nSerpent's Stalk\nA long, reed like emerald stalk that grows in forests near or in water.\nEffects: Cooling effect when applied with water, may cause rashes.\nOverdose: Mild hypothermia.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate water symbol. Typically used in antidotes, calming, and healing potions.\nNotes: Poisonous to bugs.\nShade Leaf\nA short, small plant with plain leaves, yellow flowers, and silvery veins that is commongly found anwhere there is grass and shade.\nEffects: Calming, stress releaving, bloodshot eyes, increased appetite.\nOverdose: Hallucinations\nNotes: Grows in large quantities, simmilar to normal weeds. Makes a popping noise when exposed to rain.\nSwamp Blossom\nA purple green flower with a short, thick stem, found in the branches of swamp trees.\nEffects: Nectar is like honey, and the flower is nutritious, though consuming raw can gum up the throat.\nOverdose: Smelly breath and diarrhea.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate air symbol, usually used in speed potions.\nTippen's Root\nPurple flowers with a dark yellow speckled root that grow near fallen trees in dense forests.\nEffects: Stops bleeding almost instantly, but stinks to the seven hells.\nOverdose: Blood clots, and the dangers of blood clots.\nAlchemical Properties:\nModerate earth symbol, commonly used in strength and healing potions.\nNotes: Really, seriously stinks. Really. Make sure you're prepared for the stink.\nYarrow\nA white to pink flowered plant that grows in grasslands and forests.\nEffects: Can reduce inflammation and blood pressure, as well as intensify the medicinal effects of other herbs.\nOverdose: Dizziness and fainting due to\nlow blood pressure.\nZawabate\nA plant with a tall stalk and yellow-green curled petals that grows in a desert oasis in water.\nEffects: Out of body experiences, hallucinations, pain numbing.\nOverdose: Can destroy a person's mind.\nAlchemical Properties:\nModerate water symbol, used in numbing and healing potions.\nNotes: Nectar is the medicinal part of the plant.", ""),
        StaticBook("Herbs 2", "Pine Druid Gi'Garun", "A Druid's Book of Herbs\nVolume 2\n\nHerbs from Solstice Druid Callax\n\nScribed with additions by Apple Druid Leyun\nMalin's Heart\nA white flower that grows in plains and forests.\nEffects: Chewing numbs the whole body for a few minutes.\nOverdose: Prolonged numbness.\nNotes: A bit harder to find than blissfoil.\nMandragora\nA parsnip shaped herb that grows in swamps and wetlands.\nEffects: Revitalization and regenerative properties make the plant valuable, but the spores it releases in season cause hallucinations.\nOverdoes: Can cause growths. The hallucinogenic spores often cause choking and can be fatal.\nAlchemical Properties:\nModerate water symbol, often used in healing potions.\nNotes: Harvest 2 weeks after maturity to avoid spores.\nNight Sap\nA golden sap that drips from deformed oak trees.\nEffects: Causes a sense of calm, safety, and happiness, along with tiredness. It usually makes for about 5 hours of sleep. After waking, though, it brings splitting headaches\nand paralysis for as much time as the sleep.\nOverdoes: Longer lasting effects.\nNotes: Highly addictive.\nSaffvil\nA sickly green grass that grows in swamps near dead things.\nEffects: Nausea and blood clotting\nOverdoes: Death\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate fire symbol\nSagedust\nPollen from the Alabaster plant.\nEffects: Increased metabolism and speed, along with heightened senses and a rapid heart rate.\nOverdose: Possible heart attack.\nNotes: Incredibly difficult to harvest.\nSerpent's Stalk\nA long, reed like emerald stalk that grows in forests near or in water.\nEffects: Cooling effect when applied with water, may cause rashes.\nOverdose: Mild hypothermia.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate water symbol. Typically used in antidotes, calming, and healing potions.\nNotes: Poisonous to bugs.\nShade Leaf\nA short, small plant with plain leaves, yellow flowers, and silvery veins that is commonly found anywhere there is grass and shade.\nEffects: Calming, stress releaving, bloodshot eyes, increased appetite.\nOverdose: Hallucinations\nNotes: Grows in large quantities, similar to normal weeds. Makes a popping noise when exposed to rain.\nSwamp Blossom\nA purple green flower with a short, thick stem found in the branches of swamp trees.\nEffects: Nectar is like honey, and the flower is nutritious, though consuming raw can gump up the throat.\nOverdose: Smelly breath and diarrhoea.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate air symbol, usually used in speed potions.\nTippen's Root\nPurple flowers with a dark yellow speckled root that grow near fallen trees in dense forests.\nEffects: Stops bleeding almost instantly, but stinks to the seven hells.\nOverdose: Blood clots, and the dangers of blood clo\nAlchemical Properties:\nModerate earth symbol, commonly used in strength and healing potions.\nNotes: Really, seriously stinks. Really. Make sure you're prepared for the stink.\nYarrow\nA white to pink flowered plant that grows in grasslands and forests.\nEffects: Can reduce inflammation and blood pressure, as well as intensify the medicinal effects of other herbs.\nOverdose: Dizziness and fainting due to\nlow blood pressure.\nZawabate\nA plant with a tall stalk and yellow-green curled petals that grows in desert oasis in water.\nEffects: Out of body experiences, hallucinations, pain numbing.\nOverdose: Can destroy a person's mind.\nAlchemical Properties: Moderate water symbol, used in numbing and healing potions.\nNotes: Nectar is the medicinal part of the plant.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hermetic License", "Berdisleyev", "MAGISTRATE OF HERMETICS License granted to:\n\n\n\n    SOPHIA HALCOURT\n\n\n\n\nIssued on:\nMalin's Welcome, 1655\nMAGISTRATE OF HERMETICS\n\nName:\nSophia Alexandria Halcourt\n\nRace:\nHuman\n\nHT:\n5'8\nWT:\n132\n\nEYE:\nBro\n\nHAIR:\nYellow Ponytail\n\nAPPEARANCE:\nYoung\nMAGISTRATE OF HERMETICS\n\nLicensed Magic(s):\n\n- Hydromancy\n\n- Electromancy\n\n\nPERMITTED TO PRACTICE WITHIN CANONIST WORLD\nMAGISTRATE OF HERMETICS\n\nSigned,\n\nDean of Hermetics -\nHis Excellency,\n\nBERDISLEYEV\n\n\n\n    + DEUS MAGNUS +", ""),
        StaticBook("High Elf Culture", "Gallidron Elindrow", "The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya for Beginners.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~      ~~~~~~~~~~~\nKarin'ayla to you. This book is intended as a guide through the noble culture of the High Elven people. Be you a youth of the Mali'aheral or a foreign diplomat who\ndesires to familiarize yourself with our ways, or even an older elf who has lapsed in their etiquette, this book can help you.\n\nPlease read on through the various lessons in these pages. Also see the guide to elven phrases in the back.\nLesson One\n    Avoid All Impurity\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nImpurity can exsist in two ways, Physical and mental. Both are to be treated with paramount seriousness, as they threaten the delicate balance of our civilized society.\nPhysical impurity is found when an individual is only partly High Elf, thus they are not \"pure\" in their lineage. Through out our long lives and our history we have seen, time and agian, that relations between a High Elf and others not of our kin end in\nmisery and failure. The impure products of these thoughtless and perverse relations are prone to lives of dissapointment and loneliness, as they do not truely belong anywhere. To any of the Mali'aheral, the formation of a \"romantic\" relationship with any\noutside of our people is forbidden, and will only serve to make yourself physically impure as well. The creation of children from such a bond is viewed with equal displeasure. This may sound harsh to those who are not of our people, but it is not. it is\nsimply the truth that wisdom and experience have taught us.\n\nWays to determine if one is of impure lineage include but are not limited to the following. Eyes of any color save blues, greens or purples. Ears that are rounded and short. Also a smallness of\nstature can indicate impurity. Hair amoung the Mali'aheral is normally fair, though it is not unheard of to have a brunette born amoung us. Dark hair, however, will certainly raise flags of warning to any who do not know the elf in question.\nMental impurity is a bit more difficult to detect as it can be hidden by the devious or the liar.\nIn truth, any who do not follow the Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya are considered mentally impure to some degree or another. Small degrees of impurity can be treated\nand corrected. Large ones however can, have and will result in banishment and even death. Physical Impurity usually will end with the individual being \"cleansed\" by being tossed into an acid bath. Thus removing their taint from our society.\nLesson Two\nProper Conduct in the\n            City\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nHigh Elves place etiquette on a high pedistal. We enjoy conversation, and we enjoy debate, but we insist it is done right. Emotion should not cloud one's judgment\nor reasoning, neither should it color one's argument. Logic and reason should rule the mind as it rules in the city of Haelun'or.\n\nFor those of you who are not of the people, you should consider before speaking to a High Elf, or trying to enter the city,\nthat there are a few key differences between you and us.\n\nWe are old, very old. Many of us have lived long enough to have met your great, great grand parents when they were children. As such our perspective is different than yours. High Elves are\nseen as cold or harsh in their demeanor or critisisms. In answer to this I invite you to consider these things. How would you feel if you saw an endless parade of children making the same mistakes, time and again, even though you yourself have warned them\nof the pitfalls of their poor behavoir many times over the past centuries? We grow frustrated when we see the same problems and mistakes being repeated and not fixed as logic would dictate that they must. You must also consider that a High Elf reckons\nthings in a longer time frame than you likely do. There for, one should not take our comments or critisisms personally, for they are intended to help you and your children and your children's children to be better. After all, why should one be upset by\nthe truth?\n\nWhen attempting to enter the city, if one is not of the Mali'aheral, one should not think to do so lightly or easily. Our city is precious to us, and we do not seek to sunder its purity by letting any and all who knock to enter.\nIf one seeks to enter they should do so with the right frame of mind. With patience and with humility one will go further. Also it is customary to bring a gift, that they may offer something in return for the honor of entering the gates.\nFor those of you who are of the people. I suggest looking the part. Dress appropriately for your lineage as a High Elf. Keep your hair seemly, and preferably un-dyed. Our flesh should be free of tattoos or piercings as these things only mar our natural\nbeauty. Makeup or accesories that accent our features may be worn however.\nLesson Three\n       Be Educated\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Whether you attend the Eternal College or you take it upon yourself to read and learn, all good High Elves smile upon the persuit of knowledge. Learn of art, science or even the arcane lore of\nmagic, but be knowledgable of something. One should spend their whole life aquiring new learning that they may be useful.\n\nOh be wise, what more can I say?\nLesson Four\n        Courtship\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The art of courtship is something that all young Mali'aheral should know. For one day, you may wish to impress someone of the opposite gender and unite with them in marriage. Follow this guide and you\nwill hopefully avoid becoming a social pariah.\n\nDo NOT engage in sappy, lovey dovey actions or grandiose acclamations of your love. This will not end well and is unseemly for one of our people. Rather, create works of art or music or literature that\nyou can devote to the object of your adoration. Doing so will not only let that person know that someone is interested in them, but will show that you are capable in these areas. These things should, however, be done anonymously, so as not to put any\nundue social strain on you or them. When this courtship has gone on for a while and you feel reasonably sure that they will respond in kind to your affections, then you may reveal your identity to them as their admirer. If you do not feel that things will\ngo well, or you lose interest, you may simply stop courting the individual and no one should be any the wiser who it was.\n\nAlas, these things do indeed happen.\nLesson Five\n         Marriage\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Once your courtship has gone its course and you and your beloved are together, it is expected that you will be married.\nHigh Elven marriages are usually held in large public venues or centers of\nknowledge such as a library. We do not have churches and therefore do not hold weddings in them.\n\nThe ceremony is attended by all the pure citizenry, as well as invited outsiders. An individual is given the honor to speak at the wedding and officiate the\nceremony. After they speak, a moment of silence is given for any to speak out against the union, should they choose. This is almost never done, as to speak out publically against the couple is considered rude in the extreme.\nThe two are then wed and may\nrecieve gifts, congradualtions, etcetera.\n\nIt is within the bonds of matrimony and ONLY within these bonds that the creation of High Elven children may take place. Assuming you are fertile, to have a child is an honor and a joy to be planned and\ntaken with all seriousness.\nLesson Six\n         Religion\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~This will be a rather short section. The High Elves practice no religion. We would rather devote our time to logical and, for lack of a better term, provable persuits than to sit in a church and\npray to a God that we can neither see nor hear. Rather than try to guess at the whims of deity, We will continue to unravel the mysteries of the world as we can prove it exsists.\n\nFor my High Elven readers, you would do well to devote yourself to the\npractice of our culture, rather than some faith from a distant land.\nLesson Seven\n    To Offer Insult\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The highest insult one can offer is to call another impure. This however has some stipulations. For example, if one of the leaders of the people, We'll say the El'sohaer were to call another elf impure\nthis offense could be taken with much gravity. However, if a half elf were to refer to a High elf as impure, the insult has no barb, as the half elf is impure to begin with. One way to offer such an insult is to give a High Elf gold. This should almost\nnever be done, as one High Elf to another, as the action can indicate that the reciever cares more for gold than they do for their people. Of course were a human to give an elf a bar of gold, it would have no such meaning, as a human could not be expected\nto know this. Gold jewlery or items can be given between High Elves, so long as the intent is clear. Unless you really do want to insult them.\nConclusion\n```````````````````'''''''''''''''''''   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nI hope that you have enjoyed this book, but more so I hope that you are better prepared to navigate the pitfalls of High Elven etiquette. We are a strict people, but we are\ndelightsome when you know how to behave.\n\nPlease look for my next book\n\n\"An Encyclopedic Arcanum\"\na guide to magic\n\n~Gallidron Elindrow~\n\nPublication year 1514\nA Guide to\n      Elvish Phrases\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~````````````````````''''''''''''''''''Karin'ayla- Good day\nKer'ayla- Good night\nVan'ayla- Farewell\nMali- Elf\nBortu- Dwarf\nUruk- Ork\nValah- Human\nTali'bortu- Halfling\nLlir/Lliran-Friend(s)\nMali'aheral-High Elf\nAcalin- Shop\nAiler- Wizard\nIler- Dark wizard\n\nHopefully these few phrases and words will be of use to any who learn them.", ""),
        StaticBook("His Fungi", "Motsham Malog'Yar", "((This book was written by an orc, but since most of the Blah is mispronounced common, I only wrote the words that are actually different for orcs in the Blah. The words shared between the two languages are written in Common. Sorry for the clunky OOC\npreface, but I just wanted to give the reader a heads-up.))    Many of those who gruk mi, gruk that mi have long been a devout worshiper of Orgon. Those who have visited the shrine of Orgon atop the plateau in San'Vitar, may have noticed the fungus which\npopulates the mound on which the shrine is erected. Very few people gruk the nature agh significance of the fungus, agh would ignorantly dismiss it as nub-thing more than a bunch of ugly mushrooms. These mushrooms, however, are actually a\nsupernatural phenomenon. The fungus which grows upon Orgon's mound is not of the natural world. It is a physical manifestation of Orgon's will agh influence spreading in the mortal plane. This is why lat will nub ever find any growing on their own in a\nnormal environment. Very few also gruk that the fungus is, in fact, carnivorous, but feeds almost exclusively during the feeding rituals of Orgon worship. Now, when mi blah the word \"carnivorous\", mi mean it very strongly. During the feeding ritual, the\nfungus almost instantly takes root in the flesh of the sacrifice, and begins literally consuming its prey. The process causes the victim to be rapidly digested alive within a matter of minutes. The fungus devours every last piece of its prey, leaving\nbehind neither flesh, blood, bones or organs. This is how Orgon has revealed to his followers that his sacrifices must be offered. Outside of the feeding ritual, the fungus feeds very rarely, occassionally digesting any insects that find themselves\ntrapped in the liquid secretions of the mushrooms. Now, onto the specifics. There are dub varieties of mushrooms which grow upon Orgon's sacrificial mounds: Orgon's bile and Orgon's gall. Both of these mushrooms have some similar qualities. Namely,\nneither should be taken without asking permission of Orgon and rulging him for his generosity; agh they should both be handled with care. \n Orgon's bile: These short, squat mushrooms are a bluish-purple color with white spots. On each spot grow many\ntiny black spores. The spores are easily broken, agh contain a foul-smelling black substance. It smells very much like decomposing flesh, and tastes like rotten eggs. Contact stains the skin. A slight taste of the mushroom or the oily, black substance\ncauses nausea (agh mi mean a VERY slight taste). Mi tested the effects of full consumption of the mushroom on a willing burz-albai named Mithras. Upon immediately eating the whole thing, he was beset by extreme nausea and vomiting, a cold sweat and\nsevere shaking. This was from only ash mushroom. Mi would strongly advise against eating more than ash or a particularly large specimen, as such could very possibly result in flattening. ((Note: these are the red mushrooms growing near Orgon's\nshrine))\n Orgon's gall: These somewhat taller mushrooms are related to Orgon's bile, agh are brown in color. The cap of the Orgon's gall mushroom is bowl shaped, agh constantly secretes a very bitter yellowish-brown fluid. This fluid pools in\nthe aforementioned bowl-shaped cap, and emits musty fumes which irritate the eyes upon exposure. Physical contact with the mushroom causes a slight burning sensation in the skin, as the fungus coats itself in its own digestive fluids. In small amounts,\nthe digestive fluids seem harmless, however mi have witnessed in mi own worship of Orgon how quickly these fungi digest their prey in large enough groups; agh mi gruk it safe to assume that a single mushroom could eventually cause significant damage\ngiven enough time. Mi tested the effects of Orgon's gall on a shara named Hagan, who exhibited an extremely dry mouth, blurred vision and hallucinations. As with Orgon's bile, mi would strongly recommend against eating dub or more of these mushrooms, as\noverconsumption could have dangerous effects, including flattening. Mi would also theorise that such could possibly lead to lasting impacts on mental health. \n Further discoveries concerning Orgon's bile or Orgon's gall will be recorded agh published in\nfuture books if needed.\n -Malog'Yar, witch doctor agh loyal servant of Orgon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Historiography", "Dauth Sundavar", "A Historical Evaluation of Mage Baruk'Ghaz's \"Ancient History\" Tomes \n\n\n  By Dauth Sundavar\nA critical exegesis into the narrative conventions of Mage Baruk'Ghaz's \"Ancient History\" tomes, and the Holy Scrolls; the fundamental sacred texts of Canonism, facilitate for the development of the understanding that the aformentioned historical source\nis a blatant tool for religious propaganda. This is evident through the repetition of phrases within the two two respective texts, and a comparative analysis of the two given texts alongside \"Navitas\", by one Silius Hightower, reinforces the notion that\nthe \"Ancient History\" tomes are nothing but instruments into the establishment of the strict regimen and widespread institutionalisation of Canonism within all racial factions.\n\n\"There were no planes of existence. There was nothing. Just the Void. And\na bright shining light.\" Any faithful adherent to the tenets of Canonism would immediately recognise this passage to be the opening to the Holy Scrolls. Similarly, any well-read historian would know that this is the opening passage to Mage Baruk-Ghaz's\n\"Ancient History\" tomes. Furthermore, in my studies, I have come to find this passage imbued within a great multitude of philosophical texts, \"Navitas\" being one that particularly demanded my attention.\n\nThis evident plagarism that has been noted makes me\nquestion the legitimacy and the historicity of the Mage's text. Through rigorous study and perserverance, I have come to acknowledge that both \"Ancient History\" and the Holy Scrolls are mere reflections of each other. Later phrases such as \"He [Iblees]\ngrew large wings and began to breathe terrible fire... Only Malin, Urguan, Horen, and Krug stood in front of the terror\" have been noted in both texts.\n\nNow one could argue that the Holy Scrolls recall the histories that are outlined in the Mage's text.\nI would argue in return that they are blinded by their faith, and plea that they turn their attention to the evident plagarism that has seeped into the very fabric of history.\n\nNote how I mentioned that \"Navitas\", written by Silius Hightower, too copied\nmany phrases found within the Holy Scrolls. Upon further investigation, I began to realise many phrases have been copied, with either tenses or small words being changed to create an illusion of originality. \n\nFrom what I have gathered, Silius at the\ntime of publication was a child. Now I call into question whether a child, even in their adolescence, had the patience to both transcribe the text of their faith and then provide what is regarded as \"profound philosophical wisdom\" on the writings.\nI have come to the conclusion that an elder member of House Hightower wrote \"Navitas\", and then proceeded to place Silius' name on the binding and opening cover of the text.\n\nSimilarly, the prestigious position that House Hightower has within the\nheirarchy of the Church, as noted by Theoren in his text, \"House Hightower\", I do not believe it presumptious of me to state that House Hightower, who become reflective of the Church of the Faith, to  be ecclesiatical in their approach to the history of\nMan. Theoren states that \"The House of Hightower begins its origins far and further back through the pages of the history of Man to the first High Pontiff of the Church of the Faith, Everrard Hightower\", and therefore provides proof to my claim that it is\nnot beyond those of the Church to insert their own religious motivations within their accounts of History. \n\nIt is therefore axiomatic, within my own individual contextual framework, that Mage Baruk-Ghaz's \"Ancient History\" tomes are nothing but mere\nCanonist propaganda, and provide only a historical account of Man rather than the Descendents. \n\nIf any budding or adept historian wishes to challenges my claims and provide evidence into how the Mage has provided an accurate portrayal of the origins of\nAegis, then I highly encourage them to do so, for that is the nature of history and scholarship; to develop understanding where there is none, and to search for the one Truth amidst all the falsities.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hollowed Umbrage", "UnBaed", "[!] The pages in this book are filled with neat, ink writing.\n\n\n\n\n                 Hallowed\n                 Umbrage\n[A copy from the original]\nI write the following epitaph with dire haste so much that the winds part my words.  My account of these events may not be entirely accurate, something completely acceptable under the maddening, fear stricken haze that I have left in.\nI sit here now quill in hand, wounded wit a gash so dreadfully dark that I'm not sure if it really is a wound at all.  I have become a well of life, bountiful as the succulent navy mists ooze out of this growth, this... anchor; ever so dark and dreadful.\nMy pilgrimmage to this place hath cost me the trust and faith of my only friends as despite  every loud, nagging warning against venturing here, my back was turned and my hands covered my ears.\nIt is the weakness of Man to succum to the allure of power, riches, and knowledge that of which the Abyss is said to contain.  Trust me when I say that the power hidden away here is done for a reason and should never belong to any mortal man.\nFor the corrupting mind of Men ever to wrap their greedy fingers around such incomprehensible things, it would mean our doom.  The Trolls, Harpies, and Gryphons of our world pale in comparison to the horror of the deep, dark beyond.\nLegends tell of the Abyss ruins of Aegis, a land from which Man's forefathers hailed.  I would hesitate to call the state in which the Gods left the motherland in a ruin, for truly there remains little left here at all.\nFor this Abyss, this endless chasm to which there seems no end is both the catastrophic ashes of a world once living and breathing as well as a prison for every lost soul that the world sunk with it.  North, South, East, West - it all leads to despair.\nI hath deviated from the guiding compass to venture in a new direction; downward.  For I suspected that within the bowels of this crushing nightmare there must be both a ceiling and a floor.  I, a pawn controlled by adventurous urges, took a fatal dive.\nMy sense of time has long since fled, abandoning me like many other luxuries that once made me whole.  After a measurement of time far longer than any measurement of time I've evered thought to measure.  I reached the feared and fabled end of this void.\nI dare not write about the countless demonds that scour the ebon plane despite the insanity they so passively inflict.  They do not deserve the honour of being referenced alongside the Lord of the deep, dark below.  Darkness Incarnate.\nAs my wailing, shedding flesh forced itself through the dense acidic atmosphere, my feet began to fail me.  Time hath come to truly give up, and turn my back I thought.  Yet my thoughts were ruptured by a presence so overwhelming that I could not think.\nAs I fought with myself to open my eyes I stared upon what could only be described as a living shadow, embodying umbral hellfire frigid enough to lock my very bones in place.Radiated in darkness so hollow that the Abyss stood brightly aflamed beside hi\nHe worse armor, the first sign that this impossible creation was indeed Man.  Ancient was his armor, charred and blackened from what I cannot begin to imagine.  Yet his armor, heavy as it appeard did not hinder him.\nHis form suddenly shifted all at once, phasing out at one place and in again at another.  The realm was his whim, as he did not simply move through it, but had become it.  Now, the Dark Lord towered above me, reeking of ash and death.\nAll past experiences seem like a petty joke when compared to the awesome perspective I had been blessed with.  This Man, whose blood red eyes pierced through the very veil of the Abyss had drawn forth his weapon.  A terrible greatsword, massive in size.\nDripping with the hollowing souls of the damned.  This blade, serrated like the peak of Mount Ire was shoved into my heart, slotting into my flesh like a key within a door.  In the seconds before my consciousness faded I heard something.  I heard a voice.\nA voice that would rival a Dragon.  It was then that I knew for certain - This was the Old Lord of Umbrage.  King of the Abyss.  One whose name does not touch the lips of the living, and whose sight is known only to the dead and the mad.\nHis perverted shriek defiled every corner of the Abyss, his siren call summoning the dark to his side.  As the black visage of the Old Lord faded from my sight, I heard his words.\nR A D I A N T\nI S  T H E  B L A C K\nS U N", ""),
        StaticBook("Holm is bad!1!!1", "Uglii'Gorkil", "Holm is very bad!!!", ""),
        StaticBook("Holy Scrolls - I", "Secundus de Pacha", "Holy Scrolls - I\n\nTranscribed by Jacob Chapel during the Deep Cold 1470.\n\nUse these words to keep true to your faith and to find \nstrength and knowledge.\nThere were no planes or existence. There was nothing. Just the void. And a bright shining light. It was not a light we could see, it was not really white either, but it would be the only way to explain the existence of such a Deity in contrast to the\nemptiness of the Void. None knows why, how or when this Deity existed. It is, in-fact, heresy to speculate on such matters. The all know God was this Deity.\n\nTruly none can describe the majesty of the Creator, the one and only. The Merciful Creator of\nthe Seven Skies. With his intent, and only his intent, the World of Aegis was created. All he had to do was simply want it to occur and it happened. The rolling seas, proud mountains and vast landscapes, all in a second, created by God.\nThe World was not created in play or for fun, but as a theater for the inhabitants of the World to be tested in. And tested for what? That is for us to speculate. Though I believe it is to test us for purity, how hard we can fight temptation,\nand how clean and good can our actions be.\n\nThe first mortal being to be created was a man. This man was sculpted with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, God’s creation lay there for the other immortal beings to see. The Aengul and the\nDaemon, the two spirits created before the mortal beings and before the creator of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more. God then blew his own breath of existence into the hollow shell\nand the Man lived. God then took the man and put him in the centre of all of Aegis, the same spot where the Cloud Temple now stands. God also made the Man a partner, from the exact same clay and the exact same breath, she was the first Woman. There siple\npartner, from the exact same clay and the exact same breath, she was the first Woman. There siple beings could not talk, nor did they know much about the World. They roamed the world, enjoying the prehistoric beauty. Untouched, the fresh glades\nand dark thick forests were a wonder to set eyes on. Soon they had four children in the four corners of Aegis.\n\nMalin was the first of their sons, born in the deep forests of Aegis, he had blonde hair and sharp ears.\nStanding tall, he was the father of the Elves of Aegis. Krug was born in the scorching deserts of Aegis, fierce and relentless, he was the father of the Orcs. In the fresh meadows of Aegis was born Horen, father of Humans. And lastly, in the deep\nunderground caves of the World, Urguan was born, master of the Dwarves. \n\nSoon the first Man and Woman created by God departed Aegis and climbed the seven skies to meet with God their creator, for they had achieved their goal.\nThe Sons began to explore the World of Aegis and each was stricken with grief at the loss of their parents, seeking to fill the chasm of emotion inside them they began to create civilization.\n\nAlthough none of the descendants of each Son had neither\ntheir long lives or splendour, they did carry their forefather looks and traits. The Elves with Malin at their head travelled the lands and began naming all the inhabitants of the world, they were the first to create a tongue and began t name\nthe trees and grass, the mountains and valleys across all of Aegis.\n\nAt this time, Malin, Urguan, Krug and Horen were not far apart in looks. Horen and Krug had darker hair than the other two and Krug was a bit larger in build.\nMalin had blonde hair and Urguan red. They were all close companions, friends and had much love for each other and each others people. \n\nUrguan travelled into the deep underground of the earth, naming the beautiful ores and gems,\nsharing it with his brethren. Krug travelled the harsh deserts, testing his stamina and strength against the environments of Aegis, and Horen began building the first squalid huts and villages in the valleys. The people lived for hundreds of years,\nin harmony and peace. Until the day where the great Daemons, great worshipers and squalid protectors of the Void, kin spirits to the Aengul, defected.\n\nIblees, who was once the greatest of all of God’s worshippers, was cast down into the mortal and he was\nabout to destroy the tranquility of Aegis forever. He came in the shape of a man. A gentle being who loved things delicate, he was quickly befriended by Malin, Urguan, and Horen. Krug was a great distrust of him but after many years of being convinced\nby his brothers, he finally accepted his company.\n\nLittle did Iblees know that this was part of the Great God’s plan to test the descendants of Man and Woman. Iblees wanted to destroy everything that God had designed and created, still not in a\npowerful physical form he began sowing seeds of evil in the minds of the Descendants. Prying on their needs and lusts. \n\nTo Malin, lover of nature, he promised him many children. He promised him that their laughter would resonate across their forest homes\nand that he would be content. Malin did not want anything more in this world than a bountiful amount of young to occupy the barren forests.\n\nTo Urguan, he promised infinite wealth of Gems and Ores, colours and crystals he could never\nimagine. To this, Urguan’s greed failed him.\n\nHoren, was anxious he would not live long enough to see his city completed and his lands increased. He needed more time, and Iblees struck the chord and promised immortality.\nKrug was the last to be tricked, Iblees tempted him with wealth, with food with power. None interested Krug. Iblees was furious, he then challenged Krug to open combat in fury.\n\nThe whole world witnessed Ibleeses transformation\ninto a hideous beast of the void. His skin turned to scales, fangs erupted and dark horned exploded from his head. He grew large wings and began to breath terrible fire. All stood in shock and horror. The beast terrified all inhabitants of Aegis,\nanimals fled and the Son of the Descendants were too weak of blood to stand in front of such evil fury. Only Malin, Urguan, Horen and Krug stood in front of the terror.\n\nIn Iblees’ right hand, a sword wrought in flames.\nKrug, naked and unarmed charged at the Daemon, throwing himself against the scalding scales of Iblees. He screamed in agony as his skin burned and decayed, becoming green and molten. Iblees was knocked off his feet, for the last time. He\nstood up, heaving in rage and fury, flames exploded from the pores of his skin, he roared in anger and where he struck his sword the land collapsed and the ground erupted. And Lo, great was the Valour of Urguan and the Strength\nof Krug as they fought the beast. Powerful were the arms that carried Krug’s Axe and strong was Horens’ heart as they fought in open combat upon the plains of Aegis. Malin’s sword was fast and swift, smiting Iblees upoj his breast and sides.\nFor thirty years the Descendants fought Iblees, the world became a war torn mess. The dead were defiled, summoned from their graves to follow Ibless’ mastery. The mortal descendants died, the greater Iblees’ armies grew.  It was a sad chapter\nThe brothers threw up their hands to God in prayer and in agony. Their creations destroyed, their children massacred. Woe to the Sons of Man and Woman. Krug grew bitter, his resentment of his brothers increased for befriending such a beast. Urguan grew\ngreedy, he fought valourously but began to hide his treasures underground. Malin feared for the lives of his children and did not leave his forest sanctuary. It seemed the world was destined for ruin. Iblees grew in strength and the Descendants weakened.\nUntil one day.\n\nOne day where the sound of horns could be heard from the far east. Beautiful horns echoing all across the skies of Aegis. God had heard their prayers. An army of Aengul and Daemons from the seven skies had appeared on the grand shores of\nAegis. Their majesty and beauty so strong that all The Descendants could see was a flash of power white light erupt from the east. Only Malin with his strong sight could see the figures of light as they sped across the skies towards to armies of Iblees.\nIblees’ soldiers burned where they stood, The thousands of skeletons and cadavers burst aflame and his living servants fled. There in the right middle of the world, he was cast down and chained by the Aengul and Daemon. A robed figure with brown hair\nand a black wreathed apparation stood before him. They were a terrible image to look at, all shyed down and bowed in their majesty and glory. They stood before Iblees, knowing he was immortal and could not be killed, sentencing him to banishment to\nthe void where his dar sould would be forever trapped in torment.\n\nBut before they could complete the sentence, Iblees stood tall for one last time. “You believe you may simply banish me from this plane and that my taint shall not last?\nI have touched this world with evil and it shall forever be part of the souls to inhabit it. Malin, I find no need to curse you, for so many of your kind have already willingly submitted to me now and will on my return in the distant future. The curse you\nbare, is not of my doing, but of your own. Even you have done my work if you realize it or not.”\n\n“Urguan, your greed and lust shall overcome you, you are not worthy of the weight God gave you, your descendants shall be short,\nsqualid and ugly. You will always seek to find Gold and Gems in the deep underground of the ear your hunger never satisfied.”\n\n“Horen, the immortality you hoped for will never arrive. Your longevity has already been stripped away thanks to the labors\nof the twisted heart of your brother Malin. You will age quickly and die before you ever taste the fruits of your pointless labors.”\n\n“And you Krug, the most hated of the Descendants, you shall always have the lust of war. You are strong?\nWell the strength shall be used against your brothers, used to pillage and murder! Your lust for battle shall be unsatiated and your descendants shall grow ugly and heartless.”\n\nAs soon as his words were uttered, the world grew suddenly dark.\nA great roar erupted from Iblees’ mouth and in a blast of fire he was banished from the Mortal World. The Descendants stood still for several moments, pondering over the words of Iblees. Malin, Krug, Urguan, and Horen all knew naught of what the great\nDevil had spoken of when concerning Malin’s betrayal. Dismissing it as the lies of a demon propagated to corrupt their souls, the brothers thought nothing further of Malin’s supposed treason.\n\nThe robed figure stood before the four brother.\n“There is nothing in my power that may undo what that evil did. There is only thing I may do however, and that is to bless you.”\n\n“Malin, may your forests be a sanctuary of peace and your children long lived.”\n“Urguan, may your descendants be hardy, strong hearted and strong of mind.”\n\n“Krug, may your people show valour and honour where none exist.”\n\n“And Horen, may your people one day explore the seven\nSkies.”\n\n“I can do no more, for all my power is spent. We will go back to our masters now, I believe your children may see us once more but long in the future.” And with that, the great host of Aenguls and Daemons disappeared into thin wisps in the air.\nCopied By\nSecundus de Pacha\n17th of the Sun's Smile, 1665", ""),
        StaticBook("Holy Scrolls - I", "Jacob Chapel", "The Holy Scrolls\n\n     The Book of\n     Nativities\n\nTransscribed by Jacob Chapel during the Deep Cold, 1470.\n\nUse these words to keep true to your faith and to find strength and knowledge.\nThere were no planes of existence. There was nothing. Just the Void. And a bright shining light. It was not a light we could see, it was not really white either, but it would be the only way to explain the existence of such a Deity in contrast to the\nemptiness of the Void. None knows why, how or when this Deity existed. It is, in-fact, heresy to speculate on such matters. The all knowing God was this Deity.\n\nTruly none can describe the majesty of the Creator, the one and only. The Merciful Creator of\nthe Seven Skys. With his intent, and only his intent, the World of Aegis was created. All he had to do was simply want it to occur and it happened. The rolling seas, proud mountains and vast landscapes, all in a second, created by God.\nThe World was not created in play or for fun, but as a theater for the inhabitants of the World to be tested in. And tested for what? That is for us to speculate. Though I believe it is to test us for purity, how hard we can fight temptation, and how\nclean and good can our actions be.\n\nThe first mortal being to be created was a man. This man was sculptured with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, God's creation lay there for the other immortal beings to see. The Aengul and the Daemon,\nthe two spirits created before the mortal beings and before the creation of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more.\n\nGod then blew his own breath of existance into the hollow shell and\nthe Man lived. God then took the man and put him in the centre of all of Aegis, the same spot where The Cloud Temple now stands. God also made the Man a partner, from the exact same clay\nand the exact same breath, she was the first Woman. These simple beings could not talk, nor did they know much about the World. They roamed the world, enjoying its pre-historic beauty. Untouched, the fresh glades and dark thick forests were a wonder to\nset eyes on. Soon they had four children in the four corners of Aegis.\n\nMalin was the first of their sons, born in the deep forests of Aegis, he had blonde hair and sharp ears. Standing tall, he was the father of the Elves of Aegis. Krug was born in the\nscorching deserts of Aegis, fierce and relentless, he was the father of the Orcs. In the fresh meadows of Aegis was born Horen, father of Humans. And lastly, in the deep underground caves of the World, Urguan was born, master of the Dwarves.\nSoon the first Man and Woman created by God departed Aegis and climbed the seven skies to meet with God their creator, for they had achieved their goal. The Sons began to explore the World of Aegis and each was stricken with grief at the loss of their\nparents, seeking to fill the chasm of emotion inside them they began to create civilisation.\n\nAlthough none of the descendants of each Son had neither their long lives or splendour, they did carry their forefathers looks and traits. The Elves with Malin\nat their head travelled the lands and began naming all the inhabitants of this world, they were the first to create a tongue and began to name the trees and grass, the mountains and valleys across all of Aegis.\n\nAt this time, Malin, Urguan, Krug and\nHoren were not far apart in looks. Horen and Krug had darker hair than the other two and Krug was a bit larger in build. Malin had blonde hair and Urguan red. They were all close companions, friends and had much love for each other and each others people.\nUrguan travelled into the deep underground of the earth, naming the beautiful ores and gems, sharing it with his brethren. Krug travelled the harsh deserts, testing his stamina and strength against the environment of Aegis, and Horen began building the\nfirst squalid huts and villages in the valleys. The people lived for hundreds of years, in harmony and peace. Until the day where one of the great Daemons, great worshipers and squalid protectors of the Void, kin spirits to the Aengul, defected.\nIblees, who was once the greatest of all of God’s worshippers, was cast down into the mortal world, and so he was about to destroy the tranquility of Aegis forever. He came in the shape of a man. A gentle being who loved things delicate, he was quickly\nbefriended by Malin, Urguan and Horen. Krug had a great distrust of him but after many years of being convinced by his brothers, he finally accepted his company.\n\nLittle did Iblees know that this was all part of the Great God's plan to test the\ndescendants of Man and Woman. Iblees wanted to destroy everything that God had designed and created, still not in a powerful physical form he began sowing seeds of evil in the minds of the Descendants. Prying on their needs and lusts.\nTo Malin, lover of nature, he promised him many children. He promised him that their laughter would resonate across their forest homes and that he would be content. Malin did not want anything more in this world than a bountiful amount of young to\noccupy the barren forests.\n\nTo Urguan, he promised infinite wealth of Gems and Ores, colours and crystals he could never imagine. To this, Urguan’s greed failed him.\nHoren, was anxious he would not live long enough to see his city completed and his lands increased. He needed more time, and Iblees struck the chord and promised immortality.\n\nKrug was the last to be tricked, Iblees tempted him with wealth, with food,\nwith power. None interested Krug. Iblees was furious, he then challenged Krug in open combat in fury.\n\nThe whole world witnessed Ibleeses transformation into a hideous beast of the void. His skin turned into scales, fangs erupted and dark horns exploded\nfrom his head. He grew large wings and began to breath terrible fire. All stood in shock and horror. The beast terrified all inhabitants of Aegis, animals fled and the Sons of the Descendants were too weak of blood to stand in front of such evil fury.\nOnly Malin, Urguan, Horen and Krug stood in front of the terror.\n\nIn Iblees’ right hand, a sword wrought in flame. Krug, naked and unarmed charged at The Daemon, throwing himself against the scalding scales of Iblees. He screamed in agony as his skin\nburned and decayed, becoming green and molten. Iblees was knocked off his feet, for the last time. He stood up, heaving in rage and fury, flames exploded from the pores of his skin, he roared in anger and where he struck his sword the land collapsed and\nthe ground erupted. And Lo, great was the Valour of Urguan and the Strength of Krug as they fought the beast. Powerful were the arms that carried Krug’s Axe and strong was Horens’ heart as they fought in open combat upon the plains of Aegis. Malin’s sword\nwas fast and swift, smiting Iblees upon his breast and sides.\n\nFor the thirty years the Descendants fought Iblees, the world became a war torn mess. The dead were defiled, summoned from their graves to follow Iblees’ mastery. The more mortal descendants\ndied, the greater Iblees’ armys grew. It was a sad chapter in the World of Aegis, the brothers threw up their hands to God in prayer and in agony. Their creations destroyed, their children massacred. Woe to the Sons of Man and Woman. Krug grew bitter,\nhis resentment of his brothers increased for befriending such a beast. Urguan grew greedy, he fought valourously but began to hide his treasures underground. Malin feared for the lives of his children and did not leave his forest sanctuary. It seemed the\nworld was destined for ruin. Iblees grew in strength and the Descendants weakened. Until one day.\n\nOne day where the sound of horns could be heard from the far east. Beautiful horns echoing all across the skies of Aegis. God had heard their prayers.\nAn army of Aengul and Daemons from the seven skies had appeared on the grand shores of Aegis. Their majesty and beauty so strong that all The Descendants could see was a flash of power white light erupt from the east. Only Malin with his strong sight\ncould see the figures of light as they sped across the skies towards the armies of Iblees.\n\nIblees’ soldiers burned where they stood, The thousands of skeletons and cadavers burst aflame and his living servants fled. There in the right middle of the\nworld, he was cast down and chained by the Aengul and Daemon. A robed figure with brown hair and a black wreathed apparation stood before him. They were a terrible image to look at, all shyed down and bowed in their majesty and glory. They stood before\nIblees, knowing he was immortal and could not be killed, sentencing him to banishment to the void where his dark soul would be forever trapped in torment.\nBut before they could complete the sentence, Iblees stood tall for one last time.\n\n“You believe you may simply banish me from this plane and that my taint shall not last? I have touched this world with evil and it shall forever be part of the souls that\ninhabit it.\n\nMalin, I find no need to curse you, for so many of your kind have already willingly submitted to me now and will on my return in the distant future. The curse you will bear, is not of my doing, but of your own. Even you have done my work,\nif you realize it or not.\n\nUrguan, your greed and lust shall overcome you, you are not worthy of the height God gave you, your descendants shall be short, squalid and ugly. You will always seek to find Gold and Gems in the deep underground of the earth,\nyour hunger never satisfied.\n\nHoren, the immortality you hope for will never arrive. Your longevity has already been stripped away thanks to the labors of the twisted heart of your brother Malin. You will age quickly and die before you ever taste the\nfruits of your pointless labors.\n\nAnd you Krug, the most hated of the Descendants, you shall always have the lust of war. You are strong? Well the strength shall be used against your brothers, used to pillage and murder! Your lust for battle shall be\nunsatiated and your descendants shall grow ugly and heartless.”\n\nAs soon as his words were uttered, the world grew suddenly dark. A great roar erupted from Iblees’ mouth and in a blast of fire he was banished from the Mortal World. The Descendants stood\nstill for several moments, pondering over the words of Iblees. Malin, Krug, Urguan and Horen all knew naught of what the great Devil had spoken of when concerning Malin’s betrayal. Dismissing it as the lies of a demon propagated to corrupt their souls,\nthe brothers thought nothing further of Malin’s supposed treason.\n\nThe robed figure stood before the four brothers.\n\n“There is nothing in my power that may undo what that evil did. There is one thing I may do however, and that is to bless you.\nMalin, may your forests be a sanctuary of peace and your children long lived.\n\nUrguan, may your descendants be hardy, strong hearted and strong of mind.\n\nKrug, may your people show valour and honour where none exist.\nAnd Horen, may your people one day explore the Seven Skies.\n\nI can do no more, for all my power is spent. We will go back to our master now, I believe your children may see us once more but long in the future.”\nAnd with that, the great host of Aenguls and Daemons disappeared into thin wisps in the air.", ""),
        StaticBook("Holy Scrolls -II", "Jacob Chapel", "The Holy Scrolls\n\n     The Book of\n     Horen\n\nTransscribed by Jacob Chapel during the Amber Cold, 1471.\n\nUse these words as a source of strength and widom.\nThe years passed and went on and on, as time is wont to do. The Decendant, after being cursed by the Great Devil, adapted their lives to suit their new roles. There was, for some time, peace and prosperity amongst the original realms created by the\nCreator. One day, upon the cusp of which a red sun rose from the east, King Horen of humanity was approached by an Aengul, a divine messenger of God. This Aengul shone magnificently, illuminated by the light of God, its shades and colours twisting\naround one another as it addressed Horen. Its wings swathed in blinding white, it opened its mouth and through it the Creator spoke.\n“Horen of Man. God has chosen you as his divine prophet, as his mouthpiece on this world, until the day of\nyour ascent into the Seven Skies at his order. You are the almighty king, the Creator’s chiefmost servant on this hallowed earth. Be jubilant, for you are second to none but me! Humanity is the holy divine being of God, the human body remaining the most\nunadulterated, original form of the Creator’s design, not possessing of neither corruption nor mutation. You are the chosen people, and you shall carry out my commands, and your people alone, not your brothers and their kin, shall swear to my commandments\nThey are as follows!\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, is the Creator and Guide of everything that has been created; He alone has made, does make, and will make all things.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Divine\nare the Creator’s regents in this realm and that their obedience is worship to the Creator.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Aenguls and Daemons are the Creator’s servants.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator\nBlessed be His Name, is One, and that there is no unity in any manner like His, and that He alone is our God, who was, and is, and will be.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, has no body, and that He is free from all\nproperties of matter, and that there can be no comparison to Him whatsoever.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, is the first and the last.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name,\nand to Him alone, it is right to pray, and that it is not right to pray to any being besides Him.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that all the words of the Divines are true.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the\nprophecy of Horen I our teacher, blessings be upon him, was true, and that he was the chief of the Divines, both those who preceded him and those who followed him.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the entire scrolls that is now in our possession is the\nsame that was given to our Divines, blessings be upon them.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Holy Scrolls can not be corrupted\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, knows all the deeds\nof beings and all their thoughts.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that the Creator, Blessed be His Name, rewards those who keep His commandments and punishes those that transgress them.\n\n-I believe with perfect faith that there will\nbe a revival of the dead at the time when it shall please the Creator, Blessed be His Name, and His mentions shall be exalted for ever and ever.”\n\nAnd so Horen listened, and he repeated the Creator’s words, and he carried the word\nof the Creator to his people, who listened as he did. They kneeled before Horen, first of the Divine, and pledged the commandments and supremacy of humanity over all but God. The realmn of man rallied underneath the Regent of Heven, arming themselves and\nerecting great fortresses, beginning the golden age of the Horen dynasty. For truly, it was decreed that humanity was second to none but the Creator, and the chose people would carry out his command until the end of time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Homosexual Sin", "Otto de Metz", "Homosexuality. Mental Disability, or mere choice? Firstly; in this small thesis; let's take a look at what homosexuality truly is. It is the attraction to a member of the same sex. Sex; not gender for those of Malin. My proposed theory is infact that\nhomosexuality is in fact; not a choice but a biological pre-set. Imposed upon effeminate males whom are more fem than masc, or masculine males who are more masc than fem, thus causing a confusion within their humours. The odd arrangement of sexual\ncharacteristics offputs the balance of their humours which then causes the humours to attempt to re-align, by causing a sexual 'shift'. This is to correct the confused body's perception of sexuality. Because; if a more masc than fem female appears; their\nbody will confusidly believe they are a male. This will offset the humours within their being; thus for re-assurance, the offset will cause the body to crave females instead; so that the sexual desire will cause a mental state that re-aligns the humours,\nand fixes the condition. The body will then sub-consciously believe it is of the opposite sex; and not a homosexual. Homosexuality is only a conscious concept; the homosexual himself has the illusion of choice based on mentality. Do you ever question if\ncraving the opposite sex is forced? You'd think you chose to chase them romantically. Thus, the homosexual himself believes that he or she has the illusory concept of sexual choice; not questioning if it is a biological impulse or not. Now; for as to why\nit is a disability. Firstly; we have defined that the physical offset and humouric offset causes a mental shift to fix it, we can say it afflicts the mind. So it is defined as a mental change. Then; we can define a disability as a lack or shortcoming of\nsomething. What would homosexuality disable, you may ask? The imperative desire to form a family to cause the next generation. Homosexuals however; feel no attraction to the appropriate gender and thus cannot pass their bloodline on; therefore having a\ndisability. Now if this affects the mind and is mental; and this is a lack or shortcoming of the ability to breed; a disability. Homosexuality is infact a forced disability based upon physical deformations of effemination on men and masculinity on females\nA natural correction caused by their body; that is condemned by GOD. This is a lifestyle that can be changed; and a sin caused by living the wrong lifestyle. Effemination or masculinity on the wrong gender is infact; voluntary. Thus, this is a involuntary\nmental disability caused by voluntary lifestyle choices. They do not choose to be homosexuals; but they choose to be deformed and cause it. A side-effect of sin, and a sin none-the-less.", ""),
        StaticBook("Honeysuckle Sun", "Indra Tresery", "Glistening, molten gold stares back as I\nlook up into your face, the feeling of warmth\nfills my soul with every breath.\nYour arms wrap me in layers of sweet\ncomfort and I close my eyes\nreveling in your warm golden touch,\nmy troubles forgotten.\nYour smile bathes my skin in light\nand I shiver from excitement, returning \nyour attention with delighted smiles and \ncarefree laughter.\nDuring times of trouble I could stay\nall day in your embrace, letting my\nfears and worries melt away \nwith one smile from you. \nThere are times I want to keep you to myself,\nto hide you away in our own little world forever, \nbut I cannot, your smiles and sweetness are\nnot just for me.\nThat worries me not, my love.\nFor I know that few moments a day we spend\nin each other’s embrace, that I am yours\nand you are mine:\n\nMy warm honeysuckle sun.", ""),
