        StaticBook("How to be succes", "Croesus Letholdus", "How to the hearts of the people \n\n\n william karduin didnt take out the trash becaues he was overencumbered with the sewing table he was repairing for a quick buck to spend at epicot studios where he would meet rap star drake aubrey graham and\nexch ange bodily \nfluids via saline solution as i write in this book abou t  an adventure i never went on william karduin sits in front of the fireplace trying to turn it on but he will not turn it on\ntabletop tucker is unaware of the obliging comrade that waits patiently for him to park his horse in the nearby oven water is vital and much needed for survival \n\n\n   y  e  s  t  e  r  d  a  y\n\ni \nwent for a walk acros\nfelsen \n         looking\n                   for\n                        a \n                          chap  \n                            his \n                         name\n                       was \n                      nelson\n\nnelson had just gotten in\na slimy predicament with a man noone would ever dare cross \n\nhe did it for a quick buck so he can take his shoe laces to the cobbler adam sandles richard shoelace ties shoelaces he is the ologmeister he   plays the game the game of life he walks line\non \n    \n\n\n\n\n           no \n   \n  \n\n                      mans\n\n                                  time\nthinking hes hip, thinking hes that thinking i dont make flapjacks in the morning along with some maple oat meal and six eggs with a banana and four strips of bacon for about 1,100 calories to start my day \n\nthen later i'll go the gym so i can train my\nphysique and not be ugly this way i can find a soulmate and settle down\n\nbuild a house\n\n       kill some orphans\n\nand worship chin chin\n16.9 fl oz (500 ml)\nofficial yogurt of the halflings", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Get Girls", "Amras Yeager", "How to get a girl.\n\nStep 1: If you haven't talked to her before the ask if she is new. If she says no I'm not new or something along the lines of that then you say \"Hmm I don't know how I wouldn't notice such a pretty face.\nStep 1 B: If she says that she is new then say \"Good 'cause I don't know how I would've missed such a pretty face.\nStep 2: Figure out if she has any problems like if she is sad because of something. Then comfort her and tell her it's alright.\nStep 3: Figure out what she likes and dislikes. This step might be time consuming but if you really want that girl it's worth it. Usually offering them cake is good 'cause a lot of people like cake.\nStep 4: Ask her on a date, stand up straight or she might not think well of you and think that you are a wimp. If she does accept then remember the things that she stresses with and give her good solutions to her problems and treat her to the things she\nlikes. Then continue until you have been on a few dates with her then you can propose to her. Good Luck!\n\n\nAuthor - Amras Yeager\n\nElsiln Athri and Katar Aureon help create this book.\nWARNING: \n\nMay not always work some girls are different!", ""),
        StaticBook("How to Shog", "Madeline Applefoot", "Shogging: An introduction\n\nWelcome there, reader of this book! I, Madeline Applefoot, would like to tell you how to do well in the halfling sport of shogging. While this guide is nay good enough to make someone a master, it'll at least get ye started\nTable o' Contents:\n\n1: What is shogging?\n2: How do I shog?\n3: Tips for shogging better.\n4: Ending\nChapter 1: What is shogging?\n\nShogging is a sport of the halflings involving two people balancing on floating logs trying to knock the other off their log with a wooden paddle, seems simple, right? It gets a bit more complex than that, however. Both\nparticipants must wear a pumpkin on their head at all times, which makes it harder to see and thus harder to hit your opponent off their log. You are also not allowed to jump from your log to the other's log, also known as the \"Herbwallow Hop\".\nChapter 2: How do I shog?\n\nIn order to shog, you must become one with the shog. Learn how to balance on the log without falling off, and learn how to use your paddle to knock your opponent off. Lastly, keeping a low posture (crouching) helps you balance!\nChapter 3: Tips for better shogging\n\nVelvet's Legs: Get out of your crouched position temporarily for a sudden burst of momentum across your log and towards your opponent! This takes practice, but is good when used right. Great for sudden jabs at your\nunlucky friend who'll soon be swimming to shore!\n\nDefensive Strategy: By staying towards the back of your log, you make it harder for your opponent to hit you off. This does prolong games, however.\n\nAgressive Stragety:\nby using Velvet's legs and other quick yet not too dangerous jabs at your opponent, you can catch them off guard and hopefully knock them off!\n\nSugarcane Shimmey: Just like the Velvet's Legs, but you move quickly to the side instead of quickly moving\ninto an agressive position on the edge of your shog. By moving so fast to the side, you can catch the opponent off guard and not be where he or she expects you to be!\n\nSlide Whistle: Instead of being agressive or Defensive, find out what position your\nopponent is in and do the opposite! This usually ends up with you and your opponent moving back and forth across your logs in rhythm to each other like some kinda ritualistic dance of shogging in order to avoid being caught off guard. Quite Fun!\nTricking!: In order to do some Tricking! on your opponent, pretend to be moving into a more agressive position while actually remaining mostly defensive. If your opponent moves up their log closer to you, Velvet's Leg 'em to catch them off guard in their\nforwards stance. If they stay defensive, keep on trying to Trick! them untill you either give up and try another stragety or untill they finally take the bait and advance.\nChapter 4: The End\n\nWell, this is the end of my introduction to shogging. I ended up writing more than I planned to, but that shouldn't be a problem! Madeline Applefoot, at yer service! Talk to me whenever if you need more tips on shogging! ((jumperhand3)", ""),
        StaticBook("Howl for Love", "Damien Menrow", "Silent scream under a grinning moon,\nsings out it's voiceless call.\n\nA hallowed ground echos its nearing doom,\nearth beneath catches your fall.\nBirds take flight to cry their fear,\nas the heart beats its final few.\n\nI think of the one that I hold dear,\nand howl for the love of you.\nLetters written with the sweetest musk,\nbirds carry your darkened lies.\n\nI wait for Dawn to give to Dusk,\nwhen the light fades and the shadows rise.\nMy sweetest sleeps in the ebony night,\nbut I feel you move to our lightened space.\n\nEncrouching on my loves kind sight,\nI'll make sure you will know your place.\nFollow your heart yet it leads you here,\nclutched tight and still after I'm through.\n\nThe silence is shattered by a cry so clear,\nas I howl for the love of you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Human History v3", "Bishop Cordal", "A History of Humanity From Aegis to Athera\nBy Lord Edward Winter II\nVolume III: The Second Age of Kings\nThe Second Age of Kings\n1422-1431\nOn the Continent of Anthos\nKings from the Houses of Horen, Carrion, Hightower, Elendil, Flay-Silverblade\nAlso known as: The Fractured Era, the Age of Five Kings, the Second Unrest, the First Dark Ages, the\nFirst Papal Intercession\n\nFollowing Salvus's betrayal and the disbanding of the empire, High Pontiff Goddard I claimed the dissolution of the empire had freed his territories from royal fealty, as they had been granted autonomy from direct\nrule when William took the throne. He claimed the Salvian-affiliated territory of Emperor's Forest (later formalized as the County of Kvaz in the second empire), and the Prince-Archbishopric of Savoie (composed of the County of Norfolk, Barony of\nAldersberg, Viscounty of Bar, and other minor territories) as independent of the Orenian crown. In a matter of months, the Dukes Charles Greymane of Corpathia and Siegmund Carrion of Raev also swore under the High Pontiff, who took the title Apostolic\nKing and subbed his realm the Holy Kingdom of Savoie. \n\nIn the east, the newly seceded Flay-Silverblade island Kingdom of Galahar was not as successful, and it dwindled in relevance as it faced government inefficiency, brutality, and mass emigration\nresulting from its disconnect with the Orenian mainland. It was soon forced to wild banditry in order to fund its expenditures. During this period, the Kings of Savoie, Adunia, and Oren took protectorate status under the Grand-King Thorin of the dwarven\nGrand Kingdom of Urguan in an effort to try and protect their borders from incursions by one another and the dwarven state. Despites this, Galahar continued its heavy raids until the Duke Siegmund Carrion brought the bandit-state under his command.\nThe Savoyard state was around this time then abdicated to Siegmund Carrion, who had been named heir apparent to the pontiff of Carrion blood, and the pontiff returned to matters of the faith.\n\nWhen the Grand-King of Urguan died, the human states were\nreleased from their protectorate status and were quickly at odds with one another. Renatus readied for war against Savoie's growing state, which had recently negotiated the absorption of Salvus and hte pagan nation of Adunia into its borders. The King of\nSavoie redubbed his state the Kingdom of Ruska, in reference to the culture of his people, the Raevirs.\n\nThreatened by the growth in land and power of Savoie, the King William III of Oren declared High Pontiff Goddard I excommunicated (citing the\ncaesareopapist reign of Horen V as legal precedent for state over church supremacy) in an effort to diminish the authority of the kingdom, and brought the nations of Ruska and Oren to the brink of war.\n\nThe Lord High Steward of Oren, Edward\nWinter II, met in secret with Goddard I, and the two negotirated terms contingent upon Edward's deposition of William and his gathering the support of other leading advisors and nobles. Goddard I and Edward II led a peaceful exchange of power from William\nIII to his cousin, Lord High Treasurer Silus I, who agreed to back the Ruskan-Winter agreement. Silus quickly assumed the throne and appointed countless Ruskan nobility in court positions. In thanks for his services, Edward was created King of Herendul,\nand given control of his former liege's, Duke Codrik Green of Hanseti, territories as his kingdom. Herendul, the Crownlands of Oren (now renamed Renatus), Ruska, and the weakened state of Salvus then combined into a loose confederacy governed by a\nconstitutional monarchy. King Silus then stepped down and abdicated to Otto Carrion, resulting in an imbalance of of the constitutional monarchy that ensured the election of Siegmund Carrion as Emperor of the Second Empire of Oren.", ""),
        StaticBook("Human History v4", "Bishop Cordal", "The History of Humanity from Aegis to Athera\nBy Lord Edward Winter II\nVolume IV: The Second Empire\nThe Second Empire\n1431-1447\nOn the Continent of Anthos\nEmperor Siegmund Carrion\nAlso known as: The Time of Crows, the Imperium Secundus\n\nThe Carrions emerged from the Second Age of Kings in command of humanity, and did so\nwithout interruption for several years. Siegmund's rule began with the systematic execution and seizure of property by Otto and Tuv Carrion from all of the first empire nobles that remained loyal to House Horen, wiping the slate clean for a new\nRaevir-dominated nobility. His reign was a quiet one, and primarily foccused on rebuilding a unified state after the Second Age of Kings. There was a short rebellion by Empress-claimant Sophia Horen, who was backed by several disenfranchised nobles of the\nFirst Empire, but it fell into disorder after a year. \n\nAnother rebellion followed, led by descendants of Eze'kiel Tarus, the Teutonic Order, and dwarves who challenged the Carrion's right-to-throne in open rebellion.\nSeveral prominent families of the First Empire also joined Horen and Tarus. The House Stafyre was almost pushed into joining when then-High Pontiff, who styled himself High Ecclesiarch Radomir I, nearly flogged a Stafyr for defending a heretic. However,\nthe Stafyrs were persuaded to back the empire, and their castle was used to garrison Orenian troops bolstered by the Church's Order of Saint Lucien in a victorious defense against the rebel coalition.\n\nIt was not too many years later that the\nEmperor Siegmund Carrion died of age, and in his will dissolved the second empire into its constituent states of the Kingdom of Oren and the Kingdom of Herendul.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hunting Codex", "Thorvn Bronwyn", "--------oOo--------\n\n The Beginners Guide\n        \n      To Hunting In \n\n           Atlas,\n\n\n  By Thorvn Bronywn\n\n\n\n--------oOo-------\n--------oOo--------\n\nTable of Contents:\n\nIntroduction Pg 3\n\nGear Pgs 4-6\n\nBeastiary Pgs 7-21\n\nGeneral tips Pgs 22-27\n\nMinas! Pgs 28-32\n--------oOo--------        Introduction\n\n If you are reading this, then you wish to     be a hunter nae? \n\n Tired of getting yer arse handed to you on  every single hunt?\n\n THEN LOOK NAE FURTHER THAN THIS!\n--------oOo-------\n--------oOo--------      Gear consulting\n\n For fighting most within Atlas, one must be very careful of ones surroundings, yer armor must not be too light to take blows while nae heavy to prevent mobility, one must find a balance with medium styled -\narmor (iron armor for example)\n\nAnd a well shaped shield to defect the multitude of projectiles beasts may have at their disposal, be it poison, barbs, bladed quills, feathers, even arrows from fellow man. One must be prepared properly to survive-\nthis cruel world we call Atlas.\n\nBlades are standardly kept sharp and without rust, to survive this harsh world one must be at top shape, this also applies to their weapons, don't be afraid to take extra, theres no shame in being prepared.\n--------oOo----\n--------oOo--------        Beastiary\n\nBoggens PG 10\n\nBog Beasts PG 11\n\nBilespitters PG 12\n\nBoars PG 13\n\nBandits PG 14\n\nDirewolves PG 15\n--------oOo-------- Gravens PG 16\n\nHarpies PG 17\n\nMinotaurs PG 18\n\nNullers PG 19\n\nRogue Golems PG 20\n\nMirror Slimes PG 21\n\n--------oOo-------\n--------oOo--------         Add future \n Content here: Beasts\n--------oOo--------          Boggens\n\n These creatures are deceptive, use wisps to lure in prey (exp) and attack with no warning, best bring a friend, because these are near lethal to any unsuspecting target, caution advised.\n\n--------oOo-------\n--------oOo--------         Bog Beasts\n  \n   Near undead like swamp creatures, upon death they release a toxic mist, avoidable with enough caution, bring the beasts within the water to make the situation managable, low threat.\n\n--------oOo-------\n--------oOo--------\n        Bilespitters\n\n Spiders that entrap their victims within webbing and shoot toxic substance to wear them down from afar, these beasts are to be fought with ranged weaponry, beware their numbers, moderate threat.\n--------oOo--\n--------oOo--------        Boar/Treeboar\n\n   Piggies, in short these mounds of bacon are fast and hit swift, bring them over river to get an edge, tree boars are to be strictly used with arrows, they, are, DEADLY. Moderate threat.\n--------oOo-------\n--------oOo--------           Bandits\n   \n    Man gone sour, these pilfering humanoids use axe and bow, bring your own friends to combat these evil briggands, search for the fabeled berserker axe.  Moderate threat \n--------oOo-------\n--------oOo--------         Direwolves\n  \n    Violent pups that depend on swarm tactics to overwhelm their target, fast, hard hitting, and deadly, these beasts need to be in water to cripple, beware the vibrant howl, high threat.\n--------oOo--------\n--------oOo--------          Gravens\n    \n    Spectral beings of bone and corruption, shields are useless against piercing arrows, usually found in pairs, these beasts spawn vex's upon death, beware of their fast movement as well. Moderate threat.\n-------\n--------oOo--------           Harpies\n  \n   Humanoid avian shaped creatures with a desire for flesh, they bolt upon being hit, soar into the air and shower their target with bladed feathers, shield HIGHLY advised. Moderate threat.\n--------oOo-------\n--------oOo--------          Minotaurs\n   \n     Hulking bovine humanoid hybrids that overwhelm with charging force that launches targets into the air, shield advised to block the hit, along with a-lot of men.\n EXTREMELY HIGH THREAT\n--------oOo-------\n--------oOo--------           Nullers\n\n       Small, but make up in modest number that use neurotoxin to take down their targets, armor is useless against them,  beware stage 3 of toxin, reccomend kiting tactics, low-moderate threat.\n--------oOo-------\n--------oOo--------       Rogue Golems\n \n Constructs gone Awol, these beings are to be put down with modest ease, multiple blades reccomended, so is armor, beware of seeping magic that causes you to levitate on hit, seek higher ground.Modest threat\n------\n--------oOo--------      Mirror Slimes\n     (Spiegelschleim)\n  \n  Germatic myth, these slimes upon death mimic their killer be it full armor or not, bring friends, they reflect full damage upon their image if struck by them.  Modest-high threat.\n-----\n--------oOo--------       General advice\n\n-When fighting nullers, encircle the swarm and use swords to chip them down, they're much weaker taken in that manner.\n\n-When fighting golems, kite downhill compared to upward, if struck by magic, you'll have a -\n--------oOo--------much better time surviving, bring multiple swords too, they go surprisingly fast.\n\n-When fighting Direwolves bring them to water, their numbers don't mean shite when they can barely swim as a pack.\n--------oOo--------\n--------oOo--------\n\n-When fighting Bandits, theres a rare chance to get a berserker axe as a drop, this does more damage than an iron sword, yet lowers your armor, it's a double sided weapon.\n\n-When combating Gravens, consider-\n--------oOo-------- using arrows against them, they have a habit of moving away in Melee distance.\n\n-When fighting boars, beware of the trees, they tend to hide up there.. for some odd reason.\n\n-Fighting bilespitters is as simple to fighting -\n--------oOo--------spiders, only they spit toxins and are much more suspectable to ranged fire.\n\n-Consider using different tomes at Cloud temple, Huntress's codex for more damage while luck be a lady for better drop chance  -\n--------oOo--------\n\nAlong with Kips lucky pebble, it'll make rare drops that much more common, T'was a fleshwound for extra bleedout time, 20 seconds makes all the more difference.\n\n(Not dying for dummies optional.)\n--------oOo-------\n--------oOo--------       Making Minas\n\n Aye, the real part of the guide, one doesn't become a hunter without knowing what's the most profitable aye?  In short, theres only a specific list of profit with hunting, the rest are insignificant.\n--------oOo---\n--------oOo--------  \n   -Nullers \n\n   Their drops are normally very profitable and common,  8 minas per common drop and 150 per rare gland, they're awfully nice, for such a low threat monster, beware of crowding!\n--------oOo-------\n--------oOo--------           \n\n   -Bandits\n\n   Usually with cordinated effort their drops are 'normally' profitable, one can sell or buy a berserker axe within Haense for 750/1000\nMinas respectively.\n--------oOo-------\n--------oOo--------      \n\n    -Rogue golems\n\n    Their main drop being more rare than secondary, 100 minas is no joke, along with the bundles of iron (16) and scrap additions, this is a secondary profit from nullers.\n--------oOo--------\n     -Direwolves?\n\n   Subjective, but when lead to water these puppies are helpless, be sure to collect EVERY drop, heads are a good sum, so are teeth. 80/10 pelts are only 2 but come with great abundance.\n\n--------oOo-------\n--------oOo--------        Conclusion\n\n   If followed many steps, one should be rolling in Minas as a successful hunter, the tomes may be expensive but in the longrun that much more worth the risk.\nRemember, friends make every hunt better!\n--------oOo----\n--------oOo--------\n\n Book by: Jdesarno/\n\n   Thorvn Bronwyn\n\n    Original topic: https://www.lordofthecraft.net/forums/topic/175132-feedback-on-hunting-and-its-issues/\n\nMade 8/11 !", ""),
        StaticBook("Hunting Season", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Set up a series of traps in the forest inorder to try and fight the beasts.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hydromancy", "Rosso", "Water: seemingly the simplest of elements, and yet incredibly complex. Water is a necessity of live, needed by all living things, plants and beasts alike. Just as it is the patron of life, water can also pose as the harbinger of eradication.\nDespite our best attempts; we are mortal. A single wave can take everything we own. A flood can contaminate food. A particularly harsh winter can be inescapable. Water contains raw power, a power that a hydromance yearns to wield.\nA hydromancer's training stems from the evocation and control of water itself but not the water that we know. This water can only be found in the void and some say it is not water at all. As all evocationists know, their power comes from the ability\nto control \"mana,\" but I'll leave that topic for others to discuss. After much dedication and training, a hydromancer is able to pull mana directly from the void, shaping it into a water-like substance in our world. This connection to the void is\ndifficult to put into words, as connecting to the void is more of a sensation than something that can be explained. As a mage's training progresses, connecting to the void and evoking the mana within it become more simpler tasks.\nMany mages use a staff when evoking the elements, but the truth is that the staff is not necessary. I, for instance, use a staff topped in mage-gold and carved from elderly jungle wood. This staff is fitting for me because of some of the properties\nthat is possesses, and also because it has been personalized for me. The purpose of my use of a staff is to create a simple, close point for me to concentrate on and evoke water from. When the water is pulled forth, it forms a stream from the end of my\nstaff that maintains itself midair. From here, I can move it, project is somewhere, or allow it to dissipate.\n\nOne thing about water evocation that differs from the other branches of evocation is that water can change states in our world. Novice\nwater evocationists begin with controlling pure water in its liquid form. As a hydromancer becomes more skilled ((approximately late tier 3)), he is able to change the water into ice. Ice is much more suited for battle and defence than liquid water is,\nas it can be used to create walls, freeze doors shut, block oncoming projectiles, as a form of short-distance defense, and as a method of harming others. I have personally mastered a technique of blasting an enemy with water, and then freezing\nthem in their tracks should they be hit. Magical ice is not like that which can be found in our world; void ice does not melt from the heat of the sun or a torch. To break void ice, the hydromance must either completely lose concentration, or another\nmage must do something to break the ice (i.e. a pyromancer melts the ice with magical flames). Water is not often formed into the vapor state, as the wisps of steam are too difficult for even the most trained evocationists to control.\nWater, being able to form any conceivable shape, is only limited by the caster's imagination and fatigue. With proper training, water can be suited for nearly any purpose.\nIntroduction to Hydromancy\n\nWritten by Ev Ar'ahern\nCopied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((15/6/13))", "")
    )

    private fun _ATLAS_3(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Hydromancy", "Thurak'Yar", "Hydromancy\n\nWater appears of one of the simplest elements that inhabit our world, but it is in fact incomprehensively more complex that most people think it is. To fully understand it, one must practice large amounts of time meditating,\nand indeed spending their time around said element- be it by lounging around by a pond, or studying its properties profusely in laboratories. Water is a necessity of life, needed by all living and sentient things, for example Humans, Orcs, Dwarves,\nKharajyr, Elves and also various other animals or plants. Water, also appearing as such a calm element, is also one of the more dangerous; out in the seas, a storm can take out a fleet of ships within moments. One can never fully control\nwater that isn’t evocated, unless of course one is a shaman- In which case the Spirits control the element, and in-avertedly the shaman controls the water too. Despite out best attempts, we are all mortal; we do not live forever, nor do we have amazing\npower like the ascended or the undead back in Aegis. As said before, water can be a very dangerous element; a single flood can wipe out a village just as easily as it might cause it to flourish. The element water contains raw power; a power\nthat all Hydromancers would wish to wield. A Hydromancer’s training consists of learning about the Void, being able to evocate from it, and learning about their element so they can properly evocate it. It takes years on end to learn about evocating a\nsingle element. Water which has been evocated may appear to be the same as the water we have around us, however it is completely different. The water that us Hydromancers evocate can only be created in the void and can brought forth into\nthis world by ourselves. Mana, or life-force, is the power we use to create and transport water from the void, and is vital in most, if not every known magic. If one uses too much of this mana, then they would simply fall unconscious or even die before\nthey complete their task due to overuse or too much exerted force after large amounts of dedication and training; such as learning about the void and Hydromancy, and shaping and creating their mana into an interpretation of water.\nThe connection to the void is rather difficult to explain, however; though once one has learnt about Hydromancy itself then they should be able to understand where we are coming from. One’s connection to the void is more of a sensation than something\nthat can be explained- Like feeling happy, or in love. As a mage’s training progresses, connecting to the void and evocating elements becomes a simpler task. As one would possibly notice, many mages use a staff when they’re casting their magic-\nThis however, is not necessary at all, and only aids the magician by giving them something to focus on while evocating. Water can be evocated in various forms, such as a jet of water, an orb of water, an orb of ice, and other things I have not\ngenerally experimented on yet. Hydromancers which have been learning for a long time will be able to use more things and will be able to explore completely different aspects of the element. Ice is more suitable for offence in a battle, rather\nthan defence, however, generally water evocation itself is more useful to protect the caster, as walls of water or ice can be willed to block a projectile or a strike, or simply to intercept and deflect one,though such must be done at short distance.\nIce that we evoke isn’t the same that we find in our world naturally; it cannot be melted by the heat of the sun or a torch, but it can be melted with the use of Pyromancy. To break the ice, the Hydromancy must both lose connection to the void and have\ntheir creation dissipate, or have a Pyromancer melt it with their fire, or, in the later stages of their training, with steam. \nWater, being able to form any conceivable shape, is only limited to the caster’s imagination and fatigue, and with\nProper training it can be suited for any purpose.\n\n~The Mage Adorellan", ""),
        StaticBook("Hydromancy", "[Elder] Thurak'Yar", "Water\n\nWater appears of one of the simplest elements that inhabit our world, but it is in fact incomprehensively more complex that most people think it is. To fully understand it, one must practice large\namounts of time meditating, and indeed spending their time around said element- be it by lounging around by a pond, or studying its properties profusely in laboratories. Water is a necessity of life, needed by all living and sentient things,\nfor example Humans, Orcs, Dwarves, Kharajyr, Elves and also various other animals or plants. Water, also appearing as such a calm element, is also one of the more dangerous; out in the seas, a storm can take out a fleet of ships within moments.\nOne can never fully control water that isn’t evocated, unless of course one is a shaman- In which case the Spirits control the element, and in-avertedly the shaman controls the water too. Despite out best attempts, we are\nall mortal; we do not live forever, nor do we have amazing power like the ascended or the undead back in Aegis. As said before, water can be a very dangerous element; a single flood can wipe out a village just as easily as it might cause it to flourish.\nThe element water contains raw power; a power that all Hydromancers would wish to wield. A Hydromancer’s training consists of learning about the Void, being able to evocate from it, and learning about their element so they can properly evocate it.\n. It takes years on end to learn about evocating a single element. Water which has been evocated may appear to be the same as the water we have around us, however it is completely different. The water that us Hydromancers evocate can only\nbe created in the void and can brought forth into this world by ourselves. Mana, or life-force, is the power we use to create and transport water from the void, and is vital in most, if not every known magic. If one uses too much of this mana,\n, then they would simply fall unconscious or even die before they complete their task due to overuse or too much exerted force after large amounts of dedication and training; such as learning about the void and Hydromancy, and shaping and creating\ntheir mana into an interpretation of water. The connection to the void is rather difficult to explain, however; though once one has learnt about Hydromancy itself then they should be able to understand where we are coming from. One’s\nconnection to the void is more of a sensation than something that can be explained- Like feeling happy, or in love. As a mage’s training progresses, connecting to the void and evocating elements becomes a simpler task. As one would possibly notice, many\nmages use a staff when they’re casting their magic- This however, is not necessary at all, and only aids the magician by giving them something to focus on while evocating. Water can be evocated in various forms, such as a jet of water, an orb of water,\nan orb of ice, and other things I have not generally experimented on yet. Hydromancers which have been learning for a long time will be able to use more things and will be able to explore completely different aspects of the element.\nIce is more suitable for offence in a battle, rather than defence, however, generally water evocation itself is more useful to protect the caster, as walls of water or ice can be willed to block a projectile or a strike, or simply to\nintercept and deflect one, though such must be done at short distance. Ice that we evoke isn’t the same that we find in our world naturally; it cannot be melted by the heat of the sun or a torch, but it can be melted with the use of Pyromancy.\nTo break the ice, the Hydromancy must both lose connection to the void and have their creation dissipate, or have a Pyromancer melt it with their fire, or, in the later stages of their training, with steam.\nWater, being able to form any conceivable shape, is only limited to the caster’s imagination and fatigue, and with proper training it can be suited for any purpose.\n~Adorellan", ""),
        StaticBook("Hymn of Fat Monk", "Pius", "All men are sinners and all men sin,\nThe Monk's greatest sin is no longer being thin;\n\nO' Creator, my Lord, I have found a great truth,\nAll sins plague, but mostly in youth;\nGluttony and Sloth, Wrath and Envy,\nThe pairs of evil,\nsins most deadly,\n\nEnvy and Wrath, sins for those with worldly desires,\nSomething to gain, this makes honest men turn liars;\nSloth and Gluttony, sins for those who hate labor,\nYet all monks must study, praying to love thy neighbor,\nAll men are sinners, and all men sin,\nThe Monk's greatest sin is no longer being thin;\n\nThe monk chews and swallows, a necessity for life,\nThe art of eating is everyone's delight;\nHowever, in study, when the monk does not move,\nHis belly grows large, and GOD disapproves.\n\nAll men are sinners, and all men sin,\nThe Monk's greatest sin is no longer being thin;\n\nRepent my brothers, reject the temptation,\nTo be devout is to hold moral reservation;\nMove about and spread GOD's good word,\nEnsure that the Scrolls, to all beings, are without a doubt heard.\n\nBy moving with haste and by preaching with a smile,\nYour fat decreases, and to GOD, you pass your trial;\nWork at quelling one's sins so the seven skies you may greet,\nThen you may show the present and the future, the obstacles you have beat,\n\nAll men are sinners, and all men sin,\nThe Monk's greatest sin is no longer being thin.", ""),
        StaticBook("I hoarded it all", "Ri'Zinawr", "", ""),
        StaticBook("I'm Sorry!", "Daena", "Dear Aldia\nI am so sorry for what I did I was just trying to make sure you didnt get hurt I am so sorry I didnt stay and I hope you can forgive me\n\n\n\n\n-Daena", ""),
        StaticBook("Iblees, the 2nd", "Zafirah", "The Second Coming\n       Of Iblees\n           &\nThe Rise Of Ascended\nIblees was sealed away after the first Aegis crisis. The fallen Arch Daemon had remained in the nether for hundreds, if not thousands of years afterwards. The exact timeline of such being lost and forgotten throughout the numerous years that passed.\nDuring this time, the four races of Aegis had found mostly peace. Dark, Wood and High Elves all lived within the city known as Laurelin, no such conversations went about of 'purity' or pedigree. The same was said about the Humans, Dwarves and Orcs. All\nhaving respect and allowing each their own space amongst the lands without majoir conflicts arising. It was plainly beautiful how this had transpired over the many years following Iblees' imprisonment.\nThough over this spanning of time, the seals and magic that kept the Arch Daemon at bay becan to weaken and break down by times inevitable grasp. And so it came to happen. Iblees had broken his bonds. Instead of taking on a full scale assault like\nhe had previously, his twisted mindset became to usher out a more tactical plan, laying low and silently recruiting followers to his the chaotic cause he so wished to display upon the mortals. Only when his devout had grown largely in numbers.\nDid Iblees finally send out those he had taught to create dark rifts that direclt flowed into the Nether. A realm of eternal ash and overwhelming heat. Here he ripped the very followers souls from their bodies and rended them into a twisted form of\nwhat they once were. His followers, once emerging from the Nether were changed, physically as with their souls. The first to be brought into undeath. Their own minds fully given to the Fallen One too.\nThey manipulated and cast forth dark magics, able to summon the very fires of the Nether, and cursed lightning from the skies. Capable of obliterating anything they collided into with ease. A true force of destruction these beings were.\nEven the ancient Liches of this era were no match to the undead of Iblees. \nThe undead soon fell upon outlaying towns and burnt them to the ground, leaving only chaos and destruction in their wake from pre-calculative strikes.\nLeaving many loved ones of famlies missing, or worse.\nAs the Undead grew in strength, and paranoia washed over Aegis. The descendants gathered and lashed out where they could retaliate against them. The descendant's numbers were the only thing that\ngave the mortals a slight advantage, though the cost was always high. Many were left wounded and slain in the wake of every battle. At this time, the Archaengul Aerial had watched the plague that had spread throughout the mortal lands.\nThe Undead were strong, though it came at a heavy price of the souls that were tormented and enslaved by Iblees. Aerial herself then sought out to create a counter to battle the blight known as the Undead.\nThough without damaging the soul of a descendant of course. Aerial then becan to gather followers to her own alignment. And with this, the first of the Ascended were created from her graceful abilities.\nLed by a council of Sages, they were very powerful. Their ranks, or sects were Red, Blue, Purple, Green, Orange and Gold. In this time, their numbers soared and they even had their own city to match such a size. Haven was it's name.\nThey were able to make counter measures and strike back at the Undead of Iblees. They worked along with the Descendents too in the efforts to push back teh abominational creatures that served the Fallen One.\nThough over time, the Sages, gifted with emense power began to fall into a tired mindset from constant warring, also their pride affected them greatly too. In an instant, the great city of Haven vanished from the mortal realm.\nAbandoning the descendents as the soulstream itself swallowed up the Sages and followers alike. But only a few Ascended that lingered behind. Content on staying to see the war to it's bitter end.\nThe remaining numbers were led by a woman, Preceptor Shoi was her name. At this time, one of the descendent cites had began to crumble to the war that degraded its fortifications. The kingdom of men, Alk'hazar went first.\nThen fell the Dwarvan city, Sanhar. Any who were luck enough to evade the destructive wave that washed over the remaining forces of mortals fled to Laurelin. The mortals then fought with everything they had to hold this location, as it was the last.\nThough with the constant battling outside the city, those who fell, were raised into undeath also. Only supplying Iblees' own will. The darkness moved to swallow up Laurelin. As those left alive knew the end was not far off.\nIt was then, the brillient thinking of Shoi, who had gathered up a remarkable plan, then sset it into motion. Being trained on crafting artifacts of great power by the Sages, she devised to gather the remaining powers of the Ascended.\nAfterpooling theirs all together, they used Shoi as a conduit to create such artifacts. Thus, allowing a few descendent champions to challenge the undead in their own realm, the Nether. As the Undead opened a portal to such.\nThe champions rushed in, adorned with blessed weapons and gear that protected them from such a hostile envirnment. Noone truly knows what transpired within,  except for those who traveled inside. One thing is certain, they had slain all in their path.\nIn time, they returned from the hellish portal, home once more from what cannot be fully described. In their return though, the victory was short lived. Aegis was literally tainted by the corruptive touch of the Nether.\nAnd it slowly becan to cause the great lands to crumble under earthquakes, floods and tsunamis. Ripping and tearing at the land mass as it fell apart and sinking into the ocean. All the survivors began to rush and gather onto ships.\nAs it was the only thing to do, other than sink to a watery doom. They thankfully survived in search for a new land to call home. They eventually arrived to Asulon. With this, the Ascended found their powers had fled away completely.\nThough Aerial had given them a final blessing, the gift of immortality. The descendents went about life again, things slowly got back on track and the remaining Ascended slipped into the shadows of time.\nWaiting and watching if ever Aerial had need of them again.  \n\n\nThe document read here was recorded by Zafirah with the direct information given by Master Sage Heial.\n\n\nMay Aerial Guide You.", ""),
        StaticBook("icomplete alch", "Ambis", "Greater Salve of Frost Vine\n\nT3: Frost Vine\n\nA salve made from Frost Vine, with Aqua Vitae as a base. Numbs the area poured on and is good for burn wounds.\nGreater Salve of Mandragora\n\nT3: Mandragora\n\nA salve made from Mandragora, with Aqua Vitae as a base. It has great tissue healing properties.\nGreater Salve of Serpent's Stalk\n\nT3: Serpent's Stalk\n\nA salve made from Serpent's Stalk, with Aqua Vitae as a base. Lessens pain in burns and helps with its healing.\nGreater Salve of Athin\n\nT3: Athin\n\nA salve made from Athin, with Aqua Vitae as a base. It has great cooling properties.\nGreater Drake's Poison\n\nT3: Drake's Tail\n\nA powerful poison that induces a dangerous fever to those who are unfortunate to consume it.\nGreater Dwarf's Pumpkin Ale\n\nT3: Dwarf's Pumpkin\n\nBetter drinks than Dwarf's Pumpkin only exist to a lot of people. It's very spicy and very sour. Great flavor for a drunken night out.\nGreater Blood Soup\n\nT3: Blood Lotus\n\nEver wanted to live on nothing but liquid for the rest of your life?\nHere is your answer. One vial can provide you with a days worth of energy.\nGreater Flamespitter\n\nT3: Flametongue Root\n\nA salve made from Flametongue Roots, with Aqua Vitae as a base. Quickly closes a bleeding wound, while burning the area intensively.\nGreater Salve of Larihei\n\nT3: Larihei's Fingers\n\nA salve made from Larihei's Fingers, with Aqua Vitae as a base. It makes your movements more delicate.\nGreater Salve of Halfling's Grass\n\nT3: Halfling's Grass\n\nA salve made from Halfling's Grass, with Aqua Vitae as a base. Works almost like a drug, making the drinker feel more relaxed.\nGreater Elf's Hair Infusion\n\nT3: Elf's Hair Vine\n\nAn infusion made from Elf's Hair, with Aqua Vitae as a base. It makes you appear more graceful after consumption.\nGreater Crouching Feather Infusion\n\nT3: Crouching Feather\n\nAn infusion made from Crouching Feather, with Aqua Vitae as a base. It makes you more capable to jump higher than before.\nBurn Healing Salve\n\nT3: Frost Vine, Serpent's Stalk\n\nMurky green slush that moves slowly inside the vial. Upon application, your skin tingles, cooling slowly.\nChillblain Potion\n\nT3: Frost Vine, Athin\n\nGrey, frosty scales of condensation cover the glass of the vial, blocking your view inside. Upon application, your skin chills to an icy blue, growing cold and hard.\nFreezing Salve\n\nT3: Athin, Serpent's Stalk\n\nAlmost freezing to the touch, this salve may allow you to pass through the hot climates of the world.\nBoggy Concoction\n\nT3: Mandragora, Serpent's Stalk\n\nThis swampy brew adds a soothing sensation to the areas in which it is administered.", ""),
        StaticBook("Idk what this is", "Aldur Roderick", "The Golden Stag Smithy Request Form:\n\nUsername:\nName:\nItem:\nMaterials:\nSpecifics:\n\nUsername: Shuggie\nName: Denis\nItem: Sword Cane\nMaterials: Iron Handle and Sword", ""),
        StaticBook("IDK!", "Umar Ibn Salem the 'Bloodied Hand'", "The Drifter VOL 1 \n\nC.1 \n When you open your eyes in the morning, breathing, knowing your alive, and if you realise your privlaged for such events, you have seen what this life has done to good folk. Let me tell you, of this boy. This story dear\nreader, is a story of a boy who had it all. \n\nC.2 \n \"John, wake up!\" a womans voice was heard before young Johnny awoke. \"You have to help your father on the farm, Here drink this goat milk.\" She told John. \"Ok mother.\" John tolf her with a slightly\nannoyed tone. \"Hurry up, the day has just started.\" She nudged him to pace himself. \"Ok, ok, ill be down when im ready.\" he exclaimed. *John walks down the steps and to the door* \"Father! Im here to help.\" John says walking out. \"Oh, John go feed the\nchickens, After that come help me with removeing weeds from our crops.\" Johns dad orderd. \"Ok father, ill make haste\" John said. \"No child, do it at your pace, you will not miss any steps that way.\" Johns dad lectured. \"Right, father.\" An hour later, John\napproaced his father with the news. \"Father! Where do you reside?\" John yelled out. No answer. John runs around his yard everywhere. He decided to look inside. When John walked in his home he seen his father hit the floor. And a man, with a knife, covered\nand dripping with blood. John went silent then took the cane of his grandfather, breaks it and impales the stranger. As the stranger falls turning, he looks John in the eyes and says \"Im your real dad, John.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Ill return", "Co Co", "Dear Nami,\n\nI am heading out for a few days... Old memories have caught up with the present, and I need to sort it out. I will return to you safely in a couple of days.\n\nI love you,\n\nCo Co", ""),
        StaticBook("Illusion Theory", "Valmir Audane", "Basic Information:\n\nGlamour: The illusionary alteration of the previous characteristics of an already existing physical object.  A basic glamour would be the changing of the color of an object.\nOne could change the color of a red ball without too much experience, or change the color of their eyes.  Both of these illusions would be brief at first, however it is the best introductory to the field of illusion as the concept of projected imagery is\nreinforced and given a solid shape as the budding illusionist continues to practice.\nFigment: A figment is a fully illusionary object that is created by the mage and serves useful for a variety of situations.  While a Glamour can alter a previously existing  by extending a sword for example a Figment can create it’s own complete sword.\nWith progression Figments can become readily available for more diverse and detailed illusions meanwhile allowing the illusionist to hold them for longer periods of time.\nPhantasm: A phantasm is an illusionary emotion that is brought on by an illusionist.  These would include feelings as simple as simple as hunger or sadness to things as complex as anxiety, shame, guilt, and pride.\nThis field of illusion is by far the most advanced and difficult to master and to even use.  Every phantasm must be logical as the instant feeling of dread will be easily dispelled by the will power of the recipient.\nThe creation and projection of an illusion can be simply described through the following steps.\n\nConnect to void> Create illusion in Void> Push illusion into a mind> Mind then accepts or denies the illusion.\nAt an early stage void connection should start with one figment such as a small  light source. This is the most basic of all and will help the budding illusionist not only grow comfortable with connecting to the void but also understanding the abstract\nmethodology needed to grasp this field of magic.\n\nAfter some time of practice the illusionist should start work with the senses, all senses.  Start learning touch, smell, sound and taste.\nOnce they’ve done that they’ll be true amateurs. Their illusions which will start breaking as the student can’t hold all the senses at once due to lack of practice and focus.\nAn illusionist might be able to hold a simple disguise at this level of talent for roughly five minutes if they avoid interaction with other objects and people.\nAfter several years all senses will be relatively mastered so illusions will hold much longer and be more effective in use and in mana consumption.  At this time disguises will become practical and stable.\nAt this stage an illusionist would have the ability to accurately reenact most sensations that they are familiar with.  A practitioner of illusion could slowly begin to develop the ability to cast a dual illusion.\nThis would allow the illusionist to hold two separate entities of light illusion, such as a glamour of turning herself into an extension of a book case, while another of her walking about the room.\nExample, A mage walks into a bar with a parrot on his shoulder. The Bartender says; “Hey, where’d you get that?” and the parrot says “Wyvernhymn, they’ve got them all over the place.”\nThis terrible joke is an example of a moderately experienced illusionist’s power. The illusion can be made to interact with basic things, move and speak on the fly, and incorporate multiple senses at the same time.\nSound (The voice) and sight (The parrot) being the key in the crude jest, but one could likely incorporate up to four and even all five with a great expenditure of mental energy.\n*Several pages have either fallen out of the tome or have been removed. While what is left may be a helpful resource to a practicing illusionist the tome lacks sufficient detail as to how the illusions are created in the void and therefore would not aid-\nanyone without a grasp of the essentials of the magic.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Immortal Spirits", "Thurak'Yar", "Immortal Spirits\n\nA list of the Greater Spirits inhabiting the Immortal Realm and what they represent. This may change, given time, and will be updated as new spirits come to power.\nVotar- The spirit of the hunt, commonly shown as a giant, bloodied wolf. Praised by the Phrase Glougaz Votar.\n\n      /\\_==_/\\\n      | /o   o\\ |\n      \\         /\n       \\       /\n        \\ *.* /\n          \\ /\nEnrohk- The spirit of bloodlust, savagery and war, often shown as a bastard sword covered in blood. \n        \n         /\\\n         |  |\n         |  | \n         |....|\n         |. .|\n      `==8=='\n          ||\nShezept- The spirit of revenge, plots and stealth, depicted as a woman with a lower body of a snake. \n      \n        O\n       -|-\n   ^\\_\\\\_\n   \\____/\nJevex- Spirit of order, hard work and self sacrifice, shown as a giant hammer. He's a deadly enemy to the spirit Shezept.\n \n     [======]\n     [==|  |==]\n         ==\n         ==\n        |.--.|\n         ==\nIxli- The spirit of forbidden knowledge, truth and judgement. Depicted as an eye, he provides knowledge as the cost of sanity. \n\n       |/  \\|\n      |  (.)  |\n       |\\  /|\nOgrol- Spirit of despair, sapped strength and entrapement, shown as a cage full of writhing bodies. He tries to lock up all who summon him.\n\n       ______\n       | | |  | | |\n       =<< >>=\n       | | |  | | |\n      ========\nKor- The spirit of the dead, depicted as a cloaked man with an open hand.\n          _\n          |O\\\n           |-''\n          /\\\nAnkrus- Spirit of the sea, fishermen and safe travels, often shown as an aquatic woman wielding a spear. \n\n           () |\n           oo/\n           \\/\n           /\\\n           \\/\nArwa- Spirit of fertility, harvest and farming, commonly shown as a plump female with over seven hundred breasts.\n \n           ()\n         /.oo.\\\n        /o.oo.o\\\n        |o.o.o.o.o|\n        \\_____/\n         [|]    [|]\nAnyhuluz- Spirit of destruction, malicious intent and internal strife, shown as a warrior covered in open wounds.\n\n         O   ^\n       /(`)-`|\n         [|]\n         /\\\nAkezo- Spirit of health, vitality and healing, depicted as a winged whale surrounded by a blue aura.\n\n   (\\./)\n     \\\\_/--^--.\n      =.    \"~\"   )\n        \\______/\nPaxahru- Spirit of arrogance and stupidity, depicted as a boasting fool.\n\n        /**\\\n       ( ^^ ) \n        /--\\ \n        |`~~'|\n        ====\n        \\/\\/\n         |   |\nUblulhar- Spirit of hope an new beginnings, shown as a tree sapling bursting from the ground. \n\n       _____\n      {~~~~}\n     {~~~~~}\n      {~~~~}\n       {~| |~}\n          | |\n       ~~~~~\nGhorza- Spirit of travel, depicted as an ever turning wheel.\n\n       /----\\\n      / /--\\ \\\n      |  |<:::::)|  |\n      \\ \\--/ /\n       \\----/\nRolfizh- Spirit of assassinations and poison, depicted as a dagger with poison dripping from it.\n\n        /\\\n        |  | \n        |  |\n       =||||=\n         ||\nTrokorl- The spirit of engineering, machinery and building. Depicted as a goblin with a goblin with goggles and a hammer.\n\n       {o o}\n        \\-/P\n         |. |/\n         |. |\n         ==\n        /  \\\nLuara- The spirit of the moon, often shown by the symbol of a pale, white wolf.\n\n        \\___(>\n         |===/\n         |    |\nRamakhet- Spirit of the desert, barren lands and sand. He is never seen, and therefore is rarely ever depicted as something other than his name. He has sworn to scour the earth of all life for all time.\n       ~~~~~\n      Ramakhet\nKrathol- The spirit of pain, suffering and starvation. Depicted as a pile of dry bones.\n   \n      (------)\n      (------)\nVeist- Spirit of illusion, tricks and thievery, depicted as a goblin with four eyes.\n\n      (:_:)\n      \\| |/\n       /\\\n       |  |\nFreygoth- Spirit of the wind and wild animals. He takes any form which he may desire. \n \n       ~~~~~\n        ~~~~\n         ~~~\nGlutros- The spirit of greed and obesity. He is depicted as a cake.\n   \n        , , , ,\n       |====|\n       |====|\nThulezia- Spirit of lust, pleasure and beauty, depicted as a naked slave girl. \n\n        (_)\n        |00|\n      ,/|   |\\,\n        !__!       \n       /   \\\nIsuz- Spirit of love, caring, and tranquility, depicted as an open-armed woman.\n\n       { . }\n       \\| |/\n         ||\n         ||\nOrgon- Spirit of Disease, Pestilence, and failure. Depicted as a festering, starving man with six arms, each holding a rusted and broken weapon.\n            (.)\n           |-||-|\n           i-||-i\n           !-||-!\n            /\\\nUrin- The spirit of rain and hail, depicted as a dark rain cloud.\n\n         *****\n       ********\n         *****\n         ` ` ` ` \n          ` ` `\n           ` ` `\n            ` `\nKesaroth- Spirit of envy and jealousy, usually shown as a golden bull.\n \n                 |__|\n                 ('')\n     /`-------\\/\n    / |         | |\n  '~  | |-----| |\n      ^^       ^^\nLeyd- Spirit of dominance and physical strength, symbolised by a closed fist.\n\n       ()()()\n        (   )\n         |**|\n         |**|\nScorthuz- The spirit of cleansing and purging, depicted as a vial of clear water.\n\n          (-)\n           | |\n         /--\\\n         |~~~|\n         |~~~|\n         ----\nTheruz- Spirit of intelligence and learning, shown as a wise old teacher. Brother to Betharuz.\n\n        ----\n       /     \\\n       | _  _ |\n     ('| O  O |`)\n       |  (.)  |\n       `/=.=\\'\n        \\/\\/\nBetharuz- Spirit of alcohol, cactus green and celebration, often depicted as a young dim man, in direct contrast to his brother, Theruz.\n\n       *, (.) U\n        \\_||_/\n           ||\n          /\\\nGentharuz- Spirit of smithing, smelting, industry and forging, depicted as a man with no legs, hammering an anvil.\n\n          (,)\n           ||--P\n         || ||   <==->\n         ||===| |==|\n         ||    || |++|\nDrelthok- Spirit of sleeping and dreams, often shown as a dark cloud.\n\n        %%%%%%\n       %%%%%%%\n        %%%%%%\nEathruz- Spirit of dawn and dusk, shown by the symbol of a red sun.\n\n       . .       . .\n       .\\       /.\n         \\\\ //\n         /|/\\|\\\n         \\|\\/|/\n         // \\\\\n      . /       \\ .\n      . .         . .\nKotrestruu- The spirit of memory and the recording of knowledge, depicted as an endless book.\n   \n       ______\n       ||=====/|\n       ||=====/|\n       ||=====/|\n       ||=====/|\n       ||=====/|\n       ||=====/\nLetrothak- The spirit of hindsight and excuses, shown as a goblin with eyes in the back of his head.\n\n        /----\\\n     \\\\| |  ||  | |//\n      \\,| (i)(i) |,/\n        \\      /\n         |      |\n       /        \\\n   __/ |", ""),
        StaticBook("Imp. Etiquette I", "Commodus de Jedih", "sdasdasdasdasdsaasfssImperial Etiquettekk\nsssssssssssssssssss\n\nIssued and Confirmed by His Imperial Majesty, the Holy Orenian Emperor Peter II Sigismund. Penned by the hand of Her Imperial Highness, Princess Augusta Maria\n7th of the First Seed, 1620\n\nTranscribed by Comm. 1663\nassdasdasdasdasdasasasasasa\n\nCONTENTS\n\nI. ON FASHION AND PRESENTABILITY\nII. ON MANNERS, FORMALITY, CONVERSATION AND GENERAL ETIQUETTE\n\nIII. ON THE IMPERIAL PRESENCE\n\nasdasdsadsadsadsads\n\nI. ON FASHION AND PRESENTABILITY\nIn order to be a welcome presence at court, it is required for the subject to be both fashionable and at the very least presentable. Certain aspects of court fashion are constantly changing, with most such fashion imitating the emperor’s personal tastes,-\nhowever other aspects remain the same. The expectations of men in regards to clothing are as follows:\n\nA man coming before the court must generally be clean shaven, with some exceptions. Full beards are not permitted, however, moustaches are.\nThe most fashionable and always-acceptable style of facial hair is the pique-devant, which entails of a well-groomed moustache, accompanied by a short, manicured stemming from the chin, coming to a gentle point.\nThose violating this rule have been known to be compulsorily shaven by the imperial chamberlains.\n\nA man must never wear armour or weapons at court unless he is immediately returning from a battle in which he has fought or has been -\ngranted express permission from the emperor, such as his retainers are.\n\nA man’s hair must be neat and well-groomed. The expectation is that it is to be trimmed neatly in the cavalier style. Some courtiers may opt to wear a Lovelock, using ribbons and-\nbows. \n\nA man must always be in possession of a hat in the Imperial fashion, wide-brimmed, felted and accented with a properly trimmed plume or buckle, however, he is expected to doff it when inside. Such hats are typically worn with one-\nside of the brim pinned to the crown of the hat, though men must be wary of this, as a mal-pinned hat can look extremely misplaced and out of sorts.\n\nTo look presentable in the current Imperial court, the male wardrobe must be composed of the doublet,-\nnow having high waistlines and a more billowy silhouette. Capes, matching both doublet and breeches are advised, as though sometimes it may be fashionable to have divergent hues, such is extremely rare and is often looked down upon. Breeches are worn -\nwith hose underneath, and boots had loose openings, and are adorned with latchets over the instep. Baldrics are also encouraged, onto which a sword scabbard is generally attached.  If a man finds himself well-endowed in resources, investing in a buff -\ncoat is highly encouraged, worn both under armour or as a temporary replacement.\n\nWomen’s attire should consist or the traditional low bodice sloped shoulders and covered bosom. Soft silhouettes are de rigueur. The female dress is comprised-\nof the linen shift, bodice, underskirt, over which goes the second skirt, incorporating both the top and bottom halves of the body, the stomacher and lace sleeves. Mule shoes are the preferred footwear. Taffeta, lace, and satin are the preferred textiles-\nof fashionable and well-bred women. A string of pearls high on the neck is absolutely mandatory for all cultivated women.\nadsadasdsadasdsadas\n\nII. ON MANNERS, FORMALITY, CONVERSATION AND GENERAL ETIQUETTE\nTo live a prosperous and fruitful life at court and attain your ultimate objective, one must adopt the manners and demeanour required of any courtier. There are often complex rules and procedures for matters of courtesy, however, they are quickly learned-\nby those who desire to understand the rules of good breeding, the customs of good society and to avoid incorrect and vulgar habits. \nWhen meeting and/or greeting an individual, one must employ both the proper form of verbal address aswell as the correct -\nphysical gestures. \n\nIn introducing a gentleman to a lady, address her first, thus: “Lady (Surname), permit me to present you to Lord (Surname).” If one lady is wed, you are to present the uncoupled woman to the matron.\nUpon greeting a woman of lower social standing, a man must merely bow his head whilst addressing her. No matter status, though, a well-bred man is to always kiss the hand of the lady in question, unless said lady is wed or otherwise engaged.\nLadies no matter what status must always curtsy to the male in which they are greeting, as well as any women parallel or greater in status to her.\n\nWhen a man is greeting a man of higher or equal social status to him, he must bow to him and doff his hat-\nwhen addressing him, with the proper procedure for bowing established later in this document.\n\nWhen greeting the hostess of a ball or salon, a curtsy and recognition of rank and title along with an appropriate remark is proper.\nWhen introduced to a woman a man should bow, and if he is not yet acquainted with the hostess, he should seek to express gratitude at her introduction.\n\nIt is regarded a breach of etiquette to disregard the rank and title of any person with whom-\nyou are conversing, and all members of the party are to be addressed formally, and then semi-formally, lest they are in an intimate setting.\n\nNo greater insult can be offered to polite society than to repeat the slang of barrooms and other places of -\nlowly nature. To speak vulgarities in the presence of the gentler sex and refined men of court is considered boorish, and those who dally in such offences are to be removed from the host or hostess’ salon.\n\nIt is considered uncouth to endeavour to shine-\nin all companies. Leave room for your hearers to imagine something within you beyond what you have said.\n\nIt is permissible for both sexes to attend a salon, however, it is the only social club where women are permitted to attend unless explicitly told-\notherwise under special circumstances. \n\nLadies of the Gallery are to adopt a modest, graceful and measured gait and precise knowledge of the social graces and rules of decorum. Failure to do so will result in an expulsion from court, and is considered-\nhighly contemptible. \n\nWhile strolling, a lady should be reserved and demure, and a man is to be observant and civil. If (s)he passes a friend or relative during his/her promenade, a singular greeting is acceptable. If (s)he passes a member of the -\nImperial Family, she/he is to bow and scrape or perform a simple curtsy. The doffing of a man’s hat is not necessary for such a circumstance, as to avoid the harsh ray of the sun.\n\nIn ascending order, the titles of address among members of the court are-\nas follows. In the case of an individual possessing multiple titles (As in an emperor’s second son, who is traditionally prince as well as Duke of Marna) the higher title takes precedence in address.\n\nCommoners devoid of a title are to be addressed as-\n‘Mr./Mrs. (Surname)’.\n\nDoctors with a doctorate, honorary or practical, awarded to them by an educational institution or the emperor are to be addressed as ‘Dr. (Surname)’.\n\nKnights are to be addressed as ‘Ser’.\nBarons and Baronesses are to be addressed as ‘My lord/lady’, ‘Lord/Lady (Firstname)’ or simply ‘sir/ma’am’.\n\nViscounts and Viscountesses are to be addressed as ‘My lord/lady’, ‘Lord/Lady (Firstname)’ or simply ‘sir/ma’am’.\nCounts and Countesses (As well as earls) are to be addressed as ‘My lord/lady’, ‘Lord (Firstname)’ or simply ‘sir/ma’am’.\n\nMargraves and Margravines are to be addressed as ‘My lord/lady’, ‘Lord/Lady (Firstname)’ or simply ‘sir/ma’am’.\nDukes and Duchesses, as well as Archdukes and Archduchesses, are to be addressed as ‘Your Grace’ first, however after the first address it is an option to address the person in question as either ‘Your Grace’, ‘My lord/lady’, ‘Lord/Lady (Firstname)’ or-\nsimply ‘sir/ma’am’.\n\nPrivy councillors, as well as diplomats and other high-ranking civic officials, are to be addressed as ‘Your Excellency’ first, however after the first address, it is an option to address the person in question as either-\n‘Your Excellency’ or ‘sir’.\n\nPrinces and Princesses are to be addressed as ‘Your Highness’, however, after the first address it is an option to address the person in question as either ‘Your Highness’ or simply ‘sire/ma’am’.\nKings and Queens are to be addressed as ‘Your Majesty’, however after  the first address it is an option to address the person in question as either, ‘Your Majesty’, ‘my lord/lady’ or simply ‘sire/ma’am’.\nImperial Princes and Princesses are to be addressed as ‘Your Imperial Highness’, however after the first address it is an option to address the person in question as either ‘Your Imperial Highness’ or simply ‘sire/ma’am’.\nThe Empress is to be addressed as ‘Your Imperial Majesty’, however, after the first address it is an option to address her as ‘Your Majesty’, ‘my lady’ or simply ‘ma’am’.\n\nThe Emperor is to be addressed as ‘Your Imperial Majesty’ at all times.\nIt is worth noting that in the case of the landed peerage, it is customary and an option to address them by the territory of which they rule over in the fashion of ‘Lord (Territory)’. For example, if a theoretical John Smith is entitled the Baron of -\nGrenville, he may be addressed (Even preferably at times) as ‘Lord Grenville’. However, this is never done with members of the royalty or other titles above ducal level, such as for an archduke. For example, Prince Alexander, despite also being the Duke-\nof Marna, is never addressed as Lord Marna, however, the Roswell Dukes of Istria may be referred to as Lord Istria. This is an old custom originating from the reign of Godfrey the Exalted, returned to prominence under Emperors Peter and Robert however-\nabolished once again after the latter’s deposition. With the restoration of the Empire in 1526, it has become codified into court etiquette yet again.\n\nIt is also worth noting that while the address of familiar first names has been included in this -\nlexicon, it is not customary to refer to a person using their first name unless that person is of lower or equal rank to you. For example, a duke may refer to a baron as Lord John, however, it is not recommended that a baron or commoner refer to a Duke-\nas Lord Charles. \n\nWhen referencing people in a speech to others, it is expected that you refer to them by formal title and not their personal name.\n\nIn the public environment of the court, titles and formalities are expected to be used even between-\nfamily members. For example, the Emperor will commonly refer to his brothers in a public setting as ‘sir’, and they will commonly refer to him as ‘Your Imperial Majesty’ or ‘sire’.\nSee the second transcribed issue of \"Imperial Etiquette\" for Section III \"ON THE IMPERIAL PRESENCE\".\n\n-Commodus.\n\nwwdwdwdadadasdsdsdf", ""),
        StaticBook("Imp. EtiquetteII", "Commodus de Jedih", "sadasdsadasdasdasda00Imperial Etiquetteiv\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa\n\nIssued and Confirmed by His Imperial Majesty, the Holy Orenian Emperor Peter II Sigismund. Penned by the hand of Her Imperial Highness, Princess Augusta Maria.\n7th of the First Seed, 1620.\n\nTranscribed by Comm.\n1663\nadsdasdasdsadsadsss\n\n(This is the second issue in the Imperial\nEtiquette Series - Commodus.)\nIII. ON THE IMPERIAL PRESENCE\n\nThe Imperial presence is the phrase used to refer to the company of the Holy Orenian Emperor. If you were in a palace complex, and the the emperor was in one of the chambers thereof, -\nyou would enter the Imperial presence if you entered that room. The Emperor may often be present in outdoor settings, or in single large halls without side-chambers. Therefore, the area ten feet around the emperor's person has been designated in his-\npresence. \n\nBy law and custom, no person may enter this presence without rendering courtesy to the Crown. ‘Rendering courtesy’ here means to acknowledge by a bow or curtsy that the person holds a position of honour.\nThere is a proper way to either bow or curtsy when entering the imperial presence.\n\nIn entering the Imperial presence, males are expected to bow and scrape. Scraping refers to the drawing back of the right leg-\nas one bow, such that the right foot scrapes the floor or earth. While executing such a bow, the man's right hand is pressed horizontally across the abdomen while the left is held out from the body, often with a flourish. If the man holds a cane, -\nit is always grasped in the hand held out from the body.\n\nIn entering the Imperial presence, women are expected to perform a court curtsy, in which she extends her right foot behind the left, resting on the ball -\nof the foot. Keeping her back straight and a lowered head, she must then bend her knees outward. She must lower herself down until her right knee is just barely grazing her surface of the terrain. Then, after a few moments have passed, she is to raise -\nherself gracefully before His Majesty.\n\nThis process is complicated when one enters the Imperial presence as the subject of the Emperor and/or the court’s attention, such as when entering a room where the Emperor awaits-\nyou, or example for a priorly arranged formal audience. In such events, a bow or curtsy must be completed first at the entryway to that room and then again on entering the sovereign’s immediate presence.\nKneeling before the emperor is not customary or required save in the circumstance that you are in the direct and explicit attention of the sovereign and are either:\n\nSurrendering to him, such as when taken captive.\nPledging allegiance to him, such as in a swearing of fealty.\n\nPleading for mercy or forgiveness.\n\nAsking the hand in marriage of one of his relatives.\nIf you wish to speak with the Emperor and he is not busy, wait just outside the presence until you are bidden to approach. You might make yourself more obvious by bowing or curtsying. You must never stare.\nIf you must speak to get the emperor's attention (although this isn't usually necessary) you might try ‘Forgive me, your Imperial Majesty, but…’ or ‘Your Imperial Majesty, may I approach?’\nThere may be times when one must speak with the emperor and you are unable to gracefully arrange it yourself. You might discreetly ask the Chamberlain or Archchancellor to approach the emperor on your behalf to arrange a time and place and ask them-\nto have you sent for when the emperor has time to hear you (or linger around and see if they're able to get you in right away).\nThere are several simple rules and conventions which one must never break when in the Imperial presence.\n\nOne must always address the emperor as ‘Your Imperial Majesty’ first, however after the first address,-\nit is an option to address the emperor as either ‘Your Imperial Majesty,’ ‘Majesty,’ ‘sir,’ or simply ‘sire’.\n\nOne must never look directly at the Emperor.\nOne must never touch the emperor or in any way violate his person, unless to do so would be to save him from mortal danger.\n\nOne must always remove a hat, helm or other headwear in the Imperial presence.\nOne must never turn one’s back upon the emperor, and must always exit the room backwards.\n\nOne must never interrupt the emperor, or speak while he is speaking.\nOne must not sit down in the imperial presence unless given leave by him to do so.\n\nOne must stand up on the emperor’s entering of a room.\nOne must, on entering the imperial presence and being addressed by the emperor, not exit his presence until leave is granted. If one must leave immediately or urgently, they must request, using the words, ‘By Your Imperial Majesty’s leave, I...’\nOne must never come before the emperor armed, except in certain circumstances, such as in the case of his retainers, highest officials, family or immediately following a battle in which one has fought.\nOne must never refer to the emperor’s first name in the imperial presence. However, outside of the imperial presence, such as in some publications, documents or general conversation, it is acceptable to refer to the emperor as his given name and his-\nregnal number, provided his requisite titles are also applied.\n\nOne must never refer to the emperor’s dynastic or familial name under any circumstances.\nOne must never sit in the emperor’s throne or wear one of the emperor’s crowns under any circumstances. Exceptions are made for sitting on the throne in the event of the realm’s chief judicial officer giving a verdict.\nasdasdsadsadsadsadd", ""),
        StaticBook("Imperial Writ", "Augustus", "MISSIVE FROM THE CROWN PRINCE, 1686\n\nI, Augustus Horen, hereby validate the legitimacy of the owner of this scroll in their actions for the Imperial Administration, concerning the gathering of information.\nSigned,\n\nAugustus Horen, Crown Prince of The Empire.\n\n", ""),
        StaticBook("ImperialContract", "Commodus", "15th of Sun's Smile, 1690.\n\nAt the behest of our merciful sovereign, the imperium,  request before one Witcher, operating under the 'title', Sparrow, hailing from the Aeldinic Marked School of the Sparrow, to lay before you our mission.\nA terrible entity of magical proportions has appeared and is under pursuit.  Like a beast, one that has committed heinous crimes against his Grace's subjects. Only the Most Famous Among Witchers has the ability to destroy\nto appear in legion with one Gwenllech of Taillteann. Upon aiding in matters discussed prior, he will be granted a sum of five-thousand-Mina, present entirely in Crown-coin; additionally that the behest of Gwenllech, he has relinquish the\nblades of the Grand Master of the School of the Fox of Athera.\n\nThe previously mentioned conditions valid upon completion. We shall await you in full hope that you will deign to hear of our woes and liberate our land from the clutches of fear. \nSigned,\n\nHis Imperial Highness, Commodus of the House Horen, Imperial Chamberlain and Count of Aldenburg", ""),
        StaticBook("In Sheep's Wool", "Nafis Yar", "On Wolves in Sheep's Wool\n\nAn Informative Pamphlet on the Adrian Dog and Others Associated to the Breed.\n-------------------\nWhen training man’s companion, one must start from an early age. You are to drill the sort of conduct you wish to see into them, much like you would do with a new soldier under your command or your own toddler once they begin to walk. If left alone, the\ndog becomes wild growing up. It will run amok in your household and eventually it will bite the master’s hand. While usually there re ways to remedy this after it has passed the threshold, this is perhaps the exemption where there is only one route to\ntake.\n\nReader, I ask you pay heed to the words I write in these darkest of times. Look to this particular breed of Canis that has long sincebeen allowed to run wild by humanity’s predecessor’s : The Adrian Dog. Do not put blame on those men who live on\nthrough the archives, for they had only shown mercy as taught by the Orenic Faith. But understand their mistake. I urge all readers to learn from it and do not repeat it or else the dreaded cycle of Crow continues.\n\nMy words mean nothing without evidence,\nand this I can provide, dear reader. The Adrian Dog is a carnivorous beast hell bent on the destruction of others for mere amusement. It is the thrill of the hunt that gives them activity.  If they have nothing to hunt, they grow restless. Cranky, much\nlike a baby whose sleep is disturbed. But this is no mere infant! It is a monster of a beast that will bite the master’s hand when least expected.\n\nThe Adrian Dog is one who subjugates the unwilling. Looking through the archives of Athera,\nwe witness this in practice with the genocide of the Waldenian people where my grandfather once hailed from. After the forefathers of the Adrians had robbed the throne from House Chivay, they proceeded to eliminate all those that opposed. Wishing to\nmaintain their vows to the overthrown Chivay, the Waldenian people refused to follow suit with the other Orenian vassals. This was never out of greed as it was  portrayed by Crow nor was the Konigreich of Aesterwald ever meant to be. It was through sheer\nloyalty to their vows that the Waldenian people refused to back down until the supposed “Protector of Humanity” Emperor Tuvya Carrion mobilized his armies alongside Uruks and threatened to bring Aesterwald down. Only then, to protect his people from the\ndestruction that would have came, did Konig Voron Rovin I (may he rest in peace) swear fealty. But how can one trust humanity to Crow when Tuvya rejected all peace talks and his only wish was to either subjugate or destroy the Waldenian people? When\nrebellion came and the forces of Renatus and Aesterwald defeated the Crow, the latter rolled on its back in submission. In turn, the forces of Renatus and Aesterwald spared the dogand allowed it to scamper off and lick its wounds. A mistake that haunts\nus today. Where are the Waldenian people now? Nearly all dead with few scattered about the realm. Men who wished to be free were hunted down and slaughtered after unholy forces wreaked havoc upon Vanderfell - obliterated by hell fire from cultist work.\nThese “protectors of humanity” did not come to the aid of men against this hell fire. Now why allow the dog to regain the reins of humanity?\n\nNow reader, you might bring up three questions. Are the Adrians not the same as the Waldenians and only wish to\nrule themselves? Why should we wage war on a people when we all carry the curses and sins of Iblees, is this not just a product of such? What makes the loyalists so different from the Adrians? I shall answer all these as well.\n\n1.) While both the Adrian\nDog and the Waldenians sought to rule themselves, the Waldenians had never tried making claim to the Orenian throne. In fact, they had pushed for talks of an alliance to answer Tuvya’s arguments of the need for a unified humanity.\nThe Crow is gluttonous however, and pecks at anything it finds edible. Even that of rotten flesh. Today, the Adrian Dog wishes to usurp its former master and seek the throne themselves. And the Adrian Dog will not stop there.\n2.) While it is true that we as mortals carry the affliction given by the fallen one, Iblees, the Adrians have surpassed any of its limits and have grasped the sins Iblees instilled in us as the norm. Something to be proud of. The Adrians side with\nbandits contrary to their faith and for too long all walks of life have cowered at the barbarism demonstrated by these untamed beasts. A unified front is the only answer to subduing the beast that has been created overtime.\n3.) Under Olivier I Ashford de Savoie, the realm of mortals has seen order and stability absent during the rule of Crow. To allow a just man to be usurped by the Adrian Dog is not only allowing a plague on to humanity, but on to all races across the land.\nAnd you, reader, ask why this is a plague on all? Before I continue, I admit I am not Orenian. I fight for Savoie though because should he be left alone in his just fight, we will all be next. There is a young lady I know back home who cannot fight and\nonly wishes to fish in peace and live modestly. A shepherd who is soon to be married to a woman born with no eyes at birth. Despite his economic status and her affliction, they seek happiness too. There are plenty more innocent people back in my home, but\nthe Adrian Dog is one with poor eyesight. It does not see soldier or child, elderly or woman. It sees prey. And it will rip the throats of any that is not them.\nRemember the Waldenians, who tried living just lives in peace but were near annihilated by the Crow. Remember the attempted genocide on Dwed by King Heinrik Carrion in the old lands of Anthos. Remember the raids you have all faced at the hands of the\nAdrian Dog teamed among banditry.\n\nAdrian Dog whispers ‘Mina-Mina’ to you like a dumb brain and jingles coin before you. But they will claim this back for war reparations in conquests they start against YOU.\nAnd we will fall one by one to the predator if we do not take a stand now. They will hide among your people disguised and take control from the inside. They assault holy men and seek blood for coin.\nTo those who answer this call to fight alongside me, then let me be the first to say it will be an honor to fight alongside you. The words I write are true, backed up by evidence in the history of the Adrian Dog. The enemies are snakes in the grass,\nand we must cut the grass to reveal their slither. They are dogs who have been disobedient for far too long and must be dealt with before they bite the hand that once fed them. They will not stop until they are the last in the realm.\nAnd the only way to deal with Adrian Dog is to put them down.\n \n-NY\n“To never to turn the back upon a foe” - Vander Code", ""),
        StaticBook("Individual", "Przemek of Nordengrad", "Individual Soldier Report", ""),
        StaticBook("Info on Copies 2", "Cablam", "In order to get a copy of a book on the shelves you must donate a book that we currently do not have. This book can be your own work of someone else's that you have come into possession of. \n\nIn order to request a copy of a book, put\nthe book that we do not have which you are donating in the chest labeled 'Book Copy Requests'. Along with this book you must submit a signed book in the same chest with the following details: \n1. Your name\n2. The date ((/date))\n3. The book you\n4. The book you wish to obtain a copy of\n\nTo pickup your copy you must come into the library and ask one of the librarians or scholars and if the copy has been made they will give it to you.\n\nNote: In order to request a copy the\ndonated book must be approved by either Lyeth or Armin.\n\nAdditionally, copy requests are limited to one per week unless otherwise specified. \n\nLastly, we do not loan or sell books.", ""),
        StaticBook("Inquiry", "Vanya Damaer", "Karin'ayla and Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya,  neighbor across the way. On the sign outside your door, it says your name id Athedil Haler'thilln, so I shall refer to you as Athedil for the continuance of this letter. \n\nI am Vanya Damaer and I am new to this city.\nI look to further the progress of the high elves and lend my being to it's research and development. As such, I am interested in meeting with you for an exchange of knowledge and perhaps culinary delights. Would you perhaps be interested in a luncheon\nwith me at a date and time of your choosing? \n\nI look forward to your response in due course.\n\nMaehr'sae Hiylun'ehya,\nVanya Damaer", ""),
        StaticBook("Insanity! vol 1", "Alstasia Tintia", "Hello hello! You grabbed this book? Perhaps your interested in knowing more about INSANE people, hmm? Or maybe your insane but wanna know why? heheheh. I cant quite laugh, cause im writing a book, but hey! Im crazy, I dont care. Anyway... lets go on,\nshall we?\n\nSome may say insanity is evil, but insanity in and of itself is... neutral... I suppose. Insanity isnt neccasarily evil, as a person who is insane isnt evil. Its the insanity that does it.\nLets actually talk about insanity now. Two types of insane people though.\n1. Revelers.\n\nPeople who revel in their insanity, not wanting to hide it, wishing to cause death and destruction to all whom they meet. These are the truly unpredictable ones.\n2. The hiding ones.\n\nTheir are some people who are insane, but they do a great deal at hiding it. Perhaps they are indeed good, but their insanity is brought out through... odd things. Could see something they hate, could just get tired of hiding, who\nknows? Oh! I do! hAHAhaAhahaAHAha!\n\nAnway, when you meet somebody who is insane... you should try to figure out what their insanity is, and try to use it to your advantage to escape!\n1. Random insanity\n\nThese are insane people who are totally random. They may kidnap ye, have a nice conversation for 30 minutes, then kill ya! Ya gotta figure out how to distract em, or use random logic to trick em!\n2. The murderous ones\nInsane people who will just straight up murder ya! Ya would best run from these people!\n3. Dillusionals\n\nSome people just have dillusions of grand things. Or they just see ferrets everywhere... FERRET! \n\nTry to tell them their is a fox or something behind them, when they turn around, they may just see one!\ncreated by their mind.\n\nAnyway, im not signing this, cause im also insane, a nice person though, but I dont want anybody finding me. \n\n-A Annonymos madman/woman\n\nDunno if I spelled that right! HAHAHAH!\n*A sketch of a sword with vipers slithing around it would be sketched here, quite detailed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Inspiration", "Aebek", "This is a banana,\nBanana is yellow,\nYellow is a happy color,\nI believe in you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Intelect", "The Mysterious Stranger", "Intelect.\nMost people assume they don't have any. Some assume others don't have any. Others assume everyone has some.\nIntelect is something that is undefinable. Except with this definition I will randomly say.\nIntelect is the amount of stuff you know for certain areas in your life. Intelect is not a measurable thing and not immeasurable either. Intelect must always be at any state higher then the intelect of nothing. Yet lower then the intelect of nothing. As\nnothing knows everything it needs to know and everything it doesn't need to know. \nIntelect is something everyone has and can be seperated into Five Catagories.\n1 Magic. How it works how do you do it and why you do it. simple isn't it?\n2 Nature, why is it there when was it there and how does it work?\n3 Philosophy. Why are we here, when were we here, and how are we here?\n4 Religion Who brought us here, when did he bring us here, and how did he bring us here?\n5 Combat How do I kill a man, when did I kill a man, and when should I kill a man.\nThese are the five intelects combat, religion, magic, Philosophy, and Nature. All five of these work with each other in ways that we don't know. More to come.", ""),
        StaticBook("Interview Task", "Treemma'Parir Athri", "Dedicant Tasks\n\nTask 1-\nInterview 5 Druids and ask them the following:\n\"Their name, their rank in the order, their time as an attuned Druid, most memorable Tasks, and any other questions.\"\nInterview 1 - \nQ1. The Trout Druid Kasfer.\nQ2. Archdruid.\nQ3. Almost an Elven Year.\nQ4. Making a Garden in a place of Extreme death. Went up north and planted cold weather stalks and plants.\nAdvice: Dont do things druids say if it harms-\nyou. Have patience.\nInterview 2-\nQ1. The Seed Druid Kefi.\nQ2. Hierophant and Guide.\nQ3. 220ish years.\nQ4. Grew a forest out of a baren hillside.\nAdvice: Remember that we are all family; no matter what.\nInterview 3-\nQ1. The Crocodile Druid Damai Torena.\nQ2. None in Mother Grove.\nQ3. An elven year.\nQ4. Getting drugged by Artimec and having to survive the Elven week... Okay..\nAdvice: None to give.\nInterview 4-\nQ1. The Cosmos Druid Indra.\nQ2. Archdruid.\nQ3. Two Elven Years.\nQ4. Growing a sapling into a tree that her staff came from.\nAdvice: Remember that every Druid is your family no matter what.\nInterview 5-\nQ1. The Weed Druid Riv'Su.\nQ2. Guide.\nQ3. A few Elven Months.\nQ4. Learning about the Cycle of life and how we can only accept death.\nAdvice: Don't fuck up.", ""),
        StaticBook("Intro to Alchemy", "VonEbs", "An Introduction to the Alchemist\nForward:\nGreetings, my dear reader. Within the pages of this tome I shall be explaining to you what it takes to be a true Alchemist. I shall run you through our mindset, qualities and traditions.\nChapter I: The Recipe for a Good Alchemist.\nIt takes a special breed of person to be an Alchemist; a rare combination of patience, creativity, intellect, enthusiasm, and of course, an unusual resistance to explosions. For those who wish to follow\nthe noble path of an Alchemist, you must first consider if you possess these key traits, for if you do not, much like a potion made with a flawed recipe, you will be ineffective.\nDo not mistake what I say for supremacism, but rather realize\nthat it is simply an effort to save you. If you do not possess these qualities, dear reader it is quite possible that you, in the attempt to follow our path, may indeed end up harming yourself and others. Now, allow me to go more in-depth about what\nthese traits mean, in order of their importance to an Alchemist: \nPatience. Alchemy, I’m afraid, is not a fast nor particularly interesting process. An Alchemist will spend most of their time for their elembic to boil so that the extract of\nyour ingredients may be collected for use, or simply waiting for a potion to brew. Very little of the time is takes to create a potion is actually spent creating the mixture, although this time is indeed the most interesting part of Alchemy in my\nopinion. Because of all this, dear reader, Patience is vital to an Alchemist, as it would be, in my opinion, apt to give Alchemy the formula consisting of 25 “parts”:\n7 parts waiting(brewing, waiting for the elembic’s water to boil.)\n5 parts setting\nup, cleaning up, and inspecting your equipment.\n5 parts testing(making sure your potion works.)\n3 parts failure (realizing that your recipe is bollocks and starting over.)\n3 parts extracting (boiling down the ingredients and\ncollecting the condensation using an alembic.)\n1 parts explosion (surprisingly common.)\n1 parts mixing the bloody potion.\nIntellect. You may be wondering why this is not the first on my list... Well, someone whom is completely\ndull, yet is willing to give up hours upon hours to make up for it, is much more likely to succeed than someone brilliant who will become frustrated and rushed the second they see that their brew will be taking a very long time to finish.\nSo, while this trait is near-vital, it can be made up for by a massive amount of patience and dedication.\nCreativity. Please note, that I am writing here the explain what it takes to be an Alchemist, not a good Alchemist. Creativity is something\ncompletely vital to anyone who wishes to be a master alchemist... but it is not to those whom only wish to dabble in the art. Creativity is essential for those who wish to truly excel at the art, because one cannot just follow recipes forever. There\ncomes a time, when an apprentice Alchemist must take these matters into their own hands. No more books, no more explanations as to why these particular ingredients must be used... there comes a time, when every Alchemist must learn to rely on their\nown extensive knowledge of herbs and ingredients, of what they represent... To craft a potion of their very own. This is much more difficult than it may seem... but I shan’t go into that, as this is no true Alchemical textbook, but\nrather, an introduction to the science. \nLastly, Enthusiasm. This trait may seem unusual to list, as most would automatically think of someone whom is impulsive and stupid... ‘overtly’ enthusiastic. No, Alchemy requires a special type of\nenthusiasm. One tempered by logic and patience. Enthusiasm is needed because without the drive to learn more, to improve your skill and to create potions of wonder... you are nothing, and shall go nowhere. The reason this is listed at the bottom of\nthe list instead of the top, is simply because by reading this far, you have shown an ounce of this quality, and as such, you may now take pride in knowing that you have the potential to learn this art.\nChapter 2: The Life of an Alchemist\nThe Lifestyle.\nThe life of an Alchemist, despite its labours, is a rewarding and interesting one. Many nations, many companies, and many guild need\nAlchemist, which means that an Alchemist is very rarely without options. Indeed, one of the most fulfilling parts of being an Alchemist is the satisfaction of knowing you are needed and wanted. An Alchemist rarely stays in one\nlocation whilst unemployed, often traveling from kingdom to kingdom, seeking a guild or company that has use for them. In my experience, this does not take a long time... Although it is important to measure one’s options before taking a job. This\nis not to say that an Alchemest /must/ be employed, gods know many Alchemists choos a life of reclusion and introversion; preferring the company of their ingredients and their equipment to the company of people or currency.\nAs an Alchemist, there are many different paths one may choose from; be it creating poisons or creating potions to heal the ill and wounded. These paths will play a large role in deciding how easily one can get jobs, and from whom. For example, one\nwho makes poisons may find it harder to get a job than one who create healing serums, as poisons are hard to mass-produce, which means are of no real use to an army, and they are certainly of no use for a peaceful company of guild.\nThis is much the opposite for healing potions, as oddly enough they are some of the simplest to make, and can be made in quite large quantities without losing much of their effectiveness, so all the aforementioned employers could\nhave a use for an Alchemist of healing. Do not think that these are the only two paths that an Alchemist may follow, however- and certainly no Alchemist sticks only to one branch of the science- think of it more as a specialization. I,\nfor example, specialize in incendiary and explosive concoctions.. Alchemist Fire, if you will. This means that I am often asked to work for militaries of small offensive guilds... even research companies.\nIn conclusion, the lifestyle in terms of business, for an Alchemist, is much dependent upon what they specialize in, and regardless of their business opportunities, the life of an Alchemist is rarely full, and in my opinion, very fulfilling.\nThe Morality of an Alchemist.\nMany jobs seem to have a set “morality.” Soldiers are expected to be lawful and trsutworthy, Mages to be intellectual and neutral... the Morality of an Alchemist is much the same as that of a Mage, and\nis, much like one’s business opportunities, dictated by the Alchemist’s specialization. To use the same examples as before, it would be more likely for an Alchemist specializing in poisons to fall into a darker, more “evil” morality, as they\nwould likely find their work with small groups of assassins of the like. Whereas an Alchemist specializing in healing, would be much more likely to fall into a “good” morality, as by nature, their job of choice is to help people.\nThere are not set rules, of course, a healing Alchemist may very well choose to assist an unlawful organization, and an Alchemist of poison may choose to supply a small vigilante group with his poisons. In essence, the Morality of an Alchemist is\nneutral, and is dictated completely by the individual.\nThe Living Conditions of an Alchemist\nThis section will be somewhat smaller, as there is very little that can be written about this. An Alchemist’s abode will generally have only one constant; a\nlab, usually located in a basement. This lab would contain an Alchemist’s supplies, equipment, and is generally kept locked, as much inside would be fragile or dangerous. As for why it is usually found in a basement... Well.. The earth seems to be a\nbit more resistance to explosions that wooden or cobblestone walls.\nFarewell:\nI thank your, read reader, for taking the time to read my small introduction to the Alchemist. I bid you good ever, good day, and farewell.", ""),
        StaticBook("Intro To Aspects", "Tristanm1", "Introduction to the Aspects\n\nBy Sunshine Druid Verden\nThe Mother of the Harvest, the Goddess of Change, the Green Lady. Cerridwen has many names, but all of them stem from her warm and caring demeanor toward the world. She is the matron Aspect of farmers and gardeners everywhere, and it is\nher divine radiance that blesses the crops and flora upon the world. The fragile, but beautiful flowers and the delicious fruits of the land are her domain. The seasons are gifts from her.\nThe Father of the Hunt, the King of Forests, the Green Man. Cernunnos also has many names, but all of them reflect upon who this Aspect truly is; a hunter. It was he who brought about the existence of wolves and bears -- of tigers and hawks. The predators\nof the land are his apprentices, and the thorny plants his traps. He is the patron Aspect of huntsmen and warriors everywhere, and it is his divine strength that blesses the worthy. The steadfastness of nature comes from him.\nThrough their grace, the world and all who dwell upon it came into existence. What we refer to as \"Nature\" is the combined efforts of these two infinitely powerful beings, and it was them that saved the sentient mortal races from utter destruction during\nthe Great War. It is our duty as their children to respect and aid Nature whenever possible, and by doing so give praise to their greatness.", ""),
        StaticBook("Intro. Alchemist", "Jistuma", "Forward:\n\nGreetings, my dear reader. Within the pages of this tome I shall be explaining to you what it takes to be a true Alchemist. I shall run you through our mindset, qualities, and traditions.\nChapter I: \n\nThe Recipe for a Good Alchemist.\nIt takes a special breed of person to be an Alchemist: a rare combination of patience, creativity, intellect, enthusiasm, and of course, an unusual resistance to explosions. For those who wish to follow the noble path of an Alchemist, you must first\nconsider if you possess these key traits, for if you do not, much like a potion made with a flawed recipe, you will be ineffective.\n\nDo not mistake what I say for supremacism, but rather realize that it is simply an effort to save you.\nIf you do not possess these qualities, dear reader it is quite possible that you, in the attempt to follow our path, may indeed end up harming yourself and others. Now, allow me to go more in-depth about what these traits mean, in order of their\nimportance to an Alchemist: Patience. Alchemy, I'm afraid, is not a fast nor particularly interesting process. An Alchemist will spend most of their time for their elembic to boil so that the extract of your ingredients may be collected for use, or simply\nwaiting for a potion to brew. Very little of the time it takes to create a potion is actually spent creating the mixture, although this time is indeed the most interesting part of Alchemy in my opinion. Because of all this, dear reader, Patience is vital\nto an Alchemist, as it would be, in my opinion, apt to give Alchemy the formula consisting of 25 \"parts\":\n\n>7 parts waiting (brewing, waiting for the elembic's water to boil.)\n>5 parts setting up, cleaning up, and inspecting your equipment.\n\n>5 parts testing (making sure your potion works.)\n\n>3 parts failure (realizing that your recipe is bollocks and starting over.)\n>3 parts extracting (boiling down the ingredients and collecting the condensation using an alembic.)\n\n>1 parts explosion (surprisingly common.)\n\n>1 parts mixing the bloody potion.\nIntellect. You may be wondering why this is not the first on my list... Well, someone whom is completely dull, yet is willing to give up hours upon hours to make up for it, is much more likely to succeed than someone brilliant who will become frustrated\nand rushed the second they see that their brew will be taking a very long time to finish. So, while this trait is near-vital, it can be made up for by a massive amount of patience and dedication.\nCreativity. Please note that I am writing here to explain what it takes to be an Alchemist, not a good Alchemist. Creativity is something completely vital to anyone who wishes to be a master alchemist... but it is not to those whom only wish to dabble in\nthe art. Creativity is essential for those who wish to truly excel at the art, because one cannot just follow recipes forever. There comes a time, when an apprentice Alchemist must take these matters into their own hands. No more books, no more\nexplanations as to why these particular ingredients must be used... there comes a time, when every Alchemist must learn to rely on their own extensive knowledge of herbs and ingredients, of what they represent... To craft a potion of their very own. This\nis much more difficult that it may seem... but I shan't go into that, as this is no true Alchemical textbook, but rather, an introduction to the science.\nLastly, Enthusiasm. This trait may seem unusual to list, as most would automatically think of someone who is impulsive and stupid... 'overly' enthusiastic. No, Alchemy requires a special type of enthusiasm. One tempered by logic and patience.\nEnthusiasm is needed because without the drive to learn more, to improve your skill and to create potions of wonder... you are nothing, and shall go nowhere. The reason this is listed at the bottom of the list instead of the top, is simply because by\nreading this far, you have shown an ounce of this quality, and as such, you may now take pride in knowing that you have the potential to learn this art.\nChapter 2:\n\nThe Life of an Alchemist\nThe Lifestyle.\n\nThe life of an Alchemist, despite its labours, is a rewarding and interesting one. Many nations, many companies, and many guilds need Alchemists, which means that an Alchemist is very rarely without options. Indeed, one of the\nmost fulfilling parts of being an Alchemist is the satisfaction of knowing you are needed and wanted. An Alchemist rarely stays in one location whilst unemployed, often traveling from kingdom to kingdom, seeking a guild or company that has use for them.\nIn my experience, this does not take a long time... Although it is important to measure one's options before taking a job. This is not to say that an Alchemist /must/ be employed, gods know many Alchemists choose a life of reclusion and\nintroversion--preferring the company of their ingredients and their equipment to the company of people or currency. As an Alchemist, there are many different paths one may choose from; be it creating poisons or creating potions to heal the ill and\nwounded. These paths will play  large role in deciding how easily one can get jobs, and from whom. For example, one who makes poisons may find it harder to get a job than one who creates healing serums as poisons are hard to mass-produce, which means are\nof no real use to an army, and they are certainly of no use for a peaceful company of a guild. This is much the opposite for healing potions, as oddly enough they are some of the simplest to make, and can be made in quite large quantities without losing\nmuch of their effectiveness, so all the aforementioned employers could have a use for an Alchemist of healing. Do not think that these are the only two paths that an Alchemist may follow, however--and certainly no Alchemist sticks only to one branch of\nthe science--think of it more as a specialization. I, for example, specialize in incendiary and explosive concoctions. Alchemist Fire, if you will. This means that I am often asked to work for militaries of small offensive guilds… even research companies.\nIn conclusion, the lifestyle in terms of business, for an Alchemist, is much dependent upon what they specialize in, and regardless of their business opportunities the life of an Alchemist is rarely full, and in my opinion, very fulfilling.\nThe Morality of an Alchemist.\n\nMany jobs seem to have a set \"morality.\" Soldiers are expected to be lawful and trustworthy, Mages to be intellectual and neutral... the Morality of an Alchemist is much the same as that of a Mage, and is, much like\none's business opportunities dictated by the Alchemist's specialization. To use the same examples as before, it would be more likely for an Alchemist specializing in poisons to fall into a darker, more \"evil\" morality, as they would likely find their work\nwith small groups of assassins of the like. Whereas an Alchemist specializing in healing, would be much more likely to fall into a \"good\" morality, as by nature, their job of choice is to help people. There are not set rules, of course, a healing\nAlchemist may very well choose to assist an unlawful organization, and an Alchemist of poison may choose to supply a small vigilante group with his poisons. In essence, the Morality of an Alchemist is neutral, and is dictated completely by the individual.\nThe Living Conditions of an Alchemist\n\nThis section will be somewhat small, as there is very little that can be written about this. An Alchemist's abode will generally have only one constant: a lab, usually located in a basement. This lab would contain\nan Alchemist's supplies, equipment, and is generally kept locked, as much inside would be fragile or dangerous. As for why it is usually found in a basement… Well… The earth seems to be a bit more resistant to explosions than wooden or cobblestone walls.\nFarewell:\nI thank you, reader, for taking the time to read my small introduction to the Alchemist. I bid you good ever, good day, and farewell.\nAn Introduction to the Alchemist\n\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((15/6/13))", ""),
        StaticBook("Invoice Notice", "Travis Bell", "===================           INVOICE\n    DUCHY OF ADRIA\n===================\n\n3x - Aurum Dust used\n(100 minas each) TOTAL: 300 Minas\n2x - Strigae removal\n(250 minas each)\nTOTAL: 500 Minas\nStrigae Removal\n(50 minas each)\nTOTAL: 50 Minas (as Azdrazi destroyed the first corpse)\n\n===================SUB TOTAL: 850 minas\nSPOOK TAX: 85 minas\nGRAND TOTAL: 935 minas\n\nSigned,\nTravis Bell - Vizmak Brigade of Caerhays", ""),
        StaticBook("Irhamir's Wish", "Irhamir Siil'crux", "I wish for knowledge, either coming in the form of alchemical regents or possibly even a hidden ethereal art.\n\nIrhamir Siil'crux", ""),
        StaticBook("Ironwood I", "Ser Ajax Ironwood II", "The Ironwood Family History, Part I.\nThe Ironwood family history begins with my grandfather, Augustus, and his estate. He was a freeman farmer, had a large estate, and one son, yet he had a suit of classic looking legion-styled armour.\nThe man, according to my father, stood at 5'8, was rather stout, and had flowing brown hair, with an appropiate beard. Built like a rock, he would farm on his estate even in his wealth, something that Ironwoods take pride in.\nIt's unclear if he was ever a soldier, but his blade was of very odd status, and appeared barely worn. The man was a bastion of wealth, and his wife was, according to my father, as beautiful as a Queen.\nThe sad fact is, their fate. When my father, Ajax, was just a boy of five years, a large scale raid was in progress on the estate. My father had only a pitchfork when he saw the flames from the manor, he rushed from his duty on the farm to see the event.\nTo his horror, he saw his father only in half his plates, holding off the man who had just killed his mother. Augusts at this time was a man of 45, and the raider seemed to be a young brute, capable of killing the man.\nIn quick response, my father charged the man with his pitch and hit him in the side, not enough however to kill him. Due to this, he drew all his might on Augusts, and cleaved him in two parts. The boy was shattered at this sight.\nTo this, the raider lunged on the boy, grabbed him by his right hand, and took it off; he then laughed and rode off with his raiders. The Ironwood estate was however, spotted aflame from affar, as a small adventure crew sighted it.\nAmong them was a Knight, a Dwarven blacksmith, and a ranger. The band of men saw the boy with blood pooling around him, and decided to nurse him to health. His story moved them, when he told them, and they took him in.\nThe Dwarf gave him a hand of bronze, he needed not a sword, becuase he took his father's, the knight provided him a title, the ranger taught him hunting. Through the years, the man was well enough to be on his own, giving his farewell to his comrades.\nAjax Ironwood, the name is not known to many, but to those who know it, they know the honour of this man. Ajax Ironwood eventually settled in Ostwick as knight, married Alyson the blacksmith, and had a son, whom he named after himself, who is the author.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ivlisar Trials", "Ivlisar Sagehand", "I aided Rowan Sagehand while they were drunk.\n\nI guided and protected Mal'rean while he was being attacked by ghouls. I dispatched the ghouls and took care of his wounds and I brought him to the nearest city.\nI helped Alenthir fell some trees to help him gain some money. I refused to take any money from him as I wasn't helping him for money.\n\nI helped Ardnea in her time of need as she was being attacked by bandits. I sprung into action and I managed to fi\noff the bandit.\n\nI helped Martyn Norringtan with his broken jaw. I made sure that he was fine before sending him away.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jack's Story I", "Ulric Balhjarta", "The smell of burning and decomposing flesh hung over Bastion.Undead took countless mortal lives with no emotion.Many of my comrads had fallen all around me, a dreadknight stood before me.His armor was as black as the night, he peered at me\nwith dark lifeless eyes.I was already fatigued from battle when he made his first strike,across my face,his blade cut deep into my skin through my helmet.I then also struck him with my aurum blade which pierced his skin allowing a black liquid to pour\nfrom his already tortured body.The knight grew angry and began swinging madly, I dodged\nmany of his attacks then he struck me again across my chest then plunged his gruesome blade deep into my abdomen.He then threw me into\nthe mud and moved onto attacking another soldier.\n   Laying in a pool of crimson I could hear the bellows of strength and pain all around me.I could only think of my home in Mardon and a sweet girl who lived there.Darkness fell upon my body and\nmy limbs seemed to grow as cold as ice.\n    Is this what death felt like?\nHours Later....\nI slowly began to open my eyes.The air smelt fresher now,an older man was kneeling over my body,a look of concentration on his face.My body felt warm as the man stood up, I then looked down my body to find it had been bandaged.\n\"Don't get up too quickly\"the man said in a croakey but smooth voice.Looking beside me I could see my battered armor,it is no longer usable because of the battle.\n    Eventually I gathered enough strength to sit up.\n\"you are lucky I found you when I did,or you would have died\"the mage said\n\"I am eternally thankful sir\"my voice shook a little.\"what is your name?\"\n\"Names do not matter boy\"he then gathered his things and walked out\nof this miniscule camp.\n      As he disappeared off into the dense woodland I too got up,I pulled my shirt over my scared body and climbed on a horse the mage had left for me.\n    I rode for my father's village.\nA Few Months\n          Passed...\nI had been with my father for almost a year.I helped him tend to our family's farm and did some guard training in my spare time,to ensure I did not get rusty.I have stopped having nightmares about that distant battle and spent a few more years with\nmy father until I was fully ready to ride back to Mardon and begin travelling Axios.\n    As I arrived in Mardon an old comrad of mine asked me if I would like to join the imperial garrison.I obviously said yes as I wanted to start being a soldier again.\nBeing in the garrison gave me alot of spare time,so I began to travel Axios.Alot had changed in my absense,the West never got back on it's feet.Through my travelles I met a couple of beautiful women which I had intimate relationships\nwith.Yet because of travelling and the military our relationships did not last very long. Sometimes I wonder if I'll ever settle down.\nA Month Later..\nI had found a city I had not yet visited.It was in the county of Haria and was called Al'Khaleed.It was a beautiful city and it was very warm there,I was thirsty from the heat so I headed into a nearby tavern.As I entered I could see that there\nwas not anyone working there.As I looked around a beautiful woman walked into the tavern,I asked her if anyone worked here and she told me the city is always quiet and that is why no-one works at the tavern.\n  We began talking,well she spoke mostly,\nand she told me her name was Daye.I took her to visit the city of Veris,because there was nothing to do in the city we took a walk outside of the city gates and stood looking at the water on a hidden dock.I asked her to tell me about herself and\nshe asked me the same question,it was lovely to have someone to talk to and I just hope I do not fall in love with her and break her heart.\n     Around a month later I took her to the Library of Draugr where she read some books on magic as that\nis her favorite genre,I read a book on dreadknights which took me back to the battle yet I did not let the nightmare take over me and placed the book back on the shelf and headed back over to Daye.We then went for a walk in the forest near\nthe Library. We sat under a tree and talked some more,I could feel myself falling in love with her,as we sat Daye began moving closer to me then I touched her hand,she began to blush but tried not to show it.Eventually she looked back at me and we\ncaught each others gaze.I kissed her.She got so flustered, it was cute.I got up to walk her back to her house and offered her a hand to help her up.As she took my hand she looked at our hands holding one another.I wonder what she was thinking.\nWhen we arrived at her house she invited me to stop for some tea which we shared on her rooftop,eventually we headed back indoors where we finished our tea and she took me to see some houses she was interested in.When we got back to her\nhouse once more we sat beside eachother,she leant on my shoulder and fell asleep.She is even more cute when she is sleeping,I knew this was not like any of my other relationships.I loved her dearly.\n     A few months went by,I was busy at the garrison\nso I did not have time to write to her.When I eventually got time off I wandered around the new city of Calethia.I got a property there and as I was about to enter Daye wandered down the street towards me.We decided to walk around the city\ntogether,we stopped at an area that looked as if it was for a wedding.We both sat down at a fire pit there and hugged.\n  She asked if she could see the property I had got,I said that she could and we headed off towards my house.\n  Stood\non the top floor of the house,we were talking about properties in the city.I decided to ask her if she would like to live with me.She said yes.Luckily the house had spare rooms so she could stay in one of them if she wanted to do so. We were stood\noutside my bedroom when she asked if I wanted to cuddle with her.\n   She took me into the bedroom where we sat on my bed and kissed,she was a great kisser.Yet she thought she was not and kissed me again to show that she could do better.I was not\nbothered about how well she kissed,I was just enjoying spending time with her.\n      Light began to flood into my room,I could feel her holding my chest.I held her in my arm.She has not yet noticed my scars,or if she has she has not mentioned them.\nThey are a constant reminder of the burdens of war.\nAbout a Month \n        Later.....\nOn my travelles to Sutica I was stopped by a soldier asking if I wanted to join House Silversteed of Norland, as I was releaved of my duties in the Garrison I said yes. We both travelled to Norland where I was recruited\nand given my uniform.\nI was then tested on my strength in battle by facing one of the strongest knights,I lost but I was still accepted because I put up a good fight.\nI was given some free time which did not last long as I had to rally to face a sea\nserpent.\n  As we got down into the valley by the waters edge we could see just how big the beast was.We faught hard and the beast managed to eat some of our men which made us fight harder.As we were about to kill the creature\nit coughed our men back out then lay on the shore dying.\n   The following day I headed back home.I was only home a short while when Daye entered,we talked a short while and I teased her a bit because she said her day was\nnot exciting.It seemed to make her laugh.We then walked around the city a bit and we visited the bath house.We were there for a while before we returned home.\n   Feeling her holding me, I awoke slowly.She was still sleeping.She awoke\nwhen I held her a little tighter.\n   Later that day I had to head back to Norland for training which held me there the rest of the day.Once I returned home Daye came down the stairs and we talked for a small while and\nI teased her about her strength again.We then held each other for a while,then she began to fall asleep.I carried her to our room and lay with her until she fell asleep.Then I did some planning.\n   A few months later, I headed home\nfrom Norland as I was held there for a while helping with getting the new capital built. As I arrived through the gates and glanced around a little I could see Daye looking at a fountain with her back to me. I walked up behind her and hugged her from\nbehind,she let out a little yelp and I could not stop myself from laughing.We talked a little about cities which led to briefly talking about having children, we were both alright with the idea but she is the one who needs to be completely sure about\nthe decision.I can wait until she is ready.\n Afterall I only have eyes for her.\nA Few Months\n      Passed.....\nI had received news that I was needed in Norland for a few months without leave,my commander allowed me to have a few days to myself to gather a few items before I had to go back to Norland.I did not know how to tell Daye so I sat alone for a while by\nthe fire beside the stage sharpening my sword,and gathering my thoughts. I would have to hold off my plans for a few months. However I feel I have everything ready,I just need to wait for the right moment. Daye then kissed me on my\nhead, I looked up to her sheathing my sword.How strange it was to look up to her rather than down to her,I then told her I had to go to Norland for a few months and she said she would be alright on her own.Which reasured me a little,\nit will not stop me from worrying about her. Yet she seemed more worried about my safety,I can take care of myself.\n   Returning back from Norland, I was stood at the gates of Calethia when Daye walked down the street towards me. We talked for a short\nwhile then headed back home where she made me some tea, and embraced with each other.\n    The following day,I had just came out of my office when Daye had returned from walking around the city, she came up the stairs and we hugged for a short\nwhile, I could see she was quite tired so I suggested that we sat down. As we sat I allowed her to snuggle into me, she began to grow tired so she went to bed.\n    \n \n   Continue To Part\n           Two....", ""),
        StaticBook("Jack's Story II", "Ulric Balhjarta", "Jack's Story\n         Part 2\nI have been kept in Norland for a few months for training.During one of our training sessions we received news that we were needed in battle against the Flays.The battle was quite one sided and we returned victorious.I was given the rank\nof footman as I had proven myself in battle, then we were dismissed and I headed home to Calethia.As I entered the city a man questioned if I wanted to join the guard force in Calethia but I had to turn him down as I can not be in two forces at once.\nYet if Calethia is in a battle I will obviously fight for them.Then the man walked away closely followed by a woman who is said to be the Princess of Calethia.I then headed back to my house and headed upstairs as I was quite tired, I took off my belt with\nmy sword attached and placed them in the wardrobe.As I turned to face the door Daye entered, we talked a while and I teased her as I always do about her strength.\n     Waking to her holding me, I looked down to Daye.I allowed her to wake up on her own\naccord.When she woke we lay in bed for a while and talked, I joked with her about slaying a wyvern as I always do and she always jokes back.I told her a stupid story of how we would meet a wyvern which made her laugh.I love making her laugh.\nA few months later, I was adventuring Axios when I came across the ruins of Bastion.All of the nightmares came flooding back, I could hear the screams of pain and terror echoing in my mind. The undead kept some of the bodies of the soldiers and\ncitizens as trophies, leaving them cascaded amonst the dirt where they had struck them down and ended their lives.I fell to my knees, seeing a skeleton in the uniform I used to wear so proudly.The image of the dreadknight towering over me as the darkness\nfell over my body taunted my traumatized mind.I can still remember the battle so clearly eventhough it ended years ago,the smell of burning flesh,the sound of children screaming in terror as their parents were slaughtered before their innocent eyes.\nWhy did I not turn back? Why did I do this to myself?\nClambering back to my feet,I wiped a tear from my face and began to head into the ruins.The undead had completely destroyed the city, the Westerlands army hall had collapsed and the path into the city\nhad been blown up.\nThe undead may have left the city but their destruction still scars the great city and the lives of the mortals involved in the battle.\n   Turning back the way I came, I left the remains of the city. As I walked down the path I\nturned to face Bastion one last time. I said a prayer to Owaiyn for sparing my life and did a final salute for my fallen comrads.Hail Bastion.Hail the Westerlands.May her citizens and defenders rest in peace.\nAs I arrived home from what was left of Bastion I sat down on the chair, I do not know if I will tell Daye about Bastion, I may tell her that I visited it but I will not tell her about how I felt when I was there.I do not want her to think I am weak.\nA few months had passed, I had not told Daye about Bastion and I do not think I ever will,I do not want to relive that experience.\n  As I was leaving the gates of Calethia I was approached by two Gravens,knowing their power I did not look them in the\neye,I was not willing to loose Daye.One of them spoke with me, yet I can not remember what about as the other graven knocked me out.I awoke to find I was alone,the gravens had not stolen anything or hurt me at all,someone must have disturbed them or they\ndecided they were not willing to do anything else to me.No matter now, I am just happy they did not kill me.I stood back up and returned home because I had a sore head and just wanted to rest. I headed to mine and Daye's room when she also entered the\nhouse and came up to our room.She had been out exploring Tahn,which explains why I did not see her in Caletha,we talked a little while and embraced.Which I ruined when I told her about the Gravens attacking me,she started to get worried about me and\ntold me about how they could have hurt me more.I reasured her that I was alright but it still took her a while to calm down,which I once again ruined when I joked about if I went to war which made her worry a little more.I hugged her until she calmed a\nlittle and I told her I was not ready to leave her.She then made me promise that I would not leave her,I answered that I promised I would not and then asked her to promise the same thing.She answered that she promised to never leave me and then smiled\nSometimes I think she worries a little bit too much about me,but that is just because she loves me.And I love her just as much.Eventhough she gets really flustered sometimes,like when I pay her compliments or when we kissed for the first time.\nA month later I ran into Daye when I was about to find her to see if she wanted to visit a city with me.She took my hands and seemed happier than normal,not that she is miserable, she is always happy just not this happy.She told me she had exciting news\nand led me back home.\nWhen we got there she told me she was pregnant.Which was wonderful news.I then thought that this was a good enough moment to ask her if she would marry me.At first she looked shocked,then she said yes and hugged me.She then began to\ncry which she told me was because she was really happy.We then sat down for a while and she snuggled into me.We talked about baby names and she chose Jericho as a name for a boy.Jericho was her father's name and I asked her what happened to him as he was\nnot living with her and she never told me of where he was.She said he died about ten years ago because he got ill,she also told me she lived alone until I met her and I teased her about how I have teased and annoyed her ever since,which made her laugh.I\nthen chose a girls name,Isabella.I did not want to choose my mother's name because I never met her and no matter how hard I have tried I have not found her or anything about her in Axios.It is like she never existed.I always assumed she had died,because I\nhave no reason to assume otherwise.\nAnyway,as we sat Daye began to fall asleep on me,so I let her sleep.I gently moved some hair that had fallen onto her face,tucking it behind her ears.She stayed asleep,and was asleep for a few hours before she\nawoke,when she was awake she said we should go upstairs so she could have a better sleep.I agreed and carried her to our room and lay her gently on the bed and lay beside her,allowing her to fall asleep hugging me.\n   I began to think of my mother,\nand the painting my father had got painted of them both hugging me when I was just a few months old.I remember my mother's ash blonde hair and sapphire blue eyes.And how happy she looked.My father told me she had left because she was not ready to be\na mother as she gave birth to me when she was fifteen years of age, her and father were not married they were just courting.\n  My grandmother,my mother's mother,told me she had joined a guard force that belonged to House Brawm.I visited the fort they\nowned in the outskirts of Haense, as I arrived there I found it had been destroyed. I asked a Haense soldier what had happened and he told me that they had killed everyone who were associated to House Brawm because they were rebels.I then visited the\nHaense capital to ask if I could identify my mother's body but they did not allow me to view the bodies as they were 'the kings property'.My mother did not even get a burial,they burned all the bodies once the king had made sure all of the Brawm's\nassociets had been killed.\n  My father told me as a child that he allowed me to have my mother's last name to 'remember her with',I just wish I had got to meet her to see what she was like.To test her hand in combat as my grandfather told me she was\na great fighter.\nNow I think about it Daye has never mentioned her mother to me, and her mother is not in the picture of Daye and her father.I wonder if her mother died in childbirth.I am unsure if I should ask Daye about her as I have not really spoke to\nDaye about my family.The only person I have really spoke to my family about was a girl named Annabelle I met years before the battle for Bastion.If I ask her about her mother I will tell her about my family,and about my runaway mother.\nIt had been a few months, I had not seen Daye for three months and I am beginning to miss her.The last I saw her, a baby bump was beginning to show.The ashguard have gave me a property in Norland to use while I am there for months without leave.I am\nsure that Daye and the baby are alright yet I am still worried about them.I hope I get home to see my child before it is born,so I am there to support Daye.I hate being so far from her for so long.\nA few months had passed and I was out patrolling Norland, I was told to check an old keep that house Tonsali had previously used.My instructions were to 'check if anyone was inhabiting it',as I looked around it was quite obvious that it was not in use\n.I sat on the old walls and wrote a bird to my commander to tell him all I had found,as I sent it a sparrow landed on my shoulder with a letter.It was from Daye telling me the baby was on it's way and that she wanted me to come home,I sent her a bird\ntelling her I was on my way,climbed down off of the old wall and headed to Calethia.\n  Arriving at home I could see that Daye was not down stairs so I headed to our bedroom where I found her laying on the bed. She told me to get some water and a towel\nso I did,when I returned I placed the towel on the bed and went to her side.\n  Sitting on the edge of the bed,I smiled at Daye and our new born son.Jericho.She seemed exhausted but she was still smiling,Jericho was asleep so I told her to give\nhim to me so she too could get some sleep. She questioned what I would do if he cried and I just told her I could take care of him,she then made me promise that I would bring him to her if he cried and I said I would,she then fell asleep and I headed down\nstairs with Jericho.\n   After a few hours I went back up stairs to check on Daye.She was still asleep until she herd me close the door,then she began to sit up in bed.I teased her a little and sat down on the bed beside her,still holding Jericho.Who was\nstill asleep.Daye then moved closer and hugged my shoulder, looking at our son.She\nsaid how lovely he was and that he was ours,\nthen I teased her for stating the obvious.I then handed her Jericho and placed my arm around her,I asked her how she slept\nand she told me it was easy to sleep when your exhausted and I said I would be concerned if she was not tired after having a baby.Then Jericho began to cry.Daye said that it was possibly because he was hungry and told me that I could leave while\nshe fed him, I left and waited outside our room until she was finished.After a short while she came out of our room with Jericho and I could see that he was sleeping, she also still seemed quited tired.I moved the crib into our bedroom and Daye placed\nJericho in it.Then she went back to sleep and I headed back down stairs to write to my commander telling him why I was no longer on patrol.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jacques' Poem", "Septimius Bracchus", "Senescence looms upon me as Prince-Bishop of Metz/Akin to any thoughtful man I reflect on my eminence,/Yet even my pride cannot strike a memory of Opulence,/Of Johannesburg, before Lotharingian Independence./Conjuring images as if I was to be\npossessed,/John III appears before me each time I try to rest,/Towards me this solemn man progressed,/“Do you think for your treachery that you will be blessed?”/Horror it is then even to dream,/For I do so as a younger and better man,/Worse\nyet, of everything in the capital I recall,/Comrades still merry and alive before this all./Birds beckoned dawn and sang a song,/I awoke and the fleeting dream neared gone,/What I recalled though had swallowed my soul,/For I struck humanity to\nensure its Empire wasn’t whole./                 -Prince Bishop of Metz, Jacques d'Amaury.", ""),
        StaticBook("Jarseks ERP Logs", "Frederick 'Mulligan' Santiago", "I had sex with a Kha today\n\n\n~2/21/2019\n\n\n\nI Stole this Stupid book XP\n\n~Ali\nFuckin Perv\n\n~Ali", ""),
        StaticBook("Jayas Journey C5", "Sofetios Jayamen", "Jaya's Journey\n\n            ~By Sofetios\n                 Jayamen\n\n((This is a book I'm actually writing in real life. I really need motivation to continue, so please let me know what you think.))\nChapter Five\n           Cloak\n\nWhen we got up the next morning, when we finished packing up and started walking, I asked Sofetios,\n\n“Where is Northenway?”\n“It’s on the way to the temple.” Said Sofetios. “Why?”\n\n“It’s just there’s a place I’ve wanted to visit for a while.” I lied. “A place called the purple café? My Mom told me about it once.”\n“We aren’t making any un necessary stops.” Said Sofia. “We need to get to the temple.” I didn’t want to argue, so I figured I would wait until we got there to ask again.\nAs we approached the gates of Northenway, we were approached by guards.\n\n“Halt.” Said one of the guards. “What business do you have in Northenway?”\n\n“Just passing through.” Said Sofetios.\n“Really, do you think we were born yesterday?” Said the other guard. “You are playing hooky from school. Aren’t you?”\n\n“Relax.” Said Sofia. “We came from the Village south of here. No need to get mad.”\n“Hey, you better watch yourself girly.” Said the guard back. “Or Ill make you.” That was a mistake.\n\n“Girly!?” Said Sofia steaming. Sofia was about to go off.\n“Come on Rodrick.” Said the other guard. “Let’s just go for a bit, I think our break time is on anyway. Let’s just go to The Purple Café and relax a bit, eh?”\n“Fine, see you later miss.” The guard said with a chuckle. After the two left Sofia seemed to be trying to cam herself down. Then she said,\n\n“I think we should go to The Purple Café.”\nWe entered the city, which had its town square up front. In the middle there was a man in a white robe saying things to a small crowd that had gathered. He was saying,\n“The sun dims every day! Can you not feel it? It’s as though the days are getting shorter! The nights longer! Be vigilant, the time to prove ourselves comes!”\n\n“What is he talking about?” I said.\n“It’s part of the prophecy.” Said Sofetios. I frowned a bit as we made our way down the street to a large restaurant. There was a sign hanging from the door that showed a coffee mug with steam coming from it.\nOn the top of the sign it said ‘The Purple Café’.  As we approached the door Sofia stopped and looked at a notice on the door. We gathered around it, it said,\n‘Arm wrestling day. Tournament will be in mid day. The grand champion gets 100 gold! Sign up here.’ Then there was a list of names and blank spaces. Under the notice was a pen and ink.\nSofia put her finger on the list then went down until she stopped at ‘Rodrick’.  Sofia wrote her name down so fast I thought for sure her name would be illegible. Someone came out of the door and looked at us. It was a waitress.\n“Just getting the sign up sheet.” She said taking it down and carrying it inside. We entered the café. It looked amazing. There were people at the bar drinking and the waitress cutting names off the list and putting them in a cup.\nThere was also a band playing tavern music. Then I noticed another waitress staring at us. She walked up to us and said,\n\n“Are you kids going to order something or just stand there?”\n“I’m in the arm wrestle competition.” Said Sofia. Not waiting, Sofia walked past her and went toward a table. The waitress then looked at Sofetios and I. “We’re going to watch her compete”. Said Sofetios, The waitress sighed and said,\n“Fine, just don’t cause any trouble.”\n\n“We won’t” I said. As we went in the waitress who was cutting up the names went to the center of the restaurant, then said,\n\n“Alright! Is everyone ready to arm wrestle?”\nThere were cheers through the restaurant. “Ok then. The first two contenders are…” She put her hand in the cup and drew two names. “First we have Rodrick!” There were roars from a table in the corner as the guard from before got up, Flexing.\n“Please come to the center table!” as Rodrick got there, the waitress with the names looked at the other one and said, “Second we have…” The waitress seemed to squint at the paper.\nI cringed, there was only one person that could be. “Sofia! Come to the middle table!” Rodrick was looking back at his table, which was chanting his name over and over again.\nWhen Sofia got to the table Rodrick turned to her, waited a moment as he recognized her, then laughed. \n\n“This girly is my first competition?” Said Rodrick.\n“You bet I am, unless you want to back down?” Said Sofia with a smile. There where “oo’s” from the crowd. \n\n“You’re on girly.” Said Rodrick as he smiled back. There were cheers throughout the restaurant again.\nSofia and Rodrick sat down at opposing ends of the middle table. The whole restaurant then counted, “Three!” “Two” “ONE!” There was a loud slam and a thud and it was over. The band stopped playing.\nSofia stood over Rodrick who she had slammed his arm so hard on the table he had flipped over out of his chair to the floor. He wasn’t moving. The people from his table went over and tried to pick him up.\n“Is he dead?” The waitress said concerned.  One of them put an ear to his chest and said,\n\n“Nah, he’s just drunk. Let the tournament continue!” Everyone cheered and the tournament continued.\nSofia was about to step down when the waitress said,\n\n“Wait, you need to stay up here until you lose.”\n\n“Wait, what?” Said Sofia. “Well this is going to be fun then.” I then remembered why I was here.\nI went to the waitress who wanted us to order something and said,\n\n“Could I get the Basement table?” The Waitress raised an eyebrow and said,\n“We don’t have a basement table, but we do have an attic one. Follow me.” I followed the waitress upstairs to a door. She opened it went inside as I followed. Inside was a figure in a black hood and black robes.\n“Keep watch.” He said. The waitress nodded, went out, and closed the door.\n\n“So you’re C?” I said taking out the letters\n\n“Yes.” Said the person in the robes. “But you can call me Cloak.”\n“How do you know I have the weapons?” Said Sofetios. \n\n“I know how to use Lin in ways other then your friend Sofetios showed you.” Cloak said as he got up and got a bowl from a shelve and put it on the table. He got a jug and poured water into the bo\n“Come look for yourself.” I went closer and looked into the bowl. I didn’t see anything. “One moment” He said. He pulled out a very small vial with white liquid in it. \n\n“What is that?” I said.\n“This.” He said. “Is my own lin.”\n\n“What?” I said in a slightly raised tone. There were massive cheers downstairs.\n\n“Observe.” He said as he uncorked the vial and poured it into the bowl.\nThe white liquid spread until it reached all sides of the bowl. Then Cloak put one finger so it was barely touching the side of the bowl and an image came in. It was of Sofia In at the Middle table downstairs with a huge smirk on her face.\nThe other hand was being held up by the waitress.\n\n“It seems your Friend won another round.”\n\n“How are you doing that, and who are you?”\n“I am simply using my mind to see through my Lin.” Said Cloak. “I can see places nearby, or farther if my will allows me. As to who I am.” Said Cloak removing his hood. He looked no older then I was.\n“I am the last member of the Omira.\"\n\nEnd of Chapter Five", ""),
        StaticBook("John I Frederick", "Commodus de Jedih", "sssssssssssssssssssJOHN I FREDERICK,\nHOLY ORENIAN EMPEROR 1498-1547\nsssssssssssssssssss\n\nBy Logan Macdonough, a Harrenite scholar, in an excerpt from his treatise Reflections on the Emperors of Mankind, 1602\n\nTranscribed by Comm.\nA drawing of John I hunched over his table analyzing battle plans.\n\nJohn I at His Table, 1623, Carlo Bragonolo\n\nddddddddddddddddddd\n\n“As long as his conquering armies went from one victory to the next,-\nJohn’s subjects remained boundlessly obedient, his rule and claim unchallenged. When a string of humiliating defeats by the nonhuman alliance proved him and his tacticians fallible, his enemies domestic would crouch, ready to strike like vipers-\nfrom within. He had ruled for twenty-one years, eighteen of which were total war, aging from a youth of twenty-and-eight winters to a bitter, gouty despot who had lived for just under half a century. His detractors called him a tyrant and his apologists -\nsaid that such was necessary in times of war and conspiracy.\n\nJohn sought to provide strong leadership and steadfast unity in a time of political disarray, in opposition to the debased and inhuman masses of the south-\nwho wished to see humanity divided and weak. While he had ultimately failed in breaking the cycle of disharmony, for a time he succeeded in stalwart opposition to perfidious Urguan, conquering a number of provinces (See appendix for Cascadia,-\nAvar, Erochland, Esterwick) and bringing peace, culture and law to much of the Imperial heartlands. The Emperor would leave behind seven children, six of his wife and one illegitimate, with his daughter Charlotte believed to have predeceased him,-\naswell as five young grandchildren.\n\nThe partnerships he fostered with the various first ministers he employed in the seat of the Archchancellor were legendary and the source of much of his success-\nfirstly his father the monk Charles Polycarp, secondly the Courlander Publius Bracchus, thirdly the prodigious Adrian of Rothesay and finally the greatest of his favorites, Augustus d’Amaury, whose unparalleled diligence was alone-\nresponsible for most of his success during the last third of his reign. This relationship with the Archduke was judged sorely by many of the other nobility - who found such a reliance befitting of any active monarch.\nHowever, historians have revisited the emperor’s complex relationship with the enigmatic d’Amaury - the wordsmith and poet Patrick Tilley contends the belief that ‘their various skills complimented one another, and on a personal level -\ntheir friendship was vital to the continuance of the union, for in the many fields where John was weak, Augustus was strong, and vice-versa.'\n\nThe contemporary clergyman Michiel de Loquelier was far more critical of John I-\nwriting that he was a ‘flinty, prickly, pale creature who hunched upon his throne, nursing whatever minor grievance he could perceive’ and that his ‘singular true virtue was his apparent lack of the vices of greed and lust’.\nSimilarly, the bard Hugh Anthony Cregg, more commonly known as Hugh of Lewes, wrote the following limerick (For which he was flogged by the Duke of Istria, Arthur Roswell, then Count of Pompourelia, in 1531):\n“Our emperor wears a saintly ring,\nHis word no man relies on,\nHe never said a foolish thing,\nBut never did a wise one.”\n\nMy opinion on the matter is best reflected by the writings-\nof the Kaedreni scholar Morvran aep Rheyndeith, who called John I Frederick ‘irrevocably flawed, though arguably an improvement on his immediate predecessors - his reign was not only characterized-\nby his selflessness, fairness and his incomparable dedication to the betterment of his country and people, but also by his inability to attain their love and approval,’ writing further that ‘his hatred for the old aristocracy-\nand reliance on several favorites meant that his every action would inevitably transpire contrary to the people’s wishes’.\n\nAlmost immediately after his death, the (Somewhat apocryphal) manner in which his body was preserved became an urban -\nlegend among the peasantry, who took to calling the kind of dark rum his body was immersed in ‘Emperor John’s blood’ or for short ‘Johnsblood’.\n\nOne thing is certain - the Holy Orenian Emperor who, at the height-\nof his popularity all thought would lay the Urguanites to rest would ultimately fall short of that goal, being laid to rest in a tomb of his own before he saw his work come to fruition.”\n\n\n\n\ndddddddddddddddddd", ""),
        StaticBook("John's Theory", "Johnathan Faroe", "The Light: \nMy thoughts on the Light have never truly strayed from one common idea. The Light acts as a guide for all that is good in the world. It is the shield to protect the Grey from the Dark. I almost think of it as a holy crusader.What I mean is\nthat the Light, while it guides the Grey towards good, its apathetic to how it does that. The ends justify the means so to speak. This is why I believe caution in need when using the Light. While its capable of great feats, there is no greater danger then\nman who thinks himself completely righteous. \n\n\nThe Grey: \nSimply put, the Grey is the over all balance in the world. while it will always intrinsically lean towards good, the Light and Dark will always struggle to sway its direction.\nThe Grey is always capable of both good and evil. It's important to remember that. because of this, I characterize it as a bystander who has not yet acted. \n\nThe Dark:\nIt is the complete opposite of the Light. Where the Light would see mercy, the Dark\nwould see death, Where the Light would lead the Grey towards good, the Dark would lead it astray. I characterize the Dark as an endless void. A place where impure creatures thrive. A place of entropy; a place where all things end.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal", "Unknown", "[!] The handwriting looks rather messy, though the words are still readable.[!]\n\n*Get herbs!\nElf's Hair Vine\nDrake's Tail\nAthin\nMetzli's Tangle\n\nAsk Ibar or Rose if they have Alabaster leaf.\n[!] On this page there is a sketch of a rather short tower made of stone, a little pond shimmers in the sunlight next to it.  Some tulips peak out through a light layer of snow near the water.[!]\n\n[!]In the same handwriting as page before reads, --\n-- \"Couldn't sleep, this dream was about him again.  It was the same night when he returned, though I wasn't able to do what I wanted.  Instead of me fleeing like I did when it was real I froze in fear as the door bursted open.  I couldn't do anything --\n-- but watch as he came closer.  Before he got into the doorway I woke up.\"[!]\n\n[!]The rest of the page is just sketches of several different types of herbs and flowers.  A few of the lower sketches looked a little smudged, thought you can still point --\n-- them out.[!]  [!]On this page you see a sketch of a mountain, what looks like a cave is on the side.  On the bottom of the slope there's a giant figure that looks frozen.[!] [!] Next is a sketch of a frozen lake below a steep slope, a giant ice --\n-- pillar sticks up from the ground near the slope and lake.  At the top of the slope it looks like there's some platform, below it, in the lake, there's a hole in the ice.\nWritten near the sketch reads, \"Weird place near tall mountain with ice and --\ngiant ruins with thanium and a tower\"[!] [!]Another sketch has been scribbled down, this one is of a pudgy, grey bird with a flower held in its beak, another sketch besides it shows the bird fluttering with a bunch of white peonies clutched in its feet[!]\n\"Had another dream, this time the tower burnt down with me in it.  Another dream-- #//.... ##// \\\\\" The rest of the entry is scribbled out.[!] [!]A few sketches of several designs of a strange mask are on the next few pages, one of them --\n-- is a blue mask with red hood, a steel mask with a red hood, and a few more.  They all go with a red hood.  Signed below them reads, \"Barnak designs\"[!] Here is a note that sits between the pages, looks a bit worn but still --\n-- readable.  The note first starts with a scribbled out name, \"B-/#/--,  I found something you might want to see... This thing reads, 'Herein lies Dralazar, Herald of Xion, Lord of Torment.  We are born by the dark; Made men by the Dark; Undone by the --\n-- Dark; We fear the Old Dark.'  *Next on the note is a scribble of what looks like a map, in the south there seems to be a little settlement, it's labeled Carnatia.  To the north in the mountains is labeled 'Ruins' just before the ruins --\n-- there's an area that's circled.* Signed, N-#..-\"[!]\n[!]\"Get soft relaxant for Kale.[!] [!] \"These dreams still continue even though H#//.- is gone.  A part of me thinks he will somehow come back like he did before, and when he does come back, it'd\n-- be the death of me.  This thing that I do with #o--+/n Taskan kinda helps take my mind off of it, plus I enjoy helping others.[!] [!] The rest of the page is just a rather detailed sketch of a peach plant, there's small white flowers around them.[!]\n--\n[!] Another note rests between the pages, this reads, \"Leave this land before I claim it myself.\"[!] [!]A sketch at the bottom of the page is scribbled out rather harshly.[!]\n-- [!]A sketch is on this page, it's of a narrow clawed figure with antlers.  Written below it is, \"Drawing from wendigo\"[!] [!]Here is a detailed sketch of ruins, snow rests atop of the cold bricks as the arches loom over the steps, leading to a tower --\n-- on the side of a mountain.  The tower looks over the ruins that sit at the bottom of steep, snowy mountains.  Labeled near the drawing reads, \"Sketchy plance north of Carnatia\"[!] [!] \"Continue to have trouble sleeping, nightmares --\n-- aren't as often as they were when they started.  They come about every other night or so, still about him.  I've sort of gotten use to being tired all the time, I don't really go out alone as much anymore unless it's on one of my walks.  We continue --\n-- to visit those ruins north of Carnatia, something is really off about that place.  Other than that, life is quiet.  I like it.[!] Another sketch is here, this one of a few potions and vials with flowers and herbs neard their bases, the soft --\n-- flowers are like a soft cushion for the small vials.[!] [!]\"Get mandragora, serpents stalk, dwarf's pumpkin, flametounge root, drake's tail, alabaster leaf, metzli's tangle, saffvil, and clutchers straw.\"[!] [!]A few houses --\n-- made of stone are sketched onto the page, one looks rather round and neat.  Another tall and ragged, though still nice.  Another, the stone looks oddly shaped, it looks elegant.[!] [!]\"Day one: 38 minas. Day two: 171 [!]\n[!]In messy, yet readable, handwriting reads a message,[!] \"Robe designs for Kelian.\" Below the scribble are a few sketches of an elf in dark robes, each sketch's robe design is different than the other.[!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal #1", "Serris of Deep Harbour", "11th of the Deep Cold\n207\n-------------------It has been nearly six months since we moved the Temple, and I can still hardly believe it. \n\nAs much as I think Haevolt a fool, this is ... unprecedented. To move an entire temple, from the depths of\nYatl to miles below the oceans near Kahaer? Simply remarkable.\n\nIf he could manage this, then maybe it's possible he COULD create his Titans. That way, we could finally cease our vigil and leave this accurssed Drakaar to slumber for eternity and never\npose a threat to Atlas again.\n\nI do not trust Haevolt as far as I can spit, but he may be our best hope. Atlas needs us elsewhere.\n\n-Lord Marshall Serris of the 2nd Banner", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal #1", "Ogdan Frostbeard", "Ogdan's Journal\n===================     Highly Personal\n\n\n If found, please do \n not open. Please do\n not read the contents\n of this journal.\n\n\n #1\nI have taken on an apprentice. His name is Grungot Frostbeard.\n((Reeper450))\n\nHe seemed to show very little interest.\n\nThe Grand King, Bastion Ireheart, has promoted me to High Engineer. I could not be more honored.\nI have taken an order for six pouches of blaze powder at ten minas each to an Alfred Boylen.\n((nickdabeast135))\n\nI shall keep in touch should he ever need more supplies.\nAnother lad by the name of Chrysanthos,\na High Elf, came to me very eadger about learning the arts of engineering. He seems to be the most promising apprentice I've had so far.\n((Zyra_Bot))\nAvilla Frostbeard, daugter to Kerwyr has asked me to craft her a brewing stand. I accepted for the price of fifty minas. It should be done soon.\n\nI have started progress on Kerwyr's project. We've decided to make some minas off the investment.\nWe are going to split the profits 60/40. I think that's fair for how much he has provided for me.\n\nAvilla's brewing stand is ready for pickup.\n\nI have spoken with Kalviin. He agreed to help me build the workshop. I now need\nto speak with the king once more.\n\nChrysanthos is crafting the blaze rod. Soon enough, I can get this damned workshop up! I'm sick of splitting the room with him...\n\nTads, a dwarf, was interested in joining. I should speak with him.\n12th Grand Harvest, 1594\n\nThe Coalition is Victorious. Defeating Oren for the second time, their Morale is diminished. I forsee a very quick downfall of the Holy Oren Empire.\n\nThe question it leaves me, what will happen to the loyalists?\nWhere will they find refuge? Unwanted by almost every other settlement, perhaps the Mali will take them in. Who knows.\n\n\n\nOn another note:\nThe Grand King has granted me permission to build a workshop in\none of two places, above the current smithing and mining guilds. Or, directly across, close to the Starbreaker clan hall.\n\nI should get some men to help me clear it out and design it better, although I have some faith in my abilities.\nI should also prepare a list for the king. Supplies will be necesary!\n\nI have prepared the list and he has fulfilled it! Sucess! Just need to speak with Kalviin and acquire a few helpers and the workshop will be underway,\n18th Grand Harvest, 1594\n\nUnknown beings have assaulted the gates of Kal'Omith. Their leader, claimed to be in possesion of the Axe of Urguan. He said he was also capable of destroying the whole dwarven Kingdom. It seems we have a new\nfoe nipping at our toes...\n\nThe King has tasked me with destructing caves. I shall try to bring along an apprentice to two to show them how to wire a circut. It will be a great learning experience, as well as a grand explosion.\nI have blown the caves as requested. An unfortunate dwed was trying to save the tunnels for some odd reason, however the king ordered me to blow them. So I did. Killing a fellow Dwed... I'm sometimes lay awake in bed, thinking about this moment....\nI have started progress on my workshop. It is going impressivly well. Everyone seems to enjoy it.\n\nThe Frostbeards and Grandaxes had a meeting. Grandaxes were returning to the Kingdom and were willing to sign the\nMountain Treaty/Pact?\nThey acknowledged their past wrongdoings of our clans. We came to an agreement to leave it up to the Irehearts, the other clan in the pact, to decide whether or not the Grandaxe clan will be granted permission.\nThe King stopped by the workshop. He seemed impressed. I was honored, to say the least. He requested I make him a brewing stand, which I have started promptly.\n\nI met a fellow Dwed named Agamm Ireheart. He seemed slightly interested in the\nTinkering Guild. Maybe I should try to pursue recruitment.\n((SteamedSushi))\n\nThe Grand King is going to bewed a high elf. I've witnessed them making a date. How.... odd. He even- decided to let HER make the plans... I am astounded.\nAgamm has returned. He seems quite confident in his redstone abilities. I am eadger to test him.\n\nI spoke about slag weaponry, I cant seem to get it off my mind...\nI need to find a way to encase it with sturdy enough material to move it, aswell as\na material that is frail enough to bust upon impact. I wonder....\n\n22nd of the Amber Cold, 1594\n\n===================", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal #2", "Serris of Deep Harbour", "3rd of Malin's Welcome\n205\n-------------------The first of the Titans has been completed. \n\nAfter I made a mockery of Haevolt's prototype last year, I did not have high hopes that we would ever see these Titans, but\nyesterday's display has ... changed my mind.\n\nSister Theodorus, he called it. A Golem more advanced than anything I've seen, forged from pure steel and imbued with the powers of ice and water. It is startlingly intelligent, and I daresay its power\nmight be enough to keep the Drakaar at bay.\n\nFor all our sakes, it better. I await to see the next model of the Titan; Brother Thorodus.\n\n-Lord Marshall Serris of the 2nd Banner", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal #3", "Serris of Deep Harbour", "9th of the Sun's Smile\n206\n-------------------It is done. At last we can take our leave from this accursed temple.\n\nBrother Thorodus is complete. Made from steel almost tougher than his Sister, he is imbued with fire and electricity. Combined\nwith Sister Theodorus' ice and water, the Drakaar shall never pose a threat to Atlas. Ever again.\n\nIt's time we bid them farewell. The Vaeyl Order has other threats to terminate. Atlas' safety is never assured.\n- Lord Marshall Serris of the 2nd Banner", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal 1", "Cultist Survivor", "The days tick by as we await his orders. With Koryk slain by the heretics, the plan marched closer towards completion. I have heard from my siblings that we may be sent out to eliminate the turn coat.\nSuccess! With the blessings of Vilketa I have been able to construct my own crystal caves using our modules.I suspect orders shall soon arrive on how I should proceed.\nOrders have arrived, and they were as I expected. Larwin must be eliminated for his crimes against Vilketa and our Gold Commander. It is a blessing that his memory was taken from him. If our plans should leak out... I would not want to be around the coven\nI have heard rumors from our spies and infiltrators that Larwin has awoken and begun to organize search parties for our Memory Tokens. With the seal that our module contained, I should be safe.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Entry", "Garrond", "Unknown date.\n\nThe war against that woodland God is near at end. We reign supreme in the South, having crushed what the others could not.\n\nThough that is our people alone. I and Wilhelm have set out to these wild woods, near even to\nSeptember's own resting. We've yet one more to seal.\n\nWe're close to them, now. One day away on foot. Then, the war will rest.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Notes", "Cultist of Vilketa", "She Comes soon...\nPassion returns\n\n\n\n\nunder the\nIron visage...\nv\ni\nl\nk\ne\nt\na\nSoon..", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal, I, T.V.", "Thanatos", "Thanatos's Journal\n-\n(Base Information)\n\n Making this journal out of Inspiration of a dear friend of mine her name is Nona.\n\n She also has her own journal if you. The reader cares about this information..\nMayor of Pembroke~\n\nMy name is Thanatos as you may presume..\nI am writing this journal for reasons as listed.\n\n I will be attempting to explain my story of becoming a Mayor of this town from the start to the current day..\n(Reference Pages)\n\n Chapter One: Page 5\n\nChapter Two: Page 32\n\n\n\n\n\n My next book will persist of the other chapters...\n\nChapter One...\n\n Traveling out from where I had originally resided..\n I'm a a pianist and a bard..\n I stumble across a large manor esc. structure on a hill..\n There was a large field with a couple smaller buildings surrounding the\n-large building.. Now to think of it.. it was more like a fort..\n I'd met a man named Ser Henry Lodmund and we'd exchanged pleasantries..\n\"G'day lad, To who're you..?\" Ser Henry would quote as I replied with.. \"Ti's I'm Thanatos Vhey.. A traveler...\"\nHe'd looked me down at my general apparel clearly not of residence to any lands and quoted..\n \"Say you have a job..?\" I'd replied to his question saying..\n\"I'm more a traveler... I'd not done much jobs but I'd like one if you have one avaliable..\"--\nHe'd grinned and walked me up to a building.. It was a small tavern esc. building..\nHe'd given me residency in the building and allowed me to sell drinks and such there as my work.. I'd brew drinks and sell drinks...\nThere was no sleeping grounds so I---\nhad to dig out under the tavern a place to reside.. A trapdoor in the floor to allow me to move downstairs and up at ease..\n\n I'd say a week had went by before my house was fully complete.. Not anything Mayor-like yet... Just a hole of dirt under a drunk-\nen mans feet..\n\n---some of this information I'm writing has to do when with the tavern was complete so let's resume with what happened before I was designing (the time inbetween the designing of the tavern underside)\nSer Henry was showing me the tavern and I had encountered an undead in a suit outside...\n Ser Henry spotted him up the road.. A nasty little bug named Valkenier.. He will be listed later in the story for another reason...\nThe undead was strapped in a suit of Blackish Rusty Armoring.. and talked Ghoulishly at me..\n\"OOoooOOoh.. A neewWw suBBjEcct\"\nValkenier would quote as he'd look crookedly and me and Ser Henry..  I'd stand confused...\nSer Henry would state for him to go away and the undead refused to leave..\n\n This is where it got hectic..\n\n Ser Henry would draw his blade on the undead..\nHe'd requested of me\n\"Thanatos, draw a weapon.. now..\" I'd ---\n-listen to him and draw my sword.. It was a bad piece of equipment but a sword is a sword..\n He'd made threats and such at the undead.. To no prevail the undead would not back away..\n This would upset Ser Henry and Henry and I would charge at him around--\n--the same time.. The Ghoulish undead turned around in a panic and scurried off toward a hole in the distance..\n\n Ser Henry ordered me to NOT enter the hole...\n To which we stopped for a moment and investigated the outside..\nAs we investigated there was blood leading in from the doorway.. Turns out the hole was an abondon Mining Project.. There was a roughed up patch of earth outside assumed from some sort of Sacrifice..\n\n Ser Henry gestured in and I would slowly --\n-move on forward ahead of Ser Henry..\n\n There's a wide open corridor and an      Iron door at the end of the corridor.. But there was a ladder way down half broken to reach the iron door at the end of the corridor.. We'd walked into the Corridor. Visited-\n-by hole inside the walls that have hollow spaces where it felt like you could be watched all around..\n\n We'd slowly made our way in with a patch of stone behind us popping up trapping us in..\n The undead Valkenier would speak up saying ----\n---\"TheeEEErreEE's, NoooOOoo EscAPpe\"\n\n Thanatos(me) and Ser Henry would attemp to look down the ladder where the iron door was.. A small hole with a half broken ladder..  You could still climb it if you tried but it's a bit roughed up..\nThanatos and Ser Henry were in for a fight.. We'd have our Swords at the ready as the undead would show himself.. We'd stepped away from the iron doorway to the Corridor met with him showing up at the top of the ladder..\nIn a loud burst of words Valkenier (the undead ghoul) would state \"YoOOuUUu FooOOOOlllsSs\"\n-- \"YoUU'd CoMMEee HEEreEe\" and would then go onto laugh..\n\nSer Henry would charge at him hitting him in the chest and slicing him almost clean in two... But...--\nIt looks like he wasn't even phased.. The undead menace was a brick wall, Metaphorically..\n\nThe undead would state \"YoOouUU ThiINnKKk YouUU CaNN HuurRRttt MEeE?!!\" then going onto swing his sword at Ser Henry.. I'd quickly push up to Ser Henry\nas the undead stated his sentance..\n The undead was preparing his swing and I would kick Valkenier as Ser Henry tried to back away..\n\n The undead wasn't phased or so we thought.. He'd then attempted a retreat..--\nThe undead would open up the iron door down the hole springing in and locking it..\n\nHe'd unlock the enterance we came and yelled at us the same we did when he showed to Pembroke..\n\n\"GEeeTtt OOOouOuut..!\"\n----\nWe'd flee from the undeads trapping grounds and make our way outside..\n\n We were lucky to escape unscaved...\n \n We'd come back to the residence to meet a man named Kagura..\n\nA strange man with Silver Hair.. Human..\nWe'd chat a bit and he'd move on through the small bit of town we had at the time.. \n\n\n Ser Henry would approach me again before I entered the tavern stating..\n \"Ehmm.. Lad.. You did some good fighting.. I'd like to ask you to be in our army..\"\nHe'd offer..\n\n I thanked him stating..\n\"I'm sorry but I don't think I could take that sort of job.. I'm more of a laid back person.. Things like this tavern job are more down my alley.. I'm not a fan of violence but I love the idea you find me worthy to--\njoin the army of Pembroke.\" Which at the time was also very small.. There was little to no Residence..\n\n He replied.. \"Aye.. I see.. Wel' then.. I'll see what the count thinks of you..\" \n\nI'd sit questionable at the tavern counter at what he said..\n\"Ask about what..?\"\n\nEdward Suffolk the Count of Pembroke has approached me a couple days later.. he'd talk to me about small things like my dreams and goals and I'd question him of things..\n The conversation became closed to a halt as he stated..\nsome words that I would never forget...\n \"How would you like to be Deputy Mayor of Pembroke, I'd been looking for a Deputy mayor for a while..\"\n\n     I'd pause fumbling at the question thinking of what I should even say to reply to this offer...\nI'd accept the offer moments later stating..     \"Oh... I'd love that..\"\n He'd smile and I'd chuckle afterwards..\n\n\n   That's the story of how I became..                Deputy... Mayor..\n  But not mayor... atleast not yet..\nChapter II.\n\n I'd become Mayor and would preceed to do Mayorly duties..\n\n Around this time one of the most beautiful women I'd encountered has walked into town..\nAlijol Inkalla.. She will make multiple appearances in my life later on..\nSer Henry has requested of me that I'd give her a tour of the place.. and I had..\nI'd show her to places and joke with her and had a fun time and she did as well.. She, Alijol was a Snow Elf.. not a Human as I, Thanatos was.. I'd go onto offer to her--..\n\"I'll show you the inside of the Courts Fort.. if you promise not to tell.. Showing you some parts might be not so swell of me to do.. I could be even beheaded..\" she'd reply hapilly.. \"I'd love to tour the place with you if you are sure..?\"-- I'd reply.\nI'm sure we could do this.. The count as of the time was resting during the day after some hard labor he had in endured..\n\n I'd then go onto open the front doorway to what is the Counts Fort.. We'd walked in and I'd show her just about every single room.\nThen.. we'd hit the point which is the Garden...\n \n As we would walk through the doors she'd looked in awe at the nature and beauty of his open gardenway.. It contained a pool as well which she was facisnated with...\nWe'd made plans that later the night we would sneak into there and use his pool.. \n\n So we did.. we relaxed and had a great bonding experience..\n\nWe'd became much closer friends...\n\nVery... close...\nThe next day..\n\n There was a man who was named Virkian Agnew who showed up today for housing.. This day Ser Henry would be giving the tours..\n Also the Kagura fellow mentioned before had joined the army..\nAlijol had became close to me so we'd be around each other as much as I could.. I'd do my duties as a Dep. Mayor and the town would slowly fill itself up more and more..\n\n I'd been caving out the bottom of my tavern to hit a Hot Spring located under the..\n--dirt below.\n I'd connected my basement home to a wonderful hot spring..\n\n From that day my home was a bit steamy until I added a venting system for the steam to follow outward..\n\n I'd eventually set a mood and invited Alijol to see my findings..\nShe'd happily agreed and we'd had multiple different times where we'd stopped to go to the springs relaxing as friends and becoming slowly more..   We'd eventually started courting..  Lord Edward, Gladfully did not have a problem with this...\nThe town was lively as there was a Crypt above a hill across the river..\n I.. never really noticed it.. Surprisingly..\n It'd be pointed out by someone else that I'd learned of this..\nA couple days after my learnings of this place there was a skeleton man with red robes and no visible eyes through his skull which was odd.. I'd never seen an undead skeleton before.. Even before Valkenier I'd never seen an undead even..\naround this time I would be showing a nun girl around town and Kagura and Ser Henry both army men.. and Virkian who became a trader were attempting to fight.. We were all around a good distance of the Skeleton man.. We'd attempted to talk to him..\nKagura would spit out the words agressively..\n \"What do you want with us! State your name undead..\"\nin which the undead replied.. \"Hektor.. Hektor... Blackwood...\"\n\n We'd pause for a moment and he'd reveal a blue liquid in a bottle bubbling and\nglowing..\n\n Some of us would step away.. I and the nun girl were a decent distance way but she was closer compared to me which I was a bit further..\n\n Alijol was not around at the time thankfully..\nHektor would break the potion upon the ground creating a thin smoke of blue-gray..\n\n People around the smoke who were speaker and not as muscular.. would drop to the ground including the nun..\n First thing I'd do is grab someone and carry them to the...\ntavern so they could be safe from the attack.. and hopefully recover..\n\n Closest person to me was the nun girl..\n So I'd pick her up and sit her in the tavern..\n\nWhen I'd come back out Ser Henry would be fighting with the undead..\nBy then most of the smoke has dissapated into the air and Kagura was catching his fresh air.. He'd been cought in the sleeping gas only briefly.. he was fine..\n\nVirkian was weakened struggling to stand at this point.. I'd rescued him from the smoke next.\nthen after Virkian was put up I'd dragged out a man named Arndt Sauer.. He's a lanky man in black robes and eyes as hard as a snake... I can see why the gas had put him out with ease...\n\n( Check book two for information on the next chapter.. )", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal, II, T.V", "Thanatos", "Thanatos's Journal\n-\n(Base Information)\n\n Making this journal out of Inspiration of a dear friend of mine her name is Nona\n\n She also has her\nown journal if you.\nThe reader cares about this information\nMayor of Pembroke~\n\nMy name is Thanatos as you may presume..\nI am writing this journal for reasons as listed\n\nI will be attempting to explain my story of becoming Mayor of this town from the start to the current day..\n(Reference Pages)\n\n Chapter III, Page 5\n\n Chapter IV, Page 18\n\n\n\n\n\n(Read Volume III for the rest of the story..)\n\nChapter III...\n\n ...After they'd all been rescued and brought to safety Thanatos would attempt to wake them up from their sleeping spell.. Starting with the nun girl...\n\nThanatos would shake her gently.. seeing what would wake her..\nthe shaking attempt was a success and\n\n Thanatos after a good minute or two was able to wake her..\n\n The nun tried to stand on her two feet and luckily didn't trip on her Nausea...\nShe'd start to wake Virkian Agnew..\n\n Just as Thanatos would attemp to wake the lanky Arndt Sauer..\n\nThe girl unremorsefully smacked Virkian across the face with intention of hurting him on wake...--\n(Probably because he did some.. Sketchy stuff toward the nun..)\n\n Thanatos would wake the sleeping Arndt Sauer..\n\n\n The man was heavily confused on what had happened.. The same goes for Virkian with a red mark across his-\nface..\n\n\n Everyone would attemp to get up and walk outside to watch the fight between the men and the illusionary\n\n        Hektor Blackwood\n\nas they got outside two men were fighting.\nSer Henry was fighting side by side with Kagura.. \n\n Kagura was injured as well as Ser Henry..\n\n Kagura was sliced on the side.. Luckily.. not fatal..\n\nSer Henry was roughed up mostly from small cuts and-\n-being hit with a blunt side of a weapon..\n\n Kagura and Henry would ready their swords as they charge him impaling him from two angles and then pressing him back into the ground..\n\nKaguras sword would snap as the undead broke it in two with--\n-his sword and he'd quickly free himself..\n\n Obviosly injured the undead was forced to try to evade the situation and flee..\n\n Kagura would push Hektor with his now.. Short... sword... and attempt to tackle him..\nHektor blackwood quickly slipped out a blue potion as he hopped the walls and dropped it atop kaguras face as he jumps late.. he misses the tackle..\n\n Some people were amused at his failed tackle.. The blue potion put Kagura.. to sleep..\nWe'd ressusitated at the tavern.. as we did the others prior..\n\n The nun once again would proceed to slap the color into his face.. but this numbskull took a couple smacks to awake.. His face was a ripe tomato that day..\nLater that day I had met with my courting partner Alijol and we'd talked about the intrusion of Hektor..\n\n I'd not explained how she'd looked before..\n I'll explain.\n \n\n (view next page)\nShe would wear a green top with glowing Blonde hair with Golden bells in her hair paired up with Purple and Gold flowers..\n\n She ran the Apothecary in Pembroke.\n\n (view next page)\nShe was also a Snow Elf and I am a Human. (Which... a lot of people would normally dissaprove of these types of things..)\n\n The nun girl has left Pembroke but everyone was fine where they were at..\nChapter IV...\n\n There was five or so undeads that had appeared afront Pembrokes keep..\n\n Guards on the inside requesting a reason for them coming..\nThe undeads were very specific stating they want to speak to Lord Edward Suffolk about certain problematic things...\n\n Lord Edward would appear stating \"What's the meaning of undeads coming upon my door front demanding me.. Best be good..\"\nLord Edwards tone would be cold and stern wearing his armor with a red cape around his backside with expensive weaponry at his hand.\n\n The undeads would reply and state...\n\n \"We have a... common.. enemy... you see....\"\nLord Edward would nod his head saying \n \"I see and who'm is it..?\"\n\n\n The Undeads would reply...\n(I'll have to remove this for.. purposes.. I'm sorry to the reader... ask me in person I might be nice and explain..)\nThe Undeads had intention of creating a temporary truce..\n\n Not to become friends in any way but to be truce..\n\n\nWe were very questionate but Lord Edward made decision to agree and be neutral until the\n-problem has been.. \ndone and over with...\n\n\nWe're no friends to undeads just note..\n\nPembroke has only formed a temporary truce to them for reasons as stated..\nLater on complications between us and the undead has rised..\n\n We'd both grown weary and questionate of one another as a month passed..\n \n Lord Henry was preparing a raid upon the undeads in fear they were going to--\nbreak the truce..\n\n I agreed at the time..\n\n\n We'd prepared to raid them and we'd gathered with the Prince of Hansetti Judah-Principality.\nHe'd brought his men and Edward has prepared our men.. Including me and Edward of course..\nWe wont sit idle while we're at risk from undeads..\nWE'D GATHERED AT THE GATES...\n          PEMBROKE AND THE MEN FROM HANSETTI HAD GATHERED TO ATTACK WITH US...\n\n\n(and this is not Haense it's Hanesetti.\nLord Edward & The Prince would signal people to storm the undead fortress..\nThe lot of us were halted at an iron door..\n\n We'd waited as the undead opened their doorways revealing a room with a pitfall with spikes..\nThe Undeads would welcome us to the fortress...\n\nThey clearly upset we decided to come in with armor and wanted to decide a proper way to avoid fights and conflict as we had them outnumbered...\nWe'd had a larger group.. It was expected they'd find another resolution without risking the downfall of their fort...\n\nSo we continued to play their talking game and decided to make another decision..\nUndeads are NOT allowed to come to Pembroke nor we to come to the Undeads..\n\n It should be noted Humans and Undeads had been traveling to Pembroke and from the Crypt.\nHektor Blackwood ignoring this unknowingly came to Pembroke..\n\n(He was not avaliable the day of our attack.. He was doing other sorts of things away from fort..)\nHektor engaged in a talk with me about undead things.. I'd prefer to leave out this information because it is dangerous information depending on who is aware of these sorts of things..\nHektor mid chat would claim that he spoke too much and demanded me to speak upon a subject as well and I obliged..\n\nHektor asked of me...\n\"You.. think... edward... will... break... this... truce... again...?\"\nIn which I replied..\n\"To what I know I am unsure.. but I wouldn't doubt he's likely not as of now...\"\n\n People had grown suspicious of Hektors visits as he proceeds to come back more and more.. Unaware.. of.. the agreement..\nHektor would ask things of Alijol Inkalla that had made me question if I had been getting too comfortable around him...\n\nShe'd told me what he'd asked when he came into her Apothecary.. She told me at a different occasion..\nShe'd said Hektor had come by and talked to her...\n\n after a while of talking offered to teach her simple brewing..\n\n I was enticed but later on we decided it's not a great idea..\nEdward would not approve of Alchemic uses and possibly even hang her for Witchery..\n\n I couldn't bear the thought..\n\nWe'd decided to turn down Hektors offer..\nI'd talked to Hektor a bit more personally and as he talked about undead things.. which I wont list.. He said he'd write me a book.. Translating these undead things to the human tounge from their language..\n\nI'd agreed to this.. \nHe agreed to this..\nIt was settled that Hektor would write me a book about, \"Undead Things..\"\n\n I do not know why he offered this to me..\n\n But he has told me some of his past..\n\nI'll share for you all..\nHektor had claimed.. \n\"I never wanted to be like this...... it wasn't by choice..... I used to be human.... the world has loved me as a person...... but as I was turned undead...... I watched as all my friends and family...... turned me away..disgusted.\"\nOf course.. this is all written from what I recall.. Sorry if I am not exactly correct if you're reading this\n Hektor.\n\n In which you most likely are..\n\nI'm still expecting a good book..\nDwarves..\n\nFrostbeards and other clans dwarves go together as they were going to raid the Crypt upon the hill...\n\n The people of pembroke watched in confusion to what might have of caused this problem..\nBut... before they came upon the hill.. Some of the dwarves came to town and entered the Tavern where I and Hektor was having a chat..\n\nThey'd took Hektor and used him as an ability to attemp to enter the Crypt..\nThe Dwarves had then... started to travel up the hill..\n They got to the entry-way.. and demanded entry.. after that the dwarves were tossed a what I was told later on as..\n \"A gas that was Toxic like.. Deadly feeling.. even looking at it..\"\nThe undeads had used this to create space inbetween Hektor and The Dwarves for an escape in which he fleed into the Crypt locking the door escaping from the dwarves..\n\n Minutes later.. Dwarves come rushing into Pembroke requesting drinks..\nOf course.. I was also the tavernkeep in which they explained the situation but not why they did it at the time..\n\n When the dwarves had got their drinks and left.. I'd traveled to the Crypt.. in which I had told them I'd got a lot of Dwarven Visitors --\nat my tavern... They'd handed me a green drink stating..\n\n \"You see any dwarves come by your Tavern slip some of this in their drink...\"\n \nAs of the time I am writing this Hamnil Frostbeard is selling Vials of it in Kaz'Ulrah.. I'll explain how..\nI'd came down and went to the tavern sending a bird to Hamnil.. He'd requested Dwarves to pickup the poison as I was in the tavern a couple days later they showed I was once again.. Talking to Hektor.. I'd given them the \"Package..\"\n-End of Volume II.", ""),
        StaticBook("JPH Pass. P0001", "Edward Suffolk", "\n   JUDAIC PRINZIPALITY OV \n          HANSETI\n\n   JUDAIC PRINCIPALITY OF  \n          HANSETI\n\n          PASSPORT\nHis Judaic Highness' Secretary of State requests, in the Name of His Highness the all those \nwhom it may concern to allow the bearer to pass freely, without let or hindrance, and to afford the bearer such assistance and protection as may be necessary.\nPersonal Information\nType: JPHV\nCode: JPH\nPassport No: P0001\nHouse: Suffolk\nGiven Name(s): Edward\nNationality: Suffonian\nSex: Male\nDate of Birth: 20 AC 1632\nBirth Place: Winterfold\nIssuance: 3 SS 1663\nAuthority: PBK\nIn the name and with the authority of his Judaic Highness,\n\n          Issued by\n\nThe Secretary of State of the Judaic Principality of Hanseti,\n     Lord Edward Suffolk\n      (signature & seal)", ""),
        StaticBook("Jumper Rules", "Jaya Jayamen", "Jumper\n           Rules\nJumper is a simple 2 player game. The objective is to take all your opponents tokens. You can only move diagonally.\nYour goal is to jump over the other player’s tokens. You cannot jump over your own tokens. Both players roll a 20 sided dice to decide who goes first(( use /roll 20 )). The player with the higher roll goes first.\nOn your turn you can either move one of your tokens forward one square or jump another player’s token. Then it is the other player’s turn to do the same. After their turn it is your turn again, then after that it is their turn again and so on.\nIn order to jump over a token, there needs to be space on the other side of their piece to jump to. It must be a blank space with no tokens that you jump to. When you jump someone’s token, you take that piece to the side, out of play.\nAfter you take their token, you can jump again with the same token if there is another jumpable token with room on the other side of it.\nYour tokens can only move one direction, forward, there is no backwards until one of your tokens gets to the other side of the board. Then that token is swapped for a lighter colored token. A pink token for player 1 and a light blue token for player two.\nWhen swapping, the piece you are swapping in goes in the same space as the piece that is being swapped out. The token that was swapped in has the ability to move backwards and forwards.\nWhen one player has no more tokens, the person who has tokens wins.\nPositioning the Pieces\n\nYou start with 6 tokens on your side, and 6 on the other player’s side on a 6x6 grid. Player 1 is to use red tokens as pieces and player 2 is to use blue tokens as pieces. Decide who is what color.\nAs to where on the Board your tokens start out, imagine the board like a checkered board that is black and white. You would put your 6 tokens on the bottom side of the board on only black spaces.\nYour opponent does the same on the top side of the board.  So if I were to say how many tokens are there per row on the grid starting at the top and going down, the first row would have 3 of player one’s tokens on that row in the black spaces,\non the next row would be 3 more of player one’s tokens in the black spaces, the next row would be blank, the row after that would be blank, and the next row would have 3 of Player two’s tokens on black spaces,\nand finally the last row would have 3 of player two’s tokens on the black spaces.", ""),
        StaticBook("K.S. EVALUATION", "Doctor Everage", "13th of Snow's Maiden,\n1678\n\nKacper Demetriou-Silma\nAGE: 58\nDOB: 1620\nHEIGHT: 177cm\nWEIGHT: N/A\nPSYCHOLOGICAL EVALUATION\n\n-Mood\nHe feels fine.\n-Happiness\nHe rates it 9/10.\n-Suicidal Tendencies\nHe came close to taking his own life when he was abandoned by his family and lover. He no longer experiences these feelings.\n-Extreme Emotions\nHe claims he experiences outbursts of anger where his blood \"feels like it's boiling.\" He made it clear to me that he experiences pain throughout his entire body during these outbursts. Anytime he feels he's been pushed to his emotional\nlimit, he has an outburst. During his most severe outburst, he threatened to kill his sibling and stabbed someone in the arm.\nNOTE: he was intoxicated at the time.\n-Killing Others\nHe claims he has killed many during his time in the Virarim. He\nseems to be at peace with the concept of killing, if it is for the right reasons. He never feels good about killing others.\n-Thinking?\nWhen I asked him what he was thinking about, he was recollecting his actions as a young high elf. He partook in high\nelven purist groups. He was raised thinking it was normal to torture others. He insisted that he no longer thinks in a purist way.\n-Family Relations\nHe truly feels loved by his Seed and I have no doubts nor concerns about this topic.\n-Empathy\nHe tries to help others as much as he can. He has no issue empathizing with others.\nPHYSICAL EVALUATION\n\n-Artificial Limbs\nNone.\n-Scars or Wounds\nThere is a scar between his right shoulder and neck. There is a scar underneath his right eye.\n-Chronic Pain\nNone.\n-Broken Bones\nNone.\n-Concerns\nNone.\n-Teeth\nFair condition.\nSOUL EVALUATION\n\n-Unusual Nightmares\nNone.\n-Inexplicable Pain\nNone.\n-Involunary Actions\nNone.\n-Concerns\nNone.\nCONCLUSION\n\nKacper is a recovered high elf who has become empathetic regardless of his circumstances. He may need someone to talk to about his feelings of abandonment, or the guilt he feels for what he has done in his past. I am concerned about\nhis angered outbursts, however. His body is in great condition, as is his soul, as far as I can tell.\nTREATMENT\n\nI would like to have him engage in anger management therapy. That way, he can learn how to control his emotions and prevent his enraged outbursts from interfering with his work.\nAPPROVED\n\nDoctor Harlan Everage of the Caras Eldar\n\n15th of Sun's Smile, 1678", ""),
        StaticBook("Kaiser's Love", "High Dictator Frederick II", "===Heil Vandaloria===\n\n\n    The Kaisers Love\n\n\n\n\n    Approved by the\n    Ministry of Truth\n\n\n\n==================\nThe people of Al'Wakhrah slept soundly in their beds when the Ghouls attacked. The three Ghouls stood firm at the entrance to the city, looking for easy targets to consume. Larry Kringle, an Elven officer within the Reich Ministry of Truth, sounded the\nalarm. The Kaisereich answered. The good denizens of the Hallowvale Company answered the call, headed by the Qalasheen Champion of the Hallowvale and the Kaiser himself. The company created a line of Elves and Humans alike at the gate.\nThe three Ghouls would be no match for the Kaisers finest! The elite troops pulled out their aurum blades and laid waste to the evil creatures where they stood. They never even reached the steps to Al'Wakhrah. The Champion and the Grand Conservitor worked\ntogether to take one of the ghouls head clean off! The Kaiser himself slashed with no mercy, finally impaling an aurum dagger int he eye socket of one of the animated corpses. The last was slow, behind the other two. This nightmarish creations of Iblees\norigin were hacked down by an unknown citizen of the Kaisereich. The unknown solider of Good. The Kaiser, under instruction from a wandering Cleric, ordered the building of a fire to burn the bodies of the fetid Ghouls. The group rallies, all lending a\nhand to rid the world of the monstrosities. \n\nThe Kaiser had few words for the valiant group that night, but offered his humbles thanks to all those who helped secure the safety of the children inside the walls of Al'Wakhrah. His humility\nwas unexpected, and took the group by surprise. It was then that they realized, we as an Empire, as Vanderlorians, are stronger together than we are apart. The Humans and Elves worked hand in hand, under the grace of God, and were victorious.\nThe Kaisers strongest words were the quietest spoken. \n\n\n     HEIL VANDALORIA\n     HEIL ROVINKIN\n     HEIL DECIMUS\n     HEIL TRUTH", ""),
        StaticBook("Kal'Arab", "Aeluin Tundrak", "Mostly Underground.\nlarge area\none Main Gate\nWatch Tower near front\nLarge and long walls\nmost farmland,\nLooks dwarven\nand a large chrystal in the main hall\nSeems to have a whole in the ruff", ""),
        StaticBook("Kal'Varak", "Davin Lodmund", "The Kal'Varak\nRescribed by Arch-Mage Crumena V. Illwindor on the 2nd of the First Seed, 1473.The Kal'Varak, which roughly translates as 'Mind City', is an ancient crystalline artifact. It was dug up by the dwarves of Karik just prior to\ntheir unearthing of the hibernating dragons, but the faded scratches on the side suggest it has been discovered at least once before this, perhaps by the original inhabitants of Karik. It seems to be some sort of powerful magical nexus, exerting a\nsignificant magical influence without appearing to draw magical power anywhere, as if it somehow generates it itself. Despite this, the Kal'Varak is useless as a source of magical energy. All of its power is turned inwards on itself, giving the\nKal'Varak the bizzare property that gives it its name. When a living being touches the Kal'Varak, their mind and soul are forcefully drawn from their bodies into the Kal'Varak itself. Once inside, they find themselves in a strange dreamworld, often\ntaking the form of a maze, populated by their memories, dreams and nightmares. In the Kal'Varak, people appear as they would wish to be, some see themselves as stronger, taller, more attractive, sometimes as a different race\nentirely. While the ability to walk through one's mind and the minds of any others currently 'in' the Kal'Varak may seem enticing, the dreamworld is dangerous. The dreamworld responds to moods, fears and doubts, often turning a\nguilty memory into a full-blown nightmare in an instant. The more complex the mind, the more labyrinthian the maze, and those with dark pasts they'd rather forget are often forced to face them within the Kal'Varak. Even more dangerous is\nwhen the mind and crystal form a world that one would not want to leave. The collapsed body outside the crystal still needs food, water, and is still vunerable to harm. If the body dies, the mind cannot return to it. Somewhere in the Kal'Varak maze is\na door, and those more experienced with the dreamworld can find it more quickly than others. The door is always relevant in form to the person it belongs to, often impossible to mistake for one's own. Sometimes the door is not even a door, but it is\nalways clearly an exit. Passing through your door returns you to your body, but if you pass through the wrong door, you may find yourself in the wrong body entirely.", ""),
        StaticBook("Kargala & Snagas", "Falum'Lur", "Long ago, when bands of orcs still roamed the countryside, there lived a wise and powerful shamaness by the name of Kargala. Kargala, a fearsome warrior, destroyed every opponent in her path with her mighty magic. The mere mention of Kargala’s\nname caused nearby pinkskins to scatter. Rumor had it that she cut out the eyes of all her victims and used them in spells. Humans told their children tales of Kargala, warning them never to venture too far from home or else Kargala would snare\nthem with her spells. All throughout Aegis, men whispered stories of Kargala and her strength and cunning. Among the orcs, she was highly revered and many desired her as a mate.Kargala plundered many villages and took many slaves. She had\nseveral of each race. Her favorites, however, were Berach the Dwarf, Brais the Elf, and Baldwin the Human.Berach the Dwarf was foolish and greedy. He stole food and ale from Kargala’s stores and guzzled it in secret. Even the sting of Kargala’s\nwhip would not change his ways. Fat and slothful, Berach waddled more than walked. Sometimes, if he were particularly lazy, he would simply roll along like a boulder. Boastful too, Berach would brag of his past deeds, making bold claims in his\ndrunken stupor. “I fought Iblees m’self!” He would brag, swilling down pint after pint of ale, “The only reason Kargala caught me was because I was…ZzzzZzzz…” He would always fall over asleep before he could finish. However, Berach had a nose\nfor gems, so Kargala kept him.Brais the Elf was even worse. Long legged and proud, he dared to stride beside Kargala as an equal. As punishment, Kargala broke both his legs. Even hobbling on crutches, Brais was ever proud and haughty. With a\nlong, beak-like nose and pouting lips, Brais looked down on everyone he met. “Malin himself praised me,” Brais would brag, “I was a Prince once!” But Kargala, ever wise, saw through his lies. Though proud, Brais would squeak and cower at the\nsight of a single zombie. He would whine, shake, and drool like an animal. However, Brais, with his great age, knew the many lands of Aegis well, so Kargala kept him.Finally, there was Baldwin the Human. Baldwin, cursed by the laziness of his\ncompanions, labored hard under Kargala’s whip. Even so, he complained and complained. “Oh! I am getting so old! Why must I bear this burden alone?” Night and day, he struggled with Kargala’s treasures on his back. He strained so hard that his\nhair turned grey. With every treasure added, Baldwin would complain. “Oh! Tis too heavy! I am but an old man!” Baldwin’s every breath was a groan of complaint. Even under the threat of Kargala’s lash, he moaned and moaned. Even so, his back was\nsteady and he never dropped a single treasure, so Kargala kept him.Kargala’s slaves followed her from town to town, lolling in their uselessness. The other orcs saw Kargala’s slaves and were mystified. Why would Kargala, in her great wisdom,\nkeep haughty and complaining slaves? But the wise orcs saw Kargala’s useless slaves and smiled. Next to the stupid, proud, and cowardly slaves, Kargala looked especially strong, clever, and bold. Men would look upon the slaves and their master\nand know, immediately, that the children of Krug were the strongest and cleverest. Though the slaves caused trouble wherever they went, Kargala solved each problem with her quick wit and sharp sword. “The foolish slaves may cause problems,” The\nother orcs observed, “but Kargala is too clever and powerful to let their foolishness wound her!”Kargala traveled across Aegis with her slaves, proving in each place the strength and wit of Krug’s children.", ""),
        StaticBook("Karyssmov", "Grace", "Brother, \n\nYou asked for reasons, proof that I loved you.. Your words truly took me off guard. \n\nIt hurt, that.. it was clear I was not showing enough signs of my care for you that I had to provide verbal words.\nA sister shouldn't have to do that, one.. should instinctively know such.\n\nBut it is clear I have failed you, I have failed as a comrade and your sister. \n\nYes I am afraid, so terrified that when the day comes that this brand kills me..\npeople will mourn.. cry.\nAt no point do I want this, I want to simply be forgotten.\n\nSo when my death does come, not a single person bats an eyelid. I'm so tired Karyssmov, I work to hard.. so much work that it pushes my family away. For the greater good.\nI acted like a shell because it helped.. It helped push you away, for you to walk away and remained angered with me.\n\nI'm sorry. Truly. \n\nBut I will voice that I do not approve of these secret meetings, this planning that has\nstupidity written all over it. If you get branded, you will die. If you do not swear upon the oathstone, willingly. It will end you.\n\nThe oathstone was destroyed, the second one too. Now that the both of them are gone, another Vaeyl cannot be made. So\nbeing branded is signing a prolongued suicide. \n\nThis is why I acted as I did, this is why my magic flowed. I was devastated, without any information - I thought you had gone and done it. It tore my heart in two.\nAnd.. I still doubt you. \n\nI truly believe you are marked.. and if you are. I'm sorry I failed to protect you from such. If you're not, then please do not do it. \n\nWhen you reach this note.. aspects knows where I'll end up. Darkways, off the\nedge, or lost in the Yatl. Hopefully intoxicated, you know how we are with our love for the stuff. \n\nBut do not search. Do not come and carry on with your life. \n\nIf.. you carry on with whatever you're planning. Then I beg of you to tread\ncarefully. \n\nMy reason for loving you is simple.. it cannot be explained. Our bond came naturally. \n\nAll my love, aspects guide. \n\nQuillian Axel Serrene, Caerme'onn-Lorenthus", ""),
        StaticBook("Kat's Final Will", "Vex", "The Final Will of Miss Katrina Atmorice\n\nVaran. I leave you a dog I purchased for you before my death in the hopes that you can start a family of your own.. One that will never truly leave you behind. Treat her  well.\nUncle Jakkir, you get a lantern, enchanted with Yeuflame. It will never go out unless deliberately extinguished. I shall always be watching over you from Wyrvun's loving embrace. You also get this ocarina, think of my when you play it.\nSigirath, you get the token of your esteem which you gave to me all those years ago. I treasured it. Stay yourself, you lovable crazy bastard!\nIsmic, my beloved brother, you  receive this lovely bracelet I wore wherever I went, so that you may always keep a part of me close.\nMother, I kept the statue that Wyrvun gave us after our vision. It is yours now. May his glow keep you warm through my absense. I will always love you, even after life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Khaganate CodesI", "Tulin Alvius", "Rules And Honor Codes of the Sunset Khaganate\nas of the 15th of The Amber Cold, 1589\n\nRecorded by Tulin Alvius, Boyan\nCode 1: Joining\n\nIn order to join the Khaganate, one must prove themselves worthy. For combatants wishing to join as Noyans, the best challenge for them is the Honor Klomp, taken from Orcish culture. Non- Combatans looking for citizenship can prove their\nuse with a tribute that showcases their skills. \n\nCode 2: Ranking System\nThe ranks from top to bottem are as follows: Khagan, Khan, Boyan, Yurts, Ikh'Orlok, Orlok, Kharul, Noyan, and Kokud. Any rank given is the choice of the Khagan, and those\nhe choses to be his voice. Honor Klomps are also an acceptable way of gaining rank. The rank holder you wish to take however can refuse the Klomp with permission from their Khagan.\n\nCode 3: Comradery\nRespect is one of the main things that keeps the\nKhaganate running smoothly. We are a community, sharing the basics of living with one another and trying to build up a working settlement. Desputes among the Khaganates can be settled like most things in the camp; with an Honor Klomp. If one is found to\nbe disrespectful to a higher ranking officer, the person in question will be punished in a way that the Khagan and the officer finds fitting. Examples would include cutting of parts of an ear when a Khaganate does not listen to orders. Lying and harming\nanother Khaganate member is forbidden, and will have a punishment worthy of the crime. \n\nCode 4: Leaving\nThe Khaganate does not have a blood packet or a life oath, but one can not just leave. If you want out, you have to fight for it. If you lose, you\nmust wait another month before you may try again. If you win, you are free to go. These Klomps are usually done against the higher ranks, and some times, the Khagan themself. \n\nCode 5: Additions to the code\nThe Khagan's word is law, meaning any addition\nto the codes they make stay. \n\n\nAny further additions to the code and culture will be added at a later date.", ""),
        StaticBook("Khaz'A'Dentrumm", "Hogarth Irongut", "II \n Auction of the Dead\n\nWritten by Indago Stormhammer and Morgrim Grandaxe. Copied by Hogarth Irongut. Tennant from Da Ord Nar Kadrin.\nKhaz'A'Dentrumm is said to rest within the plains of the afterlife. When a Dwarf dies their souls are carred by Dungrimm to be judged by the Brathmordakin for their actions in life. Yemekar was said to have forged the moon that inhabits the gods of the\nBrathmordakin. From here, they watch over the lives of Dwarves. It is also said to bear the Great Anvil that forged our world. The moon is only accessible by the most honorable and zealous of Dwarves, who had shown either great valor in battle or great\ndiligence in their life. When a Dwarf has passed on, a select few are invited to a grand feast within the hall of the Gods, forever to eat and drink. These individuals are known as the Paragons and act as near demi-gods in the eyes of their kin. The plane\nof the afterlife is known as Khaz'A'Dentrumm and is where all Dwarves strive to go when they die. Here, the Paragons rule while ordinary Dwarves are auctioned amongst the Brathmordakin. Those unfortunate and honorless Dwarves who fail to gain a bid\nfrom any of the gods are instead vast into Vuur'Dor, an entirely separate plane of the afterlife. \n\nThe creation of this afterlife is primarily unkown. Supposedly the void existed for as long as the Creator himself and so all of the Brathmordakin\nare believed to have devised this punishment for those Dwarves who had acted dishonorably and shameful throughout their mortal lives. This plane is otherwise known as Vuur'Dor, literally translating to Black Doom in the common tongue. When a Dwarf passes\non into this form of the afterlife, they experience an endless cycle of emotionless despair, where they wander for all eternity. It is said that honorless beings delve these depths when none of the gods have selected them to pass on into the halls of\nKhaz'A'Dentrumm. Mages are said to derive the source of their power from the void and it is further suspected that this is where Khorvad and his minions currently linger.*\n\n*Written during Asulon and therefore outdated as Khorvad\nhas returned.", ""),
        StaticBook("Khaz'a'Detrumm", "Nerah", "Khaz'a'Dentrumm is said to rest within the plains of the afterlife. When a dwarf dies, their souls are carried by Dungrimm to be judged by the Brathmordakin for their actions in life.\nYemekar was said to have forged the moon that inhabits the gods of the Brathmordakin. From here, they watch over the lives of dwarves. It is also said to bear the Great Anvil that forged our world.\nThe Moon is only accessible by the most honorable and zealous of Dwarves, who had shown either great valor in battle or great diligence in their life. When a Dwarf has passed on, a select view are invited to a grand feast within the halls of the Gods,\nforever to eat and drink. These individuals are known as the Paragons and act as near demi-gods in the eyes of their kin. This plane of the afterlife is known as Khaz'A'Dentrumm and is where all dwarves strive to go when they die.\nHere, the Paragons rule while ordinary dwarves are auctioned amongst the Brathmordakin. Those unfortunate and honourless dwarves who fail to gain a bid from any of the gods are instead cast into Vuur'Dor, an entirely seprate plane of the afterlife.\nThe creation of this afterlife is primarily unknown. Supposedly the void existed for as long as the Creator himself and so all of the Brathmordakin are believed to have devised this punishment for those Dwarves who had acted-\n-dishonorably and shameful throughout their mortal lives. This plane is otherwise known as Vuur'Dor, literally translating to Black Doom in the common tongue. When a Dwarf passes on into this form of the afterlife,\nthey experience an endless cycle of emotionless despair, where they wander for all eternity. It is said that honourless beings delve these depths when none of the gods have selected them to pass on-\n-into the halls of Khaz'A'Dentrumm. Mages are said to derive the source of their power from the void and it is further suspected that this is where Khorvad and his minions currently linger.", ""),
        StaticBook("Khorvad Vol 1", "Torkan Starbreaker", "There onced live a fellow dwarf by the name of Velkan Ironborn. Velkan Ironborn was the youngest of the eight sons of Urguan. He was the founder of the clan known as the Ironborn. The clan was known to worship the god Khorvad. Khorvad was once a member of\nthe Brathmordakin. Back in those days Khorvad was known as the god of ambition. Khorvad's worshipers grew and grew and grew. Yemekar and the rest of the Brathmordakin saw this and became jealous, their hearts filled with greed and they became obssessed.\nSo one day when Khorvad was giving blessing to his followers. Yemekar and the rest of the Council came up to Khorvad and said \"Yer numbehs 'ave grown khorvad and weh can nae stand around and wotch ye be favoured aneh longeh,\" So Yemekar took out his\nhammer and tried to put an end to Khorvad, But Khorvad moved out of the way at the right time. Yemekar and Khorvad began to fight and the two battled for many years across the sky until one day Yemekar banished Khorvad into the void.", ""),
        StaticBook("Killing orcs", "Eskel Uialben", "Eskel's guide on killing orcs, and goblins\n\nI wish to start off with a mental note:\n\n  If the orc, or goblin is wearing armor, you either run, or possibly get enslaved, might even get killed.\n-If the fucker isnt wearing armor\n\n1: Have sword\n2: keep distance and await oppertunity\n3: Aim on cutting the being's leg tendons \n4: If you do cut the tendons, end the fucker's life \n5: Cut off an arm or an leg and eat it", ""),
        StaticBook("Killing Yourself", "Archembalt", "Effective Ways of \nCommitting Suicide\n=+------<>-------+=\n\n     Perhaps you have taken this tome because you are generally a curious individual, or maybe you've considered that life is not worth living. If the latter is your case, I am\n-terribly sorry that not everything has been too satisfactory throughout your period of existence. \n\n   Nonetheless, everyone reserves the right to end their lives. I am here now to convey effective methods with which one could swiftly end\n-their life.\nSections\n=+------<>-------+=\n\nI. The Natural Way\n\nII. Poisons and Potions\n\nIII. Death, Accompanied with Solace\nThe Natural Way\n=+------<>-------+=\n\n1. Jumping off a cliff. Make sure that you are not falling into a sea. It is only more painful. Ensure that the surface is hard, or that there are stone crags at the bottom. Death will surely occur.\n2. Poisonous mushrooms. Eat an abundance. Fever, convulsing, vomiting, then succinct death. The more you take, the quicker you will reach the end. Find a mushroom with a white stalk, red head, and with white spots on its surface.\n3. Drowning. Tie a heavy rock to your feet and hop into a pool, river, ocean, et cetera. There is no escape. The struggle won't last too long. There will be a burning sensation, and shock will begin to take place. Not as swift, but effective enough.\n4. Have someone twist your head about and snap your neck. Ensure your friend/assailant is strong. Pay them some money to kill you. Tell them to make it quick. A quick severing of the spine should bring you to death in no time.\n5. Beheading. Get a trusted friend or hire someone with minas. Their blade should be sharpened, their grip confident, and they must be considerably strong. One swipe will separate your head from your body, if everything has been planned out well.\n6. Hanging. Slightly more painful, but depends on the height from which you jump. Tie a noose around your neck and then to a tree branch. Stand on the tree branch, and make sure that you are an apt height from the ground. Jump. The noose should constrict-\n-around your neck finely and perhaps crush your larynx in no time, cutting off your access to a considerable supply of air. In some cases, your spine will snap. This method is more well-known.\n7. Arbalest bolt to the temple. Acquire someone strong and able to properly load the heavy war bow known as an arbalest. The piercing power of this brutal weapon will easily end your life. Instruct them to point it at your temple (side of  your head) and-\n-stand around two meters away from you when firing. Almost as quick as beheading.\n8. Explosion. Perhaps a tad harder to set up. A stick of dynamite will do, maybe two. Strap it to your upper chest, preferably to the sternum. You may make the fuse as short as you wish. Execute this out in a field, or perhaps run into a room of -\n- individuals you absolutely despise, and light the fuse. A last 'hurrah' before you pass on. Death by explosion is nearly instant. Dynamite is also not too hard to get your hands on.\n9. Exsanguination. Slitting your forearm. Acquire a knife or something especially sharp. Draw the blade up the inside of your forearm all the way to your wristline. The cut does not have to be too deep. Ensure the severing of multiple veins. The result\n-will be extreme loss of blood. Your heart will slow and your mind will be deprived of necessary fluids. Death is soon to occur.\n10. Thanhium dust. Thanhium, surprisingly, is not too hard to get a hold of. In order to execute this suicide method properly, procure a decent-sized chunk of thanhium. Begin to break it down in order to release the toxic dust. Begin to inhale, and do -\n- not stop. You will begin to feel cold, and more than likely break into a sweat. The toxic dust will become overbearing and your mind will soon 'shut off'.\nPoisons and Potions\n=+------<>-------+=\n\n1. Overdose on sleeping potions. If one could request an abundance of sleeping potions, this method of suicide would be painless and peaceful. You would quickly fall into a deep sleep, -\n- but never to awake.\n2. Nether's Wrath. An incredibly harmful potion, scalding hot and incredibly bright. Pour into the eyes. Painful at first, but the concoction will sear through the flesh of your eyes and promptly penetrate to strike at your brain, frying it to a crisp, w-\n- ith this method only taking less than ten seconds once the potion is acquired.\n3. Greater Drake's Poison. Overdose on this, and you will overheat in no time. Your lips will become parched, your stomach aflame, and soon your mind will not be able to register much. Death is guaranteed with this.\n4. Blissfoil. Consume an abundance of this flower, or drink the potion. You will gradually lose the ability to properly move your arms or leg as you eat them, until your entire body is paralyzed. At this point, your brain cannot register\n-any pain or sensation, and once this point has been reached, you will die.\n5. Alchemist's Fire. It will melt the flesh off of your bone. Ask someone to throw it upon you and aim for the head or upper torso. More effective than regularly setting yourself on fire.\n6. Frost Oil. Primarily used as a coolant for clothing, it may also be applied to weapons. Drink it instead. Overdose will work in a similar way to blissfoil. Your body will be overcome with the cold, and your mind too will freeze. Death is guaranteed.\n7. Basilisk venom. When extracted and taken in large amounts, will cause swift death. Straightforward. This method can be applied with a wide array of venomous snakes and beasts.\nDeath, Accompanied by Solace\n=+------<>-------+=\n\n     It is up to the one committing suicide to determine whether or not they wish to settle personal qualms with other individuals, or if they do not wish for their ending to be peaceful.\nTheir reasons are their own. \n\n    Take some time to truly reflect on your life, the decisions you have taken, and consider if everything has been truly settled. If reflecting back on your life has become too painful, then do not feel the need to such.\nIf one would prefer an even more peaceful ending, however, a prime way of committing suicide would be by enjoying whatever you can before you take your life. Have a drink, eat whatever food you'd like, or take a nice nap. Maybe poison your drink so -\n- the pain will be alleviated even further. \n\n    There are a multitude of ways in which one may kill themselves, and this tome only details a few of those. Thank you for reading, and I hope you find this information useful.\n-Written by Archibald Vallero (alias: Archembalt)\n\n           -1546", ""),
        StaticBook("Kitab Alsalam.1", "Ibraheem Aladeen", "Al’iiman Rashidun\nBook of Peace(kitab alsalam)\n-------------------Definition\nRabb: Lord\nAllah: GOD\nShahada: Testimony/vow to your Faith\nNabi: Prophet\nShaitan/Shai’tan: Iblees\nJannah: Seven Skies\nHaram/Haraam: Forbidden\n-------------------☪Introduction To The Book Of Peace☪\nIn the Name of God, the Merciful and the Gracious, Allah Has sent All People andall races the book, To Guide Us and to lead us back to him,\nLike any inventor he left a book to guide us and instruct us. He has sent us prophets and those to teach you about the faith. He is the one the Almighty; there is no God but him. The book shall teach all,the ways Allah wanted us to live\nand sent to us many books and teachers, but they have been changed, manipulated to the earthly benefit of those who want to control or make his view greater, Allah shall punish those in the void and reward those who fight them.\nAllah cares for all his subjects and promises them the reward of Seven Skies if they remember and obey him.\n-------------------☪Testimony of Faith [Shahada], How to Convert☪\nConversion does not require baptism or the speaking to of an Imam.\nIf you truly wish to follow in the light of God, one must simply recite this phrase three times. “He is Allah(the Creator/God), the One and Only; Allah, the Eternal, Absolute; He begets not, nor is He begotten; And there is none comparable unto Him.\nThere is only One God and that is Allah(The Creator/God), and forever shall I follow His light.”Once spoken three times, whether, in silence or aloud, you are seen by His watchful gaze as converted and a follower of the faith.\nBe proud of what you follow,\nfor God has already given you a spot within the seven skies for your great achievement, but know Allah is both Gracious and Just. Abusing what is given to you, or following in a path of sin will only give you a place in the hellfires for eternal torment.\n☪Chapter One☪\nWho Is Allah\n------------------\nAllah is the name given to the Almighty Creator (as written of by the Wandering Wizard) by the Qalasheen and other farfolk which translates to “God”.\nThe Qalasheen believe Allah is the sole deity worthy of worship and consider all other idols false. Allah is a divine being and any attempt at his portrayal would be disrespectful for it puts limits of the deity.\nAllah is considered limitless and beyond what mortals can comprehend. He is believed to be both a merciful and generous god to his followers and a weapon of wrath to call upon when believers are met with enemies.\nOne does not need to call the Creator “Allah”, for it is just how you say God in the tongue of the Qalasheen. If your tongue calls the Creator something else other than Allah, God, or the Creator then continue to speak it so with passion and pride,\nas long as it truly translates into God or The Creator in the common tongue.\n-------------------☪Chapter Two☪\nAenguls and Daemons\n-------------------The faith adheres and shows proper respect to the Aenguls and Daemons of the\nCreator, who are recognized as His humble servants with divine powers. They are physical beings with the power to interact within our very own realm, with powers beyond our comprehension. Whilst they may be powerful beings,\nthey do not compare to the power of the Creator. The Aenguls and Daemons are loyal and submit only to the Creator.There are many of those that praise/worship an Aengul or Daemon, which is fine within the faith, as long as the Creator is worshipped\nabove them and is mentioned beforehand within a prayer that would be dedicated to an Aengul or Daemon.The Aenguls and/or Daemons that have fallen from their righteous path to bring pain and destruction to those of our proper realm\nwould be the only time you would not need to show respect, for God has damned them. The two truly evil beings that have fallen from the path of light of our timeline is Iblees and Setherien, who now are condemned to the underworld to spend the eternity\nin the hell fires alongside those that stray from the path of righteousness.  Those that follow in the path of Iblees or Setherien, or any other Aengul, Daemon, or beast that has fallen from their paths should be executed with haste so that they may\nmeet the Creator’s wrath in the afterlife.\n-------------------☪Chapter Six☪\nThe Five Pillars of Faith\n-------------------We have Given you Five Pillars Of your Faith, for You to guide your life Upon these and live upon the Mercy of Allah.\nFaith, Declare your faith proudly by reciting the Shahada (testimony of faith) and show submission to God’s will. Preach the Shahada whenever you are down, stressed, proud, happy, and so forth so you will never forget the Creator.\nPrayer, Pray to the Creator at least once a day, but no more than five times. If able, go to the Masjid[Mosque] to pray and attend sermon each Friday of the week.Fast, During the month of The Grand Harvest, we find ourselves in a great\nabundance of fruit and crops as a reward for the hardships we had faced during the winter. This is a time of usual celebration, but also a  time that gluttony takes into effect. Fast for the whole month from sunrise to sunset,\nnot only to avoid gluttony but to also feel the pain of the poor, of what they have to go through each day of their lives. If you are poor, sick, pregnant or require immediate food or hydration,\nbreak your fast so that you may continue to be in good health, but know breaking your fast without proper reason is frowned upon by Allah. Allah does reward those that properly fasts and shows about submission.\nCharity, Give charity to the poor and needy when able. It was the Creator who gave you all that you have today, and it is He who can take it all away.\nPilgrimage, Those that are physically able to should commit pilgrimage to the Grand Masjid\nat least once in their lifetime. Do not sail or take carts to wherever the Grand Masjid may be, but travel by foot from the blessed Cloud Temple to where the Grand Masjid is located. [Often times, the Grand Masjid may have to be deconstructed and built\nelsewhere due to either nation stability or the migrating of lands. \n-------------------☪Chapter Seven☪\nThe Importance of ma'an(Water)\n-------------------We have given you rivers and springs to drink from,\nIt quenches your thirst and keeps the earth alive. We have made you of clay and water, and we have made all life depends on water. We have given you this blessing So care for it,do not waste water that Allah has given you.\nWe have given you water to clean yourselves of Sin, and illness, we have given it to you to wash your worries away and to cool you from the Sun’s heat. Do not waste water, for Allah has given you it as a reward for you.\nWe have given you water to become Obedient and give you self-control. Those who waste water and taunts others with it will have their sins accounted for them on the last hour, and they will be asked\n“Have we not given you water, to share and to keep you cool and at peace?” and they will say “Yes you have, but I had a well and a stream of water to care for my needs that been there for generations.”\nand Allah will say “Yet you forbade your fellow slaves to it, Out of greed and wasted what I have given you and commanded you to take good care off.” and thus they will be accounted for their sins. Allah is indeed all-knowing.\n-------------------\n☪Chapter Eight☪\nThe Alqamar (The Moon)\n-------------------  Allah has given you the Moon, To shine bright and to remind you of the Light of his face and to guide you in the dark of night.\nThe moon's light is like a grain of sand in the largest of desserts in comparison to Allah’s light on his face. Like the Moon, The Book is your light in this world,  without it you walk aimlessly in this life like the darkest of nights.\nHe gave you the night to Bring you at peace, for there is nothing in the night leaving you with your lord to remember his greatness. Allah is Indeed the Light And most Merciful.\n-------------------☪Chapter Nine☪\nArrogance and Ignorance\n------------------\nWoe to those is of the arrogance of Allah. Allah has covered their eyes and ears and made them deaf, dumb and blind to him for their arrogance. Beware of turning to arrogance, For Allah hates such.Allah Has given you a brain and signs of him,\nAnd given you blessings and proof of his mercy. There will be one of the last hours who was of Arrogance. We will ask him “How did you answer to the lord of the worlds? Did you submit to your heart and your soul?\nHow did you answer the ones who were a mercy to you (prophets)?” The one of arrogance will say “I did not believe in them, though they never lied. I did not believe in the Almighty Allah even with the clear signs of your glory.”\nfor his arrogance Allah will punish him on the Day of Judgment for he is the judge of all things and the sentence giver. Be calm when you see those of Arrogance and ignorance, Walk within your life's\nsoftly and quietly and when they approach you and give you bad and evil,  Give them good. For there will be those in between you(and the one who is arrogant and ignorant) and they will see kindness in return of evil,\nThus bringing more friends of your faith and yourself. Allah is indeed the all knowing and all Kind.\n-------------------☪Chapter Ten☪\nKnowledge\n-------------------We Have Given you a mind and a will, We Have made those who are smarter than you,\nand those who a less of knowledge. Go out and learn, Seek New things, Learn of the things we have created and things to help you in your life, and be blessed from what Allah gives.Allah dislikes those who Do not learn and seek the truth.\nLearn, and when you have learned, Teach! Allah loves those who Learns and seeks the truth, those who go to learn to help others and community for the Sake of Allah! Allah has promised\nthose who seek for knowledge and the Truth and teaches it to others a Spot in the seventh skie. Allah says ‘Go to the farthest ends of the earth to gain knowledge.’ Allah is indeed the most Knowledgeable in all affairs and things.\n☪Chapter Eleven☪\nRepent\n-------------------  Allah has made all with faults, He has given instructions on how to handle them, and what to do if you commit a sin. Allah says ‘Do not fear and does not despair\nfor the mercy of Allah is awaiting you there(seven skies)’ Be afraid of your Rabb, and repent for your sins, but be at ease For Allah is the most merciful and the most forgiving. Allah says\n‘Even if you have murdered all of the creatures of the Earth, If you repent and turn to Me, you will be forgiven’. Remember you are not repenting for Allah, but for yourself,\nBecause the Punishment of Nether is the worst of things and never-ending. Allah Is Indeed the Most Merciful.\n-------------------\n\n(part 2 comes next)", ""),
        StaticBook("Knights of OSL", "Commodus de Jedih", "sssssssssssssssssssRecord of the Knights of the Poor Fellow Soldiers of Horen and Saint Lucien of Savoie\nsssssssssssssssssss\n\nRecorded by Commodus de Jedih, 1663\n\nAll knights have been recognized by the Church.\nGrandmaster Jack Rovin, KOJ\n\nHoly Ser Voron Rovin, KOJ\n\nHoly Ser Rymeul Elendil, KOJ\n\nHoly Ser Rosencrantz Revandir, KOJ\n\nHoly Ser Rick Felder, KOJ\nHoly Ser Raigeki Kato, KOJ\n\nSer Rydel Elendil, KoO\n\nHoly Ser Liam McLeod, KOJ\n\nGrandmaster Baudric von Aesterwald, KOJ\n\nSer Nafis Yar, KoO\nSer Darius de Denesle, KoO\n\nSer Peter von Aesterwald, KoO\n\nHoly Ser Farley Hanethor, KOJ\n\nHoly Ser Cain de Denesle, KOJ\nHoly Ser Rudiger, KOJ\n\nHoly Ser Leonhardt Crouchback, KOJ\n\nGrandmaster Rakim Yar, KOJ\n\nHoly Ser Bart de Denesle, KOJ\n\nHoly Ser Balian Crast, KOJ\nHoly Ser Romane Niwarsay II, KOJ\n\nHoly Ser Phillip Marshall, KOJ\n\nHoly Ser Avery, KOJ\n\nHoly Ser Aryan Roke, KOJ\n\nHoly Ser Heinrich, KOJ\nHoly Ser Felix Fitch, KOJ\nddddddddddddddddddd\n\nKOJ = Knight of Justice\n\nKoO= Knight of Obedience\n\nKOD= Knight of Devotion\n**There are no recorded Knights of Devotion, the lowest tier of knighthood in the Church.\n\n**Grandmaster Robert Rovin is a bishop, not a knight and is therefore not mentioned on this list.", ""),
        StaticBook("KOBOLD CRAZE", "Waldemar Morley", "KOBOLD CRAZE\n*Recent rumors have reported Kobolds extending further from their caverns than ever before.\n\n*It is unknown why, all that is known is that they're targeting Serf's from the Whispering Crossroads.\n\"Head down the East path, once you reach the pond: Take a left, heading North towards the small hill. Heard some Kobolds out there in the morning, screaming too. Get there, quick.\"\n\n(( XYZ: 509 / 61 / 55))", ""),
        StaticBook("Kreyzchurz Vol 1", "TapeSauce", "DIZKLEYMUR- WHUEBR EZ REEDIN DIZ MUZT NOH DAT DIZ BUUK EZ UHBOWT DA VERYUZ FURMZ AGH TIPEZ UB KREYZCHURZ AGH REYZEZ. RULG FUR REEDIN DIZ BUUK. UHZLO, MI ROTE UHLUT UB ET EN UH ZCHEWER.\nZcheptur Un: Da Snaak. \nSnaakz ahr wyrd. Dey ez zmull. Lat kan throogh dem et wulz. Bud, dyr ez moar tu dem dan juzt myootulazchun. En diz zcheptur, lat wil lurn ub da moar zchufiztukeytd lyfztylz ub Snaakz. Dey hev uh kumplux\nkulzchur dat lat wudnt ekzpekd. Furzt, et ternz owt dat Snaakz dunt liv en hollz. Wull, dey kynd ub du, bud dyr kuld berrohz. Deyz berrohz ahr akzchuii kwyt nyz agh dekureytd. Diz ez ub kurz ef lat kan eben fet en et. Udder dan flattin, Snaakz ahr yoozful\nfur treyding, ez Mi mit menii Snaak treydurz en dah rodz. Deyr yoozchulii vurry niiz kreyzchurz, bud deyr zo zmul dat wi lyk tu meyk fun ub dem wenebur wi peep dem. Uhlzo, Snaakz meyk fur guud berdendurz, dat ez, ef dey kan eben riizch da kowntur, ryt?\nZcheptur Tuu: Da Gharat\n\nPribiiuzly, wi lurnd uhbowt da Snaakz, smul, ugli, agh wiik kreyzchurz. Tu undurztahnd uh Gharat, ez tu undurztahnd elkohol. Lat peep, deyz Gharatz fil dyr holz wit byr, lutz agh lutz ub byr.\nDey ez uh marii reyze, muzch zo lyk da Snaakz. Dey ez uhlzo zchord lyk da Snaakz. Unlyk da Snaakz doh, Gharatz ahr phaddah, agh dey lyk tu klomp uhlmozt ez muzch ez wi Bruddahz du. Uhlmozt. Tu bii onizt, dyr ez muzch tu edmyr bowt deyze kreyzchurz. Dey ez\nuh bryd ub woryurrz Ub koarz, da Gharat kant bii kumpayrd tu da ztrengf ub uh Bruddah, bud dey ziim tu be ztrungr dan eben dah bigizt Shara. Muzch lyk uz Bruddahz, Gharatz hold dyr onurr tu uh hyooj ekztent. Bote Bruddahz agh Gharatz lyk tu yooz luskz\nagh hemmurz. Tu bii onuzt, Gharatz ahr lyk tinee, uglii, zchmellii, dum Urukz en uh wai. Mi tink dat wii zchud ztil flat dem, bud, wi niid tu uhprezchyate wai deyr zo fun tu flat agh klomp. Noaw, wyr gunna zchift gyrz hyr, agh zwhizch tu uh tullur reyze.\nZcheptur Frii: Da Albaiz\n\nDiz reyze ez un ub uh dizgreyzful zenz ub onur. Da Albaiz tink deyr beddah dan uz. Mi miin, zo du dah Snaakz agh Gharatz agh udder ztuf, but dah Albaiz ziim tu heyt uz eben moar. Deyr uh gruup ub kreyzchurz dat tink deyr zo\nbootyful agh zmurt. Bud, Mi fiil dat en zum waiz, dey ekzchulli ahr zmurt. Lat peep, dey mai bi finur, zchmelliur, agh dumr dan uz, bud Mi tink dat dey en zum wai, diip enzyd, dat Albaiz hev zum digry ub endulijinz. Purhepz Albaiz kant meyk guud wepenz ur\nurmr, ur eben guud biltingz. Bud, Albaiz ziim tu grezp da mojo vurri wil. Noaw, wi gunna dyv entoo dah zchpezifek tipz ub Albaiz.\nZcheptur Foar: Da Hy Albaiz \n\nEt ez dah Hy Albai dat zukz dah mozt, en Mi upynyon. Dyr dah unz dat RILLI tink hy uhbowt demzelthz. Kunziduriin etz en deyr nymz agh ztuf. Deyz unz liiv lung, luuk tull, ahr zupr pail, dring dah teez, eet dah\nkeykz, riid dah novullz, mok dah uddah reyzez, du deyr fenzii mojo, wayzt tym en meykin ztuf pritii, (Eben dah webenz) agh teyk dyr bafz, klyn dyr klofz agh eyrz, agh..... detz prittii muzch et. Beyzikulli, dey zuk.\nZcheptur Fyv: Da Wuud Albai\n\nNeztii lidl trii hugrz, datz wub deyze Wuud Albaiz ez. Belib et ur nub, Wuud Albaiz dunt eben yooz zwordz, luskz, ur eben toylit peypr. Dey yooz bohz. Agh fur toylit peypr, Mi tink dey yooz leyvz. Uhlzo, Trii Albaiz ahr\nmuzch lyk twigz. Datz wai anuddah nym fur Albai iz Twiggeh. Deyz Wuud Twiggehz iz uh bunzch ub panzchyz. Dey hyd en dah zchadohz tu hund fur deyr prai. Bud, uz Urukz hund fur owr prai en dah opun, kynda. Uhdoh, Wuud Twiggehz ahr guud et zneekin uhrownd.\nMi heb nub ztudyd dah Wuud Twiggehz muzch, bicuz dey ez yoozchuahlii hydin frum Mi. Zo, deyr ez ztill muzch tu leern uhbowt dem. Noaw, wi gunna teyk uh peep et dah grai unz.\nZcheptur Zekz: Da Durk Albaiz\n\nDeyz Twiggehz peep lyk da nyttyme zkyz demzelfz. Dey ez pritti muzch grai agh kynda bluu. Dey ahr pritti moduzt, peepin ez dat deyr Albaiz. Dey ziim lyk da muzt humbull ub da Twiggehz. Juzt lyk deyr mizteeriuhz\nuhpyrunz, nub muzch hez biin reykordid ub dah Durk Albaiz. Meybi deyr ez, bud dey nub zchard et wit Mi. Zo, Mi juzt gunna blah lat uhbowt deyr fizchikul uhpyrunz, rathurr dan deyr riil kulzchur. Dey haz durk zkin, durk eyz, bud dey yoozchulii drezz wit\npritti buld kulurz. Ulzo, Mi meynli nohtizd peerzingz agh grai harez. Zo, Mi dun blahin uhbowt dah Twiggehz, cuz dey ez pritti leym. Zo, noaw, wi gunna zchifd geerz uhgen agh lurn uhbowt dah sharaz.\nZcheptur Zebin: Da Sharaz ub Da Nurth\n\nGriidi, zchmellii, diplohmektik, tinee, uglii, wiik, dum, agh rilli dum. Lat knoh wub wyr blah uhbowt. Da Zharaz. Bud, deyz ahr dah Zharaz en da Nurth. Mi gethurrd diz enfurmeyzchun en dah zitii ub Ubrezchi.\nDey ahr uh kumplukeytd reyze, zo Mi gunna breyk diz op ento deberint katuhgoryz. Furzt, wi gunna blah uhbowt hoaw wi peep dem, ur hoaw dey luuk. Zharaz ahr zhortah dan Twiggehz, agh phaddah dan Gharatz. Dey kal demzelfz HOO-MANZ, agh dunt kal dem\nZharaz, bikuz dey ez dum, dey dunt knoh wub et meenz. Dey blahd wit Mi, agh zed dat dey hev zumting kald \"Pulektikz.\" Mi tink etz lyk Krughai Kunfedurazchun, bud dey zed et wuz moar uglyr. Uhlzo, dey griidi, lyk Gharatz, bud dey nub griidi fur goald, dey\nwunt minaz. Agh, dey neber edmid et. Zo, beyzikly, dah Sharaz ub da Nurth ahr moar ebil dan Mi eber thowt. Az lat knoh ahlredii, da Uhbrezchi Zharaz ahr owr alliz en mozt worz, bicuz dey ez zum ub dey unlii unz whu nub bytray uz. Noaw, wi du 'Dooneeuh.\nZcheptur Eyt: Sharaz ub 'Dooneeuh\n\nTeyk noat, Mi ubteynd diz enfurmeyzchun frum da 'Dooneeun Kinggy hemzelf, Yahrl Lazchlahn Moare Ilindul. Zo ez lat kan peep, diz buuk gev Mi da onur tu meat kowntliz uhfizchuhlz en da wurld. Enywhey, da\nZharaz ub 'Dooneeuh ahr blahd tu bii da owldizt. Deyr Kinggy blahd Mi dat wuz da furzt Zharaz uhrownd, meykin' dem muzch owldar dan da Zharaz ub 'Dooneeuh. 'Dooneeunz uhlzo hev pohlektikz lyk da Uhbrezchinz, bud deyrz ez muzch deberunt.\nLat peep, en deyr kulzchur, da yungizt boarne ez da un whu ez deztind tu liid, unlyk moar popyoolahr kulzchurz weyr da eldar liidz. Deyz 'Dooneeunz hev menii deberunt reynkz tuu, lyk uh Hy Theyn, agh Hy Morzchul. Uhlzo, deyz kreyzchurz ahr da lungizt livd\nZharaz uhrownd, biicuz uhpairuhntlii, dey hev Twiggeh bluud en deyr bohdiiz. Hoaweber, dey dunt peep lyk uhn Albai. Nub, 'Dooneeunz ahr zum ub da bigizt Zharaz Mi eber peepd. Ub korz, wi Urukz ahr ztil muzch biggah dan dem, dey ez pritti tol agh meyti.\nDey nub pyoor-brid Zharaz lyk Uhbrezchinz, zo dat liidz Mi tu tink dat dey ez da mongrohl reyz ub Anthohz. Lat reymimbur da Gharatz wi blahd uhbowt urlyr? Wil, noaw wi gunna tok moar uhbowt deyr hom.\nZcheptur Nyn: Da Katz \n\nTuu knoh diz reyze, ez tuu knoh kiddunz. Dat'z wub dey ez. Katz ahr beeg kiddunz, agh dey ahr frum uh eylund kolled Kuruhkahtuh. Dey blah wyrd, zmell wyrd, agh peep eben wyrdur. Diz reyze'z eylund bloh'd uhp, agh fur uh wyoll,\nleeved ryt hyr en Gronkkzton, en da kiddun diztrikt. Bud, dey oll muuv'd tu Mahlinoare naow, prohbublii beekuz wi Urukz wur tuu ztrong fur dem. Dyr ez fuur tiipz ub Katz, agh wi gunna dulv entuu oll ub dem ryt naow.\nZcheptur Tin: Da Tygur Katz\n\nDeyze ahr da beegizt ub da Kiddun Krezchurz, agh zum ub dem ahr ez beeg az uh Uruk. Dey peep lyk Tygurz, agh dey klomp lyk dem tuu. Dey ahr yoozchualii da woriurz ub da Kiddunz, agh dey ahr pritii duhm.\nMi dun't knoh uhlut uhbowt da Tygur Kiddunz, zo Mi gunna guu entuu da nehzxt Kiddun reyze.\nZcheptur Eeleben: Da Zcheetuh Katz\n\nDeez unz ahr da zmullizt, bud unlyk uh phat Ztowt, dey ez rillii phazt. Da zcheetuh Kiddunz peep lyk zcheetuhz, dey guut zpotz oll obur deyr zkin. Agh tuu Mi, dey'z myk da bezt karpitz, ef lat knoh wub Mi meen.\nZcheptur Dwelv: Da Durk Katz\n\nDey peep lyk Punturz, agh dey ahr zneeki, lyk Punturz tuu. Uhweyz peep owt fur da Durk Katz, kuz dey kan zteel latz ztuf et eny mohmunt. Tuu Mi, dey kynda ahr lyk da Durk Twiggehz, en uh zenze.\nZadlii, dat'z ol Mi knohz uhbowt da Durk unz, beekuz Kiddunz ahr myzteeriuhz, agh dey nub led Mi lurn uhbowt dem.\nZcheptur Dirtyn: Da Lepurd Katz\n\nDeez unz ohbveeuhzlii peep lyk Lepurdz, bud unlyk da uddah Kiddunz, deyz unz nub exeed en eny zchpezifik zkilz, bud dey ez da bezt zooted fur duueeng enytyng. Dey ez beeger dan Zcheetahz agh\nPunturz, agh dey ez phaztur dan Tygurz agh Panturz, agh dey ez zneekeeur dan Tygurz agh Zcheetuhz. Lat gunna prohbublii peep deyz unz da mozt. Wii neber peeped et dah deberunt typz ub Ztowtz, huh? Wil, wii gunna duu  dat naow.\nZcheptur Furtyn: Da Znoh Albaiz\n\nMi nebur hurd ub dem. Deyr zkin ez whyt lyk znoh. Deyr heyr ez whyt lyk klowdz. Dey ahr Znoh Twiggehz. Dey ahr endenjurd zpechiiz. Tu bii onuzt, deyz Znoh Twiggehz ahr Ahlbynoh, agh dey nub lyk et wen Wi kul\ndem dat. Da Znoh Twiggehz halb'd da Ztowtz wen da pazht wohr, zo.... Mi nub rylii lyk da Znoh Twiggehz. Dey liiv en uh pleyzch kull'd Frohztfohl. Bud, dat'z ol Mi knoh, biicuz dey nub rylii lyk Mi.\nDiz iz unlii da furzt vohlyuum ub da Kreyzchurz. \n\n\n\nDUH UHND", ""),
        StaticBook("L.R. Trans.", "Lori Oathcast", "Long Range Translocation Device Investigation.\n\nFrom what I can gather from Archmage Haadi the long range translocator is developed through a use of 'Void Translocation' magics which establish small pockets within the void to place objects and a --->\n- Enchanter. The void translocationist must take a object and place it within the void, and then a enchanter must co-operate in keeping such a object within the void without the original void translocationist present. The void translocationist must --->\n- then re-locate himself and in the area he wishes to designate the other opening pull forth the object from the void again, which the Enchanter had held there. This enables a hole to open between the two locations and stay open when powered.", ""),
        StaticBook("L.R. Trans.", "Kirrekith", "Long Range\nTranslocation Device\nInvestigation.\n\nFrom what I can gather from\nArchmage Haadi the long range translocator is developed through a use of 'Void Translocation' magics which establish small pockers within the\n- Enchanter. The void translocationist must take a object and place it within the\nvoid, and then a enchanter must co-operate in keeping such a object within the void without the\noriginal void translocationist present. The void translocationish must\n--->\n- then re-locate himself and in the\narea he wishes to designate the other opening pull forth the object from the void again, which the Enchanter had held there. This enables a hole to open between the two locations and stays open when powered.\n--->\nWrote by Lori Oathcast and re-wrote by\nKirrekith Reffahc\non the 8th of the\nDeep Cold, 1532.", ""),
        StaticBook("Land o' Green", "Madeline Applefoot", "O' the shire, land of green hills I call home, call me a midget, but nobody's low! In spirits that is, for our spirits are high. All thanks to Dunshire life, which is happy and spry!", ""),
        StaticBook("Landing Site 1", "Cultist Scout", "Landing Site 1\n\nIndiscreet Location, out of normal scouting range\n\nRuins of a dock, easy fix\n\nMany Tunnels to hide supplies in", ""),
        StaticBook("Larian Grimoire", "Jacquar le Petit", "A Rabid Man's\n        Testament\n     ------------\n Written and translated by Jacquar 'The Small' \nUnder the guidance and testimony of Wieslaw the Unlucky.\nPenned on the 13th of the Deep Cold 1686. \n             -\nForeword\n              -\n   I will tell you right now, on this second of pages that these words which are written here are by all means a written account and attempt at reproducing the scripts now lost of a certain Larian madman which dwelled in\nthe confines of the Southern Horenic Empire, Laria, Istria. Which came to the world before the events of the Duke's War. These words are not my own, I am but penning down the words of a far off bastard of the man, likely born of incest, which, through\ncontract, bound me to his bidding, as is the creation of this manuscript, a desolate offspring of madness.\n\nThe few pages of the original text that were found are of old raev, some of these have been translated, others, burned. \n\nBut most of this work\nstems from the accounts given to me by Wieslaw the Unlucky, to which I am a servant. \n\n      GOD help me.\n            xxx\nCherckassian\n           ---\n   \n   Blistering curses, homosex rapists and cockbogglers; the south is filled with degenerates like no others. It was better, down north.\nBut even the north was taken away, like my horse, and my brothers. \n\nBut I will mourn them not, for they had left me in the clutches of Percival Staunton, the fiend, the dog, the sickly bastard. Too fucking weak to even die right.\nListen close, you dispicable child. You that kneels to blood rather than flesh. \n\nDaring, stupid animal. Percival. Who locked me away for four long years, down deep below the city of Riga. \n\nWhere I howled and screamed for days on end.\nA martyr; I am no less. Isembert knows as much, for he was there to great me when I returned, free from my shackles. \n\nBut not for long enough. How many times, seven? Did you try and kill me, Staunton? The poison, the axe, the wine, the\ndagger... \n\n  Oh, mother. Help me. \nFor I have sinned, and sinned again. In my toil, in my rest and pain I have rejected the name of God.\n\nBut I am not redeemed? Am I no Saint? For was it not me, that on the cliffs of\nAvar, tore down and put to the sword the Cultists of the Devil; Iblees? Led by the retarded bastard born Alifer Amice. \n\n Was it not I that saw beyond the Moon? Put a great black pit of void. A great scar within the sky; which no mind but a true one may\nwitness, for our minds are young, and yet to behold the fruits of the world. This scar is no less than from which our Lord hath come.\n\n   Or is it from this that he has left us? I dare no hope. But is my soul given no justice, no matter crime or prayer?\nFor I, of my wretched flesh; Saza Derevo.\n\n The Rabid Man awaits. This headless throne speaks again. Where will I run? For I cannot fly; a flightless crow I am no more, I am no less. \n   \"Krov' budet nashey konchinoy.\"\nOn Lightning:\n\n  \"Shram v nebe; molnii. Daruy nam velikiy voy, potomu chto ognem ty zadumalsya. Tot, kto khochet vyzvat' takiye deystviya, dolzhen snachala byt' porazhen takovym.\"\n-Zhan-chernaya drevesina\n\"Erit autem sanguis vobis decessum nostrum.\" \n\nTruthfully, I've but one eye. I fear to give proper description of my bodily self, as if our minds belonged to ourselves, and who knows what warlocks and witches roam the hills and caves, communing\nwith the pages of tomes with no age. \n\n  I am not of those, a an alchemist, yes, yet a warlock pushes it. \n\nOr does it? Life is a feeble thing, and recreating it is no trouble, if one has the strenght to sell his freedom and career to create it.\nA botched thing, it may be, but life, it will always remain.\n\nAnd poor, poor Pilgrim. You wished to be remade? And you were, yet you are now quite unsightly. Now rot. For God has not saved you. Neither will he save me.\n\"Smotrite dal'she, uvidet' d'yavola, eto begushchiy kon', kotoryy ne zabyvayet, on takzhe ne prostit. Dlya togo, chtoby zaglyanut' vniz v pustotu, chtoby vypit' yad. I kakiye uzhasy vsmatrivat'sya vverkh ot bol'shogo vodovorota; pravda.\nVne vsyakogo ponimaniya on provoditsya v nedrakh nashego mira. Strakh eto.\" \n\nEdit; translations will not be provided, by the request of my master. Seek a Raevir.\n-Jacquar\nOne eye. Where did the other go? I will never find it, I will never retrieve it. But a deal was a deal. \n\nIt is not every day you can make a dead man smile. For my eye, the dreadful wraith, or whatever deceased monstrosity it was, told me the first of\nmany truths I would come to learn; that of my shadow. \n\nHow can one come to commune? To speak with such a thing? Our shadow is our true self, from it nothing can hide. And the shadow knows all: for a corpse is lifeless, but a corpse still bears\na shadow. Thus, the shadow remains, the shadow cannot die. Thus, our shadow is the one thing we revel in, the thing we wish we would be. For how can we judge our shadow, it is but our true self, and we mimic it, uncounsciously. The shadow comes before\nthe man, know it. Oh, how I regret, dear reader, that I am now unable to translate what inhuman utterings I was given, and this feeling that dwells now over my body, as I now posess the strenght, to spin this cloak of night, my shadow. \nLike a puppet.\nPuppets I was one day, literally. Driven to murder those around me, by the sweet words of that otherworldly demon. That long fingered crook, with that ever grinning face. The pain has left me, but what became I when that thing spoke of me, like a\ndivine beast; there I saw its purity. That thing is but our reflection, it is humanity, our lives, pain. With our greatest of feats to remain humble in this dreadful world, to survive its great pressure as the nails of our sins press down upon our very\nspirits. GOD will not forgive, and he lashes us in our folly. And his vicars will not forget. \n\nThese Saints. \n\nThe Black Cardinals.\n\nThe Knave of Graves.\n\nThose that wish for men to rule, and will not cease till our\nblood spills free upon the steps of the world. \nAnd no elf or short man will stand then. The world will be grey. And these pagan Gods; demons of yore will wage war with the beasts of this twisted dimension. And they will die. And GOD's child will die\nagain. Twice beheaded was he. \nAnd the Pale City will come again. \nThe Blue Cult will hear the mutterings of the great Beast.\nThe conception of our sins.\nBorn of a tormented woman, locked away, bleeding away.\nIn no less than the great house of God; she has granted the monstrous thing life. Then it was God that breathed life, in the hollow body of Mordskov and it's children. \n\nAnd all of it, all of it, driven by the folly of men. By the blood of the\n-------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n------------------\ndragon; of the Horen. Fake blood, or true blood.\n\nI have seen it.\n\nI have heard it.\n\nHistory repeats itself. \n\nAnd the orb of the Wayfarer lies little. A soul I sold. Yet another sin.\nBut the soul of a dead man. And a dead man I am. Should I not belong to the Throne, then? Should his great, long fingers not be wreathed accross my broken frame? \n\nFire, bring bring fire. \n\nBut no. I was forsaken. And now, truly. In the\neyes of GOD I cannot be redeemed. For my restless bones now see the life within the flesh that is not my own. \n\nThat is the gift of those cardinals. I smile at the thought of it. What a wonderful lie. \n\nFor now they drive away from their\nancient purpose, from which their gift was taken, stolen and branded. All that now means nothing.\n\nFor man is mad, and the elves are the breed of sin. \n\nAnd never may we find rest, content, joy.\nFor joy will fade away. \nFear him.\nFear God. \n\nHe is no father.\n\nAnd I dare not describe the sights I saw as I left my shadow. As I peered beyond this wretched veil and beyond the realm\nof the horrors. \n\nWe live within a nightmare, vast and unyielding. Yet know that we will not wake, never will we wake from this atrocity. \n\nFor there is nothing to wake up from. For we do not sleep. We do not dream.\nWe are but the particles, the pigment of this unsightly dream. And God, or whatever being you may be, up there, past our eyes and mind and very selves.\n\nHe dreams, and we are his creation. \n\nAnd yet one day he will wake.\nAnd we will cease to exist.\n\nThese are my words, fear them. Believe them. Mercy.\nBeyond our reach is a crimson serpent. \n\nA great beast, a thing we fear, and a thing we revel, from its conceptions, from its frame our reflection shall be seen. \n\nToil, toil hard, men of God, for He shall call us over.\nCommunion\n            -*-\n  A man is daring if he seeks to rid himself of his Time, of his destiny. Yet if this is his fate, let it be. Let it be that he shall peer down deep into the well;\n\nFor this rite most bold: Seek a place, where even silence\nmay die, let no thing, living or dead disturb your presence. \nMake prayer, in your folly release this anguish within you, fast as long as needed, and peer into the skulls of ancestors if needed be. \nAnd think. Yet your mind be free'd of its shackles.\nPeer up at the moon, sway, you of broken heart and broken mind, for all the years it may take release yourself. \nPeer down into nothingness, into the vast expanse of this unsightly nightmare.\nOver, and over, and over again.\nAnd when you shall succeed, you shall know. \n\nFor darkness wishes its presence to be known. \n\nAnd this great black current will be yours to peer down into. \n\nAnd many warlocks and witches\nhave quickly discarded this act, as if it were no more than a humble tool; push it further, over the limit, be one with this bottomless well; this undying land. \n\nCommune with it, peer into it. Greet the darkness.\n\nAnd perhaps, you shall witness\nwhat my poor spirits have always seen.\n\nYet no more can I do this, lest it destroy my poor frame, these bones that are not mine.\n\nFor too long these words hang on my lips.\nFor too long I await them.\n\nThis night, of all nights.\n\nWhere the dead will dance.\nI have seen dragons, defeated devils and partaken into the forbidden.\n\nI have beaten justice, I have survived what none should survive. \n\nAnd I have seen what lurks within my shadow. \nAnd this is my testimony.\nDyr hjerte\n\nDyr hjerte\n\nDyr hjerte\n\nSaza Derevo\n\nDiabolus etiam per clamorem parvulis\n\nBezzvezdnoye plamya ty odin.\nBy GOD. Fear it.\n\n   Boytes' blednogo goroda, boytes' chumy i boytes' chervya, potomu chto ya ikh videl.\n-Jentos Blackwood.\nThe Raven that Ran", ""),
        StaticBook("Larihei", "Aluatis Lorenthus", "=========================Larihei\nBy: Peurith\n=========================Transcribed by Peurith - Scribe of Malin.\n[Most of the text is faded away, several pages entirely missing.]\n...never leaves her library. She was offered honours and refused them. They say she tampers with the forces not of this world. It makes some uneasy. It inspires others to join her.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lat ah kunt", "Vorgak'Gorkil", "Lat juzt flat'd Vorgak'Gorkil.\nMi'z hump'd latz momo befur diz raid.\nWype dah ztainz frum dah wallz.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lean (Alchemic)", "Grim'aeldus", "The origins of Lean or more commonly known as Purple Drink (Purple Drank if you’re of Southeron dialect) precede man himself according to the legend of Lawrence Lean.\nBack in the First Era a would-be herbalist was delving far into the reaches of Aegis looking to change the face of the herbal game forever. It was after thirty years of searching that his thirst was quenched, he had discovered the Chrono root.\nIt glowed when he unearthed it on accident on a hot day in the wastes. Shocking and magnificent he gently uncovered it without severing it from its host. A perfect extraction was followed by mass excavation.\nBefore too long Lawrence Lean had a nice stockpile of Chrono and made preparations to head back to the heartland of Aegis to share his findings.\nUpon a relatively short trip back to his lab the herb fiend got to work. Mashing, grinding, and boiling Lean went wild trying to find a use for his life’s work.\nIt was in a workplace rage that he discovered the Chrono root actually grew out of root form and created a dense bush of sweetly scented buds and flowers.\nWhen a mature plant’s roots are grinded and boiled in cheesecloth Lawrence Lean found himself with a powerful elixir. It’s effects are known to slow down perceived time in the user’s mind and induce an intense warped effect about the user.\nWhen dried out the buds made for great pipe tobacco substitute. Chrono’s use as a smokable remedy has recently been made famous by Hansetians, notably avid Chrono user the late Darius “Lion”.\nLawrence Lean proclaims his elixir Lean to be the key to immortality. It has been described as a mixture that looks like the deep heavens in color and enthralling nature when staring directly into a fresh mug of Lean.\nAfter Note:\n\nTexts recovered from a Human library prior to it's closure. Original texts indicate the author was one Lion III of the Holy Oren Empire from the era of Asulon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Learn to Read", "Saviordude", "=(^x^)= Cat\n\n   [  ]\n=(^x^)= Cat in hat\n\n   [  ]\n=(^x^)= )o( Cat in hat, with a bat.\n\n   [  ]\n=(^x^)= )o(\n\\(     )/ Fat cat in hat, with a bat.\n*This book continues on like this for several hundred pages, allowing one to pick up the written word with the magic of Rhyme and Pictures*", ""),
        StaticBook("Legal Proposal", "Lord Azoth Hawksong", "FOREWORD\nThis document hereby presents collected information and reports to be discussed in an open court of law. The information was collected to try TOREN DEATHSBANE before the Exarchs of Caras Eldar. The crimes committed are as follows:\nI. Interbreeding (Section I, Article VI)\n\nII. Sex With A Minor (Section II, Article I)\n\nThis report is filed by Azoth Hawksong. Witnesses include:\n\nHareven\nElswyen\nMuildir\nNesrine\nToren\nQuillian", ""),
        StaticBook("Leo wish!", "Leonardo Gloop", "*The handwriting would be extremely scruffy and quite a few words would be spelt wrong*\n\nI want a biyg dogie tfat wil be my frend. I want to be ayble to wride on him! And he wil help me and stuf. \n\nAllso i want new clofos! But 1 wish is beter! So dogie!\n((In case you couldn't understand, with the spelling and that he wants a big dog that he can ride on and it will help.  Then he's just saying he wants new clothes but the first one is the wish.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Leolins book.", "Thorvn Bronwyn", "13th of the Amber Cold, 1683\n\nWe finally moved everything into the new house. It's everything I've wanted. It's perfect. It's cozy, but has so much room. A second room even for a possible baby in the future. I talked to a man earlier and he told me...\nhis wife is pregnant. I want a baby, always have. I grew up in a big family. So it's natural to want one of my own. If it was girl I think I would name her Elenor after my grandmother, or Faythe. If it was a boy I think I'd name him Chance.\n\n14th of the Amber Cold, 1863\n\nLeo and I talked and I believe he wants to have children soon... God, that makes me so happy. I hope it's soon. I know, I've heard pregnancies are hard, but I'm excited. I'm excited for motherhood in general.\n15th of the Amber Stone, 1863\nWe tried for the baby last night and I hope I'm pregnant\n11th of the Deep Cold, 1863\n\nI feel so nausous right now and my head it killing me.\n15th of the Deep Cold, 1863\n\nI'm pregnant and I can't believe it. It's a miracle. I never thought that whis would become a reality.\n\nI was walking in the plaza then... Then a group of orcs surrounded me. I don't remember what happened after that.\nI just woke up without a nose...\n14th of Snow's Maiden\n1868\n\nElenor just turned\n5! I am so proud of her and she has become the joy of my life since Rowan left...Happy birthday Elenor!\n\n-Leolin Silma\nYear of 1873\n\nMy Daughter Elenor has turned to the age of 10! I am so proud of the young Woman she has become so far she is so funny and full of fun,Joy and Happyness.\nHappy Birthday Elenor!\n\n-Leolin Silma", ""),
        StaticBook("Lesser Merels", "Buernoc Silvervein", "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=Common Belvitz Games\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\nVolume I\n\nLesser Merels\ncommonly know as\nApples & Oranges\nPlayed on a board of tiles, three by three.\n\nTo be played by two men, each possessing differing sets of three like items, which by tradition are to be apples and oranges.\n\nWho plays what is figured by the roll of a die. Lowest roller is apples.\nApples always go first.\n\nPlays are round-robin. Initially plays are done by placing one item onto any open tile. However after six plays, when all the items are on the board, plays are done by moving one of one's own items onto any open adjacent tile.\nThe game is won by constructing a mill, which is a vertical, horizontal, or diagonal row of three items.\n[!] A strange mark is on this page.\n[!] A different but equally strange symbol marks this page too.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter", "Seth'onn", "Titania, High Princess of Mali'nor;\n\nIf you are reading this note, I am likely already near another city or rotting dead in the woodlands. I would like to propose a final question to your motives before my exile and excommunication.\nIf one breaks into a home, as your Sentinel put it \"Burglary\" and, after corrected as to the fact that nothing was stolen, \"Attempted Burglary\" (despite the motive not entailing the stealing of any material object) and is punished with exile, I would\nsimply like to know the fate of my attacker. She who, ensured or at the very least dramatically increased my chances of death in the forests.\n\nIt is my understanding, from the information provided by your son, that she has simply been removed from\nher position on the Lumidrim.\n\nDoes severety of punishment scale with the insignifigance of crime? Or is she simply preferred because she is the daughter of Prince Khel?\n\nThe way you make your system\nout to be, one would assume tenants of fairness and justice be in place. But from the sheer circumstance of myself being torn from my home and tossed into the cold in comparison to the murderer being given a stern repremand and a flick on the nose\nimplies hasty decision making. I am asking you to rethink what you've done, and to understand the severity of a punishment that is warranted of no true malcontent, if we follow the law blindly and without question we are no better than the Valah.\nI will wait outside of the city walls until the letter is recieved. Tell your son that his kindness is refreshing and quite charming.\n\nSeth'onn\n\n*The letter is \"written\" in purple glowing writing.*", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter - Guild", "Brog Dhoon", "The name is Brog Dhoon. I come travelling from the far, Southern kingdom of Haense.\n\nHearing many a tale of the magnificents of The Dominion and her people, the stories of the Guild of Magicians has sparked in my eyes.\nI am but a worker of the land, 34 years of age, having no handle on magic nor grasping the greatness one holds with such.\n\nI seek the understanding of magic, and more specifically, the ability to flow one with The Void, and to harness the abilities it may\nso grant me. To use these new powers for the better of my land, and to take my borish life to an extent I knew not to imagine many years ago.\n\nBrog Dhoon of Haense. Council member under the Regent, but before that, a man whom pleads to be taught\nin the methods of Arcanism. I come to ask for a teacher, any teacher, to take myself under their wing and guide me to a level higher than now. \n\nYou may wish to not take a man like myself in, to which I would find most saddening.\nHowever, for if you are to accept myself into the position of student, may you send word through bird or individual to the Kingdom of Haense for my meeting. I will traverse the lands once more, and many more after, to partake in such.\nI am in your care with this letter, and regarding your response, may I be in the care of a teacher as well.\n\n\n          Well Regards,\n     \n\n         Brog Dhoon", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter By Alison", "Alison Skion", "It is I, Alison Skion. This letter might have my last words.. Hopefully not, but I want you people of Evermoor, and my dear friends to know... I want to thank you all for being part of my life. \n\nDon't come here for me, or try to save me, if I die ...\nThen it was always ment to be so... At least I will die by trying to do right, so no, don't come here.. They are waiting for you to do so just.. To get to Avalon and kill him. Risking my life over more isn't worth it. \nIf I never return, ....\n\nPlease don't give up on the Kingdom and city, keep it going... Rise it up and give the people a home they deserve. Defend the home of ours, defend the king.\n\nI will be probably killed by being a traitor to Norland, by serving the king, Avalon.\nBut I can sure you all, I know it's a right reason to die for, for the kingdom and it's people, for the king I serve. So I shall thank also Harry, who is part of Norland.. For being the only nice around here.. Trying to stop these men from killing me...\nHopefully it will work.. But shall see.. Stay safe people..\n\nWith Love\n~Alison\n\n*A heart would be drawn to the right corner of the letter*", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter for Aeran", "Ashton", "\"Dearest Aeran,\n\nI am writing to you, because speaking about how I feel always goes wrong. I either stuff my feelings inside myself, denying everything that's wrong, or I blow up with anger, panic, and do drastic things.\"\n\"So, a letter. If I become overwhelmed with emotions, I can simply walk away and come back to it later.\n\nI hope I can keep this short and sweet. I'm sorry in advance if I can't.\"\n\"I feel replaced. It's the only word I can think of. It's the only word that fits. Even though I know that isn't the case, it's the only word that belongs there.\"\n\"Up until recently, I was the only person in my dad's immediate family. His mother lived far away. His sister was in hiding. He apparently has a brother that he can't stand. He doesn't identify himself as a Winterleaf to have those relations.\"\n\"It was just us. Me and him.\n\nThe same was true with you and me.\n\nSure, the kids in the grove came to you. As far as actually hanging out and being friends, you were all I had, though.\"\n\"For a time, I illusioned myself into believing the same was true for your end. That I was your only real friend. \n\nMy dad might be your best friend, but he doesn't come around often. He doesn't talk often. When he does, it's deep and meaningful, sure.\"\n\"However, he's often fleeting and after his meaningful words are spoken, he goes back into his meditative state, not really saying much of anything for days or weeks.\"\n\"I felt like we were all a team. You, me, my dad. I felt like we were outcasts here. Everyone sort of thinks differently and acts like a jerk towards you and my dad.\"\n\"Then, Riley came back.\"\n\"Suddenly, my dad is around more, and all he wants to do is spend time with his sister.\n\nI understand. I truly do. Their mother just died. That's his SISTER. I get it.\n\nBut I was alone.\"\n\"Suddenly, you were in love with her. Every conversation was about her. About how pretty she is. About how wonderful and kind she is. About how I'll like her. About how it doesn't have to upset me that she's here. Everything was about her.\"\n\"And again, I was alone.\"\n\"I feel alone. Like I did in Felsen. Before I came to the grove. Everything is about her now. \n\nI feel like all of this is happening for the wrong reasons, but perhaps it's just because I'm not really involved.\"\n\"What I see...is two people getting married for the wrong reasons.\n\nShe wants to live her life to the fullest. Great! She wants to make up for all the time she lost while in hiding. Great! She feels like she needs to do something drastic.\"\n\"To make sure she doesn't lose any more time. That's what I see in her. Immaturity. Restlessness. The need to do crazy things to feel alive again.\"\n\"And what I see in you?\n\nI see someone who wants to prove that he has a purpose here. Someone who was almost ousted from his home, from his family. \n\nThat's what you told me when I came here.\"\n\"We are ALL family. That's what you said when I told you how alone I felt.\n\nI can't imagine how it must feel to know they wanted to unattune you. To feel like your family wanted you gone. You've been shoved away by so many people.\"\n\"I'm afraid you're going to marry my aunt, because she makes you feel like you're not alone. Like she won't shove you away. \n\nI'm scared it's for all the wrong reasons.\"\n\"But I don't know. I don't know anything. I feel so in the dark.\n\nWhen I'm around, it's not about how things really are. It's just about how perfect she is. That's all it's ever about.\n\nWith you and with my dad.\"\n\"It's always the same. I can't even say hello and talk without it turning into, \"Have you seen your aunt today? She's great, right? You like her, right? Let me tell you more about her, so you'll like her more.\"\n\nI get it. You both want me to like her.\"\n\"But I feel so replaced.\"\n\"I feel so alone.\"\n\"I feel like I don't belong here anymore.\"\n\"Or maybe I replaced her for my dad.\n\nMaybe he missed his family, and I was just their replacement.\n\nNow, he has his sister back, and I just sort of exist here.\"\n\"Maybe with you, I was just a filler until someone you could love came along. Someone pretty and nice and wonderful and smart.\"\n\"I know that isn't true. I know that's not how it is, but damn, that's how it feels.\"\n\"I'm sorry to pour all this on you, my friend.\n\nThis is a time of happiness in your life, and that's all I've wanted for you since you became my friend. I've wanted to see you smile and be truly happy, and you seem to be now.\"\n\"I'm sorry.\"\n\n\n-Ashton", ""),
        StaticBook("LETTER FROM COMM", "Commodus de Jedih", "A letter written on a giant lilypad with dark green slime that has dried and crusted over lays infront of Commodus' kitchen.\nddddddddddddddddddd\n\nDear Employers,\n\nI am requesting extended leave from work because I-\nhave become one with the wonk frog people of the 'Wonkawood'. I have smoked a pipe of Brokenblend and eaten crickets beside Mekko's fire and dug for treasure in the slime pits. They say if I keep finding the pieces of their prophecy scattered around -\nAtlas, they'll pay me handsomely with an 'Icon of Truth' which their big brother commando 'Mani' will take and answer any question I desire. \n\nPlease don't fire me,\n-Commodus.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter from Leo", "Leonard", "[!] The writer's hand shows clear signs of poverty and no education, spots of ink and crossed words found on it. Some of the letters are capitalized when they shouldn't be, and the grammar is way off and difficult to decypher.\nDear Master Kelly,\n\nI send you this letter in hopes of negotiating some form of deal to sell your famed wines to the highborns of Carolstadt in the Mos'LeHarmless Cantina. Hope to see you soon.\n\nBest regards, Leonard.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter of Marrow", "Unknown", "I know that you have been visited by the Order of Youth, what have you been doing to get them to notice you? Surely you are not contesting what he has done, he found it that’s for sure, and you know how his followers become when you question him.\nIblees would be jealous of their rage. You know that humans fear for their short lives, trying to remove hope of extending it will make them mad. I hope you didn’t get hurt by them, the best of health to you, may Aeriel bless your body.\nAs for what you asked me to get, I convinced the town’s people that their death were diseased. You will have the corpses sent to you in a week’s time. I am glad to hear that you have traded those foul potions for the study of anatomy and healing.\nIf you ever require any more wisdom or help in the study, do not be scared to ask me. I have been your friend for many years, and your doctor for far more.\n\n\nSafe study,\n     Doctor Marrow", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Elora", "Nenar", "Elora,\nI did not ever want to write this letter. But it seems as though my time in this place may soon be cut short. I've made many mistakes in my past, and one which I regret above everything else. I betrayed our people by loving a human. I cannot hide\nthis from my superiors any longer. I must tell them, though I fear it may cost me my life. If I should not return, please, care for Thilln. She deserves so much love, after the life she's had. If I cannot be there to give it to her, I hope you can. Maybe,\nwith time, she will learn to let go of my memory. I do not wish to impose on your kindness and compassion, Elora. But I must ask this favor of you, not for my sake, but for Thilln's. Do not let her mourn me. 'Tis up to the fates. I've cheated death far\ntoo long. It is time for me to return to my family.\nVan'ayla, llir. I hope one day, you can forgive me. It was a foolish decision, made in the ignorance of youth. If you cannot, I will understand. I do not deserve forgiveness for what I have done.\nAhernan, and I'm sorry. Please, give Thilln a hug for me. And never let her forget that I love her.\n\n~Nenar", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Farah", "Nenar", "My dear friend,\nYou once said you'd hate me forever were my decisions to lead to my death. I fear I must inform you now, that you were right to be angry that day. I go now to meet the Exarch. I must confess my crime and betrayal of our people. I know you\nshall be angry. You will be right in your anger. But, as I was once your friend, please, I must beg a favor of you. Watch over Thilln. She's too young, too loving to understand the gravity of what I have done. Or the consequences I go now to face. Do not\nlet her grow bitter at the world, llir. She's got such a future ahead of her.\nTake care, Farah. Would that I could stay longer by your side. I'm sorry for leaving you like this. I never wanted to hurt you.\nIf you can never bring yourself to forgive me, I\nshall understand. It is an unforgivable thing.\nMy only wish is that one day, you will be able to understand.\nVan'ayla, Farah. Take good care of Kacper and Damien. You are greatly blessed with your family. Don't ever give them up.\n\n~Nenar", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Guild", "Satelle Artoxia", "Dear Mage Guild,\n\nHello, I am Satella Artoxia. I was looking to join the Mages Guild. I have not learned any magic yet, but has read a lot on Void Magic. I would like to help the guild wherever and if I can.\n\n-Signed Satella", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to John", "Barnabas Basarab", "Letters to the\n      Duke of Adria\n7th of the First Seed, 1663.\n\nTo the Duke Jan of Sarkoz, I write to you with a heavy heart. For I fear for harm against both my eternal body and intellectual mind. I must promptly free from the city of Belvitz and resign any of the posts which have\nbeen entrusted unto me. I leavy the City Treasury which has made \$3000.00 minae to the next Maer of Belvitz whom the townsfolk will elect.\n\nMayhaps the next time I will visit Belvitz, I will see you as an old man.\n\nBarney Basarab", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Kacper", "Nenar", "Officer Kacper Silma,\nI'm sorry for betraying your trust in me sir. You welcomed me into the Dominion. You offered me a place in the Virarim. And I have betrayed that trust you placed in me. I can honestly say I have never regretted anything more. You\nwere always kind, and willing to teach. I never wanted to let you down sir. I'm sorry for betraying you, the Virarim, and the whole of the mali people by loving a human. You'll probably be disgusted as you read this. As well you should. I tell you this\nnow as I am probably going to my death. I do not wish to lie to you, or any other mali. I am confessing my crimes, and will leave my fate in the hands of the Lady Exarch, Praetor, and Queen. I wanted you to know that even though I've made mistakes sir, I\nwanted to die speaking the truth, and trying to restore my honor.\nI do not want to die in shame, but if the spilling of my blood will wash away the stain I have brought upon the Dominion, then so be it.\nI ask only one thing, sir. Watch out for Adris.\nHe's a good mali, though struggling with fitting in. He could use a guiding hand. I believe you might be able to help him sir.\n\nVan'ayla, and may the Aspects protect you sir. I'm sorry for living a cowards life.\nI hope in the end, I die with honor. ~Nenar", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to my Son", "Gray Kellian III", "To Gray Kellian III\n To my Eldest and Only son. \nI am Sorry.\nBut I relized I am not Well. So I am leaving for a while. I need time to reflect.\nI leave the house to you, Along with all my gear I kept precious to me. Do not allow anyone to use\nThem. They are yours, and only Yours.\nSecondly, I leave my Title to you. You can call yourself\nGray Kellian the Third, Keeper of the Kellian household and all her possessions.\nFarewell for now my son.\nI love you, Your father\n\n  -Ethro Kellian the Second, Retired Keeper of the Kellians", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Roscoe", "Barnabas Basarab", "A Letter to\n   Roscoe of Killeen\n7th of the First Seed, 1663\n\nTo my friend, the Lizard Roscoe of Locklear. I fear that the brigand Edgar of Sarkoz will make an attempt at my life. He has questioned me about the nature of my condition for three days now, and I believe he wish to\nstring me up. We will meet again, within the next century I presume. For now, I am on the run.\n\nBarney Basarab", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Val", "Ishralli", "Dear Val,\n\nNo-no you, but give late Krugsmas present. Seem nice.\nFrom,\n\nIshralli", ""),
        StaticBook("Level 4 Code 2", "Jaya Jayamen", "Level 4 Code 2\niyftyhoeuwsoeredtthoiwsesra", ""),
        StaticBook("Librarium Report", "Gallidron Elindrow", "A report on the Grand Library of Sutica, formerly the Lubba Atheneum.\n\n\n\nCurator Gallidron Elindrow.\nI am pleased to announce, that despite the derelict conditions that the former curator left the library in, I have brought about order and organization.\n\nAfter combing through the many, MANY donations to the library that had been\nand left to gather dust, I found a good number of tomes and novels that could make a delightful contribution to our collection. As such I have more than doubled our inventory within the sections of the Beastiary\nReligious writings\nHuman history\nand mundane healing.\n\nAs well I have added a spattering of books in the other sections of the library.\n\nI have also undertaken to increase the security of our books, given the rash of disapearances of tomes of all kinds\nacross Axios. It is a more cumbersome system, but the books won't simply vanish off the shelves anymore.\n\nI am of course endevoring to find more books of every kind to strengthen our selection. To that end I have begun speaking with the Enchantry in hopes\nthat they may have some books to trade.\n\nThis concludes my report.\n\n~Gallidron Elindrow\n\nCurator of the Grand Library of Sutica", ""),
        StaticBook("Library Treaty", "Arelion Laurir'ante", "This Note would make the deal between the Libraries of Holm, and Haelun'or Official, in which they shall agree to become Sister Libraries with one another, and trade books with one another.\n\n~Azkel 'The Scholar' Frostbeard\n~ Arelion Laurir'ante", ""),
        StaticBook("Liches.", "Jakir Axem", "[ In eloquent writing the word Liches, is spelled out on the front cover of the book. The words striking and glowing a faint golden. Under it are the words. By Jakir Axem. It seems the writing glows brighter as you get closer to it. Inviting you in.]\n[What seems to be a man shrouded in black, and clad in a dark robe. Staring out at you, watching from under his hood. The hands of the man seem to be skeletal and he is flanked by two undead zombie like figures. The words under it.] \"A Lich.\"\n[For the rest of the book, the writing seems to return to normal black ink, with less time spent on the style of writing to help the reader to clearly see the writing and understand the lessons in the tome.]\nChapter one: Introduction.\n\nFor many years Liches have roamed the earth, we do not know where they first come from. But we do know they have been around for a very long time. I myself have killed a few, but they are not to be taken lightly.\nI was gifted with the power of gods, many who read this will not be, so I decided to make this guide so you may be able to fight them without the help of others. In this book you will find the information one might need as well as my own personal.\nexperience with these dark beings so you may better survive the next encounter you may have with them. It will only have the basic knowledge for we do not know it all, and do not wish others to try to copy in their dark arts.\nChapter two: The Lich.\n\nThe Lich is a creature made of dark magic, usually necromancy. At first they were thought  to of come from the dark power of Iblees. This is true, but those Liches are long passed, today Liches are made\nfrom necromancy and many a necromancer has tried to transcend into Lichdom. But you may wonder why there is not hundreds running around. It’s because the process is deadly and requires a lot of time and effort, and also the knowledge\non creation which has been lost to most. They use the power of necromancy to move a large portion of their life-force into an object referred to as a phylactery, this is their power supply, for it connects directly to the Lich in question.\nThe only problem being it could be hidden anywhere, so the permanent death of a Lich is unlikely but it also has a time it can live, due to the removal of life-force and the tether. The Lich will die in the end and it can’t stop it.\nChapter three: Combat.\n\nAs undead creatures, the main weakness of a Lich is gold. Gold is the bane of all known undead and as such. One should use golden weaponry over all else. Liches are unable to use necromancy due\nto the lost of most of their life-force and are also unable to access voidal or divine magic. But they are strong and smart. Bound to the will of the necromancer that created them but also free to do as they please otherwise.\nThey know fear and they will target the most dangerous person first. I myself have killed only a few, and they all have tried to kill me first. Only by me being ready was I able to stop them killing me and becoming their next victim.\nA few Liches are known for ranged weapons. Due to the lack of magic they use alchemy and bows. They are the cause of the Fringe Plague for it attacked me directly with a stronger version of the plague I was only just able to bat away in time.\nSome even wear armour, but they are made of bone and dead skin, so non golden or divine weapons are almost useless when fighting them. So be careful when facing them, they are not something one should take lightly and even more so if you are alone.\nChapter four: Personal experience \n\nI am a user of divine magic, and as such I have had to face them at their most deadly and worse. They tend to enlist the help of necromancers for extra help. As such I have\nI have had to fight the beasts of the necromancers and Liches. One being a monster made of young Mali children sewn together and made alive again with the vile magics. The lich that caused the Fringe Plague\nI had to remove after it infected most of Alras killing many and infecting many others. To which I had to remove the plague from. They are deadly creatures and some of the worst beings you can find, I hope you\nnever have to use the information found within this tome, for it is a true horror what these dark beasts will do to those who mealy get in it’s way, or if it feels like having fun.\nEpilogue: \n\nI Jakir Axem made this book to help others in fighting Liches, this book will no doubt be one of many, you can tell it is of my own design by the cover. . If it does not glow, then the book is just a copy.\nThank you for taking the time and reading this tome, I hope it helps you should the worse come to pass, and I hope that you never have to use it. This is part of the collection I shall be making on this subject,\nranging from as many dark beings I have come to fight, and find within the world. Thank you once again, and if we do meet out in the world, understand that what I do, I did by choice, and that even if you do face these things\n, you can move on and you are not alone.\n\n[Once again the fancy writing returns, the small signature of Jakir Axem written in golden glowing ink pulsing lightly at the end of the book.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Liewyn's Journal", "Liewyn Annungilben", "~The Medical Journal of Liewyn Annungilben\n\n~Index\nSection 1: The Composition of the Body\nSection 2: The Application of Basic Medical Treatments\nSection 3: Practical Herbalism \n~Section 1: The Composition of the Body\n-The body is comprised of multiple organized groups divided by their function, including the circulatory, respiratory, skeletal, and muscular systems.\nEach are inherent to the proper function of the body and the spread of blood throughout the flesh, which in turn provides anima, the life-driving force of all living beings, to what would otherwise be a highly complex corpse.\nProviding healing to the afflicted first requires an in-depth understanding not only of the various parts of the body, but even more importantly how they work together.\n-The circulatory system is composed of the heart and the vessels that pump\nblood throughout the body. Without either enough blood or clean blood, the anima in a body will fail and take the patient with it. Blood can be contanimated not only by the typical suspects of dirt and diseases, but also by prolonged exposure to the air.\nHence, the proper cleaning and wrapping of bleeding areas is vital to the body.  \n-The respiratory system is comprised primarily of the lungs and throat that filter in air to the body and provide vital nutrients to the blood and anima contained therein.\nTypical respiratory illnesses can range from the common cold to something far more severe, so the proper care and soothing of respiratory symptoms is a vital process.\n-The skeletal system is composed of various bones, typically ranging upwards of 200 in\nmost bodies, joined together by muscular sinews. Broken or disjointed bones are frequently found on the battlefield, so the understanding of how they interact with each other and how they are meant to lay on the body is vital to their care.\n-The muscular system is made up of various muscle and sinew tissues, holding bones together and working in pairs to both push and pull in motion. Muscular diseases can be incredibly debilitating and need higher levels of treatment.\n~Section 2: The Application of Basic Medical Treatments\n-First Aid Kits are often carried by healers to provide general and emergency treatment to the afflicted. A good kit includes strips of clean cloth to use as bandaging material, a vial of\nalcohol to keep both the body and medical utensils clean, and gauze to apply herbal compresses to wounds. Needles and thread are required for stitching wounds shut, and bottles of water provide a variety of uses from creating herbal solutions to cleaning\nafflicted areas. Honey aids not only in infections but also to ease bitter medicines down and is therefore an additional item carried in most first aid kits. At all times, a mask is required, especially in the case of infection or spreadable disease.\n-Wounds caused by cuts or stabs must immediately be cleaned. Therefore, any materials that could further cause infection, such as dirty clothing or armor, must be removed and a material such as moss applied to staunch the blood. The wound must further be\ncleaned, typically with clear water or alcohol, before being properly treated. Typical disinfectants such as alcohol, urine, or even cauterization are often applied, before the wound is wrapped and the bandages frequently changed. At this stage, herbal\ncompresses are often applied to help soothe and treat the injury.\n-Head injuries are a frequent field of study for medics in the line of duty. When a patient is injured in the head, it is important to first get the patient to sit down while they are\nchecked for the extent of the wound, as well as any additional symptoms such as dizziness or nausea. Wrappings and herbal compresses may be applied as well if the wound is an obvious gash. Most minor head injuries can be healed through these measures and\nrest. Heavier injuries, such as the crushing of the skull, will typically render the patient unconscious. Checking for the pulse, nose, eyes, and any swelling in the face will typically indicate whether they have been severely damaged to the point of\nlittle return. In such cases, be sure to move them as little as possible and seek further help. \n-Broken bones are easily noticeable by strange lumps under the skin, a breaking of the bone through the skin, or an obvious discontinuity with the patient's\nlimbs. Sticks and cloth can be used to make splints to set the bones in question and prevent further movement of the area. Slings are a similar concept, most often used for broken arms. Dislocations, on the other hand, are not full breakages of the bones\nand require pressure to pop them back into place, which naturally guarantees plenty of pain for the patient in question; pain relievers are typically recommended in such cases. \n-Those found with lungs full of water or seemingly drowning must be brought\nonto land, placed on their side, and have their pulse checked. If a pulse is present but the patient is not breathing, recessitation may be attempted; to do so, place one hand above their heart with the other hand atop it and pump downwards 30 times.\nImmediately after, place one hand on the forehead of the patient and tilt it back to check for breath; if not present, attempt to share breath with the afflicted. Continue repeating these two steps until recessitation is achieved.\n-Injuries caused by arrows or other projectile weapons typically require the projectile to be forcefully removed before further treatment can be done. Typically such projectiles can be removed in several ways, either by pushing it through the body or in\nthe case of limbs by sawing off one end and allowing the wound to develop pus, at which point the projectile will be easier to remove. Regardless of the method, immediate cleaning of the wound and staunching of any blood flow, with fresh bandages and\nherbal compresses, will be vital to the process. \n~Section 3: Practical Herbalism\n-The use of herbs in various balms, compresses, and edible ingredients can be of great use to any medic in the field. Balms are formed by crushing various parts of herbs in\na mortar and pestle with small increments of water, and they are frequently used as compresses on bandages to over wounds. Edible herbs typically come either in their natural, drier form or boiled into tea. Below are a list of various herbs and their\ntypical usefulness in any medic’s pack, organized primarily by the afflictions they help treat.\n--Broken bones: Wheatgrass, ingested either naturally or in tea form\n--Burns: Bergamot Oil, Comfrey Root, Aloe Vera, and Mandagora when applied topically\n--Concussions: Tippen’s Root and Yarrow\n--Coagulants: Echinacea, Pot Marigold, Gumweed, Mullein, Chamomile, Lavender, Mandagora, Orchid, Strawberry, Orange Peel, Shade Leaf, and Blissfoil in tea form\n--Cuts: Blueberries, Raspberries, Strawberries, Blackberries, and Blissfoil in tea form\n--Disinfectants: John’s Wort and Kanna Flower in tea form\n--Scabbing: Yarrow, Witch’s Hazel, Dragur Tongue, Comfrey Root, and Tippen’s Root when applied topically\n--Scarring: Ginger Root, Red Raspberry Leaf, Echinacea, Lavender, Skullcap, and Crampbark in milk tea form \n--Muscle Fatigue: Beard Weed Oil, Yarrow, and Tippen’s Root\n--Pregnancy: Crampbark and Skullcap when ingested in coffee\n--Stomach Aches: Bromelian, Aloe Vera, and Gotu Kola when applied topically, not ingested\n--Sore Throats: Ginger Root, Peppermint, Chamomile, and Blissfoil in tea form", ""),
        StaticBook("Life of a Golem", "Va'Cduha", "*A whole is punched through the middle of this book, only allowing a few words to remain scribbled around the hole*\n\nGolem did this.", ""),
        StaticBook("Life Story", "William Fax", "The life of a Lil Yachty\nI was born in Asulon to Saren and Gor'ek'Gorkil. My sister and I lived a happy, quiet life, until the orcs had found our home. My father, not willing to disreguard customs or honor turning us over to the orcs in order to attone for his 'whitewash' ways\nA orc who is whitewash is seen as disnhonorable, one who has turned there back on the orc ways. By having an intimate relationship with my mother he had turned away from the orcs rule of keeping the blood pure and strong. The orcs took my sister and I-\n-in the middle of the night, leaving my mother for dead as they burnt the house to the ground, For the next ten years I grew up in the orc capital, where, dispite my vertigre, I failed to have a approite temperment of an orc, a disgrace to the name i was-\n-Abused, beaten, mocked, Where, my sister, Dispite her elven complextion, Thrived, proving herself and taking respect from the other orcs. It wasnt long before her and i were sent on our first hunt, i had come accross my fathers coprse and feard id be to-\nblame, So i ran, I ran away, to the temple. After some thought i had decided to try and find my mother, I drew posters of myself as missing and put them in the temple. Where i met a friend, Juno, a human who seemed concerned to see a 10 year old alone-\n-I didnt mind being alone though. He let me on my way afterwe talked and i went to the docks where i saw a orc party destory an elven boat, I followed them back to the city, dispite my previous reservations and found a plot for them to drive a boat-\n-of explosives into the elf city. I left the orc capital that night and returned to the docks where i found Khel and Azel, a few of the leaders, they didnt belvie me at first when i told them of the orcs plans but they took me in i told them what i could\n-find on the orcs, and he helped me find my mother. After awhile of seaching we were reunited, and life continued well enough, I shamefully didnt think much of my sister, or my orc life after that. We lived in peace until the flood came and we left for-\n-Elysiem, an island we took refuge on, I was 15 when we settled, the cities were built, the elves shareing a moutian with the dwarfs. I loved the moutian, the view, however, our neighbors, the highelfs were horrid, Kalenz, a highelf who took pleasure-\n-in using his mental magic to torture me when he could,back on Asulon, was a constant reminder i was not pureblood. i rarely saw him, but when i did, things got bad. I had started my shaman training, with my mentor lex, and i noticed someone messing with-\n-the gate of the city, after trying to stop them by using the spirit of water to splash them, they turned there attention to me, Evark, the name still brings a bitter taste, a litch who came fond of my power. I had been watching 2 other half orc children-\n-He threatened to kill them if i refused to serve him, So i relented and he introduced me to his daughter vallel, we would train with eachother, talk, she became a dear friend. We both wanted to be free of Evark, and one day, after he tried to spark my-\n-Bloodrage, i stood up to him, under the eye of meta, who saw the honor and fire in my heart, he became a father figure, a protector, i trained under him whenever i could get away from Evark, soon the choice came to decide what path to take, i shamfully-\n-left vallel behind to break free of Evark entirely. Not long after, meeting my first love, Daylen, no words can discripbe how much love i had in my heart for him. We were soon married, in time to see the end of Elysim-\nthe next city was Kalos, I was pregant and bore my first son, Talion, Daylen and i had been seperated in the evac of Elysim but i kept our child safe during his birth, I was around 18-21 at the time, i cared for him with the help of meta and the spirits.\nKalos was short lived, a stoping point, We then went to anthos, Where i reconnected with Vallel, however, After living away from the orcs for some time, i found that the spirits were displeased and refused to aide me. I was a meber of Vallels house of-\n-outcasts thinking i belonged, She welcomed daylen and i, however i slowly began to fade into a dark void as the spirits slipped away, I returned to the orcs and attoned for my whitewash ways, they accepted me back, I would slip away to see Daylen and-\nTalion when i could, until it became unbearable to be without them i left the orcs, again. However, losing the spirits cost me dearly, Vallel offered to tech me void magic, while another friend in the elven city offered druidism, i turned my back to -\n-Vallels studies and pourd myself to the druid ways. however, it did not go as planned, during my time with the orcs, one orc, kugar grew fond of me, While daylen and i were out enjoying a picnic together, Kugar had found us, and knocked me out, i woke-\n-to daylens headless body before me, my heart shattered, the only light i had was he had seen his daughter, Illera, before he was killed, Talion was 18, illera just been born, and after the death of daylen, it wasnt long before i found talion murdered-\n-in his room, stabbed in the stomach and heart. It was almost to much to bear, Vallel returned to try and help, she had daylen had never been fond of eachother, often vallel accused him of cheating while he went hunting, she set that aside to help in my-\n-time of need, however, once she left, the highelfs, kalenz, came looking for her 3 years later, They demanded i turn Illera over to them and i be put to death for knowing vallel, i promised to give them anything they wanted if they let us be, but after-\n-telling them where vallel was housed, the queen titania allowed me to be arrested, I sat in that jail for weeks until a druid put a magic vine on my arm to keep me from leaving the city,I stayed in the druids grove most of that time and found callax had-\n-brought in a half orc child, being experinced with them, i offered to care for the child, after much arguing, i was awarded custody of Lenniel. Illera and lennel were just infants, and i never told them they were not blood. however, i raised them as orc-\n-After months of the vine being on my arm, a few orcs had caught wind of the trapped half orc, they took me away, my arm cut and crushed in the process, some druids on the road found me and brought me back, i was distrought. then Vallel came back, she-\nburnt the vine off my arm, i went back to the grove where i was provked into my bloodrage as was a common theme, and after throwing a druid down a hill, breaking her arm, i was cast out, taking illera and lenniel with me to the orc capital.\nI had thankfully gotten the favor of the spirits, and not much time past before i was a shaman again, thanks to the help of Sharku, When i returned to the orcs, they were not so welcoming this time, Sharku had spoken for me and taught me to be an orc\nLenniel and Lera grew up thinking him to be there father, and he was, he raised them well, the orcs took over a human city, Salvus, and when we moved they had cast us in the slums. I paied it no mind, we spent little time in home anyway, i was teaching-\nlenniel and lera of the world, exploreing with them, and all seemed right with the world, i had little desire to return to the elves unless to see few friends, meta, being one of them. I had made such trip to see him, talking to him tempering my mind and-\n-rage, when i met Kael, a lost elf i gave directions to he grew rather fond of me and i him, as a friend. He would vist in Salvus when few orcs were around and the day came where i thought sharku had died, i was told he had been publicly exicuted as-\n-someone tried to take his spot as rex, he had been missing for some time and i belived him dead, Kael tried to get me to return to the elfs, abandon my magic and i refused, Illera and Lenniel having dissipered after they grew i had no desire to get-\nclose to anyone else, until I met Buurz, a strong orc who helped me build my house, he reminded me of jax, a half orc who i met after daylen passed away, he tried to court me, told me to give into my orcish side, He killed a man and i tried to leave-\n-his brother came into the picture and tried to attack, i killed them both in self defense, but buurz brought my spirits up like no other, he kept me confident and sure, groudned I loved him, And Athera was a time of peace, better then my time in Anthos-\nwhich was destoryed by plauge. Sharku returned, his death a lie from orcs who hated me. the rex making me pick between the two, i had saved him, and his eye, so giving me a choice rather then forcing me to sharku was his way of thanking me as well-\n-as letting Azkira be born, but before i could pick, Buurz died in a cave in, Sharku vanished, All my children as well, Illera, Len, Azkira, all of my children left at 18, never to be seen again, except for lera who came back a moment with sharku, but -\n-she to, left when the orcs tried to force her to stay, she was always a free spirit, and lenniel could not stand the harsh life of the orcs, she was build with brains, not brawn. I only wish my children well, and that they live a good decent life.\nAs everyone in my life, At least in the aspect of family, My mother (who left shortly after we arrived in Anthos) My lovers (Sharku and Burrz) my children, I have spent much time traveling, At sea, where Talion was most comfortable, and land, to run away.\nI dont want to run anymore, I have lost much, but not all, the spirits are here, I need to be there, to bring more shamans to this world, to teach, and spread knowlage, change only starts with the first step, and I belive its time I take mine.\n10th Grandharvest 1618\n(1/7/17)\n   Keeping to my promise, The child of my best student, Vorgo, proves to be well off, i've been appointed head of the libaray and will give the give of knowlage to orcs willing to learn. Spirits be with me, Im back!\n16th Sunsmile 1618 \n(2/7/17)\n  Meeting the slaves of the orc land puts a weight on my heart, these are people who have lost there homes, familes. They just wish for peace away from servitude, a dishonorable practice. Two servants today, Grace and-\n-Flynn reminded me of the hope we all try to feel, and grace, with her heart. both pure. I wish them well. Out  meeting was intreupted by an armoed figure who couldnt eat or drink, he was 'one of few' remaining, i wonder what else the days will bring.\n17 Grand Harvest 1621\n(7/22/17)\n     Zlash and I have reformed the council, Gathering the shamans together we discuseed the issues of the dark shamans, for now gathering intel and plotting. We must find out who they are and there plans before we move-\n-As well as Learning how to create a Myulek, I will not write the ritual, it being far to powerful to risk it being written down, but sha (hedgehug) found me worthy of the ritual! To be trusted with such a write is a blessing behond comapare. I feel my-\n-Life comming together being highshaman. I only hope to be a good enough teacher to Zlash, and now Ula, They should great Potenal, my prodogies. I have nothing but highest faith in them, Although Ula seems to be at risk due to her political standings-\n-She was threatend today, unacceptable. I felt myself going into rage. I want nothing but her safty as she reminds me not only of myself but my daughters. Her logical, thoughful mind, her raltional, she isnt like other orcs and proves her honor daily-\n-As a true orc should. She will be a quick study and a better student. We agree on much. The whitewashes being one of them, Although we must as the rex for approval. i have no doubt that we can reform them. The shamans comming together can only plese the-\n-Spirits, not like Zlashs storm spirit, my soul nearly shattered as his spirit stuck him down.He was revived, but i could not bear to lose another close to me. I hope this storm spirit does not abuse him. That he can control it, I will guide him to power-\n-But i can only do so much, it will be up to him, to his bond to progress and become one unit with his spirit. I worry, but he has strength, I must let him go his own path and trust he follows my techings\n12th grandharvest 1622\n(7/19/17)", ""),
        StaticBook("Life's joke", "Mika Uialben", "Breathe, breathe in the air \nDon't be afraid to care \nLeave, but don't leave me \nLook around \nChoose your own ground\nLong you live and high you fly \nAnd smiles you'll give and tears you'll cry \nAnd all you touch and all you see \nIs all your life will ever be\nRun, rabbit run \nDig that hole, forget the sun \nAnd when at last the work is done \nDon't sit down \nIt's time to dig another one\nFor long you live and high you fly \nBut only if you ride the tide \nAnd balanced on the biggest wave \nYou race towards an early grave", ""),
        StaticBook("Life.", "[Dedicant] Tierney", "Creative Component.\n\nI have decided to write a sort of short story for this task.\n\n'\n     A lost child, one of a land far from what one could call their own. Ask anyone, they would likely describe it as \"Far Away.\" The lost child resembled\na human, but resembled much more as well. Anything an infant's mind could dream of, that child was the embodiment of it. The waves of a vast sea coloured their scratchy, yet silky sweater; one could see the crashing waves\nwith each swipe of their arm.\nThe child's skin resembled parchment, oak, flickering blubs and lichen, as it was everything as one. Cold, clammy and soft hands would grasp out, light flickering, the reflections of soft feet prodding wooden floorboards visible. Hair like silk and steel\nwool, woven of leather and soft bits of bark.\n\n     The child had a soft smile, one that could end wars. Though it could also be what one would emote seconds before being beaten to death. With that smile the humanoid child led a vauge\nexistance. For they did not feel, were not aware of the beauty they possessed, they only drifted through time as an emotionless, numb husk of a being.\n\n     Though one day, the child was hit by a surge of will to live. To exist, overcome by an\nthe urge to live, to have a purpose. A large desire of which would burn brighter than any lights that composed their physical form. An itching, burning feeling of pure, unrelentless determination. \n\n     The child, with this new found desire,\nthought of how they would fufill such a burning feeling. With an intelligence of their level, the task wouldn't deem too difficult, would it? But how?\n\n     The child pondered and wondered for hours, coming to no conclusion. Unable to\nfeel frustration, they just stopped. Ceased the process of thought, trashing any and all previous plans. The child waited, before beginning to feel. To become aware of the body they inhabited, a sudden feeling of euphoria and wonder. Their fingers felt\nlike static had been woven into a glove, weaving its way down their arm. The static enveloped their body, tingling and confusing the child to the point of irritation. The point of emotion, breaking free of the cold and numb shell they had once inhabited.\nThey stayed there, emotions blossoming and popping within their chest, head and stomach. A violent cluster of everything ever felt, the flame of love and the waves of sadness. All of it, everything swirling together to an unbearable extent, mixing and\nforming into a solid mass of internal feelings, before messily crashing onto the child.\n\n     It was sudden, the change. The child was sitting, eyes closed and hands clamed tight. A small voice, one that could be labelled as a\nconciousness, spoke.\nIt spoke of altertness, and instructed the child. It instructed to keep living, to love again. It reassured the child, to the point of movement.\n\nThe child opened their eyes, fearlessly and suddenly. They stared at a ceiling, a\nwhite-washed stucco ceiling, with a lighht fixture patterning adorning it. \n\n     The child heared a shirl beeping, one that could resemble a heart monitor. A gasp, followed by jumbled words and joyful cries. The child had no strength to\nmake any efforts to see more than the bleak ceiling, but they knew something.\n\nThey knew they were alive, and that filled them with reassurance greater than any other.", ""),
        StaticBook("Light&Dark", "Gray Kellian III", "Clerical Jornal\nEntry 1:\n\nThe Question was given to me to go and think about,\n\n\"What is light and dark to you\"\n\nAnd here is my answer after careful thought\nFirst of all What is light?\n\nLight according to Tahariae, is purity with white light being the purest.\n\nBut what could you relate purity to? Innocences. And who is innocent above everything? Youth.\nLight is the youth of the world, for no child can be born evil. And the youth are the protecters of tomorrow. And we must raise them to fight the evil of tomorrow until one day. there will be no evil.\nAnd Darkness\n\nAccording to Tahariae Darkness is the Evil, the undead the ghouls, and just the 'Spooks' As the decendents have dubbed them.\n\nBut it appears to not include decendents who do evil deeds, such as murders, and bandits\nBut to me? Darkness is all forms of evil, Someone who kills and pilliages for fun, I beleive to be in the darkness. The people whos only wish is to watch other people suffer, are in the darkness.\nBut that is where the line fades, and blends together.\n\nThe point where you need to make a choice.\n\nTahariae does not give us his power to fight off bandits, and murders, but the taint, and spooks\nSo sometimes we might have to make a decision when helping people of purity. \n\nDo we use what he can to stop a murder?\n\nWould that displease Tahariae because to him, The murderer is not a Killer?\nTherefore to make that decision is a huge one, with even greater potential risks.\n\nSo choose carefuly. \nBecause this is a test of your Morals.\nSigned\n\nGray Kellian the Third\n\nKeeper of the Kellian Family, Along will her assets.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lion and Mouse", "Isabella Jameson", "Once when a lion, the king of the jungle, was asleep, a little mouse began running up and down on him. This soon awakened the lion, who placed his huge paw on the mouse, and opened his big jaws to swallow him.\n\"Pardon, O King!\" cried the little mouse. \"Forgive me this time. I shall never repeat it and I shall never forget your kindness. And who knows, I may be able to do you a good turn one of these days!” The lion was so tickled by the idea of the mouse being\nable to help him that he lifted his paw and let him go. Sometime later, a few hunters captured the lion, and tied him to a tree. After that they went in search of a wagon, to take him to the zoo. Just then the little mouse happened to pass by.\nOn seeing the lion’s plight, he ran up to him and gnawed away the ropes that bound him, the king of the jungle. \"Was I not right?\" said the little mouse, very happy to help the lion.", ""),
        StaticBook("Livestock", "Mervel Frostbeard", "Introduction to \nLivestock\n\nBy\nMervel Frostbeard\nWhat is livestock?\n\nLivestock are domestic animals, like cows pigs and chickens, that are usually raised on a farm, and for profit.\nWays of Getting Livestock\n\nMethod 1\n\nGo outside, with either a lead, or the food the animal your looking for likes, and wander around your area till you find the desired animal(s).\nMethod 2\n\nGo to an animal trader, and purchase livestock.\nWhere to Put You Livestock\n\nA good place to put your livestock is in a barn, so I suggest making one yourself. You can make a house barn, or an underground barn. Underground barns are cheaper, but more poor looking, and worse for the animals.\nHow To Produce More Livestock\n\nYou will need two of the desired livestock you wish to produce, and there favorite food. Feed the the first animal, and then the second (no crossbreeding, except for horses and donkeys.). Try to feed both of them at the >\nsame time, with great speed. This will assure the production of the desired animal.\n\nList of foods animals like\n\nChicken = Seeds\nPigs = Carrots\nSheep = Wheat\nCows = Wheat\nHorses = Wheat, Hay Bales, Sugar, Apples,>\nAnd bread.\n\nDonkeys, Mules, and Horses might all eat the same foods, But I think they all eat wheat.\n\nYou can speed the growing time of baby animals by feeding there favorite foods to them.\nYou can buy some animals near my place, located near the path leading to Kaz'Ulrah.\n\nFacts\n\nOrc clans make alot of livestock.\n\nI suggest making a farm for food, both for you and your animals. You can >\nAlso use a public farm.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNo copyright", ""),
        StaticBook("Llirame & T'Tree", "Nivndil Duskhollow", "~*~          Llirame         ~*\n            and the Tree\n\nThere was once a Wood Elf named Llirame, who lived in a cottage near Oakhearth. In the garden there grew a young apple tree. As a child, Llirame would play in the tree.\nWhen he was troubled or saddened, he spoke to the tree and he felt comforted.\nLlirame became dear friends with the tree, as they aged together.\nOver the years, the tree blossomed every Malin's Welcome and grew fruit every Grand Harvest.\nYear after year, the tree provided fruit and shelter for Llirame and his family. His children climbed in its branches, just as he had before them.\nUntil one year, when the tree's leaves became a sickly yellow.\nLlirame came out to the tree and said, \"Old friend you look gravely ill, though I know not what to do. Should I cut you down?\"\nThe tree did not reply.\nAs the Seeds went on, the tree grew worse.\nThe bark of its branches came loose and its fruit became bitter and wilted.\nLlirame came out to the tree again. \"Old friend, you are gravely ill. I should cut you down to save you from pain.\"\nThe tree did not reply.\nBut the tree grew sicker still. It's branches grew heavy and some began to fall from the tree with rot.\nIts bark began to peel from its boughs and the leaves folded inwards. Insects burrowed into its trunk.\nOne day, a Druid came to Oakhearth. Llirame sought her out earnestly.\n\"Oh wise Druid, my best friend is gravely ill and I know not what to do,\" Llirame pleaded.\n\"Very well,\" she replied. \"Take me to your friend.\"\nLlirame brought the Druid to the tree.\n\"Llirame, your friend is gravely ill,\" she said examining the tree carefully.\n\"What should I do?\" he asked. \"Should I cut it down to save it from suffering?\"\n\"No,\" replied the Druid. \"Your friend tells me that it does not want to be cut down.\"\nLlirame looked upon the tree and sighed, \"Old friend I will not cut you down unless you wish it so.\" He promised.\nThe Druid produced a talisman, made from roots woven together. She tied it around a thick branch of the tree and said, \"The tree is able to use this talisman. If your friend wishes to be cut down, the talisman will fall and not before.\"\nLlirame thanked the Druid, who left Oakhearth and went on her way.\nDays went by, when Llirame would come out to the tree and say \"Old friend you are gravely ill, is today the day when you would have me cut you down?\"\nThe talisman had not moved.\nWeeks went by, when Llirame would come out to the tree.\n\"Is today when you would have me cut you down, old friend?\"\nThe talisman did not move.\nSeeds had passed, when Llirame came out to the tree.\n\"Old friend you are gravely ill. Is today when you would have me cut you down?\" he asked.\n\nBut the tree had died.\nIts leaves had fallen and its twisted branches were bare. Its bark was black and peeled, the flesh beneath was diseased and rotten.\n\nLliram cried as he beheld the dead tree.\nHe did not eat for days, in mourning for his oldest friend.\nWhen the Druid returned to Oakhearth, she visited Llirame in his home.\n\"Oh wise Druid, my oldest friend is dead and I know not what to do,\" he sobbed.\n\"You were good to respect the wishes of your friend,\" she replied.\n\"But my friend has died in pain and suffering,\" sobbed Llirame.\nSoon after, the Druid left Oakheart and went on her way.\nDays passed, before Llirame could bring himself to remove the remains of the tree.\nHe went to it and sobbed as he peeled away its blackened bark.\nHe wept as he went to get his sharpest axe.\nBefore Llirame could ready to swing however, he saw something green and new in the tree.\nIn a hole of its trunk, where bark and splinters and soil had gathered, there grew a small sprout.\nLlirame brought it water and compost.\nLlirame tended the sprout for days, just as the tree had cared for Llirame and his family.\nAs the weeks passed and the Seeds changed, the sprout grew stronger.\nThe old tree quickly fell apart and crumbled away.\nBut in its husk the new sprout was sheltered from the wind and the heavier rains.\nWhen the Druid returned to Oakhearth a year later, she visited Llirame who presented her with a budding sapling.\nThe Druid smiled and touched Llirame on the shoulder.\n\"Just as there is death\nthere is also life. As there is decay so there is growth. As there is rot, so\nthere is blossom,\" she said to him.\nIn the years to come, the new tree became a dear friend to Llirame's children.\nIt gave fruit and sheltered many small animals.\nLlirame never forgot his old friend, but as it had been there for him, so he was there for the new tree.", ""),
        StaticBook("Llirame & The", "Nivndil Duskhollow", "(~+~)  Llirame  (~+~)\n                &\n          The Tree\n\n\nThere once was a Wood Elf named Llirame. He lived in a small cottage near Oakhearth. In the garden grew a young apple tree.\n\nAs a young Elf, Llirame played in the tree.\nWhen he was troubled or saddened, he spoke to the tree and he felt comforted.\n\nLlirame became dear friends with the tree, as they aged together.\n\nOver the years, the tree blossomed every Malin's Welcome and grew fruit every Grand Harvest.\nWhen Llirame reached three-hundred years old, he had a family of his own.\n\nYear after year, the tree provided fruit and shelter for Llirame and his family. His children climbed in its branches, just as he had before them.\nUntil one year, when the tree's leaves became a sickly yellow.\n\nLlirame came out to the tree and said, \"Old friend you look gravely ill, though I know not what to do. Should I cut you down?\"\n\nThe tree did not reply.\nAs the Seeds went on, the tree grew worse.\n\nThe bark of its branches came loose and its fruit became bitter and wilted.\n\nLlirame came out to the tree again. \"Old friend, you are gravely ill. I should cut you down to save you from pain.\"\nThe tree did not reply.\n\nBut the tree grew sicker still. It's branches grew heavy and some began to fall from the tree with rot.\n\nIt's bark began to peel from its boughs and its leaves folded inwards. Insects burrows into its trunk.\nOne day, a Druid came to Oakhearth. Llirame sought her out earnestly.\n\n\"Oh wise Druid, my best friend is gravely ill and I know not what to do,\" Llirame pleaded.\n\n\"Very well,\" she replied. \"Take me to your friend.\"\nLlirame brought the Druid to the tree.\n\n\"Llirame, your friend is gravely ill,\" she said examining the tree carefully.\n\n\"What should I do?\" he asked. \"Should I cut it down to save it from suffering?\"\n\"No,\" replied the Druid. \"Your friend tells me that it does not want to be cut down.\"\n\nLlirame looked upon the tree and sighed, \"Old friend I will not cut you down unless you wish it so.\" He promised.\nThe Druid produced a talisman, made from roots woven together. She tied it around a thick branch of the tree and said, \"The tree is able to use this talisman. If your friend wishes to be cut down, the talisman will fall and not before.\"\nLlirame thanked the Druid, who left Oakhearth and went on her way.\n\nDays went by, when Llirame would come out to the try and say, \"Old friend, you are gravely ill. Is today when you would have me cut you down?\nThe talisman had not moved.\n\nWeeks went by, when Llirame would come out to the tree.\n\n\"Is today when you would have me cut you down, old friend?\"\n\nThe talisman did not move.\nSeeds had passed, when Llirame came out to the tree.\n\n\"Old friend you are gravely ill. Is today when you would have me cut you down?\" he asked.\n\nBut the tree had died.\nIt's leaves had fallen and its twisted branches were bare.\n\nIt's bark was black and peeled and the flesh beneath was diseased and rotten.\n\nLlirame cried as he beheld the dead tree.\nHe did not eat for days, in mourning for his oldest friend.\n\nWhen the Druid returned to Oakhearth, she visited Llirame in his home.\n\n\"Oh wise Druid, my oldest friend is dead and I know not what to do,\" he sobbed.\n\"You were good to respect the wishes of your friend,\" she replied.\n\n\"But my friend has died in pain and suffering,\" sobbed Llirame.\n\nSoon after, the Druid left Oakheart and went on her way.\nDays passed, before Llirame could bring himself to remove the remains of the tree.\n\nHe went to it and sobbed as he peeled away its blackened bark.\n\nHe wept as he went to get his sharpest axe.\nBefore Llirame could ready to swing however, he saw something green and new in the tree.\n\nIn a hole of its trunk, where bark and splinters and soil had gathered, there grew a small sprout.\n\nLlirame brought it water and compost.\nLlirame tended the sprout for days, just as the tree had cared for Llirame and his family.\n\nAs the weeks passed and the Seeds changed, the sprout grew stronger.\n\nThe old tree quickly fell apart and crumbled away.\nBut in its husk the new sprout was sheltered from the wind and the heavier rains.\n\nWhen the Druid returned to Oakhearth a year later, she visited Llirame who presented her with the budding sappling.\nThe Druid smiled and touched Llirame on the shoulder.\n\n\"Just as there is death\nthere is also life. As there is decay so there is growth. As there is rot, so\nthere is blossom,\"\n\nShe said to him.\nIn the years to come, the new tree became a dear friend to Llirame's children.\n\nIt gave fruit and sheltered many small animals.\n\nLlirame never forgot his old friend, but as it had been there for him, so he was there for the new tree.", ""),
