        StaticBook("Logs", "Sarrion", "\"A Sellsword Company\"\nLogs Book Chapter One\n-Sarrion\n\nCreated-\n2nd of the Grand Harvest\n1513\n-Sarrion\n\nJoined-\n4th of the Grand Harvest\n1513\nBjael Alrikson:SK=Lumber\n-Sarrion\nJoined-\n6th of The Grand Harvest\n1513\nCole deGray:SK=Farm/Mine\n-Sarrion\n\nJoined-\n7th of The Grand Harvest\n1513", ""),
        StaticBook("LOL", "Aeluin Tundrak", "Katrina's Research Notes\n\nCase File: Sylvia and affiliated affliction.\n\nNoteworthy traits: Development of a raspy voice, an inability to feel fear.  Significant increase in height (3ft+)\nObservation Log:\n\nLog #1: Within Haense, Sylvia and an man later confirmed to be of the Ascended were in an argument, the male insinuating that the guard commander had committed an unholy act. Sylvia showed a lack of remorse, at which point the ascended\nspoke about redemption. Whitney intervened before more could be found out on the matter.\n\nLog #2: I witnessed some gossip between some townsfolk and an official. When I inquired about Sylvia, they claimed Sylvia had absorbed the blood of a Wyvern, along\nwith the leader of Haense.\n\nya yeeet Lyulen was here.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lonely Fisherman", "Arthur Caulfield", "The Lonely\n         Fisherman\n\n   A short literary\n        Piece\n\"Now I don't know a whole lot about fishing,\" he confesses. \"For twenty long years been trying. They don't even notice when I cast my line into the water.\" \n    The fisherman sat alone on a boat, in the middle of a dark blue ocean that said nothing back.\n\"My bait must be cheap,\" he muttered. \"Must be me bait.\" His face scrunched up in thought. \n   His hair had started to grey, his wrinkles had become more defined. Each day it became harder to get out of bed, though he did not blame this on age.\nAfter a while the water began to ripple. Soon it gently rocked the side of his boat in waves. \n   Looking up the fisherman found another, just like him. He waved to the man in a friendly manner but was ignored.\n   Curious, the fisherman watched.\nThe man in the other boat threw his line in after a few minutes of preperation, and within seconds had caught a fish. \n   \"How unfair,\" the old man mumbled. \"Been fishing in these ponds for years and ain't caught a damn thing.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Looted Book", "Lyuathir Daemyr", "Book Looted By A Bandit. Original Owner Is Unknown\nPossessing an Armor.\n-------------------With enough determination souls can stay in this realm and exist as a ghost. Then they can possess a set of armor and live inside it, so to speak. If armor is destroyed the ghost can find another set.\nElixir of life\n-------------------Supposedly a very gifted alchemist could create an Elixir of Life, which is supposed to prevent the soul from leaving the body under any circumstances. This creates a problem of keeping you body young and functional.\nPanacea.\n-------------------A mythical product of alchemy, said to cure all illnesses and curses. It is possible that this 'Panacea' could even cure the infamous Iblees' curse on the descendants, therefore making humans live longer (or even forever)\nGravens.\n-------------------Apparently, if a mortal is slain before he/she could reach some important goal, it can return as 'Graven'. Gravens manifest themselves as semi-physical ghosts, aware and conscious. They can be harmed in any way a mortal can be.\nDarkstalkers.\n-------------------Supposedly raised by necromancers, these undeads are often seen wearing armor. They are agile, strong, and, most important, they can raise again after being defeated many times (countless, even?). Susceptible to holy magic\nDreadknight.\n-------------------A type of undead, a product of blood magic and runes, devoid of will and flesh. Dreadknight is created over the course of several months, filled with torture and horrible medical procedures. Bound by the will of creator.\nWraiths.\n-------------------One can become a Wraith through a complicated ritual involving a special artifact, bones of three mortals and a specific altar. Wraiths are inclined to killings.\nDruids.\n-------------------Druids found a way to prolong their lives. It is said they do so at some great expense and solely to serve the Aspects longer. (What are aspects? Need investigate) This ability is called 'Gift'.\nFountain of youth\n-------------------???\nPotion of Longevity\n-------------------A dwarven alchemist named Kilgrim has discovered a formulae for a longevity potion. Dorin Irongut knows the recipe.\nTreelord\n-------------------After studying druidism for an elven year one become a treelord. In this tirual you die and allow tree to absord your soul. Tree then grows a sturdy body which you can control like your own. Using this body can ne compared to\nTreelord part 2\n-------------------mind controlling a golem. Both body and tree live forever, but if tree is destroyed, your soul dies for good.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lord Report #2", "Luna Lyeis", "Viltarens body has been taken to a safe place, to await her ressurection and ensure she isn't zombiefied or taken by necromancers. She fell during battle against the elven individual described on the following page. Harven poured acid on her remains.\nElf, Snow white hair, green eyes. White robes with gold trim. This elf threaterned the city brazier, i arrived at the grove to find him attacking viltaren along with the aid of a girl named elle.\nI arrived on the scene to witness the battle, having blindly been on patrol i walked right into a field that seemingly froze all my armour in place. the same field that had Viltaren my officer trapped. This elf used scrolls to keep me at bay, while he\nstalked down upon his prey. Vilatren condemed his actions and those of the girl named Elle who was knocked out soon after i arrived.\nHarven tried his hardest to pull viltaren to safety with his magic\nBut it was not enough, as the elf stalked closer harevens roots stuck out against him, but it was too late, the elf placed a fire scroll upon Viltarens neck frying her before our eyes. A moment later and the elf was pulled apart by Harevens roots, so\nclose he was to saving her. Me on the other hand, all i could do was watch, once the scroll faded i charged across at the female known as elle who was beginning to wake up, out of anger i didn't stop to think or properly plan my attack, my sword thrust\nknicked her neck, but that was the extent of it, she scrambled to her feet and fled leaping off from the wall down into the lake.\nI have been tasked with reporting what i saw in this incident to the Lord protector, in the hopes that an arrest warrant for\nElle Noctuid. for her part in this affront to not just the guard force, but to all of Sutica. Furthermore the yet unknown individual elf is to be banished, his identiy needs to be found out but until then this report will be the basis for a sketch and\nwanted poster.\nThe state of Sutica is becoming increasingly worrysome, citzens condeming the actions of Guards and Clerics alike. when all we do is uphold the law and protect the people of sutica. Not everyone is innocent, the people need to know that we\nare here to protect them, and that they shouldn't intervene when we try to do our jobs. Especially when it involves a banished individual.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lord's Report #1", "Luna Lyeis", "Beware, Raiders attacking those travelling on Sutican Roads.\nTwo residents were ambushed on their way to the Ceru docks by a group of Frostbeard Dwarves from Kaz'ulrah.\nDormin and Dural Doomforge newly settled landowners\nand residents of Sutica were attacked first hand. CLock tower District House 2. is there place of residence. I will hand this report to the Lord Protector Personally for him to investigate.\nFurther more the refugee Juldra arrived today. She speaks of a disaster befalling Tahn that was heard even here at the gatehouse of Sutica. I am guessing that is what the distant far off noise was, although in truth i ahd thought it was another dwarf\nsneezing in the market square. If somthing can cause such damage and be heard that far away, the lord protector needs to look into it immediately for the safety of all Suticans.\nBoth Incidents in this report are detailed in my most recent guard report #13. This Report is to be handed directly to the Lord Protector himself to make him appraised of these troubling incidents.\nP.S. The new recruit proved more than capable of handling gate house duty, and he has been suited up in proper Sutican guard armour and attire for future partols and shifts. Progress promising thus far.", ""),
        StaticBook("Losing a Hand", "Henry Winterleaf", "The following is the story of an injury that I have lived with for a long time and how it happened in the first place.\nIt all started back in Asulon as I was leaving the cloud temple one day. I had just left the borders of the temple lands where I stumbled across a band of pirates attempting to rob two young girls.\nTheir leader, a dark elf man, told me not\nto get involved or else. However, I stepped in anyway, hoping to see off these pirates. I found myself completely outmatched against these four pirates on my own. I managed to distract them enough for the girls to escape but I was\nseverly wounded in the fight. I had lost part of my left arm from just below the elbow down. I was unable to retrieve the cut-off piece so I was unable to heal it back together at the temple, as I have been told is possible. So, for many years I made\ndo the best I could.\nI wore a metal hand for many years as a replacement.\n\nHowever, recently I met an alchemist named Beros who made a potion that would regrow my arm. I have been using the potion for a while and it seems to be working.\nIt feels weird to me that, for the first time in years, I will have two working hands again.\n\nThe process is long and expensive but for me it says a lot about the powers of alchemy. So, if there's one lesson you take away from this book, make it this...\nDon't fuck with alchemists.\n\nOr pirates.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Legends v.1", "Gork'Raguk", "The Legend\n          of\n     Pow'r Garmar\n    ▬▬ι═══════ﺤ\n   by: Gork Raguk\n\n*The pages seem tattered, as if warped by some great amount of power*\n\n*You shutter for a moment before turning the page*\nOnce upon a time, there was a very powerful Orc named Pow'r Garmar. All the other Orcs hated him\nbecause he was the coolest guy around, and power emanated from his cosmic eyes like radiation.\n   Men wanted to be him, and women wanted to be him -- well,\nuhh... er [page break]\n   HE WAS A REALLY COOL GUY, ALRIGHT? You get the picture. We'll start with when he was born.\n\n    Chapter One:\n A Humble Upbringing\n   -------------\nPow'r Garmar shook the universe back into place, slayed five billion ice dragons, beat Rainbow Road on master difficulty and destroyed communism -- and then he was born.\n   On that pleasant day, birds sang and women swooned for the impending doom of\nthe world.\n   Don't let the humility fool you though. Pow'r Garmar survived nuclear fallout at birth, practically ripping his mom apart while getting out of the womb.\n   His arms are like two thick sausages that jut flaccidly out of his body; they're\nlike chiseled treetrunks, stretching 69 fathoms in length. By contrast, his legs are like towers, supporting a grossly overadequate frame (it should be added that Garmar never skips leg day).\nLegend has it that when he was a kid, all the admins got together and tried to kill him; they feared his power and were basically mad because they're bad. They called him a hacker and complained about him to the local moderator.\nGarmar, being the reasonable man he is, answered back, \"GIkini Gikiniki Gucci Gang Gucci Gang Gucci Gang Gucci Gang.\"\n   ... Alas, it seems that all the reason in the world (which Pow'r Garmar had) could not persuade the admins to see his side.\nWhen Garmar heard this heresy from his post-natal ears, he gained spontaneous flight and time travel and rushed at them full speed. The admins, with all of their forces combined, managed to stop him temporarily for a nanosecond. \"Power-gaming!\nPower-gaming,\" the admins yelled. It was growing louder and more vociferous by the minute, so Pow'r Garmar had no choice but to mute them in chat.\n   The moderator protested loudly, asking him how he attained this supreme,\nmanly, completely-deserved power. Pow'r Garmar then replied with such eloquence that he made Shakespeare look like a two-bit punk. \"Gucci Gang Gucci Gang Gucci Gang Gucci Gang.\"\nSuch beautiful words are rarely uttered throughout the course of history. The moderator began sobbing like a little girl, cowering under his Pacman bedsheets.\n   At which point, he asked, \"How?\"\n\"How did you attain such majestic displays of wisdom and power?\" Garmar replied, \"I was touched by a deathknight when I was born.\"\n   The moderator answered, \"I don't understand how rape made you so powerful. Where could you possibly absorb the power thr-\nough?\"\n   It was no use though. After that, Garmar banned the moderator.\n\n     The End.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Parchment", "Unknown", "*a single sentance seems to be repeated throughout a single big parchment many times. It seems to have always about the same caligraphy.*\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\n\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\n\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.Order of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.\n\nOrder of Youth, may Ademir Wilkins bring long human life with the water of the fountain.", ""),
        StaticBook("Love", "Joil Diagak", "War is often associated with several different words.\nDeath. Destruction. And another that is often forgotten. One that is ignored in times of aggresion. One that is abolished in moments of seriousness. What is that word? What could it be?\nIt must be something serious. It must be something so outrageous that it destroys the will of anyone who dare challenge another. However it is not. It is the single most important part of life. It connects all of us together. It binds the spirit of all\nspecies together. It connects everything on a whole new level, and represents a deep meaning of life. The death of loved ones is acknowledged, but not enough to stop war.\nThe destruction of cities and towns is acknowledged, but still cannot stop it.\nOne thing can stop it. But it is not strong enough. It has not reached it's full potential. It's a shame.", ""),
        StaticBook("Love Letter", "Kayla the Outspoken", "((A letter written on a simple piece of paper, neatly folded in grass. The paper had a pleasant scent of vanilla extract and freshly-cut grass.))\nWhen the nightingale sings\nThe woods grow green,\nLeaf and geass and blossom spring\nIn April, I believe.\nAnd love is to my heart gone\nWith a spear so keen,\nNight and day my blood it drinks\nMy heart causes me pain.\nI loved thee all this year\nSuch that I may love no more;\nI have sighed many sighs, \nFrederick, for thy pity.\nTo me love is never nearer,\nAnd that I sorely regret.\nSweet Frederick, think of me-\nI have loved thee long.\n\nSweet Frederick, I pray thee\nGiveth me one love speech.\nWhile I live in the world so wide\nNone other will I seek!\nWith thy love, my beloved, \nMy bliss you might decrease;\nA sweet kiss from thy mout would be my cure.\n\nSweet Frederick, I pray thee\nFor a gift of love.\nIf thee love me, as they say,\nAnd Frederick, as I believe,\nIf it be thy will\nMake it be seen!\nSo much I think of thee\nThat I grow green\n\nSweet Frederick, I pray thee,\nLove me a little while!\nI will sing my song\nTo the one to whom it belongs.\n\n((A rough sketch of Frederick is drawn here. Letter remains unsigned.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Love Story", "Rollo Applefoot", "Once upon a time there was a lady! \n\nThis lady was pretty lonely but then she met a nice guy!\n\nThe nice guy gave her flowers! And made the lady feel loved!\n\nThe two wished to have\neachother, more and more\nBut then he was thrown out of the village and the woman was left to be sad forever. As she never got anywhere close to that type of happiness again and spent her entire life sad and sobbing that her one and true love was dead. \nTHE END", ""),
        StaticBook("Lucicity", "Garoll Earl", "Our known states of life are awawake, concious and asleep. Right? What if I was to tell you that there was an entire new universe that your mind can explore. I understand that this might be quite a hard concept, the facts being quite complicated. However,\nI am here to explain the state of Lucicity.\nWe have all had dreams, forces sub-concious lifes... Yet- We only have them asleep. Imagine being able to tap into and live in that world, while sitting around doing nothing... I am going to call this place the\ndream-world. Through vast meditation and training, you can infact push yourself into this 'new world', one which is built to your desire. It is important to note that this is all mental, not real, however it could be used for the gaining of intelect.\nIn this world, anything and everything is possible if you put your mind to it, however you cannot just make up random things. Your mind can only stretch itself so far, you see... You are the most powerful being in your own pocket-world.\nOwn a castle, destroy islands in a flick of the tounge, create anything with a mere thought. You see... Unlike normal dreams, You have utter control of what goes on in your 'world'. Though, time is quite a strange thing in there... You can never really\ntell what the time is from the outside without poking out of your dream to see it. There is no physical benefit, to this. It can be considered a toy. Pain cannot be felt. This is by-no-means a new form of magic, infact a state of living. This could count\nas an ability due to the fact that you have to train to get fluent in it, like all meditation, it starts off near impossible. I have used this pocket multiple times. Training myself, though I gained no physical skill, I gained ideas which I could use\nin reality... In my world I was a warrior fighting at one point, the one I was against being sub-concious, everything I did, it seemed that the other knew how to stop. So I kept trying until I learnt new  possibilities. The provided example is merely one\nof infinate possibilities of what this can do to you. I am not going to go into the mental-impacts of meditation, but I can simply say that it is very much helpful... The implications of this... I shudder at the thought. You can do this on command,\nwhenever you decide to meditate, so you can always go back into your pocket world. However- Your physical body would still be here- You do not transport your body to the world, only your conciousness moves. Disclaimer: I would not advise doing this\nin public, someone might casually kill you while you are meditating, which I highly doubt you would want... But that's your call, as the meditator.\nIncase you cannot be bothered to read it all:\nYou can put yourself into a spirit world where you control everything. You do this through meditation. Your body doesn't move, conciousness does. If you wish any more information. Contact Garoll Earl.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lumi'ere", "Almisael", "La Grace et lumiere du createur, converont le ciel bleu quand les trois esprits primordiaux chanteron la chansson d'unisson.\nLa lumiere absolute du seigneur couvera le monde et purifia seux dont le coeur contient la malice.\nLa lumiere divine ne peut seuelement se trouver dans les plus absolut tenebres.", ""),
        StaticBook("Luna's Trials", "Luna Lyeis", "Clerical trials\nInteresting things, not quite what i thought although im not entirely sure what i thought they would be. I also imagine it differs from teacher to teacher, but at the very least the sutican order of clerics requires the completion of\natleast five trials before the inital connection ceremony.\nThey aren't as much about learning as i had thought, they were more a way to prove ones self, and to learn the foundation of clericalism and the religion we all pledge ourselves to.\nMy trials were mostly about my teacher getting to know me, and learning what i was made of and capable of. My first trial involved me thinking of an item that represented who i was as a person, my inital thought was shoved aside much to my own\nannoyance, but after cooling off a bit and really thinking of it i thought of the locket my husband had made and gifted to me, a heart shape with the three aspects of my being engraved on its face, even as i write this now it hangs around my neck\nnestled safely in my bossom. So i had found the perfect item that showed who i was, well along with the sotry behind each aspect anyway. The hard part was deciding if i should give it up or not. Well it wasn't that hard i would never get it up its bound\nto who and what i am. Its part of me just as the ceremonial scar that has graced my face since my acceptance as a female warrior amongst my own people. But thats a story for another time.\nSo i decided to make a wooden copy of my amulet it took quite some time, and some failed attempts but i got it in the end, and my teacher Gray accepted it along with the story behind each of the three aspects upon it. Woman, Warrior and Wolf.\nHaving completed my first trial it was onto the second, I was to learn some things about out patron the angeul of light, but first i was to write what purity meant to me as a person, as an individual knowing little of our lords true definition.\nThis took me a rather long amount of time, in truth if it hadn't been for my newborn son waking up while i was working i don't think i would of ever had a true answer, i had several drafts but none were right, i was writeing what i thought my teacher\nwanted to hear, not what i felt. What i felt.. was that love is purity, and that we should do all we can to protect it, and those we love. As well as the innocene many alive today have lost simply through the struggles of life. That i also consider pure\nThe look of my sons young face, so full of hope, curiosity and innocene, a look no man, woman elf or dwarf that lives today posses in such a pure form Its sad that many are robbed of it so early in the never ending wars and troubles\nthat corrupt and plague our lands but it is the way of the world and part of our mission as clerics to change this, so that the world may be pure once and fore all that it may bask in the light of tahariae.\nMy third trial was more in line with what i expected if im honest, i was to learn the teaching of Tahariae, what was light, what was gray and what was dark simple enough task, and using common sense its quite easy to come to the conclusion of the correct\nanswer to this. This being the case this was only part of my trial, i was to put what i learnt into practise by aiding a number of people, either through protecting the innocent, healing the injured or guiding the lost. In a peaceful world this may of\nbeen a long and tiresome task, but in reality it was a number of days before i finished it. Such is the dark times we live in, that many a souls wander this world lost to themselves and others. Dark forces strike out at the innocent seeking to corrupt or\nslay. And with such those that are lucky enough to survive a day of life often requires healing and aid, be it of the mind, soul or body.\nMy third trial completed I took a small break as it were to return to some of my duties around the city.\nI got to partake as a spectator to a pure display of our lords power, channeled through two of his more senior clerics as they fought of a number of dark beings, and a monster that i can only describe as a serpent of the sea, much akin to that which\nstandds vigil on the crest of Sutica itself. One might read into that as a bad omen, that the monster struck out at us but i see it as a test that suticans, and clerics of Tahariae passed through almost unscaved.\nAdmitedly i would of liked to do more in this entire situation, but the fact remained i was still only a guard by the standards of the powerful creatures and beings involved in this. The best i could do was distract the sea serpent long enough for our\nmy Teacher and the lord protector of Sutica to dispatch the dark beings and turn their attentions to the monster. I was at the least a use in being a distraction if only for the few moments needed to ensure our victory.\nA day or so after this i returned to my teacher gray, and so begun my fourth trial in retrospec i find it a most amusing way to teach injuring ones self and telling them to fix it. I'm just glad my teacher didn't do anything real serious\nwe talked over equipment any cleric may need in their travels, items to protect oneself and others. Medicines and bandages to offer aid to your allies and the innocent, and of course provisions such as water and food, along with anything else i could\nthink of, such as oiled rags, Chalk, Fire starting kit, spare leather, an apple. so on so forth.\nMoving on after we went over each item i presented he proceeded to run his own dagger down his forearm cutting a deep and long gash that proceeded\nto bleed seemingly endlessly, it was my task to heal it before he passed out from blood loss. A interesting task although i was up to it, any good soldier should know the basics of first aid, be quick, be effective.\nAfter rendering aid through the use of the various items in my kit i had passed my fourth trial and proven i could work under some amount of pressure and shown atleast a basic understanding of proper medical aid.\nThen came my final trial, it was one of the things i least expected, for my own teacher to turn on me and force me into a fight for my life. Although i still reason that he wouldn't of tried to kill me if it came to it, as im almost certain that would of\nbeen agaisnt the teachings of tahariae although his taunting and threats as we traded blows atop the sands only strengtherned my resolve, my desire to surive... even win. My task was to either down him, defeat him, making him bleed\nor break his focus on maintaining a floating orb of light, in truth im not sure which one i did, broke his concentration, defeated him or downed him, well i did get him on the ground and into an arm lock.\nWith this i had passed my fith and final trial.\nI had proven my worth, shown that I would stand, and not accept defeat in the face of a surperior enemy, that i would fight on until victory or my last breath. Lets just say you would of had to of been their to fully understand what i meant. I was rather\nhoplessly outmatched, he was bigger, stronger, better equiped and is a venteran cleric and warrior. While i'd say i am much faster and agile than he, that helped me little in the rather confined space causing his blows to land heavily on me often.\nregardless i had passed and it was time for the true final test. To be judged by the light and connected to the lord of Purity Tahariae. Atop the tower of the Temple of Sutican Clericism i was baptised a watery pool of light where i was accepted into the\nfold as a cleric of Tahariae. A sister of the order joining my brothers and sister in the light from now until the time of my death.\n\n These were my trials and my story. But this is also just the beginning, the end of the first chapter.\nThe path I walk now, each step a new page a new challenge for the real trials lay yet ahead.", ""),
        StaticBook("Madeleine", "Hobbs_Burrows", "Madeleine\n\nBy Hobbs Burrows\nI have often been told,\nOf a she-Halfling so bold,\nWho takes up a shovel,\nAnd after a tussle,\nWill soon have you bent over double!\n\nNow this lass says 'Harold,\nI know you're a cabbage,\nBut the truth is not savage,\nAnd though you have baggage,\nTo me you're the perfect package!'\n\nDunshire is lucky to have her, \nThat we all know and agree,\nAnd if you do doubt listen to me,\nWithout drink or cheer,\nYour charm crystal clear,\nWhat a sad world it would be!", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic dictionary", "Archrim Elmoran", "Magic dictionary:\n\nYir'sari- True wizard\nMasters of magic\nAcended- Demi god\nchildren of the aenguls\nundead- the evil\nfist of Iblees, they destroyed aegis\nArcane tranportation pad-\nstaff- a tool\nused to conduct mana and help with your connection to the void\nWand- akin to the staff but smaller and doesnt work as well\nCleric- mages who devote themselves to the learning and use of healing magic and are fueled by aenguls\nNecromancer- a user of necromancy which is a form of magic devoted to reanimation and the thievery of life\npyromancer- a mage who uses magic that has to do with fire and or smoke.\nelectromancer- a mage who is devoted to the use of electrical magic\nEvocation- the summoning of elements from the void\nfire evocation- the summoning of fire from the void\nwater evocation- the summoning of water and water realated things from the void\nElectric Evocation- the summoning of electricity from the void\nwind evocation- the summoning of wind or air fomr the void\nEarth evocation- the use of mana to summon earthen elements\nShamanism- A form of magic that requires the use of spirits\nmagic(k)- the use of mana and a connection to the void to achive great feats that can not normaly be done\nmana- the life force and energies around us and is used to form spells of any kind\nShade magic- A form a magic that is devoted to the use of shadows and or darkness\nIllusion magic- a branch of magic that is able to produce false images and feelings and project them on others\nconjuration- the summoning of living creatures\nWizard- common name for Yir'sari\nArchmage- ruler of the mages guild\nmage- one who learns and uses magic\nmagician- another name for mages and or Wizards\nAcended magic-  magic fueled by a patron aengul and is considerd holy, and akin to clerics\nundead magic- the reanimation and use of corpses, in short it is necromancy\nThe void- a earthreal place that mages call upon to help fuel their spells\nDragon- a very large and very inteligent creature who mainly roam the north, while hunting\nyello stone (endstone)- a strange stone that seems to spread corruption of different kinds\nDruidism- a form of magic that uses nature, and spirits know as the aspects\nakin to shamanism\nAlteration- a form of magic that is used to alter real world things", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic Dictionary", "Edmin Kerith", "Magic Dictionary:\n\nYir'Sari- True Wizard, Powerfull magic masters\n\nAscended - The Demi-god children of the aenguls.\n\nUndead - The Evil fists of Ibless, they destroyed Aegis.\nArcane Transportation Pad \n\nStaff- a tool used to conduct mana as well as aid you in Void Connections\n\nWand- Akin to the Staff, Doesnt Work as well.\n\nCleric - Powerfull Magicians Based mostly in healing, they are fueled by anguls\nNecromancer - Users of Necromany, a deadly magic having to do with life drain.\n\nPyromancer - Fire evocationist, magician of fire. \n\nElecromancer - User of electric magic, mostly evocationist of electricity, they are common in Anthos.\nEvocation - The use of summon elements from the Void\n\nFire-Evocation- The Summoning of mana from the Void to create fire.\n\nWater Evocation- The summoning of mana from the Void to create water or other water related things.\nElectric Evocation - The evoking of mana from the Void to form electricity \n\nWind evocation - The Use of Void mana to create wind and it's similiar elements.\n\nEarth Evocation - The evocation of mana to form earthen elements.\nElemental control - A shaman magic having to do with spirits.\n\nMagic(k) - The use of mana to conjure things, and even to control things.\n\nMana- Life force and energies around us, used to form complex spells.\nNecromancy - The Use of life drain to get mana to form complex \n\nSpells:\n\nShade Magic - Fueled by a gem, it's shadow maguc having to do with the art of tendrils and other shadow elements.\nIllusion - A arcane magic, the use of mana to form false images and feelings and project them upon others, it's impossible to illusion yourself.\n\nConjurations - the conjuring of living beings. \nWizard - common term name of the Yir'sari true Wizards.\nArch Mage - Ruler of  the mage's guild.\n\nMage - Practicer of magic \n\nMagician - Mage is it shortened.\n\nAscended Magic - Magic fueled by a patron aenguel, it is a light magic and holy it is akin to cleric\nUndead magic - Fueled by iblees, the Undeas used their necromancy to begin their conquest of Aegis.\n\nThe Void - A place where mages draw power from to fuel their spells\n\nDragon- A beast of Huge size and intelligence they roam Northern Anthos hunting.\nYellow Stone Material ((Endtone)) - A Heavily weird material, it spread corruption of many kinds.\n\nDruidisme - Magic over nature, has to do with spirits knowsn as the Aspects.\n\nAlteration- Magic that alters the properties of real world things.\nMagic Sayings\n\"Magic seeks those who don't seek it\"\n\n\"Magic is the path of the scholar, not a insolent warrior of heavy brains and no mindset\"\n\n\"magic is the path of destruction, insolent mage\" - Gavin the Druid\n\" Good and Evil doesn't decide how magic works, only the acts of the user\" - The Arcane Mage\n\nWritten by, Mythras Ardere.\n\nSources\n-History of Magic\n-the Clerical Order\n-The Mage\"s Guild\n-Salamandr's Spirit\n-Many assorted books on magic, and knowledge from other mages.\n\nCopied by Edmin Kerith", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic License", "Auberon de Clare", "As by the Codex Arcana, and the Magic License Clause, this document licenses Ceruberr Asul’Ailer to the practice of Arcanism, Arcane Shielding, Electromancy, Telekinesis and Transfiguration.\n[!] The scroll bears a scribbled\nsignature, along with a seal, in shape of a Lorraine Cross, stamped into burgundy coloured wax. [!]\n\n-Knight Inquisitor Auberon de Clare\n\n#0017", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic License", "Ser John the Maering", "This licensure is to prove that Sophia of Curon has paid all dues necessary to hold this license.\n\nIn her interview, she showed a strong urge to assist those in Haense. As such, this magic grants her access to any magic legally allowed to be\npracticed in Haense and all its territories.\n\nSigned,\nSer John Wick,\nHigh Mage of the Department of Magic", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic License", "Ser John the Handsome", "This license states that the holder, Robyn Vulnear, has paid all dues and has a clear intent to assist the Kingdom of Haense with her magical talents. She is authorized to carry out any magics within the city of Markev and the other territories of Haense.\nHer service to the college (as well as her skill with previous magics) allows her to hold this governmental license.\n\nSigned,\nSer John, Head of the Department of Magic\n\n28th of Snow's Maiden, 1650", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic Notes I", "Vaeria Ossaura", "Sal' told me there are many types of 'Voidal' Magics, those being- Alteration, Arcanism, Evocation, Illusion, Mental and Conjuration.\n\nShe knows Arcanism (both disciplines) and has mastered it. This must mean she knows Arcane Shielding and Arcane-\n'Blasting'. She also knows Eletrical Evocation and Mental Magic- she's obviously very well versed with magic to know all about this kind of stuff. I'll ask her to teach me how to 'connect' to the Void, if I really suck at it.\nThe correct term isn't Arcane 'Blasting'- it's Arcane Evocation. She evokes raw Arcane energy, and uses it against people (in the form of missiles and such).\n\nMaybe magic is why her face is faint scared. I feel faintly bad for her.\nBasic concept of Elemental Evocation- The user draws energy from the Void, 'forming' the voidal energies into an element. They then use that element in certain ways.\n\nAparantly this is a small summary of Elemental Evocation.\nBasic concept of Arcane Evocation- The user draws energy from the void, but they do not form the energy into an element. Instead, they keep it in the raw form, evoking it in certain ways.\nArcane Evocation is much harder then Elemental Evocation (due to the raw power it possesses) but is seemingly not much more powerful. \n\nThis is confusing to me- shouldn't the raw form be more powerful then the 'crafted' form?\nThe reasoning behind this- in Sal's own words- is that; 'it's not as destructive as fire or lighting, nor as sturdy as earth, nor as quick as air'. It's 'flexible'.\n\nArcane Evocation is considered the 'jack-of-all-trades'.\nIt's okay at everything, master-\nat none. Arcane Evocation is Elemental Evocation but without the elemental properties- it adapts to the whims of the caster. In my opinion, this seems so much better. \n\nAnd like always- I am wrong. Elemental Evocation isn't as wild as I thought.\nIt seems dependable, much more then I first thought. Fire and Eletrical Evocation can actually start fires!", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic Trick", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Search for a mage who may be willing to share their knowledge with the warhawkes.", ""),
        StaticBook("Malin I", "Malin", "To be a good king is to command the hearts and minds of your people. \n\nThis is to say, to be a good king is for them to believe in you with both their emotion, and their faculty of reason. These are the two things which compose any person, and so by\nbeing able to command them, you have total control over your people. \n\nIn essence, they become an extension of your body, so that you may do with them whatever you would like -- realistically, you will act to promote their happiness and freedom, but there\nare innumerable despots who are just as effective monarchs, without having a citizenry which is well-off. This is often due to the case of their nation being in a locale where mass, low-skilled labor is effective at generating wealth, and so have no need\nfor an educated, healthy, and happy populace.\n\nIn order to dominate the emotions of a people, you must play to them. Be joyful when they are happy, and weep when they cry. It is important to generally emote slightly stronger than  the average citizen,\nso that you seem deeply affected by the hardships of your people. Even should you feel nothing, you most learn to put up a facade. Eventually, this becomes very natural.\n\nFurthermore, be strong in your resolve. Your people will turn to you for\nsupport when they are, themselves, fraught with worry. This is one of the few cases where you should not emote with them, and instead support them. A courageous, kind, wise king is an image you must present at all times.\nTo control the reason of a people is more challenging. This generally involves making policy choices and administrative decisions which are in line with their morality and personal wellbeing. It is important to organize your educational and religious\nsystems in order to ensure indoctrination to a philosophy that corresponds with what you would like to invoke through policy in the future.", ""),
        StaticBook("Malin II", "Malin", "I will list hereafter some of the fundamentals of economics, first put to paper by the likes of Mankiw and Iylhier, which describe governance of commerce. \n\nTending the economy of a nation is very much like tending a flower. During the\nsummer, it must be given water so as to avoid it perishing of thirst, and in winter, it must be sheltered, to prevent it succumbing to frost. This is to say: economic policy is dictated by the environment that surrounds your nation. During a time of\nforeign military pressure, it is wise to back your own military-industrial complex to provide security, and during peace, it is wise to back the sciences and craftsmen to ensure a productive society.\n\nMoving on, to begin our discussion, I will list\nthose aforementioned fundamentals:\n\nFundamental 1: Rational people act on the margin\nA citizen will make small changes readily in order to achieve maximum benefit from an event. By 'small changes', this refers to any change where the act of changing\nitself, and performing cost/benefit analysis with regards to the change, has negligible cost. Comparison of marginal benefits and marginal cost will be able to help you in making the decision.\n\nFundamental 2: Benefits prompt change\nThe behavior of\nindividual citizens, or even guilds, changes according to the environment that they are in. For example, a period of drought promotes investment in water supplies. \n\nFundamental 3: Both parties can benefit from trade\nFor resources or manufactured\ngoods which are unique to individual citizens, guilds, or nations, trading with others provides access to resources and manufactured goods it is otherwise impossible to obtain. This is likewise true with the trading partner. \nFundamental 4: Economies function best when citizens are relatively autonomous\nThe centralization of the market, though on the surface seemingly beneficial, quickly reveals its downsides: the judgement of the individual planner, or the small planning\ncommittee, is far poorer than the judgement of thousands of homes and guilds. Maintaining the people's freedom to sell and buy goods and services is overall of benefit.  \n\nFundmental 5: Government is necessary to maintain market\noutcomes\nIn particular scenarios, usually during the development of monopolies, it is necessary, for the good of the people, to intervene. The promotion of competition is necessary to prevent a single guild from growing so powerful\nthat it can harm the citizenry, or the nation as a whole. The dominion of the state must be protected, or the people will lose faith in its ability to govern.\n\nFundamental 6: The wellbeing of people is dependent on their nation's economic\nproductivity\nIn a nation where more goods and services are produced, the standard of living is generally higher, barring unique situations. \n\nThere are additional fundamentals, but these are some of the most important. I will list them in my next\ndiscussion on commerce.", ""),
        StaticBook("Malin III", "Malin", "Justice participates the interactions between individuals in order to force them to obey the law. Unfortunately, we are animals, wild and uncontrolled even in developed society. We need force to keep us in line, because without the strong arm of\njustice, our world will be burnt down in chaos. Were the entire realm under Krug's domain, I have no doubt we'd be ashes within a week. \n\nThere is a thin line between order and madness, and the law is intended to enforce this line, to build a wall atop\nit, so our society won't fall apart.\n\nImagine the world without order, when anyone can do anything. All the psychological boundaries created in our minds, during childhood, are blurred out. Fear is the only means of control. When there are no\npunishments for the crimes that used to be violations of the law, the world falls apart, and all cultural and technology progress backslides into nothing.\n\nIn this part, it would be best to mention the most powerful instrument of justice that we have used\nsince ancient times: capital punishment. People can be burned, drowned, boiled, stabbed, and beaten to death for disobedience, though, for most cases, simple beheading is ideal, as it provides a largely painless death. It is only for more severe cases\n(e.g. treason, defilement) that more egregious means of execution are permitted.", ""),
        StaticBook("Malin IV", "Malin", "The stewardship of nature, and natural resources in general, is vital to the long-term survival of a nation. \n\nThis is quite obvious to anyone with even a basic understanding of industry and the environment. It is not required that you\nbecome a druid to understand this simple truth. The sources of our food, building materials, and other goods are limited, and take time to be replenished. If we exhaust them too quickly, we run the risk of running out of them entirely. If we are reliant\non them by the time we exhaust them, the people suffer greatly, and chance of rebellion increases.\n\nI should note here that this does not apply solely to material things. Beauty, for example, is a resource we often do not consider. For some of my\nbrothers, it is readily discarded, and for others, their lives are too short to appreciate its change. However, elves are uniquely able to appreciate increases and decreases in beauty. The redevelopment of a forest into farmland may bring displeasure to\nsome, as an offense to the senses. \n\nTherefore, you can adopt two strategies that will allow you to grow your nation, despite these issues.\n\nFirstly, promote the development of sustainable practices. Guilds and citizens which are able to\nfunction in perpetuity are ideal, as they will never succumb to the absence of resources.\n\nSecondly, harvest, but do not become reliant on, exhaustible resources. You can contract citizens of another nation to harvest these resources, and then\nsell them back to that nation, allowing you to profit, while simultaneously driving other nations' reliance on resources which will ultimately run out -- simply as an example.", ""),
        StaticBook("Malin V", "Malin", "War is an unfortunate reality. In my time as king, I have been forced to learn much about it. Here, I include some of the writings of the Sun Druid Uz'Tuylei, who, despite being a pacifist, has an understanding of war even I rely on. Particularly, this\nconcerns his laying of plans.\n\n\"War is the ultimate test for the state, and can either grant it greatness, or destroy it. There are five factors which govern it: justice, logistics, location, leadership, and strategy.\nA war must be just in the eyes of the soldiers to maximize their compliance, so that they will follow orders.\n\nLogistics pertains to the ability to supply an army with the resources needed for its proper function.\n\nLocation concerns\nthe theatre of the war, and the particular terrains in which battle will take place. This also involves the timing of those battles.\n\nThat the leadership of an army is strong is vital for its function: he must be wise and clever, but also strict and\ndutiful.\n\nFinally, there is strategy, which involves how an army is marshalled, and how it is structured with regards to rank.\n\nTo determine which of two armies will win a conflict, you need only determine which is superior with\nregards to these factors. Which of the two sides fights justly? Which has a well-supplied army? Which has the positional advantage? Which has a more-seasoned, better-projecting leader? Which has superior organization?\"\nI will go into more depth on this topic in our later lessons. \n\nNote: My king, though your motives are true, this conduct is simply inappropriate for the Order, regardless of who you teach. The other archdruids agree with me on this matter. We will\nspeak at a later time concerning what to do in the future. For now, these lessons are discontinued.\n\n-AV", ""),
        StaticBook("Malog's Parables", "Clanfather Malog'Yar", "The Gahk Scoffers\n In a bub’hosh klomp, an uruk urged gahk others to help him charge the enemy, which outnumbered them severely agh were prevailing against their goi. The gahk laugh agh blah’d, “Lat am a glob. We will nub help lat.” Agh they threw stones\nagh rotten grub at him as he charged alone to assist the rest of the brothers in defending their goi. In the end, da goi beat the attackers with the help of the brave uruk who tipped the balance just in their favor. Soon after, he became Rex. How bub’hosh\nwas his wrath against the gahk mocked him before!\n\nThe Scatternak\n A scatternak in the desert was trapped under a boulder and pled to a pair of passing jabbernaks for help. The older of the dub blah’d, “Nub!”\n “Why?!” asked the scatternak.\n“Because,” he blah’d, “lat am a scatternak. Lat will sting us.”\n “Mi would never sting ash who helps mi in mi hour of need!”\n The jabbernaks reasoned among themselves, agh decided to help the scatternak. They pushed agh pushed, until the boulder rolled\noff of him. Then, as soon as he was free, the scatternak stung both of the jabbernaks. With his final gasps, the elder jabbernak asks, “Why?!”\n “Because,” he blah’d, “mi am a scatternak.”\n\nThe Dub Boars\nIn the wilderness, dub boars argued about who was\nthe hoshest. As they bickered, a passing hunter crept up on them unawares, agh shattered both of their skulls.\n\nThe Proud Tree\n A bub’hosh tree towered above the whole forest. It spent its days gazing at the sky, agh blahing of its own bub’hoshness.\nSoon, all the mighty beasts of the forest grew tired of its arrogance agh incessant bragging. So obsessed with itself was the bub’hosh tree, however, that it did nub notice its protectors agh companions had abandoned it. With none to guard it, axemen\ncame agh chopped it down.\n\nThe Fearful Goat\n A young goat was so frightened by all other creatures that he did nub gruk where to find relief. He fled in panic at the approach of any living thing, nub aware of the power of his own horns. Eventually, he\nfled his blarg in the mountains for fear of harpies. In the forests below, he feared the bears, so he ran to the plains, only to be frightened off by the wild howlers. Yet further away, in the savannas,  the lions were too fiersome for him. Before long,\nhe found himself in the desert, where he fled into a cave at the sight of the jabbernaks. As he scurried desperately into the cave, however, the opening snapped shut on his spine, proving rather to be the mouth of a bub’hosh skhelll tortoise.\n\nThe Man In The Well\n A man lived at the bottom of an empty well, agh boasted his knowledge of the world. He ignored all who corrected him. Ash day, a bub’hosh storm came, agh he drowned.\n\nThe Bub'hosh Powers\n Ash day, the bub'hosh powers contended over\nwho was bub’hoshest.\n “Mi am bub’hoshest!” blahed the earthquake, agh he shattered the earth.\n “Nub! It is mi!” Roared the tidal wave, as he flooded the lands.\n “All of latz are wrong!” shouted the volcano, agh he erupted with smoke agh fire.\n“Globs!” hissed the tornado agh his sister, the hurricane, as they devastated whole gois.\n Finally, after raining destruction from above, the lightning suggested they ask the people to pronounce ash of them the bub’hoshest. When they sought after\nsomebody to settle their dispute, however, they found there were none left alive to ask.\n\n The Parables of Malog, Clanfather of the Yars.", ""),
        StaticBook("Malog's Proverbs", "Malog'Yar", "*As you open the book, you see in its pages a collection of proverbs written by the shaman, Malog'Yar. Each one is individually numbered for ease of memorization, it seems. They don't appear to have a particular order to them, but must\nhave been written as they came to the shaman's mind.\n((As in my other books, only those words which are actually different in the Blah are written in said language. The rest are in Common for ease of reading.))\n1. The lust for power is the beginning of shame. It concieves, agh brings forth arrogance. Arrogance, when it reaches maturity, brings forth humiliation.\n2. The path to honor is paved with sacrifice.\n3. Gold is a heavy thing, agh bub'hosh is the burden of he who hoards it. It will crush the heart, agh bring low the spirit.\n4.He who forgets his ancestors of the past will have nub future for his descendents.\n5.Food, water,\nshelter, praise; these things are wasted, when given to ash with nub honor.\n6.All is vanity for the whitewash, for he has abandoned his ancestors. He has departed from his purpose in life.\n7.Find that skill which lat are hosh\nat. Do it with honor, for even the lowly chicken farmer can glorify Krug.\n8.Do nub scorn simplicity. It is a chest of many treasures.\n9.Hosher is a small blarg with a mate agh cubs, than an empty palace.\n10.Integrity,\nuprightness, honor, discipline agh wisdom are the bones of the spirit. Without these, lat can nub stand.\n11.Hosher to be a blind man with wisdom, than a fool with many eyes.\n12.Luxury is an open gate to complacency.\n13.Complacency is a downhill path to the flatting of the spirit. It is an easy path to descend, but returning uphill is strenuous, requiring diligence.\n14.Bring up lats cubs in the way of honor, for they will take lats place in the future.\n15.This year's swineherd may be next year's Rex.\n16.Remember your brother, agh be quick to share his burden.\n17.The hardship of life is a refining furnace. It hurts for the time, but melts away that which would make\nlat weak.\n18.Lats body is a gift. Use it hoshly. Do nub abuse it, agh do nub let it wither.\n19.Life is work. Work hard or starve.\n20.The cactus lives in the dry sands, needing little nourishment. It is stronger for it.\n21.Hosher is a bag of rotten flesh, than a feast in the blarg of the dishonorable.\n22.He who lives with nub honor is like a fortress made of dry twigs or a zult made of still air: useless.\n23.Taking a title simply for the\nsake of taking a title is like eating sharp blades simply for the sake of eating.\n24.A wise blah is more precious than all the gems beneath the earth.\n25.Hosher to be flat for what is honorable, than to abandon lats\nintegrity simply to extend lats life.\n26.Honor is nub a currency to be traded. Do nub treat it as such.\n27.A life with nub honor is as meaningless as letters with nub order.\n28.Do nub tolerate weakness in body,\nmind or spirit.\n29.He who works hard will have his bread.\n30.Feeding the lazy is like planting the wind. It accomplishes nubthing.\n31.Be satisfied with food agh a cave. It may be all lat have ash day.\n32.Do nub envy the rich. Their decadence will make them soft.\n33.Do nub peep down on the poor. They are nub blinded by the glimmer of gold.\n34.Minas often do little more than disappear.\n35.Deceit agh\ntwisted words only clutter agh clog the mouth. Eventually, lat will choke on them.\n36.Blah what lat mean, nub what others want to hear.\n37.A slimy heart will slip, agh fall to its destruction.\n38.Rulers, do nub\nbe haughty. Ash day, lats reign will end, agh another will take lats place.\n39.He who is wise heeds the truthful rebuke.\n40.The fool surrounds himself with flatterers, agh is nub aware when ruin comes.\n41. Hosh is the\nfemale who bears strong cubs, agh works tirelessly to nourish their bodies agh spirits.\n42.Happy is the male who finds her, agh keeps her.\n43.Hosher is ash honorable lifemate, than ash hundred weak mates.\n44.As a blarg will\nnub stand on mist, cloud or vapor, neither will a family stand on weakness, foolishness of dishonor.\n45.Walk as Krug walked, agh honor the spirits. This will keep lats path straight.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mana?", "Davin Lodmund", "Mana\nWhat is mana?\nIn simplicity, mana is an invisible substance that encompasses us and everything we see. Imagine seeing a rock, and lifting it up. Mana resides even so much as within a pointless object such as that.\nwere to look at the person next to you, even they have mana. What makes people different than objects in terms of mana is the fact that we, as Descendants, are capable of growing and hence manipulating our mana pools.\nHow come we see mana when something is transmuted?\nYou don't. If you saw one transmute, you likely saw their Aura. An Aura is the excess that comes off of ones mana. The color is very much depending on ones mental state\nWhat is Transmutation?\nTransmutation itself is a rather simple concept. Simply altering an object to what you want it to be. In actuality, accomplishing this is difficult and requires immense study upon what you wish to change.\nYou must follow the law of equivelent exchange as well, being unable to create diamonds from dirt, or water from rock. You may very well change something like water into ice, or perhaps change the shape of stone.\nHow do I transmute something?\nWe'll use an example. Take a sphere of ferrum, able to fit in your palm and weighing five kilograms. You must first study ferrum in all its' senses. How it reacts to temperature, pressure and\neverything.\nYou must as well find its mana signature. A mana signature is the way mana is 'layed out' in a specific object. You may find this able to be done easiest by meditating with the material, and sending your own mana coursing through it at times.\nYou may stop once you have familiarized yourself with it.\nAfter this, you would summon your own mana, and envelop the ferrum sphere with it. Fill it, coat it, and everything of the like. Much akin to how one 'wills' their evocations to act, you would 'will' the ferrum's properties to change. For this, we shall\ninvision a ferrum rod. If you truely know what ferrum is, and how it works, it should begin to shape how you wish it to. The first go will be immensely tiring, as well as bear a danger shared by any and all transmutation.\nWhat is the danger?\nYour stupidity. If one was to dare try and shape it into something that would require more of the substance then what you posses, you'd find your mana rapidly drained and yourself dead. This goes for any amount.\n=--= Enchanting =--=\nWhat is Enchanting?\nEnchanting is the act of changing the properties of an item, much akin to Transmutation in that sense. The difference here is that you are changing it to have magical ability,\nrather then to look different. This does not mean you may use the enchantment as much as you wish, however. This is due to the fact that it still requires 'equivelent exchange'. For this, we shall move onto mana gems.\nWhat is a mana gem?\nTake a precious material. A finely crafted diamond, emerald, or even gold. The more valuable, the better. These materials, past their own mana, have space to hold more than what they have.\nTaking advantage of this, we may go so far as to fill the empty space with our own mana, and then order it to 'fuel' an enchantment. The gem, filled with mana, is hence called a mana gem\nHow do we actually enchant something?\nEasy! You are to use your mana much as you did with transmutation, and 'will' the object to cast a certain spell when supplied with mana. It should be noted one can not cast with a magic they can not cast.\nAlong with that, you 'will' the mana in the mana gem to supply the enchantment upon a certain order. This can be motion, sound, or physical contact. Dont lie. I know transfigurationists who enchant with things they don't know!\nOkay, you caught me. They can, but it's a difficult act. For one, they need someone who knows the magic to help them. Second, they need to fully understand said magic.\nWe'll use a water evocationist and me for example. To do 'joint enchanting' with a water evocationist, I must first understand water evocation as though I were capable of actually casting it. After that, I'll have him cast a spell to be wrapped in my\nMana.Once I envelop their spell, I will 'break it down' into its original mana that created it, and use my own to funnel it into the object I wish enchanted. The last stage requires a certain level of trust. If the other person gets scared, it will fail.\nWhy would they be scared?\nBecause, you're essentially taking their mana to do joint enchanting. It gives an odd feeling to them. Such may cause them to grow scared and cease casting, which results in failure.\n=--= Warding =--=\nWhat is warding?\nWarding is a more difficult concept, but still one able to be grasped farely quickly. To ward a magic, one must understand it as though to the extent of joint enchanting.\nThe difference between joint enchanting and warding is the fact that such can be done on your own, without aid. After you understand the magic you intend to ward, you then create a 'web' of mana. Such takes immense concentration\nand energy.After some minute of forcing mana out, you have it ready to attack the mana anchor of the magic you wish to ward. As the spell would hit your ward, it should quickly have its mana anchor 'attacked' by your own.\nAssuming your ward has more mana than the spell attacking you, it should promptly vanish. If not, or if its a magic you arent familiar with or are not currently warding against, it will simply pass the ward and hit you.\n=--= Abjurgation =--=\nWhat is an Abjurgation?\nAn Abjurgation is simply a summoned amount of mana. It works much the same as a ward in every way, yet often takes the color of ones aura.\nIt's used to be thrown at other peoples spells either before it is finished casting, or in mid air. Abjurgations themselves are created with the purpose of attacking another spells mana anchor, and are quite easy and quick to summon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Many Thanks!", "The Pale Brotherhood", "The Pale Brotherhood thanks you for your kind contribution to our coffers. Your wealth is our strength. Your gold is fuel for our greed.\n\nStrength in shadows.\nDermin va-Mer Thorok", ""),
        StaticBook("Map for Traps", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Scout out a new city, listing its none residential buildings.", ""),
        StaticBook("Marden", "David FeatherHeart", "He is the shadow in the light. He stalks his prey with the power of men. He is only named by those who fear him yet serve him. This man , no, beast is named Marden. \n                He is not a man of no goals though. He is brocken and seeks power in the\nislands of Vailor. He wants to sit on the throne of his lies in peace with his army of men. \n        He was once a man. Or more like one and not the wraps of villany that he is today. He lived on the ancient island of Kathersa. He live in fear of the worl\nd as the world feared him as well. As you can tell, this man was not of the usual. He was of the Guild of Marden. They lived upon the great moutain of God's peak and studied the art of war.The art of death. The art of insanity. At that time he was not nam\ned Marden. Then he was only a name that was hidden and despised by all. He trained thier with the guild along myself. He would train each day and by each day only his humanity drained in the hole of his thoughts. \n              Soon after our graduation h\ne and I (along with my brother) took the mighty boat , God's mass, to the islands of vailor. As we arrived I saw him look upon the land. I saw the greed in his eyes. The power in his fists. He was going to rule. I then saw a miracle happen. He smiled. But\nnot of happiness, no, but of greed once more.\n         He now plans in the shadows for no one knows his true name but I. He now only goes by Marden to represent his guild. I only serve him now along my dearest brother. \n             He now looks for follo\nwers to use. If you are in any way interested visit the lands of count Roswell nearby Felsen and find me. Then and only then will You be able to join.\n          This is a warning to all kingdoms. No. All of Vailor. Beware the power of Marden.", ""),
        StaticBook("Marsks Testimony", "Caulder Marsk", "I, Caulder Marsk, under the gaze of God himself do solemly attest that what I say here is of the purest truth and do hold my honor to these claims.\n\nVladan has proven himself a dishonorable man not worthy of his position. For a time I served under\nhis order, and left with disgust of the Order's injustice. I had hoped that Vladan was different, but he is not. \n\nWhilst on vigilant watch I heard the conversings of both Adler and Vladan and can attest to the fact that the Marshal attempted to\ninstigate conflict through the use of deplorable insults towards Adler's rank and status in society not fitting of man in Vladan's position. More heinous is that fact that Vladan blatantly tried to harm or fabricate misdoing of Adler by raising his fists\nagainst him and heavily attempting to instigate conflict. Adler, despite their beratement and vileness stood stalwart and levelheaded. \n\nThe Marshal went as far as to imply he was above the law as a result of his status and could thereby do whatever he\nwished to whomever he wished. He also implied Safwa was of a lesser class and the court held no meaning, stating she would never be ennobled as a Far Folk. \n\nSuch a man should not hold position in the fair city of Belvitz. It would aid the city greatly to\nsee Vladan face the justice he believes he is above.", ""),
        StaticBook("Material Form", "Luna Lyeis", "-A few ingots of bluesteel\n-Ironwood, fine if it's unrefined\n-Iron, crude is fine\n-Some sort of leather\n-Block of Coal\n-Windswept Branches\n\nPlease Sign this to confirm all items were accounted for\n~Luna Lyeis", ""),
        StaticBook("Maternity", "Illynora Sylvaeri", "\n\n\nUnderstanding your\nMaternity Care Parcel\nRed Raspberry Leaf Tea\no-----------------o\nThis herb has been used by all races during pregnancy, birth, and childcare for centuries.\n\nDrink 1-2 cups daily while with child, and 3 cups during labour.\nPeppermint Tea\no-----------------o\nFeeling nauseous is a common symptom of pregnancy, especially in the early stages.\n\nDrink one cup in the morning with breakfast, or at the onset of nausea.\nRaw Ginger Root\no-----------------o\nSimilarly, ginger can help to ease an upset stomach. Steep in hot water for a quarter of an hour- add honey if desired.\nLicorice Root Tea\no-----------------o\nHaving a child is exhausting. This tea serves to improve energy and fight against fatigue.\n\nDrink 1-2 cups daily, especially in the weeks after birth.\nPassionflower Tonic\no-----------------o\nIf you are having trouble sleeping, dilute one dose of this tonic into a beverage of your choosing and consume one hour before bed.\n\nThis herb is also useful for irritability and restlessness.\nMuscle Cramp Tincture\no-----------------o\nContaining valerian root, chamomile, lemon balm, and crampbark, this remedy is the perfect relief against cramps.\n\nDilute one dose into water.\nGripe Water\no-----------------o\nTo be used if your child becomes irritable between nursings.\n\nContains chamomile, fennel, caraway, peppermint, aloe, ginger, blackthorn, lemon balm, and vegetable charcoal.\nBreastfeeding Tea\no-----------------o\nContains fenugreek, aniseed, chamomile, fennel, nettle, and red raspberry leaf.\n\nDrink 1-2 cups daily during the breastfeeding period.\nAches and Pains\no-----------------o\nApply five drops of calendula oil and three drops of distilled witch hazel to bathwater.\n\nIt will help to remove aching joints, particularly a sore back and ankles.", ""),
        StaticBook("Matthew", "Grace", "Matthew, \n\nI'm sorry to be unable to give you this letter in person. But I'd hate for you to witness my state now..\n\nIt is truly shameful. \n\nI love you, truly as much as I can ever possibly can as your sister.\nBut, I cannot go on with my mind. It is a truly troubling place. The nightmares, the paranoia.. the lonliness. It's horrific and It hurts too much.\n\nI've left with you all the books and information I had with me regarding the Vaeyl.. not like you\ndon't already know it. \n\nYou were always a know-it-all. But I was proud of that, you are one of the most prescious things to me and I was truly honoured to call you a brother. \n\nPlease do not mourn for me, just know.. that wherever I end up.\nI'll be at peace, if the gods do not shun me. \n\nTake care of your family and please.. look out for my own. My children will needed someone in Hareven's absence. \n\nAspects guide you beloved brother.\n\nAll my love\nQuillian Axel Serene Caerme'onn Lorenthus.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mauktaz Jurnel", "Wargoth Akila'Lur", "Mi wunt tu ryt tu lat. Mi gruk idd zhall help uzz undaztand eechubba.\n\nVery well.. \n\nWub am latz naym?\n\nThisereh Zhall\n\nZhall?\n\nMy last name.\nLat kall mi Maukta.\n\nNice to meet you. \n\nLat dub, mi lyk latz drezz, mi am agh kraftmen ub kloth agh armagh.\n\nI'm a huntswoman I suppose, not very adept in swordsmanship however\nLat kan zhoot agh o'lig?\n\nYes.\n\nMi lyk lat alredy den.\n\nAhernan. I don't have much to do with my time so if you need aid anywhere. Let me know.\nLat kan help mi model fabrikz, mi zell lotz ub tingz amung atlaz incluudin ezotik clothin\n\n\nWell if you need a model.\n\nLat wud bi perfekt. \n\nVery well, I'd be happy to assist.\nAlzo lat kan hunt wib mi, ib latz intrezted mi kan zhow lat da weyz ub de zpiridzz\n\nI've never heard of your spirits.\n\nIdd am owagh wey ub lyf. Wi aktualyz in krug by worzhippin zpiridz wi revere\nI'd be interested to study your culture.\n\nMi tink lat cud mayk agh hozh liddul zpirid worzhippagh.\n\nI'm only little, because your kind are overly huge.\n\nIb lat am jeluz idd am ukee\nYou're a good height to be shot at.\n\nBut lat gruk betta den dat nuw.\n\nIt was a mere jest.\n\nMi gruk. lat am welkum tu make latzelf comftable\n\nAhernan once more\nDe zkah am ahernan?\n\nMeans thank you\n\nLat welkum.\n\nBlah tu mi boudd latzelf. . lat peep tu be mozt intreztin\n\nThere's not much to me, had simple parents whom ->\ntended to farmlands. I hunted the predators that attempted to feed from the lifestock.\n\nMi peep. . How did lat loze latz voyz?\n\nGeneral sickness and old age. My parents struggled with having a child for a long time. They had me when they\nwere quite old.\n\nHrm. . Mi lyk da quiet. Maukta du nub blah much tu ubbaz.\n\nUbbaz?\n\nuhh-thurz\n\nAh, I see. I was born a mute, so It does not bother me much.\nForewarnin. Ib lat zhowz owagh talkz tu uthurz mi will flat lat.\n\n\nOwagh?\n\now-ur\n\nNoted. But I do not take kindly to threats.\n\nMaukta'z wurd am alweyz zekret. ->\ntu blah idd tu anudda am tu azzept latz fayt. Mi lyk deez zhared wurdz doe\n\nI'm a Muakta?\n\nNub, mi am.\n\nOh, Apologies. Still adjusting to your speak.\n\nId am nub prublem.->\nazh day lat will gruk owagh lingo all da wey.\n\nAnd perhaps you will know mine too.  \n\nMi gruk latz well, mi tuzkz juzt mayk idd hawd tu blah\n\n I meant elvish. It's quite ironic the thought of an orc speaking elvish.\nMi wud bi happi tu lern. Maybe de maukta will hab zum guydanze fur lat azwell in de fyutcha\n\nI hope too.. Today was the most exciting I've had I suppose. Never been in a battle that large.. Or a single battle for that matter.\nZtik cloze agh Maukta will mayk agh bob'hozh Maukalus\n\nI shall, I just need to familiarize myself with targets other than large animals. \n\nLat handled latzelf hozh tudey. Mi wub ulmozt imprezzed.\nWhat do you mean almost? I was flawless today.\n\nJuzt kuz lat am preddy du nub mean lat kannub uze zum formal traynin.\n\nTrain against an orc? I'd rather not break bones.\n\nMi will nub hurt lat.\nI'm more worried about your friends, they seemed all for the idea in enslaving me.\n\nMauktaz wurd dat am nub gun happen.\n\nAyla - good. Thank you for your hospitality.\n\nLat welkum. Du lat feel zafe in de goi ur wud lat lyk tu zleep in mi towa? Mi gruk zum ub deez urukz zcare lat.\n\nI'd prefer to stay in your tower if I'm honest.\n\nLat am welkum tu du zo. Der am plenty playzez tu zleep ib mi bed am nub ->\nzuffizent fur lat.\n\nIt should be fine!\n\n\n\nWhat are you carving? \n\nPeeperz , reprezent tingz tu de maukta.\n\nAnd what exactly do they represent?\nTu mi klan, idd am agh zymbol ub Veizt. Tu agh uruk'z Azhtkaar\nMaarubh peeperz reprezent nub unlee hiz worth but zymbol awarenezz.\n\nI see.. Your culture baffles me.  \n\nLatz kulta eludez mi\n\nI barely know my\nculture, I stick to my own books and do what sits right with me. \n\nHeagh wi fokuz between owagh khatun, zpiridz ub choize, agh Azhtkaar Maarubh. \n\nYou've lost me.\n*here would be a doodle of krug*\nKhatun, in zhort am owagh wunt tu be lyk krug himzelf. Wi revere agh wizh tu aktualize in hiz hozhnezz.\nVeizt iz azh ub de few zpiridz dat gain mi worzhip agh offerinz, zame wib mozt mi klan\nAzhtkaar Maarubh, how owagh klanz zettle dizputez agh vote un ->\ntingz. Agh zymple kode ur law.\n\nI see, you folk can be odd sometimes. \n\nWub am odd aboud urukin?\n\nYou ways of things, not that it's a bad thing. Just quite different from what I'm used to. Like fighting\nfor titles and power.\n\nHuw elze du lat keep zkah'er frum bein dizhonaghble agh ztabbin zumazh in de bakk? Idd am agh zymple optiun tu dezyd whu de anzeztaghz fayvagh.\n\nRight.. Apologies it's just a new concept.\nMi am nub uhfended. Zimply agh retort.", ""),
        StaticBook("May love last.", "Melian", "The fear of you\nlosing your love for me in great in my heart.\nSo I dare not look you in the eye when I ask you a simple question...\n\nMay you say no I just leave these here...\nWill you have my hand in marriage?", ""),
        StaticBook("Medical Guide", "Vitalius Maarsen", "-Medical Notes-\n\n            By\n    Vitalius Maarsen\n\n\nIn these pages you will find basic medical prodecedures to perform for most cuts and wounds.\nOne of the most first importat steps in medical aid is identifying the problem, second step is knowing how much the person is in pain, third step is to check for pupil dialation because it happens when a person has head injury or orbit trauma, fourth step\nis to check for pulse to determine how much blood is left in their body simply put two fingers on the arteries below the chin on the neck or on the wrist, If you are dealing with an injury in a combat environment the first thing to do is to check the area\naround and make sure it's safe if not procede to carefuly retreat further back.\n-Sterilization-\nSterilization is another important step that should be done a medical kit should have pre-sterilized tools and bandages, use alcohol to clean wounds by applying some on a piece of clean cloth and gently rubbing the area where whe wound is\nto prevent any infection, change any bandages and dressings at least twice a day.\n-After Care-\nAfter any wounds or sickness one should be in a state of recovery, therefore there are some basic steps one should know. One should never drink any alcoholic drinks, during recovery the person should stay in a clean environment\nand the practice of sterilization and bandage changing should be done all the time\n-General Laceration-\nThe first thing to do should be stopping blood, carefuly sterilize the wound before applying pressure on it with a clean bandage, depending then from the type of damage it could just use some common rags, cauterization or suturing.\nCauterization consists in heating up your tool to then carefuly seal any open blood vessels by applying it on the open wound, it's reccomanded on small veins and should be avoided in delicate areas.\n-Arrow Wounds-\nArro ounds are the most deadly ones, the main problem is that the arrow head can disconnect from the shaft being lodged on in the body, that can cause infections, to check if the arrow head is disconnected from the main shaft\nlightly and carefuly turn it, if it's connected carefuly pull the arrow out and procede to treat the wound, if it's not pull out the shaft and procede to use your tools to carefuly take the arrow head out.", ""),
        StaticBook("Medical Guide,", "Eradan Dune`dien", "A Sutican Ranger`s\n        \n         Guide To\n \n\n\n     M E D I C I N E\n\n\n\n\n\n   By DT\nChapter one.\nAssessment\n\nThe key to any successful medical treatment is first identifying the problem.\nFrom arrow wounds to suturing the most important thing is getting a good idea of what your dealing with.\nDetermine if the wounded person is in pain, Adrenline can still be coursing through their body from the battle they just fought or they could be slipping into shock from bloodloss, infection or coma. Knowing how much pain a person is in key.\nThe next step is to check for pupil dialation pupil dialation is controlled by a series of muscles and nerves around the eye. Pupil dialation is found when a person has suffered a head injury or orbit trauma. Knowing will help you effectivly treat them.\nCheck the pulse of the wounded person, doing so will give you a general idea on how much blood theyve lost if any. Or what state the person is in. To check pulse put to fingers on the arteries below the chin on the neck, or the arteries on the wrist.\nSituation assesment. In the case of an active combat environment you should make sure the area where you are is safe enough to procede with treatment or if you will have to retreat.\nEven when not in combat, whatever harmed the person may still be around.\nChapter one checklist\n\n1. Pain\n\n2. Pupil dialation\n\n3. Pulse check\n\n4. Situation check\nChapter two.\n\nSterilization.\n\nThe most important step in treating someone is to help them rather than hinder, however infection of the wound will hinder alot more than it will help so sterilization is a key part in any medical procedure.\nWhen packing a medical kit you should include pre-sterilized tools, sterilized bandages as well as alcohol to clean wound and the area of the medical procedure, when about to begin a procedure such as suturing you should take a clean cloth,\ndouse it in alcohol and scrub the wound and the area surrounding the wound to prevent infection. The next step would be to use your sterilized tools. Then bandage with clean bandages. Key to after procedure treatment is cleanliness,\nyou should change any dressings and bandages at least twice a day. An operating table should always be clean and free of blood. As well as the recovery bed. Little contact with body fluids is paramount during patient\nrecovery.\nChapter three.\nAfter care\n\nAfter completing a medical procedure you should quickly usher the patient into recovery. Once in recovery the primary things a patient should be getting is food, water and care.\nWhen a patient is in recovery thet should NOT\nbe given any alcoholic drinks. During recovery the practice of sterilization should be assumed at all times. Bandages and dressings changed and constant attention will lead to a healthy and speedy recovery.\nWhen recovering its important the patient isnt in any risk. They should be looked after in a clean safe area with ample room between patients. This isolation prevents the spread of germs and disease while speeding the healing process.\nChapter four.\nGeneral lacerations\n\nLacerations or deep cuts are those which are caused by an accident in the kitchen or a slip of a knife. Regardless of the way the laceration was caused you must be quick to act. Blood\nis the bodies most important fluid,\nstopping the bleeding is your first priority when dealing with lacerations, you should take the time to Sterilize the wound and area before applying pressure on the wound with a clean bandage depending on the type of laceration it can require anything\nfrom a bandage, cauterization or suturing.\nThe most common is suturing. If you chose to bandage simply clean the wound again, apply fresh bandage and tell the patient to apply pressure for the time. If you chose Cauterization your first step is to clean!\nClean the wound again and switch out the bandages as you heat your cauterizing device. Once the cauterizing device is hot and ready for use its the delicate process of pressing the hot metal into the wound fusing any torn blood vessels and stopping the\nbleeding. This is reccomended when  used on small veins and should be avoided when the laceration is in a delicate area. Your third and final option with lacerations is to suture.\nWhen begining to suture you should first make sure your tools are clean.\nOnce you are ready clean the wound once again and begin, push the needle through one side of the skin of the laceration and across to the other, pulling it through and then tight. Repeat the process in a criss cross pattern until the wound is closed.\nthe next step is to tie the suture and cut the needle away. Once this is done you clean the wound yet again and apply bandages.\nWith this you have sucessfully stopped the bleeding and can safely move the patient to aftercare. If bleeding resumes reassess.\nChapter five.\nArrow wounds\n\nContary to popular belief arrow wounds are some of the most deadly wounds you can recieve when in battle.\nThe main problem with this is the fact that arrowheads that become disconnected to the shaft in turn become lodged.\nOnce lodged the head of the arrow will not be pushed out by the body leading the area to become inflammed and infected. Step one in any arrow wound treatment is to establish what type of situation you are dealing with.\ntwist the shaft extremly lightly to determine if the arrow head is disconnected or connected to the shaft. If disconnected you can simply remove the shaft and set to work dealing with the arrowhead. If still connected it becomes a more delicate process.\nOnce your ready to procede clean the area of the wound with alcohol and make sure you have clean tools. Pain relief herbs and potions are reccomended as a tense patient can cause a muscle contraction that can worsen the wound.\nNow that the patient is ready you should carefully take a surgical knife and at the bottom and top of the wound make a small cut allowing you to spread the wound. Once spreading the wound carefully taking mind not to hit any blood vessels.\nThen carefully remove the arrow head if disconnected or head and shaft if the head is still connected. You should remove all foreign debris before cleaning the wound once again. You should then suture and bandage before moving patient to after care.\nChapter Six.\nFever and infection\n\nFever and Infection are some of the most dangerous illnesses contracted. A fever is the bodies heigtened temperature ussually caused by the bodies response to infection.\nWhen dealing with a fever it is important to keep the body cool. Wetting a cloth and pressing it to the forehead is good treatment, you should also have them drink lots of water along with hot fluids such as tea or coffee.\nThe best foods to feed someone with a fever and infection are hot soups and stews. Its important to keep a healthy balanced diet when in aftercare. The body should be able to fight of most infections by itself.\nHowever if it looks as if the patient will die you should immediatly intervene and give them the more valube medical herbs and or potions of healing. If all else fails its important to contact a mage or ascended. Its important to seek help when needed!", ""),
        StaticBook("Medical Std. V1", "The Scribe.", "A Study of Medicine. \nPossibly Volume 1,\nAnatomy.\n\nAssisted by Salazar the Mali'Aheral.\n'One learns to figure out the limits of one's body as one travels.' ~Salazar.\n\nThe cadavers of less fortunate travelers make for good study; \nTheir bodies can be found suffering from illnesses or ailments,\nand studying them was an urge that could not be repressed.\nChapter 1: Circulation of Blood.\n\nThe circulatory system runs throughout the body. It provides blood to various muscles and organs, replenishing them with every beat of the heart. Blood provides Anima to the body, which is the life\nforce that drives us all, and gives us energy. Anima may possibly contain a variety of elements that we require to function in life. As one works more strenuously, the circulatory system does as well. This may be because as the body\nuses energy, it requires more anima to function at the previous levels.\nAilments of the Circulatory System;\n\nA disease of the circulatory system causes the blood to not coagulate where it may normally do so. This causes the patient afflicted with such a disorder to bleed profusely, until magic is introduced.\nThis disease is highly rare.\n\nAnother disease is caused by the blood vessels themselves being left open to the air or to water for a long time. This causes blood-poisoning, an infection of the blood itself.\nThis can be treated a variety of ways, though none of which are easy. Amputation is the most rudimentary form of this. The next is quick cleansing of the wound with pure water and alchemically based healing potions. The third is to use clerical magic, but\nsuch can be considered a panacea.\n\nThis condition is uncommon, as most open wounds are wrapped.\nChapter Two; Digestive.\n\nThe digestive system consists of the stomach, smaller intestine, large intestive, and the excrementory system. \n\nThe stomach contains within it a large amount of naturally produced\nacid which dissolves food that is consumed through the mouth. After the food is broken down, it seems to be passed through both intestines, where it is absorbed into the body. Of course, these broken down materials most likely filter into the blood system\nwhere the blood and the body converts the food to anima. This is why death by starvation can take place. However, the body itself can overstock these necessary nutrients, and cause fatness and obesity.\nDigestive diseases. \n\nThe stomach acid can become too concentrated and can break down the lining of the stomach. This can cause severe pain. The most common cure for this is the direct consumption of tippens root, as it brings the pH of\nthe stomach acid down to natural levels. \n\nAnother digestive issue is an illness that causes constant vomiting, or constant bowel movements. While vomitting is the bodies natural defense against bad food, this vomit is\nvery common even with high quality food. The best way to deal with this sickness is to consume mass quantites of salted water, as such replenishes the bodies well-being after their body exterts it. Sugar should also be added to the water.\nThis disease can be common or rare depending on its severity. \n\nOne may also vomit if they exert themselves to a point of exhaustion.\nChapter 3; Respiratory.\n\nThe Respiratory system contains the lungs and the windpipe. The windpipe is located behind the thick protective cover at the front of the throat. The lungs suction air from the environment\ninto them through use of a muscle underneath the lungs called the diaphragm. The lungs expand to hold the inhaled air, and then the air is pushed out. However, the body somehow utilizes the gas, most likely to produce more efficient anima.\nIf blood is deprived of the air, it turns purple and sickly looking. When re-exposed to the air, it turns bright red. My belief is that blood uses one of the gases that comprises air to convert nutrients into anima.\nBetween both of our knowledge, no diseases or ailments of the respiratory system were known, but the respiratory system can be damaged through the inhalation of coal fumes, causing 'Black-Breath'. This cannot be cured except by\nthe magic of the monks.\nChapter 4; Muscular.\n\nThe muscles are connected to the bones by tendons, stretchy bits of yellow 'flesh' that allows for the full range of motion. The muscles of the body tend to work in groups of two, one to push, and the other to pull.\nThe larger the muscle, the greater the force exerted by the movement of the muscle. As muscles are damaged through use, they heal and grow larger, thusly more powerful. This is why one is sore after strenuous exercize.\nNo ailment of the muscle is cureable. The degrading of muscle is either through use of magic, or by some ailment. Both of these result in the eventual loss of the majority of muscle.\nThere appear to be three types of muscle, involuntary, mixed, and voluntary. Involuntary muscles can not be controlled at all, such as the heart or the digestive muscles. \n\nMixed can be controlled some of the time, but for the\nmost part, operate on their own. This includes breathing, blinking, and swallowing. \n\nVoluntary muscles are only able to be used with input, such as the arms or the legs.\nChapter Five; Bones.\n\nThe bones are the structure of the body. They also offer protection. Bones are incredibly dense, most are stronger than steel. The amount of bones in a body is 206, with six tiny, tiny bones in the ears that some\nhow are linked directly to balance. The bones can heal themselves if set correctly, though clerical magic allows this process to finish faster.\nThere are no known ailments of the bone.\nAddendums; \nBruises are the pooling of blood from broken blood vessels.\n\nThe heart is an involuntary muscle.\n\nThe circulatory system involves vessels that take blood to the heart to replenish in anima,\nand arteries that take anima-enriched blood away from the heart to the muscles and other parts of the body.", ""),
        StaticBook("Medicinals 101", "Guyden Aureon", "Standard Medicinals:     Widely recognized for its ability to stop bleeding, Tippen's Root can be utilized in a few ways. By crushing the root until its vaguely paste-like in texture, applying it to the wound will halt the loss of blood. It's also used in\nnumerous alchemical concoctions to treat more extreme injuries.\n Blissfoil serves as one of the most powerful anasthetics known, capable of causing extended loss of feeling if used in excess. The oil secreted by the plant can be most efficiently used\nby grinding it with a mortar and pestle. Directly applying the petals can suffice as well, albeit to a much lesser extent.\n Known unoriginally as Frostvine, this herb- like blissfoil- can numb pain. While its effects may not be as powerful, it also\ndoesn't pose the risk of long-lasting lack of feeling. This combined with its cooling properties make it a commonly used pain reliever for broken bones, sprains, and other such injuries.\n One lesser known herb, mandragora, is capable of restoring tissue.\nThis quality makes it particularly useful when dealing with internal damages. In such instances, it would be best to prepare the meat of the plant as a potion, but it also makes quite a fine stew. It can be applied topically to tissue as well. All that\nsaid, mandragora can be rather dangerous to harvest, and should never be attempted until two weeks after releasing its spores. It should also be noted that overdosing on mandragora can cause a series of growths to appear, thus should be handled with care.\nSpecial Medicinals:\n Alabaster Leaf, while capable of causing nausea, dizziness, and fatigue, can actually nullify of effects of other poisons within the body. While this isn't an ideal solution, such can decide whether one lives or dies in a pinch.\nFor the best outcome in such scenarios, this 'poison' should be ingested as soon as possible to counteract the effects.\n Another much lesser known herb, aqua's nymph, has remarkable healing properties for burns- real and magical alike. Now, to do this\nis no easy task, as to even gather it properly, you must avoid touching it. One sound method is to lift the plant into a jar by a thin layer of sediment, placing it in without touching the sides. Then to extract its properties, you must carefully dump the\nwhole plant into a basin of boiling where. When its buds release their liquid into the water, a chemical reaction occurs, creating a fine oil that can then be applied appropriately. One should keep in mind however, that if consumed it can possibly block\na person's air passage, and should thus be used carefully.\nMiscellaneous Facts:\n-Honey has long been used to prevent infection\n-Alcohol has long served as a reliable disinfectant and anesthetic\n-Willow Bark Tea, while not very potent, can relieve pain akin to a slight headache for long periods of time\nI hope this information has been of use to you- dear reader.", ""),
        StaticBook("Medicine Vol. 1", "Kale", "A Dose of Solace\nVolume 1\n\nWritten By: Dr. Kale\n\n\nIn this book you will find effortless remedies to common day sicknesses.\n1. Stomach Pain\n\n1 cup of hot chamomile tea\n3 peppermint leafs\n\nPlace the leafs on top of the hot steamy cup of tea and drink it twice a day to ease the churning pain.\n2. Flashes (Fever)\n\n4 rags\n1 big bucket of cold water\n\nSoak the rages with water and place each rag on the forehead, under each arm pit and behind the neck. Do so as needed until it subsides.\n3. Burning Throat\n\n1 hot cup of water\n5 drips of honey\n2 tsp. of sugar\n\nMix it all together thoroughly and sip until your throat begins to feel soothing.\n4. Coughing\n\n1 rag\n1 pot of boiling water\n\nPlace it rag over your mouth and bend your head close enough to the steam and breathe it in. Do this until your coughing has calmed itself.\n5. Ear Pain\n\n   Warm up oil until it is at a lukewarm feel and pour it into the ear. Lay on the opposite ear that isn't causing you pain. The pain should stop momentarily.\n6. Bruises \n\nThere's multiple remedies to heal a bruise quickly \n\n1st- Cold Herbal Tea Compress\n2nd- Ice Block compress\n3rd- Cold Poppy Tea Compress\n7. Rashes\n\nCacutus Paste\nHerbal Tea\n\nMash the two together until it become a thick like paste. Rub the paste on the rash until it drys or can be scraped off.\n*Here would be a sketch showing how to make the rash paste*\n\n\n*Here would be a sketch showing how to apply a compress to a bruise*\n\n*Here would be a sketch showing how to make different teas*\n*Here would be a sketch showing how to mix honey with tea* \n\n*Here would be a sketch of a person breathing in the steam with a rag covering their mouth*\n\n[!] The sketch would be drawn very well", ""),
        StaticBook("Melunis the Mad", "Jaya Jayamen", "Melunis the Mad\n\n          ~Originally by\n       Sofetios Jayamen\nI was travelling to a place called Geedin in search of a philosopher called Melunis. This man was said to be the wisest in the land, according to my friend who went there a while back. So I figured I would see what wisdom he could offer me.\nI arrived in the town and walked up to a guard. I said,\n\n“Excuse me sir, could you direct me to the man named Melunis?” The guard just laughed and said,\n“The only Melunis I know is a madman, you can find him over by the alley.” I thought to myself, this madman couldn’t be the one that my friend was talking about. My friend was a very smart person and wouldn’t confuse a wise man with a madman.\nSo to satisfy my knowing of whether or not this was the correct man, I went to the alleyway and saw an old man in rags. I said to the man.\n\n“Are you the man known as Melunis?” to which he looked at me, smiled, and said,\n“Indeed so! How can I help you this fine day!” The day was overcast, and cold. I couldn’t see how it was fine.\n\n“Would you happen to know my friend, James Linson?”  The man looked overjoyed at the name and said,\n“Why yes! I remember the lad. I do hope he is doing well.”\n\n“Well he told me you were the wisest in the land…” I said, to which Melunis replied with a frown,\n“Wise? No I’m not wise. I am just a ragged old man in an alleyway. Do I look like I’m Wise?”\n\n“No you don’t.” I said. “You don’t look wise at all.” The man then got a sparkle in his eyes.\n”Not wise at all?” said the man. “Well I must agree. You being very well off must know what it means to be wise, as you are in a far better place then I.” The man thought for a second, then said, “Tell me, what does it mean to be wise.”\n“Well it means that you know a lot about things.” I said, “Like a smith knows how to smith well, he is wise in smithing.”\n\n“Ah..” said the man. “ So in a sense, being wise is having knowledge.”\n\n“Yes.” I said.\n“ Alright, well what is knowledge.” Said Melunis. “As in how would I be able to obtain it to become more wise.” I thought for a second, then said,\n\n“Knowledge is knowing something, and obtained by learning.”\n“I see!” Said the man. “But… how do I know I know something.” At this I was a bit perplexed. I said,\n\n“Could you explain what you mean?” The man nodded and said,\n“In other words, How do you know what you know is true.”\n\n“Because you know it works when applied to things.” I said.\n“Alright.” Said the man. “So knowledge is what you know works when applied to things, but how does that make it true?”\n\n“What do you mean?” I said.\n“I mean for example, we could see an abstract painting.” Said Melunis. “You could think it’s one thing, I could think its another. Both works when applied, at least to the individual, but who is right?”\n“I guess we would both be right.” I said. “It would be up to the individual.”\n\n“Ah I see now!” Said the man. “So knowledge is what works with the individual. But still, how do we know it is true? Because isn’t the truth universal?”\nI began to get frustrated. But… Then I came to a realization.\n\n“I guess the truth is up to the person.” The man looked at me and said,\n“So there is no real truth? But what about common knowledge?” I thought for a second and said,\n\n“The common knowledge is what people have a common belief in.” Melunis nodded, seeming to understand.\n“But then what is the real truth?” The man said.\n“The real truth…” I began, “The real truth is… unknowable. Even if we got to it, people still would have different opinions. And those opinions might have more people believing in it than the real truth.”\nMelunis smiled at me and said,\n\n“Thank you, I think I understand now what it means to have knowledge.”\n\nSoon after this conversation, I left. Slightly confused, but more understanding.\nThough now I realized what my friend meant by him being the wisest in the land.\n\nThe End", ""),
        StaticBook("Mental Barriers", "Thurak'Yar", "Transcribed By\n            T Y\n\n\n          _____\n         {~~~~}\n        {~~~~~}\n         {~~~~}\n          {~| |~}\n             | |\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Written By Elindor\nRecognising The\n  Backgrounds of\n  Mental Barriers\n\n  1. Birthright\n\n  2. Learnt: Emotional\n\n  3. Learn: Intellect\n\n  4: Self Aware\nWhether conscious of the fact or not, all who are of mental capacity for independent thought operate with mental barriers. An avoidance of certain foods, sentimentalities for or against an individual based on previous experiences, a shudder at rain\ndropped upon the bridge of the nose. Whether they serve a point or not is beside the point, but all with functioning minds should also have functioning mental barriers. Granted, some are more useful than others, but none should be ignored.\nConsideration One \n\nWhile minds are capable of being moulded, as in the case of a particular experiment where a disadvantaged goblin child is given the intellectual upbringing of a noble elven child (For scientific experiments only)\nand it is observed that the matter of its circumstance of birth played little consequence in its mental abilities after the experiments completion; however there is equal quantity of proof to suggest the opposite; that particulars of birth can suggest\nbetter or worse mental ability. So if all with mental function possess mental barriers at some level, then it can also be agreed that some individuals may have naturally more intentional barriers resulting from the particulars of their birth.\nConsideration Two \n\nEmotional experiences are an inevitable by-product of experiencing the company of others. What is not certain is whether the usefulness of such can be realised. It has been observed through various trials\nin which test subjects experienced the same situation that a similar emotional outcome in each subject came forth. The results were conclusive that the female subjects were more capable of becoming emotionally guarded against a similar circumstance when\nthe same tests were repeated (and with more definitive results in the older subjects). The outcome of said experiments showed that aged women are more capable of producing emotional based barriers than are young men. Of course this does not mean it is\nonly the aged woman’s’ game to create emotional barriers, but that their past experiences before commencing tests rendered them more prepared to react in an emotionally defensive manner.\nBut whether young or old, and possessing of either of the genitalia, emotionally driven mental barriers prove to be an easily formed barrier that many people demonstrate. It is the experience that heat means danger, or that a wanting look from the\nopposite sex means trouble. And such learning becomes the basis of these most simple barriers with the intent to better our future course from further danger.\nConsideration\n        Three \nLearning needs by necessity of adapted barriers (the terminology “Adapted” used to refer to any barriers that are reactive in nature) is not limited to that of emotional education, though it is certainly\nthe easier and more likely to occur in individuals who have no conscious recognition of mental barriers than those of the next type: intellectual . Mentally capable individuals, typically of a higher learning, are more aware of themselves and the\ncommencement and termination of their own thoughts, such that they might be able to deduce that the outcomes of something will be of ill consequence, and thus establish an intellectual barrier against it without requiring the emotional experience of it to\ndraw such a conclusion. Anyone with such an ability would be considered of a more valuable intellectual worth than those who remain unconscious of their circumstance until they experience it first hand, because they demonstrate a conscious control\nover adapted barriers,, knowing the beginnings of danger before the danger is present. As is the results of tests among children in which one observes another experiencing pain and assumes the outcome of the test implement used will result in\npain, without having to experience it for themselves. Individuals with intellectual adapted barriers can become conscious of a problem before the problem manifests, and thus one who intends to expose them to mental danger will\nfind their defence against it pre-emptive from the first.\nConsideration \n         Four\n\nThe last is definitively the most complicated. Tests on such subjects still remain inconclusive as the data is often too broad an array to speculate commonalities; suggesting that great caution be taken in\nanticipating the adaptive and individualistic reaction to provocation.\nIf the proposed individual be of such mental awareness as to acknowledge their own thoughts and recognise the thoughts of others within their own\nmurmurings, then any\nmental intrusion will be detected from the first by these clever adaptive barriers that prevent further intrusion of outside stimuli.\nUnderstanding such mental barriers can only be done on an individual basis, for without foreknowledge\nof the mental, emotional and experiential past of the individual, one has no way of interoperating or supposing their reaction. And no one route will have conclusive success in all cases.\nThe Boldest \n     Conclusion\n\nIf, in any of the previous cases and most cunning of the latter one, an individual were to acknowledge their own conscious existence with relation to a broader knowledge of the universe and/or\ndeities, and at the same time comprehends themselves in reference to The Void, then their mental resoluteness may account for intentional barriers of not just emotional and intellectual stimuli, but of all mental stimuli. Such an individual is capable of\nconstructing a deliberate blockade that utilises their own experiences and acknowledging their own experiential or anticipated reaction, mould it into that will require a specifically, and equally intentional, attempt to remove it.\nOf anticipating and overcoming any barriers that the source of which that has been suggested in the previous pages, this book will do no work towards. For the effort to remove a barrier is to discredit the worth of it, while the intent of this\nbook has been to acknowledge and more clearly define the circumstance from which mental barriers may have been constructed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mental Defenses", "Friedrich", "Mental Magic\n- = - = - = - = - = -\nThough this book is specifically on how one might defend themselves against that of a mental mage, knowing how the magic itself functions is a key aspect to being able to do such. Because of this, we'll begin with a\npremise of the magic itself.\n\nMental Magic is considered a vile magic to practice, often finding itself compared to the likes of dark magic due to the way it often finds itself used - to find out privately kept information. Though when used\ncorrectly it is to be considered a great asset to any group. Mental Magic requires the supposed Mage to connect to the void, forging a connection with the mind of you, the 'Victim' as we will refer to it. Even if you've a barrier to put up in defense, the\nMage may still cast a number of spells on you - namely that of Mental Illusions and Cataleptics.\n\nMental Illusions allow the Mage to bring forth any reasonable illusion they can think of to force into your mind. If it is not reasonable, and/or you fail to\nbelieve it as real, the illusion shall vanish. Mental Illusions can consist of simple illusions or complex - such at in a battle being convinced that an opponent is moving another direction. Given that case, you would only really be able to tell it was\nan illusion if you or a friend was assaulted by the one that was being altered in your head.\n\nCataleptics is in essence, a sleeping spell. Like mental illusions this goes through barriers, forcing the target to eventually fall unconscious. This\nis not a combative ability due to the severe time it takes for it to be cast, though once it has been done your mind is completely open to all assault from the Mental Mage. This includes removing, altering, and bringing back memories. We will not be\ndiscussing such within this book, as the purpose is to teach you, the reader, of Mental Barriers.\nMental Barriers\n- = - = - = - = - = -\nBarriers for short, these are the most simple and complex ways of defending yourself imaginable. Should you posess vivid imagination, or none at all, it may naturally come to you as easily as flying does to a bird.\nIf you're of the average mentality, a small amount of trouble may come - though it will still be possible.\n\nThe concept of Barriers is the most complex part, while achieving them is far easier than learning. The technical way of describing a Barrier\nis any thought, image, or idea within your mind that you use in order to stop the mental mage from viewing what they would like. As a basis, when connected to their victim's mind the Mage only knows of their surface thoughts. That being any image you\nthink about, by accident or on purpose, as well as your own \"Mental Voice\" is visible to them as well. To stop this from being devastating, you may stop and focus - heavily at first, although it will eventually grow to be easier. Think of anything.\nA room, a locked gate, a chess board. For this example, we will use a white room with a Chess board in the center.\n\nAt this point the Mage would have a number of options. As a general rule, all Mental Barriers have a simple way of getting through.\nIn this case, the 'Simple Way' is to beat the Victim in the game. This is generally a trap however, as I have made such a barrier a chess game for the simple reason that any mental mage who attempts the chess game will very likely run out of mana by the\nend of it.\n\nIf the Mage realizes the trick, he can chose among two options - making it in to a game, or forcing his way past. If he forces his way past he will expend a fair portion of his mana. Your best bet is to hope he cant find out much in the time\nhe has left, at that point. If he choses to make it into a game, it turns into a mental battle - who can defeat the focus of the other first? Through mental illusions he can alter your barrier how he would like, trying to shock you into losing your focus\nas one might due to a mage. Your job will be to maintain your own focus while at the same time changing your barrier like one would with a lucid dream to break their own focus. Keep in mind you must focus only on your barrier, and any thoughts you think\noutside of this still leak through - no barrier is absolutely perfect.", ""),
