        StaticBook("Mira's note", "Mira Arden", "Hey Clanmates, feel free to write a book, or possibly go out and collect and buy some so our shelves are filled and the clan has a way to pass some time, under this note you'll find 3 empty books to write within if you find yourself wanting to put your -\n- own work on our shelves.\n\n- Mira Arden of Clan Arden", ""),
        StaticBook("Misconceptions", "Aewion Acaele’ellir", "Misconceptions\n------------------\nOOC NOTE: Written in Common for convenience and the fact that orcs would only use their blah words to write, not their accent.\n------------------\nHello! I've written this short informative novel to explore some\nideas. These ideas pertain to the fact that other races dislike us, I seek to find out why so we can either shore up our flaws or laugh our asses off. \n\nFirst, through various conversations with Oreners on and off their soil\nI will chronicle just why they decided it was a good idea to destroy our home.\n\nSection 1: Oren\n\nChapter 1: Fear\n\nAfter a short conversation with an Orenian knight, I learned\nsomething. Oren FEAR us. They find us to be terrifying brutes, though we certainly aren't. They find us scary because of our height and our tough demeanor. Honestly, I took it as a compliment. This knight, Ser Roland, told me how Oren found the\ndifference between our two races to be unsettling. I find this hilarious.\n\nChapter 2: Ignorance\n\nOren doesn't understand us, at all. Every single soldier has been taught to think of us as cruel, sadistic\nmonsters with an unsatiable lust for war. We can help our bloodlust just as much as they can help their puny lifespan. However, the disturbing part is the blatantly false evidence they presented me. They claimed that we picked a fight with them\nwhen they destroyed our capitol. That couldn't have been more wrong. As I recall it, they saw that we were at a time of transition and weakness and they blackmailed us. We refused the blackmail, so they thought they'd annihilate us. Not only did they\nthink that, but they thought our plan with Orgon's Plague was a project to destroy Vailor. The total destruction was accidental. We just needed an edge in the war. Plus, that was a good generation or two ago- why should this generation suffer for the\nprevious misdeeds of our people. \n\n\nChapter 3: Why They're Trapped In Ignorance.\n\nOne of the worst parts of this, is that we can't teach them about our complicated people.\nThey shut us out due to complete xenophobia. Once I was shot with a crossbow at the gates. \n\nChapter 4: Blind Loyalty\n\n*This chapter is stained with blood.*\n\nToday I made my second journey\nonto orenian soil. This time, a man tried to cut me down before I even drew a weapon. All I did was ask about the war. What is my curiosity returned by? An axe to the chest. I asked him why, and he said because I was an enemy. I asked him why again and he\nresponded with an incoherent answer before fleeing the scene. My conclusion? Half of these soldiers don't know what they're fighting for.", ""),
        StaticBook("Misfortune Hunt", "Misfortune Teller", "The land is small and full of lore.\n\nThe pumpkins grow around your hoe.\n\nThe King of all is next to me, but huge to all that are in his fee.\nRoad Down to the giant Tree where people laugh and drink with me.\n\nStraight into the moon at night, lowering down onto the road.\nInto the Holy flame and water, Ying and Yang.\n\nRun through the never ending vines and fields.\nTowards the doors of young and into the water of smelly tears.\n\nYou see the grand one resting on his throne, surrounded by his minions and watching over the town.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mission", "Lei", "THe Amber Cold\n           1682\n\nThe trip was rather quick on my stead -- I left behind that sellsword as he was taking too long to keep up. After a long ride I finally managed to get to the temple. I munched through around half of my\nprovisions so I knew that I'd have enough to get back. I surveyed the location around the temple, yet I did not find anything of value or anything at all -- It was quite empty. Over all, it was a big waste of time and effort.", ""),
        StaticBook("Missive", "Artorius Thannius", "Missive to the People I - The Revolt\nThe Circle of Governance would like to inform all citizens of the Enlightened Caste that the city is now back under control: the revolt of the lesser castes has been suppressed. I would like to\nformally dispel the rumours that this revolt was led by one of the orc beasts. It is laughable that a beast of burden could conceive of a plan of revolt, instruct the lesser caste in the use of tools of labour as weapons, and lead the lesser caste up\nin arms against the Enlightened. It is obvious that this must be have been a coup attempt by one of the Enlightened, and we will spare no expense in hunting down the leader of this insurrection and reeducating them.\nI also wish to reassure the\nenlightened people of Rivel that the recent mass euthanasia of the orc beasts is to prevent the spread of disease amongst them, not, as some have had the lack of wisdom to suggest, to prevent further revolt. Orcs do not think, this is a clearly\nestablished fact. They are simple beasts possessing no capacity for higher thought nor magical skill. Likewise, the recent introduction of “reorientation” of members of the lesser caste via mental magic is simply to improve their\nefficiency and wellbeing. The idea that we are attempting to turn them into “drones” is equally unfounded, and I would request such rumours are ceased: we do not wish to agitate the Lesser Caste and reduce the efficiency of their\nservice to us.\n- Artorius Thannius, Exalted Spellcrafter Archon of Rivel", ""),
        StaticBook("Missive", "Charles Staunton", "[CLASSIFIED] BURN UPON RECEIVING\n----------------------\nTO - Mister Leopold De Anjou (Alias - Iago)\n\nTo our esteemed mercenary, we have received information that your plans of getting close to Amelia Horen have bore fruit. This close proximity to\n[CLASSIFIED]\n----------------------\nyour granted target will allow for quick ascension through the ranks of Knighthood. The assassination of Amelia shall be allowed in the next few years. \nStay safe agent, the sum of ten thousand minas will be\n[CLASSIFIED]\n----------------------\ndeposited within the usual drop-off spot outside of Carolstadt.\n\nRemember, we burn the Horenian Remnants. Ave Staunton.\n\n-----------------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Missive 3", "Tarien Arvius", "Missive to the Spellcrafter Archon III - The Hall\nTo the Spellcrafter Archon,\nWe found the Hall and found it sealed. The Forgotten Dwarves appear to have sealed it from the outside with five keys, and we know not how to open it.\nWhile I felt unease at opening this place, my fears seem to have left me. We must open this hall. It is the will of the Radiant Man. We will assist him in finding the keys, we will open this Hall, and we will find the Seal. And with it, we will strike\ndown the Ravager and ensure the eternal survival of Rivel. I will not be returning to Rivel first as planned: I no longer have any fears about mental control by the Radiant Man. We will find the keys first, there is no reason to delay.\n- Spellcrafter\nTarien Arvius", ""),
        StaticBook("Modern Lineage", "Princess Titania Hawksong", "The family tree of Hawksong is broad, some members still having incomplete sections regarding their lineage due to the erosion of time. The following records the known main branch bloodline of modern times.\nImryll bore two sons to Galaeron Hawksong, Estelar and Jeriah. On Jeriah's account, he took Elnora as his wife and sired Azoth Hawksong. Azoth in turn sired Liave Hawksong to an elfess whose name is lost to the wind. This concludes the lineage of the -\nbrother Jeriah Hawksong as of this date of writing.\n\nEstelar Hawksong took Talindra as his wife, and they were greatly bless with three children during their middle years. In order of eldest: Aerendyl, Titania, and Umbriel. Aerendyl has no recorded -\nwife or offspring.\nTitania bore one child with Emberhard Hawksong and gave him the name Elrolas. Umbriel bore one recorded son, Elodur Hawksong. Elodur has no recorded offspring.\n\nThe line continues with Elrolas son of Titania, who sired Titania II -\nand Leona Hawksong.\nTitania II has no recorded spouse or children. Leona Hawksong married Tahiti Ba'ikana and has no recorded children.\nNoteworthy estrangements.\n\nTitania II and Leona are both presumed deceaseed, but Leona was estranged due to behavior and violating Vestale.\nElrolas is presumed deceased.", ""),
        StaticBook("MonkResurrection", "Jistuma", ">|<Monk>|<\n-=~Resurrection~=-\nIt is the salvation of many lives, but I wonder why I have seen nothing written on it. The monks, as is very well known, are able to save those that have passed away. While managing my stall at the sanctuary grounds I have been able to see for myself some\nof these happenings, or so I believe. \n\nThis magic, unlike many others, is one I know very little about. Like all holy magics it seems to be manifested as a bright light, mostly used to heal those wounded. Besides the bright light, the monk performing it\nis praying to the Triumvirate. It appears to be like clerical healing, but it has other properties. Sometimes a monk arrives at the sanctuary a bit hurt after travels. It appears bandits and the like do not care that they are mugging what could be their\nsavior. What I have to say about those monks, is that unlike normal folk, their wounds heal faster. This is of course due to their magic, small flecks of light I have seen surrounding and healing the wounds. Then the monks are able to bring back the once\ndeceased fully mortal once more.\n\nThis is not to say they are necromancers. Those simply raise the dead, and they remain in a limbo state living and being deceased. The monks are able to bring the body and soul exactly like it was before the death, in\nnear perfect condition. From those I have talked to over the years in the Sanctuary, there is an always present effect of being saved. Present in all of those that I have seen, none have memories of their death or even of the events leading up to it.\nOther common effects are scars, sometimes showing how the poor soul met its end before, or of the tortures it passed. The ones that worry me the most is that sometimes the ones saved change… I have talked to some before and after saving, and changes can\nbe quite extreme. Some go crazy, others start to live in constant fear, some remain with pains in parts of their bodies. The changes they can go through are incredibly varied. I could conjure up reasons as to why that happens, all of them without means of\nproving so. I just believe death to be a terrible experience, that part of it continues on even after salvation.\n\nAnother interesting fact I have gathered, somehow by luck, is that the saved do not want to return to the location that they had\nperished. This particular thought came to me when one of the saved was hugged dearly by what I assumed was his lover. Before that, his body had been carried by another, a friend perhaps, and he and I had a chat about what happened. I knew of the exact\nlocation of his demise, and as him and the woman were moving away, he asked if they were passing through that exact area when returning home. With the confirmation of the woman, he started giving out other ways to reach their house. A big argument even\nhappened when the woman just wanted to go home as fast as she could with him, and he plainly refused to go through that area, which was the only road to their house. He didn’t know himself why he didn’t want to. Alas he returned to normal about half a day\nlater. Since then I started noticing other strange behaviors such as people staying in the sanctuary for longer times, not using their normal routes out of the sanctuary and returning shortly after leaving with a friend. I simply believe once more, that\nthe experience was so horrible, that those saved gain a subconscious fear of their death place. Besides, what would happen if they saw their own body? \n\nOn the mention of bodies, I do have to state as well, it is not necessary for the\nbody to be brought back to the monks for the resurrection. I have seen many monks bring bodies to the sanctuary, so I believe it might be quite easier with them. This is favorable, as in the lands of Anthos there are many evils. You can be decapitated,\neaten, thrown into lava, cut into little bits and drowned in the deepest of oceans. Your body may disappear and never been found once more, and you may this way still be saved. How they restore the body I do not know, and the monks seem not to answer when\nI ask them. They do answer a few questions. I learned, for instance, that the monks are neutral, and never take side in political views or wars. They also take this neutrality to those they save. I have seen those of evil whose purpose is to kill being\nsaved together with the children that never made any harm. This has brought problems to the monks before, many want others to remain dead.\n\nMost of the stories of the saved start simply with them explaining how they woke up in the monk’s care.\nSeems to always be the same as I stated. Some come back quite soon after their demise, already back before their friends and family run to the sanctuary to check, and others can take elven days. Yet this magic is not all powerful. As the monks mention,\nthey cannot save all. If the deceased does not walk out of the monks rooms an elven week after their death, they are forever lost. The same happens to those that take their own life. I believe that if they think that they don’t want to live anymore, then\nthey wouldn’t return to the land of the living.\n\nThe monks are a blessing to mortals, they are those that save so many from their shortened lives.\nWritten by Rosso, 15th of Malin's Welcome 1452", ""),
        StaticBook("MonkResurrection", "Kirrekith", "Monk Resurrection\nBy Jistuma\nPages 23\n\nNotice, this books is a rushed copy of a tome inside the Library of the Orkish capital, as made during the raid of the 16th of the Grand Harvestm 1532 The following is no way a complete nor perfect copy\nMonk Resurrection\nIt is the salvation of those lives, but it is pondered why nothing has been wrote upon it. The monks are able to and well known for being able to save those on the brink of death or those who've always passed the thresshold. While at the grounds of the\nsanctuary manning a stall I have been able to witness of these happenings, or so what I believe. \n\nThis magic, unlike others, is one we know little of and myself. Like most holy forms of magic as it takes the form of a bright light, used to heal woun\nBesides this light, the monks act is to pray to the three known as the Triumvirate. It would appear to be that of clerical healing, but uses other properties not like those of clerical magic. Monks returning to the sanctuary can come back wounded,\nhaving been attacked by bandits proberly, showing peoples lack of care for whom they attack on the roads, especially when these individuals will often bring them back from the brink. Monks are not ordinary people, they heal faster than others from\nobservation. This is likely from their magic. often I witnessed light coming from they're wounds and surrounding it. Monks can also bring back the once deceased fully mortal once more. \nThis isn't in which to say they are necromancers, those that would\nbring back the dead, and remain in a state of limbo between death and life. Monks unlike them are able to bring back body AND soul unlike those of the necromancer, and bring them back to a near perfect condition from before death. Talking to those at the\nsanctuary, there is always an effect of being saved. A present residing condition is the loss of memory that occurrs after ones life being taken to the brink or past it and brought back. I have witnessed those effected having no memory of the passing or\nthe run up to it. Other common effects that linger is the scarring, revealing how the soul nearly passed the brink permanently or the tortures it passed. Often what worries me is the effects of change that develops in those that return, in personality.\nHaving talked to those if proves my worries. It is my belief that death is a terrible experiences, and part of it remains after the salvation. \n\nAnother fact I have witnessed, is that the deceased do not wish passively return to their prior resting p\nThis came to mind when I witnessed one of the saved hugged dearly by a beloved. Before this a friend has carried his friend, the two of us talked about what had occurred. Knowing the location of his end, the twos route home took them through the place,\nand upon discussing this he began to want to take other ways home, and a argument erupted when the woman just wanted to move home swiftly, much to the mans reluctance. He could offer no explanation as to why his mind has been set to not travel that way.\nAs well this this the other strange behaviours of those visiting the sanctuary became more apparent, such as staying there durations. As well as this not using normal routes out of the temple, or swiftly returning to the santuary after having left with\nfriends. Its my assumption that those who meet their death are faced with a pain too horrible to face, what could be worse than seeing your own dead body?\n\nOn the talk of the bodies, I have a state as well, it is not necessary for the body to be brou\nback to the monks for the resurrection. I've witnessed them bring bodies back to the sanctuary, so I believe possessing them makes the process easier or favourable. In the lands of Anthos there are many evils, you could be decapitated, easten, thrown in\nlava, cut into pieces and drowned in the deepest oceans. Your body may disappear and never be found once more, and even without it can still be saved. Resoration of the body is beyond my comprehsion, and monks refuse to answer the question. They do\nhowever answer a few questions. I learned the monks are neutral, and never take sides in politics and conflict. They also are neutral in those they save, murder or saint they are rescued. This has brought them into conflict as some are desired to be dead.\nMost of the stories of those rescued begin with them explaining their awakening. Waking to the monks care. Soon come back swiftly after their demise, often before family and friends arrive. Others can take many elven days. They're magic is not all\npowerful, as monks say they can't save all those who come to them. If the deceased does leave the monks rooms within a elven week after their death it is to be presumed them to have passed to the beyond without the monks being able to act. The same occurs\nto those who take their own life in an attempt at life to end. If they no longer wish to live, their is nothing the monks can do to bring them back. \n\nThe monks are a blessing to mortals. They are those thay save many from their shortened lives.\nWrote by Rosso, 15th of Malin's Welcome 1452, copied by Kirrekith on 16th of the Grand Harvest, 1532 during the raid on the Ork Capital.", ""),
        StaticBook("Monks of Charity", "Guru Pinya", "~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n    \n The Book of Peace\n\n    By: Guru Pinya\nThrough experimentation of the arcane, I have become enlightened. Through days of meditation at a time, I have become able to let go of my earthly tether, and enter the void. I have become one with the wind. If you do not understand of what I speak of,\nI shall explain in the simpler of speech. Through meditation my soul has left it's body and enter the void through which the spirits have given me ancient knowledge. In the book I shall write down what I have been taught so that it may be passed on to the\nworld for all the nations to hear.\n   \n         -Guru Pinya\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n\n Concerning the Soul\n\nEverytime we die, our souls leave our body and wander aimlessly around. The Monks of the Cloud Temple then collect our souls and our bodys and take them to be healed back together. However,\nI must say that when one has become a light into the dark world, and their duty has been fulfilled, their spirit will be given a new body and they will be reincarnated. This is called the Natural Order.\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n\n   Concerning the \n   Spiritual Powers\n\nEverything has a life-force inside of it. Some call it energy, some call it life, but I call it Magic. This magic is not from the void, or from a deity, but from onesel! Through\ndiscipline, and patience, one is able to harness their energy an extent, and use it for the wellbeings of others. Some examples of harnessing bodily Magic is using it do increase strength, speed, become unfamished, survive during a thirst,\nset things alight, preserve dying bodies, levitating small things, healing minor wounds, increasing senses, and entering the spirit world.\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n \n   Concerning the\n     Spirit World\n\nThe spirit world is like nothing the mortal eye has seen before. In it lies the Divine Hosts, the angels, the demons, the spirits, the gods, dead spiritual people, and some of the greatest people\nof all time. You might ask how these great people have gotten there. The answer is the Natural Order. When someone has made a great change in the world, their souls do not reincarnate themselves, but they enter into the spiritual world in the peace they\nhad so desired. To enter into peace is to live and die in peace.\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n\n    The Great Path\n\nTo enter into the realm of peace, one must live and die in peace. There are eight rules to peace, and they are:\n\nRight view, viewing reality as it is, and not how it is to be.\nRight intention, intention of renunciation, freedom and harmlessness.\n\nRight speech, speaking in a truthful, and non-hurtful way.\n\nRight action, acting in a non-harmful way.\nRight livelihood, living a non-harmful livelihood.\n\nRight effort, making an effort to improve.\n\nRight mindfulness, awareness to see things for what they are with a clear consciousness.\nRight concentration, correct meditation or concentration.\nWith the eight ways to peace said, I will now explain the four ideals. One must always hope that:\n\nAll sentient beings have happiness and it's causes.\n\nAll sentient beings be free of suffering and it's causes.\nAll sentient beings never be separated from bliss without suffering.\n\nAll sentient beings be in equanimity, free of bias, attachment and anger.\nIn the spirit world, for which I have named Tashe, meaning both the spiritual realm and the state of enlightenment, Tashe may be acquired by following the teachings of myself. If you wish to leave the cycle of reincarnation and suffering, please search\nfor me, Guru Pinya.\n((AntoniusLXIV))", ""),
        StaticBook("Monster Buddies", "Andrei", "Alright, Aberrang people are doing this monster-hunting stuff all wrong. They're going to kill themselves trying to kill this tree-thing. I've got a group that is far more experienced in these matters, and will be competent. Give your father's old pal a\ncall, and let's see if my group can run a few scouting missions for Haense.\n\n- Andrei \n\nPS: You've grown so tall since I last saw you!", ""),
        StaticBook("Monster Manual 1", "Ruffus Boffin", "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wCC-hLPmGGDjvxPaWdbrwDkgWVIZpQRXR1P_VlIhVT0/edit?usp=sharing", ""),
        StaticBook("Monster Manual 1", "Diane Farsight", "=+-+=\n    The Monster\n       Manual\n       =+-+=\n        \n\n        Volume 1\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Diane Farsight\nForeword\nThe world is a dark place, and it's filled with dark things. This book, and others like it, will hopefully inform you of what is out there, and how to deal with them. After all, Ignorance is a most insidious killer.\nThe Blob\n================\nDanger: Low\nDescription: Blobs are generally docile animals shaped like big piles of goo. Their size can vary greatly, but they tend not to surpass 6 feet in height. Their color varies, but will usually be\nbe the color of the enviornment they live in. Furthermore, they are covered in an outer layer of dry skin that protects them from extreme heat. Because of this, they are often found in hot climates. If enveloped by a blob, suffocation is the only way it\nkill you, as their bodies have no acidic properties.\nWeaknesses: Blobs are quite susceptable to cold, making Thanium a perfect weapon against them.\nCreation: Blobs can create more blobs by splitting themselves apart, creating two, smaller blobs.\nThe Ooze\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Oozes are the volitile cousin of blobs. They have the same shape and color, but can be much larger and territorial than their counterpart. Their size can become a staggering 5\nmeters in height, and their body produces a potent acid capable of dissolving flesh and metal alike. Also unlike blobs, Oozes prefer the cold, and lack the outer skin that blobs possess. If you ever need to tell an Ooze apart from a blob quickly, use your\nnose. Oozes will smell much more acrid.\nWeaknesses: Oozes are slow and notably flammable. The best way to deal with one is to set them alight, then run while they burn.\nCreation: Oozes can split themselves into more oozes, just like blobs.\nThe Giant Ooze\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: On occasion, there will be a sighting of a Gargantuan Ooze. Often they come from forgotten cave systems opened by earthquakes, or humanoids digging too deep. They are like\nOozes, but much larger- usually over 10 meters in size and capable of dissolving massive castle gates in a matter of minutes. Weaknesses: Fire will still kill gargantuan Oozes, but it is imperitave that you do not attempt to hide from them- there is\nalmost no stopping one if it begins chasing you.\nCreation: Unknown. Normal Oozes should split into smaller Oozes before reaching this size. It is hypothesized that extended time in cramped conditions underground allows an ooze to grow to this size.\nThe Flesh Worm\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: The tunnel worm is a subterranian monster of epic proportions. It's full length is unknown, but it is easily several meters in diameter. Most of it's life is spent boring\nholes in the earth for it to travel in, often straight through stone. A cave created by a Tunnel worm recently will always be perfectly circular, and ribbed to allow the tunnel worm to maneuver within it easily. It is hypothesized that the Underdark\nbeneath the dwarven lands of Anthos was sculpted by the errant burrowing of tunnel worms.\nWeaknesses: Any place that isn't perfectly fitted for it's body, such as large caverns or the surface.\nCreation: Unknown.\nThe Drake\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: A Drake is, in essence, a corrupted dragon, like those spoken of in legend. Unlike their bretheren, Drakes are much smaller in size and easier to defeat. Despite this, they\nare still capable of flying and breathing fire, and as a result require a large body of able men to be killed safely. When killed, a drake's body will dissolve entirely, but if one can manage to retrieve some of its scales without killing the beast, they\ncan be used to great effect in alchemy.\nWeaknesses: None.\nCreation: Legend has it that drakes are born when a dragon is overcome with taint. This, however, has never been witnessed.\nThe Alchemical\n       Chimera\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: An alchemical chimera is a fusion of two animals. It is truely an unnatural beast, created by a devious use of alchemy. Chimera come in all shapes and sizes,\nbut all will resemble the combination of two  natural beasts. They are mindless beasts, virtually untamable, and gluttonous for flesh.\nWeaknesses: : Time. A well created Chimera will last, at max, for 2 to 3 years.\nCreation: Alchemy.\nThe Dark Chimera ===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Through the use of drakkarian magic, the normal conditions for a chimera can be subverted, allowing for fully adult humans to be partially fused with parts hewn from\nanimals. The result is a fully intelligent, remarkably stable chimera. Many dark chimera are no more than victims of dark mages, but this is not always the case. Great care should be taken when dealing with one.\nWeaknesses: None\nCreation: Alchemy\nMixed with Drakkar Magic.\nThe Vodnik\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Vodnik are tiny, fish-like creatures that inhabit rivers and lakes. When vodnik encounter a corpse of any sort, they will begin filling and infesting it. The corpse will begin\nmoving of it's own accord, and begin dragging anything so foolish as to disturb it's water under with it, to become infested as well. Eventually, this process will crescendo until a small army of shambling corpses inhabit an area. This makes clearing\ndifficult.\nWeaknesses: Attacking the arms and legs of a vodnik-infested corpse is your best bet. Cutting off the head should have no effect.\nCreation: The Vodnik reproduce by laying eggs in the corpses they inhabit.\nThe Giant Crab\n===================Danger: High\nDescription: An enormous crab, about 15 meters across, 5 meters high, and chitin thicker than plate armor. If they see you, they will try to kill you. . They attack anything that moves,\nmembers of their own species included.\nWeaknesses: Their eyes are vulnerable, but should you lack for arrows you should try attacking their underbelly, or failing that, playing dead.\nCreation: Unknown. They certainly do not reproduce.\nThe Ghost\n===================\nDanger: Low\nDescription: A corporeal entity that is not yet ready to leave this world. Specters have several stages of 'unlife'. Stage one specters are always gray, and flit in and out of existance constantly.\nWhat seperates this stage from the others is the fact that, without fail, the spirit will not be able to come to terms with the fact that they are already dead. They usually need a large amount of persuasion and occaisonally hard evidence to make them\nrealize this. Stage two specters already realize that they are dead, and are able to begin learning to control their abilities more effectively. One of two things happen to stage three specters. They will either turn blue and become good, or turn red and\nbecome pure evil. This is usually in response to how well they were treated in their unlife, or how evil they were when they still lived. Powerful specters are capable of invisibility, minor manipulation of physical objects, and ejecting ectoplasm.\nWeaknesses: Spectres can be banished with a single swing of a weapon, especially holy and gold instruments. They can and will come back to life later, however. They are also unable to cross even the thinnest of gold lines.\nCreation: Spectres are\ncreated when someone dies, but cannot come to terms with their own passing. They become stuck betwixt.\nThe Graven\n===================\nDanger: High\nDescription: Graven are evil spirits who died carrying a great obsession in their hearts. As it drove them in life, so to  does it drive them in death.These spirits will wander the lands,\nendlessly pursuing their unattainable goal, and the pursuit of that goal itself becomes the very fuel that keeps them alive. Above all else, do not look a Graven in the eye. Their eyes are portals into their maddened soul, and will instill a lasting\nmadness into the hearts of those who see it.\nWeaknesses: A graven can be banished easily with any weapon, but is particularly susceptable to gold, and holy objects. Likewise, they are unable to cross any line made of gold. In special\ncircumstances, is also possible to banish them forever by completing the task that drives their madness.\nCreation: Gravens are created when a truely obsessed person meets an untimely demise.\nThe Apparition\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: An apparition is an amalgation of many, many lost spirits combined for one purpose, and that purpose is pure evil. Apparitions are malicious, and very dangerous to fight.\nThey are capable of incredible acts of telekinesis and illusion, beyond what any living mage could ever accomplish. Normally, apparitions are bound to a central pillar, marked by many skulls and skeletons littering the area around it. If you come across\none such pillar, is vitally important that you DO NOT DAMAGE THE PILLAR IN ANY WAY, SHAPE, OR FORM. Destroying the pillar will weaken the beast temporarily, but afterwards it will be able to roam the world at large, bringing great chaos in it's wake.\nWeaknesses: An apparition is significantly more powerful than a spirit. The use of gold weaponry can keep it at bay, but the banishment itself lasts only mere moments. Only a very thick ring of gold can contain it. The only way to kill them\npermanently is through the aid of a team of Clerics or Shamen\nCreation: The exact origin of Apparitions is murky. From what can be gathered, they are formed from the death of many individuals in one place, at the same time.\nThe Boogeyman\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Yes, the boogeyman is real. Well, was real. The only known boogieman is currently dead. Boogeyman are sentient collections of bugs that swarm around a central corpse. Based on\non the only known boogeyman's example, boogiemen are intelligent, and extremely murderous, taking pleasure in killing innocents. When endangered, the bugs inside the boogieman will scatter in all directions. Because of this, when hunting the Boogiemen it\nis imperative that you take him by suprise.\nWeaknesses: Boogeymen are weak to fire, and crushing implements. Gold hurts it, but a sword will not have much effect on the swarm.\nCreation: Unknown.\nThe Oolog\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: The Olog  is roughly twice the size of an orc, and  nearly three times as stupid. A product of large amounts of orcish inbreeding, Ologs were raised for having muscle and size,\nand their bodies show it. Still descendant of Orcs, they also are capable of bloodraging, making them twice as dangerous.\nWeaknesses: Ologs are stupid. I mean, really stupid. Use that to your advantage.\nCreation: These creatures are\n(loosely) considered Natural' beasts, and reproduce normally.\nConclusion\n\nThis book has merely scratched the surface of what lurks in the night. Expect more books in the furture.\nStay Alive, Atheria.", ""),
        StaticBook("Monster Manual 1", "Bolon Stormtaker", "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1wCC-hLPmGGDjvxPaWdbrwDkgWVIZpQRXR1P_VlIhVT0/edit?usp=sharing\n\n[!] Copy of Ruffus Boffin's\nbook 'Monster Manual 1\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Morality V:I", "Theon Mallister", "Human Morality V:I\nIf the entire human species were a single individual, that person would long ago have been declared mad. The insanity would not lie in the anger and darkness of the human mind—though it can be a black and raging place indeed.\nAnd it certainly wouldn't lie in the transcendent goodness of that mind—one so sublime, we fold it into a larger \"soul\".  The madness would lie instead in the fact that both of those qualities, the savage and the splendid,\ncan exist in one creature, one person, often in one instant.\n\nWe're a species that is capable of almost dumbfounding kindness. We nurse one another, romance one another, weep for one another.\nWe're the only species with language, we told ourselves—until gorillas and chimps mastered sign language. Until cats could walk and talk. Khas, they call themselves. We're the only one that uses tools then—but that's if you don't\ncount otters smashing mollusks with rocks or apes stripping leaves from twigs and using them to fish for termites.\nWhat does, or ought to, separate us then is our highly developed sense of morality, a primal understanding of good and bad\nof right and wrong, of what it means to suffer not only our own pain—something anything with a rudimentary nervous system can do—but also the pain of others. That quality is the distilled essence of what it means to be human.\nWhy it's an essence that so often spoils, no one can say.\n\nMorality may be a hard concept to grasp, but we acquire it fast. A preschooler will learn that it's not all right to eat in the classroom, because the teacher says it's not.\nIf the rule is lifted and eating is approved, the child will happily comply. But if the same teacher says it's also O.K. to push another student off a chair, the child hesitates. He'll respond, 'No, the teacher shouldn't say that.'\nIn both cases, somebody taught the child a rule, but the rule against pushing has a stickiness about it, one that resists coming unstuck even if someone in authority countenances it. That's the difference between a matter of morality and\none of mere social convention.\nOf course, the fact is, that child will sometimes hit and won't feel particularly bad about it either—unless he's caught. The same is true for people who steal or despots who slaughter.", ""),
        StaticBook("Morgan's Poison", "Morgan Hallowfall", "Alchemical Index\n================This is the Alchemical Index, in this tome contains alchemical recipes that can be used by many after gathering the required materials\n===================\n2. Morgan's Poison:\nDescription:\nAn easily constructed poison that can be applied to weapons or food sources.\n\nForenote: Has to enter the body by some method be it injection (slicing etc) Or poisoning drink/food.\nDetails:\nGreen coloured in colouration with a strong spice for an odour.\n\nEquipment:\nMortar and Pestle\nStrong Aqua Vitae\nContainer, e.g. Vial\nIngredients & Recipe:\nMortar and Pestle required!\n-Two crushed Alabaster Leaves\n-One crushed piece of Saffvil\n-Grounded Serpent's stalk\n==================\nMix all together and dry, once dried out mix in Aqua Vitae and leave for 2 hours\nA successful concoction should have a pale green tinge and smell of strong spices once completed.\n\nFor further information about the effects, look on the next page\nEffects:\n-Kills biological matter inside the body\n\n-Burning Sensation, causes nausea and heavy sickness\n\n-Two vials worth entering body would most likely end with death\nEffects page 2:\n\n-Motor functions in the body will cease up causing contractions in the effected area, which could be potentially quite painful\n\n-Effects occur after 2-3 minutes after 'injection'\n((OOC))\nEffects take 3-4 emotes to take effect (depending on if it was directly injected into e.g. neck or something along those lines)", ""),
        StaticBook("Morghouls", "An Elder Cleric", "A Guide To\n        Morghouls\n\n\n\n            By\n     An Elder Cleric\nIntroduction\n\nA shuffling moan against the walls of the city of your nation, clanking steel and flies buzzing around an animated corpse...\n\nA short pause, as it's unseeing eyes dig into your very soul.\nIntroduction\n\nDear Reader, by now certainly you have steeled yourself for what is within this book. Know now, that any amount of discomfort you gain from reading this will be worth the knowledge you shall gain, knowledge that may save you.\nIdentifying\n\nMorghouls are corpses that have been raised by Necromancers. They are in a constant state of decay, making their bodies emit a pungent odor of death and rot.\nIdentifying\n\nThey will try to hide their form, utilizing masks and hoods. However, their sluggish movements and slurred speech are tell-tale signs of a rotting body underneath. They also avoid the light, as well as aurum.\nStrengths\n\nLike all undead creatures, Morghouls have transcended death, becoming immortal figures that exist by consuming life force. They feel no fatigue, and can fight without respite until they are victorious or defeated.\nStrengths\n\nBecause they are a mere corpse, they are able to exist even after taking wounds that would put down a mortal, such as a limb being lost. They are also unaffected by taint and corruption, as they are such themselves.\nWeaknesses\n\nLike most undead creatures that require life force to exist, they hunger it. While they can undertake substantial blows, a swift blow to the skull or decapitation will kill one.\nWeaknesses\n\nBeing an undead corpse, they are extremely weak to Aurum, Holy Magic, and fire. They are also unable to wear heavy armor nor wield anything more than an iron long sword as they are weaker than mortals with muscles.\nTemperment\n\nA Morghoul that is fed on life force is able to control its behavior to an extent, giving illusion to others that is is simply a shady character. They will often hold little to no emotion for the living, and show no remorse.\nConclusion\n\nIn conclusion, Morghouls are the basic Undead creature, meaning you'll encounter this more commonly than others. Prepare yourself with aurum or blessed weaponry and aim to decapitate them for a quick kill.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mortal Curiosity", "Enduren of Old", "Once long ago, I saw faith as a thing unique to the descendants.  I watched as they raised great temples in the names of usurpurs and fools.  I swore to myself I would not fall into the same trap.\n\nAnd yet, time changes us all.  I had found a place among\nthe ranks of the dead.  I found fellowship in the Lordsmarch, and peace in the City of the Dead.  It is a shame that the Starving Ghoul had to go and ruin it all.\n\nThe dead do not belong behind walls.  They are a thing of men, and try as we might, we will\nnever be men.  Only under the banner of death will mortalkind be united.  Only when the curses are undone will man and elf, dwarf and orc stand united.\n\nThe Gravelords may have been lost, and yet I still have faith.  The Crowned Lich has fallen to ruin,\nand yet I still have faith.  The Black Sun is shattered and broken, and yet I still have faith.\n\nI believe in the visions of the Lords.  I believe in the work of the Fallen Dragon.  I believe in a world united, with the curses of old undone.  One day\nmortalkind will find a land, a true home that will last until the ages.\n\nUntil that day comes, I will have faith.\n\n~Enduren of Old", ""),
        StaticBook("Mother Nature", "Zyvia Ba'ikana", "She ran, the world under her feet. Her feet were bare, and she could feel everything. The rotation of the earth and the sun’s movements into darkness were all known to her. She smiled knowingly to the sky, the wind running its hands through her hair.\nShe felt the bees nursing flowers, seeds digging themselves deep into the earth. Above all, she felt the blades of grass beneath her, tearing up the soles of her feet. She paused before her next step, tears flowing from her eyes.\nThe steady streams of water flooded the valleys and plains around her, creating lakes, streams and waterfalls. Pieces of her hair drifted to the ground, each taking root. These roots blossomed into trees, surrounding her and comforting her.\nAs if on cue, vines encircled her ankles, pulling her into the dirt’s warm embrace. It created a home for her, coddling her like a small child. She became one with nature. Some say she even became nature itself.\nThese were the ages before the taint destroyed our mother. These were the wonderful years of innocence.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mother's Mark", "Guyden Aureon", "~*~The Mother's~*~\n          Mark\n\nScribed by the Willow Druid.\n\nCreated by the Hawk Druid.\nWear upon your skin the mark of the mother if ye be one who tends to the feeble. If ye be a master of the cauldron, and guardian of the sick.\n\nThe mother's mark is a flesh inking as well, the mirror of the Father’s mark. It is for any and all of the\nAspectist rite whom consider themselves caretakers and healers.\n\nThe mother's mark is teal, like spring water. It may twist like a river or bloom into floral patterns and pomegranate domes, the sacred symbol of the green lady Cerridwen. The mark\nmust be worn either upon the face or upon the hands of the healing touch. To wear the mark of the Mother is to honour the lady of life. To display your allegiance to your people and your people's faith by designating yourself both as a worshipper of the\nold Aspectist rite, and a healer.\nThe Mother's Essence\n\nIf ye be a healer of the old rite, carry upon you a flask containing the waters of an attunement spring. Drink but a few drops before applying your healing hands to the sick and needy, and let the Green Lady bless you with her\nsacred essense.\n\nThe mother's essense is a vial of springwater to be carried upon the person of an Aspectist healer at all times. The water gleamed from an attunement pool of a druidic grove is the symbolic manifestation of the spirit and faith within our\nhearts, and when consumed, imbues us with the blessing of the Mother, and instills compassion and gentleness in our hearts when we tend to the injured, the sick, the old, and the young.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mountain Dwarves", "Nerah", "The grand Mountain Dwarves, originally hailing from the mountains to far north of Aegis, are known to be stalwart defenders of their cities. They came to be when a number of Urguan's sons chose to leave Kal'Urguan and instead live apart from\ntheir Cave Dwarven kin. Although unlike their underground living brethren, they stand strong on land and defend their cities and villages with strong arms and axes. Although better using an axe in combat and lumberjacking than their Dwarven brothers,\nMountain Dwarves are not quite as good miners. Mountain Dwarves generally have ginger, blonde, light brown or fiery red hair. Their skin is lighter than other Dwarves, sometimes tanned. Eye colours tend to be ordinary shades of blue, brown or green.\nThey have strong, tall builds with muscled shoulders from living in harsh enviroments. Many also cover themselves in ritual war paints. Their toughness and discipline means many make good warriors.\nGenerally, Mountain Dwarves are adventurous and welcome outsiders of other races. They are usually cheerful with a good sense of humour. They take history and traditions seriously,\nusually expressed through song, tales and poetry. Often they are more willing to accept change than other Dwarves.\nLike most Dwarves they follow a strict code of honour, which has developed over years of living amongst surface dwellers.\nand through wars with Orcs. Rites of passage include killing and skinning Orcs, taking their tusks or claiming the ears of Elves. Many Mountain Dwarves claim trophies after battle, either material goods taken or parts of dead enemies themselves.\nThey make excellent hunters, although Mountain Dwarves cannot see well in the dark. They are also good storytellers and among the best Dwarven writers, as they grow up surrounded by myths and legends. They are also highly sought after as lumberjacks.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mundane Healing", "hex37", "__Mundane Healing: The treatment of minor wounds with common herbs.__\n\nNienna’s Foreword: When I was studying medicine in Oren, a strange dwarf brought me with a book of medical recipes that used very common ingredients for the\ntreatment of various medical casualties, by an Aleya Darolien. One or two of them sounded interesting, though a large amount of them were, largely ridiculous, like one that claimed it possible to heal a major burst of an artery or internal organs with\nnothing but rose thorns and petals. In the interest of not wasting precious paper, I’ve recorded some of the more practical recipes in the book, and added one or two of my own, to make up for lost space.\n-Minor Cut (Nienna)\nSimply apply a dose of  deceased Sentient-Slime to the affected area, and wrap a light bandage around it.  The slime helps stop the bleeding, and the mildly acidic nature of it is known to remove the taint from a body.\n-Headache (Aleya)\nBoil milk. Add honey while the milk boils. Take Dandelion stems and Rose thorns and put them in a thin satchel. Dip the satchel in the milk and let it infuse with the mixture for about 2 minutes. Slowly drink the milk.\n-Stomach Ache (Nienna)\nBoil water. Once it hits a full broil, add honey until the liquid turns an amber color. Add tea leaves to a small bag, and let it soak in the mixture for about five minutes. Drink the tea slowly.\n-Soreness (Aleya)\nSimply apply rags with hot water to relax the muscles, and rest a lot.\n-Burns (Nienna)\nSet your hands on some vinegar, and drench a clean bandage with it. Apply this bandage to the affected area, and wrap a dry bandage around this to keep the vinegar from getting absolutely everywhere. The important thing about\nburns is to keep the affected area moist while it mends, as burned areas do not produce sweat properly. Vinegar is ideal for this, as it will keep the area moist, and not evaporate as water would. Be sure to check and clean the burn wound daily until the\nskin can finally reform.\n-Fever (Aleya)\nKeep the victim’s body cool using cold water. Give him hot milk steeped with brown mushroom stems and ground rose thorns. It will fight off the disease. Keep the victim rested and feed him mushroom soup.", ""),
        StaticBook("Music Vol. 1", "Evelynn Shards", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n \nThe  Sound  Of  Music\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n \nSix songs each book.\nSelf made songs and there will be more soon!\n-------------------Written by Evelynn Shards\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Page 3: The Sun Parade\nPage 4: Into Nature's Beauty\nPage 5: Lights Will Guide Us\nPage 6: All Of Us \nPage 7: Praise Our Emperor\nPage 8: Fire\n-------------------\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-The Sun Parade\n\nIt shall start soon. Our king will praise our sister, the sun...\nAnd when the light shall raise, the sword will light up. Few people to hold back. Only one Elven day shall this happen. I-its the Sun.\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Into Nature's Beauty\n\nIf you would walk into the wild and open forest. No human to see. Wide open space full of trees, animals everywhere to be seen. A small rabbit would run in the grass. An owl to fly over. Just too much..\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=- Lights Will Guide Us\n\nWhen night falls over the town. Lights will raise from upon the sky. Thou shall form one long line. Just for us to follow. They shall guide us home, and to a better place. Keep on searching to there...\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-All Of Us\n\nImagine if our God. Would be down here with us. Nobody to know anything. He built cities all over the world. Nobody to notice anything. Though everybody was happy. All of us were...\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Praise The Emperor\n\nOh, misty forest, filled with ghosts and monsters. The plains ruled by our Emperor. May our Emperor be praised. Oh, praise the Emperor (x2) He makes us happy, gives us good advice. Who doesnt honour him?\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-            Fire\n\nI see fire. In the trees going over to the houses. Licking the air like a cat. Burning down towns and forests. The fire needs to be destroyed. It needs to stay small, and keep us warm..", ""),
        StaticBook("My D-Tool", "TheNander", "*The book seems to have been printed in large quantities for the Dwarven Legion.*\n\nThis is my D-Tool. There are many like it, but this one is mine. My D-Tool is my best friend. It is my life. I must master it as I must master my life.\nMy D-Tool, without me, is useless. Without my D-Tool, I am useless. I must use my D-Tool true. I must use it better than my enemy who is trying to kill me. I must cut him before he cuts me. I will...\nMy D-Tool and I know that what counts in this war is not the enemies we decapitate, the noise of our brothers, or the holes we dig. We know that it is the hits that count. We will hit...\nMy D-Tool is Dwarven, even as I, because it is my life. Thus, I will learn it as a brother. I will learn its weaknesses, its strength, its parts, its accessories, its blade and its handle. I will keep my D-Tool sharp and ready, even as I am sharp and\nready. We will become part of each other. We will... \n\nBefore Yemekar, I swear this creed. My D-Tool and I are the defenders of my Kingdom. We are the masters of our enemy. We are the saviors of my life.\nSo be it, until victory is The Kingdom of Urguan's and there is no enemy, but peace!\n\n- Nalro Grayhammer", ""),
        StaticBook("My Deepest Fears", "Hobbs_Burrows", "10, Sun's Smile, 1656\n\nMy deepest fears have come true. I was kidding myself the past few days, telling myself it couldn't possibly be the one. How could it be? After all these years?\n\nThe Tankard of Terror has returned.\nThe discovery has hit me with the force of a thousand oak shovels. Should I tell the villagers of Dunshire? Or should I carry the burden of terror myself? No, they have to know. This is what this book is for.\n\nLet me tell you, dear reader, about the\nTankard To Rule Them All. \n\nIn Branborough days, 6 elven years ago, Petyr Brandybuck suddenly declared he was leaving one evening, and by sunrise his burrow was empty. He was off on an unknown adventure somewhere.\nMany months passed and we feared him dead, until one day we found a halfling having a lonely drink in The Drunken Sheep Inn. No one spoke to him, he looked filthy and like he hadn't slept a wink in weeks. \n\nWell it was only Petyr returned from\nhis adventure, but he weren't quite the same. He never was the same Petyr again, in fact. \n\nYou see, the Tankard changes a halfling. It's unknown what powers it truly contains, Petyr didn't want to talk about it. His quest was successful though, he used\npowerful magic to ensure the safety of the Tankard of Terror and subdue its power. For that reason, we mounted it above the Inn's fireplace as a trophy.\n\nUntil it went missing.\n\nYet the other day I learned from Madeline\nof a Halfling who drank from a tankard which compelled him to drink and drink until his body could take no more, and he perished. \n\nThat is when alarm bells started ringing for me. Had the Tankard found its way back to us?\nAnd then the evil Ent Sefirot, whose wicked and twisted roots lead me to this cavern, appeared on the shores of Lake Dunshire. The two had to be connected. \n\nThen with trembling knees, armed with only a shovel and my wits, I confronted the Tankard\nhere. I dare not go much closer than this.\n\nDo not touch it, do not drink from it, do not dream of what powers it could grant you.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Love", "Celaena Annungilben", "My love,\nI am sorry to leave things as they are, however I have to put an end to Katrina's ambitions, as her former friend and Ivae'Fenn concerned for the safety of her nation. However in order to do this, I have to cut all ties with Fenn... By the time\nyou recieve this, I will be 'dead'. I will have left Fenn under a new name, appearance, with the sole goal of putting an end to the rebellion without putting Fenn at risk with ties... As such, it will be at least a year until I can return home. However,\nI can still see you if you send a bird and I can either sneak to a meeting place, or perhaps Fenn, although this is not prefered. I am sorry to leave you so abruptly, love, and I hope you can forgive me, however it seems to be the only way to prevent what\nKatrina and the Empire seek to unleash upon Fenn... They are beyond overthrowing Aelthir, they want to start another genocide...\nI hope you can find the will to forgive me for this, however if you decide to move on without me, I understand. I would not\nwish to put you through what I experienced in waiting for your return, unknowing if you would come home or not. Thank you for everything my love, and I will miss you.\nLove,\nCelaena", ""),
        StaticBook("My Return", "Wargoth Malog'Yar", "These past several years mi have been on pilgrimage. It was nub a pilgrimage to any particular holy place or shrine, but was rather a sacred wandering of sorts. Mi explored wild and uninhabited places, and further hardened mi already thick hide.\n Mi\nhave meditated atop the highest peaks of frozen mountains. Mi have trod the scorched earth of volcanic regions where the air is clouded with smoke agh ash. Mi have stalked through the underbrush of mi people's jungles, braving the dangers of the many\npredators thereof.\n In mi travels, mi have observed the skies by morning, listened to the voice of the wind by day, gazed into fires by evening, agh dreamed both wonderous agh terrible dreams by night. All of existence, both waking agh sleepeing, blah to\nmi. The spirits guide mi through the stars agh moon, agh drive mi on through the sun. They whisper in the grass of the fields agh murmur in the caves. The waves of the sea shout to they who listen.\n Mi return this day from mi pilgrimage to find mi people\nscattered, agh their blargs empty. The streets are silent. The walls have been thrown down. Just as well though. I hated that goi. The orcs have done far hosher. San'Orca; San'Vitar; Kodar'goi; San'Thraka. These were gois worthy of Krug!\n Still though, mi\nbrothers agh sisters are left without a land. The sharas mouth boastful things in their perpetual arrogance, agh their wood albai whores have spat on the shadow of Enrohk  by stretching their hands out against his shrines. Darûkûrz bûbri, afar angathfark\nagh vadokanuk, ashdautus vrasubatlat! All who read this, heed those words. Let them be the words of all the Orcish people. Gruk them agh lock them in lats spirit.\n Meanwhile, the spirit realm screams, agh the bub'hosh powers of the universe shift. Mi\nhear the moaning agh creaking of all reality in mi sleep. The h'ash arms have fallen. Such is the price of betrayal, though mi blah it with a heavy soul. Those arms could have upheld us for all eternity, had carelessness nub taken hold of our Rex. Kharak\nwas a fine Rex, but his ambition outgrew his wisdom. Now, that which brought us such power has been layed low, agh we suffer for it. The powers with which he played are not toys, agh Orgon is nub a howler on a leesh. Had he gruk'd that sooner, things\nwould still be as they ought to be. Let all living shamans learn from his error, agh excercize due caution when wielding such power.\n Now, Kinul stands where mi old master agh the giver of mi sight once stood. These days weigh heavily on mi bones. Now,\nhowever, is nub a time to mourn. Now is the time to steel ourselves. We are nub as the sharas, who live on through their gois agh land. Wi are nub as the albai, who grow fat at the trough of comfort agh luxury. We are nub as the gazat, who hole up in\ncaves, agh find their security in riches. We are the orcs, the cubs of Krug. Our strength is to be found in hardship agh trial. \n Since the days of the Ancients, our kind has fought for every morsel of food; every cup of water; every inch of land;\nevery breath of air; agh every second of existence. These days are nub to be lamented, but rather let us stand tall as ever. Let us remember who we are. These days are not a grave to lie down in. They are a crucible to purify us. They are a fire to harden\nour skins.\n We are the uruk, the goblins, agh the ologs. We are the cubs of Krug. We are the orcs. Look upon lats ancestors, brothers agh sisters, agh shout proudly. Raise lats lusks, lats zults, lats o'ligs, agh lats fists. Bare lats tusks, stand atop\nthe bloody agh broken heaps of lats enemies, agh roar. For the spirits. For the Ancestors. For Krug!\n -Malog, Wargoth of the Yar Clan.\n 7th of The Grand Harvest, 1583.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Struggle", "Kaiser Decimus Rovin, Vandalore", "====Heil Valdoria==== \n\n\n\n     The Rise of the\n     Colored Kingdoms\n\n\n    \n        Approved by\n   The Reich Ministry\n          Of Truth\nForeward\n\nThe treatise of which follows this breif forward has been legislated upon the direct mandate of the Kaiser and his white sons. It is all very scientific, you see. Praise the Kaiser and hail the White Flame.\nSince his inception, the race of man has proved his superiority over the lesser kindred time and time again, and thus, it is undoubtedly proven by science that man is Kaiser's chosen race. There is no question in the matter, for man and only man possesses\nthe conviction and blessing to mold a mighty empire, forged from the frisson of today, and supported on all facets by our pure ancestors. The dubious assertion against our one and true God and his honor guards is that of defeatist and Serenist dogmatic\npestilence, inseminated from the vile gasses of hell and popagated by the black worms and Kharadeen sympathizers. Man is true. Man is Kaiser's chosen disciple, and let his superior and engorged-gargantuan loins deluge the slime of elgenism and defeatism\nfrom our seed. All hail Kaiser's seed and immaculate fluids.\n\nAs of thus far, the intent of our father is rather opague, but within the contents of this binding of which follows, all his glory and prowess will be clear. For one to question the prowess\nor glory of our Lordi s blasphemy. Which despite punishment by which of means which shall be shined upon in further detail in at a further period, blasphemy is a sin. Thus, if one were to follow with utmost punctuality, he would find that the treatise\nof which I have been bestowed the pious and ethereal act of concieving is in fact the unwavering voice of Kaiser. It is all very scientific, and though I doubt one may absorb his excellence with ease, for his excellence is that of an infinite well of\ngolden wine, I advise one suckle at my knowledge with great heed. One must not tug nor bite when contracting the teat of Kaiser, one must priase him with a sublt pursuing, for only then will his grace seep at a rate conceivable by his sons.\nThe Sprouting of Man\n\n   The history of man is that of great piety and virtue. In practically all corners of our realm, man's raw exuberance is sown deep within the heart of the Kaiser's Seed, and his mighty, booming prowess can be felt in each and\nevery heart of all who inhabit it. Man has fought with many breeds in his legacy, and man still remains, but not as a refugee or vagabond. Man has survived in a fashion comparable to a seed of iron-wood oak, for his blessing lay deep within the soil,\ndormant but with pride, and when time comes and the Kaiser commands the man to grow, to build, to conquer, then and only then is mans' pride as palpable as the Kaiser's own. \n   Our race emerges from the remains of lesser breeds, fueled by the purity of\nhis white pride and the blessings of our Lord and Savior. All the way he spourts, man takes most attentiveness to his every direction, constantly and diligently enforcing his prowess, his muscles of pure force bulge and pulsate under the immense pressure\nof his pride. It appears that no force could ever discourse his destined and premeditated path, for man will ascend until his most superior of faculties scrapes the heavens and is once again reunited with his benevolent father. \n   His roots at which\npoint cleave deep into the blackened earth, for the front of darkness ever will seep into our fluids. Thus we must fight, we must never, as a hope, as a dream, we must never be diluted by the inferior vestigial corpses of the damned races. And as man's\ngreat limbs spread with unmeasurable force and national pride, the worms of the black sludge will begine to fester. They cross into our realm illegally, without the blessing of the Kaiser, and they burrow deep within our cavities. The very seeds of our\npride have been sabotaged! They feast upon our flesh and excrete tar from their pores. They fester and slosh in such ooze and amass great pits of darkness. They brred with no grace or consent, they feed with glutionous intent, and they spread the foul\nlies of their filthy heathen, sub-humanist Ebolinism.\n   As the sludge of the black worms collects deep within our bowels and extremities, the flame of our brethren begins to fade. The skin of a once pure race will blacken under the tremendous, bloated\nweight of the pestilent bog, and our great minds which once yielded the venerated sciences and arts will rot and drain through our facial cavities. Soon, if we continue on our path so grossly discourse from the Kaiser's will our own beautiful race will no\nlonger be even remotely recognizeable. We will be diluted to a state so impoverished and emaciated of all pride that we will have not even the conviction to cognate the most primal of tasks. We will at this point be that of which we have fought, we will\nbe all which we have feared. We will be the elfen. \n   But alas, this is not the course of man. Man will never be so easily dissolved by such spurious doctrine, for man is the direct fluid of the Holy One, the Creator, The one true hope for the salvation\nfor nationalism and pride. So my dear white brothers, we must show the Kaiser that we are worthy. We must prove to him that we as a hope, as a dream for all that is pure in this realm, the man has not and never will forget his divine quest! Let us\nimpale the rotten flesh with scolding-bladed tapes and drain the fetis wastes from our cavities! Let us carve out the filthy conspirators and blackened worm colonies, from each and every facet of our impenetrable bark of hardened iron!\nLet us Fight, my brothers! Let us fight for the salvation of the Kaiser and his seeds!\nThe Salvation of the Kaiser\n\nPraise He, the one and only, the true voice of good in a realm so corroded by the acrid sins of the lesser races. Praise he whose might and sheer dauntlessness shall cleanse the arachnids of pit and moss, he who\nshall save our white souls from the vile feces of Ebolnism and the Serenist web. Praise he who shall and forever will be the one and the only true God, praise our Lord and our grandest of Kings. All Praise the Kaiser!\n   Praise our blessed hearth, for in\nhis glorious egg lay a seed, a hope, a dream for a world of white fire. All hail the flame of God and King, praise the fervent inferno of cleansing, and let it smolder in the hearts of each and every white man, for now and ever. For us, let the flame\nguide us, let it illuminate the blackened path into oblivion, the shady death march speckled with infected warts of flesh and pus and other such fecal jellies, that of which spawn the prickly seeds of the Degenerate race and the Serenist arachnids.\nBut alas, have not fear my fellow white brothers. Praiser the Kaiser, for through his wisdom may we purge the septic grubs with flame and gas. Let our nationalism and tenacious pride obliterate their weak and feeble and highly demonic colonies. Let our\nwhite flame raze each and every festering cesspit from which they spawn, and let us forcefully enter their diseased posterior cavities in the name of the glorious Kaiser.\n======================================\n\n\n  The Struggle of Our\n    Nation and Great\n         Charter Of\n        Vanderkind\n\n\n\n\n=====================================\nFor the glory of a great nation is to kinder the white flame of our ancestors, the divine right of our Kings, and the holy grace of our one true God. \n\nIn the wake of war and the feckless sheeding of national pride through the unrelenting plot of\nSerenist Ebliontologists in coalition with Communist doctrine, only the few, so the Kaiser wills it, only the most true and pure will survive the coming fire of the primal apocalypses. So when we, as a people, as a hope, must ask why it is that the\nof the black worms in our governments and in the highest and most divine of positions in the high counsel have become so, we must ask ourselves instead why it is that the inferior races have rejected the pious might of the one true Lord and Savior.\nThis is why we must act, for the sake of all that is holy and for the propsperity of culture and civilization, and only through the social rec-construction of our deprived filth of elfen lies and slime can we regain the trust of the Kaiser and pray for\nhis forgiveness.\n\n===The Grace Of===\n====The Kaiser====\n\nAll haill thee who flows water into our rivers, plants seeds, into our soil, delivers bread to our bellies and children to our kindred. Blessed thee, our one true Lord, who in the grace of love\nand pious does he who impregnates the seed of life to our loins and the fires of national pride into our hearts. The Kaiser, in all his glory, is the one and true God, for he and only he is divine and pure. \n\nHowever the Kaiser is displeased with\nour existence. For ages, the Serenists, the enemy of all that is good and beautiful, has festered at the hearts of our brothers. They have plagued the grace and purity of the ethereal and pure Vanders, the one true race, and they have spilled their seeds\namongst the black and sodomite flesh of the negarious degenerate race. Our Savior is furious. He holds our fate in that of which is a thread over the boiling pits of Iblees' grasp. Only his will remains as our salvation, and we have allowed it to be\nspilled out of the crucible of the one, the pure race of men. We have enabled the impure to breed for far too long.\n====The Love====\n===Of the Rector===\n\nIt is the will of the divine right of the RTector and his unfathomable purity to protect the soverignty and pride of our nation, and so it be, the glory of our nation is now buckling under the weight of the\nglutenous elfen conspiracy. Only through the love of Priorism, the one true ideology, can the love and passion of the Kaiser be felt deep within our cavities. heil the Grandmaster, for through his divine right shall we drink the blood of all who oppose\nthe might and prowess of Saradomin and his belssings upon the grace of our nation and the love of our fathers.\n===The Blessings===\n==Of Our Fathers==\n\nLoveth thee who drained the swamps, chiseled the stone, impregnated the woman and filled the Kaiser's realm with the seed of the pure men and his Birthright to Gielinor. Only through the love of our fathers\nmay our seeds be spread into the wombs of the Kaiser's purity, and therefore, the mothers of our race shall be pure. May we suckle from his teat, and love his divine will until the time of departure to the realm of the Kaiser. All hail the Kaiser and the\nfathers of our seed.\n\nIf not for the will of the Kaiser, in all of his blessed glory, shall we dictate his grace amonst the scum races of our plagued realm. Let us Educate the feeble and lost in the glory of national pride and save them from the repugnant\nsludge of Serenism. Let us feed the bellies of the poor with the love fluids of god's seed. Let us forge from the ashes of the quarreling micronations a golden utopia of the pure and strong, and let us sow the seeds of the New World Order.", "")
    )

    private fun _ATLAS_4(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Mysterious Note", "???", "Take the Skeever's the the tavern, I want them out of business by the end of the harvesting year! Your payments been delivered.\n-- P.C.", ""),
        StaticBook("N.VonSchlitchten", "Nitholiak VonSchlitchten", "Selected Writings\n           of\n       Nitholiak\n    VonSchlichten\n\nN. VonSchlichten owned the famous VonSchlitchten inn outside of Al'Khazar, a common haunt for the magically inclined, both dark and light.\nPotions and Alchemy: Dyes\n\nThe ability to brew potions is an important skill to many who study the arcane arts. There is a common misconception that Dyes are the easiest of these potions\nand requires little still. To the contrary Dyes are a great example to showcase the fundamentals of Alchemy. In order to produce potions you will need an alchemy set. Including a burner whose flame can burn at ranges from red to blue.\nThe color of the flame is important to extract the coloring essences of the dye ingredients. The Some materials may be transfigured together to form a new dye. For example, Bone Meal is one of the most versatile magical dye ingredients.\nIt lightens and brightens the host color to form rare and valuable dyes. Do not attempt to do such transfiguration unless you are comfortable with working with base dyes.\nPotions and Alchemy: Elixirs\n\nAfter Dyes, the next most complex type of potion is an elixir. However, the learning curve with alchemy slopes up in this step.\nElixirs are the first type of beneficial potion that will grant yourself immediate increases to areas you feel weak in. Elixirs of Strength improve your overall physical strength.\nElixirs of Agility allow you to become more flexible and move quickly. Elixirs of Wisdom open up the mind new new ideas. These effects sound almost too good to be true. Skilled alchemists have brewed elixirs that can make a weak man lift boulders,\na fool study the stars and a turtle sprint. But there are drawbacks to these blessings. To start, all effects are temporary. The elixirs will wear off after a certain time. Next, the elixirs depend on their alchemist's skill.\nA novice alchemist's elixir may work for 5 minutes. While a potions master can make the same elixir last for days. Third, to become comfortable enough with alchemy to attempt elixirs is a long journey. Brewing dyes is an easily learned skill.\nBut as said before, elixirs require even greater skill. To be a master of dyes, to know every detail and nuance of the art will put you into a junior novice experience level with elixirs. Brew your potions well my friends.\nObservations of the Phantasmal\n\nI entered the Inn very unaware. The Inn that lay above my store in AlKhazar has been experiencing bizarre phenomenon. Blue Sheep appeared out of nowhere.\nI rushed to Dawn's bakery/inn to see what was happening Webs were being flung across the dining room like snowballs by some unseen force. an old colleague of mine claimed it was a ghost. I did detect the precence of someone no longer there with us.\nOne of those in the Inn cursed at the ghost. The phantom was having fun it seemed. Chickens started to appear in one of the rooms of Dawn's Inn. Then Wolves. Things took a turn for the darker when deadly spiders started to show their face.\nThen the poltergeist was no longer happy Room 5# of the Inn bust into flames. It risked spreading to my own shop on the street. Just as soon as it all started, it stopped. I will continue to analyze traces of phantasmal energy and find our who..\n.or what this was. Zombies now spawn from the same room. It seems Room #5 is haunted.\nor what this was. Zombies now spawn from the same room. It seems Room #5 is haunted.\nMyths About the Undead\n\nWith the rise of the Undead the citizens of Aegis are more in danger of misinformation than the Undead themselves. Being armed with the best knowledge guarantees better chances of survival.\nMyth: The Undead are mindless drones. Answer: False. The Undead are sentient and can even communicate in our tongue. Myth: The Undead are just a local threat. Answer: False. The Undead are a threat to everyone.\nThey have portals that allow them to appear in many regions of Aegis. Myth: The Undead are all a mob. There is no real leadership. Answer: False. Undead hierarchy is just as complex as mortals. The more powerful Undead reside as leaders.\nThe bottom ranks consist of the brainless cadavers you see roaming the night. Myth:The Undead can control powerful Dark Magic. Answer: True. Not all Undead possess the Dark Arts. The ones who do have varying skill. some can command vast power.\nSome can only do minor jinxes. I hope you find this book helpful. -Nitholiak VonSchlichten", ""),
        StaticBook("Nafis to Rhewen", "Commodus de Jedih", "sadasdasdasdasdasddAn Open Letter to Rhewen Frostbeard from Nafis Yar\nsadasdasdsadasdasda\n\nPenned by Nafis Yar, Lord Protector of\nVandoria, 1546\n\nTranscribed by Comm, 1663\n\nsddddddddddddddddd\nTo the Grand King of Urguan and his Grand Council,\n\nGreetings. To those this letter is addressed to, I am Nafis Yar of Al-Dirahk - the Lord Protector of Vandoria. I write this in good will despite the war we fight.\nI hope to clarify my intentions as the new and rightful leader of Vandoria and I also hope to extend an olive branch to you in a world where friends are hard to come by.\nPlease note that while your Legion men have taken my hand and subjugated my people-\nfrom Khalestine to Tyravik, I wish to put all of this aside in order to bring peace and stability to my people.\n\nThe people of Vandoria should have never been involved in this war. As Lord Protector, I hope to bring peace and stability-\nto my people so that we may rebuild and move on from the previous regime. It was the personal desires of the former Caliph Faiz Kharadeen and the false-Vandalore Harold Winter IV that forced us into this conflict. The latter was an opportunist who came -\nout of nowhere to claim the throne and the former was personally indebted to you for previous conflicts, including the Schism War many years before my time.\n\nWith that said, I wish to make something clear:\nI AM QALASHEEN I AM NOT WALDENIAN. I OWE YOU NOTHING. I HAVE NEVER BEEN UNDER OATH TO THE FORMER CALIPH AND I OWE HIM NOTHING EITHER.\n\nIf you march south to aid the Dunamians, I will consider it an invasion and threat to the sovereignty of -\nthe Kingdom of Vandoria and you will find no mercy from me, as Harold IV found no mercy from me. And dealing with him took less than a Saint's week. Dunamis is a rebelling force who has no place in the Kingdom of Vandoria.\nAfter being asked to leave, they did not comply and conflict has engulfed eastern Vandoria and Sutica.\n\nBut I offer you the following terms for I am a GOD-fearing, merciful man who will set aside his personal grudges for the betterment of his people:\naaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaa \nThe Grand Kingdom of Urguan relinquishes all claim to Vandoria held from the defunct Vanderguanese Empire and will acknowledge and respect the independence of Vandoria and her people.\nThe Grand Kingdom of Urguan will pull all forces out of Vandoria and cease all hostilities with Vandoria for the remainder of this conflict.\n\nThe Grand Kingdom of Urguan will offer no assistance to the Dunamians in any form whatsoever in this conflict.\nddddddddddddddddddd\n\nIn exchange for meeting these terms, the Kingdom of Vandoria promises the following:\n\nThe Kingdom of Vandoria will cease all hostilities with the Grand Kingdom of Urguan for the remainder of the war.\nThe Kingdom of Vandoria will pull all forces out of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan.\n\nsssssssssssssssssss\nI offer peace or war. I leave the choice up to you, Grand King. Choose wisely and bring peace between-\nour two nations so we may begin amending ties, if you truly want peace as you claim.\n\nHis Exalted Excellency, Nafis Yar\n\nLord Protector of Vandoria\n\nsssssssssssssssssss", ""),
        StaticBook("Nativitas", "Shady_Tales", "There were no planes of existence. There was nothing. Just the Void. And a bright shining light. It was not a light we could see, it was not really white either,but it would be the only way to explain the existance of such a Deity in contrast to the\nemptiness of the Void. None knows why, how or when this Deity existed. It is, in-fact, heresy to speculate on such matters. The all knowing God was this Deity. Truly none can describe the majesty of the Creator, the one and only. The Merciful Creator of\nthe seven skies. With his intent and only his intent, the World of Aegis was created. All he had to do was simply want it to occur and it happened. THe rolling seas, the proud mountains and vast landscapes, all in a second, created by God. The World was\nnot created in play or for fun, but as a theater for the inhabitants of the World to be tested in. And tested for what?Well, that is for us to speculate. Though I believe it is to test us for purity, how  hard we can fight temptation, and how clean and\ngood our actions be. The first mortal being to be created was a man.This man was sculptured with clay and water, but left hollow. Soulless, God's creation lay there for the other immortal beings to see.The Aengul and the Daemon, the two spirits created\nbefore the mortal beings and before the creation of Aegis. Not much is known about these two spirit races, but hopefully in the future we may know more.God then blew his own breath of existance into the hollow shell  and the Man lived. God then took the\nman and put him in the centre of all of Aegis, the same spot where The Cloud Temple now stands. God also made the Man a partner, from the exact same clay and the exact same breath, she was the first Woman.These simple beings could not talk, nor talk, nor\ndid they know much about the World. They roamed the world, enjoying its pre-historic beauty. Untouched, the fresh glades and dark thick forests were a wonder to set eyes on. Soon they had four children in the four corners of Aegis. Malin was the first of\ntheir sons, born in the deep forests of Aegis, he had blonde hair and sharp ears. Standing tall, he was the father of the Elves of Aegis. Krug was born in the scorching deserts of Aegis, fierce and relentless, he was the father of the Orcs. In the fresh\nmeadows of Aegis was born Horen, father of Humans. And lastly, in the deep underground caves of the World, Urguan was born, master of the Dwarves.\nWe do not know how they fathered sons and how their lines continued but perhaps God created a partner for\neach Son to continue their lines? Soon the first Man and Woman created by God departed Aegis and climbed the seven skies to meet with God their creator, for they had achieved their goal. The Sons began to explore the World of Aegis and each was stricken\nwith grief at the loss of their parents, seeking to fill the chasm of emotion inside them they began to create civilisation.\nAlthough none of the descendants of each Son had neither their long lives or splendour, they did carry their forefathers looks\nand traits. The Elves with Malin at their head travelled the lands and began naming all the inhabitants of this world, they were the first to create a tongue and began to name the trees and grass, the mountains and valleys across all of Aegis. At this\ntime, Malin, Urguan, Krug and Horen were not far apart in looks. Horen and Krug had darker hair than the other two and Krug was a bit larger in build. Malin had blonde hair and Urguan had red. They were all close companions, friends and had much love for\neach other and each others people.Urguan travelled into the deep underground of the earth, naming the beautiful ores and gems, sharing it with his brethren. Krug travelled the harsh deserts, testing his stamina and strength against the environment of\nAegis, and Horen began building the first squalid huts and villages in the valleys. The people lived for hundreds of years, in harmony and peace.Until the day where one of the great Daemons, great worshipers and squalid protectors of the void, kin spirits\nto the Aengul, defected.Iblees, who was once the greatest of all of God’s worshippers, was cast down into the mortal world, and so he was about to destroy the tranquility of Aegis forever. He came in the shape of a man. A gentle being who loved things\ndelicate, he was quickly befriended by Malin, Urguan and Horen. Krug had a great distrust of him but after many years of being convinced by his brothers, he finally accepted his company.\nLittle did Iblees know that this was all part of the Great God's\nplan to test the descendants of Man and Woman. Iblees wanted to destroy everything that God had designed and created, still not in a powerful physical form he began sowing seeds of evil in the minds of the Descendants. Prying on their needs and lusts.\nTo Malin, lover of nature, he promised him many children. He promised him that their laughter would resonate across their forest homes and that he would be content.\n Malin did not want anything more in this world than a bountiful amount of young to occupy\nthe barren forests.To Urguan, he promised infinite wealth of Gems and Ores, colours and crystals he could never imagine. To this, Urguan’s greed failed him. Horen, was anxious he would not live long enough to see his city completed and his lands increased\nHe needed more time, and Iblees struck the chord and promised immortality. Krug was the last to be tricked, Iblees tempted him with wealth, with food, with power. None interested Krug. Iblees was furious, he then challenged Krug in open combat in fury.\nThe whole world witnessed Ibleeses transformation into a hideous beast of the void. His skin turned into scales, fangs erupted and dark horns exploded from his head. He grew large wings and began to breath terrible fire. All stood in shock and horror. The\nbeast terrified all inhabitants of Aegis, animals fled and the Sons of the Descendants were too weak of blood to stand in front of such evil fury. Only Malin, Urguan, Horen and Krug stood in front of the terror. In Iblees’ right hand, a sword wrought in\nflame. Krug, naked and unarmed charged at The Daemon, throwing himself against the scalding scales of Iblees. He screamed in agony as his skin burned and decayed, becoming green and molten. Iblees was knocked off his feet, for the last time.\nHe stood up, heaving in rage and fury, flames exploded from the pores of his skin, he roared in anger and where he struck his sword the land collapsed and the ground erupted. And Lo, great was the Valour of Urguan and the strength of Krug as they fought\nthe beast.Powerful were the arms that carried Krug’s Axe and strong was Horens’ heart as they fought in open combat upon the plains of Aegis. Malin’s sword was fast and swift, smiting Iblees upon his breast and sides.For the thirty years the Descendants\nfought Iblees, the world became a war torn mess. The dead were defiled, summoned from their graves to follow Iblees’ mastery. The more mortal descendants died, the greater Iblees’ armys grew. It was a sad chapter in the World of Aegis, the brothers threw\nup their hands to God in prayer and in agony. Their creations destroyed, their children massacred. Woe to the Sons of Man and Woman. Krug grew bitter, his resentment of his brothers increased for befriending such a beast.Urguan grew greedy, he fought\nvalourously but began to hide his treasures underground. Malin feared for the lives of his children and did not leave his forest sanctuary. It seemed the world was destined for ruin. Iblees grew in strength and the Descendants weakened. Until one day. One\nday where the sound of horns could be heard from the far east. Beautiful horns echoing all across the skies of Aegis. God had heard their prayers. An army of Aengul and Daemons from the seven skies had appeared on the grand shores of Aegis. Their majesty\nand beauty so strong that all The Descendants could see was a flash of power white light erupt from the east. Only Malin with his strong sight could see the figures of light as they sped across the skies towards the armies of Iblees.\nIblees' soldiers\nburned where they stood, The thousands of skeletons and cadavers burst aflame and his living servants fled. There in the right middle of the world, he was cast down and chained by the Aengul and Daemon. A robed figure with brown hair and a black wreathed\napparation stood before him. They were a terrible image to look at, all shyed down and bowed in their majesty and glory. They stood before Iblees, knowing he was immortal and could not be killed, sentencing him to banishment to the void where his dark\nsoul would be forever trapped in torment. But..Before they could complete the sentence, Iblees stood tall for one last time. “You believe you may simply banish me from this plane and that my taint shall not last? I have touched this world with evil and it\nshall forever be part of the souls that inhabit it. Malin, I find no need to curse you, for so many of your kind have already willingly submitted to me now and will on my return in the distant future. The curse you will bear, is not of my doing, but of\nyour own. Even you have done my work, if you realize it or not.Urguan, your greed and lust shall overcome you, you are not worthy of the height God gave you, your descendants shall be short, squalid and ugly. You will always seek to find Gold and Gems in\nthe deep underground of the earth, your hunger never satisfied. Horen, the immortality you hope for will never arrive. Your longevity has already been stripped away thanks to the labors of the twisted heart of your brother Malin. You will age quickly and\ndie before you ever taste the fruits of your pointless labors. And you Krug, the most hated of the Descendants, you shall always have the lust of war. You are strong? Well the strength shall be used against your brothers, used to pillage and murder! Your\nlust for battle shall be unsatiated and your descendants shall grow ugly and heartless.\"As soon as his words were uttered, the world grew suddenly dark. A great roar erupted from Iblees’ mouth and in a blast of fire he was banished from the Mortal World.\nThe Descendants stood still for several moments, pondering over the words of Iblees. Malin, Krug, Urguan and Horen all knew naught of what the great Devil had spoken of when concerning Malin’s betrayal. Dismissing it as the lies of a demon propagated to\ncorrupt their souls, the brothers thought nothing further of Malin’s supposed treason. The robed figure stood before the four brothers. \"There is nothing in my power that may undo what that evil did. There is one thing I may do however, and that is to\nbless you. Malin, may your forests be a sanctuary of peace and your children long lived. Urguan, may your descendants be hardy, strong hearted and strong of mind. Krug, may your people show valour and honour where none exist. And Horen, may your people\none day explore the Seven Skies. I can do no more, for all my power is spent. We will go back to our master now, I believe your children may see us once more but long in the future.\" And with that, the great host of Aenguls and Daemons disappeared into\nthin wisps in the air.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature Healing", "Kirrekith", "Nature Healing\nBy The Sequoia Druid\nPages 17\n\nThe Nature of Druidic Healing\nBy Lilith Winterleaf, the Sequoia Druid.\n\nDruid Healing is a topic many are curious about. Few, even amongst the druids know the true cost\non the person performing the action. Most of the druids use live catalysts to assist in the process of healing. This enables them to draw on this catalysts living energy, this in turn means less energy is draw from the provider to the recipient. However a\nskilled user of this magic type, can find themselves performing the action without a live catalyst without any danger to themselves. \n\nDruidic healing for the most part is basic. It is the recieving and giving of living essence from a provider to a\nrecipient. The druid focuses on the living tissue of the recipients wounds, and asks the body to mend itself, drawing on the catalyst and the druid. Giving their life essence in exchange for the healing aid.\n\nThis is where the costs and risk of a\nDruids healing is, and any would be druid healer should heed this warning well. A druid is capable of amazing feats of healing at times, however it all comes from ones self. In turn, causing possible lasting effects on the provider, and why living\ncatalysts are used to lessen the strain on ones self.\n\nI have personally healed a variety of wounds, from cuts and scrapes to sword clashed to broken bones to some far worse than that. They all draw from you to an extent, even when using a catalyst.\nSimple wounds may show no strain on you, it depends on the severity of the healing needed, and ones personal ability at healing. Practice being key in safeguarding ones self to the harmful effects. \n\nI am in the belief an example of an mistake\nis the most successful way to pass on this lesson to another, I myself, nearly lost my life while healing the King of Skravia back in Asulon. The story had them lured out to a base of mages, that had harassed their kingdom for a while. When they'd\ncornered the mage a trap was sprung, explosives unleased upon the King and Guards. Three died in the blast, others dragged the King back to Skravia (severely wounded) and to my Inn, as they knew I was a healer. His body a mess beyond words to describe, as\nanyone could imagine from an explosion of the magnitude. However one needed to try, coating his wounds in bonemeal and living slime I began my work drawing on the catalyst as well as myself to save the King. It took close to two hours of healing, and left\nhim in a coma for several days. Though I had overstretched myself, my skin a sickly colour, my eyes drained of colour, my lungs not drawing me enough air. I collapsed, and when I woke five weeks had passed, my limbs all sore and my hair a shade lighter,\nthough my skin bore a closer to normal tone. A druid, had come to restore the living essence unto me, otherwise I myself would have perished within the first days of unconsciousness, I was that weakened from the healing.\n\nUnderstand this tale to be a one\nof physical limits of ones abilities to perform healing on a mortally wounded individual without assistance or true grasp of your strength in healing. If you step to far you may risk your life as I did. Find yourself a guide in which to walk between your\npersonal sacrificing and also of the catalysts you use to strengthen your abilities, find yourself always something to ease the act of healing, be that grass around you, flowers or trees. Any living catalyst to help carry the burden.\nAs wrote by Lilith Winterleaf, the final page missing as missed during the quick jotting down of information in the raid, however it still bares wise words for anyone believing themselves a druid of power. Always know ones limits, and be sure to use all\nat your disposal.\n\nBy Lilith Winterleaf, re-wrote by Kirrekith Reffahc of the 16th of the Grand Harvest, 1532, during raid on the Orks Capital. \n\nBy Kirrekith Reffahc.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature Healing", "The Sequoia Druid", "The Nature of Druidic Healing\n\n\nBy: Lillith Winterleaf, the Sequoia Druid\nDruidic Healing is a topic many are curious about, but few, even among Druids, wholly understand the cost on the one performing it.  Most Druids use living reagents to assist in the mending process, this is so that they can draw on the living essense\nwithin the reagent and draw less from themselves, but a skilled Druidic healer can also safely mend wounds without any reagents onhand.\n\nDruidic healing is, quite simply, an exchange of living essence from the healer to the patient.\nThe Druid focuses upon the living tissue around the wound and asks the patient's body to mend itself, giving of their own living essence to aid in the healing.\n\nThis is where the cost and risk of Druidic healing is, and you should heed it well.\nA druid is capable of amazing feats of healing at times, but all of our healing derives from ourselves and it is possible to cause lasting damage to oneself while healing the wounds of another. This is why living reagents are used, to lessen the need to\ndraw from oneself.\nI have personally healed a variety of wounds, from cuts and scrapes to sword clashes to broken bones to some far worse. They all draw from you to some extent, even when using reagents.\nSimple wounds you may not even notice the drain upon yourself, it depends how strong your healing has become, and how familiar you are with the process. Practice truly makes perfect in this regard.\nI am of the belief an example of a mistake is the best way to pass on a lesson, so I will share how I nearly lost my life while healing the King of Skravia back on Asulon. He and some of his soldiers had been lured out to the base\nof a rogue mage that had harassed their kingdom for a long while. When they gained the upper hand and cornered the mage, his trap was revealed, the walls of his base were lined with explosives, and he detonated them.\nThree of the soldiers died in the blast, the others dragged a severely injured but alive King back to Skravia and to my inn, knowing I was a healer. His wounds were great, part of his skull was visible on the top of his head,\nand he had shrapnel wounds all across his body, blood everywhere. There was nothing to do but try, I coated the wounds with a mixture of living slime and bonemeal, then began the healing process,\ndrawing upon the living essences as well as myself to stabilize and mend the kind King laying before me. It took nearly two hours, but his wounds sealed and he was alive and left in a coma for a few days.\nHowever, I had given of myself far more that I should have, my skin was pale, almost white, and my eyes had lost most of their color and I could hardly breathe. I am told I lost consciousness, I awoke five weeks later, my every limb sore,\nmy hair a shade lighter, but my skin almost back to its normal tone. A fellow Druid, Jena, had to come out to restore some living essence to me or I would have perished within the first day or two, I was so weakened.\nTake my mistake with you if you seek to heal, you give of yourself, there is a limit you will reach and you should not go beyond it or you risk your life.  Find your balance between personal sacrifice and reagents to ease your burden,\nyou almost always have something available to ease your personal strain, even if it is the grass around you or a planter of flowers outside the window, any living essence can ease your burden\nif the situation is a bit beyond your ability to heal safely with nothing on hand.\n\n\n~Lillith Winterleaf, the Sequoia Druid", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature's freedom", "Nerrin Delevoye", "No ceiling here; the pure high air is sweet,\nA dreaming bird in a dark blue midnight sky,\nThrough winter chill or searing summer heat,\nGlide silently through clouds without a sigh,\nBright feathers grow, your fledgling wings spread fast,\nYou soar above red sand and blue-white ice,\nAbove grey clouds you'll soar in flight at last,\nThe life before you is your paradise,\nYou feel the many weary hours worn thin,\nTo distant mountain heights you cannot gauge,\nYou feel the many weary hours worn thin,\nThe crumbs of love locked in a gilded cage,\nFly free of summer's burn and winter's bite,\nSpread out your wide wings to the wild, wild night.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nemiisae", "Taynuel Xayarath", "~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\nNemiisae\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nThe Shadow of Death\nGrandmother Spider\nWoman of the Moon\n\nBestowed Druidic Ability: Nature's Wounding\nGoverning Season: Autumn\nManuscripts of ages long since past describe a woman of forbidden beauty and inescapable horrors. The ancient and forgotten race of the Mori'quessir once worshipped such a goddess in their caves of impenetrable darkness, where\nthose who spoke of light were sacrificed in rituals of blood and web. She is the matron of the night and dark desires, and it is she who spins the great web of destiny. Little is known for sure of Grandmother Spider, and indeed it is difficult to speak\nof her at all without reference to Cerridwen and Cernunnos.\n\nWhere Cerridwen breathes life and motherhood, Nemiisae demands death and servitude. She exists as a dark mirror of all that Cerridwen stands\nfor, and perverts her creations of happiness and love into monsters of horror and passion. Those that find themselves abandoned by the light find their way into her domain one way or another, where they emerge changed or do not emerge at all. Though it\nmay seem contrary in this light, Nemiisae is not an evil aspect. Cerridwen provides the life, and Nemiisae evokes the evolution of that life into something new but sustaining. For many species of plant and animal, Nemiisae has been their salvation.\nCernunnos teaches strength, honor, and discipline in the same way Nemiisae teaches cunning, fear, and impulse. The Woman of the Moon teaches us that these abstract concepts are all well and good, but we are better off finding\nour own light rather than basking in the light of others. Scavengers, luminescent creatures, and spiders are examples of guidance toward her ideals of self-enlightenment.\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\nRituals and Beliefs\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\nOnce knowledge of her presence was made public, several Nemiisaen witch covens began sprouting up. Currently very little is known about these reclusive groups.\nGiant Glowshrooms and other luminescent creatures are said to have been guided by Nemiisae for millennia, and successfully attained 'their own light.'\n\nThe moon is often used as her sigil, and many believe it to directly\nconfer Nemiisae's will upon the realm.\n\nCreatures blessed with the condition of Melanism are said to have been touched by Nemiisae, predisposing them as dominant and frightening.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nemir's Notes", "Nemir", "Entry one, 9th of Malin's Welcome, 1569.\nIt's another cool day here in Kovagrad, there's a nip in the air.  The cold won't be good for the crops.  Never is.  But I hardly need to worry about that.  I'm no farmer, just a simple herbalist.\nNotes of lesser accuity potions.\n-----------\nI've prepared a couple of bottles of aqua vitae, just had to soak this red root in warm water for a few hours.  It's pure alcohol, perfect for greater potions.  Along with the aqua vitae, I've prepared a couple\nof bottles of distilled water.  These are for lesser potions.  Gonna need some more coal or perhaps some charcoal soon if I want more of these lesser bases.\n\n\nAlright.  Now that I've got my bases all set up, I'm gonna put some larihei's fingers\ninto the aqua vitae.  I ended up getting a salve of larihei.  Upon using it I've noticed my movements were more... delicate for a short amount of time.  Perhaps an agility potion could come out of this.\nI added halflings grass and got something I like to\ncall a soft relxant.  It pretty much soothes muscle pain for a short amount of time.  Perfect for sore muscles!  I believe this should be enough notes for the day.  I shall continue tomorrow or perhaps sometime later on this week.\nEntry two, 12th of Malin's Welcome, 1569.\nToday I've decided to mess around with the distilled water as the base.  I will do as I did the other day, use larihei's fingers.  The outcome of this was a potion that, when drunken, I felt like my mind was\nclearer.  I was more aware of my movements, could be useful.  Upon adding halfings grass to the potion I got a liquid that was thinner than water, and it swirled nonstop within the bottle.  Upon testing it, my vision was blurred greatly, though I felt\nmore agile.  I guess it'd be helpful.\n\nEntry three, 11th of The Deep Cold, 1569.\nSimple poisons.\nRed Mushroom Poison, makes the user have an upset stomach and feel nauseated.  Good for telling someone to fuck off when they ask for wine.\nPotion of Alabaster Leaf, about the same effects as the last poison, but looks more like tea than wine.  Plus it doesn't have white particles floating around in it.  Potion could also be used as an antidote to other poisons.  If used as one, it'd still\nmake the user's stomach upset.\nPotion of Saffvil, if this is consumed in large amounts the user will die due to its poison.  If consumed in smaller amounts the user will just vomit.\nPotion of Clutcher's Straw, if this potion is taken in large amounts\nthe user's muscles will lock up, paralyzing them.  They will remain conscious.\nParalyzing Toxin, this seems to be one of the most deadly poisons I've ever made.  Any amount taken makes the user paralyzed, keeping them from seeking out an antidote.\nAnother effect is that the user will struggle to breath, eventually suffocating them.\nParalyzing Tonic, another helpful poison.  If the user takes any amount of this poison they will become paralyzed and blind for a short amount of time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nemir's Wish", "Nemir", "I wish to be so much of a skilled lumberjack that others would call my skill supercalifragilistic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nemorsa Hunt Log", "Eath'Lur", "Nemorsa\n-------\nNemorsa is the popular name, the huge imp is my name.\n\nHuge imp? No, I'd never call it a huge imp.\n\nIt's just...\n\nTerryfying...\nLed by Kharak'Raguk, me and a couple of other orcs set our foots into the outside of the desert, supposedly the first hunt after the built of San'Thraka was finished.\n\nWe were looking for something normal, that's when we saw it...\nIt was meant to stay on a tale. A giant, black beast with thick leather, It's huge claws able to cut even through the toughest armor.\n\nThe nemorsa we hunted had pale eyes, I assume it was blind as I tried to block it's view.\nTo kill it, I transformed the sand beneath it on quicksand to immobilize the beast, then, I threw a blob of sand towards it's face, blocking it's eyes, ears, jaw and nostril; the other uruks took the job of finishing it.\nWith this book, I conclude that you truly shouldn't ever try to fight a Nemorsa.", ""),
        StaticBook("NesrineTestimony", "Nesrine", "I. Toren and I mated within the Druid's Grove.\nII. Toren said it was legal because he was 'no longer an elf'.\nIII. Toren lied to me and said having intercourse would be okay.\nIV. Toren is my Guide.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nihil was here", "Nihil", "Nihil was here", ""),
        StaticBook("Nobility.", "Napoleon Fournier d'Avenese", "NOBLE CUSTOMS AND A GREATER STATE\n_____________________________By Napoleon Fournier d'Avenese\n_____________________________Squire To His Lordship of Aldersburg\n_____________________________Hello, sires, of this nation. Clergy, gentry, nobility,\nothers interested. This book is to explain the concept of Fuedalism, and lay out edicts for the perfect fuedal monarchy. It is also to explain to nobles and higher clergly how to behave and interact with the lower orders and their respective lieges.\nI sincerly hope that you enjoy this book, for I am probably to print it and produce many at the store of Jacob Chapel. If any would wish to see me about this piece, I am usually in the Avenese Estate near Pibblebonk or #I Waterfall Avenue, Aldersburg.\nI.The Concept of Fuedalism___________________                                This chapter shall be short for it should be known to all. \n\nThere is no commonly accepted modern definition of feudalism, at least among scholars.\nIt is commonly, and s\ndefined, as the nobility, in exchange for protection, swear fealty and provide labour and military power in exchange for counties and duchies. In some fuedalistic socities, kings and emperors were little more than grand dukes, with the meeting, the king\nand the nobles together having the power. However, fuedalism does seem to be on the decline, due to the absoulitist nature of the imperial monarchy. In fuedal society, the heirarchy could be described as:\nEmperor\nKing\nArchduke\nPrince\nGrand Duke\nDuke\nCount\nLord Mayor\nMayor\nGentry\nSmall Landowners\nFree Subjects\nPeasants\nII.Edicts of Nobility.\n\nI.He must be gregaroius and socially competant, and speak in a noble and \"posh\" manner (as some blackguards would call it)\n\nII.He must know the code of chivalry, save for the paragraph which says he must serve the we\nHe is free to do as he wishes with his peasants and other subjects, mistreating them is discouraged but it is not an edict to not do so.\n\nIII.He must distrivute his land amoung the gentry and other landowners and delegate tasks to his courtiers.\nIV.He must mantain a full court, and hear the advice of his courtiers, for they are gentlemen and women, and their word should be respected. \n\nV.A nobleman must seek the consel of his liege before making a major decision, including marriages. Howev\na monarch would abuse their power, it is both their right and duty to fight against the tyranny and give more power to the nobility. Just as one delegates tasks and wealth to courtiers, a king must do so with his nobles. The monarch and his nobles must be\nin balance.\n\nVI.A noble must obey the head of house except in exceptional circumstances. \n\nVII.A noble must be an advocate for the fuedal system in every aspect, organizing his army in this way.\nVIII.He must not assosciate with peasantry or other men of the lower order.\n\nIX.The head of house should not occupy himself with martial prowess or entrance into the clergly-this is the duty of the younger sons.\n\nX.He must instead focous on\nadministrative skills.\n\nXI.He must seek to be pious and faithful, for a noble should get to the fifth heaven at least.\n\nXII.As well as this, he must be able to attend mass and read the Holy Scriptures regularly, and teach it to his subjects\nlevies with such things.\n\nIII.Principles of A Stable State________________________\nI have read many books which stress the importance of absoloute monarchy. Of despots, and absoloute power. However, I think this not be true. I think it prudent\ntable of nobles, all the lords of the realm, decide together, with the ruler holding meeting regularly with noblemen. The reason absoloute monarhcy is bad is because it is brilliant if given to an able leader, an able emperor. But, if it falls under the\ncontrol of a usurper, his nobles are powerless and even then, if he is a mere bad monarch, and no usurper, the effect is much the same. The tyrant will abuse his power and inspire not with his wisdom but with his power and intimidation, many gallant\nnoblemen will be imprisoned.\n\nFurthermore, a noble should have a similar system with his gentry. He must seek their consel before making a move, and must build a good relationship with his gentry, who will then indeed serve their lieges gratefully an\nproesperity will come from the estates and martial prowess from the sons and brothers of these landed gentry. \n\nSuch a relationship should also be given to a noble's wife, who may be given administrative and diplomatic tasks. Of course, according to\ncode of chivalry, we should not risk the lives of the ladies. \n\nHonour is an important aspect, and a duke or above should be able to call the crown out on matters of honour. Whilst not going so far as dueling, as a royal's death would cause instabili\nnoble must be a paragon of honour and hope, and must make sure his liege is. And vice versa. One should improve the other, with the monarch seeking the consel of the nobles and the nobles seeking the guidance and loyalty to their liege.\n\nIn order to\nfuedal order and keep the loyalty of the subjects, absoloute monarchy must stop. \n\nNo one but dukes and above should swear direct alligience to the emperor. The dukes and above must, with the counts swearing to them, the minor nobles doing to them, t\ngentry, the peasants etc. This also, suprisingly, helps the monarch, for he has no unworthy subjects unneedily wasting his time. An emperor must be in a high, distant place, the dukes closer, the counts closer and all the way down to the small landowners,\ndirectly taking responsability for serfs. This is the ideal fuedal government, the one which embodies fuedalism the most, and the greatest enforcement of fuedalism. \n\nBut you may ask, why would the monarch ever agree to this? Well, that is a simple\nquestion, sire, and for that, I have the answer.\n\nIn return for the greater power, the nobles must give a greater amount of troops, mostly levies, to the cause. If we focous on conscripting the levies in times of war, and follow this system in which\nvassals must provide more, perhaps we can double the size of our forces. \n\nI have also written a book documenting my principles on the organization of the army. \n\nIt is to be printed soon. If you enjoy this, please read that.\nAnd with that, sires, I bid you aideu.\n\n\n\n__________________________________________________________[!]A sketch of a miltiaman in a gambeson and with spear and shield is seen here[!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Nona III", "Nona", "THE COMPLETE\n        FINDINGS OF\n   NONA THE SCHOLAR\n\n              III\nThe Deep Cold, 13th\n1663\n\nToday is a very joyous day! I was approached by the Captain who sought to speak with me in private. We met up on the tower of the chapel just as the sun was rising. He then asked if I might consider a courtship\nbetween us! We both agreed that our duties come first (his as Captain of the Crimson Rangers and mine as a travelling Scholar) and he clarified that he was not asking simply because he was intrested in producing heirs and having a house wife to handle the\nresponsibilities of a woman. He simply was interested in me. So I agreed. How could I not? He is a very kind and remarkable man. We then returned to my dwelling where we toasted to the many sunrises to come and enjoyed the merry hour before returning to\nour duties. Happy day indeed! I've been having trouble focusing on my current research since then. I fell like a silly village girl drooling over the baker's son. I must not let my mind stray too much. There is still far too much work to be done.\nThe Deep Cold, 14th\n1663\n\nI ran itno a bad dude while on a caraban run. He was a thief. I fought him off with backup that was ca lled by kind orc. My wound got hurt and is now now is heal. is no healing *The writing is sloppy and slowly tilts downward*\nThe Deep Cold, 18th\n1663\n\nApologies for the previous excerpt. To translate: On the beginning of a new caravan run, I run into a thief demanding I pay toll to travel on the road. I refused and managed to fight him off. However, while he was fleeing, he\nbrought out a bow and began firing at me. Before this, and orc had ran into us and helped me defeat him the first time. While I was fighting against the thief using his bow, the orc managed to run back to Pembrokeshire and get backup. The gaurds arrived\nand the thief fled. Unfortunately, one of his arrows had grazed my shoulder. Thanatos took me to the Apothecary and helped patch it up, but also gave me some medication that messed with my head a little bit. The wound has healed almost entirely now and I\nam preparing to embark on another journey. My next stop is the Elven Dominion. If all goes well, I hope to start a trade route between here and there.\nSnow's Maiden, 3rd\n1664\n\nI most drop EVERYTHING. I have anew quest to embark on and I fear it might be long before I return to Pembrokeshire. There are whispers of an ancient prophecy. I have yet to uncover the full story, but I\nmust find a place called the Wonkawood and the Wonk village inside it to hear more of what must be done. I embark as soon as possible. I sit in my home now with a bag by my side.\nSnow's Maiden, 11th\n1664\n\nI've found the Wonkawoods and the village, too. Quite the curious place. The Wonka are kind souls. I met with their chieften and have now learned the whole of what it is they seek. I shall write all that I have learned here:\nMany generations ago, a Kharajyr approached the Wonks and requested hospitality. In return she would give them a vision that was granted to her by her godess. They agreed, and at the next full moon, they met to hear her prophecy. The woman called her\nvisions \"moon-gazing\". She began to write down her vision on a tablet, but something went wrong. The woman ran screaming from the cave in great pain until she was burned alive out in the moonlight. The Wonk's shattered the tablet and threw it into the\nriver's. However, an inscription was found many years later. The Wonk elder recognised the writing to be a peice of the exact same text that was written on the tablet. The Wonk's now seek to know the entirety of the prophecy that is hidden all over Atlas,\ninscribed into the land.\n\nThe Chieftan also mentioned that the last few peices of the prophecy were found in swamps and mountains, but this does not gauruntee that all the inscriptions are in similar locations. \n\nAfter hearing their\ntale, among searching for the prophecy fragments, I seek to know more of this \"moon-gazing.\" Perhaps the Kharajyr know more of these visions.\nSnow's Maiden, 14th\n1664\n\nI have yet to find any peices of the prophecy or any more information on the \"moon-gazing\", I've had a few nasty run-in with some bandits, but I managed to fight each one off. I know those fragment's are out there. I'm not\ngiving up yet. Perhaps I will search near the Elven Dominion next. That area is riddled with magic and I sense that such a trait is important to the prophecy and the woman's visions. I will begin the trek first thing in the morning.\nSnow's Maiden, 18th\n1664\n\nI've made some ground on my research into moon-gazing! Upon arriving in the Elven Dominion, I ran into a Kharajyr by the name of Sa'Muja. I asked if hew knew anything of the prophecy or moon-gazing. While he knew none of the\nWonk's, a long time ago he had briefly studied moon-gazing under someone named Murka. Many years ago, in a land known as Vailor, Murka was given a monestary by a Trade Princess of Suttica. I asked Sa'Muja where I could find this Murka, but he confessed\nthat his old teacher was unfortunately dead. Though, he went on to say that he would tell me all he knew of moon-gazing at a later date. The Kharajyr departed and I hope that our paths will cross again soon. I'm eager to learn more of this craft.\nFirst Seed, 13th\n1664\n\nMy progress has been slowgoing. I have yet to see the Kharajyr again or to find a fragment of the prophecy. There's only been dead end after dead end. I've returned back to Pembrokeshire as I have used the last\nremains of my minas. It is good to see the Captain again. My only current option is to return to working the Caravan's as a merchant. I hope to find more details of moon-gazing and the prophecy so that I may continue my quest once again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Not For Crumena", "Marb", "Dargo\nDagro", ""),
        StaticBook("Note", "Aesilnoth Annungilben", "[!]A carefully written note written with nice handwriting.\n\nDear Morrigyn, It is forbidden for me to be writing this to you, but I could not hold my tounge. We met only briefly yet I saw true beauty in you. I wish I could truly sign my name to this, but\nfor now this will have to do.\n\nWith love,\n-A\n\n\n[OOC] Ignore the actual name the note was only signed with the one above.", ""),
        StaticBook("NOTE", "Ti'Khoraha", "Something is crudely scribed here. It is worn and badly faded, but you can just barely make it out.\n\nIt seems to be part of a prophecy called \n'The Turning of\nthe Seasons'.\n\nYou've heard rumors that, deep in the\nWonkawood, a strange village of frog-like people are looking for fragments of this prophecy.\n\nIf you give them this fragment, and were the first to find it, they might reward you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Note for Muildir", "Vendel", "Dear Muildir,\n\nThank you for taking the time to talk to me, and for not turning me away. I'm sorry for breaking down like that, and for dumping all of that on you. I remember Damien saying the best way to get to know you is to be entirely honest.\nSo I was honest. The few times we've managed to spend time together, I've enjoyed. There are many more sides to you than I would have anticipated. I'm glad that I got to know you, at least a little bit.\nI wanted to let you know that I'm going away. You probably won't see me again. It's better this way, my illness won't just disappear. I want you to know I wish you all the happiness in the world, and I'm sorry I wasn't brave enough to tell you myself.\nI always thought you were wonderful.\n\n[There is a sketch of a crow in flight]\n\nGoodbye Muildir\n\n[The letter is unsigned].", ""),
        StaticBook("Note from Parent", "Seth Flanagan", "A letter to Seth:\nIf you are reading this then we are dead. There is a secret we never wanted you to know. You are a dark elf. We fixed it so that when you grew up you looked like a human.\nLove, Chasadie and William", ""),
        StaticBook("Note to Leofwine", "[Child] Harley", "Harley is being held captive, we want 750 Mina and we'll release her. Not following our commands will lead in her demise. We will get her to sign this to prove we have her. Although she is too stupid to write. We will have someone meeting you at this....\nlocation. *A small hand-drawn map is attached, showing an area  co-ordinates also ((x: -100\nz: 800))\n\nWe're hoping you will not dissapoint us Leofwine.", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes", "Doryn", "https://docs.google.com/document/d/1R64LyVKhgy35_jwdY6umtN7O7eZweYhwzJGbbzi6mBg/edit?usp=sharing", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes", "Goblin Cheiftan", "The great ones...they pass\nthe blue gaze sees all\nthe rumbling never stop\nThe seal never stay shut so long\nBiz'riyk stay strong for clan\nStay\nStrong", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes on Knights", "Frederick Kelly", "Darius \"The Butcher\" Ault, a knight who has accepted bribes of Vampyre blood to enhance them within the Carolstadt Joust and Melee. Iago-Leopold was complicit in such a transaction.\n\nDated - 22nd of The First Seed, 1696\nUthred \"Gromach\" approached Leopold on the idea of being turned into Kindred. His suspicions and investigations were fueled by sniffing out the supernatural source to become one. Too sloppy, violent. Man cannot be led to be turned even though the\nwhispers say he wishes for it. Perhaps increasing the supplies from Ser Ault into Gromach will allow for a greater transformation?\n\nUnsure, unknowing.\nExperimentation upon Darius' form with the Vampyric enhancements have led to his ascension within the ranks, a grand proposal on how this works. The man is not a regular vampyre, but a hybrid which is immune to the normal signs at the current moment.\nSuperior skills in combat and enhanced senses have come towards the already, combat hardened Knight.\n\nHe is complicit and wishes to be turned, but investigation must be continued to avoid suspicion.\n\n- Frederick Kelly.", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes on Plants", "Ayrnor", "-* ~                ~ *-\n\n         Ayrnor's\n     Collected Notes\n             On\n     Medicinal Herbs\n              &\n          Poisons\n\n    Also how much I have in stock of them.\n\n-* ~                ~ *-\nAqua Nymph,\nFound in swamps, underwater.  If ingested by itself, causes severe hallucinations.  Can boil it in water to extract oil that is good for burns.\nUSE JARS TO KEEP ALIVE.\n\nCollected, 2\nAquate Root\n\nFound underwater, in oceans.  Used for hydrating dry or chapped skin when used in creams.\n\nCollected, 2\nCorvisange,\nA thin resin found in caves, can cause paralysis if consumed orally or if stabbed into someone.  In administered, small doses can be used as a strong pain-killer.  DON'T USE FOR LONG TERM.\n\nCollected, 0\nMiner's Helmet,\nA mushroom with very potent poison, if ingested will stop nervous system in a matter of hours.  Almost undetectable, except in early stages.  Can be boiled for 15 minutes to make a tasty mushroom soup.\n\nCollected, 0\nJavens,\nCommonly found plant in deserts, primarily Orcish.  It looks like a large sand spur with green colored stripes going along the green plant.  When chewed raw will render host unconcious within 5 minutes.  \n\nCollected, 0\nGijakdul, Bloodflower\nRare flower found in deserts, mainly Orcish. Smells like rotting flesh.  Used in healing, but not much is known in what it can do for healing.\n\nCollected, 0\nAtheros,\nFound in jungles, is a white plant with brown and gray spotted roots.  Used in medicine as a pain relief solution.  Best used when mixed, but can be used raw.\n\nCollected, 0\nMandragora,\nFound in swamps, the 'meat' of the plant is underwater.  Is known for making highly necrotic and hallucenagetic spores. Petals can be used in tea, the 'meat' can be used in mind & body revitalization potions and regenerate skin.\n\nCollected, 0\nBiteit,\nFound in rainforests, is a green mushroom with brown spots on top, often found under lilypads.  Can't be used for much, but is used in potions that aids in fighting off infection.\n\nCollected, 0\nAshwood tree,\nSap from Ashwood trees.  Can be used as a alchohol substitute, but tastes horrid.  Mostly used as a powerful sterilizer and disinfectent.\n\nCollected, 0\nAlabaster Leaf,\nFound in drier areas of forests, around fallen trees.  It's a small plant with alabaster hue leafs.  Commonly used as paint and dye, or as a simple poison.  Unlikely to cause death, but will cause vomiting/nausea.\n\nCollected, 0\nFlameTongue Root,\nFound on cliffsides in forests, roots are bright rust color.  Can be used to coagulate blood when applied to an open wound. \nONLY USE WHEN IN DIRE NEEDS.\n\nCollected, 0\nNight Sap,\nFound in deformed growths on the trunks of sturdy oak trees.  Commonly used drug, gives happy dreams and makes one fall asleep instantly.  Lasts for 3-5 hours, then a headache that lasts just as long.\n\nCollected, 0\nSerpents Stalk,\nFound near small bodies of water, stalks are emerald hued and have lighter green and brown ridges.  Tastes bland, is used for soothing burns due to cool juices. Can be eaten.\n\nCollected, 0\nTippen's Root,\nFound near fallen trees and dead animals.  Purple flowers with yellow and darker yellow dotted roots.  Used to stop bleeding, patient may gag or vomit due to foul smell.\n\nCollected, 0\nGislocinovi,\nUnkown where to find, unsure of what it looks like.  Must be put in hot water for 1 hour, then squeezed for juice.  Used for anti-bacterial bandage, overdose may cause; nausea, internal bleeding, nose bleeds, twitching, major seizures, or -\ndeath.\n\nCollected, 0", ""),
        StaticBook("Notice", "Cablam", "18th of Sun's Smile, 1567.\n\nI am writing this note for the scholars of the Library of Dragur to notify of some recent changes.\nOrithur, the Founder of the Library and a member of family that has been formed here at the library has left the library indefinitely. If you see him continue to treat him with the utmost kindness and respect.\n\nIf you wish to know more relating to his\ndeparture and where the Library will go from here feel free to speak with myself, Armin Ambertoe. I will be happy to answer any and all questions. \n\nFor now regular scholar duties will continue as normal unless otherwise specified.\nSafe travels to you all. \n\n-Armin Ambertoe", ""),
        StaticBook("NOTICE", "Armin Ambertoe", "On the 16th of Sun's Smile, 1556, a group of three dwarves broke into the thanhium lab. The way they managed to enter was by lockpicking the doors at the side entrance. THE SIDE ENTRANCE GATE HAS TO BE SHUT AT ALL TIMES. I noticed the lab had been broken\ninto when I went downstairs. Lyeth and Orias showed up shortly after this discovery, and we proceeded to the entrance. Orias and I went on the walls surrounding the entrance with buckets of acid, in case the thieves were hostile, and Lyeth stood at the\nfirst set of doors, lowering the bridge but not after trying to open the glass door herself. This action by Lyeth likely jammed the door system, and it trapped the dwarves inside. We did manage to spot them once they came back up to the doors, and we\ntalked with them, attempting to convince them to surrender which they failed to do. So they sat trapped in the lab, slowly freezing to death. Then, out of no where, the cracking of the large thanhium shard that was previously stolen, or at least that is\nwhat I suspect it was, could be heard. Orias had left at this point and so Lyeth and I dashed to the entrance to the vault to take cover. Revion arrived then and we huddled by the vault until the explosion happened. The glass door contained the blast, but\nended up cracking, and thanhium dust began to slowly leak out. The dwarves all likely died from the blast, and so Lyeth, Revion and I went to work attempting to seal the crack. Lyeth first piled stone in front, but that failed to contain it completly.\nNext she gathered up some gold she had lying around in her room and melted it down. With the melted down gold she made her way to the glass door and poured it on the stone barrier, sealing it shut. With the crack sealed, we made our way back up to the\nupstairs. Once there Orithur arrived and went swiftly down to the lab once notified about the situation. He began quite angry, and luckily that magical amulet managed to keep him in check. He then left the library, seemingly quite sad and upset and walked\noff to the west of the library into the woods. At this time, the downstairs area is flooded with thanhium dust, and so no one should enter without a mask on. Also, the seal on the lab should NOT be touched under ANY circumstances. It is also advised that\nany items of significant value in the downstairs rooms be moved to a different place for the time being. Lastly, venting of the dust will occur within the next few stone days so it is advised to have a mask on at all times when walking about the library\nuntil further notice.\n\nIf you have any questions direct them to Lyeth or myself. \n\n-Armin", ""),
        StaticBook("Novice Booklet", "Beltran", "[!]A novice script, the leather bound journal seems to belong to a novice monk.\n\"I have fled my teachers, the plague has been wrought upon them but an even dangerous creature lurks in the crowd of those undead! It slithers, the scales it clashes against the cobblestones. I fear I am alone in my endevaour. My peers have gone blind to-\nmy cries. My stomach grumbles but not for food but for escape, for food is what the eye wants from me.\"\n\n\n\n\n1570 -Frair Towl\n[!]Scratch marks are present on the page. Several pages are ripped apart. Blood is splattered upon the sheets in a careful manner, resembling an eye.\nThe eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye\nThe eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye\nThe eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye\nThe eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye\nThe eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye The eye\n[!]The rest of the pages are crusted, as if they have been soaked in water.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nursery Rhymes", "Kairi", "One slave\nTwo slave\nRed slave\nBlue slave\n\nBlack slave\nBlue slave\nOld slave\nNew slave\nThis one has a little star.\nThis one won't go so far.\nSay! What a lot \nOf fish there are.\n\nYes. Some are red. And some are blue.\nSome are old. And some are new.\nSome are sad.\nAnd some are glad.\nAnd some are very, very bad.\n\nWhy are they\nSad and glad and bad?\nI do not know.\nGo ask your dad.\nSome are thin.\nAnd some are fat.\nThe fat one has\nA yellow hat.\n\nFrom there to here, from here to there,\nFunny things\nAre everywhere.\nHere are some.\nWho like to run.\nThey run for fun\nIn the hot, hot sun.\n\nOh me! Oh my!\nOh me! Oh my!\nWhat a lot\nOf funny things go by.\nSome have two feet\nAnd some have four.\nSome have six feet\nAnd some have more.\n\nWhere do they come from? I can't say.\nBut I bet they have come a long, long way.\nWe see them come. \nWe see them go.\nSome are fast,\nand some are slow.\n\nSome are high.\nAnd some are low.\nNot one of them\nIs like another\nDon't ask us why,\nGo ask your mother.\nSay!\nLook at his fingers!\nOne, two, three...\nHow many fingers\nDo I see?\n\nOne, two, three, four,\nFive, six, seven,\neight, nine, ten.\nHe has eleven!\nEleven!\nThis is something new.\nI wish I had\nEleven, too!", ""),
        StaticBook("O Weary Courier", "Saeed Ibn Malek", "O Weary Courier\n-------------------A Song by Saeed Ibn  Malek\n-------------------  Wait, O Weary Courier, Pen A Salute on a letter\nEven If the darkness followed you, You must accomplish your mission\nAnd if they Enquired after us, Thank them,\nAnd tell them, they are the Way you remember..\nYour Defendant in absent, and the verdict is impermissible in absence\nA person Must deliberate, and judge fairly\nDon't mistake us to be the source of this injustice, it is justice we give & take\nDo us a Favor O courier and carry to them our salute and greetings\nWait, O Weary Courier, Pen A Salute on a letter\nEven If the darkness followed you, You must accomplish your mission\nWait, O Weary Courier, Pen A Salute on a letter\nEven If the darkness followed you, You must accomplish your mission\nTell them the restless sorrowful are spending nights raving about them\nThoughts and suspicions are playing us\nA sorrow we hide in the heart fear some people will disgrace us\nTell him the one we thank the most (Allah) knows all that is public or secret \nHe(Allah) knows what you are But He(Allah) tests his servent with ordeals\nWait, O Weary Courier, Pen A Salute on a letter\nEven If the darkness followed you, You must accomplish your mission\nWait, O Weary Courier, Pen A Salute on a letter\nEven If the darkness followed you, You must accomplish your mission\nWho Ever wants his final destination to be Seven Skies, Wouldn't accept a weak spirit\nFor Some dreams are all what they do, and for others, they make their dreams come true\nAnd the one who says: Lord, I have Faith! Will never bare despair and suspicion\nThis one becomes stronger with Kitab Alsalam, and when the caller, calls for good he responds \nO courier when you meet, tell them : We remember our promise and will fulfill it\nWait, O Weary Courier, Pen A Salute on a letter\nEven If the darkness followed you, You must accomplish your mission\nWait, O Weary Courier, Pen A Salute on a letter\nEven If the darkness followed you, You must accomplish your mission\n-------------------By Saeed Ibn Malek\n(I did not Make this Irl! I take No credit for it irl, i just added the holy book's name in this entire thing...still hope you enjoyed it!)", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations v1.", "snowshovel", "A Record of Magical Sightings in the Witch Woods of Lenfarthing.\n\nRecorded by Dedicants Eldon and Beth.\nOn their travels to the With Woods of Lenfarthing, the subject of many tales of magical anomalies, the Dedicants mentioned came upon a strange sight. This create appeared to the Dedicants as a faintly glowing blue orb which floated and could vanish at\nwill. Although one could be commonly seen, the Dedicants also observed a group hovering around one, larger orb. The Dedicants can only assume these were unnatural beings created by magical events. More records may be taken at a later date.", ""),
        StaticBook("Obsidian Planes", "Sighard An'Halstaig", "Mission Log: Obsidian Planes Temple\n\nI:\nTook the cart from the Blood Baron's keep. Horse couldn't trot from the beggining of the Planes. Time to continue on foot.\n\nII:\nTraversing the Planes isn't hard for some prepared fellows. Avoiding the\nblobs is not a hard job, and the Pigmen are docile if not hungry.\n\nIII:\nFound the temple. A portal leads within it, and there's an annatural feeling going about the place.\n\n>Inside area is warded off. Pigmen trot about the place. Further\nexpeditions with more numbers might be required to search throughout the temple's confines.\n\n\nIV:\nThe outside isn't much, though some sort of beam goes up, and leads to some sort of starry contraption. What if this is some sort of center hub for the\nObsidian Planes?\n\n\n\nOVERALL:\n\nResults have not been as fruitful as I thought. A big expedition should be formed. This isn't something to be branded as a mere cartography mission. The burning star in the sky leads me to believe that this\ntemple has an active role in the mystery that is the Obsidian Plane itself. As said, a prepared expedition of good, able men should be formed, in order to actively search for the temple's secrets.\n\n\n--END--", ""),
        StaticBook("Obtain Intel", "Regale Ba'ikana", "Gather information on two elves, not affiliated with the Warhawke group.", ""),
        StaticBook("Odd Events C1", "Jaya Jayamen", "Odd Events\n\n       ~Originally by\n     Sofetios Jayamen\nChapter One\n    \n      The Light\n\nMy name is James Geedin. My family recently settled in a new land without a name, so I call it Genway.  We were lucky enough to stumble upon an old house.\nWhoever built it, I don’t know. Some odd stuff seems to happen here, but I’m determined to stay at my new home. This is my story.\nI woke up in the middle of the night with chills running down my spine. I was around 17 at the time. I went downstairs to get something to drink.\nThat’s when I noticed it. I looked out the window and noticed a light in the distance at the woods. Though it wasn’t yellow like a fire, it was white. I thought about checking it out, but decided I should go to bed instead.\nThe next day in the morning, I went downstairs to have breakfast, but the thing was, my parents weren’t awake. That was unusual, so I went upstairs to their room and knocked on the door.\nWhen I knocked on the door it simply opened slowly from the force of my knock. I looked in, but no one was there. I spent the rest of the day looking for them, but to no avail.\nSoon it became nighttime and I was in the kitchen. That’s when I noticed it again, the same light as before. This time I went out towards the light. I came to the forest clearing where the light was coming from.\nThere was a small mirror in the center, angled towards my house. Then I noticed something, the white light wasn’t coming from the mirror, It was coming from the attic window of my house being reflected by the mirror.\nI saw a word carved into the mirror. It said “Truth”. I looked back towards the house. Could my parents be were that light is? I took the mirror and made my way back the house.\nI got to the house and made my way upstairs to look for a way up into the attic. I looked different places until I got to my parents room. I walked in and there was a small white light coming from the bookcase in there, going around the books.\nI walked up to the bookcase and looked through the cracks between the books. There was a white stairway that lead upwards.  I shifted the bookcase over and started walking up the white stairs. Until I got to a white trapdoor above me.\ncautiously, I lifted it up a crack and looked in the attic room.  There were two statues that looked just like…  I then opened the trapdoor fully and rushed into the white room towards the two statues.\nThey were exact replicas of my parents, but they had faces that looked like they were scared of something. Suddenly there was the sound of the trapdoor shutting behind me.\nI looked back to see something in white robes that covered its whole body and a light coming from under its hood.\n“Who are you?” I said scared. It simply stood there. I looked back towards my parents for a second and back again.\nThen it was right in front of me. Startled I fell back and the mirror dropped on the floor face up but didn’t break. I got up and backed up. It didn’t move.\nThen I noticed something. In the reflection on the mirror on the ground, where the thing was supposed to be was a person. The person in the reflection had light coming from its eyes.\nI took out my short sword. Getting ready to fight whatever this was. I lunged at its chest, but as it made contact with the light coming from it, the blade turned white. I dropped my sword from it happening.\nI was about to panic when I remembered the mirror, then got an idea. Keeping my eyes on the person, I picked up the mirror, careful not to get in the light.\nThen with one hand, I slid it under the light coming from the person’s hood, trying to aim it back at it. Suddenly the light coming from under the hood disappeared. Then the person in the robes simply fell over, solid as a stone.\nI turned to the statues of my parents. I wasn’t sure what to do. I talked, I yelled, but there was no response. I had never felt so alone before. My parents turned into stone, not knowing how to turn them back to normal.\nBut then that made me realize something. Something I should have thought from the start. \n\nWho had left the mirror in the woods?\n\nEnd of Chapter One", ""),
        StaticBook("Ode to Elduren", "Elder Hobbs Burrows", "\nOde to Elduren\n\nby Hobbs of Dunshire\nWhen I have fears that I may cease to be,\nBefore my quill has gleaned my teeming brain,\nBefore high-piled books, in library,\nHold like rich garners the full ripened grain,\nWhen I behold upon the night's starred face,\nThe noble solitude of your great peak,\nAnd think that I may never live to trace, \nYour shadow with the magic hand of chance,\nAnd when I feel, great mountain of our land,\nThat I shall never look upon thee more,\nNever have relish in the faery power\nOf unreflecting happiness - then on the shore\nOf the wide world I stand alone,\nOn the edge of verdant green and cliff,\nAnd think till death and hurt to nothingness do sink.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ode to Nature", "Pine Druid Gi'Garun", "An Ode to Nature\n    by The Pine Druid\n\nWe walk upon her soil,\nWe gaze upon her trees.\n\nWe're surrounded by all kinds of things, \nThat sprouted from her seeds.\nWhen one steps out of one's front door,\nOne will see her work.\n\nHer prowess great and beautiful,\nNo dark or evil mirk.\n\nWhat is it that I speak about?\n\nWhat is it that I praise?\nThe lands we roam,\nThe streams that foam.\n\nThe trees so tall,\nThe rain that falls.\n\nAll of these are of her make, for they are her and her alone. The make of two of love and great.\n\nThat be Nature.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oh My Friend", "Saeed Ibn Malek", "____Oh My Friend____\n-------------------A poem by Saeed Ibn Malek\n-------------------Like A Frolicsome Twilight, \n you Hang around the hallways of depature...\n Like a wounded sparrowhawk,\n You travel with no peace...\nAssassinate all forum of connection..\n And thunder with reminiscence. Oh My Friend...\n Every time i called you,\n The cry weeped for hearing me crying...\nAnd every time i looked at you,\n The memories of destroyed my entire entity...\n And the nostalgia made a shortcut straight to my heart...\n And the trailer of memory Returned to tear the cuts of my aches..\n Tell Me My Friend,\nwhat if tears streamed down on my cheeks\n Who would clear those tears out?\n Tell me, What if the phantom of breakdown chased me\n behind the hallways of loss?\n Where shall i find shelter and where the end will be?\nTell me,What if the birds left my sky...\n heading to the skyline of ruins...\n who would bring back the singing of bulbuls...\n How can i draw a way of eternal bestowal...\n without a hand that supports my hand...\nif it ever stumbled with demise?\ntell me who would draw me on the details of his features;\n For me to see the truth after the vanishing of mirage?\n Who whould bring me back from prudence after being foolish\n For My Sake,\n Listen to my speech,My friend, As it comes to one tone\na symphoney of remembrance that I made you own...\n And dont ask me if i miss you and miss being with you instead,\n Look between the lines of your hands,\n you'll find me as a prisoner, Fighting death back and forth\n Breathe Deeply!\nYou'll find me a very little atom fighting \n its paralles to find its way to you\n Close your eyes\n My Phatom won't vanish from your fantasy\n And smile to the drop of rain, when it streams down your forehead & cheeks...\nGreet it and wipe it away softly...\n Just the way you used to pat my shoulder\n When i run away from the world's nonsense to you\n Touch the air,you'd definitely feel my presence..\nAs i's part of your entity\n I'm some of you..\n I'm entirely you, My Friend\n I'm you, Oh you the page of the whiteness\n Gather my dispersion, and sprinkle it on the layers of substantial pain..If you decided to leave.\nLight up the night lamps in the daylight hours \n as the day wont look like a normal day no longer...\n Cover me with the garment of remembrance,\n as the cold will then breach the breath of warmth..\nAnd break up the ribs of nostalgia..\n And drink from the antidote of the past,\n with the heat of my breaths and feelings...\n Leave if you want to leave...but..let your departure be to the lands of reunion \n not to the lands of neglect and loss...\nbe a home to me\n as im an orphan with no home..\n Homeless..Driszzle with pain\n Im a wound..  With human features so,\n Be to me..\n the way of being home feels like...\n-------------------By: Saeed Ibn Malek\n   (ibraheemc2000)", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Elven Part 1", "Anthron", "Table of contents\n------------------\nAffixes: 1-13\n-------------------Seed words: 14-part 2\n-------------------\nContent provided by\nSporadic:\nhttps://www.lordofthecraft.net/topic/19254-recovering-the-ancient-tongue-of-the-elves/\nAFFIXES\nAffixes  served a very important purpose in the Elven language. You are recommended to learn of them and their purpose before anything else,  for many words are formed by the addition of affixes to the so- called 'seed words', which are listed\nbelow.\nWe further discuss our findings on affixes in the grammatical section of this volume. Furthermore, words deserving extra explanation will be handled in the 'curious words' section.\nNote: The dash indicates the location of the seed word to the affix\nac- (aca-) Honorific for an accursed.\n-------------------ah- (ahe-): Honorific for reverence. Often used in front of names to denote sainthood.\n-------------------ael-: Vile, unnatural, beastly.\n--------------------al: -Designates the completion\nof an action.\n------------------\n-an: many, full of -Mostly designates plurality.\n------------------\nan*h- (a/o/i/e/u): To direct (up/down/left/right/rotate) (more on this in 'curious words').\n-------------------\nav-: wandering.\n-------------------ay: for.\n-------------------\n-ante (-nte): Last.\n-------------------div-: Empty, devoid of (antecendent to -an).\n--------------------ento (-nto): next.\n-------------------\n-ehya: and - used at the beginning of a sentence for 'but...'\n-------------------\nel- (ele-): - Changes a noun into a pronoun, making it a title of someone, or possibly something.\n-------------------\nfi-: new, anew - Often used as prefix, but not exclusively.\n-------------------heya- (hey-): what, how, who.\n-------------------\nil- (ilu-): with\n--------------------ii: little Designated the diminutive form. Plural: iian.\n-------------------\n-ir: - Designates the purpose of someone.\n-------------------iyl-: this usually a prefix, though not exclusively.\n-------------------iyul-: that usually a prefix, though not exclusively.\n--------------------leh: -Designates affiliation.\n------------------\nma- (mar-): very -Intensifier. More on this in 'curious words'\n--------------------n: - Sometimes put behind an adjective or verb to create a noun.\n--------------------ne (-ane): not - A suffix used to indicate the negative.\n-------------------\n-onn: from, born, kin - Often a suffix, but not always. More on this in 'curious words'.\n-------------------par- (pra-): before, pre-\n-------------------res- (re-): wayward, capricious, unpredictable.\n-------------------\n-sae: Spreading, development management. - More on this in 'curious words'\n-------------------tal- (tali-): Part (of) - More on this in 'curious words'\n-------------------u-: or - Always a prefix and always used with apostrophe.\n-------------------\n-yem (-hyem): again -Can be used to make a 're-' family of verbs\n-------------------vul- (vule-): clever, intuitive, deceptive.\n-------------------\nSEED WORDS\nThese words make up the brunt of the Elven language, and may be modified by various affixes to create new words.\nacal: valuable, golden, cursed - From ac-al: Completion of the word\nac: Cursed. Beware of this double meaning. Because of this double meaning,  Elves of old may give those they wish ill a nugget of gold to declare their hostility.\nThe gesture was often wasted on other races, who considered the gold a tribute.\n-------------------acalin: shop\n-------------------acaln: gold\n-------------------\n(a)chikr: (without the a:) ***** - denotes a woman who murders her children (or neglects them to death), which is considered a horrible crime due to the value of fertility and the rarity of Elf children. Without the 'a', the word degenerates\ninto a grave insult. Know that intentional cursing in Elven attracts ill-willing aspects.\n-------------------(a)dil: needy, desiring, wanton - When one forfeits the 'a' it becomes as of a vice.\n-------------------\n(a)dont: requesting, awaiting - Without the 'a' it becomes 'demanding', -er makes verb as always.\n-------------------adri: evil, immoral, hate.\n-------------------(a)elor: abomination, faithless, demon. -Denotes any non-humanoid of intelligence.\nWithout the 'a' the word becomes an insult to call someone disfigured. Know that intentional cursing in Elven attracts ill-willing aspects.\n-------------------Aengul: Aengul - race of semi-divine beings affiliated with light.\n-------------------aetah: age\n-------------------aeth: aether\n-------------------aher: to bless.\n-------------------ahern: blessing.\n-------------------akal: valuable, golden - less ominous.\n-------------------akaleh: wealth, money, valuable.\n-------------------akalin: shop\n-------------------\nakaln: gold - less ominous way to speak of gold.\n-------------------allim: sin  - allimar: to sin; alliman: sinful.\n-------------------andria: hope\n-------------------annyer: to dance\n-------------------Asul: Sun\n------------------\nata: ugly, tainted\n-------------------athri: serpent, snake\n-------------------a)iler: Wizard, conjurer, heretic -Any wizard or spiritual humanoid that's not a druid. When one forfeits the 'a' in the word it becomes an insult.\nIt should be noted that the word 'Ailer' is not used for your everyday magic user, but reserved for a powerful, exclusive brand of spellcasters.\n-------------------alor: salmon -aloronn/alonn: salty\n-------------------ame: forest\n-------------------\nannil: guiding -anniler: to guide, direct\n-------------------ante: Last\n-------------------arche: infrequent, sporadic, rare.\n-------------------(a)rhil: just fair (without the a:) vengeful, scorned.\n-------------------\nasimulum: sanctuary, glade, asylum, dedicated place (esp. one of nature).\n-------------------aver: to wander, to roam around aimlessly, to be confused.\n-------------------avern: wanderer, confused person.\n-------------------ayal: yellow\n------------------\nay(i)lu: liked, likable - may(i)lu: loved. The 'i' is optional, but may not be used if the object is not a person.\n-------------------ayla: good\n-------------------barbu: dark, black, hedgehog\n-------------------bilok: to create, to make.\n----\nBortu: dwarf\n-------------------(a)caele: sky. - The plural, caelan, is used to reference to the Seven skies and with that, God. The lack of an 'a' in front makes the word disrespectful or insulting.\n-------------------celia: star\n-------------------\nceru: strong, mighty\n-------------------chirr: wolf\n-------------------chul: to must\n-------------------cihi: city\n-------------------cinh: to stop, to cease\n-------------------ciw: to sleep\n-------------------\ncrua: hurting, suffering - which makes cruan: pain\n-------------------Daemon: Daemon - race of semi-divines affiliated with smoke and fire.\n-------------------dion: long - dionne: short\n-------------------divu: empty\n------------------\ndrui: Druid\n-------------------draoi: Evil/corrupted druid. Warlock. Sorcerer.\n-------------------ehier: to find\n-------------------enaer: guest\n-------------------ento: next\n-------------------ern: to can, to be able to\n-------------------eth: end, to end, to die -word can be a noun, passive verb and active verb depending on usage.\n-------------------evar: to protect, preserve\n-------------------eyr: to use, apply\n-------------------faesu: horse\n------------------\nfer: tool - This word creates a wide array of words for various tools, such as torches and pickaxes. They are discussed further in 'curious words'.\n-------------------fenn: ice\n-------------------feta: cold\n-------------------fih: to eat, to feed\n--------\nfin: region\n-------------------fiyem: reborn, renewed, revitalized\n-------------------fyu: full\n-------------------hae: her\n-------------------haelun: mother\n-------------------haler: to promise, to pledge\n------------------\nharriel: square\n-------------------heial: circle, council\n-------------------hier: near\n-------------------hileia: Peace. - Has no plural\n-------------------hiuw: to twitch, to move\n-------------------hiylu: Healthy / spirited\n------------------\nibar: white, owl\n-------------------igne: flame, fire - igne'sae: destruction, war\n-------------------iheiuh: wind\n-------------------iheiuhii: voice, breath\n-------------------ihn: stick\n-------------------ihnsil: spear\n------------------\nikur: wrought, cold, gray\n-------------------ikurn: iron\n-------------------ikru: foolish\n-------------------iller: to give, to grand\n-------------------ilum: glowing - when something only reflects light. ilumr: to glow.\n------------------\ninder: to read\n-------------------indor: book\n-------------------irrin: glass\n-------------------ito: to, here, within - Can also be a suffix. More on this in 'curious words'\n-------------------iyat: thought\n-------------------iyath: to think\n-------------------iylanh: to place\n-------------------kae: me\n-------------------kalem: Malin's year, - Roughly 26 Anthos years, denotes the length of a High Prince's reign.\n-------------------kaliri: Event, party\n-------------------\nkarim: Fortday, - The measure of time from one Dwarven sleeping cycle to the next, roughly 24 Anthos days.\n------------------\nkarin(ah): sunrise, - Also used to speak of day\n-------------------kathir: foe\n-------------------\nker: dark, sunset - Also used to speak of night\n-------------------khel: darkness - Strictly a noun\n-------------------kina: murdered, killed, death, in mortal danger-a noun used for someone who is marked for death by someone or something.\n---------------\nkrafeh: corpse\n-------------------krey: single. kreyn - pair.\n-------------------lae: him\n-------------------lar: sturdy, steadfast.\n-------------------lareh: boulder, mountain, rock\n-------------------larebil: anvil\n------------------\nlarueth: netherrack\n-------------------laureh: chosen, favored, noble\n-------------------laurir: Noble\n-------------------len: song\n-------------------lenaern: inn\n-------------------lenniel: melody\n-------------------lent: to (over)grow\n-------------------\nlenti: growth, moss.\n-------------------lentos: brown\n-------------------leyu: graceful, beautiful.\n-------------------liewyn: smile - liewynh: to smile, liewyn'saer: to entertain, to amuse; maliewynh: to laugh\n-------------------\nlle: kindness, good intention\n-------------------lie: dishonest, untrue, false, deceitful -lien: lie , liear: to lie; maliear: to betray (malieir: traitor)\n-------------------llir: friend\n-------------------lin: home, place -linan'sae: town\n--------------\nllum: sorrowful, mourning - llum'saer: to sadden\n-------------------llyt: aggressive, intimidating, -llyth: to strike\n-------------------lom: to fragment, to splinter\n-------------------lomi: fragment, splinter, pebble\n------------------\nlomal: flint\n-------------------luci: grape - lucionn: sour\n-------------------luer:  to imprison, to cage \n-------------------luerlent: flowerpot\n-------------------lye: we - Used to speak of elves, a people, or even the world as a whole. Often misused.\n-------------------lyu: silent - leads to the words lyun: silence; lyuer: to silence and lyu'saer: to censor \n-------------------maehr: wisdom, knowledge\n-------------------maelu: to know\n-------------------mahnih: wall\n-------------------\nMali: elf/elven - Word is both singular and plural, noun and adjective.\n-------------------maln: father\n-------------------marn: more\n-------------------marenne: less\n-------------------masuleh: anvil\n-------------------medi: helping, helpful\n-------------------meracahe: balance\n-------------------miar: lava miar'sae: griefing, harming, spiting\n-------------------mira: warm\n-------------------miruel: red\n-------------------myumier: to carry, to bring\n------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Elven Part 2", "Anthron", "Continuation of Seed words from part 1\n1 - 27\n-------------------\nCurious Words 28- and on to part 3\n-------------------The credit for this dictionary goes to the maker, Sporadic whom made the post to make this book possible on the forums.\nnae: you\n-------------------naeri: devout one, cleric\n-------------------narn: to walk, travel through\n-------------------nealu: to teach\n-------------------nor: land - nor'sae: farming\n-------------------\no: why\n-------------------ohn: like - Either a prefix or stand-alone\n-------------------oment: to meet\n-------------------okar: to safeguard\n-------------------okarn: oasis\n-------------------orrar: to hunt\n-------------------\nothelu: sharp\n-------------------parir: harbinger\n-------------------pern: potato\n-------------------parsaer: to conceive, to kindle. \"to have an idea\". \n-------------------perith: to remember\n-------------------puer: to write, to draw, to scribble.\n-------------------puerith: to write down (of books), to memorize. to record (more formal than 'puer')\n-------------------riv: claw \n-------------------riurn: swamp\n-------------------\nraell: carrot, root, herb. (refers to subterranean parts of plants possessing healing or nourishing properties)\n-------------------san: word, news - saner: to speak\n-------------------saneyr: to debate, discuss. - saneyir: debater, public speaker, orator.\n-------------------salum: to feel, to sense\n-------------------seth: void\n-------------------sew: soup, stew\n-------------------siimah: tower\n-------------------sil: sword\n-------------------siol: lone, lonely\n-------------------\nsirame: Honor; connection to the forest. - Has no plural\n-------------------siru: mushroom -siruonn: bitter\n-------------------siyuer: to play\n-------------------\nsohae: devout one, cleric - In a militant or executive sense. sohaer: ruler (through teachings, more positive than uthir.)\n-------------------suika: sugar -\n-------------------sul: light - strictly a noun.\n-------------------sulier: to see\n-------\nsulii: eye\n-------------------sulirrin: glowstone\n-------------------taeleh: mind\n-------------------taelu: to learn\n-------------------tahorran: hawk\n-------------------tahu: high\n-------------------tahn: peak, height\n------------------\ntalar: horizon - considered a place between the heavens and earth;\n-------------------talareh: stone - evolved from the words tali and lareh.\n-------------------\ntaliyna: body, living being, aspect -'taliiyna' can be used to denoted the physical parts that allow the body to live, i.e. organ, heart, mind and blood\n-------------------taliiyh: to bleed\n-------------------taliyu: secret\n-------------------\nTalonnii: family, blood(line) - always capped\n-------------------tarem: Elven week -Equivalent to 7 'karim'\n-------------------tayna: life, energy of living\n-------------------taynei: green\n-------------------\ntaynuel: vitality, energetic, alive (noun or adverb dependent on positioning)\n-------------------tenna: until\n-------------------tennallar: ocean\n-------------------\nterh: to grind, process, churn - wehn'tehral: bread; valein'tehral: cheese; raell'tehral: salve, potion), luci'terhal: wine\n-------------------\ntiuth: triangle - the triangular shape is found as a symbol for oppression, unlike the circle, which is used to describe (just) councils; - taliuth: oppressor\n-------------------thruer: to explode\n-------------------thrur: explosive, volatile\n------------\nthrurn: explosive, dynamite\n-------------------thill: pure, refined, delicate\n-------------------thilln: silver\n-------------------thul: raw, unrefined, brusque\n-------------------thulith: metal\n-------------------thuln: ore, raw material\n-------------------tilru: serving, submissive\n-------------------tir: law\n-------------------tos: desert, wasteland, barren ground - tos'sae: razing\n-------------------tufer: to construct, to prop\n-------------------\ntur: bone\n-------------------turr: sheep\n-------------------tuva: everything, all\n-------------------\ntuveh: wool, something soft\n-------------------ueth: nether\n-------------------uhier: to seek\n-------------------\nulln: rot, withering - strictly a noun.\n-------------------ullr: rot, decay, wither - Often of dead flora.\n-------------------ullral: monster, undead -lit: decayed. Used for living beings that have severed themselves from the natural way.\n----------------\nuradh: to scowl.\n-------------------uradir: naysayer\n-------------------uriar: to shout\n-------------------urth: to rule - negative connotation to this word.\n-------------------urthir: ruler\n-------------------maruthir: tyrant\n------------------\nUruk: Orc\n-------------------ut: because\n-------------------uvul: powder\n-------------------Valah: human\n-------------------vallei: water\n-------------------valein: milk\n-------------------vallel: blue\n------------------\nvallum: crying, griefing\n-------------------valmir: artist - from purple, the color of art.\n-------------------valmuel: purple\n-------------------van: to fare\n-------------------Velulaei: moon - Named after the moon goddess worshiped by the dark elves.\n-------------------vihai: whisper\n-------------------vilut: cow\n-------------------vira: vigilant, mournful - Traditionally used for attending the wake of vigil for a deceased Elf.\n-------------------vularale: bat\n-------------------\nvull: to deceive, to trick\n-------------------vuln: fox\n-------------------waleh: to heal\n-------------------wehn:  grass, grain.\n-------------------welier: to listen, to hear - rewelier: to repeat, to echo\n-------------------\nwy: appendage - more useful are the words that can be formed in combination with 'an*h': anah'wy: head; anoh'wy: foot, anih'wy: left hand, aneh'wy: right hand; anuh'wy: hand (either)\n-------------------wyl: while\n-------------------wyn: happy\n------------\ny: upon\n-------------------yallr: to live.\n-------------------yuln: gemstone - Used as the seed for many words, including maleyuln: diamond\n-------------------\nCURIOUS WORDS\nNo doubt you are left with many questions as you skim through the Elven wordlist. Indeed, their mystique and unique language has many intricacies which are not readily understood by those who did not take ample time studying them.\nFor perusal at your leniency, I have taken apart the words with most reason to spark confusion, and gave them the special attention they require in this section.\n-------------------\nito:\nThis particle is a means to denote location. However, it has many different meanings, depending on its location and accompanying words in a sentence.\nThe simplest case:\nito narne: I/he walk(s) here / I/he walk(s) within.\nNo ambiguity arises here. However, when we add a noun to this:\name ito narne: The forests walks here\nito ame narne: I/he walk(s) to the forest.\name'ito narne: I/He walk(s) within the forest\nameto'eyha narne: And I/he walk(s) within the forest\name'eyha ito narne: And the forest walks here.\nNote that the location of ito becomes crucial here. Putting it on the place of a subject aligns it to the meaning 'to'. On the object's location\n(to understand this, educate yourself on the elven sentence order), the noun 'ame' becomes the subject instead, and ito regains the meaning 'within' or 'here'.\nIto can also be used as a suffix, which is demonstrated by the last examples. In this case, the\naddition of ito restricts the noun to an object.\nThis word is also used to create the elvish equivalent to the words 'to be' and 'to have'. This particularly might confuse a novice to the language. to read upon this, I refer you to the grammar section of\nthis tome.\n-------------------tali-:\nThis word can do two very different things to the word it is connected to. In the simplest case, it adds the modifier 'part of' to the linked noun. But sometimes, the addition of this prefix creates a whole new word:\ntalibortu: Part dwarf -> Halfling\ntalivalah: Part human -> Halfling\ntal'uruk: Part Orc -> Goblin.\n\nHowever, sometimes ambiguity can abound from this word. For example:\ntaliame: Tree\ntal'ame: Part of the forest.\n\nIt would seem that in confusing cases, elves add an apostrophe between to denote they mean multiple words rather than a single noun. However, this is not always a safe rule,\nas it may clash with other rules for using apostrophes. Caution is urged, and ambiguity may indeed arise.\n--------------------sae:\nThis word, meaning the development, spreading or management of something, can be used to create many new words in elvish\nSome of these may not seem obvious. Examples include:\n\nnor'sae: development of land -> farming\ntos'sae: spreading of desert -> pillaging\nThe combinations grow even more numerous when we consider that sae can be combined with\nir to create sair, lending a word for, exemplum gratia, 'farmer' and 'pillager'. It can also be turned to saean to create a \nplural (where applicable) and saer, turning the word into the stem of a verb, effectively giving us the words 'to farm' and\n'to pillage'.\nThese further combinations exist almost always wherever a word was created from the suffix sae. Knowledge of this fact will allow the reader much more affluency in this language.\n-------------------\nma-:\nApart from being an intensifier, used at your leisure, the prefix ma- often finds its home in places where the intense use of affix would cause the same affix to start. An example of this is found in the word 'log': The elves would consider a log\n'part of tree' thus 'part of a part of the forest'. However, talitaliame is NOT a correct word to use in Elven.\nInstead, the second tali is implied by the use of the intesifier. Thus:\nmataliame: Log\nIf used in an event where a repeated suffix is used, ma- is placed after the seed word, but before the suffix one wishes to repeat.\nInterestingly enough, ma- is one of the rare affixes that does stack on certain occasions, as seen in the word marmatelu.\n-------------------onn:\n\nThis word is much like tali, in that it can be used to further define a certain word, as well as be used to create a noun of it's own. Also like tali, he inclusion of an apostrophe in a confusing case will imply the speaker is\nmeaning to talk of multiple words\nAn example:\n\name'onn: Born of the Forest, from the forest.\namonn: wood\nThe suffix will create a myriad of new words for the advanced speaker. Study of its usage will surely be beneficial.\n-------------------fer:\n\ngrammatically, nothing is strange about this word. However, its uses in combinations are so numerous that a separate section may be devoted to it.\nfer'ame: Axe\nfer'thuln: Pickaxe\nfer'nor: shovel\nfer'sul: torch\nfer'bilok: hammer\nfer'norsae: hoe\nfer'puer: quill. Pen. A tool for writing.\nOther uses can be thought up by the cunning mind. However, bear in mind that the word fer is mostly used to speak of handheld tools, not of crafting tables, anvils or furnaces.\n--", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Elven Part 3", "Anthron", "Curious words as a continuation from part 2. 1 - 4\n-------------------Elven Grammar 5 - 41\n------------------\nElven counting 42 - 45\n-------------------more on part 3\n-------------------\nAgain, more thanks to Sporadic for making the post!\nan*h- (a/o/i/e/u):\n\nBy adding one these five vowels into the place of the asterisk the prefix takes on a new usage. This prefix gains many new meanings when combined with other affixes and relies heavily on context.\nSentence order is especially important when using this prefix multiple times.\nElan*h [a/o/i/e]: North, South, East and West respectively.\n\nanh'sae: expanding, stretching - replacing the apostrophe with a vowel specifies in which direction.\nan*h il'an*h: - refers to a diagonal path, defined by the vowel used.\n-------------------\nElven Grammar.\n-------------------Sentence Order: The common order of elvish sentences is Subject-object-verb.\n\nPlural nouns: indicated by the suffix -an.\nThe apostrophe: Used in certain cases and possibly dictates a certain pronunciation.\nCurrent known uses are:\n\n*Denoting certain honorifics (such as sainted)\n*Between a modifier and a verb\n*Between a word and its suffixes (more on this below).\n*With the word 'eyha' (and) to connect sentences and and in terms of a list.\nUse of affixes: This has shown to be a very important factor in Elven language. Elves, tend to use multiple affixes to further define their nouns and verbs, rather than using separate words. For these, the following rules exist:\n*Most affixes seems to have two forms, depending on wether or not the word it relates to ends or begins with a vowel\n*Suffixes often get added with an apostrophe between it and the word.\n*If a word has multiple suffixes, there will only be an apostrophe between the full word and its last suffix. The priority in ordering the suffixes remains unknown.\n*If a suffix is seperated by the apostrophe, it inflects as if the last letter of the word it relates to was a consonant.\n\nRecombination of words:\nWhen one understands the heavy use of affixes and their combining to forge words,\nit is not surprising that the elves relied on a dictionary where this recombination was prevalent in creating new words. \nTheir core words were little, but their abundant use of affixes and linking words still allowed them to describe nearly anything\nunder the sun.\nExamples of this are:\nnarn'vallei: travel'water -> swim\nnarn'acaele: travel'sky -> fly\nathrinarn'acaele: serpenttraveling'sky -> Dragon.\npar'karinah: Before the sunrise -> Dawn\npar'ker: Before the sunset -> Dusk.\nuvul'igne: Firepowder -> Ash\nuvul'thrurn: Explosive powder -> Gunpowder\n\nWe also see this occuring a lot when the word tali is involved.\nMany more examples may be discovered by the studious scholar soon. Take heed, however, that any particular combination, while perhaps comprehensible, may not be correct. The language of nature seems very particular on what words may coexist in harmony.\n-------------------Affiliation: The suffix 'leh (note the apostrophe) designates affiliation, the possession of the object by the subject.\nNote: If no object is present, the suffix is implied to mean something similar to 'lives' or 'spirit'. However,\nit is not placed in translation\nEx: part of a common farewell 'kaean'leh evareh', means 'may (it) protect our spirit' literally, but is translated to 'may (it) protect us'.\n-------------------\nKnown inflections of the elven verbs:\n\nIn this section, the dash indicates the stem of the word.\n\n*-e: First person singular\n\n*-a: Second person singular\n*-e: Third person singular\n*-ae: First person plural\n*-an: second person plural\n*-eyae: Third person plural\n*-eh: Optative singular\n*-erih: Optative plural The optative inflection changes slightly depending on the ending letters of a\nverb. Most verbs end in -er, but if one ends in -ar the plural inflection of the optative becomes -arih ( the -ar- syllable is not repeated!). A verb ending in -h will have the -h- replaced by the full inflection of the optative (thus eth becoming eteh\nand eterih. Other irregular verbs have the inflection simply added to the end.\n\n*The stem of a verb functions as a singular imperative.\n*The stem of a verb used as a suffix to a noun (apostrophe where required) is a modifier\n*The optative serves as a wish ('may' + verb) in most cases. However, adding the negative (-ne) affix after the verb indicates the lack of permission.\n-------------------Pronouns as a subject:\nA pronoun is usually not used to denote the subject of a word, as the inflection of the verb itself would usually denote in which person the verb is denoted. However, on occasion a rather critical ambiguity may arise, like in the following example:\name ignere: The forest burns.\nShould we 'assume' a pronoun here, we can suggest that this sentence may also be translated as 'I burn the forest' or even 'he burns the forest'. This ambiguity is too serious to ignore, and therefore we are expected\nto place another pronoun here as the subject if we wish to denote an action like such:\n\nkae ame ignere: I burn the forest.\nKnow that a pronoun used as a subject alone never gains the suffix 'leh' (this is possible when it is an object, making the implied translation \"spirit\".)\n-------------------Infinitive:\nAn infinitive can be made by tying two verbs together with an apostrophe and adding an 'o' ('or-') prefix to the second verb (the infinitive). The first verb is usually the assisting verb (possibilities include can, must, will) and needs to be the only\nstem.\nThe infinitive verb receives the inflections similar to the way to a simple, single verbed sentence would.\nBy Example:\nito ame ern'onarna: You can travel to the woods\nAn infinitve can also occur without an assisting verb. In this case, you shall add an o prefix to the verb, but no inflection. An example of this:\nito ame onarn: to travel to the woods.\nTake note that the infinitive must not be used to express a wish, as only the optative form may serve this purpose.\nPast and future tense:\n\nTo create a past or future tense, we first need to take notice to the time of day. The words an elf uses for tenses depends on whether it's day or night at the time of speaking.\nFor a past or future tense, we add one of these four words at the very end of a sentence:\nkarin'ento: next sunrise\nkarin'ante: last sunrise\nker'ento: next sunset\nker'ante: last sunset\nThough elves have taken to shortening this to karinto, karinte, kento and kente in more casual speech.\nIf it is night, we use ker'ante for past, and karin'ento for future tense.\nIf it is day, we use karin'ante for past, and ker'ento for future tense.\n\nThis remains true even if the time period one wishes to denote is more than one sunset or sunrise from the time of speaking.\n-------------------\nThe verbs 'to be' and 'to have'\nBefore reading this, you might find it beneficial to have read about the word 'ito' in the 'CURIOUS WORDS' section.\nNote that:\nito kae: To him / on him\nito kae'leh: To his spirit / on his spirit ('spirit' being implied)\nNow, should we place a noun in front of this:\nmali ito kae: An elf to him. -In elvish, this is the equivalent of 'He has an elf'.\nmali ito kae'leh: An elf to his spirit. The equivalent of 'He is an elf'.\nIt becomes easy to mix these meanings up. After all, kae'leh is the possessive form and seems the logical candidate for the verb 'to have'.\nHowever, the implied addition of 'spirit' is very important here. Elves speak of their spirit, or essence, as\nsomething deeply intimate. When something belongs to you as a person, you have it. But when something belongs to your essence, you are it.\n-------------------\nCAPITALIZATION\n\nElves do not capitalize the word at the beginning of a sentence the way we do in common. Instead, only on a select few occasions are words capitalized, namely:\n\n*Names (of persons, places, titles)\n*Races (Mali, Valah, etc.)\n*Objects of worship (Usul, Velulaei), even when the word's not used to denote the divine being tied to the object\n*When denoting aspects of nature (such as Vuln being the aspect fox.)\n*Words of significant concepts are sometimes capitalized, such as 'lye', 'talar', 'acaele' and 'tuva'\n-------------------\nELVEN COUNTING\n\nElves, while their numerical system remains a subject of discussion, were able to write numbers 'in full' like we are. That is to say, they could name numbers of any size in regular conversation.\nAn Elven number, when expressed in full, consists of multiple words. Each word represents an order of magnitude. They were written in descending order, meaning the largest part of the number came first.\nElves had words for the numbers one to ten, and words for a hundred, a thousand, and so on. To denote multiples of hundred,\nhey would take a number from one to ten, and put it in front of a word denoting an order of magnitude, linking the two with an\naprostrophe\nDiscovered words for elven numbers are as follows:\n1: oem\n2: niut\n3: hael\n4: vailu\n5: kulin\n6: banih\n7: laier\n8: esun\n9: moiel\n10: telu\n100: matelu [ma-(mar-) a preffix for 'very']\n1000: marmatelu\n-------------------CONVENTIONS OF THE ELVEN LANGUAGE \n-continues to part 4-", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Elven Part 4", "Anthron", "Continuarion of part 3!\n-------------------CONVENTIONS OF THE ELVEN LANGUAGE 1 - 7\n-------------------\nThis is the last book, so final thanks to Sporadic for making these books possible on the forums!\nThe elven tongue was almost exclusively spoken. Evidence for this is found in the ruins of Inwe, where the writings of early Dark Elves were in an ancient dialect of the common tongue. The most often used elven words in writing are names\nsuch as Mali'nor (now Malinor) and Velulaei.\nWhatever caused the language to change so drastically through the ages is not known, but is especially remarkable due to the long lives of elves, which would presumably make evolution of a language go much slower.\nIt is suggested that a taboo on elvish was enforced, though why and by who remains unknown.\nIt has been rumored that elvish was also the language of nature, which the elves either learned through study or was taught to them by certain deities.\nThey then had the power to converse with nature directly, allowing\nthem to guide the growth of trees and migration of animals as if by magic. If this were true, elvish, assuming someone was capable of mastering the long-forgotten cadence of the words, would be a very potent language indeed.", ""),
        StaticBook("OLD OAKS MENU", "Buernoc Silvervein", "=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=OLD OAKS TAVERN MENU =-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\nFare\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ Tavern Bread\n- 1 mina\nBaked Fish\n- 3 mina\nHarrison Fish\n- 4 mina\nFresh Taters \n- 4 mina\nAcacian Honey\n- 5 mina\nFrostin' Cake\n- 7 mina\nDrinks\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ALES, 3 mina\n==========\nAle; pale, stout, bitter, brown, golden, ruby.\nAdria Pale Ale\nCarpenter's Spiced Ale Bronze Ale\nWINES, 5 mina\n===========\nHOUSE SPECIAL;\nCarrion Black\n~~~~~~~~~~\nWine; red, white.\nRose' Wine\nAeldinic Wine\nCuronian Wine\nDingle Juice\nVODKAS, 3 mina\n============\nVodka\nSilmaen Vodka\n\nSPIRITS, 6 mina\n=============\nWhiskey\nEsterian Whiskey\nRum\nTequila\nGin\nTriple Sec\nAmaretto\nAbsinthe\n\nEXOTICS\n=======\nCarrion Black\n- 5 mina\nCream Beer 1649\n- 10 mina\nMare's Milk Brew\n- 10 mina\nStrawberry Ale\n- 10 mina\nLayman's Beer\n- 10 mina\nBlackberry Mead\n- 10 mina\nCorn Bear\n- 10 mina\nEggnog\n- 10 mina\nWinter Apple Cider\n- 10 mina\nMeadowsweet Beer\n- 10 mina\nBeer o' Borgin\n- 10 mina\nThe Dark Bards Brew\ncirca 1655\n- 10 mina\nBlack Rose Rum circa 1520\n- 10 mina\nAnbella's Brews; hearth lager, hearth mead, hearth pale-ale, hearth hard-cider.\n- 6 mina\nNon-alcoholics, 3 mina\n===================Water\nFresh Brewed Coffee\nHearth-Heat Coffee\nGreen Tea\nPomegranite Juice\nBrew For Cameron", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Report", "Algar", "Nyna Erwynn\nRace - Snow Elf\nFaith - N/A\nTitle - Commoner\n\nBackground\n\nN/A\nTaelisonial\nRace - Dark Elf\nFaith - Spirits (Open for Change)\nTitle - Commoner\n\nBackground\n\nBorn in carverns of his kin (Dark Elves) Little of his kin left and merged with dominion he like Rivia for work and life\nRobb William Charles Lands\nRace - Human\nFaith - Cannonist\nTitles - Commoner\n\nBackground\n\nFamily memebers dead\nDuke recruited him now is a guard for Rivia", ""),
        StaticBook("Old Song", "Simon Birchenwald", "((The paper is yellowed with age.))\n\nIn an old castle's halls\n\ndrifting to and fro the walls\n\nis a shadow with nothing to do.\n\nIt stops to rest with a sigh like the wind\nthen continues to drift on its way.\n\nIn life, she was one with a radiant smile\n\nSpreading merriment and joy where she went\n\nHer eyes were like diamonds, her head held a crown\nThough the purest of souls, to the Skies was not sent.\n\n\nShe died not too long after her throne was stolen\n\nstolen by one who had no need for it.\n\nHer short life was taken by stones and\na sword\n\nA cold broken figure tossed into a pit\n\n\nSo still wanders she\n\nthrough crumbling walls\n\nand old castle halls that she knew\nwaiting for someone\n\nthough no one knows who\n\na shadow with nothing to do.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Dragonkin", "Aruzond, Warden of the North", "On Dragonkin\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWritten and recorded by Aruzond, Warden of the North\nThere are two species of dragonkin known to have descended from Dragur, though corrupted and defiled forms of both have formerly existed. Dragur, the Daemon of Knowledge, oftentimes appears as a dragon in his true form.\nDragur’s chief descendants, the Dragaar, are sentient “greater dragons” that seek to collect and share knowledge with mortals. They can conceal themselves under the guise of mortals and other creatures, though it is a rare occasion to meet a Dragaar in\nperson. Dragons, on the other hand, are more common -- though proportionately rare compared to other living beings -- than greater dragons. They are generally referred to as dragons, though the proper classification\nis “lesser dragon.” They are non sentient, and are commonly viewed as natural predators that roam our world. However, like all living beings, they are susceptible to taint and corruption. Though a rare occasion, dragons have been known to alter their\nvery nature into a twisted, foul portrayal consumed by hatred and rage for the mortal races. The outcome of this calamity is referred to as a drake. Little is known about the purpose of the dragonkin as a whole, except that each species' intentions vary\ngreatly. \n\nDragon\n \n    The dragon (or lesser dragon) species is beastlike in nature, and generally accepted to be non sentient. Though they cannot process thought or comprehend concepts, they are highly\nintelligent in regards to instinct. The lesser dragon was once a rare sight to mortals, but they have appeared to exist in greater numbers in Anthos. Particularly, dragons roam the frozen wastelands of the North. Though they live in other regions\nof Anthos, the frigid North is home to many deep caves and caverns, which they prefer for nesting purposes. The region is cold, secluded, and tribesmen allow the food supply to remain steady. Dragons may roam the land of Anthos in search of cattle\nor mortals if they grow tired of pork flesh, and they continue to hunt until they are satisfied. Although lesser dragons have been frequently encountered in recent times, their numbers are slowly dwindling as they have begun to retreat to the deep,\ncold North.\n\nDrake\n \n    “Do not underestimate the allure of darkness, mortal. Your kind has yet to discover that even the purest of souls are drawn to it.” -Aruzond.\nThrough the malevolent desires of twisted corruption, the dragon has the potential to unwillingly alter its very existence. When a dragon degrades into a drake, its body decays into a shadowy skeleton of its former self.\nThe scales of a drake turn black as midnight, and their fangs cloak themselves in putrefying poison. While a drake does not develop sentience, its desires can be manipulated to follow any malignant alignment. Drakes forfeit any connection to their\nformer selves, and their lust for eternal damnation of life causes them to instill fear into those who would oppose it. The drake is slightly smaller in size compared to a dragon, but what it lacks in size and physical strength is compensated\nby maneuverability and lethality. It is rare to encounter an evil powerful enough to twist and taint the mind of the mighty dragon, but these influences communicate through our world more readily than we may often realize.\nDragaar\n \n    Bestowed with the gift of immortality and sentience, the Dragaar exist chiefly to seek and gather knowledge. Each Dragaar is assigned the role of gathering a distinct aspect of knowledge, and this role defines their characteristics\nand demeanor. However, they do not solely desire knowledge and wisdom. The greater dragons, or Dragaar, act as ever watching wardens over the mortal races. However, most prefer to live in seclusion  in deep thought and meditation, only to emerge when\nthe races call upon them in their time of need. The Dragaar can and often disguise themselves under the guise of a mortal or creature. This is their preferred method of watching over mortals, as it is both subtle and inconspicuous. There are only\ntwo Dragaar that have revealed themselves to the mortal races, and the decision to do so was not lightly concluded. Though the Dragaar seek to protect the mortal races, they often decide to do so by living in secrecy. Many discern that if they\nchose to associate themselves with mortal affairs too frequently, dire consequences would arise. The primary concern held by Dragaar, in regards to involvement in the matters of mortals, is that the races would eventually resort to\nrelying on them to protect mortals from any form of evil. However, the greater dragons aspire to teach the mortal races self-preservation, without them depending on the intervention of immortals.\nDrakaar\n\nTo attempt to bend the will of a Dragaar would be all for naught, and thus what can cause a Dragaar to devolve itself into a twisted abomination of hatred is unknown. The ancient ancestors of the four mortal races once believed that\nthe choice for this horrendous transformation to occur was their own, though the aftermath of such a decision would contradict their entrusted duty. The greater dragon itself is a terrifying opponent, but a Dragaar that feels no remorse and fears\nno consequence? That is the true fear of corruption; the perversion of the mind and distortion of one’s morality is a dreadful circumstance. In past times, the outcome of such an event would often be referred to as a “greater drake.”\nIt is the combination of a Dragaar’s sentience and a drake’s all-consuming hatred. The likelihood of a Dragaar devolving into a being tormented by rage is next to none, as most would, in their right mind, turn themselves into stone to prevent the\nconversion. The only verifiable event recorded of a Dragaar turning to stone is that of Velketzar. The Guardian Velketzar, consumed by self-condemnation and despair due to his failure, dramatically transformed into a stone statue\nto prevent the inevitable calamity. If a Dragaar were to fall under the hand of corruption, it would hold the power to politically corrupt nations with ease. Additionally, detecting and pursuing such a foe would be toilsome, all due to its shape shifting\nability. Fortunately, deep meditation and concentration can inhibit this rare occurrence, along with immersing themselves in their aspect of knowledge.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Dragos", "kido122", "On Dragons\nThere Life and Death\n\n      By Sam King\nChapter 1: Birth\n\n Dragons are, known by most everyone, born by egg much like our domesticated and less dangerous, Chicken. Ounce the egg is laid it goes on a one month incubation period. The mother dragon will warm her eggs with her belly,\nlaying next to to it, gently mumuring away, like a loud rumbling purr, as she increases her internal heat. She would do this for hours at a time for about a month, until the time the eggs hatch, at which point the egg now begins its life as a hatchling.\nChapter 2: Hatchling\n \n After the egg hatch's, the hatchling will, if all goes well, stand on its four legs, strecthing its wings for the first time. It is important to note that dragons are not yet able to fly at this young age, and won't be able\nquite some time. Dragons at this age are around the size of a wolf, and are thought to be relativly tame and kind, much like a puppy. For its first week a hatchling will wander around its nesting site, never traveling out of eye sight of its mother.\nIt is during the second week of a hatchlings life that is left alone, as the mother goes to hunt to provide both her and her hatchlings hunger. The Hatchling is then left to its own accord, and begins to hunt small rodents and animals. The Third month is\nwhen the hatchling is now able to hunt on its own, under normal circumstances, and is when the fires within begin to bubble up, though not able to breath its deadly fire, it is good to note, smoke can be seen from their nostrils and mouth. When the\nhatchling reaches a year of age, is when it is left alone and now considered a Drake, or \"Teenager\".\n\n\n\n  Chapter 3: Drake\n(Next Page)\nDrake are still unable to use its deadly fire, but its bow a fierce and dangerous hunter, around the size of horse and rather grumpy. This age is often considered to be their \"Awkward\" phase in their life., as they are prone to explore great distances for\nno appairent reason, which is why they where said to be the most commonly sighted age of a Dragon. They have also been said to have caused the most havoc, as they are for some reason, really agressive and proned to attack anyone who got to near to them.\nChapter 4: Adult\n\n Little is know about adult dragons, as they were rarely ever said to be sighted. What is known how ever is at this stage is whena dragon is now able to, 1-Breath Fire, 2-Fly, and 3-Mate. Adult dragons are thought to be rather\nunagressive, except for a few circumstance which I will get to soon, as they have been rarley sighted and don't attack often, if at all. Noe the mating rituals of dragons is, ofcourse, unknown, mostly likely lost in time. What is known is this, they\nbecome very agressive and is one of the few times they are said to be. During their mating season, time is also unkonw, is when they are said to attack towns, as when a Adult has its nesting site picked, nothing will stop it from nesting their, even if it\nis already occupied. It is also worthy to note that the legend and myth that dragons have a affinity to treasures, is neither proven or disproven, though most likely false. As to why and what purpose a dragon would horde treasure is unknown, except to\npossibly attract potential mates.\n\n\n\nChapter 5: Wyrm's\n\n Almost nothing is known about Wyrms, other then they are some of the oldesy and anciet dragons to ever \"Exist\". When an adult\nbecomes a wyrm is unknown, what is know though is that they are to be feared, extremly feared.\n\nChapter 6: Death\n\n Natural deaths hav enever been know or spoken of for dragons. The only few deaths of dragons\nspoken of is caused by few curagous knights/wizards, even then this legends and stories have no real reason to be thought of as fact in nearly all occasions.\nAuthors Note:\n \n This entire book is put together by a few years of researhc into myths and lengend s of these grand beast. Nothing written in this book is inherently fact, and should not be treated as such. This is just the most reasonable\npossibility's concerning \"Dragons\" few, if not no, facts on these beast exist. \n\nDedication is to all who enjoy the mysterious and unknown in the, as well as to those who enjoy our history, though this it not, per say \"History\"", ""),
        StaticBook("On Dreadknights", "The Eternal Librarian", "On Dreadknights\n\n by Cir'dian Nymphea\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Annil’sul, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Eternal Librarian\nGenesis\nThe dreadknights are beings comprised of suits of armor bound together through the engraving of specific runes unique to the blood mages, of whom draw their magic from a deity presently unknown to me. They originated in the land of Asulon,\nas did their constructs (The dreadknights). As it stands however, it is somewhat of a mystery as to where the blood mages came from, and how their magic came to be. However it is known that the dreadknights are the tools of the blood mages. They are the\nstrength behind them.\n\nCreation\nThe dreadknights are created over the process of several months through a long and arduous ritual involving the removal of freedom and physical flesh. The process begins with the abduction of a\nspecific choice being. The selection is not bound to physical aspects (Which would be removed in the end anyway) but rather decided by the quality of those taken. Usually of whom are stubborn and loyal to whom they serve. In post of their abduction- the\npatron is taken to which ever stronghold the dreadknights would presently occupy. From there they would be bound. The dreadlord then begins the process with the destruction of both knee caps, as to prevent escape and standing. No sedatives are used in\nthis process. The patron is then fitted with a suit of armor usually comprised of a metal known as black iron (Known for being particularly dense, and durable). The leader then engraves several runic symbols into the armor of the victim. This can be done\nby both dreadlord, and blood mage. These runes bind the soul of said victim to the suit of armor. Once finished, the subject is cast into a cell, and left for several days before further work is done. For the next few weeks the victim is tortured, their\nrunes left open to rot. Flesh eventually gives way, leaving nothing but the victim’s skeletal form beneath. Alongside this, the will of the victim is broken, and they are taught to love pain. By two months, the process is complete, and the new dreadknight\nmay now set out to do the will of their dreadlord or blood mage.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Enchanting", "Sarrion", "On Arcane Enchanting\n--------------->\nBy Sarrion Zytiaear\n\nThe following are my own personal notes taken from my research from interviews with other Transfigurationists and my lessons from Avenel.\nIn Transfiguration there is a sub-classed spell base called Enchanting. Enchanting is the simple art of transmuting either a command for an object or a spell  to bind to an object with a medium\nground  that powers the spell. This medium ground is almost always a mana crystal, which is any gem though the rarer the gem the more mana it can hold. The transfigurationist is to first channel his/her mana into this gem and fill it entirely\nwith his mana, then transmute the spell or command into the gem and bind it to the object arcanely. This whole progress burns /a lot/ of mana in the mage's mana pool, and it a dangerous art that can either kill the mage\nor cause a mana fluctuation. This is why that sometimes a mage may set up an enchanting lab with a “Mana Obelisk”, for those who are ignorant in the topic a Mana Obelisk is a large gem pillar that has\nbeen enchanted to contain a large mass of mana, that way when it comes time to enchant the enchanter can pull the mana from the crystal to the gem, not having to use their own mana.\nDo note the creation of a Mana Obelisk is very intricate and will need to be activated by two or more Transfigurationists.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Lyres", "Daisy Applefoot", "There once was a lass named Lire, who lived in the lands of the Shire. One day Lire caught a very large instrument with many strings, and she named it after herself. That's why Lyres have such a funky name", ""),
        StaticBook("On Mali'fenn", "Ila Galanthus", "A Theory on the Relationship of Thanhium and Mali'fenn Physical and Mental Mutations\n\nWritten by: Ila Galanthus\nSnow elves, Mali'fenn, snelves, whatever we may be called we are among the most hated and reviled cultures. An offshoot of the mali'aheral, or high elves, we have several distinctive qualities such as our incredibly pale skin and hair, and cold skin.\nUnfortunately we are also known for our tendancies to lean on the less sane side of the spectrum. While members of other groups can be insane and unstable, it seems to come in higher, more consistant numbers with the Mali'fenn.\n\nI suspect a single culprit\nin all of these mostly passive mutations: thanhium. After hours of thought and study on the once rare ore, I realized the effects of it's poisoning are remarkably similar to my kin's mutations.\n\nI do not believe this is curable, however. Perhaps a group\nof impure high elves were cast out of the silver city, and ended up settling near a vein. Unknown to them they ate tainted food, drank tainted water, breathed tainted air. Many likely died, but I doubt the onset of insanity allowed them to realize this.\nBut, of course, some survived. They multiplied, their children born with trace amounts of ore in their blood. They grew resistant to the toxin, but it still chilled and paled our flesh.\n\nThe worst effect was it's icy grip on their minds, driving them\nmad ever so slowly. Other races determined it as a parasite among our people, and anyone who joined them would begin to feel the same effects of the toxic ore all around them.\n\nOf course, this is speculation. However it is firm in my mind this is indeed\nthe origin and cause of my people.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Purity", "Quinn", "On Purity\n    An Opinion Piece\n\n \n\n\n\n\nBy: Quinn M. Faberry\nWhen asked what purity means to me, I really didn’t know. Those questions are still ringing in my ears. \nWhat is purity?\n\nWho decides what is pure in the world?\nWhat does it mean to protect that purity? \n\nThere is so much to consider, and it’s all quite personal. \n\nIn my personal opinion, purity is when things are as they should be.\nOkay, who decides that?\n\nIf I were to wield the light of Tahariae, would it be in my right to use my best judgement to decide what is pure?\nPerhaps it’s Tahariae that decides what is pure, and I am to trust in my faith to guide me in enforcing his judgements.\n\nThinking on it more, I believe the world decides. Everything was one way. It was created that way and should stay that way.\nThe evils of the world corrupt things and change them to something they shouldn’t be.\n\nIblees is one of the most notable examples. He tainted the world, raised undead, and cursed all of the Descendants.\nHe corrupted what was once pure and twisted it to his suit evil desires. To this day, undead, monstrous abominations roam the world, leaving a horrid scar on what is natural and beautiful.\nI believe nature decides what is pure.\n\nThat is further expanded upon by Tahariae’s words and tenants.\nTo protect that purity, we must fight against the ones who wish to taint it, and we must lead others towards the same goals as our own.\n\nTogether, the Clerics stand against the darkness that wishes to take hold of all that is righteous in the world.\nThat is what I wish to do as well. \n\nI feel my place in all of this is to fight against the evils of the world, to heal others, and to protect the innocent people.\nI wish to provide them with sanctuary from the taint that would corrupt their souls while guiding them down the better path.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Shamanism V1", "Thurak'Yar", "Scribed by the Farseer Thurak,\n14'th of SUn's Smile, 1487.\n1. Those Who Practise\n\n2. The Connection\n\n3. Traversal\n\n4. Utilisation\nThose Who Practise\n\nA magic almost strictly wielded by those of Krug’s descent, Shamanism is to the Orcs as Muuntrivazja is to the priests of the Kha’s; narrowly practised and highly revered. Those that fully understand the ways\nof the magic, divided into the sects of Elementalists, Lataumans, Witchdocters and Farseers, each have their own role in the Uruks’ society and all put the needs of their race above their own or any singular individual. Dark Shamanism,\na forbidden topic, shall not be discussed in this tome, as it holds no relevance to the topic being held. The first, and debatably most simple form of Shamanism, Elementalism, is based on making a connection to the Elemental Plane and the Spirits that\nreside there. A Shaman of this type, with the aid of his or her ‘bonded’ spirit(s), may control an element such as Earth or Fire that is present nearby in their own realm. It should be noted that this differs from Arcane Magic as it requires no\nconnection to the void and, rather than creating matter, simply manipulates that already existing. The next form of Shamanism, the practitioners of which are dubbed ‘Lataumans’, is much more complex. By moving their consciousness into\nthe realm of Ancestral Spirits, these shamans can contact the forms of those who were chosen as ‘honourable’ in life, and reside in a place more connected to ours than any other. The long dead such as Lur or even Krug himself (Although it has never\nbeen done) could be contacted for advice or information, and stronger Lataumans can gain blessings from these spirits; their strength or courage being ‘boosted’ for a short, albeit valuable, time, although this can’t be reproduced on\nothers by these Shamans.\nWitchdocters, the more ritualistic group of the subtypes, choose to meddle with the Immortal Spirits- those that live in a plane dedicated to the aspects of the mortal races.\nEvery emotion, every ideal and every thought can be categorised to a spirit, there, and the power of such spirits is used by Witchdocters to curse and plague those who are seen as a threat to the Shamans’ beliefs. They can do this on anything\nliving- including animals and plants, and as such these shamans are held in wary consideration by the Druids. They may also do the same with the Elementals, surprisingly- being able to call upon the lesser of such spirits to curse whomever\nthey wish. Another important part of Witchdoctery is the production of potions, which, although similar to alchemy, instead focuses on using ingredients that represent a certain spirit to call upon its power, and requires more thought on\nthe individual pieces than the brew as a whole.\nLastly, there are the Farseers. Sometimes called the Elders of the Uruks, these shamans spend their days traversing the Immortal Plane in search of enlightenment in cultural and\nhistorical matters. They bring their council to the Rex or their race as a whole, and act as the balancing force between the two planes. In much the same way as Witchdocters can curse, Farseers have the ability to bless\nplants or animals; being able to increase favourable attributes such as strength and resilience, but also those more intangible, such as hope. It is this reason why Farseers are so widely valued, as these blessings before battles or klomps prove to be\ninvaluable assets.\nThe Connection\n\nFor the following section, we’ll be referring to the connection of the Farseers to the Spirit Realm, as it is held as the both the most complex and developed form of the art among those who practise it; being one\nthat these Shamans use to constantly and fully transport their consciousness to another plane. This forced passage between realms begins when a Farseer cuts off the link between his consciousness and his body, and ends when he, or in turn\na Spirit controlling him, returns the stream to his mortal person. Unlike any other magic, the beginning of Shamanism actually requires the limitation of Mana being spent, rather than an increase in such. The regulation of mana use is vital in both\nentering and departing the spirit realm, and as such is vigorously practised by all Farseers. To let their mind wander to the place of spirits, they must almost entirely cut off the connection between their mind and their body-\nleaving only a trickle of mana as an anchor to return. When they wish to come back, they increase the mana flow to their mortal person, and their thoughts will begin to travel back to their body. Now, that being said, although controlling mana plays\na massive part in connection to the Spirit Realms, it isn’t so that anyone that can do such may actually make this connection. When an aspiring shaman is first taken on as a student, they will be put through several trials and tests, dictated\nby their teacher. Although they are sometimes seen as a filter to weed out the dedicated from the short-sighted, they are indeed much more; as a pupil’s action in these tests decide whether or not the spirits themselves will allow him or\nher to move their consciousness into their realm. An intangible filter of sorts is present, at which a group of minor spirits regulate the influx of those entering and leaving the Spirit Realm. Those that have been seen bearing positive\nattributes during these tests may be, for the first time, allowed to enter this new realm. It should be noted that the longer a Shaman has been connecting to the Spirit Realms for, the easier it will be for them to pass through the filter without\nthe spirits scrutinising over them- and as such it’s important for these Elder Shamans to do their best to regulate their own actions as honourable or otherwise.\nTraversal\n\nOnce a Shaman has connected to the Spirit Realm, an incomprehensible variety of circumstances may occur. For the first few times, chances are their senses will be dulled or non-existent as their\nmind struggles with the lack of bodily connection. Their vision may remain pitch black, and the only ‘input’ they receive may be a soft, niggling feeling of being watched. As time progresses, aspiring Shamans learn to deal with what\ninformation they’re given, and soon the senses return, albeit in situations that differ massively from those of the Mortal Realm. Their vision may be hued; the world they seen filtered as if through coloured glass. Hearing may\nbe non-existent, or they may hear cries far away as close as if whispered in their ears. The sense of feel usually comes last for those that travel the spirit realm, and it can be the most confusing of all to deal with. Sometimes, should they come\nacross a vision of a man being slaughtered, they would feel a phantom sense of pain- like a slash across their neck as they’re decapitated. It’s important for a Shaman to differentiate these Empathetic feelings to others from their\nown, especially in the Spirit Realm, as it’s been known to drive some blindly mad. Now, on to what actually occurs in this realm. When a Farseer, presumably with full use of his senses first enters the Spirit Realm, they'll find themselves, most likely,\nin an environment they haven’t yet seen. It might be a dense forest or a dank swamp; either way, a Shaman learns quickly to adapt when they traverse the spirit realm. With them is usually their Spirit Guide; a creature in a form important\nto them or their heritage which will lead them through this realm away from, or into danger, depending on the situation. A member of the Ugluk clan, for example, might have a Spirit Guide in the form of a bull, as it is Ugluk Bulls that their clan\nis so famous for- and the same can be said for Lur Wolves or Braduk Rhinos. So, led, or not, by their respective guides, a Shaman will eventually come across what they will refer to as a vision. It may be an event of the long past, the distant\nfuture, or the twisted present- usually representing something that has or will play a major part in the development of either the Uruks or the Shamans. These won’t be straightforward events, however; one may see only the form of a crying Uruk\nmother and her child, and from there they must learn to decipher its potential meaning. And it is from that that a Farseer’s real skill is discovered; the ability to learn from these small snippets of information and then advise their leaders or people\nfor or against certain actions that could, potentially, bring massive consequences for their race. \nAnother form of visions, much rarer in comparison to these odd events, are those brought forth by a spirit himself. These are no tricks to\nbe deciphered; if a spirit goes to enough effort to force a Shaman into a vision, their vision will be straightforward and commending. Usually, these occur when the Spirit feels as if their influence in the Mortal Realm could be\nincreased, and they are to call upon the aid of a Shaman to spread their influence. The Shaman, of course, has no real choice in the matter, but those stronger in the way of words may be able to convince a nagging Spirit to change their\nmind on a matter which might be otherwise impossible, or at least very consequential, to perform.\nUtilisation\n\nLast but very much not least, we come to a Shaman’s real use in Orcish culture- their ability to manipulate the Mortal Realm around them. As said earlier, each sect of Shamanism has their own ways of doing\nthis: Elementalists by meddling with nearby elemental, Lutaumans by blessing themselves, Witchdocters by cursing others or creating tribal elixers, and Farseer by blessing Orcs or others around them who are in need.\nUsually, they go about these things in similar ways. Elementalists must bind themselves to an Elemental by first impressing them by going on certain quests to draw their attention. Then, they promise the Spirit something that it seeks that they can\ngive, and then a bond will be made. As more Elemental Spirits are bonded to, sometimes a Elementalist’s proficiency in the control of a certain element may be hindered; like if one Shaman has bonded to a spirit of water as well fire, or earth\nas well as lightning. It’s up to the Shaman himself to decide what they’ll sacrifice, or if they’ll instead focus only on one element to become utmost proficient at it over all others.\nLutaumans go about creating their influence similarly. They first must call upon an Ancestral Spirit to meet with, and then they will try and gain their favour by promises of impressive feats or proof of their past honour. Once a Spirit\nagrees, they will temporarily bind their essence to the Shaman; giving them massively increased attributes such as strength or bravery for a short amount of time, which may just turn the tide of battle in their favour.\n*the book cuts off- seeming to have run out of space. Down the bottom a small entry has been scribbled in*\n\n\n\n\"See Volume Two for the remaining information of this Tome.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("On Shamanism V2", "Thurak'Yar", "On Shamanism\nVolume Two\nThe more they do this, the more word of their feats will spread among the Ancestral Plane and the more likely it is for these Spirits to accept their deals.\nWitchdoctors go about things a bit differently than others. During their rituals, they’ll present certain objects which hold relevance to the Spirit they are trying to evoke. For example, should they be trying to create a potion which causes the\ndrinker to have insatiable hunger, they would perhaps need something such as the stomach of a large animal, such as a bull, or they may burn and char excessive amounts of savouries in hopes of gaining the attention of the spirit of Greed\nand Gluttony. Should they do so, they’ll begin to call to their desired spirit in the tongue of Old Blah, asking for their aid and promising that the attributes that they represent will somehow be more prominent after the use of said potion.\nShould the spirit agree, the mixture will be cursed, and the Witch Doctor can use it as he will on his unfortunate victims. However, these Shamans must be careful, as it’s sometimes not apparent how a spirit has cursed the potion, and\nunintended effects are rampant in the brews of inexperienced Witchdoctors.\nFinally, the Farseers’ blessings are actually quite similar to that of the Lataumans’, in the way that it requires sharp tongue and wit to convince the spirits\nto give them their boon. When a Farseer decides he wishes to bless something, he must travel to the Spirit Realm and begin calling the name of the spirit that hold the attribute he needs for the blessing. Should the spirit\nanswer, then the Farseer must try and convince it that the blessing will, in some way, benefit the spirit. If this outright fails, and the Spirit refuses, a Farseer may do something else that no other Shaman may do; that being fight the\nspirit for his blessing. This is very dangerous, and is usually done only in times of desperation, as when a Shaman dies or is injured in the Spirit Realm, he dies or is injured back in the mortal realm. Once he’s\neither convinced the Spirit of the need of the blessing or beaten him in battle, it will then begin to take over a Shaman’s body. Back in the Mortal Realm a Farseer’s limbs may start to move under its will, and words in Old Blah will be\nsaid to give the blessing direction. A mist, usually hued the colour that best represents the spirit doing the blessing, will pour from the Shaman’s orifices and encompass the person, animal or plant he wishes to bless. When it's finished, the\nShaman need only to return his connection to his body and admire his handiwork; the fabric of the mortal world being shifted in his favour, albeit in only a small front.", ""),
        StaticBook("On The Drui.", "Gabriel Maul", "*The words would look a little finer, and less thicker then they did in the last reflection.* On the Drui', I was told to Write about my Thoughts on the Druid, then To Reflect on what I gather. I believe this is a wonderful near ending task for a Student,\nSo, Let us begin, Tailesin Was the Lynx Druid who spoke with me on the infomation I gathered, The Druid Serve under the Aspects, the Mother, and Father of Nature, Cerridwen And Cernunnos, I then asked them what they stood for,\nWhat Their meaning was, To Defend Nature, and Balance, They go from Grove to Grove, City to city, Curing Blight/Taint, They stride as the Defenders of Nature, and Balance, Keeping all things natrual as should be.\nTheir goal being at that, To Defend The Wild, From unatrual, Such as the Darkend Taint. How dose Tahariae see this? And Does this Somehow mix with Tahariae's goal? Well, HEre are my thoughts.\nIf their goal is to, Defend nature, Rather it be from a Crazed Halfling with a Wooden ladle, Or A Necromancer with an army of Undead, They are still Defending, The Natural side of things, and if, Like the Light, Nature is natrual,\nAren't they defending a part of the light? If we, as clerics are defending the people of The realm from Darkness, and we are pushing for a darkness free, pure life, Then we might, have a similar if not the same goal, no?\nThe Creator, 'Created' The realms, Nature, In a way their task is as our task, maybe masked under a different goal. Lilyana, In her own words spoke of how, our goals are all a like, even if they sound diffrent, they all lead down the same road.\nThat road, Being purity. I was asked to reflect what I think of Them, What I think we should do with them, should we help the Defenders of Nature? Or do we turn them away? What would Tah Do Exactly.\nI believe they are as Lily said, going down the same road we are, but they don't go out, and fight Undead, they defend their home, they defend the wild, from the Unatrual, If that unatrual is The Darkness, then so be it.\nSo, If Us, As Clerics, andthem as Drui put our task side by side, and took a deep look into it..We all are working for purity, and we all, togehter could bring Tahariae's goal within the road a-head of us.\nSo let it be, Let the Drui' The Paladins, The Clerics, and The Ascended Come together, and lets bind together as one, to bring purity to all.", ""),
        StaticBook("On the Void", "Thereon Ireheart", "Notice: These books are rushed copies of tomes in the Library of the Orkish capital, as made during the raid of the 16th of The Grand Harvest, 1532. The following is in no way a complete nor perfect copy of said book.\nOn the Void\n\nAs potential, waiting to be shaped and formed. Such is the role of an arcane mage.\n\nChapter II\n\nIn the previous chapter, everything that exists in our world exists as potential in the void.\nBut within the void, it is useless to us. Therefore, through trainning a mage can learn to connect to the void and harness its potential in various ways. One example, is evocation, the art of evoking a certain element. An evocanionist uses the void to\nForm their element out of the voids potential and then pull it into our physical world. They will have control over this evoked element (mind you the level of control depends of their skill) and it will be able to effect the physical plane (evoked flames\nwill burn, evoked winds will blow). make no mistake however, that which comes from the void does not belong in our physical plane. As such, as soon as a mage looses connention to the void, be it because he is too tired to continue, his concentration is\nbroken or he simply servers the connention, that which came from the void will return there. this applies to all arcane magic, not just evocation. You way be wondering, if the void is full of everything, why can't mages /make/ everything. The anser lies\nwith knowladge. You see, creating something from the void is no walk in the park. A mage requires absoloute knowlage of what they are attempting to create before they can create it. For this reason, arcane mages focus on one area of harnessing the void\n(or more for advanced mages). An evocationist will spend time learning and experiencing all they can about their element, a conjurer will disect creatures so as to understand how they work and an illusionist need to know how something feels before they\ncan make someone elsefeel it. So, how is it we can connect to the void?\n\nChapter III\n\nRelatively simple to learn but takes a lot of time to master. An arcane mage just starting out learning his craft (regardless of what that craft is)\nwill need to spend a lot of time meditating. Why do they meditate? To achieve the state  of nothingness needed to connect to the void. A connection to the void requires your mind to be empty. All thoughts, feelings amd emotions must be brushed aside. For\na mage just starting out, this will be quite rather difficult and requires a comfortable and secluded area in which they can meditate with extreme focus. To a mage just starting out meditating, it is best if you find somewhere quiet as when you hear a\nnoise your mind will subconsciously focus on it, which disrupts your focus. When meditation for the first time, to not expect to summon anything. When a mage has /truly/ gotten a grasp for this state nothingness they will feel a connecting to the void for\nthe very first time. Nothing will physically happen but you, the mage will most surely feel the power of the void. I can not say how exactly you will feel it. the result differs from person to person with some fainting, some feeling immense power surge\nthrough them and some having belling noses. But you /will/ feel it. After making your first connection it will slowly get easier from there as you progress now that you know what you need to achieve. You can now start experimenting with your art, assuming\nyou already have extensive knowledge on what you intend to create. Bare in mind that pulling something from the void, wether it be a feeling, an element or a creature, requires larger amounts of mana. Large and of longer sustained spells requre larger\namounts of mana to keep them from returning to the void. It is importaint that you recognise your limits, for mana has a physical strain on the body, leaving you fatigued. A mage that does not recognise his own limits may end up knocking himself out from\nhis own spell which is quite counter productive. As a new mage, Do not try anything large or long. You will not be able to sustain the provide the mana needed. Start small and work your way up. with lots of meditation and practice, there will come a day\nwhen you may connect with the void in an instant.\n\nThe way of a mage is lifelong. Mastery is simply staying the path. So stay the path.\n\nElers, Regent of the Arcane Delvers and Aeromancer 1st of suns smile 1445.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Voidial Nodes", "Arzota Des'Nox", "When writing on the existence of voidial nodes, or any natural phenomena for that matter, it is better to first examine past iterations before drawing conclusions on the concrete aspects of the phenomena in question. The most pressing cases wherein\nnodes took central stage generally involve areas of high magical activity - namely, various iterations of mages guilds. Without turning this into a full dissertation on the history of voidial anomaly, all that needs to be understood about these mentioned\ncases, some seen as recently as the Atlas Enchantery located in the high-district of Ceras Eldar, is that the nodes in question became unstable, and in all my named example imploded or exploded in a rather violent fashion. It is no mistake that institutes\nof voidal study were erected upon these sites, as it is now that we touch upon the first aspect of these nodes; the locations where one often identifies a neutral node generally are mana-rich, and fueled by the functioning of the spatial anomaly. This\nclaim is further backed up when examining instances such as the Anthosian wastes, where mages had a difficult time casting nearly any spell or even simple charm, due to the dearth of mana located on the outer reaches of the continent.\nTo expand, and perhaps to add inference to my previous point, it can be drawn that nodes in nature exist outside of our perception, on a layer above or below our plane more close to the void. As such, it is implied that these creations are of common\noccurrence across our plane, and form on an as-needed basis to serve as routes for better serving and supplying mana to starved portions of the environment, or those with heavy demand. Of course, I did mention explosion and implosion earlier, which I\nsuspect is what occurs when a node is worn out in some way or another - most clearly in our case - through overuse. To keep things brief, it is my belief that when a node exhibits signs of decay, be then minor fluctuations of light in an area, or the\nspontaneous development of arcane anomalies, that it is at a crucial turning point in its eventual destruction. If the levels of mana usage in an area stagnate, the burden taken on by another node as is the natural way, then the node will expire without\nevent and the system will rebalance itself. If levels of mana decrease dramatically, then the node will become starved - this starvation eventually leading to the explosion seen in a great deal of voidial occurances in the past, stemming from disuse of\nthe afflicted area. In the rare case that mana usage is doubled, or perhaps tripled even in volume - of which there have been very rare cases of - the node will instead likely implode, crafting a landscape not dissimilar from its original but with\na dramatic increase in voidial energy due to a yet-to-be-understood rebound effect, often manifesting in a massive pillar of ‘Ore’, or transitive voidal stone.\n    With now a foundation and basic understanding of voidial nodes and their functionality,\nlater editions of this tome will explore a means of potential creation, augmentation, and the harnessing of the energy spilled from these nodes.", ""),
        StaticBook("OOC Note", "Carsandra Ivydale", "Sorry I broke one of shopstands. It was an accident. q-q\n\n-firegirl7892467", ""),
        StaticBook("OOC PIANO GUIDE", "Jaya Jayamen", "((THIS BOOK IS OOC. IT SHOWS HOW THE NOTEBLOCK PIANO WORKS!))\n\nHow to play The Classic Jaya Jayamen Grand Piano and the song Jurassic Park. As well as a tuning guide.\n\n~By Jaya Jayamen \n( Sofetios )\nIn this book I will teach you how to play the song Jurassic park on the pianos I make (noteblock piano). First I will show you how to read notes and which notes go to which noteblocks.\nThe noteblock piano is 3x3 noteblocks, represented here by numbers. \n\n     7 8 9\n     4 5 6\n     1 2 3\n       S\nThese numbers will be used to show you which blocks to hit when playing a song. The S is where the seat is in relation to the notes.\n(for those of you who know a bit about music. The piano is tuned in C Major. The 2 block on the piano is where C starts, goes from 2 to 3 to 4 etc. then ends at 9 which is C one octave higher then the C at 2. There is an extra B at 1)\nHere is a small chart showing the notes in relation to the noteblocks.\n( ^ means one octave higher.)\n1 is B\n2 is C\n3 is D\n4 is E\n5 is F\n6 is G\n7 is A\n8 is B^\n9 is C^\nThe numbers show you which block to hit when playing a song. Dashes ( - ) are used to show a rest. When reading music, each character is 1 beat, or one moment when playing.\nYou want to play the song in an even beat, each note the same distance from each other. You may also notice that a written song is separated into sections, this is simply to keep the song easier to read.\nHere are two sample lines.\n\n2 4 6 9 - - \n9 6 4 2 - -\nIn this you would play the block at 2 on the piano, then the 4 block on the piano, the 6, the 9 , then pause for two beats as there are two dashes ( - ) then do 9, then 6, then 4, then 2, then two more pauses.\nKnowing these things, we can do the beginning of the song Jurassic Park.\nJurassic Park.\n\n9 8 9 – 6 – 5 – \n9 8 9 – 6 – 5 – \n9 8 8 9 – – 6 – \n2 – 7 – – – – –\n\n9 8 9 – 6 – 5 – \n9 8 9 – 6 – 5 – \n9 8 8 9 – – 8 – \n– – 9 – – – – –\nTuning the piano.\nThe Grand Piano is 3x3 noteblocks, represented here by numbers.\n\n7 8 9 \n4 5 6\n1 2 3\n  S\n\nThe S is where the seat is in relation to the notes.\nFrom the lowest note counting up with the lowest note being 1, the 1 block of the piano is a 6, the 2 block of the piano is a 7, the 3 block piano is a 9, and so on. The full list is on the next page.\n1 block – 6\n2 block – 7\n3 block – 9\n4 block – 11\n5 block – 12\n6 block – 14\n7 block – 16\n8 block – 18\n9 block - 19\nIf you have any questions, please msg me in-game. ( Sofetios )", ""),
        StaticBook("Opinion on Truth", "Jaya Jayamen", "An Opinion on Truth\n\n        ~Originally by\n        Geedin Jayamen\n\n     ~Transcribed by\n           Jaya Jayamen\nBefore I start, let me just emphasize that this is just my opinion. I want to share it with you and hear what you all think!\nThe truth can be a hard thing to know these days. With so many lies about various things in general flying about, it is hard to discern the truth from the false. Now I’m not here to tell anyone what the truth is in any situation.\nI just want to talk about and discuss what I feel the truth is in itself. To start out, I am going to go a bit off topic, to what I think about fear and doubt.\nSo what is fear? Fear in my own opinion is of course when you are afraid of something. Whether that be the outcome of a decision you have to make, or doing something you have never done for the first time.\nThe next question is what does it mean to be afraid of something? What causes it? I think that fear occurs the most often, though not all the time, in the absence of knowledge. Like when you aren’t sure about something.\nFear of the unknown is a very common thing, as the unknown can possibly do anything.\nNow, if someone had complete confidence that something will happen a certain way, then that person would likely have little to no fear about it unless it is something bad that is to happen.\nFor example, if I practiced day and night for a big test of some sort, and was sure I knew everything needed to pass the test and then some, I would hopefully and likely feel little fear.\nIf I was in a battle and had to get my leg amputated, I would likely fear that because I wouldn’t want to lose a limb.\nIn the second example I know what is going to happen, I know how it’s going to happen, but I will likely still fear that it will happen. As for the first example, if the person who studied day and night failed the test.\nThat would cause the next subject. Doubt.\nDoubt is something that I think causes a lot of fear. It ties in with the lack of knowledge in something. Doubt can be a very powerful thing. It changes or attempts to change your perspective on things, for better or worse, though usually for the worse.\nAn example of good doubt would be thinking about an outcome of a certain action like whether something is a good idea or not, and acting on that doubt.\nAn example of bad doubt would be something like thinking that you cannot do something due to a past experience.\nTo avoid doubt and fear, I think the best way to defeat both is to find out the whole topic of this. The truth. Truth in my opinion is very simple to ourselves, but hard to obtain from outside of ourselves.\nIf you know the truth about something that would mean that you have true knowledge in a certain part or most aspects of that something. This would defeat both doubt and fear, as fear is mainly caused by doubt, and doubt requires uncertainty in something.\nThe problem is that some outside sources do the next thing. Lie.\nLies in my opinion increase doubt and in turn fear. They corrupt the truth and make things harder to make out. A lot of things have the ability to lie. People, books, even our own memories can lie.\nI know that most people would say their memories are not faulty, and I agree that can be true for the most part. Everyone will have different interpretations of a thing that they all together witness, like an abstract painting.\nI am only saying that there is a possibility that a memory could be wrong.\nNow how to discern what is a lie and what is the truth. Well, that is quite the question isn’t it? We can usually lie at any time, so how to know what is true?\nThat brings me to something I call absolute truth, or in other words the real truth in something. The thing is, I think that we can never know the absolute truth. Don’t get me wrong. It is there, it is just usually unknowable.\nTake the abstract picture example. Both people would know what the picture looks like to them, but they would likely be two different interpretations. The object outside the two people’s minds is the absolute truth.\nWe just have interpretations of it through what we think and perceive.\nSo who would be right about what it the abstract painting is? I think they would both be right to a point. With the truth in most matters there isn’t a white or black scenario. It is usually some type of grey.\nNow, imagine white as truth, and black as false. We can get the grey a closer to white with the more truth we tell about the subject. We can also get the grey closer to black with the more lies we tell.\nNow it is certainly possible to get things to all white. This is based on both the question and the answer. If I asked, did you go to the store today, and you did and said yes. That would be a truthful statement.\nAs for the opposite with it getting to all black. That is a tricky thing. I think as soon as there is a falsehood in there, something is already not all true. Though it can get even darker the more lies are put into it.\nAs for how to get rid of all the black and grey. I see the only ways are to either be found out, or the better option which is to confess. In doing a total confession, you undo all the black and grey, leaving the truth as you know it to yourself, white.\nNow back to how to find out if something someone says or does is true or not. There is something that can help with that. Trust. Trust helps you believe what someone says is true. It both does that and helps you be more truthful to that person.\nI believe that in some cases it helps the other person be more truthful to you as well. Now when both people trust each other, that is where things get really interesting.\nI would think very plainly that when two people trust each other, the truth flows a lot more smoothly. Who should you trust? Well, that is up to you.\nAll in all, the truth is simple, yet easily diverged into a lie. I believe the more truth we tell, the clearer things will be to those we tell it to, the more trust we will gain, and the more likely people will tell ourselves the truth.\nIt is easy to tell the truth, Harder but more temporarily convenient to tell a lie, and even harder to own up to a lie. When and if all the lies are cleared up to yourself, well, what need would there be to lie again?\nIf you simply tell the truth from there onward you would be set on a much clearer path then in my opinion.\n\nThe End\nThank you for reading the Jayamen family’s books! If you have any feedback or enjoyed reading, please let me, Jaya Jayamen (( Sofetios )), know. Peoples responses help me write more books! Thanks again! ~Jaya Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Opinion On Truth", "Sofetios", "An Opinion On Truth\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                        -By Sofetios\nBefore we begin, I just wanted to say that this book will shortly cover a variety of subjects regarding my opinion of fear, doubt, truth, belief, lies, and how I think they correlate with each other. This book is just my opinion.\nYou don’t need to believe it or not believe it. To begin we will start with fear.\n\n                    Fear\n\nWhat is Fear? Fear is when you are afraid of something. But what does it mean to be afraid of something?\nI think fear occurs most often in the absence of knowledge, when you aren’t sure about something. Fear of the unknown is a very common thing, as the unknown can possibly do anything.\nIf you had complete confidence that something will happen a certain way, then you likely will have little fear about it unless it is a bad thing that will occur.\nThough if something goes the wrong way when you are fully confident about something, That may cause the next subject to happen. Doubt.\n\n                   Doubt\n\nDoubt is something that can cause fear.\nAs I explained earlier it ties in with the lack of knowledge in something. Doubt can be a very powerful thing. It changes, or attempts to change your perspective on things, for better or worse, but usually worse.\nTo avoid both fear and doubt, I think it is best to find one of the things that defeats both. Truth.\n\n                  Truth\n\nTruth is a very simple thing, Though it can be very hard, or easy, to obtain.\nIf you know the truth of something, that means you have true knowledge in a certain part or all aspects of it.  This defeats both doubt and fear, because fear is caused mainly by doubt, and doubt requires uncertainty in something.\nThere is, however, something that increases doubt. Most all of us do it. Lie.\n\n                     Lie\n\nLies corrupt the truth, they make things harder to make out.\nIn my perspective I think that the truth is a very simple thing to understand, it is lies that corrupt it and makes it more unnecessarily complicated.  In my opinion, lying causes most of doubt and fear.\nThe next and last subject I like to call absolute truth. \n\n           Absolute Truth\n\nThe thing with how doubt works is it tries to prevent us from getting to the truth.\nLies and doubt have happened so much that sometimes even if we find the absolute truth, we still doubt it, Unless of course we believe it’s the truth. And finally, what to believe is the truth. Well, that’s for you to decide.\n(Please let me know if you like my philosophical writing by telling me in person or sending a bird! ((Sofetios)) )\n\n-Sofetios", ""),
        StaticBook("Opinion Trial", "Eliza", "Name:  Brook Harper\n\nOpinion on the Light:\nDoesn't really care.\n\nOpinion on the Lord:\nStill doesnt care.\n\nOpinion on Celrics:\nShe doesnt care.\nName: Ledyard\n\nOpinion on the Light:\nDoesnt mind as long as they do not break \"God's\" will.\n\nOpinion on Tahariae:\nDoesn't mind.\n\nOpinion on Celrics:\nDoesnt mind.\nName: Candra\n\nOpinion of the Light:\nDoesnt know much about it.\n\nOpinion of Tahariae:\nDoesn't know much.\n\nOpinion of Celrics:\nDoesnt know much, but her boss dislikes them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Orc Babies", "Rosso", "Where do orc babies come from?\nYou imagine orc babies and you imagine a green thing being born from the hot sands of the war nation, somewhat like a plant. Well, that is just not true. Believe it or not, orc woman exist and actually get pregnant like humans and elves.\nThe great aspect of orc baby creation lies in the special mating ritual that is performed before the orc woman is impregnated. I had the misfortune of being made a slave to the orcs, but it did let me witness this unusual event.\nFirst of all, Klomps are made between all of the orc women, as the strongest will have the first choice on the males. Then came to men, and this is where it gets weird. In the normal Klomps, the orcs just hit each other until one is on the ground almost\ndying. The mating Klomp is quite different.\n\nIt was to my surprise that instead of punching and kicking, the male orc came dressed in what I assume was dwarven beard, and started doing other things. One chanted poetry in blah, I still do not know how\nthat is possible but it did happen. Another one started dancing, another brought a warthog, already dead, and started cooking it, using a variety of herbs and spices. I was stunt in my chains.\n\nIt appears that orc women fight only for first choice, w\nthe orc men fight to impress the women. One would think it would be by fighting each other in terms of combat, but the orc women know that their men are strong, so they chose the orc which seems to have other skills. As such, the orc man will try his best\nto impress the women, yet of course they do not like doing such.\n\nAfter the women chose their man, the orc males will have one night before they gather with their mating partners. On this night they smoke the biggest amount of cactus green that they\nand then trade blows, taking each punch to the face with honor. An orc which I saw that danced like a fairy, stood still while he received blows from another for more than half the night.\n\nThey do this ritual as to recover their honor after the great\nunhonorable performance. None laugh of others, they respect themselves for doing so, but I will never forget the orc singing in broken common, it still to this day makes me laugh. I was to be executed after the next day’s mating, which was done inside a\ntent of course, but luckily was saved by an attack of the dwarves which happened shortly after. This has changed my view on all orcs, as I never knew they could clean so many bowls in such a small amount of time, as the first chosen orc male had done.\nWhere do Orc babies come from\n\nOriginal author unknown\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Orcish Plague", "riverfyre", "The Orcish Plague has become a serious and debilitating disease that can kill those infected. With several having perished from the disease, new information has been given. While the information is not complete nor fully understood, what can be pieced\ntogether is ways to prevent further spread of this infectious disease. As such it is important to know how the disease is spread, what the symptoms are, and how to be treated. If this plague continues to spread at its\npace, entire cities could be wiped away within days of initial contact.\nHow it is Spread\n\nThe Orcish Plague has been know to spread in many various ways. How one becomes infected can be done through contact. Any contact with an infected person, creature, food, or area are at high risk of infection.\nThose with weaker immunities, children, and elderly are more prone to the disease. With just vicinity being an issue, the spread is far more concerning. The disease seems to be spread through air, consumption,\nand contact with poisoned areas. The disease seems to enter through the mouth and nose when exposed to the spores or infected air expelled from an infected individual.\nThe disease then spreads in the body from the lungs into the kidneys and other organs. When consumed, it starts with the stomach, spreading into the lungs and other organs. It is unknown what the plague does to the epidermal\nwhen touched, but the disease does pose serious health concerns. Bodies that have been infected risk infecting those that touch them. Avoid burying the dead as it can spread through the ground\nand can lead to infection of the water supply. Cremation seems to be the best solution for the dead, but take precautions with the smoke.\nSymptoms\n\nThe plague slowly devours the body internally. The organs fall one by one until the body can no longer sustain itself. As the body slowly decomposes inside, the pain becomes unbearable and the infected dies slowly and painfully.\n- Coughing within the first day\n- Lungs begin to inflame and fill with fluid\n- Lethargy\n- Eyes and flesh begin to turn yellow\n- Kidneys fail\n- Stomach rots\n- Internal organs slowly eaten away by the acid and rot\n- Death\nEven after treatment, the infected is left weak and in pain. If you see any sign of a cough or lethargy in children, immediately seek help.\nTreatment\n\nThere seems to be no normal way of treatment to spare one from this plague. However, it does appear that holy magic can be used to remove the taint from the bodies. While the plague can do severe damage, only powerful healers can\naccomplish the task on the more severe cases. Once healed, the infected can return to their normal duties after they have rested. The infection takes much of their strength and energy, leaving them exhausted\nfor several days. It appears even after treatment, one can become infected again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Order for potion", "Thurak'Yar", "         |\\\n        |V \\_\n        |   ‘  \\\n        )   <_\\\n       /     |\n      /      \\\n      |        \\\n      \\        \\\n        |        \\\n        |  |\\      |\n____ /  |_`.     |______", ""),
        StaticBook("Order Of Sirame", "Damai Torena", "The Sirame\n\nOrder of El'Sirame, translated from Elvish is \"The Order Of Honor\" is a guard force and military that seeks to bring back the 'Ame's Sirame.\nTable Of Contents\n\nI: Meaning Of Sirame\n\nII: The Motives of The Sirame\n\nIII: Rankings Of The Sirame and their meanings\n\nIV: Notable Sirame members\nV: Conclusion\n\n*The Drawing of a large sword would take up the space of the page*\nMeaning Of Sirame\n\nIn the Ancient Elven language there are singular words that elborate a full common language sentence. \n\nSirame is one of these and it's meaning is deeply planted throughout the OrderMen of El'Sirame\nIts meaning is\n\n\"One of the Most Sacred Honors, of personal integrity and connection to the Forests and Oneself\"\n\nThis Sirame is what has created havoc in the Mali'Ame because it has been lost by the Modern Mali by the destruction of Our\nForests, It is one of the Main motives of the Sirame to Reclaim this Honor, which will be elaborated in another Chapter.\n\n*A Drawing of a deer's head would cover the blank space of the page*\nMotives of The Sirame\n\nThe Sirame's main motive is to reclaim the Sirame of the Mali'Ame, as written before in  chapter one.\n\nThey seek to accomplish this by proving themselves worthy warriors and aid those who need us, We seek\nto protect the forests From the past burning's of them in Malinor.\n\nConsidering the Mali'Ame were lead by Power hungry leaders they seek to Reclaim their honor from the Ghetto's they were put in.\nRankings and Their Meanings\n\nThe Sirame has a ranking system based on your efforts in the Order, the Sirame being lead by The Prince, being followed downwards.\n>El'Avern: 'The Wanderer'. A new recruit to the Order\n\n>El'Haler: 'The Oathed' They are the Ordermen who have been oathed to the Sirame and make up the Majority of it.\n>El'Naeri: 'The Devout one'. An Orderman who has recieved prestige within the Ranks of the Sirame, holds Authority over El'Haler and below\n\n>El'Tir: 'The Law'. Junior Officers and the Dedicated to the Sirame and the protection of other\nBrothers of the Sirame and the Citizens of Laureh'lin\n\n>El'Chirr: 'The Wolf'. The Veteran warriors and Officers of the Sirame, they have shown unfaltered loyalty and dedication to the Sirame and the 'Ame's ideals.\n>El'Ceru: 'The Mighty'  A Colonel of the Sirame, they have proven their excellence in Leader ship, and shown their \nMightyness on the battle field. They are chosen by the El'Annil as their second in command.\n>El'Annil: 'The Alpha'. These men are the leaders of the Sirame and are the Mentors and teachers of the lower ranks. On the battle field they lead the Ordermen into battle and lead patrols around Laureh'lin.\nNotable Sirame Members\n\nThis will be a list of Notable Sirame members, this is based on my opinion and can be past or present Sirame who have made an impact.\nKairn Calithil\n\nKairn was an El'Annil in the Sirame before his retiring and to some, he was brutal and emotionless, to others he was just and kind.\n\nKairn made an impact in the Sirame by bringing stern punishments to disrespect from lower ranking\nmembers to higher ranking ones, he also had no tolerance for trouble-making citizens. Nick named the the \"Mad Dog\" he was a great warrior and dealt with situations in the right way.\nElrohir Aureon\n\nElvrohir, the current El'Annil is a valued leader of the Sirame and you could say a more 'Quiet achiever' than others, though he falls tough on nasty people he helps the good kindly and justly.\n\nHe is a valued fletcher of El'Sirame\nand a great Mali'Ame who is true to the Aspects words, I hope he stays in The Sirame for a long time and achieves his personal goals.\nAenor Calithil\n\nEl'Ceru Aenor, a man who is kind, respecting and good at keeping calm in tough situations, he has done many things in the Sirame and is an all round great man. \n\nHe rallies his men with ease and respect and leads us into\nbattle with pride.\n\nOne day he might just become the next El'Annil.\nCalius Terin\n\nCalius, the 'Uncle' of Laureh'lin whom everyone knows. Calius a man who was El'Chirr in the Sirame is a great, calm man all round and will be ever remembered throughout for his work in the Sirame and as Laurir.\nOther notable Sirame\n\nKatar Aureon\nEl'Chirr\n\nBerr To'Las\nEl'Chirr\n\nToren Camoryn\nEx El'Tir\n\nUiron\nEl'Tir\nConclusion\n\nIn conclusion to this book I would like to say a big Thanks to all of my Sirame Brothers for their hard work, be them El'Avern or the Prince himself they all do a great job.\n\nAME AME AME\nAuthor: Damai Torena\n\nPublished:\n21'st Of Malin's Welcome 1545\n\n\n{} [] {} [] {} [] {} [] {} §§\n[] {} [] {} [] {} [] {} []", ""),
        StaticBook("Ordr from George", "George", "\"Python\"\n\nI wish for the rapier to have a fairly normal \"blade.\" But also have some protection on the handle, not fully covered up, but just somethign like small metal bars curving around the handle making it impossible\nto hit the user's hand without  cutting through the bars first.\n\"Cerberus\"\n\nThe dagger will be short and just as easy to stab with, as it should to cut with.     It wll not be curved. And the handle should be small.\nNOTE.\nI want these to be made by iron or anything stronger.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren and Malinor", "Commodus de Jedih", "dddddddddddddddddddDecree Of The Holy Oren Empire And The City State Of Mailnor\njjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjjj\n\nIssued and confirmed by his Imperial Majesty the Holy Emperor of Oren, Horen V, 1428\n\nTranscribed by Comm.\n1664\nAt the will of his Imperial Majesty Horen V,  and agreement of The Malinor High Council.\n\n\nLet it be known throughout the Empire that the City-State of Malinor, shall now be welcome and Protected under the Empire from here on.\nThe City State of Malinor, home to the Mali, is hereby decreed, under agreement of the High Council of Malinor and our Great and Divine Emperor, to be a self-governing, independent city-state under the military protection of the Holy Empire of Oren.\nThis agreement is to upheld until such a time as the Council of Malinor decide they no longer wish to be under the protection of the Glorious Empire of Oren with clear and justified reasoning and after going through all the possibilities of solving it,-\nat which point they may dissolve it without prosecution or delay.\n\n-The Holy Oren Empire-\n\n1-  The Holy Empire is to protect and maintain the independence of the city-state from all forces.\n2- The Holy Empire, shall also have officers that supply and train the City-State’s Military.\n\n3- The Holy Empire, shall not restrict, the travel or trade of The City-States People to it or from it.\n4- The Holy Empire, shall in time when need be supply lands opening them up for future projects for the City States prosperity.\n5- The City-State of Malinor shall still hold ownership over, Darkhaven and future settlements as well, that are south of the river. Future settlements shall be created with the agreement between the City State and the Empire.\n6- Prince Avern’len San’taeleh shall be placed within the Emperor’s court. In the efforts to maintain steady and firm lines of communication between the two peoples.\n7- Citizens of Oren shall be welcomed with open arms, should their intentions be of a peaceful end. Those that do not comply with Malinor’s laws, threaten or kill any citizens within the borders of the City State of Malinor, -\nshall be dealt with as a criminal would if found guilty. Regardless of social standing.\n\n-The City State of Malinor-\n\n1-  Malinor Cede's all land south of the Elven river to the Holy Empire of Oren,-\nin the interest of unhampered patrols and overwatch and the protection of such large land.\n\n2- Malinor shall be referred to as the City State of Malinor, instead of The Princedom of Malinor, establishing it under the military protection of the Empire.\n3- Malinor will maintain its own governance, with an ambassador/representative of Oren placed within the High Council. In the efforts to maintain steady and firm lines of communication between the two peoples.\n4- The Citizens of The City State of Malinor are welcome within the lands of Oren, to be treated as class B citizens (Non-nobles) and free from undue harm, harassment, or questioning. Should they commit a crime they -\nshall be tried in accordance with the law as any citizen of Oren would be.\n\n5. Trade between The City State of Malinor and other lands in Oren shall not be restricted.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren History: I", "Jacob Chapel", "History of Oren\n       Part I\n\n\nThis history has been collected by me, Jacob Chapel. Sources are various scrolls and texts and the museum of Petrus, beside common knowledge and tales. Enjoy.\n\n((Written by Pepernoot))\nIf you're interested in the history before Al'Khazar, I suggest you pick up the first part of the Holy Scrolls, the Nativities. If you're interested in the history past Siegmund Carrion's election, then you need to find part two of The History of Oren.\nThe days of Aegis\nThe history of Oren begins in Aegis, the land of the Descendants. To the west of the Cloud Temple laid its lands. The capital of Al’Khazar was surrounded by pastures, farmlands and forests, and to the north laid the snowy lands,\ncontaining cities and towns such as Alstion and Snowy Fields. In the south were the islands known as the Whisper Isles, surrounded by the calm waters of the Whisper Lake, and filled with fishermen and craftsmen such as glassblowers.\nThe first king was Horen himself. Many Kings ruled the Kingdom wisely after him, Kings such as Saint Daniel. The Kingdom’s grand city was built by this King Daniel in 1300. Eventually King Pampo Perea, Saint Daniel’s seneschal, took power, with Edmund\nSheffield as his seneschal.\nAs time passed the Undead became stronger and bolder in their attacks on the Kingdom. Snowy Fields fell and was razed, but soldiers from Alstion retook it and the town was rebuilt. This turned out to be futile eventually as\nthe northern towns fell one by one. Even King Perea himself was killed by the Undead, within the tall walls of Al’Khazar. Edmund Sheffield took his place, but was corrupted by the dark forces and turned to the Nether. His “abduction” was accompanied by a\ngreat siege of Al’Khazar, in which a portal to the Nether opened in the city square. After a great battle the City of Man was sacked. Human refugees poured across the Kingdom and the city of Galahar, built on the ruins of the old town of Kramoroe, was\nnamed capital.\n\nEdmund’s son Enor Sheffield took his place, but under his rule the situation worsened drastically, the corruption of his father and his own weakness led to great dissent in the Kingdom.\nMeanwhile Gaius Marius, Hochmeister of the Teutons had carved out a realm for himself to the east of the Kingdom, and had even participated in wars against Oren, allying with its enemies. It is important to note that even though the Undead threatened\nOren, and although Oren was the strong defence between the Undead and the rest of the races, this didn’t deter them to wage wars against the Kingdom. Infighting between the nations of Malinor, Krug, Urguan and Oren was common.\nRebellion brew in the\nKingdom, and in Galahar the Phoenix Rebellion formed. As the weak King Enor saw his position wasn’t tenable anymore he named Gaius Marius as King of Oren. This treason lead to the rise of the rebellion and a war between the part of Oren controlled by\nthe Teutons and the Phoenix Rebellion, led by Eze’kiel Tarus as the Phoenix King. Eventually the two sides reach an agreement, splitting the realm into two parts. The Kingdom of Renatus, ruled by King Tarus, and the Realm of Hanseti, ruled by Gaius.\nAfter giving up his crown the mad King Enor and his followers settled on an island, and together with Queen Dawn Perea, wife of the old King Perea he created the nation of Salvus.\nHumanity could not rest though, as the Undead continued their march\nrelentlessly. In 1349 Galahar was attacked by the forces of evil, but even though the attack was repelled, the city was evacuated for fears of Miasma. Eventually Aegis fell in 1351, and the humans fled through the portal to the verge,\nalong with the other Descendants. \n\nA new dawn in Asulon\nAfter a brief stay in The Verge, the Descendants settled in the new lands of Asulon. Oren was still divided into the three Kingdoms, and Renatus settled around their new capital of Arethor.\nIn these turbulent times a new human nation sprung up, the Kingdom of Seventis.\n\nWhen King Eze’kiel resigned from the throne, Renatus was ruled by the Regent King Reynard Lycian until Godfrey Horen appeared. Godfrey claimed direct decent from King Horen\nand quickly received support from the Dukes and other nobles of the realm. He consolidated power and strengthened the Kingdom, which was plagued by instability and attacks from the other nations.\n\nSoon after Godfrey started his reign a coalition against\nSalvus formed by The Kingdom of Seventis, Alras, the Orcs and most importantly what was called the Twilight Army. This coalition did not have official support from Renatus, but most of its nobles supported it. Opposing the coalition were Salvus itself,\nthe Dwarves of Urguan and the Realm of Hanseti. After the humiliating defeat, and the betrayal of Queen Dawn’s guards, which murdered her, Salvus was absorbed into Renatus.\n\nAs the great plague hit Asulon, the Kingdom of Seventis was hit most severely,\npresumably due to its location close to the Cloud Temple. Most of its inhabitants died, allowing for an absorption into the Kingdom of Renatus to protect the weakened towns.\n\nThe Teutons could not stand by idly as Renatus grew, and went to war against\nthe Kingdom. Swiftly the war turned against their favour, and it became clear that they were losing the war. To avoid destruction of his nation, Hochmeister Mirtok surrendered it to King Godfrey, saying the words “I will die for this nation, but I will\nnot let it die for me”.\n\nThe annexation of Hanseti meant the unification of humanity, and the Holy Oren Empire was formed. In the Empire the Crownlands, Salvus and Hanseti were ruled as separate kingdoms, with the Emperor presiding over the individual\nkings, while also being king of the crownlands.\n\nAfter a rebellion against the crown, House Tarus, House Elendil and House Norsem were shunned and fell out of favour in the Empire. Soon though, the lands of Asulon were submerged by floods,\nand a second flight was needed.\n\nAnthos, a land plagued by war\nJust as the flight from Aegis, the new land was not reached in one trip. There were stops at the isles of Elysium and Kalos. One notable thing in Kalos was the formation of the\nPhoenix Kingdom, by Eze’kiel Tarus. The kingdom was quickly destroyed, even before leaving for Anthos.\n\nIn Asulon the Teutonic Order was nigh destroyed by the Flays, and the Hochmeister killed. A few remnants of the Order made it to Anthos, albeit\nwithout a Hochmeister to guide them. The Teutons settled on the southern side of the ice wall of the North. Meanwhile the Empire of Oren settled a bit further south, with Abresi as their capital.\n\nSoon after arriving it turned out this land was not as\nsafe as the Descendants had hoped. North of the wall the Teutons discovered a savage race of boarmen and a land filled with dragons.\n\nThis was not the most pressing issue to Oren though, as the Empress of Oren was kidnapped by the Orcs, and a joint\nHuman and Dwarf force invaded their capital and massacred nearly every orc present.\n\nEver present Elven aggression led to a crusade against the Princedom of Malinor. The Order of the White Rose quickly destroyed their forces and burned the Malenorian\nfarms. The elves eventually surrendered to the siege, proving the enormous strength of a united Oren.\n\nUnited it would not be for long, as the Teutons rebelled. In the first battle, at Kralta, the Teutons were crushed. At the second battle the\nBlackmonts stood alone against the Teutons on the Iron Fields, outnumbered two to one. The Teutonic Order was victorious.\n\nThe civil war was decided at the Siege of the Dreadfort, where the Chivays, and the Carrions (then bannermen of the Blackmonts)\ndistinguished themselves. The defeat at the Battle of Iron fields had led to close cooperation between the White Roses and the Blackmonts, which turned out to be more than the Teutons could handle. Although the Dreadfort was severely damaged the siege\nwas broken and the Teutonic Order defeated. Soon afterwards the Teutonic Order was disbanded by Emperor Godfrey.\n\nThe Scourge, the name of the goatmen and the dragons from the north made their first move south beyond the wall, destroying the old\nTeutonic castle of Greywyn with flames, and taking it for their own.\n\nThen, in a huge shock to the empire, Emperor Godfrey died. He was succeeded by his son, Horen.\n\nAs the princedom of Malinor was absorbed into the Empire as\nprotectorate, the expansion of Oren led to great concern with the other races. They formed a coalition and in the War of Anthos they attacked Oren, putting a halt to the expansion. Most prominent in the coalition were the Dwarves, angered by the\nexecution of one of their Dwarven lords by nobles of Oren. In the Battle of the Crossroads the coalition was defeated though, by a brilliant Orenian flanking manoeuvre.\n\nIn 1415 the Empire was left in disarray as Emperor Horen left, along with his\nmost loyal houses. The dwarves used this weakness to form their Grand Kingdom of Urguan in the War of Asulon. They dissolved the Empire of Oren and many parts, including Salvus and Adunia swear loyalty to the dwarves as vassal states. What remains of the\nEmpire was renamed to the Holy Kingdom of Oren and ruled by William Horen. After more chaos and disarray many more little human states sprung up or seceded from the Kingdom, leading to the current prominent Houses, states and cultures. \n \nEventually the\nGrand King of Urguan, Thorin Grandaxe dies. This caused the human vassal states to be released from their oaths to the dwarves. This made way for a renewed unification. As King William was pushing his powers and support from his nobles to the limit,\nHouse Winter made a secret pact with Ruska. This forced King William to step down, giving control of Oren to his cousin Silus. This was only temporary, as the states of Salvus, Oren, Ruska and the new state of Herendul were confederated into an empire,\nwith an elective monarchy. At the election Siegmund Carrion was voted in as Emperor of Oren.\n\nThis concludes part one of Oren's history. The events after Siegmund Carrion's election, up to the first years in Athera will be discussed in part two.\n((So you made it to the end. I hope you liked it. You can leave a message to me on the forums, username: Pepernoot))", ""),
        StaticBook("Orenian Passport", "Ser Ulric von Aesterwald", "===================JOHANNESBURG\nCAPITAL\nPOLICE\n===================SPECIAL PASSPORT\n\nCITIZEN NAME:\nValahan deGray\n\nRECORDING OFFICER:\nSer Ulric von Aesterwald\nNOTES:\nDO NOT SEARCH.\nDO NOT QUESTION.\nDO NOT ARREST OR DETAIN WITHOUT UNQUESTIONABLE EVIDENCE.\n\nCRIMINAL HISTORY:\nNone\n\nOCCUPATION:\nMarked Man\nFULLNAME:\nValahan deGray\n\nAGE:\n60-ish\n\nBIRTHPLACE:\nHoly Orenian Empire\n\nRESIDENCE:\nBlackwald, Duchy of Savoie, Holy Orenian Empire\nDESCRIPTION:\n-Old Man\n-Graying Hair\n-One Eye\n-Marked Man Medallion\n-Stern\n-Usually travels with a man named Adeon\n===================\n\n*Stamp of the Empire*\n\nHis Imperial Majesty John Owyn, Holy Orenian Emperor\n\n\n15th of the Amber Cold, 1572\n\n\n==================", ""),
