        StaticBook("Orgon Invasion 1", "Shaman Zlash'Lur", "Orgon's Invasion\n \n\n  The Vailoric Blight\nAfter the Dogger days of early Vailor, the Rexdom eventually settled upon Kharak'Raguk successing Snoop'Azog leading into a new era of Orcs abolishing the Iron Uzg and forming the War Uzg. As an era of War and Strength ended a new focus was forged in the\npath of the Spirits. There were many supporters under Kharak that he would lead the Orcs through a great spiritual movement.\n\nAs he had taken up the Rexdom, his dedicancy towards Orgon, the Spirit of Disease and Pestilence eventually went viral\nin the War Uzg as almost every Orc under Kharak began to worship Orgon giving him great influence within the Spirit Realm. Orgon eventually guided Kharak to leave a blight of his influence upon the land as a defense from the growing Empire.\nAs years passed, Kharak fell into a bit of an isolation as madness grew upon him balancing his deals with the Spirit as well as ruling the War Uzg. Without the influence of any Farseer within the nation, the Orcs continued misguided of a balance of the\nSpirit Realm. Later in Axios, the influence of Orgon and his deals grew to an extreme, it caused Phaedrus the Farseer to be killed as he brought ultimatum circumstances when he faced Kharak.", ""),
        StaticBook("Orichalcum", "Rosso", "__Orichalcum__\n\nNienna’s Foreword: I found this little gem off of a dead spy named Devin Ryder. Yes, he was a bard and a spy, and he had quite a few things in-between. I’m pretty sure he stole this book. Actually, I’m sure of it.\nOrichalcum is a precious metal that is made out of white gold and silver. It can hold powerful and magical energies and is a great material for Magical items such as staves, swords, and magical Tiaras.\nIt is used by mages to store spells so that they can release those at the right moment. When using Orichalcum, be aware of its powerful magical properties. Don’t mess around with it - it can become dangerous at the wrong moments.\n==How to make==\n\n==Orichalcum==\n\n1- Melt the white gold and silver.\n\n2- Let flow energies of white magic into the metal while forcing it together.\n3-Make one metal bar of the combined metals\n\n4- Bend the bar to the shape of the power-rune\n\n5- Power the rune\n\n6- Reshape the rune to the symbol of resistance\n-repeat step 5-\n\n7- Reshape the rune to the symbol of capacity\n\n-repeat step 5-\n\n8- Now create the object you want to make\n9-Bury your Orichalcum at a place where it can absorb energies of nature, such as a forest or grove\n\n10- After 5 days your  metal is ready and you can recover it.\nThe process is complete now, but don’t expect it to go perfectly smooth the first time. This is a process that needs experience.\n\n-Contact Aurea in Haelun’or if you have questions-\nOrichalcum\n\nWritten by Nienna\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Origin of Oaths", "Aerendyl Hawksong", "Oath to Order\n\nIn the days before the first great split of elvendom, there was a hard-fought peace that pervaded society. Hawksong flourished in trade and animal husbandry, and at that time our kin learned well the wonders of creating art -\nthrough burning and staining leather, fashioning saddles and trading armor fixings to smiths. We still practice these today, and a Hawksong-made work of leather is easily spotted with a brand in the likeness of our crest.\nDespite this, languor crept into our hearts and we lost our way as the Rochir of Hawksong. We became lazy.\n\nOnce Larihei and her brood made sail for the unknown, our Father and Founder felt shame for indirectly causing -\nthese splinters. As a show of renewed strength he swore to the High Court that our bloodline would serve Elvendom fiercely for this great debt, of which we still do this day. This is the first recorded Vestale, and known to us as the eternal debt.\nThis established Hawksong as not only a surname of stories and legends, but as an esteemed honor to serve and protect the greater good of Elvendom. Here he created our code of conduct, a method of initiation into the family just as he was given the name,-\nand a creed that all Rochir must recite to the High Court upon becoming Rochir.\n\nThis begins the modern age of Hawksong.", ""),
        StaticBook("Our Salvation", "Pierre-Francois D'Auvergne", "After a long period of battles and adventures, the prophet spoke.\n\"O Grant me the mercy of the land.\"\n\"O Grant me the joy of the heavens.\"\n\"Release me from my yoke of iron, thus shall our souls be saved.\"\nForever and ever\nForever and ever\nForever and ever\nOne day, a volano erupted. Out of the fires of the eruption, god emerged. He looked down upon the machines and said \"Pain, Happiness, Tragedy, Desires, Feelings, Sins, Awareness. The meaning of life.\nThey were found by the machines. The machines called them treasures. \nEach treasure had a different shape. \nEach treasure had a different shape.\nThe child sway over enormous strength.\nBut sadly he was also a little bit broken, he spent his long days hurting those around him. He tried really hard to be nice and gentle, but he was unable to.\nThey told him they didn't want him, and they caste him\ninto the dark seas. He called out to his mother.\n\"Mother, Mother, Mother.\" But his voice never reached his mother.\nWhether in wind or rain... Thunder or snow... Or even amidst the rising flames of war... They were always together. They never understood why, and yet they spent their lives nestled together. Forever, Forever and ever.\nThe black flower is the voice which abides in this broken eye. Where it has been since its creation.", ""),
        StaticBook("Outer Sanctum", ".", "ON THE OUTER SANCTUM\n2nd of Malin's Welcome\n204\n-------------------The Outer Sanctum is our first and final line of defense against the dragons and their armies, and the Order shall hold that line.\n\nJust this morning, Haevolt presented to the High Table\nthe first prototype for his 'Titans', which seemed just like regular golems to me. I took the thing apart within seconds, but Haevolt seemed delighted nonetheles. 'An excellent first step', the fool called it.\n\nHowever ... I hate to admit it, but Haevolt\nand his machinations may be our best chance at leaving this Temple. The Vaeyl Order cannot stand as eternal gaolers forever; Atlas faces other threats that we must see to. If we are ever to leave this place behind, I see no choice but to pray Haevolt is\nsuccessful and creates his Titan soon.\n\n-Lord Marshall Serris of Last Harbour, Commander of the 2nd Banner of the Vaeyl Order", ""),
        StaticBook("Oxford", "Kale le Prevost", "Caliphate Clinic\n\nHead Doctor Kale\n\nPatient's Name: Oxford\n\nAge: 5\n\nRace: Human\n\nGender: Male\nCondition/Injury: Three cuts from glass shards, one on the chest, one on the arm, and one on the leg. Very minor cuts.\n\nTreatment plan: Patient was brought into surgery. Easily stitched up. No numbing medicine.\nDoctor who treated the patient: Kiveck\n\nCost: 15 minas\n\nDate: 14th of The Deep Cold, 1522\nEnd result: Patient will come in for a checkup later on. Seemed to be in no real pain, although he puked in the surgical room soon after surgery ended.\n*Kivecks signature would be on this page*\n\n-Kiveck Irelia\nCaliphate Clinic\n\nHead Doctor Kale\n\nCondition/Injury: Came in for a quick checkup.\n\nTreatment plan: N/A, all wounds were healed.\nDoctor who treated the patient: Hileia'elr\n\nCost: 5 mina\n\nDate: 13th of Malin's Welcome, 1523\n\nEnd result: No issues, cuts healed.\n*Hileia's signature would be here*\n\n\n~Hileia'elr", ""),
        StaticBook("Paragon Codex", "Grigori", "The True Paragon\n          Codex\n1. Title page\n2. Index\n3. Thoromir Ruric\n4. Eirik ruric\n5. Edvard Ruric\n6. Snow Volaren\n7. Myro\n8. Vykk Volaren\n9. Bjorn Rayeckson\n10. Beo\n11. Sven Ruric\n12. Ulric Grimlee\n13. Donovan Ruric\n14. Rodrik Ruric\nThoromir\n     \"The Father\"\n          Ruric\nParagon of Paternity, Strength, and Architecture.\n\n             [!]\nA picture of a strong bearded man standing in front of a massive wall, hefting a large warhammer over his shoulder\nEirik\n      \"The Great\"\n          Ruric\nParagon of Greatness and Diplomacy\n             [!]\nAn old wrinkled man with a white beard, wearing a fine red robe with a snow cap dangling down his shoulder, he is sitting atop the throne in Nyrhold.\nEdvard\n      \"The Terrible\"\n            Ruric\nParagon of Evil and Sloth\n             [!]\nA stoic man wearing icy black plate armor, he holds a sword pointing into the ground, a snowy mountain peak sits behind his right shoulder.\nSnow\n     \"The Magus\"\n         Volaren\nParagon of Flames\n             \n             [!]\nA clean shaven elf wearing red robes. his hair a platinum white. he idly holds a fireball in his hand.\nMyro\n    \"The Wordsmith\"\nParagon of Study and Learning\n             [!]\nA halfling sitting at a desk wearing brown overalls and a white shirt. he appears to be hard at work writing at the desk with an ink quill pen.\nVykk\n     \"The founder\"\n         Volaren\nParagon of Creation and Survival\n             [!]\nA bearded elf, wearing plate armor and a ram horned helmet. He holds a handaxe by his waist. He stands upon a drawbridge coming from a large stone skull.\nBjorn\n       \"The Gruff\"\n   Rayeckson Ashtyr\nParagon of Fighting and Strategy\n\n             [!]\nA man wrapped in heavy leather armor and furs. He is holding a large greatsword, behind him a battle rages on.\nBeo\n    \"The Betrayer\"\nParagon of Failure and Treachery\n\n             [!]\nAn Angular young man with blonde hair stands with red and black plate armor, an Axe rests on his shoulder, behind him a castle covered in heaps of snow.\nSven\n       \"The Bard\"\n           Ruric\nParagon of Music and Storytelling\n             [!]\nA blonde haired man with a short blonde beard leans back in a chair at a tavern, plucking at a lute while others cheerfully drink in the background.\nUther\n        \"The Old\"\n          Grimlee\nParagon of Labor and Harvest\n\n             [!]\nA man dressed in plain clothing. He stands in a field of wheat, swinging a scythe. A woman stands behind him waving a handkerchief.\nDonovan\n     \"The Bastion\"\n          Ruric\nParagon of Defense and Vigilence\n             [!]\nA man would be dressed in rusty plate armor, the colors of house Ruric cover his breast. The scene of a Large Island looms behind him.\nRodrik\n    \"The Governor\"\n           Ruric\nParagon of Governance\n             [!]\nA man dressed in a long black woolen tunic. With gold silk outlining the outfit. He'd have greying hair, with a sent of brown. His eyes blue.", ""),
        StaticBook("Pass 1", "The Scribe", "Cold and sharp, a friend through good and bad.\n\nWood, Stone, or Iron I am all.\n\nThe end and the begining to all journeys\n\nA tool for the largest craft, a work of art for the most emplyoaed artist.\n\nThe constant in all the entropy, never left in the past.", ""),
        StaticBook("Pass 2", "The Scribe", "A weapon for the sharpest,\n\nBoth thin and wide reaching, the master of me is the master of all\n\nA permanent mark I leave, the canvas dotted with my presence\nI am mightier than the sword", ""),
        StaticBook("Pass 3", "The Scribe", "Owned by all but hoarded by few\n\nI shine and shine within everyone, burning a hole in their cloth\n\nExchange exchange exchange, everything is measured by me\nOften, I make the world iself go flat", ""),
        StaticBook("Pass 4", "The Scribe", "Stretched and I fling my seed across the world.\n\nNative of the forests, I find myself in the hands of its defenders\n\nUseless alone, unstoppable with my partner\nA tool for war, a tool for sport, and a trophy for all.", ""),
        StaticBook("Patent D.G.", "Siegmund Adler", "Alexandre de Aryn, Count of Chambery and Baron of Lumen by the Grace of GOD, to all whom it may concern, hereby appoint the trusted\n\nDONN GUTHRIE\n------------\n\n\n---->\nTo the position of Owner of the Worshipful Company of Agriculture.\n\nIn return for this boon, MR. GUTHRIE shall pay 10% of his harvest annually to Count de Aryn.\n\n\n---->\nSigned by Siegmund Adler, in his capacity as Head Steward of Chambery,", ""),
