        StaticBook("Pocket Book", "Anonymous", "Marna Court Notes\n\n*they have already started to speak, here are the words spoken after my late arrival.\n\n>A man named Konrad would say \"My fellow countrymen, long have we stood a proud kingdom, the epitome of human ideals and beliefs. While the\nFlamboyant Loser(?)\nGeneral is indeed a threat, we face growing tension with another faction, Dominion of Malin.\n\nAnother man that I do not know the name of\n\"Don't you dare forget the orcs and the Ghanyahns\"\n  *possible conflicts                   too?\nKonrad continues...\n\"My house has long been enemies of the wood elves. While we were allies with them, I stomached this hatred for the good of humanity. Now, however, we have reached the brink of war...\n\n...There was a time when humanity was\nonce fractured, once never able to handle a threat so dire alone.\n   *elves = threat?\n   *call for alliance?\nNow, we stand proud. We stand united, as an empire of man. The Dominion of Malin, no better than some upstart dagger ears\n\n*what an insult...\nwho spend their time doing unfathomable acts within fae rings, will stand no longer. United, we will defeat them easily.\n       *war inevitable\n\nBased on this clothing and armor, I believe man is the King of Santegia, he would say \"We have heard our\nvassal's and allies, the last words shall go to our mother church and its holy vicar.\"\n\nThe vicar would begin \"Dear brothers and sisters of Renatus of Santegia, of all the states of men, and of God. I will make this short...\n... We must know, brothers and sisters, that we are palced in an integral part of the history of our race.\n\nThe creator has gathered us together on this day for a reason.\n\nFor too long have we been divided as a people.\nFor too long have we watched our culture dwindle from the inactivity of Human governance.\n\nThe time is up, we must act. Today we have pledged our people to a new experiment in Human Unity.\n *new experiment as in   new empire?\nLet us bow our heads onto the Lord as we begin this fervent supplication for the success of this endeavor.\n\nAlmighty God who did enlighten the Patriarch of Humanity and mark him as our sovereign protector and defender against the assaults of the\nDefiler.\n\nSend down Thy Holy Light upon your King Aurelius and grant that he too may be magnified through his efforts in defending us, God's people, in the face of the assaults and temptations that Iblees crafts from below. Division is the\nDivider used in the encampment of Horen. Let us pray that the sin of human division may be purged from this plane in the face of unity for the glory of God.\n\nExalt your king, glorify the God.\n\nMay almighty God free us from the shackles\nof sin and return us to a stateof grace and divinity by his sovereigns this place.\"\n\nEnd of Court Session.\n*To whomever's hand may this book find itself upon, I, the writer will not have his name written for the safety of himself and his\nacquaintances.\n\nThis court session hold information that would lead to conflict and bloodshed. I should not have been there, but rumors of this meeting and my curiosity led myself to travel upon Marna.\n\nI am more than relieved to recognize\nno individual that would know my name.\n\nFrom the words that have been head by my own ears, war may be inevitable, unfortunately.\n\nI pray for peace though it is not likely.\n", ""),
        StaticBook("Poem", "Círdan", "My life suffocates\nPlanting seeds of hate\nI've loved turned to hate\nTrapped far beyond my fate\nI give, you take\nThis life that I forsake\nI've been cheated of my youth\nYou've turned this lie to truth\nPure black looking clear\nMy work is done soon here\nTry getting back to me\nGive back what used to be\nDrink up, shoot in\nLet the beatings begin\nDistributor of pain\nYour loss becomes my gain\nAll have said their prayers\nInvade their nightmares\nSee into my eyes\nYou'll find where murder lies\nInfanticide...\n\nA poem my Karren Myrsta\n\n[OOC] these are song lyrics pasted into the book by Melkor__ , not his personal work", ""),
        StaticBook("Poem", "Unsigned", "Your eyes,\nBalls that contain the harshest of storms, \nBarely contained passion and intellence that burns like the flames of battle.\n\nYour voice is like thunder,\nAnd when I hear it my heart beats in my chest like the drums of war.\nMy knees grow weak around you,\nAnd when you walk away they yearn to follow.\nIt leaves my heart empty like a long battle with no victor.\n\nYour eyes are beyond description,\nSmall blue orbs that hold all the passion of a storm,\nThe strength and determination of a boar stuck with a spear.\n\nYour eyes are what captivate me.", ""),
        StaticBook("Poem d'Ensign", "Winter", "Dedicated to Ensign Aldis Chase, to whom my life I do owe. A man with a heart of gold under an armour of old.\nT'was a night of darkness\nHe lived all alone\nIn an old, dirty barrack\nWalls made of stone.\nI met him one night, with kindess to give\nAnd see who under that armour did live.\nI glanced up and down...a strange sight to see.\nNo evil, no brilliance, not even a smile.\nNo silk robes or felt hats\nOnly boots filled with sand\nIn his eyes were pictures\nOf far, distant lands\nOn his chest- medals and badges...\nawards of every kind!\nA sobering thought...\nCame alive in my mind...\nThis man was different\nEyes dark and dreary\nI found before me a soldier\nI can see that most clearly...\nThe ensign stood guard- silent. Alone.\nHis boots on his soil\nProtecting our home.\nHis face was so gentle\nI stood in disorder-\nNot at all how I imaged\na brave Legion Soldier.\nWas this the hero by whom I was just saved?\nBeneath plates of armour...\nA floor for a bed.\nThen I realized that all the families I saw tonight\nOwed their lives to soldiers. So willing to\nfight.\nIn the morning children of Carolustadt shall play,\nAdults shall celebrate yet another peaceful day.\nWe all enjoy freedom each day of the year\nBecause of soldiers,\nLike the one standing here.\nI couldn't help how many more stood\nalone\nIn the break of day, protecting their home.\n\nThe very thought brought a tear to my eye\nI dropped to my knees.\nI started to cry.\nThe soldier looked down\nI heard his rough voice.\n\"Come on gal, don't cry.\nThis life is my choice.\nI fight for freedom!\nI don't ask for more.\nMy life is for God, My country's my core.\"\nThe soldier turned over and began to leave.\nI couldn't help it...\nI continued to weep.\nI stood watch for hours...\nSo silent and still...\nAs both of us shivered through the chilly night.\nI didn't want to leave him\nThat guardian of honour\nSo willing to fight.\nThen, the soldier turned to me with a voice soft and pure\nHe whispered-\n\"Go on, gal, go get some sleep. \nWorry not...the night's secure.\"\nOne look at my feet,\nI knew he was right\n\n\"Thank you, dear ensign, may GOD bless you this night.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Poems, On People", "Vallakai Vallakovich", "To Everyone I've Ever Cared About\n\n-Vallakai\nSer Sylvestre, Oldest knight of Curon, First friend in Atlas, True man, and truly, truly dead. \nThe Poem\nThe Old Knight\nFought His Fight\nAnd then he died,\n\"Why?!\" They cried,\nInto the blinding light.\nSer Ajax Ironwood II\nKnight, Truest friend, Honor of the Brigade, Torch in the blackness. \nThe Poem \nThe Dead Man walks\nThe dead man talks.\nIt is not the same man.\nI will do all that I can.\nTo keep his memory alive.\nSer Magnus Silversteed\nSon of Ajax. The Strong One. Heart of Arbor. Inquisitor. \nThe Poem\nMore than you know\nAs well as you think,\nGreatness in him\nNotorious\nUnanimously achived\nSo much more.\nVitalius Maarsen\nDoctor, Alchemist, Kind, Easily breakable house, The Spirit Of Arbor.\n\nHow to Describe him?\nThat's almost impossible.\nOh wait, I just did.\nSer Orym. Heir. Spirited\nThe King Of The Knights, The Truest Soldier.\n\nThere once was a man named Ser Orym.\nThey all tried to kill and gore 'im. He laughed in their faces,\nPut 'em back in their places, \nand all 'fore 9 am.\nElion Tyrannor\nMind Of Arbor, Family man, 3rd oldest, I believe, and wisest of us all.\nIf you need something, he's there.\nIf you're in danger, he's there.\nIf you need someone there, he's there.\nHis name is Elion.\nAragon Silversteed\nCount Von- I mean count of Arbor. Leader of the Silver Knights, Face of Arbor\nAragon flies.\nAragon tries.\nAragon may win,\nAragon may cause a din.\nEventually, Aragon dies.\nMy wife, Esmeralda.\nDarling, Dearest, Dead.\n\nThere once was a man, that was me.\nAnd a girl, that was she.\nThey one day were wed,\nAnd went to the bed,\nand now, alone is he.\nMy daughter, unnamed, and unborn. My love for you shall live forever. You, however, did not.\n\nThose who did not come, those who lie dead, we don't know where they go, we don't know where they rest. It's because they don't.\nAnd to one more, she knows who.\n\nThe world is a little smaller. The stool is a little taller. There is nothing left, but a cleft in space. The words that only I can say are:\nI'm sorry, okay?", ""),
        StaticBook("Poetry and Songs", "Rulan", "Collection of Poems and Songs.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDedicated to Nova.\nWandering Soul\n\nAcross the seas I travel\nThrough the woes, my mind unravels\nIn all the arts a dabble\nMy mind hits the wood\nLike a judge slams his gavel.\nBut even through all that sound\nA light shines,\nAnd my soul is bound\nTo a certain path I go\nEven through hell\nthat is what I know.\nEven through that, \nmy destination is still lost\nThough what destination is in my thoughts\nI am but a wandering in the skies\nAnd an bright flame waiting to die.\nBut even after my flame dies\nMy soul will travel,\nThat I do not deny\nTill the day I grow old\nAnd the day death knocks at my door bold\nI will travel, as a wandering soul.\nGrowing Pains\n\nOh how I watch you grow\nOh whats in your mind, I desperately want to know\nYour mind and soul elude me\nAnd I worry if you'll be set free\nFor now I must observe, as you struggle and grow,\nAnd how it pains me to see so.\nYou are loved by many\nI think that you will be oh so friendly.\nThe fiercest person alive, guards your life\nand even in the hardest times, they will fight\nTo protect is their goal\nYou will help fill a void, oh so null.\nThe world can't wait to meet you.\nFor you are my child\nAnd my love for you, is like a flame so wild, Once you are here, my flames will grow bright, For there will be no fear, Just sit there and grow,\nFor it pains me to see\nYou're not here,\nbut soon you will be,\nthat much I know.\nStory of Rulan the Brave\n\nThere once was mali'ker\nOh so handsome and brave\nHis words were so beautiful\nPut many in a daze.\nHe traveled across the land\nAnd got lost in a maze\nBut even through all that,\nHe's Rulan the Brave.\n\nStuck in hole\nWith nothing but coal\nRulan struck a fire\nAnd lifted his soul\nHe traveled across the land\nWith his sword in his hand\nAnd music to bide the time\nDamn he could rhyme.\nWhen all was against him\nHe stood there on a whim\nPunched and battered, he still rose\nFist after fist,\nPunch after punch,\nHe stood there and laughed,\nlunge after lunge.\nFor Rulan didnt worry,\nHe was so strong\nHis mind was all he needed,\nTo carry along.\nHe fought against the masses, \nThey were slower than malasses\nHe showed his craze,\nHe was Rulan the brave. \n\nOh Rulan, \nOh Rulan,\nOh how can we move on?\nThis place is dark,\nwhere do we belong,\nThe notes are our guide, and the path is the song, \nIt leads to you,\nOh Rulan,\nOh Rulan,\nAnd we found it with you, all along\nRulan the brave\nRulan the brave\nNever forget,\nRulan the brave.", ""),
        StaticBook("Poetry V1", "Jaya Jayamen", "Poetry\n        Volume 1\n\n        ~Originally by\n    Sofetios Jayamen\n\n     ~Transcribed by\n           Jaya Jayamen\nCOURAGE\n\nIt is a thing you use\nWhen you can't go to the end,\nWhen all seems lost\nAnd you can't defend.\nYou use it as\nIt combines with your will,\nAll you need to do is\nLet it give its fill.\nThe choice is yours,\nGive in or go,\nThough in the end\nOnly you will know.\nSee with your spirit\nAnd not with fear,\nfor then you will know\nThat courage is here.\nTHE DREAMER\n\nThe Dreamer,\nThe one who dares not be the same,\nFor in dreams mysteries unravel,\nAnd endless space you do travel,\nAs your dreams you try to tame.\nAs the Dreamer,\nDreams above the sky,\nAnd looks down below,\nTo the people that show,\nWho know not what lies that high.\nUnawakened, the Dreamer,\nIn a maze of thoughts,\nWandering the mists,\nWith endless twists,\nAs the path on minds paper he jots.\nThough be wary dreamer,\nAs thoughts tend to run away,\nOnly the ones you really need,\nAnd the ones you often feed,\nAre the ones that often stay.\nTHE LAKE\n\nI wander upon a path by a lake,\nWondering where it’s all gone.\nEvery day I used to come here,\nFrom the morning to the evening's yawn.\nEvery now and again I wonder,\nWhy the days have passed.\nAnd think very deeply,\nWhy they don't seem to last.\nDay by day, night by night,\nThe Lake becomes smaller still.\nThe thoughts of it become thinner,\nEven to my strongest will.\nIt has become ten times smaller and ten times shallower,\nEven thought it has not changed.\nTo other people it might be normal,\nbut to me it is considered strange.\nAN UNCOMMON SIGHT\n\nI go about my day,\nDoing the same things as before,\nThe same old road,\nFrom my humble abode,\nNot realizing it is a bore.\nI walk ever onward,\nKnowing all my tasks by heart,\nA straight narrow trail,\nWith nothing new to avail,\nAll I do is my part.\nThen one day as I'm going past,\nA park once again,\nI see a boy,\nwithout even a toy,\nwho couldn't be past ten.\nThe boy was doing something abnormal,\nsomething I hadn't seen before,\nHe was looking in the sky,\nNot even blinking an eye,\nthey didn't even seem sore.\nI wondered if there was a hawk,\nOr something in the sky,\nI didn't hear a thing,\nOnly the birds that always sing,\nSo I did wonder why.\nI looked over,\nto the boy sitting by,\nHe was being bullied by his peers,\nAnd was starting to go in tears,\nJust for looking in the sky.\nI was about to go over,\nTo try to help if I could,\nbut the parents went first,\nBefore I feared the worst,\nTo help as they should.\nI walked on my way home,\nWondering why what I saw came to pass,\nI had a thought why,\nso I looked to the sky,\nand saw it in it's great mass,\nAs I looked to the sky,\nI was transfixed,\nI hadn't done this in a while,\nAnd it did make me smile,\nAs past and current memories mixed.\nI saw the vast expanse,\nIn all its mystery,\nI watched the clouds in the sky,\nAs they changed shape and passed by,\nAs they had for all of history.\nSuddenly someone laughed to my left,\nEven thought it was mild,\nSomeone looking at me,\nLaughing at what I appeared to be,\nJust as the others had done to the child.\nFRIEND OR ENEMY?\n\nEverywhere I am\nI hide from your sight,\nIf it's in the day,\nAnd especially at night.\nI am one of sleep's worst enemies,\nAnd one of fear's best friends,\nI grow ever more larger,\nAs your will begins to bend.\nIn the day I am more friendly,\nEspecially when its hot and I'm in sight,\nBut when it turns to night time,\nI'm sure to give you a fright.\nI am a mimic of sorts,\nI try to copy you while you walk,\nI even mimic other people,\nAlthough I cannot talk.\nEven when you go about the day,\nI skulk and kind of stalk,\nFear or fear not, I am always here,\nI am the shadow on which you walk.\nTHE COBBLER AND THE CROW\n\nI was working in the night,\nAs I bent over a shoe,\nI was working very hard,\nto finish before the morning dew.\nI was just about finished,\nWhen what was this I hear?\nA tapping, slight tapping,\nAnd it seemed to be so near.\nI turned to the window,\nAnd what did I see?\nA crow tapping at my glass,\nStaring at me.\n\"Go away.\" I said,\nSternly as I did stand.\n\"Don't you know I have work to do?\"\nThough I know it didn't understand.\nBut the crow kept tapping at the glass,\nAnd I began to get mad,\nThis crow just would not stop,\nNot even a tad.\nI turned to my unfinished shoe,\nTo work as long as I could bear,\nBut then I noticed something missing,\nThat would stop me from completing the pair.\nThe golden lace that I needed,\nFor this order to be complete,\nI couldn't find it anywhere,\nAs the glass the crow did beat.\nI checked my table, checked my pockets,\nAnd then to my surprise,\nThere was a hole in one,\nThat was just the right size.\nI would never finish this shoe,\nBy the morning light,\nNow things were dire,\nand my situation was quite tight.\n\"I must have dropped it,\nOn the way back from the store!\"\nBut it was too far I thought,\nAs my confidence tore.\nBut then I realized \"What's this?\"\n\"Where was the tapping I couldn't bare?\"\nI looked to the window,\nAnd the crow wasn't there.\nI went to the window,\nAnd what was in its place?\nIt was simple and divine,\nThe golden lace.\nI opened the window,\nAnd took it with care,\nBecause of who gave this gift,\nI was certainly aware.\nI went to my table,\nAnd finished the shoe.\nBut then thought of the crow,\nIf I only knew!\nI then went to bed,\nWith not much I could say,\nI only did hope,\nThe crow would come back some day.\nIMPRINT\n\n\nI stand in a forest,\nOne that I know quite well,\nWhere the trees are tall,\nAnd they never do fall,\nAt least that's what I like to tell.\nI came here,\nWhen I was a boy,\nUsually in the day,\nBut any time I would say,\nThe forest was my favorite toy.\nI came here again,\nA few years ago,\nIt was the same place I knew well,\nAs far as I could tell,\nThere was nothing different to show.\nI open my eyes now,\nTo see the trees,\nMy eyes see an empty place,\nAs if leaving no trace,\nThough this is not what my mind sees.\n\nThe End\nThank you for reading the Jayamen family’s books! If you have any feedback or enjoyed reading, please let me, Jaya Jayamen (( Sofetios )), know. Peoples responses help me write more books! Thanks again! ~Jaya Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("Poison", "Ariana Herenden", "The softness of touch\nThe warmth of breath\nWith airs the cobra strikes\n\nBreathing hope\nBreathing love\nAnd always breathing light\nThe bitten knows not\nWhat happened then\nFor days and days she's numb\n\nBut in time\nThe poison sinks\nAnd she will at last succumb", ""),
        StaticBook("Poisons", "Teerz", "Posions\n\nPlant name\n\nPart\n\nSymptoms\nHyacinth\n\nBulb\n\nNausea, vomiting, diarrhea. May be fatal.\nNarcissus\n\nBulb\n\nNausea, vomiting, diarrhea. May be fatal.\nDaffodil\n\nBulbs\n\nNausea, vomiting, diarrhea. May be fatal.\nOleander\n\nLeaves, branches\n\nExtremely poisonous. Affects the heart, produces severe digestive upset and has caused death.\nDieffenbachia \n\nAll parts\n\nIntense burning and irritation of the mouth and tongue. Death can occur if base of the tongue swells enough to block the air passage of the throat.\nElephant Ear\n\nAll Parts\n\nIntense burning and irritation of the mouth and tongue. Death can occur if base of the tongue swells enough to block the air passage of the throat.\nRosary Pea\n\nSeeds\n\nFatal. A single Rosary Pea seed has caused death.\nCastor Bean\n\nSeeds\n\nOne or two Castor Bean seeds are near the lethal dose for adults.\nLarkspur\n\nYoung plant, seeds\n\nDigestive upset, nervous excitement, depression. May be fatal.\nMonkshood\n\nFleshy roots\n\nDigestive upset and nervous excitement.\nAutumn Crocus\n\nBulbs\n\nVomiting and nervous excitement.\nStar of Bethlehem\n\nBulbs\n\nVomiting and nervous excitement.\nLily-of-the-Valley\n\nLeaves, flowers\n\nIrregular heart beat and pulse, usually accompanied by digestive upset and mental confusion.\nIris\n\nUnderground stems\n\nSevere-but not usually serious-digestive upset.\nFoxglove\n\nLeaves\n\nLarge amounts cause dangerously irregular heartbeat and pulse, usually digestive upset and mental confusion. May be fatal.\nBleeding Heart\n\nFoliage, roots\n\nMay be poisonous in large amounts. Has proved fatal to cattle.\nRhubarb\n\nLeaf Blade\n\nFatal. Large amounts of raw or cooked leaves can cause convulsions, coma, followed rapidly by death.\nDaphne\n\nBerries\n\nFatal. A few berries can kill a child.\nWisteria\n\nSeeds, pods\n\nMild to severe digestive upset. Many children are poisoned by this plant.\nGolden Chain\n\nBean-like capsules in which the seeds are suspended\n\nSevere poisoning. Excitement, staggering, convulsions and coma. May be fatal.\nLaurels\n\nAll parts\n\nFatal. Produces nausea and vomiting, depression, difficult breathing, prostration and coma.\nRhododendrons\n\nAll Parts\n\nFatal. Produces nausea and vomiting, depression, difficult breathing, prostration and coma.\nAzaleas\n\nAll parts\n\nFatal. Produces nausea and vomiting, depression, difficult breathing, prostration and coma.\nJasmine\n\nBerries\n\nFatal. Digestive disturbance and nervous symptoms.\nLantana Camara \n\nGreen berries\n\nFatal. Affects lungs, kidneys, heart and nervous system.\nYew\n\nBerries, foliage\n\nFatal. Foliage more toxic than berries. Death is usually sudden without warning symptoms.\nWild and cultivated cherries\n\nTwigs, foliage\n\nFatal.   Gasping, excitement and prostration are common symptoms.\nOaks\n\nFoliage, acorns\n\nSymptoms appear only after several days or weeks. Takes a large amount for poisoning.\nElderberry\n\nAll parts, especially roots\n\nChildren have been poisoned by using pieces of the pithy stems for blowguns. Nausea and digestive upset.\nBlack Locust\n\nBark, sprouts, foliage\n\nChildren have suffered nausea, weakness and depression after chewing the bark and seeds.\nJack-in-the-Pulpit\n\nAll parts, especially roots\n\nIntense burning and irritation of the mouth and tongue. Death can occur if base of the tongue swells enough to block the air passage of the throat.\nMoonseed\n\nBerries\n\nBlue, purple color, resembling wild grapes. May be fatal.\nMayapple\n\nApple, foliage, roots\n\n Children often eat the apple with no ill effects, but several apples may cause diarrhea.\nMistletoe\n\nBerries\n\nFatal. Both children and adults have died from eating the berries.\nWater Hemlock\n\nAll parts\n\nFatal. Violent and painful convulsions. A number of people have died from hemlock.\nButtercups\n\nAll parts\n\nIrritant juices may severely injure the digestive system.\nNightshade\n\nAll parts, especially the unripened berry\n\nFatal. Intense digestive disturbance and nervous symptoms.\nPoison Hemlock\n\nAll parts\n\nFatal. Resembles a large wild carrot.\nThorn Apple\n\nAll parts\n\nAbnormal thirst, distorted sight, delirium, incoherence and coma. Common cause of poisoning. Has proved fatal.\nLords-and-Ladies\n\nAll parts\n\nBurning and swelling of the lips, mouth, tongue, and throat. Skin irritation after contact with root juices. Stomach pains, dizziness, and cramping after ingestion of berries.\nBlood lily\n\nBulbs\n\nSalivation, nausea, vomiting, and diarrhea.\nBlue Lily\n\nPlant sap in leaves.\n\nIrritation of skin and eyes from cell sap. Irritation and ulceration of mouth if ingested.\nBottlebrush buckeye\n\nSeeds\n\nMuscle weakness and paralysis, dilated pupils, vomiting, diarrhea, depression, paralysis, and stupor.  Possible Death.\nBurning bush\n\nAll Parts\n\nVomiting, diarrhea, weakness, chills, coma, and convulsions.\nLeucothoe\n\nLeaves and nectar from flowers.\n\nSalivation and nasal discharge, sweating, tingling sensation, headache, depression, weakness, abdominal pain, nausea and vomiting, diarrhea, possible death.\nChlorine Lepidella\n\nMushroom \n \nNausea, vomiting, dizziness, abdominal pains, etc. Symptoms occur 30 minutes to several hours after ingesting.  Possible death.\nGround cherry\n\nUnripe berries and leaves.\n\nStomach pain, lowered temperature, dilated pupils, vomiting, diarrhea, circulatory and respiratory depression, loss of sensation; may be fatal.\nTrumpet flower\n\nLeaves and flowers\n\nHeadache, incoordination, excitability, stomach pain, lowered temperature, respiratory depression; may be fatal.\nCelandine\n\nRoots\n\nNausea, vomiting, bloody diarrhea, numbness, fainting, and coma.  Possibly death.", ""),
        StaticBook("Potato, potato!", "Numa II", "Potatoes, potatoes! They grow in the ground when you dig them up they are muddy, brown and round,\nPotatoes, potatoes! Delicious mashed, But they dont taste so good if they've been bashed,\nPotatoes, potatoes! Steamy in their jacket Potatoes, potatoes! fresh in their packet,\nPotatoes, potatoes! can be made into chips, Potatoes, potatoes! Are best when they're crisps!", ""),
        StaticBook("Potions", "Jeffwise Sadget", "Regen\nNormal Water\nLilypad/Vine and tippens root\n\nHaste\nNormal Water\nPoisonous potato and egg\nStrength\nNormal Water\nRed mushroom, cactus, brown mushroom", ""),
        StaticBook("Preceptor App", "Vanya Damaer", "Application for a Preceptor's position at the Eternal College.\n\nName: Vanya Damaer\nAge: 101\nGender: Female\nRace: High Elf\nCurrent City of Residence:\nHaelun'or\n\nWhat do you wish to teach: Natural Philosophy - the study of weather\nspecifically, though I am also willing to teach about the stars and moon and how they affect our world.\n\n\n\n\n\nOOC Information: \nDiscord: sakurablossom#8726\nMC Name: countessem", ""),
        StaticBook("PRIMITIVE RULE 2", "Commodus de Jedih", "adssadsadasdasdsadsThe Primitive Rule of the Poor-Fellow Soldiers of Horen and the Temple of Saint Lucien\nsadasdasdsadasdsadsWritten by Holy Ser Jack Rovin, Grandmaster OSL\nRevised by Holy Ser Rakim Yar of Jedih, Grandmaster OSL\nTranscribed by Comm.\n\n(This is the second book of the OSL Primitive Rule.)\nasdasdsadasdasdsads\n\nX.) On Feast and Fast Days\n\nFeasting and fasting days are observed very seriously among-\nthe brothers of our order. Fasting days shall be enforced with the utmost respect and discipline, as it is good for the health of body and mental state to forfeit satisfaction. Every year, there shall be, in total, at least three weeks of fasting -\nobserved, and no more than three feast days for every week fasted. During these times of feast and fast, brothers are encouraged to remain out of work during the middle of the weeks, and to work vigorously at the beginning and end of the weeks.\nThey may abandon their normal tabard for monk robes or pressed linen robes.\n\nXI.) On the Standards of the Order\n\nThe order may carry three different types of standards, all cared for by the honorific -\n‘Standard Bearer’, who holds no authority in the title. One standard bearer may be appointed for a commandery, and one for the order as a whole. They are responsible for cleaning, repairing, and retrieving the colors as necessary.\nTo leave the colors is a grave misfortune to the Order, and one of the highest embarrassments faced by a Standard Bearer.\n\nThe Rhodesian Standard\n\nThe Rhodesian Standard is the universal symbol of the Order, -\noften portrayed 90 degrees clockwise for use on the tabard and on large standards. Otherwise, it is portrayed horizontally, with the center of the cross representing the divide between the Seven Skies and our mortal realm.\nThe Kaedrini Standard\n\nAdopted by Holy Ser Rosencrantz Revandir as the Bailiff of Kaedrin, the Kaedrini Standard represents the Order’s presence in Kaedrin, as the Kaedreni people and the tradition of the White Rose is considered by -\nmany Lucienists as a precursor to the Order. Much of the Order’s composition comes from that of the Order of the White Rose, and to hang the banner in her native land is only an appropriate gesture of respect.\nThe Prior’s Flag\n\nThe Prior’s Flag is used primarily by the leading commandery in an established priory, and signifies the domination of the area by the Order. The Prior’s Flag may also be used on the field by the Grand Prior, -\nwho may use his presence to boost the morale of the fighting ordermen.\n\nXII.) On the Awards of the Order\n\nAlthough rarely given due to the perceived humility and obedience expressed by all ordermen, -\nawards may be granted to those that give a degree of valor and servitude to the Order inexpressible through simplistic means of thanks. Therefore, a few awards may be granted by the Grandmaster on request of a Master-and-Commander.\n-Crucis Fidei Lotharingo- \n\nThe Crucis Fideo Lotharingo translated into the Common Tongue from Flexio means “The Iron Cross of Lorraine.” The traditional cross of the One Faith, this award is given to men who have proven their faith -\nin the Creator through their actions or words. It is the most common of all awards/medals given out by the Poor-Fellow Soldiers of Horen and the Temple of Ard Krallackh, ussually given to few individuals after a major accomplishment for the Order.\nXIII.) On Dormitories\n\nDormitories in the Order are to individually hold no more but no less than four beds for four ordermen, generally in the style of bunks. They will hold two chests for each orderman in the dorm.\nAbsolutely no doors shall be commissioned for use in the dorms, as these encourage sodomy and other unholy acts. Ordermen shall always sleep with a lit flame providing light in the darkness, unless encamped where darkness is vital to survival.\nThe Grandmaster, the Grand Commander, the Master-and-Commander of a commandery or bailiwick, Grand Prior, Knight Commander, and Knight Constable may be alloted paired rooms instead of four-bed dorms.\nHowever, the door rule still applies. Each one of these men may be allotted space for an appropriate office and small bookcase.\n\nXIV.) On the Size of Priories, Commanderies, and Bailiwicks\n\nThe bailiwick is the smallest and most basic institution -\nof the Order of Saint Lucien. It consists of a humble fort or small castle, often in the frontier or important place of defence. The bailiwick will provide room for 100 soldiers to rest or garrison, and have a minimum of one tower, a general room for -\nprayer, a dormitory to hold 10 soldiers, and a storage that may act as a simple kitchen. Bailiwicks are generally without walls, but are stone structures that can be defended from any angle. Refer to the designs of Holy Ser Rosencrantz Revandir during -\nthe Kaedrini Defence operation of Anthos.\n\nThe Commandery is a main base-of-operations for the Order in an area. One Commandery, generally larger than the rest, shall act as the head Commandery and seat of the Grand Master, while the rest shall-\norganize a region. The Commandery is a large, defendable fortress, which can garrison at least 200 soldiers at all times. If not under the Grandmaster or Grand Commander, the Commandery shall be lead by a Master-and-Commander, who will additionally lead -\noperations in the area, and act as the overlord of the Bailiffs and their respected bailiwicks.\n\nThe Priory is the given term for a commandery and all of its associated bailiwicks. When at full strength, the priory is administrated by a layman, -\nbut this can be done by a master-and-commander. Priories are only established by the Grandmaster.\n\nadsdadasdsadsadsads\n\nThe OSL Primitive Rule has been publically disclosed by Grandmaster Rakim -\non the 11th of the First Seed, 1663.", ""),
        StaticBook("PRIMITIVE RULE I", "Commodus de Jedih", "sdfsfdsfsfdsfsdfdsfdThe Primitive Rule of the Poor-Fellow Soldiers of Horen and the Temple of Saint Lucien\ndsfdsdfdsfdsfdsfdsfdWritten by Holy Ser Jack Rovin, Grandmaster OSL\nRevised by Holy Ser Rakim Yar of Jedih, Grandmaster OSL\nTranscribed by Comm.\nsdasdfassadasdasdas\n\nI.) On Seniority of the Order\n\nIn the Order, a direct chain-of-command shall be established to prevent the usurpation of power from a more capable commander by a more popular commander.\nIf a commander of higher standing appears, he is to take charge immediately. No orders are to be given by any other without the say of the senior.\n\nIf it does happen that one takes command for himself,he and those that followed him shall be -\npunished, either through lashings, demerit, blacklistment, or through the ancient rite of decimation. \n\nThe command shall go as follows:\n\nA.) The Grandmaster\n\nThe Grandmaster is the head of the whole order. His word is -\nrule, and his position is served for life.\n\nB.) The Grand Commander\n\nThe Grand Commander is the Grandmaster’s second, and is naturally in-charge in his absence.\nC.) Knight Commander\n\nThe Knight Commander is in-charge of all the knights, and is third-in-line in seniority.\n\nD.) The Senior Knight Constable\n\nThe Senior Knight Constable, assistant to the -\nKnight Commander, takes place as fourth-in-line.\n\nE.) The Most Senior Master-and-Commander\n\nThe Senior Master-and-Commander of a Commandery or Baliwick takes the place of a Knight Constable -\nin battle, putting him at fifth-in-line of command.\n\nF.) The Most Senior Knight Available\n\nThe most senior knight available may lead the order if the five positions above him are unable. The knights of justice hold seniority -\nover the knights of obedience, and they themselves hold seniority over the knights of devotion. \n\nG.) The Most Senior Sergeant-at-Arms Available\n\nAfter the knights, the senior Sergeant-at-Arms may be called to lead.\nHe is naturally directly in-charge of all enlisted men, often bunking amongst them in the various encampments and garrisons of the order.\n\nIf no one else is present, the brothers are to be commanded by the highest clerical or -\nmilitary presence present. \n\nII.) On the Ranks and Status of the Other Ordermen\n\nThe other ranks of the various ordermen may be confusing to the initiate or the outsider. To put it simply, the initiates are those who have -\nfreshly entered into the Order with temporary vows. They will be tested for their courage and devotion to God before obtaining a full set of orderly vows. Brothers of the Order are those who have proven themselves in such trials, and are full members of -\nthe order.\n\nBrother-Sergeants are picked from the most martial of the Brothers and Sisters, and they provide a veteran back-bone to the general enlisted corps.\nAbove the Brother-Sergeants is a Sergeant-at-Arms or multiples. They are responsible as junior officers, and are the only men in the order who may be nominated to knighthood without undertaking a squireship.\nIII.) On Blackmarking\n\nA.) The Practice\n\nBlackmarking is the old rite of stripping an oathed man of their rights and rank and putting them beneath those who have just taken oath into the order.\nBlackmarking is seen as a last attempt for a brother to save himself and his name before being excommunicated.\n\nThe Blackmarked have no rights, no honor, and no name. They are to be referred to as Blackmarked. If needed to specify, they will-\nbe named by their appearance or race.\n\nB.) The Knights’ Clause\n\nKnights, the officers and idols of the Order, are to remain in the bright light of the Creator. To fall far from grace will result in blackmarking without the ability to regain rank.\nIV.) On the Dress of the Brothers and Knights of the Order\n\nA.) Clothes\n\nAs a standard, those of the Order are to wear one color, whether it be brown, or white, or black is up to them. It is preferred that in the summer months white-\nbe worn. They are to be of simple fabric, not of sheep’s or lamb’s wool. Pointed shoes and shoelaces are never to be worn. They are an abomination to holy men and serve only pagan reinforcers.\n1.) Brothers\n\nWhile on duty, Brothers of the Order of Saint Lucien are expected to be uniformed in their standard tabards.\n\n If caught ill-prepared, harsh punishment is expected to be implemented by the senior commander.\nWhile off-duty, the Brothers are allowed to reside in plain linen fabrics or lowly clerical robes. Robes, unless in the style of monk habits, shall always be white, pure, and clean. \n\n2.) Knights\nKnights of the Church of the True Faith are expected to be in their tabards at all times. They are at all times ready to fight for the Faith. Those that have not taken their full vows wear a grey cloak with their tabard while those with all of the vows -\nwear the red cloak.\n\nB.) Armor\nThe standard set of battle for those of the Order is that of iron plate. In the case of a small skirmish or a lower-risk mission, iron maille is to be worn instead.\nThe armour is to be plain, though holy decoration is allowed. Gilded or trimmed armour is frowned upon and is often met with light punishment, though the real factors will come in battle.\nV.) On Reading of the Lesson\n\nAlways, at the Order's dinner and supper, let the Holy Scripture be read, if possible. If we love the Creator and all His holy words and His holy commandments, we should desire to listen attentively; the reader of the -\nlesson will tell you to keep silent before he begins to read. \n\nVI.) On Eating Habits\n\nTo keep in the good grace of all fellows, two meals are to be served per day, with the exception of fast days and during battles.\nDuring battles, fighting brothers may expect an extra, third meal before their fight, but only after fasting the day before. The first meal of the brothers is to be served at lunch, and it is to be the largest meal of the day. The last meal of the day, -\ndinner, is to be served humbly but sufficiently. For the sake of our Qalasheen brothers, pork is not to be served as a dish, and tea is always offered during meals. Preferably, fish shall be served as a meal, with exceptions for mutton or beef -\noccassionally made. Meat shall be accompanied by a vegetable and tuber, such as lettuce and potatoes, and with a fruit, such as an apple. Sweet dishes, such as cookies, cake, pie, or other assortments are frowned upon by the Order as -\ngluttonous temptations. As for the drinking of spirits, this is allowed in mediation. The Creator has gifted us with the ability to cleanse the water into a medicine against illness and stagnation. Brothers are encouraged to indulge in wines and simple -\nales in place of water, which has proven untrustworthy in the quest for good health.\n\nAs for the smoking of herbs, brothers are allowed to take take part in such activities after eating meals. The herbs smoked may not intoxicate the mind of the brother, -\nsuch as \"Cactus Green\" , but may be added for flavor in a rather dull life.\n\nVII.) On Saying Grace\nPray after eating, give the remains to the poor.\n\nAlways after every dinner and supper all the brothers should-\ngives thanks to the Creator in silence, if the church is near to the place where they eat, and if it is not nearby, in the place itself. With a humble heart they should give thanks to the Creator who is the Lord Provider. Let the remains of the -\nbroken bread be given to the poor and whole loaves be kept. Although the reward of the poor, which is the Seven Skies, should be given to the poor without hesitation, and the True faith doubtless recognises you among them.\nVIII.) On Faults\n\nFaults are simply actions that are committed by brothers that are in the wrong and are punishable, either through mental or physical labor.\n\nThis can include anything from copying books to being whipped-\nin public. Faults generally exist under the cardinal vices:\n\nGula (gluttony), Fornicatio (fornication, lust), Avaritia (avarice/greed), Superbia (hubris, pride), Tristitia (sorrow/despair/despondency), Ira (wrath), Vanagloria (vainglory)-\nAcedia (sloth).\n\nFaults can also be more specific. For example, harboring the condemned is a fault. If a great number of faults are committed, a brother will be sought out for blackmarking, or might be removed from the order entirely.\nIX.) On the Elderly, Sick, and Deceased Brothers\n\nThe Elderly brothers are to be relieved of their duties as soldiers, and are to remain in support roles to main forces.\n\nThis support work would involve merchanting, -\nfarming, gardening, and writing. Some may accompany the men on campaign, but will not be given weapons to fight with unless in dire circumstances.\n\nThe sick of the Order shall be quarantined from the rest of the Order to prevent disease spread.\nAt times, the use of quarantine viewing rooms may be used to study the infected, as well as the imprisoned. The surgeon of the Order shall have an office in this quarantine area shall have a diary to keep on the patients and a research book depicting -\ntreatments for various ailments. \n\nDeceased brothers will be buried in coffins at a place of their choosing, unless falling without prior plans. As a standard, the deceased will be given a stone Lorraine cross over their burial plot, -\nflowers on the grave itself, and a few different inscriptions. Their body will be buried in the Tabard, fully equipped for battle. Their personal sword shall go with them to the grave.", ""),
        StaticBook("Prince Belestram", "An Interviewer", "Interview of High Prince Belestram,\n\nL: Interviewer\nB: Belestram\nL: You're not a druid are you? What do you follow then, if anything?\nB: When I was young I was of the faith of Aeriel, I was one of her chosen before they went to darkness and strife. The caretaker does not require worship of her adherents however,\nand as such I often kept to the beliefs of Almenodrim, my family. We believe in the way of Malin.... Of late however I have taken up the rite of the Aspectists\n\nL: So are you then apart of the Naelrurir?\nB: No I do not have that honour, nor do I think its right for a high prince to belong to a priestly order. Though I do respect their influence over the wood elf flock.\n\nL: And why do you give them such control and authority over the city?\nB: The Aspectist rite is essential in the founding of the state that has become Irrinor [Wood Elven district of Caras Elder].\nL: Artimec- what do you think of him and his ways?\nB: What he does in his personal life is none of my business unless it\ntransgresses any laws of the Dominion.\nL: He seems to be above the law, and able to create his own laws. Are you aware of what he does in your absence?\nB: Some. Some are sanctioned by the Evarir Act, or the enforcement of Aspectist beliefs in\nthe Irrinor district, which is his right.\nL: Is it his right to slap a woman for defending a zephonim, or to stab a bryophite for not talking about a berry?\nB: The Zephonim have been rendered illegal by an act of Lady Awaiti.\nL: Ah, but before?\nB: Zephonim are tainted creatures, and it is my concern for the defense of elves, not Zephonim.\nL: Indeed, but it was an elf who was harmed when they asked for the Zephonim to be peacefully released.\nB: Is there something else you want to say Loras?\nMy time is limited.\n- Avoided the Question-\nL: Alright. What is your opinion on the void? Both from you personally and you as an Aspectist.\nB: The void is unnatural, its existance is an affront to creation. But I personally have no\nconcern with responsible use of magic.\nL: What would you say about people using or selling voidal enchanted things in the city?\nB: I have no opinion on that. From a Druid standpoint, any magic is corruption.\nL: Ah, and what about more large scale things like flaming swords etc.?\nB: Should follow the same logic.\nL: And what about using things with voidal magic? As using voidal magic is banned, and using the enchantments is using voidal magic by proxy.\nB: Each district is to their own. You can in the other two districts, and in Irrinor it is up to the discretion of the Virarim and Lords.\nL: So you dont know what they permit?\nB: I do, but enchanted weaponry is an undescribed quantity and you\nshould always get permission to use it.\nL: Do you plan to be a full-fledged Druid in the future?\nB: Not while I'm high prince.\nL: How are the Naelrurir essential in the founding of Irrinor?", ""),
        StaticBook("Progenitor Is: 1", "Taenost Ihnsil'dionn", "\\The Progenitor/\n\nThe Progenitor is a publication that stands to represent an unbiased report accompanied by historical accounts recorded by Taenost Ihnsil'dionn. These historical accounts are classified as primary, through the eyes,\nhands, and participation of the recorder hisself. What you will read within is as accurate of accounts as an 'aheral may achieve, no spin - no adjective to spice nor distract from the history wrought between peoples of the Fringe.\nThe Voice of the Alrasians\n\nThe High King Syrio has attested that the start of his expeditionary camp's involvement in the Zionist War came when Valesmark merchants were attacked by human bandits. Dwarven details protected the merchants and\nrebuked the attempted highwaymen attempts, allowing the Valesmark to deliver their goods to the Cloud Temple of Anthos. Thereafter, High King Syrio explained that he felt drawn towards the Zionist treaty to deter further highwaymen attempts on his own.\nHigh King Syrio remained unfidgeting with concerns of the proposed treaty from High Chancellor Wilfriche Buron of the Orenites, not revealing what he nor his council members felt or decided. \n\nThe Alrasians bound themselves to secrecy in that they did not\ndetail or reveal any of their future hopes as to their participation in the theatre of war. All that could be ascertained was that the Alrasians insist that their perch atop the karst of Kal'Arkon was temporary and that they have land speculations\nunderway. \n\nHigh King Syrio attested lastly to an attack that the Orenites committed that led the camp to be slaughtered mostly. His description bore witness that men, women, and children were put to the sword by the Orenites.\nInterviewed High King Syrio\n -2nd of Malin's Welcome, 1456\n\nTemple of Vallendar Accosted\n\nThe Temple of Vallendar currently stands along the grounds of an old, yet ruined settlement named Montefleur. A clericess by the name of Lenia Ith'ael\nbore witness to an accosting from a supposed Ruskan named Harrison de Silvarois and a polemic from Lucienists which concluded the temple to be of a heretical nature.\n\nThe Clericess has confirmed that besides those two isolated incidents, no other\nconfrontations have occurred despite the Temple being in the current theatre of the Zionist War. Lenia Ith'ael confirmed that the temple is monastic in nature, adherents of Tahariae as the Archangel of Purity and patron of the Clerical Order farm produce\non Vallendar's grounds.\n\nInterviewed Lenia Ith'ael\n -5th of Malin's Welcome, 1456\n\nThe Dwarven Casus Bellum\n\nBalek Irongut detailed the reason for their involvement in the Zionist War. A summoned emissary dispatch arrived at Vekaro from\nKal'Arkon consisting of Lords Dizzy and Zahrer along with dwarfish legionnaires. \n\nThe Orenites examined the relation between the Orkish Warnation and Dwarfish Kingdom by relating that the Warnation attacked Vekaro in the near past, date untold, and asked\nthe Dwarves to allow them to return the same treatment without intervention. The Dwarfish emissaries requested evidence of such an event and the Orenites failed to produce. Balek Irongut described the confrontation as ending with Wilfriche cursing the\nDwarfish dispatch and besetting his soldiers of Vekaro on them in which all Dwarves successfully escaped except for Lord Dizzy who was injured by a pikeman.\n\nBalek Irongut described this instance as the casus bellum that King Wulfgar acquired which led\nDwarfish Kingdom to the current Zionist War.\n\nInterviewed Balek Irongut\n -15th of Malin's Welcome, 1456\n\nAn Attempt on Wilfriche Buron\n\nUpon winning a battle at dusk against the Dwarfish, Alrasian, and Orkish forces, the Orenites sent a\ndetail along with their High Chancellor to confront Syrio on what they perceived as a betrayal of expectations as they had given a truce to the Alrasians which Syrio had to confirm with his council. Upon arriving in their expeditionary camp, Wilfriche\nbegan his warnings to High King Syrio before having an axe crash down upon hisself. An assassin of Mali'ker ethnicity informed those around of his militant dislike for the Orenites before being slain by Wilfriche's detail.\n\nThe Orenites immediately drew\nsuspicions that High King Syrio had organized the plot as they escorted Wilfriche away from Kal'Akron as legionnaires attempted to rally for what gave the Orenites fear as being a further attack on the High Chancellor.\nAccosting of the Mali'aheral\n\nThe elcihi of the Mali'aheral, Tahn'siol have been accosted and accused of taking a political stance in the Zionist War. The Mali'aheral have a reverence for neutrality, as insisted by the Sohaer himself. An issue of\nanother publication known as The Flagship has been countered by the 'aheral as being libellous and request that the publisher remove any content that attempts to tie a neutral political entity into a war. \n\nBounty on High King Syrio\n\nA bounty\nissued by the Orenites, specifically High Chancellor Wilfriche Buron has been announced on High King Syrio Forel. The current paying price for his head stands at 2,000 minas.\n\nPok'Ugluk Alive?\n\nAn infamous and key figure in Uruk culture and history\nhas been reported to being found in the Fringe. Whether reports are true could not be confirmed, although the reports reveal that Pok'Ugluk stated a disdain for the ruling Azog clan of the Warnation and a desire to remove them for their seat of power.\nScourge at Kal'Akron\n\nThis subject matter remains to being very controversial with differing narratives. The Zionists upon being capitulated and slaughtered as they fled into Kal'Akron brought about an unsubstantiated accusation that the Scourge aided\nthe Orenites. The Progenitor\nshares a statement of a witness who corrects this narrative by explaining the following: The Zionists insist that they were struck by frostfire along the fields north of Kal'Akron, but failed to remember that they had\nfailed to hold position to be struck - the Orenites had already pushed, killed, and defeated the Zionist army. In fact, it was the Orenites who had been assaulted by Harbingers in which the trajectories of their frost-fire led to some of the Orenites\nidentifying the distinct, grim appearances of Harbingers who sat along the karst of Kal'Akron nearest the Alrasian Expeditionary Camp.\n\nAn 'aheral historian recommends the following statement: When you study events in history, your best evidence\nare primary sources. Primary sources are accounts from those who lived and witnessed the particular event in person and were typically affected by said event in some way and has emotions, thoughts, and experiences to recount. The Orenites had succeeded\nin the battle whilst most, if not all of the Zionist forces had been felled. The best judgement to make in this case would be to take the Orenites' accounts as solid while the Zionist accounts are mythic explanation as to their failure in the battle at\nKal'Akron. It is typical for  collective memory to weave up an explanation of either realistic or mythical proportions to define the moments in which those people had gone through a hardship.\n\nThe Progenitor, in the next issue, welcomes editorial and\nopinionated content that will be clearly and visually separated from our journalism. The Progenitor in and of itself remains separated from the conflict and those who write for the Progenitor uphold a standard of refusing any attempts to persuasively or\nforcibly put forth libellous, flowery, and scandallous content. \n\nThank You for Reading\n\nProgenitor\n Issue I\n  Printed on:\nThe 20th of Malin's Welcome\n                      1456", ""),
        StaticBook("prophets trials1", "Faiz Ibn Qhuhafah", "Trials of the prophets Part 1\n\nby Faiz Ibn Qhuhafah\nThe prophets (peace be upon them all) have things in common and things seperating them. One thing in common is the common faith in Allah.\nThe first prophet (Allahs peace be upon him) lived and breathed for Allah. He was the first to bring us out of the time of many heads of religion where humanity worshipped the many faced god of barbery and savagry.\nthey believed him weak as a caravan found him by a burned down bush in the desert thirsty and almost starved to death. They laughed at him and asked him \"which god?\" as he said that allah had shown himself to him in the bush.\nThey believed him weak as he refused to join the savage rituals where you drank the blood of your fellow man... \n\nAs his words spread and the first believers of the Iman al-Rashidun began to gather they where scared.\nAllah had put his fear in them but the ïblis convinced them to do the unforgiveable. In the middle of the night guided by ïblis they dragged him out his bed in the middle of the night and dragged them to their camp.\nin their camp they bound him to a pike and roasted him alive above the flames of ïblis. THEY tried to get him to resign the Iman al-Rashidun... the only words he said was \"Subhanallah!\" in disbelief they kept roasting him... not a scream was let out.\nIn the morning however a broad scare of men screamt on top of their lungs as the wrath of Allah was released on the men and all where dead except one soldier to tell the tale of Allahs wrath.\nThe second prophet of Allah was once a brave warrior whom had killed countless people in battle untill he met the first prophet (Allahs peace be upon him). The first prophet inspired him to a life in peace trying to achieve the greatest of all jihads.\n“To fight against the infidels is Jihad; but to fight against your evil self is greater Jihad.” said the first prophet (Peace be upon him) to our second as our second raised his sword to defend our first. Our dear first prophet was lead off to die.\nThe second prophet gathered support from the commoners and support of Allah was spread trueout the camp. As the protests came to the cheifs tent our second prophet stepped forward towards the cheifs guards whom had swords drawn\nOur second prophet stepped forward towards the guards taking the sword from his belt dropping it in front of the guardsmen calling out their leader: \"If you want to fight come forth and kill me. If you do not let us pass.\" Seized by the compassion\nof Allah their leader surrendered and the men rejoiced in the glory of allah pronouncing: \"There is no god but allah and the prophets are his messengers.\"\n\nThis wave of peaceful protests swept a second camp but in the third camp something changed...\nThe third camp the garrison went amock leaving our prophet slain upon the field together with thousands of civilians. However Allahs plan was not over for the second prophet as he seven days later in a miracle rose from the grave for the world to behold.\nWhile dead he had spoken with Allah and in his wisdom Allah knew that the infidels would not surrender their many faced god without force but stubborn our second prophet carried on.\nHe gathered more people and led them back to the city in a peacefull wave... once more him and his companions where slain and Allah urged him to use violence but no. Thrice he was slain and thrice he was ressurected in total for Allahs plan.\nAfter his third resurection our prophet saw the damage it had done to his camp as they came together around him he asked for his sword with the words: \"We fight because He – the Glorified – commanded us with fighting\" when asked why he now suddently\nhave decided to fight.\n\nHe conqoured all the tribes and left men of the Iman al-Rashidun  to rule them independantly untill Caliph Faiz united the clans.\nAllah have plans for all of us both prophets, laymen and infidels. We may try to reject our plan but Allah will always steer us onto the path.\nInsha'Allah\n\nSubhanallah", ""),
        StaticBook("Ptah's Account", "SpamShok", "The Writings of Preeminent Savant Ptah Remneal of the Ministry of Contemplation, on the voyage of the ship the Beard Reborn to the island of Sugarshank.\nThe owner of the Beard Reborn, Admiral Golwenor Oakshadow, has been kind enough to appoint me the Officer of Scholarly Matters for the duration of the trip. I shall record any knowledge discovered here within this book. The Beard itself is quite frankly\nthe most utterly impressive ship I have ever laid eyes on, dwarfing my memories of the grand flagship of Alras, King Syrio's Beard. The name of this ship indicates to me that Admiral Oakshadow wishes to continue the legacy of the Alrasian flagship. I have\nfirm confidence in his ability to navigate this ship and, in time, lead us safely home. My associate, Savant Tenshar Karkun of the Department of Naturalism, has been made the spotsman of the crow's nest. The other officers I am not familiar with.\nA group of Orcs have, interestingly, been hired as the guards of this vessel, in the case that we chance upon hostile forces, or discontent arises amongst the crew or passengers. I do hope neither situation is fated for us. We have now set sail, and it\nseems someone on the crew has stolen the entire supply of food we had.\n-Day 2\nA giant fin was seen to our side. It could possibly have been a relatively large whale we saw, but we cannot be certain.\n--We have hit a storm, and one of our Orc\nguards fell over board. The storm grew to such intensity that we were forced to draw up the sails, drop anchor and get below deck. As I write now the winds sway the ship to an extent most disruptive to my writing. The waves are no better, and I have\nrecieved several bruises from being knocked about, even below decks. It was also revealed at this time that the one who stole our supply of food was the Dwarven Paragon Kjell Stormhammer.\n-Day 3\n--The storm withered over time, and we had\nbegun to manage the rigging again when the Beard Reborn must have hit something very, very large. Whatever it was, I was knocked overboard. A brave human by the name of Varlan Gerofe pulled me back up, and in this sentence I thank him for saving my life.\n--The spotters indicate beginning to see a dim red glow to our Lawboard, which I take to be Northeast.\n--During the night a series of large spiders poured out from the storage decks, seemingly having survived off the quartermaster's supplies.\n--We received yet another large hit to the ship at night.\n-Day 4\n--A massive create unlike any I have seen before emerged to our starboard. The crew rushed down to man the ballistae. The creature hit the hull of the boat, and in that time we manage\nget at least three successful shots into the sea creature. The beast bit into the ship, and  was shot again several more times, in the side of its head namely. The creature, wounded, retreated. The ballista responsible for the critical blow was damaged\nand the woodworkers began to repair the gaping hole in our hull. The creature reemerged from the water, and the aforementioned Paragon decided it best to go into the water and swim to it. He was promptly consumed. Many more shots went out, hitting\nthe sea monster in the throat and the gut. We happened to have an alchemist onboard, and produced for us a vial of alchemist fire. This was then fixed to a ballista bolt. The creature took out two more bites of the hull. It then came up behind the Beard\nReborn, and the bolt carrying the alchemy fire was repositioned to face it. A successful hit, the creature began to burn even when wet, and was forced to submerge itself. It is also worth noting that the red glow I reported before has steadily grown\nbrighter. Several more bites were taken out of the hull, bolts fired, and crew eaten. The beast finally fell beneath the waves, however that victory was short lived. Another creature emerged. A storm began to gather again. One bolt managed to hit the\nsecond sea monster in the eye.(delete references to second beast) The creature, maddened, charged us head on, and came directly on top of the deck. This opportunity was taken, and the crew began shooting bows, crossbow bolts and stabbing it.-night7", ""),
        StaticBook("Pumpkin and Rat", "Dedicant Popo Sandybanks", "Yay it was,\nThat Cerridwen would make\nsomething so sweet, 'twas\nA pumpkin! Pumpkin!\nSo orange and round\nwhoever saw it made a happy sound!\nThe pumpkin spread\nuntil one day\nCernunnos created a creature that filled\nthe pumpkin with dread.\nA rat! A rat!\nIn its hole it sat\nWatching the pumpkin\nHis tail thumpin'\nWaiting for his chance to strike!\nThe rat came out\nNo people around to make a shout\nand burrowed its way into the Pumpkin.\nThe rat ate and ate\nhis hunger unable to sate.\nThough the pumpkin was not sad.\nThe pupkin did not cry.\nThe pumpkin was actually glad!\nThough the Pumpkin dies\nThe rat lives.\nAnd through the rat\nMore seeds will spread\nAnd with more pumpkins\nMore rats will come, their tails thumpin'.\nAs such is the way of the Green Man and Lady,\nto bring life from death\nA balance made through equality.\nEvery living creature\nmust know one simple truth\nLet there be life when you cause death! \nLet the balance be held!", ""),
        StaticBook("Purity", "Ser Archrim Elmoran", "Purity thesis\nby Archrim Elmoran\n\nWhat is Purity? \nBy definition in a dictionary I found purity is as follows.\nPurity: Freedom from Adulteration or Contamination.\n\nThat contamination is ever present in our lives, it is the\nall the murderers, theives, undead, and tainted beings alike. It is the darkness and the evil that creates such beings that I had just named.\n\nPurity is the freedom from such things, true purity is a world without evil, a world without darkness.\nAs a cleric one must strive to spred their purity and their light to keep the ever present darkness from closing in on themselves and the ones they protect. A Cleric is a vanguard against the evil and corruption that invades our world on a daily basis.\nSo in short, what purity is to me at least, are those who fight against the dark, the ones who inforce and abide by the law, the clerics, guards, your every day women, men, and children....who do what they can for the good of the world and for eachother.\nThey are the ones who are pure, and all those who do the same. Because purity is an ideal and a state of being", ""),
        StaticBook("Purity.", "Gabriel Maul", "**Many Ink Stains cover the pages of this book, the penmanship very fine and thick** \n“I am Gabriel Maul, A student of Lilyana’s, I was asked to write down my thoughts of ‘Purity’, So, Here it Goes.\nI believe if you ask a single man or woman from each race what their thoughts of Purity is, What it is, who has it, E.c.t, You’ll get a list of different replies, , I believe Purity is something gifted to us by the Lord,\nSomething each, and every breathing, living being has, From Krug, The Malin, to Lady Lilyana, to a simple Guardsman, like myself, If all people have ‘Purity’ inside them.\nwhat are the questions?\nDo they enhance it? Do they bring out the light in themselves,\nor do they hide it under a cloak of darkness? \nThere is a Thick line between ‘Good’ And Purity.\nA man that walks along the streets of an Oren city, giving food to the poor, doesn’t make them pure,\nFor Purity, is much much deeper,  I believe Purity, is mercy, forgiveness, and Faith.\nrather it be in a god, or in your self, I’ve once met an elven man, who says he has never shed a  drop of blood, but has been brought to his knees many times, un braking his faith in the Lord,\ndespite being so beaten, That, is purity, or maybe It’s not..Maybe Purity is something more, A Gift from the Aenguls.. or simple thought in one man’s mind. But no matter how you see it,\nNo matter who’s tongue it comes from..no one can truly tell you what Purity is. A Dear Friend of mine, told me what he thought Purity was Being free from immortality, for when you’re pure, you’ll have no darkness He said.\nA Rather vague reply, but I simply nodded, Now, let me tell you what /I/ Truly think it is...\"“My Father was a noble man, for the ten years I knew him, he prayed to the Lord, and thanked the Creator for his life,\nbut by night, he slept with many, and lead his vessel to ‘impurity’, So in short, praying, loving the lord, acting as if you have faith, is not purity. For purity, is something else, it is being unmarked,\nIt is being an Untouched Vessel. It’s being able to push thru the darkness, without being lead on by it’s promises No love for gold, or heart for women should stop you from being pure.\nYou should be able to jump into a pool full of lust, and greed, and even death. But bed no more than your wife, spend no more than your own, and slay no innocent man,\nIf one can truly do this, if one can truly live thru life without being blinded by the darkness, then, Aren’t they pure? Maybe not..” **Ink drops would cover the rest of that page, as if Maul was going to say more, but went to the next page.**\n“If You have two (or more) eyes, breath your own breath, and have flesh, rather it be Green, black, or White, You have purity within you..The option to use this purity is your own. So long as your will, is your own,\nthen you can embrace your purity, and let it shine like a light that weakens the dark, and blinds the faithless For you, and only you, can lead yourself into purity, No High elf King, No Orcish Rex, and no Graven Spook can tell you you are impure..\nFor the choice is yours, and only yours,”\n“‘I am lost..broken, and unfixable,’ Something the Darkness will poke at you, and make you think to bend your will, and brake your faith, but worry not..there is hope..If you hurt the lives of innocent,\nbe it man or woman, Orc or Elf, Elder..Or Youth..Then free yourself..I say that anyone who is impure..and can pure..because why? Because, I have faith,\nI have faith that not only did the Lord gift us all with purity, but, also with Free will..One small change in your life..Could make the change, of everyone around you\nShine bright, Love all your  enemies, be loyal to your wives, and nothing. Can stop you, from being Pure..”", ""),
        StaticBook("Quen", "Azureth", "In Quen, you play as a sigil drawing wizard fighting other wizards. The game works for any amount of players. To play, you need a deck of nine Quen cards, which can be found at the end of this book.\nFirst, shuffle your deck and lay it face down. Then flip a mina or use some other method to determine the turn order. The first player does not draw a card on his turn. You begin with nine health and lose if you reach zero. Each player begins with one\ncard. On your turn, you may draw one card and use one card. Used cards are put back in your deck. For optimal fun, bet cards or minas.\nDamage - (Triangle)\n\nYour target loses three health.\nRestore - (Circle)\n\nYour target gains three health.\nDuplicate - (Square)\n\nYou may play an additional card next turn.\nErase - (Kite)\n\nYour target places a card of your choice back in their deck.\nSearch - (Ellipse)\n\nYour target draws two cards.\nDisable - (Rhombus)\n\nYour target can play one less card next turn.\nSplinter - (Star)\n\nYour target loses two health. They also lose one additional health each time they play a card next turn.\nRewind - (Hourglass)\n\nThis card is removed from the game. All players put their cards back in their decks.\nTrap - (Pentagon)\n\nPlace this card face down on the table. The next player who plays a card loses three health.\n((Your deck is the top bar of your inventory. Your hand is your hotbar. Your cards are numbered one through nine, corresponding to their slots. Roll nine sided dice to draw, rerolling if no card is in that slot.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Rabbit Anatomy", "Leyunia", "-=================-      Rabbit Anatomy\nWritten By: Leyunia\n            -=-\nThis is a compilation of my notes that were made during my dissection and study of Rabbits for the art of Conjuration. - L\n            -=-\nRabbit Skeletal System:\nThe rabbit has a much more delicate and thin skeletal structure compared to other animals, and it only makes up about half its weight. Every bone can be easily broken, yet still holds the same properties as the skeletons in our own bodies. There are\nApproximately fourty-six or so bones that make up the spinal column, seven bones in the neck, twelve bones in the chest, four pelvic bones, and sixteen bones that make up the tails structure. \n           -=-\nRabbit Muscular System:\nWild Rabbits are extremely athletic creatures, and can reach quite high speeds when running. This running exercise strengthens their muscles, hearts, and lungs, and is used when fleeing predetors.\n            -=-\nRabbit Digestive System:\nAs total herbivores, rabbits have an extremely long digestive system in order to process the plants in the most efficient way. The whole of a rabbit anatomy has evolved to survive a very poor diet. The whole digestive system of a rabbit is massive and\ncounts for just about fifteen percent of its total body weight. \nThe rabbits stomach: In an adult rabbit the total length of the canal is 4.5m, after a short oesophagus there is a simple stomach which only stores a few g's of plants. Food eaten by a\nrabbit reaches the stomach quite quickly, and only takes a few hours to digest. \nThe Liver & Pancreas:\nTwo major organs secrete into the small intestine, the liver and pancreas. Bile from the liver contains salts and many organic substances, and aids\nwith digestion. The reverse is pancreatic juice which contains a considerable amount of digestive chemicals that allow the breakdown of proteins and such. The small intestine of a rabbit, if it was laid out it would be more then ten times the length of\nthe rabbit itself, the contents of the stomach are easily entered into the small intestine in short bursts, by strong stomach movements.\nThe intestine is about 3m long and nearly 1cm, its contents are liquid, especially in the upper section.\nLarge Intestine:\nThe large intestine is made up of a few organs, and serves as a secondary break-down for anything the small intestine could not break down.\n\n           -=-\nRabbit Respiratory System:\nRabbits themselves are nasal breathers, blocking their nasal passages for any reason can lead to respiratory compromise and struggled breathing.\nThe rabbit has a small chest cavity compared with the size and weight of its digestive system. The lungs\nare soft and compact spongy masses of tissue and account for the breathing, obviously.\n           -=-\nRabbit Heart System:\nThe Rabbit's heart acts just as any other, it supplies the blood-flow and such throughout the body.\n           -=-\nRabbit Genitalia System:\nThe female rabbit genitalia acts like any other females. As does the males. I'm not going in-depth about this for fucks sake. The reproduction system is the same as-well.\n            -=-\nRabbit Urinary System:\nThe urinary tract is like any other, the kidneys and all. Urine is formed as blood goes into the kidneys and is filtered, along with feces.\n           -=-\nDental System:\nThey have teeth, flat for the most part to mold and mesh plant matter.\nEyes, Nose, and Hearing:\nThe rabbits are farsighted in most instances, and have a rather large field of vision. They have quite a strong sense of smell, and very good hearing.\n           -=-", ""),
        StaticBook("Radiancy", "Faaron", "Radiant is the black sun, it's ever watching gaze guiding the faithful and strong. Steadying their blades and guiding their aim. Mark remaining true and each strike connecting with accuracy like none other.\n\nTheir armies are dense, loyal soldiers mar\nalong in perfect columns towards the goal uttered forth by the commanders. Their plight could never be stopped, it will never be stopped.\n\nSuch are the words of a Morghuul, a loyal servant of the Abyssal Legions. Our master is a dragon, a fearsum gen\nwho demands an unquestioning attitude and rewards with improvement towards the ultimate goal.\n\nWe will win, victory each day despite any so called setbacks. In our path will lay a pool of blood and a pile of innards. Our enemies will spill their\ninner being about the land from which we walked. Villages will burn and storehouses will be pillaged. No one will live to see a glowing and loving sun ever again.\n\nDarkness has erupted from it's cold northern abode. And it is spreading, it will sprea\nuntill all is consumed. I promise you this, we shall not lose.\n\nA threat? Perhaps, but a promise indeed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Rankings!", "Luna Lyeis", "Dawn\nRiven\nme!\nWyvern\nVul\nTreemma\nAveyn\nGuinevene\nViltaren\nKefi\nDark elf 1\ndark elf 2\nDark elf 3\ndark elf 4\nFarfolk 1\nfarfolk 3\nfarfolk 2\nAll of Vul's slaves\nI kinda forgot the names... of alot of them... oops", ""),
        StaticBook("Ranks of Clergy", "Theran", "High Pontiff\nThe High Pontiff is the absolute, autocratic leader of the Church who fills the papal throne, and fulfills the role of the previous position of High Pontiff. He is considered the Vicar of God and infallible in regards to matters of\ntheology. He wears a fresh white robe made in their honor as the head of the Church and wear a gilded laurel in honor of Horen I. High Pontiffs must be celibate as decreed by High Pontiff Lucien II. The High Pontiff is to be addressed as 'Your\nHoliness'.\n¬†\nBishop\nBishops are the administrators of the Church. They manage their entire diocese, typically an immense tract of land, and are responsible for picking acolytes and naming priests within the diocese. They\nalso are a member of the Ecclesiastical Synod. They can only be ordained by High Pontiff. Bishops must be celibate. Bishops wear the aged robes of High Pontiffs past to symbolize their role in the Synod and are to be addressed as 'Your Eminence'.\n¬†\nAbbot\nThe Abbot is considered peer to the Bishops of the clergy; however, their role is more specialized to reflect their monastic vows. Abbots often are master\ntheologians who train both priests and monks in ways of secular and clerical intellectual traditions. They administer abbeys, houses of learning and monastic life, and wear the aged robes of High Pontiffs past to symbolize their role in the Synod.\nAbbots must be celibate. They are to be addressed as 'Your Eminence'.\n¬†\nPriests\nAlso known as clerics, priests are the backbone of the Church and represent the majority of the Clergy. They\npreach in settlements, perform all sacraments, morally guide communities as leaders of their parish, and may take on other professions as long as their loyalty remains chiefly to the Church. They also must serve the\nparish they were assigned to by the bishop. Serving as holy men, they may be mobilized by their superiors or sent on a variety of different clerical missions by them. A priest can be ordained by any bishop, provided they swear the Oath of\nOrdination. They may not wed once assuming the priesthood, but may wed prior and ascend to the priesthood. They are required to wear their uniform at all times, and they wear black. They are to be addressed as 'Father'.\n¬†\nMonks\nWhen many of the priesthood are aged and no longer able to administer their duties as actively as they wish, they often retire to the monastery and undergo monastic vows. Others chose the monastic life based on their\npassions towards theology and study, relieved of their duty to preach but still permitted to access church resources. Monks are the backbone of the learned institutions of the Church and focus largely on writing, prayer, alms giving, farming and\ndonation gathering over active adminstration. They are required to wear their uniform at all times, and they wear brown. They are to be addressed as 'Brother'.\n¬†\nDeacon\nDeacons are portrayed as\nnovice clergyman. They act as the servants of the parish priests and help the parish priest with the parish. They are permitted to hold mass, but they may not perform any other sacrament, such as matrimony or baptism. They are\nrequired to wear their uniform at all times, and they wear brown. They are addressed as 'Deacon'.\n¬†\nAcolytes\nAcolytes are the fresh-faced recruits to the clergy, wholly unskilled and\nuntrained in the ways of the Canon. They undergo rigorous study in an attempt to prove their literacy and knowledge in order to ascend to become Deacons. Given they have taken no vows, they do not wear any particular uniform and are addressed by\ntheir given name.", ""),
        StaticBook("Rasputin", "Abram Votyakov", "There lived a certain man, in Oren long ago.\n\nHe was big and strong, in his eyes a flaming glow.\n\nMost people looked at him, with terror and with fear.\nBut to Petrus chicks, he was such a lovely dear.\n\nHe could preach the canon like a preacher, full of ecstacy and fire.\n\nBut, he also was the kind of teacher\nWomen would desire\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nLover of the Oren Queen!\n\nThere was a cat that really was gone.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nOren's greatest love machine!\n\nIt was a shame how he carried on.\nHe ruled the Oren land, and never mind the king.\n\nBut the kasochok he danced really wunderbar.\n\nIn all affairs of state, he was the man to please.\nBut he was real great when he had a girl to squeeze.\n\nFor the queen, he was no wheeler dealer\n\nThough she'd heard the things he'd done\n\nShe believed he was a hole healer,\nWho would heal her son.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nLover of the Oren Queen!\n\nThere was a cat that really was gone.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN! Oren's greatest love machine.\nIt was a shame how he carried on.\n\nBut when his drinking, and lusting, and his hunger for power became known to more and more people, the demands to do something about this outrageous man became louder and louder.\n\"This man's just got to go!\"\nDeclared his enemies.\n\nBut the ladies begged,\n\"Don't you try to do it, please.\"\n\nNo doubt this Rasputin, had lots of hidden charms.\nThough he was a brute, they just fell into his arms.\n\nThen, one night some men of higher standing set a trap, they're not to blame.\n\n\"Come to visit us\" they kept demanding, and he really came.\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nLover of the Oren Queen!\n\nThey put some poison into his wine.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN! \nOren's greatest love machine!\nHe drank it all and he said \"I feel fine!\"\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nLover of the Oren Queen!\n\nThey didn't quit, they wanted his head.\n\nRA RA RASPUTIN!\nOren's Greatest love machine!\nAnd so they shot him 'till he was dead!\n\nOh, those Oreners...", ""),
        StaticBook("Read me", "Haise", "Dear Nikky: \n\nHey, Wasnt really sure what to get you but i figured Baked Goods are always a good choice, so i picked up some Cookies from Dunshire for you. Enjoy!\n\n- H", ""),
        StaticBook("Reading", "Antanios Rutledge", "Reading for Children\n\n1. Grandma's Puppy\nVocab: Care, For, After\n\n  I take care of the puppy with my grandma. Grandma shows me how to care for the puppy.\n  I play with the puppy inside. After we play, we take a nap!\n\n  Z-Z-Z.\nCopy the Words\n 1) Care    ______\n 2) For     _____\n 3) After   _______\n\nCombine the Words\n 1)§  Grand+ma\n     \n   § §   _________\n\n 2) In+Side\n\n     _________\n2. The Festival\nVocab: Candy, Mother, Brother\n\n  My mother gave my brother and me a few pieces of candy.\n My brother thanked mother, and we gave her a hug.\n We went outside and shared our candy.\n\n     Yummy!\nCopy the Words\n 1) Candy   _______\n 2) Mother  _______\n 3) Brother ________ \n\nCombine the Words\n 1) Out+side\n  \n    _________\n \n 2) Thank+ed\n\n    __________\nTongue Twisters\n1. A Job for Bob\n\n  Bob needs a job.\n There is a job for Bob. Rob can use Bob on his farm. Bob can pick corn on the cob.\n\n  Rob and Bob each pick the cobs. Bob likes his job with Rob.\nTongue Twisters\n2. Fun in the Sun\n\n  I like to have fun.\n I have fun in the sun. I like to run in the sun. I run in the sun for fun. I see them have fun in the sun.\n\n  We all like to run, so we all have fun.\nReading for Children #2\n1. I Have Been . . .\nVocab: Flowers, Clinic, School\n\n I have been visiting grandma at the clinic after school everyday. Grandma hurt her right leg, so I brought flowers to grandma at the clinic.\nCopy the Words\n 1) Flowers  ________  2) Clinic    _______\n 3) School   _______\n\nCombine the Words\n 1) Every+day\n\n    ___________\n\n 2) Visit+ing\n\n    __________\n2. The Day I Tried. . .\nVocab: Silly, Favourite, Laugh\n\n Mother is a great cook. My favourite food is baked chicken. She says that 'Love makes it taste good'. It sounds silly, but it's true. Mom decorates the dish, it makes me laugh.\nCopy the Words\n 1) Silly  ______\n 2) Laugh ______\n 3) Favourite ______ \n\nCombine the Words\n 1) Chick+en\n\n    _________\n\n 2) Co+ok\n\n    _______\nTongue Twisters #2\n1. Ten Hens in a Pen\n\n  The men have some hens in a pen. See them go running from the men in the pen.\n  The men count the hens, the number of hens in the pen is ten.\n\nThey have ten hens.\nTongue Twisters #2\n2. The Snow Blows\n\n  In the winter, there is snow. The snow blows hard outside. The river does not flow, it turns to snow above and ice below.\nA girl plays out in the snow, she has a hat and a pretty bow.", ""),
        StaticBook("Rebirth of Evil", "Lilyana", "The Rebirth of Evil\n\n          By\n\n        Lilyana\nShe awoke in dire pain and confusion as the livelihood of the Crimson Fist’s purpose and existence, literally, weighed heavily upon her. The Champion’s mind sporadically showed images of a battle that just collapsed the temple containing most, if not all,\nof the Sanguine Hand, sending them to an early demise. Shouts meant to be full of victory turned into blood curdling screams of pain and death as they were overrun by their attackers. As she clawed at the gravel and dirt that trapped her, she tried\nlistening to her surroundings for other survivors calling out to her. But all her ears could hear were the memories of the stone walls around her cracking, sliding, grinding against one another, as they began to collapse inward on her and the others, and\ntheir screams. Oh how the memory of the screams tortured her mind, forcing her bloody and gashed hands to sift quicker. Her hands digging and sifting faster, trying to escape the memory,  but the images and sounds only seemed to come faster as she tried\nto flee, keeping in tempo with her movement. \n\nWith a heavy grunt and thrust, she thrusts her arm through a small lit-opening, finally feeling the cool air touch her skin.  This bolstered her will, giving her the strength to push herself through the\nsmall opening and back into the outside world. The elven woman lay there in the cool morning fog for what seemed like an eternity,  time completely lost to her, breathing in deeply the fresh air.  Slowly, from the dense fog a shadowy figure approaches her\nexhausted self and shoves a bow and arrow into her face. Panting, the woman looks up at the figure as he pulls back his hood, revealing the rugged features of a hunter. The man pulled back the weapon slightly from her face and asked her for her name.\n“M-my name…”, the elven woman spoke between her labored breaths, “ My name is Cora.”\n\nSeeing Cora’s condition and state, the hunter took pity on her that fateful morning and led her to his dwelling in the forest.  There, he fed and dressed her wounds,\nnursing her back to health. Cora slowly came around to the man, knowing all too well how easily it is to lower ones guard when they begin to trust someone, but never spoke about the Crimson Fist. When he did question her about her past, she simply said\nthat she was a servant to the people that owned the, now, pile of rubble that he found her at. The man nodded, knowing it rude to question a person’s past, and went about his business. However, no matter how hard he tried to focus on cleaning his\nmorning’s kill or divert his gaze, he was mesmerized by Cora’s beauty and soon felt for her. Cora, knowing that the Crimson Hand’s was either utterly destroyed or scattered to the winds and that her previous life was too dangerous to try to start again\non her own, accepted the hunter’s affection with open arms and soon gave birth to a child of a rare complexion. The child’s skin was pale like snow, his hair like fine straws of white gold, and his eyes….crimson like blood. Because of his defining eyes,\nCora named him, Haemon, the Blood Child. \n\nHaemon’s features were the most exciting thing of his life as he lived a dull life in the forest. His father taught him how to string a bow, to catch a fish, to chop wood, and skin a kill. He promised to take\nhim hunting when he was rightfully a man and left Haemon in charge of keeping order at home when he left on his numerous hunting trips. Cora took to motherhood surprisingly well. Her swift and accurate hands that once sliced a man’s throat before they\ncould blink now directed a needle and thread through cloth; her strength and determination that kept herself alive during fights with armed guards now carried in loads of firewood or cleaned the wash. She watched over Haemon throughout the years grow into\na fine young man, but also watched herself age. She knew that with her death, the Crimson Fist died as well, as did its unfinished work. So, as her husband left on one of his hunting trips, Cora brought Haemon into the cellar of their small home.\nThere, she had him swear to keep this information from his father, and showed him the history of her people, of his people. Haemon was fascinated by the information, rituals, chants, and stories his mother knew and begged to know all of it.\nSo, every time her husband would venture out into the woods, Cora would teach Haemon the ways of the Crimson Fist.\n\nThis continued for many years until the night before Haemon’s eighteenth birthday, when everything changed.\nThe hunter returned home earlier than expected, bringing with him a new bow to give to Haemon as a gift to use on their first hunt together. However, when he approached the home, all he could see was darkness through the windows. He quickly entered\nthe home, noticing that the fire and candles had been empty and snuffed for quite some time. The darkness however, did allow the light from the under the cellar door to draw his attention. He opened the door quietly, filling the room with light,\nand was met by the voices of his family, however could not make out what they were saying. Descending the staircase he saw his wife and son, dancing while around an open fire. An animal’s carcass and bloodied knife lay next to the flame and\nits blood was painted on their naked skin in weird designs and letters that he could not understand. Haemon was the first to notice his father’s presence, quickly dropping his hands arms, breaking the dance, and backing away from the cellar door.\nCora noticed the Haemon’s fear and quickly turned, meeting the horrified gaze of her husband. He, softly, began to question Cora and Haemon, but neither responded, both afraid to unveil the lies they have been keeping from him. The hunter became angry,\nhis voice raising as he stepped down the stairs, approaching his wife. Cora remained speechless, not knowing what to say or do, she simply looked at the floor. In a fit of tears and rage the man grabbed Cora’s arms and forced her against the wall,\nshouting at her, begging to her, for answers. Haemon watched in horror and fear as his father slammed his mother against the wall across the room, shouting at her, asking her questions, spewing lines of secrets, lies, and betrayal. But it was only Haemon\nthat noticed the fire in the center of the room grow larger and only Haemon that heard the flame telling him to stop his father. Haemon tried to cover his ears to escape the raspy voice but the flame’s voiceresonated inside of him, demanding Haemon to\ntake action.\n\nHaemon closed his eyes and screamed out, trying to smother the flame’s voice with his own, but when he stopped screaming, all was quiet. Haemon opened his eyes to see his hand firmly around the bloodied knife that had sat in the\ncenter of the room, and the knife he held was deeply embedded into his father’s back. His father twisted around to look at Haemon’s eyes as he desperately tried to reach for the knife in his back. Blood began to leak from his mouth as he tried mouthing\nwords, words that Haemon would never hear. His father fell towards the center of the room, his head cracking on the hard stone floor, blood leaking out of his body towards the fire. Haemon backed away from his mother who now shriveled into herself against\nthe wall, staring at her dead husband, at the pool of blood forming around his body.\n\nThe blood of the innocent man pooled and grew, eventually reaching the fiery claws of the flame. With an immense heat and power, the flame jumped high and turned\ncrimson, sparks flew from it in all directions. Haemon now stared at the fire, mesmerized by the dancing of its flames and heard the voice that spoke to him earlier, this time much clearer. He could not disobey it if he tried, the pull it had on his very\nbeing was too strong, so he walked into the flame. Cora tried to reach out to her son, but her body was frozen, whether in fear or by the flames own power she did not know, but when she called to him nothing escaped her throat. Haemon did not feel\nthe flame burn his skin, but felt it burn his insides, as if it had reached into his heart and soul and burnt them to ash. He could not scream out nor did his body react to the pain that his mind was feeling. His vision slowly became dark and blurred, his\nsense of feeling seemed to numb away, and his mind began to close in on itself.\n\nWhen Cora woke the next morning in her bed she quickly wretched onto the floor. The nightmare was so real to her, the heat of the fire, the smell\nof her husband’s blood, the image of her son walking into the fire, all shook her deeply.  She struggled out of bed and walked down to the kitchen, finding it cold and dark as it was every morning. She started a fire and hung a pot of water to boil while\nshe called out to Haemon to wake. However, he did not return her call. When she checked his bed, he found it vacant and undisturbed from the previous morning’s making. Fear struck at her as she turned to look at the closed cellar door. Slowly approaching\nit and wrapping her hand around the latch, she closed her eyes as she opened it and was greeted by nothing but the smell of burnt flesh. At the bottom of the staircase she could see her husband’s burnt skeleton in the same spot it was\nleft in her nightmare. She cried out and slammed the cellar shut and turned to run from the house, only to see a figure standing in the doorway, shadowed from the sun coming in around the figure. Its glowing, deep crimson eyes\nwere its only distinguishable characteristic.\n \nThe figure spoke to her with two voices, both familiar but from different lives.\n \n“Hello, Mother”", ""),
        StaticBook("Recipes", "Davin Lodmund", "Tea's and their Benefits\nBy Unknown\n*Words are etched here*\nTea is meant to be served warm, with friends!\nIndex:\nHow to Brew\nEquiptment\nTea's and their effects\nAuthor's Note\nHOW TO BREW\nFirst one must take their kettle, usually a black one and fill it with water. Do not fill this with anything besides water, as it will skew the taste.\nIt will scream at you when it is ready. Take it off the fire. Thirdly you must then get the leaves and fill the pot. Fourth let it steep for a while until the flavor has taken ahold of the water. Serve in cups while warm!\nEquiptment\nTeapot\nCups\nTeabags\nSugar\nHoney\nSpoon\nTypes of Tea\nLemon Grass\nThis helps digest food, serve shortly after dinner.\nGreen Tea\nThe wonder tea! Helps with immune systems, tooth decay, and sickness.\nGinger Tea\nHelps with nausea, and arthritis.\nPeppermint Tea\nHelps sooth, as well as helps control nausea, vomiting, and motion sickness. Helps also with mild coughs, asthma, congestion, Aches\nChamomile Tea\nThe tea to help one sleep, take before bed for best results.\nRose Hip Tea\nHelps with complexion, adrenaline, and your immune system.\nLavander Tea\nHelps respiratory issues, cough, asthma, and body temperature from fever. Helps heal ulcers, sores, cuts, and wounds.\nHibiscus Flower Tea\nHelps with hypertension, and high blood pressure. Drink when you have a stressful job.\nMilk Thistle Tea\nHelps clean ones liver, and improve liver function. Drink this you drunkards!\nDandelion Tea\nHelps with arthristis, liver function, fluid retention, and soothing pain.\nHawthorn Tea\nHelps with blood circulation, and reduce stress.\nCinnamon Tea\nStrengthens body, fights viruses, Good with honey\nRed Clover Tea\nHelps with stress, and gives a peaceful sleep. Strengthens bones as well as improves memory.\nNettle Tea\nHelps with high blood pressure, rheumatism, arthritis, immune systems, colds and congestion\nAuthors Note\nTea is meant to be enjoyed, drink often as I have and you will enjoy a nice quiet life. There are plenty of plants I have forgotten so feel free to make your own tea books as well.\n*A picture of an old elven woman is sketched here, in her hand is a cup of tea*", ""),
        StaticBook("Recovered Letter", "Utaria", "[!] The handwriting is sloppy and many things are misspelled! [!]\n\nDear Morgan, \nYou may think of me as a killer but despote what you think it is not true. I have red your leter over and over and every time I am amased that you think so porly of me, your\nex sun. I have been working relly hard to be a better mali and yet you only want to see the bad in me like evryone else. It fells like evryone just wants me to bee evil and so I fell like I must be evil.  Like it is my job here. \n\nDie.", ""),
