        StaticBook("Testimony", "Dork", "The events occurred at Khel's Enchantry & Apothecary during the day. The people who were there are as follows; Elenore Ruric, Khel, Opal, and Reivyr. We were all talking when suddenly a pink must surrounded Elenore's form, not being apparent where it came\nfrom. This is where Opal began to approach Mr Khel. Only mere seconds after Opal began to approach Khel is when Elenore's clothing was visually modified to resemble that of a 'french maid outfit'. The new apparel was only seen for a few seconds before\nMiss Opal tugged on Khel's ear rather harshly, causing him to assumably lose connection and for the illusion to disappear.", ""),
        StaticBook("Thahnium's Bane", "Khaine", "Looking into Thahnium and its effect of the Imperial capital\n- Khaine Alvus\nIn 1596, the final collapse of the Orenian empire came when the sovereign triggered a thahnium blast which annihilated the capital city itself and wide area of housing, vegetation and plains in the surrounding area. This effectively served as an outwardly\nidentical effect to the state of land which possesses the mineral form of thahnium in its geology; that of a frozen, snowy and polar landscape, though due to the lack of the material's mineral form, the corruption is definitely not permanent.\nWhile druidic blight healing initially was not able to heal the frost-stricken land, I believed that somehow removing the corrupted shards, at least from the extremities of the corruption, would serve to destroy it. The means to do so, however, served as\na huge headache.\nAs is already known, regular flame has little effect on thahnium, being almost entirely neutralised by the magical properties of the mineral and the 'corruption' it causes. This leads to an issue as a generally fantastic way to destroy a tainted area is\nsimply to obliterate it with fire and then have it regrow from the disturbance through successional processes where natural vegetation returns to the area. However due to the antithetical properties of thahnium, this is rendered impossible with normal\nflame, which still plays a role when the thahnium is removed through other means.\n\nMore luck was found when using varieties of flame originating from magical beings such as dragonkin. As one might imagine however, acquiring a dragon is difficult so a\nsubstitute was found - an Azdrazi, draconic humanoids who had the unique ability to breathe fire, granted to them likely by a higher being. This type of flame DID have an effect on the outer areas of corruption, being able to burn down several tainted\ntrees in the vicinity of the Imperial capital's remnant, however the land remained corrupted despite the best efforts of the Azdrazi present. This 'magical flame' theory might be further tested with the use of a more powerful dragonkin such as a dragon,\ndrake, forktail, wyvern, dragaar or drakaar. However, for obvious reasons this would likely be extremely difficult.\n\nControlling dragons is hardly an easy task, after all. To whoever might read this, I recommend attempting to somehow have a larger\ndragonkin blast thahnium shards with their flame in order to cleanse them. This may bear fruit and be able to clean huge swathes of land in a quick period. However, I believe a more practical method is rather more mundane, related to thahnium's mana\nrelated properties.\nIdentically to many other types of magical being and object, thahnium shards appear to have a 'capacity' of sorts, for mana itself. These sources of the corruption are no different. IF the shards are overloaded with enough magical strength,\nthen I have been informed that the shards will burst and the corruption around the area may lose its magical properties and be vulnerable to cleansing by other means. A method specified to me in particular was the use of staves imbued with the mana of an\nincredibly powerful enchanter or enchantress which can be wielded by any individual with the right knowledge. This object would concentrate a large burst of mana and channel it into the shard, hopefully destroying it. Repeated, this would be able to\ncleanse an entire area of thahnium taint, leaving it ready to be cared for and regrown as the aspects intend.\n-      Conclusion     -\n\nThis book was written as a secondary measure after my enchanter contact mysterious disappeared, leaving me with only the knowledge I have penned here. Perhaps other enchanters might be able to\ncraft these staves. Perhaps others might use dragonfire to purge the area around the Imperial Capital.\n\n- KA", ""),
        StaticBook("Thania Dossier 1", "Quavinir", "Thania Dossier\n\nThe following script is penned upon the request of Queen Renn to be delivered to Praetor Sylvaeri. The following is a description of the known, and troublesome denizens of the small mountain\ntown known as Thania-\nto the knowledge of the author, Quavinir Tinuvial. The author of this text is unable to lie without a clear, noticable, and prolonged sign of having lied, and such a prolonged sign may likewise be triggered if a lie has been made in writing, so let the-\nreader of this dossier infer that all the recorded events and pieces of knowledge are made to the faithful knowledge of Quavinir, with no embellishments, exaggerations, or untruths, with any uncertainties listed as such.\nPeople:\nGaroll: Page 5-10\nCaesar: Page 11-18\nRhillen: Page 19-24\nLoras: Page 25-30\nNilth: Page 31-36\nTelos: Page 36-39\nEhier: Page 40-43\nKailu: Page 44-50\nDargo: Page 51-53\nCoCo: Page 54-56\nGaroll\n===================Garoll could be listed as the de-facto leader of the Thania group, if they were to bear one. He is the de-facto head of the town of Thania itself as to the current knowledge of the author, and seems to garner\ngenuine respect from the rest of the Thania group.\n\nGaroll is a confirmed cannibal, both from claims made by himself, and the claims of others to the author. If he still partakes of such a habit, or if he has stopped, such is not known to the author-\n(though the author is inclined to believe he has quit the habit, and not returned to such, due to no recent reports of such.).\n\nGaroll researched Thanium, and noew researches ruibrium (to the knowledge of the author at the time of writing) Garoll studied-\nThanium in Axios in the town known as Mordskov, and has claimed person responsibility for the awakening of the anomaly in Mordskov, and the subsequent destruction of the Isle of Tahn at the hands of the anomaly, though he claims such was unintional.\nGaroll is a dark elf at around 6 feet tall, he standardly wears a red or blue coat, and bears a runic prostetic arm, prosthetic leg, and prosthetic eyes. He has white hair, and many times carries 2 knives at the end of a chain as a weapon. He is a void-\nmage, and a master of water evocation.\nCaesar\n===================Caesar Curseus (Also known as Red, Epsilon, or 'Caesar Hallowfall') is Garoll's apprentice, and lover/fiance (as to the knowledge of the author at the time of writing.) \n\nCaesar has claimed to the author numerous times-\nthat he has murdered children. The initial claim was that he killed, gutted, and displayed the bodies of his wife and 2 children in Thania, this claim was confirmed by Garoll, and 2 others at the time, confirming both the presence and condition of the-\nbodies, and Caesar, covered in blood, that this was his doing. Caesar maintained for roughly 13 years, before claiming he was brainwashed by an ex-boyfriend of his named Favnir to thinking he committed the crimes, though he never provided details of such.\nShortly there-after he made the claim he was brainwashed, according to Caesar, and the halfling known as Hiro'deril, Caesar tortured Hiro, and tortured and murdered Hiro's young children. Upon further prying, Caesar confirmed such was done as payback-\nagainst D'eril for crimes D'eril committed against Caesar, and the Thania group. Caesar has yet to deny these claims, or provide an alternative explaination to the author of this text.\n\nCaesar is banished from Sutica, the reasoning from the-\ncrown is as follows:\n\"Taking the life of several Suticans in the past slandering the crown, attempted assassination before his banishment, conspiring with Sutican enemies, disruption of peace, and threatening the life of a halfling on several occassions.\"\n(The halfling I believe myself to be Hiro D'eril, though at the time of writing this such a suspicion or assumption has not been confirmed nor denied.)\n\nCaesar is a mali'ame at the height of 6'3, he has deep red hair, commonly wears glasses, and-\nbears 2 prosthetic arms, one being runic in nature, whilst the other is made of a rare alloy known as Starbronze. He commonly wears a grey coat, and has blue eyes.\nRhillen\n===================Rhillen is a mali'ame, and was for a time Garoll's bodyguard. Rhillen is a wood elf with ties the the Snow elves of Fenn, and is currently banished from the Dominion for his part in the kidnapping of Khain's wife-\nat swordpoint. \n\nRhillen is erratic, and it is difficult to lend any consistancy to his crimes. He has tried to attack me, and a student of mine many times, and I bear conflicting reports of his actions both from others, and the Thania group themselves.\nI have heard claims that he has tortured and killed members of the Thania group, but than have heard from members of the THania group that such are baseless, and lies, leaving his only 100% for certain crime being the kidnapping of Khaine's wife, and -\naiding the snow elves in raids against Caras Eldar. He was a member of the Ivae'Fenn for a number of years, than left, and years later joined the Holm brigade.\n\nRhillen is a wood elf with deep red hair, and blue eyes. He looks remarkably-\nsimilar to Caesar, and it is somewhat surprising that the two are not related. Rhillen's height has... fluctuated due to unknown means, as I, the author, have observed him at 6 feet tall, 7 feet tall, 8 feet tall, 6 feet again, than back to 8 feet tall,-\nthan finally down to roughly 6 and a half feet tall, and it is unknown  to the author if Rhillen's height has fluctuated from in the time since the last time he has seen Rhillen.\nHe does not practive any voidal arts to the author's knowledge.\nLoras\n===================Loras is a somewhat odd addition to the Thania group, and his place among them is unknown to the author, and it is currently unknown to the author if he still lives in Thania, or keeps in contact with the rest of-\ngroup. What is known to the author was that Loras at one time was a member of the Thania group, and bore a house in the mountain town of Thania. Loras was part of a multi-religeon dark cult, in service of dark beings, including that of the daemon Ibless,-\nthough after a time chose to betray the group, due to guilt of past actions. Loras has assaulted, and killed numerous people, and later even kidnapped those living in Caras Eldar to sacrifice to the September prince, so it is unlikely his change of heart-\nfrom his previous membership in the cult was permanant. The author of this text learned of Loras' actions from Loras himself confessing them tot he author in a fit of guilt, alongside a dossier of all the cult members, their level of danger, and their-\nplace in the cult. (which upon request, the author can provide.)\n\nLoras is pale skinned, and bears deep crimson hair, and blue eyes, though his eyes have been observed by the author to at times be a deep red, or briefly during the-\ntime of the purple trees, to be purple. Loras many times wears beads in his hair, and his wardrobe is varied, with various robes. Loras is skilled in the voidal arts, and can practice illussion, and enchanting magic.\nNilth\n===================Nilth is another student of Garoll, and possibly others of the Thania group. The author of this text knows exceptionally little of Nilth, and upon the recent (at the time of the writing of this text) revelation that -\nNilth worked with Loras to sacrifice Caras Eldari citizens to the September Prince, the author had assumed Nilth was simply a benign tagalong with the Thania group. Nilth, as seen through observations of the author, bears a relatively friendly -\nrelationship with most of the Thania Group, and is one of the more polite of the group. Nilth is known to use an illusory disguise when convenient, though his illussions tent to simply match a slightly altered, or idealized version of himself.\nNilth is a high elf with yellow blond hair, pale skin, and blue eyes. He bears a white metal prosthetic hand, and commonly wears a brown coat with gold trim. It is observed by the author of Nilth mentioning he knows water evocation, and other magics, but-\nwhat other magics, or who taught them to Nilth is unknown to the author at the time of the writing of this text.\n\n§\nTelos\n===================Telos is a former voidal horror, and a former member of Loras dark cult, according to Loras' dossier. Telos' place in the Thania group is unknown to the author as of writing this document, though he listens to-\nrequests and commands from Caesar quite eagerly. \n\nTelos' crimes specifically are unknown to the author at this time. Telos as both Telos, and Ichmrz have been mentioned ot the author as the source of various killings, though-\nthe author at this time lacks any specifics. Telos though has been observed to use mental magics to forcefully learn information from people, and commonly travels wearing a grey mask.\nTelos is a high elf with yellow eyes, and white hair. He commonly dresses in robes, though most commonly wears grey or black robes. Telos is a master of many voidal arts, notably mental magics.\nEhier\n===================Ehier, (also known as Ehier Evocress, or Ehier Hallowfall) is one of Garoll's close caretakers, he is notably violent, attacking both friends and enemies alike, and is very impulsive and elusive. Ehier has attacked the\nauthor of this text multiple times, though he tends to downgrade things commonly, taking attempts at someone's life as meer joking, or threatening, even if it involves genuinely attemping to strangle someone. \n\nEhier has notably attacked the author-\n, students of the author, Garoll, Caesar, and Blossom/Kailu (next member on the dossier), he is exceptionally violent and erratic. Ehier was formerly on the banishment list as a kill-on-sight, though was not transfered over to the new banishment list,-\nassumedly due to lack of proper sketch or information aside from a name. \n\nEhier is a high elf with white hair, and heterochromatic eyes. One blue, and one grey. He is a user of electrical evocation, though does not seem very experienced in such,\nKailu\n===================Kailu is a long standing member of the Thania group, though he has been banished, and re-accepted to the Thania group in the past. He is a close friend to Garoll, and partner in study with him. Kailu also goes by Blossom\nKailu's most notable crime is the torture, and murder of his 2 children. aged 7 and 9. Initially, Kailu claimed that his 9 year old tried to kill his 7 year old, and put the latter into a comatose state, though I have been told otherwise by a student of-\nmine. My student informed me that Kailu infact had been testing on both his 7, and 9 year old with science experiments pertaining to Thanium, testing Thanium on his 7 year old and forcing him into a comatose state. This state eventually killed his 7 year-\nold. In disappointment, Kailu took it out on his 9 year old, and slit his throat.\nKailu after this incident attacked his fellow denizens of Thania, though eventually regained their trust after he committed suicide with a thanium bomb agianst Ethel Serene.\nHow Kailu managed to survive, or be revived after such is unknown to the author, and the author himself finds difficulty accepting these claims as fact, despite being told by 2 separate sources.\n\nKailu is a peach skined high elf with blonde hair,-\nwith white highlights. He has heterochromatic eyes with the two being varying shades of green. His clothing varies madly, and bears no consistant basis. It is unknown to the author if Kailu knows any voidal arts, though due to his close relationship with-\nGaroll, it is an assumption of the author that he does.", ""),
        StaticBook("Thania Dossier 2", "Quavinir", "Dargo\n===================Dargo is a black kharajyr, and a new member to the THania group. He is an eccentric tag along that imposes himself into the group. It is unknown to the author how tolerated, or not tolerated he is in the group.\nDargo is young and eccentric, and imposes himself as the leader of the group, which he dubs the 'Dargo Force', though such is standardly responded to with annoyance, or dismissal from memebers of the THania group. Dargo claims he knows many magics, though\nhe has never demonstrated said abilities in sight of the author.\n\nDargo is a black kharajyr, that standardly carries a large walking stick, wears a purple robe and hat, and is somewhat short at the time of writing.\nCoCo\n===================CoCo is a elven homunculus created by Jhazeem, CoCo is a somewhat docile homunculus, though he bears no soul, as is standard for most corpse based homunculi. Coco has committed no crimes to the understanding-\nof the author (Who himself is a homunculus, though with a soul), though due to CoCo's lack of soul, the author is extremely leery in branding CoCo with any measure of stability, as homunculus bear no intrinsic value for life, and are exceptionally strong,\nand lack any capability for selflessness, love, or proper understanding, so despite CoCo's docility the author advises extreme caution.\n\nCoCo appears as a pale high elf, with sea green eyes, and white hair. He dresses in neutral colors, and is soft spoken", ""),
        StaticBook("Thank you!", "Alexandra Bradshawe", "A special gift to get you started. Thank you for settling with us!\n\n\n\n~Mayor Alexandra.\n\n[!] The signature would be written in an elaborate cursive, a small, red heart-shape drawn next to her name.", ""),
        StaticBook("The", "Wulflok Grimmrson", "The Origins:\nBefore there was soil, or sky, or any green thing, there was only the gaping void of Gegähneleere. That was the age when nothing was. There was no sand, no sea, nor cool waves. No Earth nor Sky nor Grass there, only Gegähneleere. This\nchaos of perfect silence and darkness lay between the reich of fire, Múspellsheimr, and the reich of Ice Niflheimr. Frost from Niflheimr and flames from Múspellsheimr crept toward each other until they met in Gegähneleere. Amid the hissing and storming,\nthe fire melted the ice and the from the fog and water was born Stürmthr, the first of the Urunbändig, the great chaos ones. Stürmthr in his sleep dreamt the world barren, covered in stone and sallowed earth and in his sleep he struck the two, Niflheimr\nand Múspellsheimr, from it was born the world he dreamed. Awaking to this new land Stürmthr awoke pleased and so the next night he dreamt the world was green and plentiful of crop and shrub. He awoke enraged and from the void he struck the world with\nlightning and from it was born Gäa, the Earth Mother, and second of the Urunbändig. The Children of Stürmthr and Gäe were Njorthr, Sól, Máni, and Ükko. From Sól's happiness was born Dag who Illuminated the world from darkness. From\nMáni's sadness was born Yö who shines in the dark when Dag grows weary. It was Ükko and Stürmthr who in there rage for eachother created the sky which they eternally fight over in the storms they make. Njorthr seeing his brother and father fight flooded\nthe world with his tears, taking up all the low lands with water. With the land that remained Gäe brought forth nature and life. From her blood was born Man and Women. From her tears would be born the animals of the world. From her lying with her son\nNjorthr would the fish of the sea be born. Enraged at Gäe, Stürmthr force Gäe into the Earth and struck his fist upon Njorthr, for which Njorthr cut out his fathers heart and hide it at the bottom of the sea. From The blood of Stürmthr's heart and the\nsalt of the sea was forged the children Jaern, Gull, Diamant, Kull, Smaragdgrün, and Verenki, who would be shattered by Stürmthr's lightning and sink into the Earth.\nThe First Ones:\nFrom the void Gäe looked upon the world with dismay. She given the world nature but the world had none to enjoy it. The Mother came down to the Earth and stood at Stürraseri the great tree born with Gäe in Stürmthr's great rage.\nGäe sliced her palm and bled upon the tree's bark and from it was born Perun and Sif, the first Man and Woman, and to them Gäe gave the world to live in and enjoy.\nBirth of the Flottelys:\nDuring the winter Stürmthr gazed up from the Earth upon his granddaughter Yö amazed at her beauty he granted her the Flottelys, made from his lightning, for her to wear when with her mother, Máni.\nThe Stone Heart:\nWounded from battle with Njorthr, Stürmthr took from the Earth a great stone and placed it in his chest to replace his heart. From that day Stürmthr became cold to his kin and no longer felt compassion nor love for them.\nThe Children of Ükko:\nThe First Ones, Perun and Sif, would bare a daughter by the name Mielikki whom the god  Ükko would marry for her beauty. Believing his wifes beauty would bring him glorious children he impregnated her and from her were born three\nmonsters. Grotesque in looks and twisted in nature. The first born was Snekku, a serpent with great fangs and blind eyes. Ükko cast this child into the sea hoping he would drown but instead he grew great and terrorizes the seas. The second child was\nJoukahainen, a beast with scales and wings with breath of fire, who was banished to the caves of the world to live in darkness. The third and final child was Nyyrikki, the first troll, who was abandoned under a bridge. Unable to bare a good child with his\nwife Ükko cursed Mielikki to be forever stuck within a tree.\nThe Three Sisters:\nThe Urunbändig Sól and Máni were brought together the day Yö stood before Dag and from their passion was born Forsa, Agrä and Fömiggästhi. Forsa would dwell in the woods performing dark magic and creating beast to defend the woods\nfrom mankind. Agrä would come to the men of the world and teach them to raise crops and provided them bountiful fields in return for sacrifices of blood and bone. If she were ever to be wronged or scorned she has been known to bring famine and disease.\nFömiggästhi tamed the fish of the sea and in return for sacrifice of gems she brought to the villages plentiful fishing grounds and if angered would drive them out. It would be \nFömiggästhi who would lay with Snekku and gave life to the Sirens who drown\nmen at sea.\nThe Discovery of \nHäxeriheimr:\nIn the early ages of the world Stürmthr looked upon Gegähneleere and desired to know what lies within the eternal darkness. He set off for twelve years into the void and nearly giving up he found a rip within the darkness.\nStürmthr struck the rift with lightning inciting a explosion of light when Stürmthr awoke ten years later on Earth the runes had been tattooed upon his left arm and he had aquired the knowledge of them. Equipped with the runes he became the mightiest of\nthe Urunbändig. He had learned chants that enabled him to heal emotional and bodily wounds, to bind his enemies and render their weapons worthless, to free himself from constraints, to put out fires, to expose and banish practicers of malevolent magic,\nto protect his allies in battle, to wake the dead, to win and keep a lover, and to perform many other feats like these. Once again Stürmthr set off into the void and found that rift had become a portal to the reich of Häxerheimr where magical essence\npoured out into the void and other reichs. Within Häxerheimr dwelled the four Tuoni who created the runes and gave them their power. When Stürmthr came to them and asked them to teach him how to create new runes they shunned him.  Stürmthr envied the\npower of the Tuoni yet knew conflict was not an answer to his wants. He watched over Tuoni yet could still not create new runes to use but he still bent his will toward the task of coming to know how to craft runes. Stürmthr attempted to prove his\nworthiness to the Tuoni. He returned to Earth and taught the runes to Gäe, his wife, and his children Sól and Máni, who taught the runes to their children. Stürmthr bayed them to only use the runes for good yet he himself only wanted their power for\nhimself. The Tuoni still did not teach Stürmthr their ways for his act of selflishness and sharing of knowledge. In a final attempt to gain the Tuoni's favor Stürmthr hung himself from a branch of the world tree and pierced himself with a spear. He forbad\nany Urunbändig to grant him the slightest aid, not even a sip of water and so he hung. He survived in this state, teetering on the precipice that separates the living from the dead, for no less than forty days until his death. A Tuoni having seen\nStürmthrs suffering came down to the world tree and resurrected him. The Tuoni healed the fallen self sacrificed Urunbändig and teached him the secrets of rune making, a decision the Tuoni would regret as Stürmthr never again shared his knowledge.\nTuonela: \nAfter the cursing of his wife Ükko remarried to Yö had two children,  Tuoni, and his sisterwife, Tuonetar. Tuoni looked upon the world and saw suffering in humanity. Starvation, disease, old age and more yet he did not see any end to it. He came\nto Stürmthr, his great grandfather, for council. Tuoni asked him why must all humanity must suffer eternally and Stürmthr could not give him and answer and so his great grandfather sent him to the Tuoni to ask them. Tuoni went before the Tuoni with his\nwife and asked the wise ones why must humanity suffer eternally and they responded Hel. The Tuoni told him that he must become Hel, the taker of life, and his sister Hela. They gave him two runes and with them he crafted in the void the reich of Tuonela,\na dark and lifeless place, where the dead were in a state of eternal sleep, and with the other he created souls for all living beings. So he took his throne in Tuonela, becoming Hel, and his wife her throne beside him becoming Hela. From their thrones\nthey would ponder the lives of mortals and decide the time of which they were to leave the land of the living and enter Tuonela to rest at peace.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Abjurist", "Gallidron Elindrow", "Wards & Abjuration\n^v^v^v^v^v^v^v^v^v^              a\n         study by\n\n  Gallidron Elindrow\nAbjuration is a facinating branch of voidal magic, and perhaps the most difficult. I say this because the most knowledge is required to be a succesfull abjurist or warder.\nTo cast a mighty evocation, one need only understand the element that will be their\nmedium and the art of evocating. To transmute water into ice one needs to understand the intricasies of the freezing process, to conjur one must know what they wish to make in exact detail before they can begin to even form the creature or item in the\nvoid. But to ward against these things, to abjure them into non-exsistance, one must not only understand how to cast protective magic, but they must also understand in detail the magic they wish stop.\nIt is for this reason that I say, the successful abjurist should be lauded above all other mage kind for they are at once massively powerfull and a dutiful student of all forms of magic. I would admonish any who seek to ward or abjure to learn all they\ncould of magic that they might not be caught unprepared. It would even be prudent to learn what one could of the dark arts, within the bounds of reason and safety, that they are not caught off guard by these most sinister magics.\nAn Abjuration is a more offensive style of protecting one's self or others from magic. Suppose that an enemy mage has cast a fire spell at you and a veritable flood of flame is headed in your direction. Now, you are somewhat knowledgable in the department\nof evocation and so you realize that the spell itself is functioning on the premise of converted energy. Fire is after all just energy moving from one form into another. In this case that energy is the mana of the mage and the form it has taken is shaped\nin the void. There are several ways to go about this, as is the beauty of abjuration (one is only limited by their resevoir of power and their imagination). You could try to disrupt the flow of mana from the mage to the spell, or you could break its\nconnection to the void. All in all, the most effective, fool proof, and easiest way is likely to break the connection to the void. This is called disrupting the mana anchor. The Mana Anchor is the metaphorical place where the spell and the energy for it\nmeet and create its effect. It is also what keeps the spell active in our world and not just a figment of a thought in the void. Knowing these things you craft your abjuration and destory the spell before it gets to you. Assuming of course that you are\nas powerful or more so than the mage who is trying to fry your skin off.\n\nA ward is more deffensive and takes more time to make. They are also potentially more versitile and usefull, this is the cause for the increased time of casting.\nA ward is stationary and is used like a shield against one or various forms of magic. Where as an Abjuration can be cast in the moment, it can only defend from one kind of magic. A ward can be crafted with care and forethought and thus be made to\ncounteract various kinds of magic at once. They can last for a long time, given that they have a steady supply of mana to draw upon. The larger and more intricate the ward, the more energy will be required. A ward that is crafted and placed on an object\nor in a place can be thought of much like an enchantment. In fact many enchantments are wards of one kind or another. These spells require the use of a mana gem, a kind of magical battery, to continue to function after the mage has left, and even then\nthe mana gem will only last for so long.\n\nA working knowledge of the magic to be blocked by the ward is still required to create the spell.\nPower is of tantamount importance. If you are a beginning abjurist, you cannot block the fire ball of a master evocationist. They will simply overwhelm you with the might of their spell. One must be at least equal to their opponent to bring their casting\nto a stand still.\n\nOne does not need to be a master evocationist, or even be able to cast evocation, to create wards or abjurations against it. But you will need at least a working knowledge of the element used.  Of course the more experience you have\nthe better you will fare as an abjurist.\nI hope that this book has been enlightening to you as a reader and that you will put this knowledge to good use.\n\n-Gallidron Elindrow\npublishing date 6th of\nGrand Harvest, 1519\nPlease look for my next study on the Arcane!\n\nLightning and fire and frost, oh my!\n\na study on Evocation", ""),
        StaticBook("The Accident", "Joil Diagak", "The wooden floor was terribly cold. I ran my young, strong hands along the wall. The hole in my chest continued to bleed. The yelling outside only worried me more. My two heroes boarded up the door. They were talking to each other, however my pain drowned\nout their words. The flash of light that followed their muffled chat blinded me. The long blade pierced through them both. Dressed in gray and red, he stood over me. We locked eyes. He wiped his blade on the chair, cleansing the red that once lay upon it.\nHe looked down to the heroine on the floor, and then back up to me. He was shivering. The night was freezing. His foggy breath filled the house. A call from outside beckoned him to return. He stayed silent, eyes still connected with mine.\nWithout breaking the contact, he yelled back to his outside crew. His eyes had lost all color. A single tear rolled down his cheek and neck, dispearing at his top. He looked down at the two on the floor, and looked at me once more. He then left.\nThat was the last I'd ever seen of them. That was when I vowed to make sure that I would never have to witness something like it again. They didn't deserve it, and neither did he. Nobody in the room that day will forget the actions commited.", ""),
