esistance seemed to amuse him, but without much effort he had her pinned to the wall and pounding hard. He leaned in to press a kiss to her lips, mockingly gentle and passionate as he continued to rock her until her peak.\nNameless succumbs to the rhythm of Artimec's thrusting, whimpering against his mouth during her climax. Her legs spasm noticeably and continue to quiver for a while. She grows limp and weak, face blank of emotion.\nHe pulled his shaft out of her slowly, letting the head pop out of her drenched folds as he set her legs back gently on the ground. He brushed at her hair gently and spoke in a low drawl.\n\"You are almost as shallow as you are desperate. It does not add up, considering the amount of whores lined up to be taken by you. It was you who demolished the idea of love for me and nothing can repair that. Why must you reopen wounds such as these?\"\n\"I demolished love for you?\" He asked with a brow raised in bemusement. \"I think you give me more credit than I deserve.\" He shook his palm lightly with a small grunt. \"I didn't force you into any of you, you know.\"\nThank you for reading this masterpiece that I, Blogus, uncovered in the Druidic Runes. \n\n\nPeace be with you for the rest of your days.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fear", "The Inquisitor", "The September Prince was a druid blessed with unfathomable power. He hated us and our cities with a clarity and depth that he could never explain, and, I suppose, that we would never understand.\nThe old orders tried building relics to contain and ruin him, but as far as I am aware, none of them ever succeeded. He murdered countless, crushing whole cities with a hundred years of trunks.\nHe was ravenous; he could will the gentlest creatures to commit atrocities. I know only that, after a time, he fell out of favor with the glade, and with Lyes.\nSome records suggest that he was growing too strong to control. Aureus himself could not face September directly, he was forced to ask Lyes to intercede -- which, of course, she did.\nLyes cut out a piece of September's brain, banished him from the glade, and scattered him to be lost in the world forever. I have heard stories that he has only grown more powerful and unstable since.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Final Speech", "Pius", "The Emperor rose from his sick bed, he looked over to a scribe.. \"I shall speak to my people, all of my people from every class and sect...\"\n\nThe scribe nodded as he ran out, whispering in the ear of the Imperial Herald. The Emperor's herald commanded the\nGuards to light the beacon of Abresi and to ring the bells of the church. The Guards did so, calling all people of the Empire to the Capital. After a few days, as more and more people came into the city, the crowd outside the Palace grew large. Godfrey\nslowly stepped out onto the balcony looking down at his people, his face shining bright. He looked at their faces, peasants, merchants, craftsmen, nobles, soldiers-- all of Oren mayhaps was there.\n\nHe breathed in before speaking in a loud, booming voice.\n\"Apologize, Apologize O Leader of the Faithful.\n\nApologize for bringing back dignity to a race that became used to humiliation.\n\nApologize because you achieved victory for a nation that became used to defeat.\nApologize O' Godfrey. Apologize for offering three of your sons as martyrs and for not keeping them safe in luxury.\n\nApologize for accomplishing the un-accomplishable. For uniting our land and protecting our honour.\nApologize for achieving unity in Asulon, in two years, by defeating the enemy that whole of mankind sunk so low for generations.\n\nApologize O' Godfrey for not leaving our prisoners in enemy jails. Apologize O' Godfrey for defending our women and children\nfrom races that used to rape and pillage us.\n\nApologize for standing in the face of sedition. Apologize O' Godfrey for never being tolerant of impunity.\n\nApologize. Apologize your Majesty O' Godfrey Of Oren O' Leader of Victory. Apologize for raising\nthe head of Mankind so high.\n\nApologize for Returning the dignity, honor and pride of this race, Apologize O Leader of the Faithful.\"\n\nHe took another deep breath, looking at the people once more. He then spoke again.\n\"You today, do you know who your leaders are and who you are? They are the descendents of Horen, of Edgar, of Owyn, of Daniel, And of Richard, The family of the first Divine, and the sons of the faithful companions of the Divines.\n\nYou are a people who\nhave faith such as no one else on the face of this land. And you who has chosen open warfare against this people that pride themselves on their history, civilization and culture and possess the material resources and the capacity, the expertise, the\nknowledge, the coolness, the initiative, the determination, the steadfastness and the bravery. You shall never succeed, our people have become one that cannot be disregarded, one that cannot be defeated, one that shall never kneel to foreign race\nor creed.\n\nYou have become the beacon of civilization, learning, commerce and host a mighty army that can not be defeated. Races do not so easily demand of us nor do they pillage, rape, kill and destroy us. No, no more, for we are united and when we are\nunited and our faith in the one true GOD is strong, we are INVINCIBLE!\n\nFor what you are today, I shall never apologize!\n\nBut today my task here is over. The Creator is calling me to his side soon. The Angels shall come and take me to him\nto sit by his throne and watch over you. My will shall be will here with you. My light shall be within your souls, and one day, mayhaps the Almighty in his wisdom might allow me to come back and guide you once more.\n\nBut now he has given another task to\nthe one that is named after the first Divine, my son and heir, for he shall lead on and he shall make strong what I have laid foundation to. What you were to me you are now to him. Farewell, my people.\"\n\nHe smiled down at them before walking back into\nthe palace, the curtains of the balcony closing behind him.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Final Words", "Frederick Kelly", "The Death List -\nIn case of a scenario where the man who holds this is compromised, the names are listed should be purged and executed under the command of the Unseen Codex, Anathema.\n\n- Paul Kelly of Varendoz\nRaymond Aep Rhysten\nVincent Aep Rhysten\nRaide Ashford\nLeopold De Anjou\nClaus De Anjou\nKlara Amsel\nSascha van der Linden\nRhys Briarwood\nMarja Javsku\n\nThese names are of people who shall be executed under the Atlasian movement.\nThe use of a golden or slayersteel bolt to the cranium shall suffice to execute the said beings. Ensure to store the corpse somewhere isolated to ensure no attempts of revival are made. \n\nDo not engage with vigor, use surprise to overcome the adversaries.\nThe Rhysten Brothers are located within the 'Rhysten Smithy' within Carolstadt. Leopold De Anjou and Raide Ashford are in circulation near Sutica. Sascha van der Linden is missing, presumed located within the continent of Aeldin.\nRest of information can be extracted from Raymond Aep Rhysten. Torture implements lined with silver and gold will ensure best results. Clasps with gold inlaid will ensure constant pain and struggle.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Frost Witch", "Gallidron Elindrow", "An Encounter with Frost Witches\n\nby Gallidron Elindrow\n\n\nRevised edition\nI first learned about the dreaded creatures, known as frost witches, from one of the tomes in the libraries of old Haelunor. I remember the fear that gripped me as a child when I learned of their macabre ways.\nThough as an adult of more mature understanding and greater constitution, I revisited the subject of “monsters” and relearned the available details of the frost witch. They are exclusively women so far as any adventurer who has survived an encounter\nwith them can tell.\n\nThey are horrid to look upon in their natural state. Grey skinned with eyes like ice, but it is not so easy to spot one of these slippery creatures for an ice witch is a master of disguise.\nThey employ illusion to mask their true selves, that they may, with more subtlety, intrude upon our societies and seek out their prey.\n\nIn fact, as the story goes, a frost witch will adopt the guise of a young woman and sit, crying, in the midst of\nsnowy glade. This is done to attract young and hapless men. The clever frost witch will then transform into her hideous self and dispatch the unwitting male then and there, or she will lure him back to her coven to become a grisly meal for her sisters.\nThey are, without exception, powerful magic users, though the older ones are more dangerous and adept. In fact, every frost witch draws her power from a “Witch Mother” who is the head of her particular coven. Like unto a queen bee, she will build her nest\nand gather workers who rely upon her, and she them to some extent.\n\nWhen another frost witch is of sufficient power and experience, she may set out to create her own coven. They begin by searching for women who are depressed or saddened.\nThe frost witch will then “mark” the woman with a curse. Should she succumb to her sorrow she will become a frost witch herself, and thus do their numbers swell.\nIt is reportedly a favorite tactic of the frost witches to seek out a married man\nand devour him, then they will curse his grieving widow. In this fashion do they gain both a meal and a prospective member of their coven.\nNot much is known about the curse, and there is no known way to remove it. It has been said, however,\nthat if the woman resists her sadness and sorrow that she may endure the curse and not become on of these fiends. Though she will likely live with the curse for the rest of her days.\nIn order to destroy a frost witch coven one must seek out and destroy the witch mother. In some cases this is enough to cause the coven to wither and die. In others, however, if a witch who is powerful enough survives, she may assume the role\nof witch mother and allow the coven to limp on. In any case, the most foolproof method of destroying a coven is just that, destroy the coven. All of it.\nIf one seeks to harm a frost witch I would give them this advice. Strike fast and strike true for you shall not likely receive a second chance. Also, a sellsword of types once told me that gold is good for killing all kinds of unnatural monsters,\nperhaps it applies here as well, though I do not know for certain.\nIt is important to note that  a frost witch is not a rabid animal, and they can be reasoned with. They are also possessed of terrible cunning and one should not expect the blind fury of mindless monster when dealing with them.\nIt is possible to treat with them and in fact they could exist within your own city, your very neighborhood and most would be unaware. They humor of a frost witch is quite changeable and every moment you stand in their presence you are in grave danger.\nThe truth is that they are fickle creatures, and there is no telling what a frost witch might do.\nIt is said that if one finds a frost witch in disguise and calls them on it that the witch will be bound by her curse to do the clever mortal one favor. Though this is only rumor and would prove both difficult and dangerous to study.\nIn closing, frost witches are a dangerous fascination and one should not seek them lightly. They are elusive and hide among the peoples of the world, it is for this reason that we must be ever watchful lest we become their next meal.\nI hope that this book has been useful to you, the reader. And that this information will help you, should you ever have….\n\nAn encounter, with frost witches.\nBy Gallidron Elindrow\n\nPublishing date 8th of Deep Cold, 1516\n\nRevised 18th of Amber Cold, 1520", ""),
        StaticBook("The Golden Cube", "Almisael", "It seems as though Haense has helped the Vaeyls get their hands on a old dwarven artefact that permits them to control the steel titans. \n\nIt may very well be that Haense has doomed mankind.\nThere is an intriguing stone gate inside the wonkavillage, the elder sits infront of it and looks at it all day long. \nI have examined it and i am sure there are dwarven runes inscribed on it. I wonder what could be behind it.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Golden Star", "Arnorian Elendil", "The Knights of\n           The\n     Silver Shields\n\n\n\n            By\n        Arnorian\n         Elendil\nA Knight there was, and that a worthy man, That from the time he first began,\nTo Riden out. . .\nA Knight must prove\n          Always\n\nTo be true.\nTo be brave.\nTo be kind.\nTo love his land.\nTo be a gentleman.\nTo fight for what is just and right.\nTo do no wrong of which he must be ashamed.\nThere once was a great castle deep in the woods. The castle had big thick walls, a high gate and towers that were bigger than the tallest trees. The old woods that spread around it was dark and dangerous, and many fierce giants lived in it.\n\nIn the castle\nwas a group of knights who were kept there by the King of the country. It was there job to help travelers who might be in the woods, and to make war on the giants whenever they could.\n\nEach of the knights in the castle carried a magic shield. These\nshields were not like those of other knights, but had been made by a great magician who had lived in the castle many years before. The shields were made of silver, and when a knight was brave and good, his shield shone beautifully in the sun.\nWhen a knight was first given his shield, it was dark and plain in colour. Then, as he showed himself to be brave and kind, the shield began to sparkle until he could see his face in it as if the shield were a mirror. However, if a knight were lazy and\nafraid, the shield grew so dark that he became ashamed to carry it. \n\nBut this was not all. When any knight was a very fine man and did something very brave, a golden star appeared in the middle of his shield. This was the greatest thing\nthat could happen to any man. At the time this story begins, only the captain of the castle had a gold star on his shield. The stars were very difficult, indeed, to win.\n\nNow there came a time when the worst of the giants gathered in the woods to make war\non the knights. They made a camp not far away, and killed anyone who traveled along the road.\n\nThe captain told his men that on the next day he would lead them agaisnt the giants. When they heard the news, the knights were very pleased.\nHere, perhaps, was a chance for them to earn a gold star for their shields.\n\nAmong the men in the castle was a new knight called Sir Roland. He was a fine soldier, and already his silver shield showed he was brave and strong. Sir Roland was looking\nforward to meeting the ugly giants. He promised himself that he would do his best to chase them far away.\n\nThe next morning the captain of the knights came to Sir Roland and said, \"One good man must stay here and keep watch on the gate to our\ncastle. I have decided that you are the one who must remain behind.\"\n\nRoland was sorry, very sorry to hear the captain's order, but he said nothing. Soon the knights rode away on their horses and he was left alone. An hour went by, then two hours, and\nnothing happened at the castle. A deer came out of the woods to eat grass in the shadow of the castle wall. But Roland saw no other living creature. \n\nThen, at last, the Knight saw a man coming along the road through the trees. Roland saw that it was one\nof his fellow knights from the castle. The man had been hit in the hand by an arrow. He was not a brave man, and the look in his eyes showed that we had frightened. \"Let me watch the gate for you, Sir Roland,\" he cried.\n\nRoland's heart jumped with joy.\nThen he remembered the captain's orders. Sadly he said, \"My place is at the gate. Your place is with our knights. Go back to them.\"\n\nThe knight was ashamed when Sir Roland spoke. Slowly he walked back to the woods and disappeared\namong the trees.\n\nAfter a time an old woman came along the road to the castle. She came up to Sir Roland and asked for food. He told her no one could come into the castle that day. Then he sent a servant to bring her bread and cheese.\nWhile she was waiting, Sir Roland asked her if she had seen the Knights and the giants. \"I have seen them,\" she said, \"and things go badly for your friends. If you were a real man, you would go and give them help.\" Sir Roland felt so badly that he shut\nthe gate after the old woman had her food. He did not want to listen to her any longer. After while the Knight heard a knock at the gate. \"What do you want?\" he asked.\n\"Open the gate, Sir Roland,\" someone replied. The Knight opened the gate and saw an old\nman standing a few feet away. The old fellow wore a long black cloak and carried a very beautiful sword.\n\"You should not be here,\" the man said, \"when your friends are having such a hard struggle with the giants.\" \n\n\"I have my orders,\"\nsaid Roland. \"I must not leave this gate.\"\n\"Look here! Listen to me,\" the old man cried. \"I have brought you this magic sword. Nonthing can stand before it. Take it, my friend, and help your fellow knights beat the giants.\" Roland believed that the sword\nreally was a magic one. He reached out his hand as though he would take it. The old man came forward as if he were going to cross over to the castle. \n\nBut again it came to Sir Roland's mind that he had been told to stay the gate. He called out to the man\n\"No! Stay where you are.\" The man stopped, but he waved the sword in the air and cried, \"This is your last chance, Sir Knight! If you do not take it, your friends will all be killed by the giants while you hide behind a castle wall!\"\n\nRoland feared that\nif he listened any longer, he could not make himself stay in the castle.\n\n\"Close the gate,\" he told the servant. \"I must follow the captain's orders, and remain here.\"\n\nAs the knight said these words a strange and surprising\nchange came over the old man. He began to grow bigger and bigger. Soon he was as tall as any giant in the great dark woods. At first Roland could not believe his eyes. Then he realized that the old fellow was really one of the giants. By magic he had made\nhimself look like a little old man! The Knight trembled to think of what would have happened if he had taken the sword and left the gate!\n\nWhile Sir Roland watched, the giant angrily went off down the road and was lost to sight among the trees.\nSoon after the giant had left, Sir Roland heard the sound of horses and men coming. It was the captain and his men returning to the castle. Roland signaled the servants to open the big gate and then he ran out to meet his friends.\n\nThe knights were\ntired and dusty, but they were full of joy because they had soundly beaten the giants. When they had all come into the castle, Sir Roland closed the gate once more. Then he hurried to follow them to the great hall.\n\nAs Roland came into the hall, he found\nevery man's eye upon him. \"The Shield! Look at Sir Roland's shield!\" they cried.\n\nThe Knight slowly looked down at the silver shield he carried. There, flaming in the middle of the shield was a star of gold!\n\n\"Tell us, Sir Knight,\nwhat happened here at the castle today?\" The captain asked as soon as he had gotten over his surprise. \"Did giants try to break down the gate? Did you drive them away alone?\"\n\n\"No, Sir,\" said Roland. \"Only one giant came here, and he went away quietly\nwhen he found that he could not enter the castle.\" Then he told of all that had happened throughout the long day. \n\nWhen Sir Roland had finished his tale, the captain spoke. \n\"Men may make mistakes,\" he said, \"But our magic silver shields are never\nwrong! You, Sir Knight, have been the greatest among us today because you would not leave the gate on which I had ordered you to keep watch. No matter how much you wanted to be with us, you stayed at your job!\"\n\nThen the knights jumped to their feet\nand cheered Sir Roland until the great hall rang with their cries.\n\n   \"Long Live the\n    New Knight of\n  The Golden Star!\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The Gorge, 1593", "Shaman Zlash'Lur", "Battle of the Gorge\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nscribed and translated to common by Zlash'Lur\nIn the 1590's after the desolation of San'Kharak and the murder of Rex Vorgo'Yar, the Orcs had taken salvation in the desert as refugees of Urguan. They took up and constructed a settlement named Azaghol in hiding but quickly enough they were discovered\nby a Wood Elf scout and was relayed to the Empire. As relations quickly plummeted, war eventually broke out causing a Coalition to be formed against the Orenian Empire. A time where the hunt was to be directed to the battlefield was most necessary.\nThe Imperials battled their way through the mountains eventually coming upon a valley as they planned to siege a whitewash settlement. The Coalition awaited them and when their bodies drew through the gorge the Coalition made their charge. They battled a\nlong and hard fight as the gorge quickly caused the warriors to begin wading through the mounds of bodies that littered the floor. The Commanders of the Coalition did what they could on cavalry through the piles of bodies but when the Imperials attack\nwas delayed each Commander did not hesitate to shout a key phrase amidst the battle. At the speed of sound, the word was relayed and from a hill top an explosion was made from under the land causing a major landslipe to obstruct the Imperial Legion.\nThis was a major turning point for the Coalition war and left the Empire greatly bruised by the mass of deceased caused by the landslide. The Coalition forces continued to their attack and succeeded in defeating the Imperials where they stood. A grand\ncelebration and feast was held in Urguan when the Legion finally returned home.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Grand Story", "Shaanti", "Many have heard stories of a Creator, an omnipotent God, one who has complete power, love, and knowledge. Some call him 'the Creator', others 'Yemekar', some 'Metzili'(although this is a Daemon), and many more. I have written this book so that the true\nstory of everything might be written down by hand.\n\nIt began with the creation. There was nothing physical, however there was an entire side of the world. This was called the Other Side. Today many refer to it as the 'Seven Skies'.\nNow the Other Side was entirely empty except for one. The one who was, is, and always shall be. His name is Nubia, the Creator of All.\nNubia is a God of love, and bases everything off of love. And so because the world was empty, he desired with all his\nentirety(which is entirety himself) to share his love. And so he created the first creatures, the Aenguls. The Aenguls were beings of light. The provided truth to the world, and were unable to lie. He then created the Daemons, beings of fire. Now fire and\nlight were similar, but clashed. This is why Nubia created the world, so that Light might exist in the spirit, and Fire might exist in the Flesh. \nNubia began to fall in love with the world, and so he and his children created life. He first made the\nHumans, then the Orcs, the Elves, and finally the Dwarves.\nNubia then gave the greatest gift to his favorite daughter, Metzili.\nShe was given the power to create a people in her image, and she created the Kha.\nHe then gave his most powerful\nchildren, the Aspects, power to create life made of vegetation. One of his children, Nemiisae, then became jealous. She begged Nubia to give her a gift, and so he gave her authority over all things that crawled the earth((insects)). \nNow as this all\nhappened, all the hosts of the Seven Skies watched over the world. The four peoples, and the Kha, had begun to populate and grow in number.\nAs they grew, the races became violent towards each other.\nIn order to stop this, Nubia and his Hosts\nspread the races across the world, far from each other, and they brought them different tongues to speak, so they might never communicate.\nThis failed, and they continued to war against each other. \n\nNubia then called a council with\nthe Aenguls and Daemons. They decided to bring mediators into the world. \nHe decided to imbue two people, a man and a woman, with his Spirit. He let the Daemons decide one person, and the Aenguls decide the other.\nMetzili chose an Orc by the name of\nIblees. Nubia imbued him with part of his spirit, and so he renamed Iblees. His new name was Sound.\nThe Aenguls then chose an elven woman. Her name was Elvira, and she was renamed to Silence. \nThey were called the Avatars, for they were Nubia's\nconnection to the world. Their purpose was to bring peace and balance.\nAs Silence and Sound went among the people, they brought peace, and healed the wounds of a broken world.\nAs Sound helped heal the people, he began to grow corrupt.\nSlowly, the light inside of him began to be overtaken by the darkness. Using the power of Nubia, he created a new realm, called the Void. He used this Void to hold energy. He hid this energy, and a dark plan began to unravel in his mind.\nIblees began the first magical ritual. From the Void, he summoned powerful elements. Wind, Earth, Air, Water, Fire, and Mind. He began to teach this magic to the peoples of the world. \nMagic was evil, and brought corruption to the hearts of all. And so\nthe Aenguls and Daemons put together their own magics, magics of the deities.\n\nWhen Elvira had found out that Iblees was using dark magics, she became angered, and confronted him.\nWith magic, she was killed. Elvira died, and because he loved his\ndaughter so, he instituted the Cycle, that is reincarnation. Now, everyone who dies is reincarnated into a new body. If they are virtuous, they rise into the Other Side. Only Silence can be virtuous and still reincarnate, for she has other worldly duties.\n~+~    List of     ~+~\n        Silences\n@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@\nI.) Elvira-Elf\n\nII.) Quetsiyah-Orc\n\nIII.) Thanos-Human\n\nIV.) Dovtsa-Dwarf\n\nV.) Elhael-Elf\nVI.) Kel'Tur-Orc\n\nVII.) Maris-Human\n\nVIII.) Valkryie-Dwarf\n\nIX.) Shaanti-Elf\n\n@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@There are no set laws to the Universe of Nubia except one, which is:\nAlways be as virtuous as possible, never hurt a soul, be forever kind, and ponder before action.\n\nBelievers who follow these rules may be imbued by the current Silence with abilities from Nubia.\nThe abilities will be shown on the following page.\n((Only one gift may be given to each person))\nI.) Weightlessness- The user levitates 2 feet off the ground during prayer or meditation.\n\nII.) Deathlessness- The user may kill themselves from an unknown cause at any time. They also do not\neat or drink food((in rp)). \n\nIII.) Placelessness-\nThe user may go anywhere they want, through any door.\n\nIV.) Knowledge-\nThe user may ask of God((A lore team or global mod)) any question about the past or present, and\nreceive an answer.\n\nV.) Unconquerable-\nThe user isn't able to be abducted, or conquered. They must remain entirely peaceful in order to use this power.\n\nVI.) Limitlessness- This power is only held by the reincarnation of\nsilence. The user of this power may grant to believers the other five paths.\nHierarchy of the Nubiaism Temple:\n\nReincarnation of Silence, Called the Wahid.\n\nFive Priests or Priestesses, must have different gifts.\n\nNuns or Monks.\nProphecy:\n\nIn the end, when Iblees has his most powerful, Silence shall be reborn in her last reincarnation. This reincarnation will then be brought up by the Wizard, who had been hiding. They shall destroy Iblees, and the world shall be remade. The End.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Greater Good", "Ehier", "The Greater Good\n\n  By Ehier\n\n  \n  \n  For the good, the bad, the wrong and the right.\n-The Good\n\n  Many individuals try to be good. They try to make a good life for themselves. But there are few who are really willing. Who would give their own to be as of service for others. \n  These are the ones we want to see more in this world,\nyet they are also the ones that are the most rare to find.\n  I have only found a couple myself, and none of them lived very long.\n  It is a curse, some might say.\n  Few people choose, or even dare to live like this. Not only because these\npeople tend to be used by others, but also because being 'good', in most cases, simply isn't profitable.\n\n  While what might seem good be good for a moment, in most cases turns out to be not as good as thought later.\n  In reality, our definition\nof good and bad is flawed. They are guidelines that were told to us by so called gods, or even by ourselves.\n-The Bad\n  Bad isn't wrong. Just like good isn't right. It is also flawed, just like our definition of good.\n  We could judge a person by what they are, a druid, an ascended, a void mage, a dark mage. But very rarely do we care to judge a person\nby who they are. Not only to themselves, but also to others.\n  An ascended could do things far worse than whatever a necromancer could have done. Yet we would call the ascended a good person, and the necromancer a bad one.\nAre we right to do this? Do we have any right to call someone good or bad?\n  It is something you can only answer for yourself.\n-The right\n  The right thing to do doesn't have to be good or bad. Sometimes it can be neither. Doing nothing can solve a situation just as well as doing something can.\n  The right thing to do in most cases depends on the situation. Law breaking\nmight be involved. Murder. Hurting others. All wouldn't be seen as good, but might be the right thing to do.\n  That's where doing the right thing and doing something good differs. Doing something good is doing something the right way in the eyes of\nothers. Doing something right is doing it properly in your own eyes.\n  These things can be the same, of course. Your opinion may be the same as the opinion of others.\nIn the end, it's all opinion. Good and bad do exist, and so do right and wrong.\n  They are all a way of living, and none is necessarily the wrong choice.\n\n  Everything has its right or wrong\n  Everyone has their path\n  Be wise", ""),
        StaticBook("The guard", "Arthur Caulfield", "A guard on duty\npulled out his sword\nthreatened an innocent man\n\nThe man cried \"what have I done\" but reason with the guard no one can. \n\nThe guard searched his clothes, took his food and hit him on\nthe head. \n\nThe guard shouted \"you quiet now, I kill you and you be dead!\"\n\nThis is when the man realised who he was dealing with. \n\nA guard as dumb as this one could only be a myth.\n\"How did you pass training? How have you survived?\" \n\nThe guard simply awnsered \"I stole armour, when the soldiers arrived.\"\n\nThe man slapped the sword away, landing on the floor.\nLooking to the guard he asked \"what the hell is all this for?\" \n\nThe guard shrugged his shoulders, drool falling from his chin. \n\nAfter a moment the guard tried to pick his nose, his gigantic fingers not going in.\nThen he began to sob, tears falling down his face. \n\nBut to the man, everything seemed to be out of place. \n\nHow could such a bufoon have so much strength?\nAnd in order to avoid this people we must go to such great lengths.\n\nTo take away their swords. \n\nAnd point them towards..\n\nA place run by a mayor like that\nwhere? You would like to know is such a place as that.\n\nA town not far from petrus known as Fustenberg.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Histories, I", "Alexandros", "THE HISTORIES OF ALEXANDROS\n\nThis being a SUMMARY of the inquiries of ALEXANDROS into the HISTORY of the AKRITIAN people.\nBook I-Midas, the Founder. \nBook II-The Foundation of the Polis and the Dark Age. \nBook III-The Polis Era I.\nBook IV-The Polis Era II.\nBook V-Diogenes and unfication.\nBook VI-Religious unrest. \nBook VII-The Turkin War. \nBook VIII-In Oren.\nBook IX-Axios.\n[I.]Alexandros, from Nicea, here displays his histories, in order that they be preserved from the menace of time, which, like a tide, eats away at all things august and excellent. It shall be the historian’s duty to recount the glories\nof Akritian and barbarian alike, and lastly, and most importantly, to explain the reason for their enmities and hatreds, ambitions and wants, faith and piety, greatness and pestilence; past and present.\n\n[II].The founding story of Akritos was once\nknown by even the darkest serf, but has now faded into obscurity. It began with a man called Midas, a Heartlander who led a savage warband known as the Akritians, also having under his command a certain number of dark-skinned barbaroi,\nled by a man named Alp. Both parties, in their own galleys (how a galley could make it across such seas is known not) were made up of pagans, or worse, those who believed not even in a God.\n\n[III.]Now, as it happens these\ntwo galleys reached the Western shore of the country. Seeing that the island was hilly, with only small streams, the barbarians lamented: ‘O, Mighty Tigir! Why should ye talk to us of great rivers and bountiful plains,\nonly to lead us to a shepherd's paradise?’ Midas, meanwhile, was undisturbed. He was convinced that this new island had bounties untold lying beyond these desolate hills. He argued with Alp, but the two were irreconcilable. At some\npoint in the conversation, Alp uttered an insult of some kind. Alp later claimed that it was against Midas only, and thus warranted a duel or a reconciliation, but Midas always remained convinced that, in a moment’s madness,\nAlp had insulted each and everyone of his men, and so taken up in the rage of the argument, ordered his slingers and peltasts to loose all sorts of missiles at Alp’s ship.\n[IV.]Alas! In the storm of missiles Midas lost right eye his eye to an arrow, and Alp his left to the lead bullet of a sling. Thus was born two peoples: Alp sped South-East, to occupy the neighbouring island, christening his people ‘Turkins’\nwhereas the Akritians settled on the seemingly hilly and prospectless land of Akritos. Now, some say it is the origin of the fact that Akritians make better slingers, but poor archers and vice versa, but I personally do not think\nthis is the case. The Turkins are known to be a strange people. Even for a man, to be seen naked is to be considered shameful amongst them. More likely, then, that the Turkins should adopt the strange and unwieldy bow over the obviously superior sling.\nOne thing is clear: Akritian and Turkin would grow to loathe each other evermore after this incident, with both sides each other blaming evermore also for one offensive or another.\n[V.]However, in the meantime, the two peoples separated. Midas set about exploring, colonising and conquering this new a land - a land which he named Akritos. Now, it so happened that this\nseemingly desolate land was inhabited by all kinds of strange creatures, some humanoid in manner. There are many stories surrounding Midas’ adventures in Akritos.\n[VI.]One such story comes only a few days after Midas landed in Akritos. Establishing an outpost which he hubristically called ‘Midasoupolis’ (therefore expecting it would grow up to be a city or polis), two local tribes instantly\nsuspected evil in the newcomers (The Akritians claim this to have been unprovoked but barbarians claim that the Akritians were behaving drunkenly and attacking women.) So it was that these two tribes happened to be commanded by father\nand son respectively. One, according to the Akritians, at any rate, was called Xenophon and his son was called Athenagoras. Xenophon loved Athenagoras, to the point where he actually said that no son could suffice to replace him,\nnd called him the most gallant and brave of young men. With this bravery came an independence of mind that would lead to a fateful - and fatal - state of affairs.\n[VII.]For his father received a pagan prophecy in a pagan cave from a pagan priest, and it was read aloud to great exultation: ‘For so the iron-clad man shall die under the brave Xenophon’s spear.’\nNow, all worry was wiped from Xenophon. For surely, his men were bronze-clad? His troops had not yet mastered the working of iron, and there was only one people who had - namely, Xenophon’s newly arrived guests. He then made a cunning ploy to deal with\nMidas and the Akritians - to invite them with all good measure of hospitality to an outdoor feast at night, and then to grab spear and shield and kill the iron-clad men with said spears. Xenophon, as was traditional,\nwould sit at the back of the assembly, and he and the older men would chuck spears into the wading Akritians.\n\n[VIII.]All seemed perfect, but for one flaw. Athenagoras had no knowledge whatsoever of the prophecy\n- for, despite his gallantry, Xenophon made sure not to tell him - as he did not want to risk his beloved son by involving him in the ploy. Now, it came to the moment where Athenagoras, eager to deal damage to the colony, raided the outpost’s\npickets and captured an Akritian. Athenagoras would use this advantage to destroy Midas, once and for all, going about his own plan.\n\n[IX.]Things now moved very fast. Both Xenophon and his son were eager\nto get their plans into motion, and so made stades into seconds. The Akritians arrived, and, when Xenophon raised his javelin to throw, he hit an Akritian and killed him. Midas, with a commanding voice, ordered his men to form a tight phalanx\nas the ambush bore down upon them, but in the end, they were forced to retreat into the depths of darkness.\n\n[X.]Things now became very desperate for the Akritians, as they expected to be harried at any second.\nBut, whilst Xenophon rushed after them, he recognised a groan that drove into the depths of his heart - one of the dead ‘Akritians’ was none other than his own son, Athenagoras, by his own javelin.\nTwisting and writhing like a fly whose wings had been torn off, the javelin was lodged with all severity deep into his belly. Without a word, Athenagoras died. Alas, what a man the world lost that day to the yarns of fate! And\nso did the grieving Xenophon fall upon his sword and take his own life, never again to assume the port of warlike thunder! It soon became apparent that Athenagoras had disguised himself and sought to challenge Midas from within.\n[XI.]The two leaderless tribes soon assimilated themselves to Midas’ rule, tripling his population. Now near a thousand, Midas would, by the end of his life, prove that the name ‘Midasoupolis’ to not be entirely without basis.\nOver his life, many such events happened. Midas conquered and colonised, laying the foundations for the cities which would become great. After 60 years of rule, Akritos was fully explored\nand conquered: many one-eyed, two-headed, six-legged and three-tailed beasts would fall to his bloody sword over these six decades, but that is a topic which can be explained another day.\nNotes on measurements:\nplethron=c.30 yards.\nstade=c.210 yards.\nmilion=a bit less than a mile.\nstage=approximately 20 miles.\nleague=3.4 miles.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Holy Bible", "Old Man McGuffin", "According to all known laws of aviation, there is no way a bee should be able to fly. Its wings are too small to get its fat little body off the ground. The bee, of course, flies anyway because bees don't care what humans think is impossible.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Holy Soldier", "Kili Al-Deen", "in the distance a man with a white turban and patted clothing with a stand of his turban waveing in the air,his arm raised high,with a curved sabre in hand his face is of a light tan and his eyes are dark brown with a light beard he towers over his grey\nhorse. he is know to be a hero, a warrior, a scholer.he hopes onto his steed and charges tword the claded enemy out numbered 1 to 8 as he charges his sword shimmers with a writing on it that says \"Soldier Of Allah\" to the enemys who robed thousands of\npeople they are known to rob kings and burn kindoms. Empores surrenders kingdoms to these men...but not this man. this man knows truth,the armored men laugh at this young man only in cloth charging to kill these 8 powerful warlords. slashing begins\nmen fall and shouts of pain can be heard from around the world untill there was one left but silence...until someone broke that silence..\"GOD IS GREAT!\"...the carvaners stood in shock  as they watched the turbaned man ride away until one called\n\"Who are you!\"  the turbaned warrior stops and turns and says \"I Am a Soldier Of Allah\"after saying that he smiles and says\"ma'a salama rafiqi\" and rides of into the sun set. the world knows him as a hero,a warrior,a scholer, i know him as\nA Soldier Of Allah.\n\n\n\n      by: Kili Al-Deen\n-------------------Thank you for reading I hope you enjoyed this book!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Homunculi", "Belegar", "The Homunculi\nBy Belegar Tunnelsmasher\n\nMalin’s Welcome, 1551\nPreface\nI, Belegar Tunnelsmasher, brother of Beros Oathcast whose body was made into a homunculi, am writing this to serve as a warning against dangers the homunculi pose and how to take on out if the situation comes to it.\nHomunculi 101\n\nThere are currently four tiers of homunculi being: fiend, deviant, aberrant and doppleganger. \n\nFiends\n- looks like a fiend\n- weak, very short lvied\n- not sentient\nDeviants \n- look similar to the race of the descendant whose body they are created from\n- slight disfigurements\n- odd skin colours\n- short lived\nAberrants\n- very similar look to descendants\n- unnatural skin colour\n- very small disfigurements\n- greater strength than descendants\n- average lifespan\nDopplegangers\n- extremely intellignet\n- very strong, to the point of being able to lift items such as entire iron gates\n- bodies are almost perfect\n- cannot be killed by natural means (will be explained later)\n- does not have blood, instead has a\nsubstance related to the element they were created with\n- look identical to the descendant they are made from\nHomunculi have no morals or regard for life. They only look to extend their own lives and further their own goal to achieve ‘ascendancy’. In other words, they seek to become a god. This is the fifth tier of homunculi, and the tier that has yet to be\nachieved. It is imperative that they do not achieve this.\n\nAdditionally, most homunculi do not have souls. \n\nThe process to create a homunculi will not be detailed in this book, but let it be known that in order to make one a corpse is required,\nand the homunculi will not hesitate to murder to get their hands on one.\nHow to Kill a Doppleganger\n\nIn order to kill a Doppleganger, one cannot use normal means. Simply cutting off their heads will not end their existence, as if their body is left alone, it will slowly regenerate until fully formed once again.\nThe only way to completely kill a Doppleganger is to inject their bodies with a ‘Potion of Unmaking’. \n\nThe process to create this potion requires an experienced alchemist. The reagents needed are: Metzil’s Tangle, Flame Tongue Root, Serpent's Stalk,\nLarihei’s Fingers and two lodestones. A lodestone is a rock that exhibits magnetic properties. Once this potion is made, the Doppleganger must be incapacitated and every piece of their body injected with this potion. The potion will then tear the\nhomunculi apart and end their existence.\nKnown Dopplegangers\n\nAt the time of writing, there are two know Dopplegangers. They are Prohan and Lotho. They are extremely dangerous, do NOT approach them voluntarily. \n\nBoth have air as their element of creation.\nProhan:\n\n- human\n- tan skin\n- black hair\n- looks like Daniel Nodal\n- Member of the Dawn Strider Voyagers, often seen wearing the uniform\nLotho:\n\n- dwarf\n- white skin\n- blonde hair\n- looks like Beros Oathcast\n- no accent\n- usually seen dressed in white robes with a set of goggles atop his head\nWeaknesses of Homunculi\n\nHomunculi are damaged by aurum and Holy Magic much like the undead are. If confronting a homunculi, especially a Doppleganger, it is highly recommended to wield an aurum blade and wear aurum armor.\nAlso, if possible, assistance of one versed in the arts of Holy Magic is highly recommended.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Impure", "Pius", "Men, women and children of all ages, nobles and commoners alike, soldiers of both sides stood there at the bottom of the loyalist keep. The ones who had the veil of lies put upon their faces stood side by side, brothers in arm once more. Godfrey's sadness\ncould be seen on his face and his eyes, but his voice boomed as he spoke to the masses. The look of sadness changed as he looked upon his people, standing atop the balcony. He took a breath now, and then.\n-------------------\n\"Citizens of the civilized Oren, my people, on this day we mark a transition. For years, oren stood as the crowning achievement of civilized beings. But there were those who would set against one another, and we took up arms to defend our way of life\nagainst the Impure. In doing so, we never suspected that the greatest threat came from within.\n\nThe impure put a cloud and a spell of falsehood on some within our own Court. The impure conspired to create the shadow of impurity using our\nown as their pawn. They had hoped to grind the Empire into ruin. But the hatred in their hearts could not be hidden forever. At last, there came a day when our enemies showed their true natures.\n\nThe impure hoped to unleash their destructive power against\nthe Empire by smearing lies on the head of government, corrupting our nobles and usurping control of the Army. But the aims of would-be tyrants were valiantly opposed by those without elitist, dangerous powers. Our loyal men contained the insurrection\nwithin the west and quelled uprisings on thousands of lands.\n\nThe remaining impure will be hunted down and defeated! Any collaborators will suffer the same fate. Our men that were corrupted and lead to believe the lies, if they see the truth, shall be\nforgiven. These have been trying times, but we have passed the test. The attempt on my name has left me a better Emperor, but I assure you my resolve has never been stronger. The war is over. The Impure has been defeated, and the rebellion has been\nfoiled. We stand on the threshold of a new beginning. In order to ensure our security and contuing stability, the Empire will be reorganized, for a safe and secure society, which I assure you will last for ten thousand years. An Empire that will continue\nto be ruled by this august body and sovereign ruler for life. An Empire ruled by the majority, ruled by a new rule of law!\n\nBy bringing the entire land under one law, one language, and the enlightened guidance of one individual, the corruption that\nplagued us in its later years will never take root. Regional lords will eliminate the bureaucracy that allowed the impure movement to grow unchecked. A strong and growing military will ensure the rule of Law.\n\nUnder the Empire's New Order, our most\ncherished beliefs will be safeguarded. We will defend our ideals by force of arms. We will give no ground to our enemies and will stand together against attacks from within or without. Let the enemies of the Empire take heed: those who challenge Imperial\nresolve will be crushed.\n\nWe have taken on a task that will be difficult, but the people of the Empire are ready for the challlenge. Because of our efforts, the land has traded war for peace and anarchy for stability. Millions of people now look\nforward to a secure future. The empire will grow as more lands feel the call, from the Rim to the wilds of unknown lands.\n\nImperial citizens must do their part. Join our grand fleet and armed forces. Become the eyes of the Empire by reporting suspected\ninsurrectionists. Travel to the corners of the land to spread the principles of the faith to barbarians. Build monuments and wonders that will speak of our glory for generations to come.\n\nThe Knights, now proudly wearing the name of Imperial Knights, have\ntackled the dangerous work of fighting our enemies on the front lines. Many have died in their devotion to the Empire. Imperial citizens would do well to remember their example.\n\nThe Faith of Oren has triumphed over the shadowy secrecy of shameful\nmagicians. The direction of our course is clear. I will lead the Empire to glories beyond imagination. We have been tested, but we have emerged stronger. We move forward as one people: The Imperial citizens of the Oren Empire. We will prevail. Ten\nthousands years of glory begins TODAY.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Journies", "Tyrell Blavier", "-_-(The \n         Journeys)-_-\n\nAthera in the eyes of\n     Tyrell Blavier\n-Reserved Page\n\nSribbles from long\nago that I've kept.\n\nThe true journey is how i've come so far from so little.\n/Foreword/\n\nWell I don't know how to start here honestly, the world seems so big yet so litte. Diverse people are everywhere and I feel that the common man, elf-olog or what have you should have a piece in this book about our world.\nChapter One\nWith Humble Beginnings\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-\nI've half-rounded the world once but now plan to go as far and wide as a human possibly can, i'm in search for knowledge, a purpose- I want a feel for this world and perhaps abit of fame and money...\nHow i'll find all of this is anyones guess but with how I imagine i'll be searching it must be possible. Emphasis on must. I *the word stand is crossed out here* currently sit here writing at the Viridian Pub some distance away from Petrus-\nmy only armament being a book, a quill and my way with words. Of course if I ever get in a scuffle i'd find myself pulling out this fantastic wooden dirk at my side, lets just hope that never happens as for splinters are known for being a pain in the ass.\nForward along the road I travel and I get to be greeted by Petrus for perhaps the 1000th time. It's a city I take for granted now, and I shouldn't. Imperials have much hatred going their way (for which I will not digress into.) but I must give them...\n...credit for upholding their traditions with a strong government, excellent craftmanship and a tax system. All civilized nations must have some kind of tax system. Petrus is large and sits largely surrounded by a moat and mountian. Such a well-\n-planned city. It rises almost in three tiers, starting from a common area with a church, bazaars, housing and other storefront then going into the more governmental buildings such as the regients castle and a extensive barracks.\nAt the time of writing a thread of undeath lurks not to far from the city further along the Peaks of Godfrey but a fort has been enstablished to help strenghthen the protection of this already bear of a city. Undeath cannot dapen the souls of the-\n-citizens of Oren though as a wedding is to take place here soon. A wonderful ceremony, with a- *The words are scratched out here.*\n\nWhat has become of me? I have forgot all I was. Sometimes I wish I was still young.\nChapter Two\nSwordhand\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-The wedding was a bust, poor damsel wasn't there. Best to hope she wasn't off with another man. Oren shows to be a kingdom with a *The next words are scratched out and the pages after ripped.*", ""),
        StaticBook("The Joy", "The Inquisitor", "A rare champion of the glade, Thickethand was a halfling. They were remarkably amiable. It bordered on the supernatural. A few suggest it was a powerful psionic or memetic event.\nRegardless, Thickethand was a halfling who was able to make friends with near any other sapient creature they encountered. They became personal friends with Aureus, and most of the other denizens in the glade.\nThey were kind, reserved. Thickethand maintained the glade, brought it great lushness and bounty. Their rule was otherwise unremarkable. Though it is likely apocryphal, records hold that they ultimately perished when they tried to befriend an avalanche.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kal'Varak", "Archmage Crumena", "The Kal'Varak\nRescribed by Arch-Mage Crumena V. Illwindor on the 2nd of the First Seed, 1473.\nThe Kal'Varak, which roughly translates as 'Mind City', is an ancient crystalline artifact. It was dug up by the dwarves of Karik just prior to\ntheir unearthing of the hibernating dragons, but the faded scratches on the side suggest it has been discovered at least once before this, perhaps by the original inhabitants of Karik. It seems to be some sort of powerful magical nexus, exerting a\nsignificant magical influence without appearing to draw magical power anywhere, as if it somehow generates it itself. Despite this, the Kal'Varak is useless as a source of magical energy. All of its power is turned inwards on itself, giving the\nKal'Varak the bizzare property that gives it its name. When a living being touches the Kal'Varak, their mind and soul are forcefully drawn from their bodies into the Kal'Varak itself. Once inside, they find themselves in a strange dreamworld, often\ntaking the form of a maze, populated by their memories, dreams and nightmares. In the Kal'Varak, people appear as they would wish to be, some see themselves as stronger, taller, more attractive, sometimes as a different race\nentirely. While the ability to walk through one's mind and the minds of any others currently 'in' the Kal'Varak may seem enticing, the dreamworld is dangerous. The dreamworld responds to moods, fears and doubts, often turning a\nguilty memory into a full-blown nightmare in an instant. The more complex the mind, the more labyrinthian the maze, and those with dark pasts they'd rather forget are often forced to face them within the Kal'Varak. Even more dangerous is\nwhen the mind and crystal form a world that one would not want to leave. The collapsed body outside the crystal still needs food, water, and is still vunerable to harm. If the body dies, the mind cannot return to it. Somewhere in the Kal'Varak maze is\na door, and those more experienced with the dreamworld can find it more quickly than others. The door is always relevant in form to the person it belongs to, often impossible to mistake for one's own. Sometimes the door is not even a door, but it is\nalways clearly an exit. Passing through your door returns you to your body, but if you pass through the wrong door, you may find yourself in the wrong body entirely.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kha Wish", "Zhikar", "Sa'vi Metztil in the fountain. Ju'Mukar wishes for a nice new elegant ferrum staff, the staff would have many places to attach things onto it.\n\n\nMeanwhile Mukars kitten, Zhikar,  wishes for ======(the text is crossed and unreadable but a new fast\nwas wrote) \nZhikar wishes to know the truth about Mukar. What he really is and to be happy..", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kings Vouch", "Garrond Frostbeard", "I, High King Garrond Frostbeard, recommend t'is lad tu beh trained in teh art of runesmithin", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kushgoth", "Elder Bashkuga'Raguk", "This is a story all about how my life got flipped-turned upside down\n And I'd like to take a minute\n Just sit right there\n\nI'll tell you how I became Kushgoth of a War Nation called Krugmar.\nIn West San'Kharak born and raised\n On the coast was where I spent most of my days\n Chillin' out maxin' klompin' all cool\n And slaving some elves outside of Johannesburg\n When a couple of Oreners who were up to no good\nStarting making trouble in my bruddahood\n We got in one little near miss genocide and Vorgo got scared\n He said, \"Latz mohvin' ihn wiht latz bruddahz ahn ziztahz ihn San'Raahk.\"\n\nI begged and pleaded with my Rex day after day\nBut he packaged my weapons and sent me on my way\n He gave me a headbutt and then he gave me a piece of cactus green\n I put my drum on and said, \"Mi mhyt az wehl kihk iht.\"\n\n Fast horse, yo, this is bad\nDrinking rum out of a pint glass.\n Is this what the Uruks of San'Raahk living like?\n Hmm, this might be alright.\n\nBut wait I hear  they're Kuntz, Dum-Zkahz, all that\n Is this the type of place they just send this drug addict?\nI'll see when I get there\n I hope they're prepared for the Kushgoth of Krugmar\n\nWell, the horse stopped and when I got off\n There was an Uruk that looked like an Knight standing there with a sword in hand\nI ain't trying to get klomped yet\n I just got here\n\nI sprang with the quickness like  lightning, disappeared\n\n I whistled for a Jabbernak and when it came near\n The scales were all \"Fresh\" and it had a long tail in the back\nIf anything I could   say that this    creature was rare\n But I thought, \"Nah, furgit iht.\"\n - \"Yo, ohme tuh San'Raahk.\"\n\nI pulled up to my    blarg about 7 or 8\n And I yelled to the Jabbernak, \"Yo ohme zmel lat lahytur.\"\nI looked at my blarg\n I was finally there\n\n\n\n\n To sit on my throne\n           as\n          The\nKushgoth of Krugmar\n\n - An Autobiography", ""),
        StaticBook("The Last Record", "Artorius Thannius", "Personal Records of the Spellcrafter Archon III - Desperate Measures\nWhile it seems the Ravager was defeated and destroyed, it came at the cost of Aegis: the entire continent has crumbled into some sort of Abyss. It is more than a\nfracture of matter, it is a collapse of the laws of the world. Rivel failed to escape the blast radius: the city has broken up and now floats on the magical currents as we hover over the Abyss. The cataclysm has pushed us below the minimum population\nthe scryers say we need to survive. Up here we cannot even get food. The Lesser Caste’s survivors have mostly starved to death and with food stores dwindling we will soon follow.\nI have no choice. Tonight I will conduct the ritual of lichdom. Rivel is\ndead and so are its people. The remaining few will be more than enough to serve as a sacrifice for the ritual. If Rivel must die, its leader shall live on.\nGarzardiel’s name be cursed.\n- Artorius Thannius, Former Spellcrafter Archon of Rivel\n", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lava Claw", "John Lyons", "1st of Snow's Maiden\n1627\n\nI have decided to celebrate the year of our lord 1627 by going on an adventure.\n\nafter setting out I immediatly feel fourty years longer, my target lies to the south of the Westerlands\nThe Lava Claw is a ruin that has perplexed me for a large part of my life, east of Haelun'or there's nothing but grass and the occassional tree, but then there's a massive crater, filled with lava and at the center there's a massive ruin of a stone\nclaw-like structure.\n\nThus I named it the claw. Due to it's unique shape and boring surroundings i was able to make a map of it in rather a short time.\n\nAccessing the claw itself shouldn't prove too difficult for a younger man\nbut I myself shan't do it!\n\nThe deep crater tells us a lot a bout the rock layers of this part of Tahn, it mostly consists of smoothstone with occassional patches of dirt, I spotted what i'm sure are bricks in the ground layers\nPerhaps this was once a site of the ancient Kingdom of Malin?\n\nAbout thirty meters below the surface the lava comes pouring out into a basin that surrounds the claw.\n\nThe structure appears to resist the lava easily, which is curious.\nAfter sticking around for a few hours night fell, this did not seem to affect the structure.\n\nThe Claw has not changed in decades, nor has there been evidence that it's linked to the forces of evil.\nTherefore I'm delighted to conclude that it is merely one of the many curiosities of Axios and not a threat to it's inhabitants.\n\n\nWritten for the Lyons institute by it's owner.\n\nJohn Lyons", ""),
        StaticBook("The Ledger", "Frederick Kelly", "Kelly Estate\nBusiness Ledger\n\n\n--------------------------------Details of all purchases that are performed face-to-face shall be recorded and signed in this book for the purposes of 'Law'.\n------------------------------\n17th of the Deep Cold, 1662\n\nTwo crates were purchased by Calius Terin on behalf of the Dominion Tavern. 126 bottles in total, 63 of the White 1660 and 63 of the Red 1660.\nPurchased for 2,500 minas.\n\nSigned - Frederick Kelly.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lost Memorys", "Nami", "Hello here this is my story.My name is Nami a halfbreed of dark and snow elf. I'm 6ft tall with long white hair and light gray skin and light blue eyes.When I was a child I live in the wood with my mom and father.My father was a dark elf,he a guard to\nOne day he was on patrol of the area and find my mother he fell in love with her. My father know the rule about dark elf HAVE to marry they own kind but he went against those rules. People find out that a dark elf marred a snow elf people were in rage of\nit.So they decided to execute they.But they got away in time before they find they. Mother is a snow elf she was so kind but people were mean to her because she a snow elf but she always smile. They find a house in the middle of the woods.Then they\nhad me. A day I was sleeping in my room when my dad come in and woke me up.I smelled smoke and fire my father picked me up and rush me downstairs. Then an I heard an arroe sound hitting flush. I lookat my father and saw blood on his mouth I screamed and\ncried.My mother run to me and picked me up.She saw my father lay on the floor die. Tears fell from her face. Her ran towards the window. She broke and try to jump but her clothes where stock.The flames were getting closer. She kiss me and threw\nMe out the window.I look up and see my mother being golfed in flames she screamed. I yelled \"MOMMMMM\" her scream stop. I was crying..... Now the rest of my life is blank...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lusty Hou-zi", "Door", "*The material is so graphic in explanation that not even the wandering wizard would dare to speak the word.*\n\nYou feel as if you can suddenly wield a sword in one-hand better.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Mali'ker", "Dak'ir Des'Nox", "Birth of the Mali'ker\n------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  By Dak'ir Des'Nox\nBefore I begin this tale, I'd like to state that the origin of the Mali'ker is still unknown to us. This is simply an\nold tale passed down \nthrough my clan.\nIt begins with the \nHearth Father, Malin.\nHe looked upon the Mali'ame, his first children. Their image molded after the forests they reside in. In them he saw devotion. A will to protect the trees and animals without rival.\nHe then looked to the high elves, his second children. Their display was ever the epitome of purity. In them he saw knowledge. Their desire to learn and expand in all things was unparalelled. \n\nBut he saw something they lacked. Passion.\nHe racked his mind of many days. It was not until he looked skyward as dusk fell that he saw what would design us. \n   Before him lay the night tide, a vast sea of stars and anomalies. He raises a hand to the night sky and began to collect what would\nmake us seperate from out fair colored kin. He took the dark hues from the empyrean and shaped our bodies. He took the tails of comets and darkened stone of meteorites. Giving us the blacks, whites, and faint blues of our hair.\nHe took a step back from his creation, observing the from of what would become the dark elves. Folding his arms, he thought.\n\n   What else could set these beings apart from the Mali'ame and\nthe Mali'aheral?\nNext, he looked down. His eyes falling upon the ground. Kneeling, he reached an arm into the depths of the earth and began to pull precious gems from the deep recesses. He carried the jewels back to the grey froms placing them into their eyes.\nHe favored the rubies and garnets most of all, but occasional sapphires, emeralds, and topazes glinted in their vigils.\n\n Before him stood us.\n     The Dark Elves.\nBut there was still something... What could give us the passion we lacked?\n\n   He looked above one final time and raised a careful hand. Plucking single stars from the sky and placing one within each of us. Giving us our bright and burning souls.\nHis mind lingered to the Wood Elves and High elves again.\nNature and dedication. Knowledge and Purity.\nBut what could give the Dark Elves their drive?\n\nHe pondered again. Before long, he smiled softly.\nHow could he forget? \n\n   He spoke to the still forms and uttered three words.\n\n\"Family, honor, love.\"\n\n            ...\nAnd with that, we awoke. With stars burning brightly in our chests, fueling these three things, we have become the fiercely passionate beings we are today...", ""),
        StaticBook("The Man", "Ayda Morra", "As the rain poured, the maiden lent against a rouge log for she had no home. A man of tall stature approached the poor maiden down on her luck and spoke softly \" You looking for an employee? \". The maiden was confused, She looked like a homeless person,\nWhy would she be able to afford a worker?\n\"Sorry Sir, I have no money to offer. I have no home or money. \" she spoke sadly, slumping agasint the rouge log. \" I am not asking for money but, to keep a lady down on her luck a companion. \" he smiled at\npoor maiden. Who stood up \" Thank you sir but, I can see right through you, I've seen your posters. \" she looked him in the eyes. The man was shocked and frowned. \" I have not killed any women, do you see blood on my hands? Or death in my eyes? \" he spoke\ntruthfully. The poor maiden looked at his hands then his eyes \" I see nothing, but i decline your offer, leave me be. \" she spoke firmly but, the man continued to pester her.\n\nLater that night, when the maiden was sleeping peacefully\nthe man grabbed a knife and stabbed her in the chest.\n\nThe End\n\nWritten by:\nAyda Morra", ""),
        StaticBook("The Mani Spirits", "The Owl Druid", "~*~The Mani~*~\n~*~Spirits of the~*~\n      ~*~Wilds~*~\n\nScribed by the Owl Druid.\n\nStudied and observed by the Hawk Druid and Owl Druid.\nLo and Behold the true majesty of nature and the wilds. The tells of ancient beasts, fae creatures, and other various creations of the Aspects rumored to walk upon the wilds and protect it. \n\nOne such creation has come to be known as-\nthe Mani Spirits. These animals are blessed beyond the rest to reside and watch over their respective species.\n\nAs with the beginning of all things, so was the creation of the animals by what is believed as Cernunnos, the Huntsman. These-\ncreatures formed and went across the realm to balance off the overburdening of life Cerridwen had created. As the two would become one in an neverending cycle, the Aspects's eyes fell upon the realm of men. Their greed, lacking of care and destruction of-\nthe wilds knew the deities's attention and thus, called upon the animals in return. The first animals that rose up took upon the gift and held the title of Prince. The rest would follow and now each species rumored to have a Mani Spirit guarding their -\nflock. These beings hold different attitudes, demeanors, and goals. Some more docile, others more aggressive in their wake of protecting the wilds. \n\nThough with every myth and tale, the truth speaks in whispers upon the pages. To those that-\nprove worthy to a Mani Spirit, it is said one will appear...though that much is a tale here or there. For one cannot truly control these creatures.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Matriarch", "Thurak'Yar", "THE MATRIARCH   \n\nThe tale of the daughter of Dragur.\n\n\n\nRe-Scribed by the Farseer Thurak, 21'st of The First Seed, 1489.\nFirst born of the brood of Dragur, a female, molded in his image, and adopting his unquenchable thirst of sheer knowledge. \n\"The sun will awaken each new day, followed by the rise of the moon, that will light the seemingly endless nights, and during\nthese nights it will be the Stars which will guide you. This land in which you were born in will teach you many things. And as you come to learn, you will share the knowledge which you have come to acquire in the hopes that the ones you come to\nshare with learn from it. This is my dream.\"\n\nAnd so the Daemon fell into a seemingly eternal slumber. Many centuries have come to pass since that day, and he collection continued to grow. Unfortunately, some had used bits of knowledge she had\nshared with them for their own greedy purposes. They didn’t believe in her ways of “Shared knowledge for knowledge”, and wanted it without giving anything in return. They found the place in which she kept all her books, scrolls and scrawlings, and began\nto steal whatever they thought would bring them wealth and power. Upon returning, she felt a sense of violation and mistrust, but knew and understood that time itself would heal those feelings. She began to scrawl everything she could remember from what\nwas stolen from her, but they were merely tattered fragments compared to what she once had. Hope had reached her a few years later when she found one of her books amongst some ruins and rubble. She began to hope that the others\nwill come to reveal themselves once more.\nThus, the Matriarch wanders the land, in search of the items that were taken from her, but also still learning what she can from her travels and from the land. By merely observing and keeping scrawls of what she has come to witness, to finding\nbooks, novels and scrolls from past and present civilizations of the land. This is her passion... And her only purpose.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Mighty Uruks", "Vallel", "~*~ I met a wise and strong uruk. Her name was Nurena of the Yar clan. She provided all this information to me and I tried my best to organize the information properly and be as accurate as possible with it. Thank you, Nurena! ~*~\n-=- Book dedicated to people who want to learn about this interesting race. Also to clarify and provide as much knowledge as possible about orcs.-=- [!] From this point on, the book looks like it was written by a child! Still legible.\nUruks, or orcs, are massive and large beings of these lands. They are tough, strong, and honorable. Uruks are usually seen as one of the largest race, but there are Ologs! Ologs are bigger and perhaps stronger than a regular orc.\nWith great strength of an Olog, comes a deep curse upon them. These giants are unwise and lack knowledge out of all their brothers. Goblins, however, are clever and smart, but are smaller than the average orc. All of them come in different size and color.\nThe entire race all speak a language called Blah. Most words are the common tongue, yet they are uniqely said due to their accents. Uruks greet each other with a headbutt followed by \"Ug.\" It is the most honorable and respectful greeting.\nUruks belong into a clan. Clans are a big group of orcs, ologs, or goblins who are like a family, but better! They are a matter of honor to defend their brothers and sisters. Uruks are usually born into a clan, though some may take a clanless uruk in.\nEach clan have their own traditions. Every clan comes from a great ancestor related to Krug in some way. Examples of a few clans: Yar, Gorkil, Lak, Radukz, Baduks, Lur, and Ugluks. There are still a lot more!\nWithin the uruk city, they have a leader called the Rex. I mey a past Rex called Eath'Lur who is a great orc. I am not sure how an uruk becomes a Rex, though.\nIt must take strength and honor to become a Rex. To achieve that, an uruk should make it to adulthood. Only the strongest make it to adulthood. To make a strong child to allow it to be make it to adulthood, there is a tradition uruks do.\nThey make cozy and warm dens for the moommy uruk. They call it \"nesting dens.\" The comfy caves can range from a large one to a small one, but they all make baby orcs big and strong!\nOrcs do not trust other people other than their own race, especially on thier land. Orcs are fearsome and territorial to non-orc races. Although they could kill and attack outsiders, they would not harm a child. There is no honor to kill children.\nOther non-orc races pay something called tribute. Tribute is not just giving to an orc. Tribute is giving to an orc in exchange for peace between them. Food can be used as tribute to the orcs.\nOnto their worships! Uruks praise the spirits. Spirits are powerful beings that live in the Void and can take physical form. There are three types of spirits: Immortal, Ancestor, and Lesser. All spirits are free beings to an extent.\nShamans are people who can talk to and summon spirits. They usually only call to spirits when they need help or guidance. Shamans make totems for the spirits and the spirits like their totem. A shaman can call to a spirit whenever they need to.\nThese wise people have their own staffs that they have which seem very important to them. Sadly, there are bad shamans in this place. The bad shamans are called dark shamans. They use a spirit to their own will and for other evil stuff!\nLuckily, a powerful shaman can purge the evil shaman and cut off their powers to talk and use spirits.\nIt is important to note that totems are for spiits. Every spirit have their own likes, dislikes, and gifts. The totem and area around the totem are made of things that symbolize the spirit and what they like.\nDon't be a whitewash orc and not worship spirits! Whitehwash orcs are orcs who have no honor and have disrespected the race. An uruk can become whitewash if they live with non-orcs or betray their own race. Be a good and strong orc!\n~*~ Uruks are so cool! Their culture and traditions are unique and perhaps one of the only interesting one's I've seen.\nThank you to Nurena for making all this possible! ~*~", ""),
        StaticBook("The Milkman", "Hobbs Burrows", "The Milkman\nBy Hobbs Burrows\n\nDear Reader,\nThis is an original story by Hobbs of Dunshire about a milkman and a baker fighting for the love of a woman. I hope it is an enjoyable read.\n\nYou could hear the hoof beats pound as\nthey raced across the ground, and the clatter of the wheels as they spun 'round and 'round. He galloped into Festival Street, his badge upon his chest, his name was Ernie and he drove the fastest milk cart in the west!\n\nNow, Ernie loved a widow, a lady\nknown as Sue. She lived all alone in Lidley Lane at number 22. They said she was too good for him, she was haughty, proud and chic, but Ernie got his cocoa there three times every week!\n\nShe said she'd love to bathe in milk and he said 'Alright\nsweetheart', and when he finished work one night he loaded up his cart. He said 'D'you want it pasturise? Cause pasturise is best' - she said 'Ernie I'll be happy if it comes up to me chest!' That tickled old Ernie.\n\n Now Ernie had a rival, an\nevil-looking man. Called Two Ton Ted from Teddington, and he drove the baker's van. He tempted her with his treacle tarts and his tasty wholemeal bread. And when she seen the size of his hot meat pies it very near turned her head.\n\nShe nearly swooned\nat his macaroon and he said 'If you treat me right, you'll have hot rolls every morning, and crumpets every night'. He knew once she sampled his layer cake he'd have his wicked way, and all Ernie had to offer was a pint o' milk a day.\n\nOne lunch time,\nTed saw Ernie's horse and cart outside her door. It drove him mad to find it was still there at half past four. And as he lept down from his van, hot blood through his veins did coarse, and he went across to Ernie's cart and didn't half kick his horse\n(whose name was Trigger, and he pulled the fastest milk cart in the west). \n\nNow Ernie rushed out into the street, his milk bottle in his hand. He said 'If you wanna marry Susie, you'll fight for her like a man!'\n'Oh why don't we play\ncards for her?' Ted sneeringly replied, 'And just to make it interesting we'll have a minas on the side.'\n\nNow Ernie dragged him from his van and beneath the blazing sun, they stood there face to face, and Ted went for his bun. But Ernie was too quick,\nthings didn't go the way Ted planned, and a strawberry flavoured yoghurt sent it spinning from his hand!\n\nNow Susie ran between them and tried to keep them apart, but Ernie pushed her aside and a rock cake caught him underneath his heart, and he looked up\nin pained surprise and the concrete hardened crust of a stale pork pie caught him in the eye, and Ernie bit the dust.\n\nErnie was only 52, he didn't wanna die. And now he's gone to make deliveries in that village in the sky. Where the customers\nare Aenguls, and ferocious dogs are banned, and the milkman's life is full of fun in that fairy dairy land.\n\nBut a woman's needs are many fold. And Sue, she married Ted. But strange things happened on their wedding night as they lay in their bed. Was\nthat the trees-a-rustling? Or the hinges of the gate?\nOr Ernie's ghostly milks a-rattling in their crates!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Moot", "Leyun Kameki", "The Moot\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\nThe Moot is an assembly held for all Druids of a particular Circle to come together for discussion, debate, and decision making. It is a time to worship the Aspects, to make notice of the events of the world, to commit to projects, and much more.\nMany times a Moot might serve the sole purpose of voting for a new Archdruid or Druid Guide or to cast votes on shunning a particular individual who has wronged a Druid, Druids, or the Order. Seldomly, a Moot might be held to throw a party, host a\nwedding, or perform a funeral.\n\nOnly by the word of an Archdruid may a Moot be called. Druids, Dedicants, Druid Guides, and Hierophants all can, and should, present information of importance to the Archdruids, and anyone can request\na Moot be called. However, it is up to an Archdruid to decide if and when a Moot shall be held and for what topics it shall be held to discuss. Only shall the Inner Circle, the Archdruids and Druid Guides, make a definite decision, based on a vote count,\nfor the Order. No other Druids or Hierophants are permitted to make decisions for the Order, but their opinions and advice are taken seriously and with much consideration. When serving as a meeting, a Moot is held in the Moot Room of the\nhosting Grove. While a Moot is in session, often times the Archdruid who called it will take the floor to present topics. Out of respect, all who wish to speak should wait for a pause or go-ahead. Druids should request or stand to take the floor or\npresent a topic. Dedicants aren’t permitted to attend Moots, but accepts are often made. In the case that a Dedicant is permitted at a Moot, he or she shall not speak unless asked to.\n\nThe Moot is an ancient tradition of Druidic culture. Sometimes\nnon-Druids are even invited to Moots, such as when relations are being discussed between the Order and a Nation or other group. A Moot is versatile, able to serve the purpose for many different occasions. It is one of the most formal, serious, and\nimportant aspects of Druidic culture. When in attendance of a Moot, remember to respect the speaker and follow proper etiquette. Blessed be.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Nature of", "Alem'shun Vanguard", "Let me preface this with the simple fact this is just the ponderings, thoughts and ideas of an Elf none of it is fact more of possible ideas. First in conventional clerical teaching and thinking the idea of Monochromatics is rather simple.\nThe idea that Light is perfection and therefore also good and that the dark or darkness is the absolute idea of imperfection or is of a completely unnatural origin. Then there is everything in between often labeled as\n“They Grey” or neutrally imperfective by others. This grey area is where most of everything falls. Humans, animals, plants all for the most part fall into the grey. The darkness is generally considered to be filled with creations\nof false life or daemonicly influenced beings. Clerics are often times considered to be rather towards the side of perfection on the monochromatic scales and while this could be true let another view possibly influence future teachings.\nClerics by definition are regular people which are neutrally imperfect and therefore fall into the vast grey. I believe due to the nature of a connected cleric being a person infused with aengul power it is by very definition less perfect\nthan it was before. This means clerics by my own observations are not beacons of perfection or purity but are even closer to their brethren that serve daemons.  The clerical patron Aengul themself hates aengul daemon influence into\nthe mortal world. It tampers with the ideals of perfection and while Clerics are tools of great influence in destroying imperfection and on a whole shifting the monochromatic spectrum. It can not be denied that clerics due to there own creation are rather\ncontradictory and are inherently even less perfect and even more dark than a regular person.\n\nNow while clerics may be more dark than an ordinary person of the grey it by no means strikes them as evil doers.\nThis is a popular misconception that dark means bad light means good etc etc. Good and Evil have very little to do with perfection which is what the monochromatic scale measures.\nMeaning even if a cleric is darker than a regular person a cleric can still be a person who strives for the betterment of all and indeed the ideals of perfection.\nFor instance let us look to the library Dragthar\nan institution that any and all can obtain information from. A institution which many believe to be of a good cause. The patron of this library is a daemon but this does not mean the library is an unholy order of pure evil bend\non the destruction of the planet and conquest of all people. Like mentioned earlier dark does not mean evil neither does light mean good. I believe clerics and all people who use the monochromatic scales need to understand these\ndifferences and begin to realize their full mission for purity not necessarily be a do gooder.", ""),
        StaticBook("The People", "Baldin Frostbeard", "Beware\nthere is enough treachery, hatred violence absurdity in the average\nhuman being to supply any given army on any given day\n\nand the best at murder are those who preach against itand the best at hate are those who preach love\nand the best at war finally are those who preach peace\nthose who preach god, need god\nthose who preach peace do not have peace\nthose who preach peace do not have love\nbeware the preachers\nbeware the knowers\nbeware those who are always reading books\nbeware those who either detest poverty\nor are proud of it\nbeware those quick to praisefor they need praise in return\nbeware those who are quick to censor\nthey are afraid of what they do not know\nbeware those who seek constant crowds for\nthey are nothing alone beware the average man the average woman\nbeware their love, their love is average\nseeks average\nbut there is genius in their hatred\nthere is enough genius in their hatred to kill you\nto kill anybody \nnot wanting solitude not understanding solitude they will attempt to destroy anything\nthat differs from their own\nnot being able to create art\nthey will not understand art\nthey will consider their failure as creators\nonly as a failure of the world not being able to love fully\nthey will believe your love incomplete\nand then they will hate you\nand their hatred will be perfect\n\nlike a shining diamond\nlike a knife\nlike a mountain\nlike a tiger\nlike hemlock\ntheir finest art", ""),
        StaticBook("The Pie Poem", "Elizaveta vas Ruthern", "Miss Sophia as kind as can be, baked a pie especially for me!\n\nThe lady of warmth brought the best gift to the home, and her sheer talent with baking had clearly grown!", ""),
        StaticBook("The Princess and", "Alexandria of Rothesay", "Once upon a time, in a kingdom far far away, there was a king and queen who lived in a golden castle with their beautiful daughter. They lived in peace and prosperity, and never knew heartbreak or want.\nYet one night, an ugly orc captured the princess and carried her away, locking her up in a tall, dark tower.\nThe king and queen were struck with immeasurable grief, and promised the princess’s hand to any knight who could rescue their daughter. So the knights in the land assembled, wanting to bring the princess back to be their bride.\nThe Orc roared in anger when he saw the approaching knights. And one by one, he tore them to shreds at the foot of the tower. The princess looked on in horror as her rescuers were slewn.\nShe shrunk back into the confines of her room, weeping as she thought of her fate. \n\nYet.. somone heard her cries, carried \nthrough the dark of \nthe night.\nThe princess was awakened by the sound of thunderous wings, flapping in the moonlit sky. A large Dragon, with obsidian scales clung to the side of the dragon, baring his large teeth at the orc.  The creature took a deep breath-\nand in a burst of great flame, he reduced the orc to a pile of ash and bones. \n\nHe then turned his attention to the princess. She sunk back in fear as to what was to come. Yet, the flame did not come for her.\nThe dragon pryed apart the bars that held her captive, lifting her gently upon his back. She clung onto his dark scales, and he spread his wings once more, lifting her up into the clouds.\nThe dragon returned the princess to the king and queen, and they were in awe at such a marvelous creature. Yet, how could they keep their promise? How could a dragon wed their daughter?\nWhen asked this, the dragon started to transform in a blinding light, until all that remained was a handsome prince in his place. \n\nThe princess looked upon her savior, and the dragon took her to be his loving wife.\nThey both lived happily ever after. \n\nThe end.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Pumpkin Lich", "Arlen Teharissa", "Arlen Teharissa, Son of Pumpkin Lich/Druid Aphoros.\n\nEl'Avern of the Sirame.\n\nWas here.\n\n<The journal smells of Pumpkins>\n\nCyril Duval was also here ily", ""),
        StaticBook("The Purple Trees", "John Hawkwood", "On entering the Dominion I had asked to speak to a representative of the Druids or the Dominion but was met with dislike and no measure of interest at all. Hence, I continued to stay a certain distance away from the purple tree that seems to be directly\noutside the city itself. The purple tree seems to be having hanging fragments that are of the color purple as well. The tree has what seems to be birch wood as it grows. When looking closer at the tree, it seems a small surrounding of the dirt and earth\nwas turned to purple. A sample will be provided of the dirt taken from the purple tree at the Dominion. Furthermore, while conversing with a boastful druid who apparently was part of a group called the ANG had stated these sightings of the tree are\nbecause of some Ancient witch. But that can be utterly false. The spreadness of the purple \"infection\" on the earth does not seem to spread as it is only closely linked to the tree itself. It seems that these trees are able to transform or change\nthe color and aspect of the earth around it when grown. The tree seems to be several meters high and around two to three meters wide along its trunk.\n\nAfter meeting with a few elves that had drank from the water they had reported\nthat the water is able to kill the undead or anything that is \"tainted\". They had stated they felt no other symptons and the only effect was the change in the eye color. They did state that when in the water that they felt extremely energised.\nThe effect wears off when once out of the water but when in the water it makes a person feel extremely energetic. The healing powers though seem to be extremely powerful. Amputated body parts get fully healed. The elf recalls a persons arm being regrown\nafter it was cut off in battle. But once when the person entered the water it regrew.\n\nOn further reports and questioning it seems a being appears when people harm the trees. It stated that this being is floating and stuck to a piece of quartz and\nit talks to those that harm it. It seems that when touching this quartz like surrounded being that it shocks those that harm the trees as well as shoot out projectiles. The projectiles and shock arent enough to kill a person but seems to harm them.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Radiant Man", "Davin Lodmund", "The Radiant Man - Powers and Subjugation of the Mind\nThe Radiant Man, a suspected incarnate aengul, has aligned himself with parts of the Spellcrafters of Rivel with the goal of uncovering the Forgotten Dwarven artifact known as\n“The Seal”. To those who follow him, the Radiant Man grants incredible powers. They are akin to holy magics, but are incapable of healing yet also functional against those who could not in any way be described as dark creatures. It seems to be Holy\nMagic without the requirement of being holy: an excellent addition to any Spellcrafter’s arsenal, especially when so freely given and easily mastered. Or so it would seem.\nIt appears to draw upon the Radiant Man’s power is to open one’s being\nto him: the more power one draws and the more frequently one draws it the more the Radiant Man is capable of influencing, or even controlling, one’s thoughts. We have carried out extensive experimentation on the two members\nof the Radiant Man’s following of Spellcrafters when they returned to Rivel to analyse the tomes from the Archive. Their behaviour was normal, yet they wholeheartedly refuse to accept the possibility that their minds are not fully\ntheirs, and mental magical probing is being blocked by a power beyond our own.\nPart of the danger of this is the slippery slope: once one opens one’s mind to the Radiant Man the Radiant Man can influence one to draw a little more, giving\nthe Radiant Man a little more control and thus the influence required to push one to draw slightly more power. This could rapidly lead to a complete inability to refuse the commands of the Radiant Man, and hypothetically could turn into what I\nrefer to as a “Subjugant”, an individual wielding untold power via the Radiant Man yet completely slaved to his will to the point of lacking independent thought: simply an extension of the Radiant Man’s desires. Such a being could prove\nincredibly dangerous, and I recommend total disconnection from the Radiant Man of all of his Spellcrafter followers as soon as they return from their venture to the Hall.\nSenior Researcher Falyen Darylus", ""),
        StaticBook("The Red Letter", "Edward Suffolk", "[!] the letter is written in blood [!]\nLord Devereux,\nWe art writing these words with utmost anger and grief for we art betrayed by our Curonian allies. We will not use fancy language for we art beyond courtesy, our\nson Lord James was attacked and arrested by thy henchman in thy capital. If thou deem us allies or vassals and if thou further wish us to deem thee as our ally or overlord, thou will show us that we\nhave a friend in Curon and thou art a man who upholds his word. A letter our men delivered thee and the head of the elven officer he will deliver us.\nLord Edward Suffolk", ""),
        StaticBook("The Riders", "Balduul Exrith", "The Riders of W.M\n\nThe Riders of the Winged Mark is a group of Warhawkian warriors that focus upon the art of cavalry in fighting. The Riders are solely composed of the most fit and loyal Warhawkes in the tribe. Currently, the Riders of the Winged\nMark use steeds, bears, bokolos and turtles as their cavalry. The Riders supply themselves with their own unique armors, weapons and saddles made for combat. The dark elf breeder and blacksmith, Erolas, prepares the steeds and the iron and leather armors\nfor the horses. Curator Balduul, myself, is the one who provides a portion of the leather used for armors and saddles. Also, Erolas the blacksmith, provides all metal weapons that are commonly associated with the art of cavalry. Usually, the Warhawkes use\nthe powerful, two-legged avians, known as the bokolos. Unfortunately, after the migration to a settlement provided by the High-Elven peoples, a good portion of the bokolos have had to stay in the previous herd area in the Dreadlands.\nMarshalls Erolas and\nBalduul have organized some missions with other Warhawkes to bring back the bokolos to the current village. A recent boost in economic standards for the Warhawkes has allowed them to purchase bears, a new military power. The Riders of the Winged Mark was\nspecifically created to help spread the art of cavalry throughout the Warhawke tribe and to counter the Orenian army and their own riders. The Riders are based upon democratic values and swear to protect the Warhawkes at all cost.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Rope", "Isabella Jameson", "The night fell heavy on the heights of the mountains and the man could not see anything. There was zero visibility; the moon and the stars were covered by the clouds. When he was just a few feet below the top of the mountain,\nhe slipped and fell into the air, falling at great speed. He could see only black spots as he went down, and feel the terrible sensation of being sucked in by gravity.\nHe kept falling, and in those moments of great fear, all the good and bad episodes of his life came to his mind. He was thinking now about how close death was getting, when all of a sudden he felt the rope tied to his waist pull him very hard.\nHis body was hanging in the air. Only the rope was holding him. In that moment of stillness he had no choice other than to scream, “Help me GOD.\" All of a sudden, a deep voice coming from the sky answered, “What do you want me to do?”\n“Save me God.”\n\n“Do you really think I can save you?”\n\n“Of course, I believe you can.”\n\n“Then cut the rope tied to your waist.”\nThere was a moment of silence. The moment passed, and the man decided to hold on to the rope with all his strength. The rescue team says that the next day, the climber was found dead and frozen, his body hanging from a rope,\nand his hands holding it tight. He was only one foot away from the ground. How attached are we to our ropes? Will we let them go?\n\nDon’t ever doubt GOD.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sand Dread", "Falum'Lur", "Ahead, Blawharag watched as heat rose from the sands, distorting the world in waves and sinking into his flesh. It was good to be in the desert again. Blawharag had arrived to the new world on a separate boat than his Orcish brethren. Ever since\nhe had slowly been making his way to their new capital. He could feel their spirits, they were congregating somewhere in this desert. At his back Gilgamesh, his sword that had been his companion ever since the day his first clan was shattered,\nhummed happily. Clearly the Gilgamesh is as happy as I am to be in the desert once more Blawharag thought to himself. Few environments were so beautiful or so deadly as the desert. Cacti were wonderous things, green as any Orc had right to be\nand vengeful to those bold enough to touch them. Yet if you sucked down the pain, they held water inside, a reward for the strong who deserved it. In this, they are much like our women Blawharag mused to himself as he cut his palm on a nearby\ncactus, offering his blood in exchange for water. One benefit from shamanism, he had found, was that communing with cacti was far more efficient than smashing them open. Less cacti were destroyed this way and you didn't have so many prickers to\npull out afterwords.As the Orc sat and enjoyed his cactus-water, he gazed out over the desert trying to find a likely spot the Warnation would pick for a home. In the distance he saw a particular mountain range which looked like it could harbor\na valley. An easily defensible place, one opportunity no orc could pass up. He surveyed some more, getting a feel for the land and then he spied a dune shifting across the sea of sand. Not uncommon, Blawharag thought to himself, The wind shift\ndesert sands all the time. Yet something made Blawharag uneasy. He sat there, staring for a moment at the shifting dune. In moments he realized there was no wind, and only the one dune was moving. More importantly, the dune was moving towards\nhim. A mirage perhaps?Blawharag knew better than that, however. Mirages came only to those too weak for the desert or those on spiritual journeys. Blawharag was on no journey that he knew of and fresh water in ones belly kept the mirages at\nbay.\"Skah, wutevur diz am, me nub gunna lyke id am me?\" Blawharag had a nasty habit of talking to himself when on the verge of battle. He drew Gilgamesh from his back and the blade hummed loudly, hungry for battle. Quickly Blawharag set to\nmeditating, through the blade he conjured a connection to the ancestors of his shattered clan, beseeching their wisdom. Yet none knew dunes that came to life and moved of their own accord. It would seem that Blawharag was on his own today.\nBlawharag held his blade at the ready, hoping he was going to fight some creature beneath the sand and not the dune itself. I never did care to learn how to fight a sand elemental, he thought bitterly to himself. Suddenly the elements seemed far\nmore important than they had previously.As the dune shift and twisted across the sands, it appeared to pick up pace. Soon Blawharag could feel tremors in the desert around him as the dune began making a bee line to his position. As the faceless\nenemy made its final charge Blawharag let out a roar of defiance, ready to die fighting. As if in response, the dune sunk into the desert and disappeared entirely.\"Dyd me win?\" Suddenly the world exploded around sand flew up in all directions as\nthe ground beneath him leapt up and threw him into the air. He slammed back to the earth and lost his wind. Dizzily he stared blankly at the sky where the silhouette of some great winged serpent loomed over him. The world spun around him and\nsomewhere someone was making an aweful ringing sound. The shadowy god above him reared its head and some voice deep in the back of Blawharag's mind told him it was time to move. Without a second though the warrior sprang to his feet and dived\nout of the way, just as a torrent of sand came slamming down where he had been laying. Gilgamesh in hand, Blawharag ran at a frantic pace, trying to put distance between him and his assailant. Behind him the beast let out an aweful roar. The\nwhole world shook with it's mighty below and Blawharag stumbled to his knees. By the time the roar stopped, the ringing in Blaw's ears had started again. Annoyed, Blawharag turned to get a better view at his prey and quickly realized he was\noutmatched.Before him a beast as large as a mountain loomed. A serpentine creature with two massive fin-like wings and a tail that tapered into another fin shape. The monster opened its jaw to reveal a mouth large enough to swallow an entire\ncastle whole with pointed teeth the size of people. Out came another cry so load and fearsome that the desert itself quaked with fear. Blawharag released his own defiant roar but found he could not even hear himself of over the creature.\nInstead, he switched tactics.\"Skah lat!\" Blawharag hefted back Gilgamesh and threw it with all his strength. The blade soared threw the air and slammed into the monster's gaping maw. The blade found its mark, and the foe let out a cry of pain.\nAny satisfaction Blawharag might have felt at his enemies pain was quickly forgotten when the beast flicked its tail and launched itself through the air. Diving to the side with all the haste the Orc could muster, he barely escaped where the\nserpent crashed into the sand, submerging itself back into the depths. Around him a dune began to circle. Frantic, Blawharag looked around for some means of escape. There he found it: A rocky cliff jutting out above the desert. With all the\nspeed he could manage, Blawharag ran for his desperate hope at salvation.Blawharag was no less than a hundred meters from the cliff when the serpent breached the surface in front of him, crashing back into the desert and sending a wave of sand\ntowards Blawharag that knocked him onto his back. Acting on instinct, Blawharag rolled backwards and out of danger just as the predator's head emerged from the sands and snapped shut around the space where he had fallen. In moments Blawharag was\nback on his feat and running again. As he neared the cliff face he heard his pursuer leap up from the sands behind him. A shadow passed over the ground and Blawharag knew he had a fraction of a second before impact. With on last panicked jump\nBlawharag threw himself at the cliff edge. The great hulking enemy slammed into the rocky ground around the cliff and slid across. The weight of its body carried such great momentum that the beast slid straight off the cliff. Blawharag spilled\nover the ledge and caught a hold along the cliff face just in time. Below the creature tumbled into the desert below, slamming head-first into the sands and sinking into them. For a moment, Blawharag dared hope the creature had died from the\nimpact. But no sooner had he the thought than he witnessed a dune rise in the sand and make its way slowly across the desert before disappearing back into the earth.\"Wut da skah wuz dat?\" Blawharag asked as he pulled himself back up onto the\ncliff. He sat on the cliff edge catching his breath as he waited to hear Gilgamesh hum it's response. When no sound came, Blawharag reached to his back and groped fruitlessly for the blade. Even when realization dawned on him, he was still slow\nto believe it. \"KUB UV ASH SKAHUR! LAT TEEFED ME ZULT!!! ME GUNNA SKAHUN FLAT LAT!!!\"The Warnation would have to be told. If only because Blawharag was going to need help getting his Gilgamesh back. Of course there was the safety of the\nWarnation at stake too, but mostly Blawharag wanted his blade back.\n\n(Prologue to the tome: War of the Swimming Sands)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Shattered Ve", "ፕዘቿ ዕዪቿልጠቿዪ", " GAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAACXXCVVXXAFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFEEEEEEEEEEEEEaefffffffffffffffffffffffffmgamgamgamgeoeamgoangonaogngonaognogaenoganeoooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo\n EAOGMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMMM,O,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,..........DAGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGNKPPPPPPAEVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVVV\n NGAEIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIBNKNKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKKK\n AENKGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGGG\n GANEIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIIMLGADDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDDD\n GAKEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEamlmgaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaeaea", ""),
        StaticBook("The Shun", "Leyun Kameki", "The Shun\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\nAn individual who has proven to be a threat to the Druidic Order might very well be worthy of a shun. One such individual isn’t someone who a particular Druid or a select few Druids dislike or disagree with, but is someone who has offended an entire\nCircle or the Order in some way.\n\nOnly an Archdruid may make the notion to shun an individual, which is done while holding the floor at a Moot. He or she will state the reasons for presenting the shun; following, the subject of the shun, if\npresent, will answer to the accusations before the Druids of the Moot. Finally, the Inner Circle shall openly vote to pass the shun or not.\n\nOnce a shun is passed on an individual, it shall last until the Inner Circle deems it right, with only the best\ninterests for the Order, to end. No Druid of the Order is permitted to speak to a shunned individual or affiliate with them in any way and should, therefore, answer their words with “Much wind pours from your mouth.”\nA shunned individual is never allowed to step foot on the holy grounds of a grove, unless requested by an Archdruid in the case of relieving the shun, and shall be forcibly removed from a grove, by any Druid, if he or she refuses to leave. Furthermore, if\na shunned individual continuously harasses a Druid outside the grove, and the Druid or Dedicant has spoken the single statement he is permitted to speak to a shun, then hostile actions may be taken upon the individual.\nA Druid may also be shunned from the Order, and sometimes unattuned as well, which is the most dishonored action able to be taken upon a Druid. A shun is nothing to ever take lightly and any member of the Druidic Order, or the independent Circle who has\ndeemed the shun, should follow suit only the actions allowed to be taken against a shun or face consequences him or her self. Blessed be he who is righteous and loyal and true and never deserving of the shun.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Spirit of Ma", "Mysterious Oldman", "*Strange Runes seem to Dot the\nFirst section of this page*\n\nFrom death, life.\n\nFrom dDarkness Light. \nWhen all seems hopeless.\n\nand the realm stands on the brink of destruction.\n\nOne final sacrifice shall be made. \nFor the good of the realm.\n\"An excerpt of the Tome of Blundermore. The Second Wizard Of Aegis\". \n\nMagic, according to the mages is merely a tool to be used to further one's own goals and drives. There are no true moral or immoral implications of magic. Only Magic itself.\nThis is not truly the case. For we know that magic does indeed have a light and dark side, however small or large it may be. \n\nMagic is driven by impulse and imagination. By the will and tenacity of the user but it is not the will of Mages alone whom-\ndefine what magic is alone. No, for the world itself is indeed magic. Everything and everyone within it is a magical entity of some description from the most insignificant to the mighty. \n\nI subscribe to the idea that magic is a force that connects all.\nIt is emotion, it is sanity, it is insanity, it's spirituality, it's the notion of thought and imagination and perhaps life itself. \n\nTo call it a mere tool is to insult its true nature. And to pervert it with such notions that you truly understand and\ncontrol it to its fullest extent is merely being foolish. Magic is a force to be respected and revered, not as a power or force of destruction. But as a companion almost. It is with you where ever you truly go. And should be treated with respect.\nA means perhaps of attaining a greater enlightenment of the world that exists around you.\n\nIt is the will of evil men that twists magic towards evil ends. But unfortunately for all of their lust and drive for power they will forget that the secrets of\nmagic will never truly be revealed to them through such disrespect. \n\nI've seen the extent magic can provide, and it reaches far beyond our petty notions of power.\n\nWe must- adfafmkfa\n*The page seems to end with magical symbols once more, their meaning unknown before a large tear.*", ""),
        StaticBook("The Tavern", "Hobbs Burrows", "The Tavern: A Recollection of Funny Ale Stories\n\nBy Petyr Brandybuck\n\nTranscribed by Hobbs of Dunshire\nEditor's note:\nDear reader, the following text is a collection of stories from a land long forgotten, called Aegis. The proprietor of an inn called The Cat and The Fiddle was a Halfling named Petyr, who put the his experiences working in the inn\nin Al'khazar to paper. The only known survivor of Aegis in these stories is Petyr himself, who went on to become Thane of Branborough as well as author of numerous other Halfling texts. It has become my goal to have these stories remembered.\nHello all, this is Brewer Petyr. As we have all found out, some of life's funniest moments are accompanied by alcohol. As a well-known brewer, tavern owner, and merchant, I have had my fair share of these. I hope that you enjoy.\nChapter 1 - Tom\nAll of those who frequent Al'khazar know of Drunken Tom. Most do not know of him before he was an alcoholic, however...I cannot say I knew him before he was an alcoholic either. Even the first time he came to the Cat and the Fiddle, he was\ninebriated! There are many memories of Tom, but my favourite would be the time he brought a woman. I do not know whether the woman was there out of love or out of pay, but I would guess the second. Well, like most nights, Tom had a bit too much ale. He\nstarted talking about the woman's sister, who he'd apparently bedded. The woman took her pitcher and smashed it in his face! Only the Wizard knows how much prayer the monks needed to fix him up! And the worst part? She never compensated me for the glass!\nChapter 2 - The Book-Owner\nI will not mention the name of this bloke, for he might be embarassed. However, he is very involved with books. He frequents the tavern often, and I know him well. He'd always been a bit prone to over-drinking,\nbut one night, he went far. His speech was incomprehensible! He could hardly stand! I seated him down for a while, and he ended up passing out! Thankfully no guards were there to arrest him for drinking past the legal limit.\nChapter 3 - The Ghost\n\nDid you know that spirits drink? I didn't! I did know I enjoy drinking spirits...Well, one night a ghost, right before my eyes, materialises and asks for two ales! It was nasty watching the ale drip through his transparent body.\nYet, if one pays, who am I to refuse? I believe he stole the cup as well...I will haunt him until I receive that.\nChapter 4 - The Dwarf and the Guard\n\nDwarves are drinkers. We all know that. However, something about the military turns a man into a drinker as well. The inevitable result is a drinking contest between a Dwarf and an Oren Guard.\nI remember not who initiated the contest, but I damn well remember the end! It had been about twelve glasses of AppleAle each, my most potent brew. Both were on the verge of passing out, but both determined. At that point, I was handing away the beer for\nfree, for it was so entertaining. As they were drinking the thirteenth, a most surprising occurence occured. An orc shaman walks in and orders fifteen AppleAles! He drank all of them within five minutes. After watching him, both the Dwarf and the guard\npassed out! Fifteen AppleAles should incapacitate the normal man. The moral:\nDon't challenge the shamans!\nChapter 5 - The Wizard\n\nThe Wandering Wizard of Aegis walks in and orders...............\nNay, best I don't tell this story! \n\nI hope you found this delightfully entertaining. I enjoyed writing it, and look forward to more stories in the future!\nCopyrighted by Brewer Petyr.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Time Shroom", "Mr Farfoot", "*A Mark Is Set On Page 72.*\n\n...The Time Mushroom Is A Mind Bending Sight, A Mushroom Known To Travel Through Time Itself. From My Own Studies, It Seems To Have Some Connection To The Sands Of Time. I Hope To See It Ine The Days To Come!\nIt Appears Nearly Every Year, Between The Bigg'un's Fifth Months, And The Bigg'uns Sixth Month! As Far As I Know, The Best Place To Find Said Mushroom Would Be In The Desert North Of The Orcs, Near Their Oasis...\n\n-B.G. Farfoot, Historian.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Titan Golems", ".", "It's been three weeks, but it looks like NEITHER of the Titan Golems operate within Thanvar itself.\n\nHow bloody ironic! The very fortress where the Vaeyl Order garrisons its unit of Kal'Riad Golems, and the two Titan Golems aren't among them!\n\nI will need to remain searching. The two Titan Models must be SOMEWHERE. Brother Thorodus and Sister Theodus must be in ONE of the Vaeyl sites.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Utterings", "Aila Avern", "The Utterings\n\nConveyed to the Descendants through the Prophet Ashanaak, Tahariae's Chosen.\n\nTranscribed by Aila Avern, Master Cleric.\nThe Utterings of Tahariae\n\nI am the glory of the Rising Sun.\nI am the Bringer of Light. I am the Lord of Purity and the Archon of Justice. I am the Vehement Lord. I am Tahariae. Witness Me, Ashanaak, my Chosen Prophet. Witness me.\nI, the Divine Stag, He Who Walks in Pure Light, the Great Purge, have merely watched My Servants for too long. You have Divided, and Divided you shall fall.\nYou failed to Understand the Mission I had given to you, and so you have deteriorated into mere wandering healers who know only my Blessed Name. Your mockery of Faith and Piety offends Me, and so I return once more.\nWitness me, Ashanaak, My Chosen Prophet. Witness Me.\nThe Tenets of Purity\n\nShelter and protect thy brothers and sisters in Tahariae.\n\nDo not stray in thy dedication to Tahariae.\n\nGuide and protect the Descendants of the Four against the Impure.\nDo not spill the blood of the innocent.\n\nDo not use Tahariae's blessing for anything other than His will.\nThe Eight Commands\n\nAnd now, Ashanaak, I give you these Commands, that you may live a Pure life. Recite My Sacred Words to thy Brothers and Sisters, or My Blessing shall be torn from their hearts for their Sins:\nGo forth, and spread not just my Light among the Descendants, but My Words and the Truth of My Glory.\n\nGo Forth and become true Clerics among the Descendants: Scholars, protectors, and leaders, to guide the Innocent with words, justice, and wisdom.\nGo forth, and guard yourself against marriage, for service to Me demands complete and total commitment. If you do marry, do not marry those who serve Darkness and Evil, for in doing so you taint the very nature of holy matrimony.\nGo forth, and kneel before Me in maniael: private prayer, gratitude, and submission before My Glory when you awake and before you sleep.\n\nGo forth, and kneel before Me in manaakh: prayer, worship, and submission in fellowship with your Brothers and Sisters in Me once each Elven year.\nGo forth, and respect the fallen clerics who I have sent back to you, to listen and follow what they have returned to say. And when their wisdom has been imparted, that you will have the strength and courage to send them back to My Halls.\nGo forth, and follow my Chosen Prophet, for they shall be My Light in the darkness of the world for you. \n\nGo forth, and in My Blessed Name, use any means necesary to bring Purity to the Taint and Darkness that has become the world. The realm must return to how it once was, when the Four once ruled in Peace and Taint had not yet manifested.\nThrough the suffering My Mission shall bring you, remember that it is not out of Moral Good that you must do these things, but out of Necessity.\nThe Nine Woes\n\nAnd now, my Chosen Prophet, recite My Sacred Words to thy Brothers and Sisters, or My Blessing shall be torn from their hearts for their Sins:\n\nWoe to those that turn against Me and My Mission, for they must be cast out of thy ranks.\n\nWoe to those who only know Me for My Blessing, and not for My Mission, and do not recognize Me and My Glory in prayer except when My power is needed.\nWoe to those who refuse to heal the Innocent, to return to Pure form what has been rendered Impure.\n\nWoe to those who let the Impure, the Beings of Darkness and Evil, and the Descendants who bring harm to the Innocents, walk free when they cross thy path.\nWoe to those who do not recognize Me and My Glory, who do not kneel in prayer to glorify Me except when My power is needed.\n\nWoe to those who cause harm to the Innocent, for they are those you are meant to protect. \nWoe to those who are sexually immoral, who give themselves outside of the holy bed of marriage, who dirty themselves and thus dirty the Name they represent.\nWoe to those who give themselves over to perpetual drunkenness, for they dirty themselves and thus dirty the Name they represent. Such is only acceptable in celebrations and festivities.\nWoe to those who steal, cheat, and utter vulgarities, who abuse the Innocent with their tongues and hands.\nDo all that I have commanded for you to do, and do not do all I have commanded you not to do, and you shall not perish.\nNay; once suffering consume you and you leave thy mortal coil, I shall welcome you into My Sacred Halls, to forever be with Me in Purity, to forever be witness to my Sacred Light, forever and ever more.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Vaely Order", "Alkheim Guillen", "Entry One\nI, Alkheim Guillen, Sergeant of Pembrokeshire, take it upon myself to find out the truth behind the Vaeyl Order and the Cold front that has been creeping up from the south, I journy south, though I have not yet  entered the southern lands.\nEntry Two.\nI have now just entered into the cold, the snow lies upon the floor, and I feel the cold air rush from the south. I press on to reach my goal. I am not yet close to the frozen wastelands, however, every stride brings me closer to my goal.\nEntry Three \nI have entered into the cold, I immediatly feel the air around me drop in temperture, I must conserve my energy and keep warm. The nights have become harsh and brutal. I trek on, whilst keeping my senses sharp. Something watches,\nEntry Four\nI have come across a dense forest. This shows that I am not yet close to the Ice Wall, for plants still grow. I have also come across a lake, which I have discovered to be frozen solid. The ice easily holds my weight as I cross.\nEntry Five\nI have come to the end of the forest, close to my destination. The forest has suddenly stopped and given way to slopes of Ice, sleet, and snow. I am given no protection from the falling snow, or the howling wind. I must keep warm.\nEntry Five\nIs it luck or Provedince, that I lay down to sleep not far from what I seek. I wake this very  morning, to discover that the light has not changed, However, I see an encampment. And I see the banners. The banners I seek. The sign of the Vaeyl\nOrder. I must tread carfully. I know not what type of weapons the may carry, I will carefully wait until nightfall to creep into the encampment.\nEntry seven\nNight has fallen. I now creep into the camp, however, noone appears to be around. I look through every tent for any form on information, however to no avail. I do see a portal, a strange portal. With the orders sign. I must enter to know.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Veil: I", "Artemis", "The Veil Cracks\n\n \nIt were as it once was. The void mages saw the symbols. They saw the code. Along with it, two voices, as if in conversation.\nWe are close\nThe Veil will be undone. This is our only option.\n\nWhat awaits them?\n\nAre we so sure they will even find it?\n\nIf we do not have hope, then why should they?\nThey need no hope. They need only to destroy it.\nIf they cannot. All is truley lost.\nThere had been multiple visions in the past, but this one was different. The code was was larger along with more difficult. Well so it seemed. \n\nThe code went years without being solved.  It got me curious and so I proceeded to get a voidal mage frie\nof mine to write down what she heard and saw. Then began the task of cracking the code.\n\nThe code required research into the those that were shown previously to the void mages. One major difference with the newer code was its use of how light broke u\nSimilar to how a rainbow works. The six colours. Red. Blue. Green. Yellow. Cyan. Purple. Yellow, cyan and purple were mixes of the other three and from that pattern noticed, it took a good year or so, But I finally cracked it. It read the following.\nThe splinters of the wheel scattered in the cosmic wind.\n\nAnd as the watcher grew weaker with every passing silencing of a star- The celestial chorus grew louder.\nBlinded by the third and the seventh- the stars rose up to defy the watchers will.\n\nThe watchers task was to end and with it the watchers sorrow began.\nThe watchers machination was folly and the sea of souls and its mark beyond reach.\n\nThe stars became free once more- The first age with a second birth.\nThe first age drew ever longer as they returned from the other side back to the first.\n\nWith a flash of brilliant light wrath and mercy were unshackled from their bounds.\n\nThe clash of two did begin once more.\nThe sea of souls and the falling of the few weighed heavy on the minds of the stars who knew.\n\nThus wrath did seal his hellish home within a veil top reserve that which gave the fragments life.\nThe boon wrath did protect and preserve well.\n\nAnd so the watcher stares once more- Their return brought a schemes demise.\n\nYet truth still rings clear.\nTo break the veil and meet the mark and end the wrath bringers fury.\nWhat it meant, I had no idea. It spoke of 'The first age' in the seventh verse. Could it possibly be referring to the first Mathic Age?\n\nSolving the code did not go without answer. I then heard the voices. Most likely the same voices that the\nvoid mages heard upon first seeing the code.\nI have hope. One will answer. It seems they have been able to understand our messages before.\n\nWithout them, my work is in vain. They must be there when the Veil is unraveled.\nSo the listener shall learn?\n\nThe listener shall learn. As your will stands.\nWith that, my vision went blurry. Myself, and those around me were taken from the ground we stood upon and placed into a cavern. Nothing like I had ever seen.\nTo Be Continued\n    in next book\n\n\n\n\n-Artemis", ""),
        StaticBook("The Void", "Logan Deleroth", "Chapter 1\nA Breakdown on the Void\n\nThe void, simply put, is incomprehensible to those with wills not strong enough to handle the concept of it's existence. The void itself is a realm that all magic originates from, and to all magic returns.\nIt is a realm where everything and yet nothing exist at the same time. One may ask how, however the answer is not known. The void is very similar to a mind, it can be melded by learning different forms of knowledge.\nA very common scripture is used to describe the void when being taught about to novice mages. \"The void is everything, yet nothing. Like our imagination, it may be dull and empty; or full and colorful.\" This is because the void exists purely to be shaped.\nIn order to connect oneself to the void, they must first be completely connected to their mind. This is why people under the age of sixteen are unable to access the void without causing damage themselves, because their minds aren't fully developed.\nThe void is the source of mana in every person, and as such it is infinite. When properly access, one may be able to properly cast magic nigh perfectly. This is the basics of the void.\nChapter 2\nA Breakdown on Mana\n\nMana, whether known about or not, is in every single being. Some may refer to it by different names, like 'chi,' or 'chakra.' Mana is, in lame man's terms, the life energy in all beings, alive and dead alike.\nMana is the means by which mages cast their magic, and as such have more access to it than average people such as a warrior or an archer. It allows the user to invoke the magics we see used on a daily basis, such as lightning, air, ice, and fire.\nThose that have proper control over the void have proper control over their mana, and can cast their magics at will. The reason for this, is that the mind and the void are so close in nature that they are almost exact parallels.\nIf one has a strong mind and expansive knowledge, they have a strong connection to the void and an extensive mana pool. The mana pool of a person relfects directly upon the amount of knowledge they contain, and how well they are able to access it.\nNormally nonmages have something called, 'passive mana,' which his how they have special abilities such as being able to perform minor illusions, or granting themselves small buffs to their own strength to aid them in combat. This is why mana is important\nChapter 3\nA Breakdown on Elemental Magic\n\nThe elements are often manipulated in a manner that bestows power unto those that do so. Because of this, the overall existence of the elements is directly influenced by the void.\nWhen one calls upon the power of the elements, they also call upon the power of the void. Every element has it's own individual type of energy that is different and yet the same as the previous. This is why they can constantly exist in the world.\nThe existence of these elements is constant, and infinite. So long as the world moves onward, so too will the elements that embody the aspects of the void. One might even be able to compare the emotions of a living being to the nature of these elements.\nThe existence of the elements is much similar to the human mind as well, in the figurative sense. Each element has it's own aspect that can be used to represent the emotions of oneself. They all revert back to the exact same theorem in the end.\nThe mind is the reason for everything modern that exists, such as buildings or magic. This is because us as mortals have evolved into something greater than the primitive mind that used to exist, so many years ago.\nChapter 4\nA Breakdown on the Elements\n\nAs previously stated, the elements are directly linked to the void and therefore the mind. The elements can be easily manipulated, exactly like emotions, if one can properly wield the void.\nFire - Fire can be looked at like anger. If not controlled properly it can spread like a cancer, and overtake you completely until you are spiralling out of control like a massive destructive force capable of doing extreme damage to your surroundings.\nWater - Water can be looked upon as being calm, yet at the same time capable of an extremely destructive rage. You are always capable of finding a way through, yet if it is too forced you can lose your very being.\nAir - Air can be looked at as cunning, giving one an advantage in combat so that they may either escape or fatally wound their opponent. If used properly, one could easily knock out their opponent, but if one loses control they could destroy themselves.\nLightning - Lightning can be looked at as being spontaneous. It is precise, and yet at the same time extremely destructive. If not properly struck, it could leave you wide open for something else to come, including another element.\nChapter 5\nA Summary\n\nFor those that wish to start upon the path to magic, they must first learn about the void and how it links itself to the mind and the thoughts of human beings. If the void is not properly controlled.\nThose that do not have the mental capacity to wield the void can cause great harm to themselves, and by extension others around them. The only way to properly wield the void is by learning from another so that they have the advantage of experience.\nThe void and the mind must be completely in tune with one another in order to prevent extreme damage to themselves. Some look at the void as chaotic, and unlawful. Yet each form of magic, Druidity, Magedom, and Divinity magic, has it's own form of chaos.\nPeople may not realize this because the fear of the elements suddenly colliding between eachother, and destroy the world. However the very existence of gods is destructive can cause the same thing. The same can be said for druidity.\nNature is chaotic, and wild. It is unpredictable, and in my opinion the most destructive of the magics as they could completely tear the roots of the world itself from their individual places. This is why every single magic must be controlled.\nCopyright 1672 - Logan Deleroth.\n\nFor Epsilon Hallowfall.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Void", "Laureh'thill", "The Void\n\nBy Kalameet Izalith\n\n-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-\n-The Void: Arcane magic is the archetype or magic which is fueled by the Void, or more specifically mana. The void is an empty plane of existence where things may be created with\nimagination and willpower. Many teachers of the Arcane often teach students with the following proverb: \"The Void is nothing, yet everything. Like our imagination, it may be dull and empty; or it can be full and colorful.\". The Void as a whole is simply a\nplane where nothing exists, unless the mage makes it exist.\n\n-The Anchor and Connection: Before you can make anything in the Void, you must first connect to it. This obviously means a basic line of communication must be established, generally gained\nthrough meditation and practice. This connection reaches into the Void and through this connection, you manipulate the Void in a very specific way. This manipulation is when you imagine something in the Void. For example, one may create/imagine a fireball\nin the Void, you'd then attempt to pull this fireball from the void into the real world. When you pull on this fireball you are inherently using mana from your own mana pool, and you create something called an Anchor. This mana anchor is what holds your\nspell, or fireball in this case, in the real world.\n\n-Mana: Mana is sightless and is as invisible as the air in our world. It flows through our world like streams, and is in every living thing, whether it is plants or animals. Although mana comes at\ncost, since it flows through people, Void users have gained the ability to use this mana to draw from the Void. Void users often get fatigued when over using mana, and have in rare cases died to the use of large amounts of mana.\n\nAnother drawback wit\nuse of mana is the effect (or lack thereof) on our mortal plane, when you draw on the Void for magicks such as Evocations, this element which has been evoked must eventually return to the Void. However this can become complicated with such magicks as\nAlteration, as it has the ability to prolong the existence of Void based elements in our world. Mana comes in three states; passive, active/used, and aura.\n\n-States of Mana:\n*The first is a state of passive mana. This is the mana which is already\nwithin all beings and plants alike. It cannot be manipulated by anyone aside from its owner.\n\n*The second is a state of active/used mana. This mana has been given a purpose (a spell), or has been stored inside a mana gem, and thus cannot be used like\npassive mana ever again. This is exactly why the famous \"Mana Bettery\" is impossible, and cannot be done. Once mana has been expelled from ones being forcefully, it cannot be regained. But it can be redirected, this is known by any competent Alterationist\n*The third and final is the well known state of aura. An aura directly reflects a mages personality through its color, which will be listed below this section. Auras are generally harmless and are simply a way of self expression. Aura is indeed harmless,\nand is expelled naturally by a mage, and all living things to some degree, but more so by those who are using their mana. The more mana you use to cast a spell, the more aura which is expelled from the user (Very much like a fire. The more wood you burn,\nthe bigger the smoke cloud is). There are only two beings which are capable of using aura, the first being an Arcane Evocationist to some degree, and a Shade. Although a shade literally consumes aura, in which case can become very dangerous when one uses\na large portion of their mana whilst combating such a creature.\n\n-Aura Colors:\nBlue: Calculatedness and logicallity (Sometimes emotional coldness)\nPurple: Mysteriousness\nWhite: Benevolence, order and innocence\nBrown: Nurturing and car\n(sometimes optimism)\nRed: Dominance, power and control (Sometimes tyrannical natures)\nGreen: Harmony and balance (Sometimes vanity)\nBlack: Chaos and malevolence\n\n-Mana Pools: Mana pools are how much mana we have in our person, and this de\ngrand our spells can be, along with the duration a spell can be held in our world. Mana pools are governed by two things; skill level and Magic type. Skill level is simply how skilled you are at manipulating mana for your specific Sub-type. For example;\nthe longer you train in the use of Evocations, the better and more efficient you are at manipulating mana for that sub-type. Magic type is a little more complicated, different magic Sub-types are naturally more mana consuming than others, a few examples\nof very draining subtypes are as followed: Alteration, Arcane Evocation, and Conjuration. Although far more difficult to learn if one of these are your first Sub-type, you will naturally get a bigger mana pool than someone whose first Sub-type was\nIllusion, or perhaps an Evocation.\n\n-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-~-", ""),
        StaticBook("Theory Infinity", "Jaya Jayamen", "A Theory of Infinity\n\n     ~Originally by\n        Geedin Jayamen\n\n     ~Transcribed by\n          Jaya Jayamen\nLately I have begun to think about how things are connected. Take a rug for example. We see it as just one rug, but that one rug is made up of smaller things. Wool or string, which in turn is made of smaller fibers.\nI think that things get smaller, maybe even infinitely.\n\nJust as things can be made of smaller things, so can smaller things make up one big thing. Again with the rug example.\nAll of those fibers make up wool or string, which make the rug. You may think it stops there, but what is the difference between fibers to a rug then to a rug being a part of a house?\nThe rug isn’t physically sewn into the house, yet it is part of it, the same as the fibers not being part of a rug until it is sewn into one.\nThis begins a theory of Infinity. Let me give another example. Apples and oranges. They are different, right? Well that is all a matter of perspective. Apples may be different then oranges, but they can still be grouped into what we call fruits.\nEven everything in the world, with its infinite different parts and pieces, can be grouped into what we call, well, the world.\nNow let’s get a bit deeper. What is the difference between yourself and someone else? Well, there are differences, but there are also similarities. Well let’s think, what would make you two the same?\nWell the thing is, you are part of something that doesn’t make you the same, but groups you into one thing.\nYou may be asking, how are we connected? I may ask you the opposite, how are we disconnected? As a rug is made up of fibers, so are you made up of flesh and bone.\nIf everything can be made up of infinitely smaller things and infinitely bigger things can be made of those smaller things, what does that leave, but the fact of infinity?\n\nThe End\nThank you for reading the Jayamen family’s books! If you have any feedback or enjoyed reading, please let me, Jaya Jayamen (( Sofetios )), know. Peoples responses help me write more books! Thanks again! ~Jaya Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("TheWitchsMarsh", "Domainoft", "The Witches Marsh, Told by Nienna Calm\nNienna: Have you ever heard of a place called \"The Witches Marsh\"?\nIt's a small swampland outside near Malinor. It's dark and gloomy place. I paid\nit a visit one evening, Looking for some more Mandragora\nLeaf. Though, when I\nfirst came to it the only thing I could find was a warning of the dangers\ninside.\nI ignored the warnings, Unfortunently. I thought it was just the nearby\nhalflings trying to ward people away\nfrom there vale. I was very very wrong. I\ngot lost almost immediatly as I entered the marsh. It was dark, the trees\nclouded the path ahead, and the ground made it hard to walk at all. I tried to\nmake it to the base of a nearby moutain, but as I\nreached the base I slipped\nand fell into a cave littered with webs. I was covered by them almost\ninstantly. Webs seemed to cling to the walls, the ground, everywhere. You would\nthink that walking back up looked like\nmore trouble than it was worth.\nSo I tried to look further in, to see if it was a through passage. I took no\nmore than two steps before I found myself in the middle of a large Cavern. The\ncavern was Punctuated by a single, slanted\nspike in the center. It was of a\nmaterial I'd never seen before. It was odd and slightly pale. I cut my way\nthrough more of the webs, and dropped into the room. I checked the material and\ntook a sample or two as well, but then I\n...heard something behind me. it was a\nsqueltch. Coming from a smaller alcove attached to the room I was in. I hadn't\nmuch in the way of weapons at the time. So i drew my crude stone axe annd tried\nto find the source. As soon as I was inside the\nsecond cavern though I heard a\nhiss. It's liek what the spiders make but lower..deeper. The sound came from\ndirectly above me, and as I looked up to see it. I found that i'd walked\nbeneath a spider as tall as that wall ovre there is high\n\"20ft\".\nAs soon as I heard it, it was on me. It attacked me as soon as I saw it. It\nhunched down, and tried to pin me beneath it while tring to stick it's fangs\ninto me. I was fast enough to jump away, but the spider sliced my lower\narm\nopen with one of it's fangs. I looked around the room and found that I was in\nthe larger atrium with the slanted spike in the center. I hadn't time to climb\nout of the room again, so I made for the spike. It had a flat area on the top\nof it and I managed to make my wau up it. Though unfortunently the spider was\nstill on my heels. I ran to the tip of it as fast as I could, lept, aiming for\nthe entrance to the room. Thankfully, Since I'm still here speaking to you I\nmade it. Then I rummaged through my bag for my last vial of alchemist flame,\nand threw it on the ground.\nAs soon as I got out, I fell over again. The sider was poisonous. I did what I\ncould to apply a tournoquet, and wandered back\ninto the Witch Marsh. What I\nfound was a house. I passed out immediately as I entered. To my luck, I woke up\nwith Savictus the Druid, looking down at me. Apparently he lives in those\ncursed marshes because of the\ntaint present there. He saved my life, and\nremoved the posion. And that is how I lived through a giant spider attack.\n\n-Leyu'Maehr\nVaelhaven\n*Strange Numbers\n((3/3/13)", ""),
