        StaticBook("Thomas Tantrum", "Beelzebub", "There was once a boy, he was named Thomas.\n\nThomas had a hot temper.\n\nThomas' mother warned him.\n\n\"Thomas, if you continue to be so wrathful, your head will pop like a balloon!\"\nThomas yelled at his mother.\n\n\"I do not need your advice! I do not have the patience for it!\"\n\nThomas stomped and yelled and walked away.\n\nHe was one angry boy.\nThe next day, Thomas came upon a boy playing with a toy.\n\nHe grew naughty.\n\n\"Your toy is dumb! And so are you!\"\n\nThomas knocked the toy out of the young boy's hand, breaking it.\n\nHe was one bad boy.\nThomas' head grew rounder.\n\nIt became a shade of red.\n\nHis voice became squeakier.\nThomas' mother warned him once again.\n\n\"Your head will pop, Thomas!\"\n\n\"That is what happens to mean boys!\"\n\nBut Thomas did not listen.\n\nHe ctomped and yelled and walked away.\nThe next day, Thomas came upon a boy waiting in line for something to eat.\n\nHe grew naughty.\n\n\"Give me your money!\"\n\nThe boy gave Thomas all he had.\n\nThomas was one big bully.\nThomas went home.\n\nHe looked in the mirror.\n\nHis head was a balloon!\n\"Help! My head, my head is a balloon!\"\n\nThomas called out. But his voice was too squeaky.\n\nHe stomped and yelled and stomped and yelled.\n\nUntil his head went 'pop'!", ""),
        StaticBook("Thorland", "Nerak Frostbeard", "Thorlond Frostbeard is an ambitious and eager dwed that has been an excellent chess opponent to me. He is always curious and I believe he will do well to study runesmithing.\n\nI, Nerak Frostbeard, High Prelate uv the Ar Yemarin Anaros give support to him.", ""),
        StaticBook("Thoromir", "Xalid", "Thoromir,\n\nThe blade before you was forged by me for your upcoming betrothal. The process for forging this blade has been in my family for generations and is used for the wedding of a relative.\nYou welcomed this broken stranger into your home with open arms and for that you are my brother.\n\nTwo metals were used in the process to represent you and Valencia. The charcoal infused in the blade represents the bond you have formed.\nThe blade itself represents how the combining of the three elements creates something stronger than they are alone.\n\nMay your love and bond be as strong as the blade carrying your symbol.\n\n-Xalid", ""),
        StaticBook("Thorvn's Feaths.", "Thorvn Bronwyn", "", ""),
        StaticBook("Threat, Volume I", "Varil'ja", "Concievable Threats to Haelun'or.\n\nKypris'dionne - Kypris is a known Blood Mage, Shade, as well as a Mental Mage. I have known her to be mostly mentally unstable. She wears Blindfolds frequently and uses disguises to keep herself from being found.\nVaren'thal - Varen's sanity is questionable- he was husband to Gwyneth and may have planned for many things to occur within Haelun'or with her. He is powerful within magical arts such as Arcanism- this will be updated. He is to be seen as suspicious.\nYsmay - Ysmay is chaotic as well as being incredibly dangerous- she is a Frost Witch and must not be allowed to enter the city. She frequently uses blindfolds and a cane, having the ability to disguise herself as a Mali'aheral, as most Frost Witches do.\nGwyneth - Gwyneth is an unstable Soul Puppeteer, being skilled within Soul Puppetry as well as Blood Magic. She is to be killed upon sight, and that is final. Any people who accompany her are to be immediately captured and put in solitary confinement.\nRilath - Rilath is a mysterious figure, however having been seen in Devirad, he has been seen to be using his house as a form of hospitality for many non-aherals, and is suspected of having intercourse with a Valah. Potential Shade Father/culture threat.\nCrumena Iyliar - Crumena, being the brother of Rilath, has been accused and proven to be a traitor within the past. As of recent, he has been known to appear for brief periods of time, remaining far away from anyone else, before disappearing. Threat.\nVelulaei'Ilum - Former advisor of the Court within Oren, Velulaei has been recognised as a possible Mali'aheral homosexual. Threat to Culture.\nThalrian - Thalrian is a Dark Elf, not much known about him except for his trickery and his magical ability. He has dark green eyes and black, neck-length hair. Not to be trusted, to be watched at all times whilst in Haelun'or.\nBand of Spooks - A band of Spooks, having previously raided the Haelun'or Library before attacking Arelion (Okarir'thilln), should be prevented from entering the city at all costs. If seen, they must be immediately removed- use Holy Magic on them.\nCahir - A red-haired Mali with sky-blue eyes, Cahir has been caught murdering Odessa Visaj and leaving her in the river. If seen, to be arrested and kept in highest prison security possible before put on trial for his actions.\nArtimec - Artimec has been reported in the past to have harrassed a member of the Sillumiran, an Officer known as Solaria. After the events of the band of Spooks, Solaria had been hurt and Artimec went and took her, letting her go after fooling.\nSataric - Sataric is a threat due to his concieved anger towards Hengest, the cleric. He wishes to kill Hengest, and has been dealt with once, but may return once more. If seen, he must be watched closely at all times, being very dangerous. Be on guard.", ""),
        StaticBook("TicTacToe Rules", "Jaya Jayamen", "Tic Tac Toe\n           Rules\nTic Tac Toe is a simple 2 player game. It is played on a 3x3 grid. Both players roll a 20 sided dice to see who goes first, The player with the higher roll goes first. (( use /roll 20 )).\nDecide which player gets red tokens and which player gets blue tokens. Each player must have different tokens then the other. On the first turn, the player puts one of their tokens in one slot of the 3 by 3 grid.\nThen the other player puts down one of theirs in the 3 by 3 grid in an unoccupied space. Then the first player goes again putting a token in the 3 by 3 grid in an unoccupied space,\nthen the other player goes again putting one of their tokens in an unoccupied space in the 3 by 3 grid, and it continues like that alternating turns until one player gets three of their tokens in a row either horizontally,\nvertically, or diagonally. The game also ends if all the slots of the 3 by 3 are filled. If the 3 by 3 is filled and no player got 3 in a row, then the game is a tie.", ""),
        StaticBook("Time's up", "Mika Uialben", "I am done playing games.\nyour time is up.\n\nEnjoy your time for now.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- The Red Baron\n                     [MU]", ""),
        StaticBook("Titan Guide", "?", "TITAN OPERATIONAL MANUAL\nTITAN_1\nSISTER THEODORUS\n-------------------Note: Please do not attempt to exceed your ID's basic permissions without contacting a member of the 4th Banner.\n\nSister Theodorus is to be expressly\nutilized as a security tool in order to maintain the vigil over the Drakaar threat for all eternity. Following the incident of 204, the Cooking Function has been removed.\n\nAfter stating your ID, please ask for a list of possible commands in order to\nenable your permission access from the Titan.\n\n-4th Banner Titan Team.", ""),
        StaticBook("Title", "Jakob Ludvik Ludovar III", "Dear Mister King,\n I, Lord Jakob Ludvik Ludovar the 3rd hereby ask for a title! I am of age. I am ten years old and I can manage my own land too! Please consider this!\n\n Many Thanks,\nLord Jakob of the Pumpkins", ""),
        StaticBook("TO - Kelly", "Ser Uthred Gromach", "To Mister Kelly,\nI have found a few people part of the Rhysten Smithy which are associated with a strange... organisation. I write to you because I have found in my investigations that you are all Vampyres. I will contact you and await your letters, I\nto truly become immortal. Please help me with this quest, please do so. Mister Kelly, I will offer you everything to become a true immortal, I am in your service.\n\n- Ser Uthred Gromach", ""),
        StaticBook("To Ajax.", "Vallakai", "Sir Ajax:\nI'm sorry. You are honorable, but I can't agree with you. You said death to the heathens, while I am one. I hope you will learn. I am not honorable. May your days be in peace. I will think of you.\n           -Vallakai.", ""),
