        StaticBook("To Arganos", "Maladem Uuthlini", "To Arganos\nBy Maladem Uuthlini\n\nProud Uuthlini, raise the flagon!\nSet the table for the feast!\nGather all by boat and wagon,\nAll your kin from west to east!\nCall your fellow ker together!\nLet no beast nor Undead thrall,\nNor any sort of fearsome weather,\nKeep them from the banquet hall!", ""),
        StaticBook("To Bailey", "Holy Ser Evan Abdiel", "ERP is a bannable offence.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Be a Cleric", "Aerith Oranor", "A Beforehand Note:\n\nI have gathered the following information from some of the old books I’ve collected and the time I’ve spent reading in the many libraries of different lands. (continued on next page)\nThe following is an interpretation of my own based on what I’ve read about Tahariae and his will.\nWhat is a cleric? A cleric is one calls upon the powers of their Aengul, Tahariae to heal the sick and injured and purge that which is impure and evil.\nA cleric is to serve Tahariae and enforce his will. To enforce his will is to insure the world is perfect, devoid of that which is unnatural, unnecessary and most of all, impure.\nWhat a Cleric should live by:\nThe Words of Tahariae is something a cleric must always follow and is something that a cleric must live by.\nFirst a cleric must always follow the Five Tenets of Tahariae. These are the most basic orders of The Lord of Light. In regards to the first tenet, a cleric must protect his fellow clerics and provide them with aid when needed.\nIn regards to the second tenet, a cleric must always be dedicated to Tahariae, to stray away from Tahariae is a grave mistake. In regards to the third tenet, a cleric is to guide and help the four descendant races and\nlead them against that which is impure. In regards to the fourth tenet, a cleric must always avoid spilling the blood of those who are innocent. In regards to the fifth tenet, a cleric must only use his powers for enforcing Tahariae’s  will and nothing\nelse. These five tenets are core to a cleric and should dictate how a cleric lives and what he does.\nThe Eight Woes are also extremely important to a cleric. In regards to the first woe, a cleric must always follow the Tahariae and his mission. In regards to the second woe, a cleric shouldn’t know Tahariae for his blessing but know him\nfor his mission and his glory and must enforce it. In regards to the third woe, a cleric is to always heal those in need and must purify that which is impure. n regards to the forth woe, a cleric must slay any impure being, creature of darkness or evil\nthe moment they come across them, in order to prevent the innocent from being harmed. In regards to the fifth woe, a cleric must never harm the innocent, to do this is to go against a cleric’s purpose of defending them. In regards to the sixth woe,\na cleric must be moral when it comes to intercourse, for such actions must be avoided outside of a marriage, a cleric must do this to avoid tarnishing what they represent.  In regards to the seventh woe, a cleric is to avoid alcohol\nunless during a festivity or celebration, they must do this to avoid tarnishing what they represent. and finally the eight woe, a cleric must never steal from others, cheat others and say profanities.\nNow onto the Eight Commands which tell a cleric what they are to do in order to live well. In regards to the first command, a cleric must spread Tahariae’s light, beliefs and glory amongst the descendants.\nIn regards to the second command, a cleric must be a teacher, protecter and to the descendants and guide them at all times. In regards to the third command, a cleric should avoid marriage so that they can dedicate themselves completely to Tahariae\nif they do marry however, a cleric must avoid marrying one who serve darkness and evil. In regards to the forth command, a cleric must always pray to show to Tahariae to show devotion, gratitude or submission after they wake up and before they sleep.\nIn regards to the fifth command, a cleric must always pray alongside his fellow clerics once every elven year. In regards to the sixth command, a cleric must listen to the words and knowledge imparted by fallen clerics.\nIn regards to the seventh command, the words of the Prophet Ashanaak should be listened to by a cleric, it is the light in the dark for the cleric. Finally in regards to eight command, a cleric may and must use any means necessary to\nenforce Tahariae’s will. A cleric must eradicate the taint and darkness that corrupts the world and must return the world to how it was before the taint and darkness. A cleric does not do this out of sheer kindness,\na cleric does this because it is necessary.\nFinally the Revelation of Hope. As long as a cleric does what Tahariae has commanded what to do and what not to do, the cleric will persist. By doing this a cleric will eventually reach Tahariae’s Halls,\nthis is one of the goals other than making the world pure again that a cleric should aspire for.\nNow, what boons can a cleric be granted and what can they do with these boons? A cleric is granted the power to wield Tahariae’s light, to a certain extent. They can use this light to heal those in need or slay beings that are impure,\nserve the darkness or serve evil. In regards to healing, a cleric must always heal those in need. To ignore those who require healing is to go against the purpose of a cleric. In regards to combatting evil a cleric must always slay impure and\ndark creatures the moment they come across them, to not do this is also going against the purpose of a cleric. In the end though, the ultimate purpose of a cleric is to serve Tahariae, enforce his will and nothing more.\nWhy is that I wish to become a cleric? I have lived for two hundred fifty five years now, in those years I have seen thousands upon thousands of innocent people slain, butchered, destroyed by beings that are impure, unnatural and dark.\nThe creatures didn’t care who or what they killed, whether they be old or young they were slain. The greatest moment of evil I had seen in my life though was when I was fleeing Anthos, one of the lands I lived in more than a century ago.\nMany of us fled because of an abomination called the Black Scourge which was made up of many unnatural unholy beings which threatened the descendants living there. It had destroyed entire cities and kingdoms.\nAfter seeing such a thing and seeing the countless atrocities committed by impure beings I’ve grown tired of being unable to effectively combat those beings. Tahariae’s mission is one that will allow me to further protect the innocent\nand slay the creatures that threaten them. If it means dedicating myself to the Lord of Light, I am willing to do it.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Dilory Lada", "Analee", "My good friend Dilory, I'm sorry i did this to you. But my life wasn't worth living anymore. Me and larry split loraine died, there was so much that happened. I just gave up. You were my greatest friend. I am glad i met you. I know this will be very hard\nfor you but please accept that i am happy now. I have no more pain or disappointment or depression because of everything that is happening. I love you as a friend dilory. I'm sorry you had to know this. But this is what happens to good people they get\ntired and decide maybe its time to rest. I've gotten tired and lets just say i'm finally resting now. I'm at peace with everything. Again i'm sorry. Love Kacey", ""),
        StaticBook("To Elitesy", "Malik Azarath", "Best *strikethrough*\nGreeti *strikethrough*\nGood da *strikethrough*\nHey hoi *strikethrough*\nHello Elitesy\n\nI wanted to ask you if you \nwould like *strikethrough*\nwant to *strikethrough* \nwould mind going to the \nmasqa *strikethrough*\nMasqer *strikethrough\nmasquerade with me.\n\n*the rest has clearly been added later and is a lot more sloppy*\n\nCause you know it might be dangerous with all those creepy people showing up and the Uialben's so called \"plan\". I wouldn't want you to accidentally get\nstabbed or poisoned  or eaten or drowned or anything else that is lethal.\n\nI really hope you consider it.\n\n~ Mala *strikethrough*\nMalik, the innkeeper, if you forgot who I was.", ""),
        StaticBook("to Hearth Guard", "Simon Birchenwald", "Hearth Guard-\n\nI've two Observations\nto share.\n\nFirstly, there is an Orc wandering the city.\nHe goes by 'The Scaddernack' or 'Xugulg' or just 'Xug'.\nI am not sure whether you know of his presence. He hasn't done much yet, but\nI thought it would be useful for you to know that he is here.\n\nSecondly, there is a Man wearing an odd mask shaped like the head of some strange Bird. He claims to be here with 'business', but when I asked him about it he said that he was simply visiting\na friend and began to shake visibly. I am not sure whether this is a matter prudent enough to investigate- just thought it was interesting enough to report.\n\nIf this Paper has been useless, feel free to burn it or something.\nSincerely,\n\nS. Birschenwald\n\n((The letter seems to be written hastily, which would explain the misspell of the author's name.))", ""),
        StaticBook("To Larry", "Sophia Rabbitfoot", "[!] A Small Note, Written in black ink, and scraggly cursive would appear in your mailbox.\n\"Dear Larry,\"\n\"I'm truly sorry for leaving you. . though it did not feel right to marry a man I do not love. .\"\n\"I mean this in a rather good, not teasing manner to tell you I am happy now, living with the good people of Blackreach.\"\nSincerely, \nSophia Rabbitfoot", ""),
        StaticBook("To Larry", "Unknown", "What you have done is unforgivable.\n\nShe only needed you in that hard moment.\n\nYou let her die, you should meet your end aswell.\n\nDon't you think?", ""),
        StaticBook("To Mages Guild", "Aristania Atmorice", "Dear Whom it may concern,\n\nI have a request about a particular type of magic. i know out kingdoms may be warring right now but maybe this can be the first steps to estblishing a friendship. i live part time within your city after all.\ni dont want to be a problem or cause any. if you would be willing to give me some information and possibly some training it would be helpful. thank you very much in advance. \n\nSincerely Aristania Atmorice of Fenn", ""),
        StaticBook("To Mangus", "Fay", "Dear Mangus \n\nI'm so sorry how i rushed out on you the other day, I know that you love me and you think I'm the one, but you will have to try and move on, forgive me \n\n-Fay (imagine a super awesome signiture)", ""),
        StaticBook("To Merialeth", "Pruinae Tathvir", "Dear Merialeth,\nWhen you get the chance, I would gladly like to take lessons from you on becoming a medic. I have been reading a bit up on it in the Sutica library and a bit when I went to Caras Elder to help with the fight against the September Prince,\nbut books aren't as good or as thurough at teaching as hands on or learning from a teacher. I would greatly appreciate if you could teach me, but if not I understand. \nThank you for being a role model and great family member!\nSincerely,\nPruinae T.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Mr Kastrovat", "Thomas Ironmoore", "To the owner of this establishment.\nGood day, my name is Thomas Ironmoore, and I am the Blacksmith here. I see that you have quite a quantity of iron, in which i would like to strike a deal.\nI am in constant need of iron, for tools, armor and swords but..\nI seem to run out almost instantly. That is why I would like to make you an offer. You supply my shop and me with iron, and I will sell the tools and pay back the worth of the iron and a bit more when I sell my merchandise. I strive to be able to do my...\njob, but yet again, I lack the materials to make it. Anyway, to reiterate, you supply me with iron, i sell it as tools and you get back what the iron was worth and a bit more.\nI will give you time to think about it, but write back to me when you have...\ncome to a decision. If you have any criticisms or problems; if you agree that is, do tell me.\nGood day.\n\n\n\n\n\nYours sincerely,\n   Thomas Ironmoore.\nOOC: My IGN is LegendShine btw.", ""),
        StaticBook("To my Chieftess", "Rulan Ryvienne", "Book of Poetry and Songs\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTo Chieftess Arabella\nPrecious\n\nOh I met this girl\nSo beautiful in the eyes\nA gem to this world.\nI desire her love\nIt lifts me up\nAnd i fly like a dove.\nShe is so precious to me\nAnd I desire her love to set me free.\nWith a voice so soothing\nAnd a mind so enchanting\nHer being is lovely \nand its got me prancing\nHer being is a treasure\nHer love is a pleasure\nOh my heart needs her\nI just want to kiss her\nOcean Blue\n\nI dream of world\nSo bright and blue\nTo find my passion\nA journey so true\nSo I set on way\nAcross the seven seas\nA path so perilous\nIt is my destiny.\nI told my mother\nI may not come home\nRecord my story\nwithin this tome.\nThe ocean is my abode\nThe waves my road\nMy journey has begun\nAnd towards it I lunge.\nWarhawkian Tale\n\nIn the city of Khel'seth\nYou'll find the world's best\nStronger than them all\nand better than the rest.\nA nation so free\nNo chains to lock thee\nA place of pure union\nfor all to make communion\nBokolos run wild\nThe wind blows through the isles\nThe Warhawkes are my home\nIts where I go.\nIts where I found home\nIts where the clans i know\nWe are all family\nUnited they stand with me\nA bond stronger the steel\nAnd love so deep and real\nThe Warhawkes are my home\nIts where I go\nLost in Paradise\n\nLost in Paradise\nWhy is it so nice\nThe sun shines\nThe place is so bright\nHow can it be\nA place so free\nHow can it exist \nIts where I want to be\nParadise is no place\nIt is no land\nParadise is no city\nBut I grab her hand\nMy Paradise is a person\nSo beautiful and happy\nOne look into her eyes\nAnd everything is great\nShe lights up my heart\nShe sends me so far\nShe is my paradise\nI need her in my life.\nHer voice lifts my soul\nHer being makes me roll\nI wish for her love\nI wont let it go null.\nMy paradise shines bright\nBrightest star in the night\nShe lights up my life\nShe is my Paradise.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Mylas", "Old Courier Woman", "To: Mylas\nFrom: The Old Courier\n\n\nHere I am. Another day, another delivery to your doorstep. Once again, I find myself bringing this rusted helmet to you. This time, though, I also had to drag a large carpet along as well.\nFor the helmet --\nThis was the first thing the sender would see you wear every time you visited her. It'd fall over your eyes as you shuffeled, and was the last thing they'd see as you left them.\nThey looked for that rusty shine every day to see your approach.\nFor the carpet --\n\nNo matter how troubled their mind was, you always reassured them that at the very least, their carpets were all accounted for.\nYour humor and wit made their day and your laugh is something they miss dearly. They sit by the water's edge, listening to the familiar waves, hoping your laugh will travel along them from the shores of Vailor to their new home.\nNow that's out of the way. \n\nShould you find yourself returning these things as you did the first time, keep in mind the poor old woman who has to drag them back the very next day, hmm?\nDrag them back yourself, at least. Feel the weight of the carpet rolled up on your shoulder as you carry it along from Johannesburg to Sutica. It will seem heavier with each step.\nFocus on that weight for the entire trip until it becomes too painful to carry any longer. \n\nSomething once light and silly will feel like a searing ache.\nThat is the feeling in the heart of the one that asked me to deliver these things to you. \n\nI know a sorrowful, broken heart when I see one.\nSo, kindly...If a broken heart does not move you even slightly, at least think of the old broken back that will keep carrying these things to you day after day. \n\nCarry them back yourself if you must. For me. Please.\nGood day.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Q", "Nikoru Shuroda", "Dear Q,\nMerry Krugmas.\nI figured I'd get you this because you seem to have troubles sleeping unless your snuggling someone. But then again, Tamara might find that adorable.\n With the fact that you told me you liked cats...\nI figured I'd get you something of the sorts. \n\nI hope you enjoy it and have an easier time sleeping when no one is near to help you sleep peacefully.\nAnd I don't think there's enough words in the dictenary to describe my appreciation for you helping me with the past few days.\n(( months? ))\nAnd I understand that Mika is your friend but, I don't think I can ever forgive him....\nor forget what he's done. Not only to me but multiple others.\n\n\n\n\nThank you again, though.\n\n-Nikky\nP.S\nThis is not a farewell letter. \nDon't take it as such.\nI swear it's just a Krugmas and Thank you letter.", ""),
        StaticBook("To the Industry", "Dimaethor Visaj", "The\n     Haelun'or\n      Industry\n\n\n\n\n\n   §s   \n\n             Dimaethor\n                 Visaj,\n                 1699\nThe mountain must must roar from the unearthing of ore,\nThe forges must radiate heat like never before,\nThe farms must be harvested from wall to shore,\nThe Haelun'or Industry will eradicate any reason to deplore!", ""),
        StaticBook("To the L. Scribe", "Vaeyl of Aegis", "TO LORD SCRIBE DAEFYN;\n\nI understand your concerns about such a colossal project. \n\nHowever, the Vaeyl Order now controls the majority of Atlas, through direct vassals or territories that depend on our protection. We are the indisbutible rulers of\nthis land, and an entity as prominent as the Order must have a place in which it safely store important information.\n\nAs Lord Scribe of the Order, I am entrusting this responsibility to you. The constructions near Kahaer have already begun; the Archives\nwill be built before winter comes.\n\nInformation will arrive, as directed by Yrodholm, by the Darkways portal at Kahaer, and will be safely delivered to you. \n\nAs a side note, Lord-Arcanist Haevolt plans to instal a\nbarrier defense system on each floor of the Archives, to be activated in the event of a security breach. Each barrier requires a different keystone to unlock. You will be given a master keystone, of course, while other keystones will be distributed to\nvarious officers of the Order as necessary.\n\nWe are an Empire now, Daefyn. For the sake of advancement and progression, we must maintain records, preserve history, and harbour knowledge.\n\nServe well,\n-Vaeyl of Aegis", ""),
        StaticBook("To Vanderlise", "Saqr Ibn Anwar", "You Shall know Pain, You Shall Know Death,\nGod Sees All...\nGod Knows All...\nThe Master hears his call... Your Name was selected....Your Soul Will be Collected...\nWe Know Where you Live\nWe Know What you Do\nWe See whom you love\nBe Afraid..For those\nMarked with Death...Shall never Escape it....\nAmr Al-Saqr...Is Back On the Rise...And your name...Has been Selected.....\n\n-The Messengers Of Death, Amr Al-Saqr", ""),
        StaticBook("To Vex a HighElf", "Matrim Macdunn", "How to vex a High Elf\n\n\n\n           For\n My Adunian Brothers\nThe High elf is a species of being that is usually associated with class, elegance, magic and of course power.\nHence, such qualities accumulate to a grand disgruntled vexation by the common man. As a usual high elf will look down upon 'inferior' races or\ncultures.\n\nHeaven forbid you hail from 'impurity' such as being a half elf or Adunian. Such is seen as a grand faux par, as it reminds them how they themselves were impure as to mingle with Harrenites.\n\nAs of such they often tend to haul\nthemselves up in their cities, denying access to all those whom don't hail from their mighty ancestory.\n\nOn the other hand, when these timid and commonly, rude creatures scurry from their lairs they are often condesending and harsh to all those\nnot of their kin.\n\nThis, my friends, is why I have personally taken it upon myself in to muse possible ways to disarm, vex and scare off this beast.\nMethod 1:\n\nBe from a mixed heritage, Adunian or half elf. Either will surfice.\n\nThe mere concept of love across races is dead with the high elf, so be spawned from such love is the ultimate vexation as proof that love\nconquer's order.\n\nHowever, be wary of mix-ed one. For a high elf may turn hostile. If that is the case be sure to play the racism card. If this fails, arm yourself and be sure to attack before the beast can charge a magical attack!\nMethod 2:\n\nIf they commit any actions, mutter 'Typical high elf'. Simple as that, it boils their blood good and proper.\nMethod 3:\n\nRemind them of how their past kin have been manipulative, crooked and evil to all whom are not their own. To remind them of their past brings them great tragedy. They may become snide however and claim that it was true and proper. If this is\nthe case, be sure to verbally put them down and destroy their argument.\n\nMethod 4:\n\nDistribute this guide.\n\nMethod 5:\n\nA good old punch.", ""),
        StaticBook("To: Ally Moon", "Sybbyl", "Hello. I see you have gotten a home Ally! Isn't it nice?\n\nHere's a little gift for you getting a house.\n\n-Sybbyl", ""),
        StaticBook("To: Ruin'nir T.", "Gilondir Oronar Sagehand", "Hello Ruin'nir Terin,\n\nI see your nice alchemy store and I was thinking we could perhaps meet up some time to share some knowledge, I might have a few things you'd like to buy or recipes you'd like to know!\nSend me a bird if interested!\n-Gilondir Oronar Amarthelon Sagehand Frostbeard of Faroe and de Savin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tome of Zhag", "Zhag'Yar", "=Authors Note=\n\nMuch before I returned to Krugmar I was as most would define us, white wash. Though I won’t go into much detail on this part of my life, I was not in a right state of mind. Even during this stage of my life,\nI only felt more disgusted with myself not because of who I was, but because of how I was trying to avoid the curse that lingered within me- a curse that only fueled my already present hatred and anger towards this world alike.\nThen came an even greater obstacle within my life, the fall of U’la’s rein. She was a respectable leader who was taken too soon from this hellfire of a universe. Though she was finally at rest in stargush'stroh her clan, the Yar clan, was left\nto rot and fade into the past and never to exist. It was around this time that I took initiative to self proclaim myself as Yar’s chieftain in honor of U’la’s name. My life mate, Kotturra’Braduk, was another reason I decided to return as well.\nI had a deep connection with her and I was too afraid to lose what we had- destroy her feelings for me over my own repressed emotions. Now here we are after several years of what seemed to be downfalls and ridicule, I stand my ground knowing that\nnot only have I brought redemption to U’la’s and Yar’s name, but redemption to my own name. Within this tome I will speak of some of the many things within our culture that I not only value, but I see as something to be improved upon among us.\n=PART I Honor=\n\nSome years ago, an uruk brethren by the name of Zagruck insulted my life mate and my own kub in front of my face within the walls of the Yar den. His insults were rather distasteful from what I can remember\nonly because I denied to spar him. He slandered the pure definition of dishonorable only to fit the needs of his starved ego. He labeled me as disdain in his eyes only because I denied to do what he offered. He mostly acted in a rather\nchildish manner in response to this. With that said, the definition of honor does not justify those that are pretentious or believe they have bragging rights over other lesser individuals. Neither does it justify for those that must\nfeed their ever starving ego. Honor is much more a broad idea that spanses in almost every aspect. A Lur for instance can reach a feat of hunting or slay a mighty beast to show honor, a Lak can show similar honor by a means of appeasing the spirits.\nConsidering honor is more of a general idea rather than something that can be pinpointed and centralized, I personally believe the true ideals of honor rely on not only benefiting oneself, but inspiring others- benefiting future generations and those\naround you. Just as U’la gained her honor through the respect of her people and just as Elphaba has redeemed herself on a rather spiritual level, honor comes in almost many shapes and forms. It should NEVER be slandered out of one's ego\nor greedful benefit. On top of that, honor should not be something to be disdained upon especially in the case of allies and or highly held pacts with other communities or people.  In such scenarios, honor must always be upheld to its highest standard-\nwe must never stoop so low to the scum of this world and back stab those we hold our honor to.\n=PART II Klomp=\n\nThough some fragments of our brethren have evolved to become more diplomatic and charismatic among our fellow uruk and outside of Krugmar’s walls, we at times collectively fall victim to the curse of blood rage.\nNot only is blood rage a blessing to those who honor the spirits that generalize around fighting and to those who find the act of klomping as something of sacredness, but it is also a curse- a burden some carry that have made strained attempts to\nI myself will come clean and admit that I have yet much to learn when it comes to controlling my anger. I am not near as perfect as others before me, including Yar’s before me. At times I thirst to watch the blood of mali spill before me;\nI want to watch them burn. Not because of what they’d taken from me, but it’s because who I am. Even if it is who I am, I understand that allowing my rage and inner hatred to take over me in such a violent manner is not healthy. It only plagues me\nwith an ever growing grimace of this world (at least that is how it is for me). Though at times the thought of klomp or violence typically overrules in a diplomatic and or negotiative situation,  there are always other ways for one to\nconstructively achieve their wants and needs outside of clan or honorary scenarios.\n=PART III Wisdom=\n\nJust as Yar, Gorkil, and many other ancestors have done before even to this day through the ties of the Starghush’Stroh, wisdom is a strong back bone to all cultures including the all powerful uruks.\nStrength and honor can only take one as far as to have many fear them or gaze upon them obviously as a godly figure like a herd of sheep. Wisdom on the other hand can serve one as a canvas of character and personality, allowing one to\noffer their deepest insights and experiences to kubbies, elders, and other uruk kin to come. Comprehending the purest ideals of wisdom at times can help ascend one to much higher levels of understanding despite one's intellect. In fact, anyone can show\ntraits of wisdom with or without intellect. Though debatable wisdom, unlike its realistic and logistical counterpart, is more reliant on one's experiences, awareness, character, and empathy; the list continues on and on. Wisdom is also generally\ndependent on ones openness- their ability to make reasonable decisions and come to rational compromises. Not only can wisdom be applied to those who lead, but it can also be implemented to those that follow in the case of need input or advisory.\nIntellect or not, strength or weakness, wits or sluggishness, wisdom comes to us when we are willing to accept that we are apart of something grander. The world does not revolve around us, but we revolve around it, and we have to come to terms to\nwhat is around us and how we conceive it.\n=FINAL STATEMENT=\n\nSome time ago I went on a spirit walk to the ancestral realm, the Starghush’Stroh. There with a party of uruks I consider close brethren (most exclusively Vorgak and Elphaba) I spoke to the great Yar himself.\nAround this time I was still lost, hatred filled the void within my soul; even if the spirits, Elphaba, and the rest of my brothers supported me along the way. As I spoke to Yar of my deepest darkest thoughts, he suggested me to write this tome-\nas a way to exert my emotions and to redeem the clan name as well as my own. He also asked of me to not only keep this tome between the Yar’s and I, but to also spread word of its wisdom to our brethren as a way to enlighten our own people.\nBearing this tome, do not take its contents with a grain of salt; neither should one only take these words with light consideration. The truths that this book holds should at the least be used to better oneself and to expand one's way\nof thinking, despite this tome being comprised of only several segments.", ""),
        StaticBook("Torn Page", "Ancient Dwarf", "[!] This page has been torn out from it's respective  tome.\nThe Magi have begun dissapearing. I pray to Khorvad that we find them, else we may be stuck in this accursed place. Their leader, Dwov, is still about. I fear for him, though. His mind has begun to deteriorate for reasons unkown. We've enough supplies to\nlast another three weeks.", "")
    )

    private fun _ATLAS_6(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Torrehn Elendil", "Commodus de Jedih", "Declaration Regarding the Punishment of Torrehn Elendil\n\nIssued and confirmed by His Imperial Majesty the Holy Emperor of Oren, Godfrey I, 1417\nAt the will of His Imperial Majesty the Holy Emperor Godfrey I, the man known as Torrehn Elendil is charged with High Treason for the crime of inciting rebellion, wishing harm onto the Imperial Family, plotting and conspiring against the Crown.\nHe is hereby stripped of all ranks, styles, titles, honors, and lands. He is completely, utterly, and unquestionably renounced by the One True Faith, and shall find no rest in this world or the next.\nTorrehn Elendil's lands, treasury, title, and other possessions are hereby claimed in the name of Harrion Elendil. In addition,the former Duke of Westfall and Adunian bannermen and vessels are no longer held by their oaths to him, and shall directly rule-\ntheir lands in trust to there new Lord Harrion Elendil.\n\nFurthermore by orders of his Imperial Majesty anyone seen, conspiring or harboring the Traitor shall be committed to High Treason as well and-\nAnd if any of his former subjects family members and so on and so forth follow him and take him on as there leader, or dare to follow him outside of our Empire shall do so on the pain of death, all the Adunian's must swear to Harrion as their new lord.\nAnd to any Nation, City, Village, or people that harbor him know that ye are committing offenses against Oren and we shall not take kindly to that.\n\nIssued this day, being the 11th day of the Deep Cold, in the 58th Year of Asulon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Torvin's Crown", "Nerah", "--------=-=--------The crowning of Torvin Grandaxe\nBy Richord Bearfoot\n1. Omen\n2. Blow of the Horn\n3. Speech\n4. Gifts\n5. Thoughts\n--------=-=--------\nThe hours before the beginning of the event were...problematic, to say the list. Long story short, this giant obsidian sphere of varying size would phase in and out of existence, some thought it was the immortal spirit Orgon, others an omen from the\nBrathmordakin, the mistery endured until half of the event, when a man named Alex Sliverberg suddenly shouted \"Why is there a giant black ball in the sky?\" then no other recordings seem to exist.\n--------=-=--------\nBack to the topic.\nThe throne room would start to be filled before the actual blow of the horn, because this Lenya Asterya brought food and everyone for some reason was hungry.\nThe tables and benches would start to be filled by people of all race\nkind: several kinds of Mali, both royals or travellers, a confirmed Enchantry sorcerer, members from many or all dwarven clans (my ears still ring for the Frostbeards' howling), Sutican and Kharajyr merchants, travellers, mercenaries, even the Holy\nEmperor of Oren himself appeared. Some fights erupted, for the tables were supposed to be divided among nations, but all seened friendly. Then the Grand Marshall, Svardin Grandaxe, called for silence: the Prophet was speaking.\n--------=-=--------\nThis Prophet seemed important, for he was no other than Kardel Irongut, a previous Grand King of Urguan. In the silence, he began waving a stick of burning sage, singing s loud praise in Dwarvish, here roughly translated:\n\"Glory to the Brathmordakin.\" He stops and takes one step foward \"Glory to Dungrimm.\" He steps again, discarding the sage and taking out a phial of water \"Glory to Armakak!\" He steps again, dips his hand in the phial and sprinks the water on the throne's\nsteps \"Glory to Belka and Grimdugan! And glory to Yemekar!\" He steps foward, facing Torvin, the soon-to-be crowned. He lifts the crown over Torvin's head, lifting his chin and enunciating \"Glory to King Torvin!\" And a brief moment of screams, cheering,\nhowling from the Frostbeards erupted, until the prophet stated: \"By the Divine Grace of Yemekarr and his Brahmordakin, forever may they regin, the Brathmordakin's guided will of the people has steered our Kingdom to elect its Divine Kings. For over\nthe years, the sons of Urguan, the chosen among Yemekar's creations have walked the long road towards peace and prosperity. Guided by the Brathmordakin, we have emerged into days of enlightement. Our Grand King, Torvin, inherits a kingdom at the end of a\ntroublesome era. Guided wrongly for many years, only now it's on the right path.\nTorvin Grandaxe, first of his name and chosen of the Urguani people, will continue this legacy. He will value peace and uphold justice, and will lead the people under the\nguidance of Anabella and Dungrimm, to maintain this peace. May we prosper under his reign.\nGlory to Yemekarr! Greet High King Torvin!\" and the room falls again into shouting, howling and cheering. Yet silence is found again, for Torvin has the word\n\"I will keep this short. Long I've served the nation, as my father before me. I shall bring forth prosperity and maintain the current peace. We shall continue with making the kingdom greater and greater again. After a long time we are finally back on the\nright track.\" But then, the King says the fateful words: \"Let us now celebrate this day with a feast. Get out the ale and meat!\" And the room finally falls into an endless cheering and shouting. \n--------=-=--------\nI sure hope you spend at least one (why not more, tho?) dwarven feast: nothing can describe the scent of ale and meat, the cheering and shouting, the bumps and friendly brawls that these events include. Everything could happen: this time, the same Alex\nfrom before managed to get a boat in the middle of the room, which was confiscated quickly and sold for a thousand Minas. In the middle of the gambling-less party, the Great King starts recieving gifts and meeting friendly faces, a Doomforged lady, the\nHoly Emperor of Oren John Owyn with his legionaries who gifted a symbolic block of ferrum from Johannesburg \"to help in repelling the uncouth Orcish tribes that remain\", a maiden with a cake, a tiny brawl I was yet to understand that luckily didn't fall\ninto axe dueling, a stick from Crevin Grandaxe, a friend of the King seeking help for this Ilthilien, an elf with a banner, another elf, a Frostbeard with a \"polar bear egg\" (someone must research the fauna of this land further), a shielf from the\n\"Wardwarves\", his father Fimlin who greets him with an axe form his uncle Morgrim, and in the end a Starbreaker with the \"Hammer of Ograd'ad\", which nearly fell in the decorative molten rock under the throne.\n--------=-=--------\nThe Throne room would now be empty, except for the sorcerer, who gifted us with a rare sight: a flying Orc. Gutz, his name is, seemed to have liked it.\nI want to thank the Grand King Torvin Grandaxe for giving me the honor of recording his day,\nwhich I probably didn't deserve, and I sure hope we can collaborate again one day.\n--------=-=--------", ""),
        StaticBook("Trading contract", "Aldir'tor", "Contract of trade:\n\nAldir'tor of the silver enclave.\n\nMiss. Castelo of the Empire.\nWith this contract Aldir'tor of the Silver enclave confirms the terms agreed on before. \n\nTerms:\n\nA trading deal between Family Castelo of the Empire and Aldir'tor of the Silver Enclave\nFamily Castelo will be the main wine deliverer of the Silver Enclave and will be paid for it. \n\nThe wine is to be delivered to the tavern inside the silver enclave.\nPayment will come after the order arrived. \n\nOOC: The contract was signed by Aldir'tor in a curly fashion\n\nSigned:\nAldir'tor", ""),
        StaticBook("Training", "UnBaed", "[!]The cover of this old book is a thick leather, the pages are littered with old stains.  The writing looks extremely faded, though with the right lighting, it'd be readable.  The entire book itself has a musky, earthy smell to it.[!]\nThe Blackwood Company Training Schedule\n-=-+ -=-+ -=-+\nWritten by Nemir, The Blackarrow\n\nGuild members who've joined to be mercenaries are to wake up when the sun is just peeking over the ---\n--- horizon. \nOnce the soldiers have lined up they will be ordered to take laps around the keep and farms.  As they finish up, breakfast is to be served to all guild members in the main hall.  After the newer mercenary ---\n--- members have finished eating they will be ordered to line up before the arena, just outside of the main hall.  Their skills are to be tested to see which rank best fits them, infantry, cavalry, or archery.  The choice on which rank is for them ---\n--- is to be decided later, never on the first day.  The new member needs to complete a few contracts before they may rank up.\n\nThe new recruits are to spar in the arena first.  Two fight in the pit ---\n--- at a time with wooden weapons.  Each pair are to spar two times before they next to have a go.  The fight only ends ifone man yields or is taken down.  If there are any severe injuries the injured will be taken to the infirmary where they ---\n--- will be treated by Nick.\n\nAfter sparring, the new recruits will be ordered to line up once more before the arena, just outside the main hall.  They shall then march towards the agility course.  One by one, the new recruits are to attempt ---\n--- to complete as soon as possible.  Whoever completes the course in the shortest amount of time will earn nothing but respect, this is training not a game.  After agililty training, the recruits will be granted a short break.  Once the ---\n--- break has ended, recruits are to line up infront of the arena once more and march out to the farms where Rozaliya and Vladimir will take over on horse combat.  A#- [!]The rest of the pages are completly stained a deep red, one a few words ---\n--- through out the book are readable.  The pages have an extremely faint smell of adunian wine.[!]\n\n\n# \n\n                      -           =\n\n    R                 \n                               ..\n#/                       \n\n\n                  +               .\n\n      _\n                                swor-#\n[!]On this page there is a faint shape to be seen through the faded crimson color of the page, if one were to look very close they could see a faint, leafless tree standing alone.[!]\n\n\nRise-_#  F/#..m  #_// As#e//..", ""),
        StaticBook("TRAINING", "Nemir", "Training Schedual\n\n1. Agility parkour\neveryone lines up and attemps it once, they must make it to the end and back without falling.  If we have time we can have two people go at the same time and they race eachother.\n\n2. Pit fighting\nTwo people are given-\nwood swords and they must pvp in the pit, who ever wins 2 out of 3 fights wins.  If there is time and enough arrows the two fighters can both fight with just bows, or both weapons.\n\n3. Battle practice\nThere are two teams, both will have different colored-\nleather chestplates.  Before the battle people will choose to either have a stone sword and 15 arrows OR a wooden sword with 30 arrows.  First team to win 2 out of 3 wins, no one gets popped.  After every game everyones arrows ect. gets restored.", ""),
        StaticBook("Transfig. Notes", "Nemir", "Lesson 1 Notes.\n\n-Wards are not inheritly put into objects.  WArds are a separate spell that you can cast that is a part of transfiguration that you can also enchant into an item.\n-The enchantment you make is not putting\ninto the gem.  Rather, it is putting into the item itself.  The gem merely stores the mana used for the spell\n-Transmuation is the manipulation of mana that is stored into every single object of existance.\n-In order to do anything with transmutation\none must know about the material and it's properties at its desired state. The process of it is pooling your mana into an object to tap it's mana to change certain aspects of it.\n-Enchanting is weaving a spell into an item so that the spell can be\ncasted from that object.  The mana used for it is stored in a mana gem on the object.\n-There are two types of enchantings. The 'regular' version is just simple enchanting.  Where the transfigurationist casts and uses their own spell for enchanting.\nThe other version is known as Entrapment.  More will be learned about this at a later time.\n-Abjurations are the 'anti-magic' of transfiguration.  Their bases of them is to disrupt the mana anchor of the targetted spell.\n-A mana anchor is\nthe location in the world that you create what is essentially a tear in the void in which you funnel your mana into. \n-There are two types of abjurations.  One is the abjuration, the next is a ward. An abjuration is more of a projectile.  It may only\ndisrupt one type of magic as a ward can disrupt several.  A ward is more like a barrier.  But in order to disrupt any sort of magic with either of these, the transfigurationist must have good knowledge of the magic. (By having knowledge of the magic, you\nneed to have someone describe and show it to you.) \n-Abjurations are swifter to cast than wards.\n\nHomework: Study the iron ball, sapphire gem, and list uses of transmutation.\n\n-Final note. Transmuation can\nbe done at most of an arm's length away.", ""),
        StaticBook("Translocators", "Thurak'Yar", "             [!]\nAlong the page you see many strange markings and drawings. They look to be rough copies, at best. There appears to be some sort of archway built of stone; below it, several odd, circular schematics, or perhaps a map.\n [!]\nNext to the map, the phases of the moon trail along.\n\n[OOC]- View in browser:\nhttp://tinyurl.com/slatrop\n-------------------\nAn odd name, indeed. Though, the actual device is far more mysterious and eldritch in nature. Translocators, Lori Oathcast refers to them as. Crumena took to calling them closets, as per their birthplace, the closets within Rasmot’s magical porta-potty.\nRegardless, the process for creating these translocators is a fairly complex and ritualistic one that involves both a skilled translocationist with knowledge of the subject, and a powerful enchanter capable of binding the spell to a location.\n      Creation\nAn enchanter holds the knowledge to spot. One who knows how to send matter to the void and back again must have learnt to create what is like a ‘gateway’ into the void. More than just the item itself, but anything that touches it,\neven air. Then again you do it on the other end and the mage attempts to pull the block back through the Void and the enchanter binds that to a doorway or pillar or somesuch. In short, one must reach into the Void and pull out an open space.\n Maintenance\nAfter time, it will need a mana supply, or one end will fizzle out before the other and create an endless hole. It’s advised then to have the enchanter available fairly often to refill whatever large mana gem or crystal you wish to\npower the translocators’ magic with. As far as I’m aware, this would be the only option, unless one would be able to get ahold of Kalameet’s notes on the mana obelisk. For the ignorant, this is a large pillar in which sums of mana are stored for use.\nThe mana cannot be pulled out by any means by a magi to fuel their own spellcasting, but instead it exerts energy needed to power enchantments in the area. I’d elaborate further, though I’m only going off of what I’ve seen myself.", ""),
        StaticBook("Transmutation", "The Unknown Sorcerer", "Transfiguration; The Utility magic\n\nBook One - Transmutation.\n\nWritten by an unknown mage, these scripts were found and translated by Sarrion Zytiaear.\nIntroduction:\n\nThrough the arcane’s discovery -- an ability to create and destroy -- researchers and mages sought to find a way to influence the world in such a way that man can only dream of. To morph the earth, to dispel, and to imbue.\nIn the throes of their research, the fruits gave purchase to Transfiguration, an art that manipulates the very world, be it through transmuting objects, imbuing magical powers on said items via enchanting, or dispelling magic through warding.\nAny transfigurationist one may come upon is more than likely a well learned man, in one way or another - perhaps an engineer or just a magister - for the very first bit of the magic requires one to be willing to learn and document.\nThese learned mages -- they sport an incredible ability to manipulate mana to imprint effects on the world.\nTransmutation:\n\nTransmutation is the act of manipulating an item’s properties, doing so by creating an anchor on the desired object and enacting manipulation on its mana, so long as it does not change one object to another;\nhowever feats such as fusion (molding two materials to make one) or fission (splitting an item apart to get the exact materials) has proven possible.\nThis manipulation-- typically done close by, at three meters (blocks) length-- can range far and wide, and the lasting effects can be permanent.\nThe transmutationist will require much study, having to research and document the material they wish to manipulate, studying an item much like a mage would study an element they care to evocate.\nThere are downsides to this magic however, nothing organic can be transmuted unless dead organic, and transmutation scales on the size of an item.\nThe smaller the shorter time, the larger the greater time. Even then, this art works off equivalent exchange, which effectively means something of equal value must be given for something else.\nThis means that manipulating items will require one to follow equivelant exchange of the item to gain their desired form; for example, if one wanted to make spikes on a ball -\n- they would need to make ball smaller as the metal shapes the spikes from its own being. Transmutation is required to learn Enchanting or Warding.", ""),
        StaticBook("Traveler Of Seas", "Dorin Starbreaker XII", "Traveler Of Sea's\n\n A Tale Of A Dwarf at               Sea\n\n\n\n\nBy:Dorin Starbreaker\n\n\n\n           1288\nThe year was 1160, and the time was of winter. The fire was roaring and the crys could be heard all throughout the village. But not every cry was coming from screaming villagers, but one coming from a female dwarf, Summer Starbreaker, giving birth to a\nnew dwarf. Along side her, holding her hand was Gherren Irongut. The baby was almost out when a orc raider came in and charged her, but he got no where near close as Gherren threw a fireball at his face, killing him. The baby was almost out and Gherren\ngrabed the babys body as it came out.\"w'at is it, a boy or girl?\". asked Summer \"A boy, w'at s'ould we call 'im 'oney?\" said Gherren \"I don't kn'w, 'and 'im over and i'll dicide.\". Gherren hand over the newborn, still in his birthday suit. The mother\nlooked at her new child, and said \"You know, i t'ink 'e look's like a Dorin... Yes Dorin Starbreaker.\" Don't ye t'ink 'e s'ould be called Irongut?\"asked Gherren, \"No... i want him to have my last name and be a excelent magic user... just like you!\".\nGherren though for a second, and how this could effect the baby in the future, but he did'nt think long as he had to get the baby to safty, He looked over to his wife, something was wrong however... He did not notice it untill now, but the baby had been\ncrying still in his mothers hands. Gherren knew she was having trouble breating but he did not think it was this bad... She had died. A tear droped from his face, but he did not think long, for the baby still had to be taken to safety... The docks!\nGherren grabed the baby and wraped him in a blanket, then started to run for the docks. While he was runing, he decided to hold the baby in one hand and focused for a moment, with his right hand up, a few seconds of running and a flame appeared in his\npalm, lighting the path that was dark untill now. He ran, and he could see the docks and all the light's coming from the now leaving boats's. He was just about to get off of the path onto the dock when a orc shaman appeared, and he shouted at Gherren\nwho stayed his distance as the orc shouted in a accent he could not understand. After a moment, the Shaman lifted his hand and the sky darkend up with cloud's, lighting started to spark through them... Gherren had to think fast.\nHe closed his eyes, the lightnig flaring in the backround, he concentraded and everything became quite. He stuck his hand up the fire going out, and water started to spout around Gherren and the baby, and as fast as the water had appeared, lightning\nflashed and struck the water, and the water fizziled and started to buzz, Gherren quikly made the water disapper along with the lightning. He looked up at the Shaman, who game a look of impress, but he still wanted to kill them, and he raised his hand\nagain. Gherren took fast action and put his hand up as well, and a blue flame appeared, small at first, but it quikly grew to the size of a softball, then it grew to a purple state, and the heat grew, wind started to form around it as it comsumed the air.\nHe looked to his foe, and smirked, throwing the ball, the shaman tried to run, but the Evocationest moved his hand, the fire following his command. The ball struck the orc's back and he fell down, his cloth's burned off and his skin singed to the bone.\nGherren smirked and then started to run again, he passed the dead orc and smirked. Gherren had gotten to the dock in time for the last boat, and handed the newborn over to the captin of the boat, he told him his name and said he was to be taken to his\nGrandfather, at the dwarven capital and taught magic when he get's old enough. Before Gherren could climb upinto the boat however, a arrow stuck him in the back and he fell slightly. Not even a second later, 3 more arrows hit him in the back, he fell, and\nwith his last dieing breath he managed to say \"Go!\". The captin looked and understood... He was not going to make it, he turned around and told his crew to put the sail's up and they pushed off the dock, sailing away as arrows flew at\nthem, the newborn baby crying in the distance.\n75 Years later\n\"Are ye sure ye don't want te come wit' me grandfat'er? I could use t'e 'elp wit' finding me master...\" Dorin said to his grandfather, both f them sitting around a fire, behind Dorin a bag filled with food and fire wood, a pouch set aside with about\n500minas. \"no...no ye need to go on t'is journey yerself. lot's of exsperince you will get from doing t'is on yer own... yer already almost 100... ye need te' proove yerself, so don't come back if ye 'avent masterd any magic!\". The young dwarf looked to\nhis grandfather, he was not surprised, after all, his grandfather had always been this stubern, why would it change now? Dorin was 75 now, and it was time for him to go look for a master to teach him the ways of the fire and water evocationist.\nHe had beed given food and fire wood for his travel's, and 500 minas to travel on the boats. He had everything he needed now and he was ready to set off. \"Alrig't grandfat'er, 'ave it yer way. W'en i get back ill be a Evocationist and ye will be proud!\"\nDorin said. \"Well boy, i 'ope yer rig't, because if ye don't t'en i will surely be disapointed in ye, so make me proud! Now ye better get goen, yer boat leave's at newn does it not?\".\"Aye, it does, well ill be off now.\"Dorin got up from his chair, took\none last look at his grandfather and then walked out the door, heading strait for the dwarven docks, but he was not going for just a ride... But instead a job. He had not told his grandfather that realy he was going to pursue his dream of becoming a\nsailor and crossing the seas, exsploring.\nDorin arrived at the dock and looked for the boat he had been hired to sail on for the next year, taking cargo to the distant islands. He found the ship and looked at the sun, it was newn, and it was time to leave\nhe was late! Dorin started to run for his ship hoping the captin would not yell at him for his tardyness. Dorin quikly found the boat and got aboard.\nThe captin had beed waiting for him. He was a tall man, large muscles, he must have been doing this job\nyears, as his hands were coverd in cysts, and they cracked every time he moved them. He also had a very large beard, almost as large as Dorin's beard, which went down to his chest, although it would be larger if he hadnt shaved it. \"Reporting for duty\nCpt.Theodore.\" The captin looked at the dwarf, \"you can just call me Teddy, your one of my sailors now, and we're in it togeather in the long run, so we might as well get better aquanted. You have anything you might want to be called beside's... What was\nit again? Dorin,Right?\"\nThe Cpt. said \"Aye sir, t'at be my name Dorin Starbreaker, and nay, i don't have anything id like to be called sir.\" Said Dorin. \"You can drop the formalitys, like i said, justcall me Teddy. Now then, your quarters are down stairs\n3 doors to your right, it has a bed, a desk and chair with a window, and a chest. You can get settled in and we will launch off at about 6. So get settled, maybe a nap, and wait untill i say otherwise.\n\n      Later That Day\nDorin was settled in, and started sleep, he woke up about 4 hours later, when he could hear yelling from the captin. It was time to leave and he could hear the other sailors rushing down the hall to the main deck. Dorin got up with excitement, and ran to\nthe main deck along with the other sailors. The captin called them to attention, 6 sailors standing in a row. \"Listen up! We have a newcomer to our ship. His name is Dorin, Dorin why don't you step out now, and introduce yourself to everyone?\"\n\"Aye Teddy.\" Dorin said as he stepped out to introduce himslef to the other 5 sailors, 3 other dwarfs, and 2 humans. \"I am Dorin Starbreaker, and i am hoping to become a member of this crew for a very long time, i 'ope we will all bec'me very well\naquainted on 'ur journey, and i lott forward to many adventures.\" One of the crew members, the one closest to him, put thier hand out and introduced herself. She was a thing shorter dwarf, with brown hair and a mole right by her lip.\nShe was dressed in a leather armor of sorts. \"Nice te meet a fellow dwarf sailor. My name is Diana.\" She said, her voice in a high pitched manner. \"aye nice to meet you as well.\" The captin did'nt want to waste much time on aquatinces and so he introduced\nthe others for them.\n\"from left to write this is Maveric, Sally, and Loki, and Diana has already introduced herself to you.\" Teddy said as he was slowly looking back and forth between them all. \"Aye! Nice te meat ye all, i 'ope we all become great friends\n.\" The captin raised his hand and everyone moved out to the sail's and started to unravel them, letting them loose. Dorin looked to the sun, and before he knew it the captin had already pushed them o the dock nd they were floating to the ocean.\n1 Month later\n\n\"Land ahoy!\" Yelled Maveric atop the crows nest. \"We finaly made it then? How long until we dock?\"Yelled Dorin to the man. \"About 1/2-1 hour until we dock, so get ready, and wake the captin!\" Dorin took note and then went into the\nunderdeck, heading for the captins quarters. He knocked on the door and said \"Captin, you up? We have seen land, we will be ready for docking in about an hour.\"Dorin said. Over the month that Dorin had spent with the crew, he had merged accents\nto fit thiers, and now he sounded as a human. \"Aye, im up. Tell the rest of the crew to get ready, we have a lot of work today.\"\nLater that hour, the boat slowly rocked as it floated ever closer to the dock of the island. It was filled with jungle trees\nand there were lots of cat people, all of them stairing as the boat arrived. The boat finaly touched down and some of the cat people ran up, puting a wooden pallet across the water to the boat as a little bridge. \"Dorin, get that rope and tie us up.\"\nsaid the captin. \"Aye sir!\" Dorin replyed, quikly grabing the boat's rope and tieing them to the dock. \"Get the cargo, we have to take it all the way to the palace up the road. Dorin and the other crew member's, including the captin went down into the\nhull, each coming out with a crate. They took the crates up the road where they finaly got to a palace. They stoped outside the gate where a man walked up and asked them to take them to the celler. They did as the man asked but when they got down into the\nceller, the door shut, they were traped! And they stayed traped for 315 years, at least as slaves that is.\n\n\n\n\n      315 Years later\n\"Get up! you need to get up, get your things and run for the docks!\" Diana shouted \"I can't just leave you! Besides they killed our son!\" DOrin shouted back. \"Aye, but it will take one of us to hold them off for the other to exscape, and you still have\nfamily! I don't!\" Diana shouted back. \"What about me?\" \"yes you are my family, but as i stated one of us has to get of this island, and i could'nt live without you, you can!\" She shouted \"Now go!\"Dorin had to make a desision, but he did'nt want to leave\nher. He decided it was best to leave her and ran, he got to the docks, that had been plated with iron since the last time he had seen it. He got aboard a boat and pushed off, a pair of cats running up yelling at him to give it back. He did not and a tear\nfell from his eye as he heard a scream from the night.\n\n\n\n\n   Dorin Starbreaker\nBook Two Coming Soon", ""),
