        StaticBook("Punishment II", "§bArchmage Crumena", "The Punishment of Hubris II\n\nWhat Nemiisae did not realize was that the portal had only been closed to prevent their leaving. The portal within the Verge to this new land was still open to anyone who could discover it. And discovered it was. The Dwarves were first to uncover\n\nthe portal into the Verge, as the first group to find it mined into the cavern it had been hidden in. Seeing the notes left behind by Nemiisae, they sent one dwarf ahead to try and locate the portal inside the Verge. He returned shortly, proclaiming\n\nthe glory of the land he saw reflected in the portal’s visage! Mountains, gold, diamonds, as far as the eye could see! It was right there, a short walk away! A world of their own, which they could run as they like, without having to share it with\n\nanyone! The Dwarves quickly made a decision to gather their families and things and venture through. Within the day, they were ready to venture to the Verge and then towards their new land. Greedily, they decided they had to prevent others\n\nfrom discovering this mystical, resource rich land. Using good, old fashioned Dwarven ingenuity, they collapsed the tunnel they had accidentally discovered the portal via, then quickly passed through. They quickly found the portal\n\ninside the Verge leading to this mystical new land and pass through that as well. And again, another group had fallen for the trap. The portal was closed behind them, so there was no place left to go but forward. They ventured into the\n\nland, ready to settle it and hoping to thrive. But within the next half of a millenia, they had all perished to the cursed land and it’s terrors…creatures or otherwise. All they left behind was skeletons, of their homes and of themselves.\n\n\nAbove ground, as the tunnel to the cavern shifted and collapsed, a huge crevice formed in the landscape. It had not been there the day before and as a Human merchant group passed the area they began to wonder what had caused such a\n\ncrevice. One of them suggested it may have been a tomb, full of riches. Eager to investigate, the Humans spent the next month digging down into the ground, following the slant of the crevice and eventually discovering the cavern which\n\nhoused the portal to the Verge. The Humans too spied the notes and messages Nemiisae had left behind, promising them a land free from Iblees’ curse, free for the taking! Their short lifespans would be gone and they would be immortal like their cousins!\n\nThe merchants quickly climbed back to the surface, cutting down the branches of nearby trees to cover the entrance to the land. They all quickly traveled to their homes, to fetch their families and supplies in order to settle this new land. The came\n\nback less than a week later, descending into the Cavern, through the Verge and into the new world. But they too fell into the trap. The Portal was closed behind them and they had no place left to go but forward. They ventured out to settle these new\n\nlands with their families. But within the next half of a Millenia, the majority of them had perished to the cursed land and it’s terrors. They were not made immortal as they had hoped, but rather had even shorter lifespans than usual. They became\n\ninbred, sick, ill, and in the end all they left behind were shadows of their former selves, a slow, stupid race incapable of complex thought and cursed by maladies and deformities.\nAfter the Humans had placed tree branches to cover the entrance to\n\nthe Cavern, a group of Elves ventured into that area, hearing the call of the wounded trees. They discovered the branches and removed them, wondering what foul creature had despoiled the trees in such a way and for what cause. Into\n\nthe cavern they ventured, discovering the notes from Nemiisae and the portal to the Verge. This group did not go back for more, though more would come later, as they were immediately forced through. Running from a threat, they\n\nentered the Verge and discovered the portal to the new world. Fleeing still, they had no choice but to enter. They too fell into this trap, the portal closed behind them, no way back, though they would only find this out after returning later to\n\ninvestigate. For now, they still had running to do. Immortal though they were, this land was still rife with danger. Forced to settle in it, the Elves would follow in the footsteps of their cousins, perishing within this strange lands within half a\n\nMillenia. In these lands they were susceptible not just to the terrors, but also their own curse. Far more infertile than they were in their original lands, they died out merely due to a lack of numbers. While some of them eventually interbred with\n\nNemiisae’s children, those who refused would only gain numbers through other poor fools coming through the portal. In this way the Elves too, were trapped.\nWhen the Elves first found the broken and disturbed trees as well as the secret\n\nthey hid, they did not realize they were being hunted. Following them from Malinor had been an Orc hunting party, searching for slaves, meat, or just a bit of violent fun. The Orcs assaulted the Elves at the entrance to the crevice, and\n\nhaving no other way to go, the Elves immediately fled into the Crevice and down into the Cavern. The Orcs gave chase, of course, following them through the Verge and the next portal, into the new world. The Elves had gotten ahead, fleeing to the\n\nnearest forests they could find. In the thick cover, the Orcs lost sight of them. They began to investigate the land as their cousins had. They settled, adventured, and fought. Fighting was what they were good at and they were much better\n\nequipped for the trip into this new world, to face the terrors that haunted it. But their own aggression killed them in the end. They perished at the hands of beasts, monsters they should have known they would never defeat, at least not in totality.\n\nWithin a half of a Millenia, the Orcs too were extinct, leaving behind only the skeletal ruins of their previous homes and their old enemies they had died out battling.\n\nRescribed by Archmage Crumena V. Ilwindior on the 2nd of The First Seed, 1473.\nTo be continued in the third volume.\n[Credit to TehLulu for the writing itself.]", ""),
        StaticBook("Hubris Volume 1", "§bRosso", "Table of Contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nBook One: Page 2\nBook Two: Page 18\nBook Three: Page 31\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Punishment for Hubris, Book one\n\nLet me tell you a story of the children of Malin, Horen, Urguan and Krug; A tale from the time when God’s melting pot became a boiling cauldron, and many wondered about his beneficence.\nA tale from when God was first questioned and his mortal children\n\ncried out in anguish.\nOur story takes us back to the beginning, when the Four Brother’s children were coming of age in this world known as Aegis. One stood out among the sons of Malin; Born beneath the shade of the trees under the pale light of a full\n\nmoon, his father named him Zanunder. Proud and strong was his stature, and Zanunder stood tall among his brothers and sisters, resembling their Father in many ways. His hair was the color of the noon-day sun and his eyes a vibrant shade of forest green.\n\nIblees came then, as Zanunder grew. Iblees attempted to corrupt his father and uncles, in the end unleashing upon the world a devastating curse. They said that Iblees had been a Daemon, a servant of God. Zanunder began to question this. If God was\n\nOmnipotent, surely he would not allow evil to exist. Nor would he do so were he kind, benevolent or even compassionate. But he was not the only being to begin to question the ways of the world. There was also her…she stood tall, her presence unlike\n\nanything he had laid eyes upon before. Hair black as night, lips green as ivy, but the strangest thing about her visage was surely her eyes. The whites of them were a deep, steel blue, and inside they were a light blue, like the clean waters of a gently\n\nflowing stream. He came to know her as Nemiisae, a kindred spirit in this world he viewed as cruel. In short time they fell in love, relishing in each other’s ideals and presence. They came to the conclusion quickly that they should escape these lands,\n\nhoping that in doing so they would also be able to break free of Iblees’ curse upon the lands. They retreated deep underground in order to begin their plans, for Zanunder did not wish others to know what they had planned, lest they be branded heretics.\n\nDeep beneath the ground, in a large cavern, Nemiisae created a portal to a world known as the Verge. From there it would be easier for her powers to stretch across the lands, locating a fit place for her, Zanunder, and their soon-to-be abundant children\n\nto settle. It would also protect them from the scourge Iblees unleashed across the lands. Inside the Verge the two thrived, and quickly multiplied, first growing to three, then four, then six, eight, ten, and continuing on. Nearly a hundred years after\n\nthey first arrived in that place, Nemiisae had finally found a suitable place to settle. However, during those hundred years, Kings had risen and fallen. The Brothers had all passed away. Kingdoms and Guilds began to rise to power throughout the lands.\n\nThe curse seemed to barely affect people’s lives. These events had gone unnoticed by Nemiisae and Zanunder, so wrapped up in raising their young and finding a place to flee to from Iblees’ curse. Inside the Verge, Nemiisae created another portal. It\n\nreflected the green, verdant lands they planned to settle…but not the dangers lurking within. Before they went through with their children, Zanunder stopped his love. He requested that the portal be closed behind them, as well as the portal out of the\n\nVerge that they had entered through. Zanunder did not wish for their children to be followed, believing that Iblees’ curse may seep through the Portals and into this new land. Nemiisae agreed, but it was a farce. In truth, she had always planned to leave\n\nthe portals open as well as leaving behind notes detailing where they went to.\n\n\n\n\n\n The Punishment for Hubris, Book 2\n\nNemiisae was a compassionate being, feeling love for all the races of Aegis. She believed they could all escape Iblees’ curse and did not wish to deny them the chance to do so. Little did she know that in the end, all who sought her same refuge would be\n\nlead to their dooms by it. As soon as Zanunder, Nemiisae and their children stepped through the portal, they realized it had slammed shut behind them; They could no longer return to the land they came from. At first, this was not a problem to them. They\n\nwere confident this land would be their Paradise, the savior of their children. But their children had spent decades cut off from the light of sun, while living and thriving within the Verge. They set out immediately for the thickest forest they could\n\nfind, in hopes of slowly acclimating their children to the light. But this was not to be. This land was rife with dangers, of all shapes and sizes, lurking behind corners, within the trees, in the skies, the oceans, the rivers…There was no escaping it.\n\nThe very least of these dangers were the skittering, venomous spiders of the caverns. Their children began dying off, one by one, then two by two, then five by five, then by the droves. Finally, Nemiisae chose the least of the threats of this world and\n\nblessed her children with that creature’s aspects. Her children became a mix of her blood, Zanunder’s, and that of the spiders that lurked the caverns. They migrated into these same caverns, living amongst and as the Spiders did, save from the beasts and\n\nterrors lurking on the surface. Vicious, cruel, the children shifted and changed into horrible beasts, preying and feeding upon one another.\nNemiisae knew she had to bless them in this way so that they may survive, yet still she grieved for their\n\ncorruption. As well, no matter how hard they tried, Nemiisae and Zanunder could no longer procreate. Horrified, they began to believe it had been a trap all along. A trick by God to punish them for acting out, perhaps?! Or was it just for His own\n\namusement?! Nemiisae demanded that they find a way to re-open the portal and escape from this cursed land. There was no escaping the will of God, or the curse of Iblees, she insisted. But at least their children would prosper and thrive in their original\n\nhomeland. Zanunder refused. They argued at length, until finally he threatened to take the children and go elsewhere. He firmly believed if they traveled far enough they could survive, thrive, beat God and the Curse. Frustrated and exhausted, Nemiisae\n\nknew she had to stop him somehow, or their children would all perish. She remembered the blessing she had given her children and as Zanunder turned to leave, she changed her form to that of a giant Spider. She put him to sleep with her venom and wrapped\n\nhim within a cocoon. Then, she bade the eldest and closest of her Daughters to watch over the others, before retreating into the deep with Zanunder, to try and find a way to force open the portal and escape this horrid place.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Punishment for Hubris, Book 3\n\nWhat Nemiisae did not realize was that the portal had only been closed to prevent their leaving. The portal within the Verge to this new land was still open to anyone who could discover it. And discovered it was. The Dwarves were first to uncover the\n\nportal into the Verge, as the first group to find it mined into the cavern it had been hidden in. Seeing the notes left behind by Nemiisae, they sent one dwarf ahead to try and locate the portal inside the Verge. He returned shortly, proclaiming the glory\n\nof the land he saw reflected in the portal’s visage! Mountains, gold, diamonds, as far as the eye could see! It was right there, a short walk away! A world of their own, which they could run as they like, without having to share it with anyone! The\n\nDwarves quickly made a decision to gather their families and things and venture through. Within the day, they were ready to venture to the Verge and then towards their new land. Greedily, they decided they had to prevent others from discovering this\n\nmystical, resource rich land. Using good, old fashioned Dwarven ingenuity, they collapsed the tunnel they had accidentally discovered the portal via, then quickly passed through. They quickly found the portal inside the Verge leading to this mystical new\n\nland and pass through that as well. And again, another group had fallen for the trap. The portal was closed behind them, so there was no place left to go but forward. They ventured into the land, ready to settle it and hoping to thrive. But within the\n\nnext half of a millenia, they had all perished to the cursed land and it’s terrors… creatures or otherwise. All they left behind was skeletons, of their homes and of themselves.\nAbove ground, as the tunnel to the cavern shifted and collapsed, a huge\n\ncrevice formed in the landscape. It had not been there the day before and as a Human merchant group passed the area they began to wonder what had caused such a crevice. One of them suggested it may have been a tomb, full of riches. Eager to investigate,\n\nthe Humans spent the next month digging down into the ground, following the slant of the crevice and eventually discovering the cavern which housed the portal to the Verge. The Humans too spied the notes and messages Nemiisae had left behind, promising\n\nthem a land free from Iblees’ curse, free for the taking! Their short lifespans would be gone and they would be immortal like their cousins! The merchants quickly climbed back to the surface, cutting down the branches of nearby trees to cover the\n\nentrance to the land. They all quickly traveled to their homes, to fetch their families and supplies in order to settle this new land. The came back less than a week later, descending into the Cavern, through the Verge and into the new world. But they too\n\nfell into the trap. The Portal was closed behind them and they had no place left to go but forward. They ventured out to settle these new lands with their families. But within the next half of a Millenia, the majority of them had perished to the cursed\n\nland and it’s terrors. They were not made immortal as they had hoped, but rather had even shorter lifespans than usual. They became inbred, sick, ill, and in the end all they left behind were shadows of their former selves, a slow, stupid race incapable\n\nof complex thought and cursed by maladies and deformities.\n\nThe Punishment for Hubris, Volume 1\n\nRetold by Leyu’Maehr\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Hubris Volume 2", "§bRosso", "Table of Contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nBook Four: Page 2\nBook Five: Page 14\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Punishment for Hubris, Book 4\n\nAfter the Humans had placed tree branches to cover the entrance to the Cavern, a group of Elves ventured into that area, hearing the call of the wounded trees. They discovered the branches and removed them, wondering what foul creature had despoiled the\n\ntrees in such a way and for what cause. Into the cavern they ventured, discovering the notes from Nemiisae and the portal to the Verge. This group did not go back for more, though more would come later, as they were immediately forced through. Running\n\nfrom a threat, they entered the Verge and discovered the portal to the new world. Fleeing still, they had no choice but to enter. They too fell into this trap, the portal closed behind them, no way back, though they would only find this out after\n\nreturning later to investigate. For now, they still had running to do. Immortal though they were, this land was still rife with danger. Forced to settle in it, the Elves would follow in the footsteps of their cousins, perishing within this strange lands\n\nwithin half a Millenia. In these lands they were susceptible not just to the terrors, but also their own curse. Far more infertile than they were in their original lands, they died out merely due to a lack of numbers. While some of them eventually\n\ninterbred with Nemiisae’s children, those who refused would only gain numbers through other poor fools coming through the portal. In this way the Elves too, were trapped.\nWhen the Elves first found the broken and disturbed trees as well as the secret they\n\nhid, they did not realize they were being hunted. Following them from Malinor had been an Orc hunting party, searching for slaves, meat, or just a bit of violent fun. The Orcs assaulted the Elves at the entrance to the crevice, and having no other way to\n\ngo, the Elves immediately fled into the Crevice and down into the Cavern. The Orcs gave chase, of course, following them through the Verge and the next portal, into the new world. The Elves had gotten ahead, fleeing to the nearest forests they could find.\n\nIn the thick cover, the Orcs lost sight of them. They began to investigate the land as their cousins had. They settled, adventured, and fought. Fighting was what they were good at and they were much better equipped for the trip into this new world, to\n\nface the terrors that haunted it. But their own aggression killed them in the end. They perished at the hands of beasts, monsters they should have known they would never defeat, at least not in totality. Within a half of a Millenia, the Orcs too were\n\nextinct, leaving behind only the skeletal ruins of their previous homes and their old enemies they had died out battling.\n\n\n\n\n\nThe Punishment for Hubris, Book 5\n\nIn the course of the first two-hundred and fifty years, as Nemiisae searched for a way to open the portal and leave this place, Zanunder aged within his sleep, eventually dying. Bereaved of her husband she fell into a great remorse for having\n\naccidentally killed him. Her mind became clouded, muddled, perhaps even mad. Then her children came to her with reports of these strangers in their lands. She realized then what had happened…The portal only shut on their side. It must have been an\n\naccidentally killed him. Her mind became clouded, muddled, perhaps even mad. Then her children came to her with reports of these strangers in their lands. She realized then what had happened…The portal only shut on their side. It must have been an\n\nunwittingly played a part in. She could not reopen the portal, but she could close it from her side, sealing off both the portal to the Verge and the portal within it to the new world. Then she retreated back into her Caverns, encouraging her children to\n\nlive, breath, fight, grow stronger. Punish and perish the weak and live for themselves and for her, for it was the only way to gain God’s favor. Then she left them to their own devices, her wishes for their future made clear.\n\nIt was in this way that hubris was punished, that the sins of those who came before was tested and they were proven guilty. Had these people physically gone to these lands, surely the curse would not have killed them all. But by passing through the portal\n\nof Hubris which Nemiisae had created, they doomed themselves and their kin. Other groups found the portals between the time Nemiisae realized what had happened and closed it off, but anyone who came through was doomed to suffer and die.\n\nThere was no hope for them as soon as they had passed through those portals into that world. But it is far enough removed that between the first settling of it and our time, no one has ever discovered it again. Beyond churning, whirling seas, deadly\n\nislands, leagues and weeks away from the lands settled by the Four Brothers, it would be impossible to reach without the assistance of a very strong force indeed. But perhaps it is for the best, that these ruins remain ruins, and the skeletons go\n\nundisturbed, lest we awaken old evils…\n\nThe Punishment for Hubris, Volume 2\n\nRetold by Leyu’Maehr\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven", ""),
        StaticBook("Economy & Merits", "§bOl' Man Sano", "The Myth of\n    Meritocracy\n----------------\n\nBell Sano\n\n11th of Sun's Smile, 1613\n\nPrelude:\n\nThis essay is one that should expand on a subject that I've only barely touched upon in earlier works, specifically \"The Sanoist Manifesto,\" where I discussed economics.\n\nWe are to explore the true embracement of a so called \"Meritocracy,\" and how one can truly be created, not through a capitalistic society, but through the use of socialist policies.\n\nA meritocracy, in the sense of economics, at least, is defined by the procurement of material wealth through hard work. Equal work for equal pay, essentially. Those who work the hardest will generate the most wealth.\n\nThe true creation of a meritocracy must be the most beautiful thing for a society to accomplish. Unfortunatley, the scourage of capitalism has perverted this glorious element of economics.\n\nIn a civilization dominated by the industry, otherwise, the businesses themselves, you will not see a distribution of wealth dependent on the hard labor of the working class. It will be disproportionate.\n\nShould the businesses themselves determine what is a fair wage to pay their workers, then naturally, all workers will be underpaid. It is only human nature, those at the top of the economic ladder will allow greed to take hold.\n\nHowever, that does not mean that the elimination of capitalism is the solution. While that would, admittedly, destroy the income inequality among nations, it would also prevent any meritocracy at all from being formed.\n\nSo, what is the answer to this dichotomy? Mutualism, the belief that government involvement should regulate industry to the point where the working class is able to survive by default of simply living in their own society.\n\nIt is immoral and unethical to allow the working class, the backbone of a society, to go hungry, homeless, or poor, simply because their employer has refused to pay them enough to survive.\n\nTherefor, the government and the state should intervene, setting up a default, minimum standard of living, which no individual may fall beneath. With the introduction of methods such as a minimum wage, -\n\nindustry regulation, social assistance, welfare, and much more, the government can create a safety net of sorts, a level of poverty which one musn't ever fall beneath.\n\nThis standard is to be determined by objective, measurable statistics. For example, how much wealth does one need to posess in order to pay for housing, food, clothing, and other necessary services?\n\nIf those essential necessities are covered, then no extra luxuries are to be granted to those at the bottom of the economic ladder. From there on out, capitalism is to take hold, and individuals are responsible for-\n\nprocuring their own wealth in the free market. This isn't to say that further regulation cannot be imposed on the industry to ensure that one individual or business creates a single corporate monopoly over one industry, or -\n\nso that the workers are not unfairly paid, but it does mean that the private market must be the primary benefactor of the majority of citizens. You cannot create a socialist state, in which everyone is dependent on the public sector, for -\n\nthat would be the opposite of a meritocracy.\n\nTo conclude, the answer to creating an economy where workers are paid a fair amount for equal amounts of labor is not free market capitalism, but rather, the embracement of mutualism, socialism, and regulation.\n\n\n\n\n\n~ Bell Acaele'par Amuel R. Sano", ""),
        StaticBook("Slavery Essay.", "§bAwylan Wistari", "SLAVERY\n         The Vile\n      Afterthought\n-------------------\n\nAwylan Wistari\nBell Sano\n\n13th of The First Seed, 1630\n\nFOREWARD:\nNot too long after Bell Sano and I began this essay, he succumbed to the hands of time. Bell was a rather old, fighting spirit who had the intellect of an owl who’s gaze pierced the landscape, and the resilience of a\n\nwarrior iron-clad in the armor of courage and virtue. It is in his honor that this essay is published to the Dragur library, and disseminated across the lands for all to see. The only contribution Bell was able to\n\nmake to this essay was the introductory paragraph, the rest of it was composed by myself with his inspiration and memory.\n\nSincerely,\nAwylan Wistari\n\nINTRODUCTION:\n(1614, Bell Sano)\n The institution of slavery is one which has existed for centuries, at least. It’s longevity is emblematic of the normalization of it in society, and the complacent attitudes of many\n\nindividuals who bare witness to its atrocities daily. Atrocities that have been long ignored, relegated to the category of normalcy in everyday life, looked upon as being efficient ways of\n\nearning revenue. Atrocities that have devalued each and every subject of its horrors, atrocities that have converted our perception of our fellow man to that of mere chattel.\n\nSlavery is an institution which is so deplorable, abysmal, ungodly, and immoral, that no modern day, civilized society has deemed it anything but acceptable.\n\n  Slavery is a practice which has been instituted for generations. The first documented case of slavery is not clearly detailed, but it’s origins can be traced back to the Rexdom of Krugmar, the former\n\nwar nation of the Orcs in Aegis. Originally a group of nomadic people, the brutality of the Orcish race allowed themselves to freely capture and obtain slaves of other races, domestically being addressed as \"Snagas.\"\n\nAround the early 1300’s, records of slavery began to arise. To this day, this practice continues. Even outside of the savagery of the Orcs, other races have previously adopted the institution of slavery, including that of humans.\n\nWithin the Orenian empire, for example, certain situations would legally permit slavery within the Empire. Even up until the mid 1550’s, slavery was legally acceptable.\n\nEven other nations, such as Haria, have been noted to tolerate slavery. However, simply because it is a historically widespread practice, does not make it justified.\n\nCh. 1 - A Living Being, not Property\n\nThe core component of this vicious, vexing institution is how it relegates its subjects - so called slaves - to the category of chattel. To the slavemaster or\n\nthe slave trader, the being who’s veins course with the same red blood as the rest of us, who breathe the same air we do, who function as we do is nothing more than property. Nothing more than another product to be\n\nsold and bartered for in the marketplace of this godforsaken practice. The slave master and slave trader use this terminology to do the following:\n\n1)\nAbsolve themselves of any possible blame that could come with brutally mistreating a living being.\n\n2)\nDehumanize their subject as to not feel any possible guilt that their practices would entail.\n\n3)\nJustify their practices as being nothing more than good business.\n\nOf course, despite their best efforts the truth remains a constant, unchanging like a stream flowing into a lake. The truth is that any being, no matter the external labels imposed upon their being, is a living being.\n\nProperty is not living, property is not able to think or do for itself, living beings are. Something is not stripped of it’s livelihood or it’s state of living merely by the arbitrary whim of the slave master or the slave trader, and\n\nall of those who anoint themselves with the power to arbitrate who is worthy of seeing common decency and who is not are those whom are pathological narcisscists and need to be excised from society.\n\nOther than doing the aforementioned, by calling living beings property we add a new dimension to the word property. It logically follows that if one person can annoint themselves the authority to deem others\n\nproperty, why couldn’t another follow? Not to delve into the slippery slope theory, which is faulty because it’s conclusion doesn’t follow from it’s premises, but there is a standard set by behavior in a particular\n\nsociety which may explain why the institution of slavery has flourished to the extent that it has.\n\nCh. 2 - The Self and Slavery\n\nThe self is defined as one’s core faculties, that which is internal to the being, their personality, their individuality, their abilities and their talents.\n\nEssentially, all that which composes the being of the individual, that constitutes the person, is what the “self is”. As mentioned previously, slavery seeks to subjugate the self and metamorphize it into a\n\ndried up husk of human skin, lumbering mindlessly at the arbitrary whim of the slave master.\n\nCh. 4 - Slavery is Inefficient\n\nWhen the self is neglected, is that piece of property truly a utility to its self-proclaimed owner? Think, when someone when has been stripped of everything\n\nthey knew to be true and are forced to act under the iron jackboot of a tyrant and have lost any and every sense of individuality and free will, which is the core energizer of the self, what incentive do they have to do\n\nwhat they command? The very few that DO have incentive, indeed, tend to be interested in one thing only - survival. Those are not true slaves, they are captives with a will to persist.\n\nBut the many who do not will not be compelled by anything, not even the bullwhip, to work efficiently for their master. If we accept that prospect, then wouldn’t it logically follow  that the institution is not as efficient as it\n\ncould be - or at all for that matter - as it pertains to productivity and the amount of outputs that the slave owner seeks to derive from labor that isn’t his (which is theft, a moral obscenity within itself as I will discuss shortly)?\n\nIF we accept THIS to be true, then wouldn’t it follow that due to it’s inefficiency that the slave owners are better off providing incentives to self-retaining beings, perhaps\n\nin the form of monetary reward, and providing the highest wage to he who labored most efficiently?\n\nCh. 5 - Slavery is Expensive\n\nTo ensure the efficient and prosperous operation of their nations, Governments must at the very least provide for a standing army, other defenses and laws geared to securing\n\nthe rights of the individual  to ensure the harmonious existence of their peoples. This is costly to the state exchequer in itself, to further expend the resources within the Kingdom’s treasury to provide for the\n\nmaintenance and health of what the King deems as his property, the slave, will do nothing more than drain the pocket of the crown. And that isn’t beneficial to the goals of the King or his “property.\"\n\nCh. 6 - IN CLOSING\n\nWhen the barbarous, primitive practice of slavery is abolished, we will be able to further ascend towards an era of enlightenment and prosperity.\n\nWhen we begin to see our fellow man not as property, but as an individual composed of his own individual benefits and his individual faults, we will finally have discovered that long forsaken covenant of\n\nfellowship that cowered at the harrowing sounds of the bullwhip.\nWe can only get there should practices like this fall to the ashes of history and blow away with them.\n\nThat is what we all should strive for, and that is what the late Bell Sano would’ve wanted.", ""),
        StaticBook("Book of Aengul", "§bSavet Yvonus", "There once lived a hairy wizard named Harry. He was so hairy, that the hairs on his hairy body seemed to have hairs covering their hairs. It was an odd sight to behold, as this boy named Harry seemed like a hairy ball of hair.\n\nIn school, everyone called him Hairy Harry, and he, despite being unaturally hairy, hated the nickname. But one day, he discovered he could control his hair, and bend it to his will. Mayhap he was a beardmancer, but it extended to all his body hair.\n\nSo Hary Harry entangled all the bullies within his hairy hair, and absorbed their hair with his own. He grew, and his hair grew, until he was known as Hairy Harry, the hair-ridden menace. So Hairy Harry, the hair-ridden menace went about, causing\n\nhavoc with his hair, engulfing people within his hairy depths, asborbing their hair until he was the ultimate god of the universe. All hair belonged to him, and Hairy Harry transcended.\n\nThus, the aengul of body hair was born.\n\nAll hail Hairy Harry.\n\nAll hail Hair.\n\nBrush your hair, brush your beard, or Hairy Harry will come for you.\n\nShaving and cutting hair is against his will.\n\nDo not displease Hairy Harry.", ""),
        StaticBook("AdventurersNotes", "§bUnknown Source", "I do not think I have much longer to live, no, I shall not be so negative! ...It has already become a struggle to write, I believe I am going to faint soon. It hurt a lot at first but I think I might recover soon. At least, that is what the numbness\n\nmeans, I hope. \nHowever uncertainty is like a thick blanket enveloping this small grotto and I will write down my adventure here lest I am unable to tell this tall tale someday. At least someone will know what happened to me. I am glad my hands\n\nspared, I do enjoy writing. \nMy name is Almira Smithsdottir. I am twenty-nine years old and a human, a heartlander. I came upon this foreboding cave while fleeing from my home after misunderstanding with my husband. He probably\n\nshouting at me now, ha! That’ll show him.\nWe’re happy, most of the time. But we were both born hot-headed and neither of us backs down easily. Oh well. Hopefully he will think of coming to look for me soon.\nI found this cave a few miles away\n\nafter an hour wandering through the forest. It was unwise for I hear that scum lurks beneath the cool shadows of these impressive trees, but an angered woman pays little attention to logic. I came into this cave when I saw some clouds\n\ngathering upon the horizon, I had one of my good dresses on and ruining it was not an option\nI’m lying near the entrance now, crawling wasn’t very comfortable but I wanted people to see me if they came looking. The rock around me is\n\ngathering upon the horizon, I had one of my good dresses on and ruining it was not an option\nI’m lying near the entrance now, crawling wasn’t very comfortable but I wanted people to see me if they came looking. The rock around me is\n\nblackened and burned, it was the first sign that intrigued me upon entering it. When I saw a light farther inside I decided to investigate.\nI didn’t find another adventurer, I found a long bridge over a lake of molten rock. I had never seen\n\nsuch a thing, only heard of it! The rock bridge was glowing prettily and I approached it to get a closer look. The heat didn’t bother me, I like being warm.\nI hadn’t gotten six feet that the molten rock began to bubble! I stepped forward to look\n\nand a burst of flame erupted from the lava, it struck me around the midriff. I think I screamed a lot as at it ate my robe and skin. Everything is red and blistering now, swollen beyond proportional norms. I would like some water.\nI fell back and\n\nsaw something in the lava, it was hazy but I will swear it upon the life of my good for nothing husband. There was a head poking out of the liquid fire and staring at me with eyes of burning rock. It laughed at me and faded back into it’s pool.\n\n\nI crawled away, I think I left a lot of my skin on the rough rocks, it grated against me but I didn’t feel it, I was too scared. I am glad of that. \nOh! I feel dizzy i thnk I shoulz re---___ \n/", ""),
        StaticBook("Valley", "§bAscanius Dunlain", "In the valley of the old ones, the accursed waning moon shines thinly, earing a path for its light with feeble horns through the lethal foliage of a great Elder Tree. \nAnd within the depths of the valley, where light reaches not, move forms not be beheld.\n\nRank is the herbage on each slope, where evil vines and creeping plants crawl amidst the stones of ruined palaces, twining tightly about broken columns and strange monoliths, and heaving up marble pavements laid by forgotten hands. And in trees that -\n\ngrow gigantic in crumbling courtyards leap little apes, while in and out of deep treasure-vaults writhe poison serpents and scaly things without a name. Vast are the stones which sleep beneath coverlets of dank moss. and mighty were the walls from which -\n\nthey fell. For all time did their builders erect them, and in sooth they yet serve nobly, for beneath them the grey toad makes his habitation.\n\n At the very bottom of the valley lies the river of blue, whose waters are slimy and filled with weeds. From hidden springs it rises, and to subterranean grottoes it flows, so that the Demon of the Valley knows not why its waters are red, nor whither -\n\nthey are bound.\n\n The Genie that haunts the moonbeams spake to the Demon of the Valley, saying, \"I am old, and forget much. Tell me the deeds and aspect and name of them who built these things of Stone.\" And the Demon replied, \"I am Memory, and am wise in lore of the -\n\npast.  but I too am old. These beings were like the waters of the river Than, not to be understood. Their deeds I recall not, for they were but of the moment. Their aspect I recall dimly, it was like to that of the little apes in the trees. \n Their name -\n\nI recall clearly, for it rhymed with that of the river. These beings of yesterday were called Man.\" \n So the Genie flew back to the thin horned moon, and the Demon looked intently at a little ape in a tree that grew in a crumbling courtyard.\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n Ascanius of Fenn.", ""),
        StaticBook("Grove", "§bAscanius Tathvir", "High up, crowning the cold summit of a swelling mount whose sides are wooded near the base with the gnarled trees of the primeval forest stands the chateau of my ancestors. For centuries its lofty battlements have frowned down upon the wild and rugged\n\ncountryside below, serving as both home and stronghold for the proud house whose honoured line is older than even the moss-grown castle walls.  These ancient turrets, stained by storms and generations that followed begin to ruin as the slow grains\n\nof time make their debute.\n The shadowy groves and ruins that hold refuge within our walls have seemed begin effort to cast away the wares of decay and time, at last you may see a gate of bronze emerge from the wares of time, possibly just one of the\n\nfew spoils in time.\n\n The valley to the East, blanketed with yellow papyrus with the thoughts of sages who dwelt far in the void. Some sages wrote gorgeously of the wonders beyond the irrepassable gate, but others told of horror and sorrow.\n\nI knew not which to believe, yet longed more to cross forever into the shadowy grove; for secrecy is the lure of lures. No horrors can be more terrible than the daily torture of common place, so conjured a plan I had.\n\n Last night I took on the essence of void; departure of body but not of soul. I came to the gate in a different state, the grove no longer overgrown, but yet midly untamed. The bronze gate cracked ajar as to heed my goal. From beyond came a glow that\n\nweirdly lit the giant twisted trees and the tops of the buried ruins,, and I drifted on, expectant of glories from this ripple in time.\n As the ground began to shake and drift aimlessly, rippling towards both the sky and hell, I knew that all sights and\n\nall glories were at an end; for this ripple in time was neither land nor sea, but only the void of unpeopled and illimitable space. I dissolved again into that native infinity of crystal oblivion from which the daemon life had called me for one brief and\n\ndesolate hour.\n\n\n Signed,\n         Ascanius of Fenn.\n\n\"The Age of The New Gods is on horizon\" - Unknown", ""),
        StaticBook("Arctic Flower", "§bNerah", "*There would be a large picture of a Reindeer.*\n\nArctic Flower\n\nTold By Laeila\nWritten By Nerah\n\nI stumbled upon an abandoned Inemho camp just outside the city of Sutica. There I lived off whatever I could find inside of the storage house. \nI had to live in that camp for several weeks before people started to notice my presence around the area.\n\nI met a female wood elf and she was a very beautiful woman. She took care of me every now and then and thats how I also met Aiden.\n\nI found other children. Other Inemho children! They were younger than I was and therefore I had to take care of them.\n\nWe also found a few friends to play with. Oh how innocent we were back in the day. We built a camp up in the mountains where it was cold and comfortable.\n\nTogether with my daugthers I now had a home and family.\n\nWith heart and soul I held for our friends a great speech! A speech meant to inspire them to further my people's cause and to ensure that they will support us until the very end.\n\nOur life was lovely, simple, joyful and most of all hopeful.\n\nLong nights I spent watching the dark sky filled with stars and how my breath left clouds of steam in the moonlight. \n\nOh how wonderful it was. My darlings started to grow older and older which I also did. I suddenly felt more worry.\nAh!\n\nI had run into a very common problem with a problematic twist. Boys! I must have been around fifteen winters old and.. Of course I was starting to have feelings of attraction towards the other gender.\n\nI wanted to find a partner very early and have more children to ensure the survival of my people and for one of the younger children I had adopted to have a younger sibling.\n\nAnd oh how strange the hunt was!\n\nI walked around the outsider cities with dreams of finding males my age. I cannot even recall how many times I searched the streets of Sutica.\n\nHow many times I asked the adults I knew if they knew any suitors of sorts.\n\nI cried whenever my children left me alone to 'work' because I feared that I was letting them down. I had to face the facts.\n\nThe harsh truth that the outsider men would never be as interested in an Inemho woman as they would be towards an outsider woman.\n\nThey walked with clothes I could not wear due to my size or due to my daily tasks. My second skin had become not only an armour against cold, but also an armor against the love of outsiders.\n\nThe few people interested in me being unable to have me bear human children and most of them far above my age. One offered himself to me in return for all of my power, all of my will, my freedom and the future of my people.\n\nHow strange of a time this was, the frustration just growing more and more intense as time passed. I was no longer the happy child I used to be, I was a very young adult with the world on my shoulders.\n\nHow painful! Oh how dreadful!\n\nThe world crumbling apart! Suddenly.. More and more people came to join the camp, came to join us as my children. . . all but one turned out to be my child.\n\nHe was difficult to talk to sometimes, he was stronger than I could ever hope to become, he had blue eyes unlike my brown ones.\n\nI lost hope. It was difficult to imagine us being together and therefore I searched outside the tribe but..\n\nI could never find anyone else so interesting. No other person could possibly accept me as I was and. . . Soon enough I couldn't stand it anymore. After a full night of praying and wishing.. \n\nI think he started to like me. I liked him too.\n\nOne day he just.. Asks me for my knife. Oh how I longed for his sweet embrace after I accepted his proposal.\n\nOh how happy I was! My own husband.. Faithful and Handsome. Loving and caring..\n\nAfter trying to seduce him into giving me a child for a few years I managed to get pregnant. And to this day I still try whenever I feel that I have spare time. Taking care of children or guests is what I love.", ""),
        StaticBook("Modern Warfare", "§bEdward Pavel", "Written on the 12th of Sun's Smile, 1152.\nEdward Pavel\n\n ~ Modern Warfare ~\n\n    The topic of modern warfare is deep and controversial, with each culture's style varying in massive differences as time goes along.\n\nHowever, there lies several core principles that govern all warfare waged upon our world. Much of the warfare seen in history comes from the Humans of Oren, diversity shown between either human cultures in civil disputes or Human clashes in foreign lands\n\nthat employ their own style of combat. There are three types of troops that have been used in all the combined history: Infantry, Archers, and Cavalry. Interestingly enough, Cavalry was not seen until the latter parts of existence, within the Fringe. We\n\nwill dive deeper into this later in the book. \n\nThink of warfare as a mixture of colors. You have red, yellow, and blue. However, if you mix these three, you will witness a wonderful multitude of colors and accents. Such is the same with warfare.\n\nA nation's success on the battlefield will be determined on how they use the variables present to them, and how much of each they have. Numerical superiority is an extremely important aspect to warfare, though I fear, from a scholar's perspective, it has\n\nbeen the sole focus throughout the ages. Through gauging numerical advantages and disadvantages, an inexperienced general may /think/ he can determine the outcome of a battle. However, it is the clever employment of infantry, archery, and cavalry that\n\nwill determine the outcome of the battle.\nLastly, what must be taken into account is the world around the armies waging war. Current conditions of the day, elevation, terrain, and rivers must be taken into account to properly mount a successful attack.\n\nWe will now elaborate somewhat on the points discussed so far.\n\n~Troop Size~\nAs I have stated before, the size of your army will play a major factor into a battle. However, it must never be mistaken as a winning factor. It is must always be understood as\n\na tool. There are many instances of when large armies walked into traps or made mistakes themselves, resulting in the slaughter from numerically inferior armies. A nation that greatly pulls on numbers is none but Orenia itself. Relying upon a large\n\nindigenous population of Heartlanders, Highlanders, and Farfolk, the Human race is known for sweeping the lands with shocking numbers to crush any opposition. However, they have faced significant opposition from better equiped armies in the past,\n\nsuch as Urguan.\n\n~Infantry~\nInfantry is the most popular usage of troops, and has stood the test of time. Flanks and front on assaults are devastating when used properly. Infantry has been deployed into \"Blob\" formations mostly,\n\ncatering to commanders who, again, favored the numerical advantage more than anything. Under a well disciplined army, the blob formation will fail time and time again. Further formations and an indepth analysis of the Blob Formation will be elaborated on\n\nin a seperate book.\n\n~Archery~\nArchery is as ancient as infantry, and is deployed mostly in sieges though it shares a significant role in field battles as well. Archery is most effective in suppression fire, where large amounts\n\nof archers fire into an oncoming blob formation (or formal charge) to suppress them and damage the enemy before contact is made with both side's infantry. This has determined the outcome of battle many times. Elite archers in the past have been known to\n\npick off weaker enemies with their range and devastating skill. When an archery barrage is in place, widespread panic is placed within the enemy. This is effective for numerous reasons. Archers are usually placed within an army to a 70% - 30% ratio,\n\narchers being the lower number. Though they are powerful, keep note that as soon as an infantry unit clashes with an archery unit, it is a very clear victory.\n\n~Cavalry~\nAh, the most unexplored and peculiar of options.\n\nUnlike infantry and archery, cavalry was introduced late into the Fringe. It was used by a special corps in the Holy Orenian Empire, employed against the army of the Krughanistan Bloc. A large force of thirty cavalry were used by the Imperials in a\n\ndecisive battle. Due to inexperience and widespread panic, the cavalry was slaughtered and the notion dropped by the Empire as an effective tactic. It was not used again majorly until Vailor. A young Orenian nobleman known has Xavier de Sola observed\n\nthe Orcs of the searing deserts use this tactic in battle. An Orenian host had found themselves trapped in the desert while Orcish cavalry assaulted them in every direction. Panic ensued as slowly, each man of the Orenian regiment died. This was later put\n\nto practice in the Duke's War, the de Sola's harkening in a new age of cavalry where horse infantry and horse archery was explored. Though it has become a staple in battle for mounted warriors to be used, it has /not/ been found to be in correlation with\n\ntactical procedures. Instead, many riders act on their own volition and judgement. However, the de Sola use of organized, quick, and deadly cavalry has been lost as the house went extinct. The theoritical employment of cavalry tactics shall be explored\n\nin a later time.\n\n~Terrain~\n\nTerrain matters most to the placement of castles, but also the positioning of armies. Fighting uphill yields a significant advantage to infantry as they yield a larger range with a sword,\n\nbut otherwise a significant disadvantage as archery makes easy picking for the soldiers ascending uphill. Fighting at night is obscure and leads to many deaths on both sides if not taken into account properly. Crossing a river is dangerous and costly if\n\nan enemy presence is near by. Crossing a river by cavalry is twice as dangerous. These are all examples of Terrain and their effects on battle. The good commander will take into account the route that is most beneficial and the terrain they rather would\n\nfight on; the foolish general will disregard terrain and claim superiority in whatever terrain. A smart general will place his troops in the underbrush and wait, the foolish general will charge his cavalry through the forest to cut time spent on the road.\n\nSuch costly mistakes are what determiune the outcome of battles. Terrain's uses and historical narratives shall be included in later books.\n\nThis book serves as a brief summary over the main central aspects of warfare, however there is\n\nmuch more to be elaborated on in further books. Such a book that contains /all/ there is to know about the tactical world of warfare will consist of hundreds of pages. To ease the reader, these topics will be split into seperate books where each subject\n\nwill be put under vigorous speculation and elaboration. While I aim to educate the reader on modern warfare, it is nevertheless essential that history be understood as well. Those who do not understand history are doomed to repeat it! It is because of\n\nthis we will be exploring many past major battles to fully grasp the concept of warfare and what the critical elements are that one must use to successfully win a battle. We will explore the minds of the monumental Generals of our history to discover\n\ntheir ingenuity and personal attributes that led to success. I hope you are as excited as I am to explore the art of Modern Warfare.\n\nSigned,\nEdward Pavel", ""),
        StaticBook("The Coronation", "§bLilyana", "In the dark of night, an elder man hobbles with a walking stick towards the quiet village. The man’s curiosity is pricked by the silence in the town, a town that once was bustling with life regardless of the time. But, the pain in his back and ache in his\n\nfeet quickly nudged any questions from his mind as he hobbled along the path. He had been traveling for days, braving the wilderness and streets to reach this town, and finally he was close to his destination. However, he had no idea what he was heading\n\nto or why he started this journey. He awoke one morning, some days ago, and felt a tingling sensation in his fingertips, one he had not felt for years. As the days passed, the sensation slowly began to spread throughout his body and the tingling became\n\nstronger; he began to feel an urgency to understand what was causing it. Only days ago had he remembered what this feeling, this sensation, was; it was the excitement, the rush of energy, the craving for blood he felt before he killed a target of the\n\nCrimson Fist. Though his body old and tired now with age, this sensation revitalized him enough to send him into the unknown, to this very town. With each step, the pull on him became stronger, more intense, until now, as he stood outside a large barn,\n\nthe only lit building in the entire town, did he feel like he would burst from excitement. He licked his chapped lips, wrapped his wrinkled hands around the bar, and pulled with all his might on the door, opening it.\n\n    Cora danced around the flame\n\n the center of the barn, its light dancing along the walls. The deep crimson blood markings and gold jewelry that she wore contrasted against her pale skin. She paid the old man no attention, although she knew full well of his presence, and continued to\n\ndance around the fire, chanting verses of an old Crimson ritual. As the old man stepped into the light of the fire, Evaine quieted her chanting and slowed her dance. She stopped on the side of the wall where a robe of deep crimson hung on a peg. She\n\nfluidly placed the robe about her shoulders then made her way to a corner of the barn that the fire's light did not reach. She looked back over her shoulder, smirking at the old man, before disappearing into the shadows.\n\n The old man scanned\n\nthe barn with his old eyes, his poor ears only hearing the crackling of the fire. He saw nothing, heard nothing, but his very being knew someone, or something was there. From across the fire, from under the shadow of the barn's hay loft, two piercing red\n\neyes broke the darkness and stared at the man, as if they were staring into his soul. The sensation from earlier now rocked the elder; he clung to his walking stick as a force of power pulled him down onto his knees. The owner of the glowing eyes stepped\n\ninto the light of the flame, revealing himself to be an abnormally tall, toned, young man, Haemon. His hair of white gold flowed to his shoulder, his skin as pale as snow, but his eyes, they glowed like lumps of red, hot coal, burning in his eye sockets.\n\nHaemon walked around the fire, slowly approaching the elder. With each step, the elder gripped his walking stick tighter as the power that the boy was emanating tried harder and harder to pull him to the floor. When the boy stood over the old man, he was\n\nshaking with strain and effort to remain kneeling and barely spat out the words before collapsing:\n\n“M-M-My…..L-L-Lord-d-d….M-My P-Prince”\n\nWhen the old man awoke, he found himself sitting against the wall of the barn.\n\nHe felt a sharp pain at his arm and upon inspection found it bandaged tightly, a small blood stain slowly spreading on it. He went to tug on the bandage but a delicate hand quickly grabbed his hand and pulled it from the wound. The elder looked up,\n\nmeeting Cora’s gaze as she slowly shook her head. She pulled out a skin full of water and offered it to the man who, only realizing his thirst at the sight of the skin, quickly took it from her and drank it down. She left him a small plate, some bread and\n\ncheese, and walked around the flame to the other side of the fire. Following her movement, the old man realized that the boy had been sitting across from him this entire time, watching him. Cora slid down along the wall until she was next to the boy, then\n\ncurled herself against him, passing him a vial of a crimson liquid that the old man knew all too well, a vial of blood, his blood.\n\nHaemon lifted the vial to face level, staring at it as the fire's light illuminated the contents. Haemon smiled and as\n\nfor his name.\n\n\"Eren\", the old man responded.\n\nHaemon shook his head and smiled again, but this time his eyes glowed and a voice unlike the previous one asked for his “true name”. The old man dropped hid bit\n\nof cheese and drew his limbs into him. His gaze met the fiery gaze of Haemon and memories of a life he tried hard to forget washed over him.\n\n\"Doulos, my lord.\" The old man said, maintaining eye contact with Haemon as he spoke, \"Servant to you and yo\n\ncause.\"\n\nHaemon nodded and tossed the vial of blood into the fire. The flame erupted into a shower of sparks and turned black as the night around them, all except for the center which glowed with light. The light soon warped and changed and the old m\n\nwatched his own memories, his life from his eyes play before him for all to see. He watched the battle where the temple fell where he fought as a mere Doulos, a soldier and servant to the Crimson Prince’s cause. His escape into the woods as the temple\n\ncollapsed, his struggle for survival, his search for others, his attempts to rebuild what was lost. But alas, he watched himself give into what seemed to be reality that no others had survived, and watched as he isolated himself from the world, locking\n\nthe few relics of his past life away in a chest.\n\nThe flames died down, the color returned to its orange and red glow, and the barn returned to the quiet it had once been. Haemon stood before the flame and spoke of how few of his followers survived t\n\nbattle. He made a point to mention how few had attempted to continue his cause and gracefully pointed to the hay-loft above. The elder’s vision followed Haemon’s direction until it, only now, noticed countless bodies in the loft above, wrinkled and dry,\n\nseemingly drained of their blood. The man reeled back in fear from Haemon, but Haemon only smiled and waved his hand in front of him. He reassured the man that their fate was the fate of cowards and betrayers, those that tried to hide their connection to\n\nhim. \n\n“But the few,” Haemon said as he waved his hand to Cora and back to the old man, “the few that stayed true to me now reap great rewards.”\n\nHaemon explained how the rituals Core and he performed summoned the small\n\nbit of power that the Crimson Prince left in this world. That ritual created a connection between Haemon and the Crimson Prince; that the Prince now acted through Cora’s child, Haemon.\n\n\"I must feed on the blood of the living, fueling my power to all\n\nthe Prince to return to this world as his true self. We have been traveling to settlements, slowly feasting on its populace as my power grows in strength with each feasting.” Haemon pointed above to the bodies. \"It seems as my power grows, those of the\n\nold Crimson Fist that had survived are drawn to us. We’ve tested those that come, and those to have hidden from their past have been feasted on. While those who were true to our prince, have been given power.”\n\nThe old man perked up. \"Power, my lord?\n\nWhat do you mean?\"\n\nHaemon’s eyes glowed bright, his power exerting itself in the room once more. The fire reached for the ceiling as Haemon lifted his right hand from his side. As his hand lifted, so did the elder man, levitating him in mid-air. Hae\n\nwithdrew a silver dagger and sliced a thin line down his right forearm. Haemon began to recite a dark chant from deep within his mind and the blood that was slowly seeping from the wound began to rise into the air. The blood hovered over to the elder man\n\nand began to circulate around him, slowly at first but picking up speed quickly. With quick movement, Haemon shut his fist closed, forcing the blood that spun around the old man to suddenly stop and bury its way into his body. The old man howled with pain\n\n for only a moment before his eyes glazed over and his screaming silenced. The man’s body erupted into black flames, devouring him entirely, burning the flesh from his very bones. Cora stood and approached Haemon, wrapping her arms around his torso and\n\nshoulder as they watched on together. The Black Flame finally dissipated, leaving a figure in a crimson cloak where the old man once was.\n\n“Arise”, Haemon ordered with a voice not his own, “ Arise, my new Blood Mage.”\n\nThe figure stood from\n\nthe ash of the black fire and removed his hood, revealing Eren, but as his once youthful self. Eren stared at his hands, no longer wrinkled and weak; he felt his face for saggy skin and scars of old age but only found the tight, tough skin. He felt\n\nrevitalized, no empowered. The ritual had given him a small piece of his lord’s power, and that small piece had not only turned back time to when the old man was once called Doulos, it gave him strength, power, and life.\n\n\"Blood, the essence\n\nf life, is quite a powerful catalyst, as you now see with your own eyes, Doulos. It’s power is only limited by the Mage’s imagination.” Haemon said as Cora wrapped a small bandage around his wrist. \"Ours, theirs, it matters not where it comes from, but\n\nhe purity, power, and amount, that determines the strength of magic that comes from it.” Haemon showed the wound to Doulos, “Until our true lord is able to come into this world our magic is limited, but still powerful.”\n\nDoulos nodded, \"So what is th\n\nnext step? How do we bring forth our Lord, once and for all?\"\n\nCora stepped forward, revealing documents that had thought to have been lost with the years. “Cruor Veneficus, the Blood Tome. A magical tome that the Crimson Fist once had. If we were\n\nto reclaim this tome, we would be able to channel the magical energy from it, making our magic infinite and allow Haemon to focus his feeding on bringing forth our Lord.”\n\nDoulos nodded in agreement and asked \"But where do we start looking for the\n\ntome?\"\n\nCora smiled, “According to the documentation we found on the betrayers and cowards mentions the Cruor Veneficus last being seen in the Crimson Fist’s stronghold in the mountains of the North, the mountains\n\nwhere the settlement “Raven’s Nest” now stands. Word on the street of this town was that a coronation of some sort is to take place there as well, bringing in many guests.” Cora smiled a toothy grin, “If we do not find the Cruor Veneficus, at least there\n\nwill be many for my Prince to feast on.\"\n\n “Raven’s Nest is heavily defended and manned, how are we to take the city?” Doulos questioned.\n\nYou are not the only Blood Mage, Duolos.” Haemon answered as he motioned for Cora to open the barn's\n\ndoor. “There have been others that I found worthy to bestow power upon, like yourself, that now hide themselves amongst the cities of this land. They pretend to normal folk of their race, gathering information, and working their way into cities and\n\ngovernments.\" Haemon motioned outside the barn’s open door where the sunrise was just peeking over the horizon. The low light illuminated many hooded figures walking towards them. \"And many more followers are being drawn here, as you were, and they will\n\night alongside us, wielding powerful Blood Magicks.”\n\nHis questions answered and his mind set straight, Doulus nodded and resigned. \"Yes, my Lord. Raven's Nest cannot, will not, stand against our power and cause. He smiled widely,\n\n\"Our Lord, our Crismon Prince, will rise once more”.\n\n      The Coronation\n            of the\n        True Prince\n\n  A Sequel to the\n Rebirth of Evil\n\n\n\nWritten by: Lilyana", ""),
        StaticBook("Vagmaamm", "§bVallakai Vallakovich", "Ledger On Vagmaamm\n\nDay One: I found him on the side of a road, staring at a rock. He likes rocks. he really, really likes rocks. I took him back to town, and now he stays in the basement. Oh, and Vagmaamm is a golem. A nice golem\n\nDay 2: Vagmaamm vanished this morning. We found him in Holm, as a Golemancer had called him. N____, E____, and I got him back to _R___ where we took him to stay. he vanished in the Saint's Afternoon.\n\nDay 3: I am now Vagmaamm's Impera. It's good that he's there. He's a good person.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Angry Gay", "§bGregory", "The Angry Gay\n  -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nOur story begins at the library of Dragur. \n\nGregory is a rampant homosexual, whose repulsive urges often lead him into sin. The world cannot accept Gregory for who\n\nhe is, and this makes him...\n\nAngry.\n\nGregory tried to take anger management classes, but his instructor was a gorgeous man who he could not have, and this made him angrier.\n\nThe Angry Gay, AKA Gregory, one day stumbled upon a stranger who appeared to have been chiseled by the Skygods themselves, and his name was Bastien.\n\nNo longer was Gregory attracted to men, for now his love\n\nrested with a Golem.\n\nAt last, thought the angry gay, I am cured of my homosexuality.\n\nAnd he celebrated.\n\nBut it was not to be.\n\nFor Bastien, was a male golem.\n\n\n\n\nEnd.", ""),
        StaticBook("Scares V1", "§bAiyla Torena", "-=Stories=-\n1. Lonely\n2. My eyes\n3. Fire\n4. Butcher\n5. Help..\n\n     -+=Lonely=+-\n\nIt was cold and dark...\nAll i could hear was the blood curdling screams of my friends as they were thrown into small rooms of iron.. The door to my cell was locked, that's when i relized, i was never to see the outside world ag\n\n    (+) My Eyes (+)\nI run through the forest in pitch black. the night never seems to end... the footsteps become louder and louder as i run. Where am i going? What am i running from? I reach up to rub my eyes.. then i relize.. Where are my eyes?\n\n         <>Fire<>\nI walk up to a crowd shouting and screaming about a witch, i fix my gaze to see a young girl about to be burned at the stake... A man lights the fire and all i see is smoke fill up around me... i relize that i am the one in the fire..\n\n      -*Butcher*-\nI'm lost.\nI enter a shop.\nI see a man,\nhe tries to help me.\nTaken into the back, \nI am grabbed,\nThe last thing i saw?\nThe Butchers knife..\n\n         Help..\nI am stuck to a seat writing my stories, I can't get up, i can't move.. it's like i am possesed, there is nothing else to say or write about... What should i do? Can anyone hear me scream? Help..", ""),
        StaticBook("Ode to Bastien", "§bGregory", "Ode to Bastien\n\n\n\n§iBy Gregory O'Donovan\n\n\n\n\nThis book is a publication of Gregory Press.\n\nAll Rights Reserved.\n\n1650.\n\nTo those that are unaware of Bastien, he is a simple construct. A golem of a single core, a single mind, but of great purpose.\n\nYou see for what he lacks within words and basic intelligence he holds a childlike charm. Patrolling the halls of this library\n\nwith unquestionable devotion. \n\nHis practically famous saying, \"Welcome to the Library.\" has been commonplace within the words of great beings. Nevermind Tahariae, Xan or Iblees. Bastien is truly an god for all those that meet him.\n\nSomeone speaks too loudly? There he charges, mission in hand as he shushes the intolerable swine that dare break the beautiful silence. \n\nSomeone tries to do harm to the books? He shall break them in two, even now I imagine Dragur himself looking\n\non proudly. \n\nWhilst at first you barely listened to a word I said, now the magical adventures we've been upon remain some of the finest moments in my life. \n\nSailing across the ocean within the titanic, handing out leaflets\n\nto the wizard Blundermore to ensure he knows where we are at all times, truly magical. \n\nIf one has never had the pleasure of meeting Bastien I must insist you meet him yourself, within seconds the glimmering stone of his skin\n\nwill catch your eye. His famous saying ringing within your ears, and your life forver changed for the better.\n\nHowver, on the contray.\n\nHe's dumb af.", ""),
        StaticBook("\"Weeping Willow\"", "§b[Cloaked] Willow", "\"A heart for heart, Druids for a grove, grove of Malinor, A father for me? . . . Trees will cry, Willow will die.\"\n   \"Weeping Willow\"\n\nIt all began with my upbringing in Malinor... I was an annoying child who grew a big mouth. \n  I was raised with no father. I spent my daily life being hurt, attacked or ignored...\n My mother, or so I called her for years without knowing the truth,\n\nShe's a druid. Was, and is. She tried to be a druid, and a mother.\n Who am I to say I didn't turn out well?\n Irregardless, during my time, I remember Aeyrius beating me around. Faerue pulling my hair and /carrying/ me by it. Shame on you.\n\nWhile yes, I had a father, and he was living, He wasn't there.\n Be it by his own accord or by force of others.\n   He was kept away in isolation for years, missing my childhood. \n I forget why I'm writing this...\n\nAs every child does, through my issues that most children don't face...\n I dreamed of love and happiness.\n   Not.\n\nInstead, I dreamed of books... Not about love and happiness. About war and history, mainly. My sister Ruonna wrote a book, it was eleven pages. She was a child. I believe it was about those accursed cubes.\n\nI wrote nothing. While reading and aspiring to read more; the perfect book,\n I also dreamed of becoming a Druii.\n As of now, this is debatable... I'll explain later. \nWhile the beatings and whatnot were reccuring, This is the worst.\n\n One day, while innocently walking around the square of Malinor, the well, the taverns. \n A hooded man was in one of the taverns, shouting of ale while the smell of it stung on his breath,\n\nThere was another hooded man, watching me while I entered the establishment.\n He was outside of the tavern, leaning against a tree. His two toned, black and white hair was hid loosely by cloak. \n I approached the hooded man that was shouting,\n\nI informed him of his repulsive breath stank' and told him he's to loud, my big mouth. \n  He turned slowly, grinning sinisterly.\n He threatened me with harm,\nBeing used to physical pain, I didn't back down.\n\nHe snarled under his hood, issuing another threat.\nYet, I still didn't back down.\n He growled. The hooded man outside tilted his head, observing the two.\n The man set down his mug slowly, I began to back up...\n\nThe man than began to summon magic, or so I think. It happened so fast.\n Two figures shimmered as they were conjured, they resembled blue flames that danced.\nThe apparisions assumed the look of wolves.\n\nThey then lunged at me as I turned and run, once got ahold of my shoulder, the other my right leg. I don't remember the rest.\n When I awoke, my shoulder was healing well. Albiet with slight scarring. My right leg was gone.\n\nWhen one loses a limb, I compare it to losing a family member or close loved one. Everything you do reminds you of it. Everything you can't do reminds you of it. \n I was forced to crutches for years of my life.\n\nThen, theres Aislinn and the devil child. I'll speak of one of many of his attempts. \n In the Malinor square, it had just emptied, it's former occupants fleeing to their abodes for night's rest.\n\nA cloaked mali'aheral walked into the city through the gate, tailed by a small child, no more than 10. \n I was a thinking, slim child. No muscle.\n Aislinn walked up to me and simply scouped me up, screaming and kicking, then proceeded to walk out o\n\nThe child tailed him. \nWe pass through what was Leanniel before it was established, taking the mountain back trail.\n We proceeded towards Lenfarthing, this part occuring just on the far side of Witch woods, by the giant mushrooms.\n\nI forget the man's name, and sadly cannot add his name.\n Oh, and as it turned out, the hooded man outside of the tavern was my father. Just visiting.. For the only time.\n\nAislinn and the bitch child stopped outside of Witch woods, confronted by a former Highguard before Serva Rose's disgraceful actions. \n The man, knowing me, and my father, questioned Aislinn to no end.\n\nAs the wait was prolonged, others began to arrive at the scene, a blue haired woman I now recognize as Ariana,\n Then some doctor-man.\n Eventually, it came to the point of swords drawn. Aislinn gave it, setting me down and letting me return\n\nhome with the protection of the forgotton-named-hero. Then, returning to my tale long before. In Salvus. I was about to sell substance to a man named Edward, that is all I knew of him.\n An addicted stranger on the street.\n\nI sold him several pouches of green for a disclosed amount of mina.\n \n We than began to talk. He offered to make me a prosthetic leg, of wood. (For the idiots who didn't study all their childhood.)\n\nFor absolutely nothing in return. Nothing that was voiced, anyway.\n Is it common to see such kindness these days? Put yourself in my position... A young adult put in pain and beaten all her life, to see this.\n\nI fell in love with this man.\n\nI became Willow Eilthereach through time.\n\nLittle did I know,\nI married a man who was mentally unstable.\n\nIt just goes to show what legnths one needs to go through to see kindness.\n\nThen, My father and mother split. Not so much officially.\n It was mostly done by her cheating on him for the what? Ninth time? About time, I say.\n\nShe didn't stop there, either.\n\nAfter cheating on him, she proceeded to marry the man. His name, Quity. Or is it Ouity.. Q or O...\n At this point, I was living in Adunia with Edward. I was discriminated against by those of Clan Rovyk,\n\nfor being an elf and for them not knowing the damned definition of Heretic.\n That I could ignore, untill it started to turn into phsyical violence... Reliving my childhood.\n\nAt this time, I had two things I cared for left. Edward, and my father.\n\nEdward and I had a child, we named him Jotham.\n\nBut alas, through time, Edward and I grew apart... In every way, silently. The only part of my life without violence.\n Except the one time, but I feel as I shouldn't include that in here... It's a lifestory not a book of sexual fantasies.\n\nEdward and I growing apart brings me to the present day, where my father rests on his deathbed. Self induced. Starving himself. What does this leave me with? I can take no more. At least Jotham will grow up with a father.\n\nAs stated, I can take no more. As you read this, I plunge the dagger into my heart for all who have wronged me.\n\nThese are not arranged in any specifec order.\n\nIzzy, Ouity, Devil child, Aenor, Aislinn, Faerue, Hooded man, All of the Rovyks. All who have wronged nature.\nMali'aheral and their racism.\nAeyrius.\nBilly Bob.\n\nThis, is the story, of a little elf,\n Who could take no more.", ""),
        StaticBook("The End of Alex", "§bElindor", "The End of Alex\n\n\n            or\n\n\n The Making of Adeon\n\n\n\n\n\nBy Elindor\n\nWe could hear your groaning from outside. It was clear you hadn't heeded counsel and were experimenting in the shadows, for the library was unusually dark. Torches still hung in their place, but wery little light seemed to escape the flickering flame.\n\nYou were hunched over in the corner beside my self indulgent journals. Strange how those pages supposed a good nature within all darkness, yet here were you succumbed to its will.\n\nYour face was wrinkled with lines of great shadow and the whites of your eyes darkened to a hungry midnight. But behind their cold glare it was still the same friendly dwarf. You were ever unchanging, even in your darkest hour. Last hour.\n\nWe approached you slowly. That blood upon your hands and clothes. I spent days washing it out of the stone floor afterwards. Your sword lay beside you, misshapen from recent use. He stopped in the doorway readied for a fight. I continued on. Arms forward.\n\nYou screamed at me, obsenities and and hatred. I nodded. You grew weary of speech and grabbed at the blade. He flinched as though to step in, but the blade weighed ever more than you could have expected. The metal dragged down against your struggle.\n\nWe spoke. You listened, but you could not hear. Your mind had deteriorated. Your ambitions stolen away. Replaced with chaos.\n\nA dagger hidden beneath your cloak. The glint of steel amid the din. A strike of pain, but only a little. He has stepped forward and plunged that sword of his into your chest cavity. The knife dropped. A drop of my blood on its tip.\n\nYour resign. The fighting is pointless. Even the darkness concedes. A breath of peace.\n\nYou speak to us sincerely. We promise to heed your words. He wishes it not to be. I draw an arrow. Your last genuine thoughts are towards others. We will watch out for friends and do well by your family. The arrow levitates between my fingers.\n\nYour face drops. Exhaustion from bloodloss. He vocalises a pained cry. Still the arrow floats, Expectantly.\n\nA shiver runs through your body. A voice recognised, but not yours. Your body attempts to rise. But it cannot. The arrow no longer floats between my hands. It is sunken into your forhead. Your body shrinks back down again. Stillness.\n\nHe is quiet all that day. And days afterwards. I am silenced too. These familiar walls are not the same, the songs of birds are hollow, the suns warmth cannot penetrate skin. So he leaves with little else but that sword.\n\nI watch him depart. When we next meet he will no longer be that boy. He has changed.\n\nWhat could have been of you Adeon? All the good that is within you, drawing you to noble causes. But you are forever troubled from this moment and see all the world through the reflection in your well polished sword.", ""),
        StaticBook("Navitas II", "§b[Child] Silus Hightower", "As soon as his words were uttered, the world grew suddenly dark. A great roar erupted from Iblees’ mouth and in a blast of fire he was banished from the Mortal World. The Descendants stood still for several moments, pondering over the words of Iblees.\n\nMalin, Krug, Urguan and Horen all knew naught of what the great Devil had spoken of when concerning Malin’s betrayal. Dismissing it as the lies of a demon propagated to corrupt their souls,\n\n the brothers thought nothing further of Malin’s supposed treason.\n\nThe robed figure stood before the four brothers.\n\n“There is nothing in my power that may undo what that evil did. There is one thing I may do however, and that is to bless you.\n\nMalin, may your forests be a sanctuary of peace and your children long lived.\n\nUrguan, may your descendants be hardy, strong hearted and strong of mind.\n\nKrug, may your people show valour and honour where none exist.\n\nAnd Horen, may your people one day explore the Seven Skies.\n\nI can do no more, for all my power is spent. We will go back to our master now, I believe your children may see us once more but long in the future.”\n\nAnd with that, the great host of Aenguls and Daemons disappeared into thin wisps in the air.", ""),
        StaticBook("TF: Vol. XII", "VonEbs", "The Flagship\nVolume XII  (9/30/13)\n\n===================\nContents:\nA Rex Unites the Uruks\nThe Ac’telarah Patrimony\nA New Construction in Luminaire\nAdunia Abandons the Westerlands\nRegency in Salvus\n\nThe Goldman-Horen Edicts\nLand Grants offered in Ruska and the Trog\nHeralding a New Kingdom\n==================\nA Rex Unites the Uruks\n\nThe Uruks of the Trog have of late become more and more involved in daily life\n\nin Anthos. Reversing the trend the previous decade of isolation, orcs can now commonly be found in Luminaire Plaza, outside the church in Salvus, and along the roads to the Cloud Temple. Spearheading this effort to bring the uruks into contact with the\n\nother races is the newly titled Rex Grool’Azog’Gorkil. Grool, formerly Wargoth of the Gorkil Clan, has served in many positions in the Uzg and Krugmar, from High Yazgurten to Wargoth. Some of his previous accomplishments include building the Trog,\n\nsetting up a new currency. the bone token, and leading a Waagh against Malinor.  \n\nGrool recently claimed the position of Rex, and so far has remained unchallenged. This is not the first time the pale orc has aspired to this title,\n\nhowever, in all previous Rex Klomps he was ultimately defeated. Only time will tell what path Grool will choose for Krugmar and the uruks.  \n~Ebs\n===================\nThe Ac’telerah Patrimony\n\nThe Magestate, headed by Artimec, has elected to rejoin with Malinor in the face of threats from the Kingdom of Ruska. Artimec, the current guild master of the Arcane Delvers, will become the governor of the province of Ac’telerah, including both the\n\nArcane Delver fort and the village of Lenniel. This comes after the Magestate had separated from Malinor in an act of defiance against the High Council for alleged dealings with the Dark Brotherhood, a shadowy organization filled with assassins.\n\nAc’telerah had then been formally recognized and allied with William Horen, the former King of Renatus, formerly known as Oren. This was announced with the posting of the Sapphire-Emerald Amalgamation, which has been coldly received by the\n\nresidents of Malinor, who by and large want nothing to do with the Talarans. Whether both sides will maintain their sides of the agreement is unknown, but this treaty indicates growing stability in a region plagued by shifting alliances and collapsing\n\nempires.\n===================\nA New Construction in Luminaire\n\nIf you have been in Luminaire in the past few elven weeks, you can not help but notice the looming building that has been constructed\n\non the west side of the main square. Only the Lower and High Councils have been permitted access, and with good reason. If you were to climb the newly finished stairs, you would be assaulted by a the bright light of magma shining from below what appears\n\nto be an impossible obstacle course in the form of the resurrected Gauntlet. \n\nThe Gauntlet is not new to Malinor, as there was an extremely popular version located in Laurelin during the Golden Age of Aegis. The general premise\n\nis that both Mali and other competitors attempt to complete the Gauntlet for a minas prize. It is perilous to say the least, but the prizes can become quite large. In Aegis, any Mali that completed it was awarded 5000 minas and a plaque on a wall\n\nlocated behind the obstacle course. Until it is determined exactly how difficult the current Gauntlet is, the prizes will be predictably smaller, but the accumulating pot could grow large. The entry fee will be 50 minas, half of which will go towards a\n\njackpot to be won by the next person to complete it. After nine competitors complete the course, it will be redesigned.\n\nThe Gauntlet will be opening soon, so be prepared to test your agility and endurance like never before.\n==================\n\nAdunia Abandons the Westerlands\n\nThe Kingdom of Adunia, a vassal state of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan, has moved to the south, within the contemporary borders of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan. There were clashes reported along the border,\n\nas well as raids by the Flays against the various settlements in Adunia. The land that the Adunians left behind is slowly being transformed by the strelts of Kralta, who are restoring much of its natural beauty. A large wall has also been constructed,\n\nhowever there is no sign that Ruska will be attempting to cut off Malinor from the rest of the human lands as was attempted in the past by the White Roses and the Kingdom of Kaedrin. \n\nThis is just another chapter in the history of the Adunians,\n\nwho have been moving from place to place for decades, attempting to find a permanent home to settle down in. Their stay in the Westerlands was just one stop, with other stops in Cal Dais, Vaerhaven, and even the War Uzg for a time.\n\nDespite the constant shifting of their population, they have managed to resist dispersing like the Subudai did in Asulon. With its exit from the region, Adunia has also departed the Northern Coalition, which is now dominated by King Seigmund Carrion of\n\nRuska. A further report will be filed next week detailing the conditions in the new Kingdom of Adunia in the south.\n===================\nRegency in Salvus\n\nWith the unexpected death of King Aron Bedevere, Salvus has been left with an heir\n\nnot yet eligible to take the throne. Lord-Regent Nigel Therving has been serving as the Regent of Salvus, and is holding the reins while Aron’s son, King-Infante Relenkai, matures into adulthood. Salvus is currently facing possible threats from\n\nthe other human kingdoms, who wish to annex parts of Salvus’ fertile lands, and might use this moment of weakness to strike against it. The Lord-Regent has his work cut out for him ensuring that Relenkai will have a kingdom to inherit when he comes of\n\nage.\n===================\nThe Horen-Goldman Edicts\n\nGoldman, a familiar name to some, has been appearing at the top of several documents recently issued by the Treasury of Renatus. This relative, Tuv\n\nGoldman, of the famous, or perhaps infamous, Toveah Goldman,  has apparently been granted the position of treasurer of Oren previously held by now King Silus Horen. At one point, Toveah Goldman held the largest share of property owned\n\nby a commoner in Oren, and thus the world, owning completely the towns of Baile and Aldersburg, as well as large chunks of the Westerlands and Abresi. \n\nThe Horen-Goldman Edicts seem to be targeting business in Abresi and the rest\n\nof what is left of Renatus, and have so far resulted in the threatening of closure of several shops in Abresi. Taverns are having to register with the government, and stricted taxes are being put in place, Already there are rumors of a black market\n\ndeveloping, though these rumors could not be confirmed. These are bold steps for Renatus, the economy of which has been faltering in recent years much like that of the other nations of Anthos.\n===================\nLand Grants offered\n\nin Ruska and the Trog\n\nFor the enterprising poor in Anthos, new options have opening in both Orcish and Human lands. In the former, the Trog is offering small farming plots and houses to “Pinkies” willing to pay a small amount of their crops.\n\nA similar program has been set up in Ruska, with a 10% tithe in place. Aimed at attracting new residents in Anthos, the Trog system, which has been operating for longer than the Ruska program and benefits from close proximity to the Cloud Temple, is\n\nproving quite successful. It was started by the current Rex, Grool’Azog’Gorkil, and has been considered a success by observers. Similar programs are reportedly being considered by other nations, though it is argued that the current\n\npopulation of Anthos, which has been in decline for a number of years, can only support so many farmers. Food is already extremely cheap due to Aron Bedevere driving down the prices in Salvus at the beginning of Anthos to undercut his competitors,\n\nand there is more than enough to feed everyone. The life of a farmer in Anthos tends to be comfortable, but routes for elevation in society are few outside of military circles. It is not known how this new group of farmers will affect the economy of\n\nAnthos, but food prices are expected to remain low for the foreseeable future. \n~Ebs\n===================\nHeralding a New Kingdom\n\nIn an edict issued by the Kingdoms of Ruska and Renatus,\n\nthe Kingdom of Herendul has been formally recognized. Ruled by House Winter, it is the northernmost Human nation, and consists of the Duchy of Hanseti, along with a few other northern counties. Crops do not grow well in the North, so the new kingdom might\n\nhave to import food to some extent in order to feed its growing population. It is currently forming a military from the remnants of House Winter’s personal guard, but some question how effective it will be fighting the forces in the North\n\nif they ever return in strength. Certainly King Winter has much work to do, and now has the authority to do what needs to be done to secure the North against ever threatening Chaos.\n~Ebs\n===================\n\nEditor’s Note\n\nA monthly subscription of the Flagship can be purchased for the small sum of 50 minas, with a guarantee of 4 issues an ((rl)) month. If you would like to be a journalist, or write reports for the Flagship, please contact Editor\n\nEbs Telrunya via messenger pigeon, as there is always room for more journalists on the Flagship Team.\n\nMany thanks, \n~Ebs Telrunya, Editor of the Flagship", "")
    )

    private fun _ATLAS_10(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Lumen Liber", "§bAiwendil", "~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~        Lumen Liber\n         A Book \n            Of\n    oOo Aeriel oOo\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~Blessed are those who keep the words of this ancient prophecy. But beware to those who defile it, for the destruction written in this book shall be\n\nbrought upon the cursed tenfold.\n\n~+~+~ /oOo\\ ~+~+~\n\nThe world has become desolate and unkind. A starless midnight has fallen over the world. You are losing faith, and have allowed Iblees to become the god of this world.\n\nThereby, I, Aeriel, and my Father, the Creator, shall bring destruction when the time comes. We shall destroy the world creating a new era, a new age, and a new world. Heed this warning, for I am coming soon. \n\nIblees shall take power over a large\n\nmass of people. People who are smart, yet weak. They know who they are. In that group the seventh son of a seventh son shall be brought as a gift for Iblees, and he shall have power over him so he may do his will. He shall claim power over the world, and\n\nwill declare war against Iblees. Only those who's eyes have been opened by me will see that this brood of vipers is a liar! Sadly, one of the holy children shall join him, for he shall be a peace-maker. For half an elven generation, this wolf shall lead\n\nthe world, telling lies of the darkness. At the end of this period, I will choose a group who shall fight against the dark one, the one who is nameless. This group shall be led by a King and a Queen. They shall be called the Lord of the Wood and the Lady\n\nof the Light. These two may be of any descendant race, but must be betrothed! Together they shall lead against the darkness and they shail prevail. But then, in a desolate time, one shall die at the hands of Iblees himself, and therefore half of every\n\nliving thing shall turn to dust. That is when I, Aeriel, shall fall down from the seven skies like a dew drop from the tallest of trees. All shall see my beauty and despair. I shall not be a Dark Lord, but their Queen! Along with my brethren, the Aenguls,\n\nand our cousins, the Daemons, we shall destroy all that is tainted and shall make the world anew. However, we shall wage war on Iblees, but we are no match for him. This shall be when the All-Father, the Creator, descends upon the world.\n\nA great shadow shall fall across the sky and all the stars will fall upon the world to form his sword. And his sword shall be of pure light! Brighter than the brighest lights, and all that fear the Father shall be blinded until destroyed. Taking his sword\n\nhe shall slice Iblees into a thousand pieces and scatter him across the universe. When the time comes he shall come back and rise up once again, but he shall be but a mere mortal. And with this I shall take the holy spear and throw it through his heart,\n\ndestroying the one who has forsaken the world. When the evil one dies, a great snow shall fall unto the world and all will be silent. Even the beating of the heart won't be heard. Everyone living thing will freeze and die, and all things shall end.\n\nThe All-Father shall release his pet, the serpent and it shall swallow the world whole. And a world shall be born anew with prosperity. And the ones who have love and light in there hearts shall once more be resurrected up from the dust in which they were\n\ndestroyed, and all shall have everlasting life. \n\n Long Live the Light!", ""),
        StaticBook("Moaning Of Life", "§bJudas Agnarsson", "Judas Agnarssons\nLast Memories/thoughts\n(Diary)\n\nThis book will contain Judas Agnarssons last thoughts/memories prior to his death.\n\nJudas Agnarsson\n\n1498-15____\n\nEntry #1\n\nPerhaps with this book you'll remember me by.\n\nI haven't really thought about life after death throughout my whole fifty five years of living; but i'd like to think i'd be reconnected with my child and father.\n\nEntry #2\n\nI have grown an accustom for an author I have discovered in the Libary Dragur.\nArthur Caulfield: He appears to have wrote many books, all in good condition; considering he wrote these extracts in Athera.\n\nOr what I presume was Athera, as the pages have turned a musty yellow.\nI highly doubt he is living now, but I can only hope he is out there somewhere.\n\nEntry #3\n\nMany people ask about my face.\n\"But why does it look burnt?\"\n\n\"Have you been cooking lately?\"\n\n\"Urk, disgusting!\"\n\n\"Eww!\"\n\nAll of which are reasons why I cannot simply be bothered to explain to each person why my face is disfigured.\n\nHowever I'll make an exception this once.\n\nMy right eye is engraved with a deep scar; it was a lacerated slash from a previous war.\n\nDuring the war I was fighting for Lord Percival Staunton, whom sadly passed away a while ago.\n\nMy actual face however was from a hunting trip.\nI have a camp set up North East of the docks in the Cloud Temple.\nI was tired of hunting boar so I\n\nhiked a mountain in order to find a Mountain Goat.\nHowever as I stalked my prey, traversing the cliffs.\nI noticed a figure shoot past me, I didn't acknowledge it that much as my eyes were set upon the goat.\n\nAs I lined my arrow about to release, I heard a distinctive growl from behind; soon followed by a crunch of the gravel that my feet rested on.\nI felt a serrated claw pierce into my clothes, and penetrate my skin.\nMy spine froze, yet I collapsed\n\nforward, unable to speak, I was lost of words.\nAn agonizing pain shot up my spine as I felt it claw into my back.\nI knew if I didn't stop it, I could have been killed...\nI used the last of my vigrousness to turn onto my back.\nAs I did so, I\n\nof a beast. It's breath emitted a foul, onion stench I once inhaled from Shrecks Swamp.\nI slid my hand towards my gilded scabbard, and unsheathed my hunting knife and thrusted upwards towards it's neck. My face dripped with blood as it's teeth sunk int\n\ncheeks and tore my muscle tissue, and flesh with it as it fell from my body twitching.\n\nI clambered to my feet with the adrenaline I had and repeatedly perforated it's fur, and flesh until I could no longer do so.\n\nI allowed myself to fall back onto the cliff, I lay there looking like a ruptured mess.\nI awoke to my face being wet, and ticklish. As I squinted my eyes open I was blinded almost immediatley by the sunlight.\nI awaited until my eyes could adjust; u\n\ncould see what was licking me.\nI shifted my gaze towards a bearded goat, licking the blood from my face and cleansing me.\nI whispered a \"Thankyou\"\nbefore closing my eyes.\nIt seemed like an eternity  but was a matter of hours before\n\na little boy; sharing an odd resemblance to my son.\nI was laying there in complete silence; and in a trice moment the furtive scampering footsteps emerged from the side of me.\nHis eyes were a navy blue, similar to mine. His hair had a parting in th\n\nmiddle like my sons.\nHis lips pouted for a breif second, and opened his mouth as if he was about to speak but remained quiet.\n\nHe scuttled towards me, a timid grin laid upon his face.\nHe kneeled next to me and gently stroked my cheek with his\n\nI groaned in response as he continued to stroke my hair. \nHe whispered something in my ear, but I was too weak to hear it.\nHe clambered to his feet and walked off, disappearing in the mist.\n\nMy vigourness and eagerness to get home to safety is what saved me from dying out there.\n\nEntry #4\n\nAs a young boy, my father and I travelled the vast, open landscapes in search for labour work.\n\nUp until we met a man named Alifer Amice. He owned a ranch on a farm, which me and my father worked on harvesting crops and such\n\nfor money.\n\nAfter many years, a job opportunity came up for my father Heinrich Windsor.\nTo be a personal squire to Grand King Skippy, and in return we claim a piece of land.\n\nWe named the piece of land House Windsor.\nUnfortunatley Skippy died shortly after he was pronounced King.\nMeaning Windsors were no longer allowed in the Dwarven Kingdom.\nWe were banished from our land, and our items were reposessed.\n\nAlifer soon departed from us, never to even be heard/seen again.\n\nMy father joined the St Amyas, but was killed for breaking the Code Of Chivarly. \nHis tounge was cut off, and left to bleed to death.\n\nEntry #5\n\nFamily\n\nFather: Heinrich Windsor\n(Human, Highlander)\n\nMother: Arsa Windsor\n(Wood Elf)\n\nSon: Judas Windsor (Me)\n(Human, Highlander)\n\nUncle: Edward Windsor (Human, Highlander)\n\nCousin, Edwards Son: Richard Windsor (Human, Highlander)\n\nCousin, Edwards Son: Joseph Windsor\n\nCousin, Edwards Daughter: Chloe Windsor\n\nBrother: Heinrich Windsor Junior\n\nBrother: Kalf Windsor\n\nMy brother Kalf and I changed our second name to Agnarsson due to Richard Windsor dishonouring our name.\n\nEntry #6\n\nJobs/Education\n\nMy lifetime of work has gifted me well throughout the years. I have learnt new things and I appreciate all of them.\n\n((Started this persona at age 10))\n\n10-14 Years of Age: Laboured Worker: Farming, Lumberjack, Fisherman.\n\n15-18: Saint Amyas Guard of Peremont.\n\n22-24: Manager of a bathing house in the Duchy Of Courland; working under Lord Percival Staunton.\n\n25-26: Staunton Guard\n\n27-29: Felsen Guardsman in the Military.\n\n30-32: Squire for a Knight.\n\n34-36: Bartender in Felsen.\n\n37: Worked for AMC: Aumont Mercantile Company.\n\n39-40: Owner of AMC\n\n40-47: Courland invested in AMC, and ownership given to me. Renamed to TCC (The Courlandic Company)\n\n48: Sold the Company to Mithril Goods for 1500 minas.\n\n50: Retired from work.\n\n55: Author of diaries/journals.\n\nEntry #7\n\nA rumour has been spreading around the Duchy of Courland lately about a Dragon coming to attack?\n\nI highly doubt this; however I remember when I was twenty five and living in Courland,\n\nI saw a Dragon fly over.\nIt attacked the south guard tower, luckily we fought it off.\n\nGod, forgive me for I have sinned. \nI have to repent for my malicious actions I have just committed. \n\nOur Duke was in danger of being killed by a man named Knwell Quill, whom seeked to avenge his brother who was beheaded.\n\nI found Quill, outside the city and drove my sword into his abdomen. \nHe collapsed onto the ground, a smug look on his face; before dying.\n\nI do not know how to repent for my sins, please guide me; for I am lost in guilt.\n\nI threw my Blade into the river, and watched it float down the stream; releasing the fresh blood, and allowing the blood to spread throughout the river.\n\nEntry #8\n\nSometimes I wonder how a Kharajyr was created...\n\nSomewhere along the way, a human fucked a cat!\n\nEntry #9\n\nI was on my way to Felsen today, when I noticed a commotion going on the other side of the gate.\n\nIt was quite unusual for the gates to be closed; however I assumed a robbery had previously happened.\n\nAs I peered into the other side of the gate I noticed a pack of Orcs had raided Felsen.\n\nMithril Goods Trading Co.\nwindows had been shattered.\n\nMy gaze was immediatley drawn to a red ork, who held a pitch fork.\n\nthe lustre of his fierce red eyes shot straight through me.\n\nHe had an old fellow by the scruff of his neck, and forced him onto his knees.\n\nThe old man whimpered and sobbed, until the Red Ork drove his pitch fork into his spine, killing him al\n\ninstantly.\n\nI pivoted on my heel, promptly turning to flee the scene; as I didn't want to risk my life.\n\nI heard cheers from the other Orks as the Red Ork held the old mans head up in the air in pride of his glory, and winnings.\n\nEntry #10\n\nThis might just be my last entry, due to the book having limited pages.\n\nPerhaps I will write another book; fiction next time?\n\nI must admit this journal has taken up most of time because\n\nI have forced myself to go out and do something interesting so I can write about.\n\nDo not worry if I do not write for a long period of time.\n\nI am not dead....not just yet.\n\nI don't know whether or not this will be a hobby of mine.\n\nPerhaps this book will bring me fame.\n\nIf you have any more questions about my life, I suggest you find me in Courland.\n\nAt Cranfield PLC door number 3.\n\nI will give you advice on just about anything...so as long as it's a logical question.\n\nI will hand this book into the Libary of Dragur if I can find it....\n\nI'm soon to be opening The Courlandic Company again, so perhaps that will make up most of the time I have left.\n\nFarewell all.\n\nSigned- Judas Agnarsson", ""),
        StaticBook("The Stone Giant", "§bUnknown", "The\n          Stone\n          Giant\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy Lyeth\n\nThere once was a Mali'ame whose name is Unknown, and not knowing we'll call this one None. None was adventurous and bold to a fault, and thought of themselves all the world.\n\nNone wandered the lands, called not a one home, and never did let the soles of their feet touch a thing but the flesh of the earth.\n\nOne day whilst wandering in lands not unknown, for None knew very well they were lands that None should be in,\n\nthey came upon a hill.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wilven Monks", "§bInitiate Monk Yohei", "Keldrith, Lord of the Sun, began his story like any of the rest of us mortals. He was the son of a king, king Celetiman of Celestiran, a kingdom in what is now known as Asulon, the current city of Arethor, and thereby prince and heir to the throne.\n\nAt the time the story begins, Keldrith was but a thirteen year old boy. Thousands of villagers dwelt in the kingdom, and all of them loved Keldrith, for he was simply a kind and charismatic person.\n\n As time went on, despite his young age, Keldrith fell in love with a princess. Keldrith’s love was the princess Rellenia of a small city-state outside of the kingdom’s borders. He noticed her one day when she was not at a political debate,\n\nlike his father was most hours, but out at the markets, purchasing some wheat from a poor farmer and paying him twice its worth. He was enthralled by a maiden that could be so beautiful, yet so kind He would go on and on about her, and strangely,\n\nKing Celetiman noticed this, despite his ignorance of informal matters. He went to the king of the city-state, Taron, and offered an arranged marriage between the two.\n\nTaron approved his proposition, and a marriage was planned between Rellenia and Keldrith.  Now one might think that Rellenia would be unhappy about an arranged marriage but quite the contrary, she had loved Keldrith from the moment she met him.\n\nThey were happily wed, and when Celetiman passed on, Keldrith took over as king. When time saw fit, they went out into the world, leaving the general of the military in charge of the kingdom. Time went on, and Keldrith, twenty-six,\n\nand Rellenia, twenty-four, arrived at a small hamlet known as Flowershire. In Flowershire lived a young man known as Tariel, a kind farmer who the two liked instantly. Keldrith, Relenia, and Tariel became the greatest of friends,\n\nand when they left the hamlet, Tariel came with them. They explored all of Asulon, cherishing each others’ friendship, and having many adventures. Sadly, their joy could not last. It was said that they came to a wasteland in Asulon,\n\nnothing was there except for scorched rocky mountains. Not much is known about what occurred within the valley, except a farmer a few leagues away said he saw a bright flash of light from that direction soon after they entered.\n\nIn truth, they were murdered in this place. Their bodies faded into the earth, as death does, and their belongings vanished as well, all except for one each. \n\nIt was said that, upon their deaths, the Creator took pity upon their souls\n\nand bound them to three minerals, Rellenia, a diamond, Keldrith, a bar of gold, and Tariel, a gem of Lapis Lazuli. He then waited, for he knew what would happen to the three friends. The stones stayed upon the ground for centuries,\n\nand all around them, the wasteland transformed into a paradise, water flowing from the mountain peaks reformed the land into a valley of grass, forming a pool in the center, the stones laying on the shore. Such a paradise could not go unihabited,\n\nso the Creator chose a single woman and a single man to discover it. \n\nThe man, William Alerus, and the woman, Vera Alerus, set up a home their, not knowing the stones the lied upon the shore, until one day, their child went down and explored.\n\nAmanda Alerus, their child, discovered the stones, and called her parents. They admired them, but something prevented both William and Vera from touching the stones, so Amanda went up and gathered them in her arms.\n\nThe second she touched them, bright lights shot out, the colors of the stones, and they flew into the sky, the gold to the sun, the lapis to the stars, and the diamond to the moon.\nThe Creator admired the friendship of the original three,\n\nand left knowledge upon the new three mortals living upon the shore. He told them the story of the stones, and instructed them to build a Temple in their honor. They trained a messenger bird, sending him home to their friends and extended family,\n\n speaking of the paradise and the small price to pay. They brought with them all the materials they could carry and departed for the soon-to-be Temple of the Triumvirate. Work progressed quickly, an immense library going up and the Temple\n\nitself a sight to behold. These were the original Monks of the Triumvirate.\n \nThe Celestial Triumvirate, as Keldrith, Rellenia, and Tariel came to be called, became deities in their own right, demigods of the sun,\n\nmoon, and stars. They granted their followers the ability to heal those who needed it by invoking their name in prayer, but the most powerful monks were able to do it through sheer mental focus upon them. They blessed the Temple when it was complete,\n\n that it would be forever void of any illnesses or disease of the outside world, and that it would ever be a safe haven.\n \nAs time went on, the monks forgot the old ways,\n\nbecoming lazy and not helping those other than themselves. The Triumvirate saw this and were angry, so angry in fact that they banished the monks from the Temple, magical wards preventing any from entering the paradise as long as they lived, and longer.\n\nIn fact, they did not allow anyone through until the adventurer Wilven Adonan.\n \nWilven Adonan, a young human adventurer, was among the first to originally came to the land through the portal.\n\n   Upon seeing the people become afflicted with the devastating curse, Wilven set out to find some way to cure or dispel it. He traveled long through swamps, mountains, and forests and eventually came to a grand mountain range.\n\nAt the base of the mountains, he found a partially collapsed tunnel that seemed to cut through the mountain, so he made his way through it. On the other side, he discovered a marvelous sight.\n\n \nThis place that he had found was not like the world outside it. It seemed the curse did not affect this place. Lush trees and vibrant grass covered the place and clear waterfalls streamed down the sides of the mountains.\n\nThe structures, although collapsed in some places, were beautiful as well. Another strange thing Wilven noticed about this place is that he felt healthier while inside the valley.\n\n Exploring some more, Wilven came upon a large structure with several arches. He made his way inside and eventually came upon a hidden tunnel back behind a collapsed wall.\n\nHe made his way through hallways and down staircases and found himself inside a large library. Amazingly, the library was intact and untouched by nature. After looking over several tomes and manuscripts,\n\nWilven was able to discover that this place was built long ago in order to serve as a place of worship for three beings of power, Keldrith, Rellenia, and Tariel. Together, these three beings formed the Celestial Triumvirate which  -\n\nwatched over the sky and all below. Wilven wished to discover more, but he first had to bring others to this sacred place where the curse did not reside.\n \nBy the time he returned to the humans, many of them had fallen to the effects of the curse.\n\nHe collected those whom were still well enough to travel and brought them back to the sacred valley. Once they recovered enough, Wilven sent three messengers to send word to the Orcs, Elves, and Dwarfs that there was a\n\nplace free from the taint of the curse. When the messengers returned, however, they brought with them only a handfull of people. Unfortunately, many of the other races’ people had fallen to either the curse or other\n\nunfortunate circumstances. Feeling reinvigorated by the day, the few remaining people set to work making for themselves a new home in this sacred place. \n \nFor many years,  the survivors worked hard to restore the sacred valley to its original form\n\nWhen Wilven was very old, he called the people together and told them all that he had learned of the Celestial Triumvirate. The people consecrated themselves to the Celestial Triumvirate and constructed a shrine to allow worship to all three beings.\n\nThey formed themselves into monastic order and cloistered themselves from the rest of the world. They chose Wilven as their Abbott and, together, the monks continued to live on in peace taking care of the sacred valley, giving praise to the Triumvirate,\n\nand praying for the curse to be cleansed from all the land. Upon Abbott Wilven’s death, the monks wished to pay honor to his life by naming the sacred valley after him. From that day forward, the place was known as Wilven Sanctuary.\n\n[Written and compiled by Escharian, sources: ikeyman232, shiftnative, and countjuno88] \n\nRe-written by ThePlanetAstro", ""),
        StaticBook("The Pilgrimage", "§bMonk Sudo", "The Pilgrimage\n--------------------By Monk Sudo\n\n\nIt is said that circumstances make a man, and I can assure you that the same is true for a Monk. We Monks rarely come young into the Temple, perhaps because life\n\ntakes us all on windy roads. I have known death, war, and then peace. I believe that all of us come here in search of peace. This is my own windy road.\n-Monk Sudo\n14th of The First Seed 1473\n\nHumble Beginnings\n-------------------In Anthos I was born into the arms of a slave woman, as they trecked across the Orcish desert. My mother died shortly after naming me Thry Greymane. I remained a slave of the Azogs until I was a young man, serving\n\nhappily only as a person who has known nothing else can. In the desolate Orcish wasteland, I was born in blood.\nAs I grew, physically and emotionally, I learned the history of my lineage, of my once noble blood from my father, who I once believed had b\n\nnoble in spirit as well. \nLooking back upon my teenage years, I see now what my father truly was- he was a monster as dispicable as those Orcs who owned me.\nMy father and I escaped when I was 15 years old, and we lived for a time in Urguan. One mig\n\nassumed that I was raised to be pious, to be loyal, but I was not. My father subjegated me to constant abuse, whether it be physical or verbal, and it was constant. I was constantly unhappy because of it.\nIn my mind, I was still in the desert.\n\nBaptism\n-------------------I was baptized in fire.\n\nI left the Dwarven lands with a few fellow outcasts, and we made ourselves to be makeshift mercenaries. We were roughly trained, and we had only a rough idea of what even battles\n\nwere. \n\nBut we grew up fast, with every employer who hired us, we learned another lesson, earned another scar. If I had hated the world before, I wanted to burn it afterwards.\n\nI saw the Monk on the\n\nthird day of preparation for the coming battle; we were camped on a river, with the other army across from us. He rowed out into the center of it, in his little rowboat, and he spoke. His words were for the common person, so that we could understand. He\n\nasked us why we were about to do what we all knew was going to happen. He asked what the point of it all was. He asked many questions which I couldn't answer.\n\nI left the camp in the beginning of the night, and never returned to being a mercenary.\n\nNobles of a Different Kind\n-------------------I quickly found relatives of my family in the Greymane swamp, and they quietly took me in. They educated me, and my cousin Lord Charles took me under his wing. I was 25 years old, and I did not adjust to th\n\nlife of a noble well. To hide from my previous line of work, Charles gave me a new name to live under; James Greymane. Despite my horrid social skills, I taught the children of Charles the large amount of knowledge which I had aquired in my time, in\n\naddition to swordplay. I trained young children to become ruthless killers.\n\nI realized what I was in a training accident, after ten years of servitude. I had set the two brothers upon each other, but unbeknownst to me they used swords\n\nbeyond their skill level, far sharper than they should have been.\n\nThe younger boy took the head of the older clean off his shoulders.\n\nI had too much cowardice to face Charles that night, and I\n\nran into the wilderness, as far as my legs would take me until I passed out on top of a rock outcropping.\nIt was with a view of the sea when I was reminded of the Monk.\n\nI began my pilgramage to the Cloud Temple.\n\nMonkhood\n-------------------I met the lone remaining Monk in the summer, where he quickly took me in. I stayed there for long enough that he realized I was there to stay, and he employed me with tending the lands of it.\n\nI plowed fields, I sowed what I reaped, and I reaped what I had sown. I confessed myself to the Monk, but he gave me only forgiveness.\nIn such a dire situation, I found hope.\nI cried for the first time in many years that night, but in the morning,\n\npresented with my initiate robes. He called me a new name, and I became Monk Sudo.\n\nMy pilgrimage was a long one, but I reached my holy place.\nBy Monk Sudo", ""),
        StaticBook("MonkResurrection", "§bJistuma", ">|<Monk>|<\n-=~Resurrection~=-\n\nIt is the salvation of many lives, but I wonder why I have seen nothing written on it. The monks, as is very well known, are able to save those that have passed away. While managing my stall at the sanctuary grounds I have been able to see for myself some\n\nof these happenings, or so I believe. \n\nThis magic, unlike many others, is one I know very little about. Like all holy magics it seems to be manifested as a bright light, mostly used to heal those wounded. Besides the bright light, the monk performin\n\nis praying to the Triumvirate. It appears to be like clerical healing, but it has other properties. Sometimes a monk arrives at the sanctuary a bit hurt after travels. It appears bandits and the like do not care that they are mugging what could be their\n\nsavior. What I have to say about those monks, is that unlike normal folk, their wounds heal faster. This is of course due to their magic, small flecks of light I have seen surrounding and healing the wounds. Then the monks are able to bring back the once\n\ndeceased fully mortal once more.\n\nThis is not to say they are necromancers. Those simply raise the dead, and they remain in a limbo state living and being deceased. The monks are able to bring the body and soul exactly like it was before the death, i\n\nnear perfect condition. From those I have talked to over the years in the Sanctuary, there is an always present effect of being saved. Present in all of those that I have seen, none have memories of their death or even of the events leading up to it.\n\nOther common effects are scars, sometimes showing how the poor soul met its end before, or of the tortures it passed. The ones that worry me the most is that sometimes the ones saved change… I have talked to some before and after saving, and changes can\n\nbe quite extreme. Some go crazy, others start to live in constant fear, some remain with pains in parts of their bodies. The changes they can go through are incredibly varied. I could conjure up reasons as to why that happens, all of them without means of\n\nproving so. I just believe death to be a terrible experience, that part of it continues on even after salvation.\n\nAnother interesting fact I have gathered, somehow by luck, is that the saved do not want to return to the location that they had\n\nperished. This particular thought came to me when one of the saved was hugged dearly by what I assumed was his lover. Before that, his body had been carried by another, a friend perhaps, and he and I had a chat about what happened. I knew of the exact\n\nlocation of his demise, and as him and the woman were moving away, he asked if they were passing through that exact area when returning home. With the confirmation of the woman, he started giving out other ways to reach their house. A big argument even\n\nhappened when the woman just wanted to go home as fast as she could with him, and he plainly refused to go through that area, which was the only road to their house. He didn’t know himself why he didn’t want to. Alas he returned to normal about half a day\n\nlater. Since then I started noticing other strange behaviors such as people staying in the sanctuary for longer times, not using their normal routes out of the sanctuary and returning shortly after leaving with a friend. I simply believe once more, that\n\nthe experience was so horrible, that those saved gain a subconscious fear of their death place. Besides, what would happen if they saw their own body? \n\nOn the mention of bodies, I do have to state as well, it is not necessary for the\n\nbody to be brought back to the monks for the resurrection. I have seen many monks bring bodies to the sanctuary, so I believe it might be quite easier with them. This is favorable, as in the lands of Anthos there are many evils. You can be decapitated,\n\neaten, thrown into lava, cut into little bits and drowned in the deepest of oceans. Your body may disappear and never been found once more, and you may this way still be saved. How they restore the body I do not know, and the monks seem not to answer when\n\nI ask them. They do answer a few questions. I learned, for instance, that the monks are neutral, and never take side in political views or wars. They also take this neutrality to those they save. I have seen those of evil whose purpose is to kill being\n\nsaved together with the children that never made any harm. This has brought problems to the monks before, many want others to remain dead.\n\nMost of the stories of the saved start simply with them explaining how they woke up in the monk’s care.\n\nSeems to always be the same as I stated. Some come back quite soon after their demise, already back before their friends and family run to the sanctuary to check, and others can take elven days. Yet this magic is not all powerful. As the monks mention,\n\nthey cannot save all. If the deceased does not walk out of the monks rooms an elven week after their death, they are forever lost. The same happens to those that take their own life. I believe that if they think that they don’t want to live anymore, then\n\nthey wouldn’t return to the land of the living.\n\nThe monks are a blessing to mortals, they are those that save so many from their shortened lives.\n\n\n\nWritten by Rosso, 15th of Malin's Welcome 1452", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall of Aegis", "§bMonk Scribe", "Fall of Aegis\n\nThe miasma in the north lingered ever more so. Galahar was evacuated and the cloud temple became our final stand. From the temple I shouted out into the crowds, summoning those who where chosen by the Nations as their champions.\n\nUpon arriving to Laurelin, I called all of the champions into Dawns Bakery, where a secret entrance lay.\n\nThe High Priestess handed out blessed armor pierced, enchanted in Aeriel's grace. To each of the champions. We then took a small passage,\n\ninto what was once the Laurelin Gauntlet. Entombed in a massive oak tree, lay Vardak's portal from the nether. \n\nThe champions gaze into the portal and grip the hilts of their weapons tightly. \n\nI step out of the way\n\nof the portal, clench my soulstone in my hand tightly and wish them good luck. As I vanish the brave few enter head first. \n\n- Spoken by Native in the Elf in the Deep Cold, 1351.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Love", "§bMonk Scribe", "By chance it seemed\nAnd nothing more,\nThat we would meet\nDown by the shore.\n\nWe sit on the hillside,\nAs I push back you hair.\nYou smile at me,\nAll I do is stare.\n\nI came to you,\nFlowers in hand,\n\nBut you said no,\nI would not understand.\n\nI cried that night,\nWhen you left me alone.\nI sit still,\nAs still as stone.\n\nNever again,\nHave I seen your eyes,\n\nbut they will stay with me,\nuntil our final goodbyes.\n\n- Written by Myro in Asulon.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Simple Story", "§bUnknown Author", "*The old tome is worn and dusty, and the ink is partially faded.*\n\n=================== A Story\n===================\n\n\" Two chaste Temple Monks were walking down the road during a heavy downpour of rain. They came across a beautiful young woman who was taking shelter under a tree. She called out to the monks, requesting that they carry her across a small stream.\n\nThe first monk immediately moved to help the woman while the second silently protested. The first monk scooped the beautiful lady up in his arms, and he carried her across the stream. After crossing it, he promptly set her down and continued on his way.\n\nThe two began walking down the path once more, and the second monk remained silent for several minutes as the woman disappeared from view. Finally, he spoke to his brother.\n\n'As monks of the Cloud Temple, we are not supposed to have contact with woman!\n\nWhy did you pick that women up so casually and carry her across the stream?' \n\nThe first monk replied, \n\n'Brother, I set the woman down long ago. Why is it that you have not?' \"", ""),
        StaticBook("Monk Bread", "§bSpike Vondar", "-={ Monk Bread }=-\n\nMonk bread has been a customary food item made by the Monks since the very beginning of their existence. As many of the Descendents know, this bread is unlike any other. It never rots, and it always feels fresh, having a crisp,\n\ngolden texture. Its taste of hints of butter and salt, though never making you thirsty. The feeling of warmth and brief revitalization flows throughout the consumer.\n\nAlthough the bread has been around for some time its origins have been unknown. People could \"magically\" receive the bread, though have no clue as to how it got to them, only the faint thought that it was from the Monks and safe to eat...\n\n- Baking the Bread -\n\nMonk Bread is crafted by the monks themselves, like any other regular bread. It is during the kneading process in which Monk Bread is created.\n\nAs a monk kneads the dough, hints of magic\n\nare leaked and blessed into the dough. Though because Soul Magic, the magic used by Monks, only heals people with a soul, the magic lingers.\n\nThe lingering magic stays in the bread, giving it its unique look and taste, as if it was\n\njust baked. Once eaten, the Monk Magic disperses throughout the consumers body, usually only giving them a feeling of fulfillment, as the magic is not strong enough to do much more.\n\n- Getting the Bread -\n\nAlthough Monk Bread can be given to anyone by a Monk, it also somehow reaches other people across the realm. Mysteriously appearing when one is hungry, as if by command. \n\nEven as an Elder Monk, I cannot describe\n\nhow it reaches people, nonetheless, it is a blessing of the Triumvirate.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Chill", "§bAlder Tundrak", "It began with a chill.\nThe true reason why the Triumvirate have cut connection from the Monks of the Order of Wilven is not yet known, speculation seems to point to the Triumvirate becoming angered with mortals for the disrespect and misstreatment given\n\nto those who adhere to their teachings, the Monks. I ask the question, why would the Triumvirate who in that idea wish to spite the mortals remove power from that which has been mistreated. Surely the Triumvirate are not foolish, I know not why our boons\n\nhave been halted, why our wards lifted, and why our homes have been taken, what I know is that I, Elder Monk Alder Tundrak, after many years in service to Tariel, Lord of the Stars have been left homless, with no explanation. I do not seek fabricated\n\ntales as to why such has occured, I simply seek awnsers as to what I must do now. \n\nElder Monk Alder Tundrak Cloud Temple Docks of Vailor", ""),
        StaticBook("The Falling...", "§bMonk Scribe", "The Falling of our World\n\nIn Aegis, all across the lands,\nThe Undead are making a stand.\nTheir power shown, the taint comes forth,\nit started spreading from the north.\n\nIn Al'Khazar they\n\nshowed it first,\nUndead power at its worst.\nThe city wrecked, many struck dead,\nThe King kidnapped, the people fled.\n\nThe northern cities also gone,\nCelestine and New Alstion,\nCrimson Vale, last\n\nWinterfell,\nThey stand now as empty shells.\n\nThe gaze of the Undead then turned,\nTo Alras, as we quickly learned.\nAgain a long and bloody fight,\nThe Undead try to prove their might.\n\nAlras fell to gas and flame,\nDefenders should not feel ashamed.\nTheir fight back was long and brave,\nBut Alras just could not be saved.\n\nThe Gauntlet struck, the lava flowed,\nA portal from the taint arose,\n\nLaurelin, attacked by Ghasts,\nDefenders stop their fires fast.\n\nThe taint transforms New Terriko,\nThe Undead strikes a mighty blow.\nBut defenders inflict pain,\nThe Undead there is quickly slain.\n\nIn Galahar, they strike as well,\nBut the monsters are quickly felled.\nThere is no overwhelming taint,\nNo gas that makes the people faint.\n\nResistance to the Undead grows,\nIn each attack it clearly shows.\n\nAegeans all protect their land,\nAre they gaining the upper hand?\n\nThough Human cities fall to Blight,\nThey have not given up the fight.\nThe Elves too are still full of strength,\nFighting the Undead to great lengths.\n\nThe Dwarves stand strong from underground,\nTheir defences are most sound.\nThe Orcs shout 'skah you' to Undead,\nPutting on pikes their rotten heads.\n\nDifferent, but still much the same,\nAll races share each\n\nother pain.\nIf Aegis can all fight as one,\nThe Undead surely will be done.\n\nBut if... if we fail to unite...\nWe will surely lost this fight.\n\n- Written by Josef Timothee in Aegis.", ""),
        StaticBook("Forgot, the...", "§bMonk Scribe", "Forgot, the North\n\nThe road sheered through the alpine north,\nthe snowy drift sobered by the sky's gray smoldering.\nThe path grit its cobbled stone through a lonesome coat\nof dust, collected through lack of\n\ntravel.\n\nA crow coughed at my passing\nthe first home to an old town.\nI did not forget,\nsaid the shattered oak door, clapping, creaking,\nhinged in walls of cinder.\n\nThe town wheezed with an ashen breeze,\nblackened posts echoing\nfrom bygone structures\nlike ribs clasping shriveled lungs, and I\nscraped up the sticks that were\nthe manse atop the hill, wanting\nfor its warmth.\n\nAt the town's far side is the lake's empty mirror.\n\nBeyond the bridge, a great tower looms,\nit's battlements broken arund the gate's fevered maw,\na burgled sentinel fallen on winter,\nwhere I stop, before the North's\n\nmuted expanse.\n\n- Written in Aegis after the Fall of the North to the Undead.", ""),
        StaticBook("Chills", "§bThe Chronicler", "===================\n\n\n\n\n          Chills\n\n\n\n\n\n\n===================\n\nFalling Candles\n\nI was thinking about Mum’s strawberry tarts when they descended on me.\n\nIt had looked like it was going to be another quiet night at the Cloud Temple. Not many people were gravely injured\n\nwhile they slept, it seemed, and for that, I was thankful. I was still a Novice at that time, not yet trained in the mysterious arts of healing known only to the elder Monks. I was assigned to stand watch tonight over the Cloud Temple barracks, where the\n\nseven novices maintained their unremarkable existence. I was the eldest of the novices, only a dozen or so seeds away from wearing the robe of one of the Monks of the Creator. \n\nThe thought of being one of the brothers\n\nor sisters seemed otherworldly to me, but I have dutifully labored for five years, and I was not about to give up, not now. I would take my place among them, and I would go out into the world and help the poor, the injured, the dying. I would not be\n\ndenied that honor.\n\nBut, on long nights such as this one, my resolve was not quite as strong. Keeping watch is quite possibly the most boring chore, and I was required to stand watch one night a week. Normally, I would read one of the Monk’s many tomes,\n\nor practice with the slingshot Pop had given me when I left home to journey to the Cloud Temple. I had not know when I arrived that Alstion had already fallen, and with it the rest of my family. The Creator had intervened for me, it seemed, but that did\n\nnot mean I did not blame myself for what happened. As much as the monks tried to assure me it was not my fault, I could not reconcile my survival with their deaths. \n\nOn the night that the raid happened, I was thinking about my mum’s cooking.\n\nHer fried chicken was better than the orcish variety I had tried on my journey to the Cloud Temple, and her mashed potatoes melted in your mouth. I missed her meatloaf, covered in homemade ketchup almost as much as her strawberry tarts, which oozed a swe…\n\nMy memory was interrupted by the front door to the barracks exploding inward, its hinges blown the fragments. Cloaked men stormed into the hallway, and a dark elf pointed a crossbow at me, saying, “I dare you to move. Please, do. It will give me an excuse\n\nto shoot you.”\n\nMy breath caught in my throat, and that was when I knew I was going to die. The other men moved quickly to the door to the dorms, barring the door from the outside. I could hear banging on it, the novices inside desperately trying to\n\nescape. One of the men, a Southeron, looked me over, saw that I had the keys, and hauled me out of the oak chair I was sitting in, knocking over both it and the table in the process, sending the candlestick, complete with burning candle, tumbling to the\n\nfloor. Luckily, the candle went out, but as I was hauled down the hallway I my mind finally started to thaw, and my first question was “Who they nether are these people?”\n\nI never got a chance to ask, however, as the dark elf shouted at me,\n\n“Open the fecking door!”\n\nShe was pointing at the door to the larder. At first, I did not respond, but after a crossbow was pointed at me again, I fumbled for my keyring, and after several frantic seconds, I managed to get the right key\n\nin the door. The lock clicked open, and my captors rushed in, making straight for the robes on the wall. I only had a second to wonder why they needed the robes when something knocked me in the back of the head, and I was claimed by darkness.\n\nBillowing in the Wind\n\n“I swear, I had no idea it was them. They were in the monks’ robes, what else was I supposed to think? I had no idea who they really were.”\n\nI was laying on a cot, which smelled suspiciously of urine.\n\nConfined to a bed both by my broken leg and a pair of cuffs, I was being “interviewed” by the Captain of the Watch. He had beads of sweat forming on his wrinkled forehead, and his hazel eyes surveyed me critically, taking in every detail, looking for any\n\nsign of dishonesty. I did not blame him. It all seemed rather ridiculous to me as well.\n\n“Could you go over again what happened Recruit? One final time, so that I am sure I have the whole story.”\n\n“Sir, as I have told you seven times, I was manning the gatehouse. It was a rather slow day, as harvest was over and the unusual chill was keeping most people inside, either huddled around their fireplaces or in the taverns. I could see a small mob of\n\nrobed men and women approaching the South Gate, where I had been on duty for three hours. I recall checking my timepiece as they approached. When I looked back up, the leader of the group approached the gatehouse, calling out. He said,\n\n‘Lo! Lower the gates. I have returned!’”\n\n“Who did this man claim to be?”\n\n“Saint Daniel sir. I was skeptical at first, but I quickly recognized the robes they were wearing as the robes of the monks in the South.\n\nMy superior was taking a smoke on the East Wall, and I had no reason not to let them in. So I did. I raised the gate and closed it behind them.”\n\n“Then what happened?”\n\n“They remained clustered together,\n\nand as one, as if directly out of some storybook, their cloaks flew off, flying through the air, twirling like leaves falling from an oak. Then, I saw flashes of light as they drew weapons, some of which I struggle to find names for.\n\nBefore the cloaks touched the ground, they were already headed towards the palace.”\n\n“The men and women, what were they wearing, underneath the cloaks?”\n\n“Tabards sir. \"\n\n“And, how did you break your leg?”\n\n“As the Teutons were heading towards the palace, one shot his crossbow at me. The bolt’s flight was true, and it struck me in the shoulder. It did not pierce the mail, but the force pushed me back, causing me to tumble\n\ndown the stairs. The Creator be thanked I did not break my neck.”\n\n“Thank you for your cooperation Recruit. That will be all for now.”\n\nThe Captain left, and a nurse came in to check the bandages, to check\n\nif it had become infected in the previous hour. After that, I drifted off to sleep, and I dreamed only of His face, the face of the conqueror. The face of Gaius Marius.\n\nThe Storm\n\nI don’t know how I missed their entrance, but it was impossible to miss their exit. \n\nI recall seeing the troop of Teutons marching past the Therving Tavern. They had formed two immaculate columns,\n\nboth of them so perfect that not a single soldier was so much as a step out of rhythm . I blinked once, then, galvanized, untied my apron, placed it on the counter, and started for the door. I had no customers that chilly afternoon, and after slipping on\n\nmy coat, I exited my tavern, locked the door, and chased after the Teutons. My curiosity compelled me to wish to see where the nether they were heading.\n\nAs I arrived in the square, I spotted the unit, standing around their leader.\n\nHe whispered to them for a few moments, and, as the people in the square gathered in small groups, and the windows surrounding it beginning to host intrigued faces, the man proclaimed, “I am Gaius Marius. Today, I breached Al’Khazar’s gate, palace, and\n\nthrone room. Your defenses were useless, and will not protect you from the coming storm.”\n\nA shudder ran through the crowd, and panic started to spread. The man, Gaius Marius I should say, continued to orate.\n\nI do not recall exactly what he said, but it calmed the crowd. He warned of the undead, of our foolishness, of our weakness. Most of all, he warned us about our monarchy, and how it would fail us. Many of us did not believe him, though I did. But, after\n\nthe Teutons departed, and the powers that be scrambled to explain the incident away, I kept my thoughts to myself, and continued to work the counter of the Therving Tavern, serving my customers as best I could. But the doubts remained,\n\nand would be passed down the other Thervings after me, until a Phoenix rose, and we broke our silence.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Destructi...", "§bMonk Scribe", "The Destruction of the Cloud Temple\n\nAnd so it was, that the events near the end of Aegis had unfolded. First Al'Khazar, lost to the taint of the Undead and deadly miasma. Then the north, once the greatest defense of the Undead, also fell. Soon there\n\nit was the great cities of Alras, New Terriko, Galahar and Kal'Urguan. These were terrible times, with the Undead attacking daily and smaller villages and buildings going up in flames daily. Corpses lined the streets and refugees tried to find shelter\n\nwherever they could.\n\nAnd so it was that one last attempt was made to save Aegis, and send the Undead scum back to the Nether. After years of strife and violence, with the Great War a recent memory, it is amazing that the nations managed to join\n\ntogether so quickly. Of course, the threat of Undead domination served as motivation. \n\nAnd so it was that finally, all peoples of Aegis joined together. Champions from each nation were chosen, equipped with what could be salvaged from the wreckage\n\nand sent to Laurelin. There stood a portal, raised by the Undead Vardak. It was here that the Champions of the nations prepared themselves for the final assault on the Nether.\n\nFor those who did not enter that cursed place, there are only\n\nstories. Tales of the heat, and the sickening gas, the hordes of monsters and explosions. It was the Dwarf Urir Ireheart who made it first to the Nexus and destroyed the Axe of Krug, sacrificing himself in the process. In doing so, the Nether began to\n\ncollapse.\n\nFor those waiting outside the portal, gathered in Laurelin and the surrounding areas, this was a pivotal moment. Should the Champions succeed, the Undead would be vanquished. If they failed, Iblees would be free to\n\ncontinue his tyranny upon Aegis. As it turned out...\n\nWe knew that something had gone awry when, instead of the Champions emerging victorious, Dragons suddenly appeared. Massive, black winged beasts, they seemed to strike out of nowhere.\n\nAnd they were not alone. Having seen the destruction in the Nether caused by the Champions, and knowing that his Undead were now to be trapped in the Nether, Iblees unleashed his final fury. \n\nDragons. Fireballs. Monsters. The\n\nsame tools of the Undead that had so ravaged Aegis for decades now struck again. Laurelin burned, nearly the entire city falling to flames. The Cloud Temple, the last safe place for the Descendent Races, was blown to pieces. Even across Aegis, in places\n\nthat had already been conquered by the Undead, and those that hadn't, anything that remained was torn to pieces. The fury of Iblees was remarkable to behold.\n\nStanding on the steps of the Cloud Temple, I was lucky to make it out alive. Having no\n\nnotice of the impending doom, I was saved only by chance. When the Temple exploded under my feet, I happened to land in a puddle. It was pure chaos from that point. I flung arrows into monsters, trying to seek a good vantage point. It seemed in vain, as\n\ntheir numbers quickly overwhelemed those who battled for Aegis. Many were dead instantly, others after a battle. More still retreated from fear or terrible wounds. \n\nAfter running out of arrows I turned to a sword, slashing and hacking. While a\n\nprimitive weapon, it served the purpose well. Zombies, Skeletons and Spiders fell in droves as the sky was lit up with the flames of explosions.\n\nIt was quickly clear that there was no saving the Temple. I fled south on the King's Road, hoping at\n\nleast to try and contain the violence.\n\nI shall never forget that day... the screams, the blood, the endless suffering. In the moment the Undead were gone, it would appear that Iblees had won. The Descendents had no Aegis left, it was\n\ndestroyed beyond measure. We would be forced to flee our lands, escaping through the Verge to Asulon. And yet, Iblees lost as well. His servants the Undead were sealed away in the Nether for all time, useless to him. \n\nPerhaps this is the\n\nmost important lesson of all. There were no winners at the end of Aegis. At best it is a draw, with the Descendents forced to flee and Iblees without his minions. At worst, he secured a victory paid for with the blood of untold numbers, who all died\n\nin the name of Aegis. Although the Undead are seemingly gone, we must be constantly aware of the possibility that they might rise again. Given all that has been endured, one hopes they remain sealed away...\n\n- By Lunia in Asulon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Back Into the...", "§bMonk Scribe", "Back Into the Light\n\nI remember\nOf what I said\nduring that weary, dreary, stormy night.\nThe Undead\nyou see.\nThey are here\nand there\nand well,\nalmost everywhere.\nOne for as far as I\n\ncan see.\n\nSkirmish here\nto Skirmish there.\nTheir magic never goes.\nFrom their Golden hoes,\nto their Undead robes,\nOf what\nthe World foretold.\nI see an opportunity\nto all.\n\nall who intend to join.\nFor it is\na chance.\nBack\ninto the light.\n\n- Written in Aegis by an unknown author.", ""),
        StaticBook("Limerick", "§bMonk Scribe", "There once was a halfling named Fime\nWho could cook a stew worth a dime\nAn orc came one night\nAnd paid for the sight\nOf Fime in a pot with some thyme\n\n- Author unknown.", ""),
        StaticBook("Intro. - Patron", "§bElder Monk Alder Tundrak", "Here follows the account of my findings on a specific location uncovered by myself, and a fellow Monk. \n\nAbout a year ago I began to notice something peculiar going on with a close friend and fellow Monk, Yohei.\n\nYohei was mumbling some sort of prayer, I could not understand what it was in fact. He began this once he started his daily meditation at the Temple Docks.  He would climb down from the dock in a trance like state mumbling, and would make his way to\n\nthe Temple Altar where he would kneel down and mumble. All the while I wandered around behind him following as he once again mumbled. At first I did not quite realize what was going on with this... but as I pondered more and more about the situation a\n\ntheory formed. I remembered what the head of my order, Spike Vondar once said about the Temple Altar… how it has the most imbued Triumvirate power in the lands. Knowing this I thought the trance was Triumvirate based, maybe he was getting some sort of\n\nvision from them, and sook more power. As I watched him more and more and stalked his game I found the same routine happening extremely frequently until one afternoon. It was the fifteenth of Snow’s Maiden, 1523 when it occurred.\n\nHe was beginning his trance, I was following him in toe. He began to walk off his original path, this I thought was quite peculiar. Under further inspection I noticed he was holding a gem in his hand, it was an Emerald.\n\nHe then moved down into the ruined library and did not seem to notice my presence. After he descended the steps and we both stood at the base of the circular nature riddled structure, he took the emerald in his hand and fit it into something inside the\n\nbookshelves.  To my amazement - and this a rare occurrence - I felt the ground jolt and quake and I saw dust fly aside the other half of bookshelves. After this, I wandered over to the shelves, which revealed several steps... Yohei and I then entered into\n\nan oddly shaped room littered with nature, stone brick walls, and a large collection of ruined bookshelves, there standing on an elevated surface was a pillar much like those at the Temple Altar, this one bearing an Emerald center. In this moment it\n\nbecame very clear to me that the fourth patron had the most  to do with these occurrences.\n\nIntro. Fourth Patron\nWritten by Monk Alder\nCloud Temple of Vailor 20 Snow's Maiden 1523", ""),
        StaticBook("A B C of Vailor", "§bLorena Faeliel", "An A B C of Our World.\n\n\n~A Child Friendly  A B C Book on the World and its Inhabitants.~\n\nA is for Aspects\n\n\"Aenguls of nature, a balance of two faces.\"\n\nB is for Bow\n\n\"A weapon used by all races.\"\n\nC is for Canonist\n\n\"Orens faith since its birth.\"\n\nD is for Dwarves\n\n\"What they lack in height, they make up in girth.\"\n\nE is for Elf\n\n\"Tall, thin, lithe and pointy eared.\"\n\nF is for Ferrum\n\n\"Makes reliable weapons, reputably feared.\"\n\nG is for Gorundyr\n\n\"Pagans and warriors, tough as rocks.\"\n\nH is for Halflings\n\n\"Short little men who worship pumpkin god knox.\"\n\nI is for Ironborn\n\n\"An evil empire of khorvad's desire.\"\n\nJ is for Jailers Moss\n\n\"A swampland moss, used in situations dire.\"\n\nK is for Kharajyr\n\n\"A bipedal race, feline and furry.\"\n\nL is for Leather\n\n\"Dried cow hides, can be tanned in a hurry.\"\n\nM is for Mage\n\n\"Shooting out fire and conjuring flowers.\"\n\nN is for Noble\n\n\"A man of high birth, knee deep in power.\"\n\nO is for Orcs\n\n\"Greenskinned and gruf, blood is their lust.\"\n\nP is for Paladin\n\n\"Servant of Xan, their cause is just.\"\n\nQ is for Qalasheen\n\n\"Brown skinned people who reside in the sands.\"\n\nR is for Raevir\n\n\"Dirty Sovetski, the scourge of the lands.\"\n\nS is for Sword\n\n\"A simple tool of wanton murder.\"\n\nT is for Tahariae\n\n\"A holy stag god who takes purity further.\"\n\nU is for Undru\n\n\"Some spooky masked god who lived in a schism.\"\n\nV is for Vailor\n\n\"Due sooner or later for a big cataclysm .\"\n\nW is for Wood Elf\n\n\"A woodland race who's bows are advanced.\"\n\nX is for Xan\n\n\"The holy diety patron of the golden lance.\"\n\nY is for Yamamoto\n\n\"The ancient homeland of the squinty eyed man.\"\n\nZ is for Zombies\n\n\"A rotting flesh monster, run if you can!\"\n\n\"\"\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Our world is vast. Our races varying and our stories different. \n\nThere are many different words for each letter. Do not limit yourself to these!\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~((Props to leowarrior14 for taking it on himself to rhyme every description.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Donkeh.", "§b[Unhooded]Evelyn Nithaniel", "*A Sketch of Donkeh Fills The Page~\n\nDonkeh Sarino was a wonderful soul. He lived 2013-2013. How he passed is unknown, but whoever was the cause of it is a dead man. He will live forever in our hearts, and will never never be forgotten.", ""),
        StaticBook("Battleground", "§bVarstivus", "The Divine Battleground\n\nMany recall Aegis with an air of fondness, nostalgia, reverance. However, in my centuries of abscence from that plane. I have come to realize that it contained some glaring issues that last to this day.\n\nThe land was not a utopia, nor was it a place of expression. After all this time, I have learned that Aegis was nothing bore than a chessboard for beings beyond our comprehension.\nThe battle between the Archaengul Aeriel and the Archdaemon Iblees was\n\nthe world's sole focus. The descendant races clashed, to be sure. Birthing the strange alliance between the elves and the orcs, as well as the blood oath between the dwarves and the humans. All of the war paled in comparison though, to our unified foe.\n\nThe Undead. Fear would strike anyone as thunder could be heard from just over the mountains. The Ascended were not much better, all callous to the smaller issues of the world. Battling the undead was their only purpose. The insignificance of our own lives\n\nwas palpable. All were expected to throw their lives away for the god's cosmic game.\nNothing could bring them to truely care for our lives. We won in the end, fullfilled our purpose. Then we've had none.\nThe humans in this time sought a new patron,\n\nand found one in their creator. The elven culture split in ways that were utterly ofensive at the time, but that are simply considered as normal today. The wood elves  resorted to very bad politics, while the High elves put barriers between themselves and\n\ntheir cousins.\n\nEach race coped differently. But the abandonment of the Aenguls left a fledging society that did not know what to do with themselves.\nNext you hear of Aegis being a land of peace and plenty, recall this.", ""),
        StaticBook("Library Review", "§bE.L.I.A.", "To whom it may concern:\n\nThe Executive Library Inspection Authority (E.L.I.A.) has completed its annual review of credited libraries on Atlas.\n\nThe results are as follows:\n\n5th place:\n\nSutica Library\n-------------------\n\nSeems to have stagnated mid-sorting of books, its collection is thin and the place appears unstaffed.\n\n1.5 out of 5 stars.\n\n4th Place:\n\nThe Eternal Library\n-------------------\n\nAn impressive alas, outdated collection. It seems the library is no longer maintained, no staff were ever found.\n\n2 out of 5 stars.\n\n3rd place:\n\nDunshire Library\n-------------------\n\nQuaint, efficient for its target audience. Must work to expand its collection.\n\n\n3.5 out of 5 stars.\n\n2nd place:\n\nDominion Library\n-------------------\n\nWide variety of texts on many subjects, somewhat updated. Staffed well but has room for expansion.\n\n4.2 out of 5 stars.\n\n1st place:\n\nLibrary Of Dragur\n-------------------\n\nAstonishing collection, entirely up-to-date, staffed and maintained consistently, organised and labeled very efficiently.\n\n5 out of 5 stars.\n\nThe Dominion Library and the Library of Dragur are awarded the certificate of excellency by E.L.I.A.\n\nThe other libraries have potential but great improvements are needed before reaching close to the standard of these two libraries.\n\nCongratulations to the Library of Dragur in particular, who has won the 2500 mina award.\n\nWe wish all libraries success and look forward to the next annual review.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n- The Executive Library Inspection\nAuthority", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall of the Mori", "§bArchmage Crumena", "When the murder and attacks upon the city occurred, many speculations arose within the city itself of whom was to blame and should be slaughtered for such acts against their kind -- many claimed it was the work of surfacers, others believed\n\nthat such things were only possible by those within the city.\nIt was declared and enforced that all living mori were to return to the bosom of Nemiisae and remain within the sanctum of Menorcress: behind these stragglers to return the\n\nhorror unfolded, each path and passage they journeyed through only hours before could be heard crumbling under the weight of explosives. The people were brought each in turn to the Temple of the Mother to be cleansed of their\n\ntaint, the sickness of the surface that had infested them. The final act of the Valsharess and her yathrins before the war broke out.\nMany that had broken loose from such rigid traditions fought against this cleansing and became quickly enraged,\n\nspitting in the faces of the priestess' whom dared demand their obedience and silence. It was not long before two factions emerged, the devote and the rebels.\nBeneath the surface of the world, sealed off from the blinding damnation of suns\n\nlight, the Caverns of Menorcress. Its streets littered with crude barricades, strewn with the deceased and wounded -- the one marvelled city now rots with death and destruction... crumbling under civil war. Bathed in life blood of their kith\n\nand kin, the rebellion breach upon the Yathrins' sacred enclave; banners raised in revolt, their armour and bodies marked by their treason. Once considered mere common rabble; these denizens now slaughter blessed noble born and\n\ntheir ilk standing guard at the doors of the Temple. From behind the sealed doors both rothe and mori alike stand in un-ease union against the treat of taint of its own city -- this seeded by those turned to the hubris of their Ilharn Zanunder.\n\nRescribed by Archmage Crumena V. Ilwindior on the 2nd of The First Seed 1473.", ""),
        StaticBook("Thales Treaty", "§bUnknown", "The Treaty of Thales, 1463\nFor long war has plagued this realm. The descendants of Malin, Horen, Krug and Urguan clashing has wrought only death and misery and must come to an end. These two nations have come to an\n\nagreement which ends this conflict, relegating the bad blood between these two people to a past to be forgotten.\nI. The Grand Kingdom of Urguan formally exiles all elves from within its borders. Pledging never again to offer them\n\nasylum or vassalage under their rule. Exceptions may be granted by the Sohaer of the Silver Enclave of Haelun’or.\nII. The Kingdom of Urguan expels and further denies any Human faction or sovereign state,\n\npledging to deny the aforementioned any asylum, protectorate status, vassalage, or otherwise direct support. Exceptions may be granted by the Emperor Robert Primus Aeldinicus Chivay.\nIII. The Silver Enclave of\n\nHaelun’or formally exiles all snow elves from within its borders. Pledging never again to offer them asylum of vassalage under their rule.\nIV. The Imperium Tertius expels and further denies and Dwarven faction\n\nor sovereign state, pledging to deny the aforementioned any asylum, protectorate status, vassalage, or otherwise direct support. Exceptions may be granted by the King or the Dwarven Council of Lords.\nV. Both the\n\nImperium Tertius and the Kingdom of Urguan agree to pledge their swords to the eradication of the Teutonic Order and the sovereign State of Hanseti, citing past transgressions to both the Imperium Tertius and the Kingdom of Urguan\n\nas a just cause for war.\nVI. The Establishment of an extradition court, between Urguan and Imperium Tertius, whose efforts are aimed at rooting out and delivering any fugitives to their respective\n\nnation, to be properly tried and judged based on the nations’ respective laws.\nVII. The Agreement between the Imperium Tertius, Haelun’or and the Kingdom of Urguan of a two year ((2 week)) ceasefire, should\n\nthe discovery of new lands that are more favorable for the nations to settle, guaranteeing a safe transition and peaceful settling.\nVIII. The Dwarves of the Grand Kingdom of Uraguan and Silver Enclave of Haelun’or shall cleanse the\n\nrealm of the blight known as the mali’fenn or snow elves. There is to be no mercy upon them nor peace to be made with them.\nIX. A town shall be established, ruled by both Haelun’or and Urguan. No snow elves or any\n\nelves of high elven blood may live within this town. Exceptions to the rule of no high elves may be granted by the Silver Enclave of Haelun’or.\nThe leader of this town shall be selected by a majority vote of all residents of the\n\ntown. Half elves do not count, for they are twice cursed. This leader administers the town.\nThe town shall remain neutral in all worldly conflicts.\nAn entrance will be made available for the Council of Haelun’or and Lords of Urguan to use\n\nas is required. They may not be barred entry from the town at any time.\nCriminals, the impure and undesirables may be culled and exiled from the town by either faction as they deem fit.\nThe town’s name is to be selected by the Silver Enclave of\n\nHaelun’or and must be named using elven, as is tradition for elves. This name must be used.\nBoth Haelun’or and Urguan have a veto on the creation of new laws within the town.\nBoth Haelun’or and Urguan may police and enforce laws\n\nwithin the town, as they deem fit.\nThe head of the Guard must be approved by both Haelun’or and Urguan to be appointed. If approval is revoked by either one of them at any time, another must be found.\nA guard must be\n\nestablished to enforce the laws of the town.\nThe town must provide grain and other food products to both Haelun’or and Urguan which is equivalent to 20% of their yield. 10% to one nation and 10% to the other.\n((In the event\n\nUrguan and Haelun’or are to return to war, the ownership of the town is to be decided by a /roll 2 with 1 granting Haelun’or ownership and 2 granting Urguan ownership)).\nX. Haelun’or formally apologizes for the acquisition of the\n\nGolem Anvil in Asulon.\nXII. To further strengthen this new found peace the Silver Enclave of Haelun’or and Grand Kingdom of Urguan shall agree to the uninfringed movement of labour, livestock and capital between one\n\nanothers lands, with restricted areas in place for each body.\nXIII. Similarly, to allow fair trial between one anothers nations and due process of law during cases concerning international criminality, an extradition treaty\n\nshall be signed between Haelun’or and Urguan to allow the transfer custody between one anothers nation bearing both parties agreement.\nSohaer Kalenz Uradir of the Silver Enclave of Haelun'or\n\n\nThe Grand Kingdom of Urguan\nEmperor Robert Chivay of the Imperium Tertius", ""),
        StaticBook("Death of Availer", "§bJosef Timothee", "THE DEATH OF THE\n WANDERING WIZARD\n\n\nOn Ahad, the 8th of the Deep Cold, 1336, the world of Aegis was struck by a terrible tragedy. I, Josef Timothee, record here my own experience during these events.\n\n\nI was in Al'Khazar when a voice rang out, filling all of Aegis. It identified itself as the Wandering Wizard. He said that he had three relics that needed to be taken to the Cloud Temple. If they were to fall into Undead hands, he claimed, terrible\n\ntrouble would result for the people of Aegis. He sent forth a cry over all the lands, asking for support on the journey from Al'Khazar to the Cloud Temple on the King's Road. A large crowd assembled with him in Al'Khazar, mostly humans but\n\nrepresentatives from other races there as well.\n\nThe procession headed down the King's Road and was immediately attacked. Lightning rained down from the skies, and monsters appeared out of thin air. But those in the crowd were ready, and struck back against Iblees minions. The monsters were defeated\n\nthrough sheer numbers of those opposing them, as well as the powerful magic of the Wandering Wizard. All along the journey, he kept up words of encouragement and urged the crowd onwards. The lightning and monsters were relentless, delaying\n\nthe journey terribly.\n\nBy the time the procession reached the Cloud Temple many had died trying to protect the Wizard en route. It was there that the Undead suddenly struck the most violently I have ever witnessed, not only casting lightning powerful enough\n\nto damage the Cloud Temple, but also changing the landscape around it to look like the Nether. Among this, explosions and lightning were striking everywhere, causing great suffering. The Wizard urged all present to take shelter in the Cloud Temple.\n\nI took this advice, having been clipped by lightning and set ablaze. Once inside, the extent of the damage was clear. Hundreds entered the Temple, many wounded by burns or monsters. The Temple shook as explosions rocked it from outside and pieces of it\n\nbroke off. Then...\n\nA new voice rang out, saying that the Wizard had been slain by the Undead. The outpouring of grief was immediate, and the attacks on the Temple ceased.\n\nSomeone shouted that the Undead had taken three objects from the Wizard that looked like eggs. The skies lightened, the landscape changed back, and the crowd left the Temple. But the world was altered permanently with the death of the\n\nWandering Wizard. It remains to be seen what the Undead will do with the stolen relics.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Deep Cold", "§bGregory", "The Fringe, 1461\nKhorvad, a name uttered in whispers amongst dwarven kind. And for good reason, he is believed to be an entity of woe, and this much was surely true for a plague like no other, aptly named Khorvad’s Grip. The illness was\n\nbelieved to have originated in the dwarven city of Kal’Arkon itself, decimating its population and forcing them from their homes with a violet efficiency no army could ever hope to match. But when the dwarves fled, they brought the\n\nplague with them.\nThe merchant city of Alras was quick to follow, and it perhaps because this bustling trade centre became infected that the plague rapidly spread to all corners of the map as travellers and salesmen went to and fro, unaware of\n\nthe deadly illness they were burdened with until it had spread to their friends and their loved ones. A vast number of the world’s population came into contact with the disease, and as healers were in short supply, countless lives\n\nwere lost.\nKhorvad’s Grip, is a demon of the cold. It’s habitat is one of frost, and that particular winter was relentless indeed. It’s murder was an artform, such a slow and agonising demise - it first bestowed its victims with fatigue so intense\n\nthat to travel down the roads and see moaning wretches lying on the ground, was no unusual sight. The second dastardly symptom was an intense hunger, one that decimated standards and morals. Descendants would consume anything\n\nthey could stumble upon, in some recorded cases, even other Descendants. Like ghouls, the infected roamed, crawling, shuffling, and spewing bile. Their body temperatures lowered to extreme levels and if the cold didn’t kill them,\n\neventually their organs would rupture, and they’d die a most miserable, undignified death.\nFor a time, it was easy to call it the end. The true end. Medicine was ineffective and the disease spread faster than the handful of magical healers could\n\nremedy it. All had seemed to be lost, for how can you fight an enemy that can’t be seen, that can’t be pinpointed on a map. And if it weren’t for the efforts of a particularly valiant dwarf, the Descendants journey may have ended during\n\nthose cold months, those deeply cold months.\nHis name was Onar Ireheart. The dwarf, having studied the plague since it’s outbreak, developed a cure. The world owes that dwarf a great debt, and though the snow will fall again and the\n\ncold may yet be deeper, it is thanks to him that Khorvad’s Grip remains a blurred memory, and no longer a terrifying reality.", ""),
        StaticBook("Snow's Maiden", "§bGregory", "Aegis, 1317\nWe conclude each year with the memory of a people that saw destruction like no other. We were a new world, we had flourished and thrived without obstacle or opposition for many years, but the first instance of\n\ndestruction and terror upon the world was wrought by the Descendant’s ancient foe, Iblees and his Undead forces.\nThe peaceful town was known as Snowy Fields. It sat to the north of the human capital of Al’khazar, and it was in the\n\nnorth that the first Nether Portals quietly opened, taint seeping through, releasing a true evil the likes of which the world would struggle to comprehend. Snowy Fields became the front lines, battling each day against new hordes of vile, twisted\n\nundead creatures, burning and devouring all that came in their path. For many months, the citizens of Snowy Fields lived in fear of the night, when the undead attacks would surely come. Desperate to defend themselves, their reinforced their\n\nwalls, armed their citizens, and kept a close watch over the frozen tundra that surrounded them.\nThe death toll kept rising, with no end to their turmoil in sight, the citizens of Snowy Fields prepared for a counter-attack against a large undead\n\nfortification further to their north. But in those young days of the world, the days where we had never truly known danger, the residents were caught unprepared. The undead crushed their forces, hundreds of bodies littering the snow, their blood\n\nstaining it with a deep crimson.\nWhat was once a quiet sanctuary, an isolated oasis of frost, the Snow’s Maiden, was now a worn battleground. With renewed malice and hatred, the undead struck again, and this time were victorious. The\n\ntown was eliminated - men, women and children slain in their homes. Even those that escaped the nightmare of Snowy Fields are said to have never been the same again.\nAlthough the first true loss of the Descendants, the sad tale of Snowy\n\nFields rallied the forces of Aegis together, a fresh anger ran rampant across the land as the story spread from city to city. Aegis had lost its peaceful snowy maiden, and now it stood united, the common enemy had shown us it's malevolent\n\nnature, and we would have our revenge.", ""),
        StaticBook("Atheran Eye One", "§bIgnii Ossaura", "The Atherian Eye - \n      Issue  One\n_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_\n\nYou know , among my many decades alive in this world , I've noticed a number of things. One of which , is about wood elves.\n\nMost wood elves are calm , good natured people. They focus on their plants or trees ; infact , most become Druids at a young age. Why is that?\n\n\nMaybe they have a sense of peace that we other races just can't tap into?\n\nI do know one thing , though. That one mali' stands out above the rest. Not for good reasons , oh no. This man's name is Art Camoryn , a slightly senile cinnamon mali' with a hate for necromancers.\n\nDue to my curiousity as a writer and a scholar , I had someone seek him out for an interview.\n\nWhat was found out is as follows ;\n\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-\n\nFirst question , what are your hopes for this mali' nation?\n\nWell , I suppose I would hope for a strong military. Many people know of the past failures made by mali' when it comes to a fighting force. Nether , even the mali'aherals know how shit thei\n\n'lethal silver knights' are when compared to the Akovians. I want strength that could rival even that of the green-skinned fuckers in the desert. \n\nReally? I would have assumed the first thing you would seek out would be good trading agreements?\n\nIt crossed my mind , but no. \n\nHrm. Many people have stated that you dislike the Coven of Necromancers that lurk nearby. Would you say that's correct?\n\nOf course. They're disgusting people who need to be brought-\n\ndown. Inbred and mentally ill scum , as I always say. They're only good for the Dreadknight armor. Although , I do appreciate their building skills in Embermor. Maybe if they didn't drink blood , I might have even hired them for the town hall. I could-\n\neven send out a small fighting force to crush them , if I needed. Nothing to worry about. \n\nA fair view , I suppose. Due to current state of the wood elven town , the high female population and the outragously dressed men , many people-\n\nhave started to call your nation 'New Malinor'. Would you say this is fair or correct?\n\nWhoever said that lacks any form of brain. I will not have this nation reduced to a high-price dictatorship like Malinor.\n\nBut , from current reports , you have the final saying in all decisions in the counsil in your town? Would you not call that a dictatorship?\n\nNo more questions. I'm too busy to deal with a hour interview.\n\n-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-_-\n\nAs you can clearly read , Art Camoryn is a violent , rude and brash elf. Not only is his hairline recedding , but his mental health is too! This has been the first Atheran Eye.\n\n\n- Ignii Ossaura , Atheran Eye Publisher.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hou-zi Conflict", "§bLothiriel", "A brief summary of real events having been experienced by the Zhu under the leadership of Wu-Zedong.\n\nRecently one of their own by the name of Wu-Zhan decided to pretend he was the leader of the Zhu. Wu-Zhan began to make trouble for the nearby group of humans and elves that have also settled on the island this Zhu calls home.\n\nWu-Zhan stole livestock, killed pregnant women, harrassed the villagers, all because of his hatred of elves and humans for past actions; But one must learn to forgive and move on past these feelings, lest fire burn from sparks still in ash.\n\nWu-Zhan did not forgive, nor did he forget, and the nearby residents of this island were victim to the cruelty that was born from the beast that had become his heart. The others of the Zhu always seek to bury that hatred, to quell the fire\n\nand fight the beast, lest it consume them. Wu-Zhan did not. But as a consequence of Wu-Zhan's actions, violence was brought upon the rest of the Zhu, who were blamed as well for the misdeeds.\n\nIn the morning the nearby humans and elves stormed the Zhu and their home, the sound of iron boots stomping, swords and shields crashing, as the humans and elves approached, ready to kill all of the Zhu for the actions of Wu-Zhan.\n\nOnly Wu-Kong and Wu-Zedong were present when the other natives arrived. The humans and elves brought thanhic bombs and other weaponry the hou-zi had not seen before. They stormed the gates and announced their intentions, causing\n\nWu-Zedong to prepare himself for the coming onslaught, regardless of the blood to be shed. This is understandable for a leader must always be prepared to defend his people.\n\nThe sounds of swords and shields clashing deafened the hall, and Wu-Zedong lost himself in the bloodshed, losing briefly his control to the beast all warriors carry within. But only briefly.\n\nWu-Zedong laid eyes on the body of the leader of his foes and rather than smite his wrath upon him, he chose to take him prisoner for the purposes of brokering a peace, to put an end to the bloodshed.\n\nWu-Zedong explained to the enemy leader the cause of this, the punishment already dealt upon Wu-Zhan. Then, he let the leader go, hoping they would put an end to the meaningless fighting knowing now the truthful cause of it.\n\nThe hou-zi hope this tale encourages others to seek a peaceful resolution of dialogue as opposed to violence, as blood shed is not always necessary for us to resolve our differences.\n\nScribe's note;\n\nAfter the initial hearing of this tale, the Library of Dragur Scholar, Lothiriel, volunteered to approach the human settlement to broker peace.\n\nThe humans, lead by one named Lion, were open to dialogue. Lothiriel returned to the hou-zi with this and Wu-Zedong agreed to meet with them.\n\nThe human-elf representatives were brought to the hou-zi encampment for discussions.\n\nThe Lion introduced himself as Prince Darius DeNurem, the Lion of Judah. \n\nWu-Zedong reiterated his desire for peace, though admitted that 'some' have made this desire difficult to achieve.\n\nPrince Darius offers in peace in exchange for a book the hou-zi supposedly have in their possession; As an early peace offering he grants them a number of gifts of what, food, and other supplies.\n\nPrince Darius DeNurem seeks the Book of Judah. Wu-Zedong does not know of it or if it is here, but departs to search for it. The book, it seems, is not in the hands of hou-zi.\n\nPrince Darius agrees to peace regardless. Wu-Zedong, for his part, promises that if the hou-zi find the book they will return it.\n\nPereus, the dwarf, attempts to smoke. This is offensive to their god.\n\nPereus stops, luckily, and the hou-zi take no offense.\n\nHappily peace has been achieved between these two groups, hopefully for a long, long while.", ""),
        StaticBook("Prophecy I", "§bNatayshi", "Moongazer Prophecy\n-------------------\n\nThe Black Prochecy\n\nThis particular prophecy has already come to pass, and was one of the most accurate and chilling prophecies ever to be gazed upon by the Kharajyr Moongazers. Metztli bestowed\n\nupon them a sight unlike any other, the world ablaze in fire and brimstone, corrupt minions of an unknown origin roaming the earth wielding an ancient magic.\n\nThe Moongazers interpreted this vision of the future as the coming of Absyyl, the\n\nenemy of Metztli, who is the Goddess of the Kharajyr faith.\n\nAbsyyl's image is one of the sun, the sun being the symbol of all evil and wrong doing in the world. In this image, the Moongazers believed they saw this image floating above a world ablaze\n\nThese events did occur, although temporary and not entirely in the way the Moongazers predicated. For the symbol was not the sun, but an eye. The wretched Eye of Iblees. \n\nThe prophecy foretold of an old enemy, and that it would once\n\nagain sack the world, corrupting its good and tainting its sanctity. It is for this reason that the Kharajyr mistook the visions as the returning of Absyyl.\n\nHad they have known it was Iblees, perhaps more could have been done to prepare for his seco\n\ncoming. Alas, let it be proof of a Moongazer's worth. A prophecy from a Moongazer is never to be ignored.", ""),
        StaticBook("Prophecy III", "§bNatayshi", "Moongazer Prophecy\n-------------------\n\n    The Snow Tide\n\nThis prophecy was made during the early days of Anthos. The Sage Natayshi accurately predicted the fleeing of the now supposedly extinct species known as the 'Bohra' fleeing from\n\nthe Frozen North, being carried by a great tidal wave of snow, pursued by a collosal dragon with wings as black as the night. This dragon turned out to be the wretched beast known as Setherien, who was defeated at the ending days of Anthos.\n\nAlthough the Moongazers made great efforts to inform the world of the coming threat, their warnings fell on deaf ears, and the inevitable occured.\n\nThe turmoil of Setherien and his Harbingers was devastating, but perhaps the damage\n\ncould have been lessened if the Moongazer's warning had been treated with urgency, instead of pushed to one side.", ""),
        StaticBook("Malin's Welcome", "§bGregory", "Aegis, 1305\nThe earth shifted, shoots and saplings eased through the cracks of the dry mud, intertwining and growing toward the first light of the year, a young, radiant sun. It was the year of the great inheritance - the old were to die, and\n\nthe young claimed Aegis as their own.\nIt was the first time the world was without its brothers. Horen, Krug, Urguan and Malin. The founders of life did watch over them no longer, thus from the nest we fell. And would they now marvel to see us soar. We\n\nwere the children of the greats, but it was not their world anymore, it was ours. Ours to shape, ours to nurture and ours to command. As the trees and plants reached with a yearning toward the new sun, so did we clasp at the future, for now it\n\nbelonged to the Descendants.\nThe day of Malin’s Welcome, was also the day of his goodbye. As the last of the brothers remaining, he passed the mantle to another. No longer could he cater to his children’s needs, for how were they to grow? When the\n\ncold has passed and the crops begin to sprout, with his presence his children remained a barren field. Never to learn, and worse, never to teach.\nWith grace and subtlety, the ancient elf took a final walk through his home - Laurelin. A route\n\ncarefully planned to start where the frost of the ponds melted, to where a gnarled tree stood alone amongst a nest of vines. With a gentle tap of an oaken staff, he knocked on the door at the base of the tree. A bearded face appeared,\n\nmimicking Malin’s smile, and his name was Native. The two conversed for a short while, chirpy and happy, like the birdsong that played around them with renewed vigor under the warmth of the new year.\nWithout celebration, Malin’s welcome\n\nwas over. Without applause, did the bearded elf take his staff. Without notice, did Malin stroll leisurely into the woods. And without a goodbye, he was gone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Grand Harvest", "§bGregory", "Kalos, 1417\nA tale of friendship. A tale of unlikely alliances; where two forces that by all reason should never have become acquainted, did. The simple folk most know as the Halflings were and will always be a peaceful folk, their ambitions the most\n\nhumble of us all. They care not for wealth, for stretching their borders, for any form of power over another living being - and it is perhaps these qualities that brought them close to a man that could never know mercy.\nThey found him in the dry heat\n\nof the afternoon, where the joyful halflings reaped the rewards of one of the most fruitful harvests they had seen. And who else could be responsible, but the Pumpkin Lord. He stood amongst the fields, frozen, adorning the\n\nsmiling mask of a pumpkin. From a distance it would be feasible to confuse him with a scarecrow, and so the halflings did. They approached the figure without fear, laughing and skipping. But much to their fright, the scarecrow laughed back.\n\n\nThey conversed, but the Pumpkin Lord said nothing. They celebrated, and the Pumpkin Lord smiled. They prayed, and the Pumpkin Lord was born. He had gone by many names, none particularly flattering, but his true name was Knox, and in the space\n\nof a warm afternoon he was elevated from man, to God.\nPerhaps it was his ego that caused him to stay, perhaps pity. Though his intentions could never truly be known to any but himself, the friendship was formed regardless. The halflings\n\nbrought him home, each brimming with excitement at the arrival of their lord. Knox said little, but took them by the hand and spent the coming days on the outskirts of their village. No matter what he did, no matter what random act he performed, the\n\nhalflings were blindly grateful. Celebrations like no other were thrown and for a time, all seemed well.\nAlas, Knox had business elsewhere. Though he would frequently return, the halflings would not spare the world of his malice. It\n\nwas several weeks later when his absence was truly noticed. A couple of bandits strolled into sleeping village, the pitch of night cloaking them until it were too late. They bore swords and torches, burning crops and slaying the half-folk where they\n\nstood, each wearing a perverse smile. The screams of the halflings and laughter of the murderers slowly lulled to whispers as a new laughter cracked across the sky. His silhouette against the moon, a glint of steel in his hands, the Pumpkin\n\nLord approached.\nAnd what a grand harvest it was.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sun's Smile", "§bGregory", "Elysium, 1415\nThe Descendants knew this place could never truly be home. While the land was fertile and the climate ideal, it was small. Borders remained contested, conflict arose through proximity, and each nation struggled for the land it\n\nrequired. It was on this island they called Elysium, that something very peculiar happened.\nEven though it were night, a human farmer wiped the sweat from his brow, despite the setting of the sun, the heat persisted, but at least his day was over.\n\nThis man was an experienced farmer, and his pride and joy, were his chickens. Though vegetation was rampant across the island, fresh meat was not, and the demand for food was growing exponentially. The simple farmer,\n\nwhose name was never known, started a series of events that to this day has had a rippling effect on our world.\n“Bugger” he muttered dryly. His prize chickens, dozens of them, had escaped. He had left the pen unlocked and by morning, they\n\nwere gone. Though a setback, he was sure he could climb back from it. A distant clucking however, disagreed. The soil of Elysium bore fresh seeds from native plants to the island, the grass was thicker here, and green covered all landscapes. Even\n\nthe mountains were no exception to the bombardment of foliage. This land… It was a chicken’s dream. And soon after, their worst nightmare.\nOver the course of several days, twenty chickens became forty, several more, eighty, and so on\n\nfor the coming weeks. Each night, children would peer from the windows and into the darkness, hundreds of small vacant eyes staring absently back at them, their foreboding clucks haunting their dreams. Soon thousands of\n\nchickens swarmed the island, no nation was exempt from their torment. Great hunting parties formed to cull their numbers, but it was too late. They had grown to be too many, and no amount of slaughter could stem the horde of the white feathered\n\ndemons.\nThough the days were so warm and the sky always so clear, the Descendants were driven to madness. If the sun truly were smiling, it was at nature’s most destructive practical joke. The chickens consumed all life like\n\nlocusts, their mass breeding had meant there was no longer enough food for them to expand their plague any further. Conditions worsened, where there was shrubbery, there was now only mud. The chickens starved, disease spread\n\nlike wildfire amongst them and soon their numbers fell. And fell. And fell. Now only a handful remained. Now there was no meat, and no plantlife. The descendants were forced to leave.\nTo this day, disease lives on in chicken-kind.\n\nTheir numbers continue to fall and it is unlikely that we will ever see such an abundance again. So each year, when the sun is at its highest, look up and smile. Smile, and pray that we never see the return of one of the most destructive forces we have\n\never known, the ruthless empire of the chicken.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Amber Cold", "§bGregory", "Anthos, 1439\nA party of nine trudged through the frozen mountains of Northern Anthos, each an expert in their field. They were the Order of the Golden Lance, and yet they were so far from home. These paladins had searched for\n\nyears for a vile serpent that had once escaped them, but not again. The tracks were fresh, a sickly black smog rose on the horizon, and the bare trees quaked from a distant, piercing roar.\nThey could not have been more\n\nprepared to face Setherien had they tried. Decades of training and planning had brought them to this moment, and as the roars grew louder, their confidence remained absolute. Were they to let the Drakaar live, then its power would only grow,\n\nthus the sooner the foul entity were the slain, the sooner the world could rest easy knowing there was one less hateful creature to threaten them.\nHow wrong they were. Nothing could truly have prepared them for what they faced. The air became\n\nstill as the roaring ceased, the sky darkened with colossal pillars of smoke and ash, the light of the dragon’s fires dancing across the snow with a deep orange hue. An Amber cold indeed. From the cover of the thick, pestilent smog blotting out the\n\nstars, Setherien descended with a crash, an avalanche of snow in his wake. The paladins were caught off guard, it was a trap, somehow he had known of their approach. The Drakaar mimicked the mountains with his size, his black scales glistening in the\n\namber glow. With a hoarse chuckle and not moment’s trepidation, the serpent attacked.\nThe paladin’s battle lasted but mere minutes, unaware of the the creature’s true power. When first encounterd, Setherien was a fearful\n\nhatchling, but now stood as a true monster, a lord of corruption and fire. One by one, they fell. The dragon’s immolating flame engulfing them, not only searing away their armour and flesh, but mutilating their very souls.\nIt would have been\n\na true mercy were the Paladins’ story to end there, but it was not to be. For they rose again, clad in black robes and frigid, glacial armour, the Harbingers of Setherien were born. The unholy creature had turned the world’s\n\nheroes against them, and now their march continued.\nBut no longer did they march north, now their ashen gaze loomed back to the south. And the destruction that they would bring will be remembered for centuries.", ""),
        StaticBook("Play Orc", "§bBuubHozh Hefner", "PlayOrc\n\n\n*The cover page features a caricature of a bunny with rows and rows of teeth*\n\nZlutz Uv De Munth\n\n*The following ten pages feature women with disfiguring scars in extremely high quality armor.*\n\nPruper Tuzk Care\n\n*Listed here is a long and suprisingly informed article about polishing tusks to shine. According to the article, \"Bitchez Luv Shinee Tuzkz\" *\n\n BuubHozh Hefner\n\n*This article, accompanied by a drawing of an old uruk wrestling two female uruk and a Lur Wolf at once, depicts the life of a fictitious Uruk mating tychoon named BuubHozh Hefner.*\n\nMojo ztrength, Real ur Fayke?\n\n*Depected in a picture for the article is a battle-scarred, armored elven woman lifting an entire boulder above her head.*\n*The rest of the article is about telekinetics.*\n\n  De Bear Flattin\n     Ztandurd\n*Below is a drawing of a scarred, scantily clad orc woman snapping a bear's neck with her bare hands. It folds out into 4 pages.*\n\"If Zhe can nub flat a bear wid hur bare handz, zhe iz nub Hozh Mayte!\"\n\n      Flat - Ztickz\n      Agh Lat!\n*The featured weapon this issue seems to be the famous White Rose Arbelest, accompanied by a picture of a scarred human woman firing it.*\n*To one side of it is a column comparing serrated and normal batt\n\n Lettur Frum De           Zlutz\n *There's a long (and likely fictional) letter below from a (presumably) female author about how she cant stand an uruk who doesn't smell like the blood of their enemies.*", ""),
        StaticBook("My Return", "§bWargoth Malog'Yar", "These past several years mi have been on pilgrimage. It was nub a pilgrimage to any particular holy place or shrine, but was rather a sacred wandering of sorts. Mi explored wild and uninhabited places, and further hardened mi already thick hide.\n Mi\n\nhave meditated atop the highest peaks of frozen mountains. Mi have trod the scorched earth of volcanic regions where the air is clouded with smoke agh ash. Mi have stalked through the underbrush of mi people's jungles, braving the dangers of the many\n\npredators thereof.\n In mi travels, mi have observed the skies by morning, listened to the voice of the wind by day, gazed into fires by evening, agh dreamed both wonderous agh terrible dreams by night. All of existence, both waking agh sleepeing, blah\n\nmi. The spirits guide mi through the stars agh moon, agh drive mi on through the sun. They whisper in the grass of the fields agh murmur in the caves. The waves of the sea shout to they who listen.\n Mi return this day from mi pilgrimage to find mi peop\n\nscattered, agh their blargs empty. The streets are silent. The walls have been thrown down. Just as well though. I hated that goi. The orcs have done far hosher. San'Orca; San'Vitar; Kodar'goi; San'Thraka. These were gois worthy of Krug!\n Still though,\n\nbrothers agh sisters are left without a land. The sharas mouth boastful things in their perpetual arrogance, agh their wood albai whores have spat on the shadow of Enrohk  by stretching their hands out against his shrines. Darûkûrz bûbri, afar angathfark\n\nagh vadokanuk, ashdautus vrasubatlat! All who read this, heed those words. Let them be the words of all the Orcish people. Gruk them agh lock them in lats spirit.\n Meanwhile, the spirit realm screams, agh the bub'hosh powers of the universe shift. Mi\n\nhear the moaning agh creaking of all reality in mi sleep. The h'ash arms have fallen. Such is the price of betrayal, though mi blah it with a heavy soul. Those arms could have upheld us for all eternity, had carelessness nub taken hold of our Rex. Kharak\n\nwas a fine Rex, but his ambition outgrew his wisdom. Now, that which brought us such power has been layed low, agh we suffer for it. The powers with which he played are not toys, agh Orgon is nub a howler on a leesh. Had he gruk'd that sooner, things\n\nwould still be as they ought to be. Let all living shamans learn from his error, agh excercize due caution when wielding such power.\n Now, Kinul stands where mi old master agh the giver of mi sight once stood. These days weigh heavily on mi bones. Now,\n\nhowever, is nub a time to mourn. Now is the time to steel ourselves. We are nub as the sharas, who live on through their gois agh land. Wi are nub as the albai, who grow fat at the trough of comfort agh luxury. We are nub as the gazat, who hole up in\n\ncaves, agh find their security in riches. We are the orcs, the cubs of Krug. Our strength is to be found in hardship agh trial. \n Since the days of the Ancients, our kind has fought for every morsel of food; every cup of water; every inch of land;\n\nevery breath of air; agh every second of existence. These days are nub to be lamented, but rather let us stand tall as ever. Let us remember who we are. These days are not a grave to lie down in. They are a crucible to purify us. They are a fire to harden\n\nour skins.\n We are the uruk, the goblins, agh the ologs. We are the cubs of Krug. We are the orcs. Look upon lats ancestors, brothers agh sisters, agh shout proudly. Raise lats lusks, lats zults, lats o'ligs, agh lats fists. Bare lats tusks, stand atop\n\nthe bloody agh broken heaps of lats enemies, agh roar. For the spirits. For the Ancestors. For Krug!\n -Malog, Wargoth of the Yar Clan.\n 7th of The Grand Harvest, 1583.", ""),
        StaticBook("His Fungi", "§bMotsham Malog'Yar", "((This book was written by an orc, but since most of the Blah is mispronounced common, I only wrote the words that are actually different for orcs in the Blah. The words shared between the two languages are written in Common. Sorry for the clunky OOC\n\npreface, but I just wanted to give the reader a heads-up.))    Many of those who gruk mi, gruk that mi have long been a devout worshiper of Orgon. Those who have visited the shrine of Orgon atop the plateau in San'Vitar, may have noticed the fungus which\n\npopulates the mound on which the shrine is erected. Very few people gruk the nature agh significance of the fungus, agh would ignorantly dismiss it as nub-thing more than a bunch of ugly mushrooms. These mushrooms, however, are actually a\n\nsupernatural phenomenon. The fungus which grows upon Orgon's mound is not of the natural world. It is a physical manifestation of Orgon's will agh influence spreading in the mortal plane. This is why lat will nub ever find any growing on their own in a\n\nnormal environment. Very few also gruk that the fungus is, in fact, carnivorous, but feeds almost exclusively during the feeding rituals of Orgon worship. Now, when mi blah the word \"carnivorous\", mi mean it very strongly. During the feeding ritual, the\n\nfungus almost instantly takes root in the flesh of the sacrifice, and begins literally consuming its prey. The process causes the victim to be rapidly digested alive within a matter of minutes. The fungus devours every last piece of its prey, leaving\n\nbehind neither flesh, blood, bones or organs. This is how Orgon has revealed to his followers that his sacrifices must be offered. Outside of the feeding ritual, the fungus feeds very rarely, occassionally digesting any insects that find themselves\n\ntrapped in the liquid secretions of the mushrooms. Now, onto the specifics. There are dub varieties of mushrooms which grow upon Orgon's sacrificial mounds: Orgon's bile and Orgon's gall. Both of these mushrooms have some similar qualities. Namely,\n\nneither should be taken without asking permission of Orgon and rulging him for his generosity; agh they should both be handled with care. \n Orgon's bile: These short, squat mushrooms are a bluish-purple color with white spots. On each spot grow many\n\ntiny black spores. The spores are easily broken, agh contain a foul-smelling black substance. It smells very much like decomposing flesh, and tastes like rotten eggs. Contact stains the skin. A slight taste of the mushroom or the oily, black substance\n\ncauses nausea (agh mi mean a VERY slight taste). Mi tested the effects of full consumption of the mushroom on a willing burz-albai named Mithras. Upon immediately eating the whole thing, he was beset by extreme nausea and vomiting, a cold sweat and\n\nsevere shaking. This was from only ash mushroom. Mi would strongly advise against eating more than ash or a particularly large specimen, as such could very possibly result in flattening. ((Note: these are the red mushrooms growing near Orgon's\n\nshrine))\n Orgon's gall: These somewhat taller mushrooms are related to Orgon's bile, agh are brown in color. The cap of the Orgon's gall mushroom is bowl shaped, agh constantly secretes a very bitter yellowish-brown fluid. This fluid pools in\n\nthe aforementioned bowl-shaped cap, and emits musty fumes which irritate the eyes upon exposure. Physical contact with the mushroom causes a slight burning sensation in the skin, as the fungus coats itself in its own digestive fluids. In small amounts,\n\nthe digestive fluids seem harmless, however mi have witnessed in mi own worship of Orgon how quickly these fungi digest their prey in large enough groups; agh mi gruk it safe to assume that a single mushroom could eventually cause significant damage\n\ngiven enough time. Mi tested the effects of Orgon's gall on a shara named Hagan, who exhibited an extremely dry mouth, blurred vision and hallucinations. As with Orgon's bile, mi would strongly recommend against eating dub or more of these mushrooms, as\n\noverconsumption could have dangerous effects, including flattening. Mi would also theorise that such could possibly lead to lasting impacts on mental health. \n Further discoveries concerning Orgon's bile or Orgon's gall will be recorded agh published i\n\nfuture books if needed.\n -Malog'Yar, witch doctor agh loyal servant of Orgon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Contemplations 1", "Catarrh", "The Contemplations of Malog, Goj in San’Thraka agh Wargoth of the Yars:\n\nHear what mi blah, young one, for mi blah lat h’dub honors by which the orc lives, agh h’dub pillars on which he stands.\n\nSTRENGTH\nVALOR\nBOLDNESS\nCONTENTMENT\n\nWISDOM\nFORTHRIGHTNESS\nDISCIPLINE\n\nStrength is the simplest honor. It is by nub means easy to attain, but very easy to lose. It comes with the weight of earth, yet drifts away on the currents of the river from the unwary. Yet, for he who keeps\n\nstands firm as iron. By it, the body stands strong. Without it, the bones fall as dry reeds. By the strong outer self, the strong inner self is protected.\n\nValor is that which compels us to stand. By it, we face our enemies agh conquer our fears. Tur\n\nfrom the challenges of life. Cower nub before latz foes. Stand agh face those who oppose lat.\n\nBoldness is that energy by which we charge into the flames. Be unafraid of risk. It is the gate to many rewards. As valor makes us stand our ground,\n\nboldness commands us to press forward.\n\nContentment is the key to satisfaction. Trust nub in wealth, for gold flees as the sands on the night winds. Trust nub in land, for many lands agh whole continents have been lost before this ash. Be content wit\n\nlatz lusk agh latz bread. If you have a blarg, a mate, agh cubs, lat be truly blessed beyond measure.\n\nWisdom is born of a strong mind. It is more practical than philosophy, agh goes beyond mere knowledge. It is the ability for right living, common s\n\nwit, resolution of life’s problems, agh success beyond material gain. Gruk for latself, but heed the blahings of those more experienced with the respect agh consideration due them. Learn from life, agh apply latz learning in a way that means something.\n§\n\nForthrightness is honesty agh directness. It is intentional clarity of blahing, agh the absence of deception. Blah truth. Blah to blah, nub to flatter. Do as lat blah, agh let latz blah be latz bond. If lat blah it, mean it. Live it\n\nDiscipline is th\n\nwhich keeps latz life in order. Without it, all other honors forsake lat, for honor demands that the honorable governs his life with the will of iron. Hard work agh control of the self hold body agh mind together.\n\nStand firm in all these things, agh\n\nwill stand indeed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Borguk the Lazy", "§bZar'roc'Yar", "Azh upon a tik, there was an Uruk named Borguk. Borguk was a bub'hozh, yet lazy Uruk. He always wanted to have the easy way out.\n\nAzh day, Borguk was hungry, bub'hungry. He decided to go on a quick and easy hunt off into the Savannah\n\nSo there he sat, waiting, and waiting. Until he finally peeped a Jabbernak walking across the golden grasses of the Savannah. He peeped over the bushes and loaded a ligz into his O'lig.\n\nRight as he got a hosh shot, and was about\n\nto shoot, another Jabbernak came into view. Once the Jabbernaks met peeper to peeper, they began to stand off, then even klomp.\n\nBorguk decided to wait out the klomp, and wait for ash to flat, and then take that ash home to eat.\n\nIt didn't take long for ash of the bub'hosh Jabbernak to flat. Eager, Borguk hopped out of the bushes, going to tie up the flat Jabbernak, and haul it home. The living Jabbernak stomped on Borguk till he was flat, aswell.\n\nNub be lazy, learn from Borguk. \"Strength & Patience\" - Yar code", ""),
        StaticBook("Contemplations 2", "Catarrh", "The second book of the Contemplations of Malog, Goj in San’Thraka, agh Wargoth of the Yars:\n\nHeed mi warning, all who are wise, for mi blah lat h’dub dishonors by which an orc is ruined, agh h’dub shames which may befall him.\n\nWEAKNESS\nIRRE\n\nCOWARDICE\nAVARICE\nTHOUGHTLESSNESS\nDUPLICITY\nCOMPLACENCY\n\nWeakness, blah’d plainly, is the absence of strength. Be nub frail, agh neglect nub the body. He who can-nub defend himself, how can he defend that for which he stands? To give\n\nto keep latz bub’hoshest treasure in a fortress of straw.\n\nIrresolution is the way of he who falters in the presence of adversity. Do nub quail when the storm thunders. Do nub turn away when latz enemies roar. Be nub like the rabbit, who, when he is\n\nfrightened but a little, flees to his hole for safety. The rabbit is prey, agh the orc must never be prey.\n\nCowardice halts the feet, agh binds the spirit. Nub hosh thing comes to the coward, for the coward takes nub risk. The coward never takes the\n\ndifficult path. There is no success for such an ash. All his ways are worthless, agh his life profitless.\n\nAvarice is the heart of the empty spirit. Lust for gold blinds the eyes to truth, agh numbs the mind to wisdom. It makes the senses dull, such\n\nhe whose life is governed by the mina can-nub perceive honor, agh hears nub the call of Krug.\n\nThoughtlessness is to the mind as weakness is to the body. The ash who gruks nub is nub’hosher than the blind or the deaf, for he chooses himself nub to gr\n\nthe way to live rightly. He is blind to the way in which he should walk, agh the advice of the wise enters nub his ear. All his workings are senseless, agh his feet lead him to shame.\n\nDuplicity is the forked tongue of the dishonorable. The duplicito\n\nash blahs “yub” with his mouth, but “nub” in his spirit. His blah can-nub be trusted, for he is a serpent agh a companion to serpents. With his face he grins agh flatters, but behind his back he bears a double-edged dagger to betray lat. Do nub be like\n\nsuch an ash, for the number of those who will hear him dwindles by the hour.\n\nComplacency is the quicksand upon which the glob builds a blarg. It is a hosh-smelling poison, agh a smooth road which leads to ruin. Complacency lulls lat to sleep with a\n\ntouch agh sweet songs, but, when lat have awoken, it has stolen latz strength, latz mate, agh all latz bread.\n\nThe ash who falls into any of these falls surely agh quickly to his destruction.", ""),
        StaticBook("A duel of Rexs", "§bShaman Zlash'Lur", "The Tale of Farseer  Phaedrus'Yar's Flat\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nscribed and translated to common by Zlash'Lur\n\nThe 2 Rexes came face to face after Kharak called out to Phaedrus in anger seeing that he had cleansed some of Orgon's blight.\n\n\"There is no difference between these two lands, both are unnatural...\" Kharak growled.\n\n\"These are what the lands look like, when noone has meddled with them. They are, by definition, natural.\" Phaedrus replies.\n\nBoth wished for the same thing. To see the Uruks flourish, however they both had very, very different ways of going about it, and\n\nthe scars from past times were still prominent, in memory. They spoke a great deal of time. Despite the Rex's disdain for the Elf, he never refused to listen to him. At times even laughing at the little farseer's dry humor.\n\nIn the end, it was all for\n\nnaught. Phaedrus had tried desperately to sway Kharak from continuing down the path which lead him to corrupting the lands, however the Rex was stout in his choices, determined to see them through and ensure the safety of his people.\n\n\"I will deal with my people...\" The Rex finally said, before turning to depart.\n\n\"Then where does that leave things, will you continue with this taint?\" Phaedrus asked quickly, tilting his chin upward in apprehension as he squinted toward the back of\n\nthe Rex.\n\n\"You will have to see.\" Kharak replied once more, with a sigh following shortly after.\n\n\"I need your answer now, Kharak.\"\n\n\"You will never understand. Not now.\"\n\n\"Draw your weapon, then.\"\n\nThe Rex turned around slowly, bringing his blade from his sheath as he faces the Elf. Phaedrus drawing his falchion from his waist in turn as he set his staff aside.\n\n\"You wish to fight me?\"\n\nThe Rex asked in challenge, stomping ever closer.\n\n\"I am sorry it has come to this.\" Phaedrus replied shortly after, flicking his sword into position.\n\n\"Come then, Elf.\"\n\nWith that, they clashed, kicking up clouds of\n\ndead grass and sloshing through the mud of the tainted lands while exchanging blow after blow. The Elf found his movements matched and his swings bested, he had grown softer since his time away from the harsh sands, it showed. It would be the death of him\n\nWith a final roar the Rex impaled his sword into Phaedrus' gut, the searing, incredibly painful pressure of the blade within his body causing him to gasp out in pain.\n\nPhaedrus impaled upon the blade of Kharak, drops his own as he grunts out a gasp of\n\npain.\n\n\"I told you to leave us alone, brother.\" Kharak says\n\nPhaedrus snaps his hand down to Kharak's arm, holding it for support as he struggles with his words. \"This does not change things, Kharak... Don't do\n\nthis\"\n\n\"I have too.\" Kharak simpled said, wedging the blade further into him as he glanced away.\n\nPhaedrus gasps out in pain once more before slinking to his knees, falling off the blade in a heap down on the ground.\n\nKharak shook in his bloodrage, withdrawing the blade from his body and rising to his feet.\n\nPhaedrus blinked rapidly a few times before simply resting his head against the ground, holding one hand over his wound as he closes his eyes, breathing growing\n\nshallower.\n\nKharak sheathed his sword in a languid and shaking movement, turning his focus back to Phaedrus.\n\n\"You will be with the Spirits now, Phaedrus.\"\n\nThe Rex stared down at the corpse of the Elf, the farseer, his\n\nbrother, and carried him to his final resting place in the sands of the Uzg.\n\nPhaedrus was with the Spirits now.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Case Study", "§bFalyen Darylus", "The Radiant Man - Powers and Subjugation of the Mind\nThe Radiant Man, a suspected incarnate aengul, has aligned himself with parts of the Spellcrafters of Rivel with the goal of uncovering the Forgotten Dwarven artifact known as\n\n“The Seal”. To those who follow him, the Radiant Man grants incredible powers. They are akin to holy magics, but are incapable of healing yet also functional against those who could not in any way be described as dark creatures. It seems to be Holy\n\nMagic without the requirement of being holy: an excellent addition to any Spellcrafter’s arsenal, especially when so freely given and easily mastered. Or so it would seem.\nIt appears to draw upon the Radiant Man’s power is to open one’s being\n\nto him: the more power one draws and the more frequently one draws it the more the Radiant Man is capable of influencing, or even controlling, one’s thoughts. We have carried out extensive experimentation on the two members\n\nof the Radiant Man’s following of Spellcrafters when they returned to Rivel to analyse the tomes from the Archive. Their behaviour was normal, yet they wholeheartedly refuse to accept the possibility that their minds are not fully\n\ntheirs, and mental magical probing is being blocked by a power beyond our own.\nPart of the danger of this is the slippery slope: once one opens one’s mind to the Radiant Man the Radiant Man can influence one to draw a little more, giving\n\nthe Radiant Man a little more control and thus the influence required to push one to draw slightly more power. This could rapidly lead to a complete inability to refuse the commands of the Radiant Man, and hypothetically could turn into what I\n\nrefer to as a “Subjugant”, an individual wielding untold power via the Radiant Man yet completely slaved to his will to the point of lacking independent thought: simply an extension of the Radiant Man’s desires. Such a being could prove\n\nincredibly dangerous, and I recommend total disconnection from the Radiant Man of all of his Spellcrafter followers as soon as they return from their venture to the Hall.\n- Senior Researcher Falyen Darylus", ""),
        StaticBook("Fate of Hanseti", "§bColtaine Wick", "The\nFate\nOf\nHanseti\n\n\n\nWritten by an eye\nwitness.\n\n\"I was on gate duty as usual when the first distrought citizen came to Petrus. They were screaming some lunacy about flying men and fire. after we had him calmed down, he told us the town of Hanseti was under attack by Undead.\n\nOur commander Prince Pual Carrion order me and the other men to suit up and get ready to march. Shortly there after we men of the Crow Regiment marched out of Petrus to meet the enemy at\nHanseti.\n\nNight fell as we neared the small town, even from a distance you could see the glow of flames and the distant screams. As we marched into the town proper , everything quite frankly went to shit. Shambling dead lurched out of alleyways to assault\n\nout regimental formations, men scattered in panic, which is when the real madness hit, there was a man, or something, flying through the air. some foul Iblees spawn hurling balls of flame, I saw too many of my brothers in arms\n\nbe seared to ash still in there armor, at the time I was still young and inexperianced with such things so I fled to a manor within the town that was miraculously unburned, I was not the only one there unfortunatly. Some men from the regiment made it\n\nthere along with other people from the druids grove I believe, as we peered out the windows to witness the flaming slaughter, the flying Iblees mage, flew to the manor we were in and started summoning hordes of undead to devour us.\n\nNot wanting to die, I only stayed to fight for long enough to manage an escape back outside. where I then ran full tilt into the surrounding woods to escape the remains of Hanseti. It would take several years after the fall of Hanseti\n\nfor Iblees to finally be cast down and those who lost there life to be put to rest.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("S. Council Edict", "§bJacob Chapel", "The Edict of the Small Council, 13th of Malin's Welcome, 1472.\n\nScribed down by Jacob Chapel, High Scrivener of Oren.\n\nAt the will of his Imperial Majesty Emperor Tuvya Carrion, the Petty Council is hereby declared as a minor council under the privy to help give word to the Emperor for many Lords, positions will be granted based on the Lord and the will of the Emperor.\n\nSection I\nPositions of the Council\nThe following titles are granted the right to be considered part of the council and granted the right of seat at meetings when called and will be expected to fulfill their tasked duties to assist the realm\n\n¬ Petrus Maer\n¬ High Scrivener\n¬ Guard Commander\n¬ Master of Laws\n¬ Master of the Hunt\n¬ Master of the Harvest\n¬ Master of the Ships\n¬ Champion of the Realm\n¬ Imperial Scribe\n\nEdict of the Minor Council\nAt the will of his Imperial Majesty Emperor Tuvya Carrion, these titles are hereby honored with the duties of the Minor Council and the duties that are assigned with such title.\n\nSection I\nRights and Duty of the Petrus Maer\n\nThe position of Petrus Maer is granted to an individual who is entrusted by the Emperor to maintain his Capital city. His duties and rights are as follows.\n\n¬ The duty to manage and oversee daily operations of the Capital City.\n¬ The duty to manage and oversee construction and instatement of buildings and guildhalls for other guilds and citizens of the capital.\n\n¬ The duty to manage the city's financial treasury and collect taxes from the citizens and guilds of the Capital.\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council meetings.\n\nSection II\nRights and Duty of the High Scrivener\n\nThe position of High Scrivener is granted to an individual who is entrusted by the Emperor to maintain the public knowledge and library of  his Empire. His duties and rights are as follows.\n\n¬ The duty to maintain any knowledge, document, and book in the Library of Petrus.\n¬ The duty to Oversee and maintain the Royal and Public Library of Petrus.\n¬ The duty to manage affairs of the Museum of Oren.\n\n¬ The duty to transcribe official documents for public viewing.\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council meetings.\n\nSection III\nRights and Duty of the Guard Commander\n\nThe position of Guard Commander is granted to an individual who is entrusted by the Emperor to maintain the law with in his Capital city, Petrus. His duties and rights are as follows.\n\n¬ The duty to maintain the Emperors peace within the capital of Petrus.\n¬ The duty to maintain the Emperors Guard Force of Petrus.\n¬ The right to arrest individual common men suspected for a crime.\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council\n\nSection IV\nRights and Duties of the Master of the Hunt\n\nA largely honorary title, the Master of the Hunt is foremost of huntsman amongst his peers. The title is granted to an individual who is entrusted by the Emperor to maintain his hunts.\n\nHis duties and rights are as follows.\n¬ The duty to lead the royal hunts for the Emperor.\n¬ The duty to warden his Imperial Majesty’s forests.\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council meetings.\n\nSection V\nRights and Duties of the Master of the Harvest\n\nA largely honorary title, the Master of the Harvest is foremost of farmers amongst his peers. The title is granted to an individual who is entrusted by the Emperor to maintain his farm\n\nfood stocks. His duties and rights are as follows.\n¬ The duty to supply the granaries of His Imperial Majesty, keeping such well stocked.\n¬ The duty to ensure the people of Petrus are well-fed.\n\n¬ The right to hold harvest festival and fests for the common folk\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council meetings.\n\nSection VI\nRights and Duties of the Master of Ships\n\nAn honorary title, the Master of Ships is typically reserved for a well-respected councillor and friend of his Imperial Majesty. His rights and duties are as follows.\n\n¬ If ever Oren has a navy, is responsible for the management and oversight of such navy.\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council meetings.\n\nSection VII\nRights and Duties of the Champion of the Realm.\n\nA largely honorary title, the Champion of the Realm is considered the finest warrior within the realm, Knightly or commoner.\n\nThis title is granted by merit of the Tournament of Sun’s Smiles. His rights and duties are as follows.\n¬ The duty, in times of war, to be assigned to lead a small group of elite warriors.\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council meetings.\n\nSection VIII\nRights and Duties of the Imperial Scribe\n\nThe position of Imperial Scribe is granted to an individual who is intrusted by the Emperor to draft Edicts, Letters, or Documents at the request of the Emperor, private or public.\n\nHis rights and duties are as follows.\n¬ The duty to draft any edict, document, or letter for the Emperor at his will.\n¬ The duty to hold the secrets of such edicts, documents, or letters.\n¬ The right to have seat at the Minor Council Meetings.\n\nSection IX\nRights and Duties of the Master of Laws\n\nA largely honorary title, the Master of Laws is foremost of peace-keepers amongst his peers. Has the powers to enforce laws of the Realm in any province and to appoint a Bailiff under his ho\n\n¬ The duty and power to uphold the Emperor’s peace and enforce His Imperial Majesty’s laws in any and all provinces.\n¬ The power to appoint his own provincial Bailiff over the Lord Bailiff.", ""),
        StaticBook("Oren History: I", "§bJacob Chapel", "History of Oren\n       Part I\n\n\nThis history has been collected by me, Jacob Chapel. Sources are various scrolls and texts and the museum of Petrus, beside common knowledge and tales. Enjoy.\n\n((Written by Pepernoot))\n\nIf you're interested in the history before Al'Khazar, I suggest you pick up the first part of the Holy Scrolls, the Nativities. If you're interested in the history past Siegmund Carrion's election, then you need to find part two of The History of Oren.\n\nThe days of Aegis\nThe history of Oren begins in Aegis, the land of the Descendants. To the west of the Cloud Temple laid its lands. The capital of Al’Khazar was surrounded by pastures, farmlands and forests, and to the north laid the snowy lands,\n\ncontaining cities and towns such as Alstion and Snowy Fields. In the south were the islands known as the Whisper Isles, surrounded by the calm waters of the Whisper Lake, and filled with fishermen and craftsmen such as glassblowers.\n\nThe first king was Horen himself. Many Kings ruled the Kingdom wisely after him, Kings such as Saint Daniel. The Kingdom’s grand city was built by this King Daniel in 1300. Eventually King Pampo Perea, Saint Daniel’s seneschal, took power, with Edmund\n\nSheffield as his seneschal.\nAs time passed the Undead became stronger and bolder in their attacks on the Kingdom. Snowy Fields fell and was razed, but soldiers from Alstion retook it and the town was rebuilt. This turned out to be futile eventually as\n\nthe northern towns fell one by one. Even King Perea himself was killed by the Undead, within the tall walls of Al’Khazar. Edmund Sheffield took his place, but was corrupted by the dark forces and turned to the Nether. His “abduction” was accompanied by a\n\ngreat siege of Al’Khazar, in which a portal to the Nether opened in the city square. After a great battle the City of Man was sacked. Human refugees poured across the Kingdom and the city of Galahar, built on the ruins of the old town of Kramoroe, was\n\nnamed capital.\n\nEdmund’s son Enor Sheffield took his place, but under his rule the situation worsened drastically, the corruption of his father and his own weakness led to great dissent in the Kingdom.\n\nMeanwhile Gaius Marius, Hochmeister of the Teutons had carved out a realm for himself to the east of the Kingdom, and had even participated in wars against Oren, allying with its enemies. It is important to note that even though the Undead threatened\n\nOren, and although Oren was the strong defence between the Undead and the rest of the races, this didn’t deter them to wage wars against the Kingdom. Infighting between the nations of Malinor, Krug, Urguan and Oren was common.\nRebellion brew in the\n\nKingdom, and in Galahar the Phoenix Rebellion formed. As the weak King Enor saw his position wasn’t tenable anymore he named Gaius Marius as King of Oren. This treason lead to the rise of the rebellion and a war between the part of Oren controlled by\n\nthe Teutons and the Phoenix Rebellion, led by Eze’kiel Tarus as the Phoenix King. Eventually the two sides reach an agreement, splitting the realm into two parts. The Kingdom of Renatus, ruled by King Tarus, and the Realm of Hanseti, ruled by Gaius.\n\nAfter giving up his crown the mad King Enor and his followers settled on an island, and together with Queen Dawn Perea, wife of the old King Perea he created the nation of Salvus.\nHumanity could not rest though, as the Undead continued their march\n\nrelentlessly. In 1349 Galahar was attacked by the forces of evil, but even though the attack was repelled, the city was evacuated for fears of Miasma. Eventually Aegis fell in 1351, and the humans fled through the portal to the verge,\n\nalong with the other Descendants. \n\nA new dawn in Asulon\nAfter a brief stay in The Verge, the Descendants settled in the new lands of Asulon. Oren was still divided into the three Kingdoms, and Renatus settled around their new capital of Aret\n\nIn these turbulent times a new human nation sprung up, the Kingdom of Seventis.\n\nWhen King Eze’kiel resigned from the throne, Renatus was ruled by the Regent King Reynard Lycian until Godfrey Horen appeared. Godfrey claimed direct decent from King Ho\n\nand quickly received support from the Dukes and other nobles of the realm. He consolidated power and strengthened the Kingdom, which was plagued by instability and attacks from the other nations.\n\nSoon after Godfrey started his reign a coalition agai\n\nSalvus formed by The Kingdom of Seventis, Alras, the Orcs and most importantly what was called the Twilight Army. This coalition did not have official support from Renatus, but most of its nobles supported it. Opposing the coalition were Salvus itself,\n\nthe Dwarves of Urguan and the Realm of Hanseti. After the humiliating defeat, and the betrayal of Queen Dawn’s guards, which murdered her, Salvus was absorbed into Renatus.\n\nAs the great plague hit Asulon, the Kingdom of Seventis was hit most severel\n\npresumably due to its location close to the Cloud Temple. Most of its inhabitants died, allowing for an absorption into the Kingdom of Renatus to protect the weakened towns.\n\nThe Teutons could not stand by idly as Renatus grew, and went to war agains\n\nthe Kingdom. Swiftly the war turned against their favour, and it became clear that they were losing the war. To avoid destruction of his nation, Hochmeister Mirtok surrendered it to King Godfrey, saying the words “I will die for this nation, but I will\n\nnot let it die for me”.\n\nThe annexation of Hanseti meant the unification of humanity, and the Holy Oren Empire was formed. In the Empire the Crownlands, Salvus and Hanseti were ruled as separate kingdoms, with the Emperor presiding over the individua\n\nkings, while also being king of the crownlands.\n\nAfter a rebellion against the crown, House Tarus, House Elendil and House Norsem were shunned and fell out of favour in the Empire. Soon though, the lands of Asulon were submerged by floods,\n\nand a second flight was needed.\n\nAnthos, a land plagued by war\nJust as the flight from Aegis, the new land was not reached in one trip. There were stops at the isles of Elysium and Kalos. One notable thing in Kalos was the formation of the\n\nPhoenix Kingdom, by Eze’kiel Tarus. The kingdom was quickly destroyed, even before leaving for Anthos.\n\nIn Asulon the Teutonic Order was nigh destroyed by the Flays, and the Hochmeister killed. A few remnants of the Order made it to Anthos, albeit\n\nwithout a Hochmeister to guide them. The Teutons settled on the southern side of the ice wall of the North. Meanwhile the Empire of Oren settled a bit further south, with Abresi as their capital.\n\nSoon after arriving it turned out this land was not a\n\nsafe as the Descendants had hoped. North of the wall the Teutons discovered a savage race of boarmen and a land filled with dragons.\n\nThis was not the most pressing issue to Oren though, as the Empress of Oren was kidnapped by the Orcs, and a joint\n\nHuman and Dwarf force invaded their capital and massacred nearly every orc present.\n\nEver present Elven aggression led to a crusade against the Princedom of Malinor. The Order of the White Rose quickly destroyed their forces and burned the Malenorian\n\nfarms. The elves eventually surrendered to the siege, proving the enormous strength of a united Oren.\n\nUnited it would not be for long, as the Teutons rebelled. In the first battle, at Kralta, the Teutons were crushed. At the second battle the\n\nBlackmonts stood alone against the Teutons on the Iron Fields, outnumbered two to one. The Teutonic Order was victorious.\n\nThe civil war was decided at the Siege of the Dreadfort, where the Chivays, and the Carrions (then bannermen of the Blackmonts)\n\ndistinguished themselves. The defeat at the Battle of Iron fields had led to close cooperation between the White Roses and the Blackmonts, which turned out to be more than the Teutons could handle. Although the Dreadfort was severely damaged the siege\n\nwas broken and the Teutonic Order defeated. Soon afterwards the Teutonic Order was disbanded by Emperor Godfrey.\n\nThe Scourge, the name of the goatmen and the dragons from the north made their first move south beyond the wall, destroying the old\n\nTeutonic castle of Greywyn with flames, and taking it for their own.\n\nThen, in a huge shock to the empire, Emperor Godfrey died. He was succeeded by his son, Horen.\n\nAs the princedom of Malinor was absorbed into the Empire as\n\nprotectorate, the expansion of Oren led to great concern with the other races. They formed a coalition and in the War of Anthos they attacked Oren, putting a halt to the expansion. Most prominent in the coalition were the Dwarves, angered by the\n\nexecution of one of their Dwarven lords by nobles of Oren. In the Battle of the Crossroads the coalition was defeated though, by a brilliant Orenian flanking manoeuvre.\n\nIn 1415 the Empire was left in disarray as Emperor Horen left, along with his\n\nmost loyal houses. The dwarves used this weakness to form their Grand Kingdom of Urguan in the War of Asulon. They dissolved the Empire of Oren and many parts, including Salvus and Adunia swear loyalty to the dwarves as vassal states. What remains of the\n\nEmpire was renamed to the Holy Kingdom of Oren and ruled by William Horen. After more chaos and disarray many more little human states sprung up or seceded from the Kingdom, leading to the current prominent Houses, states and cultures. \n \nEventuall\n\nGrand King of Urguan, Thorin Grandaxe dies. This caused the human vassal states to be released from their oaths to the dwarves. This made way for a renewed unification. As King William was pushing his powers and support from his nobles to the limit,\n\nHouse Winter made a secret pact with Ruska. This forced King William to step down, giving control of Oren to his cousin Silus. This was only temporary, as the states of Salvus, Oren, Ruska and the new state of Herendul were confederated into an empire,\n\nwith an elective monarchy. At the election Siegmund Carrion was voted in as Emperor of Oren.\n\nThis concludes part one of Oren's history. The events after Siegmund Carrion's election, up to the first years in Athera will be discussed in part two.\n\n((So you made it to the end. I hope you liked it. You can leave a message to me on the forums, username: Pepernoot))", ""),
        StaticBook("Akovian Regiment", "§bRichard 'the Red Lion' Reyne", "-=-The Royal Akovian Regiment of the Orenai Legion-=-\n\nIntroduction:\n\nThe Kingdom of Akovia during the great Schismatic War had no means of a true military, it depended on it's battle hardened militia corps to defeat\n\nnumerous enemies. It was brought to the attention of King Andrik Vydra of Akovia that the capability of the Nation's military could be exponentially increased. During this time, King Andrik had already formed the Orenai Legion between his allied Nations.\n\nThe Orenai Legion consist of multiple Regiments which came from multiple allied countries. The March of Adria had formed the First Regiment, the Kingdom of Akovia had formed the Second, and the Duchy of Savoie formed the Third, but kept it's\n\noriginal name, the St. Amyas Order. \n\nAt the time, there was no structure still in the Kingdom of Akovia. Chancellor Vasili Vanir, alongside Lord Steward Arik Vanir, and War Veteran Richard Reyne formed the basics of the Regiment.\n\nRanks were brainstormed to optimize it's ability. The system of Payment had to be done, and uniforms had to be tailored. The Regiment had the aid of the Kingdom itself, so supplies were extremely easy to achieve, so the Soldiers of the\n\nRegiment always were ready for battle. \n\nLike stated before, the Regiment still had not kickstarted, it took several years for the complete formation to be finalized.\n\nThe Reformed Kingdom of Oren:\n\nHuzzah, the Gryphon of House Vydra trumphs over the Dragon of House Horen. These chants could be heard through the human heartland. The Konigreich of Aesterwald had capitulated and only the Duchy of Petrus continued on the fight\n\nShortly after the fall of Aesterwald, a meeting was held between the remaining Nations of the Schism War. It was there that King Andrik Vydra struck the historical agreement. Archon Godfrey had to surrender all of his titles and possessions to the Kingdom\n\nof Akovia. The minute the meeting was over, the newly formed Regiment had begun to occupy the Capital city of Petrus, bringing it's unlawfulness to an end. The Regiment with the guiding hand of the King, established peace and order inside the City. Under\n\nthe assistance of Lieutenant Reyne, the Regiment now had a Head Quarters. A large portion of the Royal Palace was claimed for the usage of the Regiment. Every locked rooms were broken into and looted to further benefit the Regiment.\n\nWith the Capture of Petrus, the Regiment's rank grew into the thousands, it had become the main force the King depended on. The uniforms of the Regiment could be see on numerous people around Petrus. It was a wonderful sight, the city was rejuvenated,\n\nlife was pumped back into the once desolated city and people had begun settling into the Houses the Steward council had to offer.\n\nNot everything was easy for the Regiment though, it's leader, Vasili Vanir had and still is, in a sickbed\n\nthe leadership was temporarly passed on the Lt. Reyne, but it lead to a power struggle between the aide of Vasili, Arik, and the Lieutenant.\n\nWhat does the Regiment do?: The Regiment serves as the Army of the Kingdom, it does not act as a Guard Force\n\nFor Petrus. Members of the Regiment alongside their Officers desecretly raid their enemies, attempting to disrupt enemy movements while they can. They also patrol the roads of Oren, hopeful to end the lives of bandits to hunt on the weak. And when time\n\nCalls, they may also act as personal Guards to the Royal Family.\n\nThe Education system: Unknown to the citizens of Oren, the Army does infact hold informal classes. These lessons provide education to the basic soldier\n\nIt is a system established by Lieutenant Reyne, alongside his personal aides, Publius Bracchus and Jace Evans. The system teaches how armymen become the perfect model soldier of Oren. Honorifics, history, and much more are being taught to the soldiers\n\nTo ensure the capabilities of the Regiment. Rankers that hope to become Officers also have to go through a different Rigerious training which is undisclosed to the Public. This weeds out the soldiers able to lead with confidence.\n\nThe Officers:\n\nCommander-in-Chief\n(The Monarch of Oren has the capability to call on the troops without question): \n\nKing Andrik Vydra\n\nCaptain\n(A rank recognized by the State itself. None but the Commander may give orders to this rank, it is a prestigious rank and takes enourmous effort to achieve):\n\nDuke Vasili Vanir\n(Absent, Sick)\n\nLieutenants\n(This rank are officers in charge of Companies within the Regiment, it is a title gave only to the best available. It is approved by the King and is expected to do much for the Kingdom.\n\nSer Richard Reyne\n\nSergeants\n(This rank would be in charge of the management of their Squadron, they ensure the capability of their group and report to their Lieutenant for orders):\n\nBjorn Vanir\n\nRanks:\n\nMen At Arms\n\nDraftees\n\nSpecialty Ranks:\n\nChaplain\n\nBarber\n\nAide-De-Camp\n\nCurrent Military involment:\n\nDefense of Karovia:\nSuccess\n\nDefense of Petrus:\nSuccess\n\nRaid on Angren:\nFailure, retreat.\n\nRaid on Orcish Lands: Success\n\nDefense of Petrus II:\nFailure\n\nRaid on Laureh'lin:\nSuccess\n\n-By the pen of Richard Reyne.", ""),
        StaticBook("Seasons Vol. I", "SapphireShard", "The Sorrow I had to endure, all because of your departure from our home without a single word. I pondered why you left me all alone in the keep, was it because of our two twin boys who died silently in their sleep? Or had I done something the drive you\n\naway and I was never shown? I only noticed you starting to act different and more distant as I saw you make our beloved town more beautiful with the work you had done for it. If only you saw the life in it before the people left for reasons I do not\n\neven know still. The nights when I went to sleep and never saw nor heard you join in our chambers. I thought you simply went to bed later and woke up early, and I hoped you did not let the pain and sorrows of the recent events keep you up all night. But\n\nI never got to know that due to the day I wanted to confront you on those issues I was requested to to go to Godfrey’s court at once. I told you my goodbyes promising to be back in a few days or a week. I simply rode to Arethor and did the duties, quest\n\nand tasks I was assigned bringing honor to my Houses name, our name and protecting the Empire, Emperor and us. But when I returned to Riven I saw the many and wonderful changes you had done. And as I seeked you to see where you where\n\nI could not find you. I searched the keep, the town, the new buildings, the what seemed to be endless forest of Midionia for days searching. And my men in the other nations saw no signs when I would ask them if I saw them. It was clear to me you had\n\nleft the empire, our town, and me.\nI waited in the town and Keep hoping you just went on another trip to find a way to contact your sister as you did many years ago but once again, I was wrong. The next few days I spent isolated in the keep praying to\n\nthe Creator and the Patrons such as Aerial, and have cursed out names I have blamed. and having a fit of grief over what I had lost, my two sons and heirs, and my beloved wife. The pain was to consume me I felt as if I was to go mad with grief until a\n\nSquire of a knight of mine came with a message showing that the Emperor once again needed me at his court for more tasks, quest and such to do. I gave the lad a nod putting my Silver plate on and mounting my War Horse riding to Arethor. As I rode I\n\nsighed and gazed up to the skies above pondering one several subject attempting to put the pain and grief behind me. I gave myself a short nod and kicked my heels into my horses sides to make the horse to run faster to Arethor knowing I have one\n\nmore Oath I can keep true and a few more I can protect. For many weeks and possible a month or two I stayed in Arethor constantly doing work, the relation with our people and crime had go down so much with the crackdown I and others had done\n\non the many corrupted and vile criminals of oren had to face. Only to have a my Uncle the High Pontiff of the Oren clergy pestering me about me getting wed to some nations co-leader or important figure to boost diplomacy and other things he\n\nrambled on. He brought up several names, elven princess’ one I knew and had a similar recent events happen, a few minor nobles. I simply shrugged every name off speaking to my Uncle in a cold tone. “Uncle think, who in the light’s name\n\nwould want to be courted little alone wed, a seven foot half blood, who is easily angered, and who is body is partly war torn?” My uncle Boeindl shrugged “You got one lass before you could do it again!” I simply shrugged at him as I have already told\n\nhim the answer and walked off pondering to myself.“Who would else? I only knew of one, one who could look past my scars, flaws, and lies to see a gentler me, and know my true name masked in shame and pain.”\nI continued my work still but now I had\n\nmy uncle the High Pontiff pressuring me into marrying someone for a political reason. As annoying as it was I remained to the vows I had taken and continued on with my duties. But a day I did give my Uncle a break and told him at his latest scheme of\n\nmarriages and next thing I knew a day after I gave him a break and a possible chance with his schemes to help aid his House, Empire and a Broken man. He had sent a Suit to fix me exactly and a copy of an invitation to the Hightower Peace Gala. I waited\n\ntill the date and prepared my save, put my hair into its usual military style, groomed my light beard so it was not a mess, and such. Putting on the suit grumbling to myself on how I hated it because to me all of these noble clothing feel\n\njust....odd...to wear. And went to my War horse with its armor taken off mounted the steed and rode to Solace to go to King James Gala and feast and enjoy the festivities with the other Nobles of Oren and the Leaders of nations. As I entered many looked\n\nat me as if I was a stranger many going “IS that Uthor without his Armor?!” I just ignored them and the ones making jest on the subject and enjoyed the ball talking to family, friends, and allies. As I was stopped as I faced the Emperor a smile on his\n\nface saying “Grand Knight, is that the?!” I nodded and reassured him it was and he began laughing a bit “Today be a good day then, I see ye and the Hochmeister in good noble clothing! none of your steel and chain, quiet odd tis is to see ye in such”\n\nI chuckled about “Aye tis odd, but I am doing it so my uncle doesn't have a fit” The Emperor simply laughed and wished me well as he himself went to enjoy the gala and spend the knight with his duchess.\nAt the end of the party I sighed\n\nheavily knowing I should not have come, King James threw an excellent party, but my Uncle left me to do what I wanted and I mainly just talked to friends there were none who seemed to wanted to dance with me. But I simply shrugged the feeling off as I\n\nenjoyed the meal and the excellent show of cannon fire in the nights sky. But as the night came to an end I found that many have left only a few mainly the Imperial family, and the Hightowers and a few diplomatic leaders were left talking, eating,\n\ndrinking and flirting. Shaking my head I walked off to the stables outside Solace and tipped the stable bow with a mina as I mounted my steed and rode home having regrets going to the gala yet I was at the same time happy. The feelings confused me but I\n\nrode on continuously pondering the two trying to find out which of the two were dominate? And which was minor? As I reached my town of Riven I found out that the town and its people were asleep the only sign of life was the tavern and some late night\n\nmerry goers. I chuckled as I remember my younger days as a fledgling knight who drank his days away chasing skirts and full of pride and honor. I reached the stables and got my horse stabled walking the final steps to my keep. I walked into\n\ntown square and halted as I gazed at the open square’s hearth a place for travelers to rest and a place for the Riven townsfolk to warm up as they did their work on cold days. I stood and gazed into the fire warming my hands up a bit. My ears jumped up\n\nas I heard a soft, gentle voice saying “Hello Roy...”\nI immediately took a defensive stance raising my leg high grabbing onto of my blades hidden in my boots side. As I was about to question them on how they knew my name which only my brother knew and\n\nmy thought to be dead lover had I dropped my blade as I gazed on the one who smiled at me gently. As the Silver blade sank into the ground I stared at her studying her light extremely pale skin, he eyes which were as shined as if they were two light\n\ntinted sapphires, and her dark red hair which always seemed to flow just the right way as I dumbfoundedly spoke a name to my surprise. “Eml...Emlisya...?” Then I knew it was you, when you nodded to me replying “My...my...Roy at first I thought\n\nit wasn't you in that suit, I have to say you look rather dashing..” Still dumbfounded I slowly shook my head feeling pain, yet comfort as you spoke. You did not say you were sorry nor regretful on why and how long you left but the emotional sounds\n\ndeeds.” You closed your eyes for a few moments giggling as I walked closed brushing a hand on the side of your cheeck saying in one of the sofest voices I had ever spoken with “I thank the Creator and the Arch Angel Aerial for you not be another\n\ndeeds.” You closed your eyes for a few moments giggling as I walked closed brushing a hand on the side of your cheeck saying in one of the sofest voices I had ever spoken with “I thank the Creator and the Arch Angel Aerial for you not be another\n\ntrick my mind has played one me.” You giggled harder and faster now smiling then returning what i said with a simple reply “Glad I still drive you crazy..” chuckling you obviously had no idea how you did “You have no Idea “ said remaining silent\n\nbefore any of one of us said anything else you wrapped your arms around me and buried your face into my chest I could feel you holding back tears muttering “I’m Sorry Roy...” I simply stood there slowly wrapping my arms around you lowering my head on\n\ntop of yours the pain was natural do to my giant figure and your smaller wood elven one but it was a pain I was always willing to endure not saying a single word. I remember standing there as it seemed to be forever but as we stood remaining silently it\n\nfelt as if we exchanged thousands of emotionally carried words.\nAs I gathered the words and the courage to speak I did. “Tis alright Winter, there is no need for you to be worried, and saddened. It is\n\nvery true your departure caused me much pain and sadness but with your return I already feel the deep wounds healing...” You sighed as I let go slowly taking a step back attempting to give a reassuring smiles but I knew you got a small hint of\n\nthe pain you caused me. And saw the sorrow it brought you, I could never think of what would happen if you saw all the pain you caused me. I continued on saying “Why don’t we head into the keep? I have a great desire to get out of this god forsaken\n\nsuit” You giggled once more as your replied back to me “And I out of this dress, and I desire to clean up” I smiled and chuckled a bit as we made our way to the keep as I spoke once again as we reached the entryway of the keep. “Do you have your ke-” We\n\nlaughed as I saw you were already inside I as I changed my clothes to my plain blue and silver tunic and grey pants. I saw the steam coming from the bathroom as you cleaned yourself I simply retreated to my study and began writing reports, notices,\n\nletters and more with a single phrase being repeated in the back of my head “But do not all wounds leave a scar? Only to be reopened?”\nHow...how...could you...... After many years of being apart, and when you returned you act as if you were\n\nheartbroken as well? And Now.....you......leave......AGAIN?!?! For all that we once stood for? Caring? Aid? ...Love? But now you once again left me alone to be alone by my wicked thoughts and mind. In the last ten years the passing of my Parents,\n\nSister, Nephew, Sons, and now you leave? Shame on ye for leaving me once. And Shame on me for taking you back only for you to do the same... I can already feel the scars reopening tearing my mind asunder. Your pale skin, deep crystal blue\n\neyes, and fiery red hair once brought me peace and balance. And now, all it brings is rage, chaos, and a lust for blood taking me to insanity.\nFor long I held false hope near me again but one cold rainy night I realised I need to let go, let the one\n\nwho broke me heart and cursed my name to insanity go and let her rot in the nether!As those thoughts ran through my head I spotted two men, a half elf and a human they seemed to have rob a caravan that passed in front of Riven, the place we\n\nonce cherished TOGETHER. I approached the two as I heard a cry for help from one of the surviving merchants. Wearing my armor black as the scales of that drakes that burned down old Arethor I stood at them blade and shield ready at the two.\n\n\nI walked over ready to fight them which in my mind I knew it was to happen knowing these type of low lifes. Those who have some type of arms and armor and think they can fight with anyone who stands in their way. As I neared I bellowed in deep, cold\n\nand distance voice “Step away from the traders...Or ye will see that Silver spills blood then steel.” The two bandits simply laughed the human stating “Ahahaha, One man in some fancy smancy lordling armor thinks he can take two in Iron and Steel?!”", ""),
        StaticBook("Book of Shí - I", "§bYíng Zhéng", "The Book of Shí I\n Fashion and Culture\n\nGarments\nFashion in the Shíguó is quite uniform, with both commoners and government officials wearing similar styles of clothing, with the only distinguishable features being the colour and qua\n\nof the garments. Silk is considered the material of choice by high ranking individuals, chosen for its smooth and slippery texture as well as its ability to stay cool to the touch in the warm Shí climate. Vividity and variety of colours used in a piece -\n\nof garment were used as indicators of wealth, as they showed that the wearer was able to afford for the greater array of dyes. Both male and female garments were adorned with emroidery, with wealthier individuals being able to afford for more detailed -\n\nand larger works on their garments.\n\nMale\nTraditional Shí clothing is referred to as ‘shífú’, for men it consists of a ‘shēnyī’ (a long coat or robe) and a ‘zhóngyí' (shirts and trousers). The Shényí is a robe-like garment that covers the entiret\n\nwearer's arms, and reaches to their feet, it is generally worn in more formal confrontations. The zhōngyī is worn underneath the shifu and is mostly made of cotton or silk.\n\nFemale\nThe most common garment worn by women is a 'rúqún', -\n\nconsisting of a long skirt and an upper garment, decorations such as braids or ornaments may be worn with these.\n\nHairstyles and Headwear\nBoth male and females refrain from cutting their hair once they have reached adulthood, between the ages of 15 to 20, allowing their hair to grow long. This follows the ideas and teachings that every inch o an individual is a\n\ndebt to their parents and to God, that they are of their parent's flesh and blood; thus to cut your hair is to dishonour your family. The shaving of hair is a common punishment considered equivalent or worse than death.\n\nMale\nMen are allowed to t\n\nhair into a knot (jí) - that is all. The fútóu, a cloth wrap around the hair is the most common headwear for men.\n\nFemale\nWith the changing of fashion throughout the ages, many different styles of hair have come and go, such as -\n\nthe xiáfá, sánfá, and yuánfá. These hairstyles would be accomodated with various hair accessories as ornaments for the hair, such as hair pins (jiá, which were also used by males) in order to hold their hair in place. It is also common for females -\n\nto leave their hair down before marriage.\n\nNames\nAn individual’s name consists of their family name (xìng) and personal name (míng), in some circumstances it is seen as being disrespectful to use personal names. Family names originate from clan names and are patrilineal, passed from father to\n\nchild. Sub-surnames are given to government officers in order to distinguish between ranks and seniority, this is known as a 'shi'. Personal names are given by parents to have a meaning, they are used as a blessing on their child.\n\nIn formal consultations, the xìng comes before the míng, which is followed by their shì and title.\n\nExample:\nYíng (xìng) Zhēng (míng) Meng (shì) Taishi (grand historian), meaning 'to bring success'.\n\nLanguage\nThe language of the Shí is known as 'Shíhuà', its can be found in two written forms: New Shíwén and Old Shíwén. New Shíwén was introduced 200 years ago bby linguist Qian Jiegang in order to improve communication with the outside world -\n\nand vastly improve literacy rates amongst the Shí people, it is a flexiosisation of the Shíhuà (Shí tongue). Despite Shíhuà being the official language of the Shí, the 'Common' tongue has become more widespread among the Shí people, and Old Shíwén has -\n\nvastly died out.", ""),
        StaticBook("Pampo", "§bThe Chronicler", "===================\n\n\n\n         Pampo\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n===================\n\nHorror. I remember it like it was yesterday.\n\nA deep frost was strangling Al’Khazar, and the North had sent the worst winter in memory. There would be no relief any time soon, if the crazy mage in his tower was to be believed. The colossal\n\nwaste of resources stood watch over the subdued city, a silent sentinel keeping an eye out for dangers I could never hope to understand or even see. King Dan had been enchanted by the timeless sorcerer, even if no magic had been involved. Anything\n\nAmbros asked for was granted without much thought by the King, much to the chagrin of the Archbishop, who trusted neither magic nor men smarter than himself.\n\nBare branches clawed desperately at the cloudless sky\n\nas I found myself crossing the palace gardens, coming from the coast. I had been out on a walk, having tired of playing chess against myself in the palace long ago. As I approached the thick oak doors shielding the kitchens from the cold, I failed to\n\nnotice that the guard posted there was absent. As I stripped out of my frozen garments, I did not find the empty kitchens remarkable, nor the empty hallways as I walked past the silent library, its paltry excuse for books occupying just one shelf.\n\nThe rest of the poorly made bookshelves had been used for firewood earlier in the week, as there was concern if the forest was tapped too much, it would not restore itself in time for next winter. Of course Dan had chosen this Winter to travel abroad.\n\nIt was all the librarian could do to save one bookshelf when the quartermaster came for the wood, trying to keep the palace from freezing over like many of the larger manors in the city had.\n\nMy alarm first appeared as I approached my room\n\nin the palace, located in the servant’s wing. There was a guard posted outside my door, and when he saw me, he shouted an alarm.\n\n“Banok, all of the staff has been summoned to the throne room immediately. The King wants everyone\n\naccounted for.”\n\nThe King? I thought. Surely he was not back yet, he must certainly still be in the South, looking for new lands. We had not heard from him in some time, though that was not unusual. Surely, if he had returned, he would have sent word\n\nfrom Malinor. Native would have insisted on a feast in his honor, and sent word to Al’Khazar of his return. The guard escorted me down the hallway, and as we approached the throne room, I could hear the buzz of the worried domestic staff from\n\nwhere they had been gathered.\n\n“The King’s dead. That must be it.”\n\n“They are going to put us all out of work, too many mouths to feed.”\n“Don’t be ridiculous. Can you imagine the nobles washing their\n\nown clothes? In cold water?”\n\nSuddenly, as I was lead to a group of ministers, a deadly silence came over the room as Pampo Perea  entered the room. He walked deliberately towards the center of the throne, and then as a gasp filled the\n\nhall, he sat in the throne.\n\nA million thoughts flashed through my head. Was the King truly dead? Did they have the body? What is Pampo doing on the throne. He is of House Perea, not House Horen.\n\nThe man on the throne spoke, “As many of you know, I am Pampo Perea. As of an hour ago, I have declared myself King of Oren, due to the prolonged absence of Daniel Horen. The coronation will commence as soon as the Archbishop can be found. Afterwards,\n\nthere will be a grand feast.”\n\nSilence reigned after he finished speaking, if only briefly. Shouts of outrage were caught in our throats as a score of mailed crossbowmen entered the room through the side doors. They did not point their\n\nweapons at us, however, the show of force worked. The soldiers wore the colors of House Perea, and gold boots. As one, they bellowed, “All Hail King Perea! Long live the King!”\n\nShocked from the daze we had all been caught\n\nin, every voice joined in the familiar response.\n\n“Long live the King!”\n\nSlowly, in pairs and small groups, the men and women of the castle knelt to their new King. After several moments, only I remained standing.\n\nI simply could not do it. I could not command myself to kneel. Despite my pleas, my body refused to comply. It would not betray King Dan. Not like this.\n\nAnd that is how I found myself banished from Oren. Seized by\n\nthe new guards, I was thrown out of the palace without a second though. The Treasurer managed to smuggle my things, as well as most of my fortune out of the palace a month later, \nbut after a hard month on the snow clogged streets of Al’Khazar,\n\nI was finished with Oren. As I left Al’Khazar that winter, I had no idea where I was going, but I knew one thing: Finding King Dan was the only thing that still mattered to me. I would either track him down, or die trying.", ""),
        StaticBook("Edict-Holofernes", "§bTheran", "Imperial-Pontifical Edict of Holofernes 1544\n13th of Horen's Welcome\n\nIn light of recent controversy, regarding the conflicts between secular (State) knights and religious (Church) knights\n\nover Gentry-Rights. John 'the Lesser' and His Holiness, Lucien III have convened in the pontifical keep of Holofernes. After lengthy discussion, the following edict is instituted in both the Pontifical States and the Imperial State. Let known to\n\nthe realm of God, of Horen that:\n¬†\nKnights of the State are the sworn blades of the Holy Orenian Empire, as well as its Knightly Estate (the Order of the Red Dragon), in this their vows are granted by the Emperor's authority.\n\nKnights of the Church are protectors of the Faith, sworn to serve God and his Church, in this their vows and rights are granted by the Vicar of God's authority.\nThe practice, originating in ancient tradition, known as Damehood is\n\nrevised and defined in both the Pontifical and Imperial States.\nTo achieve the status of gentry in either the Church or State, one must be male.\nA Dame is defined as an exceptional warrior of the female gender, however this is an honorary title onl\n\nreserved for the rarest of occasions and grants no rights above the individual‚Äôs class\nKnights of the Church will require a writ from the Imperial Estate in order to perform their knightly duties within the borders of the State.\n\nKnights of the State will require a writ from the Clerical Estate in order to perform their knightly duties within the borders of the Pontifical States.\nKnights of the State are granted, with their vows, the rank of gentry and its rights within the\n\nHoly Orenian Empire.\nSee: Ser Rhys Roke, Ser Oscar Lancefeld, etc, etc.\nKnights of the Church may hold titles of nobility in the Holy Orenian Empire, if possessing land and a title within the State.\nSee: Prince Charles Horen, Duke\n\nStephen Sarkozic, etc, etc.\nAny Knight of the State that claims the rights of a Church Knight, as well as enacting his knightly duties within the Pontifical States, shall be put under trial of the Church if not expressed consent from the\n\nClerical Estate.\nLikewise, any Knight of the Church that claims the rights of a State Knight, as well as enacting his knightly duties within the Imperial State, shall be put under trial of the State if not expressed consent from the Imperial\n\nEstate.\nExceptions to the points V, IV, VII, and VIII include men with the title of Knight derived from both the Imperial and Clerical Estate.\n\n¬†\nJohn ‘the Lesser’ Jrent, Grand Knight\n¬†\nHoly Ser Charles Francis, Imperial Prince\n¬†\nLucien III, Vicar of God", ""),
        StaticBook("DMN-01", "liam_barnett", "Dirk Martijn Novokain\n\nArrest record\n\n14th of Malin's Welcome, 1567\n\nRecorded by Bell Sano at the time of interrogation\n\nThis was recorded as a suspect for the Felsen Dock Bombings, on the night of the 12th, was interrogated. Written by Bell Sano, along with the assistance of Velulaei'Ilum.\n\nThis man is a suspect due to multiple reports from citizens, which are a match to his own. Members of the Gold Corps handed him over to the guard. Bright, ginger hair, very light blue eyes, gold and white clothing.\n\nSano: \"Where were you on the night of the 12th of Malin's Welcome?\"\n\nDirk: \"I was in the Aethermoore tavern, bartending as usual.\"\n\nAnalysis: Suspect seems to be employed as a bar tender, and denies being at the scene at the time of the explosion.\n\nIlum: \"What is your business here in Oren?\"\n\nDirk: \"I mostly come here to buy iron for my smith, not really anything else.\"\n\nIlum: \"So you have no stake in the safety of this city?\"\n\nDirk: \"I think I have family here, so I do. Lovets are my extended family. Wouldn't want to see them in harm under any circumstances.\"\n\nAnalysis: Suspect seems to only come to Felsen for business, and may have family within the walls.\n\nSano: \"How about the night of the 11th? When the fires broke out?\"\n\nDirk: \"I came to the city when I heard of the fires.\"\n\nSano: \"So you deny being within the walls at the time of the outbreak?\"\n\nDirk: \"Yes, I do. I was arrested due to a misunderstanding when I arrived, but was released minutes later.\"\n\nSano: \"What were you arrested for then, may I ask?\"\n\nDirk: \"A twist of words, I stated Ave Orenia as I went to help with the fires, but it was twisted to seem as if I were a rebel.\"\n\nAnalysis: Suspect seems to also deny any act of arson.\n\nIlum: \"Where did you go after being set free, then?\"\n\nDirk: \"To the Aethermoor tavern, to continue bartending as I had been before the attack.\"\n\nIlum: \"Then why did you return to Oren after the second attack?\"\n\nDirk: \"I didn't, actually. I continued working.\"\n\nSano: \"Yet you were arrested at the crime scene.\"\n\nDirk: \"Karver sent a bird for me to come to the Felsen docks, so I did.\"\n\nSano: \"So you did return to Oren after the second attacks?\"\n\nDirk: \"After the second attack, yes.\"\n\nSano: \"Yet, you already claimed that you were working after the second attack?\"\n\nDirk: \"I continued to work, then came to Oren when a bird was sent. Simple.\"\n\nAnalysis: Conflicting information, will examine further. However, a man named Karver was indeed at the docks.\n\nSano: \"What's your economic background, Novokain?\"\n\nDirk: \"Blacksmith. Or do you mean as a child? Farmer.\"\n\nSano: \"That's not an answer, I asked for your economic background, not your profession. What's your wallet look like?\"\n\nDirk: \"Middle class.\"\n\nSano: \"Do you have any ties to nobility?\"\n\nDirk: \"Yes, I know many nobles. Some may even call me one.\"\n\nSano: \"That's exactly what I was looking for, thank you.\"\n\nAnalysis: Suspect may have great wealth, or ties to those of a higher social status.\n\nFinal analysis:\n\n-No noticeable motive\n-No confessed training in explosives\n-Potentially has plenty of mina\n-Seems to have no connections to the helmet found in the wreck\n\nIlum claims that explosives had been sold at the Cloud Temple market only a day earlier, for one hundred mina.", ""),
        StaticBook("NV-02", "liam_barnett", "10th of the Amber Cold, 1567\n\nNemir Valnelis\n\nThe following is the account of what took place on the night of the 15th of Sun's Smile, 1567\n\nThis will be a transcript of Miss Valnelis' own testimony, word for word.\n\nSection I:\n\nVictim claims that she arrived at the gates, alone, hoping to enter in order to purchase a drink. She found two guards arguing, presumably Corporal Crider and Lieutenant Smyth.\n\nAs the woman was arrested, on the grounds of being an 'Aheral, she was taken to the cells beneath Ancelcourt, strapped into the chair by Smyth, accompanied by Sano, Zenik, and Crider.\n\nAs the victim was trapped in the chair, Crider and Sano protested, protecting the woman. Crider lunged towards Smyth, fed up with his, quote, \"Abnormal acts of violence,\" and Zenik knocked him out cold, using\n\na glass bottle, breaking it against his head. They proceeded to hang Crider up on the wall, and Sano departed.\n\nSection II:\n\nAfter the departure, Smyth took out his knife, gliding it across the victim's cheek. He began asking the woman questions, such as the following:\n\n\"What's your name?\"\n\n\"How badly do you want to live?\"\n\n\"Who would miss you if you were to die?\"\n\nAfter answering these questions, Crider came to, starting to look around the room. As he was already pinned to the wall, unable to move, Smyth ordered Zenik to hit his head with a rock.\n\nAfter Zenik had done so, Smyth ordered him to do it again, but harder this time, and that is where Crider's head was removed. Zenik then took Valnelis' own dagger, and returned it by darting it at her feet.\n\nSection III:\n\nAfter being released, Valnelis ran outside, greeted by Sano, Crawley, accompanied by Zenik, and met with a man named Vargen, a concerned friend.\n\nThis is a compiled report of the actions of Lieutenant Smyth on the night of the 15th of Sun's Smile, 1567. Recorded by Bell Sano, and accompanied by Michael Raher and Erren Crawley.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ragnar III", "§bRagnar de Autson VI", "Ragnar de Autson III\n\nI swear to you my Lord, and the Seven Skies that I shall use my blade to defend the helpless.\n\nMy might will be used to uphold the weak.\n\nMy words will speak only the truth.\n\nMy wrath will undo the wicked.\n\nMy knowledge will defeat ignorance.\n\nMy skills will be taught to the willing.\n\nMy temper shall be held by patience.\n\nThis is the Knights oath, and if I break the oath I have just stated I will be executed.\n\n\"Almighty God, have mercy upon Ser Ragnar III, a humble Knight in Thy Divine Service.\nOh Lord, I pray for Thy indulgence and blessings.\n\nForget not Thine servant in his trials, nor his Knighthood.\n\nThe lord withdrawed a traditional ceremonial sword from a gilded scabbard and placed the sword upon Ser Ragnar's shoulder. \n\"I hereby pronounce you Ser Ragnar de Autson III\n\na Knight of Winterfell; 2nd of Suns Smile 1337: May our Sovereign live long and may his rule be blessed by the God.\"\n\nRagnar clambered to his feet; a solem expression growing upon his face.\n\n\"You shall be stationed at the South Watchtower overlooking King Edmunds Bridge.\"\n\n\"Yes, my Lord\" Ragnar dipped his head, before pivoting upon his heel and trudging throug\n\nsnow.\n\n\"Ragnar, I shall inform Queen Dawn Perea and her followers you have been Knighted. I'm sure she'll be glad to have such a courageous young man. Specifically with what's been going on in the south...\"\n\n\"Lord Brett...I give you my assurance that the Undead Spawns will not overrun us in this attack. \nThough my son has not sent word from Crimson Vale in such a long time...\"\n\n\"With the constant series of Onslaughters we have been having these past few months, I barely have time to write a letter...\"\n\nRagnar paused momentarialy before ambling forward towards the homestead.\n\nAs the day turned to dusk Ragnar staggered out of the tavern. A strong, miasmic stench of Mead emitting from his clothing.\n\nAs he stumbled towards his home, he clenched his fist into a ball thudded the base of the door, intricatley carved Dark Oak.\n\nShortly after, an alluring figure opened the door. It seemed to be one of a female, she had a slender build and carried a windsome smile.\nHer hair was long, and her lips were thin coated in natural acidity in a lemon to bring forth a red stain on her\n\nlips.\n\nShe wore a white dress which covered her shoulders.\n\n\"You've been drinking again...\" She furrowed her brows, a mellow tone exiting her throat.\n\n\"Get your breath away from me you filthy animal!\" She took a large step back from Ragnar, seemingly disappointed with his behaviour. \n\n\"I deserve a drink, for you shall now refer to me as Ser Ragnar de Autson III.\"\nHe bellowed his raspy voice thr\n\nthe small, quaint cottage.\n\nRagnar stumbled inside placing his palms on her shoulders \"You look like a harlot.\" He kissed her neck.\n\n\"Get off of me!\" She extended her arms and shoved Ragnar from her shoulders.\n\n\"We haven't even been wedded yet, and you wonder why...\" She promptly pushed past Ragnar and out the door.\n\n\"Cersei!\" Ragnar yelled, before rolling his eyes and watching her disappear over the horizon.\n\nRagnar, removed his ferrum greaves from his shins and his chainmail hauberk. \nRagnar walked along the thin and creaky floorboards, his large feet making the floorboards strain under his weight.\n\nThree Years Later\n\n\nA faint knock upon Ragnar's door echoed throughout his cottage.\n\nA widespread apathy lingered in the air, as Ragnar opened it.\n\nA bemused expression appared upon Ragnar's face. \"Lord Brett\" He dipped his head in courtesy.\n\nLord Brett; however did not acknowledge this. His shoulders were slumped making his stature seem small, he gave a despairing shrug before speaking.\n\n\"Ser Ragnar, my heart goes out to you and Lady Cersei. I am so sorry to tell you. Your son, Ragnar IV has been killed in the invasion of Crimson Vale.\"\nLord Brett had a woeful expression, a tear running down his right eye.\n\nRagnar froze, his body felt fridgid and he contorted his face.\n\nLord Brett bobbed his head towards Ragnar and pivoted on his heel walking away; leaving Ragnar looking disconsolated.\n\nPart 1 of 2.\n\n\nBy Ragnar de Autson VI", ""),
        StaticBook("Cold Uprising", "§bHistorian", "Deep Cold Uprising\n-------=-------\n\nGathered From A Collection of Historical Documents.\n\nTaking place in the year 1585.\n\nThe Deep Cold Uprising, otherwise known as Andrik's Rebellion, Was a short insurgency against the Holy Orenian Empire, orchestrated by the King Andrew II or Haense taking place in the winter of 1585 to gain independance of the Kingdom of Haense.\n\nThe rebellion occurred during the age known as Year of Four Emperors and ended with the abdication and imprisonment of Kind Andrew II, and the reaffirmation of fealty by numerous northern lords and aristocrats to the Imperial State.\n\nAndrew was executed therein after with other of his bannermen recieving punishment as well. At the start King Andrew II received support from a multitude of his vassals, including his Marshal, Marquis Brandon. Andrew II waste no time in preparing -\n\nfortifications. and started by destroying and blocking the pass through the Greyspine Mountains, obstructing any land route into the Kingdom. As time progressed, there were many  within the Kingdom who began to doubt the validity of the rebellion. Many -\n\nLords of the realm were members of Houses that had been destroyed in the Dukes War, and wished not to return to a state of exile. It was during this period of doubt that Emperor Philip released the Olive Branch petition, offering amnesty to any northern -\n\nlords who either remained neutral or fought against King Andrew II. While many were wary of abandoning the Kingdom, they were also not wanting to see their Kingdom and thier Houses destroyed. It was Count Sergius' declaration of -\n\nsupport for the Empire that gave many nobles the final push need, including Count Demetrius of Metterden. The loss of support from his top nobles caused Andrew II to give up the rebellion, and forced him to abdicate the throne to his young son Marius.\n\nSoon after the end of the rebellion Andrik turned himself in to the court of Emperor Philip, who had Andrik executed by boiling him in milk. Marius, Andrik's young son would be declared the new King of Haense, with his uncle Prince Charles,\nacting as -\n\nPrince Regent until the boy king came of age. Ser Brandon, Marquis of Vasiland would also be captured by Imperial men and his hand removed for his part in the regicide of Emperor John IV. The punishements issued by the Emperor would begin to foster anti-\n\nImperial sentiments within the North, but were put down quickly throught the works of Count Sergius of Turov, and Brandons uncle. Lukas Vanir.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fool's Sword", "§bBell Sano", "1550, 14th of the\nGreat Harvest\n\nFool's Sword\n\nLevi Shatar\n\nThe Fool's Sword is a steel longsword, which has been snapped into two seperate pieces. The tip is stained to the point of rust. Badly beaten and worn out, it was passed down to Levi Shatar by Richard Revlis.\n\nRevlis was a respected military figure in Dunamis, given the title of Marshall. During the time period that he was in command, the Oren Civil War was taking place, so it's assumed that the sword was forged around\n\nthe year 1500 or earlier. Seeing many battles, Richard Revlis passed the weapon down to his son, Danis Revlis, and then him down to Shatar. Upon obtaining the sword, Shatar pierced his own stomach with the sword in battle, causing it\n\nto snap into two pieces. His wounds were healed, but the sword remains broken. He came in contact with the sword about eleven years prior to him donating it.\n\nIt is unknown if Richard forged it himself, or if he simply used it in the Civil War.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Golden Crow", "§bWalter Marshall", "History Of The Brotherhood\n\nA comprehensive history of The Brotherhood Of The Golden Crow.\n\nBy \nWalter Marshall\n\n\nNear the close of the infamous Third Human-Dwarf War, the Urguani quickly crumbled, with numerous dwarven holdings falling to the hands of King Andrew of Oren. Most important of these newly conquered fiefs was the Hold of Hiebenhall,\n\nthe last Dwarven Hold in both Northern Athera and on the River Picataris, decimating the Grand Kingdom of Urguan’s vital supply line of timber and coal to the war effort. The victorious capitulation was lead by the one named Karl Aleksandrovic Tuvic,\n\n leading Oren-aligned levies of the County of Ayr and was joined by his Vladovic kinsman of Woldzmir.\n\necause of his role in its capture, Karl Aleksandrovic was aptly named Count of Siegrad by the King of Oren, beginning to slow process in subjugating the neighboring tribes which enjoyed extensive autonomy under both the Urguani yoke and the past Kingdom\n\n With his new office, Karl Aleksandrovic took new arms under the urging of his fellow peers and guardians, upholding the newly christened House Barbanov,\n\n named for one of the numerous Raev Princes of yore, and wielding the standard of the gold crow upon a black field, in honor of his grandfather.\n\nWhat came with his appointment was Count Karl’s creation of a primed levy force, attempting to reorganize the previous wild militia from the ruins of Waldenia and be akin to those like the noble houses of mainland Oren.\n\nIt equated into the Brotherhood of the Golden Crow, which became Count Karl’s personal retinue and staging force, joining him in the ending days of the Third Human-Dwarf War, his elevation to Duke after the death of his uncle in 1505,\n\n and his later death by the hand of the Adunian Flesh Worm Mordangai (ironically the spawn of the previous Adunian Flesh Worm Wundergar which was slain by his uncle nearly two decades before).\n\nHis son, Siguine Karovic, inherited with his demise, the Brotherhood of the Golden Crow swearing their loyalty and resuming their original post. With Duke Siguine’s unmatured age,\n\n Count Tarcell of Valles took charge as regent and wardfather for the young ducal figure, becoming de facto ruler of Haense and sole leader of the Golden Crow. Compared to Duke Karl’s constant involvement and participation in Oren’s affairs,\n\nCount Tarcell of Valles took an isolationist approach, and the Duchy of Haense and the Golden Crow remained mostly within their borders.\n\nDespite the rising tensions and conflicts between Duke Hughes of Adria and King Olivier of Oren,\n\n it came to great surprise when Count Tarcell of Valles led the Haensic levy in pillaging Dour Watch under the guise of peace, nearly killing the brothers Clement and Augustus de Sola. The Duchy of Haense informally begins to help the Adrian dissenters,\n\nand begins a full coalition against the King of Oren in 1518, for which Count Tarcell of Valles formally signed in Duke Siguine of Haense’s name.\n\nIn the spring of 1518, the Coalition forces of the Duchy of Adria, Vanaheim, and Haense scored numerous victories over the Royalist forces, with Duke Hughes of Adria marching the Adrian footman deep into the Druscan Marshes,\n\n with Count Tarcell of Valles flanking north and the Vanaheimic forces under command of Lord Britannus Vanir marching deep into the crownlands. However, the offensive began to crumble.\n\nNumerous northern lords under the Vanirs of Vanaheim launched a revolt, angered in the Vanir’s choice in supporting Duke Hughes of Adria against the King of Oren, but more importantly was the early death of Count Tarcell of Valles.\n\n The assaulting Haensic forces were intercepted by the Kaedreni loyalists of Grand Duke Cantonus, where despite the Golden Crow’s ability to beat back the ambush, Count Tarcell was captured. He was tried for treason and found guilty,\n\nbeing executed in Castle Praha in the autumn of 1518.\n\nDuke Hughes of Adria retreats back to his namesake duchy, where the Golden Crow under the young command of Duke Siguine of Haense, now of majority age, meet with him.\n\n However, before the next assault can occur, Duke Hughes is assassinated and the coalition enters into turmoil. The Golden Crow voice their loyal and loud voice to Duke Siguine,\n\nfor which he wins the election amongst the lords to become the newly titled Lord Paramount. In the spring of 1520, Duke Siguine leads the forces into the Druscan Marshes once more.\n\nHowever, with Duke Siguine’s inexperience at such a young age, the lack of guardianship with Count Tarcell’s execution, paired with the late frost which decimated Adrian crops and the land blockade on the Duchy of Vanaheim,\n\nthe Coalition is defeated at the Battle of the Blackwald in late 1520, forcing the combined forces to retreat into the fortress of Barrowyk.\n\nDuke Siguine, with the remaining forces within northern Adria, sends a token force of Golden Crow, led by the priest Enoch of Haense and Ser Sarus Mallister, to defend Haense from incursion. The pair successfully raid Royalist supply lines,\n\nhowever does not stop the Royalist capture of Barrowyk in 1521 and the later Sack of Brelus, which led to the fall of both the Duchy of Adria and Vanaheim.\n\n The remaining force of Golden Crow, however, did not surrender and it would take until 1524 that Haense falls to the force of Jan Kovachev in the name of King Guy II of Oren. The Golden Crow is officially disbanded,\n\n and many flee with other Adrian rebels from capture.\n\nBut, after the succession crisis that occurred with Duke Stefan of Carnatia and later Duke Jan of Carnatia, the House of Barbanov once again finds itself in a ducal coronet,\n\n inheriting the title as Duke of Carnatia which is formally renamed to the previous title of Haense. Duke Petyr takes the leading role, the posthumous son of Duke Siguine of Haense to Kamilla of Woldzmir,\n\nwhere he officially refounds the Golden Crow to once again stand as the protectors of the Barbanov line.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sir.Anden's Rest", "§bKnwell Quill", "The Death of a duke\n------------------\nIn the dreaded year of 1552, The City of Riga, and they whole of Courland has been through Rough times, Out of nowhere, the former duke of Courland Rose and took his place back as duke. This made the now push\n\noff duke Draumatised.\nThere are rumors of the duke to of commited sucide, By jumping of the church of Riga, But there is no clue of this.\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Vladovic Army", "§bCarleton Cassius", "The Vladovic Regiment\n\nBy Carleton Cassius\n\nThe Vladovic Regiment was formed by General Josef Vladov after the fall of The Order Of The Imperial Dragon and the The Brotherhood of Horen.\n\nAt they're peak they boasted over 20,000 troops most of them situating themselves In The Capital Of Oren Felsen guarding or in opposing Urguan.They protected The Emperor Of Oren and it's people to do this they went into large scale battles and skirms\n\nGeneral Josef Vladov directed the trench war for fort rhewenguard and Fort Khaz'Nogaak\nwhere he gained his popularity and proved effective in war but that quickly died down after his crushing defeat for Fort Khaz'Nogaak after the long campaign Urguan\n\nProved they could drive away the attacking forces of Oren after Orens succeseful long conquest in Urguan.\n\nI have also wrote up a diary.\n\nCarleton Cassius \n\nDay one. I volunteered to join up the vladovic Regiment. I was accepted they gave me duties to protect felsen and its people so I manned the walls and looked out for any bandits or enemies that could be of threat\n\nDay two. My friends and fellow troops are being sent to the front I can only pray that I am not conscripted to go there as I am unready and need much more practice. It has been a very exhausting day.\n\nDay three. I'm being sent to the front with over a quarter of the armed forces with me we marched from Felsen to the front where we where supplied with gear and weapons it stinks with rotting dead bodies and gunpowder. I pray every morning and every night\n\nthat I will not be one of the sorry bastards that have already lost there lives.\n\nDay four all the men would put on there tabards and get ready as I woke up looking to them confused one of my fellow troops woke me up pulling me out of my bed\n\nI quickly put on my tabard as with the other soldiers General Josef Vladov walked through the countless Vladovic Troops getting ontop a ladder unsheathing his sword and pointing it to the opposite side of the trenches where the dwarfs where.\n\nhe would shout a long and loud \"Imperial Armys of Oren Charge!\" \nI would fight for my lifes as the trebruches blew up the dwarfen lines I was a small dot on a massive full scale war I would watch my fellow comrades die as well as legionnares.\n\nDay Five The capture was succseful we swarmed around fort Rhewenguard drinking ale and wine we would cheer from dawn to dusk.\n\nThe Vladovic Regiment still lives\n\n-Carleton Cassius \n21st of the first seed 1539.", ""),
        StaticBook("Norland History2", "§bSaradunan Steelfist", "History of\n        Norland\n  \n         Athera \n \n*these pages look rather new than the last volume*\n\nThe people of Fi'nor land on the shores of Athera, they immediatly go in search of a new land to call their home and quickly discover the clay mountains of the north deciding to build a settlement there.\nThe people of Illica arrive at the settlement-\n\nlooking for shelter, the Fi,norians take them in with open arms allowing them to stay of the winter.\nThe people of Illicia and Fi'nor both realize the need for the principles held by the Fi'norian people and combine each other, taking the name illicia-\n\ninstead of Fi'nor due to the friction caused by the nation of  Haelun'or.\nTheodosius Visconti names himself ruler of illicia despite any formal vote or representation of the people.\nThe people from Illicia and the people from Fi'nor-\n\nclas idealistically due to disagreements about city planning, and the constant destruction of building erected by the people from Fi'nor.\nThoromir Armahnk begins construction efforts on a massive wall surounding Illicia.\nThe city of Illicia begins\n\ncreate protectorates despite the city of 'illicia's own construction efforts still having not neared completion.\nThe Mali'fenn assume control of an Illician protectorate; Tol Aviv, the city's primary source of lummber, renaming it to the Jarldom of-\n\nTanem. \nA vote is taken and the people decide to name the state of Illicia and rename the city Valeria, Valeria becoming the capital city of Illicia.\n\n*The book continues in the next volume*", ""),
        StaticBook("Writ-Ennoblement", "§bTheran", "Imperial Writ of Ennoblement for the House of Ruric, 1542\n¬†\nIssued and Confirmed by His Imperial Majesty the Holy Orenian Emperor John I Frederick, 24th of the Grand Harvest, 1542\n¬†\n\nTO OUR BELOVED SUBJECTS,\n¬†\nIt has pleased the Imperial Throne to raise Our leal vassal, Eiric Ruric, to distinguished rank among Our subjects. Accordingly, and with the grace of God and the attentions of Our realm, We do\n\nconfer the status of nobility upon the House of Ruric, in trust to Our throne for the duration of their loyal service. Its dynasts are enjoined to marry within their status, and similarly to disown such relations as shall displease Our rule. In\n\nreturn, and as a sign of Our graciousness, We do privilege their head to petition Our court, and to hold land in homage to the Holy Orenian Emperor.\n¬†\nIN NOMINE DEI,\n¬†\nHis Imperial Majesty John I\n\nFrederick of the House of Horen, by the Grace of GOD, Holy Orenian Emperor and rightful Emperor of Aeldin, forever August, Apostolic King in Oren, of Savoy, Westphalia, Kaedrin, Haense, Renatus and Salvus, Defender of the Faith, Grand Duke of Kaedrin,\n\nDuke of the Crownlands, Carimea, Erochland, Kingston and Leone, Margrave of Greater Kreden, Count of Felsen, Louvain, Beauclair, Wett and Metz, Sovereign of Humanity and Protector of the Elves, etcetera.", ""),
        StaticBook("Child Crusade", "§bWalter Marshall", "The Tragedy Of The Childrens Crusade\n\nAn accurate account ofthe massacre at the Silver City gates.\n\nBy Walter Marshall\n\nUpon the frigid and barren peak of Mount Augustus, a small assemblage of noblemen, soldiers, and guardsmen sit in a circle. Their grimly-set visages dimly illuminated by the moonlight, the men mutter tersely amongst themselves.\n\n The first to rise and speak is the Prince Boris Carrion..\nBoris paces back and forth in thought, his downward gaze denoting pensiveness. At last he speaks, an alarming tone in his voice. “The crowned prince, my cousin Roy - where is he?\"\n\nSer Lothar Horen turns to Boris in response to his frantic query. “Our last report tells us he is encamped outside of Haelun’or, the Silver City. Your cousin has amassed an entourage of boy soldiers, and he has embarked on a children’s crusade.\n\nSer Baron Corbett VanCleef acts as his guard.” Boris stops in his steps, his eyes narrowing as he glances out towards the glimmering spires of the distant elven holding. “Corbett? A loyal man. But in times such as these, we do not know who we can trust.\n\nBring me my cousin Ser, bring me my nephew, and should the Baron attempt to stop you, put a dagger through his heart.” Boris then gives a quick glance to Dederick Varodyr, who stands expectantly as he leans on his greatsword. “And you, ser?\n\nTake my ward with you, it’s about time he met the son of Heinrik.” Ser Lothar gives a quick nod, striding away. Dederick scrambles suit, following after Horen in his brusque pace.\n\nFrom the edge of the forest, Dederick perches himself on the thick branch of an ancient tree, brushing the leaves to a side to peer down at the bustling camp below. His hawk-like gaze scours the large congregation of nomads,\n\nglancing down at the children as they dart in and out of the rows of tents. Many of the young boys and girls heft up swords much too big for themselves, as they move to converge on a single lad under the looming shadow of Haelun’or.\n\nA young boy within the camp, with a bejeweled crown upon his head, swings his oversized sword wildly as he roars loudly. “In the name of the King and holy Godan! Attack!” At the rallying call of their boy leader,\n\nthe droves of children rush towards the gates of the Silver City with unimposing cries, attempting to lift the gate to no avail.\nDederick, with a look of relief upon his face, clambers down from the tree, joining Lothar at the massive timber base.\n\n“It’s him! It’s the crown prince Roy!” With an air of mirth, Varodyr begins to jog towards the group of children, Ser Lothar following with an unimpressed grunt as they near the children’s militia.\n\nAs the mass of youths surround and swarm the steel gate, hanging from the bars and whooping indignantly, Roy Carrion turns to the distant thundering sound of hooves against the cobbled roads. Riding in hard from Vekaro,\n\nthe encroaching throng of horsemen heave up the crimson banners of the Decterum. Giving a boisterous chuckle at the sight of his father’s army, Roy lifts his sword with a triumphant cry as he bellows towards the gatehouse.\n\n“Your city is truly in peril now, elves, for Heinrik’s legion has arrived! Fear the men of the Decterum, for your days are suddenly numbered!” As the young prince continues to hurl imprecations at the unyielding gates of the elven city,\n\na new and alarming sound reaches his ears - the clash of swords accompanied by shrill cries of terror. As Roy shoulders his way past the mass of armored boys at the gates, his eyes widen in despair at the treacherous and cruel sight before him.\n\nThe soldiers of the Decterum advance on the children in the camp, cutting down the young crusaders mercilessly and callously setting fire to the tents as they go. The youthful and inexperienced boys stand no match for the hardened and pragmatic soldiers,\n\nand they carve a swath through Roy’s camp as they cleave their way towards the fearfully paralysed children at the gates.\n\nMeanwhile, the two sent to rescue the crown prince stand similarly frozen in shock at the appalling and insidious massacre. As they watch the sacking of the camp, and the men of the Decterum redden their blades with the blood of the youths,\n\na deep sense of dread ran over them. Had they failed their prince?\nThe remaining children, who stood at the gates, rapped frantically on the iron bars they were moments ago attempting to pull open. Corbett VanCleef, the steadfast servant of Roy,\n\nsparred with many members of the Decterum, but as they surged onwards and surrounded him, he was brought to his knees with a series of blows and shackled. Roy, spinning around confusedly amidst the massacre,\n\nwas hoisted from the ground by a passing uruk and evacuated before the men of the Decterum could kill him.\nMeanwhile, both Lothar and Dederick watch in disarray, at the events unfold before them. Dederick began to rush forth, unsheathing his sword,\n\nbut Lothar stopped him with gritted teeth - to run into the folly ahead was sure and certain suicide. As the men watched helplessly, the surviving rabble of child crusaders swatted fruitlessly at the gates, begging for mercy.\n\nBut no mercy did come that day, and at the hands of the Decterum the gates of the Silver City were awash in red.", ""),
        StaticBook("Norland History", "§bSaradunan Steelfist", "The History\n       Of Norland\n\n          Thales\n\n*All the pages are ripped and old*\n\n         Thales\nThe nations of Oren and Haelun'or enact genocide on the mali'fenn leaving the snow elven city of Celia'fenn abandoned. Before abandoning the city; the Mali'fenn raze the farms, slaughtered the animals, and looted all the valuables\n\nVykk Volaren, a local civilian navy admiral lays claim to the city, renaming it Volaren city after him and his clan. The city becomes the first city in the Norlandic knigdom. Volaren focuses the cities values on justice, peace, and racial equality,\n\nVolaren brings the city back to life, purchasing lifestock and farming materials from his own pocket. Volaren also recruits citizens to work the land and enlists Black Water Trading co. to revive trade within the city.\nThe nation of Haelun'or threatens\n\nmilitary action unless Volaren city vassalizes beneath them. Volaren vassalizes Volaren city under Haelun'or to avoid a massacre of his people.\nVolaren city renamed Fi'nor per Haelun'ors demands, the name meaning new land.\n\nFi'nor is not given access to meetings amongst the leadership of Haelun'or and at times is not give access into the cities of Haelun'or.\nFriction builds between Fi'nor and the nation of Haelun'or due to differences of ideals, the people of Fi'nor grow-\n\nincreasingly unhappy with the nation of Haelun'or.\nFi'norians build a strange sea-faring vessal unlike any other ship in the fleet of the great departure of Thales, its purpose; to efficiently catch and prepare whales for the people of Fi'nor, its desi\n\nreminiscent of the whales used to feed its people on the upcoming journey.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Traitor", "§bIsa", "9th of The Snow’s Maiden, 1610\nThe main hall of Grimhaven filled as the Plebeians and Sariants took their positions before OrdenMarschall Tarkus and their Hochmiester, Sergei Vladov.\n\nTarkus began to inform the order about the most recent events. \nA couple of nights ago the Newest Plebeian to the order was making his way back from the mines. As he walked, he ran into three men, two of which were citizens of the town.\n\ns Magni asked what the three were up to, they attacked him by the means of magic. The Sariant Knight William was the first to approach the group of ‘spooks’ and attempted diplomacy even when the three men had weapons drawn\n\nand had severely injured the Plebeian. \nTarkus went on to know that he had allowed this “terrible attempt to play”. He watched the three criminals continue to make movements and stall for time as they exchanged vials of liquid.\n\nImmediately after they dove into the water and split up deep in the bottom of the ocean.\nTarkus and WIlliam unable to capture the men, took the two citizens by the names of Marion and Evander to the keep for questioning.\n\n Tarkus had questioned Marion about her knowledge of the men and she replied with a simple “no.” Tarkus has believed her words to be false due to the information of Kae and Marion being in some sort of relationship.\n\nCamille Vladov, the daughter of Sergei, spoke out from being Tarkus. She claimed Marion to be a whore. As well as Sariant Knight Volten, confirming that Marion and Kae were in fact in a relationship.\n\n From the line, Dax inquired if Marion had three different relations.\nThe Orden Marschall Tarkus called for Dax and Volten to step forward. Again from behind, Camille ridiculed the woman, calling her a “harlot”.\n\nIn Camille’s defense, Sariant Knight Leofric stated “Either she’s a wedded woman or a whore, the lady has a point”. Directly after, Tarkus lifted a hand to quiet the Sariant Knight.  He continued on to address Dax\n\nand Volten about them speaking out of turn. He punished them with physical exercise. \nTarkus then began to proceed with his report. He went on to say how both Evander and Marion confessed that Kae leads an undead troop and has actively fought in Bastio\n\nTarkus finds this to be an alias for Marion seems to be in love with a “tainted being”. Marion is now being held in the keep and is not allowed to leave. He ordered that a Sariant guard the woman at all times.\n\nBase of the information given by their new Plebeian, Evander will return. Tarkus ordered the Sariants to report to him if Kae comes to this keep.\nFrom the line of men, Augustus Reinhardt Von Schlichten shouts\n\n“Huzzah, Death by my shiny saber,” in response to Tarkus. Surprised, he continued to say that the order will purge Kae from the realm entirely. Some of the members praised Tarkus, in agreement with his orders.\n\n“You should burn him alive,” Camille calls out from behind. \n“We should probably interrogate him with some mort erotica,” said Dax.\nUnimpressed, Tarkus told the two to silence their ridiculous ideals.\n\n He instructed the order to have patrols done along the coast in teams of three or four. The groups shall report the findings to himself or the Hochmeister. He went on to instruct them on how to deal with a ‘spook’ with haste and efficiency.\n\nTarkus then hands the floor over to the Hochmeister as he proceed to sit down.\nAs the Hochmiester came forth, the room grew very serious as the men straightened their posture.\n\n“You heard OrdenMarschall Tarkus, there was traitors in our midst.” he stressed. \n“Such man held the Order to no high standard such as you all do. He thinks he can leave without answering for his crimes against our men. \"\n\n\"Defiling our Sariant Code and as well as our Sariant Creed altogether in one day. Sariants are we going to let this man take us for fools, or are we going to do something about it?”he asked, with a hardened gaze.\n\nThe men shouted out responses of assurance towards the Hochmiester. The seemed moved by the Sergei’s words. Some shouted out “Purge the corrupt!” Others shouted Beliae doe Orden! Death to the Traitors”\n\nThe Hochmiester continued on to instruct Volten, Maxim Vladov, and Dax to head to the nation of Courland to hang posters and offer a bounty for this traitorous man. He then went on to order that Sariant Crowley,\n\nDauros and Leofric head to the nation of Mardon to search for the man to see if the man still resides within the kingdom. \nLastly, he told Grand Sariant Titania to lead the remaining men to search the house of Lady Alwain.\n\nWith that he ended the meeting with an “Oorah!”.\n\n\nAuthor: Isa", ""),
        StaticBook("ELECTROMANCY", "§bonm224", "ELECTROMANCY\n         GUIDE\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Richard Tarus\nAdapted: Amras Lúinwë\n\nWhat is electric evocation?\nElectrical Evocation is the arcane magic form whereby a mage creates Electrical bolts for his or her purposes. Unlike other types of Evocation electrical bolts is intended to be much more difficult to control due to its\n\nspeed and high energy nature. Mages who specialize in electrical evocation will be able to form electrical bolts and streams of electricity to electrocute their targets.However, electrical evocation requires much more energy than for example\n\nfire and therefore a single electrical bolt requires much more energy than a fireball. This however is made up for by the fact the lightning bolt is somewhat equal in power to the two fireballs which could be made in the same time period.\n\nStrength\nAn electrical evocationist is capable of producing powerful electrical bolts\nBolts may travel from any point to point with speed and reliable accuracy.\nWeakneses\nElectrical evocation takes a greater amount of time to produce a bo\n\nthan other types of evocation\nElectrical evocation is dangerous to learn and during some phases of learning the mage can be incapable of producing any spark which will not injure themselves.\n\nProcess\nReaching Tier 1:\nWhen you begin to learn magic, you will start a Tier 1. At that point in time, you are unable to cast any form of magic unless you have some sort of experience and have connected to the void.At this tier you will lear\n\nhow to connect to the void, and then research electricity as an element itself. Connecting to the void will take perhaps even years of practice, and once completed,you may still have some difficulty. Researching electricity would consist of practically\n\nfinding any sort of detailand then taking note of it.\nReaching Tier 2: \nAfter their advancement from tier 1, and their connection to the void, they can now create a multitude of sparks and perhaps an even minor bolt,albeit difficult to\n\ncontrol till towards the end of Tier 2.  Even though they can create sparks, users at this tier may have an overload in which the sparks will practically burst outwards towards the conjurer.In this tier they will need heavy loads of practice in order\n\nto become more proficient with a minor bolt.\nReaching Tier 3:\nIn this tier they can finally create a full powered bolt withought major troubles, and have full proficiency. At this point they can now create streams of electricity,\n\nthough they will simply spark and singethe target, rather then cause major damage. With this tier, they are novice mages. \nReaching Tier 4:\nNow, the electrical evocation users can create the \"call-down\"of electricity, aka a bolt from a high point\n\nin the sky. They can create multiple bolts in a shorter time, although a fire evocationist could create fireballs in an even shorter time.The call-down is not very proficient, and will rarely land on the user's target.  In this tier,they can create gre\n\nstreams of electricity that will do some good damage (burns, etc.) They are very proficient with the bolts now.\n\n For more information go to this link, there is the same info + RP guide:\nhttp://www.lordofthecraft.net/topic/88498-improved-electricity-guide/", ""),
        StaticBook("Electric Evo.", "§bHaadi Mubdee", "=--=--=--=--=--=--=            Electrical\n           Evocation\n=--=--=--=--=--=--=\n\n\n     -< ^v^v^v^v^\n\nThere is an old saying that humans (mortals) fear most other humans. I believe, however, that those who say that have never looked outside the confines of the human world. If anyone has come face to face with the power of nature, they will consider the\n\nprevious proverb a joke. If this sounds like nothing more than nonsense coming from an old fool, then answer this next question. If you can possess any form of power, what would you choose? Would you choose the power of mankind, or that of a wild beast?\n\nWould it be the roars of powerful men, or the sound of thunder that shakes the heavens? Is it the limited life of men, or nature's continuous cycle of life? Whichever way you look at it, the power of man is feeble compared to the grandeur of nature.\n\nThroughout history, all of mankind has admired nature's power and though they had feared it, they tried to deny that. This is one of man's many follies. They neglect nature's power, which does not discriminate, solely because they are a part of nature.\n\nIn particular, as humans learned of Mana and started seeing a glimpse of nature's other realm, they began neglecting nature's power even more. They didn't realize that their \"magic\" was actually an imitation of nature's power. This is what worries me.\n\nThere are many students who are Wizards and Druids in training who do not understand that every magic's starting point is a natural phenomenon. I, who also boasted in my knowledge of Electric magic , did not learn this until I saw lightning strike down at\n\nthe Crown Lands Plateau of Oren. In hopes that those who come after me will not make the same mistake, I decided to write this book. In other words, I hope that beginner wizards will learn the laws of nature and have a healthy fear of it as well.\n\nAlthough this book only deals with lightning power, which is only one of nature's awesome power, if you are wise, you will take the moral of the story to heart and apply it when training other magic as well.\n\nThe Principle of Electricity series Magic Skill\n                -=-\n\nIn order to understand the principle of Electric magic, you must first learn its natural counterpart: Lightning. If you've seen anyone use Electric-based magic, you probably noticed a close resemblance to a lightning strike. The lightning strike occurs\n\nwhen Mana, the energy that surrounds us, splits into two polarities of energy for reasons unknown. These split polarities each continue to accumulate energy, when, in an instant, an explosion of energy flow occurs between heaven and earth.\n\nThe intensity of the light and heat during this process contains tremendous power. Also, because of its unpredictability of where it strikes, it has been an object of fear to mankind. There are many opinions as to when and why Mana, splits into two\n\npolarities of energy. However, before anyone could come up with any concrete evidence, the debate's focus shifted because of the ‘great’ Wizard Ambrosia, who at times lacked common sense. He claimed that he was able to stabilize his Mana to split the two\n\npolar energies in a controlled manner, which caused all the scholars to shift their focus from the conditions in which the energy splits to the process of it. (It is a shame that scholars today are not interested in insightfully studying natural\n\nphenomena, and rather just want to uncover it just for the sake of using it. This is quite foolish.) Once Mana is split into two polar energies, each polarity begins accumulating energy at a rapid rate and causes an electric discharge. Then, when the\n\nbalance of energy between the two polarities is broken, a transfer of energy occurs from the one with more energy to the other. So imagine what would happen if one could embody either of the polarities and designate his or her target as the other\n\npolarity. Then, using Mana, if he or she polarizes the Mana and also raises his/her own energy level to be higher than their target, what would happen?\nExactly. This is what is known as Electrical Energy Magic.\n\nHow to use the Lightning Bolt\n                -=-\n\nThe Lightning Bolt attack is a magic that uses the mechanic of creating static electricity, which in turn utilizes the characteristics of the negative charge for a sudden electrostatic discharge. During the energy transfusion, a bright explosion\n\nresembling a lightning strike, rushes toward your target as Mana is depleted into replicating this phenomenon. Once all the Mana is depleted from the bolt and the surrounding elements reach equilibrium, the flow of energy ends. (Just like a lightning\n\nstrike in nature.) There are many questions surrounding this magic, such as \"How powerful is it?\" and \"How easy is it to use?\", which is technically asking how much energy it needs and how long it takes. To give you an answer, there is a limit to how much\n\nenergy you can gather, and you can only maintain the energy for about 15 seconds until later coming to a greater grasp of the art. You can charge your energy multiple times to gather more energy, but it is reported that it can become highly unstable after\n\nafter the third charge which is already risky enough. Also, you only have about 15 seconds to charge all your energy. This is because of several factors, such as the difficulty of maintaining the Mana's focus, and also maintaining the polarized energy at\n\nthe same time. (Even if you have plenty of Mana, it is difficult to charge for an extensive electrical bolt). The ‘Lightning Bolt’ attack is used to strike your enemy with electricity . Once your opponent is struck with this attack, they will be in a\n\nstate of shock due to the electricity surging within them as it an energy. Not a tangible object. Since this attack is based on an instant energy explosion between you and your opponent, the lesser the energy gap between you and your opponent, the great\n\ndamage it will inflict as the longer the distance the surge of electricity must travel, the more it discharges. Wasting precious Mana in the long run.\n\n              Simple\n              Usage\n                -=-\n\nOnce you've carefully read through this book, and understood the principles behind the Lightning Bolt attack and are ready to use it, you can do so by following these simple steps. First, a connection to the Void is a must. As any form of magic. The\n\nsimplest manner in which to begin evoking such an element is to picture the empty black abyss that is the Void. A sleet of pure nothingness. Void of any life as the name suggests. Now one must mentally picture lightning crashing down upon the Earth. But\n\nstrictly the lighting. If one were to picture the scene, one could possibly border the realm of Pseudomancy (Illusionary magic) or if too much detail is placed on the Earth, soil or stone may be produced. Then you will see the static discharge enivision\n\nsuch an occurring unfolding before your palm you calm your mind to allow your Mana to polarize the energy and fuel it. Once the preparation is finished, lightning-like strands of light energy will flow around you. This indicated you have successfully\n\ncalibrated yourself with the Void and established an affinity to Electrical Evocation.\n\nThough mentioned before, I want to remind you that the intense light and heat from this attack can significantly startle your opponent.\n\n       Application:\n    Chain Lightning\n               -=-\n\nBefore we move on, I need to reiterate and explain in detail regarding multiple charges. As you know by now, the Lightning Bolt attack is very similar to the actual lightning strike that happens in nature. Does this mean that this magic is capable of\n\nimitating the continuous strikes that occur in a natural lightning strike?\n\nThe answer is yes. Scholars call this ‘Chain Lightning’. By charging the magic multiple times, you are able to hurl this energy to your target back to back.\n\nHowever, there is a limit to how many times you can strike in a row. As previously mentioned, since you can charge up to about three bolts, yet the risk increases with each charge. One interesting fact is, these bolts of energy attract to metallic\n\nobjects. Thus when in the vicinity of metal objects such as the bands of a barrel, swords and armor, iron grating, and other Ferrum or Arcarum apparel, the bolt will change it’s path of perjectory and curve to meet said object.\n\n  Continuous Attack\n    Between Lightning\n         Bolt Users\n               -=-\n\nWe looked at the principle behind the Lightning Bolt, the Chain Lightning attack, and the application of these attacks in the previous chapter. If you think you've mastered everything through these two attacks, you still have a lot to learn from mother\n\nnature. If anyone has studied lightning strikes carefully, you know that lightning does not only occur in single, or multiple chain of strikes. Sometimes, lightning strikes attract other lightning and fuse together. Thus, where there are multiple\n\nLightning Bolt users, they can fuse each other's energy to form a collaborative attack.\n\nThis is a unique trait of Electric energy based magic that other ‘generic’ elemental based magic do not possess. When a user is charging his or her Lightning bol\n\nattack, you can add on to their energy and instantly form a Chain Lightning attack. In other words, if you have charge your Lightning Bolt attack near another user that is charging, your charge will add to their charge, increasing their total number of\n\ncharges.\n\n        The Effects\n                of\n        Lightning Bolt\n               -=-\n\nSo, when is it a good time to use the Lightning Bolt attack? If you are wise, you should be able to figure it out yourself.\n\nFirst, the Lightning attack is good when facing multiple targets at once. Try it out yourself.\n\nUse skill of Electrical Evocation and attempt to fire off a bolt at a grouping of targets.. You will be amazed at how effective and convenient this property can prove to be.\n\nHowever, there is something you must remember: Chaining charges  inflicte damage which subsequently decreases with each hit. Beginners, unaware of this, might overuse the attack and find themselves out of Mana and getting attacked by the opponent.\n\nEven when you successfully use the Chain attack, the opponent might not have received as much damage as you think. Thus, the first target of the Chain Lightning Skill is very important. This is something every good wizard should be mindful.\n\nAuthor: Archmage Crumena V. Illwindior [HeeroZero]\n\nConsoliant: Electomancer Ceruberr Asul'Ailer [CaptainSheepy]\n\nCopier:\nGuildmaster Haadi Mubdee [Eladriendil]", ""),
        StaticBook("Electricity", "Fury_Fire", "12th of the Deep Cold\n((6:30))\nLightning struck some distance away. After searching for some time, it was found to be the root of a tree that had been struck. Upon examination, it was charred, a slight stench coming from it. By all appearences, the\n\nlooked to have been burned. The only thing that told me otherwise was the static electricity still in the air for a short time around it.\n\n6th of Malin's Welcome\n((12:40pm))\nSanctuary\nLightning had struck only a short distance away, in the nearby forest. After searching, the path of earth that was struck had been found. Being even near the strike that had happened moments before l\n\nthe taste of metal in my mouth, and the smell of burning grass. The ground looked as if it had caught aflame for some time, yet the downpour had put it out. Other then that, the lightning strike itself was caught in full view. It had shot down\n\ndiagonally from the sky, other minor areas branching off from the strike. It had been followed by a loud clap of thunder.\n\n5th of the Grand Harvest\n((11:44 AM))\nSpoke to Nemir, a Telekenisis user.\nShe mentioned tha\n*The rest of the page is ripped out*\n\n5th of the Grand Harvest\n((11:45 AM))\nSpoke to Nemir, telekenisis user.\nStated that every time one connects to the void, they get a tad weaker as their magic grows a tad stronger. Explained that they would clear their mind, much as done in\n\nnormal meditation, and then one would imagine said element in their mind, along with their target. As they did this, they would envision a connection with the void. Often, one would twitch someplace when they connected, and their bodies would be put under\n\ngreat stress.\n\n5th of the grand harvest, 1554.\n((11:25 AM))\nI sat in my home, having connected with the void. The spark I summoned remained there for some second, before I would aim to brighten it, as shown before. As this happened I would grow tired almost immed\n\nthe spark vanishing and I fell over, exhausted. I had felt something different then the normal rate of mana consumption, however. As I forced myself to use the mana required to make the spark brighter, I felt something that could only be described as a\n\na portion of 'life force' being withdrawn. I couldn't quite tell the amount, but I assumed this was my mana. All I could learn from this attempt was that it used up more mana then a normal spark.\n\nSometime in the Amber Cold, 1554\n((1-2 am-ish?))\nI allowed myself to be struck by electricity in my Augur form. Almost all feeling left me side pain, my entire body feeling as if it had become static. Side that, I could not tell much else about it.\n\n15th of the Amber Cold.\n((9 PM))\nI had now grown familiar with telling the amount of mana being used. As I would brighten my spark, I now fully felt the mana leave me. I had over time grown accustomed to how much Mana I had anyways, which\n\nis a major help as I determine the usage. I remain aware that my mana pool will end up growing eventually through meditation anyways, yet I would imagine it would be slow enough that I would grow used to it as such happened.\n\n11th of the First Seed, 1556.\n((5:44 PM))\n\n[!]Page has been torn out angrily!\n\n16th of the Deep Cold, 1557.\n((10:39 PM))\nI sat upon an altar in a forest with Nemir, preparing to shoot a bolt of electricity. It began with normal meditation, and the summoning of several sparks. I would concentrate them within the center of\n\nmy palm, forming a 'bolt', of sorts. After this I would hold my hand out and release it forward.\nThe bolt would hit the ground, leaving the air with a light feel of static for some moments before it would vanish and the brunt of fatigue hit me.\n\n9th of the Sun's Smile, 1559\n((3:30 PM))\nAt this point, not much had changed side my bolts growing steadily stronger as well as my ability to cast more. At this point I can cast three before I run out of mana, and the chance of me forgetting to\n\ncut the connection with the void before firing is minimal. I have finally noticed to conductive affects of metal, having cast near an iron rod once. My bolt had veered in midair, hitting the rod instead of continuing to go straight.\n\n12th of the Amber Cold, 1559\n((6:50 PM))\nA Kharajyr female was attacking a group of elves as I stood back and raised my hand, curious on how powerful my bolts had truely grown. Sparks began to form as well as sweat upon my brow, soon collecting\n\nwithin the center of my palm to form a bolt. It was obviously weak in power compared to Locke's, yet still okay in my eyes. Soon I let it fly towards the Kha, and the effects were surprising. The Kha fell over, stunned for some moments as the elves took\n\nthat chance to grab the Kha and bind it. Upon further inspection, the Kha bore a charred burn mark where the bolt had hit- although likely only caused due to her fur temporarily catching aflame.\n\n9th of the Sun's Smile, 1562\nThis hasn't been written in for some time, but it's about time to continue it. Since my last entry, my bolts have grown to full power and I'm able to cast three in a row before being unable to cast another. A full powered b\n\nwill easily leave burns on someones skin and make them paralyzed for some while. Alternatively, I can call a bolt down from the sky.. Such is done as a normal bolt is made within the hand. The difference would be that you're treating a point in the sky as\n\nthough it would be what you were summoning with instead of your hands. This alone would cause much more mana, and you'd also need a view of your target. It would take as much mana as though you summoned a normal bolt and shot it to that point in the sky.w\n\nPast that, you would pour much more mana than a normal bolt of electricity into it, soon to the point where it would be a full powered bolt of lightning ready to be launched. At first it would remain very hard to aim, and almost every  shot would miss.\n\nThese would not grow more powerful, and the reason you summon it in the sky is simple: Controlling that amount of mana close to you is stupid and dangerous. Even if you controlled it, the amount of electricity would harm you even if you are the creator.\n\nAs you continue doing such, it will become much easier to aim and not stress you as much.\n\nFinal words:\nThis book was originally aimed as a record of my learning, yet eventually I decided that it could be used to help any aspiring Electric Evocationists learn. It does not cover everything about the magic, although it still does with a lot of\n\nit. And I urge any who would use it to be cautious and find another electric evocationist to assist them in learning, be it as a teacher or mentor. This magic is dangerous to learn and at times I nearly killed myself with it.\n-Lefkos Glowsbane", ""),
        StaticBook("Electromancy", "RedBench", "Electric Evocation\n\n\nBy Gauldrim Irongut\n\nChapter 1: Uses of Electromancy.\n\nElectromancy is a very volatile form of arcane evocation, it is just as likely to veer off its course or shock the user. A source of incredible heat and force electromancy is a formidable tool.\n\nSlow to conjur and is a life long committment electromancy can be used in survival situations. Able to create fires when need be through the burning of wood or other flammable materials. Another property that can be found in electromancy is the extreme\n\nattraction to large amounts of metal. An anvil, a suit of plate armour or a large iron gate cause the electricty to be attractedd towards it and then channelled inside of it. If one is to touch a piece of metal charged with electricity they will be hurt\n\nas the electricity discharges. The most obvious use of electric evocation is the use of it in combat. A deadly force to be reckoned with once the user has achieved a high enough power to use it. Slow to conjur but fast once released electric evocation\n\nis one of the most powerful forms of arcane evocation. Able to kill a large man in full platemail in a single bolt if large enough this just lends persepective to the raw power. Electric evocationists also have the ability summon forth lightning from\n\nthe heavens in the event of a storm with verry good accuracy.\n\nChapter 2: Properties of Electromancy\n\nAttracted to metal, can be conducted through metal, has the force to shatter stone and the ability to travel through water. Electromancy is as versitile as it is powerful.\n\nElectric currents can be sent through water enabling one to shock someone that is in contact with the said body of water. This practice also applies to metal and if one is in contact with a suit of platemail when the electric current is sent towards the\n\nbearer they will experience not only the force of the bolt but the current of the electricty will also cause muscle seizure and the dulling of senses. The shattering of stone occurs when an extremely powerful bolt is sent hurtling towards stone resulting\n\nin flying rubble and scorched rock. As well as being able to scorch rock electromancy can set wood, paper and any other flammable material alight causing fire and burns.\n\nChapter 3: Conclusion\n\nElectromancy is an almighty power to be reckoned with and those that perform it should be regarded with extreme caution. Slow to cast into immense power yet still dangerous even at short range. It is adviesed that\n\nwhen in combat against such a mage that large amounts of metal armour are unadvised and even such things as steel or iron greatswords. So to wrap this short informative text up, one would be wise to heed the words of an electromancer and to regard the raw\n\npower and wisdom of those that weild it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tome: Air Evo.", "§bVioletoin", "Air Evocation\nThis book was created\nby Master Air\nEvocationist Alatar of\nthe Mage Academy.\n\nRecopied By \nVioletoin\n\nTable of Contents\n\nChapter 1: The Void\n\nChapter 2: All About Wind\n\nChapter 3: Summoning\n\nChapter 4: Basic Spells\n\nChapter 1:\nAccording to legend\nand study, the void is\nan infinite plane of\npotential thought and\nenergy surrounded by\ncomplete darkness.\nSince complete\ndarkness is rather\nhard to imagine, think\nabout a blank canvas.\n\nHypothetically,\nanything can be drawn\nout of the void if it\ndoes not contradict\nnature. The first steps\nof becoming a mage is\nlearning to understand\nthe void and it's 'blank'\nconcept. Meditation is\nmost efficent and\n\nLearn how to blanket\nyourself in a blank\nstate of mind and\nprepare to create\nyour canvas.\n\nChapter 2:\nWind and Air are\nessences to all life\naround the realm of\nexistance. You\nbreathe it into your\nvery self.\n\nWith the art of air\nevocation, you\nmanipulate it. Wind is\nunpredicatable and one\nof the best studied\nbranches of arcane\nmagics. You must\nexperience the\nelement in it's true\nform before you can\neven think about\nsu\n\nIn order to achieve\nthis, I suggest moving\nto a region of high\naltitude and feel the\nwind rush over your\nvery body. Experience\nhow pressure seeps\nthrough the cracks\nof all substance.Taste it,\nfeel it, smell it.\n\nAnother useful\nexperiment is placing\nsomething in the air\nthat can float. Watch\nhow the wind carries\nthe item and gently\ncradles it back down\nto the earth or carries\nit away.\n\nChapter 3:\n\nAfter you have\nlearned all there is\nto know about your\nelement, and your\nmeditation is firm; you\nmay begin your\nattempts in summoning\nyour element from the\nvoid. Firstly, you must\nfind a place of peace.\n\nNext, use your blank\ncanvas to imagine air,\nallow the thought to\nfill you and the\nenergy of yourself to\ncourse through your \nvery blood. Though\ncombining all of this.\nA small amount of\nwind may be conjured\n\nWarning: You may\npass out a few times\nupon first connection.\n\nChapter 4:\nAfter you have\nmastered basic\nconnection, you can\nmove onto some of the\nkey spells in an air\nevocationists arsenal.\n\nThe first and most\nobvious, is the force\npush. Essentially, a\nnovice air evocationist\nmusters all of his\nstrength for one large\nand forceful push at\nan enemy. Secondly,\nand slightly more\ndefensive, is the\nprotective\n\nA skilled air\nevocationist can\ncreate a spiraling\ncurrent of wind that\ncould potentially keep\nmost objects out of\nyour sphere. That\nconcludes this tome.\n\nFor any other\nquestions, feel free to\nvisit the Mages' Guild", ""),
        StaticBook("Tome: Air Evo.", "§bVioletoin", "Air Evocation\nThis book was created\nby Master Air\nEvocationist Alatar of\nthe Mage Academy.\n\nRecopied By \nVioletoin\n\nTable of Contents\n\nChapter 1: The Void\n\nChapter 2: All About Wind\n\nChapter 3: Summoning\n\nChapter 4: Basic Spells\n\nChapter 1:\nAccording to legend\nand study, the void is\nan infinite plane of\npotential thought and\nenergy surrounded by\ncomplete darkness.\nSince complete\ndarkness is rather\nhard to imagine, think\nabout a blank canvas.\n\nHypothetically,\nanything can be drawn\nout of the void if it\ndoes not contradict\nnature. The first steps\nof becoming a mage is\nlearning to understand\nthe void and it's 'blank'\nconcept. Meditation is\nmost efficent and\ncommon way, as I\nhave found.\n\nLearn how to blanket\nyourself in a blank\nstate of mind and\nprepare to create\nyour canvas.\n\nChapter 2:\nWind and Air are\nessences to all life\naround the realm of\nexistance. You\nbreathe it into your\nvery self.\n\nWith the art of air\nevocation, you\nmanipulate it. Wind is\nunpredicatable and one\nof the best studied\nbranches of arcane\nmagics. You must\nexperience the\nelement in it's true\nform before you can\neven think about\nsummoning it.\n\nIn order to achieve\nthis, I suggest moving\nto a region of high\naltitude and feel the\nwind rush over your\nvery body. Experience\nhow pressure seeps\nthrough the cracks\nof all substance.Taste it,\nfeel it, smell it.\n\nAnother useful\nexperiment is placing\nsomething in the air\nthat can float. Watch\nhow the wind carries\nthe item and gently\ncradles it back down\nto the earth or carries\nit away.\n\nChapter 3:\n\nAfter you have\nlearned all there is\nto know about your\nelement, and your\nmeditation is firm; you\nmay begin your\nattempts in summoning\nyour element from the\nvoid. Firstly, you must\nfind a place of peace.\n\nNext, use your blank\ncanvas to imagine air,\nallow the thought to\nfill you and the\nenergy of yourself to\ncourse through your \nvery blood. Though\ncombining all of this.\nA small amount of\nwind may be conjured\n\nWarning: You may\npass out a few times\nupon first connection.\n\nChapter 4:\nAfter you have\nmastered basic\nconnection, you can\nmove onto some of the\nkey spells in an air\nevocationists arsenal.\n\nThe first and most\nobvious, is the force\npush. Essentially, a\nnovice air evocationist\nmusters all of his\nstrength for one large\nand forceful push at\nan enemy. Secondly,\nand slightly more\ndefensive, is the\nprotective tornado.\n\nA skilled air\nevocationist can\ncreate a spiraling\ncurrent of wind that\ncould potentially keep\nmost objects out of\nyour sphere. That\nconcludes this tome.\n\nFor any other\nquestions, feel free to\nvisit the Mages' Guild.", ""),
        StaticBook("Air Evocation", "§bLilach Everupt", "Air evocation, like any elemental evocation, is a voidal art. Those who have yet to learn a voidal magic will first need to connect to the void; after doing such multiple times, aspiring magi will find that they can remain connected for long enough to-\n\ncast. They will need to study the wind; and, upon connection to the void, picture it in their minds. It is extremely important that they do not imagine more than a small breeze at first; for casting over one's ability may be lethal to the user. Even-\n\nrustling a few leaves will prove to be exhausting at first, and so the mage must consistently practice.\n\nGradually, the mage will find themselves able to preform simple actions, such as blowing out a torch or knocking over a vase, with relative ease.\n\nThey may then work on exerting more of their growing mana pool to create larger gusts of wind. This must be done with caution, as overcasting can still be dangerous. Variants of stronger spells may include making an adult fall over.\n\nThose who dedicate much time to the art will find themselves capable of impressive acts. They can knock over fully armored warriors, and do such with relative ease. Such techniques will prove helpful for self defense, for full armor will certainly-\n\nprevent most from getting up. Masterful magi will even be able to throw others backwards; this, alongside simply running off afterwards, will provide for a good advantage in fleeing from battle.\n\nThis concludes the tome.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Geomancy", "§bSarrion", "\"Geomancy\"\nEarth Evocation\n--------------->\nBy Sarrion Zytiaear\n\nThe following was transcribed through an interview with the Geomancer known as Coltaine Wick.\n\nWhat it is:\n\nEarth Evocation, in its most basic form is the drawing forth earth in its various forms, from the void. It differ greatly from the other forms of evocation in that, there is a plethora of  things you can evoke,\n\nbe it granite stone, sand, gravel, shards of quartz. You may create a massive boulder to flatten your enemy or create a whirling torrent of sand with sharp shards of quartz interspersed\n\nto scour the flesh from your enemies bones. It is a rather open ended magic, the limit being your own creativity.\n\nHow to Cast:\n\nIn casting, you must be in a state of concentration, like most other magic, to be interrupted is to lose your connection to the void. You must concentrate on that vast plain of potential known as the void and there create that\n\nwhich you seek to draw into the world, Earth  Evocation is different in, at least for me, you can't create boulders 7 feet in diameter right out the gate, you start small, and either grow or subtract from that.\n\nSuch as a pebble, you may use that pebble as a sort of bridge to draw forth more, expanding it exponentially. Sand one would evoke in large enough quantities\n\nto pressure through the void into our own world. One must be careful, all evocations have their dangers but earth more so, it is an easy thing to accidentally crush one of your own limbs, practice makes perfect.\n\nRed Lines: \n\nLike all evocations you may not evoke defined intricate forms, no statues, no flying stone birds, that would require conjuration, a whole different skill entirely . You cannot create mud or quicksand without the aid of water evocation.\n\nThe general limit in size of what one can evoke is a boulder around 7 feet in diameter give or take, it depends on the individual's skill and mana pool. To try and go beyond those boundaries risks harm to yourself and possibly death.", ""),
        StaticBook("Water Evocation", "§bHaadi Mubdee", "Water, appearing to be possibly one of the most simplest of the elements, however, it’s more than such. It’s an incredibly complex element in which one must spend a large amount of time meditating and spending there time around water in general to be able\n\nto learn such an evocation such as itself. Water is a necessity of life, needed by generally all living things, for example; Humans, Orcs, Dwarves, Kharajyr, Elves and also plants, including beasts too. Water, also appearing as such a calm element is also\n\none of the most dangerous, out in the seas, a storm can take out a fleet of ships within moments, one can never have full control over water that isn’t evocated, well, practically no control whatsoever unless you’re of course, a Shaman. Despite our\n\nattempts, we are mortal, we do not live forever nor do we have amazing powers unlike the Ascended and Undead back in Aegis; as said before, water can be a very dangerous element, a single flood can wipe out a town, contaminate food and destroy buildings\n\nwith ease. A harsh winter, such as the one's in the North of Anthos and around the Dwarven regions which could halt one's food supply for months on end. The element, water contains raw power, a power that all Water Evocationist's would wish to wield.\n\nA Water Evocationist’s training consists of learning about the void, being able to evocate from it and about the element one is learning. It takes years on end to learn about evocating a single element. Water which has been evocated may appear to be the\n\nsame as the water we have around us, however, it is completely different. The water that us Water evocationist’s evocate can only be found in the void and some say it isn’t water at all. As all evocoationists know, their power comes from the ability to be\n\nable to control ‘mana’, mana is your life force in a way. If you use it to much then one would simply fall unconscious or they can even die from the overuse of course. After much dedication and training; such as spending time to learn about the void\n\nand about Water Evocation, a Water Evocationist is able to pull mana directly from the void, shaping it into a water-like substance in our world. This connection to the void is rather difficult to explain, however, once one has managed to learn about\n\nWater Evocation itself, then you should be able to understand about it and where we're coming from. One’s connection to the void is more of a sensation than something that can be explained as a mage’s training progresses, connecting to the void and\n\nevoking said element becomes more and more simpler tasks. As one would possibly notice, many mages use a staff, however, it isn’t needed much, though, it’s easier to focus upon, usually the tip for most and you would be able to evoke water from the tip,\n\ntoo. When water has been evoked, it can be placed into many forms, such as a jet of water, an orb of water, an orb of ice and other things which I generally haven’t explored yet.\nWater Evocationist’s which have been learning for a long period of time w\n\nbe able to use more things and be able to explore other skills such as learning to control ice which is also evoked from the void. Ice is more suited for battle than defence, however, water evocation itself is mainly used for defence than anything.\n\nHowever, ice can be evoked and be used to create walls, freeze doors shut, block incoming projectiles as a form of short-distance defence, and as a method of harming others too. Ice that we evoke isn't the same which can be found in our realm, it cannot\n\nbe melted by the heat of the sun nor a torch, however - it can be melted with the use of Fire Evocation. To break the ice, the Water Evocationist must either lose concentration, or as said before, a Fire Evocationist must melt the ice with their evoked\n\nfire. In the later stages of Water Evocation, one would be able to evoke wisps of steam, however, it's possibly too difficult for even the best of Water Evocationist's to do such. Water, being able to form any concievable shape, is only limited by the\n\nby the caster's imagination and fatigue, which the exception of finely detailed creatures of sort. Such is reserved for Elemental Conjurationists. With proper training, water can be suited for nearly any purpose.\n\nCopied by Haadi Mubdee, Instructor in the Mages' Guild. 1471", ""),
        StaticBook("Geomancy", "§bSheriff Jerry Longstraw", "In this book I will not be teaching the practice of connection to the void, but instead only Geomancy, and Evoking. If you wish to learn of any other form of magic, or how to connect to the void look at another book, this is not for beginers.\n\nPart 1. Learning the Element: In order to learn any evocation one must learn how to pull it from the void, and in order to do that, one must study any element they wish to bring. This is not as simple as looking at it. You must feel  it's texture, how it\n\nreacts to things, and such things like that. To study stones I looked at them, threw them at things, and even broke my wrist by punching a big one. Remember the journey to becoming a Geomancer can hurt, but it is worth it.\n\nPart Two: How to pull things more easily. From past expirences I have learned that. One, it is easier to pull sharp things from the void because it rip through much better and two, It is a lot easier to pull a big thing from the void rather than multipul\n\nsmall things. This is simply because it is much more easy to focus on a single thing rather than multipul. Theese little tricks will make your life quite easy, or even possibly save it. A final tip to remember is to not to over do it. You may find yoursel\n\nf in more trouble that way.\n\nPart 3: Combat is a thing that magic is often used for, and although it is not my faorite thing to do, I do use it incase of Orc attacks. My personal favorite thing to do with Earth magic is to make a shield. If someone punches your shield they hurt thems\n\nelves, if they do not attack you send the shield forwards, and hit them. One time I even knocked the wind out of someone, but there is more. Because Geomancy is not just stones you can easily throw sand in someone's eyes, distrating them.\n\nThe final thing one could do is what I call the human statue. This takes a lot of practice. Basicly what you would do it move a stone around a human, and incase them in stone!\n\nNow that you have gotten a quick run through I hope you use this knowledge for good. Go out, and have fun with your magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire Evocation", "§bDorin Irongut", "A Book On the Study and Use of Fire Evocation\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWritten by Dorin Irongut\n\nTable of contents\n\nChapter 1\nLearning of Fire\n\nChapter 2\nMeditation & Void Connection\n\nChapter 3\nSummon Your Spark!\n\nChapter 4\nPractice!\n\nChapter 5\nBecoming adept!\n\nChapter 6\nAdvance Mana Control!\n\nChapter 7\nBasic Combat!\n\nChapter 8\nCreativity & Mastership!\n\nProlouge\nId like to put this bit in here before you read this book, so you know why I write this book. I write this book because, I , just like my master before me, wish to exstend my knowledge of the art to students who wish to learn. I write this\n\nto teach. And to me, teaching is a great thing. I like my master before me, and his master before him, am now spreading the knowledge passed from each of us down to the next generation, in the hopes that you will do the same. Now, lets get reading!\n\nChapter 1, Learning of Fire.\nIn order to do elemental evocation, you must first learn of your element!\nThat means learning what your element looks like, smells like, feels like, sounds like, and yes... even tastes like, in great detail... You must\n\nbe able to study a single flame for hours, remembering its every aspect.. and even then you will not be finished, as you need to learn more about fire... Many, many flames, of all types must be learned of. Take time to study flame every time you see one\n\neven if you think it is the same as another. This concludes chapter one, and the studying of flames should be done inbetween sessions.\n\nChapter 2, Meditation & Void connection\n\nThe next lesson, or lesson 1.5 and 2. Is meditation to help train the mind and body to enter the void. It is also how one enters the void. Meditation, at first, should be done in the most sutible position to y\n\nWether it be simply sitting, standing, laying, or the prefered lotus style. When meditating, to get things started, one should get into their desired position, and close their eyes... allowing all of the world to simply go away...  But also keeping mind\n\nof your surroundings.\nAfter this is done, calm your breathing, stay like this for however long you want. Eventually after hours, a day, or maybe even a little more, you should exsperince your first quick connection to the void. When this occurs, your b\n\nmay react in many diffrent ways. It could be from the more common of twitching and breaking out into a sweat, to getting sick and puking, however, you must do the same again, and again to last longer while connected to the void and blocking these symtoms\n\nout. After achieving a short connection time, and you are able to stay connected for a longer periode of time, you should move onto the next lesson.\n\nChapter 3, Summoning Your Spark!\nThis lesson is usualy the most exciting for all of my students, as you summon your very first flame. Weather you succeed or not depends on how you handled the prior lessons. \nInbetween your time of meditation and\n\nconnection, you should have studied a candle flame by now. Once you think you are ready, get into your meditation position, and face your palm up into the air... I cannot exspress how much when i say, focus on the spot ABOVE your hand, and not your hand\n\nitself... else you will be very sorry you did. Next, connect to the void, after doing so, remember all the aspects of a candle flame, then, using your mana as a anchor, pull the image from the void and above your hand... This can take a few trys, so fret\n\nnot if you fail the first time. After doing so, you should have summoned your first flame! Although you wont be able to keep it up for long, summon another after a short break and keep doing so unto tired.\n\nChapter 4, practice\n\nIn this lesson, we will be taking summoning you flame to the next level by doing simple movements with it. By now, your flame should be a little larger, and you should be able to keep it up and running for quite some time.\n\nNow, this next part is quite easy... or so it seems... After you summon your flame, keep a constant flow of mana, and image your flame moving from left to right... This will get tring but after a day or so, you should be ready to start moving it in\n\ncirlces around your palm. Do this, and keep doing this for a couple of times each day for about a stone week or so, practicing moving your flame and building your mana up.\nFrom here is where i exspress practice... it is the most vital thing you do now,\n\ndont miss a day, unless sick. Keep this in mind and you should start to increase in exsperince as each day pass's until your ready for the next lesson.\n\nChapter 5, Becoming Adept!\n\nIn this chapter is where you begin to become adept at evocation. If you have been practicing like ive exspressed in the past chapter, you should be ready to continue onto the next lesson... Throwing your fire!\n\nYour fire should now be modertaly size... that of a torch flame or so. If not, do not continue reading until so is done. Now then, if you are ready, summon your fire, whilest standing, and in a open area, as this could go wrong. Now then, after you have\n\nsummoned your flame, arc it over your back as you would, and simply throw it, imagin it being hurled over and keep the flow of mana to it, and as it hits the target your throwing it at, allow it to exsplode... Keep practicing this for about 2 or so elven\n\nweeks before moving onto the next lesson.\n\nChapter 6, Advance Mana Control\n\nYou should now be well into about 2 1/2 to 3 months of training now. And this is where we move into the more advance things... In this case, advance mana manipulation. In the past, you might have seen a evocationist\n\nevocate farther away than just a arms lenth away. With this lesson, your going to be summoning you mana in farther spots, from the left, right, and infront of you. Keep doing this only with mana, unto you are able to without to much tire, as this requires\n\nmuch mana. After you can do this, this time, do they same as you would to summon a normal fire, but in those locations of your focus away from you... Do this for quite the while, until you feel more comfortable with it, which should take a few days.\nAf\n\nyou have done this, you are now ready for the next lesson.\n\nLesson 7, Basic combat\nNow, just because this chapter is in here, does not mean you should use evocation for combat only, but it is a use fire evocation is spesialized in... But not its only use! so remember that!\n\nMoving on....\n\nIn this chapter, you will be learning how to move about and such while connected to the void and summoning fire. You will also learn how to move about while keeping a current fire you hold in hand, further more, I will say if you are in a fight, you will\n\nneed to pull fast connections, and even faster summonings.\nTo start, simple try walking around while connected to the void.... this will take a high level of concentration, but once your able to, go ahead and try a slightly faster pace, and so on to a\n\nand even further onto a run. Once your able to do this, which this could take quite the while, maybe a week, move onto keeping a fire in your hand while walking. Once your done with that, follow the same prosess up to running... But this next part, could\n\ntake even longer, and be even harder. You must now summon your fire while walking, and so on. then move onto summoning a fire at a distance while walking and so on... This means you will have to keep a concentraion on the spot your summoning. Once your\n\ndone with this keep practicing for awhile... maybe take... heh, no justing kidding. No breaks!\nAfter practicing a few more days after achiving this, move onto the next, and final lesson... or so your told.\n\nChapter 8, Creativity & Mastership!\n\nAt this point, you should have been training atleast 4-5 months. You have learned all of which i could teach you through a book, but now, you must study more!\nYes, learn as much as you can, and use that knowle\n\ncreative things, that others wouldnt use normaly! Make your evocation a art! perfect a certain fire! do things to make yourself diffrent! because that is what makes a true master... After you have gotten this far in the book, all i can say it keep\n\npracticing, and maybe, when you think you are ready, go onto have a apprentice of your own! I hope you do good with the knowledge i have givven you!\n\nWritten by one Dorin Irongut on the 15'th of the Deep Cold, 1519, in the Cloud Temple Library.", ""),
        StaticBook("Pyromancy,AGuide", "§b[In Costume] Archibald Cyrion", "Pyromancy, A Guide.\n\nFire Evocation, otherwise known as pyromancy, is the art of creating flames from the  very essence of the Void itself.\n\nGetting Started:\n\nKnow you may ask\"How do I even get to the Void?!\"\n\nWell ask no further.\n\nA simple week or two of meditation will hopefull get you along the lines of connecting to the void.\n\nImagine the void as a\n\nwindow within your mind, and through that window is energy (of sorts). To keep that window open there needs to be something holding it open, in other words: your energy, call it mana if you will.\n\nAfter connecting to the Void:\n\nAfter managing to connect to the void, a mage simply has to get better, through the means of meditation and practice. \n\nOnce a mage has formed a sort of \"bond\" with the void, they may now begin to summon flames.\n\nask? Well all you need to do is know how a flame is, how it is made, how it not only destroys but purify, how it burns, basically BE THE FLAME.\n\nOkay, I Managed With the Void and How Fire Works, Now What?\n\nNow you get to the fun part.\nWith the connection of the void and the knowing of how fire works, you probably know how to do it, somehow.\n\nAt first a mage in there first week or tw\n\nmanage to get a spark going, much less a ball of fire. However after continues effort and meditation, a mage can achieve their goal of mastering fire evocation over the course of around five elven months.\n\nFire:\n\nNow you may be asking how are you going to actually use it in the terms of combat. Well obviously you, with some practice, mold the flame into that of a sphere and condense it. The stronger larger the flame, the greater the energy. \n\nAs\n\nyou can also cause an explosion of the fire as it contact with a surface, the size of the explosion depending on the strength of the mage.\n\nNow after reading this, you may or may not want to be a mage. But good luck!\n\n- Archibald Cyrion, Head of the Cyrion Bloodline", ""),
        StaticBook("-Fire Evocation-", "§bGarsto 'Spark' Leaf", "{-----------------}         Fire Evocation\n{-----------------}This book is about Fire evocation.\n\nThe Fire Evocationists conjure appears to be real. But it is fake. One does not have power over the elements. For an Evocationist to conjure fire fr\n\nvoid they have to understand the element in the real/physical world first. The easiest way of bringing Fire into the physical world would be to light a torch by using Evocation or by creating a fire which then lights a fire. As a mage becomes more\n\nexperienced they can eventually form balls of Fire which they could shape into objects of Fire.\n\n((The Next part of this book is OOC. Its mainly for ones who already know Magic but want to Emote it. It is OOC. Remember that...\n\nGarsto is focused on a spot on a hay bale in front of him.\n\nis twitching a tad with his eyes locked on the position of the hay bale. He is muttering something. \n\nA tiny faint orange flame appears on the hay bale.\n\nThe flame gets smaller and blows itself out.\n\nGarsto falls back into a chair in fatigue.\n\nThat was an example of a Tier 1.\n\nThe next is Tier two.\n\nGarsto is concentrating on an unlit torch in front of him.\n\nHis forehead is sweating and he is breathing heavily.\n\nA Spark flickers on the coal in the torch.\n\nThe Spark lights the coal which results in the torch being lighted.\n\nGarsto's kitchen is now lit by the torch.\n\nStumbles in Fatigue.\n\nThat was a Tier Two. Next is a Tier Four.\n\nGarsto is concentrating with his hand outstretched towards the cow.\n\nHe begins to breath heavily and his forehead is sweating.\n\nHe mutters something. Flames erupt from his hand spinning into a shape.\n\nThe Shape looks something like a small dagger. Its not clear though.\n\nOpens his eyes and mutters something sending the fiery dagger towards the cow. \n\nThat was all OOC remember.))\n\nIts suggest that you meditate to help your self connect to the void. This can help you improve and go through tier 1.  At Tier two the user is able to hit a target most of the time. At the end of tier two the mage will be experimenting with conjuring Fire\n\nballs. Its said by Tier three the mage can conjure small fire balls successfully which they can conjure as Explosive or just normal. They can also vary the temperature of their fire. \n\n((Ooc: If you dont emote Fatigue you aren't doing it right.))\n\nUnless you are tier five and you are conjuring a small Spark. Even if you are Tier five you can still have Fatigue depending on how big the flame. Attempting to summon white hot flames. eah, not a great idea. You would die of heat. Or lack of Mana.\n\nSummoning fire from a distance takes time. ((Ooc: Summoning fire ON or BENEATH someone isn't allowed.)) You cant mold flames until you start to reach the end of Tier two. Even then you can only just about mold it into a ball of fire. With difficulty.\n\n((Ooc: Controlling a flame that is in the Physical world and was made in the Physical world, not drawn from the void would be considered power gaming.)) You will have increased heart rate, breathing heavily and will still get sweaty at levels above tier 3\n\nFrom personal experiences I learnt that when pulling from the void it feels like 'tugging a rope to pull something from nothingness.'\n\nI hope this book helped you with what you were looking for about Fire Evocation.\n/Signed Garsto Leaf./\n\n((Ooc: If I find you use this for some description wether its for the lore of your magic application or anything else. I will make a comment on your post saying its a copy of what I wrote origionally for when I tried to apply for magic.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire Evocation", "§bAerolun Cyredaer", "Fire Evocation: The Complete Guide.\n\nWritten and published by Aerolun Cyredaer. Teacher and lecturer on the arcane evocational arts.\n\nGiven to the Library of Norseth'onn as part of generous donation.\n\nTable of Contents\n\nChapter I: Voidal Connection, mana, the void, and theory.\n\nChapter II: Finding the Spark. Igniting the fire.\n\nChapter III: Casting the magic and forewarnings before.\n\nChapter IV: The Hierachies and skill levels.\n\nChapter V: Tangible Examples. \n\nChapter VI: Melding fire into proper shapes and sizes. \n\nChapter VII: Archaic evocation.\n\nChapter I\n\nVoidal magic is the magic which fire evocation finds itself resting in. The archetype known as arcane has good naming and reason behind it's etymology. Voidal magic is the art of drawing upon the voidal plane.\n\nFirst we need to cover some terms. Mana is the essence or energy in which mages use to cast their spells across every magic. It is a resource that when expended drains an individual's physical stamina and often fatigues them. It is comparable to lifeforce\n\nSecondly we have the void, the void is the plane of nothingness. A plane with potential energy unlimited. Not limited by any rules, or anything. A plane that exists, but doesn't, encompassing all existence on the boundary of nonexistence. This is used to\n\nshape and manifest different effects via mana. Mana is the resource which mages use to convert different distortions of reality (in our case evocation) into the physical, mortal realm.\n\nNow moving on we finally have aura, and connection. Aura is the smoke of mana, as if when you cast, you emit a sort of smoke. An energy that is aesthetic and unique to you, a colour or personal radiance. Aura that is. Aura can be anything.\n\nAlthough when aura does not usually appear, there is always a tell to ensure a mage is casting; like a feeling or presence. Finally we have the voidal connection. Something before continuing the book, you must form.\n\nWe spoke of the void, mana, aura and magical theory in general. But what of your connections. How do you use this plane to shape your own reality, destiny and power. It is simple, but not. Meditation. You must assimilate your mind with the thought of\n\nnothingness. Once you do this enough your soul will be able to reach into the void, and you will feel it's unlimited potential running through every beating nerve in your body and soul. This is an important feeling to recognize.\n\nOnce you can practice and perfect this connection to the point of not being required to meditate when casting, you are ready to progress in the evocational arts.\n\nChapter II\n\nFinding our spark. How do we summon the fire. Where do we summon it from? From the void. How do we do this? Knowledge. Knowledge is power, literally. The next pages will help you understand why.\n\nYou noticed the void was blank, filled to the BRIM with unlimited power! How do you however, shape and control this power? How do you .. create fire? You can't yet! You couldn't even hope to! Magic is a tedious practice.\n\nYou want to create fire yes? How do you create something you know nothing out of? How do you create fire if you know not it's physical and chemical properties. Study fire, in every medium and sense possible. Many are reluctant to, but you must taste, and\n\nfeel the burn of fire against your skin. Only once you can understand, and recall all the traits of fire in totality.. are you ready to progress onto actual casting. Now that you have all the administrative work out of the way. We can continue.\n\nChapter III\n\nCasting the magic itself. It is time to move onto summoning your first spark. Before you do so, ensure the following criteria is met.\n\n- you are calm, relaxed and in a comfortable position.\n- you are sitting down as if you were meditating.\n- you have been able to stabilize a voidal connection legibly.\n- you are mentally ready to perform magic. meaning no angers or sadness.\n\nNow. Recall fire in all it's totality. Recite and remember these properties, although focus on the entire picture. Focus on the void, tune into it, and visually imagine the fire. It's burning lust. It's searing touch. In all it's totality.\n\nThen push it into reality. Mentally FORCE it to become a part of our world physically. Use your mind. Use your power. BELIEVE it is ALREADY there! Remember your environment, and then open your eyes. Repeat until you've summoned something.\n\nYou will, after this find yourself heavily exhausted, extremely. This is due to your weak mana pool. In time we will be able to change this, through practice. For now stick to conjuring candleflames, and this alone.\n\nChapter IV\n\nThe hierarchies. The skills and talents of mages. How they differ, and how powerful you are. Where do you stand on this period? Where and how are you affected by it?\n\nFor simplicities sake we will classify the skills of mages into tiers. \n\nTier 1: A beginning state.\nTier 2: A student state. Tier 3: A more adept state.\nTier 4: An elite state.\nTier 5: A state of mastery.\n\nTier 1.\n\nTier one fire evocationists have trouble. They can only conjure a candlelight and are heavily exhausted by even doing such. They need support and are just starting their studies (lasts for one elven week).\n\nTier 2 \n\nTier two fire evocationists are becoming slowly more proficient. Now they are able to cast longer, although still limited to candlelights and small fires.\n( This lasts for 3 more elven weeks).\n\nTier 3\n\nTier three fire evocationists are now adept and much more skilled at their craft. They are able to shape and mould fire into fireballs and be more offensive.\n(This stage lasts for one elven month).\n\nTier 4 \n\nTier four fire evocationists are where most mages halt their studies. Now they are able to perform archaic evocation (smoke, heat, and light) alone. And cast much longer and stronger.\n(This lasts for 4 elven months usually).\n\nTier 5 \n\nTier five fire evocationists are a sight to behold. Masters of their craft; they are able to cast impressive feats of magic. Blue fire even explored at this stage although very cautiously.\n\nChapter V\n\nYou'll obviously need to study some examples of casting done in mages. This is put into literary form for your own benefit, please study the following casting instances carefully.\n\nTier 1 \n\nThe mage's hand twitch. He sits down on the ground, shutting his eyes. Shutting off his emotions, senses, focusing entirely on the void as beads of sweat started to drip down his forehead \n--\n\nThe mage would slowly start to recall every aspect of the fire in his mind. In totality. He would seem to make no mistakes in his artpiece, pushing forward the creation into reality, he opened his hands to face skyward and suddenly a small candlelight\n\nappeared. The candlelight then suddenly disappeared, the mage falling backwards, exhausted as his bodily form and voice showed evidence of this.\n\nTier 2 \n\nThe mage opens his eyes. Looking forward, he'd start to attune into the void, forming a connection as his fingers twitched.\n\nThe mage begins to recall every aspect of fire in his head--\n\ngoing to utilize his mana to push forward the creation into reality.\n\nThe candlelight would appear, lasting for around 20 seconds before suddenly dispersing into nonexistence. The mage, exhausted, but only\n\na few beads of sweat rolling down his forehead profusely. He'd collect himself, standing up as he'd walk to his kitchen, make something to eat and then return to his studies promptly.\n\nTier 3\n\nThe mage stood. His eyes locking on his target. He'd connect with the void; fingertips twitching. He raised his right hand forward, flexing his index finger forth at the combatant.\n\nSparks of fire started to exhale off the mage's index finger, signifying his casting presence very blatantly. The sparks of fire were small and short lived but most certainly made a .. statement.\n\nThen the sparks would grow, turning into larger speckles of flame as the mage continued his spell. The mana from him draining as his voice and breath grew incredibly exhausted and noticably too.\n\nThe sparks of fire would amass and mould into a relatively round fireball, the fireball would take aim at the enemy combatant promptly. His fingertips again twitching as his breaths still remained exhausted.\n\nThe fireball suddenly would shoot forward at a relatively fair speed! Aiming for his combatant, if it had striked it would ignite his combatant in a blaze. \n\n4+ emotes.\n\nTier 4 \n\nSame as tier 3, only one may be able to cast slightly faster but never without exhaustion. \n\n3+ emotes.\n\nTier 5 \n\nThis can be debatable. But generally Tier 5 everything is much like tier 3 but is heightened, and at this stage, one can start shooting torrents of fire rather than fireballs. Roleplay responsibly.\n\nChapter VI\n\nYou now begin to realize more potential in the magic. You feel the capability to become more combat oriented. You want to explore and flex your muscles a little bit. Melding fire, an important aspect of evocation.\n\nAt tier three, you can now start moulding fire into relatively obscure shapes, most commonly; a fireball. And at this tier you can even enhance your fireballs to become expanding upon impact, although this will drain you faster.\n\nTo mould your fire, control it, envision a sphere and envision your fires feeding into that sphere. Try and hold it in that sphere, not letting a single ember escape it. Then you've been able to mould properly now.\n\nChapter VII \n\nArchaic evocation. Did you know at tier four you can begin to evoke things like smoke, light, and heat alone from fire? Yes indeed. I can show you how.\n\nEnvision your fire, but divide it away, keeping the smoke, heat or light alone. Isolate it like you would do in an equation. Make sure it's by itself, focus on that, and normally evoke as you would. Push more mana into it than usual. If done right you\n\nwill have what you divided and envisioned. Finally, the most advanced technique for masters, blue fire. Heat your evocation to great lengths, and cast it forward. Notice it is blue. Do exercise this with extreme caution. Or death may come.\n\nThank you for reading my book on fire evocation! I hope you enjoyed it.\n\nI am a writer for Norseth'onn's library and am trying to spread the arcane arts across Axios!\n\nDedicated to Ambros, my original teacher, and most inspiring, yet influential figure that I've yet so far met.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fire Evocation", "§bSolirynir Ilmoriel", "A Guide to Strengthen the Mind of an Beginner Fire Evocationist\nBy: Solirynir Ilmoriel\n-------------------You know, there's more to fire evocation than just fireballs, right? I didn't know that for the longest time. I was self-taught, you see. Eventually-\n\nI learned that you can manipulate the evoked fire into whatever form you seek. If you wanted to split up an single fireball into four small, fist-sized fireballs that seperate to your sides, then you can do that with minimal effect to your mana usage. -\n\nYou can also create concussive fireballs if you spend enough time on it. This will usually drain the most experienced fire evocationists' mana quite extensively - to the point of exhaustion at least. At beginner level, it's a risky thing to attempt as it-\n\ncould very well exhaust you to the point of death. One thing that you can also attempt as a pyromancer is to focus in on a specific object, and eventually have it burst into flames. Per beginning your studies, it'd likely merely just get very warm and-\n\nthe like. On a closing note, fire evocation is a very unique form and can be used to do nearly anything that you can imagine - within limits, of course. \nPlease keep in mind, as a disclaimer I state that if you're not experienced enough in the art, do-\n\nnot attempt any of the bigger spells that require a lot of mana. You have been warned.\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Combustion Magic", "§bKypris'dionne", "Combustion Magic!\nFire Evocation Subtype.\n\nCombustion magic is the art of expanding your flame once it is thrown, causing a sort of 'explosion' of sense. To do this it is expected you have practiced the magic to the point where you'd be ready to\n\nanother student. This is because to do this requires full control of your evoked flame at all times, specifically after it's left your hand. Now the first step obviously is to connect to the void and evoke your flame. From there you are to produce more\n\nand more energy and concentration into the flame, but do not increase its size. ((This usually takes about 3 emotes to connect, create the flame, and charge.)) Then you throw the flame towards your target and use that stored energy ((the charge)) to\n\nexpand the flame outwards, spreading out the energy you charged into your attack. This will spread the flame and heat outwards making the flame less hot over all but now increased in size. This isn't nessacarily a subtype but more or less a different\n\nstrategy from a Fire Evocationist, Kypris'dionne Thylsealaes and is practiced by all of her students. \n\n((This is labeled as a subtype simply because you need to be tier 5 to do it, but it isn't really? Idk.))\n\nTL;DR\n\nYou charge fire evocation for one emote longer and throw it, expand the flame in all directions which lowers the heat but increases radius of damage.\n\nRed Lines:\n\n-Takes at least 3 emotes to cast.\n-Can only be done once per fight.\n-Requires tier 5.\n-If done with blue fire you'd roll to pass out.\n-Reduces heat\n-Increases radius", ""),
        StaticBook("Just a Prank!", "Azureth", "-=Gates=-\nA fun prank to pull on a friend is to lock them inside a set of gates. Many cities have a passageway involving two gates, which can be used to your advantage.\n\n-=The Cliff=-\nYou can really surprise your best friend by jumping off of a cliff in front of them! That'll be sure to give them a laugh! I mean, you may die, but it's worth it for a dank prank.\n\n-=Killing Best Friend Prank=-\nThis is an intricate prank requiring many people to complete. First, find two best friends. Tell one about this plan. Have the one you explained the plan to pretend to be kidnapped in front of the other friend.\n\nNext, forcibly kidnap the friend who isn't in on the prank. Take both friends to the top of a tall building, and pretend to kill the first friend. Hahaha!\n\n-=Sugar Rush=-\nThis is for all you fellow Mali'aheral out there. Or, really, anyone who enjoys tea. Put an amazingly high amount of sugar in someone's tea, to the point where it becomes 90% sugar!\n\n-=Tippen's Root=-\nTippen's root smells terrible. Why not shove it into someone's clothes, or something else they own?\n\n-=Cheating=-\nWhat's more funny than cheating? Pretending to cheat, of course. Hide some Black Sun's Spinster and a picture of another person in a place you think your mate will find it.\n\n-=High on Cactus=-\nA simple prank, which may or may not be extremely illegal! Lacing someone's tea with cactus green is sure to create some fun moments.\n\n-=Murder=-\nAh, a simple yet effective prank. Kill those you wish to prank! It's hilarious!\n\n-=Kiss my Ass=-\nPlace a donkey in a place that cannot be seen. Ask various people if they want to kiss your ass, and then reveal the donkey.\n\n-=Fetus Killing Prank, Gone Wrong=-\nGet a woman pregnant, or find one which already was. Stab them in the fetus. The great part about this prank is that it's truly a prank on the baby! You thought you were going to attain life, llir?\n\n-=Cups of Water=-\nFill an entire room with full cups of water. The person/people who utilize the room will have to dump every single cup out.\n\n-=Brown E's=-\nTell a friend that you cooked them some delicious brownies. Place some brown E's made out of paper in a pan and give it to them.\n\n-=Gravel=-\nAsk someone to hold a bag of gravel above their head. Take out a big knife, and then cut it open.\n\n-=Flaming Garden=-\nIs there someone you dislike, who also happens to own a garden? Plant a fire flower, and wait for it  to mature. Rest in peace, garden.\n\n-=Assassination Prank=-\nTalk to a friend about assassinating a public figure in a very loud whisper! Warning: The gaurds may prank you back.", ""),
        StaticBook("De Shroom Guide", "§bMadpen Brookflint", "De Purpose of this book is te ca'alouge any an' all fungi, fungus, shrooms an' differen' 'ypes of Mycelium. This lis' will undoub'udly be expanded as Me colec's more specimens. Each Specimen will be ge'ing a pic'ure an' description. -Madpen\n\nDe \"Shroom\" clasification be given te a fungi when i' meets cer'ain cri'eria. -------------------I' mus' 'ave a stalk of some sor', an' a distinc'ive cap. This 'oo par' structure is wha' seperates it. Shrooms are usualy found in groups, or clus'ers.\n\nBoomafool Shroom or\nBooming Fowl Shroom\n-------------------This Shroom is fairly common, i' grows on rocks, s'eep 'ills or under 'rees. It has a large pocket of a very ligh' gas in i's stalk. This pocket is esential. When de Boomafool begins to spo\n\nde'aches from de ground and floa's upwards. It will either hi' a tree and de'ona' or i' will get blown away. When i' takes a blow, de top section explodes releasing the spores. De spores of de Boomafool are very small and liable to ge' stuck in ye eyes.\n\n\n\n_______________/~~_________\n            \\____\n                    \\____\n\n\n\n  __\n/##\\\n_||||||________________The Boomafool -Maddy\n\nRepiluca or\nCreeping Glow Shroom\n-------------------This Shroom is fairly common in caves, generaly on limes'one it grows in spall 'oles in de wall. A Faint glow is produced by spots on i'. De Repiluca is often used in mixings of Acui'y.\n\n_____________\n                   \\\n                     \\\n                      |\n                      |\n                      |\n      /++\\    ___/\n_____||||||___/\n\nThe Repiluca\n-Maddy\nNote: The Repiluca clones oc\n\nBlack Capped River Shroom or Umbra-oom\n-------------------The Umbra-oom is much larger then previous Shrooms. It 'as a long an' curved s'alk with a bell shaped hood. I' is normaly found next to rivers as i' consumes river bir's tha' crash in'o it. The\n\nra-oom can be harvested in large chunks, and will consume an' disolve anythin' tha' falls in'o i'.\n-------------------I' is safe less you fall on de 'op. Then ye should be screaming.\n\n    __________\n   /              \\\n   |                |\n  /___________\\\n        ||||||||||||\n         ||||||||||||\n          ||||||||||||\n            |||||||||||\n             \\|||||||\\\n            /||||||||||||||\\\nT\n\nSafron Tree Shroom\nYellow Cap Shroom\n-------------------This Shroom be of'en confused with a Frazzlebush when i's small. I' is covered in a thick layer of vines and pe'als. Should any par' of the pe'als be eaten de consumer will become very agressi\n\nwill have a craving for more. De pe'als are a mix of safron an' a bright white.\n\n        #######0##\n      ###0#########\n      ########0####\n      0############\n      #############\n      ####0########\n          |||||||||||||||||||||||\n          |||||||||||||||||||||||\n          |||||||||||||||||||||||\n§\n\nFireball Shroom\nSpotted Orb Shroom\n-------------------There is nothing much to say about this shroom. Despite i's name i's no' flamable. I' is of'en made in'o soup or use' in a salad.\n\n\n\n       _________\n     /              \\\n     |                |\n     |                |\n     \\_________/\n         |||||||||||||||||\n         |||||||||||||||||\n         |||||||||||||||||\nFireball Shroom\n-Maddy\n\nDining Plate Shroom\n-------------------This Shroom comes in many sha'es and sizes. It 'as a long stalk and a reli'ivly flat and 'ard cap. I' is of'en used as a pla'e when a good one is no' available, as i' 'as no effec' on de consumer.\n\n\n\n___\n  |\n\n        __________\n        |_________|\n              |||||\n              ||||| \n              |||||\n              |||||\n___     ___\n  |         |\n\nGiant Cluster Shroom\n-------------------Las' bu' no' leas': This Shroom is a sigh' te be'old. Much like de Spotted Orb Shroom bu' this one grows in massive pods. I' 'as no inherent use bu' 'as been used as 'ousing an' is considered sacred by many.\n\n    _____________\n  /_____________\\\n           ||||||||\n ___      ||||||||\n/__\\     |||||||||\n  ||||       |||||||||\n           |||||||||    ___\n           |||||||||   /__\\\n           |||||||||     ||||\n           ||||||\n\nOther Tomes of de Fungi by \nMadpen Brookflint:\n\nA guide te infec'ions, fungus an' Myceliums\n\nRiver Fish o' Maliner\n\nA Guide te 'oilet makin'", ""),
        StaticBook("Essential Oils", "Nyxxaa", "Essential Oils - A guide to theraputic uses\n\nBy Nyx\n\n\n((ooc disclaimer: this is written mostly from Modern Essentials: A Contemporary Guide to the Therapeutic use of essential oils isbn 978-1-937702-04-5))\n\nquick Definitions:\nEssential oils: substances created inside aromatic plants that are both volatile (they evaporate) and oil soluble (they easily mix with oils and fats).\n\nAromatic: Referring to plants that have an aroma.\n\nTopical Application: Placing an essential oil directly on the skin or other surface of the body.\n\nAromatic Application: Often referred to as aromatherapy, aromatic application refers to inhaling an essential oil or it's aroma.\n\nInternal Application:\nInternalizing an essential oil, typically through the mouth.\n\nCarrier oil: A carrier oil refers to a vegetable oil, wax, fat, or other oil that an essential oil is mixed with. The carrier oil \"carries\" the essential oil and\n\nit so it's effects can be spread over a larger area.\n\nNeat: refers to applying an essential oil by itself, without diluting it in a carrier oil.\n\nDilution: refers to mixing an essential oil in a carrier oil so it's effects are not as\n\nconcentrated in one area.\n\nVolatile: a substance that will evaporate when exposed to air is referred to as volatile. Volatile substances are typically light substances with small parts.\n\nSingle oil: A single oil is one type of oil by itself.\n\nOil Blend: An oil blend is a mixture of two or more single oils.\n\nTable of Content\n\nWhat are essential oils?--------see p.9\n\nTopical application p.13\n\nAromatic p.28\n\nOils p.\n\nWhat are Essential oils? Essential oils are the volatile liquids that are distilled from plants (including their respective parts such as seeds, bark, leaves, stems, roots, flowrs, fruit, etc.). One of the factors that determines the purity and\n\ntherapeutic value of an oil is it's constituents. These constituents can be affected by a vast number of variables: the part(s) of the plant from which the oil was produced, soil condition, fertilizer, geographic region, climate, altittude, harvest season\n\nand method, and distillation process. For example common thyme produces several different effects depending on the conditions of it's growth, climate, and altitude. If it is distilled during mid summer or late fall, the oil with be more caustic or\n\nirrritating to the skin. Low pressure and low temperature are key to maintaining the purity, the ultimate fragrance, and the therapeutic value of the oil.\n\nTopical Application\n\nTopical application is the process of placing an essential oil on the skin, hair, mouth, teeth, nails, or membrances of the body. Applying eddential oils directly can sometimes be harmful  so usage of a carrier oil is needed\n\noften carrier oils are coconut oil, almond oil, olive oil, jojoba oil, etc. Several topical application methods are outlined below.\n\nDirect application:\nTo achieve best results use 1-3 drops of oil.\n\ntips\n\n- The feet are the second fastest area of the body to absorb ouls because of the large pores. other quick absorbing areas include behind the ears and on the wrists.\n\n- When massaging a large area of the body, always dilute the oils by 15% to 30% with coconut oil.\n\n- When applying to infants or small children always dilute oils using 1-3 drops of the oil and about a spoon full of coconut oil.\n\n- use caution when creating blends. oil parts can be altered and cause undesirable reactions.\n\n- Layering individual oils is preferred over mixing your own blends for topical use. Layering refers to the process of applying one oil\n\n, rubbing it in, and then applying another oil. There is no need to wait more than a couple of seconds between each oil.\n\nMassage:\nTo create a simple massage oil that includes the benefits of oils, combine 3-10 drops of your oil\n\nwith a full spoon of coconut oil. apply a small amount of this mixture on the massage location and massage it into the skin using light to medium-light strokes of the hand of fingers.\n\nContact point:\nIs a simple method of appying oils to contact points in the feet or hands. A series of hand rotation movements at those control points create a vibrational healing energy that carries the oils along the pathways. The oils either help rem\n\nany bloackage along the pathways or travel the length of the pathways to benefit the particular organ. Refer to hand and foot charts on the following pages for more details.\n\nCompresses:\nBasin. Fill a wash basin with two buckets of hot or cold wa\n\nadd the desired oils. stir the water viforously; then lay a towel on top of the water. Since the oils will float to the top, the towel will absorb the oils with the water. after the towel is completely saturated, wring out excess water, and place the\n\ntowel over the area needing the compress. for a hot compress, cover with a dry towl and a hote water bottle. For a cold compress, cover with water treated leather. finally, put another towel on top, and leave for as long as possible (1-2 hours)\n\nMassage. Apply a hot, wet towl and then a dry towel on top of an already massages area. The moist heat will force the oils deeper into the tissues of the body.\n\nBaths:\nbathwater. begin by adding 3-6 drops of the oil to the bathwater\n\nwhilst filling the tub. soak for 15 minutes.\n\nSoaps. during the creation process add 3-6 drops to 1/2 an oz of the base.\n\nCharts\nhttp://i58.photobucket.com/albums/g261/senactra/20160712_161828.jpg\n\nhttp://i58.photobucket.com/albums/g261/senactra/20160712_161856.jpg\n\nhttp://i58.photobucket.com/albums/g261/senactra/20160712_161847.jpg\n\nFor those that would wish to make blends themselves a chart for you.\n\nhttp://i58.photobucket.com/albums/g261/senactra/20160712_161948.jpg\n\nAromatic\n\nDirect inhalation: is the simplest way to inhale the aroma of an oil. hold bottle under nose and breath alternatively place 1-2 drops in your hands and cup over nose and mouth before breathing.\n\nOils:\n\nhttp://doterra.com/US/en/pl/singleoils\n\nhttp://www.sustainablebabysteps.com/uses-for-essential-oils.html", ""),
        StaticBook("Dating Armour", "§bSavet Yvonus", "Step one: Pick the cutest suit of armor in town.\n\nStep two: Get your gosh darn welly wonka shoes on, make yourself fancy as all heck.\n\nStep three: Observe with caution, suits of armor are known to be shy with love.\n\nStep four: Pick the right time. Only during a blue moon will a suit of armor feel willing to take on a mate. Observe when it's dome is the shinyest.\n\nStep five: Grease up. It is important for suits of armor to slide easily onto you.\n\nStep six: Get into postion. You must strip yourself of your earthly possetions, remove the fancy getup you've used to entice and inspire jealousy within the suit. And once bare, one must spread their arms and legs for ease of limb-access.\n\nStep seven: (optional) One must exclaim their love for the armor as it sensually slips onto their limbs, encompassing their body with it's cold embrace. Once you have worn an armor, it is yours for life.\n\nLife with a suit of armor. Depending on the reason this suit of armor is alive, life can be either simple or harsh. If it's sentient, simple husbandhood will do. If it is not, one has to deal with the constant stigma of folk accusing them of being\n\ninsane. But worry not, one's love for armor is true and real. If it is true, you will never leave your armor. Your armor is love, and your armor is life.\n\nInspired by Orithur\nWritten by Savet", ""),
        StaticBook("You Are Strong", "§bDirk Novokain", "You Are Strong!\n\nHave you ever felt as if, let's say.\nLife is a burden?\nIt isn't worth it anymore?\nGetting up in the morning is a pain?\nNo one appreciates you?\n\nWell, hang in there, bucko. And let me give you twenty reasons to NOT kill yourself!\n\nReason 1: Suicide is final!\nOnce you take your life, that's it. You have only one life. End it - and you're done. You will never, ever get a second chance.\n\nReason 2: That special person.\nThe one who keeps you strong when nobody else does. The one who stands by you when everyone walks out. Imagine the pain, the sadness, the grief they would feel when you're gone. Even if you don't think you have a special\n\nperson worth living for, you do. You just don't know it yet.\n\nReason 3: Death won’t relieve the pain.\nKilling yourself will NOT be a relief to the suffering. When you're dead, you're nothing. You no longer exist. If you want relief from your suffering, you have to choose to live. You have to reach out and find the\n\ncourage to make tomorrow better than today. Remember, there is light at the end of the tunnel. There is hope and things will get better. You're a strong person for living and you give me hope.\n\nReason 4: It will get better, I promise.\nRemember, even the darkest hour only has 60 minutes. Stop focusing on the negatives, instead, look for the positive things in life. Do you have amazing friends? Are you good at an instrument? Remember, you're here\n\nbecause a lady cared enough to bring you into this world.  So embrace that, with both hands.\n\nReason 5: All the memories, the laughs, the smiles and the hugs.\nWhat if you end up being the one that finds the cure for Kharajyr? Or the one that discovers a new voidal art?  Or the one that ends up with the most amazing spouse and family?\n\nHow will you ever know your true potential if you're not there to experience it. All the people you will never meet, all the lives you won't touch, all the souls you won't inspire. The future is a mystery; don't you want to discover its secrets?\n\nReason 6: Sunrise.\nImagine never seeing bright yellow rays light up the dark sky again. Never feeling the warmth of the sun, never feeling the beauty of way the sky illuminates as it grows brighter and brighter until the whole heavenly expanse\n\nis enlightened.\n\nReason 7: Dancing in the Rain.\nWith that one person who means the world to you. And seeing the rainbow when it stops.\n\nReason 8: Smiles.\nA smile is a curve that sets things straight. Without you, the world will have one less smile.\n\nReason 9: Music is a beautiful creation.\nThe wonderful joy of music, be it a bard playing on the street, or a concert for the Imperial Court. Music is, and will always be, wonderful.\n\nReason 10: Hearing children laughing.\nAre they your own children? Perhaps even your grandchildren? Your nieces and nephews? Your cousin? Your best friend's children? You'll never find out if you don't push on, and who doesn't want\n\nto hear the sound of their grandchildren laughing?\n\nReason 11: You are beautiful.\nEveryone is unique, there is no one exactly like you. And that, makes you, and everyone else, beautiful.\n\nReason 12: Your courage to live inspires me.\nYou've lived for so long so far. You've had to the courage to, even as dark as things've gotten, keep going.\n\nReason 13: Look at the children in the jungles who are starving. Look at earthquake and tsunami victims who have lost everything. Look at the person next to you. Doesn't heir courage to live, their optimism and their hope inspire you to do the same?\n\nReason 14: Lying beneath the stars at night and hearing crickets sing.\nThe beautiful joy of staring at the shining stars in the night. Especially, when accompanied by that special person.\n\nReason 15: Waking up every morning and realising that it's a new day.\nA new day! You're free to go out and do anything you want to! It's yours entirely for the taking!\n\nReason 16: It's cliché. Think about it? How many people have already killed themselves? You're so much more than that, you are unique, you are special, and you are NOT like them! You are not a cliché.\n\nReason 17: Giving and receiving random compliments from strangers.\nHas a stranger ever told you, that your looks nice? Or that you have a cute smile? It felt great, didn't it? To receive such a sweet compliment, but someone you haven't met before.\n\nIt's such a joy. Also telling people that their jacket is nice, that you look the colour of their eyes. It makes you feel good, and it makes them feel good.\n\nReason 18: If you kill yourself, you will hurt so many people. Imagine how much guilt, grief and anguish you will cause your loved ones.\n\nReason 19: Life is beautiful. Make the most of it. No matter what happens, no matter the situation, no matter what. Life will always be beautiful.\n\nReason 20: Stop thinking about what is wrong with your life and start thinking about the little things that make life great. Perhaps you adore fishing? Collecting swords? Those small things that make life great, purchasing a new sword for your collection.\n\nCatching that huge fish you've always wanted to catch!\n\n[!] Small initials are scribbled on the last page.\nD. M. N.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alavara", "§bAlavara", "Filth\n\nFilth is part and parcel with society and nature. Filth not only leaves a person with an oder and stains their apperence, it can create bad air that could make one ill. There are two ways to avoid the bad air created by filth:\n\nRemove the filth or remove the bad air. To be effective, one must do both.\n\nFirstly, filtering bad air is the easiest to perform. The most direct method is to wear a clean cloth over your mouth and nose. however, it must be washed daily as the air will\n\nsoil the cloth. Another option is to burn incense or anything that is non-toxic and good smelling.\n\nSecondly, and most importantly, is removing filth. To remove filth means to remove it in all it's forms. The nearest filth is one's clothing. To clean\n\nclothing, aggitate the clothing in a solution of saltwater and vinegar and dry in a clean place. Then, one must remove all dust from all surfaces as it can be kicked into the air. Do not neglect the cealing. Keep your door's closed . Remove objects from\n\nsurfaces and clean under and behind them with a vineger rag. Sweep the floors, but before cleaning anything else. Dust will be swept onto surfaces. move furnature and clean the area's covered. Never keep food in your living place. use the\n\nrestroom far from your home and always bathe afterwards.", ""),
        StaticBook("EG: Book 1", "§bAlifer Amice", "-=The Explorer's Guide=-\n\nBook 1-8\n\nContent:\n\nThe Isle of Tahn, Part 1\n1. Alifer's Bluff\n2.The Tahnari Desert\n3. The Rift of Cinder\n4. The Lost Isle\n\nDisclaimer: \n\nThe names used to name Tahn's many realms are inspired by the Island's name. The Atlas produced by the empire of Oren are \"Official\" but should be taken with a grain of salt for the sake of the explorer's out there.\n\n--------<Chapter 1>---------\n\n          Alifer's Bluff\n\nBetween the plains of Tahnar and the Tahnari desert is a pass I've named Alifer's bluff. The pass is a large messa of blisteringly hot clay and sand, the enviroment is inhospitable to life.\n\nAlifer's bluff is littered with small cacti, the juices inside the cacti can be consumed in place of water. \nWhen the sun sets, the unwelcoming touch of winter's kiss enters the Bluff, any who find themselves on the surface will require a heatsource.\n\nNote: \n\nWhen I ventured to Alifer's bluff, night creeped into the bluff and the chill of death forced me to huddle by my camp fire. In the darkness stirred the wild howls of something..strange, something I never heard before..\n\n-------<Chapter 2>----------\n\n       The Great Tahnari\n                Desert\n\nI woke up covered in minor burns, the blistering sun woke me where I slept. I packed what I could and moved north.\n\nI had to climb my way through the bluff and risk life and limb to reach the Tahnari desert. I managed to safely climb down a sandy slope, I couldn't help but feel as though I was being watched.\n\nI've seen nothing but barren sand for miles, the dunes have been disturbed somewhat but no signs of life can be seen for miles. There's quite a few cacti around the desert so water has not been an issue. How would the cacti acquire the water though?\n\nBreakthrough! I found a well containing water, the structure is made of intricate sandstone, could there have been a civilization dwelling in the desert long before we arrived?\n\nYet another breakthrough!\nI managed to find a miraculous oasis close to the well, the water here is fresh. Purer then anything I've tasted before, but that might just be my thirst.\nLarge trees have grown around the oasis, they seem quite old.\n\nNote: Sandstone tends to poke out of the dunes time from time, they look like structures. This may further prove the existence of a lost civilisation.\n\n---<The Rift of Cinders>--\nAssuming an ancient civilisation did live in this desert once, then I may have found the root of it's extinction. The Rift of Cinders is located in the north eastern centre of the Tahnari.\n\nThe bottom of the rift is covered in a blood red layer of cinder-like sand. To the north of the rift is a tranquil island, the rift could of been created as a result of the destruction of Aegis..but my gut tells me this is a lie.\n\nWhat's mysterious about the rift is the red sand, why would sand be red? Furthermore, this is a desert, why has the sand not simply covered the rift? Something has been pushing away the sand, keeping the rift from collapsing.\n\nWalls of sandstone can also be seen lining the rift, it leaves you to wonder, what could of created such a strong impact?\n\n-------<The Lost Isle>------\n\nTo the north of the rift of cinders is the Lost Isle. The isle is fertile and covered in a thick forest of birch trees. Large mushrooms seem to dot its landscape. Wildlife is also plentiful here, mayhaps they came from here?", ""),
        StaticBook("Making AFAK", "§bAzuline Elverhilin", "--------------------Making a First Aid Kit-\n \n          By\n       Azuline\n\n\n\n\n\n\n6th of The Amber Cold,\n1572\n\nItems you would need:\n\n*Strips of cloth for bandage and cleaning wounds. \n\n*A vial of vodka to clean wounds, needles, and hands.\n\n*Gauze to use for putting herbs on the bandage.\n\n* Suture needles and a spindle of thread for stitching up deep cuts.\n\n* Water bottle. For mixing herbs into a solution or cleaning eyes...or even hydration. \n\n* Honey. Allows the medicine to go down easier and helps with\n\ncolds and with new borns to start feeding.\n\n* Medical mask. Well you don't want to inhale anything that can harm you...or allow any body fluids to come into contact with your mouth or nose.\n\nThis is only for performing first aid until real help can arrive. Please have someone contact a local healer when performing first aid  on a person. For any other questions, please ask your local healer.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art of Love", "§bDavid Wycombe", "-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n'The Art of Love'\n\nby David Wycombe,\n'A connoisseur in the art of making love'.\n\n\n*a barely discernable, crude drawing of two stick figures atop of each other is here*\n\nDear readers, unto you shall I bestow the fruits of my labour and experiences within the art of love.\n\nWithin these leatherbound pages shall you unlock the key to your partner's heart and more importantly- their genitalia: as illustrated by I, the master-\n\n- of all things sex-related, David Wycombe.\n\nIn 3 easy steps shall you learn the secret of the refined art that is intercourse, which has been tinkered with and experimented for years by me, thereby maximizing the pleasure between both partners.\n\nStep 1) Find a partner, (woman, man, dog, cat, tree...)\n\nStep 2) Stick it in the hole.\n\nStep 3) Repeat Step 2.", ""),
        StaticBook("Field Guide V.1", "§bRilkor Niwarsay", "-------------------Field Guide to the\nImperium Army\n-------------------By: Rilkor Niwarsay\n((Arctic_Guard\n((Any concerns, contact me in game\n\nGuide to training\nRecruits or other\nSoldiers \n                   ---->\n\n-------------------- Chapter          1  -\n- What makes a       -\n- Good soldier       -\n-------------------There are many things that can be judged from a good soldier.\nDignity. Posture. Combat Skills. And most importantly the Quality standard soldier.\n\nIf ya wish to get anywhere in the Imperium, set a good\nexample of ya self, and act as a soldier should.\n\nThis means turning up to the standard of the best a soldier can preform. Forming bonds with others is key.\n\nThe Quality of a man judges what kind of a soldier he is. Make sure to straighten yourself out as much as possible, with your head held high to show you have dignity.\n\nCertainly showing good quality will show you are a good soldier.\nSo do that.    --->\n\n-------------------- Chapter  2          -\n- Simple Drills        -\n-------------------As a soldier you are expected to do drills.\nDuring drills showing good posture displays the quality of yourself and the army. This is important. Do not mess up.\n   --->\n\nYou will be expected to do these drills not just during intense training and formation demonstrations, but also out in the field. Wether it be traveling as a War Party, or a patrol. Your commanding officers, the Marshal, or even your superiors will\n----->\n\n-ask for you to display this as a group most likely, thus, if one messes up, you all mess up, and must suffer the pain as one. You do not question why or speak out unless spoken to. Failure to do so will result in disciplinary action.\n---------->\n\n-------------------- Chapter 3           -\n- The ABC's of the  -\n- Ranks and Your   -\n- Superiors           -\n------------------- Alright, so this Chapter, we're going to learn about who your Superiors are, and your position in the Imperium.\n--->\n\nFirst off, there is some what of a division between the Military, and the Nobility of Oren. Nobility will generally have more power over the military standard.\nLearning who what people are will help you a lot. \n\n------------>\n\nAt the top of the pyramid is the Emporer. Emporer Robert Chivay, of house Chivay. There are many different houses in Oren, with the Chivay's control firm of the throne.\nThen there is Empress Constance Chivay. They must both be shown the utmost respect. ->\n\nThe Emporer has his own personal guard.\nThey are considered superior to the Imperium Soldiers, for they are the finest.\nThere are, as I've said, other houses besides the Chivays, who also have members included within them.\n--->\n\nIn the Military, you have probably been put into one of two of the regiments of the Imperium. The First Regiment, consisting of burly front-line men, and the Second Regiment, consisting of the rest of the men who form the ranks, and carry out covert\n--->\n\n-missions. These men are considered to be more quick moving then the others. There are specifically chosen men who carry out the orders of these regiments, they are decurions. Not to be confused with Decanus. If ya be a footman, and require help, you --->\n\n-should report to them. They are your utmost importance, as they make or carry out the orders. These orders are given by most likely the Lord-Imperial Marshal. The Marshal will be leading the army into raids, or battles, and should be respected.\n-->\n\nBelow the Decurion, there is the Ensign, the Ensign doesn't have as much power as the Decurion, but can be seen as akin. They carry out the orders given by the Decurion.\nAs a footman, it is the bottom of the food chain, but very needed, for they are --->\n\n-the future soldiers of Orenia. And must be trained as such.\n*A diagram is shown*\nFootman < ManAtArms<\nRhoswenian < Lance\nDecanus < Decanus < QuarterMaster = Sergeant\n\nThat is a basic Diagram of the LOWER ranks.\nOnward ->\n\n-------------------- Chapter 4           -\n- Knowing People    -\n-------------------Getting to know as many people as you can will help you in the marathon. So do that. Form bonds with your human kins-man of the Imperium and of not. For you might find\n-->\n\n-Yourself in situations where you'd need help from your allies and such, this is why you make friends. Since when doesn't calling in your /home boys/ from the streets to help you kill bandit scum a crime? Never. Form strong bonds. You'll need em.\n-->\n\n-------------------- SECTION 2           -\n- COMBAT AND SUCH  -\n-------------------- Chapter 5           -\n- The Laws            -\n-------------------As being apart of the Imperium, you take an oath to server the Emporer, listen to your officers,\n-->\n\n-Fight for humanity and Oren, and uphold justice to the Humans. This means you will need to follow the laws, most of which are not to do anything daft. Conjurering, and magic is banned, this means druids and mages are outlaws. Also, Heretics should be -->\n\n-burned at the stake. ((Also follow the server's pvp rules, unless you want to get br'd and temp banned or perma banned))\nArresting without reason will result in penalties against you, such as de-ranking, or pyshical punishment. Killing enemies is ok. -->\n\n-------------------- Chapter 6           -\n- Raids                 -\n-------------------Occasionally the Marshal will call for a raid, when this happens, you are expected to wake from yur slumber ((get online)) and meet at a given place to prepare for -->\n\n-Battle, during battle you will be expected to identify yourself along-side your allies and bretheren. ((Set /status)) During a raid, you are supposed to be able to identify your enemy, and kill. If you're not sure if you can be the burly man you are\n--->\n\n-in a one versus five, then retreat to your allied company, and ask for assistance or tell of the enemies position. Surely you will be able to not get murdered and rather do the murdering.\nBe sure to be able to sustain yourself with LOTS OF FOOD.\n-->\n\nRemember to try not to die, or atleast die with your bretheren, and hopefully it's not in vain.\n\n\n\n\n((BLANK SPACE))\n\n\n-->\n\n-------------------- Chapter 7           -\n- Wars                 -\n-------------------There will come a time where Humanity will have to defend itself agaisnt the barbaric ways of the enemy. War is self explainatory. ((Server rules of wars))\n-->\n\n-------------------- Rules and such    -\n-------------------\n\n-------------------- Chapter 8           -\n- Arbalest What Is  -\n-------------------Every soldier should be able to cary and use an arbalest. It is the finest of Human made ranged weaponry. ((Rp weapon that is very deadly))\nTo learn to use an arbalest, ->\n\n-First one must aquire an arbalest and get proper training, not from the text I'm about to write. If you don't know who to ask to learn to use an Arbalest, then you probably should do some review. \nImmersive Instructions Follow.\n--->\n\nStep 1 : Pull out Arbalest in hand\n\nStep 2: Place Arbalest under foot\n\nStep 3: Pull back the mechanism till an audible *click* is heard\n\nStep 4: Load bolt\n-->\n\nStep 5: Put Arbalest to your shoulder\n\nStep 6: Comfortably and accurately aim\n\nStep 7: Fire and hope you hit ((Target and you both /roll 20, if shooter rolls higher, target is his))\n\n-->\n\n-------------------- Chapter 9           -\n- Patrolling           -\n-------------------Alright, Patrolling? -You ask, yes this is a thing you must be notified about.\nGenuinely, you are not supposed to wear any armor when patrolling. Why? Because a -->\n\n-man in full iron armor walking along the roads would seem scary to you wouldn't it? Yes it would. That's why you don't wear armor while patrolling, unless you spy some bandits or a criminal, then you gear up and arrest or kill them.\n\nEnough said. -->\n\n-------------------- Rilkor's Tips to    -\n- Combat              -\n-------------------Hopefully these tips will help make you better in combat ((MC PVP)). These secrets should not be told to anyone else, for they might end up in the enemy's hands.\n-->\n\nTip 1: When fighting, don't walk straight forward, that is the dumbest thing I see people do, and I take advantage of it. YOU NEED TO STRAFE. This will help you dodge attacks and position yourself more favorably.\n\n-->\n\nTip 2: Low ground means it's harder for the enemy to attack you as they need to reach down. YOU WANT THE LOW GROUND. If you have the low ground, it will be easier to hit.\n\n\n\n-->\n\nTip 3: When using a bow, contemplate where your enemy is going to be in the second the arrow you fire would hit. JUDGE THE DISTANCE AND SPEED. Shooting at a target far away means they have time to dodge the arrow.\n\n-->\n\nTip 4: For the love of everything, the more people you have on your side, the better the odds are you lot would win a fight, SO STICK TOGETHER. Unless you end up all to be very bad at combat, then I say to you, rest in peace.\n\n-->\n\nTip 5: Blocking is about as useless as bringing a knife to an arbalest fight. ((knife to a gun fight)). YOU SHOULD SWING AS MUCH AS POSSIBLE. Don't stop hitting the enemy! No regrets, no remorse, may only victory be upon you. ((That means spam hitting)\n->\n\n-------------------- End of the Field   -\n- Guide                 -\n-------------------Hopefully you learned something and became a better soldier. I wish ye luck out there.\n\n~Rilkor\n\nAve Chivay, Ave Orenia, Ave Humanity.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Vex a HighElf", "§bMatrim Macdunn", "How to vex a High Elf\n\n\n\n           For\n My Adunian Brothers\n\nThe High elf is a species of being that is usually associated with class, elegance, magic and of course power.\nHence, such qualities accumulate to a grand disgruntled vexation by the common man. As a usual high elf will look down upon 'inferior' races\n\ncultures.\n\nHeaven forbid you hail from 'impurity' such as being a half elf or Adunian. Such is seen as a grand faux par, as it reminds them how they themselves were impure as to mingle with Harrenites.\n\nAs of such they often tend to haul\n\nthemselves up in their cities, denying access to all those whom don't hail from their mighty ancestory.\n\nOn the other hand, when these timid and commonly, rude creatures scurry from their lairs they are often condesending and harsh to all those\n\nnot of their kin.\n\nThis, my friends, is why I have personally taken it upon myself in to muse possible ways to disarm, vex and scare off this beast.\n\nMethod 1:\n\nBe from a mixed heritage, Adunian or half elf. Either will surfice.\n\nThe mere concept of love across races is dead with the high elf, so be spawned from such love is the ultimate vexation as proof that love\n\nconquer's order.\n\nHowever, be wary of mix-ed one. For a high elf may turn hostile. If that is the case be sure to play the racism card. If this fails, arm yourself and be sure to attack before the beast can charge a magical attack!\n\nMethod 2:\n\nIf they commit any actions, mutter 'Typical high elf'. Simple as that, it boils their blood good and proper.\n\nMethod 3:\n\nRemind them of how their past kin have been manipulative, crooked and evil to all whom are not their own. To remind them of their past brings them great tragedy. They may become snide however and claim that it was true and proper. If this\n\nthe case, be sure to verbally put them down and destroy their argument.\n\nMethod 4:\n\nDistribute this guide.\n\nMethod 5:\n\nA good old punch.", ""),
        StaticBook("How2KillMonsters", "§b[Ghost] The Eternal Librarian", "Monsters\n        and\n   How to Defeat\n        Them\n\n    by Seth Calith\n\nMonsters roam our lands, and a good fighter has to know how to repel them as well as their strengths and weaknesses. In this book, the reader will find a guide on how to defeat each beast using either a bow or a sword.\n\nZombies\nZombies are creatures that, wanting to attack, follow you around. With that knowledge, a bow is a useful tool to defeat these monsters. The key to this fight is charging a shot in your bow while running. Once it is charged, shoot the arrow to\n\nhit it while still charging another arrow.\nIf it is of your preference to use a sword, you can take advantage of the Zombie’s low terrain-calculation properties. Try to stand higher than its head so that it is unable to strike you.\n\nSkeletons\nThe average skeleton is not as strong as the zombie, yet deadlier because of his fine use of the art of archery and bowmastery. It is recommended to use a sword against such creatures since they are bad in close combat and can only\n\nshoot at a determined rate.\nTo do such, circle around it fast enough so you can avoid its arrows, which is not recommended unless you are wearing good armor. When it fires, sprint towards it and slash him as hard as you can. With an average iron sword\n\nand a good reaction, you can defeat it while only taking one arrow, probably to the knee, due to its position upon death. If you can’t dispose of these requirements, you will have to study its rapidness of shot or withstand some more arrows, which is not\n\nrecommended unless you are wearing good armor.\nFor profficient bow-wielders, a duel can be had against one of these creatures. One should find a place to cover oneself and do so. When it shoots, wait for the sound of the arrow to crash against your\n\nhiding place and leave it. Shoot it once with a good aim and hide again. It will surrender sooner or later.\n\nBlazes\nThe blazes’s combat is not very different of the skeleton's, and with the blaze shooting fireballs instead of arrows, three at a time. If using a sword, follow the steps for the skeleton with a slight change. Wait for three shots to be fired,\n\nnot one, and make sure you don’t step on the fires set ablaze by the blaze itself. Do a similar thing with the bow. You can know when he is about to shoot because it fires up.\n\nSlimes\nSlimes come in various sizes, and upon death they divide into smaller ones. Use a bow to defeat all but the smallest, that are inoffensive and can be easily defeated with a sword.\n\nEnderbeings\nThese are strange beasts. They can move from a place to another in a blink, known as teleporting. When fighting one, the only tip I can give you is to jump in some water. Oddly, these beasts are hurt by it, so it will die in its chase.", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide to Reason", "§bGrigor Grandaxe", "A Guide to Reason. A Philisophical Bestseller by Grigor Grandaxe.\n\nHey you.\nYeah You.\nWhat do you know about Philsophy? Here in this book I will give you statements to help you to reson with yourself, to think and\n\nto reflect on actions based on the Philosophical premises that I will give to you.\n\nInstustions for use of this book:\n1. Open this book\n2. Follow the guidelines of each statement\n3. Keep it to one statement a day\n\nso that you may have the designed, 10 day reading period here, weather you read this at church, at work, in bed or at home.\n\nOn the next page your journey through Philoposphy will begin.\n---->\n\nDay One, Statement One.\n\"Progress just means bad things happen faster.\" - Grigor Grandax.\n\nConsider the connotations of this statement and its effect on you and your life, are bad things happening to you?\n\nDay Two, Statement Two.\n\"I think therefore I am.\"\n\nWHat do you want to be? HAve you tried to be this? Mabye you are all you want to be, and if so have you considered how you got there?\n\nDay Three, Statement Three.\n\"I can't go back to yesterday, because I was a different person then.\"\n\nHow much have you changed since yesterday? since last week? last year?\n\nDay 4, Statement 4.\n\"Don't bitw off more than you can chew because nobody looks attractive spitting it out\"\n\nWho has strived for something so far out of their reach they injure themselves whilst striving for it?\n\nDay 5, Statement 5.\n\"All is fair in love and war.\"\n\nThink on this statement for yourself and apply its Philosophy to your life. It has important conotations.\n\nDay 6-10\nPlease purchase Part Two of the Grigor Grandaxe Philosophy\nReading Plan for the added statements, remeber you will become a better persons if you apply the Philosophies of this book.", ""),
        StaticBook("HowToNotAnnoy", "§bMorgan Keerie", "How to not be annoying for dummies\n\nBy Morgan\n'The Annoying One'\n\nIF THIS BOOK IS STOLEN GIVE IT THE FUCK BACK OR I WILL FUCKING FUCK FUCKETY FUCK YOU UP.\n\nHELLO THERE!\nSooooo, you wantta' know how to not be annoying eh?\n\nWell, here is a brief introduction to what 'being annoying' is, through self research I have found out about this SHIT!\n\nWHAT IS ANNOYING?\nWhen people call you annoying, it can mean multiple things.\n\n1. They naturally need to hate someone, you seemed to be defined into the 'everyone hates you' category.\n\n2. You've introduced yourself too wrongly for their standards so now they are going to keep a deep hatred for you, even if you try to change.\n\n3. You interrupted their discussion (If they have a partner)\n\n4. You interrupted their mediation (If they are alone)\n\n5. You naturally do not fit into their friendship category, these categories may include:\nSpooky,\nAnti-Spook\nWeirdo\nMage.\n\nWHY DO PEOPLE HATE YOU?\n\nPersonally I find that people use me as a punching bag, this is one of the things you can be happy about! People may bully you just to make them - Nicer!\n\nWHAT TO DO WHEN YOU ARE TOLD TO KILL YOURSELF\n\n\nTake in deep breaths, ignore Cru-People who say this to you, and continue on living, show those -MEANIES whose boss!\n\nREMEMBERING WHO YOU ARE\n\nYour personality is yours, shifting personalities is a hard task, people will make it even harder, just try to tone it down, self-correction and third-party correction is a beautiful method of resolving this issue.\n\nHOW TO NOT ACT WHEN AROUND PEOPLE:\n\nOverly loud\n\nFourth Wall breaking\n\nAsking too many questions\n\nBeing dumb\n\nAnything that may annoy or irritate\n\nWHAT IS ANNOYING?\nAnything can be annoying, just try your best, subtlely and in a shadowlike manner copy those around you, this will help you fit into your surroundings and befriend people like Cru--Mages.\n\nA small list of personal discoveries that can irritate, annoy, aggrovate, piss off, cause assault or bodily harm:\n\n1. Talking too much.\n2. Asking for magic.\n3. Asking for friendship.\n4. Asking questions.\n\n5. Being loud\n6. Copying\n7. Earwigging without joining a disucssion\n8. Joining a discussion after earwigging too long\n9. Joining a conversation naturally.\n10. Being an asshole.\n11. Hitting on people\n\n12. Asking relationship status\n13. Asking private questions\n14. Screaming\n15. Asking about how not to be annoying\n16. Insulting people\n17. Talking back after being insulted\n18. Not talking back after being insulted\n19. Not understanding something\n\n20. Understanding but not showing you understand something\n21. Being yourself\n22. Being not yourself.\n23. Trying to be someone else.\n24. Not trying to be someone else.\n25. Not being dead\n26. Being alive\n27. Being Dead\n28. Being real\n29. Not being real\n\n30. Opening your mouth\n31. Backchatting powerful mages.\n32. Backchatting Oreners\n33. Not backchatting powerful mages\n34. Not backchatting Oreners\n35. Not backchatting\n36. Backchatting\n37. Having one eye\n38. Having two eyes\n\n39. Not knowing something because they haven't told you about this something\n40. Knowing something without being told by the person this something\n41. Being different\n42. Being alike\n43. Being you.\n44. Not finishing things\n45. Finishing things\n\nTHANK YOU FOR READING, IF YOU WOULD LIKE TO CONTACT THE AUTHOR PLEASE FUCKING DON'T BECAUSE I DON'T WANT TO DIE\n\n-Morgan.", ""),
        StaticBook("Just a Prank", "Azureth", "There are many ways to pester your friends.\nOr, you know, random people on the street.\nPranks are a fun passtime. However, they can be taken too far. This is recommended for your enemies, or simply people you don't like.\n\n-Shadeleaf-\nShadeleaf is a good pranking material. Feed someone a couple of these leaves and they'll be wandering into the forest, chasing after an invisible fairy.\n\n-Tippen's Stench-\nThe roots of a Tippen's root smell almost as bad as an Olog. This makes them perfect for pranking! Stuff a couple of these into someone's clothes or something.\nDwarf's pumpkin is a good subsitute.\n\n-Blazing Garden-\nHave an unsavory neighbor, or just like to screw with people's lives? The fire flower is for you! They burst into flames when they mature. Perfect for burning down gardens... or homes.\n\n-Miner's Death-\nA more deadly 'prank', Miner's Death can kill someone. Do I need to say anything more?\n\n-House on Fire-\nWhat's better than scarring kids for life? Nothing! Now you can scar some children, too! Pretend to set their homes on fire by filling it with smoke. How? I don't know.\n\n-Public Bombing-\nYou can scare the living daylights out of people by pretending to be a suicide bomber. Strap a fake explosive to your chest, and have fun!\n\n-Stabbing-\nWhat a surprise it is to be stabbed in the back! Ha ha! Got you!\n\nThese have only been a few prank ideas. Have fun, fellow pranksters!", ""),
        StaticBook("A", "Rurikk", "*the journal in your hands is covered with tanned leather and tied shut with a leather chord, branded upon the cover is: \"A Huntsman's Guide to Surviving the Wilderness\"\n\nIntro:\n\nHello everyone, this book was written by an experienced survivalist in hopes that all who wish to venture out into the wilds will be prepared for the trials and hardships they may face along the way.\n\nAfter reading this booklet you will\n\nsurvive on your own without any extra aid from outside sources. \n\nNow let us begin then.\n\nChapter One \"What You\nWill Need\":\n\nThe most important items that a survivalist needs to well... survive, are the tools that he/she either finds or brings with him/her on the way to their journey into the wilds.\n\nHere is a list of helpful items:\n\n1. Flint & Steel\n2. A Small Hatchet\n3. Preserving Salts\n4. Needle and Thread\n5. Skinning Knife\n6. Waterproofed Satchel\n7. Small Fishing Hook\n8. Sturdy Clothing\n9. Sufficient Rations\n\nChapter Two \"What To Expect\":\n\nOnce you have acquired all the supplies listed in the previous chapter you are now ready to begin your journey.\n\nFirst things first, to survive in the wilds you need to know at least a basic background of the\n\nenvironment you plan on venturing into, such as weather patterns, what kinds of vegetation grows in the region, as well as the different beasts that make their home in the area.\n\nRemember to study maps and acquire as much information about the region\n\npossible before you decide to make the trip. Failing to do so could result in dismemberment or even death.\n\nOnce you have done your research and acquired all of your supplies for the trek into the unknown, you will finally be ready to begin.\n\nChapter Three \"Setting Up Camp\"\n\nIn this chapter you will learn the basics of setting up a safe and reliable camp site to live in during your stay in the wilderness.\n\nOnce you have found a suitable place to set up camp, you need to make\n\nsure that the area you have picked is in fact a safe place to stay in. To do so, please check off everything on this list:\n\n1. Is it dry and warm?\n2. Does it protect you from the elements?\n3. Is it close to a source of water?\n4. Can you e\n\nlost?\n5. Does it protect you from unwanted visitors?\n\nIf all of the above checks off as okay, then you have done a great job in picking out a location for your campsite!\n\nChapter Four \"Exploring The Wilderness\"\n\nSo far so good, if you've gotten this far then that means you haven't killed yourself yet. Good job!\n\nIn this chapter we will be going over the basics of wilderness exploration.\n\nWhen an experienced survivalist arrives in uncharted lands, they usually do one or more of these things listed:\n\n1. Find a high place and survey the lands before you, taking notes of key land marks in the immediate area.\n\n2. Preparing themselves for long treks away from the safety of their camps, make sure to pack extra food, you may be away from home for a while!\n\n3. Preparing for all possible outcomes, make sure to think of everything that could happen while you are\n\nfrom the camp; things such as being captured by jungle pigmy's to the occasional bear destroying your camp can easily be prevented if you just prepare ahead of time.\n\nCarrying out with at least one of these tips can make your life out in the wilderne\n\nmuch easier, and could possibly save your life.\n\nChapter Five \"Returning Home\":\n\nCongratulations, you've survived your trip and are ready to break camp and return home with a multitude of new stories from your trip.\n\nRemember that when you are ready to leave to make sure you try to leave\n\nthings just as they were when you first arrived at the location you chose for your camp.\n\nOnce you have finished returning things as they once were, you can then begin to journey back home. Make sure not to forget any trinkets or trophies that you mi\n\nhave found while exploring the wilderness!\n\nThanks for reading\n\nA little bit about the Author:\n\nCharles Silverblade:\nCharles was born in the small farming town of Riven, where his cousin Uthor Silverblade helped to raise him and teach him to become a fine young man in terms of Oren society. When he turned 18\n\nage, he enlisted in the Oren Military as a conscript and quickly ascended the ranks of hierarchy in the military until he finally acquired the title of Ser and received Knighthood in the Order of the Red Dragon. Charles now lives with his Wife and four\n\nchildren with the rest of the Silverblade family who reside in the Duchy of Furnestock.", ""),
        StaticBook("Witcher's Inform", "§bSylas von Schummer", "A Witch-Hunter's Informational \n\nBy Sylas von Schummer.\n\nOne's work of slaying the dead can oftemtimes prove annoying and time consuming, dragging one from the welcoming hearth at home, from their woman in bed, out into a murky and desolate swamp to slay some damned beast.\n\nIt's not commomplace to find gen\n\nenjoyment in the surroundings of your evershifting workplace, but hopefully this simple guide will assist in the actual dispatching of the creature you're searching for.\n\n-- Part One ---\n\nWalking Dead, Ghouls\nThe most basic form of a damned creature, returned from the afterlife in their previous ever-decaying body. These creatures are oftentimes rather powerful despite their rotting beings, and come with an inate\n\nto pain from standard blades. It is reccomended to use Aurum, fire, and blunt weaponry to slay the creature. When faced off alone a Ghoul is generally rather easy to dispatch, however it is common to find them in groups, and a situtation like such\n\nbecomes far more dangerous, as numbers will overwhelm you.\n\nLich, and Darkstalkers\nLiches are the revived souls of the dead via arcane energy by a necromancer. They tend to prove highly intelligent and agressive, using manipulation and murder to\n\nwhatever end they seek. When destroyed, like most dead a Lich will return to life to haunt and kill again, the only known way to end a Lich's life is to find it's phylactery. A phylactery is any object created to hold the Lich's soul, usually found as a\n\ngemstone or locket, variety of jewlery and the like, it however has been known for a phylactery to be placed within a tree, or other unexpected objects. Darkstalkers, unlike Liches are found wearing heavy armour head to toe, their prime focus in regards\n\nto combat is with melee weaponry, whereas a Lich shall oftentimes use magic since their focus is much harder to break than a mortal mage. Darkstalkers are known to have draining spells used to rip the very lifeforce from your body. To slay a Darkstalker\n\nyou must find it's phylacrery.\n\nWraiths, Ash-kin\nWraiths are shadowy, smog like creatures born of hatred and pure evil. They come in two forms, one haunting a specific area that it is bound to, another free and independant, roaming the countrysid\n\nat will. They appear as black swirling masses of dark material, usually floating above the ground. They have the capability to cast powerful dark and voidal magics, and wield standard weaponry. They are most susceptible to aurum weaponry and holy magics.\n\nIt is also rumored that certain wraiths are capable of raising dead around them to fight on their behalf, this however is not confirmed.\n\nDreadknights\nBorn of blood magic, a Dreadknight is a walking suit of intelligent sentient armour, born to ki\n\nextremely dangerous, it is reccomended to avoid fighting them without Holy mage assistance, or with a large group armed with blunt aurum weaponry.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ho", "§bSammy \"Mungo\"", "How to be a Silvertongued Devil- By Mungo the Bandit.\n\nIn life you may come upon times where reaching for your sword may not be the most ideal way to go, you may not be the best fighter, or you simply can't speak for your life, hopefully, this guide\n\nsorts may assist you in swindling, lying, persuading and overall being a great talker. Now, me being me, I was born with the natural talent of making people absolutely adore me, whether this was being brought up in a tevern or my mother being\n\nquite a social escort, I cannot say, but what I can say is that this skill of mine has gotten me out of many  tight situations and into many fair maidens' dreams. But, enough of me glamourizing myself, I'll try to keep this book short and to the point.\n\n1.\nBe as polite as can be without seeming as if you want to kiss someone's backside, being polite leads to people liking you, and even giving you free things such as minas and food.\n\n2.\nBe eccentric and posh with your words. This of course excludes Orcs, they will most likely cave your face in if you use anything more complicated than six letter words. Use words such as indeed, gent, gentleman, kind, fine and so on, this\n\nmay lead to some thinking you a pompous whoreson, but to others you will seem a much more upper class gent or lady than you actually are, helping you achieve your goals whether it be getting that promosion, lying, succesfully conning,\n\nor simply being all the talk at spiffing Balls.\n\n3.\nSeem lighthearted, relaxed and calm, the calmer and more lighthearted you are, the more it will rub off on whoever you're trying to swindle, leading them to dropping their guard, taking a liking of you, or simply another way to seem that\n\nyou have no idea why there's a dead body infront of you while you hold a bloody knife, you just found it there of course.\n\n4.\nBe kind, even if it might not be in your nature, seeming like a kind person will help you in many ways, tricking people, this will lead to you making unlikely allies, you'll have more sway to your word, and if it comes to a tavern brawl\n\neveryone will believe you when you say you didn't start it.\n\n5.\nLast, but not least, be charismatic, even if you're quite the reserved person, this will inspire those around you, and lead to people believing your word over others.\n\nAnd so, that ends my short guide to being a charming and cunning criminal such as myself, whether you use it for good or evil, is your choice, I was just bored in the corner of a tavern waiting for someone to play some blackjack.\n\n-Signed, Mungo, the Charming Bandit.", ""),
        StaticBook("How To Fish", "Gargled", "How To Fish\n\n1) Make A Rod\n\n2) Put bait on the end of it!\n\n3) Find a pond, lake, or ocean!\n\n4) Cast your line by holding the spinner, releasing the hold, and throwing your rod forward, but don't actually throw your rod!\n\n5) Wait patiently. If your cast is bad, reel it back in using the reeler. Spin it clockwise. \n\n6) If you catch a fish, use a cloth or towel to grab it, and carefully remove the hook from its mouth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Gaide te Fizhin", "§bYat'in", "--- Te Gobo's riate ---\n\n*Scribbles of a fishing pole casted in to the water would cover the front page*\n\n\"Et taks tik wen fizhin. Wen lat i'd fizhin mak zur te hoald vary zill. \n\n*A picture of Yat'in fishing with for hours, showing no movement at all*\n\nEevn te zligtezt movmant wail zcare te fizhi awae.\n\n*A diagram of a Fishing Net and the multitude of nots used in making it would be shown. Then a picture of it being thrown by Yat'in would be drawn below*\n\nTe must efficint wae te gat moest fizhi, i;d by usin azh net. Te net wail set an captur te fizhi.\n\nAlwaiz attend to te net oar it cud rip.", ""),
        StaticBook("Lord of the Lies", "§bJames H. Kyd", "Lord of the Lies\n\n\n\n\nA guide to lying, written by:\n\nJ.H.K.\n\n\n\n\n To successfully lie to another, one must first succesfully lie to themself.\n\n Lying- is it alright? Is it morally justifiable? Chances are, that if you are reading this, you've made up your mind. I am not writing this to debate whether lying is write or wrong, but to teach you, the reader, how to do it properly.\n\nPart One - The Lie\n\n First, you must know what you are going to lie about. You should then consider the effects of your lie, and how things may turn out. This may sound simple, but it is a common mistake made by amateur liars.\n\n Always remember to think ahead before you act. \"Is your lie believable?\" \"What may be the consequences of this lie in the future?\" Are questions you should ask yourself before lying.\n\nPart Two - Lying to Yourself\n\n To be a succesful liar, you must first lie to yourself. After all, if you don't even believe yourself, who will? This may not make much sense, but you must make an effort to convince even yourself that what you\n\nsay is true. Most likely, you will not be able to completely convince yourself through conventional means, but if you cannot confidently lie to another's face, then you should not lie at all.\n\nPart Three - Lying to Another\n\n Now comes the actual act of lying. Be aware not to show any nervousness through physical movement, or as I like to call, 'body language', or in your speech. After all, for all YOU know, you're not lying at all. You're\n\ntelling what you know and believe to be true. Act casually, as if it were just any other day.\n\nConclusion\n\n This concludes my guide to lying. I hope my instruction suits you well, but of course I cannot guerantee your success. That solely depends on YOU. I have provided the knowledge, so you must provide the appliance.\n\nOther Notes\n\n There may be an elaborated volume soon enough.\n\n[!]The paper is elegantly and neatly signed.\n\n\n\n\nJ.H.K.", ""),
        StaticBook("Combat: Volume I", "§bGerald Elgan", "===================\n\n\nMarked Combat:\nVolume I\n\nTranscribed by\nGerald Elgan\n\n\n\n\n==================\n\nThe Magical Versus the Mundane- The Knight's Way of Defense Against the Supernatural:\n===================Through the ages, mankind has faced countless threats, both mundane and magical. The wars against the undead have taught us techniques and-\n\n\n===================countermeasures that can be- with ample experience, skill and prayer- successfully utilized against the unholy and the profane.\n\n\n===================What is Recommended:\n-Numbers\n-Ranged Weaponry\n-Light Armor\n\nExcerpt taken from \"The Guide to Hunting Mages\"\n\nMarked Combat\n===================Combat Basics:\n------------\nThe 3 Stances\nHigh- Form is leaned in, knees bent. Arms arced in pre-wind-up. Blade is to be pointed skyward.\nReferred to as the \"Counter\" stance. Used in an effort to -\n\n\n===================counter-act movements from mid-guard and stanceless efforts.\nMid- Form is relaxed, blade pommel is parallel to one's waistline. Knees bent and arms relaxed. Known as the \"Assaulting\" stance.\n\n\n===================Attacks vary on situation, be in Arc or thrust. Used to counter low stance and when assaulting shielded or untrained foes.\nLow- Form is lowered, knees bent, body leaned in. The arms are left in a -\n\n\n===================half-wind-up with the blade parallel to the flooring. Referred to as, \"Wounding\", stance. Used to counteract High-guard, spearmen and is only used to hinder movement or knock a foe off balance. This stance is used with two handed.\n\nMovement\n===================When in combat, keep the foe in your direct line of sight. Movements are circular in nature, there are to be no steps taken forward or backward, instead side-step in.\n\nMovement, cont.\n===================When Assaulting, nature may say rush the target head on, instead, aim to the target's right or left with movements. Aim to strike the target and take place on either flank or rear of the target. Should the target-\n\nMovement, cont.\n===================continue to stand after the inital blow, aim for immediate execution, striking to either the neck or lower-spine.\n\nMovement, cont.\n==================\nWhen countering, side-step, parry or retaliate. Know the range of the Foe's weapon, if the range of your own counter-acts that of the enemy's, retaliate with side-step, aiming to either cleave limb or behead the f\n\nMovement, cont.\n===================Should the weapon be lesser or equivalent, parry and close the gap. The strike won't likely be lethal. Instead, aim to disarm or hinder.\n\nCombat Stance\n===================So, think of the three stances as a game of Rock, Paper, Scissors. When on even grounds, and not taking situation at hand, the three stances are as such\nHigh-Rock\nMid- Scissors\nLow-Paper\n\nCombat Stance, cont.\n===================When starting combat, take stance. Do not suddenly switch stance, since it exposes yourself, parry or sidestep while shifting. Shifting to counter will result in a half stance, which is a stance of valuable parri", ""),
        StaticBook("A. by A. (VOL3)", "§bAshur", "===================Archery by Ashur\nVOL III: Hunting \n===================\n\n*The cover page depicts a Dark Elf concealed behind low brush, nocking an arrow while herds of swine graze in the valley before him.*\n\nI am Ashur Uilosson of Laurelin, once Prince of the Holy Princedom of Malinor. My eyes have seen the rise and fall of kingdoms, races, and entire worlds. I can tell you from experience that life as we know it has few constants. Archery is one of them.\n\nHunting is archery's most valuable application. It provides food for yourself and others, hides to tan and apply as raw material, it sharpens the senses... and if caught somewhere you ought not be, it provides a decent excuse.\n\nBefore setting out, you should have solid knowledge of the terrain and local life. Unfamiliar plants and animals alike can spell disaster for the inexperienced hunter, so consult with a local expert beforehand. Maps are a bonus, if available.\n\nWhether your excursion is 8 hours or 8 days, you should be prepared to handle any malfunction in your equipment, yet light enough with your gear to move nimbly across the landscape. Consider this list as a starting guide:\n\n-Arrows (10 x day)\n-Boots\n-Bowstring (x2)\n-Cloak\n-Compass\n-Flint & Steel\n-Foods (dried)\n-Gloves\n-Map\n-Pack\n-Quiver\n-Rain protection\n-Skinning knife\n\n-Sleep system (sack, pad, rain sheet)\n-Socks (x2 pair)\n-Spare arrowheads\n-Spare fletchings\n-Spare twine\n-Tinder supply (fire)\n-Water supply (3 liters x day)\n\nThis is by no means definitive. Change and adapt as you see fit.\n\nThe first style of hunting I will cover is \"Stationary\", commonly used to survey a single location or plot of land over time. This requires more preparation but arguably yields the most material for the hunter, given practice and training.\n\nWhen surveying land as possible hunting ground, you should ask yourself questions:\n\n--How far is the nearest town, on foot or by horse?\n--Do others use this land?\n--How difficult is the terrain?\n\n--Is my prey small enough to manage by myself, or do I need others?\n--Are there any hostile plants or animals I should be aware of?\n--Are there any temples/shrines to unholy gods that will possess me? (I'm serious, by the way.)\n\nYou should judge the land based on where and how you can position two constructs: the FUNNEL, and the STAND.\n\nFUNNELs are landmarks, natural or manmade, that force wildlife down a certain path, \"funneling\" them a specific direction.\n\nSTANDs are locations for you to operate out of while hunting. The tried-and-true method is an elevated wooden platform reached via ladder, which gives you an aerial view of the funnels you're observing. Also good against bandits.\n\nBefore setting out for your trek, however, you must remove the scent from yourself and all other equipment. Unfamiliar scents will doom you to ill results, so you must thoroughly embrace an easily-accessible scent: smoke. Smoke yourself and your gear.\n\nOnce you've covered your scent, set out for your stand with several hours before your prey is most active. Moving efficiently through the wilderness is a topic worthy of several books, but I'll summarize the key tenants here:\n\n--When walking, keep your weight on the back foot, stepping with the outer ridge of your feet and slowly rolling inwards.\n--If you make a loud noise, freeze completely for at least 5 minutes. The animals are watching you, more than likely.\n\n--Take your time. There's no rush, assuming you planned properly.\n-Scramble your steps rather than walking at a steady pace. The normal walking cadence of a hunter will scare off everything in sight. Be creative.\n\nOnce you've arrived, take the time to get yourself comfortable and prepared. It may be several hours before your prey is out and about. Remember to keep noise to a minimum, and don't do anything to spread unfamiliar scents in the area.\n\nOnce your prey is in sight, resist the urge to attempt a kill immediately. Take the time to observe its movements - what is it doing? Are there others near? Is it acting odd? The animsl may know something you don't, and observation will reveal it to you.\n\nIf practicable, a shot to the brain will provide the cleanest and most efficient kill. Otherwise, aim for the \"boiler room\" - the heart and lungs. Merciful kills provide the least suffering for the animal, and the least effort to recover its body.\n\nBeware, however, the \"instant drop\", when your prey collapses immediately when struck. It may simply be in shock, only to recover and lash out when you approach. If this happens, wait a few minutes and watch the beastie before moving to claim it.\n\nMore often than not, however, your prey will travel for several meters before meeting its demise. For this reason, mentally mark the exact location where you shot the animal before moving there. Firing another arrow as a mark may be useful for novices.\n\nOnce you find the location, use all of your senses to find its blood trail. Don't just look on the earth! Low brush may bear signs of passage. Listen for movement or cries. Check for the smell of blood or urine. See if its tracks deteriorate over time.\n\nOnce you find the corpse, don't succumb to the temptation of waltzing up and poking it to check for life. For example, if the thing's eyes are closed, it is almost certainly still alive. A blade or bolt to the jugular will mercifully end its suffering.\n\nRecovery of the animal should be planned out in advance. You should strive to harvest as much of the animal as you can, so if you are hunting prey too large to handle by yourself... bring more hunters. A simple solution to a simple problem.\n\nMy recommendation would be to bring the entire animal with you, all parts included, and dissect it in the comfort of your home. Brains are used for tanning, the organs can be eaten or sold, the meat can be cooked, and so forth. Be meticulous. Use it all.\n\n-=MOBILE HUNTING=-\n\nThis skill requires FAR more practice and knowledge, covering multiple topics: tracking, animal lore, concealment, and geography among them. Hunting in this manner is used when on the move... or the run, more accurately.\n\nDisguising yourself and your signs becomes paramount. Interweave local fauna with your clothing and avoid situations where you may stand out - for example, if you stand on a ridge and your prey is below, your body is easily visible on the horizon.\n\nConsider moving through regions once, and only once, to minimize your scent and impact.\n\nTruly, your goal with mobile hunting is not to discover prey, but SIGNS of prey, and follow them to their makers. This requires discretion and attention to detail.\n\nAs previously stated, you should find a local expert of the land and ask for his wisdom on local hunting grounds, animal behavior, any local banditry, and so forth. This will set you leagues above the other whelps out hunting for the same herd as you.\n\nThis is only the briefest of introductions to hunting with the bow and arrow, and while secondhand experiences are helpful for the student, the only true way to learn is practice, constantly and repeatedly. I wish you luck with your excursions.", ""),
        StaticBook("A. by A. (VOL2)", "§bAshur", "===================Archery by Ashur\nVOL II:\nApplied Skills & Training\n===================\n\n*Here lies an illustration of a Dark Elf, instructing four younger elves as they practice on an archery range.*\n\nI am Ashur Uilosson of Laurelin, once Prince of the Holy Princedom of Malinor. My eyes have seen the rise and fall of kingdoms, races, and entire worlds. I can tell you from experience that life as we know it has few constants. Archery is one of them.\n\nOnce the aspiring bowman has familiarized themselves with proper creation and upkeep of the bow, as detailed in Volume I, the next obvious step is learning how to be effective with one. This is far simpler to write on paper than to actually practice.\n\nThese rules are geared towards expanding your knowledge and skills, and not a single one should be skipped. I can say from centuries of experience that these tenants will always hold true, given enough time and training.\n\n--STANCE\nYou should be standing with your chest sideways, in perspective with your target. Right-handed shooters (the hand you grip the arrow with) should face the right, and the reverse for left-handed archers.\n\n--STANCE, CONT.\nSpace your feet to shoulder width, rotating them so they point directly in line with your body - facing to the right or left. Stand straight, naturally aligning your spine, and rotate your chin over the shoulder (or as close as you can.)\n\n--STANCE, CONT.\nRotate your hips so they are tucked or rolled under your upper body. This flattens your lower back, which allows you to lower your chest and ribs downward towards your stomach. Also push your shoulders downward.\n\n--STANCE, CONT.\nWhen practicing, you should go through these steps like a checklist, every single time you fire an arrow. Repetitions develop muscle memory, and muscle memory will separate you from the whelp fighting on the other side.\n\n--STANCE, CONT.\nStay focused and sharp while practicing. Initially, you should fire 30 arrows in one session before ending for the day. With each successful day, add more arrows, minding your stance with every single one. Remember: muscle memory.\n\n--NOCKING\nEach archer has their own style when nocking the arrow to the string, and there is no single doctrine for this manuever. This is simply something you must practice until it flows for you, which is uncomfortable at first. Persevere.\n\n--NOCKING, CONT.\nThe nock of the arrow should /snap/ onto the string the same way and the same amount of force, with every single arrow. This is why handcrafting your arrows is so important! You must build them to your specific bowstring.\n\n--NOCKING, CONT.\nNocks that fit differently, even by a little, will influence the arrow's flight. Loose nocks might indicate that your center serving is compressed and needs replacement. Adjust your equipment as such, ensuring the best for your gear.\n\n--GRIP\nThe grip of the bow should sit in the web of your hand, between your thumb and index finger. Position your thumb so that it points at your target when the bow is raised. Then, relax your other fingers as they wrap 'round the grip.\n\n--GRIP, CONT.\nWhen the bow is raised, the knuckles on the arrow side should create a 45 degree angle. The bow hand must remain absolutely still through the entire shot process.\n\nNow, onto your bowstring hand.\n\n--GRIP, CONT.\nGently wrap the first 3 fingers of your bowstring hand below the arrow shaft. The string should be at the first groove of the fingers, with the index finger pushed up against the dock of the arrow. Your drawing hand must be relaxed and flat.\n\n--SETUP\nWith a proper grip prepared, extend the bow-arm forward, its elbow rotated vertically. The forearm of your bowstring hand should remain as close to, or parallel to, the arrow during the next action.\n\n--SETUP, CONT.\nRaise the bow-arm slightly above nose level, pointing towards your target. As you do so, rotate your chest and shoulders so your upper body is parallel to the arrow. The bowstring hand should be raised to nose level as well.\n\n--SETUP, CONT.\nThe bow-arm's elbow should be rotated to the inside joint at the elbow is straight up and down.\n\nNote that you still haven't pulled the arrow back. This comes next! Be patient and mindful. Every step counts.\n\n--DRAWING\nDraw the bowstring back towards the side of your face, ending in a position where your index finger rests at the far corner of your mouth. Move your drawing arm back and down as far as possible. Picture your shoulder blade rotating.\n\n--ANCHOR\nPoint your thumb down into the palm of your hand, and fold your little finger toward the palm as well. Press your hand snug against the side of your face. Note that the bowstring should be located just off the side of your nose.\n\n--ANCHOR, CONT.\nYour anchor position is when you are primed to fire, holding the whole draw weight of the bow. It must be EXACTLY THE SAME, every single time you do it, if you want consistency in your archery. Practice constantly. Obviously.\n\n--TRANSFER\nNow you will move the draw weight from your arms and shoulders, into your back. Align the bow arm and shoulder through your chest to be in-line with the drawing arm shoulder. Rotating your upper torso helps here.\n\n--TRANSFER, CONT.\nMove your drawing arm elbow directly behind the arrow, holding this position with your back muscles. The forearm and the back of your drawing hand should be relaxed.\n\nBy doing this, you free your arms of unneeded agony.\n\n--AIMING\nLook down the shaft of the arrow, placing the point on the target, also using your thumb as a reference. Quickly check your form: weight evenly distributed? Hips over your knees and feet? Chest down? Lower back flat?\n\n--AIMING, CONT.\nCarefully sight up the bowstring and line it up with the center of the bow limbs. Remember that by this point, your back muscles should be supporting the bulk of the draw weight.\n\n--FIRING\nBegin the release process by expanding from the center of the chest, outward, towards your shoulders. At the same time, allow the bowstring to leave your fingers. Pushing it slightly may help you when learning.\n\n--FIRING, CONT.\nOpen the fingers in a crisp but smooth motion. If you slowly open your fingers and let it roll off, you risk the arrow deviating from the path. Snap the fingers open and let it fly straight.\n\n--FIRING, CONT.\nContinue the expansion process by letting your chest expand, increasing the intensity of your back muscles at the same time. Using the diaphragm here is a helpful aid when first learning to harness the lower muscles.\n\n--FOLLOW-THROUGH\nThere is a minute, but very much real, period of time inbetween the arrow's release and when the arrow fully leaves the bow. If you muck about with your stance during this moment, your arrow will fly falsely, and do you discredit.\n\n--FOLLOW-THROUGH, CONT.\nContinue to engage the back muscles. Your drawing hand should move straight back along the side of your dace, stopping slightly below and behind the ear. The bow arm should keep the bow completely still. Remain until arrow leaves.\n\nThese are the steps to success as an archer. There are no hidden secrets here - the path to skill only asks diligence and patience. Even if you are not naturally inclined towards the art of archery, your dedication and practice will supercede\n\n--natural talents by far.\n\nPractice is the only way. Find a target, prepare your tools, and begin immediately. The best time to practice was yesterday, and the second best time is right now.", ""),
        StaticBook("A. by A. (VOL1)", "§bAshur", "===================Archery by Ashur\nVOL I:\nCreation & Manufacture\n===================\n\n*A magnificent drawing is depicted of a Dark Elf ranger, standing amidst numerous bodies of undead thralls.*\n\nI am Ashur Uilosson of Laurelin, once Prince of the Holy Princedom of Malinor. My eyes have seen the rise and fall of kingdoms, races, and entire worlds. I can tell you from experience that life as we know it has few constants.\n\nArchery is one of them.\n\nArchery's roots trace beyond the first Holy Princedom, to the bands of Wood Elves that used them for hunting and defense. While each race has adapted the tool to their own devices, the art of the bow and arrow has several uses, to include:\n\n-- Hunting of small and large game\n\n-- Battle and warfare\n\n-- Competitive sport\n\n-- Exercise of the chest, shoulder, arm, and hand musculature\n\n-- Wooing the attractive sex\n\nThe new bowman should devote their time to learning the upkeep and components of their tool. Many owners simply purchase a bow from a merchant and leave it to rot in a chest, only to experience failure.\n\nStudy these terms:\n\nBACK - The side of the bow facing away from you, and towards the target.\n\nBELLY - The side of the bow facing towards you when properly gripped.\n\nBOWSTRING - A woven cord of varying material attached at the limb tips.\n\nBRACE HEIGHT - The location in the bowstring where you nock (place) your arrow.\n\nCENTER SERVING - A thicker portion of the bowstring, either reinforced material or a sleeve, centered in the middle of the string. Used for reinforcement.\n\nEND SERVING - Same as the center serving, but on the ends of the bowstring. The loops of the string are typically made from these.\n\nLIMB TIP - The far end of the bow, usually shaped like an arrowhead with a narrow base for the bowstring's loop.\n\nLOWER LIMB - The bottom half of the bow.\n\nNOCKING POINTS - A pair of beads sometimes placed in the bowstring to mark the center serving. Arrows are nocked between the beads.\n\nSTRING NOCK - The loop on either end of the bowstring, usually made by \"whipping\" or re-weaving the fibres of the end cord back into the string after tying a loop. Made of the end serving.\n\nUPPER LIMP - The top half of the bow.\n\nWhen selecting the wood for the bow, you judge the candidate by two factors: type of wood, and amount of imperfections. Woods vary in texture, strength, and lifespan, and some seemingly feeble flaws in the wood only worsen over time.\n\nConsider oak, lemon tree, hickory, yew, black locust, or teak as a solid hardwood. Some woods are flexible, such as juniper or mulberry. Make sure your wood is completely dry, however; if you must cut it while still green, give it 3-4 weeks to dry out.\n\n1) CURVE\nAll wood has a natural curve. Place your wood on the ground, holding the top tip with one hand, and press lightly against the middle. It will swivel so that its natural belly faces you, and its back faces out. Mark these appropriately.\n\n2) SHAPE\nPlace the bottom end of the bow on your foot, one hand atop the bow, and use a knife to shave (on the belly only) ontil the upper and lower limbs curve the same way. You want it strongest and thickest in the middle, at the handhold.\n\n3) NOTCHES\nCut notches that begin at the sides and curve around toward the belly of the bow. There should be one on each limb, within 2.5 - 5 cm from the tip. They should be just deep enough to hold the string in place without sacrificing integrity.\n\n4) BOWSTRING\nNot stretchy! Suitable materials for string creation are:\n\n-- rawhide\n-- hemp\n-- fishing line\n-- cotton or silk\n-- twine\n\nBut they must be braided, or they will fail.\n\nYou can either braid the strands by hand until they are tight, or you can tie them next to each other on a stick, on both ends. Then twirl the two sticks in opposite directions until the fibres bind together into a solid strand. Experiment!\n\n5) TILLER\nHang the bow upside-down from a limb or rafter and slowly pull the string downwards, watching how your bow reacts. It should stretch comfortably to the length of your arm extended from the shoulder.\n\n6) ARROWS\n*A beautiful diagram of the common hunting arrow is displayed*\n\nARROWHEAD - an attachment to the arrow's point. Metal, rock, glass, bone - all are effective.\n\nFLETCHING - feathers attached below the nock, for stability.\n\nINDEX FLETCHING - a differently-colored fletching that will face outward from the bow, towards you, when nocked.\n\nNOCK - The U-shaped end of the arrow that is tucked into the string.\n\nPOINT - The bare end of the arrow.\n\nSHAFT - The body of the arrow.\n\nArrows should either be half the length of the bow, or the distance between the brace height and middle of the bow when drawn. You can shape arrows by holding them gently above hot coals, then held straight while cooling.\n\nArrowheads can be attached by shaping a U-shaped notch into the point, and shaping the bottom of the arrowhead to fit snugly within. Ensure it's weighted equally on both sides so it doesn't throw off the arrow's flight.\n\n7) STORAGE\nUnstring your bow when not being used, to increase its lifespan. Keep stored in a cool, dry place - or however you can manage. Working folk like you and I don't have the best options sometimes... and we can bend the rules from time to time.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Art of Warp1", "§bDionysus the Akritian", "THE ART OF WAR\n_____________________________\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy Adolf von Manstein\n\nI.Raising An Army\n_____________________________I.In the art of war, the matter of, to say with no exageration of any kind, the most import is levying a force large enough to carry out your campaigns.\n\nII.And so the forces of the realm\n\nmay be divided into these categories: Sergeants, Knights and Squires, Levied Peasantry, Bugher Watches or Militias; Specialised Mercenaries.\n\nIII.When levying knights to your cause, it is not uncommon for a soveriegn king or prince to offer financi\n\nincentives to gentry to take up arms. These may come under movable property of any sort, be it minas, cattle, or otherwise. It must be said this may be financially straining, so it is good for a sovereign, be he in a time where his knights\n\nand squires are needed badly, to offer riches in the form of the possessions in his house. In the practical art of war, where the profit of the sovereign is of importance, we must see this as a last resort. \nIV.For it is well known to be\n\nnot very prestigious. If a king gives his household personal goods such as gold objects, jewelry and weapons, riding horses and destriers, rival princes, dukes, kings and caliphs will see your realm as poor, and you as weak, for you are giving the\n\nhonoured goods of your family.\n\nV.The use of giving enemy riches, which would usually go the sovereign, to knights and squires as a financial reward and incentive is much less of a poor course, however. For you have taken it from the enemy,\n\nat no cost to the prestige of your own house.\n\nVI.Therefore, it may be summarised as this: Financial incentives (and punishments) must be observed to get the best service, and these are preferably\n\nand these are preferably done from minas and loot, rather than your own possessions. For though the knights have an obligation to fight for you, they will do so best with incentive.\n\nVII.A final note is that horses are the most expensive part of a knight’s equipment, and they are prone to disease, death on the battlefield and other losses. Therefore, to the men who have more horses, there must be more pay. It must be added that\n\nthose who are use riding horses such as  palfreys on the march, and then ride destriers and coursers into battle. To these people it must be said, that they have gone out of their way to have more horses, and must be given more wealth. It is also frequent\n\nto replace lost horses out of the commander's purse.\n\nIX.Sergeants are another important force on the battlefield. It is these spearmen and light horsemen who have ensured Oren’s victories for the last few decades.\n\nAny who comes under this category is a man who is not gentry or noble, a mere common man, but one who is a professional soldier, always at the call in the manner of a retinue. For example, most of the Order of Saint Amyas’ footmen count as sergeants.\n\nIX.The sustenance of sergeants is of some, but not of great cost. They only expect low wages, and in some cases can afford their own equipment. Many of them are craftsmen themselves, able to repair and maintain their own spears,\n\nkettle helms, shields and arming swords without interruption.\n\nXI.Their training is well too, but can they match the wealth and training of a knight? Nay, but they may be relied upon well to hold the line well.\n\nIs it little wonder their use is so common in the realm?\n\nX.It may be necessary for the nobility of the realm to pay for the arming and training of these troops, as it has become something of a convention. That is what is expected,\n\nand the expectancy to pay for one’s own equipment will be greeted with hostility. The wise commander and lord sees his own sergeants equipped with his own wealth, which will be greeted with elation.\n\nXII.t is rare to get good sergeants out of a feudal obligation, as is common with levies and knights. Instead, one must ensure the critical task of sending out recruiting parties often and gaining the affection of the people so that they may volunteer.\n\nXIII.These two aforementioned groups form most of the best men besides from mercenaries, and throughout the course of our history the proportion of knights to sergeants has changed. In modern times, it is often 1 knight for every 24 sergeants.\n\nXIV.It is much quicker and easier to raise sergeants, for they are ready and may be called upon. It does well to have a large force of these fellows in case a desperate situation ensues, or to dispute a man of his land without expecting actual fighting.\n\nXV.The city militias and watches are to be rarely called onto the field, mostly used to garrison the various cities of the realm. However, if they are levied, it may be customary to offer rudimentary pay, even of a low sort.\n\nXVI.These men are the quickest to call upon in a levy, for they already have basic training and arms, and merely require calling into arms. It may be said that they can be used to merely boost the number of soldiers on the field, used in a siege,\n\nor to act as auxiliaries of sorts to their more well-equipped and trained counterparts. Many are equipped with crossbows, which are quite simple to use, and used to attack the enemy with missiles.\n\nXVII.It must be said that though the Codes of Saint Edmond (Chivalry) prohibit a mean sacking of cities, the militiamen and sergeants must have their regards. You must forage from the enemy, and loot from civilians.\n\nThese men are not knights, and are not bound by this code. This will be ample payment, and there is little need for additional incentive, should you use them in the field.\n\nXVIII.Levymen form the bulk of your missile troops\n\nand garrisons. Levies must buy their own equipment, and usually are unarmoured and untrained. This is why they are only useful for missile troops. Again, these men need no additional incentive but that which they forage from the enemy.\n\nXIX.Mercenaries allow a sovereign or a marshal to gain troops that are specialised, such as horse archers, light cavalry, missile troops such as crossbowmen, as well as high quality infantry.These men require payment to such a degree\n\nthat they will be a heavy financial burden on the realm. They will be covered in greater detail in the next part.\n\n“O, wealth of burghers! Your money of Petrus is most needed in times of war, and you are surely richer than those of the country, yet you feel you pay enough? Nay, damndest burghers, you mock poor fellows thus!”-Harald Von Manstein, 1499\n\nII.Mercenaries and Their Uses\n_____________________________I.There are two times when the use of mercenaries may be considered good or necessary. \nOne:-When your own subjects are disloyal or unwilling to fight, or dislike the marshal. You must\n\nwill not defect or run, for they care not for loyalty when the man who they are loyal to is unpopular.\n\nTwo:-When your realm is approaching a war that is critical or important. Mercenaries are a true financial burden on the realm,\n\nfor they expect pay at a specific time, and a specific amount and their sustenance is very costly. If you do not pay them, they will desert. They also require huge financial incentives, so do not use mercenaries\n\nin wars which are small and minor, or which your standard army can win without. \n\nII.The general who makes but few calculations on whether his troops are of good enough quality and quantity to defeat the enemy\n\nwill waste his wealth away, or watch his troops die. It is well to form a council before a war with all the great men of the realm, to discover if mercenaries are necessary.\n\nIII.Therefore we can see mercenaries\n\ncan be used badly or well. Sometimes, if the marshal is inexperienced, the mercenaries must be left to their own commands. For he is not versed in their speciality, merely in standard warfare. Saint Theodosius’ blessings, horsemen of Adria!\n\nFor he is the man of heralds and messengers and horses and all good and honest horsemen, and you will fight with valour. But be damned to your pay, for you cost your realm too much!\n\nIII.The Acquisition of Ships\n_____________________________I.The cheapest and quickest way of acquiring ships is requisitioning merchant vessels. If you do not wish for the merchant class to hate you, you may buy them,\n\nbut then it will be cheaper to build your own war galleys. Therefore, if you are using merchant ships, take them by force. Then they are are cheap, can be modified and are excellent for transporting troops.\n\nII.The second cheapest way of acquiring ships is to take them from the enemy or cause them to defect. This may be done by seizing enemy ports,or in naval engagements. This can be done from previous wars,\n\nand you should never attempt to sink the enemy for their ships will prove useful later. Rather, board them and kill them, or compel them to surrender using heavy missile fire. Then, you can use the conquered foe to augment one’s own strength.\n\nIII.Of course, the third cheapest way is to build your own ships. This takes time and wealth, but you may use the latest naval technology and have specialised galleys and other vessels.\n\nIV.And the final course which is completely inadvisable\n\nin any way is to hire mercenary fleets. Because ships are of such high sustenance, you will find yourself not only paying for the expensive cost of mercenaries but for their ships. They will expect monstrous pay, to the\n\npoint where your fleet will cost hundreds of ounces of silver each month, until, after a few years, one third of your income will be dissipated. And sometimes, they will be less effective than your own ships too.", ""),
        StaticBook("ART OF WAR p2", "§bDionysus the Akritian", "PART II OF THE ART OF WAR\n_____________________________\n\nIV.Siege Warfare and Its Importance\n_____________________________I.Sieges are what win wars, not battles. To meet the enemy of the field you win nothing but the enemy’s shame and reduction of troops, whereas\n\nduring a siege you may slowly depart him from his kingdom. If done well, this can be done with minimal loses. If done badly, sieges are the most costly part of warfare.\n\nII.Therefore, the value of siege engineers is immense. An army without them is no\n\narmy all,but a useless rabble, of no use at all. Therefore, a commander must make an effort to get a numerous amount of the best siege engineers, or he will fall into inability.\n\nIII.Merely throwing your heavy infantry at a castle\n\nwith little prior preparation is most inadvisable, for in your impatience, you will cause the enemy troops to reduce your forces, with no progress made. In sieges, you must be patient.\n\nIV.Stone-throwing artillery is most valuable during a siege.\n\nSome engineers will require prior assembly, but a true master of siege equipment can assemble them in the field. The trebuchet is most famous, but large ballistae may also be used. It is not necessary in all cases to storm a breach:\n\nsometimes, the threat of a breach will implore the enemy to surrender. In a siege, you must be patient. \n\nV.In addition, it is advisable to set up barracades and pavises and fortifacations in your own siege camp,\n\no that your crossbowmen may wittle down the enemy’s numbers, and so that you may fight the enemy with ease should he decide to sally forth.\n\nVI.Siege towers are also very worrying to the enemy,but take time and skill to construct. They are far preferable\n\nto ladders. The ancients often used to merge ram and siege tower in a single, masterful combination.\n\nVII.If no artillery can be constructed, mines are the next best option. If your mines are\n\ndiscovered, dig more. You must have patience. The enemy will set up countermines, and you must retreat from your current mines and block them to prevent any trouble stirring.\n\nVIII.Or alternatively,\n\nyou may not do this so the enemy will think you are coming from there, and then dig somewhere else. They will deploy troops in case you attack from the other mines. If the enemy sends reinforcements everywhere, he will everywhere be weak.\n\nIX.Remember this above all: The worst possible course of action is an unprepared attack. You will lose many of your men, and so you must be patient. \n\nX.And so you need not even take the castle, merely compel him to surrender. This is\n\nthe best possible course, for you will lose little men. The captured soldiers should be treated with kindness and kept, and then rulers will respect your benevolence and justice, as well as your own men and the enemy.\n\nXI.If the enemy surrenders, do not sack the castle or city. If he does not, and you have to take it by force, you are at liberty to plunder. Preferably, the citizens will be spared of death, but there will always be many deaths regardless. You\n\ncan not stop soldiers, for many are blackguards and curs.\n\nXII.However, plundering will make your men adore you, for you have given them wealth. You must not do it if the enemy surrenders\n\nbecause you will get a reputation for cruelty and being dishonourable. Rival princes and nobles will dislike you, and then your realm is nothing. The same goes for ordering a deliberate massacre of enemies.\n\nYou must not do this, but if the enemy refuses to surrender, you must sack. There will be deaths then, but you will not be held responsible. If your troops are truly disciplined and do not kill anyone during a sacking, you are a truly brilliant\n\ncommander and you are favoured by Saint Thomas. Your troops will then be commended and their praises sung, and you will be famed and your troops morale will be high.\n\nXIII.If you fail to take the castle, return to your own realm. The\n\nskillful soldier need not raise a second levy. Instead, you must merely hold your own castles, and wait for your troops to recover. Then, you may try again. If your losses are terrible, then do raise a second levy, but this will be regretful.\n\nV.Logistics and Maneuvering\n_____________________________I.An army is said to march on its stomach. While the men who fight in an army are often hardy men, they are carnivores. They must have ample food. It is said in one day, the\n\nsoldier will consume 1 flagon of wine or 2 of ale, 2 pounds of bread, 1 pound of cheese and a pound of meat.\n\nII.Knights will consume noticeably more, and in addition the cavalry of the army will need to feed their horses, of which they can have many.\n\nIII.Therefore, a wise general does not merely forage, nor takes pre-prepared supplies. He does both. To forage from the enemy will damage his people’s morale, for they will see their sovereign as weak. \n\nV.But in case\n\nthe enemy takes a policy of scorched earth, it is always advisable for your troops to be well-supplied, regardless of foraging.\n\nV.In a brief manner, bring supplies with you, but make a point of replenishing your supplies with ones foraged from the enemy.\n\nVI.For the quick moving of your army in the field you must ensure that the cavalry have both riding and fighting horses, and have spare ones to replace fallen horses. You cannot dither, especially with a cavalry force, with the replacement of horses. You\n\nmust acquire them, and do well by them.\n\nVII.To the infantry, the baggage train of wagons which is often imagined is of complete falsehood. Nay, what is carried must be done so on their backs or in donkeys. This will ensure a fast-moving\n\narmy. For though having a baggage train of heavy goods may be advantageous to your supplies, it will be very slow.\n\nVIII.And for the entertainment of expensive guests, this will increase prices. You must only entertain guests if they will improve morale,\n\nor are willing to travel in the manner of a common soldier, or at the best, a knight. They will simply slow you down if otherwise with special requirements and niceties.\n\nV.In Battle!\n_____________________________I.In battle, commanders divide their fources into four acies. It is preferable to dismount some knights, in order to form 3 acies of foot and 1 of horse. The acie of horse must be kept in reserve and used only\n\nwhen the enemy is near breaking; cavalry is useless in sustained warfare, and are useful only at the tipping point of battle, defeating the enemy in a single charge or retreating. Not stopping to fight, but charging, retreating, and charging again, until\n\nthe foe is broken.\n\nII.For this you must ensure the cavalry are firmly grouped together when they do charge. Therefore, give always your most trusted commander command of the cavalry, or perhaps you yourself should take it.\n\nIII.The infantry are usually deployed in a defensive formation, but advance into an offensive formation as the battle progresses. With an army strong in heavy infantry you must ensure the flanks are strong so that you may surround the enemy,\n\nrelying on the cavalry to do the finishing blow.\n\nIV.With an army of missile troops, you must deploy stakes and wait. If you are trapped, they will fight to the death and show great valour. You must stand your ground,\n\nand incite your enemy’s anger to cause him to charge. This is a tactic that works even outnumbered, especially with terrain that prevents enemy flanking. You must group the few men-at-arms you have on the flanks. You must have a large reserve.\n\nV.A force of mostly cavalry must break the enemy with the initial charge, and if they cannot, they must retreat. If they cannot retreat, they should not charge in the first place, but dismount and fight as infantry.\n\nVI.The same goes if the enemy's’ cavalry greatly outnumbers your own. Your own cavalry must dismount and aid your infantry. Otherwise they will be made useless.\n\nVII.In the case of a rout, if you wish to rally your men, do it on\n\nhigh ground. If the enemy routs, do not use mounted knights to pursue them, but light cavalry.\n\nVIII.If you fight horse archers, if they advance, as if they mean to attack, do not advance. They are merely baiting you and will destroy your infantry\n\nwith missiles. Withdraw, and wait for another battle where you may take them by surprise.\n\nIX.If the enemy is of infantry and you cavalry, you must feign disorder or rouse him to anger to cause him to want to attack you. If you\n\nthink battle may be offered under better conditions, or you do not wish to fight at all, withdraw! \n\nX.And remember this above all: the mark of a good commander is to know when to withdraw, and dare to do it. If\n\nyou think battle may be offered under better conditions, or you do not wish to fight at all, withdraw!\n\nXI.Remember the biggest enemy of a cavalry man is missiles at close range in unfavourable weather, for the horses will be made slow by mud\n\nand vulnerable. If there are many missile troops in such conditions, do not charge headlong. If he is in such a position where outmaneuvering is impossible, then do not charge at all, but withdraw and take him another day.\n\nXII.It is often appropriate to have men in light armour but equipped as swordsmen to run down skirmishes. These should be the fastest men.\n\nVII. Horses:Dangers, Types and Sustenance\n_____________________________\n\nI.Horses may be divided into three categories: War horses, riding horses and saddle horses.\n\nII.Under war horses fall horses such as destriers, who are bred for us in battle.\n\nIII.Under riding horses fall\n\n horses bred to be used to travel or hunt with great speed. These include rouncies, cobs, etc.\n\nIV.Saddle horses are poorer horses which yeomen can afford.\n\nV.A good knight will have at least 1\n\nwarhorse and a riding horse, and will see to their sustenance. Many will have more, and those that do would require such a baggage train for feed that the army would be slowed massively. It would\n\nbe wise to sustain an army of largely cavalry with foraging.\n\nVI.Now your light cavalry are poorer, and often you must buy their horses, or they can only afford one. it is good for them to buy rouncies or cobs. These\n\nhorses are for general purposes and are essentially the compromise of riding and warhorses.\n\nVII.With saddle horses a commander should not trouble himself with, but allow the yeomen and other classes of people of your army to buy for themselves.\n\nVIII.Therefore, it is so advis’d that those armies who wish to travel merely on their baggage train and not commit to foraging of any sort, to take as few horses as possible. This may be done by having dismounted knights and sergeants,\n\nand if you require cavalry taking a small amount.\n\nIX.And it shall be noted that those who do are in territories where the enemy is implementing a scorched\n\nearth policy or you are in an infertile or destitute region, the same aforementioned rule applies. Take but few horses and cavalry as possible without severely crippling your forces.", ""),
        StaticBook("BlacksmithGuide", "willsiren", "A Blacksmithing General Handbook By Viscar Van'Eer Of Astfield.\nDISCLAIMER: I may be only proficient in the art of blacksmithing, however, my knowledge is unrivaled througout Oren.\n-------------------[!] There would be a drawing of two men dueling.\n\nHeavy armor must be designed to take a lot of punishment. It will receive direct blows from all sorts of weapons while protecting the wearer.wearer. Leather strips are used to make the straps and bindings in all armor.\nFerrum and steel are easy to\n\nFerrum armor requires a large number of Ferrum ingots. A smith might need a couple of dozen to complete a full set of Ferrum armor. Steel armor primarily uses steel ingots, but some Ferrum is used as well.\nOrcish armors require lots of bone and leather\n\nelded with a bit of Ferrum. Heat should be used sparingly, lest it become brittle. The Orcs are masters of this technique, but it can be learned by any smith with patience and skill.\nSteel plate mail is made by adding steel With Coal and Minerals.\n\nThe alloy is stronger than either metal by itself. Coal minerals can be a finicky material requiring the heat from the forge to be steady and not vary much. Bluesteel can only be worked when heated.It will develop small cracks that eventually shatter t\n\nmaterial if hammered cold. Unlike most other armors, Bluesteel will not alloy with iron. It must be used pure.\nI can only tell you tales of how to make Undead armor. I have never seen it myself, nor do I know anyone that has. The stories say that it sh\n\nd always be worked on at night... ideally under a new or full moon, and never during an eclipse. A red harvest moon is best.Flesh and Bone is the principal materials, but at the right moment a heart of a pure person or animal must be thrown into the fi\n\nI hope my blacksmithing demonstrations can help you too better your knowledge. \n-Viscar Van'Eer\n\n((This knowledge should be demonstrated Rp'ly not literally))", ""),
        StaticBook("High Elf Culture", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "The Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya for Beginners.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~      ~~~~~~~~~~~\nKarin'ayla to you. This book is intended as a guide through the noble culture of the High Elven people. Be you a youth of the Mali'aheral or a foreign diplomat who\n\ndesires to familiarize yourself with our ways, or even an older elf who has lapsed in their etiquette, this book can help you.\n\nPlease read on through the various lessons in these pages. Also see the guide to elven phrases in the back.\n\n       Lesson One\n    Avoid All Impurity\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nImpurity can exsist in two ways, Physical and mental. Both are to be treated with paramount seriousness, as they threaten the delicate balance of our civilized society.\n\nPhysical impurity is found when an individual is only partly High Elf, thus they are not \"pure\" in their lineage. Through out our long lives and our history we have seen, time and agian, that relations between a High Elf and others not of our kin end in\n\nmisery and failure. The impure products of these thoughtless and perverse relations are prone to lives of dissapointment and loneliness, as they do not truely belong anywhere. To any of the Mali'aheral, the formation of a \"romantic\" relationship with any\n\noutside of our people is forbidden, and will only serve to make yourself physically impure as well. The creation of children from such a bond is viewed with equal displeasure. This may sound harsh to those who are not of our people, but it is not. it is\n\nsimply the truth that wisdom and experience have taught us.\n\nWays to determine if one is of impure lineage include but are not limited to the following. Eyes of any color save blues, greens or purples. Ears that are rounded and short. Also a smallnes\n\nstature can indicate impurity. Hair amoung the Mali'aheral is normally fair, though it is not unheard of to have a brunette born amoung us. Dark hair, however, will certainly raise flags of warning to any who do not know the elf in question.\n\nMental impurity is a bit more difficult to detect as it can be hidden by the devious or the liar.\nIn truth, any who do not follow the Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya are considered mentally impure to some degree or another. Small degrees of impurity can be treat\n\nand corrected. Large ones however can, have and will result in banishment and even death. Physical Impurity usually will end with the individual being \"cleansed\" by being tossed into an acid bath. Thus removing their taint from our society.\n\n        Lesson Two\nProper Conduct in the\n            City\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nHigh Elves place etiquette on a high pedistal. We enjoy conversation, and we enjoy debate, but we insist it is done right. Emotion should not cloud one's judgment\n\nor reasoning, neither should it color one's argument. Logic and reason should rule the mind as it rules in the city of Haelun'or.\n\nFor those of you who are not of the people, you should consider before speaking to a High Elf, or trying to enter the c\n\nthat there are a few key differences between you and us.\n\nWe are old, very old. Many of us have lived long enough to have met your great, great grand parents when they were children. As such our perspective is different than yours. High Elves are\n\nseen as cold or harsh in their demeanor or critisisms. In answer to this I invite you to consider these things. How would you feel if you saw an endless parade of children making the same mistakes, time and again, even though you yourself have warned them\n\nof the pitfalls of their poor behavoir many times over the past centuries? We grow frustrated when we see the same problems and mistakes being repeated and not fixed as logic would dictate that they must. You must also consider that a High Elf reckons\n\nthings in a longer time frame than you likely do. There for, one should not take our comments or critisisms personally, for they are intended to help you and your children and your children's children to be better. After all, why should one be upset by\n\nthe truth?\n\nWhen attempting to enter the city, if one is not of the Mali'aheral, one should not think to do so lightly or easily. Our city is precious to us, and we do not seek to sunder its purity by letting any and all who knock to enter.\n\nIf one seeks to enter they should do so with the right frame of mind. With patience and with humility one will go further. Also it is customary to bring a gift, that they may offer something in return for the honor of entering the gates.\n\nFor those of you who are of the people. I suggest looking the part. Dress appropriately for your lineage as a High Elf. Keep your hair seemly, and preferably un-dyed. Our flesh should be free of tattoos or piercings as these things only mar our natural\n\nbeauty. Makeup or accesories that accent our features may be worn however.\n\n      Lesson Three\n       Be Educated\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Whether you attend the Eternal College or you take it upon yourself to read and learn, all good High Elves smile upon the persuit of knowledge. Learn of art, science or even the arcane lore of\n\nmagic, but be knowledgable of something. One should spend their whole life aquiring new learning that they may be useful.\n\nOh be wise, what more can I say?\n\n      Lesson Four\n        Courtship\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The art of courtship is something that all young Mali'aheral should know. For one day, you may wish to impress someone of the opposite gender and unite with them in marriage. Follow this guide and\n\nwill hopefully avoid becoming a social pariah.\n\nDo NOT engage in sappy, lovey dovey actions or grandiose acclamations of your love. This will not end well and is unseemly for one of our people. Rather, create works of art or music or literature that\n\n you can devote to the object of your adoration. Doing so will not only let that person know that someone is interested in them, but will show that you are capable in these areas. These things should, however, be done anonymously, so as not to put any\n\nundue social strain on you or them. When this courtship has gone on for a while and you feel reasonably sure that they will respond in kind to your affections, then you may reveal your identity to them as their admirer. If you do not feel that things will\n\ngo well, or you lose interest, you may simply stop courting the individual and no one should be any the wiser who it was.\n\nAlas, these things do indeed happen.\n\n       Lesson Five\n         Marriage\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Once your courtship has gone its course and you and your beloved are together, it is expected that you will be married.\nHigh Elven marriages are usually held in large public venues or centers\n\nknowledge such as a library. We do not have churches and therefore do not hold weddings in them.\n\nThe ceremony is attended by all the pure citizenry, as well as invited outsiders. An individual is given the honor to speak at the wedding and officiate\n\nceremony. After they speak, a moment of silence is given for any to speak out against the union, should they choose. This is almost never done, as to speak out publically against the couple is considered rude in the extreme.\nThe two are then wed and ma\n\nrecieve gifts, congradualtions, etcetera.\n\nIt is within the bonds of matrimony and ONLY within these bonds that the creation of High Elven children may take place. Assuming you are fertile, to have a child is an honor and a joy to be planned and\n\ntaken with all seriousness.\n\n       Lesson Six\n         Religion\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~This will be a rather short section. The High Elves practice no religion. We would rather devote our time to logical and, for lack of a better term, provable persuits than to sit in a church and\n\npray to a God that we can neither see nor hear. Rather than try to guess at the whims of deity, We will continue to unravel the mysteries of the world as we can prove it exsists.\n\nFor my High Elven readers, you would do well to devote yourself to the\n\npractice of our culture, rather than some faith from a distant land.\n\n     Lesson Seven\n    To Offer Insult\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The highest insult one can offer is to call another impure. This however has some stipulations. For example, if one of the leaders of the people, We'll say the El'sohaer were to call another elf\n\n this offense could be taken with much gravity. However, if a half elf were to refer to a High elf as impure, the insult has no barb, as the half elf is impure to begin with. One way to offer such an insult is to give a High Elf gold. This should almost\n\nnever be done, as one High Elf to another, as the action can indicate that the reciever cares more for gold than they do for their people. Of course were a human to give an elf a bar of gold, it would have no such meaning, as a human could not be expected\n\nto know this. Gold jewlery or items can be given between High Elves, so long as the intent is clear. Unless you really do want to insult them.\n\n        Conclusion\n```````````````````'''''''''''''''''''   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nI hope that you have enjoyed this book, but more so I hope that you are better prepared to navigate the pitfalls of High Elven etiquette. We are a strict people, but we are\n\ndelightsome when you know how to behave.\n\nPlease look for my next book\n\n\"An Encyclopedic Arcanum\"\na guide to magic\n\n~Gallidron Elindrow~\n\nPublication year 1514\n\n         A Guide to\n      Elvish Phrases\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~````````````````````''''''''''''''''''Karin'ayla- Good day\nKer'ayla- Good night\nVan'ayla- Farewell\nMali- Elf\nBortu- Dwarf\nUruk- Ork\nValah- Human\nTali'bortu- Halfli\n\nMali'aheral-High Elf\nAcalin- Shop\nAiler- Wizard\nIler- Dark wizard\n\nHopefully these few phrases and words will be of use to any who learn them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Surviving travel", "§bIlbryn", "Snow's Maiden, 1595\nA traveller's guide to\nsurvival by Ilbryn\n\nSo, you find yourself on the road. You've plenty of food, and know where you are going. You may think you are safe, however you aren't. When I travel, I follow several rules religiously. At\n\nnight time, I climb a large tree to rest. Many aren't as skilled at climbing as I, so if you can't easily climb a tree, you should find a place off-road and secluded to rest. If someone tries to lure you from the tree, do not come down. They may be\n\nscreaming for help, however that's easily pulled off, and nearly got me killed. When travelling, you should not stop for anyone asking you to, or to come with them, no matter how nice or convincing. They're likely muggers, or worse, as a man on the road\n\nwith no place to go should not be trusted. I've only had one experience with coming along was a bortu inviting me to the grand opening of a blackjack hall, I only went with because he was with a group of humans. Also, the same can apply to entering a new\n\ntown. Whilst in Johannesburg, I was invited to a house for tea. Instead, I was mugged under threat of battle-axe, and lost several tens of mina, as well as my weapon, and several magic apples.\n\n-Ilbryn", ""),
        StaticBook("Smithing Guide", "§bIan", "Blacksmithing for Dummies, by a (Sort of) Dummie\n\nThe art of shaping metal is one that many do but most are not entirely sure how they do such things almost coming as second nature to some. However, to get the most out of what you work with and what you shape in order to make extremly deadly and in some\n\ncases beautiful works with metal you must give it the attention like an artist to a canvas.\n\nTools: First and foremost you will need the requirements to begin working without it you will not get far\n\n*An anvil\n*Tongs\n\n*Bellows\n*A variety of hammers varying in size for shaping and finishing\n*Swages - Tools, variously shaped or grooved on the end or face, used by smiths to aid in the shaping process\n*Fullers - A half-round set hammer, used by a blacksmith for\n\ngrooves and spreading iron.\n*Punches - Tools for making usually circular holes\n*Drifts - Slightly tapered tools of steel for enlarging or shaping a hole in metal, by being forced or driven into\n*Chisels\n\nOnce you have that you'd obviously need an area to store it in usually a well mantained and circular in interior area for keeping the air from escaping and your fire from dying down which leads to the next topic of beginning to work.\n\nBlacksmithing is usually a two or in some cases three man job. A man on the bellows to keep the fire burning at decent enough tempeture. And obviously someone that works the anvil, hammer, and tongs heating the metal in the forge and shaping it.\n\nI have found to work metal efficently requires only two things. Heat, and Precison. For the first if your fire does not burn hot enough you end up pounding a peice of metal making no progress and wasting time. As for the second, Precison of strikes like a\n\nwell trained swordsman finding weak points in an enemies armor so does a smith as he works. A well trained eye and precise strikes with a hammer to find the weak spots of the metal and pound it out.\n\nWithout getting to in depth of how to shape metal into blades, axes, armor, trinkets, etc. They are all diffrent each artist has a style and none of them are wrong. Experiment, find what works best for you with this basic guide.", ""),
        StaticBook("Glyphs for Bgn's", "§bJoseph Alexander", "Table of Contents\n\n1: Unbreaking\n\n2: Efficiency\n\n3: Smite\n\n4: Material Information\n\n         Unbreaking\n\n(x is where the material used is placed.)\n\nx-x\n-x-\nx-x\n\n        Efficiency\n\nx--\n-xx\nx--\n\n         Smite\n\n-xx-\nxxxx\nxxxx\n-xx-\n\n         Materials\n\n*Lapis: cheapest, fastest material. Weak\n\n*Emerald: Moderate speed, chance for higher power\n\n*Gold: Slow, unstable, offers high power.\n\n Continues on -->\n\n        Materials (Continued)\n\n*Diamond: Expensive, fast with moderate power", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Ones", "§bTedyn Isilioleth", "------------------\nA Guide To Communicating With your Lost Ones\n------------------\n\nTo start I shall say by no means is this book a masters guide, however is rather the experience of a pupil. From my experiences I shall impart the knowledge as to how I\n\nfind it easiest to contact my 'Lost Ones'.\n\nI often visit my father on occasion for idle chat, as well as to ask questions, however getting there takes some practice and also a little bit of patience.\n\nTo begin, I collect the memories I have of\n\nhim. For example, the tunic he left with me before he departed all those years ago, and I put it on. I then decide to seclude myself to my room and make sure I'm comfortable. I nestle myself between the quilts and make sure the torch by my bedside isn't\n\nso bright yet not too dull that I can no longer see infront of me. \n\nI then reach to my table and gather my pipe and the few dried herbs I have sitting. I believe you can use whatever you can find however I tend to use Cactus Green, mostly because of it's\n\navailability and relaxing properties, however I have seen an old uruk simply relax himself without the aid of a drug.\n\nIt only takes a few moments for the herb to catch alight before I draw the smoke from the barrel of the pipe. Hencefore my body relaxes\n\nand I feel what seems to be the world around me loosen slightly.\n\nShortly after I've found myself indeed comfortable and indeed relaxed I begin to call to him. \"Skaat-izg-u krank. Luk-lab bugd-u-lat, traum lat-u-izg.\n\nSkaat-izg-u krank\". I would say, however since that is specific to my father you may find yourself comfortable using other words.\n\nI begin to form a rythhm as I speak the words. I can feel them growing louder and louder as my ears twitch to the sound.\n\nMy feet begin to tap as I wrestle the words into a beat, a song almost as I call out to him. Then not before long I awaken and continue my journey to go and meet with him.\n\n-An Elf.", ""),
        StaticBook("Combat Manual", "§bTemp Thersist", "Combat     Basics\n\n         The 3 Stances\n\nHigh - Form is leaned in, Knees bent. Arms arced in pre-wind-up. Blade is to be pointed skyward. Referred to as the \"Counter,\" stance. Used to counter-act Mid-guard and stanceless men.\n\nMid-Guard - Form is relaxed, blade pommel parallel to the user's waistline. Knees bent and arms relax. Referred to as the \"Assaulting,\" stance. Attacks vary on situation, be it arc or thrust. Counters Low stance and untrained fodder.\n\nLow - Form is lowered, knees bent and body leaned in. The arms are left in a half-wind-up with the blade parallel to the flooring. Referred to as the \"Wounding,\" stance. Counters High Guard, spearsmaan and isn't typically used to kill a target.\n\n             Movements\n\n\nWhen in combat, keep your foe in direct line of sight. Movements are circular in nature, there are to be no steps forward or backward, instead, side-step in or out.\n\nWhen Assaulting - Nature may say rush at the target head-on. Instead, aim to the target's left or right with movement. Aim to strike the target and take place on either flank or rear of the target. Once flanked, strike either the neck or lower back.\n\nWhen Countering - Side-step, parry, or retaliate. Know the range of the opponent's weapon. IF your range is superior, retaliate with a side-step and aim to cleave limb or behead the enemy. If your range is lesser, parry the blow of the enemy and close\n\nWhen Countering cont... \n\nthe gap, making an effort to disarm or hinder.\n\n         Crossbow Usage\n\nThe following is a petty guide for loading and firing a crossbow.\n\nSet weapon, if required. Simply setting it grip-first onto the ground.\n\nDraw back string, with device or hand.\n\nMove foot from grip.\n\nLift weapon and load with bolt/munition.\n\nShoulder weapon and aim.\n\nFire.\n\nRepeat as needed.\n\nNote loading device.\n\nCreated for usage by the Caerngard of Kaedrin. \n\n - Temp Thersist of Kaedrin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Killin' a troll", "§bJentos", "xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n     Killin' a troll\n\n\n  By Jentos Adam, last representant of the house of Blackwood.\n\n\n\n\n\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n\"Dear reader, in this book you shall learn to: recognize, flee and kill a troll.\"\n\nIntroduction\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\"Troll. Nasty, cruel and stupid creatures capable of destroying whole towns, And fierce war-beasts.\"\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\nWere to find a troll?\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\nTroll's can be found about everywhere in these wild lands. From the frozen dwarven plains. To the heat of the Caliphate!\"\n\n\"Troll's like to live in unforested mountainous regions, dark caves in the\n\nmountains. Or in a big clearing in the forest.\"\n\nRecognizing a troll\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxWho has never pictured a troll? Big ugly figure walking in the forest? But the're are alot of different types of orcs and sub-trolls like half trolls half\n\nmen!\"\n\n\"Trolls can vary from 8 feet when young to a giant 20 feet tall!\nThey have a relative big orc like head with a few men-like features.\"\n\n\nFleeing a troll\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxRunning away from a\n\ntroll in a rather forested area is easier than in a mountainous or flat region.\"\n\nTactic's: \n\"If you find yourself in a forested or near a forested region, your best bet is to simply go we're the tree's are smaller so you can slow the troll\n\nand get out of its reach.\"\n\n\"Hiding in a cave isn't a good idea, a hungry troll is apt to wait a long time to be able to get his supper (especially if it's the trolls own cave!).\"\n\nKillin' a troll!\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n\"In this final section, you will learn how to \n\n       Slay\n      -----\nThese mighty creatures!.\n\n\"The troll's weak spot, (like many other beats) are the eye!\nUnfortunatly it is easy to see that being able to get a good shot at them isn't easy.\"\n\n\"The trick is to, hack the legs until it falls, wait t'ill it reaches down or bend or simply atta\n\nfrom a good height!\nxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx\n\n\"On this. I say to you! Have thy luck I never had!\"", ""),
        StaticBook("HTBAP", "§bCarsandra Ivydale", "How To Be A Pacifist.\n\nBy Carsandra Ivydale\n\nBeing a pacifit isn't about the label. Don't be a pacifist just because all your friends are one, or because you want to brag your one. Don't jump into it because everybody else is. Try to identify your reasons, and talk them out with somebody\n\ntrusted. If you both agree on them, then your good to follow that path.\n\nStart with the small changes that come with pacifisim. Start by not harming small creatures, animals, and so forth. Killing animals for meat doesn't count, as you need to survive. Being a pacifist is all about -balance-. Kill when you need for survival,\n\ndon't because of your emotions or just randomly.\n\nTry reading up on the more pacifist religions. Trying talking to people who are pacifists. Interveiw them, ask them questions. Don't be afraid to go around and ask people things. Learn! Learning is the most important thing you can do.\n\nLearn to let go of things and forgive others for their wrongdoings. Forgive people for their acts of revenge and emotions, such things only lead to unessiary anger.\n\nDon't blame organizations or groups for violent actions. They think what their doing is right. Even if you don't think it is, and you can disagree, the people want the change within the world.\n\nIf you ARE really upset about a groups or religions actions, consider hosting or joining a peaceful protest. A peaceful protest is basically holding a candle and standing there, with no violent actions, and shouting your choice of words.\n\nRemember that being a pacifist isn't an instant change. It takes a long time of pratice and patience in order to perfect it.", ""),
        StaticBook("How To Hunt", "§bDaina", "How do I hunt?\n\nIts not that hard, you simply find a good - sharp sword. A bow might use good, aswell.\nThen you need to get a good ammount of arrows, ofcourse a skilled archer will need only one. Also if you are fighting a\n\nlarge animal then you should get a shield. A good hunter will carry a horn to call for help if needed. Once you have all that you are ready to go. Find a closest forest and search for wolf, bear, fox or any other animal's trails. It wont be\n\neasy, which means you need to try hard. There are chances you wont find a single animal, but dont give up.\nOnce you find the animal use your bow or sword to take it down. Animal may run and strugle but im sure you will get them.\n\nBiggest moto in hunting is.\n\nNEVER GIVE UP!\n\nSo yea, thats it. This is a small book that will let you provide food for your family.\n\n-Daina ((Turko))", ""),
        StaticBook("A Dark Liturgy", "§bDiscalus", "A Dark Liturgy\n    ==============\n    [ A Safety Guide ]\n\n        ==========\n        By: Discalus\n        ==========\n\n[ THIS BOOK IS NOT CANON ]\n\nHave you ever met a dark mage or sorceror? If you haven't you're lucky. But, now that they are becoming more of a common threat, we people of Atlas need to know how to defend ourselves from these terrors. This book will instruct you on how to fend off\n\nthese dark creatures.\n\nNecromancy\n\n==========\n\nNecromancy is a very old form of dark magic, if not the oldest. It is a fairly easy magic to distinguish. Necromancers generally look very fatigued and their skin is very lifeless. Sometimes they wear\n\nblack cloaks in order to hide their features. You can also tell if a necromancer is near by if the you start feeling saddened or very tired abruptly. There are certain ways to negate the necromantic effects on a person. Sapphire, topaz, and soladite all\n\ncan help to lower the effects of a necromancer's life drain. However, the more powerful the necromancer, the less these gemstones will help. Necromancers are also weaker to holy objects and magic. If you do see a necromancer, contact a nearby cleric\n\nimmediately, never try to fight one yourself.\n\nLiches, Darkstalkers, and Ghouls\n\n===================\n\nThese creatures are deceased that have been summoned by a necromancer to do their dark bidding. Liches are the deceased form of previous necromancers who\n\nare summoned by other necromancers. They appear very skeletal and raggy. They are very powerful, and yet very defendless. Due to their frail, boney body, they may easily be dispatched and killed. Liches are also weak to gold and, especially, holy magic\n\nsuch as clericism. Darkstalkers are the warrior form of a Lich, Instead of the raised wielding magic, a Darkstalker is a master of the blade. They are much stronger than Liches and can take much heavier damage. They are not weak to fire but are very weak\n\nto sunlight and clericism. While they are durable, their skeletal bodies can eventually be worn down. Ghouls are soulless beings of the dead. They are deprvied of all sensability and rely on animalistic instincts. They can easily be summoned by a\n\nnecromancer but most of the time they're randomly found wandering around. Ghouls are slow and are weak to gold and holy magic. They are fairly easier to beat than Liches or Darkstalkers.", ""),
        StaticBook("Body Training.", "§bDunstan Zytiaear", "Table of contents.\nPg3. Introduction.\npg5. Starting.\npg8. Self Dicipline\npg11. Endurance.\npg17. Strength.\npg22. Disease & Injury.\npg25. Pain & discomfort.\n\n\"\"\n\nIntroduction.\nIf one wants to harness their mind and body to its greatest ability they must face the challenge of their own willingness. Once you can overcome your own mind then you can over come your own body. All information in this book is\n\nuseless if one can not muster the will and humility to conquer themselfs.\n\nStarting.\nThe final statement of the introduction is the most important in this stage. You have been asked to embrace humility as it is the requirement to learn where you stand. If you believe your what you are not then you will fail. If you believe\n\nyou can throw a small tree but struggle to swing a stick how would you learn to move larger trees? You must come to terms with what you truly can do if you wish to change it. You must accept weakness to become strong. You must accept injury to recover.\n\nYou must accept to change. Find your self if you wish to better yourself.\n\nSelf Dicipline.\nOnce you have found where you stand you must embrace the emotions that come with it and use it. The pain, anger, frustration, and sadness that come form embraceing your own falts are your ultimant tools. But you must learn to wield\n\nthese tools with skill. You must controll yourself to drive your self. If you cannot learn to controll your tools you can not craft any quality. All you will do is destroy your self if you can not controll your emotions.\n\nYour emotions can be the most precise of tools and the most deadly of parasites. Unchecked rage has lead to the downfall of nations while honed rage has lead to the creation of nations.\n\nEndurance.\nA quite simply physically painfull aspect to hone. Training may seem simple but time will tell it is not. Pick a simple task and do it with repetition for an extended period of time. Running is a recommended task for this. When you start to\n\nrun you may feel fine. Within the first minute your hearts pulse will quicken and your breathing will heavy. Soon your legs and lungs will start to feel a burning sensation. This burning sensation will begin to slowly start to spread throughout your body.\n\nThe desire to stop will suck at your mind like a leech  and you will begin to take measures to attempt to make the action take less effort. You will begin to argue with your self whether or not or not you have done enough. You dont know what enough\n\ntruly feels like. You will need to excersise self dicipline to own your emotion and have it assist you into going farther. The moment you collapse is when you will know every thing. The moment you have collapsed is the moment that teaches you what\n\nenough is. At this moment you may puke and will be covered in sweat. Your body will be screaming for both rest and nutrient. Find where you stand as you have to make a decision on what you need more. My personal siggestion is to drag yourself to a tavern,\n\nembrace the humility of fumbling over your self to walk, and order a meal.\n\nStrength.\nIncreasing the ammount of pure phyisical power you can exert is a tasking process that will cause a great physical change on your body. You will require both a viraty of heavy movable objects and a signifigant ammount of nutrents. Find what\n\nyou are able to lift then find something lighter and heavier. You will start with the lighter and you will do it with the aim of repetition. Move to the middle weight and lift to a number that will be decided as your secess point. Once you have lifted the\n\nmiddle weight go to the heavy weight and lift with the goal of reaching your success point. If you reach your success point move to a heavier weight and go for your success point again. Do this untill you fail. Remember where you have failed for the next\n\ntime you will try to pass this. You will be sore on a regular basis. This is the feeling of your muscles growing. You will learn enjoy this feeling. As your muscles grow you must also feed them, thus you must eat more and you must eat with proper\n\nattention to nutrition.\n\nDisease & Injury.\nThese go hand in hand as injury can result in disease and disease can result in injury. It is more important to clean ones wounds than it is to heal them. If ones calf is sliced open it should be cleaned before any attempt to mend\n\nthe calf back together is done. An uncleaned injury can lead to infection which if left further unchecked can lead to organ failure which will come back around to further injury and possable death. Disease is an entire beast in its self as all you can do\n\nwith out extensive training is collect rest and eat healthy foods.\n\nPain & discomfort.\nMany mistake this as ones enemy when in reality it can be ones ultimate ally. It is the manner in which one is consciously alert to detail of their body which may not be the most apparent.\n\nYou must learn to befriend pain and discomfort if you want to be able to tame it. If you want to tame it you must embrace it. If you want to embrace it you must be familiar with it. Push your self. Endure the cold bare back. Run the extra mile and\n\ndo it upon blistering feet. Revel in the feeling and progress will be made.", ""),
        StaticBook("Monster Manual 1", "§bDiane Farsight", "=+-+=\n    The Monster\n       Manual\n       =+-+=\n        \n\n        Volume 1\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Diane Farsight\n\n       Foreword\nThe world is a dark place, and it's filled with dark things. This book, and others like it, will hopefully inform you of what is out there, and how to deal with them. After all, Ignorance is a most insidious killer.\n\n      The Blob\n================\nDanger: Low\nDescription: Blobs are generally docile animals shaped like big piles of goo. Their size can vary greatly, but they tend not to surpass 6 feet in height. Their color varies, but will usual\n\nbe the color of the enviornment they live in. Furthermore, they are covered in an outer layer of dry skin that protects them from extreme heat. Because of this, they are often found in hot climates. If enveloped by a blob, suffocation is the only way it\n\nkill you, as their bodies have no acidic properties.\nWeaknesses: Blobs are quite susceptable to cold, making Thanium a perfect weapon against them.\nCreation: Blobs can create more blobs by splitting themselves apart, creating two, smaller b\n\n     The Ooze\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Oozes are the volitile cousin of blobs. They have the same shape and color, but can be much larger and territorial than their counterpart. Their size can become a stagger\n\nmeters in height, and their body produces a potent acid capable of dissolving flesh and metal alike. Also unlike blobs, Oozes prefer the cold, and lack the outer skin that blobs possess. If you ever need to tell an Ooze apart from a blob quickly, use your\n\nnose. Oozes will smell much more acrid.\nWeaknesses: Oozes are slow and notably flammable. The best way to deal with one is to set them alight, then run while they burn.\nCreation: Oozes can split themselves into more oozes, just like blobs.\n\n  The Giant Ooze\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: On occasion, there will be a sighting of a Gargantuan Ooze. Often they come from forgotten cave systems opened by earthquakes, or humanoids digging too deep. They\n\nOozes, but much larger- usually over 10 meters in size and capable of dissolving massive castle gates in a matter of minutes. Weaknesses: Fire will still kill gargantuan Oozes, but it is imperitave that you do not attempt to hide from them- there is\n\nalmost no stopping one if it begins chasing you.\nCreation: Unknown. Normal Oozes should split into smaller Oozes before reaching this size. It is hypothesized that extended time in cramped conditions underground allows an ooze to grow to this size.\n\n  The Flesh Worm\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: The tunnel worm is a subterranian monster of epic proportions. It's full length is unknown, but it is easily several meters in diameter. Most of it's life is spent\n\nholes in the earth for it to travel in, often straight through stone. A cave created by a Tunnel worm recently will always be perfectly circular, and ribbed to allow the tunnel worm to maneuver within it easily. It is hypothesized that the Underdark\n\nbeneath the dwarven lands of Anthos was sculpted by the errant burrowing of tunnel worms.\nWeaknesses: Any place that isn't perfectly fitted for it's body, such as large caverns or the surface.\nCreation: Unknown.\n\n     The Drake\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: A Drake is, in essence, a corrupted dragon, like those spoken of in legend. Unlike their bretheren, Drakes are much smaller in size and easier to defeat. Despite this,\n\nare still capable of flying and breathing fire, and as a result require a large body of able men to be killed safely. When killed, a drake's body will dissolve entirely, but if one can manage to retrieve some of its scales without killing the beast, they\n\ncan be used to great effect in alchemy.\nWeaknesses: None.\nCreation: Legend has it that drakes are born when a dragon is overcome with taint. This, however, has never been witnessed.\n\n   The Alchemical\n       Chimera\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: An alchemical chimera is a fusion of two animals. It is truely an unnatural beast, created by a devious use of alchemy. Chimera come in all shape\n\nbut all will resemble the combination of two  natural beasts. They are mindless beasts, virtually untamable, and gluttonous for flesh.\nWeaknesses: : Time. A well created Chimera will last, at max, for 2 to 3 years.\nCreation: Alchemy.\n\n The Dark Chimera ===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Through the use of drakkarian magic, the normal conditions for a chimera can be subverted, allowing for fully adult humans to be partially fused with parts hewn from\n\nanimals. The result is a fully intelligent, remarkably stable chimera. Many dark chimera are no more than victims of dark mages, but this is not always the case. Great care should be taken when dealing with one.\nWeaknesses: None\nCreation: A\n\nMixed with Drakkar Magic.\n\n    The Vodnik\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Vodnik are tiny, fish-like creatures that inhabit rivers and lakes. When vodnik encounter a corpse of any sort, they will begin filling and infesting it. The corpse will\n\nmoving of it's own accord, and begin dragging anything so foolish as to disturb it's water under with it, to become infested as well. Eventually, this process will crescendo until a small army of shambling corpses inhabit an area. This makes clearing\n\ndifficult.\nWeaknesses: Attacking the arms and legs of a vodnik-infested corpse is your best bet. Cutting off the head should have no effect.\nCreation: The Vodnik reproduce by laying eggs in the corpses they inhabit.\n\n  The Giant Crab\n===================Danger: High\nDescription: An enormous crab, about 15 meters across, 5 meters high, and chitin thicker than plate armor. If they see you, they will try to kill you. . They attack anything that moves,\n\nmembers of their own species included.\nWeaknesses: Their eyes are vulnerable, but should you lack for arrows you should try attacking their underbelly, or failing that, playing dead.\nCreation: Unknown. They certainly do not reproduce.\n\n    The Ghost\n===================\nDanger: Low\nDescription: A corporeal entity that is not yet ready to leave this world. Specters have several stages of 'unlife'. Stage one specters are always gray, and flit in and out of existance co\n\nWhat seperates this stage from the others is the fact that, without fail, the spirit will not be able to come to terms with the fact that they are already dead. They usually need a large amount of persuasion and occaisonally hard evidence to make them\n\nrealize this. Stage two specters already realize that they are dead, and are able to begin learning to control their abilities more effectively. One of two things happen to stage three specters. They will either turn blue and become good, or turn red and\n\nbecome pure evil. This is usually in response to how well they were treated in their unlife, or how evil they were when they still lived. Powerful specters are capable of invisibility, minor manipulation of physical objects, and ejecting ectoplasm.\n\nWeaknesses: Spectres can be banished with a single swing of a weapon, especially holy and gold instruments. They can and will come back to life later, however. They are also unable to cross even the thinnest of gold lines.\nCreation: Spectres ar\n\ncreated when someone dies, but cannot come to terms with their own passing. They become stuck betwixt.\n\n    The Graven\n===================\nDanger: High\nDescription: Graven are evil spirits who died carrying a great obsession in their hearts. As it drove them in life, so to  does it drive them in death.These spirits will wander the l\n\nendlessly pursuing their unattainable goal, and the pursuit of that goal itself becomes the very fuel that keeps them alive. Above all else, do not look a Graven in the eye. Their eyes are portals into their maddened soul, and will instill a lasting\n\nmadness into the hearts of those who see it.\nWeaknesses: A graven can be banished easily with any weapon, but is particularly susceptable to gold, and holy objects. Likewise, they are unable to cross any line made of gold. In special\n\ncircumstances, is also possible to banish them forever by completing the task that drives their madness.\nCreation: Gravens are created when a truely obsessed person meets an untimely demise.\n\n   The Apparition\n===================\nDanger: EXTREME!\nDescription: An apparition is an amalgation of many, many lost spirits combined for one purpose, and that purpose is pure evil. Apparitions are malicious, and very dangerous t\n\nThey are capable of incredible acts of telekinesis and illusion, beyond what any living mage could ever accomplish. Normally, apparitions are bound to a central pillar, marked by many skulls and skeletons littering the area around it. If you come across\n\none such pillar, is vitally important that you DO NOT DAMAGE THE PILLAR IN ANY WAY, SHAPE, OR FORM. Destroying the pillar will weaken the beast temporarily, but afterwards it will be able to roam the world at large, bringing great chaos in it's wake.\n\nWeaknesses: An apparition is significantly more powerful than a spirit. The use of gold weaponry can keep it at bay, but the banishment itself lasts only mere moments. Only a very thick ring of gold can contain it. The only way to kill them\n\npermanently is through the aid of a team of Clerics or Shamen\nCreation: The exact origin of Apparitions is murky. From what can be gathered, they are formed from the death of many individuals in one place, at the same time.\n\n  The Boogeyman\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: Yes, the boogeyman is real. Well, was real. The only known boogieman is currently dead. Boogeyman are sentient collections of bugs that swarm around a central corpse. B\n\non the only known boogeyman's example, boogiemen are intelligent, and extremely murderous, taking pleasure in killing innocents. When endangered, the bugs inside the boogieman will scatter in all directions. Because of this, when hunting the Boogiemen it\n\nis imperative that you take him by suprise.\nWeaknesses: Boogeymen are weak to fire, and crushing implements. Gold hurts it, but a sword will not have much effect on the swarm.\nCreation: Unknown.\n\n     The Oolog\n===================\nDanger: Moderate\nDescription: The Olog  is roughly twice the size of an orc, and  nearly three times as stupid. A product of large amounts of orcish inbreeding, Ologs were raised for having muscle an\n\nand their bodies show it. Still descendant of Orcs, they also are capable of bloodraging, making them twice as dangerous.\nWeaknesses: Ologs are stupid. I mean, really stupid. Use that to your advantage.\nCreation: These creatures are\n\n(loosely) considered Natural' beasts, and reproduce normally.\n\n    Conclusion\n\nThis book has merely scratched the surface of what lurks in the night. Expect more books in the furture.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  Stay Alive, Atheria.", ""),
        StaticBook("IHBH:SA", "§bSer Paul Ryan", "- - - - - - - - - - - -         It's Hard\n    Being Handsome:\n\n  How to survive in \n  Athera, and other\n        life tips\n- - - - - - - - - - - - \n   By: Ser Pavl Ryan\nWith special foreword         by Emperor \n   Tuvya Car\n\n TABLE OF CONTENTS: \n\n- Foreword\n- Authors Note\n- Chapters I-V\n- About the Author\n\n        FOREWORD\n-------------------\n\nMeeting Ser Paul Ryan, much less becoming good personal friends with him, will most certainly be one of the most defining moments of my life. I've seen much in my time as the Emperor of Athera's greatest nati\n\nnever have I seen such strict dedication to greatness as I have in Paul. Whether it was making him part of my privy council, calling upon him to lead a heroic charge in times of war, or simply asking the favor of his attendance to my young daughters\n\nnameday party, I knew I could count on a man as loyal and reliable as Paul. Reading his first book, as well as getting a sneak peak at his upcoming biography, granted me a different outlook on life, and how I live it. Never before have I experienced such\n\na thrilling page turner as I have when reading \"It's Hard Being Handsome\". I recommend this fantastic encyclopedia of majesty to all men and women, regardless of age, race or gender, who one day wish to become sucessful.\n\n     AUTHORS NOTE\n-------------------In my times of travel around the land of Athera, I've come to learn a great deal of things, both through speaking to some of the oldest and wisest masters of \nmany skills, and trial and error as I blundered\n\nmy way through city after city, town after town. I've learnt how to fight great mythical beast, how to drink a \ndwarf under the table, how to hide from halflings, sell my legitimate wares to all kinds of illigitimate folk, and a great deal of other ski\n\n. But if there's \none thing I've learned above all else, it's this; \nIt's hard \nbeing handsome. \n\nHi, I'm Ser Paul Ryan, and this is my book.\n\nMany times through the years, I've been approached by great kings and lowly merchants, all desperate for my advice. I've been the honored guest in many foriegn \ncourts, and handed out justice in my own lands.\n\n I recieved many great awards, both for my continued service to House Carrion and Oren as a whole, and for helping\nout the distressed through all kinds of situations. Yet I soon found out that, no matter how great I was (and trust me, I was great),\n\n my life always seemed....\nempty. By the time I had done all of these great things and achieved knighthood and gentry status, all at the ripe old age of 18, I decided to write down my \nadventures, and, more importantly,\n\nthe rules with which I've come to live life. In the following pages, you too will learn to live by these rules. Good luck, friend,\nand I hope you enjoy it!\n\nCHAPTER ONE (I)\n-------------------Find friends:\nOne of the earliest lessons I learned in life was this; EVERYTHING'S better with friends, friend. Becoming close acquaintance to esteemed men and women like the \nruling class of Oren,\n\nor simply the pal of the local drunk and homeless, friends help you through all sorts of trouble. Need a place to stay? Fine a friend. Need\na loan? Find a friend. Need help breaking Goldsteins' stinking knees, because he still hasn't paid you back\n\nfor that time in the brothel? Find a friend. No matter\nwhere I go in all of Athera, I can always count on finding room and board, courtesy of my good pals. If you really think you're a step above the rest, you can even\ntry to become one of MY frien\n\nand join Paul's Pals™, my adventuring group of heroes. For better or for worse, helping out someone in need of a hand can result \nin some good luck coming your way down the road. Remember my original and trademarked saying:\n\n A friend in need is a friend indeed, who, in the future, will owe you™. \n\nCHAPTER TWO (II)\n-------------------Find fortune\n\nOne of the greatest assets any man has in lifes' adventure is his coin purse.\n\nMany a schlub can be bribed, and it never hurts to have the pocket coinage to buy that\nfancy new automatic crossbow, or perhaps donate to your favorite local political party. But how does one obtain such vast, impressive wealth like that owned by\n\nthe plutocrats of our age, such as Emperor Tuvya, or Ser Paul Ryan? Well, friend, let me tell you; hard work, creativity, and a good bit of honest borrowing can go far. I myself made my first fortune when I founded CapCo™, Oren's premier\n\nentreprenuerial company, which now is valued at roughly 500,000 minas. By working hard to achieve\nyour dream, and marketing your products correctly, you'll soon build the capital needed to further your endeavors, like\n\nperhaps launching a new, better company. Good\nbusiness partners are a must have, and I myself continue to hold close correspondance with my good friend and investor, Jacob Goldstein, of Goldstein & Company. After I safely handed over CapCo™\n\nto the care of my board of directors, my next startup companies, Paul's Pawn & Picking™, Paul's Tonics & Powders™, Paul's Ghost Hunting™, \nand Paul's Travelling Stall™all quickly flourished under my careful experience. Need some help starting down the\n\npath to vast wealth? Try finding a local investor\nto give you a startup fee, and bleed that sucker dry! If you need some immediate cash, perhaps to pay back the loan shark who threatened to break your fabulous \ncheekbones, consider\nborrwing som\n\nsomeone elses valuables and using those to pay. Remember, friends: It's not illegal if you're not caught. \n\nCHAPTER THREE (III)\n-------------------Find your talents\n\nIt never helps to have good qualities, friend.\n\n I myself am incredibly handsome and creative, and possess a myriad of skills that would make a jack of all trades cry\nuncle. But how can you exploit the talents you have? Simple; by deceptively manipulating others. Are you a heavy hitter? Consider\n\nstrong arming your way into the \nlocal tavern, and borrowing some of his ale to sell later at a profit. Small and sneaky? Deceptively sneak into a store after hours, and help yourself to the register. \nOr perhaps you're like me,\n\na reknown inventor throughout the lands, sought after for his political savviness and charm. Remember that in this life, NOTHINGS free. Make\nsure you charge the right amount to give that little girl the location you saw her lost dog in, or to hide that\n\nhalfling running from some hungry orcs. If you don't \ncapitalize on all of your chances to make yourself more marketable, you'll never make it in our dog-eat-dog world.\n\nCHAPTER FOUR (IV)\n-------------------Find adventure\n\nSure, friend, you may be able to talk the talk, but can you walk the walk? It doesn't matter if you've accomplished all of these other steps to becoming great, if you don't USE them! Go out on\n\nroad, and venture into lands previously uncharted. Have a drink at that edgy tavern, or consider stopping by your good dwarf friends\nto see what they've been up to lately. Seeing the world is its own lesson, one that anyone can take, and for free.\n\n Learn how to fight or talk your way out of \nany situation by haggling with the Vanirs over the price of a fish, or wrestling with Orcs in their sand pits. Awe the local milkmaid with tales of your completely\nlegitimate exploits, or spend a night s\n\nat a tavern to cover your room and board. Life in our world is uncertain, friend, but it's always worth checking around the \ncorner to see what kind of trouble you can get into. Fall down and break a leg, or wake up without memory in the temple of thos\n\nmonks who definitly enchanted this\nholy water I can sell you at a discount price? Get back up, and try again. If you're ever torn between relative safety, or a possible adventure, ask yourself one \nthing: What would Paul do?\n\nCHAPTER FIVE (V)\n-------------------Putting it all together, and surviving the process\n\nYes, friend, it's challening to learn how to be as great as me, and even more challenging to try, but the results will always pay off. By combining\n\nmy advice with\na little salt-of-experience you gain on your own, you'll quickly find yourself developing into the man or woman you only dreamed of becoming. Go out there, learn\nyour good qualities, get rid of your bad ones, and make\n\nsome good memories while you're at it. Work your way from the gutter to a palace, and go from using that\nrusty dagger to defend yourself to summoning the most powerful of magics. You will fail at first, friend. After all, no one is perfect.\n\n(well, actually, speak for yourself, bub)\nbut the lessons you learn in your failure will help you in years to come. Inevtiably, the great success you'll achieve will make the lesser peons\nof this great realm jealous of you. They'll wish they had yo\n\ncreativity, your work ethic, and above all, your dashing good looks. There's a great deal I've learned\nmyself in my many adventures, most of all I've found that, yes, it really IS hard, being handsome. But would I ever give it up?\n\nNot for anything in this world, friend. \n\n- Ser Paul Ryan\n\nSome Quick Tips! \n\nWant to get better at those strange moments of your life, when everyone suddenly has magical symbols above their heads, and people start hitting each other? Try \npracticing in your free time with some pals and a wooden\n\nsparring sword, or, if worse comes to worse, learn how to flee effectively! To fight another day, of course.\n\nDon't try so hard to win all of the time, friend! In gambling, tussling, or even a friendly debate, losing can often yield more than winning.\n\nIf you see Paul or one of his many friends throughout the land, consider stopping for a chat or challenge with them, rather than strangely running and jumping by.\n\nPick a skill or service, become talented in it, and learn how to make a living through it. Sell your paintings or swords in a stall, or on the road, like me! Get a job as a petty laborer to garner experience, before ultimately starting a rival\n\ncompany up with stolen secrets, and crush your former boss!\n\nGo outside every once in a while, friend. And I don't just mean leaving your hovel in Athera.\n\n\nHave fun, friend. What else are we here for?\n\n - About the Author - -------------------Ser Paul Ryan is a successful warrior, statesman, and inventor of great reknown. Founder and CEO of CapCo™, and a number of other popular brands, such as \nPaul's Pawn & Picking™,\n\n Paul's Travelling Stall™, Paul's Pals™, and Paul's World Fair™, he was born in the small village of Wesconsen, before squiring under Boris Carrion III. \nKnighted by the late Emperor Peter Chivay for valor extraordinare in the field of battle.", ""),
        StaticBook("Unsound Spells", "Anawkin", "Upon Unsound Magic\n\n A relatively weaning magic in the eyes of it's users, Unsound is derived of three basic elements that I shall relay to you today.\n\nFirstly, one must make contact with either a voidal horror or teacher of said magic to obtai\n\naltered spellcasting.\n\nSecondarily, you must establish a connection with a fabbled watcher of which haunts your mind fervently. This is done through the horror or teacher's will.\n\nNext, we have the draining effects\n\nto one's persona, an unsound mage will succumb to a variety of personal afflictions, each of which is dependent upon how the user reacts. This could range from uncoth twitchings, bi-polar disorder and even murder.\n\nLastly, are anomalies,\n\nwhich are practically rifts to the void. An unsound mage can cast these only when attuned to their observer (( a second connection)) and the effects are rather crippling. They eat everything at a slow pace, but seem to draw towards mana.\n\nWritten by Orias.", ""),
        StaticBook("Smoke Evoking #3", "§bMythras Sylvari", "More Smoke-Evoking notes.\n\n30th of the snow's maiden, 1445.\n\nI write this, currently. I plan on soon taking apprentices, though I am in personal debate on whether to also teach the secrets of smoke-evocation.\n\nI write this after heavy thought, and think I might not. . But then what form of teacher am I, one who hoards knowledge?\n*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*-*\n\nNow, to begin. I discovered, that the manipulation of the smoke, is quite simple.\n\nYou must study its properties more than I originally did, or the spell may fail multiple times. \n\nThe properties you should study, is its gass like form, and spell, and even perhaps how it feels, steamy, and weird.\n\nYou must learn first previous to this, to channel your energy so that you may connect with the Void.\n\nThe Void is patron to all mages of the arcane, and as such, must be used in this new form of magic.\n\nFor now, this'll be my third note, I shall keep this in my library. I believe I should avoid from handing these notes to any apprentices for now, until they've expanded their mana pool.\n\nWritten by,\nMythras Sylvari", ""),
        StaticBook("Against Nature", "§bNyxxa", "- Not Against Nature-\n\nGreetings and Salutations Esteemed Readers. I am called Nyxxa and today I am writing this book for the sole purpose of the examination of voidal magic, from the stand point of a non void mage, and for the result of better infor\n\nThose that have cast out void mages as heretical against the natural order.\n\nTo begin, First let us state the problem. The complaint that has been paramount about void magic is that it is in fact a corruption of nature.\n\nLet us then knowing that this is the problem examine nature a moment.If the book 'The History of Magic' original pronounced by Arch Mage Slayer is correct in the beginning there was only the void.\n\nLet us think on that for a moment. If in the beginning there were in fact only the void then all thing, and I do mean all things, MUST have begun there. \n\nThis would mean that those that are called \"void mages\" are in direct contact with the plane th\n\ncreated all things. We can therefore easily conclude that \"void magic\" is simply another method to access the basest of elements, the power that was the beginning of everything.\n\nHowever, I recognise that not all person will be eager to follow the wo\n\nof an Arch Mage, a practitioner of \"void magic\" himself. So I will examine this from another angle.\n\nDeities, where did they come from, there has been no referance in all of my readings safe for the afore mentioned book.\n\nThis paper will not speculate on the creation of such greater beings, instead let us examine how they function.\n\nThere are a miriad of novels on this subject. From 'The Book of Xan' to 'A Harbinger's Tale'\n\nFor the purpose of this paper will will only examine but a few. firstly 'A Harbinger's Tale Vol. 2'\n\nA very contriversial piece of work 'tis true however in this volume it is described that this greater being bestowed power upon these mortals, and th\n\nfeeling and method of such. it also speaks of bloodstones. Bloodstones are much like shade gems, and shade gems are produced using a fairly standard method of \"void magic\". Without being able to examine a diety or greater being directly, one could not\n\nhave absolute proof of such, however I speculate that they may have the same origins. \n\nThis brings up a question, the creation of the world. I will be writing another book upon this particular segment after a journey to speak with\n\nthe denizens of the immortal plane, however at current what I will state is this.\n\nWhile there are many theories on the creation of everything does the creation of everything not have a singluar starting point?\n\nIn all of the tales it does. This means far stretched as it maybe that the origin of druidic, shamanistic, deity, and void magic must, in absolution be the same.\n\nSo in conclusion, Void magic in and of it'self came from the same origin as all other f\n\nof magic on this and other planes, the way it is used is what defines a mage, not the direct connection that a void mage makes to this origin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Translocators p2", "_Elad_", "Translocators Mk.1:\n\nFirst Observations-\n\nThere appears to be a delay on the appearance of entities through a set of portals, but it otherwise works just as Rasmot's closets had. The creation of the portal at first results in a great\n\npulling force towards the opening. Such an effect may be troubling to observe, but otherwise seems harmless. Further tests may be required. Organic matter has yet to be tested for transportation, but normal objects as stated transport successfully.\n\nAn era of magic has dawned, and we are the Harbingers of the future.\n\nHuman Trials-\nThe first guinea pig passes through the gateway as I write. We are hopeful, but it is uncertain whether or not the elf quite literally walks into his own death.\n\nFootnote:\nIn waiting, we have coined this delay in translocator transportation with the name \"lag\". \n\nHuman Trials Cont.-\nGlacio has passed through the portal. We watched with anticipation for his return, and a few elven minutes later, there\n\nhe was. This new delay still brings concern, but i'm certain with some manner of tinkering, and perhaps more exotic and rare gems, it can be lessened. Organic and non-organic manner is officially clear for teleportation.\n\nNew developments in world events render the translocator useless. These 'tomes of power' have made my invention defunct, and now I am stuck with nothing more than a fancy arch. Shame.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elements", "§bJerry_Man", "PROLOGUE\nThis book was recovered from Aegis and is dated around 1378 of the last age of Aegis. The author has since dissappeared from existence.\n\n          WATER\nThe neccesity of life. All animals, plants, and even we, the races of Aegis, need it to survive. Water can often be associated with emotion, art, time, and especially healing.\n\n         EARTH\nIt is the first thing you need for almost everything, to ensure stability and endurance. Earth is a reliable element, peaceful and tranquil. Earth is the most passive and strong element, although it can be quite destructive.\n\n           AIR\nIt is invisible, unpredictable, unreliable, soothing, inspiring, and destructive. Air is the representation of everything we cannot see; our spirits, our souls, our minds, and our hearts.Of that what lies beneath, or beyond some\n\nscholars say. The unpredictable and changing wind can become a devestating Hurricane, or a playful breeze.\n\n            FIRE\nIt has been an important part of all cultures and religions in the past to modern day Aegis. Fire is bright, strong, takes charge, and wants control. Fire is never subtle, it proudly shows itself. Fire never stops unless acted upon b\n\n another element or force, and it consumes everything it touches.\n\n  To Become A Mage\n There is much an apprentice must learn before becoming a Mage. Your Guild Master may send you on quests of sorts, but I prefer to study in the Library, the source of much information. Here, you can learn everything you need: ...\n\nThe Elements, Self-Control, Mage Powers, and much more. This is the first part in become a Mage, studying. You need to learn all you can from your experiences and readings. Once an Elven Week has passed, possible longer, you will be asked to gather\n\n materials. These will be used to create your staff. The particular ingredients in your staff will cause a different outcome,  than if you were to use different materials. This Staff you create will be specially connected with you, your spirit\n\nenergy will be infused with the energy of the staff, thus the connection. Once you have earned your staff, you will become a Mage, and be given a job within the guild.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Mechanics", "§bTasko", "((OOC NOTE: YOU CANNOT LEARN MAGIC FROM THIS TOME, IT MERELY EXPLAINS WHAT THE MAGIC IS.))\n\n    Arcane Evocation\n\n             by\n\n           Tasko\n\nChapter 1: Basics\n\n   When one uses evocation magics such as Pyromancy, Hydromancy, etc, you form the element in the void and pull it into the physical realm.\n\n   When one uses Arcane evocation, however, you form\n\nyour aura in the void, manifesting it in the physical realm in a variety of forms. This magic is incredibly complicated, and is practically impossible to learn on one's own.\n\nChapter 2: Manifestation\n\n   Arcane energy is essentially condensed gas. It is made up of hundreds of tiny wisps of gas that coalesce in your mind. However, it is able to become semi-solidified when formed in the physical realm.\n\n   When manifesting your aura, it can take many forms. You are almost only limited by your imagination. A few impossible things include making solid barriers, armor, and platforms. A few uses include making permanent moving art fixtures, animals made from\n\nyour aura, and arcane missiles that are essentially fist-sized balls of arcane energy that can be conjured easily and fired with incredible speed.\n\n   One must be warned, however, that beginners creations have a chance of\n\nexploding on contact with the physical. This only appears to be an explosion, and does not knock back or damage those near it.\n\n   On another note, you cannot merge this magic with other types of evocation. In theory, it is because it is not an eleme\n\ncapable of being merged with the existing four elements. Also, you can make things that appear to be fire or water, however they will not give off a temperature.", ""),
        StaticBook("Illusion Magic", "Sorairogyoku", "The Art of Illusion Magic\n\nAlong with the sub sections of it.\n\n-Sensory Magic\n-Mental Magic\n-Cognatism\n\nSensory Illusion\n\nAs of today it's not very understandble in it ways, as all magics have the under Illusion magic has the ability to create a illusion of some type, this one is the best at making them. As they last longer and tend\nto be more deta\n\nThey can sway the 5 senses of any human, elf, of what ever creature it might be. Making them hear, touch, small, see, or taste something the not really there. Or replace the item with another. A person who is master at this skill can get any men to drink\n\nmercury. It requires hard work, and back ground information on the magic, really magic itself to use this magic. So it's not a type that begginers should start on.\n\nMental Magic\n\nHave a unique ability to connet other mines, or to invade them. They also have the power to create illusions, but they're not as powerful as a sensory illusion mage's. This too is not a magic for noobs.\n\nThis also requires background information before a student can even think of using it. A mental mage can break into a person mine and listen to their thoughts by enter thought into the person's head (normally in the person's own voice) to sway them to a\n\nideal.\n\nCognatism\n\nLast of the three sub types. Here the mage can split their mines into smaller one to preform a purpose. It's a complaccated magic, hard to discribe. And user that uses cognatism magic cannot use mental magic since they do not mix.\n\nOne must understand the magic before seeking a teacher. This is no easy task. Most time the magic is used to collect information across an area. Where revelation happen for the user.\n\nMisunderstanding of Illusion Magic\n\n-Users cannot do mine control, only put thoughts into people heads.\n-This magic cannot effect the pshical plane of the land, they are only illusions\n-Normally illusion come from the person's\n\nown experience. So you can make a illusion of somebody dying since, well you didn't die.", ""),
        StaticBook("Time Warping", "Minuscule_Evil", "Time Warping\n\n      by, Tahjeet\n   Asul'mira Mubdee\n\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\n\nIf the theory of time as an illusion is correct then it is possible that time itself can be warped, molded or shaped, by the will of a person.\n\nTime, although a perception, an illusion is viewed as reality anymoment where the perception of ti\n\nis changed, it is in the eyes of all, truly changed as a reality.\n\nBut to be able to learn to warp the perception of time, an illusion, a person must know how to create and mold illusions.This can be done with, perhaps, one’s mana alike how\n\nevocationists can create and change the arcane through the casting of mana.\n\nTo make a comparison, time is like a piece of iron and the one who can mold this piece of iron is the blacksmith, in this case an illusionist.\n\nTo shape and mold the iron, it requires the iron to be heated., the casting of ones mana, then to shape the piece of iron it requires a hammer, this will be the illusionist’s ability to mold and shape the illusion or perception.\n\nFor example, if the blacksmith hammers the iron flat it become elongated- lengthening time-if the blacksmith hammers the iron into a smaller length it becomes shorter – shortening time– if the blacksmith hammers the iron from a different angle,\n\n becomes bent - perhaps stopping time.\n\nWhat may be that separates simple illusions and the warping of the time illusion, which may be the reason no illusionist, is that time is an illusion seen by all and perceived as a reality.\n\nThis changes what that iron is. The piece of iron the blacksmith had been shaping was just a small piece of a large statue.\n\nThe illusion of time surrounds us, we are immersed in it, fragments of the illusion can be shaped, changing what we see and feel. It is impossible for anyone to truly see time as an illusion even though it is known to be so.\n\nLiving beings are designed to perceive time as a reality, to see old and new, growth and withering, life and death.\n\nTo understand time is to not see through its illusion.\n\nTo warp time is left in the hands of the curious.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Concepts", "Eenhoornheid", "Arcane Magical Concepts \n\n          by Kalenz Uradir\n\n      It is the arcane mage which summons their spells from the void. However, simply connecting to the void and summoning forth what a mage desires is no simple affair.\n\n    Just as the novice artist finds themselves incapable of painting in as much detail as a master, a mage must learn the simple aspects of arcane magic which makes said magic possible before they are capable of producing anything desired.\n\n    Let us then look at the casting of a spell. It is the mage who uses their mind to connect to the void. Which in turn is combined with the energy of their mana to form their desired arcane subtype.\n\n    However, even if one is to know that, there are many other simple elements of magic which must be known to the apprentice mage. Shifting to the topic of aura.\n\n    Aura is quite simply is a field of mana which surrounds a mage's body while they cast their magic.\n\n    Almost each and every mage is to take upon an aura, though they are often very faint and are only evident to the careful observer at an almost uncomfortable range. Thus, to pick a mage out by aura alone is difficult if not impossible.\n\n    It is often said that aura takes the color of a mage's personality. Each having a different color depending on their particular person.", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic: Vol. 2", "§bRatemenatorz59", "Void Magic is the art of extracting elements from the void, and commanding the elements.\nThe Void is an endless space, in which elements reside in. Those who delve in the arts of the arcane are able to pull these elements from this 'endless space' and\n\nare able to command it to do their will.\nIt is not 'creating things out of nothing', however. To command these elements at will, and to extract them from the void, you will need mana.\nThe exhaustion of mana varies upon the magnitude of your spell.\n\nFor example, though you won't succeed, trying to mold fire as a beginner may exhaust an incredible amount of mana. Don't try this, it may kill you.\nTo be able to use void magicks, you require a connection to the void, but that is a story for another da", ""),
        StaticBook("EWOROENLETEA", "§bThurak'Yar", "Entities within our realm of Existence no Longer Existing, And Then Existing Again.\n\nOr, Void Translocation\n\nRescribed by the Farseer Thurak, 1'st of Snow's Maiden, 1488\n\n1. Introduction\n\n2. Study\n\n3. Sensory Overhaul\n\n4. Destruction\n\n5. Re-Creation\n\nIt does no take much searching within a library to gain some concepts of the Void as an alternate existence outside, winin and with no relation at all to our reality. Arcanists, Mages, Sorcerers- whatever the name- users of voidal magic pull a 'thing'\n\ninto this realm that did not previously exist within it, and hold it there for as long as they can wield a void connection. But no ‘thing’ pulled from the void is retained here. Such power is reserved to The Creater to pull real matter from The Void.\n\nBut what is a ‘thing’ –be it inanimate, plant, animal, edible- already existed? Then the connection to The Void need only be instantaneous, because the ‘thing’ is not created, but simply IS.\n\nStudy\n\nTake within your hands something that exists. \nAny kind of thing will suffice and for the sake of example we shall call it and any potential other thing \nan 'Entity'. Begins your examination in the simplest of interests:\nForm.\n\nWhat size is it?\nWhat’s it made of?\nHow heavy is it?\nHow malleable is the material?\nDoes it react to heat?\nWhat happens under great pressure?\n \nIf already you are struggling then you should return this book whence it came.\n\nSecondly you will need to form these observations into a mental map of the object. This is a far more complex procedure and verges on a particularly niche form of magic known as cognitism; however Telekinetics may find themselves more easily inclined\n\ntowards this type of thinking. You cannoy be bound by your perceptions in understanding the world. If you are purely an experiencer of your surroundings then you will never formulate any greater understandings of anything ever. So work on that.\n\nIf you are able to mentally comprehend the object beyond what is merely visible and physical and can mentally calculate the entity’s existence, then it is time to understand it magically.\n\nSensory Overhaul\n\nThere may be some slight overlapping of comprehending an entity scientifically through its calculable values and perceiving the entity’s magical value. Aside from universally shifting perspective\n\nwith the aid of magic, the quantity of information required to mentally re-create the entity can be better fulfilled by magically understanding it. All things are magical. All things were originally pulled from a real in which is not a single thing\n\nbut the potential for all things. And thereby all things that exist are still magic. Perceiving magical value is a skill that requires much practise and isn’t really teachable as you either find yourself able to perceive the presence of magic or not.\n\nCertainly with practise comes the strengthening of such a skill; but to attempt to explain to another how they are to ‘feel’ an apple tree from a dozen metres is (in almost all instances) utterly fruitless.\nThe complexities of such a thing all being la\n\n\"\"\n\ndown, what you do understand this entity in such a detailed way, you muse measure its mana supply and sacrifice that same amount of your around; surrounding its attachment to the void with your own so that the entity is no longer isolated in this\n\nworld but, in losing its own link to The Void of its origin, becomes a part of ones’ self. The sliding scale of difficulty is seen here in that the more ‘alive’ an entity is, the more rapidly it produces mana. Anything that has a soul is independently\n\nexisting within this realm and as a consequence produces and burns through mana with such a drastic suddenness that it would be impossible to balance that in any one instant. Soul-less entities then exist somewhere between a completely lifeless sliver of\n\nglass and a being with a soul. As mentioned the more ‘alive’ it is the more mana that will be present, and the briefer the instant at which one may be able to match said supply of mana before it shifts.\n\nNo Longer Existing\n\nEvoked magic automatically returns to The Void when a mage is no longer forcing it to exist in this realm. As it leaves this plane of existence it also ceases to exist itself on all planes. What once was tangiable\n\njust stops and is no more. \nSo it can be in the reverse that something that DOES exist independently of a void connection can have that original connection from the moment of its diving creation re-instated, and therefore able\n\nto return to the nothing from which it came. Within The Void there is potential floating around aimlessly. When it is given an aim through the use of Arcane Magics it is no more the potential of being something but becomes of itself a something\n\nfor that fleeting moment. But without being birthed into existence by the creator it cannot remain as that. However entities that already exist are somewhat different. Though they cease to exist entirely, there becomes a new potential within The\n\nVoid that is assigned to being that entity.\nSo fear not that an entity which by your hand no longer exists may not be brought back into our reality as something temporary or destructive like an arcane missile or a shield of ice. For the\n\npotential of that thing has some divine marking upon it that keeps it sacredly linked to once again become what the Creator made it to be (or more accurately the way that it was, as a ceramic teapot will not become a crude clay but remains a teapot).\n\nTo Return Again\n\nIt is a good thing that all those mental calculations were required to adequately assess the entity before it could be eradicated from reality; because that mental reconstruction of the original entity is the only\n\nthing that maintains it as something that ever existed. A sacrifice of identical mana to cover its original quantity so that a newly independent existence outside of The Void is made (I.e redoing the Creator’s work) will assign the potential\n\nwith its destined form. And the forgetting of such things means eternal damnation upon an entity that once existed in relative peace before you came along and destroyed it.\n\nGood Job,\nYou Meanie.", ""),
        StaticBook("Evocation: Basic", "SerahLove", "In order for Sorcerers to put into use their craft, they must have a deep attunement with and knowledge of their element. A caster must know that fire begins with friction and the many stones that make up the earth. A common rule of thumb is:\n\n\"If the Sorcerer does not know how something functions, he cannot make it work himself.\" This simply dictates that a mage MUST know how water flows and how wind gusts, just as much as he must know how fire feels to the touch. Due to this, sorcerers often\n\nspend a great deal of time in study, on a deep spiritual level, of their respective element(s). Despite this rigorous training, their spells may still deal them harm, just as much as it may harm their opponent.\n\nEvocation is often quite physically an\n\nmentally taxing on the Sorcerer- as it takes a great deal of mana to cast. The larger the object one wishes to bring forth, the more mana is required of him to cast the spell. And just as any other magical branch of the arcane tree, the mage must be\n\ncapable of envisioning where he is casting, and at what- that he must first visualize the spell itself, in his own mind, in order to bring forth its full fury. Therefore, a mage cannot simply conjure a fireball behind a wall, nor can he cause a wave of\n\nwater to appear in an area so distant- so beyond the caster's field of vision. Due to this law, Sorcerers are limited in some regard- hindered by the reaches of their sight.\n\nDespite the seemingly passive nature that any one mage may seem to possess,\n\nhowever remain filthy adominations- dangerous and unholy grotesqueries- who must be promptly taught that such profane powers can bring no good, and must be wholly forgotten, for the sake of every man, woman, and child- for all who walk upon God's blessed\n\nearth.\n\n\n    The Basics of Evocation\n\n\n\n\n\n              - Arthur Versluis\n\n   Revisions by E.S. and A.F.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Telekinesis", "§bSarrion", "On Telekinesis\n------------->\nBy Sarrion Zytiaear\n\nThe following is written from my knowledge as a master of the art of Telekinesis. I was taught by the Infamous Beltran, one of the best at the art I know to this day.\n-Sarrion\n\nTelekinesis is the arcane art of alteration on the environment around the mage by changing a materials gravity and velocity. Simply enough it’s achieved by intently studying the world around the mage by understanding\n\na material inside out and able to weight this material just by a glance. The mage then establishes a mana anchor between them and the object they’re casting on and giving an intense focus\n\non the thought of changing the property of the materials gravity. Distance of the caster and object vary between the skill of the caster, where one who is a student may not be able to lift an object unless it’s a foot in front of them\n\nto a master who may lift an object on the other side of a tea room. When casting the mage is rooted in place due to the intense amount of focus it requires to shift an object, even if it’s just a cup of tea the user must stand still.\n\nIt’s also known that like any other alteration the mage may not lift organic material, fluids, or sands due to how complex the materials are.\n\nCommon combative uses of Telekinesis is the use of throwing knives which can be thrown at the speed of a crossbow bolt by changing it’s velocity, or any other normal day object as a projectile.", ""),
        StaticBook("Rugged Notes", "§bUnknown Scholar", "[!] Along the page you see many strange markings and drawings. They look to be rough copies, at best. There appears to be some sort of archway built of stone;  below it, several odd, circular schematics, or perhaps a map.\n\nNext to the map, the phases of the moon trail along.\n\n[OOC]- View in browser:\nhttp://tinyurl.com/slatrop\n-----------------------------\n\nAn odd name, indeed. Though, the actual device is far more mysterious and eldritch in nature. Translocators, Lori Oathcast refers to them as. Crumena took to calling them closets, as per their birthplace, the closets within Rasmot’s magical porta-potty.\n\nRegardless, the process for creating these translocators is a fairly complex and ritualistic one that involves both a skilled translocationist with knowledge of the subject,\n\nand a powerful enchanter capable of binding the spell to the locations in question.\n\nCreation\nAn enchanter holds the knowledge to spot. One who knows how to send matter to the void and back again must have learnt to create what is like a ‘gateway’ into the void. More than just the item itself, but anything that touches it,\n\neven air. Then again you do it on the other end and the mage attempts to pull the block back through the Void and the enchanter binds that to a doorway or pillar or somesuch. In short, one must reach into the Void and pull out an open space.\n\nMaintenance\nAfter time, it will need a mana supply, or one end will fizzle out before the other and create an endless hole. It’s advised then to have the enchanter available fairly often to refill whatever large mana gem\n\nor crystal you wish to power the translocators’ magic with. As far as I’m aware, this would be the only option, unless one would be able to get ahold of Kalameet’s notes on the mana obelisk. For the ignorant,\n\n For the ignorant, this is a large pillar in which sums of mana are stored for use. The mana cannot be pulled out by any means by a magi to fuel their own spellcasting, but instead it exerts energy needed to power enchantments in the area.\n\nI’d elaborate further, though I’m only going off of what I’ve seen myself.", ""),
        StaticBook("Enchants", "§bCloven Fallentree", "~Lotha's Enchants~~\n\n1) Unbreaking, any armor, weapon, or tool.\nSelf explanatory.\n\n2) Luck of the Sea, any fishing rod. Makes your lure more appealing to fishies! Keep in mind your own fishing skills, though, as results are largely based on enhancing them by some fac\n\n3) Silk Touch, works on all tools. Want stone, instead of cobble stone? Use silk touch and you shall receive!", ""),
        StaticBook("Conjuration", "§bMythras Sylvari", "Conjuration:\n          \nConjuration, is the bringing of life forms formed in the void by the conjurationist, into the world itself.\n\nThe three sub-magicks of Conjuration, are.\n- Primodrialism\n- Perenial\n- Morp\n\nMorphon, is the conjuring of animals, and the creating of them as a entity. \n\nIt's to bring a animal into existence, after lots of study put into the animals insides, and outsides, essentially, interior or exterior.\n\nPerenial, is the conjuring of plant life, after the study of the interior and exterior workings, to do such, is the arcane art of the conjuring of perenials.\n\nEssentially, the conjuring of a studied plant.\n\nPrimordial, is the bringing of elementals into the physical plain.\n\nYou must be learned in the art of evocation, and the added art of conjuration.\n\nIt's essentially summoning creatures made of your arcane element.\n\nConjuration, is as said, a hard art, the many theories enacted suggest slowness in the power of the art.\n\nTo evoke animals and plants, and even elementals, is a valuable skill.\n\nSources:\n\n- Goliath\n- Random Magician \n- Learnings in delver bas.\n\n- Inquisition\n- Theories", ""),
        StaticBook("Arcane Origins", "Eenhoornheid", "Arcane Magic:\n       Origins\n\n   by Kalenz Uradir\n\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Lin’evaral, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Tilruir’Indor Lelien\n\nSince long into the past mages have existed. Pulling their spells and magic into reality. Different mages find themselves specializing in different forms of the arcane. However, the root of this magic throughout those who practice the arcane magic\n\narts is the same. Each arcane mage finds their source of magic from a realm known as the void, to which each living and sentient being is connected.\n\nThe void itself is a realm of infinite potential, yet almost paradoxically is entirely comprised of nothing. It is from this absolute and undetermined potential which spells and magic is pulled forth from. Connecting only with their minds a mage take\n\nthis void and change it into the form which they desire. For an evocationist this may be their preferred element: earth, wind, water or fire. For others this may be an illusion, twisting and bending the minds of their targets.\n\nHowever, it is to be noted that pulling such power from the void is no easy task. For one to be able to control both the amount of power and the form of their desired magic is no easy feat. Indeed, many a novice find themselves rendered unconscious\n\nsimply upon their first connection to the void. But, with practice over time balance is achieved and thus some of the most potent arcane magic is created.", ""),
        StaticBook("Telekinesis", "§bSanguine", "~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~       Telekinesis\nA guide to learning\n\nWritten by Magister\n      Sanguine\n~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~+~\n\nFirst off Telekinesis is a form of Alteration magic, Alteration magic impacts the world around it unlike its void counterparts.\n\n Telekinesis works by altering the force of gravity pushing down on an object. The process of telekinesis is rather simple Focus on an object then with the help of the void alter its gravity allowing it to float.\n\nAlthough at higher progression you will have a better grasp of the object being able to redirect, push and stop different objects.\n\nStarting out you should only be able to lift a few small objects such as a Pebble, but with time you will be able to lift more and heavier objects and that pebble you started with will now be a boulder.\n\nKnow you must have learned a thing or two but here are some Practical uses of Telekinesis: \n~Throwing knifes: They are light allowing you to throw them at your enemies with ease\n~Doors: No problem for any telekinetics just apply force against it.\n\n~People: Now the living are a bit tricky to manipulate so you must indirectly using clothing is a good bypass for it.", ""),
        StaticBook("T.F. Notes I", "§bSarrion Zytiaear", "As I had guessed the art of Transfiguration seems to be just as easy as telekinesis, though this time it requires thorough understanding of Equivalent Exchange and alteration. Every object, no matter how small or large, has dormant mana.\n\nThis mana controls the alchemical make up of every object and such is where alchemy gets its powers, by tapping such and creating elixirs of the likes. This time the idea is to tap this mana using your own,\n\nnot to just change the velocity of this object but to change the whole makeup in your own way.. to alter the material how /you/ choose, though the law of equivalent exchange must be followed, so no turning Ferrum to Aurum any time soon.\n\nMy first connection seemed to be more easy than when I had first connected to control an object’s velocity when I had learned about telekinetics, but this time instead of using my connection to the void\n\nto ‘grip’ an object by this dormant mana, I was actually using my own mana to tap into this mana, and activate it! It was incredible, it had felt like I was one with this object.\n\nEven at my fairly low training with this magic I understand vastly on how this whole concept can be used in the most complex scenarios. For now I am to stick to heating this ball up, or cool it down.\n\nA simple task as temperature is a mere thought, though because of how new I am to this spell It seems to take a toll on my body as if I was a student once more, an odd feeling.\n\nAvenel, after our first lesson, has provide me with this metal ball. I will be using such to practice my first and many attempts of Transmutation, as it’s one of the most easiest matters to understand, especially as a blacksmith such as myself,\n\nor rather ex-blacksmith. It was simple, I had understood the weight of the ball when I had first held it, and I knew the makeup of Ferrum. So it was merely just /thinking/ of the reaction.\n\n-Sarrion\n2nd of Snow's Maiden\n1547", ""),
        StaticBook("Elemental Evo:", "§bEnedor Pastly", "Elemental Evocation\n___________________\n\nElemental Evocation is the art of drawing a temporary form of an element from the void using mana. This sounds simple however it is much harder to do in practice. This is because you cannot actually\n\npull an element from the void, you actually pull a substance that mimics the properties of a chosen element. This means when learning magic, one must study their element in order to understand how it works. \nIt is worth noting that evocationists have\n\nNO power over existing elements.\n\nThe Void\n___________________\n\nThe void is discribed as a dark, eternal plane of nothingness.\nWe find 'nothing' very hard to imagine, therefore the first steps to learning any\n\narcane magic is to meditate in order to try and understand the void.\n\nIt is believed that the creator pulled everything into existence from the void and therefore it is possible for us to use some of the void's energy\n\nto cause changes to the world around us.\n\nMana\n___________________\n\nMana is like an invisible liquid. It flows around the world and exists in all living things, including us.\n\nMages use mana to draw their spells from\n\nthe void.\n\nThe term 'Mana Pool is used to describe how much mana an individual has. Your mana pool determines the strength and duration of spells that a mage can cast. The more experienced a mage is, the better they can manipulate mana.\n\nTypes of Elemental \nEvocation\n___________________\n\nEach evocable element is treated as a subtype of magic as each element has specific properties that have to be studied before one can perform the magic.\n\nFire Evocation\n___________________\n\nFire Evocation is perhaps the most widly performed  evocation as it has many uses. One can create fireballs that can be used in combat or simply create a heat or light source for traveling.\n\nFire evocation is said to be one of the easiest elements to evoke but one of the hardest to control.\n\nEarth Evocation\n___________________\n\nEarth evocation, like fire evocation has many uses aside from combat. The art of summoning rocks and minerals found in the earth is quite useful defensive and brute force combat although the art of\n\ncreating and using materials found in the eath has many more uses.\n\nEarth is a harder element to evoke  as it is more solid then, for example, water.\n\nWater evocation\n___________________\n\nWater is a very diverse element. Water can be found as liquid, solid and gas, all of which can be evoked. \nIce is normally used in combat.\nWater can be used for more day to day tasks like cleaning.\n\nSteam isn't evoked much as it has little use and is hard to learn.\n\nWater evocationists also have control over the temprature of their water.\n\nAir Evocation\n___________________\n\nAir evocation is certainly one of the least used evocations. It generally has less uses then the other evocations. Air evocation can be used for defensive combat as one can use it to push back enemies\n\nand even block some magical attacks.\n\nAir can also be used for more simpler tasks such as cleaning and cooling oneself down with a breeze. Air evocation is hard to study as the element is invisible to our eyes. Instead a mage must feel it to learn\n\nhow it works.\n\nElectrial Evocation\n___________________\n\nElectrial Evocation is one of the most powerful evocable elements however it is very hard to control and consumes a lot of energy. \nCommonly Electrial evocationists create\n\nbolts of electricity to combat their enemies though they have to be careful because just like electricity, the element is easily attracted to metal.\n\nIt also takes longer to summon electricity then the other elements because it uses more energy and\n\nmore mana then, for example, a small ball of water.\n\nDangers/side effects of elemental evocation.\n___________________\n\nThe side effects of Elemental Evocation are similar to other arcane magics and should certainly be looked into before\n\ndeciding to learn the magic.\n\nSide effects include:\n\n-Decreased life span.\n\n-Becoming physically weaker and frail. (This is why many mages use staffs)\n-On some occasions mages have been driven mad by the lust\n\nfor power.\n\nMost of these problems are caused by the fact that magic isn't a natural task for our bodies to carry out and therefore it damages us.\n\nLearning magic\n___________________\n\nIf you decide you want to learn the art of evocation, the best way to go about this would be to find a teacher. This is a hard and lengthy process that can take many years, however, the way you do this is up\n\nto you.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alteration", "§bLefkos Amethil", "=---=   Mana   =---=\n\nWhat is mana?\n\nIn simplicity, mana is an invisible substance that encompasses us and everything we see. Imagine seeing a rock, and lifting it up. Mana resides even so much as within a pointless object such as that. If you\n\nwere to look at the person next to you, even they have mana. What makes people different than objects in terms of mana is the fact that we, as Descendants, are capable of growing and hence manipulating our mana pools.\n\nHow come we see mana when something is transmuted?\n\nYou don't. If you saw one transmute, you likely saw their Aura. An Aura is the excess that comes off of ones mana. The color is very much depending on ones\n\nmental state.\n\nWhat is Transmutation?\n\nTransmutation itself is a rather simple concept. Simply altering an object to what you want it to be. In actuality, accomplishing this is difficult and requires immense study upon what you wish to change.\n\nYou must follow the law of equivelent exchange as well, being unable to create diamonds from dirt, or water from rock. You may very well change something like water into ice, or perhaps change the shape of stone.\n\nHow do I transmute something?\n\nWe'll use an example. Take a sphere of ferrum, able to fit in your palm and weighing five kilograms. You must first study ferrum in all its' senses. How it reacts to temperature, pressure, and everything.\n\nYou must as well find its mana signature. A mana signature is the way mana is 'layed out' in a specific object. You may find this able to be done easiest by meditating with the material, and sending your own mana coursing through it at times.\n\nYou may stop once you have familiarized yourself with it.\n\nAfter this, you would summon your own mana, and envelop the ferrum sphere with it. Fill it, coat it, and everything of the like. Much akin to how one 'wills' their evocations to act, you would 'will' the ferrum's properties to change. For this, we shall\n\ninvision a ferrum rod. If you truely know what ferrum is, and how it works, it should begin to shape how you wish it to. The first go will be immensely tiring, as well as bear a danger shared by any and all transmutation.\n\nWhat is the danger?\n\nYour stupidity. If one was to dare try and shape it into something that would require more of the substance then what you posses, you'd find your mana rapidly drained and yourself dead. This goes for any amount.\n\n=--= Enchanting =--=\n\nWhat is Enchanting?\n\nEnchanting is the act of changing the properties of an item, much akin to Transmutation in that sense. The difference here is that you are changing it to have magical ability,\n\nrather then to look different. This does not mean you may use the enchantment as much as you wish, however. This is due to the fact that it still requires 'equivelent exchange'. For this, we shall move onto mana gems.\n\nWhat is a mana gem?\n\nTake a precious material. A finely crafted diamond, emerald, or even gold. The more valuable, the better. These materials, past their own mana, have space to hold more than what they have.\n\nTaking advantage of this, we may go so far as to fill the empty space with our own mana, and then order it to 'fuel' an enchantment. The gem, filled with mana, is hence called a mana gem.\n\nHow do we actually enchant something?\n\nEasy! You are to use your mana much as you did with transmutation, and 'will' the object to cast a certain spell when supplied with mana. It should be noted one can not cast with a magic they can not cast.\n\nAlong with that, you 'will' the mana in the mana gem to supply the enchantment upon a certain order. This can be motion, sound, or physical contact.\n\nDont lie. I know transfigurationists who enchant with things they don't know!\n\nOkay, you caught me. They can, but it's a difficult act. For one, they need someone who knows the magic to help them. Second, they need to fully understand said magic.\n\nWe'll use a water evocationist and me for example. To do 'joint enchanting' with a water evocationist, I must first understand water evocation as though I were capable of actually casting it. After that, I'll have him cast a spell to be wrapped in my mana\n\nOnce I envelop their spell, I will 'break it down' into its original mana that created it, and use my own to funnel it into the object I wish enchanted. The last stage requires a certain level of trust. If the other person gets scared, it will fail.\n\nWhy would they be scared?\n\nBecause, you're essentially taking their mana to do joint enchanting. It gives an odd feeling to them. Such may cause them to grow scared and cease casting, which results in failure.\n\n=--=   Warding   =--= \n\nWhat is warding?\n\nWarding is a more difficult concept, but still one able to be grasped farely quickly. To ward a magic, one must understand it as though to the extent of joint enchanting.\n\nThe difference between joint enchanting and warding is the fact that such can be done on your own, without aid. After you understand the magic you intend to ward, you then create a 'web' of mana. Such takes immense concentration and energy.\n\nAfter some minute of forcing mana out, you have it ready to attack the mana anchor of the magic you wish to ward. As the spell would hit your ward, it should quickly have its mana anchor 'attacked' by your own.\n\nAssuming your ward has more mana than the spell attacking you, it should promptly vanish. If not, or if its a magic you arent familiar with or are not currently warding against, it will simply pass the ward and hit you.\n\n=--= Abjurgation =--= \nWhat is an Abjurgation?\n\nAn Abjurgation is simply a summoned amount of mana. It works much the same as a ward in every way, yet often takes the color of ones aura.\n\nIt's used to be thrown at other peoples spells either before it is finished casting, or in mid air. Abjurgations themselves are created with the purpose of attacking another spells mana anchor, and are quite easy and quick to summon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cognitism", "oblivionsbane", "<>*<>*<>*<>*<>*<>*<>*<>          Cognitism\n<>*<>*<>*<>*<>*<>*<>*<>\n\nCognitism is a magic that allows one to see their own illusions. As any illusionist knows, this is normally impossible due to the nature of illusionary magics. Normally, an illus\n\nvanish if someone were to realize that it was, in fact, an illusion. Getting around this done through a technique known as the observers eye, and it is no over-estimation to say this is the key to this magic. It is done by separating the mind in two,\n\nwhere one views the illusion and the other manipulates it. They communicate through a subconscious connection, never truly being separate. This can cause mild to severe mental issues at first, but eventually as the mage progresses these subside or at\n\nlessen to the point that they aren't noteworthy.\n\nThe ability to see your own illusions through Cognitism creates many uses. I have categorized these uses into three subtypes: Tools, Virtual Representations, and Visual Assistances.\n\nTools are the simplest of the three. They are anything you create that allows you to perform a specific function. Examples of these would be illusionary meter-sticks, measuring squares, and protractors. These are the simple, beginners tools, however.\n\nExperienced Cognats are able to create their own tools which perform significantly better, but they are only possible through Cognitism. An example of this is an illusionary bar that can extend and tell you visually the exact height of a certain object.\n\nThis leads us into our next subtype, Virtual Representations. These are separated into two types, models and overlays. Models are detailed three-dimensional illusions. They can be as large and intricate as a cathedral, and as small and simplistic as a\n\ntack. One use of models is when designing something. For instance, a blacksmith would be able to plainly view the sword he wants to design and make real time alterations to said design rather than simply using the foggy picture in his head.\n\nThen we have overlays, which are basically flat, two-dimensional models. These are useful for scribing and creating blueprints or planning out paintings. Anything that would be have to do with work done on a flat surface could be aided using overlays.\n\nIt is also possible to convert one to another, which makes this particular part of the magic work well with blueprints, since an overlay of a blueprint could be made, then changed into a model.\n\nFinally, we have the real magical aspect of Cognitism, Visual Assistances. This is where all of the \"legendary\" aspects of Cognitism reside. The most basic use of this subtype is creating numbers and symbols to do mathematical operations visually.\n\nThis allows one to not have to worry about paper, and it removed the physical lag between writing the next part of an operation down. If done enough, this can get to the point moderate calculations can be done in a mere moment, and advanced ones might\n\nonly take half a minute or less, depending on the individual. It should be noted that Cognitism does not make one \"smarter\". The person is as smart as they will ever be, but what it does allow is it allows them to do things faster, which is why so many\n\npeople seem to think it can, in fact, make someone smarter. Visual Assistances also allow someone to, technically, improve their memory. This is done through the storing of Visual Assistances, which can give a Cognat highly detailed photographic memories.\n\nNow, we come to a part of Cognitism that is indeed considered legendary, Hyper Thought. Hyper thought is achieved through a state of meditation, where a Cognat speeds up their thinking using Cognitism in an attempt to discover a solution or revelation\n\nover a problem. There is not much more I can say about it, other than it can occasionally leave one mentally fried, with a severe migraine, inability to organize thoughts, and loss of some motor capabilities.\n\nIt also cannot be used in a fight. It ta\n\ngood toll on your concentration to even use Cognitism due to the spectators mind, and any extreme stresses would interrupt the fragile technique. \n\nOverall, if you are a tradesman or simply someone wishing to learn a magic that will enhance your abil\n\nto think and work rather than destroy or manipulate, I would say Cognitism is right for you.\n\n- - - - - - - - - - - \n\nWritten by the master Cognitism mage, Mark Lander\n\n- - - - - - - - - - -", ""),
        StaticBook("Tele Studies", "Cablam", "Telekinesis Studies by Armin Ambertoe\n\nUses of telekinesis:\n- lifting objects\n- throwing objects\n- holding objects in place\n- deforming objects\n- changing a moving object's direction\n- slowing down objects\n\nApplications in a real life scenario:\n\n- lifting a box\n- throwing a ball\n- shooting a projectile\n- holding an object in place\n\nOut of the box ideas:\n- cleaning the house\n- farming\n- fishing\n\n- Drawing, painting (art stuff)\n\n1. Weight\n2. Speed\n3. Amount of objects\n\nWeight: The weight of an object determines how much mana it posseses. For one to perform telekinesis they must use more mana than the object posseses. Therefore, the heavier the object the more mana it\n\nwill take to lift it. \n\nSpeed: As an object is moving it becomes more difficult to focus on the faster it moves. This is because as its location changes it becomes more difficult for a mage to latch a mana anchor onto it.\n\nAmount of objects: As stated earlier, the way one lifts an object with telekinesis is by expending an amount of their mana equal to or greater than the mana of the object they wish to lift. Therefore when attempting to lift multiple objects a mage must\n\nsplit their mana amongst the objects. The same cumlulative weight can be lifted however it is just split between the multiple objects.\n\nTalk with other Telekinetics\n\nTelekinetic 1:\n- Uses telekinesis around the kitchen while baking to help with getting things from across the kitchen, saving her the effort of having to walk around the kitchen constantly.\n\nWas once tied up and kidnapped by a lady and used some heavy steamer trunks to bludgeon her captor.\n\nTelekinetic 2:\n\nUses it to tidy up. Also used it to kill a man with a door who broke his ex-wife's ribs.\n\nUses it to read multiple things at once. Uses it to shoot pointing things at people.\n\nTelekinetic 3:\n\nUses telekinesis to fuck shit up.\n\nUses it in enchanting, making objects travel at high speeds and to ensnare things or make them lighter.\n\nAlso uses it to touch dangerous objects.", ""),
        StaticBook("LWJ: Vol.3, Ed.2", "§bLouis", "\"THE DIARY AND MEMOIR OF LOUIS THE LONE WANDERER VOL. 3:§0\\\n§09th of The First Seed, 1672:§0\\\n§0Met a woman named Marianne riding an unnamed horse at the CT today. Never actually seen someone with a steed ‘round these parts before.§0\\\n\"\n\n\"17th of The First Seed, 1672:§0\\\n§0I’m currently tending the bar of the Frosted Hunter with a new co-worker, Nivias. Seeing as he’s a dark elf, I hope I don’t get hexed or something like what that creature from Vol. 2 did to me.§0\\\n§0I found a new Arborian recruit \"\n\n\"in the form of a snow-elf named Ryku (I think? I forgot Nivias’ name a few times tonight; late-night shifts and long-term insomnia don’t pair well). Notably, she stands at about seven feet tall, almost as high as the average orc. It was a surprise, \"\n\n\"considering every other of their kind was either my height or shorter. Though her speech is broken, her heart is not. I hope to become friends with her (& Nivias).§0\\\n§0\\\n§017th of Malin’s Welcome, 1672:§0\\\n§0I've gone and messed up again. A witness to the \\\"cutting \"\n\n\"incident” was found rotting out in the plaza; his desecrated body haunts the square. His jaw and tounge are cut from his body, he’s covered in gashes and his skin has been saturated by his own blood. Trying to comfort Zat, who was talking about the man\"\n\n\"(Lorenzo)’s death, I accidently unleased centuries of horrific memories, telling her that this kind of thing was out of our control. For the first time in knowing her, her face filled with wrinkles and she burst out in tears. God forbid her PTSD drives\"\n\n\"her to do something drastic; she locked herself in her room and won’t come out.§0\\\n§0\\\n§010th of The Grand Harvest, 1672:§0\\\n§0Once again, my trust has lead me to death’s hand, just to be dropped on the floor like an unwanted child.§0\\\n\"\n\n\"A man in black armor, standing eight feet tall, came to me at the CT and told of an elven family being ransacked on the trail. Blind to the obvious signs this was a trap, I followed him into a clearing off the path where I was stabbed in the abdomen with \"\n\n\"a cleaver, had my insides twisted, and left to die. Going limp, he stole my quiver without checking for a pulse. §0\\\n§0Should’ve gone for the head.§0\\\n§0I limped to Dunshire, not far from the fork in the road, and collapsed in their tavern on the verge of death. A \"\n\n\"nurse named Rose (9) clotted my wound while Kacey gathered supplies to further aid me. I now owe my life to three people.§0\\\n§0After waking up to find my lower stomach carved out and not a trace of anyone, I'm heading back to Arbor to see if I can get better\"\n\n\"medical assistance.§0\\\n§0Kacey sewed up my bloody shirt while I was out. At least I’m not bare-chested.§0\\\n§0\\\n§016th of The Grand Harvest, 1673:§0\\\n§0Found some more lost wanderers today and guided them to Arbor (some disbanded on the trek; more cake for us! Like, at \"\n\n\"future dinner parties and such.). After some consideration from the self-proclaimed leader of the group, they deemed themselves the House of Opus. Trey IV, the leader, only has his father as the last trace of his lineage. A rouge-type elf named Phantom, a\"\n\n\"Wild Man covered in hair, and a loner with white hair and yellow eyes named Yukimura accompanied him. She threatened to to kill me if I asked her for her name, but she wrote it on her trunk, so it wasn’t that that hard to find out. We sympathized on our\"\n\n\"fear of death.§0\\\n§0On moving into their Arborian abode, The Wild Man begun burrowing under the floor, creating a basement (or “cave”, as he’d like to refer to it). Phantom’s asleep, Yuki refuses to work, and Trey is stuck with them.§0\\\n§0I got \$1200 for that \"\n\n\"recruitment. Heck yeah. Still doesn’t fill the void where my snowbank used to be. It didn’t melt until I almost died the other day… what happened to it?§0\\\n§0\\\n§05th of Sun’s Smile, 1673:§0\\\n§0Note to self: Visit Pembrooke (west of CT on way to DOM) and \"\n\n\"visit Nenar. She’s the friend you met negotiating with a Dunshire Halfling, Rosyra, for her horse. She eventually gave it to an elven man (Oakland?). Hope Rosyra has safe passages; 2 1/2 feet isn't a lot of legroom. Not even Ellie or Kersley are that \"\n\n\"small. Ellie’s going to need assistance with babysitting soon, so don’t go too far from home. Keep an eye on Phantom; she’s been upset about something that only The Wild Man knows of.§0\\\n§0\\\n§017th of The Deep Cold, 1673:§0\\\n\"\n\n\"RULES OF ATLASIAN TIME, HUMAN-ELVEN PERCEPTION CHART (& NOTES):§0\\\n§0-30 days in a month§0\\\n§0-7 months in a year§0\\\n§0-Days pass VERY QUICKLY§0\\\n§0-Human week = a few elven hours§0\\\n§0-Elven week = human year§0\\\n§0(The only discrepancy I know of is that I'm\"\n\n\"not an elf. Why do I percieve time like this?)§0\\\n§0\\\n§0An old woman made advances on me. Cyrene, becoming somewhat of a prominent Sutican political figure, built a sauna under the town plaza. After debating death and the like with her and her adult \"\n\n\"friends, they invited me to a pool party where the woman in question farted on me and tried to rope her arms around me. They were all high and watched me struggle. Not accounting for this world’s rapid aging, I'm a minor. It's sickening that Cyrene just \"\n\n\"stood by and smoked some foreign drugs while I struggled to get away. I said I’d rather kill myself than live in such a manner, and one of the guards handed me his knife to finish the job, right then and there.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I pussied out of it. I broke it on a table\"\n\n\"in the Frosted Hunter and threw the broken pieces in the bay next to the entrance. I can’t take this anymore, I’m headed home. Not like I have anywhere else to go; left the keys to the bar at home.§0\\\n§0\\\n§014th of Snow’s Maiden, 1674:§0\\\n\"\n\n\"My house was robbed: books, tools, materials for the bunker; gone. All that’s left scattered on my water & mildew-infused floorboards are lilypads and seeds. Why does this world hate me?§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I was summoned here without my consent and try to make the best \"\n\n\"of it, and all I’m met with is treachery. Worse, I just blew a few hundred on a collection of pulp fantasy novels that turned out to be rubbish. Rather than make use of them as tinder, I donated them to the Arborian Library. §0\\\n§0Met some wood elf with red\"\n\n\"hair named Lorax. “I speak for the trees”, she says. Her parents are dead, so she only trusts trees. A natural progression, I assume; it’s not like a tree can rot away.§0\\\n§0\\\n§017th of Snow’s Maiden, 1674:§0\\\n§0Saw Nenar at the CT and invited her to Arbor. She \"\n\n\"obliged, and made the journey to Arbor. Tour was cut short when she started talking to another half human/elf child and bonded over that fact (the hybrid thing, not the age thing). Glad both of them could grow from that experience.§0\\\n§0How have 3 days passed?\"\n\n\"Went to the Avern Mansion in Sutica to check up on Zat; met her father instead. Despite being scarred and burnt down one side of his body (and apparently having 4 lives), he was an overall gentleman. After convincing him that A) I wasn’t there to confess \"\n\n\"my love to her, and B) I wasn’t going to kill myself after the interaction, I asked him to relay my apologies for accidentally triggering her PTSD and my thanks for all the opportunities she’s given me, in friendship and work. He told me that he would \"\n\n\"never forget this day because of this odd request, and that such kindness would be remembered (something along those lines). §0\\\n§0Life’s looking up.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0???, Grand Harvest, 1674:§0\\\n§0Nevermind. My life's being wagered upon in a dirt hole.\"\n\n\"Roof-hopping this morning (as per usual), I greeted a woman on the street. She asked what I was doing, perhaps breaking or entering, but I politely denied the accusation and tossed her a potato. She walked off, and I thought nothing of it until I heard \"\n\n\"glass breaking from the way she went. I rushed to the source of the sound to find her with a bludgeoning tool, standing in a pool of shattered glass. Pointing the frayed stick at me, it began to spark. She glared at me with a malefic grimace, telling me \"\n\n\"to leave or get killed. I did and tried to snitch, but no guards were present. Anywhere. Wasn’t until I saw her “making deposits” in the town square that I reported her. In return, she suggested I be locked up in an asylum for having even the slightest \"\n\n\"audacity to accuse her of such fictitious crimes. She must’ve fled the scene as soon as I left, for no chests were broken. Only the glass stood as evidence, and her freshly-cleaned hands gave no indication that she’d committed the break-in.\"\n\n\"Going back to the center, I saw Zat arguing with the Demon and Necromancer, something about the ethics of him reviving Zat. The former two ditched the argument, for the Demon had a present to present. I followed them, stumbling and falling off a rock face\"\n\n\"in the process, but managed to climb back up without them noticing. She handed him some gray jar, but saw me peeking over the cliff. I was greeted with an attempted jab to the eye, claws extending from the gestalt of its tightly-formed mass. A simple bob \"\n\n\"and weave, and I was able to keep my eyes. A kick to my skin ntroduced me to the keen, blade-like impression of her claws, which dug and tore through my left shin with the savageness of a wolverine. A final scratch across my face left me glazed, and the\"\n\n\"two walked off. If I were a wiser man, I would’ve cut my losses then and there. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0But I was determined to gain its fellowship, somehow. Not through charm, or shitty puns, but through genuine interaction of two fellow comrades of this life. So when she \"\n\n\"offered to play cards in the rubble of the recently-demolished sauna, I accepted. I knew when I was in the wrong place when I heard the door lock behind me.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Thief and the Demon are playing a game of High-and-Low (dice game; sum of dice 2-6, low;\"\n\n\"8-12, high; 7 for a lucky 7. Extra points for wagering 7 correctly). I was placed on the bid as an “extermination favor”, though it works in the greater interest of them both. I'm signing this so that, if this goes south, there's some record of what \"\n\n\"happened to me. God rest my soul.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0-Louis§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Footnotes:§0\\\n§0\\\n§09) Thomas Bell's her husband, as per coincidence\"\n\n\"Afterward:§0\\\n§0\\\n§0In journal 3.5, I discussed how I saw Aldonza traveling down the road. She's married to Rolando and has kids. I was bewildered, unaware of how much time had passed. I'm just as surprised now. Oh well, gonna die soon anyway. Never had\"\n\n\"cake with the House of Opus, either; haven't seen any of them since the raid on Arbor a few weeks back...§0\\\n§0\\\n§0END VOLUME 3\"", ""),
        StaticBook("LWJ, Vol.2, Ed.2", "§bLouis", "\"THE DIARY AND MEMOIR OF LOUIS, THE LONE WANDERER: VOL. 2:§0\\\n§016th of Snow’s Maiden, 1669:§0\\\n§0I still don’t understand how a year has passed in such a short time. I think I’ll travel to the Library of Dragur to investigate this anomaly. I’m currently in Holm; a \"\n\n\"gentleman greeted me, and, after asking, agreed to lend me his empty journal. No such luck in finding books in the library. I did meet an Argur passing along the roadways fighting some men. . It’s some cloud-like being. I don't remember its name, but why \"\n\n\"would I? How did I get to meet it in the first place?§0\\\n§0That’s odd, I have a blank space for a few hours in between the road to and from Holm. Another strange sight along the highway was a group of people scourging a body, looking at me quite strangely when\"\n\n\"I asked them directions to Holm. I’d just asked a man for food, and§0\\\n§0\\\n§0why would I beg some stranger for food? I stockpiled stuff at my place in Arbor…§0\\\n§0they tried to ignore me until one of them pointed off in its direction to shoo me off... strange people.\"\n\n\"I have no idea what happened to Aldonza, Rolando and Vittore, for I woke up in the clearing with their tents gone and fire reduced to ashes. I’ll have to meet them at the Capital to see what happened. Hopefully Sancho’s been taken care of.§0\\\n\"\n\n\"13th of the First Seed, 1669:§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Arriving at the Capitol, the Legion (along with Arbor and Retanus) announced they’d be heading south to kill the Frost Wyrven. I decided to tag along. (Note: The city is called Horen, apparently. Someone just shouted to hail\"\n\n\"it.)§0\\\n§0We’re here. I have a halberd in one had and this journal in the other. Hope I don’t die exacting retribution or anything…§0\\\n§0We were smart enough to bring actual artillery; scorpions (giant crossbows) with pitch (flammable, tar-like substance) were \"\n\n\"assumed enough to take down the beast.§0\\\n§0It’s here.§0\\\n§0It’s dead.§0\\\n§0I’ve torn the claws from its right hand, the one that snatched both me and Rolando. I gave one (or at least tried to, before being ignored) to everyone who originally fought the beast (minus one\"\n\n\"character named jeff who ran off for help and never came back). I hope one day I can be better friends with Aldonza and Rolando. For now, I head through the deep south. Nothing of importance besides another abandoned castle and a gravestone marked\"\n\n\"“Luna Ross”, who was apparently “always loved”. God rest her soul.§0\\\n§0\\\n§016th of the First Seed, 1669:§0\\\n§0I’ve come across a giant ship in the middle of the Eastern Sea. Managing to climb aboard, I found all the cabins abandoned and locked. Only one\"\n\n\"belonging to a “Cerulean” was accessible. The slowly decaying remains on bonsai trees litter the unkempt floor of the cozy room. A little while westward of the ship is another large port city similar to Sutica: Santegia. The town seems to be deserted...\"\n\n\"probably because it’s close to two in the morning…§0\\\n§0\\\n§010th of Malin’s Welcome, 1669:§0\\\n§0I was killed in an attack on one of the Reiver towers. I remember nothing but Magnus crying “DESPACITO” as we broke down their gates. I dropped this at the scene of the\"\n\n\"attack, but a survivor was able to pass it back to me, along with the information (Thank you, Cedric). Aragon’s been taken captive.§0\\\n§0\\\n§017th of Malin’s Welcome, 1669:§0\\\n§0I’ve finally figured it out. Revival to the CT causes memory loss. That's why I've gone\"\n\n\"gone through such a huge memory wipe, and subsequently smaller ones. This revelation happened upon me when a passing stranger mentioned the Argur from Belvitz, expressing expressing anger at me for “stopping him from killing that daemon. Guess I'll never \"\n\n\"know how I died…§0\\\n§0I’ve traveled to the most Southeastern corner of the island before the ice wall and found a frozen city (not floating, as recent pulp exploration books would tell). The “Xion Tower” on the edge of it did not allow access or show any\"\n\n\"remnant of society, but I was able to scale the wall easily. I saw one man in his home and nobody else. I just realized I lost my Wyrven claw when I was killed by the Reivers. God, I’m an idiot!§0\\\n§015th of the Sun’s Smile, 1669:§0\\\n\"\n\n\"On a hike through the Northlands, I found two abandoned elven settlements. Winterleaf boasted its wealth on the surface level with luxurious houses, a giant shrine to some forest deity, and a massive farm built into their bay via a stone dike. The rest of\"\n\n\"their town was concealed underground; this included bunking, the library and communal area. I donated a copy of Lumiere. Warhawkes held a much grander tale. As I sailed around its fortifications, I finally came to the main entrance. There was\"\n\n\"nobody there, and the gates to the temple were locked (nullifying my efforts to scale the wall and deactivate their security measures, which I successfully did). The remains and offspring of many mystical animal types and incredible feats of technology\"\n\n\"line this ancient camp. Perhaps one of these ancient peoples can assist in my journey home…§0\\\n§0\\\n§015th of the Amber Cold, 1669:§0\\\n§0Came back from the ice city (forgot its name) just to meet a resident at the CT. They were apparently guarding the day I jumped the \"\n\n\"wall and they didn’t notice. Kristine noted that the Blackwell fortress was looking for new inhabitants, and agreed to assist Arbor on a journey to the city. I have low faith in her observation skills (judged by my ability to scale the walls without her\"\n\n\"noticing), but she’s kind. That’s enough for me.§0\\\n§0\\\n§018th of the Deep Cold, 1669:§0\\\n§0In Arbor, I built two snowmen before getting bored and hiking to Belvitz. A man pointed a knife at me on the road and, thinking he was robbing me, offered him my \"\n\n\"Ocarina (as a decoy, rather than being mugged a second time). Rather than being interested in my clay toy or money, he wanted help in rescuing a halfling that was dragged into a tunnel by some rat creature. It was deemed unsafe to go under, though, and no\"\n\n\"one was allowed in. Seeing my service as unnecessary, I wandered into the open doors of a nearby castle, where I was promptly evicted.§0\\\n§0\\\n§014th of Malin’s Welcome, 1670:§0\\\n§0Came across a small farm owned by some rich noble. Though it was walled,\"\n\n\"overgrowth around it made it easy enough to climb up to the roof & climb in through the unlocked balcony. A while more eastward, I found an isle that was conquered by Retanus. Some Barony of the Swordfish?§0\\\n§0There was just an earthquake coming from the NW. \"\n\n\"It’s most likely something worth enquiring about when I get back to Arbor.§0\\\n§0\\\n§018th of Sun’s Smile, 1670:§0\\\n§0Met a kind girl named Melody in Sutica today. She said she was hungry, and some rando popped out of his house and threw a sack of potatoes at \"\n\n\"me. Upon offering her a few, she declined, but said she’d like to keep in touch. She lives in Holm. I actually made a friend!§0\\\n§0(Also ventured the Dominion and CT to no avail).§0\\\n§018th of the Amber Cold, 1670:§0\\\n§0Was robbed again (6). How do I even play this damn\"\n\n\"ocarina?§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Had a fever dream where I woke in the middle of a murky swamp and got bit up by mosquitoes before some guy named March Ash shoves me into a cave and starts preaching about environmentalism before he gives me some stupid riddle. \"\n\n\"The answer was literally the first letters of a red herring sentence. The relevancy was so ham-fisted that I couldn’t take it and killed myself in-dream, but of course I didn’t remember it, and when I woke up I was covered in mud! The hell was that even\"\n\n\"about? Some new person is becoming the September Prince?§0\\\n§0\\\n§016th of Sun’s Smile, 1671(7):§0\\\n§016th of Sun’s Smile, 1671:§0\\\n§0I’ve been camping on a desert island in the middle of the ocean. I forgot how I got here, but there's a huge Aztec-like temple in th\"\n\n\"center. Blood lines the stairs and alter on top of it. I forget how long I’ve been here (8).§0\\\n§0\\\n§016th of the Deep Cold, 1671:§0\\\n§0A man named Dale told me that there may be a way out of this blasted world through the void, but advised against it. A woman named \"\n\n\"Eurielle Sistine Skelt gave me a better alternative; she suggested I find someone to love and settle down in this realm. At turning her offer down, she told me that all I was doing was dragging myself down into a pit of self despair. I couldn't agree more\"\n\n\"with her. I came to the epiphany that, maybe, my youth was so full of experience that it seemed infinite. Maybe this is all just a dream that, when I die, I’ll wake up from and continue in another life. Who knows? I’ll know how life and death works in \"\n\n\"this world when I die. Whenever these people or this world decide to expel me, I’ll gladly leave. Maybe I’ll be granted entry back to this realm one day. For now, I’ll just have to wait and see what my life has waiting for me…§0\\\n\"\n\n\"17th of the Snow Maiden, 1672:§0\\\n§0I just had the worst day of my life. I walk into Sutica and see Cyrene talking to some blackened, masked being. When I asked what it was to the couple, it dissappeared after showing I'd pissed it off. In a puff of smoke, she\"\n\n\"reappeared, slicing me across the chest thrice. Bleeding horribly from this attack, Cyrene applied some green medical paste to my butchered flesh.§0\\\n§0This induced horrible hallucinations and spasms. I blacked out and woke up at the gates of the Dominion,\"\n\n\"where it began snowing. Three people said they’d help me, but left me to freeze. It was a golem that opened the gates, led me into the town, and laid me to rest. 0/10, would not goop again.\"\n\n\"Afterward:§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Never found my claw, never found the spirit's name, never found a real purpose.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Footnotes:§0\\\n§06) A large inkblot would destroy most of my work here in the original copy.§0\\\n§07) Originally dated incorrectly to 1670.\"\n\n\"8) ((1304, -2604))§0\\\n§0\\\n§0END VOLUME 2\"", ""),
        StaticBook("LWJ Vol.1, Ed.2", "§bLouis", "\"THE DIARY AND MEMOIR OF LOUIS, THE LONE WANDERER – VOLUME ONE:§0\\\n§010th of the Amber Cold, 1668 (1):§0\\\n§0I can’t recall the last time I saw my family; as a matter of fact, I can’t remember what they look like, their jobs, or even my own family name.\"\n\n\"This is my current dilemma, which is the fact that I love those who are long gone and who I most likely have no hope of ever seeing again. Nevertheless, my current quest is to find someone in this strange land who can assist in restoring my memory & \"\n\n\"guiding me home. I have failed to accomplish this quest multiple other times, which I shall record later on, but there are more pressing things to be rediscovered, such as my surname, age, homerealm, etc. I need to clear my amnesia before retelling my \"\n\n\"life story.§0\\\n§0Thus begins my Atlas Anecdote...§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Two weeks ago (or two years, depending on who you ask). I awoke in the Cloud Temple, greeted by a monk who told me he hadn’t the slightest idea why the higher monks had summoned me. Great.\"\n\n\"He added that I may have been a wandering soul from the void. Surviving on potatoes and other rubbish along the road, I headed south until a skeleton attacked me (2). I was saved by a passing knight, who recruited me to join the Barony of Arbor. \"\n\n\"I gladly accepted Orym’s request and headed to Arbor. There, I met Aragon Silversteed, their leader. He gladly accepted me. When I told him I wanted to keep exploring in pursuit of finding someone who could help me, he donned upon me the role of \"\n\n\"Acquisitioner. A recruitment scout, to put it in layman’s terms.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I traveled along a road leading off from Arbor shortly afterwards and ended up in the trade city of Sutica. Asking locals for theories on how I ended up in this strange\"\n\n\"world only ended in mockery and our combined confusion. It wasn’t until I wandered into a tavern in the town center that I was granted some sort of hospitality. The Frosted Tavern & Inn housed a woman named Zatanaes Avern, my boss as of writing this. \"\n\n\"I didn’t ask for a job; as soon as I walked in, she told me to get to work. I double as a barkeep and security officer, protecting patrons against outside instigators and those unruly among them.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0One day at the Barony, we were attacked by a local group \"\n\n\"of thieves known as the Reivers. Recently, their numbers have diminished; both of their bases close to Arbor have crumbled due to the efforts of us and the Renatians.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I met a Golem in the Sutican town square named Zyphr. After asking about how to find a\"\n\n\"way home, she told me I was annoying and that I should kill myself.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Recently, I met a guard named Lilith, who, after jumping across roofs in Sutica, told me to get down or I would be arrested. All I’d done to prompt this was giving friendly salutations.\"\n\n\"It was apparently her first day on the job. The commotion I caused while fleeing her, preaching something about proletariat liberty, shocked her and required her to call in backup to get me to stop. At least, that’s what she recalls happening. I know this\"\n\n\"because she herself gave me this journal (3). She had a bit of an accent, so it was a bit hard to understand what she was saying. She picked it up from the library of some town up north, “’Olm”. I’m just surprised and flattered she gave a scrap notebook \"\n\n\"to a complete stranger.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0A few days ago, a ghoul wandered into the tavern and started trouble. Luckily for my patrons and I, two Orcs were among the company and easily helped me rid the premises. If only I could remember their names...\"\n\n\"An event that occurred earlier this week that threatened my chances of ever finding my family again. Some green, fuzzy monster walked into town (4), covered in jewels. After escorting nearby kids into the tavern and away from the beast, I went back to it,\"\n\n\"where it forebodingly stood over overlooking citizens. I got close to it, ready to strike. Suddenly, Zatanaes threw a spear at it and pierced its side. Realizing the beast was a moving bomb upon the sound of a fuse lighting, I ducked behind my shield and \"\n\n\"was thrown backwards into one pillar of the city’s welcome arch. All I remember is getting up, feeling a large chunk of shrapnel lodged into the back of my skull, and screaming in pain before passing out. Awaking in my bed a few hours later (I assume \"\n\n\"Madam Zat either carried or led me back), I realized I was suffering from another episode of amnesia. It wasn’t until I found the piece of shrapnel that so incapacitated me that gave me my memory back. This must’ve been the work of some powerful / rich \"\n\n\"/ rich figure who was aiming to kill one target, but garnered the attention of many unwanted victims.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Sailing around the coast of Atlas near Sutica in a small rowboat, I beached upon a small island, on which I found a book caught in the palms of\"\n\n\"a tree. It was titled “Lumiere”, and, according to Madam Zat (who could read the foreign script it was in), it contained a generic prophecy of light destroying darkness. I plan to travel Atlas, copying and spreading books. My next trip will be to “Olm” to\"\n\n\"purchase more blanks. Maybe I may find a priest who can send me home or something along the way. Who knows? Maybe I’ll get answers to why years pass in days, or maybe I’ll be given nothing at all.§0\\\n§0\\\n§017th of the Amber Cold, 1688: §0\\\n\"\n\n\"(Just like that, in the span of a few hours, people claim a week has gone by! Whatever, I suppose.)§0\\\n§0On my way to Holm I headed North from the Cloud Temple instead of South (5). This mistake was doubled onto by accidentally wandering into the Orc\"\n\n\"settlement Krugsmar. The sign for it was almost illegible, compared to the neat calligraphy of the sign for the Druid town on a branching road from it. I was greeted by a strange man offering me “shekels” upon arrival. Venturing into the city center, I \"\n\n\", I was met by a seven-foot tall, red beast. It was called Zhtupid by its master, who ordered my arrest and locked me in a cage to be sold into slavery. I would’ve been the victim of kidnapping had it not been for the lucky coincidence that two kids came\"\n\n\" across my cell. The orc child pried the lock from the cage and told me to scram. I ran back to the crossroads I’d come from, where one of the children from earlier found me. Her name was Aurora, and she’d often go to Krugsmar to play with the other kid. \"\n\n\"This was all I could glean from her before an orc standing three feet taller, covered in entrails and smelled of rot began to stare at us with dark, red eyes. He grabbed Aurora and threatened to slit her throat if I didn’t come back with him. I instantly\"\n\n\"drew my blade, ready to slash through the beast. Thank God the orc child, having followed at a slower rate, caught up and talked the beast out of killing her. We both bolted, after her complaints to stay behind. We got split up, but when I went back to\"\n\n\"find her I was met with the orc child, upset that he’d been reprimanded for letting us go. I gave him bread for his troubles. I can only imagine the hell that other enslaved “pinkies” who are not so easily freed go through… It is so cruel that a nation \"\n\n\"should capture and sell unwitting guests to their civilization. This practice must be stopped.§0\\\n§0\\\n§013th of the Deep Cold, 1668:§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Heading south from Sutica, I was greeted with a jagged glacier stretching for miles, almost encapsulating\"\n\n\"the land. No wonder this season is called the “deep cold”. My boat was destroyed, broken across the glacier, and I had to walk across it to get back to the mainland. Everything else in my memory is dark and blurred, up until the point a 30s-something \"\n\n\"Halfling couple named Larry and Kacey revived me in front of a tavern fire. While I was there, I asked for supplies to recopy the prophecy and my journals. In their library basement, they had a few, along with some broken test tubes and odd recordings \"\n\n\"showing that certain people had been cloned. They also had a control station for nuclear launch sequences. I’m not sure how they procured any of this technology, but I wasn’t surprised. . It surely shook Kacey, who was very quick to escort me out of the \"\n\n\"It was a tight squeeze, though. They didn’t even bother to ask or accept payment for the books. Strange people…§0\\\n§0Some facts about halflings:§0\\\n§01- They are short§0\\\n§02- They don't wear undergarments (discovered climbing up a ladder from the library basement.\"\n\n\"Gross.)§0\\\n§0While writing the previous document, a woman named Aldonza Cervantes greeted me along the road, along with her parrot Sancho. She was the member of some legion, sent to map the Southern Isles, and asked me to accompany them on their journey.\"\n\n\"We are now lost.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0We were attacked by an Ice Wyrven in the Southern Ice Fields. Locked out of a small hamlet, we had no choice but to confront it. Closing distance with it on a solid concrete structure (with no way in; would’ve bunkered in it if we could)\"\n\n\"we deflected its ice breath. Unfortunately, we were less successful in weakening the beast. Our arrows ricocheted off of its scales. It flew off, so maybe it was just teasing us.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0NEVERMIND ROLANDO IS MAYBE ALSO PROBABLY DEAD NOW\"\n\n\"Ok, Rolando (the captain) is not dead. He was just thrown badly by the beast, as was I. It almost crushed my ribs holding me in its massive, cold, rough-textured claw. I think at least one cracked… We ran away from the beast, northward, at Rolando's\"\n\n\"command. I got separated from the group, but was re-introduced at the sound of Aldonza screeching at the Wyrm’s returned presence. Downed by the majority of the party, I helped Aldonza escape its grasp. She was left with a huge gash across her face from \"\n\n\"the monster's talons. This was not the worst injury of the battle, however. Rolando, being the closest to the dragon, was the first one it grabbed when the beast recovered, smashing him into the ground and destroying his ribcage. We couldn’t move him. The\"\n\n\"beast, though injured, had won, and flew off.§0\\\n§0He would have died, had it not been for a trio of traveling Druids, lead by a Thomas Bell (I believe that’s his name?), who used a strange, green gel on the infected area after punching him in the face to \"\n\n\"knock him out and digging into his chest where his shattered ribs had been affected. The other guard of the party, a Vittore, tried to pin the incident on me when help arrived. None of them wanted to hear his accusations, or my personal defense. §0\\\n§0Why am I\"\n\n\"still here? I've got to find my family soon...§0\\\n§0I've run out of ink...§0\\\n§0\\\n§0is today the 19th?§0\\\n§0\\\n§0*Dedicated to the lack of memory of my family (and, of course, my family themselves)*\"\n\n\"Author's note:§0\\\n§0As discussed earlier in the script, I noted that I got this journal a week or two after I arrived in Atlas. This is why many dates are not listed. I assume I arrived here around the year 1664. As will also be discussed later on in the \"\n\n\"entries, it took a while for me to put together I was experiencing time through the perspective of an elf. Strange, considering I'm human, but even stranger that I seem to feel as I did in my youth while those around me comment that I look like I'm in my \"\n\n\"late thirties. Ah well, won't matter in a day or two anyways.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Footnotes:§0\\\n§01) Throughout the first journal, I mistakenly dated the entries 20 years into the future. Thank goodness I fixed that!§0\\\n§02) This was, actually, upon the steps to the\"\n\n\"gates of Holm. Had I not been attacked and saved, my story may have resolved very differently.§0\\\n§03) Not this copy, the master copy used for the original log.§0\\\n§04) A... a creeper, I think?§0\\\n§05) Another discrepancy in the journal; I assumed the South was North\"\n\n\"because of the ice wall. Assumed Atlas was in the Northern Hemisphere.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0END VOLUME 1\"", ""),
        StaticBook("LWJ, Vol.4 Ed.2", "§bLouis", "\"14th of the First Seed, 1677:§0\\\n§0Lost the other book fighting a cake monster in Sutica. Some psycho named “The Baker” tried to invade and I got vored by the golem. It was huge, could barely fit through the gates. I acted as a flank, running around his \"\n\n\"his hordes. That’s how it got me; whacked me against the wall and swallowed me whole. It’s gastro-chambers were lined with liquid fat. Some asshat did the same thing as Zat during the Creeper incident and activated some sort of bomb in it, sending me \"\n\n\"flying into the bay. Besides a broken rib, I should be fine. Been staying in Sutica trying to find the girl I handed the other book off to, Ellie. She hasn’t turned up.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Begged Zat for my job back, but this memory loss thing has become too much of a \"\n\n\"liability for her to even afford to care about me. She’s already downsized her staff significantly and still can’t make ends meet. She asked if I needed anything before she left to see her sister, and I asked for a blank journal to write this one. She \"\n\n\"told me they sold them at CT, and left.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Is there even any purpose for me in this world anymore? I’ve not found any, and the day I landed in the CT must’ve been some centennial miracle. That was the only day that a monk was even present there. Don't think\"\n\n\"I’ll find any value sitting around here, using blood from the carcass of a rotting chicken in the Warhawkes settlement. Seeing as I’ve seen no one here, I guess I’ll have to wander about to find some sense of purpose.\"\n\n\"Apparently that September Prince thing wasn’t the result of some hazy fever dream, and he’s really going to kill everyone and everything in an event of eco-terrorism. Sucks to be alive.§0\\\n§0Came across a deserted mining settlement near the camp. Found a book\"\n\n\"and some picks. Not that big, but still of value.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Turns out it was just an outpost. A giant, red castle stood in a desert clearing, with homes made out of adobe-like sand bricks dug into the valley enclosing it. Most text is in orcish. The town is\"\n\n\"crowned with a large arc and a ridgeside. The area it encloses is soaked with blood and the emblems of a faded society. On top of the ridge is an oasis, where I peacefully observe the past bloodshed.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Farther south, I found a \\\"Monument of Lost Friends\\\". I\"\n\n\"marked the one I ended up continuing this journey for. She’s as good as dead, but the hope that she’s out there somewhere keeps me going. I know I won’t find her in these blasted wastes. Sunset looks beautiful out here in the ruins of Cantos. \"\n\n\"Wandered through the jungle into some part of Krugsmar. A giant pit, outlined with the effigies of other unfortunate wanderers, greeted me. Traveling down its spiral staircase were the memorials to past orcs, culminating in a large pool of blood.\"\n\n\"Left the Krugsmar “library” with a dozen blanks. All of their other shelves were empty, so I don’t think they’ll be missing these.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Found some deserted loot in their mines. Found some unfinished novella in one of the miner’s bunks (unfinished, as in a\"\n\n\"single page of notes. Had to drop my improvisational inkwell behind. Rest peacefully down here, Ferguson.§0\\\n§0\\\n§014th of the Amber Cold, 1678:§0\\\n§0Turns out that Krugsmar was destroyed in a war with the Dominion. Good. \"\n\n\"A memorial lies in their town square dedicated to the memory of those who died fighting the beasts.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0There’s a dragon in Arbor. Will update later.§0\\\n§0\\\n§014th of the Snow’s Maiden, 1678 (10):§0\\\n§0It hasn't been that long since I wrote\"\n\n\"the last entry right? I was just at the Dominion yes--------§0\\\n§0\\\n§0month= day§0\\\n§0week= year§0\\\n§0I’ve only been here for 3 months and been withering away quicker by the day. I need to get back to my family before I die.\"\n\n\"What happened yesterday?§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Broken in doors and windows, blood steeped into the stoney streets…§0\\\n§0We lost, didn’t we? I need to find Aragon, he’ll be able to tell me.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Dragon ate Aragon. There are now two people alive that\"\n\n\"still care about me. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0I’m going to go tear this overgrown, gluttonous lizard’s motherfucking throat out.§0\\\n§0\\\n§015th of Snow’s Maiden, 1678:§0\\\n§0\\\n§0It’s the middle of the night. I'm covered in the blood, sweat, and \"\n\n\"tears of my comrades and self, and what’s left of Aragon. He returned as a shade to fight along with the Frost Wyrven, controlled by the mage that initially killed both him and I (11). The Dragon attacked Holm. We managed to push Aragon and the mage into \"\n\n\"the molten moat, but they disappeared in a cloud of smoke. The dragon then flew over to Belvitz, where they awaited the coming armies. On my way over I tripped on a rock and almost bled out. Had it not been for a traveling knight, unaware of the battle\"\n\n\"occurring until coming across me, I might not have made it back to Arbor to relay the tale.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Wyrven and its minions attacked the Belvitz Keep. Dozens of ladders were thrown over its sides for accessibility to the demon and his artificial right hand in\"\n\n\"instances where they chose to perch themselves upon the roof of the keep from which they laid their wrath upon us. Though both the mage and dragon were struck down, Aragon lives. I saw him outside the city and chased him through the forest to a small \"\n\n\"cluster of houses in Belvitz. Me and 2 others tried and failed to down him. I called for reenforcements, but nobody came and I was struck down.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Aragon revived me… He must have some piece of himself left, able to recognize comrades where they may be.\"\n\n\"Glad to be one of them.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Though I’m glad to have ripped the throat from the beast’s scaley husk and watch its dirty elixir pour onto the street, the teeth I pulled from its skull were confiscated by the captains. I've been left with no memento but that of\"\n\n\"death.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Coming back to Arbor, I saw Aragon had flown back. He was perched upon the roof of the old tavern, converted into an armory in his absence. One of the captains who accompanied me back, Khazara, attempted to shoot Aragon, but couldn't bring\"\n\n\"herself to do it. Aragon vanished in a puff of smoke, seconds before I could push him off the roof.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0There is no purpose anymore. I either leave or die.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0“Home is where your family is”, the monk says. The only authority of truth in\"\n\n\"this world. The one who tells me my family doesn’t remember me. One of those responsible for my captivity.§0\\\n§0There is no truth in this world.§0\\\n§0\\\n§016th of The First Seed, 1678:§0\\\n§0Wandering and came across a mountainous tree sprouting out of\"\n\n\"a mountain. The hill itself was reduced to rubble. It looks as though someone dropped a hydrogen bomb on it and planted the tree in its place. Rubble from indistinguishable buildings were faintly scattered around the trunk. Near the tree, I saw two giants\"\n\n\"that appeared to be made of wood, even taller than the tree. It seems they didn’t notice me, as they just stood there. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Menacingly.§0\\\n§0\\\n§016th of The Grand Harvest, 1679:§0\\\n§0There is truly no more purpose in this world. All who have cared\"\n\n\"about me are either estranged or dead. My bones grow weaker by the day, stripping me of the supposedly infinite youth I once was granted. All this world has done is corrupt my body, mind, and soul. I've had enough. I know my purpose; to wander aimlessly \"\n\n\"and be used by those around me, left in the shed to rust when I myself am caught in fireshower. The denial of kinship from others has driven me to the realization that my presense is a waste, and my body will only serve to fertilize the grounds that have \"\n\n\"stripped away my being.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0So this is how I leave my legacy. I’ll be working on this until the anniversary of my Atlasian Arrival, and on that day I’ll accept myself from who I am; a Wandering Friend. I will go to the temple where I marked the name of the \"\n\n\"one who I’ve searched for over the course of my youth to no avail. In my search to bring her from ashes, I must become one with them. I plan to leave y body, the lock damning me to this moral coil, and transcend into whatever realm awaits me, either to\"\n\n\"reward me for my good or punish me for sin. All that should remain is this ruined corpse and its memoir, used for everything but itself, used to recall and document its own sufferings.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I am the shell of a man, and Atlas has gutted me.\"\n\n\"Had to stop writing because I saw someone moving about my roof. Went outside to inspect and some knight just started spouting something about being on watch and ran off without explaining themselves.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Had to stop a second time for some guy who called me a\"\n\n\"cunt for asking why I should let him in the city. Fuck you too, Alexander. Never gonna revise this with all these distractions.§0\\\n§0\\\n§016th of Snow’s Maiden, 1681:§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Got evicted from my home. Fell asleep for a year again. Shit.\"\n\n\"Saw Zatanaes in the Arborian town center? She didn’t see me at all.§0\\\n§0Seeking refuge in the House of Opus. Doesn’t look good; they have overdue taxes.§0\\\n§0\\\n§014th of the Grand Harvest, 1685:§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I’ve been wandering life as a dream for the past few days,\"\n\n\"months – years, not seeing anything but the beauty of nature. Nothing outside of civilization has harmed me thus far. It has only brought a relief for me, an escape from the cruelty of man. It has only brought a relief for me. §0\\\n§0I've come back to Arbor to \"\n\n\"find my foreclosed house in shambles. The House of Opus is unoccupied, disregarding the rotting body of a hog seeping blood into the floorboards. §0\\\n§0I’ve been gone for so long. There’s a HUGE city expansion being worked on east of the square. But that \"\n\n\"doesn’t interest me anymore. Nothing does anymore. I’m just waiting for the ripening of this shell and to metamorphosise as a peaceful soul. The day of reckoning is soon. I’ve been working around the clock to finalize these journals before this world is\"\n\n\"destroyed, but I hope to be dead long before that dreary end comes to pass. Once I finish this, I’ll put an end to this mode of existence once and for all.§0\\\n§0\\\n§015th of the Grand Harvest, 1685:§0\\\n§0The Sutican Library has been replaced by the Sutican Spa, and\"\n\n\"the former contents being pushed to a small storage hut on the hill near it. Honestly a natural progression, considering the city's management. I hate this place.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Found Zat. The Frosted Tavern's been put to \\\"A Good Knight's Rest\\\", so\"\n\n\"to speak. She’s some priest for a temple above the spa worshiping some light deity. Some kid came in asking about dark mages and the clergy threatened to kill him if he didn’t submit to inquisition.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Had some vision about some elk with stars adorning its \"\n\n\"antlers. Whack.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Footnotes:§0\\\n§0\\\n§010) Accidentally notes \\\"1672\\\" in original transcription.§0\\\n§011) Apparently he wasn't eaten, just killed. The person who told me this in Arbor was as confused on the details as I.\"\n\n\"END VOLUME 4\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Urguan - Axios", "§bBorin Grandaxe", "\"Under the reign of Grand King Drynn Ireheart, the Dwed settle in the new capital of Kal'Nikaer. Seeking a new ally for the times ahead, Grand King Drynn Ireheart turns to allies of old. A defensive treaty is signed with The Holy Orenian Empire,\"\n\n\"the first of its kind with the human nation since the First Great War in Anthos. Grand King Drynn Ireheart leads numerous expeditions into the Deeproads found beneath the city. In these trips, it is discovered that Feral Elf settlements still\"\n\n\"exist and that a celestial presence resides deep inside the Deeproads. Grand King Drynn Ireheart and Emperor John Owyn Horen form a blood pact between the Empire of Oren and the Grand Kingdom of Urguan. Grand King Drynn “The Peacemaker” Ireheart\"\n\n\"resigns from office after many stone months of reign and names Zahrer Irongrinder as the presiding official over the following §0election.Torvin§0 Grandaxe is elected by the Grand Kingdom of Urguan, continuing the tradition of inviting the Harian\"\n\n\"and Orenian royalty to his coronation. The Grand Kingdom of Urguan march to war against the Orcish nation alongside the Orenian Empire and her vassals, razing and destroying the Orcish Capitol. Grand King Torvin Grandaxe passes a bill through\"\n\n\"the senate to allow the senate the ability to choose the new Grand King of Urguan. The Grand Kingdom of Urguan marches alongside the Holy Orenian Empire against a coalition of Snow Elves, Orcs, and Dreadlander remnants. A swift victory is\"\n\n\"granted to the Grand Kingdom and the Empire, with the coalition forces quickly being defeated. Grand King Torvin Grandaxe is removed from the throne and Hogarth Irongut is appointed Lord Regent by the Senate of Hammers until a new Grand King is\"\n\n\"elected. After 2 stone weeks, Algoda Frostbeard is elected the new Grand King of §0Urguan.After§0 being elected Algoda Frostbeard led the dwarves to a new, grand city. Kal'Omith. It's size was overbearing and spread deep and vast within the\"\n\n\"mountains. It's name came from the great builder Omithel Strongbow himself. After erecting the kingdom a new spark lit among the dwed. Algoda is often heeded for his great success for reforming it's economy and bolstering it's militaristic\"\n\n\"strength. Algoda is credited with conceiving the Axionite Coalition, from it's creation to his death. Algoda Frostbeard, after reforming the Grand Kingdom, is arrested by Orenian forces in the town of Ostermark and §0executed.The§0 next stone day,\"\n\n\"Bastion Ireheart is elected Grand King of Urguan. With his sudden rise to power Bastion inherited the war against Oren, aligning himself with the Courland-lead Axionite Coalition. Bastion himself oversaw his forces with the Coalition find\"\n\n\"victory at the Battle of Goldfields, proving to be the killing blow against the Orenian Empire. Following the conclusion of the war, Bastion is credited with enacting numerous reforms, such being: a revision of the Articles of Urguan, Codex of\"\n\n\"Laws, re-establishing past guilds and improving the wealth of Urguan. After awaking from a coma he committed suicide, tumbling off the balcony of the King's Palace into the streets belowAfter five years of war, Urguan surrenders to the Kingdom\"\n\n\"of Kaz'Ulrah in 1636.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarven Unity", "§bBorin Grandaxe", "\"Grandaxes have strived to maintain dwarven unity, but also have oftentimes attempted to move further away. Grandaxes had historically established their separate holds many times throughout the ages, however after the Fall of Avar, the enthusiasm\"\n\n\"and drive over making holds collapsed. Afterwards Grandaxes understood the need for unity far better and no longer desired to separate as much as they had before. Additionally Grandaxes believe actions such as rebellion are dishonorable and thus\"\n\n\"take them very seriously. The last Grandaxe rebellion in Kal'Bogrin was bloodless and the clan promised to help the Grand Kingdom against Oren. Though the favor wasn't expected to be returned. The Grandaxes have a relentless loyalty to the\"\n\n\"Dwarves as a people and respect for the articles, however the clan typically desires to maintain its ability to operate with moderate independence and self-rule.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Urguan - Aegis", "§bBorin Grandaxe", "\"The Grand Kingdom of Urguan was officially founded by Grand King Thorik Grandaxe in the year 1329. Thorik wished to differentiate the new Kingdom of the Dwarves from the old and failed Kingdom of the Dwarves in the past. Due to threats of war\"\n\n\"from both the Orcish Nation of Krugmar and the Holy Princedom of Malinor, and absent of King Gotrek Firemane, the Lord Marshal, Thorik Grandaxe (At the time known by the name of his bloodline, Braveaxe), opted to form a War Council. The war\"\n\n\"council intended to act as a counterbalance to the dwarven High Council, which had slowly displayed a growing ineptness in running the Kingdom in recent years. The War Council consisted of many of Thorik's closest commanders and advisers in the\"\n\n\"Legion, along with the Archbishop at the time, Thordan Irongut. When a secret meeting was held to determine how the War Council should act, it was ultimately decided that a military coup was in order. After the absence of King Gotrek for near an\"\n\n\"elven week, Thorik declared himself Grand King of Urguan. He named the first of his council, Valen Grandaxe, Grand Councilor of Diplomacy, Chaecus Grandaxe, Grand Councilor of War, Stronghold Grandaxe, Grand Councilor of Economics and Broski\"\n\n\"Grandaxe, Grand Councilor of §0Guilds.For§0 most of its history, the Grand Kingdom of Urguan thrived, achieving great feats whilst in power. In its early years, the race of dwarves was united under a single banner again, it's military revamped and\"\n\n\"its culture spreading by the day. When the Great War broke out across Aegis, the Grand Kingdom allied with the human Kingdom of Oren, battling back the orcs into the deserts of Krugmar, while the elven Wardens, the dwarven Legion's one time\"\n\n\"mortal enemy and rival were disbanded by the very leaders they served to protect. Though the Great War eventually ended in a treaty of white peace, the course of the war had made it glaringly obvious that the dominant powers had shifted, the\"\n\n\"dwarf-human alliance taking the role that the orc-elf alliance had once held. In the years following the Great War, Grand King Thorik did his best to protect his people from the dangers of the outside world, as well as attempting to retain a\"\n\n\"natural balance and peace that would lead to unity in the face of the ever growing threat of Iblees and the undead. However, after conflict arose between the Ascended Order and the Merchant City of Alras, a bounty was placed on the head of Kjell\"\n\n\"Ireheart. In response, the dwarves, feeling a challenge to their honor had been made, laid siege to and sacked the city of Alras. They also chose to abandon the worship of Aeriel and the Ascended in favor of the dwarves' ancient religion of the\"\n\n\"Brathmordakin.The§0 Dwarves of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan flee to the Verge with the other mortal races of Aegis following the Battle of the Cloud Temple. Many dwarves refused to leave Kal'Urguan, Kjell Ireheart being most notable. Others were\"\n\n\"lost on the way to Asulon, such as Valen Grandaxe. In the Verge, a quick coalition of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan, the Kingdom of Oren, and the Kingdom of Alras is made - dubbed Tazarak. Alras shortly dropped out of this coalition as their High\"\n\n\"King Syrio had his chests lockpicked by some greedy §0dwarf.Upon§0 the time of landing upon the shores of Asulon, Thorik had lost much of his original council and found himself struggling to rule without the advisers he had once held close to his\"\n\n\"side. In the newly rebuilt city of Kal'Karik, disagreements arose between Thorik and the Irongut Clan Father, Hiebe Irongut, leading a group of dwarves to leave the Kingdom, forming the island nation of Holm in the far north east of the\"\n\n\"continent. When Thorik was believed to be assassinated by cultists of Ondnarch, it was his son, Broski Grandaxe, who took on the reigns of power. However, over time the Kingdom slowly began to crumble, following a policy of isolationism. During\"\n\n\"this time, the old human alliance was lost amid power shifts in Oren lands and the formation of the Holy Oren Empire. As criticism of the nation's leadership continued, Broski stood down from the throne and handed the crown to his distant\"\n\n\"cousin, Stronghold Grandaxe, who was quickly ousted after Dwarves learned of his ties to a notorious bandit group, the Hollowed §0Bandits.Kjell§0 Ireheart was then elected as the next King. The Dwarves began to prosper under his rule due to the\"\n\n\"successful ongoing war against the War Nation of Krugmar. The end of the First Kingdom of Urguan was brought about after Gorum Frostbeardhanded the Kingdom of Alras and all of its lands over to Urguan after years of successful espionage, marking\"\n\n\"the birth of the First Empire of Urguan. Shortly after, a dwarven resurgance would take place during the fifty year brutal war against the §0Orcs.Asulon§0 had been abandoned due to natural disasters and so the dwarves had been forced to flee to the\"\n\n\"Isles of Elysium. The former Grand King, Thorik Grandaxe, through to be dead, is found deep within the caves of the Elysium volcano, possessed by the spirit Ondnarch. Valen Grandaxe destroys the source of Ondnarch's power with the Hammer of\"\n\n\"Urguan and Thorik is released from his will. After grievances over King Hiebe Irongut's actions, Tortek Silverfist, Gorum Frostbeard and Kjell Ireheartagree to place Thorik back in power. After speaking with then Consular Valen Grandaxe, it is\"\n\n\"agreed that Thorik holds rightful ownership over the Kingdom. With Thorik's bid for power, House Silverblade and House Hightower reconfirm their strong ties with the dwarven nation after renouncing the Dwarves due to Hiebe Irongut's rule.\"\n\n\"However, removing Hiebe from power unsettles Malinor and House Tarus. Despite earlier rifts, the Dwarves agree to assist the White Rose and the War Uzg in laying siege to the newly reformed House Flay and the Teutonic Order. The battle is a\"\n\n\"success and Emperor Godfrey Horen gives the victory his blessing. Thorik Grandaxe is officially crowned Grand King of the Kingdom of Urguan and beneath him, Valen Grandaxe, Gorum Frostbeard, Omithiel Strongbrow, Tortek Silverfist and Kjell\"\n\n\"Stormhammer are made dwarven Lords. This caused political outrage from the Ironguts, they grew upset over Hiebe Irongut's recent removal and demanded representation among the Lords Council. Lord Gorum Frostbeard allowed Hiebe Irongut to replace\"\n\n\"him as lord to avoid inner conflict during a crucial time. After relations improve between The Kingdom of Urguan and the Holy Oren Empire, Grand King Thorik Grandaxe and Emperor Godfrey sign the Treaty of Aturial, and make a blood pact between\"\n\n\"the two nations, promising an alliance between them. For the first time in over fifty years, the dwarves and humans enter an alliance §0together.After§0 the golem crafting anvil goes missing, it is found to be in the hands of High Elves. In his\"\n\n\"fury, Lord Kjell Stormhammer breaks the alliance with Malinor, with no objections from the Lord's Council. For Lord Tortek's part in hiding the true location of the anvil, he is voted out of the Lord's Council. Replacing him is the Grand King's\"\n\n\"eldest cousin, Bazian Grandaxe. Under the new Rex Vrogak Gorkil, the orcs of the War Uzg invade the Kharajyr stronghold while a group of allied dwarves are stationed there. The stronghold is pillaged but later rebuilt by the dwarves. Only two\"\n\n\"dwarves survive the battle but bring word of the attack the the Kingdom of Urguan. Enraged at the orc's betrayal of the peace treaty, the Lord's Council agrees on a full scale invasion of the War Uzg. Emperor Godfrey offers his support and\"\n\n\"together, the Kingdom of Urguan and the Holy Oren Empire fight side by side, surrounding orc held territory in a matter of weeks. In the first true battle, the stronghold which later becomes known as Kazad'Urkus is put under dwarven\"\n\n\"control.Thorik§0 Grandaxe steps down as Grand King and calls for a re-election. Omithiel Strongbrow is crowned and elected King of the Kingdom of Urguan. Upon his coronation, he appoints former Lord Gorum Frostbeard to replace him in the Lord's\"\n\n\"Council. Under King Omithiel Strongbrow, the dwarves travel to the Isles of Kalos where the war with the War Uzg continues to rage on. The death toll is high on both sides of the conflict as the two races prepare to set sail for Anthos. Many\"\n\n\"great battles have occurred in the island of Kalos, most of which led by the Commanders Thorin Grandaxe, Gorum Frostbeard, and Lord Marshal Kjell Ireheart . The Legion was then a notorious force among all of the races, feared by many and loved\"\n\n\"by §0most.The§0 nations sail for Anthos, finally arriving in the newly constructed city of Kal'Azgoth.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Urguan - Vailor", "§bBorin Grandaxe", "\"The dwarves of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan arrive on the Isles of Vailor during the year 1513. Led by Grand King Balek Irongut, construction begins on Kal'Akash, the city of metal. During construction, an ancient runic golem was found which\"\n\n\"dated back to Asulon. A giant who went by the name of Armin was also discovered, living on top of the mountain Kal'Akash was settled under. After a duel with the Grand Marshal Jorik Grandaxe, it became a quick §0ally.Two§0 years after settling\"\n\n\"Kal'Akash, the city has to defend from multiple bandit raids. The Legion's moral drops during these times, causing the first joint dwarf-orc military practice to correct problems in the legion and to increase morality. Thought to of corrected\"\n\n\"the issues in the legion, Grand King Balek Irongut sailed out to sea on the S.S. Irongutia to attempt to slay the Devourer. The ship is massacred and most dwarves die at sea, Balek Irongut was missing amongst the dwarves. As well, the Grand\"\n\n\"Marshal Jorik Grandaxe had been kidnapped by a mysterious clan known as the §0Sundur.As§0 the nation was in chaos, a new election for Grand King was taking place. The three main contenders were Skippy Irongut, Verthaik Frostbeard, and Lathros\"\n\n\"\\\"Oilbeard\\\" Irongrinder. After three days of tough campaigning, Skippy Irongut emerged as the Grand King of Urguan. Upset at the thought as Skippy as the Grand King, Verthaik Frostbeard along with the holds of Tal'Azwyr and Kal'Krest went against\"\n\n\"the Grand Kingdom in open rebellion. The rebellion was named the Mountain Monarchy, led by Verthaik and many other Frostbeards and Blackfists. The rebellion took part in many raids on the dwarven capital of Kal'Akash, but ultimately after a few\"\n\n\"stone weeks of fighting the rebellion was destroyed by the Legion in 1520. A year later, the Grand King Skippy Irongut finally has his coronation - delayed by fixing the mess the Mountain Monarchy had made.A year after Grand King Skippy's\"\n\n\"coronation, mysterious entities attack Kal'Akash with the intent to destroy the city. Because of this new mysterious threat, and other worldly problems, Skippy Irongut and Caliph Faiz Kharadeen sign the Alliance of Sand and Stone, acting as an\"\n\n\"alliance between the Grand Kingdom and the Caliphate of Khalestine. At the same time, Grand King Skippy Irongut along with the Grand Prince of the Snow Elves help create the Southern Vailor Coalition; a short lasting coalition to secure the\"\n\n\"south, which worked well while it was §0around.Upon§0 the year 1525, the Grand King Skippy Irongut was assassinated by an assassin of Dark Elven race, who was found to be contracted by a dwarf still unknown to this day. Therefor, nominations for\"\n\n\"Grand King begin. Notable nominations include Uldar Irongut, Duren Hammerfist, and Demagol Doomforged. After months of campaigning, Uldar Irongut is crowned Grand King of the Dwarves. His reign was filled with questionable reforms, and after a\"\n\n\"couple of years of being Grand King, Uldar abandoned the Kingdom and illegally left Gauldrim Irongut as Lord §0Regent.Gauldrim§0 Irongut had attempted to split the Grand Kingdom into two separate nations and allowing every other settlement their\"\n\n\"independence from the Grand Kingdom. Every dwarf in Kal'Akash was against this, as they saw it as a way for the humans of Oren and the orcs of the Iron Uzg to claim their land and stormed the King's Palace and forcefully removed Gauldrim, now\"\n\n\"clanless. In his place, Midgor Ireheart was placed as Grand King without any §0opposition.Midgor§0 Ireheart is placed as Grand King of Urguan as no other dwarf ran against him in the election. Midgor Ireheart with the support of the dwarven people\"\n\n\"march to Felsen to demand Oren release their vassals and are denied. The reason for this happening is traced back to tensions between the dwarven people and the Orenians over the stone weeks following Uldar's abandoning of the Grand §0Kingdom.The\"\n\n\"Holy Oren Empire declares war on the Grand §0Kingdom.Oren§0 wins initiative in the war, going on to conquer Rhewengrad though quickly being routed off the mainland by the §0Legion.The§0 Orenian Navy later sets its focus on the Island of Avar, conquering\"\n\n\"it after 3 battles - the last leaving the Orenian navy at 10 §0men.The§0 forces of Oren again attempt to invade the mainland and Manteiv Valley, assaulting the fortress of Kal'Ordholm. The human forces are routed from the field before they have a\"\n\n\"chance to scale the front §0walls.Following§0 the end of the war, Kardel Irongut is elected as Grand King. From the Obsidian Throne, he ushers in a new system of government for the Grand Kingdom and reigns peacefully throughout his time as Grand\"\n\n\"King. After falling ill, he steps down and leaves behind a legacy as one who would do whatever it took to keep the §0peace.Grand§0 King Kardel “The Neutral” Irongut falls ill and names Drynn Ireheart as his regent. Numerous public works projects are\"\n\n\"carried out to bring a new age of cultural development are carried out by the §0Regent.In§0 a unanimous nomination, the assembled senators elect Drynn Ireheart to be the next Grand King. He is later coronated with many notable guests including the\"\n\n\"Emperor of Oren and Faiz Kharadeen of Haria.A creature of daemonic power known as the Dharok is freed from a seal beneath the capital. A consumer of holy relics, he is impervious to most conventional means of assault but is eventually slain by\"\n\n\"the Rune Lords, Zahrer Irongrinder and Yeulf Irongut, when he consumes a runic bomb disguised as a §0relic.With§0 the city in ruins following the assault of the Dharok, an infestation of silverfish, and the attack of an orcish spirit, the Dwarves\"\n\n\"flee the ruins of the south aboard the flagship of the Irongrinder Fleet, Da Kavir Kor. They take refuge for a time outside of the Cloud Temple before fleeing with the rest of the descendents through the spirit realm.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elvenesse 3", "§bKardryn Oranor", "The Elvenesse Papers\n            [3]\n\n\n\n\n     On the unequal\n distribution of votes.\n\nThe Dominion of Elvenesse, the land of mali, is since 1659 a meritocratic commonwealth, meaning those with skill or good abilities get to hold power. Our High Prince stands as the lead of our nation and thus gets to appoint the leading class of this\n\noligarchy. To compensate for his power and to give the people a say too, there's the ability for citizens to vote on a new High Prince when one is to be elected, bringing a small bit of democracy into our oligarchic system of government.\n\nBut why is it then, that this compensation for the citizens is essentially useless? This is very simple, as all citizens of Elvenesse, no matter how many of them vote, get combined into one singular vote.\n\nIt is true, and it's a scandal. Whenever our government gives us the ability to give input on a matter, all of us together get 1 vote while each member of the sitting government gets a vote PER PERSON. Even more ridiculous is the fact that the High Prince\n\ngets two votes. This means that essentially, our democratic compensation for this oligarchic government, is useless, as we citizens of the Dominion get too little input to make a difference. That is why I hereby plead for this to be changed.\n\nIt is a problem that us citizens of the Dominion don't get a proper say in electing a High Prince, for this high prince can appoint whoever he wants to have in his administrative court, meaning he could simply pick individuals who would vote for him.\n\nAnd with the administrative court having three times as many votes as all citizens in Elvenesse, it is clear why this is a ridiculous problem. Thus, by publishing this paper, I ask the citizens of Elvenesse as well as the government to stand up for change\n\nWe must have a proper election for choosing a new High Prince. An election where every individual gets one equal vote per person rather than having them all combined. If we are supposed to have a say in picking  the leader of our nation, then let us have\n\na proper say in the matter, and not one that isn't heard by the government for it isn't loud enough. Why should the Treasurer for instance, an individual appointed by the High Prince and his government have just as much say in choosing a High Prince as\n\nall the citizens that inhabit, work and live in this prosperous nation? Both the situation created here by our constitution and the fact that nobody does anything about it, are ridiculous.\n\nWith great consideration,\n\nYour obedient servant,\n\nK. Oranor", ""),
        StaticBook("Required Topics", "§bThe Library Of Dragur", "Required Books:\nHou-Zi\nClaimed By: N/A\nVoidal Nodes\nClaimed By: N/A\nRasmot\nClaimed By: N/A\nAeriel\nClaimed By: N/A\nApohet\nClaimed By: N/A\nMetztli\nClaimed By: N/A\n\n\nSatyr\nClaimed By: N/A\nCervitaur\nClaimed By: N/A\nArchons\nClaimed By: N/A\nVoidal Horror\nClaimed By: N/A\nStrigae\nClaimed By: N/A\nDarkstalkers\nClaimed By: N/A\nThe Soul\n\n\nClaimed By: N/A\nAzdrazi\nClaimed By: N/A\nDralachite/Vehement\nClaimed By: N/A\nFocus Crystals\nClaimed By: Nemir (UnBaed)\nCelestialism\nClaimed By: N/A\nVoidal Shifting\nClaimed By: N/A\nArcane Revenants\n\n\nClaimed By: N/A\nRuibrium\nClaimed By: N/A\nGazardiael\nClaimed By: N/A\nMalin\nClaimed By: Nemir (UnBaed)\nJohannesburg\nClaimed By: N/A\nWord Altars\nClaimed By: N/A\nMordring\n\n\nClaimed By: N/A\nEzekiel Cunningham\nClaimed By: N/A\nThe Fringe\nClaimed By: N/A\nDoor of Eternity\nClaimed By: N/A\nKhorvad’s Grip\nClaimed By: Benjamin W. Goldhand (thebulter)\nOrithur\nClaimed By: N/A\n\n\nGorloth Staff\nClaimed By: N/A\nTomes of Power\nClaimed By: N/A\nBlack Nexus\nClaimed By: N/A\nGolem Anvil\nClaimed By: N/A\nGolems\nClaimed By: N/A\nSpace\nClaimed By: Steven (spodokaiba of\n\nkaibacorp)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Elvenesse 5", "§bKardryn Oranor", "The Elvenesse Papers\n            [5]\n\n\n\n\n On the protection of\n      our economy.\n\nSome stalls scattered across the city, an occasional shop or two and... that's it. That is essential all our economy entails. A few small market stalls or shops. Nothing more nothing less. Now this seems fine, but our economy's increasingly stalling.\n\nWhy is this and what does this mean? It means that our economy isn't growing, it's growth is slowing down as the market gets saturated. Why is it so easily saturated? Because nothing is done to promote economic growth. But more importantly, no measures\n\nare taken to protect our already fragile economy from being ruined. No laws exist to ensure fair prices, to keep healthy competition or on the contrary, the lack of competition. There's no restrictions on what can be sold and there's nothing to protect\n\nthe every consumers, which includes you and I, from being monetary abused by the merchants and companies that provide us the goods that we buy. So, what ought to be done?\n\nFirstly, there should be restrictions on what goods are to be sold and what goods aren't to be sold. Would you want drugs to be sold in an environment where children roam around? Should it be sold at all? Note that drugs are just an example here, there's\n\nof course much worse items that, at the moment, can be freely sold on Elvenesse's streets. Think about items that hold dark magic for example. Restrictions on what can be sold would prevent these goods from simply being bought at the grocery store, making\n\nit harder for one to get their hands on them. \n\nFurthermore, there should be restrictions on how many outlets are allowed to sell a certain good. This provides a certain good from flooding the market and sets a bar for joining the market.\n\nSay you wish to sell iron. If there's going to be dozens of shops selling iron, it's likely that you won't sell your iron, because the market is flooded, oversaturated. There's to much supply  for the demand, making the prices drop dramatically or else\n\nthere won't be sales. Now this is good for the consumers of course, cheap iron! But this is horrible for producers, for they will make barely any profit or no profit at all, causing them not to wish to sell on the market of the Dominion.\n\nThe last protective measure that we will be adressed and that our government ought to instate is making the formation of cartels illegal. A cartel an agreement between companies or producers about fixed prices.\n\nSay, for example, that there are 10 companies that sell iron in Elvenesse. These 10 companies could come together and agree to sell their iron for a minimum of 15 minas, setting a high price so they make more profit. Because all companies agree to this,\n\nthere's no competition between the companies thus they won't feel the need to lower their prices to compete with their rivals. This is of course a horrible way to abuse financial power to the consumers' disadvantage.\n\nThus cartel formation should be made illegal, to protect our economy along with the other measures I described and possibly many other measures that could be taken to protect our market, but simply aren't taken by the government, for whatever reason.\n\nWith great consideration,\n\nYour obedient servant,\n\nK. Oranor", ""),
        StaticBook("101-1", "§bFabius Bracchus", "\"Imperial Voter§0\\\n§0§nIdentification Card         §0\\\n§0\\\n§0§lName: §0Theodosius Amatias§0\\\n§0\\\n§0§lYear of Birth: §01658§0\\\n§0\\\n§0§lResidency: §0Markev§0\\\n§0\\\n§0101-1\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Scavenger Hunt", "§bLayla Ithelanen", "\"\\\n§0         The First Gladewynn §0\\\n§0        Scavenger Hunt. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0             By. Layla\"\n\n\"            The Rules:§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Work Independently, there is only one winner. §0\\\n§0Solve the Riddles, take a screenshot with the answer. §0\\\n§0First one to collect them all, gets a nummy sketch. §0\\\n§0No cheating. §0\\\n\"\n\n\"                   1§0\\\n§0Where stone meets field and into sky, §0\\\n§0Through grass and flower, and marble high. §0\\\n§0The hunter’s prize, the hawk’s clans token. §0\\\n§0This mani’s generosity never broken. §0\\\n\"\n\n\"                 2§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Upon the roost on mountain high, §0\\\n§0Outstretched wings eclipse the sky.§0\\\n§0This Mani knows the price of beauty, §0\\\n§0Just one more aspect of the deceiver's duty. §0\\\n\"\n\n\"                   3§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Proudly he stands, on a pile of victory§0\\\n§0His sigil flown high as a symbol of royalty. §0\\\n§0Sharp fang causing enemy to flee. §0\\\n§0He will bring honor onto thee. §0\\\n\"\n\n\"                   4§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Within mountain tall of stone §0\\\n§0You'll find the crowned turtle’s throne. §0\\\n§0. The den of wolves, painted red. §0\\\n§0           Knelt at the seat, where Morea Led. §0\\\n\"\n\n\"                   5§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Upon the edge of September’s grove§0\\\n§0Sits Hamatsa’s dark and murky cove. §0\\\n§0This is for those brave enough to reach the shrine§0\\\n§0Of the green skinned demon covered in vine. \"", ""),
        StaticBook("Voidal FeelingV1", "§bJim", "\"Voidal feeling §0\\\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ §0\\\n§0Mages have a great understanding of their mana and to understand that is to be a mage thats where voidal feeling surely comes in wehn one begins to develope a mana pool and to see our inner self and gather that feeling of \"\n\n\"the void. However these are my own §0theories...Voidal§0 feeling is a way to discover more about an item and how much mana can fit within different shapes and sizes the the greater understanding of utilizing the void will allow you to learn about the other\"\n\n\"aspects of the void like air fire and water plus earth using this technique to look deeper into yourself can also probably be able to control the input of mana and accelerate the mana you generate like tightening a hose connected to the void\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Voidal FeelingV2", "§bJim", "\"Voidal feeling Notes §0\\\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~To use the void you have to allow it to seep in and use that cloud of mana by slowly transform its gasious form in a liguid then gather it and form it when youre doing spells you make it have certain aspects.\"\n\n\"Like Ice which I think is the combination of earth and water as it has a solid shape and thus all solids come from the earth as well as water aspect which formed the inistial mana into water before the earth aspect took over... However I can only assume\"\n\n\"with these theorims... Forcing mana like creating a mana hose where you squeze the gasious mana seeping in and making it into a flood of mana rushing into you will tax more energy and consentration of the user showing signs of stress on their body.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Voidal FeelingV3", "§bJim", "\"Voidal Feeling Notes~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ §0\\\n§0Voidal feeling allows one to learn about any object by seeping their mana within the object it must not be forced in this stage because its like learning something new it takes time and patience.\"\n\n\"the information acquired by voidal feeling are about Average temperture of the substance, what its made of, its boiling and freezing points. I believe that voidal feeling also has the potential to probe different spells and learn how their cast.\"\n\n\"It can learn what combination make what and also can be seen in use by ge\\\\reat alchemists. I belive that voidal feeling has a lot to do with equivalent exchange and its actually the base of both alchemy and magic because of its learning attributes.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Voidal FeelingV4", "§bJim", "\"Voidal Feeling Notes §0\\\n§0~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ §0\\\n§0Loike all magic you have To use your hands morion ands consentration to accentuate the desired outcome of the mana your using. You also have to be aware of mana drain and also how much mana you use.\"\n\n\"Voidal feeling is helpful with deciding the outcomes based on information. But without a certain level of atttention to what your doing you could seep to much mana in and object and it could possibly implode. Because of this many mages are careful when \"\n\n\"their deciphering their desired objects. Voidal feeling must be taught to you as things can go terribly wrong when even tapping into the power. So it matters how it is used and is far safer to learn the craft from a teacher rather than your own study.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Fall of the Mori", "§bThurak'Yar", "The Fall of the   \nMori. \n\nWhen the murders and attacks on the city occurred, many speculations arose within the city itself of whom was to blame and who should be slaughtered for such acts against their kind;\n\nmany claimed it was the work of the surfacers, others believed that such things were only possible by those living within the city.\n\nIt was declared and enforced that all living Mori were to return to the bosom of Nemiisae and remain within the sanctum of Menocress; behind these stragglers to return the horror unfolded, each path and passage that journeyed through only\n\nhours before could be heard crumbling under the weight of explosives. The people were brought each in turn to the Temple of the Mother to be cleansed of their taint, the sickness of the surface that had infested them.\n\nThe final act of the Valsharess and her Yathrins before the war broke out.\n\nMany that had broken loose from such rigid traditions fought against this cleansing and became quickly enraged, spitting in the faces of the priestess’ whom dared demand their obedience and silence. It was not long before two factions emerged;\n\nthe devout and the rebels. Beneath the surface of the world, sealed off from the blinding damnation of the sun’s light, the Caverns of Menocress’ streets were littered with crude barricades, strewn with the deceased and wounded;\n\nThe once marvelled city now rots with death and destruction… crumbling under the civil war. Bathed in life blood of their kith and kin, the rebellion breached the Yathrins’ sacred enclave; banners raised in revolt, their armour and bodies marked by\n\ntheir treason. Once considered mere common rabble; these denizens now slaughter blessed noble born and their ilk standing guard at the doors of the Temple. From behind the sealed doors both rothe and Mori alike stand\n\nin the un-ease union against the threat of tait to its own city – this seeded by those turned to the hubris of their Ilharn Zanunder.\n\nRescribed by the Farseer Thurak’Braduk, 14th of the First Seed 1484.", ""),
        StaticBook("Yrodholm Diary", "§b...", "Vanhart's genius in creating the stone can hardly be fathomed. If Vanhart is no longer of this world, then I must take it upon myself to reproduce his most prized product.\n\nThe components of the stone itself are simple, but to empower it, I will need a\n\ngreat deal of souls. A great deal of death.\n\nPerhaps Avendal will finally come in useful. I have the perfect place in mind for him to pay a visit to.", ""),
        StaticBook("Caribou III", "§bCaribou Druid Hyulahon", "\"Our prince's wood is the trembling giant, the quaking aspen. Truly, a magnificent display of our highest power, for he has done what no other lord of the tree has done: spread. Whole swathes of land have turned green, flourishing with brilliant emerald \"\n\n\"leaves. His soul is the largest, grandest one of them all, stretching from sea to sea, and beneath the earth in gargantuan roots.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0It is an old druidic proverb that all of nature is connected, but it is embodied in none more clearly than our prince. The\"\n\n\"air and water flowing, and he sees and feels it all. In his whisperings, he has spoken of how he can hear the cries of all nature, across all the world.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Every blade of grass, trampled in man's foolish lust for progress. Each tree\"\n\n\"felled so that he can feed the furnace of his ambition. Our prince feels them, and truly, is there anything more to being a druid? Following our prince is the closest we can be to following the Aspects themselves.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0So, this is why we must go out, and\"\n\n\"purge the violet corruption. Ever since our prince journeyed south, the violet corruption has gripped the land, tainting his trees, one by one. They have committed a terrible atrocity in fracturing his soul. I have even heard word that the \"\n\n\"dark power behind them has calved the trees, forcing them to produce seeds in a most unnatural way.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The bright green flame has scorched many to ash, but still, I fear in some isolated pockets of the world, the purple-leafed abominations still \"\n\n\"rest.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Woe! This curse of sleep. Were only it not so strong, we could hunt them all down. Though… should I sleep, I do wonder if the totem of the Caribou will live on. It is a rare path to take. Oh well. There are more important things\"\n\n\"to consider, now.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Caribou II", "§bCaribou Druid Hyulahon", "\"I have heard tales before of word altars. Ancient artifacts of power and tongues, that could allow its bearer to control whole swathes of forest. In their stone was carved the true tongue of the Aspects, and of all nature. When it was spoken, the world \"\n\n\"listened.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Legend holds that, before they were outlawed, in Malin's City itself, there was entombed a word altar. This was before my time in the order, and so all I know of are the stories. I am not sure if it was real. Perhaps it was all a \"\n\n\"myth. It matters very little, for now that our prince is here, we have no need for myths or legends any longer.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0When he speaks, the world listens in ways I cannot begin to describe. The smallest insect can be compelled by his \"\n\n\"voice, just as the largest of the scaddernaks can be. I have seen even the rain and earth tremble at his behest. The sky sunders itself by his command, and the waters leave the ocean so that he may walk across the sandy beds. There have been miracles \"\n\n\"that no mere druid would ever be capable of.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0It makes me more certain than ever that our prince is the will of nature made manifest.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0We need no word altar to see nature's revenge upon the \"\n\n\"constructions of men, for we need only our prince.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Sporophytes", "§bCaribou Druid Hyulahon", "\"Truly, I am the slightest bit jealous of them. They are creatures which are closest to our prince.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Even when I was a druid unawakened to the truths of our prince, I had heard stories of bryophytes, even seen a few of the creatures in Malin's\"\n\n\"City. They were creatures born from the veridian moss, green through and through. They were not born of the Fae, but were closer to it than most, with plant-minds and plant-brains. There was even the rare druid who voluntarily slept in the moss, as\"\n\n\"a way to reach oneness with nature.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The moss which is kept by our prince upon his great body is not so mundane! Indeed, I would go so far as to call it §0§oroyal§0 veridian moss, for it is above what the plebian moss might be able to do. \"\n\n\"Harboring it in the hollows of his body, and nurturing it, our prince can use the royal veridian moss to usurp control of a heathen's body from their mind, and assume direct control of it. Over time, their minds are eaten away, and their bodies subsumed, \"\n\n\"turned into a fungi-ridden monument to our prince's power.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0It is a magnificent display. Still, with our prince fast asleep, I am not sure I will ever see this glory again. I can only pray to the Aspects that our deliverer wakes soon. \"\n\n\"I would rather not be taken by the sleep, myself.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Elk Diary", "§bElk Druid Tah'rayho", "\"14th of Sun's Smile§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I have overheard a few things from the hierophants. Alriel seems to have had a vision. They've sent off some of the birds to scout out the ocean around the city, and look over Tahn. I worry what they are keeping from me, and\"\n\n\"the rest of the novice druids. We may not be old, but we can help, too!§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I can only imagine how bad it is for the dedicants.\"\n\n\"15th of Sun's Smile§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The waters around the city are rising. Most of the citizenry are not too concerned, but I know something is afoot. Still, the elder druids refuse to tell me anything. It is deeply frustrating. I can see the scowls and the worry\"\n\n\"plastered on their faces!§0\\\n§0\\\n\"\n\n\"16th of Sun's Smile§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Some sort of creature has arrived in the city. I write this hurriedly. Already, we were so weak, I am not sure if we will be able to repulse it. This thing... the hierophants speak of it like it were a legend, but it is not one I have\"\n\n\"ever heard of. I can only imagine it has been scrubbed from history, if it is one.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0It is the size of the sky, larger than the mother tree. Never have I seen such a monster before. When it speaks, even our most loyal animal kin, and the mother tree\"\n\n\"herself, have struck out against us.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I worry. I go now, to fight with my brothers and sisters.§0\\\n\"\n\n\"26th of Sun's Smile§0\\\n§0\\\n§0All is over. The dream of Malin is done. I have seen our future, and it is wooden.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I... I am not sure what side to take. I do not want to die.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I'm afraid.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Kor and Luara", "§bThurak'Yar", "\"  §3 §0\\\n§3    Transcribed By§0\\\n§3            T Y§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§3         §8 _____§0\\\n§8         {~~~~}§0\\\n§8        {~~~~~}§0\\\n§8         {~~~~}§0\\\n§8          {~| |~}§0\\\n§8             | |§0\\\n§8~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~§0\\\n\"\n\n\" §4    Kor and Luara§0\\\n§0\\\n§4         |\\\\§0\\\n§4        |V \\\\_§0\\\n§4        |   ‘  \\\\§0\\\n§4        )   <_\\\\§0\\\n§4       /     |§0\\\n§4      /      \\\\§0\\\n§4      |        \\\\§0\\\n§4      \\\\        \\\\§0\\\n§4        |        \\\\§0\\\n§4        |  |\\\\      |§0\\\n§4____ /  |_`.     |______ §0\\\n\"\n\n\"\\\n§0 §0§oShe was born in a§0\\\n§0§o Cacophony- a white§0\\\n§0§o Silence in blaring§0\\\n§0§o Synaesthesia.§0\\\n§0§o Her father called§0\\\n§0§o Her Luara and cast§0\\\n§0§o Her Skyward, giving§0\\\n§0§o Him an anchor inside§0\\\n§0§o The constellations.§0\\\n§0§o Daughter of Time.\"\n\n\" To begin a tale of§0\\\n§0 such magnitude, some§0\\\n§0 context might not be§0\\\n§0 terribly out of§0\\\n§0 place. We'll start with§0\\\n§0 Time.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0 Time was Luara's§0\\\n§0 father in only the§0\\\n§0 broadest senses of§0\\\n§0 the word. As many§0\\\n§0 can attest a father§0\\\n§0 isn't necessarily§0\\\n§0 someone who raises\"\n\n\" You. A father§0\\\n§0 doesn't have to know§0\\\n§0 you and frankly§0\\\n§0 (although this may§0\\\n§0 only be the opinion§0\\\n§0 of rebellious teens§0\\\n§0 and certain writing§0\\\n§0 blocked Uruks), a§0\\\n§0 father doesn't have§0\\\n§0 to understand you.§0\\\n§0 To Luara he was the§0\\\n§0 word she used to§0\\\n§0 describe her very\"\n\n\" Beginning (probably§0\\\n§0 apt), and everything§0\\\n§0 else since then she§0\\\n§0 attributes rather§0\\\n§0 proudly to herself,§0\\\n§0 her peers and those§0\\\n§0 bothersome, fawning§0\\\n§0 mortals.§0\\\n§0 But it was with§0\\\n§0 Sandru she gained§0\\\n§0 her first purpose.\"\n\n\" When the Spirits§0\\\n§0 first interacted with§0\\\n§0 the mortal world,§0\\\n§0 Elementals alone§0\\\n§0 couldn't represent§0\\\n§0 what existed there.§0\\\n§0 Ideas existed which§0\\\n§0 couldn't be§0\\\n§0 explained by Earth,§0\\\n§0 by Wind, by Chaos§0\\\n§0 Order and, most §0\\\n§0 importantly, Time. \"\n\n\" Chaos needed §0\\\n§0 substance, Earth§0\\\n§0 needed Life and§0\\\n§0 Time needed §0\\\n§0 counting. So, in what§0\\\n§0 can possibly be §0\\\n§0 called the worst §0\\\n§0 event in the history§0\\\n§0 of the world, the §0\\\n§0 Immortals were§0\\\n§0 created.§0\\\n§0 The Immortals are §0\\\n§0 the unholy §0\\\n§0 amalgamation of \"\n\n\" The black and white§0\\\n§0 ideals of the§0\\\n§0 Elementals and the§0\\\n§0 shitstained cultures,§0\\\n§0 experiences and §0\\\n§0 contexts of the§0\\\n§0 mortals. Luara§0\\\n§0 began simply as a §0\\\n§0 being made to fill§0\\\n§0 an empty slot. In this§0\\\n§0 brave new world§0\\\n§0 Time, Sandru found,§0\\\n§0 needed Order.§0\\\n§0 Gross.\"\n\n\" Luara was created§0\\\n§0 for, or possibly §0\\\n§0 because of, the §0\\\n§0 mortal desire to §0\\\n§0 count time. Days.§0\\\n§0 Seasons. By Luara §0\\\n§0 the mortals would§0\\\n§0 live their lives, plant§0\\\n§0 their crops, bear§0\\\n§0 their children, plan§0\\\n§0 their festivals and§0\\\n§0 generally cause §0\\\n§0 ruckus and, for \"\n\n\" The first few very §0\\\n§0 successful moments,§0\\\n§0 that's precisely what§0\\\n§0 she did. The world§0\\\n§0 spun about her, and§0\\\n§0 with each frantic§0\\\n§0 revolution she lead§0\\\n§0 them ever closer to§0\\\n§0 their deaths. She §0\\\n§0 was their guide §0\\\n§0 through time.\"\n\n\" Their anchor in§0\\\n§0 space. Their§0\\\n§0 Shepard.§0\\\n§0 Then things got§0\\\n§0 messier.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0 We could blame§0\\\n§0 poets, but they're§0\\\n§0 just the most§0\\\n§0 obvious culprits. We§0\\\n§0 could blame lovers,§0\\\n§0 but they're pretty§0\\\n§0 much the same thing§0\\\n§0 just with their hands\"\n\n\" and mouths busier.§0\\\n§0 Frankly it was§0\\\n§0 inevitable, but§0\\\n§0 someone deserves§0\\\n§0 the blame and,§0\\\n§0 unfortunately, it's§0\\\n§0 probably Luara.§0\\\n§0 More than counted §0\\\n§0 time, mortals saw in§0\\\n§0 the moon distance,§0\\\n§0 silence and longing.§0\\\n§0 More than their days§0\\\n§0 and their years and\"\n\n\" their deaths they§0\\\n§0 saw (as is their§0\\\n§0 tendancy) §0\\\n§0 themselves, and§0\\\n§0 through this the§0\\\n§0 moon became more§0\\\n§0 than just what§0\\\n§0 Father Time intended.§0\\\n§0 §0\\\n§0 When alone, mortals§0\\\n§0 looked up and felt§0\\\n§0 compassion with the§0\\\n§0 distant moon. \"\n\n\" When sad, mortals §0\\\n§0 sighed at the sky §0\\\n§0 and pulled empathy§0\\\n§0 from her endless§0\\\n§0 surface.§0\\\n§0 And when in love- as§0\\\n§0 of course many §0\\\n§0 mortals were- they§0\\\n§0 had eyes for only§0\\\n§0 each other in the§0\\\n§0 moon's gentle light.§0\\\n§0 And so Luara knew§0\\\n§0 love.\"\n\n\" Not only are the§0\\\n§0 Immortals shaped by§0\\\n§0 Mortals, but by§0\\\n§0 bother Immortals§0\\\n§0 too. Their§0\\\n§0 interactions with§0\\\n§0 each other are§0\\\n§0 almost as important§0\\\n§0 as with the§0\\\n§0 bothersome§0\\\n§0 creatures below and§0\\\n§0 from them grew§0\\\n§0 personalities not§0\\\n§0 even the mortals\"\n\n\" could begin to§0\\\n§0 decipher. Great§0\\\n§0 feuds- The terrible§0\\\n§0 rivalry of Shezept §0\\\n§0 and Jevex; Great§0\\\n§0 Friendships- the§0\\\n§0 strong brotherhood§0\\\n§0 of Theruz and§0\\\n§0 Betheruz; and§0\\\n§0 eventually great§0\\\n§0 Loyalties. In this§0\\\n§0 category came the §0\\\n§0 bond of Luara and§0\\\n§0 Kor.\"\n\n\" Kor was another§0\\\n§0 bourne from Time,§0\\\n§0 but unlike Luara he§0\\\n§0 was not quite so §0\\\n§0 interested in the§0\\\n§0 journey as much as§0\\\n§0 the destination. He§0\\\n§0 was the mortals'§0\\\n§0 finale. Their full§0\\\n§0 stop. Usually, he was§0\\\n§0 the quiet end to a §0\\\n§0 fussy life. If he was§0\\\n§0 lucky, he was\"\n\n\" the very loud end§0\\\n§0 to a very fussy life.§0\\\n§0 He- though he§0\\\n§0 wouldn't admit it-§0\\\n§0 enjoyed this.§0\\\n§0 And to him Luara§0\\\n§0 was desperately§0\\\n§0 loyal.§0\\\n§0 Through all time,§0\\\n§0 Luara dragged all§0\\\n§0 souls his way. From§0\\\n§0 birth through life,§0\\\n§0 through all counted§0\\\n§0 and countless\"\n\n\" moments Luara§0\\\n§0 dragged them§0\\\n§0 willingly or not to§0\\\n§0 where she was§0\\\n§0 supposed to- Death.§0\\\n§0 This was, of course,§0\\\n§0 the original purpose§0\\\n§0 Sandru gave her,§0\\\n§0 and damned if she§0\\\n§0 couldn't do at least§0\\\n§0 that. §0\\\n§0 At first she called §0\\\n§0 it her Duty- her §0\\\n§0 job, naturally. \"\n\n\" It was her only one.§0\\\n§0 For some time she§0\\\n§0 called it loyalty-§0\\\n§0 She knew of the idea§0\\\n§0 and thought it apt.§0\\\n§0 But it was with the§0\\\n§0 painfully inflicted§0\\\n§0 eons that Luara§0\\\n§0 eventually knew its§0\\\n§0 true name. Spirits§0\\\n§0 are the most human§0\\\n§0 of deities- that is§0\\\n§0 their\"\n\n\" nature. So it was with§0\\\n§0 human agony- human§0\\\n§0 longing, perhaps- §0\\\n§0 that the moon§0\\\n§0 became deeply,§0\\\n§0 hopelessly lovesick.§0\\\n§0 In Kor she saw, for§0\\\n§0 the first true time,§0\\\n§0 the beauty of §0\\\n§0 someone in her§0\\\n§0 moonlight.\"\n\n\" Silence, however,§0\\\n§0 was in Luara's§0\\\n§0 nature.§0\\\n§0 Distance,§0\\\n§0 unfortunately, was§0\\\n§0 what the mortals§0\\\n§0 knew her by. Not§0\\\n§0 only was a spirit in§0\\\n§0 love- staggering, §0\\\n§0 she was Shy as well.§0\\\n§0 What a mess.\"\n\n\" She tried sending §0\\\n§0 gifts, but Kor was§0\\\n§0 quiet too. That's his§0\\\n§0 shtick.§0\\\n§0 The best she gave§0\\\n§0 to him herself- by§0\\\n§0 his gates she §0\\\n§0 arrived, piously §0\\\n§0 taking the form of a§0\\\n§0 great, white wolf. Her§0\\\n§0 loyalty to him- for it§0\\\n§0 was (perhaps for§0\\\n§0 love it has to be) a\"\n\n\" Great loyalty-§0\\\n§0 settling her into§0\\\n§0 this form for the §0\\\n§0 rest of her time. §0\\\n§0 Lovers and poets,§0\\\n§0 Kings and scientists.§0\\\n§0 All of them she took§0\\\n§0 to his hand, but§0\\\n§0 never did he say a§0\\\n§0 word. He nudged§0\\\n§0 them on, through his§0\\\n§0 silent gates, and she§0\\\n§0 grew\"\n\n\" Distraught. What if§0\\\n§0 he thought them §0\\\n§0 gifts of Freygoth?§0\\\n§0 Or Theruz? Or,§0\\\n§0 worst of all, Isuz!§0\\\n§0\\\n§0 It was in the middle§0\\\n§0 of her pining that §0\\\n§0 Luara looked down.§0\\\n§0 On this day her eye§0\\\n§0 blared on the world,§0\\\n§0 opened fully as was§0\\\n§0 the convention for§0\\\n§0 that time\"\n\n\" of month. It was§0\\\n§0 days like this that§0\\\n§0 dark things, mad§0\\\n§0 things and, most§0\\\n§0 importantly,§0\\\n§0 desperate things§0\\\n§0 clawed their way§0\\\n§0 from the shrubs §0\\\n§0 and howled to the§0\\\n§0 sky. And Luara was§0\\\n§0 banking on it.\"\n\n\" The §0§oMaehr§0 were a§0\\\n§0 group Elves §0\\\n§0 travelling to gain§0\\\n§0 knowledge for their§0\\\n§0 king. There's §0\\\n§0 another story- §0\\\n§0 tragic and long-§0\\\n§0 that tells of what§0\\\n§0 evils befell them, §0\\\n§0 but it will be simple§0\\\n§0 enough to say that,\"\n\n\" at journey's end, §0\\\n§0 they were not in§0\\\n§0 good shape. Their§0\\\n§0 leader, §0§oVeluluai§0, had§0\\\n§0 lose her mind§0\\\n§0 alongside her people§0\\\n§0 from the curse of§0\\\n§0 some ancient evil§0\\\n§0 and after an§0\\\n§0 unfortunate event§0\\\n§0 involving murder,§0\\\n§0 pillaging and arson§0\\\n§0 they were cast§0\\\n§0 away- \"\n\n\" Banished to an empty§0\\\n§0 isle with fading from§0\\\n§0 history as their§0\\\n§0 final punishment. §0\\\n§0 Barely, just barely,§0\\\n§0 §0§oVeluluai§0 sunk her§0\\\n§0 claws into what§0\\\n§0 remained of her mind§0\\\n§0 and drove it to pray.§0\\\n§0 Her people, who§0\\\n§0 were dying beside§0\\\n§0 their sanity, watched§0\\\n§0 on\"\n\n\" Mutely as their§0\\\n§0 beloved §0§oVeluluai§0\\\n§0 offered all she§0\\\n§0 was for their minds-§0\\\n§0 Her body- Her soul-§0\\\n§0 her very own being-§0\\\n§0 to with power that§0\\\n§0 was listening. §0\\\n§0 Unfortunately, those§0\\\n§0 with powere usually§0\\\n§0 don't listen.§0\\\n\"\n\n\" But Luara did.§0\\\n§0 While it wasn't a fair §0\\\n§0 deal, for §0§oVeluluai§0\\\n§0 and her §0§oMaehr§0 it was§0\\\n§0 quite literally a§0\\\n§0 godsend. What harm,§0\\\n§0 surely, could do the§0\\\n§0 moon, so beautiful§0\\\n§0 and distant?§0\\\n§0\\\n§0 It could have been§0\\\n§0 quite a lot really.\"\n\n\" Thankfully Luara§0\\\n§0 settled for their§0\\\n§0 bodies and their§0\\\n§0 souls.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0 These she took-§0\\\n§0 plucking from them§0\\\n§0 their pure white skin§0\\\n§0 and looking at it§0\\\n§0 with a frown.§0\\\n§0 No good.\"\n\n\" For Kor, she§0\\\n§0 shrouded their§0\\\n§0 moonlit skin in a cape§0\\\n§0 of ebony, smooth as§0\\\n§0 bone- Her moonlight,§0\\\n§0 she decided, would§0\\\n§0 be saved for Him§0\\\n§0 and only Him.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0 For Kor, she took§0\\\n§0 their eyes; the§0\\\n§0 green of Freygoth§0\\\n§0 and the intelligence\"\n\n\" Of Theruz were §0\\\n§0 covered with the red§0\\\n§0 of her Bloodmoon-§0\\\n§0 they would look at§0\\\n§0 the world through§0\\\n§0 her ancient iris.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0 For Kor, she marked§0\\\n§0 their souls. Each§0\\\n§0 one would be his as§0\\\n§0 much as hers, and§0\\\n§0 death would reach§0\\\n§0 their kind for as§0\\\n§0 long as Time.\"\n\n\" For Kor the §0§oMaehr§0\\\n§0 became black, ashen§0\\\n§0 and beautiful.§0\\\n§0 They were her gift-§0\\\n§0 ivory turned ebony§0\\\n§0 for the Spirit of§0\\\n§0 Death.§0\\\n§0 Their minds returned§0\\\n§0 to them, many of the§0\\\n§0 Maehr managed to§0\\\n§0 feel anguished with§0\\\n§0 their new form. Their§0\\\n§0 waking moments were\"\n\n\" Filled with horrified §0\\\n§0 gasps- To what§0\\\n§0 Spirit had §0§oVeluluai§0\\\n§0 given their souls?§0\\\n§0 What cruel new§0\\\n§0 curse had she set§0\\\n§0 upon their bodies?§0\\\n§0 Horrified, they§0\\\n§0 balked, and the §0\\\n§0 beginnings of panic§0\\\n§0 bled into this new§0\\\n§0 race of Elves. Under§0\\\n§0 placid moonlight\"\n\n\" They wept for lost§0\\\n§0 beauty.§0\\\n§0 Before it spread, §0\\\n§0 §0§oVeluluai§0 set forth§0\\\n§0 and calmed them with§0\\\n§0 a word. This was her§0\\\n§0 duty. Another one-§0\\\n§0 an easier one, §0\\\n§0 perhaps- she had§0\\\n§0 payed to the Spirit§0\\\n§0 of the Moon.§0\\\n§0 \"\n\n\" To see your beauty,§0\\\n§0 she told them, you§0\\\n§0 need only look up.§0\\\n§0 To see your life,§0\\\n§0 she affirmed, you§0\\\n§0 need only look§0\\\n§0 forward.§0\\\n§0 To see your soul,§0\\\n§0 she stressed, you§0\\\n§0 need only look within.§0\\\n§0\\\n\"\n\n\" And so it became§0\\\n§0 that the §0§oMaerh§0\\\n§0 dubbed themselves§0\\\n§0 Dark Elves and §0\\\n§0 civilised their§0\\\n§0 reclusive isle,§0\\\n§0 staying silent and §0\\\n§0 distant from their§0\\\n§0 past atrocities.§0\\\n§0 During a lifetime§0\\\n§0 Luara became a God§0\\\n§0 to these, her§0\\\n§0 prosperous gifts \"\n\n\" And, although she§0\\\n§0 had of course §0\\\n§0 intended for them to§0\\\n§0 eventually die, it was§0\\\n§0 with sorrow that she§0\\\n§0 escorted the first §0\\\n§0 of their dead to the§0\\\n§0 gates of Kor.§0\\\n§0 Eons upon eons §0\\\n§0 shuddered as, with§0\\\n§0 the §0§oMaehr§0 by their§0\\\n§0 side,\"\n\n\" Silence was broken§0\\\n§0 between Death§0\\\n§0 and the Moon.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0 The rest, in fact, is§0\\\n§0 rather brief.§0\\\n§0 Kor took the young§0\\\n§0 §0§oMaehr§0 in handy and,§0\\\n§0 with a skeletal grin,§0\\\n§0 beckoned the wolfish§0\\\n§0 Luara by his side.§0\\\n§0 She followed, of§0\\\n§0 course, and always§0\\\n§0 would. \"\n\n\" In the Ancestral§0\\\n§0 realm Kor created§0\\\n§0 a pocket to store§0\\\n§0 Luara's gifts- the§0\\\n§0 Groth'Stroh- and by§0\\\n§0 hand he took all of§0\\\n§0 the Dark Elves when§0\\\n§0 their time upon the§0\\\n§0 mortal plane drew to§0\\\n§0 a close. Luara, with§0\\\n§0 Kor sharing the§0\\\n§0 sentiment, never§0\\\n§0 rushed this.\"\n\n\" With love like theirs,§0\\\n§0   they could wait.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes of Auta", "§bKradac Yavarn", "\"Elder tree is the connection to all knowledge, we can connect to it some how. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Rituals involving the cannabalization of others mana §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Nature energy does not draw from the void is this Elder tree its source?\"\n\n\"Mana can be used to form things mages use it what do druids use §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Druid relationship with nature is strange and conspicuous §0\\\n§0\\\n§0I wonder if auras can change or if you can physically change auras through ritual practice\"\n\n\"Telekenisis seems to be used in druid magic as well they seem to use a form of mass telekenisis I wonder what type of r §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Trees have interconnecting systems that means a whole forest could be one organism or even several forests\"\n\n\"Druid power is gifts from the aspects §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Elder tree is just a tree not source of druids power in any way but druid can still connect tothe tree  §0\\\n§0\\\n§0A totem is unigue to each druid and has a hidden meaning decided by the user \"\n\n\"Psychological extraction of druid minds succesful they feel frightened and have shown that their willing to defend themselves if they see something wrong §0\\\n§0\\\n§0No voidal arts in grove\"", ""),
        StaticBook("BioDome 1", "§bKradac Yavarn", "\"They believe I am innept and unhinged for my invention. But I assure you it is the opposite those foolish druids think that they can handle the storm thats coming. But they are stuck in their ways unwilling to further any advancements. \"\n\n\"The Biodome is in a sense a revolutionary micro environment designed by me of course. It is capable of sustaining a variety of flora at once with a single unit. \"\n\n\"My invention is field deployable and can go wherever you are. Via of course an advanced system of piston and slime work. All the plants must be saved if I am to continue my work.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("BioDome book 2", "§bKradac Yavarn", "\"Nivndiltoday denied my idea the fool even showed off her new alchemical sunlight. Wait that makes my biodomes plausible.... Alchemical sunlight might beable to sustain plants even under ground.\"\n\n\"From my herboly guide I found four types of flora that would make my dreams a reality. One, one of air, two one of frost, three one of heat, and finally four one of fertility.\"\n\n\"The system in place would transport the araus of the preselected floral types. The arau's in theory would make it to the containment module and in theory stabilize the environment. From their humidity and general climate would be selected.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Greg Chron. I", "§bGregory", "\" §0\\\n§0\\\n§0§l§nChronicles of Greg §0                §i§0§l§nI§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0   §0§oGregory O'Donovan\"\n\n\"\\\n§0\\\n§0This Book is a Publication of §0§oGregory Press.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0All Rights Reserved.§0\\\n§0\\\n§01646.  \"\n\n\"       §0§l§nForeword§0\\\n§0\\\n§0This series of books written by my own hand shall detail the many events of my life leading to this moment, it has dawned upon me that within my many years much of what I have done remains unknown within the public sphere. Details\"\n\n\"of various encounters, events and history could perhaps remain forever lost upon my death, therefore to a certain degree this account serves as my personal connection to the many fading memories of my lifetime it also serves as a historical account for\"\n\n\"whatever purpose that may serve. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0I shall start from my earliest memories and end with the writing of this book within the halls of Dragur, nothing shall be left out and names shall not be withdrawn. If you've ever wished to know a thing about me\"\n\n\"then more than likely it shall be contained within this series of books. And under the circumstances you know nothing about me at all, then I can merely hope the contents of these many pages will peak your interest within all things historical, arcane, \"\n\n\"magical and borderline fantastic, if I were to say so myself. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Nevertheless without hesitating further here are the Chronicles of Greg.\"\n\n\"              §b§i§0 §0§l§nI§0\\\n§0\\\n§0My life started within a small Orenian fishing town, nothing of interest or note, the place to which typically one is born, worked and buried within their lifetime. At this moment my name wasn't Gregory but instead\"\n\n\"Edwyn Lynderly, named after my great grandfather. It would have been a simple existence, the town barely making its name upon maps nor the lips of passing men with its only prominent feature being the shipyard owned by my father. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0For what I lacked\"\n\n\"within early education I had gained within manual labour, some of my earliest memories are working within the shipyard and once schooling fully concluded it became my permanent position. My skills barely reflected that of my father but my curiosity\"\n\n\"constantly got in the way, my need for something beyond the boundries of this isolated little town. People would constantly pass by, speaking accounts of adventures, treasure, politics and wealth, my desire for what they held became too \"\n\n\"much, my need to escape the boundries of my little childhood town as becoming too much. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Then, at the age of twenty five, my father became angered at my constant allusion to the shipyard. My dreams of something greater than what \"\n\n\"he had built left him disappointed and afraid, and so he declared upon his death the shipyard wouldn't be left to me but instead that of a close friend. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0For some reason this angered me more, I hated the shipyard and moreso hated the \"\n\n\"thought of being its lifelong owner but the lack of acknowledgement hurt more, knowing that my own father entrusted someone else with his legacy rather than me. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0I confronted the friend, and within heated debate I would find him dead at my\"\n\n\"own hands. Truthfully, this is one of the most regrettable acts of my long life. One that I would be so ashamed of that I would never truly confront, instead I feared the consequence to my actions and fled. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Offering myself to steer the ship for a\"\n\n\"group of local villagers who dared to tempt the outside world I left the village and remained with them for some time. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Upon arrival within the heartland of Orenian Athera we found ourselves struggling for land, eventually settling for a small\"\n\n\"plot within the murky swamplands of Embermoor. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Embermoor was not a place attributed for its beauty, it instead was a vacated place to which barely supported life beyond its dark forestry. Rumours seemed to keep many away also, with fears\"\n\n\"about it being alive, its capability to consume souls or the living nightmares that supposedly haunted the tree tops. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0To a certain degree they were right to be terrified of this forest, for I later learnt of an early cult lead by one known as Adrazius. \"\n\n\"This cult has attempted something truly sinister, whatever that may be, and in doing so had shattered the barrier between our world and the spirit realm. The forest of Embermoor has become a place truly haunted by the dead, but nevertheless a place\"\n\n\"for some reason we decided to call home. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0For a number of years we would struggle, with little to our names and living within perhaps the most inhospitable of enviroments food became sparse. Yet somehow we managed, using our combined skills we built a\"\n\n\"small keep within the only patch of usable land the bog had to offer. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0The group to which I had grown close chose to spend their time within the courts of Oren, trying to solidify their names whilst climbing the ranks of power. Yet I remained\"\n\n\"within the halls of our small keep, the grief of leaving home and the murder of a close friend has left me considerably broken. I felt despite my achievements within this new world it wasn't enough, that the greater purpose I dreamt about was still\"\n\n\"missing. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0It would be then I stumble upon a text detailing the druidic guild, an order dedicated to the preservation and restoration of the natural order. My grief saw this as an opportunity, to become\"\n\n\"apart of a greater goal and to aspire to be something more. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0I would find myself become a dedicant of this order beneath the soon to be Archdruid Arinisilia, I still oddly remember the series of trials issued to me. For one I was asked to\"\n\n\"camp within the wilderness for several days, making a log of my various experiances and the influence nature had upon me. I even remember settling near a fallen log to serve as a bench, right upon a stream of water.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Another was to grow\"\n\n\"a tree, vastly boring and dull if I remember correctly but there I was seeking some deluded purpose within the halls of a elder tree. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Then, finally my 'Grand Task'. I remember now created a tome of fifty pages, detailing a series of ruins within\"\n\n\"Athera. I wish I still had a copy, but alas I do not. Nor do I exactly know how this task has any relevence to druidism and its beliefs, but I did it nevertheless. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0To a certain degree the beliefs of the druids have stayed with me, not in relation\"\n\n\"to trees, plants and all things natural but instead through the concept of balance.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Within everything there is a sense of balance, a constant battle between two forces, to disrupt this balance is to betray your purpose as a living soul through causing\"\n\n\"unneeded chaos and death. War is a prime example, the balance becomes disrupted by ones need for power or wealth, the need to overcome some little nation which poses no threat. But, these are mere rambles of an elderly man, do not consider my beliefs\"\n\n\"without criticism for they are beliefs after all. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Continuing, I presented this book with such high expectations. My Grand Task completed I expected my attunement, the connection to the fabled 'gods' I had been taught so much\"\n\n\"about. But instead of being met with praise I was simply greeted with criticism and concern, Arinislia who had served as my tutor for this period saw a certain inpatience and restlessness within me and asked for more interviews and trials, I of course\"\n\n\"failed to see the need. I had done my trials, I had proved myself within the eyes of the druids and I voiced my detest towards these unneeded barriers. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Now I look back, I'm almost thankful for them. Without them I may still be alligned within the\"\n\n\"druidic circle, one to which I have come to see as nothing greater than a magical cult. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0But, angered by this I quickly left my role within the druidic ranks. The years I had spent as an aspiring dedicant left me with nothing, simply wasting my time and \"\n\n\"barely resolving the grief I continued to hold close to me. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0From here I spent a number of years without purpose, living place to place, role to role, lost among the busy atmosphere Athera had to offer. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0One day after leaving\"\n\n\"my home within Oakhearth, strolling past the now abandoned keep I  had once built and lived within, the people I once was close to left astranged and missing, past the druidic grove to which once accepted me as one of their own, I arrived upon a\"\n\n\"graveyard.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0For why I decided to explore it I've little idea, but there I was ambling around the aged gravestones and dying wreaths when I stumble upon a cavern. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0At this point my natural curiosity was too much, for a place so clearly\"\n\n\"evil I just had to know what was contained within its depths. Firstly a maze, a simple one truth be told but nevertheless the puzzle intrigued me further, what could someone possibly wish to protect within the depths of a graveyard?\"\n\n\"The maze opened into a large cavern, littered with corpses to which causes a smell even to this day I remember. I later learned that this would be the resting place of a young Adorellan, a famed necromancer and holder of the shade curse. Within his\"\n\n\"leftover possessions I found much of interest to my youthful mind. Books upon twisted and cursed topics; shades, necromancy and even the Kal'Varak. However perhaps of even greater importance was a morbid blade forged from a dark steel, its name Amnesia, \"\n\n\"the reach of horros. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Sliding it into my ill-fitting scabbard I quickly fled the cavernous ruin and back to my embraced home within Oakhearth. Buring the blade beneath the floorboards and scouring the rotting texts I had found, a\"\n\n\"new desire become formed. The desire for necromancy. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0I often consider as to why this cursed art intrigued my young mind so much, to which I attribute to my time within the druidic order. They had created foundations within my beliefs, the\"\n\n\"need to manipulate life to preserve the balance. For the tools they had denied me, I now sought out a new means. Necromancy offered me what they did not, as cursed as the artform may be that is all I seemed to care about. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Now, shouting from the\"\n\n\"rooftops about ones desire to become a necromancer would lead nowhere. So for a number of years my studies into this dark magical artform was contained within the stolen texts, every word became intrinsically intertwined within my memory. \"\n\n\"It was by chance then I met one, who at this time, was called Salvator. Within a tavern upon a busy crossroads we began conversation, one that soon included our pasts and desires. My time within the druids was spoken about, alongside my brooding \"\n\n\"hatred towards their order and cause. To which he met with mutual appreciation, our hatred towards the druids led to a friendship and he soon informed me about his strength within the illicit acts of necromancy.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Of course I asked, to\"\n\n\"which whilst first he was hesitant he eventually agreed. The goal I had sought for such a long period was finally coming into the light, my capability to manipulate life was going to become unlocked through the wise teachings of this man I met within the\"\n\n\"odd halls of this tavern.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0To a certain degree I almost thought that of an external force was playing upon my fate, as if something was guiding me beyond my control. Now I see it merely as rare coincidence within a world of difficult\"\n\n\"understanding. But, as a youthful mind in this situation with an ego inflated beyond even mine of the later years, I could still imagine as to why I believed that Edwyn Lynderly was of some greater purpose.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0So, there I was, sitting within my home at\"\n\n\"Oakhearth as I pondered the capability of what I may become. Finally after years of roaming the land, seeking a guide to my desired knowledge I had found it. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0So upon my next meeting with Salvator, after being warned regarding the\"\n\n\"consequences to my actions, I accepted my fate for the next perhaps hundred years.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I was to become a necromancer.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Spirit Scroll 2", "§bCuthwin Wheaton", "\"Epistle to the Orcs§0\\\n§0\\\n§06:1  Grace to you and peace from our Lord GOD the Most Merciful, Singular, and Omnipotent. I am Owyn Son of Godwin, servant of the Lord, called to prophetic vocation in His service.\"\n\n\"6:2 Verily, brother, the Lord GOD saw the punishment of the first brothers in their sin. And verily they took their reckoning in the marks of Iblees, and in many future marks.\"\n\n\"6:3 But the mark of Iblees springeth not from the hand of GOD, but our own sin and folly. And such is the nature of all reckoning before the Lord, for there is no vengeance in GOD.\"\n\n\"6:4 The Lord is the Lord GOD without peer, but thou hast conjured in His place a wicked and vengeful host. And this is a sin of senseless imprudence, for there is no God but the Most Merciful GOD, and He created all things, and all things ...\"\n\n\"are His children. So before the Lord, all murder is the fratricide of Krug, and indeed thine own spirits do slay each other, and bid thee to slay. And for what purpose? There is none.\"\n\n\"6:5 So I find that thou seekest power in wrath, but there is no power like unto the Lord GOD’s. For he is the Most Merciful, the Most Powerful, and even the thousand petty wraths of the spirits overcometh not His infinite mercy.\"\n\n\"6:6 Verily, brother, the Lord GOD is the Most Benevolent, and giveth only mercy. And verily thou must find that pain cometh not from the wrath of the Lord, but as we reject him.\"\n\n\"6:7 So to ye Sons of Krug, who have fallen to other faiths, I admonish: GOD punishes not, but protects. And there is no pain with GOD, but without him. And so thou sufferest not in retribution but in separation, and in the Skies all shall find solace.\"\n\n\"Epistle to the Magi§0\\\n§0\\\n§07:1 Grace to you and peace from our Lord GOD, the Most Merciful, Singular, and Omnipotent. I am Owyn Son of Godwin, servant of the Lord, call to prophetic vocation in His service.\"\n\n\"7:2 Verily, brother, the Lord GOD put many powers into the heart of man. And verily we are all commended into the service of the Lord, and into the service of others, be we physician, craftsman, or king.\"\n\n\"7:3 But thou reservest thy gift for thine own power, and thine own gain, and even unknowingly, the gain of Iblees. But His is the eternal power, the mysterious power with no part nor piece, no mere anatomy. For who can imitate the Most Unknowable?\"\n\n\"7:4 The Lord is the Lord GOD without peer, but thou seekest power alike to his, and indeed, power equal. And this is a selfish and impossible sin, for thou seekest the supreme power, the ultimate ability, but indeed, there is no supreme but GOD,\"\n\n\"no ultimate but Him. For He is the Lord GOD incomparable, and who can truly understand Him?\"\n\n\"7:5 So I find that thou seekest impossible knowledge not for the good of all men, nor for mere wisdom, but in desire of power, and indeed, an insatiable desire, for none can overcome the Lord. For this is the greatest sin of envy, the sin of desire ...\"\n\n\"that cannot be attained, and the deepest blasphemy.\"\n\n\"7:6 Verily, brother, the Lord GOD is the Most Incomparable, and none can surpass Him, for He has no equal. And verily thou must find satisfaction in service of thine own realm, the realm of all men.\"\n\n\"7:7 So to ye magicians I admonish: GOD is unknowable. He cannot be divided nor made again, and His mysteries are the holy mysteries, and no art is alike to His boundless ability.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Spirit Scroll 1", "§bCuthwin Wheaton", "\" The Scroll of Spirit§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Originally translated and published by Hektor the Skinless Loremaster. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Recovered by Scribe Cuthwin Wheaton for the Dragur Public Library. \"\n\n\"Epistle to the Godwinites §0\\\n§0\\\n§01:1 Grace to thee and peace from our Lord GOD, the Most Merciful, Singular, and Omnipotent. I am Owyn, Son of Godwin, servant of the Lord, called to prophetic vocation in His service.\"\n\n\"1:2 Verily, brother, the Lord GOD hath given no compulsion in faith. And verily thou art commended for thy virtue and indeed thy people keep fast to their fealty. §0\\\n§01:3 But a tremendous sin ariseth in thy home.\"\n\n\"1:4 The Lord is the Lord GOD without peer, but ye Sons of Godwin givest Him a vulgar and worldly name, and abscribe Him many partners. And this is a sin of tremendous quality, for none but the Lord reside in the Highest Sky, \"\n\n\"and it is His throne, and His home alone. And even Horen, who spake the Virtues, falls short of GOD.§0\\\n§01:5 So I find that professing thyselves to be wise, thou hast made thyselves fools. For thou hast traded the glory of the Lord GOD without peer ...\"\n\n\"for the imperfections of men. Even in our time we bear the failure of Horen, for the corruption of Iblees lasts. Wilt thou worship fallible men? For the greatness of GOD is His fullness and in His purity. \"\n\n\"But thy stories raise men up with GOD for their power or virtue. Shall I worship the strong man? Shalt thou worship the tallest among ye? Nay, for the glory of GOD is not in mere magnitude, but in His fullness and His perfection.\"\n\n\"1:7 So to ye Sons of Godwin I admonish: There are no partners to GOD. For he is foremost in the sky, and has no equal, no part, no manifestation. In His name, I beg thee, brother, turn away from false gods, and seek salvation in the One.\"\n\n\"Epistle to the Jorenites§0\\\n§0\\\n§02:1 Grace to thee and peace from our Lord GOD, the Most Merciful, Singular, and Omnipotent. I am Owyn Son of Godwin, servant of the Lord, called to prophetic vocation in His service.\"\n\n\"2:2 Verily, brother, the Lord GOD spake the Virtue to Horen. And verily thou art commended for thy virtue in defense of man, and indeed thine own king kept me from death. \"\n\n\"2:3 But whilst thou maintainest the kingdom of man, the kingdom of GOD languisheth.§0\\\n§02:4 The Lord is the Lord GOD without peer, but thou failest in thy defense of His Word, and indeed, thine own brothers do mingle the word of lesser beings among His,\"\n\n\"and lapse in His commands in favor of new and foreign ways. And this is a sin of great heedlessness, for the Word of GOD lasts into the eve of the world, and the fruit of virtue cannot rot. What the Lord GOD spake, the Lord GOD spake indeed, \"\n\n\"and His Word is not abrogated, never annulled.§0\\\n§02:5 So I find that thou art strict in thy arms but lax in thy prayers, but to pray is the armor of men. For the hand of GOD is the greatest weapon to bear, and His Word the paramount strategy. \"\n\n\"2:6 There can be no laxity in faith for any reason, not war nor peace, not wealth nor poverty. So the Lord lasteth through all adversities, for He is their remedy, and without Him, they are uncured.\"\n\n\"2:7 So to ye Sons of Joren I admonish: There is no innovation in faith. For GOD is as he was and shall be, and the holiness of Horen is as the holiness of all men, forever.\"\n\n\"Epistle to the Harrenites§0\\\n§0\\\n§03:1 Grace to you and peace from our Lord GOD the Most Merciful, Singular, and Omnipotent. I am Owyn Son of Godwin, servant of the Lord, called to prophetic vocation in His service.\"\n\n\"3:2 Verily, brother, the Lord GOD hath devised for us the metals of the earth, and the wine of the vineyard. And verily he hath granted the pleasures of the flesh and ordained the estates of all men, high and low.\"\n\n\"3:3 But he hath too spake the Virtue, and commended us to His Word. And indeed, thou livest only by His grace, and upon His earth.\"\n\n\"3:4 The Lord is the Lord GOD without peer, but thou failest in His Virtue, and neglect the good of GOD for what is forbidden. And this is a sin of sightless pride, for what the Lord bids, he Has thus bidden. And who shall escape His sight?\"\n\n\"All things live and perish before Him, and even the mountains are but shifting dunes in His eye. What iniquity shalt thou hide?\"\n\n\"3:5 So I find that thou professest thy worth but spurn His Word, and there is no man worthy before Him. For he who rejecteth holiness doth reject the Lord, and there is no GOD but the Most Holy GOD, the GOD of Horen, and of all things.\"\n\n\"Though the thief may find refuge and the blasphemer speak softly, the Lord’s eye is cast over all sin, and to reject Him in sight of no other is the truest rejection, the lasting condemnation.\"\n\n\"3:6 Verily, brother, the Lord GOD is the wisest GOD, and He knoweth all things, in darkness, in light, in the din of the market, in the silence of the mind. And what judge is there but the all-seeing? Who shall advocate against surety?\"\n\n\"3:7 So to ye Sons of Harren I admonish: There is no refuge from the sight of GOD. For He sees all things, and no sin is hidden before him, even in the farthest realm.\"\n\n\"4:1 Grace to you and peace from our Lord GOD the Most Merciful, Singular, and Omnipotent. I am Owyn Son of Godwin, servant of the Lord, called to prophetic vocation in His service.\"\n\n\"4:2 Verily, brother, the Lord GOD hath created all the beasts of the earth, and the vegetation, and the fruit-bearing trees. And verily he hath raised from the earth the high mountains, and placed the greater and lesser lights in the sky.\"\n\n\"4:3 But he hath created too the first men, and instilled in our hearts the means of invention, and the forest grove and city market are equal in worldly vulgarity.\"\n\n\"4:4 The Lord is the Lord GOD without peer, but thou hast reserved thy worship for his worldly creations, and divided the world into what is holy and what is unholy. And this is a sin of remarkable folly, for there is no holiness in ...\"\n\n\"creation but with the Lord, and thou canst not divide what is vulgar betwixt what is with God and what is without Him. For all things are the Lord’s creation, and what is vulgar cannot be holy.\"\n\n\"4:5 So I find that thou exaltest the beasts and trees, and impugnest the work of man, and each act is alike in folly. For the glory of God is pervasive and universal, and divine grace suffuses all things. And to divide holiness is to dismiss...\"\n\n\"it, for the qualities of the Lord GOD are infinite and eternal. Where art thy spirits in the great underground domiciles of the dwarves? In the wastes of the south, where no being dareth flourish?\"\n\n\"4:6 Verily, brother, the Lord GOD is in all things, and He is eminent above them. And verily thou must find salvation and glory in His grace, not in His creations.\"\n\n\"4:7 So to ye Sons of Malin, who have fallen to other faiths, I admonish: GOD is in all creation, and divinity cometh not from the verdure nor beasts of this world, but are breathed into them by His grace. And GOD is with all holy...\"\n\n\"things, be they of glade or village.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Epistle to the Dwarves §0\\\n§05:1 Grace to you and peace from our Lord GOD the Most Merciful, Singular, and Omnipotent. I am Owyn Son of Godwin, servant of the Lord, called to prophetic vocation in His service.\"\n\n\"5:2 Verily, brother, the Lord GOD breathed life into the Aenguls and the Daemons, and He put into them their power, and made their home in the Skies. And verily the virtuous are worthy of our regard, and from them we may claim precious wisdom.\"\n\n\"5:3 But the Lord too hath created the holy Word, and breathed life into all things. And what breath among all the heavens is so sacred? There is none truly alike to Him.\"\n\n\"5:4 The Lord is the Lord GOD without peer, but thou hast divided his infinite authorities among many beings, and in such thou profane what is divine. And this is a grievous sin, for in parting holiness, thou destroy it, and thou hast traded ...\"\n\n\"one GOD of infinite power for many of little worth. And more so, the Denier is wicked, and he takes many guises. And soon, for their weakness, he may creep into idols of thy temples, and into the vast halls of thy false gods, and ...\"\n\n\"little by little take many roles, and bring great iniquity.§0\\\n\"\n\n\"5:5 So I find that thou raisest up what is strong in thine own eyes, but weak before the Lord, and soon thou shalt find the Denier among thee. For as Saul, a mere servant, once walked amongst men, it was the wife of Horen who cast him out.\"\n\n\"And without the strength of GOD, who among ye can hope to cast out Iblees?\"\n\n\"5:6 Verily, brother, the Lord GOD is the greatest power, and even all the many forces of the world marshalled against Him are as but a breeze before a mountain.\"\n\n\"5:7 So to ye Sons of Urguan, who have fallen to other faiths, I admonish: GOD is able to do all things. And His power is not parted among His many servants, but imitated, and even in His multitude of ways, He is above them all.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Greg Chron. II", "§bGregory", "\"\\\n§0\\\n§0§l§nChronicles of Greg§0\\\n§0              §0§l§nII§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0 §0§oGregory O'Donovan\"\n\n\"\\\n§0\\\n§0The book is a Publication of §0§oGregory Press.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0All Rights Reserved.§0\\\n§0\\\n§01646. \"\n\n\"             §0§l§§  §0§l§nII§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The last issue covered around the first thirty years of my life, so I shall quickly recap the events that had occured so far. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0I was born into a small fishing town before I was forced to flee due to morbid \"\n\n\"circumstance. I became close friends with those I had left with, settling with them for some time within the cursed forests of Embermoor. However still filled with grief, I continued to seek further purpose.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I believed to have found purpose within\"\n\n\"the Druidic Order, yet after being denied my chance (fortunately) for attunement I grew angry, leaving the order behind and seeking my purpose elsewhere.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0After discovering a series of books my knowledge was expanded to that of\"\n\n\"more cursed magical forms, and by mere chance I found a figure known as Salvator to guide me upon this path. After some discussion he would offer me the chance to learn necromancy as his student. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0If you wish to know\"\n\n\"more details regarding this period, please read the prior edition. Nevertheless we shall continue from where we left off. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0            * * *§0\\\n§0\\\n§0There I was, now a student of perhaps one of the most twisted magical forms ever\"\n\n\"discovered by mortal life. Ignorant towards the moral and physical consequences my lessons would continue for some time, and during such I sought out a new group.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I befriended a high elf known as Kalenz, once a highly regarded figure within the\"\n\n\"Haelun'or political circles. He had decided to engage with a new endeavour, forming a group of scholars known as the Crimson Hearts. Oddly enough they would too settle within the cursed swamps of Embermoor, to which once more I would help construct.\"\n\n\"Truth be told their exact purpose seems to elude me, however I found use within their members. Most were youthful and ignorant, I commonly found myself abusing this fact to get what I needed. Nothing truly sinister, however still perhaps morally wrong. \"\n\n\"Nevertheless although this group witnessed some success within the short term, the long term would not match such success. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0With the halls of the Crimson Hearts falling empty I found myself seeking a new purpose once more, and it would be with this I\"\n\n\"found myself first attuned with the arcane. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Meeting a curious high elven mind, Iatrilemar, he was seeking a means to teleport within the blink of an eye. Nevertheless he found himself struggling within his studies, thus I offered my own\"\n\n\"hand within his research. It took some time, however eventually we began to see progress, firstly developing the voidal anchor before eventually we figured out a means to tame the chaotic maze that was the voidal plane. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Naming our new \"\n\n\"process Voidal Shifting, we left each other on good terms. The relationship between us was perfectly sculpted for research and science so once our goal had been compelted we had no reason to further communicate. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0I sometimes consider\"\n\n\"why this topic would become one of my lifelong goals, the idea of researching into the arcane. I believe now I can recognise the sense of power it provides, knowing that you've unlocked a piece of knowledge that nobody else even begins to understand. \"\n\n\"Within my youth this would inflate my ego considerably, I would consider myself a godlike man above everyone else. Now, within my old age I see how stupid I was to consider myself like this. The idea of conserving knowledge, not informing and teaching,\"\n\n\"it makes little sense. What I learnt I wish I was quicker to teach others, perhaps this is why I now found comfort within the halls of the library. A place of learning and sharing, one in which I'm able to narrate my own experiances. \"\n\n\"Continuing, I had grown bored of Edwyn. I believed him to be too defined by his past, a figure rooted within stone that I struggled to break away from. So it would be this that lead me to create my first persona, an usual character known as the\"\n\n\"Sage of Aurich. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0By utilizing an illusionary artefact I had paid for, alongside some makeup and hair dye I took upon the apperance of an elderly man. To a knowledgeable eye, they would've seen through my disguise within an instant. \"\n\n\"So for its success to be completed I settled within new lands, the small town of Aurich (to which my name derived from). §0\\\n§0\\\n§0I would impress the many members of the town with my magical prowess, often shouting cantations and various, random\"\n\n\"slurs that made little sense which seemingly evoked magic from thin air. They offered me a decaying tower upon the outskirts of their town, to which I settled for some time. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0It would be hear I would experiment with transfiguration further, both the\"\n\n\"voidal form and that of the ruinic. Using my years within the town I grew quite adept, and still to this day utilize its many uses within everyday life. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0But, as seems to become a common ending to my many tales, the town would be short lived. Its\"\n\n\"leadership and citizens disappearing to go about new business elsewhere, and even so I remained within my given tower. I had nowhere to go, nobody to stay with, instead I just remained within this settlement and continued practicing my arcane and dark\"\n\n\"magic. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0This state of isolation had left me not within stable mind, and after several further months I finally decided that leaving was the only choice. The small space of the basement was rotting my mind, but my desire for research was\"\n\n\"still there.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0So, with my goal in mind I persued Haelun'or. They held a vast library, underground labs and a matching burning passion for research. However there was an issue, I was no high elf but a mere human. To be accepted among their\"\n\n\"ranks would be an impossible feat. What was I to do?§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Well, using my previously obtained skills of disguise combined with further illusionary items I was able to construct a new apperance; that of a high elf. Claiming to be slightly stunted within\"\n\n\"growth, and my now frail body from extended time as a necromancer I somehow managed to find a place among their ranks. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0My position was further solidifed with the fall of Athera, when a monolith of a worm seemingly ate the earth beneath all the major\"\n\n\"settlements and the citizens were forced to flee. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0It would be here I further solidfy my position within the high elven circle, using the blueprints provided by Yuln I used my skills within construction to assist within the production of their\"\n\n\"new settlement, a large single building to which would house the entire populous of Haelun'or. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0My efforts would be quickly recognised by the people of the city, when through election I was granted the position of Okarir'leyun. It was quite something\"\n\n\"really, one of human blood leading the so-called 'pure elves' of Haelun'or. I'm just hoping enough time has passed since Vailor to justify the passing of this information, otherwise I may still§0\\\n§0face consequence from their rather differing councils. \"\n\n\"Nevertheless, keeping up my disguise became difficult. To act and play along with their values without truly believing within them is rather taxing. Eventually, after one mistake too many I would be challenged on my position by the Okarir'akalyn. \"\n\n\"The vote of incompetence would not pass however, despite a close formal meeting and court. Within my youth I was offended, insulted even that he would dare consider me not worthy of my title. I sometimes think I perhaps forgot my true blood, the \"\n\n\"disguise barely had any time left after all. I aged much quicker and years had passed since my introduction into Haelun'or, I'm suprised nobody had noticed already.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0So, this persona I had developed, Vesyrn Volodar, became my weapon within\"\n\n\"revenge. I would take out my anger upon the high elves, specifically those that dared to challenge me. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0I had developed a means to manipulate thanhium into an explosive substance, it was naturally volatile so didn't require much tampering. The exact\"\n\n\"method I used however shall be withdrawn, for I do not wish to advise those with malicious intent on how to cause vast amounts of harm to those underserving. §0\\\n§0There I went about serving up my revenge, using my technique to cause harm to the halls \"\n\n\"I once built with my very own hands. Was there a need for my actions? Were they justified? Not at all, truthfully I believe my time within high elven culture had warped my mind significantly.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Nevertheless I would be quickly found out,\"\n\n\"I was foolish in choosing targets and one known as Suliin'thill quickly uncovered the truth through correlation. Left revealed, Vesryn Volodar would be outcast from the community he was once respectable within. \"\n\n\"With nothing left for the persona, I dropped it. It would be my last true disguise, from this moment onwards I would retain my human features and motivations. However, I would not be called Edwyn any longer. For me that name represented a life I wished\"\n\n\"to leave behind, a history to which I'm unable to evolve beyond. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Therefore, I was take upon the name I keep to this day. Gregory. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0It would be here where I first discovered the Founders Hall, and it would become my\"\n\n\"obsession for a number of years. One that would even lead to developing my own skills, such as telekinesis, for lifting the ridiculous amount of rubble left behind by age. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0The halls, to which I intend to write a seperate text upon,\"\n\n\"were truly magnificent. Ancient, unoccupied and yet still beyond our comprehension. The magical arts locked within its walls were endlessly interesting yet impossible to decipher, despite the amount of time I spent studying their context.§0\\\n\"\n\n\"What I did find however is that the halls once served as a base for an ancient order lead by three individuals; Neldor, Nalgrem and Tarius. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Each was skilled within a different magical art, Neldor was of elven blood and practiced the arcane, Helgrem\"\n\n\"came from dwarven kin and beared the secrets of runesmithing and golemanacy. The final was a twisted individual, a human by the name of Tarius. He strived for the dark arts, ancient forms of necromancy... he seemed motivated by extending his life,\"\n\n\"he aged quicker than his two peers and thus felt he deserved to live as long. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0There is much to say about these halls, they were truly fascinating. However its end would be bought about by Tarius and his wicked means. Through a series of events he\"\n\n\"would bind a dark spirit to the halls, yet with his plan revealed the other two members would be furious towards his actions. The group becoming disbanded and the fate of the trio lost. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0But it would be Helgrem's creation that would be most \"\n\n\"interesting, a hyper-intelligent golem beyond the mind of any mortal being. Its cores were interconnected as far as the eye could see, it and I spoke on many occasions. He didn't confide much within me, he constantly sought a means to escape the confines\"\n\n\"of the halls but would never find success. I ensured my own entryway was sealed and unknown to him, although the halls had become his playground I quickly found means locked within the secrets of the founders to hide from him. \"\n\n\"There was one room however that was incredibly interesting to me at the time, a ruibrium processing facility. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0By using this ancient machine I was able to process a supply of destructive and rare ruibrium into a consumable\"\n\n\"substance, and an addictive one at that. I found texts that detailed how the founders manipulated this to gather funds for research, supplying the dark underworld in exchange for vast wealth. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0My own curious mind\"\n\n\"could not resist trying, and so after some time I perfected the process they had spoke of. Processing Ruibrium into a new drug to be distributed among the citizens of Vailor. \"", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwedmar Hist. 1", "§bBenjamin W. Goldhand", "\"          -Aegis-§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Dwarven Race is created by YEMEKARR§0\\\n§0\\\n§0-----§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Uruguan creates the first Kingdom of Urguan, by founding the city of Kal'Urguan.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0A fall Aengul named Ondnarch brings an\"\n\n\"eternal winter by attacking northern Dwarf holdings.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Empire of Khorvad is built from the ashes of Ondnarch's attack.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Velkan Ironborn assumes rule of the Empire and establishes the Ironborn clan.\"\n\n\"The Great Collapse occurs, where Thorngar Ironborn burns almost all books and scrolls from previous eras.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Dwarf Simppa establishes a Dwarven Confederation in the North to resist the Empire.\"\n\n\"King Simppa reestablishes the Kingdom of Urguan by defeating Thorngar Ironborn.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0After growing ill, Simppa is replaced by Charles Grimlie. King Grimlie rules like a dictator and expands Dwarven cities across Aegis.\"\n\n\"Kal'Bryst falls under the new Undead threat.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Caravan war begins between the Orcish Rexdom and the Kingdom of Urguan.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0After Human subterfuge in the Kingdom's vault, King Grimlie declares war on the Kingdom of Oren, an unpopular     move\"\n\n\"The Grandaxe splits into the Braveaxes and Blackaxes after disputes between Decks Grandaxe and King Grimlie.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Blackaxes found Kal'Domhain while the Braveaxes remain loyal.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Kal'Alras declares independence and\"\n\n\"founds the nation of Alras.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0King Belin Irongut succeeds King Grimlie adn brings the Kingdom back to its democratic roots.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Outer Kal'Urguan is developed, becoming known as The Crag.§0\\\n\"\n\n\"King Algrim Irongut begins his rule, assuring in an era of stagnation. Many Dwarven clans leave Kal'Urguan during this period.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Clan Blackaxe returns to Kal'Urguan under the leadership of Bazian Blackaxe to revive the city.\"\n\n\"The Dwarven legion sees its first action in battle against the Undead as they defend the Elven city of Malinor.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Fort Fairleaf is constructed as a joint defence project agains the Undead between the Wardens and Legion.\"\n\n\"The Legion and Wardens launch a successful assault on Wrath's Clutch. However, tensions over each sides' commitment to the battle are raised.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Relations between the Elven nation and Dwarven nation are damaged as Fort Fairleaf is demolished\"\n\n\"The Legion is sent to defend Al'Khazar as its King Edmund Sheffield is corrupted.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Marshall Thorik Braveaxe uses the Legion to repulse Queen Cassandra's Undead assault on Kal'Urguan.\"\n\n\"The Legion begins tis first peacekeeping mission on the King's Road as the Orcish nation and Human nation go to war.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0King Algrim Irongut is captured by Undead and is eventually corrupted, leading to his arrest.§0\\\n§0\\\n\"\n\n\"The shortlived reign of Gotrek Starbreaker is followed by the establishment of a ruling War Council.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0As the Orcish-Human War winds down to a close, The Legion assist the Orcs in the assault of Al'Khazar.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0A defensive pact is signed between\"\n\n\"Kal'Urguan and the Nation of Oren.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0A joint Legion-Oren assault is lead on an Undead keep that threatens Aeriel's Keep.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The War council is overthrown by Thorik Braveaxe, with support of the Braveaxes and Blackaxes.\"\n\n\"The Tazarak is established as an alliance between Alras, Oren, and Urguan which creates tensions with the Orcs and the Wardens. Alras soon backs out of the alliance.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Verge is discovered and ventured into.\"\n\n\"The first Grand Tournament is held, with Kjell Ireheart named as the first Grand Champion of Urguan.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0War is sparked across Aegis after several skirmishes between Legion and Orcish forces.\"\n\n\"The Great War begins as Dwarven, Human, and Kaxil Clan troops march against Orcish, Warden,a dn Teutonic troops.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The seige of Galahar is begun and ended as news that the Dwarves and Humans plan to seige Krugmar, the capital of the Orcs.\"\n\n\"The Wardens power declines as the war goes on, eventually leading to their disbandment and the end of the Orc - Elf alliance.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0new alliances are made between Kal'Urguan and Oren, and between the Kaxil Clan and the city of Aeriel.\"\n\n\"A period of Dwarven isolation occurs as the Undead attacks increase.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0A map peice is delivered to and deciphered by Dwarven scribes. The map would show the path to escape Aegis to Asulon.§0\\\n\"\n\n\"Refugees from Al'Khazar flee to Kal'Urguan and Alras after the Undead capture the city.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Valen Blackaxe and Warlord Mogroka'Gorkil sign a peace treaty, establishing the United Aegis Coalition.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Councillor Gimrik Braveaxe is \"\n\n\"corrupted by Undead when he surrendurs the Legion fort by Wrath's Clutch to the undead.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Legion marches to the aid the Phoenix rebels in Galahar against Orcish armies. This results in the split up of Oren between Hansetti and Renatus.\"\n\n\"Kal'urguan is removed from the United Aegis Coalition after Urir Ireheart massacres hundreds of Alrasian citizens.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0After King Syrio of Alras sends bounty hunters after the Irehearts, the Blackaxe and Frostbeard clans defend the Irehearts.\"\n\n\"The Legion and Knights of Galahar assault Alras to recover the map that would show the path out of Aegis.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0An alliance is established between Kal'Urguan, Renatus, and Malinor. Preliminary work is put in to add Hansetti and Krumar.\"\n\n\"Kal'urguan falls to Undead armies, leading to Dwarven reguees fleeing ot Tazarak.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The first Doomforge is born, a mixed race of Urir Ireheart and Faeyin the Dark Elf.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Kjell Ireheart, Urir Ireheart, and Valen Blackaxe enter the Nether to defeat the\"\n\n\"Undead. Urir Ireheart sacrifices himself to save the races of Aegis, while Kjell Ireheart and Valen Blackaxe manage to escape.§0\\\n§0\\\n\"\n\n\"The Dwarves and other nations of Aegus flee to the Verge and escape form the chaos. Kjell ireheart however refuses to leave his home of Kal'Urguan, while Valen Blackaxe is knocked overboard when a lightning bolt strikes the ship's mast.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Founders Halls", "§bGregory", "\"\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0§l§nThe Founders Halls§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0        §0§oBy§0\\\n§0§o  §0§oGregory O'Donovan\"\n\n\"\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0This book is a publication of §0§oGregory Press.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0All Rights Reserved.§0\\\n§0\\\n§01647.\"\n\n\"     §0§l§o§nForeword§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Founders Halls were a location first explored by myself during the realm of Vailor, it was an ancient construction to which I learnt the history through scattered texts and illustrations. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Despite such, some\"\n\n\"information remains unknown. I shall cover my own theories of their purposes however nothing is entirely certain.\"\n\n\"     §0§l§nHistory§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Founders Hall were established by three figures; Neldor, Halgrem and Tarius. Each came bearing of a different race, each skilled with a different art. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Neldor was born with elven blood and\"\n\n\"was a masterful arcane mage. Halgrem was of dwarven kin and beared great knowledge of runesmithing and golemancy. The final, Tarius, was a human, a twisted individual he neglected the arcane in favour of the dark arts. §0\\\n§0\\\n\"\n\n\"His main purpose was to find a means to extend his life, he found it unfair his peers would live long beyond him merely due to the actions of his ancestors. For the most part he was succesful, his body was twisted and broken but he would be one to live \"\n\n\"much longer than the average human. How? I've not the faintest idea, he would often hide his research within riddles and chaotic notes. Most the§0\\\n§0time barely legible.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Nevertheless the unlikely trio recognised their individual prowess \"\n\n\"and formed a mutual alliance. Their bond attracted the many curious minds of the world and they quickly found themselves with an array of followers, an order established within secrecy to which few beyond their ranks knew the existence of.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0But, they were\"\n\n\"without home. Some city states offered individuals research spaces, however it wouldn't be enough. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0They decided to move deep beneath the worlds crust, shifting dirt and stone until they established the first sections of their halls. Intially, they\"\n\n\"were small. But soon found themselves growing, Halgrem's golems would become workers among the halls and easily construct whatever they required. No room was without purpose, each seemingly a new exploration of the unknown and knowledge. \"\n\n\"However it would be the discovery of a fascinating piece of even more ancient technology that would push them to the limit.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The discovery? The Elders Forge, a beautiful construction of quartz and arcane. But even with their combined knowledge\"\n\n\"they would be unable to fully understand it, so therefore Halgrem developed a solution. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0A golem, but one constructed of a vast number of cores. More and more were added, within attempt to uncover the secrets. For some time it would work, they uncovered\"\n\n\"every arcane fluctuation until the paradoxs before them unfolded. Unknown dimensions, teleportation, portals, it was a seemingly endless pool of knowledge. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0However the end would come soon for the trio, with Tarius' \"\n\n\"introduction of a dark spirit into the halls. However the other two disagreed, they believed Tarius to be greedy and foolish, ordering him to remove it from the halls. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0But it was already present, a difficulty to remove. He eventually found a means to\"\n\n\"confine it but it would involve corrupting one of the most prized artefacts within the halls. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0A set of armor discovered deep within the forge, capable of sealing mortal vessels within its core. Nevertheless he continued, but his\"\n\n\"plan was rooted within failure. The only result was the corrupted armor, to which left the other two enraged.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Thus, they formulated a  plan. To use the armor to seal away Tarius, away from the halls and unable to cause harm. But, the golem, Nargun, had\"\n\n\"other plans. Within the expansion of its cores it had broken free of its impera, it warned Tarius of their plan to seal him within the armor. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0From here, all records seemingly end. There wasn't any evidence within the halls, as if they had simply\"\n\n\"vanished.\"\n\n\"§l§nAreas in the Halls§0\\\n§0\\\n§0§nRuibrium Processing§0\\\n§0A large construction empowered by the arcane, and other seemingly complicated techniques. It would be used to process Ruibrium into a new substance, originally thought to have medicinal purposes\"\n\n\"however it would soon found to be addictive, destructive and rare. There is evidence that the Founders used this to find wealth, fueling much of the research within the barren halls. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0§u§0§nThanhium Manipulator§0\\\n§0A room, through enchanting, that\"\n\n\"retained below freezing temperature. Without decent clothing the skin would become frozen, with any moisture struggling to coexist with the excess ice. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Its purpose was to seemingly provide an enviroment to which it was safe to\"\n\n\"manipulate thanhium, that by removing all heat from the room it would be considerably more stable and less prone to exploaded. From what I read they found some success, however limited, but it would seemingly be neglected following the expansion of the\"\n\n\"halls. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0§nGolem Core§0\\\n§0The centre of the golem that oversaw the facility, not only acting as a means of storing knowledge but also ensuring each individual room operated with success. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Though it was left\"\n\n\"fractured and broken by time (at least seemingly so), with the aid of a peer I was able to restore some function. Nevertheless due to it exceeding its need for an impera long ago, it was seemingly of its own motivations. §0\\\n§0\\\n\"\n\n\"§nElder's Forge§0\\\n§0A beautiful artifact that wasn't constructed by the founders but something even before them. Despite discovering some of its potential, it is to be believed that its true capability remained locked away. For the most part however\"\n\n\"it operated as a giant enchanter, to which its control panel was a large organ like construct to which keys produced a sound unlike any other. Nevertheless, by playing certain pieces of 'music' certain pedestals would unlock and would imbue an item with a\"\n\n\"particular effect. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0It was a difficult piece to understand, with the pieces of music lost to time its true potential was also lost. Even the weakest of enchantments required vast knowledge to create, knowledge that I would be unable to find myself.\"\n\n\"§nFisherman's Wharf§0\\\n§0An odd construct by the hands of Tarius, it would be a fishermans hut constructed within a seemingly natural cave. However bound to this place would be a dark spirit. Haunting the area, challenging any who dare enter its resting\"\n\n\"place. It would appear Tarius used this to research the nature of spirits, in relation to the many spirits and apparitations that float this ground before losing control. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0§nArmour Vault§0\\\n§0A medium sized room to which at the end sat a glimmering set\"\n\n\"of armour, encased within a transmuted glass that was resistant to damage. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Standing within rows however were skeletal warriors, glad within armor and wielding sword or bow. If one attempted to cause§0\\\n§0harm, or steal the armor they would\"\n\n\"seemingly activate. Protecting the artifact and attacking that which they percieved to be a thief. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0By my presumption it was of Tarius' creation, however the exact details like much else has been lost.\"\n\n\"§nThe White Prison§0\\\n§0A room built entirely out of quartz with a single cell at its centre. It would be an odd construct, entirely made of glass with enough space to house one person for any given time. But wickedly there would be another element to the\"\n\n\"prison that haunts my thoughts to this day.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Upon the activation of a switch fine thanhium dust would flood the chamber. Quickly killing anything inside, for what purpose it served I didn't dare research further.\"\n\n\"  §0§l§nFinal Thoughts§0\\\n§0\\\n§0This has been a somewhat detailed account of all I uncovered regarding the Founders Halls, ever since Vailor it has remained seemingly locked away from prying eyes so my research has been restricted. If one\"\n\n\"is able to rediscover its incredible rooms I do hope this book is of aid, and if not this merely serves as a historical account of a facility now lost.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Greg Chron. III", "§bGregory", "\"\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0§l§nChronicles of Greg §0             §0§l§nIII§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0  §0§oGregory O'Donovan\"\n\n\"\\\n§0\\\n§0This book is a publication of §0§oGregory Press.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0All Rights Reserved.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§01647.\"\n\n\"            §0§l§nIII§0\\\n§0\\\n§0So, to once more recall all that has happened so far (as much as I advise you read the prior two editions before this one), I left my home village following an incident with a group of locals. Becoming close friends, \"\n\n\"we settled within the swamps of Embermoor where we constructed§0\\\n§0a keep.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0However, still feeling without purpose I had thought to find such within the druidic order. Entering as a dedicant, I finished the process before being denied entry due\"\n\n\"to my supposed anger and lack of patience. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0So within my hatred I began finding a new purpose, one within the twisted dark arts after discovering tomes within an old hideaway of Adorellan. After finding a teacher I would engage with this path, becoming a\"\n\n\"necromancer.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Continuing forward I would cycle through many groups, the Crimson Hearts, the town of Aurich, before finding myself within the high elves as Vesryn Volodar. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Here I would climb the ranks despite my true\"\n\n\"humanity hiding behind the disguise, before being called out and angered once more. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Etcetera, etcetera.. We found ourselves within the founders hall with my ruibrium refining process perfected. At first it was merely me, distributing the product\"\n\n\"among the population and making small amounts of mina. But then, I began hiring others to sell on my behalf. At one point I had around ten employees across Vailor selling my illicit substance.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Even the governments of nations seemingly\"\n\n\"ignored me, the substance was new and foreign. They barely even recognised the harm it causes to those addicted.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0But, the morality of the situation barely came to my mind. The mina the substance was making was indeed phenomenal, but more importantly\"\n\n\"was vital within increasing my research and ensuriing progress was constantly being made. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0But, the income eventually became too much for me to even spend. My bank account stretched to around fourty thousand mina\"\n\n\"from ruibrium trade alone, and with the constant allusion to the harm it caused with every sale.. Even I couldn't handle it.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Withdrawing the remaining product and stopping production, it would be the last time I engaged with the criminal underworld.\"\n\n\"Besides, my efforts has not gone unnoticed. Several groups has taken interest within the wealth granted to me by the substance. Even death threats were sent my way, continuing within this field would surely lead to consequences I'd be unable to handle.\"\n\n\"So, with money in hand and criminal world behind me I left to settle within a newly established town, one particularly popular with mages. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Truth be told, I forget the name. However it was quite the magnificent little town, located upon an\"\n\n\"island deep within a forest.. Its buildings were sculpted from quartz, with evidence of magical prowess upon every corner. It was indeed quite the gathering of minds with seemingly neverending conversation. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0But, more importantly I found a rich deposit\"\n\n\"of thanhium nearby. It happened as I explored the island, I had noticed a chill within a particular segment. Upon further exploration I found that beneath the earth thanhium sat waiting to be mined.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Thus, after asking the city for permission\"\n\n\"I built a beautiful mine. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0It was quite something, even the process to refine it into usable substance was one entirely sculpted by myself and my partner, Avenel. As per usual however I would feel the need to research, so beneath the mine I built a\"\n\n\"new complex. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0It featured a vast library, research spaces, meeting rooms and more importantly a vault to which size was undefeated. Inside were a series of artefacts now lost to§0\\\n§0the collapsing worlds. However at the time was quite the marvel. \"\n\n\"My research projects were vast and of differing success, one project even involved attempting underground farming however I could never get the crops to properly form.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0One invention that did work however was the arcane relay, a means\"\n\n\"of long range communication. By utilizing an adapted form of the original holocron/lexicon engineered by Kalameet alongside new enchants, etc, it was able to project someones image across the realm. I perhaps shall write a book detailing exactly how,\"\n\n\"to allow replication for any budding mage. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0I would come to invite people to attend the space, offering them space for their own research. Firstly Avenel, then Leoric (a figure I had grown close to over the past few years). Eventually our numbers\"\n\n\"extended to around 10 members. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0I wished to achieve something similar to the founders hall, a group of scholars each with their own aspirations for knowledge and research. The order, named The Brotherhood, was hidden beneath\"\n\n\"Gregory Corp. It was the perfect cover, providing a shroud to hide the organisation and its travels whilst also fueling the needed research through its many business areas. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Speaking of Gregory Corp, its main distribution was \"\n\n\"thanhium, specifically the Thanhium Ice Boxes we distributed across the realm to keep food chilled.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0We never really did much investigation into the toxicity until later on, when we found that food within would be so toxic it'd quite actually be unsafe to\"\n\n\"eat. However, by the time we'd discovered such everyone seemingly had one. So, well, oops. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0The mine would eventually expand to a ruibrium deposit nearby, this time however I would not use it within the creation of a illicit\"\n\n\"substance but one for magical invention and use. Although it never truly sold well, it was always a pleasant asset to have for the order beneath Gregory Corp. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0It would be this order to which we accomplished much, perhaps notably \"\n\n\"however would be the closing of the voidal node that sat beneath the Caliphate. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Quite the dangerous thing, it would be chaotic and volatile.. Spawning all beings of the void to which would inflict harm upon the civilians. So, tasked with removing it \"\n\n\"(whilst simultantiously trying to avoid it being abused by those of evil intent) we explored the depths of its core.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Truth be told, much of my memory remains lost of this exercise. The swarms of chaotic energy that pulsated around the final chamber\"\n\n\"began corrupting my mind, growing restless I supposedly attacked the central pillar to which eventually caused the voidal nodes downfall. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Then I awoke, within the shattered remains of the node. I was convinced to be in some form of limbo, trapped\"\n\n\"between life and death. Until I heard a voice, almost mine but echod and metallic.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Behind me stood a figure of my height, barely human its entire existance was formed of a pulsating red light. Almost as if my very own aura had given birth to child, it \"\n\n\"was truly an odd sight.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0It would disappear, and I wouldn't think much of it. Instead I quickly left the cavern and returned to the campus I had constructed, those there were shocked. They had saw me trapped within the heart of the node when it exploaded,\"\n\n\"and presumed me dead.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0My only presumption is that the being I saw must've saved me somehow, a construct of the arcane. It would be a number of years before I rediscovered it, within its own terrain known as the Stratum Lands. \"\n\n\"They were truly something else, constructed by the arcane construct to which a place where the voidal and mortal realm were one. The barrier which once kept them seperate was weakened, it was simultantiously the only place the construct was truly\"\n\n\"comfortable. Without these lands it would suffer, be within constant pain. It was a feeding ground almost, and also where I learned the truth about its existance.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0It would inform me it is a revenant, a reflection of a mortal soul but constructed\"\n\n\"entirely from the arcane. During the explosion, the raw strength of the voidal energies that ruptured throughout the chamber shattered my own soul. By the hand of the revenant, it would be saved. But as a consequence, it was created. \"\n\n\"A mirror of myself, it and I became reliant upon one another. Whilst my own death would lead to its demise, my life remained at his arcane whim. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0It wouldn't truly be harmful, it would corrupt land for survival and people would perceive it as a \"\n\n\"threat.. Entering its land and attempting to defeat it, causing him to corrupt even further land under the means of obtaining more power to defend it.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0But.. As Vailor fell, I would seemingly never hear from it. I believe it remained within its land, \"\n\n\"unchallenged by mortal kin and able to continue growing its stratum lands to the point of self-sufficiency. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0However the truth to the situation is that I shall perhaps never know, I've no means to contact it and it doesn't wish to speak\"\n\n\"with me. Only time shall tell if I will face the consequence of its existence, or if I shall merely perish due to natural circumstances.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0From here much fell apart, the city I had once adored fell empty and into ruin. My organisation went their \"\n\n\"seperate ways, even the thanhium mine began to dry up for excessive mining. I withdrew myself for some time, reflecting upon what I had accomplished. I began to regret certain things, see certain parts of my personality as foolish and without\"\n\n\"decent motivation. Within all my years I had seemingly served nobody other than myself, everything I achieved was selfish and usually morally questionable. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Thus, I began to reconsider my position. I donated large parts of my bank to those\"\n\n\"who needed it, I closed down much of the indecent experimentation that needed not to be discovered. But, I also looked upon a strength that had become a plague to my existence. Necromancy.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0One something I strived for, I now found\"\n\n\"myself truly hating it. Everyday would be suffering, finding means to sustain myself, the consistant smell of rot that seemingly overwhelmed my senses. I had enough, yet the near one hundred years put within the art had left me dependant. \"\n\n\"So as Vailor fell and Axios came into the light, I spent the majority of my time seeking a solution. Anything to allow me freedom from this curse, I was even considering accepting an offer of wraithdom.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0For some reason I felt that existing as such\"\n\n\"would be less painful, but eventually came to be senses and pleasantly denied. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0I was seemingly stuck with my curse, but I had to do something. So there I isolated myself for the majority of Axios, for years I suffered beneath the wrath of necromancy.\"\n\n\"It constantly pleaded to be fed, but I denied it. On a few occasions I wasn't strong enough, and gave in, but eventually after much trial and error I found msyelf mostly free from the curse. From that moment I forever stopped practicing, refusing to \"\n\n\"corrupt myself with dark magical arts ever again. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Do I blame people that choose to engage with it? No, not really. I often plead they avoid it, that they walk a different path. However I understand from being in their position, the pull of\"\n\n\"the dark and all its mystical secrets are truly something. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0Seemingly free from the plague I had so long seeked to remove, I left Axios alongside the populus and arrived upon this current world. With old 'friends' within the Library of Dragur\"\n\n\"I found myself a place among their halls, a new purpose and something good to work towards. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0I no longer wished to be one within the shadows, someone who constantly sought means of doing harm or self empowerment. Here I'm provided with a sense of\"\n\n\"pride not grounded within the dark arts, or voidal invention but the aiding of others. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0This shall be the last journal for the time being, perhaps more shall arise within my elderly years worth writing about. In which case, I shall indeed  write about\"\n\n\"them. However for the time being, this would be mostly everything I have done within my life. At least all the important things. §0\\\n§0\\\n§0I hope perhaps this helps someone, one who strays from the proper path. Otherwise, I suppose this is my legacy. \"", ""),
        StaticBook("Leufroy's Tale", "§bSeptimius Bracchus", "An early morning sun smiled upon the two masons on a brisk spring day. Two craftsmen, alike brothers in arms, plied their trade together with great success; the quality of their work unparalleled. Of them, one was named John, who was stronger\n\nyet less skilled, and the other was Lothar, who was a craftsman who produced beautiful designs.Between both, an agreement was reached that was both fair and reasonable; labour, lifting, and all other less precise work would be John’s, whilst the\n\nLothar would sit for hours and work his craft. Each took an equal sum on their commissions, and enjoyed great prosperity for it.Toiling a long time throughout the day, Lothar sat and carved miserably for hours to ensure each tiny detail was to\n\nhis liking, as John merrily completed his heavy labours around midday.“By God, should we be paid by the hour, I would make two-fold what you do!” Exclaimed the bitter Lothar, “You have not earned all of your salaries, you are but a leech!”“Good\n\nLothar, why do you resent me so?” Exclaimed John, unpleasantly surprised! “Our arrangement was to your liking not even a week ago!”“A week ago I needed you, next week I will not; your services are no longer required, how hard is it to move\n\nrocks?”John was shocked and hurt by the betrayal, but his pleading would crash like a cart against the wall that was Lothar’s pride. Cast away, all the work and bounty lay before Lothar, and he excitedly told his wife and family of the wages he\n\nwould now earn. Rejoicing at the promise of more, they celebrated with him late into the night, so late that he awoke with a fog of his mind as he plied his trade along for the first time.Returning to his workshop, he completed a design from the\n\nday prior whence his Lord appeared before him in company.“Good Lothar,” The Lord exclaimed, “I wished to see what you could do, now that I hear that fellow John is to move away. My hope is to see the quality of the work maintained.”Anxiety and\n\nexcitement shot through Lothar, and though dulled, knew he simply had to chip away at a new stone until his Lord, but in trying to lift one to his workshop, he had hurt his back. Trying not to distress in this time of trial, he continued, only\n\nto stumble and fall - the rock falling upon his hands and crushing them.“Good man, are you okay? You seem to have greatly impaired yourself on this visit today! My doctors are competent should you accept some aid.”“No,” He said with pridefully,\n\n“For this was the simply task, you have come to see more.”Having refused his lords help, his work was even slower, and poor at best. It did not take long before he was thanked, and his was left alone to his injuries. Little did he know, these\n\nwere not strains, but crippling handicaps he opted not to treat. For his folly, the ultimate irony - the lord sought new masons seeing the poor work at the insistence of the man.Decades passed as Lothar’s fortunes drained, and his family\n\nabandoned him for opportunities. Alone, wretched, and ever pained and tired, he was accompanied by only his pride… Until the arrival of John’s son one day.“Who might you be?” The old man hissed from his porch to the strong young man.“The son of\n\nJohn. I have come to collect the last wage you owed him.” Anyone who beheld the countenance of the powerful lad would see a thinly concealed wrath.“I have nothing left, with him went my livelihood - he took it wherever he moved to.” Lothar\n\noffered in frustration.“Nothing left? You took both his and your own wages, you ought to now be rich. I ask for only a day’s worth of working wages, nothing more.” The boy’s tone grew ominous, as he ascended the man’s porch without\n\nwelcome.“S-stop!” Lothar ordered, but his word meant nothing and he was powerless - the boy simply lifted the man to menace him. “I have only my heirlooms, take them if you must!” Tossing Lothar aside, he paid little mind to him as he entered\n\nhis home to take his family’s dues - the emptiness of it all surprised him though, as he heard Lothar once had a large family.Returning outside with some jewelry, he found Lothar dead on the floor from the short fall from being pushed aside. It\n\nwas a fitting end to a weak and prideful man.    -His Grace, Duke Leufroy d'Amaury of Lorraine", ""),
        StaticBook("A Vow", "§bWren Vanvir", "\"Evening and dusk§0\\\n§0a mix of ash§0\\\n§0the crossing of lives§0\\\n§0the burnt and the fallen: §0\\\n§0the wails. the screams,§0\\\n§0the dark will never prevail amoung the vanvir line. Hidden blood, nor race can find. I line that cross honor and knowledge, I pledge to Seek knowledge \"\n\n\"for good and peace. The birds of Vanvir fly for peace. Cross oceans to meet and greet. Their wings shead no identity, only with their own. To own a vanvir name is nothing more then a promise. §0\\\n§0Can thy accept that promise?\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Apocrypha I", "§bLady Blightheart", "\"As fate rests on the will of gods,§0\\\n§0\\\n§0So fables are birthed from the will of men.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0How the faded live and alive fade,§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Shall all be but the subjects of my pen.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Apocrypha II", "§bLady Blightheart", "\"Cold hearts, blades of steel,§0\\\n§0\\\n§0A brilliant light, a deafening roar.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The fates of men on a god's wheel,§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Their souls sundered and scored.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Apocrypha III", "§bLady Blightheart", "\"Futures foretold are not man's to change,§0\\\n§0\\\n§0But antiquity's chain shall mortals yet disclaim§0\\\n§0\\\n§0As branch joins hands with decaying crust§0\\\n§0\\\n§0They defy apocalypse, but embrace the dusk.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Apocrypha IV", "§bLady Blightheart", "\"Born of Dusk, the Veil shatters.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0In desperate times, Legends scatter.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0When the final chorus is sung, gaze to the bright star.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0For in the final hour, shall your soul be marred.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwemdar Volumes", "§bAirebys Sylric", "\"The following is an immense copy of several Dwarven literary works by Jorvin 'Kazarinkadan' Starbreaker, citizen of Agnarum.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Transcribed and copied by Airebys Sylric, Scholar to the Grand Library of Dragur. Finalized 11th of The Grand Harvest, 1700\"\n\n\"Prince's Folly§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Fall of Kal'Tarak§0\\\n§0\\\n§0On Doctrine§0\\\n§0\\\n§0((DM Maury#8922 or click the relevant signs))\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Donation Log III", "§bThe Library Of Dragur", "Donation Log III:\n15th of The Amber Cold, 1669 - Recent Book Arrivals﻿\nThe Vermianae - Unknown (Creatures)\nDruid Vision - Unknown (Druidism)\nThe Eldest Brother - Ebs Telrunya (Elven History)\nDeities: Worship -\n\nFriedrick (Greater Beings)\nThe Skygods - Knom The Monk (Greater Beings)\nA Dark Liturgy - Discalus (Guides)\nHistory Of Nine - Unknown (Guilds, Cults &amp; Orders)\nSeasons - Unknown (Human History)\nPampo - The\n\nChronicler (Human History)\nVote Falk - Falk (Human Literature)\nA Soldier's March - Evan Lythian (Human Literature)\nMount Thahn - Unknown (Locations)\nMotley Ravine - Urangoi Ballenz (Locations)\nUndead: An\n\nOverview - Friedrick (Magical Creatures)\nChills - The Chronicler (Monk Literature)\nFeverfew - Nemir (Plants &amp; Farming)\nDeep - The Chronicler (Poetry &amp; Song)\nHempshine - The Chronicler (Poetry &amp; Song)\n\n\nFabled Forge - Unknown (Poetry &amp; Song)\nSluthery Snail - Herbert (Poetry &amp; Song)\nEmerald Collection I - Aemyn Verde (Poetry &amp; Song)\nEmerald Collection II - Aemyn Verde (Poetry &amp; Song)\nCrumbling Tower -\n\nUnknown (Poetry &amp; Song)\nJaya's Poetry - Jaya Jayamen (Poetry &amp; Song)\nVarious Works Volume I - Fenris Cross (Poetry &amp; Song)\nVarious Works Volume II - Fenris Cross (Poetry &amp; Song)\nAir - Azureth (Studies)\n\n\nMountain High - Unknown (The Black Scourge)\nArcane: An Overview - Friedrick (Void Magic)\nMental Magic: Barriers - Friedrick (Void Magic)\nThales Treaty - Unknown (World History)\nQuen - Azureth\n\n(World Literature)\nDawn - The Chronicler (World Literature)", ""),
        StaticBook("Donation Log II", "§bThe Library Of Dragur", "Donation Log II - 11th of The Amber Cold, 1659\nGreatr Celandine - Nemir (Plants and Farming)\nMalin's Welcome - Gregory (World History)\nThe First Seed - Gregory (World History)\nGrand Harvest -\n\nGregory (World History)\nThe Sun's Smile - Gregory (World History)\nThe Amber Cold - Gregory (World History)\nThe Deep Cold - Gregory (World History)\nSnow's Maiden - Gregory (World\n\nHistory)\nKal'Varak Tale - Saeldur Asul'Ailer (Magical Artifacts)\nIn Lieu With You - Luin Eynon (Poetry and Song)\nChurch Hypocrisy - Cuthin Wheaton (Human Literature)\nFlowers - Nerah (Poetry and Song)\nArctic Flower -\n\nNerah (Plants and Farming)\nVarious Works I - Fenris Cross (Poetry and Song)\nDryads - Nerah (Magical Creatures)\nScyd The King - Cuthwin Wheaton (Human Literature)\nNotorious B.I.G - Cuthwin Wheaton (Human\n\nLiterature)\nDraegon Founder - Corann Daevaer (Human Literature)", ""),
        StaticBook("Library Info", "§bThe Library Of Dragur", "The Grand Library\n       Of Dragur\n-------------------\n\nThe Library Of Dragur is a non-profit organisation now three elven years old, making it the longest lasting non-magical guild.\n\nThe library stresses\n\nneutrality in its politics, and hails to no nation or empire, although is frequently sponsored and assisted by various groups.\n\nOur collection is vast, the largest that has and likely will ever exist in all the known world,\n\nand with you, our patrons' support, it will continue to grow.\n\nIn our guild's early years, we were a secret organisation intent on preserving knowledge, Founded by Orithur, Harbinger of Anthos with the assistance of a Dragaar named Aedrex.\n\nToday however, we are open to the public, and we wish to continue our founders' vision of giving free, uncensored access to the largest trove of knowledge that mortal-kind has ever come to acquire.\n\nWhether you come seeking magic, history, poetry\n\nor anything inbetween, we have it. And if we don't, then by the Creator we'll get it.\n\nWe truly believe that this library can bring about a brighter, more intelligent world. So we would humbly ask for your respect when browsing our halls, this\n\nlibrary is a free resource for all and to dirty such an image would be a great mischief indeed.\n\nOn behalf of the Library, the Founders, and the loyal scholars of our halls, we hope you enjoy your stay.", ""),
        StaticBook("Book-copy policy", "§bThe Library Of Dragur", "While books must remain within the library and can't be taken out, the library does offer a book-copy service.\n\nIf you bring the library a new book we don't have, you can exchange it for a copy of one we do have.\n\nAlternatively, we sell copies for 100 mina each. Please note that as some texts are quite old, they are not able to be safely copied [[Some books are a copy of a copy, thus can't be copied again]].\n\nIf you are the original author of a book\n\nwithin the library, then you are able to request a copy of said book(s) for free at any time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Donation Log I", "§bThe Library Of Dragur", "Donation Log I - 8th of Snow's Maiden, 1657\nWyvrun - Hamlin (Dwarvern Literature)\nParagon Or Liar - Dorvaar Godsworn (Dwarvern History)\nNelurir Origins - Nerah (Guilds, Cults &amp; Orders)\nThe Golden Fish -\n\nLurcano Car’dann (Halfling Literature)\nBiddo &amp; The Wizard - Evyn Brittlefoot (Halfling Literature)\nCarrion’s Return - Roy Carrion (Human Literature)\nA Knight’s Story - Dederick Varodyr (Human Literature)\nThe Squire Volume\n\nI - Dederick Varodyr (Human Literature)\nThe Squire Volume II - Dederick Varodyr (Human Literature)\nHedge Knight Volume I - Dederick Varodyr (Human Literature)\nHedge Knight Volume II - Dederick Varodyr (Human Literature)\nHedge Knight Volume III -\n\nDederick Varodyr (Human Literature)\nThe Stran - Diedrick Carrion II (Human Literature)\nHalstaig Hydra I - Adelmar Stonehallow (Human Literature)\nHalstaig Hydra II - Adelmar Stonehallow (Human Literature)\nRegarding Heial - Azoth Hawksong\n\n(Journals &amp; Biographies)\nBael Tunnelsmasher - Bael Tunnelsmasher (Journals &amp; Biographies)\nProphian - Prophian (Journals &amp; Biographies)\nThe Ice Wall - Balt (Locations)\nAn Orc’s Art - Maxistraw Orion\n\n(Orcish Literature)\nA Trio Of Poems - Balt (Poetry &amp; Song)\nApple Poem - Harold Withfoot (Poetry &amp; Song)\nRoyalty &amp; Ruled - Tyus Ropano (Theories)\nThe Mind - Tyus Ropano (Theories)\nHou-zi Conflict - Lothiriel (World\n\nHistory)\nThe Old Tree - Nodian Elric (World Literature)\nOde To Bastien - Gregory (World Literature)", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwed Language I", "§bAgamm \"Ruins-Delver\" Ireheart", "THE LANGUAGE \n           OF THE\n             DWED\n \n\n    By Agamm Ireheart\n\n\n\n      Research from\n Tyrras var Emrys\n\nI myself speak the tongue of the dwed, but, I use Tyrras's way order as a way to format the Lexicon.\nEnjoy the book, and I hope you can use it well.\n\n           RACES\n\nDwarves- Dwed/Dwedmar, Khazad/Khazadmar\nElves-\nElger/Elgus\nOrcs-\nOrk/Orkos\nHumans-\nUmri/Umros\nGoblins-\nGrobbi/Grobbins\n\nForeign/Foreigners-\nYrrok/Yrrommar\n\n             A\nA(singular)- E\nAbove-Morred\nAdjective Suffix(used only for clans and on people, a possessive  suffix or prefix can be used as well.)-Mos/Os/Rum\nAdvisor-Thelur\nAgain/Another-Narhe\nAge-Kez\nAir-Kaas\n\nAlchemy-Gauld\nAlcohol-Graz\nAlcohol = Naztrak\nAle = Beoir\nAll (This tem is tricky. Explained slightly more in the special term division) = Khrum\nAlly / Allies = Karrim / Karrimar\nAlso = Nar’os\nAncestor = Keznol\nAncient = Karik / Hraaken / Den\n\nAnd = Nar / Na\nAnger = Krav\nAnguish = Azmoroth\nAnvil = Kadrin / Kazdorin\nAny = Vos\nAnyway = Vosirk\nArch (Leadership Position) = Ard- / Nak-\nAre = Ath\nArena = Kahros\nArmor = Klad\nArrival = Karnes\n\nAttack = Kahr\nAxe (High uses the same word, but used in different instances, each word differentiates from itself.) = Az / Kathadun\n\n           B\nBack (Refers to the anatomical “Back”, which comprises all muscles located in the fore body, which the person cannot see.) = Fraed\nBad (Synonym to evil) = Vad / Vaador\nBag (Sack, a mobile “Chest” ) = Alaek\nBalance = Unn\n\nBane = Alar / Noril\nBar (Tavern) = Beorim\nBattle = Krazdran\nBe (If used with adjective forms “Been”) = Mer\nBear = Hefjhor\nBeard = Trumm\nBeast (Suffix, must have a substantive before it) = -Dharok\n\nBeast (Suffix, must have a substantive before it) = -Dharok\nBefore (Used to refer to a long past) / (Verb (needs suffix) ) = Den Kezzan / Dekan\nBelow = Yarred\nBetray = Ogdaros\nBetter (Good + Potential) = Thorokian\nBirth = Threin\nBlack = Khorok / Vuur\n\nBlackaxe = Kharadunvuur\nBlaze = Nook\nBlood = Ardol\nBoat (Syn. to Ship) = Wathol\nBoiler (Synonym to furnace) = Nokri\nBook (Usually used to define lore of olden Dwarves. synonym to Scrolls and Tomes) = Kron\nBourbon = Galraz\n\nBow (Action to kneel before a king or superior) = Nelaraz\nBow (Item / Weapon) = Thrimmek\nBravery (Syn. to courage) = Parathak\nBrawl (Usually used to depict a fight out of trivialities, Friendly fight.) = Nazaig\nBreach = Kodeh\nBreak = Nazka\nBring = Nighi\n\nBroad (Synonym to wide, can work as an adjective, if preceded by a possesive.) = Nazad\nBrothel = Belkar\nBrother (Can be used to refer a clan member) = Kronul\nBrow (Eyebrow) = Trullki\nBull = Demm\nBurn = Karaave\n\nBurrow / Hole / Privy = Undor / Undo\nBut = Ur\n\n            C\nCan = Ovar\nCannon = Ithring\nCarcass (Corpse) = Naktrul\nCarve = Thruz\nCave = Umgor / Ulnafer / Skulder\nCave's Folk = Umgorumm\nChair = Nakhimir\nChampion = Baladan / Az'adar\n\nChancellor = Darmag\nCharge = Velannak (Vel'Annak)\nChicken (Animal) = Pul\nCity = Kal’ (Used as a prefix.)\nCivilization (Usually used as a prefix for an empire) = Onor\nClan = Kazamar\nClan suffix (Used when speaking of a person who belongs to a clan) = -rumm\n\nClose = Nerak\nCloud = Norkai\nCluster (Used to determine a group of plants, animals, or Orkos.) = Nozagar\nCollar (Necklace) = Nahibelk\nComfort = Salez\nCommand = Velerak\nCommon = Omur\n\nContinent prefix (Can be used for defining the term “World”, also stands for a massive landscape, or something that has massive ammounts of.) = Khor’\nCore = Derkon\nCouncil = Nozkron\nCow = Keed\nCreate (Syn. to Make) = Yemka\n\nCrown = Rulkahd\nCrystal = Krest\n\n             D\nDaughter = Bedwan\nDay = Lakh\nDeath = Kavir / Kraviil\nDeep = Nerroth\nDefend = Verdig / Kerli\nDiminutive Suffix = -ki /-eki\nDiscomfort (Synonym to anything that may seem hard or uneasy for a Dwarf.) = Krovehni\n\nDo = Kav\nDoom (Synonym to Chaos and Corruption) = Dor\nDoomforge = Dorkadrel\nDoomseeker = Dorgrond\nDoor/Doorway/Gate/Entrance = Edhekal\nDragon = Drakna / Drakmar\nDrink = Drinkir\n\nDwarfling(Child Dwarf)= Dwedki\n\n            E\nEast = Kahae\nEmpire = Oramar\nEnemy = Kaznok\nEnergy = Manok\nEngineer = Klazrel\nExile = Tagar\n\n           F\n\"Fuck\"=Gilthok/Gailuk\nFantasy = Akaneh\nFarewell = Yankar\nFast (Swift, Quick) = Vlokon\nFather = Ka'az \nFeast = Anbekiamar\nFeline = Mew\nField = Aindar\nFind / Found = Nadra / Nadraaz\n\nFire = Karaad\nFish = Wurok\nFishing = Kavir wurok\nFist (Can be used as a syn. to strength) = Rym\nFlee = Vervak (Stems from the word Defend)\nFlesh = Ka- (Used as a prefix) / Kadeek\nFood = Anbek\n\nFor (Reason, if used with a possesive it could be used like “For someone”) = Yoth\nForest = Hefruth\nForest's Folk = Hefrumm\nForge = Kadrel\nForgeling (One who works the forge, used ONLY as a sustantive) = Kadros\nFort = Kaz'ad\nFriend = Nak\n\nFriendship = Nakaran\nFrost = Azwyr\nFrostbeard = Azwyrtrumm\n\n            G\nGlory = Narvak\nGo (synonym to “Come”) = Harath\nGoat = Lann\nGold = Aurok\nGolem = Khoren\nGone (Can be used to define dead, too.) = Haritz\nGood = Thorok\nGrand = Bak / Kathaik\nGrandaxe = Kathaikaz\n\nGrape = Anmar\nGreed = Derkalimin / Dermin\nGreetings = Kazahar\nGross (Displeasing)=Kossog\nGroup = Barel\nGuard = Akvel\nGuide = Akhoral\nGuild = Barimmar\nGut (Sometimes used as a slang term for Courage) = Rul\n\n             H\nHall = Khaz\nHammer = Ord\nHand = Anar\nHave = Zal / Aghar\nHe (Male derogative) = Ka\nHeart = Amoruk\nHello = Oz\nHelp (Aid) = Ghoran\nHer = Laad\nHidden (Used with verb forms Hide) = Rhadav\n\nHigh = Az\nHim = Kaad\nHold = Tal'\nHoly = Kirkja / Yemarin\nHonour (Can be used as Pride) = Anart\nHorn = Ordul\nHow = Ekor\nHowever = Ekorien\nHunt = Grunga / Grung\n\n            I\nI = Tha / K\nIf = Kolun  \nIn (Inside, also synonym for “On”) = Nir\nIndustry = Nolvar\nInert (Death or limit of objects, such as someting running out of fuel.) = Narrek\n-Ing = -Uroz / -Geron\nInto = Nirlak\n\nIreheart = Khronammoruk\nIron = Khro / Khron\nIronborn = Khrothrein\nIrongut = Khrorul\n\n            J\nJournal = Kronotharem\nJourney = Otharem\n\n             K\nKill = Kavok / Kerr\nKing (Literally “High Lord”) = Thrummaz\nKing = Kunnek\n\n            L\nLake = Wunder\nLarge / Huge / Big = Ahran\nLarge (Used in Objects, and length.) = Melkan\nLava (Syn. Magma) = Boor\nLeader = Rikkin\nLeather = Kudelek\nLeft (Direction) = Neeft\nLegend = Kronos\n\nLegion = Arkammar\nLess (Suffix) = -Avos \nLetter (Synonym for Design, and used with potential forms “Word” and then also used with a verb forms “Speech” or “Speak”) = Galat\nLife = Anym / Konym\nLight = Varekan\nLimb = Trullak\nLizard = Knut\n\nLord = Thrumm / Rik\nLose (Synonim to Lost) = Vroth\nLove = Nogazen\n\n            M\nMagic = Lordak\nMaiden (Fe-Dwarf who is un-married) = Lathain / Vilket\nMarch = Veloz / Velak\nMason Station (Mason Table) = Kaladok vo-Nakhum\nMaster = Kronok\n\nMate (To define a person who belongs to the same guild or group of the speaker) = Barithon\nMate (To engage in intercourse) = Nogaak\nMeat (Can be used as a prefix to denote meat of (something))= Ust\n\nMerchantry / Merchant (If used with a person, add an adjective.) = Bergukli\nMetal = Ithor / Akash\nMight = Daar\nMind = Varak\nMine (As in cave.) = Mugdor\nMine (Synonym to My) = Thas\nMoney = Minek\nMother = Beka\nMountain = Agnar\n\nMountain's Folk = Agnarumm\nMouth = Waerod\nMyth = Akkor\n\n            N\nName = Daram\nNether = Kharvul\nNight = Uloon\nNo (Negative. Can  used as a suffix.) = Lare / -are / -vare / -fhare\nNorth = Nikaer\nNothing = Olkodran (Can be used to define Void.)\n\nNumber = Volein (If used with plural forms \"All the Numbers\" or \"Count\" (Not the title.) )\n\n            O\nObsidian = Orvul\nOf (belonging to) = Eron\nOf (Part of, used as a interim suffix to merge two words (King' of 'dwarves) = -'ur'-\nOf (sword OF sth) = -ram / -ethos\nOpen = Aarak\nOr (As in \"Sth OR sth\") = Ov\n\nOrder (Almost never used in common day-to-day, refers to a group of people, like a guild.) = Dverga\n\n             P\nPact = Khroven (Blood Pact is Ardol yol-Khroven)\nPale = Arakrumm\n\nPart (Of. It means that something that is fragment of something, can be used to denote, for example, the stone needed for stonebrick, or, even so, to resume sentences like “Armor Piece”) = -Trihim / -Ohin.\n\nPattern (Refers to all terms of the words, including patterns of behaviour. It can be a synonym to trace.) = Vlazeth\nPelt (Synonym for Fur) = Kudelor\nPickaxe = Azarak\nPig = Kerrem\nPlural suffix= -mar\n\nVolume two will follow up on the rest.", ""),
        StaticBook("Calendera Clover", "§bAverroa", "The Calendera Illisium Clover-An Anesthetic\n-Averroa Dewhurst\n\n  As written in the Study of the Effects of the Calendera Illisium Clover, Calendera demonstrated potential in use as a painkiller-having\n\npotency in grown elves at just 50μL. A fellow scientist, Lucion Sullas, suggested creating an anesthetic from the clover, and for the past year I've been trying various mixtures, combining the clover infusion with everything from spider venom to pumpkin\n\nwine.\n  After undertaking these studies, I've discovered that the painkilling properties of the clover are heightened when combined with the latex of the common poppy. In addition, the combination works as an effective anesthetic, potent\n\nfor an hour on average. However, I have yet to conduct these studies on creatures other than mice or chickens, so the following should only be used in practical applications after further research.\n\n  To prepare the Calendera Illisium Clover infusion: Simmer 10mg of fresh clover in one liter of water for 4 minutes. (The clover can be found among the roots of large trees near the Nawari Gypsy camp as well as in certain Elven forests.)\n\n  The mixture and how to prepare it: Mix 700mg of poppy latex with 20mL of simmering water and simmer for 3 minutes. Turn of the heat and quickly add 10mL of the Calendera infusion while the solution is still hot and stir quickly until well mixed.\n\n  50 microliters (μL) seemed to be the optimum dosage for the mice I tested on. After scraping away some of their skin and applying salt water to increase their pain, this dosage caused them to cease squirming and fall into a sleeplike state.\n\nHowever, about 0.05% of the mice became asphyxiated and nearly died at this dosage, leading me to believe that some creatures are more sensitive to the mixture than others. In addition, as I gradually increased the dosage, the chance of\n\nasphyxiation also gradually increased until an average lethal triple dose of roughly 150μL.\n  When I performed the same procedures on chickens, I found that a higher dose of 1.5mL was required to have the same effect. Similarly, a triple dose of 4.5mL was\n\nthe average lethal dose.\n  From these results, I hypothesize that body mass influences the amount of dosage required for the desired result. As the mice weighed 20g on average and the chickens weighed roughly 3.2kg on average,\n\nthe dosage may be proportional to body weight. As such, it may be practical to weigh patients before giving them their appropriate dose, if possible.\n  Hopefully these results will assist others in further research as well as healers in treating\n\npatients with more severe injuries or scientists hoping to prod into living organisms.\n   -§iAverroa Dewhurst", ""),
        StaticBook("Ame Folktales", "§b[7M Pregnant] Rhea Acius", "Folktales From\n   Better Times\n \n by Artimec Camoryn\n\nIt is said that while malin’s children were still young, and the first war of Iblees fresh in our minds, there existed a town of mali’ame far away from the rest of the descendants. This town knew no outside contact from the rest of the world. It's\n\ninhabitants lived their lives in peace and content, immersed in the nature our kind loves.\n\nThis town forbid the harming of Malin’s blessed forests, and so it’s people were forced to build homes out of stone, making mining a prevalent\n\ntrade in this small community. Among these miners were two young mali, by the names of Faenor and Eleyas.\n\nOne fateful day along the forest path back into town, poor Eleya’s pickaxe got clipped on a branch, and thrown into a lake adjacent to the path!\n\nEleyas did not know how to swim, nor had he any other way to retrieve his tool. That pickaxe was his only form of livelihood, and with no means to create a new one, he knew for sure he was ruined, he fell to his knees in front of the water and wept.\n\nLo and Behold, from the water rose an apparition of the blessed Aspect of Nature, Cerridwen. A shimmering entity of ever changing form, she gazed down on the weeping elf.\n\n\"Why do you cry, my child?\"\n\n“I have lost my livelihood.” Eleyas sobbed. “My only means of living given to me by my father.”\n\n\"Do not despair, my child.\" The aspect soothed in an otherworldly tone. “I will retrieve your tool for you.”\n\nAnd so a lovely golden axe hovered from out of the water into the hands of Eleyas, a brand new intricate tool, carved by a master.\n\n“This...This isn’t mine.” Eleyas gulped, hoping not to offend the Aspect.\n\n“Very well.” The apparition chimed, before sinking back beneath the waves. \n\nThis time, a fine silver axe hovered into the miner’s hands, a very fine piece of work, perhaps not as intricate as the golden one, but indeed a tool that would make him\n\n\"\"\n\nenvy of the village.\n\n“This is not mine either.” The miner said miserably, giving the Aspect a pitiful look.\n\n“Very well, I will look one last time.” Cerridwen said, sinking back beneath the waves.\n\nThis time, a shoddy bronze pickaxe appeared in Eleya’s hands. A worn, torn and old looking tool, not anything anyone would be proud to own.\n\n“This! This is mine!” Eleyas exclaimed joyously, He thanked the aspect wholeheartedly.\n\nImpressed by the miner’s honestly, Cerridwen granted him not only his old axe, but the gold and silver ones too, sending him on his way home.\n\nSoon Eleyas was the talk of the town, for whom owned not only more than one tool, but a gold AND a silver\n\npickaxe? The miner Daenor grew envious of these tales and decided to test the truth of them. \n\nAt the same path and the same lake, Daenor the jealous miner tossed his worn bronze axe haphazardly into the lake without hesitation,\n\nhe then collasped in front of the water, crying fake crocodile tears.\n\nJust as she had done with Eleyas, the aspect of nature rose from the water, in flickering ever changing forms.\n\n“Why do you cry, my child?”\n\n“I..I dropped my pickaxe in the river.”\n\nAnd just as she had done with Eleyas, the kind aspect dived back into the water, and an amazingly intricate golden axe rose from the surface,  floating into the hands of the greedily awaiting Daenor.\n\n“Is this your axe, my child?”\n\n“Yes!” Daenor cried out gleefully. “Yes it is!”\n\nThe entire forest seemed to rumble in anger around the deceitful elf.\n\n“You are a liar. Plagued by greed.” The voice of the aspect boomed. “You shall recieve nothing, not a golden tool, nor the one you had. Let this be a lesson to you.”\n\nAnd so, the golden axe in Daenor’s hands vanished into thin air, leaving him with\n\nnothing, not so much as a wooden shiv. \n\nThere is a lesson to be had here, children of malin. Greed and deceit are traits of a bortu. Beings cursed not only with short stature and flat, ugly faces, but with an inherent desire to trick and bargain\n\ntheir way to riches.\n\nMali do not lust for wealth. Our society is one talonnii, one family. We do not seek to rise above one another, only to support each other.\n\nGreed is not a trait of mali'ame.", ""),
        StaticBook("Urguan - Anthos", "§bBorin Grandaxe", "\"The dwarves settle into the grand city of Kal'Azgoth, hoping for a peace never before seen in dwarven history. With an alliance with Oren, prospects looked higher than ever. Shortly after arriving, the Empress of Oren and Wife of Emperor Godfrey\"\n\n\"Horen is kidnapped by a group of orc raiders. She is taken the to the War Uzg and placed in a sky cell. Upon learning of this, a joint Human - Dwarf raid is launched upon the orc capital and the inner city is breached with ladders. The orcs make\"\n\n\"a final charge but are eventually defeated, while only a small number escape with their lives. The Kingdom of Urguan launches a military strike into the territory of the War Uzg, first by targeting an orc fortress along the crossroads. After a\"\n\n\"large battle, the dwarves push the orcs back into the fort until they are eventually slain and the land is laid claim to by the dwarves. This mere crossroads outpost went on to become the notorious Storms §0Crossing.After§0 a long and bloody war the\"\n\n\"Orcs attempt to have peace negotiations with the Dwarves. Lord Valen Grandaxe and Lord Gorum Frostbeard gave them one option, they were to return the Arken Stone in return the war would end. The Orcs refused and the war raged on. As per\"\n\n\"tradition, The Fourth Grand Tournament of Urguan was held during the war against the War Uzg. Oyvind Frostbeard became the Champion of Urguan, earning him a commanding role in future battles against the §0Orcs.As§0 the war waged on Kal'Azgoth began\"\n\n\"to dwindle. The Merchant guild, led by Dun Irongut, couldn't successfully deliver goods and services to other Kingdoms as a result of the constant raids by the Orcs. As a result of a lack of trade, other guilds throughout the city began to\"\n\n\"suffer. Nalro Greyhammer's Engineering guild couldn't complete projects without import, Darain Grandaxe's mining guild couldn't export ore, and the Remembrancer guild led by Kilgrim Irongut couldn't properly chronicle the affairs of other\"\n\n\"nations due to the blockade set up on Dwarven roads. King Omithiel was growing frail and weak, he was no longer able to attend to the needs of the Kingdom as well as he used to due to his old age. Lord Gorum Frostbeard, Omithiel's closest\"\n\n\"advisor, assumed the responsibilities of the Kingdom after Valen Grandaxe's death. He paid the Legion, the Smithing Guild, the Alchemy Guild, the Mining Guild, and the Tavern workers out of his own pocket thanks to his successful business\"\n\n\"endeavors in other nations. Both Lord Gorum Frostbeard and Legion Commander Thorin Grandaxe kept the Kingdom on its feet after most Dwarves of old either vanished or died in battle. During these trying times King Omithiel Strongbrow passed away\"\n\n\"peacefully in his sleep. The Lords Council was summoned and candidates were determined for an immediate election. Gorum Frostbeard and Kjell Ireheart were slated to be the primary candidates for Kingship. However, Gorum Frostbeard tragically\"\n\n\"fell down the steps of Kal'Azgoth rendering him a cripple and unfit to serve as King. He entered Thorin Grandaxe's name in the election in his place. With little to no opposition, Thorin Grandaxe won the election and became the next Grand King\"\n\n\"of §0Urguan.When§0 Thorin took the throne of Urguan, he was able to select multiple Lords, whose predecessors had either died or stepped down. However, he had inherited a fragmented Kingdom that had endured years of continuous warfare, particularly\"\n\n\"with its old time enemy, the orcish the War Uzg. During his reign, separate Kingdoms were brought beneath the banner of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan, effectively creating an empire. Thus, a new phase in the history of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan\"\n\n\"was declared, leading it to be known by some as the Second Grand Kingdom of Urguan. During this time, the Kingdom's economy prospered, in part due to the new ruler's policy of forcibly taking minas as taxes from the majority of wealthy dwarves\"\n\n\"within the Kingdom. This effectively centralised the Kingdom's economy and led the Grand Kingdom of Urguan towards becoming the richest in Anthos. Additionally, the young ruler forced the holds and Kingdoms that lived beneath him to pay quotas\"\n\n\"to his government, so as to pay off any expenses in return for Legion protection. However, a rebellion soon erupted in Kal'Azgoth, many dwarves claiming Thorin a tyrant. When this rebellion was eventually stamped out, it only served to\"\n\n\"strengthen his rule however. He used the situation to his advantage, routing out his opponents, as well as gaining a better foothold on power within the Kingdom. This allowed him to create an amendment, granting himself near absolute authority\"\n\n\"over the Kingdom. Despite the ascent of a new Emperor, Horen V, he was also able to retain close ties with Oren throughout most of his reign, making many friends and allies among the human nation's §0nobility.However§0, this peace was not to last.\"\n\n\"Many had long held their doubts about the Blood Pact, being viewed by some as a rather murky and unusual alliance, in light of past allegations against the Holy Oren Empire that it had been acting in support of the orcs during the fifty year war\"\n\n\"of Asulon. Though Thorin was viewed by some as a tyrant, he like many of his predecessors had attempted a gentle hand in foreign relations, unwilling to break Yemekar's Balance upon the world. With the Oren Empire's annexation of the elven\"\n\n\"nation of Malinor, pressure was placed upon Thorin to act. With the murder of Lord Nalro Grayhammer by a bannermen of the White Rose, Thorin in anger, looked to his allies from within Oren to seek help in destroying the Empire once and for all.\"\n\n\"It was from there that Lucius Blackmont and Pius Silverblade stepped forward, guaranteeing the support of their Houses in the event of an invasion. Reassured that his plan would work, Thorin held a meeting with his council and the decision was\"\n\n\"taken to declare war on Oren. As the dwarves made their advance north across the Cloud River, the Orenian army, headed by the White Rose met them in battle. To Thorin's surprise however, he was betrayed. From the nearby mountains, a flanking\"\n\n\"charge was led by House Blackmont, House Silverblade and House Carrion, while the White Rose and the rest of Oren made their charge from the front. Met with defeat in battle, the dwarves shamed and forced to retreat, planned for the imminent\"\n\n\"defence of Storm's §0Crossing.When§0 the hour was at its darkest for the sons of Urguan, something quite unusual occurred. Emperor Horen V, alongside the Order of the White Rose, abandoned Oren and traveled far into the north, for reasons that are\"\n\n\"still unknown to this day. With faith in its Empire shattered, human nobility was left in disarray. The Kingdom of Salvus defected to the Grand Kingdom of Urguan and once again, the Legion advanced, this time far into what was once the territory\"\n\n\"of the Holy Oren Empire. From there, Thorin delivered his ultimatum to the newly coronated, Emperor William III. Among his terms, he demanded that the empire be dissolved and Malinor granted its independence. Leading a nation, fractured by\"\n\n\"disunity and disloyalty, William surrendered Oren and accepted the terms of peace. Some did not accept his rule however and from the remnants of the Holy Oren Empire, the independent Kingdoms of Adunia and Savoie were formed, to add to the\"\n\n\"presently existing Kingdoms of Oren and Salvus. Eventually, every one of these Kingdoms pledged its loyalty to Thorin and the Grand Kingdom of Urguan, fearing that one would outdo the other if they did not. Hence the territories of the Grand\"\n\n\"Kingdom expanded, reaching their greatest whilst covering the Karakatuan Empire, the Kingdom of Oren, the Kingdom of Adunia, the Kingdom of Savoie, the Kingdom of Salvus, as well as previously held dwarven territories to the south. Most remained\"\n\n\"beneath dwarven rule until Thorin's death at the hands of the fallen Aengul, Ondnarch, the only exception being Salvus which later betrayed the dwarves and was destroyed by a joint force of dwarves and orcs. As the final order before his death,\"\n\n\"Thorin drew back on his previous policies that neared Imperialism and set the dwarves on a path to becoming far more isolated once §0more.Upon§0 Thorin's death by the fallen Aengul, Ondnarch, Dizzy Irongrinder was elected to power. However, due to a\"\n\n\"massive assault upon Kal'Azgoth by Ondnarch's minions, Dizzy was forced to abandon the city and relocate his kin to the captured fortress of Storm's Crossing which was subsequently developed into a city and renamed, Kal'Ithrun. Dizzy was eager\"\n\n\"to continue from Thorin's legacy and did his best to have the Grand Kingdom reside peacefully among the nations of Anthos. Meanwhile in Oren however, a new dynasty of Kings had taken power. House Carrion had outdone the rest of Oren nobility and\"\n\n\"set itself as the leading House of a new Kingdom of Oren. Initial relations with the Grand Kingdom of Urguan were hostile, as raids were sent between the two nations. Grand King Dizzy eventually opted to declare war, though no advances were made\"\n\n\"and there were ultimately very few hostilities until peace was eventually declared in the Treaty of Krelmstad. The Lord's Council later voted to remove Dizzy Irongrinder from power, resulting in the election of Grand King Indago Stormhammer.\"\n\n\"Though initially promising peace with Oren, Indago later approved of a motion that divided the Lord's Council, in a decision to break the treaty with Oren and invade human lands, assisting a rebellion from House Tarus. This proved to be a fatal\"\n\n\"error and the dwarves were battled back into their own lands. For a time, the war went cold and it appeared that hostilities may have come to an end. Upon the coronation of King Heinrik Carrion however, an advance was made by Oren into dwarven\"\n\n\"territories, immediately seizing the border fortress of Thoringrad. After the fall of Kal'Azgoth to Ondnarch and the threats from the north of both the United Anthos Coalition and the Black Scourge, the situation in Urguan had become very bleak\"\n\n\"indeed.It§0 was amid such turmoil however that the Grand Kingdom of Urguan once more found itself in a position to fight back. Refusing to surrender against the coalition that Oren had created, the dwarves were eventually able to push their foes\"\n\n\"back beyond the Cloud River, until a treaty of mutual peace was signed. However, the war had led to a mounting opposition movement from within the Grand Kingdom, hoping to either reform or completely remove the Articles of Urguan. It had\"\n\n\"steadily become apparent that the dwarven people had become divided by various allegiances, while the sense of unity that had existed for hundreds of years had slowly begun to diminish. Upon Indago's death, Wulfgar Grandaxe was subsequently\"\n\n\"elected to power, upon the back of the promise that he would show a greater restraint in dealing with Oren than his predecessors and that he would attempt to grant the clans a higher say within dwarven government. Shortly after he was coronated,\"\n\n\"he immediately set to work upon reclaiming dwarven lands, leading at the forefront of the assault upon Kal'Azgoth, in a final effort to slay the fallen Aengul, Ondnarch. It was there that a dwarf by the name of Igor Ireheart sacrificed his life\"\n\n\"to release the purified Aengul, Wyrvun, thus being named his hero among the halls of Khaz'A'Dentrumm. However, after years beneath Ondnarch's corruption, the great stone pillars that held up Kal'Azgoth had become unstable, posing potential\"\n\n\"dangers for any who lived beneath them. For that reason, Wulfgar concluded that the dwarves would continue living in Kal'Ithrun for the foreseeable §0future.In§0 attempting to reform the Grand Kingdom's government, Wulfgar signed into passing an\"\n\n\"amendment that established the first Clan Council of Urguan. However, prevented by the Lord's Council from granting it too many powers, it ultimately had fewer powers than originally desired but instead would prove to act as a stepping stone to\"\n\n\"what would eventually become something greater. In dealing with Urguan's foreign affairs, Wulfgar looked towards the dwarves' ancient enemies, the orcs. Beneath the leadership of a new Rex, Urik'Azog, he declared a defensive alliance between the\"", ""),
        StaticBook("The Maker", "§bBorin Grandaxe", "\"Before anything, there was nothing. The only thing that could be described by today’s standards was the Void. The world was a vast emptiness that we can only barely describe. Yet within nothing, there was still him, slumbering away the ages. He\"\n\n\"is not something that any mortal can hope to truly comprehend. His existence is beyond what our minds were created to understand. He is called many different names, and is interpreted in many different aspects of what we understand. Few know who\"\n\n\"he really is, and of these few, only the dwarves know. He is Yemekar, The Creator, The Smith. One day, as The Creator, known to the dwarves as Yemekar, looked out into the void he said to himself “I will create a world, forging it with the four\"\n\n\"aspects along with those who will populate it” So, Yemekar went to his forge and began to build. Using the divine materials of the elements, he went about forging the world and the heavens. As he forged, more and more power flowed into his\"\n\n\"eternal §0smithy.The§0 stars began to shine brighter, the world of Aegis began to bud into life, as animals came forth. When he finally completed all his grand works he looked upon it and felt it to be empty of true life, it rested in the void\"\n\n\"longing of beings of his likeness to work it, to live in it, and to praise him of such works of awe and splendor. To think beyond the instinct of a feral beast. And so, his mighty forge ringing with new found zeal, he began to craft again,\"\n\n\"making those beings that would shape the world. The forging took many millennia, the power of his forge being so strong that the very things used within it became. From his anvil flew sparks, sparks that grew into flames where they struck and\"\n\n\"from these sparks to living creatures, creatures made of the power of the forge’s flame. Lesser gods in themselves, these were known as Daemons. As he cooled his creations in the water, a great steam arose. The power of the forge was in the\"\n\n\"steam as well and it condensed, growing to pools that turned to yet more lesser gods. These gods were the Aenguls. These Daemons and Aenguls became the rest of the Brathmordakin, the gods of all §0creation.But§0, Yemekar’s forging was incomplete. He\"\n\n\"had not yet made creatures to inhabit the world. So, he continued to forge, the Brathmordakin at his side. The first creature he made was too rough, too harsh, unbreakable but unlike to Yemekar. This was the first of the orkos. Without\"\n\n\"destroying his creation, he placed the ork, Krug, into the harsh deserts of Aegis, where it was too rough and uninhabitable for other beings to live. Yemekar, seeing his first creation to be too rough went to craft a fairer being. However, he\"\n\n\"overcompensated for his previous mistake and the next that was born was the first of the elgus, Malin, soft and fair yet never dulling in shine, lasting ages. They, unlike the orkos were not violent, yet overly passive, and unwilling to act in\"\n\n\"the name of their creator. Their lives would last so long that they would surely grow tired of the world he had created for them. So he chose that the best place for them would be amongst the great forests of Aegis, where they would soon become\"\n\n\"entrapped and imprisoned by the dense foliage as it grew around them. So, continuing on with his pursuit to create a creature like himself to roam the world, he returned to his anvil once more and crafted a new being. Worried of creating a\"\n\n\"creature too strong or too long lasting he made one weaker, but bearing less of an effeminate appearance. As a solution to the deformity of the elgus, he had them grow great beards and fancy moustaches, as a display of their masculinity. These\"\n\n\"beings, he named the umros, the first of them being Horen. However, they were far too brittle for his liking, simple and uninteresting beings. Furthermore, they were prone to shave and remove the beards he had gifted them with. So he cast them\"\n\n\"upon plains and grassland, where their lives were so short that they would surely all die out in time. Finally, the creator forged from the earth, a being, strong, wise and hearty, capable of a life long enough to experience the full greatness\"\n\n\"of the world he had created. Though tough and built for battle, they were not so mindless as the orkos. Bearing beards and facial hair, even greater and stronger than that of the umros, they were truly crafted in his image. He named these the\"\n\n\"dwedmar, the favoured of all the races he had created, the first of their kind named Urguan. He found for them, the finest and most visually pleasing of the lands he had built. Here, amongst great mountains and valleys, he allowed the dwedmar to\"\n\n\"build a §0home.The§0 forging of the perfect race had not come without cost however. Through time, his creations would surely war and fight amongst one another. So Yemekar, in his divine righteousness, bestowed upon the dwedmar a purpose to which\"\n\n\"they and their ancestors were to serve. Though the orkos, umros and elgus were not the beings he had intended to create, he looked upon them mercifully. For if any one of his creations were to outdo the other, the delicate balance of the world\"\n\n\"he had created would over time, collapse into ruin. The prosperity of one of his creations would surely lead towards the suffering of another. So he spoke to Urguan and asked that if any of his creations were to prove a threat to another, the\"\n\n\"dwedmar would intervene. For all eternity, they would act as the guardians of the balance that had existed from the start of time. So Urguan agreed to Yemekar’s wish and for years the four races continued to grow, forging mighty kingdoms upon\"\n\n\"the face of Aegis. For a time, the kingdoms were at peace, prosperous and bountiful. But, this peace was not to §0last.There§0 was one amongst the Brathmordakin, a Daemon of ambition, one whose light had grown dark before he grew to life grew yet\"\n\n\"darker. Corrupt and evil, the Daemon Khorvad sought to take greater power for himself. Looking upon the creation of Yemekar, he saw the four races and thought to himself to take them for himself, thus becoming their God. Descending upon the\"\n\n\"world, he began to speak whispers into the ears of Krug, Malin, Horen, and Urguan. To Krug, he whispered words of war and bloodshed. Krug accepted this readily, ever hungry for such things. To Malin, thoughts of the forest filled with his\"\n\n\"children, a secret wish of the elven father. Horen, growing old, was promised long life to see his creations completed. All three fell to these temptations. Only Urguan, filled with honor and in likeness to his father, Yemekar, ignored the\"\n\n\"whispers of Khorvad. Angered by the stubbornness of Urguan, Khorvad flew over the skies of Aegis, showing his true form, a being of smoke, fire, and shadow. The other brothers, seeing his form, rallied with Urguan to fight this §0horror.The§0 war\"\n\n\"waged for years, Khorvad using his power to raise the dead to his cause until finally, the brothers met with him in combat. Krug rashly charged in towards him but, due to being the brother most corrupted by Khorvad, he was changed, his skin\"\n\n\"growing a sickly green, tusks protruding from his mouth. But even this could not stop Krug’s bloodlust. Khorvad had made his hunger for battle too great and he would not stop now. The other brothers joined in, Urguan’s hammer blazing a trail of\"\n\n\"light, Horen’s sword swinging strong in hand, and the arrows of Malin streaking through the night. The battle was fierce, and in the end, the brother’s and their armies succeeded, driving Khorvad to the void. In his last shout, the evil Daemon\"\n\n\"lay a curse upon each of the brothers. Krug’s curse, beyond what he had, was to be forever at war with his brothers, especially Urguan who had been the strongest against Khorvad. Malin was cursed to have a womb closed, his children few. Horen,\"\n\n\"cursed with short life, grew frail and bent on the spot. To Urguan finally, Khorvad cursed with short stature. Yet as Khorvad was finally sealed, the Aengul Anbella, wife of Yemekar, came to the brothers, giving blessings to them all. To Krug\"\n\n\"she granted strength. To Malin, peace in the forests. To Horen, the promise of one day exploring the Seven Skies. Finally to Urguan was granted hardiness and strong mind and the heart to fight evil.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Kal'Bogrin Vol I", "§bBorin Grandaxe", "\"After the reign of Fimlin Grandaxe the Grandaxe Clan had faced prejudice from the government, starting with a conflict with Grand King Vorstag Ireheart about the joint Grandaxe-Irongrinder naval hold Ote'Kathaz. Vorstags reign did not last long\"\n\n\"and Zahrer Irongrinder was elected after, and gave the Grandaxes the newly conquered land from the Undead known as Ash Castle, once known as Hanseti. In its place the Grandaxes built a hold named Kal'Bogrin after their founder, constructing a\"\n\n\"small village along a keep built into the mountain. North of Kal'Bogrin a fort was constructed and named Kaz'ad RumThe initial conflict between the Grandaxes and the council was started when Grand King Zahrer tried to re-institute the Lord's\"\n\n\"Council he was once part of, the amendment was blocked by the Grandaxes and the Frostbeards but the other three thanes, Uldar Irongut, Lori Ireheart, and Lathros Irongrinder removed the Frostbeards from Thaneship and replaced them with the\"\n\n\"Doomforged who passed the §0amendment.This§0 sparked outrage amongst the Grandaxes, and thus the Lords were appointed from those that approved the passing and none to the Grandaxes or §0others.The§0 situation only worsened from there, the tension rose\"\n\n\"until Jörik Grandaxe was accused of slaying an elf. Grand King Zahrer and the new Lords Council met to determine his banishment, but the Lords Council wanted to banish the entire Grandaxe clan because of their opposition. Grand King Zahrer\"\n\n\"vetoed the decision but was removed from King and the Grandaxes left for the safety of Kal'Bogrin with all their belongings. The Grandaxes thus seceded from The Grand Kingdom of Urguan and became indeed entry lead by the Grandaxe leaders Fili\"\n\n\"Grandaxe, Fimlin Grandaxe, and Jörik §0Grandaxe.Seeing§0 the opportune moment to attack the dwarves the newly reformed Kingdom of Oren marched for the Irongut hold of Hiebenhall. Knowing the importance of maintaining the Grand Kingdom the Grandaxes\"\n\n\"prepared for war to protect it despite not receiving the same from the Lords §0Council.However§0 it came to be that all the dwarves who were against the Lords Council moved in with the Grandaxes and eventually collapsed the Grand Kingdom and allowed\"\n\n\"for the Grandaxes to liberate it. As a result the only candidate for Grand King left was Hodir Doomforged and he was elected Grand King and made a new government where a loose senate was the only opposition to the King and thus removing the\"\n\n\"corruption of the Lords and Thanes Council once and for all.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Cool Air Sinks", "§bThurdan Orathon", "Cool Air Sinks\n\nOne can assume that the opposite effect of hot air rising is that cool air sinks.\n\nOriginal text by Thurdan Orathon", ""),
        StaticBook("Hot Air Rises", "§bThurdan Orathon", "Hot Air Rises\n\nHow can this be proven scientifically? For example, when water is boiled to a high level of heat, it will change to its gaseous form. Once steam appears, it will begin to ascend. It will continue to ascend until the heat\n\nof the steam starts to diminish. At this moment, the steam will change back to its former state, and form water droplets.\n\nDue to these results, one can confirm that hot air rises.\n\nOriginal text by Thurdan Orathon\n\n*a pile of paper has been neatly stacked*", ""),
        StaticBook("Urguan - Athera", "§bBorin Grandaxe", "\"Shortly after arriving on the new continent of Athera and constructing the city of Kal'Agnar however, Midgor was removed from power by the newly formed, Thane's Council. This caused disagreement throughout Urguan, many feeling that the Grand\"\n\n\"King was only removed due to his attempts to stem power away from the ruling council. In Midgor's place, Fimlin Grandaxe, a former Thane and Lord himself, as well as a cousin of former Grand King, Wulfgar Grandaxe, was elected to power and\"\n\n\"assumed his title of Grand King upon the promise that he would once more restore stability and unity among the nation of §0dwarves.The§0 Town of Greyhaven is made a town officially under the Grand Kingdom of Urguan. The elven honorable dwarf,\"\n\n\"Kirrekith Grandaxe, is placed as the §0Jarl.The§0 Grand Kingdom of Urguan assists the Azog Clan to overthrow the current Rex, due to them being deemed incompetent of leading the Rexdom of Krugmar. Meanwhile notable clans grow back in power such as\"\n\n\"the Strongbrows and Doomforged. With the returning of multiple dwarven clans, the Grand Kingdom leads an expedition into the most ancient city of the dwarves - dating back to Urguan's days. Although the exploration took many casualties, the\"\n\n\"dwarves found a way to open the door into the room which kept Iblees trapped. Despite figuring this out quickly and closing the door, they were too late for someone nudges a lever that broke the seal, allowing Iblees to roam the lands again.\"\n\n\"Because of this, the capital of Kal'Agnar is attacked by an assault of undead minions. Though the dwarves successfully route the undead force, a drake bursts out from the portal with an aged dwarf in blue armor on its back. It is discovered the\"\n\n\"Paragon Urir Ireheart, who many thought died in the nether, had survives and escaped via the portal in which the attacking undead §0used.The§0 Grand King Fimlin gives out orders to banish all High Elves from the Grand Kingdom, and kill those who\"\n\n\"know the art of golemancy in order to solve the dwarven grudges concerning their knowing of golemancy. The Kingdom later joins in on the assult of Annil'Sul, the capital city of the High Elves. With the wood elves, orcs, and Aesterwaldians, they\"\n\n\"capture the §0city.Focusing§0 their attention on the undead, the Grand Kingdom attends a meeting of all nation leaders to discuss fighting Iblees. Later the Grand Kingdom marches alongside the armies of Krugmar and Oren to destroy an\"\n\n\"Undead-controlled tower in the southwest \\\"shard\\\". The mission is a success. After a raid on Kal'Agnar by the \\\"Under-Kingdom\\\", a rebelling force of Starbreakers, it's found that they had allied with the Ironborn and Undead, and planned to siege\"\n\n\"Kal'Agnar. Knowing this, Grand King Fimlin united leaders of major nations and guilds with the Treaty of the Sun's Smile in order to secure a win in the coming siege. Although, in the Ironborn Invasion the Ironborn Clan with the Iblees cultists\"\n\n\"defeat the combined forces of Athera, and bring the fall of Kal'Agnar. Many dwarves flee to Hiebenhall. Quickly, the Grand Kingdom unites the nations once again with the common goal of recapturing their city from the Undead. The desolated city\"\n\n\"of Kal'Agnar is demolished and purified by the Druidic Order. The city is renamed Kal'Karaad and construction begins. Grand King Fimlin Grandaxe is later removed from kingship after a vote is called by former Grand King Vorstag §0Ireheart.Vorstag\"\n\n\"Ireheart wins the next election. dwarves debate whether to go to war against the Kingdom of Renatus or the Kingdom of Akovia. Grand King Vorstag is later slain in single combat by an undead by the name of \\\"Dungrimm's Bane\\\", who reclaim Urguan's\"\n\n\"armor in the fight. Zahrer Irongrinder wins the later §0election.After§0 retaking the Undead-ridden lands of Hanseti, the land is given to the Grandaxes where they found the hold of Kal'BogrinGrand King Zahrer Irongrinder declares war on the Kingdom\"\n\n\"of Akovia. One of the dwarves' most valuable allies, Aesterwald, collapses. The Duchy of Nerezza vassalizes under the Grand Kingdom of Urguan. Due to the attempted banishment of the Grandaxe Clan over the killing of an elf, Zahrer Irongrinder\"\n\n\"was forced to resign from kingship. Despite this, the Grandaxes start the Grand Exodus of the Grand §0Kingdom.Hodir§0 Doomforged becomes Grand King of Urguan in a landslide victory. The Reformed Kingdom of Oren declares war on the Grand Kingdom of\"\n\n\"Urguan, aiming to throwing them out of The North. In his first military battle, the Battle of Hiebenhall, Hodir Doomforged wins against Oren. This brings back dwarven nationalism. Despite this, the Grand Kingdom is still at a disadvantage\"\n\n\"against Oren. The Orcish Rex breaks an alliance with the dwarves, though pro-dwarven dwarves continue fighting with the Legion. The Jarldom of Polaris is established under the Grand Kingdom to act as a warfront against the nearby castle\"\n\n\"Drakenburgh and the City of Ayr. Ioannis Kommunis is declared the Jarl of Polaris. The Dwarven Legion marches to attack the Orenian holdings south of Polaris but are defeated in the Battle of Drakensburgh. The Orenian Navy quickly attack the\"\n\n\"Dwarven Navy, sinking the ships and drowning Grand King Hodir §0Doomforged.Balek§0 Irongut is nominated Grand King of the dwarves. The dwarven legion is later defeated at the Battle of Nerezza against the Reformed Kingdom of Urguan. Looking to\"\n\n\"peace, Balek Irongut has the Grandaxe Clan settle in the Kazradin Foothills in exchange for the right to negotiate terms with Kal'Bogrin as a factor. Peace is denied by Oren, and Hiebenhall is conquered overnight by Orenian armies. Despite\"\n\n\"marching upon the capital of Kal'Karaad, Oren backs out for unknown reasons. Peace is finally made, relinquishing all dwarven claims on the northern holdings and preventing any offensive wars started by the dwarves, as well as war reperations\"\n\n\"payed to the Kingdom of Oren. Meanwhile, Vrograk'Gorkil claims the title of Rex for himself once again, causing the dwarves and orcs to enter a collision §0course.The§0 newly forged Iron Uzg begins to invade the Grand Kingdom of Urguan. The Grand\"\n\n\"Kingdom loses in a skirmish outside the orcish swamps, allowing the Iron Uzg to slowly advance to Kal'Eknar, the newly made Grandaxe Village. The Iron Uzg sets up camp and begins to siege Kal'Eknar, but are defeated by a flank led by Agor\"\n\n\"Grandaxe and Vladovs - allowing the main force to charge. Grand King Balek and Rex Vrograk'Gorkil meet in Kal'Karaad and create the Horde of Iron and Fire, a Dwarf-Orc alliance. Athera is then attacked by large worms, forcing them to leave\"\n\n\"Athera with the rest of the mortal races.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("LWJ: Afterword", "§bLouis", "\"Afterword:§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I guess I should apologize for not correctly annotating the beginning of Volume 4, but I don’t care at this point. In the end, these are just scraps of papers that will be dealt to the wind to handle, as has been demonstrated in the\"\n\n\"lack of care for the arts I’ve seen in my time here. I guess some who have the assumption that I was somewhat significant in at least one person’s life. At a point, I was, but people just decided they didn’t want to deal with me when I became bitter about\"\n\n\"my condition. I hardly blame them; if they chose to be friends in shine and distant in rain, so be it, for at least I could rely on those who truly cared about me.§0\\\n§0Except... there was nobody. Despite my best efforts, I was never able to create a lasting, \"\n\n\"interpersonal connection with anyone here. I was just your average joe-shmo drifter looking for work after all, of course I didn’t deserve the right to feelings. Everyone who I truly felt anything for is dead, physically or in their mental state. \"\n\n\"There is nobody left but myself.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I tried my best to uphold principles of loyalty, service, and friendship, and I believe I did. There are multiple events I didn’t record of my journals. Most of them consisted of other events in which I\"\n\n\"talked to strangers, sharing food and assisting each other on the roads. After a while, though, people just stopped accepting my gratuity, not even bothering to talk to me. It's been a slow decline in sociality for me over the past few weeks, and it shows\"\n\n\"in my essential isolation from society. Whenever I’ve awoken from my inconsistent sleep schedule, I’ve found arbor overrun with frost and completely abandoned. Damn that, for I apparently slept through Arbor's fall. I don't know what happened, but \"\n\n\"nobody's here and all of these buildings lay unattended. I guess I expected to make some sort of friend here meeting new people, but everyone else had their own lives to attend to. Still, I gave my all to do everything I could for anyone else, but I'd \"\n\n\"never really be thanked for anything. I just did it. If I didn’t, I was told how much of an idiot I was. There was nobody to work for but myself, and I messed that up too.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Multiple times I tried to involve myself in various causes, from warding off evil \"\n\n\"to rebuilding after tragedies. Every time, I was left shortly afterwards. I’ve never been the most skilled fighter or the best carpenter. I guess it’s what they say about the Jack of all trades being the master of none. I was just riding on the hope that \"\n\n\"it might be better than just being the master of one, but I’ve gotten nothing from my mediocrity. My only real goal was to find a home, and this whole time I’ve been split on trying both to settle down here and to return home. There is no home to return \"\n\n\"to here, though. Arbor's dead. Aragon's dead.§0\\\n§0Thinking about it, I've been dead this whole time. I've just been having a bad dream that I haven’t woken up from. There is no purpose for me here, and I’ve yet to find one again.\"\n\n\"This was supposed to explain why I’ve decided to kill myself, but I think it’s just made matters more confusing. I’ll leave it to whoever lives on past me to explain why I couldn’t take it anymore. The journals should be enough evidence; I don't care to\"\n\n\"explain myself any further. I don’t care that this piece isn’t as deep as I wished it to be. I just don’t care.§0\\\n§0I’m taking back the one thing I was granted in this world; choice. So before I take my own life, I'm going to go tie up some loose ends I've\"\n\n\"been neglecting.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0But before I go, I guess I should introduce the reader to my parting gift from this world. My corpse shall serve as the breeding ground of a horrid, putrid parasite, destined to live in its own favor, make connections with only those it \"\n\n\"could profit from, and to serve one man and one man only; himself. I send my best beyond and leave my worst to serve as a cruel parody of this world. I’m uncertain of when it should root itself in this land.... Maybe it's been in all of you all along.\"\n\n\"Until then, be sure to always treat others with kindness, dignity, and respect. Maybe then, you won’t have to worry about me, becoming part of the pollution of this land. I can’t wait for the September Prince to bring an end to this self-serving race.\"\n\n\"don’t know who will bear witness to my self-inflicted demise, but I hope to have at least someone that will alert others to my death. Still, who knows. Surely not I.§0\\\n§0Onwards to freedom. Stay strong, unlike the shriveled mess I’ve become.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I miss you Fae.\"\n\n\"Signing off for the final time,§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Louis.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I'm coming home, ma.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0See you on the other side, guys.\"", "")
    )

    private fun _ATLAS_11(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Bloody Diary", "§bTargoth Glottgut'Raguk", "\"Tidwald's diary.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Started on;§0\\\n§011th of Snow's Maiden 1655.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0\\\n§0ARTWINKLE PUDD IS NOT TO PEEP INSIDE THIS BOOK!!!!!! NO NO NO\"\n\n\"11th of Snow's Maiden 1655.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Hello Haense, it's Tidwald. It's chilly enough again this year, but that's to be expected. I found a load of damp books in a soaked crate by the lake, handy. Artwinkle still hasn't had any luck with finding magic. I feel sorry\"\n\n\"for the clumsy mess. THE CLUMSY MESS.§0\\\n§0               _____§0\\\n§0\\\n§012th Snow's Maiden 1655§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Was up at the home of the Warhawks earlier, out near that Ascended HQ and shor what only did I see, A BATTLE! Some lich, Orsul, and 2 bands\"\n\n\"of folk. Very exciting, saw some new magnetic earth magic as well, very interesting stuff. Flaming swords, crazy disintigrating magic, springy elves pulling tunics over peoples heads. I'd never be able for such galavanting. §0\\\n\"\n\n\"8th of First Seed 1655§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I CAN NOT BELIEVE THIS. MY SWEET BELLE LEFT ME FOR THAT HUNKY SMITH. I CAN NOT COMPETE WITH THE YOUNG AND HEALTHY IN MY OLD AND SHAKEY STATE. I MUST FIND THE FOUNTAIN OF YOUTH.\"\n\n\"Artwinkle's Magic Log§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I've had several lessons, now, all spanning months and months, and years. Lythian has cut me loose as a student, now, after an incident in Holm wherein an explosion caused perhaps by me unsettled the peace.\"\n\n\"But this wasn't the reason - He merely wasn't able to take me further as a student. As discussed at the start, now that I'm a Tier-Four Fire Evocationist, he's taught me all he can. Very happy with where I am today. Bet I could show them High Elves now!\"\n\n\"Would serve 'em right fer doubting me!§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Now. The hunt for an Arcanist lives on...§0\\\n§0---§0\\\n§0Sixteen Eighty Nine.§0\\\n§0-§0\\\n§0This blasted blizzard. The house is freezin'. I do my best to keep the place heated at all times, with my Heat Evocation, \"\n\n\"but I am unable to cover all hours of the day, and I can only keep it so when I'm here. I worry for Tid. He spends most of his days in bed, now. He's gettin' old, for certain. He's always been old! But I fear that age is finally draggin' him down, now.\"\n\n\"I will look after him as I can. He's even stopped using this journal! He loved this journal!§0\\\n§0\\\n§0I head to Aberrang now to seek out that Alchemist, whom I bought a potion of wizard's wisdom from at that fayre in Markev. Perhaps he can help.\"\n\n\"Began to use my middle name as my proper surname. 'Pudd', kept tricking folk to believing I'm a Halfling, til they met me in person. Only an issue on official forms and letters, but I suppose then that those are the most important times of all.\"\n\n\"[!] The page would be smeared with blood, and clearly messy writing would make up the pages[!]§0\\\n§0\\\n§0-=FOR KRUGMAR=-\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Wuds Life", "§bElder Bogrum'Lak", "\"Fae Ring\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Lost Legends v.2", "§bGork'Raguk", "The Legacy\n          of\n     Pow'r Garmar\n    ▬▬ι═══════ﺤ\n    by: Gork'Raguk\n\n*the print looks very old, yet still somehow newer than the copy of the series*\n*not knowing what to expect, you take a deep breath, and turn the page tentatively*\n\n   Chapter Two:\n     The Dark\n   Brotherhood\n -------------\n*the narrator's introduction seems to be too faded for reading*\nƸ̵̡Ӝ̵̨̄ƷƸ̵̡Ӝ̵̨̄ƷƸ̵̡Ӝ̵̨̄ƷƸ̵̡Ӝ̵̨̄ƷƸ̵̡Ӝ̵̨̄ƷƸ̵̡Ӝ̵̨̄ƷƸ̵̡Ӝ̵̨̄ƷƸ̵̡Ӝ̵̨̄ƷƸ̵̡Ӝ̵̨̄ƷƸ̵̡Ӝ̵̨̄ƷƸ̵̡Ӝ̵̨̄ƷƸ̵̡Ӝ̵̨̄ƷƸ̵̡Ӝ̵̨̄ƷƸ̵̡Ӝ̵̨̄ƷƸ̵̡Ӝ\n\n   After banning the plebs, Pow'r Garmar got really bored. He was forced to do what any rational Orc being would do in his situation:\n\n... Join a cult, of course!\n\n   Firstly, though, he had to decide on one. Pow'r Garmar had been barred from joining all suicide cults as of recent, because he had survived the last 14 suicides (suicide could never hope to beat Pow'r Garmar).\n\n   Suicide had originally called death on Pow'r Garmar, but Pow'r reported Suicide for not having a bio and the death was nullified. Even excluding suicide cults, however, there were still a suprisingly large number of options:\n\n1.) On the top of his list, there was the Seven Sins Cult. Pow'r declined their invite though, because they turned out to be a weeb club -- and Pow'r can't stand nerds! Pow'r is an alpha male jock, a real manly man... er... Orc?\nHe's a MAN FOR NOW, okay?\n\n2.) There was the Elder Vampire Cult, but... Pow'r didn't want to contract HIV while feeding like the last initiates. Because, as you know, that wouldn't be the first time Pow'r Garmar dealt with Aides.\n\n3.) There was the Mile High Club, which turned out to be nothing like he thought it was (Pow'r can stretch to a length of one mile while on his tippy toes). Needless to say, it wasn't a viable option once he realized what it was.\n\n4.) His last choice was the Dark Brotherhood, which he remembered from playing Skyrim on insane difficulty (on the ultra rare, super special retarded edition). He now just had to go about finding the group and joining.\n\n   According to ancient folk lore, the only way to join the Dark Brotherhood is to kill Grelod the Kind; however, he never knew what 'kind' of Grelod to kill. He thought of calling his younger brother, Meh'tah Garmar, to find out...\n\nbut they'd recently had a falling out when Mehtah got too clingy (he kept using social spy to watch Pow'r RPeeing). Metah, however, vehemently denies this, and they haven't talked since.\n\n   Luckily, Pow'r Garmar suddenly remembered his miraculous deathk-\n\nnight ability to smell and track all things living or dead.\n\n   He took a deep whiff of the air. *FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH*\n\n\"I can smell the flavor,\" he said.\n\n*FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH*\n\n\"I can SMEEELL the grandma oils!\"\n\n*FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH**FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFUUUHH*\n\n   Meanwhile, Pow'r Garmar wasn't the only one on a trail. The developers got super jealous of Pow'r's sheer realism and ability and decided to commission an investigation.\n\n   The loremasters became busy pouring through every article, every mention,\n\nevery lore scrap, trying to find Pow'r's completely immersive smelling ability.\n\n   Pow'r Garmar followed his trail until he finally made it to Grandmaville, where they make the grandmas. From there, he decided that the best course of action would be to\n\nmurder all old ladies named Grelod in the tristate area. IT WORKED TO SUCCESS! In celebration, Pow'r Garmar wringed all hte empty lifeless Grelod corpses of grandma oil and then headed to the Sleeping Giant Inn. He rented a room for the night and slept.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bouquet", "§bNoelle Holt", "Bouquet\n\nThis fist full of delight\nCan make the meanest persons day\nThe colors are more vibrant than a rainbow\nThey're one of the best gifts to give away\n\nThe soft pedals,\nThe sweet smell of many kinds of flowers\n\nAnd to make them this way\nYou'll need to wait for rain showers\n\nYou can make them for anyone\nParents, teachers, even a friend\nBut sadly its vibrant colors have an end\n\nBut in a few days you look at where you found the flowers\nYou look at the field of flowers with doubt\nBut your frown doesn't last long\nWhen you see even more flowers sprout\n\n-Noelle Holt", ""),
        StaticBook("Melunis the Mad", "§bJaya Jayamen", "Melunis the Mad\n\n           ~Originally by\n       Sofetios Jayamen\n\n       ~Transcribed by\n           Jaya Jayamen\n\nI was travelling to a place called Geedin in search of a philosopher called Melunis. This man was said to be the wisest in the land, according to my friend who went there a while back. So I figured I would see what wisdom he could offer me.\n\nI arrived in the town and walked up to a guard. I said,\n\n“Excuse me sir, could you direct me to the man named Melunis?” The guard just laughed and said,\n\n“The only Melunis I know is a madman, you can find him over by the alley.” I thought to myself, this madman couldn’t be the one that my friend was talking about. My friend was a very smart person and wouldn’t confuse a wise man with a madman.\n\nSo to satisfy my knowing of whether or not this was the correct man, I went to the alleyway and saw an old man in rags. I said to the man.\n\n“Are you the man known as Melunis?” to which he looked at me, smiled, and said,\n\n“Indeed so! How can I help you this fine day!” The day was overcast, and cold. I couldn’t see how it was fine.\n\n“Would you happen to know my friend, James Linson?”  The man looked overjoyed at the name and said,\n\n“Why yes! I remember the lad. I do hope he is doing well.”\n\n“Well he told me you were the wisest in the land…” I said, to which Melunis replied with a frown,\n\n“Wise? No I’m not wise. I am just a ragged old man in an alleyway. Do I look like I’m Wise?”\n\n“No you don’t.” I said. “You don’t look wise at all.” The man then got a sparkle in his eyes.\n\n”Not wise at all?” said the man. “Well I must agree. You being very well off must know what it means to be wise, as you are in a far better place then I.” The man thought for a second, then said, “Tell me, what does it mean to be wise.”\n\n“Well it means that you know a lot about things.” I said, “Like a smith knows how to smith well, he is wise in smithing.”\n\n“Ah..” said the man. “ So in a sense, being wise is having knowledge.”\n\n“Yes.” I said.\n\n“ Alright, well what is knowledge.” Said Melunis. “As in how would I be able to obtain it to become more wise.” I thought for a second, then said,\n\n“Knowledge is knowing something, and obtained by learning.”\n\n“I see!” Said the man. “But… how do I know I know something.” At this I was a bit perplexed. I said,\n\n“Could you explain what you mean?” The man nodded and said,\n\n“In other words, How do you know what you know is true.”\n\n“Because you know it works when applied to things.” I said.\n\n“Alright.” Said the man. “So knowledge is what you know works when applied to things, but how does that make it true?”\n\n“What do you mean?” I said.\n\n“I mean for example, we could see an abstract painting.” Said Melunis. “You could think it’s one thing, I could think its another. Both works when applied, at least to the individual, but who is right?”\n\n“I guess we would both be right.” I said. “It would be up to the individual.”\n\n“Ah I see now!” Said the man. “So knowledge is what works with the individual. But still, how do we know it is true? Because isn’t the truth universal?”\n\n I began to get frustrated. But… Then I came to a realization.\n\n“I guess the truth is up to the person.” The man looked at me and said,\n\n“So there is no real truth? But what about common knowledge?” I thought for a second and said,\n\n“The common knowledge is what people have a common belief in.” Melunis nodded, seeming to understand.\n\n“But then what is the real truth?” The man said.\n\n“The real truth…” I began, “The real truth is… unknowable. Even if we got to it, people still would have different opinions. And those opinions might have more people believing in it than the real truth.”\n\nMelunis smiled at me and said,\n\n“Thank you, I think I understand now what it means to have knowledge.”\n\nSoon after this conversation, I left. Slightly confused, but more understanding.\n\n Though now I realized what my friend meant by him being the wisest in the land.\n\nThe End\n\nThank you for reading the Jayamen family’s books! If you have any feedback or enjoyed reading, please let me, Jaya Jayamen (( Sofetios )), know. Peoples responses help me write more books! Thanks again! ~Jaya Jayamen", ""),
        StaticBook("farming contract", "§bNalla corvinus", "\"Agreement:§0\\\n§0\\\n§0-Nalla provides one row of wheat.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0-Psycho gives Nalla one stack of iron ingot.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Signatories:§0\\\n§0Psycho Strongbrow§0\\\n§0Nalla\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Farming Contract", "§bBrother Tristifier Ross", "\"Agreement:§0\\\n§0\\\n§0- Tristifier Ross gives Psycho one row of wheat.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0-Psycho gives Tristifier ross one stack of iron ingots.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0Signatories:§0\\\n§0Psycho Strongbrow§0\\\n§0Tristifier Ross \"", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal, I, T.V.", "§bThanatos", "Thanatos's Journal\n-\n(Base Information)\n\n Making this journal out of Inspiration of a dear friend of mine her name is Nona.\n\n She also has her own journal if you. The reader cares about this information..\n\nMayor of Pembroke~\n\nMy name is Thanatos as you may presume..\nI am writing this journal for reasons as listed.\n\n I will be attempting to explain my story of becoming a Mayor of this town from the start to the current day..\n\n(Reference Pages)\n\n Chapter One: Page 5\n\nChapter Two: Page 32\n\n\n\n\n\n My next book will persist of the other chapters...\n\n\"\"\n\nChapter One...\n\n Traveling out from where I had originally resided..\n I'm a a pianist and a bard..\n I stumble across a large manor esc. structure on a hill..\n There was a large field with a couple smaller buildings surrounding the\n\n-large building.. Now to think of it.. it was more like a fort..\n I'd met a man named Ser Henry Lodmund and we'd exchanged pleasantries..\n\"G'day lad, To who're you..?\" Ser Henry would quote as I replied with.. \"Ti's I'm Thanatos Vhey.. A traveler...\"\n\n He'd looked me down at my general apparel clearly not of residence to any lands and quoted..\n \"Say you have a job..?\" I'd replied to his question saying..\n\"I'm more a traveler... I'd not done much jobs but I'd like one if you have one avaliable..\"--\n\n He'd grinned and walked me up to a building.. It was a small tavern esc. building..\nHe'd given me residency in the building and allowed me to sell drinks and such there as my work.. I'd brew drinks and sell drinks...\nThere was no sleeping grounds so I---\n\nhad to dig out under the tavern a place to reside.. A trapdoor in the floor to allow me to move downstairs and up at ease..\n\n I'd say a week had went by before my house was fully complete.. Not anything Mayor-like yet... Just a hole of dirt under a drunk-\n\nen mans feet..\n\n---some of this information I'm writing has to do when with the tavern was complete so let's resume with what happened before I was designing (the time inbetween the designing of the tavern underside)\n\n Ser Henry was showing me the tavern and I had encountered an undead in a suit outside...\n Ser Henry spotted him up the road.. A nasty little bug named Valkenier.. He will be listed later in the story for another reason...\n\nThe undead was strapped in a suit of Blackish Rusty Armoring.. and talked Ghoulishly at me..\n\"OOoooOOoh.. A neewWw suBBjEcct\"\nValkenier would quote as he'd look crookedly and me and Ser Henry..  I'd stand confused...\n\n Ser Henry would state for him to go away and the undead refused to leave..\n\n This is where it got hectic..\n\n Ser Henry would draw his blade on the undead..\nHe'd requested of me\n\"Thanatos, draw a weapon.. now..\" I'd ---\n\n-listen to him and draw my sword.. It was a bad piece of equipment but a sword is a sword..\n He'd made threats and such at the undead.. To no prevail the undead would not back away..\n This would upset Ser Henry and Henry and I would charge at him around--\n\n--the same time.. The Ghoulish undead turned around in a panic and scurried off toward a hole in the distance..\n\n Ser Henry ordered me to NOT enter the hole...\n To which we stopped for a moment and investigated the outside..\n\n As we investigated there was blood leading in from the doorway.. Turns out the hole was an abondon Mining Project.. There was a roughed up patch of earth outside assumed from some sort of Sacrifice..\n\n Ser Henry gestured in and I would slowly --\n\n-move on forward ahead of Ser Henry..\n\n There's a wide open corridor and an      Iron door at the end of the corridor.. But there was a ladder way down half broken to reach the iron door at the end of the corridor.. We'd walked into the Corridor. Visited-\n\n-by hole inside the walls that have hollow spaces where it felt like you could be watched all around..\n\n We'd slowly made our way in with a patch of stone behind us popping up trapping us in..\n The undead Valkenier would speak up saying ----\n\n---\"TheeEEErreEE's, NoooOOoo EscAPpe\"\n\n Thanatos(me) and Ser Henry would attemp to look down the ladder where the iron door was.. A small hole with a half broken ladder..  You could still climb it if you tried but it's a bit roughed up..\n\n Thanatos and Ser Henry were in for a fight.. We'd have our Swords at the ready as the undead would show himself.. We'd stepped away from the iron doorway to the Corridor met with him showing up at the top of the ladder..\n\n In a loud burst of words Valkenier (the undead ghoul) would state \"YoOOuUUu FooOOOOlllsSs\"\n-- \"YoUU'd CoMMEee HEEreEe\" and would then go onto laugh..\n\nSer Henry would charge at him hitting him in the chest and slicing him almost clean in two... But...--\n\n It looks like he wasn't even phased.. The undead menace was a brick wall, Metaphorically..\n\nThe undead would state \"YoOouUU ThiINnKKk YouUU CaNN HuurRRttt MEeE?!!\" then going onto swing his sword at Ser Henry.. I'd quickly push up to Ser Henry\n\nas the undead stated his sentance..\n The undead was preparing his swing and I would kick Valkenier as Ser Henry tried to back away..\n\n The undead wasn't phased or so we thought.. He'd then attempted a retreat..--\n\nThe undead would open up the iron door down the hole springing in and locking it..\n\nHe'd unlock the enterance we came and yelled at us the same we did when he showed to Pembroke..\n\n\"GEeeTtt OOOouOuut..!\"\n----\n\nWe'd flee from the undeads trapping grounds and make our way outside..\n\n We were lucky to escape unscaved...\n \n We'd come back to the residence to meet a man named Kagura..\n\nA strange man with Silver Hair.. Human..\n\n We'd chat a bit and he'd move on through the small bit of town we had at the time.. \n\n\n Ser Henry would approach me again before I entered the tavern stating..\n \"Ehmm.. Lad.. You did some good fighting.. I'd like to ask you to be in our army..\"\n\nHe'd offer..\n\n I thanked him stating..\n\"I'm sorry but I don't think I could take that sort of job.. I'm more of a laid back person.. Things like this tavern job are more down my alley.. I'm not a fan of violence but I love the idea you find me worthy to--\n\njoin the army of Pembroke.\" Which at the time was also very small.. There was little to no Residence..\n\n He replied.. \"Aye.. I see.. Wel' then.. I'll see what the count thinks of you..\" \n\nI'd sit questionable at the tavern counter at what he said..\n\n \"Ask about what..?\"\n\nEdward Suffolk the Count of Pembroke has approached me a couple days later.. he'd talk to me about small things like my dreams and goals and I'd question him of things..\n The conversation became closed to a halt as he stated..\n\nsome words that I would never forget...\n \"How would you like to be Deputy Mayor of Pembroke, I'd been looking for a Deputy mayor for a while..\"\n\n     I'd pause fumbling at the question thinking of what I should even say to reply to this offer...\n\n I'd accept the offer moments later stating..     \"Oh... I'd love that..\"\n He'd smile and I'd chuckle afterwards..\n\n\n   That's the story of how I became..                Deputy... Mayor..\n  But not mayor... atleast not yet..\n\nChapter II.\n\n I'd become Mayor and would preceed to do Mayorly duties..\n\n Around this time one of the most beautiful women I'd encountered has walked into town..\nAlijol Inkalla.. She will make multiple appearances in my life later on..\n\n Ser Henry has requested of me that I'd give her a tour of the place.. and I had..\nI'd show her to places and joke with her and had a fun time and she did as well.. She, Alijol was a Snow Elf.. not a Human as I, Thanatos was.. I'd go onto offer to her--..\n\n \"I'll show you the inside of the Courts Fort.. if you promise not to tell.. Showing you some parts might be not so swell of me to do.. I could be even beheaded..\" she'd reply hapilly.. \"I'd love to tour the place with you if you are sure..?\"-- I'd reply.\n\n I'm sure we could do this.. The count as of the time was resting during the day after some hard labor he had in endured..\n\n I'd then go onto open the front doorway to what is the Counts Fort.. We'd walked in and I'd show her just about every single room.\n\nThen.. we'd hit the point which is the Garden...\n \n As we would walk through the doors she'd looked in awe at the nature and beauty of his open gardenway.. It contained a pool as well which she was facisnated with...\n\n We'd made plans that later the night we would sneak into there and use his pool.. \n\n So we did.. we relaxed and had a great bonding experience..\n\nWe'd became much closer friends...\n\nVery... close...\n\n The next day..\n\n There was a man who was named Virkian Agnew who showed up today for housing.. This day Ser Henry would be giving the tours..\n Also the Kagura fellow mentioned before had joined the army..\n\nAlijol had became close to me so we'd be around each other as much as I could.. I'd do my duties as a Dep. Mayor and the town would slowly fill itself up more and more..\n\n I'd been caving out the bottom of my tavern to hit a Hot Spring located under the..\n\n--dirt below.\n I'd connected my basement home to a wonderful hot spring..\n\n From that day my home was a bit steamy until I added a venting system for the steam to follow outward..\n\n I'd eventually set a mood and invited Alijol to see my findings..\n\n She'd happily agreed and we'd had multiple different times where we'd stopped to go to the springs relaxing as friends and becoming slowly more..   We'd eventually started courting..  Lord Edward, Gladfully did not have a problem with this...\n\n The town was lively as there was a Crypt above a hill across the river..\n I.. never really noticed it.. Surprisingly..\n It'd be pointed out by someone else that I'd learned of this..\n\n A couple days after my learnings of this place there was a skeleton man with red robes and no visible eyes through his skull which was odd.. I'd never seen an undead skeleton before.. Even before Valkenier I'd never seen an undead even..\n\n around this time I would be showing a nun girl around town and Kagura and Ser Henry both army men.. and Virkian who became a trader were attempting to fight.. We were all around a good distance of the Skeleton man.. We'd attempted to talk to him..\n\n Kagura would spit out the words agressively..\n \"What do you want with us! State your name undead..\"\nin which the undead replied.. \"Hektor.. Hektor... Blackwood...\"\n\n We'd pause for a moment and he'd reveal a blue liquid in a bottle bubbling and\n\nglowing..\n\n Some of us would step away.. I and the nun girl were a decent distance way but she was closer compared to me which I was a bit further..\n\n Alijol was not around at the time thankfully..\n\n Hektor would break the potion upon the ground creating a thin smoke of blue-gray..\n\n People around the smoke who were speaker and not as muscular.. would drop to the ground including the nun..\n First thing I'd do is grab someone and carry them to the...\n\ntavern so they could be safe from the attack.. and hopefully recover..\n\n Closest person to me was the nun girl..\n So I'd pick her up and sit her in the tavern..\n\nWhen I'd come back out Ser Henry would be fighting with the undead..\n\n By then most of the smoke has dissapated into the air and Kagura was catching his fresh air.. He'd been cought in the sleeping gas only briefly.. he was fine..\n\nVirkian was weakened struggling to stand at this point.. I'd rescued him from the smoke next.\n\n then after Virkian was put up I'd dragged out a man named Arndt Sauer.. He's a lanky man in black robes and eyes as hard as a snake... I can see why the gas had put him out with ease...\n\n( Check book two for information on the next chapter.. )", ""),
        StaticBook("Malog's Parables", "§bClanfather Malog'Yar", "\"The Gahk Scoffers§0\\\n§0 In a bub’hosh klomp, an uruk urged gahk others to help him charge the enemy, which outnumbered them severely agh were prevailing against their goi. The gahk laugh agh blah’d, “Lat am a glob. We will nub help lat.” Agh they threw stones\"\n\n\"agh rotten grub at him as he charged alone to assist the rest of the brothers in defending their goi. In the end, da goi beat the attackers with the help of the brave uruk who tipped the balance just in their favor. Soon after, he became Rex. How bub’hosh\"\n\n\"was his wrath against the gahk mocked him before!§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Scatternak§0\\\n§0 A scatternak in the desert was trapped under a boulder and pled to a pair of passing jabbernaks for help. The older of the dub blah’d, “Nub!”§0\\\n§0 “Why?!” asked the scatternak.\"\n\n\" “Because,” he blah’d, “lat am a scatternak. Lat will sting us.”§0\\\n§0 “Mi would never sting ash who helps mi in mi hour of need!”§0\\\n§0 The jabbernaks reasoned among themselves, agh decided to help the scatternak. They pushed agh pushed, until the boulder rolled \"\n\n\"off of him. Then, as soon as he was free, the scatternak stung both of the jabbernaks. With his final gasps, the elder jabbernak asks, “Why?!”§0\\\n§0 “Because,” he blah’d, “mi am a scatternak.”§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Dub Boars§0\\\n§0In the wilderness, dub boars argued about who was \"\n\n\"the hoshest. As they bickered, a passing hunter crept up on them unawares, agh shattered both of their skulls.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Proud Tree§0\\\n§0 A bub’hosh tree towered above the whole forest. It spent its days gazing at the sky, agh blahing of its own bub’hoshness.\"\n\n\" Soon, all the mighty beasts of the forest grew tired of its arrogance agh incessant bragging. So obsessed with itself was the bub’hosh tree, however, that it did nub notice its protectors agh companions had abandoned it. With none to guard it, axemen\"\n\n\"came agh chopped it down.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Fearful Goat§0\\\n§0 A young goat was so frightened by all other creatures that he did nub gruk where to find relief. He fled in panic at the approach of any living thing, nub aware of the power of his own horns. Eventually, he\"\n\n\"fled his blarg in the mountains for fear of harpies. In the forests below, he feared the bears, so he ran to the plains, only to be frightened off by the wild howlers. Yet further away, in the savannas,  the lions were too fiersome for him. Before long,\"\n\n\"he found himself in the desert, where he fled into a cave at the sight of the jabbernaks. As he scurried desperately into the cave, however, the opening snapped shut on his spine, proving rather to be the mouth of a bub’hosh skhelll tortoise.§0\\\n§0\\\n\"\n\n\"The Man In The Well§0\\\n§0 A man lived at the bottom of an empty well, agh boasted his knowledge of the world. He ignored all who corrected him. Ash day, a bub’hosh storm came, agh he drowned.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0The Bub'hosh Powers§0\\\n§0 Ash day, the bub'hosh powers contended over\"\n\n\"who was bub’hoshest.§0\\\n§0 “Mi am bub’hoshest!” blahed the earthquake, agh he shattered the earth.§0\\\n§0 “Nub! It is mi!” Roared the tidal wave, as he flooded the lands.§0\\\n§0 “All of latz are wrong!” shouted the volcano, agh he erupted with smoke agh fire.§0\\\n\"\n\n\" “Globs!” hissed the tornado agh his sister, the hurricane, as they devastated whole gois.§0\\\n§0 Finally, after raining destruction from above, the lightning suggested they ask the people to pronounce ash of them the bub’hoshest. When they sought after \"\n\n\"somebody to settle their dispute, however, they found there were none left alive to ask.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0 The Parables of Malog, Clanfather of the Yars.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Quen", "§bAzureth", "In Quen, you play as a sigil drawing wizard fighting other wizards. The game works for any amount of players. To play, you need a deck of any nine cards. This is the second edition of Quen.\n\nFirst, choose a card from your deck as your Quen card, then lay it face up to the side. Next, shuffle your remaining eight cards and place them face down. Flip a mina or use some other method to randomly determine the order of players' turns.\n\nAll players begin by drawing two cards. Every turn except the first, draw an additional card. If your deck contains no cards, you may draw your Quen card. Every turn, you may play as many cards as you like. Once a card is played, shuffle it back into your\n\ndeck. Quen cards go back to the side. Finally, declare the end of your turn. You have eight health and are removed from the game if you reach zero; the last player standing wins.\n\nFor optimal fun, make bets of minas or cards.\n\nNormal Cards\n\nTriangle - Your target loses two health.\n\nCircle - Your target gains two health.\n\nKite - Your target shuffles two random cards back into their deck.\n\nPentagon - Your target draws two cards.\n\nEllipse - You can play the Ellipse after any other card is played, regardless of the current turn. That card does nothing.\n\nSquare - The next card that's played is removed from the game.\n\nRhombus - The next player who plays a card loses two health.\n\nHourglass - Your target searches their deck for a card and draws it.\n\nStar - Your target shuffles their hand back into their deck. You lose health equal to the cards lost.\n\nQuen Cards\n\nTriangle - Your target loses four health.\n\nCircle - Your target gains four health.\n\nKite - Your target shuffles four cards back into their deck.\n\nPentagon - Your target draws four cards.\n\nEllipse - Your target's Quen card is removed from the game.\n\nSquare - The next two cards played are removed from the game.\n\nRhombus - The next player who plays a card loses four health.\n\nHourglass - Your target searches their deck for two cards and draws them.\n\nStar - All players shuffle their cards back into their decks.\n\n((Your deck is the top row of your inventory, with your Quen card in the ninth slot. To randomize draws and shuffles, roll a d8. Reroll on empty slots. Your hotbar is your hand.))", ""),
        StaticBook("Halfling Laws", "§bPippin Mousiki", "This book contains all, if not a vast majority, of the unspoken laws of being a Halfling! If you don't follow these laws, you're not a true Halfling.\n\n1.)\nDON'T WEAR SHOES\n\n2.)\nDON'T LOCK YOUR BURROW DOORS\n\n3.)\nNEVER LIGHT PLACES WITH ANYTHING BUT TORCHES AND PUMPKINS\n\n4.)\nPUMPKINS AND CARROTS\n\n5.)\nNEVER BE AFRAID TO DRINK SPIRITS, unless you're dangerous when you're drunk!\n\n6.)\nDON'T BE A THEIF OF YOUR FELLOW KIN\n\n7.)\nDISCOURAGE VIOLENCE\n\n8.)\nALWAYS HAVE THE BEST OF PARTIES\n\n9.)\nALWAYS HAVE A PANIC ROOM IN YOUR BURROW\n\n10.)\nDON'T HAVE BIG BURROWS FOR ONLY YOURSELF\n\n11.)\nSHARE\n\n12.)\nALWAYS USE SHOVELS TO DEFEND YOURSELF\n\n13.)\nPUMPKINS AND CARROTS\n\n14.)\nDEFEND YOUR FELLOW KIN\n\n15.)\nRESPECT YOUR LITERAL AND METAPHORICAL ELDERS\n\n16.)\nRESPECT EVERYONE\n\n17.)\nBE NICE\n\n18.)\nDON'T LIVE IN EXTRAVAGENCE\n\n19.)\nDRINK AND BE MERRY\n\n20.)\nDrink Mousiki Spirits", ""),
        StaticBook("MUNGO!", "§bMungo Proudfoot", "________\n       _|         |_\n       |_________|\n        | __   __ |\n        | ||_|   ||_| |\n        |    __    |\n        |________!\n\nMUNGO!", ""),
        StaticBook("Halfling Babies", "§bRosso", "Where do halfling babies come from?\n\nHalfling birth is by far the most magical and sweet birth of all the races. I first found out about how the halflings are born when I went to the halfling town, which I have forgotten the name of. Quite hungry when I arrived, I asked permission from one\n\nof the elders to remove a few plants form the farm, permission which was granted to me. \n\nAs I walked through the farm I took a few carrots and potatoes, then I found an overly grown cabbage. I thought as a thank you, I would cook the\n\ngreat cabbage and make the Halflings a great cauldron of Cabbage soup. As I was about to take the cabbage from the fertile land, a Halfling came shouting through the fields for me to stop, seeming quite stressed. Believing that somehow I was in the wrong\n\nfield, or that cabbage was of prized goods, I stepped away from the cabbage, and awaited the Halfling. While huffing, the Halfling, still stressed, checked the cabbage for damage, before hitting me in the shin with his shovel.\nIn pain I fell to the gro\n\nwhile grabbing my leg, wondering what kind of prized cabbage that could be. The Halfling looked angry and even shouted “Wha’ were y’ goin’ t’ do t’ me son?!” I was amazed, the cabbage was so important to him, he called it his son. I apologized and said\n\nthat as a thank you I was going to cook his “son” for the Halflings, but that I didn’t know it belonged to someone. I couldn’t finish explaining before I hit repeatedly by the shovel. The Halfling was shouting as he hit me “Y’ disgustin’ man, how dare’ye\n\ntry t’ feed us one o’ our own babies!”\n\nI was shocked, I didn’t understand. I apologized and said many times that I didn’t know, and after a while, the Halfling stopped hitting me. After he stopped I continued asking, in serious pain I might add. I a\n\nwhat did the cabbage meant to the Halflings, and he told me a story I will never forget.\n\nThe story he told me was one of love, the love two Halflings feel for each other. I already knew at the time how dwarf babies were born, and knew that Halflings\n\ndescendents of both Horen and Urguan, so I was confused how they mated and had children, I didn’t know if it was the dwarven way, or the human way. And what I was told, was nothing more than magical.\n\nHe told me of him and his wife, wife for many\n\nyears now. They clearly loved each other quite dearly, and one day decided to have a child. They began their evening by drinking and smoking together, alone in their house, only the two which love each other. They do what they love most together, drinking\n\nthe finest Halfling ale, and smoking the best Halfling weed. When the moon was high, they went into the fields together, carrying a single seed, a normal seed. After planting the cabbage in the patch, they prayed to their pumpkin god.\n\nThe seed, bles\n\nwith the love of the soon to be mother and father Halfling, and the power of the pumpkin god, started growing quite large, into what was now the cabbage I almost took. The baby Halfling grows within the cabbage, to be born at the time of the harvest\n\nseason. It was still a few elven days from the harvest, and as such, if I had took the cabbage, I would give birth to the baby too soon. I decided to stay for a while longer to witness the birth, and it was as they said.\n\nI helped with the harvest th\n\nday, and soon, all the Halflings gathered by the cabbage. The mother and father started carefully removing the big leaves of the cabbage. It took a while for the small Halflings to remove the leaves, but soon enough, in the middle of it, a tiny sleeping\n\nbaby could be seen. The father thanked the pumpkin god once more as the mother took the baby. That night, they made a feast, for the harvest, and the newborns. The name for the newborns? They thought of them while drunk and high.\n\nWhere do Halfing babies come from\n\nOriginal author unknown\nCoppied by Rosso\nVaerHaven\n\n((initial idea by Jexdane))", ""),
        StaticBook("Shovels & Spades", "§bArmin Ambertoe", "On Shovels and Spades\n\nBy Armin Ambertoe\n\nTable of Contents\n\n1: Parts of a Shovel and Spade\n2: Shovel vs. Spade - The Differences\n3: Shovels and Spades as Weapons\n4: Miscellaneous Uses\n\n1: Parts of a Shovel and Spade\n\nThe shovel is divided into three parts: the handle, the shaft and the head. \n\nThe handle is usually a piece of metal but is also occasionally made of wood. The handle’s purpose is to provide a location to grip th\n\nshovel as well as work in conjunction with the shaft to act as a lever, making it easier to operate. \n\nThe shaft provides a way for the handle and head to connect to one another as well allow the shovel to act as a lever providing easier operation. T\n\nshaft is usually made of wood. \n\nThe head of the shovel is the most important part, as without it you have a stick with a handle. The head is almost always made of metal as you need a solid and sharp edge to allow for prolonged use and to make breaki\n\ngrass easier.\n\n2: Shovel vs. Spade - The Differences\n\nOne common misconception is that a spade and shovel are the same thing. It is true that they share the same main components being a handle, shaft and head with the handle and shaft being identical, but the\n\ndifferences arise in the shape of the head and their uses.\n\nA shovel’s head is curved and comes to a point at the end. A shovel is best used for digging.\n\nA spade on the other hand has a flat end and is ideal for gardening and\n\nbreaking up grass.\n\n3:Shovels and Spades as Weapons\n\nAs the weapon of choice for every halfling the shovel or spade sees much use outside of their uses as tools. Not only do they serve as a powerful blunt weapon but its smaller size lends to its potency in the hands of\n\nhalfling, allowing them to deliver precise blows.\n\n4: Miscellaneous Uses\n\nThe shovel also has a use in the sport of Shogging. In this sport two players stand atop separate floating logs and attempt to knock the other player off the log while wearing a pumpkin on their heads.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Golden Fish", "§bLurcano Car'dann", "Long ago, there was a king of a far away land that was turning blind. A bard in his court claimed that he could heal the king if a golden-headed fish was brought to him in ninety days, for he had to leave in ninety days. The Prince went out to the sea\n\nwith his men, and fished for it. A hundred days and nights passed before the Prince finally caught the fish. Too late to bring it back, the Prince threw the fish back into the ocean for he did not wish to waste a life. Upon his return, the King did not\n\nbelieve in the Prince's efforts to catch the fish, and sentenced him to death. The servants warned the Queen, who proceeded to smuggle him out of the city to an island, with normal clothes and some gold. Before they parted, she left him with the warning,\n\n\"Do not take unto your service the man who wishes to be paid every month.\" At the island, the Prince bought a house, and interviewed many servants who wanted to be paid by the month, before finally taking in a Halfling, who wanted to be paid every year.\n\nOn this island, a terrible monster ravaged its people. Whoever went to fight this monster fell asleep. The Halfling approached the King and asked what he would get for slaying the beast, and the King offered half his land and his daughter. The Halfling\n\nasked instead that he share in whatever he gained. The King agreed, and the Halfling went out and slayed the monster. After, he urged the Prince to take the credit. The King gave the prince a ship at his request, and secretly filled the ships hold with\n\njewels. The Halfling and the Prince sailed off to another far off land, and upon landing, the Halfling urged the Prince to marry the king's daughter. The king warned the Prince however that his daughter had been married one hundred and ninety nine times,\n\nand that no man had lasted the twelfth hour. Despite his reservations, the Halfling urged the Prince to marry the king's daughter anyway. They were married, and that very same night as the Prince was with his bride, he looked out the window to see a grave\n\nin his shape being dug. At that moment a snake leapt from the princess' mouth towards the Prince, but the Halfling was there, and he cut the creature down. This ended the spell held over the princess, and she and the Prince remained happily married.A year\n\nlater, a messenger ran into the Prince's hall and said, \"Your father is dead, and your mother begs you to return immediately so that you may be the king in succession.\" The Prince prepared a splendid ship immediately and set sail for his former home. Upon\n\nhis arrival, the Queen, in spite of her grief for her husbands death, was overjoyed at the return of her son. He was crowned the next day with much joy from the people. The Prince was very happy until one night the Halfling came, and asked for permission\n\nto return to his old land. The Prince, though saddend by the loss of his loyal servant, would not keep him from returning after all his loyal service. As the Halfling was to leave, the Prince offered up anything the Halfling wanted as return for all he\n\nhad done for him. The Halfling refused however, for he was the Golden-headed Fish.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Armin", "§bMaaz", "On Armin \n\nby Maaz\n===================\n\n  Armin Ambertoe is a middle-aged halfling who works at the Library of Dragur, alongside the other scholars who reside within those stone walls. He took on the role of a scholar\n\nsome time back in Vailor, if I remember correctly. His history is not well-known to me, but given his current demeanor, I would have to say that he's been around other races for a longer time than he has been around his own people. He is a race traitor.\n\nA whitewashed half-man. I'm not sure if he has any family, but if he does, I can't imagine what they'd look like. Perhaps he has told me, but I've simply forgotten.\n\n  Armin is a nuisance to me, and I've come very close to impulsively killing him. He\n\ntakes after Lyeth, the previous librarian, who I would much prefer dead. She is a mentally ill wood elven woman who acts like every one else's mother. But this book is not about her. This is about Armin. \n\n  Armin has shown a p roficiency in\n\ntransfiguration, arcanism, and telekinesis. He is also an Archon, or a being composed of mana who can float and is hard to strike. I've learned that while he looks like a halfling, he may be killed very easily. I struck his nose and it began to bleed.\n\nArmin tries to act like a father figure, and I suppose he does succeed somewhat in imposing his will over others (excluding myself, as I am capable of dominating his flimsy body). This halfling tries his best to protect his friends. He enjoys peace and\n\nhates war, just like his people. It's just as they say. \n\nYou can take the x out of the y, but you can't take the y out of the x.\n\nHaha.\n\nArmin Ambertoe has unkempt brown hair and wears brown pants. He used to wear overalls, but now he wears a comfortable-looking light brown sweater. He has green eyes. Pale skin.\n\nIf one spots Armin Ambertoe, go up to him and say 'hi', and that Maaz told you to do this. \n\nHowever, I would much rather you killed him on sight.\n\nHaha.\n\nWritten on the 8th of Sun's Smile, 1594", ""),
        StaticBook("Gnomish", "EclecticBoogaloo", "GNOMISH FOLK SONGS\n\nMah pa 'n de bar-lass\n\n\"Dere wonce were ah lass so foine, ah saw 'er at de tavern, 'oldin down de drink. \n\nSheh ootdrank e'eryone at de bar, 'cept fer meh.\n\nAh took 'er to mah hole, de drink kickin' in.\n\nSheh lifted up 'er bloose, and it turnes ou; sheh's mah pa!\"\n\nBilly Bob de Tater God\n\n\"Dere's a strong man out dere in de fields.\n\n'E's farmin' 'n ho'in 'n makin' yer food.\n\nDe man's name beh Billeh, de great' man ye knew.\n\n'is name beh Billeh, 'n dat beh truu.\n\n'e c'n outdrink de bes' 'n outparty de hardest. 'e gets all de women 'n all de bed ceremonehs.\n\nYeh moigh' fink dat dere beh ah meenin' ter de song.\n\nDere's no'. 'e's jus' a good guy.\"\n\nTavern Song\n\n\"Ah was told ter wroigh' ah song aboot de Tavern.\n\nSo ah made dis song.\n\nEs aboot drinkin' 'n stumblin' 'n smokin' de green.\n\nEs aboot livin' 'n willin' 'n fillin' de sadness wif ale! \n\n'N aboot here dere's ah lute riff.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("ManfestMoe", "JavaWizard", "This iz a buk wit ten bye Moezez Ambearto!\n\nArm in iz beg;; Moezez iz smal;;\n\nAye doont lik buks beacause ther havy!\n\n*A large ink stain is here taking up the rest of the page*\n\n*An odd drawing is here.... it looks like a fish with wings and a tail*\n\n        Moezezzz \n\n     ManIfesTO\n\nMoezezzz MAnifesto\n\n_ _ ____ _ >\n\nSaVe AnmalS and playnts !\n\nHalp evryony for fre!\n\nTeche how too do thing! (fre)\n\nDont ALLow mean!\n\nStope Bad wURds!\n\nEvryony egual!", ""),
        StaticBook("Gnomish Nature", "KBR", "Teh Great Gnomish\n                     Poem\nBy: Nobsen Ambertoe\n\nGnomes are small\nBiggots are tall\nThey are the gnomes\nSome say they came from the Catacombs\nNo one knows where they really came from\nBut it is generally\n\nestablished that they are dumb", ""),
        StaticBook("Serene Wayfare", "§bBerilac Goldworthy", "This will be the journal of my travel to the East. Not exactly what I would do when still being pissed at erry five hours by a bunch o' aengul choirs (weather these days) but I still should document the travel for whatever posterity it is we'll have. B.G\n\nAfter taking a barge to Leuvardeen, I've paid the local cathedral a brief visit, drawn by a dim chance of searching through the religious archives. While the chance has proven obvious, Fortune wasn't my lady again, and I didn't find anything of use.\n\nI'll take a look at the supplies I've prepped and then get going, one foot after the other, through the Amyasites' hills 'till I see the red rock over the shore and I'll be forced to find new means for sailing southwards from that point. 1st of Deep Cold.\n\nI've passed the Garden of Edale and the majestic fortifications beside the mighty rivers, eking ahead east. Had to get wet to get through, but at least it's not as difficult as arguing with Heartlander nobility. \n2nd of Deep Cold.\n\nCrossing the mt. Aeriel has proven to be the worst ordeal of this travel - at least, as of current - but the sights were well damn worth it. Coulda sworn I can see the old Akovia from here... 3rd of Deep Cold,\n\nNow that I have reached Ostiredge, do I truly understand that my journey - a preparation for a better tomorrow... (mayhaps a one tad less rainy) ... is at it's very craddle and as I step onto the fishing boat, thankful to Creator for the humans' kindness,\n\nI can't help but miss the home left way behind the cloudy mountainside.\nLate 3rd of Deep Cold. \nAboard \"Sunstride\".\n\n\"Sunstride\" passed the very tower of Rasmot today, or, whatever it is these lunatics galore seem to call it. Made me skin crawl, and the fishermen alltogether anxious. Can't say I wasn't glad when we finally left it out of our sight. 4th of Deep Cold.\n\nAfter nearly crashing the boat into a Farfolker war galley, fishermen captain ordered the crew - and his one passenger - to drop the anchor, knowing we're nearing the Isles and the foggy weather has already endangered us enough. 5th of Deep Cold\n\nAnd here they finally are. Isles of Serenity. Never did I think, not even as a child listening to aulder stories, that I would actually have a chance to see them with my own eyes. A place of peace, a place of beauty, and perhaps, a home for our people,\n\nthat is, if I am still in any way correct. \"Sunstride\" will be departing soon, so I will do my utmost to memorize - and draw - some of the things I've discovered or experienced. Creator's blessings be upon them fisher lot. \n6th of Deep Cold\n\nMy journey back begins, and as sorrowed as I am to leave these outlandish wonders, I still come back a richer man - richer in knowledge, and mayhaps, happiness. Who would have thought that of all things in Athera, it would be nature to poke that feeling\n\nback into me sorry head. 8th of Deep Cold, returning on \"Sunstride\"\n\nRather then keep the spot for meself at \"Sunstride\", I offered to leave closer, nearefore the de Oryden holding, so as to ensure I still have a chance to map the shores on the travel. Here, to ensure these stay more secret then the little journal, I will\n\nsee to it's end. I thank the captain Alabaster and his crewmates, and all the kind folks that didn't bother killing a lonely Halfling on the roads of me wayfare. God bless Gimblewood and wee folk. 9th of Deep Cold, de Oryden.\n\n\"O but loud they shout\nLighting out all the crowd\nThrashing onto the thatch\nWashing away every kind of grass\nRed and white all have bloom\nThere we’ve nothing to gloom.\"(In honour o' Ben Haze)", ""),
        StaticBook("Big Bad Bigguns", "§bVelvet Roundbottom", "-==-\n           Big\n            Bad\n             Bigguns\n           -==-\n           And\n            You\n           -==-\n\nBigguns are a curious species of animal, posessing the ability to walk upright and communicate- But don't be fooled!\n\nBigguns are dangerous! Even deadly to us Halflings!\n\nBigguns must be approached with caution, if they decide to try and have you for dinner, there's only one thing you can do!\n\nGrab your trusty mallet, shovel, trowel, and hammer away at their dumb, stupid knees!\n\nThey'll be severely crippled and you might be able to even capture one as a pet!\n\nTaming a biggun is very difficult and requires time, patience, food, and whips.\n\nWhen a biggun acts out of hand or naughty, it is a good idea to give them a good spanking.\n\nBigguns are rather useful animals, for when we need that extra reach in our kitchens, or to do our chores. \n\nOr even have them carry us around obediently!\n\nIt is never a good idea to remove or release a biggun slave, as they are likely to communicate with their fellow species and attempt to murder us!\n\nBigguns come in many flavors: human, elf, orc, and many others.\n\nThey also have a variety of odd colors sometimes, such as greens, purples, reds, or the regular white color.\n\nEach biggun type looks different from the last and can even perform certain other tasks better than others!\n\nOrcs are perfect farming equipment, whilst elves and humans are perfect for reading goodnight stories and cooking (some times).\n\nNow... Bigguns are rather easy to find if you find their right habitats. They sometimes live in giant stone cities or other odd places. These bigguns are always feral and any halfling would be wise to try and avoid a direct confrontation with these beasts\n\nJust a reminder, all bigguns are inferior to us small folk, they're dumb, crazy, and smell funny- and wear shoes!\n\nSo remember that you're better than them in every way!", ""),
        StaticBook("O' t'a Shire", "§bMadeline Applefoot", "T'a lan's o' t'a shire are t'a bes' I say,\nT'a swee' wa'ers on yer tongue in t'a 'morn,\nAn' if beh Knox's will I wouldn' beh ah 'alflin', I'd rathah 'ave no' 've been born!", ""),
        StaticBook("AHoH", "§bMonk Bungo", "A History of Halflings:\n\nBy: Petyr Brandybuck\n\n\nRe-Written by Monk Bungo.\n\nPreface-\n\nAs is common knowledge, the origins of the halfling race reside began with couples consisting of a human and a dwarf. Nowadays, the halflings have distinct traits of their own, practically unmistakable when compared with-\n\n- the modern counterparts of their progenitors. The purpose of this book is to educate the populace about the culture and history of the halflings. The information in this book has been preserved either in ruins, in literature, or in folklore.\n\nChapter 1 - Beginnings - Years 0-300\n\nThough there are many conflicting accounts regarding the creation and following years of Aegis, most records agree that the race of humans and that of dwarves most likely had contact before-\n\n-year 50. And, as when any two cultures collide, so do their blood, and so at some point in time, humans began to mate with dwarves. We can trace some traits back to this point, such as brewing and farming talents, but as we will see, other generic-\n\nhalfling traits developed over time.\n\nIndeed, it is hard to pinpoint the first halfling. After researching animal breeding as well as magical oddities, I would propose that, intially, the children of a dwarf/human couple would not be classified as a halfling. You see, it would make much more-\n\n-sense if halflings were a height in between that of a dwarf and human, but instead, they are actually shorter! This would indicate that, some time in the past, a great outer influence caused the future children of these mixed couples to have this odd-\n\nheight\n\nIt is reasonable to conclude that halflings as we know them today were present by Year 300, based on folklore and literary records.\n\nChapter 2 - Early Developments - Years 300-600\n\nA combination of small stature and inherant greed drove some of the first halflings to thievery, a very viable profession for nimble hands in the cities. They gained a reputation for being-\n\nmischievous and devious, and thus gained little respect for their brewing or farming prowess. There was some prejudice against them, no doubt; never once in history or literature does one hear of a heroic or powerful halfling. To say that they-\n\n-were suppressed would be incorrect, but people did find them a thing to be \"tolerated\".\n\nOver time, of course, most halflings developed a sort of fear of violence and arguments, reducing the number of thieves. As well, most halflings\nmoved to Or\n\nescape the war-mongering attitude of the dwarves. This is estimated to have taken place over the time span of Years 400-600 The humans were little better, though.  And, over time, halflings began to move to more rural areas, escaping those that would-\n\n-persecute them. Small communities on the very border of human cities were formed, and there halflings began to develop customs to cheer them up. Indeed, good food and good times seemed to become the goal of every halfling.\n\nChapter 3 - Later Developments - Years 600-1200\n\nHalflings continued migrating farther and farther out of the city. It came to be that small communities of halflings were spread out in the vast plains surrounding Oren, with the halflings only-\n\n-revealing themselves occasionally to trade goods. Over time, the negative connotation towards halflings mostly disappated, but the halflings enjoyed their semi-solitary lifestyles.\n\nThe countryside is where the art of halfling brew and cooking truely matured into the art form that it is today. Indeed, the herbs and spices that could be found in the countryside of Oren had never been truly used to their full potential, and so-\n\nhalflings were the first to utilize them. Some of these herbs include the yellow wildflower, spice of apple, and fern dust. The ale, while very potent, began to develop more of a focus on flavor and aftertaste. This also was the case with halfling ale and\n\ncider.\n\nIt is important to note that there were still some halflings living in cities at this point (~Year 800). Most halflings were born of halfling/halfling, but some were still born of a human/dwarf couple. These halflings enjoyed a much-\n\n-easier life than their ancestors.\n\nAround this time in history, the number of halflings had indeed grown to a point where surnames were required to identify with, as previously, only single names were used.\n\nNames, both first and last, were usually one or two syllables. Notable surnames and houses that began at this time were the houses of Took and Brandybuck, founded by Tulkan and Grombadook, respectively.  The Tooks had the traits of what might be called\n\na quintessential halfling - friendly, yet shy, of average height and demeanor. The Brandybucks, however, were a tad more adventurous, with darker hair than most halflings. Each family lived in a single burrow hill most of them in the general of another.\n\nThese family hills were the closest thing to a town as had truely ever existed yet in halfling culture. However, in around Year 1010, some families started to break apart from population pressure. Families like the Brandybucks eventually spread-\n\nall throughout the land.\n\nBy around this time, halflings had been isolated enough that, not only did this unique culture of peace and merriment develop, but the halflings actually forgot or disbelieved in the creation stories and of Aenguls, -\n\n-  Daemons, and God. Indeed, the halflings didn't really develop a totally obscure faith, but instead took on a quasi-religious outlook that revolved around the things they held dear: harvest and food, companionship, nature, and peace. No \"gods\" were ever\n\n named, nor was worship very common, but there was a common belief that, if a halfling betrayed his tight-knit community, that the harvest and the tranquility of life would be lost.\n\nChapter 4 - The Rise and Decline of the Village Era - Years 1200-1304\n\nAround the year 1200, a small group of halflings, from both Took, Brandybuck, Goodbody, and other families, decided to form a self-sufficient-\n\n-community apart from the family burrows. They had decided to make it a collection of hills, hidden from society by the waters and hills surrounding it. This community eventually came to be named Dunwood, and it remains the most notable halfling town to-\n\n-date. There are massive wheat fields and a beautiful, clean lake. This town was always notable for being quite territorial, for as the humans began to urbanize more and more, family burrows were abandoned, and Dunwood was one of the last retreats for\n\ncountry-loving halflings. As word of the town's existence came to be, spread by the word of the Wandering Wizard, halflings from both cities and family hills came to try and gain a burrow here.The founders of Dunwoodwere initially very-\n\nwelcome, but soon, the onrush of want-to-be residents came to such a high number that it was impossible to distinguish which would be beneficial to the community. The aspect of companionship was always very emphasized, and as a later resident of the town-\n\n I can vouch for this fact. By the time that I moved to Dunwood, it was impossible to walk through the streets of Al'Khazar without being pestered for the town's semi-secret location.\n\nEnvious of the town, many halflings and non-halflings began-\n\nmaking similar towns in the surrounding hills, a more known one by the name of Thistledown.\n\nI am now qualified, at this point, to tell the history from a first-person perspective. Yes, for I arrived in Dunwood, during a small population boom-\n\n when the town was thriving and more inhabitants came every day. The Elders of the town at the time were Kip Took, Len, Gimblo. I was first escorted to the town by Gimblo, who took Bell and I for a visit.  And, as I mentioned earlier, we were persued-\n\nthrough the streets of Al'Khazar by nosy people! Gimblo turned a corner, snapped his finger, and suddenly Bell and I were in Dunwood (a trick I have yet to emulate perfectly). The smell of hot bread and ale wafted from the ale garden, and I could hear a-\n\nhalfling singing with a lyre in the distance. Indeed, it was truly the ideal place for a halfling. Indeed, soon, the whole town took a trip to Al'Khazar to pledge allegiance to the newly-kinged Edmund.\n\nAfter many a year of drinking, story-telling\n\n and visitor-shoveling, the town seemed to go into a cultural decline. The Elders grew a tad sickly, and so they appointed Owen Sturdyfoot II as the Mayor to help govern. However, even his efforts did not maintain the vitality of the town, as Brian left-\n\nto becomean Ascended, Biodoc passed away, Rusty moved to Al'Khazar, and Lilly was kidnapped. This decline occured in other towns, too, leaving an area surrounding Dunwood filled with empty hill-homes and the likes. I, too, left after a call from-\n\n the Druids, though the years of countryside living would have a profound influence on me for my entire life.\n\nChapter 5 - Up to Modern Day - Years 1304-Present Day\n\nAfter many years, around 1340, I decided along with a few relatives to restore the popularity and culture of Dunwood, and so we hosted DunFest a large-\n\n festival with much merriment. There was drinking, dancing, singing, and the likes, of course. However, afterwards, it did not have the profound influence on the town population that I would have liked. And so, I went back to Malinor, only to try another-\n\nfestival later. Indeed, it appeared that our selective ways way long ago had a profound influence on the interest in the town, and so many gave up their hopes of moving and settled in the city. Many halflings have forgotten the joy of simple and clean-\n\n- life, to my surprise. While I certainly traveled and was no typical halfling, the air off of Lake Dunwood in the early morn still stirs my soul like very little else does.\n\nAt the most recent DunFest, I did meet some fellows quite interested in culture, but none were halflings. I have tried to embrace the city-dwelling halflings with open arms, but very few have answered the call.\n\nWith the division of Oren, I as one of the only remaining Elders of the town decided to not immediately pledge our allegiance to either faction, instead remaining independent for some time. I did, however, set up a trade caravan of goods between Dunwood-\n\n- and Galahar, trying to make use of our overstocked wheat.\n\nAt the time of writing this, the state of the world grows dim as the Undead continue to win victory after victory. The future will surely deserve another tome of halfling history, perhaps m\n\nin depth, as this was merely a general overview.\n\nHopefully this has been an informative and enjoyable read.", ""),
        StaticBook("Halflings Vol. 1", "§bPetrus Frondor", "Halflings: A History\n              Vol. I\n\n\n     A History of Halflings\n      By Petyr Brandybuck\n\n    Edited by Petrus Frondor\n\nPreface\nAs is common knowledge, the origins of the halfling race reside began with couples consisting of a human and a dwarf. Nowadays, the halflings have distinct traits of their own, practically unmistakable when compared  with the modern counterpart\n\nof their progenitors. The purpose of this book is to educate the populace about the culture and history of the halflings. The information in this book has been preserved either in ruins, in literature, or in folklore.\n\nChapter 1 - Beginnings\nYears 0-300\n\nThough there are many conflicting accounts regarding the creation and following years of Aegis, most records agree that the race of humans and that of dwarves most likely had contact before Year 50. And, as whe\n\ncultures collide, so do their blood, and so at some point in time, humans began to mate with dwarves. We can trace some traits back to this point, such as brewing and farming talents, but as we will see, other generic halfling traits developed over time.\n\nIndeed, it is hard to pinpoint the first halfling. After researching animal breeding as well as magical oddities, I would propose that, intially, the children of a dwarf/human couple would not be classified as a halfling.  You see, it would make sense if\n\nhalflings were a height in between that of a dwarf and human, but instead, they are actually shorter! This would indicate that, some time in the past, a great outer influence caused the future children of these mixed couples to have this odd height.\n\nIt is reasonable to conclude that halflings as we know them today were present by Year 300, based on folklore and literary records.\n\nChapter 2 - Early Developments\nYears 300-600\n\nA combination of small stature and inherant greed drove some of the first halflings to thievery, a very viable profession for nimble hands in the cities. They gained a reputation for being mischievous\n\ndevious, and thus gained little respect for their brewing or farming prowess. There was some prejudice against them, no doubt; never once in history or literature does one hear of a heroic or powerful halfling. To say they were suppressed would be\n\nincorrect, but people did find them a thing to be \"tolerated\".\n\nOver time, of course, most halflings developed a sort of fear of violence and arguments, reducing the number of thieves. As well, most halflings moved to Oren to escape the war-mongering\n\nattitude of the dwarves. This is estimated to have taken place over the time span of Years 400-600 The humans were little better, though. And, over time, halflings began to move to more rural areas, escaping those that would persecute them. Small\n\ncommunities on the very border of human cities were formed, and there halflings began to develop customs to cheer them up. Indeed, good food and good times seemed to become the goal of every halfling.\n\nChapter 3 - Later Developments Years 600-1200\n\nHalflings continued migrating farther and farther out of the city.  It came to be that small communities of halflings were spread out in the vast plains surrounding Oren, with the halflings only revealin\n\nthemselves occasionally to trade goods. Over time, the negative connotation towards halflings mostly disappated, but the halflings enjoyed their semi-solitary lifestyles.\n\nThe countryside is where the art of halfling brew and cooking truly matured in\n\nthe art form that it is today. Indeed, the herbs and spices that could be found in the countryside of Oren had never been truely used to their full potential, and so halflings were the first to utilize them. Some of these herbs include the yellow\n\nwildflower, spice of apple, and fern dust. The ale, while very potent, began to develop more of a focus on flavor and aftertaste. This also was the case with halfling bread and cider.\n\nIt is important to note that there were still some halflings living in cities at this point (~Year 800). Most halflings were born of halfling/halfling, but some were still born of a human/dwarf couple. These halflings enjoyed a much easier life than their\n\nancestors.\nAround this time in history, the number of halflings had indeed grown to a point where surnames were required to identify with, as previously, only single names were used. Names, both first and last, were usually one or two syllables.\n\n Notable surnames and houses that began at this time were the houses of Took and Brandybuck, founded by Tulkan and Grombadook, respectively. The Tooks had the traits of what might be called the quintessential halfling- friendly, yet shy, of average height\n\nand demeanor. The Brandybucks, however, were a tad more adventurous, with darker hair than most halflings. Each family lived in a single burrow hill, most of them in the general vicinity of another. These family hills were the closest thing to a town as\n\nhad truely ever existed yet in halfling culture.\nHowever, in around Year 1010, some families started to break apart from population pressures. Families like the Brandybucks eventually spread all througout the lands.\n\nBy around this time, halflings had been isolated enough that, not only did this unique culture of peace and merriment develop, but the halflings actually forgot or disbelieved in the creation stories and of Aenguls, Daemons, and God. Indeed, the halflings\n\ndidn't really develop a totally obscure faith, but instead took on a quasi-religious outlook that revolved around the things they held dear: harvest and food, companionship, nature, and peace. No \"gods\" were ever named, nor was worship very common,\n\nbut there was a common belief that, if a halfling betrayed his tight-knit community, that the harvest and the tranquility of life would be lost.\n\nChapter 4 - The Rise and Decline of the Village Era\nYears 1200-1304\n\nAround the year 1200, a small group of halflings, from both Took, Brandybuck, Goodbody, and other families, decided to form a self-sufficient community apart from the family bur\n\nThey had decided to make it a collection of hills, hidden from society by the waters and hills surrounding it. This community eventually came to be named \"Dunwood\", and it remains the most notable halfling town to date. There are massive wheat fields and\n\na beautiful, clean lake. This town was always notable for being quite territorial, for as the humans began to urbanize more and more, family burrows were abandoned, and Dunwood was one of the last retreats for the country-loving halflings. As word of the\n\ntown's existence came to be, spread by the word of the Wandering Wizard, halflings from both cities and family hills came to try and gain a burrow here. The founders of Dunwood were initially very welcome, but soon, the onrush of want-to-be residents came\n\nto such a high number that it was impossible to distinguish which would be beneficial to the community. The aspect of companionship was always very emphasized, and as a later resident of the town, I can vouch for this fact. By the time I moved to Dunwood,\n\nit was impossible to walk through the streets of Al'Khazar without being pestered for the town's semi-secret location.\n\nEnvious of the town, many halflings and non-halflings alike began making similar towns in the surrounding hills, a more known one by the name of Thistledown.\n\nI am now qualified, at this point, to tell the history from a first-person perspective. Yes, for I arrived in Dunwood during a small population boom, when the town was thriving and more inhabitants came every day. The Elders of the town were Kip Took,\n\nLen, and Gimblo. I was first escorted to the town by Gimblo, who took Bell and I for a visit. And, as I mentioned earlier, we were pursued through the streets of Al'Khazar by nosy people! Gimblo turned a corner, snapped his finger, and suddenly Bell and I\n\nwere in Dunwood (a trick I have yet to emulate perfectly). The smell of hot bread and ale wafted from the ale garden, and I could hear a halfling singing with a lyre in the distance.  Indeed, it was truly the ideal place for a halfling. Soon, the whole\n\ntown took a trip to Al'Khazar to pledge allegiance to the newly-kinged Edmund.\n\nAfter many a year of drinking, story-telling, and visitor-shoveling, the town seemed to go into a cultural decline. The Elders grew a tad sickly, and so they appointed Owen Sturdyfoot II as the Mayor to help govern. However, even his efforts did not\n\nmaintain the vitality of the town, as Brian left to become an Ascended, Biodoc passed away, Rusty moved to Al'Khazar, and Lilly was kidnapped. This decline occured in other towns, too, leaving an area surrounding Dunwood filled with empty hill-homes and\n\nthe likes. I, too, left after a call from the Druids, though the years of countryside living would have a profound influence on me for my entire life.\n\nChapter 5 - Up to Modern Day\nYears 1304-Present Day (approx. 1351)\n\nAfter many years, around 1340, I decided along with a few relatives to restore the popularity and culture of Dunwood, and so we hosted DunFest, a large festival with much merrime\n\nThere was drinking, dancing, singing, and the likes, of course. However, afterwards, it did not have the profound influence on the town population that I would have liked. And so, I went back to Malinor, only to try another festival later. Indeed, it\n\nappeared that our selective ways way long ago had a profound influence on the interest in the town, and so many gave up their hopes of moving and settled in the city. Many halflings have forgotten the joy of the simple and clean life, to my surprise.\n\nWhile I certainly traveled and was no typical halfling, the air off of Lake Dunwood in the early morn still stirs my soul like very little else does.\nAt the most recent DunFest, I did meet some fellows quite interested in culture, but none were halflin\n\n I have tried to embrace the city-dwelling halflings with open arms, but very few have answered the call.\nWith the division of Oren, I as one of the only remaining Elders of the town decided to not immediately pledge our allegiance to either faction,\n\ninstead remaining independent for some time. I did, however, set up a trade caravan of goods between Dunwood and Galahar, trying to make use of our overstocked wheat.\n\nAt the time of writing this, the state of the world grows dim as the Undead continue to win victory after victory. The future will surely deserve another tome of halfling history, perhaps more in depth,as this was merely a general overview.\n\nHopefully this has been an informative and enjoyable read. \n\nPetyr Brandybuck", ""),
        StaticBook("The Halfling Pt1", "§bFelix Stoutfoot", "The Halfling: The Quest for the Ocafluta\n\nBy Felix Stoutfoot\n\n~A True Story~\n\nDay 1\n\nToday, I set off with a few measly supplies, alongside this journal, and a wooden axe and this very rare Yew Sapling to find a nice spot.\n\nDay 2\n\nYesterday I made some nice progress outwards, until I hit the ocean. I travelled around the coast, and made it to a town, I decided to stay at the stables in town. In the dead of night, I swore I could hear the sound of hay being moved.\n\nDay 2 Night\n\nDuring tonight, I had a small flashes of dreams. Some of them were nightmares of people I loved. And then there was one in particular, a powerful warrior went up to me in a blinding light, and whispered a name to me, but I couldn't catch\n\nDay 3\n\nToday I move from the town and again into the wilderness, I plan to head to a forest full of beautiful soil. In the farthest lands, near Mastah Veren's Grove, I hear that is perfect soil for a rare Yew plant like this fella.\n\nDay 3 Night\n\nTonight, I stayed in a small grotto. Again, I slept and I had more nightmares of me failing challenges due to my size. The big warrior that I see sometimes seems to know my name....but its not my name...I still can't make it out.\n\nDay 4\n\nToday I left the quaint Grotto to head down and outwards into the valley. When I reached the Valley, I saw a large foresty area at the top of the cliffside. Tonight, I will rest up for my strength to climb the cliffside.\n\nDay 4 Night\n\nTonight, I slept up, and then I had a terrible, yet wonderful dream of Mira. I dunno what got into me. But when I woke up, I felt a breathing on me, and it was actually the licking of a Red Weasel. When I pet it though, it was prickly.\n\nDay 5\n\nToday, I climb up the mountain. I told my new friend (Who I called Samuel) to climb on my shoulder. I climbed up the first few rocks, but the stuff was too steep for my little body to handle. I decided to rest up, and fish up some food for us.\n\nDay 5 Night\n\nTonight was very quaint with Sam and I. I told him a lot about how I felt, and he seemed to nod as if he understood me. We then snuggled up and rested up our strength for tomorrow.\n\nDay 5 Night continued\n\nThe dreams kept getting worse and worse, but today. I could swear I could see the great warrior had spiky hair as he slew mighty, flying beasts. With a claymore and shield in hand, he rescued me and overcame expansive challenge\n\nDay 6\n\nAs dawn broke, Sam purred like a fox on my body. And I got up, planning my next way of attack. Today, I would try going horizontally.\n\nDay 6 Night\n\nTonight, I write this halfway up the cliffside, in a small grotto. I am resting while making a small fire in this cool cavern. Sam kept watch for any suspicious enemies.\n\nDay 6 Dreams\n\nI sleep today, and I see Mira at a lakeside with me, when all the sudden, I collapse down into the lake. As I fall into the deepest reaches of darkness....I can hear the jolly laughter of some devil, I dunno. And I hear the squealling o\n\nDay 7\n\nToday I broke out in a sweat. I dunno what was causing anything last night. I am going to reach the top today, and set up a small camp up above.\n\nDay 8\n\nI climbed up nonstop today, and through the night. The coolness of the night made it difficult. But I have made it up there to watch the dawn of Day 8. I am totally pooped as I suddenly collapse into a nap.\n\nDay 8 Dreams\n\nAs I collapse, I feel the same falling feeling as if I was letting go of her. And I can't reach out for my Uncle. The darkness is just....blank. I sometimes make out large, fiery foes in the dark.\n\nDay 8 Dreams\n\nAs I rest, I can hear a light saying \"S....Stou...\" but I can't hear. It is saying something. Before I can figure it out, a small figure appears and says \"Awaken.\"\n\nDay 14\n\nIt appears that winter has finally ended (I left during Winter). I dunno how long I was in that trance, but Surprisingly, Sam has been around, keeping watch and bringing all these flowers somehow. At least I think so.\n\nDay 15\n\nToday, I am going to plant this Yew plant. Surprisingly, it has kept its shape since I've left it. I dig a small hole, and plant it. I give a small prayer to the Yew, to become strong and hardy.\n\nDay 60\n\nThe past two months has been tedious and long. Fun times with the tree during the day, but nightmares during the night.\n\nDay 60 Night\n\nTonight, I plan to explore the darkness. I hug Sam goodnight and rest my poor eyes.\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nI explored the darkness today, the past few times, I have been seeing pictures of Her being tortured and a man cackling from doing things....I dunno what...but I just hear squeals of pain that hurt my heart.\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nI travel farther and farther through the depths, until I reach a giant red castle. I sneak into it with all my strength. The castle reeks of necromancy, and blight but the darkness already did anyways.\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nI slowly sneak through the forces to try and find any source of actual life. I stumble upon a cell soon with a Knight in a helmet, chained up and bloodied. I decide to open up the cell.\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nTo my surprise, he wakes up in an instant and I can hear a smile within the helmet. \"Well, if it isn't Stoutfoot, Son of Salmon?\" I then point at myself as he nods inside his helmet, he then removes it to show prickly, spiky hair as if\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\n-it were quills on a porcupine. \"My name is Samuel. And I am chosen to be your guardian.\" he then kneels as if I was some sorta king. Outta sort of impulse I just say, \"Rise Samuel.\" He then rises as if some sorta knight out of a book.\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\n\"I was sent out by the Three in search of Relic, it is known as a Core. Used to create a powerful, and rare instrument, barely known by Men.\" I slightly nod and just say I am searching for a friend I love.\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nWith a swift nod he just says, \"I guess our paths have crossed by the Three's Decision. Let's go now.\" He goes out of the cell, suddenly having a claymore and tower shield to match his tabard torn armor. He then slices through the near\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nThe nearest Skeleton, jumping back and forth as swift and cunning as a Fox. After a couple of foes down, we head downstairs as I ask where did he learn that? \"Anything is feasible, ya just gotta set yer mind to it.\" he says.\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nWe then arrive deep in a ritual room, full of Daemon magic, and a hooded man cackling with a crack of a whip as squeals are heard from behind. \"Let's finish this.\" I say. The man cackles while swinging a Druidic marked stone in the air\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\n\"The Core!\" Samuel says, as he charges head first into the battle. I then think of what I can do to help. And suddenly I just grapple onto the back of the man, so he can't control any of his magic. So, I suddenly felt a sharp pain in m\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\n-pain in my chest, as I see a sword coming through the Hooded man as he dissipates. I then collapse on the ground as I see the girl being taken away.\n\n\"Stoutfoot, Son of Salmon.\" is the last four words I hear.\n\nDay ???\n\nI wake up to feel water splashing on me. it is raining, and Where I see the once sapling I was planting, I see a great tall Yew plant. I then awake to see Sam at my side, nudging me to be awake and towards the Yew plant.\n\nDay ???\n\nI nod to the loyal pal, as I slowly chop down the tree with a soft respect and gaze. When the tree lands with a loud thump, I can see a Wooden Core, where it is thickest. I carve out a certain section of it. I then pray and thank the Aspects\n\nDay ???\n\nFor this wonderful gift. I then sit there, wondering what I am supposed to craft. I think hard about this, and I hear the whispers of grass as if it was saying \"Stoutfoot.\" but it wasn't.\n\nDay ???\n\nI then come up with the idea of a larger Ocarina, but with as many holes as a standard flute. As I begin to craft this, Sam nudges me and I carve in multiple Druidic symbols, like one meaning 'Courage'.\n\nDay ???\n\nI soon finish within a few days of work and toil. I painted it with light green. As I sat there I wondered what my life will be like with this new instrument. I then pack up my stuff, and start heading back a changed man.\n\nDay ???\n\nAs Stoutfoot........Son of Salmon.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Black Book", "§bThe Fallen Monk", "Dear reader,\n\nI am afraid I cannot sign this book, or it will be my doom. And should you be unfortunate enough to read this, it will be yours too.\n\nBefore I begin, let me ask you a simple question:\n\nWho has been watching us since the beginning? Who has been catering to us since mortals were first birthed upon the world? Who has been guiding and directing us our entire lives, whose presence is so common that we have learned to ignore them?\n\nThe beauty of it is as astonishing as it is terrifying. That we rely on them so dearly, and yet, pay them no heed. They walk in our shadow and we willingly allow them to guide our hand but, we do not notice them.\n\nI know this, because I am one of them.\n\nI speak of course, of the Wilven Monks. The Caretakers of every Cloud Temple to have existed.\n\nNot all of us, of course. The lesser monks have no idea. It is the ones you do not see. Have you not wondered why you never see the monks that spare us\n\nfrom death? How when we awake, they are nowhere to be seen?\n\nThey do this, because they are not monks. I do not know what they are but mortal, they are not. Why have we never stopped to wonder why we do not see them? Or how they can hold such\n\nextraordinary powers of revival, without ever taking on students? They have existed since the birth of time. And I have heard them speak.\n\nI found myself in a place I shouldn't have been through a series of mis-steps. Several unlocked doors and a\n\nstumble into a secret passage. I have heard the leaders of the Wilven Monks speaking to these entities, or perhaps one entity.\n\nAnd they do not wish life upon us as we have been lead to believe. They seek death.\n\nEach time we near the end, they pull us back to the world. They draw upon our souls each time, and feed a ravenous hunger for power. With each death, their power grows. And because we are revived, we exist to then simply die again.\n\nMy next question in the hopes of making you, dear reader, believe these words:\n\nWhy is there a way to bypass it? The monks do not revive a soul that has died by means of suicide.\n\nYou will be glad to know, or perhaps\n\ngrieved to know, I have an answer.\n\nIn the old days of Aegis, their scheme was discovered. A group of monks learned of their evil and were thus imprisoned. The monks, knowing that the only way to escape would be to commit suicide\n\nand awake in the cloud temple, did so. But the old monks could see their plan before they had finished it, and in their magical web, their unnatural hold over life and souls on our mortal plane, they simply plucked away one string. One single clause, that\n\nstopped a soul from returning to life after suicide.\n\nThe monks died, and never returned. The great secret, forever kept.\n\nBut dear reader, in case you still remain unconvinced, I have one more question\n\nfor you:\n\nWhy do we fear death? I want you to think about this one carefully. It is well-known that should we die by any means, we will return, revived at the Cloud Temple.\n\nAnd yet, in the moment, we dread the end. It is as if we are being\n\nforced to forget that the monks exist.\n\nAnd now you see how this web of lies all falls into place. We pay so little attention to the monks, and allow their power to grow, because they own our souls, and can force us to see whatever they desire.\n\nIf we lived in a world where we knew death was pointless, because we would be revived, there would be no death. No food for the monks to feed upon.\n\nWe are all playing out their carefully orchestrated plan, and even as I write this, I can feel the\n\nend approaching. I am being compelled to kill myself. Perhaps it is simply because of the horror I have learned, perhaps it really is my own decision.\n\nBut perhaps they know I have discovered them, and are pulling me closer and closer to suicide.\n\nAll I know is, it must be done. I am sorry, dear reader. For perhaps the same will now happen to you.\n\nI would pray to the Creator, but who is to say he is not the one behind it.\n\nGoodbye, dear reader.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Known Azdrazi:§0\n§0\n§0Ryder§0\n§0\n§0Hillith§0\n§0\n§0Favnir", ""),
        StaticBook("Prayer To Skygod", "§bAnnoyed Player", "\"The thing is with such requests are that we deny them straight away\" -Ragino", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sunless Day", "§bOrithur", "The Sunless Day\n-------------------\n\nWhile no truly living mortal could have witnessed the Sunless Day, after many years we have finally come to understand the truth behind what happened to the homeland of the races.\n\nAegis, we called it. The birthplace of the four brothers.\n\nWhen we fled the realm through a verge portal to a new land called Asulon, what happened to Aegis we could never have known. We as a collective species were satisfied with\n\nthis mystery for centuries. That was until, we found Mordring's Gate.\n\nI have covered Mordring's Gate and the Abyss it leads to in a variety of some of my other works, but what we learned was that the Abyss, is what is left of Aegis.\n\nSomehow, the entire continent imploded upon itself and sunk deep into the ground to form the Abyss, and from the creatures remaining in the Abyss I have learned the nature of this cataclysm - The Sunless day.\n\nIt was said to have\n\noccured on the 12th of the Amber Cold, 1355. But it was not Iblees' attack upon Aegis that caused this, no, even he could not be that powerful. What happened, was a battle unlike any other. A battle between Aenguls and Daemons - those specifically\n\ninvolved is unknown. But this writer suspects that it took place between Iblees and his loyal Daemons, against his natural enemy; Aeriel, and likely many of Aenguls.\n\nSomehow, the entities materialised upon the abandoned realm and fought it each other\n\nafter we had left. But this opens up a whole new approach to how we understand our Gods. For seldom do they make a presence on our mortal world.\n\nThe question I must beg the reader, is if they were able to wipe out a continent while it was abandoned, what\n\nis to stop them doing it while we are present? This is the first clear example of ultimate divine power - should these greater beings ever choose to make our world the gameboard of their disputes again, we may not be as so lucky to not be present at the\n\ntime. The Sunless Day is evidence that our gods are more powerful than we may have thought. They have to power to eliminate us entirely at a whim, and are evidently choosing not to. Our entire fates are determined by their disagreements.\n\nAny day could very well be our last.\n\nWe have so little freedom, it is clear now. They control everything. If fate is a true concept, then it is the property of Aenguls and Daemons, and that scares me more than any one rogue Daemon ever could.\n\nThe Sunless Day was an example, and for whatever reason, I do not believe these gods ever intended for us to know of this divine battle's existence.\n\nThey are hiding their power from us, they clearly do not desire us to know of the great power they truly\n\nhold over us. For this reason, I shall be putting this book in the restricted section of our library. \n\nThough I doubt the knowledge of this event to be particularly dangerous, I dare not work against the desires of these great\n\nentities of destruction. \nI am wise enough to know that should it be desired by creatures up above, my existence on this world will become an abrupt thing should I displease them.\n\nI have had the fortune of speaking to\n\nAenguls briefly in the past, and I do not put it past them to intervene in any of our fates.\n\nI pray we never see another Sunless Day, but allow to me laugh at the irony of who I intend to pray to.", ""),
        StaticBook("Deity Funnelling", "§bGudour", "For a great many millennia, descendants have known of the presence of Aenguls and Daemons. And, for almost as long, they have worshipped and pledged themselves to them, gaining magical abilities in return so they may further the cause of their\n\nchosen deity (or, in some cases, the Deity that had chosen them).\n\nWhat they didn't take into consideration however, is the very fact that funnelling the power of an Aengudaemon through a frail mortal vessel is\n\nbound to cause problems.\n\nJust as funnelling the power of the Void causes a weakness in Voidal Mages, so does funnelling the power of a Deity, though the results are often specific to how the power\n\nis funnelled and how often it is funnelled.\n\nAs a Voidal Mage taps into the unlimited potential of the Void, they are bound to suffer the side effects of harnessing this power.\n\nThis is due to the Void being a foreign power, one which descendant bodies are not made to funnel.\n\nIn this case, continued and frequent use of Voidal Magics causes physical degradation, often making master mages\n\nfrail and thin.\n\nIn a similar manner, harnessing and funnelling the power of an Aengudaemon causes a similar stress on the mortal coils of the Descandants, as the mortal coil is not made to withstand such\n\npower.\n\nAs stated before, the effects of this power vary greatly. It has been seen that Druids find themselves largely sueptible to madness due to the continuous harnessing of their Aspects' powers,\n\nwhilst their bodies are left completely unchanged.\n\nInversely, those utilising Tahariae's boons are mentally sound, though they are susceptible to incredible pains in limbs, muscles and organs if the\n\nboon is overused, courtesy of the power flowing through their body.\n\nMuun Priests grow blind upon excessive use of Moongazing, and Shamans put themselves at the mercy of spirits such as Ixli, Ikuras,\n\nor even spirits of mental instability if they are not cautious with their abilities or over-exhaust themselves.\n\nFar more examples exist, but the nature of this phenomenon remains the same;\n\nPractitioners of deific magics find themselves negatively affected in some way, be it mentally, physically, spiritually or more.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lie Of Xan", "§bOrithur", "The Lie Of Xan\n\nXan, the aengul of guardianship and order, was not there to guard us when the Golden Lance were felled. He turned his back on us, like he has done to so many before. We were fanatics, and we were blind to his deciet until\n\nit was too late.\n\nWhen one mentions an Aengul, most would assume it to be a loving, benevolent force. Xan however, was anything but benevolent.\n\nBy the will of Xan, creatures that may have been spared or\n\nsaved an unjust death, were to be purged. Anything that was not in his eyes 'pure' of essence, was simply another target, another obstacle to destroy.\n\nWhile many may even agree that to purge the world's impurities would be a great\n\nbenefit, impurity takes many forms.\n\nDuring my service of the Golden Lance, by the will of Xan we were ordered to burn down a remote village that bore dragon idols. We did as commanded, and none survived. Men, women and children died that day -\n\nthe Aengul Xan, does not comprehend mercy, nor understand any value on life.\n\nTypical of an immortal, to place descendant life so low. Xan is not a person, he is a machine, a cog wound series of certainties, dealing only in brutal, unforgiving\n\nabsolutes. Those who stand against him, are destroyed. It matters not whether they be a dark creature, a dragon, or your comman man, to defy Xan is to defy order, and to defy order is to die.\n\nFor you see, Xan's use of the word\n\n'order' is in itself a great insult to the entire concept of it. Xan does not preach order, he preaches control.\n\nHe disguises his misdeeds with terms that descendants value highly. He is a master manipulator that is capable of brainwashing\n\nanyone that falls into his fold.\n\nAllow me to put his manipulative evil into words more easily digestable:\n\nI was a Harbinger of Setherien. Setherien corrupted and took over my mind and psyche almost entirely,\n\nbut I was able to break free. I was able to see the wrong I was doing and after many years of servitute under the creature, abandon it.\n\nI served far many more years under Xan and his Golden Lance, and thoughts of betrayl or abandonment\n\nhad not once crossed my mind. He had ensared us all with violent efficiency. Each day, we did not work toward a better world, we built a world in Xan's image, a world that Xan could control.\n\nAt least Setherien was honest with his intentions, Xan's evil\n\ntakes on the form of a companion, a fellow that stands to protect you.\n\nPart of me admires it, for his scheme was so complex and so twisted that even to this day his evil goes unnoticed. Another part of me thinks that the reason Xan did not\n\ncome to our protection when we were felled by Setherien, was that we, the Golden Lance, knew him the best. We were the one uncertainty in his game. We had done so much in his name, and one day, perhaps one day soon, we may have realised his evil.\n\nAnd thus, very conviniently, the Golden Lance arrived to meet a creature that was more powerful than even the Aengul Xan himself could have anticipated, and suddenly, we were no longer a problem.\n\nIt is my sincere belief that the Aengul very much wished\n\nto be rid of us.\n\nI urge you reader, to find the servants of Xan. Speak to them, ask them of their intentions, and watch them smile with glee as they preach unto you the holy words of their leader. But, think not of the words themselves, for that is how\n\nhe worms himself into your mind. Think on the actions that these words entail.\n\nHis guardianship is a front, to make you believe him an ally. His order is control, so that we may do his bidding, and very gradually increase his influence over our\n\nworld.\n\nI do not believe that Xan is an Aengul at all. And dear reader, I am old. I have seen so much horror, so many battles. I have seen gods clash swords and new worlds arise and fall. I bear the world's largest hold of knowledge that\n\nlikely will ever exist. So please, take my vast experience as my word, when I tell you Xan is a Daemon.\n\nThere is nothing good about the Aengul, if one takes the time to read into his history on the world, it is a series of misery and death, with each\n\nloss of life blamed on a conviniently common enemy, and each time, he grows more powerful and gains more influence.\n\nNo Daemon could ever hope to achieve what Xan has achieved. And he does it, because we let him. Because he has lied to so many and\n\nconvinced us all that he is the great protector.\n\nWe are so blind. He makes enemies for us, and joins us in defeating them, and our adoration for him only grows.\n\nXan has become more powerful than Iblees,\n\nhe is the true Arch-Daemon. And I do pray that the day will never come, that we as a species realise it.\n\nBecause by then, it will be too late to stop him.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dusty Book", "§bUnknown", "[!]The entire page has been torn out.\n\nEntry one\nI figured I start writing this all down, help keep track of everything and to ease my thoughts.  They're alwats swirling in my mind as I feel around for something else to investigate, leading me to forgetting small\n\ndetails.\n\nMost names in this book are altered for the safety of the poor afflicted souls that I care for.  Not everything in this book is going to be on the same topic.\n\nSeveral years ago, a dear friend of mine that I shall call\n\nLudleth opened up to me that he had been cursed with a Shade.  I hadn't known very much on the magic/curse at the time, so I wasn't able to provide much help at the time.\n\nAfter a few days of digging around, I discovered that the Shade's curse can\n\nbe cured by a powerful cleric, but only if its found in its early stages.\n\nThe Shade supposedly grows stronger as time continues on and it turns less of an annoyance and more of a tormenter to the host.  A different newly cursed friend mentioned\n\nthat he heard only voices in his sleep and experienced frequent nightmares.\n\nLudleth looked awfully tired whenever I saw him, along with acting rather paranoid.  He said he kept seeing shadows on the corners of his eyes that wouldn't be there if he l\n\ndirectly at them.  He said he felt as if he were always being followed and often heard a voice in his head, a cruel one.\n\nI know that it is too late to save Ludleth, all I can do is make life easier for him to ease him through his suffering.  I am aw\n\nthat there is a chance of him exploding one day, breaking; the Shade will take over and I will need flee until he can regain control of himself again.  I understand any violent actions made won't be from him, but from the monster inside him.\n\nEntry Two\n[!] The entire page has been scribbled out completely.\n\n[!] This page has been scribbled out as well.\n\nreason was because Albert was \"annoying\" to him.  He was also the one to give Albert the curse, and perhaps with Ludleth as well since he recalled who he was when I described him.\n\nLudleth has said this elf kind once you know him, but I'd still prefe\n\nkeep my distance and remain unnoticed by him.  Another thing which I find rather unsettling and peculiar is that Ludleth refers to this unknown elf as a father-like figure along with never speaking his name. \n\nLudleth has said to me that this elf is\n\nto be helping him in learning how to use the dark tendrils of a Shade.  He says it's at least one upside from all of this mess and that he wishes to do good.  I still hope he manages through all of this.\n\nEntry Three\nI had discovered an old journal of mine from back in Vailor.  I noticed a few entries involved my discoveries of these frozen ruins north of my old tower in Carnatia, which used to be a duchy in the Old Orenian Empire.\n\nThese have caught my interest, the enteries and notes.  They may be of use for me in the nearing future.\n\nI came across a tomb burrowed into the mountainside north of my old home and there were engravings reading this,\n\n\"Herein lies Dralazar, Herald of Xion, Lord of Torment.  We are born by the dark; Made men by the dark; Undone by the Dark; We fear the Old Dark.\"\n\nAnother ominous finding was within one of the mountain peaks north-west from the tomb.\n\nAfter reaching the top, I discovered a gaping hole which formed into a dark stairway that swirled deeper into the hard earth.  If I hadn't carried candles with me, I would have been in pure darkness.  A ladder\n\nwaited for me at the bottom of the steps, and when I carefully climbed down it, I saw a source of light in that cold, dark place.\n\nFollowing it, I came into a cavern-like room with a sanguine altar.  Words were written above it, in the stone, saying,\n\n\"Aknu'gul, Remniscent of the Old Fire; an unbeknownst power reborn- his vessel, his will, his herald of ebon.  The abyss will endure.  We. Fear. The. Old. Dark.\"\n\nI have heard and see the phrase mentioning the Old Dark several times in my time.\n\nI wonder if the Old Dark is to mean anything about the Abyss or who/what may lurk within.\n\nI plan to try to learn more soon.\n\nEntry Four\nI have met the elf who cursed my friends.  I have not learned his name, and if I ever do, I will keep from writing in here for the safety of myself, my friends, and him.\n\nThe elf expressed how he didn't like giving others the curse due to how terrible it was, when I questioned him.  But had also said that he wasn't entirely a good person, and continued to give it those who seemed fit for it, and who asked him.\n\nI understand how he'd say that with Albert, but Ludleth?  It can't possibly be true that he'd ask for something so terrible and dark to happen to him.  I plan to bring this up to him the next time I visit him.\n\nI had grown worried for Ludleth, he seemed to be getting worse.  He moved out from his old home and into another. \n\nWhen I visited, everything within was destroyed.  It was as if a fight had gone on in there.  Ludleth claimed\n\nthat it was the shade's doing since he doesn't remember how the destruction came to be.\n\nBut the elf had given him some amulet, saying it will help him with the voices.  He had also shown him how to use this \"#/-=\" in front of me.\n\nI suppose it's what the tendrils are, since a thick darkness began to form around their hands when they practiced it.  And their eyes turned as dark as pitch.  I was terrified through all of this, to be truthful, but I feel a bit at ease, I guess?\n\nI know more on this whole deal and I'm feeling more hopeful that Ludleth will make it through this and that he won't harm anyone or himself if he can control this.\n\nEntry Three\nRemember \"Siegwald of Gelt\"\n\n6th of The Grand Harvest, 1609\nA strange altar I had discovered  hidden beneath the rather enigmatic mountains north-east of Sutica appears to have been broken.  I found a note beside it, reading -\n\n\"The Uzg follows you without relent. - Gijaak'Raguk\"\n\nPerhaps if things go silent for me for a bit, I can try to distract myself by investigating this.\n\n5th of The Sun's Smile, 1609\nI've started going on my walks again.  They help take my mind off of things and are a way for me to get out of the #[-#/,,. [!]The rest is all unreadable.\n\nWhile I was on a walk today, I came across a peculiar thing in the Enchanted Forest beside Haria on Asul.  A large, wooden door was discovered on the side of one of the mountains.  Past it, is a ruined cavern-like hall leading up to a curious and rather\n\nornate door.\n\n[!] The rest of the book appears to be unfinished.", ""),
        StaticBook("Soul Trees", "§bUnknown", "There was a great and powerful Druid. He walked the wood with his gnarled staff and ancient wisdom, and with each step his energies encouraged the flora around him to flourish. He was a true soul of the forest; his great longing not to live\n\nin the company of others yet to spend an eternity serving the Aspects of Nature in any way he could.\nThis Druid was clever-his mind was sharp and he knew that his body was just a vessel for his soul which connected all nature in some\n\nway. With this in mind he traveled the forests, the plains, the rolling green hills spread with verdure, and he found a Sacred Grove, filled with the natural energies of the world, and he picked a sapling from a most ancient tree.\nHe took this\n\nsapling in hand, and harnessing the power of his Druidic arts, he began to grow it, first binding his hands, binding his arms,legs, wrapping around him as if a spindly, gnarled, oaken rope. As the elder Druid let out a final gasp, a cry to the Aspects,\n\nhe pierced his very body with the roots of this tree, and with the last of his effort drove the roots into the ground, stained with his blood and sucking out the tasty nutrients of the earth.\nThere was a great tree in his place, gnarled,\n\nbeautiful.\nFor many weeks, even months this tree stood, tall, resilient, silent, until one quiet morn with the rise of the sun-its great trunk began to bow outward, and like wax from a candle, or a great boiling ball of water something\n\nbegan to take shape. The nearby wildlife did not retreat, rather they came to bear witness to such a momentous event-it was a miracle of nature. The boiling blob took shape, and bare before the wildlife stood the ancient Elf, his complexion that of\n\nbark yes but still very much alive. And this, is the ancient and tightly kept secret of the Soul Tree.\n~The Druii’ithirn, Arcanum of Ancient Secrets", ""),
        StaticBook("Drakaar List", "§bOrithur", "It is my advice that the reader does not pursue a Drakaar. Though they may tempt with knowledge and power, their intentions can only ever be destructive to both servant and enemy alike. This book will be stored in the Restricted Section.\n\n-Orithur\n\nSetherien:\n\nPerhaps the most widely known Drakaar to have lived. He was responsible for the Harbinger Wars of Anthos, a long war that devastated the continent.\n\nHis desires were simple;\n\ndestruction and malice. \nHe grew into his power after escaping an expedition of dwarves digging beneath their city of Kal'Karik.\n\nHis sister was slain there, but he escaped to be later encountered in Anthos.\n\nSetherien's appearance is disturbing in both his forms. A collosal black drake in dragon form, and a twisted red and black robed figure with unnatural piercing yellow eyes in humanoid form.\n\nSetherien was slain by\n\nthe Order of the Golden Lance at the end of Anthos' timeline, releasing his servants, the Harbingers, of his will.\n\nChysteria:\n\nChysteria was Setherien's sister, slain as a fledgling upon hatching in the dwarven city of Kal'Karik.\n\nShe never achieved a human form, and was a tiny creature when slain.\n\nAzdromoth:\n\nEasily the oldest of all Dragonkin, and I know this, because he was the first. He was the original Dragaar, and the first to become corrupted by Iblees.\n\nHe claimed the title of 'Arch-Drakaar',\n\nconsidering himself the firstborn child of Dragur himself.\n\nHe was awakened from a prison by circumstances unknown to me, and fate saw it that his reign of terror was brief.\n\nI met the Drakaar twice, and what I found unusual about him was that there was no madness in his mind (a trait common in Drakaar).\n\nThe creature was calm and calculated, and never once posed any danger to me.\n\nThe fate of the creature now is unknown, I have heard reports that by some act of divine intervention, he was imprisoned once more.\n\nAnother report from a close friend, tells me that he has gone into hiding.\n\nThe latter report scares me significantly, it is not for a Drakaar to go into hiding, and if he has, it is because he is waiting.\n\nMordring:\n\nMordring is the ruler of the Abyss, the remnants of Aegis. While incredibly magically potent, physically the Abyss has torn him asunder.\n\nI do not believe he may frequently leave his\n\nhome of the Abyss, known locally as the Sunless Sanctum.\n\nI also had the fortune of meeting this Drakaar, and while his mind is as warped as I would expect, he bares very little threat to our world.\n\nHis focus remains mostly on preserving his race of Dragons, and not on the destruction of mortals.\n\nI know for a fact he and his drake servant Satar are still alive.\n\nMordring in his dragon form appears as an enormous skeletal drake, his physical form is a blend of grey flesh and bone.\n\nHis physical corruption is so deep he cannot hold a pure disguise, and will always remain distorted.\n\nDrakaar are ultimately killing-machines, though I have discovered some to be more than hospitable.\n\nRegardless, one should not pursue a Drakaar. From firsthand experience, let me tell you that there are things far\n\nworse than death.\n\nAnd the Drakaar are capable of all of them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragur Library", "Wretched", "The History And Tale Of The Library Of Dragur\n                 -Orithur\n-------------------\n\nThe Library of Dragur stands today as a monument to the betterment of our world, no library may ever hope to match its vast expanse of knowledge across\n\na variety of topics from ancient history to modern magic. The library continues to grow each day, as more and more of the world's Descendants discover the blossoming hope that is the Library of Dragur. As its size grows, so does its influence and\n\npopularity. More take notice, more come to its halls, more donations are left. But, this was not always the way.\n\nI am the co-founder of the Library of Dragur, my name is Orithur, and this is my account of my dearest Library's journey:\n\nIt was during the early days of the Descendants arrival to Athera, that I found myself particularly lost, and without purpose. As a fallen Harbinger of the now deceased Drakaar known as Setherien, I was immediately shunned by every civilised culture upon\n\nthe landmass. Many of my kin were driven to suicide, and those that were not either went into deep hiding, or became consumed with the hatred against them, and went on blood thirsty rampages.\n\nThis of course, did myself no aid in trying\n\nto find a new place to fit in, and a new purpose to have. \n\nIt should be known that I served as Setherien's keeper of tomes, and before that, I existed as the book keeper within the Order of the Golden Lance. Being a librarian, has always been\n\nwithin my nature. And it was this inherent nature toward the preservation, that did draw the most unlikely of friends to my path.\n\nThis friend, just so happened to be a Dragaar named Aedrex. For those unaware, Dragaar act, to the best of their abilities,\n\nas guardians of the Descendants. They seek to collect and preserve knowledge in order to further better the descendant races - thus this remains as our library's primary goal and focus.\n\nAedrex recruited me, and showed me his very well\n\nconcealed home. It was a vast empty hall with many empty shelves. He told me, he intended to fill them, and that he would be honoured if I were to assist him on this great task.\n\nI could never have anticipated what this quest would mean for not only\n\nmyself, but the world. Almost immediately we began to make contact with all known nations, and began to acquire copies of books scattered across the realm. We delved deep into ruins, we scavaged through cities that had fallen to war to salvage their\n\nlibraries. These cities had of course been looted, but none thought of the value within the library.\n\nWe began to make significant political ties, and to this day hold these ties to various nations and their leaders, which greatly assists in the\n\npreservation of the library. One such political tie was Tristen Tresery, who later became the Prince of Malinor.\n\nYou see as our shelves expanded, the workload became too much for Aedrex and I to manage by ourselves. We recruited\n\nscholars to assist our efforts, I had even tailored a unique red uniform for them to wear which, to my deep surprise they did.\n\nOur numbers expanded, and thus we became the Order Of Dragur. However, we still very much remained a secretive\n\norder. Very few knew of the existence of the hidden library, located behind a complex hidden door, deep underground. We did this out of fear, our order was young and there existed dangerous forces in the world that would surely tear it all apart should we\n\nbe naive enough to reveal our knowledge to the world. It is only now that I write this that I realise how ridiculous that sentiment was, but perhaps it did do us good.\n\nWe continued to grow. First to one hundred books, then two hundred, then three\n\nhundred. We ventured and explored the realm, plundering dungeons, recording events, filling in the gaps in history that had been lost or neglected, and we did this with such pride and such purpose. Never before had I felt a joy as pure as recording and\n\ncollecting our broken little world into books and tomes, all organised neatly upon shelves.\n\nEven in these early days of the order, we had already become the largest known library to ever exist throughout the history of the Descendant\n\nraces. But the title meant very little to us, and still we continued to grow and expand.\n\nEven deeper below the library in the library vault, we kept a large Dragaar's Lexicon, belonging of course to Aedrex. This, absorbed all the knowledge upon the\n\nshelves so that in the event that the books were lost, the library would not be. Also in this vault, we safeguarded several powerful objects. And these objects, were Dragon Eggs.\n\nAedrex, upon entering our realm did so with seven Dragon Eggs that he hoped\n\nto safeguard and nurture until they may hatch. So they sat in our vault, growing slowly. Dragons are some of the most powerful and intelligent creatures in the known realms, it is no surprise that they grow very slowly, and take a significant amount of\n\ntime to hatch. But for the longest time, they were safe.\n\nSome time into the order's existence, Aedrex and I found ourselves in council with the Aengul of Order and Guardianship, Xan. There was a new threat to the realm, and this threat\n\nwas the Arch-Drakaar named Azdromoth. We communicated with the Greater Entity with his clerical and paladin patrons, and this was not the first time our order found itself in contact with an Aengul. \nThe Aengul who called itself 'Wyrvun' made several\n\nvisits to our library for what I believe to be purely curiousity reasons. Ours was a passtime for even Gods, it would seem.\n\nAnd so it seemed that nothing could go wrong, that we could only ever continue to progress and expand. But then disaster struck.\n\n\nWe had drawn the attention of Aenguls, we should have expected the same of Daemons. A Daemon who remains unknown in name or purpose, attacked our library with peculiar spectral entities. We defended the library valiently, and were joined by\n\nthe paladins of Xan to fend off the invaders. Alas, Aedrex could not transform into his enormous Dragon form without destroying the library.\n\nThe battle was destructive, and took place within the library halls itself. Fires raged, pillars toppled, the\n\nroof began to cave in. The library was destroyed.\n\nOur biggest concerns of course, were the Dragon eggs and the Lexicon. Both were thankfully unharmed but the vault would not stand for long. Another force recognised this, and\n\nXan himself pulled the Dragon eggs out of the library and into his realm, where one of his patrons named Herun Athna informs me they still exist today. Aedrex also managed to safely transport the Lexicon to a nearby cave system, but this attack had...\n\nChanged him.\n\nWe suspended the duty of the scholars and sent them out into the world. We closed off the entrance to the secretive library for good, and Aedrex saw that the Lexicon remained in a safe, inaccessible location. After this was done, Aedrex came\n\nto me with a heavy heart. With the attack, the threat of unknowns and the obvious threat of the Arch-Drakaar, Aedrex told me he was leaving, likely forever. Where to, he never did specify. Another land, another realm, I could not say for certain. All I\n\nknew was that he left me with the Lexicon, and a duty to see the Library of Dragur not only restored, but improved.\n\nAnd it was in Vailor, that I saw to the construction of an enormous structure that would house the knowledge stored within the giant\n\nlexicon. I met many troubles, many groups approached me with distrust, the repuation I still held with certain key political figures was the only thing allowing me to do this.\n\nOf course, this time the library was to exist to the public. I had a theory\n\nthat when people saw the library's potential, the inherent good within people would allow it to flourish, and they would assist it. Much to both my relief and joy, I was correct.\n\nI began to recruit scholars once more, and very soon the old magic\n\nof the library returned to my hollow frame. I began to feel at home once more. It could never replace the sensation of family I felt around Aedrex, but it felt good regardless.\n\nWe began to go on expeditions, we recruited scholars as dedicated as I was to\n\ncollecting and documenting knowledge. We wrote much, we made a great number of friends, we formed new political ties. Our collection continued to grow on mostly donation alone from the comman man. I have now grown very close to the scholars working here\n\nthe longest.\n\nBut again we are not without our troubles. Hostility has arisen between myself personally and the Holy Orders that I once served under, and once aided us. To draw their attention away from the library so that their rage may not be\n\ntaken out upon it, for some time I left the library to go in hiding. It is only recently from writing this that I make my return, believing the dust to have now settled. However I now understand that my active presence in the public eye of the library\n\nwill only ever cause chaos. I have therefore left it in the very capable hands of my most trusted Scholar, and now Librarian: Aluuvia. Or, Lyeth, as she now goes by.\n\nMy role in the library exists in the background now, until such a time that\n\nI believe it safe for my presence on the library floor to become commonplace.\n\nBut all of this aside, the library continues to flourish and grow. We now near close to a thousand unique books upon our shelves, and our library's reputation has grown so\n\nsignificantly. Teachers and students alike of many paths of study flock to our halls for a taste of its knowledge - we continue the work of Aedrex most efficiently.\n\nBut I miss him dearly.\n\nThere exist unsolved mysterious of the\n\nlibrary, such as, what was the creature that destroyed the original library, what was its goal, and will it attack again? What will Xan do with Aedrex's Dragon Eggs? Will they be returned to me, will he destroy them, or simply guard them for all eternity?\n\nAnd of course, where is Aedrex now? I gave up praying for his return some years ago. His duty upon our world was concluded, he is the reason this library stands today, it would not surprise me if I were to never see him again.\n\nThe Library of Dragur will\n\nstand strong throughout the events, ages and realms to come. It will remain a beacon of peace and study for all for centuries more, of this I am sure. We will have further troubles ahead no doubt, but we must never forget that no matter what, it will\n\nsurely be worth it.\n\n- Orithur, Paladin of the Golden Lance, Harbinger of Setherien, and co-founder of the Library of Dragur.", ""),
        StaticBook("A slim grimoire", "§bUnknown", "ＦＡＬＬＥＭ´ＲＯＣＨ\n       ＢＨＡＫＴＡＬ\n         III\n  III     I     III\n   I   I  I  I   I\n   IIIIII I IIIIII\n     I  II II  I\n     II  III  II\n      IIIIIIIII\n        IIIII\n        IIIII\n        I I\n\n           [!]\nAn odd grimoire with tattered black leather\ncover sits in your hands. By the looks of it, it probably has something to do with magic, but the entirety of the book is written in an odd language that aches the head of those who can't r\n\nHazk,\nmerin'gnu vegaati zu'nokion. \n\nRe'nokion talsh vokarl\nya'pelosr therthe'pelosr-bhaktalserthek-unkra zu'gathan.\n\nE\nOdurnur blothr zu'kraemsal\n\nDu\nPelosr'basular koneg\nqsuzph'dvemd\n\nDo'nekaro kuram savurr'zu bhakthal.\n\n[]  []  []  []  []  []  []\n\nKraemsal lerikah odurnur ubyz'fikt koneg vurrsht-chelion\nil do'jhorvastur \nsavurr'vegaati qsuzph'dvemd\n\naza uvot, do'varsku -\nO'ag'vokarl\n\nE\nDo'odurnur bhatti'dvemd\n\nDu\nDo'kree haurz qsuzph\nkon kreoz'bhaktal\n\n           [!]\n  Pictures have been\n  drawn alongside the\n  instruction.\n\n            [!]\nThe first picture seems to have an odd lump of rock.\n\nIn the second one, some sort of hollow figure has been molded from the ore.\n\nVe\nDo'kree thur'hadan\nfhi al'kraemsal\n\n   o  -->  ö\n   O        []/\n\neg zmask, a'kyoni Kha.\n\nCul\npelosr'basular koneg'qsuzph\n\nZin\nDo'infinst qsuzph egodar burz'fhi yatha\n\n\n     Undere dayn!\n\nqsuzph lerikah ezg saiz undere aldunr lerikah al'kraemsal.\n    ö \n  \\[] -> ,;     ✔\n\n            [!]\nAnother set of pictures are on the side. In the first, the figure is made to resemble a kharajyr.\n\nIn the second one, the kharajyr shrinks considerably in size.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n             ☬\n\n\n\n\n\n                   -1496\n                   - Z.C.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragaar List", "§bOrithur", "To prevent a breach of Dragaar secrecy, this tome is to be stored in the restricted section of the Dragur Library.\n\nThe information in the following pages may put hiding Dragaar in significant danger of discovery.\n\n-Orithur\n\nTaynei'Hiylu:\n\nTaynei is considered one of the oldest Dragaar, sharing a strong bond to the elves (or perhaps druids, discovered texts on her are unclear). \n\nWhile original sightings\n\nwere from Aegis, there are reports from further sightings from the Druids in Axios.\n\nHer mortal disguise is known to be a wood elven woman, and her current whereabouts are unknown.\n\nThere is rumour that\n\nshe has fallen prey to a magical binding spell that has, in some manner, sealed her from further interacting with the world.\n\nAlas, we have no means to confirm this.\n\nAruzond:\n\nAruzond, otherwise known as 'The Warden' interacted with the descendant races during the Harbinger Wars of Anthos, appearing to directly warn us of the threat Setherien posed.\n\nI myself spoke to\n\nthe Dragaar on occasion long after the events of Anthos concluded, my last sighting of him was in Vailor.\n\nAruzond takes upon the guise of an old man with a long, tattered grey cloak, appearing human.\n\nThough I have not seen him in some time and have not been able to contact him again, I believe he is still alive and in hiding.\n\nGudour:\n\nGudour has been cleansed of his Drakaar nature, and returned to the state of Dragaar. This is the only instance of purifying a dragon to have been successful.\n\nGudour poses as a\n\nchampion of man, from what I have learned this belief is rooted in his creator's original intentions for Dragon-kind; to rule over man.\n\nAfter causing much trouble during his early Drakaar years, Gudour became\n\nthe reason for the forming of the Order of the Golden Lance.\n\nHis appearance has changed frequently, and his current whereabouts are unknown.\n\nThe Dragaar had a reputation for pride and battle,\n\nthus it is my belief that the Dragaar was slain in battle.\n\nHis personality does not align with one that would go into hiding.\n\nAedrex:\n\nAedrex was a Dragaar that first revealed his identity to me in Athera, and with him we founded the Library of Dragur, initially just to expand his horde of knowledge.\n\nHe could be noticed by his vibrant green eyes, brown beard, and oak brown cloak he would wear. Should one peer under the cloak, he also had a small pair of grey horns.\n\nAedrex was one of the few Dragaar to actually reveal his\n\nidentity to various people, which is ultimately what resulted in his downfall.\n\nAedrex drew the attention of the Arch-Drakaar, Azdromoth. Assuming the reader knows how dangerous Drakaar\n\nare to Dragaar, it is clear why he decided to flee.\n\nAfter his library was destroyed, he vanished back into hiding, clearly learning a valuable lesson.\n\nHis collection grew into the Library of Dragur,\n\nand while I am sure he would be proud to see what it has become, I do not believe I will see him again.\n\nAs far as I know, he could be watching us right now.\n\nIf I had not made it clear already, Dragaar are a species out of place in our world.\n\nThey were destined to be powerful caretakers, but Iblees' corruption over them has meant they must remain in\n\nhiding, or risk becomming Drakaar.\n\nTruth be told, we only know of the Dragaar that have revealed themselves to us, which for their own safety they tend to avoid.\n\nThere could be any\n\nnumber of Dragaar, roaming out streets, watching over us, living in seclusion. \n\nAs long as their ego does not get the better of them, they are masters of hiding. And it is our duty to them, to ensure their secrecy remains intact.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Scrollcase", "§bUnknown", "The Scrollcase\nof Balance\nand well-kept,\neasily lost\nSecrets.\n\n\n\nA gift from one\ngood friend to another.\n\nAs we used to say;\n\n\"Some secrets are better off lost than left in the hands of the inept and the unlearned.\"\n\nWith that in mind, I've had this made for your personal use.\n\nI know there are doubtless a countless number of things you might place within. Whatever you use this for, take care not to place anything within that you would not mind losing to the aforementioned.\n\nThe case is a tad tricky to open once sealed.\n\nYou'll note the water and magma in opposite ends of the case's seals. Once you put the whole thing together, you'll find those two elements won't be as well confined as previously.\n\nSeal the case appropriately and the two ends will twist into position aligning with the inner tubes which connect to the interior case, where whatever parchment you wish to safekeep should be placed.\n\nIt should only take a day or so for enough pressure to build within, by the function of the opposing temperature ends, that the scrollcase will become pressure-sealed, either cap becoming irremovable.\n\nFear not! Opening the case again is possible if you're clever enough (and I know you are!). That is, opening it without damaging the precious parchment perched within. This is where the glass tubes within come into play.\n\nIn order to open the case once more, you will need to release the pressure on either end, allowing that end's cap to be unscrewed and removed. Again, you will need an extra pair of hands, or several, for this!\n\nTo release the pressure, you must lower the gates retaining the flow of whichever element, water or lava, on both available tubes. The respective element will then begin travelling down the tube, relieving the pressure enough to allow opening.\n\n You may have just noticed all the tubes lead into the interior case holding the parchment.\n\nYou didn't think it was that simple, did you?\n\nHaaa.\n\nIn order to safely remove the parchment, you'll also need to keep either element from getting into the interior chamber, and prevent it from ruining whatever secrets you may have chosen to hide within.\n\n Happy Keeping!\n\nTo those who may be seeking to open that contained within, take heed.\n\nSome secrets maintain their status for just cause.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Change", "§bThe Old Man", "I found myself sitting there, staring into the dark pit, my heart racing and my brow covered in sweat due to the extreme conditions within the nether. I was encased in some sort of atmospheric bubble which allowed me to maneuver through the nether,\n\nunharmed by its toxic effects. As I looked around, ichor and lava encompassed the surrounding region. It was one of the most beautiful and terrifying places I have ever laid my eyes upon.\n\nThe mere presence of the area itself was breathtaking, yet belittling due to the fact that the sheer power that Iblees’ realm possessed would make any mortal feel inferior. The fortress itself was incredible and the first time\n\nI walked through it with the Undead Overlord Sprat, he showed me around its various rooms and corridors but was obviously focused on the task at hand. He led me to the spot of the pit that would soon change my life forever.\n\nWhen looked into it, I could feel myself having a doubt here and there as to what I was about to give up, life. After conversing with Sprat, I finally made my decision to serve Iblees and become a conduit of which he would use to complete his mission.\n\nI looked into the pit one last time then back to Sprat who had a stern look on his visage before nodding once, so I took a deep breath, and began my first steps forward into a new life. I took upon the name Seraphim the Damned\n\nwhich I would become known as among my fellow ‘brothers’ and mortals of the realm. This domain of Iblees was to be my new home, a safe haven for those who were beyond death… Then my chance to unleash terror on the realm of Athera began… As I look back\n\nupon that experience that occurred so long ago, I can’t help but think that if I could do it all over again, I wouldn’t change a thing.\n\n~Signed \nSeraphim the Damned, Undead of the Chaos Sect.", ""),
        StaticBook("Paladinos", "§bUnknown", "Ianril Waveharp\nLeric Tresery\nRyder Athna \nIbar of Xan\nVailoen Winterleaf\n\nCelairil Aurela Alfakyn\n\nZafirah of Xan", ""),
        StaticBook("Poetic Vision", "§bOrithur", "The following is an unusual poem experienced by Kharajyr Moongazers and Orc Shaman Farseers. We can assume it was something powerful, to be able to stretch across multiple forms of magic, but its purpose is unknown:\n\nOrigins all but absolute,\nweave not past my own dispute.\n\nStrands of fate now do entwine,\nboth mind and soul are my design.\n\nSafeguard not my children near,\nmine is the vessel of love and fear.\n\nPity not the weight of strain,\nI do this time and time again.\n\nFruits of life do beg my pardon,\nroaming astray my endless garden.\n\nMy will sees metal turn to rust,\nand men grow tall from all but dust.\n\nFind me not in book nor tome,\nFor I'm the breath of life and home.\n\nForge noble beasts and kings that reign,\nI do this time and time again.\n\nHammer to the highest hand,\nfather to his faithful land.\n\nMaker of the lurks so foul,\nlover to the subtle cowl.\n\nBlessed to the Gods below,\ncrops of life are what I sow.\n\nLight is the sun, dark is the grain,\nI do this time and time again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Book Of Endings", "§bDoomsayer", "The Book\n        Of Endings\n-------------------\nOnce shall he come, with fire and brimstone. His name shall we never forget, for he is the ultimate enemy with a fate entwined with mortals. He will show us his hate, and from it we will learn hate.\n\nTwice, shall he come. To show us he is undying. The eternal enemy of life beyond life, undeath most solace. We will be arrogant to him, and he will be driven back again. We inherit his resistance, but it is a quality that shall expire.\n\nThrice, shall he come. The lord of endings is he. The king of fire with his ever patient eye, to be known by many names but one name above all. Iblees will return again, and an ending he will bring. One fit for the twisted souls of Mortals.\n\nLet them know of his coming, and all will be at an end. To forget the enemy is the only way to defeat it. Let the knowledge die, or only memories shall remain.\n\nKorvad, Absyyl, Daemon, Curser, Iblees.\n\n\n\n\n           ----\n         /       \\\n         |   [ ]   |\n         \\       /\n           ----\n\n*The Eye Of Iblees is sketched onto the last page*", ""),
        StaticBook("Frostos", "§bUnknown", "Yuln - Red headed High Elf usually seen in a white dress.\n\nArelin - Black hair, Adunian. Silver/Grey eyes. \n\nAlera - Black robes, silver hair, High Elf, purple eyes.\n\nDiana - One green eye, one blue eye. Silver hair, High Elf.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Fjarriauga", "§bThe Veiled Scribe", "Legends of the Volsung - The Fjarriauga\n\nOf all the tales and legends of the Volsungs, the Fjarriauga are the darkest. In Skjoldier, homeland of the Volsung family, stories of the Fjarriauga are told to scare misbehaving children into submission at n\n\nThey are said to be wicked ice spirits, taking on the guise of fair and innocent maidens to draw their prey to them. Young boys and girls alike are warned against venturing into the forests where they dwell, lest they are never to be seen again.\n\nIt is said that Kriemhild, the first Fjarriauga, was a woman abandoned at the altar by her betrothed. Broken-hearted she stumbled out into a snowstorm, collapsing amidst the swirling snow and frozen drifts. As she waited for death, Old Father Winter, one\n\nof the Volsung gods, discovered and took pity upon her. He leaned in and gave her the wedding kiss she longed for, transforming her into a vengeful - and powerful - ice spirit.\n\nWhile Fjarriauga are malicious creatures, they are also cunning, powerful and ageless. Many of the greatest seers and fortune-tellers in Skjoldier were Fjarriauga, and were both feared and respected by all. Brave or foolhardy men would often seek them\n\nout, seeking to make use of their talents, powers or insight; although rarely without cost.\n\nHowever, those with a sharp eye who identify a Fjarriauga even through her maiden disguise may secure her aid. Although fickle and cunning creatures, a Fjarriauga is bound to aid those who discover her with a single favour - no more and no less. Such a\n\ntoken should not be squandered nor taken lightly, as although she may be bound to fulfil the favour, it is unwise to earn the ire or wrath of a Fjarriauga.", ""),
        StaticBook("Shades", "§bTriplewing", "------Shades--------------------------  I     I         I    I\n II   II    I   II    II\n  III III  II  II   III\n   II  II II    II II\n    III III  III III  II\n   IIIIIII  III  IIIIII\n     IIIIII I I IIIIII\n     IIIIIIIIIIIIIIII\n   IIII  IIII   III II\n\nIn the time of Aegis, a\npale and apparently evil man lived by the name of Lucas Black,\nhe acted as the leading figure of the Shades. Capable of such feats as corrupting apprentice\nof the archmage into the state known as shade. He is not where the shades\n\nbegan from, but he is one of the most notable people to be a shade.\n\nThese people known as shades are often deemed evil, but is that\ntruly the case? Many seem to think that the\nshades have vanished,\nand that they have.. but rumours spread.\n\nShades are capable\nof performing an apparent former form\nof Arcane Magicks; the      Shade Magic\n-------------------Shade Magic is magic\nthat seemingly draws it's power from a gem.\nIt's often simply called 'tendrils' since that's what really describes the\n\nmagic. The Shade Gem, where the shades would draw their power to perform the magic from, is very powerful, but rumours say that the gem was broken. Actually.. when it was found, it wasn't active, but it was re-activated by an Archmage.. but somehow it's\n\nstill broken. The shades can't use the\nmagic unless it's activated, apparently.\nChances are that it's\njust made up though.\nThe magic in action looks like black tendrils, a bit like squids tentacles. Their\nmagic is destructive, and corrupting. Not really\n\nsomething to seek for.\n    Some say the Shade Magic is blessed by Iblees, and therefore truly unholy. Known shades are very few though; \nIn Aegis, Lucas Black\nwas known to be one.\nIn Asulon, Salamandra\nwas known to be one.\nThey have kept themselves hidden\n\nor very subtle in their actions in Anthos thus far, but I've heard that a man named Adorellan is one.\n  If the Gem is currently broken, this\nman I mentioned can somehow still use the tendrils.. or maybe it's\nnot broken. The Shade\nGem on the other hand\n\nlooks like this:\n-------------------             [!]\nThe page has a detailed but quite\nsmall illustration of\nthe gem. Depicted\nfrom an upwards\nperspective.\n-------------------\n\nThe Shades are truly\na faction shrouded in mystery, but atleast I could reveal some of them.\n-------------------        Ein Sarard\n       ¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨\n   1st of Deep Cold\n   ¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨¨\n  Schattenburg, 1453\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Stone of Metztli", "§bTli'Mukar", "The Stone of Metztli.\n\n\n\n              [!]\n A crude drawing of the holy relic, suspended in the air, sits here.\n\n\nThe stone of Metztli is that of pure power. It provides every kharajyr\n\ntheir connection to Metztli herself. Without it such would falter, the magic she had gifted render null as they would no longer be able to access the power gained from the ancient relic.\n\nThe stone is a pure crystal of empowered lapis. Pure energy sw\n\nwithin the stone, the energy the priesthood/Fylax use to master the art of\nMuun'trivazja.\n\nThoughout history everybody but the kharajyr who stood infront of the stone was forced to their knees infront of the stone. The voice of Metztli filling th\n\nears, turning them insane. It would be a fools errand to try to damage or touch it.\n\nBut throughout history there has been doccumented incidents where, for unknown reasons, they were able to get close enough to cause damage or even explode the holy\n\nrelic. The outburst of the explosion being catastrophic. In one incident the blast was so large it consumed a whole island. Though such was forseen and evacuation was already complete before the relic exploded.\n\nThe stone is also, though there has\n\nnever actually been any incidents so far, employable to corruption and taint. Such is prevented by the many barriers and defences that lay in wait for unsuspecting vandals or dark art users.\n\nThe crystal is also able to be damaged by\nmana\n\nleeches. The mana leech was able to absorb all of the energy residing within the empowered stone. Killing the leech only made it near impossible to gain the power of the energy again. A searing pain engulfed those attuned to the stone.\n\nThough while\n\nstone is able to be destroyed. They may also be re-created. The majority of the time Metztli creates new ones in underground tombs.\n\nIt is the icon of power and a direct connection to the goddess Metztli.", ""),
        StaticBook("Paladins of Xan", "§bHerun Athna", "Xan:\n~~~\nA burning light in the\nunforgiving darkness.\nA sword and shield to\nthe order of the realm.\nXan is an Aengul, that which embodies the illuminating hope of Guardianship and Order. Xan was known for his war with a threat to th\n\n- realm. A Drakaar, one so strong and wise he was thought to be the herald of the Drakaar themselves. Xan's once powerful and strong order fought endlessly with Setherien. He bestowed his boons upon a line so ancient Xan 's blood mixes with theirs. The -\n\n- Athna's. Hilan Athna, the grandfather of the three siblings, Sarah Athna, Hilan Athna the II and his Guardian, Herun Athna now known as Xath. Hilan, the grandfather had his order convene and thus a might weapon of war had been forged. -\n\n- 'The Golden Lance.' A weapon so powerful that Hilan named their Order after it. This weapon was fueled with Aengulic power that of Xan's which gave it it's fierce, golden shine. Years passed and nine of HIlan'sd CHampions were slain and drafted into -\n\n- the dark side. Years passed and Hilan had passed away, bestowing his gifts and magics upon his grandchildren whilst Xan's bestowed the gifts of mind, strength and will to the three. By this time, Setherien had split the Lance in three which was -\n\n- was soon re-forged by Herun Athna with an immense amount of magic. Later, the Golden Lance was plunged into the depths of Setherien's chest, ending his reign of tyranny over Anthos & The Fringe.d Now, it is said Herun and Crumena were born anew as -\n\n- Xan's Guardianship and Order which were drawn together like brothers in arms.\n-------------------\n\n\nXan, however, fights a war of his own which only the likes of Aengul's and Daemon's can fight.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ascended-Unveil", "§bGranantar Fournier Ateus", "Seeking the Ascended is a daunting task. It requires mental fortitude that rivals that of the hardest steel, tempered by the most fiery inferno.\n\nOn the contrary, what may be home to the Ascended, resides in a harsh wintery, frozen land.\n\nWith Spikes of Ice skewering the chilled air, blade-like glass that sever one's legs and lenghty spires that seem like broken bridges.\n\nAmongst the frosty wrath, is a floating fortress. Gently hovering in the air-less sky. Peerless, but forgotten.\n\nThis frosty land can be found just South of Kal'Agnar, the home of the Dwarves. Beyond the peaked frosty mountains and slightly west of a large lake. But beware, only the dwarves can withstand the chill of this frozen hell.", ""),
        StaticBook("Immortal Spirits", "§bThurak'Yar", "Immortal Spirits\n\nA list of the Greater Spirits inhabiting the Immortal Realm and what they represent. This may change, given time, and will be updated as new spirits come to power.\n\nVotar- The spirit of the hunt, commonly shown as a giant, bloodied wolf. Praised by the Phrase Glougaz Votar.\n\n      /\\_==_/\\\n      | /o   o\\ |\n      \\         /\n       \\       /\n        \\ *.* /\n          \\ /\n\nEnrohk- The spirit of bloodlust, savagery and war, often shown as a bastard sword covered in blood. \n        \n         /\\\n         |  |\n         |  | \n         |....|\n         |. .|\n      `==8=='\n          ||\n\nShezept- The spirit of revenge, plots and stealth, depicted as a woman with a lower body of a snake. \n      \n        O\n       -|-\n   ^\\_\\\\_\n   \\____/\n\nJevex- Spirit of order, hard work and self sacrifice, shown as a giant hammer. He's a deadly enemy to the spirit Shezept.\n \n     [======]\n     [==|  |==]\n         ==\n         ==\n        |.--.|\n         ==\n\nIxli- The spirit of forbidden knowledge, truth and judgement. Depicted as an eye, he provides knowledge as the cost of sanity. \n\n       |/  \\|\n      |  (.)  |\n       |\\  /|\n\nOgrol- Spirit of despair, sapped strength and entrapement, shown as a cage full of writhing bodies. He tries to lock up all who summon him.\n\n       ______\n       | | |  | | |\n       =<< >>=\n       | | |  | | |\n      ========\n\nKor- The spirit of the dead, depicted as a cloaked man with an open hand.\n          _\n          |O\\\n           |-''\n          /\\\n\nAnkrus- Spirit of the sea, fishermen and safe travels, often shown as an aquatic woman wielding a spear. \n\n           () |\n           oo/\n           \\/\n           /\\\n           \\/\n\nArwa- Spirit of fertility, harvest and farming, commonly shown as a plump female with over seven hundred breasts.\n \n           ()\n         /.oo.\\\n        /o.oo.o\\\n        |o.o.o.o.o|\n        \\_____/\n         [|]    [|]\n\nAnyhuluz- Spirit of destruction, malicious intent and internal strife, shown as a warrior covered in open wounds.\n\n         O   ^\n       /(`)-`|\n         [|]\n         /\\\n\nAkezo- Spirit of health, vitality and healing, depicted as a winged whale surrounded by a blue aura.\n\n   (\\./)\n     \\\\_/--^--.\n      =.    \"~\"   )\n        \\______/\n\nPaxahru- Spirit of arrogance and stupidity, depicted as a boasting fool.\n\n        /**\\\n       ( ^^ ) \n        /--\\ \n        |`~~'|\n        ====\n        \\/\\/\n         |   |\n\nUblulhar- Spirit of hope an new beginnings, shown as a tree sapling bursting from the ground. \n\n       _____\n      {~~~~}\n     {~~~~~}\n      {~~~~}\n       {~| |~}\n          | |\n       ~~~~~\n\nGhorza- Spirit of travel, depicted as an ever turning wheel.\n\n       /----\\\n      / /--\\ \\\n      |  |<:::::)|  |\n      \\ \\--/ /\n       \\----/\n\nRolfizh- Spirit of assassinations and poison, depicted as a dagger with poison dripping from it.\n\n        /\\\n        |  | \n        |  |\n       =||||=\n         ||\n\nTrokorl- The spirit of engineering, machinery and building. Depicted as a goblin with a goblin with goggles and a hammer.\n\n       {o o}\n        \\-/P\n         |. |/\n         |. |\n         ==\n        /  \\\n\nLuara- The spirit of the moon, often shown by the symbol of a pale, white wolf.\n\n        \\___(>\n         |===/\n         |    |\n\nRamakhet- Spirit of the desert, barren lands and sand. He is never seen, and therefore is rarely ever depicted as something other than his name. He has sworn to scour the earth of all life for all time.\n       ~~~~~\n      Ramakhet\n       ~~~~~\n\nKrathol- The spirit of pain, suffering and starvation. Depicted as a pile of dry bones.\n   \n      (------)\n      (------)\n\nVeist- Spirit of illusion, tricks and thievery, depicted as a goblin with four eyes.\n\n      (:_:)\n      \\| |/\n       /\\\n       |  |\n\nFreygoth- Spirit of the wind and wild animals. He takes any form which he may desire. \n \n       ~~~~~\n        ~~~~\n         ~~~\n\nGlutros- The spirit of greed and obesity. He is depicted as a cake.\n   \n        , , , ,\n       |====|\n       |====|\n\nThulezia- Spirit of lust, pleasure and beauty, depicted as a naked slave girl. \n\n        (_)\n        |00|\n      ,/|   |\\,\n        !__!       \n       /   \\\n\nIsuz- Spirit of love, caring, and tranquility, depicted as an open-armed woman.\n\n       { . }\n       \\| |/\n         ||\n         ||\n\nOrgon- Spirit of Disease, Pestilence, and failure. Depicted as a festering, starving man with six arms, each holding a rusted and broken weapon.\n            (.)\n           |-||-|\n           i-||-i\n           !-||-!\n            /\\\n\nUrin- The spirit of rain and hail, depicted as a dark rain cloud.\n\n         *****\n       ********\n         *****\n         ` ` ` ` \n          ` ` `\n           ` ` `\n            ` `\n\nKesaroth- Spirit of envy and jealousy, usually shown as a golden bull.\n \n                 |__|\n                 ('')\n     /`-------\\/\n    / |         | |\n  '~  | |-----| |\n      ^^       ^^\n\nLeyd- Spirit of dominance and physical strength, symbolised by a closed fist.\n\n       ()()()\n        (   )\n         |**|\n         |**|\n\nScorthuz- The spirit of cleansing and purging, depicted as a vial of clear water.\n\n          (-)\n           | |\n         /--\\\n         |~~~|\n         |~~~|\n         ----\n\nTheruz- Spirit of intelligence and learning, shown as a wise old teacher. Brother to Betharuz.\n\n        ----\n       /     \\\n       | _  _ |\n     ('| O  O |`)\n       |  (.)  |\n       `/=.=\\'\n        \\/\\/\n\nBetharuz- Spirit of alcohol, cactus green and celebration, often depicted as a young dim man, in direct contrast to his brother, Theruz.\n\n       *, (.) U\n        \\_||_/\n           ||\n          /\\\n\nGentharuz- Spirit of smithing, smelting, industry and forging, depicted as a man with no legs, hammering an anvil.\n\n          (,)\n           ||--P\n         || ||   <==->\n         ||===| |==|\n         ||    || |++|\n\nDrelthok- Spirit of sleeping and dreams, often shown as a dark cloud.\n\n        %%%%%%\n       %%%%%%%\n        %%%%%%\n\nEathruz- Spirit of dawn and dusk, shown by the symbol of a red sun.\n\n       . .       . .\n       .\\       /.\n         \\\\ //\n         /|/\\|\\\n         \\|\\/|/\n         // \\\\\n      . /       \\ .\n      . .         . .\n\nKotrestruu- The spirit of memory and the recording of knowledge, depicted as an endless book.\n   \n       ______\n       ||=====/|\n       ||=====/|\n       ||=====/|\n       ||=====/|\n       ||=====/|\n       ||=====/\n\nLetrothak- The spirit of hindsight and excuses, shown as a goblin with eyes in the back of his head.\n\n        /----\\\n     \\\\| |  ||  | |//\n      \\,| (i)(i) |,/\n        \\      /\n         |      |\n       /        \\\n   __/ |       | \\__", ""),
        StaticBook("On Shamanism V2", "§bThurak'Yar", "Volume Two of \nOn Shamanism, Scribed by the Farseer Thurak, 14'th of Sun's Smile, 1487.\n\n... The more they do this, the more word of their feats will spread among the Ancestral Plane and the more likely it is for these Spirits to accept their deals.\nWitchdocters go about things a bit differently than others. During the rituals,\n\nthey’ll present certain objects which hold relevance to the Spirit they are trying to evoke. For example, should they be trying to create a potion which causes the drinker to have insatiable hunger, they would perhaps need something\n\nsuch as the stomach of a large animal, such as a bull, or they may burn and char excessive amounts of savouries in hopes of gaining the attention of the spirit of Greed and Gluttony. Should they do so, they’ll begin to call to their desired\n\nspirit in the tongue of Old Blah, asking for their aid and promising that the attributes that they represent will somehow be more prominent after the use of said potion. Should the spirit agree, the mixture will be cursed, and the Witchdoctor can use\n\nuse it as he will on his unfortunate victims. However, these Shamans must be careful, as it’s sometimes not apparent how a spirit has cursed the potion, and unintended effects are rampant in the brews of unexperienced Witchdocters.\n\nFinally, the Farseers’ blessings are actually quite similar to that of the Lataumans’, in the way that it requires sharp tongue and wit to convince the spirits to give them their boon. When a Farseer decides he wishes to bless something, he must travel\n\nto the Spirit Realm and begin calling the name of the spirit that hold the attribute he needs for the blessing. Should the spirit answer, then the Farseer must try and convince it that the blessing will, in some way, benefit the spirit.\n\nIf this outright fails, and the Spirit refuses, a Farseer may do something else that no other Shaman may do; that being fight the spirit for his blessing. This is very dangerous, and is usually done only in times of desperation, as when a Shaman\n\ndies or is injured in the Spirit Realm, he dies or is injured back in the mortal realm. Once he’s either convinced the Spirit of the need of the blessing or beaten him in battle, it will then begin to take over a Shaman’s body. Back in the Mortal Realm\n\na Farseer’s limbs may start to move under its will, and words in Old Blah will be said to give the blessing direction. A mist, usually hued the colour that best represents the spirit doing the blessing, will pour from the Shaman's orifices\n\nand encompass the person, animal or plant he wishes to bless. When its finished, the Shaman need only to return his connection to his body and admire his handywork; the fabric of the mortal world being shifted in his favour, albeit in only a small front.", ""),
        StaticBook("Pursuing Purity", "§bAshanaak", "------=+=------\nFor Those Who Pursue Purity...\n------=+=------\n\n\n\nA Guide for Those Who Pursue Knowledge of Tahariaean Clericism\n\n------=+=------\nMasjid al Nur al-Haqq\n------=+=------\n\nThe Masjid al Nur al-Haqq is the building before you, serving as a gathering place for the clerics of the Aengul of Purity, Tahariae. Tahariae has given us the abilities to establish Puri\n\nrealm, which comes in two forms. The first is the eradication of injuries, blemishes, and sickness from the mortal races. The second is the eradication of the servants of darkness throughout the realm, such as dark mages, tainted beings, and those with\n\nfraternal relations with such beings.\n\n------=+=------\nThe Five Tenets of Tahariae\n------=+=------\n\nWhen one becomes a cleric, they must follow a set of five tenets, or five main rules, told to the Prophet Braxis in Anthos by Tahariae Himself. The rules are to ensure the cleric kn\n\nor she must do for Tahariae and His duty. Breaking even one of these rules will mean forceful disconnection from Our Lord:\n\n[*] Shelter and protect thy brothers and sisters in Tahariae. [*]\n\nThe other clerics are much like your brothers and sisters, a family. You must always be ready to come to their aid, and to allow them to die intentionally is impure.\n\n[*] Do not stray in thy dedication to Tahariae. [*]\n\nNever stray from your duty, your duty is to heal those in need and to purge the darkness that roam around Vailor. To allow a simple matter to draw you away from such duty is impure.\n\n[*] Guide and protect the Descendants of the Four against the Impure. [*]\n\nNo matter their race or personal prejudice, cast all hatred aside, as we aid all. Help guide them onto the right path and ensure they are healed and protected from Impurity.\n\n[*] Do not spill the blood of the innocent. [*]\n\nDo not attack or kill an innocent person, even if they have insulted you or another. We clerics are the healers of the innocent, not slaughterers of the innocent. Such is impure.\n\n[*] Do not use Tahariae's blessing for anything other than His will. [*]\n\nTahariae’s power is only for His Mission. To use it to harm those innocent of crimes or for your own selfish needs is impure.\n\n------=+=------\nWalking the Path of Purity\n------=+=------\n\nWe are willing to take in those willing to become a cleric, although becoming one is not a simple matter of gaining His power and using it of your own free will. One must be willing\n\ntrials and be prepared to put Tahariae’s duty before all, including what is most precious to you personally. Most of all, you must follow the Tenets without hesitation; failing to do so will mean permanent disconnection.\n\nIf you truly have desire to\n\nLight and Purity into this realm, you shall meet with one of our masters and put through a series of trials that the master decides. These trials will help demonstrate to us your devotion and dedication, as well as help you understand the roles of the\n\nclerics. Once your trials are complete and the master deems you ready, you will be brought before Tahariae Himself. If He deems you ready, He will grant you His blessing of Light, and your duty as a cleric shall begin under the guidance of the master who\n\nconnected you to Tahariae.\n\nIf you wish to walk the Path of Purity, leave a letter explaining who you are, why you wish to serve Tahariae, what skills you have, and if you have any questions regarding us. Simply leave the letter in the chest at the\n\nMasjid al Nur al-Haqq, in the Caliphate of Khalestine, and await our response.\n\nIf you require healings, protection, or blessings, do not hesitate to send a bird to one of the Four Archons of the Masjid al Nur al-Haqq.\n\n------=+=------\nThe Four Archons\n------=+=------\n\n-[ The Mind ]-\nRamza Mantisuku\n((Zeeer0))\n\n-[ The Mouth ]-\nAshanaak\n((Ventusyr))\n\n-[ The Heart ]-\nAndriel Z'lorn\n((jlyoko))\n\n-[ The Arm ]-\nElvira Mantisuku\n((Farryn))\n\n[!] This page is dedicated to a map of the Caliphate, with a small, simply-drawn temple symbol in one of the corners of the city. [!]\n\n((-2197, 1061))", ""),
        StaticBook("Muun'Trivazja.", "§bTli'Mukar", "Muun'Trivazja.\n--------------\n\n\n           [!]\nAnother crude drawing of a blue trident lays within the centre of the page, rich blue in colour.\n\n\nMuun'Trivazja is the holy magic that Metztli\n\ngifted to us during the first plague. She saw her children falling, unable to heal others without being affected themselves, unable to see up coming dangers and unable to defend themselves.\n\nShe gifted the magic to the wise and old Sage that is Natay\n\nshe is most wise and powerful at Muun'trivazja. A true master of the art.\n\n\nChronoshaping\n--------------\nThis was the first gift Metztli bestowed upon her children. The ability to fast forward time or bring time backwards.\n\nThis can work on both corrupted lands and wounds, wounds being the easiest to work on, corrupted land being the hardest.\n\nWhen a kharajyr is casting chronomancy they will form a blue bubble-like sphere from there hands, whatever in the sphere, the us\n\nwould be able to fast forward of bring back, such is the way corruption is removed. Time reverses where there was no corruption. It has been known for priests to gather and cast a conjoint chronomancy bubble to cover a larger area and preserve energy.\n\nMoon fire.\n----------\n\n\nMoonfire is an easy thing to produce. Utilising the energies from the moonpool and manipulating them to form a hot flame, often used for attack, defence or carving into rocks. Sometimes even at rituals.\n\nMoongazing.\n------------\n\nMoongazing is the art of seeing into the past, future and present. It will be a fools errand to hide from a moongazer, moongazers are most powerful as they can use moongazing to their advantage.\n\nMetztli grants those attuned to the stone with prophecies. Such is how the moongazers predicted the Black Scourge destroying the holy relic that is the stone of Metztli.\n\nThey were also able to forsee the great winter of Thales, and made preperations\n\nleave the realm.\n\nMoonpools.\n----------\n\n\nMoonpools are the holy pools which we consume the energies from. They are simply pools of water with the energy running through them.\n\nTli'Mukar\nHead Priest of the Fylax\n\nEx-Sage", ""),
        StaticBook("Necromancers V I", "§bFreyr Mantisuku", "Investigations into Necromancers Volume I\n\nA picture of a man in dark robes standing over dying man a stream of dark green is slowing from the dying man into the robed man hand, two decaying zombies stand behind the dark robed man awaiting his orders*\n\n\nArthur: Freyr Mantisuku\nCo-Author: Crineas Acosta\n[Forewarning: Do not confront Necromancers unprepared]\n[Always Bring a Paladin or war cleric with you during hunts]\n\n\nA Short Introduction\nNecromancy is the defined pragmatically as the utilisation of Life-Force. Necromancers usually have tell-tale signs of their necromancy,\n\n It is like poking a hole in a bucket they can take others life force with the imbalance but their own life force is slowly drained.\n Necromancy is the draining of life-force for nefarious purposes commonly, it’s an art shunned by many.\n\nAppearance\nThey look like us, For all you know one could be next to you they are very hard to find the only true tell is that many will have a very pale look and are extremely sensitive\n\nand weak but this does not go for all necromancers. Basically, signs of decay on their bodies would be a significant give-away.\n\nBehavior\nDue to the extreme difficulty of actually picking one out in a crowded this second cant be added in details.\n\nStrengths\nThey have the power to resurrect the dead and use them as Minions.\nThey can drain the life force of living things leading to a quick death.\n\nWeakness.\nLike all mages they are physically weak and can be killed easily..\nSome instances, holy magic can effect them but it's not always the case. \nThey also have the ability to curse other by modifying life force.\n\nOrigins and Additional details\nHow mortals found this magic is unknown, but it's safe to conclude that the undead under Iblees was instrumental to the art during Aegis\n\nIt’s likely that they drain life-force whilst using their own bodies to draw it, whether through physical means or through other ways such as mists.\n\n\nA note of warning. \nLearning Necromancy is a taboo and would lead to severe repercussions on one’s own wellbeing and health.\n\nNotes:\nAny extra, Corrections or confirmations on information can be\nSent to Either Freyr, or Crineas (( samsan99, Sharkali ))Further Volumes will be compiled as more information is made available.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Wights", "§bRevion Tathron", "On Wights\nBy Revion Tathron\n\nWights, first and foremost, are the creations of a Dark Art known as Mysticism, on which a book shall be written at a later date. They are, as it was put to me, \"Transcendent spectral entities\". They boast a wealth of powers from their state; these\n\ninclude:\n-Telepathy\n-Telekinesis\n-Manifestation Control\n-Better prowess in Mysticism\n-The ability to \"Haunt\" husks.\n\nWhat is haunting, you may ask?\nHaunting is the ability of Wights to 'possess' empty bodies. These can range from empty suits of armor to corpses. In this state, their magic is weaker depending on how heavy their 'body' is. However, it does provide\n\nsome protection against that enemy of all undead, Gold.\n\nAs Wights have the ability to control what they look like when they manifest, and they can possess husks, there are no common defining features, if you're merely looking at them. Wights are mostly made of 'Ectoplasm', which is a mixture of mana and\n\nlife-force that all spectral beings consist of.\n\nAs stated in the beginning of this tome, Wights are created through Mysticism. Only a few details are known about this ritual; firstly, that the to-be Wight is a master over Mysticism and ectoplasm, whereupon the 'sacrifice' themselves to\n\ntranscend to their spectral state from their bodies. However; their bodies turn as hard as rock, and if their former body is destroyed, the Wight perishes.\n\nThe odds are, you will never see a Wight; this is not due to the fact that they have so much control over their forms; rather, that there is only one currently in existence. This may change, however.\n\nThe Wight I talked with was perfectly reasonable, and did not attempt to kill me at all (as other things I've studied had.) It seemed relatively free from the instability that other undead are known to possess (See: Ghouls). \n\n\nEND.", ""),
        StaticBook("Frost Demons", "§bBruta Thersist", "Frost Demons\n                                  \n\nThese creatures typically take the form of a woman. Typically only Elven or Human. The Creatures are pale skinned, clawed and sharp toothed. A true abomina\n\nCreator's design.\n\nArmed with Evocation and typically assisted by whatever fool they've seduced into their bidding. \n\nIt should be noted that these women are also Illusion mages. Hiding their true forms.\n\n       Counter Measures\n                                        \n\nExposure to open flame, typically close to the skin, disrupts the illusion magic at play.\n\nThe Creatures are deathly cold to the touch.\n\nThe Women have abno\n\nSimply check a woman for all the standard signs associated with these creatures and there should be no issue.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Wraiths", "Toodles", "On Wraiths\n\nBy: Someone who isn't stupid enough to reveal their true name.\n\nNot much is known about the actual physical characteristics of Wraiths by the author, but what they do know shall be written down. Wraiths (also known as Harbingers) are shadowy undead beings with a proclivity for killing.\n\nThe most recent incarnation of Wraiths are produced by the machinations of the Drakaar Mordring, through the utilization of certain altars, one of which is in the Sunless Sanctum. (The process of becoming a Wraith is described in another book.)\n\nThe Wraith, once created, is bound to Mordring's Will; basically, to bring about a resurgence of the Dragonkin. Wraiths have the ability to summon some form of Vessel, which fill with lifeforce when a mortal dies in the vicinity of it. It takes fifteen\n\ndeaths for the Vessel to be full, upon which a Dragon or Drake will spawn. If the Vessel is destroyed before the amount of lifeforce is acquired, all the accumulated lifeforce will vanish, but the Vessel can still be summoned. If the Wraith attempts to\n\nharm the newly-made Dragon or Drake, the Wraith will perish. After thirty years, Wraiths are released from Mordring's service, but they retain the ability to summon Vessels. Wraiths have the ability to husk\n\nempty bodies, much like Wights; but there are unknown complications regarding the eyes of such a body.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fjarriauga", "§bLulma", "The Fjarriauga; Maidens of Ice\n\nThe curse of the Fjarriauga is given to, often times, grief stricken or depressed women in their lowest point. Once cursed by a Frost Mother, the young witch will begin to undergo many changes and abandon her race prior. Once cursed, the witches body is\n\nfrozen in time, granting them immortality. Something to be noted: A witch who is cursed in peak physical health will remain that way forever, regardless of whatever other magics she may pick up. It takes roughly a year for the cursing process to finish\n\nand the witch will undergo many changes both mental and physical.\n\nThe first thing a young witch will notice is that other foods she used to normally enjoy no longer sustain her, nor do they taste the same. The new flavor for normal food is ash.\n\nA witch will find that her new craving is for the flesh of men, and if she chooses to resist this hunger she will find herself going mad. This is what most Witch Hunters refer to as 'going feral'. A witch can feed of the flesh of animals, raw of course,\n\nbut this will not sustain them forever.\n\nA Fjarriauga has the ability, to physically changed their body and makeup. These changes are like a sculpture, not illusionary. They have the ability to disguise themselves as any of the four decendant\n\nraces being: Human, Elf, Dwarf and Orc. However, their internal makeup never changes. Their blood is still slush, which is any easy way to catch one.\n\nThe next ability of a witch is their control over pre-existing ice. They are able to control and\n\nmanipulate ice in their surrounding area or moisture in the air. However, in hot temperatures they will be unable to use this ability. Another way to catch a witch is a woman in a warm area who is suffering from similar symptoms of a heat stroke.\n\nNow, for the most important part to catching a witch, the favour. When a witch is caught in her disguise she is forced to offer you a wish in exchange for her secret to be kept. \n\nNote: Seeing a witch in her true form will not force her to give a wish.\n\nThis book was written by Lulma. \n\nThe legitimacy of what is written in the books has come from studies on witches and stories told first hand by ACTUAL Witch Hunters.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Darkstalkers", "§bRevion Tathron", "Darkstalkers\nBy Revion Tathron\n\nA NOTICE BEFORE READING: Darkstalkers are /incredibly dangerous/ and should NOT be approached without adequate preparation.\n\nDarkstalkers, at first, appear to be merely a man in a suit of armor; however, nothing could be farther from the truth. They are Necrotic Undead; or beings raised by Necromancers. They are also capable of draining life-force, presumably to fuel\n\nthemselves; this may manifest as black miasma. They are fast and incredibly agile, despite all of their armor. And, akin to other undead creatures, if struck down they will rise again. In addition to this, they do not /show/ pain; whether they feel it\n\nor not is unknown to this author. However, Darkstalkers are capable of speech and reason, and are weak to holy magic. They are also supposedly weak to Aurum weaponry, due to its lifeforce-conduction properties, but this was not tested. But as they are\n\ncorporeal, they can also be slain with more mundane weaponry, such as Ferrum.\n\nIn conclusion, Darkstalkers are fast, use swords and a lifeforce-draining ability to attack, and when slain leave behind empty armor. They should not be approached without due caution and preparation.\n\nEND.\n\nThe information in this tome was acquired through observing Darkstalkers kill people, observing Darkstalkers being killed, and talking with a Paladin who seemed knowledgeable on the subject of Darkstalkers.", ""),
        StaticBook("To Be a Wraith", "Toodles", "Becoming a Wraith\n\nBy: Someone who's not stupid enough to reveal their name.\n\nPrerequisites:\n-Must be a practitioner of the dark arts or undead.\n-Must have a 'catalyst'; some sort of bone that the Drake, Satar, gives to certain people.\n\nThe hopeful Wraith must acquire such a catalyst, and then place it on a certain type of Altar, one example of which is located in the Sunless Sanctum. Upon doing this, they must find, kill, and take a bone from three mortals.\n\nThey then must take these bones to the altar... But the author is not quite sure what happens to them. But once they've been used, the Wraith-to-be must stab themself with an Aurum sword. After much immolation and probably pain, they\n\nwill become a Wraith. Huzzah!", ""),
        StaticBook("On Gravens", "§bValmir Audane", "*The handwriting is neat but seemingly rushed.*\n\nThroughout my time as a Delver I have experienced a near countless number of encounters involving beings of another existence, and by that I mean ghosts. Granted the concept of the undead is very much true, and we’ve lost countless souls to their numbers\n\nduring the days of Aegis, with the simple zombies and skeletons which walk around the lands of Anthos.\n\nWe must first define what exactly a ghost may be.  Perhaps a ghost is the physical manifestation of one one’s mana left behind by some unseen forc\n\nPerhaps it is created when the monks are unable to recover the body for some time and the soul of the person is simply unable to move on by some unseen force. Whatever the cause may be of most of these spirits I am unsure of and may never exactly know.\n\nHowever there is another type of spirit which roams the lands of Anthos that I can explain.  These would be the beings known as 'Gravens'.  I will attempt to best describe them through my experiences.\n\n\"What is a graven exactly?\" you may be thinking if you are unfamiliar to the term.  A graven is a special type of undead, I should note that I use the term 'undead' somewhat loosely as they are still in a sense alive.\n\nThe main difference between a Graven and the stereotypical ghost is that a Graven has the ability to manifest itself for short periods of time and interact with the world around it almost as if it had never left.\n\nA Graven is far from some evil spirit or being, a Graven is simply a soul that is stuck on our world and holds a desire strong enough to keep it bound here.\n\nA graven is often created when a someone is slain and who has devoted his or herself to a specific task in their life.  Their death has ripped them from their devotion to that goal and leaves behind a being of great willpower, desire, and resolve.\n\nAs their body is laid to a final rest their true inner-being is anything but still.\n\nIt is possible for one to become a Graven in order to seek out revenge or to fight against evil, however centuries may pass before that being may become a graven, if at all.  I have personally encountered two Graven.\n\nthe one known by simply the name Bishop, and one whom was bent or creating the perfect song, I have referred to him as The Bard.\n\nMy personal experiences with Bishop has taught me very much about the Graven's goals and desires.\n\nEach Graven possesses it's own desires and goals, acting independently of each other.  Bishop's goals are to destroy heretics and to spread love of the Creator as he was a Bishop in life before his untimely demise.\n\n-=Physical characteristics of a Graven=-\n\nA graven takes on a very wispy form of existence when it manifests itself, appearing almost as a shadow in the case of The Bard, and a humanoid shape of blue flame in the case of Bishop.\n\nThese beings have been able to physically interact with the real world, extinguishing candles and even operating gate mechanisms.\n\nThese beings appear in a form that they find similar to the ones that they once had or wanted to be by my understanding.  Bishop, for example, wears a white and gold tunic of sorts, depicting his religious beliefs and faith in the creator.\n\n-=Manifestations=-\n\nA Graven can only stay in it's manifested form for short periods of time before it fades away from our world of physical existence, although it is anything but gone.\n\nGraven possess the ability to hear, see, and speak even while they are not manifested.\n\nUpon receiving physical harm a Graven's ability to keep itself manifested weakens, resulting in it fading from existence much faster than it normally would have.\n\n In my discussions and observations a Graven has been able to slightly affect the world around it while it is de-manifested to a minor degree such as blowing out a candle, however I doubt that this is a typical event of the Graven.\n\nBishop shows no attitude or desire to simply toy around with the world around him.\n\n-=Harming a Graven=-\n\nGraven are a special breed of spirit, you do not need a magical sword, a weapon of gold, or a mage’s assistance to fight these spirits.  They are as physically harmed by conventional weapons as a Human, Elf, or Kha may be.\n\nA Graven may be more harmed than it may be killed.  This is because of A Graven’s tendency to manifest itself.\n\nI have had no reason to seek out and harm the Graven myself as I have found the two I have met rather pleasant and did not wish to test these myself although Bishop does inform me that it possible to do this.\n\nBishop has also informed me that a fatal wound may be enough to simply kill a Graven.  By kill I assume it would only de-manifest the Graven, perhaps for a longer period of time, however it may be possible to fully slay it through these means.\n\nOn a semi-related note I theorize that it would be possible for someone to capture the soul of a Graven as they are almost a being of pure soul.\n\nHowever this would not be be possible for myself and colleagues and therefore beyond my own observations so I will avoid this topic as I may be incorrect.\n\n-=Spirit People=-\n\nTo my observations, experiences, and discussions with others on the same topic the topic of weather a Graven should be considered a ‘Person’ is somewhat debatable.\n\nThey would show signs of both being fully conscious but are yet similar to ghosts and spectres in regards to their forms.\n\nIn my ethical opinion I would classify a Graven as living and therefore deserving of whatever treatment you may deem worthy of those around you.\n\nGravens are not all evil by my observations and discussions with Bishop, in fact it may even be worth befriending the Gravens you meet as they are simply trapped souls looking to end their tasks and to possibly move on.\n\nBesides, whom may be better to converse with in regards to ancient civilizations?\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWritten by,\nValmir Audane", ""),
        StaticBook("The Azdrazi", "§bIcarus Adil", "The Azdrazi\n\n        Haelun'or,\n           Axios\n\n     Published 1592\n\n\n\n     by Icarus Adil\n\nThe Azdrazi\n===================   The Azdrazi are an odd creature, draconic in nature, which have recently returned to some prominence in the land of Axios. Upon their head are long, brown horns, and their skin is unmistakably scaly. Their eyes are ora\n\nand serpentine, their pupils slitted, long and thin. They can retract these fearsome features to a certain extent, though not all choose to. At a glance, the Azdrazi are monsters, and will likely strike fear in the hearts of those who see them.\n\nFortunately, this is false.\n   In this work, it is my hope to spread understanding regarding the Azdrazi, for these misgivings not only pose undue risks to their well-being, yet also hamper them in pursuit of their noble task. The Azdrazi should not be\n\nregarded as monstrosities of evil, or as ne'er do wells of any sort. Instead, they should be treated as neutral creatures pursuant of a righteous task, as I shall explain below.\n   To begin, one must look to the history of the Azdrazi, for their existe\n\npredates most of our own. The creatures first emerged during the Great War, borne with the sole intent of stopping the darkness of the Betrayer Iblees. Much of their history has been lost to time or otherwise destroyed, but it is known that the current\n\niteration of Azdrazi stem from the line formed by Azdromoth, prior to his present affliction.\n   The current brood of Azdrazi began with the stirring of one known as Alistair, the child of Azdromoth, and father of the remaining Azdrazi, at least as far\n\nas is currently known. He returned and began to create other Azdrazi, though the method of doing so is still unknown. Unfortunately, it was not until after this began that they learnt of Azdromoth’s descent to existence as a Drakaar, a fate most Dragaar\n\nescape by confining themselves to stone.\n   With this knowledge, the Azdrazi have severed ties with their progenitor, instead pursuing the goals their very existence is predicated upon. They exist to protect man against the forces of darkness, and\n\nhope to one day find a cure for the blight which affects their father and grandfather, Azdromoth the Arch-Drakaar.\n   Though these creatures have found conflict against the Paladins of Xan, as is natural giving their order's aversion to the dragonkin,\n\nwould seem a truce may be found. The disciples in the Cult of Azdromoth also combat the Azdrazi, as is natural for those who worship the Arch-Drakaar in its present form. Yet beyond this, the Azdrazi hold no conflict with man, and should indeed be treated\n\nin accordance to their intentions: to protect man against the dark.\n   In conclusion, I encourage all who find themselves in the presence of Azdrazi not only to stay any hostility based on assumptions of their aesthetic, yet also to thank them for thei\n\nservice to the realm of mortality. It seems that we all owe them our appreciation, and they are yet to find it.\n\nNotes\n===================\n\nThe information for this piece was gathered through the author's interview of Mister Suldaeroth and Mister Favnir, two Azdrazi who freely gave information regarding their existence. Their support of\n\nintellectual pursuit will not go unforgotten, so long as the information they have offered does not prove false. If you see them, thank them for their service both through this tome, yet also against those who promote darkness in our realm.", ""),
        StaticBook("Graven Laws", "§b'The Shrieking Knight'", "Orders of thy Graven\n-------------------Thou shall follow thou's task.\nThou shall honor thy master.\nThou shall honor thy Brethern.\nThou shall honor thy comrade.\nAmen.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Dreadknights", "§bThe Eternal Librarian", "On Dreadknights\n\n by Cir'dian Nymphea\n\nIf this book is found anywhere else than the Eternal Library of Annil’sul, the Enclave of Haelun’or, it is stolen.\n\nBoth buyers and sellers will be punished.\n\nSigned, the Eternal Librarian\n\nGenesis\nThe dreadknights are beings comprised of suits of armor bound together through the engraving of specific runes unique to the blood mages, of whom draw their magic from a deity presently unknown to me. They originated in the land of Asulon\n\nas did their constructs (The dreadknights). As it stands however, it is somewhat of a mystery as to where the blood mages came from, and how their magic came to be. However it is known that the dreadknights are the tools of the blood mages. They are the\n\nstrength behind them.\n\nCreation\nThe dreadknights are created over the process of several months through a long and arduous ritual involving the removal of freedom and physical flesh. The process begins with the abduction of a\n\nspecific choice being. The selection is not bound to physical aspects (Which would be removed in the end anyway) but rather decided by the quality of those taken. Usually of whom are stubborn and loyal to whom they serve. In post of their abduction- the\n\npatron is taken to which ever stronghold the dreadknights would presently occupy. From there they would be bound. The dreadlord then begins the process with the destruction of both knee caps, as to prevent escape and standing. No sedatives are used in\n\nthis process. The patron is then fitted with a suit of armor usually comprised of a metal known as black iron (Known for being particularly dense, and durable). The leader then engraves several runic symbols into the armor of the victim. This can be done\n\nby both dreadlord, and blood mage. These runes bind the soul of said victim to the suit of armor. Once finished, the subject is cast into a cell, and left for several days before further work is done. For the next few weeks the victim is tortured, their\n\nrunes left open to rot. Flesh eventually gives way, leaving nothing but the victim’s skeletal form beneath. Alongside this, the will of the victim is broken, and they are taught to love pain. By two months, the process is complete, and the new dreadknight\n\nmay now set out to do the will of their dreadlord or blood mage.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Ghouls", "Toodles", "On Ghouls\nBy: Revion M. Tathron\n\nGhouls, the lowest of all undead creatures I have yet encountered. Slavering, mindless beings, these rotten corpses are only driven by the need for life-force.  While Ghouls may be killed, as for all undead, their death is merely temporary. They will\n\nrise again, despite the efforts of common or holy men. When they do rise, they will be hungrier and more angry than ever before. The reason that Ghouls do not die is because they have soul shadows, rather than souls. Soul shadows can be compared\n\nto souls as embers are to flame. However, there a few Ghouls capable of mastering their Soul Shadows and retaining some semblance of humanity, but this is uncommon.\n\nGhouls are normally created through the machinations of Necromancy, but the author has been told by an unverifiable source that a Ghoul will inevitably rise from any dead body as time passes.\n\nGhouls are vulnerable to Aurum and holy magics, as all undead are. Their cravings of life-force can be assuaged by a Necromancer to cease their attack.", ""),
        StaticBook("Wishes", "§bAmadeus \"Balorien\" Glaciem", "Dear Headless horseman.\n\nI want your skeleton horse for halloween thank you!\n\n\n\n       Sincerly Amadeus", ""),
