        StaticBook("Writ", "§bTuvya", "By writ of His Imperial Majesty those creatures known as Ascended may put their wards over Petrusia.\n\nTrickery, curses, or decievery will be met with the execution of\nperepetrator and\naffiliates.\n\n~Tuvya", ""),
        StaticBook("Mental Barriers", "§bElindor", "Recognising the backgrounds of\nMental Barriers\n\n1: Birthright\n\n2: Learnt: Emotional\n\n3: Learnt: Intellect\n\n4: Self Aware\n\nWhether conscious of the fact or not, all who are of mental capacity for independant thought operate with mental barriers. An avoidance of certain foods, sentimentalities for or against an individual based on previous experience, a shudder at rain dropped\n\nupon the bridge of the nose. Whether they serve a purpose or not is beside the point, but all with functioning minds also have functioning mental barriers.\nGranted, some are more useful than others, but none should be ignored.\n\nConsideration 1:\nWhile minds are capable of being moulded, as is the case of a particular experiment wherein a disadvantaged goblin child is given the intellectual upbringing of a noble elven child (for scientific purposes only) and it is observed\n\nthat the matter of its circumstance of birth played little consequence in its mental abilities after the experiment's completion; however there is equal quantity of proof to suggest the opposite: that particulars of birth can suggest better or\n\nworse mental ability. So if all with basic mental function posess mental barriers at some level, then it can also be agreed upon that some individuals may have naturally more intentional barriers resulting from the particulars of their birth.\n\nConsideration 2:\nEmotional experiences are an inevitable by-product of experiencing the company of others. What is not certain is whether the usefulness of such can be realised.\nIt has been observed through various trials\n\nin which test subjects experienced the same situation that arised a similar emotional outcome in each subject. The results were conclusive that the female subjects were more capable of becoming emotionally guarded against a similar circumstance\n\nwhen the same tests were repeated (and with more difinitive results in the older subjects). The outcome of said experiments showed that aged women are more capable of producing emotional based mental barriers than are young men.\n\nOf course this does not mean that it is only the aged woman's game to create emotional barriers, but that their past experiences before commencing tests rendered them more prepared to react in an emotionally defensive manner.\nBut whether young or old, and\n\nposesssing either of the genitalia, emotionally driven mental barriers prove to be an easily formed barrier that many people demonstrate. It is the experience that heat means danger, or that a wanting look from the opposite sex means trouble. And\n\nsuch learning becomes the basis of these most simple barriers with the intent to better our future course from further danger.\n\nConsideration 3:\nLearning needs by neccessity of adapted barriers (the terminology \"adapted\" used to refer to any barriers that are reactive in nature) is not limited to that of emotional education, though it is certainly the easier and more likely to\n\noccur in individuals who have no conscious recognition of mental barriers than those of the next type: intellectual.\nMentally capable individuals, typically of a higher learning, are more aware of themselves and the commencement and termination of their\n\nown thoughts, such that they might be able to deduce that the outcome of something will be of ill consequence, and thus establish an intellectual barrier against it without requiring the emotional experience of it to draw such a conclusion.\n\nAnyone with such ability would be concidered of a more valuable intellectual worth than those who remain unconscious to their circumstance until they experience it first hand, because they demonstrate a conscious control over adapted barriers, knowing\n\nthe beginnings of danger before the danger is present. As is the results of tests among children in which one observes another experiencing pain and assumes that the outcome of the test implement used will result in pain, without having to experience it\n\nfor themselves.\nIndividuals with intellectual adapted barriers can become conscious of a problem before the problem manifests, and thus one who intends to expose them to mental danger will find their defense against it pre-emptive from the first.\n\nConsideration 4:\nThe last is difinitively the most complicated. Tests on such subjects still remain inconclusive as the data is of too broad an array to speculate commonalities; supposing that great caution be taken in anticipating this adaptive and\n\nindividualistic reaction to provocation.\nIf the proposed individual be of such mental self awareness as to acknowledge their own thoughts and recognise the thoughts of others within their own murmurings, then any mental intrusion will be detected from the\n\nfirst by these clever adaptive barriers that prevent further intrusion of outside stimuli.\nUnderstanding such mental barriers can only be done on an individual basis, for without foreknowledge of the mental, emotional and experiential past of\n\nthe individual, one has no way of interpreting or supposing their reaction. And no one route will have conclusive success in all cases.\n\nThe boldest conclusion:\nIf, in any of the previous cases and most cunning in the latter one, an individual were to acknowledge their own conscious existence with relation to a broader knowledge of the universe and/or deity(s), and at the\n\nsame time comprehends themselves in reference to The Void, then their mental resoluteness may account for intentional barriers of not just emotional and intellectual stimuli, but of all mental stimuli. Such an individual is capable of constructing a\n\ndeliberate blockade that utilises their own erperience(s), and acknowledging their experiential or anticipated reaction, mould it into a barrier that will require a specifically, and equally intentional, attempt to remove it.\n\nOf anticipating and overcoming any of the barriers that the source of which has been suggested in the previous pages, this book will do no work towards. For the efforts of removing a barrier is to discredit the worth of it, while the intent of this book\n\nhas been to acknowledge and more clearly define the circumstance from which mental barriers may have been constructed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Electrical Evo", "§bLelien", "Electrical\n     Evocation\n\n   §\n\n*Once you flip to the second page, a current, about the strength of a electrical fence, would jolt through you. Most likely rendering you unconcious.*\n\nWith magical love,\nSilvos and Lelien.\n*A small heart is drawn at the bottom*", ""),
        StaticBook("Frost Demons", "§bBruta Thersist", "Frost Demons\n                                  \n\nThese creatures typically take the form of a woman. Typically only Elven or Human. The Creatures are pale skinned, clawed and sharp toothed. A true abomination to the...\n\nCreator's design.\n\nArmed with Evocation and typically assisted by whatever fool they've seduced into their bidding. \n\nIt should be noted that these women are also Illusion mages. Hiding their true forms.\n\n       Counter Measures\n                                        \n\nExposure to open flame, typically close to the skin, disrupts the illusion magic at play.\n\nThe Creatures are deathly cold to the touch.\n\nThe Women have abnormally sharp teeth.\n\nSimply check a woman for all the standard signs associated with these creatures and there should be no issue.", ""),
        StaticBook("An Odd Wish - SB", "§bSam", "\"I wish that I my hair becomes dark blonde, my eyes bright blue, and my skin a lighter color.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("One Wish..", "§bAbigail M. Eumelia", "My wish is to leave a legacy on the world. To be remembered as a great mali'aheral.\nI just want to make everyone..happy...living in peace.\n\nPeace between the races, and to leave my legacy on the world, being remembered as a Great Mali'Aheral.\n\nPeace...\n\nRememberance...\n\n\n\n\n\n         Abigail\n         Eumelia.", ""),
        StaticBook("Seed of Laurelin", "§bTristanm1", "The High Prince of Malinor and The Seed of Laurelin\n\nScribed by Zevandir\nTold by High Prince Native\n\nA powerful Arch Druid from one of Malinor's eldest cities came to Aegis to help us with the erecting of Laurelin's trees. I met him at the cobblestone spires to the west of the Aegis Temple.  We set off on foot to a mountain gorge I had come across that\n\nwould act as a natural barrier to our foes. Once we arrived, the Druid wandered around in the valley reaching into a pouch at his hip every so often. He showed me the seeds in said pouch and they had tiny, intricate vines woven around them, with a shine\n\nvery similiar to glowstone. Whilst my brigade of builders were creating the city's defensive wall, trees began to grow exponentially! It seemed as though the trees grew faster the taller they got and soon the canopy raised hundreds of feet above us. It\n\nwas a wonderful sight, the leaves sprung out of the branches with a burst of the similiar glowstone sheen, and sprinkles of metallic dust swirled down from the tree tops.\nThere was still, however, a large clearing in the centre of the city. This of course\n\nwas for the mother tree. A tree to harbour them all. He grabbed a bit of parchment from his satchel and look over at me reassuringly. The Arch Druid then walked to the centre of the clearing, and began to cast a powerful spell upon one of the seeds.\n\nleaves suddenly spun around him wildly, and a wonderful green color radiated from him like an aura.\nThe tree' trunk sprouted around him, and he was no longer in view. I was rather frightened when I saw this, hoping he hadn't cast the spell incorrectly. As\n\nthe Mother Tree grew to its ultimate height, I saw a small opening half way up the tree. Low and behold, the Arch Druid stood in the opening proclaiming \"This is where the stone alter shall lie.\"\nOnce the trees seemed to stop growing, we climbed up the\n\ntrees with packs of wooden planks and began setting down the first few platforms. In time, Laurelin had become of the finest city's of Malinor, and to think it had all begun with just a pouch of seeds and a pinch of Druid Magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("V Veritatis 6", "§bJacob Chapel", "Verbo Veritatis\nSixth Edition\n23-3-1480\n\nIn this edition:\n*Knights Rebellion\n*City of Dwarves reclaimed\n*The Karovian Column\n*Words from the Emperor\nAnd much much more!\n\nReporters needed for the newspaper\nDear readers, as always we are in great need of reporters for our esteemed newspaper, especially now Ralph Riley has stepped down from his position because of his prolonged battle with illness. Since patronage has\n\nbeen secured, we are able to pay much better rates for articles. As a reporter you can expect up to 500 minas per article!\n\nThe work is freelance, and you are paid per article delivered. Please contact Jacob Chapel if you are interested.\n\n((Contact me (Pepernoot) ingame or on the forums!))\n\nThe Knights Rebellion\nIn one of the greatest moves of treachery in our time, Maric Varodyr, once Grand Knight of the realm, and part of the Order of the Red Dragon has taken up arms against the Empire. After word had reached the Emperor that Maric was\n\nconspiring against the integrity of the Empire, intending to break it up into pieces. Immediately the Emperor dismissed him from his position, but Maric fled to the Keep of Angren and barricaded himself in there, along with a few rebels.\n\nOur grand Emperor demanded Maric to leave the keep, but the traitor defied these orders and claimed the keep for his own. Hiding inside the keep he proclaimed himself King of Renatus, a claim so audacious and without any real claim to the title,\n\nhe must surely be absolutely mad drunk on power.\n\nAs of now the traitors are still hiding behind the walls of Angren, awaiting their certain and inevitable death. Quoting our Emperor: \"Do not recognise this traitor who has so aptly deemed fit to call\n\nhimself King without any form of legitimization from the Church or the faith. Fight back against the foreign tyrants who would dare infringe upon our sovereignty, despite their signing of various treaties intended to ensure such would not be so.\n\nYet do not fight because of who you are, Highlander, Heartlander or Farfolk. Fight because by the creator above, you will never allow such a spineless snake-tongued worm as Maric Varodyr to sit upon the throne of humanity”\n\nCarry on Carrion!\n\nThe City of the Dwarves reclaimed\nSince the reconquest of the dwarven capital, the dwarves have been very busy to rebuild and reclaim their old capital. Nearly all signs of the Undead occupation have been removed and a lot of work is being done to\n\nrebuild the homes of the dwarves, under the guidance of Lord Balek Ironguy and Thurland Grandaxe, the architects of the arts guild. The new city will be completely situated in the mountains, with farmland in the valley in front of the entrance to\n\n the mountain home.\n\nThe new city has been named Kal’Karaad, and it should be ready for habitation in 2 saints days ((11 November)). We of the Verbo Veritatis wish the dwarves happiness and prosperity in their new capital, and hope that it may last\n\n a thousand years. Sadly the dwarves have not returned our goodwill to help in the current rebellion of the knights, and have retracted their offer to come to our assistance.\n\nFormation of the House of Magnates\nThe Emperor has formed Oren's first legislative body! Known as the House of Magnates, it consists of representatives, or magnates, of all the nobles of the realm, along with the burghers of Petrus. The higher one's\n\n title is, the more representatives and votes, one gets. The body votes on appointing various ministers, akin to privy councillors, who make up the government. It is led by the Lord Chancellor who acts as virtually any under-king to the Emperor,\n\nworking on the day to day affairs of the realm. Currently the Chancellor is Joachim var Sarkoz, a learned barrister from the court of King Francis who has been appointed by the Emperor to help facilitate the establishment of the Magnates while the nobles\n\nand emperor focus on the military expenditures at hand. He shall rule for three years, before he is either voted in again by the various Magnates or a new Chancellor, or known more colloquially as the Prime Minister, is appointed by the Magnates.\n\nLet us hope Prime Minister Joachim can guide our country to glory!\n\nHoly ward over Petrus\nOn the 10th of The First Seed, mages have cast an undead weakening ward over our grand city of Petrus. The main effects of this is to dispel the effects of their magics. The mages creating the magic, one of them being the ancient\n\nwizard Blundermore, forged a magic crystal and lifted it up into the air, defying gravity. From the crystal lights and other magical effects originate, bringing a feeling of safety and calm over the city.\n\nThe populace can rejoice over this noble effort of the mages, and it is hoped that the ward will keep the undead away for a long time.\n\nThe Karovian Column\nA Tragic End\nOver to the news from Karovia this week, and it appears that her husband’s reluctance to give her a child has finally pushed poor Lynn Rovin over the edge. The other day, her body was found lying at the bottom of\n\na cliff face, her stomach punctured with knife wounds. Though it has not yet been confirmed, early evidence appears to suggest that the blows were self inflicted. What an unpleasant end to what could have surely been a most enduring marriage...\n\nThis newspaper would like to extend its deepest condolences to her widowed husband, the Imperial Prince, Aleksandr Carrion for his tragic loss.\n\nIn other news, yet more spook-filled sightings of the Imperial Prince’s late twin brother, Yakov Carrion!\n\nAs reported in Edition Five, little is known of Yakov’s decision to betray Oren to the Undead scourge, though recent events suggest he has returned to to seek vengeance against close members of his family. We can only hope that the guard remain viligant\n\n in these dark and dreary times. In brighter news however, Aleksandr is said to have found a new wife to replace his dearest beloved. Rumour has it that this is said to be Lynn’s very own sister! We suspect it shall not be long before we have another\n\nroyal wedding on our hands!\n\nSo dear readers, with his wife’s demise and his brother’s fall to the Undead, where will Aleksandr turn now? Find out next time in the Karovian Column of Verbo Veritatis, Edition Seven!\n-Our anonymous source in Karovia\n\nWords from the Emperor\nTo the loyal fellows of Orenia,\n\nThough some minor rebellion plagues our lands, a simple matter it will be to drive out the meager forces assembled under the traitor Maric Varodyr.\n\nSuch a petty uprising is of little consequence in the grand scheme of our Holy Empire, such writing on this day regards the welfare of our capital, Petrus.\n\nWhen I had first been elected by the Electorate to serve as Emperor,\n\nPetrus had been little more than a ghost town. Now I am happy to say Petrus is the single most populated city in not only our realm, but of the world itself. This cannot be attributed to I, but to the true heartlanders of Petrus who have graced this city\n\nwith life. Petrus stands as the jewel of our modern world, in not just the strong economy, but in terms of cultural regards, social mobility, and military might. \n\nNowhere else in Athera can one find a public library with such a vast array of knowledge\n\navailable to the public, nowhere else in Athera maintains our efficient system of free food, and nowhere else in Athera upholds a city guard as do our Wardens of the Imperial Watch, a Watch at current roster twenty-four men strong.\n\nThe average daily income to Petrus coffers is 5,000 minas. The average yearly budget for the Imperial Watch is 20,000 minas. Petrus maintains a budget of 44,000 minas for building improvements and public works. Average yearly tax income is 4,000 minas.\n\nPetrus holds 53 separate plots, of which only 8 are not filled at the time of this writing; 43 plots had paid taxes last tax cycle. Truly the economic structure of Petrus is unmatched by any city in the world, and this does not take into account the great\n\nndustrial capability of our Holy City. Within Petrus are produced the finest weapons and armor in the entire world, with the most efficient labor force in the world harvesting vast quantities of wheat, ores, stone, and wood everyday.\n\nUnlike the treasuries of many other nations, the majority of goods produced are not stashed away but sold as surplus to the citizens of Petrus, weapons and armor worthy of Kings can be found for open sale and in quantity, at a pittance compared to what\n\none may find at the cloud temple auctioneer.\n\nThough there is much more than just numbers to Petrus, I hope this has given some insight into our holy Capital and I am proud for all the fellows of Petrus who make our city the jewel of the world.\n\nCreator watch over us all,\nTuvya Sigismundovic Carrion\n\nReturn of the Order of Saint Amyas\nThe Order of Saint Amyas has been reformed, with Adrian de Bar as its new Grand Master. Shockingly though, Adrian quickly pledged his support to Maric’s traitorous cause and was convicted of treason.\n\nAfter persuasion by Oren, and a lot of mercy on the side of the Emperor, he was returned to the fold quickly though. Hopefully he is wise enough to not betray Oren again.\n\nWe hope that the Order will become a beacon of purity and righteousness, especially in these dark times, and that honest God-fearing men fight for its cause.\n\nPetrus tavern under new management\nAs the old Throdo has not been able to properly take care of the tavern at the central square in Petrus, the tavern has been granted to a new owner. The tavern has been renamed “the Drunken Dragon”,\n\nand it has been quite busy indeed.\nThe Verbo Veritatis wishes Sam good luck with running the tavern, and may many drinks be drunk!\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nWe hope you enjoyed the newspaper, and remember: Athera’s greatest bookstore, “Books of Oren”, is the publisher of this great paper. There are shelves upon shelves of amazing books for incredibly low prices. Visit us at Abbey Road 13, Petrus!", ""),
        StaticBook("Sally's Wish", "§bSalendys", "\"I wish for a pet spider. A big fluffy one.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Wish", "§bProfessor Beros Oathcast", "*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*\n\nThis Pumpkin Day, I Beros Oathcast wish for another alchemical creation involving pumpkins... It would be useful with all these excess pumpkins laying around.\n\nMay this wish come true. ~ Beros\n~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*~*", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Hist. V3", "§bMage Baruk-Ghaz", "\"The Ancient History\"\n\n*The next lines are curved*\n\"These volumes contain the Origins of Aegis, written by the \"Wandering Wizard\" in the second seed of year 84 at the Cloud Temple of Aegis.\"\n\n*The book apears to be in good shape, it must be a copy*\n\nKrug was the last to be tricked, Iblees tempted him with wealth, with food, with power. None interested Krug. Iblees was furious, he then challenged Krug in open combat in fury.\n\nThe whole world witnessed Ibleeses transformation into a hideous beast of\n\nthe Void. His skin turned into scales, fangs erupted and dark horns exploded from his head. He grew large wings and began to breath terrible fire. All stood in shock and horror. The beast terrified all inhabitants of Aegis, animals fled and the Sons of\n\nthe Descendants were too weak of blood to stand infront of such evil fury. Only Malin, Urguan, Horen and Krug stood infront of the terror.\n\nIn Ibleeses right hand, a sword wrought in flame. Krug, naked and unarmed charged at The Daemon, throwing himself\n\nagainst the scalding scales of Iblees. He screamed in agony as his skin burned and decayed, becoming green and molten. Iblees was knocked off his feet, for the last time. He stood up, heaving in rage and fury, flames exploded from pores of his skin, he\n\nroared in anger and where he struck his sword the land collapsed and the ground erupted. And Lo, great was the Valour of Urguan and the Strength of Krug as they fought the beast. Powerful were the arms that carried Krugs Axe and strong was Horens heart as\n\n they fought in open combat upon the plains of Aegis. Malins sword was fast and swift, smiting Iblees upon his breast and sides.\n\nFor thirty years The Descendants fought Iblees, the world became a war torn mess. The dead were defiled, summoned from their\n\ngraves to follow Ibleeses mastery. The more mortal descendants died, the greater Ibleeses armys grew. It was a sad chapter in the World of Aegis, the brothers threw up their hands to God in prayer and in agony. Their creations destroyed, their children\n\nmassacred. Woe to the Sons of Man and Woman. Krug grew bitter, his resentment of his brothers increased for befriending such a beast. Urguan grew greedy, he fought valourously but began to hide his treasures underground. Malin feared for the lives of his\n\nchildren and did not leave his forest sanctuary. Horen was too ambitious, too weak of a leader, many of his people fought for Iblees and many of them died of recklessness. It seemed the world was destined for ruin. Iblees grew in strength and\n\nThe Descendants weakened. Until one day.\n\nOne day where the sound of horns could be heard from the far east. Beautiful horns echoing all across the skies of Aegis. God had heard their prayers.\n\nAn army of Aengul and Daemons from the Seven Skys had\n\nappeared on the grand shores of Aegis. Their majesty and beauty so strong that all The Descendants could see was a flash of power white light erupt from the east. Only Malin with his strong sight could see the figures of light as they sped across the\n\nskies towards the armies of Iblees.\n\nIbleeses soldiers burned where they stood, The thousands of Skeletons and Zombies burst aflames and his living servants fled. There in the right middle of the world, he was cast down and chained by The Aengul and\n\nDaemon. A robed figure with brown hair and a black wreathed apparation stood before him. They were a terrible image to look at, all shyed down and bowed in their majest and glory. They stood before Iblees, knowing he was immortal and could not be killed,\n\nsentencing him to banishment to the void where his dark soul would be forever trapped in torment.\n\nBut..\n\n\n*You quickly grab the next volume*", ""),
        StaticBook("Pyromancy,AGuide", "§b[In Costume] Archibald Cyrion", "Pyromancy, A Guide.\n\nFire Evocation, otherwise known as pyromancy, is the art of creating flames from the  very essence of the Void itself.\n\nGetting Started:\n\nKnow you may ask\"How do I even get to the Void?!\"\n\nWell ask no further.\n\nA simple week or two of meditation will hopefull get you along the lines of connecting to the void.\n\nImagine the void as a\n\nwindow within your mind, and through that window is energy (of sorts). To keep that window open there needs to be something holding it open, in other words: your energy, call it mana if you will.\n\nAfter connecting to the Void:\n\nAfter managing to connect to the void, a mage simply has to get better, through the means of meditation and practice. \n\nOnce a mage has formed a sort of \"bond\" with the void, they may now begin to summon flames.\n\nHow do you\n\nask? Well all you need to do is know how a flame is, how it is made, how it not only destroys but purify, how it burns, basically BE THE FLAME.\n\nOkay, I Managed With the Void and How Fire Works, Now What?\n\nNow you get to the fun part.\nWith the connection of the void and the knowing of how fire works, you probably know how to do it, somehow.\n\nAt first a mage in there first week or two will barely\n\nmanage to get a spark going, much less a ball of fire. However after continues effort and meditation, a mage can achieve their goal of mastering fire evocation over the course of around five elven months.\n\nFire:\n\nNow you may be asking how are you going to actually use it in the terms of combat. Well obviously you, with some practice, mold the flame into that of a sphere and condense it. The stronger larger the flame, the greater the energy. \n\nAs of this,\n\nyou can also cause an explosion of the fire as it contact with a surface, the size of the explosion depending on the strength of the mage.\n\nNow after reading this, you may or may not want to be a mage. But good luck!\n\n- Archibald Cyrion, Head of the Cyrion Bloodline", ""),
        StaticBook("HarbTale Vol.II", "§bOrithur", "A Harbinger's Tale\n\nVolume II\n-------------------\n\nWe went under many names. Harbingers, Dark Leuitenants, Hiishtgul, but no matter what we were called, our reputation for hideous destruction,\nmutilation and fear\n\nwas known universally. Our first major target was the Druidic Grove of Anthos, were the Nine Harbingers gathered with the corrupted footsoldiers to slay the peaceful tree-folk. Needless to say, it was a slaughter. And we loved every moment\n\nof it. The acts of evil we performed were bliss to us.\n\nWe resided in Setherien's distant corrupted lands where I, the keeper of his knowledge and his library, constructed a mighty spire where it might be stored. Despite my corruption\n\nit seems my love for books remained untouched. It was here that I endlessly studied the races, and even the Order of the Golden Lance. Those seeds of doubt within my ashen mind grew small sprouts upon discovering so much about the world we sought to\n\nvanquish. Nothing made sense to me, and I at first voiced my concerns to my brothers. They spoke of treachery and it was then I saw that I was the only one, the only one to not be entirely mindless to the whim of Setherien.\n\nMany moons passed,\n\nand many more acts of slaughter proceeded. Continually villages and cities fell, more and more innocent victims of the Drakaar would fall, their bodies rising as twisted, distorted versions of their previous selves.\n\nI initially watched with a sense of\n\nglee, but this glee faded as those seeds of doubt stretched into long vines, and the realisation of what was occuring continued to gradually dawn upon me.\n\nI decided action needed to be done, and I summoned my library spire to the\n\nfallen elven capital where I had told Setherien I'd be expanding the library's knowledge. Although a Drakaar, Setherien's lust for knowledge as all dragons do lust for was also untouched, and he willingly accepted my quest. In truth, I had wanted\n\nto contact the elves in a nearby settlement, as often adventurers would venture to my corrupted spire, where I would speak and discuss things endlessly with them. Needless to say I was threatened and often attacked, but despite this, I continued to learn.\n\n\nAs my painful release from Setherien's corrupted began to reach its close, I was attacked. The elves only saw that I was a Harbinger, the creature that had destroyed their home and loved ones, so I do not blame them for felling my spire.\n\nSetherien however, did begin to see what was becomming of me. I sensed his eyes watching me always, his distrust of me would be my undoing and I knew this. So I escaped. I latched my lifeforce to one of his Bloodshards and fled from Anthos. Alone.", ""),
        StaticBook("A letter", "§bAnonymous", "Fear the Old Dark as Ryder did.\n\nThis is only the beginning.\n\nThere shall be no end.\n\nGod is with us.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Dragos", "§bkido122", "On Dragons\nThere Life and Death\n\n      By Sam King\n\n     Chapter 1: Birth\n\n Dragons are, known by most everyone, born by egg much like our domesticated and less dangerous, Chicken. Ounce the egg is laid it goes on a one month incubation period. The mother dragon will warm her eggs with her belly,\n\nlaying next to to it, gently mumuring away, like a loud rumbling purr, as she increases her internal heat. She would do this for hours at a time for about a month, until the time the eggs hatch, at which point the egg now begins its life as a hatchling.\n\n Chapter 2: Hatchling\n \n After the egg hatch's, the hatchling will, if all goes well, stand on its four legs, strecthing its wings for the first time. It is important to note that dragons are not yet able to fly at this young age, and won't be able to for\n\nquite some time. Dragons at this age are around the size of a wolf, and are thought to be relativly tame and kind, much like a puppy. For its first week a hatchling will wander around its nesting site, never traveling out of eye sight of its mother.\n\nIt is during the second week of a hatchlings life that is left alone, as the mother goes to hunt to provide both her and her hatchlings hunger. The Hatchling is then left to its own accord, and begins to hunt small rodents and animals. The Third month is\n\nwhen the hatchling is now able to hunt on its own, under normal circumstances, and is when the fires within begin to bubble up, though not able to breath its deadly fire, it is good to note, smoke can be seen from their nostrils and mouth. When the\n\nhatchling reaches a year of age, is when it is left alone and now considered a Drake, or \"Teenager\".\n\n\n\n  Chapter 3: Drake\n(Next Page)\n\nDrake are still unable to use its deadly fire, but its bow a fierce and dangerous hunter, around the size of horse and rather grumpy. This age is often considered to be their \"Awkward\" phase in their life., as they are prone to explore great distances for\n\nno appairent reason, which is why they where said to be the most commonly sighted age of a Dragon. They have also been said to have caused the most havoc, as they are for some reason, really agressive and proned to attack anyone who got to near to them.\n\n  Chapter 4: Adult\n\n Little is know about adult dragons, as they were rarely ever said to be sighted. What is known how ever is at this stage is whena dragon is now able to, 1-Breath Fire, 2-Fly, and 3-Mate. Adult dragons are thought to be rather\n\nunagressive, except for a few circumstance which I will get to soon, as they have been rarley sighted and don't attack often, if at all. Noe the mating rituals of dragons is, ofcourse, unknown, mostly likely lost in time. What is known is this, they\n\nbecome very agressive and is one of the few times they are said to be. During their mating season, time is also unkonw, is when they are said to attack towns, as when a Adult has its nesting site picked, nothing will stop it from nesting their, even if it\n\nis already occupied. It is also worthy to note that the legend and myth that dragons have a affinity to treasures, is neither proven or disproven, though most likely false. As to why and what purpose a dragon would horde treasure is unknown, except to\n\npossibly attract potential mates.\n\n\n\nChapter 5: Wyrm's\n\n Almost nothing is known about Wyrms, other then they are some of the oldesy and anciet dragons to ever \"Exist\". When an adult\n\nbecomes a wyrm is unknown, what is know though is that they are to be feared, extremly feared.\n\nChapter 6: Death\n\n Natural deaths hav enever been know or spoken of for dragons. The only few deaths of dragons\n\nspoken of is caused by few curagous knights/wizards, even then this legends and stories have no real reason to be thought of as fact in nearly all occasions.\n\n   Authors Note:\n \n This entire book is put together by a few years of researhc into myths and lengend s of these grand beast. Nothing written in this book is inherently fact, and should not be treated as such. This is just the most reasonable\n\npossibility's concerning \"Dragons\" few, if not no, facts on these beast exist. \n\nDedication is to all who enjoy the mysterious and unknown in the, as well as to those who enjoy our history, though this it not, per say \"History\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Foul Play", "§bHileia'elr", "-----Foul Play-----\n\nWritten by Hileia'elr\n\nCan a simple man overcome his feelings for the most lovely creature he's ever met; Or will he have to express his true feelings?\n\nIt was a day like any other in the Caliphate. The sun was shining, there were few clouds to be seen, and there were plenty of travelers coming to Al- Wakhrah looking to make some coin, or buy some supplies.\n\nIn fact, for Larrion, it was the perfect day to run a shop. His store was flooded with customers, wanting to buy some goods from the man. Larrion would shout out, pleading with the sea of people in his tiny shop to make a single-file line.\n\nAfter about an hour of the alchemist selling to the large amount of travelers in his shop, a man in a red hat approached the counter. It was his friend, Keltran. \"Aye, Larrion, how you doing?\" Larrion simply groaned, wiping off the counter.\n\n\"What do you want?\" Larrion said with a neutral tone.\n\n\"Well...\" Beltran began, \"I felt somewhat sorry about what I did to you a while ago...\"\n\n\"Wait.\" Larrion started. \"What did you do now?\"\n\n\"Oh! S-So you don't know?!\" Keltran exclaimed.\n\n\"You fool... The hell did you do now?\"\n\n\"U-Uhm... Why don't you go for a nice walk while I watch your store?!?\" Keltran nervously stated.\n\nLarrion gave him a dead look. \"This isn't over... Here are the keys.\"\n\nAs Keltran watched the store, Larrion walked out of his shop, turning to the left to see the lines of small stores set up.\n\nHe walked pass the fountain, and made a sharp turn into his friend's store.\n\nAs he opened the doors to the small shop, he noticed a person behind the counter, sorting some books.\n\nIt was none other than Netiley the Vixen. She was sorting her collection of magic books, guides, and novels for sale.\n\n\"Ooh, hello, Larrion!\" she said. \"Have you come for your royalties today?\"\n\n\"Er, yes...\" Larrion replied. \"How many of my books have you sold?\"\n\nNetiley plopped a brown sack on the counter. \"See for yourself.\" she said.\n\nAs Larrion opened the pouch, about 85 minas shimmered with a sparkling flare. Larrion then dipped his nose inside the bag and took in a deep breath.\n\n\"Aah, minas...\"\n\n\"Thank you, Netily.\" Larrion said, as he placed the pouch into his bag. \"Yuuup! No problem.\" Netiley replied.\n\nAs Larrion was just about to leave, he noticed yet another figure over the counter...\n\nIt was a chicken. A small, white, chicken, sitting behind Netily on it's lap.\n\nLarrion stared for quite some time. \"Who is that?\"\n\nNetily pointed. \"Aye, that would be Hegory.\"\n\nLarrion stared at the bird for moments, when he finally asked, \"Can we go upstairs? I want to introduce myself to your friend.\"\n\nNetiley shrugged, and opened the door to the upstairs area for him and Hegory.\"\n\nAs Larrion and Hegory sat down at a table for two, they stared eachother in the center of their eyes for quite some time. It was only a minute or so, but to Larrion, it felt like hours.\n\nLarrion broke the iceberg.\n\n\"So... what is it you do in the shop?\"\n\nThe chicken made a clucking noise.\n\n\"Cluck.\"\n\nLarrion placed his elbows on the table, and rolled his eyes.\n\n\"Do you have any hobbies?\"\n\n\"Cluck.\"\n\nFamily?\n\n\"Cluck.\"\n\nJob?\n\n\"Cluck.\"\n\nAt this point, Larrion decided to talk about himself.\n\n\"Well, I am especially interested in alchemy. Aside from that, I run a small store.\"\n\n\"Cluck. Cluck cluck, cluck-- Cluck cluck cluck, cluck CLUCK!\"\n\nAt this point, Larrion was blushing. Never before had anyone shown such compassion, such sympathy, and such care for what Larrion went through everyday. He finally found someone who would listen to him.\n\nLarrion removed the goggles that rested on his eyes, and held Hegory's left wing in between his own two. Larrion bent down to kiss the top of his love interest's wing, and smiled. Hegory couldn't smile, but instead looked to the ceiling.\n\nThe very next day, no one could seem to find Hegory or Larrion. Any sign of the two ever being there in the first place had vanished. As everyone searched for them, little did they know that the two were already at the docks, planning their new lives.\n\nThe two decided to live out at sea on a house boat. For the next 15 years, the two lovers would survive off of fish and fried eggs. They met few people during their time at sea, and that's just how they liked it...\n\n\n-The End", ""),
