        StaticBook("Wish Sumary ->", "§bKeovan Scarfen", "-------=[]=-------\nA Wish Part 2\n\nNow when i think about\nit, it may be a bit over dramatic..\nIm.. just wishing for a teacher is all..\nAs.. of now im looking for a teacher in alchemy or/and a teacher in Arcane Shielding.. But theres many people wanting\n\nfor their wish to be taken.. So.. i guess this is just a dream for me\n\n~Keovan Scarfen\n(( nanoninja23 ))", ""),
        StaticBook("Aeriel Question", "§bBael Tunnelsmasher", "THE AERIEL QUESTION\n-------------------\n\nA discussion on the worship of the diety\n    \" A E R I E L \"\n\n\n\n\n\n       Archbishop\n Bael Tunnelsmasher\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nFor the longest period of time, certain members of the Irongut clan; dwarves of otherwise good repute, have been accused of heresy.\n\nUpstanding individuals, such as Hiebe, Algrim and Phelrin have professed faith in Aeriel as a true God\n\nand have, by some twisted circumstance, suffered because of it.\n\nWith no historical evidence, whether in ruins, artefact or record, holding that Aeriel was ever worshipped by the early Dwarven societies, and the\n\nsignificant distaste for Aeriel was compounded further by the betrayal of the dwarves by the Ascended sages in the late-Aegis period.\n\nSave for a few faithful, Aeriel-belief is detested and even branded heretical by some factions of the\n\ndwarven people, most significantly found in the faction of Kjell and his clansmen.\n\nBut historical reasoning aside, is there any true founding for such distaste and hostility?  \nThe Sages were revealed in the end\n\nto have been corrupted by Iblees, so their motives were certainly not pure, but neither were they the orders of their patron. Which brings us to the \"Aeriel Question\".\n\nIs Aeriel-worship compatible with the dwarven faith?\n\nMany would say \"no\".\nFewer yet say \"yes\".\n\nMost care very little, but for the sake of religious stability, I will examine the similarities and attempt to reconcile the mainstream creed with that of the Aerielist faction in the faith.\n\nThe most common claim is that Aeriel is merely another name for the commonly accepted divinity named \"Anbella.\" A mistake to be sure.\n\nAeriel is best known for being the opponent to the fallen daemon Iblees as the other divinities stood\n\nstill and allowed him to rampage on the mortal realms, however, those informed few of us are aware that Aeriel is infact a guardian of the Dead.\n\nA sphere that is totally incompatible with the Godess of Life and Living: Anbella. Many would rejoice\n\nat hearing of this incompatibility; particuarly the Irehearts, however, the sphere of Aeriel is compatible with another divinity in the dwarven faiths:\n\nDUNGRIMM\n\nI suggest that Aeriel is infact an aspect of\n\nDungrimm. Now it is also knowledge to the learned that Aeriel is not a war-like diety, whereas Dungrimm is the embodiment of righteous war.\n\nMy suggestion is not that Dungrimm is Aeriel, but rather Aeriel is the personification of Dungrimm's more\n\nfeminine traits. The feminine aspects of a certain diety, while Dungrimm is the personification of the masculine traits of the same diety.\n\nOf course, even as I am the supreme shepherd and lord of the Dwarven faiths, it is not within my\n\nauthority to add or subtract from the established order as many others would do with impunity, but rather should I succeed in recalling the other remaining bishops, this matter of doctrine will be sealed in Synod and all will be bound by decree.\n\nSEALED BY\nHIS HOLINESS;\nBAEL TUNNELSMASHER\nIN THE REIGN OF\nHIS HIGHNESS;\nKING THORIK GRANDAXE\n\nSigned:\nAbsp. Bael T.\nBsp. Thrym I.\nBsp. Dominic I.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Wish.", "§bOsmond Swiftheart", "*The handwriting seems to be written in cursive, yet much more advanced*\n\nA wish.\nMy wish would be to become a strong cleric under the guidance of the blessed Tahariae.\nI wish to protect all that I love,\n\nAll whom I've befriended, and dispose of all the dark beings who wish on one's destruction or even the entire world. \nTo heal those who are in need. To make my mark on the world, make Hesh proud.\nThat is my wish.\n\n*On the final page is a name written as a signature*\n\nSincerely,\n\n        Osmond\n      Swiftheart", ""),
        StaticBook("Paladin of Xan", "§bAdorellan Sintel", "Xan:\n~~~\nA burning light in the\nunforgiving darkness.\nA sword and shield to\nthe order of the realm.\nXan is an Aengul, that which embodies the illuminating hope of Guardianship and Order. Xan was known for his war with a threat to the mortal -\n\n- realm. A Drakaar, one so strong and wise he was thought to be the herald of the Drakaar themselves. Xan's once powerful and strong order fought endlessly with Setherien. He bestowed his boons upon a line so ancient Xan 's blood mixes with theirs. The -\n\n- Athna's. Hilan Athna, the grandfather of the three siblings, Sarah Athna, Hilan Athna the II and his Guardian, Herun Athna now known as Xath. Hilan, the grandfather had his order convene and thus a might weapon of war had been forged. -\n\n- 'The Golden Lance.' A weapon so powerful that Hilan named their Order after it. This weapon was fueled with Aengulic power that of Xan's which gave it it's fierce, golden shine. Years passed and nine of HIlan'sd CHampions were slain and drafted into -\n\n- the dark side. Years passed and Hilan had passed away, bestowing his gifts and magics upon his grandchildren whilst Xan's bestowed the gifts of mind, strength and will to the three. By this time, Setherien had split the Lance in three which was -\n\n- was soon re-forged by Herun Athna with an immense amount of magic. Later, the Golden Lance was plunged into the depths of Setherien's chest, ending his reign of tyranny over Anthos & The Fringe.d Now, it is said Herun and Crumena were born anew as -\n\n- Xan's Guardianship and Order which were drawn together like brothers in arms.\n-------------------\n\n\nXan, however, fights a war of his own which only the likes of Aengul's and Daemon's can fight.", ""),
        StaticBook("Caenir's Task", "§bCaenir", "Dedicant Essay: §0\n§0Caenir. §0\n§0\n§0The matter I fear most in this life, which has been given to me by the Aspects; is not one of death, loneliness nor loss of lliran. What strikes fear in me is the thought of losing the 'way of our people'. The thought that all\n\nwe hold dearest to ourselves be it family, Aspectism, Druidism, or the homes that we sleep in, may be taken from us by those who despise us. For me, it is the idea of losing Malin's teachings, the disintegration of the druii, the fall of the Dominion and\n\nthe burning of our ancient scrolls that if any keep me in fear. Now, there is no manner that comes to mind of how I may overthrow this fear. The only way to do this is to persevere. Through thick and thin, that we continue the way of our ancestors.\n\nTeaching the next generation what we know in the hope they too will pass on what they learnt. As a result, though this dedicancy has opened my mind much more to the Aspects than it had been prior, the fear that dawns on me can not be mended by such.\n\nThe Aspect that I believe myself to relate most to, if it was not already obvious, is Cernunnos, the Father, the Horned Man. As an 'Ame who was brought into the Sirame of Linandria as a guard when I was a mere thirty-seven years old. I was thought to hunt\n\nkill and trained to fend off any threat as a child soldier. Through my experiences and confrontations with different races, and bandits, it was Cernunnos's cycle of nature that I became most accustomed to from a young age. Since, whenever I was required\n\nto load my bow, it was he who guided my arrow to reach its mark. Though this may seem very sinister at first. It was only through this thought pattern that I became even more acquaintanced with the teachings that the Father has to offer. As in time I\n\nwould understand his balance of nature more thoroughly. That 'death' is not sinister, as so many believe. That it is merely the way of life. We are born to grow under the Green Lady, before Cernunnos claims us. Through this understanding alongside my\n\npersonal experiences is why I believe myself to relate more to Cernunnos out of the two Aspects. Seeing how my life and duty revolves around defending my home and kin through violence, as a Virarim. Mainly of which ends in blood and death, it is Cernunnos\n\nthat looks over this balance of nature. As he and I are both men of the hunt, I feel a degree of familiarity with him. §0\n§0\n§0From the pages I have written prior I hope that I may have conveyed my opinions clearly and efficiently on, 'did my dedicancy help me\n\novercome my fear' and 'what Aspect do I feel I relate to most and why' as asked for this task. However, for a bit of assurance, I shall give a short summary of my essay. Firstly on my fear, that it can not be overcome by that of my dedicancy, for reasons\n\nexplained. Secondly, that I feel Cernunnos is the more relatable Aspect, given my duty, and necessity to fight. §0\n§0Ahernan for reading.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Wishes", "§bDecimus", "I'm unsure if this is an OOC or IC wishing well so I'll provide a wish for both.\n\nOOC:\nI want a regular purple nametag without the perks of the donator!\n\n\nIC on Second Page\n\nIC:\n\"I would like some sort of object that constantly produces air- magically.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("My Wish", "§bRodney Altman", "I wish I was an extraordinary blacksmith and could make great weapons and armor ((Daemonic or Aengulic Blacksmith))", ""),
        StaticBook("Mundane Healing", "hex37", "__Mundane Healing: The treatment of minor wounds with common herbs.__\n\nMatron’s Foreword: When I was studying medicine in Oren, a strange dwarf brought me with a book of medical recipes that used very common ingredients\n\nfor the treatment of various medical casualties, by an Aleya Darolien. One or two of them sounded interesting, though a large amount of them were, largely ridiculous, like one that claimed it possible to heal a major burst of an artery\n\nor internal organs with nothing but rose thorns and petals. In the interest of not wasting precious paper, I’ve recorded some of the more practical recipes in the book, and added one or two of my own, to make up for lost space.\n\n-Minor Cut (Matron)\nSimply apply a dose of  deceased Sentient-Slime to the affected area, and wrap a light bandage around it.  The slime helps stop the bleeding, and the mildly acidic nature of it is known to remove the taint from a body.\n\n-Headache (Aleya)\nBoil milk. Add honey while the milk boils. Take Dandelion stems and Rose thorns and put them in a thin satchel. Dip the satchel in the milk and let it infuse with the mixture for about 2 minutes. Slowly drink the milk.\n\n-Stomach Ache (Matron)\n\nBoil water. Once it hits a full broil, add honey until the liquid turns an amber color. Add tea leaves to a small bag, and let it soak in the mixture for about five minutes. Drink the tea slowly.\n\n-Soreness (Aleya)\n\nSimply apply rags with hot water to relax the muscles, and rest a lot.\n\n-Burns (Matron)\nSet your hands on some vinegar, and drench a clean bandage with it. Apply this bandage to the affected area, and wrap a dry bandage around this to keep the vinegar from getting absolutely everywhere.\n\nThe important thing about burns is to keep the affected area moist while it mends, as burned areas do not produce sweat properly. Vinegar is ideal for this, as it will keep the area moist, and not evaporate as water would. Be sure to check the burn wound\n\n daily until the skin can finally reform.\n\n-Fever (Aleya)\nKeep the victim’s body cool using cold water. Give him hot milk steeped with brown mushroom stems and ground rose thorns. It will fight off the disease. Keep the victim rested and feed him mushroom soup.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Wish <3", "§bJudas Windsor", "My wish: Judas Windsor\n\nI would like three horses: A faster jumper, a strong one, and a fast runner.", ""),
        StaticBook("My wish!", "§bIyath the Toymaker", "I wish to become a veteran at tinkering, please !\n\n-Iyath, the toymaker (a little\nheart has been drawn) <3", ""),
        StaticBook("Rivenza's Wish", "§bRivenza Acosta", "I wish for my granddaughter Beatrice to grow wealthy, powerful, and happy.", ""),
        StaticBook("My Last Thoughts", "§bAzoth Hawksong", "12, First Seed\n1614\n\nI don't know exactly what wretches at my heart. I know who, however.\n\nIndra, the Druid of the Cosmos, makes me feel happy and secure in the raging current that is this world. But I cannot and will not\n\nadmit any affection for her openly. I do not even know if I do.\n\nShe is enthralling and beauty to the highest level, yes, but she is also a good friend that I do not wish to jeopardize as I have in the past.\n\nPerhaps I view her as another task\n\nto undertake. A helpless woman to correct and fix...\n\n... no, that isn't it. Nether, she is stronger than me! Heh.\n\nPerhaps what I'm feeling is torn. She is with a man I respect though know is no lover. Perhaps I want to try and rescue\n\nher... or perhaps rescue myself. She is all I've ever wanted, yes, but the only way to keep her is to not try and take her.\n\nI will think on this more clearly soon.\n\n\nA. Hawksong\n\n14, Sun's Smile\n1614\n\nToday I grew the closest to Indra I think I have so far. We learned of one another's sensitivty around our ears and it sparked into a kissing and licking event of each other's respective regions.\n\nIs this wrong? It feels right but I cannot honestly say from where I stand. Her lips grazing my neck and ear was one of the most intense feelings my heart has felt since my connection to Aeriel.\n\nShe seemed to enjoy me returning the favor... it left\n\nme wondering if this is something I should be doing.\n\nNo, we didn't kiss nor make love but... I still feel odd for the interaction. There is obviously attraction among us both, both friendly and sexual. I am confused.\n\nWhat would Tristin do\n\nif he were to learn of this atrocity. He'd most likely attempt to spear my head like a cantalope but is it wrong I'd find it worth it? That Indra's lips against my flesh brings even my most basic morals into question?\n\nDear journal, I fear I\n\nam falling for my dearest Indra faster and faster with each coming day. Soon I will even come to the conclusion that my feelings are too unbearable... but I need to remain her friend. I cannot lose her lov- *scribbles* Not love. It can't be. I\n\ndeny it. We are simply great friends.\n\nOr is it love.\n\nI cannot judge this with my mind clouded with the feeling of her hair wrapped around my neck... I must retreat for now.\n\nA. Hawksong\n\n15, Sun's Smile\n1614\n\nIn our journeys the last few days I've realized my feelings finally. I feel a love for Indra the Cosmos Druid unmatched by any I've felt in centuries. But I fear I'll most likely never be able to express it outside the bounds\n\nof these pages.\n\nWe will be good friends and we will be excellent in the years to come... but I do not think we can afford to become lovers.\n\nIf the universe permits it, I hope we can someday. With all my heart.\n\nFor now I write these last entry. I will then give her this journal to read when the time comes, so...\n\nIndra, I love you. I don't exactly know in what regard, but I do. You make me the happiest mali in the world with just being with me through thick\n\nand thin. If you're reading this because I passed... live your life. Make good choices. And remember me and our time together.\n\nIf you're reading it on a whim... well, I hope you and I can make whatever we decide work.\n\nStay safe and Aeriel\n\nguide your exquisite soul.\n\nLove,\nA, Hawksong\n\n\nPS I won.", ""),
