        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-=-What Keeps a cleric going?-=-§0\n§0\n§0Aerith Oranor§0\n§0Bio: Originally from the city of Ker'nor back in Axios, he ventured out at the age of eighteen. Aerith met a dwarven friend which they opened a guild with in Sutica.\n\nWhy does he fight and for what?§0\n§0Aerith has a desire to protect those dear to him, also a desire to help others more than normally, he fights for his loved ones.§0\n§0\n§0Why did he become a cleric? §0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Aegrothond Case File §0\n§0         Subject #01", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Mother Grove:§0\n§0Went to cooking class, met Amber, tried to hook Amber and kasfer up, made an aeroplane swan, worked on a project at home, spoke to Emac about his lost violin.§0\n\nFenn:§0\n§0Arrived, moved into a house with a friend called Uka who was disguised as a girl to get close thi his father, played hide & seek, set up rooms, got some drinks, had a snowball fight and had an argument about me not slapping him\n\nSutica: §0\n§0Saw my gay undead friend get turned back to human form by ascended blood. Bought some potions.§0\n§0Met with Millie, Met with Kalesius (Head of Halsworthy military).§0\n§0Spoke to Sighard about Eye-Glow potion. Fought a weird gargoyle.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "This Songbook is dedicated to all Musicians, anyone who tries to sing. Never give up, practice.§0\n§0\n§0Kyral Winterleaf§0\n§0The Scroll Druid§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Song 1 - Memory\n\nI look through the window of my past.§0\n§0\n§0What will happen next?§0\n§0Is the question in my head§0\n§0I try to hold on to memories of you§0\n§0But they slip one by one§0\n§0If I could relive the miracle of you and me§0\n§0Would I truly be happy?\n\nBut I try, forever try§0\n§0\n§0Tossing away sadness I formed new bonds§0\n§0Lost in the sorrow of me and you§0\n§0I don't know, I truly don't§0\n§0If the past me couldn't live in the future§0\n§0Those days are gone, time to live again!\n\nHolding onto my memories§0\n§0\n§0Rain began to fall, and I broke down once again§0\n§0The pain from yesteryear had come back in waves§0\n§0I hold on to memories of you§0\n§0They will slip one by one\n\nI could relive the miracle of you and me§0\n§0But would I truly be happy?§0\n§0\n§0The answer is§0\n§0\n§0With new bonds formed I pressed forever onwards§0\n§0The sorrow of me and you given light by another", ""),
