        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "1. Murder Tepah§0\n§02. Update the Company about the Situation§0\n§03. Fix issue with House Dunnin§0\n§04. Trading Company§0\n§05. Organize army/recruit people§0\n§06. Look for employees §0\n§0(Neighbours, Gary, Contacts)", ""),
        StaticBook("Sacrifice", "§bShaman Falum'Lur", "The Purpose of\n         Sacrifice\n\n\n\n\n\n\nScribed by Falum’Lur\nTranslated by Tajo the Bald\n\nI. Sacrifice in the World\n\nIn the world, any man or woman comes to face many trials in plight of seeking their own destiny. Sacrifice is necessary among those who wish to continue their strife and salvation caused within the world itself.\n\n If one loses the perception of sacrifice it will often cause a state of refusal in sight of losing something that may be held dear or in other words simply something they would not hope to let go. Through the sacrifices that are made within the World\n\nand the Realm bring great knowledge upon the young as they come to understand the relentless nature of the World. Sacrifice in the world must be presented to remember our strengths, and those who cannot fathom the sacrificing that is made around them\n\nhave come to be preserved from the nature of the world.\n\nII. The Spirits and Sacrifice\n\nThe Spirit Realm remains the ultimate gain of sacrifice performed by the Descendants. The vastness of the Realm calls of the influence of many upon many Spirits casted upon the Mortal Realm.\n\nThe greatest sacrifice one can make is of mortal belonging or mortality itself and through these sacrifices the Spirits receives greater influence and grows upon the Realm. Praisal of a Spirit’s name is a form of worship and often does not require\n\n sacrifice but  provides miniscule Spirits to the Greater’s domain.\n\nIII. Mortality\n\nLife upon the world is never guaranteed with the best of every opportunity such is common nature. After the great struggle Man and Woman learned to rise against and fight these threats that wish to claim us at the end.\n\nThe end of a destiny is all that is expected while the ages of survival pass. It is a cruel fate to live upon this world by any means, but those who rise and search for their destinies have a long road ahead they are ready to endure. Others believe that\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nto die in battle while fighting the good fight is the best way to leave this Mortal world.", ""),
        StaticBook("D.L", "§bDavin Lodmund", "Missive to the Spellcrafter Archon I - The Archive of Urguan§0\n§0To the Spellcrafter Archon,§0\n§0The Radiant Man led us to a cave beneath the Thahn Mountain. There he performed some magic unknown to us and the door opened. Beyond it\n\nwas an archive, with a great rotating crystal set into the middle. One of our number was fool enough to touch it and fell into a coma from which he could not be roused. Unable to wake and thus unable to eat or drink he died within a few days.\n\nhe archive itself was a trove of Forgotten Dwarven texts, some sort of archive. They were so ancient that in our enthusiasm we unfortunately caused damage to a few. We took all texts that appeared to be of significance and are bringing them back to\n\nRivel for study. The Radiant Man believes the Forgotten Dwarves hold the key to the defeat of the Ravager. If they held the power to strike down an archdaemon, why are they extinct?§0\n§0- Spellcrafter Tarien Arvius", ""),
        StaticBook("Code of Conduct", "§bTaynuel Xayarath", "Druidic Code of Conduct§0\n§0\n§0Originally written by Dragon Druid Apollan§0\n§0\n§0Revised and restored by Tortoise Druid Muildir and Hare Druid Taynuel§0\n§0\n§019th Snow's Maiden, 1638\n\n1) Respect and love your brothers and sisters, no matter their transgressions, with the exception of druids who bring harm and danger to their kin. Such druids forsake their brothers and sisters and deserve no such care.\n\n2) Defend your brothers and sisters in times of danger as you would defend yourself, no matter their color or creed. We are all children of the Aspects, and as such we should be ready to take up arms for our family.\n\n3) No matter the consequences, a druid must always speak the truth. When we are caught in a lie, trust is lost, and with it respect. Without each, we cannot hope to grow strong as a family.\n\n4) A druid must never show favoritism with any one group. The balance is blind to the squabbles of the descendants, and to serve it best we must be accepting of all that need help.\n\n5) A druid may act as an advisor, but a druid at the head of a nation is destined for split loyalties and favoritism. Such can never be permitted without repercussion.\n\n6) In the event that a major conflict arises between druids that cannot be solved by the involved parties, the event should be brought before a neutral archdruid or hierophant to aid in solving the dilemma.\n\n7) Only a guide or archdruid of an affected circle may make decisions that affect that circle.§0\n§0\n§07a. Any druid below that rank or from a separate circle has no authority over that circle.\n\n7b. Shuns are Order-wide. In the case of a shun, a representative of each circle must be present for the shunning so that all circles are aware of the reasoning behind the shun.\n\n7c. In regards to decisions that affect the Order as a whole, a meeting must be called between the archdruids and guides of all circles to make a decision.\n\n7d. In the event of an emergency where no archdruids or guides of any circle are available, a hierophant may be called upon for a split-second decision. This may only occur if no archdruid or guide is available.\n\n7e. In the event that a hierophant's decision is found to be damaging to a circle or the Order as a whole, it may be revoked by an archdruid.\n\n8) A druid must never use overly critical or insulting language when referring to or speaking to their brothers and sisters. As an example, a druid can say their actions are stupid, but it is not okay to call the druid stupid.\n\n9) When criticizing a fellow druid for their actions, avoid being overly harsh. We are all descendants, and we are all very capable of making mistakes. Until we stop breathing, however, they are not irredeemable.\n\n10) A druid should never take from their brothers and sisters without permission. Stealing damages the bonds of trust required for strong, healthy relationships between druids to form.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n11) A druid should never intentionally cause damage to any property of another druid or the Order.\n\n12) A druid must carry themself in a mature, respectable manner at all times. Remember that you represent the entire Order in all interactions. Your actions reflect on druids as a whole.\n\n13) A druid must never boast of their achievements or their strength, nor should they ever seek power for power's sake. Absolute power corrupts absolutely.\n\n14) A druid must never use their gifts in such a way as to show off their capabilities purely for the sake of showing off.§0\n§0\n\n14a. If a druid is caught misusing their gifts, it should be immediately reported to an archdruid or hierophant for a proper investigation of the matter.\n\n15) When an archdruid makes a decision, all druids of the circle should do all in their power to heed their archdruid's word. Have faith in the judgement of the archdruids you have chosen.\n\n16) If a guide or archdruid feels that a decision made by an archdruid was not in the best interest of their circle, they may challenge the decision if at least one third of the active population of the circle is in agreement. In such a case, a\n\nneutral elder should be called forth to help resolve the matter. If a neutral elder is unavailable, a neutral archdruid may be substituted.", ""),
        StaticBook("D.L", "§bDavin Lodmund", "Missive to the Spellcrafter Archon IV - A Warning§0\n§0To the Spellcrafter Archon,§0\n§0I hope this message reaches you in time. We were deceived, the Seal was a false lead, the Radiant Man, or as he is truly called, the aengul Garzardiel, had\n\nhis own agenda all along, and Rivel faces imminent attack and possibly §0annihilation.Most§0 of the Spellcrafters in the task force are fully under Garzardiel’s sway, mere puppets to his will. I have broken free of his influence and escaped but in\n\nturn have lost both my powers from him and my skill with the Arcane. I fear how many of my decisions in the past months have been acts based not on my own judgement but on his influence!When we opened the Hall we found it littered with\n\nskeletal corpses: the Forgotten Dwarves were wiped out by a civil war: the ruling caste trying in desperation to give the Seal enough fuel to defeat the Ravager, and the people fighting back. It seems too that the ruling caste won the war and the death\n\nsimply fueled the Seal further. The city was also filled with hundreds of war constructs designed for raiding the surface for harvesting more souls: I suppose when you’ve enacted a near total genocide on your own people in the name of\n\nsurvival the deaths of a few hundred surface dwellers aren’t going to bother you. It seems these constructs wiped out the surviving Forgotten §0Dwarves.As§0 for the Seal, the machine itself is complete, but damaged: we\n\nsuspect the damage allowed vengeful souls to leak out and possess the constructs, wiping out the surviving dwarves. Garzardiel revealed that the goal of the Forgotten Dwarves was impossible: the Seal could never hold enough souls to\n\ntrap the Ravager, which begs the question, whatever does he want it for?§0\n§0Once he had access to the Seal Garzardiel took control of the constructs and ordered the elimination of all loose ends, all who knew about the Seal.\n\nThat means the Spellcrafters of our company that were not fully under his sway and Rivel itself. I attempted to conceal myself, but without my arcane powers it was most difficult. The last I saw of Garzardiel was him headed to the Seal Chamber\n\nitself, a writhing mongoose held by the neck in his grip. After that I was forced to flee the city, and as I left I realised the direness of our situation.§0\n§0The majority of soul harvesting constructs left for Rivel hours ago: I know not how long\n\nyou have to formulate a defence against their oncoming assault on the walls.§0\n§0I will find the keys and reseal this Hall. My last act will be to return the keys to their hiding places. I don’t know what Garzardiel really wanted to trap in\n\nthat machine, but Urguan’s Hall must never again be found.§0\n§0- Spellcrafter Tarien Arvius", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal, II, T.V", "§bThanatos", "Thanatos's Journal\n-\n(Base Information)\n\n Making this journal out of Inspiration of a dear friend of mine her name is Nona\n\n She also has her\nown journal if you.\nThe reader cares about this information\n\nMayor of Pembroke~\n\nMy name is Thanatos as you may presume..\nI am writing this journal for reasons as listed\n\nI will be attempting to explain my story of becoming Mayor of this town from the start to the current day..\n\n(Reference Pages)\n\n Chapter III, Page 5\n\n Chapter IV, Page 18\n\n\n\n\n\n(Read Volume III for the rest of the story..)\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nChapter III...\n\n ...After they'd all been rescued and brought to safety Thanatos would attempt to wake them up from their sleeping spell.. Starting with the nun girl...\n\nThanatos would shake her gently.. seeing what would wake her..\n\nthe shaking attempt was a success and\n\n Thanatos after a good minute or two was able to wake her..\n\n The nun tried to stand on her two feet and luckily didn't trip on her Nausea...\n\n\n She'd start to wake Virkian Agnew..\n\n Just as Thanatos would attemp to wake the lanky Arndt Sauer..\n\nThe girl unremorsefully smacked Virkian across the face with intention of hurting him on wake...--\n\n(Probably because he did some.. Sketchy stuff toward the nun..)\n\n Thanatos would wake the sleeping Arndt Sauer..\n\n\n The man was heavily confused on what had happened.. The same goes for Virkian with a red mark across his-\n\nface..\n\n\n Everyone would attemp to get up and walk outside to watch the fight between the men and the illusionary\n\n        Hektor Blackwood\n\nas they got outside two men were fighting.\n\n Ser Henry was fighting side by side with Kagura.. \n\n Kagura was injured as well as Ser Henry..\n\n Kagura was sliced on the side.. Luckily.. not fatal..\n\nSer Henry was roughed up mostly from small cuts and-\n\n-being hit with a blunt side of a weapon..\n\n Kagura and Henry would ready their swords as they charge him impaling him from two angles and then pressing him back into the ground..\n\nKaguras sword would snap as the undead broke it in two with--\n\n-his sword and he'd quickly free himself..\n\n Obviosly injured the undead was forced to try to evade the situation and flee..\n\n Kagura would push Hektor with his now.. Short... sword... and attempt to tackle him..\n\n Hektor blackwood quickly slipped out a blue potion as he hopped the walls and dropped it atop kaguras face as he jumps late.. he misses the tackle..\n\n Some people were amused at his failed tackle.. The blue potion put Kagura.. to sleep..\n\n We'd ressusitated at the tavern.. as we did the others prior..\n\n The nun once again would proceed to slap the color into his face.. but this numbskull took a couple smacks to awake.. His face was a ripe tomato that day..\n\n Later that day I had met with my courting partner Alijol and we'd talked about the intrusion of Hektor..\n\n I'd not explained how she'd looked before..\n I'll explain.\n \n\n (view next page)\n\n\n She would wear a green top with glowing Blonde hair with Golden bells in her hair paired up with Purple and Gold flowers..\n\n She ran the Apothecary in Pembroke.\n\n (view next page)\n\n\n  She was also a Snow Elf and I am a Human. (Which... a lot of people would normally dissaprove of these types of things..)\n\n The nun girl has left Pembroke but everyone was fine where they were at..\n\n Chapter IV...\n\n There was five or so undeads that had appeared afront Pembrokes keep..\n\n Guards on the inside requesting a reason for them coming..\n\n The undeads were very specific stating they want to speak to Lord Edward Suffolk about certain problematic things...\n\n Lord Edward would appear stating \"What's the meaning of undeads coming upon my door front demanding me.. Best be good..\"\n\n Lord Edwards tone would be cold and stern wearing his armor with a red cape around his backside with expensive weaponry at his hand.\n\n The undeads would reply and state...\n\n \"We have a... common.. enemy... you see....\"\n\n Lord Edward would nod his head saying \n \"I see and who'm is it..?\"\n\n\n The Undeads would reply...\n(I'll have to remove this for.. purposes.. I'm sorry to the reader... ask me in person I might be nice and explain..)\n\n The Undeads had intention of creating a temporary truce..\n\n Not to become friends in any way but to be truce..\n\n\nWe were very questionate but Lord Edward made decision to agree and be neutral until the\n\n-problem has been.. \ndone and over with...\n\n\nWe're no friends to undeads just note..\n\nPembroke has only formed a temporary truce to them for reasons as stated..\n\n\n Later on complications between us and the undead has rised..\n\n We'd both grown weary and questionate of one another as a month passed..\n \n Lord Henry was preparing a raid upon the undeads in fear they were going to--\n\nbreak the truce..\n\n I agreed at the time..\n\n\n We'd prepared to raid them and we'd gathered with the Prince of Hansetti Judah-Principality.\n\n\n He'd brought his men and Edward has prepared our men.. Including me and Edward of course..\nWe wont sit idle while we're at risk from undeads..\n\n\n\n\n   WE'D GATHERED AT THE GATES...\n          PEMBROKE AND THE MEN FROM HANSETTI HAD GATHERED TO ATTACK WITH US...\n\n\n(and this is not Haense it's Hanesetti.\n\n\n\n\n\n Lord Edward & The Prince would signal people to storm the undead fortress..\n\n\n\n\n\n The lot of us were halted at an iron door..\n\n We'd waited as the undead opened their doorways revealing a room with a pitfall with spikes..\n\n\n\n The Undeads would welcome us to the fortress...\n\nThey clearly upset we decided to come in with armor and wanted to decide a proper way to avoid fights and conflict as we had them outnumbered...\n\n We'd had a larger group.. It was expected they'd find another resolution without risking the downfall of their fort...\n\nSo we continued to play their talking game and decided to make another decision..\n\n\nUndeads are NOT allowed to come to Pembroke nor we to come to the Undeads..\n\n It should be noted Humans and Undeads had been traveling to Pembroke and from the Crypt.\n\n\n\n Hektor Blackwood ignoring this unknowingly came to Pembroke..\n\n(He was not avaliable the day of our attack.. He was doing other sorts of things away from fort..)\n\n\n Hektor engaged in a talk with me about undead things.. I'd prefer to leave out this information because it is dangerous information depending on who is aware of these sorts of things..\n\n\n\n Hektor mid chat would claim that he spoke too much and demanded me to speak upon a subject as well and I obliged..\n\nHektor asked of me...\n\"You.. think... edward... will... break... this... truce... again...?\"\n\n\n\n In which I replied..\n\"To what I know I am unsure.. but I wouldn't doubt he's likely not as of now...\"\n\n People had grown suspicious of Hektors visits as he proceeds to come back more and more.. Unaware.. of.. the agreement..\n\n\n Hektor would ask things of Alijol Inkalla that had made me question if I had been getting too comfortable around him...\n\nShe'd told me what he'd asked when he came into her Apothecary.. She told me at a different occasion..\n\n She'd said Hektor had come by and talked to her...\n\n after a while of talking offered to teach her simple brewing..\n\n I was enticed but later on we decided it's not a great idea..\n\n\n Edward would not approve of Alchemic uses and possibly even hang her for Witchery..\n\n I couldn't bear the thought..\n\nWe'd decided to turn down Hektors offer..\n\n\n I'd talked to Hektor a bit more personally and as he talked about undead things.. which I wont list.. He said he'd write me a book.. Translating these undead things to the human tounge from their language..\n\nI'd agreed to this.. \nHe agreed to this..\n\n\n It was settled that Hektor would write me a book about, \"Undead Things..\"\n\n I do not know why he offered this to me..\n\n But he has told me some of his past..\n\nI'll share for you all..\n\n Hektor had claimed.. \n\"I never wanted to be like this...... it wasn't by choice..... I used to be human.... the world has loved me as a person...... but as I was turned undead...... I watched as all my friends and family...... turned me away..disgusted.\"\n\n Of course.. this is all written from what I recall.. Sorry if I am not exactly correct if you're reading this\n Hektor.\n\n In which you most likely are..\n\nI'm still expecting a good book..\n\n Dwarves..\n\nFrostbeards and other clans dwarves go together as they were going to raid the Crypt upon the hill...\n\n The people of pembroke watched in confusion to what might have of caused this problem..\n\n But... before they came upon the hill.. Some of the dwarves came to town and entered the Tavern where I and Hektor was having a chat..\n\nThey'd took Hektor and used him as an ability to attemp to enter the Crypt..\n\n The Dwarves had then... started to travel up the hill..\n They got to the entry-way.. and demanded entry.. after that the dwarves were tossed a what I was told later on as..\n \"A gas that was Toxic like.. Deadly feeling.. even looking at it..\"\n\n The undeads had used this to create space inbetween Hektor and The Dwarves for an escape in which he fleed into the Crypt locking the door escaping from the dwarves..\n\n Minutes later.. Dwarves come rushing into Pembroke requesting drinks..\n\n Of course.. I was also the tavernkeep in which they explained the situation but not why they did it at the time..\n\n When the dwarves had got their drinks and left.. I'd traveled to the Crypt.. in which I had told them I'd got a lot of Dwarven Visitors --\n\nat my tavern... They'd handed me a green drink stating..\n\n \"You see any dwarves come by your Tavern slip some of this in their drink...\"\n \nAs of the time I am writing this Hamnil Frostbeard is selling Vials of it in Kaz'Ulrah.. I'll explain how..\n\n I'd came down and went to the tavern sending a bird to Hamnil.. He'd requested Dwarves to pickup the poison as I was in the tavern a couple days later they showed I was once again.. Talking to Hektor.. I'd given them the \"Package..\"\n-End of Volume II.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Avery§0\n§0Elisabella Vesryn - Belvitz Healer§0\n§0Acacia Moonves - Belvitz Healer§0\n§0North Bellatrix Stow - Arbor", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Dear Murielle,§0\n§0I know you think I am a traitor to Halsworthy, but hear me out. I was doing it for us, so we can know how to beat them.§0\n§0Now that the whole ordeal is over. I'm leaving them, and I shall suffer the consequences of doing so...\n\nwhether it be death or be hunted. I want you to know I am sorry. I was never a traitor.§0\n§0\n§0-Illiaana Acrenox§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The moon shines on§0\n§0my fair lover§0\n§0While the scent of hycanith drifts about§0\n§0\n§0Mayilu, Leyuan§0\n§0My attention is all yours§0\n§0Can't you see your spell has succeeded?§0\n§0\n§0Mayilu, Leyuan?!§0\n§0My eyes have fogged over all I have\n\nnow is your song.§0\n§0\n§0Hurry please find me§0\n§0I can bear it no longer§0\n§0Parting with you is a certain sin.§0\n§0\n§0Mayilu! Leyuan!§0\n§0Come to me now§0\n§0Before the sun rises§0\n§0Whisk me away in the dark of night§0\n§0Hold me so tightly§0\n§0Then never let go\n\nMayilu, Leyuan§0\n§0With my final sane breath§0\n§0I do declare my love immortal§0\n§0\n§0So please hurry to me§0\n§0\n§0Take no delay§0\n§0\n§0Whisk me away §0\n§0With you§0\n§0\n\nNormally I dedicate my writing to poetry and only poetry. It used to aggravate me to write something that could not be used, something that was purely self indulgent, but now I want nothing but myself. From the time I was a youth and on I threw myself in\n\nto different religions,philosophies, or revolutions trying to find something better. I suppose I have always had a giving heart, a desire for everyone to have a better life.§0\n§0- In an abandoned camp in the wastes\n\nI find myself writting thoughts again when I would be writting a sonnet for my lover, my fiance. I fear I will end up with an absent partner even if I join the Edict and if I join the Edict I fear I will be joining another false cause. My mind is tangled\n\nin worry; for my sons, for my fiance, for my future. Death certainly would be the most effective route, but I am much too proud for that and truthfully I think while I may benefit greatly from such everyone else would suffer. It is strange how I give so\n\nmuch of myself away with no price. It is strange that not a soul ever seems to be around for me when I struggle, is this from my lack of trusting or am I truly being used? §0\n§0-A fire in Holm\n\nWhile hunters run for their prize, trap her, and pierce her§0\n§0\n§0This medicine woman§0\n§0searches long for her treasure§0\n§0She walks long miles through brambles and thickets§0\n§0Her eyes set on the promise of the ruby of the forests\n\nand upon finding this§0\n§0powerful, elusive flower§0\n§0\n§0She takes a moment to lovingly caress it's petals, feel each detail§0\n§0\n§0And after having become so familir with each other§0\n§0She gently reaches under to pull up this flower\n\nand hold it so§0\n§0closely to her chest§0\n§0to start this alchemy§0\n§0\n§0A heart once§0\n§0frozen now thaws§0\n§0A flower once alone§0\n§0begins to spread§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "just talked to ozneat again, quite like em§0\n§0\n§0started smithing today, getting the hang of t?§0\n§0\n§0met gilda silvervein, quite like er§0\n§0\n§0made me first sword t'day§0\n§0\n§0met a GM i dont like em\n\nyou're gay bro lol§0\n§0\n§0sandk1ng was here§0\n§0lol", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "sorry I took your book, may the gods return it to you you poor soul who struggles with blah§0\n§0\n§0- a pagan\n\nQuick Reference Page:§0\n§0- Ug = Hello§0\n§0- Agh = And§0\n§0- Gruk = Know§0\n§0- Blarg = Home§0\n§0- Uruk = Orc§0\n§0- Snaga - Slave§0\n§0- Throm'ka = Formal greeting§0\n§0- Rulg = Thank you§0\n§0- Nub/yub = no/yes§0\n§0- Lat = you§0\n§0- Mi = I/me", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0WANDERING WARES§0\n§0Ledger\n\n6 DEEP COLD, 1645§0\n§0\n§0Books - 39§0\n§0Ink - 192§0\n§0Cactus - 70§0\n§0Feathers - 64§0\n§0Thanium - 1\n\n7 DEEP COLD, 1645§0\n§0\n§0Feathers - 0§0\n§0Paper - 64§0\n§0Books - 38§0\n§0Ink - 231§0\n§0Cactus Greens - 70§0\n§0Iron Swords - 6§0\n§0Candles - 6§0\n§0Sugar Cane - 64\n\n6 SNOW MAIDEN, 1646§0\n§0\n§0Lapis - 9§0\n§0Paper - 64§0\n§0Books - 31§0\n§0Ink - 93§0\n§0Cactus Greens - 70§0\n§0Swords - 9§0\n§0Candles - 3§0\n§0Sugar Cane - 64\n\n17 SNOW MAIDEN 1646§0\n§0\n§0Lapis - 9§0\n§0Paper - 64§0\n§0Books - 23§0\n§0Ink - 93§0\n§0Cactus Greens - 69 (nice)§0\n§0Swords - 8§0\n§0Candles - 3§0\n§0Sugar Cane - 41\n\n8 MALIN WELCOME 1646§0\n§0\n§0Lapis - 9§0\n§0Book - 17§0\n§0Ink - 74§0\n§0Cactus Greens - 69§0\n§0Sword - 4§0\n§0Candles - 3§0\n§0Sugar Cane - 100\n\n12 SUN SMILE, 1646§0\n§0\n§0Lapis - 5§0\n§0Shields - 8§0\n§0Books - 0§0\n§0Ink - 73§0\n§0Cactus Greens - 69§0\n§0Iron Sword - 21§0\n§0Candles - 3§0\n§0Sugar Cane - 100\n\n10 Amber Cold 1646§0\n§0\n§0Lapis - 5§0\n§0Shield - 7§0\n§0Book - 0§0\n§0Ink - 56§0\n§0Cactus Greens - 69§0\n§0Sword - 16§0\n§0Candles - 3§0\n§0Sugar Cane - 100", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "(The writing of the title page appears in large fine bold print)§0\n§0\n§0The Art of the Turtle§0\n§0\n§0By: Ragus Erischi\n\n(From here forward the writing looks like a very neat cursive, almost as if written with a calligraphy pen.)\n\nSwordsmanship is an acquired skill, though ironically many may see the art as mundane. Arguing that preposterous assumption, swordsmanship is a graceful, and very powerful art that one should master before they age into an elder.\n\nSwordsmanship is far from an easy sport. There are many different forms, and many different swords to choose from. There is the shortsword, the broadsword, the longsword, and the greatsword. Greatswords are too heavy for use, as only larger, non-humans\n\nweild them, but despite that they are an unecessary waste of fine iron. For this art, a general broadsword is recommended. Anything too short or too heavy would yield failing results.\n\nNow, to describe the action of using this Art, i'll refer to it as \"turtling.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§lCuron Court:§0\n§0\n§0§lList of Applicants:§0\n§0\n§0§lFirst Applicant:§0\n§0Sylverstre III Halcourt§0\n§0\n§0Reports that his Castle North of Curon has been build together with its Farms.\n\nThe Farms posses a good yearly Yield and the keep should ( So the Applicant) meet the required standarts.§0\n§0\n§0§lSecond Applicant:§0\n§0- Li Fin§0\n§0He would like to be the Judge of Curon, for the courts of Curon. §0\n§0\n§0(Von Croë Informs him though\n\nthat there are no written laws in curon and thus no fixed judge nor courts at this time. Whence there shall be we might contact Li Fin Again for thus §0position....Perhaps)§0\n§0\n§0- Li Fin then Asks to be in Charge of Law Making§0\n§0\n§0This has been Refused\n\n§o------------§0\n§0§o           -----------------§0\n§0\n§0§o ---------------------§0\n§0\n§0§o-------  ---------------§0\n§0\n§0§o*what had been written has been removed*\n\nas lawmaking is a power of the Duke and his Council.§0\n§0\n§0Li Fin thus asked to be part of it and the Witans presents discussed it.§0\n§0\n§0We decided to petition the Duke to make him a fellow Witan.\n\nThe Duke then Arrived. and Questioned Li Fin about his Ambitions and if he is right for the Job.§0\n§0\n§0His Grace Finally decided that if Li Fin makes a Draft/a proposal for laws and resides more often in Curon, that he would consider him for the position of\n\nWitan.§0\n§0\n§0§lFirst Applicant:§0\n§0\n§0The Duke Informs the First Applicant that he will soon tour the Holdfast, and then discuss the future of his Family with him.\n\n§lThird Applicant;§0\n§0\n§0§l- Aron§0\n§0\n§0He Asks about the Restaurant in the Commons District. Restaurant whoms former Owner has left and striped it of all belongings. He asks the Duke about the Ownership of the Restaurant , place that he wishes to\n\nAcquire Together with another man named Hunter.§0\n§0\n§0The Duke would agree to sell it for 400 Minas to them both (200 each)", ""),
