        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-----§0\n§05 bet§0\n§05 bet§0\n§0\n§0Naztherak\n\nThe Horizone Rose\n\nSSMRSMRHSRH\n\nRavena Avern§0\n§0An elven woman ready to devote herself completely to a cause.§0\n§0\n§0Has a daughter and a lover named Loras.§0\n§0Family in Sutica.§0\n§0\n§0Needs to get rid of her desires.§0\n§0She thinks she is in control, requires heavy guidance.\n\nWhat needs to be done?§0\n§0\n§0- Ears must be clipped§0\n§0- Evoke infertility§0\n§0- Teach new ideals§0\n§0- Teach what fear is§0\n§0- Family ties severed§0\n§0\n§0*** Evie, daughter of Ravena in Caroulstadt§0\n§0Wife is a witch, Celeste.§0\n\nEhier Evocress§0\n§0A voidal mage, in the gray area morally.§0\n§0\n§0Family to the infamous§0\n§0Evark Evocress, a danger in itself. Thus, requires a lot of guidance. §0\n§0\n§0Casts: §0\n§0** Electric evocation§0\n§0** Mental magic§0\n§0** Translocation\n\n-------------------Notes on politics:§0\n§0- Divided in two§0\n§0* Aurelian Party§0\n§0constists of liberals§0\n§0* Priorist Party§0\n§0priority of conserving human values\n\nSerenity Al'abass§0\n§0* resident of Antonius Avenue 12§0\n§0* presumably a mage§0\n§0* often seen with other women§0\n§0* house of three floors, somewhat rich\n\nCarolus Lane 1§0\n§0-> Resident is a white haired elf that doesn't want to know people§0\n§0>>>something to hide?§0\n§0-> Roguelike endeavor§0\n\nRozmeo§0\n§0* Caius Circle 1§0\n§0* Owns a building of atleast four levels§0\n§0* Presumably rich§0\n§0\n§0Scathach§0\n§0* Blood magi§0\n§0* Capable of helping      produce a new form§0\n§0-------------------Thanhium dealer:§0\n§0>>>find out\n\nLoras§0\n\nRavena§0\n§0- Killing", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Direwolf Entry:§0\n§0\n§0General information:§0\n§0Direwolves are bigger, stronger and much more aggressive then your standard wolf. These creatures are capable of reaching very high speed levels making them able to cover big areas of their territory\n\nIf you see one Direwolf or a few of them then don't expect that those are the only ones in the area. If they spot you, they will alarm other Direwolves in the area by howling. In no time the others will show up and swarm you.\n\nAppearance:§0\n§0Their furs can vary in many colors and patterns like your average wolves. They can grow to become twice the normal size of a normal wolf and have bloodshot eyes.\n\nLocation:§0\n§0The Direwolf territory we had entered was located in the south of Mixed Knolls where the desert bordered the Gules mountains.\n\nStrenghts:§0\n§0Their speed and numbers is what gets you. The minute one spots you and you hurt it, all the other wolves in the area start pouring in, chasing you with high speed.§0\n§0\n\nWeaknesses:§0\n§0Mixed Knolls is a desert land, there's nothing to climb there to get out of there reach and when a huge group of them is swarming you, you won't get the chance to fight back.§0\n§0\n§0Although near the Gules mountains, north of their territory\n\nis a small pond coming out of the mountains. This is where you can lure them in to and fight them in the waters where they're easy to handle§0\n§0\n§0Value:§0\n§0Their pelts can be sold as well their teeth and heads§0\n§0\n§0pelt: 2 minas§0\n§0Tooth: 10 minas§0\n§0head: 80 minas\n\nAggresive rating: Hostile, they attack on sight§0\n§0\n§0Danger rating: 5§0\n§0if a lot of them is c", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Surviving and Thriving in the Empire of Man§0\n§0\n§0by Acolyte Costello of the Canonist Church\n\nTables of Contents:§0\n§0\n§0Introduction§0\n§0\n§0I. Horen Bloodline§0\n§0II. Nobility§0\n§0III. Church§0\n§0IV. Minor Tidbits\n\nIntroduction:§0\n§0\n§0As of late, I have noticed a sharp increase in newcomers that are executed, shot in the head with crossbow bolts, shot off of balistas and have had their hands cut off. I am a kind man, and therefore\n\nhave drafted this guide for newcomers to survive, and even thrive, in the Empire.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Enjoy.\n\nI. The Horen Bloodline§0\n§0\n§0Firstly, let's start with the top. The Horen family makes up all the Imperial royalty. They are the big-shots, the head-honchos, the capo di capi. They are distinctly identifiable by their wearing of purple aristocratic outfits.\n\nThey are heavily protected by the Nauzica (Imperial Guard). Always refer to the Emperor as \"His/Your Imperial Majesty\" and any Princes/Princesses as \"His/Her/Your Imperial Highness\". Treat them with the utmost respect.\n\nII. The Nobility§0\n§0\n§0While the Horens are all good and dandy, one must keep in mind that they do not micromanage the entire empire. They break up the political power. The Empire is made up of Kingdoms. The amount of kingdoms will change, obviously. But the\n\nbig ones are Renatus (the Kingdom containing the capital), Haense (the home of Raevir/Waldenian folk), Curon and Adria. The King leads their respective kingdom. After this, the power is then broken up towards nobility. Counties, Baronies, etc.\n\nHowever, most people are gathered in the capitals of these kingdoms, rather than the local fiefdoms. Always count on the Imperial capital to host the most people. Don't make the mistake of treating the Horens nicely while spiting the Nobility and Kingdom\n\nroyalty. It can get you killed. Knights are a branch distinct from Nobility. The Knighthood is often unified under particular Orders of chivalry. In order to become a Knight, one must squire (apprentice) under an existing knight, or be personally granted\n\nthe title by the Nobility or King, mayhaps even the Emperor himself. Obviously, squiring is far more common. When speaking to a knight, the best way to refer to them would be \"Ser\". I will not go through the hassle of listing the noble families.\n\nIII. The Church§0\n§0\n§0Too many people make the mistake of admiring the secular side of a government, yet forgetting about the spiritual side. I will not try to convert anyone to Canonism, but when you're in the Empire, respecting God is paramount to your\n\nsurvival. In fact, it's definitely the most important variable. The Church's policies bleed into even secular systems and laws. For example, many women are assaulted and detained for exposing parts of their body via lack of clothing.\n\nCover yourself head to toe, ladies. If you insult Canonism, you can and will get killed. Sometimes by a guard, sometimes by a Knight. Hell, sometimes by some random schmuck with a Crossbow. Us Imperial citizens love God. Now, Church policies change with\n\nthe coming and going of every High Pontiff (leader of the Church). Therefore, you should keep yourself up-to-date on the Church policies. One year, you can cast magic willy-nilly, the other, the Pontiff calls a Deus Vult situation and you're ganked as you\n\ncast a single spell. That's right, I'm looking at you, mages. Aren't mages supposed to be smart? Why do they always come to the city of God looking for a fight? It's beyond me...\n\nIV. Random Tidbits§0\n§0\n§0-Foreign Recruiting is currently illegal. Don't do it.§0\n§0\n§0-Sometimes, you", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Today, I watch the sunrise in the feilds of Cyrilsburg. There's a beautiful tree here, with soft pink blossums. My house may be in the city, but my heart certainly remains in the wilds of Atlas. §0\n§0\n§0-Ellie\n\nIt's snowing outside today. I'm glad my house has these large windows. I've seen some with almost no windows at all. It's like a dream, even if I don't have any furniture yet. §0\n§0\n§0-Ellie\n\nWhile I love living in the city, I can't help but §0feel...lonely§0. My house is wonderful, and the people here are very friendly. But I go on all my adventures alone and the closest I have to friends are the older men who helped me settle in.\n\nI miss home, with my family. I tried to get back to Norland but I couldn't find it. I might really be all alone out here.§0\n§0\n§0-Ellie\n\nI think I made a friend! Her name is Esther Lester, she sells honey all around Atlas. We climbed on roof tops and she asked me about my life plan, but I didn't really have an answer. I guess I want to travel, but I don't want to do it alone.\n\nMaybe this is the companionship I am looking for. She does seem up for an adventure after all.§0\n§0\n§0-Ellie", ""),
        StaticBook("Melchiors diary", "§bSigtrygg \"Skald\" Bjarnisson", "I don't know what's going on anymore. They were all fine. There was nothing to worry about. I mean cure worked, but Reinhart seems to be showing symptoms again. I have to get him back into the lab and make sure it'll all be fine. I just have to.\n\nIt's not going well. He's getting more sick. His skin turned black the other day. I don't understand! It all was fine!\n\nOthers are showing symptoms too. They are coming to be for the same cure, but it doesn't work anymore. Maybe if I trible the dosage? Yes. It should work. It must work.\n\n[!] Blood is splattered over this page. Odd. Seems more... black than normal.\n\n GOD save them. Please. I didn't know. I really didn't know! It was good! IT WAS WORKING! Please!\n\nI... I think... I found something. It seemed to work better than previous cure... it doesn't turn them back from... from... that. But it stopped some of them from turning.\n\n Cure... Or... whatever it is.\n\nRight lever, central button, left button, back lever, right button, left lever, back lever again.\n\n Don't fuck it up Melchior... You have to save them. Save him. He's your little brother.", ""),
        StaticBook("´`", "§bCorvus Keint", "Short stories series: \n\n           RAVEN\n\n\nShe had her mission. As Always.\n\nQuickly, she transformed herself for the third time that night and flew off into the stormy sky.\n\nWhen she neared the castle, she swooped down to the throne room and entered through an open stained glass window depicting a phoenix.\n\nShe landed on the red carpet in front of the king. Heavily armored knights stood on each side of the room.\n\nThey snickered at the \"clumsy\" bird. Inclunding the king who slouched in his red-cushioned seat of gold.\n\nSuddenly, a strong, silver wind whirled around the bird as it grew to the size and shape of a human, clothed in a long black cloak.\n\nShocked, the guards flinched and the king sat up in his throne, his hands gripping the armrests. Before him stood a black figure with a hood. All he could see were the tender lips on its face. \nInhaling deeply, she let her ebony hair tumble down her back\n\nas she removed her black hood.\n\n\"I am Raven\", she proclaimed, her forest green irises glaring straight into the stunned eyes of the malicious king. \"And I have come bearing a message. Step down from your throne and\n\nand crown the rightful ruler of this kingdom King Phoenix. If you do not, you shall be cursed for the rest of your days.\n\nKing Vulture's eyes stormed with fury. Raven could see lightning flashing in them.\n\n\"Never! Guards! Kill her! Now!\"\n\nThe knights charged at her, shouting. But Raven simply transformed back into a small raven. She lunged at the king. He blocked his face with his arms, but it was no use. The raven's claws\n\nhad touched the top of his head. The curse had been cast.\n\nFor the rest of his days, King Vulture was known as the Beggar Serpent. He could do nothing but crawl for his life, struggling to escape the phoenixes ready to devour him.\n\nHe lived in the holes of the Phoenix Palace, determined on getting revenge on Raven.\n\nRaven, she had returned to Phoenix to tell him the good news. He returned to his palace, defeated the army of Vulture's remaining men and took back his throne and\n\nand kingdom. As he sat in this throne, one day, gazing at the scarlet and orange stained glass windows, he noticed a little black bird at his side.\n\n\"Raven? Why are you still here?\"\n\nI am waiting for you to tell me what to do next.\n\n\"You don't need to do anything else for me. You have saved the kingdom. You are free\"\n\nAnd that lifted the curse on Raven.\n\nPhoenix was the first human being to ever say that to Raven, instead of throwing at her more orders.\n\nShe had been cursed to do whatever she was told and many took advantage of that. But Phoenix was selfless. Instead of flying away to do whatever she pleased, Raven used her freedom to stay with Phoenix. They were soon wed and lived merrily all their days.\n\n\n\n\nWritten by:\n\n\nCorvus Keint,\n\n\nLord Merentel's squire.", ""),
        StaticBook("Congratulations", "§bGrigori", "Congratulations!§0\n§0\n§0u r big dumb", ""),
        StaticBook("To Prince", "§bRed", "To his Imperial Majesty,§0\n§0\n§0The hearts of all Adrians congratulate you on your wedding.§0\n§0\n§0Accept these 11 bottles of Carrion Black™ as a token of our eternal love for you and yours.§0\n§0\n§0-Ratibor & Ostrobor\n\nSale #1:§0\n§0128 arrows - 180M§0\n§0-32 arrows (Me)§0\n§0-15§0\n§0-26§0\n§020 arrows - 28M§0\n§0\n§0TOTAL = 208\n\nPaid #1:§0\n§0- 8 arrows (11.2)§0\n§0-32", ""),
        StaticBook("Dear Mama", "§bRomulus", "Dear Mama§0\n§0\n§0\n§0To Mama, a woman so strong,§0\n§0You have to keep going on§0\n§0You face adversity,§0\n§0But you have to keep flying free§0\n§0A heart a gold§0\n§0You are so bold,§0\n§0And I know you'll never fold.\n\nWhats man without a woman§0\n§0Can you tell me again?§0\n§0If you need a friend§0\n§0Your son will be there till the end§0\n§0\n§0Dear Mama§0\n§0I love you§0\n§0Those words so true§0\n§0Do anything for you§0\n§0Because I love you§0\n§0I'm going make so proud\n\nYou're going to scream loud.§0\n§0Remember you're so strong§0\n§0Dont let any man tell you off§0\n§0You're your own boss§0\n§0Dont let yourself get locked.§0\n§0\n§0Dear Mama§0\n§0Your family, §0\n§0you mean a lot to me\n\nI want to see you happy§0\n§0Not to be sappy§0\n§0but sadness is crappy§0\n§0\n§0Dear Mama§0\n§0stay happy§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0(yo molly, I know you haven't really been §0\n§0in the best spirits\n\ncuz of how you're treated in rp and ooc and its wrong and should not ever be like this. So i decided to write you this poem to help you feel better. While it's rp, it does have ooc meanings behind it. If you really do need someone to talk to or you're\n\nfeeling down, ill be here to help you out, as will any other of our friends.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0stay cool dingus§0\n§0\n§0-dylan", ""),
        StaticBook("Report", "§bCamillia Havenhelm", "Slavers outside Belvitz:§0\n§0-goblin, green, short, blue eyes, \"Bird Man\"§0\n§0-darky, pointy ears, long hair with half head shaved, name of \"Aylish\" §0\n§0Both armed, goblin has nightsap§0\n§0-dark elf has white hair, looks like raiders signed, Faolan R.\n\nAddendum: §0\n§0These slavers have a girl, looks teenage, with white hair, elf ears, wearing tattered clothes. Pale skin§0\n\nJohnothan (Shweden)§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0The report written before this name was resolved, we helped the girl get back home, the persons name above would like to join The Legion.§0\n§0\n§0-Camillia Havenhelm", ""),
