        StaticBook("A Book Of Cure", "§bKatala Runar", "A Book Of Medical Cures§0\n§0\n§0By Katala Runar\n\nA Cure For Swollen Joints§0\n§0\n§0Apply frostvine for swelling§0\n§0Apply blissfoil for pain§0\n\nA Cure For Birth Fluid Stuck In The Windpipe§0\n§0\n§0Hold the infant upside down and gently pat their back until the fluid emerges.\n\nA Cure For Cuts And Scrapes§0\n§0\n§0Clean the wound with water§0\n§0Disinfect with Dragurstongue§0\n§0Apply bandage if needed\n\nA Cure For Gashes§0\n§0\n§0Disinfect the wound first with Dragurstongue§0\n§0Stitch if needed (slowly and closely)§0\n§0Apply blissfoil for pain§0\n§0Bandage thoroughly§0\n\nA Cure For Broken Bones§0\n§0\n§0Look for the position of the bone§0\n§0If sticking out, set and treat like gash§0\n§0Stablize with sticks (splint) sling for arm§0\n§0DO NOT ADD STICKS FOR BROKEN RIBS JUST BANDAGE\n\nA Cure For Burns§0\n§0\n§0First Degree§0\n§0wet rag§0\n§0frostvine§0\n§0\n§0Second Degree§0\n§0clean with cool rag§0\n§0apply Dragurstongue frostvine and blissfoil§0\n§0\n§0Third Degree§0\n§0treat like second except more carefully\n\nChild Birth§0\n§0\n§0Cool rag on forehead§0\n§0Get her in to position§0\n§0Cut cord if around neck\n\nA Cure For The Loss Of An Appendage§0\n§0\n§0usually means death§0\n§0use a tourniquet to save them§0\n§0wrap fabric around amputated limb and tighten with stick§0\n§0when blood flow stops, cauterize§0\n§0place blissfoil and bandage around wound", ""),
        StaticBook("Evocation: Basic", "§bLaergul Aldirar", "===================                                                        Evocation:§0\n§0               Basics§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0       Copied from the§0\n§0              Library§0\n§0                  by§0\n§0        Laergul Aldirar§0\n§0===================\n\nIn order for the sorcerers to put into use their craft, they m ust have a deep attunement with and knowledge of their element. A caster must know that fire begins with friction and the many stones that make up the earth. A common rule of thumb is:§0\n\n\"If the Sorcerer does not know how something functions, he cannot make it work himself\" This simply dictates that a mage MUST know how water flows and how wind gusts, just as much as they must know how fire feels to touch. Due to this, sorcerers often§0\n\nspend a great deal of time in study, on a deep spiritual level, of their respective element(s). Despite this rigorous training, their spells may still deal them harm, just as much as it may harm their opponent.§0\n\nEvocation is often quite physically and mentally taxing on the Sorcerer, as it takes a great deal of mana to cast. The larger the object one wishes to bring forth, the more mana is required of him to cast it. And just as many other magical branch of the§0\n\nArcane tree, the mage must be capable of envisioning where he is casting his spell, and at what. He must first visualize the spell itself, in his own mind, in order to bring forth its full fury. Therefore, a mage cannot simply conjure a fireball§0\n\nbehind a wall, nor can he cause a wave of water to appear in an area so distant, so beyond the caster's field of vision. Due to this law, Sorcerers are limited in some regard, hindered by the reaches of their sight. Despite the seemingly passive nature§0\n\nthat any one mage may seem to possess. They however remain filthy abominations, dangerous and unholy grotesqueries, who must be taught that such profane powers can bring no good, and must be wholly forgotten, for the sake of every man, woman and child,§0\n\nfor all who walk upon God's blessed earth.", ""),
        StaticBook("Void Mag: Basics", "§bLaergul Aldirar", "===================§0\n§0\n§0           Void Magic:§0\n§0              Basics§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0     Transcribed by§0\n§0      Laergul Aldirar§0\n§0    From the Library§0\n§0          of Dragur§0\n§0===================\n\nVoid Magic is the art of extracting elements from the void, and commanding the elements.§0\n§0The Void is an endless space, in which elements reside in. Those who delve in the arts of the arcane are able to pull these elements from this \"endless space\" and§0\n\nare able to command it to do their will.§0\n§0However, it is not \"creating things out of nothing\". To command these elements at will, and not extract them from the void, you will need mana. The exhaustion of mana varies upon the magnitude of your spell.§0\n\nFor example, though you won't succeed, trying to mold fire as a begginer may exhaust an incredible amount of mana. Do not try this, it may kill you.§0\n§0To be able to use void magics, you require a connection to the void, but that is a story for another day.", ""),
        StaticBook("F.S.", "§bOlivier Galba", "Journal of Fjordin Sylver§0\n§0\n§0Began on the 17th of The First Seed, 1698.§0\n§0\n§0Realm of Atlas\n\n17th of The First Seed, 1698...§0\n§0\n§0I decided to start writing a journal, since I've since lost the company of others to share my thoughts with many decades ago. I now go by the alias Olivier Galba, named after King Olivier de Savoie.\n\nAs would be no secret to those that knew me, my fondest memories died with the realm of Athera. It was a realm crawling with life; from the human capital of Petrus, one might spy the shining spires of Haelun'or; the High Elf city.\n\nThis was a time rife with death and destruction, as eras often face. The Holy Orenian Empire, which controlled most of Athera's great nations, purged the realm of most non-human entities that stepped outside of their comfort zone.\n\nThe Order of Saint Amyas, which served for a long time as the bulk of Oren's military, was at the forefront of most atrocities against non-humankind. Wood elves, high elves, and orcs would often find themselves slaughtered, beaten, or otherwise harassed.\n\nI was among those poor unfortunates to find themselves outcasted, and abused. I realized I could not integrate into Orenian society peacefully, and I was never fond of the pacifist and druidic nature of the Wood Elves, so I struck off into the wilds.\n\nIt was here that I found refuge. An untamed wilderness, ripe with opportunity and potential. I found similarly suffering souls in my infrequent visits to the mainland, and together we built our own refuge: Sylverport.\n\nPeace, however, would not last. In time, as the city truly began to shine, we encountered the everyday threats we aimed to avoid encroaching on our borders: bandits, orc slavers, and mercenary gangs. We realized that in strength, we were weak.\n\nSo I signed our lives off to the only entity I knew that could protect us: Oren. I became good friends with a Public Bacchus, a promising lieutenant of the Order of St. Amyas. Despite the behavior of his compatriots, he was a shrewd diplomat.\n\nPublius eventually went on to proclaim his own noble house, where I was offered a place as a provincial governor. Olivier de Savoie, Orenian king and great friend to Publius, effectively took us both under his wing.\n\nThere was much hardship on the horizon, but I'll save that for another time. There is plenty of time to talk about the destruction of Athera, and the Duke's War, and the fall of Aesculus. This is the story of Olivier Galba, not Fjordin Sylver.\n\n18th of The First Seed, 1686...§0\n§0\n§0Today a raid was launched against Caroloustad, my place of residence. Bandits of some variety, though not the Wyvern's Fang. Reinforces the point about this realm being a dangerous place.\n\nThey were ill-equipped, and easily dispersed by the Legion, though Chava Warblade advised me not to underestimate them, as they once inflicted noticable casualties on the Legion during one of their first raids (which they've since learned from).\n\nEven stranger, however, were the 'Eastern Farfolk' that the Legion reluctantly offered refuge at the gates. They had a strange dialect, peddling alien foods like 'calamari' and 'dumpling'. Perhaps I can learn something about traditional healing from them.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Blue", "§bPrzemyslaw Forrester", "Sergeant Valguria,§0\n§0\n§0There is no other way I could begin this letter but with a congratulacje. Where they see a little girl, I see a young woman. Nazdrovia, Bernadette.§0\n§0\n§0I must keep this letter short, however. I send to thee a set of poems along with thy\n\ncurrent orders. I want thee to recruit men and women of capable bodies. Garrison them within the capital in secret. I do not trust those Imperials for what they have done.§0\n§0\n§0Hold onto that lad thee are engaged to. If thy words are true, and he does become\n\na knight, he may become a valuable asset to have under my strings.§0\n§0\n§0Signed, §0\n§0Lord Regent Przemyslaw Forrester§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragons V 1", "§bJim", "A tale of dragons \n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~The rumor of dragons has been around for centuries. In those centuries humanity has come across many different dragons... Dragon that are small dragons that are tall. dragons that are wide dragons with a thick hide.\n\nSome dragons keep themselves locked from the outside world some dragons like to roam free. Some dragons have wings some dragons dont. Some dragons find peace in the sky some dragons find peace deep in the sea. \nTheir are different colours of dragons.\n\nThe red dragon represents strength and honour. The green creativity and nature. The whotwe purity and light. The yellow cowardise and flight. Puple  dragons are magic and pull from the aspects. Blue dragons represent the unending waves of the sea, Black\n\ndragons represent the end of all things never fight an ender dragon without back up or they will keep you in the end forever....", ""),
        StaticBook("137-1", "§bFabius Bracchus", "Imperial Voter§0\n§0§nIdentification Card         §0\n§0\n§0§lName: §0Caius Horen§0\n§0\n§0§lYear of Birth: §01885§0\n§0\n§0§lResidency: §0Carolustadt§0\n§0\n§0137-1", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "[The hand writing is poor: stiff, and the charcoal lines dig deep into the paper, indicating it's a struggle to write]\n\nYour name is Jon Morrigan.§0\n§0\n§0Your father is Victor.§0\n§0\n§0You used to be alive.§0\n§0\n§0Your father used to beat you. §0\n§0\n§0Why?? It was for a reason. Same reason why you drank.\n\nCan't remember why he beat me.§0\n§0\n§0He was a priest. Was something before?§0\n§0\n§0He hurt you.§0\n§0\n§0Whipped you, too. Whips don't scare you.§0\n§0\n§0You have three friends. John. Dean. Ben.\n\nBen is important. Before you died, too. Why??§0\n§0\n§0Horsemen killed you. Cut your tongue out, hurt your leg. Priest wanted to crucify you. You bled a lot. Ben was going to kill you, but wasn't. You just thought he was.\n\nYou've killed 1/7§0\n§0\n§0                2/7§0\n§0\n§0                3/7§0\n§0        §0\n§0                4/7§0\n§0\n§0                5/7§0\n§0\n§0                6/7§0\n§0\n§0                7/7\n\nBen wants you to be a darkstalker.§0\n§0\n§0He didn't name the dog yet.§0\n§0You got him the dog.§0\n§0(It's the ghost one)§0\n§0\n§0Don't forget to clean clothes.§0\n§0\n§0Also Ben's a skeleton.\n\nYou should get new clothes. Old ones are getting hard to fix.§0\n§0\n§0Starting to notice more with each body. And feel a little more. Still hard to be angry, but there's at least the feeling of being annoyed. Feet don't feel as heavy. Feel a little bad\n\nwhen I get people.§0\n§0\n§0But I'll remember better soon. And feel better. It'll be better.§0\n§0\n§0I'll be myself again.", ""),
