        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Far away, in the middle of the desert, in the night, orcish cubs sometimes spot an evil creature with shining red eyes in the dark. §0\n§0\n§0    No child or adult that has seen these evil eyes has ever reported anything about this creature, thus making\n\nwriting a book or a report on such vile monster something impossible.§0\n§0\n§0    The monster's red, red like when you stab weak humans to offer they blood to the Devil.\n\nHis hair is long, and he will reach for you, with his army of tiny red monsters.§0\n§0\n§0They spit.§0\n§0They are ruthless.§0\n§0And they will say one thing.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0DO YU KNO DE WE?", ""),
        StaticBook("The Cantina Menu", "§bAmelia Philippa", "The Cantina\n        Menu\n\n        Sangria\n\nA Santegian Alcoholic Beverage made with red wine and chopped fruits. A touch of brandy and orange juice is added to the mixture to give a more citrusy flavour. Better to drink this with others than alone!\n\nThe Emir's Palm Wine\n\nAlso known as Jedih Palm Wine, it is made from the sap of the local palm trees located along the Sophanem River that runs along the city of Jedih.\n\nThe palm wine is milky white colour with fruity taste balanced with the alcoholic taste from fermentation. It is a favoured drink among the ladies and secretly many men, too.\n\nThe Lady Bella's\nPirate Rum\n\nA golden rum spiced with cinnamon and has added caramel. It’s been aged in a charred birch tree barrels. A potent Spirit with a sweet taste, served usually with orange juice.\n\nThe Drink is named after former buccaneer ‘Lady Bella’ who made the recipe.\n\n      Roseglow\n         Wine\n\nA bottle of Roseglow wine with the order of Saint Lucien’s Rhodesian Cross on the label. A popularized drink from the Anthosian Era, it was made in the Orenian Blackmarsh originally.\n\nIt has since become the signature drink of the Holy Order.\n\nWaldenian Lager\n\nThe Waldenian Lager Hails from Vanderfel, the Grand Capital of the Konigreich of Aesterwald from the Atheran Era. Light and Refreshing, it’s crisp taste compliments any meal it is served with or is great by itself.\n\nI don’t always drink beer, but when I do, I prefer Waldenian drinks.\n\nCharles' Whiskey\nA rye whiskey brewed originally in the Charles’ Cantina of Carolustadt. Made in honor of Charles Elliot Horen, the former Archchancellor of the Empire. This Whiskey emits a smell of warmed spices, oak, and rye bread;\n\nwhilst taste is hot and spicy in the beginning, delivering its potent punch. However, it becomes more mellow towards the end with a more herbal and savory taste for the palate. Surely, a drink of nobility.\n\n Echo Bay Sake\nThis Sake is brewed in the way of how the Easterners of Echo bay would brew it. The rice is left to ferment for 5 months in a Cedar cask. The process enhances the flavour and gives it a kick when drunk.\n\n This is due to the alcohol being left to ferment for an extended period of time. The colouring of the Sake is darkened brown due to the colouring of the wood seeping into the Sake which also gives off a slightly bitter taste.\n\nWhen heated up though the Sake gives off a more sweetened taste and more pleasant to drink.\n\nFresh Lemonade\nFreshly squeezed Lemonade, perfect for a tiring day of work! Icy and cool, this lemonade is meant to rejuvenate the drinker. It is placed in a transparent glass bottle, with a label stating “The Cantina” wrapped around it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Cantina Food", "§bAmelia Philippa", "§i     The Cantina \n     Food Menu\n\nNutmeg Custard Pie\n\nFresh out of the oven, this custard pie is a bite-sized treat served warm. Made in a circular shape, with a crusty outer ring and soft custard filling. A perfect blend of nutmeg, milk, and eggs.\n\n        Choc Ice\n\nA frozen bar of chocolate best enjoyed on hot days. A qalasheen treat created by Adil the Eagle-Eyed of Al-Wakrah.\n\nBaby Back Ribs\nBaby back Pork Ribs glazed with Tamarind. The tamarind provides a sweet and sour taste to the fork-tender ribs, glazed prior to grilling. The taste of honey subtly accompanies the tamarind glazing, and the warmth of the ribs\n\nallows it to be the perfect dish for the weathers of winter.  The dish is compiled with a side of salad and cut lime wedges.\n\nThe Tourney Treat\nPuff pastry molded to be shaped as a horse, covered in a coat of sugar that sprinkle over it’s surface. The crisp of the crust is accompanied by the softness of the pastry within.\n\n§§ Inside, there is a filling of chocolate still warm from the heat of the oven, rich in flavour.", ""),
        StaticBook("Scholar List", "§bThe Library Of Dragur", "Scholar List:\n\n15th of the Deep Cold, 1659\n\n- Balt, Kha'Pantera\n\n- Nerah, Dryad\n\n- Muildir, Elf\n\n- Nemir, Elf\n\n- Anorak, Dark Elf\n\n- Dreek, Dwarf\n\n- Cuthwin, Human\n\n- Veres, Human\n\n- Guyden, Human\n\n- Lurcano, Orc\n\n- Travis Bell, Human", ""),
        StaticBook("On Reverence", "§bPontian II", "Thesis on Reverence:§0\n§0By Father Theodoric of Markev, published 1683§0\n§0\n§0Steadfast and indelible, the most encompassing aspect of canonist doctrine is, by it own  nature, GOD. The omnipotent and omnipresent GOD lords over the Seven Skies, observing from afar\n\n the subjects of His own creation. Aenguls and Daemons alike, along with every being in existence, descendent or otherwise, fall under His purview. Through this hierarchy, it is abundantly clear to each devout canonist that the greatest precedence of\n\nfaith, law, and lifestyle shall be granted unto Him, the Creator, in order to act as instruments of His will.§0\n§0\n§0However, as the existence of the First Sky demonstrates, one need not be a member of the church to act in accordance with the principles of the\n\nFaith. The nature of virtuous living is inherent in all descendents, each one driven to benevolent action by the invisible hand of GOD’s will. Whether they acknowledge the divine supremacy of the one true GOD or not, even the majority of pagans appear\n\ngenerous and warm-hearted, although their righteous actions can not be properly rewarded without active submission to His doctrine. Even so, there exist those that, while aware of the church, shun GOD’s blessing to devote their finite mortal experience to\n\nlesser benefactors.§0\n§0\n§0“One must acknowledge that it is GOD who is supreme and he hath created Aenguls to serve Him.” (Fides et Vita Floruerunt, 6:13)§0\n§0\n§0Submitting oneself to the ostensible service of a mortal liege lord is societally natural for the\n\nmajority of Horen’s sons. It is a fact of life for the common peasant, that he, in exchange for housing, food, and protection, much offer deference, obedience, and the fruits of his labor to his lord. As a lord commands, his humble villein is compelled to\n\ndo. This is, of course, not heresy, nor heathenry, because both partners in this feudal relationship offer deference to their Creator, the one true GOD. To place an offering before the grave of a deceased sibling, or to offer a prayer at the back-road\n\nshrine of a Saint, isn’t, either. And in this same vein, to make a pact of service with an Aengul, spirit, or Aspect is not necessarily contrary to the teachings of the faith.§0\n§0\n\n“Grace to thee and peace from our Lord GOD, the Most Merciful, Singular, and Omnipotent.”§0\n§0 (Owyn, 8:2)§0\n§0\n§0A significant, and insurmountable problem exists, however, when those accepting the mortal blessings and protection of a powerful entity fail to\n\nplace themselves before the altar of GOD, or refuse to acknowledge His existence. When Aspectists, clerics, paladins, shamans, etc. shirk their responsibilities to the Divine, they are knowingly leading themselves down a path of idolatry and ignorance\n\nthat will eventually lead to an eternity of torture in the Void. Thus, to all of you embroiled in a pact with a lesser being, take heed! If your patron requests of you an action contrary to GOD’s will, humbly refuse!\n\nFor no spirit, no Aengul, and no Daemon can shield you from the righteous judgement of GOD.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alchemy Notes 1", "§bMario Costello", "Sheriff Mario's Alchemy Notes\n\nEquivilant Exchange\n - Nothing comes from nothing.\n - Reagents are \"given\"  in  exchange for \"potion\"\n -All bout balance\n -Some things are worth more than others in alchemy\n -Not monetary, metaphorical representations\n\nSymbols\n -Fire, Air, Earth, Water\n -Paired with representations well\n -Fire is for burning, consumption, fury, destruction, power, chaos. Used for damage\n -Also used with passionate emotions\n\n -Water symbols used as a base (due to liquid state)  for  oils/potions\n -Liquid bases; aqua vitae (most powerful,  basically distilled alcohol), purified water (weakest) and lard (used for oils)\n -Water useful for healing potions, but can be used\n\nin poisons.\n -Earth used for bases more advanced (transmutation, chimeras)\n -Two variations of earth symbols can be compared to rock and dirt; rock is hard to break and sturdy, also associated with minerals/metals. Dirt\n\nrepresents life.\n -Air for speed, travel, quickness.\n -Lab must be CLEAN\n -Gloves, mask recommended for SAFETY\n -Mortar and pestle, knife, etc needed for gathering.\n\nUseful Potions:\n\nPotion of Mending:\n -Heals most ailments (physical or biological).\n -Power of potion should be proportional to ailment \n\nMINOR:\n -base of distilled water\n -1 water symbol of life\n\n -1 earth symbol of life\n\nLESSER\n\n -base of distilled water\n -2 water symbols of life\n -1 earth symbol of life\n -1 air symbol of quickness\n\nGREATER\n\n -base of aqua vitae\n -2 water symbols of life\n -2 earth symbols of life\n -1 air symbol of speed\n\nPotion of Regeneration\n -Regrows limbs\n \nRECIPE:\n\n -base of blood taking the potion\n -Mandragora\n -liver  of a pregnant mother (same race as subject)\n -2 Earth symbols of life\n\n -1 air symbol of grace\n\nPotion of Clerity:\n\nMakes you faster, more agile.\n\nMINOR:\n\n -base of water\n -1 air symbol of speed\n\nLESSER:\n -base of distilled water\n\n -2 air symbols of speed\n\nGREATER\n\n -base of aqua vitae\n -2 air symbols of speed\n -1 fire symbol of power\n\nPotion of Accutity:\n\nHeightens Senses\n\nMINOR\n -base of water\n -2 air symbols of perception\n\nLESSER\n -base of distilled water\n -3 air symbols of perception\n\nGREATER\n -base of aqua vitae\n -4 air symbols of perception\n\nPotion of Wizard's Wisdom\n\nMakes you smarter\n\nMINOR:\n -base of water\n -2 water symbols of balance and clarity\n -1 fire symbol of power\n -2 earth symbols of endurance\n\n -1 air symbol of perception\n\nLESSER:\n  -3 water symbols of clarity and balance\n  -2 fire symbols of power\n  -3 earth symbols of endurance\n  -2 air symbols of perception\n  -base of distilled water", ""),
