        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Dear, Daughter§0\n§0\n§0I know that we have just started to get to know each other but I am going to be married to another woman. He name is Al", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Notes upon Jerry Cali. §0\n§0-The man was not in a meeting with a stranger for long. When I entered I saw the stranger showing what weaponary he held to Jerry.§0\n§0\n§0-The meeting had not been on for even five saints minutes before he dismissed it and told me he had\n\nquickly concluded.§0\n§0\n§0- Upon our meeting, he first asked for more keys. Specifics: Dungeon keys. Barrack keys. §0\n§0\n§0-Spoke that Matthew said he was going to craft him a blade, however he wishes the weapon to be 'notable'.\n\n- He states he's trying to recruit for the Haense guard force. Wishes to have two personal 'private' guards. §0\n§0\n§0- Stated that due to losing a war something within the force has to change. §0\n§0\n§0-States he only recruits as a side\n\nthing. Avoided answering if he had permission from the captains twice. §0\n§0\n§0-So clearly there is more to discuss in his meetings other than Haensetian recruitment.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Alchemy by Karyssmov.§0\n§0\n§0What is Alchemy? Changing the aspects of one structure to benfit another§0\n§0\n§0Symbols? Fire, Earth, Water, Air. §0\n§0Fire-Destruction, Passion§0\n§0Earth- Growth§0\n§0Water- Healing§0\n§0Air- ???\n\nLaw of Equivlant Exchange§0\n§0To take, something of equal value must be given.§0\n\nFundemental Tools §0\n§01)Morta and Pestle.§0\n§02)Heating utinsles§0\n§03) Glass Beakers§0\n§04) Clean water (Not pond or river!)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0§lAlchemy Lesson§0\n§0§l        Notes§0\n§0§l    §0\n§0§l        -=+=-§0\n§0\n§0 Different symbols:§0\n§0\n§0Fire, water, earth and air. Combining these ideas with different herbs can cause different types of reactions.\n\nNeeded tools: Heating station, to heat tools. §0\n§0\n§0Distilled water, never river or pond water.§0\n§0\n§0Motar and pestle.§0\n§0\n§0Clean surfaces.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§l A collection of §0\n§0§l  poems to Robert§0\n§0§l Barbanov from§0\n§0§l Elizaveta vas §0\n§0§l      Ruthern.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0§l        -=+=-§0\n§0\n§0§l   Enjoy my love.\n\n   §0§lWhen Morning§0\n§0§l       Breaks§0\n§0\n§0§l §0When the winters whistle and creak, when the medows prowl and shriek. §0\n§0\n§0To your arms I do find my refuge, the kind gentle smile you give in return.\n\nIn the nights, I quiver and fear. But do find my calmness when you are near. §0\n§0\n§0Tis' a gentle feeling, your hand within mine. A devine warmth - that keeps us safe from the north.§0\n§0\n§0Our guardians frown, seeing us together about the town.\n\nBut carless are we, oh so dear are thee. §0\n§0\n§0The nights grow cold, but the truth we do behold. Our love, pure and our fears - tis' the cure.§0\n§0\n§0But the morning breaks, like shimmer of gold. Caressing the early heavens.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Aewion, §0\n§0\n§0I cannot thank you enough for travelling with me to get those herbs. I would have brought you money but there is too little to gift. So I hope you like fish sticks, chocolate, and seeds for your birds. Ahernan again§0\n§0llir.§0\n§0        Sincerely\n\nNesiwen K.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0[!] This book would be filled with Witchery, spells [!]\n\nWitchery:§0\n§0\n§0Alohomora:§0\n§0This spell makes the user be able to open almost every locked door.§0\n§0\n§0Riddikulus:§0\n§0transforms the most scary things into something silly.\n\nLumos:§0\n§0This spell creates a little boll of light above the item the spell gets used with.§0\n§0\n§0Expelliarmus:§0\n§0This spell makes the user be able to disarm its upponment, from anything they hold in their hands.§0\n§0(this costs a lot of mana)\n\nAvada Kedavra:§0\n§0This is a very powerful killing curse if used on a living person, he dies instantly.§0\n§0\n§0Obliviate:§0\n§0Makes the user be able to erase a specific memory by both itself and its upponment.\n\nIn the Dark of Night§0\n§0\n§0Originally, this nightmare spell is part of the selection of real black magic spells from another section. This spell will help bring nightmares to another person. The supplies are:§0\n§0\n§0(Spell is p-7 till p-11)\n\nOne black candle§0\n§0Dried mugwort§0\n§0Dragon's blood (a resin incense)§0\n§0Charcoal tablet§0\n§0Heat-proof dish or tile§0\n§0Large piece of white paper or fabric§0\n§0Black paint\n\nOn the paper or material, drawn 3 concentric circles and an x in the middle of the smallest inside circle.§0\n§0Place the dish with a charcoal tablet right on the x, and the candle outside the circles on the left.\n\nLight the charcoal and get it burning, put a pinch or two of dried mugwort on it along with a chunk of Dragon's blood.§0\n§0 When they are both smoking nicely, light the black candle.§0\n\nWatch the smoke rising from the dish and picture it floating through space to your intended target.§0\n§0It brings nightmares and fear into their sleep, so picture that scene for several minutes and focus on the person.\n\nRepeat their name in your head as you do.§0\n§0\n§0After a few minutes of this concentration, put out the charcoal and switch the dish and candle so the candle is on the x in the center.§0\n\nLeave it until it fully burns down.§0\n§0\n§0The person you're targeting will have bad dreams and nightmares starting the next night and it will last for 3 days.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "s", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "9th of The First Seed, 1675.§0\n§0\n§0Studies of the aged tome, 'Druidic Records I'.§0\n§0\n§0The pages begin with the inker, striking proud as a follower of the September Prince. States that the documented testament shall show the true\n\nwill of the aspects. §0\n§0\n§0It then goes onto stating, that he is the last druid in the prince's service, the remaining brother's and sister's in a slumber of some sorts. Perhaps the same state that the sleeping September Prince finds himself within, as we\n\nspeak. §0\n§0\n§0Within the fading scribing of the tome, it states that the blessed State of our home had been deteriorating for years. §0\n§0\n§0Little contact had been made throughout the flowing years, the villages about the\n\ngreen empire had already been destroyed by the September Prince. §0\n§0\n§0Now what I personally find abnormal about these historical writings is that the prince was priorly rumoured to be an omnibenevolant being. Though through clear recordings\n\nthis 'prince' caused nothing but sheer destruction upon helpless villages surrounding the Dominion of Malin.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "lol", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "9th of Sun's Smile§0\n§01679,§0\n§0\n§0Over the past few days, I have grown to be much, much older - at least, it feels like such. It all started when my friend had told me there were voices all around, speaking to her. It was hard to believe at first though I\n\ntried to find the help that she was looking for. When I couldn't get it, I came back to see that the door leading out to the balcony where she sat was closed. By the time I had barely creaked open the door, she had fallen from the side of the balcony and\n\nto the next, smaller roof below it - or, was pushed.", ""),
