        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Hey this is lorax. one of the people who helped build the palace. ive been gone for a while and i come back to all my stuff taken and evrything even my house taken. i was gine for a good reason. my brother got into a really bad wreck and i couldnt be home\n\nim sorry if i have any spellig errors i have long nails nd it makes my spelling horrid. im not rping so dont take this as that just please contact me at bunnylove4849 as my snap and insta is §0_peach._.scone_§0 thank you§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Poop, does in fact§0\n§0stink underwater, regardless of what you think. §0\n§0Poop is a terrible substance to encounter physically as the smell, and texture is enough to cause one to vomit repeatably.\n\nFarts, when introduced to submerging underwater. Causes the stench of the fart to increase tenfolds. One can best describe this horrific, unseen vapor as being one of the most vile creations placed upon the lands of the living.\n\nVomiting is yet another foul secretion that most bodies produce. The remains of meals, partially digested foods, liquids and stomach acids are combined to become a fast-paced projectile where ever an indivial is aimming. It is a disgusting act regardless.\n\nWhen one studies so many varibles of smells regarding the bodies of the living, and undead at times. You can start to wonder if everything in existence is... Just a shitty smell. A big, steaming hunk of shit.§0\n§0\n§0          Yep.\n\n  Slimy rocks from the sea are not a good combination for making soup. Some rocks though, are great! Eat more stone pebble stew!§0\n§0\n§0Recommended that you have no teeth, or aim to have lesser!\n\nDo you ever wonder to yourself if it is worth trying for that extra hunk of pie? Or maybe altering your taste to that of a cherry flavored dumplings.§0\n§0\n§0Think§0\n§0Of§0\n§0It.\n\nWuuuuuuub! Wub dat skahhhh! Yub! Du lat tink ub latzylf az hoooozh! Er Bubbbb'hozh! Skkkkkah lat, Skkkkkah lat! Skah'n lat am everi'azh! Skah iht uhb!\n\n Do you truly know your last moments in life, this realm? Perhaps nub. We wyll peep. Unli da zky'gud'z kan anzur dat tu lat, nub Aerial, nub Xan. Unli Zky'Gud'z.\n\nWisps of violet-blue streaks fill the sky when rain is present. The constant thumming of sound echoing across the lands. Watch as the lights flash and dance for our entertainment.  The Skygods must be mad.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Ergoth's Journal\n\nThere are three kinds of spirits, The Immortals, The Elementals and The Ancestors. Though the Ancestors are simply uruk that have transcended. I do not know what they control, for the elementals focus upon the fabric of the world. The Immortals control\n\nemotion, things about life that cannot be explained.§0\n§0\n§0For this, I do not know of every Immortal. Neither does any uruk. One of the more respected uruk had not heard of Orgol. A horror of a being that lies in the back of all minds.§0\n§0\n\nThe elementals I believe are nameless, or infinite. I do not fathom how they function except for the twisting of the fabric of our existence to suit the whims of the Shomo. It also appears that most that are granted such an ability have bouts of insanity\n\nor stupidity.§0\n§0The Ancestors, I do not know their purpose other than guidance. The Immortals are the spirits that truly influence everything, and this is what I wish to explore. The influence of the Immortals.\n\nThe Spirits of Votar and Leyd are worshipped frequently around the uzg. Bastions of power. One of the Hunt, the other of what I believe is power. That is what it said in accordance to the teachings of Thurak.§0\n§0Others can be ignored and unknown, but their\n\npower is a constant struggle which creates balance. According to the wise Elphaba. For spirits must rise and fall in influence, just as ideals do within the society of the uruk.§0\n\nThere are various branches of the spirits that link to how the uruk serve them. Witch Doctor, Ancestor Speaking, something called Farseer. I do not know such things entail. Also, Elementalism. I do not know of what these types do, or what they utilise\n\nbeyond the spirits they serve. But we all serve the spirits, a brother called Vorgak focuses upon the Ancestors. Talking in a strange tongue that is beyond me, but perhaps that is significant to those he tries to contact. §0\n§0I do not understand how one\n\nmakes contact with the spirits. I have never fathomed their influence personally, even their depictions are seen within the writings of Thurak. Except Ramakhet. A strange spirit but neverless.§0\n§0\n§0I have not seen or understood what most of these spirits do\n\nor how they truly create our world. All I do is observe and watch, blood is spilt and the clouds move in a cycle. Others claim that other 'Gods' do it, but there are no true gods. They are only spirits.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n\nThe Stargush'Stroh is where the Ancestors lie, according to Vorgak and another. The Ancestors need sacrifice to worship them, to fuel them with power perhaps? The Old Blood of corpses signifies a great honor to those of the Ancestors.\n\nIt seems the clans all have ancestors that relate to them. Krug's Children. The Thagruz Grizh is what is used to bind such a blessing.§0\n§0\n§0Otherwise, I have not heard of other markings of the shomos. The shrines are spread, but they are infrequent on the\n\nlands I have travelled. The spirits are only whispered of, bar Votar and Leyd. Even Lakhul. But otherwise many do not mention those that were found in the studies, or even outside of the writings of Thurak. §0\n§0Confusing, why do the spirits not gain true\n\nreign. Even though the last time this happened was the Blight of Orgon, it does not make sense why they all do not focus upon the spirits.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Wolven Spirit§0\n§0\n§0By: Alydril Daemyr\n\nIntroduction:§0\n§0This is a fictional tale of two lovers, a man and a woman, who had never thought of being together. Faced with an upcoming war and running for their very lives, these two lovers are in for the ride of their lives.\n\nChapter I: Ruelle§0\n§0\n§0In this world, people often have high expectations for themselves and their friends. When it comes to families it is no exception.\n\nIt is often a custom, for a father to have expectations for their son, and likewise for the mother and daughter. You could say that my family has the same expectations for myself.\n\nAllow me to introduce myself. . .I am Ruelle, daughter of a military veteran and a high standard noblewoman. I am the eldest of my three siblings, so of course, you can expect my parents to place high expectations on myself.\n\nI was supposed to be wed to a rich aristocrat, whom I never met. My family only did the arranging of the wedding so they can get back on top, since they were clearly broke. But. . .\n\nWhen I first met the aristocrat, I didn't really like him. He always talked so dramatically, he hated getting dirty, and he always ordered servants around like they were animals.\n\nHowever, I never really paid a heed to these, as I wanted to make my family happy, and nothing was going to stop me. That's. . .what I thought at least.\n\nChapter II: Liekos§0\n§0\n§0My name is Liekos, and as you can expect, I'm not the average guy. At least, that's what most people say, even my family.\n\nI grew up as an orphan for five years, since I was five years old. That was, until a poor family took me in. They lived in the high freezing cold mountains, in a small village which was isolated from most. In fact, it was the only one.\n\nWhen I was little, people didn't treat me very kindly. They considered myself weird, out of place, like I should never exist. Yet my adopted mother and father thought different.\n\nThey considered me to be special, one of few who was. They said I was destined to do great things, even if it meant doing so in the shadows. I believed them, but the more time passed, the harder it got to believe such. Then, one night. . .\n\nI was seventeen at the time, when it happened. I found my parents' cottage, burning with the licking flames. I went inside, but found no trace of my parents. That was. . .until I went to the backyard. I found them brutally killed, and\n\nthe killers were still here. In a rage, I did something I thought I never could have done before. They said I transformed, they said I transformed to that of a wolf. They said I went after them, and killed every single one of them. But me. . .\n\nI didn't remember much, all I remember is finding the killers' eaten corpses, and then. . .the townsfolk who stared at me with wide eyes. They went after me, to kill me.\n\nI of course didn't stand there long. I ran for the forests, scared and upset. When I escaped from their hands, I found a pool of water and looked at the reflection. It was true, I was a man who turned wolf. And I hated it.\n\nChapter III: Ruelle", "")
    )

    private fun _ATLAS_15(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Hello! I'm Ianite Grimlee, I was raised by an elf who's my brother. (There would be a sketch of a wood elf with dark drown hair,eyes and tan skin) I also was with my twin sister...(A drawing of a human with blonde hair and blue eyes would be here)\n\n(A drawing of a small woman in a dress would be carrying twins in her arms she would be smiling down at them, she would have very light blond hair with two different color eyes one green the other blue, her children would have blues eyes with light blond\n\nhair)\n\n\"Why does she always do that..I didnt do anything but she blaming everything on §0me..her§0 pulls on my hair and push me. My brother helps me something...\"\n\n(A drawing of an child elf would be here he has short blonde hair with greens eyes)§0\n§0\n\nMy goal first was to find more about my mother, but I find myself stuck with two men in love with me..I dont want to hurt §0anyone..in§0 the end I did .I got pregnant and he killed the other person who loved §0me..my§0 friend died by my lover..I'm sorry so sorry.\n\n(there would be more drawing of elves,Kha's,orcs, and humans but there would be more elves then anything else.)\n\n(A sketch of a tall human with black hair and eyes would be here he would be holding a sword)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Entry 1:§0\n§0For days I have secluded myself from socialization and my brothers. . . though not for nothing. My work is coming together and these equations are something I can work with.\n\n[!] Littered across the page are random equations and seemingly random rumbers and letters. [!]\n\nEntry 2:§0\n§0Argh, progress has been slow across the past few days. Hours along have rendered my mind to wander, thought of my mortality and the futility of my existence plague me. . . [!]\n\n[!] Sketchings of primitive engines and pulleys are scrawled across the parchment. [!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "[!]Another note written with the same handwriting as last§0 enclosed in the note is a single white rose.§0\n§0\n§0\"Dear Morrigyn, I write to you once again in secrecy, however this time with deep regret. I saw you again on the roads, but instead this meeting was-\n\nnot of a peaceful nature infact I was ordered to strike you down as a spy. There was nothing I could do I had to follow my orders. I only wish you to know I pulled my swing trying not to hurt you too much. I hope you'd forgive me. If you would like an-\n\napology in person simply leave the rose in your mailbox if I find it there I will find you and introduce myself.§0\n§0\n§0With best regards,§0\n§0-A", ""),
