        StaticBook("Level 1 Code 1", "§bJaya Jayamen", "Level 1 Code 1\n\ni!fy !!our !ea d! thi!s t! el! lm! e th!ew !ord! c! ak! e", ""),
        StaticBook("china man", "§bBelrose", "there once was a chink who enjoyed lemun chekyen, with fryed noodal, prawn kraker with blayk bean sauce, but then he reyalised that he was a fake ashun livin in Thailand, who was actyully black. He now likes fried chikyen", ""),
        StaticBook("MI BOOK NOW", "§bGrubgobbla'Raguk", "This is the legendary book of the Elf known as Aulus Ithelanen> All that was wrtitten was a simple word. \"Kaz Ithelanen is a cock.\" \n\nDIZ BOOK IZ NOW TAKEN OVUR BY DA BIGGEZT AGH DA BADDEZT AGH DA REDDEZT! DATZ MI, GRUBGOBBLA!", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I think what you did was brave. They dont see the logic, but I suppose that would mean they dont matter, hmm?§0\n§0\n§0I've lived too long to have children insult me. I'm a grumpy old man, I suppose, but that's between you and I.\n\nI dont think you could be that old.. and I would rather be called a old man instead of a child. I'm constantly mistaken for an ome'ii.. when I'm 126. And who better to tell things to than to someone who cannot speak?§0\n§0\n§0You speak now, even if it isn't\n\nthrough sound. It's a powerful weapon, writing, and even now you can see the edge it grants us. My friend, I've been alive for years past the count. I saw the days of Aegis come and go, and each realm after do the same.§0\n§0\n\nI suppose in valahs terms you are old. But you still can stnd on your own and seem strong enough to do the things I saw here. Dont sell yourself short, Loriens. §0\n§0I know, I know. Time has treated me well enough, though old wounds haunt me in ways unseen.\n\nMen such as the one in front of us are young in their vigilance - with ego overcoming their goodness. I've tried for so, very long to avoid men such as he, but after having wandered this realm homeless I figured I might as well settle.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-=+= Fish Stock =+=-§0\n§0\n§0_1673_§0\n§0\n§0@11th Suns Smile§0\n§0*9 Catfish§0\n§0*7 Lakefish§0\n§0*7 Floudfish§0\n§0*6 Wormfish§0\n§0*6 Perch§0\n§0*5 Cutthroat§0\n§0*5 Herring§0\n§0*3 Mudsucker§0\n§0*1 Harrison Fish\n\n@2nd The Amber Cold§0\n§0*19 Catfish§0\n§0*12 Lakefish§0\n§0*24 Flounder§0\n§0*8 Wormsfish§0\n§0*10 Perch§0\n§0*12 Cutthroat§0\n§0*10 Herring§0\n§0*8 Mudsucker§0\n§0*1 Harrison Fish\n\n_1674_§0\n§0\n§0@3rd The Deep Cold§0\n§0*23 Catfish§0\n§0*15 Lakefish§0\n§0*27 Flounder§0\n§0*10 Wormfish§0\n§0*11 Perch§0\n§0*15 Cutthroat§0\n§0*11 Herring§0\n§0*9 Mudsucker§0\n§0*1 Harrison Fish\n\nI know what lat did.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Beggining of another Life§0\n§0\n§0As my partner died, I found another one. Her name's Azure Skye. I'm always saying sorry to Willow... But what can I do. I met a Lori. She's cool... So, yup. That's everything for now.\n\nAzure Skye...§0\n§0\n§0Azure is beautiful, she is so kind and sweet. I can't stop thinking about her... She left somewhere probably... I hope to see her. She'll brighten my life...§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Sorry, Willow§0\n\nDear Lorelei...§0\n§0\n§0My lost sister. My parents told me about her. The same night I was born, she dissapeared. But, I get memories, like I know what's going on... And from the day I was born and she dissapeared, I got this weird scar on my shoulder...\n\nA book.§0\n§0\n§0I'm thinking of writing a book. About a group of people, going on a adventure... They're on a quest to find or return something... I don't know the name, but on the next page, I'll start writing it.\n\n        THERE AND§0\n§0        BACK AGAIN§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0             By§0\n§0     Elnor Whitewater\n\nThe Treehouse.§0\n§0\n§0There once was a little girl named Azure. She was lovely, living in a treehouse with her parents. She loved to wonder around. She had a friend, Malik, who was older than her. He was a druid, he showed her creatures and he cared for her, as\n\nAzure's parents were always of somewhere.§0\n§0One night, a stranger came to her treehouse, knocking at the door. As she was brave and curios, she opened the door. But no one was there... There was just a note. It was saying: \"When you turn 120 years, come to\n\nthe Hollow tree in dusk.§0\n§0\n§0-A friend.\n\nThe Hollow Tree§0\n§0\n§0And as the years passed, Azure was finally 120. She came at the Hollow Tree at dusk.§0\n§0          . . .§0\n§0No one was there.§0\n§0A message came.§0\n§0I won't finish this, sorry...§0\n\nCome back, Azure§0\n§0\n§0Where ever you are, come back. I want to see you, you're like a sun to me. My life is shit, I need someone to smile at when I'm sad, angry or whatever.§0\n§0Come back§0\n§0\n§0Come back, my love.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Taxes:§0\n§04,300 minas§0\n§0\n§0Total:§0\n§031,383 minas", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "From Mom §0\n§0To Avalynn T.§0\n§0\n§0  Dear Sweet Lyna, I love you so much dear. I love you so much that it hurts me to send you away. It may be to quick, to fast. To.. weird. For me to do so, although I have a very good reason to do so. During your live, I\n\nhave did nothing but just watch as your father puts this.. ideology of his to yours. Please, please understand that that is not the way to live! You are allowed to grow and meet people and cheerish them for whom they are! The world is not that cruel Lyna.\n\nIt might be, but if you keep hiding from it. You'll miss out on the good thing that can actually come, because they will. They will I promise you, please Lyna. I.. have failed you as a mother Lyna, I have failed to show you the world I have known, to show\n\nyou or to tell you that you are capable of being more then just a household wife, because I let that fear overtook me. That is the biggest regret of my life, and I don't want the same thing to happend to you. §0\n§0\n§0You'll be so happy with my friend! I promise\n\nhe will show you the world, he will show you everything.. and you will be finally free.§0\n§0\n§0I love you Lyna..§0\n§0\n§0Goodbye..§0\n§0\n§0Within these pages I have wrote things that might be useful for you.\n\nTiming of the Drop§0\n§0---------------§0\n§0Lyrics§0\n§0------§0\n§0\n§0Drop, drop, drop, to the timing of the drop. §0\n§0\n§0Drop that seeps to the roof from the pouring rain.§0\n§0\n§0Drop, drop drop, the rain poured its-\n\nthunder, it mourn, it cried.§0\n§0\n§0Drop, drop, drop, to the timing of the drop, like the dandelion does, when the water shifts.§0\n§0\n§0Drop, drop, drop.. he no longer follow it. No longer follow the drop, his out of the stream.\n\nDrop.. drop.. drop.. he loses him self, of what his truly as. He hurt so many.§0\n§0\n§0Drop..§0\n§0\n§0Drop..§0\n§0\n§0Follow the drop~§0\n§0\n§0Drop.. drop.. drop..\n\nTiming of the Drop§0\n§0----------------§0\n§0Musical Sheet§0\n§0------------§0\n§0\n§05 5 5 3 2 1 1 5 6 5§0\n§03 2 1 1 5 6 5 3 2 1 6 5§0\n§0\n§0[Adjust according to lyric]\n\nRecipe for Lyna's Favorite soup :§0\n§0\n§01. Carrot and union chopped, let it simmer for 5 minutes.§0\n§0\n§02. Add Parsley shavings.§0\n§0\n§03. Crack an egg and add a slight bit of milk to make it creamy, cook it over a low fire with\n\na pan, constanly move the pan around while stiring it with a spoon.§0\n§0\n§04. Add the union and carrot along side with the scrambled egg. Add vegtable to your liking. Season with salt and Pepper.§0\n§0\n§05. Key : Avalynna's favorite is lettuce.\n\n6. She likes it served with cut out apples and watermelon juice.§0\n§0She have a weird taste, but if shes like it.. its fine with me§0\n§0\n§0[OOC : page 11-12 is a ripped paper that is glued into a book, the handwritting looks messy but readable]\n\nMom's Note: Keep loving horses Lyna <3§0\n§0\n§0How to comfort Horse§0\n§0------------------§0\n§0\n§01. To make a horse comfrotable in its living space. You should always provide hay and water.§0\n§0\n§02. Treats are good! They love Carrots\n\nand apples.§0\n§0\n§03. Brush them frequently!§0\n§0\n§04. Look at their tooth!§0\n§0an overgrown tooth is dangerous for them.§0\n§0\n§05. Take your time when bonding with them.§0\n§0\n§06. Keep giving them treats, but not to muc!\n\nHorse Treat Recipe :§0\n§0-----------------§0\n§0\n§01. Mix hay shavings, and shaved carrots together.§0\n§0\n§02. Bake.§0\n§0\n§03. Done.§0\n\nThe begining of Avalynna's Journal§0\n§0-----------------§0\n§0\n§0Entry 1#:§0\n§0  I figure I'll use the book my mother gave me to wrote daily questions, things I feel.. this is.. my first time living alone so this will be a first.\n\nEntry 2# :§0\n§0Dominion is weird, but.. beautifull. The trees are so high, but whenever I look at them. I just think about how dangerous it is for someone to live there. I just settle in on a small apartment by the square. The steward was very nice. I figured\n\nIt's my time to go. I've caused to much trouble for my uncle. §0\n§0\n§0Entry 3#:§0\n§0\n§0  I figure I wrote about my uncle and his family here, they we're.. nice. He had 2 daughters and one baby boy who can barely talk. I feel I'm baby sitting them.\n\nAlthough, they spoil me to pieces, which is guild tripping me day by day. Also.. It's saddens me that they want to move out of their humble state because they found out I was an elf. They could've kick me out, but they din't. They hold on to me. I kick my\n\nit happend twice now in Atlas, so thats when I decide I should move out. I'm going to visit them soon.§0\n§0\n§0Entry 4# :§0\n§0\n§0  I meet a druid today, he was nice, although he said something about our prince being a traitor to his kind?\n\nI try to force a smile and hold my judgement of him. What I get from the conversation though is prespective§0\n§0\n§0Entry 5# :§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Timing of the Drop§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "[!] The parchment would have a lingering lavender scent. Its contents would be written in meticulous cursive.§0\n§0\n§0Come the maiden herself with the dawn,§0\n§0\n§0I yearn for thee like a Siren's song.§0\n§0\n§0With eyes that shine\n\nbrighter than all the stars in the sky,§0\n§0\n§0And a very presence that makes my heart fly up on high.§0\n§0\n§0With faith and grace paralleled by none,§0\n§0\n§0My passion for thee flaring like the Sun.§0\n§0\n§0Be it over lands set\n\nablaze, frozen, or gone without a trace,§0\n§0\n§0Your light shall be my guide, as I seek thy embrace.§0\n§0\n§0- You know who", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Once upon a time, there was an outstanding illusionist. This illusionist, although practicing no magic, could perform the greatest of tricks and guise with only a few tools. The illusionst was completely versatile and skilled in his craft.\n\nThere was no illusionist nor magician that could match wits and precision as this one. Along with this master deciever, came his various guises. To this day, his real name remained a mystery. For the sake of this story, however, we will call him 'Zeten.'\n\n'Zeten,' often performed his tricks out in the general public. It would draw crowds to gaze at his sleight of hand in awe. 'Zeten' thrived by this energy, the energy to be adored. Dozens of the crowds gave 'Zeten' fame, gold, and glory.\n\nIf this illusionist were to have a family and then some - his ancestors would be well off. They would not understand what hunger nor poverty was. This was the capcity of his vast popularity.\n\nThough, this was not so. 'Zeken,' although had much fame, gold, and glory, could not obtain this gift we call relationships. His entire life was led by both mischief, pride, and greed.\n\nA particular ethereal being had caught sight of this on-going boasting and avarice, and so he made haste to manifest upon on of 'Zeken's' shows. \"Come on and come all, for not even a God himself could catch the tricks I bring,\" 'Zeken' bragged.\n\nAn old beggar lady protested against his claim, \"You should not talk so ill for what granted you such blessings.\" The old beggar beared wisdom, though to the crowd and 'Zeken', it was foolishness.\n\n\"Observe!\" 'Zeken' announced to the crowd, \"A trick already done. Seems we have a gullible one to those above.\" The crowd laugh, ostracizing the elder. And by the wag of her crippled finger, the guise was broken.\n\nBefore them all stood a jester. A jester with many relics, bells, and colorful patterns. All stood speechless, only the sound of the falling cloak to be heard. \"Then perhaps your own deceit shall plague you,\" the Jester boomed.\n\nJust a snap of his finger, 'Zeken's' form transfigured to that of an octopus. This Octopus squirmed, inked, and camoflauged by its own embarassment. As for the Jester, it had vanished before the others could blink.\n\nAll fame had vanished, all gold was gone.§0\n§0As he was banished,§0\n§0by his own blind brawn. §", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Alchemy is the study and practice of the natural principle of the equivalent exchange. The equivalent exhange is the principle that to get anything you must put something of equal value.\n\nThe alchemists job is not to mix up the ingredients like a soup, but knowing which ingredients to use, when to add them and how to prepare them. Alchemy Recipes do not speak of exact quantities or times, for there are many ways og having the same value\n\nThe use of symbols is not to because not only the ingredients have perfect representation, but sibling representations are as well necessary to create proper results. The four symbols are Earth, Water, Fire, and Air", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Out Of Character§0\n§0----------------Notable§0\n§0The Sentinel§0\n§0Wisteria Druid§0\n§0Renn§0\n§0Murlocs§0\n§0----------------Murlocs Holds The Record For - Creaction Of Multiple  Druidic Rewrites And Lore Pieces.\n\n----------------Murlocs Holds The Record For - Conservation Of Druidic Lore Against The Opressive Lore Team(Tm)§0\n§0----------------Murlocs Holds The Record For -", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-=-§0\n§0 The Ralengard Novel§0\n§0\n§0            -*-§0\n§0Greed is prominant in the men and woman of Atlas, they strive for false legitimacy and other tangible victorys that they can use to help boost their confidence and prove to themselves that\n\nthey are worth something, but, i can assure you that they are not - no one in this world means anything, just another figure to diminish away over time, just another speck of dust in the wind. It is for this reason selflessness is seldom in these lands,§0\n\npeople know they mean nothing, that is why they strive for pleasing tangible objects to ease their eternal lifely pain in existance.§0\n§0            -=-§0\n§0The Interpretation of modern homosexualites             -*-§0\n§0Homosexuality - a virus, a disease?\n\nMany would beg to differ on the theory of mine, though, they have yet to convince me. It is to my belief that once anothers mans lips intimately connect with your own, you will be infected! §0\n§0\n§0AVOID INTIMACY WITH OTHER MEN AT ALL COSTS - in the name of GOD\n\n            -=-§0\n§0The heathenites shall be smited, their kin shall be spited - for no such crime trumps the lack of faith in GOD. I shall continue to strive for holiness and utter acceptance into the golden gates whilst sending the dirty heathen -\n\nhomosexualites to the firey gates of Iblees.§0\n§0            -*-", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "uhf", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Lost Knights             Travels Vol. I§0\n§0\n§0My name is Kagura Balisri, and this is my story of how i not only became a captain of a guard. but how my life has been that I could remember. As my past has been taken... Here is my tale.............\n\nChapter I- The Awakening. §0\n§0\n§0 The first thing I noticed when i awoke was a splitting headache, one that felt like you would get if you fell off a cliff and live. However that was only the pain, When i tried to open my eyes they almost begged to stay\n\nshut. When i opened my eyes so slowly, it was as if time was slowed down. My eyes felt like they were burning against the blinding rays of the lights of the sun. When i turned to my right i was aware i was on my back at the time. maying on rather soft\n\ngreen grass. My very sight was still a blur for a moment before my sight had caught up to my suroundings i was at a temple by a small pond it seemed. My head had.. rather calmed for the moment after i regained my vision and surroundings.\n\nI was greeted by a monk, dawned in a ragged brown cloak and a  rope around his waist. He exstended his right hand toward me and helped me up, dusting off the little bit of dust and dirt as\n\n*you see the page was scribbled with ink all over it. you can see that a not was eft clean in the middle of it. the hand writing different than the normal author.\"hah, you got pranked.\"was written cleanly on to the paper§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Passport No.:P0002§0\n§0Given Name(S): Thomas§0\n§0Nationality: Suffonian§0\n§0Sex: Male§0\n§0Birthplace: Pembroke§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Light of the moon§0\n§0moves west...§0\n§0thy flowers' shadows§0\n§0creep eastwards§0\n§0\n§0**the short poem seems to be written in yultharan**\n\nThy black cat atop thy tree, the Darker sky on top of we, a white moon shines brightly...§0\n§0\n§0\n§0 I sit and watch §0\n§0on this day of rain§0\n§0for mother nature§0\n§0is crying again...\n\nAs the ocean waves hit the shore, my heart beats, like a fish moving...§0\n§0\n§0A bird on some tree§0\n§0Tweeting loudly.§0\n§0The sun shining just for you and me...", ""),
