        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Cairnforth Ledger§0\n§0\n§0[The book appears to be completely void of any writing of any kind besides the title.]§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "There was a young hafling, Her name was§0\n§0Darby. She came to dunshire alone, and alone she was always. Then she met Marco he and her became the best of friends. She was never alone then. \"so darby..\" marco would start off. \"Yea marco?\" she would ask\n\ncuriously. \"Would you... Erm will you... Errrrrr\" Marco just stopped there unable to let her know he liked her. \"What marco?\" darby asked even more curiously. \"Nothing.\" Marco sighed and turned to walk away. Years went by and darby never knew. She met\n\nanother halfling named malibu, and she began to have feelings for him but her feelings for darby where stronger and she didn't know how to tell him. \"Hey darby..\" malibu said waving at her. \"Oh hey malibu.\" she said smiling \"well i like ya alot.\" he said\n\n\"oh... you do?\" darby said looking down at her feet. \"Yes darby, be my girlfriend?\" Malibu said smiling and holding a flower out to her. \"Erm.. sorry i have feelings for another..\" Darby said and Marco was watching them far away he thought she said yes.\n\nHe was very sad. He ran off into the woods and and sat down on a short stump and cried. He cried till his heart stopped hurting. Even till he couldn't cry anymore. \"oh really who?\" malibu asked. \"Marco.\"She said confidently. \"ah okay good bye then.\" he\n\nsaid and left her alone. \"marco?!\" she shouted out for him but he didnt respond. \"marco please i have something really important to tell you!\" she said yelling around the forrest where he was at. Yet he heard her he still didn't respond. \"i dont love\n\nmalibu! i love you!\" she yelled around where he was. His heart skipped a beat hearing those words. He came out from hiding and scared her from behind. \"i love you too.\" he said smiling  \"You do?!\" she said appearing extremely happy. \"go out with me?\" he\n\nasked her. \"YES A MILLION TIMES YES!\" She screamed and leaped into his arms.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Valor Bell§0\n§0\n§0Charged with:§0\n§0\n§0-Forcing himself onto a female human§0\n§0-Impregnating the female human§0\n§0-Marriage to the woman in order to not birth a bastard§0\n§0-Deserting the army of Arbor\n\nFor this: Valor Bell shall be cruxified under the Canonist Cross, so that God may take mercy onto his soul.", ""),
        StaticBook("Fucc U Ugly Cunt", "§bMûrak'Gorkil", "{\"text\":\"\"}", ""),
        StaticBook("Voidal Basics", "§bKoralon Onyxheart", "§lVoidal Basics§0\n§0\n§0- - - - - - - - - - - §0\n§0\n§0By§0\n§0§oKoralon Onyxheart§0\n§0\n§0\n§0§oTeaching Coursebook§0\n§0§ofor learning Arcane Theory.§0\n§0\n§0§o------------------\n\n§i§0§l1. Soul & Mana§0\n§0\n§0§§§0Every object, every living being is made of mana. Every soul expels excess mana.§0\n§0\n§0This excess mana can be used to manifest spells.\n\n§i§0§l2. The Void§0\n§0\n§0The void is an emptiness. A realm that can be altered with mana, and a realm from where mana can draw on effects to affect the mundane.\n\n§l3. Void Connection§0\n§0\n§0§l§§§0Any mage will need to §0develop a void connection. A connection has to be widened through practice. Connection drains one's strength, both actively and passively. One has to connect to the void to cast spells.\n\n§l4. Mana Anchors§0\n§0\n§0All spells are sustained by a mana anchor. These can be targeted by abjuration, sometimes by physical attacks even. These may be visible.\n\n§l5. Line of Sight§0\n§0\n§0Imagine mana anchors bound to the mage by a string. This string cannot be broken. The mage needs to maintain line of sight to their anchor, and thus, to their spell.\n\n§l6. Aura Theory§0\n§0\n§0Every mage has an aura, with a specific colour. This manifests in most of their spells, and is visible when they connect to the void.\n\n§l7. Voidal Corruption§0\n§0\n§0The void is not without dangers. A mage too power-hungry, or a mage non-careful may easily rip a tear into the void. Similarly, sites of rituals or great spells may leave so-called \"tears\".\n\nThese can be temporary or permanent. A tear is a site where voidal energies freely flow into the mundane world and influence the surroundings in a chaotikal (pun intended) way.\n\n§l8. Mage Circles§0\n§0\n§0Multiple mages may cast a spell together using circles. Circles, however, have a fair chance of ripping a tear into the mundane.\n\n§l9. Mana Gems & Obelisks§0\n§0\n§0Mana may be stored in mana gems. These cannot be used to cast, per se, but to fuel enchantments.§0\n§0\n§0Mana gems have to be regularly re-charged by mages.\n\nA mana obelisk is a giant mana gem with a large amount of mana. Mana obelisks are used to mass-recharge mana gems without exposing mages to fatigue.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Lesser potion of mending:§0\n§0\n§0>Water base§0\n§0>Biteit§0\n§0\n§0-----------------------------There are no weak reagents that actually heal wounds, they are moderate and above so Biteit is the closest one, which is used to clean wounds\n\nModerate potion of speed:§0\n§0\n§0>Distilled water base§0\n§0>Swamp blossom (Speed)§0\n§0>Desert berry bush (Empowerment)\n\nGreater potion of Strength:§0\n§0\n§0>Aqua vitae base§0\n§0>Dwarf's pumpkin (Power, Strength)§0\n§0>Drilltongue (Hardiness)§0\n\nModerate potion of vision:§0\n§0\n§0>Distilled water base§0\n§0>Larihei's fingers (Focus)§0\n§0>Dwarf's pumpkin (Power)\n\nWeaker potion of Love:§0\n§0\n§0>Water base§0\n§0\n§0\n§0-----------------------------Most likely not possible with the current base, the only known herb to have the love aspect is Crimson vase, which is a strong herb.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Fox:§0\n§0\n§0What does a fox do? The fox just kinda walks around with his adorable little orange eyes, going about his regular life as a fox man. This fox's name is 'Jezzabellamarie' and she's a quaint little foxy foxeroo.\n\nThe fox just kinda hangs about, doing his lil thang. The fox goes about biting into fruits and meats and enjoys tapping his feets against the ground like the quaint little guy he is. The fox also just kinda goes about his life as a happy happero camper yo\n\nWhen the fox dies, he kinda realizes that \"Hey, my life was swell, I shouldn't be THAT SAD that im dead\" and so it kinda, just kneels into its next existance. Making fox noises as it yips and yipees into the next bloodline of fox-er-dom or whatever.", ""),
