        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "--------------------------------------          Naztherak\n\n- Grimoires§0\n§0- Green flames, horns, flakey, scaley skin§0\n§0- Potentially a cult of sympathizers around§0\n§0- Karyssmov Faroe§0\n§0- Sylvia\n\nThe dark magic, Naztherak is cast often using a grimoire.§0\n§0An abomination upon this world, its wielders corrupted with horns, peculiar skin, records of even green flames§0\n§0licking the features of the users have been about; The Zar'ei or Zar'kiel.\n\nTheir magic burns with a flame that burns the very soul of its victim,§0\n§0thus only affecting creatures with souls.§0\n§0The fire appears green to the eye.§0\n§0Zar'ei are also capable of summoning demons unto our world using the grimoires they carry with them\n\nZar'ei are derived from descendants, corrupted into their demonic forms. They have basic intelligence, yet tend to be very violent. §0\n§0\n§0It is implied that a cult of sympathizers revolves around these demons.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Milkman§0\n§0      By Hobbs Burrows§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Copied by Fetish\n\nDear reader,§0\n§0This is an original story by Hobbs of Dunshire about a milkman and a baker fighting for the love of a woman.  I hope it is an enjoyable read.§0\n\nYou could hear the hoof beats pound as they raced across the ground, and the clatter of the wheels as they spun 'round and 'round.  He galloped into Festival Street, his badge upon his chest.  His name was Ernie and he drove the fastest milk cart in the\n\nwest!  Now Ernie loved a widow, a lady known as Sue. She lived all alone in Lidley Lane at number 22.  They said she was too good for him, she was haughty, proud and chic, but Ernie got his cocoa there three times every week!  She said she'd love to bathe\n\nin milk and he said \"Alright sweetheart.\"  And when he finished work on night he loaded up his cart.  He said \"D'you want it pasteurized?  Caused pasteurized is best.\"  She said \"Ernie I'll be happy if it comes up to me chest!\"  That tickled old Ernie.\n\nNow Ernie had a rival, an evil-looking man.  Called Two Ton Ted from Teddington, and he drove the baker's van.  He tempted her with his treacle tarts and his tasty wholemeal bread.  And when she seen the size of his hot meat pies it very near turned her\n\nhead.  She nearly swooned at his macaroon and he said \"If you treat me right, you'll have hot rolls every morning, and crumpets every night.\"  He knew once she sampled his layer cake he'd have his wicked way, and all Ernie had to offer was a pint o'milk a\n\nday.  Once lunch time, Ted  saw Ernie's horse and cart outside her door.  It drove him mad to find it was still there at half past four.  And as he lept down from his van, hot blood through his veins did coarse, and he went across to Ernie's cart and\n\ndidn't half kick his horse (Whose name was Trigger, and he pulled the fastest milk cart in the west).  Now Ernie rushed out into the street, he milk bottle in hand.  He said \"If you wanna marry Susie, you'll fight for her like a man!\"  \"Oh why don't we\n\nplay cards for her?  Ted sneeringly replied, \"And just to make it interested we'll have minas on the side.\"  Now Ernie dragged him from his van and beneath the blazing sun, they stood there face to face, and Ted went for his bun.  But Ernie was too quick\n\nthings didn't go the way Ted planned, and a strawberry flavoured yoghurt sent it spinning from his hand!  Now Susie ran between them and tried to keep them apart, but Ernie push her aside and a rock cake caught him underneath his heart, and he looked up\n\nin pained surprise and the concrete hardened crust of a stale pork pie caught him in the eye, and Ernie bit the fust.  Ernie was only 52, he didn't wanna die.  And now he's gone to make deliveries in that village in the sky.  Where the customers\n\nare Aenguls, and ferocious dogs are banned, and the milkman's life is full of fun in that fairy dairy land.  But a woman's needs are many fold.  And sue, she married Ted.  But strange things happened on their wedding night as they lay in their bed.\n\nwas that the trees a rustling?  Or the hinges of the gate?  Or Ernie's ghostly milks a rattling in their crates!", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Arhadirs notes on the  boiling points of 4 metals§0\n§0\n§0List of Metals§0\n§0Ferrum (Iron)§0\n§0Aurum (Gold)§0\n§0Steel§0\n§0Copper§0\n§0Titanium\n\nFerrum (Iron)§0\n§0The melting point for is around Iron is around 1,500°C and the boiling point is around 2,900°C\n\nAurum (Gold)§0\n§0The melting point for Aurum is around 1,100°C and the boiling point is around 2,700°C\n\nSteel§0\n§0Steel is an Alloy of ferrum often crafted by Humans. Its metling point is around 1400°C and the boiling point is around 2800°C\n\nCopper§0\n§0The melting point for Copper is 1,085 °C and the boiling point is around 2,500 °C\n\nTitanium§0\n§0The melting point of Titanium is 1,668 °C and the boiling point is around 3,300°C", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I've sucsessfully reached the top of the ice wall with my friend Leslie! Thanks to some pickaxes, rope and some dwarven ruins, we made it to the top. There's nothing up there besides some penguins, no sign of undead roaming on the top. The views are very\n\nbeutifull and its very cold up here. I'm going to go see if Leslie has found anything of importance, we divided ourselves to inspect the top faster since we dont have as much time as i initially thought. §0\n§0Finally found Leslie, we're going to camp up here\n\nand eat out provisions, then we're going to head down for the day.\n\nNow i am in Belvitz tavern, im sitting in the one seater, my clothes are still damp from the trip, good thing this Hoo-Kah gives off some nice warmth. Right now i'm sitting next to a couple, a girl and a guy, the man doesn't seem very talkative and this\n\nis quite fun to watch, these two would make a good comedian duo. An aquaintance of mine just came in, Vlad i think his name is... he sat next to the man but left soon after he saw that he wasn't very welcomed at the table. Seems like those two know each\n\nother more than i anticipated, they are not whispering to each other, don't know what they are saying but they've exchanged some gift, oh she's coming o [!] there are bloodstains on the cover of the book [!].\n\nBblackish (Natalia vasiliev)§0\n§0Nectorist (Andrei)§0\n§0^^ OOC Info, dont use\n\nIn Belvitz again, sitting next to a couple, they're not doing much, this could end like last time so i'll be extra catious. The girl doesn't seem very old, but the man seems way older than her. They're whispering so I can't really figure out what they're\n\nsaying, not that I care, really, its not my buisness so i wont even attempt to listen. Thanks to the Barkeep i figured out her name is Anwen, but the barkeep called the guy her new toy, found that pretty funny. This barkeep is very nice, the person who\n\nsaw my asilants isn't called Vlad, its Vladan, and he is captain of the guard in Belvitz. And the guy next to me is aparently the leader of the Trident Rangers, so getting his name later shouldn't prove too difficult. Sorry, not Trident, Trigent Rangers.\n\nWell I'm off to the manor again, I found some nice gifts i can give to the family.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "--=-(x)-Day1-(x)-=--§0\n§0\n§0It's duh first dey when moi, moi lil' cuzin and moi lil' bruddah are goin' in a travel tu learn majic.§0\n§0\n§0Day: Gettin' ready tu leave, we went tu get duh pay from Dwifar.§0\n§0After dat we started our trip.§0\n§0\n§0Evening: We\n\narrived at Holm wondering for people to teach us magic.§0\n§0Until now the supplies are looking good for us.§0\n§0We have finally meet Dark Elves who can learn majik.§0\n§0We have been told that at Warhawke is someone that can teach us.\n\nNight: We arrived at a wizard tower but there was no activity.§0\n§0I left a sign, hopefully i will get a bird back.§0\n§0First day was a failure, we were forced to get back to Kaz'Ulraah because the dark was coming.\n\n--=-(x)-Day2-(x)-=--§0\n§0Day: Moi, moi bruddah and moi cuzin 're goin' tu follow different paths.§0\n§0I've been told tu find moi way towards Caras Eldar located in Dominion of Malin§0\n§0\n§0Evening: They said i didnt had duh standarts tu learn lordak in Dominion\n\nso I started tu gu with moi cuzin at Holm.§0\n§0Oi arrived at Holm and it seems like no one is tellin' is anythung.§0\n§0Nothin' happend yet§0\n§0Lookin' at duh map, at -1397 47 2186 a red haired elgus is lettin' people at her home", ""),
        StaticBook("A Sealed Scroll", "§bCaliph Faiz Kharadeen", "Dearest David Campos or any Salvian official,\n\nI hope all is well within the nation of Salvus, may prosperity continue to reign over your lands! I bring you news over the terms of allianceship between our two humble nations.\n\nThe council meeting of advisors has just finished, and I write this letter fresh after the meeting. \n\nThe council unfortunately have come to the decision of declining any sort of allianceships/defensive pacts\n\nat this time. 9 against the idea of a defensive pact while 3 in favor. It is a unanimous decision, I am afraid. \n\nEach one has brought up convincing arguments agianst a defensive pact, such as how both our militaries are not prepared\n\nfor warfare, and the many disadvantages to going to war if it comes to it. We spoke long and plenty on it, and I have to agree with my advisors on this. I am no leader if I desregard what my people want. I am sorry.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nMay peace be with you and your people, perhaps in the future things can turn in a different direction.\n\nSigned by,\nCaliph Faiz Kharadeen", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "golden commander§0\n§0velkan II§0\n§0Siege of Kal'Agnar§0\n§0iron elder§0\n§0Shallmandril§0\n§0Simmpa§0\n§0Egregore", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0\n§0          Atrithar's§0\n§0            Journal§0\n§0\n§0               1676\n\nOn the 13th of The Grand Harvest,§0\n§0\n§0In Halsworthy, for the first time in many years, I had come across a mali'aheral. We were joined by Evie Avern, an elf who left quite an impression. She had traveled alone since she was a child. We had noticed a...\n\n...visible§0 affliction. A woman called Hiro D'eril tortured her in order to send some sort of message to her adopted mother. This particular menace, Evie mentioned, lives in Arbor, but often travels to Holm and Haense. Perhaps I ought to avoid this...\n\n...particular§0 character in my future travels.\n\nOn the 14th of The Great Harvest,§0\n§0\n§0I gathered supplies and departed for a trip to the North by sea. Soon after I arrived, I came across a young Farfolk girl who, due to necessity, joined me on my travels as an assistant. We traveled the North for...\n\n...a few days prior to making the decision to return South to visit my homeland of Haelun'or. Word had traveled that the mali'aheral had begun returning home. Maybe it was about time.\n\nOn the 18th of The Grand Harvest,§0\n§0\n§0My assistant and I found the newly-established Echantry guild here in the city, where we met two strange men. One man who went by Varys led the three of us to the library, which we had all been searching for. After...\n\n...arriving§0, Varys departed. The remaining man, mysterious as he was, asked us for aid in finding a particular book on illumination magic. Shortly thereafter, the man revealed to us he is a clinician from the city of Ceras Eldar, but is rather vague on...\n\n...the§0 details. Harlan Everage was the man's name. The doctor seemed impressed by my education in the natural sciences, and noted that he sought the guild, where we decided to visit. Unfortunately, no one was available at the guild building. So...\n\n...naturally§0 attempted to lockpick a door. We were caught by a handful of guild members, one of which was well-aquainted with the doctor. They speak alone in the Enchantry courtyard while the rest of us make small talk. Soon thereafter, when speaking...\n\n...with§0 the doctor, he reveals to me his identity: an Ascended, one who was resurrected. I had not expected this, but was inclined to believe this man. As he departed, he tells me he will be watching me in whatever I choose to do, whether I join the...\n\nEnchantry or not. \"I see great potential in you\" he tells me. He's right. I must stay here in the city and continue my studies.\n\nOn the 11th of Sun's Smile,§0\n§0\n§0I spend the day in the library to refresh myself on the New Elvish dialect, which I'm afraid I have not had the chance to use in a great many years. I read through all five volumes, authored by Kalenz Uradir.\n\nOn the 12th of Sun's Smile,§0\n§0\n§0I settle in to my new home here in the city at Tower Six. After unpacking what little belongings I have, I left to return to the library for further reading. But I hear a voice call for me from across the courtyard.\n\n\"Just the young elf I was looking for!\" says the man, who emerged from behind the foundtain. Harlan Everage and I reaquaint and I invite him into my home. Harlan brought a gift: a great steel sword with a glistening silver hilt. upon which is an...\n\n...engraved§0 mongoose. Harlan told me to speak the words \"Tasmeth, ignite.\" Upon verablizing these words, the blade's entire surface covered in a vaguely green holy flame. Harlan assured me the flame would not harm the user, but would severely burn...\n\n...those§0 with altered, corrupted souls upon contact. I gratefully thanked the doctor and decided to join the man as he returned to the Enchantry for some personal business.\n\nOn the 14th of Sun's Smile,§0\n§0\n§0Both I and the doctor waited patiently in the lobby of the Enchantry. Harlan penned a letter and sent it off to notify the guildmaster of our arrival. He soon arrived to fetch us, leading us into a vault in the lower...\n\n...echelon§0 of the guild building. There, the guildmaster handed Harlan a mysterious ring, which he mentioned was a ring of illusion. I noticed a change in color in the doctor's eyes as he slipped it on to his finger.\n\nOn the 15th of Sun's Smile,§0\n§0\n§0Harlan and I were led out of the vault by Morgan Hallowfall, a fellow mali'aheral of the Enchantry guild. The man revealed he was an adept mage, but when asked by Harlan to produce a display of sensory...\n\n...illusion§0 magic, rolled up his sleeve to reveal a curved tattoo of red processed ruibrium. He claimed he could not currently use any sort of magic and assured us that it was merely for testing. But looking at Harlan's expression, perhaps there was...\n\n...more§0 to this story than the man was willing to let us know. We continued with small talk in the hall for quite a while, but soon departed ways.\n\nOn the 16th of Sun's Smile,§0\n§0\n§0I returned to the library and resumed reading on the topic of New Elvish linguistics. Finishing this, I wandered upstairs to inquire into mali'aheral societal works. \"On Racism\" by Lucion Sullas in particular caught...\n\n...my§0 eye. The sentiment expressed in the book did not fall on deaf ears, but was perhaps preaching to the choir. Clearly the mali'aheral ought to remain dutifull to the purity of our bloodline. I am beginning to feel right at home here in...\n\n...Haelun'or§0. The sense of community and pride in oneself, but also in one's race is a truly refreshing change from the lack thereof during my travels. I am quite looking forward to my stay here. I may be able to learn much from the popular Enchantry...\n\n...guild§0 which has moved to this city, their home, expressing a duty to their people. I may be able to gleen some further knowledge of the wider world I seem to have missed on my travels studying the natural sciences from the doctor during his stay. He...\n\n...plans§0 to remain here in the city for some time to establish a clinic.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "-=(+)=-------------Kaz'ulrah Clinic Logs\n\nKori Stormbreaker§0\n§0Cured a sore throat, by having the patient ingest half a bottle of Minor Mending potion.§0\n§0Payed 15 mina§0\n§014th of The Amber Cold, 1678\n\nErik§0\n§0Treated a large ankle laceration, by using supplies provided in a Druidically Enhanced Healing Kit, and used all of its contents. The laceration was LARGE, and it went through half of his ankle!§0\n§0No mina payed. It was 175.§0\n§015th of The Amber§0\n§0>\n\nCold, 1678§0\n\nEmbo Silvervein§0\n§0Treated a neck laceration with a Triage kit, and a Lesser Mending Potion. He will need the stitches removed in a week or so.§0\n§0No mina payed. It was 65 mina.§0\n§05th of The Suns Smile, 1678\n\nKoralon Onyxheart§0\n§0Extracted a sprite shard from patients neck, used a druidic healing kit, and a triage kit. With the aid of Kazrin, she was saved.§0\n§0No mina payed. It was 190 mina.§0\n§013th of The Suns Smile, 1680", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Smithing Arts are that which many a dwarf has fallen in love with. The challenge, the sense of purpose, the satisfaction of crafting a masterpiece.\n\nWhile no book can teach the smithing art, this one aims to give the outside observer, the scholar, the merchant, or merely the curious a glimpse into what smithing is and why it is, truly, an art.\n\nChapter 1: The Blacksmith§0\n§0\n§0Blacksmith are the bread and butter of the smithing arts, they make Stone and iron tools. Every apprentice begins as a Blacksmith, making hoes for farmers or pickaxes for miners.\n\nThe Blacksmith's art is one of honed perfection. Crafting hoes or pickaxes until they can do it more efficiently, more effective, than anyone. A masterpiece of a Blacksmith is well treasured, many a dwarf miner would love a masterwork pickaxe.\n\nChapter 2: The Armorsmith§0\n§0\n§0\n§0The Armorsmith is the second most common after the Blacksmith, for every nation's military requires a set of armor for their men, and of course the best armor is smithed, not stiched.\n\nArmorsmith's are known for crafting legendary masterpieces that do their job well. If ever you hear a sword grind across your body, but do no harm, you will know what brings satisfaction to armorsmiths.\n\nCh 3: The Bladesmith§0\n§0If its sharp, a bladesmith is responsible for making it. Bladesmiths craft arrows, swords, battleaxes, or any number of sharp tools. §0\n§0Every mighty weapon has a bladesmith standing behind it.\n\nBladesmith's are generally more ambitious, trying to craft masterpieces that outdo anyone else. There is always the race between them because the Bladesmith whose weapons pierce any armor will have their name recorded through all history.\n\nCh: 4 The Goldsmith§0\n§0Goldsmith's are artists usually less capable or they would be making a masterpiece of Iron. They make jewelery, or parts required to be made of gold. Occasionally they even make Armor or weapons, but it is largely decorative.\n\nGoldsmith's masterpieces tend to be the mundane base for objects of incredible magic power. Many Goldsmiths are also merchants that buy trade and sell other goods. They tend to be the least trustworthy kind of smith. Ye have been warned.\n\nCh 5: The Engineer§0\n§0The Engineer is a kind of smith unlike any other. They have often mastered all the previous forms of smithing and put their experience to the test to create something new. The sword was once a new invention.\n\nEngineer's satisfaction comes from creating something new that changes how something functions for the better. The one who invented a bow changed war forever. §0\n§0If you have ever seen a trebuchet fire then you can understand why what engineers do is an art.\n\nCh 6. Runesmiths§0\n§0Runesmith's are a rare, select, group of people who crafted many ancient dwarves sacred things. Their process is so secret that there is no information outside of being very dexterity demanding.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Roland O'Castro§0\n§0\n§0(Username: Cranky_Varangian)§0\n§0\n§0Engineer/scholar wishes to exchange notes", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Trade deal with Sutica§0\n§0\n§0Terms of the Trade agreement with Sutica:§0\n§0\n§0- No aggression will be had between both kingdoms§0\n§0- Kaz'Ulrah will recieve a store, with a built in house§0\n§0- The two kingdoms will sign a friendship agreement with one\n\neachother.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Signed by§0\n§0\n§0Garrond Frostbeard,§0\n§0High Remembrance§0\n§0Gorum Frostbeard,§0\n§0High Ambassador§0\n§0\n§0Sutica leader: ______", ""),
