        StaticBook("Book of Things", "§bAluatis", "{\"text\":\"\"}", ""),
        StaticBook("My Struggle", "§bKaiser Decimus Rovin, Vandalore", "====Heil Valdoria==== \n\n\n\n     The Rise of the\n     Colored Kingdoms\n\n\n    \n        Approved by\n   The Reich Ministry\n          Of Truth\n\nForeward\n\nThe treatise of which follows this breif forward has been legislated upon the direct mandate of the Kaiser and his white sons. It is all very scientific, you see. Praise the Kaiser and hail the White Flame.\n\nSince his inception, the race of man has proved his superiority over the lesser kindred time and time again, and thus, it is undoubtedly proven by science that man is Kaiser's chosen race. There is no question in the matter, for man and only man possesses\n\nthe conviction and blessing to mold a mighty empire, forged from the frisson of today, and supported on all facets by our pure ancestors. The dubious assertion against our one and true God and his honor guards is that of defeatist and Serenist dogmatic\n\npestilence, inseminated from the vile gasses of hell and popagated by the black worms and Kharadeen sympathizers. Man is true. Man is Kaiser's chosen disciple, and let his superior and engorged-gargantuan loins deluge the slime of elgenism and defeatism\n\nfrom our seed. All hail Kaiser's seed and immaculate fluids.\n\nAs of thus far, the intent of our father is rather opague, but within the contents of this binding of which follows, all his glory and prowess will be clear. For one to question the prowes\n\nor glory of our Lordi s blasphemy. Which despite punishment by which of means which shall be shined upon in further detail in at a further period, blasphemy is a sin. Thus, if one were to follow with utmost punctuality, he would find that the treatise\n\nof which I have been bestowed the pious and ethereal act of concieving is in fact the unwavering voice of Kaiser. It is all very scientific, and though I doubt one may absorb his excellence with ease, for his excellence is that of an infinite well of\n\ngolden wine, I advise one suckle at my knowledge with great heed. One must not tug nor bite when contracting the teat of Kaiser, one must priase him with a sublt pursuing, for only then will his grace seep at a rate conceivable by his sons.\n\nThe Sprouting of Man\n\n   The history of man is that of great piety and virtue. In practically all corners of our realm, man's raw exuberance is sown deep within the heart of the Kaiser's Seed, and his mighty, booming prowess can be felt in each and\n\nevery heart of all who inhabit it. Man has fought with many breeds in his legacy, and man still remains, but not as a refugee or vagabond. Man has survived in a fashion comparable to a seed of iron-wood oak, for his blessing lay deep within the soil,\n\ndormant but with pride, and when time comes and the Kaiser commands the man to grow, to build, to conquer, then and only then is mans' pride as palpable as the Kaiser's own. \n   Our race emerges from the remains of lesser breeds, fueled by the purity o\n\nhis white pride and the blessings of our Lord and Savior. All the way he spourts, man takes most attentiveness to his every direction, constantly and diligently enforcing his prowess, his muscles of pure force bulge and pulsate under the immense pressure\n\nof his pride. It appears that no force could ever discourse his destined and premeditated path, for man will ascend until his most superior of faculties scrapes the heavens and is once again reunited with his benevolent father. \n   His roots at which\n\npoint cleave deep into the blackened earth, for the front of darkness ever will seep into our fluids. Thus we must fight, we must never, as a hope, as a dream, we must never be diluted by the inferior vestigial corpses of the damned races. And as man's\n\ngreat limbs spread with unmeasurable force and national pride, the worms of the black sludge will begine to fester. They cross into our realm illegally, without the blessing of the Kaiser, and they burrow deep within our cavities. The very seeds of our\n\npride have been sabotaged! They feast upon our flesh and excrete tar from their pores. They fester and slosh in such ooze and amass great pits of darkness. They brred with no grace or consent, they feed with glutionous intent, and they spread the foul\n\nlies of their filthy heathen, sub-humanist Ebolinism.\n   As the sludge of the black worms collects deep within our bowels and extremities, the flame of our brethren begins to fade. The skin of a once pure race will blacken under the tremendous, bloated\n\nweight of the pestilent bog, and our great minds which once yielded the venerated sciences and arts will rot and drain through our facial cavities. Soon, if we continue on our path so grossly discourse from the Kaiser's will our own beautiful race will no\n\nlonger be even remotely recognizeable. We will be diluted to a state so impoverished and emaciated of all pride that we will have not even the conviction to cognate the most primal of tasks. We will at this point be that of which we have fought, we will\n\nbe all which we have feared. We will be the elfen. \n   But alas, this is not the course of man. Man will never be so easily dissolved by such spurious doctrine, for man is the direct fluid of the Holy One, the Creator, The one true hope for the salvati\n\nfor nationalism and pride. So my dear white brothers, we must show the Kaiser that we are worthy. We must prove to him that we as a hope, as a dream for all that is pure in this realm, the man has not and never will forget his divine quest! Let us\n\nimpale the rotten flesh with scolding-bladed tapes and drain the fetis wastes from our cavities! Let us carve out the filthy conspirators and blackened worm colonies, from each and every facet of our impenetrable bark of hardened iron!\n\nLet us Fight, my brothers! Let us fight for the salvation of the Kaiser and his seeds!\n\nThe Salvation of the Kaiser\n\nPraise He, the one and only, the true voice of good in a realm so corroded by the acrid sins of the lesser races. Praise he whose might and sheer dauntlessness shall cleanse the arachnids of pit and moss, he who\n\nshall save our white souls from the vile feces of Ebolnism and the Serenist web. Praise he who shall and forever will be the one and the only true God, praise our Lord and our grandest of Kings. All Praise the Kaiser!\n   Praise our blessed hearth, for\n\nhis glorious egg lay a seed, a hope, a dream for a world of white fire. All hail the flame of God and King, praise the fervent inferno of cleansing, and let it smolder in the hearts of each and every white man, for now and ever. For us, let the flame\n\nguide us, let it illuminate the blackened path into oblivion, the shady death march speckled with infected warts of flesh and pus and other such fecal jellies, that of which spawn the prickly seeds of the Degenerate race and the Serenist arachnids.\n\nBut alas, have not fear my fellow white brothers. Praiser the Kaiser, for through his wisdom may we purge the septic grubs with flame and gas. Let our nationalism and tenacious pride obliterate their weak and feeble and highly demonic colonies. Let our\n\nwhite flame raze each and every festering cesspit from which they spawn, and let us forcefully enter their diseased posterior cavities in the name of the glorious Kaiser.\n\n======================================\n\n\n  The Struggle of Our\n    Nation and Great\n         Charter Of\n        Vanderkind\n\n\n\n\n=====================================\n\nFor the glory of a great nation is to kinder the white flame of our ancestors, the divine right of our Kings, and the holy grace of our one true God. \n\nIn the wake of war and the feckless sheeding of national pride through the unrelenting plot of\n\nSerenist Ebliontologists in coalition with Communist doctrine, only the few, so the Kaiser wills it, only the most true and pure will survive the coming fire of the primal apocalypses. So when we, as a people, as a hope, must ask why it is that the\n\nof the black worms in our governments and in the highest and most divine of positions in the high counsel have become so, we must ask ourselves instead why it is that the inferior races have rejected the pious might of the one true Lord and Savior.\n\nThis is why we must act, for the sake of all that is holy and for the propsperity of culture and civilization, and only through the social rec-construction of our deprived filth of elfen lies and slime can we regain the trust of the Kaiser and pray for\n\nhis forgiveness.\n\n===The Grace Of===\n====The Kaiser====\n\nAll haill thee who flows water into our rivers, plants seeds, into our soil, delivers bread to our bellies and children to our kindred. Blessed thee, our one true Lord, who in the gra\n\nand pious does he who impregnates the seed of life to our loins and the fires of national pride into our hearts. The Kaiser, in all his glory, is the one and true God, for he and only he is divine and pure. \n\nHowever the Kaiser is displeased with\n\nour existence. For ages, the Serenists, the enemy of all that is good and beautiful, has festered at the hearts of our brothers. They have plagued the grace and purity of the ethereal and pure Vanders, the one true race, and they have spilled their seeds\n\namongst the black and sodomite flesh of the negarious degenerate race. Our Savior is furious. He holds our fate in that of which is a thread over the boiling pits of Iblees' grasp. Only his will remains as our salvation, and we have allowed it to be\n\nspilled out of the crucible of the one, the pure race of men. We have enabled the impure to breed for far too long.\n\n====The Love====\n===Of the Rector===\n\nIt is the will of the divine right of the RTector and his unfathomable purity to protect the soverignty and pride of our nation, and so it be, the glory of our nation is now buckling under the weight of the\n\nglutenous elfen conspiracy. Only through the love of Priorism, the one true ideology, can the love and passion of the Kaiser be felt deep within our cavities. heil the Grandmaster, for through his divine right shall we drink the blood of all who oppose\n\nthe might and prowess of Saradomin and his belssings upon the grace of our nation and the love of our fathers.\n\n===The Blessings===\n==Of Our Fathers==\n\nLoveth thee who drained the swamps, chiseled the stone, impregnated the woman and filled the Kaiser's realm with the seed of the pure men and his Birthright to Gielinor. Only through the love of our fathers\n\nmay our seeds be spread into the wombs of the Kaiser's purity, and therefore, the mothers of our race shall be pure. May we suckle from his teat, and love his divine will until the time of departure to the realm of the Kaiser. All hail the Kaiser and the\n\nfathers of our seed.\n\nIf not for the will of the Kaiser, in all of his blessed glory, shall we dictate his grace amonst the scum races of our plagued realm. Let us Educate the feeble and lost in the glory of national pride and save them from the repu\n\nsludge of Serenism. Let us feed the bellies of the poor with the love fluids of god's seed. Let us forge from the ashes of the quarreling micronations a golden utopia of the pure and strong, and let us sow the seeds of the New World Order.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bestiary V1", "§bAdeon of Rhoswen", "The Marked Man's Bestiary\n\nContents:\n1. Beasts of Nature\n2. Natural Monstrosities\n3. Sentient Supernaturals\n3. Supernatural Monstrosities\n4. Constructs\n\n-Beasts of Nature-\n\nThese creatures are the beasts commonly seen throughout the world and pose no real threat to the innocent mundane.\n\nCanines: Either intelligent pack hunters or less witty companion animals, the canine often possesses sharp teeth and fur- unlike their Ursidae cousins, they are not often large and do not possess significantly sharp claws. Canines are known to be tamable.\n\nRats: These creatures are the messengers of coming pestilence and death, they've the standard qualities expected of small rodents. Extended exposure to these creatures often leads to sickness, earning them the nickname \"Plague bearers\".\n\nBats: These creatures are physically quite similar to the common rat despite the fact that they have wings and do not possess a tail.\nThey're generally nocturnal and have an enhanced sense of hearing which makes up for their poor vision.\n\nBirds: Variations of these are seen far and wide. From the common pigeon to the barn owl. The creatures have near countless variations and are often used to carry messages over long distances. They are mostly harmless.\n\nSand Tortoise: These creatures are of staggering size. We've precious little information on the beasts and taking one down would require no less than a siege party. The creature grows in size rivaling a small keep. They are extremely rare.\n\nSand Lizard: A common sight within the Orcish deserts. These creatures are surprisingly fast and can topple a target with very little effort. Their hide is nothing worthy of note. Their bones are of decent density and genuinely sturdy.\n\n-Natural Monstrosities-\n\nThese are the creatures commonly found within nature but are considered perverse and diluted in purpose. They're to be hunted and their existence extinguished.\n\nThe Harpy: These monsters have the ability to fly and resemble ugly women- their skin is extremely oily and susceptible to fire. They're bones are quite brittle and will crack under pressure. Their feathers are fine for use in arrows and their pelts make-\n\n-for good middle class clothing. They've a cruel sense of humor. They are known to scoop up targets and drop them from lethal heights. If a Harpy nest is discovered it is suggested that it be burned immediately.\n\nKrummavisur: Resembling a Raven, though staggering in size. These beasts have awe-inspiring wing spans and considerable strength.\nThey scoop up their prey and toss them immeasurable distances. The beast is not to be fought alone. They can kick up dust-\n\n-with the density to block sight for yards. When effort is applied they can shove a man in full plate to his knees with the power of the air from their wings alone. It is suggested that the feet are struck, as they are quite thin and easy to amputate.\n\nCockatrice: An odd looking creature. Standing at the height of a small building with the width to match.\nThey are quite intimidating to fight up close and are able to fly, rendering close combat to be the inevitable result of an encounter.\n\nThe Cockatrice has the ability to exhale a thick gray smog that turns whoever comes in contact with it to stone. Being submerged in water will negate this effect.\nTheir skin is unholy in strength, steel will hardly damage it, an aurum blade is required\n\nThe Beast's bones are strong as stone and they've the strength to topple a building with ease.\n\nLeaf Apes: Fundamentally illusive creatures that have flesh as hard as rock and bones like fresh timber. They possess decent strength for their size but struggle to penetrate leather. They tend to rush a target and make an effort to climb atop its face.\n\nOnce atop the victim's face, the Leaf Ape will tear at the flesh. Bladed steel weapons are practically useless against these creatures and will often break upon contact with their skin- blunt weapons are suggested as well as aurum swords.\n\nCave Leeches: A beast that drops down on it's targets and spews acid onto them, it has the strength to render armor useless. They only attack in complete darkness. \n\nNo one has survived an encounter thus far.\n\nDrakes: Creatures with bat-like wings, the ability to breathe flame, scaly hides, complete with muscular legs and tail-- these truly majestic beasts have captured the awe of men for centuries. Despite this, magical perversion has lead to the Drake species\n\nundergoing various mutations and become near extinct. It is expected that combat with a Drake be avoided and alternative methods to killing be used to neutralise the threat such a beast poses. The Drake's main weaknesses are its wings, mouth and eyes,\n\n-however this beast will continue fighting until the last drop of blood runs from it's wound. Decapitation and siege weaponry is suggested.\n\nEnlarged Arachnid:\n\nThe average spider, though colossal in size and extremely venomous- they are susceptible to fire and relatively easy to defeat compared to other beasts in this compendium.\n\n-Sentient Naturals-\n\nThese beings are to be reasoned with if possible and relocated away from areas where they may have negative effects on the local mundane population.\n\nTroll: Usually found lurking under bridges, in caves or forests. These beasts can be at times helpful and friendly-- at other times they are forces to be reckoned with. Trolls are generally quite intelligent and are capable of speech, complex emotion and-\n\n-co-operation. The best method of slaying a Troll is to use aurum and to disable it's method of movement, trolls are known to carry enormous amounts of weight in the form of fat around their waist and are unable to get up if any of their legs are damaged.\n\n-Sentient Supernaturals-\n\nThese beings are to be reasoned with and if possible relocated away from areas where they may have negative effects on the local mundane.\n\nSpecters: Spirits without bodies, these beings can be benevolent, neutral or malevolent, just like a living person. They can only be harmed by aurum as normal metals will pass straight through them.\nSpecters have the ability to wield enchanted weaponry\n\n-and don enchanted armor, some have the ability to fly and cast spells, those that have this ability use it to deadly effect. It is suggested that aurum weaponry be used combined with a high-guard stance.\nSpecters are vulnerable to salt and it is-\n\n-suggested that the perimeter in which the spirit is manifesting be surrounded by lines of pure sea salt.\n\n-Constructs-\n\nThese are the result of spells or golemmancy, they are able to fit into the supernatural sentient category as well as the monstrous supernatural category depending on what they are- constructs usually have a master and a purpose to foll\n\nHunters: \n\nSharing many traits with a specter, the Hunter has the ability to fly- it wears large, heavy armor but is not impeded in any way by this fact. The Hunters are apparently a sort of Golem gone rogue, they once served a holy order and sought\n\n-slay dangerous Magi. Now they slay any who wield magic, including Marked Men. Hunters explode when defeated and it is advised that those who have defeated it clear the area before it does so, as shrapnel is often projected.\nAurum seems to weaken the-§\n\n-creature considerably, though it is probably wise to use steel in order to damage the armor before an aurum weapon is presented.\nHalf swording is suggested due to the armored nature of this foe.\n\nGolems: The result of powerful runes and magic, Golems can take many forms- from colossal lumbering humanoid to slithering metal snake, all Golems have an 'Impera' who dictates their every action-- Golems will attempt to protect these individuals at all-\n\n-costs. These constructs are often the result of a soul being bound to the magegold core, destroying this would most likely neutralise the threat. \nWays to destroy the Golem depend on a number of things including environment and the material the Golem\n\n-made of. Golems made of stronger materials may need to be cast from great heights, thrown into watery depths or toppled into a substance hot enough to melt metal.\n\n-Supernatural Monstrosities-\n\nThese creatures defy all reason. They serve no purpose in this world and are to be slain.\n\nNecrophages: These creatures come in two variations; Fleshed and Skeletal.\n\nFleshed typically maintain a slumped posture, they've considerable strength and an immunity to pain.\n\nAurum weaponry is recommended for these types of creatures.\n\nAlone, their presence is a joke, but when amassed it's often best to simply route.\nThe method of reanimation is unknown, however it is to be noted that they appear more frequently around areas of frequent fighting or wickedness.\nFire is a weakness.\n\nLich: The ultimate product of an individual's greed for power or knowledge. Liches are beings that have made a transformation into entities powered purely on arcane energies and a deep seated hatred for those that get in the way of more power.\n\nTypes of Liches vary broadly and improvisation is to be expected. One recurring trait seems to be the presence of a crystal known as the phylactery- it is where the Lich's soul is rumoured to be kept, destroying this crystal will kill the creature.\n\nBloodsuckers/Sangbriseur:\nThese creatures take the form of an obscene lump of slimey acid. Depending on their environment, the creature can absorb it's surroundings and become deadlier-- there are such things as Bloodsuckers who have absorbed fire,\n\nbecoming thrice as dangerous as their acidic counterparts. To dispose of the creature, it is suggested that it be cut into smaller pieces and set alight-- be sure that every chunk is burnt or else it will regenerate over time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sheet Music: 433", "§bHeruza", "{\"text\":\"\"}", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0§l    The Halfling§0\n§0§l      Civil War§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0§l     §0      By§0\n§0          Utaria§0\n§0  Helenson-Anarion\n\n§lChap. I §0\n§0§lThe Rising Crisis§0\n§0\n§0In 1686, Rollo Applefoot made declaration that the Elders of Dunshire had done nothing to progress the Halflings of Dunshire past their current point. He declared his intentions to seize the Thainship for himself.\n\nHowever, as the situation progressed it became clear that the Halfling Elders would not back down from their position of tradition. Primary leadership on the Anti-Rollo side lay in the Halfling Elder Harold.\n\n§lChap. II§0\n§0§lThe Battle of Dunshire§0\n§0\n§0With Political lines drawn, the Halflings decided the only way to decide a leader was a snowball fight. In late 1686, the battle broke out between two snowforts set up in the outskirts of Dunshire.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Clerics", "§bKaryssmov Faroe", "The concept of holiness. The grasp of Purity. \nThe Light.\nThe Flame.\nThe Fire.\nThe Stag.\nThe Vehement Lord.\n\n\nWhat does it mean? \nWhat are these things?\nHow does one work to\nbetter themselves via them?\n\nThere are many paths of purity, seeker. There are methods and concepts beyond our own grasp, set in forth by the Aengul, Tahariae.\n\nBut who is Tahariae?\n\nTahariae is the Aengul of Purity. He represents the Light that is both a concept, and a literal thing. Perhaps you have been healed by a Cleric before. Have you felt the warmth and calmness flow through you? That is the Light, made manifest.\n\nThe Light has many properties to it, but it always comes from the Lord of Light. The Light can heal, purge taint, remove poisons, even remove curses...\n\nBut at the same time, that is not always enough.\n\nThen comes the Clerics of War, myself being one. War Light is slightly different from the Light used to heal. It is manifested from emotions, thus the more passionate a Cleric becomes, the stronger their spells are as well.\n\nHatred. Zeal. Vengeance. This can fuel the Light of a War Cleric. But at the same time, some choose to not call upon the more primal of emotions. Instead, they focus upon anger. Sorrow. The thoughts of what would happen, should they fail.\n\nRegardless of it all, the War Light is still Light in it's stature. One may notice it is 'hard' compared to the 'liquid' state of regular Light. This is due to the Cleric, who wills it into this shape to better combat the forces of darkness.\n\nAll Clerics may be both a 'Priest' Cleric and a 'War' Cleric. There is no need to choose merely one. I am trained in both, using them to their extents to render the Lord's will upon this plane.\n\n\"But,\" I hear you say.\n\"What is the Lord's will?\"\nWell, my friend, it is simple. It is to eradicate 'impurity'. What is impurity? It is taint. Look towards a ghoul or lich. They are different from you and I. They are not 'Descendants' anymore.\n\nThey have given their soul for the ruinous powers. How unjust, how folly their decision. They are wrong, and as such, the Lord of Light sends us to right these wrongs. We are the instruments of the Lord's will. And it is His will that you are protected.\n\nClerics have a duty to purge undead and impurity, wherever they should find it. They do it to keep you safe. Not out of desire for violence, not out of desire to subjugate, but simply to keep us safe, and because the Lord demands.\n\nIt is why the Clerics will always heal you. They will preserve you, return you to your normal form. For injury is Impurity, for it is not who you were. It is wrong, and thus the Light grants us the strength neccesary to save both your life...and soul.\n\nWe are bound by what are known as 'Tenants'. These five rules dictate the lives of a Cleric, and they must follow them closely, lest their soul be torn apart and expelled. Yes, big stakes. \n\nWhat are the Tenants?\nLet's find out.\n\nThe First Tenant\n\n'Shelter and Protect thy\nBrethren'\n\nTranslated, meaning...\nTo protect fellow Clerics in their time of need.\n\nThe Second Tenant\n\n'Cannot Stray from Thy Faith'\n\nTranslated, meaning...\nDo not stray in dedication to the Lord. Be diligent in prayers and thanks to Him for His Gifts to us.\n\nThe Third Tenant\n\n'Shall Guide the Lost'\n\nTranslated, meaning...\nTo guide the Descendants of the Four, and protect them from the forces of Impurity. (I.E Undeath)\n\nThe Fourth Tenant\n\n'Shall not Kill, Harm, Nor Spill the Blood of a Descendant.'\n\nTranslated, meaning...\nClerics cannot harm a Descendant for no reason.\n\nThe Fifth and Final Tenant\n\n'Abuse of Thine Gift and Punishment Shall Fall to You'\n\nTranslated, meaning...\nWe cannot avoid healing a Descendant. We must, for the Lord commands.\n\nThat's alot of rules!\nIt's true, but they guide the path of the Clerics as they go forth to fulfill His Holy Mission.\n\n'But what is that?!'\nWell...let me tell you.\n\nTahariae's mission upon these realms is to preserve Purity, and the Descendants of the Four. The thing standing in his way of that, is Impurity. The Undead, for instance, are one such Impurity. They are to be expunged, unless they serve the Light.\n\nAn interesting part of being a Cleric is their Gift. Now, you may not know much about followers of Aenguls, but oftentimes those who follow one do not experience voidal poisoning, therefore we keep our muscle mass. This is because our aengul blesses us.\n\nI thank you for spending some time reading through this instructional book. Should you have any questions, feel free to ask any nearby Cleric. They'd appreciate any thanks you could give, for our job is oftentimes a thankless one.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-Karyssmov Faroe, 8th of Snow's Maiden, 1637", ""),
        StaticBook("Cleric Trial", "§bEliza", "Ser Duncan L. :\n\nWhy he became a Celric:\nWanted to be able to help those harmed and prevent death-deprived from causing further harm.\n\nWhat drives him:\n\"Celric.\" And the fact that he wishes to protect those he\n\ncares about.\n\nWhat he can tell me that he knows now:\n\"Listen to your peers, and don't be afraid to ask for help.\"\n\nSer Grey K. :\n\nWhy he's a Celric:\n\"To protect his people.\"\n\nWhat drives him:\n\"To protect his people.\"\n\nWhat he can tell me:\n\"Don't give up.\"\n\n Rose C. :\n\nWhy she's a Cleric:\nAbused as a child, forced into marriage at age 50.\n\nWhat drives her:\nDoesnt want people to feel the pain she felt.\n\nAdvice:\n\"Don't fear Tah'.\"\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\n ((Correction:))\n((Celric: x, Cleric: ✓))", ""),
