        StaticBook("Diary Entry 1", "§bBernadette \"Blue\" Valguria", "16th of Malin's welcome§0\n§01962§0\n§0Dear Diary,§0\n§0I have decided to try you out. Uncle said that a diary would be a good way to practive reading and writing. I don't really see much point in it, though. However, I must confess that I am truly in love-\n\nI am not aware of how it happened. What started with an odd encounter ended up with me falling in love almost a year later. I cannot believe it. I feel the butterflies raging in my tummy. What if he doesn't like me back, though? Perhaps I should learn a\n\npoem for him. §0\n§0\n§0I have suffered a wound in my groin. I am not sure how the situation arose, but it hurt, and it still hurts. The woman at the clinic said I have \"Lady issues\". She gave me some bandages, but they're extremely uncomfortable.\n\nI hope it stops before I bleed to death.", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Naevia", "§bBernadette \"Blue\" Forrester", "Dear Naevia,\n\nI'm okay. I miss thee, and I'm sorry. I meant well, I had no idea Augustus would react the way he did. Do nay listen to him, he is using thee. Thee still have the key to my house, feel free to come here with Henry, if thee need time alone.\n\nI love thee, and we shall work this out sometime. Cassian and I have married in Nordengrad, and I have gained control over a fief. I'm safe. We shall see each other soon, I'll try to stay in touch.\n*A heart is drawn here*", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Record of all Foreign§0\n§0Travelers to Kazulrah and known criminals.§0\n§0\n§0Use for checking any visitors to Kazulrah.§0\n§0If Traveler or known criminal is not in this logbook than add them in listing their name, race, gender, nation, desc, and crimes if any.\n\nName: Marzooq§0\n§0Race: Farfolk§0\n§0Gender: Male§0\n§0Nation: Nottingham§0\n§0Desc: wears black cloathing and armor and claims to be a trader, is a friend to the dwarves§0\n§0Crimes: none\n\nName: Li Xin§0\n§0Race: Men§0\n§0Gender: Male§0\n§0Nation: Unknown§0\n§0Desc: Has Black hair, Black Chainmail and trimmed armor, which gold trim and red undercloathing. Was part of a gang that terrorized the town of halsworthy.§0\n§0Crimes: Kidnapping and Theft.\n\nName: Vera de Castro§0\n§0Race: Men§0\n§0Gender: Female§0\n§0Nation: Santegia§0\n§0Desc: Dark brown Hair, brown eyes, wears som revealing clothes, and traveles with a man named Mikhail Duninn§0\n§0Crimes: unknown\n\nName: Mikhail Dunin§0\n§0Race: Men§0\n§0Gender: Male§0\n§0Nation: Santegia§0\n§0Desc: Wears ragged torn armor, black hair, and black eyes, travels with Vera de Castro.§0\n§0Crimes unknown.\n\nName: Taleos.§0\n§0Race: Snow elf (Mali'fenn)§0\n§0Gender: Male§0\n§0Nation: Right by Holm§0\n§0Look: White skin, blue coat. Yellow eyes.§0\n§0Crimes: None, for now.\n\nName: Telos Tathvir§0\n§0Race: Elf§0\n§0Gender: Male§0\n§0Desc: White, blonde hair. Long, obviously. Golden eyes, fine blue clothes. soft yellow trousers and brown boots.§0\n§0Crimes: None, for now.§0\n§0(Being an elf?)\n\nName: Hanz Muller§0\n§0Race: Heartlander§0\n§0Gender: Male\n\nwisovan uialben§0\n§0Business: Shopping§0\n§0crimes:none§0\n§0from:uialben estate\n\nName: Wuffary§0\n§0Race: heartlander§0\n§0Reason: looking to become a runesmither§0\n§0Gender: male\n\nNames: Devon§0\n§0Race: Unknown§0\n§0Reason: Looking to be a runsmither§0\n§0Gender: male\n\nNames: Ser Roland Castelo§0\n§0Race: Human§0\n§0Gender: Male§0\n§0Reason: Just travelling\n\nName: Aldonza Castelo§0\n§0Race: Human§0\n§0Gender: Female§0\n§0Reason: travel\n\nName: Bokib babo§0\n§0Race: human§0\n§0reason: looking around§0\n§0Crimes: Ressiting arrest, attacking 5 dwarves, escaping arrest.§0\n§0FUCKING ARREST THIS CUNT, DO NOT LET HIM ESCAPE\n\nHekkaes Anvilaxe§0\n§0\n§0Reason for travel: visiting old home?§0...buyin§0 goods§0\n§0\n§0Crimes: Slavery?-suggested by mervel§0\n§0\n§0stayed for about 5 minutest, closely watched, then left\n\nName: taurus Silver§0\n§0Race:Farfolk§0\n§0:reason Drinking\n\nName: devon§0\n§0Race: Human§0\n§0Reason: drink§0\n\nName:unkown§0\n§0Reason for travel: unknown, brief talk that left\n\nName:§0\n§0Race:Elf§0\n§0From:dominion§0\n§0found outside, said he was sightseeing, and started mentioning that the dominion was upset for allowing the orcs to stay here. talked to him for a while, never revealed his name, left sudden and seemed in a hurry.\n\nname: murzan gompai§0\n§0visiting to request to become a citizen of kal'ulzrah.\n\nName: Gerome Luderfield§0\n§0\n§0Race: Human§0\n§0\n§0Reason for visit: To look at the shops and wares Kaz'Ulrah has. §0\n§0\n§0Additional Notes: Seemed a very friendly traveller; visit lasted a few minutes\n\nName: Timothy§0\n§0\n§0Race: Heartlander§0\n§0\n§0Reason for visit: Came offering cobblestone, said any price would suffice, he just needed to unload. I (Bo Goldhand) bought 5 stack of 64 for 50 minas.\n\nName: Esther Lester§0\n§0Race: Human§0\n§0Faction: Herself§0\n§0Gender: Female§0\n§0Reason: Selling food\n\nName:§0 Alwin§0\n§0Race: Elf§0\n§0Faction: Dominion§0\n§0Gender: Male§0\n§0Reason: Golems search §0\n§0Notes: Owned a large supply of arms was let in on a warning not to draw any weapons\n\nName: Dewlox§0\n§0Reason of coming: Visiting§0\n§0Race: Human§0\n§0Look: Wearing armor, helmet too, his skin be white, male, black-dark blue hair. Light blue eyes\n\nName: Greagory Dowd§0\n§0Reason: Merchant§0\n§0Race Human §0\n§0Nation:§0 Belvitz\n\nName: Ouros Elthanar§0\n§0Race: Dark Elf§0\n§0Reason: Traveling to find shelter§0\n§0Faction: Ker'nor§0\n§0\n§0(note)§0\n§0\n§0Weapons were removed upon entering the city by Borin Grandaxe reason the Queen was in the city\n\nName: Ser Aldrick Wulff§0\n§0Race: Human§0\n§0Reason: Looking for a smith§0\n§0Faction: Haense\n\nName: Eric Karstaag§0\n§0Race: Hearthlander§0\n§0Gender:Male§0\n§0Nation:nationless§0\n§0Description: Black hair, wears a chainmail and blue eyes\n\nName: Aldrunn Karstaag§0\n§0Race: Hearthlander§0\n§0Gender: Male§0\n§0Nation: nationless§0\n§0Description: Black hair, chain armur, green eyes.\n\nName: Raven Foggs§0\n§0Race: Human§0\n§0Nation: Sutica§0\n§0Reason to visit: Here for the silverveins§0\n§0Description: A blind human woman who seems to be in her 40s§0\n§0Any weapons?: Hatched for self protection (Does not pose a threat)\n\nName: Desimir§0\n§0Race: high elf§0\n§0Nation: none§0\n§0Weapon: sword§0\n§0Reason: Visiting\n\nName: Albondiel Skift§0\n§0Race: Snow Elf§0\n§0Nation: Fenn§0\n§0Weapons: Sword§0\n§0Gender: Male§0\n§0Reason for comnig: A female dwarf told him he can get some good aurum objects in Kaz'Ulrah.\n\nName: Egoi Stormfist§0\n§0Race: Mountain Dwarf§0\n§0Nation: Kaz'Ulrah???§0\n§0Weapons: Feather§0\n§0Description: White hair, green eyes, old.\n\nName: Gwenllech§0\n§0Nation: Renatus§0\n§0Gender: Male", ""),
        StaticBook("Note To Leydon", "§bBilly the Bread Vendor", "Leydon,§0\n§0The following have yet to pay taxes and I would like you to collect them:§0\n§0\n§01. Bodin's Stall§0\n§02. Leydon's Stall§0\n§03. Kenswey's Stall§0\n§04. Carina's Stall§0\n§05. Robin's Tavern§0\n§0NordenGrad Den's§0\n§0#2, and #'s 4-9, and #'s 11-12\n\nThe Following Clan's also need to pay taxes:§0\n§0\n§0Arden§0\n§0Mournstone", ""),
        StaticBook("Note to Norlands", "§bKayla the Outspoken", "This woman has been accused of wytchery by the Imperials. Please do grant her refuge within Nordengrad, for I believe she is innocent. Hear out our pleas for help, in the name of the All-Father.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§9§lEvocress Produce Company Book Record of Drinks§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0By Evark Evocress.§0\n§0\n§0(Main website: §0http://minecraft.tools/en/potion.php)\n\n§nThe Gummy Bear Margarita:§0\n§0\n§0Name:§0\n§0Gummy Bear Margarita§0\n§0Colour Code: &b.§0\n§0\n§0Description:§0\n§0A drink of a thousand colours! What colour will you find?§0\n§0Colour Code: &f,b,d,a§0\n§0\n§0Effect: Invis,Glow,Slow\n\n§nBlack Liquorice Cocktail§0\n§0\n§0Name: Black Liquorice Cocktail.§0\n§0Colour Code: &8.§0\n§0\n§0Description: §0\n§0An Acquired taste, yet still delicious.§0\n§0Colour Code: &f, &7.§0\n§0\n§0Effect:§0\n§0Nausea, Saturation.\n\n§nCotton Candy Delight §0\n§0\n§0Name: Cotton Candy Delight §0\n§0Colour Code: &c§0\n§0\n§0Description: A sweet rum with a fairy top. Some with a Cherry Kiss.§0\n§0Colour Code: &f, &d , &4§0\n§0\n§0Effect: Saturation, Slow Fall, Blindness.\n\n§lChristmas Drink:§0\n§0§nRudolf’s Glowing Elixir§0\n§0\n§0Name: Rudolf’s Glowing Elixir§0\n§0\n§0Description: A drink that holds a tingle in one's eye... body... soul, you glow!§0\n§0Colour Code: &f§0\n§0\n§0Effect: Glow, slow.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Lover's Day.", "§bKili Al-Deen", "they shine brightly in the moon lit gaze,i have traveled near and far yet seen not such beauty as this\nlike a diamond strong and proud yet pretty and pleasing to the eye.their touch is of a gentil flower on a warm sunny day,their voice is soft and\n\ngentil that fills the heart with a warm reassurance and a aw that makes you feel as thuo you have been touched and carryed away by a cloud,you get lost in their gaze as one gets lost in a sunset and your mood rises like the sun in the dawn. you yearn\n\nto be around them with and want to see their smile and happyness you feel as if its your duty to make them smile and joyfull.thy are my warm sunrise and Beautiful jem.to rise before you and make you your favorite dish and bring you roses of compasion is a\n\nhonnor and love that goes to no one but you,My dear love.\n___________________\n\n         By:Kili Al-Deen\n      (ibraheemc2000)\n\nnotes from writer:\nI made this for the enjoyment of the read and the warmth of the heart-Kili Al-Deen.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "This is a log of my life and adventure with my friends and family.§0\n§0Entry #1: Today, I spent the entire day with my lovely wife and I helped her bake her honey bread. She is amazing at it and it tastes so good. Then we went to Cloud Temple and we met the\n\nbronzesmith Quavinir. He challenged me to a music battle. The winner was undecided as the judge decided to run away before they could answer.§0\n§0Edit #2: Today, I met a new elven woman today and we spent time at Curon. We met with another woman there too.\n\nThey were nothing compared to how amazing my wife is. §0\n§0Edit #3: I helped my friend Paisley today after she had been stabbed. §0\n§0Edit #4: The same main that stabbed Paisley, tried to kidnap the kids of my friend Xavis and his wife Wren. Sadly he was hung\n\nfor his crimes.§0\n§0Edit #5: I started my studies of Yeu Rthulu after learning about it from Quavinir. It seems very interesting and I like the way it sounds. Hopefully I can still be Imam Rashan however.§0\n§0Edit #6: Sadly my shrine was not what it was supposed\n\nto be, but what is great is that I got a chance to fix it and I really like the way the new one is coming along. §0\n§0Edit #7: With the help of a few friends, my wife, and my baba, we were able to take down a cultist in the nearby ruins. He had some\n\ninteresting powers, but they were demonic so they were not very nice.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Guess who? :)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "16th of The Sun's Smile, 1675. §0\n§0\n§0This.. madness.. the pain.. the dreams.. a endless cycle that I cannot even begin to come to terms with. §0\n§0\n§0It's eating away at me.. almost corrosive, burning away any good left in me. They say that, faith rivals all\n\nbut I have faith in little. No faith in my friends.. family.. gods. Once again I have been tossed into the gushing torrents of shadows, left to the horrific torment that is my own mind. §0\n§0\n§0Everyday is like walking a living nightmare, my efforts.. sacrifice\n\nhas been done for nothing. The realm is growing cold, beloved faces turn to strangers.. my mind to dust. §0\n§0\n§0What is the use of remaining within a realm that has long turned its back. My true tabard seems to be abandonment.. Mayperhaps it was\n\nfate to be branded. §0\n§0\n§0To be forgotten in time eventually. Remaining nothing but a husk of fractured memories. §0\n§0\n§0This hole.. it once hurt. Like a pressing dagger, being twisted. Applying acid to an open wound, unearable. But now.. I feel nothing.\n\nNo love.. trust.. hope.. faith.. it's all been consumed. Like a sinkhole in my mind. §0\n§0\n§0I can't.. do this. The pain.. I'm slowly losing myself. My sanity. §0\n§0\n§0When that anger takes over me, the whispers taunting me. It's.. like someone else is stood in my\n\nshoes. That.. all I can do is sit and watch as my magic grows. The anger boils. §0\n§0\n§0I just want the blessing of eternal rest. A quick death and to be met with my beloved sons in the soul stream. I've failed. As much as I hate to accept the fact.. it is but\n\ntruth.§0\n§0\n§0[!] Odd stains of Ichor mar the pages. §0\n§0\n§0My family.. what is that word anymore. It feels so foreign.. so lost. §0\n§0\n§0Lost..§0\n§0\n§0I am lost. Forgotten.. alone.\n\nThis sensation, I truly believed it would be one that would grow to a comfort.. the safety of being in my own company. Removing any possibilities of being harmed.. betrayed.. abused.. §0\n§0\n§0But no.§0\n§0\n§0There is no equilibrium.\n\nIt's a chaotic mess that I cannot win. There's no end game, just constant torture... §0\n§0\n§0[!] A new entry is added§0\n§0The 4th of The First Seed, 1685§0\n§0\n§0Torture ends upon the precipice of Hope. Do not falter, Do not stray, for your suffering is Noble,\n\nyet your path is hazed. Take heed, the world is as dark as a person makes it. A fool finds pleasure where the philosopher finds dread. An ending? What joy! For new tales will be told.§0\n§0\n§0Take heed, my Light, keep Determination as your motto, writhe in\n\noptimism, and recount that there is always a way. Survival depends on the limitless imagination bestowed unto us, to forget this is to admit defeat to a life itself. Stay true, stay strong, be Kind.", ""),
        StaticBook("Velian Missive", "§bCanus", "To the peoples of§0\n§0the Kardasi Caliphate§0\n§0\n§0We gift to you one quality horse of Velian blood. This horse is the wind's will made manifest, A gift fit only for a son of golden blood. Care for it as you would a well groomed heir.\n\nAlongside this, we gift to you 1 Jar of Velian Garum. Perfectly aged, perfectly seasoned. Able to make even the most vile of concoctions edible.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Beside these pleasantries, we must relay unfortunate news.\n\nThe war has made a move through hostile territory impossible. Whilst we still maintain a desire to relocate to those distant sun touched lands, it would put too many sons of Velia in harm's way, something we simply can not and will not do at this time.\n\n- Tribunus Canus Regillus", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "hey uhm i didnt really know what to say this to your face but. i think i like you.§0\n§0i dont know what i feel really its so weird .§0\n§0i really think  that you are a good guy. i dont know what im going to do with my boyfriend.§0\n§0i dont want to hurt you both.\n\nits a really hard decision for me to choose.§0\n§0i hope you will give me time to figure thing out.§0\n§0if by then your feelings are gone then i live with it.§0\n§0because it happens sometime.§0\n§0\n§0and i never really had a relation on the internet or whatever you wanna -\n\ncall it before.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Sorry >_< §0\n§0\n§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "whyyyyyy you force mehhhhhhhhhh§0\n§0\n§0meany §0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0imma leave call when im going to give you this.§0\n§0(love you)\n\nsorry for that.. i bet your shy to now arent ya....§0\n§0\n§0im always shy about this kind of stuff..§0\n§0\n§0i always end up silents.§0\n§0\n§0if i spell that right XD§0\n§0\n§0i cant write romantic things because of my bad english\n\nhere i got more stuff that will make you shy.§0\n§0\n§0-sweety§0\n§0-honey§0\n§0-uhmmm something dirty what im noy gonna typ XD§0\n§0- schatje§0\n§0-cutie§0\n§0-my love§0\n\nits much easier to say it in a book.§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Rafias Drazorver§0\n§0\n§0My Journal§0\n§0\n§021st of MW 1700,§0\n§0\n§0I Have Just Bought this Book from CT and it only cost 10 Mina! Cheaper than any other book for sale, Thats for sure.\n\n21st of MW 1700,§0\n§0\n§0I hae gone to The Grand Library of Dragur, It held much information on magic and Golems, Luckily I already have quite a few limbs, though I should get more from a Dwarven Smith... Not only that but I found Information of Magic\n\nand how to start your first connection with Magic, and not only that but Information of Bounty's of Creature's along with Information on many artifact's Ranging from a Lance, A Sacrad Mask, Gem Types, I need to get a Saphire and Diamond soon...\n\nNot only that but how some golems are made. Once I finish the Procedure with a willing subject Im going to Write it down for others, though it will be a long process, probably involoving a Arcane Repeater...\n\n22nd of MW 1700,§0\n§0\n§0I was able to buy a Diamond and Sapphire for cheap from a Ka-Kadarsi? If thats how you say it, It will be helpful in giving a full golem personalitys so that will help!\n\n22nd of MW 1700,§0\n§0\n§0That Reminds me I stole a Garnet, Which will remove toxins from my blood, The Diamond will boost it, and The Sapphire will boost my Peace and Happyness! Though I need Sugilite, Carnelian, Hematite, Jasper, and Topaz. Tiger's Eye\n\nwould be helpful indeed. Peridot, Pearl Soladite would also Help. You Know whats Hilarious the Fact... Hehehe, It was all sold at CT for 25 Mina a Gem... its insane how cheap it all was... Or Atleast Cheap in my opinion.\n\n23rd of MW 1700,§0\n§0\n§0I've done work for the Past Three Days, Im Sleeping in Kadarsi Tonight, I need to Get a home with the Druids or in the Dominion... Hopefully I can make that Dru- [!] The Rest is Scratched out [!] Half Golem, Half Human or Elf.\n\n7th of The GH 1700,§0\n§0\n§0I must have slept a while... No need the man who his helping me make The Golem, has some dwarven friends. §0\n§0I'll Have to meet up with him later. I still Need to get a house...§0\n§0I'll have to talk to one of the men I rode with Yesterday.\n\n8th of The GH 1700,§0\n§0\n§0Well I got more herbs, to crush down, and Gems. I've met a Traveler in Kadarsi, He said he might have a Golem Part or two.\n\n16th of The GH 1700,§0\n§0\n§0Its Been double the time since I last Wrote, I captured and killed a few Suticans with some Kadarsi Friends, The Reason I helped was Because they supplied me with a home! For Free! I also found Wonka Village...\n\n17th of The GH 1700,§0\n§0\n§0[!] A Flattened Red Fern Lies within the Book, You want to take it But your mind is much more Powerful than your body, so you didnt take the Red Fern [!] I found some Weird Fern, I should Study it more, I need to contact the\n\nDruids Soon, as I wish to be one... I'm Currently at The Druidic Order now... The Dominion is being attack by the September Prince's Servant's I can't help without a weapon so im last Defense... I'll try and Find out who I can talk to about becoming a\n\nDruid. [!] A Bit of Blood Stains the Book and a few Drawings are made of the Battlefield [!] Also I got to the top of some weird Green Pillar, Nothing Happened once I reached the top though... [!] A Drawing Of Rafias at the Top is here [!]\n\n18th of The GH 1700,§0\n§0\n§0I Helped a hobbit in the attack, and burned down a few Tendril's with help from A Hobbit (Erick) and Yew, I buned a Animated Being, It seems to be covered in Overgrown Fungus, Huminiod Figure inside. The Figures are September§0\n\nPrince Cultist gone mad and covered in Fungu, I'll take the Robe just in case. A Kadarsi Man burned the Robe, though Cut a pice off for me... Not Only that but Sugilite Is the only stone that works! and Sugilite Barely works, Barely healing a broken nose.\n\n19th of The GH 1700,§0\n§0\n§0((Don't Try the Gemstones out unless Lore is made for it! you will get a warning!)) Im going to sleep for a while again. I dont think I will donate this book to anyone...", ""),
        StaticBook("KRIA InfoHB Ed01", "§bXaemon Al'Ghul", "INTRODUCTION\n\nWelcome, to the Kadarsi Royal Institute of Academics, center to the finest scholars of the Kadarsi Sultanate for both learning of all degrees and scientific research, and the center to all those whose curiosity strives one’s self towards the\n\nname of one as the disciple of knowledge itself, to which is considered a great respect to be of command from, and for, those that value among what sought forth. We welcome all ages, and all levels and methods of learning, for we have vastly progressed\n\nand advanced in our understanding of psychology and its implications of intellectual development. Our sociological ideologies to blend the line (often defined by societal norms carved from bureaucratic and economic perspectives) between the stages of\n\nlearning (both new and higher learning), study and academic advancements has brought us with cutting edge research, knowledge, technology, and understanding advanced for our time.\n\nAcademy Policies and Code of Conduct:\n\n- No weapons of any form, unless accepted for religious purposes and permitted by school administration. Regardless, no *use* of weapons of any kind. \n\n- No menial profanity, mere imbecile idiocy,\n\nor uncivilized behavior of any kind.\n\n- No racist, sexist, or otherwise socially inappropriate comments, attitudes and behavior.. This is a place of inclusive acceptance and support.\n\n- No fighting, harassment, bullying,\n\nor any form of disorderly Conduct! This is a school! Keep it civilized.\n\n- No magic, of any form, at any time! Unless explicitly given permission by the Head Grandmaster and/or a professor\n\n- No defecation or\n\nvandalization academy property\n\n- No Plagiarism or unauthorized duplication or replication of institute textbook content\n\n- Do not commit any crimes stated in this code of conduct or stated in Kadarsi Sultanate Law.\n\nFailure to not commit crimes may result in sultanate military involvement.\n\nAny acts resulting in breaking any of these laws will result in immediate expulsion. No Refunds if package is purchased.  The Institute does not issue suspensions\n\nfor reasons and ideologies taught in the Philosophy course.\n\nCOURSES AND ADMISSION GUIDELINES\n\nAt the K.R.I.A, we seek a new approach from the conventional schooling system. One Price to explore any and as many field(s)\n\nof study taught in its program package. We are built upon the philosophy of true freedom of education and discovery of knowledge, without arbitrary restrictions such as prerequisites, redundant course requirement, or any excessive bureaucratic policies\n\n that restrain on one’s academic progression. Classes are commissioned by its respective professors and time slots are scheduled for respective levels of its courses taught in its respective classrooms at the institute.\n\nApplied to Kadarsi Citizens as per Kadarsi cultural ideologies, all forms of education is free.\n\nTuition Fees for Foreign Students (students appartenir not with the identity as a citizen of the Kadarsi Sultanate whose primary residents is within,\n\n sultanate territory), includes the following purchasable packages:\n\n[1,290 Standard IG 1 Year]\n\n[1,840 High Studies IG 1 Year]\n\nNote: 1,000 Minas Scholarships may be granted by the K.R.I.A or the Kadarsi\n\ngovernment......\n\nStandard Package grants the following programs and services:\n\n- Mathematics & Calculus\n- Astronomy & Astrophysics\n- Classical Physics\n- Alchemy\n\n- Environmental Sciences\n- Geology and Mineralogy\n- Anatomy, Medicine, and Biological Sciences\n- Mechanical Engineering & Technology\n- K.C.S.M.W.T (Kadarsi Combat Strategy, and Military Warfare Tactics)**\n\n- Access to the Common Room\n- Partial Access to the Academy Library\n- Limited Access to the Cutural and Historical Museum\n- Unlimited Access to all Labs\n- Private Tutoring (when time permits)\n- Unlimited Access to\nSwimming Facilities\n\nHigh Studies Package grants the following programs and services:\n\n- All the courses of the Standard Package\n- Philosophy (includes sociology, psychology, and political science) - K.H.A.C (Kadarsi History, Arts and Culture)\n\n- L.L.L.W (Language, Linguistics, Literature and Writing)\n- Architecture & Design\n- Business and Economics\n- Music Studies\n\n- Access to the Common Room\n- Access to the High Studies Common Room\n\n- Full Access to the Academy Library\n- Private Tutoring (when time permits)\n- Unlimited Access to the Cultural and Historical Museum\n- Unlimited Access to all Labs\n- Unlimited Access to Swimming Facilities\n- Advancements options\n\n- Family Extension Package*\n\n* the family extension package, extends can have the high studies package apply to all family relatives… [up to 4 generation]\n\n**special course, permitted only through individual request to the K.R.I.A, and\n\nacceptance by the Kadarsi Sultanate Government\n\nNote: Law Enforcement and Politics are refrained as a valid field of study within the academy due to ethical reasons taught in the course which may  implement elements of these two “subjects” with a\n\nphilosophical or sociological perspective.\n\nSTUDENT APPLICATION\n\nTo Apply, simply walk right into the K.R.I.A building towards the front desk, or contact a professor, student or any Kadarsi citizen. He/she will then refer you to the K.R.I.A\n\n front desk henceforth. \n\nUpon application, and payment of tuition fees, students will receive the following two items:\n\n- A  Kadarsi Royal Institute of Academics Information Handbook, and,\n\n- A Kadarsi Royal Institute of Academics Admission Paper\n\nThe K.R.I.A Information Handbook is the guideline system of the entire academy whose information is within the book whose information about the book about the info is about the book with info about\n\nthe info about the book.*\n\n*[ Note that none may republish, replicate or reprint any of the contents of, and product of the K.R.I.A Information handbook without explicit permission from Academy Administration, which in turn, must follow the procedure\n\nto receive authorization from the Director of Education, aka the Grandmaster of the Institute.  The Information Handbook and ALL content, formats, and systems within the institute, including the content of any textbook is strictly copyright K.R.I.A,\n\nfrom the beginning to the end of time. ]\n\nThe Kadarsi Royal Insititute of Academics Admission Paper is validity of application at the K.R.I.A as a student, granting one access to not just the main entrance of the building,  but the library, labs and every\n\n facility of the K.R.I.A. DO NOT LOSE IT.\n\nDue to the production of this paper having the requirement of importation from facilities not within the Institute, but instead, of another Kadarsi department, replacement of an admission paper will cost 400 Mina\n\nReplacement of the K.R.I.A Information Handbook will cost a book and quill. \n\nINSTITUTE SYSTEM - ACADEMIC DEGREES OF CERTIFICATION\n\nThe K.R.I.A welcomes all ages, degrees of proficiencies and levels of learning. As such, an admission\n\ntest is contradictory and therefore, unnecessary, to this academic institution. And time taken to accomplish each advancement of education is relative to the individual. From being able to earn a degree in a week to a year, only indefinite guidelines of\n\napproximate average periods of time of completion may be presented; a median of 1 - 4 IG years per degree. A standardized test, varying on the field of study, consist of 2 parts: a written assessment (ex: essay, article, book), and a scored evaluation.\n\nThe line between what identifies the intervals of expertise is but the products of institutional enforcements of simplification towards academic credences that seek the marginalization of classes of academic progress. Thus, the amalgamation of these lines\n\nwithin our system, such as of “student and teacher”, “scientists and scholars, and administration and staff”, “learning and inspiration, and research and discovery”, the administration and staff ARE the scientists and scholars whom oversee every\n\naspect of the institute, including its members of the academic community. One can serve as a student of introductory degree on a subject, while operating on an experienced level on another subject. And to that, a flexible, indefinite approximation of time\n\nto which one must dedicate to, to one’s preferred objective of degrees of certification, which includes the following details:\n\n- Rudiments Degree\n- Preliminary Degree\n- Foundation Degree\n- Associate Degree\n- Bachelor Degree\n- Honours Degree\n\n- Masters Degree\n- Doctorate Degree\n\nRudiments Degree:\nOften given to young children, as their first acknowledgement of achievement, the rudiments degree marks the right path to academic success. The foundations of general knowledge, such as basic\n\nreading, writing, and the world around them, as well as an glimpse - an introduction to their chosen field of study. To those first entering the institute, a quick and short diagnostic assessment test is given, or evaluation of intuitive demonstration.\n\nNote, that a Rudiments Degree for the course “General Knowledge\" is also offered, often recommended to individuals of early childhood stage. See front desk for details.\n\nPreliminary Degree:  With sufficient comprehensive knowledge and dedication of one's\n\npursued field of study, marks an in depth proficiency in their path of educational career. Earning a preliminary degree requires the disciple to achieve a passing grade of their first standardized test, respective to the course.\n\nFoundation Degree: Highly proficient in the subject of their studies they have been taught, advanced as a practitioner, a foundation degree solidifies their profession of that field, as a passing grade to a second standardized test, respective to the\n\ncourse, is required.\n\nAssociate Degree: An additional degree slightly above the previous, an Associate degree represents a fastidious expertise and mastery potentially sufficient for fields of studies  to reach maximum capacity of knowledge and\n\ncomprehension. An acceptance of one’s First dissertation is required to achieve this degree.  The course K.C.S.M.W.T, and the subject Pseudoscientific Alchemy caps off at this degree. Achievement of this degree in Courses’ subjects whose content cap off\n\nat said degree, are titled academically equivalent to a Bachelor degree of other courses.\n\nBachelor Degree: Formalizing the position of a first degree expert, often equivalent to the expert grade of other schools. A passing grade of a third\n\nstandardized test is required. A symposium is recommended for the celebration of such an achievement. No, a bachelor party is not a celebration of an expected interrelation of marriage, but rather a celebration of  the achievement of a bachelor degree!\n\nA teacher with this degree and above is respectively considered a “professor”.\n\nHonours Degree: Formalizing the position of a second degree expert, an acceptance of a second dissertation is required for an Honours Degree.\n\n Fields of studies that cap off at this degree are titled academically equivalent to a Bachelor Degree to other courses, and are: Environmental Sciences, Scientific Alchemy, Geology & Mineralogy, and K.H.A.C. \nMasters Degree: Formalizing the position of a\n\nthird degree expert, a passing degree of a fourth standardized test is required for earning a Masters Degree. Fields of studies that cap off at this degree are academically equivalent to the same degree, and are Classical Physics, Business & Economics,\n\nAnatomy, Medicine, & Biological Sciences, Mechanical Engineering & Technology.\n\nDoctorate Degree: Formalizing the position of a final degree expert and the supreme mastery of their field, through the requirement of both a passing degree of a fifth\n\nfifth standardized test and an acceptance of  third dissertation, is the academic recognition of qualification that will always symbolize, exemplify, and indicate the highest frontier of knowledge and comprehension of its respective fields unmentioned yet", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Book of", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Table of contents:§0\n§02. Rogue golems.§0\n§03. Nullers.§0\n§04. Graven.§0\n§05. Bilespitters.§0\n§06. Minotaurs.§0\n§07. Spiegelschleim.§0\n§08. Boars.§0\n§09. Direwolves.§0\n§010. Bogbeasts.§0\n§011. Boggen.\n\nRogue Golems:§0\n§0Big, metal brutes far south. Fight with projectiles that induce levitation. Yield golem scrap, masses of iron, and the rare faded golem core.§0\n§0\n§0Low danger, small groups, high yield. Easiest way to get iron.\n\nNullers:§0\n§0Hard-swarming, desert-dwelling, lethally-poisonous bugs. Extremely profitable yield of chitin and venom glands. Do NOT let them surround you or bite you frequently.§0\n§0\n§0Bring extra gear, high minas profit.\n\nGraven:§0\n§0Possesed undead. Wield neurotoxic arrows. The ghost continues to strike post-mortem.§0\n§0\n§0Bring lots of food. Do not attack on low health. High supply of bones and ectoplasm.§0\n§0\n§0Occasionally, their rare arrows can be stolen.\n\nBilespitters:§0\n§0Smaller than average giant spiders. Not only are they lethaly poisonous, they can spit toxic cobwebs great distance and are agressive in daylight.§0\n§0\n§0Low value yield, difficult to hunt. I reccomend only hunting if you need their bile.\n\nMinotaurs:§0\n§0Hulking bull-men. Able to kill in a single strike and run great distances. Valued for their axes and horns. Their leather is that of a regular cow.§0\n§0\n§0Lethally powerful. Should only be hunted for their horns. Only if necessary.\n\nSpiegelschleim:§0\n§0Able to create clones of their attacker. These clones transfer damage to their attacker. Ultra-dangerous to hunt, but the greatest supply of slime and ethereal ooze to date.§0\n§0\n§0Bring food, secure locations, and lots of time.\n\nBoars:§0\n§0Not particularly dangerous, they yield sturdy hooves, delicious truffles, and lots of pork. Unfortunately, they can climb trees. This makes it difficult to hunt them.\n\nDirewolves:§0\n§0Fast, strong, and hunt in groups. A direwolf is an extremely dangerous hunt. My advice would be to stand on a pillar and stab down at them.§0\n§0\n§0They yield valuable hide and teeth, and a head makes an exceptional trophy.\n\nBogbeasts:§0\n§0Bogbeasts are slow, weak, and difficult to distinguish from a zombie. The difference is that, upon death, bogbeasts rupture in a terrible cloud of poison. They are easy to hunt. Unfortunately, they are worth only a pittance.\n\nBoggen:§0\n§0Horrible flying creatures which are impossible to hit until they land, and they only land after they strike, and their attacks deliver wither poison.§0\n§0\n§0They are also worth almost nothing.", ""),
        StaticBook("Teh all halflins", "§bAnnabeth Shoals", "To ever'one, Oi'm 'ired o livin... An, Oi jus don' wan' ter live anehmore.. So Oi'm sayin goo'bye.. Ferever...Yeh were realleh good teh meh, escpecialley darceh, and Rollo, Bu' 'his isn' for me aneh mer, Oi feel loike a was'e of space.. So, Oi guess 'tis\n\nbe it ever'one. Goo'bye... ~annabe'h shoals", ""),
        StaticBook("A Complaint", "§bLily May", "To: teh sheriff\n(whoever that is)\n\n\n A Formal Complaint\n------------------\n\n\nTo whoever it may concern: I am utterly disappointed in you.\n\nI can barely understand the\n\nselling of my house. I was gone for a long time and did not inform anyone of my leaving.\n\nBUT I am utterly disappointed in the laziness shown by the law. \n\nI came home to a /decomposing/ body on my floors! I looked around, but\n\nthe sheriff was nowhere to be found. A body left for that long could have stained the floors!\n\nFurthermore, I understand if ye don't give me back my house, but I will not have anyone else taking my plants, and I request that I be given another burrow.\n\nAlso: I left the note I found in here too. If you had been there when I was looking for you, then you would have had the note by now. \n\n\nSir, please fulfill your duties like a PROPER halfing. \n\n-May", ""),
        StaticBook("OOC C. Hobbits", "§bJaya Jayamen", "(IMPORTANT: You need to have read the book “OOC PIANO GUIDE” To understand how to read this music. It is located in the Piano Essentials section of the piano shop.)\n\n(The contents of this book is all OOC. In RP it can be used as sheet music for the song. Since the grand piano in RP is a regular piano and not 9 blocks with only 9 notes, in RP the contents of this music sheet would be different then what is written.)\n\nConcerning Hobbits **\n\n2 – 6 – 9 – 6 –\n2 – 6 – 9 – 2 3 \n4 – 6 – 4 – 3 – \n2 – – – – – 4 6\n\n7 – 9 – 8 – 6 –\n4 – – – 3 – 2 3 \n4 – 6 – 4 – 3 – \n2 – – – – – 4 6\n\n7 – 9 – 8 – 6 –\n4 – – – 3 – 2 3\n2 – – – – – – –\n– – – – – – – –", ""),
        StaticBook("Fey's SpellTome1", "§bFeyrith Selgauth", "Wind/Air:\nAerokinesis - manipulate the air, wind, and gas.\nAeroportation - teleport using air/wind currents.\nAir Mimicry - transform into a cloud of gas, fog, or mist.\n--->\n\nAtmokinesis - manipulate the weather by mixing water, ice, fire, earth, air, and lightning/electricity.\nWind Generation - create blasts of wind.\nAir Generation - create or generate blasts of air.\n Aeromancy - Divination via air/wind currents.\n\nPure Wind/Air Manipulation - create and control pure winds.\nDark Wind/Air Manipulation - create and control corrupted winds.\nFlight - have the ability to fly at will.\n\nLevitation - the ability to make anything rise up in the air and move around under your control.\nEarth:\nGeokinesis - control, manipulate, create, generate and reshape or shape earth/rocks/stones\n\nEarth Mimicry - have a body made up of earth or earthen substance\nAtmokinesis - control and manipulate the weather by mixing water, ice, fire, earth, air, and lightning/electricity.\nCrystallokinesis - manipulate minerals and crystals.\n\nFerrokinesis - manipulate metal at will.\nFraxikinesis - manipulate burnt matter.\nGeo-Thermokinesis - manipulate, control, and create lava, magma and volcanoes.\nGolem Creation - make golems out of inanimate materials like rocks, wood, plants, magma, etc.\n\nGranulation - can turn things into sand.\nGeomancy-- Divination via earth and earth-based minerals.\nHalokinesis - control and manipulate salt.\nHyalokinesis - control and manipulate glass.\nKoniokinesis - manipulate and control dust particles.\n\nPlassikinesis - manipulate and control all forms of plastic.\nPsammokinesis - can control and manipulate sand.\nTerrakinesis - control, manipulate and alter/reshape the surrounding terrain and landscape at will.\n\nTerraportation - teleport via the earth and earth-based materials. \nPure Earth Manipulation - Create, manipulate and control pure and good earth minerals.\nBlack Earth Manipulation - Create, manipulate and control corrupted and evil earth minerals.\n\nFire:\nPyrokinesis - create, control and manipulate also generate fire, flame and heat.\nAtmokinesis - control and manipulate the weather by mixing water, ice, fire, earth, air, and lightning/electricity.\nFire Breath - breathe out flames.\n\nFire Mimicry - have a body made up of fire\nGeo-Thermokinesis - manipulate lava, magma and volcanoes.\nHeliokinesis - manipulate and control the sun and sunlight.\nHell-Fire Manipulation - Generate and control flames of hell.\n\nHoly Fire Manipulation - Generate and control flames of Heaven.\nInflammation - burn things.\nMelting - heat molecules to melt things.\nPlasmakinesis - can control plasma.\nPyromancy- Divination via fire.\n\nPyrotechnics - create fireworks.\nSelf-Detonation - explode self and reform.\nThermokinesis - create, control and manipulate heat.\nPyroportation - teleport or move though fire.\n\nWater:\nHydrokinesis - manipulate and control liquid water and mold it into any desired shape or form.\nAquatic Adaptation - adapted to underwater living.\nAquatic Respiration - breathe underwater.\n\nAtmokinesis - control and manipulate the various aspects of the weather by mixing water, ice, fire, earth, air, and lightning/electricity.\nDehydration - absorb water.\nHydroportation - teleport across short or long distances through liquid water.\n\nHydromancy - Divination via water.\nWater Mimicry - turn into liquid water.\nWater Generation - generate water.\nHoly Water Manipulation - create, manipulate and control graceful waters.\n\nDark Water Manipulation - create, manipulate and control evil and dangerous waters.\nVoid/Darkness:\nUmbrakinesis - can manipulate and control darkness or shadows.\nAnimated Shadow - Animate one's shadow.\n\nLight Absorption - block out light in an area.\n\nNight Vision - able to see in the dark.\nSacred Darkness - create holy darkness.\nShadow Camouflage - be unseen in shadows.\nShadow Mimicry - become a shadow.\n\nUmbraportation - teleport via the shadows and darkness.\nElectricity:\nAtmokinesis - control and manipulate the weather by mixing water, ice, fire, earth, air, and lightning/electricity.\n\nQuintessence Force - generates whitish-blue lightning that also contains pure life energy.\nElectrokinesis - control, generate or absorb electric fields and shoot lightning bolts.\nActivation & Deactivation - turn stuff on and off.\n\nPositron Manipulation - control positrons, the antimatter counterpart to electrons.\nElectrical Absorption - absorb electricity.\nElectric Mimicry - transform entire body into a lightning-like being of pure electrical energy.\n\nElectroportation - teleport with lightning/electricity\nDivine Lightning Manipulation - create and control the brightest lightning.\nBlack Lightning Manipulation - create and control the darkest lightning.\n\nEnergy:\nAtmokinesis - control and manipulate the weather by mixing water, ice, fire, earth, air, and lightning/electricity.\nCryokinesis - control ice, snow and other forms of frozen water.\n\nFreeze Breath - freeze things in solid ice.\nFreezing - lower the temperature in kinetic atoms to freezing temperatures.\nFrigokinesis - control snow either as precipitation or already on the ground.\n\nIce Mimicry - have a body made up of ice\nIce Beam - shoot beams of freezing energy.\nIce Generation - generate ice, similar to Water Generation.\nIce Absorption - absorb ice.\nFreezing Fire - Fire that cold as ice.\n\nLight:\nDark Light Manipulation - create the darkest light in existence.\nWhite Light Manipulation - create the purest light in existence.\nPhotokinesis - create and manipulate pure light and photons.\n\nForce-Field Generation - create protective shields of solid photons.\nInvisibility - be unseen.\nLaser Emission - bend light wavelengths to create lasers.\nLight Absorption - absorb the light around you.\n\nLight Generation - emit blinding light or glow in the dark.\nLight Mimicry - take on the traits of light.\nPhotoportation - teleport by using light.\nProjective Invisibility - turn other things invisible.\n\nEvil Banish - banish all spirits of evil and black magic.\nAbsolute Light - The user can create a field of absolute light that blinds the targets either temporarily or permanently and may also dull or even completely negate the other senses.\n\nMany other Magic types exists, and lurk where you do not see. We will soon discover such power and bring it to light, uniting all mages across the land.\n\nMagic is an anchored part of our world. When The Creator pulled all things from nothing and breathed life upon an endless Void, He did so with magic. When he created the first of the mortal beings he did so with magic.ewa\n\n And when the Four Fathers of nations were blessed with peace, strength, honour and eternity, their sons and daughters received those blessings with magic.\n\nAnd so, since the beginning of time, magic has always existed and within every living thing exists the ability to use that magic. Though for some their souls may be less inclined towards the pull of magic,\n\nor their minds be consumed with the work of the simpler things, yet all of this world are born with the ability to connect with magic.\n\nVoid or Arcane based magics tend to be easier to learn, depending upon mental ability and supply of Mana to establish a void connection.\n\nThe Void is a separate plane of existence that exists everywhere, all the while never being perceived. It is simultaneously nothing and everything. Nothing exists in The Void except for endless potential.\n\nVoid magics operate by firstly abandoning mental perception of our world to open one’s mind up to the limitless nothing. Once a connection with the void is made, the individual’s mana is required to wield the Void’s energy for magical purposes.\n\nUsing mana to connect to The Void is a very unnatural process, and the body will show some physical sign of the action that it is undertaking, whether it be a physical tick, twitch or tremor.\n\nStates of Mana:\nPassive\nThis is found everywhere, in everything. Souls produce passive mana, too (every sort of soul, including those of dogs, liches and every other soul-holder). Souls can only directly manipulate passive mana produced by themselves.\n\nIf passive mana is produced by a soul, that soul can convert it into active mana. Thusly, a ‘mana pool’ is how much passive mana a soul has produced.\n\nTypically, a soul never uses its passive mana pool, and the excess passive mana seeps away as aura. Passive mana is not found on one’s physical person, and is instead found around their soul.\n\nWhen passive mana is produced by a soul, it is specific to that soul, and thus when it seeps to become aura or is converted to active mana and burned, it has a specific aura colour. All soul-bearing individuals require passive mana to survive,\n\nand thus converting all of one’s passive mana into active mana results in death (the death occurs due to being unable to do anything, be it breath, think or move). Passive mana is capable of being manipulated or changed,\n\nthough this is an ability that only magics can do. Shade magic, for example, may convert passive mana into Amber, whilst alteration may manipulate passive mana and alter the properties of objects.\n\nActive\nThis is passive mana that has been given a task, and is thus active. All magics use active mana, and active mana is used to fuel all sorts of magical actions. Thanhium produces active mana when converting heat into mana,\n\nexplaining why it is so useful. Active mana may not be reverted to passive mana, and burns away (instead of seeping away, like passive mana does) into aura when used or when in excess.\n\n Active mana may be stored in gems, which prevent it from burning away as quickly, effectively powering enchantments. Active mana gems, however, may run out, though this would take many centuries to occur.\n\nAnti-magic works by tearing active mana away from spells and other forms of magic and disposing it into the void, effectively nullifying the spells. Wards work and abjurations in a similar way,\n\nthough one must understand exactly how the active mana is applied in order to ward a spell. The active mana is then redirected away from the purpose of fueling the spell, thus causing the spell to vanish.\n\nAura\nThe ‘smoke’ of mana. Passive mana slowly degrades to become aura if it is in excess (such as when it is in a soul that produces lots of passive mana, such as a mage’s soul).", ""),
        StaticBook("8 Elements C1", "§bJaya Jayamen", "8 Elements\n\n   ~By Jaya Jayamen\n\n       Chapter One\nThe Adventurers Guild \nI opened my eyes to a scene. I was in a dark room. There was a man in black clothes with a sword up against some girl’s throat in front of him. Across the room from him was myself.\n\nI was clothed in light green robes.  There were also 8 pedestals in the room.  The dark clothed man spoke,\n\n“You, stay back or the girl dies.” To which the other me responded.\n\n“I am not afraid of you. I know your kind, dark magic, you just want the power in the temple!” to which he responded\n\n“Stay back! Or the girl dies.” To which the other me responded,\n\n“You won’t be able to harm her, you may have been trained in the dark, but I have been trained in the light!” At this the other me’s body started shining incredibly bright, blinding me from then scene. I then woke up with a start.\n\nPanting, I tried to calm myself down from the dream. I looked out of my window. It was still dark out. Sighing, I laid back down in my bed. What a dream… I thought. Then a thought clicked in my mind, today was the day I enter the Light adventurers guild.\n\nI lived in Revan town. A place that is a sub-city in the Light tribe’s land. The land was half city half forests. I had been feeling a bit uneasy about joining the guild, there was a test that no one was allowed to talk about.\n\nWell at least not about what is in the test. I wonder if it would be hard, what type of test would it be? Slowly but surely, I drifted back into sleep.\n\nWhen I woke up the next morning things started alright, I woke up to the smell of bacon. I slowly sat up from my bed. I got up and god dressed, equipped my sword, and headed into the kitchen.\n\n“Good morning Lethan.” Said my mother, placing a plate full of food on the table.\n\n“morning mom.” I replied, taking a seat. I began to dig into the meal.\n\n“Made you a big breakfast, I’m proud you are going to the adventurers guild.” My mom said to me as I ate. “It’s not easy being a part of the guild, from what I’ve heard from friends at least.” I stopped eating a moment swallowing some food and said,\n\n“I have been looking forward to it. I have been anxious about it for the last week.”\n\n“I’m sure you will do well.” Replied my mom. “Just do your best and I’m sure things will go well.”  To which I nodded finishing up my food.\n\nWhen I finished my food, I got up and got my backpack, in it I had a map of the town, a skin with water, some other things like rope, my invitation letter to the Light Adventurers Guild, and finally an old music box about half a foot large.\n\nThe music box was something I had found while I played in the woods years ago. I could wind the key, but it never played after I wound it. I figured it was jammed. I took it with me because this was the last time I would be home for a while.\n\nAdventurers guild members live at the guild.\n\nI turned to my mom and nodded my head. “I guess it’s time to go.” I said, “I love you mom, I’ll do my best.” To which my mom embraced me in a hug saying,\n\n“Be safe and come visit often.” Nodding at her after the hug, I then headed out the door to the Light Adventurer’s Guild.\n\nThe Light Adventurers Guild was located at a large building on the edge of a huge forest at the side of town.\n\nI walked up to the large building very nervous from the sight of the imposing building. I took a moment to take in the sight and then walked into the large doorway of the building.\n\nAs I walked down the large hallway I could hear odd noises coming from some of the rooms, what sounded like a lecture from others, and other types of noises from the rest of the rooms.\n\nMy invitation had said to go to the office at the end of the hall from the entrance to the guild. I continued walking down the hall until I got to a doorway. Cautiously I knocked on the door. A voice said,\n\n“Come in!” I turned the handle and went inside. As I Walked in the room I noticed myself feeling a sense of calm and peace.\n\nIn the room was a desk, two chairs in front of it and one larger chair behind it, there was also two large bookshelves at the back of the room. In the large chair behind the desk sat a young woman with blond hair.\n\n“You must be new, may I see your invitation please?” I nodded and walked to the desk taking off my backpack. I undid the latch on my bag rummaged inside it taking out a slightly crumpled invitation. I then handed it to the lady.\n\nThe young woman took the invitation and studied it thoroughly. After a few minutes she said, “everything checks out. Welcome to the guild Lethan.”\n\n“Thank you maim. “ I replied, to which she laughed lightly.\n\n“please, call me Jenna.” She said. She opened a drawer in the desk and pulled out a key, a piece of paper, a map, and a ring.  She placed these items one by one on the desk.\n\n“the key is to your room, the map here will guild you to your classes and your way around the guild, this paper has all of your classes listed on it, finally this ring symbolizes that you are a member of the Light Adventurers Guild.\n\nYou will have three roommates. Kevan, Jess, and Closen. Kevan is a student from the Fire Adventurers Guild, Jess is a student from the nature guild, and Closen is a Member of our guild, the Light Adventurers guild.”\n\nI simply nodded taking in all the information. Jenna then said, “you have about an hour to get settled in, then you will be taking your first class, Free for all.”\n\nI raised a brow slightly at this, “I didn’t realize I would be taking a class so soon.” I said. “What kind of class is free for all?” to which Jenna smiled a bit and said.\n\n“It is a class where students show what they can do. The objective is to reach the flag in the middle of the training ground. You cannot kill or maim anyone, only light injuries are permitted. The rest will be explained at the start of the class.”\n\nI nodded with a slight gulp. Then I remembered something. “what about the test? I thought there was one I needed to take before joining.”\n\nThe free for all serves at a test in itself. “said Jenna. “I and others will be observing your skill and the other students’ skills as it goes on. As for passing or failing the test, if your abilities are not good enough,\n\nyou will be put in learning classes helping you get to a basic level. If you do well, you will take normal classes, if you exceed expectations, you will be put in advanced classes. Understand?”\n\n“yes.” I said, now much more nervous than when I entered. \n\n“better hurry to your room, and don’t be late for the class!” I nodded and exited the room.\n\nEnd of Chapter\n\nThank you for reading the Jayamen family’s books! If you have any feedback or enjoyed reading, please let me, Jaya Jayamen (( Sofetios )), know. Peoples responses help me write more books! Thanks again! ~Jaya Jayamen", ""),
