        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Begginer's Notes on Magic. Kale Donager.§0\n§0\n§0The Void:===========§0\n§0\n§0The Void is the source of all arcane magic, it is a realm closely connected to our own. Anything that happens in our own physical world can also affect the Void. This is a concept known\n\n\"Voidal Tethering.\" It it thought that with how closely connected our physical world is to the Void that our world was created in the Void and then brought into existence. The Void itself is a realm of infinite potential, where everything exists in\n\nconcept alone, not in any actual physical form. A Mage however can create physial things within the Void using their willpower and imagination. In order to do this, a mage must first connect to the Void. This process sounds easy in concept but\n\nbecomes incredibly dfficult when put to practice. The biggest obstacle when attempting to connect to the Void is that in order to do so, one must clear their mind to reah the peace and serenity that is required to connect to the Void. This clarity is\n\noften achieved through meditation and here is where the tricky part of connecting to the Void becomes apparent. One would think that clearing their mind would be as simple as to not think of anything at all, but even the slighest sound, a leaf crunching,\n\nthe leaves of a tree whispering, the slighest distraction can cause a mage's mind to instictively focus on the sound and lose focus on connecting to the Void. With practice and time a mage's technique for connecting to the Void can eventually become\n\nsecond nature, so that they can connect to the Void almost without thinking about it. A mage must use something called \"Mana\" in order to connect to the Void, which brings us to our next section.\n\n\n§0Mana:===============§0\n§0\n§0Mana is an invisible energy that every living creature in our physical world possess and it permeates the entirety of the Void. Every Descendant has something known as a scar on their soul\n\nand it is from this scar that mages can connect to the Void. A mage must use their mana to create a sort of link or bridge between themselves and the Void. Once they have done this, they can begin to pull their creations from the Void and into our\n\nphysical realm. Commonly, anything that is taken from the Void is known as a spell and the process of taking things from the Void is known as casting a spell. However, not all spells created in the Void are equal and larger or longer spells will require\n\nmore mana to summon and sustain. When a mage casts a spell and brings it into our physical world, something known as a \"Mana Anchor\" is created. Mana Anchors are some of the mana a mage uses to sustain their spell in the physical world.\n\nSometimes a Mana Anchor can also take on physical affects such as distorting the space around them. If a Mana Anchor is destroyed then the spell ends and whatever the mage pulled from Void will return to the Void. §0\n§0Next it is important to note that a mage\n\ncan lose concentration while casting a spell, either by being distracted, becooming exhausted or simply choosing to end their connection. When this happens, the Mana Anchor disapears and the spell returns to the Void, though in some cases their effects\n\nmay remain. A mage can only cast spells for so long until they must stop however, this is determined y the size of something known as a \"Mana Pool.\" a Mana Pool is how much mana any creature currently has within itself\n\nand the size of a mana pool is dictated by two very important aspects: The first being the skill level of the caster and the skill level of what they are casting. As a caster grows in skill and becomes more porficient with their art, they will learn to\n\nuse their mana more efficiently and casting spells will become easier for them, effectively growing the size of their mana pool. When spells are cast, a mage emenates a part of their mana called \"Aura.\" Aura is a bit like a fire giving off smoke,\n\nthe more wood that is added to the fire, the more smoke the fire puts out. Something similar happens with Aura in that if a mage uses more mana, their Aura flares out more. The colour of an Aura can often betray the personality of a mage.\n\nThis is a quick guide to understanding Aura.§0\n§0Blue: Calculating and Logical.§0\n§0Purple: Mysteriousness.§0\n§0White: Benevolence or innocence.§0\n§0Brown: Nurturing and caring.§0\n§0Red: Dominance and power.\n\nGreen: Harmony and Balance.§0\n§0Black: Chaos and malevolence.§0\n§0\n§0Lastly, it is important to note that Mana is directly linked to a person's life force and as such, using mana can be exhausting.\n\nUsing too much mana can cause a mage to become physically fatigued and even pass out, obviuously preventing them from further casting their spells. In rare cases, mages have died from over exhausting themselves while casting.\n\n\n§0Aeromancy:==========§0\n§0\n§0Lastly is the topic of Aeromancy and recomended way to approach learning Air Evocation. Air and wind are considered to be vital elements of life as all cratures brath air around them. With\n\nair evocation we learn to create Wind and control the wind that we summon. Air and wind is often though to be unpredicatable despite being one of the most well researched evocation arts, this will help with understanding air magic as there are many\n\nmaterials on the topic to study from. Though it is not enough to just read about the element of wind, one must learn about wind by feeling it and studying it. Some reccomended areas to learn and study about wind are the following. Anywhere that has a high\n\naltitude or open expanse such as plains. While studying the wind, try tossing something light into the air, such as a feather and watch how the air cradles it down toards the earth again.\n\nWhen First learning how to cast air magic, it is important to remember to start small, even light gusts of wind can be exhausting for a begginer and attmpting to create large amounts of wind while just begining can be dangerous to the caster.\n\nOnce connected to the Void, the trainee mage should only focus on what they have seen in nature in order to keep their powers under control and not expend more mana than what they have. Laslty, it is important to note what kinds of things\n\nAeromancers CANNOT do. Here is a list:§0\n§0\n§0Aeromancers cannot fly, it is simply too difficult to maintain concentration while moving at high speeds.§0\n§0\n§0Aeromancers cannot control wind, only create wind.\n\nAeromancers cannot control the weather, it is simply to grand of a feat for anyone to acomplish.§0\n\n\n§0Kale's Personal Notes§0\n§0===================§0\n§0\n§0I sat myself outside the Santegian Capital amid the grassy fields. I can see the trees off in the distance, swaying to and fro, the crops that the city grows are some distance away as well.\n\nA gentle gust rolls through, the breeze feels cool and refreshing as it hits my face. I settle down as I try to relax and observe the details of my surroundings. The wind feels welcoming as if to invite me back to the outside after secluding myself in the\n\nlibrary for so long. It helps to relax me as I slow my breathing, the leaves catch the breeze passing by as the trees begin to dance rythmically to a song I can't hear. I try to match my breathing to sound of the trees rustling in hopes of gaining a\n\nbetter understand of the feeling of air. I wait, and I watch. Trees, sway, the grass rolls, I feel calm, serene. It takes me a moment to realize that this is the first time in a while, even before begining my studies, that my mind hasn't been racing with\n\nsome thought or another. I look around once more. There's nothing between me and anything else I can see. I don't think I fully understand yet everything about wind and the air, but I feel like I have a start. A liberating feeling, free and persistant.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Hamza de Savin y Kharadeen's Journal §0\n§0\n\nDay 1: I Just met my twin  sister! With Padre, She is so kind and a little mean at tims§0\n§0\n§0Day 2: I'm So lucky to have sis and Padre, I love them so dearly§0\n§0\n§0Day 3: I wish some day i meet the Kig And Quen Of sanegia\n\nDay 4: I just went somewhere with Padre and It was talking about a Empie?§0\n§0\n§0Day 5: This is the best day ever! I just tasted A \"Bilys pie\" And it was so good!§0\n§0\n§0Day 6: I Met my aunt, and she was so nice! And I even met my new cousin!", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Santegia", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0      §0\n§0      THE COMPLETE§0\n§0        FINDINGS OF§0\n§0   NONA THE SCHOLAR§0\n§0\n§0              IV\n\nSun's Smile, 6th§0\n§01664§0\n§0\n§0Nothing of interest has happened up until today. Nothing beyond some minor bandit encounter's and the occasionally friendly exchange that is. Along my caravan runs I have yet to find a SINGLE PROPHECY FRAGMANT. It\n\nis rather infuriating. Oh, there was something interesting that occured, though I was not there for it. A while back, there was a meeting held in Marna called by the King to discuss the formation of a new Empire. Important Noble's from all over were in\n\nattendance including important people of Pembrokeshire. I was invited to join as a member of the Merchant's Guild via bird, but I was on the other side of Atlas at the time on another trade route and could not be there. On to today's encounter. While in\n\nthe Elven Dominion for trade, there was a cry for help. Someone yelling that there was a Lich at the gates of the city. It had managed to cross the boundry line used to keep out the undead. Of course, I instantly ran to assist. I was not of much help in\n\nthe actual fight, but a Spriggin managed to fight it off. As it was turning to leave, a man attempted to throw a powder upon it after splashing the power with water. The lich was knocked aside but a second undead beast that had come up to assist and no\n\nreaction took place. Anyways, the fight was over and the undead left. I pulled aside the man who had thrown the powder and brought him to the tavern to speak. He told me that powder was his owne creation. It reacted to large amounts of heat such as lava\n\nor lightning. When the reaction occured it caused it almost instantly melted through highly durable metals and could even cause small fire's if close to something flammable. The man's name was Charles Napier. I hope we meet again to continue discussing\n\nthis strange powder. Something I've forgotten to mention is that an Academy has been opened up in Holm. My next trip will be to visit this academy in hopes of applying. Charles Napier attends this Academy and perhaps we can meet again there.\n\nThe Deep Cold, 5th§0\n§01664§0\n§0\n§0I've been accepted as a Scholar within Pembrokeshire. As soon as the Scholar's Tower is complete, I will be provided an office where I can work more on my researches. I'm also officially a student\n\nwithin the Academy earning a major in Scientific Studies and a minor in journalism. This is all very exciting! I've also begun sorting my discoveries into their own novels, rather than putting it in these Journals that are simply an account of my personal\n\nlife. The first book I publish will be one over the Flora and Fauna I've found along my travels. Truly quite interesting stuff and plenty to record on the matter. I hope to enlist the help of a mage who can help record the magical uses and properties.\n\nThe First Seed, 7th §0\n§01665§0\n§0\n§0I return to Pembrokeshire to find trouble. Alijol is dead. I barely new her, but she was a kind soul and deserved a long life. I've come back to find Thanatos stricken by grief. He was planning on proposing to her soon\n\nas well. They've been together for a while after all and it is clear he loved her dearly. He's tried to poison himself. I fear he might try again. I've convinced him to travel with me. So I can show him the beauty the world has to offer. Perhaps by the\n\ntime we return, Alkheim will be home from the mission he's been sent on. These tragedies cause me to miss him very dearly.\n\nThe First Seed, 12th§0\n§01665§0\n§0\n§0We've returned to Pembrokeshire. Thanatos and I visited many places. Marna, Belvitz, Holm and the Academy. He says I remind him of Alijol. I do not know how to respond to this. His grief is unmeasurable.\n\nBut I think he found comfort in our travel's all the same. Perhaps I'll take him to the Wonkawoods next. It's rather soothing in there. He's requested to read my journal's. I agree. He's reading the first one now as I make this entry.\n\n*The following words are written in a messy scrawl* §0\n§0\n§0i had wine and it good wine and tasty driinks thananantoss colleccts ddrinks s an i win contest in drr ink contest", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0\n§0            NONA§0\n§0       THE SCHOLAR§0\n\nMalin's Welcome, 9th§0\n§01666§0\n§0===================§0\n§0\n§0I've yet to discover more on the art of \"moon-gazing\". Tepah knowns nothing apparently. Where the hell did that first kharajyr get to anyways? I've decided to return to the Dominion once again in\n\nhopes of finding a mage that knows more of the art. If not, perhaps I can find someone who knows more of the undead. Alkheim's recent endeavor's in searching for crypts has aroused my curiosity in how they come about and what forms of undead\n\nactually exist. Besides, I've yet to have a rude encounter in the Dominion or with any descendent of Malin for that matter though Horen folk may dislike them.§0\n§0\n§0            -=-§0\n§0\n§0Well, I've encountered something interesting\n\non the way to the Dominion. There seems to be quite the gathering outside of an orc fort along the road. I think I may have just missed a battle. There's several Elf's here too, but I'm not sure that now is the best time to approach them and ask my\n\nquestions. I'm not sure whether to stay here for a little bit or just continue on to the Dominion. Perhaps I'll see if anything interesting comes to pass and if not, I'll simply be on my way.§0\n§0\n§0            -=-§0\n§0I've met several Dwarf folk in my life, but\n\nnone quite as loud as THIS guy! I don't even know his name. What kind of throat and lungs does he have that let's him scream like that? Should I investiagte it? Perhaps I'll bring it up during class at the Academy.§0\n§0\n§0            -=-§0\n§0Well this is an\n\neventful day. There's a bunch of elf's that look as if they plan to raid the orc's. I think I'll stick around a little longer..... off to the side of course.\n\nMalin's Welcome, 10th§0\n§01666§0\n§0===================§0\n§0\n§0Thing's are a bit hectic outside of the Dominion. Perhaps I should come back later. It seems like the entire population of Krugmar is here! I can't even get in the gates. I don't think it's\n\nworth sticking around. Don't want to get caught up in some big fight and lose my head. Guess I'll have to pay Dominion a visit at a later date. For now I suppose I'll continue my Caravan runs. Gotta make the minas someway, you know?", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0Is í seo an iris an-sean, a thabharfaidh teanga duit sean-tíre Adunach duit, Nuair a bheidh tú críochnaithe beidh tú ina mháistir. §0\n§0Ní féidir go bhféadfadh an teanga seo a labhairt, ach is ealaíontóir den chineál Adunian é trully. §0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "D I A R Y§0\n§0\n§0Belonging To:§0\n§0Illiaana Acrenox\n\nDear Diary,§0\n§0Yes I know I am over 30 years old and have a diary. But I guess things just happen. A old friend of mine Murielle Aureon hates me. She thinks I am a traitor to where I live, Halsworthy. Although I just want to help out by getting intel but...§0\n\nthats over and I am leaving them now. I wrote a letter telling her, I hope she believes me, I mean my daughter does say I am pretty persuasive.§0\n§0\n§0-Illiaana Acrenox", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Vladan's Diary§0\n§015th of The Amber Cold, 1661.§0\n§0\n§0Today, I have been invited to the position of Marshall to the Duke of Haense. I shudder at the responsibility, but have accepted readily.\n\n14th of the Deep Cold,§0\n§01661.§0\n§0\n§0I have recruited a new man today by the name of Bigge. He is a scrappy and spry young lad; I see promise in him. The Pale fucker made me pay taxes today. Basarab must be taxed himself.\n\n14th of Snow's Maiden§0\n§01662§0\n§0\n§0Today, Trial was held in court. The accused was a goblin who got into a fight with a guard. There were many hijinks, and many poor translations from blah into commonspeak.\n\n13th of the Grand Harvest, 1663.§0\n§0\n§0I've recently acquired a hammer that shoots lightning upon contact with an opponent.. the caravans bring untold treasures to Belvitz. Barnabas Basarab fled, under accusations of being a Striga. What lunacy.\n\n6th of The Grand Harvest, 1667.§0\n§0\n§0Today, I go to war with the Reiver. He shall be fierce, and shall endure a great deal of combat, but I am sure we shall prevail.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Small Note", "§bMaster Keeper Sighard \"The Blind\" Af Markev", "My dearest love of my life, my sunshine and star, my blood in my form.§0\n§0\n§0I eternally love you Millie, so I have given you some things to show I care, I know it i not much, but it is all I can muster for now, your eternal beauty is fantatical, and I hope\n\nand wish you want to be with me in a loving relationship.- Your Lover Sighard.", ""),
        StaticBook("Behind FP-02 #2", "§bAntanios Rutledge", "He continued to barrage me, before pulling me out by my hair. Bloodied, I managed to see the body of Miss Hatheway, seemingly devoid of her fair life. I only hope she rests well.\n\nI was detained in the cells, for many days.\n\nThey teased about pinning the murder on me as an \"Unfortunate death caused by Antanios's instability\".\n\nThey chortled about how they could just execute me, and no one would think twice.\n\nAnd then they left me in the cells, and smeared my name.\n\nIt wasn't until many days later that Sheriff Adler called me up to his office. His visage was demented, more insane than I had been. Eerily, he leaned forward, his lips curling into a devious grin. \n\nHe chuckled, and chills ran down my spine.\n\nThen, after what seemed to be a long and unnerving silence, Adler spoke.\n\n“Join the Indigo Gang and serve me, or I will kill you and pass Rivaini around the gang.”\nAnd that was all, he let me out of the compound.\n\nI hid Rivaini, and I ran. I ran until I could not run anymore. It was dark, it was storming. My clothes were soaked and my body wanted to drop. I came upon the Kadarsi Caliphate, and they took me in. A man cared for me, calling me 'Akhi'.\n\nAkhi meant 'brother'. I stayed in the Kadarsi, and I finally understood why some people thought I was a farfolk. It was like a home I never knew of. The Kadarsi people were caring, and I remained until 1681.\n\nThen I returned Home Sweet Adria.\n\nI joined the Sarkozic Levy, and then I proposed to Rivaini. \n\nWhen I heard that Adler's body was not found amongst the corpses from the unsuccessful coup, deep down I knew he was not dead.\n\nNo one believed me.\n\nThen he came back. After a disturbing talk, Adler considered me as a traitor. I admit, I should have done something than run away. So I offered some help, and I told him to come back another day.\n\nI birded a few friends, arranging help.\n\nIt was too late. Adler was executed by the Empire the next saint's day. I wish he hadn't died so soon, that I could attempt to bring him back into the sanity and the loyality I knew he used to be. \n\nAdler used to be a good man, a caring man.\n\nHe was someone that protected Adria, and for that I respected him. I am thankful that he helped me.\n\nI do not regret my past, because I cannot change it.\n\nI can only use it to change my future.\n\nWitnesses:\n§S\nSer Seth Renault\nAmphion Enthelor\nEve\nEdwar 'Fang'\nRivaini\nAxel Swale & Erin Wood Adler & Ser Atticus\nNicholas Bolivar\nDemetria Hathway\nUnknown Kha\nUnknown Halfing\nZhag'Yar & Azag'Yar\n\nAs stated, I did serve my time for this attempted murder.\n\n\n\n\n\nWritten on the 14th of the Sun's Smile, 1692.\n(12/02/2018)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Herb Log:§0\n§0Claudia Zey§0\n§0Herba\n\nStall 10:§0\n§0(Imagine_May) (Three Horses) (SpottBrown, PaintBrown, Brown)§0\n§0\n§01/03/19:§0\n§0*Log Empty*§0\n§0\n§01/04/19:§0\n§0(Valion Guard) (Two Horses) (Chestnut, Brown)\n\nStall 2:§0\n§0(Valion Guard) (One)§0\n§0(Brown)§0\n§0Stall 5:§0\n§0(Herley Dudley) (One)§0\n§0(Red)§0\n§0Stall 9:§0\n§0(Claudia Zey) (Three)§0\n§0(Brown, Mule, Donkey)§0\n§0Stall 10:§0\n§0(Claudia Zey) (Three)§0\n§0(White,SpotB,Brown)\n\n1/05/19:§0", ""),
        StaticBook("The Travels I", "§bOrfea Iridium", "The Travels\n    Of a Wood Elf\n\n           By\n     Orfea Iridium\n\n       Volume I\n\nAll events are true to the best of my ability to recount them. All names have been less unchanged unless it is stated otherwise.\n\n5th of Deepcold, 1665\nHerein lie a log of the adventures of I, Orfea Iridium, a wood elf seeking her fortune. I have started this log on my way from the Dominion back to Cloud temple, hoping there to receive some tips on how to become a merchant. To that\n\nend, I posted a note on the door of The Caravan Company, in a village very shortly south of Cloud Temple, on the advice of a kindly man named Roland, whom I met on my last excursion to the Temple. A llama, I am told, is essential to the trade of a\n\ncaravaneer, as one of the few creatures that can carry the volatile substances in that are in such demand all over Atlas.\n\n7th of Deepcold, 1665\nI agin met Roland on my arrival in Cloud Temple. The man in blue, who affectionately refered to me as a \"Shrub\n\nElf,\" offered to travel with another stranger and I, to Belvitz, where Roland says I might have better luck, not yet receiving notice from The Caravan Company.\n“Keep yer hood up in Berlitz” was his advice to me, when we set off, which I took to mean that\n\nI was to keep my wits about me. This, I am sorry to say, I failed to do.\n             *\nThe road, at night. Nothing but the sound of our own footsteps disturbed the cool air. A figure sprinted past, all in black. A glint of recognition came across\n\nRoland’s face and he gave chase. The other traveller and I followed, confused. I, bow in hand, watched as the figure escaped, Roland cursing. \n\"Who was that?\" I asked.\n\"A bandit. A craven bandit\"\nI said nothing as we moved on, but I looked at my full\n\nquiver, and cursed my negligence\n\n8th of Deepcold, 1665\nThe rest of the journey passed uneventfully. We were joined by a monk and a warrior, the latter of which Roland seemed to some acquaintance to. The former, though clearly an ascetic, had a love\n\nof carrots, and at one point slowed our entire troupe down with his snacking.\n             *\nWe arrived in Belvitz and I bade Roland farewell. After searching around the town, and quizzing several of its denizens, I was no closer to finding a llama than\n\nwhen I started. Belvitz, just south-east of the Temple, lay at an important crossroad, right near the legendary Library of Dragur, which I dedicated some time to exploring before I dejectedly began my long journey back to Cloud Temple\n\n9th of Deepcold, 1665\nSuccess! I dropped into the Caravan Company, on my way back to the temple. They have agreed to take me on as a trainee caravan driver. In a few days, my training begins.\n             *\nI was approached by a mysterious pair of fellow\n\nelves, who made an interesting proposition. They have a camp nearby, I was told. I’ll give no details of our discussion, and refer to them only as F and M, for they seemed to be operating in secret, but in later volumes of this work perhaps I shall\n\ndocument further encounters with this pair.\n\n11th of Deepcold, 1665\nWhat an eventful day! With nothing to do until the commencement of my training at the Caravan Company, I returned to the Dominion. Here, I found my home city of Caras Eldar in chaos. A\n\ncrowd of perhaps a dozen or so elves, including guards and stewards, were running up and down the length of the city. Eventually, at the city gates, they accosted a woman, who for the sake of protecting her against further accusation, I'll refer to as 'M'\n\nShe was accused of consorting with a banished elf, who had been sighted inside the city. This elf, Darius, was seen talking to her, but then stabbed her and fled. A group was organised to pursue him to a nearby settlement, though M remained under\n\nsuspicion. Afterwards, I was approached by a druid, Artimec Caerme’onn, who offered to formally induct me into Aspectism - the native faith of the woodelves and a ceremony I, like many elves of my generation - had yet to participate in. I gladly accepted,\n\nand paused only to jot down these words.\n              *\nThe events of tonight will stay with me for the rest of my life. The ceremony was conducted under the stars, in front of a shrine to the Green Lady and the Horned Man. I was inducted alongside one\n\nAnhel Kyrawn, a fellow elf. Together, in front of a small crowd on onlookers, we swore oaths and shed blood over holy fire. It is hard for a simple traveller like myself to put in words the reverence I felt in that moment, but suffice is to say that I\n\nhave never felt so connected to my heritage. I was invited afterwards to spend the night in the druids’ grove, a surprisingly large and incredibly beautiful section of the city, which I took no time to appreciate in my desire for sleep.\n\n14th of Deepcold, 1665\nBut to wake in the grove of Caras Eldar every morning, and I would be happy everafter. Trickling water and vines and soft grass and the musty scent of nature fills the place. To remain in that meditative silence, in harmony with\n\nnature, would be dreamlike. Alas, I cannot stay. Even if my feet did not itch for the road, only druids can stay in the grove in permanent residence. Still, I intend to spend several more days in contemplation before I return to the Caravan Company.\n\n1st of Snowmaiden '66\nA new year, a new life. I fear my training with the Caravan Company shall never begin. The village in which it exists, as yet unnamed, is undergoing vast construction projects, and I don’t think they have time to talke on a new\n\napprentice, as much as they would like to. They’re voting on a name for the village, and I cast a vote for 'Bellamoor,' though at the time 'New Brightstone' was leading.\n\n4th of Snowmaiden '66\nI travelled yet again to the Caravan Company, and was met\n\nby naught but a single man, one Louis Consalvo Castrov. He was, according to him, the banished King of Santegia. He had a target on his back, he told me, because he was working to overthrow what he described as a \"Horen puppet to Renatus.\" A fascinating\n\ngentleman, but alas I am no closer to my new life as a Caravaneer. I intend to spend the night in the local inn.\n\n5th of Snowmaiden '66\nDisaster! Threat of war has lead the Caravan Company to uproot. They are talking now of deconstructing the\n\nentire city and reconstructing it inside the Dominion. I have all but given up hope on becoming a successful merchant, and of travelling the world.\n\n6th of Snowmaiden '66\nI met my friend Nervzza, and exchanged some news. Later, an Uruk named\n\nAzgorn kicked up a fuss outside the city gates. I sat and chatted with him awhile, though he mostly could only speak Orc. When the guards deigned to show their faces, they refused to let my new friend in, on account of his race. I of course ranted and\n\nyelled until they relented. How low my beloved Dominion has sunk.\n\n8th of Snowmaiden '66\nAn eventful day indeed! I purchased a home in Caras Eldar for 200M, from a steward named Leonhardt. A beautiful little apartment overlooking the\n\nmarket. Darius the Scoundrel was sighted again, though I still do not know the full story of who he is or why he was banished. He was in the square, yelling, before being escorted out by a man claiming to be his lawyer. He was held at the gate for some\n\ntime, despite his furious protestations, but was eventually let got. Someone from the crowd whispered that he or one of his companions was a prince from a neighbouring realm, and had had his assets inside unjustly seized. I overheard the phrase \"Covert\n\nOperation Wolfhund\" from Darius, which meant nothing to me.\nAfterwards, I was approached by Kardryn Oranor, a lawyer-in-training at Roswell College. He had seen me taking notes and was himself author of a series of political essays - the Elvenesse Papers.\n\nHe asked me about my book and then offered me a job, reporting on the day-to-day affairs of the Dominion. He said to forward him a copy of this volume once I have published it, and we could talk some more.\n\n22 Snowmaiden, 1666\nI met a woman at the gates of Caras Eldar. Although I haven’t the authority to open the gates, I allowed her access to the city by means I cannot share in this volume. In thanks, she offered to read my fortune. At a loss of what to do\n\nwith my life since my caravaneering plan fell through, I accepted. Daria - for that was the woman’s name - drew a deck of the most beautiful purple cards, seemingly from nowhere. Liquidsmooth she shuffled them and chanted: \n\"As fate would hold -\n\nyour card so bold, to reveal fortunes both young and old.\"\nShe asked me to draw three. I did so, and two disappeared. The third depicted an enchantingly real image of the moon at night.\n\"The moon,\" she said, \"A fateful draw, my friend\"\n\n\"What does it mean?\" asked I.\n\"You may suspect your friends of plotting against you, but ultimately, it is your own lack of truthfulness that determines if you are right, or if you are wrong. A storm brews. It is one of challenge and adventure. You will\n\nhave to tell more than one lie to get through. At the end is a promise of serenity, a dedication to the quiet nights, if you can get there. Some say the moondraw is good, others bad. What can truly be said is that it will be filled with smiles and sobs.\n\n8 Grand Harvest, '66.\nHere ends this volume. You may be wondering what I've been up to in the interim. I will admit, I have not been merely editing this volume, My time has been filled with ruins, warewolves, death, bribery, joy, sorrow.\n\nSmiles and sobs.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Dear Elliot,§0\n§0\n§0My child, I am sorry to have passed, and to have left you on your own in this world. It be a shame as it may, there are many a things I have not disclosed to you, so I shall do so in this letter.\n\nFirst off, I leave my inheritance to you. A subtle amount of money is left for you, and I leave you my sword, the Pathileon. §0\n§0\n§0Secondly, it is important that you continue with your sword training, and become a guard.\n\nThird, kill off Euclectus. That horrible man hurt us both, so do what you did last time I married a man. For your precious mother, you would do anything, you said, so do this. Take his belongings, and sell them off. It shouldn't be a problem for you.\n\nFourth, find your father. I know I have never even told him your name, or that he has a child, but it is time. Since I can no longer care for you, it is imperative he does. Look for him in the northern regions. His name is Padrick O'Rourke.\n\nI love you so much son, and I am watching over you.§0\n§0\n§0       -Thalia Malchaster", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Druids undergo years of training and study to connect with nature. Druids do not consider those who do not take the time to go through studying as Druids. Those who have are considered druids, and have a totem. Druids are some of the best healers.\n\ndruids can restore sight and even bring back people from the brink of death. Druids do not control nature, but serve it. protectors of nature. Not violent, but will do whatever they need to in order to protect the nature.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "It is time my friends, for a revolution. In hopes of changing the way this world sees things, I am willing to die for my cause. It is time to show the world that fear shall no longer control us, but we shall control it.\n\nThings are about to change. Take up your arms, and join forces with me, against the wicked!", ""),
        StaticBook("Lmaooo", "§bAnnabelle Lyndon", "Fix the fucking chests its so annoying and confusing§0\n§0\n§0- uwu Annie", ""),
        StaticBook("Jieru's drinks", "§bJieru Yehenara", "Stravodka: strawberry, cherry tomato, mild chili, vodka§0\n§0\n§0Honeybee: basil, clover honey, gin, sake§0\n§0\n§0Think Pink: Pisco, grapefruit, pink peppercorn, champagne§0\n§0\n§0Pear and cardamom soda.\n\nopen sesame: Toasted sesame gin, cucumber, mint, champagne§0\n§0\n§0Yuzu Fresh: Bourbon, blanc and sweet vermouths, tea, yuzu§0\n§0\n§0LA PLAYA: tequila, prickly pear, lime, champagne foam§0\n§0\n§0Blackberry & juniper soda\n\nshiso leaf: Aloe vera juice, vodka, shiso leaf, chartreuse§0\n§0\n§0matcha latte with white chocolate§0\n§0\n§0mimosa: orange juice with cava§0\n§0\n§0peach bellini", ""),
        StaticBook("To Avon", "§bAlani Faladir", "Dear Avon,§0\n§0Since you got me a Krugmas gift, I of course wanted to return the favor. I found this at Cloud Temple while looking for a name tag and thought you might make use of it!§0\n§0\n§0Merry Krugmas!§0\n§0         ~Alani", ""),
