        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "- Treasure Log -§0\n§0\n§0Alex Dering\n\n-Rivia Southeast, 4000 meters§0\n§0-Rivian Road, Haense§0\n§0-Rivia: Old nation, possibly abandoned§0\n§0-East coast, southern wall§0\n§0-To get to road, take left just before Markev§0\n§0-Sleetfell land by Markev\n\n*words are scribbled, as if the writer was rushed* §0\n§0\n§0I believe I found the campsite described in the map. §0\n§0\n§0(( -232 / 50 / 2364", ""),
        StaticBook("GoldenAleRestock", "§bAlex Dering", "-Restock Golden Ale-§0\n§0\n§0I've gotten complaints that the quality of the golden ale has signifcantly decreased. I can agree with this, the flavor's lousy and it ain't even golden. We should restock it with GOOD golden ale.§0\n§0\n§0-Alex Dering", ""),
        StaticBook("Ugh idk", "§bAnnabelle Lyndonn", "Dear Alex,§0\n§0\n§0so I know you don't want to talk to me now, or anytime I guess. Which is understandable actually. I'd cut ties with people that swear out my name as well. Ahah I just have the worst shortcomings i guess. but thats besides the point.\n\nAnways, seeing you don't want to talk to me, I did the next best thing which is this letter. So I'm sorry about what happened. I should'nt have sworn you out or kept calling you Alexander. I'm quite the impulsive person, though I know it's no excuse. I\n\nfeel like our relationship has hit rock bottom again. But I guess i can only blame that on me. I mean, its up to you if don't want to be friends anymore. I honestly wouldnt be friends with myself after that. Oh god it sounds like I'm pitying myself\n\noh well I can't go back on my words I guess. Though, your words hurt yesterday, they were pretty much true. And i should find an insult that doesnt include canonist faith. I should really keep my mouth shut and all that Jazz as I keep causing more problem\n\nwith people I have good relationships with. Ah well I guess§0\n§0\n§0Sincerly, Annabelle Lyndonn", ""),
        StaticBook("T. Log #1", "§bTelmarill Azaghul", ":-: Telmarill logbook:-:\n\n:-: Balista improvement :-:§0\n§0\n§0I was inspecting the baslistas the other day on my daily routine, they dont look in top condition. I can fix that if you allow me to. below I will list all the thing i need for 1 balista.§0\n§0\n§0birch slabs x4§0\n§0sos\n\ndark oak slabs x8§0\n§0birch planks x2§0\n§0birch stairs x1§0\n§0spruce slab x2§0\n§0spruce stairs x 4§0\n§0\n§0and of course some tools to remove and renovate the balista completely§0\n§0\n§0-Telmarill\n\nwow, didnt expect to go blind. that dang wolf I ALMOST HAD HIM, but he scratched me up real good. took both me eyes out.§0\n§0\n§0not very good defenses and military personell. let me train em and they will be good. but fcourse im just a footman\n\nAgnarum has changed a lot since i was there, many bearlings show no respect nor honour but that doesnt matter to me. all i need is discipline if ye have that yer good. hopefulleh the improvement will be accepted, the balistas are absolutely garbage ere.\n\naperently ive become rusteh, a bearlin beat me in a foight. i do accept the defeat but he does need to learn some honour. at age eight he would sacrifice that, its not a good way to begin.§0\n§0\n§0starting on the azaghul clan hall, looks more epic then the other\n\nmining duty, pretty fun but allllll the blody gravel.§0\n§0druids are needed, but i dont like em, im gonna stude there.§0\n§0\n§0bjor is a lil fat but that doesnt matter, hes my friend i think. im not sure how he feels about et\n\nElumeria§0\n§0Dark elf§0\n§0Blue eyes§0\n§0blond/blue hair§0\n§0magic?§0\n§0purple robes\n\nEmpire hasnt changed, think someone wants to buy a home there, Conclusion: War upon the empire.§0\n§0\n§0quite lonely inside the mountain§0\n§0\n§0did i resolve a matter of political strikes??.§0\n§0think i just did\n\ndont think i like the blind man, i mean im blind but hes so stupid. he sees sitting on stairs as loitering§0\n§0\n§0met maebh  in empires heart today, shes  not changed still like her §0\n§0\n§0Magistraite, ritz goldwitch\n\nam i to become deputy bailiff?§0\n§0\n§0Bruce said that i should get 150 mina for the goodies in the chest tax office§0\n§0\n§0i am deputy bailiff§0\n§0Aldis refuses to show me his wanted board\n\nElumeria was in belvitz today, i had a taste of her brews§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Last message", "§bTelmarill Azaghul", "Please miss/lad, if you found this it means: either i died in battle, going away with no intend of return or lived out of my days peacefully as possible elsewhere.§0\n§0This will be the final message of me, ive grown quite fond of my apprentice. i told the lad\n\nthat he needs to wear the same as me at the last time i was seen, most likely that would be my shops outfit: a white gambeson over the common adrian armour and shoulder guards. i leave the business to him and all that i posses including my money. please\n\npay your respects to him, he just lost his dad, and may i have a good farewell/funeral.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0-much love,§0\n§0Telmarill.", ""),
        StaticBook("read me", "§bTelmarill", "only my son will be able to open the chest.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writ of Deputy", "§bArthur", "Write of Deputy Bailiff§0\n§0\n§0This man, Telmarill Azaghul, is to be made a deputy bailiff under trial Bailiff Arthur Blaze until the end of his trial period in 1699. In the meantime, Deputy Azaghul will be put in charge of following Bailiff Blaze's\n\norders and assisting him in his efforts for the law in Adria, alongside trial Bailiff Wigberht.§0\n§0\n§0Signed, trial Bailiff Arthur Blaze, 1697", ""),
        StaticBook("3 TAX PAPERS", "§bTelmarill Azaghul", "REMEMBER TO PAY 3 TAX PAPERS", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "You Suck", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Guess i can use this as a journey.§0\n§0I managed my way to Belvitz, i looked for some job in the local INN, but nothing interesting. The merchant said I could find the elf here, but still nothing, I'll keep searching.\n\nDay-2§0\n§0Some idiot with a banner on his head approached me, and said something usless. I guss this town is wierd as fuck.", ""),
        StaticBook("Buy me VIP", "§bJames", "Roses are red\nViolets are blue\nBuy me VIP\nBecause I am poor", ""),
        StaticBook("A Friendly Input", "§bAn Anonymous Tipster", "To the powers of Adria:  Antanios Rutledge is a threat to all of the lands. He is a bonded man of the September Prince. I know  this for sure, as I have seen him bonded by the September Prince's Archdruid named Rel'Talonir. He has battled against us\n\nheavily onside of the Prince's legions, he has slaughtered countless lives in name of some Deity. This will not stand, Adria. This will not. He is a threat and as a collective whole we beg of you to stop this, for any attempts we have made were shut down\n\nby his blades end.§0\n§0\n§0Adria, do what's right. §0\n§0Imprison this menace.§0\n§0Set right what he has done wrong. No man of September should walk among the walls of Adria, for this is a free people! A good people! A just people.§0\n§0\n§0- A Friend, 1693.", ""),
        StaticBook("Printing Guide", "§bLorson Goodwinn", "===================     Printing Guide§0\n§0===================§0\n§0\n§0   This volume has examples of different fonts, colors, and dingbats available to you.  If there is something you want, and it is not in this book, please ask if it can be procured.\n\n§4Red§0\n§4\t§cLight Red§0\n§6Gold§0\n§eYellow§0\n§2Dark Green§0\n§aGreen§0\n§bAqua§0\n§3Dark Aqua§0\n§1Dark Blue§0\n§9Blue§0\n§dLight Purple§0\n§5Dark Purple§0\n§7Gray\n\n§8Dark Gray§0\n§0Black (Standard)§0\n§0\n§0\t§0§lMAKE A MARK WITH BOLD TEXT§0\n§0\n§0§l\t§0§l§mStrike Through§0\n§0\n§0§nUnderline Important Information§0\n§0\n§0§oItalicize Items\n\n§n\t§0§o§nCombine multiple font types for an unique page!§0\n§0\n\n===================§0\n§0       Dingbats§0\n§0===================§0\n§0Stars§0\n§0★ ✡ ✿ ❋ ✴ ✦ ✪ ❂§0\n§0\n§0Arrows§0\n§0↖ ↗ ↘ ↙ ⇦ ⇧ ⇨ ⇩ ➤ ➢ ➣ ➵ ➶ ➷ ➸ ➹§0\n§0\n§0Office & Law§0\n§0© ® ™ ℗ № ✂ ✒ ✑\n\nChess & Cards§0\n§0♔ ♕ ♖ ♗ ♘ ♙ ♚ ♛ ♜ ♝ ♞ ♟§0\n§0♤ ♠ ♧ ♣ ♡ ♥ ♢ ♦§0\n§0\n§0Musical Notes§0\n§0♩ ♪ ♫ ♬ ♭ ♮ ♯ ° ø ≠ ≭§0\n§0\n§0Weather§0\n§0ϟ ☀ ☁ ☂ ☃ ☉ ☼ ☽ ☾ ♁ ♨ ❄ ❅ ❆ §0\n§0\n§0Heart Symbols§0\n§0დ ღ ♡ ❣ ❤ ❥ ❦ ❧ ♥ ۵ ლ\n\nMale & Female§0\n§0♀ ♂§0\n§0\n§0Face Symbols§0\n§0☹ ☺ ☻ ☠ §0\n§0\n§0Mathematical§0\n§0π ∞ Σ √ ∫ ∆ ∼ ≈ ∴ ∶ ∷ ∵ ≤ ≥ + - / = X ( ) §0\n§0\n§0If you do not see what you want, ask!", ""),
        StaticBook("Receipt", "§bVexalia Al'Abass-Avern", "Proof that Lorson Goodwinn purchased one stamp for 10 minas on 10th of The Deep Cold 1693. The stamp was then used to deliver a newspaper to a Richard Baruch in Sutica.§0\n§0\n§0-Signed Vexalia Al'Abass Avern", ""),
        StaticBook("Songbook", "§bJaya Jayamen", "7 8 9 \n4 5 6 \n1 2 3 \n\n1 – B\n2 – C\n3 – D\n4 – E\n5 – F \n6 – G\n7 – A\n8 – B^\n9 – C^\n\n((jurrasic park))\n9 8 9 6 5\n9 8 9 6 5\n9 8 8 9 6\n2 7\n\n9 8 9 6 5\n9 8 9 6 5\n9 8 8 9 8\n9\n\n((concerning hobbits))\n2 6 9 6 \n2 6 9\n\n2 3 4 6 4\n3 2\n4 6 7 9 8\n6 4 3\n\n2 3 4 6 4\n3 4 3 2\n4 6 7 9 8\n6 4 3 2 3 2\n\n((hey jude))\n6 4\n4 5 7 3\n3 3 4 5 9\n9 8 6 7 6 5 4\n\n6 6 7 7 7 9\n8 8 9 7 6 \n2 3 4 7 6\n6 5 4 1 2", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Belvitz House Status§0\n§01. Diana§0\n§02. -§0\n§03. Ross§0\n§04. Edward§0\n§05. Antonio Montfort§0\n§06. MM Guild§0\n§07. -§0\n§08. Retinue Dwarf§0\n§09. Ludovico Montfort§0\n§010. -§0\n§011. Feremyr§0\n§012. George (Morghuul\n\n13. Piede (house undone)§0\n§014. -§0\n§015. - (smith)§0\n§016. - (bakery)§0\n§017. Klaus (niv_mizzet)§0\n§018. -§0\n§019. Amelina§0\n§020. Ashlyn Dantes§0\n§021. Matilda Maud§0\n§022. Quavinir§0\n§023. Harkon §0\n§024. Wynn§0\n§025. Osbert\n\n26. Lorelle§0\n§027. - unfinished", ""),
        StaticBook("A Gift", "§bCaulder Marsk", "Katrina,§0\n§0\n§0Greetings once again. Though I do not offer tax slips, this time, I hope to offer something equally useful. I am leaving the continent to travel and explore abroad, and therefore am parting with a good deal of my trinkets I've collected over\n\ntime as a relic curator. For you, the town healer, I leave this ring. I know not of where it came from, nor much of anything about its origins. What I do know is that upon placing it on a wounded person, it changes color based on their wellness. My\n\nhope is somehow this is of use to you and the city of Belvitz by extension. If not, perhaps as an additional boost of mina on the market. Do with it what you will, it is yours. §0\n§0\n§0\n§0Marsk.", ""),
        StaticBook("To - Mr Barnabas", "§bFrederick Kelly", "To Mr. Barnabas,\n\nYour letter found my abode and I have understood your message. The shining enigma that falls upon your mind is someone that even, I can not get in contact with.\n\nAs a philosopher, I understand the majesty and beauty that comes with\n\nseeing such a woman. Though, I offer my condolences on not being able to provide an introduction.\n\nShe is one of immense beauty, many suitors. Even those that are Illatian, try to find her grasp.\n\nPray the the Fertility Goddess, Lorenitus.\n- Mr. Kelly", ""),
        StaticBook("OOC Bethlehem", "§bJaya Jayamen", "(IMPORTANT: You need to have read the book “OOC PIANO GUIDE” To understand how to read this music. It is located in the Piano Essentials section of the piano shop.)\n\n(The contents of this book is all OOC. In RP it can be used as sheet music for the song. Since the grand piano in RP is a regular piano and not 9 blocks with only 9 notes, in RP the contents of this music sheet would be different then what is written.)\n\nIn the little town of Bethlehem – music box version **§0\n§0\n§04 3 2 – – 3 4 5§0\n§06 – – – 7 8 9 –§0\n§08 – 7 – 6 – – –§0\n§07 8 9 – 8 – 7 –§0\n§0\n§06 – 7 – 8 – 9 –§0\n§06 – 5 – 4 – – –§0\n§04 3 2 – – 3 4 5§0\n§06 – – – 7 8 9 –§0\n\n8 – 7 – 6 – – –§0\n§07 8 9 – 8 – 7 –§0\n§06 – 7 – 8 – 9 –§0\n§06 – 5 – 4 – – –§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Amaya's Journal", "§bAmaya Shelor", "Amaya's Journal§0\n§0\n\nDay 1§0\n§0I have just bought this journal in the nearby village. Hopefully it will come of some use to me.§0\n§0I have joined a mercenary camp. Hopfully it will provide me with some source of money, and the leader seems nice enough. Even though it has been four\n\nyears now, I cannot help it. I still mourn Qeta. The disease was so §0merciless...she§0 suffered for two days before death claimed her.§0 Damn. Now I'm getting all teary-eyed thinking about this.§0\n§0\n§0-Amaya\n\nDay 2§0\n§0\n§0Alden's going to Salwin-Salvin-Saldin-§0\n§0Damn, I can't remember the name-tomorrow. I think I shall try to recruit people in Cloud Temple tomorrow. Anyway, I might also find some §0leather...hopefully§0.§0.§0. Maybe I should check out the towns further\n\nnorth tomorrow. I need more recruits-preferably female, since I have another space in my tent available.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0-Amaya\n\nDay 3§0\n§0\n§0No luck recruiting again. I need to try another strategy. Although, I saw the most heartwarming exchange between a little girl and a Halfling... He was so nice to her and agreed to take her in. Part of me wishes I had been the one, though...\n\nPerhaps it would have helped me ease my conscience about Qeta. To think, she saw an abandoned, shivering five-year-old girl, and she took me in without hesitation... I shall strive to be like her.§0\n§0\n§0-Amaya\n\nDay 4§0\n§0I have just gotten back from the Cloud Tmple. Still no luck recruiting. Sucita was beautiful, and I saw the little girl again! She looked like she was locked out of an armory (?) and I said hi. Also, when I went to cloud temple, some goblin had the\n\nnerve to spit on me! I could barely keep my temper under control. I really hope that I can find somebody to recruit soon.§0\n§0\n§0-Amaya\n\nDay 5§0\n§0\n§0Today, to most beautiful and terrible thing happened to me. I fell in love with a man named Leon. He was so kind, but he was going to get executed by the King. We kissed, we sparred, he had to leave. We were saying our last goodbyes when some\n\npigspawn came up to us and provoked him. They fought, and having no armor, he lost. I attacked him, infuriated by Leon's death, but I thought with my fists rather than my mind. Some high elf saved me. I have been humiliated by this abomination. I shall\n\ntrain vigorously so that this never happens again.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0-Amaya\n\nDay 6§0\n§0\n§0I travelled to Sucita last night. I forgot to bring this journal, which is why I am not writing this until the day after. A high elf thought he had the right to tell me that I was too skinny. The nerve! I'm sorry, Mr. Judgemental, but I think that\n\nI get to decide what my shape is. On a different note, it started snowing today... It is beautiful! I love the first snowfall, it's so peaceful.§0\n§0\n§0-Amaya", ""),
        StaticBook("OOC Saints March", "§bJaya Jayamen", "(IMPORTANT: You need to have read the book “OOC PIANO GUIDE” To understand how to read this music. It is located in the Piano Essentials section of the piano shop.)\n\n(The contents of this book is all OOC. In RP it can be used as sheet music for the song. Since the grand piano in RP is a regular piano and not 9 blocks with only 9 notes, in RP the contents of this music sheet would be different then what is written.)\n\nThe Saints Come Marching In **§0\n§0\n§02 4 5 6 – – – – §0\n§02 4 5 6 – – – –§0\n§02 4 5 6 – 4 – 2§0\n§0– 4 – 3 – – – –§0\n§0\n§04 4 3 2 – – 2 4§0\n§0– 6 6 6 5 – – –§0\n§0– 4 5 6 – 4 – 3 §0\n§0– 4 – 2 – – – –§0", ""),
        StaticBook("OOC Poke Route 1", "§bJaya Jayamen", "(IMPORTANT: You need to have read the book “OOC PIANO GUIDE” To understand how to read this music. It is located in the Piano Essentials section of the piano shop.)\n\n(The contents of this book is all OOC. In RP it can be used as sheet music for the song. Since the grand piano in RP is a regular piano and not 9 blocks with only 9 notes, in RP the contents of this music sheet would be different then what is written.)\n\nPokemon red/blue route 1 ****§0\n§0\n§02 3 4 – 4 – 4 –§0\n§02 3 4 – 4 – 4 –§0\n§02 3 4 – 4 – 5 –§0\n§0– 4 3 – – – – –§0\n§0\n§01 2 3 – 3 – 4 –§0\n§01 2 3 – 3 – 4 –§0\n§01 2 3 – 3 – 4 3§0\n§0– 4 2 – – – – –§0\n\n2 3 4 – 4 – 4 –§0\n§02 3 4 – 4 – 4 –§0\n§02 3 4 – 4 – 5 –§0\n§0– 4 3 – – – – –§0\n§0\n§01 2 3 – 5 – 4 –§0\n§03 – 2 – 1 – 1 – §0\n§01 – 7 – – – 1 –§0\n§02 3 4 – 2 – – –§0\n\n4 5 6 – 6 – 4 –§0\n§02 – 9 – 8 – 7 – §0\n§08 – 6 – 4 – 2 –§0\n§0– 4 3 – – – – –§0\n§0\n§04 5 6 – 6 – 4 –§0\n§02 – 9 – 8 – 7 –§0\n§0– 5 6 – 9 – 8 – §0\n§09 – 9 – – – – –§0", ""),
