        StaticBook("Tavern Menu", "§bDemetria Hatheway", "§6§lOld Oaks Tavern§0\n§8§l§m---§0\n§c§lBeverages§0\n§0\n§0* Wine: 5 minas§0\n§0* Ale / Vodka: 3 minas§0\n§0* Rum / Spirit: 5 minas§0\n§0* Exotic Alcohol: 10 minas§0\n§8§oNon - Alcoholic§0\n§0* Coffee: 7 minas§0\n§0* Green Tea: 7 minas§0\n§0* Water: 1 mina\n\n§c§lFood/Meals§0\n§0\n§0* Fish: 3 minas§0\n§0* Mutton/Porkchops: 4 minas§0\n§0* Baked Taters: 3 minas§0\n§0* Homeade Frostin' Cake: 10 minas§0\n§0* Chicken Breast: 4 minas", ""),
        StaticBook("Opinion on Truth", "§bJaya Jayamen", "An Opinion on Truth\n\n         ~Originally by\n         Geedin Jayamen\n\nThe truth can be a hard thing to know these days. With so many lies about various things in general flying about, it is hard to discern the truth from the false. Now I’m not here to tell anyone what the truth is in any situation.\n\nI just want to talk about and discuss what I feel the truth is in itself. To start out, I am going to go a bit off topic, to what I think about fear and doubt.\n\nSo what is fear? Fear in my own opinion is of course when you are afraid of something. Whether that be the outcome of a decision you have to make, or doing something you have never done for the first time.\n\nThe next question is what does it mean to be afraid of something? What causes it? I think that fear occurs the most often, though not all the time, in the absence of knowledge. Like when you aren’t sure about something.\n\nFear of the unknown is a very common thing, as the unknown can possibly do anything.\n\nperson would likely have little to no fear about it unless it is something bad that is to happen. For example, if I studied day and night for a big test, and was sure I knew everything needed to pass the test and then some,\n\nI would hopefully and likely feel little fear. If I was a soldier and was about to get my leg amputated to save it, I would likely fear if my leg getting cut off. In the second example I know what is going to happen, I know how it’s going to happen,\n\nbut I will likely still fear that it will happen. As for the first example, if the person who studied day and night failed the test. That would cause the next subject. Doubt.\n\nDoubt is something that I think causes a lot of fear. It ties in with the lack of knowledge in something. Doubt can be a very powerful thing. It changes or attempts to change your perspective on things, for better or worse, though usually for the worse.\n\nAn example of good doubt would be thinking about an outcome of a certain action like whether something is a good idea or not, and acting on that doubt.\n\nAn example of bad doubt would be something like thinking that you cannot do something due to a past experience.\n\nTo avoid doubt and fear, I think the best way to defeat both is to find out the whole topic of this. The truth. Truth in my opinion is very simple to ourselves, but hard to obtain from outside ourselves.\n\nIf you know the truth about something that would mean that you have true knowledge in a certain part or most aspects of that something.\n\nThis would defeat both doubt and fear, as fear is mainly caused by doubt, and doubt requires uncertainty in something. The problem is that some outside sources do the next thing. Lie.\n\nLies in my opinion increase doubt and in turn fear. They corrupt the truth and make things harder to make out. A lot of things have the ability to lie. People, books, even our own memories can lie.\n\nI know that most people would say their memories are not faulty, and I agree that can be true for the most part. Everyone will have different interpretations of a thing that they all together witness, like an abstract painting.\n\nI am only saying that there is a possibility that a memory could be wrong.\n\nNow how to discern what is a lie and what is the truth. Well, that is quite the question isn’t it? We can usually lie at any time, so how to know what is true?\n\nThat brings me to something I call absolute truth, or in other words the real truth in something. The thing is, I think that we can never know the absolute truth. Don’t get me wrong. It is there, it is just usually unknowable.\n\nTake the abstract picture example. Both people would know what the picture looks like to them, but they would likely be two different interpretations.\n\nThe object outside the two people’s minds is the absolute truth. We just have interpretations of it through what we think and perceive.\n\nSo who would be right about what it the abstract painting is? I think they would both be right to a point. With the truth in most matters there isn’t a white or black scenario. It is usually some type of grey.\n\nNow, imagine white as truth, and black as false. We can get the grey a closer to white with the more truth we tell about the subject. We can also get the grey closer to black with the more lies we tell.\n\nNow it is certainly possible to get things to all white. This is based on both the question and the answer. If I asked, did you go to the store today, and you did and said yes. That would be a truthful statement.\n\n. As for the opposite with it getting to all black. That is a tricky thing. I think as soon as there is a falsehood in there, something is already not all true. Though it can get even darker the more lies are put into it.\n\nNow back to how to find out if something someone says or does is true or not. There is something that can help with that. Trust. Trust helps you believe what someone says is true. It both does that and helps you be more truthful to that person.\n\nI believe that in some cases it helps the other person be more truthful to you as well. Now when both people trust each other, that is where things get really interesting.\n\nI would think very plainly that when two people trust each other, the truth flows a lot more smoothly. Who should you trust? Well, that is up to you.\n\nAll in all, the truth is simple, yet easily diverged into a lie. I believe the more truth we tell, the clearer things will be to those we tell it to, the more trust we will gain, and the more likely people will tell ourselves the truth.\n\nIt is easy to tell the truth, Harder but more temporarily convenient to tell a lie, and even harder to own up to a lie.\n\nWhen and if all the lies are cleared up to yourself, well, what need would there be to lie again? You would be set on a much clearer path then in my opinion.", ""),
        StaticBook("Kitab Alsalam.P3", "§bIbraheem Aladeen", "☪Chapter Eighteen☪\nProphecy Of The Second Caliphate\n-------------------We Give you A promise, That One Of the Names Of Kharadeen, Will Bring you A Second Caliphate. He will Be A Just, Honorable Leader, He Will Follow the Book\n\nWith His heart, And He will Be One OF the Best Caliphs. He will Unite the Farfolk And Qalasheen People and save them from falling to history. He will Bring Peace and Prosperity For Many Years. He Will Unite many races Under His\n\nbanner. There will Be those who Come and try to stop him, But Allah will strike them down. He will be one of the Purest of the sons of Faiz Kharadeen And Bring a better future to the world. Allah Indeed knows all, and is the best of planners.\n\n☪Chapter Nineteen☪\nProphecy of Faiz Kharadeen\n-------------------We have sent down a Man, to unite the tribes, and to liberate you from the krugite clan. He will be a conqueror and save your people. He will form the First Caliphate\n\nand will be A Hero For all True Followers of the book. Those who deposes him are truly in the wrong. He will be the best man Upon the Earth, And his Children will lead the farfolk people to a better Horizon, There will be people who Will oppose\n\nthe View Of the Kharadeen Family of the Farfolks Living with other races, and they are indeed the wrong doers. There will be one day, When all of the farfolks are disunited, and People will say “We need another Faiz Kharadeen, in our time.”\n\nand people will mourn and wish for his return. Allah indeed knows all, and is the master of all.\n-------------------☪Chapter Twenty☪ \nProphecy of the Farfolk Oppression\n-------------------\n\nThere will be a time where the farfolks will be Oppressed From Many and all. There will be people who will plot to destroy them and the holy faith. They Will Suffer Injustice and many will lose their lives, They will be outcasted and fear to\n\nleave their very homes, Children will be killed and Families will be torn apart. There will be a Great Divide, All wishing for a Son of the family Kharadeen to save them from the hardship, and lead them. They will say “Oh where are you oh\n\nFaiz Kharadeen, We mourn for your return! Send us your sons to Lead us and save us from this great despair!” Allah will grant them this wish and send them one of the Best of Men, And he will great the Second Caliphate and save the farfolks from\n\ndestruction. Fear not, For we placed this as a test for you, Keep your faith in Allah, And you will be rewarded with the best of things, Seven Skies. Allah Says “With Hardship Comes ease.” Indeed Allah is best in all and the savior of all.\n---------------\n\n☪Chapter TwentyOne☪\nFood From Allah\n-------------------We have sent to you Food Of Many Kind, So you may eat and enjoy yourselves and stay healthy and strong. There are foods we have also sent down to tempt you\n\nand take you away from us, For this life is indeed a test. We have given you Honey and Milk And fruits of Sweets. Eat them but do not eat Pig and boar, and stay away from alcohol, for they will dull your mind and take you away from us. Allah is\n\nindeed the best of givers and best of rewarders.\n-------------------☪Chapter TwentyTwo☪\nThe Earth and its creatures\n-------------------We have Given you the Earth, For you to walk Upon and grow families and\n\nworship. We give you a task to protect and care for your environment, Do not pollute and Destroy it, We have made it for both(you and the earth) to rely upon each other for your survival. We Have place Small Pieces Of seven skies upon the\n\nEarth for you to enjoy, and protect. We have made the earth with everything in it, All Perfect, All in harmony. One The Last Hour will be a man, Who committed many sins his entire life that they would be able to be made into the largest\n\nmountain, and his good deeds of a palm of his hand...We will save him from the nether for he took care of the earth and he will be granted seven skies. We have also set upon the earth Animals for you to tame, eat and use. Take care of them,\n\nand do not abuse them. Care for them and protect them as if were your very jugular vein.\n Allah is indeed the most Powerful and the lord of the whole universe and all that is in it.\n-------------------\n\n☪Chapter TwentyThree☪\nThe Aenguls Raced To Save Him\n-------------------We give you a story of a Merchant and a thief, To remember Allah and his greatness. There Was A merchant, Who used to go through one city, to the other as\n\na tradesman...and he uses to pass through this valley...One day he passed through the valley... Holding his merchandise on top of his camel...when suddenly...a Thief stops him...In the middle of the valley...\n\nalone...There is no one around... He put the sword to his neck and he says....'I am going to kill you, and take your merchandise..' The Merchant said to him, 'please take everything...but spare my life' and the thief said to him..'no!' 'Im going to take\n\nyour merchandise and I'm going to kill you...' when the merchant found out the thief was insisting on killing him, he said to him... 'Okay, You can kill me and take my merchandise, but please allow me to do one thing and then after that you can kill me.'\n\nHe said...'Do whatever you like, But then I'm Going to wait for you and kill you'...he said 'allow me to pray two Rakat(Salah)'... The thief made a mistake by letting him pray two rakat..so he prayed the two rakat.. he prayed the first rakat\n\nthen he prayed the second rakat… And in his prostration...Because We in the book said...'You are closest to Allah When you're in your prostration..so ask Allah for the things you want in your prostration.'...In the merchant's prostration, he said one\n\ndua. He said 'I ask you...Oh, Allah By the Nur (light) of your face which has filled the pillars of your throne' And then he began to ask Allah, by all of his names, by his wonderful attributes.And finally, He said..'Oh the one who responds to the dua\n\nof the one in need, Oh the One Who responds to the one who really needs him...Save me from this thief...' And then he says three times, 'OH THE ONE WHO SAVES..SAVE ME! OH THE ONE WHO SAVES..SAVE ME! OH THE ONE WHO SAVES..SAVE ME!'\n\n he did not complete his Dua..then all of a sudden he hears the galloping of a horse.Racing so quickly and so fast...on top of that horse was a man, a warrior, and he had covered his face... with a sword in his right\n\narm. The thief looked at him, before he could do anything...The Man on the horse chopped and slit his throat..and the thief died..the merchant looked up and he hugged him and kissed him on each cheek and he said to him 'May ALLAH bless\n\nyou, where are you from? where did you come from?' then he said...'I am an Aengul, from the fourth sky You asked Allah in the first part of your dua, and we heard you,\nthen you asked with the second part of your dua, The sky shook,then you asked in\n\nthe third part of your dua, We raced to Allah, so I raced and beat the other Aengul to Allah, and said, Oh Lord send me!, and so Allah allowed me' then the Aengul faded away...the Dua of the person who is in need, Allah WILL RESPOND.\n\nAllah is indeed the most merciful and the helper of those in need.\n-------------------☪Chapter TwentyFour☪\nThe Last Hour\n-------------------We Have Set A Time For the World And Universe, And All things Living to come\n\nto me. To be Judged, All will bear witness to all sins and everyone Will Speak About What they Have witnessed, Even your Very Hands Will Speak And Say What you have done with them, Brothers will run from each other Because they of\n\ntheir fear of themselves and their sins being exposed. The Earth, the Stars, The water, The Very trees will speak of what you have done, Every step you took, Every breath you done. We will take all shyness and all darkness from all’s hearts\n\nso no one will judge each other for their sins. Your Lord Will Judge you For your sins and decide if you are to be sent to the Nether Or to Seven Skies. The last Hour will be as if it was a thousand years to you but it will be as fast as the day. You will\n\nbe asked ‘What is your creed’ The believers will say ‘Al’iiman Rashidun’ You will Be asked ‘Who was your God’ the Believers will say ‘The Lord who created us from a drop of water, My Rabb(lord) The Almighty Allah’ and then they will be\n\njudged for either you have passed your test or you have failed. Before this all happens Allah will ask his Aengul Of Death ‘WHO REMAINS!’ The Aengul will say “you my lord,I the Aengul Of Death, The Aenguls,Daemons,And the Creatures\n\nof the earth” Allah Will Say “TAKE THE SOULS OF THE CREATURES OF THE EARTH” the Aengul Of Death will go and take the souls of the Creatures of the earth and say “The Souls Of the Creatures of the earth has been taken, My\n\nlord.” and Allah will say “WHO ELSE REMAINS!?” The Aengul of death will say “you my lord, I the Aengul Of Death, The Aenguls, Daemons.” Allah will then say “take the Souls of the Daemons” And the Aengul Of death will take the souls and\n\nreturn to Allah and say “The Souls Of the Daemons Have been taken, My Lord” And Allah will say “WHO ELSE REMAINS!?” The Aengul Of death will say “you my lord,I the Aengul Of Death, The Aenguls.” Allah will then say “take the\n\nSouls of the Aenguls” And the Aengul Of death will take the souls and return to Allah and say “The Souls Of the Aenguls Have been taken, My Lord” And Allah will say “WHO ELSE REMAINS!?” The Aengul of death will say “you my lord\n\nand I the Aengul Of Death.” Allah will then Say “Take your very soul.” The Aengul Of Death will take his soul and Allah will then say “I AM THE ONE! THE ONLY! WHERE ARE YOUR FALSE GODS! WHERE ARE THE IDOLS YOU\n\nWORSHIPED? WHERE ARE YOUR KINGS? I AM THE ONE, THE ONLY, THE ALMIGHTY, THE KING OF KINGS, THE MASTER! YOU WERE THE ONES WHO THOUGHT YOU WOULD NOT RETURN TO ME! I AM THE KING OF THE WORLD, THE KING OF UNIVERSE, THE KING OF\n\nEVERYTHING, THE MAKER OF ALL!” and then he will gather all souls and judge them.\nAllah Is the Best Of Judges and the most merciful, the Justice, The Sentence, the all-powerful.\n-------------------☪Chapter Twenty-five☪\nObey your Parents\n-------------------\n\nWe have sent to you your Parents who Cared for you and taken care of you when you were but a child, Obey your parents for they sacrifice their Daily lives For you and take care of you Allah says ‘If your parents are angry with you Allah is angry\n\nwith you.’ The only time you may disobey your Parents is when they ask you to Abandon your faith and to lead you Astray, Lo! Allah has set upon you a Path so that you may be reunited with him in the Seven Skies, Allah says ‘the Easiest way\n\nto the Seven Skies is your parents.’ Do Not roll your eyes or scoff at your Parents for that Indeed a Sin and Allah will Place you into the Nether. Do not back talk your Parents for they have taken you into this world with Allah Mercy and\n\nBlessing, Allah loves those who Respect their Parents and Obey. Allah is indeed the most Just and Kind.\n-------------------☪Chapter Twenty-six☪\nCharity\n-------------------Allah has bestowed on you Wealth and food for you to eat However there will be\n\nthose who will have neither As a test of Faith towards his rabbi, so Allah says ‘Prove to me, that you will take care of your Brothers or sisters, for an act of Kindness can Lead you to the Seven Skies.’ Allah loves those who take care of\n\nothers and Surely he will reward you, Allah is the best of rewarders. Lo! Remember for Allah has a punishment for those who do such just for fame or his own Desire and those who do not give charity in act of Kindness and Pure Intent\n\nAllah will send them to the Nether so Beware! Indeed Allah Is the Best Of helpers and the most merciful.\n-------------------(part 4 will come soon!)", ""),
        StaticBook("Writ of Bailiff", "§bRitz Gloshwitz", "Writ of Bailiff§0\n§0\n§0This man, Arthur Blaze, is to be deputized as a Bailiff of His Eminence, Bishop Ritz Gloshwitz, Magistrate of Adria until the year of 1699.§0\n§0By which time it shall either be renewed or rendered null and void. In the meantime, Bailiff\n\nBlaze will be charged with the execution and persecution of the law in Adria alongside Bailiff Wigberht. §0\n§0\n§0Signed Bishop Ritz F. Gloshwitz, 1697", ""),
        StaticBook("The Kelpie", "§bKardryn Oranor", "§0\n§0        The Kelpie\n\nThe sun was burning down on Angelica and her horse, flies buzzing all around them as they rode across a small hunting path that cut the dense bushes of the woodland in half. It had been a particularly warm summer, and she'd found today was a good day to\n\nhead out into the wilderness of Atlas to head out on Juniper and let the horse run around a bit in the shallow waters of the fen that sat deep in the forest. She let out a little sigh as they rode into the shade of the canopy again, the sun no longer\n\nburning in her face. \"It really is warm today, isn't it Juniper?\" She said with a smile, patting the horse's neck. The horse let out a soft whinny, as if it responded in agreement. Angelica loved Juniper, her father gave the horse to her as a foal when\n\nshe was fourteen. For four years now, they'd been best friends, riding off to everywhere and anywhere. Today they hadn't gone far out into the wilderness of Atlas though, the forest fen was not far away from their farmstead so it was a natural choice for\n\npicking a place to swim and let Juniper have some fun. From the sound of dozens of frogs she could already determine they were closeby and soon the fen suddenly appeared before them between the trees. Angelica and Juniper stopped as they walked onto the\n\nbeach of the small lake, which was little more than a flat spot of dried white mud. They were all alone, it was only them and the sound of countless frogs and bugs like dragonflies. Angelica was somewhat suprised by this, she'd expected to see some kids\n\nfrom the village nearby, or perhaps even one of those elven druids that came there from time to time to meditate. Not today though, there was nobody present except them. Angelica smiled and got off her horse, loosening its harness before taking off the\n\nsaddle and patting Juniper's back as a sign of being free to head off into the water. Immediatly the horse did so, charging at the fen, right through the reeds into the water. Angelica chuckled and would grab a towel and flask of apple liquor she'd taken\n\nwith her from her father's basement. She and her boyfriend Frederick did that often without any trouble, but this time she almost got caught by her younger brother. Always the snitch, little Eric. She loved him though.\n\nSuddenly she was awakened from her little nap by panicked sounds of her horse. She got off the towel on which she'd been laying. \"Ow!\" She yelped in pain upon her movement. When looking down, she saw that the parts of her skin that weren't covered by her\n\nwhite dress were a crimson red from laying in the sun too long. She frowned. Sunburned... How long had she been asleep for? Only then it struck her that the sun no longer burned down on her, it was beginning to get dark already, clouds covering the sky\n\nnow and a light mist beginning to form above the fen. Then she heard Juniper again and she quickly ran to the lake where the horse's sounds came from. She waded into the water, through the reeds \"Juniper?! Where are you?!\" She heard a splash and more\n\nneighing, panicked, frightened neighing. Suddenly she stood right before Juniper, the horse seeming stuck in some branches that laid underwater. Angelica tried to calm down the horse but it did little. The water stood waist high and Juniper's panicked\n\nmovements made it splash everywhere. Angelica realized she'd have to get the branches out of the way, or Juniper wouldn't get loose. She took a deep breath before lowering herself into the water, She could somewhat see the big branches through the murky\n\nwater, a tree that had fallen over into the fen. She'd soon be faced however, with the hard truth that this was a terrible idea. A hard smash on her back. A kick to her head. She was below Juniper, who stomped around in the fen in panick. A panick that\n\nhad now spread to Angelica. She tried to get up, kicked down again, all the remaining air kicked out of her stomach. She gasped for air. Water. Another kick on her back. She was being kept underwater by Juniper. Her head hit the tree. In complete panick\n\nshe continued trying to breathe and to get up, but all that went in was water. Juniper stood on top of her, preventing her from getting up, preventing her from breathing, preventing her from living another day. Within a few minutes, she had drowned.\n\nShe would however rise again. Many weeks later, during a cold night that kept the forest in darkness and the fen covered in mist, she rose up from the water. No longer though was she the young Angelica. She rose from the muddy shallows of the fen as\n\na spectral being, blighting and enchanting the lake and it's surrounding forest with a dark form of magic, a kind that can only be described as witchcraft. As suddenly as she'd risen from the lake, covered in mud and kelp, she disappeared into\n\nthe reeds and the forest. The forest was dark, evil-looking and misty, though only at night, her spell making it a place of enchantment and beauty during the day.\n\nMany days. Many days had Angelica's parents and friends sought for her. They had found Juniper, all alone, coming back home after a few days. Nobody knew where she had gone with the horse, but it coming back alone had been a sign of trouble.\n\nSearch parties were sent out day after day, patrolling the region, looking for the poor Angelica, though none had found her, laying on the bottom of the damned fen, hidden between treebranches and mud. §0\n§0If anyone were to look there now however, they still\n\nwouldn't find her. Angelica was gone, was no more even. She had been reborn into a dark spectral being.§0\n§0\n\nThe sun was burning down on the soldiers and their horses, flies buzzing all around them as they rode across a small hunting path that cut the dense bushes of the woodland in half. It had been a particularly warm summer, and they'd found today was a good\n\nday to patrol the region. They came across a forest fen that laid on the hunting trail, it was covered in the beauty and be-witchery of nature's bounty, entrancing those who came across it. They walked along it's beach, that was little more than dried\n\nmud. Then, one of them noticed something in the shallow part of the water and shouted. A young woman's corpse laid floating in between the reeds, fair hair, a tattered white dress and a sickly pale skin. While they were working on getting the corpse out\n\nof the lake, a white mare suddenly appeared from the forest, completely silent. It simply stood before them, covered in mud and kelp, it's mane drenched in water. The men simply stared at it for a moment before one of them moved forth to place himself\n\non top of the horse. As soon as he sat atop it, the mare walked forth into the lake, entrancing the soldier that sat atop her. Letting him drown. §0\n§0\n§0Rather than backing away, one by one the soldiers went to sit atop the white mare each time it came back\n\nfrom the water, one by one all the soldiers became entranced. And one by one, each and every one of them drowned under the spell of the horse covered in kelp.§0\n§0\n§0They say that the kelpie, as it's become known, still roams around near the shores of lakes\n\nand other bodies of water. Waiting for any soul to come near to the waterline. Waiting for another soul to drown under it's spell...", ""),
        StaticBook("Kitab Alsalam.p2", "§bIbraheem Aladeen", "☪Chapter Twelve☪\nThe Nether\n-------------------The fire Of the Nether is the punishment of those who forsaken Allah and disobeyed him. With the drink of boiling water and tree made of pure of ash and soot bearing fruit of burning taste with sour and pain.\n\n There will be lakes and rivers of things hotter than lava yet looks of lava, Those who have disobeyed Allah, their flesh will be hung by meat hooks of red heat and they will be burned and cut and boiling blood will spray their eyes,\n\nThey will not sleep and die slowly over and over again and each time they die and come back to life it will be worse and worse. Allah gave a task to a gatekeeper and after seeing the Nether, he never smiled again.\n\nThose in the Nether will have blood-curdling screams begging Allah to free them from the Nether, but woe to them for they have disobeyed Allah and thought they could out think and trick Allah and the all knowing and all seeing.\n\nAllah says there will be a man who lived the happiest life on Earth,  we will bring him before Allah and ask him of how is life was on the Earth he will say ‘Allah has blessed me with the greatest of lives’\n\n yet this man indulge in complete sin of every kind and murdered those to be happy.Allah then takes the man and only dips him into the Nether for one second and returns him and asks ‘what happiness did you have in your life?’\n\n the man will say ‘I have had nothing of good in my life’ Allah shows us that just a second in the Nether will make anyone forget their happiness. That is the punishment of those who disobey Allah and do wrong to the world.\n\nAllah Is indeed the best of punishers and the most Just.\n-------------------☪Chapter Thirteen☪\nSeven Skies\n-------------------Allah has created the Seven Skies as a reward For Mankind and his creations.\n\n Each level being more greater than the next. In seven skies there will be gardens of which rivers flow, there will be streams were gardens will be within, there will be fruits of every kind in pairs,There will be servants Pouring drinks of juices\n\n and water as well as any drink you could wish for, even those that were forbidden in your past life. Allah will give everything to their heart's content. They will have homes of marble and the most handsome of husbands and most beautiful of wives,\n\nevery time you look away and then look back they will become even more beautiful to where in the past life you would have dropped dead for your heart could not take it. Anything your heart would desire you will be given, You will have a tree\n\nthat’s shade will spread a thousand miles, that bears the sweets and largest of fruits. Your Face will shine bright compared to the number of good deeds you have done. Allah will take jealousy and greed and ill thoughts from your mind\n\nand give you a constant happiness. You will be so happy that people will rush to Allah and beg him to bring their friends and families, and they will await happily, There will be animals of every kind tamed and happy and there will be animals you\n\nhave never seen before, But in the Seventh skie, It is the most beautiful and best of places of all creation, this is where those who have served Allah the almighty the most will be,This is where those Who have Fought in Jihad will be,\n\n this is where the martyrs will be. Allah is indeed the most merciful and most generous.\n-------------------☪Chapter Fourteen☪\nJihad and Rules of Jihad\n-------------------Jihad is one of the Greatest things a creation of Allah can do.\n\nWe have given you two Jihads, one of the mind, and one of the body. The Jihad of the mind is a struggle of tests from Allah, Allah says that ‘He who is in hardship,and pain and suffering, is one who fights Jihad’ In everyone's life they will fight a Jihad\n\n of the mind, many times. We have then Given you the Jihad Of the Body. Jihad is declared upon these things. If you have been driven from your home unjustly, If you have been invaded,\n\nIf one tries to destroy Your faith, To fight the Tyrants, to fight injustice, and to fight those who worship false gods, If they are of those who harm mankind, to fight those who oppress,  and to help the oppressed. In the Jihad\n\nThe followers of the righteous shall fight against the infidel and tyrants, fighting for Allah and Martyrdom or Victory. We have set to you rules for Jihad, So that you may not go and do wrong.\nThe followers of the righteous shall fight against\n\n the infidel and tyrants, fighting for Allah and Martyrdom or Victory. We have set to you rules for Jihad, So that you may not go and do wrong. Dont Cut a Tree unless you need to, Do not Kill a Child, Do not Kill Old People\n\n, Do not Destroy Places of Worship, Do not destroy a Building, Do not Kill those who have surrendered, Do not Kill those who run away(from battle and in general), Do not Kill a Woman, Do not Kill a Sick Person, Do not Kill those dedicated to worship\n\n(Ie. Monks and priests), Do not disfigure the dead, Do not Kill a animal except for eating, Be good to Prisoners and feed them, Do not Enforce The faith.\nThose are the rules of Jihad, When Fighting In Jihad Allah says\n\n ‘When you suffer pain they to suffer pain, But you have hope from Allah that they will never have’ Allah tells us that when you fight Allah, Do not forget to Praise him, Remind your brothers and sisters of the path of Allah,\n\n and shout together a warcry of “ALLAH IS GREAT!” When one shouts it all are required to respond.When you have Won your Battle remember to Praise Allah and have One say “TAKBIR!”\n\n and have the responding call of “ALLAH IS GREAT!” and say it three times or more, For Allah is the Granter of victories and the best of planners, and the giver of defeats.\n\n Indeed Allah Is the most Powerful, So do not forget to Answer upon Jihad for those who fight Jihad and those who died in Jihad are promised the best of homes, the best of wives and husbands, the best of the best, and a spot at dining table with Allah.\n\nThey will be given the highest of statuses and best of things in the seventh skie and they will be cared for personally by Allah himself. Allah Is indeed the best of helpers and the best of gifting.\n-------------------☪Chapter Fifteen☪\nMartyrdom\n---------\n\nWe have given you the chance of Martyrdom, The Greatest honors Allah bestows, Dining in the Path of Allah, is of greatness. Allah says to those who lose one that has become a Martyrdom ‘Think not of those who are slain in Allah's way as dead.\n\nNay, they live, finding their sustenance in the presence of their Lord; They rejoice in the bounty provided by Allah. And with regard to those left behind, who have not yet joined them (in their bliss), the (Martyrs) glory in the fact that on them\n\n is no fear, nor have they (cause to) grieve.’ So be at Ease, for those who die a martyr is, in fact, the best if people. So go to their graves and visit them and give them your salaams and salutes for they have died for Allah\n\n and your faith and give them silent prayer so that they may take the good prayer for them and present them to Allah.\nIf one is to die a martyr do not wash him of blood and leave him in his clothing,\n\n So on the day he goes before Allah, he may show his blood and his enemy's blood that he has died for his cause, put in his grave his weapons and helmet So he may stand tall as he waits to be judged and show his great sacrifice for Allah.\n\n Allah says there will one who come before Allah as a martyr and is blessed with Seven skies but the first thing he asks Allah is ‘ OH MY LORD, Send me down again so I may fight and die for you again, Allow me to die again for your path\n\n and allow me to feel the pain of death Again for your sake, so your word may remain high’ Allah would smile and laugh at the bravery  and courage and obedience and love of his servant and say ‘You Have done well, Now\n\n rest and Be happy of all the pleasures you desire! You will sit next to me at my table and be a friend To your lord!’  with this the martyr would forget all earthly things just upon hearing the great honors Allah has blessed him with and becoming\n\n the friend of Allah. So do not fear of death from an infidel, You will be given martyrdom and be given the greatest of honors. Allah is indeed the best of rewards, Truly Allah is He Who bestows the best provision.\n-------------------\n\n☪Chapter Sixteen☪\nMedicine\n-------------------We Have set upon the earth a cure for every illness and disease, Do not forbid the use of Medicine unless it is made of Alcohol and Pig.The Best of Cures Is recitation of the Holy book.\n\n Seek to learn How to help Cure all illness and disease, and to help Allah’s creations, Those who go to learn and help treat these will be granted a Special reward in seven skies that is too great to be even spoken of.\n\nAllah gives all illnesses and gives all cures and remedies, for we placed them on the earth to test you and to remind you of duty to Allah and increase your faith to Allah. Allah is indeed the all-Knowing and the best of cures.\n-------------------\n\n☪Chapter Seventeen☪\nMarriage \n-------------------We Have Created Two Genders, One Male, and One female, So that the two Can Live In Peace and Harmony and Love each other, And to raise Children together and make families.\n\nAnd to raise Children together and make families. We also tell you how to find out between the two if you both wish to marry. You must go to her home officially with friends and family of hers\n\nnot yours, and eat dinner with them, everyone will have tea but you(the man), she will then bring the tea out for you so only know you know, if she agrees to be interested in you. If the tea is bitter with salt then she does not wish to,\n\n but if it is sweet with sugar then the man may go to her oldest relative or closest friend and ask permission. We give the way on How to Perform the marriage,  The man must bring his soon to be wife into town on a camel,  as he brings the camel over,\n\n he must shout allowed his declaration of faith, he will sing about his love for allah and how he became blessed with his soon to be wife. Before he may enter the musjid, he must Show his willingness to get married,\n\n he must take 10 lashings, and he will then enter into a musjid and They tell each other their vows, the imam will then marry the two and the two will split a date fruit, eat half each, and then drink Water out of the same small bowl.\n\n When the two are married they are allowed to have a celebration, You must have at least 1 witness for the marriage to be official and have the marriage public.Once the two are married the man must go and sacrifice two sheep and give the meat to charity.\n\nWe allow you to marry others in different faith, But never change your faith, Though it will be difficult, For the child will not grow up learning the righteous way of Al’iiman Rashidun, this may be allowed But it is not recommended.\n\nWhen proposing to marry, the man or woman must ask the other’s parents, if they do not have their parents ask their oldest family member, If they have no family,   Ask a Priest to go ask for permission from that person,\n\n or ask their noble who they are under for permission. Allah Is Indeed the most loving and most compassionate.\n-------------------\n(Part 3 coming soon)", ""),
        StaticBook("Kitab Alsalam.P6", "§bIbraheem Aladeen", "☪Chapter FortySeven☪\nThe Power of Faith\n-------------------Allah makes mention of a man named Abdullah, who was well renowned in his faith and was given command of the army. Taken prisoner by a tyrant king during a\n\nbattle between the believers and the non-believers, The king Believed that Since Abdullah was a Sahabi that Abdullah had a supernatural power, so the king Thinking he had supernatural power wanted that within his bloodline. So When the\n\nking heard that they Captured Abdullah, he was so happy that he told the servants to bring Abdullah to him, After the servants brought Abdullah to the Tyrant King the king said ‘I want you to marry my daughter, But you have to Convert and\n\nrenounce your faith.’ so Abdullah said ‘No.’ The king was surprised by Abdullah Immediate answer, so the king said “Don't you want to think about it?’ ‘No.’ Abdullah would reply in a heartbeat. The king would then say ‘Marry my daughter\n\nand I will give you half my Kingdom, Only if you renounce and convert.’ ‘NO.’ Abdullah would reply swiftly again, Now the king becoming agitated he then says ‘if you don't marry my daughter and renounce your faith and convert, I will Kill\n\nyou’ Again Abdullah would refuse. So the King would tell the servants to bring a large Pot of Oil and light it with fire and the Oil got so Hot that it boiled and begin to smoke, Then the king tells the servants to bring another prisoner so the servants\n\nbrought him and the King Demanded Again for him to renounce his faith and converts and Abdullah Refuse, So the King threw the Prisoner into the Oil and the Oil was so hot that the Bones Began to stick out of the prisoner’s body. The king\n\nthen says to Abdullah ‘if you don't convert and renounce your faith then I will throw you into the boiling Oil.’ and Abdullah says ‘No, I will never surrender my faith.’ so the king ordered the guards to throw Abdullah into the Oil. As the guard\n\nwas taking Abdullah to the Oil Abdullah would begin to Cry and the King notice this so he said ‘Stop! Bring him back here.’ so the guards brought him back and the king asked him ‘Why were you crying? Is it because you will miss your wife? Is it\n\necause you will be leaving your children behind without a father? Is it because you miss your land you are from? Is it because who hold your life Precious to yourself?’ Abdullah would respond ‘La, don't think I'm crying because I fear death\n\nI'm crying because I Only have one soul and I wish I have a Hundred Soul so I can die as a Martyr a Hundred times in the path of Allah.’ this shocked the king and at this Instant the king became the captive and Abdullah was the king. So the king in\n\nshock says ‘If you kiss my forehead I would set you free.’ Abdullah would then say ‘I won't kiss your forehead Unless you free all the Prisoners and me.’ this shocked the King even More as the king looking at Abdullah’s concern about the\n\nwellbeing of the prisoner and strong in his faith. The king then Agreed, so Abdullah kisses the King forehead and the King released All of the prisoners and Abdullah. Remember Allah is always on the side of the Believers and is the best of Planners.\n-----\n\n☪Chapter FortyEight☪\nRenouncing the faith\n-------------------We Give you Warning of renouncing your faith. We promise those who flee from good and the righteous the nether and they will have the worst punishment. There\n\nwill be one on the final hour who renounced his faith and did so publicly, in which he erased all his good deeds and made all his bad deeds multiplied by 10,000 each, and that every good deed he has done after that it will be erased, for he gave up on\n\nthe truth and began the following shaitan! Their punishment will be meathooks of glowing Heat piercing their throats and rabid rats eating them from the inside, they will suffer from their limbs being ripped apart, They will have a heat hotter than\n\nthe sun and brighter than lava melting them away slowly, and then we will remake their body so they can relive it again but it will worsen each time for the rest of time.  Allah indeed punishes the ignorant and keeps his promises, and is indeed the\n\nmost just.\n-------------------☪Chapter FortyNine☪\nHoren’s Companion \n-------------------We give you a Story of the Prophet Horen and his Companion.\nHoren and His companion Hamza and Yusuf were walking, when they have gotten\n\nattacked by lions. Hamza went missing and the Prophet Horen told Yusuf ‘Go find Hamza, I can not find him anywhere.’ Yusuf went into the forest where he last seen him around and found him lying on the ground dieing...and Yusuf said ‘Oh Hamza!\n\nThe Prophet sent me to find you and see what is your condition!’ Hamza gathering his breath told Yusuf ‘Tell my Beloved Nabi(Prophet) that I am in a condition where I can smell the fragrance of seven skies….Give him my Salam(greetings)\n\nand tell him that I pray that Allah grants him the best of rewards among the prophets to come! OH, yusuf...tell my family...that if the prophet is harmed while they are fine….that I will testify to Allah against them on the day of judgment.’ he\n\nthen said his shahada and then passed away. Allah granted him Seven Skies for the Great love he had for the prophet. We give this story to show you to love your prophets we have given you, and the great love of a man even in his last moments.\n\nAllah is the most merciful and most kind.\n-------------------☪Chapter Fifty☪\nPrayer\n-------------------We Command you to pray, Once a Day so you may save yourself from the Nether.\n\nYou first must wash your body, Washing your hands halfway up your arm three times each going from right to left, then you must rinse your mouth Three times,then you breathe and sneeze water from your nose once, then you wash your\n\nface three times, The wash your feet three times each beginning from the right to left. Once you have washed yourself, cleaning all filth and sins away, you must do it every time before you pray. Then we tell you how to call to prayer. You must\n\nshout so others may come ‘Allah is great, Allah is Great...Come To Prayer, Come to Prayer, Come Pray to the Almighty, Allah Is Great, Allah Is great, There is no God But Allah!’ once you call for prayer, you have the Imam or someone more\n\nknowledgeable of the faith or if you pray by yourself lead the prayer. You Begin the prayer by saying ‘Bismillah’ and then begin folding your hands and keeping your gaze on the ground. You then recite allowed ‘Chapter Eight’ In Qalisheen\n\nwith your best voice, Throughout the entire prayer you will speak in Qalisheen. Once you have finished reciting Chapter Eight then recite any chapter from the Holy Book. After Finishing the second recitation, You say ‘Ya Allah.’ and go down\n\nonto the floor and place your head onto the ground and recite quietly to yourself where others can not here you and you say ‘One Rabb’ Three times, Once you repeated it three times Say allowed ‘Ya Allah.’ and raise your body while on your\n\nknees and say once to yourself ‘Oh Allah forgive me’ and then go down onto the floor and place your head onto the ground and recite quietly to yourself where others can not here you and you say ‘One Rabb’ Three times, Once you repeated it\n\nthree times Say allowed ‘Ya Allah.’ and then raise your body standing up again. You then Recite allowed ‘Chapter Eight’ and once you Once you have finished reciting Chapter Eight then recite any chapter from the Holy Book. After Finishing\n\nthe second recitation, You say ‘Ya Allah.’ and go down onto the floor and place your head onto the ground and recite quietly to yourself where others can not here you and you say ‘One Rabb’ Three times, Once you repeated it three times Say\n\nallowed ‘Ya Allah.’ and  raise your body while on your knees and say once to yourself ‘Oh Allah forgive me’ and then go down onto the floor and place your head onto the ground and recite quietly to yourself where others can not here you\n\nand you say ‘One Rabb’ Three times, Once you repeated it three times Say allowed ‘Ya Allah.’ raise your body while on your knees and say once to yourself ‘He is Allah(the Creator/God), the One and Only; Allah, the Eternal, Absolute; He begets\n\nnot, nor is He begotten; And there is none comparable unto Him. There is only One God and that is Allah(The Creator/God), and forever shall I follow His light’ And then you end your prayer by saying allowed turning your head to your right\n\nshoulder looking down ‘No god but Allah’ and then roll your head slowly to the left shoulder saying ‘No god but Allah’. Pray to avoid The Nether. Allah is indeed the most merciful and most kind.\n-------------------☪Chapter FiftyOne☪\nMix Breeds\n-----------\n\nWe Come to you on a Matter Of Two different Races Breeding and marriage, We have Made it a Sin worthy of the Nether For Breeding of two Different races, Yet Allah does not punish the offspring of them. We Have Given each a male and a\n\nfemale for each race, If the two different races are breeding, Do not Harm them, but Push them away and stay away from them. We Now tell you how to deal with the offspring of Mix Breeds, Treat them with respect and honour as you do with\n\nanyone else, For they had no choice in how they were born, The offspring’s race will be judged on their physical attributes, we give you an example so you may have better understanding, A Human-Elven half breed, if they are taller than a\n\nhuman, and hold pointy ears, then they will be accounted as an elf, If they are some what taller than a normal human, but is not close to the size of a elf, and does not hold pointy ears, they are human. For Allah blessed them with difficulty in life and\n\nhardship, so they are granted the same honor of martyrs seven skies IF they follow the righteous way and do not commit sin. They are free from all sin of their parents. As Followers of the righteous way, and how the book is for all of Allah's\n\ncreations, you must respect them, and do not hear harassment, for this is the word of Allah and a mercy. Allah is Indeed all Kind and most merciful.\n-------------------☪Chapter FiftyTwo☪\nAllah Many Names\n-------------------\n\nAllah has many beautiful name and should always be remembered for he is indeed The All-Compassionate, The All-Merciful, The Absolute Ruler, The Pure One, The Source of Peace, The Inspirer of Faith, The Guardian, The Victorious, The\n\nCompeller, The Greatest, The Creator, The Maker of Order, The Shaper of Beauty, The Forgiving, The Subduer, The Giver of All, The Sustainer, The Opener, The Knower of All, The Constrictor, The Reliever, The Abaser, The Exalter, The\n\nBestower of Honors, The Humiliator, The Hearer of All, The Seer of All The Judge, The Just, The Subtle One, The All-Aware, The Forbearing, The Magnificent, The Forgiver and Hider of Faults, The Rewarder of Thankfulness,\n\nThe Highest, The Greatest, The Preserver, The Nourisher The Accountant, The Mighty The Generous, The Watchful One, The Responder to Prayer, The All-Comprehending, The Perfectly Wise, The Loving One, The Majestic One, The\n\nResurrector, The Witness, The Truth, The Trustee, The Possessor of All Strength, The Forceful One, The Governor, The Praised One, The Appraiser, The Originator, The Restorer, The Giver of Life, The Taker of Life, The Ever Living One, The\n\nSelf-Existing One, The Finder, The Glorious, The Unique, The Single, The One, The Indivisible, The Satisfied of All Needs, The All Powerful,The Creator of All Power, The Expediter, The Delayer, The First, The Last, The Manifest One, The\n\nHidden One, The Protecting Friend, The Supreme One, The Doer of Good, The Guide to Repentance, The Avenger, The Forgiver, The Clement, The Owner of All, The Lord of Majesty and Bounty, The Equitable One, The Gatherer, The Rich One,\n\nThe Enricher, The Preventer of Harm, The Creator of The Harmful, The Creator of Good, The Light, The Guide, The Originator, The Everlasting One, The Inheritor of All, The Righteous Teacher, The Patient One, The King Of Kings.\n(The End!)", ""),
        StaticBook("Kitab Alsalam.P4", "§bIbraheem Aladeen", "☪Chapter TwentySeven☪\nThe Man And the Dog\n-------------------We give you the story of The Man and the Dog.\nThere was a Man who committed many sins and opposed the faith of\n\nrighteousness, It was a Hot day and he was lost in the Desert, Only having a small amount of water left. He then stumbled upon a thirsty and dying dog, He looked at the dog and felt pity for it but he could not give the dog the water with bag of water\n\nwhich he had, which was low or it would spill in the hot sand. He took his shoe off and poured it into his shoe and gave it to the dog He then died of thirst. We granted Him Seven Skies For his pity and mercy on the dog, Though he fought against us,\n\nthis small and simple deed gave him the garden within rivers. Allah is indeed the most merciful and most generous.\n------------------\n☪Chapter TwentyEight☪\nCoercion\n-------------------We warn you of Forcing those Into your faith,\n\nAllah Hates this and has promised those who force those into the faith a punishment of the unthinkable in the nether! BEWARE of coercion, for it will lead you to The nether and it will bring the wrong\n\nview of the Faith. We have made it Haram(forbidden) to coerce anyone into your faith. The one who finds the faith by themselves hearts will be shining as bright as the Sun a thousand times, Do not coercion anyone into the faith for those that do\n\nwill have the punishment of the Nether. Allah is indeed the most Just and the most wise in all affairs\n------------------\n☪Chapter Twentynine☪\nThe Great Sin Of Suicide\n-------------------\n\nWe Give you Warning Of Committing Suicide! Suicide will erase all good deeds you have done and you are promised The Nether. Those who say they commit suicide in the name of Allah, Will have the worst punishment in the nether and will\n\nrelive how they commited suicide every time they die, And we will punish them with hot glowing Irons around their throats that tightens and melts the skin and bone, We will make it unable for you to be happy or have a moment of peace, you\n\nwill be forced to drink boiling water of ash and you will be cut slowly by a dull grain of hair that will burn hotter than the Nether’s air which burns the hairs off you and begins melting your very skin, it will cut you piece by piece and then we\n\nwill put you together, we will sow your mouth with this grain of hair and every time you scream you will rip it open, and then we will sow it again, this is your punishment for committing this sin, you will never have peace and you will never\n\nbe able to breathe, you will breathe ash and your eyes will burn with the lava of blue. Allah is indeed the punisher of those who commit sin and stray away from him and the most just. Indeed Allah knows all and is the most just in all affairs.\n\n☪Chapter Thirty☪\nRules of Charity\n-------------------When you are Performing your duties and give Charity to the Poor and the needy there will rule on how to do so for Allah knows what's best, When you are handing\n\nWealth to the Poor and needy you Must have it Concealed whether in a Pouch or a chest, Do not be prideful and boast about how you gave away your Wealth For Allah hates those who Boast about fame For the Charity you have done is Between\n\nWealth to the Poor and needy you Must have it Concealed whether in a Pouch or a chest, Do not be prideful and boast about how you gave away your Wealth For Allah hates those who Boast about fame For the Charity you have done is Between\n\nknowing all praise. Indeed Allah Is the Most Merciful and most kind.\n-------------------☪Chapter ThirtyOne☪\nlaws of Slavery\n-------------------We have given you a right to hold a slave But LO! Allah has Indeed set rules upon\n\nsuch! You may buy a slave from the market or if you Captured a slave from battle or was given to you as a gift you must take care of them Dress them in your Clothing and eat with them from the same Table For All races are equal in Allah's\n\neyes, The Slave has a rights just as you for they can ask What payment they need for freedom And is Allowed to Do work for the Payment outside of your home If you allow them And you are not allowed to take that money unless it was given to\n\nyou without force but on their own free will! If the Slave Gathers his or her Payment and gives it to you, you must free them, They Are Allowed to Go Out of your Home And do as they Please Once they have finished their work, They Are\n\nAllowed to Do charity and have rights to pray to their Religion for Allah says all faiths must be respected, You cannot place a price of Freedom Over 10,000 mina they can't ever pay For you must be just and kind to them. Allah says if you break\n\nthe rule Allah set upon you the Slave will have rights of Freedom and can take you to court for breaking Allah's rules but he would need evidence to prove such! Remember For the best deed beside Jihad is freeing a Slave but remember Allah\n\nfrowns upon those who Do not care for their slaves but loves those who treat their slave with respect and honor and obey by Allah's rules for Allah is All-knowing all Praise are due to him. Allah Is Indeed the All knowing and all wise.\n-------------------\n\n☪Chapter ThirtyTwo☪\nChildren\n-------------------We Have Given you Children, to bring you joy and happiness of this life. Children Are A Blessing From Allah, Boys, And Girls. Do Not Bury your Daughters Like\n\nyou have done in the past, Your Daughters are a Greater blessing than a Boy. Allah Says ‘If you Raise Four Girls Right In manners and in the Faith, you are Granted Seven Skies As long As you don't Leave the path of righteousness.’ We Have\n\nCommanded You For Every new Born you Recite the Shahada(Testimony of Faith) The Newborn's Ear three times, And Take a date Fruit and chew a small piece and feed it to your newborn. Be caring And do not Discard your Children! We Also\n\nyou to Adopt Orphans And Do not force them to Convert, But have them live the lifestyle Of a Follower of righteousness, Have them grow with the morals and mind of a follower of right. Those Who Adopt are Beloved Of Allah and a close\n\nfriend of Allah. Raise them To be young active members of their community and Raise them to be the Most respectful and most kind, Raise them to be kind and honorable. Allah is indeed the Most merciful and most kind.\n-------------------\n\n☪Chapter ThirtyThree☪\nFealty Of A Leader to Allah\n-------------------We Have Given You Leaders, To lead you and Help your Nation And Raise the Banner Of Righteousness. They Must Swear Publicly Before their People and Say\n\nthe Shahada(Testimony of Faith) three time Aloud, They Then Are Given A sword Which they will Kiss and set it upon their forehead three times, They will then be given their Nation’s flag folded and they will kiss it and place it on their forehead\n\nthree times, they will then be given the Holy Book and they will kiss it and set it upon their forehead three times, the will then place their hand on the holy book and recite their vows to their nation and allah the almighty saying ‘I swear to protect\n\nthe weak, the old, the cripple, and the man who works the fields. I swear to Uphold the Book of Allah and follow Allah laws and preserve Justice to our lands and others, I will fight in the path of Allah and I will protect my People from this day\n\nto the end of my Days May Allah guide me and never let me Falter and Follow the wrong path, I swear by Allah this is my promise’ and thus he is a leader of your nation. Allah is Indeed the King Of Kings And the Best of leaders.\n-------------------\n\n☪Chapter ThirtyFour☪\nFealty Of A Imam/Dervish/Grand Imam to Allah\n-------------------We have given you Priests Of your faith, they all Swear to Allah and In order to become an official Priest they must be given from the Main Leader Of The Nation\n\nOf faith or That Of A Priest, They Must Swear Publicly and Say the Shahada(Testimony of Faith) three time Allowed, They will then Be given a White Turban and they will kiss it and place it on their forehead three times and then\n\nplace it on their heads, they will then be given the Holy Book and they will kiss it and set it upon their forehead three times, the will then place their hand on the holy book and recite their vows to allah the almighty saying ‘I Swear By Allah That I\n\nwill Teach, Preach And follow Allah’s Orders. I will study Allah’s holy book, Allah guides me and never let me Falter and Follow the wrong path, I swear by Allah this is my promise’ And thus He will be a Priest of the righteous faith. Allah\n\nis the Almighty and most powerful.\n-------------------☪Chapter ThirtyFive☪\nThe Deeds of Eating and drinking properly\n-------------------Allah has placed on this earth food and water for you to clench your needs and\n\nthing on earth you should not eat such as pig, Boar, and Alcohol. Lo! Allah sent another gift to you that you may earn good deeds for eating properly Allah is All knowing and deserve All praises, When drinking you take three sips and not in\n\ngulps Allah says that for indeed Gulping drinks can Damage your body and make you unhealthy so drink Properly, Allah says you should chew your food for if you do not Allah says that to can Cause problems for your Body and eat with your\n\nmouth close Allah did not create you so you may eat like a pig instead he made you so you may be the most Honorable creation and the most respected. Allah is Indeed the most merciful and most generous. \n-------------------\n\n☪Chapter ThirtySix☪\nNashud\n-------------------We Gift You A way To Be Creative, To Express your Love For Allah And your Faith. We Call It Nashud, Where You Sing Of things you love of Allah, His\n\nProphets, His Gifts, His Soldiers of Allah, those who represent your faith, your heroes, your leaders, And Everything He had made. Be Proud When You Say Nashud And say it with your best voice, Be Happy and Proud of your faith, Do not\n\nReplace Zikr With Nashud, For Zikr reminds you of Allah. Allah Indeed Knows All, And is All-wise and all kind. Allah is indeed the best of helpers and the most merciful.\n-------------------☪Chapter ThirtySeven☪\nImportance of Mothers\n-------------------\n\nAllah has placed upon this earth your mother Who bore you and taken care of you when you were but a child and Allah bless those mothers with Holy Love for their children for Allah loves those who love their mothers, Allah Says ‘Lo! I have\n\nplaced the Seven Skies under your mother's feet! So don't disrespect her and don't abuse your mothers love, for surely if your mothers angry with you I am Angry at you!’ And Allah places another blessing Upon you for the Easiest way to the seven\n\nSkies is your mother so don't disrespect her. Allah Is indeed the All-knowing and all kind and wise.\n-------------------☪Chapter ThirtyEight☪\nImportance of Peace\n-------------------\n\nRemember That you are all Brothers and Sisters and how Allah has created you so you may Worship him and praise him for his mercy upon you, Allah created you so you may show others the Mercy of Allah. Lo! He did not create you so you may\n\nCause Corruption and evil throughout land and that you Shed your brothers and sisters Blood For Allah Surely has to Punish those with nethers for Eternity, Allah Loves those who stop Violence and the ones who stand for peace in times of Evil\n\nBut remember Allah does not condemn those who fight in self-defence or fight against Corruption and Haraam For Allah loves those who fight in Jihad for Peace and the destruction of Evil. Allah is indeed the most compassionate and the best at\n\nplacing peace.\n-------------------(part 5 soon! ik ik this is a big book!)", ""),
        StaticBook("Poetry V1", "§bJaya Jayamen", "Poetry\n\n          ~Originally by\n       Sofetios Jayamen\n\nCOURAGE\n\nIt is a thing you use\nWhen you can't go to the end,\nWhen all seems lost\nAnd you can't defend.\n\nYou use it as\nIt combines with your will,\nAll you need to do is\nLet it give its fill.\n\nThe choice is yours,\nGive in or go,\nThough in the end\nOnly you will know.\n\nSee with your spirit\nAnd not with fear,\nfor then you will know\nThat courage is here.\n\nTHE DREAMER\n\nThe Dreamer,\nThe one who dares not be the same,\nFor in dreams mysteries unravel,\nAnd endless space you do travel,\nAs your dreams you try to tame.\n\nAs the Dreamer,\nDreams above the sky,\nAnd looks down below,\nTo the people that show,\nWho know not what lies that high.\n\nUnawakened, the Dreamer,\nIn a maze of thoughts,\nWandering the mists,\nWith endless twists,\nAs the path on minds paper he jots.\n\nThough be wary dreamer,\nAs thoughts tend to run away,\nOnly the ones you really need,\nAnd the ones you often feed,\nAre the ones that often stay.\n\nTHE LAKE\n\nI wander upon a path by a lake,\nWondering where it’s all gone.\nEvery day I used to come here,\nFrom the morning to the evening's yawn.\n\nEvery now and again I wonder,\nWhy the days have passed.\nAnd think very deeply,\nWhy they don't seem to last.\n\nDay by day, night by night,\nThe Lake becomes smaller still.\nThe thoughts of it become thinner,\nEven to my strongest will.\n\nIt has become ten times smaller and ten times shallower,\nEven thought it has not changed.\nTo other people it might be normal,\nbut to me it is considered strange.\n\n\nFRIEND OR ENEMY?\n\nEverywhere I am\nI hide from your sight,\nIf it's in the day,\nAnd especially at night.\n\nI am one of sleep's worst enemies,\nAnd one of fear's best friends,\nI grow ever more larger,\nAs your will begins to bend.\n\nIn the day I am more friendly,\nEspecially when its hot and I'm in sight,\nBut when it turns to night time,\nI'm sure to give you a fright.\n\nI am a mimic of sorts,\nI try to copy you while you walk,\nI even mimic other people,\nAlthough I cannot talk.\n\nEven when you go about the day,\nI skulk and kind of stalk,\nFear or fear not, I am always here,\nI am the shadow on which you walk.\n\nTHE COBBLER AND THE CROW\n\nI was working in the night,\nAs I bent over a shoe,\nI was working very hard,\nto finish before the morning dew.\n\nI was just about finished,\nWhen what was this I hear?\nA tapping, slight tapping,\nAnd it seemed to be so near.\n\nI turned to the window,\nAnd what did I see?\nA crow tapping at my glass,\nStaring at me.\n\n\"Go away.\" I said,\nSternly as I did stand.\n\"Don't you know I have work to do?\"\nThough I know it didn't understand.\n\nBut the crow kept tapping at the glass,\nAnd I began to get mad,\nThis crow just would not stop,\nNot even a tad.\n\nI turned to my unfinished shoe,\nTo work as long as I could bear,\nBut then I noticed something missing,\nThat would stop me from completing the pair.\n\nThe golden lace that I needed,\nFor this order to be complete,\nI couldn't find it anywhere,\nAs the glass the crow did beat.\n\nI checked my table, checked my pockets,\nAnd then to my surprise,\nThere was a hole in one,\nThat was just the right size.\n\nI would never finish this shoe,\nBy the morning light,\nNow things were dire,\nand my situation was quite tight.\n\n\"I must have dropped it,\nOn the way back from the store!\"\nBut it was too far I thought,\nAs my confidence tore.\n\nBut then I realized \"What's this?\"\n\"Where was the tapping I couldn't bare?\"\nI looked to the window,\nAnd the crow wasn't there.\n\nI went to the window,\nAnd what was in its place?\nIt was simple and divine,\nThe golden lace.\n\nI opened the window,\nAnd took it with care,\nBecause of who gave this gift,\nI was certainly aware.\n\nI went to my table,\nAnd finished the shoe.\nBut then thought of the crow,\nIf I only knew!\n\nI then went to bed,\nWith not much I could say,\nI only did hope,\nThe crow would come back some day.\n\nIMPRINT\n\n\nI stand in a forest,\nOne that I know quite well,\nWhere the trees are tall,\nAnd they never do fall,\nAt least that's what I like to tell.\n\nI came here,\nWhen I was a boy,\nUsually in the day,\nBut any time I would say,\nThe forest was my favorite toy.\n\nI came here again,\nA few years ago,\nIt was the same place I knew well,\nAs far as I could tell,\nThere was nothing different to show.\n\nI open my eyes now,\nTo see the trees,\nMy eyes see an empty place,\nAs if leaving no trace,\nThough this is not what my mind sees.", ""),
        StaticBook("Kairi The Znaga", "§bKairi", "The Greatest Female Slave Under U'la's Rule\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nTimes were looking grim in the orclands. Female znagas would come and go, with their sassy, childlike voices echoing off the high towers of the Rex's palace as they screamed.\n\nFor some reason, every female znaga that set foot in the orclands felt the need to talk back to their masters. They would refuse to work, sit around all day, and cry out loud.\nBasically, they were like toddlers.\n\nThen, seemingly out of nowhere, came Kairi.\nAt first she had stood up for herself, trying to take on the famous Wargoth Orgoth Braduk.\n\nWhat a fucking fool she was. As fast as the fight had began, it had ended; a punch to her skull knocking her out\n\ncold. Kairi was promptly chained, and her time as an orc znaga had begun.\n\nThe stigma following female znagas was surely not a good one. Most expected Kairi to be just that, a total bitch.\n\nFrom the ashes of slavery rose a\n\npowerful Kharajyr, one whos name would surely go down in orc history -- at least to the znagas.\n\nShe grew to be a notable slave, serving beside Cohan.\n\nAs she assisted in making Rex U'la'yar thousands upon\n\nthousands of mina, she began to gather respect from the orcs.\n\nLegend says that she is still a slave to this day, but perhaps we will never know.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis book is totally not exaggerated in any way.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "For poetry, ideas and songs, by Kardryn Oranor.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\"The best way to have a good idea is to have a lot of ideas.\"\n\n1. Waterskins.§0\n§0\n§0Yesterday I was selling some of my handmade waterskins. One man was wanting a custom made one. I said it was possible, but he was very demanding. §0\n§0\n§0Therefore I told the man:\n\n\"You can have it good, you can have it cheap and you can have it fast. Pick two.\"§0\n§0\n§0He told me I was a wise young man and paid for his waterskin.\n\n2. Enchanting Forest§0\n§0\n§0I enjoy strolling along the narrow path, §0\n§0As it meanders through the forest.§0\n§0It generates a feeling of relaxation, §0\n§0And puts my troubled mind to rest.§0\n\nThe forest is peaceful and quiet.§0\n§0I appreciate its immense cover of shade, §0\n§0And I feel focused and comfortable§0\n§0In this sanctuary nature has made.§0\n\nI feel a sense of enchantment§0\n§0In the cool, refreshing air, §0\n§0As I seek the hidden secrets§0\n§0That the forest had to bear.\n\nI hear the strange sounds of the forest§0\n§0As I quietly make my way, §0\n§0And stop to observe the wonders§0\n§0Nature unfolds for me this day.\n\nI enjoy strolling along the narrow path, §0\n§0It brings a welcome peace of mind to me.§0\n§0I thank the forces of nature§0\n§0For this moment of soothing serenity.\n\n3. San mali§0\n§0\n§0Haesiea tir'id ehya prenu danta, nam ha ana heya nae dil, unya ha ana akaleh'ii ha.§0\n§0\n§0Forget the risk and take the fall, if it is what you want, then it is worth it.\n\n4. My Flower§0\n§0\n§0My flower is so wonderful and sweet,§0\n§0I'd want her to never leave my side,§0\n§0She's planted deep inside my heart,§0\n§0My flower is a special friend,§0\n§0So wonderfully truthful too.§0\n\nMy flower is a special friend,§0\n§0Like the one I have in you.\n\n5. Marching song for the Virarim I§0\n§0\n§0Down by the river,§0\n§0We took a little walk,§0\n§0Ran into a White Rose,§0\n§0And had a little talk.§0\n§0\n§0We pushed him, §0\n§0We shoved him,§0\n§0We threw him in the river,§0\n§0And laughed as he drowned.\n\nWe don't need a White Rose hanging around.§0\n§0\n§0Hey don't be a fool,§0\n§0Somebody said we were number two.(They lied)§0\n§0We're number one,§0\n§0VIRARIM!§0\n§0\n§0Alternates White Rose:§0\n§0Void Mage, Frost Witch.\n\n6. Tinuviel§0\n§0\n§0How very lovely§0\n§0\n§0Is the nightingale's singing§0\n§0\n§0Yet swans have no voice\n\n7. An Ocean Blue§0\n§0\n§0There's a lot off stuff to tell you§0\n§0To lie about, there's even more §0\n§0A lot of dirt around to dig in§0\n§0Burning way down to the core§0\n§0To be better than before\n\nAn ocean blue, the pain away§0\n§0Guess it's true, what they say§0\n§0Change your mood, everyday§0\n§0Ocean blue... to take the pain away§0\n§0\n§0Oh please, take the pain away§0\n\nIf there's anything I'd wish for§0\n§0Before the wishing well dries out§0\n§0Is that I won't outlive my children§0\n§0Though when all is said out loud§0\n§0Let they be fine without\n\nIf there's an ocean to escape in§0\n§0Where you'd never be alone§0\n§0Well I've been beggin' to stop crying, pretty please\n\nCause I'm so tired of being scared§0\n§0and I've been crawling for too long§0\n§0I'll get up out of the dirt§0\n§0and I'll be strong\n\nIf there's an ocean to escape in§0\n§0Drift away from jealousy§0\n§0Love to dream and to awake in§0\n§0An ocean blue, for you and me\n\nAn ocean blue, the pain away§0\n§0I guess it's true what they say§0\n§0Change your mood every day§0\n§0Ocean blue, please take the pain away§0\n§0\n§0The pain away\n\n8. Legacy§0\n§0\n§0Many of us are concerned about our legacies.§0\n§0What is a legacy you ask me?§0\n§0It's planting seeds in a garden you'll never get to see.\n\n9. Death§0\n§0\n§0Death doesn't discriminate between the sinners and the saints, it takes and it takes and it takes, and we keep living anyway.", ""),
