        StaticBook("BW Pass - Gothar", "§bDarius", "FREE TRAVEL PERMIT\n------------------\nThe bearer of this permit, GOTHAR, is not to be halted within the town by the Belvitz Watch under the standard order of halting and interrogating Orcs.\n\n~ Maer-Commandant\n             Darius", ""),
        StaticBook("BW Pass - Wyssek", "§bDarius", "FREE TRAVEL PERMIT\n------------------\nThe bearer of this permit, WYSSEK, is not to be halted within the town by the Belvitz Watch under the standard order of halting and interrogating Orcs.\n\n~ Maer-Commandant\n             Darius", ""),
        StaticBook("Contracts", "§bSighard", "PROOF OF PURCHASE\n\n\n I,  Sighard Cathwulf.  Pledge the service of the  Bears of the Bolin Wood. For the sum of 10,000 minas. To be used within the conflict of revenge against the Crown of Renatus-Marna.\n\n  Sighard Cathwulf.\n\n PROOF OF PURCHASE\n\n I,  Sighard Cathwulf  pledge the service the true claimants of the Renatus-Marna crown. That of the blood of the sparrow, named 'Roland'. Also promised with the procurement of 20,000 minas.\n  Sighard Cathwulf\n\n PROOF OF PURCHASE\n\nI,  Sighard Cathwulf,  pledge of the services of the Holt Butchers for the sum of 8,000 minas for the reclaiming of the Renatus-Marna Crown underneath the 'Sparrow' Claimaint.\n\n Sighard Cathwulf.", ""),
        StaticBook("Contracts", "§bBartholomew", "PROOF OF PURCHASE\n\n I, Bartholomew of Rhysten , pledge the services of the Gwynon Dragons for the sum of 15,000 minas. All to help in the reclamation of the Renatus-Marna Crown for the 'Sparrow' Claimaint.\n\n  Bartholomew of Rhysten\n\n RESPONSE TO CONTACT PURCHASE\n\n The Gwynon Dragons do not wish to take part in such a contract. Breaking the Sovereignity of the Atlasian Crown will result in war. I spit upon you and the Sparrow Claimaints.\n\n- Rhys 'Fireblood' of Gwynon\n\n PROOF OF PURCHASE\n\n  I,   Bartholomew of Rhysten  pledge the services Hachi Demons to slaughter the supernatural menace linked to the Renatus-Marna crown. As discovered by Adeon of Rhoswen for the bounty of 8,500 minas\n  Bart of Rhysten\n\n PROOF OF PURCHASE\n Two Hundred and Fourty Ships\n I,  Bartholomew of Rhysten will hire the Vanheimian Naval Forces for transport to Atlas. War-time expenses for 20,000 minas upon acceptance.\n\n  Bart of Rhysten\n\n PROOF OF PURCHASE\nTO-Arabella Entweser\n\nI,  Bartholomew of Rhysten sanction the assassination of Ser Carolvac and Arch Chancellor, Charles Elliot for the combined sum of 15,000 minas. Method - Accidental.\n Bart of Rhysten", ""),
        StaticBook("Secret Journal", "§bZaos Sylvar", "My new neighbor is the most beautiful girl i have ever seen, i spent some time with her and and she taught me some things and i bought her a silver ring and necklace but i don't think she is going to be easy to getwith her.I might just give up.....", ""),
        StaticBook("In Regards", "§bVanya Damaer", "To Mali’thill Sylvar,§0\n§0\n§0My mailbox contained a book that I had not ordered. Upon examination of the cover, I noticed it has your name upon it’s binding along with the word private. I assure you I have not placed my eyes upon its contents. I have\n\nreturned it to your care. Please make sure not to leave it laying about so carelessly that someone might take it and read it. §0\n§0\n§0May Larihei smile upon you,§0\n§0- Vanya Damaer", ""),
        StaticBook("Picture", "§bVulmar", "A small picture of a smiling duo, appearing worn by the years.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Laethis Izalith§0\n§0-§0\n§0&§0\n§0-§0\n§0Chaolnia Tahn'thill", ""),
        StaticBook("Orders", "§b[!]", "ORDERS FOR ORDERMAN TARROW OF THE 3RD BANNER§0\n§0-------------------Orderman, your orders are as follows;§0\n§0\n§0You are to infiltrate the invaders' stronghold, which appears to be named Markev. The method of this infiltration\n\nmay be determined by you. Your orders are to enter the city without notice. Lord Arcanist Haevolt has confirmed the Oathstone has been forged into a sword that now lies in the city. You are to obtain this sword; failing that, information on its location.\n\nThe rest of the 3rd Banner will follow shortly. Suceed, Orderman; for Atlas' sake.§0\n§0\n§0Issued by LORD EXECUTIONER CHARO, Commander of the 3rd Banner", ""),
        StaticBook("Fix the Pothole!", "§bCaulder Marsk", "I know not where the pothole on Soothsayer's square came from, but it is a considerable hazard, especially considering its close proximity to the sewers. A sudden collapse could prove dangerous for both the surrounding area and any passerby.", ""),
