        StaticBook("Worker Menu", "§bAlex Dering", "- Crossroads Inn -§0\n§0   and Tavern Menu§0\n§0 §0\n§0\n§0Bartender/Barmaiden          Reference\n\nFood Items§0\n§0\n§0\n§0- Bread - Two mina§0\n§0\n§0- Fish - Four mina§0\n§0\n§0- Potato - Four mina\n\nHard Alcoholic Drinks§0\n§0\n§0\n§0- Five Mina -\n\nNon-Alcoholic Drinks§0\n§0\n§0\n§0- Four Mina -\n\nAles and Wine§0\n§0\n§0\n§0- Five mina -\n\nSpecial Brews§0\n§0\n§0\n§0- Ten mina -\n\nToday's Special§0\n§0\n§0\n§0- Eight mina -\n\n\n§0\n§0\n§0Written 14th of the Grand Harvest, 1700§0\n§0by Alex Dering and Claudia Zey", ""),
        StaticBook("Restock", "§bClaudia Zey", "Stuff We need a restock on:§0\n§0\n§01. 2 Stacks Carrion Black§0\n§02. 1 Stack Cream Beer§0\n§03. 1 Stack Champagne§0\n§04. Annabella's Pale Ale§0\n§05. 1 Stack of Billy's Flavored Soda§0\n§06. 1 Stack Strawberry Ale§0\n§07. Meadowsweet Beer(1 stack)\n\nFood:§0\n§02 Stacks Porkchops§0\n§02 Stacks Bread§0\n§0Egil and I can go fishing later, so we will take care of that.§0\n§01 Stack of Steak\n\n2 Stacks VOdka§0\n§02 Stacks Whiskey§0\n§01 Stack Brandy§0\n§02 Stacks Rum§0\n§01 Stack Stout Ale§0\n§01 Stack Pale Ale§0\n§01 Stack Ruby Ale§0\n§03 Stacks Water Bottles§0\n§02 Stacks Green Tea§0\n§01 Stack Black Tea§0\n§02 Stacks Hot Cocoa§0\n§02 Stacks Juice\n\n Gracias for hopefullly doing thi, but we are very low on supplies.§0\n§0\n§0-Your (I BETTER BE THE DAMN FAVORITE I TOOK TIME TO WRITE THIS BOOK) Favorite Bartender, §0\n§0 Claudia", ""),
        StaticBook("gracias mi amigo", "§bClaudia Zey", "STUFF FOR A RESTOCK:§0\n§0\n§0Vodka(64)§0\n§0Rum(64)§0\n§0Whiskey(64)§0\n§0Red Wine(64)§0\n§0White Wine(64)§0\n§0Golden Ale(64)§0\n§0Ruby Ale(64)§0\n§0Stout Ale(64)§0\n§0Green Tea(64)§0\n§0Hot Chocolate(64)§0\n§0-->\n\nBrandy(64)§0\n§0Apple Juice(64)§0\n§0Champagne(64)§0\n§0Carrion Black(128)§0\n§0\n§0if i think of anything else, ill pm you. Thanks!§0\n§0\n§0-Imagine_May", ""),
        StaticBook("Some Recipes", "§bNikoru Shuroda", "Recipes for you to use.\nI made them myself...\nHope you like them, even went through the trouble of creating and baking them all myself.\nI also taste tested them all, but the sole taste depends on how great of a cook you are..\n-Nikky\n\nRecipe 1\n~~~~~~~~\n1 Flounder\nCook it thoroughly. Once cooked cut it up into 4 pieces and set them in a + sign formation. \n~~\n1 Apple\nSlice the apple into pieces.\n\nThen place each apple slice on either side of the flounder slices around the plate.\n\nThe left over apple slices can be used to create apple sauce in which you shall put in the center of the plate.\nI'll leave naming this dish up to you.\n\nRecipe 2\n~~~~~~~~\n2 flounders\nCook both,\nand set them side by side on the plate.\n~~\n4 potatos\nCook all four and place 2 on either side of the flounders.\n\n1 loaf of bread.\ntake the loaf of bread and slather butter on it and place it between the flounders.\n\nI'll leave naming this dish up to you aswell.\n\n(( I know i'm not that great at coming up with recipes. but cut me some slack, it's not everyday i do this. E for effort. ))", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Chapter 1: Future§0\n§0\n§0I know he's ashamed. I know he doesn't care but.. I care. I care so much. I want to feel his hugs again. I want to feel that kindness behind that cold icy stare. He looked at me and realized I... wasn't completely gone. I was still\n\nthere, barely grasping on.§0\n§0\n§0The endless mocking, the beatings, the fears. They all surrounded me so quickly after I wanted to bring others joy.§0\n§0\n§0They all turned on me but he... He helped me. He loved me.. Even if it was just for a bit and even now I\n\ncan't help but... feel safe. Feel welcomed whenever I hear his name. He may have gotten rid of me. He may not love me anymore but he was my father. My first REAL father.§0\n§0\n§0And I love him. Even if he hurts me I can't help but feel safe as his fist connects\n\nwith my face. Something is sseriously wrong with me. No matter how many times... he hurts me. I keep fighting... hoping... dreaming... I could be the son he always wanted to be before I went in too deep. §0\n§0\n§0I'm too far gone now. There's no saving me. I'm\n\nhopeless. This is torture, father. This is so much agonizing torture. I can't stop fighting. No matter how many times I fall I just keep getting right back up again.§0\n§0\n§0I found what I needed when it was too late. I thank you though, father. I thank you for\n\nevery single thing you've done. I know I can never make you proud but I... I'm going to try.§0\n§0\n§0[!] The letter would get more twisted from this point forward.§0\n§0\n§0Did you get my note? The one that said the world was going to be mine? Let me correct myself...\n\nThe world is mine.§0\n§0\n§0\n§0It belongs to me. It always had and I never realized it.§0\n§0\n§0I created this world for me. I created this own hell for myself but I had help. I was so stubborn, not listening to the ones that were trying to get me out of the own grave I\n\nwas digging. I'm sorry, papa. I'm so, so sorry. Papa, please forgive me. I'm trying. I'm trying so hard.. I can't do it without you. I'm weak, I'm so weak.. Morgan, please hold me and tell me everything will be alright like before. That's all I could ever\n\nwant right now. I know you're never coming back and I'm not okay with that.. I can't win this war. I feel so alone, so helpless. I want to vomit my brains out but most importantly...§0\n§0\n§0\n§0I want to have a future where I can be happy.\n\nAll I do is suffer... I've attempted to end my life too many times and It was stupid of me. I just... I'm so alone. I just need... someone. Anyone.. To save me from this fucking hell.§0\n§0\n§0I can't stop causing a scene. I can't stop acting out. It's like I'm\n\ntrying to call out for help but I don't know how. I don't know how to set my heart free.§0\n§0\n§0My heart aches. My head is pounding. §0\n§0\n§0[!] This next part is written in different handwriting§0\n\nThere's Hope for me, I am who I am, I am the best version of me, I can be better, I am good enough, I am special, I am kind, I am caring, I am not alone.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "- When performing evocation one must form the evocated element in the void and then draw it out by will. - Arcane evocation is a lot like other evocation except for the fact that it uses arcane gas from the void and is much more shapable.\n\n- An evocationist must be 'attuned' to their element, knowing how it feels and it's scientific properties. It also must act like it would in the real world. Fire evocation is just like regular fire, so it will at the same.\n\n- Conjuration involves pulling objects and even creature from the void.§0\n§0\n§0[!] A diagram would show a picture of a voidal horror.§0\n§0\n§0- A conjurist must know the thing they are conjuring inside and out.\n\n- The void is a realm of infinite potential. However, it is almost paradoxically comprised of nothing.§0\n§0- One must not overstep their boundaries and mana pools as that may render them unconscious or even killed.\n\n- A person drawing from the void must have some connection to that source or any other source they cast from via a mana anchor.§0\n§0- We learn magic because it is our duty to teach others.\n\n[!] A pictogram sketch fills the page. Several runes are written in subtext below.\n\n===================FIRE EVOCATION§0\n§0===================[!] A sketch of a flame was on the page. §0\n§0\n§0- Study the flame, how it moves, acts, etc.", ""),
        StaticBook("Karl's Chronicle", "§bKarl Silverblade", "The History of the\n   Silverblade Family\n       as told by\n    Karl Silverblade\n      Written 1700\n\nPreface\n-=-=-=-=-\nThis is a collection of the history of the Silverblade family that descends from Javert Silverblade. These are just a collection of stories that I have been told from my father and brother as well as my own. I hope to expand as\n\nthe ages progress, but I am starting these now as a way of preserving the history before it is lost to time. I hope my descendants continue the tradition, but I can do little more than hope and attempt to persuade their actions.\n\nLuminous\n-=-=-=-=-\nFather seldom spoke of Luminous, and what I do remember from our days in High Rock is foggy. He spent many a day in his office, designing more of the keep, or on a business trip to Holm or Belvitz. From our few interactions I got the\n\npicture that he was a stern and duty driven man. There was only one event that I remember clearly of the man which was his falling out with my father. Once they had parted ways and returned the keep to the hands of the greedy dwarves of Holm, Javert took\n\nmy brother Caine with him and I was meant to as well, but I was stolen away in the night by one of Luminous's associates. We met with his caravan as it headed off to start his next project, but it was attacked by bandits and in an effort to to get away,\n\nhe drove his wagon forward as the one I was being kept in was ransacked. I had managed to make a break for the treeline, and hideout, but I was lost from civilization for a decade of living off nature and lost from family for a few years more than that.\n\nJavert\n-=-=-=-\nJavert's life began as a bastard living in a small woodland town to a human woman, and a father he would not meet until well after he had become a man. He struck origionally as a man hounting bounties, but then he was hired for a\n\nmerchant ship. He spent a few weeks along a few shipping lanes before his sheep was marooned upon a small island off the coast of Norland. He was the sole survivor, and was trapped there for multiple weeks before he had recieved a vision. The Creator\n\nhimself had visited Javert in the form of a ball of light. The ball saved his life by pointing him in the direction of an old smuggler's outpost. This assistance did not come without a cost. In order to seal his bond of eternal servitude to the Creator,\n\nhe slashed out his left eye. Now I know not the full validated of this story, but this was the story he spoke of whenever questioned as to why his eye was missing. Once he had returned to land, he worked odd jobs before meeting with one Luminous\n\nSilverblade. Fate had unknowingly brought this bastard son back to his father. They had plans to contruct a keep upon the islands within the bay of Belvitz, but that was eventually shut down by the government. They were without a home, so they travelled\n\nsouth east, to the plateaus of Holm. Construction of High Rock began without the permission of either Holm or Courland who both laid claim to the lands and keep. Holm eventually won full control of the lands, and High Rock was forced to swear fealty or\n\nface destruction. Little did any party learn that they had caught the attention of another third party, a tribe living beneath the keep within the mountain itself. Shortly after Javert made contact with the All Mother and her people, and nine months later\n\na set of twins was born. Javert spent his time governing High Rock before following the advice of Luminous and giving control of the keep up to Holm. The business ventures did not pan out, and Javert was forced to turn to drinking in order to cope with\n\nhis sorrows and it eventually led to his death when he wandered into the woods in a drunked stopor, and never returned.\n\nThe All Mother\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-\nAlthough never officially married, Javert and the tribal All Mother had five children together. The first two came as a set of twins and the final three all died before the age of six. I know not much of the\n\nAll Mother's past other than she had been leading her cave dwelling tribe since she was a young girl, and Caine and I's height comes mainly from her as she was 7'2. My memories of my mother are only those of training to be a warrior as we spent the rest\n\nof our time within High Rock keep learning the ways of nobility and civilized society. For how little affection she shared for my brother and I, her training helped us survive the trying times that followed our father's apparent suicide. She and her tribe\n\nvanished one day before my brother and I were able to remake a connection. At this point they have likely been exterminated by either some racist soldier types or a cave in or any other plausible end.\n\nCaine\n-=-=-\nCaine was born 44 years ago. The exact date is unknown as our mother's people did not keep records of the date, and only revealed our birth a month or two after we had been born. Caine was always the more dependant of us, a fact that may\n\ncome as a shock to people that had known him. He cared more about the affection and acceptance of our parents than had I. I focused more on my own studies and advancement. When we went out on a hunt, he captured the deer because he wanted to impress the\n\nAll Mother and Javert, and caught the biggest deer I could find because I wanted to. Catching the biggest deer would get me the most money, and I could have more to eat. When he drew a map he wanted to show that he could draw a map, I drew the maps\n\nbecause I wanted to know the landscape. He stayed with Javert after the fall of High Rock. He spent his time doing work hunting criminals and working under many alliases. He worked under the name Lestat, Javert, and his own name of Caine. He found the\n\ngroup Camis with Antanios Rutledge, Bolon, and Axel Swale. They worked to fight undead and protect the innocent. He heard of my survival in a far southern town, and decided to take the trip to bring me back to High Rock. This would be his last journey as\n\na blizzard set in as we were returning. We were forced to make camp and we were attacked on the third day of camp. Fifteen men were slain that day, and Caine was among them. He made me swear to protect the families of High Rock and deliver a set of\n\nletters to the Rutledge family. He was buried with his sword and his banner wrapped around his body.\n\nKarl\n-=-=-\nAs stated previously, Caine and I were born 44 years ago, but due to our family's lack of record keeping, we knew not the exact date of our birth. After the fall of High Rock and escape from bandits, I spent my days living in the woods in the\n\nfar south for nearly a decade. I survived off the land, scavenged for wild produce and hunted whenever I could. I was discovered by a hunting party that took me back to their village where I lived for the next few years. The news of my existance had\n\ntraveled back to High Rock which had been repurchased by Caine. He heard of me, and decided to make the perilous journey to bring me back. After his demise I started the journey back, but I knew not where to go other than High Rock, but a brief stint in\n\na prison and a sometime spent working an old quarry in allowed me the funds to complete the journey. However, once the journey was complete, it had been twenty years, and Antanios had been killed, High Rock obliterated, and Camis abolished. A new chapter\n\nwas starting, and I know not where it will lead", ""),
