        StaticBook("Contract", "§bThe Bergentrückung", "I Ajax Ironwood II otherwise known as Ajax Steelheart, or Bergentruckung hereby sell the property of Stautan Alley Nr 2 to Ulrick Vontuk for a value of one hundred mina.", "")
    )

    private fun _ATLAS_17(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Muhammad Hamza Mocmood's \"Book\"§0\n§0===================Day 1: Today was good day we moved into the city. I found a Book and Quill. Inside it said \"Erwin\" \"160\" \"Elf\". Odd to know someone else lived here. Anyways King Cauis I Is talking to some men about\n\nBastion And other things. We have big plans, And we have alot of work to do.§0\n§0===================END DAY.\n\n===================DAY SKIP§0\n§0===================§0\n§0WE HAVE FOUND ARE SELFS IN SOME WEIRD PLANE! WE PUT ON WEIRD HEMS NOW WERE HERE ILL KEEP YOU UPDATED\n\nDay ?idk?§0\n§0===================We have moved out of about four citys now we have new land we move there soon. We are moving are items there soon. hope to keep up to date.§0\n§0Lets say its day 100\n\nDay 300? idk bro§0\n§0===================§0\n§0We have ESCAPED the island of AXIOS§0\n§0we have made it to new lands and the GODS have given me my bOOK BACK!!!!!§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0we shall recap on next page>>\n\nSTARED with the holy WESTERLANDS is where atlest me old muhammad lived first. I had PRENKUS CAUIS Sir ROBERT the FAT monk§0\n§0and KONK the GOBLIN RATTIGAN...§0\n§0\n§0we had fat plans of massive LAND for monk PRENKUS but before we could start the plan-\n\nLORD CAUIS I was \"MURDERED\" sending the kINGDOM in to SHOCK!!@!@!@ soon AFTER the fat fkn UNDEAD ATTACKED THE WESTERLANDS AND STOLE IT ALL IN UNDER 7 HOURS§0\n§07 HOUR WAR§0\n§0so we were FORCED to leave the westerlands in search for NEW land...\n\nWE CAME ACROSS NEW HOLY LAND OFF THE SHORE of some monkeys home we named it \"CLOWNITONSKY\"!§0\n§0THIS WAS our new LAND we had FARMS rats HOMES livestock. everything a monkey could WISH for!!!@ but with ONE downside-\n\nThere was a fat evil pagan witch den on the island.... A STRANGE DOOR leading deep underground full of evil PAGAN rats and BEINGS.... the EVIL pagans would ATTACK§0\n§0every OTHER day distroying farms and livestock EACH time... §0\n§0BUT Us HOLY CLOWNS§0\n§0had backup-\n\nBACKUP OF THE THE ONE SAINT CLOWNTH MC CLOWN!!!!! St clownth was the holyest clown in all history full of PRANKS goofs and gaffs st clownth was a HOLY name... ST CLOWTH would ASSIST us in the RAIDS of the pagans!!!§0\n§0\n§0st clownth would only appear at times-\n\nSt clownth would give SIGNS of his living viea BLESSings and the SUCH... st clowth was the holyest of holyness... a true holy name...§0\n§0\n§0BUT NOT ALL WAS GOOD ON THE ISLAND... one day the pagans were RAGED by our lands...§0\n§0THEY ATTACKED-\n\nTHEY ATTACKED THE WORST THEY ATTACKED BEFORE CAUSEING A HUGE FAT CLOWN WAR OF CLOWNS VS PAGANS!!!@@@§0\n§0\n§0the fat WAR raged on for WEEKS before it ENDED§0\n§0\n§0in the end the evil PAGANS retreated back to there DEN-\n\nVICTORY!! FOR THE CLOWNS!!!§0\n§0\n§0we had a massive feast in the cherch§0\n§0\n§0and the island was holy and grate for the next TWO YEARS....§0\n§0\n§0\n§0Two years after the massive pagan ATTACK -\n\nWhen the city was SLEEPING or AWAY §0\n§0\n§0THE EMPIRE OF OREN ATTACKED OUR HOLY LAND DISTROYING HOLY BUSTS AND BLESSED GIFTS... THEY LOOKED THE BUILDINGS THEY STOLE EVERYTHING!!§0\n§0\n§0so the clowns were FORCED to leave there land yet again.... :(-\n\nThe clowns had no where ELSE to go so they escape to ADLEBURG...§0\n§0\n§0Adleburg was an OKAY\" City we had sir robert the fat in the KINGS GAURD... The king was a evil sinner tho bad man evil evil...-\n\nBUT that did not stop the clowns the clowns carryed on with there new home and started NEW plans... AND UNDERGROUND MASSIVE BUNKER!!!! After DAYS of DIGGING and MINING the safehouse was looking GOOD with a cookery for muhammad A Bar for-\n\nOUR LONG LOST DWARF BROTHEREN . . . URIST COALMAN!!! HE WAS LEFT IN THE MINES OF THE WESTERLANDS WITH HIS BAR... HE WAS STUCK DOWNTHERE IN THE DARK FOR 10 YEARS!!!§0\n§0\n§0After we sent a party to return him to land he was soon re interduced to.. EVERYTHING...\n\nSo.. we had MUHAMMADS cookerys.. URIST DWARFEN tavern... ----'s Wookworkers desk As well as Lady BEANVILLS woodworkes desk... And PREKUSES office of holyness...§0\n§0\n§0Everything was well for about a YEAR (again) for the CLOWNS untill-\n\nThe higher ORDER of the CITY KICKED US OUT THEY KICKED OUT THE CLOWNS!!!!!!!@@@§0\n§0\n§0So the clowns packed there bags insulted the king and left for NEW NEW NEW holy lands...", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "𝓘 𝓮𝓲𝓽𝓱𝓮?", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "I Met a girl and her name is Amaya, She's now my lover, I am writing this to remember if something were to happened... Please give this back to me if i were to not know who might she be, but I'm sure I'll know who she is when I get to see her again...", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "9th of Snow Maiden 1691§0\n§0I know what I must do, but I fear to do it. I must Journy into the south and discover who is there, what is there. People could surly live in the shadow of the wall of Ice, and I could very well be the Vaeyl Order. I will travel\n\nto the south soon to discover for myself if they indeed dwell there, and what they are doing. I must stop them from expanding the Cold Front for all of Atlas.", ""),
        StaticBook("Temporary 131-1", "§bTheodoric of Markev", "Provisional Voter Identification: Amelia Philippa§0\n§0\n§0Please speak to Fabius Bracchus post-election to receive an official election identification card.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Dwed: Khorvad", "§bRazik", "{\"text\":\"\"}", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "lietenant bell insubordination §0\n§0was being immature and calling me stupid §0\n§0should be disiplined appropriatly", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Checkup #1§0\n§0Name: Mythan Annungilben§0\n§0Weight: 27 pounds§0\n§0Height: 35 inches§0\n§0Age: 2 years old§0\n§0\n§0Physical features are all normal, appetite and other things normal. Healthy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Ascanius Tathvir:§0\n§0Complains of eyes changing color after an interaction with a 'magical being'§0\n§0\n§0He has a bump on his head and a purple lump on his back. §0\n§0\n§0The strange being said 'Lye ern fiyem in adri igne'sae, mali'", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Me", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "===================     Blackden Dossier§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0          6th of§0\n§0     Malin's Welcome§0\n§0           1687§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0==================\n\n===================Objective: Take a census of the people of Blackden. Do this and then assess the buildings and structures of the town. From that point ask the Lord of Blackden where the boundaries of his lands lay. Make note of all he claims.\n\n===================Census:\n\n===================Buildings:", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Alliance between Ram and Eagle. - The Ram grows Wings.§0\n§0\n§012th of The Deep Cold, 1663 Ser Siegfried-Gregor III var Wettin-Eisenach, Minister of Foreign Relations at the Margrave's court sat down with Virkian Agnew of Pembrokeshire, High Treasurer.\n\nA writ of proposal for lord Edward Suffolk of Pembrokeshire.§0\n§0\n§0The major vassalstate, Margravate of Ostmark, has taken interest in the sister state of Pembrokeshire. We see a formal alliance to bind the two states most fit. §0\n§0\n\nWe propose a mutual military relation between the two states. In this alliance it shall be formed that both states are expected full aid when called upon. §0\n§0\n§0This accounts for any and all small to large scale offensives, defensives and skirmishes -\n\nthat the states see fit.§0\n§0\n§0If a call were to be denied, the two lords shall agree upon what happens to this alliance by the two of them.§0\n§0\n§0This social biding of states will also come with Economical aid and freedom if required. Free Trade is expected -\n\nwhilst economic aid is not and thus talks about economic aid will be conducted between the lordhsips themselves or their representatives.§0\n§0\n§0Just like the trade, movement of troops is expected to be free through out the other territories unless -\n\nspecificly called for not to by eighter one of the two lords.\n\nLord of Pembrokeshire, lord Edward Suffolk. We hope to hear back from you within 3 saints days. To eighter clarify or radify the writ we hope to see you within the capital of Ostmark, White Peak.§0\n§0\n§0Please send us a note for your arrival so we can prepare -\n\nthe Margrave's court and the required paperwork.§0\n§0\n§0- Siegfried-Gregor var Wettin-Eisenach.§0\n§0-Virkian Agnew §0\n§0High Treasurer of Pembroke", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0\n§0\n§0-------------------          WHY FENN §0\n§0   SHOULD BE SPARED§0\n§0-------------------\n\n[!] The book was empty.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "jaxin is an asshole", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Offences against the Person Act 1678.§0\n§0Section 1 to 2 - Murder§0\n§0Section 1 - Penalty for Murder§0\n§0It shall be unlawful for any person or agent of that persons to cause the death of another non-undead being by the act of murder. A person who is\n\nconvicted, or pleads  nolo contendere to the act of murder, shall be guilty of a felony punishable by public execution, and official banishment from Arbor.\n\nSection 2 - Disposal of body§0\n§0The body of every person that has died from execution shall be disposed of to the disrection of the current leader of Arbor. If the current leader of Arbor is not available, the decision falls to the Chief of Justice.\n\nSection 3 to 4§0\n§0Section 3 - Soliciting to murder§0\n§0It shall be unlawful for any person or agent of that person to solicit another person or persons to cause the death of a non-undead being. A person who is convicted, pleads guilty or pleads\n\nnolo contendere to the act of solicitation for murder, shall be guilty of a felony punishable by punishable by public execution and official banishment from Arbor. The act of soliciting to murder may be thought of as \"hiring a hitman\", though the word\n\n\"hiring\" is used loosely, and the act requires no financial transaction to qualify as such. Merely the intent to engage another in an act of murder qualifies as soliciting.\n\nSection 4 - Conspiracy to murder§0\n§0It shall be unlawful for any person or agent of that person to conspire to cause the death of a non-undead being by the act of murder. A person who is convicted, pleads guilty or pleads nolo contendere to the act of\n\nconspiracy to murder, shall be guilty of a felony punishable by official banishment from Arbor.\n\nSection 5 - Manslaughter§0\n§0It shall be unlawful for any person to cause the death of a non-undead being by the act of Manslaughter. Manslaughter is to be defined under this section as the crime of killing a non-undead being without malice aforethought, or\n\nin accidental circumstances.§0\n§0\n\nSection 6 to 10 - Attempt to murder§0\n§0These sections are to define the act of attempting to murder.§0\n§0Section 6 - Administering poison or wounding or causing grievous bodily harm with intent to murder\n\nSection 7- Destroying or damaging a building with gunpowder with intent to murder§0\n§0\n§0Section 8 - Setting fire to or casting away a ship with intent to murder§0\n\nSection 9 - Attempting to administer poison, or shooting or attempting to shoot, or attempting to drown, suffocate or strangle with intent to murder§0\n§0\n§0Section 10 - Attempting to commit murder by any other means\n\nIt shall be unlawful for any person or agent of that person to attempt to cause a death of a non-undead being by means covered in the sections 6-10. A person who is convicted, pleads guilty or pleads nolo contendere to the act of attempt to murder shall\n\nbe guilty of a felony punishable by official banishment from Arbor.\n\nSection 11 - Threats to kill§0\n§0The making of a threat to kill is an offence wherein the defendant intends the victim to fear it will be carried out. It is immaterial whether it is premeditated or said in anger.§0\n§0\n§0Although the normal sentence is\n\nseizing of their weaponary, and monthly searching of their properties to check for weapons (which is banned on their personel at all times), as well as the permit for any blackguard to search them at any given time, if the citizen is not Aborian, or it is\n\nthe Arborian's 2nd offense, shall be guilty of a felony punishable by official banishment from Arbor.§0\n§0\n\nSection 12 to 20 - Bodily harm§0\n§0Section 12 - This section creates the offences of wounding and causing grievous bodily harm, with intent to cause grievous bodily harm, or to resist arrest. §0\n§0\n\nWhosoever shall unlawfully and maliciously by any means whatsoever wound or cause any grievous bodily harm to any person with intent to do some grievous bodily harm to any person, or with intent to resist or prevent the lawful apprehension or detainer of\n\nany person, shall be guilty of felony, and being convicted thereof shall be liable to be getting a public execution.\n\n*This page has been scribbled out neatly.*\n\nSection 13 - This section creates the offences of infliciting wounding and inflicting grievous bodily harm, when the harm done was more consequential rather than intentional, and/or the wounding was less serious.\n\nWhosoever shall unlawfully and maliciously wound or inflict any grievous bodily harm upon any other person, either with or without any weapon or instrument, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and, being convicted thereof shall result in the defendant being\n\nofficially banished from Arbor.\n\nSection 14 to 15 - Garrotting, etc. – Administering chloroform, etc.§0\n§0Section 14 and 15: Attempting to choke, administration of drugs to knock somebody out, or the use of strangulation, is unlawful, and whomever is convicted, pleads guilty or pleads\n\nnolo contendere to the act of such shall be guilty of a felony punishable by public execution, and official banishment from Arbor.\n\nSection 16 - Neglecting or causing bodily harm to servants§0\n§0This section deals with the problem of neglect by an employer who failed to provide adequate food, clothing and accommodation for staff and servants. It is punishable on conviction of a fine\n\nranging from 1000-5000 Minas.\n\nSection 17 - Assult on women with child§0\n§0It shall be unlawful for any person or agent of that person to assult a woman with child by any means (as covered in sections 6-10).  A person who is convicted, pleads guilty or pleads nolo contendere to the act of\n\nsuch shall be guilty of a felony punishable by public execution, and official banishment from Arbor.\n\nSection 18 - Assaulting or obstructing a clergyman in the execution of his duties§0\n§0Whosoever shall, by threats or force, obstruct or prevent or endeavour to obstruct or prevent, any clergyman or other minister in or from celebrating divine service or\n\notherwise officiating in any church, chapel, meeting house, or other place of divine worship, or in or from the performance of his duty in the lawful burial of the dead in any churchyard or other burial place, or  shall strike or offer any violence\n\nto, or shall, upon any civil process, or under the pretence of executing any civil process, arrest any clergyman or other minister who is engaged in, or to the knowledge of the offender is about to engage in, any of the rites or duties in this section\n\naforesaid, or who to the knowledge of the offender shall be going to perform the same or returning from the performance thereof, shall be guilty of a misdemeanor, and being convicted thereof shall be liable to arrest. You may be handed over to the\n\nInquisition if they so request. Otherwise, we charge a fine of 500-5000 Minas.\n\nSection 19 - Abandoning a child under the age of two§0\n§0It shall be unlawful for any person or agent of that person to abandon a child under the age of two. A person who is convicted, pleads guilty or pleads nolo contendere to the act of such, shall be\n\nguilty of a felony punishable by a fine ranging from 1000-5000 minas. The execeptions to such an act are: if the defendant is under the age of 16, the the defendant does not have the responsibility for the child (if they are not the parent or primary\n\ncarer), or if the child is a bastard.§0\n§0\n\nSection 20 - Explosives, etcc.§0\n§0It shall be unlawful for any person or agent of that person to set explosives up with the intent to cause bodily harm or damage of property. A person who is convicted, pleads guilty or pleads nolo contendere to the act of\n\nsuch shall be guilty of a felony punishable by public execution, and official banishment from Arbor.\n\nSection 21 - Bigamy§0\n§0It shall be unlawful for any person to marry a man or women already married. A person who is convicted, pleads guilty or pleads nolo contendere to the act of Bigamy, shall be guilty of a felony punishable by a fine of 1000 Minas,\n\nand we let the church take over and give you further punishment if they wish to do so.\n\nSection 22 - Abduction§0\n§0It shall be unlawful for any person or agent of that person to abduct another non-undead being. A person who is convicted, pleads guilty or pleads nolo contendere to the act of such, shall be guilty of a felony punishable by\n\nofficial banishment from Arbor. If the abducted person/persons is under the age of 16, the defendant shall face public execution as well as official banishment from Arbor. If the defendant attempted to, conspired to, solicited someone to, or otherwise\n\nplaned to do the deed, the punishment is the same.\n\nLaw written by North Stow on 7th of The Sun's Smile 1678.§0\n§0\n§0Law approved by Ellie Undertree on 10th of The Cold Amber, 1678.§0\n§0\n§0Law passed by", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Raided by reivers", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "13th of the first seed, 1695.§0\n§0\n§0Today, I met two mages... they knew how to makeothers see things that were not there. They call if sensory illusion. They promised to teach me once they're done with their other pupils.§0\n§0I know magic is a sin, but I truly\n\nbelieve it can be used to save lifes...§0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Training was fun today ( ◡‿◡ *)\n\nI have an escape route now... if I have to escape my house,, I know how§0\n§0-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-9th of the snow maiden, 1997§0\n§0\n§0I moved today. the house feels empty.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "1. Option 4§0\n§02. Option 3§0\n§03. No§0\n§04. Option 2§0\n§05. Option 3§0\n§06. As a child, I always had the need to diplomatically diffuse situations rather tha see them escalate into fights. I know how people tick, and I can always seem to find a way to convince the opposing\n\nside that they are in need of whatever I have to offer. I make sure to become aware of what the person that I am negotiating with is like before I take action. This allows me to almost always have the upper hadn in a situation.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "question 1: option 4§0\n§0question 2: option 3§0\n§0question 3: option 3§0\n§0question 4: option 2§0\n§0question 5: option 3§0\n§0question 6: I belive, that as a lawyer, I can apply a tactical eye to the situation and pick out deceptions. I already have experience\n\nrepresenting people as well. I can disprove arguments against us. I can be reasonable and diplomatic while firmly asserting my position.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Leagues away from the comfiest burrow and the tastiest tea, there lied a pumpkin. Not a pumpkin sat in tilled soild, nor a pumpkin that held fine ale. This was a pumpkin meters wide and 4 meters tall. A pumpkin that was protected by guards and flanked by\n\nwalls that towered over the might of man. For it was such a treasure that not even the nobles of the city that held it could lay a finger upon it. Yet despite all fortifications, all obstacles, there was still a desire to attain such a trophy. But not\n\ndesire from man. Not desire by orc. Not even a dwarf wished for it. In fact, desire laid upon the most unlikely candidate of all. A halfling. A creature of such small stature, and such odd customs, that perhaps the journey that laid upon the halflings\n\nthat day, was not even expecting such.§0\n§0\n§0That is where it all began.§0\n§0A halfling.§0\n§0A party.§0\n§0A raid.§0\n§0A pumpkin.\n\nRollo Applefoot, sturdy of build, nimble of speed, was the halfling. For all intention, the party that day was just a mere celebration. An average one in a day of the life of a halfling.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Diary of Brooklyn Wood§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0\n§0After moving to curon, §0\n§0[!] all diarys have been burnt apart from this one.\n\nLog one:§0\n§0\n§0was it a good idea to move? I have isabella but its not what i thought it would be when i left my tribe.. maybe i should go back for a bit or travel to the north§0\n§0\n\nlog two:§0\n§0\n§0its been weeks and nothing has changed... im treated like dirt.. i never wanted to be in the military.. my life is so lonely. heading to see my father soon and brothers. mothers gravely sick..\n\nlog three:§0\n§0\n§0i dont think mother will make it through the year.. my father wants me to marry but i dont want that. oh well but i might travel and come back to curon who knows at this rate\n\nlog four:§0\n§0\n§0Im back in curon and on my way back i met this guy called Javien Pablo... hes so sweet and strong but comes off as a little shy.. who knows where it may go with him..\n\nlog five:§0\n§0\n§0Javien has moved in with me as he cannot afford to live else where but my small house isn't big enough.. need to move to a bigger house when possible.\n\nLog six:§0\n§0\n§0It's been a while since my last log and Javien hasn't been home in ages... he has just disapeared. oh well.. he has my heart and has sailed away with it.. still need to move houses...\n\nLog seven:§0\n§0\n§0Isabella has a sister?!? very odd.. and oh my gosh shes rude saying that i serve her just cuz im the military farmer.. bitch. dont have to feed her if i dont want to..\n\nLog eight:§0\n§0\n§0I recived a letter from my father saying my mother is on her death bed and that i should come back for a §0while..its§0 just if i do i may never return to curon... im already so lonely maybe returning home isn't a bad idea after all.\n\nLog nine:§0\n§0\n§0I have planned when im leaving curon to head home.. im only visiting and staying for mother.. after that i will return to curon for a little bit. there is nothing much for me here and its so lonely.. I hope Javien is okay..\n\nLog ten:§0\n§0\n§0Javien has sent a letter to me and is okay but he fears that he won't return.. i miss him dearly.. my brothers have warned me that father is not the nicest anymore. §0\n§0i should disapear out of the south just incase..\n\nLog eleven:§0\n§0\n§0Its almost time for me to return to the place i once called home.. but then again where is home... home is no where for a lonely wood elf like me...", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Drug Notes§0\n§0\n§0Mixtures§0\n§0-Cactus Green§0\n§0-Grass§0\n§0Mixture Two§0\n§0-Blue Orchird§0\n§0-Green Dye§0\n§0-Light blue dye§0\n§0-Fern§0\n§0Mixture = Blueberry Cactus\n\nMixture Three§0\n§0-Mushroom stew§0\n§0-Green Dye§0\n§0-Fern§0\n§0Mixture = Baby Brain", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Current report-§0\n§0Recent training has been successful. §0\n§0Everthing seems to be in order, nothing more than minor troubles between people- Nothing major.§0\n§0\n§0Update-§0\n§0One of our patrols have been ambushed. The only casualty reported was a horse\n\nwhich belonged to one of the men. The assailant was said to threaten the men with a horde of orcs. -according to Jackson of Nordengrad.§0\n§0I have sent him back out to reinforce the men and apprehend the assailant- if the assailant is not found, return home\n\nand prepare for a possible assault.§0\n§0\n§0The men are gone for longer than expected, I have headed out out of worry for their safety.§0\n§0\n§0A short search has proven unsuccessful. Perhaps it was unwise to let Jackson lead the patrol on his own.\n\nThe patrol returned during my absence. At this moment, I am sitting with Jackson,§0\n§0\" 'Llama-selling' individual followed us.\" Jackson stated. The name of this individual is unknown. Will look into the situation and have them face the boot of the law!\n\nThe individual produced a bow and slew a loyal steed of Nordengrad. This may not go unpunished. During his attempted escape, his own horse has been slain, but he managed to run off, threatening to send a horde of orcs on us.§0\n§0\n\nSeperate case- One of the new recruits, Ren, a female 18 year old, has been causing trouble. She refuses to wear the appropriate uniform, despite being ordered to wear it while on duty. She has also been accused of murdering livestock belonging to\n\nNordengrad. She shall be spoken to about her behaviour. If it continues, she will have to be discharged. There will be no incompitence in my company.§0\n§0\n§0Side note- The men are being molded into proffessional soldiers. Their combat skills are impressive, so\n\nis their ability to follow the chain of command. With just a little more discipline and training, there shall be no match for our army. I have made it in my best interest to organize them to the best of my ability.\n\nThe same man responsible for the ambush has also stole a horse. Two eyewitnesses have reported it what they have seen. \"Adawulf\" is responsible for the murder of a horse and the theft of a saddle and a horse.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The values of a good soldier are: Loyalty, Duty, Respect, Selfless Service, Honour, Integrity and Personal Courage. It is essential for a soldier to have these values in order to be entrusted with the responsibility of taking the life of another\n\nliving being. A soldier is expected to fight and obey his superiors. Though his loyalty must be devoted to his lord, obedience to his company captain and all its sergeants is nonetheless important. Treason, cowardance and desertion are\n\nnot to be tolerated in any company.§0\n§0\n§0Discipline plays an important role in everybody's life, whether a soldier or peasant. No one can achieve their target if they're not well disciplined. Be on time, be prepared, maintain cleanliness and go\n\nabove and beyond thy expectations. Be a multi tasker and do more than you are expected to. By doing this, you show your commander that you can be counted on.§0\n§0\n§0Show the ability to follow command. Soldiers must do what they are ordered to\n\nwithout questioning and without delay. The chain of command must be followed in order for an army to be mighty. Never may a soldier go over his superior's head. §0\n§0\n§0Aside from having an armoury that can kill a thousand or more enemies in the name of\n\ntheir lord, a solider must have a strong affection for their country whom they are serving. Nationalism is encouraged. Raise that banner high and mighty, let no bastard disrespect it. §0\n§0\n§0A soldier is not just a person in uniform- a true soldier forms\n\nspecific character traits over the years. I like to call these traits \"Warrior values\"- They are some of the first words you've read in this book.§0\n§0\n§0An outstanding soldier will stick out among his company, he will be noticed by his\n\nleaders and often awarded. Show them how much you are worth.§0\n§0\n§0Be brave and fearless. It is better to die a hero than live a coward. Grow a moustache or a beard, it shows the enemy you are a true man.\n\nI, myself, have been involved in warfare ever since I have left home at the young age of 17 Winters. Since then, I have led mercenary companies through countless campaigns. Currently I am serving Nordengrad, as one of the Earl's bannermen.\n\nIf you are a young lad, or lass, even, consider joining up. Nordengrad is a country worth fighting for.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "t\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\ntt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\ntt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\nt\n\ntt", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "'A untraveled road'§0\n\n\"I woke up again today, except everything seemed... off? There is a ringing in the back of my head, probably from the boat crash.\"§0\n§0\n§0\"A voice... it calls to me...\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Idk what this is", "§bAldur Roderick", "The Golden Stag Smithy Request Form:§0\n§0\n§0Username:§0\n§0Name:§0\n§0Item:§0\n§0Materials:§0\n§0Specifics:\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nUsername: Shuggie§0\n§0Name: Denis§0\n§0Item: Sword Cane§0\n§0Materials: Iron Handle and Sword", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Journal-=-§0\n§0\n§0My name's Ademar Hollifae, and this is my journey on joining the Druidic Order.§0\n§0\n§017th of Malin's Welcome, 1700§0\n§0\n§0It's been almost a month now, I've been in their library in and out. I learned many things about the Druidic Order. Now I\n\njust need to gain the attention of a Guide to become a Dedicant. I made some few friends within the Mother Grove. Namely, Liri. She is the first friend I made in the Grove. When I first met her, she was only a Druid awaiting to be attuned. I wonder what\n\nshe would be attuning to. A few days ago, I asked her to lend her aid on finding a Guide. She agreed, and said she would ask around for one. I should be there with her though, a Guide would like to see who they'll be teaching.§0\n\n20th of Malin's Welcome, 1700§0\n§0\n§0I've just been pacing around the Grove for the past few days. Today, I met a Druid that looks like a Guide. I'd like to ask... but last time I tried, all he said was to go ask around, and that he was sorry. I feel that he\n\ndislikes me or some sort. Probably, because of my lack of confidence.\n\n7th of The Grand Harvest, 1700§0\n§0\n§0I plan on heading back to Nordengrad for a while. I heard that the rally would be taking place in a few days. Problem is, I don't remember where I put my old uniform. I guess I have to request new ones. After that though, I\n\nhope that I am able to make new friends within the Mother Grove. It's quite enjoyable being here. Once I finally become part of it, I want to meet my old friends again. I wonder what the two snow elf sisters are doing now. I'm guessing Iron Fist would\n\nstill be finding an arcane teacher to teach him. We're in the same page, to be honest. Speaking of which, how am I able to hide myself once I actually become part of the Order in the Empire? The capital surely hates those who worship other gods than\n\ntheirs. I hope Captain Harold would help me with that.\n\n9th of The Grand Harvest, 1700§0\n§0\n§0I joined in the War Games, as part of Haense. I was put in the Haense A party. Currently, Haense B is fighting whilst I am writing this. I do hope I would do alright when it is our party's turn. This is the day I am\n\nfinally able to use my training of the swords to use.§0\n§0\n§010th of The Grand Harevst, 1700§0\n§0\n§0The War-Games is over, I am unsure who won or not, but it was fun. I'm going to retire as a Guard, and take on the field of medicine. Lord Cassian Snow\n\nannounced that the doctor occupation is open, and have a teacher. I will have to take this opportunity for myself. Maybe with this knowledge, I am able to utilize it as part of the Druidic Order.\n\n14th of the Grand Harvest, 1700§0\n§0\n§0I finally found a Guide. I took their interview, I almost passed. However, I need to do a few more studying. I'll be returning again in a year, or One elven week. I hope I am able to pass the next time I do it.\n\n10th of Sun's Smile, 1700§0\n§0\n§0I retired as a Guard of Nordengrad, and took the opportunity to become their doctor. I'm currently an apprentice of Mayan. I know little to nothing, I hope I don't give Mayan too much trouble. Hehe...\n\n14th of The Deep Cold, 1700.§0\n§0\n§0Lord Cassian was killed in Belvitz today.. Truly, a time of despair. I am very dejected of this unthinkable event. Cassian Snow, the man who welcomed me to his town. The man who payed my education with Mayan... I can not\n\noverlook this. However, I feel the most deepest sorry for his wife and daughter. I heard his head was chopped, right infront of his daughter. Why must good men die?\n\n15th of The Deep Cold, 1700§0\n§0\n§0Currently, I am in the court of the Capital. The trial is between the killer and Bjolfr. Anna, Lord Cassian's daughter, apparently had the intent of killing the killer of his father. She was escorted out. Just sentence\n\nhim to his death already! Darius's verdict is that Cassian had conspired with various unlawful acts. I did not catch the proof if they had announced any.\n\n8th of Malin's Welcome, 1701.§0\n§0\n§0I have met Harold again. Hoping I would be able to attempt my interview, the second time. I don't quite remember how long it has been, but he did say an elven week. I believe I've been here for almost a year. Not sure\n\nthough. Hope he would be able to recognize me again.. A few hours have come by now, yet again. I have failed my second interview. I will have to make sure I will pass the third interview.§0\n\n10th of Malin's Welcome, 1701.§0\n§0\n§0I have met Madorn, Iron Fist, for the first time in a year now. Still hadn't able to find a teacher. I will be helping him to get started.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Zombie Research Log§0\n§0\n§0Within these pages are the complete summary of my research into the common undead, zombie.§0\n§0\n§0Ye be warned.§0\n§0\n§0-Bodin of Nordengrad\n\n13th of Sun's Smile§0\n§0Year 1681§0\n§0\n§0A zombie made its way within Nordengrads walls today. I have  captured it, and imprisoned it within the basement below my market stall. Hopefully the neighbors do not notice the noise.\n\n15th of Sun's Smile§0\n§0Year 1681§0\n§0\n§0Testing has begun. I have found the zombie unable to withstand sunlight, yet other lights appear safe. It is willing to consume only flesh, descendant race flesh preferred.§0\n§0\n§0The zombie also is able to climb ladders.\n\nThe zombie is apparently able to reach between its bars. Fortunately, it is neither smart enough to take anything nor strong enough to remove the bars.§0\n§0\n§0Never the less, I have taken precautions and moved the Hoo-Kah away when not using it for tests.\n\n11th of Deep Cold§0\n§0Year 1681§0\n§0\n§0The zombie shows no focus for anything other than general terrain shape and flesh. It cannot plan for complex puzzles nor jump gaps, nor does it care for riches.§0\n§0I need to find a way to get the diamond out of its cage.\n\n10th of Malins Welcome§0\n§0Year 1682§0\n§0\n§0Zombie went missing today. I suspect th neighbors had it... silenced. Oh, well. Some information was gained.\n\n14th of Deep Cold§0\n§0Year 1683§0\n§0\n§0I have a new zombie today. Bignose type.§0\n§0I've secured it deeper underground, to render it inaudible to the surface.§0\n§0\n§0I have less time to perform experiments now, as I have other, more pressing duties.\n\n15th of Deep Cold§0\n§0Year 1683§0\n§0\n§0The zombie shows little care for my presence. It occasionally reaches for me, but otherwise spends most of its time inspecting its cell.§0\n§0\n§0Interesting. I certainly want to cure this one now.\n\n5th of Grand Harvest§0\n§0Year 1689§0\n§0\n§0It has been several years since my previous entry. The zombie has shown no rot, interestingly. After all this time, I have still not discovered a cure in any libraries. In other news, if no buisness shows up,\n\nI may have to move in search of work. Naturally I would be unable to take the zombie with me. As such, I am spending less and less time researching and more and more peddling wares or running caravans. It is unlikely I will make another entry.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mira's note", "§bMira Arden", "\"Hey Clanmates, feel free to write a book, or possibly go out and collect and buy some so our shelves are filled and the clan has a way to pass some time, under this note you'll find 3 empty books to write within if you find yourself wanting to put your -\"\n\n\"- own work on our shelves.§0\\\n§0\\\n§0- Mira Arden of Clan Arden\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Turning [12/16]", "§bNoria Onyxheart", "\"His blazes drew the second's praises, hearing death for the first. Undone by their ignorance, for with their savior they are cursed.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Turning [9/16]", "§bNoria Onyxheart", "\"For gracious silence, he needed violence, purging all their kind. This land was but just another, and then the fates came aligned\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "roses are red and violets are blue§0\n§0im worth a lot of money let me split it with you§0\n§0if she were still alive youd be approved by my mama§0\n§0you are as white as my llama §0\n§0your hair is gold like my other llama §0\n§0lets make a lot of ninos!\n\nfor you i end cactus green-o§0\n§0The end!", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "1st of The Grand Harvest, 1687§0\n§0\n§0I have woken up from a dream about the Far Glade. March Ash told me that the Glade is looking for a new champion. I have decided that I will either aid the chosen champion in his/her journeys or strive to become the\n\nchampion myself.\n\n4th of The Grand Harvest, 1687§0\n§0\n§0I am on my way to Fenn to see an old friend. He has recently been recruited to the Ivae'Fenn, and will be fighting the forces of the September Prince. I will aid him and fight off the old Champion of the Far Glade. Maybe I\n\nwill learn something that might help me in my quest.\n\n5th of The Grand Harvest, 1687§0\n§0\n§0I have reached Fenn and have been let in it's walls. I would seem that Caius isn't in the city at the moment, so I am waiting for him. I have decided to do what I do at every grand city: get on top of the walls. I\n\nhave finally succeeded in getting on top of the wall. I have gotten bored of waiting for Caius so I am travelling to the Wonkawoods so I can get a glimpse of the battlefield and scope out the area.\n\n9th of The Grand Harvest, 1687§0\n§0\n§0I did not end up finding the Wonkawoods so I have decided to gater up materials and forge myself some weapons and armor. I am going to the Warhawkes mines in search of metals.\n\n15th of The Grand Harvest, 1687§0\n§0\n§0I missed the battle against the September Prince. I am travelling to Warhawkes to gather resources so I am better prepared for the next battle. While I am there I will gather information on how the battle fared.\n\n5th of The Sun's Smile, 1687§0\n§0\n§0I have arrived at Warhawkes. I am struggling to find a mine but I have found a rather nice settlement. I may buy it at some point. I have not seen anyone in the city so far, so I still have no idea how the\n\nbattle went. I have decided I will go back to Dominion.§0\n§0\n§0I have arrived in Dominion. It seems very empty and quiet. I wonder what happened. I am looking for the Oakhide Fletchery because I saw a job poster saying they are or were hiring.\n\nIt turns out that the Oakhide Fletchery is somewhat of a myth, because everyone has seen signs for it, but no one knows where it is. I have decided to travel to Cloud Temple instead. Maybe I will learn of the battle here. I have found a Band Poster in\n\nDominion. They are looking for 2 drummers and a pianist. I might apply.\n\n6th of The Sun's Smile, 1687§0\n§0\n§0I had an encounter with some men of a clan. They wished to recruit me. I denied. Then a strange fellow wrapped in vines and roots and leaves came near me. He had a strange aura to him. I wish to see him again and learn more\n\nabout him.\n\n7th of The Sun's Smile, 1687§0\n§0\n§0I ran into a man on my way to Holm. As I was walking by he shouted for help. A bandit was trying to rob him. I quickly ran over. We both geared up, ready to fight the bandit. The bandit tried to fight, but we beat him to the\n\nground. Hopefully he's learned his lesson.\n\n8th of The Sun's Smile, 1687§0\n§0\n§0I have arrived at Holm. It is a nice little town. I especially like the inter-town railroad.§0\n§0\n§0I have stumbled across a conversation that intrigues me. I think some men are talking with a mage about some sort of\n\nHIVE telescope. Not sure what it is. I am currently hiding and listening in to the conversation.\n\n9th of The Sun's Smile, 1687§0\n§0\n§0Some bandits came into Holm and started threatening citizens. I ran back to Cloud Temple to call for help. When I was coming back I ran into what I believe to be a Wight. It looked like a tall suit of armor filled with\n\ndarkness. I am sure it was a Wight. I am now back in Holm, searching for the earthen creature.\n\n11th of The Sun's Smile, 1687§0\n§0\n§0The creature that I thought was a Wight sent me a bird. He told me to meet him in a inn to talk. He told be about how he used to be a wraith, and how it is evil. I learnt that wraiths have no control over what they do. They\n\ndo evil things, and slaughter many. I have decided not to be a Mystic or Wight now. He is going to take me to his town or city, and I shall live there and learn all sorts of things.\n\n10th of the Amber Cold, 1687§0\n§0\n§0After talking to the wood elf (whose name will remain unsaid) he took me to his city (name will again remain unsaid). After showing me around, he went about his duties while I explored. Later, I stumbled past the\n\nWonkawoods, the forest in which the most recent battle with September happened. I figured I could learn much from these woods, and I was right. I found a Wonk village with an ancient Druidic library in it. I will study everything there is to know about\n\nDruids here.§0\n§0\n§0So far I have gathered 14 books:§0\n§0\n§0Malin's Teachings I-V§0\n§0Druidic Records I-IV§0\n§0Caribou Druid's Log I-IV§0\n§0Elk Druid's Diary§0\n§0\n§0I shall read all these books and hopefully get a better\n\nunderstanding about what this war is all about.\n\n9th of The Deep Cold, 1687§0\n§0\n§0I have finished reading all the books I had looted from the ancient Druid library. Malin's Teachings taught me much about keeping a nation together, and didn't aid me in my search for knowledge of the September Prince.\n\nThe other books though, were all about the September Prince and the old Druids. The Druidic Records spoke of the ancient Druids and the September Prince. It told of how all natural things listened to him, and how he destroyed all the cities on Axios and\n\nsome on Atlas, and of his plans. Caribou Druid's Logs was about a Druid of the Prince. They explained how the Prince has power much like that of a Word Altar (possibly World Altar. Was spelt Word Altar in book). Elk Druid's Diary was about a young Druid,\n\nwho was most likely newley recruited. It is at the time when the September Prince first attacked a city after his long sleep. Elk Druid says how the Elder Druids are keeping silent, not telling the newer Druids of what is happening. Later, Elk Druid\n\ndescribes the September Prince as taller than the Mother Tree. They also tell of how all of their most loyal animals went to his side and how the Mother Tree did his bidding.§0\n§0\n§0I now venture off into the Wonkawoods. I shall re-visit the wonk village, maybe\n\nfind new hidden things there. I will also explore more of the woods and perhaps find the creature wrapped in vines and roots there.\n\n11th of The Deep Cold, 1687§0\n§0\n§0As I write this, I am sitting at the entrance of the Wonk village. I have come back from exploring every nook and cranny. I found the chieftain's hut, a wyvern, and to my surprise, a dwelling of the Mani. I explored the\n\nMani dwelling. It is a big cave opening, with a big pond covering the stone floor. It is filled with plantlife of all shapes and sizes. It is a beautiful place. I did not find a Mani. After finding all there is to know about the Wonk village, I have\n\ndecided to continue exploring the Wonkawoods.\n\n9th of Snow's Maiden, 1687§0\n§0\n§0After exploring most of the Wonkawoods in a very unorganised fashion, to my avail, I found nothing. I think I might do a more organised search in the future, but for now I shall go back to civilization.\n\n1st of The First Seed, 1688§0\n§0\n§0I am travelling to Warhawkes so that I might find the Misty Isle. I don't know what I would do there but I feel like it would be an interesting place.\n\n8th of The Grand Harvest, 1688§0\n§0\n§0After exploring the oceans around Atlas for quite some time, I came back empty handed. I found nothing. I have come back to Gladewynn and am goind to rest in the Wonkawoods.\n\n10th of The Sun's Smile, 1688§0\n§0\n§0I came back to Gladewynn this morning and discovered that all of Gladewynn was geared up for war. They gave me armor, weapons and a sheild and told me we were fighting for good. I had no clue what we were fighting for, but I\n\nwent anyways. I did not attack anyone, only observe. From what I could tell, we completely decimated them. I still have no clue what happened. The fight was over within half a day. It is now night time and I am back at Gladewynn. Everyone is celebrating\n\nin the tavern. I am sitting on the cliff edge, looking out over the Wonkawoods, trying to pull my thoughts together. From what I can tell, we were fighting bandits. It was 100 Oren (who I sided with) vs 15 Reivers (bandits).\n\n1st of Snow's Maiden, 1688§0\n§0\n§0I am travelling to the new Library of Dragur so that I can continue my search for knowledge. I will read up on the lore books first I think.\n\n10th of The First Seed, 1690§0\n§0\n§0It has been two years since I started studying at The Grand Library Of Dragur. I have learned much since I started, but in the grand scheme of things, I know nothing. I am now going to spend some time in the wonk village, and\n\nreallign my soulstone to the Gladewyn pillar.\n\n14th of The First Seed, 1690§0\n§0\n§0I have arrived at the wonk village and decided to go into the ancient libraries. I only really noticed then, that all the plants were growing towards the roots of a colossal tree in the center. Only it's root were visible but\n\nthey moved, as if they were alive. Then it struck me. I believe that tree to be the September Prince. That would explain how the flowers grew so tall without any sunlight and how all the plants grew towards it. I have a suspicion that it is either a Mani,\n\nor at least a reincarnation of a Mani (I say it because I am not sure if I should call a tree a he or not).", ""),
        StaticBook("Thorvn's Feaths.", "§bThorvn Bronwyn", "{\"text\":\"\"}", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "§0           JOURNAL§0\n§0\n§0       Property Of§0\n§0\n§0    _______________", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "the fenn stink xd§0\n§0signed §0\n§0the dominion", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Krug-Fu, the Orkish Martial Art§0\n§0\n§0Written by Guru Xugulg of Krugmar§0\n§0\n§0*a sketch of an Uruk with nothing but monastic robes and bloodied fists, standing over a pile of mauled Elves*\n\nTABLE OF CONTENTS§0\n§0\n§0Preface\n\nPREFACE:§0\n§0\n§0Be you an Orc aspiring to greatness, a curious reader wishing to know more, or perhaps an outsider wishing to absorb the techniques to bolster their own fighting style, I welcome you to The Art of Krug-Fu, the magnum opus of all my studies into\n\nthe martial arts of the Hou-Zi and Easterners. As a child, I had plenty of hatred and unbalance in my heart ever since my parents were taken away from me by Human hunters seeking the priceless ivory of an Orc's tusk. This hatred burned into my soul, and\n\nafter I assaulted the tribal wiseman, the Chieftain gave me one choice: die, or seek absolution through trekking to an old Uruk's cabin in the middle of nowhere. I took the latter, and began my trek. This Uruk initiated me into the start of a rather...\n\nlong, education. From his lessons, I've learnt to channel my bloodlust into productive form, squelch the burning fire of Iblees's curse by spending it on training. Granted, I still have some issues to  this day with anger, like any other Orc, however I\n\nwould have ended up dead were it not for that education. I expanded my studies of balance and inner-peace through self-teaching the concepts of various Hou-Zi and Easterner forms of combat. However, this is a story about my art, not about myself, that\n\nbrings us to the next section of Philosophy.§0\n§0\n§0PHILOSOPHY:§0\n§0\n§0Krug-Fu recognizes that Orcs are angry,  bloodlusting warriors. Use this to your advantage, yet do not let it consume you. Blood-rage is a flame. Let it fester unchecked and it will\n\nresult in a forest fire. Yet monitor it with discipline, training and honor, and that fire gives warmth, life and industry. Let your hatred and rage propel you forward. You'll have much more of an advantage than the standard combatant.\n\nKrug-Fu recognizes that virtually any foe can be defeated, everything has something which makes them tick. This also means the Krug-Fu practitioner does, as well. Such calls for the monk to be in a constant state of self-improvement and learning. Being a\n\nGuru, or master, is paradoxal. It is attainable by recognizing it is never attainable, perfection is attained by recognizng it can never be attained. Such is the nature of Krug-Fu. One can always hit harder, move faster, and think quicker.\n\nAnother aspect of Krug-Fu is that the preferrable monk have no self-esteem or pride. Tis not to say that they shouldn't feel good  about themselves or their accomplishments, however when pride and envy clouds reason, disaster is soon to follow.\n\nTHE FOUR WAYS:§0\n§0\n§0Krug-Fu is built on the Four Ways, the cornerstones of the art in terms of training. They are The Way of the Tiger, the  Way of the Crane, the Way of the Bear, and the Way of the Turtle.\n\nTHE WAY OF THE TIGER:§0\n§0\n§0This emphasizes strength, muscular endurance and might. To train this aspect, the traditional physical exercises are needed. First, bench-presses are superb at establishing upper-body and shoulder strength. Dumbell curls are\n\ngood at developing the strength of arms. Sit-ups and crunches are great for the abdomen. As for the legs, simple squats shall work. It is a commonly held belief that if one cuts back  on food, they will gain muscle quicker. This is a lie. When one\n\ndeprives the body of nutrients, the body begins to actually conserve fatty mass in the body and stunt muscle development. While this is good in a survival situation, it is not preferrable for getting jacked. A hardy warrior's diet is necessary to build up\n\nmuscle.§0\n§0\n§0THE WAY OF THE CRANE:§0\n§0\n§0This measures agility and grace of movement. What distinguishes Krug-Fu from a simple brute pugilist is not just the philosophy, but the fact that a proper Krug-Fu monk can run and\n\nhit faster than a crossbow bolt, fighting with the ferocity and perception of a Wood Elven acrobat. How to develop this, is simple. After every exercise, stretch. Also, cardio such as running is great for elongating and increasing the dexterity of muscle.\n\nI recommend getting your hands on gymnastics equipment when you feel you're up to the task. When you're quick enough to catch a knife mid-air, match the speed of a Kharajyr rogue, you  will be ready for the next aspect of Krug-Fu.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Wise men say only fools rush in§0\n§0But I can't help falling in love with you§0\n§0Shall I stay?§0\n§0Would it be a sin§0\n§0If I can't help falling in love with you?\n\nLike a river flows surely to the sea§0\n§0Darling so it goes§0\n§0Some things are meant to be§0\n§0Take my hand, take my whole life too§0\n§0For I can't help falling in love with you\n\nLike a river flows surely to the sea§0\n§0Darling so it goes§0\n§0Some things are meant to be§0\n§0Take my hand, take my whole life too§0\n§0For I can't help falling in love with you§0\n§0For I can't help falling in love with you§0", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", ":) REEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEE§0\n§0\n§0My book now :P", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "4th of Malin's Welcome, 1677.  §0\n§0\n§0Today I went To fight Norland and other cities.  Great Book enteries.  I went to fight a Minataur and All I could remember was cutting its head off And after that, nothing.  I just Woke up at Cloud Temple.  I hope Tommorow\n\nIs better.  -Magnus§0\n§0\n§016th of the Grand Harvest, 1678.§0\n§0\n§0I havent seen Kaetheryn in over a year, I fear she will be gone for much longer.  I miss her and hope she is safe.  -Magnus§0\n§0\n§03rd of Sun's Smile, 1678.  §0\n§0\n§0I jut got to markev and\n\nfound some people in the city punching eachother.  Its crazy.  -Magnus", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Journal of§0\n§0KRAKENGOTH GHORBASH§0\n\nDay 1: The boat is underway. We've set up a cove near Sutica, to funnel our loot and serve as a temporary camp. Zagarak be praised, Clan Nargol will not fail in his task. We are going to dominate the Seas, and will drag the others down to the seafloor.", ""),
