        StaticBook("Letter to Bianca", "§bEgoi \"Liberator\" Stormfist", "The wise women of elder days used to say to small dwedmar; A perfect lass had is a warrior with a good heart, soft but strong. Unapologetic and honest. She is the type of lass you go to war besde, she's is the type of lass you have to marry.§0\n\nI see these characteristics in you. I want to marry you and have the dwedmar of legend sing our songs in Dungrimm's hall for eternety.§0\n§0I hope to hear from you soon.§0\n§0- Egoi \"liberator\" Clan Father of the Stormfists", ""),
        StaticBook("Ramblings o Love", "§bCount Durlak", "She is for me all what the mountain means to our people. Strong she stands before all odds. The blustering wind of those who call out against her in conflict dancing over the stalwart defence that has captured my eye and heart\n\n-=Bianca The Mountain=-\n\nHer hair falls and drapes her Marble face like veins of lava coursing through the mountains core. A firey wild heart burns with in the emerald eyes. Lo' before this creature of carnal mystery I stand stilled, in awe for truly there is no greater gem to be\n\nfound in the depths of this realm. She does not stand though as others of her clan draped in the green ink to marr her supple ivory flesh. Now this stunning titant of an enchantress has not come to rest long enough to be covered in the limits of a life\n\nover come by vines. It is from this one notices her drive. The Huntress of the mountain knows her realm and prowls with an elegant pose not but the aenguls hope to up hold.\n\n-=A Womans Many forms=-\n\nI have been blessed to work with many metals in my life, but not one comes close to that which I see with in her. Her wit is that of the finest edge one could find, fireland blades of obsidian falling dull and lackluster when measured against her.\n\nThe confidence in which she speaks and acts resonates with the makings of steel. The resonating beats of hammering from this realm upon her fail to but change a single minor detail of her form. Before this steel falls weak and useless like that of Aurum.\n\nThis is not to say though that Aurum stands against her, no for when she smiles or speaks her looks and wisdom force it to dull and pale in splender. She has clearly been found by any and all who know her to be the greatest material in any realm.", ""),
        StaticBook("An ancient tome", "§bUnknown Source", "This book looks ancient, as if it predated the arrival of the Aegean Exodus to Asulon. It is filled with indecipherable texts and strange diagrams. While the text is incomprehensible, the pictures seem to show a method of golem creation.\n\nThis book looks ancient, as if it predated the arrival of the Aegean Exodus to Asulon. It is filled with indecipherable texts and strange diagrams. While the text is incomprehensible, the pictures seem to show a method of golem creation.\n\nThe first stage of golem creation seems to be the creation of the core. The images show a block of gold held aloft by a being not disimilar in appearance to a dwarf. It could possibly have been one of the race that built Karik. The picture also\n\ncontains what looks like a shaman of some sort, but certainly not a dwarven one. At the centre of the drawing is a bolt of unnatural looking lightning. It seems as if the shaman is summoning the magical lightning to strike the core. In the next diagram,\n\nthe golden core and the dwarf holding it seems to be enveloped in some sort of field of lightning. A third diagram shows the dwarf holding the core, which is now transparent, with a mist swirling inside it. It is possible that this is making an\n\nimpression of the dwarf's essence and soul onto the core, rather than the crude rituals used in Aegis to transfer the soul entirely. Further on in the book, there is a diagram of a golem body being forged by the same dwarf that held the core\n\naloft. The anvil strongly resembles the anvil of Karik, albeit in better condition than the one in Karik today. The body is far more ornate and intricate than the comparatively primitive golems of Aegis. The next diagram is a cross\n\nsection of the golem. It seems to be made of several interlocking parts, all either forged or carved from what looks like no more than common ore or stone. In the centre of the body is a large central cavity. The final images show the craftsman placing\n\nthe the core into the open central cavity, the body being enveloped in the magical lightning, and then the golem sitting up and looking at its creator. This book seems to confirm that the Ancients of Karik had the power to make golems, and used that\n\npower. Given that golems have the ability to live almost indefinitely, this raises the question: where are they all?\n\nOOC: Contact Lagomorphia for further questions or before any golemancy related activies.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwed Clergy V1", "§bMiscellus", "THE FIRST MEETING OF THE DWARVEN CLERGY\n\n9TH OF THE SUN'S SMILE, 1520\n\nHigh Prophet Hogarth Irongut began the meeting by speaking of uniforms. He stated concisely that Demagol Doomforged is able to supply\n\nuniforms & robes to any who might need them, as a unifying symbol is key. The robes themselves are symbolic of your patron god, and of your own personality; the trim differs from Dwed to Dwed, allowing a bit of a look into their own state of mind.\n\nFor a quick note:\nOgrahad is green. \nWyrvun is teal. \nDungrimm is dark red.\nGrimdugan is gold.\nArmakak is also gold, as they both represent merchants. Yemekar is also gold, though his gold represents divinity rather than wealth.\n\nAnbella is orange. \nBelka is the same red as Dungrimm. \n\nThe next matter of business was the newly constructed temple. It was confirmed that all future sermons and meetings would be held here, directly above Kal'Akash.\n\nA road was confirmed to be in planning for construction, though the date is unknown for when it shall be finished, as the hike up the mountain is steep and inhospitable for a well-paved road. \nIn normal Dwarven fashion, the material of the road was argued\n\nover vehemently; the king yelled gold, a man yelled blackstone, and another simple lapis. One dwarf even dared to recommend simple gravel! There was no conclusion met by the end of the topic. \n\nDemagol and Conan were assigned to work on the road, and the\n\nrest of the volunteers were set to construct vast shrines to the Brathmordakin. The Doomforged's patron, Dormarr, has already been constructed as an effigy; the rest shall be scattered around the kingdom in places that exude their greatness.\n\nGauldrim Irongut was then promoted to the status of priest due to his help in construction of the church and the altar of Ograhad. \n\nWe then went towards the ritual site; hidden under the arena, this water-based altar was filled with\n\nglowstone, fire, and a mouth to the ocean, allowing water to flow in freely. Its isolation shows the introverted and introspective power of Ograhad; its fire shows the hidden passion and ambition of the scholar-god. Magical glowstone represents his arcane\n\narts, and runes flow throughout the walls, though I know not their meaning. \n\nHogarth assured that this was a great altar, though we should not copy it in making our own: it was the only one he's ever seen hidden from the public eye, and each\n\ngod should have individual artifacts and runes inscribed for their offerings. We were told to speak to him if we ever had an idea for our own places of worship, or sermons to spread to the people of Urguan. \n\nHe ended the meeting by bringing up an\n\nunnerving topic: the ex-High Prophet, Beros Oathcast. He has been attempting to start his own church, to undermine Dwarven authority and religion; Hogarth, obviously, does not like this, and wishes to put a stop to it, for he will not come and debate or\n\nspread his ideas with honor. He says to contact him if Beros ever tries to speak to any of us and to let him handle it, though I wonder if that will truly work. From what I understand, Beros has quite the silver tongue... \n\nAlgoda Frostbeard recommended\n\nHogarth make an official statement, a first move against Beros and the heretics. The Irongut was hesitant, but assured us that he would figure out a solution soon. \n\nThe meeting ended with a reminder to start our assigned temples and not to linger.\n\nThe first meeting of the Dwarven clergy was a success, and I hope each meeting afterwards can be just as productive!", ""),
        StaticBook("College Conduct", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "College Of Sutica\nCode of Conduct\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nEvery student and Professor must follow these guidelines, failure to do so could lead to termination from the college and access to the campus.\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Behavioral Rules\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-1. Every student and staff is expected to act mature and serious about their work.\n2. Rudeness and tormentation of others is not tolerated, you have a right to be at the college like everyone else.\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Class Rules\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-1. Everyone must take their class seriously, goofing off and being a distruption during class time can result in expulsion from the class.\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Dormatory Rules\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-1. Students must keep their dorm space clean and tidey. Failure to keep a clean sleepspace could result in the loss of it.\n2. No Girls in the boys dorm, Vice Versa.\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Library Expectations\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-1. Respect the books you sign out, you can and will be charged if a book is lost or destroyed.\n2. Keep a low voice in the library, people may be studying for a final exam, or presentation.\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-Campus Rules\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-1. No using dangerous magic unsupervised\n2. No practicing the latest fighting tecnique on other students.\n3. The campus courtyard has training dummies for fighting practice and magic, no explosive magic.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Apple of Ice", "§bIrish Delfina", "Apples. Apples of various shapes, colours and shapes grew on a tree made entirely of ice.\n\nI picked the apple, knowing not of the curse that would ensue. But how could I have not endulged my desires?! \n\nThey were so beautiful! Perfect, even. It was odd.\n\n\nI shall return later.\n\nIt has been two weeks, and the tree deep within the depths of the library of Tahn has revealed to me it's most beautiful of gifts.\n\nAn apple made entirely of gold.\n\nPerhaps this is what the password was. The key to all knowledge. I shall take a small bite\n\nAͩ͊ͬͧ̔ͤ͏̼̦̱͔ľ̞͆̽͜l̖̙ͨ͋͡ ̺͎͓k̢͈̠͈̪ͣͮͮͬͨ̅͑n̊ͧ͐͊͂̚ǫ͎̯ͤ͋w̲̺̘̹̗̞ͬ̎̾l̓̊̋͛͋ͭͮ͝ḙ͚̉͛̓̄̀d̲̳ͫg͇͇̼ͨͣ͠e̲̥̬͚̗̹͌̒ͯͩ ̴͙̻̯̻̗̝̥̄̀ͭi͔̲̼͕̬̗͚ͤ͆͋̽̄s͍̫̤̺͉ͥͦͭ͒ ̜̯̄ľ͉o̗̰͌̓ͩ́s̺̭̪͕t̎̀͏̝̰̥͉͈̟.̮̬̊̉̃\n\n\n\nB͕̝̝̺̘̓͡u̥͕͎̙̹͈ͬtͦ ̱̺͔̬̥̋̽̂̍ͅeͧ̒̄̽v̥͋͗ͨ̐e̖̗̣̯̼̫͙͛̎͑͐ͬ͋ͫṙ҉̖̝̞͔ȳ͙̺̘̙̭ͮͨ̄ͨt̼̥̟̮ͣ̇̒ͯ͂h̸͎̱̬̲͔̗͇͐͆ͨ̉͒͛̀i̻̘̖̗̤̞͂̎̐ͪ̍ͩ͆n͕͎̊ͮ̉̄̈̇͢ͅġ͓̙̲ͅ\n\nh͉̜̓ͥ͑̃̓ͩa̢͕̠ͧ̓͋̈́̍̓͌s̸͉ͥͮͭͣͩ̋̾ ̑̅҉̬̦̘̤͍b̰̖͙e̘͠e͚͈̐̌͜n͚̠̪͔͛͗̂̑͐͑ ̑̐g̙̫̰ͮ̏̊ͣͬ͟a̱̠̙̤̣͖̿ͥ̊ĭ̤͓̒̌̉̅ͥn̉͐̓ͨͨ͊̃͏̲̳̪̰̥̯ͅe̪͔̺̟͆̂̾́͊̑̈́ḍ͖̩̯͍̦̍.̅͘ͅ\n\n̐͛ͯ͏̘T͙̹̖͔̽h͓ͯͧ́͆̚͞ȩ̞̣͉͕̀ ̬̗͙̥͓ͣͩ͊D͔͓̫o̞͖̯̩ͯ́o͉̲̞̥͔͢r̸̤̜ͫͮͭ̄ͫ ͕̩͍̣̦͖͆͒̉͒ͥͅh̟̣̥̠͍͓ͨͬͨͭ̂͝á̴͇̰̭̻̮ͦ̄̊̔ͅs̵̲̳̙̩̯̝ ͧ͂͗̽̀̿̔ŏ̍͌̓̋̾p͚̬͒͌̚e̲̺̯͎̘ͦ̿̑̊͛ͥͬ͢n̯̰̎̈́̄͂̂e̴̿ͦ̾̓͂̃d̰̜̫̑͑̓ͪ̈ͭ\n\na͎͕̦̦͇ͤ̓͗̓ͪn͉̂̌̓͑̇̚ͅd̙͙̄͐̚ ̦͇̝̥͓̽̎ͥ̿͟I͒̄̓ͫ̊'̬͔̰̍ͣ̓ͨv̳̼̹̦͎͒͛̐̇e̺̾̑̈́̓͠ ̥͖̦̇\n\n ̥͖̦̇s͔ͭ́ͨ͆͑͒t̡̜̺ͭ͋e̐̑́̂̓͑̂p͏̤͎p͖̦̗͖̗ͮͥ̾̂ͅȅ͓̗͙̗͓̣͖ͯ̂͒̇̇d̼̜́͠ ̝̖̺̗̤́̇͛ͨ͟i̜̿́ͮ͘n̮͙̟͇̞ͭ̽ͅţ͉̪͔̭̭̜̐͌͛͂o͕̞̤̚ ̙̗̲̤̹̟͙̐ͩ́ͯ̔̄̋t͕̪͓̞̔̈̌h̲ͭe͛҉͇̮̻͚̣͔ ̶̭̤̠̤̾͐d̹̥ͩ͢r̈́͞e̩̜̯̞̞̅̐a̶͔͍̲̝̫̲̓̀̽̆m͇̤̖͔̲ͩ̆͌̈.̞̦͎́ͨ̈ͅ\n\n̖̙͉̮̳͕̳-̤̺̟̦̺̋ͨI̼̲͆̂ͅr͉͓i̤̫̫̺͆́s͔͎̥̄̄́ḩ̺̪̤̹̫͒̽ͫ̃ ̟̉ͨ͒D̤̯̼ͤ͒ͬa̺̪͕̥̱̘͑ͦ͟ḻ͔̭̠͚̔ͥͯ̈ͭ̅͝f͇ͯͤ̉̀̄̄i̙̪͈͔̪͍͇͐ͤ͂͗ͮ̐ñ̲͙͍̭͙̈̅ͯͧ͠a͚͛̒ͭ̔̈ͭ͂", ""),
        StaticBook("Lily's Tale [1]", "§bLuxeanna Du Couteau", "Teh Tail Of\n\n        Teh Wulf\n\n            Nd\n\n        Teh Gazl\n\n\n          Bi: Lileh\n\n        Pt. 1 of 2\n\n       The Tale Of\n\n         The Wolf\n\n              &\n        The Gazelle\n\n          By: Lily\n    Recorded by:\nLuxeanna Du Couteau\n\n        Pt. 1 of 2\n\nIn the deepest part of the mainland, a forest exists that has gone untouched by man for all eternity. Here, animals and plants exist in a natural order, they way the great creators had intended.\n\n Living a life of meaning and happiness. And here, is where our tale begins.\n\nThe animals of this forest lived in a serene community. Each one, from the birds and the rabbits, to the deer and the bears, had a place in this community and lived amongst each other in harmony.\n\nHowever, there was one beast that lived outside this circle- The Wolf. The wolf would live in its den, hidden by the shadows of the thick forest. Few animals ventured to the wolf’s den, and even fewer returned.\n\nAll the animals understood the order of nature, they understood that the wolf was cursed with its hunger for meat and flesh, and they did not hold it against it. However the wolf’s personality, his menacing look,\n\nand his lack of patience, often made the other animals flee in fear of it.\n\nOf the few animals that tried to reach out to the wolf, children were often among them. They would hear the stories of the wolf and wish to play with it.\n\nHowever, the wolf found the games the children wished to play tiresome and annoying. In the wolf’s rage, he lashed out at one, taunting it with the bones of animals it had eaten and scaring it away.\n\nIn another instance the wolf lost his temper when dealing with an arrogant youth, letting its sharp teeth wrap around the child’s neck. The stories of the wolf go on and on, and the entire forest knew of them.\n\nBut what they didn’t know about was how lonely the wolf felt. Cursed by his rage, his temper, his looks, and his hunger the wolf was destined to live alone until the end of its days, watching the other inhabitants of the forest laugh and play.\n\nThat was, until the Gazelle arrived. Easily standing out with its foreign appearance and behavior, the gazelle wandered into the forest from a far away land, one with different customs and things.\n\nThe animals of the forest welcomed the gazelle, trying to make the gazelle feel welcomed amongst their busy life. The gazelle smiled brightly and followed their directions, confused and unsure of their behaviors, but maintained a happy\n\npersonality to look like one of them. For the gazelle had come from a land of destruction and chaos. Fighting amongst the animals would happen daily and then Man found its way into their home, obliterating it.\n\nThe gazelle was alone, lost and confused and simply wished to find a new family, but at the same time, desperately missed her own.\n\nAs the animals celebrated the gazelle’s welcome, the wolf slinked onto the edge of the festivities, carefully watching her.\n\nThe animals of the forest were celebrating amongst each other, eating berries and drinking honey, but the gazelle sat by herself. Although the festivities were for her, she felt like an outcast and was left\n\nby herself, the other animals unaware of her feelings because of the happy smile she wore at all times. But the wolf could smell the gazelle’s true feelings. Fear. Desperation. Terror.\n\nAll smells that the wolf had come accustomed to when smelling its prey now greeted him in the middle of a happy festival, and all were coming off so pungently from this new comer.\n\nThe gazelle graciously smiled to the animals as they celebrated, but as soon as they had turned to take another bite of blackberry, she ran. She dashed through the trees and lept over the logs, trying to get away. The sounds of the festival slipped away\n\nbehind her as she ran, but the thudding of paws greeted her. In a clearing the wolf leapt from the shadows of the trees and circled the gazelle slowly. The wolf questioned the gazelle as to why she left the party so soon\n\nand was surprised when she answered thatshe preferred to be alone sometimes. The wolf inquired about the gazelle, and as she told him the story of her homes fall and her travels, the wolf realized that the smellsof fear and desperationwere drifting away.\n\nThe gazelle followed the wolf back to his den, far from the other animals of the forest, in the quiet depths of the forest. She asked the wolf questions about the animals here, and the wolf answered her questions honestly.\n\nHe told her how the animals would squabble over who had the tastiest walnuts, how they had ridiculous dances, and were always full of energy, never resting.The gazelle laughed at many of the wolf’s stories, finding a comfort in the honesty and help.\n\nThe wolf’s den was also a comfort to the gazelle. Unlike the fancy burrows of the animals, the den remained natural in the depths of the forest, reminding her of her home.\n\nAs the days passed, the gazelle would often stop by the wolf’s den to take a break from the busy life of the forest animals.\n\nOther days the wolf would meet the gazelle at the crystal pond for some water. The other animals at first would scatter, hiding behind the trees and roots, but soon saw how the wolf would sit by the gazelle and drink peacefully.\n\n With a few recurrences, the animals no longer feared the wolf when he came to drink and welcomed him when he went to festivities with the gazelle. The animals noticed how much tamer the wolf was around the gazelle and were happy at this.\n\nBut they wondered how much the gazelle really knew about the wolf, and the dance with death she could possibly be playing.\n\nIt was decided amongst the animals that the gazelle must become aware of the wolf’s curse and his past. The animals debated about ways to separate the gazelle from the wolf to speak to her about the issues, but it wasn’t decided until\n\nan old turtle crept into the center of the discussion. The turtle spoke slowly, stating that while the concern for the newcomer warmed her old heart, she implores the community to not forget that the wolf has feelings too.\n\nThe wolf should be allowed to explain himself to the gazelle, and let his case be made known by himself, and not spoken of behind his back. The animals listened to the wise turtles words and agreed,so the following day their plan was put into action.\n\nThe field mice went to the gazelle, asking for her aide in knocking some berries from a small tree. With the gazelle away, the bear approached the wolf, for surely he was the safest of the animals should the wolf become angered.\n\nThe bear asked the wolf for its feelings about the gazelle, and for the first time that the wolf could remember saying, he said she made him happy. The bear smiled at this and informed the wolf that all of the animals wanted the wolf to be happy,\n\nbut they wanted the gazelle to be safe. The wolf stood up and declared that he too wanted her to be safe and would defend her from anything. The bear simply stared at the wolf and asked him how he would defend her from himself.\n\nThe wolf could not respond, realizing the bears words. The bear urged him to speak to the gazelle about his past before she finds out on her own and to let her make a decision on what to do.\n\nThe wolf thought long and hard about what to do, whether to hide his past and his curse, hoping for the best, or to be honest with the gazelle.\n\nThe gazelle approached the wolf’s den, excited to tell him about the trip she had taken with the field mice and the berries she had found, but the wolf was sullen and silent.\n\nWhen the gazelle nudged the wolf he became serious in a manner that she had never experienced before.The wolf told her of his curse. He told her of his rage, how he taunted and murdered the young animals of the forest.\n\nHe told her more stories existed, some even worse than the ones he had revealed, but could not say what he had done.But he looked to the gazelle and with honest eyes told her that her presence quenched the thirst he had,\n\n it quieted the rage, and dampened his temper. He told the gazelle about how happy she had made him, and felt like he had a meaning in life once more, to live and protect her.\n\nThe wolf became silent, looking at the gazelle for a sign of her acceptance, anything at all.\n\n But a tear fell from her eye and she ran away from the wolf.\n\nHe chased after her, calling after her to come back, to be with him, but the gazelle sprinted away, leaving the wolf in its tracks, fleeing from the forest.\n\nAs the days went on, the animals of the forest talked amongst themselves in whispers. They had seen the gazelle flee the forest, but they had not seen the wolf at the pond to drink.\n\nNone of the animals reported seeing the wolf stalk its food either, and they became concerned. The bear walked to the wolf’s den and found him sitting in the deep reaches of it, hidden by the shadows.\n\nThe wolf refused to speak to the bear, but the bear could tell that the wolf was dying. Not only from a lack of water and food, but it felt like the wolf’s spirit, one that would be intimidating to even the bear, was gone, drained from its body.\n\nThe animals feared they had done this to the wolf, that they would be the cause of the wolf’s death for scaring away the gazelle. They began blaming each other, the field mice pointing fingers at the briar rabbits, the birds ridiculing the deer.\n\n. But the old turtle sat on her stone quietly, looking into the forest, looking at something. Eventually the animals noticed the old turtle smiling and looked to see what was making the old girl happy at a time like this.\n\n Light filtered through the trees and a shadow moved slowly, overly cautious and unsure.\n\nThe gazelle walked slowly through the forest, past the animals that stared at it silently, towards the wolf’s den. The wolf crawled out of its den slowly, limping and shuffling through the hole before laying on the ground at the dens opening.\n\nThe gazelle kneeled down and looked at the wolf, withered and dying. The wolf smiled lightly between coughs, amazed that she had came back.\n\n“Yo-You came back….” the wolf sputtered between short breaths.", ""),
        StaticBook("Poem", "§bBeluar the Botanist", "Kypris the beauty\nOh how I love thee so much\nWe have barely spoke\n\nWhat is wrong with me?\nLove with a female so soon?\nI am a failure\n\nOh but I would fail\nBut I would fail a thousand times a day so\n\nI could have her hand\n\nShe says I'll find love\nI wonder who it will be\nHopefully it's her\n\nThey call her evil\nI see her as a flower\nShe may be a witch", ""),
        StaticBook("Philosophorum", "§bLanavia Zytiaear", "An Introduction to the\nPhilosophorum Society\n------------------------------\n\nThe information provided within these pages are to simply help you understand what the Society is and what exactly we stand for.\n\nIf you still have questions contanct\n\nSarrion (Toxzero), Elric (Jacey) or Lanavia (Creete).\n\n\nEnjoy~\n\n-\nLanavia\n\nWhat is the Society? \n\nThis has to be the most asked question we get here in the Society - at the same time it is the easiest to answer.\n\nThe Society is more a community than a guild.\n\nWe are a gathering of like-minded individuals that have a thirst for knowledge.\nIt is this thirst for knowledge that has pulled us all together and has led to the creation of the Society, and is the thing that still keeps us together.\n\nAre there any fees?\n\nNo. We have never charged new members any type of mina fee to join our ranks.\n\nThe only thing we ask is that if you stumble upon a book we might be interested in that you would donate it to the Society.\n\nWhat does it mean to be a member of the Society?\n\nThis one is also easy to answer. To be a member of the Society simply means you are a part of something more – you are trying to better yourself and the world around you.\n\nYou are not wasting the most precious thing you own: your mind.\n\nBeing a member of the Society means you are searching to answer the unknown and learn from others who have already started their personal quests to do just that.\n\nWhat’s with the jackets?\n\nThis is one thing we share with a lot of guilds or schools, we have a matching uniform of sorts. The navy colored jackets are a symbol of your ties to the Society – and thus your eagerness to learn and spread knowledge.\n\nA fact about the jackets that you need to know is that the colored trimmings do mean something. A student with gold trims on his jacket with a student of magic, whereas a student with a jacket that has a silver trim is a student of science.\n\nMany students study both science and magic – the jacket they decide to wear is up to them but should be trimmed with the colors associated with whichever of the two they focus more heavily on.\n\nThe best way to know what a student studies is to ask them.\n\nWhat is the purpose of the Society?\n\n\nThe Society’s purpose is simple. We are here to gather, document, and share knowledge – that is it.\n\nDo you need to be an Elf to be a member?\n\nNo. We do not care what race you are, so long as you are like-minded you are welcome here.\n\nThis is the basis of the Society put into the simplest terms I could. If you have any other questions about it feel free to ask any member you see – if they can’t answer your questions they can point you in the right direction. \n\nBe well~!", ""),
        StaticBook("A l", "§bEradan Dune`dan", "A song lifts my heart\nIt dances through\nlike a kind wind\nbeneath the wings of a bird.\nYet the song ends,\nvanishing.\nThe bird falls,\nmy heart drops,\nand my eyes\nhave been opened.\n\nDawn's early light spreads \n\nLike an unfolding lily,\n\nShowing me the way\n\nthe river rushes\n\naway on an unseen path\n\nAway to it's home\n\nA chance to be\nA chance to breathe\nA chance to love\nAnd a chance to live.\n\nHow can I prove,\nWith sweets and the sunrise?\nWith affectionate words?\nOr say it plainly,\nI adore you.\n\nWhen I look at you\nThe summer is in your eyes,\nand I adore you.\n\n\n\n-Eradan", ""),
        StaticBook("New Elven Vol I", "§bKalenz Uradir", "New Elven Lessons: Volume 1\nby Kalenz Uradir\n\nIn elven grammatical structure is often different to that of common. For one instead of placing an adjective before a noun it is placed after said noun. This becomes particularly important for the most basic of greetings.\n\nKarin'ayla - Goodmorning\nKer'ayla - Goodnight\nVan'ayla - Goodbye\n\nEach places the time of day before the adjective describing it. Noun and adjective are separated by an apostrophe.\n\nOther important words for the beginner in elven include race names:\n\nMali - Elf\nUruk - Orc\nValah - Human\nBortu - Dwarf\n\nIn order to form sub-races of elves, adjectives are taken to add more detail to the word Mali.\n\nMali'ame - Wood Elf\nMali'aheral - High Elf\nMali'ker - Dark Elf\n\nIn order to form sub-races of other cultures the suffix tali- may be used. This word most directly means 'part of'.\n\nTali'uruk - Goblin (Lit. Part Orc)\nTali'valah - Halfling (Lit. Part Human)\n\nOther basic phrases include exclamations including:\n\nAyla - Good\nSul'leyun - Brilliant (Lit. Beautiful Light)", ""),
        StaticBook("Forty Thieves", "§bArnorian Elendil", "Ali-Baba and the\nForty Thieves\n\nA long time ago there were two brothers named Cassim and Ali Baba. They lived in a far off land. Cassim, the older of the two brothers, had married a rich wife. He had a fine big home and did not\n\nneed to work for a living. Ali Baba, the second brother, had married a poor woman. He worked very hard indeed. Each day he went away from home to cut wood, which he sold in the city. \n\nOne day Ali Baba was at work. Suddenly, he\n\nheard the sound of horses' hoofs. He was frightened, and hid behind a tree. There were many bad men n the land, and he knew that it was wise to keep out of their way!\n\nAli Baba just had time to hide before a group of men rode up. They\n\nwere the forty thieves who had been stealing gold and rich goods from the countryside for many years. The leader of the thieves stopped his horse at the side of a big hill. \"Open, Sesame,\" he cried, so loudly that Ali Baba could hear\n\nhim. \n\nNo sooner were the words out of his mouth, than a magic door opened in the hillside. There was a deep dark cave behind the door. The forty thieves went into the cave and the door shut behind them. Ali Baba waited\n\nfor what seemed a very long time. At last the door opened, and the forty thieves came out again.\n\nThis time the chief of the band called out \"Shut, Sesame!\" The door closed, and the men rode away.\n\nAli Baba wanted to know what was in the cave. After a minute or two, he ran up to the side of the hill. Just as he had heard the leader of the thieves do, Ali Baba cried out, \"Open, Sesame.\" Once again, the hidden door opened. He went through the\n\ndoorway. The door closed behind him. \n\nAli Baba found himself in a huge cave. It was filled with rich goods and gold which the thieves had carried there. Ali Baba trembled with fear. What if the thieves should find him!\n\nQuickly, Ali Baba cried \"Open, Sesame,\" and ran out of the cave. He found the old horse he had left in the woods and led him back to the cave. There he loaded four big bags of gold on the poor beast. Then he hurried out of the cave.\n\nHe called out, \"Shut, Sesame,\" and went home as fast as his horse would travel. His wife could hardly believe him when Ali Baba told her that they were rich. Her eyes sparkled with joy when she saw the gold. \n\nNow Ali Baba was\n\nso happy that he just had to talk about the gold. That was a big mistake. He told his brother, Cassim, where he had found the gold. Ali Baba was so kindhearted he even told Cassim the words that opened the magic door. And, he said that he would give\n\nhim half the riches in the cave.\n\nAli Baba's brother was a mean and selfish fellow. He did not want half the gold in the cave. He wanted all of it. Early the next morning, long before the sun was up, Cassim took ten horses.\n\nThen he set out to the cave. He planned to load all the riches onto his animals and leave none for Ali Baba.\n\nWhen he got to the hillside, Cassim cried out, \"Open, Sesame!\" When the door swung open, he led his horses into the cave.\n\nThen the opening in the hil closed behind him. Cassim hurried to load his horses. He knew it would be dangerous if the fourty thieves found him in their hide-out. When he had taken all the gold that his horses could carry, Cassim\n\nled the animals to the door.\n\nSuddenly, Cassim turned white with fear! He had forgotten the magic words that made the door swing open! He could not get out of the cave!\n\nIn a few hours the\n\nthieves came back to their hide-out. There they found the rtembling Cassim. \"Do not kill me!\" he cried. \"It was not I who found your cave. It was my brother, Ali Baba, who did it. He sent me here to take your gold.\"\nThe fierce leader of the thieves\n\nlaughed. \"That is all I wanted to know!\" he said. \"We will soon visit this brother of yours.\" Then the chief ordered his men to beat Cassim with heavy sticks. They beat Cassim until they had killed him. The leader next told his men of a plan to kill Ali\n\nBaba because he had found their cave. \"In a few weeks, Ali Baba will think that he is safe,\" the chief said. \"He may guess that we have caught his brother, but he will not know that his brother told us that Ali Baba found our hiding place.\"\n\n\"We will get a string of horses,\" th chief went on. \"On the horses we will put forty oil jars, each one big enough to hold a man. You will get into the oil jars. I will lead the horses to Ali Baba's house. I will tell him that I am a travelling oil-seller\n\nand that there is no room for me to sleep at the inn. Ali Baba will then let me stop for the night at his house. \"Later, when Ali Baba sleeps, I will call you,\" the chief said. \"You will cut your way out of the jars with your knives. Then we will pull Ali\n\nBaba from his bed. We will kill him and his wife. Then no one will know about our cave.\"\n\nEverything happened just as the leader of the thieves had said. When Cassim dissapeared, Ali Baba thought his brother had gone\n\nto the cave and been caught. But when he neither saw nor heard of the thieves, Ali Baba decided that he himself was safe.\n\nWith hte four bags of gold he had taken from the cave, he had bought a new house\n\nand fine clothes. People who had once passed Ali Baba without a word now treated him like an old friend. He was happy indeed. Then, late one afternoon an oil-seller came by Ali Baba's new house. He led a long string of horses. Each one\n\nwas loaded with large leather oil jars. Of course, the oil-seller was really the leader of the thieves. Ali Baaba had seen him at the cave. But he did not know that his visitor was the same man. Ali Baba invited the chief to come in when he heard that\n\nthere was no room for him at the inn. \"Please come in,\" said Ali Baba. \"You can have supper with us, and a warm bed to sleep in until tommorow.\" Now it happened that Ali Baba had a wise and beautiful servant girl. She worked as a cook in his house. While\n\nshe was making supper, she found out there was no cooking oil in the kitchen. \"There is plenty of oil in the jars in the yard,\" the girl said to herself. \"I think it will be alright if I take just a little. Then I can cook the supper.\" And off she went to\n\nget some oil in a boil.\n\nWhen the girl drew near to one of the jars, she was greatly surprised to hear someone inside. It was one of the thieves, who said, \"Is it time for us to climb out and kill Ali Baba?\" The girl thought\n\nquickly. \"Not yet,\" she said, making her voices sound deep as if the chief of the thieves were talking. Then she ran to tell her master that there were strange men in the oil jars.\n\nAli Baba guessed that the thieves were hiding in the\n\noil jars. \"Run and bring the soldiers!\" he ordered. \"They will be happy to meet our visitors.\" \n\nIn a few minutes the soldiers came on the run, led by the servant girl. Then, very quietly they crept into Ali Baba's house. There they caught\n\nthe surprised leader of the thieves. When the leader had been tied up with rope, Ali Baba led the soldiers to the yard where the oil jars stood along the wall. \"Come out! Come out! It is time!\" Ali Baba called. Out popped the thieves -\n\nright into the hands of the awaiting soldiers. Ali Baba was so pleased with the little servant girl that he gave her his son's hand in marriage. There was a great feast. Everyone in the city came. And why should they not, for Ali Baba\n\nwas now rich and well known for catching the thieves!\n\nAnd whenever Ali Baba, his son, or even his grandson needed gold, there was always the hidden cave to keep them rich to the end of their days.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Shun", "§bTristanm1", "The Shun\nInscribed by Dawn Druid Maiavel\n\nThe Great Druid can impose a strong, nonviolent sanction upon those who have offended the circle. All must shun someone placed under the shun; no druid in the circle will aid, speak to, or associate with the target of the shun. When an entire town or\n\nvillage suffers the shun, no druid may enter that area or speak to or aid any resident. Some druidic allies volunteer to follow the custom of the shun as well.\nThe great druid has the right to pronounce a shun on any druid in the circle.  A shun also can\n\nnondruids, whole communities, or druids visiting from other domains (except the Grand Druid and personal servants), to demonstrate the circle's displeasure. \nTo pronounce the shun, the great druid stands up during a moot and  announces to the group the\n\nreasons to impose the shun. Then the subject of the shun--if present--answers the accusations before the assembly. Finally, the High Council of the Moot votes on the matter openly, usually at sunset. If a majority of the council votes in favor of the shun\n\n, it passes. If not, the great druid should start keeping an eye on the circle's archdruids--the opposition to the shun likely reflects an impending challenge. \nA shun punishes a druid for violating the tenets of the druidic order or reprimands a\n\ncharacter whose actions, while within the bounds of the druidic ethos, nevertheless were contrary to the Order's interests. A shun generally lasts 10 summers. However, the inner circle can vote to lift a shun early or (once the time is up) to extend it.\n\nThe shunning does not extend outside the domain, so shunned druids usually choose to go into exile--the result the great druid probably intended in the first place.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Lonely Cow", "§bKarter", "The Lonely Cow\n\n   There once was a cow that was in a pen with many other cows. The cow lived a short life of watching his friends get murdered and breeded over and over and over again. He needed to stop it, all of it. But he couldn't do anything, so he\n\nkept waiting to get murdered and either get eaten or have his skin put on others. He waited a lot more but never got murdered. He just sat in the pen, but eventually he was set free! He escaped and ran as far as he could then a man named Archrim walked to\n\nthe cow, he pulled out his bow and arrow and shot the cow in the face and ate it with his son later. \n\n\n\n        THE  END!", ""),
        StaticBook("MonkResurrection", "§bKirrekith", "Monk Resurrection\nBy Jistuma\nPages 23\n\nNotice, this books is a rushed copy of a tome inside the Library of the Orkish capital, as made during the raid of the 16th of the Grand Harvestm 1532 The following is no way a complete nor perfect copy of said book.\n\nMonk Resurrection\n\nIt is the salvation of those lives, but it is pondered why nothing has been wrote upon it. The monks are able to and well known for being able to save those on the brink of death or those who've always passed the thresshold. While at the grounds of the\n\nsanctuary manning a stall I have been able to witness of these happenings, or so what I believe. \n\nThis magic, unlike others, is one we know little of and myself. Like most holy forms of magic as it takes the form of a bright light, used to heal wounds.\n\nBesides this light, the monks act is to pray to the three known as the Triumvirate. It would appear to be that of clerical healing, but uses other properties not like those of clerical magic. Monks returning to the sanctuary can come back wounded,\n\nhaving been attacked by bandits proberly, showing peoples lack of care for whom they attack on the roads, especially when these individuals will often bring them back from the brink. Monks are not ordinary people, they heal faster than others from\n\nobservation. This is likely from their magic. often I witnessed light coming from they're wounds and surrounding it. Monks can also bring back the once deceased fully mortal once more. \nThis isn't in which to say they are necromancers, those that would\n\nbring back the dead, and remain in a state of limbo between death and life. Monks unlike them are able to bring back body AND soul unlike those of the necromancer, and bring them back to a near perfect condition from before death. Talking to those at the\n\nsanctuary, there is always an effect of being saved. A present residing condition is the loss of memory that occurrs after ones life being taken to the brink or past it and brought back. I have witnessed those effected having no memory of the passing or\n\nthe run up to it. Other common effects that linger is the scarring, revealing how the soul nearly passed the brink permanently or the tortures it passed. Often what worries me is the effects of change that develops in those that return, in personality.\n\nHaving talked to those if proves my worries. It is my belief that death is a terrible experiences, and part of it remains after the salvation. \n\nAnother fact I have witnessed, is that the deceased do not wish passively return to their prior resting place.\n\nThis came to mind when I witnessed one of the saved hugged dearly by a beloved. Before this a friend has carried his friend, the two of us talked about what had occurred. Knowing the location of his end, the twos route home took them through the place,\n\nand upon discussing this he began to want to take other ways home, and a argument erupted when the woman just wanted to move home swiftly, much to the mans reluctance. He could offer no explanation as to why his mind has been set to not travel that way.\n\nAs well this this the other strange behaviours of those visiting the sanctuary became more apparent, such as staying there durations. As well as this not using normal routes out of the temple, or swiftly returning to the santuary after having left with\n\nfriends. Its my assumption that those who meet their death are faced with a pain too horrible to face, what could be worse than seeing your own dead body?\n\nOn the talk of the bodies, I have a state as well, it is not necessary for the body to be brought\n\nback to the monks for the resurrection. I've witnessed them bring bodies back to the sanctuary, so I believe possessing them makes the process easier or favourable. In the lands of Anthos there are many evils, you could be decapitated, easten, thrown in\n\nlava, cut into pieces and drowned in the deepest oceans. Your body may disappear and never be found once more, and even without it can still be saved. Resoration of the body is beyond my comprehsion, and monks refuse to answer the question. They do\n\nhowever answer a few questions. I learned the monks are neutral, and never take sides in politics and conflict. They also are neutral in those they save, murder or saint they are rescued. This has brought them into conflict as some are desired to be dead.\n\nMost of the stories of those rescued begin with them explaining their awakening. Waking to the monks care. Soon come back swiftly after their demise, often before family and friends arrive. Others can take many elven days. They're magic is not all\n\npowerful, as monks say they can't save all those who come to them. If the deceased does leave the monks rooms within a elven week after their death it is to be presumed them to have passed to the beyond without the monks being able to act. The same occurs\n\nto those who take their own life in an attempt at life to end. If they no longer wish to live, their is nothing the monks can do to bring them back. \n\nThe monks are a blessing to mortals. They are those thay save many from their shortened lives.\n\nWrote by Rosso, 15th of Malin's Welcome 1452, copied by Kirrekith on 16th of the Grand Harvest, 1532 during the raid on the Ork Capital.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Agustus Raid", "§bFinel Cole", "I am keeping track of what things I see, hear, feel, and touch. What I also eat, too. I will record what the people are like, what they think of the destination, their occupation. There is a long journey ahead of me, and I hope this is a success.\n\n So far I am in Oren. The people around me have this wierd accent. I will classify these things in my way. I will attempt to make my own language for it to spread around. I will call these people Orenians. The architecture around here is very complex.\n\n This job that I am doing right now is a Menel. A Menal is someone who records the information around them and makes new things. Now, there is something called Mountain Agustus. Who lives in there are fighters. Protecters of Oren.\n\n Dwarves are attacking. There will be a battle. Todays date is the 30th of The Grand harvest, 1456. This battle will be called The Battle of Oren. The humans are currently in a world war with everyone. I will call the world war, The War of All.\n\n The humans fought the dwarves over, but it isn't over yet.\nThe dwarves have taken over the fort. We have lost control. We are contesting over Fort Vekaro, which is the fort that we lost. The battle is not over yet. The dwarves are almost in.\n\n  I am not calling it a battle anymore. It is no longer The Battle of Oren. It is now The Agustus Raid. Orenians took back Fort Vekaro, no one has won the The Agustus Raid. The dwarves will come back.\n\n They have come back. We fought them back, but they WILL come back. It turns out they were a mix of races in the group. Elves, orcs, and dwarves. They went back to their city, Kal'Alras. Orenians are strong. But are they strong enough?", ""),
        StaticBook("Pursuing Purity", "§bAshanaak", "------=+=------\nFor Those Who Pursue Purity...\n------=+=------\n\n\n\nA Guide for Those Who Pursue Knowledge of Tahariaean Clericism\n\n------=+=------\nMasjid al Nur al-Haqq\n------=+=------\n\nThe Masjid al Nur al-Haqq is the building before you, serving as a gathering place for the clerics of the Aengul of Purity, Tahariae. Tahariae has given us the abilities to establish Purity in this\n\nrealm, which comes in two forms. The first is the eradication of injuries, blemishes, and sickness from the mortal races. The second is the eradication of the servants of darkness throughout the realm, such as dark mages, tainted beings, and those with\n\nfraternal relations with such beings.\n\n------=+=------\nThe Five Tenets of Tahariae\n------=+=------\n\nWhen one becomes a cleric, they must follow a set of five tenets, or five main rules, told to the Prophet Braxis in Anthos by Tahariae Himself. The rules are to ensure the cleric knows what he\n\nor she must do for Tahariae and His duty. Breaking even one of these rules will mean forceful disconnection from Our Lord:\n\n[*] Shelter and protect thy brothers and sisters in Tahariae. [*]\n\nThe other clerics are much like your brothers and sisters, a family. You must always be ready to come to their aid, and to allow them to die intentionally is impure.\n\n[*] Do not stray in thy dedication to Tahariae. [*]\n\nNever stray from your duty, your duty is to heal those in need and to purge the darkness that roam around Vailor. To allow a simple matter to draw you away from such duty is impure.\n\n[*] Guide and protect the Descendants of the Four against the Impure. [*]\n\nNo matter their race or personal prejudice, cast all hatred aside, as we aid all. Help guide them onto the right path and ensure they are healed and protected from Impurity.\n\n[*] Do not spill the blood of the innocent. [*]\n\nDo not attack or kill an innocent person, even if they have insulted you or another. We clerics are the healers of the innocent, not slaughterers of the innocent. Such is impure.\n\n[*] Do not use Tahariae's blessing for anything other than His will. [*]\n\nTahariae’s power is only for His Mission. To use it to harm those innocent of crimes or for your own selfish needs is impure.\n\n------=+=------\nWalking the Path of Purity\n------=+=------\n\nWe are willing to take in those willing to become a cleric, although becoming one is not a simple matter of gaining His power and using it of your own free will. One must be willing to undergo\n\ntrials and be prepared to put Tahariae’s duty before all, including what is most precious to you personally. Most of all, you must follow the Tenets without hesitation; failing to do so will mean permanent disconnection.\n\nIf you truly have desire to bring\n\nLight and Purity into this realm, you shall meet with one of our masters and put through a series of trials that the master decides. These trials will help demonstrate to us your devotion and dedication, as well as help you understand the roles of the\n\nclerics. Once your trials are complete and the master deems you ready, you will be brought before Tahariae Himself. If He deems you ready, He will grant you His blessing of Light, and your duty as a cleric shall begin under the guidance of the master who\n\nconnected you to Tahariae.\n\nIf you wish to walk the Path of Purity, leave a letter explaining who you are, why you wish to serve Tahariae, what skills you have, and if you have any questions regarding us. Simply leave the letter in the chest at the\n\nMasjid al Nur al-Haqq, in the Caliphate of Khalestine, and await our response.\n\nIf you require healings, protection, or blessings, do not hesitate to send a bird to one of the Four Archons of the Masjid al Nur al-Haqq.\n\n------=+=------\nThe Four Archons\n------=+=------\n\n-[ The Mind ]-\nRamza Mantisuku\n((Zeeer0))\n\n-[ The Mouth ]-\nAshanaak\n((Ventusyr))\n\n-[ The Heart ]-\nAndriel Z'lorn\n((jlyoko))\n\n-[ The Arm ]-\nElvira Mantisuku\n((Farryn))\n\n[!] This page is dedicated to a map of the Caliphate, with a small, simply-drawn temple symbol in one of the corners of the city. [!]\n\n((-2197, 1061))", ""),
        StaticBook("Dominus Tecum", "§bGuru Pinya", "In this book I shall write of the Order of St. Amyas and their error. The Creator teaches Divine love and mercy, yet these men give no unbeliever the chance to convert or see the truth. These men are HERETICS, they claim that they are setting an example\n\npersecuting pagans, and heathens! What fools! I have been following them and making religious observances. One accused me of being a sodomite! They do not even realize their error of their religious fallacies and indoctrinaztion! Another moment\n\nI listened to a conversaion of theirs! Two soldiers called a church 'the house of God' when it is merely a house of worship! These foul mouthed, idiotic hypocrites don't even realize the blasphemies they utter. They suggest that God is incompotent and\n\nis limited to such a small building! On several occasions I was forced to correct them in their ways IN FRONT OF OTHERS. What an abomination. They also do not realize the meaning of Church! I have spoken that I wait for the Church, and do you know what\n\nthey replied? 'The Cathedral is in the town square!'. The Church is not a building! It is the mystical body of the Creator and it is made up of all the believers! The fools even tryed to take away my Creator-given freewill! They use FORCE to spread the\n\nlove of the Creator! A farmer of hate will never sow a seed of love! It is impossible and contrary! To the foolish men in the Order of St. Amyas, change your ways before God's wrath is brought about for your hypocracy.", ""),
        StaticBook("Of the Hand", "§bShynys Itesti", "Disciples of the Hand\n\nFaction Skills:\n\n-Alchemist\n-Blacksmith\n-Chef\n-Enchanter\n-Leatherworker\n-Stonemason\n-Tinker\n-Woodworker\n\nDisciples of the Hand\n\nFaction Discription:\n\n- Individuals that work raw materials into fine armor, ancient enchants, and funny gadgets.\n\nDisciples of the Hand\n\n- These individuals work long hours, perfecting their crafts, training their skills, and trying to make a name for themselves by paying great attention to detail on singular items.\n\nDisciples of the Hand\n\n-These workers use raw materials to create and manufacture expensive products that can be sold throughout the world.\n\nDisciple of the Hand\n§\\\n\nFaction Speaker:\n\n-These individuals represent their faction at meetings with the leader.\n\n-They inform the leader of any pressing matters or concerns within their faction.\n\nDisciple of the Hand\n\nFaction Speaker:\n\n- These individuals negotiate things with the town leader.\n\n- These individuals are elected by their faction. Elections take place once a month.\n\nDisciple of the Hand\n\nFaction Speaker:\n\n- Should this position become vacant, or the individual become disposed for over a week, emergency election will be held.\n\nDisciple of the Hand\n\nSpeakers to Date:\n\n- Shynys Itesti 8/24", ""),
        StaticBook("-=Promise=-", "§bKlaudia Crast", "-------------------\n\n     ---=()()()=---\n\n          Promise\n\nBy Lady Klaudia Crast\n\n-------------------\n\nHis steps pounded the pavement with a steady beat; a paradox of the quickened rhythm of his heart thrumming against the walls of his chest like a jackhammer.\n\nSix long years had passed since he last laid eyes on her and their home.\n\nThey had become nothing short of a dream that both haunted and soothed his soul, wishing with every desperate breath he took for his dream to become a reality. \n\nIt may have taken six years, but his wish was finally granted, and the elation he felt -\n\ncouldn’t overpower the anxiety and uncertainty that raided his heart and mind. It threatened to reduce him to the memory of what put him in this situation to begin with, and although he tried not to think the worst, he'd witnessed more than any twenty-\n\neight year old man should. Yet, despite his seemingly positive aura, doubt shadowed his presence. \n\n He carried on, taking a moment to revel in the memories he had once created with her, even in their short time together.\n\nIt had been the last night before his departure. He’d lain there, his body entwined with hers, inhaling the scent that clung to the warmth of her skin, the scent of the lavender fields that she’d lain in just hours before he claimed every inch of her.\n\n“I’m going to miss this,” he whispered, kissing the top of his wife’s head. She snuggled in closer, tracing the pad of her finger along the contours of his chest and stomach.\n\n\n[!] A drawing of the lady and man resting would be here in great detail.\n\n“I wish you didn’t have to leave.” Her breath tickled the hair on his chest. “Just promise me you’ll return to me?” Lifting her head up to meet his eyes, she quickly added,\n\n“I know that’s a silly request, and I shouldn’t have asked that of you, -\n\nit’s just…I can’t bear the thought of anything happening to you.”\n\n“Nothing is going to happen to me,” he’d reassured her. “I wont be over there for very long. Before you know it, I’ll be back, and we can start the family we’ve always wanted.”\n\n“Oh?” She questioned, her eyebrows raising in amusement. Dragging her bottom lip between her teeth, she said, “If we have a boy, I want to name him Michael.”\n\n“My middle name?” He questioned, taking a mental note of how soft her skin felt against his -\n\n and the fullness of her lips that beckoned his to caress. Her smile was his answer, and he couldn’t find it within himself to argue. He would give her anything she desired.\n\n“Then, we name our baby Adalind if it’s a girl.”\n\n“No,” his wife protested. “You can’t do that.”\n\n\n“Do what? Use your middle name if it’s girl, just like how you want to use my middle name if it’s a boy? A little hypocritical, don’t you think?”\n\nHe watched in amusement as his wife’s jaw dropped, words caught on the tip of her tongue, unable to form a rebuttal.\n\n\n\nSo beautiful....\n\n“It’s such a strange name, David.”\n\nHe laughed. “Since when did strange phase you? You’ve never been one to settle for ordinary.\n\nBesides, I love your name. I love everything about you.\n\nAnd when we do have a baby, that baby will be a part of you, and I love the thought of naming her after the one woman who stole my heart the day she purposely dumped her tea on me.\"\n\nHis wife looked up into his eyes before snorting in laughter,\n\nburying her face into his chest. “You deserved it! You shouldn’t have been such a pompous arse.\"\n\nBrushing her golden waves aside and tucking them behind her ear, David took a deep breath in, revelling in his wife’s perfection.\n\n“This pompous ass got what he wanted. You’re mine, Quinn. Always and forever.”\n\n“Promise?”\n\n“Promise.” He meant it, with every breath he took, every beat of his heart, and within that moment as he covered her body with his-\n\nhe had never felt so sure of anything in his life.\n\n------------------- \nShall the tale end here? \n\nShall it move forth and elaborate upon their future? \n\nFind out soon! Promise 2 COMING SOON!", ""),
        StaticBook("Strange Letter", "§bKaitlyn", "For the Ratti brothers as their first task of the ambassadors of Sutica, it's their immediate mission to receive compensation from the emperor of Oren. They must not come back empty handed.\n\n*A signature and print is delicately and cautiously forged.*", ""),
        StaticBook("The Flagship v2", "§bThomas Denims III", "THE FLAGSHIP VOL II\nSnow's Maiden, 1594.\n\nContents:\n-John d'Amaury Captured, Escapes\n-A New Grand King\n-Kingdom of Lorraine\n-Uproar in Haelun'or\n-Criticism of Dominion\n-Market Journal\n\nJOHN D'AMAURY\n--Captured--\n--Escapes--\n\nThe newly minted King of Lorraine, John d'Amaury, was taken into custody by Orenian forces under unclear circumstances. Imperial officials attempted to move him\n\nto the Dominion of Malin, but the King was liberated by rebel cavalry numbering about 15 following a shorty clash with numerically superior (estimated 50) Orenian and Dominion escorts.\n\nA NEW GRAND KING!\n\nFollowing Emperor Philip I Frederick's execution of Grand King Algoda, the Senate, composed of each of the dwarven clans, convened to elect a new Grand King. Three candidates were nominated: Bastion Ireheart by\n\nGrandaxe and Doomforged, Wulfstag Ireheart by Frostbeard, and Kilgrim Irongut by the Ironguts. After speeches by the three candidates, Bastion Ireheart was elected with the support from Grandaxe, Doomforged, and Starbreaker clans.\n\nThe new Grand King provided the following comment to The Flagship: \"Without the dwed of Urguan, the crown means nothing, and the dwed who wears the crown, means nothing. I wish to thank all those who supported my campaign for the Grand Kingship, and\n\npromise, that upon my coronation, I will, with the help of the very dwed who make up this stoic nation, bring back the glory of the past. I will, through dedication, passion, and perseveranc, make the Grand Kingdom of Urguan truly grand once more.\n\nDUCHY OF LORRAINE            DECLARES          ---INDEPENDECE---\n\nThe Archduchy of Lorraine, formerly a realm of the Holy Oren Empire, has declared independence, citing the tyranny and incompetence of the current Emperor. This comes following an\n\nattempted coup of the Duchy instigated by the current Imperial administration that places Ser Otto in charge of the ducal city of Metz. However, the rest of Lorraine has pledged to the rebellion, including the Despotate of Nicea and other holdings.\n\nThis has greatly boosted the Stauntons with both territory and men.\n\nSTAUNTON REBELS SCORE VICTORIES IN\n----SKIRMISHES----\n\nThere have not been any major confrontations since the now famous (or infamous) Battle of the Gorge, but there have been numerous small to mid sized skirmishes in this war, and the\n\nrebels have prevailed more often then not. This is a remarkable reversal of the norm, as Orenian forces typically prove victorious in the brutally savage and quick fighting and raiding that makes up most modern wars. It remains to be seen how this will\n\nimpact Orenian morale or if it will translate to further losses in the coming days, when large open field battles and seiges will predominate.\n\nAXIOT COLATION \n--ANNOUNCED--\n\nThose rebelling against the Holy Oren Emperor as well as their allies have announced a treaty that adopts a structure for their joint effots to remove Philip I Frederick from power. Along with the\n\nStauntons of Courland, the d'Amaurys of Lorraine, the Grand Kingdom of Urguan, Krugmar, and several other form Orenian realms are signatories. This treaty likely represents one of the largest coalitions of men and material ever arrayed against the\n\nHoly Oren Empire since the Great War during Anthos, which ultimately ended in the collapse of the HOE and the rise of a handful of independent Kingdoms (Ruska, Savoy, Renatus, Salvus, and Hanseti), from where we can find the roots of the political\n\nsituation that caused the Duke's War as well as the current conflict.\n\nMARKET JOURNAL:\nIron: 2 mina Kal'Omith\nGold: 1 mina Kal'Omith\nDiamond: 4 mina Kal'O\nLogs: .02 mina Sutica\nHay Bale: .01 Sutica\nJohannesburg\n\nUPROAR IN HAELUN'OR\n\nThere has been much confusion and consternation in Haeluno'or as competing groups claim to be leading the city and maintain that they have the authority to enter into treaties. Much of the conflict appears to be rooted\n\nin the vigil affair. It seems as if one side has taken decisive action regarding the current rebellion while the other has claimed that said action is illegitimate, though one wonders what they hope to accomplish with lengthy missives few take the time to\n\nread. Updates on the situation will be provided, hopefully after details become clearer.\n\nCRITICISM OVER DOMINION INVOLVEMENT -----MOUNTS-----\n\nThe government of the Dominion of Malin is facing mounting criticism over its involvement on behalf of the HOE in its internal conflict as citizens question why elven blood must be\n\nspilled on what could potentially be the losing side, resulting in a catastrophe for the mali. The government has attempted to assuage fears, but one does not see an easy resolution on the horizon. War is coming to the Dominion, and judging how forces\n\nacquitted themselves poorly under the current leadership, it remains to be seen if the correct choice has been made.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sanhar: B. Blood", "§bDominus Bein", "Sanhar\n     Born of Blood\n\n      Dominus Bein\n\nThe riverside attack came quickly as a surprise, they jumped through the glass in the gatehouse and ran outside. They stabbed Jackel through the chest before he could even get his sword out.\n\nBein pulled out his sword and managed to cut down one before the others slashed him down. The Riversiders held Sanjezal for two days before they surrenderd it back to Bein Very soon after a counterattack was made on Riverside.\n\nIt soon erupted into a Civil War. Four sides battled it out. The Orcs of Krugmar, The Blackguard, the Riverside Rebels and the Riverside Loyalists. The Blackguard left after killing all the Riversiders they could find, but underground the battle\n\nwent on between the Rebels and the Loyalists. Riznam led the Rebels to victory over the Loyalists and their Leader Gorn drove them out. When he returned to the top though, he saw the Orcs had claimed Riverside as their own.\n\nThe Orcs however stayed and decided to build a new town there. With permission from Warlord Tythus, they began building Sanhar. Dominus bein was put in charge and he and his workers destroyed part of a mountain and demolished\n\nRiverside before the began building. Sanhar was built in the normal Orc way, \"We will build it out of nice material untill we run out of materials, and use anything else\". Soon they completed the walls, then the buildings, then the shops,\n\nthen the outer walls and finally the Fort where Bein now Resides. Sanhar has been born, but not of Treaties or happy working, but of blood of many soilders and innocents ,and we must never forget what happend in those battles.\n\nThe writings of Dominus Bein on Sanhar: Born of Blood Year: 1300 Scrolled by Librarien_Tribune_Ulrack (TheMiner15)", ""),
        StaticBook("Undru's Notes", "§bThe Lord of Undru", "One will always come.\n\nIt never dissappears as long as the Sildur is up in it's hands.\n\nWe won't die.\n\nIt's not the End\n\nWe are the End.\n\n\n\nDeath is only the start.", ""),
        StaticBook("Redstone Studies", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "Day 1\n\nI, Gallidron Elindrow, have begun my study of Redstone. I intend to gain greater understanding of this substance that I may learn to manipulate it to more fascinating purpose, perhaps even that of an arcane one.\n\nTo this end I am beginning with basic observations of the material in question. Redstone is found in the earth as an ore much like iron, however it is fragile in nature and breaks down into a dust when extracted. Not unlike Thanhium when it is extracted,\n\nwhich causes me to think the two might have a connection, but this is just a musing of mine.\n\n The dust is coarse to the touch and grainy, but gives off a slight shine. It is capable of being compressed into a block and then seems to be much more dur\n\nthan in its natural form as an ore. Hence it does not break apart when struck. The compressed block is decidedly smoother than the dust or the ore, but this is just a product of the refinement process.\n\nThis concludes my observations of its physical nature.\n\nDay 2\n\nRedstone is primarily used for its conductive nature. My experiments today are centered around this aspect. Redstone is so conductive that it can be laid in a line as a powder and still hold an electrical current.\n\nThis is a common way to use the material, as it is not necessary to enclose redstone while transferring power through it. The current will eventually taper off however, thus showing that while uninsulated some of the power is indeed lost in transfer.\n\nA compressed block of redstone can obviously hold more energy and act as a greater conduit due to its increased mass. More water flows through a bigger pipe, the same is true of energy it would seem.\n\nAs well, a compressed block of redstone seems to produce and electrical current all on it’s own. Whether this is the result of some electrical energy generation that occurs within the higher density of the block or just latent charge held within its form\n\nis a matter for debate.\n\nRedstone is used for transferring electrical energy and can be used as a conduit for errant electrical static, especially if one has a large quantity of it available in the open air.\n\nDay 3\n\nI have enlisted the aid of a Tier 5 Electromancer in this next phase of my studies. It was my intent to record the behavior of redstone when encountering measured amounts of electrical charge. Here are the results.\n\nControl: The electromancer is set up 15 meters from a stone target. Upon firing a single bolt of lightning of what I was assured is “medium strength.” They hit the target at it’s center.\n\nExperiment 1\nPurpose: To determine if the presence of uncharged redstone can alter the course of an electrical discharge.\n\nSet up: A stone target set 15 meters from the Electrical source, I.E. The Electromancer. Between the source and target are 5 lines of redstone powder, each one separated by 1 meter of distance, the lines are connected on the sides and hold no charge.\n\nResult: The source fires a singular bolt of electricity at the target and the bolt curved down to strike the base of the target.\n\nExperiment 2\nPurpose: To determine if the presence of charged redstone can alter the course of an electrical discharge.\n\nSet up: A stone target set 15 meters from the Electrical source, I.E. The Electromancer. Between the source and target are 5 lines of redstone powder, each one separated by 1 meter of distance, the lines are connected on the sides and hold a charge.\n\nResult: The source fires a bolt of electricity which immediately arcs down to the red stone. Both the bolt and the red stone are consumed entirely.\n\nExperiment 3\n\nPurpose: to determine the effect of a condensed block of redstone upon an electrical discharge.\n\nSet up: A stone target set 15 meters from the Electrical source, I.E. The Electromancer. Approximately halfway between the source and the target and a meter to the right (as reckoned by the source) is a single block of condensed redstone.\n\nResult. The source fires a bolt of electricity which veers directly to the redstone block. The Block takes the charge and remains intact, but does give off a somewhat brighter glow.\n\nConclusion: Redstone is perfectly capable of affecting the trajectory of an electrical discharge, magical or otherwise. It seems that Redstone that is already laden with a charge is more effective at doing so. It is my understanding That the Redstone\n\nlines were consumed in experiment 2 because their mass was not great enough to take the energy of the bolt. The block of Redstone in experiment 3 however, was both more dense and possessed over all more mass and so could withstand the sheer voltage.\n\nThis concludes journal 1 of my findings on Redstone and its properties. \n\nGallidron Elindrow\n\nPublished\n9th of Sun's Smile\n1600", ""),
        StaticBook("Dogger Bay", "§bImperial Historian", "The Battle of Dogger\n          Bay\n\nThe history of Imperial armed conflict at sea is one scattered and wildly misunderstood. Generals of the Empire can always harked to the tactics employed in the Battle of the Dreadfort, the Battle at Milvian Bridge,\n\nand the grace of the Dukes’ War’s field skirmishes as staples of human military tradition and excellence. But aside from the destruction of the dwarven fleet by the King of Hanseti during the First Northern War in 1372, Orenian naval battles were not won\n\nthrough strategic brilliance, but by levee en masse: waves of Orenian men crashing against the decks of lesser ships in a dedicated assault against their heinous adversaries.\n\nThe Battle of Dogger Bay was no exception. Upon reading the\n\nCount of Estavar’s missive to the crown informing that the House of Ruric had intended a naval assault on the City of Felsen, the Lord High Admiral, the 4th Duke of Courland, was charged with repelling the incoming invasion and ensuring the safety  of the\n\nof the loyalist strongholds in West Avar. The Orenian fleet set sail on the fifth of the Grand Harvest led by HIM The Princess Phillipa, the Orenian flagship constructed by the late Holy Orenian Emperor John I Frederick in a planned naval invasion of the\n\ndwarven capital. The heavy carrack sailed through Oren waters, flanked by the battered HIM The Empress Adelheid and HIM Saint Julia along with numerous lesser galleys. But in three days they had spotted the rebel expedition force, spearheaded by the\n\nQuadinaros, which had dwarfed the Princess Phillipa with a titanic hull thrice the size of the Emperor’s own warship. \n\nEach battleship, as if stray hounds in a Felsen alley, sized each other up and inched closer, the waves crashing against their hulls.\n\nAs the two met closer, a massive shape appeared below them. “Pull back!” The call was too late. The ear was pierced with no noise, the hulking wooden beasts tossed aside as if simple men. Between the two ships had appeared a massive whale, its stomach\n\n ripped from its back and left abreast for the whole world. The ships, having been too late in their reaction, now sat opposed to another before the carcass, unable to maneuver past safely without giving their adversary an advantage.\n\nSeconds turned into minutes, and minutes to hours as they sloshed in the waves. Before long, long planks and small dinghies emerged from the Quadinaros, as the Dreadmen host swarmed the husk of the whale in a defensive position. Emulating the rebels\n\nadvance, the Princess Phillipa released her vanguard as well to meet them in open combat led by the papal prince Charles Philip.\n\nWith the sun at their backs and the songs of St. Thomas in the air, the Orenian levies took to amphibious assault upon the\n\nwhale's opened ribcage. They were met by volleys of arrows by the encamped rebel forces, with those dead staining the Shattered Sea red before the Imperial forces took landing upon the pectoral fin. Wave upon wave of Orenian levies beached upon the\n\nthe whale’s appendage, storming up the rotten blubber to meet the Norlanders with steel in hand, their march supported by the arrows of Elf and Savoyard. \n\nFor hours the two armies clashed upon the whale, dead men failing deep into the\n\nocean below. But imperial grit prevailed over the cobbled together coalition of pirates, barbarians, and bandits. Slowly but surely, the brunt of the Empire barrelled through the enemy armies. When Lord Oscar Lancefeld and Hetman Sveneld had forced\n\n‘Rat Tom’ Ruric and his Dreadguard into a hasty retreat through single combat, the Norlander line collapsed and the rebel army entered into ultimate disarray.\nPleas of victory and attempts to holdfast had fallen to deaf ears as Dreadman took to rafts,\n\ndinghies, and even piecemeal flesh to make their retreat back to their battleship. The imperial standard stood tall and proud over the great stinking mass of the fallen whale, a testament of imperial dignity over the filth of the world. Men rejoiced,\n\nthough they knew not the battle was over; the Quadinaros was yet to be seized. Tarchar Turkmen, Larian regiments, and the Nauzica honorguard began to plan an assault upon the great ship itself to seize the day and crush the remnants of the Ruric army.\n\nBut however, the assault never came.\n\nThe whale began to shake violently, the waves of the Shattered Sea retching and reaping against the nearby galleys. Erupting swiftly from the red waters came the gigantice tentacle,\n\nwrapping about the mass of the Quadinaros without hinder or hault. The rebels cried and attempted to attack the large arm, but to no avail. The mass was ripped in one fatal thrash, before the beast below the water showed itself to its victims.\n\nIt was none other that the Beast of the Shattered Sea: the Vierathan. Rumored by sailors to be the vengeful form of the drowned King Olivier, taking its spite upon unsuspecting merchant vessels, the kraken loomed above the Quadinaros as a mountain toants.\n\nWith its unsoundly strength, its second tentacle ripped through the hull of the flagship from below, splitting the once jewel of Avar like a knife to butter. \n\nWater rushed into the split flagship, the chaos ensuing gave the Imperial Navy\n\nchance to split open the rebel line. The hired sellsails of the rebels, once seeing the splinter of the Quadinaros before them, unfurled their lifeboats and retreated south,  diminishing the numbers of the Ruric invasion fleet by half.\n\nThe Imperial vessels crashed into the leftover galleys which still held their foolhardy blockade, making quick work of the undermanned, inexperienced lesser ships which sacrificed their resources to man the huge beast Quadinaros.\n\nThe remnants of the once great Ruric fleet, under the ineffective command of Thomas Ruric, fled south, battered, broken, and bowed before the might of the Empire.\n\nWith minimal vessels lost, the Imperial Fleet reformed by the Duke of Courland’s orders,\n\nretaking formation at the edge of Dogger Bay under the leadership of The Princess Phillipa, which hauled the remains of the Quadinaros as war spoils. Those captured at sea were given choice between the galleys or Lord Sigmar Vladov’s axe; most of them,\n\nwith the urging of their captors, chose to serve in the open sea, being assured a later death as war fodder. With the shouts of victory and the mourning for the dead, the Imperial Navy continued their course, with new mission: capture the\n\nrebel stronghold of Ostavar and decimate the Ruric Rebellion once and for all.\n\n10th of the Grand Harvest, 1557\nDogger Bay, the Shattered Sea.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal I", "§bRoopak Khalin", "Hi, my name is Roopak Khalin. This is my journal. The reason why I am writing this is because I wish to document the events that are about to follow. I hope one day my brother finds this, if he's still alive, or my mother, or maybe even my children if I\n\ndecide to have some. \n\nIt all started going downhill about 2 years ago when my brother, Silus went missing, assumed dead. I have no idea what's happened to him, maybe he's dead, maybe he's returned to the life of banditry, maybe he's perfectly fine but is\n\njust ignoring me. I don't know. I send him birds, but I get no reply. Anyways, about a month or two ago the Salvian civil war started. I was casually walking through Salvus when I saw Lily. I turned around to speak to her about the farms moving location.\n\nShe was weeping. I asked her why, and she told me something bad was about to happen. She said she didn't want it to be like this. She pointed behind me, to the horizon. I suddenly knew what was happening. Silv'ar and Ehsan were in danger. I was just about\n\nto set off for them, but then suddenly a Ghoul appeared behind me! The Ghoul tried to attack me, but luckily a kind Elf helped me and shot a arrow in the Ghoul's arm. The Ghoul didn't fall, and sliced my arm. I was bleeding, and it was incredibly painful.\n\nNext thing I know the rebels who attacked Silv'ar and Ehsan walk up to me, and Enrique is with them. He tells me to run, so I do. The rebels were after me, so I ran for my life. Luckily none of them followed me, and I managed to get back to the Caliphate.\n\nA kind Cleric healed my arm, and I told her what had happened. She prayed for my safety, and I left the clinic. I recieved a bird, from David. He wanted to meet up with me. I waited for him at the Caliphate gates. I met up with him, and he told me to stay\n\nout of the war. He said I was like a brother to him, even though he was slaughtering my friends and family. But then again, he saved my life. He told me to give him a list of people I didn't want dead, and I gave him a small list of three people. Lemik,\n\nLinda and Giliath. They were just friends that were on the top of my head. He told me Lemik was already safe, but Linda wasn't co-operating with the rebels. He also said that he would make sure Giliath would be safe.\n\nI still think I will fight in this\n\nwar, I shall not sit idly as I watch my friends and family get slaughtered.", ""),
        StaticBook("Unfinished Story", "§bPrince Toren of Malinor", "The Unfinished Tale\n     Prince Toren\n    (RubberStamp)\n\nThey reclined in a grassy part of the garden; the encompassing mist parting just enough for them to see beyond the forest pines at the distant and unreachable glistening sea. The ocean breeze gently swirled around them and stirred their flaxen hair.\n\n It was a small respite and comfort for them - sitting beside one another like this. A rare insouciant smile graced her lips as she braided a windflower crown. The air was peaceful and silent, almost lazy. And for once they felt no dire urgency.\n\nHere, for now and this time, he was not the Hero and she was not the Princess. They were but lovers beneath the cerulean sky, whose titles and duties carried little weight. Upon the grass, beside her dearly beloved, she had no country to mind;\n\nno mother-queen to please and no insolent prince to wed. Likewise he, under the golden sun crowned by his paramour with a windflower circlet, had no malevolence to challenge; no demesne to save and no Princess to win. \"Tell me of us,\" he encouraged.\n\nShe tilted her head slightly to one side as though to ask if he had forgotten. He smiled reassuringly at her for how could he ever forget? She grinned in an amused way, understanding it was her turn to spin a story - their personal fairytale.\n\n\"Once upon a time when our souls were first entwined, innumerable worlds ago when the realm was greener with new found life, and when we were young.,\" she began. \"There was a fair Lady and a valorous knight, whose love transcended even time.\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Music & Silence", "§bVannessa Longridge", "Music with no Sound\n\nHe kept his gaze down, shuffling his legs, trying to hurry down the narrow streets. Men leered at him, dwarfing him while elves continually scowled at him whenever he passed by.\n\nHis gaze suddenly tilted, and pain filled his eyes. He looked up at the guard, who's ribs had just collided with him, while his friends chuckled behind. He picked himself up and continued to his destination, a shabby 2 storey building.\n\nThe man let himself in, a sense of relief and calm washing over him. He smiled at the magnificent instrument in front of him and sat on its leather plush seat. His fingers began to move, as if they were on their own accord making beautiful sounds out\n\nof the Grand Piano.\n\nWhile he played his talent, he was unaware of the menacing eyes set on him from the window.  \n\nHe continued playing the symphony before leaving shortly before dusk.\n\nHis discriminatory routine continued the next day, his thoughts only on playing that Piano again. When at last he reached his house, a sense of fear suddenly came close to overwhelming him. He creaked open the broken door and saw what he dreaded.\n\nHis piano, smashed and broken left against the floor. Tears at once appeared to his eyes as he ran to his piano, cradling and feeling its touch. He sat on the now torn plush leather seat.\nHis fingers moved across the fractured keys, hearing music that\n\nwould never be heard again.", ""),
        StaticBook("Staves", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "The\n          Wizard\n             &\n        The  Staff\n```~~~~~`\\I/'~~~~~'''\n\n\n            By\n Gallidron   Elindrow\n\nThe staff. This iconic piece of equipment is placed firmly in the minds of individuals everywhere as the tool of every wizard and mage. We all can imagine an elderly and bearded wizard, swathed in robes and leaning upon a gnarled staff.\n\nMost of us tend to think that the staff or even the rod and wand are an indispensable part of the mage’s arsenal. while it is in fact useful to a mage and can help to focus their arcane might, staves are, in fact, ultimately unnecessary.\n\nThe staff is a crutch in a literal and figurative sense. They help the often frail, physically weak, or aged mage to stand or to walk long distances. In this way they are of basic utility.\n\nIn the figurative sense these implements are useful in helping a mage focus their powers on a physical point in the world, the end of their staff. This simply makes it easier for a mage’s mind to form the spell\n\nand choose a place to bring it into the world. Magic after all is developed wholly in the mind before it becomes a reality. A veteran mage may have no need whatsoever for such a focus or aid.\n\nAnother use for the staff is to store a spell or spells within it to be cast when certain criteria are met. For example, an evocationist stores the spell, that summons a fireball, within their staff. The spell is set to go off when the mage\n\npoints the staff forward and says the command word or words. This can be incredibly useful, though also potentially dangerous. Make the command word to obvious or likely to be said, and a bystander could accidently set off your stored\n\nspell while you're having afternoon tea. Of course, make the criteria too complicated and you might not be able to get the spell to work when you really need it.\n\nThis of course, doesn’t even go into the possibility of a misfire. At this point you are not casting the spell with the same level of control you would have, had you drawn it straight from the void. The fireball could be set offin any given direction,\n\neven back at you.It is for this reason that a many mages will use a focusing crystal which has the ability to funnel your spell in the right direction.\n\nI, myself, am practiced in the trade of carpentry. As such I have made a few staves in my time. The experienced woodworker or the astute buyer of such things will note that some staves are of better make than others.\n\nThis, to my knowledge, affects nothing that the staff does magically. This is merely a statement of finery and fashion. A finer carved staff is simply nicer to look at and perhaps more comfortable to hold.\n\nOnce again, it is my hope that this book has been both interesting and informative. It is my sincere desire that you are left the better for having read it.\n\n-Gallidron Elindrow\npublishing date  10th of Deep Cold, 1519\n\nPlease read my guide to arcane magic!\n\n\"An Encylopedic Arcanum\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Thanhium", "§bOrithur", "-- == Thanhium == --\n\nWhat is Thanhium?\n\nThanhium in its most natural form is an ore burried beneath the earth, bearing a similarity to the commonly decorative ore known commonly as 'Lapis'. However, the traits of Thanhium\n\nare quite different, and easy to spot. For once, Thanhium is often located in incredibly large veins of ore close to the surface, and are consistently found in areas covered in both snow and frost, but as I will explain later, this is no coincidence.\n\nThanhium in its ore form is significantly more brittle than Lapis, but it is most noticible by its freezing aura. Thanhium is incredibly cold to the touch, and when in a large amount, like a vein of ore, it is capable of changing the very nature of the\n\nbiome it resides in to one of a deep cold, ridden with frost and snow. One example of this would be the Frozen North of Anthos, that was only frozen due to the masses of Thanhium ore burried beneath its surface.\n\nIs it dangerous?\n\nThanhium is one of the most destructive, and toxic substances known to our world, particularly when ingested. Thanhium is quite poisonous to all mortal men, however its affects vary between mages and non-mages.\n\nWhile it is known to have the victim struck with intense headaches, in mages it interferes with their personal supply of manner, and from here the effects may vary. Some mages report having a massive rush of uncontrollable mana, others, more commonly,\n\nclaim that the Thanhium negates their magical power entirely. Non-mages would find themselves arush with a newfound power they can't possibly hope to understand. They would become quite surged and overwhelmed with mana, likely rendering them uncouncious,\n\nor even killing them outright. Death is possible with both mages and non-mages alike, and it has been recorded that close proximity to Thanhium for an extended period of time, causes severe cases of madness.\n\nWhat do I do with it?\n\nThanhium must be processed and purified for its usefulness to be extracted. A variety of methods exist and many scholars of Thanhium's nature will give you a different example on how to bring the ore\n\nto its purest form, creating that of a 'shard' or 'crystal. It is important to note that the Thanhium does not generate cold, it instead draws in heat and leaves cold in its wake, transforming this heat into mana. It is for this reason that Thanhium in\n\nits purest form is commonly used to empower enchantments, and keep them sustained. Enchantments can tap into their supply of mana and feed off it indefinately while it continues to drain heat from the air to fuel itself. The ore\n\nas a rule is more useful when in purified form, and from here it has a variety of uses, ranging from a powerful explosive, to a deadly poison, to a useful attachment to an enchantment, allowing for enchantments to be sustained with mana, and a great deal\n\nmore. I have personally found ways to forge unique armours fashioned from Thanhic alloys, and have studied into the effects of harnessing the power of Thanhium to change the very weather.\n\nWhat more is there to Thanhium?\n\nThe short answer, is that we do not know. Constantly new discoveries are made surrounding Thanhium and its many properties. The study of Thanhium is a particularly rewarding field to any\n\naspiring scholar. Its potential is almost limitless, but it is to be noted that while great things may be achieved through Thanhium, it is in its nature a destructive element. While it is capable of achieving great good, it is admittedly easier to achieve\n\ngreat evil. Responsibility is a necessity when handling Thanhium, for in its study I know from experience that its dangers become quite apparent, its potential as a weapon is often stumbled upon.", ""),
        StaticBook("On Eternal Laws", "§bLorolith Iira", "On Eternal Laws\n\n-----=====+=====-----\n\nAeternum Iuris\n\n-By Lorolith Iira\n\nJust as the reasonable mortals of this universe have confined their societies to the order of rule of law. This is moral and legislative law. Similarly, it would appear that the universe itself has (at least in the past, leading up to now) confined itself\n\nto working 'eternal laws'. These laws, like moral and legislative laws, regulate behaviour. But instead of regulating the behaviour of conscious agents, they regulate the bahviour of nature itself.\n\nWithin this book I aim to dicuss why I think these laws\n\nprove to be persistant as well as my own understanding of existing laws of the physical universe. This piece is an essential companion to anyone wishing to delve into the field of natural philosophical study.\n\nContents:\n\n1) Persistence.\n2) The law of equivalent exchange. \n3) Laws of interaction.\n4) How we may hope to understand these laws in the future.\n\nChapter 1\n-----==========-----\n\nPersistence\n\nAs it would seem, at the very moment I write these words, the world is 'ordered'. Meaning, it seems to continue to be stable (upon reflection of past events) and similar causes produce similar effects. Thing I drop fall down. When my skin is cut, I draw\n\nblood. When a moving object interacts with another stationary object, the stationary object recieves some part of the first object's speed. I could go on. However, it follows that these results have only been observed in controlled circumstances. Outside\n\ninfluences can always alter observation. As is a pain in formal study. But still, these rules persist. I would also argue that these laws have *always* persisted. There would not have been any time after the birth of the material world that these rules\n\nwould not have existed. \n\nI say I know this because it would seem that the order of the present is contingent on the order of the past. I.e. if things didn't always fall down, we would observe strange chaos in the world around us as some part of our world\n\nbe absent, sent off into the abyss of the heavens. There are also rules of existence that our very lives are contingent on. If the rules of nature did not persist in our past, little is to stop nature itself destroying the lives of all descendants through\n\napocolyptic storms and quakes. Yet, most likely due to the natural restrictions on these powers, we are still here to discuss. This is the simple reason that I beleive it is necessary that these laws exist.\n\nChapter 2\n-----==========-----\n\nThe Law of Equivalent Exchange.\n\nThe law of 'equivalent' exchange is, I would argue, the longest known physical law. Not only is it extremely intuitive but it has become clear within the practice of alchemy since the ancients first tried their luck within the art. Simply, the law is a\n\nprinciple that states that you can never get more 'out' than you put 'in'. Most alchemists (however effective in their trade) who haven't done extensive study will know this law to mean that you cannot recieve more from the properties of any final\n\nproduct than from the properties of composit parts. A potion created for healing will only be able to do so because their composing parts had properties that, once taken together, allow for this to happen. Essentially, there are set properties allowed to\n\ncome from certain types of ingredients. However, this law, as far as I can see, applies universally. Eternally. For example, when we alchemists create these new substances, we can weigh them and find that the final weight is equal to the total weight of\n\ncomposit parts. Nothing extra has been 'created' and nothing has been 'destroyed'. \n\nThis concept also exists within magic, it would seem. It's well known to all mages that, once something is 'evoked' from the void, it will *always* return. This is\n\nessentially a 'magical' embodyment of the law of equivalent exchange. You cannot *end* with more than you started with. No matter how long it sticks around. \n\nHowever, one problem I found myself with when considering this was the idea that although the\n\nphysically evoked substance of any spell cannot stick around, its effects on our physical universe *does*. \nI will explain this problem after first defining the term 'energy'.\n\n'Energy' as it is commonly used, is vauge in its definition. I have only\n\never heard it comprehensively a few times. However, here is my own: \n\n'Energy' is the property or state of being able to impose physical change. \n\nFor example, a vibrating ball would have a high energy. This is because, when another object comes\n\ninto contact with it, it would impose motion on that other object. Most (if not all) of the physical 'change' I will be referring to will be to do with the idea of physical motion. \n\nNow, the idea that a fire can be evoked and have it's physical\n\nchanges remain, seems to involve having physical change come from nothing. \nAllow me to illustrate:\n\nWhen a normal fire is lit, the energy from the fire (heat could indeed be considered energy since it has the capacity to burn and break down matter as\n\nfuel, hence imposing change) comes from originally striking the flame. An evoked flame essentially comes from nothing and, once it has done its work, goes back into nothing. If the results of this burning fire remain, the universe is in a state equivalent\n\nto having a fire burn without a starting flame. \n\nMuch like the existence of physical material, 'energy' (as previously defined) cannot come from nothing or simply disappear, it would seem. All motion and change in the universe appears to come from\n\npreceding motion and change. Set up a line of balls. Roll one towards them and watch the chain reaction of transfer of motion. The energy of each ball comes from the energy of the last.\n\nNow, if magic itself were to follow the principle of equivalent\n\nexchange, as I am to argue, it takes the mana of the 'evoker' to actually keep this change in existence. This makes sense because, unlike the material substance of a spell (such as earth evoking), energy transfered from this material into the physical\n\nworld *does* exist before the spell is cast. In the form of mana. This is what mana truley is. It is pure energy, as I have defined. Having mana is identical to having the potential to cause physical change in the universe *through* access to the void.\n\nSo, if I am right, we can conclude that the mana used in evoking some kind of magical substance from the void is in some way equal to the mana/energy required to actually drag this substance into the material world and the energy 'created' by this magical\n\nsubstance.\n\nThis would explain why maintaining a spell without properly casting would cost the caster much less mana. It would still cost some as this magical substance would interact with the physical world by emitting heat or interacting with the airs\n\nand materials around it whilst being maintained. Most of the mana would have to come from the real interactions between that magical substance and its target. Then, once that substance has returned to the void, the energy it has 'created' remains. This\n\nenergy is acutally sapped from the caster's mana. \n\nThis rational definition of 'mana', to my knowledge, has never existed before. We can think of it as essentially equivalent to the actual heat of a fire, or the motion of the winds. It is just as much an\n\nimposing force of nature as anything else.\n\nThere are some ways I can test these assertions soon enough. I plan on seeing the relationship between consumed mana and imposed motion at some point in the future with the help of a telekenetic mage in a\n\ncontrolled environment.\n\nI plan on releasing one or several volumes titled 'Science of Magic' that explore how would consider the laws of magic and the various mana to energy transfers that happen in different areas of the magic arts.\n\nIf anyone has found the contents of this chapter of this tome particularly confounding, yet they wish to inquire further, you may feel free to contact me directly to ask questions or even help with this area of research.\n\nChapter 3\n-----==========-----\n\nLaws of Interaction\n\nThere are, similar to the law of 'equivalent exchange', laws that govern the interactions between physical things, it would seem. Not only their existence. \n\nI wish to briefly discuss these along with what has been discussed in the previous chapter.\n\nThese come as a mixture of my own findings in research and my further reading.\n\n----------\n\nIt is clear, as I have explained previously that energy can be transfered between physical bodies. Although I have no way to quantify\n\n'energy' at this time, we can observe the transfer of motion upon collision of physical objects.\n\nNot only this, but we can observe that, once an object has recieved a forceful impulse, it begins to slow down. I beleive (although I cannot at this time,\n\ndescribe mathematically) that what truley slows this object down is the influence of surroundings like air and wind. Really, if you were to set an object in motion and nothing were to collide with it or slow it down, this motion may continue constantly\n\nforever. Simply put, if you try to move your hand through water (a thicker fluid), you experience more resistance than through air (a thinner fluid). It's harder to do so. You can therefore imagine that, if these mediums were to be removed *all together*,\n\nnothing would stop motion as nothing resists it. \n\nIt would follow, actually, that imposing motion on an object actually causes an increase in its speed, rather than giving it a set speed, as many may believe. Especially since, without this imposition,\n\nspeed can still be maintained.\n\nChapter 4\n-----==========-----\n\nHow we May Hope to Understand These Laws in the Future\n\nI hope that, upon further reflection on the details and observtaions I have discussed in this book, I cand find ways in greater detail to describe the course of motions in our universe. I have yet, as I have said, to collect detailed observations to test\n\nmy theories about energy transfer from mana. Which itself may be difficult to do without detailed mathametical basis. \n\nSoon I wish to be able to calculate the motions of all objects in our universe. If not in great detail, at least enough to have be\n\nable to truley watch the work of whatever gods lay beyond the heavens.", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes", "§bAerith Oranor", "[!] Each of the papers seem to have been written on different times or days.\n\nBloody javelin to the back, how terrible that could have gone...\n\nFighting a false goddess, oh joy how great that'll be...\n\nWill it be anything like Gazardiel?\n\nI wonder if he might come back...\n\nWill I even survive either?\n\n[!] Near unreadable sentences would be found on a few pieces of paper, the words that could understood were \"survive\", \"live\" and \"die\"\n\nI don't know if I've spent enough time with either Eris or the child after what the Princess told me...\n\nWill I really make it through the trial...?\n\nWhat even is the trial...?\n\n\"Some come out the trial changed.\" That's what her words were...\n\nHow much will I truly change?\n\nWill it help with my sanity?\n\nOr will it not?\n\nAmara's birth was probably the one thing that brought the most joy in my life...It's as though I truly felt sane for once...\n\n[!] More unreadable sentences accompanied by random sketches\n\nIf you're reading this, it most likely means I either forgot about these papers while submitting to my own madness for some time or I perished somewhere, somehow. And I hope it isn't the latter...\nIf it is the latter...\n(continue on next page)\n\nThen I succumbed to my own madness, was slain by the impersonating goddess, failed my final trial or something.\nBut anyways...\n\nIf I really did perish or disappear, I just wanted to let you know Eris, that I love you and Amara dearly. For nothing has brought greater joy in my life than the two of you.\n\n\n             -Aerith", ""),
        StaticBook("The Volcano", "§bTippen Oaklend", "10th of The Grand Harvest, 1506\n\nIt seems as though a Volcano has began to errupt near the Oasis grove. Many of the druids and dedicants, including myself have become quite worried. There seems to be quite a large amount of white smoke coming from\n\nthe opening, but it's not too hot, only challenging to breathe. I attempted to convince the druids to let me descend in the volcano, just a bit in order to study it further, but none of them would condone this. I have decided to set up camp at the base\n\nof the volcano, in order to see how it acts and reacts to certain things.\n\nLooking from the top of the volcano there seems to be a small island in the molten lava, which containes gems and jewels of all sorts in the form of ore, and even solid blocks. The surrounding lava boils and bubbles, but does not rise.\n\nThe smoke at the top is very white and thick, it produces a scent similiar to sulfer and seems to be potentially toxic. I've ran tests by exposing certain natural substances to the smoke. Saplings and flowers would brown and wither, while anything that\n\noriginally came from the ground seemed to become stronger and calcified.\n\nOn certain surfaces of the volcano, some of the ore that can be seen in the middle of the lava can also be seen outside the volcano. Taking tests of this ore would prove that minerals from the ore closer to the volcano seemed to be much stronger and\n\nharder to form and tamper with than that of ores from mines.\n\nAfter studying the Volcano for a fair amount of time, I realize it isn't the Volcano, nor the lava that is the most impressive part. It's the heat. The heat that is capable of melting rock and boiling air. Where does it come from? How is it so\n\npowerful? I've been preforming more experiments with how the heat and magma react to precious materials.\n\nThe more I study the volcano, and the heat it produces, the more I am intruiged by the entire concept. Becoming a Dedicant was the best decision I've ever made. I'm glad I've joined this family.", ""),
        StaticBook("Verden's Review", "Jallentime", "I sent Gavin and Plonas to survey and lessen the presence of undead in a forest that had become infested with them.\n\nThey both brought back a specimen of an undead spider, and provided information vital to restoring the area.\n\n                          ->\n\nI taught Gavin about the dangers of the unnatural, and how we as druids not only look after nature, but also seek to remove that which is detrimental to the balance of the world.\n\nPlonas was asleep somewhere. You may want to give him a recap.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Realization", "§bSilv'ar Vanguard", "\"Dear Madam lily.\"\n*Hand Drawn Tree Would Sit here it would cover most of the page. It's Brances would weave and dive. Laced into the tree would be little leaves each containing a name. It's a family tree.\n\n\"I have come on to learn something. Something I knew deeply but feared all the same it. One of my most core belives has failed me. Infact it is the core belive of a whole race and people. The Laws of Gold and Silver have failed me.\n\nThis most likely means nothing to you but I hope to make it clear in this journal of my life and finally in my closing notes I will explain my new found understanding.\n\nThe Fires of Aegis. I was only told stories of this time as I was but a small child but these times forever haunted my father Eldorn for the rest of his life. As in the final mouments as he and my Mother Char'ame were rushing to leave my grandfather\n\nto the end with the remaining members of the White Ravens to prevent the dark forces from reaching the portal to the verge. \nNone the less I shall progress further. During the time spent in the Asulon rather intresting things\n\ntranspired. Of that the most important to my tale would be the seperation of the Elves. This is were the once united Mali slipt forming they're crude and weak ideals. The idea of purity rose from this. It's spiny ideals created me\n\nbut my father wasn't so easily tamed by it's will. Him and his wife Char'ame both found the laws just horrible. They felt all people all races were one and the same. Because of this they fled the city.\nI spent the next 160 years with them and the rest of\n\nFamily. helping to care for all of the adopted family members that my parrents brought into the Vanguard house hold. I loved each one of them as a brother and sister thinking nothing of they're 'Purity'. That is till we landed on the shores of Vailor.\n\nThis is where it all changed for me. It had only be two weeks since we had landed and my mother was deadly ill. It was belived to be one of the last cases of the plague from the fringes. We tried day and night to find a cure. Though\n\nthere was one place we had not tried. The Silver City of the Pure Elves. I knew that they held great alchemical knowlege. But Eldorn my father told me a I must not venture into thoughous walls because I would face untold horrors. I was navie and only\n\nThought of my mother's life. I ventured into the city. I passed every test of purity they had by the skin of my teeth. But I was in. I soon forgot even why I was there I was so involved with the ways of the Pure Elves.\n\nI belived every last scrap of information I was given. I studied the Silver and Golden laws to death. Some might even say I was a scholar in them. It wasn't till the faithful day when the last king of the Pure Elves killed 20 so called impure children by\n\nremoving every one of they're eyes while they were alive and pouring molten gold into they're eye sockets and finally hanging them by they're arms from the gates of the city did cracks begin to form in my head about what these laws really\n\nimplyed. They were sick laws that governed all. This is when I to fled the city shortly before it fell to the hand of Oren. I soon faced my dying father. Who told me of the final days of my mother who simple wanted to see her\nlong gone son\n\nwho left her on her death bed... *A small carefully drawn portrait of a well rounded elf's face would sit here. Her eyes firm but happy her lips gentle but demanding. at the bottom would be the name 'Char'ame Vanguard'\n\n\"Shortly after my father passed away I left in search of a new way forward. I found this with the Tahu'norian Elves. It was a small band of Elves who lived at the time at the foot of a small village called Salvus.\n\nI will keep this part short as it's a rather hard time in my life. I came to live with these Elves as my Cousin Ante'ame was one of them she was kind and led me out of my sadness of my time spent with the 'Pure Elves'. He spent his days\n\nworking the fields tending to the animals and generally just leading a calm life in the woods. till the events of 1501. When Salvus killed almost 70% of the Tahu'nor elves but I will keep that tale short. I was lost with the aparent death of my cousin\n\nthe last living family member I had. I found comfort in the laws of Silver and Gold beliving that they could under a fairer hand. I knew that the city of Haelu'nor was not the place to try this. I saw the place that killed my last love ones and I saw a\n\na spark. In the year 1505 I joined the Salvian Guard. and spent the next 6 years defending that city and all it belived. I met many of my current friends such as Lemik, Roopak, and Archrim all great lads. But most importantly I had a purpose I grasped for\n\nit to develop and create the world in which people could be the best they can be. Through the laws of Silver and Gold. Because of this I gained the title of Consul of Salvus. The Second in command of the nation in Vailor.\nBut these were\n\nturrbulent times. As you well know. With the birth of the Salvian Rebles under the rain of David Campos I was instated as the 2nd and last Chancellor of\nSalvus and for 3 months I fought to save the nation I belived in but failed.\nThrough your\n\nfear and kindness you gave many of us a way out. A safe way to Sutica. Where I once again as the old leader was voted in as the First Trade Prince of Sutica. but this is where my real tale starts. I had lost what I had strove for. I had lost my trust in\n\nthe laws of Silver and Gold. They had failed me once more. I didn't have my heart in the job and as such I felt unfit to rule. I stepped down after 2 years. Taking for the first time in 30 years a break from the world of politcs. I begain to look else\n\nfor some redeeming part of the laws of silver and gold and as a last act of trust I married a women I did not love. Lori'liem. A wonderful women I wasted. We had three children. Two were twins Alem'sion and Ale'sul. Both boys and we had\n\none girl. Lori'sul. When they were around the age of 17 and 23 Lori'leim killed her self. It was a dark time when I simplely fell apart. My children disowned me as I simple didn't love or care for them. I found my last peace in my work as a builder.\n\nI poured my heart and soul into every design hoping to find something they're for my dead heart and my dying mind. Fast forward a bit till you become the Trade Princess. I saw you as yet another leader whom I would serve to the best of my ability\n\nIt wasn't untill I was mid through the redesign of the city when I started to relized who you really were... *A small sketch of a park with a house in the corner would sit here covering the rest of the page.* such a kind and wonderous women\n\none who I would relish to oppertunity to learn and spent more time with. Though I should make my intensions clear. I am not seeking... such a crude term but Sex or Children. Simply someone to share my never endding days with. I have already had my fair\n\nshare of children and simplely do not which for more. *Finally a carefully sketched out and colored drawning of Lilyana sitting on a bench next to a large willow tree with a small set of roses. A small turtle would be sitting in the edge of the pond its\n\n*head looking up towards the Madam who was flipping through a small booklet her silken light blue dress would flow slightly in the wind her eyes would be looking down into the pond. They're deep green pupils gazing down into the water of the lightly\n\ncolored water* The reason I ask you is because I have learned my beloved laws of Silver and Gold were never the truth. *The Book would end with another smaller tree*\n\n((OOC NOTES))\nI just want to make this clear as I know most of your other relations you have on this server tend to be mostly OOC I'm not looking for an OOC relation this is Silv'ar\nnot me. Just want to make that clear so I don't mislead you\n\nat all. Not that I'm saying we can't plan things OOCly but I'd like to keep the relation mostly IC.\n((OOC NOTE END))", ""),
        StaticBook("Bloodied Note", "§bHearth Underson", "Love is a beautiful lie\n\nLove... Love is a lie,\nSuch lie that makes us feel alive, that makes us feel jealous even though the love we feel might not find a way to connect to the loved one...\nAnd so love is... something hard to explain.\n\nThe feeling that we don't want and want to feel at the same time... Why does it sadden us when we lose the person that we love? We know what we did wrong, or perhaps we don't, perhaps the loved one traded us for another that he or her loved more...\n\nAlthough there are those that even having a loved one, love others at the same time, but they'd still not trade the loved one for another, some of them just want to give love to everyone, they don't want others to feel lonely,\n\nand sometimes loving more than one person makes us anxious when others are around, although, we know that we can't express what we feel, sometimes it hurts to keep the feel inside us because we're scared to not get love back...\n\nSometimes we are married but our wife or husband disappears... although... we know that they're returning soon... we don't want to feel lonely and so we seek more love, which can lead to bad results... although, we expected that.\n\n        A Poem\n\nI can't hold it back anymore,\nThis that I never felt before,\nMy great love for you,\nSomething that appeared out of the blue,\nMy heart hurts near you,\nand only you can fix it.\n\nWhy is love so cruel... My heart hurts when I see other men", ""),
        StaticBook("A found Journal", "§b:", "An Itharel's journal:\n\nIt's interesting really, even after ascending to a height of Demi-Godhood that many a Valah would dream of and many a Mali, Uruk or Bortu might envy...I feel little difference and yet I still fear it. The loss of my soul...not the literal soul I remind\n\nyou...you being me in the future. I fear it because...well look at my cousin...I hardly see a scrap of him left in that hollow golden shell...\n\nSo starting from this day I'll note the simple things...the taste of bread, the trees...\n\nthe coitus, the masonry, the books I read and poems that made me cry...that way I'll have memories to cling to...the pile of experiences that define us as people and thus will save me. \n\nI pray my mortality does not leave me too quickly...I must also\n\ntell Mia...and Skale...and those ignorant of this matter. It's a saddening truth and a cruel one for them and myself...but alas it is so...\n\nI am bound by the chains of service until I'm cast aside.\n\nYet another is lost. I can't blame him, the stress is damaging and the sights can drive any man past sanity...or good...\n\nIt would have been me had I not *several words have been erased as if the reader couldn't decide*\n\nwell...if I wasn't what I am...\n\nSeems as soon as we lose one, we recieve a new one. One of Katari's creatures...now one of Hesh's....I named him grandmaster.\n\nThe new Cleric is Luna. Impure but...pretty...\n\nalas the frailty of mortality. Like a small sculpture of glass and china. Fascinating yet...so delicate.\n\nSo this Rose tavern is clearly going to be nutcase central, perhaps I can fix that....maybe not.\n\nI see interesting folk here, the Gwyn individual appears again...she seems less...brute-ish.\n\nAll sorts in here actually. Old faces and new...one of Ivanus' past.\n\nSo for those interested, this is how you can be an Itharel:\n1. Man up- Ivanus.\n\nWell...I would note that usually sitting on a Shrine's altar would be...most...cruel.\n\nHowever...this particular one is in Lenia's name...so I doubt she'd mind.\n\nBesides I'm a walking steamboat of Tahariae's favour\n\n\n-------------------", ""),
        StaticBook("Tend'el'sJournal", "§bTristanm1", "The Travel Journal of: Tend'el\n\nFirst scribed on Kamees, 19th of Snows Maiden, 1312 \n\nI am visiting the Mage's Tower. I believe I can faintly sense Slayer now. I must be such a failure at magic; he and Bell instructed me so greatly and I have still awakened so little.\n\nThinking on Bell only reminds me that I have lost her. \n\nI...I...did not know how hard that line would be to write. I cared for you dearly Bell, loved you even. Moreso than the love men share so commonly with their partners. You became a friend, and I\n\nnever concerned myself for your aid, only you with mine. I would ask for forgiveness, butut that is pleading to the page, sulking in sorrow. \n\nYou taught me better than that. I must ask for forgiveness from God for my mistakes,\n\nand forgive myself, then press on. We have to accept the consequences of our actions and change for the better. You would have told me so, right Bell? Right? \n\nI am so confused, Bell. If only I had your buoyancy of spirit.\n\nSecond Entry: Ahad, 8th of The Deep Cold, 1314 \n\nVery tired, buteen walked to and from the guildhouse in Laurelin and my Inn, putting pieces of the guildhouse away for safe-keeping in my cellar.\n\nI'm also writing a few books of my own, but as of right now that's not really going anywhere.\n\nThird Entry: Kamees, 26th of Malins Welcome, 1314\n\nI have met for the second time with a man by the title Lord Lucius Murmillo. He showed me a small wooden church down the path from my inn. Upon meeting him for a second time, in a few\n\ndays he had built an entire wall for a city to help supplicate the Dwarven Kingdom. He says he studied architecture at a young age in Laurelin. I believe I'll be helping him with his town, so an old goal of mine and Lex of the Dwarves can be realized. I\n\njust met up with Bawapy, we've been reminiscing, butut he is sad about Ademas. I found out the Dwarves' city of Outer Kal'Urguan is falling due to a craig...or quake. Lucius told me the Elf who live on the other side of the small forest is Godswood.\n\nHe goes there to pray.\n\nFourth Entry: Joma, 27th of Malins Welcome, 1314 \n\nHelped a Dwarf move out of his home with Lucius, went by the name of Rolden. Such a shame too, his home could have been fixed up to look like those Halfling Homes.\n\nFifth Entry: Sabet, 28th of Malins Welcome, 1314 \n\nI have spoken to Felune. It appears Ademas is gone to be with God now. His final rest is come. I regret not being a part of the last batte, butut my friend would have understood. I have\n\nnow just been told of a new complication in the Ragthieu story. The Fighter, The Archer, The Spellsword (Ademas), and The Blacksmith. These are the men that have significance in that family, I was told the story would end with Ademas' son.\n\nHe must be trained.\n\nSixth Entry: Sabet, 28th of The First Seed, 1315 \n\nWell, this is strange. I just woke up in the birthing place of the Cloud Temple. I must investigate. I am now more than miffed. Someone is claiming I attacked them, and I just found out my\n\nroad was repaved...in WOOD!\n\nSeventh Entry: Joma, 13th of The Second Seed, 1315 \n\nI just considered that I have never mentioned my birthday to anyone. I believe it's perfectly understandable, considering my less than understandable childhood, but being 121 I believe it's time\n\nto mention it. I was born on 7th of The Amber Cold, 1193. That is all I will speak of my childhood for now. I am not in the mood.\n\nEighth Entry: Irba, 25th of The Grand Harvest, 1315 \n\nWe made a miscalculation in building the wall of Lord Lucius' Estate. It's rather embarassing. We must move the whole wall down one.\n\nNinth Entry: Tolta, 3rd of The Amber Cold, 1315 \n\nIt is the third, and my birthday is fast approaching. I believe I should begin making preparations, perhaps a cake? Sadly, I wonder who will even show up. I feel so alone as of late, like\n\nno one is around. But I mustn't sink into depression. We choose to wallow, don't we? Then I choose to press forward, for the brighter days are nigh.\n\nTenth Entry: Irba, 4th of The Amber Cold, 1315 \n\nI went travelling today. I swam toward some great trees that were bare after leaving the mines under the Desert Star. As of now, I am spending the night in an inn owned by an Orc and his elven niece. I\n\ncouldn't sleep. My birthday is coming soon. Why is it unsettling me? I must spread the word of the Dragon's Breath Inn. I said I would try.\n\nEleventh Entry: Joma, 6th of The Amber Cold, 1315 \n\nI spoke to Alvaska, who has changed the name of the Grey Wardens to the White Ravens. He knows of Lucius Murmillo, and tells me it is a foolish idea to help him. He and the AFF, who are allied,\n\ndisagree with Murmillo's vision of Feudalism. They believe such a system will cause the weaker people to rise up and overthrow Murmillo. This is foolish, these three keeps could band together for unity among this great piece of land. I don't know who to\n\ntrust, and will keep myself far from seeking power, but I must unite thes e kingdoms. Even if Lucius does not know how to lead, I can help him. I fear I have ambitions of overthrowing Lucius...what right do I have? I must remember  my own teachings,\n\nand Bell's. Greed, and Lust for power is foolish. Even if the castle is in a forest I only HELPED create (I must remember that I didn't finish the forest and Leafwind helped greatly, even if I did start the movement) It is not mine, nor a creation from my\n\nmind. It would be like unto usurping a painter's masterpiece.\n\nTwelfth Entry: Sabet, 7 of The Amber Cold, 1315 \n\nMy birthday has come and gone, I spent the day working on another man's castle. I did not even make myself cake. It is oddly, warmly familiar of my first few birthdays, the elves who had took\n\nme in sweet words how precious my birth was. They all knew the secret that I had not. They allowed me to be that dirty, carefree boy. I can only imagine the kindness they shew me, shielding me from what had happened. No boy... nay, I even, a man... can\n\nhandle what happened to you. Mom. Dad. I am sorry I could not have healed you of the illness that took you. I swear I will not be consumed in searching for cures. I will live the life you allowed me. I am sorry I had to know, to know of you. They kept it\n\nfrom me and I pried. I know you would have had me ignorant, so I could live a life without knowing. I never knew either of you. I love you, I love you both. But I know that you would have me never love you, and thus never hurt. I now know that every piece\n\nof knowledge has its own price. God give me strength.\n\nThirteenth Entry: Ahad, 8th of The Amber Cold, 1315 \n\nI sense that evil has awoken. Was it like this for Bell? or Slayer? Did they awaken by sensing? As foolish as chasing this feeling is, I must go. I should know if it is an arbitrary thought or\n\nif anyone is in danger.\n\nFourteenth Entry: Sabet, 7th of The Deep Cold, 1320 \n\nFour long years have passed, like nothing. I have been working with Lord Murmillo, whom I know on a first name basis so really Lucius. We have, in this amount of time, created a village worth standing,\n\na short walk from my inn. Aeriel's Crown. We are planning on starting an academy. I hope this would please Bell. I trust Slayer knows I do not mean to shirk my responsibilities as a Guildmaster in Laurelin. But what am I to do? I have been hard at work\n\nhere, and the magic he eagerly promised has not yet found its fruition in me. I hold fast that he was right though, and in this line of thought, help edify a place of scholasticism.\n\nBut I long for adventure, as my boyish youth once\n\nlonged for it.\n\nFifteenth Entry: Joma, 20th of Malins Welcome, 1322 \n\nI have awoken. I hardly know where I am, and feel as if I have been shaken from a deep dream. I spoke to one of Murmillo's Bannerman, Ser Twi Osit. I have lost 2 years, since my last\n\nentry...in the journal! What happened? Last I remember I was holding the book. Now I awake in a refurbished part of the castle in Aeriel's Crown. A new town has sprung up for Aegis' Sake! I need to see Slayer. I need to heed the words of Bell, and see the\n\nDruids. Perhaps I misunderstood Eindry'el's Curse. Will I forget everything? As much as I hate the druids, they might know something. Ser Twi also tells me that the Undead are massing under a man named Wrath.\n\nThe world is so cruel and confused now. I am befuddled by my own village. Even the open world on the King's Road brings me unknown sights.\n\nSixteenth Entry: Kamees, 5th of The Amber Cold, 1325 \n\nJust 2 days from my birthday I have finished the construction of my establishment - The Blue Print! I should have a sale in celebration, up until my birthday!\n\nI was blessed enough to enjoy a birthday dinner with Lucius, as well as three members of the Whispering Order, the militia of Whispering Isles. The members were the General, Alethion, and the two Commanders, Anora and Akorta. It appears I slipped up and\n\nforgot how old I was when I was speaking to my guests. How foolish of me to forget my own age! I told them it was my 131st birthday, when in actuality I turned 132. Oh well, it is a small trifle.\n\nSeventeenth Entry: Itnan, 16th of The First Seed, 1328\n\nIt has been two years. The time has passed amicably enough. I long for adventure, once again. It also deeply wounds me, that I have not seen my closest friends, the men of Wilder Farms for as\n\nlong as it has been. Is it I who has grown apart? Or can blame be placed in such things?", ""),
        StaticBook("Stoutchasms, V1", "§bMiscellus", "11th OF SUN'S SMILE, 1521\n\nA man came up to Dimlin Hammerfish, asking him if he knew of a (previously murdered) Dza the Old. After notifying the stranger that Dza was, in fact, dead, the man did not believe him: he repeated many times\n\nthat he had been 'out' for so long, then refused any evidence about Dza's murder. Dimlin told him that the murder took place a full 15 years ago before, annoyed, this man seemed to float out of the tavern he met the dwarf within. \n\nThis stranger was\n\nof a deep gray skin, a Cave dwarf not Doomforged but almost ethereal. His habit of... floating and coloration would suggest that he would be a ghost, but the only cases that I've heard of such were when a Dwarf met a Paragon himself! \n\nAfter a while, the\n\n'ghost,' as I will call him, entered the establishment once more. Dimlin asked him to leave and, when he went to put a hand on him to shove him out, his skin did not connect; the limb went straight through the translucent figure as it would with any kind\n\nof revenant. \nDimlin was confused. He asked the \"man\" to, if he was truly there, act upon a nearby torch; the torch proceeded to fall down, extinguished, almost at his command. \n\nThe ghost's name was Dunham Stoutchasm, which is a name that\n\nreminds me of.. something. The Stoutchasms are referenced at the statue of Hogarth, but I know not why. Something is in their midst, but I do not know what! I have heard that they are a clan of mystics and magicians, but not much more.\n\nThe spirit soon disappeared as Dimlin went to find me. As we have talked, many strange events have occurred: wind has blown in from all directions, even in the protected caverns of Kal'Akash, and a feeling of someone watching permeates my skull. It seems\n\nlike--\n\nIt just happened again.\n\nThe doors flew open! We now follow the events we see..\n\nAn arm protrudes around the corner.\n\nDear Dungrimm, it's a ghost.\n\nDunham has asked to find a Dzralen. Dimlin told him that Dzralen was dead, and so was he, but the ghost refused the answers, just asking if he could see the King. I awkwardly stumbled my words as he asked more and more confusing questions, talking to in-\n\nvisible beings outside of our sight... He asked for paper, said he could go for a drink, all out of nowhere... The torches in the alley go out. It becomes hard to write. The ghost disappears. \n\nDimlin managed to see the shadow of the ghost return to\n\nhis pub, and we have been following him. It's too fast to write much about. \n\nI have found out about the Stoutchasms from Hogarth Irongut himself. They were a clan of dwarves that lived here in Vailor before we came here-- they were\n\nan incredibly advanced race, with towering golems and amazing cities. They were quick to attack us Aegisian Dwedmar with what they thought was superior tech, but our numbers and strength held true: we fended them off for a long time before the Stoutchasms\n\nsimply faded away. They were not exterminated, but they did.. disappear. Dzralen was a higher-up in the clan, possible even the Clan Father. It is imperative that we find this ghost again and find out what happened to the rest of the Stoutchasms.", ""),
        StaticBook("Ancient Elves", "§bArchrim Elmoran", "Achient elves\n\nA long time ago, before written history, the world was inhabited by a single race known now as the achient elves and were the first ofthe Aegis, the build marvels in what is now niben bay\n\nThe achient elves built cities that are now considerd marvels and large statues of birds, lions, and also dragons, and it should be noted the elves learned how to befriend dragons aswell.\n\nthey knew the friendship between them was strong and so the dragons tought them the basics of what is know nowdays as magic, they also taught them on how to store energy within crystals and use them to power cities and give them light\n\nEventually a dragon by the name of Akron took power of the empire that had previously been formed by the elves and dragons. Akron hated the other newly formed races including the elves and so he started creating large crystals and using them for war\n\nbut there were dragons who did not agree with him and stood in the way of his plans, and so Akron called upon the forces of Iblees\nHe then used this power to slowly drain the life of the other dragons. and then the dragons seeing the inevitable end, used\n\ntheir remaining strength to close the gate to the nether that supplied Akrons Evil power. They died in the progress of closing the portal. The few dragons remaining turned them selves to stone waiting to one day be awoken\n\nWith the dragons out of the way Akron started the inslavement of the other races and with that came the great war witch lasted decades.\nFinnaly Akron was one day defeated and with that the humans took control of the crystals of power the dragon once owned\n\nThe human eventually became mad with power and started the genocide of the Anchient elves and burnt their cities to the ground, few managed to escape, and those few are now the ancestors of the current elven peoples\n\nAnd thus ended the Anchient elves", ""),
        StaticBook("Ceru VII", "§bMarch Ash", "Taken by the hunt, everything else fades away. We fail to listen. Not to other people, but to the World. Here, in the black, damp, heat -- nature's voice comes in its purest form. Nothing is hidden. It is naked. It is as easy as fucking.\n\nIt whispers to me so quietly: kill them all.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dragons", "§bArchrim Elmoran", "Dragons\n\nDragons are now days know by most everyone, much like our less dangerous chicken, the dragon egg goes into a one month incubation period in which the mother warms the eggs under her belly\n\nThe mother dragon increases her body temperature to that of a large and very hot fire for more than hours at a time, for about a month, then the eggs hatches and the dragon progresses to the stage of a hatchling\n\nThe young dragon is not yet able to fly but it does have wings none the less and they wont be able to fly untill much later,\nDragon hatchlings are normaly the size of a male wolf but are usually pretty tame and are much like a big puppy\n\nonly within its second week of life the young hatchling is left on its own and goes to hunt and live for itself, not long after this time the dragon reaches its ability to summon fire, not in the ammount to be deadly by it is noted that smoke can be seen\n\nrising from the nostrills and mouth about this time. After about a year the hatchling is no longer a baby but is to be considerd a drake\n\nAt this age the dragon cannot yet summon the full power of fire but are actually quite deadly hunters and\n\nare known to be quite grumpy. they are also seen wondering farther from their nest at this age to help satisfy their curiosity, for this reason they are the most commonly seen dragon since they tend to wonder close to cities and towns\n\nbut out in the wild they are know to attack and kill any who come near them\n\nYears later the dragon now becomes a full adult and is now able to do 3 things\n1- summon fire\n2- fly\n3- mate\n\nAdult dragons are mainly unaggresive since they do not care much about what the other races do but still it is not recommended to approch or sneak up on a dragon for it could mean the end for you, But there are time in which a dragon tends to be aggresive\n\none of which is during their mating season, if a town is within a certian distance of a chosen nesting spot they will destroy it\nIt should also be noted that the well known myth of dragons having a affinity for gold and or gems has never been proven or\n\ndisproven and should be kept in mind while exploring caves, also it is known that dragons enjoy riddles I have no idea if its true but this should be remembered if you come face to face with a dragon within its nest, it might just save your life.\n\nEventually if the dragon survives adulthood it becomes a wyrm, which is a very old dragon and very few of them have ever been said to exist\nThey should be feared and never sought out but I would say judging by how dragons attitudes are they are mostly\n\nnonagressive and would see us as if we were no bigger than a fly, and could care less about what we do, and I would imagin that they are extreamly wise at the same time, but none the less do not try to find a wyrm because death is still possible", ""),
        StaticBook("Dwarven Civil Wa", "§bHamlin Frostbeard", "War Of The Beards\n\nThe War of the Beards known as the Dwarven Civil War was fought by Kaz'ulrah and Urguan\nAfter losing the Throne war, the Frostbeards of New Jornheim the other clans which lived within the walls of New Jornheim decided to establish the\n\nKingdom of kaz'Ulrah which became a rival of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan. Over the course of five years the tension between the two Kingdoms soon became overwhelming which lead to a declared war.\n\nMany years go on with the two dwarven Kingdoms fighting until the Grand Kingdom of Urguan was conquered and dissolved for the first time ever in dwarven history which lead to the Kingdom of Kaz'Ulrah becoming the capital of the dwarfs.\n\nNew Jornheim\n\nWithin the small settlement of New Jornheim lived a number of clans most known was the Frostbeards which created the town to begin with when there mountain keep was taken by spiders and other unknown creatues.\n\nAnother clan within the wars of New Jorneim was the Blackaxes a clan which split off from the Grandaxes known for there warriors and military might and a Elder Clan known as the Goldhands master merchants and highly respected clan.\n\nIn the year 1626 the clans got together to create the colours of there new Kingdom which represented all of them so it was decided Blue for Frostbeards Yellow for the Goldhands and Black for the Blackaxes which lead to the Kingdom of Kaz'Ulrah being born.\n\nThe Dwarven Civil war was fought not only by the dwarfs both sides obtained as many allies as they could High King Verthaik II made many friends in his years which aloud him to obtain many allies which formed the Coalition which contained the War Nation\n\nof Krugmar, Kingdom of Norland, Kingdom of Santegia and the Warhawke Chiefdom.\n\nThe allies which the Grand Kingdom of Urguan obtained was on the Holy Orenian Empire rumor was that King of Urguan wanted to ensure victory by buying sellswords into his ranks\n\nIn the year 1634 the Urguan and Oren forces advance on New Jornheim which lead to the dwarfs of Kaz'Ulrah fighting upon their fields the battle was later known as the Battle of Jornheim Fields the victory of this battle was Kaz'Ulrah to celebrate.\n\nThe following year the Kaz'Ulrah armies advance upon the fores of Urguan and began there siege on Fort Kovakirr Kaz'Ulrah once again won this battle and had the glory and honor to show for it.\n\nIn 1636 Urguan surrendered to Kaz'Ulrah with terms that the High King agreed upon leaving some of Urguans land to become inderpendent and the main city would become part of the Kingdom of Kaz'Ulrah this lead to the end of the war and the fall of Urguan\n\nit also lead to the fall of the Orenian Empire as well.", ""),
        StaticBook("Minotaur Report", "§bCultist Scout", "We have watched them for many days.\n\nThey seem different than the others. They are not beasts like the others.\n\nPerhaps they are the more advanced? Maybe they strive for a purpose.\n\nTheir ancestors live nearby, perhaps the mark of Vilketa drives them on to free their kin.\n\nPerhaps", ""),
        StaticBook("Kal'Bogrin Vol I", "§bBorin Grandaxe", "After the reign of Fimlin Grandaxe the Grandaxe Clan had faced prejudice from the government, starting with a conflict with Grand King Vorstag Ireheart about the joint Grandaxe-Irongrinder naval hold Ote'Kathaz. Vorstags reign did not last long\n\nand Zahrer Irongrinder was elected after, and gave the Grandaxes the newly conquered land from the Undead known as Ash Castle, once known as Hanseti. In its place the Grandaxes built a hold named Kal'Bogrin after their founder, constructing a\n\nsmall village along a keep built into the mountain. North of Kal'Bogrin a fort was constructed and named Kaz'ad RumThe initial conflict between the Grandaxes and the council was started when Grand King Zahrer tried to re-institute the Lord's\n\nCouncil he was once part of, the amendment was blocked by the Grandaxes and the Frostbeards but the other three thanes, Uldar Irongut, Lori Ireheart, and Lathros Irongrinder removed the Frostbeards from Thaneship and replaced them with the\n\nDoomforged who passed the amendment.This sparked outrage amongst the Grandaxes, and thus the Lords were appointed from those that approved the passing and none to the Grandaxes or others.The situation only worsened from there, the tension rose\n\nuntil Jörik Grandaxe was accused of slaying an elf. Grand King Zahrer and the new Lords Council met to determine his banishment, but the Lords Council wanted to banish the entire Grandaxe clan because of their opposition. Grand King Zahrer\n\nvetoed the decision but was removed from King and the Grandaxes left for the safety of Kal'Bogrin with all their belongings. The Grandaxes thus seceded from The Grand Kingdom of Urguan and became indeed entry lead by the Grandaxe leaders Fili\n\nGrandaxe, Fimlin Grandaxe, and Jörik Grandaxe.Seeing the opportune moment to attack the dwarves the newly reformed Kingdom of Oren marched for the Irongut hold of Hiebenhall. Knowing the importance of maintaining the Grand Kingdom the Grandaxes\n\nprepared for war to protect it despite not receiving the same from the Lords Council.However it came to be that all the dwarves who were against the Lords Council moved in with the Grandaxes and eventually collapsed the Grand Kingdom and allowed\n\nfor the Grandaxes to liberate it. As a result the only candidate for Grand King left was Hodir Doomforged and he was elected Grand King and made a new government where a loose senate was the only opposition to the King and thus removing the\n\ncorruption of the Lords and Thanes Council once and for all.", ""),
        StaticBook("Journal Notes", "§bCultist", "She comes soon...\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWe must....\nPrepare\n\nPassion courses through\n\n\n\n\nthe\n\n\nlands\n\nThe Old....\n\n\nis the new\n\nwe have\n\n\n\nbeen found\n\nv\ni\nl\nk\ne\nt\na", ""),
        StaticBook("Lily's Tale [2]", "§bLuxeanna Du Couteau", "The gazelle nuzzled against the wolf, “Of course, Of course I came back.” She could feel the wolf’s bones through its thin and sickly skin. “Oh if only I had gotten here sooner….”\n\nThe wolf closed his eyes, “Maybe it’s better-it’s better this way.”\n\n“Don’t talk like that. You’ll be alright,” the gazelle lied, trying to hold back her tears, “We’re together now, everything will be fine, you’ll see.\"\n\nThe wolf opened his eyes slowly and smiled, nuzzling the gazelle. “At-At least I got to see you….one last time.”\n\nWith this the last breath of the wolf escaped its mouth and his eyes closed.\n\nThe gazelle nudged the wolf as her tears flowed, “N-no….No...Please, you can’t…..please don’t leave me….”\n\nThe animals of the forest looked on in sadness, their hearts sunken low. It felt as if the wolf’s death, a part of the forest had died as well, and all of the animals could feel the loss the gazelle was feeling.\n\n\nThe gazelle nuzzled against the wolf as her tears fell on him, muttering softly, “I love you.”\n\nWith these words, her tears glistened brightly and touched the wolf’s body. Behind the forest animals, a green light shined so bright that it at first blinded them as they turned around. As their eyes adjusted, they gasped in amazement.\n\nThe old turtle that sat on the stone was the source of the light, and as they looked on, they watched the turtle transform. Soon, where the turtle once sat a shimmering Wood Elf sat.\n\nThe animals looked on in both fear and amazement, but the Elf spoke to them.\n\n“Fear not my friends. I am not here to harm you,” the elf announced, “For all eternity I have been assigned to ensure that the veil that protects this forest remained intact, protecting the life within, and its meaning.\"\n\nThe druid stood and walked over to the animals slowly, “The family you created here amongst each other, this is what our creators tried to have throughout the world, but it has failed in many, many places.\n\nBut you succeeded. Your love for one another, it stands the test of time, it stands against the evils of this world, and it will keep all of you together.”\n\nThe druid would make its way over to the gazelle, who had been staring at the wolf this entire time, and carefully lifted her face.\n\n “And you, one who knows loss more than anyone here, you were able to find companionship…..you were able to find love, where others saw fear.”\n\nThe druid would smile and caress the gazelle’s face, “And your love will stand the test of time, young one.”\n\nWith this the forest glowed brightly, the trees swayed, and the grass blew swiftly. The wolf’s body was lifted with the wind and spun as the light entered its body. With a blinding light, the wolf was set down, not on its side, but on its paws.\n\nThe wolf stood on its own, opening its eyes, and looking amazed. The gazelle rushed to the wolf, nuzzling him and he her.\n\n“You two, your love will defend not just each other, but all of those you love,” the druid said as it slowly began to fade from view, its being disappearing into the wind.\n\nWith the druid’s disappearance, the animals and the forest remained hidden in peace,  guarded against the evils of the world by the wolf and gazelle for the rest of time.", ""),
        StaticBook("Winter Presence", "§bJaskier of Krinfrid", "Winter's Presence\n   ---------------\n\nThe frosted fangs of winter try to bite,\n\nHand of white frost reaching out at night.\n\nWhat made him so cold and bitter?\n\nFrozen lips making bones jitter.\n\nChilling presence, frozen breath,\n\nIt carried the stench of death,\n\nBlades of wind to cut through men,\n\nThey will rise and fall again.\n\nWhite armour torn apart,\n\nTo reveal his icy heart.\n\nMen marching upon the storm,\n\nHis army they shall form.\n\nSwift steeds of ice painted red,\n\nRiding until all that lives, is dead.\n\nSome day winter shall come,\n\nIt is then our time is done.\n\nWhere nothing was, is he.\n\nShall nothing will there be.\n\n- Jaskier", ""),
        StaticBook("Wolf Watches", "§bQuinn", "[!]\nThe first page of the journal is covered in spots of blood and blotches of ink. The ink blotches have seemed to have bled over certain sketches around the page. In the center, a string of words is underlined and hastily scribed.\n\"The Wolf Watches\"\n[!]\n\n===================The lone wolf stalks, away from his pack, away from those whom abandoned him, and those whom gawked.\n\nThis lone wolf seems to lie upon the minds of sheep, what does he do here, what does he wait for while his pack members weep?\n\n===================O' one of the Wolf, O' one whom hunts. Who will claim your ancient pelt, which is sought by those whom wish to cut.\n\nThe hunt, the boon of the hunter, the hunted get no forgiveness, nature's cruel intent striking those whom fall behind.\n\n===================Though the lone wolf now hunts, as he hears the members of his pack stray away, breaking off from those who lead from the front.\n\nBlood stains the rivers, the grounds and the hunters. Blood paints in this world as a misfortuned-\n\n===================saunter.\n\n[!] Sketches litter this page, shapes of blades and of a branch. Somehow having diagrams of merging the two, or shaping the said staff with a blade? It is the only two things which can be assumed [!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Homunculi V.I", "§bHamlin Frostbeard", "Homunculus a creature of Alchemy made from descendent with strong alchemic ingredients.\n\nThe new creature reborn from alchemy takes the shape resembling what was used but never the same. If a body was not used to create the creature it will become chaotic\n\nThere are four types of creatures which are called Homunclus.\n\nA Fiend is one which is a failed creation with a disfigured apperance with little to no hair with the shortest life span of the four however a Fiend takes on a animalistic lifestyle going of\n\nbasic needs.\n\nThere weakness like most unholy creatures are holy magic and gold there is said to be a final weakness which isnt known to most.\nThe weapon which these creatures use are only primitive weapons such as swords, axes or mace\n\nOnce killed a Fiend cannot be brought back to life.", ""),
        StaticBook("Love's Ending", "§bFranswaar Kellian", "The day was starting to fade as the sun slowly crept across the sky towards the ever nearing horizon.  I left my home in a hurry wearing the most formal clothes I could manage to find laying around in my home. Nervous and slightly, I finally arrived at my\n\ndestination. She was more beautiful then ever. Her long, flowing auburn hair, striking hazel eyes, and smile were enough to make a man collaspe. The indigo dress swayed in the wind as we walked towards the ballroom.\nOur hands intertwined, I, walking a\n\nslightly faster pace. \nInside was full of elegant music and exquisite decor. The chandelier lit up room from above. As we began to dance together, our eyes were inseperable. Though the ballroom was filled to the point where moving was nearly impossible,\n\nI could only see her. Every second see smiled my stomach fluttered with astounding joy. As the night came to a close, I strolled with her until we could see the sun begin to tower over the mountains. We sat in the meadow watching the sun rise, her head on\n\nmy shoulder. At that moment, I knew I was in love. Months passed and seasons changed. Every spare second I had I spent it with her. She was the only I seemed to care about. Time spent apart seemed as if it were a life time. Though the day came where I was\n\nneeded on a cargo ship to sail across the oceans to sell goods. \n3 years were spent on the water exporting, though it felt more like 30 years. When I arrived home, all I wanted to do was see her. When I exited the boat I ran to her home. Excitement\n\ncoursing through, and adrenaline pumping. I arrived to be greated by a baby crawling on the lawn. Tears began to rush down my face as I learned I became a father. I knelt down to the baby, only to be screamed at by the mother, not realizing who I was.\n\nI stood up a looked her in the eyes, only to she her change from angry to shock. Together we began to sob as we ran into eachother's arms. We spent the rest of the day conversing about my travels and where I've been. I then asked why she didn't tell me\n\nshe was pregant when I left. Her reply was as if a dagger was stabbed into my heart, then was proceeded to be ripped and forced into it again. The baby was not mine. I learned that in my absence the woman I spent every moment with, the woman that I\n\ndevoted my life for, married another man and bore him a child. I lied as best I could fighting the tears congulating her on the new born. She began to explain that I was gone for 3 years and that she began to fall in love with another man.\n\nI left her home with full intent of drowning myself in the harbor. I stood on the edge of the pier, looking out into the now black water, for night has fallen, and prayed that my soul be given mercy. I shut my eyes and began to lean forward.\n\nHalf way into my fall or the pier, a hand ripped me away. I struggled to free myself, but I was restrained against the cold, damp floor. My 'Savior' began to scream at me, though he was tuned out as I began to rethink what I should do.", ""),
        StaticBook("Pembroke Treaty", "§bVirkian Agnew", "Pembroke-Kaz'Ulrah§0\n§0\n§0The council of pembroke would like to sign a non aggresion pact with the leaders of Kaz'ulrah. As we are rarely affected by the politics of Atlas, we seek friends and allies among our neighbors. Assisting each other has become key\n\nI, the High Treasurer Virkian Agnew. Have come bearing Golden Axe on the shield of Pembroke-shire. In hopes to harbor and retain relations between our two cities. The parameters of the treaty are negotiable, But we wish it to only entail the following.\n\nBoth cities will help each other in conflicts unrelated to specific nations. The undead, Bandits, Things of the like.§0\n§0\n§0Both cities will keep in touch with local politics. Sharing our knowledge of Atlas with eachother\n\nBoth cities will be open to supporting each other in times of crisis. Whether it be Famine, Disease, or Rebuilding after a§0\n§0War Effort.§0\n§0\n§0That is the end of the desired terms from Pembroke\n\nSincerely, §0\n§0High Treasurer of Pembroke§0\n§0\n§0Virkian Agnew,", ""),
        StaticBook("Odo's Story", "§bOdo Komninus", "This is the story of a young boy named Odo. He is 12 years old and lives with his caretakers who are Helzya and Ioannis. He has lived a rough life his two parents put him in a orpanage before he could remember them. Odo and his sister Lilly were raised\n\nby human farmers. These farmers taught Odo how to farm which lead to his cooking intrest. The farmers sent him away at age 10 because of growing danger for him there. He dosent know why he was sent away but he was told it was for the best. Him and Lilly\n\nsoon found refuge in Kal'Karrad, Ironicly it was the mortal enemy of the Humans, but Helzya and Ioannis took him and Lilly in, they lived in a tarvern for a bit untill Ioannis let them move into his manor! What was really hard was Odo getting used to\n\naround people. Over the years he was taught to hate the dwarven race, not cherish them. Now he loves it and studys it. Odo wants to become a master Chef, but he is really good at fishing. \n\nWritin by Odo Komininus\nAge: 12", ""),
        StaticBook("Feudal Rights v2", "§bChristopher d'Ibelin", "A SUGGESTION OF A FEUDAL LAW\n_____________________________By Francois d'Ibelin. \n\nSecond Edition and transcription by Christopher d'Ibelin. \n\nA document wherein a suggestive replacement for the Feudal Law of Oren is contained.\n\nIntroduction\n-----------------------------Greetings, fair men of the new Empire. The Feudal Law was a document detailing clergymen, burgher, peasants, yeomen and nobles, and the roles thereof. This was accepted by the good King Olivier, yet it is doubted\n\nthat a similar document is required for the Holy Orenian Empire of his Imperial Majesty, John I. I find this most distressing. The Feudal Law was itself an expression of traditional privaleges.\n\n-Ser Francois d'Ibelin\n\nI.Definitions\n\nI.A feudal vassal (otherwise known as a secular vassal) is a secular nobleman who owns a landed title within the Empire, be they directly or indirectly loyal to the crown. With these category, there are two further subcategories:\n\nOne:Minor nobles are those nobles who are lower than the rank of count.\n\nTwo:Senior nobles are those who are counts or higher.\n\nII.A senior clergyman (otherwise known as a Canon vassal),\n\nis one who holds an ecclesiastical, or non-secular title, titular or otherwise, that is a bishopric or higher.\n\nIII.Those who are under this rank are categorised as lesser clergy.\n\nIV. Landed gentry are those who hold a knighthood and an estate but hold no other titles. For example, a duke who is also a knightly estate-owner is considered part of the senior noble class, not the landed gentry.\n\nV.Those commoners who are not bound to any land, own no property and lack any sort of allegiance are called free subjects, these being the majority of our empire. \n\nVI.Those skilled commoners who work in the arts and crafts\n\nor any trade for a liege are known as craftsmen. \n\nVII.Those commoners bound to the land of a secular or canon vassal in agricultural labour are called serfs or villens.\n\nVIII.Those who hold council titles in a county, ducal, princely\n\nor imperial council are known as unlanded nobles.\n\nIX.Those who hold such titles as “Lord Mayor” and are given governance of a city are known as burgher titles.\n\nII.Vassalage and Obligations.\n\nI.The vassals are obligated to support their liege during a war. If the Emperor calls the realm to war, then he may be sure that the vassals give their full military strength in support of his cause; if they do not,\n\nthe Emperor is at will to revoke their titles or imprison them.\n\nII.The Emperor is obligated to maintain the feudal privileges of the vassals; if he rules with tyranny, and attempts to revoke feudal laws such as this,\n\nvassals are under no obligation to follow him. \n\nIII.Each man of the landed gentry, unlanded nobles and secular vassals is required to keep a destrier or a courser, riding horses; his own arms and armour of the highest quality.\n\nIV.It is the feudal duty of the commoner to be armed with the most basic of weapons.\n\nV.Burgher vassals are free from the obligation to fight or provide levies, as they provide extra financial contributions to the realm.\n\nVI.The clergy likewise are under no such obligation.\n\nVII.It is thus requested burgher taxes can be up to double those of the feudal vassals, however, they are under no obligation to go to war with their liege.\n\nVIII.The Emperor is obligated to defend his vassals and come to their aid when they are attacked. \n\nIII.In Respect of the Lexicon of Ashford and the Ducal Law.\n\n[note-henceforth the Lexicon of Ashford has been superseded\n\nwith a new law, yet the principle remains the same - Christopher.]\n\nI.It is said no Emperor will revoke the privalege of the dukes to create their own ducal laws, no Emperor shall ever revoke this privalege, this privalege will not be revoked!\n\nII.The Lexicon of Ashford takes place only in those duchies without a Ducal Law, or that are in possession of the Emperor.\n\nIII.Counties, baronies and so forth may not make their own laws.\n\nIV.In Respect of the Rights and Responsabilites of the Commoners.\n\nI.It is said that the commoners of any rank are only to be judged by either the Law of Ashford or their respective Ducal Law, by no other law they may be tried, and\n\nonly when proven guilty may they be persecuted. \n\nII.Further, the serfs can be expected to marry at the behest of their liege. This is because their children will be serfs as well.\n\nIII.No noble may displace a law-abiding citizen unless he has been inactive for one Saint’s week.\n\nIV.He shall not be permitted to visit a man’s court without the approval of his liege.\n\nV.Any man born of a free family shall not be taken as property of any foreign or local power.\n\nVI.Each peasant, whether serf, yeoman, or otherwise, has the right to own weaponry. [and, furthermore - a responsability if an adult male]\n\nV.In Respect of the Incarceration of the Nobles and Clergy.\n\nI.The clergy are only to be imprisoned by their liege only with the approval of the High Pontiff.\n\nII.The Emperor may only\n\nrevoke a man’s titles or imprison him on one or more of the following conditions: He has a legitimate claim on one of their titles, he has committed treasonous acts with ample evidence to support such a case, he has committed a crime\n\nof the first or second degree.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tale of a Hunt", "§bTever Softfoot", "The moon was high as I stalked my prey. I came across signs of a small herd of deer early this morning. I had lost the trail about mid afternoon after they crossed through  several creeks, but I picked it up again a little later. They were moving fast.\n\nThe moonlight lit the trail quite well. Being small and light on my feet let me move fast and quietly, I made good ground. \nIt took most of the next day to catch up to the deer.\nThe night was nearly upon me. Hunting under the light of the moon\n\ngives me a feral feeling. Like the moon approves of my actions. The air is calm and cool, the insects singing, a low mist on the ground. It is magical, the feeling I get, when the sun sets. I could hear a slight rustling of grass in a small copse of trees\n\nahead. I knocked an arrow, my muscles becoming tense, the thrill of the hunt coming upon me. I crept foward slowly without a sound, coming to a small clearing where the deer were preparing to bed down for the night.\n\nHiding behind a tree I drew my bow and pulled the arrow back, ready to loose the moment I got a clean shot. All sounds drowned out by the beating of my heart. One of the deer moved away from the herd to chew some grass that hadn't been trampled.\n\nNow was my chance, I let loose my arrow piercing the deers heart, dropping it to the ground without a chase. The other deer snorted and bounded away white tails raised in alarm, I had my prey however.  \nI kneeled over the still warm body of the deer\n\nand thrust my dagger into it's heart once more to ensure it was not suffering still. I then began the arduous task of cleaning the animal. I skinned and gutted it, saving the edible parts. I scraped the hide clean of fat and muscle and layed it aside.\n\nI quarterd the meat, leaving the bones in for now. I took the skull and split it open, taking the brain out. I mixed it with water in a bowl and used the mixture to begin tanning the hide so it would not dry out. The brain has high levels of tannin which\n\nis used by leatherworkers to tan leather. I then rolled it up and tied it with twine. I then deboned the qaurters and wrapped the meat in parchment paper to keep the bugs out. I packed it all in my leather bag.\n\nI cleaned the bones by rubbing them with sand to remove any muscle left over. The tendons I wrapped around a wooden dowel for later use as bowstrings. I added the bones to the pack and made my way home. The return trip took quite a while longer due to the\n\nheavy burden.\n\nAfter I returned home I packed the meat in the cold cellar. I took the hide and stretched it on the tanning rack. I positioned my rack next to my kiln so the heat will dry the skin faster. I took the tendons and chewed them until\n\nthey were malleable. I then stretched them into sinew for a bow string. \nAfter about a week or so the hide has been tanned. It needs to be softened so it can be shaped into armor. \nI out it into a pot of boiling water until it was soft.\n\nI then melted a few pounds of bees wax and put the leather into it. The hot leather soaks up the wax making it flexible and soft. After it cools I scraped the excess wax from the leather and becan tracing the shapes of the armor sections onto it.\n\nI took some shears and cut out the marked segments and began sewing them together with some sinew from a previous kill. \nI ordered some ferrum studs from the smithy and attached them for a little extra protection.\n\nThe studded leather armor is soft and very flexible. It allows the hunter to handle a bow unrestricted by the armor. I sat the armor on my armor stand and grabbed the new roll of sinew and headed to the workshop to begin the process of making a new bow.\n\nI grew a few dark oak salpings specifically for the purpose of making bows. As they grew I trained them into a curve. It makes the bows stonger when the wood is naturally curved like that. I had cut them about a year or so ago so that they would be dry by\n\nthe time I needed to use them. I then soaked them in a salt brine to make the wood malleable without messing up the natural grain. I then took a stave from the brine and set it onto a mold to set the shape. I took a plank and drilled holes into it\n\nin order to insert pegs to wrap the soft stave around. i then take the mold and put it into the kiln for a few hours. While that is drying I took the new sinew and boild it for a few minutes and covered it in wax. This will keep it protected from the\n\nelements and wear. I make loops in each end using a special braid. After the stave has dried it is taken off of the mold and flexed to break up the salt in the wood. it is then put into vat of linseed oil and soaked for a week. It becomes impregnated with\n\noil sealing the grain. It is then put into the kiln a second time. As it dries the oil cooks and hardens the bow making it very durable but still flexible. After about an hour it is removed and layed flat to air cool to room temperature.\n\nI then test the flex, if all is well I then test fire it. \n\nI have hunted an animal and used all parts of it.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Journal", "§bHearth Underson", "-={=}=-\n\n         Eradan`s\n           Diary,\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nStarted 7th of the Deep Cold  1599 ;\nSutica.\n\nEntry 1 7th Deep Cold\n\nI Have Decided to begin a Journal,\nThis book will be used to write down my many\ndifferent storys, notes, and Sketches,\nI look forward to my nexy Entry,\n\n-Eradan Dune`Dien\n\nEntry 2, 8th Deep Cold\n\nI`ve taken an overnight trip to courland to get supplies for my next journey to the enchantry, what a nice town they have here...\n\n\n\n-Eradan Dune`Dien\n\nEntry 3,  1st of the\nSnow`s Maiden\n\nToday i encountered a Druid, Nice guy...\nI once tried to become one of them, the grove is just so beautiful...\n\n\n\n\n-Eradan Dune`Dien\n\nEntry 4 8th of the\nSnow`s Maiden,\n\nToday I think I just met  the most attractive Woman in Axios, the moment I spotted her i fell deeply in love, I cant stop thinking about her... \n-Eradan Dune`Dien\n\nEntry 5 22nd of the\nGrand Harvest,\n\nDruids, kind folk,\nI may become one soon...\n\n\n[!] A sketch of a cat\nis drawn neatly at\nthe bottom of this page,\n\nEntry 6 9th of\nMalin`s Welcome 1607\n\nGhouls, Undead Everywhere,\n\nTime to do my job,\n\n-E.D\n\n6th of Sun`s Smile,\n1624...\n\nIts been a while, But\nI`ve managed to find\nthis old thing again,\n\nAlot has happened,\nSo I cant note it all,\n\nBut all needed to be\nsaid, is that, I don`t\nthink this realm will\nstand much longer...\n\n? ? ? ? 16XX\n\nThe void is consuming,\nDark, yet darker,\nthe darkness keeps growing, shadows cutting deeper, This next task, will take so much... Power...\n\nE.D Rosevale", ""),
        StaticBook("The Goat Murder", "§bNicolas Bolivar", "A man called Jerry was born 1623 became the murderer we know today as \"The Goat Murderer\" He murdered peoples goats from 9 to 12, and later on he killed people and robbed people wearing a goat mask, and was imprisioned 1653 and on\n\nthe 16th of some month was executed by the family members of ones killed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Hmmm...", "§bEris Oranor", "Strange Book.\n\n\nWander what's it for.\n\n\n\nMaybe I should keep reading.\n\n\n\n\n\nEh, dosn't look like much.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nMaybe...\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nNa...\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nOkay, you're being messed with now.\n\nLove you Aerith.\n-Eris", ""),
        StaticBook("Enchanting Glyph", "§bLorien Vesitza", "[!]The book seems burnt badly, as if someone had tried to dispose of it in a fireplace, but then decided against it and pulled it out of the fire...too late, however, as half of it is burnt away[!]\n\nEnc__nt__ G-_ph\nF_r Unb__-k__-\n\n[]  []\n  []\n_--__---|__|]----___\n\n[!]The rest of the pages are burnt away[!]", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes III", "§bArchmage Crumena", "Eighth of the Sun's Smile, 1497\nCrumena Ilwindior \nI took the liberty today to carry out an experiment for I could not quell my curiosity. It was early in the morning as I did not want to disturb anyone nor do I want Lotheriel\n\n\ncoming across my studies. I traversed the halls of this tower with my Shade trailing behind. The damned mist expanded its reaches outward and clutched any it could. Finally at the garden between Ceruberr’s Arch-Mage quarters and the meeting\n\n\nhall I had discovered something. Something pulsated above. For one second I was certain it was just above the ceiling and then without worry it circling about. Like a roach skidding away for dear life. Quickly its height altered with every moment.\n\n\nHigher and higher and then it dropped. Right before my Shade lost its grasp of the anomaly it seemed like an ocean away. I truly wonder if we should further dwell in Rasmot’s domain.§§", ""),
        StaticBook("Stable Contract", "§bCyler Cottonwood", "Contract\n\nCyler Cottonwood is in need of a new stable and has asked Sordodan Cottonwood to build it\n\nReward\n???\n\nSigned\nCyler Cottonwood\nSordodan Cottonwood", "")
    )

    private fun _ATLAS_18(): List<StaticBook> = listOf(
        StaticBook("A Carrot Poem", "§bFranswaar Kellian", "A Carrot Poem\n       By:\n          Franswaar\n\n\n    Based on true \n         events\n\nRotten Carrots serve as no treat, The Knight is very displeased at this feat\nDeath is his sentence, what a poor man, The Knight must cleanse the rotten carrot land\nA twist in the story, what is this! An outsider now comes into action from the mist\n\nFighting in the streets, blood on the walls oh my! Does everyone have to die because of this rotten carrot guy?\nBlood covers the ground, screams are heard all around. Someone please help kill these hounds.\n\nHow could carrots ever escalate to this. Canon would be displeased, these men will be given no bliss", ""),
        StaticBook("Dream of Lilies", "Lithaeril", "May you dream the dreams of Lilies, where all your worries cease. Whilst you sleep the sleep of the oak tree full of love, contentment, and peace. Braids of vines tumble from the hair of the ancient walls. Flowers sprout in fertile places whilst the\n\nliving pnod look like friendly faces. The singing sound of the stream rolling over the stones. Beauty in the way the butterfly flutters. The soaring of the great eagle sailing on the great blue waves of the sky. Weaving through the white peaks and the\n\nhorse galloping through amber waves of grain. Natures music the whistle of the wind, the rustle of the branches, the hoot of the owl, the river rolling. May you dream the dreams of Lilies,\nwhere all your\nworries cease. Whilst you sleep the sleep\n\nthe oak tree, full of love, contentment and peace.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Dwed War, V1", "§bMiscellus", "MISCELLUS THE CLANLESS'S JOURNAL OF THE EVENTS OF THE DWARVEN ELECTION OF 1517, VOLUME ONE\n\nIt is a concerning matter, this election. There are calls of tyranny and corruption and vote-changing, and many are attacking the two major players of\n\nthe election. I am worried about our country, and am not sure if war is soon to break out. For all of our sakes, I truly hope not. \n\nThe election days themselves seemed peaceful. I first met Skippy Irongut, the King to be, when I first entered this g\n\ncity. He introduced me to the kingdom, gave me a home, job, place to be and belong to. I thank him for that. Clanfather Verthaik Frostbeard, on the other hand, introduced me to the tavern and to ale. He was a benevolent host who brought free ale to his\n\nfriends and accomplices, being about as friendly as possible. I came to know him quite well, I would think. Both parties, in the days of election, just seemed to try and bring dwarf after dwarf to their side. Normal politics, really; nothing shady as of\n\nyet.\n\nThe problems began on the day the election ended. Skippy was crowned High King, but it was not a simple process. Many called treason, of cheating; they claimed that the voting was rigged, and that Skippy was no rightful king. My question,\n\npersonally, was why.\n\nAnd, of course, I tried to learn more! I first found out that many people, though I do not know them by name, claimed their votes for Verthaik did not count in the ending count of 37 to 41 votes. I do not know how they know thei\n\nvotes did not count, seeing that it was privately tallied. That alone seemed suspicious to me.\n\nSoon after, I went to see Verthaik to question him about the election. He solidified the notion that he did not approve of Skippy as king\n\nand would not follow him as a leader. I asked if he believed the voting was rigged, and he said yes: he blamed it on one dwarf in particular, a Jovik Grandaxe. The Grandaxe, it seems, had a vendetta against Verthaik due to an old conflict where Verthaik\n\nrefused to aid him in his ascension to Grand Marshall, and in fact opposed his rise at all. By Verthaik's words, Jovik went against him and against honor, joining both Skippy's and corruption's side in re-tallying the votes. Even by Verthaik's story,\n\nSkippy might still be innocent.\n\nOf course, I cannot go by Verthaik's word alone. I went back to the kingdom of Urguan to find out more, and met a dwarf by the name of-- oh, what was it again-- Shogath, I believe. I asked him if he new a Jovik,\n\nhe confirmed that it was the Grandaxe, and then said that he had been /missing/. Missing! Captured by Orcs, but he also reassured me that he'd be back by the next day. Quite the strange attitude for someone with their friend kidnapped! \n\nJovik was no\n\nonly kidnapped, though, but also honored.. or threatened.. or part of a threat. I'm not quite sure, to be honest. A grand statue of a dwarf was recently erected, and upon its base is inscribed the following:\n\n\"Jorik is ours, Hogarth in your midst trusted the Stoutchasms.\"\n\nI have no idea what this means. This was erected just yesterday or today, the same day that the election ended or the last day of it. I do not know Jorik, Hogarth, or the Stoutchasms...\n\nI must find out more. This is all I have for now, but I must find Skippy, Jorik, or this Hogarth and interrogate them further...\n\nBefore I forget, I have heard one important message:\n\n\"Those deemed unworthy of being counted will have their votes dismissed.\" Who determines if a dwarf is worthy? Is this why many are claiming corruption? Who is behind this strange saying?\n\n16TH OF THE SNOW'S MADIEN, 1517\nIt seems I was wrong\n\non almost all accounts. Verthaik, from what I gather, is simply a liar. \nJovik Grandaxe is, apparently, an \"Oathbreaker\"-- what Urguan is now calling Verthaik and the Frostbeards, along with any who join their side. War has more or less been declared.\n\nJovik, also, was not behind vote counting at all, leading me to believe that Verthaik was either completely misinformed or lying. The statue with his name on it was a red herring from a time long gone, with details that remained due to workers not taking\n\nit down. Apparently, a Frostbeard himself counted the votes, but I do not know if this is true. I will have to find more sources.\n\nWhat I do know are the facts: a civil war is soon to begin. The Frostbeards claimed the mines, but Urguan claimed them\n\nand tensions are at a high. The Oathbreakers and the Kingsmen are quite the warriors, and I fear for our kingdom in the times to come...\n\nI have been attacked by Dark Elves. I do not know why as of yet.\n\nThe attack was a \"prank,\" as they put it\n\nHmph. Unimportant, and not an ambush by either side. Whatever.\n\nI asked Verthaik. There is most definitely a civil war, and I am speaking to him about it now.\n\nFrom what I understand, some are on Verthaik's side because they believe\n\nhe is not a fitting leader, whether or not the majority voted for him. Others are convinced that he is not the right king and is absolutely lying to his people. All I need to find out is whom is behind the election's main dispute, and how to dissolve this\n\nas peacefully as possible. Wish me luck, Yemekar!\n\nSkippy refuses to publicize the vote, though he does not know who tallied it himself. He says it is to protect the Dwarves that tallied the vote, and that the votes were recounted many times. I\n\nthink it odd that he does not even know the vote talliers themselves. I need to find them, but I so far do not know how.\n\nI am now worried that even with the correct votes being counted, the war will not end. Both sides seem very adamant in their\n\ndecisions, and it is truly hard to trust anyone. I worry for this kingdom.\n\nIt is to note that Skippy claimed that the council of voters was of both Verthaik and Skippy supporters. How can he claim this when he says that he does not know who they wer\n\n19TH OF MALIN'S WELCOME, 1518\n\nI am too late. War has started, and it is truly a sad one. Dwarf against dwarf, for... hell, I don't even know anymore. The mines are down, reclaimed and destroyed by both sides. The Dwedmar nation has fallen into some\n\nof gehenna hell, and I do not know what kind of divine manna could save us. \n\nThe halls seem emptier than before, though the same amount of people patrol. Everything just feels... worse.\n\nAnd I still don't know who's right.\n\n-Miscellus, still clanless", ""),
        StaticBook("Stormfists", "§bOya II Stormfist", "--------------------------------------\n\nStormfist Bloodline\n\n--------------------------------------\n\nStarting as a clan the Stormfist later became a bloodline once the \"Blue-Silver Concordat\". In article four of the Blue-Silver Concordat it states that all Stormfist are no longer there own clan but are hence forth none as Silvervein.\n\nBefore Boreas Stormfist second generation Clan Father sighned the Concordat the Clan were a vassal clan of the Frostbeard. The Stormfist were loyal to the Frostbeards and to there Clan Fathers however once the death of King Kerwyr Frostbeard happened\n\nthe Stormfist found out that they were unwanted by both Urguan and the Clan they once served forcing them into exile hidden away ontop of cold mountain tops trying to survive the bitter cold. During this time bith Clan Father Exnord and clan father Begrig\n\nwere lost upon that mountain which lead to the Stormfists having no one to lead the remaining Stormfist elected Exnord's twin sons Boreas Stormfist and Notos Stormfist to become the new Clan Father. The Dwarfs who remained in the Stormfist Clan held no\n\ngrudge for what there kin did to them, Stormfist see grudges as weakness that will hurt them in the furture. The Second Generation Clan Fathers Boreas and Notos lead the Stormfist back into Kaz'Ulrah where they expected new beginings for there\n\npeople but instead of serving the Frostbeards they served themselves and the unified nation of Kaz'Ulrah.\n\n--------------------------------------Stormfist in Kaz'Ulrah\n--------------------------------------Boreas Stormfist was granted a clan hall by the King of Kaz'Ulrah Verthai II Frostbeard which allowed the Stormfists to grow until the Silverveins came.\n\nIn time the Stormfistss had a large amount dwarfs with there clan name only but it wasnt big enough Edel Silvervein along side his Clan kin set a proposal upon the Stormfist Clan Fathers the Clan Hall or they will kin slay all Stormfists. Boreas\n\npresented a second deal of the Stormfists becoming Silverveins and having there culture taken then replaced by theres in the position Edel agreed to these terms in writing of the Blue-Silver Concordat in 1635.\n\nBeing part of the Silverveins now Boreas Stormfist became clan father of the clan but only was for a short amount of time for later his body was found next to the Clan Hall of the Frostbeards. The Death of Boreas lead to the Stormfists to be hunted\n\ndown and killed upon the spot if they remained within the Dwarven City of Kaz'Ulrah.\n\n--------------------------------------Stormfists Beliefs\n--------------------------------------Stormfists are worshippers of Wyrvun and are known as children of Wyrvun they will help nation and people who openly worship Wyrvun and gladly march in her\n\nname.\n\nDeceased members of the Stormfist are taken to mountaintops so they can make there travel to Wyrvun's embrace being granted a place amoung the stars and remains can be one with the mountain once more.\n\nSince the Blue-Silver Concordat the Stormfists worship the Brathmordakin instead of Wyrvun. Some worship both.\n\n--------------------------------------Immportant Stormfists\n--------------------------------------\n\nBaldin Frostbeard Grandaxe - The creator of the Stormfist bloodlind when he ...\n*the rest of the page has been scribbled out*\n\nExmord \"The Tall\" Stormfist - First Generation Clan Father\n\nBelig \"The Short\" Stormfist - First Generation Clan Father.\n\nBoreas Stormfist - Second Generation Clan Father\n\nNotos Stormfist - Second Generation Clan Father\n\nVestrig \"Mighty\" Stormfist - Third Generation Clan Father\n\nEgoi Stormfist - Third Generation Clan Father", ""),
        StaticBook("Bogrin Offensive", "§bKazrin Starbreaker", "The Battle of Boiling BloodThe Battle of Boiling Blood was fought on two fronts, the Dwarves on one front in their war camp and the Elves and Men in another, surrounding the dwarven war camp were trenches and archer posts. In the middle laya\n\ndwarven artillery comprised of trebuchets and Bolt Throwers which would become a key factor in the coming battle. The second front boasted a much larger force comprised of men of all nations and Elves of all nations, however unlike the dwarfs\n\nhad barely any defenses, instead trading defense for firepower. The elves constructed a magic cannon capable of blasting powerful magical balls of energy at the enemy and sported many numbers capable of handling larger forces some of which were\n\nadept in the arcane arts. The first wave of September Prince Cultists marched onto both war camps, the elves and men took the larger force however suffered losses. The dwarves took less numbers but still suffered a casualty here and there. As\n\nthe battle waged on, the elves and men managed to repel back the now much depleted forces of the september cultists. Knowing that there numbers would be the end of them the Cultists instead rallied and attacked the dwarven war camp, which would\n\nlater on prove to be a fatal blow as they were met with volleys of bolts and charging dwarfs heavily clad in armor. Proving to be ineffective the cultists retreated, as they did so the descendants had won the first wave of the battle. While\n\nwatchmen kept to the hour waiting for the next wave the descendants setted up defenses, healing the wounded and replenishing supplies and ammunition. But before they could get either, both war camps came under siege by a large force of undead\n\nand monsters. ”What i tell you now reader is the accounts of myself Kazrin Starbreaker, I do not know what befell the elven camp at this time but i do know that it was a hard battle. Our dwarven war camp had a stone platform built on top the\n\ngrass, on it were various artillery including dwarven trebuchets and Bolt Throwers. Many trenches were outlined around the war camp making the undead having to go through them, slowing them down. When the undead horde were unleashed upon us, the\n\ndwarves rallied heavily armoured in ferrum, and equipped with dwarven axes and swords. At first the large numbers of the undead seemed to be a victory for the dwarfs, their poor equipment and lack of skill made the dwarfs win the fight. Then the\n\nattacks stopped, we tried our best to replenish our health, and arm incoming dwarfs who had come to join or rejoin the fight. While our numbers held steady the undead had come and with them they brought armored troops ontop spiders and large\n\npacks of Direwolfs”.-Kazrin StarbreakerOnce again the dwarfs held steady against the onslaught but this time the Undead had come with more powerful troops compromised of wither skeletons, harpies, direwolfs and spider riding ghouls. As the\n\nbattle looked to the dwarfs favor, a large titan sent by the september prince himself appeared from out of the clouds (no joke). It was a massive shark the size of an admiral’s ship with teeth as sharp as daggers and a face that could have the\n\nbravest of men run in terror. The shark flew overhead, heading straight for the elven war camp, with the shark now in eyesight to both the war camps, the dwarves fired their bolt throwers, while the elves used their magics and cannons to fire on\n\nthe beast. The Sky Shark (as it was named) flew overhead vomiting deadly acid that would boil and melt any flesh it touched. Once again both camps took massive casualties, the SkyShark proving to be a worthy foe, vomited all over the elven war\n\ncamp. With the beasts attention turned towards them, the dwarfs were able to fire on the beast without the worry of vomit however still suffered losses to the undead hordes. The battle looked in favor of the prince until a dwarven bolt found its\n\nmark at the head of the beast cracking the skull, piercing the brain, and left vulnerable. With the bolt catching the attention of the shark, its gaze turned to the dwarfs, abandoning the elves, it flew charging straight forward at the dwarfs.\n\nThe dwarfs (a little worried) gave the command for the artillery to fire at will. Bolt after bolt, barrel after barrel, the artillery heavily wounded the beast, sending it crashing down in the trenches below. By this time both the elves, dwarves\n\nand men had already dealt with the undead. Seeing no immediate panic both men and elves had forsaken their war camp instead the remnants leaving for the dwarven forces. Which had already suffered massive losses at the hand of the undead. With\n\nthe shark now defeated and its corpse lay lifeless along the trenches, the dwarfs took it as a sign to rest and heal. But they were caught off guard, out of nowhere the torso and head of shark exploded. Letting out a tide of boiling acid from\n\nthe stomach, and from that stomach birthed giant magma cubes, the dwarves alarmed, shot at the monsters. Now with the dwarves wounded, their armour rent and tired from fighting the titan, had to fight there way through trenches filled with\n\nboiling acid blood and magma cubes. The artillery ineffective at close range, the dwarfs held their ground, slowly but surely their defenses were being filled with boiling acid and many lives were lost in the trenches. But then from out of the\n\nblue came the elves and men, armed with bows and swords they rallied with the dwarfs, slaughtering the magma cubes and evacuating the trenches. But the descendant hadnt won yet, more and more magma cubes were being birthed from the corpse of the\n\ntitan and the acid was still overtaking the trenches soon the land around it would be covered in it. Until Dimlin leader of one of the dwarven nations took out from his beard a dwarven artifact. This artifact would indeed be the hammer of\n\nUrguan, and with it he charged at the corpse. With a mighty swing he brought the hammer down upon the beast and from the sky came a bolt of lightning from Yemekar himself, smiting the titan corpse, ceasing the acid blood from flowing ever on and\n\nthe spawning of the Magma Cubes. Seeing that the dwarven gods were with their people the September retreated his forces. The descendants though at a cost had won the conflict that would later be known as The Battle of Boiling Blood.Kazrins\n\nAccount”What i tell you now reader is the accounts of myself Kazrin Starbreaker, I do not know what befell the elven camp at this time but i do know that it was a hard battle. Our dwarven war camp had a stone platform built on top the grass, on\n\nit were various artillery including dwarven trebuchets and Bolt Throwers. Many trenches were outlined around the war camp making the undead having to go through them, slowing them down. When the undead horde were unleashed upon us, the dwarves\n\nrallied heavily armoured in ferrum, and equipped with dwarven axes and swords. At first the large numbers of the undead seemed to be a victory for the dwarfs, their poor equipment and lack of skill made the dwarfs win the fight. Then the attacks\n\nstopped, we tried our best to replenish our health, and arm incoming dwarfs who had come to join or rejoin the fight. While our numbers held steady the undead had come and with them they brought armored troops ontop spiders and large packs of\n\nDirewolfs”.-Kazrin StarbreakerIts funny looking at how Kazrin and Mervel writes stuff downMERVELS ACCOUNTWe and me dwarf brothers rallied in Kal’Bogrin, and then ran over to the battle field, and prepared forThe incoming attack. Then they\n\nattacked. First, a giant white shark appeared, no eyes, just a mouth.Looked like Kazrins mom, VERY terrifying. It spewed forth lava from its mouth. It then summonedHordes of evil creatures to kill us. The humans and elves camp got destroyed, and\n\nretreated to ours.We had MASSIVE flippy thingies, and big heavy bows to shoot at the shark. We fended off the horribleCreatures, and shot down the white shark. We danced on its dead corpse and had a very nice timeAt the tavern. 10/10 would do\n\nagain.There should be more food. Reminder: “bring more food”", ""),
        StaticBook("The Grandaxes", "§bBorin Grandaxe", "Clan Grandxe\n\nThe Grandaxes are an elder clan from the northern mountains in Aegis. The clan was founded by Bogrin Grandaxe one of the sons of Urguan. He was known for his fierce aggression on the battlefield. He is also Known as the first axe master.\n\nThe Grandaxe clan members are known for their red and orange hair, they value honor and tradition above all else. The Grandaxes are known to have a long line of kings. The clan has strived to maintain dwarven unity between all three dwarven nations.\n\nThe Grandaxe clan is known to defend their honor with their life, Grandaxes do not steal or harm other dwarves as it is considered highly dishorable and nearly unforgivable. They are also known to keep their word and hold blood oaths, and will never break\n\nthem. The Grandaxe clan can be found in the city of Kal'Bogrin and often will give help if needed. Long livu Kal'Bogrin, long livu da kathaikaz kazamar!", ""),
        StaticBook("Dark Shamans", "§bHektor Blackwood", "A new foul being has inserted itself into our Lands. This being is extremely resiliant, capable of great feats of magic. It is no Wraith, Archon, or Lich. In fact, it is not of Light or Dark. It is of a Spiritual Nature. They are, The Dark Shamans.\n\nDark Shamans are known as practitioners of a vile art, not their own Creature or Race. Your writer understands this, though your writer also has faced a new breed of Dark Shaman. It all started in Courland. I encountered a skeletal being wielding\n\nscorching hot air that singed flesh upon contact. I made battle with this being, with the help of brave Men and Elves. Eventually we toppled this foul creature, and I recovered some of the ash left behind when it dis-integrated. It may have been a Lich,\n\nthough Liches cannot combine Evocations. They also cannot be unimpacted by Clerics, which this being was during the fight. I had a compulsive need to fully understand this creature (Which to this day, I do not). A Druid appraised the Ash I collected, and\n\nstated that it was of a Shamanistic nature. I met some Orcs in Sutica. One of them was kind enough to tell me that the creatures were Dark Shamans. I was quite puzzled. I've read of brief bits and pieces of the Dark Shamans from Athera. They looked\n\nnothing like the ones from the days of Athera. I theorize that perhaps this is caused by the source of the Vile Being's magic. Dark Shamans back in Athera derived their power from enslaving Spirits. Perhaps these Skeletal Shamans interact with the\n\nSpirit-Gods of the Mythical Realm in a different way. In a way that truly saps and stretches out their very being. Even with someone as such a keen mind as your Writer, I cannot even fathom how these Dark Shamans interact with the Spirits.\n\nI still keep the Ash with me to this day as a means of both symbolism and practical use. To me, it symbolizes knowledge and it's practical use. If the men and women of Axios can probe the secrets of these horrific beings, we can surely defend ourselves.", ""),
        StaticBook("Elven Children", "§bNiera Acal'elor", "~*~*~*~*~*~*~\n\n\n     Elven Children\n       And  You.\n\nTo be elven is to be with and without blessing. Our blessing is that of a long life, yet that is also part of our curse. It is a long life full of infertilitym yet every few decades Malin smiles upon us, and gives the blessing of a child.\n\nBy now, you should know how children are made. That is not the subject of this piece, and should you wish to know how to, I am sure you can find that written upon a bathroom stall in an oren tavern.\n\nThis book will teach you what to do and what will happen once you and your husband decide to start a family.\n\nAn elven woman comes of age at the age of 50, she is not able to have children before then. \nElven children are not brought about easily. It often times takes years of trying to bring one into the world.\n\nDo not be disheartened, it is our curse that children are not brought onto us. Often times a pregnancy will take, but they are fragile and often times the child may be lost. Elven women can have children ever 15 years.\n\nNow, when Malin has finally blessed you with a child, you will notice a few things. FIrstly the illness. You will feel like you’re rocking on a sinking ship, constantly nauseous and ill. It is important to stay in bed during these times.\n\nOur pregnancies are fragile,and must be cared for. You will also notice strange cravings for food you had never had before. Mine was cake, I was always hungry for cake, I could not get enough of it.\n\nNext, your body will begin to swell. This of course is unpleasant and oftentimes leave the body sore. It is important to no longer travel long distances once you begin showing, as it is hard on the body and the pregnancy. You will get fat.\n\nThe child grows inside the mother for about a year, then, the child is born. If you wish to know more about this, get an anatomy book. \n\nYou now have a little elven child, and have a long life together ahead of you.\n\nYour child will need constant attention, and care. It is important that the child is taught at an early age, so that their mind may develop into something great.\n\nYet playtime is also important. Surround your child with toys and love, and they will prosper in life. \n\nDo not pressure them too much, or limit their dreams. They must be permited to forge their own path.\n\nYour child will begin to walk at about 1-2 years of age, followed by teeth, and the use of simple words. \n\nThis is the prime time to introduce your elven child to books, and educational materials. Be patient, everyone has their own speed-\n\nOf learning.", ""),
        StaticBook("Kazadmar Galraz", "§bHamlin Frostbeard", "Dwarven Language\n-=================-\n\nThe Basics\n\nThe language of the dwarfs is a very complex for other races very few speak the anicent words but most speak the simplest of them yet they never can form basic sentences but most dwarves will always say something on the lines of\n\n\"Narvak Oz Azwrytrumm\"\n\nWhich translates to \"Glory to Frostbeards\"\nbut it isnt always Azwrytrumm which means Frostbeards most of the time Glory to then a clan would be shouted out or a city or kingdom.\n\nEvery Day Words\n-=================-Dwed - Dwarf\nDwedmar - Dwarves\n\nElf - Elger\nElves - Elgus\n\nOrc - Ork\nOrcs - Orkos\n\nHuman - Umri\nHumans - Umros\n\nGoblin - Grobbi\nGoblins - Grobbins\n\nForeign - Yrrok\nForeigners - Yrromar\n(Used mostly to whom aren't Dwarves.)\n\nHello/To - Oz\n\nFarewell - Yankar", ""),
        StaticBook("Yemekar", "§bHogarth Irongut", "IV-Yemekar's Balance\n\nWritten by Morgrim Grandaxe and copied down by Hogarth Irongut, tennant from Da Ord Nar Kadrin.\n\nFrom the dawn of time it was said to be the creator, Yemekar, who selected the Dwarves as the chosen amongst all his creations. However, with this great honour, there too came responsibility. Yemekar commanded of Urguan that he and his kin would forever\n\nemsure that none of his creations would ever bear the power to completely destroy another. \"Go forth my children, and preserve the balance of my creation. For you are the pillars that uphold the world.\" Though these words held many different meanings\n\nthroughout various ages of Dwarven history it is generally accepted by most within the Dwarven Clergy as a matter that remains relevant to this day. Urguan accepted his creator's bidding and thus the Dwarven race, throughout the vast majority of its\n\nexistance, remained vigilant in the event that an empire were to rise. This has in practice become better known amongst the Dwarves as Yemekar's Balance. For if ever a nation were to cast aside its morality in favour of the pursuit of power, the\n\nprosperity of other nations would surely suffer at its hands. \n\nThe concept of Yemekar's Balance therefore revolves largely around a fierce opposition towards policies of expansionism and the invasion of another nation's sovereign\n\nterritory without a cause deemed righteous in the eyes of the gods. Furthermore, in the majority of circumstances, wars that are declared in the name of Yemekar's Balance are almost exclusively made in the defense of nations deemed to lack the\n\ncapability to defend themselves. However, there are a few unique examples that can indeed be to seen to differ from this norm. If a nation is found to be harboring a capability that is deemed wither unholy or dangerous in the wrong hands, the Dwarves may\n\nchoose to act against them. For example, golemancy, gifted unto the hands of the Dwarves by Yemekar himself, is considered a very real threat in the hands of those who are not to be trusted. \n\nToday, we may take no extraordinary effort in viewing tha\n\nDaemon, Khorvad, was once one amongst the Brathmordakin, represented by a will for ambition. Yet with ambition, came the everlasted desire for more. It was thought that plagued the Ironborn ruler, Velkan, as he departed from the ways of Yemekar and\n\ninstead opted to follow in Khorvad's footsteps. So too was it a driving force behind the Holy Oren Empire and its reign of terror upon the Princedom of Malinor. For this, Thorin Grandaxe, former Grand King of Urguan opted to be commended for his actions,\n\neven in going up against a power that  for a period of its history, held the capacity to conquer much of the world. For when the Empire fell, Thorin had within his grasp the opportunity to take both Malinor and Oren for himself, he did not give in to such\n\ntemptations. If we are indeed to tkae one lesson from Thorin's actions, it is that even when we are seemingly on the verge of victory, it is never in any case wise to forsake Yemekar's will. Though greed is a natural blessing, bestowed upon Dwarves by the\n\nBrathmordakin, Grimdugan, ambition and a thirst for power are what drives mortal beings mad. Consequently, it is by no coincidence that empire building is deemed an act of sin in the eyes of many of Urguan's descendants.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Twin Leaders", "§b[Cosmic Guard] Regale Ba'ikana", "The Twin Leaders.\n\nRei and Ray fought as one.\nAll day under the mighty sun.\nGuided by the stars in the sky.\nLike hawks the two will fly.\nIf it ever came to war.\nThe pair would be forced to soar.\n\nNo enemy ever to strong or fast.\nTheir bond together shall make them last.\nTheir strength and wit gave them their might.\nBut what is greatest, is their sight.\nTo lead the warhawkes through and through.\nLooking to the sky as the elements ensue.", ""),
        StaticBook("Nature Healing", "§bKirrekith", "Nature Healing\nBy The Sequoia Druid\nPages 17\n\nThe Nature of Druidic Healing\nBy Lilith Winterleaf, the Sequoia Druid.\n\nDruid Healing is a topic many are curious about. Few, even amongst the druids know the true cost\n\non the person performing the action. Most of the druids use live catalysts to assist in the process of healing. This enables them to draw on this catalysts living energy, this in turn means less energy is draw from the provider to the recipient. However a\n\nskilled user of this magic type, can find themselves performing the action without a live catalyst without any danger to themselves. \n\nDruidic healing for the most part is basic. It is the recieving and giving of living essence from a provider to a\n\nrecipient. The druid focuses on the living tissue of the recipients wounds, and asks the body to mend itself, drawing on the catalyst and the druid. Giving their life essence in exchange for the healing aid.\n\nThis is where the costs and risk of a\n\nDruids healing is, and any would be druid healer should heed this warning well. A druid is capable of amazing feats of healing at times, however it all comes from ones self. In turn, causing possible lasting effects on the provider, and why living\n\ncatalysts are used to lessen the strain on ones self.\n\nI have personally healed a variety of wounds, from cuts and scrapes to sword clashed to broken bones to some far worse than that. They all draw from you to an extent, even when using a catalyst.\n\nSimple wounds may show no strain on you, it depends on the severity of the healing needed, and ones personal ability at healing. Practice being key in safeguarding ones self to the harmful effects. \n\nI am in the belief an example of an mistake\n\nis the most successful way to pass on this lesson to another, I myself, nearly lost my life while healing the King of Skravia back in Asulon. The story had them lured out to a base of mages, that had harassed their kingdom for a while. When they'd\n\ncornered the mage a trap was sprung, explosives unleased upon the King and Guards. Three died in the blast, others dragged the King back to Skravia (severely wounded) and to my Inn, as they knew I was a healer. His body a mess beyond words to describe, as\n\nanyone could imagine from an explosion of the magnitude. However one needed to try, coating his wounds in bonemeal and living slime I began my work drawing on the catalyst as well as myself to save the King. It took close to two hours of healing, and left\n\nhim in a coma for several days. Though I had overstretched myself, my skin a sickly colour, my eyes drained of colour, my lungs not drawing me enough air. I collapsed, and when I woke five weeks had passed, my limbs all sore and my hair a shade lighter,\n\nthough my skin bore a closer to normal tone. A druid, had come to restore the living essence unto me, otherwise I myself would have perished within the first days of unconsciousness, I was that weakened from the healing.\n\nUnderstand this tale to be a\n\nof physical limits of ones abilities to perform healing on a mortally wounded individual without assistance or true grasp of your strength in healing. If you step to far you may risk your life as I did. Find yourself a guide in which to walk between your\n\npersonal sacrificing and also of the catalysts you use to strengthen your abilities, find yourself always something to ease the act of healing, be that grass around you, flowers or trees. Any living catalyst to help carry the burden.\n\nAs wrote by Lilith Winterleaf, the final page missing as missed during the quick jotting down of information in the raid, however it still bares wise words for anyone believing themselves a druid of power. Always know ones limits, and be sure to use all\n\nat your disposal.\n\nBy Lilith Winterleaf, re-wrote by Kirrekith Reffahc of the 16th of the Grand Harvest, 1532, during raid on the Orks Capital. \n\nBy Kirrekith Reffahc.", ""),
        StaticBook("Mount Gorgon", "§bImperial Historian", "**A red hardcovered book lies before you, with the crest of the Holy Oren Empire and House Oren etched in gold on the cover.**\n\n         Victory\n            at\n     Mount Gorgon\n\nA golden-tailed eadly spread its wings to full glide and released a powerful screech. which pierced through the think howling alpine winds on the mountains of Northern Tahn. From a bird's eye\n\nview, one wouldn't be blamed for thinking all was peaceful in the jagged, snowy peaks. Yet, nestled into the crags was a stone fortress built into the mountainside, the bustle of men and the roaring industrious flames emanating from within.\n\nThe Imperial Army had been garrisoned in the mountains for days, mustering, preparing and consolidating their forces. It had been a hard march from St. Karlsburg, but the commanders of the northmen- Karl Barbanov and Andrei Kovachev, were confident that\n\nthis is where the Dwarven host would meet them on the battlefield.\n\nAs it turned out, their suspicions were validated when scouts poured into the encampment. exhuberantly proclaiming that the Urguanite levies had\n\nbeen seen marching across the peaks. The Orenian was machine bustled, the soldiers donned their helms and got into formation, marching out onto the frigid mountains to meet their foe. Soon, they saw the enemy rise over the hill.\n\nA deep warhorn blew, The battle had commended.\n\nThe fighting began with a roar. A narrow wooden bridge connectiong two mountainous peaks was all that seperated the armies of Orenia and the hordes of the Orcs and Dwedmar.\n\nThe Imperials linked their shields in front of the bridge, while the Elves of the Dominion, High Prince Tresery at the head- stood atop high ground, raining death upon the enemy with explosive arrows fired from ironwood bows. The Orcish and Dwarven host\n\nmade the the fateful decision to charge the bridge, and the Imperials followed suit.\n\nThe fight became a bloody slog, with masses of bodies pushing hard against one another at the center of the bridge. One gaining some ground at one moment\n\nthen being pushed back the next. All the while, foes were struck down, and the corpses of orc and dwarf-kin fell from the bridge like dead flesh from a toe.\n\nWith overwhelming numbers, the Imperials, Northmen and Elves pushed through the\n\nUrguanite horde with a ferocious, collective roar. The Dwarves and Orcs scattered as they lost the bridge, fleeing into the mountains. Yet, they were cut down by spectral warriors, an arcane imbued infantry regiment led by Ser Avenal and Count Glewya of\n\nMireton.\n\nAnd so what had once been a moughty struggle between two great armies became a game of cat and mouse, with the imperials hunting down pockets of surviving dwedmar and uruk who had taken to hiding in alcoves in the\n\nmountain.\n\nThe battle came to no romantic, ceremonious end, but simply finished as the last dying cry of the last surviving dwarf was drowned out in the mountain howl.\n\nA flag of imperial purple flew over the\n\nbattlefield, undisturbed. This battle had been an imperial victory.\n\nScribed by an Imperial Historian after confering with the Emperor, Frederick I Phillip.", ""),
        StaticBook("Song Anthology 4", "§bAeran", "Song Anthology: Volume 2\n\nWhen Malin Walked the Forest\n\nThe Oren Knight's Wife\n\nMy Dryad Lover\n\nWhen Malin Walked the Forest\n\nThere was no war\nThere was no razing\nThere was no harming\nWhen Malin walked the forest\n\nSongs were sung\nLands were farmed\nElves within towns\nWhen Malin walked the forests\n\nWe wait with hope\nWe wait with mourning\nWe wait with vigilance\nWe wait for the time when Malin walks the forest once more\n\nThe Oren Knight's Wife\n\nThe Oren Knight's wife was as fair as the sun,\nand her kisses were warmer than spring\nBut the Oren Knight's blade was made of black steel,\nand it's kiss was a terrible thing\nThe Oren Knight's wife would sing as she bathed,\n\nin a voice that was sweet as a peach\nBut the Oren Knight's blade had a song of it's own,\nand a bite sharp and cold as a leech.\nAs he lay on the ground with the darkness around,\nand the taste of his blood on his tongue,\n\nHis brothers knelt by him and prayed him a prayer,\nand he smiled and he laughed and he sung\n\"Brothers, oh brothers, my days here are done,\nthe Oren Knight's taken my life,\nBut what does it matter, for all men must die, and I tasted the Oren Knight's wife!\n\nMy Dryad Lover\n\nWalking through the woods with no care\nWell, no big ones, to be fair\n\nAnd I felt a smack!\nAnd heard a whack!\n\nI was under assault!\nI was not even at fault!\n\nAcorns were launched with no end\nI was confused, I could not even pretend\n\nBit there I saw it\nI had more on my hands than I thought, I admit\n\nBut it rushed at me!\nScreaming like a banshee!\n\nI was tacklde to the ground\nWas quickly bound\n\nBut, soon it became clear\nUpon my cheek appeared a tear\n\nMy Dryad lover!", ""),
        StaticBook("I am Karter", "§bKarter Igne'tahorran", "I am Karter.\n\nMy name is Karter Igne'tahorran I have chosen the fate to be made into a construct and work under Lily of Sutica. I am a Wood Elf with blue eyes and only one ear (my left ear) I now have black air and I am 56 years of age.\n\nAs stated in the first page I am volunteering to become a construct working for Sutica, more precisely under Lily, the princess herself. I understood that I will not remember anything about myself after I have changed into my 'new form'.\n\nAfter I have changed my only wish is to serve for Sutica as long as I possibly can, and assist all of those in need under Lily's command of course.\nI choose to do this because I want to serve Sutica in a more honorable way than most have ever done.\n\n I would like to thank all of those that I have ever met and See you later!   Bye. . .", ""),
        StaticBook("Codex Puritatem", "§bElvira Naromis", "[!] The red leather cover of the pocket-sized book bears only an embossed golden symbol that appears to be a round hollow diamond with a dot in the center: the Clerical Eye. Its white pages turn easily, and each is covered completely in smooth\n\nflowing handwriting. [!]\n\nThe Codex Puritatem\n\n\nThe Doctrines and Beliefs of the Tahariaen Clerics.\n\nWritten by Ashanaak, formally known as Heshakomeu Sohae\n\nIntroduction\n-----------\nMay His Light be with you, servant of Tahariae.\n\nIt is through unified belief that the priests and clerics of Tahariae are strongest. This tome contains the beliefs and doctines of Tahariaean Purity\n\nheld by the Sacred Priesthood of Tahariae, as remembered, developed, decided, and recorded by the High Priest Heshakomeu Sohae.\n\nNever again shall the ways of the priest be forgotten.\n\nThe Five Sacred Tenets of Tahariae\n-----------------\n\n* Shelter and protect thy brothers and sisters in Tahariae. *\n\n* Do not stray in thy dedication to Tahariae. *\n\n* Guide and protect the Descendants of the Four against the Impure. *\n\n* Do not spill the blood of the innocent. *\n\n* Do not use Tahariae's blessing for anything other than His will. *\n\nThe Mission of Tahariae and Purity in His Eyes\n--------\n\nEntities of this world can be divided into three categories: Light, Gray, and Dark.\n\n- A Light entity is an Aengul, one of the holy patrons that grant us mortal servants their powers to purge evil from the realm.\n\n-A Gray entity is a mortal. They are the ones clerics have sworn to protect.\n\n- A Dark entity is a servant of taint and evil. They use unholy powers for personal power or control of the realm by their patron.\n\nWhat is Pure in Tahariae’s eyes is the worship and servitude of Light entities, the protection, aiding, and healing of Grey\n\nentities, and the purging of Dark entities. This is the Mission of the clerics. True Purity shall be established when there is a world without injury or pain, and a world without taint.\n\nThe Holy Lights\n-------------\n\nUpon connection, a cleric receives an aura from our Lord in one of four sacred colors:\n\n- White is the Light of the Pure. Clerics with white light are the wisest members of the clerics, the keepers\n\nof relics and maintainers of purity. They bring light to dark places, and keep the already existing lights glowing.\n\n- Silver is the Light of the Servant. Clerics with silver light are characterized by their dedication to purity and the clerics as a\n\nwhole. They are looked to as leaders within the many orders that have been founded.\n\n- Blue is the Light of the Warrior. Clerics with blue light are the focused hunters of impurity and its effects on the realm. Always the first to be healing the wounded\n\nand on the front line of battles, they are considered the grunts of Tahariae.\n\n- Gold is the Light of the Knight. Clerics with gold light became clerics to protect those they love and use the power of Tahariae to bring good to the world.\n\nValor, bravery, and unfailing courage characterize them.\n\nThe Doctrines of Purity: Doctrine of Dedication\n---------\n\n- A cleric is dedicated to Tahariae and Tahariae alone. To His will and His alone are you subject.\n\n- To violate the Five Sacred Tenets in pursuit of personal\n\ngoals is Impure.\n\n- To abandon or be distracted from Tahariae’s Mission for any reason is Impure.\n\n- A cleric owes worship to Tahariae, thy Lord and Bringer of Purity. You may acknowledge and worship beings equal to and above Him,\n\nbut His command is ultimately the one you follow and His Pristine Being deserves thy honoring. To forsake prayer and worship to Him is Impure.\n\nDoctrine of Separation\n-------------------\n\n- A cleric must separate themselves to anything that may distract or deter them from the Mission Tahariae has given us.\n\n- To hold rank within a nation is Impure, for the responsiblity will distract the cleric\n\nfrom doing what is needed of them, and the decisions you shall be part of making could lead to the deaths of Gray beings, who we swore to protect with the Third and Fifth Tenets.\n\n- To be part of any national military is Impure, for that is supporting and\n\nooperating with an organization that breaks the Third and Fifth Tenets.\n\n- To marry is Impure, for one cannot be fully dedicated to the family while fully dedicated to the Mission. Marriage is only allowable when the spouse is equally dedicated to\n\n the establishment of Purity, whether as a cleric themselves, or of another guild or faith that fights evil. If the non-cleric spouse is none of these things, they must understand that their partner must put their duty above all else.\n\n- To be sexually promiscuous is Impure. The carnal pleasures of this world are distracting, and it is a moral embarrassment for a cleric to engage in them. \n\n- To run an economic establishment is Impure. You cannot dedicate yourself equally to keeping\n\na business financially stable while also dedicating yourself to the Mission.\n\nDoctrine of Justice\n----------------\n\n- A cleric must seek to bring justice wherever they go. To overlook acts of injustice is to overlook the Mission, and is thus Impure.\n\n- To draw distinction between patients for healing based on race, nationality, gender, physical deformities, personal grudges, or what sins they may have committed is Impure. All Gray entities are to be healed and protected. The only distinction a cleric\n\nhould draw is between a Gray and a Dark entity; those who serve unholy forces are not to be helped, unless it would somehow support the Mission.\n\n- To allow a Dark being to harm Gray entities under the cleric’s watch is Impure. We cannot let evil occur\n\nwithout action. The only excuse for inaction is if action is less effective than informing the other clerics of the evil and organizing a group to bring justice to it.\n\n-  To harm a Gray entity for any reason other than self-defence is Impure. We are the\n\nprotectors, not the assaulters, of the Descendants.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Abjurist", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "Wards & Abjuration\n^v^v^v^v^v^v^v^v^v^              a\n         study by\n\n  Gallidron Elindrow\n\nAbjuration is a facinating branch of voidal magic, and perhaps the most difficult. I say this because the most knowledge is required to be a succesfull abjurist or warder.\nTo cast a mighty evocation, one need only understand the element that will be th\n\nmedium and the art of evocating. To transmute water into ice one needs to understand the intricasies of the freezing process, to conjur one must know what they wish to make in exact detail before they can begin to even form the creature or item in the\n\nvoid. But to ward against these things, to abjure them into non-exsistance, one must not only understand how to cast protective magic, but they must also understand in detail the magic they wish stop.\n\nIt is for this reason that I say, the successful abjurist should be lauded above all other mage kind for they are at once massively powerfull and a dutiful student of all forms of magic. I would admonish any who seek to ward or abjure to learn all they\n\ncould of magic that they might not be caught unprepared. It would even be prudent to learn what one could of the dark arts, within the bounds of reason and safety, that they are not caught off guard by these most sinister magics.\n\nAn Abjuration is a more offensive style of protecting one's self or others from magic. Suppose that an enemy mage has cast a fire spell at you and a veritable flood of flame is headed in your direction. Now, you are somewhat knowledgable in the department\n\nof evocation and so you realize that the spell itself is functioning on the premise of converted energy. Fire is after all just energy moving from one form into another. In this case that energy is the mana of the mage and the form it has taken is shaped\n\nin the void. There are several ways to go about this, as is the beauty of abjuration (one is only limited by their resevoir of power and their imagination). You could try to disrupt the flow of mana from the mage to the spell, or you could break its\n\nconnection to the void. All in all, the most effective, fool proof, and easiest way is likely to break the connection to the void. This is called disrupting the mana anchor. The Mana Anchor is the metaphorical place where the spell and the energy for it\n\nmeet and create its effect. It is also what keeps the spell active in our world and not just a figment of a thought in the void. Knowing these things you craft your abjuration and destory the spell before it gets to you. Assuming of course that you are\n\nas powerful or more so than the mage who is trying to fry your skin off.\n\nA ward is more deffensive and takes more time to make. They are also potentially more versitile and usefull, this is the cause for the increased time of casting.\n\nA ward is stationary and is used like a shield against one or various forms of magic. Where as an Abjuration can be cast in the moment, it can only defend from one kind of magic. A ward can be crafted with care and forethought and thus be made to\n\ncounteract various kinds of magic at once. They can last for a long time, given that they have a steady supply of mana to draw upon. The larger and more intricate the ward, the more energy will be required. A ward that is crafted and placed on an object\n\nor in a place can be thought of much like an enchantment. In fact many enchantments are wards of one kind or another. These spells require the use of a mana gem, a kind of magical battery, to continue to function after the mage has left, and even then\n\nthe mana gem will only last for so long.\n\nA working knowledge of the magic to be blocked by the ward is still required to create the spell.\n\nPower is of tantamount importance. If you are a beginning abjurist, you cannot block the fire ball of a master evocationist. They will simply overwhelm you with the might of their spell. One must be at least equal to their opponent to bring their casting\n\nto a stand still.\n\nOne does not need to be a master evocationist, or even be able to cast evocation, to create wards or abjurations against it. But you will need at least a working knowledge of the element used.  Of course the more experience you hav\n\nthe better you will fare as an abjurist.\n\nI hope that this book has been enlightening to you as a reader and that you will put this knowledge to good use.\n\n-Gallidron Elindrow\npublishing date 6th of\nGrand Harvest, 1519\n\nPlease look for my next study on the Arcane!\n\nLightning and fire and frost, oh my!\n\na study on Evocation", ""),
        StaticBook("Element Quality", "§bAmbros", "Of the Four Elements and Their Natural Qualities\n\nBy Ambros\n\nIT is necessary that we should know and understand the nature and quality of the four elements, in order to our being perfect in the principles and ground-work of our studies in the arcanic Art.\n\nTherefore, there are four elements, the original grounds of all corporeal things, viz. fire, earth, water, and air, of which elements all inferior bodies are compounded; not by way of being heaped up together, but by transmutation and union; and when they\n\nare destroyed, they are resolved into elements. But there are none of the sensible elements that are pure; but they are, more or less, mixed, and apt to be changed the one into the other: even as earth, being moistened and dissolved, becomes water, but\n\nthe same being made thick and hard, becomes earth again; and being evaporated through heat it passes into air, and that being kindled into fire, and this being extinguished, into air gain, but being cooled after burning, becomes earth again, or else\n\nstone, or sulphur; and this is clearly demonstrated by lightning. Now every one of these elements have two specifical properties: the former whereof it retains as proper to itself; in the other, as a mean, it agrees with that which comes directly after\n\nit. For fire is hot and dry--earth, cold and dry;--water, cold and moist--and air, hot and moist. And so in this manner the elements, according to two contrary qualities, are opposite one to the other: as fire to water, and earth to air. Likewise, the\n\nelements are contrary one to the other n another account: two are heavy, as earth and water--and the others are light, as fire and air; therefore the Stoics called the former, passives--but the latter, actives. And scholars distinguishes them after\n\nanother manner, and assigns to each of them three qualities, viz. to the fire, brightness, thinness, and motion--to the earth, darkness, thickness, and quietness; and, according to these qualities, the elements of fire and earth are contrary. Now the\n\nother elements borrow their qualities from these, so that the air receives two qualities from the fire,--thinness, and motion; and the earth one, viz. darkness. In like manner water receives two qualities of the earth,--darkness and thickness; and the\n\nfire one, viz. motion. But fire is twice as thin as air, thrice more moveable, and four times brighter; the air is twice more bright, thrice more thin, and four times more moveable. Therefore, as fire is to air, so is air to water, and water to the earth;\n\nand again, as the earth is to the water, so is water to air, and air to fire. And this is the root and foundation of all bodies, natures, and wonderful works; and he who can know, and thoroughly understand these qualities of the elements, and their\n\nmixtures, shall bring to pass wonderful and astonishing things in magic.\n\nNow each of these elements have a threefold consideration, so that the number of four may make up the number of twelve; and, by passing by the number of seven into ten, there may be a progress to the supreme unity upon which all virtue and wonderful\n\nthings do depend. Of the first order are the pure elements, which are neither compounded, changed, or mixed, but are incorruptible; and not OF which, but THROUGH which, the virtues of all natural things are brought forth to act. No man is able fully to\n\ndeclare their virtues, because they can do all things upon all things. He who remains ignorant of these, shall never be able to bring to pass any wonderful matter.\n\nOf the second order are elements that are compounded, changeable, and impure; yet such as may, by art, be reduced to their pure simplicity; whose virtue, when they are thus reduced, doth, above all things, perfect all occult and common operations of\n\nNature; and these are the foundation of the whole of Natural Magic.\n\nOf the third order, are those elements which originally and of themselves are not elements, but are twice compounded, various and changeable into another. These are the infallible medium, and are called the middle nature, or soul of the middle nature;\n\nvery few there are that understand the deep mysteries thereof. In them is, by means of certain numbers, degrees, and orders, the perfection of every effect in what thing soever, whether natural, celestial, or supercelestial: they are full of wonders and\n\nmysteries, and are operative as in Magic natural, so divine. For from these, through them, proceeds the binding, loosing, and transmutation of all things--the knowledge and foretelling of things to come--also, the expelling of evil, and the gaining of\n\ngood spirits. Let no one, therefore, without these three sorts of elements, and the true knowledge thereof, be confident that he can work any thing in the Occult Science of Magic and Nature.\n\nBut whosoever shall know how to reduce those of one order into another, impure into pure, compounded into simple, and shall understand distinctly the nature, virtue, and power of them, in number, degrees, and order, without dividing the substance, he\n\nhe shall easily attain to the knowledge and perfect operation of all natural things, and celestial secrets likewise; which teaches all these before mentioned; and, by a perfect knowledge thereof, we perform many rare and wonderful experiments.", ""),
        StaticBook("A note", "§bHearth Underson", "A little something to help you get settled in, \nKindly- Underson", ""),
        StaticBook("The Martyr", "§bSporan Kyroc", "If I could bear your sadness, I would.\n\nIf I could, for a minute, take away your pain and make it mine, I would.\n\nIf I could tell you there is a reason for this, I would.\n\nI will do anything to take away your pain.\n\nBut sometimes life makes some unexplainable twists and unfortunate turns\n\nAnd the world seems cold and unfeeling...\n\nI can't tell you how sorry I am.\n\nThat I cannot shelter you from this.\n\nBut I will leave you with this thought...\n\nI am here.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nIf you want to talk, if you find comfort in sharing silence with me. I am here.\n\nYou are important to me...\n\nI care.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Flagship", "§bSt. Thomas Denims III", "----The Flagship---\nAXIOS WAR BULLETIN I\nThe Amber Cold, 1583\n\n--Contents--\n~Grand King Executed\n~Oren Suffers Loss at THE GORGE\n~Allies Stand Firm Behind Emperor Philip Frederick\n~Religious Roundup: Reforms and Schism\n\n~Debate in Haelun'or Over Security\n~Haria Reigns in Military\n\nGRAND KING ALGODA EXECUTED BY ORENIAN -------FOES-------\n\nAlgoda, Grand King of Urguan, was executed by Orenian officials after being seized in the Orenian town of Ostermark. This has hardened opinions in Kal'Omith in favor of the the war and the\n\nSenate of the Grand Kingdom of Urguan will be convening this Saint's Day to select a new King.\n\nOREN SUFFERS HUMILIATING LOSS AT THE GORGE, ATTEMPTS TO CONSOLIDATE CONTROL IN LORRAINE\n\nThe forces loyal to the Holy Oren \nEmperor Philip I Frederick were decimated and roted from the field of battle in the opening classh of the\n\nStaunton rebellion. The Stauntons and their allies held firm against a numerically superior and more advanced foe. This marks a rare loss for the Holy Oren Empire and promises to prolong the current conflict.\n\nTHE DUCAL CITY OF\n~~~~~~METZ~~~~~~\n\nMetz, located in the Archduchy of Lorraine, has experienced heavy fighting between rebels from the Staunton family and loyalists led by Sir Otto. Forces loyal to the emperor currently control the city,\n\nwhile rebels control much of the rest of the Archduchy of Lorraine, setting up what is sure to be a pivotal battle in the current war.\n\nALLIES STAND FIRM BESIDE PHILIP I \n---FREDERICK---\n\nThe Dominion of Malin and the Kingdom of Haense have reaffirmed their loyalty to the throne of the HOE despite the recent loss. However, public opinion in the Dominion of Malin appear divided,\n\nas many wonder why elvish blood should (and indeed was) spilled in the internal affairs of the valah. Old debates about th true independence of the Dominion and the true allegiances of it's leadership have also resurfaced. The Kindom of Haense, however,\n\nhas moved to actively supress any rebel activity within its border in addition to aiding the war effort.\n\nRELGION ROUNDUP: REFORMS AND SCHISM\n\nThe Church of Lorraine, also known as the Lotharic Communion, has announced a schism from the Church of the One True Faith. The rebels of Lorraine and Savoy have often raised\n\nallegation of interference against the Emperor in regards to reforms of the Church, and this appears to be the logical course now that the rebellion is being waged.\n\nAdditionally, the Accords of Johannesburg were\n\nadvanced by the Emperor and High Pontiff Adrian I, further cementing the state control over the Church of the One True Faith. Only time will tell whether the schism will be sealed and if the reforms will stand.\n\nDEBATE IN HAELUN'OR OVER SECUIRTY\n\nCahir aep Ophael, Braxus Ni'leya, and Icarus are vying for an appointment as the elokarir'tir. Cahir appears to have the most support among the citizenry, but it is up to the Silver Council to decide who\n\nget the post. There is pressure on the Silver Council to act swiflty, as recent events have revealed that lax security can lead to needless bloodshed within the Silver City.\n\nHARIA REIGNS IN \n---MILITARY---\n\nThe Lord Regeant of Haria, Fakhri Kharadeen, has established a court system to prevent the military from harassing citizens and visitors with little to no oversight. This will hopefully make Haria\n\na more pleasant place to visit, having removed the threat of state violence against individuals without any due process.\n\n\n~Ebs Telrunya\nEDITOR IN CHIEF\n~St. Thomas Denims\nPRINTER OF PONCE", ""),
        StaticBook("Vuurdor", "§bTorkan Starbreaker", "Vuurdor also known as The Void in common tongue is to be seen as a dark an a empty realm but no one has really seen the void and what it looks like. I on other hand believe the void looks similar to our realm but different. What I mean is I\n\nthink the void looks like a past self of our earth and that it almost looks like an old battle ground, with broken down buildings, dead trees, covered in ash and dust. The void is only an image of our past worlds, and it only shows the\n\ndevastation that happened after we abandoned them. The Void is a place where the dishonorable go as it is said by some. Some people believe that is where true dwed go and live on freely. I say this because many believe that after a dwarf dies\n\nhis or her body goes to Khaz’A’Dentrumm where they serve one of the brathmordakin for an eternity doing whatever the god commands. When I die I do not wish to go to Khaz’A’Dentrumm but to the void where I can walk the halls of past cities and\n\nclimb mountains that have long been destroyed. That is a place I feel ill truly be free.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Irongut Clan", "§bTorkan Starbreaker", "The Irongut Clan: A clan of Cave Dwarves, the Ironguts were one of the first clans to regain their history and band back together again during the reign of King Simmpa. Irongut dwarves are known magic users of the dwarven nation, having also\n\nbeen known to become members of the Ascended and Undead orders. Their clan members are very closely knit and defend each other at any chance they can. Almost all members of the clan follow the Brathmordakin and have had members in all guilds at\n\nsome point in time. Ironguts also pride themselves on their use in the magical arts, collecting artifacts, and recording the histories of their clan and the Kingdom.", ""),
        StaticBook("Alsace Catacombs", "§bNoach Hughes", "The excavation of the Alsace Catacombs.\n\n10th of the Grand Harvest, 1532.\n\nAfter days of heavy rainfall, the entrance to the old catacombs is subsiding. Noach Hughes and Father Augustus, Priest of Alsace decided to --\n\nexcavate the catacombs, after slowly digging up the dirt and rubble, a staircase was revealed that lead to the underground system of tunnels and chambers. \nThe two slowly descended further into the catacombs --\n\nrevealing ancient ritual sacrifices, coffins and treasures that the disceased had taken into their graves and burial chambers.\n\n10th of the Grand Harvest, 1532.\n\nNoach and Augustus spent most of their -\n\ntime inside the catacombs, uncovering the long forgotten past. At first the catacomb appeared to be rather small, but after clearing out all the rubble and dirt they uncovered a large tunnel network that was greater than they could ever imagine.\n\n17th of the Grand Harvest, 1532.\n\n7 days had passed since the excavation had started, both Noach and Augustus felt rather sick, exhausted and fatigued. But somehow they were still inside the catacombs, as if a strange power --\n\nhad taken control of them. Slowly they began developing dark intentions and thoughts. Rumour has it that the two have been shackled by the catacomb's magical power.\n\n24th of the Grand Harvest, 1532.\n\nDays slowly passed--\n\nand Noach and Augustus start to act normal again, like if nothing had happend to them. Both went on to continue living their normal lives. \n\nIt would appear that the curse that was cast upon the two had been banished from their souls.\n\n* The pages appear to have been ripped out of the book, leaving only the first 7 remain in the book *", ""),
        StaticBook("Hello", "§bIdril Aureon", "Dear Eradan and Jason,\n\n   I can't see you anymore. Things between us are just akward. Uh, bye I guess.\n\n    -Idril Aureon", ""),
        StaticBook("Vailor, A Report", "§bFygmor Khen'aum", "The State of Vailor 1557, A journal.\n\nVailor is the place where the decendants live, The Orcs, The Dwarves, The Humans, The Halflings, The Elves, and the Kha. Amoung other magical constructs and creatures. It is a large island where most of\n\nthe cities sit upon plains or mountians, or even smaller minor islands. \n\nChapter 1 : The Monk Temple.\n\nThe main hub to all of vailor is the dock owned by the Monks.\nNo blood can be shed here, because it is under protection.\n\nIt is the hub to all of Vailor, like stated before, because of all of its carriages and boats that lead to the major cities of Vailor. It is a safe place for many and has its own shops and auction areas. \n\nChapter 2: Haelun'or\n\n\nThe large city of Haelun'or, home to the High Elves. A place with winding paths, towering buildings, and many many people. It is where most 'pure' high elven people live, but many high elves live elsewhere. The main area is home to a Tavern, a bank, and\n\nan auctioneer. \n\nAt the time of writing this, their stalls are empty or coming soon. I have yet to go into the walls of the main area of the city. \n\nThe houses in the outside area of the cities follow a road and wind up a hill, these houses at the\n\ntop of the hill have nicer doors, and nicer stone. The stone they use is a nice smooth one. Since I do not have sight I can not tell for certain what it is. \n\nChapter 3: Felsen\n\nPerhaps it self a mini-hub, felsen is home to the humans.\n\nIn it's center, after stepping of the cart. Are many other carts and a rough, coarse dirt ground, mixed in with gravel and some cobblestone. The Orenian people inhabit this land, they are the main leaders of humans, because no other human civilization\n\nis as strong in manpower as the Orenian one. Its rough path leads across a moat, if you could call it that, not of water but of trash. Once you cross this bridge you find yourself in an even rougher, winding, huge city. You would not be surprised to know\n\nthat most of the population is part of the army. So the people here are rough and though. Stalls surround the area along with some buildings. The place seems barren and void of any substance. It is a wonder to me why people live here. To each their own.\n\nBut on that note, it may have to do with loyalty. \n\n\nRacism in Oren:\n\nIt seems some of the people who live in felsen or the areas surronding it have a racial or cultural hate towards a clan of hillmen named the Raevirs. I can not tell\n\nwhy they hate these people, but it has something to do with them thinking they are tribal.\n\nChapter 4: The Caliphate\n\nSandy, desolate, uninteresting. This describes the caliphate. It is under construction, it seems\n\nbut the construction seems to have no workers. But the druid grove near it has people in it, and a nice, but small library. More on librarys next chapter.\n\nChapter 5: The Dragur Library\n\nThe Library of Dragur is one of the biggest\n\nlibrarys in all of vailor, to my knowledge at least. It is filled with books from magic, to fiction, and even history. It is a place where you can learn. But it is a public place so do not expect it to be too quiet. But do not expect it to be too exciting\n\nIt is a place I like to visit. It's 'scholars' are nice and the books are of good quality.\n\nThe library is the biggest in Vailor.\n\nChapter 6: Sutica\n\nSutica is a merchant island that sits upon the sea, to be more precise upon 10+ tiny\n\nislands. You can taste the salt on the air and the smell the scent of mushrooms on the west wind. It is a place where you can buy many things, for example: I recently bought myself a twisted staff. The island runs on trade and economy like this. It is a\n\nfairly peaceful area.\nSutica houses very valuable resources in a vault, inside the bank. About 100 people live in the city of Sutica. The city is said to have been around for a long time now, it had started in \"The Now Lost Salvus.\"\nSources: \nShynys\n\nItesti.\n\nChapter 7: The Iron Uzg.\n\nThe Iron Uzg is the place where the orcs reside. When you come upon the Iron Uzg's Capital, heading up the road will grant you access to a, what I assume is large from the echo, building.\n\nTo get to the Iron Uzg, you must either walk here, or take the boat from the dock. The front path is rough and rocky, but it is not hard to walk past it. When you come to the main path there are some smaller buildings leading up to the large one.\n\nThe Orcs are known for being quite rude to visitors, so I must go! \n\nChapter 8: Kal'Ishtul\n\nKal'Ishtul, home of the dwarves. The dwarven city of Kal'Ishtul is located quite deep in a cavern. If you would like to get into the city you through a short\n\ntunnel, then come out of it, and then you cross a bridge. It seems to currently be in construction but once it's done, it seems it will be huge.\n\nOn the dwarves, they are not seen around the capital nearly as much as you would think! Strange.\n\nChapter 9: Willow Hollow.\n\nWillow Hollow,\nHome of the halfings,\nThe smell of flowers and tea lingers in the air for all to smell. The grass is soft and fertile. Willow Hollow is as small as the halflings, and it does not seem to have such a high\n\npopulation. But I could be wrong, the halflings do usually share a home with their family, it would be selflish in their culture if they did not. The towns citizens are said to be nice. It is like any other town, but seems peaceful and smells wonderful, I\n\n would wager that if I could see, it would be much better! It is a farming town, as the halflings are a farming people. For more on halflings I reccomend the history of halflings in the Monk Literature section.\n\nChapter 10: The Rebelious State of\n\nthe Dreadlands. \n\nA place where it is said, they have no laws and complete freedom. Currently in a war against the orenians, so by the time I am done writing this chapter they may already be gone... It is a dangerous place here, and an ugly looking\n\none too. I think it is a bad idea to have no rules at all, it makes it dangerous and attracts the wrong kind of people. They have rough orenian style buildings, which parallels their former liege. There is only one well in the city, and barely any other\n\nwater... Or anything for that matter. This place is strange, and dangerous.\n\n\nThe End.\n\nWritten By Fygmor Khen'aum.\nSources: Armin Ambertoe, Shynys Itesti, and others.", ""),
        StaticBook("New Elven Vol II", "§bKalenz Uradir", "New Elven Lessons: Volume 2\n by Kalenz Uradir\n\nJust as in common, pronouns may be used to replace nouns. The pronouns in elven are as follows: \n\nKae - Me \nLae - Him/He \nNae - You \nLye - We - Used to speak of elves, people or the world. \nHae - Her/She\n\nFor example the sentence 'elvulnir van ayla' (The trickster fared well) may be transformed into 'Lae van ayla' (He fared well). \n\nIn addition to this, other good language supplements to anyone learning elven include basic affixes. These affixes may b\n\n added to create further detail or form critical grammatical structures in a sentence.\n\nThe dash denotes location of seed word. Affixes and seed words are separated by an apostrophe. \n\nac- (aca-) - Honorific for accursedness. \nah- (ahe-) - Honorific for reverence. Often used as a prefix for scholars. For example: Ah'Lucion.\n\nfi- - New or anew.\ncer- (Slang from Ceru) - Honorific for strength. Often used as a prefix for those of high military rank. For example: Cer'Silir.\n-ante (-nte) - Last \n-ento (-nto) - Next \n-onn - From or born. \nu- - Or\n\nvul- (cule) - Clever or deceptive. \n-ir - Designates purpose of someone or something. \n-sae - The spreading, development or management. \n-ii - Diminutive form. For example: Malii, meaning little elf.\n\nAs always, a full list of affixes may be found in the Elven Dictionary.", ""),
        StaticBook("Studying Humans", "§bGrimsly Copperpot", "A Study of Humans: Volume I\n\n*The pages are filled with crumbs*\n\nHumans! Fascinating creatures.  Having lived among them many years as a Halfling serving as an alchemist, they seem to have some of the same tendencies as Halflings, such as eating, drinking, and debauchery.\n\nThe life span of humans is relatively short, around 70 years or so, almost a third of that of any halfling and an eight of any elf.  The young tend to embrace fighting and war, while the old tend to squabble over petty politics.\n\nThat's not to say they are all bad.  Some of them can be just as merry as any halfling, while others might require a pint or two of ale.\n\nIf meeting a human always follow the general rule of thumb: you don't know them.  Personalities of humans vary from human to human, making  any broad overlap of them.  Don't trust one until you've had a drink with one.  \n\n--G.C.", ""),
        StaticBook("Observations", "§b[Dedicant] Thickfeet", "Observations\n            on\n        Enchantments\n\n      \n\n\n\n\nWritten by\nLethius Thickfeet\n\nAs my learnings during my druid dedicancy continue, it has come to my attention the unnatural tendencies of the magical realm.\n\nIt its known that the source of most arcane magics is the great endless Void.\n\nIt is also believed by some the damaged cause by such usage is severe and slowly affects the greater realms that we live in.\n\nI was tasked to witness this in person. \n\nI spent a few days looking to the locals of Kal'Archon for\n\na regular magic user. Unforunately I found noone in the safety of the newly built city.\n\nOf course within the Druid Grove itself that kind of search would be futile.\n\nSurprisingly my search led me right under my nose.\n\nI was sifting through old belongings and came across a small journal I had purchased decades before.\n\nAmong my collection stood a very unique\n\nitem. A mage's journal had described the usage and discoveries she had made involving Enchantments.\n\nI glanced through the pages where a short collection of glyphs and its attributes were described in detail.\n\nIt was clear to me that such magical imbuement must have come from the same source as most Arcane magics.\n\nWhat I found was not wrong, and what found me was unnatural in every way.\n\nI began by searching the city markets for the magical reagents needed to perform enchantments.\n\nAfter collecting a few cheap tools and swords, the natural emerald stone which takes most precidence in the profession, and a mixture of other\n\npowders and artifacts required, I set out into the mountains to find a secluded and safe place to examine and study.\n\nThe first few days of attempts yielded nothing of value. \n\nMost attempts ended with absolutely no\n\nchange to the item in question. Some attempts the enchantments didn't hold but I had started to gain progress.\n\nFor most of those days, deep meditation and rebalance of the area is how I kept my focus. For every single attempt I\n\nmeditated to find signs to stop my continued attempts. It seemed to me that nature itself approved of me finding out the dangerous truth of the Arcane.\n\nI also repaid my attempts with various planting of flowers and herbs. Thankfully my work in gathering\n\nleft me with the stores to do so.\n\nEventually my labor bore fruit. I managed to enchant an old sword with a magical sharpness. It was almost as if the enchantment itself took precidence to the edge of the old blade. Ahead of the blade\n\nwas a magical barrier that cut through most things much easier than the obvious dull blade would have ever done alone. \n\nI rested that night after planting a healthy sapling nearby.\n\nThat night was some of the worst sleep I could have imagined. I dreamed of a darkness swallowing all around me. I couldn't outrun it, and eventually it over came me as I ran for my life.\n\nI awoke in the middle of the night\n\nknowing that something dark was coming due to the actions I had taken in those mountains. \n\nThe sounds of the area were too silent. The life of the area had fled and I could feel an unnatural emittion from the sword.\n\nI picked up the sword with both hands and felt the great weight atop the used hilt.\n\nI turned to see that a group of undead abominations had found me.  Running up the hill I felt the sweat and pain in my legs as I gained hieight but not distance.\n\nTaking a few wild swings I was able to stop a few of them as I ran. \n\nThe feeling of futility overcame me as the more I used the sword, the more monsters I had seemed to see. \n\nWhat had I unleashed? This was obviously\n\nno intent behind the enchantment, but I was starting to believe the author of that journal might have known exactly what they were doing when writing down a 'Sharpness' enchantment.\n\nI had been tricked and I was paying the price.\n\nI began slashing more wildly at everything in sight.  If I could wear out the blade and break it, I knew the enchantment would cease.  \n\nWhile this included some of the monsters around, I also slashed at the stoney earth.\n\nThe clangs of metal and stone probably agitated more of these monsters and the pain seared in my arms with every swing.\n\nI thought of death and how I had truly deserved it by naively jumping into a magic I didn't understand.\n\nA piercing wail filled my ears and a satisfying relaxation overcame me as the weight was lifted from my hands.\n\nThe enchantment had ended and the old sword was scrap at my feet.\n\nAs I stood watching the creatures come\n\nfor me, I decided to earn my fate. \n\nMy pulse filled my hearing, my body shook with fright, and I realized my folly.\n\nI closed my eyes and asked the aspects for forgiveness as the footsteps came closer and closer...\n\nA sudden silence filled my ears as powerful as a dragon's roar.\n\nIt felt like an age passed before I gained the courage to open my eyes. \n\nI sat on my knees completely astonished. As swiftly as the creatures appeared,\n\nthey had suddenly dispersed into the darkness.\n\nI spent a few days longer within the trees just thinking of the events. I hid the remainder of the items I purchased around the area hoping they would be lost with time.\n\nOnce I returned to the Grove I immediately penned what you have just read.  I hope that my story can help in those that come after me. \n\nDo not delve into what we know least about without guidance and carefulness.\n\nThe void contains a power that we are simply unable to wield elegently and it is not to be toyed with.\n\nI pray that my actions do not reflect poorly on the order, nor did I do too much damage to nature itself.\n\nDedicant\nLethius Thickfeet\n\n13th of the Grand Harvest.\n\n1457", ""),
        StaticBook("Deity Magic", "§bGallidron Elindrow", "I I\n             I I\n       ___\\I I/___\n       ----I I----\n         `~/I I\\~'\n             I I\n             I I\n             \\/\n            The\n   Power  of  Prayer\na guide to deity magic\n             By\n   Gallidron Elindrow\n\nDeity magic, unlike arcane magic, is highly contingent upon the relationship between the \"caster\", for lack of a better term, and the source of their power. For example a cleric or an aengulic faith may recieve great power from their patron aengul. Given\n\nthat they are trusted enough and have gained sufficient favor with the patron. Indeed, the practitioner of deity magic must learn to rely almost wholly upon their otherworldy masters and their whims for a scrap of their might.\n\nIn these pages I will attempt to list and off a brief explanation as the to each of the known branches of Deity Magic.\n\n          ~ONE~\n        The Cleric\n-------------------Clerics tend to gain power through the worship of the \"Creator\" and the veneration of His Aenguls. The powers gained depend largely upon the aengul from which they come though are usually\n\ncentered around healing, light and protection.\nThe aenguls are listed here.\nAeriel- Arch~aengul and caretaker of souls\nEshtael-Balance and destiny\nGazardiael-curiosity and new beginings\n\nNemiisae- aengul queen of spiders\nTahariae- purity and patron of clerics\nWandering Wizard- An aengul who wander the seven lands.\nWyrvun- Cold and virtue\nYeu Rthulu- contentment and compassion\nXan- order\n\nMost clerics venerate Tahariae or Xan though worship of the others is not unheard of.\n\n           *TWO*\n           Druids\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~Druidism is perhaps the oldest of the deity magics, but this depends on whom you speak with. The druids have, for ages taken it upon themselves to protect nature and to keep its secrets. They order of\n\ndruids is most definately an old one and has survived relatively unchanged. This is due to the certain level of indoctrination that take place amoung the acolytes who seek to join the order. This process is called Dedicancy and is evidently\n\nquite effective. After some time of being given tasks to complete and lectures to attend, the worthy new-comer is led to a pool of attunement and placed in its waters. The high concentration of druidic energies there attune the mind of the individual to\n\n\"The will of nature\", or so it is said. Whether or not this is the case the druid gains impressive control over nature and usually becomes wholly devoted to protecting the natural world.\n\nThe powers of the druid, so far as I have been able to catalog are listed here.\n\nCONTROL OF NATURE-\nA druid can coax life from even the driest ground. They can cause trees to spring immediately from tiny saplings. They can\n\ntie their foes in vines and mold trees into new shapes. The Druid is a master of manipulating nature in almost endless ways.\n\nBLIGHT HEALING- When necromancy is used there is often an occurance of blight. The land becomes cursed and all life in it withers\n\nIt is within the druids power to remedy this, though depending on the strength of the blight it may take time and more than one druid.\n\nHEALING- Druids are talented healers that seem to increase the bodies natural ability to heal itself. It is said that\n\nonly monks and clerics are better at it.\n\nSHAPE SHIFTING- This is perhaps the most facinating branch of their magic (no pun intended). The Druid, when powerful enough, can change their very physical and biological make-up and become a mariad of different\n\nthings. Not much is known about this abillity, in fact very few even know about it. Even I, who have read all I can find on the subject, am not sure if it is even a reality or just a rumor. One thing remains certain, that this is one of the most closely\n\nguarded secrets of the druids.\n\nCOMMUNION WITH NATURE- This is perhaps the most important of the druid's abillities. Not because it is the most powerful or awe inspiring to witness, but because this is from where all their other powers stem.\n\nIn truth the druid does not command nature. They speak with it and ask it to do things for them, and if nature is willing it complies.\n\n          %Three%\n          Shamans\n-------------------It is believed that Shaman originated from the orcs. As the story goes, thinner, smaller orcs were thought to be more apt at intellectual persuits than the brutal aspects of a stronger orc's\n\nlife, and so the art of Shamanism was born. These orcs learned to commune with spirits of various natures and there by gain magical power of various natures as well. The entire practice of Shamanism has to do with the contact and appeasment of spirits.\n\nThe spirits are catagorized into three different types.\n\nELEMENTAL- These are spirits of the elements and embody the aspect that they represent.\n\nIMMORTAL- These represent various aspect of life. These spirits are not so flashy\n\nbut are highly sought for various reasons. For examply, one might commune with the spirit of the hunt if they wish to be \"blessed\" in their hunting efforts. There other Immortal spirits of course, each having to do with different aspects; Honor, strength,\n\nhusbandry, battle, wisdom, ect...\n\nANCESTRAL- These are the spirits of the dead. Those who came before and might be called upon to offer wisdom and proctection. They are often refered to as Ancestrals rather than spirits.\n\nGREAT SPIRITS- While not exactly one of the three base distinctions, it is wise to denote that a Great Spirit is of some import. They are the most powerful of their kind. The is a great fire elemental spirit as there is a great spirit of fertility, and so\n\non. These are akin to kings over their kind of spirit.\n\nShamans call upon these spirits to gain different effects though most develope an affinity for one or another.\nThese shaman subtypes are as follows.\n\nELEMENTALIST- A caller of elemental spirits to devistating effect.\n\nFARSEER- One who communes with Immortal spirits to gain blessings that increase strength, prowess, healing, ect...\n\nLATAUMAN- Uses Ancestrals to increase their combat prowess.\n\nWITCHDOCTOR- These interesting shamans use potions and brews to gain the effects and help of all types of spirits.\n\n       CONCLUSION\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThese are the main kinds of deity magic users. There are also The Temple Monks and the Muun'Trivazja, but these two sects are not covered in this work.\nIt is my hope that the subject of deity magic has been illuminated\n\nsomewhat for you and that this book has left you, if not wiser, then more educated at least.\n\n-Gallidron Elindrow\n\nPublication date\n11th of Sun's Smile 1518\n\nPlease look for my next book!\n\nARCANISTS AND WORSHIPERS\na comparison of magics.", ""),
        StaticBook("Aspects: Fear", "Valmir_", "Aspect Tome: Fear\nAuthor Unknown\n\nFear, another emotion that drives the Will of a man. This Book will describe all it can, for fear can not be a good thing for the Druids, not at all... The emotion of Fear is susceptible but can be very deceitful, it can drive people to do things they\n\nhave no choice of doing, an example would be like this:\n\nmagine a man with the perfect life and perfect family, then a stranger says that all of it will be taken away in the blink of an eye if he does not kill someone. Unless his Will is strong, this\n\ncan and will murder someone for the sake of his family, and the emotion that is currently driving him is the power of fear... It is the easiest emotion to spot within yourself and another man, and too much fear can lead to insanity.\n\nThe Druid should\n\nnot to be seduced to the madness of fear. Everybody gets scared all the time, it is part of the nature of Life, but the dark side is that it can control you if you do not fight back. In order to overcome fear, you must have Confidence and Willpower; then\n\nhis darkness that lies within you shall disappear. But Fear can never die, it is like a disease that can never be cured and a fire that will never be put out, remember this, my friends, and do not give in to it...", ""),
        StaticBook("Along the Shore", "§bHamlin Frostbeard", "--===============--Along the Shore\n--===============--\n\nThe calm sea can be heard as the dwarf sits along the sand of the beach looking off to the boats in the distance the dwarf leans back upon the sand slowly his head lifts to see the sky of\n\npure beauty with clouds bearly to be seen allowing the sound of the crashing waves and birds making there noises as they make the dwarf know of there location.\n\nSuddenly voices can be heard as the dwarf of blue eyed in colour slowly brushes his\n\ncharcoal like hair placing his hand upon the hilt of his sword as the dwarf was in lands which his people were no longer aloud he moves his cloak to the side reviled a steel armed dwarf with a sky blue crystal within the middle of his belt he looks to the\n\nleft only the see rocks and sand with the slowly moving sea waving over it to the right are pointed ear beings sword drawn looking towards the dwarf slowly walking towards him shouting to him the dwarf would draw his sword a jagged blade with a ruby\n\nwithing his handle made of pure steel.\n\nThe pointed ear beings come closer and closer the closer they get the more the dwarfs sees of them all wearing fancy clothing of blues greens golds and whites the dwarf throws his cloak\n\nover shoulder before charging shouting to them in a deep dwarven accent smiling as he knows blood will be spilt this day but he very much doubts it will be his.\n\n\"Narvak Oz Azwyrtrumm\" \nThe final words of the dwarf", ""),
        StaticBook("Walker-Kalameet", "§bKharis", "A young male elf and a female stand along the road talking to each other. The man said \"Clever\" Continuing the conversation. She replied with \"It is me after all.\" He then said \"I see.. No interests at all?\" She said \"Mostly.\" The man then said \"I see...\"\n\n\"Sounds uninteresting\" The woman speaks \"I like it that way\" The man then says a bunch of stuff. The woman saying a bunch of things too. And lastly the man asks if he wants the woman for him to leave. The woman saying \"If it has a use of me then you can-\n\nTell me about it\" He says \"What are you capable of?\" She says \"Besides walking, You mean?\" He says \"Indeed.\" She says \"Writing and a bit of combat training is all I have of use.\" He says \"I see... Walker would you like a job?\" She then says \"I'm down dawg\n\nThe man then rudely says \"We do not shake hands ya shank\" She says \"Then what is customary for you?\" He Says \"Good.\" Then they both walk off with a job. The end\n\n-Conversation in Malinor, Kalameet and Walker.", ""),
        StaticBook("I Have a Dream", "§bTyrone Agashi", "I Have a Dream\n\n-Tyrone Agashi\n\n\"Faith is taking the first step even when you don't see the whole staircase.\"\n\nExperiences\n\nI sat in a puddle of my own excretment on a bench. \nMy hands raw with blisters, and the skin on my back ripped open from a whip.\nWithout proper food I knew I'd be gone within a Saints Week.\n\nWas I that expendable?\n\nWas I as easy to replace as a damaged tool?\n\nThe shackles around my ankles were heavy, and after thirty hours I'd been sat there to work, no sleep permitted.\n\nMy thoughts became random as as the delirium set in and I lost track of where I was and the consequences for misbehaviour. \nI stood up abruptly, and struck my fist at an overseer. He crumpled to the deck, and I stepped back bewildered and unsteady on my\n\nfeet. \n\nIn minutes the other overseers trudged over, and rained down blows on me, before gripping the scruff of my neck and dragging me down to the lowest deck.\n\nWere they to come to me as a friend, I would give them everything. My heart, my labour, my soul. \nInstead they tied me to a chair littered with thorns.\nThey beat with a stick that which I would have willingly surrendered with a loving heart.\n\nYou think it foolish to stand meek, but you are wrong, for it is we that inherit the earth.\n\nAs they each took turns burning me, cutting me, whipping me. I could only feel sorry for them.\n\nThey treated us no better than cattle or pigs. They'd encourage us to have children and then rip the family apart, selling the family members to different plantations across the isles of Axios.\n\nOnce I became independent, and had escaped from my overseers.\n\nI was awoken from a sleep by hoarse cackles, and yelling coming from outside. \nMy fingers became entwined in the woollen blanket, gripping it as if it were more\n\nthan a square of yarn. \nI built up the courage to scramble to my feet, and peered outside. \n\nA mob swarmed my home, torched in their hands and pitchforks.\n\nI watched as flames engulfed my cottage, scorching my skin and singeing the surrounding trees. \nWreathes of smoke filled my nostrils as I stumbled my way towards the door. \nI managed to swing open my door, only to be met with the crowd.\n\n\"Leave Darkskin! We don't want your kind here!!!\" One of them bellowed.\n\nMy feet slip outwards on the wet leaves as I round the corner, the cold evening air shocking my throat and lungs as I inhale deeper, faster.\n\nBehind me I could hear the baying howls of the dogs and jeering laughter of the mob. \n\nI eventually lost them, and found upon a town: Sutica, which is where I now reside.\nThe attitudes here are mixed, but far better than Johaneesburg.", ""),
        StaticBook("RiseofTruRectide", "§bHochmeister Gaius Marius", "The Rise\n           of\n     True Rectide\n\n   Transcribed by\n   Archmage Slayer\n\nAn Order, composed of the truest and most intelligent men and women, begin their rise. Steadily, the Order coldly calculates their every move, even resource they gather, every body they count. The Order remains engulfed in the cloak of secrecy,\n\nknowing in it's infancy, arrogant kingdoms and groups would happily kill the young with no remorse. The members remain secretive of their truest intentions for the Order, knowing the words passed along can alert the most corrupt of the Order's intentions.\n\nRumour has it that this Order has erected their first bastion, yet it is equally as shrouded in the veil of secrecy as this Order's intentions and members are. Travelers who do perhaps stumble upon this bulwark by chance will be awed at the extremities\n\nthis Bulwark was built upon and how the men whose masonry built the very walls survived in the climate. Travelling into the deeply encrusted lands of snow and ice of Northern Oren, the figure gasps in complete awe upon the awkwardly rigid form\n\nthat appears through the blinding wintry precipitation. A citadel with an aura of glad tidings beckons this figure to slowly step backwards to take into account the enormity of this formation. After the long pause of minutes, taking ever detail of the\n\ncitadel to memory, the figure stumbles and walks back; suffering from the awe inspiring features that he just witnessed. Upon returning from his original location, it is deemed that the Order will dispatch a member of eloquence to beckon a meeting with\n\nthose who inhabit this citadel in the North. The cries for amnesty, mercy, and beginnings of rest, food, and shelter ring within Gaius's ears as he limps throughout the battlefield. Despite his injuries and the limping as a result,\n\nGaius ensures his every step is carefully placed as he walks upon ground painted with blood and hosts the strewn bodies of humans, orcs, and elves. Witnessing and beholding the final siege upon the Keep of the Undead,\n\nGaius tempers the cold as he fights the demons now placed inside him, the sights and sounds of death blow knots inside his stomach and a constant torture upon his mind. Yet despite this torture of what he witnessed, yet another thing he witnessed brings\n\njoy to his heart, the truest victory he has ever tasted, the redemption of those hundreds of men, women, and children that were slain by the devils themselves. Upon the success of the latest siege, Gaius heads back to the Order, smiling\n\nalmost maniacally at the news that is on his tongue and wishing release as glad tidings. Upon returning to his Sariant Monks, Gaius reveals the heralded news and the men let out a cheer of triumph. As the chill of night sets, Gaius reveals a warning to\n\nhis men and an urge that the Order must progress much faster to answer any future threats. this certainly cannot be the last trick up the sleeve of Iblees so to speak. The bustling of a newborn village keeps Gaius's senses alive and hearkens all that\n\ngoes on around him. His title, Hochmeister, gives him complete control over Nuremburg and with it, the tiresome responsibilities. Despite the stress, he knows this village will thrive and grow and the military will alongside it.\n\nHe gives greetings to two of his fellow knights passing along the freshly hewn stone path, already giving the path a beating of dust and dirt from their armoured bodies as they approach the Fort of Nuremburg to gather needed materials.\n\nHochmeister Gaius is impressed with the progress, especially increasing due to the destruction of the Undead Keep, giving relief to the tested nerves of the Teutonic Knights so far. Gaius knows now that his Order have released themselves\n\nfrom the thick fogs of the mountainous forests, he must pay even more crucial attention and thought to the progress from here on out. Just as was spoken of days before, the calculated possibility of a reemergence has proven true.\n\nLightning stands contrast on the horizon compared to the ink black night skies, the Knights pick up their pace along the stone paths to their homes to gather supplies. The Hochmeister marches his OrdenMarschalls Alizyn and Lunar throughout Nuremburg\n\nto answer to the heralds causing commotion within the town. Word brought of a figure sprawling out from a cavern, wretched in sight and sound as it ran swiftly throughout the woodlands. The heralds told of how the creature spoke of the Undead,\n\nof Iblees mocking the destruction of his Keep in the North and how he will rise swiftly back to higher station. Gaius sighs heavily and knows the time is closing, he must secure his position and empower the military structure of the Teutons\n\nand ensure that they can readily respond to any encroaching threat. With the events that have happened recently, it has become increasingly imperative that the Order begin to recruit the most honest and hard-working individuals of Oren\n\nd the other regions alike. The expansion of the town has gone very well, with newly linked roads being used in modest manner and new homes being constructed of the finest yew, stone, and fabricated with craftsman quality.\n\nAdornment of the streets with the wildflowers of the area and the roses of the thickest thorn crown have given the town a much more livelier atmosphere. The townspeople have shown gratitude to the Hochmeister for his wise civil initiatives\n\nin the town and many civil works have been planned for the town. The Hochmeister has sent a few of his Knights to act as messengers, to recruit from the lands the most intelligent and hardened men to act as Monks and fellow Sariants of the Order.\n\nWith the influx of Sariant Knights to the town of Nuremburg, the terraced hills expand from the origin; the Fortress of Nuremburg. Rolling hills now flattened, sprawling streets and homes of various sizes and heights s[ring upon the freshly dug\n\nplanes of land. Hochmeister Gaius issues his best agents to pursue espionage missions in the North, eager to start his next phase for military preparedness. Gaius knows that the first moves of the Order in the military aspect will be crucial to the\n\nsuccess of campaigns that the Order may pursue. Rumors that the strongest servants of Iblees may have fallen back onto guerilla tactics and inhabiting Snowy Fields secretly has given Gaius a start for his spies to start searching for any organization\n\namongst the Undead. Trusting his agents well, he sends them off with morale raising words as he turns his masonry skills to the next task, a barracks fit for training Knights of the Teutonic Order. Gaius stammers in utter amazement as a man appears before\n\nhis eyes, greeting this mysterious man, he is responded with the gift of calling this man The Wandering Wizard. Gaius gives this Wandering Wizard a tour of the town of Nuremburg, at the end, the Wandering Wizard exclaims extraordinary wishs\n\nof great success for the town, somehow brightening the day of Gaius's, weathered down by the past hours of hard labour and sweat inducing activities.\n\nThe grunts and shouts are Sariants ring along the cold stone walls of the Duel Arena in Nuremburg, accompanied by the stretching sounds of arrows being nocked into place and the whirl of missiles plastering across various bullseye targets.\n\nThe Brethren have made great strides to train for military campaigns, hopefully the training will finally pay off. Gaius enters a rustic tavern, noticing the cabaret entertaining the folks sitting upon wooden stools and along tables filled with food\n\nand drink. Scanning the faces are merriment and intrigue, Gaius finally finds who he is looking for and approaches in a nonchalant fashion. Reaching the tavernkeeper, Gaius and the tavernkeeper sit amongs the more populated side of the room,\n\nentranced by the musicians seducing their drunken minds with instrumental jubilee. Leaning into their own conversation, Gaius and the tavernkeeper trade many a word before heading their separate ways.\n\nGaius shifts a parchment scroll from his left to right hand and back again, eyeing the contents contained little by little. Gaius walks carefully throughout the crowds gathered in the main square of AlKhazar and walks out the main gate\n\nto meet a few of his Sariants gathered on the King's Road. Sliding his hands against the grime riddled walls of the dimly lit sewers, Gaius steps ever so carefully through the briny liquids of waste and decay as he navigates the sewers.\n\nUpon reaching his destination, he wipes his hands upon the mail skirt to rid them of any residue and commences grappling onto a ladder and pushing himself up step by step. With the lift of the trapdoor, he peers around the edge of the opening and hoists\n\nhimself up and out from the hole and crouches to belittle his figure in the city. Skipping along the paths intertwining within the city, Gaius climbs and moves amongst rooftops and picks a spot that gives him clarified view of a hooded man sitting in a\n\nshop, his hand gestures tell that he is awaiting a guest. Gaius whispers, 'Black Hand' and furrows his eyes to notice any other details in the shop that he is missing. As both men's breathe began to synchronize with each movement closer,\n\nGaius tilts with his last step and leaps at the man he was trailing within the forests of Oren. Gaius's dagger thrusts into the figure, quick and serene is the process, but even quicker is the process to gather the limp body and orchestrate\n\nits defiling within a nearby cesspool. The lagoon blossoms and blooms with velvety red as the body begins to float ever so slightly along the surface of the water, Gaius sifts through the man's pockets for any parchment or maps, then looks around\n\nand starts to dart amongst the oak. The rustling of forest decay cloak the conversations amongst the group of men traversing the Tundras of the North. Hochmeister Gaius and his Teutons, making up the left column of the army peer silently across the\n\nlandscape, now billowy white in soft snow in search of any lingering spies. Accompanied by the House of conDoin, Cataris and his nobles make up the right column and then citizens of Kramaroe filled in between.\n\nIt was only hours before when Kramaroe was razed by what was perhaps an attack by the Black Hand, Gaius and Cataris answered the pleas of the residents misplaced by the disaster and mustered their men to the ready and marched forth from AlKhazar.\n\nWeary of any stragglers, Gaius and Cataris move through the woodlands to spot any possible heathens wishing to take count of the impending force moving through. Gaius, with information gathered from his tavernkeeper, speaks of a tower made of stone\n\nand obsidian, but then stares in stark surprise as the tower seemingly appears from within the fog as they move steadily forward. Ordering his men to spread looser and to find hiding places, he moves forward with Cataris and hear a faint whimper.\n\nUpon closer examination, a woman lies upon a dirt mound near a destroyed home, with a creature of sorts crouched across her. Gaius and Cataris unsheathe their swords as quietly as possible, but the creature peers at the two approaching men and sneers,\n\nflesh dribbling from its mouth and flashes its blood caked teeth at them. Drawn back, the two stare in horror as the woman chuckles and sighs hysterically and beckons them with greetings, the creature lifts itself up and presents itself in a more humanlik\n\n form, a necromancer it calls itself. Gaius and Cataris glance at each other then call their men forward, the necromancer skips backwards from the mutilated woman and shrieks threats of death and despair. Upon hearing a rush of yells\n\nand crunched leaves, Gaius turns about and attempts to yank a man by his linen shirt, but misses as the men of Kramaroe rush forward and scream curses and wishes to relinquish their revenge upon this necromancer.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Under Ways", "§bKazrin Starbreaker", "11th of Sun's Smile, The retaking of the Tal'Nerroth The Deep Hold.  In Karak Azgaryum, an expedition was held to retake lost dwarven halls of Kal'Nerroth. Earthquakes struck the lower halls of Karak Azgaryum, an attack then came from the Ratikki other\n\nwise known as the ratmen. The first we heard was the chittering and chattering within the stone walls. The crawls of filthy paws on stone floor echoed through the halls. Then the Ratmen bursted out of the dark, the dwarfs matched their overwhelming number\n\nwith quality armor and weaponry. The dwarfs pushed them back into the lower halls once more. As the Ratmen retreated the dwarfs followed them to a much larger hall held by large stone pillars. The hall outstretched towards the back of the mountain opening\n\nto more rooms and temples. However it was blocked by walls haunted chains around it making siege to it impossible and a close to a horrible fate. Seein this the dwarfs investigated the rooms opened up on by the earthquakes. The dwarfs then investigated\n\nforge. Until the lava rose and transformed into the shape of a dwarf. The dwarf called himself an ancestor of the deep dwarfs another subrace. With his help the dwarfs broke the chains, but beyond the wall we awoke a monster of lava hiding in the shadows.\n\nIt roared like a lion and broke the wall, lava spewing through the cracks until the whole wall melted and burned. The dwarfs unable to fight lava, hid into the temple, the holy water shielding the entrance from the attacks of the elemental. With the\n\ndwarfs held up and trapped inside the temple, took out a book they found in the temple and cite the ancient chants of the deep dwarfs. Afterwards the dwarfs were saved by the dwarf ancestor who turned himself into a water elemental killing the lava\n\nmonster.  The dwarfs pushed forward making there way into the old tavern. I myself saw the dwarf skeletons scattered along the grounds, a trail of old echoes of the past that lead to a single room at the end of the hall. This hall would end up being a\n\ncouncil chamber. A single ghostly king would hover above the table. We each took a seat at the council table, the king would later name himself as King Kurgan Ironbeard the last king of Kal'Nerroth. Sadly it was only a reenactment, the fallen king\n\nlooked upon each of us as if we were his trusted friends from before. It was later learned that Kurgan was trapped in a time lock forever to act the same event over and over till the dwarfs once more came to reclaim these holds. I myself was called the\n\nforgemaster and the king himself asked for my advice, i told him to fight to the end...a path i fear the dwarfs of these mountains did... None the less King Kurgan grabbed from the void a shining green gem, giving it to Gimli our expedition leader. It\n\nwasnt an apparition and turned out to be real. I told them to keep it safe, I then called it a dwarven artifact known as The loss Gem of Kurgan Ironbeard. And with that the expediton ended which leads me to writing this very book.\n\nTake heed in this account of this tale, and remember the loss hold of Kal'Nerroth and the people that lived there. [!] At the bottom would be stamped the emblem of the remembrancers a brown owl with a book.", ""),
        StaticBook("Latsi's Journal", "§bLatsi", "Latsi's Journal\n\nForeword: This is the journal of the (in)famous Undead, chronicling his fall to that terrible scourge that beset the Descendants in Aegis.\n\nEntry 1\n\nToday, I became an ascended. The life is great, except we are not supposed to leave Haven, it depresses me. I made my house finally! I think it looks great. Today I thought about why we have those big boats, with no crew.\n\nI also have been trying to find secrets in the city! I have only found one so far. Becoming unamused in Haven; not much to do anymore. I went against the Sage's word today, and left Haven. Many weeks have passed and I never returned to Haven...\n\nand I don't plan on going back now.\n\nEntry 2\n\nI have been enjoying life outside of Haven, and decided to write my journals with more prestige. The last one was fairly crummy, and childish almost.\n\nToday, I was in the Isles when a man in chainmail armour approached me. He asked me to follow him, which I did. We went into a treehouse near the Isles, where, he asked me a few questions. My Life changed forever.\n\nEntry 3\n\nI have been working on completing my trials. The first one went well . I just had to simply kill someone. I killed my old best friend, John. The second trial went better than planned. I had to tempt someone to evil.\n\nI chose my brother's son. It felt great, and I began to be what Kaizo wanted me to be, to him. The third trial went much better than planned. I had been plotting to sacrifice Atriana of the Oren Guard. Instead, I sacrificed King Edmund and Ivrae.\n\nThe fourth trial was hard, I almost failed it. It was a large series of tests, but I will not get into it.\n\nEntry 4\n\nToday... is the day of the ceremony. I am not sure if I am ready yet. I am doing this . so I can kill that Sage though. The Sage that killed Bell. I am leaving to go to the ceremony now.\n\nI am no longer myself. I am a new being. This power running through me is immense. I cannot wait to make that Sage suffer. The joy it will bring me is endless. I am never giving up this power, it is beyond belief. The only tie I had to this world was Bell\n\nand now she is gone. So what I do doesn't matter anymore.\n\nEntry 5\n\nWe killed many today. Many of those smelly, greenskins. I have no memory of it, but I was told of it by one of the others. I have been sitting in the Nether, listening to Ghasts scream.\n\nThis is my life, and I am not sure if it is what I thought it would be. I have never come close to the opportunity of killing that Sage, and my life seems pointless. I am going to stop writing for a while.\n\nEntry 6\n\nAegis hates me. I cannot bear to live in this world any longer. There is nothing for me.\n\nEntry 7\n\nI found something to keep me going, for now. Guraim told me that Lotheriel is Bell's daughter... this could help change me. I confronted her, and she would not believe me.\n\nWe talked about much... and my thoughts of killing that Sage have changed. I wish this to end my suffering... but how?\n\nEntry 8\n\nThis may be my final Journal. I am going to ask Lotheriel if she knows what I can do. I must confront the Sage, Arcadius. He may be able to end me... and take me out of this world.\n\nI am heading off to the FOA base... with no return. Goodbye Aegis . and in my last wish, give my belongings to . *a paint spill blocks out the bottom right side of the book, possibly with more text underneath it.", ""),
        StaticBook("Kaiser Quotes", "§bKaiser Decimus Rovin, Vandalore", "===Heil Valdoria===\n\nExcerpts from the speech made by the glorious Kaisereich Decimus Rovin.\n\n\"...racial species must preserve the purity of the blood which Gott has given it!\"\n\n  ====Page One====\n\n  ===Heil Valdoria===\n\n\"It is not for men to discuss the question of why Providence created different races, but rather to recognize the fact that it punishes those who disregard its work of creation.\"\n\n  ====Page Two====\n\n  ===Heil Valdoria===\n\n\"...revolutionary change in our knowledge and therewith a radical reconstruction of the picture which human history gives us of the past and will also change the course of that history in the future.\"\n   ===Page Three==\n\n\n\n\n     And remember, \n       If you see a glorious member of the Kaisereich, yell\n\n   \"HEIL VALDORIA\"\n   \"HEIL THE KAISER\"\n   \"HEIL DECIMUS\"\n\n ===Approved By===\n\nThe Reich Ministry of Public Enlightenment and Propoganda.\n\n-Goseph Joebbelstein.", ""),
        StaticBook("Title, Poem.", "ScarletBlood", "I didn't really know, what to write.\n\nThis really isn't... my strongest point and I might.\n\nJust give up and drop the quill.\nBecause I have lost, all my bloody\nwill\nTo write this bloody pednik poem.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tablet Riddles", "§bCheza", "\"The Breaking\" \n\nNow broken, once whole. 7 knots in a rope.\nThe children of sea, betrayed by their hope.\nUnfinished promises, an entente unbound,\nas both of our tribes, lay sleeping underground.\n\nA prophet, the ocean, master of none,\nMaster of nothing, fatherless son.\nFather of nothing but what has been done,\na rope now broken, leaving its sons.\n\n\"Grieving of brothers.\"\n\nMan of him does not trick us like them\nman of him will not slay us instead.\nFor men of stone fall not for his act.\nFor men of stone still remember our pact.\n\nWe care now for seven, sons of the ocean.\nBut even now, we lose all motion.\nTired we slumber beneath the dirt.\nAs we return to dwell in our mother's hearth.\n\n\"Tales of the fall\"\n\nLet it be known, the danger of words.\nDanger of silence, danger of herds.\nDangers of mouthless phrases unheard.\nDanger of trickers and mission spurred.\n\nRest now, for tricksters do trap us alive,\ntrap us for power, trap us and bind,\ntrap us in guilt, worry hindsight,\ntrap us in questions of why we were blind.\n\n\"A price paid\"\n\nPeople yearn for gold and silver,\ncoins of copper, bars and silver.\nSilvers of soul, shards of dust,\ncurrency of monsters, beings above.\n\nCurrency they pay, brothers in debt,\nto the trickster of faith as he marks them for death.\nMark them for harvest, a farmer that sows,\nReaping of lives come a second toll.", ""),
        StaticBook("Bloody Poetry", "§bAlan Marlsbush", "Eldre-home\n\nHoilelio goiu holias\n\nAna viev \n\nDel Dorini ec Eldre Enshu\n\nHoilelio\nBe hoilelios hoilas\"\n\nritiou\n\n Petals pooled in crimson red.\nLife flowing out and leaving him dead.\nSo came the book man,\nwith no ill intent.\nTo the noble city full of discontent.\nHe meant no trouble and caused no strife,\nbut the city's guards\nchose to end\n\n Empty it lies, \nAsleep in the cold,\nJust another lost city, with a tale to be told.\nWith high towers and statues so great,\nYet silent it stands,\nForever open it's gate. ", ""),
        StaticBook("Guide To", "§bKazrin Starbreaker", "Diplomacy\nThe art of Diplomacy is a craft that is honed by years of practice. A wordsmith with the right set of words can raise entire kingdoms to the ground, inspire troops or bring fear to the most brave of men. Likewise wordsmithing is not an easy task\n\nbut with the right guidance, one can learn to be an exceptional diplomat. The first lessons in any diplomatic missions is to know who your dealing, what makes them tick, what are they known for? Are they shrewd and cunning, or a warrior who cares nothing\n\nmore than to be done with it. The reasoning behind this is quite simple, to know who your dealing with gives you an edge over how to deal with someone. To appeal to their ego or character and get things done your way. The secong lesson one can learn is\n\nan important one which to compromise. The first step to fixing a problem is recognizing there is one, to learn what the problem is and the very roots of how the problem came to be is a good step in the right direction, but if both parties are not willing\n\ncompromise then there can never be true peace in times of war, or a deal being struck within your terms. Often or not another lesson one must learn is who to bring along, never bring those you know that are emotionally compromised into the talks, it will\n\nresult in less of a civilized talk but more of a angry debate fueled by rage and emotion, who you bring and who they bring is also a clear sign of what the enemy, or person thinks of you. With that being said there are times when diplomacy fails which is\n\ninevitable so do not hesitate to bring a guardforce with you. Another quick note is to be humble not proud, to not fall easily to traps or insults this shows to all that you arent so easily overtaken. Another lesson one should learn is through failure\n\nFailure is the greatest teacher there is, and experience is the greatest confidence builder we have. Do not be angered or distraught when you fail, many great diplomats are forged through failure and suffering only then do people truly shine as\n\ndiplomats. To go to war is foolish when there are alternatives, do not be swayed by pride or stubborness but be reasonable, recognize the faults on both sides, no side in war is ever perfect, we arent gods we are mortals. Hear the other persons story what\n\ndo they have to say? why do they think this? Questions like these is what helps usher in peace during times of war. But what if diplomacy fails, then it fails, remember that you did all you can provided you listen to these lessons and rules, sometimes\n\npeople must experience horror or foolishness before they are willing to compromise, which is perfectly fine. Which leads to the last lesson although you may have been right or you have the upperhand or maybe you won the war, do not rub it in there face,\n\nyou are merely prvoking bitterness and resentment, so keep a level head, and like the previous lessons, do not fall into pride and arrogance, many would be suprised how often those two can turn the most noble of men into the most scummy.\n\nAnd so those are the lessons I Kazrin Starbreaker, High remembrancer, and ambassador of Kaz'Ulrah to the elves say to those who read this book. Follow these lessons and the odds shall be more even.\n\n*The sigil of the remembrancers would be seen on this page, It would appear as a brown owl, watching over a mountain valley\"", ""),
        StaticBook("Magic Dictionary", "PiercingDarkness", "The Magic Dictonary:\n\nYir'sari - True Wizard, powerful magic masters.\n\nAscended - The demi-god children of the aenguls.\n\nUndead - The evil fists of Iblees, they destroyed Aegis.\n\nArcane Transportation Pad - \n\nStaff - a tool used to conduct mana, as well as aid you in Void connections.\n\nWand - Akin to the staff, doesn't work as well.\n\nCleric - Powerful magicians based mostly in healing, they are fueled by aenguls.\n\nNecromancer - Users of Necromany, a deadly magic having to do with life drain.\n\nPyromancer - Fire evocationist, magician of fire.\n\nElectromancer - Users of electric magic, mostly evocationist of electricity, they are common in Anthos.\n\nEvocation - The use of summong elements from the Void.\n\nFire-Evocation - The summoning of mana from the Void to create fire.\n\nWater-Evocation - The summoning of mana from the Void to create water or other water related things.\n\nElectric-Evocation - The evoking of mana from the Void to form electricity.\n\nWind-Evocation - The use of void mana to create wind and it's similiar elements.\n\nEarth-Evocation - The evocation of mana to form earthen elements.\n\nShamanism - Magic having to do with the use of spirits.\n\nElemental control - A shaman magic having to do with spirits.\n\nMagic(k) - The use of mana to conjure things, and even to control things.\n\nMana - Life force and energies around us, used to form complex spells.\n\nNecromancy - The use of life drain to get mana to form complex\n\nspells.\n\nShade-Magic - Fueled by a gem, it's a shadow magic having to do with the art of tendrils, and other shadow elements.\n\nIllusion - A arcane magic, the use of mana to form false images and feelings, and project them upon others, it's impossible to illusion yourself.\n\nConjuration - The conjuring of living beings.\n\nWizard - Common term name for the Yir'sari, true wizards.\n\nArch-Mage - Ruler of the mage's guild.\n\nMage - Practicer of magic.\n\nMagician - Mage is it shortened.\n\nAscended Magic - Magic fueled by a patron aenguel, it is a light magic, and holy, it is akin to cleric.\n\nUndead-Magic - Fueled by Iblees, the Undead used their necromancy to begin their conquest of Aegis.\n\nThe Void - A place where mages draw power from to fuel their spells.\n\nDragon - A beast of huge size and intelligence, they roam Northern Anthos, hunting.\n\nYellow Stone Material ((Endstone))\n\nA heavily weird material, it spreads corruption of many kinds.\n\nDruidism - Magic over nature, has to do with the spirits known as the Aspects.\n\nAlteration - Magic that alters the properties, of real world things.\n\n-------------------\n\nMagic sayings:\n\n\"Magic seeks those who don't seek it.\"\n\n\"Magic is the path of ths scholar, not a insolent warrior of heavy brains and no mindset.\" \n\n\"Magic is the path of destruction, insolent mage!\" - Gavin the Druid\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n\"Good and evil doesn't decide how magic works, only the acts of the user.\"\n\n- The Arcane Mage\n\n\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nWritten by, Mythras Ardere.\n\nSources:\n\n- history of magic\n- The Clerical Order\n- The Mage's Guild\n- Salamandra's spirit\n- Many assorted books on magic, and knowledge from other mages.", ""),
        StaticBook("Arbor", "§bAvalon Silversteed", "Arbor Agreement\n\n\n\nKingdom of Kaz'Ulrah\n\n\n\nKingdom of Arbor\n\nTerms\n\n-The Kingdom of Arbor will swear fealty to the Kingdom of Kaz'Ulrah.\n\n-The Kingdom of Kaz'Ulrah will protect the Kingdom of Arbor.\n\n-The Kingdom of Arbor's citizens are affored all rights as Kaz'Ulrah citizens.\n\n-The banner of Kaz'Ulrah will be flown on all territories held by Arbor.\n\nSignatories:\n\n~ High King Verthaik II Frostbeard\n\n~ King Avalon Silversteed of Arbor", ""),
        StaticBook("Last Words", "§bCristen Irl", "To the person reading this,\n\nIf you are reading this, then it means I am no longer with you. Take this book to Dawn Irl, in Sutica.\n\nDawn,\n\nUnder the bar is a chest. Take this key and unlock it. I am sorry I couldn't stay longer.\n\n[!] A key is pinned to the pages of the book", ""),
        StaticBook("dont read it yet", "§bDutch", "i am pissed off, maybe not coming back im not sure. ill see ye\n\n\"I will swim the river of truth, wherever it takes me.\"§0\n§0The truth is much like a river; it flows in one direction, and then another, fluid like water. This truth must be sought out, and followed, no matter what occurs.\n\n\"As the trees watch over us, I will watch over others in need\"§0\n§0The trees are the bulwark of the forest, of nature. The trees watch over the drui, in exchange the trees wish for us to watch over the ones they cannot watch over.\n\n\"I will seek to preserve the balance, even as dusk approaches\"§0\n§0The balance is like a counter-weight. This balance can be disrupted, it must be protected. Protection of the balance must be maintained, no matter what the situation is.\n\n\"I hereby vow to uphold my duties as a Dedicant of the Druidic Order.\"§0\n§0The duties of a dedicant are sealed with a vow. This is to ensure they remain on the correct path as a dedicant.", ""),
        StaticBook("Tomb Secrets", "§bLemik Rextiureus", "{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nPrologue\n\nThe veil fizzled out and Seisi became visible just as the last of the dark priests about to leave. \n\nAss Dung. Seisi thought, Seisi turned and ran towards the River. He sensed a disturbance behind him and threw himself to\n\nthe ground. A bile green torrent of light shot over his head, thundered into a palm grove, disintegrating the trees into powder.\n\nThat had been a Tail of Sobek, one of the forbidden spells. A spell, that also required divine energy, which meant... Seisi\n\nshot up from where he was lying and zig-zagged thorugh the reeds. He heard whomping sounds and his inner eye beheled green coulds behind him. His pursuer was getting closer. \n\nSomething silvery screeched past his nose, burying itself into another palm\n\ntree.\n\nA Dagger of Khons! One of the other dark priests has returned. Seisi focussed on his sun-flow, ripped an amulet from his collar, rasped an invocation to Hapy from his burning lungs and races across the spongy surface of the river.\n\n\"Have to reach the other side...\" He thought to himself\n\nHe sensed movement on the bank, twisted-an invisible fist slammed nto his back, the spell broke and he plunged into the river. \nNot again! Seisi thought as he sank through the murky green depths of\n\nHapy's domain. His consciousness waas fading fast, yet he knew he ould awaken again. But then it would be too late to pass on what he had learned. Too late for Metjen, too late for his love-and too late to protect the people of Caliphate from annihilation", ""),
        StaticBook("Royalty & Ruled", "§bTyus Ropano", "Royalty and the Ruled\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nBy: Tyus Ropano\n\nSociety can be divided into two groups. Those with power, and those without it. Among these two main groups are countless people. Each wishing to obtain the power of those greater than them. At the top lie the rulers- the people which make the laws. Their\n\npower is near absolute. With this power comes many responsibilities.\n\n1. Those with power must be the 'Guardians of the Poor'\n\nIt is the duty of those with power to give aid to those who don't. It is the kingdom's\n\njob to protect those it shelters. Because, what is a king without the people they rule? Where does the wealth that maintains the king's and the kingdom's power come from?\n\nFrom the people. It is the people who endow the rulers with power without them,\n\na kingdom cannot function. So in order to preserve this system, kings must resolve themselves to protecting their subjects. \n\n2. Seeking Power\n\nThere are two groups, those with power, and those without, but these groups can be\n\nfurther divided into those that are content and those that seek power. Often times it is the powerful which hold a greater desire to seek more power, because there will always be something which seeks greater power, and no ruler ever wants their control\n\ncontested. \n\nBut by seeking greater power, one's heart is open to corruption. The path to power is one laden with obstacles, each one is determined to drive one further into the pursuit of power, and with this growing obsession comes many problems.\n\nFirst of all, one can lose sight of everything important to them. The path to power narrows one vision. He will often times only see what can make him stronger. This blinds him to his surroundings, he becomes ignorant of what occurs around him. Things...\n\nlike family begin to lose their importance.\n\nSecondly, power changes one. The most kind and just rulers can be corrupted into tyrants. This pursuit of power changes how they percieve things. Those that were originally family and friends only wishing\n\nto help transform into seekers of power. Those that wish to build become those that only seek to destroy. The pursuit of power blinds one to the truth.\n\n3. The Content\n\nThe content are seen as the weak. Those that do not wish\n\nto gain more power will inherently fall under the dominion of those that still seek it. But the content, arguably are stronger. Because they lack the desire to gain more power. They lack a form of insecurity seen in the people who continously seek out po-\n\n-wer. \n\n4. The Purest Power\n\nPower exists in two types- the one that corrupts, and the one that strengthens. The power that corrupts is gained through self-gain. It is done only for the sake of oneself, most time it is done for dubious\n\nactions. Things like greed, power, and envy are all lead to this type. \n\nBut the power that strengthens, that heals, is created a differently. It is created through things like justice, friendship, and love. It is created through\n\nthings that give a reason for protection. This power is inherently good and pure, and does not corrupt, it can only heal. Power gained through friendship, love, and justice not only empower the seeker, but everyone the seeker aims to protect. In this way\n\nthe power is spread out for all to recieve. This is the power that the kings must seek. The power to protect, not control. If you protect the citizens, they will follow you to the ends of the world. They will gladly give their life to protect the home th-\n\n-ey live in. The power to control will always lead to a revolution, it may take 10 years, 100 years, or even 1000 years, but it will happen. The only solution, the only way to prevent it is to seek the power to protect. Because by seeking this sort of po-\n\n-wer, one's soul is influenced, but instead of it being influenced with things like greed and pride, it is endowed with the qualitites like just, holy, and love. Through these qualities, the best rulers are created. \nThrough the best rulers, the\n\nbest kingdoms are created. Through the best kingdoms, the best world is created. And through the best world, the best lives are allowed to flourish.", ""),
        StaticBook("Adunian Poems", "§bHamish", "Open your eyes and watch the sky,\nto see the blue and the white,\nand view the stars that roam up above\nand watch the birds in flight.\nTo see the seasons change with time\nand the people grow and age,\n\nto see the kindness in their hearts\nand their dark eyes that hold their rage.\nOpen your eyes to notice the difference\nbetween the rumours and praise,\nfrom the people who honestly care\nto those that could not be more blasé.\n\nTo notice the change from black to grey\nfrom purple to blue, orange to red,\nand see green turn to yellow,\nthe rich comforted and the hungry get fed.\nOpen your eyes to watch the pain\nthat others hide from the rest.\n\nThey might be the man on the street\nor the masquerade, best dressed. \nNotice the seasons wash the air new\nto make room for their colours, \nand make the people change their clothes\nas well as watch out for others.\n\nOpen your eyes to their lives going by,\nto their hopes flickering and fading,\nthe things they want most leaving\nand their dreams gone from trading.\nWatch out for a puddle of tears\nnear a gravestone of the loved,\n\nand see those who longed to be touched\nas they keep their fingers gloved.\nOpen your eyes to see the compassion\nthat seems to flow in this realm,\nfrom the caring and the kindness\nto the comfort that can overwhelm.\n\nBut also take note of the depression\nthat sits at the bottoms of the lakes, \nthat rots on the tree branches\nand in the corners of the crates.\nOpen your eyes to see what I see, \nthe final realisation;\n\nthat with every new begining\ncomes yet another civilisation.\nBut just rest and take it all in,\nwith your eyes wide open\nand see this shattered realm like me,\nwith my heart completely broken.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nShattered,\nThe fact that I am broken,\nBroken,\nEven with what I said;\nTattered, \nMy heart is thankful for use,\nSmashed,\nEven though all out my heart bled.\nHalting,\n\nMy world, but seems to keep spinning,\nCrushed,\nAs my mind searches for support;\nImperfect, \nHe is gone forever as they said,\nUneven, \nAnd I did not have the energy to retort.\nDisturbed,\n\nThey told me, when I asked what happened,\nSnapped,\nThey said, when he fell with my heart,\nDefeated,\nHe was, as he was carried outside,\nCracked,\nThey described he was not that smart.\n\nStopped, \nas I cannot hear it anymore,\nDestoryed,\nmy heart to the very core,\nAltered, \nas I think its beat has changed,\nDefective,\n\nand it has made me beyond poor. \nIs,\nwhat a time that this has been,\nWhat,\nI have been through is too much,\nI,\nonly wanted to see him again,\nFeel,\n\nhis heart and his touch.\nMy,\nThree, dear Three, bless him,\nElton,\nfor he was my net under the ledge,\nIs,\nhe really, truly with you now?\n\nDead,\nand gone, straight over the edge?\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nHis green eyes never leave my gaze\nand his beard will always be brown,\nhis kilt never lost its colour\nas he kept not a trace of a frown.\nHis high stature has yet to be forgotten\nwhat with his boom laughter and grin,\n\nand his highspirits not only with his family\nbut also in the tavern with his gin.\nHis comforting words kept me going\nas his form took shape in my mind,\nfor it was I who kepts his memories,\nit was I that he never left behind.\n\nI cannot say I enjoyed all of it\nfor that man saw too many wars,\nbut he also had his moments of triumph,\nand those he loved dearly of course.\nHe kept his mind straight and level\neven under the most pressure,\n\nhe always knew where his place was\nand respected those who were lesser.\nSometimes he forgot right from wrong,\nbut then again, we all to at some point,\nand yet he knew how to keep people motivatied\neven though he was hard to dissapoint.\n\nAnd though I miss him still to this day,\nwith years gone since he passed,\nI still wish Hanrahan was here with me,\nbut for now his memories will stay glassed.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nI tried to paint you with the finest paints,\nto bring your green eyes and brown hair,\nbut the picture simply slipped from my mind,\nand on the canvas you were not there.\nI had the colours perfectly mixed,\nmy brush poised and ready,\n\nbut when it came to shaping your face,\nI could not keep my hand steady.\nI ended up painting a landscape;\nit was one that I knew all too well,\nit had trees in the back and buildings around,\nbut little did I know that I fell.\n\nI watched my hand with curiosity,\nnot knowing what it was doing, \nand suddenly I forgot where I was,\nand even the tea I had brewing.\nI forgot my life and all my memories,\nI forgot who I had lost,\n\nI only knew about the place at hand,\nand I could not see the lines I crossed.\nI backed into my own painting\nof the trees and of the buildings,\nand backed right into the old Clinic of ours\nand I found the stash of old kindlings.\n\nI relit the fire just behind the counter,\nand leaned on it as I looked towards the door,\nI had washed the floors and that silver bell,\nand waited for your arrival once more.\nAs I stood in the Clinic of Memories\n\nI seemed to trick myself,\nbut at the time I could not see you\nas I restocked the shelf.\nYou walked in quietly as you always did,\nand I hung my coat on a hook.\nBut I could tell that I was not alone\n\nas you stood in that corner and looked.\nI turned around to see your expression,\nthose green eyes sunked into your face,\nand when you told me simple words that calmed me,\nthey helped me find my place.\nYou stepped closer and hugged me,\n\nyour words were soft and kind,\n\"You will be all right, I promise,\" you whispered,\nand suddenly it was I who was hard to find.\n\"Can't I just go back to the Clinic?\"\nI almost cried as you came near,\n\n\"Yes, anything you want, I promise,\nbut for now, Arial, you must stay here.\"\nSomething happened just then, \t\nwhen you promised I would be okay.\nI knew that the person I was then\nwould not be the person I am today.\n\nFor now I know that Arial\nwas the one who you wanted to protect,\nso she took her things and kept them safe,\nleast she be the one I forget.\nAnd now your dreams can come true,\nfor your daughter now walks these lands,\n\nand I can assure that Arial will be all right, \nbecause she is in your own hands.\nShe may call herself Annabelle,\nbut that is only for your sake,\nbecause she knows your daughter is in her\nand her soul was always yours to take.\n\nBut I did lose myself in the Clinic that day,\neven though it was just a painting.\nAnd even though it was all in my mind,\nI know it was real and Arial is still waiting.\nShe will wait for you until the end of time,\nuntil the brush is steady,\n\nuntil your face can be painted again\nand until you think she is ready.\n\n{\"text\":\"\"}\n\nPostscript.\n\nA collection of poems\nwritten by a famous Adunian poet in the late Anthosian period.\n\nLet her memory be charished by all those who read her delightful words.\n\n-Hanrahan Brae", ""),
        StaticBook("Communism", "§bgoghoun frostbeard", "The “Manifesto of the Communist Party” was written by Marx and Engels as the Communist\nLeague’s programme on the instruction of its Second Congress (London, November 29-December 8,\n\n1847), which signified a victory for the followers of a new proletarian line during the discussion of the\nprogramme questions. When Congress was still in preparation, Marx and Engels arrived at the conclusion that the final\n\nprogramme document should be in the form of a Party manifesto (see Engels’ letter to Marx of\n\nNovember 23-24, 1847). The catechism form usual for the secret societies of the time and retained in\n\nthe “Draft of a Communist Confession of Faith” and “Principles of Communism,” was not suitable for\n\na full and substantial exposition of the new revolutionary world outlook, for a comprehensive\n\nformulation of the proletarian movement’s aims and tasks. See also “Demands of the Communist Party in Germany", ""),
        StaticBook("Ho", "§bSammy \"Mungo\"", "How to be a Silvertongued Devil- By Mungo the Bandit.\n\nIn life you may come upon times where reaching for your sword may not be the most ideal way to go, you may not be the best fighter, or you simply can't speak for your life, hopefully, this guide of\n\nsorts may assist you in swindling, lying, persuading and overall being a great talker. Now, me being me, I was born with the natural talent of making people absolutely adore me, whether this was being brought up in a tevern or my mother being\n\nquite a social escort, I cannot say, but what I can say is that this skill of mine has gotten me out of many  tight situations and into many fair maidens' dreams. But, enough of me glamourizing myself, I'll try to keep this book short and to the point.\n\n1.\nBe as polite as can be without seeming as if you want to kiss someone's backside, being polite leads to people liking you, and even giving you free things such as minas and food.\n\n2.\nBe eccentric and posh with your words. This of course excludes Orcs, they will most likely cave your face in if you use anything more complicated than six letter words. Use words such as indeed, gent, gentleman, kind, fine and so on, this\n\nmay lead to some thinking you a pompous whoreson, but to others you will seem a much more upper class gent or lady than you actually are, helping you achieve your goals whether it be getting that promosion, lying, succesfully conning,\n\nor simply being all the talk at spiffing Balls.\n\n3.\nSeem lighthearted, relaxed and calm, the calmer and more lighthearted you are, the more it will rub off on whoever you're trying to swindle, leading them to dropping their guard, taking a liking of you, or simply another way to seem that\n\nyou have no idea why there's a dead body infront of you while you hold a bloody knife, you just found it there of course.\n\n4.\nBe kind, even if it might not be in your nature, seeming like a kind person will help you in many ways, tricking people, this will lead to you making unlikely allies, you'll have more sway to your word, and if it comes to a tavern brawl\n\neveryone will believe you when you say you didn't start it.\n\n5.\nLast, but not least, be charismatic, even if you're quite the reserved person, this will inspire those around you, and lead to people believing your word over others.\n\nAnd so, that ends my short guide to being a charming and cunning criminal such as myself, whether you use it for good or evil, is your choice, I was just bored in the corner of a tavern waiting for someone to play some blackjack.\n\n-Signed, Mungo, the Charming Bandit.", ""),
        StaticBook("Basic Cooking V2", "§bLillian Hill", "<><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Basic Cooking V.2\n   Soups And Stews.\n          \n            By\n       Lillian Hill\n\n\n\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~   <><><><><><><><><><>\n\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n\nFor each of these recipes a bowl will be needed. These can be easily brought from most stores, or if you feel skilled enough, easy to carve yourself from wood. This is the second installment of the 'Basic Cooking' books.\n\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~Sailor's delight~~~\nIngredients: A cooked fish of your choice. \n\nAdd a small amount of water to your cooking pot, and allow it to warm. Meanwhile, finely dice your fish, making sure to skin and bone it, removing the head. Place\n\nthe chunks of fish in the hot water, and allow it to reach boiling point. At this point, you may feel free to add herbs or salts of your choice, such as tarragon, dill weed or basil. After the broth has boiled for half an elven hour, take a ladle and pour\n\nit into a bowl, taking care not to spill any of the liquid, as it may burn. Fish are an easy ingredient to attain, making this the perfect recipe for an easy and cost effective meal that would satisfy the hunger of your whole family.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~Mushroom Stew~~\nIngredients:\nOne red browncap shroom.\nOne brown browncap shroom.\n\nTo start with, add a large quantity of water to your cooking pot, lighting your fire underneath the\n\ncauldron of water. As the water warms, peel your mushrooms of the top layer, as this allows for flavour to soak into the water. Then continue to slice your mushrooms into a few reasonable size chunks. After the water has started to bubble, throw in the\n\nmushrooms, adding some salt and perhaps some butter or lard, if you have the resources to do so. Allow the mushrooms to cook, stirring the broth occasionally. Once the mushrooms have coloured slightly, and the aroma begins to fill the room, ladle the stew\n\ninto a bowl. An easy recipe, as this type of fungi are commonly found in the wild, or can be bought from a store. This recipe makes enough for one person, though can be easily changed to make enough for the whole family.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~Chicken Stew~~~\nIngredients:\nOne large piece of roat chicken.\nStart by lighting your fire and pour some water into the cooking pot to halfway, allowing it to heat and boil. Take the chicken and remove the skin. Then, make sure to\n\ncut it into bite size chunks, making sure to carefully place them in the cooking pot to avoid the splashing of water. After doing this, allow the chicken to cook before adding any extra vegtables. Once the chicken has browned further and the aroma fills\n\nthe room, remove the pot of broth from the heat and pour into a dining bowl. Allow to cook slightly before eating.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ <><><><><><><><><><><>\n\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~Pork Soup~~~~\n\nIngredients: \nCooked Pork\n\nStart off by lighting your fire and heating your cauldron, before placing the cooking pot over the boiling water. This creates a Bain Marie.\n\nAfter doing this, fill your cooking pot halfway with water. Next, slice up the pork, removing the fat. Place the slices into the cooking pot with salt and rosemary or sage. Stir the soup occasionally. After leaving it to cook for about half an elven hour,\n\nremove the bowl from the heat. Pour the soup into a serving bowl, though allow it to cool as the water would be boiling.\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~Vegtable Soup~~\n\nIngredients:\nTwo baked potatoes. \nFour carrots.\n\nCreate the Bain Marie once more and add your cooking pot. Fill the cooking pot with warm water to about\n\na quarter of the way. While the water is warming, slice your potatoes into chunks, and add them to the water. Next, cut your carrots into thin round disks. Add these to the water. If you wish, salt and rosemary can be added to give the soup some seasoning\n\nand flavour. Soon after, remove the cooking pot from the heat. Pour the contents into a serving bowl. \n <><><><><><><><><><>\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "The Wronged§0\n§0Officer Grudgebeard§0\n§0\n§0The person who Wronged him§0\n§0Dwifar Goldhand§0\n§0\n§0Reason for Grudge: Dwifar caused the injury and loss of an uruk, Grudgebeard paid the Uruk§0\n§0Settle the grudge§0\n\nTerms to settle the grudge§0\n§030 crossbow bolts§0\n§0a crate of provisions§0\n§0one full set of armor§0\n§0Or §0\n§0All those in cost via mina prices are set to cloud temple prices§0\n§0\n§0Signature §0\n§0\n§0Borin Grandaxe\n\nThe Wronged§0\n§0Borin Grandaxe§0\n§0\n§0The Wronger§0\n§0Carven Ithelanen§0\n§0\n§0The grudge§0\n§0Carven shaved Borins beard off in the dominion§0\n§0\n§0To settle the grudge§0\n§0clip both his ears off completely\n\nDate of grudge made§0\n§013th of the Deep Cold, 1674§0\n§0Signature§0\n§0Borin Grandaxe\n\nThe Wronged§0\n§0Durar Grandaxe§0\n§0\n§0The wronger§0\n§0Carven Ithelanen§0\n§0 §0\n§0The Grudge§0", ""),
        StaticBook("The 3 Seasons", "§bSuliin Faelith", "Plantlife withering and freezing where they stand.\nWhite snow falling, and blanketing the lands.\nFarmers crops dying, and long lakes vanishing.\nOnly a chill fills the air, the warmth of the sun banished.\nThis is the Deep Cold.\n\nWhen the snow would melt away, life would be rebirthed. \nDaisies and daffodils would resprout anew, the birds would sing, the deers would graze happily once more.\nThe air would grow warmer, and every inhabitant, happier.\n\nThis is Malin's Welcome.\n\nThe scorch of a hot sun, breathing life down upon the people and crops.\nThe sounds of children playing gleefully, in the sun, sea, over the hills and fields.\nThe lengthy days, and the brief,\n\nswiftly passing nights.\nThis is The Grand Harvest.", ""),
        StaticBook("Diet of Salstone", "§bImperial Historian", "The Diet of Saltstone\n          1552\n\nOn the 9th of the First Seed in the year of our Lord, 1552, an assembly had been held in order to resolve the succesion crisis within the Duchy of Courland. With substantial evidence it has been determined\n\nthat the noble Alexander Staunton is the trueborn brother and heir to the late Duke Andrew Staunton. Alexander Staunton, now Duke of Courland invested with the comital realms of Oesal and Curon, has fulfilled his oaths of fealty and homage as proof of\n\nleal service to the empire and is raised to the peerage.\n\nThe assembled lords did concede the status of Kraken's Watch was contested between the House of Vanir and the Duke of Courland due to machinations of the late Duke before his self-imposed death.\n\nDespite breaching imperial peace in their hostilites towards another, the two parties were pardoned at the behest of His Grace, the Archchancellor Rothesay, who imposed martial law upon the land of Curon on the first week of the First Seed to restore\n\npublic order. The Northern households were summoned towards Saltstone and instructed to recite their grievances upon another. While both parties cited their historical difficulties, a peace was reached, with Britannus Vanir named Baron of Kraken's Watch\n\nand pledging fealty to the Duke Courland. In turn, the Vanirs would rescind and avow their holdings in Erochland, reclaiming their ancestral seat after over twenty-five years, and vow to aid and serve the Duke Courland as his rightful vassal.\n\nTo compensate the Duke's lost holding, the crown pardoned his retainer, hedge knight Demetrios Palaiologos, for his impersonation of imperial gentry and conferred him status as a knight of the Order of the Red Dragon. The Ser was styled 'the Inquisitor'\n\non behalf of his feats of valor and zeal in the Alsacian Inquisition and afforded the fief of Vijland in northern Curon. Finally, the Emperor affirmed imperial law in denying the inheritance of the late Duke's unborn child. The crown enforces agnatic-\n\ncognatic primogeniture upon its vassals. Babes in the womb cannot stand to inherit and are passed over due to their incapabilities. \n\nIN NOMINE DEI\n\nScribed by Imperial Historian from proclimation by\n\nHis Imperial Majesty John II Sigismund of the House of Horen", ""),
        StaticBook("Warrior", "§bDra'Khataba", "Woke up early with the bright rising sun. Picking up and cleaning a well-worn axe. The wounds are deep and cause much pain. Stumbling along the road as it starts to rain.\n\nPainfully thinking of all the battles long past. Time starting slowly to slip from his grasp. Throat burning and so dry he cannot even talk. Slowly moving forward he continues to walk.\n\nMemories pull a single tear that rolls from his eye. Finally realizing that now he will surely die.\nNow, Beaten he stops and in the grass does he lay.\nAnd, waits for the release of death to come to his this day.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Coronation", "§bLilyana", "In the dark of night, an elder man hobbles with a walking stick towards the quiet village. The man’s curiosity is pricked by the silence in the town, a town that once was bustling with life regardless of the time. But, the pain in his back and ache in his\n\nfeet quickly nudged any questions from his mind as he hobbled along the path. He had been traveling for days, braving the wilderness and streets to reach this town, and finally he was close to his destination. However, he had no idea what he was heading\n\nto or why he started this journey. He awoke one morning, some days ago, and felt a tingling sensation in his fingertips, one he had not felt for years. As the days passed, the sensation slowly began to spread throughout his body and the tingling became\n\nstronger; he began to feel an urgency to understand what was causing it. Only days ago had he remembered what this feeling, this sensation, was; it was the excitement, the rush of energy, the craving for blood he felt before he killed a target of the\n\nCrimson Fist. Though his body old and tired now with age, this sensation revitalized him enough to send him into the unknown, to this very town. With each step, the pull on him became stronger, more intense, until now, as he stood outside a large barn,\n\nthe only lit building in the entire town, did he feel like he would burst from excitement. He licked his chapped lips, wrapped his wrinkled hands around the bar, and pulled with all his might on the door, opening it.\n\n    Cora danced around the flame in\n\n the center of the barn, its light dancing along the walls. The deep crimson blood markings and gold jewelry that she wore contrasted against her pale skin. She paid the old man no attention, although she knew full well of his presence, and continued to\n\ndance around the fire, chanting verses of an old Crimson ritual. As the old man stepped into the light of the fire, Evaine quieted her chanting and slowed her dance. She stopped on the side of the wall where a robe of deep crimson hung on a peg. She\n\nfluidly placed the robe about her shoulders then made her way to a corner of the barn that the fire's light did not reach. She looked back over her shoulder, smirking at the old man, before disappearing into the shadows.\n\n The old man scanned\n\nthe barn with his old eyes, his poor ears only hearing the crackling of the fire. He saw nothing, heard nothing, but his very being knew someone, or something was there. From across the fire, from under the shadow of the barn's hay loft, two piercing red\n\neyes broke the darkness and stared at the man, as if they were staring into his soul. The sensation from earlier now rocked the elder; he clung to his walking stick as a force of power pulled him down onto his knees. The owner of the glowing eyes stepped\n\ninto the light of the flame, revealing himself to be an abnormally tall, toned, young man, Haemon. His hair of white gold flowed to his shoulder, his skin as pale as snow, but his eyes, they glowed like lumps of red, hot coal, burning in his eye sockets.\n\nHaemon walked around the fire, slowly approaching the elder. With each step, the elder gripped his walking stick tighter as the power that the boy was emanating tried harder and harder to pull him to the floor. When the boy stood over the old man, he was\n\nshaking with strain and effort to remain kneeling and barely spat out the words before collapsing:\n\n“M-M-My…..L-L-Lord-d-d….M-My P-Prince”\n\nWhen the old man awoke, he found himself sitting against the wall of the barn.\n\nHe felt a sharp pain at his arm and upon inspection found it bandaged tightly, a small blood stain slowly spreading on it. He went to tug on the bandage but a delicate hand quickly grabbed his hand and pulled it from the wound. The elder looked up,\n\nmeeting Cora’s gaze as she slowly shook her head. She pulled out a skin full of water and offered it to the man who, only realizing his thirst at the sight of the skin, quickly took it from her and drank it down. She left him a small plate, some bread and\n\ncheese, and walked around the flame to the other side of the fire. Following her movement, the old man realized that the boy had been sitting across from him this entire time, watching him. Cora slid down along the wall until she was next to the boy, then\n\ncurled herself against him, passing him a vial of a crimson liquid that the old man knew all too well, a vial of blood, his blood.\n\nHaemon lifted the vial to face level, staring at it as the fire's light illuminated the contents. Haemon smiled and asked\n\nfor his name.\n\n\"Eren\", the old man responded.\n\nHaemon shook his head and smiled again, but this time his eyes glowed and a voice unlike the previous one asked for his “true name”. The old man dropped hid bit\n\nof cheese and drew his limbs into him. His gaze met the fiery gaze of Haemon and memories of a life he tried hard to forget washed over him.\n\n\"Doulos, my lord.\" The old man said, maintaining eye contact with Haemon as he spoke, \"Servant to you and your\n\ncause.\"\n\nHaemon nodded and tossed the vial of blood into the fire. The flame erupted into a shower of sparks and turned black as the night around them, all except for the center which glowed with light. The light soon warped and changed and the old man\n\nwatched his own memories, his life from his eyes play before him for all to see. He watched the battle where the temple fell where he fought as a mere Doulos, a soldier and servant to the Crimson Prince’s cause. His escape into the woods as the temple\n\ncollapsed, his struggle for survival, his search for others, his attempts to rebuild what was lost. But alas, he watched himself give into what seemed to be reality that no others had survived, and watched as he isolated himself from the world, locking\n\nthe few relics of his past life away in a chest.\n\nThe flames died down, the color returned to its orange and red glow, and the barn returned to the quiet it had once been. Haemon stood before the flame and spoke of how few of his followers survived that\n\nbattle. He made a point to mention how few had attempted to continue his cause and gracefully pointed to the hay-loft above. The elder’s vision followed Haemon’s direction until it, only now, noticed countless bodies in the loft above, wrinkled and dry,\n\nseemingly drained of their blood. The man reeled back in fear from Haemon, but Haemon only smiled and waved his hand in front of him. He reassured the man that their fate was the fate of cowards and betrayers, those that tried to hide their connection to\n\nhim. \n\n“But the few,” Haemon said as he waved his hand to Cora and back to the old man, “the few that stayed true to me now reap great rewards.”\n\nHaemon explained how the rituals Core and he performed summoned the small\n\nbit of power that the Crimson Prince left in this world. That ritual created a connection between Haemon and the Crimson Prince; that the Prince now acted through Cora’s child, Haemon.\n\n\"I must feed on the blood of the living, fueling my power to allow\n\nthe Prince to return to this world as his true self. We have been traveling to settlements, slowly feasting on its populace as my power grows in strength with each feasting.” Haemon pointed above to the bodies. \"It seems as my power grows, those of the\n\nold Crimson Fist that had survived are drawn to us. We’ve tested those that come, and those to have hidden from their past have been feasted on. While those who were true to our prince, have been given power.”\n\nThe old man perked up. \"Power, my lord?\n\nWhat do you mean?\"\n\nHaemon’s eyes glowed bright, his power exerting itself in the room once more. The fire reached for the ceiling as Haemon lifted his right hand from his side. As his hand lifted, so did the elder man, levitating him in mid-air. Haemon\n\nwithdrew a silver dagger and sliced a thin line down his right forearm. Haemon began to recite a dark chant from deep within his mind and the blood that was slowly seeping from the wound began to rise into the air. The blood hovered over to the elder man\n\nand began to circulate around him, slowly at first but picking up speed quickly. With quick movement, Haemon shut his fist closed, forcing the blood that spun around the old man to suddenly stop and bury its way into his body. The old man howled with pain\n\n for only a moment before his eyes glazed over and his screaming silenced. The man’s body erupted into black flames, devouring him entirely, burning the flesh from his very bones. Cora stood and approached Haemon, wrapping her arms around his torso and\n\nshoulder as they watched on together. The Black Flame finally dissipated, leaving a figure in a crimson cloak where the old man once was.\n\n“Arise”, Haemon ordered with a voice not his own, “ Arise, my new Blood Mage.”\n\nThe figure stood from\n\nthe ash of the black fire and removed his hood, revealing Eren, but as his once youthful self. Eren stared at his hands, no longer wrinkled and weak; he felt his face for saggy skin and scars of old age but only found the tight, tough skin. He felt\n\nrevitalized, no empowered. The ritual had given him a small piece of his lord’s power, and that small piece had not only turned back time to when the old man was once called Doulos, it gave him strength, power, and life.\n\n\"Blood, the essence\n\nf life, is quite a powerful catalyst, as you now see with your own eyes, Doulos. It’s power is only limited by the Mage’s imagination.” Haemon said as Cora wrapped a small bandage around his wrist. \"Ours, theirs, it matters not where it comes from, but\n\nhe purity, power, and amount, that determines the strength of magic that comes from it.” Haemon showed the wound to Doulos, “Until our true lord is able to come into this world our magic is limited, but still powerful.”\n\nDoulos nodded, \"So what is the\n\nnext step? How do we bring forth our Lord, once and for all?\"\n\nCora stepped forward, revealing documents that had thought to have been lost with the years. “Cruor Veneficus, the Blood Tome. A magical tome that the Crimson Fist once had. If we were\n\nto reclaim this tome, we would be able to channel the magical energy from it, making our magic infinite and allow Haemon to focus his feeding on bringing forth our Lord.”\n\nDoulos nodded in agreement and asked \"But where do we start looking for the\n\ntome?\"\n\nCora smiled, “According to the documentation we found on the betrayers and cowards mentions the Cruor Veneficus last being seen in the Crimson Fist’s stronghold in the mountains of the North, the mountains\n\nwhere the settlement “Raven’s Nest” now stands. Word on the street of this town was that a coronation of some sort is to take place there as well, bringing in many guests.” Cora smiled a toothy grin, “If we do not find the Cruor Veneficus, at least there\n\nwill be many for my Prince to feast on.\"\n\n “Raven’s Nest is heavily defended and manned, how are we to take the city?” Doulos questioned.\n\nYou are not the only Blood Mage, Duolos.” Haemon answered as he motioned for Cora to open the barn's\n\ndoor. “There have been others that I found worthy to bestow power upon, like yourself, that now hide themselves amongst the cities of this land. They pretend to normal folk of their race, gathering information, and working their way into cities and\n\ngovernments.\" Haemon motioned outside the barn’s open door where the sunrise was just peeking over the horizon. The low light illuminated many hooded figures walking towards them. \"And many more followers are being drawn here, as you were, and they will\n\night alongside us, wielding powerful Blood Magicks.”\n\nHis questions answered and his mind set straight, Doulus nodded and resigned. \"Yes, my Lord. Raven's Nest cannot, will not, stand against our power and cause. He smiled widely,\n\n\"Our Lord, our Crismon Prince, will rise once more”.\n\n      The Coronation\n            of the\n        True Prince\n\n  A Sequel to the\n Rebirth of Evil\n\n\n\nWritten by: Lilyana", ""),
        StaticBook("Song Anthology 3", "§bAeran", "Song Anthology: Volume 3\n\nThe Maiden of Alrash\n\nThe Great Pumpkiness\n\nThe Money-Grubbing Dwarf\n\nThe Maiden of Alrash\n\nA maiden from Alrash/\nThe subject of my wonder/\nAnd also the rash/\nThat is down under/\n\nFatbuttum Silverblade/\nSecond of her name/\nAlthough I'm not afraid to admit I paid/\nI still felt flayed/\n\nAnd on the morrow/\nMy wallet empty, my needs fulfilled/\nTo my horror, I gaze upon her/\nMy eyes were unskilled/\n\nThe ale must have gotten to me/\nFor that was no wench/\nIt was King Syrio, pretty as a flea/\nBut oh, his stench!\n\nThe Great Pumpkiness\n\nMy father came up to me one day/\nHe said 'Son, I hope you won't have to pay/\nFor in my life I've sinned, true to God/\nBecause one day, I messed with a pumpkin broad/\n\nI can remember that night so clearly/\nBetter than the night I met your mother, although I do love her dearly/\nTwo strangers came by/\nSo frightful, nearly made me cry/\n\nA pumpkin on each other their heads/\nI had to make sure I was not on meds/\n\nWhere are those, anyways?/\nI talk in rhymes without them... Are they in the entry way?/\n\nBut I dress/\nOne wore a pretty dress/\nDarker than your uncles soul/\nEven if it was dipped in coal/\n\nThe other was a man, so I did not care/\nThe nicest woman I've ever met, I swear/\nMy heart flutter, my knees quiver/\nBut I could not look at her without a shiver/\n\nSo I knew what must be done/\nI knew it was not a good idea, in the long run/\n\nBut I gave that pumpkin a yank!/\nAnd she pulled out a shank!/\n\nThat's why they call me One-Ball Jon/\nFor one of my eyeballs, is gone/\nSo if you see the Pumpkiness/\nJust stare at the dress, not her breats!\n\nThe Money-Grubbing Dwarf\n\nThere was a dwarf, his name unknown/\nHis beard would morph, when the wind had blown/\nHe came across, one fateful eve/\nA she-dwarf skillled at basket-weave/\n\nThey wed that week, little did her know/\n\nShe was antique, and very old./\nShe was however weel-endowed,/\nIn more ways than one, so when she bowed/\n\nMore was seen, than was decent/\nLet's keep it clean, her wealth came recent/\nHe father'd died the night before/\n\nBeen murdered by a pretty whore./\n\nTo him she left all that she owned,/\nSo when she'd die, her love'd not groan/\nFor he'd inherit all she had,/\nHer money'd rid him of the sad.", ""),
        StaticBook("Human History v1", "§bBishop Cordal", "A History of Humanity, From Aegis to Athera\nBy Lord Edward Winter II\nVolume I: Introduction and The First Age of Kings\n\nAuthor's Note: The states of the modern realm were formed in a time of civic unrest caused by militarized cultural differe\n\nwithin the Fourth Empire. However, while these nations differ in culture, they retain a simple heritage of governing states, so that the modern man may understand the liegestate to which he pays homage. While my cousin Cordal Winter sought to chronicle\n\nthe timeline of humanity and my fellow writer Procopius sought to color them with his heart, I seek to establish a coherent and continuous history connecting the modern nations to those of the past, and documenting the states through which humanity\n\nprogressed, to allow the modern man to draw parallels between this time and the times before.\n\n-Edward Winter II\n\nThe First Age of Kings\n600s-mid 1300s\nOn the Continent of Aegis and Asulon\nKings from the houses of Perea, Sheffield, Tarus, Horen, Marius, de Nurem\nAlso known as: Aegisian Ages, the First Unrest\n\nIn the first years of recorded histor\n\nformed by the conquering lords of the House Horen, who united many smaller sovereign feudatories into one nation. The last reigning king from the first regnal dynasty was King Daniel Horen, whose seneschal took the crown in a coup, and styled himself King\n\nPampo Perea. Upon his death, his own seneschal, King Edmund Sheffield, took power. King Edmund was then corrupted by the Undead and tried to eat the flesh of his wife and himself died. He was succeeded by his son, King Enor Sheffield.\n\nThe Sheffield\n\nDynasty was fraught with inaction and sloth, and in a coup known as the Phoenix Rebellion, Zibaen Vivayean and Eze'kiel Tarus split from the kingdom and formed their own, called Renatus, with Eze'kiel as king. King Enor Sheffield granted the remainder of\n\nOren to the Hochmeister of the Teutonic Order, Gaius Marius, who named it Hanseti.\n\nHochmeister Gaius Marius died, and he was succeeded by Hochmeister Samuel Bealcrest. The King Eze'kiel Tarus, fearing the military threat of the Teutons,\n\ndemanded their disbandment. The resolution of the ensuing war occurred when King Eze'kiel met a sariant, a soldier of the Teutonic Order, in a duel and was defeated.\n\nThe Kingdom of Salvus was formed on a nearby island by the dethroned Enor\n\nSheffield, alongside his wife Dawn Perea. They lived apart from the warfare of the human realm for a short while. On the mainland, King Eze'kiel left his governance to his regent, Reynard Lycian.\n\nThe kingdoms' citizens moved to a new continent when\n\nundead plague threatened their survival on Aegis, and were joined by the newly founded Kingdom of Seventis. This new kingdom joined Renatus in defending against an assault by the Realm of Hanseti, the dwarven Kingdom of Urguan, the Kingdom of Salvus, the\n\nmulti-racial Kingdom of Alras, and the Orcish war-state.\n\nUrguan, Salvus, and Hanseti then aligned themselves against Renatus, Seventis, Alras, the Orcs, and a dissident faction within Salvus led by Lorethos Basileus called the Twilight Army. Salvus\n\ndefeated, and was absorbed into Renatus. The noble House of Hightower was given control of the Salvian realm. Seventis was shortly after stricken with plague and devastated, and its lands too were absorbed into Renatus. The then-Hochmeister Mirtok de\n\nNurem, following a conflict with Renatus and an internal dissident faction called the Wolverines, surrendered his lands too to Godfrey Horen, a politician who had been handed control of Renatus and later was crowned Emperor of Oren.", ""),
