        StaticBook("Piano Tutorial", "§bRoth Jayamen", "((OOC))\n\nThe noteblocks layout on the floor (3x3 square) goes with numbers. The numbers match the piano in this way.\n\n7 8 9\n4 5 6\n1 2 3\n\nThe 2 through 9 in Real life notation (if you know this) Is C note through C note. or an octave. The Key is C major.\n\nAnother way to think about it is that 2 through 9 is like Do through Do in the phrase 'Do, Re, Mi, Fa, So, La, Ti, Do'.\n\nThe Number 1 of the noteblocks is the Note B. It is basically one white key below C.\n\nThe Piano is based in all white keys.\n\nSongs that I write in-game are based on the 1-9 layout. Just follow the song books numbers in order to play them.\n\nIf you have any questions, Ask me In-Game or through the forum. IGN: Sofetios", ""),
        StaticBook("Cassandara's Log", "§bCassandara", "So then... The life of Cass- I guess that would include Garoll-- You probobly don't know Garoll do ya... Well then- This is going to be a strange story-- I will explain it after but for now. Enjoy I guess.\n\nOne crappy day, Little 10 year old human female, Cassandara was in her house playing with her little dog. A knock at the door and Little Cass comes to see- This person was a witch. I don't really know what I was thinking back then... I think it was mental\n\nmagic- Anywho. I went to a room, with Garoll with this witch and another guy. Who is a golemancer- I learned that... The golemancer tried to put me into a golem! Garoll objected after seeing who I was. He attacked the golemancer. And this timing was shit-\n\nAnd to sumarise. My 'soul' is now in this Dark Elf body. This dark elf is Garoll... Now- You may be asking 'Oh no! What happened to Garoll'.. He is still here- Safe.. I will explain his life now then I will go onto Cass before the shift and then after.\n\nGaroll. Raised an orphan, no family or friends. His only friend turned out to be a deamon and his family (before he left) abused him. Garoll ran off- Where he came to Vailor and struggled to get involved in society. Here he learned Air Evocation as he was\n\ncommonly attacked. This is when he met his few friends- he traveled alot back then and found a lover, Odran... What a kind person he was. It was at this time that Cass crashed into Garolls life. Long story short- Garollandara\n\nwas hated and went on a huge travel to hide from everyone... When Garoll returned everyone he knew was dead from old age. We were gone for about 60 years! Garolls lover had died. When Garoll found his grave well- He has not been awake since- He is still..\n\nCass before the little trade. A young human- Lived with her family... So kind. Cass' father was taken by the madness! He killed all of Cass' family- and then the village they lived in. Cass stayed at the home, even when her dad ran away...\n\nAfter the swap? Well- Cass took a while to come to grips with what was going on. I thought that Garoll was a mental illness and i sought Psychological help to sort him out... Not much happened. Cass ventured around and met so many beautiful people!\n\nLike Garoll, Cass had to go on an adventure, most of his friends are now... Dead.\n\nAdventure Garollandara went on:\n\nGaroll was a pirate at one point: Killed a kraken!\n\nCass was a psychopath and killed countless people.\n\nGaroll was forced into a war against orcs (They somehow one!)\n\nCass destroyed some undead shrines...\n\nGaroll:\nGay, Dark Elf, Male.\nKind, Caring, Loving: Loves all life and tries to help everyone he can, even when he cannot do it well.\n\nCass:\nStraight (Basically).\n10 year old Human female (Before the swap)\nCurrently a dark elf...", ""),
        StaticBook("Message to Ponce", "§bEdward Baldrwin", "Dear Prince;\nPlease do me the honor of joining my wife and I as well as the Bishop of Metz in a small feast to celebrate GOD and friends in these trying times!\n\nYour courier can give you directions to the County of Cleves.", ""),
        StaticBook("1519 Diary Toren", "§bToren Amroth", "13th of Malins Welcome, 1519:\n\nMight as well start off with who I am. \n\nMy name is Toren Amroth, I have a brother named a stoic and a beautiful girlfriend named Juliel.\n\nFamily:\n\nSo I was the youngest out of me 4 brothers: Brock, Boic, Stoic, George and me.\n\nBrock died when I just maybe coming up to three years old. Didn't remember him that well, he had curly brown hair that ran to his shoulders.\n\nBoic was a tall and sturdy man, us highlanders are known for our height he was 6'6!\n\nHe had a scruffy stubble, and dark brown eyes, his voice was deep and raspy like my fathers.\n\nWhen he was 21 he moved to Petrus and joined the soldiers.\n\nThis was in Athera by the way.\n\nHe was patrolling with his men until a group of savage orcs ambushed them and slaughtered them.\n\nBit's of blood and crushed bones were all of left behind. He wore a gold ring which my brother stoic took for memories.\n\nGeorge:\n\nHe had wavy blonde hair like my mother, bright blue eyes and a skinny build. His face was boneless and his lips were thin.\n\nHe worked as a carpenter until he was 17, and moved out with his girlfriend.\n\nI never saw him again after that.\n\nStoic:\n\nSo that leaves Stoic. He's my best friend, also best brother. He can be harsh but I love him, he's the muscular one, took after me father: Hodrick Amroth.\n\nHe's more of soldier than a...whatever I am.\n\nHe always takes care of me, although i'm smarter than him.\n\nAnd that leaves me: Toren Amroth.\n\nI have navy blue eyes and a slender, skinny build like my mother, I never took notice in war I never liked violence.\n\nI prefered to fish, collect flowers, talk to people rather than join the army.\n\nMe and my girlfriend Juliel met a few days ago, I started speaking to her and offered her into the tavern we began talking for hours. That was also the day I asked her out.\n\nShe's so pretty: She has long brown hair thats silky and smoothe.\n\nHer eyes are wonderful, and she is quite delicate.\nShe looks after me and listens to my complaints.\n\nI love her very much.\n\nWell thats all for now i'll write later.\n\n22nd Of Malins Welcome 1519:\n\nWas approached by a huge beast today, it looked Orcish and some what human.\nDalia said it's name was Gregor it was huge I fell back onto a rock as took a giant step forward.\nIt's large feet sunk into the soil.\n\nHe had long black hair, and wore ripped trousers his body was exposed it had thick, black hairy chest hair on it it's grimy yellow teeth shone in the sunlight.\n\nI fell onto the ground shielding my face from him, he picked me up and bear hugged me.\n\nI could have died.\n\nI have a weird feeling that Dalia may have an interest in me. She says she's married but i've never seen her husband.\n\nSometimes I have to remind her that I have Juliel and I love her very much.\n\nWhat happens if she tries to kiss me, and Juliel walks in?\n\nI'm going to speak to Stoic about Gregor and see if he can do anything about it, because I was petrified about it!\n\nI was strolling around in Felsen, and a guard approaches me I was looking nervous and wiped some sweat off my forehead. He patted me on the shoulder and gave me a leaflet to join the Military. \n\nI rejected it and gave it back to him.\n\nHe called me a coward and a traitor.\nPretty soon we had a big crowd amongst us, I wasn't ready to fight and knew if he punched me he wouldn't be punished.\n\nI left the crowd by pushing past everyone and running back home. \nI locked myself in my cellar.\n\nDalia asked if I could go kill some undead with her as it gets boring doing it alone.\n\nI hesitated but then realised she could die out there, so I came prepared with an iron sword.\n\nIt wasn't hard: just slice and dice the undead bastards.\n\n2nd Of The First Seed 1519:\n\nI spent a majority of my day fishing, catched about three barrels full.\n\nI then went into oren to buy myself some iron for a hook, until I heard a lot of shouting from the tavern and outside it.\n\nI cautiously walked nearer to the crowd all speaking at once staring into the tavern. I walked inside and saw Dalia with a sword up to her throat not sure if she saw me.\n\nI froze in my spot and slowly backed out of the tavern to join the crowd.\n\nI watched from a distance, and saw that Dalia tried to headbutt the man, but he raised his sword and it went straight into Dalia's throat.\n\nI closed my eyes tightly and heard the deceased body collapse onto the floor with a 'thud'.\n\nA lot of people stared inside for a few minutes, children began crying so I left Felsen. Perhaps it is best to avoid Dalia now.\n\nI wont speak to her make eye contact, or even try and see her if possible.\n\nIt could put my life in danger if Guards see me\n\nwith her.\n\nI was thinking of proposing to Juliel.\nIs it still too early, I don't want to ruin what we have now.\n\nI have the ring. I just don't, want to ruin it.\n\n14th Of The First Seed 1519: \n\nSo Dalia is now dead, it's a little bit of a relief because she followed me around a lot. \n\nI always felt as if she was trying to seduce me. But on the other hand she was a good person sort of.\n\nHer sister came up to me today and asked about what happened with her.  I told her that all I know is she slapped a noble in the face, and paid the price for it.\n\nI know I sound harsh as if I don't care which is completley untrue ofcourse I care.\n\nShe was always mean calling me names like: Coward, stupid, lack common sense.\n\nI'm not a strong being, because my father never pushed us to fight he never taught. \n\nMy brothers however apart from George knew how to fight because they trained.\n\nI made a room for me and Juliel today for when I propose, it's a dark room with candles lit making it romantic. \n\nShe'll see when I finally propose.\n\n5th Of The First Seed 1519:\n\nOnce I was done fishing I salted them, and put them in the cooking pot. \n\nIt took a good few hours to cook the buggers but in the end they were all cooked and put on a plate and served to the people.\n\nI was wondering if I should sell this Diary when it is finished?\n\nBut then it could be that some of my secrets are shared to the world so I'll probably just store this one.\n\nLast time I wrote a diary was back when I went on a ship to catch a wale, the trip was a failure but I did get to see a blue wale.\n\nIt almost smashed our boat to pieces when we stuck a harpoon in it. I did suggest we get a bigger ship.\n\nEight of us left to hunt it, only four returned, including me.\n\nI hid in the lower deck, which was slowly filling up with water.\n\nI remember my friend came through slipping in the water which was up to his knees, he was calling my name.\n\nI came out from hiding in a barrel, and went to meet him. I took a step closer about to open my mouth and say \"Here!\" when suddenly, the boat split in two. \n\nA large wooden pillar that held the sails together, collapsed and smashed onto my legs.\n\nI fell on the floor gasping for air. Spitting out bits of sea water I let out a scream and tried to crawl forwards, but I was stuck.\n\nIt was slowly sinking to the bottom, but my legs were trapped.\n\nMy friend slid down the boat, and grabbed my wrist he tried yanking me out of it, but it was no use the pillar was stiff.\n\nMy body was soaked in water, and I could feel the gritty salt in between my teeth.\n\nI told him to go, he hesitated and then hugged me. He ran to top deck which had large holes and cracks in it. I heard his feet run across the deck and a then a large splash.\n\nHe plunged into the sea, and began swimming not knowing where.\n\nI couldn't even tell if anyone else was on the ship with me.\n\nIt fell to a silent yet eery noise. Just the running of water and my heavy breathing with me spewing out sea water everytime it got into my mouth.\n\nI tried to turn around, but my legs were lodged in tight.\n\nI could feel the water coming to my neck, I took one last deep breath and held it.\n\nThe water filled my face pretty soon. I could feel the pillar slowly moving out of place.\n\nIt rolled off my left leg which was now free. I still couldn't get my head high enough to get it out of the water.\n\nI began praying hoping it'd release my right leg.\nI felt it roll off and felt my bone in my right leg\nshatter as it did so.\n\nI let out a high pitched yelp, and swam to the top. Bits of wood and debris filled the ocean top.\n\nEverytime I kicked my leg I would feel an intense burning pain shoot up my leg. \n\nIt was as if someone was trying to stab it.\n\nI found a large and thick piece of debris and managed to climb onto it, I layed on it and used a stick that was floating by to paddle myself. It was an extremely slow pace, but I did manage to find shore.\n\nA crowd was already there it turns out my friend that dived off, made it to the same island I did and was telling the Guards of Petrus of what happened.\n\nThis was back in Athera, only a few stone days we moved there.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Alphabet", "§bEris Oranor", "A for Apple\nB for Backwards\nC for Cat\nD for Dwarf\nE for Elf\nF for Fish\nG for Goat\nH for Horse\nI for Inside\nJ for Jacket\nK for King\nL for Leave\nM for Missing\nN for Needing\n\nO for Orange\nP for Pumpkin\nQ for Queen\nR for Rest\nS for Sunflower\nT for Tree\nU for Under\nV for Vest\nW for West\nX for Xen\nY for Yeast\nZ for Zebra", ""),
        StaticBook("Edel Deserter", "§bBaldin \"Ironside\" Frostbeard", "Edel has left the Frostbeard clan to create his silvervein clan. By doin so he left the beardguard, breaking his oath to the guard. Let it be known that this dwarf is dishonorable. No one leaves the bear guard. Only death shall make us leave our rank.", ""),
        StaticBook("Two Brothers", "§bTorkan Starbreaker", "There was once two brothers by the name of Armakak, and Khorvad. The two brothers were part of the Brathmordakin council, Armakak also known as The merchant father, and Khorvad was known as the God of Ambition. These two brothers were always\n\nwith each other, helping one another gain more followers. Khorvad would appear upon the dwarves and tell them “go out and follow your hearts and you will succeed if you promise to always follow my worship.” The dwarves would set out making\n\nKhorvad pleased by the many followers he was receiving. After years have past Khorvad began gaining more and more followers and even gained more followers than his older brother Armakak. When Armakak realized that Khorvad was gaining more fame\n\nthan himself, Armakak became Jealous of Khorvad. A couple of decades went by until Armakak was furious of Khorvad and all the fame he was getting. Armakak attacked Khorvad and what was once a brotherhood between the two, became nothing but a\n\nrivalry. “Greed is a powerful and dangerous thing and can split up the most of loving relationships” - Varden Ironborn", ""),
        StaticBook("Letter to Avilia", "§bBaldin \"Ironside\" Frostbeard", "Beloved  Avilia,§0\n§0I am off to war, this letter might be the last kiss of this burned dwed. Dark child of the outlands. My heavy heart will take this last goodbye. Our Legionaries willhave brave souls for this last stand. Spilled blood on my charred hands.\n\nI sacrifice to know you will stay alive. When the fire has come. I will die to protect you. Pray to Dungrimm for me. My Queen don't cry tonight. There's a dream left to cling to. I will rest in ash. To leave you safe, I pray.§0\n§0\n§0My love I most not waver now\n\nfaced by death. Deep earth where the fires glow. Faced down with the unknown. A whispered vow to you on my last breath. When the fire has come. I will die to protect you. My Queen don't cry tonight. There is a dream left to cling to I will rest in ash to\n\nleave you safe I pray.§0\n§0\n§0If you have recived this letter it means I have fallen in the battle field. There is no greater honor than to die for this kingdom. I just wish I could see you one more time. My love for you makes me fear death, even if its one as\n\nhonorable as a legionarie's death fighting for Urguan.§0\n§0Avilia I love you.§0\n§0Bastion is a looky dwed.", ""),
        StaticBook("Personal Letter", "§bBaldin \"Ironside\" Frostbeard", "I look at my uniform and I do not what to feel. We have marched in to the council of hammers and murdered the council members of the clans. All for a throne? Why have we obeyed such orders! We have dammed our souls to the Nether! Every night I see their\n\nfaces, their blood, the blood of my brothers. My father was a grandaxe and I murdered his (and my) clan mates. What can of dwed does this! The family of Urguan is breaking appart, and its all our fault. Our hands are covered in the blood of the innocents.\n\nAll the Frostbeards that have died for this kingdom and now we are ready to destroy it, just to claim a throne.§0\n§0I fear the dwarves might not recover from this action.§0\n§0Brathmordakin have mercy on us.", ""),
        StaticBook("List of Suspects", "§bBaldin \"Ironside\" Frostbeard", "List of Suspects for the murder of Avilia Frostbeard:§0\n§0- Bastion Ireheart§0\n§0- Axel Ireheart§0\n§0- Kerwyr Frostbeard§0\n§0- Oyvind Frostbeard§0\n§0- Morug (Born Frostbeard)§0\n§0- Zahrer Irongrinder§0\n§0\n§0I know I am close to finding who killed the Queen. Justice must\n\nbe served.§0\n§0\n§0I swear I will not rest until I find the dwed (if such individual can be called one) that killed her.", ""),
        StaticBook("New Recruit", "§bBaldin \"Ironside\" Frostbeard", "I met Throri's son today. He wanted to join the bear guard. The lad looked so flimsy and with such a tiny beard that I hesitated. However, Throri proved to be a loyal underling so I decided to approve his son Edel (?) to join the bear guard. As it is\n\nrequired for a bear guard to have a title I gave Edel (?) the title of \"Honorable\". His Father kept telling me how honorable his son was so I guessed it was a decent title to give the beardling. I most say his fighting skills arent §0great...but§0 he seems to\n\nknow how to please his higher ups some how. I hope the lad is not doing things the Brathmordakin would dissaprove of to gain the approval of his higher ups.§0\n§0\n§0I miss my children...", ""),
        StaticBook("Fuckin Druids", "§bBaldin \"Ironside\" Frostbeard", "Druids kicked me out of the groove after I flirted with one of the Druids. Apparenttly its not the attitude they look from folk that seek to learn druidism. They can kiss my ass I say. I had to write poems for those cunts and now they kick me out for this\n\nshit. I hope they get attacked by Oren and we let them fend for themselved. Pumpus assholes.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Observations", "§bKetiley Strong-Heart", "-~=  The Observations  =~-\n\n*All observations and notes taken are written and seen by Ketiley of Orvar.\n\n*Small writtings below are scribbled quickly and messily, but more in a though-proccessed fashion.*\n\nMushmushmushmushmush\nmushmushmush\n\nObservation One:\n\n20th of The Deep Cold, 1472\n\nMorvan and I have decided to start our observations in an old Ruin, to which I, at least, presume was owned once by a Necromancer due to the dried blood on the top\n\nstory. Nonetheless, my decision for such a place is due to the overgrowth of Mushrooms. Large ones at that.\nMushmushmushmushmush\n\nIt seems with time, the ruin was to decay and nature had one more taken it's beauty back and overthrew the manmade stone\n\ndesign. In my personal opinion, I believe the decay of such a building, holding vast secrets, though very morbid and very dangerous, is absolutely, peacefully, beautiful when natures takes back it's rightful place among the tall stature of the tower. The\n\nlarge mushrooms within the odd ruin really add to it. Give it character and seem to coexist perfectly and gorgeously within the stone walls of the masonry. There is, surprisingly, a mechanism that shows Aegis within the tower. And seems oddly preserved.\n\nBut even then, the rest of the crumbling walls remain together because of the sturdy stalks of the pretty mushrooms that hold the tower together with the years it remains.\nThe musrooms come iin dull colours and vibrant. Tall and small. I could watch them\n\nfor hours.. T'is truly a sight to behold.\n\n*A rather detailed, very shaded and beautifully drawn, sketch of one of the larger mushrooms, holding dots and leaking small dust clouds of spores, takes up the rest of the page.*\n((X: -63 Z: -208))\n\nObservation Two:\n\n21st of The Deep Cold, 1472\n\nMorvan and I have now made our way to a grand tree. Very VERY large... Towers completely over the rest of the land... Reminds me of the great tree that harbours the Druids in the Grove.\n\nThe reason this particular site attracted me is because it has a calming nature about it. Beautiful crystals float below the grand tree. The light from the crystals allow the leaves of the magnificent tree to lightly shine with a dull light that hangs\n\nbelow the large branches. The lovely jade and emerald leaves canopy most of the forest from the tree that towers so easily over the land. I notice that the trunk harbours spiders in it. But.. T'is the way of nature..\nVery large bees, fireflies, and other\n\ninsects seem to have made a peaceful home here among the great forest while the large tree offers shelter. Like that of a mother for her children. Reminds me much of Andarta..\nOur first time here, Morvan and myself, was when we bound ourselves together\n\nthe very first time. Andarta would be The Maiden of The Forest. The Goddess that trusts no one and tends only to her beloved tree. I now see why she loves them so.. The amount of shelter, beauty, trust, and safehaven this Grand tree offers is nothing that\n\ncan be described or even compared to.. The way the incects seem to take shelter in the tree is... Indescribable... For lack of better words, it's a very gorgeous sight to behold. To be frank.. Even though spiders swarm the land now... This is most\n\ndefinitely my favourite place to be... The awe, wonder, and love that I feel radiate from this wonderous tree is absolutely incomparable. Watching the sun rise in the east and sparkle so dully against the canopy of leaves is is-... indescribable.. Truly..\n\nHowever... Morvan and I had to retreat to a safe distance due to the over-swarm of the undead and spiders...\n\nEven from such a great distance... It's clear to see this Mother tree completely towers over her younger saplings and smaller trees..\n\nNurturing them in her embrace of shady leaves and the friendly light from the crystals.\n\n*An acurate drawing of the Grand Tree, from afar, is shown here, partially showing the very crystals that offer a dull glow.*\n((X: -437 Z: -407))\n\n~-=*                              *=-~\nObservation Three:\n\n13th of Snow's Maiden, 1473\n\nI've decided to settle at a white stag statue, south of Haelun'or, and sit and observe a pretty blue orchid. The way the wind blows so softly\n\n~-=*                              *=-~\nagainst the small, pretty, blue petals of the viney flower is rather peaceful to watch. The colour of the flower itself reminds me of the ocean and the sky combined as one. And even though it's sibling flowers,\n\n~-=*                              *=-~\nlike the variety of colourful tulips, and lilys, the pretty azure, I think, flowers seem to dance in the same movements of the orchid, in the calming wind, the blue orchid stands out. They're definitely something\n\n~-=*                              *=-~\nyou'll spot first in a crowd of anything.. I think this may be one of the flowers I love the best. Though my love for the rest of the flowers is equally shared.\n\n*a depiction of the blue orchid is drawn here.*\n\n~-=*                              *=-~\n\n~-=*                              *=-~\n\n~-=*                              *=-~\n\n~-=*                              *=-~\n\n~-=*                               *=-~\n\n~-=*                               *=-~\n\n~-=*                               *=-~\n\n~-=*                              *=-~\n                 Notes:\n\n- There was a very, VERY, gorgeous, peaceful, pretty, and amazing little cave that had a hotsprink, and bunnies, and so many pretty flowers.\n<3!\n\n~-=*                              *=-~\n*an acurate graphite depiction of a peony is drawn here among blades of grass.*\n- We then went to an absolutely magnificent place that held the most pretty and largest white trees... I was completely\n\n~-=*                              *=-~\nawestruck by the absolutely amazing and indescribable scenery... Officially my FAVOURITE place now... Just south of Haelun'or.. Found a little town, too..\n*A picture of the scenery, drawn in a graphitelike\n\nmaterial is drawn on the previous page, just below the writings.*\n\n((X: 668 Z: 897))\n(( http://oi62.tinypic.com/sw5xef.jpg ))", ""),
        StaticBook("Notes II", "§bArchmage Crumena", "Seventh of the Sun's Smile, 1497\nCrumena Ilwindior \nI looked back to my notes and scribblings when Elindor and I attempted to decipher Rasmot’s enchantments on the closest. Nothing was comprehensible. It was only until\n\n\ndiscover something almost like a thread. Though this thread wielded unbridled power. We could not trace its origins but we realized that thread was the source of power for each transporter.", ""),
        StaticBook("A tale", "§bAlan Marlsbush", "Once upon a time there was an elf. The elf wasn't very happy with its life, they had no reason to be. They grew up alone, and after a while their parents left them. They couldn't understand why, the only logical conclusion was that they were unwanted.\n\nThey wandered until they were found by a young elven woman who raised them as their elder sister. She was away often, and was not a soft kind person, however she did her best to care for the child. The elf rarely spoke, when they did it was uncomfortable,\n\nstiff, and they cut out as many words they could. They communicated the best they could through hand gestures and expressions, and found games to play by themself. They were ill often, but it didn't bother them. They were used to being ill and being\n\nalone. They continued to play alone and read. They loved most to make small snowmen and rabbits, then they could make as many friends as they wanted. Their sister took care of them the best she could, and they were the closest to happy they could have\n\nbeen, but it couldn't last. They were frightened, so frightened that their sister would leave them too. So they ran away. I could not hope to explain their motivations, the elf was still a child at the time, and a frightened child is not the most logical\n\nbeing. So they left. However their illness caught up to them. There was no way they could take care of themself. They wandered until they were found by a woman who offered to take them in. However not long afterwards the woman disappeared, leaving\n\nthem alone once again. They grew up eventually, however they had no idea how to interact with other people, and even when they were seen as a friend by another, they could not trust these people not to leave them too. They were alone, whether surrounded\n\nby others, or isolated in their home it made no difference. Then, one day, they fell in love. She was a beautiful elf, with vibrant red hair and green eyes, and she loved them as well. It frightened them. They couldn't bear the thought of losing her. She\n\nmade them happier than they knew was possible. Being seperated from her frightened them, perhaps she would grow bored of them. They did lose her, but not how they expected. She died. They didn't know how to cope, and completely shut down. They wouldn't\n\ntalk, and wished they'd never met her. For now that they knew what it was to be so happy, living without it seemed unbearable. They didn't know what to do anymore. It was not enough to just be alive anymore. They had been aware of their lonliness before,\n\nhowever the grief with no one to comfort them made it as sharp as a knife. They grieved and wandered and then they found someone else. He swept through the elf's life like a windstorm. To say they loved each other would be inaccurate. He loved the elf's\n\nbeauty, and they desperately needed someone to notice them. However he left as quickly as he came, and died as well. The elf resigned themself to remaining alone, as painful as it was they did not know what to do aside from accepting it. Just when they\n\nfelt that it was such they met someone. A cousin they had not known about. They quickly grew to adore her, she was kind and an accomplished doctor. However they found it difficult to talk to her about anything. She was significantly younger than them, and\n\nthey did not want to burden her. They couldn't. They cared about her too much, and trusted her too little. It was enough to keep them going. They pushed through day to day. Their cousin fell in love, and married someone whom the elf had been well\n\nacquainted with for a very long time. They found themself able to talk to him, if just a little. After a long while it was too much, and they grew apart from the small amount of family they'd found. They couldn't trust her or their friend enough, and\n\ncould truly believe themself to be loved. They tried, they really tried, however they did not know how. They did not know what they should do, what they could do. They had never been taught how. They got a job at a tavern as a chef, and once again met\n\nsomeone. They fell deeply in love with him, and he loved them in turn. Once again they felt happy. Their companion seemed to genuinely care for them, and wanted to be with them. Which made it all the more painful when he too passed away. They did their\n\nbest to carry on living, and for a few years they could. But now, maybe they should just give up? No one will miss them if they're gone. If they die, who cares? No one will mourn them. What is the point of continuing to fight, fight their poor health,\n\nfight their own thoughts? They may just give up.", ""),
        StaticBook("The Sewer", "§bArthur Caulfield", "The Sewer\n           By\n         Arthur\n        Caulfield\n\nIt is the sewer, in which I live. A rank and stinking tunnel of which no man would ever set foot. I am alone down here, sitting quietly, waiting. The darkness creates shadows of harrowing ghouls. Even I find myself jumping at each echoed sound.\n\nThis is why I am paranoid. No sound is ever pure. In a world of tunnels and halls every sound is one that has been bounced around and repeated over and over, so that by the time it reaches your own ears, you may never know where it originated.\n\n\n   But of course, the question you ask. Why would such a feared creature such as me, be afraid of boogie men in the dark? I tell you now, in the sewers I am not to be feared.\n\nFor if you have ever ventured into a sewer at what would be the lowest point in your life, you will know that what lay down there would destroy the minds of high elves and orcs alike.\n\nNothing stops them from venturing to the surface, they could invade cities, burn down petrus with their horrid image. The eyes of citizens would melt, leaving only liquid to run down their cheeks.\n\nOf course, I get ahead of myself, for if you are reading you have not been down here. To a place of O such abandoned horror, not too mention the distaste of all who are civilized. Which is why I would like to describe for you,\n\nthe image of such creatures scarier than me. \n   Bright yellow spots on their backs, painful and sore. Balding heads, with fragments of fragile hair left and unkept.\n  Spines so bent they can not walk without pain.\n\nFeet featuring sharp toe nails that could cut a nobleman's sword. Noses that smell and pick out their prey. Skin as pink as a rich woman’s nails but as soft as fresh dough in your hands. \n  This is what I face every day.\n\nThough down here there is no day or night, only darkness all of the time. I feel myself going crazy, I don’t understand it. I have over a dozen eyes but am subject to the worst view and the most terrifying life.\n\nYou shouldn’t try to save me. I would hurt you. My fangs, over three inches long equipped with venom, would paralyse you before I even realised what I had done.\n   It’s not your fault. And it’s not mine.\n\nI can’t run the risk of greeting something that could be my doom. I’ve seen plenty of my own kind decapitated, ripped apart and eaten. I don’t want to hurt you, but I don’t want to die. \n  This is why I choose to stay in my tunnel.\n\nIt is mine. Scattered with web, damp and dark. Far enough away from any nest of the abominations. Close enough to the entrance that I can hear the world. \n  I can’t leave of course. No one down here has ever done that.\n\nGoing out there would scare the civilized. And scaring the civilized means being taken down by a mob of weapons. So I sit down here, content with just listening. \n  Every now and then I will here parts of conversation.\n\nSomeone bought a stale loaf of bread, another is excited about a wedding. I do not understand the context of what they say, but I revel in the idea of having a conversation with another being.\n\nI am apart of an aggressive species. Dominance is the only way to live life. It is my duty, nay, my instinct to destroy every other of my kind. I do not want to, I must.\n\nI enjoy the rain. It is supposedly cleaner than the water down here. It does not have the musky odour or the putrid colour. \n  The sound is hypnotic, listening to each drop hit the earth above calms me, it lets me ignore every other sound.\n\nIt let’s me remove my guard for just a day, before I am aware of the dangers once more. \n  Somedays, when all is quiet. And only the ripples in the dirty water move.\n  I stare at the tunnel walls.\n\n I wonder how long ago it must have been, when humans built it. How long ago it must have been since they were last down here.\n   The walls have begun to deteriorate, sometimes I hope it will crumble,\n\nand I will be sealed into this tomb worthy only of my presence.  Even with eight legs I could not escape that fate. \n   But my kind is supposed to act on instinct, and so I do.\n\n So I do not look for a way to better my existence, I simply live out what has been given to me. I do not try to escape.", ""),
        StaticBook("Sunless Sanctum", "§bKass", "===================\n\n  The Cloud Temple\n        Of Aegis\n===================\n\nThe Cloud Temple of Aegis was once a great place some of the eldest living members of society have fond memories of. But that place is no longer a place of light and hope. It is now the Abyss or Sunless Sanctum, and it is the place of darkness and\n\ndesolation. The only way to get to the Sanctum is to find or have someone who knows where it is, take you there. The portal is larger than a small house, maybe even a medium sized one.  But one thing is for sure, Ghouls, Wraths, and other Dark Creatures.\n\nMost will not like you, some will simply see you as a meal, and some may simply want to make you a slave of their dark purpose. I write this book so that no one will need to go there themselves. All that enter, will not leave the same. The weight of what\n\nis seen, is worse than the weight on your soul that is gained while there. This is the first and final warning to you, the reader. Now, to carry on.\n\n___________________      Observations\n___________________ \nThe Abyss is a place seeming to exist in it's own dimension of darkness, no light from anywhere but that seen from the lights around it. Warped pillars are thrown about randomly about, except on\n\nthe dark paths, leading to the different places of residence each species takes. In the center of the Abyss, and first structure to come into view, is the ruins of the Cloud Temple Of Aegis.\n\n*A sketch in red ink, or blood. a dragon eating it's tail lies upon the page. no eye defined as if it lies elsewhere....*", ""),
        StaticBook("Love's Ending 2", "§bFranswaar Kellian", "Love's Ending 2\n\n               By: \n   Franswaar Kellian\n\nThis Book is Dediciated to those who have lost everything\n\n3 years have passed since I learned. \n\nWe barely speak, though you don't have too. Whenever I see you, memories flood my mind. When we were inseperable. When we had our lives planned out. \n\nI will never undstand.\n\nYour daughter has grown  so much. She has your eyes, your nose. When I see her playing in the street, I see you in your youth. When we would play jokes on others. When I first learned that you were the love of my life, my angel\n\nI will never understand.\n\nEveryday since I have returned I have thought of no one else but you. \n\nYou were everything I had. Everything I was. Everything I wanted to achieve. I am in constant pain, though I do nothing. Tears seep down through my heart, though men are told not to\n\ncry. If this is so, I am no man.  \n\nI am a coward. I am afraid. I was born to say I love you. Every Breathe you ever took next to me, filled me with life. \n\nI will never understand.\n\nI am tired being so alone, but I am not welcome. \n\nNothing can mend my wounds, for time caused them. \n\nOnly myself is blame, I left. I told you I had too, but that is not true. I only wished to view the world. I guess my ambitions are my demise.\n\nRegrets and Guilt fill my mind as my heart is posioned by the prick of your quick removal from my life. I long to be with you again. I spend most my time overlooking the city a top the mountains unable to move, so I unwillingly climb down.\n\nSo I guess I will live alone. In your shadow. \n\nThough I have nothing to live for, nothing to hope for. No one else saw me the same as you did. \n\nI can't keep my eyes off of you. Words can't describe how I am feeling. Though I must turn away.\n\nI crawl home, in tears. There is nothing left for me on this planet. \n\nI climb apon the mountains again. The trail leads to the waterfall. \n\nPeaceful\n\nElegant \n\nBlissful\n\nSerenity\n\nI am at peace, the thoughts of you leave. I can finally go. \n\nA hand is placed on my shoulder. Darkness masks their face, but their touch is all but to well known.\n\nWhen I finally found peace to let go, you return into my life\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nI will never understand", ""),
        StaticBook("The Inner Circle", "§bLeyun Kameki", "The Inner Circle\n\nScribed by Hierophant Callax, the Solstice Druid\n\nExisting within the structure of the Druidic Order Circle of Malinor, which is the primary and mother Circle of Druids, is an Inner Circle. The Inner Circle is rather different than a Druidic Circle, however. It is part of an existing Circle, composed of\n\nthree Archdruids and no set number of Druid Guides who all take responsibility for the inner working of the Order.\n\nThe Druids of the Inner Circle are those who are permitted to guide and attune Dedicants as well as train Druids in the\n\nways of teaching or in harnessing the Gifts of Nature. During a Moot, the Druids of the Inner Circle cast their votes, with only the best interests of the Order in mind, to make a particular decision for the Order.\n\nThe Inner Circle doesn't dictate the\n\nOrder, nor does it dictate or manipulate individual Druids. Rather, the Inner Circle has, for countless centuries, only served to maintain order by making larger decisions for the Order and effectively upbringing new generations of Druids.\n\nThe Archdruids and Druid Guides of the Inner Circle are crucial to the function and future of a Druidic Order. This ancient and important aspect of Orderly structure should never be forgotten. Blessed be.", ""),
        StaticBook("Song of Fel'ina", "§bArchrim Elmoran", "Out in the west Vailor town of felsen I fell in love with a highelven girl. Night time would find me in rose's cantina, music would play and fel'ina would whirl. Blacker than night were the eye's of fel'ina, wicked and evil while casting a spell.\n\nMy love was deep for this highelven maiden, I was in love but in vain I could tell. One night a wild young guardsman came in, wild as the west vailor wind. Dashing and daring a drink he was sharing with wicked fel'ina the girl that I loved.\n\nSo in anger I challanged his right for the love of this maiden, downward his hand for the sword that he wore. My challange was answerd in less than a heart beat, the handsome yound guardsman lay dead on the floor.\n\nJust for a moment I stood there in silence, shocked by the foul evil deed I had done.\nmany thoughts raced through my mind as I stood there, I had but one chance and that was to run. Out through the bock door of rose's I ran, out where the horses were\n\ntied. I caught a good one, it looked like it could run up on its back and away I did ride. Just as fast as I could from the west vailor town of felen, off to the badlands of caliphate I go. Back in felsen my life would be worthless, everythings gone in\n\nlife, nothing is left. Its been so long since ive seen the yound maiden, my love is stronger than my fear of death. I saddle up and away I did go, riding alone in the dark. Maybe tomrrow a arrow will find me but tonight nothings worse than this pain in my\n\nheart. And atlast here I am on the hill overlooking felsen, I can see rose's cantina below. My love is strong and it pushes me onward, down of the hill to fel'ina I go. Off to my left I see five hundred guardsmen, off to my left ride a dozen more.\n\nshouting and shooting I cant let them catch me, I have to make it to rose's back door. Somthing is dreadfully wrong for I feel a deep burning pain in my side. thought I am trying to stay in the saddle Im getting weary unable to ride.\n\nBut my love for fel'ina is stong and I rise where Ive fallen, Though I am weary I cant stop to rest. I see the shine from the head of the arrow, I feel the shaft go deep in my chest.\n\nFrom out of nowhere fel'ina has found me, kissing my cheek as she kneels by my side. Cradled in two arms Ill die for, one little kiss and fel'ina goodbye.....\n\n(ooc- parody song of \"El paso\" by marty robbins)", ""),
        StaticBook("The Halfling Pt1", "§bFelix Stoutfoot", "The Halfling: The Quest for the Ocafluta\n\nBy Felix Stoutfoot\n\n~A True Story~\n\nDay 1\n\nToday, I set off with a few measly supplies, alongside this journal, and a wooden axe and this very rare Yew Sapling to find a nice spot.\n\nDay 2\n\nYesterday I made some nice progress outwards, until I hit the ocean. I travelled around the coast, and made it to a town, I decided to stay at the stables in town. In the dead of night, I swore I could hear the sound of hay being moved.\n\nDay 2 Night\n\nDuring tonight, I had a small flashes of dreams. Some of them were nightmares of people I loved. And then there was one in particular, a powerful warrior went up to me in a blinding light, and whispered a name to me, but I couldn't catch it.\n\nDay 3\n\nToday I move from the town and again into the wilderness, I plan to head to a forest full of beautiful soil. In the farthest lands, near Mastah Veren's Grove, I hear that is perfect soil for a rare Yew plant like this fella.\n\nDay 3 Night\n\nTonight, I stayed in a small grotto. Again, I slept and I had more nightmares of me failing challenges due to my size. The big warrior that I see sometimes seems to know my name....but its not my name...I still can't make it out.\n\nDay 4\n\nToday I left the quaint Grotto to head down and outwards into the valley. When I reached the Valley, I saw a large foresty area at the top of the cliffside. Tonight, I will rest up for my strength to climb the cliffside.\n\nDay 4 Night\n\nTonight, I slept up, and then I had a terrible, yet wonderful dream of Mira. I dunno what got into me. But when I woke up, I felt a breathing on me, and it was actually the licking of a Red Weasel. When I pet it though, it was prickly.\n\nDay 5\n\nToday, I climb up the mountain. I told my new friend (Who I called Samuel) to climb on my shoulder. I climbed up the first few rocks, but the stuff was too steep for my little body to handle. I decided to rest up, and fish up some food for us.\n\nDay 5 Night\n\nTonight was very quaint with Sam and I. I told him a lot about how I felt, and he seemed to nod as if he understood me. We then snuggled up and rested up our strength for tomorrow.\n\nDay 5 Night continued\n\nThe dreams kept getting worse and worse, but today. I could swear I could see the great warrior had spiky hair as he slew mighty, flying beasts. With a claymore and shield in hand, he rescued me and overcame expansive challenges.\n\nDay 6\n\nAs dawn broke, Sam purred like a fox on my body. And I got up, planning my next way of attack. Today, I would try going horizontally.\n\nDay 6 Night\n\nTonight, I write this halfway up the cliffside, in a small grotto. I am resting while making a small fire in this cool cavern. Sam kept watch for any suspicious enemies.\n\nDay 6 Dreams\n\nI sleep today, and I see Mira at a lakeside with me, when all the sudden, I collapse down into the lake. As I fall into the deepest reaches of darkness....I can hear the jolly laughter of some devil, I dunno. And I hear the squealling of her\n\nDay 7\n\nToday I broke out in a sweat. I dunno what was causing anything last night. I am going to reach the top today, and set up a small camp up above.\n\nDay 8\n\nI climbed up nonstop today, and through the night. The coolness of the night made it difficult. But I have made it up there to watch the dawn of Day 8. I am totally pooped as I suddenly collapse into a nap.\n\nDay 8 Dreams\n\nAs I collapse, I feel the same falling feeling as if I was letting go of her. And I can't reach out for my Uncle. The darkness is just....blank. I sometimes make out large, fiery foes in the dark.\n\nDay 8 Dreams\n\nAs I rest, I can hear a light saying \"S....Stou...\" but I can't hear. It is saying something. Before I can figure it out, a small figure appears and says \"Awaken.\"\n\nDay 14\n\nIt appears that winter has finally ended (I left during Winter). I dunno how long I was in that trance, but Surprisingly, Sam has been around, keeping watch and bringing all these flowers somehow. At least I think so.\n\nDay 15\n\nToday, I am going to plant this Yew plant. Surprisingly, it has kept its shape since I've left it. I dig a small hole, and plant it. I give a small prayer to the Yew, to become strong and hardy.\n\nDay 60\n\nThe past two months has been tedious and long. Fun times with the tree during the day, but nightmares during the night.\n\nDay 60 Night\n\nTonight, I plan to explore the darkness. I hug Sam goodnight and rest my poor eyes.\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nI explored the darkness today, the past few times, I have been seeing pictures of Her being tortured and a man cackling from doing things....I dunno what...but I just hear squeals of pain that hurt my heart.\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nI travel farther and farther through the depths, until I reach a giant red castle. I sneak into it with all my strength. The castle reeks of necromancy, and blight but the darkness already did anyways.\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nI slowly sneak through the forces to try and find any source of actual life. I stumble upon a cell soon with a Knight in a helmet, chained up and bloodied. I decide to open up the cell.\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nTo my surprise, he wakes up in an instant and I can hear a smile within the helmet. \"Well, if it isn't Stoutfoot, Son of Salmon?\" I then point at myself as he nods inside his helmet, he then removes it to show prickly, spiky hair as if it-\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\n-it were quills on a porcupine. \"My name is Samuel. And I am chosen to be your guardian.\" he then kneels as if I was some sorta king. Outta sort of impulse I just say, \"Rise Samuel.\" He then rises as if some sorta knight out of a book.\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\n\"I was sent out by the Three in search of Relic, it is known as a Core. Used to create a powerful, and rare instrument, barely known by Men.\" I slightly nod and just say I am searching for a friend I love.\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nWith a swift nod he just says, \"I guess our paths have crossed by the Three's Decision. Let's go now.\" He goes out of the cell, suddenly having a claymore and tower shield to match his tabard torn armor. He then slices through the nearest-\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nThe nearest Skeleton, jumping back and forth as swift and cunning as a Fox. After a couple of foes down, we head downstairs as I ask where did he learn that? \"Anything is feasible, ya just gotta set yer mind to it.\" he says.\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\nWe then arrive deep in a ritual room, full of Daemon magic, and a hooded man cackling with a crack of a whip as squeals are heard from behind. \"Let's finish this.\" I say. The man cackles while swinging a Druidic marked stone in the air.\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\n\"The Core!\" Samuel says, as he charges head first into the battle. I then think of what I can do to help. And suddenly I just grapple onto the back of the man, so he can't control any of his magic. So, I suddenly felt a sharp pain in my-\n\nDay 60 Dreams\n\n-pain in my chest, as I see a sword coming through the Hooded man as he dissipates. I then collapse on the ground as I see the girl being taken away.\n\n\"Stoutfoot, Son of Salmon.\" is the last four words I hear.\n\nDay ???\n\nI wake up to feel water splashing on me. it is raining, and Where I see the once sapling I was planting, I see a great tall Yew plant. I then awake to see Sam at my side, nudging me to be awake and towards the Yew plant.\n\nDay ???\n\nI nod to the loyal pal, as I slowly chop down the tree with a soft respect and gaze. When the tree lands with a loud thump, I can see a Wooden Core, where it is thickest. I carve out a certain section of it. I then pray and thank the Aspects for-\n\nDay ???\n\nFor this wonderful gift. I then sit there, wondering what I am supposed to craft. I think hard about this, and I hear the whispers of grass as if it was saying \"Stoutfoot.\" but it wasn't.\n\nDay ???\n\nI then come up with the idea of a larger Ocarina, but with as many holes as a standard flute. As I begin to craft this, Sam nudges me and I carve in multiple Druidic symbols, like one meaning 'Courage'.\n\nDay ???\n\nI soon finish within a few days of work and toil. I painted it with light green. As I sat there I wondered what my life will be like with this new instrument. I then pack up my stuff, and start heading back a changed man.\n\nDay ???\n\nAs Stoutfoot........Son of Salmon.", ""),
        StaticBook("Twilight Sleeps", "§bSul'irrin Audane", "The Twlight Sleeps\n\nWhile the sun doth shine\nand the moon doth glow\n\nOne wonders, where do they go? Do they flow freely on waves of light Or perhaps they move, just out of sight.\n\nThe ebb and they flow, weave and go through spaces unknown to even us.\n\nThey move with passion, with grace and form. They seem to live Long-term. \n\nNeedless be the moon and sun, for the light of each is but a pun.\n\nA pun of life, a game that's lost, the moment we decide what's greater the cost.\n\nWe move with strides, Day-to-Day perhaps one moment we'll find a way.\n\nA way to move among the waves, with the moon, the sun, and among the brave.\n\nWe ebb and flow with time as we please, as the sun and the moon stay at ease.\n\nBut still we smile as night turns to day, for no more darkness can stand in our way.", ""),
        StaticBook("Dommery Case CH1", "§bThomas", "A book written by the\nmale Highlander known\nas Thomas. Of no house or other name.\n\nA story told to me by Hamlin Smith - a wise old man who had cared for me until age of 18.\n\nThis is written in his memory.\n\nThere were three Highlanders. James Dommery, Robert Dommery and last but not least Jem Dommery.\n\nThey were brothers to one another - cared for each other and had spent all their life together.\n\nAs usual on a night when they're all without burden of work they would go out to their local Inn - The Frog's Leg.\n\nThey would stay until the late hours, laughing and singing old songs of adventure and tales however it wasn't a normal night.\n\nThey were approached by a man - great in height but small in width. He wore a black robe with the hood up, tightened to only reveal his pale face.\nHe asked them\n\"What do you want in life boys?\"\nThey were puzzled.\n\n\"What are you on about you daft bastard?\"\nThey continued to laugh mockingly and ignore the man's signs of seriousness, he seemed to hold the situation with upmost of importance. However, luckily for the man Jem had not been as drunk as his brothers.\n\n\"Why would you ask then mate?\" Jem questioned.\nThe pale man then proceeded to lower his body, slumping into the stool opposite the three men.\n\"I can predict your future or even change it for that matter.\"\n\nThe three brothers looked at each other, holding in their grinns to only then burst out laughing.\nAlthough, again Jem had remained interested and leaned closer to the man across the table.\n\"Why would you help us?\" Jem asked.\n\nThe man searched his pockets, looking for something quickly to then reveal three gems from his pocket. He laid them out in his palm, gently bouncing them off one another.\n\"These will give you a wish per gem, they can grant your deepest desires and darkest\n\nfantasies\"\nJem quickly swapped his view from the man's face to the gems and cycled between the two images to then reach for the gems. However, he was responded with the pale man to retract them slightly out of his reach.\n\n\"These are dangerous rocks, from the depths of our world as we know it. Once you make a wish there is no turning back.\"\nThe man then extended his arm so the gems were in Jem's reach - he reached out for them and pocketed them into his trousers.\n\nAnd when he looked up again, the man was gone.\nHis brothers had not noticed the exchange of the gems, they were too drunk and obsessed with the maid to pay attention.\n\nThe next day - after being woken by the cuckoo of the chickens he then knew one of his wishes.\nRunning down the stairs, he left objects on the walls to clatter as he ran past - some falling to the ground and denting the wooden floor.\n\nOutside the door was a batch of their chickens that belonged to them, he riddled one of the gems in his palm to then say \"I wish the chickens would lay gold eggs\".\nHe waited for a indicator of achievement but nothing happened.\n\nJem was dissapointed, he was fooled and led to believe that his life could've changed for the better.\nThat day he had work - he was a guard at the Renigen Outpost. Where activity was low and boredness was present.\n\nHe slumbed on the stool leaning against the coble tower that overwatched the mossy road. In his palm he rotated the gems, clicking one another into each other.\nThey were still valuable he thought. For the materials inside them - maybe a diamond.\n\nLater on in the day he saw someone far away - running it seemed towards the outpost.\nUpon the figure coming closer he made it out to be his brother James. Then begin the faint sound of \"Jem!\" and it grew louder as he drew closer.\n\nJames had stumbled infront of him like some dansel in distress.\n\"Jem, Jem you have to come home now!\"\n\"Why, what's the matter?\"\nJames looked around carefully, in the tower and on the road.\n\"The eggs Jem, the chickens are laying fucking golden eggs!\"\n\nThis moment Jem realised one of the gems in his palm was missing. It worked.\nIt left him with thoughts of all the things he could do and achieve.\nThis was the start of the Dommery brother's downfall.\n\nChapter 1 of The Dommery Case", ""),
        StaticBook("Rovin Commission", "§bMarcus Rovin", "To the Lyons Estate:\n\nI am Marcus Rovin, a former general now residing in my family estate of Arnheim. My family wishes to employ the services of a cartographer in order to map the general area, as well as to dictate an illustration that would provide\n\nthe populace with a clear route from the Cloud Temple to our home. Payment should be of no concern - simply state your price and send a reply to my office.\n\nArnheim is located between the Republic of Vrakai and the \"Kingdom\" of Marna, on the west bank\n\nof the bridge that crosses the river Baltas. Please send a reply to my office in this castle.\n\nSincerely,\nM. Rovin", ""),
        StaticBook("Poems For My <3", "§bGonzalo de Castro", "Those lips that Love's own hand did make Breathed forth the sound that said \"I hate\" To me that languished for her sake;\nBut when she saw my woeful state, Straight in her heart did mercy come,\nChiding that tongue that ever sweet,\n\nWas used in giving gentle doom,\nAnd taught it thus anew to greet:\n\"I hate\" she altered with an end,\nThat followed it as gentle day,\nDoth follow night, who like a fiend\nFrom heaven to hell - is flown away.\n\n\"I hate\" from hate away she threw,\nAnd saved my life, saying \"not you.\"\n\nBlank Page)\n\nMusic to hear, why hear'st thou music sadly?\nSweets with sweets war not, joy delights in joy.\nWhy lovest thou that which thou receivest not gladly,\nOr else receivest with pleasure thine annoy?\n\nIf the true concord of well tuned sounds,\nBy unions married, do offend thine ear,\nThey do but sweetly chide thee, who confounds\nIn singleness the parts that thou shouldst bear.\n\nMark how one string, sweet husband to another,\nStrikes each in each by mutual ordering;\nResembling sire and child and happy mother,\nWho, all in one, one pleasing note do sing:\n\nWhose speechless song, being many, seeming one,\nSings this to thee: 'Thou single wilt prove none.'\n\n(Blank Page)\n\nLook in thy glass, and tell the face thou viewest\nNow is the time that face should form another;\nWhose fresh repair if now thou not renewest,\nThou dost beguile the world, unbless some mother.\n\nFor where is she so fair whose unear'd womb\nDisdains the tillage of thy husbandry?\nOr who is he so fond will be the tomb\nOf his self-love, to stop posterity?\n\nThou art thy mother's glass, and she in thee\nCalls back the lovely April of her prime:\nSo thou through windows of thine age shalr see,\nDespite of wrinkles, this thy golden time.\n\nBut if thou live, remember'd not to be,\nDie single, and thine image does with thee.\n\n(Blank page)\n\nFrom fairest creatures we desire increase,\nThat thereby beauty's rose might never die,\nBut as the riper should by time decease,\nHis tender heir might bear his memory:\nBut thou, contacted to thine own bright eyes,\n\nFeed'st thy light's flame with self-substantial fuel,\nMaking a famine where abundance lies,\nThyself thy foe, to thy sweet self too cruel.\nThou that art now the world's fresh ornament\nAnd only herald to the gaudy spring,\n\nWithin thine own bud buriest thy content\nAnd, tender churl, makest waste in niggarding.\nPity the world, or else this glutton be,\nTo eat the world's due, by the grave and thee.\n\n(Blank Page)\n\nMy mistress' eyes are nothing like the sun;\nCoral is far more red than her lips' red;\nIf snow be white, why then her breasts are dun;\nIf hairs be wires, black wires grow on her head.\n\nI have seen roses damasked, red and white,\nBut no such roses see I in her cheeks;\nAnd in some perfumes is there more delight\n\nThan in the breath that from my mistress reeks.\nI love to hear her speak, yet well I know,\nThat music hath a far more pleasing sound;\nI grant - I never saw a goddess go;\n\nMy mistress, when she walks, treads on the ground.\nAnd yet, by heaven, I think my love as rare\nAs any she belied with false compare.\n\n(Blank Page)\n\nTake, o take those lips away, \nThat so sweetly were forsworn, \nAnd those eyes, the break of day,\n\nLights that do mislead the morn! \nBut my kisses bring again, \nBring again; \nSeals of love, but seal'd in vain, \nSeal'd in vain!\n\n(Blank Page) The next poem is for Ariana)\n\nWhen we first fell in love \nI thought that nothing could compare \nTo the magical romance \nThat you and I had come to share.\n\nBut as time passed, feelings deepened,\nAnd our closeness grew \nThe romance turned into \nA real and lasting love with you.\n\nYou care for me in all the ways \nI want and need so much. \nI’ve felt your warmth and tenderness \nWith every word and touch.\n\nI  know I can depend on you\nFor support and honesty, \nThat patient understanding \nThat you always give to me.\n\nThere’s a special kind of happiness \nThat only love can bring, \nAnd I’ve found that happiness with you...\nYou are my everything.\n\n(Blank Page)\n\nShe is truly beautiful to behold\nFrom a distance, see her angelic shell\nDeep down she is just a demon from Hell\nHer heart is cold, to the devil it’s sold\n\nHer wrath on men has begun to unfold\nShe never loves them\nthey are blind to tell\nFrom the beginning \ncaught in her spell\nShe hurt them deeply\nmade their hearts grow cold\n\nIt is true, beauty is only skin deep\nWhat I am saying\nis the proof to see\nShow him your heart \nhe’ll be yours to keep \nListen to me \nonly true love is the key\n\nFind a man that loves you \nthen you will see\nYour love will last\nfor all eternity\n\n(Blank Page)\n\nShall I compare thee to a summer's day?\nThou art more lovely and more temperate.\nRough winds do shake the darling buds of May,\nAnd summer's lease hath all too short a date.\n\nSometime too hot the eye of heaven shines,\nAnd often is his gold complexion dimmed;\nAnd every fair from fair sometime declines,\nBy chance, or nature's changing course untrimmed.\n\nBut thy eternal summer shall not fade\nNor lose possession of that fair thou ow'st;\nNor shall death brag thou wand'rest in his shade,\nWhen in eternal lines to time thou grow'st,\n\nSo long as men can breathe or eyes can see,\nSo long lives this, and this gives life to thee.\n\n(Blank Page)\n\nNever seek to tell thy love,\nLove that never told can be;\nFor the gentle wind doth move\nSilently, invisibly.\n\nI told my love, I told my love,\nI told her all my heart,\nTrembling, cold, in ghastly fears.\nAh! she did depart!\n\nSoon after she was gone from me,\nA traveller came by,\nSilently, invisibly:\nHe took her with a sigh.\n\n(Blank Page)\n\nI lay in bed at night trying to fall asleep all I can think about is you,you like my fantasy my dream come true,I never knew our love could be this strong half of it probably hasn't been shown,I love the way you smile,I love the way you laugh\n\nI love the fact that you care so much even though we haven't met and the fact that you don't give up even when times get rough,I love when you say I love you and that I always get butterflies even when I'm thinking of you...\n\n.I'll love you till my dying day,You might not understand how much you mean to me or how much you have changed my life for better not for worse I thank you I should say I owe my life to you!\n\n!I love you with all my heart,I want to love and spend the rest of my life with you,Your my angel from above girl and I thank god that I have you!\n\n\nTime for a New Jornal", ""),
        StaticBook("The M&H: Part 1", "§bAthedil Haler'thilln", "----------------Maehr’sae Hiylun’ehya\nChapter 1\n________________As interpreted by Lucion Sullas, former Okarir, Tilruir, Sohaer, and Maheral of Haelun’or.\n\nThe Way of Purity is greatly discredited around the civilized world due to the actions of uninformed adherants and their unfortunate victims. Misinformation upon its tenets run rampant amongst the uninitiated,\n\nthus I write this short series upon its history, its ideals, and common misconceptions. It is a desire to inform, rather than ‘convert’ that drives this humble quill, therefore do not consider this a threat to any local\n\nreligions/philosophies/mysteries that currently occupy your own people.\n\nTo those that read on, Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya to you. - L. Sullas\n\nIn the beginning, long before Iblees, there was Aegis. And within Aegis, there were elves. Nor of any racial denominations as we have today, but of a singular, primal form. Of this time we know little, save for what\n\nscraps we have recovered during the days of Asulon. During this time, a particular elf caught ancient Malinor’s attention-- a woman known as Larihei. This woman changed herself through ‘bathng in and\n\ningesting the waters of enchanted pools of gold.’ This eventually lead to Larihei’s exile, and the self-imposed exile of many followers. By means unknown they arrived in Asulon and constructed ‘Cihi’thilln.’ Or\n\n“Silver City” in the common tongue. Within this place they built many lost wonders, discovered bizarre and mysterious magics, and then disappeared entirely. Many reasons have been postulated for this--namely a\n\ngreat plague that coincided with other cataclysms that rocked the Dervas and the Mori. Regardless, the city that the Aegisian High Elves found was a ruin. Within the crumbling Eternal College, they found remnants of\n\nan ancient essay; one the previous occupiers based their society upon. It’s hypothesis was ‘Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya’ Or ‘The pursuit of wisdom and health.’\n\nThe newly-dubbed “Mali’aheral” (Blessed elves) chose to honour these ancestors by following their lost ways. What was originally a cultural focal-point eventually became a way of life. A philosophy that drives\n\nmany individuals to this day.\n\nUnderstand that this history is short only due to a complete lack of information that was lost over the eras. Our way is older than most empires and religions. It lives to this day, and may well continue to exist so long\n\nas there are Mali’aheral to revere it.\n\nMaehr’sae hiylun’ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("The M&H: Part 2", "§bAthedil Haler'thilln", "----------------Maehr’sae Hiylun’ehya\nChapter 2\n----------------As interpreted by Lucion Sullas, former Okarir, Tilruir, Sohaer, and Maheral of Haelun’or.\n\nTo follow the tenets of the Maehr’sea hiylun’ehya one must first know the meaning behind the ancient elven that masks it. Its most accurate common translation is “The pursuit of wisdom and health” or simply\n\n‘wisdom and health.’ So revered is this term that is akin to a blessing given between adherents. The Maehr’sae pertains to the acquisition and sharing of knowledge amongst fellow Mali’aheral. Our race is\n\nknown for many things, but poor academics are not included. After being changed by the magics of the Golden Pools, we were blessed with studious minds, and gifted great talent with magic of any form. Thusly,\n\nit is imperative that we embroil ourselves utterly within tasks that further our people’s knowledge.\n\nThe Hiylun’ehya pertains to the bloodlines and fortitude of the people. Pure bloodlines are the ones that best retain the blessings of the ancient pools. To sully them with poorly-reasoned mixed breeding thins the\n\nblessings that we gained, and therefore makes the maehr’sae hiylun’ehya more difficult to complete--if not impossible. In guarding our bloodlines we must show discipline and fortitude. Things that detract the health\n\nof the people; violence against the pure, mixed-breeding, and being too lenient and accepting towards the other races. One must always be diligent when regarding impurities. The small concessions of today always\n\nlead to the vilest impurities tomorrow beings. It has been observed, and thus it is known.\n\nThe ultimate goal of the Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya is its completion. To reach true enlightment , the Mali’aheral strive to understand all through constant learning, and a pure people. When all is understood,\n\nwe will be beyond the simple meanderings of the mundane world. It is unknown what will occur when this day of total enlightenment occurs, but one suspects the Mali’aheral will know precisely what to do.\n\nMaehr’sae hiylun’ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("The M&H: Part 3", "§bAthedil Haler'thilln", "----------------Maehr’sae Hiylun’ehya\nChapter 3\n----------------As interpreted by Lucion Sullas, former Okarir, Tilruir, Sohaer, and Maheral of Haelun’or.\n\nAs with any ideology, there are misconceptions amongst the uninitiated. Mainly upon the desires of its adherents, the reasons behind their actions, or perhaps even mere differences in personality. It is difficult\n\nto write a truly concise list, but one hopes the ones he lists are relevant to the reader.\n\n----------------1. On Racism and Seclusion\n----------------The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya does not support illogical hatreds of other peoples. Rather, it supports rational\n\nwariness of dangerous outsiders--such as urukan, tal’urukan and suspicious strangers. The urukan and tal’urukan are beings with a natural aversion to elven thought and philosophy. Though there can be\n\nexceptions, they are often ignored or destroyed, should they be in the presence of the Pure. They cannot be trusted under any circumstances. In regardes to the other races, it is most certainly dependant on the\n\nMali’aheral in question. I am yet to meet a Mali’aheral aside gtom Uradir who truly despised all peoples equally. It is for these reasons adherents separate themselves from contemporary society.\n\n----------------2. On Insults and the Insulted\n----------------The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya does not support arbitrary personal attacks. It does however, support learning,\n\nadvising, and truth. Should an individual speak without merit or evidence upon an individual with the purpose of cruel amusement, then they are a poor adherent, and have provided nothing to anyone.\n\nHowever, advise can often be misinterpreted as insult. Adherents are taught to despise falsehood, therefore should something be perceived as incorrect they rightly feel the need to amend it. If an individual\n\nhas their feelings hurt during the process, it is their issue, and not the adherent’s.\n\n----------------3. On Violence and Aggression\n----------------The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya does not support physical violence of any kind. It does support safeguarding the\n\npurity of its people. Often, death to those who would sully the purity of the adherents is the first and foremost answer to such crimes. However, violent actions belong to beasts, and are beneath us.\n\nOurs is an order built upon the mind, not the passions of raised fists.\n\n----------------4. On ‘Purges’ and Murder.\n----------------Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya does not support ‘purges’, or murder. It does, however, support the exaction of\n\njustice to craven monsters. Some individuals are so profane in their existence that they insult and endanger our way. Such people are more often-than-not loathed throughout all civilised lands.\n\nSuch individuals are few and far between, but if by the act of living they injure us, then they must be destroyed for the good of all. Exile ought to be the first and foremost method of drastic punishment in any case.\n\n----------------5. On Experimentation and Learning\n----------------The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya does not support unethical and cruel experiments.\n\nIt does support the vigorous acquisition of knowledge. Those that would perform any experiment on a living, sentient, non-consenting induviduals are preforming a disgusting act that harms their own purity through reckless\n\nand untethered curiosity, as well as harming the reputation of their own people. It is bizarre, cruel, unethical, and the findings never outweigh the cost.\n\n----------------6. On Emotion and Aversion to it.\n----------------The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya does not support and emotionless state in the individual.\n\nRather, it encourages logic, foresight, and wisdom over passionate outbursts. It is wiser to think before feeling. In public, it is beneath an adherent to act by the whims ofemotion--it shows a lack\n\nof self-control and would likely offend those around yourself.\n\n----------------7. On Superiority and Arrogance\n----------------The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya does not declare Mali’aheral to be superior to other races. It does, however,\n\nsupport that those who follow its path closely are greater than others, as they seek enlightenment through the unravelling of truth, rather than the mundanities of life. Identifying adherents as ‘arrogant’ is simply an\n\ninnocent misinterpretation on the side of the uninitiated. Should one encounter an adherent that claims themselves to be ‘superior’ generally speaking, one would advise you to ask them their current academic projects.\n\nShould they refuse to answer, it is safe to say their ego speaks, and not the Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya.\n\n----------------8. On adherents and Their Qualities\n----------------The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya supports that only the Mali’aheral, with their inherent blessings,\n\ncan successfully follow the Pure Way. But this is only true in theory. The Maehr’sae hiylun’ehya encourages community cohesion and the search for truth. Theoretically, any race (with the exception of perhaps\n\nlye’urukan) may adopt and follow the path to enlightenment. No other race has attempted to adhere to it, thus perhaps it will never be known for certain.\n\nOne hopes that this series has been illuminating. Seek out L. Sullas, if you can, should questions be sought. Otherwise, good luck on your own twisting path.\n\nMaehr’sae hiylun’ehya.", ""),
        StaticBook("A Hundred Years", "§bDeven", "A hundred years is a very long time!\n\nHo,yes,ho!\n\nA hundred years is a very long time!\n\nA hundred years ago!\n\nThey used to think that pigs could fly!\n\nHo,yes,ho!\n\nI don't believe it, no, not I!\n\nA hundred years ago!\n\nThey thought the moon was made of cheese!\n\nHo,yes,ho!\n\nYou can believe it if\n\nyou please!\n\nA hundred years ago!\n\nThey thought the stars were set a-light!\n\nHo,yes,ho!\n\nBy some good Angle every night!\n\nA hundred years ago!\n\nThey hung a man for making steam, they cast his body in the stream!\n\nA hundred years ago!\n\nA hundred years is a very long time!\n\nHo,yes,ho!\n\nA hundred years is a\n\nvery long time!\n\nA hundred years ago!", ""),
