        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "*a set of hand drawn pictures would be writen in the book, describing many scenes*§0\n§0\n§0The First: A well drawn man with pointed ears and a band around his head, and many females around him,\n\nSecond: A women with a Rose in her hair, and a upset expression drawn, next to another pregant women.\n\nThird: A Pregnant Women kissing a differnt elf man in front of a building, which resembles a tavern in Marna\n\nFour: Elf with the band fighting many men inside a building. Resembling the insides of Marna's Tavern.\n\nFive: Elf Man with band is sitting outside, with female girl with the Rose in her hair, the Human man who was fighting is watching them.\n\nSix: Human Male is facing the Elf with the band, and has a Cross Bow pointed at him, Many losely drawn people around them.\n\nSeven: Human man, stabbing Elf with the band, and blood is pooring out of the elf, Many are still drawn around them.\n\nEight: Elf man with the band, lies on the floor, as human girl with the rose in her hair, looks at him sadly.\n\nNine: Human man looks at the human girl with the rose in her hair, and spits in her direction.\n\nTen: Human girl with the rose in her hair, is drawn on steps, crying.\n\n*many deep marks, the resemble pen stabings, and ink scattered everywhere, crunched pages that look once wet remain*", ""),
        StaticBook("Enchanting", "§bLefkos Glowsbane", "Efficiency:\nEfficiency is one of the quickest and easiest of all of the enchantments to make. The purpose of this is to make any desired tool do its job faster. Using it, you may find that your pickaxe digs through stone like a knife through butter, or\n\naxe may fell a tree in one or two swings. Even though it may be a cheap enchantment, it remains one of the most well known and used.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        ---------                ----x----                ---x-x---                ----x----\n\nUnbreaking:\nThis would probably be the second most used enchant, its purpose rather simple and self explanatory. I will review it anyway. Unbreaking is meant to make your tools harder and stronger. Tougher to break. Using it, you may notice that tools\n\nthat used to break after you use them for a while may still be functional. Its another easy enchantment that wouldnt cost to much to purchase.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        ---------                -x-x-x-x-                --x---x--                -x-x-x\n\nSharpness:\nThis is a rather difficult enchantment, much to hard for a novice to make, and a rather expensive one as well. With this enchantment, you may find that your swords cut through bodys easier, making your opponents fall before your blade.\n\nThose that seek out an enchanter for this enchantment are normally guards, or people about to go to war.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        --x------                xxxxxxxx-                xxxxxxxxx                --x------\n\nPower:\nAn enchantment similar to sharpness, but for a different item. Power is made for bows, and when using it, you may find arrows you shoot from your bow hitting harder, enough to crack stone and injure your opponent more then a normal arrow. Only\n\nProffesional marksmen and archers will seak out this enchantment.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        xx----x--                --xxxxxx-                --xxxxxxx                xx----x--\n\nFire Aspect:\nOne of the oldest and harder enchantments to master. Many seek this enchantment on their blades for its usefullness. It is a must have for armies and a hard level enchantment. Adventurers and high ranking officers may seek out an enchanter\n\ncapable of this for their army. Fire aspect gives your blade an arcane power that, upon cutting any living creature, will set them aflame. Its thought of as a brutal but useful enchantment.\n\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        -x-x-x-x-                -x-x-x-x-                -x-x-x-x-                -xxxxxxx-\n\nFlame:\nVery similar to Fire Aspect, Flame is another hard level enchantment. It lets your arrows catch fire, and burn whatever they hit.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-        x--x--x-x                -xxxx-x-x                x--x--x-x                ------xx\n\nKnockback:\nOne of the best enchantments in my opinion, knockback is sure to prove useful to anyone, no matter who they are fighting. This enchantment, rather then strengthening the actual blade, strengthens the arm holding the blade.\n\nIt is called \"Knockback\" because at that point, if you hit someone with your arm at full force, you possess the strength to send them flying back. Combine this with Fire aspect and you can shoot little fireballs called 'your opponent.'\n\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-         --xx-----                --xxxxx--                --xxxxx--                --xx-----\n\nProtection:\nOne of the less common used enchantments, but more useful. Protection was made to make your armor harder, so an arrow that would once pierce your heart wouldnt even reach it. The only reason it isnt commonly used is because not many\n\npeople have the time to wait for their armor to be enchanted.\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-         --xxxxx--                --xxxxx--                --xxxxx--                ---xxx---\n\nFeather falling:\nA rarely used enchant. Infact, not a single person has asked me for it. I will put it here anyways. Feather falling increases the strength of your feet in terms of impact for the ground. Normally if you would barely survive after a 10\n\nmeter drop, you would be fine for this handy enchantment. Most people under value this enchantment, until they slip and fall!\n-=-=-=-Recipe-=-=-=-         -----xx--                ----xxx--                ----xx---                ---x-----", ""),
        StaticBook("Inquiry", "§bVanya Damaer", "I look forward to meeting with you to discuss my possible employment at the Eternal College. Thank you for your swift response. §0\n§0\n§0May we meet on the following elven day at approximately midday for tea and lunch at my home?§0\n§0\n§0Maehr'sae Hiylun'ehya,§0\n§0Vanya D.\n\nOOC: You can give me a date and time that you're available and I'll try to move my schedule to match so we can meet up!", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "14th of Malin's Welcome, 1689§0\n§0\n§0I received devastating news earlier today. Alanah, the elven barwaitress working at the Belvitz tavern had been reenslaved by the orcs. I met with Myrdin at the Cloud Temple and we organized a plan to free her. She's\n\nbeing held at the Iron Uzg. We stopped in Nordengrad to purchase some gear and supplies for our journey. While Myrdin rests, I've been making small talk with the citizens. They're rather.. interesting, to say the least. Their tax collector beat a woman to\n\nthe ground and threatened to murder her because she insisted that she had already paid her taxes. The citizens seem to have a very violent nature. I fear the orcs will be more violent than these people around me. §0\n§0\n§0-Al\n\n15th of Malin's Welcome, 1689§0\n§0\n§0Myrdin still insists on staying in Nordengrad. The city is very strict about their tax laws, it seemed. I saw the tax collector and a man in armor brawling in the streets and shouting over whether they payed or not. The\n\ncity feels welcoming, but seems to be corrupt. I hope Myrdin decides to continue on the adventure soon. §0\n§0\n§0I recieved another note from Alanah. She said that the fee for her freedom is 1000 mina. I'm prepared to pay it for her. Hopefully the orcs are\n\npeaceful and give her freedom.", ""),
        StaticBook("Writable Book", "", "Target§0\n§0~~~~~§0\n§0Ser Brand von Denhardt§0\n§0[!] A drawing of the man would be seen below. Natural dyes would be used to color in his face. Pale, brown hair, brown eyes, beard.§0\n§0It would be marked§0\n§0KOS\n\nTarget§0\n§0~~~~~§0\n§0Ingvildr §0\n§0Crime: Beating Saoirse§0\n§0Punishment: Death§0\n§0[!] A sketch of Ingvildr would be here. §0\n§0It would be described as: White blonde hair, blue eyes, tall. Skilled warrior.§0\n§0It would be marked with blood\n\nTarget§0\n§0~~~~~§0\n§0Dainn§0\n§0Crime: Beating Saoirse§0\n§0[!] A sketch of the man would be here. Brown hair, beard, deep blue eyes. Tall.§0\n§0It would be marked with blood\n\nTarget§0\n§0~~~~~§0\n§0Grungah§0\n§0Crime: Killing Islene, Threatening Saoirse§0\n§0[!] A sketch of the goblin would be here. Green and brutish, with tusks.§0\n§0It would be marked with blood§0\n\nTarget§0\n§0~~~~~§0\n§0Edward Devereux§0\n§0Crime: Hurting Saoirse§0\n§0Punishment: Death if he touches her again§0\n§0[!] A sketch of the human male. Dark brown, nearly black hair. Emerald green eyes, tall and wearing armor of Curon.§0\n§0It would be marked with blood.", ""),
        StaticBook("Pico Rules", "§bJaya Jayamen", "Pico Rules\n\nThis is a 2 player game. The game is composed of 11 cards. These are numbered 4 through 13 plus 16 and each also bears a number of stars. (From one on the 4 card to four on the 16 card.) A round is played as follows:\n\n each player is dealt 5 cards. After you deal the cards, there should be 1 left. This is the eleventh card. You show the eleventh card to both players.\n\n(Note that this means that you know exactly what cards your opponent holds.) (( I recommend using /roll (number) to randomly pick the cards being dealt.\n\n As to which cards are which number when rolling, Just have the 11 cards next to each other in your inventory and go in the order top to bottom, left to right, the top left card being 1 and the next one in the order being 2 and so forth.\n\nStart with /roll 11 to pick the first card from your inventory to be dealt, then /roll 10 to choose the second and so on. You want to lower the number you roll by 1 each time.))\n\nEach turn both you and your opponent secretly select one of their respective cards and reveal them simultaneously. (Note you don’t need to say the stars on the card when revealing which card you chose, just the number.)\n\n(( just have a card in mind, then when both are ready, countdown from 5 to 1 saying each number in two second intervals, then say your card after the 1. (you need to say it in two second intervals because of the time limits with the chat,\n\nit says “Please wait 1 second to speak” if you go too fast. Note that counting at the same pace down from 5 to 1 helps make the reveal of the cards more at the same time.\n\nIf you are getting the “Please wait 1 second to speak” message, try counting even slower. Doing it slowly and getting no “please wait” messages is better then going fast and getting the “please wait” messages.\n\nSo make sure to do it slow enough. Also, Pvp countdowns take too long with their cooldowns, so counting manually is better.) ))\n\nThe higher card wins and that player sets that card aside scoring the number of stars on it. The loser retains his/her played card.\n\n However, if the higher card is more than twice the lower card then it's the lower card that is placed aside and scored. So the 13 will beat the 10 but lose to the 6. Play continues until one player is left with but a single card.\n\nPoints are then scored and players swap hands and do it again. Make sure you remember how many stars you scored before swapping hands.\n\nSwapping hands ensures that each game is exactly fair as both players will have equal opportunity to play a strong/weak hand. After these two rounds the points are totaled and a winner declared.\n\nThere are, at most, fourteen card plays in a game and so the game is usually over in two or three minutes. (( just in case it comes up, the two red stars by “Player Approved” do not count when scoring cards. ))", ""),
